globalThis.WG_CATALOG={"meta":{"version":"2026-10-23.v2","wordCount":6008,"gsatCount":160,"senseCount":13913,"exampleCount":27828,"incompleteSenses":0,"missingWords":[],"sources":{"official":"https://www.ceec.edu.tw/files/file_pool/1/0N118345621497981164/%E9%AB%98%E4%B8%AD%E8%8B%B1%E6%96%87%E5%8F%83%E8%80%83%E8%A9%9E%E5%BD%99%E8%A1%A8%28111%E5%AD%B8%E5%B9%B4%E5%BA%A6%E8%B5%B7%E9%81%A9%E7%94%A8%29.pdf","dictionary":"https://github.com/ahpxex/open-dictionary/releases/tag/v2.0"},"scope":"核心義；核心義不足兩項時補充常用義。排除非官方詞性、古語、冷僻與可疑義項；不宣稱是所有可能義項的完整辭典。","sourceNotice":"# 字庫、義項與例句來源\n\n本版：2026-10-23.v2。\n\n## 分類與詞條\n\n「官方 6000 字」收錄大考中心《高中英文參考詞彙表（111 學年度起適用）》六級主表，共 6,008 詞條。保留官方的斜線及括號分組。已核對依級別與字母排序兩張主表，並修正 sportsman/sportswoman 在 PDF 跨行造成的擷取斷字。\n\n來源：https://www.ceec.edu.tw/xmdoc?xsmsid=0K213553204833715309\n\n原始字表權利屬財團法人大學入學考試中心基金會。原文件載明僅供非營利使用，轉載須註明出處；營利使用須事先取得基金會書面授權。\n\n「學測常考單字」為 160 個第 3–6 級詞條，在 111–115 學年度至少兩份正式英文試卷出現。統計包含題幹、選項和文章，不代表只計算字彙題正確答案，亦非官方必考排名。分析方法及各年度官方試卷網址見 gsat-frequent-160.json。同一詞條同時屬於兩類時，共用字義與學習進度，沒有另造一份重複字。\n\n## 中文義項與例句\n\n主要字典資料：ahpxex/open-dictionary v2.0。\n\n- 版本與下載：https://github.com/ahpxex/open-dictionary/releases/tag/v2.0\n- 專案：https://github.com/ahpxex/open-dictionary\n- 上游內容：Wiktionary/Wiktextract 與 Wiktionary 貢獻者；經原專案使用語言模型補寫中文學習釋義及例句。\n- 來源詞條連結顯示於每個義項下方，例如 https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank 。這些連結是詞條出處，不表示本版中文與例句逐句取自該 Wiktionary 頁面。\n- 資料授權：CC BY-SA 4.0，https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ 。原專案授權說明另附 OPEN-DICTIONARY-LICENSE-DATA.md。\n\n改作內容：依官方詞條擷取相符字形，優先保留核心義，核心義不足兩項時補充常用義；依官方詞性篩選，移除可疑、過時、專名等不適合本學習用途的義項；以 OpenCC 的 s2twp 設定轉換繁體中文。字典資料來源缺漏的詞條另行補寫。亦修正少數原資料英中欄位顛倒、英文欄誤填中文，以及例句使用不同詞形或詞根的情況。原有例句不足兩句時，由 Wordgrove 的編輯流程補寫不同情境的英文例句；每句的來源標記隨資料保留。新增英文例句沒有自動附上未經核對的中文翻譯。\n\n本次字典衍生內容及 Wordgrove 補寫的釋義、例句以 CC BY-SA 4.0 提供；大考中心的詞條清單、級別與試題來源保留各自原有權利與使用條件。字典授權不會替代大考中心對原清單的使用條件。\n\n此版收錄 13,913 個核心／常用學習義項，共 27,828 個例句，每個收錄義項至少兩句。這是學習用義項選集，不是單字全部古語、方言、專業義項的窮盡辭典。原資料與補寫內容均可能有誤，並未宣稱經過逐條人工辭典級審訂；頁面提供編輯義項與例句的功能以便修正。\n\n## 繁簡轉換\n\nOpenCC / opencc-python-reimplemented，用於將來源的簡體中文轉為繁體臺灣用語。\n\n- https://github.com/BYVoid/OpenCC\n- https://github.com/yichen0831/opencc-python\n\n字型使用使用者提供的 GENJYUUGOTHIC-BOLD.TTF；英文維持 Times New Roman。\n"},"words":[{"id":"ceec-4c9750e9da8174cf217a","word":"a/an","forms":["a"],"officialPos":"art.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"a","forms":["a","an"],"pos":"art.","zh":"一個；某個（不定冠詞）","examples":[{"en":"A bird is singing in the tree outside my window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She ate an orange after lunch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-df864c0596aa1a432205","word":"abandon","forms":["abandon"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ee8d8a1ed16ff38","term":"abandon","forms":["abandon","abandons","abandoning","abandoned","abandonest","abandonedst","abandoneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放開控制；任憑情感支配","explanation":"既可以指放棄對某事的控制，也可以指放開對自己的約束，任憑情感、慾望或衝動支配自己。","examples":[{"en":"After years of caution, she abandoned herself to the joy of dancing.","zh":"謹慎了多年之後，她終於盡情享受跳舞的快樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He abandoned himself to anger and said things he regretted.","zh":"他任由憤怒支配自己，說了些後來後悔的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abandon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de7c2ed356a747ec","term":"abandon","forms":["abandon","abandons","abandoning","abandoned","abandonest","abandonedst","abandoneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放棄；停止堅持","explanation":"指不再繼續做、支援或遵循某件事，例如計劃、習慣、做法、觀點或承諾；重點是把原本抓住的東西放開。","examples":[{"en":"The team abandoned the project after the costs doubled.","zh":"費用翻了一倍後，團隊放棄了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mara abandoned her campaign when her supporters withdrew.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abandon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-400bd4aa6007e1b5","term":"abandon","forms":["abandon","abandons","abandoning","abandoned","abandonest","abandonedst","abandoneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拋下；遺棄","explanation":"指把人、地點或物品留在身後，不再照料、陪伴或承擔相應責任，尤其是在困難或危險情況下離開。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers abandoned their car when the road became impassable.","zh":"道路無法通行後，徒步者們只好把汽車留在那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The owner abandoned the dog outside a shelter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abandon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a9b5995cc8158c603b2","word":"abbreviate","forms":["abbreviate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"abbreviate","forms":["abbreviate"],"pos":"v.","zh":"縮寫；縮短","examples":[{"en":"You may abbreviate the month as Jan. on this form.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Please abbreviate the title so it fits on one line.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-072469151f6451023b0c","word":"abide","forms":["abide"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-531a3462a2244cdd","term":"abide","forms":["abide","abides","abiding","abode","abided","abid","abidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忍受；容忍","explanation":"指面對自己不喜歡的人或事仍然忍著，不表現出無法承受；它延續了“站住、不退”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I can't abide people who interrupt constantly.","zh":"我受不了那些總是打斷別人說話的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She could hardly abide the noise from the construction site.","zh":"她幾乎無法忍受建築工地傳來的噪聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7ef3fe461940696","term":"abide","forms":["abide","abides","abiding","abode","abided","abid","abidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵守；遵照","explanation":"在 abide by 中，原來的“站住、不退”變成“站在規則一邊並按它行動”，所以表示接受並遵守規則、法律、決定或約定。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone must abide by the safety rules.","zh":"每個人都必須遵守安全規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both sides agreed to abide by the court's decision.","zh":"雙方同意遵從法院的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bcffaab67df49e37c9e3","word":"ability","forms":["ability"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-07371185893dbd23","term":"ability","forms":["ability","abilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"能力；能夠做某事的條件","explanation":"指完成某件事所需要的實際能力或條件，可以用於人，也可以用於裝置、系統等。它強調“具備做成這件事的可能和力量”，正像一把能開啟目標之門的鑰匙。","examples":[{"en":"This phone has the ability to update its software wirelessly.","zh":"這部手機能夠透過無線方式更新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her ability to remain calm helped the team.","zh":"她保持冷靜的能力幫助了團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c6f83904332650b","term":"ability","forms":["ability","abilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"技能；才幹","explanation":"指某人在某項活動中表現出來的具體本領、熟練程度或才幹。這裡的 ability 更像一把已經適合某扇特定門的鑰匙，因此可以指閱讀、音樂、語言等方面的能力。","examples":[{"en":"The school offers extra support for students with different abilities.","zh":"這所學校為能力水平不同的學生提供額外支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her musical ability earned her a scholarship.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0ad6bc1931197750fa8","word":"able","forms":["able"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a4d29e08e8c66d5","term":"able","forms":["able","abler","ablest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有能力做到","explanation":"指具備完成某件事所需要的力量、能力或資源，因此事情做得成；這是 able 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She is able to lift the box without assistance.","zh":"她能夠獨自搬起這個箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After resting for an hour, I was able to finish the report.","zh":"休息一小時後，我終於完成了報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/able","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-094d3862b556d7be","term":"able","forms":["able","abler","ablest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可以；不受阻礙","explanation":"指沒有規則、環境或其他障礙阻止某人做某事，所以在當時的條件下“可以做”。重點不一定是能力，而是沒有被禁止或妨礙。","examples":[{"en":"With the new system, users are able to change their passwords online.","zh":"有了新系統，使用者可以線上修改密碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Guests are able to enter after security opens the gates.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/able","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5129a4a62c66ddf286d4","word":"abnormal","forms":["abnormal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a21a9670feae859","term":"abnormal","forms":["abnormal","more abnormal","most abnormal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"偏離通常狀態的","explanation":"指不符合通常規律、標準或型別的情況，重點是“和一般情形不一樣”，不一定涉及疾病或道德問題。例如時間、數量、形狀或過程都可以是 abnormal。","examples":[{"en":"The patient showed an abnormal heart rate during the test.","zh":"病人在檢查中出現了異常的心率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had an abnormal delay because of the storm.","zh":"因為暴風雨，我們遇到了不同尋常的延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abnormal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4746278a78b6b7e","term":"abnormal","forms":["abnormal","more abnormal","most abnormal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"行為或心理狀態不合常規的","explanation":"特指行為、情感或心理狀態偏離社會通常接受的標準；它仍然是“離開正常軌道”的意思，但比一般的“不尋常”更容易帶有評判或醫學色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The report examined whether the child’s behavior was abnormal for his age.","zh":"這份報告研究了這個孩子的行為是否偏離其年齡段的正常範圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The psychologist assessed his abnormal fear of ordinary doorbells.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abnormal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4fb10800cbeeca991a6b","word":"aboard","forms":["aboard"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eec81779999860b2","term":"aboard","forms":["aboard"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在船、車、飛機上；登上其中","explanation":"表示人在船、火車、飛機等交通工具上，或正在登上、進入其中；核心畫面就是“登上甲板並留在裡面”。","examples":[{"en":"We all climbed aboard before the storm arrived.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，我們都登上了船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were already aboard when the train left.","zh":"火車開走時，孩子們已經在車上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aboard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7982b492058180e5","term":"aboard","forms":["aboard"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……上；登上……","explanation":"表示進入或處在船、火車、飛機等交通工具中，直接把交通工具當作“登上的平臺”。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone was aboard the plane before the doors closed.","zh":"艙門關閉前，所有人都已經登上飛機了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We went aboard the ferry at sunrise.","zh":"我們在日出時登上了渡船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aboard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cae1452b5d0bcb60e24","word":"abolish","forms":["abolish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d65e7446839446dc","term":"abolish","forms":["abolish","abolishes","abolishing","abolished","abolisht"],"pos":"verb","zh":"廢除；取消制度","explanation":"指透過正式行動，使一項法律、制度、習俗或長期做法不再存在。這是 abolish 最核心、最常見的意思，重點是徹底拔掉原有的制度根基。","examples":[{"en":"The government abolished the outdated law.","zh":"政府廢除了這項過時的法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country abolished the death penalty.","zh":"這個國家廢除了死刑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abolish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ac764df349506ab397f","word":"aboriginal","forms":["aboriginal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d68d96f4fcc0c67","term":"aboriginal","forms":["aboriginal","more aboriginal","most aboriginal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最初的；原生的","explanation":"指按照歷史或科學記錄最早存在的，或本來就生長、生活在某地的事物；核心畫面就是“從一開始就在這裡”。","examples":[{"en":"This tree is aboriginal to the island.","zh":"這種樹原生於這座島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers documented the aboriginal plants of the valley.","zh":"研究人員記錄了這個山谷的原生植物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aboriginal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22d9801ddadcb6e6","term":"aboriginal","forms":["aboriginal","more aboriginal","most aboriginal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"殖民前當地居民的","explanation":"指外國人殖民或大規模遷入以前就生活在某地的居民；它把“最初紮根於土地”的概念具體用於人群。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a collection about the aboriginal inhabitants of the island.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了有關該島原住民的資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They studied aboriginal settlements predating European contact.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aboriginal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b253a2520329806ed6f","word":"abortion","forms":["abortion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72b50b64e323b236","term":"abortion","forms":["abortion","abortions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人工流產","explanation":"指透過醫療方式有意終止妊娠，使尚未發育完全的胎兒不能繼續發育。這是現代英語中最常見、最重要的含義。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to have an abortion after discussing the decision with her doctor.","zh":"她和醫生討論後，決定做人工流產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new law limits access to abortion.","zh":"這項新法律限制了人們獲得人工流產服務的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abortion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9088fcb448dd776","term":"abortion","forms":["abortion","abortions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"妊娠過早終止","explanation":"指胎兒尚未發育完全，便從子宮排出並失去胎兒的情況。這是較早或較寬泛的醫學用法，現代一般語境中不如人工流產這一義常用。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor explained that the pregnancy had ended in an abortion.","zh":"醫生解釋說，這次妊娠以流產告終。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The veterinary report recorded a spontaneous abortion in the mare.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abortion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b891c3aca3b23fa5400b","word":"abound","forms":["abound"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd058ae49e692526","term":"abound","forms":["abound","abounds","abounding","abounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"大量存在；數量充足","explanation":"這是最核心的意思：人、動物、機會、問題等在某處或某種情況下大量存在，像東西不斷湧來一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Birds abound around the lake in spring.","zh":"春天湖邊有大量鳥類出沒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Opportunities abound for people with practical skills.","zh":"具備實用技能的人有很多機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c641601b74ba3ef0","term":"abound","forms":["abound","abounds","abounding","abounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"充滿；擁有大量供應","explanation":"表示某處被大量供應某物，和“東西從那裡湧出來、到處都是”的核心畫面相連；重點在某處具有豐富的某物。","examples":[{"en":"The forest abounds in mushrooms after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨過後，森林裡長滿了蘑菇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These shallow waters abound with colorful reef fish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4262e1c9bcbc1721eb3","word":"about","forms":["about"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4104a27f2e8fcfc","term":"about","forms":["about"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在周圍；環顧四周","explanation":"表示從一箇中心向四周看、移動或分佈，重點是“圍著周圍一圈”。","examples":[{"en":"She looked about before crossing the street.","zh":"她環顧四周後才過馬路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hearing footsteps, the guard turned about nervously.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/about","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ea2c38b12858900","term":"about","forms":["about"],"pos":"adv","zh":"大約；近似地","explanation":"表示數字、時間、程度或質量只是接近某個值，不要求完全準確。它像是在一個數值周圍畫出大致範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The journey takes about two hours.","zh":"這段旅程大約需要兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There were about fifty people at the meeting.","zh":"會議上大約有五十個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/about","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0811ec509b1ebe30","term":"about","forms":["about"],"pos":"prep","zh":"即將；正要","explanation":"“be about to do”表示某事已經臨近，馬上就會發生，或某人正準備做某事。它把“在某事周圍”推進到了“站在發生之前的邊緣”。","examples":[{"en":"The film is about to start.","zh":"電影馬上就要開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was about to call you when you arrived.","zh":"你到達時，我正準備給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/about","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3027c90f277e33c2","term":"about","forms":["about"],"pos":"prep","zh":"關於；涉及","explanation":"表示談話、文章、問題或感情所圍繞的主題，即“圍著某件事展開”。","examples":[{"en":"We talked about the new project after lunch.","zh":"午飯後我們談了談新專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This book is about life in a small town.","zh":"這本書講的是小鎮上的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/about","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-88c7f08d0be5407e361c","word":"above","forms":["above"],"officialPos":"prep./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0faf89275474d615","term":"above","forms":["above"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在正上方","explanation":"表示某物垂直位於另一物的上方，最直接地體現“沿豎線向上”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A bright lamp hung above the table.","zh":"一盞明亮的燈懸掛在桌子正上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A helicopter hovered above while rescuers searched below.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/above","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94b8ab685b5c8282","term":"above","forms":["above"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……上方；穿在……外面","explanation":"表示某物位於另一物上方，或衣物套在另一件衣物外層，最接近“向上的豎直關係”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a scarf above her sweater.","zh":"她在毛衣外面圍了一條圍巾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lamp hangs above the kitchen table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/above","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1809879f97e20cda","term":"above","forms":["above"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……上方；高於……表面","explanation":"表示某物處在另一個物體或地點的更高位置，是“在上方”這個核心概念最常用的介詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"A bird flew above the trees.","zh":"一隻鳥飛過樹梢上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A helicopter hovered above the flooded stadium.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/above","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-029d9afc10914c2a","term":"above","forms":["above"],"pos":"prep","zh":"高於；勝過；超過標準","explanation":"由空間上的更高引申為質量、能力、程度或保護狀態更高，表示超過某個標準或不受某種低下事物影響。","examples":[{"en":"Her work is well above average.","zh":"她的工作水平遠高於平均水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inspector considered that workmanship above the required standard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/above","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6278590a4ba1f3cea11","word":"abroad","forms":["abroad"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e8f89619cb6a0f8","term":"abroad","forms":["abroad"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在國外；到國外","explanation":"指離開本國、處在外國，或前往外國；這是 abroad 最重要、最常見的意義。它把“越過本國邊界到了外面”的畫面直接用於人的旅行、居住或活動。","examples":[{"en":"She went abroad to study architecture after finishing college.","zh":"她大學畢業後去了國外學習建築學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many young people want to work abroad for a few years.","zh":"許多年輕人想去國外工作幾年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abroad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92582ef8bdbe9cbe","term":"abroad","forms":["abroad"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在客場；在外地比賽","explanation":"在體育語境中，指球隊離開自己的主場，到對手或別的地方比賽；核心仍是“在自己的範圍之外”。","examples":[{"en":"The team has played abroad three times this season.","zh":"這支球隊本賽季已經在客場比賽過三次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our club rarely wins when playing abroad.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abroad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03e2c07ec321e5cc0679","word":"abrupt","forms":["abrupt"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78d2d2d1a74f421c","term":"abrupt","forms":["abrupt","more abrupt","abrupter","most abrupt","abruptest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"突然的；倉促結束的","explanation":"事情像被一刀切斷，事先沒有給人準備或適應的時間，因此顯得突然、倉促，有時也帶有不夠周全的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting came to an abrupt end when the fire alarm sounded.","zh":"火災警報響起後，會議突然結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her abrupt departure surprised everyone.","zh":"她突然離開讓所有人都很驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42b7da8c968a82e4","term":"abrupt","forms":["abrupt","more abrupt","abrupter","most abrupt","abruptest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"說話生硬的；唐突的","explanation":"說話沒有緩衝或客套，像把交流突然截斷，所以給人簡短、生硬、不夠體貼的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"His abrupt reply made the customer feel unwelcome.","zh":"他生硬的回答讓顧客覺得自己不受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was abrupt with me because she was under pressure.","zh":"她當時壓力很大，所以對我說話很生硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1888101dae1d8fc2c564","word":"absence","forms":["absence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f8bf0bb49c04bde","term":"absence","forms":["absence","absences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不在場；離開","explanation":"表示某人離開了原本所在的地方，或沒有和同伴在一起，強調“不在場”這一狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Her absence from the meeting was noticed by everyone.","zh":"她沒有參加會議，大家都注意到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Absence makes the heart grow fonder.","zh":"小別勝新婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ad0de1d8b67e151","term":"absence","forms":["absence","absences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"離開的一段時間","explanation":"表示某人不在的整個期間，重點不是“沒有到場”這一事實，而是這段持續的離開時間。","examples":[{"en":"During Daniel's absence, his assistant handled the calls.","zh":"丹尼爾不在期間，由他的助理接聽電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her three-month absence ended with an unexpected visit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2da2aa9ed06bb3a0","term":"absence","forms":["absence","absences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺乏；沒有","explanation":"把“人不在”引申到抽象事物：某種品質、感覺或條件本應存在，卻沒有出現，因此表示“缺乏”。","examples":[{"en":"The absence of clear instructions caused several mistakes.","zh":"由於缺少明確的指示，出現了幾處錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We enjoyed the absence of traffic noise.","zh":"沒有交通噪音讓我們感到很愜意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ad38304b535c2987dbd","word":"absent","forms":["absent"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49f33c68a6724ea9","term":"absent","forms":["absent","absenter","absentest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不在場；缺席","explanation":"指某人沒有出現在應在的地方，或某物原本應在那裡卻不在；核心就是“從現場離開了”。","examples":[{"en":"Maya was absent from work because she had a fever.","zh":"瑪雅因為發燒沒來上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several students were absent from the morning class.","zh":"有幾名學生缺席了早上的課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7099769231e13bc6","term":"absent","forms":["absent","absenter","absentest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不存在；缺少","explanation":"指某種東西、部位或特徵根本沒有出現，像是它從應在的位置上消失了。","examples":[{"en":"The report noted that the usual warning signs were absent.","zh":"報告指出，通常的警告跡象並不存在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Any mention of compensation was absent from the letter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-747355bdc2a224032fd4","word":"absolute","forms":["absolute"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39aaa437ce702a13","term":"absolute","forms":["absolute","more absolute","absoluter","most absolute","absolutest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無條件的；不受限制的","explanation":"指不受任何限制、例外、資格條件或外部規定影響的狀態。它強調“完全放開”，例如某種自由或權利沒有附加條件。","examples":[{"en":"The law does not give parents absolute freedom to choose their children's names.","zh":"法律並沒有賦予父母給孩子取名的絕對自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No leader should have absolute power.","zh":"任何領導人都不應該擁有絕對權力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absolute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdb9ba4f342d6a51","term":"absolute","forms":["absolute","more absolute","absoluter","most absolute","absolutest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完美的；完全體現某種性質的","explanation":"指某種性質達到完整、理想或最純粹的程度，幾乎沒有缺陷。這裡的重點不是“沒有條件”，而是“把某種特徵體現到了極致”。","examples":[{"en":"The design is a model of absolute simplicity.","zh":"這個設計完全體現了極簡之美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For her, absolute honesty was essential.","zh":"對她來說，徹底的誠實至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absolute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c218030dd2a12d3a","term":"absolute","forms":["absolute","more absolute","absoluter","most absolute","absolutest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"徹底的；完全的","explanation":"指某件事沒有減弱、保留或緩和，程度達到徹底的地步。它可以修飾否定、拒絕、沉默等，突出“完全沒有例外”。","examples":[{"en":"The proposal met with absolute rejection.","zh":"這項提議遭到了徹底拒絕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the announcement, the room fell into absolute silence.","zh":"公告發布後，房間裡陷入了徹底的寂靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absolute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22b090dd46c756d3c307","word":"absorb","forms":["absorb"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-736680d9c4bcdd48","term":"absorb","forms":["absorb","absorbs","absorbing","absorbed","absorpt","absorbest","absorbedst","absorbeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吞併；使不再獨立存在","explanation":"把某物完全吞沒、併入或消除，使它不再以原來的獨立形式存在；這是“吸進去直到看不見”的總義。","examples":[{"en":"The larger company absorbed its smaller competitor.","zh":"那家大公司吞併了規模較小的競爭對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The darkness absorbed the last traces of light.","zh":"黑暗吞沒了最後一點光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absorb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e45628422435b90","term":"absorb","forms":["absorb","absorbs","absorbing","absorbed","absorpt","absorbest","absorbedst","absorbeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸收；吸入","explanation":"像海綿吸水一樣把液體、氣體或其他物質吸進內部；也可指身體或化學物質把某物接納進去。","examples":[{"en":"This towel absorbs water quickly.","zh":"這條毛巾吸水很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roots absorb nutrients from the soil.","zh":"根部從土壤中吸收養分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absorb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22d7e9af20412e68","term":"absorb","forms":["absorb","absorbs","absorbing","absorbed","absorpt","absorbest","absorbedst","absorbeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使全神貫注；完全佔據注意力","explanation":"某件事把人的注意力整個“吸進去”，讓人專心到幾乎注意不到周圍其他事情。","examples":[{"en":"She was absorbed in a book and missed her stop.","zh":"她全神貫注地看書，坐過了站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were absorbed in building a sandcastle.","zh":"孩子們全神貫注地堆沙堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absorb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c59ddd3f7ba697a4b820","word":"abstract","forms":["abstract"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a5fa8f31612430e","term":"abstract","forms":["abstract","more abstract","abstracter","most abstract","abstractest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"抽象的；概念性的","explanation":"表示不直接指向某個具體的人或物，而是談一般的概念、性質或觀念。它就像把具體細節抽走，只留下可以思考的骨架。","examples":[{"en":"Justice is an abstract idea, but it affects everyone's life.","zh":"正義是一個抽象概念，但會影響每個人的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lesson moves from concrete examples to abstract principles.","zh":"這節課從具體例子講到抽象原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-55b4eea1eb77a78d6e69","word":"abstraction","forms":["abstraction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e90678987614672f","term":"abstraction","forms":["abstraction","abstractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽取特徵；抽象化","explanation":"指暫時忽略一個物件的其他細節，只把其中某個特徵單獨抽出來考察。例如不看不同物品的具體外形，只關注它們共同的“顏色”或“形狀”。","examples":[{"en":"Abstraction allows us to focus on the essential features of a problem.","zh":"抽象化讓我們能夠專注於問題的關鍵特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The model is an abstraction of the real world.","zh":"這個模型是對現實世界的一種抽象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc7dd6196ad4ec9b","term":"abstraction","forms":["abstraction","abstractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"概括；歸納","explanation":"指比較不同事物的共同點，抽掉各自的特殊細節，再按共同特徵歸成一類；也可指這種概括出來的結果。這正是從許多具體事物走向一般概念的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Through abstraction, we can treat different machines as members of the same class.","zh":"透過抽象化，我們可以把不同的機器看作同一類物件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theory is based on an abstraction from many individual cases.","zh":"這個理論建立在對許多個別案例進行概括的基礎上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36afc43e200d711a","term":"abstraction","forms":["abstraction","abstractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽象概念；理論觀念","explanation":"指脫離具體事物、主要存在於思想中的概念或觀念，例如自由、正義或數學中的物件。它是把具體經驗中的細節抽走後留下的思想。","examples":[{"en":"Freedom is not merely an abstraction for the people in this country.","zh":"對這個國家的人民來說，自由不只是一個抽象概念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children found the idea too much of an abstraction.","zh":"孩子們覺得這個想法太抽象了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abstraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5caab99c7830a1f670ea","word":"absurd","forms":["absurd"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7f114e506e69c89","term":"absurd","forms":["absurd","absurder","more absurd","absurdest","most absurd"],"pos":"adj","zh":"荒謬的；不合常理的","explanation":"指某個想法、說法或做法明顯違背常識和邏輯，荒唐到讓人覺得可笑或無法認真對待。","examples":[{"en":"It would be absurd to blame her for the mistake.","zh":"把這個錯誤歸咎於她是荒謬的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan is so absurd that nobody takes it seriously.","zh":"這個計劃荒謬得沒人當真。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absurd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3564cc0d2a502462","term":"absurd","forms":["absurd","absurder","more absurd","absurdest","most absurd"],"pos":"adj","zh":"荒誕的；缺乏意義的","explanation":"用於人生、世界或人的處境時，表示它們沒有清晰的秩序或可發現的意義，人的生活因此顯得荒誕。這裡的重點不是某一件事可笑，而是整體處境彷彿無法與合理的意義接上。","examples":[{"en":"The novel portrays people trying to live in an absurd world.","zh":"這部小說描寫了人們努力生活在一個荒誕的世界裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Beckett's characters wait for meaning in an absurd universe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/absurd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b153927875d34ea4115e","word":"abundance","forms":["abundance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fe3301dd36b85fe","term":"abundance","forms":["abundance","abundances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量；許多","explanation":"指某類東西數量很大，彷彿容器裡裝得滿滿的。它可以用於具體物品，也可以用於機會、選擇等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The library has an abundance of books for young readers.","zh":"這家圖書館有大量適合年輕讀者的書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The abundance of choices made it hard to decide.","zh":"選擇太多，反而讓人難以決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abundance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d3843d0687888dd","term":"abundance","forms":["abundance","abundances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"充沛；豐富到過量","explanation":"強調充足甚至滿溢的狀態，不只是數量多，還帶有“供應非常充足、幾乎用不完”或“多得過頭”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh fruit was available in abundance during the summer.","zh":"夏天有大量新鮮水果供應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report contains an abundance of unnecessary detail.","zh":"這份報告包含過多不必要的細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abundance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-942c4efe53ad523622de","word":"abundant","forms":["abundant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa679e326345af00","term":"abundant","forms":["abundant","more abundant","most abundant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"豐富的；充足的","explanation":"表示某種東西數量很多、供應充足，達到幾乎不擔心缺少的程度。它可以形容自然產物、資源、機會、證據等，核心畫面就是東西多得像要溢位來。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water is abundant in this mountain region.","zh":"這個山區淡水資源很豐富。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden produces abundant tomatoes every summer.","zh":"這個花園每年夏天都產出大量番茄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abundant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-151f460f2186e35d","term":"abundant","forms":["abundant","more abundant","most abundant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富有的；充滿的","explanation":"表示某人、某地或某種事物擁有大量某種東西，或充滿某種品質。它和核心義相連，只是重點從“東西很多”轉向“某個主體裡面有很多”。","examples":[{"en":"The region is abundant in wildlife and natural beauty.","zh":"這個地區擁有豐富的野生動物和自然美景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The valley is abundant in freshwater springs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abundant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a60a2bb10fad676b72cd","word":"abuse","forms":["abuse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbb7dbd912139362","term":"abuse","forms":["abuse","abuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不當行為；濫用","explanation":"指把權力、制度或某種做法用於不正當目的，造成不公或腐敗；也可指這種錯誤做法本身。","examples":[{"en":"The report exposed serious abuses of power.","zh":"這份報告揭露了嚴重的權力濫用行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law was designed to prevent abuse of the system.","zh":"這項法律旨在防止濫用這一制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea61facf860788bb","term":"abuse","forms":["abuse","abuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辱罵；粗俗言語","explanation":"指帶有侮辱、貶低或憤怒攻擊意味的粗俗話語，也可指一連串辱罵。","examples":[{"en":"The player faced a stream of abuse from the crowd.","zh":"這名運動員遭到觀眾一連串的辱罵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two neighbors exchanged abuse in the street.","zh":"兩位鄰居在街上互相辱罵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f04e0c4019879e3c","term":"abuse","forms":["abuse","abuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"虐待；殘酷對待","explanation":"指對人或動物進行身體或心理上的傷害、殘酷對待，常常不是一次偶然事件，而是持續或反覆發生的傷害。","examples":[{"en":"The charity helps children who have suffered abuse.","zh":"這個慈善機構幫助遭受過虐待的兒童。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke openly about years of emotional abuse.","zh":"她坦率地談到了多年來遭受的情感虐待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96f70aaa709dc19b","term":"abuse","forms":["abuse","abuses","abusing","abused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"濫用；誤用","explanation":"指把權力、地位、制度或某物用於不正當或錯誤的目的；核心畫面就是把原本應正常使用的東西“用歪了”。","examples":[{"en":"He abused his authority to silence his critics.","zh":"他濫用職權壓制批評他的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company abused customer data for profit.","zh":"這家公司為了獲利而濫用客戶資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ddeaede206c2789f","term":"abuse","forms":["abuse","abuses","abusing","abused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"虐待；殘酷傷害","explanation":"指反覆或嚴重地傷害、虐待某人，使其受到身體或心理上的痛苦。","examples":[{"en":"The child was abused by a trusted adult.","zh":"這個孩子受到了一名受信任的成年人的虐待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No animal should be abused or neglected.","zh":"任何動物都不應遭到虐待或忽視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5035db9824e5eb2","term":"abuse","forms":["abuse","abuses","abusing","abused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辱罵；侮辱","explanation":"指用粗俗、憤怒或惡意的語言攻擊、貶低某人。","examples":[{"en":"The caller abused the receptionist over the delay.","zh":"打電話的人因為延誤而辱罵了接待員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Drunken spectators abused the referee throughout halftime.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8a98203ec9d769d748b","word":"academic","forms":["academic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac6d9da4850bdfa6","term":"academic","forms":["academic","more academic","most academic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"學院的；學術的","explanation":"指與學院、大學、高等教育機構、學術團體或學術研究有關的事物。這是最常見的基礎義，學習、研究、課程和機構都可以用它來修飾。","examples":[{"en":"She is applying for an academic position at the university.","zh":"她正在申請那所大學的學術職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report is based on recent academic research.","zh":"這份報告以最近的學術研究為依據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/academic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6fd49a14a7ee210","term":"academic","forms":["academic","more academic","most academic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"理論性的；不實用的","explanation":"指停留在理論、推測或過度細節中的事物，與現實用途或實際行動聯絡不強。這個意思仍然來自“學院裡的理論”，只是語氣常帶有“不夠實用”的評價。","examples":[{"en":"He has an academic interest in how old machines work.","zh":"他對老機器的工作原理有理論上的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal sounds academic but offers no practical solution.","zh":"這個提案聽起來很理論化，卻沒有提供實際解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/academic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6f933f76267778a781c","word":"academy","forms":["academy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edc09a1eadaf6435","term":"academy","forms":["academy","academies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高等教育機構","explanation":"指提供較高層次教育的學院或大學，常見於私立教育機構的名稱或正式介紹中。","examples":[{"en":"She received her degree from a private academy in Boston.","zh":"她從波士頓的一所私立學院獲得了學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The naval academy awards degrees in marine engineering.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/academy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-300602fb3361c334","term":"academy","forms":["academy","academies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專門訓練學校","explanation":"指教授某種專門技能或藝術的學校、訓練場所，例如軍事、騎術、音樂或語言學校。","examples":[{"en":"He trains at a military academy in the north of the country.","zh":"他在該國北部的一所軍事學院接受訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She enrolled in a dance academy at twelve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/academy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e4158dcf700a3dd","term":"academy","forms":["academy","academies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學術界","explanation":"指由大學、研究機構和學者構成的整體，也就是圍繞知識生產和研究活動形成的學術世界。","examples":[{"en":"Many researchers move between industry and academia.","zh":"許多研究人員在企業界和學術界之間轉換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her departure sparked debate throughout the academy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/academy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70430045cb502bc00fef","word":"accelerate","forms":["accelerate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7aa4bfed787f83bc","term":"accelerate","forms":["accelerate","accelerates","accelerating","accelerated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……加速","explanation":"指讓人、車輛或其他正在運動的東西以更快的速度移動，也就是踩下“加速踏板”讓它快起來。","examples":[{"en":"The driver accelerated the car to pass the truck.","zh":"司機加速讓汽車超過了卡車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She accelerated her pace when it started to rain.","zh":"開始下雨後，她加快了腳步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accelerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a19003ca80bb1efb","term":"accelerate","forms":["accelerate","accelerates","accelerating","accelerated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加快程序","explanation":"指讓原本會逐步發生的過程更快完成，例如增長、發展或恢復被推快。這裡加快的不是單純的移動速度，而是事情推進的速度。","examples":[{"en":"The new treatment may accelerate the patient's recovery.","zh":"這種新療法可能會加快病人的康復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Warmer temperatures accelerated the ripening of the peaches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accelerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7c5019557c2de4c","term":"accelerate","forms":["accelerate","accelerates","accelerating","accelerated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"自己加速","explanation":"指人、車輛或其他運動中的東西自身變得更快，重點是主語發生了速度變化，而不是主語讓別的東西變快。","examples":[{"en":"The train began to accelerate after leaving the station.","zh":"火車離站後開始加速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclist accelerated down the hill.","zh":"騎腳踏車的人加速衝下山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accelerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3a7f053ae2eadb1fb93","word":"accent","forms":["accent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8571bcf16c88eb98","term":"accent","forms":["accent","accents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重音","explanation":"在一個詞或短語裡，某個音節因為更響、更長或音高更突出而成為重點，這個突出位置就是 accent。","examples":[{"en":"The accent in \"computer\" is on the second syllable.","zh":"“computer”的重音在第二個音節上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to put the accent on the first syllable.","zh":"試著把重音放在第一個音節上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78752b312a1bb663","term":"accent","forms":["accent","accents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重點；強調","explanation":"它可以從聲音上的突出引申為一般意義上的“把注意力或重要性集中到某處”。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy puts an accent on public safety.","zh":"新政策把重點放在公共安全上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accent is on simplicity in this design.","zh":"這個設計強調簡潔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f92ae2ad21c1fc66","term":"accent","forms":["accent","accents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口音","explanation":"一個地區、社會群體或母語背景長期形成的獨特發音方式，就是某人的 accent；外國人說英語時留下的發音特點也可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"She speaks English with a slight French accent.","zh":"她說英語時帶有一點法國口音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I could tell from his accent that he was from the north.","zh":"我從他的口音聽出他來自北方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c125d0397b605657bc89","word":"accept","forms":["accept"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abe4b81316ca1035","term":"accept","forms":["accept","accepts","accepting","accepted","acceptest","acceptedst","accepteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"接受並認可","explanation":"把某物接過來並表示願意接受，常帶有贊同、認可或不拒絕的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She accepted the gift with a smile.","zh":"她微笑著接受了禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I gladly accept your help.","zh":"我很樂意接受你的幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accept","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a67ca858d454356","term":"accept","forms":["accept","accepts","accepting","accepted","acceptest","acceptedst","accepteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承認屬實","explanation":"把某個說法、觀點或事實看作合理、真實或可以相信，就像在心裡把它接納下來。","examples":[{"en":"I accept that mistakes happen.","zh":"我承認錯誤是會發生的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She accepts the explanation as true.","zh":"她認可這個解釋是真的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accept","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdaa1c5a79b4c926","term":"accept","forms":["accept","accepts","accepting","accepted","acceptest","acceptedst","accepteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"同意提議","explanation":"接下對方提出的條件、建議、請求或解釋，表示同意照此辦理。","examples":[{"en":"He accepted the job offer immediately.","zh":"他立即接受了這份工作邀請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They accepted our proposal.","zh":"他們接受了我們的提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accept","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-129b70f8672ecacafe6a","word":"acceptable","forms":["acceptable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc670310dbf102cc","term":"acceptable","forms":["acceptable","more acceptable","most acceptable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可以接受的","explanation":"指某人或某物達到基本要求，因此能夠被接受或得到認可，通常帶有中性或略正面的評價。","examples":[{"en":"We need to find an acceptable present for Jeff.","zh":"我們得找一份傑夫能接受的禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposed solution is acceptable to everyone on the team.","zh":"團隊裡的每個人都能接受這個提出的解決方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acceptable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f8978004dc6ff68","term":"acceptable","forms":["acceptable","more acceptable","most acceptable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"還過得去的","explanation":"指質量或表現雖然不突出，甚至低於理想水平，但仍達到可以透過或使用的程度；核心仍是“過了接受標準這道門”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel was acceptable, but the room was smaller than we expected.","zh":"這家酒店還過得去，但房間比我們預想的小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soup was acceptable, though rather bland.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acceptable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1514c6cdad166c18aa5","word":"acceptance","forms":["acceptance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4c26b8106d84467","term":"acceptance","forms":["acceptance","acceptances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接受；認可","explanation":"指把別人提供的東西、職位、觀點或安排接納下來，並帶有同意、贊同或滿意的意味。重點不是單純“收到”，而是願意接受它。","examples":[{"en":"Her acceptance of the offer surprised everyone.","zh":"她接受了那份提議，讓大家都很驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The acceptance of new ideas takes time.","zh":"接受新想法需要時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acceptance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-777ff91739c7f190","term":"acceptance","forms":["acceptance","acceptances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相信；同意","explanation":"指接受某個觀點、解釋或說法，認為它是可以相信或認可的；這裡接納的是思想，而不是物品。","examples":[{"en":"There is growing acceptance of the evidence.","zh":"越來越多人認可這些證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theory gained acceptance among scientists.","zh":"這個理論逐漸得到科學家的認可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acceptance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-378de1035da6de8d","term":"acceptance","forms":["acceptance","acceptances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被接受的狀態","explanation":"指某人或某事已經得到他人、群體或社會的接納和認可，強調結果狀態。它可以是“被接納”的社會或心理狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The child worked hard to gain acceptance from her classmates.","zh":"這個孩子努力爭取同學們的接納。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Acceptance within the community took several years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acceptance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0561fd649cdb6baa784","word":"access","forms":["access"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55472367fc1eeea3","term":"access","forms":["access","accesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進入的通道","explanation":"指通向某地或某物的入口、道路或其他方式，重點是“怎樣進去或接觸到裡面”。","examples":[{"en":"This gate provides access to the garden.","zh":"這扇門通向花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tunnel gives workers access to the lower level.","zh":"這條隧道讓工人能夠到達較低樓層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/access","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1bfdc5d79ed287b","term":"access","forms":["access","accesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進入或使用的權利","explanation":"指被允許進入某地、接觸某人或使用某項資源的權利或機會；重點是“有沒有資格或許可”。","examples":[{"en":"Only authorized staff have access to these files.","zh":"只有獲授權的工作人員才能訪問這些檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum gives visitors access to its research library.","zh":"這座博物館允許參觀者使用它的研究圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/access","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cdf30b76d2809a8","term":"access","forms":["access","accesses","accessing","accessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲得進入或使用機會","explanation":"指設法進入某處，或取得使用某項資源、服務的機會；它把“拿到鑰匙並進去”的整體動作說成一個動詞。","examples":[{"en":"Employees can access the training materials from home.","zh":"員工可以在家訪問培訓材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She accessed the building with a temporary pass.","zh":"她用臨時通行證進入了這棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/access","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89c683ba0c58f5476cbf","word":"accessible","forms":["accessible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c43b5b38986b2265","term":"accessible","forms":["accessible","more accessible","most accessible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易到達的","explanation":"指地點或路線容易接近、進入，不需要克服很大的距離、障礙或困難；這是“門容易推開”這一核心形象的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The village is accessible by train.","zh":"這個村莊坐火車就能到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trail is accessible even in winter.","zh":"這條小徑即使在冬天也容易走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accessible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80f89ff92f67e84b","term":"accessible","forms":["accessible","more accessible","most accessible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無障礙的","explanation":"特指建築、網站、裝置或服務等經過設計，使殘障人士也能較方便地使用或進入；可以看作“這扇門對更多人開放”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has accessible entrances and elevators.","zh":"這座博物館設有無障礙入口和電梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app is accessible to users with visual impairments.","zh":"這款應用便於視障使用者使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accessible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f306223ed74a46b4","term":"accessible","forms":["accessible","more accessible","most accessible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易理解或欣賞的","explanation":"指文章、音樂、藝術作品或觀點不太難懂，普通讀者或聽眾也容易進入其中；抽象內容也像一扇沒有門檻的門。","examples":[{"en":"The book explains complex science in an accessible way.","zh":"這本書用容易理解的方式解釋複雜的科學知識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her music is accessible to listeners of all ages.","zh":"她的音樂各個年齡段的聽眾都容易欣賞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accessible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a460acdb952873b50ef","word":"accessory","forms":["accessory"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34b41a1d2b1ca33e","term":"accessory","forms":["accessory","more accessory","most accessory"],"pos":"adj","zh":"附加的；輔助的","explanation":"指不是主體、但附著在主體旁邊並提供補充或幫助的；可以形容功能、物品或作用。","examples":[{"en":"The store sells accessory equipment for camping.","zh":"這家商店出售露營用的輔助裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A scarf can be an accessory garment in cold weather.","zh":"天氣冷時，圍巾可以算作一種輔助性衣物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accessory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2660fe69ed44e7b","term":"accessory","forms":["accessory","accessories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"配件；附屬物","explanation":"指屬於某個主要物品、依附於它並起補充作用的東西，例如手機配件或裝置附件。","examples":[{"en":"The phone comes with several useful accessories.","zh":"這部手機附帶幾件實用的配件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought accessories for my new camera.","zh":"我給新相機買了一些配件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accessory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-899c67db19be99d7","term":"accessory","forms":["accessory","accessories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服飾配飾","explanation":"指用來搭配基本服裝、完善整體穿著的小件物品，如圍巾、手套或包。","examples":[{"en":"She chose simple accessories to match her dress.","zh":"她選了簡潔的配飾來搭配裙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A silk scarf was her only bright accessory.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accessory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5489eb1d2a0285016de3","word":"accident","forms":["accident"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5180835d01d7f694","term":"accident","forms":["accident","accidents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意外事件","explanation":"指並非當事人有意造成、卻帶來不良後果的事件。它是最寬的核心意思，交通事故只是其中一種；重點是事情突然發生，而且結果通常不理想。","examples":[{"en":"She broke the vase in an accident while moving the table.","zh":"她搬桌子時意外打破了花瓶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one was hurt, but the accident damaged the store entrance.","zh":"沒有人受傷，但這起意外損壞了商店入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd5d4665d2279a43","term":"accident","forms":["accident","accidents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交通事故","explanation":"指車輛、飛機等交通工具相撞或失事，導致交通工具受損，並可能造成附近人員受傷或死亡。這是日常新聞和對話中非常常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A truck accident blocked both lanes for nearly an hour.","zh":"一場卡車事故堵住了兩條車道，持續了將近一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accident left a motorcycle wedged beneath the van.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1d49246a90e3dade064","word":"accidental","forms":["accidental"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02798ac0d21714a7","term":"accidental","forms":["accidental","more accidental","most accidental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非本質的；附帶的","explanation":"指某個性質、因素或結果不是事物本質的一部分，只是附帶存在或次要的。核心觀念是它偏離了事物的“主幹”，但並不決定事物是什麼。","examples":[{"en":"The color is accidental and does not affect the design.","zh":"顏色只是附帶因素，並不影響設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ownership is essential; the owner's height is accidental.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accidental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef402f511324b0b8","term":"accidental","forms":["accidental","more accidental","most accidental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"偶然的；無意的","explanation":"指事情碰巧發生，或沒有按照通常計劃發生，尤其常表示行為不是故意的。它仍然體現“偏離預定路線”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The damage was accidental, not deliberate.","zh":"這次損壞是意外造成的，不是故意的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An accidental click closed the document.","zh":"一次無意的點選把文件關掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accidental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d09f9f72a9a0becbe1a","word":"acclaim","forms":["acclaim"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-337214922f686283","term":"acclaim","forms":["acclaim","acclaims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喝彩；讚譽","explanation":"指人們公開而熱烈的讚揚，既可以指一陣喝彩聲，也可以指某人或某事獲得的廣泛認可；它正是“喊出讚美聲”這一核心畫面的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The young director won international acclaim for her first film.","zh":"這位年輕導演的第一部電影贏得了國際讚譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her translation brought her widespread critical acclaim.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acclaim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1b48be56c4fd8ae","term":"acclaim","forms":["acclaim","acclaims","acclaiming","acclaimed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"高度讚揚","explanation":"指公開而熱烈地認可某人、作品或成就，像人群用喝彩聲把它托起來一樣；這是現代英語中最重要的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Critics acclaimed the novel as a major work of contemporary fiction.","zh":"評論家稱讚這部小說是當代小說中的重要作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chef was acclaimed for bringing fresh ideas to traditional cuisine.","zh":"這位廚師因給傳統菜餚帶來新想法而廣受讚譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acclaim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87b477dbf62042149950","word":"accommodate","forms":["accommodate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb8af3a8859754bb","term":"accommodate","forms":["accommodate","accommodates","accommodating","accommodated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使適應；使相合","explanation":"把人、計劃或做法調整到適合當前情況的狀態，使它們能夠配合起來。也可以說一個人主動改變自己來適應環境。","examples":[{"en":"She quickly accommodated herself to the new schedule.","zh":"她很快適應了新的時間安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The design was changed to accommodate the needs of older users.","zh":"設計經過修改，以適應年長使用者的需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accommodate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce366d95b50757b6","term":"accommodate","forms":["accommodate","accommodates","accommodating","accommodated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"容納；裝得下","explanation":"某個地方、容器或場所能夠舒適地裝下或接待一定數量的人或物。","examples":[{"en":"This hall can accommodate five hundred people.","zh":"這個大廳可以容納500人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box is large enough to accommodate all the cables.","zh":"這個盒子足夠大，可以裝下所有電纜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accommodate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a05744e1bf9b659d8b0c","word":"accommodation","forms":["accommodation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5257bc6c8cdfb1d6","term":"accommodation","forms":["accommodation","accommodations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"住宿；住處","explanation":"指旅客、囚犯等獲得的居住空間或住宿安排。這裡的核心畫面是“把人安排到一個可以住的地方”。","examples":[{"en":"We need to book accommodation near the station.","zh":"我們需要預訂車站附近的住宿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel provides comfortable accommodation for families.","zh":"這家酒店為家庭提供舒適的住宿條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accommodation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13cead64829e2765","term":"accommodation","forms":["accommodation","accommodations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"適應性調整","explanation":"指把身體、物體或安排調整到適合某種條件或功能的狀態，也就是“為了合適而改變”。","examples":[{"en":"The design includes accommodation for people with limited mobility.","zh":"這項設計考慮了行動不便者的需要並作出了相應調整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The body makes rapid accommodation to changes in temperature.","zh":"身體會迅速調整以適應溫度變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accommodation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca661cc657cf16dfe419","word":"accompany","forms":["accompany"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72ac946d5f63b0ce","term":"accompany","forms":["accompany","accompanies","accompanying","accompanied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"陪同；伴隨同行","explanation":"指陪著某人一起去某處或一起做某件事，重點是“跟在旁邊同行”。","examples":[{"en":"Her brother accompanied her to the doctor's appointment.","zh":"她哥哥陪她去看醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A guide accompanied us during the mountain hike.","zh":"徒步爬山期間，一名嚮導陪著我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accompany","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1dcf03267ed5069","term":"accompany","forms":["accompany","accompanies","accompanying","accompanied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"伴隨著；為……增添","explanation":"指某種聲音、感覺或附加因素跟著另一件事出現，使整體內容更豐富或影響更強。","examples":[{"en":"A sense of relief accompanied the good news.","zh":"這個好訊息伴隨著一種如釋重負的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thunder accompanied the sudden downpour.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accompany","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07142b7d74a8192f9113","word":"accomplish(ment)","forms":["accomplish","accomplishment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0f74b87539f2a87","term":"accomplish","forms":["accomplish","accomplishes","accomplishing","accomplished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成功完成","explanation":"指把一項任務或事情順利做完，強調結果已經完成並取得成功，而不只是開始做或做過一部分。","examples":[{"en":"She accomplished the task before dinner.","zh":"她在晚飯前成功完成了這項任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With careful planning, we accomplished everything on time.","zh":"透過周密計劃，我們按時完成了所有事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accomplish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac1f43103e3d048d","term":"accomplish","forms":["accomplish","accomplishes","accomplishing","accomplished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"實現目標；履行承諾","explanation":"指把計劃、目標、願望或承諾落實並完成，強調原先設定的事情最終變成了現實。","examples":[{"en":"The team accomplished its main goal this year.","zh":"這個團隊今年實現了主要目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kept working until he accomplished his promise.","zh":"他一直努力，直到兌現了自己的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accomplish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0229269c388096f","term":"accomplishment","forms":["accomplishment","accomplishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完成；實現","explanation":"指把一件計劃中的事做完、使目標實現，重點在“完成這件事”這一過程或事實，而不一定強調成果有多了不起。","examples":[{"en":"The accomplishment of the project took nearly two years.","zh":"這個專案的完成花了將近兩年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team celebrated the accomplishment of its main goal.","zh":"團隊慶祝了主要目標的實現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accomplishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec699df3303dbdb4","term":"accomplishment","forms":["accomplishment","accomplishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成就；成果","explanation":"指已經做成、並且值得肯定的一件事或一個成果；它是前面“完成”之後留下的、可以被別人認可的結果。","examples":[{"en":"Finishing the marathon was a major accomplishment for her.","zh":"跑完馬拉松對她來說是一項重大成就。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Restoring the ruined chapel became the village's proudest accomplishment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accomplishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4ef49fb50c0c07d2102","word":"accord","forms":["accord"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df7f022e9f42596b","term":"accord","forms":["accord","accords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一致；意見相合","explanation":"指兩方或多人在意見、意願或行動上彼此一致，像不同的心思對上了同一個方向。","examples":[{"en":"The committee acted in accord with the wishes of the residents.","zh":"委員會按照居民的意願行事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two reports are in accord on the main facts.","zh":"兩份報告在主要事實方面是一致的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-114c123276e1536d","term":"accord","forms":["accord","accords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自願；主動意願","explanation":"主要出現在 of one's own accord 中，表示沒有人要求或強迫，某人憑自己的意願主動去做某事。","examples":[{"en":"No one asked Maya to help; she came of her own accord.","zh":"沒人要求瑪雅幫忙；她是自願來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child apologized of his own accord.","zh":"那個孩子主動道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9362cec3c0e673b","term":"accord","forms":["accord","accords","according","accorded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相符；和諧","explanation":"指兩件事彼此吻合、協調，或人的言語和內心一致；核心仍是“對上了”。","examples":[{"en":"Her explanation accords with the evidence.","zh":"她的解釋與證據相符。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His actions do not accord with his promises.","zh":"他的行為與承諾並不一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec805d17ad4f6cf298cd","word":"accordance","forms":["accordance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-293c66a4b4f1cf63","term":"accordance","forms":["accordance","accordances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"符合；遵照；一致","explanation":"表示某人的行為、決定或某件事與法律、規則、要求或約定對齊，因此可以理解為“按照……辦”或“與……一致”。","examples":[{"en":"The work was completed in accordance with the safety regulations.","zh":"這項工作是按照安全規定完成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The payment will be made in accordance with the terms of the contract.","zh":"付款將按照合同條款進行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accordance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d6d9986d16de724ac00","word":"accordingly","forms":["accordingly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8b0403396694b1d","term":"accordingly","forms":["accordingly","more accordingly","most accordingly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"相應地；適當地","explanation":"前面的情況決定了後面的做法，後面的行動因此與實際需要相匹配。它強調“根據情況採取合適的行動”，不一定表示前後有嚴格的因果關係。","examples":[{"en":"The room was too cold, so we dressed accordingly.","zh":"房間太冷了，所以我們相應地多穿了些衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the instructions carefully and plan accordingly.","zh":"請仔細閱讀說明，並據此作出相應安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accordingly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec8c843c69aaacc7","term":"accordingly","forms":["accordingly","more accordingly","most accordingly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"因此；於是","explanation":"前面已經說出的事實自然推出後面的結果，可以把它理解為“既然如此，接下來就這樣”。這是“相應地”這一核心概念在邏輯連線上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The weather forecast warned of heavy rain. Accordingly, the match was postponed.","zh":"天氣預報警告會有大雨，因此比賽被推遲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge was closed; accordingly, we took the ferry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accordingly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9af211329b2fc82e5efe","word":"account","forms":["account"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8aec01b5c3118cd","term":"account","forms":["account","accounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賬目；賬單記錄","explanation":"指把收入、支出、債務、信用等事項記錄並核算出來的賬目，也可以指對某類事情進行整理和審查的書面記錄。","examples":[{"en":"The company hired an auditor to check its accounts.","zh":"這家公司聘請了審計員來核查賬目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The annual accounts show a small loss.","zh":"年度賬目顯示有一筆小額虧損。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/account","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-054c55b270027de0","term":"account","forms":["account","accounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解釋；說明","explanation":"指對某件事為什麼發生、某人為什麼這樣做，或某種現象如何產生作出說明。它強調給出原因、依據或解釋框架，而不只是講述經過。","examples":[{"en":"The report gives an account of why the project failed.","zh":"這份報告說明了專案失敗的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are still looking for a convincing account of the results.","zh":"科學家仍在尋找一個令人信服的結果解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/account","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4eeea07e2ac3048","term":"account","forms":["account","accounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"註冊賬戶","explanation":"指某個系統中為特定使用者登記的身份和訪問許可權，使用者可以用它登入並使用服務。","examples":[{"en":"You need an account to save your settings.","zh":"你需要註冊一個賬戶才能儲存設定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't log in to my account after changing my password.","zh":"我改了密碼後無法登入我的賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/account","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2fca19e7d36a5ad","term":"account","forms":["account","accounts","accounting","accounted","accountest","accountedst","accounteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說明原因；佔據；考慮到","explanation":"在 account for 中，核心都是“把某件事算進解釋裡”：可以說明原因或解釋某個數字，也可以表示某部分佔總數的一部分；在 account for someone 中還可表示對某人的去向或行為負責、作出交代。","examples":[{"en":"This factor accounts for most of the difference in cost.","zh":"這個因素解釋了成本差異的大部分原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Online sales now account for nearly half of our revenue.","zh":"如今線上銷售額約佔我們收入的一半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/account","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80380aa41a90c033dcc1","word":"accountable","forms":["accountable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c5e45ce2b3420b5","term":"accountable","forms":["accountable","more accountable","most accountable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對行為負責","explanation":"指某人必須對自己的行為、決定或造成的結果作出說明，並接受相關人的追問或評價；重點是“有責任交代”，不一定意味著已經犯錯。","examples":[{"en":"Managers are accountable to the board for their decisions.","zh":"經理們要向董事會說明自己的決定並承擔責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each employee is accountable for the quality of their work.","zh":"每名員工都要對自己的工作質量負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accountable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93d99100f4824376","term":"accountable","forms":["accountable","more accountable","most accountable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對賬目或財物負責","explanation":"特指某人負責保管財物、處理資金或儲存記錄，因此必須把賬目記準確，並能說明每筆錢或每件物品的去向。","examples":[{"en":"The treasurer is accountable for all the club's funds.","zh":"財務負責人要對俱樂部的全部資金負責，並能交代資金去向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cashier remains accountable for the money until the next shift arrives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accountable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29d8c99ec25b271007f0","word":"accountant","forms":["accountant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d2ee95a8740a933","term":"accountant","forms":["accountant","accountants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負責賬務的專業人員","explanation":"指熟悉賬目處理、維護或調整的人，也可以是在公共機構中負責管理賬目的工作人員；這是“有人守住並解釋賬目”這一核心形象的典型體現。","examples":[{"en":"The company accountant prepares a monthly report for the director.","zh":"公司的會計每月為主管準備一份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our accountant found two invoices entered twice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accountant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0e4ea11f3afdebd","term":"accountant","forms":["accountant","accountants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負責整理和審計記錄的會計人員","explanation":"現代最常見的職業義，指替個人或機構組織、維護並核查記錄的人，記錄通常是財務賬目，但也可以包括其他正式記錄；核心仍是把賬和記錄管理清楚。","examples":[{"en":"We hired an accountant to organize the business records and prepare the tax return.","zh":"我們聘請了一名會計來整理商業記錄並準備納稅申報表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our accountant found several unpaid invoices in the records.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accountant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a31aefa266db9cca794","word":"accounting","forms":["accounting"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b4f9413840ad1a3","term":"accounting","forms":["accounting","accountings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"會計；財務核算","explanation":"指建立並使用一套方法，記錄、整理和分析個人或企業的財務交易及財務狀況。它把“錢從哪裡來、到哪裡去”算清並留下可檢查的記錄。","examples":[{"en":"Good accounting helps a small business control its costs.","zh":"良好的會計核算能幫助小企業控制成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company changed its accounting system last year.","zh":"這家公司去年更換了會計系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accounting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d1d52c3d18efcfdc850","word":"accumulate","forms":["accumulate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da405b9a86d86465","term":"accumulate","forms":["accumulate","accumulates","accumulating","accumulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"積累；聚集","explanation":"指把東西一點點聚到一起，既可以是實際物品，也可以是金錢、經驗、證據等抽象事物；重點是數量逐步堆起來，而不是一次性得到。","examples":[{"en":"She worked for years to accumulate enough money for a house.","zh":"她工作了很多年，逐漸積攢了足夠買房的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dust had accumulated in the corners of the room.","zh":"房間的角落裡已經積了不少灰塵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accumulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2df50e51cd909d1c","term":"accumulate","forms":["accumulate","accumulates","accumulating","accumulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸增加","explanation":"指某種數量或問題自己越變越多，像一堆東西不斷變高；常用於債務、壓力、證據、經驗等會隨時間增長的事物。","examples":[{"en":"By the end of the month, unpaid bills had begun to accumulate.","zh":"到了月底，未支付的賬單開始越積越多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Snow accumulated against the locked basement door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accumulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d904d3b531e6e77a4ca7","word":"accumulation","forms":["accumulation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-557f1459b2bc7202","term":"accumulation","forms":["accumulation","accumulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"積累；聚集","explanation":"指把東西一點點聚攏、收集起來的行為或過程，重點在“不斷積起來”。物件可以是物品，也可以是財富、問題等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The accumulation of savings allowed her to buy a house.","zh":"積累下來的儲蓄讓她買得起一套房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of data accumulation have improved the study.","zh":"多年來的資料積累改善了這項研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accumulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2eeb0dfd2a154b7f","term":"accumulation","forms":["accumulation","accumulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"逐漸增多；積成大堆","explanation":"指某物持續增加，最終變成數量很大的堆積或總量；可以是沙土、財富，也可以是不好的事情等。","examples":[{"en":"The accumulation of snow blocked the mountain road.","zh":"積雪越積越多，堵住了山路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A gradual accumulation of small errors caused the system to fail.","zh":"小錯誤逐漸積累，最終導致系統失靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accumulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5879092f86c5e019a15c","word":"accuracy","forms":["accuracy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d7841d069ef1cb5","term":"accuracy","forms":["accuracy","accuracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正確性；無誤程度","explanation":"指資訊、判斷、說法、計算或做法沒有錯誤、與事實相符的程度。重點是“做對了多少”，因此可以用於非常廣泛的日常和正式場景。","examples":[{"en":"We checked the accuracy of the report before publishing it.","zh":"我們在釋出報告前檢查了它的準確性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accuracy of her prediction surprised everyone.","zh":"她預測的準確性讓所有人都感到驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accuracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cefbdafb752d2eb","term":"accuracy","forms":["accuracy","accuracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"與真實值或標準的符合度","explanation":"指測量值、記錄、證詞或其他結果與真實情況、規定標準或基準值相符合的程度。它是“放到標準尺上比較”的準確性，常用於資料、儀器和事實核對。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers tested the accuracy of the new measuring device.","zh":"研究人員測試了這種新測量裝置的準確性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the scale's accuracy against a known weight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accuracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10cdb6d6fe701fe6c1bf","word":"accurate","forms":["accurate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58eff3a05dd6453d","term":"accurate","forms":["accurate","more accurate","most accurate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"準確的；精確的","explanation":"指資訊、答案、計算結果或測量結果與事實相符，沒有實質性錯誤，就像校準好的尺子量得很準。","examples":[{"en":"The report provides accurate information about the accident.","zh":"這份報告提供了關於這起事故的準確資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The calculator gave an accurate result.","zh":"計算器給出了準確的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accurate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-450fa72fe1b34339","term":"accurate","forms":["accurate","more accurate","most accurate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"偏差很小的；說得準的","explanation":"強調結果不一定絕對完美，但與真實情況非常接近，偏差在可以接受的範圍內；因此預測、描述或估計也可以是 accurate。","examples":[{"en":"Her estimate of the repair cost was surprisingly accurate.","zh":"她對維修費用的估計準確得出人意料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His estimate proved accurate within two millimeters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accurate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35bf75021158f423286b","word":"accusation","forms":["accusation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5720756b2f7a398d","term":"accusation","forms":["accusation","accusations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指責行為","explanation":"指責某人、把責任歸到某人身上的行為本身；重點在“提出指責”這個動作，而不一定已經形成具體罪名。","examples":[{"en":"She made an accusation against her manager during the meeting.","zh":"她在會議上指責了自己的經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His accusation destroyed the trust between the brothers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accusation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80b5fbbae0e1506c","term":"accusation","forms":["accusation","accusations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式控罪","explanation":"指在法庭或法律程式中正式提出的控罪，像是把“某人有錯”的指責寫入法律檔案，成為需要處理的案件內容。","examples":[{"en":"The court dismissed the accusation for lack of evidence.","zh":"由於證據不足，法院駁回了這項控罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Prosecutors withdrew the accusation after reviewing the footage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accusation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-208f5f7857b8d322","term":"accusation","forms":["accusation","accusations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未經證實的指控","explanation":"指聲稱某人做了壞事或犯了錯，但這個說法本身未必已經得到證明；它可以是日常爭執中的指責，也可以出現在新聞或正式爭論中。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper published several unfounded accusations against the actor.","zh":"那家報紙刊登了幾項針對這名演員的毫無根據的指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accusation collapsed when witnesses checked their calendars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accusation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-603ec1f360e298520b39","word":"accuse","forms":["accuse"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac34d0fc36655998","term":"accuse","forms":["accuse","accuses","accusing","accused","accusest","accusedst","accuseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指責；歸咎","explanation":"表示認為某人做錯了事，並把責任歸到他身上，不一定涉及犯罪。它是“把過錯指向某人”這一核心概念最一般的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She accused me of ignoring her messages.","zh":"她指責我無視了她的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He accused his brother of breaking the window.","zh":"他指責弟弟打破了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ac42b2deb47da52","term":"accuse","forms":["accuse","accuses","accusing","accused","accusest","accusedst","accuseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指控犯罪或違法","explanation":"表示正式或嚴肅地說某人實施了犯罪或其他違法行為，把具體罪名指到他身上。這是“指責”在法律語境中的強化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The police accused him of stealing the car.","zh":"警方指控他偷了那輛汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was accused of fraud but denied the charge.","zh":"她被指控欺詐，但否認這一指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f42e528e3a41a75fb375","word":"accustom","forms":["accustom"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"accustom","forms":["accustom"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使習慣於","examples":[{"en":"We must accustom the puppy to being alone for short periods.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A few practice sessions will accustom you to the new controls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f7111e5e2ef50b5711d","word":"ache","forms":["ache"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0b1748f2536f03d","term":"ache","forms":["ache","aches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隱痛；持續疼痛","explanation":"指持續一段時間、強度通常不突兀的疼痛，例如肌肉、牙齒或身體某處一直隱隱作痛。它和突然刺痛或一陣陣痙攣式疼痛形成對比。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a dull ache in my shoulder after carrying the boxes.","zh":"搬完箱子後，我感到肩膀隱隱作痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A persistent ache kept her from sleeping comfortably.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ache","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-048670295e8ab3fb","term":"ache","forms":["ache","aches","aching","ached","oke","aken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持續疼痛；感到隱痛","explanation":"表示身體某處持續而隱隱地痛，也可表示人因疼痛或憂苦而難受。它和名詞ache共享同一個核心畫面：疼痛不是突然閃過，而是拖著不散。","examples":[{"en":"My legs ached for two days after the long hike.","zh":"長途徒步後，我的腿疼了兩天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His jaw ached whenever he chewed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ache","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25f93ec7450364a91cb1","word":"achieve(ment)","forms":["achieve","achievement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c174c939a7262e6","term":"achieve","forms":["achieve","achieves","achieving","achieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取得成功；表現出色","explanation":"指在某方面做得成功，尤其常用於學習、考試或工作表現。這裡重點不是完成某一個具體動作，而是最終達到了較好的成績或水平。","examples":[{"en":"She achieved excellent results in her final exams.","zh":"她在期末考試中取得了優異成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With patient coaching, even hesitant students can achieve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/achieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d32869a61c1be91","term":"achieve","forms":["achieve","achieves","achieving","achieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成功完成；做到","explanation":"指經過努力把一件任務或計劃成功做成，強調“做到了”以及結果令人滿意。賓語可以是目標、計劃、改變或某項成就。","examples":[{"en":"With careful planning, the team achieved its goal.","zh":"透過周密計劃，團隊實現了目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can achieve anything if you put your mind to it.","zh":"只要你專心去做，就能實現任何目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/achieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43b123cbff197c2c","term":"achieve","forms":["achieve","achieves","achieving","achieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲得；實現（目標或成果）","explanation":"指透過努力贏得或獲得想要的結果，例如名聲、成功、地位或某個目標。與“成功完成”相近，但更突出最後得到的成果。","examples":[{"en":"The young scientist achieved international recognition.","zh":"這位年輕科學家獲得了國際認可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After years of training, he achieved his dream of becoming a pilot.","zh":"經過多年的訓練，他實現了成為飛行員的夢想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/achieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c5cb7e59635dca5","term":"achievement","forms":["achievement","achievements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成就；成果","explanation":"指完成某件事、達到某個目標後取得的成功結果，既可以是一項具體成果，也可以泛指取得成功這件事。","examples":[{"en":"Building the new library was a major achievement for the small town.","zh":"建成這座新圖書館是這個小鎮的一項重大成就。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her achievements in science have earned her international respect.","zh":"她在科學領域取得的成就贏得了國際尊重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/achievement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9746175951a5d2a0","term":"achievement","forms":["achievement","achievements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英勇功績；壯舉","explanation":"當完成的事情特別困難、危險或需要勇氣時，achievement可強調它是一項值得稱道的壯舉或功績。","examples":[{"en":"Crossing the mountains alone was an extraordinary achievement.","zh":"獨自翻越群山是一項非凡的壯舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their rescue of the trapped climbers was an extraordinary achievement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/achievement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae5eebff12dd75af2fc9","word":"acid","forms":["acid"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da5ca12f27098b1b","term":"acid","forms":["acid","acider","acidest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"酸的；有酸味的","explanation":"指食物或飲料嚐起來像醋一樣酸，核心畫面就是酸味在舌頭上帶來的尖銳刺激。","examples":[{"en":"The acid berries made my mouth water.","zh":"這些酸漿果酸得讓我直流口水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The acid juice needed a spoonful of sugar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0a5bf6966d555c1","term":"acid","forms":["acid","acider","acidest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"酸性的；與酸有關的","explanation":"指物質、環境或性質屬於酸，重點不是嚐起來酸，而是具有化學上的酸性。","examples":[{"en":"Some plants grow well in acid soil.","zh":"有些植物在酸性土壤中長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Acid solutions gradually dissolved the limestone sample.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9386f5af56df951c","term":"acid","forms":["acid","acids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酸；有酸味的物質","explanation":"指嚐起來酸的物質，或概括地指能帶來酸味的東西；這是由“酸的”直接名詞化形成的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The acid in the lemon gives the sauce its sharp taste.","zh":"檸檬裡的酸使這道醬汁帶有鮮明的酸味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spilled acid ate through the metal tray.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee3a539c0e6b9996665c","word":"acknowledge(ment)","forms":["acknowledge"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17f0bf99677e8975","term":"acknowledge","forms":["acknowledge","acknowledges","acknowledging","acknowledged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承認事實","explanation":"指承認某件事確實存在、發生，或承認某個說法是真實的；重點是把心裡知道的事實明確說出來。","examples":[{"en":"The company acknowledged that the mistake had caused serious problems.","zh":"公司承認這個錯誤造成了嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She acknowledged the risks before making her decision.","zh":"她在作出決定前承認了其中的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acknowledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efebbb43c054d7d3","term":"acknowledge","forms":["acknowledge","acknowledges","acknowledging","acknowledged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認可身份或地位","explanation":"指承認某人具備某種身份、品質、關係或權威，實質上是公開表示“這個人或這種關係算數”。","examples":[{"en":"The award acknowledged her as a leader in the field.","zh":"這個獎項認可了她在這一領域的領導地位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He finally acknowledged the child as his son.","zh":"他最終承認這個孩子是自己的兒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acknowledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dacf4626b7c724e","term":"acknowledge","forms":["acknowledge","acknowledges","acknowledging","acknowledged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對幫助表示感謝","explanation":"指明確指出並感謝別人給予的幫助、支援或好處；這是把“受到的恩惠”公開說出來。","examples":[{"en":"I would like to acknowledge your generous support during the project.","zh":"我想感謝你在專案期間給予的大力支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The author acknowledged her editor's valuable advice.","zh":"作者感謝了編輯的寶貴建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acknowledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97f09541bbbd5b0abd52","word":"acne","forms":["acne"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-daaed0cb6f867a17","term":"acne","forms":["acne","acnes","acnae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痤瘡；青春痘","explanation":"指一種常見的皮膚病，尤其常見於青少年，通常會使面部出現紅色痘痘。這是 acne 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"He struggled with severe acne during his teenage years.","zh":"他在青少年時期一直受到嚴重痤瘡的困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her acne became worse after several nights of poor sleep.","zh":"她連續幾晚睡眠不足後，痤瘡變得更嚴重了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acne","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d71cb8e303a85d3","term":"acne","forms":["acne","acnes","acnae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痘痘和紅斑的一片表現","explanation":"也可指某一片皮膚上由痤瘡造成的痘痘、紅斑等外在表現，重點從“疾病本身”轉向“皮膚上看得見的一片問題”。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor examined the acne on his back.","zh":"醫生檢查了他背部的痤瘡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Concealer barely covered the acne along her jaw.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acne","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66ac77df5e969eddb205","word":"acquaint","forms":["acquaint"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"acquaint","forms":["acquaint"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使熟悉；告知","examples":[{"en":"The guide will acquaint visitors with the history of the town.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Please acquaint yourself with the safety rules before using the machine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-195fc281cbc47b31e774","word":"acquaintance","forms":["acquaintance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c645d0dc24138403","term":"acquaintance","forms":["acquaintance","acquaintances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認識；熟悉","explanation":"表示與某人或某事有一定接觸和了解，但關係或瞭解程度不深；對人的認識通常還沒有達到朋友般的親密程度。","examples":[{"en":"I have some acquaintance with classical music, but I am not an expert.","zh":"我對古典音樂有一些瞭解，但不是專家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had no acquaintance with the local customs.","zh":"她不瞭解當地的風俗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acquaintance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e6d053bfb0436d3","term":"acquaintance","forms":["acquaintance","acquaintances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熟人","explanation":"指你認識但並不十分親近的人，也就是“點頭之交”或一般熟人；這裡的重點從“認識這件事”轉到了“被認識的人”。","examples":[{"en":"I ran into an old acquaintance at the train station.","zh":"我在火車站遇到了一位老熟人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is only an acquaintance, not a close friend.","zh":"他只是個熟人，不是親密的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acquaintance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5df61d74243bc947cb9","word":"acquire","forms":["acquire"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fe91c1f58526b33","term":"acquire","forms":["acquire","acquires","acquiring","acquired","acquirest","acquiredst","acquireth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取得；得到","explanation":"最寬泛的用法，指把某件東西、機會或資源弄到手，不特別強調是購買、繼承還是透過努力得到。","examples":[{"en":"The museum recently acquired several rare paintings.","zh":"這家博物館最近獲得了幾幅稀有畫作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company acquired the rights to distribute the film.","zh":"這家公司取得了發行這部電影的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acquire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-477a41078a30f9f8","term":"acquire","forms":["acquire","acquires","acquiring","acquired","acquirest","acquiredst","acquireth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲得；養成","explanation":"強調靠自己的學習、練習或長期經歷逐漸擁有某種技能、習慣、知識或資格，重點在“獲得的過程”或個人努力。","examples":[{"en":"She acquired the skills needed to manage a large team.","zh":"她獲得了管理大型團隊所需的技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He acquired a strong interest in astronomy at school.","zh":"他在學校裡逐漸培養起了對天文學的濃厚興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acquire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31de312977fc2ebdfead","word":"acquisition","forms":["acquisition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35722533710730ba","term":"acquisition","forms":["acquisition","acquisitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獲得；取得的過程","explanation":"指把某物獲得、取得到手的動作或整個過程，重點在“怎麼獲得”這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"The acquisition of new skills takes time and practice.","zh":"獲得新技能需要時間和練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The acquisition of sports equipment can be fun in itself.","zh":"獲得運動器材本身就可能很有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acquisition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-572d20d4903465b6","term":"acquisition","forms":["acquisition","acquisitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獲得的東西；所得","explanation":"指已經獲得的具體東西或成果，也就是“拿到手的收穫”，而不是獲得這一過程。","examples":[{"en":"That graphite tennis racquet is quite an acquisition.","zh":"那把石墨網球拍真是一件不錯的收穫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This rare atlas is my favorite acquisition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acquisition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9687f37a648e57bbab7e","word":"acre","forms":["acre"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73ef2cda7bab8ffe","term":"acre","forms":["acre","acres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英美製面積單位","explanation":"acre是英美製的土地面積單位，約等於4046.86平方米，常用於描述農場、森林或其他大片土地。","examples":[{"en":"The farm covers nearly 300 acres of fertile land.","zh":"這座農場佔地近三百英畝，土地很肥沃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The park includes an acre of woodland.","zh":"這座公園有一英畝林地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acre","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09085292881243f4","term":"acre","forms":["acre","acres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"其他體系中的類似面積單位","explanation":"在介紹不同國家或歷史制度時，acre也可以泛指名稱或大小相近的其他土地面積單位，具體數值要看所用制度。","examples":[{"en":"The guide compares the local acre with the modern English acre.","zh":"這本指南比較了當地的土地面積單位和現代英畝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An Irish acre covered more ground than an English acre.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acre","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-deb538b50cb6318b008c","word":"across","forms":["across"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1a9960b15caac97","term":"across","forms":["across"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到另一邊","explanation":"表示從所在的一邊移動到另一邊，重點是完成了橫向穿越。","examples":[{"en":"A volunteer helped the child across the busy road.","zh":"一名志願者幫助孩子穿過繁忙的馬路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river was shallow enough to wade across.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/across","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34ea0151def8ea2f","term":"across","forms":["across"],"pos":"prep","zh":"穿過，到另一邊","explanation":"表示朝著某個橫向延伸的地點或障礙物移動，從這一邊到另一邊。","examples":[{"en":"We rowed across the lake before sunset.","zh":"我們在日落前划船穿過了湖面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We dragged the canoe across the muddy bank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/across","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7bf55496c8ef34f","term":"across","forms":["across"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……對面","explanation":"表示某物位於道路、河流等間隔物的另一側，重點是靜態位置。","examples":[{"en":"The pharmacy is across from the train station.","zh":"藥店在火車站對面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bakery stands across the road from the clinic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/across","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f83f07be16e270186d35","word":"act","forms":["act"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1414f94049040016","term":"act","forms":["act","ACTs","Acts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美國大學入學考試","explanation":"ACT 是美國大學入學考試的一種，學生透過參加考試取得成績，並可用成績申請大學。可以把它和記憶鉤子中的“把某事做出來”分開記：這裡的 ACT 是考試名稱。","examples":[{"en":"Many students take the ACT during their final year of high school.","zh":"許多學生在高中最後一年參加 ACT 考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her ACT score improved after a summer preparation course.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/act","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cacfeb02153d0be","term":"act","forms":["act","acts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行為；所做的事","explanation":"act 是一個具體做出來的行為或事情，尤其常指帶有某種目的、影響或道德意味的行動。記憶時抓住“把某事做出來”：做出的這件事就是 an act。","examples":[{"en":"Helping a stranger was an act of kindness.","zh":"幫助陌生人是一種善舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The act changed how people saw her.","zh":"這個行為改變了人們對她的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/act","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5fe6dd7fe99c854","term":"act","forms":["act","acts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戲劇的一幕","explanation":"在戲劇、歌劇或音樂劇中，act 是整場演出的一個大分段，幕與幕之間通常會改變劇情階段或場景。可以把它記成演員把故事“做出來”後，演出被正式分成的一段。","examples":[{"en":"The main character does not appear until the second act.","zh":"主角直到第二幕才登場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a short break between the two acts.","zh":"兩幕之間有一段短暫的休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/act","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fdfaf53319bb2a3","term":"act","forms":["act","acts","acting","acted","actest","actedst","acteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"執行；做成","explanation":"把某項事情、任務或計劃付諸行動並完成；這裡突出“做出來”，而不只是決定去做。","examples":[{"en":"The team acted on the manager’s advice and changed the schedule.","zh":"團隊按照經理的建議採取了行動，調整了日程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She acted on her decision and moved to another city.","zh":"她把自己的決定付諸行動，搬到了另一座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/act","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd938c688f49b77c7fc5","word":"action","forms":["action"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04e5a131c9662c75","term":"action","forms":["action","actions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動；做某事","explanation":"指付出努力去做某事的過程，重點是“動手做起來”，而不是隻停留在想法上。","examples":[{"en":"We need to take action before the problem gets worse.","zh":"問題惡化之前，我們需要採取行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee took immediate action to protect the river.","zh":"委員會立即採取措施保護這條河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/action","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d09982dbb331795","term":"action","forms":["action","actions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"所做的事；行動","explanation":"指為了達到某個目的而做出的具體事情或措施，可以把它看成行動留下的實際結果。","examples":[{"en":"The company took action against employees who broke the rules.","zh":"公司對違反規定的員工採取了措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her actions showed that she cared about the team.","zh":"她的行動表明她很在乎這個團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/action","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96879611650f80a81392","word":"active","forms":["active"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9bffc9eba5fbe5b","term":"active","forms":["active","more active","most active"],"pos":"adj","zh":"主動發揮作用的","explanation":"指某人或某事物具有行動、施加影響或促成變化的能力，而不是僅僅接受作用；核心畫面就是“正在動起來併產生作用”。","examples":[{"en":"She took an active role in planning the community event.","zh":"她積極參與了社群活動的籌劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chemical contains an active ingredient that kills bacteria.","zh":"這種化學制品含有能殺死細菌的有效成分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/active","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e28ef4f846bf2f08","term":"active","forms":["active","more active","most active"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正在生效或運作的","explanation":"指規則、計劃、裝置或過程已經開始並仍在發揮作用，處於實際運轉狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The new safety rules are active from January 1.","zh":"新的安全規定從一月一日起生效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check that your membership is still active.","zh":"請確認你的會員資格仍然有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/active","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc68baa984c5bbfd","term":"active","forms":["active","more active","most active"],"pos":"adj","zh":"積極忙碌的","explanation":"形容人持續主動做事、精力充沛並勤勉投入，而不是消極等待或只停留在想法上。","examples":[{"en":"He is active in several local volunteer groups.","zh":"他積極參加當地的幾個志願者團體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students stayed active throughout the summer break.","zh":"這些學生整個暑假都保持著積極忙碌的狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/active","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2b5e68aa91b38db759b","word":"activist","forms":["activist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58aa5ee3126027d9","term":"activist","forms":["activist","activists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治或社會活動人士","explanation":"指為了政治、社會或公共議題而主動組織、宣傳、抗議或爭取改變的人，例如環境保護、人權等方面的活動人士。這是 activist 最核心、最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The activists organized a campaign to protect the local river.","zh":"這些活動人士組織了一場保護當地河流的運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became an activist after her community lost access to clean water.","zh":"社群失去清潔用水後，她成了一名活動人士。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/activist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0651863bf5d902262b17","word":"activity","forms":["activity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec1f57bf4a528402","term":"activity","forms":["activity","activities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"活躍；活動量","explanation":"指人、地方或組織處於忙碌、不斷運作的狀態，也可以指這種狀態所表現出的活動量。這裡關注的是“整體有多忙、動靜有多大”，不是某一件單獨的活動。","examples":[{"en":"There was a lot of activity outside the station this morning.","zh":"今天早上車站外面人來人往，十分熱鬧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Business activity usually slows down during the holiday.","zh":"假期期間，商業活動通常會放緩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/activity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb30dee905ad54e3","term":"activity","forms":["activity","activities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一項行動；所做的事","explanation":"指一個人實際做出的某件事或一連串動作，重點是“做了什麼”。它可以是日常事務，也可以只是為了安排時間而進行的一項事情。","examples":[{"en":"Our first activity was a short walk around the village.","zh":"我們的第一項活動是在村子裡短途散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher planned three activities for the afternoon.","zh":"老師為下午安排了三項活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/activity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3ef884ca3b2868f62dce","word":"actor/actress","forms":["actor","actress"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3f58bb03d7eaa12","term":"actor","forms":["actor","actors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演員","explanation":"指在戲劇、電影或電視中扮演角色、進行表演的人。這是現代英語中最常見、最容易首先遇到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The actor gave a convincing performance in the film.","zh":"這位演員在電影中的表演很有說服力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She plays a detective in the new television series.","zh":"她在這部新電視劇中飾演一名偵探。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/actor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55427272a16df43a","term":"actor","forms":["actor","actors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動者；執行者；參與者","explanation":"指實際採取行動、推動事情發生的人、組織或其他實體。這裡的 actor 不一定是演員，而是“把某件事做出來的行動者”。","examples":[{"en":"The government was a key actor in the peace talks.","zh":"政府是和平談判中的一個關鍵參與者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several regional actors participated in the peace negotiations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/actor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ae910cc60d97fd0","term":"actress","forms":["actress","actresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女演員","explanation":"指在舞臺、電影、電視劇等作品中透過表演扮演角色的女性。記住“在銀幕上把角色演出來的女性”這一畫面即可掌握這個現代核心義。","examples":[{"en":"The actress gave a powerful performance in the new film.","zh":"那位女演員在新電影中的表演很有感染力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to become an actress one day.","zh":"她希望有一天能成為一名女演員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/actress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5c6fde86910ded72db5","word":"actual","forms":["actual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-897a694a9c8f5a6c","term":"actual","forms":["actual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"實際存在的；確實發生的","explanation":"指某事是真實存在、確實發生或已經成為事實的，而不是僅僅可能發生、被假設出來或透過估算得到的。它抓住了actual的核心：事情已經落到現實中。","examples":[{"en":"The actual cost was higher than we expected.","zh":"實際費用比我們預想的更高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to understand what actually happened.","zh":"我們需要弄清楚實際發生了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/actual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a926d170f932b87","term":"actual","forms":["actual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正是實際的；確切的；非常","explanation":"放在名詞前加強語氣，強調所說的是那個真實、具體或確切的物件，有時可理解為“真正的”或“正是這個”。它不是另一個完全獨立的概念，而是從“實際存在”發展出的強呼叫法。","examples":[{"en":"The actual problem is much simpler than it first appeared.","zh":"真正的問題比一開始看起來簡單得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Did you meet the actual inventor of this device?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/actual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-edb18f1a1d5884f245c4","word":"acute","forms":["acute"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f427ccef5b3028f1","term":"acute","forms":["acute","acuter","more acute","acutest","most acute"],"pos":"adj","zh":"敏銳而強烈的","explanation":"表示感覺、知覺、判斷力或情感非常敏銳，也可表示某種疼痛、問題等強烈得像尖刺一樣。","examples":[{"en":"She has an acute sense of responsibility.","zh":"她有很強的責任感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt an acute pain in his shoulder.","zh":"他感到肩膀一陣劇烈疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c5b449f745f43e1","term":"acute","forms":["acute","acuter","more acute","acutest","most acute"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迫切的","explanation":"表示需要、危險或問題已經尖銳到不能再拖延，因而十分緊迫。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital faces an acute need for more nurses.","zh":"這家醫院迫切需要更多護士。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drought has created an acute food shortage.","zh":"乾旱造成了迫切而嚴重的糧食短缺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db05579066c7525c","term":"acute","forms":["acute","acuter","more acute","acutest","most acute"],"pos":"adj","zh":"銳角的","explanation":"在幾何學中，表示角度小於九十度；它保留了“頂端尖”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The two lines meet to form an acute angle.","zh":"這兩條線相交形成了一個銳角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Draw an acute angle inside the triangle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1f61cc7216e18012d97","word":"adapt","forms":["adapt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76415f5eb0b4aaa9","term":"adapt","forms":["adapt","adapts","adapting","adapted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使適合；使相配","explanation":"把某物調整到合適的狀態，使它符合某種需要、條件或物件。重點在於“調到合適”，不一定意味著徹底重做。","examples":[{"en":"We adapted the lesson to suit younger students.","zh":"我們調整了這節課，使它適合年齡較小的學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company adapted its services to local needs.","zh":"這家公司調整了服務，使其符合當地需求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adapt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dfa7bb7e36a1c914","term":"adapt","forms":["adapt","adapts","adapting","adapted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改造；調整用途","explanation":"對原有事物進行具體改動或重新設計，讓它能用於不同的目的；比一般的“使合適”更強調實際改造過程。","examples":[{"en":"They adapted the old warehouse for use as a community center.","zh":"他們把那座舊倉庫改造成了社群中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide was adapted for children.","zh":"這本指南經過改編，適合兒童使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adapt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c73d17306b961f14","term":"adapt","forms":["adapt","adapts","adapting","adapted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"適應；適應新環境","explanation":"改變自己的行為或狀態，使自己能夠在新的環境、條件或生活方式中正常生活。這裡是“自己變得合適”，不是主動改造外部事物。","examples":[{"en":"It took her several weeks to adapt to her new routine.","zh":"她花了幾周時間才適應新的日常生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children often adapt quickly to change.","zh":"孩子通常能很快適應變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adapt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2fe1d615f7fb24b99fb8","word":"adaptation","forms":["adaptation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-47b3bb124b417926","term":"adaptation","forms":["adaptation","adaptations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"適應或調整的過程","explanation":"指為了適合新的條件、用途或環境而進行調整、改變的過程，重點在“正在變得合適”這一過程本身。","examples":[{"en":"The adaptation of the software to smaller screens took several months.","zh":"把這款軟體調整到適合小螢幕使用花了幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Successful adaptation to a new school can take time.","zh":"適應新學校可能需要一段時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adaptation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fac87aac41c95fa8","term":"adaptation","forms":["adaptation","adaptations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體的調整或改變","explanation":"指為適應某種條件而實際作出的一項或多項改變，也就是“調整後的做法或變化”。","examples":[{"en":"The new timetable includes several adaptations to help parents.","zh":"新時間表作了幾項調整，以方便家長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This adaptation to the design makes the chair safer.","zh":"對設計作出的這項調整讓椅子更安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adaptation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f3529ed3e8110a8","term":"adaptation","forms":["adaptation","adaptations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"改編的過程","explanation":"指把小說、戲劇、遊戲等作品從一種媒介或形式改造成另一種媒介或形式的過程，例如把小說改編成電影。","examples":[{"en":"The adaptation of the novel for television took two years.","zh":"把這部小說改編成電視劇花了兩年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The director is responsible for the adaptation of the play.","zh":"這位導演負責這部戲劇的改編。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adaptation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e9e5ac30f2216fd0fd6","word":"add","forms":["add"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65288037ad86d9c9","term":"add","forms":["add","adds","adding","added","addest","addedst","addeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……加到……中","explanation":"add 的基本動作是把一個東西併入另一個東西，使整體變多或變大；可以用於物品、數量、人員和抽象內容。","examples":[{"en":"Add the chopped tomatoes to the soup.","zh":"把切好的西紅柿加到湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She added my name to the guest list.","zh":"她把我的名字加到了賓客名單上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/add","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-605f85af62b0bf12","term":"add","forms":["add","adds","adding","added","addest","addedst","addeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把數字加起來","explanation":"add 也表示在頭腦中或按運算規則把數字合在一起，求出總數。","examples":[{"en":"Can you add these numbers for me?","zh":"你能幫我把這些數字加起來嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add the receipts to find our total expenditure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/add","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a205014d55328fee","term":"add","forms":["add","adds","adding","added","addest","addedst","addeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"補充說","explanation":"說話者在原有陳述後再接一條資訊時，可以用 add，表示把這句話也“加進”談話內容中。","examples":[{"en":"He added that the meeting would start at nine.","zh":"他補充說，會議將在九點開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He added that parking would be free.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/add","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4d6f7752759a758df9e","word":"addict","forms":["addict"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8141f376c775823c","term":"addict","forms":["addict","addicts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成癮者","explanation":"指被毒品或其他有害物質牢牢控制、難以停止使用的人；核心畫面就是“被某物綁住的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic offers support to people struggling with addiction, including many drug addicts.","zh":"這家診所為與成癮作鬥爭的人提供幫助，其中包括許多吸毒成癮者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recovering addict attends a support group every Tuesday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/addict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc0c8c193cb161de","term":"addict","forms":["addict","addicts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狂熱愛好者","explanation":"指對某種活動、作品或事物投入得像被它綁住一樣的人，語氣通常比“成癮者”輕鬆，也可以只是誇張地說自己特別喜歡某物。","examples":[{"en":"I'm a coffee addict, so I drink it every morning.","zh":"我是個咖啡狂熱愛好者，所以每天早上都喝咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a crossword addict, he finishes three puzzles daily.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/addict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-056dc4cc3470ead924d1","word":"addiction","forms":["addiction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ad2995c9d651b21","term":"addiction","forms":["addiction","addictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成癮狀態","explanation":"指對藥物或某種能帶來強烈滿足感的行為產生強迫性依賴，雖然已經造成傷害，仍反覆進行，難以自行停止。這是這個詞最重要、最嚴格的含義。","examples":[{"en":"His addiction to gambling left the family in serious debt.","zh":"他的賭博成癮使全家背上了沉重的債務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sought treatment for her addiction to painkillers.","zh":"她為自己的止痛藥成癮尋求治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/addiction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d23959df9e9cb81f","term":"addiction","forms":["addiction","addictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沉迷；強烈偏愛","explanation":"指對某種活動、事物或思想形成很強的依戀，注意力總被它吸引。這個用法可以沒有嚴格醫學意義，常帶有“迷上了、離不開”的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"Her addiction to online shopping is becoming expensive.","zh":"她沉迷網上購物，花費越來越大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her addiction to crossword puzzles fills every lunchbreak.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/addiction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77f930e4b1a527037bb9","word":"addition","forms":["addition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7e1ca27535e4291","term":"addition","forms":["addition","additions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"增加；新增這一動作","explanation":"指把新的東西、人員或內容加到原有整體中的行為，重點在“加進去”這個過程，而不是加進去的東西本身。","examples":[{"en":"The addition of a new bus route will make commuting easier.","zh":"增加一條新的公交線路會讓通勤更方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The addition of salt changed the boiling point slightly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/addition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e2925ca89840895","term":"addition","forms":["addition","additions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新增的東西","explanation":"指已經加到某個整體中的人、物或內容，也就是“新添的那一部分”。它關注的是加進去的結果，而不是新增這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The small garden is a welcome addition to the school.","zh":"這個小花園是學校裡一個令人欣喜的新添部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The latest addition to the exhibition is a Roman silver coin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/addition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-658e83fb64c26222","term":"addition","forms":["addition","additions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"加法","explanation":"指把兩個或多個數合在一起求總數的數學運算。這裡不是泛指增加，而是明確的算術步驟。","examples":[{"en":"Children usually learn addition before multiplication.","zh":"孩子們通常先學加法，再學乘法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This exercise involves the addition of three numbers.","zh":"這道練習涉及三個數相加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/addition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b476727faf3f30a18e7","word":"additional","forms":["additional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28db0b1af3d4117f","term":"additional","forms":["additional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"額外的；附加的","explanation":"它指在原有內容、數量或安排之外再加上的部分；原來的東西仍然保留，只是多了一項或多了一些。","examples":[{"en":"You may be charged an additional fee for late payment.","zh":"逾期付款可能會被收取額外費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course provides additional support for new students.","zh":"這門課程為新生提供額外支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/additional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d80c9bf910f144738ef9","word":"address","forms":["address"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b11572ef2b03e16a","term":"address","forms":["address","addresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地址；通訊地址","explanation":"指用來確定某個地點、郵箱或網路位置的一組資訊；它把郵件、人員或資料準確地“指向”目標。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your new address on this form.","zh":"請在這張表上填寫你的新地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sent the file to the wrong email address.","zh":"我把檔案發到了錯誤的電子郵件地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/address","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-638b8f8cd0d03b8b","term":"address","forms":["address","addresses","addressing","addressed","addrest"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向……講話；向……發出資訊","explanation":"把口頭或書面資訊直接指向某人、機構或群體，表示向其講話、寫信或提出請求。它和“地址”的共同點是都把資訊準確地送向目標。","examples":[{"en":"I addressed the manager directly about the delay.","zh":"我直接向經理談了延誤的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The notice addresses all residents in the building.","zh":"這則通知是發給樓裡所有居民的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/address","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7be71da39e731e63","term":"address","forms":["address","addresses","addressing","addressed","addrest"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處理；解決（問題）","explanation":"把注意力和行動直接指向問題、風險或需要改進的地方，並設法處理它；這裡不是單純“提到”問題。","examples":[{"en":"We need a clear plan to address the safety problem.","zh":"我們需要一個明確的計劃來處理安全問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy addresses concerns about privacy.","zh":"新政策回應並處理了人們對隱私的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/address","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-018fd478959f02a3a1cc","word":"adequate","forms":["adequate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e466a7f61f717e24","term":"adequate","forms":["adequate","more adequate","most adequate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"足夠的；符合要求的","explanation":"某物的數量、能力或質量達到任務所需的標準，因此可以使用或完成任務，但不一定特別好或特別多。它就像對齊了要求線，剛好夠用。","examples":[{"en":"The equipment is adequate for a small research project.","zh":"這套裝置足以應付一個小型研究專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her experience was adequate to the demands of the job.","zh":"她的經驗符合這份工作的要求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adequate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6bd2e8f08779ff81062","word":"adjust(ment)","forms":["adjust","adjustment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b7911394b08c97c","term":"adjust","forms":["adjust","adjusts","adjusting","adjusted","adjustest","adjustedst","adjusteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調整；改動","explanation":"把某個事物改一改，使它更適合特定的人、目的或條件。改動不一定表示原來錯了，重點是讓它更合用。","examples":[{"en":"The chef adjusted the recipe to suit local tastes.","zh":"廚師調整了配方，以適應當地人的口味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please adjust the screen brightness before the meeting.","zh":"請在會議前調節螢幕亮度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6dc936455f8947b","term":"adjust","forms":["adjust","adjusts","adjusting","adjusted","adjustest","adjustedst","adjusteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修正；改正","explanation":"根據新的事實或發現，把原來的判斷、說法或做法改得更準確、更合理。這裡的核心仍是把某物撥回合適的位置，只是調整物件通常是觀點或結論。","examples":[{"en":"We adjusted our forecast after reviewing the latest figures.","zh":"檢視最新資料後，我們修正了預測。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adjust the spelling before sending the application.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be0d53f5cbfab4a8","term":"adjust","forms":["adjust","adjusts","adjusting","adjusted","adjustest","adjustedst","adjusteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"適應；適應變化","explanation":"改變自己的行為、期待或生活方式，使自己適合新的環境或情況。這裡不是調整外部物品，而是把自己“調到”新環境能正常運轉的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"It took me a few weeks to adjust to working from home.","zh":"我花了幾周才適應在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New students usually adjust quickly to campus life.","zh":"新生通常很快就能適應校園生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d794a6b7f1d915b5","term":"adjustment","forms":["adjustment","adjustments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調整這一動作","explanation":"指把某個東西、計劃或安排改到更合適狀態的行為本身，重點在“正在調整”這個過程，而不是最後得到的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The adjustment of the schedule took several hours.","zh":"調整時間表花了幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to make an adjustment to the plan.","zh":"我們需要對計劃作一項調整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjustment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-128f871da2579742","term":"adjustment","forms":["adjustment","adjustments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調整後的改動","explanation":"指調整所產生的具體變化，通常是幅度不大的修改、糾正或變更；可以把它看成“撥動之後留下的那一點改變”。","examples":[{"en":"After a few adjustments, the chair was much more comfortable.","zh":"作了幾處調整後，這把椅子舒服多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer made a minor adjustment to the color.","zh":"設計師對顏色作了一點小改動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjustment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2d361e757127b921b2f","word":"administer/administrate","forms":["administer"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72ce37138ed9e6b3","term":"administer","forms":["administer","administers","administering","administered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"管理；執行","explanation":"負責把機構、制度或一項事務安排並執行好，也可以表示監管其執行方式和具體過程。","examples":[{"en":"The university administers several scholarship programs.","zh":"這所大學負責管理幾個獎學金專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The test was administered under strict conditions.","zh":"這項測試是在嚴格條件下進行的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1655da723a364b74","term":"administer","forms":["administer","administers","administering","administered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給藥","explanation":"把藥物以口服、注射或其他方式給病人或動物使用，強調施藥這一動作和過程。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse administered the medication to the patient.","zh":"護士給病人用了藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor administered the vaccine by injection.","zh":"醫生透過注射給病人接種了疫苗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-512afb6c763173d396ba","word":"administration","forms":["administration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04734ab649ddb85d","term":"administration","forms":["administration","administrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理；行政","explanation":"指組織、指導和執行事務這一整套活動，重點是“把事情管理起來並辦下去”，不一定指某個具體部門。","examples":[{"en":"The administration of the museum requires careful planning.","zh":"博物館的管理需要周密的規劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works in the administration of a large university.","zh":"她在一所大型大學的行政管理部門工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6aad0214d94a5270","term":"administration","forms":["administration","administrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政府行政當局","explanation":"指政府中負責執行法律、處理公共事務的行政班子，通常包括最高領導人及其內閣或顧問團隊。","examples":[{"en":"The new administration promised to improve public transport.","zh":"新政府承諾改善公共交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The administration proposed a new national housing policy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43031e3c11945722","term":"administration","forms":["administration","administrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某位領導人執政期間的政府","explanation":"指某個國家在特定領導人執政期間的政府及其政策體系，重點是“這一屆政府”。","examples":[{"en":"The Johnson administration introduced new environmental rules.","zh":"約翰遜政府推出了新的環境規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The administration introduced reforms during its first year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51f6f029928f3d0d10b5","word":"administrative","forms":["administrative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75ca93925366a2b6","term":"administrative","forms":["administrative","more administrative","most administrative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"行政管理方面的","explanation":"指與管理機構日常運作有關的，例如處理檔案、安排流程、核算費用等事務；重點是“讓組織正常運轉”的後臺工作，而不一定涉及制定主要政策。","examples":[{"en":"The school is trying to reduce administrative costs.","zh":"這所學校正努力降低行政管理成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She handles most of the administrative work in our office.","zh":"她負責我們辦公室的大部分行政事務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administrative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4194d1706ed1f408d5e0","word":"administrator","forms":["administrator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e014db4cbb6011d","term":"administrator","forms":["administrator","administrators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理者；行政負責人","explanation":"指負責安排、指導或執行某個機構、專案或公共事務的人。重點不只是參與工作，而是要讓相關事務按計劃運轉。","examples":[{"en":"The school administrator approved the new safety plan.","zh":"學校管理人員批准了新的安全計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Administrators must make sure that all departments follow the rules.","zh":"管理人員必須確保所有部門都遵守規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administrator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40f4a72d41080ff7","term":"administrator","forms":["administrator","administrators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"系統管理員","explanation":"在計算機領域，指負責安裝、維護和管理計算機或網路的人。他透過管理系統設定、使用者許可權和資訊維護，讓整個系統正常執行。","examples":[{"en":"Please contact the system administrator if you cannot access the shared drive.","zh":"如果你無法訪問共享硬碟，請聯絡系統管理員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only the administrator can restore your network account.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/administrator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6cfff2cec8f2396035d","word":"admirable","forms":["admirable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-320ea9689fffe3f2","term":"admirable","forms":["admirable","more admirable","most admirable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得欽佩的","explanation":"指某人的品格、努力或做法特別值得尊敬和讚賞，重點是這個人或做法本身有令人敬佩的價值。","examples":[{"en":"It's admirable that Shelley overcame her handicap and excelled in her work.","zh":"謝莉克服了自己的障礙，並在工作中取得出色成績，這一點令人欽佩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her admirable patience helped the team through a difficult year.","zh":"她令人欽佩的耐心幫助團隊度過了艱難的一年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admirable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c5f916a546f0a0a","term":"admirable","forms":["admirable","more admirable","most admirable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"英勇而值得讚賞的","explanation":"指某個行動本身很勇敢、正義或有益，因而值得讚賞；這裡不一定是在評價一個人的整體品格。","examples":[{"en":"The firefighters' decision to enter the burning building was admirable.","zh":"消防員決定進入著火的大樓，這一行動十分英勇，令人欽佩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her admirable courage kept the trapped children calm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admirable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11353194bbff01263cfc","word":"admiral","forms":["admiral"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11e54cb674651b29","term":"admiral","forms":["admiral","admirals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"艦隊指揮官","explanation":"指統領一支海軍分艦隊或整支艦隊的人，重點是實際負責指揮艦隊，不一定強調正式軍銜。","examples":[{"en":"The admiral ordered the fleet to change course before nightfall.","zh":"艦隊司令命令艦隊在天黑前改變航向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The admiral of the squadron inspected every ship.","zh":"這支分艦隊的指揮官檢查了每一艘船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02fc686552c7fd6b","term":"admiral","forms":["admiral","admirals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海軍統帥","explanation":"指被任命來統領一個國家海軍的人；這裡的重點是職務，而不是某一次戰役中的臨時指揮。","examples":[{"en":"The admiral of the navy announced a new training plan.","zh":"海軍統帥宣佈了一項新的訓練計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The admiral ordered the fleet into harbor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4379558257a408f","term":"admiral","forms":["admiral","admirals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海軍上將軍銜","explanation":"指海軍中的高階軍銜，通常相當於陸軍中的上將級別；也可指擁有這一軍銜的人。","examples":[{"en":"She was promoted to admiral after thirty years in the navy.","zh":"她在海軍服役三十年後晉升為海軍上將。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Admiral Chen will speak at the ceremony.","zh":"陳上將將在儀式上發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8264153b4653dc0fe947","word":"admiration","forms":["admiration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ca5c439d835adc3","term":"admiration","forms":["admiration","admirations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讚賞；敬佩","explanation":"指因為某人或某事出色、令人驚歎，而產生的積極情感；可以是對能力、品格、成就或表現的欣賞和敬佩。","examples":[{"en":"She has always had great admiration for her mother.","zh":"她一直非常敬佩自己的母親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young athlete earned the admiration of the whole town.","zh":"這名年輕運動員贏得了全鎮人的讚賞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admiration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13f31855069f273d8fb4","word":"admire","forms":["admire"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-374a36640489270f","term":"admire","forms":["admire","admires","admiring","admired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欣賞","explanation":"表示帶著愉悅和讚許去看待某人或某物，覺得它值得喜歡或稱讚；這是從“驚喜地看”自然發展出的現代核心義。","examples":[{"en":"I really admire her courage.","zh":"我非常欣賞她的勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stopped to admire the view.","zh":"我們停下來欣賞風景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9901eabdefa7cbb6","term":"admire","forms":["admire","admires","admiring","admired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敬佩","explanation":"表示高度評價並由衷敬重某人或某種品格，重點從“喜歡看”進一步變成“看得起、尊敬”。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone admired the firefighter's bravery.","zh":"所有人都敬佩那名消防員的勇敢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I admire her courage in admitting the mistake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a6ba702490a37479175","word":"admission","forms":["admission"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd2c0aad16028ca3","term":"admission","forms":["admission","admissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"准入；入場","explanation":"指允許某人進入某處的許可，也可以指實際進入的資格或行為；核心畫面就是“門被開啟，讓人進去”。","examples":[{"en":"Admission to the garden is free on Sundays.","zh":"星期日進入這座花園免費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought admission for two adults and one child.","zh":"我們買了兩名成人和一名兒童的入場資格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-965d9164bcd89c14","term":"admission","forms":["admission","admissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承認；認可","explanation":"指承認一個尚未完全證明、但自己接受其部分真實性的說法或立場，相當於把這個說法“放進自己的話語中”。","examples":[{"en":"His apology included an admission that he had made a mistake.","zh":"他的道歉中承認自己犯了一個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report was an admission of the company’s poor planning.","zh":"這份報告承認了公司計劃不周。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-358970fc5c749bdd2821","word":"admit","forms":["admit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-efa40f372b542a1e","term":"admit","forms":["admit","admits","admitting","admitted","admittest","admittedst","admitteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"允許進入","explanation":"讓某人或某物進入一個地方、範圍，或讓某個想法進入自己的考慮之中；核心畫面就是“把它放進門內”。","examples":[{"en":"Only members are admitted to the reading room.","zh":"只有會員獲准進入閱覽室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finally admitted the possibility into her thinking.","zh":"她最終把這種可能性納入了自己的思考。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67a01867528caa00","term":"admit","forms":["admit","admits","admitting","admitted","admittest","admittedst","admitteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承認事實或錯誤","explanation":"把一個無法繼續迴避的事實、錯誤或指控“放進自己的判斷裡”，即承認它為真實或有道理。它既可以表示說出承認，也可以表示某事實本身得到承認。","examples":[{"en":"He admitted that he had made a serious mistake.","zh":"他承認自己犯了一個嚴重的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She admitted to taking the last cookie.","zh":"她承認是自己拿走了最後一塊餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bba397637be816735edb","word":"adolescence","forms":["adolescence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-425b76b1c82e2f46","term":"adolescence","forms":["adolescence","adolescences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"青春期；青春階段","explanation":"指人從兒童成長為成人的過渡時期。這一時期通常同時包含身體成熟、心理變化以及逐漸建立獨立性等發展過程。","examples":[{"en":"During adolescence, many people become more independent from their parents.","zh":"在青春期，許多人會變得更加獨立，不再那麼依賴父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her interests changed considerably during adolescence.","zh":"她在青春期的興趣發生了很大的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adolescence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-183275732b387ac43c6d","word":"adolescent","forms":["adolescent"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bdbd2d11ef20122","term":"adolescent","forms":["adolescent","more adolescent","most adolescent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"青春期的；青少年的","explanation":"指處在兒童向成年人過渡階段的，或與這一階段有關的事物，核心是“正在長大成人”。","examples":[{"en":"The program helps parents understand adolescent development.","zh":"這個專案幫助家長了解青少年的成長髮展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adolescent behavior can change quickly under stress.","zh":"青少年的行為在壓力下可能會迅速改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adolescent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-338909ac96390b3d","term":"adolescent","forms":["adolescent","adolescents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"青少年","explanation":"指已經進入青春期、但還沒有成為成年人的人，也就是正在長大成人的青少年。","examples":[{"en":"The counselor works with adolescents who are struggling at school.","zh":"這名輔導員幫助在學校遇到困難的青少年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program pairs each adolescent with an adult mentor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adolescent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0ad2485845e6b91eced","word":"adopt","forms":["adopt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30c085572ae7e787","term":"adopt","forms":["adopt","adopts","adopting","adopted","adoptest","adoptedst","adopteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"領養；收養","explanation":"指依法或正式地選擇一個孩子等人成為自己的家庭成員、繼承人或受接納的成員。這個意思最具體，體現了“把原本不屬於自己的物件選進自己的關係範圍”。","examples":[{"en":"They decided to adopt a child after years of trying to start a family.","zh":"他們多年努力組建家庭未果後，決定領養一個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They hope to adopt a sibling pair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adopt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5a1db7326fa99ca","term":"adopt","forms":["adopt","adopts","adopting","adopted","adoptest","adoptedst","adopteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"採用；採取","explanation":"指主動把原本不屬於自己的外表、習慣、做法或身份接過來，當作自己的一部分。比如採用一種新形象，就是把它“選進”自己的生活。","examples":[{"en":"She adopted a more professional look for her new job.","zh":"她為了新工作採用了更加職業化的外表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school adopted a more flexible attendance policy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adopt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-503c8a0858cfc984","term":"adopt","forms":["adopt","adopts","adopting","adopted","adoptest","adoptedst","adopteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"採納；透過","explanation":"指選擇並接受某人的觀點、某項政策或某種方案，使它成為自己的立場或正式做法。它是“把一個想法選進自己的判斷或行動系統”的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The committee adopted the proposal after a long discussion.","zh":"委員會經過長時間討論後採納了這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council adopted the revised safety rules unanimously.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adopt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-31a42ea12ec1dd6bee07","word":"adore","forms":["adore"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-135f7cb5255f8ff8","term":"adore","forms":["adore","adores","adoring","adored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"深愛；深深敬愛","explanation":"adore 某人，就是把對方放在心上，懷有非常深的愛、欣賞和敬意；常用於親人、伴侶、朋友或偶像。","examples":[{"en":"She adores her grandparents and visits them every weekend.","zh":"她深愛自己的祖父母，每個週末都去看望他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He absolutely adores his young daughter.","zh":"他非常疼愛自己的小女兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-605c0d212a33a926","term":"adore","forms":["adore","adores","adoring","adored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"非常喜歡","explanation":"adore 某件事或某種活動，表示喜歡得不得了，像把喜歡的東西捧在心裡；感情通常比普通的 like 強。","examples":[{"en":"I adore walking by the sea in the early morning.","zh":"我特別喜歡清晨在海邊散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My cousins adore camping beside the lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fdc3e8038e87ff56a0e","word":"adult","forms":["adult"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a07b39148edae16a","term":"adult","forms":["adult","more adult","most adult"],"pos":"adj","zh":"成年的；長大的","explanation":"指人、動物或植物已經完全長大，不再處於幼年階段。這是adult最基本的“跨過成長界線”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The adult elephant stayed close to its calf.","zh":"那頭成年大象待在幼象旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This plant is still small, but the adult form is much taller.","zh":"這株植物還很小，但成年形態要高得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-859fef13d1ba78c8","term":"adult","forms":["adult","more adult","most adult"],"pos":"adj","zh":"面向成年人的","explanation":"指某種衣物、食品、節目或其他事物是為成年人設計、準備或限制給成年人使用的，而不是給兒童的。它仍然圍繞“成年人的需要或界線”這一核心。","examples":[{"en":"The store sells adult clothes in a wider range of sizes.","zh":"這家商店出售尺碼範圍更廣的成人服裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum offers an adult documentary about the history of the city.","zh":"博物館提供了一部面向成年人的城市歷史紀錄片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3b9fd6ed40f8b67","term":"adult","forms":["adult","adults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成年人","explanation":"指已經達到法定成年年齡的人。這個名詞意義把“長大”進一步落實為社會和法律上被視為成年人的身份。","examples":[{"en":"Children must be accompanied by an adult on this trip.","zh":"參加這次旅行的兒童必須由一名成年人陪同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course is open to adults of all ages.","zh":"這門課程向各個年齡段的成年人開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e40dfff1a71eb7baf65e","word":"advance","forms":["advance"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdc138a71923fdfb","term":"advance","forms":["advance","advances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進步；進展","explanation":"指某種能力、知識、健康狀況或事業向前發展，比原來更進一步。","examples":[{"en":"Recent advances in medicine have saved many lives.","zh":"醫學近來的進步挽救了許多生命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project has made great advances this year.","zh":"這個專案今年取得了很大進展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c958968cdfb74f9","term":"advance","forms":["advance","advances","advancing","advanced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促進；推動","explanation":"指幫助某個目標、事業、利益或計劃向前發展，使它取得進展。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy could advance women's rights.","zh":"這項新政策可能促進婦女權利的發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took the job to advance her career.","zh":"她接受這份工作是為了推動自己的職業發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9aa5b539f00236aa","term":"advance","forms":["advance","advances","advancing","advanced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使向前移動；使提前","explanation":"指讓人、物體或時間向前移動，或把某件事安排到更早的時間。","examples":[{"en":"The airline advanced the departure time by two hours.","zh":"航空公司把出發時間提前了兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commander advanced the troops toward the town.","zh":"指揮官讓部隊向城鎮推進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d21f85ea38166303ce58","word":"advanced","forms":["advanced"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-737732a3e2c65911","term":"advanced","forms":["advanced","more advanced","further advanced","farther advanced","most advanced","furthest advanced","farthest advanced"],"pos":"adj","zh":"先進的；前沿的","explanation":"指技術、方法或產品已經達到很高水平，接近當時的前沿。這裡的“向前”不是單純位置移動，而是發展到別人較少達到的階段。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital uses advanced imaging technology.","zh":"這家醫院使用先進的成像技術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new drone has advanced navigation systems.","zh":"這款新無人機配有先進的導航系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advanced","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb91622283224dac","term":"advanced","forms":["advanced","more advanced","further advanced","farther advanced","most advanced","furthest advanced","farthest advanced"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高階的；複雜的","explanation":"指內容、功能或操作比基礎階段更復雜，需要更多知識或技能，常見於課程、設定、裝置功能和說明文件。","examples":[{"en":"You can change the display language under advanced settings.","zh":"你可以在高階設定中更改顯示語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Advanced navigation equipment helps the vessel avoid submerged rocks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advanced","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fe4915f1609d6c7","term":"advanced","forms":["advanced","more advanced","further advanced","farther advanced","most advanced","furthest advanced","farthest advanced"],"pos":"adj","zh":"進階的；發展成熟的","explanation":"指學習、研究、產品或專案已經越過初始階段，發展到較成熟或較高的層次。它強調“已經走了很遠”，不一定表示在所有方面都處於世界前沿。","examples":[{"en":"This book is intended for advanced learners of Chinese.","zh":"這本書面向漢語高階學習者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is testing an advanced prototype before production begins.","zh":"生產開始前，團隊正在測試一個較成熟的原型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advanced","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":3,"counts":{"111":2,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-7db0558a5cdaa5ff8773","word":"advantage","forms":["advantage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bfa6ad6b2353ca5b","term":"advantage","forms":["advantage","advantages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有利條件；有利位置","explanation":"指能提高成功機會的條件、位置或機會。它可以是實際位置上的優勢，也可以是資源、時機等帶來的有利條件。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers had an advantage because they knew the trail well.","zh":"這些徒步者熟悉小路，因此佔有優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Being close to the station gives the shop a clear advantage.","zh":"靠近車站讓這家商店擁有明顯的優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advantage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c24b870080411256","term":"advantage","forms":["advantage","advantages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"好處；益處","explanation":"指某種條件、做法或事物帶來的實際益處、收益或便利。它和“優勢”相連，但重點從競爭中的領先轉向對自己有幫助的結果。","examples":[{"en":"One advantage of working from home is the shorter commute.","zh":"在家工作的一項好處是通勤時間更短。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One advantage of cycling is avoiding parking fees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advantage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47360b8c5f58c5ba04c8","word":"adventure","forms":["adventure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36b3ee88b4741f8c","term":"adventure","forms":["adventure","adventures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冒險精神","explanation":"指渴望新鮮、刺激和未知事物的心情，像是想主動走進一張還沒有探索過的地圖。","examples":[{"en":"Her sense of adventure led her to travel alone across the desert.","zh":"她的冒險精神促使她獨自穿越沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children need a little adventure in their lives.","zh":"孩子們的生活中需要有一點探索和冒險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adventure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b91dd0971f724c0","term":"adventure","forms":["adventure","adventures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冒險經歷；奇遇","explanation":"指一件非同尋常、值得講述的經歷，通常帶有未知、意外或刺激的成分。","examples":[{"en":"Our weekend in the mountains turned into an unforgettable adventure.","zh":"我們在山裡的週末變成了一次難忘的冒險經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Getting stranded overnight became our greatest adventure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adventure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2bf1b9cfb93ab6f","term":"adventure","forms":["adventure","adventures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大膽冒險；冒險行動","explanation":"指明知結果未知、可能遇到危險，仍然敢於採取行動的冒險行為；它比一般的經歷更突出勇氣和風險。","examples":[{"en":"Climbing the unfinished tower was a dangerous adventure.","zh":"攀登那座尚未完工的塔是一次危險的冒險行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They were looking for adventure, not a quiet holiday.","zh":"他們想尋找冒險，而不是過一個安靜的假期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adventure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39f4bf4ed1ac3dbb7725","word":"adverse","forms":["adverse"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0facd1c7d6952f2","term":"adverse","forms":["adverse","more adverse","adverser","most adverse","adversest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"敵對的；有害的","explanation":"表示某種力量、態度或行動在方向上反過來，直接對抗某人或損害其利益；重點是“主動形成阻力或敵意”。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy drew adverse criticism from local residents.","zh":"這項新政策受到了當地居民的負面批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medicine may cause adverse effects in some patients.","zh":"這種藥可能會對一些患者產生不良影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-727140b70ef54f40","term":"adverse","forms":["adverse","more adverse","adverser","most adverse","adversest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不利的；有礙發展的","explanation":"表示環境、條件或形勢朝著不利於某一目標的方向發展，使事情更難完成；這裡不一定有明確的敵意，核心是結果對人不利。","examples":[{"en":"The team continued working despite adverse circumstances.","zh":"儘管處境不利，團隊仍繼續工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adverse weather delayed the search for two days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ab15d071f3df885e468","word":"advertise(ment)/ad","forms":["advertise","advertisement","ad"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22a0ba9c625a859e","term":"advertise","forms":["advertise","advertises","advertising","advertised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"公開宣佈","explanation":"把某件事公開告訴公眾，使大家都知道；重點是把資訊放到公共視野中，不一定涉及賣東西。","examples":[{"en":"The museum advertised the opening date on its website.","zh":"博物館在網站上公佈了開放日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company advertised the changes several weeks in advance.","zh":"公司提前幾周公布了這些變動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advertise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25fe5beb0af5fb2e","term":"advertise","forms":["advertise","advertises","advertising","advertised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為商品或服務做廣告","explanation":"透過電視、廣播、網路等公開渠道宣傳商品或服務，目的是讓更多人注意並增加購買或使用的可能性；這是日常生活中最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant advertises its lunch specials on social media.","zh":"這家餐館在社交媒體上宣傳午餐特惠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small businesses can advertise cheaply through local websites.","zh":"小企業可以透過本地網站低成本做廣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advertise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d5c3f62d341af7d","term":"advertisement","forms":["advertisement","advertisements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業廣告","explanation":"指為了賣出商品、服務或類似事物而公開傳播的資訊，是 advertisement 最常見的意義。它可以出現在紙張、螢幕、路牌等不同媒介上。","examples":[{"en":"I saw an advertisement for a new phone on the train.","zh":"我在火車上看到了一則新手機廣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company spends a lot of money on advertisement.","zh":"這家公司在廣告上花了很多錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advertisement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfa4cfd8ede12c73","term":"advertisement","forms":["advertisement","advertisements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公開公告","explanation":"指面向公眾釋出的通知，目的是讓人們知道某項安排、變化或訊息，不一定是在推銷東西。比如政府或機構可以透過報紙釋出道路施工通知。","examples":[{"en":"The town put an advertisement in the newspaper about the road closure.","zh":"鎮政府在報紙上刊登了一則道路封閉公告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An advertisement in the newspaper announced the public hearing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advertisement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0e78444c8b229e7","term":"ad","forms":["ad","ads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣告","explanation":"ad 是 advertisement 的常用縮寫，指報紙、網站、電視等媒介中用來宣傳商品、服務或活動的一條廣告。","examples":[{"en":"I saw an ad for a new language app online.","zh":"我在網上看到了一款新語言應用的廣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That ad made me want to try the restaurant.","zh":"那則廣告讓我想去試試那家餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02c97447687b4871b00a","word":"advice","forms":["advice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-277e56acabc257a4","term":"advice","forms":["advice","advices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建議；忠告","explanation":"指為了幫助對方而告訴他應該怎樣做，通常來自說話人的經驗、判斷或專業知識。它保留了“把自己看到的路指給別人”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"My sister gave me some advice about finding a new job.","zh":"我姐姐給了我一些關於找新工作的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You should take his advice and get more rest.","zh":"你應該聽他的建議，多休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bac8ab1286b879dca503","word":"advise","forms":["advise"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5d7a01f9472748c","term":"advise","forms":["advise","advises","advising","advised","advisest","advisedst","adviseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建議某人做某事","explanation":"把你認為更合適的做法告訴某人，希望對方照著做；畫面就是你先看清前面的路，再給對方指路。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor advised me to get more sleep.","zh":"醫生建議我多睡一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I advised her to check the address before leaving.","zh":"我建議她出發前核對一下地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c6fa936fc57cb13","term":"advise","forms":["advise","advises","advising","advised","advisest","advisedst","adviseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推薦某種做法","explanation":"不直接針對某個人，而是把某種行動說成值得采用的辦法；這仍然是“看清哪條路更好後給出指引”。","examples":[{"en":"Most travel guides advise booking a room in advance.","zh":"大多數旅行指南都建議提前訂房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic advised replacing both rear tires.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad3591b8141e9e717bd6","word":"adviser/advisor","forms":["adviser","advisor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88179930b823bd09","term":"adviser","forms":["adviser","advisers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顧問；諮詢者","explanation":"指為別人分析情況、提供建議並幫助其作出決定的人，例如財務、法律或學習方面的顧問。核心形象就是站在旁邊幫人看清方向。","examples":[{"en":"She spoke to a financial adviser before buying the house.","zh":"買房前，她諮詢了一位財務顧問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The adviser helped me compare the two plans.","zh":"顧問幫我比較了這兩個方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adviser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c473f4db2c583356","term":"advisor","forms":["advisor","advisors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顧問；建議者","explanation":"指為別人分析情況、提出建議或提供指導的人，可以是正式職位，也可以只是承擔這類作用的人。這個詞的核心就是“幫助別人作出更好決定的人”。","examples":[{"en":"She works as a financial advisor.","zh":"她是一名財務顧問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I asked my academic advisor which courses to take.","zh":"我問了學業顧問該選哪些課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advisor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-644c4a77ffa6df24068f","word":"advisory","forms":["advisory"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c6d79d32fda7986b","term":"advisory","forms":["advisory","more advisory","most advisory"],"pos":"adj","zh":"提供建議的","explanation":"指能夠提出意見、指導或建議的人、機構或組織。這裡的重點是“給別人出主意”，不一定擁有最終決定權。","examples":[{"en":"The advisory committee could only offer advice, but its recommendations were usually accepted.","zh":"這個諮詢委員會只能提出建議，但它的意見通常都會被採納。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The panel has an advisory role in curriculum decisions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advisory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c054e0895eb388192f4","word":"advocate","forms":["advocate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9e62541850c2924","term":"advocate","forms":["advocate","advocates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出庭辯護的律師","explanation":"在法庭上替當事人陳述理由、進行辯護的人，是“替別人說話”這一核心畫面的法律化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The advocate presented several arguments on behalf of the defendant.","zh":"這名辯護律師代表被告提出了幾項論據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her advocate questioned the witness about the missing receipt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25ecd4792b5efa66","term":"advocate","forms":["advocate","advocates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支援某事的倡導者","explanation":"公開表達對某種觀點、政策或做法的支援，並努力讓別人也接受它的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is a leading advocate for affordable housing.","zh":"她是保障可負擔住房的主要倡導者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An advocate for accessible housing addressed the council.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-967ef4cfa22fe3f1","term":"advocate","forms":["advocate","advocates","advocating","advocated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"倡導、主張","explanation":"公開表示應該支援某種做法，並努力推動別人接受它。","examples":[{"en":"Many doctors advocate getting regular exercise.","zh":"許多醫生倡導定期鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several teachers advocate shorter homework assignments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b0f45b16b28f28a","term":"advocate","forms":["advocate","advocates","advocating","advocated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"進行倡導活動","explanation":"不直接說明具體主張，而是泛指持續為某項事業或改變公開發聲、爭取支援。","examples":[{"en":"Local groups are advocating for safer streets.","zh":"當地團體正在倡導讓街道更加安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They advocate tirelessly for accessible public transportation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6b80b03ebc086c657a0","word":"aesthetic","forms":["aesthetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9022ea5a5e919e9e","term":"aesthetic","forms":["aesthetic","more aesthetic","most aesthetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"審美的；藝術效果上的","explanation":"表示某事物涉及美感、藝術表現或外觀給人的整體感受。它可以描述建築、設計、服裝等外在效果，也可以描述人對這些效果的審美判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The new café has a warm, natural aesthetic.","zh":"這家新咖啡館有一種溫暖自然的審美風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building is practical, but its aesthetic qualities are easy to overlook.","zh":"這座建築很實用，但它的審美特點很容易被忽視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aesthetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75c929eb04a7c25c3026","word":"affair","forms":["affair"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c7d25102ddfca65","term":"affair","forms":["affair","affairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事務；要處理的事情","explanation":"指需要處理、安排或討論的事情，範圍可以從商業工作到公共事務；核心感覺就是“一攤要辦的事”。","examples":[{"en":"Managing the museum is a complicated affair.","zh":"管理這座博物館是一件複雜的事務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She handles the company's financial affairs.","zh":"她負責處理公司的財務事務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be7f0392a72084c1","term":"affair","forms":["affair","affairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某件事情；某種行動","explanation":"用於不具體說明內容時，泛指某件事情、行動或事件，常帶有“這件事該如何評價”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The whole affair left everyone deeply embarrassed.","zh":"整件事讓所有人都感到非常尷尬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repairing the roof became a costly affair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8528058461899c6b3e79","word":"affect","forms":["affect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e365b4a278d9fc82","term":"affect","forms":["affect","affects","affecting","affected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"影響、改變","explanation":"指某件事作用到人或事物，使其狀態、行為或結果發生變化。這是現代英語中最常見的 affect 動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The new schedule will affect everyone in the office.","zh":"新時間表會影響辦公室裡的每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can affect your concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足會影響你的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-930d0e8d965799aa","term":"affect","forms":["affect","affects","affecting","affected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"假裝、裝出","explanation":"指故意表現得像自己其實並不是那樣，或擺出某種態度、狀態。這是另一條核心用法：不是外界作用於人，而是人主動把某種樣子“做出來”。","examples":[{"en":"He affected surprise when he heard the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息時，他裝出一副驚訝的樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She affected an accent to impress her guests.","zh":"她故意裝出一種口音來給客人留下深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14c67414e0dfb1fff879","word":"affection","forms":["affection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-707525d0df6d3be3","term":"affection","forms":["affection","affections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜愛；依戀","explanation":"指對某人或某物的溫暖喜愛和強烈依戀，是這個詞最值得優先掌握的意思；它強調心被對方牽動，而不一定表示戀愛。","examples":[{"en":"I have a lot of affection for my younger sister.","zh":"我非常疼愛我的妹妹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old dog showed great affection for its owner.","zh":"那隻老狗對主人表現出深厚的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9742e25d7f9d6adc","term":"affection","forms":["affection","affections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情感；感情","explanation":"指會牽動人的情緒和思想的感情或自然衝動，範圍比“愛”更廣，可以指對人、動物或事物的感情。","examples":[{"en":"Her affection for animals began when she was a child.","zh":"她從小就對動物有感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His letters reveal deep affection for his brothers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eea7bd05fecf9ef7720c","word":"affectionate","forms":["affectionate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1163169e6608c342","term":"affectionate","forms":["affectionate","more affectionate","most affectionate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親切有愛；疼愛人的","explanation":"形容一個人對別人表現出溫暖、關心和喜愛，尤其常用於親人、朋友之間；也可以說某人本身性格親切有愛。","examples":[{"en":"My grandfather was gentle and affectionate with all his grandchildren.","zh":"我的祖父對所有孫輩都溫和而親切疼愛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave her dog an affectionate hug before leaving.","zh":"她離開前親切地抱了抱自己的狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affectionate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0a00177771dbade","term":"affectionate","forms":["affectionate","more affectionate","most affectionate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"帶有愛意的；溫柔親切的","explanation":"形容表情、語氣、話語、照料或行為本身流露出愛和關懷；重點不在“誰有這種感情”，而在這種感情如何被表達出來。","examples":[{"en":"He sent his mother an affectionate message from the road.","zh":"他在路上給母親發了一條充滿愛意的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave his granddaughter an affectionate squeeze.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affectionate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e6f3ef30c9311c70865","word":"affiliate","forms":["affiliate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c36fe77e736c43d","term":"affiliate","forms":["affiliate","affiliates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關聯成員；附屬機構","explanation":"指加入某個更大組織網路、但本身仍作為獨立單位存在的機構或成員，例如與全國電視網相聯絡的地方電視臺。","examples":[{"en":"The local station is an affiliate of the national network.","zh":"這家地方電視臺是該全國電視網的關聯機構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The regional affiliate broadcasts its own morning news.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affiliate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-934a426989f7a155642f","word":"affirm","forms":["affirm"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a20956d9dceec87","term":"affirm","forms":["affirm","affirms","affirming","affirmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確認；肯定回答","explanation":"表示對問題或說法作出明確肯定，確認自己同意、答應或核實了相關內容。它把“是”說得更清楚、更鄭重。","examples":[{"en":"She affirmed that she would attend the meeting.","zh":"她確認自己會參加這次會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Asked whether the signature was hers, she affirmed it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affirm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2eee37a8a025845f","term":"affirm","forms":["affirm","affirms","affirming","affirmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"斷言；堅稱","explanation":"表示有把握地說某事是真的，並堅持這一說法。與前一個意思相比，這裡重點不是回答別人，而是主動提出並維護一個判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The report affirms that the plan is financially sound.","zh":"報告斷言這項計劃在財務上是可行的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She affirmed that every signature was genuine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/affirm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f901528b18bc7e90bcae","word":"afford","forms":["afford"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ee59464f15c654b","term":"afford","forms":["afford","affords","affording","afforded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承擔得起；買得起","explanation":"表示手頭有足夠的錢、時間、精力或餘地去承擔某件事，不會因此造成難以承受的損失；所以既可以說買得起東西，也可以說抽得出時間或承擔得起等待。","examples":[{"en":"We can afford the extra hour it will take.","zh":"我們抽得出這額外的一小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't afford to replace my laptop right now.","zh":"我現在買不起新膝上型電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afford","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70df9c5b7dc7ec9d","term":"afford","forms":["afford","affords","affording","afforded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"帶來；提供","explanation":"表示某件事自然地帶來、提供某種機會、幫助或結果，也就是從事物本身向外“騰出並給出”某種東西；常用於較抽象的內容。","examples":[{"en":"The quiet room afforded us a chance to talk.","zh":"這間安靜的房間給了我們交談的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The balcony affords a sweeping harbor view.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afford","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-180366dd3b2cc124570a","word":"afraid","forms":["afraid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3ea1c9d67d6d913","term":"afraid","forms":["afraid","more afraid","most afraid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"害怕；感到恐懼","explanation":"面對危險、未知事物或不好的結果時，心裡產生害怕和顧慮，就是這種“往後縮”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"I’m afraid of dogs.","zh":"我害怕狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was afraid to ask for help.","zh":"她害怕開口求助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afraid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1574b5b9fb46017","term":"afraid","forms":["afraid","more afraid","most afraid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"恐怕；很遺憾","explanation":"說話人預料到對方可能不喜歡聽某件事，於是先用害怕的語氣墊一下，委婉地表示遺憾、拒絕或無法答應。","examples":[{"en":"I’m afraid we can’t change the booking.","zh":"恐怕我們不能更改預訂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm afraid the last train has already departed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afraid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f39592393ef0859cb196","word":"after","forms":["after"],"officialPos":"prep./conj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f51a476211e9a3e","term":"after","forms":["after"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在後；隨後","explanation":"表示某人或某物跟在前面的人、物後面，也可以表示動作發生在之後；這是“沿著前面物件往後走”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The little boy ran after his sister into the garden.","zh":"小男孩跟著姐姐跑進了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I called after her, but she did not hear me.","zh":"我在她身後喊她，但她沒有聽見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/after","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17c6df1b0441d3ea","term":"after","forms":["after"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……之後","explanation":"表示某件事發生在另一件事之後；這是最常見、最基礎的時間用法。","examples":[{"en":"We went for a walk after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們去散步了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please lock the door after you leave.","zh":"你離開後請鎖好門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/after","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e53a55098942bac","term":"after","forms":["after"],"pos":"prep","zh":"追求；尋找","explanation":"表示把某人或某物作為追趕、尋找或爭取的目標，像沿著前方物件一路追過去。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is going after a place on the school team.","zh":"瑪雅正在爭取校隊中的一個名額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog went after the ball across the yard.","zh":"狗追著球跑過了院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/after","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8e07c1ac268eae0661e","word":"afternoon","forms":["afternoon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8944eb39c127cb2a","term":"afternoon","forms":["afternoon","afternoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下午","explanation":"指從中午或午飯後到傍晚之間的一段時間，是 afternoon 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I have a meeting in the afternoon.","zh":"我下午有個會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It started raining this afternoon.","zh":"今天下午開始下雨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afternoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c20e9614df0efb57381d","word":"afterward/afterwards","forms":["afterwards"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38b2b6f226082458","term":"afterwards","forms":["afterwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"後來；之後","explanation":"指前一件事發生或結束以後，時間線繼續向後，另一件事隨後發生。它強調的是“在那之後”，不一定表示緊接著發生。","examples":[{"en":"We went for coffee afterwards.","zh":"後來我們去喝了咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She apologized afterwards.","zh":"她後來道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afterwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4c9e14061c2fd453b36","word":"again","forms":["again"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-62445920a7e16a77","term":"again","forms":["again"],"pos":"adv","zh":"再一次","explanation":"表示同一個動作或事件再次發生，重點是“做第二遍或更多遍”。這是最常見、最先需要掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I enjoyed the concert so much that I went again the next evening.","zh":"我太喜歡那場音樂會了，第二天晚上又去了一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please knock again; she may be upstairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/again","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4db41886ccfe9d65","term":"again","forms":["again"],"pos":"adv","zh":"重新；恢復原狀","explanation":"表示人、事物或狀態回到先前的樣子，或重新恢復某種情況。它不一定表示同一個動作重複，而是強調“回到原來的狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"The garden looks beautiful again after the rain.","zh":"下過雨後，這座花園又恢復了美麗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the repairs, the fountain flowed again.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/again","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a718e3e9aefa308ac31b","word":"against","forms":["against"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecc7e94ea08e4cb9","term":"against","forms":["against"],"pos":"prep","zh":"逆著；朝相反方向","explanation":"表示運動或作用方向與某個方向相反，好像在頂著阻力前進。","examples":[{"en":"We had to row against the wind.","zh":"我們不得不逆風划船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat moved slowly against the current.","zh":"船逆著水流緩慢前進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/against","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dd40f36928c5fce","term":"against","forms":["against"],"pos":"prep","zh":"撞著；衝擊著","explanation":"表示雨、浪、聲音或其他力量直接打在某個表面上，帶有碰撞或衝擊感。","examples":[{"en":"Branches rattled against the roof all night.","zh":"樹枝整夜在屋頂上 rattled 作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Waves slammed against the harbor wall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/against","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f23b7c5b21e5acca","term":"against","forms":["against"],"pos":"prep","zh":"靠著；倚著","explanation":"表示一個物體與另一個物體接觸，並以它為支撐或倚靠物件。","examples":[{"en":"She left her bicycle leaning against the gate.","zh":"她把腳踏車靠在門上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He rested his shoulder against the wall.","zh":"他把肩膀靠在牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/against","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-181ee31d49ea8339","term":"against","forms":["against"],"pos":"prep","zh":"和……比賽；對陣","explanation":"把兩個隊伍、選手或陣營放在相對的位置上進行比賽或較量。","examples":[{"en":"Our team is playing against the league champions tonight.","zh":"我們的隊今晚要對陣聯賽冠軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have never competed against someone with her experience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/against","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41fcd71e990460e8","term":"against","forms":["against"],"pos":"prep","zh":"違背；違反","explanation":"表示某件事與原則、規則、法律或個人信念相沖突，好像在和它對著幹。","examples":[{"en":"It is against the rules to park here.","zh":"把車停在這裡違反規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That decision goes against my advice.","zh":"那個決定違背了我的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/against","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-013f54400c82da080377","word":"age","forms":["age"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1ea9219ffc1f9a4","term":"age","forms":["age","ages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"年齡；年數","explanation":"指人、動物或事物從出生、產生或開始存在，到現在或某個指定時間所經過的時間，通常用年、月、日等計算。","examples":[{"en":"What is the age of your youngest child?","zh":"你最小的孩子幾歲？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The age of this building is nearly two hundred years.","zh":"這座建築有將近兩百年的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/age","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a34ea9987ec8baf","term":"age","forms":["age","ages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時代；歷史時期","explanation":"指歷史上具有鮮明特徵的一段時期；這裡的時間線從個人生命擴大到了整個社會、文化或行業。","examples":[{"en":"The city flourished during the golden age of trade.","zh":"這座城市在貿易的黃金時代繁榮起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are entering a new age of medicine.","zh":"我們正在進入醫學的新時代。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/age","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9043c427382ab863","term":"age","forms":["age","ages","aging","ageing","aged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變老；變舊","explanation":"指人、動物或事物隨著時間推移而變老、變舊，或顯出時間留下的痕跡。","examples":[{"en":"People age differently, even when they live similar lives.","zh":"即使生活方式相近，人們變老的方式也各不相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wood ages beautifully in the sunlight.","zh":"這木材在陽光下會自然地變得更有韻味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/age","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c4b2af4722ee54e31767","word":"agency","forms":["agency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-beb61dcfd90b616d","term":"agency","forms":["agency","agencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自主行動和選擇的能力","explanation":"指個人能夠獨立作出選擇，並按照自己的意願採取行動的能力。討論責任、道德、心理或社會處境時，這個義項尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"Young people need the agency to make decisions about their own future.","zh":"年輕人需要自主決定自己未來的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program gives patients more agency in managing their treatment.","zh":"這個專案讓患者在管理治療方面擁有更多自主權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c696508ccc3d523","term":"agency","forms":["agency","agencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代辦業務的機構","explanation":"指受他人委託、替客戶辦理業務或提供服務的機構，也可指這種機構的辦公地點或業務區域。例如幫助求職者找工作的機構就是就業中介機構。","examples":[{"en":"She found the job through a local employment agency.","zh":"她透過當地的一家就業中介機構找到了這份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The advertising agency designed a campaign for the new product.","zh":"這家廣告公司為新產品設計了一項宣傳活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df71fb0bd94cb72795ba","word":"agenda","forms":["agenda"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-85624c2ac18dcd85","term":"agenda","forms":["agenda","agendas","agendae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動計劃","explanation":"指按時間或步驟安排好的待辦計劃，說明接下來準備處理哪些事情。它像一張從“要做什麼”展開的總清單，範圍可以是一項工作，也可以是一整套長期行動。","examples":[{"en":"The committee published its agenda for the next six months.","zh":"委員會公佈了未來六個月的行動計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a clear agenda before we start this project.","zh":"我們開始這個專案之前需要一份明確的行動計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agenda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f33a59c9d0b1b59e","term":"agenda","forms":["agenda","agendas","agendae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"會議議程","explanation":"指會議中準備依次討論或處理的事項清單。它把“要做什麼”的清單放進一次具體會議裡，幫助參加者知道討論順序和重點。","examples":[{"en":"The budget was the first item on today’s agenda.","zh":"預算是今天會議議程上的第一個議題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Staffing shortages are first on tomorrow's agenda.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agenda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-d4f0bc5a29de06b510f9","word":"agent","forms":["agent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0896b1302125127a","term":"agent","forms":["agent","agents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動者；有行動能力者","explanation":"agent 的最基本概念是“能夠主動做事併產生行動的人或事物”。它強調行動能力，而不一定表示這個人受誰委託。","examples":[{"en":"Every person is an agent capable of making choices.","zh":"每個人都是能夠作出選擇的行動者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The device acts as an agent of change.","zh":"這個裝置充當了促成變化的力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76fd6aec92e97b73","term":"agent","forms":["agent","agents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代理人；代表","explanation":"指受另一個人或機構授權，代替對方處理事務的人。這個人不是單純在幫忙，而是有權代表委託方作決定、談判或辦事。","examples":[{"en":"She hired an agent to negotiate the contract.","zh":"她聘請了一名代理人來談判合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist's agent handles all business inquiries.","zh":"這位藝術家的代理人負責處理所有商務諮詢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b5e95e8dae8d977eb68","word":"aggression","forms":["aggression"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5d8e7edeacf8c80","term":"aggression","forms":["aggression","aggressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主動發起敵對行動或入侵","explanation":"指一方先採取軍事或其他敵對行動，尤其是進攻、入侵或奪取控制權；重點在於不是被動防禦，而是主動開始攻擊。","examples":[{"en":"The invasion was condemned as an act of aggression against a neighboring state.","zh":"這次入侵被譴責為對鄰國的侵略行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"International monitors reported continuing aggression along the border.","zh":"國際觀察員報告說，邊境沿線的侵略行動仍在繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aggression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-309fb72630b58bbe","term":"aggression","forms":["aggression","aggressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敵對或破壞性行為","explanation":"更寬泛地指帶有敵意、攻擊性或破壞性的行動，不一定是正式戰爭，也可以發生在個人、群體或日常互動中。","examples":[{"en":"The coach intervened when the player's aggression frightened the younger children.","zh":"那名球員的攻擊性行為嚇到了年幼的孩子，教練於是介入了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher intervened when teasing escalated into physical aggression.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aggression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42eddc67a7444c08abac","word":"aggressive","forms":["aggressive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-036874436c5e1882","term":"aggressive","forms":["aggressive","more aggressive","most aggressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好鬥的；有攻擊性的","explanation":"指人、團體或行動帶有明顯的進攻性，容易主動攻擊、強硬爭辯，或以壓迫、挑釁的方式達成目的。這裡的“攻擊”既可以是實際行動，也可以是政策、態度或言語上的進逼。","examples":[{"en":"The dog became aggressive when a stranger came near its food.","zh":"有陌生人靠近它的食物時，那條狗變得很有攻擊性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company used an aggressive campaign to drive its competitors out of the market.","zh":"這家公司採取強硬的營銷行動，試圖把競爭對手趕出市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aggressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78df616f9506c303","term":"aggressive","forms":["aggressive","more aggressive","most aggressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"激進的；不惜一切擴大運用的","explanation":"指某種方法會把資源、規則或技術潛力盡量推到更高程度，甚至為了效果而接受較大的複雜性或風險。它保留了“不斷加力、向前推進”的核心感覺，但不一定涉及人與人之間的敵意。","examples":[{"en":"The software uses aggressive optimization to reduce the time needed to process large files.","zh":"這個軟體採用激進的最佳化方式，以減少處理大檔案所需的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company pursued aggressive expansion into overseas markets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aggressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-1d8e08fd632682840b41","word":"ago","forms":["ago"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"ago","forms":["ago"],"pos":"adv.","zh":"以前","examples":[{"en":"We moved to this city three years ago.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"I finished my homework an hour ago.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb5597d8647d451aba9c","word":"agony","forms":["agony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a22819c4271cbc1f","term":"agony","forms":["agony","agonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極度痛苦","explanation":"指強烈到難以忍受的身體疼痛或精神痛苦，像是被痛苦逼到極限的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She was in agony after twisting her ankle.","zh":"她扭傷腳踝後痛苦不堪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Waiting for the test results was pure agony.","zh":"等待檢查結果的過程簡直是一種煎熬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dae2d2d794670470","term":"agony","forms":["agony","agonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臨死掙扎","explanation":"指生命即將結束時的最後掙扎，把“痛苦達到極限”的畫面推進到死亡來臨之前。","examples":[{"en":"The wounded animal made one last movement in its agony.","zh":"那隻受傷的動物在臨死前又掙扎了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wounded animal shuddered in its final agony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3db3773386a2e016ed66","word":"agree(ment)","forms":["agree","agreement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-389a7bd64f7195fa","term":"agree","forms":["agree","agrees","agreeing","agreed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"意見一致","explanation":"表示兩個人或多個人對某個觀點、事實或行動有相同看法，也就是大家站到了同一邊。","examples":[{"en":"I agree with you about the need for change.","zh":"我同意你關於需要改變的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two teams agree on the main facts.","zh":"兩支隊伍對主要事實看法一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-180ebab7a72c1a0e","term":"agree","forms":["agree","agrees","agreeing","agreed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表示同意","explanation":"表示接受別人提出的建議、要求或安排，答應照此辦理。","examples":[{"en":"She agreed to help us after work.","zh":"她同意下班後幫助我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They agreed to the new schedule.","zh":"他們同意了新的時間安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a00e36b179b72fdf","term":"agree","forms":["agree","agrees","agreeing","agreed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相符；一致","explanation":"表示一件事與另一件事在內容、外觀或結果上對得上，不一定涉及人的意見。","examples":[{"en":"The figures in the report do not agree with the original records.","zh":"報告中的數字與原始記錄不符。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His description agrees with the security camera footage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a5f8ac343bdd047","term":"agreement","forms":["agreement","agreements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"約定；協議","explanation":"agreement 可以指兩個或多個個人、團體或機構共同接受的做法和條件，也就是大家把行動對齊後形成的約定。","examples":[{"en":"The two companies entered into an agreement to share the new technology.","zh":"兩家公司達成了一項共享這項新技術的協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We reached an agreement on how to divide the costs.","zh":"我們就如何分攤費用達成了協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agreement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2aeda4e38369e88","term":"agreement","forms":["agreement","agreements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一致；相符","explanation":"agreement 也表示不同的人、觀點或結果彼此不衝突、相互吻合，強調的是一種“已經對齊”的狀態，而不是一項具體約定。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers are in agreement about the cause of the change.","zh":"研究人員對變化的原因看法一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her account is in agreement with the available evidence.","zh":"她的敘述與現有證據相符。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agreement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c4d198d85419b7f63fa","word":"agreeable","forms":["agreeable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5dff261021aad7a6","term":"agreeable","forms":["agreeable","more agreeable","most agreeable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人愉快的","explanation":"表示某人、聲音、氣味、味道、天氣或經歷讓人感到舒服、滿意或愉快，是 agreeable 最重要、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We spent an agreeable afternoon by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個愉快的下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tea has a mild and agreeable flavor.","zh":"這種茶味道溫和，令人愉悅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agreeable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5a049f96836618f","term":"agreeable","forms":["agreeable","more agreeable","most agreeable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與……相合的","explanation":"表示某事物符合另一事物的性質、要求或條件，因而在原則上相稱或合適；這裡的“合”不一定涉及人的同意。","examples":[{"en":"The plan must be agreeable to the terms of the agreement.","zh":"這項計劃必須符合協議中的條款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposed settlement is agreeable to both parties.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agreeable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bb0b3a466ce8e7684da","word":"agricultural","forms":["agricultural"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-723513aedeb47dbe","term":"agricultural","forms":["agricultural","more agricultural","most agricultural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"農業的；與農業有關的","explanation":"指和耕種、畜牧、農產品生產或農業產業有關的事物，也就是從“田地”這個核心意象延伸出來的形容詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The region's economy is still largely agricultural.","zh":"這個地區的經濟仍主要依靠農業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government is investing in agricultural research.","zh":"政府正在投資農業研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agricultural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f52a423f8ebd4ccad56","word":"agriculture","forms":["agriculture"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-656519227a8ce0e3","term":"agriculture","forms":["agriculture","agricultures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農業；農耕業","explanation":"指利用土地種植和收穫作物，並飼養、管理牲畜的一整套活動，也可以指研究或經營這些活動的農業領域。它比單獨的“種田”範圍更廣。","examples":[{"en":"Agriculture is the main source of income for many families in the region.","zh":"農業是這個地區許多家庭的主要收入來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Modern agriculture uses technology to grow crops more efficiently.","zh":"現代農業利用技術更高效地種植作物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/agriculture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0b4034c6ca7ee87f65c","word":"ahead","forms":["ahead"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d9c24bf45e18399","term":"ahead","forms":["ahead"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在前方；朝前","explanation":"指某人或某物位於說話者面對或前進的方向前方。這是最具體的基本畫面：視線和道路向前延伸，目標就在前面。","examples":[{"en":"The island was directly ahead.","zh":"那座島就在正前方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep walking; the station is just ahead.","zh":"繼續往前走，車站就在前面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ahead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ef79e0b00a2998c","term":"ahead","forms":["ahead"],"pos":"adv","zh":"領先；進度更快","explanation":"從“在前面”的空間畫面引申為在比賽、工作或發展進度上走在別人前面，也就是領先或佔優勢。","examples":[{"en":"She finished two laps ahead of me.","zh":"她比我早完成了兩圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our team is already ahead in the project.","zh":"我們團隊在這個專案上已經領先了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ahead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42c0827e7fd61c3e","term":"ahead","forms":["ahead"],"pos":"adv","zh":"將來；前方將有","explanation":"把未來想成還在前方的路，因此表示接下來會遇到的時間、事情或困難，常帶有“未來在等待著我們”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"There may be difficult days ahead.","zh":"未來可能會有艱難的日子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have a long journey ahead.","zh":"我們前面還有很長的路要走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ahead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-109d79437bb9079b50bc","word":"aid","forms":["aid"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd134ba2cdcc54b5","term":"aid","forms":["aid","aids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫助；援助","explanation":"aid 是別人伸出的援手，也就是幫助、援助本身；它強調讓陷入困難的人或事情得到支援。","examples":[{"en":"Her neighbors came to her aid after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，她的鄰居們來幫助她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity raised money in aid of homeless families.","zh":"這家慈善機構為幫助無家可歸的家庭籌集了資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eebe276df49b79d8","term":"aid","forms":["aid","aids","aiding","aided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"幫助；支援","explanation":"作動詞時，aid 就是把援手伸向某人或某件事，幫助其完成任務、擺脫困難或繼續發展。它既可以幫助人，也可以支援計劃、事業或程序。","examples":[{"en":"The grant will aid researchers in developing a safer treatment.","zh":"這筆撥款將幫助研究人員開發更安全的治療方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new bridge aided trade between the two towns.","zh":"這座新橋促進了兩個城鎮之間的貿易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a27f98238d2c1c02f2a1","word":"aim","forms":["aim"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1fd6a1db19ea7d19","term":"aim","forms":["aim","aims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瞄準方向","explanation":"指武器、物體或話語朝向目標的瞄準方向，核心畫面就是沿一條線把力量指向某處。","examples":[{"en":"The archer took aim at the center of the target.","zh":"弓箭手瞄準了靶心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speech took aim at rising prices.","zh":"這次演講把矛頭指向不斷上漲的物價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78198225b6931ef7","term":"aim","forms":["aim","aims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目的；目標","explanation":"指一個人或計劃想要達到的結果，把“指向某個目標”的畫面轉成了抽象的行動方向。","examples":[{"en":"The main aim of the project is to reduce waste.","zh":"這個專案的主要目的是減少浪費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her aim is to become a doctor.","zh":"她的目標是成為一名醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e795403bac93ed3","term":"aim","forms":["aim","aims","aiming","aimed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"瞄準","explanation":"指把武器或投射物朝向某個位置，想讓它擊中目標，是“沿著指向目標的直線行動”。","examples":[{"en":"He aimed at the target, but the arrow flew over it.","zh":"他瞄準了目標，但箭從目標上方飛了過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Aim the camera at the sign.","zh":"把相機對準那個標牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c7e49993ea4b32a","term":"aim","forms":["aim","aims","aiming","aimed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"力求；旨在","explanation":"指把自己的意圖或努力指向某個結果，努力想實現某個目的。","examples":[{"en":"The new rules aim to make the streets safer.","zh":"新規定旨在讓街道更安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are aiming for a higher score this year.","zh":"我們今年力求取得更高的分數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fe430e5274621be5189","word":"air","forms":["air"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be03d6ff8f1efa54","term":"air","forms":["air","airs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空氣","explanation":"指構成地球大氣、供人和動物呼吸並能被壓縮或流動的氣體。它是air最基本的意思，通常把它想成我們周圍看不見的環境。","examples":[{"en":"The machine uses compressed air to clean the parts.","zh":"這臺機器用壓縮空氣清潔零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Open the window and let some fresh air in.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f754b650f44a23b","term":"air","forms":["air","airs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空氣；新鮮空氣","explanation":"指人周圍可以呼吸的空氣，尤其強調出去接觸空氣或獲得新鮮空氣。和s1相比，這個意思更常出現在日常生活和呼吸的語境中。","examples":[{"en":"I need some air, so I am going for a short walk.","zh":"我需要透透氣，所以要出去短走一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Open a window and let some air inside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e49526f8d5c139d3","term":"air","forms":["air","airs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空中；天空下的空間","explanation":"指地面以上由空氣充滿的開放空間，也就是鳥、飛機或跳起的人進入的“空中”。它把“空氣”擴充套件成空氣所在的整個空間。","examples":[{"en":"The birds rose into the air when the dog ran toward them.","zh":"狗朝它們跑去時，鳥兒飛上了空中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The juggler kept five clubs spinning in the air.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d10149eecff30f56d947","word":"aircraft","forms":["aircraft"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afcfa99c0a9e9c6a","term":"aircraft","forms":["aircraft"],"pos":"noun","zh":"航空器；飛行器","explanation":"指能借助空氣中的浮力或升力在大氣中飛行的交通工具或裝置，例如飛機；因此它不只等於日常所說的“飛機”，而是一個更概括的類別名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The aircraft landed safely despite the strong wind.","zh":"儘管風很大，這架航空器還是安全降落了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displays several historic aircraft.","zh":"這家博物館展出了幾架歷史上的航空器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aircraft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b288c5c6dc91655abda","word":"airline","forms":["airline"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35af935cac53c951","term":"airline","forms":["airline","airlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"航空公司","explanation":"指經營飛機航班、把乘客和貨物運到不同地方的公司；從記憶上看，就是負責經營“空中線路”的企業。","examples":[{"en":"This airline has daily flights to Tokyo.","zh":"這家航空公司每天都有飛往東京的航班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many airlines are expanding their cargo services.","zh":"許多航空公司都在增加貨運服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-9bede13982e70436ba4d","word":"airplane/plane","forms":["airplane","plane"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-daf45b4ab9fc969b","term":"airplane","forms":["airplane","airplanes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機","explanation":"指一種有發動機、比空氣重、靠固定機翼飛行的航空器，是 airplane 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The airplane took off just after sunrise.","zh":"飛機剛過日出就起飛了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw several airplanes flying over the city.","zh":"我們看見幾架飛機從城市上空飛過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airplane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-585a7c5cd47cf7d5","term":"plane","forms":["plane","planes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平面；平坦表面","explanation":"指平整的表面，或把平整表面作為一個整體來談。它是其他許多義項的共同形象基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The shelf must be fixed in a level plane.","zh":"架子必須固定在一個水平面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Light reflects from the plane of the glass.","zh":"光線從玻璃平面上反射出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-501ef1a99165a7fb","term":"plane","forms":["plane","planes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幾何平面","explanation":"在幾何學中，指可以向各個方向無限延伸的平面，或其中被界定出來的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"The two lines lie in the same plane.","zh":"這兩條線位於同一個平面內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three points determine a plane in geometry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2a4a94e5ba3b3be","term":"plane","forms":["plane","planes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機","explanation":"指用機翼在空中飛行的航空器，是 plane 最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Our plane leaves at six in the morning.","zh":"我們的飛機早上六點起飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She booked a plane to Seoul for Friday.","zh":"她訂了週五飛往首爾的機票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ccc9ff052aee8da1c7d6","word":"airport","forms":["airport"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75390689a752e146","term":"airport","forms":["airport","airports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機場","explanation":"供飛機起飛、降落和停靠，並讓旅客辦理手續、進出飛機的整套場所和設施；它就像飛機使用的“港口”。","examples":[{"en":"She met Sam and the others at the airport at 7:00 am.","zh":"她早上七點在機場見到了薩姆和其他人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We arrived at the airport two hours before the flight.","zh":"我們在航班起飛前兩個小時到達了機場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b79cddf7034b6a96b439","word":"airtight","forms":["airtight"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41f05324611296c5","term":"airtight","forms":["airtight","more airtight","most airtight"],"pos":"adj","zh":"密封不透氣","explanation":"指容器、包裝或封口做得非常嚴實，空氣和其他氣體都進不去或出不來。它突出的是“封得緊”，不只是一般的蓋上或關閉。","examples":[{"en":"Keep the coffee in an airtight container.","zh":"把咖啡放在密封不透氣的容器裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lid is airtight, so the food will stay fresh longer.","zh":"這個蓋子密封得不透氣，所以食物能更久地保持新鮮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airtight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa74afe3d2c7ffe3","term":"airtight","forms":["airtight","more airtight","most airtight"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴密無漏洞","explanation":"比喻觀點、論證、計劃或案件嚴密得幾乎找不到可以反駁或攻破的地方，就像一個沒有縫隙的密封容器。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer presented an airtight case.","zh":"律師提出了一個無懈可擊的案件論證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The detective needed an airtight case before making an arrest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airtight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc4d4a57a36805e05e7b","word":"airway","forms":["airway"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-361bb8b2cdd45914","term":"airway","forms":["airway","airways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氣管；呼吸道","explanation":"指人體中空氣進出肺部所經過的管道，通常可譯為“氣道”或“呼吸道”，在較具體的語境中也指氣管。","examples":[{"en":"Smoke can irritate the airways and make breathing difficult.","zh":"煙霧會刺激氣道，使呼吸困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Swelling in the throat can obstruct the airway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37c2e9a673c8b928","term":"airway","forms":["airway","airways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機航線","explanation":"指飛機在空中按照規定使用的飛行路線，可以把它想成天空中的“道路”。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot changed course to avoid a busy airway.","zh":"飛行員改變航向，以避開一條繁忙的航線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The airway crosses several mountain ranges.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/airway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0145be012aa0a4428a20","word":"aisle","forms":["aisle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e2e2ce9da08c81a5","term":"aisle","forms":["aisle","aisles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"座位間過道","explanation":"指一排排座位之間留出的清楚通道，方便人們走動；這是在飛機、火車、公共汽車、電影院等場所最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep the aisle clear while the passengers are boarding.","zh":"乘客登機時請保持過道暢通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A child was walking up and down the aisle of the bus.","zh":"一個孩子在公共汽車過道里來回走動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aisle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c1e6af44e672ec5","term":"aisle","forms":["aisle","aisles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商店貨架間走道","explanation":"在超市或商店裡，aisle 是兩排貨架之間供顧客通行、兩側擺放商品的走道。","examples":[{"en":"You can find the pasta in aisle six.","zh":"你可以在六號走道找到義大利麵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You'll find chickpeas halfway down the canned-food aisle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aisle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e94ec139442cfe98f5c","word":"alarm","forms":["alarm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20f698765e33763a","term":"alarm","forms":["alarm","alarms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"危險警報；警告訊號","explanation":"指用聲音、資訊或其他訊號告訴人們危險正在接近，或提醒他們立即注意並採取行動。它可以是抽象的警告，也可以是實際響起的警報聲。","examples":[{"en":"The guard sounded the alarm when he saw smoke.","zh":"警衛看到煙後拉響了警報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report raised the alarm about unsafe drinking water.","zh":"這份報告對不安全的飲用水問題發出了警告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3828c25d60a80b6a","term":"alarm","forms":["alarm","alarms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚恐；憂慮","explanation":"指人突然意識到危險後產生的害怕和不安。這裡不是發出警報，而是聽到或想到危險之後的心理反應。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden noise caused alarm among the passengers.","zh":"突然的噪聲讓乘客們感到驚慌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looked at the broken window with alarm.","zh":"她驚恐地看著那扇破窗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b82df4fe3e04a43","term":"alarm","forms":["alarm","alarms","alarming","alarmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"警告；使警覺","explanation":"指把即將發生的危險或必須採取的行動告訴某人，使其提高警惕、做好準備。它像是把危險訊號傳給人，而不一定已經讓對方害怕。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor alerted, rather than alarmed, the patient about the mild side effect.","zh":"醫生向病人說明了輕微副作用，並沒有把他嚇到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The falling rocks alarmed the hikers into turning back.","zh":"落石使徒步者警覺起來，轉身往回走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2f98d2af6166fc9","term":"alarm","forms":["alarm","alarms","alarming","alarmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使驚慌；使擔憂","explanation":"指某種聲音、訊息或情況使人突然意識到危險，從而感到害怕、焦慮或不安。這是“警報”在人心中產生的情緒結果。","examples":[{"en":"The empty streets alarmed visitors who had never seen the city so quiet.","zh":"空蕩蕩的街道讓從未見過這座城市如此安靜的遊客感到不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not be alarmed by the flashing light; it is only a test.","zh":"不要被閃爍的燈嚇到，那只是在進行測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca7cad8166758cb97d37","word":"album","forms":["album"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0dd96d357c3eb724","term":"album","forms":["album","albums","alba"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相簿；收藏冊","explanation":"album可以是專門用來儲存照片、郵票或簽名的冊子。它的核心概念是把一組值得儲存的東西集中整理在一起，因此相簿不只是裝照片的容器，也可以是其他收藏冊。","examples":[{"en":"She showed me an old album filled with photographs from her childhood.","zh":"她給我看了一本裝滿童年照片的舊相簿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We keep our family photographs in this album.","zh":"我們把家人的照片儲存在這本相簿裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/album","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-566792231f295bfd","term":"album","forms":["album","albums","alba"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂專輯","explanation":"album最常見的現代音樂義是由多首錄音組成、作為一個整體發行的音樂專輯。它可以透過實體唱片、下載或流媒體釋出，關鍵在於這些歌曲被組合成一套作品。","examples":[{"en":"Her new album comes out next Friday.","zh":"她的新專輯將於下週五發行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I listened to the whole album on the train.","zh":"我在火車上聽完了整張專輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/album","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7c7eb1087c4e24d4c12","word":"alcohol","forms":["alcohol"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e88e4a095931dcb","term":"alcohol","forms":["alcohol","alcohols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乙醇","explanation":"這裡特指乙醇，也就是許多酒類飲料中使人產生醉意、並可作為消毒劑或溶劑使用的那種酒精。","examples":[{"en":"The test found a small amount of alcohol in his blood.","zh":"檢測發現他的血液中含有少量乙醇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This hand sanitizer is alcohol-based.","zh":"這款洗手液是以乙醇為主要成分的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alcohol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b96d0db6c586f3fb","term":"alcohol","forms":["alcohol","alcohols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒類飲料的總稱","explanation":"在日常語境中，alcohol 常泛指含乙醇的酒類飲料，如啤酒、葡萄酒和烈酒，而不是單指其中的化學成分。","examples":[{"en":"She stopped drinking alcohol last year.","zh":"她去年戒酒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Never drive after drinking alcohol.","zh":"喝酒後絕對不要開車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alcohol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f088c450592cb8198208","word":"alcoholic","forms":["alcoholic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d362308e877f614","term":"alcoholic","forms":["alcoholic","more alcoholic","most alcoholic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含有酒精的","explanation":"它明確說明某種飲料或液體不只是有酒精氣味，而是實際含有一定量的酒精；重點在成分。","examples":[{"en":"He ordered an alcoholic beverage with his dinner.","zh":"他吃晚飯時點了一杯含酒精的飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Alcoholic drinks are not served at this event.","zh":"這次活動不提供含酒精的飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alcoholic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f099ffda677fe209","term":"alcoholic","forms":["alcoholic","more alcoholic","most alcoholic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與酒精依賴有關的","explanation":"這裡的酒精不再只是飲品成分，而是和依賴、酗酒問題聯絡在一起；可描述相關疾病、行為或受影響的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic provides treatment for alcoholic dependence.","zh":"這家診所為酒精依賴提供治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His alcoholic behavior damaged the whole family.","zh":"他的酗酒行為傷害了整個家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alcoholic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7fd3da4a4bcc166","term":"alcoholic","forms":["alcoholic","alcoholics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒精依賴者","explanation":"這裡指一個人的飲酒已經發展成依賴問題，而不是普通的飲酒者；它強調長期的個人狀況。","examples":[{"en":"He admitted that he was an alcoholic and sought help.","zh":"他承認自己有酒精依賴，於是尋求幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been sober for five years after recovering from alcoholism.","zh":"她擺脫酒精依賴後，已經戒酒五年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alcoholic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df905058dd67a409fef8","word":"alert","forms":["alert"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9c76fa20bbb5696","term":"alert","forms":["alert","more alert","most alert"],"pos":"adj","zh":"警覺的；警醒的","explanation":"形容一個人清醒並主動留意可能發生的事情，像站崗的人一直觀察周圍動靜。","examples":[{"en":"Stay alert when walking through the crowded market.","zh":"在擁擠的市場裡走路時要保持警覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was alert to every change in his voice.","zh":"她敏銳地察覺到他聲音中的每一點變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12bdd0432fe1de40","term":"alert","forms":["alert","alerts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"警報；報警","explanation":"指提醒人們有危險、問題或緊急情況的訊號或通知；它就是守望者發現異常後發出的提醒。","examples":[{"en":"The alarm system sent an alert to the security team.","zh":"報警系統向安保團隊發出了一條警報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Residents received an alert about the approaching storm.","zh":"居民收到了一條關於暴風雨即將來臨的警報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf19f105e67073b6","term":"alert","forms":["alert","alerts","alerting","alerted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提醒；警告","explanation":"指把危險、問題或重要資訊及時告訴某人，使對方也像守望者一樣提高警覺並採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"Please alert the staff if you see any damage.","zh":"如果你發現任何損壞，請及時通知工作人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report alerted us to a serious safety risk.","zh":"這份報告提醒我們注意一個嚴重的安全風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec752d1d10b6d764a0e3","word":"algebra","forms":["algebra"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cbf1227ef1f09a2","term":"algebra","forms":["algebra","algebras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"初等代數","explanation":"指用字母或其他符號表示未知量，並按照規則在等式、公式中進行運算和求解的數學體系。這是學生課程和日常數學語境中最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I learned algebra in high school, but I still find some equations difficult.","zh":"我在高中學過代數，但有些方程仍然覺得很難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Algebra helps us find the unknown number in this problem.","zh":"代數能幫助我們找出這道題中的未知數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/algebra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dd4fda399a0bb6a","term":"algebra","forms":["algebra","algebras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽象代數","explanation":"指現代數學中更抽象的代數研究領域，關注不同數學結構的性質、分類、對稱關係，以及結構之間保持這些關係的對映。它是在初等代數的符號整理思想上進一步抽象出來的分支。","examples":[{"en":"She is taking a course in abstract algebra this semester.","zh":"她這學期正在上抽象代數課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This algebra course introduces groups, rings, and fields.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/algebra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a49c1d0380688dd9e189","word":"alien","forms":["alien"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3edddb34c15a6a5d","term":"alien","forms":["alien","more alien","most alien"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外國的；外來的","explanation":"指不屬於本國、本地或當前政治、社會群體的事物，重點是“來自圈子外面”。","examples":[{"en":"The new law affects alien residents who have lived here for years.","zh":"這項新法律影響到那些已經在這裡生活多年的外國居民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displays several alien plants brought from overseas.","zh":"這家博物館展出了幾種從海外帶來的外來植物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alien","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-782810b5662f1636","term":"alien","forms":["alien","more alien","most alien"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外星的","explanation":"在科幻或幻想語境中，指屬於地球之外生命的形態、特徵或事物。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists discovered signs of alien life beneath the ice.","zh":"科學家在冰層下發現了外星生命的跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The creature had an alien appearance and moved without making a sound.","zh":"這個生物有著外星般的外貌，行動時一點聲音也沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alien","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ea34e905cd10a03","term":"alien","forms":["alien","aliens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外星人","explanation":"指來自地球之外的生命體，是“圈子外來的生命”這一概念在科幻語境中的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"In the film, an alien hides in a family's garage.","zh":"在這部電影裡，一個外星人藏在一家人的車庫裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children drew pictures of friendly aliens.","zh":"孩子們畫了友善外星人的圖畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alien","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f87d507a0353fdcdefe4","word":"alienate","forms":["alienate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4144a45be0dcf657","term":"alienate","forms":["alienate","alienates","alienating","alienated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使疏遠；使反感","explanation":"指某人的行為、政策或態度破壞了原有的感情和信任，使別人不再親近，甚至對他產生反感；可以想象成把人從原來的關係中推開。","examples":[{"en":"The harsh decision alienated many longtime supporters.","zh":"這項嚴厲的決定使許多長期支持者感到疏遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His constant criticism alienated him from his family.","zh":"他不斷的批評使自己與家人漸漸疏遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alienate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-872a59cecc5e5d2f","term":"alienate","forms":["alienate","alienates","alienating","alienated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉讓所有權","explanation":"指主動放棄並把財產、產權或某項權利的所有權轉給別人，重點是原所有者不再擁有它。","examples":[{"en":"The owner cannot alienate the land without the court's approval.","zh":"未經法院批准，所有者不能轉讓這塊土地的所有權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The deed forbids owners to alienate the property.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alienate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-adcbf60c01c985eef836","word":"align","forms":["align"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4523595d5eb78978","term":"align","forms":["align","aligns","aligning","aligned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排成一列","explanation":"人或物自己移動或排列，使彼此處在同一條線或整齊的佇列中。這個意思就是“線上的東西自己排好了”。","examples":[{"en":"The students aligned along the wall.","zh":"學生們沿著牆排成了一列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Align the tiles carefully along the chalk line.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/align","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e24d22875f3b47b","term":"align","forms":["align","aligns","aligning","aligned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使對齊","explanation":"把物體或人的位置調整到同一條線、同一方向或整齊的排列中，是“把東西拉到線上”。","examples":[{"en":"Please align the chairs with the table.","zh":"請把椅子和桌子對齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She aligned the picture frames along the wall.","zh":"她把畫框沿牆排得整整齊齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/align","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd601657e6ff4ece","term":"align","forms":["align","aligns","aligning","aligned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使一致、協調","explanation":"把計劃、行動、標準或不同部分組織到同一個方向上，使它們彼此協調一致。這裡看不見一條真實的線，但各部分像被拉到了同一條線上。","examples":[{"en":"We need to align our plans with the company's goals.","zh":"我們需要讓計劃與公司的目標保持一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy aligns with our values.","zh":"新政策與我們的價值觀一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/align","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0bd51e0416194e148ce","word":"alike","forms":["alike"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8f672b067da7afb","term":"alike","forms":["alike","more alike","most alike"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相像；相同","explanation":"指人或事物在外表、性質等方面彼此相像，區別不明顯；重點是比較物件之間的相似，而不是說它們完全是同一個東西。","examples":[{"en":"The two sisters look very much alike.","zh":"這兩個姐妹長得非常像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The houses are alike in size but not in color.","zh":"這些房子的大小相同，但顏色不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b8984adcaff03c9","term":"alike","forms":["alike","more alike","most alike"],"pos":"adv","zh":"同樣地；一視同仁地","explanation":"指不同的人或事物受到相同的處理，或以相同的方式、程度發生；可以理解為把它們放在同一標準下。","examples":[{"en":"The coach treats every player alike.","zh":"教練對每一名隊員都一視同仁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rules apply to beginners and experts alike.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-135fc7a09da25f03e44f","word":"alive","forms":["alive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea25767f93bca5a4","term":"alive","forms":["alive","more alive","most alive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"活著的","explanation":"指人、動物或植物仍有生命，沒有死亡；這是 alive 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The fish is still alive.","zh":"這條魚還活著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plant stayed alive through the winter.","zh":"這株植物熬過了冬天，仍然活著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4617a7a6ceea68fe","term":"alive","forms":["alive","more alive","most alive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"仍在發揮作用","explanation":"把“活著”的概念用於火、傳統、希望、討論或計劃時，表示它們還沒有熄滅、停止或失去效力。","examples":[{"en":"They worked hard to keep the old tradition alive.","zh":"他們努力讓這項古老傳統延續下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A little water kept the fire alive.","zh":"加了一點水？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ef5ef0364b6939c4ca6","word":"all","forms":["all"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./pron./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdd8c6badb39d34d","term":"all","forms":["all"],"pos":"adv","zh":"完全；徹底","explanation":"all 放在狀態或程度表達前，表示“整個狀態都達到這個程度”，也就是“完全、徹底”。例如 all alone 是“完全獨自一人”，all done 是“全做完了”。","examples":[{"en":"The room went all quiet when the teacher entered.","zh":"老師進來時，房間一下子完全安靜了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I finished the project all by myself.","zh":"我完全靠自己完成了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0663094764bda87a","term":"all","forms":["all"],"pos":"det","zh":"所有的；全部的","explanation":"all 把一個類別整體圈起來，表示其中沒有例外的每個人、每件事或全部物質。它通常修飾複數名詞或不可數名詞，例如“所有參賽者”或“所有水”。","examples":[{"en":"All students must submit the form by Friday.","zh":"所有學生都必須在星期五前提交表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used all the flour to bake the bread.","zh":"她把所有面粉都用來烤麵包了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ca89cec6a29de54","term":"all","forms":["all"],"pos":"det","zh":"整個；整整","explanation":"all 放在表示時間的詞前，表示這一整段時間從頭到尾都包括在內。all day 是“整天”，all night 是“整夜”。","examples":[{"en":"We walked around the city all day.","zh":"我們在城裡走了一整天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stayed awake all night checking the instruments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52b5045df5cb36b4","term":"all","forms":["all","alls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全部力量；全部所能","explanation":"one's all 指一個人能夠投入的全部力量、努力或能力，彷彿把自己所有能給出的東西都拿出來。","examples":[{"en":"She gave her all to finish the race.","zh":"她為了跑完比賽竭盡了全力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave her all during the final sprint.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b887ce8d6864739","term":"all","forms":["all"],"pos":"pron","zh":"所有的一切","explanation":"all 單獨作代詞時，可以把所有擁有的東西、所有涉及的事情或全部內容合在一起，表示“所有的一切”。","examples":[{"en":"She gave all to protect her family.","zh":"她為了保護家人付出了一切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All was lost when the warehouse burned down.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5c0ec655092f3d01f3f","word":"allege","forms":["allege"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1af3bcdd77b9af94","term":"allege","forms":["allege","alleges","alleging","alleged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聲稱，指稱","explanation":"指提出一個主張，尤其是指責某人做了某事，但說話者並不表示這件事已經得到證明。新聞和法律語境中常用它來保持距離，說明這只是當事方提出的說法。","examples":[{"en":"The report alleges that the company hid safety data.","zh":"報告稱這家公司隱瞞了安全資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She alleged that her supervisor had threatened her.","zh":"她指稱自己的主管曾威脅過她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allege","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d2e0e006393430f5252","word":"allergic","forms":["allergic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35a9beb9fddd7aee","term":"allergic","forms":["allergic","more allergic","most allergic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對……過敏的","explanation":"指人的身體會對某種物質產生過敏反應，例如花粉、食物或動物皮屑；這裡的 allergic 不是一般的喜惡，而是身體層面的強烈反應。","examples":[{"en":"I am allergic to cats, so I take an antihistamine before visiting my sister.","zh":"我對貓過敏，所以去看姐姐之前會服用抗組胺藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you allergic to any ingredients in this soup?","zh":"你對這湯裡的任何成分過敏嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allergic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4e55ab552836358","term":"allergic","forms":["allergic","more allergic","most allergic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"過敏相關的","explanation":"指與過敏或過敏反應有關，常用於醫療、健康等語境，說明某種症狀、藥物或狀況與過敏有關。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor explained that the rash was an allergic reaction.","zh":"醫生解釋說，這種皮疹是過敏反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cream helps relieve allergic inflammation of the skin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allergic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d128b6760194ca992454","word":"allergy","forms":["allergy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a64deac671fad895","term":"allergy","forms":["allergy","allergies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過敏；過敏性反應","explanation":"指身體的免疫系統把通常對大多數人無害的物質當成威脅，因而產生異常反應，例如對花粉、食物或藥物過敏；這裡的重點是“免疫警報器誤鳴”。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter has an allergy to peanuts.","zh":"我女兒對花生過敏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This medicine can cause a serious allergic reaction in people with an allergy to aspirin.","zh":"這種藥可能會讓對阿司匹林過敏的人產生嚴重的過敏反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allergy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63c3db2891ee51be","term":"allergy","forms":["allergy","allergies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴格意義上的免疫性過敏","explanation":"在嚴格的醫學用法中，它專指由免疫系統介導的過敏性超敏反應，而不是所有接觸某物後出現的不耐受或不適。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor confirmed that his rash was caused by an allergy to the drug.","zh":"醫生確認他的皮疹是由藥物過敏引起的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her peanut allergy triggers an immune response within minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allergy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00e7684c0e1559e4078b","word":"alley","forms":["alley"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-905306313164ff93","term":"alley","forms":["alley","alleys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小巷；狹窄通道","explanation":"指建築物之間或街區內部的狹窄通道，常用於通往建築物後方、停車場或後門。它比一般的街道更窄，常帶有“夾在建築物之間”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant has a back entrance in the alley.","zh":"這家餐館在小巷裡有一個後門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked through a quiet alley behind the library.","zh":"我們穿過了圖書館後面一條安靜的小巷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alley","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df78d834fe7d097c","term":"alley","forms":["alley","alleys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外野手之間的空檔","explanation":"在棒球中，alley是兩名外野手之間的區域；球打進這個空檔，就像沿著一條通道飛向外場深處。","examples":[{"en":"The batter drove the ball deep into the alley.","zh":"擊球手把球深深打進了外野手之間的空檔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He drove a double into the left-center alley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alley","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80db4218688d7406fb73","word":"alliance","forms":["alliance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f2b6a5f066646f7","term":"alliance","forms":["alliance","alliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結盟狀態","explanation":"表示處於聯合或結盟的狀態，重點是“已經聯合起來”這一整體情況，而不是某一次具體的結盟行為。","examples":[{"en":"Alliance between the two countries has kept the region stable.","zh":"兩國之間的結盟使該地區保持了穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two kingdoms remained in alliance for decades.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7dc717987f6370fa","term":"alliance","forms":["alliance","alliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯盟；同盟關係","explanation":"表示家庭、國家、政黨等之間為共同利益而建立的具體聯盟或聯絡，常由婚姻、條約、協議或共同目標促成。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries signed an alliance after years of negotiation.","zh":"經過多年的談判，兩國簽署了同盟協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their marriage created a powerful alliance between the two families.","zh":"他們的婚姻使兩個家族結成了強大的聯盟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f00c70d5fa9867d7bd2","word":"alligator","forms":["alligator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac9ce3ca023ad540","term":"alligator","forms":["alligator","alligators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短吻鱷","explanation":"一種生活在河流、湖泊和沼澤等水域附近的大型爬行動物，嘴裡有鋒利牙齒，顎部力量很強；通常特指美洲短吻鱷或中國揚子鱷。","examples":[{"en":"We saw an alligator resting beside the lake.","zh":"我們看見一隻短吻鱷躺在湖邊休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The alligator disappeared beneath the muddy water.","zh":"那隻短吻鱷消失在渾濁的水下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alligator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33b7bcc005217d257f0e","word":"allocate","forms":["allocate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36e12333113dd7fb","term":"allocate","forms":["allocate","allocates","allocating","allocated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為用途預留","explanation":"把資源先留出，明確規定它只能用於某個目的；重點是“這部分已經被指定用途，不能隨便拿來用”。","examples":[{"en":"We allocated part of the budget for emergency repairs.","zh":"我們預留了一部分預算用於緊急維修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the chairs allocated for the visiting students.","zh":"請保留這些給來訪學生使用的椅子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5539902c5e8d1d1c","term":"allocate","forms":["allocate","allocates","allocating","allocated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按計劃分配","explanation":"按照既定計劃，把有限的資源分給不同的人、部門或地方；它把“預留的一堆資源”進一步分成具體的份額。","examples":[{"en":"The committee allocated more funds to rural schools.","zh":"委員會把更多資金分配給了農村學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each team was allocated two hours for the task.","zh":"每個團隊都被分配了兩個小時來完成這項任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-410083735735a10e658a","word":"allow","forms":["allow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94b44ac48faaabbc","term":"allow","forms":["allow","allows","allowing","allowed","allowest","allowedst","alloweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"允許某人做某事","explanation":"表示不阻止某人做某事，核心就是“給他開啟這扇門”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum allows visitors to take photos without flash.","zh":"這家博物館允許遊客在不使用閃光燈的情況下拍照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our teacher does not allow eating in the classroom.","zh":"我們老師不允許在教室裡吃東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-257bf4980f6b96d9","term":"allow","forms":["allow","allows","allowing","allowed","allowest","allowedst","alloweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為某事預留或考慮","explanation":"表示做計劃或估算時主動留出時間、金錢或可能出現的困難，也就是“給未來的變化留出空間”。","examples":[{"en":"Allow for extra time if you are traveling during the holiday.","zh":"如果你在假期出行，要預留額外時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The budget must allow for unexpected repairs.","zh":"預算必須考慮到意外維修的費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32f09fa1e0d7bc303890","word":"allowance","forms":["allowance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-87dfce68dab04255","term":"allowance","forms":["allowance","allowances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固定分配的一份；津貼","explanation":"表示預先分配給某人或某用途的一定數量，尤其是錢、食物或其他供應；孩子定期得到的零花錢就是最典型的allowance。核心概念是“劃出一份，規定只能用這麼多”。","examples":[{"en":"My parents give me a small allowance every Saturday.","zh":"我父母每週六給我一小筆零花錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers received a daily allowance of water.","zh":"徒步者每天得到定量的飲用水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allowance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caa9961ec928c8a1","term":"allowance","forms":["allowance","allowances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酌情餘地；扣除","explanation":"表示在作決定或評估時，先為某種困難、過失或特殊情況留出餘地，再作較公平的判斷。這裡也是“劃出一塊空間”，只是劃出的不是錢或物，而是對情況的寬容和調整。","examples":[{"en":"We should make allowance for the fact that she is new to the job.","zh":"我們應該考慮到她剛開始做這份工作這一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final score makes allowance for difficult weather conditions.","zh":"最終得分考慮了惡劣天氣條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allowance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f41a1bd34b0005cc7e2","word":"ally","forms":["ally"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c0b93350e409d20","term":"ally","forms":["ally","allies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盟友；夥伴","explanation":"指願意與某人合作、幫助某人或站在某人一邊的人，是最基本的“盟友、支持者”意義，不一定涉及正式條約。","examples":[{"en":"She has always been a loyal ally in difficult times.","zh":"在困難時期，她一直是忠實的支持者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need an ally who understands the problem.","zh":"我們需要一位瞭解這個問題的盟友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-334cd5e24f7ee397","term":"ally","forms":["ally","allies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同盟國；結盟的一方","explanation":"指因共同的政治、軍事或其他重要目標而聯合起來的個人、組織或國家，常譯為“盟友”或“同盟國”。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries became allies after signing the treaty.","zh":"兩國簽署條約後成為了盟友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our allies sent supplies to the region.","zh":"我們的盟友向該地區運送了物資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1057f4c01be3892","term":"ally","forms":["ally","allies","allying","allied","allyest","allyeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使聯合；結成聯盟","explanation":"指讓人、家庭、組織或國家聯合起來，形成共同關係或共同目標；核心畫面就是把雙方連到一起。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement allied the two organizations against a common threat.","zh":"這項協議使兩個組織聯合起來，共同應對威脅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The marriage allied two powerful families.","zh":"這樁婚姻使兩個有影響力的家族結成了聯盟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-90e62b92a956add6e1c3","word":"almond","forms":["almond"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93fd719da924afe6","term":"almond","forms":["almond","almonds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"杏仁","explanation":"指杏樹果實中的種子，通常去殼後作為堅果食用；這是最常見、最核心的意義。","examples":[{"en":"I added some chopped almonds to the salad.","zh":"我在沙拉里加了一些切碎的杏仁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These almonds are lightly salted.","zh":"這些杏仁只加了少量鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9602eec8ca1a03bb0860","word":"almost","forms":["almost"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8aeeb2a962609d31","term":"almost","forms":["almost"],"pos":"adv","zh":"幾乎；差一點","explanation":"表示某事非常接近某個狀態或結果，但實際上還沒有完全達到；可以理解為已經到了終點線附近，只差一點。","examples":[{"en":"The train was almost empty when we boarded.","zh":"我們上車時，火車裡幾乎空無一人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I almost forgot your birthday.","zh":"我差點忘了你的生日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c2598cec5537547","term":"almost","forms":["almost"],"pos":"adv","zh":"幾乎全部；除極少數外","explanation":"用於數量或範圍時，表示其中絕大多數都包括在內，但根據語境仍可能有少數例外；almost all people 就是“幾乎所有人”，不等於每一個人。","examples":[{"en":"Almost all the students submitted their work on time.","zh":"幾乎所有學生都按時交了作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Almost everyone in the village attended the ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-facf8b54e5c0b8c426bb","word":"alone","forms":["alone"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b62ba7e23ce7de5","term":"alone","forms":["alone"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獨自；單獨","explanation":"表示一個人沒有同伴，或某物沒有其他東西陪同；核心畫面就是“一個人單獨站著”。","examples":[{"en":"I can't ask for help because I am alone.","zh":"我一個人，沒法尋求幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She walked home alone after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，她獨自走回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-567249a3b6a50d83","term":"alone","forms":["alone"],"pos":"adv","zh":"獨自地；單獨地","explanation":"表示某人沒有別人陪同而行動，或某事由一個人單獨完成；核心仍是“一個人站著做這件事”。","examples":[{"en":"She walked home alone.","zh":"她獨自走回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He prefers to travel alone.","zh":"他更喜歡獨自旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fbc17ea2a8ba2af","term":"alone","forms":["alone"],"pos":"adv","zh":"只有；唯有","explanation":"緊跟在名詞後，表示只有這個人或這個機構擁有某種權力、資格或作用，其他人不算在內。它把注意力從整體中圈出一個物件。","examples":[{"en":"The president alone has the power to approve the plan.","zh":"只有總統有權批准這項計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Experience alone cannot guarantee sound judgment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-768c49c9383c77ac0a2a","word":"along","forms":["along"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-394b61623283d20e","term":"along","forms":["along"],"pos":"adv","zh":"一起；跟著做","explanation":"表示加入別人正在做的事情，和大家一起行動或一起發出聲音。這裡的畫面不是“沿著某處”，而是和別人朝同一個方向一起做事。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone sang along with the band.","zh":"大家都跟著樂隊一起唱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She laughed along with her friends.","zh":"她和朋友們一起笑了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/along","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-349786f8fa6e128a","term":"along","forms":["along"],"pos":"prep","zh":"沿著；順著","explanation":"表示某物位於一條有長度的線、邊或路線旁，或人在這條線上移動。可以把它想成沿著長路、河岸或牆邊展開。","examples":[{"en":"There are small shops along the river.","zh":"河邊沿線有一些小商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked along the beach at sunset.","zh":"日落時我們沿著海灘散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/along","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0cfcdc2f0991b0be4482","word":"alongside","forms":["alongside"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17d6565f4d6997b7","term":"alongside","forms":["alongside"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在旁邊；並排","explanation":"表示某物來到另一物的側邊，和它並排處在一起；核心畫面就是兩樣東西貼著側面排列。","examples":[{"en":"The small boat moved alongside the ferry.","zh":"小船駛到渡輪旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our canoe drifted alongside as they repaired their paddle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alongside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c23fc27f94bd2ac","term":"alongside","forms":["alongside"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……旁邊；與……並排","explanation":"把某物放在另一物的側邊，或讓兩者並排移動，重點仍是“肩並肩”的空間關係。","examples":[{"en":"A row of bicycles stood alongside the wall.","zh":"一排腳踏車停在牆邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow footpath runs alongside the railway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alongside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02bd3abc3c5423e9","term":"alongside","forms":["alongside"],"pos":"prep","zh":"與……一起；同時","explanation":"從“並排在一起”引申為和某人或某事一起行動、合作，或與另一件事同時發生。","examples":[{"en":"She worked alongside experienced volunteers.","zh":"她和有經驗的志願者一起工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Volunteers worked alongside nurses throughout the emergency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alongside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd8b4b29bdd97ed50aa4","word":"aloud","forms":["aloud"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f85ddb8bb43b3dc","term":"aloud","forms":["aloud"],"pos":"adv","zh":"大聲地；出聲地","explanation":"表示用嘴把話說出來，並以足夠讓人聽見的聲音發出；有時也帶有聲音較大的意味。核心畫面是把聲音從心裡或低聲狀態中放到外面。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the instructions aloud so everyone can follow them.","zh":"請把說明大聲讀出來，好讓大家都能跟上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She said the new words aloud several times.","zh":"她把這些生詞出聲說了好幾遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aloud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ca4fee1a1340766","term":"aloud","forms":["aloud"],"pos":"adv","zh":"出聲地，而非默默地","explanation":"強調一個想法、答案或文字不是隻在腦中默想，而是實際說了出來並能被聽到。重點在“說出口”這一對比，而不在聲音的大小。","examples":[{"en":"I was only thinking about the answer, but I accidentally said it aloud.","zh":"我本來只是在心裡想答案，卻不小心把它說了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the instructions aloud for everyone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aloud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4dd4f3835505cd95950f","word":"alphabet","forms":["alphabet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-125f32676bd01125","term":"alphabet","forms":["alphabet","alphabets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一門語言的整套字母","explanation":"指一門語言書寫時使用的全部字母，重點是“整套字母的集合”，而不是其中某一個字母。例如英語的二十六個字母合在一起，就是英語的alphabet。","examples":[{"en":"Children learn the English alphabet before they read simple books.","zh":"孩子們在閱讀簡單書籍前先學習英語字母表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Greek alphabet has only twenty-four letters.","zh":"希臘字母表只有二十四個字母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alphabet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efbea389eca44842","term":"alphabet","forms":["alphabet","alphabets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"字母書寫系統","explanation":"指一種用字母表示語音的書寫系統。這裡關注的不只是字母清單，還包括用這些字母記錄語言聲音的整套方式，與用單個字元表示詞語的文字系統或表示音節的音節文字相對。","examples":[{"en":"Unlike Chinese characters, the Latin alphabet represents sounds with separate letters.","zh":"不同於漢字，拉丁字母用分開的字母表示聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The language adopted the Latin alphabet centuries ago.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alphabet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea53396caebc40d702a9","word":"already","forms":["already"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3cef2305bbcdf54a","term":"already","forms":["already"],"pos":"adv","zh":"已經","explanation":"表示某事在現在、過去某時或未來某個參照時間之前就完成或發生了；重點是“那盞燈在相關時間點前已經亮起”。","examples":[{"en":"She has already sent the report.","zh":"她已經把報告發出去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By noon, we had already finished the work.","zh":"到中午時，我們已經完成了工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/already","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57e4b077f8734c84","term":"already","forms":["already"],"pos":"adv","zh":"這麼快就","explanation":"表示某事比說話人預期更早發生，常常帶有驚訝意味；燈亮得太快，所以可譯為“這麼快就……了”。","examples":[{"en":"Are you leaving already?","zh":"你這麼快就要走了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is the cake already gone? I just sliced it!","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/already","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb8c8605c55dcc2d650e","word":"also","forms":["also"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-704cd0f6cc9b538a","term":"also","forms":["also"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也；還","explanation":"在已經提到一個情況之後，再補充一個同類情況，表示“也、還”。它可以說明另一個人做了同樣的事，也可以說明同一個物件還有另一項特點。","examples":[{"en":"I also want to join the meeting.","zh":"我也想參加這次會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel is clean and also very quiet.","zh":"這家酒店很乾淨，而且也非常安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/also","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c0ea37f8baaead4a586","word":"alter","forms":["alter"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49ed8b8047071496","term":"alter","forms":["alter","alters","altering","altered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改變；改動","explanation":"把某物的形狀、結構、安排或狀態改成另一種樣子，重點是“使它不同”，不一定意味著徹底重做。","examples":[{"en":"We had to alter the design to make room for the new equipment.","zh":"我們不得不修改設計，為新裝置騰出空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A few small changes can alter the way the room feels.","zh":"幾個小改動就能改變這個房間給人的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0248f55d6928124","term":"alter","forms":["alter","alters","altering","altered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發生變化","explanation":"主語本身變得不同，而不是主動把另一個東西改掉；可以說外貌、情況、聲音或觀點逐漸發生變化。","examples":[{"en":"The landscape began to alter as the road climbed higher.","zh":"隨著道路不斷升高，景色開始發生變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her priorities altered after she became a parent.","zh":"她成為父母后，生活重點發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f251db73f53a7fba194","word":"alternate","forms":["alternate"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00254cb14f8e65a2","term":"alternate","forms":["alternate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"輪流的；交替的","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物按照次序一個接一個地出現或發生，重點是這種輪換會重複進行。","examples":[{"en":"The team works on alternate days.","zh":"這個團隊隔天工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Light and shadow alternate along the path.","zh":"小路上光影交替出現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alternate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cedf36ffd113d53d","term":"alternate","forms":["alternate","alternates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"替代者；候補者","explanation":"指在原來的人不能履行職責時，預先指定來接替他的人。它把“替代的”這個概念具體化為一個可以頂上的人。","examples":[{"en":"She was chosen as an alternate for the committee.","zh":"她被選為委員會的候補成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An alternate stepped in when the lead dancer fell ill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alternate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81951cf6c618d006","term":"alternate","forms":["alternate","alternates","alternating","alternated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輪流發生；交替","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物自己按次序一個接一個地發生或行動，核心畫面就是輪流上場。","examples":[{"en":"The rain alternated with bright sunshine all afternoon.","zh":"整個下午時而下雨，時而陽光明媚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two presenters alternate throughout the program.","zh":"兩位主持人在整個節目中輪流出場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alternate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27747689baf9903c9aae","word":"alternative","forms":["alternative"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e97e6b672a485dc","term":"alternative","forms":["alternative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可供選擇的","explanation":"表示某個方案、意見或做法可以作為多個可能性中的一項來考慮，重點是“有別的選擇可選”。","examples":[{"en":"The committee considered an alternative proposal.","zh":"委員會考慮了一個可供選擇的提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need an alternative plan in case the weather changes.","zh":"我們需要一個備用方案，以防天氣發生變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alternative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-335f914a143267b6","term":"alternative","forms":["alternative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"另一種的；不同的","explanation":"表示某個事物不是正在談論的那個，而是與它不同的另一種可能；這裡不一定涉及正式的二選一。","examples":[{"en":"They are looking for an alternative way to reduce costs.","zh":"他們正在尋找另一種降低成本的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need an alternative entrance while repairs continue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alternative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec023f010e924ad2","term":"alternative","forms":["alternative","alternatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇；選擇局面","explanation":"表示必須在兩個或多個彼此排斥的可能性之間作出選擇的情況，重點是“只能選其中一種”。","examples":[{"en":"The alternative is to leave now or wait until morning.","zh":"可選擇的辦法是現在離開，或者等到早上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Faced with that alternative, she chose to resign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alternative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-2e1d76579d44d7cfe5f3","word":"although","forms":["although"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"although","forms":["although"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"雖然；儘管","examples":[{"en":"Although it was raining, the game continued.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"I enjoyed the film, although the ending was sad.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0a708d7a9b0c25273ca","word":"altitude","forms":["altitude"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-911934c9bc54796b","term":"altitude","forms":["altitude","altitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海拔高度","explanation":"指某個地點相對於海平面的高度，尤其常用於山地、飛機和高原等語境。這裡的重點是統一以海平面為基準來量高度，而不是隻看它離附近地面的距離。","examples":[{"en":"At this altitude, the air is thin and the nights are very cold.","zh":"在這個海拔高度，空氣稀薄，夜裡也非常冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plane began to descend after reaching an altitude of ten thousand meters.","zh":"飛機達到一萬米的高度後開始下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/altitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a01a6f09607cb021","term":"altitude","forms":["altitude","altitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"垂直距離","explanation":"泛指豎直方向上量出的距離，可以是兩個點之間的高度差，也可以是某個物體從底部到頂部的高度。它比“海拔高度”更寬，不一定以海平面為基準。","examples":[{"en":"The instrument measures the altitude between the roof and the ground.","zh":"這個儀器測量屋頂與地面之間的垂直距離。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Calculate the triangle's altitude from its base and area.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/altitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87e56ce6429768c90138","word":"altogether","forms":["altogether"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cfd3556854a39b64","term":"altogether","forms":["altogether"],"pos":"adv","zh":"完全；全然","explanation":"表示某種狀態達到完全程度，或“沒有例外地”如此。它常修飾形容詞、分詞等，強調程度，但不一定表示說話人完全贊同這個判斷。","examples":[{"en":"I am not altogether convinced by his explanation.","zh":"我並沒有完全被他的解釋說服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan was altogether impractical.","zh":"這個計劃完全不切實際。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/altogether","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91f82dd0ed6e6583","term":"altogether","forms":["altogether"],"pos":"adv","zh":"總的來說；總體上","explanation":"把各方面情況合在一起考慮後，給出總體判斷，相當於“總的來看”或“綜合考慮”。這裡強調的是整體評價，不是某一項達到完全程度。","examples":[{"en":"Altogether, the trip was more enjoyable than I expected.","zh":"總的來說，這次旅行比我預想的更愉快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Altogether, the expedition was worth the expense.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/altogether","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42592d8f0f1badc8","term":"altogether","forms":["altogether"],"pos":"adv","zh":"總共；合計","explanation":"把若干項數量、費用或部分合在一起計算，得到最後的總數。這個意思仍然來自“全部合到一起”，但重點是實際的合計結果。","examples":[{"en":"Altogether, we spent three hundred dollars on the repairs.","zh":"修理費用合計花了三百美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs cost eight hundred dollars altogether.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/altogether","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-faaa92f6df65089fb68b","word":"aluminum","forms":["aluminum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-994c0baf2003c6fc","term":"aluminum","forms":["aluminum","aluminums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋁（美式拼寫）","explanation":"指一種銀白色金屬，也可指用作材料的鋁；aluminum 與 aluminium 意義相同，只是地區拼寫不同。","examples":[{"en":"The frame is made of aluminum.","zh":"這個框架是鋁製的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This aluminum can is easy to recycle.","zh":"這個鋁罐很容易回收。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aluminum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9cdc6c47aa193ae7fdab","word":"always","forms":["always"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd5afa9a7653c132","term":"always","forms":["always"],"pos":"adv","zh":"始終；永遠","explanation":"表示從過去到現在，或在所說的整個時間範圍內，情況一直如此，沒有間斷。它強調的是貫穿全部時間，而不只是經常發生。","examples":[{"en":"She has always loved books.","zh":"她一直都喜歡書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sky is always clear here in winter.","zh":"這裡冬天的天空總是晴朗的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/always","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bff4b9b6ae2e373b","term":"always","forms":["always"],"pos":"adv","zh":"總是；一向","explanation":"表示在某個特定時期內反覆、按習慣或按固定規律發生，重點是“每次或通常都這樣”，不一定延續到所有時間。","examples":[{"en":"Our neighbors always walk their dog after dinner.","zh":"我們的鄰居總是在晚飯後遛狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Grandpa always whistles while he washes the dishes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/always","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84fdec857493387658fa","word":"am/a.m.","forms":["a.m."],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a44c077b22bc107","term":"a.m.","forms":["a.m."],"pos":"adv","zh":"上午；午前","explanation":"它把一天標在從午夜到中午的前半段；因此說某事發生在 A.M.，就是說發生在上午或午前。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic opens at 8 A.M. on weekdays.","zh":"這家診所工作日上午八點開門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I usually finish my exercise before 10 A.M.","zh":"我通常在上午十點前做完運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/a.m.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8dd9ed10798ded82a255","word":"amateur","forms":["amateur"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21478344569a3828","term":"amateur","forms":["amateur","more amateur","most amateur"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非職業的；業餘的","explanation":"指不是以某項活動為職業、而是出於興趣參與的。它強調身份或參與方式，不直接判斷這個人的水平高低。","examples":[{"en":"She is an amateur photographer, but her pictures are excellent.","zh":"她是一名業餘攝影愛好者，但她拍的照片非常出色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The club welcomes amateur astronomers.","zh":"這個俱樂部歡迎業餘天文學愛好者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amateur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e16dee1da6149c67","term":"amateur","forms":["amateur","more amateur","most amateur"],"pos":"adj","zh":"業餘人士製作或參與的","explanation":"指由非職業人士創作、完成或參加的事物，例如業餘運動或業餘比賽。重點在參與者不是職業人員，而不一定表示成果很差。","examples":[{"en":"The town holds an amateur drama festival every summer.","zh":"這個小鎮每年夏天都會舉辦業餘戲劇節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival opened with an amateur production of Hamlet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amateur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad6446e975a27fd0","term":"amateur","forms":["amateur","amateurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"業餘愛好者；非職業參與者","explanation":"指出於興趣學習或從事某項活動、但不以此為職業的人。這個人可以很有水平，核心仍是“熱愛並參與，卻不是職業人士”。","examples":[{"en":"The competition is open to amateurs and professionals.","zh":"這項比賽向業餘人士和專業人士開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An amateur photographed the comet from his garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amateur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9e9acdceb79d4006e4dc","word":"amaze(ment)","forms":["amaze","amazement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3cfb4232de4b46d1","term":"amaze","forms":["amaze","amazes","amazing","amazed","amazest","amazedst","amazeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使驚訝；使驚歎","explanation":"指某件事強烈地衝擊人的預期，使人驚訝、驚歎，甚至一時說不出話。這是 amaze 在現代英語中的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"The magician's final trick amazed everyone in the audience.","zh":"魔術師最後的絕技讓現場每個人都驚歎不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was amazed by how quickly she solved the problem.","zh":"她解決這個問題的速度讓我驚歎不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9242fadd6300aa31","term":"amazement","forms":["amazement","amazements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚愕；驚歎","explanation":"指面對意外、非同尋常或令人震撼的事情時產生的強烈驚訝和驚歎，常常帶有一時說不出話、目瞪口呆的感覺。這是現代英語中最重要、最常見的含義。","examples":[{"en":"She stared at the painting in amazement.","zh":"她驚愕地盯著那幅畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"To my amazement, the old computer still worked.","zh":"令我驚訝的是，那臺舊電腦居然還能執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amazement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb74b011cacb3da551f9","word":"ambassador","forms":["ambassador"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dfd412acdc977ca2","term":"ambassador","forms":["ambassador","ambassadors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"駐外大使","explanation":"指國家派到外國、代表本國政府或國家元首開展外交工作的最高階別外交官。這個人不只是傳話，還要正式維護本國的立場和利益。","examples":[{"en":"The ambassador to France met with the foreign minister.","zh":"駐法國大使會見了外交部長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was appointed ambassador to Japan last year.","zh":"她去年被任命為駐日本大使。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambassador","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-895b6cb63f5f5155","term":"ambassador","forms":["ambassador","ambassadors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式使者；代表","explanation":"泛指被派去傳達立場、完成任務或代表某一方的人。它保留了“代表並傳達資訊”的核心，但不一定具有大使的外交級別。","examples":[{"en":"The king sent an ambassador to negotiate peace.","zh":"國王派了一名使者去談判和平協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An ambassador arrived carrying the emperor's reply to our proposal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambassador","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0978cd572355e3636beb","word":"ambiguity","forms":["ambiguity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-227ecc395b6e1484","term":"ambiguity","forms":["ambiguity","ambiguities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歧義狀態；含義不明確","explanation":"指一種整體狀態：說話、寫作或資訊留下了多個可能的解釋，讀者或聽者無法確定真正的含義。這裡關注的是“模糊不清”這一狀態，而不是某一個具體的模糊詞句。","examples":[{"en":"The ambiguity in the instructions caused several teams to make the wrong choice.","zh":"說明中的歧義導致幾個團隊作出了錯誤選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contract was rewritten to remove any ambiguity.","zh":"這份合同經過重寫，以消除任何歧義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambiguity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4af230874fd18f1b","term":"ambiguity","forms":["ambiguity","ambiguities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一處具體歧義","explanation":"指一句話、一個詞或一段說明中具體存在的多種解釋。它是前面那種“模糊狀態”的一個例項，可以單獨指出、分析或列舉。","examples":[{"en":"There is an ambiguity in the final sentence of the report.","zh":"報告最後一句中有一處歧義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A misplaced comma introduced an ambiguity into the contract.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambiguity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a651134eb4b24becd9a","word":"ambiguous","forms":["ambiguous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9bd772cbb07400a7","term":"ambiguous","forms":["ambiguous","more ambiguous","most ambiguous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含義不明確的；有多種解釋的","explanation":"指一句話、一個答案、規則或立場沒有清楚地指向唯一意思，因此不同的人可能作出不同理解；這正是“在岔路口向不同方向延伸”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The contract uses ambiguous language about who pays for repairs.","zh":"這份合同在維修費用由誰承擔的問題上措辭含糊不清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her ambiguous answer left us unsure whether she agreed.","zh":"她含義不明的回答讓我們不確定她是否同意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambiguous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ab02ca2432a47c41c76","word":"ambition","forms":["ambition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ffec653b7c4f03c1","term":"ambition","forms":["ambition","ambitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雄心；抱負","explanation":"指一個人強烈地想獲得成就、地位、榮譽、權力或聲望的願望，重點在於向上爭取和證明自己。這種願望可以受到讚賞，也可能因過分強烈而顯得自私。","examples":[{"en":"She has the ambition to become a doctor.","zh":"她有成為醫生的抱負。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His ambition drove him to work harder every day.","zh":"他的雄心推動他每天更加努力地工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c245e20df67e9f7","term":"ambition","forms":["ambition","ambitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抱負；目標","explanation":"指一個人強烈想實現的具體事情，是“雄心”所指向的目標，而不是追求成功的心理品質本身。","examples":[{"en":"My ambition is to write a novel.","zh":"我的目標是寫一部小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her ambition is to design affordable artificial limbs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e428ee1e7df9cd6b863c","word":"ambitious","forms":["ambitious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98aa4527356ba7d7","term":"ambitious","forms":["ambitious","ambitiouser","more ambitious","ambitiousest","most ambitious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有抱負的；有野心的","explanation":"形容人想取得很大成就、地位或影響力，並且有強烈的進取願望。它可以讚美一個人目標明確、積極上進，也可以暗示其追求權力或榮譽過多，具體感情色彩要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"She is ambitious and hopes to lead the company one day.","zh":"她很有抱負，希望有一天能領導這家公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is an ambitious politician who wants more influence.","zh":"他是個野心很大的政治家，想獲得更大的影響力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambitious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d84cd7b24079808b","term":"ambitious","forms":["ambitious","ambitiouser","more ambitious","ambitiousest","most ambitious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"雄心勃勃的；要求很高的","explanation":"形容計劃、專案、目標或行動體現出很大的抱負：它想達到的範圍廣、影響大，或者需要投入很多資源和能力。這裡不是說計劃“有性格”，而是說它背後有很大的目標。","examples":[{"en":"The city has announced an ambitious plan to reduce traffic.","zh":"這座城市宣佈了一項雄心勃勃的減堵計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They launched an ambitious project to restore the old theater.","zh":"他們啟動了一個要求很高的專案，準備修復那座老劇院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambitious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-efdfcc0967c1b7cfe88a","word":"ambulance","forms":["ambulance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af2827b0c8b6abb1","term":"ambulance","forms":["ambulance","ambulances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"救護車","explanation":"ambulance 最常指配有急救裝置、把重病或受傷者送往醫院的車輛。它的核心形象就是一座在路上移動的急救站。","examples":[{"en":"Someone has been hurt—call an ambulance!","zh":"有人受傷了——快叫救護車！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ambulance took her to the nearest hospital.","zh":"救護車把她送到了最近的醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ambulance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eaf4242791d184c6f2ea","word":"amend","forms":["amend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-285d9e2005618286","term":"amend","forms":["amend","amends","amending","amended","amendest","amendedst","amendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改進；使變好","explanation":"表示主動修正有問題的事物，使它變得更好，可以用於做法、計劃、文字或狀況。這個義項體現了“把毛病修好”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The company amended its policy after receiving complaints.","zh":"公司收到投訴後修改了政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fresh planting would amend the neglected courtyard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91d4d312c8f346de","term":"amend","forms":["amend","amends","amending","amended","amendest","amendedst","amendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式修訂","explanation":"表示透過增加、刪除或改寫文字，正式修改法律、報告等檔案。這是“把有問題的內容修好”在制度和文字中的重要用法。","examples":[{"en":"Parliament voted to amend the law.","zh":"議會投票決定修訂這項法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parliament amended the law to include domestic workers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f27280293d3b0bb2786d","word":"amid/amidst","forms":["amid","amidst"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-530136ab4bcf168b","term":"amid","forms":["amid"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……之中；被……包圍","explanation":"表示人或事物處在一片環境、事物或人群的中央，四周都被它們包圍。它強調“身處其中”的畫面，而不只是抽象地說明地點。","examples":[{"en":"She remained calm amid the confusion.","zh":"她在一片混亂中仍然保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small café stood amid the trees.","zh":"一間小咖啡館坐落在樹木之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3392e45d74baf3b","term":"amidst","forms":["amidst"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……之中；被……包圍","explanation":"表示某人或某物處在一片事物、環境或局勢的包圍之中。它可以描述具體的周圍環境，也可以描述抽象的困難、變化或情緒，核心畫面都是“身處其中”。","examples":[{"en":"Amidst the noise of the market, she found a quiet corner.","zh":"在市場的喧鬧聲中，她找到了一個安靜的角落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He remained calm amidst all the confusion.","zh":"在一片混亂之中，他仍然保持鎮定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amidst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-766c1d13a3e06c4dfcfc","word":"among","forms":["among"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-376ed1e7bacef108","term":"among","forms":["among"],"pos":"prep","zh":"混在……之中","explanation":"表示某人或某物處在一群彼此分開的物件中，與它們混在一起或共同生活、活動。重點是“進入一個群體內部”，不只是位於兩個東西之間。","examples":[{"en":"She lived among the local farmers for a year.","zh":"她在當地農民中生活了一年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small red flower stood among the tall grasses.","zh":"一朵小紅花立在高高的草叢中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/among","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2de48d179e3f90d1","term":"among","forms":["among"],"pos":"prep","zh":"屬於……之列","explanation":"表示某人或某物屬於一個群體、類別或數量範圍，是“在這群人或事物當中”的意思，常用來指出某個成員或少數成員。","examples":[{"en":"Maya was among the first students to arrive.","zh":"瑪雅是最早到達的學生之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This book is among the most useful guides for beginners.","zh":"這本書屬於最實用的入門指南之列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/among","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf38d95c9c6b1d9d5125","word":"amount","forms":["amount"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-341e34c5b107a736","term":"amount","forms":["amount","amounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總量","explanation":"指某種物質、資源或現象累積起來的總量，重點是把它看作一個整體，而不是逐個數出的專案。","examples":[{"en":"The amount of waste produced by the city is increasing every year.","zh":"這座城市產生的廢物總量每年都在增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to reduce the amount of energy we use.","zh":"我們需要減少能源使用量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c14ec87623819de","term":"amount","forms":["amount","amounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一份；分量","explanation":"指某種東西的一定分量或體積，常用於說明要取、倒入、使用多少。","examples":[{"en":"Add a small amount of salt to the soup.","zh":"往湯里加少量鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Set aside a small amount for emergencies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d3e197a6fa4a545","term":"amount","forms":["amount","amounts","amounting","amounted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"總計為","explanation":"表示把錢、數字或各項數值加在一起後，總數達到某個數額，核心仍是“堆積後達到的總量”。","examples":[{"en":"The repairs amounted to more than five hundred dollars.","zh":"維修費用總計超過了五百美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All the small expenses amount to a considerable sum.","zh":"所有這些小額開支加起來是一筆相當可觀的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff44b37dca63b0db0f9d","word":"ample","forms":["ample"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70390c354877f23c","term":"ample","forms":["ample","ampler","amplest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬大；寬敞","explanation":"指空間、範圍、容量或體量很寬大，足以容納或覆蓋較多內容；重點是“有很大的餘地”，而不只是尺寸大。","examples":[{"en":"The new library has ample room for study groups.","zh":"新圖書館有足夠寬敞的空間供學習小組使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An ample cloak covered his winter clothing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ample","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c253d9f65dcc298","term":"ample","forms":["ample"],"pos":"det","zh":"足夠而有餘","explanation":"放在名詞前，表示數量完全夠用，而且通常還有餘量；它把“寬大的容器”這個形象轉成了“寬裕的份量”。","examples":[{"en":"We have ample time to finish the project before Friday.","zh":"我們有充裕的時間在星期五前完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cellar provides ample storage for our winter vegetables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ample","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29e60c5e58d13ce60ed5","word":"amplify","forms":["amplify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecfb51e1d362f635","term":"amplify","forms":["amplify","amplifies","amplifying","amplified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放大；增強","explanation":"把某種聲音、效果或影響變得更強、更明顯，核心仍是把原有的東西“擰大”。","examples":[{"en":"The microphone amplifies her voice so everyone can hear her.","zh":"麥克風放大了她的聲音，讓大家都能聽見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Social media can amplify a small mistake.","zh":"社交媒體可能會放大一個小錯誤的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amplify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a545d7e97ba37b7f","term":"amplify","forms":["amplify","amplifies","amplifying","amplified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擴充；詳加說明","explanation":"在已有文字、觀點或說明上新增細節、例子或解釋，使內容更充分、更展開；這也是把原來的內容“放大”到更大的篇幅。","examples":[{"en":"Could you amplify your explanation with a simple example?","zh":"你能用一個簡單的例子把你的解釋講得更詳細些嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness amplified her statement with several concrete details.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amplify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48da16de2a38c91048fb","word":"amuse(ment)","forms":["amuse","amusement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-781030d7dcd68f5d","term":"amuse","forms":["amuse","amuses","amusing","amused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使開心；逗樂","explanation":"某件事以愉快、有趣的方式吸引某人的注意力，讓對方開心或覺得好玩。它強調的是帶來輕鬆愉快的感受，不一定真的讓人笑出聲。","examples":[{"en":"The children were amused by the magician's silly tricks.","zh":"孩子們被魔術師滑稽的小把戲逗得很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I watch these movies because they amuse me.","zh":"我看這些電影是因為它們能讓我開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f06d92a078edcf0","term":"amuse","forms":["amuse","amuses","amusing","amused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逗笑；使發笑","explanation":"這裡把“使人開心”具體化為“使人覺得好笑並笑出來”。笑話、滑稽的行為或意外場面都可以 amuse 某人。","examples":[{"en":"Her impression of the teacher amused everyone at the party.","zh":"她模仿老師的樣子把聚會上的每個人都逗笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her imitation of the conductor amused everyone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96373daa0744b244","term":"amusement","forms":["amusement","amusements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂趣；娛樂","explanation":"指觀看或經歷有趣事情時產生的開心和消遣感，重點是“得到的樂趣”，而不是某一項具體活動。","examples":[{"en":"To my amusement, the cat tried to climb into the tiny box.","zh":"令我覺得好笑的是，那隻貓試圖鑽進那個小盒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She watched the street performers for amusement.","zh":"她觀看街頭藝人表演來消遣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amusement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d4d51a53a0f7e35","term":"amusement","forms":["amusement","amusements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消遣活動；娛樂活動","explanation":"指為了獲得樂趣而進行的一項具體活動，例如跳舞、釣魚或其他休閒活動；這裡強調“做什麼來娛樂”。","examples":[{"en":"Dancing was a favorite amusement at the summer party.","zh":"跳舞是夏日聚會上大家最喜歡的娛樂活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fishing became his favorite amusement during retirement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amusement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd7bdeae637576ba80a7","word":"analogy","forms":["analogy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aafd1cdca3655572","term":"analogy","forms":["analogy","analogies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"類比；相似對應","explanation":"指兩個情況、人物或物體在某些方面相似，因此可以把一個用來幫助解釋或推測另一個。它不是說兩者完全相同，而是藉助這座“相似之橋”來理解問題。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher used an analogy between the brain and a computer to explain how memory works.","zh":"老師把大腦和電腦作類比，以解釋記憶是怎樣運作的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a useful analogy between learning a language and training a muscle.","zh":"學習語言和鍛鍊肌肉之間有一個很有幫助的類比。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analogy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f44e85c4b8ea2addc796","word":"analysis","forms":["analysis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a1ca21b097dbd55","term":"analysis","forms":["analysis","analyses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拆解研究","explanation":"把複雜的事物、概念或理論拆成幾個部分，分別研究它們的特點和關係，這個過程叫 analysis。重點不只是“看一看”，而是有條理地拆開並理解整體。","examples":[{"en":"The report includes a comparative analysis of the two companies.","zh":"這份報告包括對兩家公司的比較分析。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her analysis of the problem revealed several hidden causes.","zh":"她對這個問題的分析揭示了幾個隱藏的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analysis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6050dc3260374e9e","term":"analysis","forms":["analysis","analyses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分析結果","explanation":"analysis 也可以指拆解研究之後形成的解釋、判斷或結論，也就是“分析結果”。因此它既能指做分析這件事，也能指寫出來或說出來的那份分析。","examples":[{"en":"According to the analysis, the fall in sales was temporary.","zh":"根據這份分析，銷量下降只是暫時的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His analysis was clear, but the conclusion was too optimistic.","zh":"他的分析很清楚，但結論過於樂觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analysis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f44ceb062e35dfeea6ed","word":"analyst","forms":["analyst"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa7357ae2fe8d050","term":"analyst","forms":["analyst","analysts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分析者","explanation":"泛指透過研究資料、事實或問題的各個部分來形成判斷的人。這是 analyst 最寬的含義，其他許多專業稱呼都可以看作它在特定領域中的具體化。","examples":[{"en":"The analyst examined the data before making a recommendation.","zh":"這名分析師先研究了資料，然後提出建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An analyst can help us understand what went wrong.","zh":"分析人員可以幫助我們弄清楚出了什麼問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analyst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b74f5c55b35fe2e2","term":"analyst","forms":["analyst","analysts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金融或商業分析師","explanation":"指分析市場、公司、行業或業務資料，並據此評估風險、表現或發展方向的專業人員。這是現實職場和新聞中最常見的具體用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The financial analyst expects the company's profits to rise next year.","zh":"這名金融分析師預計公司明年的利潤會增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A business analyst helped the company reduce delivery costs.","zh":"一名商業分析師幫助公司降低了配送成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analyst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05aa6659dbc4d45231c4","word":"analytical","forms":["analytical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d36530e869c204f","term":"analytical","forms":["analytical","more analytical","most analytical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"分析的；解析性的","explanation":"指圍繞分析展開，或透過把整體拆成要素來研究的。它可以修飾方法、過程、實驗等，重點是弄清各部分及其關係。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used an analytical method to identify the substance.","zh":"研究人員採用分析方法來鑑定這種物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report provides an analytical study of the causes of the problem.","zh":"這份報告對問題的原因進行了分析性研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analytical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-045b74ba55d38335","term":"analytical","forms":["analytical","more analytical","most analytical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"善於分析推理的","explanation":"形容人的頭腦或思考方式善於把複雜問題拆開，比較各個部分並根據理由得出判斷。這裡的“分析”從一種方法延伸成了穩定的思維特點。","examples":[{"en":"Her analytical mind helped her find the error in the plan.","zh":"她善於分析的頭腦幫助她找出了計劃中的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His analytical mind quickly spotted the contradiction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analytical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09cbad3beca70ddbcc89","word":"analyze","forms":["analyze"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ca53ad3b8d16bbbb","term":"analyze","forms":["analyze","analyzes","analyzing","analyzed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分析某事","explanation":"對某個問題、情況或物件進行系統考察，試圖弄清它是怎樣構成的、為什麼會這樣或意味著什麼。","examples":[{"en":"The team analyzed the survey results before making a decision.","zh":"團隊在作出決定前分析了調查結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We analyzed the water to identify the contaminant.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analyze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83d96e59bfd3969f","term":"analyze","forms":["analyze","analyzes","analyzing","analyzed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分解複雜問題","explanation":"把一個難以直接理解的整體拆成若干要素或步驟，再分別檢視，從而解決或理解它。","examples":[{"en":"Let's analyze the problem one step at a time.","zh":"我們一步一步地分析這個問題吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineer analyzed the system to find the source of the failure.","zh":"工程師分析了這個系統，以找出故障的來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/analyze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d490151378f5fc99bba9","word":"ancestor","forms":["ancestor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2eda6c308a434e47","term":"ancestor","forms":["ancestor","ancestors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祖先；先輩","explanation":"指一個人或群體在血緣上由其後代延續下來的先人，可以是父母任何一方的祖先，也不受代數限制。這裡的核心就是“在家譜鏈條上走在你前面的人”。","examples":[{"en":"Many of my ancestors lived in this valley.","zh":"我的許多祖先都生活在這座山谷裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is researching her ancestors on her mother's side.","zh":"她正在研究母系一方的祖先。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancestor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd0761117d5102fd","term":"ancestor","forms":["ancestor","ancestors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前身；早期型別","explanation":"指某種動物、技術、制度或其他事物在發展鏈上更早的型別，也就是後來事物的“祖先”或前身。它保留了家譜中“由更早者發展而來”的畫面，只是物件不再是人。","examples":[{"en":"This simple device was an ancestor of the modern computer.","zh":"這種簡單裝置是現代計算機的早期前身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This bulky machine was an ancestor of today's laptop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancestor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-79bfb0e2ba76b9d44760","word":"anchor","forms":["anchor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7771bed4342bb21d","term":"anchor","forms":["anchor","anchors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船錨","explanation":"一種沉入海底或河底、靠抓住底部來固定船隻的重型裝置；它把船牢牢停住，是“固定住”這一核心畫面的直接體現。","examples":[{"en":"The captain dropped the anchor near the quiet island.","zh":"船長在安靜的小島附近拋了錨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stayed at anchor until the storm passed.","zh":"暴風雨過去之前，我們一直停泊在錨地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anchor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5390bb0ad1ceda28","term":"anchor","forms":["anchor","anchors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穩定支點","explanation":"比喻能給人安全感、讓局面保持穩定的人或事物；就像船錨讓船不再漂走一樣，它讓人或計劃有可以依靠的支點。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm advice was an anchor for the family during the crisis.","zh":"危機期間，她冷靜的建議成了全家人的穩定支點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small routine became an anchor in his busy life.","zh":"這個小習慣成了他忙碌生活中的穩定支點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anchor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b69a0b0835decef","term":"anchor","forms":["anchor","anchors","anchoring","anchored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用錨固定","explanation":"把船或其他物體連線到固定點，使它牢牢停住，就像用錨把東西固定下來。","examples":[{"en":"The crew anchored the boat near the small island.","zh":"船員把船停泊在小島附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We anchored the floating platform to the riverbed.","zh":"我們把浮動平臺固定在河床上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anchor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45bbd3d6423f18e9","term":"anchor","forms":["anchor","anchors","anchoring","anchored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拋錨停泊","explanation":"船自己拋下錨並停在水上，重點是從航行狀態變為固定停泊狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The ferry anchored in the bay before sunset.","zh":"渡船在日落前停泊在海灣裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain ordered the ship to anchor for the night.","zh":"船長下令讓船拋錨過夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anchor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41dda3b2113b5898b198","word":"ancient","forms":["ancient"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b1ba368ecdbc984","term":"ancient","forms":["ancient","ancienter","more ancient","ancientest","most ancient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古老的；年代久遠的","explanation":"指某個地方、建築、物品等存在了很長時間，年代非常久遠，重點是“老”。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon exploring an ancient city.","zh":"我們整個下午都在探索一座古城。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village is famous for its ancient stone bridge.","zh":"這個村莊以古老的石橋聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0380e2d0cfdb5c3f","term":"ancient","forms":["ancient","ancienter","more ancient","ancientest","most ancient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古代的；屬於久遠過去的","explanation":"指發生在很久以前，或屬於古代社會、人物和文化；重點是“屬於過去的時代”。","examples":[{"en":"Ancient writers described the city as a center of trade.","zh":"古代作家把這座城市描述成貿易中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People in ancient times traveled mostly on foot.","zh":"古代人出行大多靠步行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6201111b83a0cb5b0922","word":"and","forms":["and"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"and","forms":["and"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"和；而且","examples":[{"en":"I packed a sandwich and a bottle of water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The room was warm and comfortable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-519ba91a5a5b4afb9dc6","word":"angel","forms":["angel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3b9bee6e69d7707","term":"angel","forms":["angel","angels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天使；神聖使者","explanation":"指侍奉神或其他神聖存在、負責傳達資訊的非物質神聖使者，傳統形象常是長著翅膀、穿長袍的年輕人。記住“從天上來傳遞資訊並提供幫助的使者”這個核心畫面即可。","examples":[{"en":"The child drew an angel with bright wings.","zh":"那個孩子畫了一個長著明亮翅膀的天使。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prayed for an angel to watch over her family.","zh":"她祈禱有一位天使守護她的家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c150d4d2737bf77a","term":"angel","forms":["angel","angels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天使中的低階者","explanation":"在亞伯拉罕諸教的分類體系中，指低階的天使類存在，等級低於“德能”等更高階存在。","examples":[{"en":"The book places angels in several different orders.","zh":"這本書把天使分為幾個不同的等級。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medieval text places angels below archangels in rank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4cc56aa47e0b5c789d4","word":"anger","forms":["anger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-257219e09fcecd0c","term":"anger","forms":["anger","angers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"憤怒","explanation":"anger 是因受到冒犯、傷害、威脅或不公平對待而產生的強烈不快情緒，常伴隨著想爭吵、責罵或反擊的衝動。它就像內心被壓得難受，壓力最終變成了怒氣。","examples":[{"en":"She struggled to control her anger during the argument.","zh":"爭論時，她努力控制自己的憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He vented his anger by slamming the door.","zh":"他砰地關上門來發洩怒氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49387897bee2bee3878c","word":"angle","forms":["angle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a30655b4f4de5593","term":"angle","forms":["angle","angles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幾何角","explanation":"兩條從同一點出發的射線形成的圖形，或多個平面相交形成的立體圖形，中文通常稱為“角”。","examples":[{"en":"Draw an angle with one side along the horizontal line.","zh":"畫一個角，讓其中一邊沿著水平線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The angle between the two roads is very narrow.","zh":"兩條路之間的夾角很小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7b0f40a298db887","term":"angle","forms":["angle","angles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"角度大小","explanation":"指一個角張開的程度，通常用度數或弧度表示；例如四十五度就是一個角的大小。","examples":[{"en":"Set the machine to an angle of 45 degrees.","zh":"把機器調到四十五度角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The angle between the lines is 30 degrees.","zh":"兩條線之間的角度是三十度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e9a6926cf908a28","term":"angle","forms":["angle","angles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀點、看法","explanation":"由“看事情的方向”引申為觀察、理解或討論某件事的方式，也就是“看問題的角度”。","examples":[{"en":"Let's look at the problem from another angle.","zh":"我們換個角度來看這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her angle on the issue made me reconsider my view.","zh":"她看待這個問題的角度讓我重新考慮了自己的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a96f1960786d85f9e12","word":"angry","forms":["angry"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-283f000d11a1a9bd","term":"angry","forms":["angry","angrier","more angry","angriest","most angry"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生氣的；憤怒的","explanation":"指一個人感到或表現出強烈的不滿和憤怒，就像怒氣已經從表情、語氣或行為中顯露出來。","examples":[{"en":"She was angry with me for forgetting her birthday.","zh":"我忘了她的生日，她對此很生氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gets angry when people interrupt him.","zh":"別人打斷他說話時，他就會生氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fad07c2f80722551","term":"angry","forms":["angry","angrier","more angry","angriest","most angry"],"pos":"adj","zh":"紅腫疼痛的","explanation":"形容傷口、皮膚或身體區域性因受傷、感染等而紅腫、發炎並疼痛，彷彿那裡也在“發怒”。","examples":[{"en":"The scrape on his knee looked angry and swollen.","zh":"他膝蓋上的擦傷看起來紅腫而疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An angry rash spread beneath the adhesive bandage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab91a82d14cfc6125c1a","word":"animal","forms":["animal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6372709b080b3226","term":"animal","forms":["animal","animals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物","explanation":"指動物界中的成員：它們通常能活動，細胞沒有植物那樣的堅硬細胞壁，並透過攝取其他生物獲得能量。人類也屬於動物，但日常談話中常把“人”和“動物”分開說。","examples":[{"en":"Humans, like other animals, need air and food to live.","zh":"人類和其他動物一樣，需要空氣和食物才能生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children watched a small animal drinking by the river.","zh":"孩子們看著一隻小動物在河邊喝水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/animal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-696af3693f3ba07202da","word":"animate","forms":["animate"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1596a3c5f8652e6","term":"animate","forms":["animate","more animate","most animate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有生命的","explanation":"指本身活著、具有生命的東西，和沒有生命的物體相對。這是“體內有一口氣”的最基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"The story divides the world into animate and inanimate things.","zh":"這個故事把世界分成有生命的事物和無生命的事物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every animate creature needs energy to live.","zh":"每個有生命的生物都需要能量才能生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/animate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6d239ec3efa36fa","term":"animate","forms":["animate","more animate","most animate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生動有活力的","explanation":"形容人、講話、討論或氣氛充滿精神和動感，好像注入了生命力。這是“有生命”引申到表現和風格上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She became an animate speaker once the discussion turned to music.","zh":"討論轉到音樂後，她立刻變成了一個充滿活力的演講者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The animate debate kept everyone awake.","zh":"這場生動熱烈的辯論讓所有人都保持清醒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/animate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10d76528de8a35f6","term":"animate","forms":["animate","animates","animating","animated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使動起來","explanation":"指給靜止的影象、模型或物件加入運動，或製造出運動的效果。可以把它記成“把生命的氣息注入沒有動靜的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"We can animate the model to show how the machine works.","zh":"我們可以讓這個模型動起來，展示機器的工作方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer animated the character's face.","zh":"設計師讓這個角色的臉動了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/animate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2831c2041aab6063","term":"animate","forms":["animate","animates","animating","animated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使有活力","explanation":"指激發人的精神、熱情或行動力，也可使談話、活動和氣氛變得熱烈。這裡是把“生命力”注入人或場面，而不一定產生實際運動。","examples":[{"en":"Her questions animated the quiet meeting.","zh":"她的問題使原本沉悶的會議活躍起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach's speech animated the tired players.","zh":"教練的講話激發了疲憊球員的活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/animate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9abfc382e356ede3cbeb","word":"ankle","forms":["ankle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1bc103a89c6dfa03","term":"ankle","forms":["ankle","ankles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腳踝；踝關節","explanation":"ankle是小腿和腳連線的活動關節，也常指這個關節周圍的腳踝部位。走路、跑步和跳躍時，腳踝負責讓腳相對小腿彎曲和轉動。","examples":[{"en":"I twisted my ankle while playing basketball.","zh":"我打籃球時扭傷了腳踝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her ankle is still swollen after the fall.","zh":"她摔倒後腳踝仍然腫著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ankle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40c12bd9c3e15b47999a","word":"anniversary","forms":["anniversary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7940ad585a6c530","term":"anniversary","forms":["anniversary","anniversaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"週年紀念日","explanation":"指某個重要事件發生後，恰好經過一整年、兩年或更多整年時對應的那一天。前面的序數詞說明這是第幾個週年，例如第五十週年就是事件發生五十年後的同一天。","examples":[{"en":"Today marks the twentieth anniversary of the bridge opening.","zh":"今天是這座橋通車二十週年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum held a special exhibition for the hundredth anniversary of the artist's birth.","zh":"這家博物館為紀念這位藝術家誕辰一百週年舉辦了特別展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anniversary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b02bfafcd6f6abd0","term":"anniversary","forms":["anniversary","anniversaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某人的週年紀念日","explanation":"同樣表示按整年計算的紀念日，但常見於說話者把這一天當作自己的或某個群體共同慶祝的里程碑，例如某段關係、某項合作或某個組織成立後的週年日。","examples":[{"en":"We are celebrating our tenth anniversary with a small dinner tonight.","zh":"我們今晚用一頓小晚餐慶祝自己的十週年紀念日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They planted a tree on their tenth anniversary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anniversary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-765c7af26df03d6711f0","word":"announce(ment)","forms":["announce","announcement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddbad6e56e9bb1e3","term":"announce","forms":["announce","announces","announcing","announced","announcest","announcedst","announceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"公開宣佈","explanation":"把訊息、決定、計劃或某件事情正式公開說出來，使公眾或一群人知道。重點不在於訊息是好是壞，而在於它被正式傳達出來。","examples":[{"en":"The company announced a new plan to reduce waste.","zh":"公司宣佈了一項減少浪費的新計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They announced that the museum would reopen in June.","zh":"他們宣佈博物館將在六月重新開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/announce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e230321bef1e6046","term":"announce","forms":["announce","announces","announcing","announced","announcest","announcedst","announceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"播報比賽","explanation":"在體育比賽或其他活動現場，用聲音介紹程序、選手或結果，擔任現場播報員。","examples":[{"en":"She will announce the championship game on Saturday.","zh":"她將在星期六播報這場冠軍賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He announces college basketball games on local radio.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/announce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57bca16f65fd50d0","term":"announcement","forms":["announcement","announcements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宣佈的行為","explanation":"指把某件事公開告訴別人、正式作出通知這一行為，重點在“宣佈”這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The manager made an announcement before the meeting began.","zh":"經理在會議開始前作了宣佈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stood up to make an announcement to the whole class.","zh":"她站起來向全班作了宣佈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/announcement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83c54aed8e744628","term":"announcement","forms":["announcement","announcements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"釋出出來的通知","explanation":"指承載或傳達已宣佈事項的那條通知、公告或釋出資訊，重點在“大家看到或聽到的訊息載體”。","examples":[{"en":"The announcement was posted on the school website this morning.","zh":"這則通知今天早上釋出在學校網站上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An announcement on the noticeboard listed the new opening hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/announcement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-799524ffd2ba5417a367","word":"annoy","forms":["annoy"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b42d639ce6ac7a2","term":"annoy","forms":["annoy","annoys","annoying","annoyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打擾；惹惱","explanation":"指某人持續或反覆做令人不快的事，使另一個人感到煩躁、受打擾。這是現代英語中最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The constant noise annoyed everyone in the office.","zh":"持續不斷的噪聲把辦公室裡的每個人都弄得很煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please stop annoying your brother.","zh":"請別再煩你弟弟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annoy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-443f3fc81f2b8311","term":"annoy","forms":["annoy","annoys","annoying","annoyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使人不快；惹怒","explanation":"表示某人的行為或某種情況讓別人不高興、覺得麻煩，重點仍是“造成煩擾”，不一定達到強烈憤怒的程度。","examples":[{"en":"It annoys me when people interrupt.","zh":"別人打斷談話時，我會覺得很煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repeated clicking began to annoy everyone nearby.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annoy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32bbd2ba21c8c37e8c17","word":"annoyance","forms":["annoyance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd371061f1c6e5cb","term":"annoyance","forms":["annoyance","annoyances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煩人的事；麻煩","explanation":"指某件會讓人不舒服、分心或生氣的具體事情，重點在於“這件事本身很煩人”。","examples":[{"en":"The constant noise from the construction site is a real annoyance.","zh":"施工現場持續不斷的噪聲真讓人煩惱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Having to reset the password every week is a minor annoyance.","zh":"每週都得重置密碼是一件小麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annoyance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0105a29446d5f878","term":"annoyance","forms":["annoyance","annoyances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煩惱；惱火的情緒","explanation":"指人在被打擾、惹惱或遇到不順心的事時產生的心理狀態，也就是“感到煩”的情緒本身。","examples":[{"en":"She sighed with annoyance when the train was delayed again.","zh":"火車又晚點時，她煩惱地嘆了口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tried not to show his annoyance during the long interview.","zh":"在漫長的面試中，他儘量不表現出自己的煩惱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annoyance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee5e2878c48558bcbd8d","word":"annual","forms":["annual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e51ad40b8138387c","term":"annual","forms":["annual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"每年一次的","explanation":"指某件事每隔一年發生一次，通常會按固定週期重複；核心畫面就是一年轉一圈，事情隨之再來一次。","examples":[{"en":"The school holds an annual sports day in June.","zh":"這所學校每年六月舉行一次運動會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The annual report will be published next week.","zh":"年度報告將於下週釋出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd9eda899eeb95bd","term":"annual","forms":["annual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"年度的；按年計算的","explanation":"指以完整的一年為計算、觀察或安排週期的事物，例如收入、利潤或自然變化；重點不是“發生一次”，而是“按一年這一整圈來算”。","examples":[{"en":"The job offers an annual salary of sixty thousand dollars.","zh":"這份工作提供六萬美元的年薪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company reported a rise in annual profits.","zh":"公司報告稱年度利潤有所增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f183a4e64493af3f377","word":"anonymous","forms":["anonymous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a0c82152f29a949","term":"anonymous","forms":["anonymous","more anonymous","most anonymous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未署名的","explanation":"指作品、信件、捐款或其他行為沒有公開負責人的姓名，讀者知道有一個責任人，但不知道是誰。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper received an anonymous letter about the missing documents.","zh":"報社收到了一封關於檔案失蹤的匿名信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An anonymous donor paid for the children's new books.","zh":"一位匿名捐款人為孩子們的新書付了錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anonymous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3873b9a71562502","term":"anonymous","forms":["anonymous","more anonymous","most anonymous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"姓名不明或被隱去的","explanation":"指某人的姓名尚不知道，或已經被有意隱去；它常用於作者、訊息來源、證人等人的身份說明。","examples":[{"en":"The novel was first published by an anonymous author.","zh":"這部小說最初由一位姓名不詳的作者出版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An anonymous source provided the reporter with the documents.","zh":"一名匿名訊息人士向記者提供了這些檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anonymous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae448ac86c4e8e4dec64","word":"another","forms":["another"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37a54a875c1a55c4","term":"another","forms":["another"],"pos":"det","zh":"再一個；再來一份","explanation":"在已經有一個或一些同類事物的基礎上，再增加一個同類事物，強調數量多了一個。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have another cup of tea?","zh":"我可以再喝一杯茶嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered another ticket for her friend.","zh":"她又為朋友買了一張票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/another","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5db96376963dc96","term":"another","forms":["another"],"pos":"det","zh":"另一個；不同的","explanation":"不再選擇眼前這個，而是選擇同類中不同的一個；重點是物件發生了替換或區別。","examples":[{"en":"This seat is uncomfortable; let's find another one.","zh":"這個座位不舒服，我們找另一個吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is there another way to solve the problem?","zh":"還有別的方法可以解決這個問題嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/another","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-baf005b7a5aa1127","term":"another","forms":["another"],"pos":"pron","zh":"再來一個","explanation":"省略已經說過的同類名詞，表示在已有物件之外再增加一個。","examples":[{"en":"This pen is out of ink, so I need another.","zh":"這支筆沒墨了，所以我需要再拿一支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The first cookie was delicious, so I had another.","zh":"第一塊餅乾很好吃，所以我又吃了一塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/another","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a6dca97f5a12f77","term":"another","forms":["another"],"pos":"pron","zh":"另一個","explanation":"代替前文的同類名詞，表示當前這個不合適或不想選，因此改選不同的一個。","examples":[{"en":"I tried one jacket, but I chose another.","zh":"我試了一件夾克，但最後選了另一件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This glass is cracked; bring me another.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/another","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0db52f4076c082518412","word":"answer","forms":["answer"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03c1174957d42089","term":"answer","forms":["answer","answers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"回答；回應","explanation":"指對問題、話語、請求或行為作出的回答或回應，可以是說出來的話，也可以是一個行動。它是“面對某件事並作出回應”這條核心意義最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I asked her a simple question, but she gave me no answer.","zh":"我問了她一個簡單的問題，但她沒有回答我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His answer to the proposal surprised everyone.","zh":"他對這項提議的回應讓所有人都很驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/answer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5051706adfa4ce7c","term":"answer","forms":["answer","answers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解決辦法；答案","explanation":"指解決問題、困難或疑問的辦法，不一定是一個簡短的具體回答。這裡的“回答”從語言回應擴充套件成了對難題的有效回應。","examples":[{"en":"There is no easy answer to this problem.","zh":"這個問題沒有簡單的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The answer is to reduce waste and use less energy.","zh":"解決辦法是減少浪費並少用能源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/answer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38460d599a1fdd3f","term":"answer","forms":["answer","answers","answering","answered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"回答；回應","explanation":"指對某人的話、問題或請求作出回答或回應，是 answer 作動詞時最基本的意義。回應可以是說話，也可以是書面或實際行動。","examples":[{"en":"Please answer my question honestly.","zh":"請如實回答我的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She answered him with a quiet smile.","zh":"她帶著平靜的微笑回應了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/answer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc15af2ad0eedaf0","term":"answer","forms":["answer","answers","answering","answered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"接聽；應門","explanation":"指對電話、門鈴、敲門或類似呼叫作出回應，實際接起電話或開啟門。這仍然是“對外來的呼叫作出回應”。","examples":[{"en":"Could you answer the phone while I make dinner?","zh":"我做晚飯時，你能幫我接一下電話嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one answered the door when I knocked.","zh":"我敲門時沒有人應門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/answer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-511974b551cccd59","term":"answer","forms":["answer","answers","answering","answered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滿足需要；適合用途","explanation":"指某物足以滿足某種需要、目的或實際要求。這裡是把“作出回應”擴大為“給出足夠有效的回應”。","examples":[{"en":"This simple tool answers the need for a cheap way to store water.","zh":"這個簡單的工具滿足了人們以低成本儲水的需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sturdy crate will answer our purpose perfectly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/answer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67a333356cdc566e6e34","word":"ant","forms":["ant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7cd2fb430f7a067","term":"ant","forms":["ant","ants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螞蟻","explanation":"指蟻科的一類小型昆蟲，通常生活在由大量個體組成的群體中。記住“沿路線移動、一起生活”的畫面，就能把它和網路爬蟲的用法聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"An ant carried a crumb across the kitchen floor.","zh":"一隻螞蟻叼著麵包屑穿過廚房地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched an ant struggle to drag a dead beetle uphill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f66f87d87754f4a79fe5","word":"anthem","forms":["anthem"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0a455d99a35acde","term":"anthem","forms":["anthem","anthems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頌歌；合唱歌曲","explanation":"指為宗教、政治、學校或其他共同體創作並集體演唱的歌曲，歌詞通常表達讚美、理想或歸屬感。它往往不是個人獨唱的小歌，而是能代表某種共同立場的作品。","examples":[{"en":"The choir performed the university anthem at the opening ceremony.","zh":"合唱團在開幕式上演唱了這所大學的校歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The song became an anthem for the campaign for equal rights.","zh":"這首歌成了平等權利運動的代表性歌曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anthem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f7040458cca5d3d","term":"anthem","forms":["anthem","anthems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讚美或忠誠的頌歌","explanation":"強調歌曲是在讚美某個信仰、國家、組織或共同理想，表達敬意、忠誠或歸屬感。它是“共同唱出的讚美之聲”這一核心形象最直接的體現。","examples":[{"en":"The crowd stood together and sang an anthem of peace.","zh":"人群一起站著唱了一首和平頌歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd sang an anthem honoring the resistance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anthem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-856fa50792e3c8450607","word":"antibiotic","forms":["antibiotic"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d077a82f0c44871","term":"antibiotic","forms":["antibiotic","more antibiotic","most antibiotic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與抗生素有關的","explanation":"表示“和抗生素或抗生素治療有關的”，例如描述治療、藥物作用或細菌對藥物的反應。它不是在說某個具體藥物，而是在給相關事物分類。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor recommended antibiotic treatment for the infection.","zh":"醫生建議用抗生素治療這種感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers are studying antibiotic resistance in hospitals.","zh":"研究人員正在研究醫院中的抗生素耐藥性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antibiotic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc280bb1d5de4bba","term":"antibiotic","forms":["antibiotic","antibiotics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抗生素；抗菌藥物","explanation":"指能殺死細菌或抑制細菌等微生物生長的物質，通常用於治療細菌感染。這裡說的是藥物本身，而不是“抗生素治療”這一類相關事物。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor prescribed an antibiotic for her bacterial infection.","zh":"醫生給她的細菌感染開了一種抗生素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You should finish the full course of antibiotics.","zh":"你應該完成整個抗生素療程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antibiotic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-209665ea9dca91a10d42","word":"anticipate","forms":["anticipate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5106211e9a78225c","term":"anticipate","forms":["anticipate","anticipates","anticipating","anticipated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預先採取行動","explanation":"指在某人採取行動或某事發生以前先做出應對，尤其是為了阻止或減輕其影響；也就是把行動提前到對方之前。","examples":[{"en":"The team anticipated the protest by closing the gates early.","zh":"團隊提前關上大門，以防有人抗議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We anticipated shortages by ordering extra batteries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cafe99a8d42bdcd8","term":"anticipate","forms":["anticipate","anticipates","anticipating","anticipated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預料；預期","explanation":"指在事情發生以前，根據現有情況想到它可能會發生或會有某種結果，重點是事先形成判斷。","examples":[{"en":"We anticipate heavy traffic on the highway this evening.","zh":"我們預計今晚高速公路上會很擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We anticipated resistance from the neighboring landowners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff5b0e225b4dc7a5","term":"anticipate","forms":["anticipate","anticipates","anticipating","anticipated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"熱切期待","explanation":"指因為想到未來即將發生的好事或重要事情而興奮、盼望它到來；這是“提前想到”發展出的感情色彩更強的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children eagerly anticipated the school trip.","zh":"孩子們熱切地盼望著學校旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She anticipated the concert so eagerly that she barely slept.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24dfc16f0ca60df9eeed","word":"anticipation","forms":["anticipation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a92a660ed79c7fa7","term":"anticipation","forms":["anticipation","anticipations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預先想到；預感","explanation":"指在事情真正發生前，先在腦中想到、判斷或作好心理準備；這種事先的預感也可以是對壞事的擔心。","examples":[{"en":"The anticipation of a difficult conversation made her nervous.","zh":"想到即將進行一次艱難的談話，她就緊張起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The anticipation of the injection was worse than the injection itself.","zh":"對打針的事先恐懼比真正打針還難受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdac7b5ffe96e248","term":"anticipation","forms":["anticipation","anticipations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"期待；期盼","explanation":"指等待某件即將發生的好事時產生的興奮、急切心情；重點不只是“想到”，而是帶著盼望等它到來。","examples":[{"en":"The children waited with anticipation for the festival to begin.","zh":"孩子們滿懷期待地等著節日開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a growing sense of anticipation before the concert.","zh":"音樂會開始前，期待感越來越強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anticipation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e08ac7e5b3c9bf288ece","word":"antique","forms":["antique"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-485af5bd0bd5b711","term":"antique","forms":["antique","antiquer","antiquest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古代的","explanation":"指存在於古代、源自古代，尤其常用於與古希臘、古羅馬有關的人、物或風格。它強調歷史上的久遠年代，而不是僅僅使用時間很長。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a collection of antique Roman coins.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了一批古羅馬錢幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studies antique Greek architecture.","zh":"她研究古希臘建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antique","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf20a89334680fad","term":"antique","forms":["antique","antiquer","antiquest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古老而非現代的","explanation":"指屬於過去時代、已經不再現代或顯得過時的事物、制度和風格。相比“古代的”，這個義項可以指較近的過去，也常帶有“老式”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The house still has an antique heating system.","zh":"這所房子仍然裝著一套老式供暖系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He dislikes the antique rules of the organization.","zh":"他不喜歡這個組織那些過時的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antique","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d24393366fcb2022","term":"antique","forms":["antique","antiques"],"pos":"noun","zh":"古董；古老物品","explanation":"指年代久遠、通常具有收藏或歷史價值的物品，尤其是傢俱、器物和裝飾品。它把“古老的東西”這一核心概念變成了可以收藏、買賣或展示的物件。","examples":[{"en":"They bought an antique at the weekend market.","zh":"他們在週末集市買了一件古董。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room is filled with antiques.","zh":"房間裡擺滿了古董。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antique","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a9dfa3ca3b2709ff16a","word":"antonym","forms":["antonym"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"antonym","forms":["antonym"],"pos":"n.","zh":"反義詞","examples":[{"en":"An antonym of hot is cold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Can you think of an antonym for the word generous?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab0231f72dd9f07809f0","word":"anxiety","forms":["anxiety"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40b101afd89e59d5","term":"anxiety","forms":["anxiety","anxieties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"焦慮；擔憂","explanation":"指因為未來或某件不確定的事而產生的不安、緊張和反覆擔心。它像心裡那根被拉緊的弦，未必已經發生壞事，卻讓人難以放鬆。","examples":[{"en":"She felt a wave of anxiety before the interview.","zh":"面試前，她突然感到一陣焦慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His anxiety about the exam made it hard for him to sleep.","zh":"他對考試的焦慮讓他很難入睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anxiety","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da3e4deb9a8e86ba","term":"anxiety","forms":["anxiety","anxieties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"渴望；急切期待","explanation":"指因非常想得到或實現某事而產生的急切、不安的心情。這裡的“拉緊”不是擔心壞事，而是被強烈願望牽著走。","examples":[{"en":"There was growing anxiety to hear the final decision.","zh":"大家越來越急切地想聽到最終決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In his anxiety to help, he interrupted twice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anxiety","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-faef616df2ec24420964","word":"anxious","forms":["anxious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dff7eae7eb50f18","term":"anxious","forms":["anxious","more anxious","anxiouser","most anxious","anxiousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"焦慮不安的","explanation":"形容人因為擔心、緊張或心裡沒底而感到不安，像心裡一直繃著一根弦。","examples":[{"en":"I felt anxious before the interview.","zh":"面試前我感到很不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child became anxious when his parents were late.","zh":"父母遲到時，那個孩子變得焦慮不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anxious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-262a50b61b07fbf1","term":"anxious","forms":["anxious","more anxious","anxiouser","most anxious","anxiousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"急於；渴望","explanation":"表示非常想做某事，帶有急切、迫切的感覺；這裡的“緊繃”不再是害怕，而是盼望儘快實現願望。","examples":[{"en":"He is anxious to please, so you can count on him.","zh":"他很想讓大家滿意，所以你可以信賴他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were anxious to see their new puppy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anxious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6a7cd2a7371b1a15d54","word":"any","forms":["any"],"officialPos":"pron./adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e02d08689a7f6da8","term":"any","forms":["any"],"pos":"adv","zh":"絲毫；哪怕一點","explanation":"這裡的 any 把“開放選擇”擴充套件到最小程度：哪怕只增加或達到一點點，也算在內。最常見於比較級，表示“再……一點就會……”。","examples":[{"en":"If you get any taller, you'll have to duck through the doorway.","zh":"你要是再高一點，就得低頭才能透過門口了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I cannot lift this lid any higher.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/any","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2798b4af1c95113","term":"any","forms":["any"],"pos":"det","zh":"任何一個；一些；一點","explanation":"在疑問句中，它詢問“有沒有至少一個或一些”；在否定句中，它表示“一個都沒有”或“一點也沒有”。這裡的重點不是特定物件，而是開放地檢查數量是否達到一個。","examples":[{"en":"Do you have any questions about the homework?","zh":"你對作業還有什麼問題嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't have any cash with me.","zh":"我身上一點現金也沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/any","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8c12e2715afbab0","term":"any","forms":["any"],"pos":"det","zh":"任意的；隨便哪個","explanation":"這裡表示物件不受身份、種類或性質限制：在範圍內挑哪一個都可以。它把“一個”擴大成“任何一個”，因此帶有自由選擇的意味。","examples":[{"en":"You can choose any seat near the window.","zh":"你可以隨便選靠窗的任何一個座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pick any postcard from the display rack.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/any","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1104508a50dc7bb82fc","word":"anybody/anyone","forms":["anybody","anyone"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7855ae9290de577d","term":"anybody","forms":["anybody"],"pos":"pron","zh":"任何人；誰都","explanation":"指不確定範圍中的任意一個人，重點是“這個人是誰並不重要，誰都可以”。在不同句子裡可譯為“任何人”“有人”或“誰都”。","examples":[{"en":"If anybody needs help, please raise a hand.","zh":"如果有人需要幫助，請舉手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Anybody can learn this skill with practice.","zh":"任何人經過練習都能學會這項技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anybody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac9975238c723dd0","term":"anybody","forms":["anybody"],"pos":"pron","zh":"有頭有臉的人","explanation":"在非正式說法中，指在某個圈子或地方有地位、受認可、算得上重要的人；這是從“任何一個人”引申出的社會評價。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone who wanted to be anybody showed up at the mayor's party.","zh":"所有想在當地成為有頭有臉的人的人都參加了市長的聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Anyone who was anybody attended the duke's reception.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anybody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3ade4ef6944691a","term":"anyone","forms":["anyone"],"pos":"pron","zh":"任何人；隨便哪個人","explanation":"anyone 把人群中的物件完全不指定，意思是“任何一個人”或“誰都可以”。例如說能力或可能性時，它可以表示沒有特定限制的人。","examples":[{"en":"Almost anyone can learn to use this app.","zh":"幾乎任何人都能學會使用這個應用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can anyone help me carry these boxes?","zh":"有人能幫我搬這些箱子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anyone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1dc916819e3f87ae935","word":"anyhow","forms":["anyhow"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d33583fcf8a221bd","term":"anyhow","forms":["anyhow"],"pos":"adv","zh":"無論如何；反正","explanation":"用於承接前面的情況，表示後面的事實或結論不會因此改變，意思接近“不過說到底”或“反正”。","examples":[{"en":"We may miss the first train, but anyhow, we will get there tonight.","zh":"我們可能會錯過第一班火車，但無論如何，今晚都會到那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Anyhow, the decision has already been made.","zh":"反正決定已經作出了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anyhow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55e7c5c514b46bcf","term":"anyhow","forms":["anyhow"],"pos":"adv","zh":"隨便地；亂七八糟地","explanation":"表示做事不講究順序、整潔或安全，像是匆忙或不負責任地“隨手一弄”。這是“怎麼都行”發展出的負面意味：方法雖不受限制，卻完全沒有認真安排。","examples":[{"en":"He threw his clothes anyhow on the floor and went to bed.","zh":"他把衣服亂七八糟地扔在地板上就睡覺了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The papers were left anyhow on the desk.","zh":"檔案被隨手亂放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anyhow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee0874170b7f6f32b8c2","word":"anything","forms":["anything"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4de3b5ed6badb4a","term":"anything","forms":["anything"],"pos":"pron","zh":"任何事物；什麼事情","explanation":"anything 是一個範圍很大的代詞，可以指任何物品、行為、狀態、事件或事實。疑問句裡常譯為“什麼”，否定句裡常譯為“什麼都不”，重點是“不限定具體是哪一個”。","examples":[{"en":"Did you find anything useful in the box?","zh":"你在盒子裡找到什麼有用的東西了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wouldn't change anything about the design.","zh":"我不會改動這個設計的任何地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anything","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75eb6224d3db03d60e08","word":"anytime","forms":["anytime"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-268dde8c3e89b459","term":"anytime","forms":["anytime"],"pos":"adv","zh":"隨時；任何時候","explanation":"它把時間限制完全開啟，表示某事可以在任意時候發生，或某個選擇無論何時都成立。核心畫面就是“時間之門隨時開著”。","examples":[{"en":"Call me anytime if you need help.","zh":"如果你需要幫助，隨時給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I would choose fresh fruit over candy anytime.","zh":"無論什麼時候，我都會選新鮮水果而不是糖果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anytime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97519f7c288b3602aae0","word":"anyway","forms":["anyway"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d73dc695aa8ebd79","term":"anyway","forms":["anyway"],"pos":"adv","zh":"無論如何；還是","explanation":"前面提到的困難、反對意見或不利條件，並不能改變後面的行動或結果；即使如此，事情還是照樣發生。這是 anyway 最核心、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I was tired, but I went to the meeting anyway.","zh":"我當時很累，但還是去開會了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It might rain, but we're going anyway.","zh":"可能會下雨，但我們還是要去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anyway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21c735374624120a","term":"anyway","forms":["anyway"],"pos":"adv","zh":"反正；不管怎樣說","explanation":"說話人先表達一個看法或判斷，隨後用 anyway 補上一點理由、證據或限定，意思接近“反正我這樣說是有根據的”。它不是在推動一個新行動，而是在為前面的說法收尾或加強它。","examples":[{"en":"I don't think the shop is open; there are no lights on, anyway.","zh":"我覺得那家店沒開門，反正裡面連燈都沒亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Anyway, we still need to finish the report.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anyway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c6e53937390517982c4","word":"anywhere/anyplace","forms":["anywhere"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d487b314f2e7d4a","term":"anywhere","forms":["anywhere"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在任何地方","explanation":"指某人或某物所在的地點沒有限定，或者說話人不知道具體地點；重點是“地點可以是任意一個”。","examples":[{"en":"I don't know where I left my keys. They could be anywhere.","zh":"我不知道把鑰匙落在哪裡了，它們可能在任何地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can return the bicycle anywhere within the marked district.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anywhere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b73a7beb60c3d629","term":"anywhere","forms":["anywhere"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到任何地方；無論到哪裡","explanation":"指行動的目的地沒有限制，可以去任意地方；放在地點或行動的語境中，也可引出“無論到哪裡”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Anywhere you go in France, there will be bread and wine with dinner.","zh":"無論你在法國走到哪裡，晚餐都會有面包和葡萄酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The portable radio goes anywhere you travel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anywhere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d40973eccd8c0aacfed","word":"apart","forms":["apart"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20d5761ba4f13bfd","term":"apart","forms":["apart","more apart","further apart","farther apart","most apart","furthest apart","farthest apart"],"pos":"adv","zh":"分開地；彼此隔開","explanation":"表示人或物在空間或時間上彼此分離，不在一起；這是 apart 最常見的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep the clean clothes and the dirty clothes apart.","zh":"請把乾淨衣服和髒衣服分開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sat apart during the exam.","zh":"考試時孩子們分開坐著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58e8a0df8dcb552a","term":"apart","forms":["apart","more apart","further apart","farther apart","most apart","furthest apart","farthest apart"],"pos":"adv","zh":"拆開；拆散","explanation":"表示把一個完整物體拆成幾個部分，讓原來連在一起的東西分離出來。","examples":[{"en":"Dad took the radio apart to find the broken wire.","zh":"爸爸把收音機拆開，尋找斷掉的電線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toy came apart when I dropped it.","zh":"我把玩具掉在地上後，它散架了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,113],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-6f347b04efac92cf6edc","word":"apartment","forms":["apartment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb5e521181e41821","term":"apartment","forms":["apartment","apartments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公寓；套房住宅","explanation":"指一棟建築物中獨立的一套住宅，通常有臥室、起居空間等，並由住戶單獨使用，常常用於出租。它是 apartment 最常見、最需要優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Many students share an apartment near the university.","zh":"許多學生合住在大學附近的一套公寓裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their apartment overlooks the tram stop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apartment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb3cad5b7bea92b58319","word":"ape","forms":["ape"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54dc40edde4384e2","term":"ape","forms":["ape","apes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猿","explanation":"ape指猿類動物，例如類人猿；它們通常比猴子大，而且沒有尾巴。這個詞首先應作為具體的動物名稱來記。","examples":[{"en":"The zoo has a quiet enclosure for the apes.","zh":"這家動物園為猿類設有一個安靜的圍欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young ape swung between the branches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d7925903f3e8bfc0300","word":"apologize","forms":["apologize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ac7e559e6aba49b","term":"apologize","forms":["apologize","apologizes","apologizing","apologized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"道歉；承認過錯並表示遺憾","explanation":"做錯事、造成不便或冒犯別人時，主動承認問題並表達後悔，希望彌補關係。這是現代英語中最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I apologize for the delay.","zh":"我為耽擱一事道歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She apologized to her friend for speaking harshly.","zh":"她因說話太沖而向朋友道歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apologize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c4af01d5d088ac3","term":"apologize","forms":["apologize","apologizes","apologizing","apologized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對某事發生表示遺憾","explanation":"有時說話人並不是造成事件的人，只是對某個不好的結果表示遺憾或歉意；重點是對事情本身感到抱歉。","examples":[{"en":"We apologize for any inconvenience caused.","zh":"由此造成的不便，我們深表歉意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We apologize for the unexpected interruption to your service.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apologize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e161201db018aac5127c","word":"apology","forms":["apology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-298243d51bd8dc3b","term":"apology","forms":["apology","apologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道歉；歉意","explanation":"指因為自己的言語或行為傷害了別人，而表達後悔和歉意的話或行為。它可以是一次具體的道歉，也可以指道歉本身。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a sincere apology after the misunderstanding.","zh":"誤會之後，她真誠地向我道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His apology helped repair their friendship.","zh":"他的道歉幫助修復了他們的友誼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e3477194b2c969d","term":"apology","forms":["apology","apologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式辯護","explanation":"指為某個人、觀點或行動進行正式的解釋和辯護，像是在公開場合“為自己說話”。這種意思和“道歉”不同，不一定表示做錯了事。","examples":[{"en":"The book is an apology for freedom of speech.","zh":"這本書是為言論自由所作的辯護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her essay is an apology for religious tolerance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0794afd1bc3cdba65210","word":"apparent","forms":["apparent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b3b1f6b7b997ffb","term":"apparent","forms":["apparent","more apparent","most apparent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯而易見的","explanation":"指事實、原因或問題已經清楚到不難看出或理解，幾乎不需要進一步證明；它是從“顯現出來”延伸到人的認識中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"It soon became apparent that the plan would cost more than expected.","zh":"很快就明顯看出，這項計劃的費用會超出預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mistake was apparent from the first page of the report.","zh":"從報告的第一頁就能明顯看出這個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apparent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2bab13f6b0507e1","term":"apparent","forms":["apparent","more apparent","most apparent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表面上如此的","explanation":"指某種情況從外表或現有證據看起來成立，但還不能保證它就是真實情況；重點是“顯出來的樣子”與“實際情況”之間可能有距離。","examples":[{"en":"The apparent simplicity of the task was misleading.","zh":"這項任務表面上的簡單具有誤導性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was no apparent damage to the building after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，這座建築表面上沒有明顯損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apparent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da7e2d4b40b63f98e9fc","word":"appeal","forms":["appeal"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08fe30f1f7109be4","term":"appeal","forms":["appeal","appeals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上訴申請","explanation":"指向更高一級的法院或法官提出申請，請他們重新審查並推翻下級法院的判決或命令。它保留了“把問題向更高權威呼求”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The family plans to file an appeal against the court's decision.","zh":"這家人計劃對法院的判決提出上訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoner's appeal reached the court on Monday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be823979ce43f96f","term":"appeal","forms":["appeal","appeals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"呼籲或請求","explanation":"指向某個人、團體或權威發出請求，希望得到決定、幫助、支援或證實。它仍然像是把自己的需要“呼喊”給能回應的人。","examples":[{"en":"The charity made an appeal for volunteers after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，這家慈善機構呼籲志願者前來幫忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her appeal to the manager finally brought a response.","zh":"她向經理提出的請求最終得到了回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0176619aa7f9fb6","term":"appeal","forms":["appeal","appeals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸引力","explanation":"指某人或某事物能引起興趣、好感或參與願望的力量。它可以理解為某事物向人發出“來關注我”的無聲呼喚。","examples":[{"en":"The game has strong appeal for families with young children.","zh":"這款遊戲對有小孩的家庭很有吸引力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The quiet design of the house appeals to many buyers.","zh":"這棟房子的簡潔設計吸引了許多買家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72159c702bac45d1","term":"appeal","forms":["appeal","appeals","appealing","appealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提出上訴","explanation":"指不服下級法院或法官的裁決，向更高一級法院申請重新審查。動作的重點是把爭議交給更高權威處理。","examples":[{"en":"Dissatisfied with the ruling, the company decided to appeal.","zh":"公司不服這項裁決，決定提出上訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoner appealed against the conviction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38bb349e161997db","term":"appeal","forms":["appeal","appeals","appealing","appealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向權威求助或求證","explanation":"指向某人或某種權威尋求裁決、證實、支援，或請求對方維護自己的權利。它把自己的主張交給一個可能回應的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers appealed to the public for information.","zh":"研究人員呼籲公眾提供資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She appealed to the committee to reconsider the rule.","zh":"她請求委員會重新考慮這項規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bea57fed09476434","term":"appeal","forms":["appeal","appeals","appealing","appealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"有吸引力","explanation":"指某人或某事物能引起某人的興趣、好感或參與願望。這裡不是主動發出請求，而是某種特徵自然地“招來”關注。","examples":[{"en":"The simple menu appeals to customers who want a quick meal.","zh":"這份簡單的選單吸引了想快速用餐的顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flexible schedule appeals to working parents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-adf5a890f0aec8298377","word":"appear","forms":["appear"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eadb05f43d99d034","term":"appear","forms":["appear","appears","appearing","appeared","appearest","appearedst","appeareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出現；顯現","explanation":"原本不在視野中的人或物進入視線，變得看得見。它強調“顯現出來”的過程，而不只是已經在那裡。","examples":[{"en":"A rainbow appeared after the rain.","zh":"雨後出現了一道彩虹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She appeared at the door just before dinner.","zh":"她就在晚飯前出現在門口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24eeb441f19bcf08","term":"appear","forms":["appear","appears","appearing","appeared","appearest","appearedst","appeareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯得明顯；顯現於認識中","explanation":"某個事實、問題或結論進入人的理解範圍，變得可以看出或證明。這是把“進入眼睛”擴充套件成“進入頭腦”，所以不一定真的能看見。","examples":[{"en":"It appears that the meeting has been canceled.","zh":"看來會議已經取消了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The problem appears to be more serious than we thought.","zh":"這個問題看來比我們想的更嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7b7f9f434b61c73","term":"appear","forms":["appear","appears","appearing","appeared","appearest","appearedst","appeareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看起來；似乎","explanation":"從外表、行為或現有跡象判斷某人或某物具有某種狀態，但這只是呈現出來的樣子，不保證事實完全如此。它把“顯現出來”進一步變成“顯得像”。","examples":[{"en":"He appeared calm during the interview.","zh":"面試時他看起來很鎮定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge appears stable despite the visible cracks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d1622d0f2bc1a5dba81","word":"appearance","forms":["appearance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96ca655947f14075","term":"appearance","forms":["appearance","appearances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出現；現身","explanation":"指人或事物從看不見到進入視線的動作或事實，重點在“出現”這一過程，而不是出現之後的外貌。","examples":[{"en":"His sudden appearance surprised everyone.","zh":"他的突然出現讓大家都很驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The appearance of dark clouds warned us of rain.","zh":"烏雲的出現提醒我們可能要下雨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appearance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3882d8e345a81034","term":"appearance","forms":["appearance","appearances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外表；外在樣子","explanation":"指一個人或事物呈現在眼前的樣子，包括身體外觀和整體給人的視覺印象，是“出現並被看見”後留下的外在形態。","examples":[{"en":"The building has changed a lot in appearance.","zh":"這座建築的外觀變化很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm appearance hid how nervous she was.","zh":"她平靜的外表掩蓋了她內心的緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appearance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-abbe51030b1dbc63a354","word":"appetite","forms":["appetite"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6a1d0e5355ae6d8","term":"appetite","forms":["appetite","appetites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胃口；食慾","explanation":"指身體想吃或想喝東西的狀態，也就是胃口。運動、空腹等情況可以使 appetite 變強，而生病或看到不合胃口的食物可能使它消失。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, I had a huge appetite.","zh":"長途徒步後，我胃口特別好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smell of the medicine took away my appetite.","zh":"藥味讓我沒了胃口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appetite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c87bb0ef83b82adf","term":"appetite","forms":["appetite","appetites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈慾望；渴望","explanation":"這裡把“胃想要食物”的畫面擴大到“人強烈想要某種東西或經歷”，可以指對刺激、成功、冒險等的熱切渴望。","examples":[{"en":"She has an appetite for adventure.","zh":"她強烈渴望冒險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audience showed a strong appetite for change.","zh":"觀眾表現出對變革的強烈願望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appetite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-439872a2ee86c812ae38","word":"applaud","forms":["applaud"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8569dfeef430acb4","term":"applaud","forms":["applaud","applauds","applauding","applauded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鼓掌表示讚賞","explanation":"指用拍手這一實際動作表示對錶演、演講或其他事情的認可，重點在現場的鼓掌行為。","examples":[{"en":"The audience applauded for several minutes after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，觀眾鼓掌了好幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone applauded when the winner came on stage.","zh":"獲勝者上臺時，大家都鼓起了掌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/applaud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6a9443351ae0237","term":"applaud","forms":["applaud","applauds","applauding","applauded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"讚許；稱讚","explanation":"把“拍手認可”擴大為表達態度上的讚許：你可以 applaud 某人的決定、努力、勇氣或動機，即使並不贊同全部細節。","examples":[{"en":"We applaud her efforts to make the school more accessible.","zh":"我們讚賞她努力讓這所學校更便利、更易於使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Residents applauded the decision to preserve the old library.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/applaud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e1dad7c250f5ba7b435b","word":"applause","forms":["applause"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1877e5474d73ac1c","term":"applause","forms":["applause","applauses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"掌聲；公開讚許","explanation":"指人們透過鼓掌、歡呼等方式公開表示讚賞；也可以不只指聲音本身，而指這種公開認可。演出結束時響起的掌聲，就是最典型的 applause。","examples":[{"en":"The singer received loud applause after her final song.","zh":"歌手唱完最後一首歌后，贏得了熱烈的掌聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new plan won applause from local residents.","zh":"這項新計劃贏得了當地居民的公開讚許。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/applause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a7bd3e2360a3d29eea4","word":"apple","forms":["apple"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38b3b8fc0fa3833d","term":"apple","forms":["apple","apples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蘋果","explanation":"指蘋果樹結出的常見圓形水果，通常可以直接食用，也常用於烹飪。","examples":[{"en":"I packed an apple for my lunch.","zh":"我給午餐帶了一個蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These apples are sweet and crisp.","zh":"這些蘋果又甜又脆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8ab6bcabd2dd890","term":"apple","forms":["apple","apples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蘋果（省略形式）","explanation":"仍然表示蘋果，只是某些上下文中省略了完整表達或作為簡略寫法出現，和基本水果義沒有區別。","examples":[{"en":"We bought apple and pear juice for the trip.","zh":"我們為旅途買了蘋果汁和梨汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She packed an apple beside her sandwich.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e87bdd39792a988e1955","word":"appliance","forms":["appliance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d398013a980bcf6","term":"appliance","forms":["appliance","appliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家用電器","explanation":"最常見的意思是家中使用的電器，尤其是冰箱、洗衣機、烘乾機等幫助完成家務的裝置。它仍然保留著“為某種用途服務的裝置”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Please unplug all appliances before you leave the house.","zh":"你離開房子前請拔掉所有電器的插頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new kitchen appliances use less energy than the old ones.","zh":"這些新的廚房電器比舊的更省電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a2a094651f55e92","term":"appliance","forms":["appliance","appliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用於特定目的的器具或裝置","explanation":"它可以泛指為完成某個具體目的而使用的工具、器具或裝置。核心意思是“把某種用途落實到一個能派上用場的東西上”，範圍比家用電器更廣。","examples":[{"en":"The workshop bought a new appliance for cutting thick sheets of metal.","zh":"這家車間買了一臺用於切割厚金屬板的新裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This simple appliance makes it easier to remove stains from fabric.","zh":"這個簡單的器具讓去除織物上的汙漬更容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6f50bf21d58cd3c605d","word":"applicable","forms":["applicable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9253c7456aa70ada","term":"applicable","forms":["applicable","more applicable","most applicable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"適用於；對……適用","explanation":"如果一條規則、條件或方法能夠覆蓋某個物件或情況，就可以說它對該物件或情況 applicable，也就是“適用、相關”。","examples":[{"en":"This rule is applicable to all visitors.","zh":"這條規則適用於所有訪客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discount is not applicable to sale items.","zh":"這項折扣不適用於特價商品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/applicable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42aef2f386567bd5a6a3","word":"applicant","forms":["applicant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8a9b919d4b31877","term":"applicant","forms":["applicant","applicants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"申請人；申請者","explanation":"指為了得到職位、名額、許可或其他東西而提出申請的人，重點是“提出申請的人”這一身份。","examples":[{"en":"The company received applications from more than fifty applicants.","zh":"這家公司收到了五十多名申請人的申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each applicant must provide two references.","zh":"每位申請人都必須提供兩名推薦人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/applicant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b0fbdac54e60eec","term":"applicant","forms":["applicant","applicants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律申請人","explanation":"在法律語境中，指向法院或其他有權機關提出正式請求的人；它仍然是“把請求遞出去的人”，只是請求具有法律程式性質。","examples":[{"en":"The applicant asked the court to review the decision.","zh":"申請人請求法院複審這項決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As the applicant for an injunction, she had to demonstrate immediate danger.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/applicant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1fe289205936c3fdb611","word":"application","forms":["application"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9de593ae1b40718","term":"application","forms":["application","applications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"應用；運用","explanation":"指把知識、方法、規則或手段用於實際目的，即把某個想法真正放到具體問題上使用。","examples":[{"en":"The course focuses on the application of theory to real-world problems.","zh":"這門課重點講把理論應用於現實問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The practical application of this formula saves engineers time.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/application","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5843f77bdbd6aa3","term":"application","forms":["application","applications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"應用程式","explanation":"指為明確用途設計的計算機程式，使用者把它當作一個完整工具來使用，例如社交、辦公或繪圖軟體。","examples":[{"en":"This application lets users share files securely.","zh":"這個應用程式可以讓使用者安全地共享檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This application tracks expenses without an internet connection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/application","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f89c1bc7d06efdf","term":"application","forms":["application","applications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"申請；申請材料","explanation":"指為求職、入學、參加課程或獲得某種機會而提交的正式請求，也可指提交的申請檔案。","examples":[{"en":"She submitted her application for the research position yesterday.","zh":"她昨天提交了研究職位的申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Submit your application with a copy of your diploma.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/application","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97a5e41b45ddd2b23810","word":"apply","forms":["apply"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ead323a712c3bff8","term":"apply","forms":["apply","applies","applying","applied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塗上；貼到","explanation":"把某種物質或東西放到另一個表面或物件上，突出“接觸並覆蓋或附著”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Apply the cream to the rash twice a day.","zh":"每天在皮疹處塗兩次藥膏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She applied a fresh coat of paint to the door.","zh":"她給門刷了一層新的油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-377d544f173a283d","term":"apply","forms":["apply","applies","applying","applied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用於；運用","explanation":"把錢、資源、時間或工具投入某個具體用途，相當於把它“接到”那個用途上。","examples":[{"en":"The charity applied the donation to building a new shelter.","zh":"這家慈善機構把這筆捐款用於建造新的收容所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She applied her experience to the new project.","zh":"她把自己的經驗運用到了這個新專案中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3205127425929c3","term":"apply","forms":["apply","applies","applying","applied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"申請","explanation":"把自己提交給機構或職位選擇過程，表示正式請求獲得工作、課程、許可等機會。","examples":[{"en":"I applied to three universities for a place on their engineering courses.","zh":"我向三所大學申請了工程課程的名額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She applied for a part-time job at the bookstore.","zh":"她申請了書店的一份兼職工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8c8e58878939908e985","word":"appoint(ment)","forms":["appoint","appointment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48d2f38d77e64a80","term":"appoint","forms":["appoint","appoints","appointing","appointed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確定時間、地點或會議","explanation":"把某件事正式定在某個時間或地點，尤其用於會議、會面等安排；也可以直接說確定這場活動本身。核心畫面是把事情釘在一個明確的“點”上。","examples":[{"en":"The committee appointed Friday morning for the final interview.","zh":"委員會把最後一次面試定在星期五上午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They appointed a quiet room for the meeting.","zh":"他們把一間安靜的房間定為會議地點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appoint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-447b992837876047","term":"appoint","forms":["appoint","appoints","appointing","appointed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"任命某人擔任職位","explanation":"正式指定某人承擔某個職位、角色或職責，就像把這個人固定到一個崗位上。這個意思常見於政府、公司、學校和其他組織。","examples":[{"en":"The board appointed Maya as the new finance director.","zh":"董事會任命瑪雅為新的財務總監。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was appointed to lead the investigation.","zh":"她被任命負責這項調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appoint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-124f01bd577f3d42","term":"appointment","forms":["appointment","appointments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"任命；任用","explanation":"指任命某人擔任職位、承擔受信任的職責這一行為，重點在“作出任命”這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"Her appointment as director was announced yesterday.","zh":"她被任命為主任的訊息昨天公佈了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The board approved his appointment to the committee.","zh":"董事會批准了對他的委員會任命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appointment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec0316cdcf33721c","term":"appointment","forms":["appointment","appointments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預約；約定的會面","explanation":"指事先把見面的時間和安排定下來，也可以指已經約定好的那次會面。這是現代日常英語中最常見的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"I have an appointment with the dentist at three.","zh":"我三點和牙醫有預約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could we make an appointment to discuss the project?","zh":"我們可以約個時間討論這個專案嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appointment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3e8234402a37d502b91","word":"appreciate","forms":["appreciate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e58f1873e99ecf21","term":"appreciate","forms":["appreciate","appreciates","appreciating","appreciated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感激","explanation":"看出別人付出中的價值，因此表示感謝。它常用於感謝幫助、時間、努力或支援，語氣通常真誠而禮貌。","examples":[{"en":"I really appreciate your help with this project.","zh":"我真的很感激你對這個專案的幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We appreciate you taking the time to meet with us.","zh":"感謝你抽出時間來見我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appreciate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1ad1539fccea1cc","term":"appreciate","forms":["appreciate","appreciates","appreciating","appreciated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欣賞；重視","explanation":"認識到某人或某物的價值、優點或美好之處，因此對它抱有欣賞或重視的態度。","examples":[{"en":"As I got older, I learned to appreciate quiet mornings.","zh":"隨著年齡增長，我學會了珍惜安靜的早晨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She appreciates good design and careful craftsmanship.","zh":"她欣賞優秀的設計和精心的工藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appreciate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be49f6d6b2f6ae049681","word":"appreciation","forms":["appreciation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9688e0739f844c34","term":"appreciation","forms":["appreciation","appreciations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感激；讚賞","explanation":"表示對他人的幫助、努力或長期付出給予認可和感謝，常帶有敬意；這就是“看見別人付出的價值”。","examples":[{"en":"We gave her a card as a small token of our appreciation.","zh":"我們送給她一張卡片，聊表我們的感激之情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I want to express my appreciation for your patience.","zh":"我想對你的耐心表示感謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appreciation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-edbbf517a921a120","term":"appreciation","forms":["appreciation","appreciations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理解；體會","explanation":"表示準確地看清一件事的難處、意義或複雜性，而不只是知道它存在；也就是“看見它真正的價值或分量”。","examples":[{"en":"Living abroad gave him a better appreciation of the challenges faced by immigrants.","zh":"在國外生活讓他更能體會移民所面臨的困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need an appreciation of the risks before making a decision.","zh":"在作出決定前，你需要充分了解其中的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appreciation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-042b8f64044ee7990f52","word":"apprentice","forms":["apprentice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c445ef9a1b8399f3","term":"apprentice","forms":["apprentice","apprentices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學徒；學藝者","explanation":"指在有經驗的師傅、工匠或專業人士指導下，透過實際工作學習某種手藝或行業技能的人。這是這個詞最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She started work as an apprentice electrician at eighteen.","zh":"她十八歲時開始當電工學徒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apprentice learned the trade by working beside an experienced carpenter.","zh":"這名學徒透過跟著一位有經驗的木匠工作來學習這門手藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apprentice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cec9111de36d4a50c3e6","word":"approach","forms":["approach"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f64db1195a6d8d9","term":"approach","forms":["approach","approaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接近；臨近","explanation":"指人、事物或時間逐漸靠近，也可以引申為某件事即將發生。","examples":[{"en":"The approach of winter brought colder nights.","zh":"冬天的臨近帶來了更寒冷的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the approach of the storm from the beach.","zh":"我們在海灘上看著暴風雨逐漸逼近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8ce5ed403eb8865","term":"approach","forms":["approach","approaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通道；入口","explanation":"指通向建築物、地點或目標的道路、通路，也可以比較抽象地指接觸某人的途徑。","examples":[{"en":"The narrow approach to the village was blocked by snow.","zh":"通往村子的狹窄道路被雪堵住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge provides the main approach to the island.","zh":"這座橋是通往該島的主要通道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-264fed9afee9752c","term":"approach","forms":["approach","approaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方法；思路","explanation":"指處理問題、制定政策或完成任務時所採用的思路和方式，也就是“從哪條路接近問題”。","examples":[{"en":"We need a new approach to reducing energy use.","zh":"我們需要一種減少能源使用的新思路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm approach to difficult clients works well.","zh":"她處理難纏客戶時採取的冷靜方式很有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfc97fd793a01bbb","term":"approach","forms":["approach","approaches","approaching","approached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"靠近；接近","explanation":"指人在空間或時間上向某人、某物或某個時刻靠近。","examples":[{"en":"She approached the door quietly.","zh":"她悄悄地走近門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The deadline is approaching fast.","zh":"截止日期很快就要到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55586fe16ef14a08","term":"approach","forms":["approach","approaches","approaching","approached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向……靠近","explanation":"指向某人、某物或某個目標移動，也可引申為逐漸接近某種狀態、水平或價值。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer approached the judge's desk.","zh":"律師走近了法官的桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature is approaching zero.","zh":"溫度正在接近零度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ceb51f36a5cadd58","term":"approach","forms":["approach","approaches","approaching","approached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"著手處理","explanation":"表示開始用某種思路或方式處理政策、問題或任務，也就是選擇一條“接近問題的路”。","examples":[{"en":"We need to approach the problem from a different angle.","zh":"我們需要從不同角度處理這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team approached the task carefully.","zh":"團隊認真地著手處理這項任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c39a7d54f55beb0050b6","word":"appropriate","forms":["appropriate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8dbee2400b1547c7","term":"appropriate","forms":["appropriate","more appropriate","most appropriate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合適的；恰當的","explanation":"指某個選擇、做法或事物符合當前目的和情況，放在這裡正合適。","examples":[{"en":"We need to find an appropriate way to explain the change.","zh":"我們需要找一個合適的方式來解釋這項變動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That would be an appropriate response to the situation.","zh":"那會是對這種情況恰當的回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appropriate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-039f6dba49d398ee","term":"appropriate","forms":["appropriate","more appropriate","most appropriate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"得體的；合乎禮儀的","explanation":"特指言語、衣著或行為符合特定社交場合的禮貌和分寸，不會讓人覺得失禮或冒犯。","examples":[{"en":"Please wear something appropriate for the interview.","zh":"請穿適合面試場合的衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dark formal clothing would be appropriate for the memorial.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appropriate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9deb65b8788f41ff94a2","word":"approval","forms":["approval"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5de266ce98fa007","term":"approval","forms":["approval","approvals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"批准；同意","explanation":"指有權作決定的人或機構表示“可以”，因此可以是對提議的同意，也可以是確認某人、某物或某項安排符合要求。它尤其常用於正式流程、申請和工作檔案中。","examples":[{"en":"We need approval from the manager before we place the order.","zh":"下訂單前，我們需要得到經理的批准。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan received approval from the city council.","zh":"這項計劃獲得了市議會的批准。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acdcc0f922fb0d54","term":"approval","forms":["approval","approvals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讚許；認可","explanation":"指對某人的表現、選擇或作品持肯定態度，並透過話語、表情或鼓勵表現出來。它不像正式許可那樣強調權力或程式，而是讓人感到“做得好、我支援你”。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents showed their approval by cheering loudly.","zh":"她的父母大聲歡呼，以此表示讚許。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He nodded in approval when he heard the suggestion.","zh":"聽到這個建議時，他點頭表示贊同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74e21680eac7385ca408","word":"approve","forms":["approve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0db75242d0904fcc","term":"approve","forms":["approve","approves","approving","approved","approvest","approvedst","approveth","-","approven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式批准","explanation":"指有權決定的人或機構經過判斷後，正式接受某項方案、申請、決定或規定，相當於在上面蓋上認可章。","examples":[{"en":"The committee approved the new safety plan.","zh":"委員會批准了新的安全計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your loan application has been approved.","zh":"你的貸款申請已經獲批。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6ec1ad1328413a8","term":"approve","forms":["approve","approves","approving","approved","approvest","approvedst","approveth","-","approven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為好並表示贊同","explanation":"指說話人認為某個想法、決定或做法是好的，因此表示認可或贊成；重點不一定是擁有正式批准權。","examples":[{"en":"Most parents approve of the school’s decision.","zh":"大多數家長都贊同學校的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His parents approved of his decision to study music.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f02d05415bda6501","term":"approve","forms":["approve","approves","approving","approved","approvest","approvedst","approveth","-","approven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"贊同、認可某人或某事","explanation":"指對某人、某種行為或某個選擇感到滿意，認為它值得接受；尤其常用於表達是否喜歡或接受某人的伴侶、朋友或做法。","examples":[{"en":"My parents don’t approve of my new job.","zh":"我父母不贊成我換的新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She approves of the way you handled the problem.","zh":"她贊同你處理這個問題的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00efcee9cb2a3a1f720b","word":"approximate","forms":["approximate"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e67152f9e5637b3","term":"approximate","forms":["approximate","more approximate","most approximate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"接近的；相似的","explanation":"表示某人、某物或某種性質接近另一個目標，但不一定相同；這個“靠近”可以是實際距離，也可以是外觀、性質或程度上的接近。","examples":[{"en":"The two paintings are approximate copies of each other.","zh":"這兩幅畫是彼此很相近的仿作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box is of approximate size and shape to the original.","zh":"這個盒子的大小和形狀與原來的大致相近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approximate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64fd616ff5ee49c7","term":"approximate","forms":["approximate","more approximate","most approximate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大致準確的","explanation":"專門說數字、結果或答案接近真實值，但還沒有精確到完全無誤；因此它帶有“只夠作大概參考”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The approximate cost of the repair is five hundred dollars.","zh":"這次維修的費用大約是五百美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We only have an approximate answer at this stage.","zh":"現階段我們只能得到一個大致答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approximate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ccdcdd8fb231382","term":"approximate","forms":["approximate","approximates","approximating","approximated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"估算","explanation":"根據已有資訊算出一個接近真實值的結果，而不是求得完全精確的答案；這是“向目標值靠近”的動詞版本。","examples":[{"en":"We approximated the travel time at three hours.","zh":"我們估算路程時間約為三個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We can approximate the distance using the map's scale.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/approximate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e79e8a37b08ee66604ad","word":"apron","forms":["apron"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3598787d881afb29","term":"apron","forms":["apron","aprons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圍裙","explanation":"圍在身體前面、通常覆蓋胸部和腿部的一件衣物，用來防止做飯、清潔或工作時弄髒裡面的衣服；它的核心形象就是擋在身前的一層保護。","examples":[{"en":"She tied an apron around her waist before cooking dinner.","zh":"她做晚飯前在腰間繫上了圍裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Flour covered the front of his apron.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dadcb6d9eb4b2721","term":"apron","forms":["apron","aprons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機場停機坪","explanation":"機場中緊鄰跑道、航站樓或其他設施的硬質鋪面，飛機可在這裡停放、上下客或進行地面作業；它保留了“圍在區域邊緣、承受活動”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"Several aircraft were waiting on the airport apron.","zh":"幾架飛機正在機場停機坪上等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fuel truck crossed the apron toward the waiting jet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5009a047a11fbd680bb4","word":"apt","forms":["apt"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e9f06f3d77c8ddb","term":"apt","forms":["apt","apter","more apt","aptest","most apt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"恰當的；合適的","explanation":"某個詞、例子、行動或安排與當前情況非常相稱，用它正合適。這個意思就是“嵌到了正確的位置上”。","examples":[{"en":"That is an apt metaphor for the situation.","zh":"那個比喻很貼切地說明了這種情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose an apt title for her article.","zh":"她為文章選了一個恰當的標題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89a9bb9ef93ca4e9","term":"apt","forms":["apt","apter","more apt","aptest","most apt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易；傾向於","explanation":"表示某人或某物有穩定的傾向，常常容易出現某種行為或結果。它不是說事情一定發生，而是說這種情況很容易發生。","examples":[{"en":"Young children are apt to lose interest quickly.","zh":"小孩子容易很快失去興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old engine is apt to stall in rain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cfb685eeca5933543873","word":"aquarium","forms":["aquarium"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-488c4d8e6ba742b1","term":"aquarium","forms":["aquarium","aquaria","aquariums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水族箱","explanation":"指通常由玻璃製成、裝有水、用來飼養活魚或其他水生動物的箱子。它就是把一個小型水下世界放進透明容器裡。","examples":[{"en":"We keep two small turtles in the aquarium.","zh":"我們在水族箱裡養了兩隻小烏龜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are watching the fish in the aquarium.","zh":"孩子們正在看水族箱裡的魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquarium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e1db16c063cea76","term":"aquarium","forms":["aquarium","aquaria","aquariums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水族館","explanation":"指向公眾展示活魚和其他水生動物的場所，通常有許多大型水池或水族箱。它可以看作把許多“小型水下世界”集中起來的公共展館。","examples":[{"en":"We visited the aquarium during our trip to the city.","zh":"我們去這座城市旅行時參觀了水族館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The aquarium keeps rescued turtles in a separate tank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquarium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-890cabe271136403326f","word":"arch","forms":["arch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8c114cac72ed1f5","term":"arch","forms":["arch","arches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拱形","explanation":"指向上彎曲、兩端較低的倒置U形，也就是一種拱起的弧形。它是拱門、拱頂等結構共同的基本形狀。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow arch was cut into the wall above the fireplace.","zh":"壁爐上方的牆上開了一個狹窄的拱形結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her eyebrows formed a graceful arch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5efec521c29a4aeb","term":"arch","forms":["arch","arches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承重拱","explanation":"指由梯形石塊或類似構件組成的拱形結構，能把上方的壓力向兩側傳開，因此可以支撐上面的重量。","examples":[{"en":"The old stone arch still supports the entrance to the castle.","zh":"這座古老的石拱仍然支撐著城堡的入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stone arch supports the narrow bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec5e78da5db4ebcf","term":"arch","forms":["arch","arches","arching","arched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拱起","explanation":"使身體或物體彎成向上隆起的拱形，例如貓把背拱起來；核心仍是從平直狀態變成弧形。","examples":[{"en":"The cat arched its back when it heard a noise outside.","zh":"貓聽到外面的聲音時把背拱了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat arched its back at the barking dog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed82e79b1df27dee2cf1","word":"archaeology","forms":["archaeology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a32467263c13e090","term":"archaeology","forms":["archaeology","archaeologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考古學；考古研究","explanation":"透過發掘遺址並分析器物、建築遺蹟等物質遺存，研究人類過去的學科或活動。它像是在地下尋找線索，再用這些線索還原古人的生活和歷史。","examples":[{"en":"She studied archaeology at university and later worked on Roman sites.","zh":"她在大學學習考古學，後來參與了羅馬遺址的研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archaeology of the island reveals how its first inhabitants lived.","zh":"這座島的考古研究揭示了最早居民的生活方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/archaeology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2e40fc1edb72ee9ed58","word":"architect","forms":["architect"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6606637c22ed8fe","term":"architect","forms":["architect","architects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築師","explanation":"指以設計建築物或其他結構為職業的人，通常還負責準備方案、協調施工或監督建造；核心形象就是負責整座建築藍圖的“總設計師”。","examples":[{"en":"Her dream is to become an architect and design public libraries.","zh":"她的夢想是成為一名建築師，設計公共圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The architect supervised the construction of the new museum.","zh":"這名建築師監督了新博物館的建造。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/architect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfe9423d16197584","term":"architect","forms":["architect","architects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"策劃者；幕後設計者","explanation":"指為達到某個目標而設計計劃、安排步驟並促成結果的人。這裡不一定和建築有關，而是把建築師設計藍圖的形象借來描述重大計劃或事件的主要策劃者。","examples":[{"en":"She was the architect of the agreement that ended the dispute.","zh":"她是那項結束爭端的協議的主要策劃者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was the architect of the club's financial recovery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/architect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ca303a3bf7ddf7be865","word":"architecture","forms":["architecture"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24e2d3d8af22cb88","term":"architecture","forms":["architecture","architectures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築設計與建造","explanation":"指設計建築物和其他構築物，並安排其建造的藝術與技術；通常也包含比例、裝飾和整體美感。","examples":[{"en":"The architecture of the old city reflects several different cultures.","zh":"這座老城的建築風格體現了多種不同的文化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied architecture at university.","zh":"她在大學學習建築學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/architecture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-782855f54458da32","term":"architecture","forms":["architecture","architectures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築風格","explanation":"指某一時期、地區或流派共同採用的建築設計樣式，是“藍圖”在外觀和形式上的一類具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"The town is famous for its medieval architecture.","zh":"這個小鎮以其中世紀建築風格聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cathedral combines Gothic architecture with a modern entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/architecture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d87c5483061e40d0","term":"architecture","forms":["architecture","architectures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"系統或產品的設計結構","explanation":"指系統、產品或軟體由哪些部分組成，以及這些部分如何協作的總體設計；它就是“建築藍圖”在非建築領域的最常見延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The new software architecture makes the application easier to update.","zh":"新的軟體架構讓這個應用更容易更新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The software's architecture keeps customer data separate from billing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/architecture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":3,"counts":{"114":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-0eb3e36bfb24dcd9bb1d","word":"archive","forms":["archive"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdc1aca3bb93fb08","term":"archive","forms":["archive","archives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檔案庫；檔案館","explanation":"指專門儲存舊檔案、信件、報紙、記錄等資料的地方，通常供研究、查證或瞭解歷史使用。它可以是實體的檔案館，也可以是數字檔案庫。","examples":[{"en":"The letters are kept in the city archive.","zh":"這些信件儲存在市檔案館裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found the photograph in an online archive.","zh":"我在一個線上檔案庫裡找到了這張照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/archive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12f9b222536e7162","term":"archive","forms":["archive","archives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檔案資料；資料庫","explanation":"指被儲存下來的資料整體，例如某人的信件、某段歷史的記錄或某一學科收集的文獻。這裡的archive不是存放資料的地方，而是“被儲存的那批資料”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has an archive of old newspapers.","zh":"這家博物館收藏著一批舊報紙檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive contains letters from displaced families.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/archive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a91ee5f0106c2b35c11","word":"area","forms":["area"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58c2f71f5456baed","term":"area","forms":["area","areas","areæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面積","explanation":"指一個表面所佔的大小，通常用平方單位來測量；它就是把空間圈出來後計算其大小。","examples":[{"en":"The area of the room is twenty square meters.","zh":"這個房間的面積是二十平方米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island is about 300 square kilometers in area.","zh":"這座島的面積約為三百平方公里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/area","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e00f3225718f3711","term":"area","forms":["area","areas","areæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"區域；地區","explanation":"指地理上被看作一個整體的地方，可以是城市中的一片地方，也可以是更大的地區。","examples":[{"en":"There are several good restaurants in this area.","zh":"這一帶有幾家不錯的餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rain flooded the low-lying area near the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/area","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88e86e8bd2f474ba","term":"area","forms":["area","areas","areæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"範圍；領域","explanation":"把被圈出的空間引申為思想、知識、工作或能力所涉及的範圍，也就是某個話題或活動領域。","examples":[{"en":"She has a lot of experience in the area of education.","zh":"她在教育領域有很多經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report needs improvement in several areas.","zh":"這份報告有幾個方面需要改進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/area","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-572e31f55b6ac1b13fd5","word":"arena","forms":["arena"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80544d49d42026e4","term":"arena","forms":["arena","arenas","arenae","arenæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽或表演場地","explanation":"指圍起來供比賽、表演或其他大型活動進行的區域，可以是露天場地，也可以是專門的比賽場。核心畫面是人們聚集在中央、觀眾圍坐在周圍。","examples":[{"en":"A large crowd filled the seats of the arena.","zh":"大批觀眾坐滿了場館的座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The skaters entered the arena to thunderous applause.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arena","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-807a81f396adf240","term":"arena","forms":["arena","arenas","arenae","arenæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"容納場地的大型建築","explanation":"指裝有這種活動場地的整座大型建築，通常用於室內體育比賽、音樂會等重大活動。也就是說，s1偏重中央的活動區域，s2偏重包住它的建築。","examples":[{"en":"The arena is grey with white beams.","zh":"這座場館是灰色的，配有白色的橫樑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The arena can seat twenty thousand spectators.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arena","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a21678b6a493d3e4a680","word":"argue(argument)","forms":["argue"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03f0716a073a1e32","term":"argue","forms":["argue","argues","arguing","argued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯示；說明","explanation":"某個事實、跡象或結果把人引向一個結論，說明這個結論可能成立。這裡不是人在爭吵，而是證據在“替某個結論說話”。","examples":[{"en":"The steady rise in costs argues for a different plan.","zh":"成本持續上升說明應該換一個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These results argue against changing the schedule.","zh":"這些結果說明不宜更改日程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7757f9e7a4405038","term":"argue","forms":["argue","argues","arguing","argued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"爭論；辯論","explanation":"兩方或多人就不同觀點交換理由、表示反對或試圖說服對方。重點是觀點對立和理由交鋒，不一定已經發展成吵架。","examples":[{"en":"The two scientists argued about the best way to test the theory.","zh":"兩位科學家就檢驗這一理論的最佳方法展開了爭論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They argued for stronger safety rules.","zh":"他們主張制定更嚴格的安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-670f8d0557066109","term":"argue","forms":["argue","argues","arguing","argued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提出並維護觀點","explanation":"把一個觀點或論點講出來，並用理由支援它；可以理解為把“理由擺到桌面上，為自己的觀點辯護”。","examples":[{"en":"She argued that the policy would hurt small businesses.","zh":"她提出理由認為，這項政策會損害小企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She argued that shorter shifts would improve safety.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-877d41bc540c57e06ac1","word":"arise","forms":["arise"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6f825992639f154","term":"arise","forms":["arise","arises","arising","arose","arisen","arised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起身；站起來","explanation":"表示人或物從較低的位置向上起來，重點是姿勢或位置發生了向上的變化。例如跪著的人站起來，就可以用 arise。","examples":[{"en":"She arose from her chair and walked to the window.","zh":"她從椅子上站起來，走到窗邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone arose when the judge entered.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c49d1d53402fd844","term":"arise","forms":["arise","arises","arising","arose","arisen","arised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起床；起身","explanation":"表示從床上或休息處起來，尤其指起床。這仍然符合“從靜止狀態向上出現”的核心畫面，但語氣比日常的“起床”更正式。","examples":[{"en":"He arose before dawn to begin the long journey.","zh":"他在黎明前起床，開始了漫長的旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monks arise before the morning bells.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7583c6836a66122b","term":"arise","forms":["arise","arises","arising","arose","arisen","arised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出現；產生；開始發生","explanation":"表示某種現象、問題、行動或感覺從原本不明顯的狀態中出現，並開始被看見、注意到或發揮作用。雲升起並遮住陽光、問題產生，都可以理解為某物“冒出來”了。","examples":[{"en":"Several problems arose during the project.","zh":"專案期間出現了幾個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A thick fog arose over the river at night.","zh":"夜裡一層濃霧在河面上升起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca75eaf4e00caa4b9b1d","word":"arithmetic","forms":["arithmetic"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee92a5648f02512a","term":"arithmetic","forms":["arithmetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"算術的；與算術有關的","explanation":"表示某個概念、方法或物件屬於算術，和數字的基本運算有關；它是名詞 arithmetic 的形容詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"We used an arithmetic calculation to check the result.","zh":"我們用算術計算檢查了結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students learned how to find the arithmetic mean.","zh":"學生們學習瞭如何求算術平均數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arithmetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64e4cf9aad980039","term":"arithmetic","forms":["arithmetic","arithmetics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"算術；基本數運算","explanation":"arithmetic 是處理整數、有理數、實數或複數，並進行加、減、乘、除等基本運算的數學分支；日常也可指這些基本計算本身。","examples":[{"en":"The child is learning basic arithmetic at school.","zh":"這個孩子正在學校學習基礎算術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I checked the arithmetic before sending the report.","zh":"我在傳送報告前檢查了計算結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arithmetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ddf7ff5ebd9d66ce1614","word":"arm","forms":["arm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7529db8334b948fc","term":"arm","forms":["arm","arms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手臂","explanation":"arm 最基本的意思是從肩膀延伸到手腕、通常也包括手的上肢部分。它正好對應“伸出去並提供力量的部分”這一記憶線索。","examples":[{"en":"She raised her arm to ask a question.","zh":"她舉起手臂提問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hurt his left arm while playing tennis.","zh":"他打網球時弄傷了左臂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3ea855ad5cc7483","term":"arm","forms":["arm","arms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"武器","explanation":"arm 可以指武器，尤其常用複數 arms 泛指槍械等武器。它與“讓對方擁有可行動的手臂”這一記憶線索相呼應。","examples":[{"en":"The guards were trained to use arms safely.","zh":"警衛接受了安全使用武器的訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law strictly controls the sale of arms.","zh":"法律嚴格管制武器銷售。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f62f95c0a62fa19","term":"arm","forms":["arm","arms","arming","armed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提供所需能力","explanation":"不僅可以給人武器，也可以給人或組織提供完成任務所需的工具、知識、權力、資訊或能力；也就是讓對方擁有能夠行動的“手臂”。","examples":[{"en":"The training armed her with the skills she needed to lead the project.","zh":"這次培訓讓她掌握了領導這個專案所需的技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report armed the committee with enough evidence to challenge the proposal.","zh":"這份報告為委員會提供了足夠的證據，使其能夠質疑這項提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc083dbe056a217097b6","word":"armed","forms":["armed"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64784ccbf68d46c8","term":"armed","forms":["armed","more armed","most armed"],"pos":"adj","zh":"配備武器的","explanation":"指人、軍隊、國家或其他事物已經配有武器，處於可以用武器行動的狀態。這是 armed 最核心的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"The guards were armed with rifles.","zh":"警衛們配有步槍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two armed guards stood outside the vault.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/armed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7f6b671e1d93180","term":"armed","forms":["armed"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有手臂的","explanation":"指某人、動物、雕像或其他形體具有手臂，尤其常說明手臂的數量或型別。這是從 arm“手臂”延伸出的另一條主線。","examples":[{"en":"The statue shows a three-armed figure.","zh":"這座雕像表現的是一個有三條手臂的人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A six-armed figure stood beside the temple entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/armed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d86982d2329abe574051","word":"arms","forms":["arms"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d85d6efdc027f2e0","term":"arms","forms":["arms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"武器","explanation":"表示供戰鬥或防衛使用的武器裝備，核心畫面就是一個人手中或身邊的武裝。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers laid down their arms and left the town.","zh":"士兵們放下武器，離開了城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country has agreed to stop selling arms to the region.","zh":"該國同意停止向這個地區出售武器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arms","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2fd5cdba2b1484db46c","word":"army","forms":["army"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-588d07b9c2265ed8","term":"army","forms":["army","armies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地面作戰軍隊","explanation":"army最基本的意思是規模較大、組織嚴密、主要負責地面作戰的軍隊。它強調的是一整套有指揮和編制的地面武裝力量，而不只是幾個士兵。","examples":[{"en":"The army moved into the city before dawn.","zh":"軍隊在黎明前進入了這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined the army after college.","zh":"她大學畢業後參了軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/army","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3efd1897d690ac17","term":"army","forms":["army","armies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"為同一目標行動的大群人","explanation":"在比喻用法中，army把“組織嚴密、人數很多、朝同一目標行動”的畫面移到了人群上，例如一大群專業人員共同完成任務。","examples":[{"en":"An army of volunteers helped clean the park.","zh":"一大群志願者幫忙清理了公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It took an army of lawyers to prepare the case.","zh":"準備這個案子需要一大群律師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/army","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4a00c840fc355991927","word":"around","forms":["around"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30bc37029d7a5e82","term":"around","forms":["around"],"pos":"adv","zh":"繞圈、環繞","explanation":"表示沿圓形或近似圓形的路線移動，核心畫面是“繞著一箇中心轉”。","examples":[{"en":"The birds circled around above the field.","zh":"鳥兒在田地上空盤旋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy chased its tail around and around.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/around","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66a15383c99591b3","term":"around","forms":["around"],"pos":"adv","zh":"圍在周圍","explanation":"表示人或物聚集到某人或某物周圍，像圍成一個圈。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone gathered around to hear the story.","zh":"大家圍過來聽這個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children gathered around to watch him juggle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/around","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b304c2efcf0e9bc0","term":"around","forms":["around"],"pos":"prep","zh":"圍繞","explanation":"表示某物環繞著另一個物體，形成一圈或近似一圈的關係。","examples":[{"en":"He tied a red ribbon around the box.","zh":"他在盒子周圍繫了一條紅絲帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sat around the campfire sharing stories.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/around","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0b4965f5e0dd0a4df84","word":"arouse","forms":["arouse"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bf3b357de7373a8","term":"arouse","forms":["arouse","arouses","arousing","aroused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"激起情緒或興趣","explanation":"指使某種感情、反應或興趣從平靜狀態中出現或變強，例如激起同情、嫉妒、憤怒或好奇心。","examples":[{"en":"The story aroused my curiosity.","zh":"這個故事激起了我的好奇心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unfair decision aroused public anger.","zh":"這項不公平的決定激起了公眾的憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b3d15707a3580f3","term":"arouse","forms":["arouse","arouses","arousing","aroused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喚醒","explanation":"指把睡著、昏沉或失去知覺的人弄醒，使其重新恢復清醒。","examples":[{"en":"The loud alarm aroused everyone in the house.","zh":"響亮的警報聲把屋裡所有人都叫醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was aroused from sleep by a knock at the door.","zh":"她被敲門聲從睡夢中驚醒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef79234764ffda26b1d7","word":"arrange(ment)","forms":["arrange","arrangement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a989442b96424994","term":"arrange","forms":["arrange","arranges","arranging","arranged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"整理；排列；組織","explanation":"把人、物品、資訊或步驟按照一定順序放好，使整體變得有條理。這個意義保留了“排成一列”的基本畫面，也可以引申為組織一項活動或事務。","examples":[{"en":"She arranged the books by subject.","zh":"她按主題把書整理好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to arrange the chairs before the meeting.","zh":"我們需要在會議前把椅子擺好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab32b449f839b415","term":"arrange","forms":["arrange","arranges","arranging","arranged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預先安排；籌劃","explanation":"提前把將要發生的事情計劃妥當，例如約定見面、準備晚餐或安排交通。這裡排好的不再只是物品，而是未來的時間、人員和步驟。","examples":[{"en":"I arranged to meet her outside the station.","zh":"我安排好在車站外和她見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They arranged for a taxi to pick us up.","zh":"他們安排了一輛計程車來接我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f0130c1196d8cfb","term":"arrangement","forms":["arrangement","arrangements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安排；整理","explanation":"指把人或事物按一定目的放到合適位置、順序或狀態中的行為，強調“安排”這個過程。","examples":[{"en":"The arrangement of the chairs took less than an hour.","zh":"安排這些椅子的位置不到一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to discuss the arrangement of the meeting.","zh":"我們需要討論會議的安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrangement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e81b45ca80ddad8","term":"arrangement","forms":["arrangement","arrangements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"準備；安排","explanation":"指為即將發生的事情預先做好的一系列安排和準備，通常包括時間、地點、人員或所需物品。","examples":[{"en":"We have made arrangements for your visit next week.","zh":"我們已經為你下週的來訪做好了安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is making arrangements to move to a new apartment.","zh":"她正在安排搬到一套新公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrangement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7efc4c3f3db72b0","term":"arrangement","forms":["arrangement","arrangements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"協議；約定","explanation":"指雙方或多方透過協商達成的安排，明確各自要做什麼或事情將怎樣進行。","examples":[{"en":"We have an arrangement with the landlord to pay the rent on the first day of each month.","zh":"我們和房東約定每月第一天交房租。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two companies reached an arrangement to share the costs.","zh":"兩家公司達成了分擔費用的協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrangement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dbe42cc09c16704aa3d6","word":"array","forms":["array"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0f3d69911e0353f","term":"array","forms":["array","arrays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有序排列的一組","explanation":"指按照一定順序排成的佇列、系列或整體。它把“許多東西”與“整齊有序地擺在一起”這兩個概念結合起來，是 array 最重要的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"An array of lanterns lined the path to the entrance.","zh":"一排排燈籠沿著通往入口的小路排列著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers examined an array of samples.","zh":"研究人員檢查了一組按序排列的樣本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/array","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-734bab68eb56bdd2","term":"array","forms":["array","arrays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量選擇或事物","explanation":"表示數量很大、種類很多的一批東西，常讓人覺得選擇豐富、場面壯觀。它仍然保留了“整齊擺出一大片”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The website offers a wide array of language courses.","zh":"這個網站提供各種各樣的語言課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Guests enjoyed an impressive array of desserts.","zh":"客人們享用了種類豐富、令人印象深刻的甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/array","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15f2e00b1492c562","term":"array","forms":["array","arrays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陣列","explanation":"在程式設計中，array 是把多個同類或相關元素按順序存放的資料結構，通常可以用數字下標找到每個元素。它就是“排好位置的一組資料”的技術化版本。","examples":[{"en":"The program stores the temperatures in an array.","zh":"程式把這些溫度值儲存在一個陣列中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the index to access the first element of the array.","zh":"使用下標訪問陣列中的第一個元素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/array","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f1c0fd436e9f13c99b0","word":"arrest","forms":["arrest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63944e3c2b5bea98","term":"arrest","forms":["arrest","arrests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"截停；阻止","explanation":"指把某個正在移動、進行或發展的東西截停，強調“停止這一動作或事件”本身。它可以用於具體運動，也可以用於抽象過程。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden arrest of the machine stopped the whole production line.","zh":"機器突然停住，整條生產線都停止了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new measures led to an arrest of the decline in sales.","zh":"新措施使銷售額的下滑停止了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e515999332e272a6","term":"arrest","forms":["arrest","arrests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拘捕；逮捕","explanation":"指警方或其他執法機構依法把嫌疑人控制並帶入法律羈押程式。這是“把人截停並控制住”在法律場景中的專門用法。","examples":[{"en":"The police made three arrests after the protest.","zh":"抗議活動後，警方逮捕了三人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The arrest of the suspect was reported on the evening news.","zh":"晚間新聞報道了這名嫌疑人的被捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aad3016e94b516b","term":"arrest","forms":["arrest","arrests","arresting","arrested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"阻止；遏制","explanation":"指使一個正在發展的過程、趨勢或局勢停止或減緩，例如阻止暴力升級。這裡不是把人抓起來，而是把事情的程序截住。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement helped arrest the spread of the rumors.","zh":"這項協議幫助遏制了謠言的傳播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Quick action may arrest the damage before it gets worse.","zh":"及時採取行動或許能在損害擴大前遏制住它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-160c63c146d720f0","term":"arrest","forms":["arrest","arrests","arresting","arrested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"依法拘捕","explanation":"指執法人員依法奪取某人的行動自由，把對方帶入拘押狀態。這是“把人截停並控制住”的法律用法。","examples":[{"en":"The officers arrested a suspect near the station.","zh":"警察在車站附近逮捕了一名嫌疑人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was arrested for driving without a license.","zh":"她因無證駕駛被逮捕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ba137ba3df58ba75a42","word":"arrival","forms":["arrival"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00a0187d491d9ccb","term":"arrival","forms":["arrival","arrivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"到達某地","explanation":"這是最基本的意思，指人或交通工具抵達某個地方這一動作或事實，核心畫面就是“到達終點”。","examples":[{"en":"We waited outside for the arrival of the train.","zh":"我們在外面等火車到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her arrival at the hotel was later than expected.","zh":"她抵達酒店的時間比預想的晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1dc0187db02ea6a","term":"arrival","forms":["arrival","arrivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某時刻的到來","explanation":"“抵達終點”的畫面也可以用於時間：某個日期、時刻或事件終於到來。","examples":[{"en":"The arrival of summer brought long, warm evenings.","zh":"夏天的到來帶來了漫長而溫暖的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With the arrival of winter, the mountain roads closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6dc09a300747b82d8bfe","word":"arrive","forms":["arrive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27a0f5a176758eb8","term":"arrive","forms":["arrive","arrives","arriving","arrived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到達某地","explanation":"表示人或物抵達某個地方，也就是走到“岸邊”並在那裡出現。它是 arrive 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We arrived at the station just before noon.","zh":"我們在中午前剛好到達車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The package has arrived at my office.","zh":"包裹已經送到我的辦公室了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40e59a8f1ead2a6e","term":"arrive","forms":["arrive","arrives","arriving","arrived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取得成功或聲望","explanation":"把成功看成抵達一個更高的社會位置：某人終於進入受認可的領域，獲得名望或成就。","examples":[{"en":"After years of hard work, she finally arrived as a leading designer.","zh":"經過多年的努力，她終於成為受認可的頂尖設計師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After her second bestseller, critics agreed she had arrived.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10c0dca2c547dc94","term":"arrive","forms":["arrive","arrives","arriving","arrived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"時間到來","explanation":"時間也可以被想象成來到我們面前；表示某個時刻終於到來，尤其是重要、期待或必須面對的時刻。","examples":[{"en":"The time has arrived for us to make a decision.","zh":"我們作出決定的時刻到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spring has arrived earlier than usual this year.","zh":"今年春天比往常來得更早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d471a50f43148bb9ab65","word":"arrogant","forms":["arrogant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6ed3d7e25f462fd","term":"arrogant","forms":["arrogant","more arrogant","most arrogant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傲慢的；自大的","explanation":"指一個人把自己看得過高，覺得自己比別人更重要、更聰明或更有資格，並表現出對別人的輕視和不尊重。它不只是“有自信”，而是自信膨脹到開始俯視別人。","examples":[{"en":"He sounded arrogant when he said that nobody else could do the job.","zh":"他說沒人能做這項工作時，聽起來很傲慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her arrogant attitude made it difficult for the team to work with her.","zh":"她傲慢的態度讓團隊很難和她合作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrogant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-864ea39fe7e2b27155a2","word":"arrow","forms":["arrow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c85ceaa53d3cd31","term":"arrow","forms":["arrow","arrows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"箭","explanation":"箭是由箭桿、箭頭和尾部穩定翼組成、用弓射出的投射物。它最基本的形象就是沿直線飛向目標的物體。","examples":[{"en":"She drew an arrow and aimed at the target.","zh":"她搭上一支箭，瞄準了靶子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The arrow flew straight into the center of the target.","zh":"箭筆直地飛進了靶心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ca62449275910ef","term":"arrow","forms":["arrow","arrows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"箭頭符號","explanation":"箭頭是畫出來的箭形符號，用來告訴人們方向、路線或下一步要看的位置。它保留了真實箭“指向前方”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Follow the arrows to find the main entrance.","zh":"沿著箭頭指示的方向就能找到正門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red arrow points to the emergency exit.","zh":"一個紅色箭頭指向緊急出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3cec99112255db9bf49","word":"art","forms":["art"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-602e0ad660f830a6","term":"art","forms":["art","arts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術","explanation":"art 是把聲音、色彩、形狀、動作等有意識地組織起來，以表達思想和情感、產生審美效果的創造活動。繪畫、音樂、舞蹈和文學都可以歸入這個概念。","examples":[{"en":"Many people see street murals as art rather than vandalism.","zh":"許多人把街頭壁畫看作藝術，而不是破壞行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Art can express feelings that words cannot capture.","zh":"藝術可以表達語言難以捕捉的情感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/art","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ce766f9ecd397d1","term":"art","forms":["art","arts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創造性的情感表達","explanation":"這裡的 art 強調把頭腦中的形象、感受或觀念創造性地表達出來，不限於視覺作品，也可以透過聲音、動作或社會互動來表達。","examples":[{"en":"For her, art is a way to make private feelings visible.","zh":"對她來說，藝術是一種讓私人情感變得可見的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For him, art became a way to express grief.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/art","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae3071c2e31b932e","term":"art","forms":["art","arts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高超技巧","explanation":"art 也可以指經過練習形成的、需要創造性和判斷力的技巧，所以任何複雜活動都可能被說成“一門藝術”。","examples":[{"en":"She has mastered the art of asking difficult questions politely.","zh":"她已經掌握了禮貌地提出難題的技巧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Making a good soup is an art.","zh":"做好一鍋湯是一門藝術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/art","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84393add8c489d335693","word":"article","forms":["article"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36a003eb7973d176","term":"article","forms":["article","articles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文章","explanation":"指報紙、雜誌、網站、期刊或百科全書中圍繞一個主題寫成的一篇文章。它可以是報道、說明、評論或研究性文字。","examples":[{"en":"I read an interesting article about urban farming.","zh":"我讀了一篇關於城市農業的有趣文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newspaper published an article on the effects of sleep loss.","zh":"那家報紙發表了一篇關於睡眠不足影響的文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/article","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaf020b6e1ecbda2","term":"article","forms":["article","articles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物品；專案","explanation":"指一個具體物品，或某一類事物中的一個成員。它強調這個東西是整體或類別中被單獨拿出來的一項。","examples":[{"en":"Every article of clothing must be labeled with its size.","zh":"每件衣服都必須標明尺碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every article of luggage must carry an identification tag.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/article","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c32e24174a185b9","term":"article","forms":["article","articles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冠詞","explanation":"語法術語，指放在名詞前後、用來說明名詞所指範圍或是否特指的詞；英語中的a、an和the都是冠詞。","examples":[{"en":"In English, “a” and “the” are articles.","zh":"在英語中，a和the都是冠詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This noun usually takes the definite article.","zh":"這個名詞通常要用定冠詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/article","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b788bcce1bb80bda0cb2","word":"articulate","forms":["articulate"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e946a628c9aa8715","term":"articulate","forms":["articulate","more articulate","most articulate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表達清楚而有效的","explanation":"形容表達有條理、意思明確，並且能有效傳達給別人；重點不是聲音大，而是說得讓人容易理解。","examples":[{"en":"The new manager is articulate and persuasive.","zh":"新經理表達清楚，而且很有說服力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students offered articulate accounts of their experiences.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/articulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e721696703b1bb4e","term":"articulate","forms":["articulate","more articulate","most articulate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"口齒清晰、善於表達的","explanation":"專門形容一個人說話發音清楚、措辭得當，能把想法有效地講出來。","examples":[{"en":"She is an articulate young scientist who explains difficult ideas clearly.","zh":"她是一位善於表達的年輕科學家，能把難懂的想法講清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The articulate teenager explained her invention with remarkable confidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/articulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-312688351c463267","term":"articulate","forms":["articulate","articulates","articulating","articulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使表達清楚有效","explanation":"把原本模糊或零散的內容整理成清楚、有效的表達，使別人更容易理解。","examples":[{"en":"The report articulates a clear plan for improving public transport.","zh":"這份報告清楚地闡述了改善公共交通的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interview helped articulate concerns residents had struggled to express.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/articulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c5798fcf21393a1","term":"articulate","forms":["articulate","articulates","articulating","articulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"清楚發音或說話","explanation":"把詞語的音節和聲音清楚地說出來，讓聽者能分辨每個詞；也可泛指說話清楚。","examples":[{"en":"Please articulate each word so everyone can hear you.","zh":"請把每個詞都說清楚，讓大家都能聽見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please articulate each syllable slowly for the recording.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/articulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d9c857381b8451e","term":"articulate","forms":["articulate","articulates","articulating","articulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把想法說出來","explanation":"把心裡已有但還不清楚的理由、感受或觀點變成具體的話說出來；這是“把內容分清並表達”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"I understand the problem, but I can't articulate why it bothers me.","zh":"我明白問題在哪裡，但說不清它為什麼讓我困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He struggled to articulate his fears during the interview.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/articulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d2971726bc45d4f7ce6","word":"artificial","forms":["artificial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65d1956a2c7aa424","term":"artificial","forms":["artificial","more artificial","most artificial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"人造的","explanation":"指由人製作出來、不是自然生長或自然形成的東西。它只說明來源是人為的，不一定表示質量差，也不一定表示有欺騙意圖。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel lobby was decorated with artificial flowers.","zh":"酒店大堂用人造花裝飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sweetener is made from artificial ingredients.","zh":"這種甜味劑由人工成分製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artificial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f77a4ac5319386f5","term":"artificial","forms":["artificial","more artificial","most artificial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"做作的；不真誠的","explanation":"形容人的態度、笑容、聲音或情感像是刻意裝出來的，缺少自然流露的真誠。這裡的“人造”從物品延伸到了人的表現。","examples":[{"en":"His smile seemed artificial, so I ended the conversation quickly.","zh":"他的笑容顯得很做作，所以我很快結束了談話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her artificial cheerfulness vanished as soon as the guests left.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artificial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70b1e8e06785cae45149","word":"artist","forms":["artist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9187b0551a04bf5","term":"artist","forms":["artist","artists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術創作者","explanation":"指創作藝術作品的人，例如繪畫、雕塑或其他藝術形式的創作者。這個詞的核心形象是把想法變成藝術作品的人。","examples":[{"en":"The artist is preparing a new exhibition for next month.","zh":"這位藝術家正在為下個月準備新的展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist carved birds from fallen branches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6543980896623d86","term":"artist","forms":["artist","artists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某方面的高手","explanation":"透過“藝術家”這個核心形象，詞義可以擴充套件為在某項活動中技藝高超、做事很有創造力的人，尤其常見於複合詞或比喻性表達。","examples":[{"en":"She is an artist at turning simple ingredients into elegant meals.","zh":"她很會把普通食材變成精緻的飯菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our goalkeeper is an artist at saving penalties.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5bd6cd5b42dc7f1fef2","word":"artistic","forms":["artistic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b72aa4b117f0a8bd","term":"artistic","forms":["artistic","more artistic","most artistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有藝術創造力的","explanation":"形容人或其作品顯示出創造性和藝術技巧，重點是“像藝術家一樣會創作、會表現”。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is very artistic and loves designing her own clothes.","zh":"瑪雅很有藝術天賦，喜歡自己設計衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His artistic talent was clear from an early age.","zh":"他從小就顯露出了藝術才能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13121f338fc4ef72","term":"artistic","forms":["artistic","more artistic","most artistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"藝術的；藝術家特有的","explanation":"表示某事物屬於藝術領域，或具有藝術家、藝術創作所特有的性質；這裡不一定是在評價它好不好看。","examples":[{"en":"The museum gives young artists a space for artistic expression.","zh":"這家博物館為年輕藝術家提供了進行藝術表達的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is known for her artistic vision.","zh":"她以自己的藝術視野而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4bf9f7fcbedaba0392f","word":"as","forms":["as"],"officialPos":"conj./adv./prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a76dadf54dcd5524","term":"as","forms":["as"],"pos":"adv","zh":"同樣程度地","explanation":"用於把兩個程度對齊，表示“和另一方一樣……”。它通常出現在比較結構中，幫助說明兩者在高度、快樂等方面達到相同程度。","examples":[{"en":"This bag is as light as my old one.","zh":"這個包和我的舊包一樣輕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My second attempt was as successful as my first.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/as","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a44a6d6c634b9b3f","term":"as","forms":["as"],"pos":"prep","zh":"和……相比；與……一樣","explanation":"放在比較物件前，說明前面的性質或程度是以誰或什麼為參照的。它和比較副詞用法連在一起時，構成英語最常見的同等比較框架。","examples":[{"en":"You are not as tall as my sister.","zh":"你沒有我姐姐高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This rope is twice as long as that one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/as","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54c2dd691c9ca0cb","term":"as","forms":["as"],"pos":"prep","zh":"作為","explanation":"把某人或某物放在一個身份、角色或觀察角度中，表示“以……身份”或“就……而言”。這裡的核心仍是把物件放進一個特定的關係框裡。","examples":[{"en":"What is your opinion as a parent?","zh":"你作為家長有什麼看法？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked as a translator during the negotiations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/as","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ea802eeb4485cf32398","word":"ascend","forms":["ascend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33ab1c7e71cd3996","term":"ascend","forms":["ascend","ascends","ascending","ascended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向上升起；飛昇","explanation":"指人、動物或物體向上移動，尤其是升到空中、飛昇或高高上升。這是“沿著路向上走”這一核心影象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The balloon slowly ascended into the clear morning sky.","zh":"氣球慢慢升入晴朗的晨空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers watched the eagle ascend above the valley.","zh":"徒步者看著鷹飛昇到山谷上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ascend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aedbcd4b232012f9","term":"ascend","forms":["ascend","ascends","ascending","ascended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"登上；走上","explanation":"表示沿樓梯、山路等向上走，或登上某個較高的位置。重點是把“向上移動”作用到一個具體的路線或地點上。","examples":[{"en":"We ascended the stone steps to the observation deck.","zh":"我們登上石階，來到了觀景臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ascended to the roof to check the antenna.","zh":"她上到屋頂去檢查天線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ascend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-972323a8d49a2bcf","term":"ascend","forms":["ascend","ascends","ascending","ascended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上升；提高到更高層次","explanation":"指地位、價值、境界或重要性變得更高，是把實際的“向上”擴充套件到抽象層面。它可以表示人變得更有地位，也可以表示事物達到更高、更理想的程度。","examples":[{"en":"Through years of work, she ascended to a position of great influence.","zh":"經過多年的努力，她升到了極具影響力的職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel ascends above a simple adventure story.","zh":"這部小說超越了普通冒險故事的層次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ascend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-037d390cd4ef796e5d75","word":"ash","forms":["ash"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab24b9c5bd1d535c","term":"ash","forms":["ash","ashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燃燒後的灰燼","explanation":"指木頭、紙張、香菸等燃燒後留下的細小固體殘留物，是這個詞最基本的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Only ash remained after the fire.","zh":"火災後只剩下灰燼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She brushed the ash from her coat.","zh":"她撣掉了外套上的灰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7033d94a97c35e8e","term":"ash","forms":["ash","ashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火化後的骨灰","explanation":"指人或動物火化後留下的遺骸，通常說 ashes，把它看成“人的灰燼”。","examples":[{"en":"Her ashes were placed in a small urn.","zh":"她的骨灰被放進了一個小骨灰盒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They scattered his ashes from the fishing boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6d9e56c88ad43624db4","word":"ashamed","forms":["ashamed"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5dc5715cb8b2397","term":"ashamed","forms":["ashamed","more ashamed","most ashamed"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到羞愧；慚愧","explanation":"指一個人因為自己的行為不對、表現不好，或覺得自己丟了臉而感到難為情、內疚。這個詞把重點放在“心裡覺得應該感到羞恥”上，而不只是外界看來難堪。","examples":[{"en":"She was ashamed of lying to her parents.","zh":"她為欺騙父母而感到羞愧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt ashamed when he realized he had blamed the wrong person.","zh":"他意識到自己怪錯了人，感到很慚愧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ashamed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d07bce046a93196a8b94","word":"aside","forms":["aside"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d89733b75675e9fe","term":"aside","forms":["aside"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向一邊；到一旁","explanation":"表示人或物向旁邊移開，從而不擋路或暫時離開主要位置。這是“向一邊”的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She stepped aside to let the children pass.","zh":"她走到一邊，讓孩子們過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please move aside so I can open the door.","zh":"請讓到一邊，我好開門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00ea07f227b400e5","term":"aside","forms":["aside"],"pos":"adv","zh":"暫且不考慮；撇開不談","explanation":"表示先把某個因素、情緒或話題放到一邊，不讓它影響眼前的判斷或討論；這是從“放到一邊”引申出來的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Joking aside, we need to find a solution today.","zh":"玩笑歸玩笑，我們今天得找到解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Putting the cost aside, this is a very good design.","zh":"先不考慮成本，這個設計非常好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f2fc7f2e9ce13b09b84","word":"ask","forms":["ask"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-862df6129662a2ce","term":"ask","forms":["ask","asks","asking","asked","aks","aksed","askest","askedst","akses","asketh","asken","-","aksing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人詢問","explanation":"表示向某人提出問題，以獲得資訊，例如詢問年齡、原因或情況。","examples":[{"en":"I asked Mia her age.","zh":"我問了米婭的年齡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He asked me about the meeting.","zh":"他問了我會議的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8976d903306361fd","term":"ask","forms":["ask","asks","asking","asked","aks","aksed","askest","askedst","akses","asketh","asken","-","aksing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"請求某物","explanation":"表示請求得到某物、幫助或機會，常常不說明向誰請求。","examples":[{"en":"I asked for a second helping.","zh":"我又請求添了一份飯菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He asked for a blanket and some water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78815ab763e4a46f","term":"ask","forms":["ask","asks","asking","asked","aks","aksed","askest","askedst","akses","asketh","asken","-","aksing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"請某人做某事","explanation":"表示請求或要求某人完成一個動作，把請求遞給某人並指向具體行為。","examples":[{"en":"Emma asked Jim to close the window.","zh":"艾瑪請吉姆關上窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I asked them not to wait for me.","zh":"我請他們不要等我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1986e60e41a78314","term":"ask","forms":["ask","asks","asking","asked","aks","aksed","askest","askedst","akses","asketh","asken","-","aksing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提出問題","explanation":"表示把一個問題正式或口頭提出來，等待別人回答。它強調動作本身，後面可直接接 question。","examples":[{"en":"The student asked an important question.","zh":"那名學生提出了一個重要問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ask the guide which trail reaches the waterfall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea51ae6e548ffbb851d2","word":"asleep","forms":["asleep"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0448c9e09a3c2ee0","term":"asleep","forms":["asleep"],"pos":"adj","zh":"睡著的","explanation":"指人正在睡眠中，或處於安靜休息、沒有清醒反應的狀態。這是 asleep 最基本的意思，核心畫面就是“人關機了”。","examples":[{"en":"I was asleep when you called.","zh":"你打電話時我已經睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby fell asleep on the train.","zh":"嬰兒在火車上睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asleep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fefedc6dc9dd06fe","term":"asleep","forms":["asleep"],"pos":"adj","zh":"麻木的","explanation":"指手、腿等身體部位暫時失去正常感覺，常伴有針刺般的麻癢感，好像身體的一小部分暫時“關機”了。","examples":[{"en":"My left foot fell asleep during the long meeting.","zh":"開了很久的會，我的左腳麻了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I stood up because my leg was asleep.","zh":"我的腿麻了，所以我站了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asleep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd8bf4f1e8c62eb16adf","word":"aspect","forms":["aspect"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aff23972e1109c5c","term":"aspect","forms":["aspect","aspects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方面；層面","explanation":"指一個整體中可以單獨拿出來討論的特徵或層面，也就是“這件事的一個方面”。它不一定是有形的部分，經濟、文化、風險等抽象內容都可以成為aspect。","examples":[{"en":"Cost is an important aspect of the project.","zh":"成本是這個專案的一個重要方面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report examines every aspect of the problem.","zh":"這份報告考察了這個問題的各個方面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c711bfb31102a4d","term":"aspect","forms":["aspect","aspects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外觀；視角下呈現的一面","explanation":"指從某個方向看一個事物時呈現出來的樣子或一面。這裡保留了“看”的原始意象：觀察者改變位置，看到的aspect也可能隨之改變。","examples":[{"en":"The building looks very different from this aspect.","zh":"從這個角度看，這座建築的樣子很不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The abandoned hotel had a strangely welcoming aspect.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8b4677937b26b7f","term":"aspect","forms":["aspect","aspects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方面；角度","explanation":"指從某個觀點或考察角度來看，事物所呈現出的一個側面。它和s1關係很近：s1強調整體中的層面，s3強調觀察和評價時採用的角度。","examples":[{"en":"In many aspects, the two plans are quite similar.","zh":"在許多方面，這兩個計劃相當相似。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We examined the financial aspect of opening another branch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfe0a8205d1917c9f109","word":"aspire","forms":["aspire"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8d95c9e775e9a9c","term":"aspire","forms":["aspire","aspires","aspiring","aspired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"立志；渴望實現","explanation":"指心裡懷有強烈而明確的抱負，並希望透過努力達到某個目標，常用於職業、成就或人生理想。它比一般的“想要”更強調志向和目標的高度。","examples":[{"en":"She aspires to become a doctor and help children in her community.","zh":"她立志成為一名醫生，幫助社群裡的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many young writers aspire to publish a novel.","zh":"許多年輕作家都渴望出版一部小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa260d27847dec909fc5","word":"aspirin","forms":["aspirin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b44accb45c6e639","term":"aspirin","forms":["aspirin","aspirins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"阿司匹林藥物","explanation":"指乙醯水楊酸這種藥物本身，核心作用是緩解疼痛和退燒。這裡關注的是藥物這一類東西，而不是某一片具體的藥。","examples":[{"en":"I took aspirin for my headache.","zh":"我吃了阿司匹林來緩解頭痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Aspirin can help reduce pain and fever.","zh":"阿司匹林可以幫助減輕疼痛和退燒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspirin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c16d091e07dd0803","term":"aspirin","forms":["aspirin","aspirins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一片阿司匹林","explanation":"指含有阿司匹林成分的一片藥；這裡把藥物看成一個可以逐片計數的具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"She took two aspirins after the long hike.","zh":"長途徒步後，她吃了兩片阿司匹林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She swallowed an aspirin with a little water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspirin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2062f80093066633876b","word":"ass","forms":["ass"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63c2b67cbf5fe471","term":"ass","forms":["ass","asses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驢","explanation":"一種像馬的馱運動物，尤其指家驢；這是這個詞最直接、最中性的本義。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer loaded the ass with sacks of grain.","zh":"農夫把幾袋糧食放在驢背上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An ass can carry heavy loads over rough ground.","zh":"驢能馱著重物走過崎嶇的地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b31c8fc135af8cd","term":"ass","forms":["ass","asses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蠢人；討厭的人","explanation":"借驢固執、遲鈍的形象，指一個愚蠢、粗魯、無體諒或令人討厭的人。","examples":[{"en":"Don't be an ass—she's already having a difficult day.","zh":"別這麼討厭——她今天已經夠難受了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was an ass for ignoring your message.","zh":"我沒理你的訊息，真是太不應該了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2fb71154eeb5d8dbd9d1","word":"assassinate","forms":["assassinate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d68531a3569b3f39","term":"assassinate","forms":["assassinate","assassinates","assassinating","assassinated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暗殺重要人物","explanation":"指為了政治、意識形態或其他目的，以突然、隱蔽的攻擊殺死重要人物。它不只是泛指殺人，而是突出目標的重要性和暗殺方式。","examples":[{"en":"The president was assassinated during a public ceremony.","zh":"總統在一次公開儀式上遭到暗殺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The group plotted to assassinate the military leader.","zh":"這個團體策劃暗殺那名軍事領導人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assassinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-451ffde6e1084197","term":"assassinate","forms":["assassinate","assassinates","assassinating","assassinated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徹底毀掉名譽或事業","explanation":"比喻用誹謗、惡意攻擊或背叛手段，徹底損害某人的名譽、形象或事業，就像在暗處一擊毀掉目標一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The article was written to assassinate the senator's reputation.","zh":"這篇文章是為了徹底毀掉那名參議員的名譽而寫的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Anonymous allegations were used to assassinate the researcher's character.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assassinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b074093a573c93f866d","word":"assault","forms":["assault"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6abb830af8bb2a7f","term":"assault","forms":["assault","assaults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體攻擊","explanation":"指用拳腳、武器等實際暴力手段發動的攻擊，重點是“猛地衝向並傷害對方”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The victim reported the assault to the police.","zh":"受害者向警方報告了這起襲擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers launched an assault on the town.","zh":"士兵們向那座城鎮發動了進攻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assault","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bd3a297ad7adf50","term":"assault","forms":["assault","assaults","assaulting","assaulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攻擊；抨擊","explanation":"指對人發動身體攻擊，也可比喻性地猛烈攻擊某個觀點或物件；核心畫面仍是“衝上去施加衝擊”。","examples":[{"en":"The man was arrested for assaulting a passenger on the train.","zh":"那名男子因在火車上襲擊一名乘客而被捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report assaults the basic assumptions of the plan.","zh":"這份報告猛烈抨擊了該計劃的基本假設。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assault","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63ebfab6ce4e84c4f846","word":"assemble","forms":["assemble"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb70d781740c4312","term":"assemble","forms":["assemble","assembles","assembling","assembled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組裝；拼裝","explanation":"把多個零件、部分或材料按照一定方式拼在一起，使它們成為一個完整的東西。重點不是單純把東西放在一起，而是形成一個可以使用的整體。","examples":[{"en":"We assembled the table in less than an hour.","zh":"我們不到一個小時就把這張桌子組裝好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children assembled the model plane from a kit.","zh":"孩子們用套件組裝出了這架模型飛機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assemble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0fb8726a3128225","term":"assemble","forms":["assemble","assembles","assembling","assembled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"集合；聚集","explanation":"人們從不同地方來到同一個地點，組成一個臨時的群體。這裡的“聚到一起”不一定表示被組織成固定機構，重點是當時聚集起來。","examples":[{"en":"The students assembled outside the main entrance.","zh":"學生們在大門外集合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A crowd assembled to watch the rescued seal return to sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assemble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e020bdf568793dee747a","word":"assembly","forms":["assembly"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e1652591ca97f4c","term":"assembly","forms":["assembly","assemblies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"元件；總成","explanation":"指由多個零件組合而成、能夠一起工作的整體，例如機器中的齒輪箱總成。它強調“組合完成後的東西”，而不是組裝動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic replaced the entire brake assembly.","zh":"修理工更換了整套剎車總成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This assembly contains several small gears.","zh":"這個元件裡包含幾個小齒輪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assembly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a76f224e8c21b789","term":"assembly","forms":["assembly","assemblies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組裝；裝配","explanation":"指把零件、片段或其他要素逐步組合起來的動作或過程，也就是把分散的部分集合成一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The furniture is easy to assemble, but the assembly takes time.","zh":"這套傢俱很容易組裝，但組裝過程需要時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please follow the assembly instructions carefully.","zh":"請仔細按照組裝說明操作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assembly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-645d1e37214afb50","term":"assembly","forms":["assembly","assemblies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"集會；集合","explanation":"指為了某個目的聚集在同一地點的一群人或這種聚集活動，例如學校的全校集會。這裡的“集合”物件從零件變成了人。","examples":[{"en":"The principal spoke at the morning assembly.","zh":"校長在早晨的全校集會上發了言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All students must attend the school assembly.","zh":"所有學生都必須參加學校集會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assembly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25450689bdd44d014020","word":"assert","forms":["assert"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ff27f70e4ff4831","term":"assert","forms":["assert","asserts","asserting","asserted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"明確斷言；肯定地說","explanation":"把一個判斷清楚、堅定地說出來，語氣比普通的“說”更強，強調說話人明確表示自己認為它是真的。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers assert that the treatment is safe.","zh":"研究人員明確聲稱這種治療是安全的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She asserted her innocence throughout the trial.","zh":"整個審判期間，她一直堅定地聲稱自己無罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8e09130d1a2b462","term":"assert","forms":["assert","asserts","asserting","asserted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堅持表達自己；爭取被重視","explanation":"主動說出自己的需要、意見或界限，並堅持讓別人認真對待自己；它把“明確表達”進一步用在個人處境中。","examples":[{"en":"She learned to assert herself during team meetings.","zh":"她學會了在團隊會議中堅持表達自己的意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can assert yourself without speaking harshly.","zh":"你可以堅持表達自己，而不必用刻薄的語氣說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9094a2c13d9d3dbea488","word":"assess(ment)","forms":["assess","assessment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45345ba8b9754981","term":"assess","forms":["assess","assesses","assessing","assessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"評估；判斷","explanation":"指經過觀察、分析或考慮後，對某件事的價值、狀況、風險或結果作出判斷。重點不是隨口猜測，而是有依據地衡量。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse assessed the patient's condition before calling the doctor.","zh":"護士在叫醫生之前評估了病人的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to assess the risks before making a decision.","zh":"我們需要在作決定前評估風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26d11d4da4c5519c","term":"assess","forms":["assess","assesses","assessing","assessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"評定處罰","explanation":"指裁判、監管機構或其他有權者根據違規行為正式確定處罰，尤其是罰款或比賽中的罰罰分等。這裡強調的是“定出應受的處罰”，不只是籠統地表示懲罰。","examples":[{"en":"The referee assessed a penalty against our team for wasting time.","zh":"裁判因我們隊拖延時間而判罰了我們隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge assessed a substantial fine for noncompliance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8980f375dba9c818","term":"assessment","forms":["assessment","assessments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"評價；評估結果","explanation":"指對某人、某物或某種情況作出的系統判斷，也可指這次判斷形成的結論或報告；它就是“稱一稱之後給出的評價”。","examples":[{"en":"The safety assessment identified several serious problems.","zh":"安全評估發現了幾個嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a careful assessment of the situation before deciding.","zh":"我們需要先仔細評估情況，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assessment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-094384f11f0e3eb5","term":"assessment","forms":["assessment","assessments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"評估行為；核定金額","explanation":"指進行估量、判斷的行為，或根據這種核定得出的稅、費、徵收款等金額；重點是“把數量或應繳額算出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The tax assessment arrived in the mail yesterday.","zh":"昨天郵寄來的稅費核定通知到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The assessment of the damage took three weeks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assessment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d59386e0ae435e292fbe","word":"asset","forms":["asset"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93afe8ba69c19310","term":"asset","forms":["asset","assets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資產；有價值的資源","explanation":"指有經濟價值、能產生收入或帶來其他實際收益的東西，例如股票、房產，也可以泛指某人或某組織擁有的有價值資源。","examples":[{"en":"The company sold some assets to pay its debts.","zh":"這家公司出售了一些資產來償還債務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her patience is a real asset in this job.","zh":"她的耐心是做好這份工作的一項真正優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2adf15469c523e45","term":"asset","forms":["asset","assets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可複用的有價值元件","explanation":"在技術、工程和科學語境中，指可以被利用、組合或重複使用的元件、模型、流程、框架或其他有價值物件；重點不在它是否值錢，而在它能否發揮作用。","examples":[{"en":"The design team stored its reusable assets in a shared library.","zh":"設計團隊把可複用的資源存放在共享庫中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer saved each illustration as a reusable asset.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9f88f4ef6533cb01b6f","word":"assign(ment)","forms":["assign","assignment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-868fa0c054a06909","term":"assign","forms":["assign","assigns","assigning","assigned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指定用途；劃定","explanation":"把某個時間、地點、資源或其他事物明確留給某種用途，相當於在它上面貼標籤並規定它要用於什麼。","examples":[{"en":"The manager assigned a room for the interview.","zh":"經理為面試指定了一間房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court assigned a date for the hearing.","zh":"法院為聽證會確定了日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-997ae630cac67348","term":"assign","forms":["assign","assigns","assigning","assigned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分配任務","explanation":"把一項任務、工作或責任交給某人完成；這裡的核心仍是把任務明確放到某人名下。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher assigned us a short essay.","zh":"老師給我們佈置了一篇短文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was assigned to check the invoices.","zh":"我被分配去核對發票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d794affc113fe9ac","term":"assignment","forms":["assignment","assignments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分派；分配","explanation":"指把某項工作、任務或責任分給某個人或某些人這一行為，重點在“分派出去”這個過程。","examples":[{"en":"The assignment of duties was completed before the meeting.","zh":"職責的分派在會議前已經完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The assignment of desks caused unexpected arguments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assignment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f25ec87010b18a54","term":"assignment","forms":["assignment","assignments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分派的任務","explanation":"指某人被交代去完成的一項任務，是assignment在工作和一般生活中最直接的含義之一。","examples":[{"en":"She finished the assignment before dinner.","zh":"她在晚飯前完成了那項任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My new assignment requires me to travel every week.","zh":"我的新任務要求我每週出差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assignment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10d6accd713eaab1","term":"assignment","forms":["assignment","assignments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作業；課程任務","explanation":"指老師佈置給學生的作業或課程任務，可以是書面作業、報告或需要完成的專案。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gave us a difficult assignment due next Friday.","zh":"老師給我們佈置了一項困難的作業，下週五要交。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I spent the weekend working on my history assignment.","zh":"我整個週末都在做歷史作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assignment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b0363b65576ead3e362","word":"assist","forms":["assist"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7e742d865bdfdc9","term":"assist","forms":["assist","assists","assisting","assisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"幫助；協助","explanation":"表示站在某人身邊提供實際幫助，使對方更容易完成任務或解決問題；這是 assist 最基本、最常見的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"This guide will assist you in planning your first trip abroad.","zh":"這份指南將幫助你規劃第一次出國旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A nurse assisted the doctor during the procedure.","zh":"一名護士在操作過程中協助醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfa1102f63afcdbcd5fd","word":"assistance","forms":["assistance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-871f88b3ee0af72d","term":"assistance","forms":["assistance","assistances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫助；援助","explanation":"指為解決某人的困難而提供的幫助，也可以指提供這種幫助的行動或結果；重點是“在旁邊扶持一把”這一概念。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers offered assistance to the flood victims.","zh":"志願者向洪災受害者提供了幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please ask for assistance if you cannot use the machine.","zh":"如果你不會使用這臺機器，請尋求幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assistance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a39a7ffad4a3013f29da","word":"assistant","forms":["assistant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b2c8a13b16c4ba7","term":"assistant","forms":["assistant","assistants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"助手；助理","explanation":"指實際幫助某人完成工作、處理事務或提供支援的人，是這個詞最核心的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"My assistant will send you the documents this afternoon.","zh":"我的助理今天下午會把檔案發給你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works as an assistant to the director.","zh":"她擔任那位主管的助理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assistant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-178b6e061a04a75e46b8","word":"associate","forms":["associate"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eaf28157ae84b9d1","term":"associate","forms":["associate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"副職的；助理級的","explanation":"表示某人已經加入某個職位或工作關係，但級別低於正式的高階職位，像是“連線上上、但還不是最高層”。","examples":[{"en":"She was promoted from assistant editor to associate editor last year.","zh":"她去年從助理編輯晉升為副編輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An associate professor will lead the seminar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/associate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ec161d184992826","term":"associate","forms":["associate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"準成員的；享有部分資格的","explanation":"表示某人已經和一個俱樂部、機構或團體連在一起，但只享有部分成員資格或權利。","examples":[{"en":"As an associate member, she can attend meetings but cannot vote.","zh":"作為準成員，她可以參加會議，但不能投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The society offers associate membership to researchers based overseas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/associate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0bb905084eb26ae","term":"associate","forms":["associate","associates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合作者；商業夥伴","explanation":"指和某人一起做專案、經營事務或承擔工作的夥伴，核心仍是“連在同一件事上”。","examples":[{"en":"I met one of her business associates at the conference.","zh":"我在會議上見到了她的一位商業夥伴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His business associate manages their overseas accounts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/associate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-612e3d70b4c4234e","term":"associate","forms":["associate","associates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同事；共事者","explanation":"指和自己在同一單位或工作領域有聯絡、一起工作的人，重點是工作上的連線。","examples":[{"en":"Several former associates still ask her for advice.","zh":"幾位以前的同事現在仍然向她徵求意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her business associate handles the overseas accounts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/associate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3720aac97fc68ee1","term":"associate","forms":["associate","associates","associating","associated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使結為夥伴；使結盟","explanation":"表示把自己或別人加入某個夥伴、事業或觀點的一邊，主動建立合作、支援或友好聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"She associated herself with the campaign for cleaner public transport.","zh":"她表示支援改善公共交通、使其更清潔的活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treaty associated the smaller states with the federation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/associate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ec5366e1313064a","term":"associate","forms":["associate","associates","associating","associated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連線；結合","explanation":"表示把兩個或多個事物實際連在一起、混合在一起或看作一個組合，體現最基本的“連線”概念。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers found gold associated with other minerals.","zh":"研究人員發現黃金與其他礦物結合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experiment associates each button with a different sound.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/associate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f12683b685315a8f","term":"associate","forms":["associate","associates","associating","associated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聯想到；聯絡起來","explanation":"表示因為記憶、經驗或證據，在頭腦中把一個人或事物和另一個概念聯絡起來；這條線不一定真實存在，而是心理上的連線。","examples":[{"en":"I always associate that song with long summer evenings.","zh":"我總是把那首歌和漫長的夏夜聯絡在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I associate that perfume with my grandmother.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/associate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b514913789f890c4af8","word":"association","forms":["association"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3db573addba41fb","term":"association","forms":["association","associations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯絡、聯結這一行為","explanation":"指把人、事物或想法聯絡、聯結起來的行為本身，重點在“建立聯絡”這一過程，而不是聯絡之後形成的具體關係。","examples":[{"en":"The association of certain colors with emotions varies from culture to culture.","zh":"不同文化把某些顏色與情感聯絡起來的方式各不相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The association of sounds with letters develops through practice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/association","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d80cb7ccb8baf50","term":"association","forms":["association","associations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯絡、關聯；聯想","explanation":"指聯絡形成後的狀態，或一個事物引起的記憶、聯想；一件物品可能讓人聯想到某段經歷，這種聯想就是 association。","examples":[{"en":"The old house has strong associations with my childhood.","zh":"這座老房子讓我強烈聯想到童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For many people, the smell of bread has pleasant associations.","zh":"對許多人來說，麵包的香味會帶來愉快的聯想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/association","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9254e4cefe26962f","term":"association","forms":["association","associations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"協會；組織","explanation":"指一群為了共同目標而組織起來的人，也就是協會、團體或社團；這裡的“聯絡”從人與人之間的關係擴大成了一個正式組織。","examples":[{"en":"She joined a local association for independent artists.","zh":"她加入了一個面向獨立藝術家的地方協會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The neighborhood association organizes monthly cleanups.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/association","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82e05dae00a818a38267","word":"assume","forms":["assume"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d49b08604356cbd","term":"assume","forms":["assume","assumes","assuming","assumed","assumest","assumedst","assumeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"假定；認為","explanation":"把尚未證實的事情先當作真的來推斷或討論，常常是為了繼續作決定或分析。","examples":[{"en":"I assumed that the meeting had been canceled.","zh":"我以為會議已經取消了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We cannot assume that everyone has received the message.","zh":"我們不能假定每個人都收到了訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1862a2e7b6d33ca","term":"assume","forms":["assume","assumes","assuming","assumed","assumest","assumedst","assumeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承擔；擔任","explanation":"把職位、職責或某種身份接到自己身上，開始負責相應的工作或行動。","examples":[{"en":"She will assume responsibility for the project next month.","zh":"她下個月將負責這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He assumed the role of team leader after the manager left.","zh":"經理離開後，他擔任了團隊負責人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c081dd376ba93a530dd0","word":"assumption","forms":["assumption"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ba5d6cf9a8428fd","term":"assumption","forms":["assumption","assumptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承擔；接手","explanation":"指主動把責任、職務或任務接到自己身上，也就是“接手並負責”。這裡的核心不是猜測，而是接受某項責任或角色。","examples":[{"en":"Her assumption of leadership brought the team together.","zh":"她接任領導職務後，團隊團結了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The assumption of these duties will require extra training.","zh":"承擔這些職責需要額外培訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assumption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d4f02081830d7f5","term":"assumption","forms":["assumption","assumptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未經證明的假定","explanation":"指沒有充分證據，卻先把某種說法當作事實來接受；這種假定可能是錯誤的，甚至是不合理的。","examples":[{"en":"We made the assumption that everyone had received the email.","zh":"我們假定每個人都收到了那封電子郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His assumption that I was angry was completely wrong.","zh":"他以為我生氣了，這完全錯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assumption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b2d53abee432c914a12","word":"assurance","forms":["assurance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ecdcf9c77284cd0","term":"assurance","forms":["assurance","assurances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保證；讓人放心的話","explanation":"指為了讓別人完全放心而作出的保證、承諾或說明，也可以指這種保證本身。它像是遞給對方一張“放心憑據”，使對方不再擔心。","examples":[{"en":"The manager gave us assurance that the problem would be fixed soon.","zh":"經理向我們保證，問題很快就會解決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm reply gave me assurance that everything was under control.","zh":"她鎮定的回答讓我相信一切都在掌控之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assurance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da63c7863ed7d363","term":"assurance","forms":["assurance","assurances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"確信；把握","explanation":"指心裡沒有疑問、對某事完全相信的狀態；它是“保證”進入自己內心後的把握。這個把握可以來自證據、信念或他人的保證。","examples":[{"en":"She spoke with assurance that the plan would succeed.","zh":"她很有把握地說這個計劃會成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We left the meeting with assurance that our concerns had been heard.","zh":"我們離開會議時確信自己的擔憂已經得到重視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assurance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5c46c67f87b1339","term":"assurance","forms":["assurance","assurances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自信；鎮定","explanation":"指面對事情時心態堅定、舉止鎮定而不猶疑的自信。它和“確信”相連，但更突出這種把握在行動和氣勢上的表現。","examples":[{"en":"Despite the difficult questions, she answered with assurance.","zh":"儘管問題很難，她還是自信而鎮定地作了回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She answered the hostile questions with quiet assurance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assurance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63be8044d77188f24a00","word":"assure","forms":["assure"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-762d8e3d295cfccd","term":"assure","forms":["assure","assures","assuring","assured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確保；使確定","explanation":"把某件事穩穩托住，使它能夠按預期發生或保持可靠。這裡的重點是結果本身被確保，而不是某個人聽到了保證。","examples":[{"en":"A written schedule assures that everyone knows what to do.","zh":"一份書面日程確保每個人都知道該做什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular maintenance assures reliable operation throughout the winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88f9b94d0f007d97","term":"assure","forms":["assure","assures","assuring","assured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人保證","explanation":"把可靠的資訊或承諾遞給某人，使對方相信某件事是真的、會順利進行。這是 assure 最容易遇到的核心用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"I assure you that the package will arrive tomorrow.","zh":"我向你保證，包裹明天會到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician assured us that the repair was safe.","zh":"技術員向我們保證，這次維修是安全的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-695b2ea90ecaa863bc5e","word":"asthma","forms":["asthma"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70891478e1adfe06","term":"asthma","forms":["asthma","asthmas","asthmata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"哮喘","explanation":"一種會使氣道反覆變窄的長期疾病；氣道收緊時，患者可能喘鳴、氣短、胸悶或咳嗽，過敏原、冷空氣、運動和情緒壓力都可能誘發症狀。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter has asthma, so she carries an inhaler.","zh":"我女兒患有哮喘，所以隨身帶著吸入器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cold air can make his asthma worse.","zh":"冷空氣會使他的哮喘加重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asthma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23d1dfa5f92d54f4d1b3","word":"astonish(ment)","forms":["astonishment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21b7ac9d31dc1748","term":"astonishment","forms":["astonishment","astonishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈的驚訝","explanation":"指人因事情完全出乎意料而產生的強烈驚訝，彷彿驚得暫時停住了。這個詞比一般的驚訝更強，常帶有震驚或錯愕的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"She stared at the empty box in astonishment.","zh":"她驚愕地盯著空盒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"To everyone's astonishment, the small team won the final.","zh":"令所有人驚訝的是，那支小隊贏得了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astonishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a69fb45beffa06c7","term":"astonishment","forms":["astonishment","astonishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人驚訝的事物","explanation":"指某件非常出乎意料、足以讓人驚訝的事情或結果。這裡的 astonishment 不是情緒本身，而是引起這種情緒的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden announcement was an astonishment to everyone.","zh":"這個突然的公告讓所有人都感到驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That tiny house was an astonishment of clever design.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astonishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87d1c61845d3ad264827","word":"astray","forms":["astray"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecb926dfadf3501c","term":"astray","forms":["astray"],"pos":"adv","zh":"偏離方向；迷路","explanation":"指人或事物沒有沿著正確、預定的方向前進，因而迷路、走失，或被帶離原來的路線；也可以進一步表示行動或思想誤入歧途。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers went astray in the thick fog.","zh":"徒步旅行者在濃霧中迷了路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bad influence led him astray.","zh":"不良影響使他誤入了歧途。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df0c29d39619e8cf2d4b","word":"astronaut","forms":["astronaut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8cc1a7e037a6455c","term":"astronaut","forms":["astronaut","astronauts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宇航員","explanation":"經過專門訓練、作為宇宙飛船或其他航天器成員進入地球大氣層以外執行任務的人。這個意思保留了“駕駛星星之船的水手”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The astronaut spent six months aboard the space station.","zh":"這名宇航員在空間站上待了六個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to become an astronaut one day.","zh":"她希望有一天能成為宇航員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astronaut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6b23b0f2cf0f9912912","word":"astronomer","forms":["astronomer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e16cdebaa7f3e2a","term":"astronomer","forms":["astronomer","astronomers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天文學家","explanation":"研究恆星、行星、星系以及宇宙規律的科學家；這個詞強調以科學研究為職業或專業，而不只是喜歡看星星的人。","examples":[{"en":"The astronomer studies how stars are born and die.","zh":"這位天文學家研究恆星如何誕生和消亡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to become an astronomer one day.","zh":"她希望有一天成為一名天文學家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astronomer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-603354159847d671cd7c","word":"astronomy","forms":["astronomy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d6e827951f2a916","term":"astronomy","forms":["astronomy","astronomies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天文學","explanation":"指研究地球大氣層以外宇宙的科學，包括測定天體和其他宇宙物質的位置、性質，以及研究宇宙中的輻射等。它就是把“抬頭看星空”發展成系統科學的學科。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to study astronomy after seeing Saturn through a telescope.","zh":"她用望遠鏡看到土星後，決定學習天文學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Modern astronomy can detect planets orbiting distant stars.","zh":"現代天文學能夠探測到圍繞遙遠恆星執行的行星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astronomy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1d6b91b67c2afa5e322","word":"at","forms":["at"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fbbc523ffea41eb6","term":"at","forms":["at"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在某處；靠近某地","explanation":"表示人在某個地點或地點附近，把地點看成一個可以靠近的點；重點常是所在位置，而不是進入建築物內部。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll meet you at the station after work.","zh":"我下班後在車站和你見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is waiting at the front door.","zh":"她正在前門等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/at","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdfd1bae83e773cf","term":"at","forms":["at"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在活動或事件中","explanation":"表示人在某項會議、聚會、比賽等活動現場或參與其中，把活動看成一個可以靠近的事件點。","examples":[{"en":"Were you at the school meeting yesterday?","zh":"你昨天參加學校會議了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I met several old friends at the festival.","zh":"我在節日活動上遇到了幾位老朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/at","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9407a42b0aabb52","term":"at","forms":["at"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在某時；在某個時間點","explanation":"表示事情發生在一個明確的時間點，或在說話者看來較短的時間段內，如鐘點、黎明、夜間或某個年齡。","examples":[{"en":"The last train leaves at eleven tonight.","zh":"末班火車今晚十一點開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I woke up at dawn and went for a walk.","zh":"我在黎明時醒來，出去散了會兒步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/at","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23a1f74bc589fe525387","word":"athlete","forms":["athlete"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-894971aa29c08b06","term":"athlete","forms":["athlete","athletes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參加競技體育專案的人","explanation":"指參加田徑、道路跑、越野跑、競走等一組競技體育專案的人，通常強調訓練和比賽身份。這是“為了比賽而訓練的人”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She became a professional athlete after winning the national race.","zh":"她贏得全國賽後成為了一名職業運動員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young athlete trains before school every morning.","zh":"這名年輕運動員每天早晨上學前訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/athlete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65026b5c6c451f30","term":"athlete","forms":["athlete","athletes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"積極參加體育運動的人","explanation":"泛指積極參加體育運動、特別是有較好運動技能的人，不限於田徑專案，也不一定是職業選手。它把核心形象從某一類參賽者擴充套件到了各種運動專案的運動員。","examples":[{"en":"She's the best athlete on our college basketball team.","zh":"她是我們大學籃球隊裡綜合運動能力最強的隊員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lifelong athlete, she still swims before breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/athlete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0abb7566fe831745fce","word":"athletic","forms":["athletic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5f5aa98a8ec27bb","term":"athletic","forms":["athletic","more athletic","most athletic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與運動員或體育有關","explanation":"表示某事物屬於運動員、體育組織或競技活動的範圍，重點是“和體育有關”，不一定表示某個人本人正在運動。","examples":[{"en":"She received an athletic scholarship from the university.","zh":"她獲得了這所大學的體育獎學金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school is building a new athletic center.","zh":"這所學校正在建一座新的體育中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/athletic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22d59da28bce5a77","term":"athletic","forms":["athletic","more athletic","most athletic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愛運動的；運動能力強的","explanation":"形容一個人經常進行身體活動，或很擅長運動；重點在運動能力和活躍程度，而不是職業身份。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is very athletic and plays three sports.","zh":"我姐姐很有運動能力，還參加三種運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has always been athletic and energetic.","zh":"他一直都很愛運動，也很有活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/athletic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59ab849db966d7b1de9c","word":"athletics","forms":["athletics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a2abc3441a30797","term":"athletics","forms":["athletics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"田徑運動","explanation":"指由短跑、長跑、跳躍、投擲等專案組成的田徑運動；可以把它記成運動員在賽道和場地上用速度、力量與技巧競爭。","examples":[{"en":"She has competed in athletics since she was twelve.","zh":"她從十二歲起就參加田徑比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school is building a new athletics track.","zh":"這所學校正在修建一條新的田徑跑道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/athletics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c62fbdbd7fe6fd08","term":"athletics","forms":["athletics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育活動","explanation":"在美國英語中可泛指體育運動或學校、大學的體育專案，不限於田徑；核心仍是透過訓練和比賽展現體能與技巧。","examples":[{"en":"Many students receive scholarships for college athletics.","zh":"許多學生因參加大學體育專案而獲得獎學金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"School athletics helped him discover a love of running.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/athletics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfd5a8ed7357ec4de959","word":"atmosphere","forms":["atmosphere"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3079029f37b97444","term":"atmosphere","forms":["atmosphere","atmospheres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大氣層","explanation":"指包圍地球或其他天體的氣體層；這是“包圍某物的環境”這一核心概念的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The spacecraft re-entered the Earth's atmosphere at high speed.","zh":"這艘航天器高速重新進入地球大氣層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are studying the atmosphere of Mars.","zh":"科學家正在研究火星的大氣層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atmosphere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe092d0cf1f36f82","term":"atmosphere","forms":["atmosphere","atmospheres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"營造出的氛圍","explanation":"指音樂、燈光、佈置等環境條件共同營造出的氛圍；這些可見或可聽的因素像一層環境包圍著人，並影響人的感受。","examples":[{"en":"Soft lighting and quiet music created a calm atmosphere in the restaurant.","zh":"柔和的燈光和安靜的音樂為餐廳營造了平靜的氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The candles changed the atmosphere of the room.","zh":"蠟燭改變了房間的氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atmosphere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-1bf521836de96e75fac7","word":"atom","forms":["atom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a90e25ad4ae39231","term":"atom","forms":["atom","atoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原子","explanation":"atom 是仍然保留某種化學元素性質的最小物質單位；它並非完全沒有結構，而是由原子核和周圍的電子組成。","examples":[{"en":"A single oxygen atom can combine with two hydrogen atoms to form water.","zh":"一個氧原子可以和兩個氫原子結合形成水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sample contains atoms of iron and carbon.","zh":"這個樣本含有鐵原子和碳原子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56f77ab88c6bda08","term":"atom","forms":["atom","atoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一點點；絲毫","explanation":"由“最小顆粒”引申，atom 可表示極少的一點，常用於強調某物幾乎不存在。","examples":[{"en":"There isn't an atom of truth in that story.","zh":"那個故事裡一點真實成分都沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She didn't show an atom of fear.","zh":"她絲毫沒有表現出害怕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd43322a4da6f0e914c9","word":"atomic","forms":["atomic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc334f0381ea7bea","term":"atomic","forms":["atomic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"原子的；由原子構成的","explanation":"指直接涉及原子、由原子組成，或以單個原子為單位的事物。這是 atomic 最基礎的含義，核心畫面就是“原子本身”。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists observed a stream of atomic hydrogen.","zh":"科學家觀察到一股原子氫流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The model illustrates atomic structure using colored spheres.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atomic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eea6e1b0feb2e329","term":"atomic","forms":["atomic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"核能的；核反應的","explanation":"指利用原子核釋放的能量，或涉及核反應過程的事物。它從“原子”進一步聚焦到原子核，因此常與能源、武器和核技術有關。","examples":[{"en":"The country is investing in atomic energy.","zh":"這個國家正在投資核能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The submarine is powered by an atomic reactor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atomic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f744fee730b88a8d44ed","word":"attach(ment)","forms":["attach","attachment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98f8f33dec2484e6","term":"attach","forms":["attach","attaches","attaching","attached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……固定到……上","explanation":"把一個物體牢牢連線到另一個物體上，就是用“鉤子”把它掛住或固定住；也可以用於較抽象的連線。","examples":[{"en":"Please attach the label to the outside of the package.","zh":"請把標籤貼在包裹外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Attach the safety line to your harness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2b6210271c01cef","term":"attach","forms":["attach","attaches","attaching","attached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隨電子郵件附上","explanation":"把檔案“掛”在電子郵件後面傳送，也就是把檔案作為附件一同發出；這裡不表示把檔案固定到實體物品上。","examples":[{"en":"I’ve attached the signed form to this email.","zh":"我已將簽好字的表格附在這封電子郵件中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Attach your portfolio when you email the studio.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9756b42d40d5a6ae","term":"attachment","forms":["attachment","attachments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連線；附著","explanation":"指把一個東西連線到另一個東西上的動作或過程，也可用於較抽象的連線。它是“掛上去”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The attachment of the sensor to the wall took only a few minutes.","zh":"把感測器安裝到牆上只花了幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the attachment of the safety rope before climbing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attachment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-243c5302ef6a7e00","term":"attachment","forms":["attachment","attachments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"依戀；感情聯絡","explanation":"指對某人或某物產生的強烈感情聯絡，好像在心裡把自己“連”在對方身上。它可以是親密感，也可以是捨不得離開的感情。","examples":[{"en":"She has a strong attachment to her childhood home.","zh":"她對自己童年住過的房子有很深的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His attachment to the battered violin puzzled its prospective buyer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attachment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db3ece7f53d098ff","term":"attachment","forms":["attachment","attachments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子郵件附件","explanation":"指隨電子郵件或其他訊息一起傳送的檔案，好像把檔案“掛”在訊息上。這是現代英語中非常常見的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"I forgot to include the attachment in my email.","zh":"我忘了把附件放進郵件裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I could not open the attachment on my phone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attachment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fca30679635be3bbce1c","word":"attack","forms":["attack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cadd0c48dfdff860","term":"attack","forms":["attack","attacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攻擊；襲擊","explanation":"指為了傷害、擊敗甚至殺死對手而主動採取的行動，既可以是人或動物的襲擊，也可以是軍事攻擊。","examples":[{"en":"The village was evacuated after a series of attacks.","zh":"一連串襲擊發生後，村民被疏散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog made an attack on the cyclist.","zh":"那條狗襲擊了騎腳踏車的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d720a1f6800ab3ee","term":"attack","forms":["attack","attacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抨擊；攻擊性批評","explanation":"指用言語、文章或其他方式貶低某個人、觀點或事物的價值和可信度，不一定包含身體暴力。","examples":[{"en":"The article was a sharp attack on the government's policy.","zh":"這篇文章尖銳地抨擊了政府的政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her article launched a fierce attack on the housing policy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e995709aa5e2ef2","term":"attack","forms":["attack","attacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疾病突然發作","explanation":"指疾病或身體狀況突然出現並開始影響人，強調“突然衝來”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"He had an attack of asthma during the night.","zh":"他夜裡哮喘發作了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A panic attack left her unable to speak.","zh":"一次驚恐發作讓她說不出話來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52614537d3697a77","term":"attack","forms":["attack","attacks","attacking","attacked","attackt","attackted","attackest","attackedst","attacketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攻擊；襲擊","explanation":"指用暴力或其他強力主動傷害某人或某物，是名詞“攻擊”的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The snake will attack only when it feels threatened.","zh":"這條蛇只有感到受到威脅時才會攻擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several soldiers were attacked on their way home.","zh":"幾名士兵在回家的路上遭到了襲擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c22cebade490edb0","term":"attack","forms":["attack","attacks","attacking","attacked","attackt","attackted","attackest","attackedst","attacketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抨擊；嚴厲批評","explanation":"指用語言、文章或公開言論猛烈挑戰某人、觀點或政策的價值和可信度。","examples":[{"en":"The senator attacked the proposal during the debate.","zh":"這名參議員在辯論中抨擊了這項提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editorial attacked the mayor's handling of the flood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c7bae9ffef71206a3d6","word":"attain(ment)","forms":["attain","attainment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8387ebc6479427a","term":"attain","forms":["attain","attains","attaining","attained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲得目標或結果","explanation":"經過努力、學習或持續行動，最終獲得想要的目標或結果；重點是“夠到並取得”目標。","examples":[{"en":"She worked for years to attain her goal of becoming a doctor.","zh":"她努力了多年，終於實現了當醫生的目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With patience, the team attained the result it had hoped for.","zh":"憑著耐心，這個團隊取得了它一直期待的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64475b808d1fa259","term":"attain","forms":["attain","attains","attaining","attained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"達到或到達","explanation":"沿著某種進展或移動，最終到達一個地點、時間、階段或狀態；這裡的“達到”不一定是獲得一個東西。","examples":[{"en":"The spacecraft attained orbit after several difficult maneuvers.","zh":"飛船經過幾次艱難的操作後進入了軌道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By winter, the tree had attained a height of three meters.","zh":"到了冬天，這棵樹已經長到了三米高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c5abe54d247287e","term":"attainment","forms":["attainment","attainments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"達到；取得的過程","explanation":"指經過努力而達到某個目標、水平或狀態這一過程，重點在“夠到目標”這件事本身，而不是目標之後的具體成果。","examples":[{"en":"The attainment of fluency in a new language takes time and patience.","zh":"達到一門新語言的流利程度需要時間和耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her attainment of the required standard allowed her to enter the program.","zh":"她達到了規定的標準，因此可以進入該專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attainment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0da3ab64b6ae8505","term":"attainment","forms":["attainment","attainments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成就；取得的成果","explanation":"指努力之後已經獲得的成就、資格、能力或其他成果，也就是“夠到手裡的東西”。它既可以指一項具體成就，也可以泛指一個人的成就總和。","examples":[{"en":"Her academic attainments earned her a place at a leading university.","zh":"她的學術成就使她獲得了進入一流大學的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Graduation celebrated the students' academic attainments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attainment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7ce66d0fb14e3c2d4d9","word":"attempt","forms":["attempt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f8327d7f8b7b79c","term":"attempt","forms":["attempt","attempts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘗試；努力","explanation":"指為了完成某事而採取的一次行動或作出的努力，重點是“試著做”，不保證成功。","examples":[{"en":"We made an attempt to repair the old bicycle.","zh":"我們試著修理那輛舊腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their first attempt to cross the desert failed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attempt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68b4c4e348f149c9","term":"attempt","forms":["attempt","attempts","attempting","attempted","attemptest","attemptedst","attempteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"試圖；嘗試","explanation":"指著手去做某事，強調行動和努力，而不是結果；可以用於成功或失敗的嘗試。","examples":[{"en":"The climbers attempted to reach the summit before sunset.","zh":"登山者試圖在日落前到達山頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He attempted a difficult puzzle but gave up after an hour.","zh":"他嘗試解一道很難的謎題，但一小時後放棄了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attempt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-192f9a06d1dd2d246239","word":"attend","forms":["attend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14a2cbf18aae0b6c","term":"attend","forms":["attend","attends","attending","attended","attendest","attendedst","attendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處理、照料某事","explanation":"指把注意力和精力用於某項事務，負責處理它或照料它，常常暗含及時解決問題的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please attend to these emails before the meeting.","zh":"請在會議前處理好這些電子郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The staff will attend to your request shortly.","zh":"工作人員很快會處理你的請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bac978f7f65ac28b","term":"attend","forms":["attend","attends","attending","attended","attendest","attendedst","attendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"留心、注意","explanation":"指認真聽、看或考慮某人說的話或某件事，把注意力明確集中到物件上。現代英語中這個意思主要保留在“attend to”結構裡。","examples":[{"en":"The committee must attend to the safety concerns raised by residents.","zh":"委員會必須認真處理居民提出的安全問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Attend to what she is saying before you answer.","zh":"回答前先認真聽她在說什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a3bcbcef5b4e4d069cf","word":"attendance","forms":["attendance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4b047c62a034ede","term":"attendance","forms":["attendance","attendances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出席；到場","explanation":"指參加某個會議、課程、活動等並在現場；重點是“到場”這一行為或狀態，而不是到場的人數。","examples":[{"en":"Attendance at the meeting is required.","zh":"出席這次會議是必須的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her attendance at the training was confirmed yesterday.","zh":"昨天確認了她會參加培訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attendance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ee5c7f237f0ebe7","term":"attendance","forms":["attendance","attendances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出席者；出席人數","explanation":"指已經到場的那些人，或這些人的總數；例如老師點名時，記錄的就是誰在場以及一共有多少人。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher took attendance before starting the lesson.","zh":"老師在開始上課前點了名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Attendance reached four hundred despite the storm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attendance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c5e0e76beb309633527","word":"attendant","forms":["attendant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3c90d5587f3a2ae","term":"attendant","forms":["attendant","attendants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服務人員；照料者","explanation":"指在某個地方工作、為他人提供幫助，或看守、照料某人某物的人。核心畫面仍是“在旁邊隨時提供服務”。","examples":[{"en":"The parking attendant took my keys and parked the car.","zh":"停車場工作人員接過我的鑰匙，把車停好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The attendant helped the passenger into her wheelchair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attendant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0787d272a439bb74b76","word":"attention","forms":["attention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4ed42ac61e54822","term":"attention","forms":["attention","attentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"注意力","explanation":"指人的心思集中在某個物件、任務或資訊上，也就是“認真留意”的能力或狀態。這是attention最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please pay attention to the safety instructions.","zh":"請注意安全說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bright picture immediately caught my attention.","zh":"那幅鮮豔的圖片立刻吸引了我的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87bb1701ee74015d2546","word":"attic","forms":["attic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c02c062f07a90d33","term":"attic","forms":["attic","attics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"閣樓；頂樓空間","explanation":"指房屋屋頂正下方的空間，通常在最上層，常用來存放物品，也可能被改造成居住空間。可以把它想成房子最上方、貼著屋頂的房間。","examples":[{"en":"We went up to the attic to look for the old photo albums.","zh":"我們上閣樓去找那些舊相簿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They turned the attic into a quiet bedroom.","zh":"他們把閣樓改成了一間安靜的臥室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b67cab457e406488e88a","word":"attitude","forms":["attitude"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90ee37c6c89be816","term":"attitude","forms":["attitude","attitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體姿態","explanation":"指身體站立、行走或擺放時呈現出來的姿態和儀態，重點是外在的身體狀態。它是“態度”這個核心概念最直觀的起點：先看一個人身體怎麼擺。","examples":[{"en":"The dancer crossed the stage with a relaxed attitude.","zh":"那名舞者以放鬆的姿態走過舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sat with an upright attitude during the interview.","zh":"面試時，她一直保持挺直的坐姿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ca6c7aa1f3e1f07","term":"attitude","forms":["attitude","attitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理態度","explanation":"指一個人對人、事或情況所持的心理傾向和表現出來的待人方式，例如積極、消極、尊重或敵意的態度。身體姿態讓人看見外在狀態，這個義項則把“姿態”擴充套件到了內心和行為。","examples":[{"en":"Her attitude toward new ideas is open and curious.","zh":"她對新想法持開放而好奇的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A positive attitude can make difficult work easier.","zh":"積極的態度能讓困難的工作變得容易一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5561ba03cac2c86f883d","word":"attorney","forms":["attorney"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b12fcd0f8cc202cd","term":"attorney","forms":["attorney","attorneys","attornies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"律師","explanation":"指以法律事務為職業、為客戶提供法律建議或在法律程式中代表客戶的人，這是現代英語中最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She hired an attorney after receiving the court notice.","zh":"她收到法院通知後聘請了一名律師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His attorney advised him not to sign the contract.","zh":"他的律師建議他不要簽署這份合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attorney","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a3dd784b14b179f","term":"attorney","forms":["attorney","attorneys","attornies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受權代表","explanation":"指得到他人正式授權、可以按照對方指示代為處理事務的人；這個意義比“律師”更寬，代表者本身不一定從事法律工作。","examples":[{"en":"She appointed her brother as her attorney to manage the sale of the house.","zh":"她指定弟弟為自己的受權代表，負責處理房屋出售事宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her attorney may sign documents during her absence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attorney","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bec0a29bc921c822367","word":"attract","forms":["attract"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-346cea25a5759024","term":"attract","forms":["attract","attracts","attracting","attracted","attractest","attractedst","attracteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"物理吸引","explanation":"指物體在沒有接觸的情況下把另一個物體拉向自己，最典型的情景是磁鐵吸引鐵屑。","examples":[{"en":"A magnet attracts iron filings.","zh":"磁鐵能吸引鐵屑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charged balloon attracted small pieces of paper.","zh":"帶電的氣球吸引了小紙片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e2a3608dd9d14d1","term":"attract","forms":["attract","attracts","attracting","attracted","attractest","attractedst","attracteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸引人或注意力","explanation":"指憑藉外表、魅力、價值或興趣把人、注意力或感情吸引過來；也可以中性地表示引起性吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"The bright display attracted many shoppers.","zh":"醒目的展示吸引了許多購物者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm voice attracted everyone's attention.","zh":"她平靜的聲音吸引了所有人的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21c0fbc5d08ad4b948ce","word":"attraction","forms":["attraction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-024f8c461c11668d","term":"attraction","forms":["attraction","attractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸引力；引力","explanation":"指把物體、人與物等拉近或使其彼此靠近的力量或傾向，既可以是物理上的引力，也可以泛指某種吸引力。這是“把東西拉過來”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The attraction between the two magnets is strong.","zh":"這兩塊磁鐵之間的吸引力很強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The attraction of the countryside is its peace and quiet.","zh":"鄉村的吸引力在於寧靜安逸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-905192b6685a8a55","term":"attraction","forms":["attraction","attractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸引；好感","explanation":"指一個人對某人、某地或某件事產生的吸引感覺或好感，重點是“被拉近”的內心感受，不一定是愛情。","examples":[{"en":"She felt an immediate attraction to the old house.","zh":"她立刻對那座老房子產生了好感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a strong attraction between them.","zh":"他們之間有很強的吸引力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b61536a45e19a73","term":"attraction","forms":["attraction","attractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸引遊客的地方；景點","explanation":"指能把遊客或當地居民吸引來的活動、地點或商店等，通常是值得參觀、體驗或消費的具體物件。它是“把人拉過來”在旅遊和城市生活中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The aquarium is the city's most popular tourist attraction.","zh":"這家水族館是這座城市最受歡迎的旅遊景點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restored lighthouse has become the island's main attraction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ef3b00039e62bc072ce","word":"attractive","forms":["attractive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-134bf27c7f688a82","term":"attractive","forms":["attractive","more attractive","most attractive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"誘人；有吸引力","explanation":"指某個提議、機會、價格或條件很好，讓人產生興趣並願意接受；這裡被吸引的不是外貌，而是它帶來的好處或令人滿意的特點。","examples":[{"en":"The company offered her an attractive salary.","zh":"這家公司給她開出了很誘人的薪資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Buying the house now is an attractive option.","zh":"現在買下這套房是個很有吸引力的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attractive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-759a92a24146fbfb","term":"attractive","forms":["attractive","more attractive","most attractive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有魅力的；討人喜歡的","explanation":"指人的外貌、氣質或整體特點令人愉快、容易產生好感，常可譯為“有吸引力的”或“有魅力的”。在談潛在戀愛物件時，它可以明確表示外表或個人魅力令人心動，但不只限於戀愛場景。","examples":[{"en":"She is confident, friendly, and very attractive.","zh":"她自信、友善，而且很有魅力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His kindness made him attractive to everyone he met.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attractive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a92bfd02c450af0360de","word":"attribute","forms":["attribute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-db1d057a24581552","term":"attribute","forms":["attribute","attributes","attributing","attributed","attributest","attributedst","attributeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……歸因於","explanation":"表示認為某個結果、現象或行為是由某種原因造成的，也就是把結果的標籤貼到某個原因上。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor attributed his improvement to the new treatment.","zh":"醫生把他的好轉歸因於新的治療方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She attributed the delay to heavy traffic.","zh":"她把延誤歸因於交通擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attribute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-95482ba25b7bf178dde1","word":"auction","forms":["auction"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-966e0077b0c01a3a","term":"auction","forms":["auction","auctions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拍賣會；公開競價","explanation":"指一種公開出售活動：賣方展示物品，買家依次出價，通常由出價最高的人買下。它也可以指這一整套競價出售的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The painting was sold at auction for twice its estimated value.","zh":"這幅畫在拍賣會上以估價兩倍的價格售出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We went to an auction and bid on an old bicycle.","zh":"我們去參加了拍賣會，還競價買了一輛舊腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e1e2bfd0fb9dfbe","term":"auction","forms":["auction","auctions","auctioning","auctioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拍賣","explanation":"指把物品或財產拿到公開競價活動中出售，讓買家出價並按規則決定買家。","examples":[{"en":"The museum will auction several rare books next month.","zh":"博物館下個月將拍賣幾本珍 rare 的書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They auctioned the donated paintings for charity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-adf0e0999386dae758e1","word":"audience","forms":["audience"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7f02029ba0445eb","term":"audience","forms":["audience","audiences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現場聽眾或觀眾","explanation":"指聚集在一起聽演講、看演出或觀看其他活動的人群，是最基本、最容易見到的意思。這個詞把大家看成同一個受聲音或表演吸引的群體。","examples":[{"en":"The audience fell silent when the singer walked onto the stage.","zh":"歌手走上臺時，觀眾安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We joined the audience just as the lights went down.","zh":"燈光剛暗下來，我們就加入了觀眾席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/audience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c27a41b0243c9418","term":"audience","forms":["audience","audiences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣播或電視的受眾","explanation":"指收聽某個廣播節目或觀看某個電視節目的一大片公眾。這裡的人不一定在同一個地方，而是透過同一媒體接觸內容。","examples":[{"en":"The new documentary attracted a large audience across the country.","zh":"這部新紀錄片吸引了全國各地的大量觀眾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary reached an audience of six million viewers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/audience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ed8919ce20490a5e3ad","word":"audio","forms":["audio"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1cd6a7875c1b41f","term":"audio","forms":["audio","more audio","most audio"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聽覺的；聲音方面的","explanation":"指依靠耳朵接收、以聲音為重點的事物，與依靠畫面的 visual 相對。它描述的是資訊傳遞的渠道或側重點，不一定表示聲音本身的音質。","examples":[{"en":"The course offers audio instructions for learners who prefer listening.","zh":"這門課程為喜歡聽講的學習者提供音訊說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camera records audio commentary alongside each clip.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/audio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b81f37a043a6f767e7c9","word":"audit","forms":["audit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aed54bba95f1d700","term":"audit","forms":["audit","audits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨立審計","explanation":"指由相對獨立的人員檢查記錄、活動和控制措施，判斷制度是否充分、是否遵守既定政策，並提出改進辦法。這是現代商業和機構語境中最重要的義項。","examples":[{"en":"The company hired an independent auditor to review its data security controls.","zh":"公司聘請了獨立審計員來檢查其資料安全控制措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audit found several weaknesses in the reporting process.","zh":"審計發現報告流程中存在幾處薄弱環節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/audit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-492f0278e5832fed6f9d","word":"auditorium","forms":["auditorium"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a2ed47e4093dae8","term":"auditorium","forms":["auditorium","auditoriums","auditoria"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大型禮堂或觀眾廳","explanation":"指供公眾開會、聽講、看演出或參加其他活動的大型室內場所，重點是整間廳堂本身。","examples":[{"en":"The students gathered in the auditorium for the school concert.","zh":"學生們聚集在禮堂裡參加學校音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university built a new auditorium for lectures and performances.","zh":"這所大學建了一座新的禮堂，用於講座和演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auditorium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcf5d6d74b6beae4","term":"auditorium","forms":["auditorium","auditoriums","auditoria"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀眾所在區域","explanation":"在談論演出或放映現場的空間佈局時，auditorium 也可特指觀眾坐著、觀看活動的那一片區域，而不是舞臺或表演區域。","examples":[{"en":"The auditorium was almost full when the lights went down.","zh":"燈光暗下來時，觀眾席幾乎已經坐滿了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ushers checked every row of the auditorium before admitting guests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auditorium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a892fec0a7ca63b4b442","word":"aunt","forms":["aunt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d15895e929d84bb0","term":"aunt","forms":["aunt","aunts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"父母的姐妹或姻親姐妹","explanation":"指父母的姐妹，或父母兄弟的妻子等女性姻親。在不同家庭和語境中，它可以對應中文裡不同的親屬稱謂，但共同點都是“父母那一輩的女性親屬”。","examples":[{"en":"My aunt is coming to dinner on Sunday.","zh":"我姨媽星期天要來吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My aunt taught her younger brother to swim.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd9ec773920f8ac4","term":"aunt","forms":["aunt","aunts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對父母朋友等年長女性的親切稱呼","explanation":"也可指比自己年長一輩、尤其是父母的女性朋友，即使沒有血緣關係，也像家人一樣稱她為 aunt。這是把家庭中的親屬稱呼擴充套件為親切稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"The children call our neighbor Aunt May.","zh":"孩子們把我們的鄰居梅阿姨叫作梅姨媽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Aunt Rosa has been Mum's closest friend since school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-343600e3385c2d55d2f5","word":"authentic","forms":["authentic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df11c8e5a456417c","term":"authentic","forms":["authentic","more authentic","most authentic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真品的；確實出自所稱來源的","explanation":"指某件東西確實來自它聲稱的來源，不是仿製品、偽造品或冒充品，就像蓋有真實出處印章的真品。","examples":[{"en":"The museum confirmed that the painting was authentic.","zh":"博物館確認這幅畫是真品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They checked whether the signature was authentic.","zh":"他們核實了這個簽名是否真實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/authentic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13819c1c7c855a69","term":"authentic","forms":["authentic","more authentic","most authentic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真實可信的；自然不做作的","explanation":"指內容符合實際、因此值得相信，或人、作品和表達保留了真實自然的樣子，沒有刻意偽裝或迎合。","examples":[{"en":"Readers trust her because her writing feels authentic.","zh":"讀者信任她，因為她的文字讓人覺得真實自然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her diary gives an authentic account of village life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/authentic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-636485868971eac5aca3","word":"author","forms":["author"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09a678ed0e2098e5","term":"author","forms":["author","authors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作品創作者","explanation":"author 首先指創作一部作品的人，尤其是書、文章等文學或書面作品的創作者；合作作品可以有多個 authors。","examples":[{"en":"The author of this novel grew up in a small coastal town.","zh":"這部小說的作者在一個小海濱城鎮長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three authors contributed chapters to the book.","zh":"三位作者為這本書分別撰寫了章節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/author","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92ed79fd0fe653b2","term":"author","forms":["author","authors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"版權登記上的作者","explanation":"在版權和智慧財產權語境中，author 指法律上被認定或登記為作品創作者的人或機構；這個身份有時不等於實際寫作的人。","examples":[{"en":"The company was listed as the author on the copyright registration.","zh":"該公司被列為版權登記上的作者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The registration names the studio as the author.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/author","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f76fd501bb68ef71f4e","word":"authority","forms":["authority"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96d2cdf125ada71e","term":"authority","forms":["authority","authorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"權力；職權","explanation":"指某人因職位、法律或職責而擁有的發令、制定規則或要求別人服從的權力。它強調“誰有資格決定或強制執行”，不一定表示這個決定本身正確。","examples":[{"en":"Only the manager has the authority to approve the refund.","zh":"只有經理有權批准退款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law gives local councils authority over parking rules.","zh":"法律賦予地方議會制定停車規定的權力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/authority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1707bb8f043ce3f5","term":"authority","forms":["authority","authorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"當局；官方人員","explanation":"指佔據官方權力職位的人或機構的合稱，尤其常指警察、政府部門等負責處理事務和執行規則的當局。","examples":[{"en":"The authorities closed the road after the landslide.","zh":"山體滑坡後，當局封閉了這條道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The health authority closed the contaminated swimming pool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/authority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3d6b72f00de7044","term":"authority","forms":["authority","authorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"權威來源；權威專家","explanation":"指在某個領域被認為最可靠、最有資格提供資訊的人、書籍或其他來源。這裡的authority不是發號施令，而是憑知識和專業性讓人信服。","examples":[{"en":"She is a leading authority on coastal wildlife.","zh":"她是海岸野生動物方面的權威專家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This handbook is regarded as an authority on traditional architecture.","zh":"這本手冊被視為傳統建築方面的權威資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/authority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a2dbd905287e75a5d2b","word":"authorize","forms":["authorize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b91bc02f20249dc2","term":"authorize","forms":["authorize","authorizes","authorizing","authorized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"授權；批准","explanation":"指正式允許某人做某事，並賦予其相應的權力；也可指正式批准某項行動，就像在檔案上蓋許可印章。","examples":[{"en":"The board authorized the manager to sign the contract.","zh":"董事會授權經理簽署合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city has authorized construction to begin next month.","zh":"市政府已批准施工於下個月開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/authorize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f425acab181532f91d03","word":"autobiography","forms":["autobiography"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8090292d25eddc63","term":"autobiography","forms":["autobiography","autobiographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本人寫的生平故事","explanation":"指一個人親自寫下的、講述自己人生經歷的書或文字作品；作者既是敘述者，也是這段人生的主人公。","examples":[{"en":"She published an autobiography about her years as a journalist.","zh":"她出版了一部講述自己記者生涯的自傳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In her autobiography, she describes growing up aboard a boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autobiography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bc329bfd4636b93","term":"autobiography","forms":["autobiography","autobiographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自傳文學體裁","explanation":"指把“本人講述自己生平”作為一類文學作品來看的自傳體裁，而不是某一本具體的書。","examples":[{"en":"Autobiography has become an important form of modern literature.","zh":"自傳已經成為現代文學的一種重要形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course examines autobiography as a literary genre.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autobiography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc8da953dc3014a525f9","word":"autograph","forms":["autograph"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3bc880da5a7fc72","term":"autograph","forms":["autograph","autographs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親筆簽名","explanation":"指某人親手寫下的名字或字跡，最常指名人給粉絲留下的簽名。","examples":[{"en":"The children waited outside the stadium to get the player's autograph.","zh":"孩子們在體育場外等著拿到那名球員的簽名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps her favorite singer's autograph in a small notebook.","zh":"她把自己喜歡的歌手的簽名儲存在一個小筆記本里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autograph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e08c134576cf6fac","term":"autograph","forms":["autograph","autographs","autographing","autographed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為某物簽名","explanation":"指在書、球衣、照片等物品上親筆簽下自己的名字，通常是為了留念或贈送給別人。","examples":[{"en":"The actor autographed a poster for a young fan.","zh":"那名演員為一位年輕粉絲在海報上籤了名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you autograph my book?","zh":"您能在我的書上籤個名嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autograph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-53e0ff348c9be93a14d0","word":"automatic","forms":["automatic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ddf0096e872a4a2","term":"automatic","forms":["automatic","more automatic","most automatic","dubious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自動執行的","explanation":"指機器或裝置不需要人持續操控，便能按照設定自行執行。重點是控制過程被裝置接手了，並不一定表示完全沒有任何設定或啟動操作。","examples":[{"en":"The automatic doors opened as we approached.","zh":"我們走近時，自動門開啟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An automatic sprinkler watered the lawn at dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/automatic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f079a799459c725a","term":"automatic","forms":["automatic","more automatic","most automatic","dubious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"下意識的；習慣性的","explanation":"指人沒有經過有意識的思考，就按照習慣或本能作出反應；這裡不是機器在執行，而是人的反應像“自己發生”一樣。","examples":[{"en":"When the ball came toward her face, she raised her hands automatically.","zh":"球朝她臉上飛來時，她下意識地抬起了手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her automatic response was to check the locks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/automatic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fae5c21a6da57eb","term":"automatic","forms":["automatic","more automatic","most automatic","dubious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"必然的；按規定直接產生的","explanation":"指某個結果由法律、規則或邏輯直接決定，不需要另外判斷或討論；一旦觸發條件，結果就像自動出現一樣。","examples":[{"en":"A second yellow card means an automatic suspension for the next match.","zh":"第二張黃牌意味著下一場比賽自動停賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Missing three payments triggers automatic cancellation of membership.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/automatic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9bd6be621ddbca374b21","word":"automobile/auto","forms":["automobile","auto"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93da71863f85e6db","term":"automobile","forms":["automobile","automobiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽車","explanation":"指靠自己的發動機或其他儲存的動力在地面行駛、主要用來載人並帶少量物品的機動車。它正好體現了“自己會移動”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Her automobile is small, reliable, and easy to park.","zh":"她的汽車很小，可靠又容易停車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road was crowded with automobiles during the holiday.","zh":"假日期間，這條路上擠滿了汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/automobile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17dbe3b3ac4ab28d","term":"auto","forms":["auto","autos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽車","explanation":"auto是automobile的簡稱，指一輛汽車或與汽車有關的事物；這是最值得優先掌握的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"My brother works as an auto mechanic.","zh":"我哥哥是汽車修理工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop sells used auto parts.","zh":"這家店賣二手汽車零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7c77a3e1f96a091","term":"auto","forms":["auto","autos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自動變速箱","explanation":"指汽車中負責自動換擋的變速箱或變速系統；它是“汽車自動運轉”這條主線在部件上的具體化。","examples":[{"en":"This model comes with a four-speed auto.","zh":"這款車型配有四擋自動變速箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic replaced the failing auto with a manual.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e94d787f61ea3ee8eede","word":"autonomy","forms":["autonomy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0abace633643677","term":"autonomy","forms":["autonomy","autonomies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自主權；獨立治理","explanation":"指個人、組織或地區有權按照自己的規則作決定和行動，而不是由外部權力替它作主。重點是“自己管理自己”，不一定意味著完全脫離更大的體系。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy gives local schools more autonomy over their budgets.","zh":"新政策讓當地學校在預算方面擁有更多自主權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She values the autonomy to choose how she organizes her work.","zh":"她很看重自己選擇如何安排工作的自主權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autonomy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fc326780c15fea8","term":"autonomy","forms":["autonomy","autonomies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自主決策能力","explanation":"指一個人能夠在瞭解情況、沒有被強迫的情況下，自己作出決定。它把“自己拿方向盤”進一步用於人的意志和判斷能力。","examples":[{"en":"Patients should have the autonomy to decide whether to accept the treatment.","zh":"患者應當有權自主決定是否接受治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course encourages students to develop greater intellectual autonomy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autonomy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ddd9818abacfde7afed6","word":"available","forms":["available"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-57217b619e088a48","term":"available","forms":["available","more available","most available"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可用的；可供使用的","explanation":"指某物現成存在，能夠被拿來完成某件事；重點是“能派上用場”，不一定表示免費。","examples":[{"en":"We need all available staff to help with the event.","zh":"我們需要所有能抽調的工作人員來協助這次活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is there a quiet room available for the interview?","zh":"有沒有可以用來面試的安靜房間？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/available","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6df274de07477c26","term":"available","forms":["available","more available","most available"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可獲得的；買得到的","explanation":"指某物可以找到、買到或取得，強調獲取並不困難或已經有供應。","examples":[{"en":"The new model is now available in three colors.","zh":"這款新型號現在有三種顏色可以買到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fresh bread is available from the corner bakery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/available","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-125ec1a292b92eed0b53","word":"avenue","forms":["avenue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8801f19ad1f257b1","term":"avenue","forms":["avenue","avenues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大道；林蔭道","explanation":"指城市中較寬的街道，尤其是兩旁有樹的道路，也可作為城市道路名稱的一部分。它保留了“寬闊地通向某處”的基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is on Park Avenue.","zh":"這家酒店在公園大道上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A line of trees runs along the avenue.","zh":"一排樹沿著這條大道延伸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avenue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-020b9e59583519b5","term":"avenue","forms":["avenue","avenues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"途徑；辦法","explanation":"表示實現目標、解決問題或獲得結果的一種辦法。這裡的“路”不再是實際道路，而是通向目標的抽象路徑。","examples":[{"en":"The team is exploring new avenues for reducing costs.","zh":"團隊正在探索降低成本的新途徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Education may be an avenue to a better career.","zh":"教育可能是通向更好職業的一條途徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avenue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-184df936d41b2da8d101","word":"average","forms":["average"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1b8f74142f41cad","term":"average","forms":["average","more average","most average"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平均的；與平均數有關的","explanation":"表示某個數值、特徵或物件與一組資料的平均水平有關，重點是“由一組數或物件算出的中間水平”。","examples":[{"en":"The average age of the participants was 18.5.","zh":"參加者的平均年齡是18.5歲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Average rainfall is highest along the northern coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/average","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91bed5bd47e4b104","term":"average","forms":["average","more average","most average"],"pos":"adj","zh":"中等水平的","explanation":"表示水平不高不低，處在同類物件的中間位置，既不是優秀，也不是特別差。","examples":[{"en":"I soon found I was only an average chess player.","zh":"我很快發現自己只是箇中等水平的棋手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An average swimmer could manage this gentle current.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/average","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15fc66bac749927e","term":"average","forms":["average","averages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平均數；平均值","explanation":"指用來代表一組資料中心水平的數值，可以是數學上的均值，也可以廣義地指中位數、眾數等集中趨勢指標。它把許多個別資料壓縮成一個便於比較的中心值。","examples":[{"en":"The average of the five test scores was 82.","zh":"這五個測試成績的平均數是82分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"On average, the train takes forty minutes.","zh":"這趟火車平均需要40分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/average","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbb77cb45bce6909","term":"average","forms":["average","averages","averaging","averaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"求平均值","explanation":"指把一組數字合併計算，得到它們的算術平均數；也就是從一組資料中找出代表性的中間數值。","examples":[{"en":"If you average 10, 20, and 24, you get 18.","zh":"如果把10、20和24求平均，結果是18。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher averaged the scores before entering them.","zh":"老師先把分數求了平均，再錄入成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/average","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4f0eb14a8be73512705","word":"avert","forms":["avert"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a8831b2c8e11626","term":"avert","forms":["avert","averts","averting","averted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉開目光或注意力","explanation":"把目光、臉或注意力從某物上轉開，不去看或不去面對它。這是“把某物轉開”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She averted her eyes when the argument became intense.","zh":"爭吵變得激烈時，她移開了目光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She averted her eyes during the painful scene.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f7ddc9a71e9a1eb","term":"avert","forms":["avert","averts","averting","averted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"防止危險或壞事發生","explanation":"把危險、損害或不良結果“轉開”，也就是採取行動使它不發生或減輕其影響。這是從“轉開目光”擴充套件到“轉開危險”的常用抽象義。","examples":[{"en":"Quick action helped avert a major crisis.","zh":"迅速採取行動幫助避免了一場重大危機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Quick action averted a collision at the junction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab97542e73d2ca454912","word":"aviation","forms":["aviation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09bc18b28edc7b7e","term":"aviation","forms":["aviation","aviations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"航空學與飛行技術","explanation":"指製造飛機並讓飛機飛行的技術、知識和實踐，是圍繞“讓飛鳥升空”形成的整個領域。","examples":[{"en":"She studied aviation at university.","zh":"她在大學學習航空學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Advances in aviation have made air travel safer.","zh":"航空技術的進步讓乘飛機旅行更加安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aviation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-436ab59815dcdbf5","term":"aviation","forms":["aviation","aviations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛行與航空運營","explanation":"指飛機飛行、駕駛和運營飛機這一整套活動，也就是“讓飛鳥持續飛行並安全執行”。","examples":[{"en":"The history of aviation is full of daring pioneers.","zh":"航空史上充滿了勇敢的先驅者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Aviation safety remains a major concern.","zh":"航空安全仍然是人們高度關注的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aviation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3270f7fe8acead1d13ab","word":"avoid","forms":["avoid"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6faf4f6790299273","term":"avoid","forms":["avoid","avoids","avoiding","avoided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"避開某人","explanation":"指有意不和某人見面、交談或來往，把自己從對方身邊移開，常帶有躲著對方的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She has been avoiding me since the argument.","zh":"爭吵之後，她一直在躲著我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took the back stairs to avoid his landlord.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avoid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfe464cd86d85e50","term":"avoid","forms":["avoid","avoids","avoiding","avoided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"躲開有害之物","explanation":"指及時離開或繞開可能造成傷害的東西、動作或情況，讓自己不被它碰到或影響。","examples":[{"en":"He stepped aside to avoid the falling branch.","zh":"他側身避開了掉下來的樹枝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wear boots to avoid sharp stones on the trail.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avoid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-434fa90fee1681ea","term":"avoid","forms":["avoid","avoids","avoiding","avoided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遠離某物","explanation":"指有意識地不接近、不參與或不接觸某種人、場所、活動或事物，把它排除在自己的行動之外。","examples":[{"en":"We avoid crowded restaurants on Friday nights.","zh":"我們週五晚上會避開擁擠的餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Avoid the unstable cliffs during your walk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avoid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00701f45abff0505","term":"avoid","forms":["avoid","avoids","avoiding","avoided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"避免做某事","explanation":"指設法不做某事，或防止某種不想要的結果發生；這裡是把某個行為或結果從計劃中移開。","examples":[{"en":"Try to avoid making the same mistake twice.","zh":"儘量不要把同樣的錯誤犯兩次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good planning can avoid unnecessary delays.","zh":"周密的計劃可以避免不必要的延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avoid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1aefe47e20eb91fa38a5","word":"await","forms":["await"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3d6f314b04c0204","term":"await","forms":["await","awaits","awaiting","awaited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"等待；等候","explanation":"指耐心等著某人、某事或某個答覆到來，重點是等待的物件就在前方。這個義項是 await 在現代正式英語中的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"We await your decision before moving forward.","zh":"我們會等你作出決定後再繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee is still awaiting a reply.","zh":"委員會仍在等待答覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/await","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a70ebaf9b9b17fb0","term":"await","forms":["await","awaits","awaiting","awaited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"期待；預期","explanation":"表示預先認為某件事會發生，帶有把目光投向未來、等它到來的感覺。它可以是積極期待，也可以只是中性地預期。","examples":[{"en":"Investors await further news about the company.","zh":"投資者在等待有關這家公司的進一步訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We await your response with considerable interest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/await","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b743af620780adb","term":"await","forms":["await","awaits","awaiting","awaited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"等待著發生；等待降臨","explanation":"表示某種機會、結果、命運或經歷已經在前方等著某人，強調未來會來到此人面前。這裡不是人在等待，而是事情彷彿主動在那裡等候。","examples":[{"en":"New challenges await the team next season.","zh":"下個賽季還有新的挑戰在等待著這支隊伍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A warm welcome awaits you at the guesthouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/await","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f245940166d1611d76b3","word":"awake","forms":["awake"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c862086e14f9684","term":"awake","forms":["awake"],"pos":"adj","zh":"醒著的","explanation":"指人沒有睡著，處於有意識的狀態；重點是“醒著”，不一定表示精神特別好或已經起床。","examples":[{"en":"I was still awake when the first train passed.","zh":"第一班火車經過時我還醒著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby remained awake throughout the long flight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5626994891c82d58","term":"awake","forms":["awake"],"pos":"adj","zh":"警覺的；意識到的","explanation":"從身體醒著擴充套件到頭腦保持警覺，或已經意識到某個事實、危險和可能性。","examples":[{"en":"The team is awake to the risks of relying on one supplier.","zh":"這個團隊已經意識到依賴單一供應商的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Voters are increasingly awake to the dangers of corruption.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba71c3656bb30c58","term":"awake","forms":["awake","awakes","awaking","awoke","awaked","awoken","awaken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"醒來","explanation":"指人從睡眠中恢復意識，和形容詞“醒著的”是同一條核心意象的動態版本。","examples":[{"en":"She awoke before dawn and opened the window.","zh":"她黎明前醒來，開啟了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I awoke to the sound of church bells.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-cdd35a708cf7fbc0a70f","word":"awaken","forms":["awaken"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dcd1c8f5a234e01d","term":"awaken","forms":["awaken","awakens","awakening","awakened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喚醒；叫醒","explanation":"使睡著的人醒來，也可以指使處於沉睡狀態的事物開始有反應。核心畫面是把別人從睡夢中叫醒。","examples":[{"en":"The soft music awakened the baby.","zh":"輕柔的音樂把嬰兒喚醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The news awakened her to the seriousness of the problem.","zh":"這條訊息使她意識到問題的嚴重性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awaken","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-862b4bf7b8620fe8","term":"awaken","forms":["awaken","awakens","awakening","awakened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"醒來","explanation":"指自己停止睡眠、醒過來。它仍然保留“從沉睡狀態中醒來”這個核心畫面，只是沒有把別人叫醒。","examples":[{"en":"She awakened before sunrise and opened the window.","zh":"她在日出前醒來，開啟了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She awakened to sunlight streaming through the curtains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awaken","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65438fd6e027a09e","term":"awaken","forms":["awaken","awakens","awakening","awakened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喚起；激發","explanation":"把原本沉睡或沒有發揮作用的熱情、能力、興趣等激發出來，使它們開始活躍。這是從“叫醒”自然發展出的比喻意義。","examples":[{"en":"The trip awakened her interest in photography.","zh":"這次旅行喚起了她對攝影的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach awakened a new confidence in the team.","zh":"教練激發了這支隊伍新的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awaken","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4009662c0116dac4f17","word":"award","forms":["award"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b624fed951cf322","term":"award","forms":["award","awards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式裁決","explanation":"指仲裁員或其他有權作決定的人在審查情況後作出的最終裁決，尤其常指法律爭議中的裁決結果。","examples":[{"en":"The arbitrator's award required the company to pay damages.","zh":"仲裁員的裁決要求公司支付賠償金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Neither party challenged the award issued by the arbitration panel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/award","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dde0d40dddad9cec","term":"award","forms":["award","awards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎項；榮譽","explanation":"指因成就、表現或比賽成績而正式授予的獎項、獎牌或榮譽，是日常生活中最常見的名詞義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"Her first novel won a major literary award.","zh":"她的第一部小說贏得了一項重要的文學獎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The award recognized her decades of community service.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/award","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8512f1d5211fe5ec","term":"award","forms":["award","awards","awarding","awarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式作出裁定","explanation":"指有權威的一方經過審查後正式決定結果，核心仍是“判斷後把決定定下來”。","examples":[{"en":"After reviewing the evidence, the panel awarded in favor of the workers.","zh":"委員會審查證據後作出了有利於工人的裁定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court awarded custody to the child's grandparents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/award","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7c85f1685487143","term":"award","forms":["award","awards","awarding","awarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"授予獎項或款項","explanation":"指按照正式評定結果，把獎項、經費或其他明確的授予物件交給獲選者。","examples":[{"en":"The committee awarded a grant to the young scientist.","zh":"委員會向那位年輕科學家授予了一筆研究經費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jury awarded her damages for the injury.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/award","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bf9fd4be091a1baa7d3","word":"aware","forms":["aware"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73d5be6d5839b2a8","term":"aware","forms":["aware","more aware","awarer","most aware","awarest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"警覺的；提防著的","explanation":"心裡的燈亮著，人在留意可能出現的危險、問題或困難，沒有放鬆防備。","examples":[{"en":"Stay aware when you are walking alone at night.","zh":"晚上獨自走路時要保持警覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stay aware of cyclists approaching from behind.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aware","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eba99c653887a573","term":"aware","forms":["aware","more aware","awarer","most aware","awarest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"知道的；意識到的","explanation":"心裡的燈照到了某個事實、情況或正在發生的事，表示人已經知道或意識到了它；在特定上下文中也可表示處於清醒狀態。","examples":[{"en":"I wasn't aware that the meeting had been moved.","zh":"我不知道會議已經改時間了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you aware of the revised departure time?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aware","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-378ce56a9d146d5174c8","word":"away","forms":["away"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0024a72c4ef862d","term":"away","forms":["away"],"pos":"adv","zh":"離開；從某處去","explanation":"表示從當前地點離開，去別的地方；核心畫面就是人或事物從眼前移走。","examples":[{"en":"We went away for the weekend.","zh":"我們外出度週末了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children ran away when the sprinkler started.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/away","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d863866dbe87c92d","term":"away","forms":["away"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向旁邊；移開","explanation":"表示從原來的方向或位置偏開，轉到一旁或另一方向；例如避開接近的人。","examples":[{"en":"She turned away when she heard her name.","zh":"聽到有人叫她的名字時，她把身子轉開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Move the vase away before opening the window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/away","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c910b84f914524f9","term":"away","forms":["away"],"pos":"adv","zh":"扔掉；丟開","explanation":"表示把東西移到自己不再保留或處理的位置，因此引申為扔掉、棄置；常見於 throw away 等短語。","examples":[{"en":"Please throw away these empty boxes.","zh":"請把這些空盒子扔掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Throw those moldy peaches away.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/away","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-544551b5e55a8d93","term":"away","forms":["away"],"pos":"adv","zh":"逐漸消失","explanation":"表示某種狀態、聲音、痕跡或生命從存在中慢慢退去，直到減弱或消失；這是“離開原有狀態”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The pain slowly faded away.","zh":"疼痛慢慢消退了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their voices died away as the train gathered speed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/away","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-589229fdcd6660b1d3f7","word":"awe","forms":["awe"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95ce74ba388695f8","term":"awe","forms":["awe","awes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敬畏","explanation":"awe是一種面對強大、崇高或令人敬畏的事物時產生的情感，既有害怕或震懾，也有尊敬。它常讓人感到自己的渺小，或不敢輕慢眼前的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The visitors stood in awe of the ancient temple.","zh":"遊客們對這座古老的寺廟充滿敬畏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The power of the storm filled us with awe.","zh":"暴風雨的力量讓我們既敬畏又震撼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe90cac4088043cc","term":"awe","forms":["awe","awes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚歎","explanation":"awe也可以突出面對極其宏大、美麗或不可思議的事物時產生的驚歎。這裡不一定有害怕，而是被景象的規模、力量或奇異之處深深震撼。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the northern lights in awe.","zh":"我們驚歎地觀看了北極光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glacier's vast blue walls filled us with awe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c240d1df43e4d916","term":"awe","forms":["awe","awes","awing","aweing","awed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使敬畏、震撼","explanation":"awe表示某人或某物使另一個人產生敬畏和震撼，通常因為它顯得宏大、崇高、強大或令人難以置信。它把名詞awe所表示的感覺施加到別人身上。","examples":[{"en":"The scale of the cathedral awed the young visitor.","zh":"大教堂的宏大規模令年輕遊客肅然起敬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was awed by the silence of the desert.","zh":"她被沙漠的寂靜深深震撼了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-705db0603fd5431451da","word":"awesome","forms":["awesome"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df332ba5283795f9","term":"awesome","forms":["awesome","more awesome","awesomer","most awesome","awesomest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人敬畏的；震撼的","explanation":"形容規模、力量或景象強大到讓人產生敬畏、驚奇，甚至有些害怕。它保留了“強烈到令人驚歎”這個核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The waterfall was an awesome sight after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後的瀑布景象令人震撼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team faced the awesome power of the ocean.","zh":"這支隊伍面對著海洋令人敬畏的力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awesome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1bcbc68f897aa694","term":"awesome","forms":["awesome","more awesome","awesomer","most awesome","awesomest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別棒的；精彩的","explanation":"口語中表示“非常好、令人興奮或讓人印象深刻”，是把“令人驚歎”的強烈感覺轉成熱情稱讚。","examples":[{"en":"That concert was awesome!","zh":"那場音樂會太精彩了！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The concert was awesome from start to finish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awesome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87e1315329cf22c9ce14","word":"awful","forms":["awful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb76d00f4864502f","term":"awful","forms":["awful","awfuller","more awful","awfullest","most awful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"糟透的","explanation":"表示某事物質量很差、令人不快，或某段經歷糟糕得讓人不想再經歷。","examples":[{"en":"The traffic was awful this morning.","zh":"今天早上的交通糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soup tastes awful.","zh":"這湯難喝得不得了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ee2d6a9a5e72ef247e0","word":"awhile","forms":["awhile"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-697514e96bc69b00","term":"awhile","forms":["awhile"],"pos":"adv","zh":"一會兒；暫時","explanation":"表示某個動作或狀態繼續一小段時間，通常帶有“先這樣一陣子”的感覺。它常用於請求、建議或描述暫時停留、等待和保持某種狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Sit with me awhile.","zh":"陪我坐一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We waited awhile before the bus arrived.","zh":"公共汽車到來前，我們等了一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awhile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ee41686ee634498f333","word":"awkward","forms":["awkward"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-011ea4159804e2b9","term":"awkward","forms":["awkward","more awkward","most awkward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"動作笨拙","explanation":"指手腳或使用工具時不靈活，動作不協調，像是總有一點兒“卡住”。","examples":[{"en":"I was awkward with the scissors and cut the paper unevenly.","zh":"我用剪刀時很笨拙，把紙剪得參差不齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is awkward at dancing, but he is getting better.","zh":"他跳舞時動作很笨拙，但正在慢慢進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awkward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6c011bc47d4e451","term":"awkward","forms":["awkward","more awkward","most awkward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人尷尬；難以處理","explanation":"指某個場面、問題或時刻讓人不知該說什麼、做什麼，因而顯得尷尬或難以應付。","examples":[{"en":"There was an awkward silence after her question.","zh":"她問完問題後，現場出現了令人尷尬的沉默。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was awkward when both of us reached for the same chair.","zh":"我們倆同時伸手去拿同一把椅子時，場面很尷尬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awkward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3ca38ef0e8554b39ce6","word":"baby","forms":["baby"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af4ee3d91782e71b","term":"baby","forms":["baby","babies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嬰兒","explanation":"指出生後不久、還很小，通常尚未完全學會走路的人。這是baby最基本、最直接的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The baby is asleep, so please close the door quietly.","zh":"嬰兒睡著了，請輕輕地關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their baby started walking last month.","zh":"他們的寶寶上個月開始學走路了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4adf75314434ac7ad502","word":"bachelor","forms":["bachelor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99de408e6b4b88af","term":"bachelor","forms":["bachelor","bachelors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未婚男子","explanation":"指尚未結婚、通常被社會視為有結婚能力的男子，核心畫面就是“還沒有結婚的男人”。","examples":[{"en":"He has been a bachelor for most of his adult life.","zh":"他成年後的大部分時間都是單身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My uncle is a confirmed bachelor.","zh":"我叔叔是個堅定的單身主義者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bachelor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b959821565f68399","term":"bachelor","forms":["bachelor","bachelors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學士學位","explanation":"指大學授予的第一級或基礎學位，也就是通常所說的學士學位；這是“大學學習階段的第一張學位證”這條記憶線。","examples":[{"en":"She earned a bachelor's degree in biology.","zh":"她獲得了生物學學士學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bachelor's degree is required for this position.","zh":"這個職位要求具有學士學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bachelor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c482346f375027677fa","word":"back","forms":["back"],"officialPos":"adv./n./v./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cff3347acd797ec1","term":"back","forms":["back","more back","most back"],"pos":"adj","zh":"後面的","explanation":"把 back 想成“背後這一面”，它可以表示位於某物後面的，或靠近後部的。","examples":[{"en":"Go in through the back door of the house.","zh":"從房子的後門進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please use the back entrance after six.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07b1b675d5ba4ed5","term":"back","forms":["back","further back","farther back","furthest back","farthest back"],"pos":"adv","zh":"回到原處或原狀","explanation":"把 back 想成回到“背後那一面”或原來的位置：它表示返回原處，也表示把東西恢復或歸還到先前的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"He gave back the money he had borrowed.","zh":"他歸還了借來的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the dictionary back on its shelf.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c069d6cf58e7eb5","term":"back","forms":["back","backs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"背部","explanation":"指人的背部，也就是與胸部和腹部相對、從頸部延伸到脊柱下端的身體部分。把它記成“背後這一面”最容易理解。","examples":[{"en":"Could you scratch my back?","zh":"你能幫我撓撓背嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My back hurts after carrying the boxes.","zh":"搬完這些箱子後，我的背疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bec5c3ab16a4a39","term":"back","forms":["back","backs","backing","backed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支援","explanation":"表示站在某人的“背後”支援他，願意幫助、相信或贊成某人，也可以支援某個計劃、決定或主張。這裡的 back 不是身體動作，而是從背後給人力量。","examples":[{"en":"I will back you all the way.","zh":"我會一直支援你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The board backed her proposal.","zh":"董事會支援了她的提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2e78e3a5bb1d60df728","word":"backbone","forms":["backbone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6673ecf56c7f134a","term":"backbone","forms":["backbone","backbones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脊柱","explanation":"身體裡的“背部骨頭”就是脊柱：它位於背部中央，支撐身體，並保護脊髓。","examples":[{"en":"The accident injured his backbone.","zh":"那場事故傷到了他的脊柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A healthy backbone helps keep the body upright.","zh":"健康的脊柱有助於保持身體直立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backbone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e34b94952c555f9","term":"backbone","forms":["backbone","backbones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"骨幹；核心支撐","explanation":"把一個系統想成身體時，backbone 就是其中不可缺少的中軸和支撐。它可以指交通、通訊、商業或組織中維持整體運轉的核心部分。","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses are the backbone of the local economy.","zh":"小企業是當地經濟的骨幹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reliable volunteers form the backbone of the organization.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backbone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89b91df19d9d75d4cf36","word":"background","forms":["background"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8beb40f3e7cfb8cc","term":"background","forms":["background","backgrounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人背景；經歷","explanation":"指一個人的社會、教育、家庭或職業經歷，也就是塑造現在這個人的“身後底色”。它常用來說明某人為什麼具備某種知識、身份或經驗。","examples":[{"en":"The new manager has a background in engineering.","zh":"新經理有工程學方面的經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her background in farming shaped her research interests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/background","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9083a89f68c8f8ca","term":"background","forms":["background","backgrounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"後景；背景","explanation":"指主體後面的景物、顏色或影象部分；引申時也可指襯托主體的環境。它保留了“主體在前、背景在後”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"There are snow-covered hills in the background of the photo.","zh":"照片的背景中有被雪覆蓋的山丘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are playing, with the school in the background.","zh":"孩子們正在玩耍，學校位於他們身後的背景中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/background","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f00368a6ad231c3c439","word":"backpack","forms":["backpack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bff8635be700e25","term":"backpack","forms":["backpack","backpacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揹包","explanation":"一種用肩帶背在背上的包，用來裝書、衣物、食物或徒步裝備。重點是它由人揹著，而不是手提或拖行。","examples":[{"en":"She carried a small backpack with water and snacks.","zh":"她揹著一個裝有水和零食的小揹包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My keys are in my backpack.","zh":"我的鑰匙在我的揹包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backpack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4445307a6cc7b604","term":"backpack","forms":["backpack","backpacks","backpacking","backpacked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揹包徒步旅行","explanation":"揹著自己的裝備到偏遠地區徒步，並在途中露營過夜；這裡的 backpack 不只是攜帶揹包，而是指一種以揹包為主要裝備的野外旅行方式。","examples":[{"en":"We went backpacking in the mountains for a week.","zh":"我們在山裡揹包徒步、露營了一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They plan to backpack across the national park this summer.","zh":"他們計劃今年夏天揹包徒步穿越這座國家公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backpack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47823b565d4a696e1db5","word":"backward","forms":["backward"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3264b3683b316a55","term":"backward","forms":["backward","more backward","most backward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"後部的；後面的","explanation":"指位置在後方或靠近後部，重點是物體本身所處的位置，而不一定表示它正在向後移動。","examples":[{"en":"The backward section of the machine is covered with a metal panel.","zh":"機器的後部覆蓋著一塊金屬板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The backward portion of the wagon held luggage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52cbaab9146c9441","term":"backward","forms":["backward","more backward","most backward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"倒退的；不利於進步的","explanation":"把“向後”引申為事情沒有向前發展，反而回到較差的狀態；因此常譯為“倒退的”或“退步的”。","examples":[{"en":"Cutting the library budget would be a backward step for the town.","zh":"削減圖書館預算對這個城鎮來說將是一種倒退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Closing the library would be a backward step.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a8366da9908ca11644c","word":"backward/backwards","forms":["backward","backwards"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a138ad1394085523","term":"backward","forms":["backward","more backward","most backward"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向後；往後面","explanation":"表示朝著後方移動，或人在移動時朝後退；這是最直接的“背向前方、往後走”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The dancer took two steps backward and raised her arms.","zh":"舞者向後退了兩步，舉起了雙臂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He walked backward toward the door without turning around.","zh":"他沒有轉身，向後朝門口走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e98e8a9ea6d6713","term":"backward","forms":["backward","more backward","most backward"],"pos":"adv","zh":"倒退地；每況愈下地","explanation":"表示計劃、專案或形勢沒有進步，反而向更差的狀態發展；這是“往後走”對抽象進展的引申。","examples":[{"en":"After the new rule was introduced, the negotiations started going backward.","zh":"新規定出臺後，談判開始倒退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team has made progress, but it cannot afford to move backward now.","zh":"這個團隊已經取得了進展，現在不能再倒退了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e134b84761376b50","term":"backwards","forms":["backwards","more backwards","most backwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向後地；朝後方","explanation":"說明動作朝身後或後方進行，例如倒著走、向後看、向後移動；這是“身體或視線轉向後面”的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She walked backwards across the room without turning around.","zh":"她沒有轉身，倒著走過了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car rolled backwards down the slope.","zh":"汽車沿著斜坡向後滑了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5583c53d3ee8e29cfee","word":"backyard","forms":["backyard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4f1ab568aec442e","term":"backyard","forms":["backyard","backyards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房屋後院","explanation":"指住宅或類似住所後面的院子，是這個詞最直接、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We planted tomatoes in the backyard.","zh":"我們在後院種了西紅柿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are playing in the backyard.","zh":"孩子們正在後院玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backyard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4f6f76d37a84cdc","term":"backyard","forms":["backyard","backyards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"住處附近","explanation":"把自己熟悉、經常去的住處或工作地點周圍看成自己的“後院”，所以可指日常活動範圍內的附近區域。","examples":[{"en":"There’s a wonderful hiking trail right in our backyard.","zh":"我們家附近就有一條很棒的徒步小徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We discovered a rare orchid right in our backyard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/backyard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9cca0703342e24806a9f","word":"bacon","forms":["bacon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06e0a0eca0b470d5","term":"bacon","forms":["bacon","bacons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醃製豬肉","explanation":"指經過醃製、來自豬的背部、腹部或側面的肉，通常作為早餐或配菜烹調。這裡強調的是這種肉本身，不一定已經切成細長條。","examples":[{"en":"We had bacon and eggs for breakfast.","zh":"我們早餐吃了培根和雞蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cooked the vegetables in bacon fat.","zh":"她用培根油脂烹調了蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bacon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b6b665a9f6ad66d","term":"bacon","forms":["bacon","bacons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"培根薄片","explanation":"指把醃製豬肉切成長條薄片後的形態，通常煎至變脆後食用。這個意思是從整塊醃肉進一步切片得到的具體形式。","examples":[{"en":"He wrapped the dates in bacon before baking them.","zh":"他先把棗裹上培根，然後再烘烤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three strips of bacon sizzled in the skillet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bacon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ca82203124aaaaf3e64","word":"bacteria","forms":["bacteria"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-acfa870605258c95","term":"bacteria","forms":["bacteria","bacterias"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細菌；某類細菌","explanation":"指能在顯微鏡下觀察到的細菌，也可以在特定語境中指某一種、某一類或某一株細菌。這是 bacteria 最重要、最常見的意義，通常把它看作 bacterium 的複數。","examples":[{"en":"Some bacteria can survive in extremely hot water.","zh":"有些細菌能在溫度極高的水中生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers found a strain of bacteria that breaks down plastic.","zh":"研究人員發現了一株能分解塑膠的細菌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bacteria","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f05d4b689d270cafb02","word":"bad","forms":["bad"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-406ba5c1751469ca","term":"bad","forms":["bad","worse","badder","more bad","worst","baddest","most bad"],"pos":"adj","zh":"質量差；不好","explanation":"指東西、作品或服務沒有達到正常或理想的質量標準，也就是記憶鉤子裡最直接的“壞”。","examples":[{"en":"The food at that restaurant was really bad.","zh":"那家餐館的食物真的很差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is a bad movie.","zh":"這是一部很差的電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5590ef0c1831ed87","term":"bad","forms":["bad","worse","badder","more bad","worst","baddest","most bad"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不利；負面；不佳","explanation":"指情況、結果、政策或做法帶來不好的影響，整體偏離了理想狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Too much screen time can be bad for children.","zh":"看螢幕時間過長可能對孩子不利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team had a bad start to the season.","zh":"這支隊伍本賽季開局不佳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9f1a52247e6d4a1","term":"bad","forms":["bad","worse","badder","more bad","worst","baddest","most bad"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有害；不利於健康","explanation":"指食物、習慣或環境會損害健康，或對某類生物有害；這也是“偏離正常狀態”在身體方面的表現。","examples":[{"en":"Eating too much salt is bad for your health.","zh":"吃太多鹽對健康有害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chocolate can be bad for dogs.","zh":"巧克力可能對狗有害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8805cdea2b197df5fd55","word":"badge","forms":["badge"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03fa65df05fd191e","term":"badge","forms":["badge","badges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身份徽章；標誌","explanation":"佩戴在衣服或其他地方、用來表明身份、等級或組織成員資格的徽章或標誌。它是badge最核心的形象：一個讓別人認出你屬於哪裡、擔任什麼角色的標記。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a badge showing that she was a volunteer.","zh":"她佩戴著一枚表明自己是志願者的徽章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The blue badge identifies members of the rescue team.","zh":"藍色徽章表明佩戴者是救援隊成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b17dfa9c87ed4decdd50","word":"badly","forms":["badly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d78629dab99a25b","term":"badly","forms":["badly","worse","worst"],"pos":"adv","zh":"很差地；糟糕地","explanation":"它把“壞”加到一個動作或進展上：事情做得不好、結果不理想，或局面發展得不順。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting went badly because nobody had prepared.","zh":"會議開得很不順利，因為沒人做好準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She played badly in the first half.","zh":"她上半場表現得很差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-741ae4d3b45cf88d","term":"badly","forms":["badly","worse","worst"],"pos":"adv","zh":"非常；迫切地","explanation":"當願望或需要強烈到幾乎讓人難受時，badly 表示“非常、迫切地”，不表示做得差。","examples":[{"en":"I want a quiet weekend badly.","zh":"我非常想要一個安靜的週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team badly needs a break.","zh":"這個團隊迫切需要休息一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99e1ff400202a2d6ac68","word":"badminton","forms":["badminton"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-865415e229e93649","term":"badminton","forms":["badminton","badmintons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羽毛球運動","explanation":"一種在場地上隔著球網進行的球拍運動，可以單打，也可以雙打；運動員用球拍把羽毛球擊到對方一側。","examples":[{"en":"We play badminton at the sports center every Saturday.","zh":"我們每週六都在體育中心打羽毛球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She won the badminton match in straight games.","zh":"她以連勝兩局贏下了這場羽毛球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badminton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c018019b6a8b01ab5868","word":"bag","forms":["bag"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-339fa3469ca2880e","term":"bag","forms":["bag","bags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"袋子","explanation":"一種頂部敞開的柔軟容器，用來把食物、商品等東西裝起來並帶走。","examples":[{"en":"She put the apples in a paper bag.","zh":"她把蘋果裝進了紙袋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please bring a bag for the groceries.","zh":"請帶一個袋子來裝買的雜貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e75a2f41fcb7ad9","term":"bag","forms":["bag","bags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"包；旅行袋","explanation":"一種通常帶提手、用來裝個人用品、衣物或旅行所需物品的容器，範圍包括購物袋、書包、手提包和行李箱等。","examples":[{"en":"He packed his clothes in a large travel bag.","zh":"他把衣服裝進了一個大旅行包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I left my bag on the bus.","zh":"我把包落在公交車上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0982a35fddf7e069","term":"bag","forms":["bag","bags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偏好；擅長的事","explanation":"在口語中表示某人喜歡或適合的事物，相當於“這正是某人的興趣或風格”；不喜歡時常說“not my bag”。","examples":[{"en":"Jazz is really her bag.","zh":"爵士樂正是她喜歡的型別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Large parties aren't really my bag.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d6f21ea90c6de24052b","word":"baggage","forms":["baggage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61920948ef8a517e","term":"baggage","forms":["baggage","baggages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅行行李","explanation":"指旅行時隨身攜帶的箱子、大包和其他物品，不只是一隻包，而是作為整體看待的行李。","examples":[{"en":"Please put your baggage in the trunk.","zh":"請把行李放進後備箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We checked our baggage before boarding the train.","zh":"我們上火車前辦理了行李託運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baggage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfb659a1959a336b","term":"baggage","forms":["baggage","baggages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理負擔","explanation":"把過去的創傷、矛盾或未解決的問題比作一直揹著的行李；這些心理負擔會影響一個人正常生活或與人相處。","examples":[{"en":"He brought a lot of emotional baggage into the new relationship.","zh":"他把許多心理負擔帶進了這段新的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Therapy helped her unpack the baggage of a painful childhood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baggage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fb532081657b0142eaa","word":"bait","forms":["bait"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0e48ec764d73ddf","term":"bait","forms":["bait","baits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誘餌；魚餌","explanation":"放在鉤子、陷阱或網附近，用來吸引魚或其他動物靠近並咬住的食物或物質。","examples":[{"en":"Put some fresh bait on the hook before you cast the line.","zh":"把新鮮誘餌掛到鉤上再把魚線丟擲去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fish ignored the bait and swam away.","zh":"魚沒有理會魚餌，遊走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46c2b4c0f57b53c9","term":"bait","forms":["bait","baits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誘因；誘餌","explanation":"任何用來吸引某人或某物靠近、接受某件事或採取某種行動的東西；物件也可以是人。","examples":[{"en":"The free trial was bait to get customers to sign a long contract.","zh":"免費試用是吸引顧客籤長期合同的誘餌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They used a fake message as bait to lure the thief outside.","zh":"他們用一條假訊息作誘餌，把小偷引到外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90ba217ae65abfaa","term":"bait","forms":["bait","baits","baiting","baited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"誘使；引誘","explanation":"用食物、利益或其他誘因把人或動物吸引過來，使其上鉤或採取某種行動。","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement baited shoppers into buying a more expensive package.","zh":"這則廣告用誘因誘使顧客購買更貴的套餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He baited the dog with a piece of meat.","zh":"他用一塊肉引誘那條狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c8c082e47323c2858b0","word":"bake","forms":["bake"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c18209c8b9931c7","term":"bake","forms":["bake","bakes","baking","baked","book","baken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"烤制食物","explanation":"指把食物放進烤箱，用熱力把它烤熟；也可以表示為別人烤某物。","examples":[{"en":"I baked a lemon cake for my sister.","zh":"我為姐姐烤了一個檸檬蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bake the vegetables until they are tender.","zh":"把蔬菜烤到變軟為止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-144ac86d05c00f559949","word":"bakery","forms":["bakery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92280280674ea146","term":"bakery","forms":["bakery","bakeries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麵包店；烘焙店","explanation":"指烘烤並通常也出售麵包、蛋糕、糕點等食品的地方，重點是“做或賣烘焙品的店”。","examples":[{"en":"I stopped by the bakery to buy a loaf of bread.","zh":"我順路去麵包店買了一條麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That bakery makes excellent cakes for birthdays.","zh":"那家烘焙店做的生日蛋糕非常好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bakery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5751e048eb6fee3eb9bb","word":"balance","forms":["balance"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cadacc43ae9de658","term":"balance","forms":["balance","balances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平衡；均勢","explanation":"指相反的力量、因素或部分彼此相稱，整體因此穩定、不偏向任何一邊。它可以是自然狀態，也可以是經過調整後達到的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The design achieves a balance between comfort and style.","zh":"這個設計在舒適與時尚之間取得了平衡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise helps me keep my balance.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於我保持平衡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a4f68d2ace12c25","term":"balance","forms":["balance","balances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餘額；借貸差額","explanation":"指賬戶中借項和貸項相抵後得到的結果，尤其常指銀行賬戶裡目前剩下的錢或可用金額。","examples":[{"en":"I checked my bank balance before paying the bill.","zh":"付款前我查了銀行賬戶餘額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The statement shows a remaining balance of eighty dollars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e80b96cdf06bfb8","term":"balance","forms":["balance","balances","balancing","balanced","balancest","balancedst","balanceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使穩住；把……放在支點上","explanation":"指把物體放在狹窄或不穩定的支點上，同時調整位置使它不掉落；這就是把“天平式平衡”用於單個物體。","examples":[{"en":"He balanced the tray on one hand.","zh":"他用一隻手託穩了托盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I balanced my phone on the edge of the desk.","zh":"我把手機小心地放在桌邊上使它保持不倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4095f603052daa790350","word":"balcony","forms":["balcony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-352fceba8f68c9fa","term":"balcony","forms":["balcony","balconies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築物外牆上的陽臺","explanation":"指從建築物外牆伸出去、可以走上去的平臺，通常位於窗戶或房間外面，供人站立、休息或觀看外面的景色。","examples":[{"en":"We had breakfast on the balcony and watched the city wake up.","zh":"我們在陽臺上吃早餐，看著城市甦醒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apartment has a small balcony overlooking the park.","zh":"這套公寓有一個俯瞰公園的小陽臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balcony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b220583d3360d1d","term":"balcony","forms":["balcony","balconies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劇院的樓座","explanation":"指劇院或類似場所中位於較高處、可以俯瞰舞臺的觀眾席區域；這裡不是建築物外牆上的私人陽臺，而是供觀眾看演出的高層座位。","examples":[{"en":"We found two cheap seats in the balcony for the evening show.","zh":"我們找到了兩張晚場演出的便宜樓座票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our seats in the balcony overlooked the orchestra.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balcony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62cc13e735700e53bee3","word":"bald","forms":["bald"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a5bedabb1d7afa5","term":"bald","forms":["bald","balder","baldest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"禿的；沒有毛髮的","explanation":"指頭髮、毛髮或羽毛很少，甚至完全沒有，核心畫面就是表面被剝光了。","examples":[{"en":"My uncle is bald.","zh":"我叔叔是禿頂的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He started going bald in his thirties.","zh":"他三十多歲時開始禿頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bald","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-088c2a72944f9fcf","term":"bald","forms":["bald","balder","baldest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"禿頂的","explanation":"專門指人的頭頂沒有頭髮，或頭頂有一大片裸露的頭皮；即使兩側還留著頭髮，也可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"The bald man with glasses is our teacher.","zh":"那個戴眼鏡的禿頂男人是我們的老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His grandfather was completely bald by forty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bald","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9de08263f4ad49131d3","word":"ball","forms":["ball"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb60555dbfd96a4d","term":"ball","forms":["ball","balls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球狀物","explanation":"指實心或空心的球體，或大致呈圓球狀的一團東西；核心概念就是“圓球”。","examples":[{"en":"The child made a ball of clay and placed it on the table.","zh":"孩子把黏土揉成一個球，放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small ball of paper blocked the drain.","zh":"一團小紙球堵住了下水道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f0a0f8ca5aa8b78","term":"ball","forms":["ball","balls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育比賽用球","explanation":"指足球、籃球、網球等運動或遊戲中被傳、接、踢、拍、擊打或追逐的球；不同運動的大小和材質可以不同。","examples":[{"en":"She kicked the ball into the corner of the net.","zh":"她把球踢進了球門的角落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pass me the ball.","zh":"請把球傳給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efb495e138bac770","term":"ball","forms":["ball","balls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式舞會","explanation":"指人們穿著較正式的服裝聚在一起跳舞和社交的正式活動；這是與“圓球”無關的獨立詞源義。","examples":[{"en":"They attended a charity ball at the city museum.","zh":"他們參加了在城市博物館舉行的慈善舞會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a new dress for the winter ball.","zh":"她為冬季舞會買了一條新裙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0b8c5a363cba987","term":"ball","forms":["ball","balls","balling","balled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揉成球狀","explanation":"把鬆散或柔軟的東西揉、卷或纏成一個圓球，正如把材料變成“圓球”。","examples":[{"en":"She balled the cotton into a small lump.","zh":"她把棉花揉成了一個小團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She balled the wet paper in her fist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24db8654347d2e3e5023","word":"ballet","forms":["ballet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e19b5366481152cc","term":"ballet","forms":["ballet","ballets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"古典芭蕾舞","explanation":"指一種強調姿態、腳步、身體控制和動作協調的古典舞蹈形式；這裡說的是舞蹈本身，而不是某一場演出。","examples":[{"en":"She started learning ballet when she was six.","zh":"她六歲時開始學習芭蕾舞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ballet requires strength, balance, and years of practice.","zh":"芭蕾舞需要力量、平衡能力和多年的練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9283d449783ef553","term":"ballet","forms":["ballet","ballets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"芭蕾舞劇或演出","explanation":"指由芭蕾舞蹈構成的舞臺演出，通常配有音樂，有時還透過舞蹈講述故事。","examples":[{"en":"We are going to see a ballet at the city theatre tonight.","zh":"我們今晚要去市劇院看一場芭蕾舞劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company premiered a ballet inspired by ocean currents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00477ad8a4431d45d6ea","word":"balloon","forms":["balloon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa8cd7f7fae496f7","term":"balloon","forms":["balloon","balloons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"充氣物；氣球","explanation":"一種充入空氣或其他氣體後會鼓起、通常還能浮起的柔軟物體；最典型的就是氣球。","examples":[{"en":"A red balloon floated above the crowd.","zh":"一個紅氣球飄在人群上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue team used a large balloon to lift the equipment.","zh":"救援隊用一個大型充氣物吊起裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balloon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f776e74e285f551e","term":"balloon","forms":["balloon","balloons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玩具或裝飾氣球","explanation":"指兒童玩具或聚會裝飾用的氣球，是普通生活中最常見的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"We hung colorful balloons around the room for the party.","zh":"我們為聚會在房間四周掛上了五顏六色的氣球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red balloon floated above the birthday table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balloon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22732000cdd4b3328093","word":"ballot","forms":["ballot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa111aea3d562d9c","term":"ballot","forms":["ballot","ballots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選票","explanation":"ballot 原本是投進容器、用來表示選擇的小球，現在通常指紙質選票、卡片，或任何用來表示投票選擇的方式。","examples":[{"en":"She cast her ballot before leaving for work.","zh":"她上班前投了票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your ballot must be signed and returned by Friday.","zh":"你的選票必須簽名並在星期五前交回。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6142b4305fde57c6","term":"ballot","forms":["ballot","ballots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投票；一輪投票","explanation":"ballot 也指透過選票進行的投票過程，尤其是秘密投票或某一輪表決；重點不再是紙張，而是“用選票作出選擇”這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The members approved the proposal in a secret ballot.","zh":"成員透過無記名投票批准了這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee will hold a ballot on the new rules.","zh":"委員會將就新規舉行投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a6fe0d4a1e8de1d","term":"ballot","forms":["ballot","ballots","balloting","balloted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投票；透過投票決定","explanation":"作動詞時，ballot 表示用選票投票，或透過投票來決定某位候選人、某項提案等；它正是“把選擇放進投票箱”這一核心畫面的動作化。","examples":[{"en":"Members will ballot for a new chair next week.","zh":"成員下週將投票選出新主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shareholders balloted on the merger.","zh":"股東就合併事項進行了投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-add1743eae5bbd8ea17b","word":"bamboo","forms":["bamboo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1b638f9ddee66e4","term":"bamboo","forms":["bamboo","bamboos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"竹子","explanation":"指一種生長很快的草本植物，莖中空、筆直並有明顯的節；這是 bamboo 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Bamboo grows quickly in warm, wet climates.","zh":"竹子在溫暖潮溼的氣候中生長得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tall bamboo was growing beside the path.","zh":"小路旁邊長著一株高高的竹子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bamboo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58bb31d11403763d","term":"bamboo","forms":["bamboo","bamboos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"竹材","explanation":"指從竹子取得的材料，可用於建築、傢俱和其他物品。","examples":[{"en":"The table is made of bamboo.","zh":"這張桌子是用竹材製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bamboo provides a strong, lightweight material for scaffolding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bamboo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":3,"counts":{"112":2,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-b2a96c3d3fc2b6accdb4","word":"ban","forms":["ban"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51cec0a944b3f1af","term":"ban","forms":["ban","bans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禁令","explanation":"ban 是由政府、機構、平臺等正式宣佈的禁止規定，即“某事不準做或某物不準使用”。","examples":[{"en":"The city introduced a ban on smoking in public parks.","zh":"這座城市出臺了禁止在公共公園吸菸的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ban will remain in place until next year.","zh":"這項禁令將持續到明年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ban","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7d528ca72f73882","term":"ban","forms":["ban","bans","banning","banned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"禁止","explanation":"ban 作動詞時，表示由機構、平臺或其他有權力的一方正式禁止某人、某行為或某物參與、使用或繼續存在。","examples":[{"en":"The school banned students from using phones during exams.","zh":"學校禁止學生在考試期間使用手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The platform banned the account for repeated violations.","zh":"該平臺因該賬號屢次違規而封禁了它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ban","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b493d48364afe44d11c0","word":"banana","forms":["banana"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-248e9e81217a9ae4","term":"banana","forms":["banana","bananas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香蕉","explanation":"指香蕉植株結出的細長彎曲熱帶水果，外皮通常光滑，果肉柔軟。既可以說一個香蕉，也可以泛指這種水果。","examples":[{"en":"I packed a banana for the train ride.","zh":"我帶了一個香蕉，在火車上吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sliced a banana into her oatmeal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65f15ce8fee25b248445","word":"band","forms":["band"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-341ad7f7092aaf83","term":"band","forms":["band","bands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶子；箍帶","explanation":"指用來加固、捆紮或連線物品的一條狹長材料，像把東西綁在一起的帶子。","examples":[{"en":"The box was held together with a strong metal band.","zh":"這個箱子用一條結實的金屬箍帶固定在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a silver band around her wrist.","zh":"她的手腕上戴著一條銀色帶子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/band","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57c3adf2d30f8b9b","term":"band","forms":["band","bands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紐帶；聯絡","explanation":"指把人或群體連線起來的關係或共同感情，是從“帶子把東西連在一起”引申出的抽象義。","examples":[{"en":"Shared memories created a strong band between the two friends.","zh":"共同的回憶在兩位朋友之間建立了牢固的紐帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ceremony strengthened the band between the community and the school.","zh":"這場儀式加強了社群與學校之間的聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/band","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53b8a2c6a7fda45f","term":"band","forms":["band","bands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂隊","explanation":"指一起排練、演出或錄音的音樂家團體，是“一群人被組織在一起”的具體例子。","examples":[{"en":"My brother plays drums in a local band.","zh":"我哥哥在一支本地樂隊裡打鼓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band is recording a new album this summer.","zh":"這支樂隊今年夏天正在錄製新專輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/band","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe4190c0bc0ee116b11c","word":"bandage","forms":["bandage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2290e9988d52f90","term":"bandage","forms":["bandage","bandages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繃帶","explanation":"包紮傷口或支撐受傷部位的布條，通常由紗布等材料製成。它的核心作用是把受傷處蓋住並保護起來。","examples":[{"en":"She put a clean bandage on the cut.","zh":"她在傷口上貼了一塊乾淨的繃帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bandage around his wrist was too tight.","zh":"他手腕上的繃帶太緊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bandage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-922212de6886e31f","term":"bandage","forms":["bandage","bandages","bandaging","bandaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用繃帶包紮","explanation":"把繃帶纏到傷口或受傷部位上，使其得到保護或支撐。這個動作義直接來自名詞“繃帶”。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse bandaged his ankle before he went home.","zh":"護士在他回家前給他的腳踝纏好了繃帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse bandaged his injured ankle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bandage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ae3d35454b6ddf20432","word":"bang","forms":["bang"],"officialPos":"n./v./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8bd8864462eb8b28","term":"bang","forms":["bang","bangs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巨響","explanation":"指突然、響亮的撞擊聲或類似的爆裂聲，來源可以是錘子敲擊、門猛關上等；它就是“猛地撞上去，砰的一聲”中的聲音。","examples":[{"en":"A loud bang came from the kitchen.","zh":"廚房裡傳來一聲巨響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard a bang upstairs and ran to look.","zh":"我們聽見樓上傳來一聲巨響，便跑去檢視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-993232790c15d913","term":"bang","forms":["bang","bangs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"齊劉海","explanation":"指從頭髮中剪出、整齊橫著垂在額頭前的部分；這是由“切得整齊、橫著落下”的形狀引申出來的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She cut her bangs just above her eyebrows.","zh":"她把齊劉海剪在眉毛上方一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her bangs kept falling into her eyes.","zh":"她的齊劉海總是垂到眼睛裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a8d1f79d5c9a714","term":"bang","forms":["bang","bangs","banging","banged","bangest","bangedst","bangeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出巨響","explanation":"表示突然或反覆發出很大的撞擊聲、爆炸聲等，就像猛地撞上去後連續響起“砰砰”聲。","examples":[{"en":"The fireworks banged away all through the night.","zh":"煙花整夜不停地砰砰作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Something banged loudly against the window.","zh":"有什麼東西重重地撞在窗戶上，發出巨響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4381dc2ab14285160c80","word":"bank","forms":["bank"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c54845db0e4d669c","term":"bank","forms":["bank","banks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銀行","explanation":"bank最常見的意思是銀行：人們可以在那裡存錢、借錢，並辦理轉賬、付款等金融事務。記憶時可以把櫃檯想成“有邊有臺的一塊隆起”，資金和服務都集中在這張“臺”後面。","examples":[{"en":"I went to the bank to open a savings account.","zh":"我去銀行開了一個儲蓄賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bank approved her loan application.","zh":"銀行批准了她的貸款申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-202065edf16750c2","term":"bank","forms":["bank","banks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"河岸；湖岸","explanation":"bank可以指河流、湖泊或其他水道邊緣的陸地，也就是水邊那條“有邊有臺的隆起”。","examples":[{"en":"We had a picnic on the bank of the river.","zh":"我們在河岸邊野餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were playing near the lake bank.","zh":"孩子們在湖岸附近玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e464e97a2800ad8","term":"bank","forms":["bank","banks","banking","banked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辦理銀行業務","explanation":"表示個人或機構與銀行往來、使用銀行服務；可以把它記成站在“櫃檯邊”辦理資金事務。","examples":[{"en":"I bank with a local credit union.","zh":"我在當地一家信用合作社辦理銀行業務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bank online because the nearest branch closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94bc876841511b31","term":"bank","forms":["bank","banks","banking","banked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"飛機側傾轉彎","explanation":"指飛機向一側傾斜，以便完成轉彎；可以想象飛機沿著一塊斜坡側傾過去。","examples":[{"en":"The plane banked sharply to avoid the storm.","zh":"飛機猛地向一側傾斜，避開了暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We banked left as we approached the runway.","zh":"我們接近跑道時向左側傾斜轉彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-397e53a194b68b89e0a4","word":"banker","forms":["banker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b8d15d8f9e699ae","term":"banker","forms":["banker","bankers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銀行家","explanation":"指經營銀行業務、管理存款和貸款，或從事資金、票據等金融交易的人。它通常比“銀行職員”範圍更窄，強調金融業務的經營或管理角色。","examples":[{"en":"Her father is a banker in London.","zh":"她父親是倫敦的一名銀行家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The banker approved the company's loan.","zh":"銀行家批准了這家公司的貸款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dce8dd0d3634884","term":"banker","forms":["banker","bankers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賭場莊家","explanation":"指賭場或某種賭博遊戲中代表莊家、負責收取和支付賭注的人。","examples":[{"en":"The banker dealt the cards and collected the losing bets.","zh":"莊家發牌，並收取輸掉的賭注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The banker dealt another hand of baccarat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a1298a317a3ba845cdd","word":"bankrupt","forms":["bankrupt"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-47fc063ade86db2c","term":"bankrupt","forms":["bankrupt","more bankrupt","most bankrupt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"破產的；無力償債的","explanation":"指個人或企業已經無力支付到期債務、履行財務責任；在法律語境中，也可指已經被正式宣佈破產。它保留了“錢路斷了、長凳被砸壞”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The company went bankrupt after losing its biggest customer.","zh":"這家公司失去最大的客戶後破產了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bankrupt shop could not pay its suppliers.","zh":"那家破產的商店無法支付供應商的款項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bankrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d5131707bc9dfa8","term":"bankrupt","forms":["bankrupt","more bankrupt","most bankrupt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"徹底缺乏某種品質的","explanation":"用於比喻某人、組織或制度完全缺乏本應具有的道德、思想或其他重要品質。就像破產者沒有可用的錢一樣，這裡強調某種價值已經“空了”。","examples":[{"en":"The scandal revealed a morally bankrupt leadership.","zh":"這起醜聞暴露出這個領導層在道德上已經徹底失守。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The regime was morally bankrupt long before it collapsed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bankrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c7ed2d9be59e21cf7cf","word":"banner","forms":["banner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f7b011286fdb923","term":"banner","forms":["banner","banners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旗幟","explanation":"banner是懸掛、舉起或插在旗杆上的大旗，常用來表示某個國家、組織、軍隊或統治者的身份。","examples":[{"en":"A green banner flew above the entrance to the school.","zh":"學校入口上方飄著一面綠色旗幟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red banner fluttered above the castle gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05b8320681cb7a7d","term":"banner","forms":["banner","banners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大幅標牌或橫幅","explanation":"banner也可以是不一定有旗杆的大幅布質或軟材料標牌，用來讓遠處的人看見資訊或慶祝內容。","examples":[{"en":"The town hung a banner across the street for the festival.","zh":"小鎮為節日在街道上方懸掛了一條橫幅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A banner over the entrance welcomed the returning sailors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb96f3b575737c09","term":"banner","forms":["banner","banners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旗號；事業","explanation":"從“聚集在一面旗幟下”引申而來，banner可以指一個人或團體所支援的事業、目標或社會運動。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers worked under the banner of clean water for every family.","zh":"志願者們以讓每個家庭都用上清潔用水為目標開展工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several charities united under the banner of child welfare.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4549a19d61970efe812","word":"banquet","forms":["banquet"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05f9dae9165fa246","term":"banquet","forms":["banquet","banquets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盛大的慶祝宴席","explanation":"指為慶祝某件事而準備的豐盛大餐，重點是食物豐富、場面隆重，常有許多人參加。","examples":[{"en":"The town held a banquet to celebrate the team's victory.","zh":"鎮裡舉行了一場盛宴，慶祝球隊獲勝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the ceremony, the guests sat down to a lavish banquet.","zh":"儀式結束後，賓客們坐下來享用豐盛的宴席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banquet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71381e88e18375ee","term":"banquet","forms":["banquet","banquets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"多人參加的正式宴會","explanation":"強調這是為許多人安排的正式晚宴或慶典聚餐；它既可以指宴席，也可以指圍繞這頓飯舉行的社交活動。","examples":[{"en":"Delegates from twenty countries attended the opening banquet.","zh":"來自二十個國家的代表參加了開幕宴會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The visiting delegates attended a banquet that evening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banquet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e64577bf4286148","term":"banquet","forms":["banquet","banquets","banqueting","banquetting","banqueted","banquetted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"赴宴；盡情吃喝","explanation":"指參加 banquet 並享用其中的豐盛食物，也就是在宴席上盡情吃喝。","examples":[{"en":"The guests banqueted with the mayor late into the evening.","zh":"賓客們和市長一起赴宴，直到深夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The victorious soldiers banqueted late into the night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banquet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcde2b2edba56bf40860","word":"bar","forms":["bar"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-262f11f2fed45d5f","term":"bar","forms":["bar","bars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"杆；條","explanation":"bar 最基本的形象是一根長度明顯大於寬度的硬直物，通常由木頭或金屬製成；它就像橫在路上的那根杆。","examples":[{"en":"The window has strong steel bars across it.","zh":"窗戶上橫著結實的鋼條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He lifted the heavy bar above his head.","zh":"他把那根沉重的槓桿舉過頭頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4d2e89902ed7a5d","term":"bar","forms":["bar","bars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒吧","explanation":"bar 可以指供應酒精飲料、供顧客在店內飲用的場所；它也常泛指這種店鋪本身。這個場所仍然保留著“橫向櫃檯”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"We met at a small bar near the station.","zh":"我們在車站附近的一家小酒吧碰面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That bar stays open until two in the morning.","zh":"那家酒吧一直營業到凌晨兩點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13f9c47c7c0f71bf","term":"bar","forms":["bar","bars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"障礙；阻礙","explanation":"bar 可以是實際或抽象的障礙，擋住人、行動或目標；這正是“橫在路上的杆”最直接的引申。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of money was the biggest bar to their plans.","zh":"缺錢是他們計劃面臨的最大障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing should be a bar to a child's education.","zh":"任何事情都不應成為孩子接受教育的障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0fd697d0008d7cf","term":"bar","forms":["bar","bars","barring","barred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"阻擋通行","explanation":"bar 表示把人或物擋在路上，使其無法透過；就像一根橫在路上的杆，直接截住前進的方向。","examples":[{"en":"A fallen tree barred the road.","zh":"一棵倒下的樹擋住了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The locked gate barred us from entering the garden.","zh":"鎖著的大門擋住了我們進入花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf8108731757e7da3594","word":"barbarian","forms":["barbarian"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68186e9f21ccf0d0","term":"barbarian","forms":["barbarian"],"pos":"adj","zh":"野蠻的；不文明的","explanation":"形容某個人、社會或習俗被認為缺乏文明、文化或應有的行為規範，核心畫面就是“站在文明城牆外、只靠蠻力生活”。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers were shocked by the barbarian customs they encountered.","zh":"士兵們對遇到的野蠻習俗感到震驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The invading army's barbarian cruelty terrified the villagers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbarian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28da2d95e27be593","term":"barbarian","forms":["barbarian","barbarians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"野蠻人；粗野無文化的人","explanation":"指被認為沒有文明教養、只會依靠蠻力解決問題的人，是從“城牆外的野蠻者”這一核心畫面發展出的主要名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Anyone who enjoys hurting helpless animals is a barbarian.","zh":"喜歡傷害無助動物的人就是野蠻人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers regarded the raiders as barbarians.","zh":"村民們把那些襲擊者視為野蠻人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbarian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f1270d146272da7","term":"barbarian","forms":["barbarian","barbarians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殘暴無情的人","explanation":"指特別殘忍、野蠻、具有攻擊性且缺乏同情心的人；這裡“城外的野蠻者”進一步突出為會傷害他人的暴徒。","examples":[{"en":"The murderer was described as a heartless barbarian.","zh":"那個殺人犯被形容為一個冷酷無情的野蠻人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a barbarian would deliberately destroy those irreplaceable paintings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbarian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab5c95d2cc5bf9000e8d","word":"barbecue","forms":["barbecue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ea946ebf9c81d59","term":"barbecue","forms":["barbecue","barbecues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燒烤架；燒烤爐","explanation":"指通常在戶外使用、以炭火等高溫熱源烤食物的裝置，可以是燒烤架，也可以是燒烤坑或爐。","examples":[{"en":"We cooked our vegetables on the barbecue.","zh":"我們在燒烤架上烤了蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clean the barbecue before lighting the charcoal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b75caced0f17b9de","term":"barbecue","forms":["barbecue","barbecues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燒烤聚會","explanation":"指以燒烤食物為中心的一頓飯或社交活動，通常在戶外舉行，也可以泛指這類聚餐。","examples":[{"en":"We're having a barbecue in the garden on Sunday.","zh":"我們星期天要在花園裡舉行燒烤聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our neighbors invited us to a barbecue on Sunday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b8c2e6e4d112eaa","term":"barbecue","forms":["barbecue","barbecues","barbecuing","barbecueing","barbecued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"燒烤；煙燻","explanation":"指把食物放在 barbecue 上烤，或用煙和間接熱量慢慢把食物燻熟。","examples":[{"en":"He barbecued the chicken slowly over indirect heat.","zh":"他用間接熱量慢慢煙燻雞肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We barbecued the ribs slowly over applewood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barbecue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b67b8e2e8472a0a87a3d","word":"barber","forms":["barber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dc9685c5ea69fd1","term":"barber","forms":["barber","barbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理髮師","explanation":"理髮師就是用剪刀、剃刀等工具為顧客剪頭髮、修剪鬍鬚的人；這個職業正是整個詞的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I have an appointment with the barber this afternoon.","zh":"我今天下午和理髮師約好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The barber trimmed his beard and cut his hair.","zh":"理髮師給他修了鬍鬚，還剪了頭髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b828d53402d6e332ef0","word":"bare","forms":["bare"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b3b3caf5b56294a","term":"bare","forms":["bare","barer","barest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最低限度的","explanation":"表示數量或條件只達到最低要求，剛剛夠用，幾乎沒有餘量。","examples":[{"en":"The proposal passed by a bare majority.","zh":"這項提案以勉強過半的多數票透過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We packed only the bare essentials for the trip.","zh":"我們只為這次旅行收拾了最基本的必需品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd231cd5b699db1a","term":"bare","forms":["bare","barer","barest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"裸露的","explanation":"指身體或表面沒有衣物、遮蓋物保護，直接暴露出來。","examples":[{"en":"She walked across the grass in her bare feet.","zh":"她光著腳走過草地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not touch the hot pan with your bare hands.","zh":"不要徒手碰那個熱鍋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3034d3087e6ae3c8","term":"bare","forms":["bare","bares","baring","bared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭露；使裸露","explanation":"表示把原本遮住的身體、牙齒、事實或情緒露出來，正是把覆蓋物剝開的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The dog bared its teeth when I came closer.","zh":"我靠近時，那條狗露出了牙齒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finally bared her feelings to her friend.","zh":"她終於向朋友袒露了自己的感受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-cd288d089e5ae48fc845","word":"barely","forms":["barely"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a897e87df9ae568","term":"barely","forms":["barely","more barely","most barely"],"pos":"adv","zh":"勉強；差一點沒能","explanation":"表示某件事最終做到了，但只是在最低限度上做到，幾乎就要失敗或不夠了。","examples":[{"en":"I barely caught the last train.","zh":"我勉強趕上了末班車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She barely passed the exam.","zh":"她勉強透過了考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de17c6f76c9a4f08","term":"barely","forms":["barely","more barely","most barely"],"pos":"adv","zh":"幾乎不；幾乎沒有","explanation":"表示某種動作、感覺或數量接近於零，實際上幾乎沒有發生或幾乎不存在。","examples":[{"en":"I could barely hear him over the noise.","zh":"噪聲太大了，我幾乎聽不見他說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was barely enough food for everyone.","zh":"食物幾乎不夠每個人吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-60bca9331d028dd7de2f","word":"bargain","forms":["bargain"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1acef9f324d6f802","term":"bargain","forms":["bargain","bargains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交易協議；契約","explanation":"指交易雙方就財產、服務和代價達成的正式約定，重點是雙方都作出承諾並受約束。它是交易桌上“談妥並定下來”的那份協議。","examples":[{"en":"The written agreement turned their bargain into a legally binding contract.","zh":"書面協議把他們達成的交易約定變成了具有法律約束力的合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They sealed the bargain with a handshake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bargain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48e6fd57abd56f81","term":"bargain","forms":["bargain","bargains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"便宜貨；低價買到的東西","explanation":"指以明顯低於通常價格的錢買到的東西，核心是這次交易讓買方覺得“撿到了便宜”。它可以指商品本身，也可以指買到它這一結果。","examples":[{"en":"This jacket was a real bargain at half the original price.","zh":"這件夾克只賣原價的一半，真是撿了個大便宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sturdy desk was a bargain at twenty dollars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bargain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a22a2fc1a906a27c","term":"bargain","forms":["bargain","bargains","bargaining","bargained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"討價還價；協商交易","explanation":"指交易前後不斷談價格、條件或交換內容，直到雙方接受一個方案；畫面就是交易桌前把條件談攏。","examples":[{"en":"She bargained with the seller until he lowered the price.","zh":"她一直和賣家討價還價，直到他把價格降了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They bargained over the terms of the deal for an hour.","zh":"他們花了一個小時就這筆交易的條件討價還價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bargain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14ea6507645c2ba7e973","word":"bark","forms":["bark"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f26b3dec94b1989f","term":"bark","forms":["bark","barks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狗等動物的吠聲","explanation":"指狗、狐狸等動物突然發出的短促而響亮的叫聲；這是 bark 最常見的名詞義之一。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden bark woke the baby.","zh":"一聲突然的狗叫把嬰兒吵醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard the bark of a fox in the woods.","zh":"我們聽見樹林裡傳來狐狸的叫聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-717715a1b945c0d4","term":"bark","forms":["bark","barks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樹皮","explanation":"指覆蓋在樹幹和樹枝外面的保護層，是 bark 作為名詞的另一核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"The bark of this tree is unusually smooth.","zh":"這棵樹的樹皮異常光滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children collected pieces of bark from the ground.","zh":"孩子們從地上撿了幾片樹皮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e49a0a9ea932246","term":"bark","forms":["bark","barks","barking","barked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吠叫","explanation":"指狗等動物發出短促、響亮的叫聲；這是動詞 bark 最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The dog barked at the mail carrier.","zh":"那條狗衝著送信員叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dogs often bark when they hear strange noises.","zh":"狗聽到奇怪的聲音時常常會叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f7addc0c99c22f2","term":"bark","forms":["bark","barks","barking","barked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"厲聲說話或下令","explanation":"把人說話的方式比作狗叫，表示用短促、尖厲、命令式的口氣說出話來。","examples":[{"en":"The coach barked an order at the players.","zh":"教練衝著隊員厲聲下令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He barked at me to move aside.","zh":"他厲聲叫我讓開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e43a7ece3a362be44a9e","word":"barn","forms":["barn"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc23ab08584cc748","term":"barn","forms":["barn","barns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穀倉；牲畜棚","explanation":"指農場中用來存放糧食、乾草等物品，或飼養牛等牲畜的大型建築。可以把它想成農場裡把糧食和動物安置在一起的寬敞棚屋。","examples":[{"en":"The cows are resting in the barn.","zh":"奶牛正在牲畜棚裡休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stored the hay in the barn before the storm.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，我們把乾草存進了穀倉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4e8236fa1d1702e","term":"barn","forms":["barn","barns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育場館","explanation":"非正式地指體育比賽或大型活動的場館，尤其是讓人聯想到寬敞、結實、能容納很多人的地方。它是從“寬大的棚屋”這個形象引申出來的。","examples":[{"en":"The team always plays better in this old barn.","zh":"這支隊總是在這座老體育館裡發揮得更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans packed the old hockey barn for the playoff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e8bbe6423a622988680d","word":"barrel","forms":["barrel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae90d6e39f5167c6","term":"barrel","forms":["barrel","barrels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"桶；圓筒形容器","explanation":"指中間鼓起、兩端較平的圓筒形容器，傳統上常由木板和箍製成，也可以由金屬等材料製成。","examples":[{"en":"They stored the wine in a wooden barrel.","zh":"他們把葡萄酒儲存在一個木桶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers rolled a barrel across the yard.","zh":"工人們把一個桶滾過院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad20a291a211c2ae","term":"barrel","forms":["barrel","barrels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一桶的量","explanation":"指一個完整桶所能裝的數量，而不是桶這個容器本身；具體容量會隨地區、商品和規定而變化。","examples":[{"en":"The farm produces several barrels of apple cider each autumn.","zh":"這家農場每年秋天都會生產幾桶蘋果酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brewery sold a barrel of beer to the local pub.","zh":"這家釀酒廠賣給當地酒吧一桶啤酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72c0c8f6f0759124f4f5","word":"barren","forms":["barren"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef9c15ee86741d91","term":"barren","forms":["barren","barrener","more barren","barrenest","most barren"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不能生育的","explanation":"形容人或動物不能生育，像一塊無法孕育生命的土地；也可表示沒有子女。","examples":[{"en":"The couple learned that she was barren.","zh":"這對夫妻得知她無法生育。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The barren ewe failed to produce a lamb for three seasons.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barren","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4672b69ffb3cb663","term":"barren","forms":["barren","barrener","more barren","barrenest","most barren"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貧瘠荒蕪的","explanation":"形容土地缺乏肥力，難以長出植被或供人耕種，因此顯得荒涼、無人居住。","examples":[{"en":"Only a few tough grasses grow on the barren hillside.","zh":"只有幾叢耐旱的草長在那片貧瘠的山坡上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The expedition crossed a vast, barren plain.","zh":"探險隊穿過了一片廣闊而荒蕪的平原。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barren","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49543885bacb2607","term":"barren","forms":["barren","barrener","more barren","barrenest","most barren"],"pos":"adj","zh":"缺乏……的","explanation":"引申指某事物像貧瘠土地一樣缺少某種內容、資源或有用的東西，常表示整體上沒有產出。","examples":[{"en":"The report was barren of useful evidence.","zh":"這份報告沒有提供任何有用的證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speech was barren of practical suggestions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barren","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0dc3075f012ecffa922","word":"barrier","forms":["barrier"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-501baf2658145605","term":"barrier","forms":["barrier","barriers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"屏障；隔離設施","explanation":"指橫在道路、入口或兩個區域之間、用來阻擋通行的實體設施，就是記憶中的那扇“擋路的門”。","examples":[{"en":"The security barrier opened when the car approached.","zh":"汽車駛近時，安全閘門開啟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A glass barrier separates the pool from the walkway.","zh":"一道玻璃隔欄把游泳池和走道隔開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2911bcb4a06ff356","term":"barrier","forms":["barrier","barriers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"障礙；阻礙","explanation":"指擋住某人做成某事或獲得某物的因素，可以是費用、語言、恐懼等抽象事物；它們像一扇看不見的門，阻止人繼續前進。","examples":[{"en":"The cost of childcare is a major barrier to returning to work.","zh":"托兒費用是重返工作崗位的一大障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Language barriers made it difficult for the visitors to ask for help.","zh":"語言障礙讓遊客很難尋求幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cae662172fd450bb0cd7","word":"base","forms":["base"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90fd053084c56c75","term":"base","forms":["base","bases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基礎；根基","explanation":"指支撐其他事物的最下面、最穩固的部分，可以是建築的根基，也可以泛指某種事物賴以存在或發展的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The statue stands on a solid stone base.","zh":"這座雕像立在堅固的石基上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trust is the base of a good friendship.","zh":"信任是良好友誼的基礎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/base","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c53286e82982b80","term":"base","forms":["base","bases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"依據；出發點","explanation":"指進行推理、判斷或思考時所依靠的出發點，就像從一個穩固支撐點向外展開思路。","examples":[{"en":"The report gives us a base for further discussion.","zh":"這份報告為我們進一步討論提供了依據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made her decision on the base of reliable evidence.","zh":"她根據可靠證據作出了決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/base","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d305c6adbfaf03dd","term":"base","forms":["base","bases","basing","based"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……設在某地","explanation":"把人員、團隊、公司或活動安排在某地作為固定駐地；這個地點就是它開展活動的“基地”。","examples":[{"en":"The company is based in London but has offices around the world.","zh":"這家公司總部設在倫敦，但在世界各地都有辦事處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are basing the research team at the university this summer.","zh":"今年夏天我們把研究團隊安排在這所大學駐紮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/base","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a01edad91c00abe7be5b","word":"baseball","forms":["baseball"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb3e9f7e51e3c66b","term":"baseball","forms":["baseball","baseballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棒球運動","explanation":"一種用球棒擊球、讓隊員依次繞四個壘跑動得分的團隊運動。日常說 baseball，通常首先指這項運動，而不是單獨的一隻球。","examples":[{"en":"My friends play baseball every Sunday.","zh":"我的朋友們每個星期天都打棒球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a baseball game after dinner.","zh":"我們晚飯後看了一場棒球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baseball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f094b00d64c66a7","term":"baseball","forms":["baseball","baseballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棒球","explanation":"指打棒球時使用的那隻球，是一個具體的圓球。這個意思是從“棒球運動”縮小到運動器材本身。","examples":[{"en":"A baseball broke the window during practice.","zh":"練習時，一隻棒球打破了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A baseball shattered the neighbor's greenhouse window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baseball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6f91dfd2c7321f316bc","word":"basement","forms":["basement"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ff08d40cb3131f9","term":"basement","forms":["basement","basements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地下室；地下層","explanation":"指建築物中低於地面的一層或幾層，通常用於儲物、裝置、洗衣或居住等用途。它是 basement 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We keep the old furniture in the basement.","zh":"我們把舊傢俱放在地下室裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The basement apartment has a small window near the ceiling.","zh":"那套地下室公寓在靠近天花板的地方有一扇小窗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7eaee599e49c4030","term":"basement","forms":["basement","basements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地下室的省略說法","explanation":"這是在上下文已經明確時對建築物地下層的省略或簡略用法，意思仍然圍繞“地下室”這一核心概念，並不是另一種樓層。","examples":[{"en":"The laundry room is in the basement, next to the stairs.","zh":"洗衣房在地下室裡，就在樓梯旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stored the spare chairs in the basement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fbb7b5bf4ca348eeeebf","word":"basic","forms":["basic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9449c0594b3edb8e","term":"basic","forms":["basic","more basic","most basic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基礎且必需的","explanation":"像地基一樣，是某種事物能夠成立或運作所不可缺少的部分；重點是“必要”，不只是“簡單”。","examples":[{"en":"Clean water is a basic necessity for every community.","zh":"清潔的水是每個社群不可缺少的基本需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Flour is a basic ingredient in most breads.","zh":"麵粉是大多數麵包中不可缺少的基本原料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f09fd2b882e5eef","term":"basic","forms":["basic","more basic","most basic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基本的；簡單實用的","explanation":"指只包含最基礎、最實用的內容，像剛搭好的地基，功能夠用但沒有複雜或豪華的部分。","examples":[{"en":"The cabin is basic, but it has everything we need.","zh":"這間小屋很簡陋，但有我們需要的一切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This course teaches the basic principles of photography.","zh":"這門課講授攝影的基本原理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad5fb69f39914e76d1f1","word":"basics","forms":["basics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"basics","forms":["basics"],"pos":"n.","zh":"基本知識；基礎","examples":[{"en":"This course teaches the basics of computer programming.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"You should master the basics before attempting the advanced exercises.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-163834bf87e4f8bcb9bc","word":"basin","forms":["basin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e589e352e143c43","term":"basin","forms":["basin","basins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬口盆","explanation":"basin 是一種寬而淺的盆，常用於洗手、洗臉或盛水，有時固定在牆上。它保留了“把水收在裡面”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She filled the basin with warm water and washed her face.","zh":"她把盆裝滿溫水，洗了洗臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old bathroom still has a porcelain basin fixed to the wall.","zh":"那間舊浴室裡仍有一個固定在牆上的瓷洗臉盆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b05c29da7351a04f","term":"basin","forms":["basin","basins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流域","explanation":"在地理學中，basin 是一片向同一個出口排水的土地，也就是一個共同匯水的流域。這裡的“盆”不再是容器，而是由地形把水導向同一處的大片區域。","examples":[{"en":"The river basin supports farms, forests, and several growing towns.","zh":"這個流域養育了農田、森林和幾座不斷發展的城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rainfall flooded villages throughout the river basin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7a3c8f654761303e495","word":"basis","forms":["basis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb09d97df2a2b71f","term":"basis","forms":["basis","bases","baseis","basises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀點或論證的依據","explanation":"指一個觀點、判斷、猜測或論證賴以成立的事實和理由。也就是把“地基”從建築物引申到思想：沒有這個依據，結論就站不住。","examples":[{"en":"There is no basis for blaming her without more evidence.","zh":"沒有更多證據，就沒有理由責怪她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal is based on a careful study of local needs.","zh":"這項提議以對當地需求的仔細研究為依據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa76d99ad957d952fb37","word":"basket","forms":["basket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2ffbbc567319f2c","term":"basket","forms":["basket","baskets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"籃子；筐","explanation":"一種通常較輕、頂部敞開的容器，用來裝東西；形狀常像上寬下窄的籃子或筐。","examples":[{"en":"She carried a basket of apples into the kitchen.","zh":"她提著一籃蘋果走進廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the towels in the laundry basket.","zh":"把毛巾放進洗衣籃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4d15669e5526951","term":"basket","forms":["basket","baskets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"購物籃","explanation":"商店裡用來裝準備購買的物品的金屬絲或塑膠容器，通常由顧客手提。","examples":[{"en":"I grabbed a basket before entering the supermarket.","zh":"我進超市前拿了一個購物籃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She removed the duplicate item from her online basket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd2ed8fccf246f28","term":"basket","forms":["basket","baskets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"籃筐","explanation":"籃球場上帶有籃網的圓環，球員要把球投進其中。","examples":[{"en":"The guard drove to the basket and passed to his teammate.","zh":"後衛突破到籃筐附近，把球傳給了隊友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ball bounced off the rim instead of going into the basket.","zh":"球彈離了籃圈，沒有進籃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f02c96357481972443a2","word":"basketball","forms":["basketball"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec9f37785c0297ab","term":"basketball","forms":["basketball","basketballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"籃球運動","explanation":"由兩隊參加、透過把球投入籃筐來得分的運動；這裡說的是這項運動本身，而不是某一個球。","examples":[{"en":"My sister plays basketball after school.","zh":"我姐姐放學後打籃球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched basketball on television last night.","zh":"我們昨晚在電視上看了籃球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basketball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0a459a42de448d2","term":"basketball","forms":["basketball","basketballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"籃球","explanation":"指打籃球時使用的那個球，是一種通常有彈性的圓球。","examples":[{"en":"There is a basketball under the table.","zh":"桌子下面有一個籃球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The basketball bounced beneath a parked car.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basketball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-441349e1ec2f7fd0aa17","word":"bass","forms":["bass"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a14495c08af66d1","term":"bass","forms":["bass","basser","bassest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"低音的；低沉的","explanation":"形容聲音或樂器的音高較低，聽起來比普通說話聲或高音更沉、更厚。它是“低音”這條主線的形容詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The singer has a deep bass voice.","zh":"這位歌手有一副深沉的低音嗓音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bass notes made the floor vibrate.","zh":"低音讓地板都震動起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ebc5293a61e42545","term":"bass","forms":["bass","basses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低音；低頻音","explanation":"指音域較低的一組聲音或音調，尤其是音樂、錄音和音響中的低頻部分。它是“低沉的聲音”這個核心概念本身。","examples":[{"en":"I turned down the bass because the music sounded muddy.","zh":"我把低音調小了，因為音樂聽起來渾濁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Turn down the bass; the windows are vibrating.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca5bcec12f716f44d974","word":"bat","forms":["bat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1abc60f74bf501f1","term":"bat","forms":["bat","bats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蝙蝠","explanation":"bat指一種通常在夜間飛行的哺乳動物，許多種類以昆蟲或果實為食。記住夜裡飛行的“蝙蝠”這個畫面，就能掌握它最常見的動物義。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a bat flying around the garden at dusk.","zh":"黃昏時我們看見一隻蝙蝠在花園上空飛來飛去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bats often come out at night to look for food.","zh":"蝙蝠常在夜間出來覓食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa38c25bb5117fba","term":"bat","forms":["bat","bats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球棒","explanation":"bat指棒球、壘球、板球等運動中用來擊球的球棒，正是手中揮動的“球棒”這個核心畫面。不同運動的球棒形狀和材料可能不同，但共同作用都是擊球。","examples":[{"en":"She picked up the bat and stepped into the batter's box.","zh":"她拿起球棒，走進了擊球區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach checked the bat before the game began.","zh":"比賽開始前，教練檢查了球棒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c35c879efe1b48e3","term":"bat","forms":["bat","bats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擊球機會；一輪擊球","explanation":"在球類比賽中，bat還可以指某人輪到用球棒擊球的一次機會或一段擊球時間。它由“球棒”這個具體物件引申而來，重點變成“輪到你揮棒”。","examples":[{"en":"It is my turn now—can I have a bat?","zh":"現在輪到我了——我可以擊一輪球嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He had a short bat before the rain stopped the match.","zh":"他剛擊了一小輪球，比賽就因下雨中止了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00f28ce9bd204401","term":"bat","forms":["bat","bats","batting","batted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用球棒擊打","explanation":"把球棒這個核心畫面直接變成動作，表示用球棒擊打某物，也可以比喻像揮棒一樣把某物開啟或打走。","examples":[{"en":"She batted the ball over the fence.","zh":"她用球棒把球擊過了圍欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child batted every pitch into the net.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4bb24efc9641afc5ded1","word":"batch","forms":["batch"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6bb0222ffc2ba65","term":"batch","forms":["batch","batches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次烘烤的一批食品","explanation":"指一次放進烤箱或類似裝置、同時做出來的一批麵包、餅乾等烘焙食品。這是 batch 最具體、也最容易幫助記憶的意義。","examples":[{"en":"I baked a batch of cookies for the children.","zh":"我為孩子們烤了一批餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This recipe makes two batches of bread rolls.","zh":"這個食譜能做兩批小麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-accd1276a1122ae6","term":"batch","forms":["batch","batches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次生產或產出的一批","explanation":"從“一次烤出一批食品”擴充套件而來，指任何一次操作中生產、得到或發放的一定數量的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The machine produces a fresh batch of ice cubes every hour.","zh":"這臺機器每小時生產一批新冰塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bakery discarded a batch of burnt rolls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0de8ab6315488d30b61d","word":"bath","forms":["bath"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b6bb54b1191c07c","term":"bath","forms":["bath","baths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"浴缸；浴池","explanation":"指用來洗澡的容器或水池，是“把人浸在水裡清洗”這一核心場景中最具體的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The children are playing in the bath.","zh":"孩子們正在浴缸裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a larger bath for the new bathroom.","zh":"我們需要給新浴室換一個更大的浴缸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a8c1b3f9995cc1a","term":"bath","forms":["bath","baths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洗澡；一次洗浴","explanation":"指洗澡這一行為或一次洗澡，是從浴缸、浴池這一具體場景自然延伸出的活動義。","examples":[{"en":"I usually have a bath before bed.","zh":"我通常睡前洗個澡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby needs a warm bath.","zh":"寶寶需要洗個溫水澡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2520ca0043ee42af4fe7","word":"bathe","forms":["bathe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ac972a995eaaf21","term":"bathe","forms":["bathe","bathes","bathing","bathed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洗澡；沐浴","explanation":"指自己把身體浸入水中或用水清潔身體，也就是洗澡、沐浴；核心畫面是讓水接觸幷包住身體。","examples":[{"en":"She bathed in the warm water after the long journey.","zh":"長途旅行後，她在溫水中洗了澡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bathed before sitting down to dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bathe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e393f9289e1751b5","term":"bathe","forms":["bathe","bathes","bathing","bathed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在水中游泳或浸泡","explanation":"指為了享受或恢復精神而把自己或身體的一部分浸在水裡，也就是下水游泳或泡在水中；重點不一定是清潔。","examples":[{"en":"The children bathed in the river all afternoon.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在河裡游泳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bathed in the warm lagoon until sunset.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bathe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aed866d356b0eb8e","term":"bathe","forms":["bathe","bathes","bathing","bathed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"籠罩；包圍","explanation":"用於比喻時，表示光線、顏色、氣氛等像水一樣包圍並覆蓋某處或某物，例如月光籠罩房間。","examples":[{"en":"The garden was bathed in soft evening light.","zh":"花園籠罩在柔和的暮光中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old street was bathed in golden sunlight.","zh":"老街沐浴在金色的陽光中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bathe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3486577cd905f87072a2","word":"bathroom","forms":["bathroom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00b273eb8ebe2de9","term":"bathroom","forms":["bathroom","bathrooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"浴室；衛生間","explanation":"指家中或公共建築裡供人洗澡、洗漱的房間，通常有淋浴間或浴缸，也常設有廁所。這個詞的核心畫面就是“用於洗澡的房間”。","examples":[{"en":"I left my towel in the bathroom.","zh":"我把毛巾落在衛生間了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are brushing their teeth in the bathroom.","zh":"孩子們正在衛生間刷牙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bathroom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9fc7780ad8681054","term":"bathroom","forms":["bathroom","bathrooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廁所；洗手間","explanation":"在一些英語地區，bathroom 也常用來委婉地表示“廁所”，即使說話人實際主要是要使用馬桶，而不是洗澡。它仍然保留“衛生間這個房間”的整體概念。","examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, could you tell me where the bathroom is?","zh":"不好意思，請問洗手間在哪裡？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Excuse me, where is the nearest bathroom?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bathroom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c83805b8676c466d0c5","word":"batter","forms":["batter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6569e5da8945d6e3","term":"batter","forms":["batter","batters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麵糊","explanation":"把麵粉和液體等攪打在一起，就得到 batter；它可以用來烤薄餅、蛋糕，也可以裹在食物外面再油炸。","examples":[{"en":"The pancake batter is too thick, so add a little milk.","zh":"薄餅麵糊太稠了，加一點牛奶吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dip the fish in batter before frying it.","zh":"把魚裹上面糊後再炸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fc6fe6099c038e5","term":"batter","forms":["batter","batters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擊球手","explanation":"batter 就是站到擊球位置、試圖用球棒擊中球的球員；這個意義直接來自“用 bat 反覆擊打”。","examples":[{"en":"The batter hit the ball over the left-field wall.","zh":"擊球手把球擊過了左外野的圍牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The batter stepped aside to adjust her helmet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29ae9ca2d7861f6f","term":"batter","forms":["batter","batters","battering","battered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猛擊；反覆打壞","explanation":"batter 表示連續而猛烈地擊打某物，常常打到門、牆或其他東西受損；“反覆敲打”的畫面是這個詞的主線。","examples":[{"en":"The firefighters battered down the locked door.","zh":"消防員猛力砸開了鎖著的門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm battered the coast all night.","zh":"暴風雨整夜猛烈衝擊著海岸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e285ed9c792f88e8","term":"batter","forms":["batter","batters","battering","battered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裹上面糊","explanation":"batter 作動詞時，表示把麵糊裹在食物外面再烹調；它和名詞“麵糊”直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant batters the fish just before frying it.","zh":"這家餐館在炸魚前才給魚裹上面糊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cook batters each courgette flower and drops it into hot oil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3d1701e1d575e129478","word":"battery","forms":["battery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e08ae7364e1108d2","term":"battery","forms":["battery","batteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電池裝置","explanation":"由一個或多個電化學電池連線而成、用來給裝置供電的裝置。可以把它看成把電能集中在一起、隨時輸出的“能量組”。","examples":[{"en":"This camera needs a fresh battery.","zh":"這臺相機需要換一塊新電池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The backup battery kept the alarm working all night.","zh":"備用電池讓警報器整夜保持運轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/battery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb6314b208fb4af0","term":"battery","forms":["battery","batteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電量","explanation":"非正式地把“電池裡儲存的能量”直接叫 battery，也就是裝置還剩多少電。這裡說的不是電池這個硬體，而是它提供的可用電能。","examples":[{"en":"I can't make another call—my phone has almost no battery left.","zh":"我沒法再打一個電話了，我手機幾乎沒電了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My phone has barely any battery left.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/battery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16f5e2322d05ddf58fa7","word":"battle","forms":["battle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dcb822d87ce47dd","term":"battle","forms":["battle","battles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一場較量","explanation":"battle 可以泛指兩方為了目標而進行的激烈較量，不一定真的使用武器；人生中的困難、競爭或爭論都可以被說成 battle。","examples":[{"en":"Finding a good job can be a real battle.","zh":"找一份好工作可能是一場真正的較量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She won her battle against fear.","zh":"她戰勝了恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/battle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96cbd7d05dd495d7","term":"battle","forms":["battle","battles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍事戰役","explanation":"在軍事語境中，battle 是軍隊之間的一次戰鬥或交戰，規模可以比普通的區域性衝突更大，但通常仍是戰爭中的一次具體行動。","examples":[{"en":"The army won the battle at dawn.","zh":"這支軍隊在黎明時贏得了戰鬥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The battle of the river lasted three days.","zh":"那場河畔戰役持續了三天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/battle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27231b4e07192ff0","term":"battle","forms":["battle","battles","battling","battled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加戰鬥","explanation":"作不及物動詞時，battle 表示投入戰鬥或與別人較量，重點是雙方正在進行對抗。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams battled for the championship.","zh":"兩支隊伍為冠軍展開了較量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers battled through the night to defend the bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/battle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0efeb5e6e5a74d5","term":"battle","forms":["battle","battles","battling","battled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與困難抗爭","explanation":"作及物動詞時，battle 表示努力對抗疾病、困難或問題，常常暗示這種鬥爭持續了一段時間。","examples":[{"en":"He is battling a serious illness.","zh":"他正在與一種重病抗爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town is battling severe flooding.","zh":"這座城鎮正在努力應對嚴重的洪災。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/battle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a21dfce2c27396ca29a3","word":"bay","forms":["bay"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f7b2f946d8ccebd","term":"bay","forms":["bay","bays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海灣","explanation":"指海岸線向內凹進去、由陸地包圍一部分的水域，通常與海相連。按記憶中的“凹進去的一塊”來理解，就像海岸向內凹出的一片水面。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the sunset across the bay.","zh":"我們隔著海灣觀賞了日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small boats were anchored in the bay.","zh":"幾艘小船停泊在海灣裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37e038f9fecd5f19","term":"bay","forms":["bay","bays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"月桂葉","explanation":"指月桂樹的葉子，常放進湯、燉菜或醬汁中增添香味，食用前通常會取出。","examples":[{"en":"Add a bay leaf to the stew and remove it before serving.","zh":"在燉菜裡放一片月桂葉，上桌前取出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soup gets a deeper flavor from bay.","zh":"月桂葉讓這道湯的味道更濃郁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27ee295e22439114","term":"bay","forms":["bay","bays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凹入隔間","explanation":"指室內向裡凹入、三面被圍住的一塊空間，例如車輛、倉庫或裝置所在的隔間。記住“凹進去的一塊”，就能把它和普通房間區分開。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic drove the van into the service bay.","zh":"修理工把麵包車開進了維修隔間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Boxes were stacked along one side of the loading bay.","zh":"裝貨隔間的一側堆滿了箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46599c5bb5c33101f80c","word":"be","forms":["be"],"officialPos":"v./aux.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0558199ffc1971ba","term":"be","forms":["be","am","'m","was","'s","were","are","'re","is","-","being","been","art","'rt","wast","wert","beeth","bes","weren","beest"],"pos":"verb","zh":"構成被動語態","explanation":"be 和過去分詞連用，把重點放在“某事被做”或“某人受到某個動作”上；這裡的 be 像是把物件放進“被作用”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The window was broken during the storm.","zh":"窗戶在暴風雨中被打破了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All applications are reviewed by the committee.","zh":"所有申請都由委員會稽核。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/be","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c734ff439a770fdb","term":"be","forms":["be","am","'m","was","'s","were","are","'re","is","-","being","been","art","'rt","wast","wert","beeth","bes","weren","beest"],"pos":"verb","zh":"構成進行時","explanation":"be 和現在分詞連用，表示動作正在進行或處於持續過程中；be 把動作放進“正在發生”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"They are waiting outside.","zh":"他們正在外面等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was reading when you called.","zh":"你打電話時我正在讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/be","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b37f92e6d71f4167","term":"be","forms":["be","am","'m","was","'s","were","are","'re","is","-","being","been","art","'rt","wast","wert","beeth","bes","weren","beest"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表示某物或某人存在","explanation":"在 there be 結構中，be 表示“有、存在”，把某個事物引入眼前的場景；它不主要說明身份，而是說明某處存在什麼。","examples":[{"en":"There are two messages on your phone.","zh":"你的手機上有兩條訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a long line outside the store.","zh":"商店外面排著一條長隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/be","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4686b86ccb336824","term":"be","forms":["be","am","'m","was","'s","were","are","'re","is","-","being","been","art","'rt","wast","wert","beeth","bes","weren","beest"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表示身份或等同","explanation":"be 連線主語和名詞、形容詞等補語，說明“某人或某物是什麼、怎麼樣”；這是“把物件放在某個身份或狀態裡”的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is a doctor.","zh":"我姐姐是一名醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The keys are on the table.","zh":"鑰匙在桌子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/be","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab36e84344729d2bc762","word":"beach","forms":["beach"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a69ca8b1a41a4dea","term":"beach","forms":["beach","beaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水邊的灘","explanation":"beach 是水體邊由沙子或卵石組成的灘地，最典型的畫面就是海邊可以走、坐或曬太陽的地方。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon on the beach.","zh":"我們在海灘上度過了整個下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children ran down to the beach.","zh":"孩子們跑到海灘去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d412446d0f54ec7","term":"beach","forms":["beach","beaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙灘地帶","explanation":"這個意思強調水邊那條平坦的陸地帶，而不只是“岸邊”這個抽象位置；它通常由沙子構成，也可以由卵石構成。","examples":[{"en":"A long sandy beach stretches along the bay.","zh":"海灣沿岸延伸著一片長長的沙灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beach narrowed where the cliffs reached the water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb51e12c48fbcdef2baf","word":"bead","forms":["bead"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa4ca134293a0f62","term":"bead","forms":["bead","beads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小圓珠；小圓體","explanation":"這是最基本的意思：一個小而圓的固體物件，通常可以穿起來、縫上去或用來裝飾。","examples":[{"en":"The children made a bracelet from colorful glass beads.","zh":"孩子們用彩色玻璃珠做了一條手鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tiny bead was stuck in the pocket of my coat.","zh":"我的外套口袋裡卡著一顆小珠子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae4b867cf2eeb128ceab","word":"beam","forms":["beam"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7c5d54be0ad8a00","term":"beam","forms":["beam","beams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長條梁材","explanation":"指一根相對厚度而言很長、可用於建造或支撐的木材或鐵材。它體現了記憶鉤子中“從中心向外伸展的堅固長條”。","examples":[{"en":"The workers lifted a heavy wooden beam into place.","zh":"工人們把一根沉重的木樑吊到指定位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old beams in the roof need to be replaced.","zh":"屋頂裡的舊梁需要更換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0748cf28729b5744","term":"beam","forms":["beam","beams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光束","explanation":"指太陽或其他發光體發出的、方向大致平行的一束光。它正是記憶鉤子中從一箇中心向外放射的光線。","examples":[{"en":"A beam of sunlight came through the window.","zh":"一束陽光從窗戶照了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flashlight sent a bright beam across the room.","zh":"手電筒發出一道明亮的光束，照過整個房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f41fe37684636629","term":"beam","forms":["beam","beams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燦爛笑容","explanation":"指寬闊而明亮的笑容，彷彿笑意從臉上向外綻放。這裡對應記憶鉤子中“表情上的光束”。","examples":[{"en":"A broad beam spread across her face when she heard the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息時，她臉上綻開了燦爛的笑容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child greeted his grandparents with a beam.","zh":"孩子帶著燦爛的笑容迎接祖父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5c62664848b0e8b","term":"beam","forms":["beam","beams","beaming","beamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發光；放射","explanation":"指光線從某處向外伸展、發出或放射，正如記憶鉤子中從中心向外伸展的光束。","examples":[{"en":"Bright sunlight beamed through the gaps in the curtains.","zh":"明亮的陽光從窗簾的縫隙中射進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lighthouse beamed a powerful light across the dark sea.","zh":"燈塔把強烈的光束射向漆黑的海面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3fa55f98fcfcaf6a15a","word":"bean","forms":["bean"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d154b31d8c10534","term":"bean","forms":["bean","beans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豆類植物","explanation":"bean可以指豆科中許多會結出可食用種子或豆莢的植物，例如菜豆、蠶豆等。這裡強調的是整株植物，而不是摘下來的豆子。","examples":[{"en":"These beans grow well in warm soil.","zh":"這些豆類植物在溫暖的土壤里長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beans climbed rapidly up their bamboo supports.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3159edaf1bf38266","term":"bean","forms":["bean","beans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豆子；豆粒","explanation":"bean也指豆類植物結出的可食用種子，也就是我們煮食或加入菜餚中的一粒粒豆子。","examples":[{"en":"I added a handful of beans to the soup.","zh":"我往湯里加了一把豆子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ate beans and rice for lunch.","zh":"她午飯吃了豆子和米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39c2b0c7e52ebfe9","term":"bean","forms":["bean","beans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豆莢","explanation":"bean還可以指豆類植物的可食用豆莢，尤其是還沒有剝出豆粒、可以整條烹調的嫩豆莢。","examples":[{"en":"We steamed the green beans until they were tender.","zh":"我們把青豆莢蒸到變嫩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Split the bean open and remove the seeds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc98bb50e8094b2ac3ce","word":"bear","forms":["bear"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a72fbfea50b8c23b","term":"bear","forms":["bear","bears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熊","explanation":"指一種體型較大、毛較厚、腳掌扁平且通常雜食的哺乳動物；這是“熊”這一主線的基本含義。","examples":[{"en":"A bear wandered into the campsite at night.","zh":"一隻熊夜裡走進了營地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw several bears near the river.","zh":"我們在河邊看到了幾隻熊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c17a91776cc8f9ba","term":"bear","forms":["bear","bears","bearing","bore","bare","borne","born","bearest","borest","barest","beareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攜帶；帶來","explanation":"表示把人、物品或某種抽象事物帶著或帶到某處，是“承載”這條主線中最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"They came bearing gifts for the new neighbors.","zh":"他們帶著禮物來拜訪新鄰居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The letter bears the signature of the director.","zh":"這封信上有主任的簽名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de3870a5ef7dfae6","term":"bear","forms":["bear","bears","bearing","bore","bare","borne","born","bearest","borest","barest","beareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支撐；承受","explanation":"表示物體支撐重量，或人、事物承受壓力、困難和責任，正是“承載”主線的核心延伸。","examples":[{"en":"These beams bear the weight of the roof.","zh":"這些橫樑支撐著屋頂的重量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He could not bear the thought of losing his home.","zh":"他無法承受失去家園的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-941192abb086502a3dfe","word":"beard","forms":["beard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c667d2734dd1cbb1","term":"beard","forms":["beard","beards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鬍鬚","explanation":"指生長在下巴、面頰、下頜和頸部的面部毛髮，通常是男性面部毛髮的整體。","examples":[{"en":"He grew a short beard during the winter.","zh":"他在冬天留了一小撮短鬍鬚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need to trim my beard before the interview.","zh":"面試前我得修一修鬍鬚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19e4aff4dd1a95fc","term":"beard","forms":["beard","beards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鳥喙根部的羽毛","explanation":"指某些鳥類喙根部成簇、像鬍鬚一樣的細小羽毛。","examples":[{"en":"The bird has a dark beard beneath its beak.","zh":"這隻鳥的喙下有一簇深色的羽毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bird's beard bristled around the base of its bill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bf417bd87162d5d77a5","word":"beast","forms":["beast"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ee5eb47c0ee077e","term":"beast","forms":["beast","beasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"野獸；大型或危險的動物","explanation":"指動物，尤其是體型較大、生活在陸地上或可能有危險的動物。這個最基本的形象是其他許多比喻義的來源。","examples":[{"en":"The beast disappeared into the forest before anyone could see it clearly.","zh":"那頭野獸還沒等人看清，就消失在森林裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers were afraid of the large beasts in the valley.","zh":"村民害怕山谷裡的大型野獸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f0d0e139b8f6030","term":"beast","forms":["beast","beasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棘手的事情","explanation":"把難以控制、處理或解決的事情比作一頭野獸，表示它令人費力、麻煩而且不好馴服。","examples":[{"en":"Fixing the old house turned into a beast of a problem.","zh":"修繕這座老房子最後變成了一個棘手的大難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final exam was a real beast.","zh":"期末考試真是難得嚇人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9eeb63bf773f4b0854d","word":"beat","forms":["beat"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b61fa304410c62c5","term":"beat","forms":["beat","beats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基本節拍","explanation":"在音樂中，指聽眾感受到的基本時間單位；許多節拍連續排列，就形成音樂的節奏。","examples":[{"en":"Clap along with the beat of the song.","zh":"跟著這首歌的節拍一起拍手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drummer came in on the first beat.","zh":"鼓手在第一拍進入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f135000b4290bde","term":"beat","forms":["beat","beats","beating","beated","beaten","beatest","beateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打；擊打","explanation":"表示用手、工具或其他力量敲擊某人或某物，就像有一下明確的“敲擊”。","examples":[{"en":"The boy beat the drum with a wooden stick.","zh":"男孩用木棍敲鼓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She beat the dust out of the rug.","zh":"她把地毯上的灰塵拍了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7342a6a0cabe3e5d","term":"beat","forms":["beat","beats","beating","beated","beaten","beatest","beateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擊敗；勝過","explanation":"表示在比賽、競爭或比較中勝過某人或某事物，可以把它理解為在競爭中“敲過對手”。","examples":[{"en":"Our team beat the league leaders by two goals.","zh":"我們隊以兩球之差擊敗了聯賽領頭羊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This phone beats my old one in almost every way.","zh":"這部手機幾乎在各方面都勝過我的舊手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6a1427d7119cd3c049d","word":"beautiful","forms":["beautiful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-709ac854d57b6d79","term":"beautiful","forms":["beautiful","more beautiful","most beautiful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"美麗的；漂亮的","explanation":"指外表或外觀具有美感，能給人留下賞心悅目的印象。這是 beautiful 最直接、最常見的意思，可以形容人、景物、物品等。","examples":[{"en":"The garden is especially beautiful in spring.","zh":"這個花園在春天尤其美麗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looked beautiful in her wedding dress.","zh":"她穿婚紗時看起來很漂亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beautiful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3dffce45297926f","term":"beautiful","forms":["beautiful","more beautiful","most beautiful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可愛的；善良而令人喜愛的","explanation":"指一個人本身很值得喜歡，尤其是因為善良、體貼或令人感到溫暖，而不只是因為外貌好看。這是從“令人感到美好”擴充套件出來的人的內在美。","examples":[{"en":"She is a beautiful person who always puts others first.","zh":"她是個非常善良的人，總是把別人放在第一位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her beautiful generosity touched everyone in the shelter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beautiful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-136ebbc795e975366bfb","word":"beautify","forms":["beautify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"beautify","forms":["beautify"],"pos":"v.","zh":"美化","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers planted flowers to beautify the empty lot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"New murals will beautify the walls around the school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5610de1f6ffecc890aa","word":"beauty","forms":["beauty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c206775c674971e","term":"beauty","forms":["beauty","beauties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美；美感","explanation":"beauty首先指讓人覺得漂亮、和諧、令人愉悅的品質，尤其常用於外表，也可以指藝術或自然帶來的美感。它說的是“美這一品質”，不是單獨某個漂亮物件。","examples":[{"en":"The beauty of the lake amazed everyone.","zh":"這座湖的美讓所有人都驚歎不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beauty of the desert surprised us at sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beauty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bda68273f7e43b45","term":"beauty","forms":["beauty","beauties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精彩的東西；漂亮的表現","explanation":"當某個動作、作品或結果特別出色、令人滿意時，也可以說它是a beauty。這裡的“美”從外表擴充套件成了“精彩、漂亮”。","examples":[{"en":"That was a beauty of a goal.","zh":"那是一個精彩絕倫的進球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That overhead volley was an absolute beauty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beauty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1d070a29351209e","term":"beauty","forms":["beauty","beauties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"妙處；高明之處","explanation":"在the beauty of...結構中，beauty指某個計劃、決定或安排最吸引人的優點，尤其是它巧妙、方便或有效的地方。這裡的“美”變成了一個方案的內在妙處。","examples":[{"en":"The beauty of this plan is that everyone benefits.","zh":"這個計劃的妙處在於人人都能受益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beauty of this design is its simplicity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beauty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a511aeeeb8a119931a67","word":"because","forms":["because"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"because","forms":["because"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"因為","examples":[{"en":"We stayed indoors because the storm was getting worse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She chose this school because it has a strong science program.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ebb1e6f5b2adf424b66","word":"become","forms":["become"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66f12257d6a48b5e","term":"become","forms":["become","becomes","becoming","became","becomen","becomed","becomest","becamest","becamedst","becometh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變成；成為","explanation":"表示人或事物從原來的狀態進入另一種狀態，或獲得某種身份。這是 become 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She became a doctor when she was 25.","zh":"她二十五歲時成為了一名醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small village became a busy town.","zh":"這個小村莊變成了一個繁忙的小鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/become","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b52e53ab4e398877","term":"become","forms":["become","becomes","becoming","became","becomen","becomed","becomest","becamest","becamedst","becometh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"後來變得怎樣","explanation":"主要出現在固定問法中，詢問某人或某事後來去了哪裡、變成什麼情況或有了什麼結果。這裡的核心仍是“後來走到了什麼狀態”。單獨表示“發生、出現”是較舊的用法。","examples":[{"en":"What became of your old neighbor?","zh":"你以前的鄰居後來怎麼樣了？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What became of the kitten you rescued?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/become","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5052532c2206140dfdc","word":"bed","forms":["bed"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54f6fbe2631de29b","term":"bed","forms":["bed","beds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"床","explanation":"最常見的意思是供人躺下、休息或睡覺的傢俱。它通常指具體的一張床，也可以泛指家中或房間裡的睡眠位置。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter left her book on the bed.","zh":"我女兒把書落在床上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought a new bed for the guest room.","zh":"我們給客房買了一張新床。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-118dc8eb7f7cd9ec","term":"bed","forms":["bed","beds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上床睡覺","explanation":"在 go to bed、get into bed 等表達中，bed 表示“上床、進入睡眠休息狀態”，重點不是傢俱本身。","examples":[{"en":"The children went to bed after the story.","zh":"孩子們聽完故事後就上床睡覺了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhausted travelers bedded down beside the fire.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b142eb71f76823b8","term":"bed","forms":["bed","beds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承託面；鋪底","explanation":"由“供身體躺著的床”引申為“承託其他東西的底面或鋪層”。例如食物放在生菜上，生菜就是食物的 bed。","examples":[{"en":"The fish was served on a bed of rice.","zh":"這條魚鋪在一層米飯上端了上來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place the flowers on a bed of fresh leaves.","zh":"把花放在一層新鮮葉子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a05e6feb79c854166f6c","word":"bedroom","forms":["bedroom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2666cfc6588af1a2","term":"bedroom","forms":["bedroom","bedrooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臥室","explanation":"家、公寓、酒店等住所中放床供人睡覺的房間，就是 bedroom。它強調房間的用途，不一定只住一個人。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't enter my bedroom without knocking.","zh":"請先敲門，不要直接進入我的臥室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel has two small bedrooms and a bright kitchen.","zh":"這家酒店有兩間小臥室和一間明亮的廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bedroom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62cb81b5904a262ffaee","word":"bee","forms":["bee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fab2b70cefc743fb","term":"bee","forms":["bee","bees","been"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜜蜂","explanation":"bee首先指蜜蜂，即會飛、通常採集花粉的昆蟲；這個核心形象也構成了其他許多義項的聯想基礎。","examples":[{"en":"A bee landed on the yellow flower.","zh":"一隻蜜蜂落在了那朵黃色的花上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We moved the cup outside so the bee could escape.","zh":"我們把杯子移到外面，好讓那隻蜜蜂逃出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27849543032aed3c","term":"bee","forms":["bee","bees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拼寫競賽","explanation":"bee可以指多人集中參加的競賽，最常見的是spelling bee，即參賽者輪流拼寫單詞的比賽；它保留了“大家像蜂群一樣聚在一起忙碌”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"Maya won the school spelling bee on Friday.","zh":"瑪雅星期五贏得了學校的拼寫競賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final round of the geography bee was surprisingly difficult.","zh":"地理知識競賽的決賽環節出人意料地難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa415c4e8890cf0fec78","word":"beef","forms":["beef"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00816875036e88d9","term":"beef","forms":["beef","beefs","beeves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牛肉","explanation":"指牛的肉，是 beef 最基本、最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I don't eat much beef, but I like beef soup.","zh":"我不太吃牛肉，但喜歡牛肉湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe calls for half a kilo of beef.","zh":"這道菜譜需要半公斤牛肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beef","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb46bc140e12e5e5","term":"beef","forms":["beef","beefs","beeves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不滿；過節","explanation":"俚語中指對某人或某事的牢騷、反感或不信任，也可以指產生這種不滿的理由；可以把它記成心裡“壓著一塊有分量的牛肉”。","examples":[{"en":"I have no beef with her; we just see things differently.","zh":"我和她沒有什麼過節，只是看法不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a beef with the new parking rules.","zh":"他對新的停車規定很不滿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beef","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d01b7ce9154ef0264ce7","word":"beep","forms":["beep"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34d3c7f4db37a8fb","term":"beep","forms":["beep","beeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘀聲；喇叭聲","explanation":"指汽車喇叭或類似裝置發出的短促聲音，就是記憶中的那一聲“嘀”。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a beep behind me and moved aside.","zh":"我聽到身後一聲喇叭響，就讓到了一邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The microwave gives a beep when the food is ready.","zh":"食物準備好後，微波爐會發出一聲提示音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b06f3103e14bb764","term":"beep","forms":["beep","beeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子提示音","explanation":"指裝置發出的短促、通常單調的電子音，用來提醒、確認或提示某個狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The machine makes a beep when you press the button.","zh":"按下按鈕時，機器會發出一聲提示音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three beeps told us that the door was locked.","zh":"三聲提示音告訴我們門已經鎖上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e751f261d56cbc2c","term":"beep","forms":["beep","beeps","beeping","beeped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出嘀聲","explanation":"指裝置、汽車喇叭或人使某物發出短促的“嘀”聲，是名詞核心義直接變成動作。","examples":[{"en":"Cars began beeping their horns in the traffic jam.","zh":"堵車時，汽車開始不停地按喇叭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The timer beeped just as dinner was ready.","zh":"晚飯剛準備好，計時器就響了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d8b4cf854cd42f48688","word":"beer","forms":["beer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09ae9e42f83c591d","term":"beer","forms":["beer","beers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啤酒","explanation":"指用含澱粉的原料發酵製成的酒精飲料，最常見的是以麥芽為主要原料，並常帶有啤酒花的苦味。這是 beer 最基本、最需要先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Beer is brewed all over the world.","zh":"世界各地都釀造啤酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She does not drink beer.","zh":"她不喝啤酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c6c41901292fe970","term":"beer","forms":["beer","beers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一杯或一瓶啤酒","explanation":"指作為一份飲品的啤酒，實際可指一杯、一瓶或一罐，不強調具體容器。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a few beers for the party.","zh":"我為聚會買了幾瓶啤酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two beers and a lemonade, please.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b3e7cdfdbca8bb5463e","word":"beetle","forms":["beetle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fcd885a68eecbd47","term":"beetle","forms":["beetle","beetles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"甲蟲","explanation":"甲蟲是一大類昆蟲，前翅硬而像外殼，停下時會覆蓋並保護後翅；日常說 beetle，通常首先想到這種昆蟲。","examples":[{"en":"A shiny green beetle landed on the windowsill.","zh":"一隻閃亮的綠色甲蟲落在了窗臺上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found several beetles under the old log.","zh":"我們在那根舊木頭下面發現了幾隻甲蟲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beetle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6db7d803e74f1ffa7d8f","word":"before","forms":["before"],"officialPos":"prep./conj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7a4938d2a01f687","term":"before","forms":["before"],"pos":"adv","zh":"以前；之前","explanation":"表示某個動作或經歷發生在現在或另一個參照時間以前，重點是“早些時候”。","examples":[{"en":"I've never tried sushi before.","zh":"我以前從沒吃過壽司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had visited that village twice before.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/before","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eae07394d3f812e5","term":"before","forms":["before"],"pos":"prep","zh":"早於；在……之前","explanation":"表示某事發生在另一個時間點、事件或動作之前，也就是先完成前一件事。","examples":[{"en":"Please finish the form before Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前填完這張表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wash your hands before eating.","zh":"吃飯前要洗手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/before","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d93b5d04a8e1e021","term":"before","forms":["before"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……前面","explanation":"表示一個人或物在另一個人或物的前方，強調空間位置，而不是時間先後。","examples":[{"en":"A tall tree stood before the house.","zh":"房子前面有一棵高大的樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accused stood before the judge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/before","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa0d6cbcca9473a66800","word":"beforehand","forms":["beforehand"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba20db71eff11900","term":"beforehand","forms":["beforehand"],"pos":"adv","zh":"事先；提前","explanation":"表示某事在另一個時間點或事件之前就已經完成、安排好或被知道，核心感覺就是“先放到前面處理”。","examples":[{"en":"Please let me know beforehand if you need extra time.","zh":"如果你需要額外時間，請事先告訴我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reserve your seat beforehand to avoid disappointment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beforehand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e80f71a8d731192771d8","word":"beg","forms":["beg"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f2435d61efe26a5","term":"beg","forms":["beg","begs","begging","begged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"乞求幫助或金錢","explanation":"指為了得到幫助、金錢等而低姿態地請求，常讓人聯想到街頭向路人伸手求助。","examples":[{"en":"The man begged passers-by for money.","zh":"那個人向路人乞求錢財。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She begged for a chance to start over.","zh":"她苦苦請求一個重新開始的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eff6a8967875f2ce","term":"beg","forms":["beg","begs","begging","begged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懇求某人做某事","explanation":"指非常迫切地請求某人提供幫助、答應請求或做某事，比普通請求更能表現出情緒和壓力。","examples":[{"en":"I begged her to give me one more chance.","zh":"我懇求她再給我一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He begged his parents for permission to go.","zh":"他懇求父母允許他去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d5afdf3c070bed1b01f","word":"beggar","forms":["beggar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1945dadf3935a425","term":"beggar","forms":["beggar","beggars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乞討者","explanation":"指靠向別人要錢、食物或其他幫助生活的人。這個詞把“伸手討要”的核心畫面直接說出來，但通常帶有較強的負面色彩。","examples":[{"en":"A beggar asked me for money outside the station.","zh":"車站外有個乞丐向我要錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old beggar slept under the bridge.","zh":"那個年老的乞丐睡在橋下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beggar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-019f5a3d3b8287e2","term":"beggar","forms":["beggar","beggars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"窮困潦倒的人","explanation":"強調一個人窮到幾乎一無所有，未必明確靠乞討為生。它和“乞討者”的意義相連，都突出生活資源已經被掏空。","examples":[{"en":"After losing his job, he was left a poor beggar with nowhere to go.","zh":"失業後，他變成了一個一無所有、無處可去的窮人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruined investor died a penniless beggar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beggar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6f07d43b5c21db0fbb9","word":"begin","forms":["begin"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0dd37db62a78a784","term":"begin","forms":["begin","begins","beginning","began","begun","beginnest","beganst","begannest","beginneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開始做；啟動","explanation":"表示從某個時刻起開始做一件事，或啟動一項活動。它對應記憶中的“推開門，邁出第一步”。","examples":[{"en":"She began learning Spanish after moving to Madrid.","zh":"她搬到馬德里後開始學習西班牙語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting began at nine.","zh":"會議九點開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/begin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5e9c6659a22863c","term":"begin","forms":["begin","begins","beginning","began","begun","beginnest","beganst","begannest","beginneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開始存在；產生","explanation":"表示某事物從無到有、進入存在狀態，強調它的起點。它仍然是同一幅“門後出現新事物”的畫面，只是開始的物件不是人的行動，而是事物本身。","examples":[{"en":"The story begins with a child finding an old key.","zh":"這個故事從一個孩子找到一把舊鑰匙開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trouble began with a leaking pipe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/begin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0c2ebfa3490d41a60d9","word":"beginner","forms":["beginner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-141c9d61929716ca","term":"beginner","forms":["beginner","beginners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"初學者","explanation":"指剛開始學習、練習或從事某項活動的人，重點是經驗還不多。這個詞通常只針對某一方面：一個人在工作上很有經驗，也可能是某項新愛好的初學者。","examples":[{"en":"I'm a beginner at Finnish, so I still need a lot of practice.","zh":"我是芬蘭語初學者，所以還需要大量練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This course is designed for complete beginners.","zh":"這門課程是為完全沒有基礎的初學者設計的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beginner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21c55231a57076375787","word":"behalf","forms":["behalf"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb70cf3652a68b1c","term":"behalf","forms":["behalf","behalves","behalfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某人的利益或福祉","explanation":"指某人或某個群體應得到的利益、照顧或保護；站在某人這一邊併為其爭取，就是在維護其利益。","examples":[{"en":"We raised money on behalf of the local animal shelter.","zh":"我們為當地動物收容所籌集了資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She campaigned tirelessly on behalf of injured workers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behalf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adda8e124924f40a","term":"behalf","forms":["behalf","behalves","behalfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表某人；代替某人的身份或許可權","explanation":"指一個人代替另一個人站在某個位置上，以對方的名義發言、行動或作出決定；這裡的重點不是誰受益，而是誰被代表。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer signed the agreement on behalf of her client.","zh":"律師代表她的客戶簽署了協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She accepted the medal on her father's behalf.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behalf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6ac32cfa83f20537057","word":"behave","forms":["behave"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5419870d9f6504e9","term":"behave","forms":["behave","behaves","behaving","behaved","behavest","behavedst","behaveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"管好自己；守規矩","explanation":"指約束自己的行為，表現得體、守規矩，尤其常用於提醒或要求某人不要胡鬧。這裡的核心仍是把自己“管住”。","examples":[{"en":"You need to behave yourself during the ceremony.","zh":"你在儀式期間要規矩一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children behaved themselves at the restaurant.","zh":"孩子們在餐館裡表現得很規矩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13e20d5cb77f7e38","term":"behave","forms":["behave","behaves","behaving","behaved","behavest","behavedst","behaveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"以某種方式表現","explanation":"指某人以特定方式行動或表現，重點不是好壞，而是行為呈現出的樣子；也可以說某事物執行或反應得怎樣。","examples":[{"en":"He behaves like a child whenever he is tired.","zh":"他一累就表現得像個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new engine behaves differently in cold weather.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08bf2418cca97fefbdf7","word":"behavior","forms":["behavior"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08a0675249b037bd","term":"behavior","forms":["behavior","behaviors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的行為舉止","explanation":"指人在社會中表現出來的做法和舉止，通常會聯絡到他人對禮貌、規矩或得體的期待。它是“從外面看得見的做法”這一核心概念最典型的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher praised the student's behavior in class.","zh":"老師表揚了這名學生在課堂上的表現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parents often worry about their children's behavior online.","zh":"父母常常擔心孩子在網上的行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behavior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9592b50a4bfc881","term":"behavior","forms":["behavior","behaviors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物的行為方式","explanation":"指人以外的動物或其他生物通常怎樣活動、反應和生活；重點不在“好”或“壞”，而在於它表現出的方式。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers observed the behavior of the birds at night.","zh":"研究人員觀察了這些鳥在夜間的行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camera recorded the foxes' hunting behavior.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behavior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113,114],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-b1b886ce5f5750a00ae3","word":"behind","forms":["behind"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c698274f32cdbb0","term":"behind","forms":["behind","more behind","behinder","most behind","behindest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在後方","explanation":"某物位於另一個位置或物體的後面，是最直接的空間意義。","examples":[{"en":"A small garden lies behind.","zh":"後面有一個小花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclists disappeared ahead, leaving me far behind.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2607f2bf4729236f","term":"behind","forms":["behind","more behind","behinder","most behind","behindest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"落在後面","explanation":"某人或某物在位置、速度、進度、排名或時間上沒有跟上別人，落到了後方。","examples":[{"en":"If you miss two lessons, you may fall behind.","zh":"如果你缺兩節課，可能就會跟不上進度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our car was far behind the others.","zh":"我們的車遠遠落在其他車後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ad1ade1efc8ac24","term":"behind","forms":["behind"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……後面","explanation":"某人或某物位於另一個人或物的後方，是 behind 最直接的介詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children were hiding behind the wall.","zh":"孩子們躲在牆後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a parking lot behind the library.","zh":"圖書館後面有一個停車場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/behind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85574fa07dae32132675","word":"being","forms":["being"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c3f18936c6e76f0","term":"being","forms":["being","beings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生命體；生物","explanation":"指一個有生命、能夠存在和活動的個體，既可以是真實的人或動物，也可以是想象中的生命體。這個意義就是“正在存在的東西”最具體的體現。","examples":[{"en":"Every living being needs water to survive.","zh":"每個有生命的生物都需要水才能生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story describes a strange being from another world.","zh":"這個故事描寫了一個來自另一個世界的奇異生命體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/being","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-988e4320cae757b9","term":"being","forms":["being","beings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"存在；生存狀態","explanation":"指某物或某人存在、具有意識或處於生命狀態這一事實，重點不在“是什麼東西”，而在“存在著”這一狀態本身。","examples":[{"en":"The new organization came into being last year.","zh":"這個新組織於去年成立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was grateful simply for the joy of being alive.","zh":"她只是因為活著的喜悅就心懷感激。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/being","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f31852d7e68e8ab27032","word":"belief","forms":["belief"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-023caf001a8acdcd","term":"belief","forms":["belief","beliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相信某說法為真","explanation":"指一個人在心裡接受某個說法，認為它是真的，不一定已經有充分證據；重點在於“把它當真”。","examples":[{"en":"It's my belief that the missing documents are still in the office.","zh":"我相信那些丟失的檔案還在辦公室裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His belief in the witness's honesty never wavered.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3eaae8dfbc703976","term":"belief","forms":["belief","beliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宗教信仰","explanation":"指對宗教、神或某種超越性力量的信仰；這裡的 belief 不只是暫時的判斷，而是能長期支撐一個人的信念。","examples":[{"en":"Her belief helped her remain hopeful during the difficult years.","zh":"她的信仰幫助她在那些艱難的歲月裡保持希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His religious belief sustained him through years of exile.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85d3a5c52d98d529","term":"belief","forms":["belief","beliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人的宗教或道德原則","explanation":"指一個人所堅持的宗教或道德觀念，尤其是會影響其選擇和行為的原則；複數形式常表示一整套個人立場。","examples":[{"en":"He refused the offer because it went against his beliefs.","zh":"他拒絕了這個提議，因為它違背了他的信仰和原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His beliefs prevent him from working on holy days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f078209dfece953500ee","word":"believe","forms":["believe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aceda8cef8c820ba","term":"believe","forms":["believe","believes","believing","believed","believest","believedst","believeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相信某事為真","explanation":"指把一個事實、說法或判斷接受為真的，但不一定擁有絕對證據；這是 believe 最基本的“在心裡認為可信”。","examples":[{"en":"I believe the report is accurate.","zh":"我相信這份報告是準確的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She believed his story at first.","zh":"她起初相信了他的說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/believe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49dfc41037d53d78","term":"believe","forms":["believe","believes","believing","believed","believest","believedst","believeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相信某人或某事物的存在、價值或真實性","explanation":"believe in 把“可信”擴充套件到一個人、理念、力量或事物本身，表示相信它存在，或相信它值得信任、支援；例如可以相信神、鬼、夢想或某人的能力。","examples":[{"en":"My parents always believed in me.","zh":"我的父母一直相信我、支援我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you believe in ghosts?","zh":"你相信鬼魂存在嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/believe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f683740cded6680d9d94","word":"bell","forms":["bell"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de20dec1a4e34280","term":"bell","forms":["bell","bells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鍾；鈴","explanation":"bell通常指敲擊後會發出清脆聲音的金屬或其他硬質物體，形狀常像倒扣的杯子；它可以是鍾，也可以是小鈴。","examples":[{"en":"The old bell rang across the village at noon.","zh":"中午，古老的鐘聲傳遍了村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tied a small bell to the cat's collar.","zh":"她在貓的項圈上繫了一隻小鈴鐺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fdb2ae39eac3a5ff","term":"bell","forms":["bell","bells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電話；來電","explanation":"在英國非正式用法中，bell可以指一次電話或來電，體現了“透過鈴聲聯絡”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"I'll give you a bell after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Give me a bell when you reach the station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d38f6d6072843eeb841","word":"belong","forms":["belong"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-397c03946388f7d8","term":"belong","forms":["belong","belongs","belonging","belonged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處在合適的位置","explanation":"表示某件東西應該放在某處，因為那裡是它合適、正常的位置；重點不是“擁有”，而是“放對地方”。","examples":[{"en":"These books belong on the top shelf.","zh":"這些書應該放在最上面的架子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These tools belong in the locked cupboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c2527f24ec11f57","term":"belong","forms":["belong","belongs","belonging","belonged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"屬於某個群體","explanation":"表示某人或某物是某個群體、組織或環境的一部分，和那裡有歸屬感或合適的聯絡。它把“找到自己的位置”從具體地點擴充套件到了社會關係。","examples":[{"en":"I finally feel that I belong to this team.","zh":"我終於覺得自己屬於這個團隊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finally felt she belonged among the musicians.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-868551593c5dd6c4","term":"belong","forms":["belong","belongs","belonging","belonged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"歸某人所有","explanation":"表示某物是某人的財產或應歸某人所有，也就是物品和主人之間有明確的歸屬關係。","examples":[{"en":"That blue bicycle belongs to my sister.","zh":"那輛藍色腳踏車是我姐姐的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That blue umbrella belongs to the receptionist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da0f5bb767ed966565e0","word":"belongings","forms":["belongings"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"belongings","forms":["belongings"],"pos":"n.","zh":"個人物品；所有物","examples":[{"en":"Please take all your belongings with you when you leave.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She packed her belongings into two small suitcases.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b34c922c3f3c83900c5","word":"beloved","forms":["beloved"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55abcd2ba52ae2dc","term":"beloved","forms":["beloved","more beloved","beloveder","most beloved","belovedest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深愛的；心愛的","explanation":"指某人或某物被深深地愛著、珍視著，比一般的“喜歡”更有感情。它可以形容親人、朋友、故鄉、作品等。","examples":[{"en":"She returned to her beloved hometown after many years abroad.","zh":"她在國外多年後回到了深愛的故鄉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beloved teacher was remembered by generations of students.","zh":"這位深受愛戴的老師被一代又一代學生銘記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beloved","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b28afd3b96d17838","term":"beloved","forms":["beloved","beloveds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心愛的人或事物","explanation":"把形容詞的意思直接變成一個名詞：beloved 就是那個被深愛、被珍視的人或事物，最常指心愛的人。","examples":[{"en":"He placed a rose beside his beloved's photograph.","zh":"他在心愛之人的照片旁放了一朵玫瑰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote a final letter to her beloved.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beloved","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ada24bf6bf313927389","word":"below","forms":["below"],"officialPos":"adv./prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1858fe7315f18653","term":"below","forms":["below"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在下方","explanation":"表示某人或某物處在較低的位置，或向較低處延伸。核心畫面就是“在下面”。","examples":[{"en":"The village lies below the mountain.","zh":"村莊坐落在山下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small boat disappeared below the waves.","zh":"一艘小船消失在海浪下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/below","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8dbc0c83a77a16e","term":"below","forms":["below"],"pos":"prep","zh":"低於某處","explanation":"表示某人或某物的位置低於另一個地點或物體，是“向下”這個核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"We found a quiet campsite below the waterfall.","zh":"我們在瀑布下方找到了一處安靜的營地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature below the surface was much colder.","zh":"表面以下的溫度冷得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/below","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f4f045d317c6bb4cce5","word":"belt","forms":["belt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7315134e0bcfae3d","term":"belt","forms":["belt","belts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腰帶；帶子","explanation":"belt是圍在腰部的帶子，可以用來固定褲子、攜帶武器，也可以只是服裝裝飾。它體現了“用帶子繞住並固定”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"He wore a leather belt with his jeans.","zh":"他穿牛仔褲時繫了一條皮帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The belt on my old bag is starting to tear.","zh":"我舊包上的帶子開始裂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-956818b0369a877d","term":"belt","forms":["belt","belts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安全帶；約束帶","explanation":"belt也可以是為了安全而把人固定住的帶子，例如汽車裡的安全帶。重點不是裝飾，而是把身體穩穩地束住。","examples":[{"en":"Please fasten your seat belt before the plane takes off.","zh":"飛機起飛前請繫好安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child was secured with a safety belt.","zh":"孩子用安全帶固定住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9e40517a61c5be8","term":"belt","forms":["belt","belts","belting","belted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"圍住","explanation":"belt作動詞時可以表示像帶子一樣環繞某個地方或物體，把它包在周圍。","examples":[{"en":"The village is belted by fields of wheat.","zh":"這個村莊四周環繞著麥田。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trees belt the property along its eastern boundary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e1dcd0c916e02ca","term":"belt","forms":["belt","belts","belting","belted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"大聲唱出","explanation":"belt out表示用強而響亮的聲音唱歌，像把聲音有力地甩出去。它和“帶子傳遞力量”的核心形象相連。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone belted out the chorus at the concert.","zh":"音樂會上所有人都大聲唱出了副歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She belted out her favorite song in the kitchen.","zh":"她在廚房裡放聲唱自己最喜歡的歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/belt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b32c28cb38c05480ecc","word":"bench","forms":["bench"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ae9c1fada4852e0","term":"bench","forms":["bench","benches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長凳","explanation":"指供多人並排坐的長條座椅，可以有靠背，也可以沒有，常見於公園、學校等地方。它體現了bench最基本的“供人停留的水平座面”這一概念。","examples":[{"en":"We sat on a bench in the park and watched the children play.","zh":"我們坐在公園的長凳上，看孩子們玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a wooden bench outside the school.","zh":"學校外面有一條木長凳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bench","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf476dacf56bcf7e","term":"bench","forms":["bench","benches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法官席","explanation":"指法庭中法官就座並作出裁決的位置，也可以藉此指法官或法庭本身。這裡的長凳意象從普通座位擴充套件成了具有裁判權的席位。","examples":[{"en":"The judge asked the lawyers to approach the bench.","zh":"法官要求律師走到法官席前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The decision came directly from the bench.","zh":"這項裁決直接由法庭作出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bench","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36e110819a318dddc3f8","word":"bend","forms":["bend"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43c6531643ea4e94","term":"bend","forms":["bend","bends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彎曲處；彎道","explanation":"指道路、河流等不再保持直線而形成的弧形部分；把直線掰出弧度，就有了一個 bend。","examples":[{"en":"Slow down before the sharp bend in the road.","zh":"在前方急彎前減速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A roadside mirror helps drivers see traffic around the bend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-707e8152c1cf8089","term":"bend","forms":["bend","bends","bending","bent","bended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使彎曲","explanation":"把直的東西用力或透過其他作用掰出弧度，就是使它彎曲；這正是把一條直線掰出弧度的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful not to bend the metal frame.","zh":"小心別把金屬框架弄彎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bent the wire into a small circle.","zh":"她把鐵絲彎成了一個小圓圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bed8bd476c323e1","term":"bend","forms":["bend","bends","bending","bent","bended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變彎","explanation":"原本較直的東西自己形成弧度或彎曲狀態，例如樹在風中彎下去；這裡不是誰把它弄彎，而是它變彎了。","examples":[{"en":"The young trees bent in the strong wind.","zh":"小樹在強風中彎了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shelf began to bend under the weight of the books.","zh":"書的重量壓得架子開始彎曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78ca5739ef856727","term":"bend","forms":["bend","bends","bending","bent","bended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使轉向","explanation":"把“彎”用於方向，就是使某人、某物或注意力轉向某處；好像把原本直行的路線掰向另一個方向。","examples":[{"en":"The guide bent the group toward the quieter path.","zh":"嚮導讓隊伍轉向那條更安靜的小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bent her attention to the problem.","zh":"她把注意力轉向了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f3ca61c7e8e99361399","word":"beneath","forms":["beneath"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9661d0ef14fb4500","term":"beneath","forms":["beneath"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……下面","explanation":"表示某人或某物位於另一物的下方，是“低處”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow stream runs beneath the bridge.","zh":"一條窄溪從橋下流過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The keys were hidden beneath a loose floorboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beneath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bec2d07a1b569699a18e","word":"beneficial","forms":["beneficial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7a7d5a42aea1686","term":"beneficial","forms":["beneficial","more beneficial","most beneficial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有益的；有好處的","explanation":"形容某事對人、環境或某個目標有幫助，能夠帶來積極結果。它強調“產生益處”，不只是說某事令人滿意或看起來不錯。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise is beneficial to your health.","zh":"經常鍛鍊對你的健康有益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A short break can be beneficial for concentration.","zh":"短暫休息有助於集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beneficial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e97469619c0d7aa7bf47","word":"benefit","forms":["benefit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9bf8b53a588ec790","term":"benefit","forms":["benefit","benefits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"好處；益處","explanation":"指某件事帶來的幫助、便利或積極結果，也可以指某人從中得到的好處。它既可以是具體幫助，也可以是較抽象的優勢。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise has many benefits for your health.","zh":"經常鍛鍊對健康有很多好處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used the subtitles for the benefit of her elderly father.","zh":"她使用字幕是為了方便年邁的父親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/benefit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f698a962f5e93aa","term":"benefit","forms":["benefit","benefits","benefiting","benefitting","benefited","benefitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……受益","explanation":"指某個行動、事物或安排給某人、某群體帶來好處。主語通常是措施、變化、產品或事件，賓語是得到好處的人或事物。","examples":[{"en":"The new library will benefit students in the area.","zh":"新圖書館將使這一地區的學生受益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Additional shade benefits plants during the hottest part of summer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/benefit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f3b7c182c1e8998","term":"benefit","forms":["benefit","benefits","benefiting","benefitting","benefited","benefitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從……中受益","explanation":"指某人、某物或某個系統得到某項措施、經驗或條件帶來的好處。這裡的重點是“好處落在主語身上”，來源通常用 from 引出。","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses can benefit from the new training program.","zh":"小企業可以從新的培訓專案中受益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gardeners benefit from exchanging seeds with their neighbors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/benefit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-73cce42f1f0e9099688b","word":"berry","forms":["berry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3995561cb4f59592","term":"berry","forms":["berry","berries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漿果；小漿果","explanation":"berry通常指小而多汁、可以直接食用的果實，例如草莓、藍莓或覆盆子等日常所說的漿果。","examples":[{"en":"She added fresh berries to her breakfast.","zh":"她在早餐里加了新鮮漿果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This berry is sweet but very soft.","zh":"這種漿果很甜，但非常軟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/berry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d8231352d5b19c4","term":"berry","forms":["berry","berries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物學上的漿果","explanation":"在植物學中，berry是一類由單個子房發育而成、種子不包在硬核裡的軟果；這個定義比日常用法更嚴格。","examples":[{"en":"Botanically, a tomato is a berry.","zh":"從植物學上說，番茄是一種漿果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unlike a strawberry, a grape is a true botanical berry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/berry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bcaffed4d27f7b2dd93","word":"beside","forms":["beside"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c4b10dffaecc4b1","term":"beside","forms":["beside"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……旁邊","explanation":"表示某人或某物緊挨著另一物，處在它的一側。這是 beside 最直接、最核心的畫面：一個東西站在另一個東西旁邊。","examples":[{"en":"She left her umbrella beside the door.","zh":"她把雨傘放在門旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A child was sitting beside me on the bus.","zh":"公交車上有個孩子坐在我旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00b9c9cb3cda7dc5","term":"beside","forms":["beside"],"pos":"prep","zh":"與……無關；偏離重點","explanation":"把某個問題想象成站在討論主題的旁邊，表示它不相關、沒有切中要點。它常用於說明某個事實、意見或爭論與當前問題無關。","examples":[{"en":"Whether he likes the plan is beside the point.","zh":"他是否喜歡這個計劃並不是重點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Arguing about last year is beside the point; we need a solution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-745c9326c6e9f07755f0","word":"besides","forms":["besides"],"officialPos":"adv./prep.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d37147a862cc547","term":"besides","forms":["besides"],"pos":"adv","zh":"此外；另外","explanation":"表示在已經說出的內容之外，再補充一個事實或情況，相當於“此外、另外、還”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is cheap, and besides, it is close to the station.","zh":"這家旅館很便宜，而且離車站也近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room is too small; besides, it leaks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/besides","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5994791cc1a5b4c","term":"besides","forms":["besides"],"pos":"adv","zh":"而且；況且","explanation":"用於強調後來補上的理由特別重要，常表示“況且、再說”，使前面的判斷更有說服力。","examples":[{"en":"I don't want to drive tonight. Besides, the roads may be icy.","zh":"我今晚不想開車。再說，路面可能會結冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should leave now; besides, everyone is ready.","zh":"我們現在就該走了，而且大家都準備好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/besides","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35ae7055cfd225b0","term":"besides","forms":["besides"],"pos":"prep","zh":"除……之外還……","explanation":"表示某物件之外還有其他物件也包括在內，相當於“除了……還……”。這是介詞 besides 最常見的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"Besides English, she speaks Spanish and French.","zh":"除了英語以外，她還會說西班牙語和法語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Who besides Maria knows the answer?","zh":"除了瑪麗亞以外，還有誰知道答案？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/besides","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f4375ec65c2c4092a1c","word":"best","forms":["best"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a51bcfedb8dec43","term":"best","forms":["best","bester","bestest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最好的","explanation":"它是 good 的最高階，表示在比較範圍內質量或表現最好的人或事物。","examples":[{"en":"She is the best teacher I have ever had.","zh":"她是我遇到過的最好的老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This orchard produces the best peaches in the county.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/best","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a8a6609b4e2d970","term":"best","forms":["best","bester","bestest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最優的；最合適的","explanation":"它表示說話人認為某個選擇、條件或方案最令人滿意、最有利，因此中文常譯為“最好、最合適”。","examples":[{"en":"This is the best place for a quiet dinner.","zh":"這裡是安靜吃晚飯的最佳地點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This route offers our best chance of arriving before dark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/best","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb6fbdea78185014","term":"best","forms":["best"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最好還是；最好","explanation":"在建議或警告中，它表示按照某種做法最穩妥、最有利，常帶有“你最好這樣做，否則可能有麻煩”的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"You'd best leave before the roads get busy.","zh":"你最好在路上變擁堵前離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You had best bring a spare pair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/best","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6e7ed613305f40a","term":"best","forms":["best","bests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"竭盡全力；最大努力","explanation":"它指一個人在當時條件下能拿出的最大努力或最高水平，do my best 就是“我盡力而為”。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll do my best to finish the report tonight.","zh":"我會盡力今晚完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We did our best despite the equipment failure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/best","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ae467cc10e077a17e83","word":"bet","forms":["bet"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b492b6ff1848c7a","term":"bet","forms":["bet","bets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賭注；賭局","explanation":"雙方約定根據某件事的結果付出或贏得錢等東西；押對的一方獲勝，押錯的一方承擔賭注。","examples":[{"en":"I lost a bet and had to cook dinner for everyone.","zh":"我打賭輸了，只好給大家做晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She placed a small bet on the home team.","zh":"她在主隊身上押了一小筆賭注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f0971a66b9b4c3b","term":"bet","forms":["bet","bets","betting","betted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打賭；下注","explanation":"把錢、物品或承諾押在某個結果上，結果揭曉後由輸的一方付出賭注。","examples":[{"en":"I bet ten dollars that our team would win.","zh":"我押了十美元，賭我們隊會贏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They bet on which movie would sell more tickets.","zh":"他們打賭哪部電影會賣出更多票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d0e65fe58b0cfc3","term":"bet","forms":["bet","bets","betting","betted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確信；指望","explanation":"表示說話人非常有把握，認為某事一定或很可能如此，彷彿願意拿賭注來證明自己的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"I bet you'll enjoy the new restaurant.","zh":"我敢肯定你會喜歡那家新餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"“Can you help me move?” “You bet.”","zh":"“你能幫我搬家嗎？”“當然可以。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fff1513949cbf175c91","word":"betray","forms":["betray"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-769d1e00786ed2f4","term":"betray","forms":["betray","betrays","betraying","betrayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出賣給敵人","explanation":"指因背信或欺詐，把原本信任自己的人、組織或地方交到敵人手裡。這是“背叛”這一核心畫面的最具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The guard betrayed the refugees to the enemy.","zh":"那名守衛把難民出賣給了敵人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An informer betrayed the fugitives to enemy soldiers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/betray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83bc202e751a1c03","term":"betray","forms":["betray","betrays","betraying","betrayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"背叛；辜負","explanation":"指對信任自己的人、某項事業或某種原則不忠，用行動證明自己不可靠。它不一定涉及把人交給敵人，但都包含“辜負信任”這條主線。","examples":[{"en":"She felt that her closest friend had betrayed her.","zh":"她覺得自己最親近的朋友背叛了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He would never betray the cause he believed in.","zh":"他絕不會背叛自己所信奉的事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/betray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21799958e5fb74e0","term":"betray","forms":["betray","betrays","betraying","betrayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"無意暴露","explanation":"指某個細節、動作或跡象不由自主地顯露出原本想隱藏的事實。這裡不一定有背叛或惡意，而是“隱藏的東西從門縫裡露了出來”。","examples":[{"en":"Her nervous smile betrayed her fear.","zh":"她緊張的笑容暴露了她的恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His accent betrayed where he grew up.","zh":"他的口音暴露了他在哪裡長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/betray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7d5dcc369426e2e5f8d","word":"better","forms":["better"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8303d7ffd31cf324","term":"better","forms":["better","betterer","betterest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"更好的","explanation":"這是 good 的比較級，表示某人或某物比另一個更好，或比以前的狀態更好。","examples":[{"en":"This plan is better than the old one.","zh":"這個計劃比原來的更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I feel a little better today.","zh":"我今天感覺好一點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/better","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7ff055eb5f131f4","term":"better","forms":["better","betterer","betterest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"狀態更好","explanation":"這是 well 的比較級，表示做某事的狀態或效果比以前更好，尤其常說身體狀況或工作表現。","examples":[{"en":"She sings better after taking a few lessons.","zh":"她上了幾節課後唱得更好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her ankle feels better after a night's rest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/better","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbdd08b5750d9638","term":"better","forms":["better"],"pos":"adv","zh":"做得更好","explanation":"表示某個動作進行得比以前更順利、更有效或效果更好。","examples":[{"en":"The computer works better after the update.","zh":"電腦更新後執行得更好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sings better when she feels relaxed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/better","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86ab4440177f049c","term":"better","forms":["better"],"pos":"verb","zh":"最好還是","explanation":"在口語中表示某人最好採取某個行動，否則可能有不好的結果；它來自 had better 的縮略。","examples":[{"en":"You better save your work before closing the program.","zh":"你最好在關閉程式前儲存工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You better not be late again.","zh":"你最好別再遲到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/better","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fbb27fbdc4f4dd04e216","word":"between","forms":["between"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1fb4963c00c5cb97","term":"between","forms":["between"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在兩者之間","explanation":"表示某人或某物位於兩個物件、地點、時間點或程度之間；重點是它處在兩端所形成的中間位置。","examples":[{"en":"The café is between the library and the station.","zh":"那家咖啡館在圖書館和車站之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please call me between six and seven tonight.","zh":"請在今晚六點到七點之間給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/between","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81b1f0f3d6643eee","term":"between","forms":["between"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在選項之間作選擇","explanation":"把兩個或幾個選項放在兩端，表示必須從這些選項中選出一個或作出取捨。","examples":[{"en":"We have to choose between taking the train and driving.","zh":"我們必須在坐火車和開車之間作出選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She must choose between medicine and engineering.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/between","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27648bbe98f14b9d6fb4","word":"beverage","forms":["beverage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-44f502807e67a6ef","term":"beverage","forms":["beverage","beverages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飲料","explanation":"指供人飲用的液體這一大類，包括茶、咖啡、牛奶、果汁、軟飲料和酒等，通常不把水作為這裡的典型例子。它強調“可飲用的飲品”這一類別，不限定必須含酒精。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel offers tea, coffee, and other hot beverages.","zh":"這家酒店供應茶、咖啡和其他熱飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please choose one beverage with your meal.","zh":"請從套餐中選擇一種飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beverage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bbcd79620297d1a4681","word":"beware","forms":["beware"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea8bb8f2f2da82c5","term":"beware","forms":["beware","bewares","bewaring","bewared","bewore"],"pos":"verb","zh":"當心；提防","explanation":"表示看到潛在危險後提高警惕，提醒自己或別人不要受到傷害、欺騙或不良影響；核心畫面就是看到警告牌後“當心”。","examples":[{"en":"Beware of stray dogs when you walk through this neighborhood.","zh":"在這個社群走路時要當心流浪狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Beware: the steps are slippery after it rains.","zh":"當心：下雨後這些臺階很滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beware","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e8818d1dd1914902733","word":"beyond","forms":["beyond"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e29481686e7f25d","term":"beyond","forms":["beyond"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……更遠處","explanation":"表示某物位於參照點的更遠一側，先從實際空間中的“越過這條線”來理解。","examples":[{"en":"A small village lies beyond the hills.","zh":"群山那邊有一個小村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old monastery lies beyond the hills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36150876cccf0788","term":"beyond","forms":["beyond"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……的另一邊","explanation":"表示在某個邊界、標記或限制的遠側，常用於說明某處不應繼續進入或進行某事。","examples":[{"en":"Please do not walk beyond the gate.","zh":"請不要走到大門外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The orchard lies beyond the railway embankment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3143b3937a533158","term":"beyond","forms":["beyond"],"pos":"prep","zh":"超過；超出","explanation":"表示實際表現越過了某個標準、預期或能力上限，因此可理解為“超過那條線”。","examples":[{"en":"The team went beyond our expectations.","zh":"這個團隊的表現超出了我們的預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs are beyond my mechanical skills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-deb2ebbc7ce94294","term":"beyond","forms":["beyond"],"pos":"prep","zh":"超出理解範圍","explanation":"表示某事越過了某人的知識或理解能力，因此那個人無法理解、解釋或掌握它。","examples":[{"en":"The mathematician's explanation was beyond me.","zh":"那位數學家的解釋超出了我的理解能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Quantum theory remains beyond my understanding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa4824e83746480e1029","word":"bias","forms":["bias"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53c54a1118aff70e","term":"bias","forms":["bias","biases","biasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偏見；偏向","explanation":"指一個人、群體或制度不完全中立，習慣性地更支援某一方，因而影響判斷或行動。它保留了“向一邊斜”的畫面：思想沒有保持平衡，而是朝一邊偏去。","examples":[{"en":"The article shows a clear bias against small businesses.","zh":"這篇文章明顯帶有反對小企業的偏見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to check our own bias before making a decision.","zh":"作出決定前，我們需要檢查自己的偏見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bias","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4abc0474b8f787e6","term":"bias","forms":["bias","biases","biasses","biasing","biassing","biased","biassed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使偏向；影響判斷","explanation":"指某種偏見、經驗或外部因素把人的看法、判斷或行動推向某一方，使其不再完全中立。它是名詞“偏向”的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"Personal experience can bias the way we judge risks.","zh":"個人經歷可能會影響我們判斷風險的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wording of the question biased the results.","zh":"問題的措辭使結果產生了偏向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bias","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a648c8bec4cfcb5d2f61","word":"bicycle/bike","forms":["bicycle","bike"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14e71a1196d3478d","term":"bicycle","forms":["bicycle","bicycles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腳踏車","explanation":"一種通常有兩個前後排列的車輪、車把、座位和腳踏板的車輛，騎車人透過踩踏板使它前進。","examples":[{"en":"She rides her bicycle to work every day.","zh":"她每天騎腳踏車上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My bicycle is locked outside the library.","zh":"我的腳踏車鎖在圖書館外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bicycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfdac80d692d7764","term":"bike","forms":["bike","bikes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腳踏車","explanation":"最常見的意思是腳踏車：有兩個輪子、車把和座位，通常靠人踩踏板前進。","examples":[{"en":"I ride my bike to work when the weather is good.","zh":"天氣好的時候，我騎腳踏車上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her bike is locked outside the library.","zh":"她的腳踏車鎖在圖書館外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0e0efc4fc56af4904d5","word":"bid","forms":["bid"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75ab0ac59bd16f21","term":"bid","forms":["bid","bids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拍賣出價；投標報價","explanation":"bid 是買方願意支付的價格，也可以指為獲得一項工作而提出的報價；拍賣時就是把自己的“價碼”喊出來。","examples":[{"en":"Her bid for the painting was the highest.","zh":"她對那幅畫的出價最高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company submitted a bid for the construction project.","zh":"這家公司為該建築專案提交了投標報價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3ee3209b08100a4","term":"bid","forms":["bid","bids","bidding"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出價；競價","explanation":"bid 作動詞時，表示在拍賣中報出自己願意支付的價格，也就是把自己的價碼喊出來。","examples":[{"en":"Several people bid for the antique vase.","zh":"有幾個人競價購買那隻古董花瓶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He bid $500 for the bicycle.","zh":"他為那輛腳踏車出價五百美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ca8be8f47a18336","term":"bid","forms":["bid","bids","bidding"],"pos":"verb","zh":"報出某個價格","explanation":"這個及物用法強調把某個具體金額作為報價報出來，是“出價”動作的直接表達。","examples":[{"en":"The collector bid ten thousand dollars for the sculpture.","zh":"那位收藏家為這件雕塑出價一萬美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one was willing to bid that much.","zh":"沒有人願意出那麼高的價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a21fe6d592a19b7de89","word":"big","forms":["big"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82ae3b96bd0092bd","term":"big","forms":["big","bigger","biggest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大的；體積大的","explanation":"表示東西的體積、尺寸或佔用空間超出通常尺度，也可以形容動物或建築物等整體很大。","examples":[{"en":"Elephants are big animals.","zh":"大象是體型很大的動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a big table for everyone.","zh":"我們需要一張能坐下所有人的大桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a10dc3eec3bfea60","term":"big","forms":["big","bigger","biggest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"重要的；意義重大的","explanation":"表示某件事的影響、意義或重要性超出通常程度，也就是“事情變大了”或成了大事。","examples":[{"en":"Getting this job is a big opportunity for her.","zh":"得到這份工作對她來說是一個很大的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It’s a big decision, so take your time.","zh":"這是一個重大決定，所以你慢慢考慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0e560ab404e938a4a9c","word":"bilateral","forms":["bilateral"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13ef863644e6fcfa","term":"bilateral","forms":["bilateral","more bilateral","most bilateral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"雙方的；雙邊的","explanation":"表示某事涉及兩個國家、組織、團體或其他方面，重點是“有兩方參加或受影響”。它不一定說明雙方地位相同，只說明範圍限於兩方。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries resumed bilateral talks after a long pause.","zh":"兩國在長時間中斷後恢復了雙邊會談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both sides called for stronger bilateral cooperation.","zh":"雙方都呼籲加強雙邊合作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bilateral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b25021ab7c9fa33d","term":"bilateral","forms":["bilateral","more bilateral","most bilateral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"雙方共同的；雙向的","explanation":"在“雙方共同參與”的基礎上，這一義項更突出兩方都以相應的方式參加，而不是隻有一方單獨行動。可以把它理解為那座橋由兩邊一起使用、一起維護。","examples":[{"en":"The talks were conducted on a bilateral basis, with both sides given the same amount of time.","zh":"會談以雙邊方式進行，雙方獲得了相同的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two universities signed a bilateral exchange agreement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bilateral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-623210167553939c87ed","word":"bill","forms":["bill"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38d815d649190252","term":"bill","forms":["bill","bills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法案","explanation":"bill是提交給立法機關討論、表決並可能成為法律的擬議法律文字。它仍處於提案階段時叫bill，透過並生效後通常稱為law。","examples":[{"en":"The government introduced a bill to improve road safety.","zh":"政府提出了一項改善道路安全的法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bill passed the Senate last night.","zh":"這項法案昨晚在參議院獲得透過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc1cc264aa3adc41","term":"bill","forms":["bill","bills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紙幣","explanation":"在美國和加拿大英語中，bill指一張紙幣，也就是面額明確的現金紙鈔；它正好符合“寫著金額的正式紙張”這一記憶線索。","examples":[{"en":"I found a twenty-dollar bill in my jacket.","zh":"我在夾克裡發現了一張二十美元的紙幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you have a ten-dollar bill for the bus fare?","zh":"你有十美元的紙幣付公交車費嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d6354861130cd98","term":"bill","forms":["bill","bills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賬單；發票","explanation":"bill是列出商品、服務或工作專案及其應付金額的賬單或發票；這就是“寫著事項或金額的正式紙張”的最常見用法。","examples":[{"en":"Could we have the bill, please?","zh":"請把賬單給我們，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The electrician sent us a bill for the repair.","zh":"電工給我們寄來了這次維修的賬單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-585bfc15cf96e714","term":"bill","forms":["bill","bills","billing","billed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開賬單；向……收費","explanation":"bill作動詞時表示把費用列入賬單並向某人收費，正是從“寫著金額的正式紙張”引申出來的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel billed us for the damaged towel.","zh":"酒店因毛巾損壞向我們收取了費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic will bill your insurance company directly.","zh":"診所會直接向你的保險公司收費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80c697e9924a526066b2","word":"billion","forms":["billion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0edc4e5e7266b1ca","term":"billion","forms":["billion","billions"],"pos":"num","zh":"十億","explanation":"在現代英語中，billion 通常是十億，即 1,000,000,000。它可以表示人口、金額、債務等具體而巨大的數量。","examples":[{"en":"The project will cost three billion dollars.","zh":"這個專案將耗資三十億美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"More than a billion people use the service every year.","zh":"每年有十多億人使用這項服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/billion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-607ce11c91fab90d","term":"billion","forms":["billion","billions"],"pos":"num","zh":"數不清的多","explanation":"在非正式、誇張的表達中，billion 可以不表示精確的十億，而是說某物多得驚人，類似“無數、成千上萬”。","examples":[{"en":"I have told you a billion times to lock the door.","zh":"我都告訴過你無數次要鎖門了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I've reminded you a billion times to lock up.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/billion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51a1f05af85e342e3c84","word":"bin","forms":["bin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0414c8553f5f3b1e","term":"bin","forms":["bin","bins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"箱、桶、儲物容器","explanation":"指有邊界、用來裝東西的箱子、桶或類似容器；它是“收納格”這一核心意象的最基本用法，不一定專門裝垃圾。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer keeps the corn in a large bin.","zh":"農民把玉米放在一個大箱子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the toys back in the bin.","zh":"請把玩具放回箱子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f08dd851c430f52f3fbe","word":"bind","forms":["bind"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5826c5ede07dbc5","term":"bind","forms":["bind","binds","binding","bound","binded","bounden","ybound","ybounden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"捆綁；繫住","explanation":"指用繩、帶子等把東西繫住，使它們不能散開或自由移動，是整組詞最具體的核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"They bound the books together with a length of string.","zh":"他們用一根繩子把這些書捆在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer bound the harvested wheat into bundles.","zh":"農夫把收割的小麥捆成了一束束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2683d78f541f2b5","term":"bind","forms":["bind","binds","binding","bound","binded","bounden","ybound","ybounden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……捆緊；固定在一起","explanation":"指主動用繩、帶、鏈子等把多個東西牢牢固定在一起，是“綁”的直接及物用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please bind the papers together before you file them.","zh":"請先把這些檔案裝訂在一起，再歸檔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bound the branches with soft wire.","zh":"她用軟鐵絲把樹枝捆在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1a9de9f4094eed9","term":"bind","forms":["bind","binds","binding","bound","binded","bounden","ybound","ybounden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"束縛；牽制","explanation":"指用物理力量或其他力量把某人、某物牢牢限制在某處或某種狀態中；重力把行星留在軌道上就是同一條“牽住”的思路。","examples":[{"en":"The heavy chain bound the gate to the post.","zh":"沉重的鏈條把大門牢牢拴在柱子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gravity binds the moon to Earth.","zh":"重力把月球牽制在地球周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08eb0ba299423db2","term":"bind","forms":["bind","binds","binding","bound","binded","bounden","ybound","ybounden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使受義務或承諾約束","explanation":"指法律、責任、承諾、誓言或感情像繩子一樣牽住某人，使其必須遵守或承擔某種義務。","examples":[{"en":"The contract binds both sides to the agreed schedule.","zh":"合同使雙方都必須遵守約定的時間表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt bound by her promise to help.","zh":"她覺得自己受諾言約束，必須提供幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a2f99869acda1bc80ef","word":"biography","forms":["biography"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0945981e9415f0eb","term":"biography","forms":["biography","biographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳記；生平故事","explanation":"指以書籍或其他較完整的形式，講述某個人一生經歷的故事，尤其是已經出版的作品。它把零散的人生經歷整理成一條可以閱讀的故事線。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a biography of Marie Curie for my sister.","zh":"我給妹妹買了一本居里夫人的傳記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several biographies of the actor have been published.","zh":"這位演員的幾部傳記已經出版了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d220495429bf7364","term":"biography","forms":["biography","biographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳記寫作藝術","explanation":"指把人的一生寫成傳記這一整套寫作方式或藝術，不是某一本具體的傳記，而是“如何書寫人生故事”這一領域。","examples":[{"en":"The course explores the art of biography.","zh":"這門課程探討傳記寫作藝術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The seminar explores biography as a literary art.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f6ec582c1001e4d33947","word":"biological","forms":["biological"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-07e33cca4ef3335c","term":"biological","forms":["biological"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生物學的；與生物學有關的","explanation":"指研究生命、生物及其活動的學科，或指建立在這類研究之上的觀點、方法和證據。它是最寬的一層含義：凡是和“生物學”這門學科相連的，都可以用 biological 描寫。","examples":[{"en":"The report examines the biological causes of sleep problems.","zh":"這份報告研究睡眠問題的生物學原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are studying the biological effects of the new drug.","zh":"科學家正在研究這種新藥對生物體的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biological","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ba22c62cb18c269","term":"biological","forms":["biological"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體的；解剖學的","explanation":"指身體的結構、功能或生理特徵，重點從“生物學”進一步落到人的身體上。談到 biological sex 時，它強調身體和生理層面的性別特徵，不等同於社會或個人認同。","examples":[{"en":"The test measures several biological changes in the body.","zh":"這項檢測測量身體中的幾種生理變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Biological differences influence how the drugs are absorbed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biological","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af8f827a0c20db87fdd3","word":"biology","forms":["biology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a2f74ba42fc37bb","term":"biology","forms":["biology","biologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生命科學","explanation":"biology 是研究所有生命和生命現象的學科，包括生物的結構、功能、變化以及彼此之間的關係。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to study biology at university.","zh":"她決定在大學學習生物學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Biology helps us understand how living things adapt.","zh":"生物學幫助我們理解生物如何適應環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3086bd63fe11d7e","term":"biology","forms":["biology","biologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某種生物的生物學特徵","explanation":"在“the biology of + 生物”中，biology 指某種生物的結構、身體功能、行為以及它如何生活；這是把“生命地圖”放大到一種生物上。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are studying the biology of the honeybee.","zh":"研究人員正在研究蜜蜂的生物學特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Little is known about the biology of this cave fish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a5179eecc0fe18760ba","word":"bird","forms":["bird"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d5c402aa5e417b8","term":"bird","forms":["bird","birds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鳥","explanation":"bird 是有羽毛、通常有翅膀並能產卵的鳥類動物的通稱，麻雀、鴨子等都屬於 bird。","examples":[{"en":"A small bird landed on the garden fence.","zh":"一隻小鳥落在了花園的圍欄上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched birds from the kitchen window.","zh":"我們從廚房窗戶看鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bird","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7a18611f42eff8d5fba","word":"birth","forms":["birth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edf081dd4f17887e","term":"birth","forms":["birth","births"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出生；分娩","explanation":"指嬰兒或其他胎生動物從母體出來、開始生命的過程；重點是“出生”這一生命起點，而不是具體某一天。","examples":[{"en":"The baby needed medical care immediately after birth.","zh":"這個嬰兒出生後立刻需要醫療護理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The midwife assisted at the baby's birth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/birth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06d7aedd586b7276","term":"birth","forms":["birth","births"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誕生；起源","explanation":"從“生命開始存在”引申為某個國家、制度、運動、想法或時代開始形成，也就是它的誕生或起點。","examples":[{"en":"The invention marked the birth of a new industry.","zh":"這項發明標誌著一個新產業的誕生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discovery marked the birth of modern genetics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/birth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-660f2dd5a2e102002a44","word":"biscuit","forms":["biscuit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e2e38ec8d0873cef","term":"biscuit","forms":["biscuit","biscuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餅乾；小甜餅","explanation":"在英國、澳大利亞、紐西蘭等地，biscuit通常是小而扁的烘焙食品，可以硬而脆，也可以較軟但有一定硬度，常作為點心或配茶食用。","examples":[{"en":"She offered me a chocolate biscuit with my tea.","zh":"她給我一塊巧克力餅乾，和茶一起吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Crumbs from his biscuit covered the open newspaper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biscuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0e2b28d803d22bf","term":"biscuit","forms":["biscuit","biscuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鬆軟鹹味小麵包","explanation":"在美國和加拿大，biscuit通常是用膨鬆劑做成的小型鬆軟麵包，口感蓬鬆、略帶酥層，一般不甜，常作為正餐配食。","examples":[{"en":"We had warm biscuits with gravy for breakfast.","zh":"我們早餐吃了熱的鬆軟小麵包，配肉汁一起吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He split a warm biscuit and added gravy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biscuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0013c2e0a387e4c6e69","word":"bit","forms":["bit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d175f7dbf76cf69","term":"bit","forms":["bit","bits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一小塊；一點","explanation":"指某物的一小塊或少量。","examples":[{"en":"A bit of plaster fell from the ceiling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"He saved the last bit of cake for his sister.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ac64653b87abeac","term":"bit","forms":["bit","bits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一點兒","explanation":"可表示程度很小，也可用於強調完全沒有。","examples":[{"en":"Could you move your chair a bit closer?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She left a tiny bit of toast on her plate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e8f8ffed14647b2","term":"bit","forms":["bit","bits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"二進位制位","explanation":"bit可以理解為被切到最小的一份數字資訊：它只能取0或1這兩個值中的一個。","examples":[{"en":"Each bit in the code is either 0 or 1.","zh":"這段程式碼中的每一位不是0就是1。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A single bit can store only one of two possible values.","zh":"一個二進位制位只能儲存兩個可能值中的一個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8420c85c2aadaebac268","word":"bite","forms":["bite"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bacd2e5f0aaf82bb","term":"bite","forms":["bite","bites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咬這一動作","explanation":"指用牙齒咬的動作，核心畫面是牙齒夾住目標並對它產生作用。","examples":[{"en":"The dog gave the toy a quick bite.","zh":"狗迅速咬了一下玩具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We waited for hours but never got a bite.","zh":"我們等了好幾個小時，卻始終沒有魚咬鉤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69f73c5ae73a6e7c","term":"bite","forms":["bite","bites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咬傷；咬痕","explanation":"指被動物或人咬後留下的傷口或痕跡，也就是牙齒夾住目標後留下的作用。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor cleaned the dog bite and checked for infection.","zh":"醫生清理了狗咬傷，並檢查是否感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I still have a small bite mark on my hand.","zh":"我的手上仍有一個小小的咬痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61a70272a8e8367a","term":"bite","forms":["bite","bites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一口；一小塊食物","explanation":"指大小大致適合一口吃下的食物分量；它體現的是牙齒一次能夾住並咬下的量。","examples":[{"en":"Try one bite of the cake before you decide.","zh":"你先嚐一口蛋糕再決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child took tiny bites of the apple.","zh":"孩子一小口一小口地吃蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1793004fba81e94","term":"bite","forms":["bite","bites","biting","bit","bitten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"咬下一口","explanation":"用牙齒夾住並切入食物或其他東西，通常會咬下一部分；這是“牙齒夾住並留下作用”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She bit into the apple and smiled.","zh":"她咬了一口蘋果，笑了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to bite your tongue.","zh":"小心別咬到舌頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbe8e9531e011540d71b","word":"bitter","forms":["bitter"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5a075e731c6ad43","term":"bitter","forms":["bitter","more bitter","bitterer","most bitter","bitterest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"苦的","explanation":"指味道帶有明顯苦味，常用於咖啡、藥物、蔬菜等；這是 bitter 最直接、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The coffee was too bitter to drink without sugar.","zh":"這咖啡太苦了，不加糖喝不下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some medicines leave a bitter taste in your mouth.","zh":"有些藥會在嘴裡留下苦味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bitter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59fe7994b1c9fb6c","term":"bitter","forms":["bitter","more bitter","bitterer","most bitter","bitterest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"刺骨的；刺耳的","explanation":"從苦味帶來的刺激感引申，形容寒風、寒冷、言語或經歷等讓人感到強烈不適、尖銳或難以忍受。","examples":[{"en":"A bitter wind was blowing across the empty field.","zh":"刺骨的寒風吹過空曠的田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke in a bitter voice after the argument.","zh":"爭吵後，她用尖刻的語氣說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bitter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6e4acc0d58497837b12","word":"bizarre","forms":["bizarre"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35e4f7859f576a68","term":"bizarre","forms":["bizarre","more bizarre","bizarrer","most bizarre","bizarrest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"怪誕的；離奇的","explanation":"形容某人、某事或某種行為明顯偏離常規，顯得古怪、離奇，甚至誇張得讓人側目。重點是“不同尋常而醒目”，不一定包含道德上的負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"His bizarre behaviour caused people to stare at him.","zh":"他古怪的行為引得人們紛紛盯著他看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a bizarre story written on the wall.","zh":"我們發現牆上寫著一個離奇的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bizarre","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c006c7e3ab14d686f635","word":"black","forms":["black"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a831f706b933b488","term":"black","forms":["black","blacker","more black","blackest","most black"],"pos":"adj","zh":"黑色的","explanation":"指物體吸收大部分光、幾乎不反射光，因此呈現黑色；這是“光被吸收、看不見”這一核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a black coat to work.","zh":"她穿了一件黑色外套去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Black ink stained his white sleeve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d6d4890ccc21d15","term":"black","forms":["black","blacker","more black","blackest","most black"],"pos":"adj","zh":"邪惡的；不祥的","explanation":"由“看不見光”的畫面引申，指壞的、邪惡的或帶來厄運的事物，常讓人聯想到黑暗的一面。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers feared that the old book contained black magic.","zh":"村民們害怕那本舊書裡有黑魔法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They feared a black curse had fallen upon the family.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03d2f4b2381c3c08","term":"black","forms":["black","blacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑色","explanation":"指吸收光線、幾乎不反射光線時呈現的顏色，也可以指這種顏色本身；這正是“光被吸收、看不見”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Black absorbs more sunlight than white.","zh":"黑色比白色吸收更多陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was dressed in black from head to toe.","zh":"她從頭到腳都穿著黑色衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00c764f20f35309838fb","word":"blackboard","forms":["blackboard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7edfb9167ac48c2","term":"blackboard","forms":["blackboard","blackboards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑板","explanation":"一種平整的書寫板，通常用粉筆在上面寫字、畫圖，講完後可以擦掉；它是課堂講解和展示圖表的工具。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher drew a map on the blackboard.","zh":"老師在黑板上畫了一張地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please clean the blackboard before the next class.","zh":"請在下一節課前把黑板擦乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackboard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13ffbb2f9bbad7fa8248","word":"blade","forms":["blade"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f1d56a6836a99fc","term":"blade","forms":["blade","blades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刀劍等的鋒刃","explanation":"指刀、劍、剃刀或其他切割工具上真正用來切割的鋒利部分，可以把它記成工具上的“切割葉片”。","examples":[{"en":"The knife blade is sharp enough to cut through the rope.","zh":"這把刀的刀刃鋒利得足以割斷繩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He carefully cleaned the blade after shaving.","zh":"他刮完鬍子後仔細清潔了刀片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7ccadd227b708dd","term":"blade","forms":["blade","blades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"槳葉、螺旋槳葉等工作部件","explanation":"指槳、螺旋槳、渦輪、冰球杆、鑿子等器具上扁平並負責推動、切削或接觸工作的部分，就是這類器具的“功能葉片”。","examples":[{"en":"One blade of the wind turbine was damaged in the storm.","zh":"風力渦輪機的一片葉片在暴風雨中受損。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The canoe paddle has a wide blade.","zh":"這把獨木舟槳有一片寬大的槳葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff65902168ad359f","term":"blade","forms":["blade","blades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"草葉；禾本科植物的葉片","explanation":"指草或穀物那種細長的葉片；這裡的 blade 就是植物真正的“葉片”。","examples":[{"en":"A single blade of grass pushed through the crack in the pavement.","zh":"一片草葉從人行道的裂縫中鑽了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dew covered the blades of wheat at sunrise.","zh":"日出時，麥葉上沾滿了露水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e7434f45c5ecbda1678","word":"blame","forms":["blame"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-534f74df0dcfa982","term":"blame","forms":["blame"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指責；責備","explanation":"指向某人或某事的負面批評，重點是“有人在責怪”。","examples":[{"en":"Blame came from every side after the decision was announced.","zh":"決定宣佈後，各方面的指責都來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tried to avoid blame by admitting her mistake immediately.","zh":"她立即承認錯誤，試圖避免受到指責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-680ffa744e6a3dde","term":"blame","forms":["blame"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過錯；應負的責任","explanation":"指壞事發生時某人或某事應承擔的過錯，重點是“責任歸誰”。","examples":[{"en":"The blame for the delay lies with the shipping company.","zh":"延誤的責任在運輸公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one knows where to place the blame for the failure.","zh":"沒人知道這次失敗的責任該歸到誰身上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae0c0e398cd2aaf4","term":"blame","forms":["blame","blames","blaming","blamed","blamest","blamedst","blameth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把責任歸給；責怪","explanation":"把壞結果指向某人，認為這個人是原因或應承擔責任的一方。","examples":[{"en":"The coach blamed the players for losing focus in the final minutes.","zh":"教練責怪球員在最後幾分鐘注意力不集中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don’t blame yourself for a mistake anyone could have made.","zh":"這種任何人都可能犯的錯，不要責怪自己。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff71cf74abb3ccb005b8","word":"blank","forms":["blank"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11e6c5594a668c50","term":"blank","forms":["blank","blanker","more blank","blankest","most blank"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空白的；未填寫的","explanation":"像一張還沒有寫字的白紙，表面沒有文字、印刷內容或其他標記，通常等著人填寫或使用。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your address on the blank form.","zh":"請在這張空白表格上填寫你的地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She handed me a blank sheet of paper.","zh":"她遞給我一張空白紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-79ee06325ab8ddfe","term":"blank","forms":["blank","blanker","more blank","blankest","most blank"],"pos":"adj","zh":"面無表情的；茫然的","explanation":"人的表情像暫時變成了空白，通常因為沒聽懂、沒反應過來，所以臉上沒有明顯的情緒或理解。","examples":[{"en":"When I asked him the question, he gave me a blank stare.","zh":"我問他那個問題時，他茫然地看著我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a blank expression during the explanation.","zh":"講解過程中，她臉上沒有任何表情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2449e16559b39443","term":"blank","forms":["blank","blanks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空白處","explanation":"blank 是紙張、表格或螢幕上沒有文字、數字或其他內容、等待填寫的空白處，就像白紙上還沒有寫字的地方。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your phone number in the blank at the bottom of the form.","zh":"請把你的電話號碼寫在表格底部的空白處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fill in the blanks with the correct words.","zh":"用正確的詞填空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7cd0fc6ee61e2a57b030","word":"blanket","forms":["blanket"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce2bed7b54d22ea6","term":"blanket","forms":["blanket","blankets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毯子","explanation":"一種通常較厚、用於睡覺或休息時保暖的織物，通常蓋在身體上。","examples":[{"en":"The baby was cold, so his mother put a blanket over him.","zh":"寶寶覺得冷，所以媽媽給他蓋了一條毯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I keep an extra blanket at the foot of the bed.","zh":"我在床腳放著一條備用毯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blanket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dd43cca88d60953","term":"blanket","forms":["blanket","blankets","blanketing","blanketting","blanketed","blanketted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"覆蓋；籠罩","explanation":"把某物蓋住，或使某處像被毯子蓋住一樣；覆蓋物可以是真正的毯子，也可以是雪、霧等。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh snow blanketed the fields overnight.","zh":"一夜之間，新雪覆蓋了田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The valley was blanketed in smoke after the fire.","zh":"火災後，山谷籠罩在煙霧中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blanket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-982d3cec0c8e060d5b71","word":"blast","forms":["blast"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37e6518f046327b5","term":"blast","forms":["blast","blasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈的風","explanation":"指突然猛烈衝來的風，也可指車輛行駛時迎面形成的強風；核心畫面就是一股風力強勁地衝出來。","examples":[{"en":"A blast of cold wind hit us when the door opened.","zh":"門一開啟，一股猛烈的冷風就迎面吹來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclists faced blasts of wind on the exposed road.","zh":"騎車人在無遮蔽的道路上遇到了陣陣強風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c6794a4578f721e5","term":"blast","forms":["blast","blasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爆破","explanation":"指為了炸碎或摧毀岩石等物體而進行的爆炸；強大力量從內部猛烈衝出是這個義項的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Workers used a controlled blast to remove the old concrete wall.","zh":"工人用一次受控爆破拆除了舊混凝土牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The blast broke the rock into smaller pieces.","zh":"爆破把岩石炸成了更小的碎塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-587a3bdba3b9995d","term":"blast","forms":["blast","blasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痛快的經歷","explanation":"非正式地表示一段非常開心、盡興的時光，像經歷了一次強烈而令人滿足的衝擊。","examples":[{"en":"We had a blast at the beach yesterday.","zh":"我們昨天在海灘上玩得特別痛快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You’ll have a blast at the music festival.","zh":"你在音樂節上一定會玩得非常盡興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7fdc5f3d1f78d0b","term":"blast","forms":["blast","blasts","blasting","blasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把音樂開得很大聲","explanation":"指透過揚聲器把音樂以很大的音量播放出來，聲音像猛烈地衝到四周；常帶有口語色彩。","examples":[{"en":"They blasted music from the car all afternoon.","zh":"他們整個下午都把音樂從車裡放得震天響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don’t blast the television while the baby is sleeping.","zh":"寶寶睡覺時，請別把電視開得那麼大聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-88a5c49d8cb7f295df95","word":"blaze","forms":["blaze"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cc2a20e46392fbe","term":"blaze","forms":["blaze","blazes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈的火焰","explanation":"指燃燒迅猛、火焰很多併發出強光的火，畫面比普通的小火更猛烈。","examples":[{"en":"The blaze lit up the whole hillside.","zh":"熊熊火焰照亮了整片山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Firefighters worked through the night to control the blaze.","zh":"消防員連夜奮戰，控制住了大火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blaze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d3e9fabfdcadb07","term":"blaze","forms":["blaze","blazes","blazing","blazed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"熊熊燃燒","explanation":"指火正在猛烈燃燒併發出明亮火焰，正是 blaze 的核心動態畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The campfire blazed brightly against the dark sky.","zh":"篝火在黑暗的天空下熊熊燃燒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dry branches blazed fiercely in the fireplace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blaze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2cde8d18812e77ae6c37","word":"bleach","forms":["bleach"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c971c654ba746a7f","term":"bleach","forms":["bleach","bleaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漂白劑","explanation":"bleach 是能把東西的顏色漂淡、漂白的化學品，也常用於消毒。日常語境中常指含氯或含過氧化物的漂白製劑。","examples":[{"en":"Keep the bleach away from children and pets.","zh":"把漂白劑放在兒童和寵物夠不到的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Never mix bleach with other cleaning products.","zh":"絕不要把漂白劑和其他清潔產品混合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bleach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-755c554536d6b795","term":"bleach","forms":["bleach","bleaches","bleaching","bleached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漂白；使變淺","explanation":"指用漂白劑等處理衣物、紙張或頭髮，使它們變白或顏色變淺。這是 bleach 最常見的動詞義，核心畫面就是把原來的顏色“洗淡”。","examples":[{"en":"She bleached her hair before the summer holiday.","zh":"她在暑假前把頭髮漂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cleaner used bleach to remove the stain.","zh":"清潔工用漂白劑去除汙漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bleach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-680f2c08fd03836aa181","word":"bleed","forms":["bleed"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5c4196eb249adc3","term":"bleed","forms":["bleed","bleeds","bleeding","bled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"流血","explanation":"指受傷的血管流出血，主語通常是人、動物或身體部位；這是 bleed 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Her nose started to bleed in the cold air.","zh":"她的鼻子在冷空氣中開始流血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Press on the cut until it stops bleeding.","zh":"按住傷口，直到它不再流血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bleed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c6617c551ad0e252","term":"bleed","forms":["bleed","bleeds","bleeding","bled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滲開；洇出","explanation":"指液體、顏色或墨水從原本限定的位置向周圍擴散，像血從傷口向外滲一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The red ink bled into the wet paper.","zh":"紅墨水洇進了溼紙裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The red dye bled into the white fabric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bleed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-727c1e414b34819f8cb5","word":"blend","forms":["blend"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26209bc15b0750d0","term":"blend","forms":["blend","blends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合體；融合物","explanation":"指兩種或多種東西混合後形成的整體，重點是各種成分結合在一起，呈現出新的整體效果。","examples":[{"en":"The café serves a blend of Colombian and Ethiopian coffee.","zh":"這家咖啡館供應哥倫比亞咖啡和衣索比亞咖啡的混合咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sauce is a blend of yogurt and herbs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bb441a825242d3f","term":"blend","forms":["blend","blends","blending","blended","blent"],"pos":"verb","zh":"混合；融合","explanation":"指把不同的東西混在一起，使它們結合成一個整體；也可以指讓某物逐漸融入另一物。","examples":[{"en":"Blend the chickpeas with olive oil, lemon juice, and garlic.","zh":"把鷹嘴豆、橄欖油、檸檬汁和大蒜混合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer blended modern lines with traditional details.","zh":"這位設計師把現代線條和傳統細節融合在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2ba2144f6cd7505f252","word":"bless","forms":["bless"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c91d920b4ed404e2","term":"bless","forms":["bless","blesses","blessing","blest","blessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使神聖；祝聖","explanation":"指透過宗教儀式使某物或某人歸於神聖，用祝福把普通物件置於宗教保護之下。這是 bless 最直接、最傳統的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"The priest blessed the new church before the first service.","zh":"牧師在第一次禮拜前為新教堂舉行了祝聖儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family asked the priest to bless their home.","zh":"這家人請牧師為他們的家祝福。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1707d5bf6d44d568","term":"bless","forms":["bless","blesses","blessing","blest","blessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"祈求神恩","explanation":"指向神祈求，讓某人、某物或某件事得到神的恩惠、保護或良好結果。它仍然保留了“伸出祝福之手”的核心畫面，但重點從使其神聖轉為求神施恩。","examples":[{"en":"May God bless you and keep you safe on your journey.","zh":"願上帝賜福於你，讓你一路平安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The priest blessed the animals gathered outside the chapel.","zh":"牧師為聚集在小教堂外的動物祈福。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-588d3cff31162034f6f6","word":"blessing","forms":["blessing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9bc60ecd7be4e0e9","term":"blessing","forms":["blessing","blessings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神聖的助佑","explanation":"指神明或超自然力量給予的保護、幫助或恩賜，像一道從上方降下來的好意。","examples":[{"en":"The family believed the safe journey was a blessing from heaven.","zh":"這家人認為平安的旅程是上天的恩賜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They asked for a blessing before starting the long trip.","zh":"他們在開始長途旅行前祈求祝福。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blessing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe4c001011cda06d","term":"blessing","forms":["blessing","blessings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祈福或祝福詞","explanation":"指在宗教儀式中正式說出的、用來祈求神聖助佑的話或儀式性宣告。","examples":[{"en":"The priest pronounced the blessing after the wedding ceremony.","zh":"牧師在婚禮儀式結束後進行了祝福。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone stood quietly while the blessing was read.","zh":"宣讀祝福詞時，大家都靜靜地站著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blessing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21032ad3ff45a3ab","term":"blessing","forms":["blessing","blessings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"批准","explanation":"指有權力的人正式表示同意或支援，彷彿把“可以進行”的許可賜給某項計劃。","examples":[{"en":"We won't publish the report without the director's blessing.","zh":"沒有主任的批准，我們不會發布這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She moved abroad with her parents' blessing.","zh":"她得到了父母的同意後去了國外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blessing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5b84c89f624a40cdfdc","word":"blind","forms":["blind"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ea66b82931171a4","term":"blind","forms":["blind","blinder","blindest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"失明的；視力受損的","explanation":"指眼睛完全看不見，或只能看見很少的東西；也就是眼睛真的被“擋住”了。","examples":[{"en":"The accident left him blind in one eye.","zh":"那場事故導致他一隻眼睛失明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A blind musician played the piano beautifully.","zh":"一位失明的音樂家鋼琴彈得非常優美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-224965aa3922a63a","term":"blind","forms":["blind","blinder","blindest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沒有察覺的；視而不見的","explanation":"指人沒有看清、承認或意識到某個事實，像是理解事物的視線被擋住了。","examples":[{"en":"He was blind to the risks of the plan.","zh":"他沒有意識到這個計劃的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Love can make people blind to each other's faults.","zh":"愛情會讓人看不見彼此的缺點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d39f1ed4613ddc07","term":"blind","forms":["blind","blinds","blinding","blinded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變暗或矇蔽","explanation":"指讓眼睛看不清東西，或讓人因為資訊、情緒等原因看不清事實；也就是記憶鉤子裡的“遮蔽、矇蔽”。","examples":[{"en":"Anger blinded her to the risks of the decision.","zh":"憤怒矇蔽了她，使她看不到這個決定的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thick smoke blinded the drivers on the highway.","zh":"濃煙遮住了視線，讓公路上的司機看不清路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e14a51fded1fb9b43de8","word":"blink","forms":["blink"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cebc4117b5d1310c","term":"blink","forms":["blink","blinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眨眼","explanation":"指雙眼迅速合上再睜開的動作，通常只發生一次或次數很少。","examples":[{"en":"He gave me a quick blink and smiled.","zh":"他快速眨了一下眼，然後笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bright light made her blink.","zh":"強光讓她眨了眨眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-222b491632fdd7ef","term":"blink","forms":["blink","blinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一瞬間","explanation":"指短到幾乎只夠眨一次眼的時間，常用來強調事情發生得非常快。","examples":[{"en":"The children disappeared in the blink of an eye.","zh":"孩子們轉眼間就不見了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finished the whole sandwich in a blink.","zh":"她轉眼就把整塊三明治吃完了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c112e46727570b3d","term":"blink","forms":["blink","blinks","blinking","blinked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"眨眼","explanation":"指雙眼快速合上再睜開，通常是不及物動作。","examples":[{"en":"The loser in the staring contest blinked first.","zh":"對視比賽中輸的人先眨了眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She blinked at the sudden flash.","zh":"突如其來的閃光讓她眨了眨眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bdd593cbf98d2e1","term":"blink","forms":["blink","blinks","blinking","blinked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"眨掉","explanation":"指透過眨眼使淚水等從眼中消失，或眨眼後恢復清楚視線。","examples":[{"en":"He blinked away his tears before answering.","zh":"他眨掉眼淚後才回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She blinked the dust out of her eyes.","zh":"她眨了眨眼，把眼裡的灰塵弄了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-496aca80e4d8f29fb8e8","word":"block","forms":["block"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5153af21d1f86222","term":"block","forms":["block","blocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"塊狀物","explanation":"block可以指一塊結實、通常近似立方體的材料或物體，就像擋在路上的實體塊一樣。","examples":[{"en":"A block of ice fell from the roof.","zh":"一大塊冰從屋頂掉了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He used a block of wood to hold the door open.","zh":"他用一塊木頭撐住門，讓門保持敞開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/block","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-abc939a4d1016f4f","term":"block","forms":["block","blocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堵塞物","explanation":"block可以指擋住通道、使東西無法透過的東西或情況，就像一塊實體物堵在路上。","examples":[{"en":"There is a block in the drain, so the water is rising.","zh":"下水道堵了，所以水位正在上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fallen tree formed a block across the road.","zh":"倒下的樹橫在路上，擋住了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/block","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57022c422d977139","term":"block","forms":["block","blocks","blocking","blocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堵住通道","explanation":"把一條路、管道或其他通道用東西堵滿，使人或物無法透過；就像一塊實體塊正好擋在通道里。","examples":[{"en":"Leaves blocked the drain after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，樹葉堵住了排水管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fallen tree blocked the mountain road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/block","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2ebf730972351bc","term":"block","forms":["block","blocks","blocking","blocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遮蔽賬號或聯絡人","explanation":"把某個人、機器人、賬號或聯絡人擋在通訊或網路服務之外，使對方不能再聯絡你或訪問相關服務；這正是“把聯絡的路堵住”。","examples":[{"en":"I blocked the account after it sent me several unwanted messages.","zh":"那個賬號給我發了好幾條騷擾訊息後，我把它遮蔽了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can block a caller without deleting the contact.","zh":"你可以遮蔽來電者，而不必刪除聯絡人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/block","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c7d2d9c37b913456cf7","word":"blond/blonde","forms":["blond","blonde"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb6c68730da1a3a0","term":"blond","forms":["blond","blonder","more blond","blondest","most blond"],"pos":"adj","zh":"淺金黃色的","explanation":"指接近淺黃色或金色的顏色，最典型的是頭髮的顏色；記住那束被陽光照亮的淺金色頭髮即可。","examples":[{"en":"She has long blond hair.","zh":"她有一頭長長的金髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Blond wood gave the kitchen a warm appearance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ab478747875ba2c","term":"blond","forms":["blond","blonds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"淺金黃色","explanation":"指這種淺黃色或金棕色本身，尤其常說頭髮的顏色；它就是那束淺金色頭髮所呈現的色澤。","examples":[{"en":"The blond of her hair looked almost golden in the sunlight.","zh":"陽光下，她頭髮的淺金色幾乎像金子一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a pale blond for the nursery walls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-469838fa8c407eb0","term":"blonde","forms":["blonde","blonder","more blonde","blondest","most blonde"],"pos":"adj","zh":"金髮的；金黃色的","explanation":"這是 blond 的另一拼寫形式，表示頭髮、毛髮或相關顏色呈淺金黃色；說人時常用於女性，但也能修飾其他事物。","examples":[{"en":"She has long blonde hair.","zh":"她有一頭長長的金髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child was born with blonde eyelashes.","zh":"這個孩子出生時睫毛就是淺金色的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blonde","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f956e1cbf137191d","term":"blonde","forms":["blonde","blondes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金髮女性；金髮的人","explanation":"指頭髮呈淺金黃色的人，實際使用中尤其常指女性；這裡的重點是“一個金髮的人”，不是單純的顏色。","examples":[{"en":"A blonde was waiting by the entrance.","zh":"一位金髮女性正在入口處等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actress played a clever blonde in the film.","zh":"那位女演員在電影中飾演一名聰明的金髮女性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blonde","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e8e40c0af5f5ea5a948","word":"blood","forms":["blood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11678c078cd65d4f","term":"blood","forms":["blood","bloods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"血液","explanation":"指動物體內迴圈的液體，負責輸送氧氣和養分；日常說“血”時，通常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse took some blood for the test.","zh":"護士抽了一些血來做檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cut on his hand was still bleeding.","zh":"他手上的傷口還在流血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2146c13b4969df59","term":"blood","forms":["blood","bloods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"血緣","explanation":"指因出生而形成的親屬關係，強調共同的家族血統，而不是婚姻或收養關係。","examples":[{"en":"She is my only blood relative in the city.","zh":"她是我在這座城市裡唯一的血親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are related by blood through their grandmothers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1de83442dea1fe1bfbdc","word":"bloody","forms":["bloody"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3830f8598c43bdfe","term":"bloody","forms":["bloody","bloodier","bloodiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"帶血的","explanation":"表示某物表面有血，或被血弄髒；重點是看得見的血跡，而不是事件本身殘酷。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse changed his bloody bandage.","zh":"護士給他換下了帶血的繃帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her shoes were bloody after the hike.","zh":"徒步回來後，她的鞋上沾滿了血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34659fd61a72a85204b4","word":"bloom","forms":["bloom"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4893a9cdff89d04","term":"bloom","forms":["bloom","blooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"花朵；盛開的花","explanation":"指植物開放的花，尤其強調從花苞展開後的花朵。","examples":[{"en":"A single pink bloom opened beside the path.","zh":"小路旁開出了一朵粉紅色的花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden is full of spring blooms.","zh":"花園裡滿是春天盛開的花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f929a3d3ed475c38","term":"bloom","forms":["bloom","blooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開花狀態","explanation":"指花正在開放或已經處於盛開的狀態，常用於描述植物的開花期。","examples":[{"en":"The apple trees are in bloom this week.","zh":"蘋果樹這周正在開花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roses came into bloom after the rain.","zh":"雨後玫瑰開始開放了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63aeac003e9dc285","term":"bloom","forms":["bloom","blooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"青春或事物的盛期","explanation":"像花開到最美時一樣，指人或事物處在美麗、清新、充滿活力的階段。","examples":[{"en":"She was in the bloom of youth when she moved abroad.","zh":"她移居國外時正值青春年華。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town was in the bloom of its prosperity.","zh":"那座城鎮正處於繁榮發展的時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b4026e74bc1156c","term":"bloom","forms":["bloom","blooms","blooming","bloomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開花；花朵開放","explanation":"指植物長出並開放花朵，是名詞“bloom”的直接動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The roses bloom every June.","zh":"這些玫瑰每年六月開花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The desert blooms after the winter rain.","zh":"冬雨過後，沙漠開出了一片花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3795130de25b4d71","term":"bloom","forms":["bloom","blooms","blooming","bloomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"興盛；煥發活力","explanation":"指人、事業或地方進入成長、健康、美麗而充滿活力的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The small business bloomed after the new owner arrived.","zh":"新老闆到來後，這家小企業興盛起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bloomed in the supportive new environment.","zh":"在這個充滿支援的新環境中，她煥發出了活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59d98c516f8b4e28e554","word":"blossom","forms":["blossom"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdb8c66882b90133","term":"blossom","forms":["blossom","blossoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"花朵；花簇","explanation":"blossom 指花朵，尤其常指果樹上預示即將結果的花；也可以集體指一片或一樹花。","examples":[{"en":"The apple tree is covered with pink blossoms.","zh":"這棵蘋果樹開滿了粉紅色的花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A single blossom fell onto the path.","zh":"一朵花落到了小路上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0e9540110802036","term":"blossom","forms":["blossom","blossoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開花期","explanation":"blossom 也表示植物正在開花的狀態或季節，即花朵大量出現的時期。","examples":[{"en":"The orchard is in blossom this week.","zh":"這周果園正值花期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A late frost destroyed much of the apple blossom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0afebd979d08361","term":"blossom","forms":["blossom","blossoms","blossoming","blossomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開花","explanation":"植物 blossom 就是開啟花朵、進入開花狀態，和名詞“花朵、花期”的核心意象直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"The cherry trees blossom in late March.","zh":"櫻花樹在三月底開花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pear trees blossom early in sheltered valleys.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0166d4ce9dc49cef","term":"blossom","forms":["blossom","blossoms","blossoming","blossomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開始興盛；發展起來","explanation":"比喻意義上，某人的才能、性格或某件事像花一樣展開，由初具潛力變得成熟而有活力。","examples":[{"en":"With encouragement, the shy child blossomed into a confident speaker.","zh":"在鼓勵下，那個害羞的孩子成長為自信的演講者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small club blossomed into a successful community project.","zh":"這個小俱樂部發展成了一個成功的社群專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08e4643a2789e07298cc","word":"blot","forms":["blot"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fde6ea3afff015ba","term":"blot","forms":["blot","blots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汙漬；汙點","explanation":"指有顏色的液體留下的斑點或汙漬，尤其是墨水等弄在紙張、衣物或其他表面上的痕跡。","examples":[{"en":"There was a large ink blot on the corner of the page.","zh":"頁面的一角有一大塊墨水汙漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tried to remove the blot with a damp cloth.","zh":"她試著用溼布擦掉那塊汙漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d05d9f60f98a7558","term":"blot","forms":["blot","blots","blotting","blotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄出汙漬","explanation":"指把有顏色的液體灑到某物上，使其出現汙點；這是名詞“汙漬”對應的直接動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"A drop of ink blotted the white shirt.","zh":"一滴墨水把白襯衫弄髒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to blot the document with wet paint.","zh":"小心別讓溼油漆把檔案弄髒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58416ccf252b740f","term":"blot","forms":["blot","blots","blotting","blotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抹去；刪除","explanation":"指把書寫、記號或某件事徹底消除，就像把紙上的墨跡抹掉一樣；最常見於固定短語 blot out。","examples":[{"en":"She blotted out the wrong answer and wrote a new one.","zh":"她把錯誤答案抹掉，重新寫了一個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thick clouds blotted out the moon.","zh":"厚厚的雲層遮住了月亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e094b416432919c2a8d","word":"blouse","forms":["blouse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80fe99feaeca5a40","term":"blouse","forms":["blouse","blouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女式上衣","explanation":"指女性或女孩穿的上衣，常有紐扣和領子，但款式可以比普通襯衫更寬鬆、更偏女性化。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a white blouse to the interview.","zh":"她穿了一件白色女式上衣去參加面試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This blouse goes well with your skirt.","zh":"這件上衣和你的裙子很相配。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d92c1baf669c4e13","term":"blouse","forms":["blouse","blouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬鬆制服外套","explanation":"指制服的一種寬鬆上衣或外套，常見於軍隊、警察或其他需要統一著裝的場合。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers were issued a new field blouse.","zh":"士兵們領到了一件新的野戰制服外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldier buttoned his uniform blouse before inspection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7cf6b0597fe4e3cb3559","word":"blow","forms":["blow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36d9db4d849ab48c","term":"blow","forms":["blow","blows","blowing","blew","blown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吹氣；產生氣流","explanation":"指用嘴或其他方式產生並向外送出氣流，是“力量突然向外移動”這條主線最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She blew gently on the hot soup.","zh":"她輕輕地吹著熱湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind was blowing hard all night.","zh":"風整夜颳得很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4e9c2daf447c002","term":"blow","forms":["blow","blows","blowing","blew","blown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"爆炸；突然發生","explanation":"指某物因內部壓力或力量突然向外釋放而爆炸、破裂，也可表示某事突然發生。","examples":[{"en":"The old gas tank could blow at any moment.","zh":"那個舊煤氣罐隨時都可能爆炸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm blew in just before midnight.","zh":"暴風雨在午夜前突然襲來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16477688c0e00699c6cf","word":"blue","forms":["blue"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-389d9de3d4d629db","term":"blue","forms":["blue","bluer","more blue","bluest","most blue"],"pos":"adj","zh":"藍色的","explanation":"表示具有藍色色調的，是“藍色”這一基本顏色義；可以聯想到晴朗的天空和深邃的海洋。","examples":[{"en":"The deep blue sea stretched to the horizon.","zh":"深藍色的大海一直延伸到地平線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a blue coat on the cold morning.","zh":"她在寒冷的早晨穿了一件藍色外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3bb7e9980d419ac1","term":"blue","forms":["blue","bluer","more blue","bluest","most blue"],"pos":"adj","zh":"憂鬱的","explanation":"表示情緒低落、憂鬱或沮喪；陰沉的藍色在這裡聯想到人的消沉心情。","examples":[{"en":"I felt blue after my friends moved away.","zh":"朋友們搬走後，我感到很沮喪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was a little blue on her birthday.","zh":"她生日那天情緒有些低落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f89b904c76918af","term":"blue","forms":["blue","blues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藍色","explanation":"指晴朗天空或深海那樣的藍色，也可泛指這種顏色本身；這是由“藍色”這一核心意象直接形成的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Blue is the colour of the sky on a clear day.","zh":"藍色是晴天天空的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The walls are painted a soft blue.","zh":"牆壁刷成了柔和的藍色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb79caae5f8c42a67e56","word":"blunt","forms":["blunt"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab4dc3743c914306","term":"blunt","forms":["blunt","blunter","bluntest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鈍的；不尖的","explanation":"指刀、針、鉛筆等的邊緣或尖端變厚、不再鋒利，因而不容易切開或刺入東西。這是 blunt 最具體、最容易延伸出的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"This knife is too blunt to cut the tomatoes.","zh":"這把刀太鈍了，切不了西紅柿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A blunt pencil makes writing difficult.","zh":"鉛筆尖鈍了，寫字會很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be7c46098d5fa029","term":"blunt","forms":["blunt","blunter","bluntest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直截了當而不客氣的","explanation":"形容說話或表達不繞彎子，直接把真實想法說出來，甚至顯得生硬、粗魯。它像一把沒有鋒刃但仍會撞疼人的鈍刀：不一定惡意很重，卻可能讓人不舒服。","examples":[{"en":"To be blunt, I don't think this plan will work.","zh":"直說吧，我覺得這個計劃行不通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her blunt reply hurt his feelings.","zh":"她直截了當的回答傷了他的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d2d976ec8e5bbb9","term":"blunt","forms":["blunt","blunts","blunting","blunted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變鈍","explanation":"指把刀刃、尖端等磨厚或損壞，使它不再鋒利。這是形容詞“鈍的”變成動作後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Cutting cardboard all day blunted the scissors.","zh":"剪了一整天紙板後，這把剪刀變鈍了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cutting wire will blunt those kitchen scissors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e42932b7a79c40e45f6b","word":"blur","forms":["blur"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b69d4ca33e372fc4","term":"blur","forms":["blur","blurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汙跡；塗抹痕","explanation":"指墨水、顏料等被擦開後留下的模糊痕跡，就像清楚的輪廓被抹掉了一樣。","examples":[{"en":"There was a dark blur on the corner of the page.","zh":"紙張的角落有一處深色汙跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wet sleeve left a blur of ink across the letter.","zh":"溼袖子把信上的墨水蹭成了一片汙跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83f39ab2586e77ea","term":"blur","forms":["blur","blurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"模糊的影像","explanation":"指雖然看到了某個東西，卻只能看到沒有清楚輪廓的一團影像。","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist passed me in a blur.","zh":"那個騎車人從我身邊一閃而過，只剩下一團模糊的影像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without my glasses, the departure board was a blur.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81e89f9fe58c524c","term":"blur","forms":["blur","blurs","blurring","blurred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使模糊；使朦朧","explanation":"指讓照片、輪廓或視線失去清晰度，就像在上面蒙上一層霧。","examples":[{"en":"Rain blurred the view through the window.","zh":"雨水使窗外的景色變得模糊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor blurred the child’s face in the video.","zh":"編輯把影片中孩子的臉打了馬賽克。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13de8a510f336bb84a78","word":"blush","forms":["blush"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-566c0c733dab9557","term":"blush","forms":["blush","blushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臉紅；紅暈","explanation":"指因害羞、尷尬、羞愧、愛慕或激動等出現在臉上的紅色，也可以指臉紅這一動作或狀態。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden blush spread across her cheeks when everyone applauded.","zh":"大家鼓掌時，她的臉頰突然泛起了紅暈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tried to hide his blush by looking down at the table.","zh":"他低頭看著桌子，試圖掩飾自己的臉紅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba142e0cd3505ddd","term":"blush","forms":["blush","blushes","blushing","blushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"臉紅","explanation":"指臉因害羞、尷尬、羞愧、愛慕、激動等變紅，有時還伴隨發熱感。","examples":[{"en":"She blushed when her friends started talking about her new boyfriend.","zh":"朋友們開始談論她的新男友時，她臉紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That compliment made him blush.","zh":"那句恭維話讓他臉紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-859169b38185780daa54","word":"board","forms":["board"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38624d8203e0c3ba","term":"board","forms":["board","boards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"板子；木板","explanation":"指相對長、寬而薄的平面材料，最典型的是木板，也可以是其他類似材料製成的板。它是許多引申義的基礎形象。","examples":[{"en":"We used a wooden board to repair the shelf.","zh":"我們用一塊木板修好了架子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The carpenter cut the board in half.","zh":"木匠把木板切成了兩半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/board","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48a9daeeec04fae3","term":"board","forms":["board","boards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棋盤；遊戲盤面","explanation":"指帶有格子、路線或其他標記、供棋類或桌面遊戲進行的平面。它就是“把遊戲放在上面的板”。","examples":[{"en":"Place your piece on the board.","zh":"把你的棋子放到棋盤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game ends when no moves remain on the board.","zh":"棋盤上沒有可走的步時，遊戲結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/board","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d239cc03f98c540","term":"board","forms":["board","boards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"委員會；董事會","explanation":"指負責管理組織事務的委員會，尤其是公司的董事會。這裡的“板”來自圍桌討論和作決定的形象，已經表示一個管理機構。","examples":[{"en":"The board approved the new budget.","zh":"董事會批准了新預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are waiting for the board to make a decision.","zh":"我們正在等待董事會作出決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/board","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc2594e970d6129f","term":"board","forms":["board","boards","boarding","boarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"登上交通工具","explanation":"指走上、爬上或進入船、飛機、火車等交通工具。核心畫面是登上船板或交通工具的入口。","examples":[{"en":"Passengers should board the train now.","zh":"乘客現在應該登上火車了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We boarded the plane at noon.","zh":"我們中午登上了飛機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/board","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d265d1416b14d7aa3678","word":"boast","forms":["boast"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a160f8a0223312d5","term":"boast","forms":["boast","boasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自誇；吹噓","explanation":"指把自己的能力、成績或優點說得很突出，以顯示自己了不起；重點在這種自我誇大的說法或行為。","examples":[{"en":"His claim to be the fastest runner in school was just a boast.","zh":"他聲稱自己是學校裡跑得最快的人，只是在吹噓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her boast made everyone at the table laugh.","zh":"她那番自誇讓桌邊的人都笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a17693073c32fe32","term":"boast","forms":["boast","boasts","boasting","boasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"自誇；吹噓","explanation":"指大聲或自信過頭地稱讚自己，強調把自己的能力、成績或身份說得很了不起。","examples":[{"en":"He kept boasting about how much money he had made.","zh":"他不停地吹噓自己賺了多少錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nobody likes it when someone boasts.","zh":"沒人喜歡別人自吹自擂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba7b478f6f0ef676","term":"boast","forms":["boast","boasts","boasting","boasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"誇耀；炫耀","explanation":"指把某人、某事或某種成就拿出來誇讚，以顯示自己有眼光、能力或值得驕傲；比單純“提到”更有自我炫耀色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The company boasts of its fast delivery service.","zh":"這家公司誇耀自己的快速配送服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He boasted about finishing the marathon without training.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25cdb46d8d2115a24eb1","word":"boat","forms":["boat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd6db9958ca4d7b3","term":"boat","forms":["boat","boats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船；小型船隻","explanation":"boat是能夠在水上航行並載人或載物的船，動力可以來自船槳、發動機或風。它常讓人聯想到河流、湖泊或近海使用的較小船隻。","examples":[{"en":"We rented a small boat to explore the lake.","zh":"我們租了一條小船去遊覽湖泊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fishermen brought the boat back before dark.","zh":"漁民們在天黑前把船開了回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44d425af1945e76862d5","word":"bodily","forms":["bodily"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72793beac836caba","term":"bodily","forms":["bodily","more bodily","most bodily"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體的；與身體有關的","explanation":"指與身體本身有關，或涉及身體狀況、身體缺陷和身體受到的影響。它把注意力從思想、精神等方面轉到肉身這一層面。","examples":[{"en":"The accident caused serious bodily injuries.","zh":"這場事故造成了嚴重的身體傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment improved her bodily condition.","zh":"這種治療改善了她的身體狀況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bodily","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66df9b66ae5b79ac","term":"bodily","forms":["bodily","more bodily","most bodily"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有實體的；肉身的","explanation":"指具有身體或物質形態，而不是純粹的精神、靈魂或抽象概念。它突出“確實以實體存在”這一點。","examples":[{"en":"The story describes the ghost's bodily form.","zh":"這個故事描寫了那個鬼魂的實體形態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the legend, the god appears in bodily shape to guide travelers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bodily","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-230d8358dc8e8890b4c5","word":"body","forms":["body"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1f6453ef5ce2a81","term":"body","forms":["body","bodies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體；軀體","explanation":"指人或動物的整個有形軀體，是body最基本、最常用的意思。這個“完整的身體”概念也構成了它後來表示各種“整體”的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"She covered her body with a warm blanket.","zh":"她用一條暖和的毯子蓋住了身體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise keeps your body strong.","zh":"經常鍛鍊能讓你的身體保持強健。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/body","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69a890e3ee711ffc","term":"body","forms":["body","bodies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一群人；團體","explanation":"body可以指一群作為一個整體行動或被看待的人，重點是“成員聚在一起形成一個有凝聚力的整體”。","examples":[{"en":"A body of volunteers helped clean the park.","zh":"一群志願者幫助清理了公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The governing body approved the new policy.","zh":"管理機構批准了這項新政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/body","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-539673b26433b311","term":"body","forms":["body","bodies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大片水域；一片物質","explanation":"指被看作一個完整整體的大片水、空氣或其他物質；“一片水域”就是許多水聚成的一個有邊界的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The lake is the largest body of water in the region.","zh":"這座湖是該地區最大的水域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A broad body of water separated the villages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/body","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3051a595b940142dc893","word":"bodyguard","forms":["bodyguard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6662b281d0e8db6d","term":"bodyguard","forms":["bodyguard","bodyguards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保鏢；護衛","explanation":"指專門負責保護某個人或某一組人的人，往往需要隨身陪同，必要時防止他受到傷害；也可以指承擔這項任務的一組人。","examples":[{"en":"The singer hired a bodyguard for the long tour.","zh":"這位歌手為長途巡演僱了一名保鏢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bodyguard accompanied the witness to court.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bodyguard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a692cc5ecc3c159c6f1","word":"boil","forms":["boil"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be4b1625852bf4f7","term":"boil","forms":["boil","boils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沸點","explanation":"指液體開始轉化為氣體、也就是開始沸騰的溫度或狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Add the rice when the water comes to the boil.","zh":"水燒開後加入米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bring the mixture to the boil, then reduce heat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-022eeba8638d6c2c","term":"boil","forms":["boil","boils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沸騰；煮沸過程","explanation":"指液體沸騰這一動作或過程，重點是讓液體持續冒泡、受熱沸騰。","examples":[{"en":"Give the water a good boil before you drink it.","zh":"喝之前把水充分煮沸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bring the soup to a gentle boil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-601ba5cdd79013aa","term":"boil","forms":["boil","boils","boiling","boiled","boilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把液體煮沸","explanation":"指加熱液體，使它達到開始冒泡並轉化為氣體的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Boil some water in a small pot.","zh":"在小鍋裡燒開一些水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Boil the water before adding the pasta.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b09600e3e8700d9b","term":"boil","forms":["boil","boils","boiling","boiled","boilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在沸水中煮","explanation":"指把食物放進沸水中烹調，使它煮熟；也可不帶賓語，表示進行煮這種烹調。","examples":[{"en":"Boil the eggs for six minutes.","zh":"把雞蛋煮六分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Boil the potatoes until a fork slides through.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2391133c2e637a18","term":"boil","forms":["boil","boils","boiling","boiled","boilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"沸騰","explanation":"指液體自己受熱達到沸點並開始冒泡、汽化，而不是某人把它煮沸。","examples":[{"en":"Wait until the soup boils, then lower the heat.","zh":"等湯沸騰後，把火調小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kettle began to boil while I washed cups.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0007a5bca8d91586274","word":"bold","forms":["bold"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d89eeceb656b0ae4","term":"bold","forms":["bold","bolder","more bold","boldest","most bold"],"pos":"adj","zh":"勇敢大膽","explanation":"形容人或行為有勇氣，敢於面對風險、困難或反對意見。","examples":[{"en":"It was a bold decision to leave her job and start a company.","zh":"辭職創業是一個大膽的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firefighter made a bold rescue in the middle of the storm.","zh":"消防員在暴風雨中進行了一次勇敢的營救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f5a8216ef0298bb","term":"bold","forms":["bold","bolder","more bold","boldest","most bold"],"pos":"adj","zh":"醒目突出","explanation":"形容顏色、設計、想法或行動等非常顯眼，具有強烈的視覺或整體效果。","examples":[{"en":"The designer chose a bold red for the front door.","zh":"設計師為前門選用了醒目的紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her bold idea changed the way the team worked.","zh":"她大膽而突出的想法改變了團隊的工作方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0b3cba71f725563d316","word":"bolt","forms":["bolt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-feabd8c74ceed003","term":"bolt","forms":["bolt","bolts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螺栓","explanation":"一種通常由金屬製成的緊韌體，主體呈圓柱形並帶有螺紋，一端有較大的頭，通常穿過孔後用螺母固定。它體現了 bolt 把物體牢牢固定住的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Use a wrench to tighten the bolt on the bicycle wheel.","zh":"用扳手擰緊腳踏車車輪上的螺栓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge is held together by large steel bolts.","zh":"這座橋由大鋼螺栓固定在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bolt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e77345e77e95085","term":"bolt","forms":["bolt","bolts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鎖閂；插銷","explanation":"門鎖或閂的機構中可以滑動的金屬桿或銷，用來把門固定在關閉位置。它就像一根橫向滑入鎖孔的直杆，把門牢牢鎖住。","examples":[{"en":"She slid the bolt across before going to bed.","zh":"她上床睡覺前把門閂滑上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old door has a heavy iron bolt.","zh":"這扇舊門裝著一根沉重的鐵門閂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bolt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3709a5a241c401d4","term":"bolt","forms":["bolt","bolts","bolting","bolted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用螺栓連線","explanation":"把兩件或多件東西對準後用螺栓固定起來，就像用一根筆直而結實的金屬桿把它們鎖在一起。","examples":[{"en":"Bolt the shelf to the wall before putting books on it.","zh":"先把架子用螺栓固定在牆上，再往上放書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic bolted the seat securely to the frame.","zh":"修理工把座椅牢牢地用螺栓固定在架子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bolt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80172e9d72e13706","term":"bolt","forms":["bolt","bolts","bolting","bolted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然逃跑或猛衝","explanation":"像箭或閃電一樣突然衝出去，常指人或動物受驚後迅速逃跑。","examples":[{"en":"The dog bolted when it heard the fireworks.","zh":"狗聽到煙花聲後突然逃跑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bolted for the exit as soon as the alarm rang.","zh":"警報一響，她就猛衝向出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bolt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb0afd90509c50678e29","word":"bomb","forms":["bomb"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce8dcd20f283d023","term":"bomb","forms":["bomb","bombs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"炸彈；爆炸裝置","explanation":"指用於武器目的、能夠爆炸的裝置，尤其包括從飛機上投下的炸彈。","examples":[{"en":"The police found a bomb near the railway station.","zh":"警方在火車站附近發現了一枚炸彈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The aircraft dropped bombs on the military base.","zh":"飛機向軍事基地投下了炸彈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bomb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50d6113e535b9461","term":"bomb","forms":["bomb","bombs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"徹底失敗的作品","explanation":"指電影、產品、演出或商業專案等徹底失敗、沒有獲得預期反響的事物，體現了“衝擊力反過來變成失敗”的比喻。","examples":[{"en":"The expensive sequel was a box-office bomb.","zh":"那部高成本續集在票房上徹底失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new product turned out to be a commercial bomb.","zh":"這款新產品結果成了商業上的失敗品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bomb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc3c50d6287fbf9e","term":"bomb","forms":["bomb","bombs","bombing","bombed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轟炸","explanation":"用一枚或多枚炸彈攻擊某個地點或目標，造成爆炸和強烈衝擊。","examples":[{"en":"The planes bombed the military base before dawn.","zh":"飛機在黎明前轟炸了軍事基地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city was bombed during the war.","zh":"這座城市在戰爭期間遭到轟炸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bomb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f21dea74d898cfeaf836","word":"bond","forms":["bond"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e446a39631d9ef00","term":"bond","forms":["bond","bonds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"債券","explanation":"指借款人發行的債務憑證：投資者先出藉資金，發行者按約定付息，並在到期時償還本金。它把借款人和債權人透過法律義務聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"She invested part of her savings in government bonds.","zh":"她把一部分積蓄投資於政府債券。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bond pays interest twice a year and matures in ten years.","zh":"這份債券每年支付兩次利息，十年後到期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2a1d197767f0b2f","term":"bond","forms":["bond","bonds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情感紐帶","explanation":"指人與人之間使雙方保持親近、信任或團結的感情聯絡，就像看不見的紐帶把人連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"Caring for the child created a strong bond between them.","zh":"照顧這個孩子讓他們之間建立了深厚的感情紐帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Shared experiences can strengthen the bond between teammates.","zh":"共同的經歷能夠加強隊友之間的紐帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b88cde62b5e80837","term":"bond","forms":["bond","bonds","bonding","bonded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連線、固定或捆住","explanation":"把 bond 記成“把東西綁在一起的紐帶”：這個用法強呼叫繩索、鏈條或其他方式把人或物固定、繫牢，使它們不能輕易分開。","examples":[{"en":"The workers bonded the heavy gate to the steel frame.","zh":"工人把沉重的大門固定在鋼架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The adhesive bonds the rubber to the metal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-812abd5bc9ed21df","term":"bond","forms":["bond","bonds","bonding","bonded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建立感情聯絡","explanation":"指人與人透過共同經歷、相處或互相支援，逐漸建立親密的友誼或情感聯絡；這正是“把兩個人連成紐帶”。","examples":[{"en":"The new teammates bonded over their shared love of hiking.","zh":"新隊員們因為都喜歡徒步而建立了感情聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bonded with my neighbor while we were caring for our injured dogs.","zh":"我們照料受傷的狗時，我和鄰居建立了感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8dacf657fe92b6064db","word":"bone","forms":["bone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-280ccb1cdc1015ee","term":"bone","forms":["bone","bones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"骨骼；骨質","explanation":"指構成大多數脊椎動物骨骼的堅硬組織，主要由礦物質和膠原等組成；這是“骨頭”這一核心概念的總體說法。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise helps keep your bones strong.","zh":"規律運動有助於保持骨骼強健。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scan showed that the bone had healed.","zh":"掃描顯示這塊骨頭已經癒合了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e3f242ab9806e03","term":"bone","forms":["bone","bones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一根骨頭","explanation":"指骨骼中的某一根具體骨頭，例如手臂、腿或肋骨中的一根。","examples":[{"en":"He broke a bone in his hand while playing basketball.","zh":"他打籃球時摔斷了手上的一根骨頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog buried a bone in the garden.","zh":"那隻狗把一根骨頭埋在花園裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f220b4a45832c0710e5","word":"bonus","forms":["bonus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4184ad4f4c0c36b1","term":"bonus","forms":["bonus","bonuses","bonusses","boni"],"pos":"noun","zh":"額外好處","explanation":"bonus 是在原有收穫之外再增加的一項好處，可以是錢、福利、機會或其他讓結果更好的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The free parking is a nice bonus.","zh":"免費停車是一個很不錯的額外好處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a bonus, the hotel gave us breakfast for free.","zh":"另外，酒店還免費給我們提供了早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7a60238e8f9d9cf","term":"bonus","forms":["bonus","bonuses","bonusses","boni"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎金；額外報酬","explanation":"bonus 可以是僱主因員工表現、公司業績等額外發放的錢，也可以是給股東等人的額外款項。","examples":[{"en":"She received a performance bonus at the end of the year.","zh":"她在年底拿到了績效獎金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each employee received a bonus after the successful launch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92719fe0cf8cd51592af","word":"book","forms":["book"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b8c6007297f8549","term":"book","forms":["book","books"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書；書籍","explanation":"把文字、圖片等資訊收進裝訂成冊的紙頁中，就是一本書；電子書也可以這樣稱呼。這個意思最直接地體現了“把資訊收進一本冊子裡”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"I borrowed a book about birds from the library.","zh":"我從圖書館借了一本關於鳥類的書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps her favorite books beside the bed.","zh":"她把自己最喜歡的書放在床邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/book","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b8998d3897754b6","term":"book","forms":["book","books"],"pos":"noun","zh":"著作；長篇作品","explanation":"book 也指一部適合出版的較長作品，通常是小說、教材等；它強調完整的著作，不只是裝書的紙頁。","examples":[{"en":"Her first book became a bestseller.","zh":"她的第一部著作成了暢銷書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is writing a book about city life.","zh":"他正在寫一部關於城市生活的書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/book","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4d7a8eaf514e11b","term":"book","forms":["book","books","booking","booked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預訂","explanation":"把未來要使用的房間、座位、票或服務提前收進安排記錄裡，也就是預訂。它體現了“把安排收進冊子裡”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"I booked a table for six at the new restaurant.","zh":"我在那家新餐館預訂了一張六人桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you booked your train tickets yet?","zh":"你預訂火車票了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/book","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d378750c5463621","term":"book","forms":["book","books","booking","booked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"記下；登記","explanation":"把資訊寫入冊子或正式記錄中，使它被儲存、備案；這裡不是把東西預訂下來，而是把資訊“收進記錄裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The clerk booked the payment in the company's records.","zh":"職員把這筆付款記入了公司的記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please book every change in the maintenance log.","zh":"請把每一項變更都記入維修日誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/book","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2d683d6d25d990886de","word":"bookcase","forms":["bookcase"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a399f5d3624d0a8","term":"bookcase","forms":["bookcase","bookcases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書櫃；書架","explanation":"指專門用來存放、整理並展示書籍的傢俱，可以是帶門的櫃子，也可以是開放式的架子。","examples":[{"en":"There is a large bookcase beside the window.","zh":"窗戶旁邊有一個大書櫃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She put all her novels on the bookcase.","zh":"她把所有小說都放在書架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bookcase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67530dc7ae96e0d6524e","word":"booklet","forms":["booklet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73061cf9f645a26a","term":"booklet","forms":["booklet","booklets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小冊子","explanation":"指一本比普通書更小、更薄、內容較集中的書冊，通常圍繞一個主題，用於介紹資訊、提供指南或說明事項。","examples":[{"en":"The museum gave us a booklet about the exhibition.","zh":"博物館給了我們一本介紹這次展覽的小冊子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the booklet before using the machine.","zh":"使用這臺機器前，請先閱讀說明小冊子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/booklet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24507df15ae5fe5c32ff","word":"bookstore","forms":["bookstore"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df60f5f2da28e582","term":"bookstore","forms":["bookstore","bookstores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書店","explanation":"出售書籍的商店，人們可以在那裡買書，也常能找到與閱讀有關的商品。","examples":[{"en":"I stopped by the bookstore to look for a travel guide.","zh":"我順路去了書店，想找一本旅行指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a small bookstore near the station.","zh":"車站附近有一家小書店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bookstore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81f52337ebb4cb1669bb","word":"boom","forms":["boom"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d16705ae336a08df","term":"boom","forms":["boom","booms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繁榮時期","explanation":"boom 指經濟、市場或某個行業處於繁榮和高度活躍的時期，體現了“向外擴張”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Many small businesses grew quickly during the housing boom.","zh":"房地產繁榮期間，許多小企業迅速發展起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boom created thousands of jobs in the region.","zh":"這次繁榮為該地區創造了數千個就業崗位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11023559def8832c","term":"boom","forms":["boom","booms","booming","boomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出轟鳴聲","explanation":"指突然發出低沉、洪亮而有迴響的聲音，就像聲音一下子爆發開來。雷聲、炮聲、機器聲和遠處傳來的巨大聲響都可以這樣描述。","examples":[{"en":"Thunder boomed over the hills.","zh":"雷聲在山丘上空轟鳴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old furnace boomed when it started.","zh":"那臺舊爐子啟動時發出轟鳴聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e81b7b8cca44b4f6","term":"boom","forms":["boom","booms","booming","boomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蓬勃發展","explanation":"指人口、經濟、行業或市場突然快速增長、繁榮起來，正好對應“向外擴張”的畫面。它強調增長勢頭強，而不只是緩慢變好。","examples":[{"en":"The local tech industry has boomed in recent years.","zh":"當地的科技行業近年來蓬勃發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town boomed after the new railway opened.","zh":"新鐵路開通後，這座城鎮迅速繁榮起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca4264faf5970fc613d8","word":"boost","forms":["boost"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08301320838c2159","term":"boost","forms":["boost","boosts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"託舉；推一把","explanation":"指從後面或下面推、託一個正在攀爬或上升的人，幫助他更高地到達目標；它是所有引申義的具體動作基礎。","examples":[{"en":"Can you give me a boost so I can reach the window?","zh":"你能從下面託我一把，讓我夠到窗戶嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With a boost from her brother, the little girl climbed onto the horse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f925df564342afb6","term":"boost","forms":["boost","boosts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"助推；促進","explanation":"指某種幫助或力量讓事情變得更強、更有效或更容易成功，就像給事情從後面推了一把。","examples":[{"en":"The new advertisement gave our small business a boost.","zh":"這則新廣告給我們的小企業帶來了助推。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The favorable review gave ticket sales a boost.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2bc8b9e0ed25190","term":"boost","forms":["boost","boosts","boosting","boosted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"托起；推上去","explanation":"指從後面或下面推、託某人，使他向上移動或爬得更高，是“推一把”這個核心畫面的直接動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"She boosted the child up onto the wall.","zh":"她把孩子託上了牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She boosted the toddler onto the low branch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f7d77c8bfa6d325","term":"boost","forms":["boost","boosts","boosting","boosted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促進；提高","explanation":"指幫助某事增加、改善或變得更有成效，例如提高銷量、信心、機會或表現；抽象意義仍然是“推一把”。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise can boost your energy levels.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以提高你的精力水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The grant will boost research into drought-resistant crops.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-4509beb0ab401d71fa4a","word":"boot","forms":["boot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50d4eefd1e47ea7d","term":"boot","forms":["boot","boots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"靴子","explanation":"boot 是一種高過腳踝、覆蓋小腿一部分的鞋，常用於保暖、防水或保護腳和腿；可以把它想成記憶鉤子裡的“裝備”。","examples":[{"en":"She put on her boots before walking through the muddy field.","zh":"她在走過泥濘的田地前穿上了靴子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These boots are warm enough for winter.","zh":"這雙靴子足夠暖和，適合冬天穿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e77c5830cc6dd4d","term":"boot","forms":["boot","boots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽車行李廂","explanation":"在英國、澳大利亞、紐西蘭和南非英語中，boot 是轎車後部存放行李的空間；記憶鉤子把它聯想到像靴筒一樣能裝東西的汽車後部。","examples":[{"en":"I left the groceries in the boot of the car.","zh":"我把買來的食品留在汽車的行李廂裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you put these bags in the boot?","zh":"你能把這些袋子放進行李廂嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8bf23c626029e76","term":"boot","forms":["boot","boots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啟動；引導","explanation":"在計算機語境中，boot 就像給機器穿上靴子後讓它開始行動，指裝置啟動或重新啟動的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The computer took two boots before it started normally.","zh":"這臺電腦啟動了兩次才正常執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laptop boots in less than ten seconds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4cf2aaf611d80b2","term":"boot","forms":["boot","boots","booting","booted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"踢","explanation":"這個義項直接來自“靴子可以踢人”的記憶：boot 表示用腳或靴子踢某人或某物。","examples":[{"en":"He booted the ball across the field.","zh":"他把球踢過了球場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An angry spectator booted the advertising board and hurt his foot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-046b34e558dbffcc05c0","word":"booth","forms":["booth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2085fa533e1ec67d","term":"booth","forms":["booth","booths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小攤位","explanation":"指在市場、集市或展會上擺放和出售商品的小攤，通常有一個明確的展示或交易空間。","examples":[{"en":"We bought handmade soap at a booth near the entrance.","zh":"我們在入口附近的一個攤位買了手工肥皂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A vendor sold handmade candles from a tiny booth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/booth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-401e583d03e7f725","term":"booth","forms":["booth","booths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小隔間","explanation":"指剛好能容納一個人站立的封閉小空間，例如電話亭或投票間。","examples":[{"en":"She stepped into a phone booth to call her parents.","zh":"她走進電話亭給父母打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Voters entered the booth one at a time.","zh":"選民一個接一個地進入投票間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/booth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":6,"counts":{"111":1,"113":5}}},{"id":"ceec-4f1a55de40bce9010e81","word":"border","forms":["border"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3da35754dc2095d","term":"border","forms":["border","borders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊界；國界","explanation":"指分隔兩個國家、地區或地理區域的線或地帶，重點是“這邊”和“那邊”之間的界限。","examples":[{"en":"We crossed the border into Mexico before sunset.","zh":"我們在日落前越過了邊境，進入墨西哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A river forms the border between the two countries.","zh":"一條河構成了兩國之間的邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/border","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e56cf2103420b0c","term":"border","forms":["border","borders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外緣；邊沿","explanation":"指物體、地方或區域最外面的部分，也就是圍住內部空間的那一圈邊。","examples":[{"en":"Small stones mark the border of the path.","zh":"小石頭標出了小路的邊緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She embroidered tiny flowers around the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/border","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3610501e40e55c83","term":"border","forms":["border","borders","bordering","bordered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與……接壤","explanation":"表示一個國家、地區或土地直接挨著另一個國家、地區或土地，共有一段邊界。","examples":[{"en":"The state borders the ocean on the east.","zh":"這個州東面與海洋相鄰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Poland borders Germany to the west.","zh":"波蘭西部與德國接壤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/border","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-706cd6dbd0cf60397cab","word":"bore","forms":["bore"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-182fc62f17998035","term":"bore","forms":["bore","bores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鑽出的孔；內徑","explanation":"指用鑽削或銑削等方法在物體中做出的孔，也可以進一步指這個孔的直徑。核心畫面是鑽頭穿進材料後留下的通道。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic checked the bore of the cylinder before installing it.","zh":"技工安裝氣缸前檢查了它的內徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pipe's bore narrowed where mineral deposits accumulated.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45555c491c7d2760","term":"bore","forms":["bore","bores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無聊的人","explanation":"指總讓別人感到厭煩、缺少趣味的人。這個意義可以看成話題不停“鑽”下去，卻沒有帶來興趣。","examples":[{"en":"He is such a bore that everyone leaves when he starts talking about work.","zh":"他太無聊了，一開始談工作，大家就都離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He becomes a terrible bore when discussing his investments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ed51d295eafbfc8","term":"bore","forms":["bore","bores","boring","bored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使厭煩","explanation":"指讓某人失去興趣、感到厭倦。它保留了“不斷鑽進、磨損耐心”的畫面，所以重點是某人或某事對別人造成無聊感。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep the story short; I do not want to bore the children.","zh":"請把故事講短一點，我不想讓孩子們感到無聊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Long speeches bore the younger children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-845ea11b46211d9e","term":"bore","forms":["bore","bores","boring","bored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鑽穿","explanation":"指用鑽頭或類似方法在某物上打穿一個孔。核心畫面就是旋轉的工具穿過材料。","examples":[{"en":"They bored a hole through the wall for the new pipe.","zh":"他們在牆上鑽了一個孔，好讓新管道穿過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They bored through the rock to lay cables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60e6aa4ad2d315ff8ab5","word":"bored","forms":["bored"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-481cf829c8426c05","term":"bored","forms":["bored","more bored","boreder","most bored","boredest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到無聊的","explanation":"指因為沒有有趣的事情可做，感到無趣、煩悶，甚至有些坐立不安。它描述的是人的感受，正好對應“心裡像被挖空了一樣”。","examples":[{"en":"I was bored, so I started reading a book.","zh":"我感到無聊，於是開始讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children get bored when the weather keeps them indoors.","zh":"天氣讓孩子們只能待在室內時，他們會感到無聊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bored","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19c78c130ee2e84f7785","word":"boredom","forms":["boredom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-454cb9be6c1b851b","term":"boredom","forms":["boredom","boredoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無聊；乏味狀態","explanation":"指因為沒有足夠的興趣、活動或刺激而持續感到無聊的狀態，是 boredom 最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The long wait filled him with boredom.","zh":"漫長的等待讓他感到無聊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reads to escape boredom.","zh":"她透過閱讀來擺脫無聊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boredom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f953f70b9132340e2782","word":"boring","forms":["boring"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d67653c3fb23e097","term":"boring","forms":["boring","more boring","boringer","most boring","boringest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人厭煩的","explanation":"指某件事、某個地方或某個人的表現讓人覺得無聊、疲倦或不耐煩，就像鑽頭反覆鑽進耐心一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The lecture was so boring that several students fell asleep.","zh":"那堂講座無聊得讓幾個學生都睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a more interesting book; this one is boring.","zh":"我需要一本更有趣的書，這本太無聊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0822963756ce70ec17b8","word":"born","forms":["born"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05b1ef2350c807a8","term":"born","forms":["born"],"pos":"adj","zh":"天生的；與生俱來的","explanation":"指某種品質、性格、能力或狀態從出生時就已經存在，彷彿一出生就帶在身上，而不是後來培養或獲得的。","examples":[{"en":"She is a born leader who brings the team together.","zh":"她是個天生的領導者，能把團隊凝聚在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was born blind but learned to read Braille at an early age.","zh":"他生來失明，但很早就學會了讀盲文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/born","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d106ccb1fe638b61e4cf","word":"borrow","forms":["borrow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c3de221000ddf1c","term":"borrow","forms":["borrow","borrows","borrowing","borrowed","borrowest","borrowedst","borroweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"借來使用","explanation":"borrow 表示暫時從別人那裡拿來某物使用，並通常期望之後歸還。重點是“拿到自己這邊暫用”，不強調對方把東西交出去的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Can I borrow your umbrella until the rain stops?","zh":"雨停之前我可以借用一下你的雨傘嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I borrowed a book from Maya and returned it yesterday.","zh":"我向瑪雅借了一本書，昨天已經還給她了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/borrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ab32a9a8e5e6a9a","term":"borrow","forms":["borrow","borrows","borrowing","borrowed","borrowest","borrowedst","borroweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"借錢","explanation":"borrow money 指先取得銀行或其他出借方的錢，並同意以後按約定償還，常常還包括利息或分期付款。","examples":[{"en":"They borrowed money from the bank to buy a house.","zh":"他們向銀行借錢買了一套房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She borrowed enough to replace the broken furnace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/borrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-529b7ecf563bf78ff19d","word":"bosom","forms":["bosom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8819a2359d4663e","term":"bosom","forms":["bosom","bosoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受保護的內部；懷抱之中","explanation":"表示被某個家庭、群體或環境包圍並保護的內部空間，像被懷抱住一樣；這是“胸前容納東西”這一核心影象的引申。","examples":[{"en":"The children grew up in the bosom of a loving family.","zh":"孩子們在充滿愛的家庭懷抱中長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village lies in the bosom of the mountains.","zh":"這個村莊坐落在群山環抱之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bosom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5e7c002443743c58367","word":"boss","forms":["boss"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f4fbfd85dd1ca9f","term":"boss","forms":["boss","bosses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上司；主管","explanation":"指負責監督和安排別人工作的人，也就是某人的上司或主管；核心畫面是“掌控工作方向的人”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to ask my boss before I change my schedule.","zh":"我得先問過我的上司，才能改工作安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her boss gave her a new project.","zh":"她的主管給了她一個新專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8bd7ab0ecae9b5a5","term":"boss","forms":["boss","bosses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"老闆；公司負責人","explanation":"指掌管企業或公司的負責人，重點是對整個經營單位擁有決定權的人。","examples":[{"en":"The boss approved the plan this morning.","zh":"老闆今天上午批准了這個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone stopped talking when the boss walked in.","zh":"老闆一走進來，大家就停止了交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df7cdd0c88e75414","term":"boss","forms":["boss","bosses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關底強敵","explanation":"指遊戲一個關卡或階段末尾特別難對付、通常必須擊敗才能繼續推進的敵人；它仍然保留“掌控局面、擋在前面”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We spent an hour learning how to beat the final boss.","zh":"我們花了一個小時研究怎麼打敗最終關卡的強敵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This game has a boss battle at the end of every chapter.","zh":"這款遊戲每一章結尾都有一場首領戰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff7772053abf7d817d6e","word":"both","forms":["both"],"officialPos":"pron./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3eff7f91b4844d5a","term":"both","forms":["both"],"pos":"det","zh":"兩者都","explanation":"指明確的兩個物件，一個不漏地都包括在內；它像一個圈，把這兩個物件一起圈進去。","examples":[{"en":"Both students passed the test.","zh":"兩個學生都透過了考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both of my parents work from home.","zh":"我的父母都在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/both","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1224a5d30c59557","term":"both","forms":["both"],"pos":"pron","zh":"兩個都","explanation":"不再重複名詞，直接用 both 指前面已經說過的兩個物件，表示這兩個物件全部被選擇、擁有某種性質或參與某件事。","examples":[{"en":"Would you like tea or coffee? — Both, please.","zh":"你想喝茶還是咖啡？——兩種都要，謝謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are both ready to leave.","zh":"他們兩個都準備好要走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/both","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56568d25931009bd526d","word":"bother","forms":["bother"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0426ec1253559805","term":"bother","forms":["bother","bothers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麻煩；費事","explanation":"bother 也就是一件需要額外時間、精力或安排來處理的麻煩事；因此說 no bother，就是“沒關係，不麻煩”。","examples":[{"en":"Thanks for bringing these documents. — No bother.","zh":"謝謝你把這些檔案帶來。——不麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It's no bother to pick you up on my way.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-168f6f9d3b4408ad","term":"bother","forms":["bother","bothers","bothering","bothered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打擾；使煩惱","explanation":"某人或某事給你添了麻煩、讓你不得安寧，就是 bother 你；它可以是實際打斷，也可以只是讓你覺得煩。","examples":[{"en":"Would it bother you if I opened the window?","zh":"我開窗你會介意嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The noise didn't bother me after a while.","zh":"過了一會兒，那噪音就不再讓我煩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7cb7648c3e857566","term":"bother","forms":["bother","bothers","bothering","bothered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在意；操心","explanation":"當你願意為某件事花心思、讓它佔據自己的精力時，就是 bother about it；否定形式則常表示“不在意、不操心”。","examples":[{"en":"I don't bother about what other people think.","zh":"我不在意別人怎麼想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't bother about lunch; I've already packed sandwiches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7def9c79e5be6d7a7002","word":"bottle","forms":["bottle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5de5e585c5cb2b5","term":"bottle","forms":["bottle","bottles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓶子","explanation":"一種通常由玻璃或塑膠製成、上窄下寬的容器，主要用來裝液體。這是 bottle 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She filled the bottle with cold water.","zh":"她把瓶子裝滿了冷水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please recycle the empty bottles.","zh":"請把空瓶回收。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af3fa3638e89d080","term":"bottle","forms":["bottle","bottles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一瓶的量","explanation":"不強調容器本身，而是指瓶子裡裝著的全部東西，尤其是飲料；“一瓶啤酒”中的“一瓶”就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"We shared a bottle of sparkling water.","zh":"我們分喝了一瓶氣泡水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We drank a whole bottle of apple juice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1465b8c31e968d6b","term":"bottle","forms":["bottle","bottles","bottling","bottled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝瓶儲存","explanation":"把液體裝進瓶子並封好，以便以後使用或飲用；也可比喻把某種東西暫時封存起來。","examples":[{"en":"The company bottles spring water from the local hills.","zh":"這家公司把當地山裡的泉水裝瓶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bottled the homemade sauce for winter.","zh":"我們把自制醬汁裝瓶，留到冬天用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be9b7607e070383c083b","word":"bottom","forms":["bottom"],"officialPos":"n./adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d57bc7b674115a98","term":"bottom","forms":["bottom"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最底部的；最後的","explanation":"把 bottom 想成容器最下面的“底”，作形容詞時表示位於最底部、最低處，或排在最後。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the heavy books on the bottom shelf.","zh":"請把那些厚重的書放在最下面一層架子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write your initials in the bottom box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4520257d1ae5ec41","term":"bottom","forms":["bottom","bottoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"底部；最下面部分","explanation":"把 bottom 想成容器最下面的“底”，它可以指任何物體最下面的部分，也可以指這個部分本身。","examples":[{"en":"There was a layer of sand at the bottom of the jar.","zh":"罐子的底部有一層沙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box has a hole in the bottom.","zh":"這個盒子的底部有一個洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e8112496f4860c4","term":"bottom","forms":["bottom","bottoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基礎；根本方面","explanation":"從“最底層”引申，bottom 可以指支撐事物的基礎，或一個人的根本性格和本質。","examples":[{"en":"At bottom, the disagreement was about trust.","zh":"歸根結底，這場分歧涉及的是信任問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At bottom, he wanted his parents to be proud of him.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36faaa70185cade6","term":"bottom","forms":["bottom","bottoms","bottoming","bottomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到達底部","explanation":"沿著容器、洞穴或其他空間到達最下面，也就是終於抵達那個“底”。","examples":[{"en":"She bottomed the jar and found one last cookie at the bottom.","zh":"她把罐子裡的東西吃到了底，發現底部還剩最後一塊餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog bottomed the food bowl in seconds.","zh":"那隻狗幾秒鐘就把食盆裡的食物吃光了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c400e0c0e1c7ddea24be","word":"boulevard","forms":["boulevard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76fb93cb3bae5b49","term":"boulevard","forms":["boulevard","boulevards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬闊的綠化大道","explanation":"指寬闊、鋪設良好並經過綠化的城市道路，重點是整條大道的道路空間和景觀設計。","examples":[{"en":"We walked down the boulevard after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，我們沿著林蔭大道散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Plane trees shaded the broad boulevard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boulevard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-411285398dde0c37","term":"boulevard","forms":["boulevard","boulevards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大道兩側的綠化","explanation":"指大道兩邊的樹木、草地等景觀帶，也就是構成大道景觀的綠化部分，而不是道路本身。","examples":[{"en":"The city replaced the old trees in the boulevard landscaping.","zh":"市政府更換了大道綠化帶裡的老樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city planted flowering shrubs along the boulevard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boulevard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d6723e5e454779e2bd1","word":"bounce","forms":["bounce"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56f270806c03a33e","term":"bounce","forms":["bounce","bounces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反彈；彈起","explanation":"指球或其他物體撞到地面、牆面等之後改變運動方向，彈起或反彈回來；核心畫面就是“撞到東西后彈回來”。","examples":[{"en":"The ball took a strange bounce off the wet grass.","zh":"球碰到溼草地後產生了奇怪的反彈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lucky bounce gave our team the winning goal.","zh":"一次幸運的反彈讓我們隊打進了制勝球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9698b082463eaea","term":"bounce","forms":["bounce","bounces","bouncing","bounced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反彈","explanation":"物體撞到牆、地面等障礙物後改變運動方向，彈向另一處；可以把它想成撞到東西后“彈回來”。","examples":[{"en":"The ball bounced off the pavement and rolled into the garden.","zh":"球從路面反彈起來，滾進了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The light bounced off the mirror and filled the room.","zh":"光線從鏡子上反射回來，照亮了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44939910318220b8","term":"bounce","forms":["bounce","bounces","bouncing","bounced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上下彈動","explanation":"人或物快速地上下移動一次或反覆移動，像被彈簧帶著一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The child bounced excitedly on the bed.","zh":"孩子興奮地在床上蹦跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bounced up and down while waiting for the results.","zh":"她等結果時不停地上下蹦跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65e3e54dcda0b1f2","term":"bounce","forms":["bounce","bounces","bouncing","bounced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"郵件退回","explanation":"郵件因地址錯誤、收件箱問題等投遞失敗而退回發件人，像郵件彈回來了。","examples":[{"en":"The message bounced because the recipient’s mailbox was full.","zh":"這封郵件因收件人的郵箱已滿而退回。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If the email bounces again, check the address carefully.","zh":"如果郵件再次退回，請仔細檢查地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e1cf42878df58fea7bf","word":"bound","forms":["bound"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bad47db62936facf","term":"bound","forms":["bound","bounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大跳","explanation":"表示一次幅度較大的跳躍或躍過，畫面是身體用力騰空並跨過一段距離。它和動詞“跳躍”共享同一個“向前彈起”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The deer cleared the fence in a single bound.","zh":"那隻鹿一躍就跳過了籬笆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With one bound, the athlete reached the other side.","zh":"運動員一躍就到了另一邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9be8487c4d167ab7","term":"bound","forms":["bound","bounds","bounding","bounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跳躍前進","explanation":"表示連續地跳著移動或一躍向前，常讓人聯想到兔子、鹿等動物輕快地越過路面。","examples":[{"en":"The rabbit bounded across the field.","zh":"兔子蹦跳著穿過田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog bounded up the stairs to greet us.","zh":"狗蹦跳著跑上樓來迎接我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-931534c0c145d0a99631","word":"boundary","forms":["boundary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5187a188d0b8822","term":"boundary","forms":["boundary","boundaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"區域之間的分界","explanation":"指把兩個地方、區域或範圍分開的實際界線，也可以指這條界線所在的位置。它不一定是正式國界，城市、土地或其他區域之間都可以有這種分界。","examples":[{"en":"A low stone wall marks the boundary between the two gardens.","zh":"一堵矮石牆標出了兩個花園之間的邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river forms the boundary between the two counties.","zh":"這條河構成了兩個郡之間的邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boundary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86d54993d96c4460","term":"boundary","forms":["boundary","boundaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽象的界限","explanation":"指某種行為、關係或職責的範圍邊界，例如個人舒適區、隱私範圍或工作職責的界限。越過這種界限，就意味著做了對方不舒服、過分或不屬於自己職責範圍的事。","examples":[{"en":"It is important to set clear boundaries between work and home life.","zh":"明確劃分工作和家庭生活的界限很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He apologized after realizing that he had crossed her boundaries.","zh":"他意識到自己越過了她的界限後道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boundary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c177affdff64002e3062","word":"bow","forms":["bow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91681752dfb35f4c","term":"bow","forms":["bow","bows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"射箭用的弓","explanation":"弓本身就是一個“彎”的工具：兩端用弦連線，靠弦的彈力把箭射出去。","examples":[{"en":"The hunter carried a bow and a quiver of arrows.","zh":"獵人帶著一把弓和一筒箭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned to shoot a bow at the local club.","zh":"她在當地俱樂部學會了射弓箭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5775e8250727a04","term":"bow","forms":["bow","bows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彎曲處；弧形","explanation":"這裡仍然抓住“彎”這個畫面，指杆、平面或河流形成的弧形彎曲部分。","examples":[{"en":"There is a slight bow in the wooden shelf.","zh":"這塊木架有些輕微的彎曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river makes a wide bow around the village.","zh":"這條河在村子周圍形成了一個大彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4832149b9461c4ef","term":"bow","forms":["bow","bows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞠躬；鞠躬動作","explanation":"人把頭或上身彎下去就是鞠躬，通常表示尊敬、致意或禮貌；這正是“彎”這個核心畫面的另一種用法。","examples":[{"en":"He gave a polite bow before leaving the stage.","zh":"他在離開舞臺前禮貌地鞠了一躬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancer took a bow after the performance.","zh":"演出結束後，舞者鞠躬致意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9fdecffeb7d82206","term":"bow","forms":["bow","bows","bowing","bowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變彎；彎曲","explanation":"表示某物受到重量、壓力或其他作用後自己彎了起來，正是“彎”這個核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The old shelf bowed under the weight of the books.","zh":"舊書架在書本的重量下彎曲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wooden door bowed slightly in the heat.","zh":"木門在高溫下輕微地彎曲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9f2babb167353d05584","word":"bowl","forms":["bowl"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9225dfecce457916","term":"bowl","forms":["bowl","bowls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碗；碗狀容器","explanation":"一種通常呈圓形、底部較深的容器，用來盛放、混合或端上食物，也可以盛其他東西。這是 bowl 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She mixed the salad in a large bowl.","zh":"她在一個大碗裡拌沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had a bowl of rice for lunch.","zh":"我午飯吃了一碗米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bowl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-472de632654658760cad","word":"bowling","forms":["bowling"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32765c7790f83ee4","term":"bowling","forms":["bowling"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保齡球運動","explanation":"bowling 最常見的意思是保齡球運動：把球沿球道滾出，儘量撞倒前方排列的球瓶。","examples":[{"en":"We go bowling every Friday night.","zh":"我們每週五晚上都去打保齡球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bowling alley is crowded today.","zh":"今天保齡球館裡人很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bowling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26f8567f2569182294c3","word":"box","forms":["box"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2494f6f0c6ae16e","term":"box","forms":["box","boxes","boxen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盒子；箱子","explanation":"指有邊界、通常有底和側面的容器，可以用來裝、運或儲存東西；這正是“把東西放進盒子”的基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"She put the books in a cardboard box.","zh":"她把書放進了一個紙箱裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a box of cookies on the table.","zh":"桌上有一盒餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/box","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b70ecf5a22f4803b","term":"box","forms":["box","boxes","boxing","boxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝箱","explanation":"把物品放進一個或多個盒子裡包裝起來。這個義項最直接地體現了記憶鉤子中“把東西裝進盒子”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We boxed the books before moving to the new apartment.","zh":"我們在搬到新公寓前把書裝進了箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She boxed up the old photos and stored them in the attic.","zh":"她把舊照片裝進盒子，存放在閣樓裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/box","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-faaec71ff5644abe","term":"box","forms":["box","boxes","boxing","boxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"困住；包圍","explanation":"把人或物圍在一個受限制的範圍內，使其難以移動或脫身，就像被困在一個看不見的盒子裡。","examples":[{"en":"The defenders boxed the striker in near the corner.","zh":"防守隊員把前鋒困在角落附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy traffic boxed us in on both sides of the road.","zh":"擁擠的交通把我們困在道路兩側之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/box","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e2f1e29ea4db5ff","term":"box","forms":["box","boxes","boxing","boxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用拳擊打","explanation":"用拳頭擊打某人，通常指拳擊動作或格鬥中的出拳；這對應記憶鉤子中“用拳頭裝進對方防守空隙”的拳擊畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The champion boxed his opponent carefully in the opening round.","zh":"這位冠軍在第一回合謹慎地用拳擊打對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He boxed the heavy bag for ten minutes after practice.","zh":"訓練後他對著沙袋打了十分鐘拳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/box","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe9cc099f5c02135e8f8","word":"boxer","forms":["boxer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dfd7c039df427a50","term":"boxer","forms":["boxer","boxers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拳擊手","explanation":"指參加拳擊比賽、用拳頭與對手較量的人，可以是職業選手，也可以是業餘選手。這是boxer最核心、最常見的含義。","examples":[{"en":"Her older brother is a professional boxer.","zh":"她的哥哥是一名職業拳擊手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young boxer won the final round.","zh":"那名年輕拳擊手贏下了最後一回合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boxer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5b4d899a884069c","term":"boxer","forms":["boxer","boxers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水平對置發動機","explanation":"指一種內燃機，氣缸分列在曲軸兩側，像從中心向左右相對展開。它主要出現在汽車和發動機技術語境中。","examples":[{"en":"This sports car is powered by a six-cylinder boxer engine.","zh":"這輛跑車採用六缸水平對置發動機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A boxer engine gives the motorcycle its distinctive shape.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boxer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-114049bf85580c9d5a69","word":"boxing","forms":["boxing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e3bd802a1b7fa6b","term":"boxing","forms":["boxing"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拳擊運動","explanation":"兩名選手戴著拳套互相擊打頭部和軀幹，以得分或擊倒對手取勝的運動。比賽可能打滿規定回合，也可能因擊倒或技術性判定提前結束。","examples":[{"en":"She started boxing when she was sixteen.","zh":"她十六歲時開始練習拳擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Boxing requires speed, balance, and discipline.","zh":"拳擊需要速度、平衡和自律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boxing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc6a778404ea557da554","word":"boy","forms":["boy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b35dcddfa58d13c5","term":"boy","forms":["boy","boys","boyz"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男孩","explanation":"指未成年的男性兒童，是boy最基本、最中性的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The boy is learning to ride a bike.","zh":"那個男孩正在學騎腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two boys were playing in the park.","zh":"兩個男孩正在公園裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1571752af9a11efd","term":"boy","forms":["boy","boys","boyz"],"pos":"noun","zh":"年輕男子","explanation":"在非正式語境中，boy也可以指年輕男子，尤其是說話人把他看作年輕人時。","examples":[{"en":"She met a boy named Daniel at the concert.","zh":"她在音樂會上認識了一個叫丹尼爾的年輕人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That boy is already twenty-five.","zh":"那個小夥子已經二十五歲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aee566239c5b56383111","word":"boycott","forms":["boycott"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f2feb3ac21f0b04","term":"boycott","forms":["boycott","boycotts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抵制行動","explanation":"指個人或群體為了表達抗議，集體停止購買、使用某種產品，或停止與某人、某組織打交道的行動。它把“避開某物件”變成了一種公開的抗議手段。","examples":[{"en":"The group called for a boycott of the company’s products.","zh":"這個團體呼籲抵制這家公司的產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boycott continued until the company changed suppliers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boycott","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac1c4761f4e47fbe","term":"boycott","forms":["boycott","boycotts","boycotting","boycotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抵制","explanation":"指個人或群體為了表示抗議，主動不買、不用某種產品，或不與某人、某組織打交道。核心畫面就是“為了施加壓力而集體避開物件”。","examples":[{"en":"Many customers are boycotting the store because of its unfair policy.","zh":"許多顧客因為這家商店的不公平政策而抵制它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students decided to boycott the event.","zh":"學生們決定抵制這項活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boycott","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3da83d37afaeb057e063","word":"brace","forms":["brace"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a028735f9e0ec4a5","term":"brace","forms":["brace","braces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支撐物；固定帶","explanation":"能把東西牢牢撐住、固定住或包紮住的物品，例如支架、夾帶或護具。","examples":[{"en":"The injured player wore a brace on his knee.","zh":"那名受傷的球員膝蓋上戴著護具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A metal brace supports the damaged wall.","zh":"金屬支架支撐著受損的牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7eeda7a918caad8","term":"brace","forms":["brace","braces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大括號","explanation":"排版或數學、程式設計中用來把兩個或多個詞、行或專案連成一組的彎曲符號：{ }。","examples":[{"en":"Put the two related lines inside curly braces.","zh":"把這兩行相關內容放在大括號裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Enclose the statements within a pair of braces.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-734386656d39628f","term":"brace","forms":["brace","braces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牙齒矯正器","explanation":"由金屬絲、託槽和彈性部件組成的牙齒矯正裝置，用來逐漸調整牙齒排列或咬合。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter got braces last month.","zh":"我女兒上個月戴上了牙齒矯正器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her dentist fitted a brace to straighten her teeth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a2650c09dfac6f7","term":"brace","forms":["brace","braces","bracing","braced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做好承受準備","explanation":"提前讓身體或心理處於準備狀態，以承受即將發生的撞擊、壞訊息或困難。","examples":[{"en":"Brace yourself for a bumpy landing.","zh":"做好準備，著陸時會很顛簸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should brace for heavy rain tonight.","zh":"我們應該做好準備，今晚會有大雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-193f7ed209a3af1d","term":"brace","forms":["brace","braces","bracing","braced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撐住；抵住","explanation":"把身體或物體放到能抵抗壓力的位置上，使其不容易被推倒或移動。","examples":[{"en":"She braced herself against the door as the wind blew.","zh":"風吹過來時，她抵住門撐住自己。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He braced the ladder against the wall.","zh":"他把梯子斜靠在牆上固定住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc3742238bfd1deb","term":"brace","forms":["brace","braces","bracing","braced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繃緊；增強","explanation":"把身體、神經或某物拉緊、強化，使它能夠承受更大的壓力；它和“撐住自己”的核心概念相連。","examples":[{"en":"He braced his muscles before lifting the box.","zh":"他在搬箱子前繃緊了肌肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team braced its nerves for the final minutes.","zh":"球隊繃緊神經，準備應對最後幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da7fc2ffdb753178e421","word":"bracelet","forms":["bracelet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eae08ce8ee4dc621","term":"bracelet","forms":["bracelet","bracelets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手鍊；手鐲","explanation":"指戴在手腕上的裝飾性環帶，可以由金屬、珠子、皮革等製成；核心畫面就是“圍住手腕的一圈飾物”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a silver bracelet to the party.","zh":"她戴著一隻銀手鐲去參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave his sister a bracelet for her birthday.","zh":"他送給妹妹一條手鍊作為生日禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bracelet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-014231fb1f479e23","term":"bracelet","forms":["bracelet","bracelets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手錶錶帶","explanation":"指把手錶固定在手腕上的帶子，尤其常指金屬製成、像一圈鏈節的錶帶。","examples":[{"en":"The metal bracelet on my watch is too loose.","zh":"我手錶的金屬錶帶太鬆了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The watch's steel bracelet pinched his wrist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bracelet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbbf7a6412d6d3e8244a","word":"brain","forms":["brain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c84aba6143d211a","term":"brain","forms":["brain","brains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大腦","explanation":"指位於頭骨內、負責感知、思考、記憶、情緒和行動控制的大腦。它是“總指揮”這一核心形象的本義。","examples":[{"en":"The brain controls everything from breathing to complex reasoning.","zh":"大腦控制著從呼吸到複雜推理的一切活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Doctors examined his brain after the accident.","zh":"事故後，醫生檢查了他的大腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7af693ad640b8b5d","term":"brain","forms":["brain","brains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭腦；思緒","explanation":"由真實的大腦引申為人的思維和心裡正在處理的事情，也就是“腦子裡裝著什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"I have too much on my brain today.","zh":"我今天腦子裡裝的事情太多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clear your brain and start again.","zh":"清空思緒，重新開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cf2306d44e6a8f0","term":"brain","forms":["brain","brains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"智力；才智","explanation":"指一個人進行思考、理解和解決問題的能力，即“總指揮”所體現出的才智。","examples":[{"en":"The team brought plenty of brains to the project.","zh":"這個團隊為專案帶來了很強的才智。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has the brains to solve this puzzle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-876797249822df52fd57","word":"brake","forms":["brake"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75ec804d25b23c8c","term":"brake","forms":["brake","brakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剎車；制動器","explanation":"車輛或車輪上的 brake 是透過摩擦等方式減慢或停止運動的裝置；也可以指控制這個裝置的部件，例如汽車裡的剎車踏板。","examples":[{"en":"The car in front stopped suddenly, so I hit the brakes.","zh":"前面的車突然停下，所以我趕緊踩了剎車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic says I need new brake pads.","zh":"修理工說我的車需要換新的剎車片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a36da2b219712cf","term":"brake","forms":["brake","brakes","braking","braked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剎車","explanation":"作動詞時，brake 表示使用剎車使車輛或車輪減速，重點是主動進行制動這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"Brake gently on the wet road.","zh":"在溼滑的路上要輕輕剎車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He braked sharply when the deer appeared.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f38c764c8aa00b6578f4","word":"branch","forms":["branch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3d88b9ca22f2dc2","term":"branch","forms":["branch","branches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樹枝","explanation":"指從樹幹或較粗的枝條上長出的木質部分。它是“主幹向外延伸”的最具體形象，也是其他分支義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"A small bird landed on a low branch.","zh":"一隻小鳥落在了一根低矮的樹枝上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old branch broke during the storm.","zh":"那根老樹枝在暴風雨中折斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-210e344e7963a0ea","term":"branch","forms":["branch","branches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構分部","explanation":"指一個擁有多個地點的組織在某個地方設立的分部或辦事處。它把“樹幹分出樹枝”的形象轉用於一個組織的不同地點。","examples":[{"en":"I deposited the check at the nearest bank branch.","zh":"我在最近的銀行分行存入了這張支票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company opened a new branch in the city center.","zh":"這家公司在市中心開了一家新分部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db04f982911d8fd6","term":"branch","forms":["branch","branches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領域分支","explanation":"指某個較大知識、研究或商業領域中的一個專門方向。它把一個寬廣領域看成主幹，再把具體方向看成向外伸展的枝條。","examples":[{"en":"Ecology is an important branch of biology.","zh":"生態學是生物學的一個重要分支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Botany is the branch of biology she enjoys most.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7cecb5f6e9a3ce22","term":"branch","forms":["branch","branches","branching","branched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從主幹長出","explanation":"指樹枝從樹幹或較大的枝條上生長出來。這個動詞直接呈現了“從主幹向外伸出”的核心影象。","examples":[{"en":"Several thin limbs branch from the main trunk.","zh":"幾根細枝從主樹幹上分叉出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New shoots branched from the damaged trunk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c42e0036b054ad66","term":"branch","forms":["branch","branches","branching","branched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分成幾支","explanation":"指道路、河流、組織或其他整體分成不同部分，也可指使某物分成幾個方向。它是從樹木分叉義擴充套件出的最常用抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The trail branches into two paths near the lake.","zh":"這條小徑在湖邊分成了兩條路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company branched into online education last year.","zh":"這家公司去年拓展到了線上教育領域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04a9fba2f0c404565e6b","word":"brand","forms":["brand"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09558c93953656fd","term":"brand","forms":["brand","brands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"品牌；品牌形象","explanation":"brand指一個產品或服務透過名稱、標誌及相關形象在公眾心中形成的獨特身份。它不只是一個圖案，而是讓人辨認並聯想到某種產品或體驗的整體印記。","examples":[{"en":"The company is trying to build a trusted brand.","zh":"這家公司正努力建立一個值得信賴的品牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brand is known for simple, durable products.","zh":"這個品牌以產品簡潔耐用而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33a28bc4f5826ca76cf8","word":"brass","forms":["brass"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20032a9102201ceb","term":"brass","forms":["brass","brasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黃銅","explanation":"一種主要由銅和鋅組成的金屬，常用於製作管道、五金件和樂器。它是這組詞義的核心，其他許多義項都從它的顏色、聲音或金屬質感引申而來。","examples":[{"en":"The plumber replaced the old pipe with brass.","zh":"管道工把舊管子換成了黃銅管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Brass is strong enough for many household fittings.","zh":"黃銅足夠堅固，適合製作許多家用五金件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aed39c295c68e1d","term":"brass","forms":["brass","brasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銅管樂器；銅管聲部","explanation":"指用金屬製成、靠演奏者嘴唇振動發聲的一類管樂器，也可指樂隊或管絃樂隊中的銅管聲部。它延續了黃銅常被用來製作樂器這一具體聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The brass enters during the final chorus.","zh":"銅管聲部在最後一段副歌時加入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brass entered loudly above the quiet strings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d1d974a88d955abf63d","word":"brassiere/bra","forms":["bra"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-543cca4778afae7a","term":"bra","forms":["bra","bras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胸罩","explanation":"一種通常穿在衣服裡面、用來支撐胸部的內衣。它是具體的一件衣物，所以談一件時通常要用相應的數量或限定形式。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a new bra that fits comfortably.","zh":"她買了一件穿起來很舒服、尺寸也合適的新胸罩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a sports bra for running.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1bb216b2bbb7eb30b25","word":"brave","forms":["brave"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fedbd99e83ea489","term":"brave","forms":["brave","braver","more brave","bravest","most brave"],"pos":"adj","zh":"勇敢的","explanation":"指面對恐懼、危險或困難時仍敢於行動，不因害怕而退縮。","examples":[{"en":"She was brave enough to speak up in front of everyone.","zh":"她很勇敢，敢在所有人面前發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was brave of him to admit his mistake.","zh":"他敢於承認錯誤，真是很勇敢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3749f9a3a6ed51b3fad","word":"bravery","forms":["bravery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a554dfe5818ef45","term":"bravery","forms":["bravery","braveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勇氣","explanation":"它指人在危險、困難或壓力面前仍敢於行動的心理力量，重點是“站出來”的勇氣，而不是單純沒有害怕。","examples":[{"en":"The firefighter showed great bravery during the rescue.","zh":"那名消防員在救援過程中表現出了極大的勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It took real bravery to speak up against the unfair decision.","zh":"要站出來反對那項不公平的決定，確實需要很大的勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bravery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-985604c2b60243122c24","word":"bread","forms":["bread"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c01ecc1344c0a975","term":"bread","forms":["bread","breads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麵包這種食物","explanation":"bread 是用穀物麵糰烘烤成的食物，通常切片食用，也常用來搭配其他食物。","examples":[{"en":"We had bread and soup for lunch.","zh":"我們午飯吃了麵包和湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought fresh bread from the market.","zh":"她從市場買了新鮮麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57e2f1f644c8a5d6","term":"bread","forms":["bread","breads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作為食材或餐食的麵包","explanation":"這裡仍是麵包本身，但重點放在它作為食物材料或一餐中的一部分，而不是把它當作某種抽象食品類別。","examples":[{"en":"I used the bread to make sandwiches.","zh":"我用這些麵包做了三明治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is some bread on the kitchen table.","zh":"廚房桌上有一些麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9df66185dda71b6d93c0","word":"breadth","forms":["breadth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71c0ab4dd0be3618","term":"breadth","forms":["breadth","breadths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬度；橫向尺寸","explanation":"指物體從一邊到另一邊的距離，也就是它有多寬。它把“向兩側展開”的核心畫面直接用於實際尺寸。","examples":[{"en":"The breadth of the corridor is 4.5 metres.","zh":"這條走廊的寬度是4.5米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Measure the breadth of the doorway before ordering furniture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breadth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7c6fb39de22ec5e","term":"breadth","forms":["breadth","breadths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣度；範圍","explanation":"指知識、技能、經驗或興趣橫向覆蓋的領域有多廣。一個人的 breadth 越大，通常表示涉獵的方面越多，而不一定表示每一方面都很深入。","examples":[{"en":"The breadth of her knowledge impressed everyone on the team.","zh":"她知識面的廣度給團隊裡的每個人都留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course surprised me with its intellectual breadth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breadth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14ebe56a5008e7c25110","word":"break","forms":["break"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f011755bd4e9784b","term":"break","forms":["break","breaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斷裂；破裂處","explanation":"指物體被打斷後分成兩塊或更多部分的情況，或這種斷裂本身。它體現了把一個連續整體打斷的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The X-ray showed a small break in her wrist.","zh":"X光顯示她的手腕有一處小骨折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a clean break in the glass.","zh":"玻璃整齊地裂成了兩塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/break","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d616879e5ef2c33a","term":"break","forms":["break","breaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"休息；休息時間","explanation":"指工作、學習或活動暫時停下來的一段時間，讓人恢復精力。這是把正在進行的程序暫時斷開的時間。","examples":[{"en":"Let’s take a ten-minute break.","zh":"我們休息十分鐘吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I checked my messages during my lunch break.","zh":"我在午休時間檢視了訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/break","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f4d3cf5d6877a53","term":"break","forms":["break","breaks","breaking","broke","brake","broken","breakest","brokest","breaketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"斷裂；打碎","explanation":"把一個完整的物體打斷成兩塊或更多部分，或物體自己裂開、碎掉；這種斷裂通常不能輕易恢復原狀。這正是把連續整體打斷的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful not to break the glass.","zh":"小心別把玻璃杯打碎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The branch broke under the weight of the snow.","zh":"樹枝在積雪的重量下折斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/break","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-969aa6bf03e0d71f","term":"break","forms":["break","breaks","breaking","broke","brake","broken","breakest","brokest","breaketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打斷；終止","explanation":"中斷一個正在持續的活動、過程或習慣，使它不再繼續。這延續了“把連續程序打斷”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"I am trying to break my habit of checking my phone at night.","zh":"我正努力改掉晚上檢視手機的習慣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A loud knock broke the silence.","zh":"一陣響亮的敲門聲打破了寂靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/break","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aefd8e134c3a939c5fe5","word":"breakdown","forms":["breakdown"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9636853b558d2a7","term":"breakdown","forms":["breakdown","breakdowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機器或車輛故障","explanation":"指機器、車輛等機械裝置失靈，不能正常運轉，尤其常用於車輛在路上拋錨。它體現了“整體停止運轉”這條核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"Our car had a breakdown on the way to the airport.","zh":"我們的車在去機場的路上拋錨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old washing machine is prone to breakdowns.","zh":"這臺舊洗衣機很容易發生故障。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakdown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ca72c1ac4e38480","term":"breakdown","forms":["breakdown","breakdowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分解後的分類明細","explanation":"指把一個整體拆成若干部分來分別說明，或拆分後得到的結構和明細。例如把總預算分成工資、裝置和交通費用。這裡的“拆開”不是損壞，而是為了看清組成。","examples":[{"en":"The report includes a breakdown of the project costs.","zh":"這份報告列出了專案成本的分項明細。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you give me a breakdown of the survey results?","zh":"你能把調查結果分項說明一下嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakdown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4788e0e5f7004527","term":"breakdown","forms":["breakdown","breakdowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關係或系統的崩潰","explanation":"指關係、合作、溝通或組織系統失去正常運作，逐漸陷入混亂甚至無法繼續。它把機器的“停止運轉”延伸到了人與制度。","examples":[{"en":"The project failed because of a breakdown in communication.","zh":"這個專案因為溝通失靈而失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dispute led to a complete breakdown of trust.","zh":"這場爭端導致信任徹底崩潰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakdown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c58ea253628feed6583","word":"breakfast","forms":["breakfast"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-074cb3723974bfc1","term":"breakfast","forms":["breakfast","breakfasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"早餐；早飯","explanation":"指一天中通常在早晨吃的第一頓飯，核心畫面就是結束夜間禁食後開始進食。","examples":[{"en":"I usually have breakfast at seven.","zh":"我通常七點吃早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A healthy breakfast gives you energy for the morning.","zh":"健康的早餐能為你上午的活動提供能量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakfast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f72622a5dbcd355","term":"breakfast","forms":["breakfast","breakfasts","breakfasting","breakfasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃早餐","explanation":"表示進行早餐這件事，也就是結束夜間禁食並吃早晨的第一頓飯。","examples":[{"en":"We breakfasted on fruit and yogurt before the hike.","zh":"徒步前我們吃了水果和酸奶當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We breakfasted on the terrace overlooking the harbor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakfast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2142487324cdb6d8c504","word":"breakthrough","forms":["breakthrough"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60afbe506bc8b642","term":"breakthrough","forms":["breakthrough","breakthroughs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重大突破；重大進展","explanation":"指衝破長期存在的難題後取得的重大成果，例如重要的創新、發現或研究進展。這是名詞最核心、最常用的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers made a major breakthrough in cancer treatment.","zh":"研究人員在癌症治療方面取得了重大突破。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This invention could lead to a breakthrough in clean energy.","zh":"這項發明可能會帶來清潔能源領域的突破。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakthrough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3c5945726cb99451644","word":"breakup","forms":["breakup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3308d390ad937b26","term":"breakup","forms":["breakup","breakups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解體；分裂","explanation":"指原本完整的物體、組織或事件過程被突然拆散、分裂成部分，重點是“完整狀態被打破”。","examples":[{"en":"Investigators are still trying to determine what caused the breakup of the aircraft.","zh":"調查人員仍在設法確定是什麼導致了飛機解體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The breakup of the federation created several new states.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-175409b989dd3e3c","term":"breakup","forms":["breakup","breakups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分手；關係結束","explanation":"指友誼或戀愛關係被結束，像是把兩個人原本的聯絡拆開；日常使用中最常指情侶分手。","examples":[{"en":"She has been having a hard time since the breakup.","zh":"分手後，她一直很難熬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their breakup surprised everyone at work.","zh":"他們分手讓單位裡的所有人都很意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38136d6e343860f65e61","word":"breast","forms":["breast"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59f7ef3f75779089","term":"breast","forms":["breast","breasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乳房；胸部前側","explanation":"指人胸前含有乳腺的器官，通常說女性的乳房，但男性也有相應的胸部器官。這是 breast 最重要的身體義，和“胸前隆起的部位”這一核心形象直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"She noticed a small lump in her left breast.","zh":"她注意到左乳房裡有一個小腫塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Breastfeeding can be difficult at first.","zh":"母乳餵養一開始可能會很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-270877b46a373533","term":"breast","forms":["breast","breasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胸部；胸膛","explanation":"指人體從頸部以下到腹部以上的前胸區域，比 s1 的“乳房”範圍更大。拍打或挺起胸部時，描述的就是這一整片胸前。","examples":[{"en":"He held the baby against his breast.","zh":"他把嬰兒抱在胸前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt a sharp pain in her breast.","zh":"她感到胸口一陣劇痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c1ed57d55efca85","term":"breast","forms":["breast","breasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禽類胸肉","explanation":"指從雞、火雞等鳥類胸部取下的肉，也可以指某些其他動物的胸部肉塊。選單和購物中常見，通常肉質較瘦。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered grilled chicken breast with rice.","zh":"我點了烤雞胸肉配米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This recipe uses two turkey breasts.","zh":"這道菜要用兩塊火雞胸肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-367a1c592458c1b0ab94","word":"breath","forms":["breath"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-564a75501dee78bb","term":"breath","forms":["breath","breaths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"呼吸","explanation":"指吸氣和呼氣這一整個過程，也就是生命活動中持續進出的氣流；這裡關注的是呼吸本身，而不是某一口氣。","examples":[{"en":"The room was so quiet that I could hear my own breath.","zh":"房間裡安靜得我都能聽見自己的呼吸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His breath formed small clouds in the freezing air.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a27b365a73c7b57","term":"breath","forms":["breath","breaths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一口氣","explanation":"指一次吸入或撥出的氣，是連續呼吸中可以單獨數出來的一次；“深深地來一口氣”也常用它來表示調整狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She took a deep breath before answering the question.","zh":"她回答問題前深深吸了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hold your breath while I take the picture.","zh":"我拍照時請屏住呼吸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa8430ca0e63091efb65","word":"breathe","forms":["breathe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99c070853cdcb0bf","term":"breathe","forms":["breathe","breathes","breathing","breathed","breathest","breathedst","breatheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"呼吸","explanation":"指把空氣吸進肺裡，再把空氣撥出去，是人和動物維持生命的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"Take a slow breath and breathe normally.","zh":"慢慢吸一口氣，然後正常呼吸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was hard to breathe in the crowded room.","zh":"在擁擠的房間裡很難呼吸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breathe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94c3481eabd18b72","term":"breathe","forms":["breathe","breathes","breathing","breathed","breathest","breathedst","breatheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"透過氣體交換呼吸","explanation":"也可用於魚、昆蟲和其他生物，表示它們從周圍環境取得所需氣體並排出廢氣。","examples":[{"en":"Some insects breathe through tiny openings in their bodies.","zh":"有些昆蟲透過身體上的小孔呼吸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whales must surface regularly to breathe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breathe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8ff1c41b8415cb2ae57","word":"breed","forms":["breed"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91901c3fb826f5b7","term":"breed","forms":["breed","breeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"品種","explanation":"指同一種動物或植物中，因遺傳特徵相近而形成的品種，例如某種鬱金香品種。","examples":[{"en":"This breed of dog is known for its calm temperament.","zh":"這個犬種以性情溫順而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She grows several rare breeds of tulip.","zh":"她種植幾種稀有的鬱金香品種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad2f1047037db880","term":"breed","forms":["breed","breeds","breeding","bred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繁殖；生育","explanation":"指動物或植物進行繁殖併產生後代，核心是讓下一代出現。","examples":[{"en":"These birds breed in the wetlands every spring.","zh":"這些鳥每年春天在溼地繁殖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmers breed goats for milk.","zh":"農民飼養山羊以繁殖產奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86e116dd2111a547","term":"breed","forms":["breed","breeds","breeding","bred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"選育；培育","explanation":"指有計劃地讓動物繁殖，以便使下一代保留或增強某些品質。","examples":[{"en":"They breed horses for endurance and speed.","zh":"他們培育馬匹，以提高耐力和速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shelter breeds dogs that are suitable for rescue work.","zh":"這個機構培育適合救援工作的犬隻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fec96f2245f3887","term":"breed","forms":["breed","breeds","breeding","bred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"養育；撫養","explanation":"指從嬰兒期到童年照料並培養一個人，使其長大成人；重點是成長環境和教養。","examples":[{"en":"She was born and bred in a small coastal town.","zh":"她出生並在一個小海濱城鎮長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was bred to value honesty and hard work.","zh":"他從小受到的教育使他重視誠實和勤勞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71d6fe12b0cfb606","term":"breed","forms":["breed","breeds","breeding","bred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"造成；滋生","explanation":"指某種情況或行為產生、滋生另一種結果，像繁殖一樣讓結果不斷出現。","examples":[{"en":"Unfair treatment breeds resentment.","zh":"不公平的待遇會滋生怨恨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Poor communication breeds resentment among colleagues.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-7e92c11499fd4106a899","word":"breeze","forms":["breeze"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2aae7d38311d649","term":"breeze","forms":["breeze","breezes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微風","explanation":"breeze 是輕柔、舒服的風，通常比強風弱，常讓人聯想到空氣輕輕流動。","examples":[{"en":"A cool breeze came through the open window.","zh":"一陣涼風從開著的窗戶吹了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The evening breeze moved the curtains gently.","zh":"晚風輕輕吹動了窗簾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0115d9783a40011","term":"breeze","forms":["breeze","breezes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕而易舉的事","explanation":"把事情想象成被微風輕輕帶過：a breeze 可以指某件事非常容易，幾乎不費力。","examples":[{"en":"The final exam was a breeze after all that practice.","zh":"練習了那麼久之後，期末考試簡直太容易了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With this map, finding the trail will be a breeze.","zh":"有了這張地圖，找到那條小路就輕而易舉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-312deacf985c6f2e","term":"breeze","forms":["breeze","breezes","breezing","breezed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕鬆隨意地移動或推進","explanation":"像一陣風不受阻礙地飄過一樣，breeze 表示輕鬆、自在地移動，或毫不費力地取得進展。","examples":[{"en":"She breezed through the interview and got the job.","zh":"她輕鬆透過了面試，得到了那份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He breezed into the room as if nothing had happened.","zh":"他若無其事地輕鬆走進了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fce07324e0e72e071842","word":"bribe","forms":["bribe"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c5d287415e04414","term":"bribe","forms":["bribe","bribes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賄賂","explanation":"指為了影響某人的決定或讓對方違法、違背職責而給的錢、禮物或其他利益。重點不是“送東西”本身，而是用好處換取不正當幫助。","examples":[{"en":"The company was fined for offering bribes to government officials.","zh":"這家公司因向政府官員行賄而被罰款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer refused the bribe and reported it.","zh":"那名官員拒絕了賄賂並舉報了此事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22eafd1f550cfba2","term":"bribe","forms":["bribe","bribes","bribing","bribed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"行賄；收買","explanation":"指給某人錢或好處，換取對方改變原本的決定，尤其是讓對方違法、撒謊或違背職責。它就是把名詞 bribe 遞給別人並要求對方採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"They tried to bribe the witness into changing her story.","zh":"他們試圖收買證人，讓她改變證詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He bribed an official to approve the permit.","zh":"他行賄收買了一名官員，讓對方批准許可證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c762830741c126f19e44","word":"brick","forms":["brick"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abeae24c888c0a89","term":"brick","forms":["brick","bricks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"磚塊","explanation":"指用泥土、黏土等燒硬或壓制成的長方形建築塊，用來砌牆、鋪路等。它是最基本的實體義，也是其他“堅硬、沉重、磚狀”引申義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"The workers used bricks to build the garden wall.","zh":"工人們用磚砌花園圍牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She picked up a brick from the path.","zh":"她從小路上撿起一塊磚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a8c64b68df1deda","term":"brick","forms":["brick","bricks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"磚這種材料","explanation":"把許多磚作為一種建築材料整體來談，而不是強調某一塊磚。這裡關注的是房屋或牆所用的材料。","examples":[{"en":"The old house is built of brick.","zh":"這座老房子是用磚建成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Brick is still a popular building material.","zh":"磚仍然是一種常用的建築材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3908536141146c393575","word":"bride","forms":["bride"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd8c0e3641076dd9","term":"bride","forms":["bride","brides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新娘","explanation":"指正在結婚或剛結婚的女性，重點是她處在婚禮前後這一階段，而不只是已經結婚的女性。","examples":[{"en":"The bride smiled as she walked down the aisle.","zh":"新娘沿著過道走來時露出了微笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bride's sister helped her choose a dress.","zh":"新娘的姐姐幫她挑選禮服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97581f1bacd0961b76cf","word":"bridegroom/groom","forms":["bridegroom","groom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d05408d02deda87","term":"bridegroom","forms":["bridegroom","bridegrooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新郎","explanation":"指正在結婚、即將結婚或剛剛結婚的男子，也就是婚禮中的男方。它和 bride 相對，二者共同構成婚禮上的一對新人。","examples":[{"en":"The bridegroom smiled as he walked down the aisle.","zh":"新郎沿著過道走來時露出了微笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridegroom and bride thanked their families after the ceremony.","zh":"儀式結束後，新郎和新娘向家人表示了感謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridegroom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22c2764cae436750","term":"groom","forms":["groom","grooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新郎","explanation":"指即將結婚或正在舉行婚禮的男子，也就是婚禮中的新郎。","examples":[{"en":"The groom smiled as the bride walked down the aisle.","zh":"新娘走過通道時，新郎笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The groom thanked everyone for coming.","zh":"新郎感謝大家前來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/groom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e138d1532a06779d","term":"groom","forms":["groom","grooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬伕；馬匹護理員","explanation":"指負責照料馬匹的人，包括給馬刷洗、整理和日常護理。","examples":[{"en":"The groom brushed the horses before the race.","zh":"馬伕在比賽前給馬刷了毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The groom brushed mud from the horse's legs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/groom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-17f29b073143d8cd97b5","word":"bridge","forms":["bridge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91ee6e6520f97d45","term":"bridge","forms":["bridge","bridges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橋","explanation":"指橫跨河流、峽谷、道路等分隔物的建築或自然結構，讓人、車輛或其他東西能夠從一邊到另一邊。","examples":[{"en":"We crossed the old bridge over the river.","zh":"我們走過了河上的那座舊橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rope bridge swayed in the wind.","zh":"吊橋在風中搖晃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e27f72165380e7d4","term":"bridge","forms":["bridge","bridges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紐帶；橋樑","explanation":"指把兩個國家、群體、思想或領域聯絡起來的人、事物或渠道；它把“跨過分隔”這個實體形象延伸到了抽象關係。","examples":[{"en":"The program serves as a bridge between schools and local businesses.","zh":"這個專案充當學校和當地企業之間的橋樑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Food can form a bridge between unfamiliar cultures.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a94afaea478d84e6","term":"bridge","forms":["bridge","bridges","bridging","bridged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"架橋；跨過","explanation":"指在障礙上架起橋，或讓某物像橋一樣跨過溝壑、河流等分隔物。","examples":[{"en":"The new road will bridge the narrow valley.","zh":"新公路將跨過這條狹窄的山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They bridged the stream with a wooden walkway.","zh":"他們用一條木棧道跨過了小溪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2226a7584c44914","term":"bridge","forms":["bridge","bridges","bridging","bridged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"彌合；連線","explanation":"指縮小兩方之間的差距、分歧或隔閡，把原本分開的兩邊重新聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"Open discussion can bridge the gap between the two groups.","zh":"公開討論可以彌合這兩個群體之間的隔閡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement helped bridge their differences.","zh":"這項協議幫助他們彌合了分歧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29a8825bd242f14386ee","word":"brief","forms":["brief"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e55dd213bd4f3860","term":"brief","forms":["brief","briefer","more brief","briefest","most brief"],"pos":"adj","zh":"短暫的","explanation":"表示某件事持續的時間不長，很快就結束；它仍然可能十分引人注目或重要。","examples":[{"en":"They had a brief meeting before lunch.","zh":"他們午飯前開了一個短會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her visit was brief but memorable.","zh":"她的來訪很短暫，卻令人難忘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-496ec6454f6d09aa","term":"brief","forms":["brief","briefer","more brief","briefest","most brief"],"pos":"adj","zh":"簡潔的","explanation":"表示說話或寫作使用的詞不多，內容表達得很集中。","examples":[{"en":"Please give us a brief explanation of the problem.","zh":"請簡要解釋一下這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager gave a brief update on the project.","zh":"經理簡要通報了專案的最新情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5643d256949f1331","term":"brief","forms":["brief","briefs","briefing","briefed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人作簡要彙報","explanation":"把一項新進展、背景和可能影響整理成重點，告訴擁有決策權的人。它像把一份簡短而有用的紙交給負責人，使對方能迅速掌握情況。","examples":[{"en":"The director was briefed on the safety concerns.","zh":"主任獲悉了安全方面的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please brief the team on the new schedule.","zh":"請向團隊簡要說明新的日程安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-645274c37697db3f009b","word":"briefcase","forms":["briefcase"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96b1ee1e6e92edbc","term":"briefcase","forms":["briefcase","briefcases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公文包","explanation":"一種通常呈長方形、用來攜帶檔案和辦公用品的包，常見於商務或辦公場合。可以把它想成把重要檔案裝在一個便於提拿的“檔案盒”裡。","examples":[{"en":"He carried a black briefcase into the meeting.","zh":"他提著一個黑色公文包走進了會議室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her briefcase was full of contracts and reports.","zh":"她的公文包裡裝滿了合同和報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/briefcase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a87b3e348ccb598ecb71","word":"bright","forms":["bright"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2724ef75699956c","term":"bright","forms":["bright","brighter","brightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明亮的","explanation":"光線很充足，發出或反射出明顯的亮光，像記憶鉤子裡光亮向外擴散的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The bright morning light filled the kitchen.","zh":"明亮的晨光充滿了廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bright lantern lit the whole tent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26c171ca9f8443f1","term":"bright","forms":["bright","brighter","brightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"快樂樂觀的","explanation":"形容人的精神狀態明快、有希望、對事情抱有樂觀態度，就像內在的光亮向外擴散。","examples":[{"en":"She stayed bright and hopeful during the long recovery.","zh":"在漫長的康復過程中，她始終保持樂觀和希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her bright outlook lifted everyone's spirits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5f3a4d4365072a6","term":"bright","forms":["bright","brighter","brightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聰明的","explanation":"形容人理解快、思路清楚、解決問題的能力強，是“頭腦發亮”的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"Mina is bright and learns new software very quickly.","zh":"米娜很聰明，學新軟體學得非常快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bright student spotted the error immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6255e14abc09aa5c8882","word":"brilliant","forms":["brilliant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c9dec3b56a4cc23","term":"brilliant","forms":["brilliant","more brilliant","most brilliant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"耀眼的","explanation":"形容光非常強、非常耀眼，像寶石反射出的光一樣奪目。","examples":[{"en":"Brilliant lights lined the harbor at night.","zh":"夜晚，耀眼的燈光沿著港口排列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Brilliant sunlight reflected off the freshly fallen snow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brilliant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31c9b8f63dda6793","term":"brilliant","forms":["brilliant","more brilliant","most brilliant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"卓越非凡的","explanation":"形容表現、作品、計劃或結果好得突出，令人讚歎；這是把耀眼的光彩比喻到成就上。","examples":[{"en":"That was a brilliant solution to a difficult problem.","zh":"那是解決難題的一個絕妙辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pianist gave a brilliant performance of the concerto.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brilliant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18cae8735d338285","term":"brilliant","forms":["brilliant","more brilliant","most brilliant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其聰明的","explanation":"形容人的智力、洞察力或才華非常突出；這是把耀眼的光彩進一步比喻成頭腦的出眾。","examples":[{"en":"She is a brilliant mathematician.","zh":"她是一位極其聰明的數學家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brilliant student solved a problem that baffled everyone else.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brilliant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4311902217ad5aa4d966","word":"bring","forms":["bring"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-421fa4f2a28b5f46","term":"bring","forms":["bring","brings","bringing","brought","broughten","brang","brung","bringed","bringest","broughtest","bringeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"帶來；帶到","explanation":"把人或物從別處帶到說話人、聽話人或句子設定的目標地點，也可以表示替某人帶來某物。這是 bring 最基礎、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could you bring me a glass of water, please?","zh":"請你給我拿一杯水來，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please bring your passport to the appointment.","zh":"請帶上你的護照來赴約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28e95d1ed4f6f04e","term":"bring","forms":["bring","brings","bringing","brought","broughten","brang","brung","bringed","bringest","broughtest","bringeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"導致；帶來","explanation":"把某個結果帶到現實中，也就是造成或促成某事。這裡沒有具體物品被搬運，但“結果被帶來”的核心概念仍然存在。","examples":[{"en":"The decision brought a wave of criticism.","zh":"這項決定帶來了一陣批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement brought peace to the region.","zh":"這項協議給該地區帶來了和平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd50eb17ec5144854078","word":"brink","forms":["brink"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17e003d2577ed46d","term":"brink","forms":["brink","brinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陡峭處的邊緣","explanation":"指懸崖、河岸等陡峭地方的最外側邊緣，也就是再向前就可能跌落或越過邊界的位置。這是“臨界關頭”比喻義的具體影象來源。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers stopped at the brink of the cliff.","zh":"徒步者們在懸崖邊停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow path led us to the brink of the river.","zh":"一條狹窄的小路把我們帶到了河岸邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b958656d36f3523","term":"brink","forms":["brink","brinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臨界關頭","explanation":"比喻某人或某事已經接近一個關鍵結果或重大變化，只差一步就會進入新的狀態。它保留了“站在邊緣、再往前就跨過去”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The company is on the brink of bankruptcy.","zh":"這家公司正瀕臨破產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stood on the brink of a major decision.","zh":"她正處在作出重大決定的關頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9331f09c96d5e52ecbef","word":"broad","forms":["broad"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-969e9135cce5d9a3","term":"broad","forms":["broad","broader","broadest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬的","explanation":"表示從一邊到另一邊的距離較大，強調實際的橫向寬度。","examples":[{"en":"The table is broad enough for six people.","zh":"這張桌子夠寬，可以坐六個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A broad river separated the two towns.","zh":"一條寬闊的河流隔開了兩個城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a89205d4485f746a","term":"broad","forms":["broad","broader","broadest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全面的；寬泛的","explanation":"表示考慮的範圍很大、立場不狹窄，能夠涵蓋許多情況或觀點。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement sets out broad principles for cooperation.","zh":"這項協議提出了合作的總體原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a broad understanding of modern history.","zh":"她對現代史有較全面的瞭解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-845c3ed1217c4713","term":"broad","forms":["broad","broader","broadest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"概括的；總體的","explanation":"表示只說總體方向或大致情況，不涉及具體細節；這是“範圍向外展開”在語言和觀點上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"We are in broad agreement about the main goal.","zh":"我們在主要目標上基本達成了一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave us a broad outline of the plan.","zh":"他向我們概述了計劃的大致框架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e88199c423228a456677","word":"broadcast","forms":["broadcast"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e20a3033612e65c4","term":"broadcast","forms":["broadcast","broadcasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣播；播送","explanation":"指把聲音、影象或資訊透過廣播、電視等方式傳給所有可能接收的人，重點是“向廣大範圍撒出去”的傳送行為。","examples":[{"en":"The president gave a live broadcast from the capital.","zh":"總統從首都進行了現場直播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We listened to the broadcast together.","zh":"我們一起收聽了這次廣播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broadcast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47782b6d9eab73b9","term":"broadcast","forms":["broadcast","broadcasts","broadcasting","broadcasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"廣播；播出","explanation":"把訊息、聲音、影象或節目透過廣播、電視或電子手段傳給許多人，就像把內容撒向廣大的聽眾。","examples":[{"en":"The station broadcast the emergency warning nationwide.","zh":"這家電臺向全國播出了緊急警報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The match was broadcast live last night.","zh":"這場比賽昨晚進行了現場直播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broadcast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf304672dda5383706b4","word":"broaden","forms":["broaden"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9dae59f68c3e130d","term":"broaden","forms":["broaden","broadens","broadening","broadened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變寬；擴大範圍","explanation":"表示主動把某物變得更寬、更廣，既可以指道路、空間等實際寬度，也可以指知識、經驗或視野等抽象範圍。核心畫面是把原本有限的範圍向兩邊展開。","examples":[{"en":"Reading widely can broaden your knowledge of other cultures.","zh":"廣泛閱讀可以拓寬你對其他文化的瞭解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course broadened her experience in working with children.","zh":"這門課程拓展了她與兒童合作的經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broaden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-787041c0d4172016","term":"broaden","forms":["broaden","broadens","broadening","broadened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變寬；變廣","explanation":"表示某物自己變得更寬或範圍逐漸擴大，不強調有人主動使它改變。它可以描述道路等實際物件，也可以描述興趣、討論範圍等抽象內容。","examples":[{"en":"The narrow road gradually broadened as we approached the town.","zh":"我們接近城鎮時，狹窄的道路逐漸變寬了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river broadens as it approaches the sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broaden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c318132fa32974d9b455","word":"brochure","forms":["brochure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d63095064aad1ea","term":"brochure","forms":["brochure","brochures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宣傳冊；小冊子","explanation":"指一本篇幅較短、印有文字和圖片的小冊子，用來介紹產品、服務、地點、活動或其他資訊，常帶有宣傳目的。它的核心畫面是“把介紹內容裝訂在一起，遞給讀者檢視”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel gave us a brochure about local attractions.","zh":"酒店給了我們一本介紹當地景點的宣傳冊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have a look in the brochure for information about the new vacuum cleaner.","zh":"請在宣傳冊裡看看這款新吸塵器的資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brochure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f75410494f0b1ca06a54","word":"broil","forms":["broil"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"broil","forms":["broil"],"pos":"v.","zh":"用上火烤；炙烤","examples":[{"en":"Broil the fish for five minutes until the surface turns golden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We usually broil the steaks instead of frying them.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad8fdaf22c809ba3d2e6","word":"broke","forms":["broke"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1678ba43b229c92","term":"broke","forms":["broke","broker","more broke","brokest","most broke"],"pos":"adj","zh":"破產的","explanation":"指一個人或機構的錢已經耗盡，經濟上無法維持，接近或已經破產；核心畫面就是經濟狀況“破掉了”。","examples":[{"en":"The small company went broke after two bad years.","zh":"這家小公司經歷兩年經營不善後破產了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm broke until my next paycheck arrives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4456485b10c173a6","term":"broke","forms":["broke","broker","more broke","brokest","most broke"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身無分文的","explanation":"表示手頭一點錢也沒有，重點是當前沒有可用的錢，不一定表示已經正式破產。","examples":[{"en":"I can't go out tonight—I’m completely broke.","zh":"我今晚不能出去——我完全沒錢了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm completely broke until my wages arrive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcbbcd5a59bf48a18e71","word":"bronze","forms":["bronze"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d68c96ec9eff69aa","term":"bronze","forms":["bronze","more bronze","most bronze"],"pos":"adj","zh":"青銅製的","explanation":"表示物品由青銅製成，重點是材料，而不是顏色；例如青銅門或青銅飾件。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a bronze statue of a horse.","zh":"這座博物館有一尊青銅馬雕像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bronze statue guarded the entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7575bc8d07c2d5aa","term":"bronze","forms":["bronze","bronzes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"青銅","explanation":"指銅與錫等金屬組成的合金，常用於雕像、器物和裝飾；這裡強調真實的材料。","examples":[{"en":"The statue was cast in bronze.","zh":"這座雕像是用青銅鑄造的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bronze is harder than pure copper.","zh":"青銅比純銅更硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60793c345e3940b4","term":"bronze","forms":["bronze","bronzes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"青銅色","explanation":"指類似青銅的紅棕色，可以是物體本身的顏色，也可以指這種顏色的材料或色調。","examples":[{"en":"The curtains are a warm bronze.","zh":"窗簾是溫暖的青銅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painter mixed bronze with a little white.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b79624284645b7cba19d","word":"brook","forms":["brook"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30ae222a1865bd38","term":"brook","forms":["brook","brooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小溪；溪流","explanation":"brook 是一條比河小的自然水流，可以想象成在田野、樹林或山谷中不斷流動的小溪。","examples":[{"en":"A clear brook runs through the forest.","zh":"一條清澈的小溪流過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children crossed the brook on stepping-stones.","zh":"孩子們踩著踏腳石過了小溪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-100a07d1e4368153d76b","word":"broom","forms":["broom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd6d42bbb2db4d1b","term":"broom","forms":["broom","brooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"掃帚","explanation":"掃帚是把纖維或刷毛綁在長柄一端、用來清掃地面和其他表面的工具。它正是“把東西掃開、掃走”這一核心形象的起點。","examples":[{"en":"I used a broom to sweep the leaves off the porch.","zh":"我用掃帚把門廊上的樹葉掃掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a broom behind the kitchen door.","zh":"廚房門後面有一把掃帚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-915db8f30b8d03054fe4","word":"broth","forms":["broth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-814313670ffa5c00","term":"broth","forms":["broth","broths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煮出的湯汁","explanation":"指肉、蔬菜等食材在水中煮過後得到的有味湯汁，重點是用來煮食材或作為其他菜的液體基礎，而不一定是一道完整的湯。","examples":[{"en":"The noodles are served in a rich chicken broth.","zh":"這碗麵浸在濃郁的雞湯汁裡端上來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She added the vegetables to the broth and let it simmer.","zh":"她把蔬菜加入湯汁中，讓它慢慢燉煮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0073982785aae40e","term":"broth","forms":["broth","broths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"以湯汁做成的湯","explanation":"指在煮出的湯汁中加入蔬菜、香草、肉塊等配料後做成的一道湯；此時關注的是可以端上桌食用的完整湯品。","examples":[{"en":"The chef served a spicy broth with mushrooms and noodles.","zh":"廚師端上了一碗加有蘑菇和麵條的辣湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We warmed ourselves with bowls of vegetable broth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b4bd77cec705cf5df01","word":"brother","forms":["brother"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-280182f5f428ac80","term":"brother","forms":["brother","brothers","brethren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兄弟","explanation":"指和另一個人有相同父母的男性，是最基本、最常見的家庭關係義。","examples":[{"en":"My brother lives in a small town near the coast.","zh":"我哥哥住在海邊附近的一個小鎮上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her younger brother is starting university this year.","zh":"她的弟弟今年要開始上大學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-722c7b1034a38b3d","term":"brother","forms":["brother","brothers","brethren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有共同父母的男性兄弟","explanation":"範圍比“親兄弟”更寬，只要至少和另一個人有一位共同父母，就可以稱為“brother”，包括同父異母或同母異父的兄弟。","examples":[{"en":"I met my half-brother for the first time last summer.","zh":"去年夏天我第一次見到了同父異母的哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My brother and I share our mother's curly hair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b49c7fc0eee09b9c3685","word":"brotherhood","forms":["brotherhood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6680580dec8cefe3","term":"brotherhood","forms":["brotherhood","brotherhoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兄弟關係；兄弟情誼","explanation":"指兄弟之間的身份、關係或親密團結，也可以不按血緣來理解，表示像兄弟一樣互相支援的情誼。這是“兄弟圈”這一核心形象最直接的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The team developed a strong sense of brotherhood during the difficult season.","zh":"這支隊伍在那段艱難的賽季中培養出了強烈的兄弟情誼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their brotherhood survived many years of separation.","zh":"他們之間的兄弟情誼經受住了多年的分離。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brotherhood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbfd777dc1271519","term":"brotherhood","forms":["brotherhood","brotherhoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共同體；團體","explanation":"指一群因為共同目標、信仰或活動而組織起來的人，成員不必真的互為兄弟。它是把“兄弟圈”擴大成有共同身份的組織或團體。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers formed a brotherhood to help families after the flood.","zh":"志願者們組成了一個共同體，幫助洪水後的家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was proud to belong to a brotherhood of skilled craftsmen.","zh":"他以屬於一個技藝精湛的工匠團體為榮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brotherhood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5eb67f9f8409b9c3f739","word":"brown","forms":["brown"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49d48141eb5c9dce","term":"brown","forms":["brown","browner","more brown","brownest","most brown"],"pos":"adj","zh":"棕色的","explanation":"指顏色像巧克力、咖啡或深色木頭一樣的棕色，是 brown 最基本、最常見的形容詞意思。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a brown coat and black boots.","zh":"她穿著一件棕色外套和一雙黑靴子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaves turned brown in late autumn.","zh":"深秋時，樹葉變成了棕色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13d4228d4155bf79","term":"brown","forms":["brown","browns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棕色","explanation":"指棕色這種顏色；複數 browns 可表示畫面或物品中的多種棕色色調。","examples":[{"en":"The painting uses warm browns and greens.","zh":"這幅畫用了暖棕色和綠色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He mixed brown with a little white.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5128d032cf1fcf5c","term":"brown","forms":["brown","browns","browning","browned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變成棕色","explanation":"指食物或其他東西自己逐漸變成棕色，核心畫面就是顏色由淺或其他顏色變深、變棕。","examples":[{"en":"Fry the onions until they brown.","zh":"把洋蔥炒到變成棕色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The grass browned during the hot, dry summer.","zh":"炎熱乾燥的夏天裡，草變黃褐了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f0f9050a80bce67","term":"brown","forms":["brown","browns","browning","browned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把食物煎成棕色","explanation":"指透過加熱把食物表面煎到棕色，通常也意味著形成更香的焦黃色表面。","examples":[{"en":"Brown the meat before adding the tomatoes.","zh":"加入番茄前，先把肉煎成棕色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Brown the garlic lightly in olive oil.","zh":"用橄欖油把大蒜略微煎成棕色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25070cd932a7309a6e0b","word":"browse","forms":["browse"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a4b49625f836265","term":"browse","forms":["browse","browses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瀏覽行為","explanation":"指沒有明確目標地翻看、逛看，像動物邊走邊挑食一樣，看看有什麼感興趣的東西。","examples":[{"en":"I had a browse through the local market before lunch.","zh":"午飯前我在當地市場隨便逛了逛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A quick browse through the catalog revealed several bargains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/browse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c62a9126f00d4a32","term":"browse","forms":["browse","browses","browsing","browsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隨意瀏覽","explanation":"指沒有預先確定目標，只是四處看看、遇到感興趣的內容再停下來了解，像動物邊走邊挑食。","examples":[{"en":"I'm just browsing around, so please take your time.","zh":"我只是隨便看看，你不用著急。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He browsed through the shelves for a gift.","zh":"他在書架間隨意翻看，想找一件禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/browse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9f4b8a0587af2d0c080","word":"bruise","forms":["bruise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0898c4fe621f9d04","term":"bruise","forms":["bruise","bruises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮膚瘀青","explanation":"指皮下受到撞擊後形成的青紫色痕跡，通常皮膚沒有破裂；它是“外力留下的表面傷痕”這一核心概念最典型的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She had a large bruise on her knee after the fall.","zh":"她摔倒後膝蓋上有一大片瘀青。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A purple bruise spread across her shin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c51a0ad776ca4bc5","term":"bruise","forms":["bruise","bruises","bruising","bruised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把人打出瘀青","explanation":"指用撞擊使人的皮膚留下瘀青，重點是造成了外表可見的傷痕而沒有打破皮膚。它是名詞核心義轉成動作後的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"The fall bruised his shoulder.","zh":"摔倒使他的肩膀出現了瘀青。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bruised her arm against the door.","zh":"她的手臂撞到門上，撞出了瘀青。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07829281031d4a33b91c","word":"brunch","forms":["brunch"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0dd4b77303e066d","term":"brunch","forms":["brunch","brunches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"早午餐","explanation":"指在早餐之後、午餐之前吃的一頓飯，通常把早餐和午餐的時間或食物特點結合在一起。","examples":[{"en":"I normally have brunch at the café next to work.","zh":"我通常在公司旁邊的咖啡館吃早午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a late brunch on Sunday.","zh":"我們星期天吃了一頓較晚的早午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brunch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-029f33c2a6a1143cf125","word":"brush","forms":["brush"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ccfcb6ff89adb129","term":"brush","forms":["brush","brushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刷子","explanation":"指由許多刷毛或類似細絲固定在柄上製成的工具，用來清潔、塗漆、整理頭髮等。它是 brush 最核心、最容易聯想到的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I need a small brush to clean the keyboard.","zh":"我需要一把小刷子來清潔鍵盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a brush for painting the fence.","zh":"她買了一把刷子來給柵欄刷漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e71654929604098","term":"brush","forms":["brush","brushes","brushing","brushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刷洗","explanation":"表示用刷子清潔某物，最典型的例子是刷牙。動作重點是反覆讓刷毛掃過表面以去除汙物。","examples":[{"en":"Brush your teeth before you go to bed.","zh":"睡覺前刷牙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I brushed the mud off my boots.","zh":"我把靴子上的泥刷掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e6747bd219dfaa7573f","word":"brutal","forms":["brutal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17508b9d72c9f2dc","term":"brutal","forms":["brutal","more brutal","most brutal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"殘酷暴力的","explanation":"指行為、衝突或對待方式極其兇殘，帶有造成嚴重傷害、毫不留情的感覺。它描寫的不只是“很激烈”，而是通常含有暴力、殘忍或冷酷的一面。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers carried out a brutal attack on the village.","zh":"士兵對那個村莊發動了一次殘酷的襲擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers fled the army's brutal campaign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brutal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b50af052f606e7f","term":"brutal","forms":["brutal","more brutal","most brutal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直截了當而不加掩飾的","explanation":"指說話或表達完全不粉飾令人不快的部分，直接把刺耳的事實擺出來。它和“冷酷的”有聯絡，但重點是表達方式不繞彎、不安慰，而不一定表示說話者惡毒。","examples":[{"en":"I need your brutal honesty before I submit this proposal.","zh":"在我提交這份提案前，我需要你毫不留情的實話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor gave a brutal assessment of my draft.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brutal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df4ac416257333cf770e","word":"bubble","forms":["bubble"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d08f1a29d271bc0","term":"bubble","forms":["bubble","bubbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氣泡；泡沫","explanation":"指由空氣或其他氣體形成、通常被液體薄膜包住的球狀小體，比如肥皂水裡的泡泡。順著記憶鉤子，它就是那個不斷上升、膨脹的真實氣泡。","examples":[{"en":"The children chased bubbles across the garden.","zh":"孩子們在花園裡追逐泡泡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bubble rose slowly to the surface of the water.","zh":"一個氣泡慢慢升到水面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3b0d442cc1d3efd","term":"bubble","forms":["bubble","bubbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"市場泡沫","explanation":"指某種資產因投機而在短期內漲到遠超實際價值的水平，隨後價格又迅速下跌。它正對應記憶鉤子中“氣泡膨脹過度後破裂”的經濟比喻。","examples":[{"en":"Many investors feared that the housing bubble would burst.","zh":"許多投資者擔心房地產泡沫會破裂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technology bubble pushed share prices far above their real value.","zh":"科技泡沫把股價推到了遠高於實際價值的水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6b298082c9b80c6","term":"bubble","forms":["bubble","bubbles","bubbling","bubbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒泡；沸騰上湧","explanation":"指液體、食物或表面產生氣泡並向上冒，就像記憶鉤子裡不斷上升的真實氣泡。也可形容塗層等表面鼓起成泡。","examples":[{"en":"The soup began to bubble as soon as it reached a boil.","zh":"湯一沸騰就開始冒泡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paint is bubbling near the window.","zh":"窗戶附近的油漆正在起泡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48a3bb6f2abf08a6","term":"bubble","forms":["bubble","bubbles","bubbling","bubbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐層上湧；向上傳遞","explanation":"指資訊、事件或變化像氣泡上升一樣，穿過一個系統或層級，逐漸傳到更高層。它強調從較深處向表層或上級浮現。","examples":[{"en":"Questions from the local teams soon bubbled up to senior management.","zh":"地方團隊提出的問題很快傳到了高階管理層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Useful ideas often bubble up from informal conversations.","zh":"有用的想法常常從非正式交談中逐漸浮現出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5879b8d250ca6e74ca6","word":"bucket","forms":["bucket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10b360784f3619eb","term":"bucket","forms":["bucket","buckets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"桶；提桶","explanation":"一種通常帶提手的硬質容器，用來裝水、食物或其他小物品；這是 bucket 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please fill the bucket with clean water.","zh":"請把桶裝滿乾淨的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carried a bucket of sand to the garden.","zh":"她提了一桶沙子到花園裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bucket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51bf59055ac512c1","term":"bucket","forms":["bucket","buckets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一桶的量","explanation":"不強調桶這個容器，而是指桶裡能裝下的那一份數量。","examples":[{"en":"The horse drank a whole bucket of water.","zh":"那匹馬喝下了整整一桶水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pour another bucket of water into the trough.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bucket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb354856ade3a6275867","word":"bud","forms":["bud"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-395223ece72ed12e","term":"bud","forms":["bud","buds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"芽；花蕾","explanation":"bud 是植物剛長出來、還沒有完全展開的葉芽或花蕾；它像一個包住新生命的小小突起，是這個詞最核心的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The rose bush is covered with buds.","zh":"這株玫瑰上長滿了花蕾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The buds will open in a few days.","zh":"這些花蕾幾天後就會開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7296c5cca798074f","term":"bud","forms":["bud","buds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"萌芽中的事物","explanation":"bud 可以把“芽”這個形象用於抽象事物，表示某種能力、變化或發展剛剛開始，還沒有完全形成。","examples":[{"en":"The idea was still only a bud of a larger project.","zh":"這個想法還只是一個更大專案的雛形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She nurtured the first buds of his musical talent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f704663d979da0f","term":"bud","forms":["bud","buds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"朋友；夥伴","explanation":"bud 是 buddy 的簡短形式，表示朋友或夥伴；它和“芽”的聯絡可以理解為一起成長、關係親近的人。","examples":[{"en":"I'm meeting a few buds for lunch.","zh":"我要和幾個朋友一起吃午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My bud helped me move into my new apartment.","zh":"我的朋友幫我搬進了新公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0027334063aa620","term":"bud","forms":["bud","buds","budding","budded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發芽；長出花蕾","explanation":"bud 作動詞時，最基本的意思是植物長出芽或花蕾，也就是名詞義中“芽”開始形成的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The apple trees are beginning to bud.","zh":"蘋果樹開始發芽了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden usually buds early in spring.","zh":"這個花園通常在早春就開始萌發新芽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0af96a8ed622a394e8b2","word":"budget","forms":["budget"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-951288ab29ecef2a","term":"budget","forms":["budget","budgets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預算額度","explanation":"指為某項活動、機構或某段時間預先劃定的可用金額或資源，也就是“袋子裡允許使用的錢”。","examples":[{"en":"The project has a limited budget for equipment.","zh":"這個專案用於裝置的預算有限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are on a tight budget this month.","zh":"我們這個月的預算很緊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/budget","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f08efa8f5ef150e","term":"budget","forms":["budget","budgets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預算表","explanation":"指把預計收入、支出及各項用途列出來的計劃或檔案，相當於把袋子裡的錢分項寫清楚。","examples":[{"en":"The finance team prepared next year's budget.","zh":"財務團隊編制了明年的預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The budget lists every department's expected spending.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/budget","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2dc5e0d5223c817","term":"budget","forms":["budget","budgets","budgeting","budgeted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編制預算","explanation":"指制定預算，計算在某段時間內有多少錢、要花在哪裡，也就是把袋子裡的錢規劃清楚。","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses must budget carefully during slow seasons.","zh":"小企業在生意淡季必須仔細編制預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We budget carefully for the quieter winter months.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/budget","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"114":2}}},{"id":"ceec-198becaf9c45016fec5d","word":"buffalo","forms":["buffalo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef47a036085e67ef","term":"buffalo","forms":["buffalo","buffaloes","buffalos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水牛","explanation":"指真正的水牛類動物，包括非洲水牛和亞洲水牛等大型牛科動物。記憶時可把它看成一頭生活在野外或水邊、體格強壯的牛。","examples":[{"en":"A herd of buffaloes crossed the river at dawn.","zh":"一群水牛在黎明時渡過了河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide warned us not to approach the Cape buffalo.","zh":"嚮導警告我們不要靠近非洲水牛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffalo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2d0017282739403","term":"buffalo","forms":["buffalo","buffaloes","buffalos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"北美野牛","explanation":"在北美語境中，常指北美野牛，而不是嚴格意義上的水牛。它保留了“大型、強壯、難以對付的牛科動物”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"We watched buffalo grazing across the prairie.","zh":"我們看著北美野牛在大草原上吃草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A herd of buffalo grazed beyond the railway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffalo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3603a9780bdecf2bb5bf","word":"buffet","forms":["buffet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29619b3b67a490c1","term":"buffet","forms":["buffet","buffets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自助餐檯","explanation":"指擺放食物和飲料、供人自行取用的櫃檯或餐檯；重點是“到這裡自己拿吃的”。","examples":[{"en":"We left our coats by the door and went straight to the buffet.","zh":"我們把外套放在門邊，直接去了自助餐檯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fresh salads stood at one end of the buffet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1041c381c1d9dccc","term":"buffet","forms":["buffet","buffets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自助餐食","explanation":"指已經擺出來、讓客人自己取用的整套食物，而不是餐檯本身；也就是“自助餐”這種吃法或餐食。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel serves a buffet breakfast from seven to ten.","zh":"這家酒店七點到十點供應自助早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The buffet included salads, roast chicken, and fresh fruit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83a89776c2c3fa18","term":"buffet","forms":["buffet","buffets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛擊；一記打擊","explanation":"指手、物體或風猛烈地打來的一下；核心畫面就是某種力量迎面撞擊身體或物體。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden buffet from the wind knocked the hat off his head.","zh":"一陣突如其來的狂風猛擊，把他的帽子從頭上掀掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A buffet from the shield knocked him backward.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buffet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecb53f367b3541da3a14","word":"bug","forms":["bug"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b87d42d16c7cb51e","term":"bug","forms":["bug","bugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"昆蟲","explanation":"指昆蟲，尤其可指半翅目昆蟲；記住那個到處惹麻煩的小蟲，就是這個詞最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"There was a bug crawling across the kitchen floor.","zh":"有一隻小蟲在廚房地板上爬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She brushed the bug off her sleeve.","zh":"她把那隻蟲從袖子上拂掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d528bf19c48eaa4e","term":"bug","forms":["bug","bugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"程式錯誤","explanation":"指軟體、系統或裝置中需要修復的問題；它就像藏起來搗亂的“小蟲”，使程式出現不應有的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The latest update fixed a bug that caused the app to crash.","zh":"最新更新修復了一個導致應用崩潰的程式錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a bug in the payment system.","zh":"我們發現支付系統中有一個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71834adcdfa18e59","term":"bug","forms":["bug","bugs","bugging","bugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使煩惱；打擾","explanation":"像一隻到處惹麻煩的小蟲一樣，持續打擾某人或使某人感到煩惱。","examples":[{"en":"Please stop bugging me while I'm trying to work.","zh":"我正在工作，請別再煩我了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constant noise really bugs our neighbors.","zh":"持續不斷的噪音確實讓我們的鄰居很煩惱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44575cf5b28512d75644","word":"build","forms":["build"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f8d1e887cf604dd","term":"build","forms":["build","builds","building","built","builded","buildest","buildedst","buildeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建造；組裝","explanation":"build最基本的意思是把材料或部件組合起來，搭成一個完整的東西。","examples":[{"en":"They are building a small bridge across the stream.","zh":"他們正在小溪上建一座小橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We built the table from recycled wood.","zh":"我們用回收木材做成了這張桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/build","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4dd2f5f481ae8c7c","term":"build","forms":["build","builds","building","built","builded","buildest","buildedst","buildeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"形成；打造","explanation":"build也可以按照計劃把抽象事物逐步做出來，例如建立事業、產品或影響力。","examples":[{"en":"She built a successful business from a small idea.","zh":"她從一個小想法起步，打造出了一家成功的企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is building a new service for local families.","zh":"團隊正在為當地家庭開發一項新服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/build","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a39b0912f4deeefb","term":"build","forms":["build","builds","building","built","builded","buildest","buildedst","buildeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐步增強","explanation":"把更多東西一層層加上去，就能使力量、信心或影響逐漸變大；build因此也表示“增強、積累”。","examples":[{"en":"Regular practice will build your confidence.","zh":"堅持練習會逐漸增強你的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runners built up speed on the final hill.","zh":"跑步者在最後一個坡道上逐漸加快了速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/build","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5167e9677e1fbc500ecb","word":"building","forms":["building"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-251ca049e127d08e","term":"building","forms":["building","buildings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建造過程","explanation":"指把橋、房屋等東西建起來的行動或整個過程，強調“搭起來”這件事本身，而不是最後形成的建築物。","examples":[{"en":"The building of the new hospital took three years.","zh":"這家新醫院的建造用了三年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building of the bridge is almost finished.","zh":"這座橋的建造快要完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/building","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f8e9f17d60062ff","term":"building","forms":["building","buildings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築物","explanation":"指已經搭建起來、通常有牆和屋頂的實體，如房屋、辦公樓或公寓樓。","examples":[{"en":"My sister lives in that apartment building.","zh":"我姐姐住在那棟公寓樓裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tallest building houses the city archives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/building","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4942fb4e8b58995227b","word":"bulb","forms":["bulb"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7071045ad63c940","term":"bulb","forms":["bulb","bulbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物球莖","explanation":"指鬱金香等植物地下的球莖：它由縮短的莖和多層肥厚的鱗片葉組成，能夠儲存養分並重新長出整株植物。這個意義體現了“圓圓鼓起、孕育後續生長”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"We planted tulip bulbs in the garden in autumn.","zh":"我們秋天在花園裡種下了鬱金香球莖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each bulb should produce several flowers next spring.","zh":"每個球莖明年春天應該會開出好幾朵花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bulb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf8348b4107daaacf154","word":"bulk","forms":["bulk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cfe679704d561366","term":"bulk","forms":["bulk","bulks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體積；分量","explanation":"指物體佔據的空間大小，或由密度和體積共同形成的總體分量；核心畫面就是“一大堆東西有多大、多重”。","examples":[{"en":"The bulk of the machine makes it difficult to move.","zh":"這臺機器體積龐大，很難搬動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The material has little weight but considerable bulk.","zh":"這種材料重量不大，但體積相當可觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bulk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5349da113ad04844","term":"bulk","forms":["bulk","bulks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大部分；主體","explanation":"指一個整體中數量、內容或影響最大的一部分，也就是“主體部分”。它由“一大堆東西”進一步引申為“整體中最大的一塊”。","examples":[{"en":"The bulk of the work was finished before lunch.","zh":"大部分工作在午飯前就完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bulk of the guests arrived by eight.","zh":"大多數客人在八點前到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bulk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d087b612de88bb812445","word":"bulky","forms":["bulky"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-273de2d722c21d7d","term":"bulky","forms":["bulky","bulkier","bulkiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"體積大；分量大","explanation":"形容物品的體積、分量或外形明顯偏大，給人“鼓鼓囊囊、佔地方”的感覺。它既可以說行李、傢俱等實物，也可以說身材寬大或壯實的人。","examples":[{"en":"This bulky suitcase won't fit in the overhead compartment.","zh":"這個體積很大的行李箱放不進頭頂行李艙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sofa is too bulky for this small room.","zh":"這張沙發對這個小房間來說太佔地方了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bulky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b24d4ed439c34784","term":"bulky","forms":["bulky","bulkier","bulkiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"笨重；不便使用","explanation":"這裡從“佔地方”進一步強調物品不好搬、難以收納或使用起來不靈活。重點不只是它大，而是它的大使處理它變得麻煩。","examples":[{"en":"The old camera is reliable but bulky to carry around.","zh":"這臺舊相機很可靠，但帶著到處走很笨重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bulky suitcase would not fit overhead.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bulky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c67c1263651459822c34","word":"bull","forms":["bull"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d20fc53f19bbacc3","term":"bull","forms":["bull","bulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公牛","explanation":"指成年雄性家牛，也就是通常所說的公牛；這是 bull 最基本的形象，記住“公牛般向前頂”即可。","examples":[{"en":"The bull stood quietly beside the fence.","zh":"那頭公牛安靜地站在籬笆旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers keep the bulls separate from the cows.","zh":"農場主把公牛和母牛分開飼養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41ff0fa164a85a44","term":"bull","forms":["bull"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胡說廢話","explanation":"指沒有道理、沒有事實根據的胡說或廢話；可以把它記成公牛般強硬地向前頂，卻脫離了事實。","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement's promise of instant success is a load of bull.","zh":"那則廣告關於立刻成功的承諾純屬胡說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't give me that bull—I checked the figures myself.","zh":"別跟我說那套廢話——我自己核對過數字了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed12eb20000f3e53945e","word":"bullet","forms":["bullet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10e667bbe6d6ad22","term":"bullet","forms":["bullet","bullets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"子彈頭","explanation":"指從槍中高速射出的彈頭，通常由金屬製成。它是 bullet 最基本、也最能幫助記憶其他義項的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The bullet passed through the wall.","zh":"子彈穿過了牆壁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor removed a bullet from his shoulder.","zh":"醫生從他的肩膀裡取出了一顆子彈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bullet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b7486f364b4a046","term":"bullet","forms":["bullet","bullets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專案符號","explanation":"指列表中用來標記各項內容的實心圓“•”。它像一個縮小的彈頭，後來從形狀上借用了 bullet 這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"Use a bullet for each item on the list.","zh":"列表中的每一項都使用一個專案符號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The main points are shown as bullet points.","zh":"要點以專案符號列出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bullet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b00309351013716c","term":"bullet","forms":["bullet","bullets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極快的","explanation":"作定語時表示速度極快，直接把“像子彈一樣飛快”的形象放在名詞前。","examples":[{"en":"We took the bullet train to the coast.","zh":"我們乘高速列車去了海邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He enjoys playing bullet chess online.","zh":"他喜歡在網上下超快棋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bullet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24c5f5564184a4fb93ec","word":"bulletin","forms":["bulletin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec9062600811ef2f","term":"bulletin","forms":["bulletin","bulletins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"官方簡報","explanation":"指由公司、政府或其他機構正式釋出的短報告，目的是讓訊息迅速傳開，常常會被廣播或公開傳播。","examples":[{"en":"The company bulletin announced changes to the policy.","zh":"公司的簡報宣佈了政策變更。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The health department issued a bulletin about the outbreak.","zh":"衛生部門釋出了一份關於疫情暴發的簡報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bulletin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff907b30acdf6340d169","word":"bully","forms":["bully"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d53e7c71d3334100","term":"bully","forms":["bully","bullies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"霸凌者；欺負弱者的人","explanation":"bully 是故意利用力量、地位或優勢，反覆在身體或情感上欺負他人的人，尤其針對自認為無法反抗的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The school called the boy's parents after a bully threatened him.","zh":"一個霸凌者威脅那個男孩後，學校聯絡了他的父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bully demanded money from smaller pupils.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bully","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de4e5327b3cb10c3","term":"bully","forms":["bully","bullies","bullying","bullied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欺負；恐嚇","explanation":"作動詞時，bully 表示像霸凌者一樣故意壓制、威脅或傷害別人，尤其是針對較弱勢的人。","examples":[{"en":"You should never bully someone because they seem different.","zh":"絕不應該因為某人看起來與眾不同就欺負他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The older students bullied him into giving them his lunch.","zh":"高年級學生威脅他，把他的午飯逼著交給了他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bully","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5fbde9bb9c3fd8c22402","word":"bump","forms":["bump"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa3ca0bdc38e9451","term":"bump","forms":["bump","bumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕微碰撞","explanation":"bump 可以指身體或物體之間不嚴重的撞擊，正是“撞出一個凸起”這個記憶鉤子的起點。它通常比 crash 或 accident 輕。","examples":[{"en":"The bike got a small bump against the wall.","zh":"腳踏車輕輕撞了一下牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt a bump when the bus turned sharply.","zh":"公共汽車急轉彎時我感到了一下顛簸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be7ef26ce554e81c","term":"bump","forms":["bump","bumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表面隆起","explanation":"bump 可以指平面上鼓起的一塊，例如道路、地板或物體表面的凸起；這正是“撞出一個凸起”中由碰撞結果形成的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"Slow down—there’s a bump in the road.","zh":"開慢點，路上有個凸起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old table has a bump on one side.","zh":"那張舊桌子的一側有一處凸起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a305f81eff6356e","term":"bump","forms":["bump","bumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮膚腫塊","explanation":"bump 還可以指因受傷或生病而在皮膚上鼓起的腫塊，例如撞到頭後出現的包。","examples":[{"en":"He got a bump on his forehead when he fell.","zh":"他摔倒時額頭上撞出了一個包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse checked the bump on my arm.","zh":"護士檢查了我手臂上的腫塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a607f8668b3fa3ff","term":"bump","forms":["bump","bumps","bumping","bumped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"碰撞","explanation":"表示身體或物體突然、輕微地撞到另一個物體，正像“撞出一個凸起”這個記憶畫面中的第一步。撞擊通常不強調嚴重破壞。","examples":[{"en":"I bumped my knee on the corner of the table.","zh":"我的膝蓋撞到了桌角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two bicycles bumped into each other on the narrow path.","zh":"兩輛腳踏車在狹窄的小路上撞到了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08d1082cc8d85a0833da","word":"bun","forms":["bun"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14e1c1fd11cbf6ba","term":"bun","forms":["bun","buns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小圓麵包；甜麵包","explanation":"指通常較小、較圓的麵包或甜麵包，可以單獨吃，也可以剖開後夾入其他食物；這是最值得優先掌握的意思。它保留了“烤成的小團”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"I bought two buns for breakfast.","zh":"我買了兩個小圓麵包當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the sausage in a warm bun.","zh":"把香腸放進溫熱的小圓麵包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8767636fbc34671e","term":"bun","forms":["bun","buns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"髮髻","explanation":"指把頭髮盤成的圓團，通常位於腦後或頭頂。它和麵包義都帶有“把東西聚成一個小團”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"She wore her hair in a loose bun.","zh":"她把頭髮鬆鬆地盤成了髮髻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I tied my hair into a messy bun before cooking.","zh":"做飯前，我把頭髮隨意盤成了一個髮髻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be7f251c25c4a89fe8c7","word":"bunch","forms":["bunch"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b49527298343880","term":"bunch","forms":["bunch","bunches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一串；一簇；一團","explanation":"指許多相似的東西自然聚在一起，或被系在一起形成的一團，例如葡萄、花或鑰匙。核心畫面就是“分散的東西聚成一團”。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a bunch of bananas at the market.","zh":"她在市場上買了一串香蕉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bunch of grapes hung above the path.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bunch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20908e315080087e","term":"bunch","forms":["bunch","bunches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一夥人","explanation":"指關係較近、經常一起活動的一群朋友或熟人，是把“聚成一團”用於人的說法。語氣通常非正式。","examples":[{"en":"We met the same bunch of friends after work.","zh":"我們下班後見了還是那一夥朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cheerful bunch of volunteers painted the fence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bunch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e6ed65d77d6364eeaed","word":"bundle","forms":["bundle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dceb70e9c03e03b7","term":"bundle","forms":["bundle","bundles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一捆；一組紮在一起的東西","explanation":"指若干物品被繩子、包裝紙等包住或紮在一起形成的一組，重點是“聚成一捆”。","examples":[{"en":"She carried a bundle of firewood into the house.","zh":"她把一捆柴火搬進了屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bundle of old letters lay beneath the loose floorboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bundle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e008eee9a4e89505","term":"bundle","forms":["bundle","bundles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"包裹；捆好的東西","explanation":"指已經包好或紮好、方便攜帶的一件東西，關注的是它作為一個整體被拿走或運送。","examples":[{"en":"A small bundle was waiting by the front door.","zh":"前門旁放著一個小包裹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bundle of newspapers waited beside the gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bundle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0cf52185d52bfdbb20e","word":"burden","forms":["burden"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff4f7b484b7e5ea8","term":"burden","forms":["burden","burdens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沉重負荷","explanation":"指需要背、搬或承受的沉重東西，核心畫面就是壓在身上的重物。","examples":[{"en":"The workers carried the burden up the narrow stairs.","zh":"工人們把重物搬上了狹窄的樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The donkey struggled beneath its heavy burden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-670fc7198025c1b2","term":"burden","forms":["burden","burdens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"責任或負擔","explanation":"指一個人必須承擔的責任、義務或壓力，就像揹著一件看不見的重物。","examples":[{"en":"She felt the burden of responsibility after the manager resigned.","zh":"經理辭職後，她感到了責任的重壓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Caring for his elderly parents became a heavy burden.","zh":"照顧年邁的父母成了一項沉重的負擔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b887db186a5c2224","term":"burden","forms":["burden","burdens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人憂慮或壓抑的事情","explanation":"指持續造成煩惱、憂慮或精神壓力的人和事，是把“沉重的負擔”進一步抽象化。","examples":[{"en":"He did not want to become a burden to his friends.","zh":"他不想成為朋友們的負擔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keeping that secret became an unbearable burden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ebc2d6fc52c19ca","term":"burden","forms":["burden","burdens","burdening","burdened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使承擔負擔","explanation":"指把實際重物或抽象責任壓到某人、某群體或某物上，使其變得更難承受。","examples":[{"en":"The new rules burden small businesses with extra paperwork.","zh":"新規定讓小企業承擔了額外的文書工作負擔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not burden yourself with problems you cannot solve.","zh":"不要讓自己揹負那些你無法解決的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-210760fba8185013b535","word":"bureau","forms":["bureau"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8103e4b037eac9e2","term":"bureau","forms":["bureau","bureaus","bureaux"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理機構；政府部門","explanation":"指政府或其他組織中負責某類事務的管理單位。它強調一個有明確職能的機構，而不只是工作人員所在的房間。","examples":[{"en":"The bureau issued new guidelines for energy conservation.","zh":"該管理機構釋出了新的節能指導方針。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works for the Bureau of Labor Statistics.","zh":"她在勞工統計局工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureau","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dff9b02a1701972","term":"bureau","forms":["bureau","bureaus","bureaux"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資訊服務機構","explanation":"指收集、整理或提供資訊、訊息和相關服務的機構，例如新聞機構、旅行服務機構或就業服務機構。","examples":[{"en":"We booked the tour through a local travel bureau.","zh":"我們透過當地的旅行社預訂了這次旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tourist bureau supplied maps of nearby trails.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureau","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f8b73d9a3cfbd0ef331c","word":"bureaucracy","forms":["bureaucracy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e632104634f5e68","term":"bureaucracy","forms":["bureaucracy","bureaucracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"官僚行政制度","explanation":"指把行政工作分成不同部門和職位，按固定程式和等級許可權，由大量辦公室例行處理的組織制度；這是最適合描述一種完整管理體系的中性用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company introduced a bureaucracy to manage its rapidly growing operations.","zh":"這家公司建立了一套官僚行政制度來管理迅速擴大的業務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reform replaced royal patronage with a professional bureaucracy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa93c7982c6a971c","term":"bureaucracy","forms":["bureaucracy","bureaucracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"官僚主義；繁文縟節","explanation":"指行政制度中不必要的手續、層層審批和機械慣例，導致辦事緩慢或不靈活；這裡從“辦公室按程式辦事”進一步變成了對過度程式化的批評。","examples":[{"en":"The new rules are meant to cut bureaucracy for small businesses.","zh":"這些新規定旨在減少小企業面臨的繁文縟節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent weeks dealing with bureaucracy before getting the permit.","zh":"我們花了好幾個星期處理繁瑣的官僚手續，才拿到許可證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c576c6ee6eebf8845158","word":"bureaucrat","forms":["bureaucrat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cde6680ea9fe57a3","term":"bureaucrat","forms":["bureaucrat","bureaucrats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"官僚體系中的官員","explanation":"指在政府或其他官僚機構中依照制度辦理事務、執行管理工作的人。這個詞把重點放在他所處的制度和許可權體系上，而不只是“在辦公室工作的人”；有時還會讓人聯想到辦事刻板、層層審批。","examples":[{"en":"The bureaucrat explained which forms we needed before approving the application.","zh":"那名官員說明了我們需要哪些表格，然後才批准了申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Residents were frustrated by the slow response from local bureaucrats.","zh":"居民對當地官員遲遲沒有回應感到很不滿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bureaucrat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afd5d0b3c1b4e31cd009","word":"burglar","forms":["burglar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93bb7ea96683d3c9","term":"burglar","forms":["burglar","burglars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入室竊賊","explanation":"指闖入房屋、商店、博物館等場所，意圖偷東西的人；重點是“闖入場所後行竊”，而不只是偷偷拿走物品。","examples":[{"en":"The police arrested the burglar outside the house.","zh":"警方在那所房子外逮捕了入室竊賊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A burglar broke into our shop during the night.","zh":"一名竊賊夜裡闖進了我們的商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burglar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c991cf8e303d8013a9b","word":"burial","forms":["burial"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-063acfd95985afc9","term":"burial","forms":["burial","burials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下葬；埋葬","explanation":"指把死者遺體埋入土地的行為，也可以指為此舉行的下葬儀式；重點是“安放進土裡”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The whole family attended his burial.","zh":"全家人都參加了他的葬禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The burial took place the following morning.","zh":"下葬在第二天早上舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-859facc5a4c9b80ac2ee","word":"burn","forms":["burn"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b534239ec575f45","term":"burn","forms":["burn","burns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燒傷；灼傷","explanation":"指熱、寒冷、電、輻射或腐蝕性化學物質造成的身體損傷，正是“熱力造成變化”留下的實際傷害。","examples":[{"en":"She burned her hand on the hot pan.","zh":"她的手被熱鍋燙傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child was taken to hospital with serious burns.","zh":"那個孩子因嚴重燒傷被送往醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-850cb262f67de470","term":"burn","forms":["burn","burns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"灼熱感；刺痛感","explanation":"指像燒傷一樣的灼熱、刺痛感覺，不一定真的有皮膚損傷；辣椒、藥物或強烈刺激都可能帶來這種感覺。","examples":[{"en":"This cream caused a slight burn on my skin.","zh":"這種藥膏讓我的皮膚有輕微的灼熱感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chili left a hot burn in my mouth.","zh":"辣椒讓我的嘴裡留下了火辣辣的灼熱感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec64914786a1542c","term":"burn","forms":["burn","burns","burning","burned","burnt","brent","burnest","burnedst","burntest","burneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"燒燬","explanation":"指用火把某物燒掉，使它因熱力而被毀壞；這是“熱力造成變化”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"They burned the old letters in the fireplace.","zh":"他們把舊信在壁爐裡燒掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fire burned the shed to the ground.","zh":"大火把小棚子燒成了灰燼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-331185039dbccdbe","term":"burn","forms":["burn","burns","burning","burned","burnt","brent","burnest","burnedst","burntest","burneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"燃燒","explanation":"指物體自己著火併持續燃燒，重點是火焰發生在這個物體上，而不是有人把它燒掉。","examples":[{"en":"The dry leaves burned quickly.","zh":"幹樹葉很快就燒著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the house burn from the hill.","zh":"我們在山上看著那座房子燃燒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57d59e28722dfd55524b","word":"burst","forms":["burst"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98caa7787dd5f5f4","term":"burst","forms":["burst","bursts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爆裂；爆發的一下","explanation":"指爆裂、炸開等事情本身，或由此產生的一聲、一陣突發聲響。它強調突然發生和力量集中，而不是平穩持續地進行。","examples":[{"en":"The loud burst woke everyone in the house.","zh":"那聲巨響把屋裡所有人都吵醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A burst of laughter interrupted the lecture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-287203902679b203","term":"burst","forms":["burst","bursts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一陣強烈表現","explanation":"指短時間內突然而強烈地表現出某種情感、活動或能量，也可以指事情分成幾小段突然進行。核心仍是某種力量集中湧出，而不是平緩展開。","examples":[{"en":"She finished the report in short bursts of work.","zh":"她分幾陣集中工作，完成了報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A burst of applause interrupted her speech.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04fa9839f1e0687a","term":"burst","forms":["burst","bursts","bursting","brast","bursted","bursten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"爆裂","explanation":"指物體因內部壓力太大而自行破裂，例如氣球或管道突然炸開。重點是內部力量衝破了外殼，並不一定涉及火焰或真正的爆炸。","examples":[{"en":"The balloon burst before the children could catch it.","zh":"孩子們還沒來得及抓住氣球，它就爆裂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The frozen pipe burst during the night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62fda7887ccae4d3","term":"burst","forms":["burst","bursts","bursting","brast","bursted","bursten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使爆裂","explanation":"指施加過大的內部壓力，使某物突然爆裂，是上一個義項的使動用法。","examples":[{"en":"He burst the balloon with too much air.","zh":"他充氣太多，把氣球弄爆了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pressure burst a pipe beneath the kitchen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a11e07d92e44673446c","word":"bury","forms":["bury"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0611d779423202b","term":"bury","forms":["bury","buries","burying","buried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"埋葬","explanation":"把死者按儀式放入墳墓或墓穴中並用土蓋住。這是“蓋住、藏到下面”這一核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The family buried her beside her husband.","zh":"家人把她安葬在丈夫身旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They buried their grandfather beside the old church.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73e21cac8c6d32a8","term":"bury","forms":["bury","buries","burying","buried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"埋入地下","explanation":"把物品放進地面或其他材料中並蓋住，例如把骨頭埋起來、把餘燼埋進土裡；重點是物體實際進入地下。","examples":[{"en":"The dog buried the bone under the tree.","zh":"狗把骨頭埋在樹下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They buried the time capsule beneath the oak.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ed7e3bb31434621","term":"bury","forms":["bury","buries","burying","buried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"藏住；遮住","explanation":"像用土蓋住東西一樣，把臉、手或其他事物藏起來，使它不容易被看見；也可指被某種物質覆蓋。","examples":[{"en":"She buried her face in her hands and started crying.","zh":"她把臉埋在手裡，哭了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She buried her face in the pillow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04e027e4990a203f4899","word":"bus","forms":["bus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad4ba0c2132f1e4a","term":"bus","forms":["bus","buses","busses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公共汽車","explanation":"一種沿道路行駛、一次運送許多人的大型汽車，是 bus 最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We took the bus to the city center.","zh":"我們乘公共汽車去了市中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The last bus leaves at midnight.","zh":"末班公共汽車在午夜發車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f002203b1728355e","term":"bus","forms":["bus","buses","busses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共享連線線路","explanation":"在電氣系統中，bus 是一條共同連線多個電路或部件的線路；它像一輛公共汽車，讓多個部件共享同一條“通道”。","examples":[{"en":"All the devices share the same data bus.","zh":"所有裝置共享同一條資料匯流排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The processor sends signals along the bus.","zh":"處理器沿著匯流排傳送訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-749a1a16c343bf7b315a","word":"bush","forms":["bush"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-405d04be309308da","term":"bush","forms":["bush","bushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"灌木","explanation":"一種通常較矮、從多個枝幹向外生長的木本植物，常見於庭院、田野和林地邊緣。","examples":[{"en":"A small bird was hiding in the bush by the fence.","zh":"一隻小鳥躲在籬笆旁的灌木叢裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We planted three bushes along the walkway.","zh":"我們沿著小路種了三株灌木。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e595bc5b181febb","term":"bush","forms":["bush","bushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"荒野；未開發的天然植被地帶","explanation":"由灌木、樹林等天然植被覆蓋、很少開發或耕種的偏遠土地，重點不是單獨的一株灌木，而是整片野地。","examples":[{"en":"They spent a week camping in the bush.","zh":"他們在荒野裡露營了一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lost hikers were found in thick bush.","zh":"人們在茂密的荒野植被中找到了迷路的徒步者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11d40417959631d3d242","word":"business","forms":["business"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61a622ca1c9eb448","term":"business","forms":["business","businesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"企業；商店","explanation":"指一個具體經營商品或服務的商業單位，可以是公司、店鋪或家族經營的生意。","examples":[{"en":"She runs a small business with her brother.","zh":"她和哥哥一起經營一家小企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family business has been open for forty years.","zh":"這家家族企業已經營業四十年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/business","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a89b83764c2de74","term":"business","forms":["business","businesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業；行業；工作","explanation":"指一個人的職業、所從事的行業，或以此為生的工作領域。","examples":[{"en":"My aunt has been in the restaurant business for years.","zh":"我姑媽從事餐飲業很多年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What business are you in these days?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/business","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de37699b947f02ad","term":"business","forms":["business","businesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業活動；營業","explanation":"指做生意或經營活動本身，強調一個企業是否在運轉、是否繼續營業。","examples":[{"en":"The shop stayed in business despite the difficult year.","zh":"儘管這一年很艱難，這家店還是堅持營業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Business slowed sharply after the tourist season.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/business","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4afe32db19490581","term":"business","forms":["business","businesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人的事；隱私","explanation":"指與某人本人有關、別人不應隨意干涉的事情，是“這一攤事屬於誰”的延伸用法。","examples":[{"en":"Where I spend my money is none of your business.","zh":"我怎麼花錢是我的事，與你無關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please mind your own business.","zh":"請別管閒事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/business","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c75a266d47deb2424c31","word":"businessman","forms":["businessman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c5d5039a5d21087","term":"businessman","forms":["businessman","businessmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商人；商界人士（男性）","explanation":"指以商業活動為職業，或在商業機構中工作的男性；重點是他屬於商界，不一定擁有自己的公司。","examples":[{"en":"The businessman traveled to three countries to negotiate a new contract.","zh":"這位商人前往三個國家談判一份新合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her father is a successful businessman.","zh":"她的父親是一位成功的商人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/businessman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9bc072f4fa8189466c2","word":"busy","forms":["busy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f874c7178b61ace","term":"busy","forms":["busy","busier","busiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"繁忙的；擁擠的","explanation":"指某個地方同時有很多人、車輛或活動，顯得熱鬧而擁擠；重點是“事情在這個空間裡不斷髮生”。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful when you cross this busy road.","zh":"過這條繁忙的馬路時要小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The café is always busy on Saturday mornings.","zh":"這家咖啡館星期六上午總是很熱鬧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/busy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29a7b9d11a45f69a","term":"busy","forms":["busy","busier","busiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正忙著的；沒空的","explanation":"指人的時間或注意力已經被某項工作、活動或別人佔用，所以此刻沒有空做別的事。","examples":[{"en":"I'm busy right now, but I can call you tonight.","zh":"我現在正忙，不過今晚可以給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was busy answering emails all morning.","zh":"她整個上午都在忙著回覆電子郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/busy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cdc29937887188ad3702","word":"but","forms":["but"],"officialPos":"conj./prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75abfffc717306a5","term":"but","forms":["but"],"pos":"adv","zh":"僅僅；不過","explanation":"表示數量、次數或程度很少，意思是“僅僅、不過、只”。它把範圍縮小到一個很小的限度，正好體現了“在界線之外排除其他可能，只留下這一點”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The old bell rings but twice a day.","zh":"那口舊鐘一天只響兩次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have but one request.","zh":"我只有一個請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cb378c8d8aecd72","term":"but","forms":["but"],"pos":"prep","zh":"除……之外；不包括","explanation":"表示把某人或某物排除在一個整體之外，意思是“除……以外，其餘都……”。這是“在外面、劃出界線”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone but Lina stayed for dinner.","zh":"除了莉娜，其他人都留下來吃晚飯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box contained nothing but old letters.","zh":"盒子裡除了舊信，什麼也沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/but","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01303d3beb16b992be93","word":"butcher","forms":["butcher"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebfa8fa5cff3493f","term":"butcher","forms":["butcher","butchers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"屠夫；肉商","explanation":"butcher 是處理肉類、把肉切割並出售的人，有時也親自屠宰動物。現代語境中，它既可以指傳統肉鋪裡的屠夫，也可以指賣肉的商人。","examples":[{"en":"The butcher cuts the beef fresh every morning.","zh":"屠夫每天早上都把牛肉現切出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought some sausages from the local butcher.","zh":"我從當地肉商那裡買了些香腸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butcher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1dc43fe21ec9ac47","term":"butcher","forms":["butcher","butchers","butchering","butchered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"屠宰並處理","explanation":"butcher 作動詞時，表示像屠夫一樣宰殺動物並把肉處理好，通常是為了出售或進入市場。這是名詞“屠夫”直接發展出的核心動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The workers butcher the pigs and prepare the meat for market.","zh":"工人們把豬宰殺並處理成準備上市的肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer butchered a pig for the festival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butcher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9b82b90ae572c840a76","word":"butter","forms":["butter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7dab454689b7adb","term":"butter","forms":["butter","butters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黃油；奶油","explanation":"指把牛奶中的奶油攪拌後製成的柔軟、油脂豐富的食品，通常抹在麵包上或用於烹飪。這裡的 butter 通常就是日常所說的黃油，不是泛指所有奶製品。","examples":[{"en":"I spread butter on my toast every morning.","zh":"我每天早上都在吐司上抹黃油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Melt the butter in a pan before adding the onions.","zh":"加入洋蔥前，先在鍋裡把黃油融化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad83dfca86e8a511","term":"butter","forms":["butter","butters","buttering","buttered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塗黃油","explanation":"指把黃油均勻抹在麵包、吐司等食物表面，正是“黃油被抹開”這一核心畫面的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Butter the bread while it is still warm.","zh":"麵包還熱的時候，把黃油抹上去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He buttered the toast and added some honey.","zh":"他在吐司上抹了黃油，又加了一些蜂蜜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcfd075cbe367c158d5c","word":"butterfly","forms":["butterfly"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9961e3f4ddc1ce9b","term":"butterfly","forms":["butterfly","butterflies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蝴蝶","explanation":"一種白天活動、通常色彩鮮豔的鱗翅目飛蟲；這就是butterfly最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A blue butterfly landed on the flower.","zh":"一隻藍色的蝴蝶落在花上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children watched butterflies in the garden.","zh":"孩子們在花園裡觀察蝴蝶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butterfly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3e2d78f3ff335724b40","word":"button","forms":["button"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3dd19fe7ff4796c","term":"button","forms":["button","buttons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣物紐扣","explanation":"縫在衣服上的小圓片，穿過釦眼後把衣片扣在一起；它正是“連線或啟動的小圓點”這個記憶鉤子中負責連線衣物的部分。","examples":[{"en":"One button is missing from my winter coat.","zh":"我的冬大衣少了一顆紐扣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fastened the top button of her shirt.","zh":"她扣上了襯衫最上面的紐扣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/button","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac3fc8ce3c112f77","term":"button","forms":["button","buttons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實體按鈕","explanation":"裝置上用手指按下的實體小裝置，用來接通或斷開電路，或啟動某個機械功能；它對應記憶鉤子中“按它啟動”的小圓點。","examples":[{"en":"Press the red button to stop the machine.","zh":"按下紅色按鈕來停止機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pushed the button and the doors opened.","zh":"他按下按鈕，門就開啟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/button","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26496e6be49dbd2c","term":"button","forms":["button","buttons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螢幕按鈕","explanation":"螢幕上可點選或選擇的控制元件，執行開啟頁面、提交資訊等附帶功能；它對應記憶鉤子中“點它執行功能”的小圓點。","examples":[{"en":"Click the button to save your changes.","zh":"點選這個按鈕以儲存更改。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tap the blue button to continue.","zh":"輕觸藍色按鈕繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/button","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f46ef810f1a185f","term":"button","forms":["button","buttons","buttoning","buttoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用紐扣扣好","explanation":"把衣物或其他帶紐扣的東西扣起來，就像用這個連線小圓點把兩邊固定住。","examples":[{"en":"Button your coat before you go outside.","zh":"你出門前把外套扣好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She buttoned up her shirt and left the house.","zh":"她扣好襯衫就離開了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/button","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e8197b20f8e71e429645","word":"buy","forms":["buy"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0ef6167a751d105","term":"buy","forms":["buy","buys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"買來的東西；划算的購買","explanation":"指已經買下的東西或一次購買，常暗示價格相對低、物有所值。例如，一張便宜而實用的二手桌子可以被稱為很划算的買賣。","examples":[{"en":"This used bicycle was a great buy.","zh":"這輛二手腳踏車買得很划算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These sturdy boots were an excellent buy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5be638b619d3fd5","term":"buy","forms":["buy","buys","buying","bought","boughten","buyest","boughtest","buyeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"買；購買","explanation":"用錢或等價物取得某樣東西，這是 buy 最基本、最常用的意思。畫面就是把錢遞出去，把商品拿回來；也可以說明是替誰買。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a warm coat for my sister.","zh":"我給妹妹買了一件暖和的外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought tickets at the station kiosk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fff3bcb10ca5e87b810","word":"buzz","forms":["buzz"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3287864da9978df3","term":"buzz","forms":["buzz","buzzes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嗡嗡聲；嘈雜低語聲","explanation":"指持續不斷的低沉聲音，像蜜蜂飛動時的嗡嗡聲，也可以指許多人壓低聲音交談形成的嘈雜聲。","examples":[{"en":"The buzz of bees filled the garden.","zh":"蜜蜂的嗡嗡聲充滿了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A quiet buzz rose from the crowd.","zh":"人群中響起一陣輕微的低語聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buzz","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-982dbc2d921800ef","term":"buzz","forms":["buzz","buzzes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"興奮感；輕微醉意","explanation":"指一種讓人精力充沛、興奮或受到刺激的感覺，也可以指飲用咖啡、酒精等之後產生的輕微亢奮或醉意；它仍然像“嗡嗡聲”一樣讓身體和情緒持續振動。","examples":[{"en":"I got a buzz from performing on stage.","zh":"在臺上表演讓我感到一陣興奮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strong coffee gave me a buzz.","zh":"濃咖啡讓我感到精神振奮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buzz","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20f3566f2739f0bb","term":"buzz","forms":["buzz","buzzes","buzzing","buzzed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出嗡嗡聲","explanation":"指像蜜蜂翅膀那樣發出持續、低沉或帶嘶嘶感的聲音，是 buzz 最直接的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"A fly buzzed around my head all morning.","zh":"一隻蒼蠅整個早上都在我頭邊嗡嗡飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old refrigerator is buzzing again.","zh":"那臺舊冰箱又在嗡嗡作響了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buzz","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7e2d26e8d15814dd9c6","word":"by","forms":["by"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb70348f15aa0949","term":"by","forms":["by"],"pos":"adv","zh":"經過旁邊","explanation":"表示沿著某人或某物旁邊經過，畫面是從旁邊走過去。","examples":[{"en":"I watched the parade as it passed by.","zh":"遊行從旁邊經過時，我一直看著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several ambulances hurried by without stopping.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/by","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e09477a4276a11c","term":"by","forms":["by"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在附近","explanation":"表示某人或某物就在附近，仍然保留“靠在旁邊”的空間感覺。","examples":[{"en":"There was a shepherd close by.","zh":"附近有一位牧羊人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stay close by in case I need help.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/by","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51566c59520485d4","term":"by","forms":["by"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……旁邊","explanation":"表示某人或某物靠近另一個地點或物體，核心畫面就是“在旁邊”。","examples":[{"en":"The mailbox is by the bus stop.","zh":"郵箱在公交車站旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She left her umbrella by the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/by","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d88c668e5d330bb0","term":"by","forms":["by"],"pos":"prep","zh":"經過……旁邊","explanation":"表示從某物旁邊經過並繼續向前，空間上是沿著旁邊越過去。","examples":[{"en":"The stream runs by our back door.","zh":"小溪從我們後門旁邊流過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked by the bakery on our way home.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/by","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7096588a81d5ae54","term":"by","forms":["by"],"pos":"prep","zh":"不晚於","explanation":"表示動作或事件必須在某個時間點之前完成，包含這個時間點也可以。","examples":[{"en":"Please send me the report by Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前把報告發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please return the keys by noon tomorrow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/by","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adc3dffd2ddefaa7","term":"by","forms":["by"],"pos":"prep","zh":"由……做出","explanation":"在被動結構中指出動作的施事者，即事情是透過某人的行動或存在而發生的。","examples":[{"en":"The final decision was made by the committee.","zh":"最終決定是委員會作出的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mural was painted by local teenagers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/by","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fda8ad40094febd","term":"by","forms":["by"],"pos":"prep","zh":"透過……方式","explanation":"表示藉助某種手段、線索或感官來完成事情或識別物件，意思是“靠什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"She recognized him by his voice.","zh":"她憑聲音認出了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned Spanish by listening to radio dramas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/by","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f271a122bf4230c7c217","word":"bypass","forms":["bypass"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f52d54134d93d82c","term":"bypass","forms":["bypass","bypasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繞行道路","explanation":"為了不讓車輛穿過擁堵的市中心、居民區等地方，在外圍修建的道路就是 bypass。它本質上是給交通另找一條從旁邊經過的路線。","examples":[{"en":"The new bypass has taken heavy traffic away from the town center.","zh":"新的繞行公路把繁重的交通從市中心引開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took the bypass to avoid the morning traffic.","zh":"我們走繞行公路，以避開早高峰的交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bypass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a52f682167f98a13","term":"bypass","forms":["bypass","bypasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繞行；繞開的行為","explanation":"bypass 也可以指“從旁邊過去”這一行為，而不是那條道路本身。這個抽象意義連線著道路、管道和其他所有替代通路的概念。","examples":[{"en":"The bypass of the main entrance helped reduce the crowd.","zh":"繞開主入口有助於減少人群擁擠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clever bypass of security checks alarmed investigators.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bypass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0922d2d1b4f9ba90","term":"bypass","forms":["bypass","bypasses","bypassing","bypassed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繞過障礙","explanation":"作動詞時，bypass 表示不直接穿過障礙，而是從旁邊經過，或修建、使用替代路線。物件可以是道路上的障礙，也可以是系統中的某個環節。","examples":[{"en":"The driver bypassed the flooded road by taking a mountain route.","zh":"司機走山路繞過了被洪水淹沒的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This update lets users bypass the installation problem.","zh":"這次更新讓使用者可以繞過安裝問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bypass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a7a27bedd1f822ac176","word":"cabbage","forms":["cabbage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25d056353fdbbcbe","term":"cabbage","forms":["cabbage","cabbages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捲心菜植物","explanation":"指長出緊密葉球的捲心菜或甘藍這種可食用植物；可以把它想成“長著一個葉子頭的植物”。","examples":[{"en":"We planted cabbages in the backyard this spring.","zh":"今年春天我們在後院種了捲心菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cabbages grow best in the sunniest vegetable bed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabbage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-087656de13812923","term":"cabbage","forms":["cabbage","cabbages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捲心菜葉，作為食物","explanation":"指把捲心菜的葉子當作蔬菜吃，而不是指整株植物；這裡的 cabbage 通常相當於一種食材。","examples":[{"en":"I usually add cabbage to the soup.","zh":"我通常會在湯里加捲心菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cabbage is good for you.","zh":"捲心菜對身體有好處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabbage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2764182d02bee1c55fc0","word":"cabin","forms":["cabin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d053037432d647d","term":"cabin","forms":["cabin","cabins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊疆小木屋","explanation":"指邊疆地區簡陋的小住所，常讓人聯想到用木頭和簡單工具建成、供人居住的小屋。它強調的是小而樸素的居所，不一定泛指所有鄉間房屋。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the weekend in a log cabin beside the lake.","zh":"我們週末住在湖邊的一間小木屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family built a small cabin in the woods.","zh":"這家人在樹林裡建了一間小木屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b4bf0751b4cc1b9","term":"cabin","forms":["cabin","cabins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船上私人房間","explanation":"指船上供船長、船員或乘客單獨使用的房間，尤其是可以休息或睡覺的房間。它仍然保留了“小而封閉的空間”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The captain returned to his cabin after checking the deck.","zh":"船長檢查完甲板後回到了自己的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our cabin was small but comfortable.","zh":"我們的船艙很小，但很舒適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cafe0ad5a67dafaf","term":"cabin","forms":["cabin","cabins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機客艙","explanation":"指飛機內部供乘客乘坐的區域，也就是乘客所在的封閉空間。這裡的重點是整個乘客區域，而不是某一具體座位等級。","examples":[{"en":"Please remain in the cabin until the seat-belt sign is off.","zh":"請留在客艙內，直到安全帶指示燈熄滅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cabin became quiet after takeoff.","zh":"飛機起飛後，客艙裡安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6e42a44e79e131a63d2","word":"cabinet","forms":["cabinet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-15be5ca993b1201a","term":"cabinet","forms":["cabinet","cabinets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"櫃子；壁櫃","explanation":"指獨立擺放或嵌在牆裡的儲物櫃，通常有門和內部隔層，用來收納物品。","examples":[{"en":"We keep the glasses in the cabinet above the sink.","zh":"我們把玻璃杯放在水槽上方的壁櫃裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The carpenter built a cabinet into the wall.","zh":"木匠把一個櫃子嵌進了牆裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabinet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2b553311039b159","term":"cabinet","forms":["cabinet","cabinets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顧問班子；決策小組","explanation":"由一群顧問組成、共同向政府或企業領導提供意見並參與決策的班子；它延續了“關在一個小空間裡集中商議”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor met with her cabinet before announcing the plan.","zh":"市長宣佈計劃前先和她的顧問班子開了會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The director formed a small cabinet of trusted advisers.","zh":"主任組建了一個由可靠顧問組成的小型決策班子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabinet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3af776eff131c2f1","term":"cabinet","forms":["cabinet","cabinets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內閣","explanation":"在許多議會制等政府體制中，指由各部門部長組成、負責制定政策並監督行政部門的政府核心班子。","examples":[{"en":"The Cabinet approved the new economic policy.","zh":"內閣批准了新的經濟政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several Cabinet ministers attended the emergency meeting.","zh":"幾位內閣部長出席了緊急會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabinet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d6e18d0ff4bed3b1d1f","word":"cable","forms":["cable"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6abc58a9e852f670","term":"cable","forms":["cable","cables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"纜線；粗繩狀連線物","explanation":"cable 是一條較粗、較結實的線狀物，用來把裝置、地點或其他物體連線起來；它可以是電纜、通訊纜線，也可以泛指類似繩索的連線物。","examples":[{"en":"Connect the monitor to the computer with this cable.","zh":"用這根纜線把顯示器接到電腦上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers lowered the equipment on a steel cable.","zh":"工人用鋼纜把裝置降了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81d1e6b7a70dcac0","term":"cable","forms":["cable","cables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有線電視或網路服務系統","explanation":"cable 也指透過同軸纜線或光纖網路提供電視、網際網路等服務的系統；說某人的 cable 出問題時，常常指這項服務中斷，而不是某一根實體纜線壞了。","examples":[{"en":"Our cable was out during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，我們家的有線電視和網路服務中斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel offers cable in every room.","zh":"這家酒店每個房間都提供有線電視服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e9076f075e8c05d","term":"cable","forms":["cable","cables","cabling","cabled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……裝纜線","explanation":"作動詞時，cable 表示給裝置、地點或系統安裝纜線，使它能夠連線或傳輸。這個意思直接來自名詞“纜線”作為連線工具的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The company is cabling the new office for high-speed internet.","zh":"公司正在為新辦公室鋪設高速網際網路纜線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They cabled the entire building last year.","zh":"他們去年給整棟樓鋪設了纜線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41d6f409e16df1200721","word":"cafeteria","forms":["cafeteria"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ad780a9054f2cc3","term":"cafeteria","forms":["cafeteria","cafeterias"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自助餐廳","explanation":"指顧客先在櫃檯或一排視窗挑選並領取食物，再端著托盤到桌邊吃飯的餐廳。重點不在菜式，而在這種“自己取餐、端走用餐”的方式。","examples":[{"en":"We had lunch in the cafeteria near the station.","zh":"我們在車站附近的自助餐廳吃了午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choose your meal at the counter and take it to a table in the cafeteria.","zh":"在櫃檯選好飯菜，再把它端到自助餐廳裡的桌邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cafeteria","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bee72a5d587d638e","term":"cafeteria","forms":["cafeteria","cafeterias"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構食堂；用餐區","explanation":"指學校、公司、醫院等機構裡的集中用餐場所。這裡的飯菜可以由食堂出售，也可以由機構提供，甚至由用餐者從別處帶來；核心仍是大家在同一個用餐區吃飯。","examples":[{"en":"The students usually eat together in the school cafeteria.","zh":"學生們通常一起在學校食堂吃飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nurses ate lunch together in the hospital cafeteria.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cafeteria","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9251f129e36d22db1b07","word":"caffeine","forms":["caffeine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a361a1ab168c9149","term":"caffeine","forms":["caffeine","caffeines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咖啡和茶中的提神成分","explanation":"咖啡因是一種天然存在於咖啡、茶等植物中的物質，能輕度刺激中樞神經系統，使人暫時更清醒。它指的是飲品中的成分，不是咖啡或茶本身。","examples":[{"en":"This tea contains less caffeine than coffee.","zh":"這種茶的咖啡因含量比咖啡低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I try not to consume caffeine after dinner.","zh":"我儘量不在晚飯後攝入咖啡因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caffeine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5943be120e49e99345f3","word":"cage","forms":["cage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81a2d802ecbc7c21","term":"cage","forms":["cage","cages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"籠子","explanation":"cage最基本的意思是用欄杆、金屬條等圍成的空間，通常用來關動物，有時也能暫時關人或物品。","examples":[{"en":"The parrot spends most of the day in its cage.","zh":"這隻鸚鵡一天大部分時間都待在籠子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The zookeeper cleaned the lion's cage.","zh":"動物園管理員清洗了獅子的籠子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b8e025cd01d51d7","term":"cage","forms":["cage","cages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"束縛自由的處境","explanation":"cage可以比喻限制人的制度、環境、關係或心理狀態；重點不是實際的鐵欄杆，而是人被困住、難以自由行動或選擇。","examples":[{"en":"She felt that her routine had become a cage.","zh":"她覺得自己的日常生活已經變成了一種束縛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new job gave him money but kept him in a cage.","zh":"新工作給了他錢，卻把他困在了束縛之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76ce486b3a5384db","term":"cage","forms":["cage","cages","caging","caged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"關進籠子","explanation":"cage作動詞時最直接的意思是把動物或人放進籠子並關住，動作方向是“把某物關起來”。","examples":[{"en":"The rescuers caged the injured wolf for its safety.","zh":"救援人員為了受傷狼的安全把它關進了籠子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The birds were caged overnight.","zh":"這些鳥整夜都被關在籠子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5d64cdb5ac0cfa7","term":"cage","forms":["cage","cages","caging","caged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"限制行動或創造力","explanation":"cage也可以比喻限制某人的行動、思想或創造力，使其無法自由發展；這裡是把“關進籠子”的畫面用於抽象處境。","examples":[{"en":"Too many rules can cage a child's imagination.","zh":"過多的規則會束縛孩子的想象力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refused to let fear cage her ambitions.","zh":"她不讓恐懼束縛自己的抱負。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32cdb619196200050ab0","word":"cake","forms":["cake"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebaf2430c8d50f5b","term":"cake","forms":["cake","cakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛋糕","explanation":"由麵粉、糖和雞蛋等烘烤而成的甜點，通常還會塗上糖霜或奶油。這是 cake 最常見、最應該先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered a chocolate cake for her birthday.","zh":"我們為她的生日訂了一個巧克力蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like some cake with your tea?","zh":"你想來點蛋糕配茶嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c07136a795dd93206101","word":"calcium","forms":["calcium"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b8e5d2e94c356da","term":"calcium","forms":["calcium","calciums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鈣（化學元素）","explanation":"指原子序數為20的化學元素，是一種柔軟的銀白色金屬；在自然界中常以化合物形式存在於石灰岩和其他岩石裡。","examples":[{"en":"Limestone contains a large amount of calcium.","zh":"石灰岩含有大量鈣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Calcium is an important element in many rocks.","zh":"鈣是許多岩石中的一種重要元素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calcium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-edca249d8d1f9a5b7d1a","word":"calculate","forms":["calculate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fe485bde05292e37","term":"calculate","forms":["calculate","calculates","calculating","calculated","calculatest","calculatedst","calculateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"計算出；算出","explanation":"透過數學運算確定某個數值、答案或問題的解決辦法。它是 calculate 最直接、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Can you calculate the total cost before we place the order?","zh":"下訂單前，你能算出總費用嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program calculates the distance between the two cities.","zh":"這個程式會計算兩座城市之間的距離。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calculate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb193643ac4306bd","term":"calculate","forms":["calculate","calculates","calculating","calculated","calculatest","calculatedst","calculateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"進行計算；算得出","explanation":"不特別指出計算物件，只表示進行數學計算或推算出答案，重點在“算這個過程”。","examples":[{"en":"I can calculate faster on paper than I can in my head.","zh":"我在紙上計算比在腦子裡心算快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This pocket calculator can calculate square roots.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calculate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-361900df8e883931f0ca","word":"calculation","forms":["calculation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdb19ed068455be9","term":"calculation","forms":["calculation","calculations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算過程","explanation":"指運用數字、公式或推理得出答案的過程，重點在“怎麼算”，而不是最後得到的數字。","examples":[{"en":"The calculation of the total cost took several hours.","zh":"計算總成本花了好幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Accurate calculation is essential in this experiment.","zh":"準確計算對這項實驗至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calculation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1c1d91911ed7879","term":"calculation","forms":["calculation","calculations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算結果","explanation":"指算出來的具體數字、答案或結果，也就是“算完後得到的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Please check my calculation before we send the report.","zh":"在我們發出報告前，請檢查一下我的計算結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calculation puts the total at seventy dollars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calculation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2d4a592700b0920658e","word":"calculator","forms":["calculator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77703786db4c5191","term":"calculator","forms":["calculator","calculators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算器","explanation":"指用來進行加減乘除等數學運算的機械或電子裝置，最常見的是隨身攜帶或裝在電子裝置中的小型計算器。","examples":[{"en":"I used a calculator to check the total.","zh":"我用計算器核對了總數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps a small calculator in her desk drawer.","zh":"她在書桌抽屜裡放著一個小計算器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calculator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5152790e278eb89039f8","word":"calendar","forms":["calendar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6613700858ec853d","term":"calendar","forms":["calendar","calendars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"曆法；日曆制度","explanation":"calendar 可以指把時間劃分為日、周、月、年的整套制度，例如公曆、猶太曆或伊斯蘭曆。這裡說的是組織時間的規則，不一定是一本或一張實際的日曆。","examples":[{"en":"The Gregorian calendar is used in most countries.","zh":"大多數國家使用公曆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lunar calendar bases its months on the phases of the moon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calendar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7af65504c04fdfc","term":"calendar","forms":["calendar","calendars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日曆；日曆本","explanation":"calendar 也指載有日期和時間資訊的實際物件或電子頁面，供人查日期、記錄紀念日和安排事情。它就是那張把時間格子化、讓人可以往裡寫東西的表。","examples":[{"en":"I wrote my sister's birthday on the calendar.","zh":"我把姐姐的生日寫在日曆上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Circle your appointment date on the kitchen calendar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calendar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7edb360f06acaef2cc80","word":"call","forms":["call"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cfa612ec7637002","term":"call","forms":["call","calls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"召喚；召集","explanation":"指用呼喚、要求或某種強烈吸引力把人召來，或促使人去做某事；重點仍是透過“發出聲音去聯絡”來推動行動。","examples":[{"en":"The emergency call brought volunteers to the town hall.","zh":"這次緊急召集把志願者召到了市政廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She answered the call to help her neighbors.","zh":"她響應號召去幫助鄰居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/call","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-531ee98f7c88b5be","term":"call","forms":["call","calls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電話；通話","explanation":"指透過電話進行的聯絡或一次電話通話，是把“發出聲音去聯絡某人”延伸到遠距離的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I got a call from my sister this morning.","zh":"我今天早上接到了姐姐的電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor is on a call with a patient.","zh":"醫生正在和一位病人通電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/call","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0fbf1c12ba42368","term":"call","forms":["call","calls","calling","called","call'd","callest","calledst","calleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"呼喊求助或引起注意","explanation":"用聲音向遠處或附近的人發出訊號，通常是為了求助、提醒或讓對方注意到自己。這是“發出聲音去聯絡某人或某物”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She called for help when she saw smoke coming from the kitchen.","zh":"她看到廚房冒煙時呼喊救命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I called to the children to come inside.","zh":"我向孩子們喊，讓他們進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/call","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc8b5c6f3f878afa","term":"call","forms":["call","calls","calling","called","call'd","callest","calledst","calleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"稱呼或命名","explanation":"給人或事物起名稱、規定稱呼，或告訴別人應該怎樣稱呼它。這體現了用聲音叫出名稱來確認身份。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone calls her Mia, although that is not her full name.","zh":"大家都叫她米婭，雖然那不是她的全名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can call me Sam.","zh":"你可以叫我薩姆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/call","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e262dc864e788d60b1e1","word":"calligraphy","forms":["calligraphy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8a9f090b8b2e1d5","term":"calligraphy","forms":["calligraphy","calligraphies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書法藝術","explanation":"指把字寫得具有裝飾性和藝術感的書寫藝術或實踐，重點不只是寫清楚，還包括線條、比例、結構和整體美感。","examples":[{"en":"She began studying calligraphy after visiting the museum.","zh":"她參觀博物館後開始學習書法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temple is famous for its traditional calligraphy.","zh":"這座寺廟以傳統書法聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calligraphy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60d1f90dcd0181ee","term":"calligraphy","forms":["calligraphy","calligraphies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種書法風格","explanation":"指某一種有鮮明裝飾特點的書寫風格；這裡關注的是“怎麼寫出來的樣式”，而不是書法這門藝術的總稱。","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition compares several calligraphies from different regions.","zh":"這場展覽比較了來自不同地區的幾種書法風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manuscript uses an elegant Persian calligraphy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calligraphy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b4b2eadf7b2aece598d","word":"calm","forms":["calm"],"officialPos":"v./adj./n","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f98fbb31dd95aaab","term":"calm","forms":["calm","calmer","more calm","calmest","most calm"],"pos":"adj","zh":"情緒平靜的","explanation":"指人沒有明顯的憤怒、焦慮或恐懼，心情穩定，能夠不慌張地應對事情。這是 calm 最重要的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She stayed calm when everyone else began to panic.","zh":"其他人開始慌張時，她仍然保持鎮定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A calm voice helped the child feel safe.","zh":"平靜的聲音讓孩子感到安心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-530d2b6bf2de8941","term":"calm","forms":["calm","calms","calming","calmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使平靜","explanation":"指透過言語、行動或安撫讓人、動物或局面減少激動和混亂，回到比較穩定的狀態。它就是“讓水面停止起波”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse spoke softly to calm the frightened patient.","zh":"護士輕聲說話，讓受驚的病人平靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This music usually calms me down.","zh":"這音樂通常能讓我平靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9257e627eb2e0c76","term":"calm","forms":["calm","calms","calming","calmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得平靜","explanation":"指人、動物、局面或環境自己從激動、混亂或不安中恢復平靜，不強調有人主動使它平靜。","examples":[{"en":"Give him a few minutes; he will calm down.","zh":"給他幾分鐘，他會平靜下來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd calmed after the announcement.","zh":"宣佈訊息後，人群平靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-492bd6197b168675faf0","word":"calorie","forms":["calorie"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5108b3c86592946b","term":"calorie","forms":["calorie","calories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"千卡；食品熱量單位","explanation":"在食品和健康語境中，calorie 通常指千卡，即讓一千克水升高一攝氏度所需的能量；它就是人們常說的“卡路里”。","examples":[{"en":"This snack contains 200 calories.","zh":"這種零食含有200卡路里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I burned about 500 calories during the hike.","zh":"徒步時我大約消耗了500卡路里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calorie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e1eecacd4135ac2","term":"calorie","forms":["calorie","Calories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"千卡","explanation":"這裡的 calorie 是 kilocalorie 的同義用法，指食品和營養學中使用的千卡；它和物理學裡的小卡不是同一個大小的單位。","examples":[{"en":"The label says that one serving has 150 calories.","zh":"標籤上寫著每份含有150卡路里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The snack contains two hundred calories per serving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calorie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4812585e944994cb91ca","word":"camel","forms":["camel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-888d837d75cfa814","term":"camel","forms":["camel","camels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"駱駝","explanation":"一種能在乾旱地區長途行走、常被用來馱運的哺乳動物。記住它背上的駝峰和耐旱形象，就能把其他幾個相關義項串起來。","examples":[{"en":"We rode camels across the desert at sunrise.","zh":"日出時，我們騎著駱駝穿過沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camel carried water and supplies for the travelers.","zh":"那頭駱駝為旅行者馱著水和物資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89e8b9518d92279489bb","word":"camera","forms":["camera"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-766c4ac9257b012e","term":"camera","forms":["camera","cameras","cameræ","camerae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相機；攝像機","explanation":"指透過鏡頭捕捉照片或影片的裝置，既包括照相機，也包括攝像機等拍攝裝置。","examples":[{"en":"She used her camera to record the concert.","zh":"她用相機錄下了那場音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camera takes sharp pictures even in low light.","zh":"這臺相機即使在弱光下也能拍出清晰的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camera","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df3bb7edd781990d","term":"camera","forms":["camera","cameras","cameræ","camerae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊戲視角","explanation":"在三維遊戲或模擬環境中，camera指玩家或觀察者看到世界的虛擬位置和方向，不一定是真實存在的攝像裝置。","examples":[{"en":"You can move the camera behind your character.","zh":"你可以把視角移到角色身後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rotate the camera to see behind the character.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camera","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ccefcd91405c728f09cf","word":"camp","forms":["camp"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d373fa102d038cb3","term":"camp","forms":["camp","camps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"露營地","explanation":"指用帳篷、小屋等簡易臨時住所組成的戶外居住地，也就是記憶鉤子中的“臨時搭起的據點”本身。","examples":[{"en":"We found a quiet camp beside the river before sunset.","zh":"日落前，我們在河邊找到了一處安靜的營地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We returned to camp before the storm arrived.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-922e4a239a3462d8","term":"camp","forms":["camp","camps","camping","camped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"露營","explanation":"住在帳篷或其他臨時住所裡，把臨時搭起的據點當作住處。","examples":[{"en":"We plan to camp by the lake this weekend.","zh":"我們打算這個週末在湖邊露營。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They camped in the field until Sunday.","zh":"他們在田野裡露營，一直待到星期天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0882dcf52317ee8","term":"camp","forms":["camp","camps","camping","camped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搭建營地","explanation":"把臨時住所和相關設施搭起來，建立一個可以停留的營地。","examples":[{"en":"The guides camped the group near the river before sunset.","zh":"嚮導們在日落前把這群人安置在河邊紮營。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scouts camped beside a sheltered stream.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3dc260b2472062d9c57b","word":"campaign","forms":["campaign"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43a2de78e1689195","term":"campaign","forms":["campaign","campaigns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"為目標展開的一系列行動","explanation":"指為了實現同一個目標而持續、有計劃地進行的一系列行動，重點不在某一次活動，而在整個推進過程。","examples":[{"en":"The charity launched a campaign to reduce plastic waste.","zh":"這家慈善機構發起了一項減少塑膠垃圾的行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is leading a campaign for safer streets.","zh":"她正在領導一項爭取更安全街道的行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/campaign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2787b167dd8ad9cf","term":"campaign","forms":["campaign","campaigns","campaigning","campaigned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為目標持續奔走","explanation":"指個人或組織圍繞某個目標持續採取行動、宣傳或爭取支援，就是把名詞所說的“一系列行動”變成實際進行的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Residents are campaigning for better public transport.","zh":"居民們正在為改善公共交通而奔走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The organization campaigned against the new law.","zh":"這個組織持續反對那項新法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/campaign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42c97db3df4b1373d948","word":"campus","forms":["campus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-243de2abb5ae4162","term":"campus","forms":["campus","campuses","campusses","campi"],"pos":"noun","zh":"校園；校區","explanation":"指學校、大學、公司、醫院等機構所屬的一整片場地，包括建築物、道路和其他設施；最常見的是指大學或學校校園。","examples":[{"en":"The new library is on the north side of campus.","zh":"新圖書館在校園北側。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many students live on campus during their first year.","zh":"許多學生第一年住在校內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/campus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-260d443e69071510","term":"campus","forms":["campus","campuses","campusses","campi"],"pos":"noun","zh":"校園生活；校園共同體","explanation":"這裡不只是指土地和建築，而是把校園看成由學生、教師、活動和共同氛圍組成的整體，因此可以談校園裡的社會風氣或集體事件。","examples":[{"en":"The issue has sparked a lively debate across campus.","zh":"這個問題在整個校園裡引發了熱烈討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The entire campus rallied behind the injured student.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/campus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f584196e7fe6de85d38","word":"can","forms":["can"],"officialPos":"aux./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2f002c824ef71a2","term":"can","forms":["can","cans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金屬罐或容器","explanation":"指通常用金屬製成、用來盛裝液體或其他物品的容器；這是“容器”主線最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I keep a can of fuel in the shed for emergencies.","zh":"我在棚子裡放著一罐燃料，以備緊急情況使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dented can held the leftover nails.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/can","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e893884dc3c4970","term":"can","forms":["can","able","could","couth","canst","cannest","couldst","couldest","could'st","canneth","-","canning"],"pos":"verb","zh":"能夠","explanation":"表示某人實際上有能力完成某事，即“能夠做到”，是“有能力或得到許可”這條主線的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"I can finish the report before lunch.","zh":"我能在午飯前完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can your brother swim?","zh":"你哥哥會游泳嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/can","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b2c5abec91dac8f","term":"can","forms":["can","able","could","couth","canst","cannest","couldst","couldest","could'st","canneth","-","canning"],"pos":"verb","zh":"可以；獲准","explanation":"表示某人得到許可，可以做某事；這裡的“可以”不是能力，而是“被允許”。","examples":[{"en":"You can use my laptop while I am away.","zh":"我不在的時候你可以用我的膝上型電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students can leave after the bell rings.","zh":"鈴響後學生可以離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/can","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8db73ff58173203","term":"can","forms":["can","able","could","couth","canst","cannest","couldst","couldest","could'st","canneth","-","canning"],"pos":"verb","zh":"可以……嗎；請……","explanation":"用於提出請求，詢問對方是否願意或能夠做某事，常可理解為“請你……可以嗎”。","examples":[{"en":"Can you send me the address, please?","zh":"請你把地址發給我，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you hold the door for me?","zh":"你能幫我扶一下門嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/can","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1501284e7c8472b91779","word":"canal","forms":["canal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39cb0eebcd0c76b2","term":"canal","forms":["canal","canals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人工水道","explanation":"指人工挖掘或改造的水道，用來通航、運輸、灌溉或排水。它和天然形成的河流不同，重點是人為修建或改善了水流路線。","examples":[{"en":"The old canal still carries water to the farms.","zh":"這條老運河仍然把水引到農場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Barges moved slowly through the narrow canal.","zh":"駁船緩慢地駛過狹窄的運河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2374d91794b79f4fb4ec","word":"cancel","forms":["cancel"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84d830906f4f65ec","term":"cancel","forms":["cancel","cancels","canceling","cancelling","canceled","cancelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"劃掉","explanation":"指用線或其他標記把文字、符號或內容劃掉，使它看起來不再有效或不應保留。其他許多意思都可以看作從這個“劃掉”動作發展而來。","examples":[{"en":"Please cancel the last item on the list.","zh":"請把清單上的最後一項劃掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cancel the incorrect figure with a single line.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cancel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7019d4f8f7f55189","term":"cancel","forms":["cancel","cancels","canceling","cancelling","canceled","cancelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取消；使作廢","explanation":"指讓原定的活動、訂單、預約、合同或計劃不再進行或不再有效。這是現代英語中最常見、最需要優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We had to cancel the picnic because of the rain.","zh":"因為下雨，我們不得不取消野餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I cancelled my hotel reservation yesterday.","zh":"我昨天取消了酒店預訂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cancel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5600ae99b14ef8e5eb75","word":"cancer","forms":["cancer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-059c7ce6b729b8c2","term":"cancer","forms":["cancer","cancers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"癌症","explanation":"指人體或其他組織中的細胞失去正常控制而不斷增殖形成的疾病；詞源中的“螃蟹”形象來自腫瘤周圍擴張的血管像螃蟹的腳。","examples":[{"en":"She was diagnosed with breast cancer last year.","zh":"她去年被診斷出患有乳腺癌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers are testing a new treatment for lung cancer.","zh":"研究人員正在測試一種治療肺癌的新方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cancer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dda18a0e21ae47c53b43","word":"candidate","forms":["candidate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abed0488f20e1a4b","term":"candidate","forms":["candidate","candidates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"競選或申請職位的人","explanation":"指主動爭取透過選舉或任命獲得某個職位、資格或機會的人，最常見於競選和職位申請語境。","examples":[{"en":"She is the youngest candidate for mayor in the city's history.","zh":"她是這座城市歷史上最年輕的市長候選人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Voters will choose between three candidates in November.","zh":"選民將在十一月從三名候選人中作出選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candidate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc71151d99d77f37","term":"candidate","forms":["candidate","candidates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被認為有希望的人","explanation":"泛指被認為很可能獲得某個職位、榮譽或機會，或被認為有資格獲得它的人；不一定涉及正式選舉。","examples":[{"en":"After her successful interview, Maya became a strong candidate for the job.","zh":"面試成功後，瑪雅成了這份工作的有力人選。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young striker is a strong candidate for captain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candidate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6fa599fe7b02fec029e9","word":"candle","forms":["candle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2043f0095356fea","term":"candle","forms":["candle","candles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蠟燭","explanation":"一種用蠟、動物脂或石蠟等固體可燃材料製成、裡面有燈芯的照明物。它是這個詞在日常英語中最主要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She lit a candle when the power went out.","zh":"停電時，她點燃了一支蠟燭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please blow out the candles before you cut the cake.","zh":"切蛋糕前，請把蠟燭吹滅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df39220189ca8225b3ef","word":"cane","forms":["cane"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4992c010606d0eb","term":"cane","forms":["cane","canes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物的莖","explanation":"指竹子、甘蔗等具有簡單直立莖的植物，或泛指這類植物的莖，是“cane”最基礎的植物義。","examples":[{"en":"The basket is made from cane.","zh":"這個籃子是用藤莖編成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers cut the cane by hand.","zh":"工人們用手收割甘蔗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98a580943c5e5e07","term":"cane","forms":["cane","canes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手杖","explanation":"指幫助人行走或保持平衡的手杖，是現代普通語境中最常見的具體器具義之一。","examples":[{"en":"After the operation, she walked with a cane.","zh":"手術後，她拄著手杖走路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left his cane by the door.","zh":"他把手杖放在門邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e23af357a9fc7e41b80","word":"canoe","forms":["canoe"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7568adc7049613ff","term":"canoe","forms":["canoe","canoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨木舟；划艇","explanation":"一種敞口、細長、兩頭尖的小船，乘坐者通常坐著或跪著，用單槳向前劃。現代 canoe 不一定真的由整段樹幹挖成，但核心形象仍是這種輕便的划船。","examples":[{"en":"We rented a canoe and paddled along the quiet river.","zh":"我們租了一條獨木舟，沿著安靜的河流划行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They paddled their canoe through the quiet reeds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canoe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0a6bf44c081f476","term":"canoe","forms":["canoe","canoes","canoeing","canoed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"劃獨木舟；乘獨木舟","explanation":"指乘坐或划著 canoe 在水上前進：名詞義中的那條船變成了一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"They canoed across the lake before sunset.","zh":"他們在日落前劃獨木舟穿過了湖面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They canoed along the river at dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canoe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a457e8f04aa796dc5077","word":"canvas","forms":["canvas"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d93a3707fd98f05d","term":"canvas","forms":["canvas","canvases","canvasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帆布","explanation":"一種結實、粗糙的厚布，傳統上常用於做帆、帳篷和各種覆蓋物，也可泛指這種布料本身。","examples":[{"en":"The old backpack is made of thick canvas.","zh":"這個舊揹包是用厚帆布做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tents were made from heavy waterproof canvas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canvas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04cd430f18619092","term":"canvas","forms":["canvas","canvases","canvasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"畫布","explanation":"繃在畫框上的帆布或類似布面，畫家在上面繪畫；它是canvas最常見的藝術語境義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"She is painting a landscape on a large canvas.","zh":"她正在一塊大畫布上畫風景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stretched fresh canvas over the wooden frame.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canvas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ccd5bb525550bf6","term":"canvas","forms":["canvas","canvases","canvasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創作基礎","explanation":"比喻可以在其上展開創作或表達的基礎；它把實際的畫布擴大成了承載思想、故事或風格的“面”。","examples":[{"en":"The city became a canvas for young artists.","zh":"這座城市成了年輕藝術家的創作舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plain ceramic plate offers children a canvas for their designs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canvas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff2a8a3987ef4645f85d","word":"canyon","forms":["canyon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d77c9aa274cad0d5","term":"canyon","forms":["canyon","canyons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"峽谷","explanation":"指河流在岩石中長期向下切割形成的長而窄、兩側陡峭的谷地。記住“河水把岩石刻成深溝”的畫面，就能把它和較寬緩的一般山谷區分開。","examples":[{"en":"We hiked through the canyon before sunset.","zh":"我們在日落前徒步穿過了峽谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river runs through a narrow canyon.","zh":"這條河流經一條狹窄的峽谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canyon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45e84635bc4803c5cc5d","word":"cap","forms":["cap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70096fe679bfa723","term":"cap","forms":["cap","caps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"便帽；鴨舌帽","explanation":"指貼著頭戴的帽子，通常沒有很寬的帽簷，常用於遮陽或保暖。它正是“蓋在最上面的一層”這一記憶中的帽子。","examples":[{"en":"The children wore caps to keep the sun out of their eyes.","zh":"孩子們戴著帽子，防止陽光照進眼睛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He put on a baseball cap before going outside.","zh":"他出門前戴上了一頂棒球帽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b45dba9c7ec47a44","term":"cap","forms":["cap","caps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上限；限額","explanation":"指人為規定的不能超過的最高數值或數量，就是給某件事“蓋住”的上限。","examples":[{"en":"The city put a cap on rent increases.","zh":"這座城市對租金漲幅設定了上限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a cap of twenty students in each class.","zh":"每個班最多只能有二十名學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae62cce493d482fe","term":"cap","forms":["cap","caps","capping","capped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蓋住；封住","explanation":"把cap理解為在東西最上面蓋上一層，就是用蓋子或類似物把某物蓋住、封住。","examples":[{"en":"Cap the bottle tightly before you put it in the bag.","zh":"把瓶子蓋緊後再放進袋子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers capped the pipe to stop the leak.","zh":"工人給管子封上了蓋，以阻止漏水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c13275e0e722d1aa","term":"cap","forms":["cap","caps","capping","capped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設定上限；達到上限","explanation":"這裡的cap仍然是“蓋住最上面”，但蓋住的是一個不能再往上的數值，因此表示給工資、費用或數量設定最高限額，也可表示達到這個上限。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy caps rent increases at three percent a year.","zh":"新政策把房租年漲幅限制在百分之三以內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company capped wages for senior managers.","zh":"公司給高階管理人員的工資設定了上限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38a5be91af79d7e5ba98","word":"capability","forms":["capability"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56e4419545c2e9da","term":"capability","forms":["capability","capabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"能力；功能；潛力","explanation":"指某個人、組織、裝置或系統完成某件事、產生某種結果的能力或功能，也可以指尚未充分發揮的潛力。這個詞關注“有沒有條件做到”，而不表示事情已經做成。","examples":[{"en":"The new camera has the capability to record clear video at night.","zh":"這臺新相機具備夜間錄製清晰影片的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is developing its capability to respond quickly to emergencies.","zh":"這個團隊正在提升快速應對緊急情況的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80415b2524ae7dd4e36e","word":"capable","forms":["capable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd649b563b411f74","term":"capable","forms":["capable","more capable","most capable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有能力的；能勝任的","explanation":"指某人具備完成特定任務所需的能力，做事通常也比較可靠、高效；也可表示某人有做某事的能力或傾向。","examples":[{"en":"She is capable of handling the project on her own.","zh":"她有能力獨自處理這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is a capable manager who keeps the team organized.","zh":"他是一位能幹的經理，能讓團隊保持井然有序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec21b3b973a3a0e70503","word":"capacity","forms":["capacity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a923b3159a255b3","term":"capacity","forms":["capacity","capacities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"容納能力","explanation":"指容器、空間或人的身體能夠接收、裝下或吸收多少，是“容器能容納什麼範圍”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The tank has enough capacity to store a week's worth of water.","zh":"這個水箱的容量足以儲存一週用的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater's capacity to absorb sound was surprisingly good.","zh":"這座劇院吸收聲音的能力出人意料地好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capacity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b92e4984ef9a49e1","term":"capacity","forms":["capacity","capacities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完成事情的能力","explanation":"指人、組織或裝置完成某項任務的能力，也就是這個“容器”能夠承擔多少事情、發揮多大作用。","examples":[{"en":"She has the capacity to lead a much larger team.","zh":"她有能力領導規模大得多的團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new system has greater capacity for handling urgent requests.","zh":"新系統處理緊急請求的能力更強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capacity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-043765ab32b1bc93","term":"capacity","forms":["capacity","capacities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學習能力；智力","explanation":"指人的理解、思考和學習能力，是“頭腦這個容器能接收和處理多少”的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"The child has a remarkable capacity for learning languages.","zh":"這個孩子有很強的語言學習能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exercises test a child's capacity to reason.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capacity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ed2fa2539de546945af","word":"cape","forms":["cape"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-875048e01544f10e","term":"cape","forms":["cape","capes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"岬角；海角","explanation":"cape 是伸入海洋或湖泊的陸地尖端，好像海岸向水中伸出的一隻角。","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse stands on a rocky cape.","zh":"燈塔坐落在一處多岩石的岬角上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ship rounded the cape before sunset.","zh":"船在日落前繞過了海角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03c4faf76e329a2b","term":"cape","forms":["cape","capes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斗篷","explanation":"cape 是從脖子或肩部垂下、覆蓋背部和肩膀的無袖衣物，像一片布披在身上。","examples":[{"en":"The actor wore a long black cape for the performance.","zh":"那名演員為了演出穿了一件黑色長斗篷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrapped the cape around her shoulders.","zh":"她把斗篷裹在肩膀上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd08022e8fb80701512c","word":"capital","forms":["capital"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d45bf32a525e5661","term":"capital","forms":["capital","capitals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資本；資金","explanation":"指用來購買商品、服務或開展經營活動的錢和財富，尤其是創業或投資所需要的資金。可以把它想成掌握在手中、能換取更多資源的“經濟力量”。","examples":[{"en":"She raised enough capital to open a small bakery.","zh":"她籌集了足夠的資金，開了一家小麵包店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is looking for new capital to expand overseas.","zh":"這家公司正在尋找新的資本，以便向海外擴張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17ced364762a1b1b","term":"capital","forms":["capital","capitals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"首都","explanation":"指一個國家、州或其他行政區域中政府所在地，通常也是政治上最重要的城市。它就是“頭部城市”：在整個地區中處於核心位置。","examples":[{"en":"The capital of Canada is Ottawa.","zh":"加拿大的首都是渥太華。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thousands of people marched through the capital.","zh":"成千上萬的人走過首都街頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c202849a64c0e52","term":"capital","forms":["capital","capitals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大寫字母","explanation":"指採用大寫形式的一個字母。它對應形容詞義“大的、首要的書寫形式”，就像字母在頁面上被突出出來。","examples":[{"en":"The first word of the sentence begins with a capital.","zh":"這個句子的第一個詞以大寫字母開頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Begin each proper name with a capital.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b63d4bbac9f7ae6842fb","word":"capital(ism)","forms":["capital","capitalism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f234c81f18159f74","term":"capital","forms":["capital","capitals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資本；資金","explanation":"指用來購買商品、服務或開展經營活動的錢和財富，尤其是創業或投資所需要的資金。可以把它想成掌握在手中、能換取更多資源的“經濟力量”。","examples":[{"en":"She raised enough capital to open a small bakery.","zh":"她籌集了足夠的資金，開了一家小麵包店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is looking for new capital to expand overseas.","zh":"這家公司正在尋找新的資本，以便向海外擴張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-726733419d0b10fb","term":"capital","forms":["capital","capitals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"首都","explanation":"指一個國家、州或其他行政區域中政府所在地，通常也是政治上最重要的城市。它就是“頭部城市”：在整個地區中處於核心位置。","examples":[{"en":"The capital of Canada is Ottawa.","zh":"加拿大的首都是渥太華。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thousands of people marched through the capital.","zh":"成千上萬的人走過首都街頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7d1d9c9e440d689","term":"capital","forms":["capital","capitals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大寫字母","explanation":"指採用大寫形式的一個字母。它對應形容詞義“大的、首要的書寫形式”，就像字母在頁面上被突出出來。","examples":[{"en":"The first word of the sentence begins with a capital.","zh":"這個句子的第一個詞以大寫字母開頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write your surname in capitals on the form.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8c9cb49cd4a56dd","term":"capitalism","forms":["capitalism","capitalisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"私人資本主導的社會經濟制度","explanation":"指一種社會經濟制度：重要資源或資本主要由私人擁有，經濟活動圍繞私人經營、交換和獲利展開。這個意義著重說明整個社會如何組織生產和分配，不一定強調市場是否完全不受國家干預。","examples":[{"en":"Under capitalism, businesses usually compete to attract customers and earn profits.","zh":"在資本主義制度下，企業通常透過競爭吸引顧客並賺取利潤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book examines how capitalism has changed family life.","zh":"這本書研究了資本主義如何改變家庭生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capitalism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76f8a4c1a9fdb1be","term":"capitalism","forms":["capitalism","capitalisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"私人擁有生產資料並以利潤為目標的經濟制度","explanation":"這是對資本主義核心經濟結構的更具體說明：土地、工廠、礦山等生產資料由私人擁有，並主要為了利潤而運營。相比s1，這個意義更突出“私人所有”和“以利潤為目的的生產”。","examples":[{"en":"Critics argue that capitalism puts profit before workers' needs.","zh":"批評者認為，資本主義把利潤置於工人需求之上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Industrial capitalism transformed the way goods were produced.","zh":"工業資本主義改變了商品的生產方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capitalism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbd764dc67947219b4e1","word":"capitalist","forms":["capitalist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d300b11e91a12c11","term":"capitalist","forms":["capitalist","capitalists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資本家；擁有大量資本的人","explanation":"指擁有相當多資本、財富或資產的人，傳統上尤其指能把這些資本用於土地、企業等投資的人。","examples":[{"en":"The capitalist bought several factories and invested in new technology.","zh":"這位資本家買下了幾家工廠，並投資於新技術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wealthy capitalist financed the new steelworks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capitalist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-881df12b68cd344e83f6","word":"capsule","forms":["capsule"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d44c42397a2325d","term":"capsule","forms":["capsule","capsules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"包膜；囊狀外殼","explanation":"指包住某種內容物的薄膜或囊狀外殼，是“用殼把東西包起來”這一核心概念的基礎義項。","examples":[{"en":"The virus is protected by a thin protein capsule.","zh":"這種病毒受到一層薄薄的蛋白質包膜保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The capsule surrounding the implant became inflamed.","zh":"包圍植入物的包膜發炎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capsule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a76fff47ddabaa03","term":"capsule","forms":["capsule","capsules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥物膠囊","explanation":"指裝有一劑藥物的小容器，通常由可吞服的外殼包住藥粉或藥液，是日常最常見的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"Take one capsule with water after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後用水服一粒膠囊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This medicine is available in capsule form.","zh":"這種藥有膠囊劑型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capsule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f64b2650cf4040bc","term":"capsule","forms":["capsule","capsules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簡明壓縮版","explanation":"作定語時表示把較大的內容壓縮排一個“小殼”裡的版本，如簡短的歷史概述或資訊摘要。","examples":[{"en":"She gave us a capsule summary of the report.","zh":"她給我們作了這份報告的簡明摘要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The opening paragraph offers a capsule of his argument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capsule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2780b8eef998d6eaca5d","word":"captain","forms":["captain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92060eeee895d738","term":"captain","forms":["captain","captains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"首領；負責人","explanation":"泛指站在隊伍最前面、負責指揮和作決定的人，是 captain“帶頭者”這一核心概念的最寬泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"She became captain of the rescue team after years of experience.","zh":"她積累多年經驗後，成為了救援隊的負責人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain led his people through the difficult journey.","zh":"這位首領帶領他的人走過了艱難的旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-794298a018cd658c","term":"captain","forms":["captain","captains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船長","explanation":"指依法負責船隻及船上人員的船長；“在船上帶頭並承擔最終責任”是首領概念的具體化。","examples":[{"en":"The captain ordered everyone to stay below deck during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，船長命令所有人留在甲板下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We thanked the captain when the ferry reached the harbor safely.","zh":"渡船安全抵達港口後，我們向船長道了謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9c75183b555a092","term":"captain","forms":["captain","captains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球隊隊長","explanation":"指被指定代表球隊與裁判溝通、參與決定並帶領隊友的運動員；這是“帶頭並負責發言”的日常化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The team captain spoke to the referee after the final whistle.","zh":"終場哨響後，球隊隊長與裁判進行了交涉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our captain encouraged us when we were two goals behind.","zh":"我們落後兩球時，隊長鼓勵了大家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-176ca52906b001daa816","word":"caption","forms":["caption"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d1626d90c18389a","term":"caption","forms":["caption","captions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標題或欄題","explanation":"它可以是檔案、文章某一部分或表格上方的標題，幫助讀者知道下面內容屬於什麼主題。它體現了“貼在內容上作提示”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The caption at the top of the form tells you which section to complete.","zh":"表格頂部的標題告訴你該填寫哪一欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The photograph appeared beneath the caption 'Winter Market.'","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41ed16821e788274","term":"caption","forms":["caption","captions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圖片說明","explanation":"它是附在照片、插圖、漫畫或介面元素旁邊的簡短文字，用來說明畫面內容、背景或用途。可以把它記成“給圖片貼的說明標籤”。","examples":[{"en":"Please add a short caption under each photograph.","zh":"請在每張照片下面加一段簡短的圖片說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The caption explains where the painting was found.","zh":"圖片說明解釋了這幅畫是在什麼地方發現的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-234d5f0e7d42a37b","term":"caption","forms":["caption","captions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影視字幕","explanation":"在電影、電視節目或現場轉寫中，它是顯示在螢幕上的文字，用來呈現對白，有時也說明聲音或音效，方便聽不見或聽不清的人觀看。","examples":[{"en":"We turned on the captions because the actors were speaking softly.","zh":"因為演員說話聲音很輕，我們開啟了字幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Turn on captions if the dialogue is unclear.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f97829bf44614288","term":"caption","forms":["caption","captions","captioning","captioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給文字或圖片加說明","explanation":"它表示給文章、插圖或其他內容配上標題或說明文字，也就是把“貼在內容上的說明”這個動作做出來。","examples":[{"en":"She captioned the drawing with a quote from the story.","zh":"她給這幅畫配上了一句故事中的引文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please caption each photograph with its location and date.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3a64834115b092efd42","word":"captive","forms":["captive"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf644df5198a7fce","term":"captive","forms":["captive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"被俘的；被囚禁的","explanation":"指一個人被抓住、關押，因而不能自由行動；也可泛指處於受限制狀態的人。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers were held captive for two days before they were rescued.","zh":"這些徒步旅行者被扣押了兩天才獲救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captive soldiers were finally released.","zh":"那些被俘士兵最終獲釋了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23b9415dbebb3c9b","term":"captive","forms":["captive","captives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"俘虜；被囚禁者","explanation":"指已經被抓住、關押或限制自由的人，是“被牢牢抓住”這一核心概念的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The rebels took three aid workers captive.","zh":"叛亂分子俘獲了三名援助人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captive was given food and water.","zh":"那名俘虜得到了食物和水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4aa07dda9de888fac3e4","word":"captivity","forms":["captivity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96e094850dd0cdbe","term":"captivity","forms":["captivity","captivities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被俘狀態","explanation":"指人或動物被他人控制、關押，因而不能自由行動的狀態；重點是“失去自由”，不一定只限於監獄。","examples":[{"en":"The rescued wolf spent several months in captivity.","zh":"這隻獲救的狼在被關養的狀態下度過了幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldier was held in captivity for two years.","zh":"那名士兵被俘關押了兩年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captivity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12e3a94fdad50456","term":"captivity","forms":["captivity","captivities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"囚禁時期","explanation":"強調一個人被監禁、限制行動或奴役的持續時期，也就是在那隻“看不見的籠子”裡度過的一段人生。","examples":[{"en":"She wrote poems during her long captivity.","zh":"她在漫長的囚禁歲月中寫下了詩歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He learned the language during his years of captivity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captivity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"114":2}}},{"id":"ceec-460ee6aa3a80359181b7","word":"capture","forms":["capture"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46d283d980d872af","term":"capture","forms":["capture","captures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抓獲；捕獲","explanation":"指用力量、計策或行動把人、船隻等抓住並控制住，也可以指這樣的抓獲行為。","examples":[{"en":"The capture of the escaped criminal ended the search.","zh":"逃犯被抓獲後，這場搜捕結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The navy reported the capture of an enemy vessel.","zh":"海軍報告說捕獲了一艘敵方船隻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3f4322a42f97656","term":"capture","forms":["capture","captures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"贏得；吸引住","explanation":"指某種吸引力把人牢牢“抓住”，使其產生興趣、愛意或強烈關注。","examples":[{"en":"The singer's voice was the capture of everyone's attention.","zh":"這位歌手的嗓音吸引了所有人的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team's capture of public attention surprised advertisers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5f81dda81019a1e","term":"capture","forms":["capture","captures","capturing","captured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓獲；奪取","explanation":"指用力量或計策抓住並控制敵人、船隻、罪犯等目標。","examples":[{"en":"The police captured the suspect near the station.","zh":"警方在車站附近抓獲了嫌疑人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team captured the flag before sunset.","zh":"這支隊伍在日落前奪取了旗幟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8732f4bca4fb2873","term":"capture","forms":["capture","captures","capturing","captured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸引住；打動","explanation":"指某人或某物牢牢抓住別人的注意力、想象力、興趣或感情。","examples":[{"en":"The painting captured my imagination immediately.","zh":"這幅畫立刻激發了我的想象力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her story captured the audience's attention.","zh":"她的故事吸引了觀眾的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b2961a431b23c9007ef","word":"car","forms":["car"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56570b3c5854055c","term":"car","forms":["car","cars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽車","explanation":"car最常指由發動機或其他機械動力驅動、供個人乘坐的汽車。記住“能自己移動、載人出行的車”，就能掌握這個核心義。","examples":[{"en":"I left my car in the parking lot.","zh":"我把車停在停車場了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She drives to work by car every day.","zh":"她每天開車去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/car","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3eb46f4c7dd56c4","term":"car","forms":["car","cars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軌道車廂","explanation":"在北美英語中，car也可指沿鐵路執行的一個車廂，尤其是被機車牽引的車廂。它仍然符合“沿軌道移動、負責載人或載物的車體”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The workers attached another car to the train.","zh":"工人又給火車接上了一節車廂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Passengers moved into the next car to find seats.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/car","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28d79d50ff515a797803","word":"carbon","forms":["carbon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-821140c5bb5f64a4","term":"carbon","forms":["carbon","carbons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碳元素","explanation":"carbon是化學元素“碳”，元素符號為C。它既存在於石墨、鑽石等純物質中，也構成許多生物分子，是“碳”這一核心概念的根本意思。","examples":[{"en":"Carbon is an essential element in all known forms of life.","zh":"碳是所有已知生命形式都不可缺少的元素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This pencil contains a mixture of graphite and clay, not pure carbon.","zh":"這支鉛筆含有石墨和黏土的混合物，而不是純碳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carbon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e19754893f2b188","term":"carbon","forms":["carbon","carbons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碳原子","explanation":"在化學結構或分子組成的語境中，carbon可以指一個碳原子，而不是泛指這種元素。","examples":[{"en":"The molecule contains one carbon bonded to three hydrogen atoms.","zh":"這個分子含有一個與三個氫原子相連的碳原子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each methane molecule contains one carbon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carbon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8367cd66fdd136bba8ba","word":"card","forms":["card"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f52d16d0eccd9b5","term":"card","forms":["card","cards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紙牌","explanation":"指紙牌遊戲中單獨的一張牌；它是一張可拿在手裡、帶有點數或圖案的資訊卡片。","examples":[{"en":"She drew a card from the deck and smiled.","zh":"她從一副牌中抽出一張牌，笑了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I put my last card on the table.","zh":"我把最後一張牌放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/card","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93097f2e758b3abe","term":"card","forms":["card","cards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"卡片；硬片","explanation":"指用紙、塑膠等製成的扁平、通常為長方形的物件，可以攜帶或承載資訊，如銀行卡、會員卡或識別卡。","examples":[{"en":"Please show your card at the entrance.","zh":"請在入口處出示你的卡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I keep the card in my wallet.","zh":"我把這張卡放在錢包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/card","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-671915e49543fcbb","term":"card","forms":["card","cards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名片","explanation":"指印有姓名、職位、聯絡方式等資訊的商務卡片，方便別人聯絡持卡人。它是一張把個人工作資訊隨身攜帶的卡。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me her business card after the meeting.","zh":"會後她給了我一張名片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I handed him my card so he could contact me.","zh":"我把名片遞給他，好讓他聯絡我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/card","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2fb41c42cec5d64aee37","word":"cardboard","forms":["cardboard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f84215f99501237","term":"cardboard","forms":["cardboard","cardboards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"硬紙板","explanation":"一種比普通紙厚而硬的紙質材料，常被裁切、摺疊或印刷，用來製作盒子、紙箱和標牌。","examples":[{"en":"She cut a piece of cardboard to cover the broken window.","zh":"她剪了一塊硬紙板來擋住破窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store recycles cardboard from its delivery boxes.","zh":"這家商店回收送貨箱用的硬紙板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardboard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a09783b1c474294d122","word":"cardinal","forms":["cardinal"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a055ed853b3d3c0","term":"cardinal","forms":["cardinal","more cardinal","most cardinal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"關鍵的；根本的","explanation":"指對事情起決定作用、不可忽視的，像所有變化都圍繞它轉的鉸鏈一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Keeping client information private is a cardinal rule of our profession.","zh":"為客戶資訊保密是我們這個行業的一條基本原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trust is cardinal to a successful partnership.","zh":"信任是成功合作關係的根本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardinal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92617d295bd5e3d1","term":"cardinal","forms":["cardinal","more cardinal","most cardinal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基數的","explanation":"指表示數量的數，如零、一、二、三，而不是表示順序的“第一、第二”等序數。","examples":[{"en":"In the phrase “three books,” three is a cardinal number.","zh":"在“三本書”這個短語中，three 是基數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One, two, and three are cardinal numbers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardinal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19f8026d2ee07a32","term":"cardinal","forms":["cardinal","cardinals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鮮紅色","explanation":"指一種比猩紅色略柔和的深鮮紅色，來源仍與樞機主教的紅色服飾有關。","examples":[{"en":"The curtains were a rich cardinal that warmed the room.","zh":"窗簾是濃郁的鮮紅色，讓房間顯得更溫暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A streak of cardinal brightened the otherwise gray painting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardinal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9ed2b54fd72ac165257","word":"care","forms":["care"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40cd9d5a7005c5f8","term":"care","forms":["care","cares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關心；注意；責任","explanation":"表示把注意力和責任放在某人或某事上，認真對待它並小心處理。","examples":[{"en":"Care should be taken when holding babies.","zh":"抱嬰兒時要小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She handled the old vase with great care.","zh":"她非常小心地拿著那個舊花瓶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/care","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe33a2d8751bff89","term":"care","forms":["care","cares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"護理；照護服務","explanation":"表示為有需要的人提供持續的幫助、保護和治療，尤其指醫療或社會照護工作。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital provides excellent patient care.","zh":"這家醫院提供很好的患者護理服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospice provides round-the-clock care for its patients.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/care","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af364c66f9f6f0f5","term":"care","forms":["care","cares","caring","cared","carest","caredst","careth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在意；關心","explanation":"表示把心思放在某人或某事上，關心它的結果或看法。","examples":[{"en":"She doesn't care what you think.","zh":"她不在意你怎麼想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I care deeply about my family.","zh":"我非常關心我的家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/care","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1231cbee965bed32","term":"care","forms":["care","cares","caring","cared","carest","caredst","careth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"照顧；照料","explanation":"表示把注意力和責任落實到行動上，負責保護、餵養或幫助某人或某物。","examples":[{"en":"Young children can learn to care for a pet.","zh":"小孩子可以學著照顧寵物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stayed home to care for her sick father.","zh":"她留在家裡照顧生病的父親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/care","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89b7505ad79ad4892d6f","word":"career","forms":["career"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7eba736c3e34533c","term":"career","forms":["career","careers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業；一生的事業","explanation":"指一個人長期認真從事的職業或事業，是他反覆走在其中的一條工作道路，不只是某一份短期工作。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a career in medicine after volunteering at a hospital.","zh":"她在醫院做志願者後，選擇了從事醫學事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is considering a career as a teacher.","zh":"他正在考慮把教師作為自己的職業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/career","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ea5d8ca5c27ab83","term":"career","forms":["career","careers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業生涯；事業發展歷程","explanation":"指一個人在某一職業領域中經歷的整個發展過程，包括開始、變化、成就和持續推進，強調這條職業道路怎樣展開。","examples":[{"en":"Her career as a designer took her to several countries.","zh":"她的設計師生涯讓她去過好幾個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The award marked an important moment in his career.","zh":"這項獎標誌著他職業生涯中的一個重要時刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/career","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-7a3657478ae038cdf02a","word":"carefree","forms":["carefree"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64c823e627d58fd5","term":"carefree","forms":["carefree","more carefree","most carefree"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無憂無慮的；輕鬆自在的","explanation":"指沒有煩惱、擔憂或需要操心的事，因而感到輕鬆自在；可以形容人，也可以形容一段時光、生活或經歷。它的重點是“心裡沒有負擔”，不是“做事不小心”。","examples":[{"en":"He left his cell phone behind and enjoyed a carefree summer day at the beach.","zh":"他把手機落在了身後，在海灘上享受了無憂無慮的夏日時光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As children, we spent carefree afternoons playing in the park.","zh":"小時候，我們常常在公園裡無憂無慮地玩一下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carefree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-191c415261817259c49f","word":"careful","forms":["careful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fbfc5f1679e22b46","term":"careful","forms":["careful","more careful","most careful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"小心謹慎的","explanation":"表示做事前把可能的危險、錯誤或傷害放在心上，因此行動謹慎、避免出問題。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful when you cross the road.","zh":"過馬路時要小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is always careful with her personal information.","zh":"她總是很謹慎地保護自己的個人資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/careful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc97bc3cd1d4bedb","term":"careful","forms":["careful","more careful","most careful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"認真細緻的","explanation":"表示做事把細節放在心上，過程周密、下足功夫，強調準確和全面，而不只是避免危險。","examples":[{"en":"After a careful review, we corrected three errors in the report.","zh":"經過仔細審查，我們改正了報告中的三處錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Careful measurements prevented an expensive fitting error.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/careful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c10a04e2cc8dbf3067d","word":"caretaker","forms":["caretaker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-074c6fde912a268d","term":"caretaker","forms":["caretaker","caretakers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看護人；管理員","explanation":"指負責照看某個地方或物品、做日常維護並確保其正常狀況的人，例如負責墓地、學校或建築物的人；核心仍是“接過照看責任”。","examples":[{"en":"The school caretaker checks the heating every morning.","zh":"學校管理員每天早晨檢查供暖裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Report the broken classroom lock to the building caretaker.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caretaker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3322532d8589f95c912a","word":"cargo","forms":["cargo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59b3a7fffa1e583e","term":"cargo","forms":["cargo","cargos","cargoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運輸中的貨物","explanation":"cargo 指裝在船、飛機或機動車上、準備運輸或正在運輸的貨物，重點是它作為運輸載荷被運送。它可以是許多物品的總稱，也可以指一批具體貨物。","examples":[{"en":"The ship is carrying cargo to the island.","zh":"這艘船正把貨物運往那座島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plane was loaded with cargo before dawn.","zh":"飛機在黎明前裝滿了貨物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cargo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67627795bbc4b6146494","word":"carnival","forms":["carnival"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5392bc62f342d4b5","term":"carnival","forms":["carnival","carnivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狂歡節","explanation":"指四旬齋前舉行的節慶活動，通常包括遊行、音樂、舞蹈、特別食物和各種娛樂。","examples":[{"en":"The streets were packed with dancers during the city carnival.","zh":"城市狂歡節期間，街道上擠滿了舞者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought sweet pastries at the carnival.","zh":"我們在狂歡節上買了甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carnival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5df301605832394","term":"carnival","forms":["carnival","carnivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱鬧的慶典","explanation":"泛指充滿遊行、表演、食物和娛樂的歡樂場合，不一定與宗教節期有關。","examples":[{"en":"The school held a carnival with games, music, and food stalls.","zh":"學校舉辦了一場有遊戲、音樂和食品攤位的慶典。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The square became a carnival of music and dancing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carnival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb613b14eef090eef0e7","word":"carpenter","forms":["carpenter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ba64b3b38baa046","term":"carpenter","forms":["carpenter","carpenters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"木匠","explanation":"木匠是專門加工木料的人：他們把木頭切割、拼接，用來建造房屋或其他結構。這是 carpenter 最常見、最值得先掌握的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The carpenter built a wooden staircase for our house.","zh":"木匠為我們家做了一段木樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My uncle works as a carpenter.","zh":"我叔叔是一名木匠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carpenter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c59ba38922292b97661","word":"carpet","forms":["carpet"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a056464a085e0ade","term":"carpet","forms":["carpet","carpets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地毯","explanation":"鋪在地面上、覆蓋一整片區域的織物，通常用來保暖、裝飾或讓地面更舒適。","examples":[{"en":"We replaced the old carpet in the living room last spring.","zh":"去年春天，我們換掉了客廳裡的舊地毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel room has soft blue carpet under the bed.","zh":"這間酒店客房裡，床下鋪著柔軟的藍色地毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carpet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15d586ad56572699","term":"carpet","forms":["carpet","carpets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"像地毯一樣鋪滿","explanation":"指草、花、落葉或其他東西連續鋪展在某個表面上，形成像地毯一樣的覆蓋層。","examples":[{"en":"A carpet of yellow leaves covered the path after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，一層黃色的落葉鋪滿了小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A soft carpet of moss muffled our footsteps beneath the pines.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carpet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dacfaa3f7271e40","term":"carpet","forms":["carpet","carpets","carpeting","carpeted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鋪地毯","explanation":"在某個區域鋪設地毯，或讓工人把地毯安裝到那裡。","examples":[{"en":"They plan to carpet the upstairs bedrooms next month.","zh":"他們計劃下個月給樓上的臥室鋪地毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had the office carpeted before the new staff arrived.","zh":"新員工到來前，我們請人給辦公室鋪好了地毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carpet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13bfabb07807921f6ce3","word":"carriage","forms":["carriage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da7d2adacee33a7d","term":"carriage","forms":["carriage","carriages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運送；運輸","explanation":"指把人或物從一個地方運到另一個地方這件事，重點是“承載並帶著走”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The carriage of fresh food requires special vehicles.","zh":"新鮮食品的運輸需要專用車輛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The price includes carriage to your nearest depot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carriage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7637d03db967689e","term":"carriage","forms":["carriage","carriages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交通工具；運輸手段","explanation":"指用來載人或載物的工具或方式，是“運送”這一動作所藉助的承載物。","examples":[{"en":"The company arranged carriage by boat to the island.","zh":"公司安排了乘船前往該島的運輸方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The merchants relied on river carriage for heavy goods.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carriage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f74175ea9a3e3a4d","term":"carriage","forms":["carriage","carriages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬車","explanation":"通常指由馬拉的、主要用來載人的車，常讓人聯想到舊時代或觀光場景中的四輪馬車。","examples":[{"en":"They took a carriage ride through the old town.","zh":"他們乘馬車遊覽了老城區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A horse-drawn carriage waited outside the hotel.","zh":"一輛馬車停在酒店外等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carriage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5803587e6791c11992f3","word":"carrier","forms":["carrier"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c299170dd5520f38","term":"carrier","forms":["carrier","carriers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承載者；運輸工具","explanation":"carrier 最基本的意思是“把某人或某物帶走、運送或承載的人或物”。它既可以指人，也可以指車輛、裝置等，所以 armored personnel carrier 是“裝甲人員運輸車”。","examples":[{"en":"The carrier delivered the medical supplies before noon.","zh":"承運方在中午前送到了醫療用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An armored personnel carrier moved the soldiers across the field.","zh":"一輛裝甲人員運輸車載著士兵穿過了原野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carrier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26ce00d6a0d8e44c","term":"carrier","forms":["carrier","carriers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"航空母艦","explanation":"在軍事語境中，carrier 常是 aircraft carrier 的省略，指搭載並運用飛機的航空母艦。","examples":[{"en":"The aircraft carrier returned to port after the exercise.","zh":"這艘航空母艦在演習後返回了港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The carrier launched two aircraft before sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carrier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b96482290a873ee98752","word":"carrot","forms":["carrot"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-57ef397f8e2b738b","term":"carrot","forms":["carrot","carrots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胡蘿蔔","explanation":"一種通常呈橙色、根部可食的蔬菜；日常說到這種食物時，這是最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I chopped two carrots and added them to the soup.","zh":"我切了兩根胡蘿蔔，把它們加進湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Carrots keep well in the refrigerator.","zh":"胡蘿蔔放在冰箱裡能儲存得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carrot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b93a63e50dae146","term":"carrot","forms":["carrot","carrots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎勵性激勵","explanation":"指為了讓人做某事而擺出的獎勵或好處，像把胡蘿蔔掛在前面引人向前走；它與強迫或懲罰相對。","examples":[{"en":"The company offered bonuses as a carrot to employees who met their targets.","zh":"公司用獎金獎勵達到目標的員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy uses carrots rather than penalties to encourage recycling.","zh":"新政策用獎勵而不是罰款來鼓勵回收。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carrot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ef49cacb4c39f8fe29c","word":"carry","forms":["carry"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e2403027546a530","term":"carry","forms":["carry","carries","carrying","carried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搬運；帶到別處","explanation":"表示拿起某物並帶著它移動到另一個地方，正是“把東西帶著走”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Can you carry these boxes upstairs?","zh":"你能把這些箱子搬到樓上嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ambulance carried the injured man to the hospital.","zh":"救護車把傷者送到了醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e21fcecde3578128","term":"carry","forms":["carry","carries","carrying","carried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持有；維持","explanation":"表示身上、手頭或賬戶中擁有並持續保有某物，也可表示持續維持某種保障或安排；這是把東西“帶在身上或手裡”的抽象延伸。","examples":[{"en":"You should carry enough insurance for your home.","zh":"你應該為住房購買足夠的保險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop carries replacement batteries.","zh":"這家店備有替換電池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52461c34618fe1d7","term":"carry","forms":["carry","carries","carrying","carried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隨身帶著","explanation":"表示把某物帶在自己身上，例如放在口袋、包裡或手中；這是“把東西帶著走”最直接的日常用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"I always carry my keys in my backpack.","zh":"我總是把鑰匙放在揹包裡隨身帶著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carries a small notebook everywhere.","zh":"她走到哪裡都隨身帶著一個小筆記本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c42ddc0285b9c25135b","word":"cart","forms":["cart"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c2b095ab3d0f09a","term":"cart","forms":["cart","carts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小車；推車","explanation":"指由人或動物推動、拉動的小型有輪車輛，通常用來運貨，常見形態是兩輪或結構開放的車。記住“裝著東西被輪子帶走”的畫面，就能和後面的搬運義聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer loaded the boxes onto a cart.","zh":"農夫把箱子裝上一輛小車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A horse pulled the cart up the hill.","zh":"一匹馬把那輛車拉上了山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-038520e421beb8c4","term":"cart","forms":["cart","carts","carting","carted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用車運送","explanation":"表示把某物裝在車上並運到別處，是名詞“運貨小車”直接發展出的動作義。重點是運輸方式與車輛有關，而不只是一般的 carry。","examples":[{"en":"They carted the vegetables to the market before sunrise.","zh":"他們在日出前把蔬菜用車運到了市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers carted the stones out of the yard.","zh":"工人們把石頭用車運出了院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94741ea49e3a3278b99a","word":"carton","forms":["carton"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5a9b7e54097ef0b","term":"carton","forms":["carton","cartons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紙盒；盒裝的一份","explanation":"carton是用紙板、蠟紙等輕質材料做成的盒狀容器，也常直接指裝在其中的一盒東西，例如牛奶或雞蛋。這裡的重點是“輕便紙盒”和“按盒出售的一份”這條聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a carton of milk for breakfast.","zh":"我買了一盒牛奶當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are six eggs in the carton.","zh":"這個蛋盒裡有六個雞蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e8c680ebef8a7cc","term":"carton","forms":["carton","cartons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一條香菸","explanation":"在香菸語境中，carton指把多包香菸集中包裝在一起的一整條，通常約有十包。它仍然是“用輕質包裝裝成一份”的延伸意義。","examples":[{"en":"He bought a carton of cigarettes at the airport.","zh":"他在機場買了一條香菸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The customs limit allows each traveler only one carton of cigarettes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15830f493c714309a282","word":"cartoon","forms":["cartoon"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc05b83742893894","term":"cartoon","forms":["cartoon","cartoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幽默漫畫","explanation":"指用簡潔、誇張的畫面表現笑料或觀點的漫畫，可以是單幅圖，也可以由多幅圖組成連續故事，常配有文字說明。","examples":[{"en":"She drew a cartoon about life in a busy office.","zh":"她畫了一幅關於忙碌辦公室生活的漫畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cartoon made everyone at the table laugh.","zh":"那幅漫畫逗得桌邊的每個人都笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cartoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a15300efa5c1c2b","term":"cartoon","forms":["cartoon","cartoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動畫片","explanation":"指由連續畫面製作成的動畫影視作品，可以是短片、電影或電視節目，內容不一定真的幽默。","examples":[{"en":"The children watched a funny cartoon on TV.","zh":"孩子們在電視上看了一部有趣的動畫片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This cartoon tells the story of a young fox.","zh":"這部動畫片講述了一隻小狐狸的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cartoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e74a35a12fd8c154","term":"cartoon","forms":["cartoon","cartoons","cartooning","cartooned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"畫成漫畫","explanation":"指用誇張、簡化的方式畫出人物或事件，通常為了幽默、諷刺或形成漫畫效果。","examples":[{"en":"The artist cartooned the politician with enormous ears.","zh":"那位藝術家把這名政治家畫成了有著巨大耳朵的漫畫形象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cartoons everyday problems for a local magazine.","zh":"她為當地雜誌把日常問題畫成漫畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cartoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4ab04449fe1544e80d0","word":"carve","forms":["carve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36415735a7a0f49e","term":"carve","forms":["carve","carves","carving","carved","carven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"切肉分食","explanation":"指把烤肉、火雞等切成片，準備分給大家吃；動作既包括切，也包括按適合食用的方式分配。","examples":[{"en":"Dad carved the turkey while everyone waited at the table.","zh":"大家在餐桌旁等著，爸爸把火雞切好分給大家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you carve the turkey while I serve vegetables?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0aab11f2536fd2b","term":"carve","forms":["carve","carves","carving","carved","carven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"雕刻成形","explanation":"指透過切、刻材料做出具有特定形狀的作品或圖案，也可以把文字刻進木頭、石頭等表面。這裡的核心仍是用切割動作“做出形狀”。","examples":[{"en":"She carved a small bird from a piece of wood.","zh":"她用一塊木頭雕刻出了一隻小鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone had carved a name into the old bench.","zh":"有人在那張舊長椅上刻了一個名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbfcd4160a1e8674dac6","word":"case","forms":["case"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-160bc3f346eac731","term":"case","forms":["case","cases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體情況；事例","explanation":"case可以指一個真實發生的事情、情況或事實，也就是把某件事單獨框出來討論。它常用於說明“在這個具體情況下”發生了什麼。","examples":[{"en":"In this case, waiting is the safest choice.","zh":"在這種情況下，等待是最安全的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is a clear case of mistaken identity.","zh":"這是一個明顯的身份誤認事例。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/case","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d673d5e0f99de94","term":"case","forms":["case","cases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"案件；訴訟","explanation":"在法律語境中，case是由法院或執法機構處理的案件、訴訟或起訴事項。它把一組法律事實和程式框成一個正式物件。","examples":[{"en":"The court dismissed the case for lack of evidence.","zh":"法院因證據不足駁回了這起案件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prosecutor is building a strong case against the suspect.","zh":"檢察官正在為指控嫌疑人建立有力的證據鏈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/case","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3f133f70a1c3f17","term":"case","forms":["case","cases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盒子；套；外殼","explanation":"case可以是用來容納或保護某件物品的盒子、套子或覆蓋物。它正好體現了記憶鉤子：把物品框進去，讓物品更安全、更容易攜帶。","examples":[{"en":"Keep your glasses in their case when you are not wearing them.","zh":"不戴眼鏡時，請把它放在眼鏡盒裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a protective case for her phone.","zh":"她給手機買了一個保護殼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/case","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b05086f5f926091","term":"case","forms":["case","cases","casing","cased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包住；加外殼保護","explanation":"指用外殼、套子或其他包覆物把某物包起來並保護住，就像把物品框進一個保護層裡。","examples":[{"en":"The cable is cased in a tough plastic coating to protect it from water.","zh":"這根電纜包有堅固的塑膠外層，以防進水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The metal frame was cased in wood for the exhibition.","zh":"金屬框架被木材包覆起來用於展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/case","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab0fcec08e18a7bccda1","word":"cash","forms":["cash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cd15c147113463d","term":"cash","forms":["cash","cashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現金；現鈔","explanation":"cash指紙幣和硬幣等可以直接拿來付款的錢，與支票、信用卡或電子支付相對。它強調錢已經以可立即支付的形式在手邊。","examples":[{"en":"I only have cash, so can I pay here?","zh":"我只有現金，可以在這裡付款嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop does not accept cash after 8 p.m.","zh":"這家店晚上八點後不收現金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2271e5bdd2d1aaa1","term":"cash","forms":["cash","cashes","cashing","cashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"兌現支票","explanation":"cash作動詞時，指把支票交給銀行或其他機構，換成紙幣、硬幣或賬戶中的可用資金。它把“現金”這個結果變成一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"I need to cash this check before the bank closes.","zh":"我得在銀行關門前把這張支票兌現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cashed her paycheck on Friday.","zh":"她星期五把工資支票兌現了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a79b51fec89db977e62","word":"cashier","forms":["cashier"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-57618492750e2668","term":"cashier","forms":["cashier","cashiers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收銀員","explanation":"cashier 是在商店、餐館等收銀臺為顧客收款、處理付款的人；記住“守著錢箱的人”就能抓住這個核心義。","examples":[{"en":"The cashier gave me the receipt and wished me a good day.","zh":"收銀員把收據給我，並祝我今天愉快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please ask the cashier if this coupon can be used.","zh":"請問問收銀員這張優惠券能不能用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cashier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-405e6e0273215dab5aa0","word":"casino","forms":["casino"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6f3eef4c028ade6","term":"casino","forms":["casino","casinos","casinoes","casini"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賭場","explanation":"指向公眾開放、以賭博為主要活動的建築物或房間；可以把它想成一座專門讓人下注和玩賭博遊戲的娛樂場所。","examples":[{"en":"They spent the evening at a casino near the beach.","zh":"他們在海邊附近的一家賭場裡度過了晚上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has never gambled in a casino.","zh":"她從未在賭場裡賭博。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casino","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-603705cc260e946d130a","word":"cast","forms":["cast"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad71244d7d05bf3e","term":"cast","forms":["cast","casts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投擲動作","explanation":"指把某物向外投出去的動作，正是“把東西投向外面”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"With one strong cast, she sent the ball over the fence.","zh":"她用力一投，把球投過了柵欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His first cast landed close to the target.","zh":"他第一次投擲落在目標附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aa17eef7bfefb61","term":"cast","forms":["cast","casts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演員陣容","explanation":"指共同出演一部戲劇、電影或其他作品的全部演員，也就是把演員“投”進各個角色後形成的陣容。","examples":[{"en":"The cast of the new film includes several well-known actors.","zh":"這部新電影的演員陣容包括幾位知名演員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined the cast after the first rehearsal.","zh":"她在第一次排練後加入了演員陣容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf413921c1c2f710","term":"cast","forms":["cast","casts","casting","casted","castest","casteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鑄造；澆鑄成形","explanation":"表示把熔化的金屬等材料倒進模具，使它冷卻後形成特定的物品；也就是把材料“投進”預定形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The artist cast the statue in bronze.","zh":"藝術家用青銅鑄造了這座雕像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory casts small metal parts for bicycles.","zh":"這家工廠為腳踏車鑄造小型金屬零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ec19d2c65ff2399","term":"cast","forms":["cast","casts","casting","casted","castest","casteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投送網路影片","explanation":"表示把影片透過網際網路或本地網路投送到電視等裝置上觀看；可以理解為把內容“投”給網路中的觀眾或螢幕。","examples":[{"en":"We cast the film from my phone to the television.","zh":"我們把電影從我的手機投屏到電視上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cast a live video to the screen during the meeting.","zh":"她在會議期間把實時影片投到螢幕上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-913a53d7df2fad651bed","word":"castle","forms":["castle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7441170a157a67ea","term":"castle","forms":["castle","castles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城堡","explanation":"castle是有城牆、塔樓等防禦設施的大型居住建築，過去常供貴族或國王居住；現代也可泛指帶有中世紀城堡外觀的大宅。","examples":[{"en":"We visited an old castle on the hill.","zh":"我們參觀了山上的一座古老城堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The castle was surrounded by a deep moat.","zh":"這座城堡四周環繞著一條很深的護城河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/castle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46cc2cc92699880d","term":"castle","forms":["castle","castles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王車易位","explanation":"在國際象棋中，castle指一次王車易位：王向一側移動兩格，同時相應的車越過王，來到王的另一側。這是一種把王置於更安全位置的防守動作。","examples":[{"en":"White castled early to protect the king.","zh":"白方很早就王車易位來保護國王。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He decided to castle on the queenside.","zh":"他決定進行後翼王車易位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/castle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c633eb52f63cec1d6b02","word":"casual","forms":["casual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-693c7506e1b6e328","term":"casual","forms":["casual","more casual","most casual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非正式的；輕鬆的","explanation":"指談話、關係或場合不遵循正式禮儀，氣氛自然放鬆，就像沒有被嚴格規矩拴住一樣。","examples":[{"en":"We had a casual conversation over coffee.","zh":"我們喝咖啡時輕鬆地聊了一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interview was surprisingly casual.","zh":"那場面試出乎意料地輕鬆隨意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4f589457af82a50","term":"casual","forms":["casual","more casual","most casual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"日常穿用的；休閒的","explanation":"指為日常生活設計、不要求正式場合穿用的衣物或鞋子；它把“不正式”具體延伸到穿著上。","examples":[{"en":"The invitation says casual clothes are fine.","zh":"邀請函上說穿休閒裝就可以。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wore casual shoes to the office.","zh":"他穿著休閒鞋去了辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ad2022fdda05f046ba4","word":"casualty","forms":["casualty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-115b13dee7a104b1","term":"casualty","forms":["casualty","casualties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意外或災禍","explanation":"指偶然發生、尤其是不幸的事件，例如事故、災難或其他造成損失的事情。這個意義強調“發生了什麼”，而不是事件中的具體人員。","examples":[{"en":"The storm was a casualty of unusually warm ocean temperatures.","zh":"這場風暴是異常溫暖的海水溫度所造成的一次不幸後果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge collapse was one of the worst casualties of the earthquake.","zh":"橋樑坍塌是這場地震造成的最嚴重災禍之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casualty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-026941966d5404a5","term":"casualty","forms":["casualty","casualties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傷亡人員","explanation":"指因事故或暴力而受傷或死亡的人，重點是這些人是事件造成的直接受害者；不一定已經死亡。","examples":[{"en":"Several casualties were taken to nearby hospitals after the crash.","zh":"事故發生後，幾名傷亡人員被送往附近的醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fire caused no civilian casualties.","zh":"這場火災沒有造成平民傷亡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casualty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77af778b51abd4a3c51c","word":"cat","forms":["cat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92551a459fee95de","term":"cat","forms":["cat","cats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貓；貓科動物","explanation":"指貓這種動物，通常首先想到家貓，也可以在分類或科學語境中泛指某些貓科動物。記憶時先抓住“貓”這個核心形象，其他義項大多是由它延伸出的名稱或術語。","examples":[{"en":"The cat is sleeping on the sofa.","zh":"那隻貓正在沙發上睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cats can see well in low light.","zh":"貓在弱光下視力很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2504e52b8b07484a2b6","word":"catalogue","forms":["catalogue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f51ad8e6c2f0690","term":"catalogue","forms":["catalogue","catalogues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目錄；系統清單","explanation":"把書、名字、圖片等按照一定系統列出來的目錄或清單。重點不在於它是一本書，而在於它把許多專案有條理地集中列出，方便查詢。","examples":[{"en":"I found the book in the library catalogue.","zh":"我在圖書館目錄裡找到了這本書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has published a catalogue of its new exhibition.","zh":"這家博物館出版了一本新展覽目錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catalogue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29935da81c1dd9d0","term":"catalogue","forms":["catalogue","catalogues","cataloguing","catalogued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編入目錄","explanation":"把某個專案按照一定順序或分類放進 catalogue，使它能被查詢和管理。","examples":[{"en":"The librarian catalogued the new books before putting them on the shelves.","zh":"圖書管理員把新書編入目錄後，才把它們放上書架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Volunteers catalogued the donated books by subject.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catalogue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebb061cadf57628eee35","word":"catastrophe","forms":["catastrophe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ac8cb0c38dd9473","term":"catastrophe","forms":["catastrophe","catastrophes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重大災難","explanation":"指規模很大、後果嚴重並具有重大影響的災難，例如戰爭、核事故或大範圍的自然災害。它描寫的是整個局面被徹底掀翻，而不只是一次普通的失敗或不便。","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake was a catastrophe for the entire region.","zh":"這場地震對整個地區來說是一場災難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without emergency supplies, the storm could become a catastrophe.","zh":"沒有應急物資，這場暴風雨可能會釀成一場災難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catastrophe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc962e43e1dfb7c9","term":"catastrophe","forms":["catastrophe","catastrophes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遠超預期的慘重損失","explanation":"在商業、保險等語境中，指結果壞到遠遠超出原先預期，造成特別慘重的損失。它仍然保留“局面被徹底掀翻”的核心畫面，但重點放在損失的意外程度和嚴重程度上。","examples":[{"en":"The failed merger was a financial catastrophe for both companies.","zh":"這次失敗的合併對兩家公司來說都是一場財務災難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Losing every shipment in one storm was a commercial catastrophe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catastrophe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f925cdc4feedda4d9ae","word":"catch","forms":["catch"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9564c5eb58a32977","term":"catch","forms":["catch","catches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隱藏條件；隱患","explanation":"指一項看起來很好的安排、交易或提議中，藏著沒有立刻被“抓住”的限制、代價或問題。","examples":[{"en":"The free trial sounds attractive, but what's the catch?","zh":"免費試用聽起來很誘人，但隱藏條件是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a catch: canceling early means losing your deposit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ccbb755f0517e6db","term":"catch","forms":["catch","catches","catching","caught","catched","catchest","caughtest","catchedst","catcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓住；趕上","explanation":"表示把人或動物抓到手，也可以表示追上並趕上某個目標。按照記憶鉤子，就是把目標真正“抓到手”。","examples":[{"en":"The children tried to catch the escaped chicken.","zh":"孩子們試著抓住那隻逃跑的雞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ran to catch the last bus home.","zh":"我們跑著去趕上回家的末班車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea0b1d8effc14928","term":"catch","forms":["catch","catches","catching","caught","catched","catchest","caughtest","catchedst","catcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓住；抓住某處","explanation":"表示用手突然抓住某人或某物，強調動作把物件牢牢控制住。它和記憶鉤子中的“抓到手”最直接對應。","examples":[{"en":"She caught me by the wrist before I fell.","zh":"我快要摔倒時，她抓住了我的手腕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He caught hold of the railing on the stairs.","zh":"他抓住了樓梯上的欄杆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1dca889046b1309a","term":"catch","forms":["catch","catches","catching","caught","catched","catchest","caughtest","catchedst","catcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聽懂；領會","explanation":"表示透過聽覺或思考抓住姓名、話語、意思等資訊。按照記憶鉤子，就是把聲音或意思“抓到”自己的理解裡。","examples":[{"en":"Sorry, I didn’t catch your name.","zh":"抱歉，我沒聽清你的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Did you catch what the teacher meant?","zh":"你聽懂老師的意思了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-edb2cd3b74c999af70f0","word":"category","forms":["category"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80653d8866c21948","term":"category","forms":["category","categories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"類別；組別","explanation":"指按照相似性、用途、難度或其他明確標準，把若干事物歸在一起形成的類別；也可以指這種類別本身的名稱或編號。","examples":[{"en":"This book belongs in the history category.","zh":"這本書屬於歷史類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Which category does this product fall into?","zh":"這個產品屬於哪一類？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/category","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be2925a2333b21d0a7a5","word":"cater","forms":["cater"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c50120e526f7ba22","term":"cater","forms":["cater","caters","catering","catered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承辦餐飲","explanation":"為聚會、婚禮等場合準備並提供食物和飲料，是這個詞最核心的現代用法。","examples":[{"en":"A local restaurant catered the wedding.","zh":"一家當地餐館承辦了這場婚禮的餐飲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They cater for parties and business events.","zh":"他們為聚會和商務活動提供餐飲服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9294e3b8106c5ce2","term":"cater","forms":["cater","caters","catering","catered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提供所需的食物或服務","explanation":"不侷限於某一種場合，表示按照物件的需要提供食物或相關服務。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel can cater for large groups.","zh":"這家酒店可以為大型團體提供餐飲服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel caters to guests with special dietary requirements.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44af44af682dd68e","term":"cater","forms":["cater","caters","catering","catered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迎合；滿足願望","explanation":"把“提供所需之物”引申到抽象需求上，表示順著某人的喜好、要求或願望去滿足他。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant caters to customers with special diets.","zh":"這家餐館滿足有特殊飲食需求的顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The show seems designed to cater to young viewers.","zh":"這檔節目似乎是專門迎合年輕觀眾的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-baffdf37aa5d3961c77b","word":"caterpillar","forms":["caterpillar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f995230991d0b0f","term":"caterpillar","forms":["caterpillar","caterpillars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毛蟲；幼蟲","explanation":"指蝴蝶或蛾的幼蟲，通常身體柔軟，有許多節，常在植物上爬行或取食。這是caterpillar最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The bird just ate that green caterpillar.","zh":"那隻鳥剛把那條綠色的毛毛蟲吃掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found three caterpillars on the cabbage leaves.","zh":"我們在捲心菜葉子上發現了三條毛毛蟲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caterpillar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cef50e2f11d80b60","term":"caterpillar","forms":["caterpillar","caterpillars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"履帶式車輛","explanation":"指用連續履帶代替普通車輪、能夠在鬆軟或崎嶇地面上行駛的車輛，也可泛指履帶本身帶動的爬行式車輛。這個意思來自毛蟲一節一節向前移動的外形聯想。","examples":[{"en":"The heavy machine moved over the mud on its caterpillar tracks.","zh":"那臺重型機器靠履帶駛過了泥地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A caterpillar cleared the muddy track for the trucks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caterpillar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca71d3ec52ddc8527345","word":"cathedral","forms":["cathedral"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d11872bd2c39ffc","term":"cathedral","forms":["cathedral","cathedrals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主教座堂","explanation":"主教座堂是一個教區中供主教辦公、主持宗教事務，有時也居住的主要教堂；其重要標誌是主教的座位。它是 cathedral 最核心、最具體的名詞義項。","examples":[{"en":"We visited the cathedral during our tour of the old city.","zh":"我們遊覽老城時參觀了那座主教座堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bishop preached in the cathedral on Sunday.","zh":"主教星期日在主教座堂裡講道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cathedral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-add0b887395735c131c7","word":"cattle","forms":["cattle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a3e33cbbf3946e1","term":"cattle","forms":["cattle"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牛；牛群","explanation":"指家養的牛類動物，包括母牛、公牛、閹牛和役牛等；重點是把它們看作一群家畜，而不是一隻具體的牛。","examples":[{"en":"The cattle are grazing in the field.","zh":"牛群正在田裡吃草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer moved the cattle into the barn before the storm.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，農夫把牛趕進了牲口棚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cattle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d29267339441b199","term":"cattle","forms":["cattle"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牲畜","explanation":"在較寬泛或舊式的用法中，cattle不只指牛，也可把羊、豬、山羊等家畜歸入這類牲畜；這是從“可飼養、管理和交易的家畜”這一核心概念擴充套件出來的。","examples":[{"en":"The old farm records listed cattle, sheep, and pigs under one heading.","zh":"舊農場記錄把牛、羊和豬列在同一個類別下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cattle gathered beside the watering trough.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cattle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a7ef1ed9f15c2f59ab7","word":"cause","forms":["cause"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b19e6940f19d9d50","term":"cause","forms":["cause","causes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原因；起因","explanation":"指引起某件事或某種結果的源頭，尤其常用於解釋問題、損害等不良結果是怎樣發生的。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor is trying to find the cause of her headaches.","zh":"醫生正在設法找出她頭痛的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Investigators found the cause of the fire.","zh":"調查人員找到了這場火災的起因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-113ef7d756971350","term":"cause","forms":["cause","causes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理由；充分理由","explanation":"指足以支援某種擔心、行動或判斷的理由；這裡關注的不是事情的物理起因，而是“有沒有理由這樣做或這樣想”。","examples":[{"en":"There is no cause for concern; the problem has been fixed.","zh":"不用擔心，問題已經解決了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sudden disappearance gave us cause for concern.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed68e50442cce531","term":"cause","forms":["cause","causes","causing","caused","causest","causedst","causeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"導致；造成","explanation":"表示某個因素把結果推了出來，使某件事發生；它正是“源頭流向結果”這條記憶線的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rain caused serious flooding in the town.","zh":"暴雨導致這個城鎮發生了嚴重洪災。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The broken window caused water to enter the house.","zh":"破窗使水進入了屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3cf083c28255868b5f46","word":"caution","forms":["caution"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60ed26b53a498268","term":"caution","forms":["caution","cautions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"謹慎；小心","explanation":"指面對可能的危險或傷害時保持警惕，並採取措施避免出問題；重點是先停下來、不要貿然行動。","examples":[{"en":"Use caution when walking on the wet floor.","zh":"在溼地板上行走時要小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sign advised caution near the edge of the cliff.","zh":"告示提醒人們在懸崖邊緣附近要小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12ebf09594a78d59","term":"caution","forms":["caution","cautions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"審慎考慮","explanation":"指在採取行動前仔細考慮可能的後果，以免失敗或造成傷害；它比一般的“小心”更強調對結果的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The report urges caution before expanding the project.","zh":"報告敦促人們在擴大專案之前要慎重考慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She approached the unfamiliar investment with caution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11e55a63033cb523","term":"caution","forms":["caution","cautions","cautioning","cautioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"警告；提醒注意","explanation":"指主動把可能的危險或不良後果告訴別人，提醒對方採取謹慎態度；也就是把心裡的警示燈指給別人看。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor cautioned her against returning to work too soon.","zh":"醫生警告她不要過早回去工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They cautioned us about the icy roads.","zh":"他們提醒我們注意結冰的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-7f0c68cb87de6c2a8536","word":"cautious","forms":["cautious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e32f623a7728a87","term":"cautious","forms":["cautious","more cautious","most cautious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"謹慎的；小心的","explanation":"形容人在面對未知情況或可能的風險時先觀察、衡量，再行動，不貿然往前。這種謹慎可以是實際行動上的小心，也可以是判斷和表達上的保守。","examples":[{"en":"He took a few cautious steps toward the cave.","zh":"他小心翼翼地朝洞穴走了幾步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should be cautious about making promises too soon.","zh":"我們不應該過早作出承諾，要謹慎一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cautious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b89a199ea81b6a925de7","word":"cave","forms":["cave"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71b6999f1e859019","term":"cave","forms":["cave","caves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洞穴","explanation":"指地下或山坡、懸崖內部自然形成的大空洞，人或動物可以進去。它是cave最典型、最容易聯想到的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We found a cave on the mountainside and sheltered there from the rain.","zh":"我們在山坡上發現了一個洞穴，就在那裡躲雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children explored the cave with flashlights.","zh":"孩子們拿著手電筒探索了那個洞穴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f71d330e6617851","term":"cave","forms":["cave","caves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隱居處；私人避難空間","explanation":"它可以比喻一個讓人躲開外界、獨處休息的地方，比如專屬於某人的房間或空間；本質上仍是“像洞穴一樣把自己藏起來”。","examples":[{"en":"After work, he retreated to his little cave to read.","zh":"下班後，他回到自己的小天地裡讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His basement cave contains books and old records.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2f4b7e20548e76a","term":"cave","forms":["cave","caves","caving","caved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"屈服；讓步","explanation":"指人在壓力、威脅或持續要求下像失去支撐一樣撐不住，最後讓步或屈服。它通常不是主動選擇，而是被壓力逼到退讓。","examples":[{"en":"She finally caved under pressure and accepted the offer.","zh":"她最終迫於壓力讓步，接受了那份提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wanted to refuse, but I caved in to their demands.","zh":"我本來想拒絕，但最後還是向他們的要求屈服了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5529f50764844dcb","term":"cave","forms":["cave","caves","caving","caved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塌陷","explanation":"指屋頂、牆壁或地面因失去支撐而向內塌下，正像一個空洞的頂部垮掉。","examples":[{"en":"The old tunnel caved in after the heavy rain.","zh":"暴雨後，那條舊隧道塌陷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Part of the roof caved in during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，屋頂的一部分塌了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31eb5cb46700fa44a322","word":"cavity","forms":["cavity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-771185d6c6409a5a","term":"cavity","forms":["cavity","cavities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空洞；凹陷","explanation":"指固體內部或表面形成的空著的部分，大小可以不同，例如岩石、牆壁或其他物體上的洞和凹處。這個意思是“裡面被掏空”的基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater collected in a cavity in the rock.","zh":"雨水積在岩石的一個凹洞裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dentist discovered a deep cavity beneath the damaged filling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cavity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf15bff27ece1ba3","term":"cavity","forms":["cavity","cavities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛀洞；齲洞","explanation":"指牙齒被齲齒侵蝕後形成的小洞，也常泛指洞周圍已經受損的軟化區域。它是 cavity 在日常牙科語境中非常常見的專門用法。","examples":[{"en":"The dentist found a cavity in one of my back teeth.","zh":"牙醫發現我的一顆後牙上有蛀洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dentist filled a small cavity in my molar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cavity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2de1585bf8d440577ae3","word":"cease","forms":["cease"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be151f17167435d4","term":"cease","forms":["cease","ceases","ceasing","ceased","ceasest","ceasedst","ceaseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停止；終止","explanation":"表示某個動作、活動或狀態停下來，就像原本持續的線突然斷了。主語通常是正在發生的事情，也可以是人或其他主體。","examples":[{"en":"The rain finally ceased before dawn.","zh":"黎明前，雨終於停了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine ceased to operate without warning.","zh":"機器毫無徵兆地停止運轉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19e5d8fcf7e9fdbd","term":"cease","forms":["cease","ceases","ceasing","ceased","ceasest","ceasedst","ceaseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停止做某事","explanation":"表示某人或某個主體不再繼續做某件事，即讓正在進行的動作停下來。","examples":[{"en":"The company ceased producing the old model last year.","zh":"那家公司去年停止生產舊型號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory ceased producing engines last spring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96f16e929047d5fa07f1","word":"ceiling","forms":["ceiling"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58e63b764fadab34","term":"ceiling","forms":["ceiling","ceilings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天花板","explanation":"指房間內部上方封住空間的表面，通常是人抬頭能看到的頂部。它是“覆蓋在上方”的核心形象，也是 ceiling 引申出“上限”之意的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The dining room had an ornate ceiling.","zh":"餐廳有一面裝飾華麗的天花板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A crack appeared in the ceiling above the bed.","zh":"床上方的天花板出現了一道裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceiling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c36167e03dff702","term":"ceiling","forms":["ceiling","ceilings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上限","explanation":"指某種速度、數量、價格或表現所能達到的最高界限，就像碰到了頭頂的天花板，不能再向上。它可以是規定設定的，也可以是實際能力造成的限制。","examples":[{"en":"The new law puts a ceiling on rent increases.","zh":"新法律為租金上漲設定了上限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of funding has placed a ceiling on the team's growth.","zh":"資金不足限制了這支團隊的發展上限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceiling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c457a4c48c5fe751b46","word":"celebrate","forms":["celebrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a873c03c4dd4047","term":"celebrate","forms":["celebrate","celebrates","celebrating","celebrated","celebratest","celebratedst","celebrateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"慶祝或紀念","explanation":"為生日、節日、週年紀念日等重要時刻舉行活動，以表達喜悅、尊重或紀念；重點是把這個日子鄭重地標記出來。","examples":[{"en":"We’re celebrating her birthday this weekend.","zh":"我們這週末要慶祝她的生日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town celebrates the festival every spring.","zh":"這個小鎮每年春天都會慶祝這個節日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celebrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3839f5e2063dd850","term":"celebrate","forms":["celebrate","celebrates","celebrating","celebrated","celebratest","celebratedst","celebrateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"高興地慶祝","explanation":"因為某件令人高興的事而進行歡慶活動，常常不說明具體形式；可以是聚餐、聚會，也可以只是和別人一起分享喜悅。","examples":[{"en":"We won the match, so let’s celebrate!","zh":"我們贏了比賽，慶祝一下吧！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They celebrated with dinner after the announcement.","zh":"訊息公佈後，他們一起吃晚飯慶祝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celebrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c7871235e7eb44af958","word":"celebration","forms":["celebration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e6d72a740ed1501","term":"celebration","forms":["celebration","celebrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表達喜悅或紀念","explanation":"指透過行動或社交活動表達感謝、喜悅、讚賞或紀念；它可以是一個具體活動，也可以泛指慶祝這一行為。","examples":[{"en":"The players danced in celebration of their victory.","zh":"隊員們跳舞慶祝勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum held a celebration of the artist's life.","zh":"博物館舉辦了紀念這位藝術家一生的活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celebration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22d612d5dec905bd","term":"celebration","forms":["celebration","celebrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慶祝聚會","explanation":"指為慶祝某件開心的事而舉行的社交聚會，通常包括吃飯、聊天、娛樂等活動；它是“把慶祝具體辦成一場聚會”。","examples":[{"en":"We are having a celebration for my father's new job.","zh":"我們要為我父親找到新工作舉辦一個慶祝聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We held a small celebration for her retirement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celebration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-d9e218ac870d788c2b76","word":"celebrity","forms":["celebrity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-573da61dac9fab7b","term":"celebrity","forms":["celebrity","celebrities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名人","explanation":"指因為成就、工作或公眾曝光而被廣大人群認識的人。這個詞不只指演員或歌手，也可以指運動員、作家、商界人士和其他廣為人知的人。","examples":[{"en":"The athlete became a celebrity after winning the Olympic gold medal.","zh":"那名運動員贏得奧運金牌後成了名人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several celebrities attended the charity event.","zh":"幾位名人參加了那場慈善活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celebrity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9bcd15d0391c09e","term":"celebrity","forms":["celebrity","celebrities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名聲；名望","explanation":"這裡指一個人受到公眾廣泛關注、議論和認可的狀態，也就是“名聲”或“名望”。它強調被很多人知道這一狀態，而不是具體的某一位名人。","examples":[{"en":"She achieved celebrity after her novel became a bestseller.","zh":"她的小說成為暢銷書後獲得了名聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His sudden celebrity made shopping in peace impossible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celebrity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ddc5177b9204093a5462","word":"celery","forms":["celery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f445a6ffb1ac0fd0","term":"celery","forms":["celery","celeries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"芹菜植物","explanation":"指傘形科的芹菜這種植物，強調它作為一種植物或作物的整體形象。","examples":[{"en":"Celery grows well in cool, moist soil.","zh":"芹菜在涼爽溼潤的土壤里長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Slugs damaged every celery plant we had planted near the fence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a41da8b566eb3140","term":"celery","forms":["celery","celeries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"芹菜莖","explanation":"指從芹菜植株上掰下、用來生吃或烹調的莖；日常談到買菜、做湯或加沙拉時，通常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"I chopped some celery and added it to the soup.","zh":"我切了一些芹菜，加進了湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chop two stalks of celery for the soup.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39d02b42938b2b75d027","word":"cell","forms":["cell"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bd3c61c71010e4f","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監獄牢房","explanation":"指監獄或拘留所裡關押一名或多名犯人的小房間；它仍然是“封閉的小隔間”。","examples":[{"en":"The prisoner was taken back to his cell.","zh":"那名囚犯被帶回了牢房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two men spent the night in separate cells.","zh":"那兩名男子分別在不同的牢房裡過了一夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2015d3534089cf0a","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物細胞或組織小室","explanation":"在生物學中，cell 是構成生物體的基本小單位；某些組織或器官中也有承擔特定功能的小室。","examples":[{"en":"These cells help repair damaged tissue.","zh":"這些細胞有助於修復受損組織。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor examined the sample under a microscope for abnormal cells.","zh":"醫生用顯微鏡檢查樣本中是否有異常細胞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-161a1c6092834433","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大結構中的分隔部分","explanation":"泛指較大結構中的一個小分割槽或隔間，不一定是真正的房間；這是從“小室”擴充套件出的最通用抽象義。","examples":[{"en":"The spacecraft is divided into several cells for different tasks.","zh":"這艘航天器被分成幾個承擔不同任務的分割槽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The honeycomb consists of hundreds of hexagonal cells.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-880839ff6b9e8465","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電池單元","explanation":"指儲存電能的基本單元；一個電池組可能由一個或多個 cell 組成。","examples":[{"en":"This flashlight runs on two small cells.","zh":"這個手電筒用兩節小電池供電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One cell in the battery pack is damaged.","zh":"電池組裡有一個單元損壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce80dc99b9d155e4","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物體的細胞","explanation":"指生物體能夠進行生命活動、製造蛋白質並繁殖的基本單位，是生物學中最重要的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"Every living cell needs energy to survive.","zh":"每個活細胞都需要能量才能生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment uses healthy cells to replace damaged ones.","zh":"這種治療利用健康細胞替代受損細胞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9be4142e42d39300","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動通訊小區","explanation":"指無線通訊網路覆蓋範圍中的一個區域；許多小區連線起來，組成更大的行動通訊網路。","examples":[{"en":"Our phones switched to a new cell as we drove north.","zh":"我們向北開車時，手機切換到了新的通訊小區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village has weak cell coverage.","zh":"這個村子的行動通訊訊號覆蓋很弱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab89fffd24693fda","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表格單元格","explanation":"指電子表格或統計陣列中由一行和一列交會形成的一個格子。","examples":[{"en":"Enter the total in the last cell of the row.","zh":"把總數填入這一行最後一個單元格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Click the cell and type the new value.","zh":"點選這個單元格並輸入新數值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1df6b480cdebd1ec","term":"cell","forms":["cell","cells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手機","explanation":"cellular phone 的簡稱，指行動電話；它來自無線通訊網路把覆蓋範圍分成許多小區的概念。","examples":[{"en":"I left my cell at home, so I could not call you.","zh":"我把手機落在家裡了，所以沒法給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please send the address to my cell.","zh":"請把地址發到我的手機上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08d78d084e8c1ffd2228","word":"cellphone","forms":["cellphone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"cellphone","forms":["cellphone"],"pos":"n.","zh":"手機；行動電話","examples":[{"en":"Please turn off your cellphone during the performance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She used her cellphone to call a taxi.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-000f4ef5a9a4092da2fa","word":"cellular","forms":["cellular"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5178129cc633c33c","term":"cellular","forms":["cellular","more cellular","most cellular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"細胞的；與細胞有關的","explanation":"指屬於細胞、涉及細胞，或由細胞組成的事物。它把“細胞”這個小單位擴充套件為相關的結構、活動和系統。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied how stress affects cellular activity.","zh":"研究人員研究了壓力如何影響細胞活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This treatment protects cellular structures from damage.","zh":"這種治療可以保護細胞結構免受損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cellular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fc0c94a7d6e5679","term":"cellular","forms":["cellular","more cellular","most cellular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有規則小孔的；蜂窩狀織物的","explanation":"指布料有規則排列的小孔，整體看起來像許多相連的小細胞格子；也可指用這種布料製成的衣物。","examples":[{"en":"He wore a cellular sports shirt on the hike.","zh":"他徒步時穿了一件蜂窩狀透氣運動衫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cellular cotton blanket kept the baby comfortable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cellular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-618a6bf55b14f703d6c2","word":"Celsius","forms":["Celsius"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"Celsius","forms":["Celsius"],"pos":"n.","zh":"攝氏溫標；攝氏","examples":[{"en":"Water freezes at zero degrees Celsius.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The temperature reached thirty degrees Celsius this afternoon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac800699bdf654a62fad","word":"cement","forms":["cement"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea93542bb553826c","term":"cement","forms":["cement","cements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水泥粉","explanation":"cement 是把石灰石和黏土高溫煅燒後製成的粉末，加水後能產生很強的黏結力，是混凝土的重要成分。","examples":[{"en":"The builders mixed cement with sand and water.","zh":"建築工人把水泥、沙子和水混合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the bags of cement dry until needed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e09b986cf2038273","term":"cement","forms":["cement","cements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牢固的聯結","explanation":"由“把東西粘牢”的具體意義引申而來，cement 可以指使朋友、家庭或社會成員緊密團結的關係或力量。","examples":[{"en":"Shared traditions are the cement of the community.","zh":"共同的傳統是維繫這個社群的紐帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Shared hardship became the cement of their friendship.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-360d2d4ee9913e4e","term":"cement","forms":["cement","cements","cementing","cemented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使牢固團結","explanation":"比喻地說，cement 表示把人、關係或團體牢牢聯結起來，就像水泥把磚石粘在一起一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement cemented relations between the two countries.","zh":"這項協議鞏固了兩國之間的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their shared ordeal cemented a lifelong friendship.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a9e5490c1828bfb8a97","word":"cemetery","forms":["cemetery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7bdfba9c5843233","term":"cemetery","forms":["cemetery","cemeteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"墓地；公墓","explanation":"指一整片安葬死者的地方，通常有許多墳墓，有時還設有道路、樹木或紀念設施；重點是“墓地這個場所”，而不是其中某一座墳。","examples":[{"en":"The old cemetery is just outside the village.","zh":"那座老墓地就在村子外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found her grave in the village cemetery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cemetery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7969bf2d3a9ceff9f774","word":"census","forms":["census"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9324b70047dadd24","term":"census","forms":["census","censuses","censusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人口普查；正式清點","explanation":"由政府或其他正式機構在某一地區、某一時期系統地統計居民或其他群體的人數，通常會定期進行。重點不只是得到一個數字，而是按統一辦法把物件逐一登記和彙總。","examples":[{"en":"The government will conduct a census next year.","zh":"政府將於明年進行人口普查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The latest census recorded a sharp increase in the city's population.","zh":"最近一次人口普查顯示，該市人口大幅增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/census","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c388fa9a52705a2ce0ee","word":"cent","forms":["cent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b200370b44fb5366","term":"cent","forms":["cent","cents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貨幣的百分之一","explanation":"指許多國家貨幣基本單位的百分之一，例如一美元的百分之一；符號通常寫作 ¢。它強調的是金額單位，而不一定是實物硬幣。","examples":[{"en":"The price went up by two cents.","zh":"價格上漲了兩分錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This phone costs ninety-nine cents.","zh":"這部手機要九十九分錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf036c8609ee7da5","term":"cent","forms":["cent","cents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一點錢","explanation":"在非正式表達中，cent 可以泛指一小筆錢，重點不在精確的百分之一，而在“哪怕最少的錢”。","examples":[{"en":"She saved every cent for her trip.","zh":"她為旅行省下了每一分錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I won't lend him another cent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f179a509d32bd92c923f","word":"center","forms":["center"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-83b96fc73677b597","term":"center","forms":["center","centers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓心","explanation":"圓的中心點；從這個點到圓周上各點的距離相等。這是“中心”最具體的幾何意義。","examples":[{"en":"The dot marks the center of the circle.","zh":"這個點標出了圓心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place the compass point at the circle's center.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/center","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c6a4208e8208ba3","term":"center","forms":["center","centers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中部；中央","explanation":"指一個物體、區域或範圍中遠離邊緣的部分。它不一定是精確的幾何點，更多時候是日常所說的“中間位置”。","examples":[{"en":"There is a fountain in the center of the square.","zh":"廣場中央有一個噴泉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please fold the paper down the center.","zh":"請沿著紙張中線把它折下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/center","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9900ebd67f1fd2dd","term":"center","forms":["center","centers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"焦點；核心議題","explanation":"指某個討論、爭議或思考中最重要、最決定性的物件。話題彷彿圍著這個中心展開，因此它不一定是空間上的中心。","examples":[{"en":"The safety of the workers is at the center of the debate.","zh":"工人的安全是這場爭論的核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her research is at the center of the discussion.","zh":"她的研究是討論的焦點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/center","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e60061df78be5e38d0bf","word":"centimeter","forms":["centimeter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21cea8750b9c78bb","term":"centimeter","forms":["centimeter","centimeters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"釐米","explanation":"一種長度單位，一釐米等於一米的百分之一，常用來描述較小物體或距離的長度；這個詞也是 centimetre 的另一種英語拼寫。","examples":[{"en":"The box is only ten centimeters wide.","zh":"這個盒子只有十釐米寬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The caterpillar grew another centimeter in a week.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/centimeter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8cb6279a8e1b12a96774","word":"central","forms":["central"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41313212adbda1f9","term":"central","forms":["central","more central","most central","centralmost","centremost","centermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"位於中心的","explanation":"表示處在某個地方、區域或事物的中心位置，重點是空間上的“在中間”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is in a central location near the station.","zh":"這家酒店位於車站附近的中心位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The central courtyard brings light into every room.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/central","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09ceceaa026e2ada","term":"central","forms":["central","more central","most central","centralmost","centremost","centermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"關鍵的；核心的","explanation":"把“中心”從空間意義延伸到重要性：如果某人、某事是 central 的，許多事情都圍繞它展開，因此它起著關鍵作用。","examples":[{"en":"Trust is central to a successful team.","zh":"信任對一個成功的團隊至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She played a central role in the negotiations.","zh":"她在談判中發揮了關鍵作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/central","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-545a20faf7cbb6f33a5a","word":"century","forms":["century"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a70e1897b1dd083","term":"century","forms":["century","centuries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一百年；世紀","explanation":"century 是連續的一百年，也常指按約定編號的一個世紀。例如，第二十世紀嚴格來說從1901年到2000年；第一世紀則從1年到100年。","examples":[{"en":"The city has changed dramatically over the last century.","zh":"這座城市在過去一百年裡發生了巨大變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are living in the twenty-first century.","zh":"我們生活在二十一世紀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/century","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb816f613ff3b3600ab6","word":"ceramic","forms":["ceramic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb274d68e3c6d584","term":"ceramic","forms":["ceramic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陶瓷的；陶製的","explanation":"指由黏土、礦物等無機非金屬材料經過高溫燒製而成，或具有這種材料性質的東西。核心畫面就是“進窯燒成陶瓷”，所以 ceramic vase 就是陶瓷花瓶。","examples":[{"en":"A ceramic vase stood on the table.","zh":"桌上放著一個陶瓷花瓶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A ceramic bowl shattered on the stone floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceramic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ebe34412eb57e9d9","term":"ceramic","forms":["ceramic","ceramics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陶瓷材料","explanation":"指經過高溫燒製形成的堅硬而易碎的無機非金屬材料，常見原料包括黏土。這裡關注的是“燒出來的材料”本身，而不是某一個具體器物。","examples":[{"en":"The bowl is made of ceramic and can withstand high heat.","zh":"這個碗是陶瓷制的，可以承受高溫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manufacturer replaced metal with heat-resistant ceramic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceramic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38c09b54483898f2aea7","word":"cereal","forms":["cereal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84eb2b2bbba8c8df","term":"cereal","forms":["cereal","cereals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穀類作物","explanation":"指為獲取可食用穀粒而栽培的禾本科作物，例如小麥、水稻或燕麥。這裡說的是正在田裡生長的作物，而不是單獨收下來的穀粒。","examples":[{"en":"Rice is a major cereal in many parts of Asia.","zh":"水稻是亞洲許多地區的重要穀類作物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers sowed cereal on the higher, drier fields.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cereal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a24ae4f33bd0655","term":"cereal","forms":["cereal","cereals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"早餐穀物食品","explanation":"指早餐吃的加工穀物食品，通常裝在碗裡，配牛奶或其他食物。它是“穀粒”從農業原料走到餐桌後的日常用法。","examples":[{"en":"I usually have cereal with milk before work.","zh":"我通常上班前吃加牛奶的早餐穀物食品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He poured milk over his breakfast cereal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cereal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b3a7b8b9dcb165c4bb9","word":"ceremony","forms":["ceremony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4d558961ce6227c","term":"ceremony","forms":["ceremony","ceremonies","ceremonys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儀式","explanation":"指具有宗教、文化或傳統意義的一套正式儀式，就像把某種神聖或重要的行為按規定鄭重地做出來。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers held a ceremony to give thanks for the harvest.","zh":"村民舉行儀式，感謝這一年的收成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ceremony begins with a traditional song.","zh":"儀式以一首傳統歌曲開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceremony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31d96d204aba1f3a","term":"ceremony","forms":["ceremony","ceremonies","ceremonys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式典禮","explanation":"指為慶祝、紀念或正式宣佈某件事而舉行的活動，例如畢業、開幕、授獎等；這是把重要時刻公開而鄭重地標記出來。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents attended the graduation ceremony.","zh":"她的父母參加了畢業典禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The opening ceremony featured a traditional drum performance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceremony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70d16cbbf8e41719a091","word":"certain","forms":["certain"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae566335c9bb90cd","term":"certain","forms":["certain","more certain","certainer","most certain","certainest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"確信的","explanation":"指說話人心裡非常有把握，認為某事是真的或某個判斷不會錯。","examples":[{"en":"I am certain that we left the keys on the table.","zh":"我確信我們把鑰匙放在桌上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is certain of her decision.","zh":"她對自己的決定很有把握。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a26c2b3ea944d62","term":"certain","forms":["certain","more certain","certainer","most certain","certainest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"必然的","explanation":"指某事肯定會發生，幾乎沒有避免的可能；重點在結果的必然性，而不是誰的心理判斷。","examples":[{"en":"With this lead, our team is certain to win.","zh":"有這樣的領先優勢，我們隊肯定會贏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is certain to notice the change.","zh":"她肯定會注意到這個變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6107d8fd2d0987e5","term":"certain","forms":["certain","more certain","certainer","most certain","certainest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"某個特定的","explanation":"指物件確實是特定的，但說話人沒有說明是哪一個，或暫時不想進一步說明。","examples":[{"en":"A certain customer keeps leaving messages for you.","zh":"有個特定的顧客一直給你留言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every town has a certain charm.","zh":"每個城鎮都有某種獨特的魅力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d14d5090afcde8381fc2","word":"certainty","forms":["certainty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-497836f0bf32487b","term":"certainty","forms":["certainty","certainties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"確定性；確信","explanation":"指一個判斷被牢牢釘住、沒有多少懷疑的狀態，重點是“確定無疑”本身，而不是某個具體物件。","examples":[{"en":"No one can say with certainty what will happen next.","zh":"沒人能確定地說出接下來會發生什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The test results gave us greater certainty about the cause.","zh":"檢測結果讓我們更確定病因了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certainty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67b6cfaa3e0a980c","term":"certainty","forms":["certainty","certainties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"十拿九穩的事","explanation":"指某個具體的人、事或結果，被認為幾乎必然會出現、成功或實現；它是“確定性”落在一個具體目標上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"After her outstanding performance, a promotion seemed a certainty.","zh":"她表現出色，升職似乎已是十拿九穩的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With those clouds overhead, rain is a certainty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certainty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03d66dd08835c1ca3f12","word":"certificate","forms":["certificate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f064c061cc6bfaf","term":"certificate","forms":["certificate","certificates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式證明檔案","explanation":"指一份正式檔案，其中寫明並確認某個事實、狀態或資格。例如，它可以證明某人透過了檢查、某物符合標準，或某件事確實發生過。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor gave me a certificate confirming that I was fit to work.","zh":"醫生給了我一份證明，確認我適合工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need a birth certificate to apply for a passport.","zh":"申請護照需要出生證明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certificate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dff9d15469d064c3","term":"certificate","forms":["certificate","certificates","certificating","certificated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"簽發證明","explanation":"指經過稽核後，為某人、某物或某項事實提供正式證書。它把名詞 certificate 所代表的“證明檔案”變成了簽發或確認這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The agency certificated the product as safe for children.","zh":"該機構為這款產品簽發了兒童使用安全證明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency certificates inspectors after their final assessment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certificate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6706b672c3d63aa4b4c6","word":"certify","forms":["certify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f87d0f972c421e04","term":"certify","forms":["certify","certifies","certifying","certified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式證明屬實","explanation":"指以可靠、正式的方式證明某個事實是真的，重點是“為事實作出確認”。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor certified that she was fit to return to work.","zh":"醫生證明她適合回去工作了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inspector certified the report as accurate.","zh":"檢查員證明這份報告準確無誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1adf29fce1c6d8a","term":"certify","forms":["certify","certifies","certifying","certified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"官方認證達標","explanation":"指官方機構或有資格的組織確認產品、服務、機構或人員達到了規定的標準或要求。可以把它理解為給物件“蓋章確認合格”。","examples":[{"en":"The laboratory certified the water as safe to drink.","zh":"該實驗室認證這水符合飲用安全標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inspector certified the elevator as compliant with safety standards.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/certify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9414886b1ebf025db067","word":"chain","forms":["chain"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36f1b3abacc8c57e","term":"chain","forms":["chain","chains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鏈條","explanation":"由許多金屬環或鏈節扣在一起組成的物體，可用來裝飾、牽引、固定或鎖住東西。","examples":[{"en":"She locked the gate with a heavy chain.","zh":"她用一條粗重的鏈條鎖住了大門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wore a silver chain around his neck.","zh":"他脖子上戴著一條銀項鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36899f7de1cf646b","term":"chain","forms":["chain","chains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一連串；連續系列","explanation":"許多彼此相連或前後有關的事物組成的連續整體，例如山脈、事件或反應。","examples":[{"en":"A chain of small mistakes caused the delay.","zh":"一連串小錯誤導致了延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One broken pipe triggered a chain of failures.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2459f8dd57ad02a","term":"chain","forms":["chain","chains","chaining","chained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用鏈拴住","explanation":"用鏈條把物品固定在某處，防止被移動或偷走。","examples":[{"en":"Please chain your bicycle to the fence.","zh":"請把腳踏車用鏈條鎖在柵欄上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They chained the gate to prevent unauthorized entry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5854f8c19bce5a3f","term":"chain","forms":["chain","chains","chaining","chained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使受束縛","explanation":"像被鏈條拴住一樣，使某人因依賴、上癮、責任或處境而難以離開或改變。","examples":[{"en":"She felt chained to her desk by endless paperwork.","zh":"沒完沒了的文書工作讓她覺得自己被拴在辦公桌前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Debt chained the family to exhausting factory work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3d7eb3d3dab17ee509a6","word":"chair","forms":["chair"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ffb8a3440b591ca","term":"chair","forms":["chair","chairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"椅子","explanation":"供一個人坐的傢俱，通常有座面和靠背，有時還有扶手或輪子。這是chair最基本、最常見的意義，其他許多意義都從“座位”延伸而來。","examples":[{"en":"She pulled up a chair beside the window.","zh":"她在窗邊拉來一把椅子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pull up a chair and join us.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32ecfe6cd3a60933","term":"chair","forms":["chair","chairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主席；主持人","explanation":"是chairperson的簡略形式，指主持會議或委員會的人；這裡的“座位”已經引申成了坐在主持席上的人。","examples":[{"en":"The chair asked everyone to keep their comments brief.","zh":"主席請大家把發言控制得簡短一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chair invited questions from the audience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5ec50c2a3f26796","term":"chair","forms":["chair","chairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主席職位；主持席","explanation":"指擔任主席的職位或權力，而不是具體坐著的那個人；“in the chair”就是處在主持席、主持會議的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Dr. Patel took the chair for the afternoon session.","zh":"帕特爾博士擔任了下午會議的主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She assumed the chair after the previous president resigned.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-940729b383cfec5c","term":"chair","forms":["chair","chairs","chairing","chaired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"主持","explanation":"指擔任會議主席、負責安排發言和維持會議進行；它來自“坐在主持席上”這一職位意義。","examples":[{"en":"Professor Lee will chair the hiring committee.","zh":"李教授將主持招聘委員會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discussion was chaired by an independent mediator.","zh":"這場討論由一名獨立調解人主持。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c65ef70765852e6dbae9","word":"chairperson/chair/chairman/chairwoman","forms":["chairperson","chair","chairman","chairwoman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78fa9b7ee00bb568","term":"chairperson","forms":["chairperson","chairpersons","chairpeople"],"pos":"noun","zh":"會議或組織的主持人","explanation":"chairperson 是負責主持會議、組織討論並帶領作出決定的人，可以是男性，也可以是女性；這個職位不侷限於某一次會議，也可以屬於董事會或其他組織。","examples":[{"en":"The chairperson opened the meeting and invited everyone to speak.","zh":"主持人宣佈會議開始，並邀請大家發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Maria was elected chairperson of the committee.","zh":"瑪麗亞當選為委員會主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chairperson","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8db3a7d6fc865830","term":"chair","forms":["chair","chairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"椅子","explanation":"供一個人坐的傢俱，通常有座面和靠背，有時還有扶手或輪子。這是chair最基本、最常見的意義，其他許多意義都從“座位”延伸而來。","examples":[{"en":"She pulled up a chair beside the window.","zh":"她在窗邊拉來一把椅子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wooden chair wobbled on its uneven legs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9edb2e7927b4b720","term":"chair","forms":["chair","chairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主席；主持人","explanation":"是chairperson的簡略形式，指主持會議或委員會的人；這裡的“座位”已經引申成了坐在主持席上的人。","examples":[{"en":"The chair asked everyone to keep their comments brief.","zh":"主席請大家把發言控制得簡短一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our committee elected a new chair yesterday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bacc22b9875dbcf","term":"chair","forms":["chair","chairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主席職位；主持席","explanation":"指擔任主席的職位或權力，而不是具體坐著的那個人；“in the chair”就是處在主持席、主持會議的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Dr. Patel took the chair for the afternoon session.","zh":"帕特爾博士擔任了下午會議的主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee elected him to the chair last spring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ce7518d7e712b3a","term":"chairman","forms":["chairman","chairmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"會議主持人","explanation":"指坐在會議主持位置、負責引導討論和處理會議流程的人，不一定是該組織的最高負責人。","examples":[{"en":"The chairman asked everyone to vote on the proposal.","zh":"會議主持人請大家對這項提案進行表決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chairman called the meeting to order.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chairman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7e89e31253e7c23","term":"chairman","forms":["chairman","chairmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"董事會或委員會負責人","explanation":"指董事會、委員會或其他正式機構中處於最高主持位置的人，既負責主持相關會議，也代表這個機構承擔領導職責。","examples":[{"en":"The chairman of the board approved the proposal.","zh":"董事會主席批准了這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chairman called an emergency board meeting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chairman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-507a04d0d4095703","term":"chairwoman","forms":["chairwoman","chairwomen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女主席；女主持人","explanation":"指負責主持會議、領導委員會或擔任某個組織主席的女性。核心畫面就是一位女性坐在主持人的主席位上，安排討論並帶領大家作出決定。","examples":[{"en":"She was elected chairwoman of the local committee.","zh":"她當選為當地委員會的女主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chairwoman opened the meeting with a short speech.","zh":"女主席用一段簡短的發言開始了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chairwoman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c886ff11f6a51b611a86","word":"chalk","forms":["chalk"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1009906b664f897","term":"chalk","forms":["chalk","chalks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"白堊；白色石灰岩粉末","explanation":"chalk 首先是一種柔軟、白色、容易變成粉末的石灰岩材料。粉筆的主要材料也與這種白色粉末有關，因此這個義項是其他許多義項的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The cliffs are made of soft white chalk.","zh":"這些懸崖由柔軟的白堊構成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chalk in the cliffs crumbled beneath our fingers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chalk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4ce7a63a088aaa1","term":"chalk","forms":["chalk","chalks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"粉筆；一塊書寫用粉筆","explanation":"chalk 也指把粉末壓制成的、用來寫字或畫圖的粉筆，尤其是黑板粉筆。這個義項把“白色粉末留下痕跡”的核心形象變成了日常工具。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher wrote the answer on the board with a piece of chalk.","zh":"老師用一塊粉筆把答案寫在黑板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was chalk dust all over the desk.","zh":"桌子上到處都是粉筆灰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chalk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5aac58279fbeb4da","term":"chalk","forms":["chalk","chalks","chalking","chalked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……塗粉筆或防滑粉","explanation":"chalk 作動詞時，可以表示把粉筆或粉末塗到某物上，例如把防滑粉抹在手上。這個動作直接來自“使用白色粉末”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"Chalk your hands before you start climbing.","zh":"開始攀巖前，先在手上抹些防滑粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He chalked the tip of his billiard cue.","zh":"他給檯球杆的杆頭塗了粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chalk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2dd00bd77e0222ced882","word":"challenge","forms":["challenge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e29ebd43b85b7689","term":"challenge","forms":["challenge","challenges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"當面對決或叫陣","explanation":"指把對方叫到面前，要求進行競爭、對抗或證明實力的挑戰，常帶有“你敢不敢應戰”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"His challenge to the champion surprised everyone.","zh":"他向冠軍發起的挑戰讓所有人都感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boxer accepted his rival's challenge immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/challenge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7c1c8ab1654eee6","term":"challenge","forms":["challenge","challenges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"需要克服的難題","explanation":"指一件不容易完成的事；正因為有難度，它往往也能激發人的興趣和鬥志。","examples":[{"en":"Learning to play the piano is a rewarding challenge.","zh":"學彈鋼琴是一項很有收穫的挑戰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keeping the remote clinic supplied remains a constant challenge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/challenge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd32efbfc9b7f428","term":"challenge","forms":["challenge","challenges","challenging","challenged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"邀請參加競爭","explanation":"指主動邀請某人參加比賽或競爭，把對方推到需要應戰的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Mia challenged her brother to a game of chess.","zh":"米婭邀請她哥哥來下一盤棋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The champion issued a challenge to any willing opponent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/challenge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41a4cef84d207139","term":"challenge","forms":["challenge","challenges","challenging","challenged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"質疑或爭辯","explanation":"指認為某個說法、數字或結論不可靠，並公開提出爭辯或要求重新檢驗。","examples":[{"en":"Several scientists challenged the accuracy of the report.","zh":"幾位科學家質疑了這份報告的準確性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She challenged the assumption behind his proposal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/challenge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e1637f032b1ffc7b9a4","word":"chamber","forms":["chamber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fccc98a28459e53","term":"chamber","forms":["chamber","chambers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房間；一組房間","explanation":"指一個房間，或彼此相連、共同使用的一組房間。這個詞常讓人聯想到較正式、古典或有特定用途的房間。","examples":[{"en":"The old castle has a private chamber overlooking the sea.","zh":"這座古堡有一間俯瞰大海的私人房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She opened the chamber door and stepped inside.","zh":"她開啟房門，走了進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chamber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8af82caf75ca11e2","term":"chamber","forms":["chamber","chambers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房間；一組房間（英國用法）","explanation":"在英國英語中，chambers 還可以指律師、法官等專業人士使用的一套辦公房間或事務所。","examples":[{"en":"The barrister returned to her chambers after the hearing.","zh":"庭審結束後，那名出庭律師回到了自己的辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The barrister met her client in chambers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chamber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b5105d80367eca48a11","word":"champagne","forms":["champagne"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae6ff14adf6421ef","term":"champagne","forms":["champagne","champagnes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香檳酒","explanation":"指用葡萄釀造的起泡白葡萄酒，核心上是法國香檳地區生產的那一類酒。這個義項是整詞最重要的中心：地區名轉成了當地最有代表性的產品名。","examples":[{"en":"They opened a bottle of Champagne to celebrate the promotion.","zh":"他們開了一瓶香檳酒來慶祝升職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We served champagne with the dessert.","zh":"我們給甜點配了香檳酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/champagne","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d14a7310bdf55b8ffeb7","word":"champion","forms":["champion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c674345d1ec1b98","term":"champion","forms":["champion","champions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冠軍；衛冕者","explanation":"指在比賽或競賽中獲勝的人或隊伍，尤其可以指正在保持冠軍頭銜、準備再次參賽的一方。這是 champion 最直接、最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The defending champion won the final in straight sets.","zh":"衛冕冠軍直落兩盤贏得了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The defending champion lost in the opening round.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/champion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d686b6378ff937ae","term":"champion","forms":["champion","champions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事業捍衛者","explanation":"指積極支援並推動某項事業、理念或權利的人。他不是在字面上參加比賽，而是像冠軍一樣站出來為目標爭取。","examples":[{"en":"She became a champion of equal access to education.","zh":"她成了教育機會平等的積極倡導者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a tireless champion of prison reform.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/champion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cedf4c8fa75b5c9ffadf","word":"championship","forms":["championship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1373430d7443a6bc","term":"championship","forms":["championship","championships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冠軍賽；冠軍爭奪賽","explanation":"指為了決出冠軍而舉行的比賽，尤其可以指一系列比賽的最後一場或最後階段。核心畫面是“透過比賽把 champion 選出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The championship begins next month with teams from twelve countries.","zh":"這項冠軍賽將於下個月開始，參賽隊伍來自十二個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reached the championship final for the first time.","zh":"她第一次進入了冠軍賽決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/championship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b944971ea523ed5c","term":"championship","forms":["championship","championships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冠軍地位；冠軍頭銜","explanation":"指成為冠軍這一地位或所獲得的冠軍頭銜，是比賽獲勝後的結果。這裡的重點不是比賽本身，而是“已經站在冠軍的位置上”。","examples":[{"en":"The boxer won his first world championship at the age of twenty-four.","zh":"這名拳擊手二十四歲時贏得了自己的第一個世界冠軍頭銜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is determined to defend its championship.","zh":"這支隊伍決心衛冕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/championship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cb09fe72a3471a776f9","word":"chance","forms":["chance"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1180095001ae22c","term":"chance","forms":["chance","chances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機會","explanation":"指可以做某事或獲得某種結果的時機；重點是這個機會是否來到你面前。","examples":[{"en":"I finally had a chance to talk with my manager.","zh":"我終於有機會和經理談了談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take this chance to ask any questions.","zh":"抓住這次機會提問吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aae4f0f543e38619","term":"chance","forms":["chance","chances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偶然性；聽天由命","explanation":"指事情沒有被完全安排或控制，而是任由偶然因素決定；這裡不是“一個機會”，而是“偶然本身”。","examples":[{"en":"We met by chance at a small café near the station.","zh":"我們偶然在車站附近的一家小咖啡館見面了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She never leaves important decisions to chance.","zh":"她從不把重要決定交給偶然性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7b5955371d71eb9","term":"chance","forms":["chance","chances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機率","explanation":"指某件事發生的可能性大小，可以用百分比或“高、低”等詞來說明；它把“事情可能落到你面前”量化了。","examples":[{"en":"There is a good chance of snow tonight.","zh":"今晚下雪的可能性很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is only a small chance that the train will be late.","zh":"火車晚點的可能性很小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12ea12eace7d655f471c","word":"change","forms":["change"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-684cb2bd9328a047","term":"change","forms":["change","changes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變化","explanation":"指人、事物或情況逐漸或突然變得不同，重點是“從原來的狀態變了”。","examples":[{"en":"The product is undergoing a change to improve its design.","zh":"這款產品正在進行改進設計的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There has been a big change in the weather.","zh":"天氣發生了很大的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/change","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65760dc4b585743f","term":"change","forms":["change","changes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"找零","explanation":"指付款金額超過商品價格後，商家退回的差額；它也是“換錢”這個核心畫面在買東西場景中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The cashier gave me two dollars in change.","zh":"收銀員找給我兩美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check your change before leaving the shop.","zh":"離開商店前請檢查詢零是否正確。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/change","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a585acf13633ee3f","term":"change","forms":["change","changes","changing","changed","changest","changedst","changeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改變；變成","explanation":"表示某人或某物從一種狀態變成另一種狀態，主語可以自己發生變化，不一定有人主動操作。","examples":[{"en":"The tadpole changed into a frog.","zh":"蝌蚪變成了青蛙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaves change color in autumn.","zh":"樹葉在秋天會變色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/change","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ed3ffd13cdf2f27","term":"change","forms":["change","changes","changing","changed","changest","changedst","changeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使改變；把……變成……","explanation":"表示主動把某物改造成不同的狀態或形式，是“讓東西換個樣子”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"A fresh coat of paint changed the room into a brighter space.","zh":"重新刷一層漆把房間變成了更明亮的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor changed the article from a report into a story.","zh":"編輯把這篇文章從報道改成了故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/change","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69e36568cd8b4659389b","word":"channel","forms":["channel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac69f19efdb806ed","term":"channel","forms":["channel","channels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水道；水流的槽道","explanation":"指河流、海水或其他水體流過的凹槽或水床，是水透過的自然或人工通道。把 channel 想成“讓東西透過的通道”，這裡透過的是水。","examples":[{"en":"The flood widened the channel of the river.","zh":"洪水衝寬了河道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The water flowed quickly through the narrow channel.","zh":"水流很快地透過狹窄的水道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/channel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-956b4667d816d537","term":"channel","forms":["channel","channels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海峽","explanation":"指夾在兩塊陸地之間的狹長水域，船只可以從中透過。這裡的 channel 就是連線兩片較大水域的水上通道。","examples":[{"en":"A strong current runs through the channel between the islands.","zh":"群島之間的海峽中有一股強勁的水流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ferry crosses the channel twice a day.","zh":"渡船每天兩次穿過這條海峽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/channel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6dac35232b0faa77","term":"channel","forms":["channel","channels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"渠道；媒介","explanation":"指資訊、訊息、商品或其他東西傳遞到另一處所經過的方式或媒介。新聞透過傳播渠道傳出去，商品也透過銷售渠道到達顧客。","examples":[{"en":"The company uses several channels to reach new customers.","zh":"這家公司透過多種渠道接觸新客戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please send the request through the official channel.","zh":"請透過官方渠道提交這項請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/channel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5212561a48eb36d","term":"channel","forms":["channel","channels","channeling","channelling","channeled","channelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引導；導向","explanation":"把人、車輛、資金、情緒或其他流動的東西引到指定方向或路徑上，就像把它們引入一條合適的通道。","examples":[{"en":"The barriers channeled pedestrians toward the main entrance.","zh":"這些隔離欄把行人引向了主入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She channeled her frustration into writing music.","zh":"她把自己的挫敗感轉化為創作音樂的動力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/channel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b9b466c8b4a9de465b6","word":"chant","forms":["chant"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eada84d2064e486b","term":"chant","forms":["chant","chants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吟唱","explanation":"指通常沒有樂器伴奏、也沒有複雜和聲的唱法，重點是用單一或簡單的音調持續吟唱。","examples":[{"en":"The monks began a quiet chant before the ceremony.","zh":"儀式開始前，僧侶們唱起了輕柔的吟唱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her voice moved between singing and chant.","zh":"她的聲音在歌唱和吟誦之間轉換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34a74cababb5c225","term":"chant","forms":["chant","chants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反覆吟唱","explanation":"指反覆唱的一小段歌曲或話語，常用於口號、咒語、儀式或集體活動；核心仍是用有節奏的重複聲音來加強氣氛或統一行動。","examples":[{"en":"The crowd repeated the same chant throughout the match.","zh":"整場比賽中，人群一直反覆喊著同一個口號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They used a short chant to begin the ritual.","zh":"他們用一段簡短的吟唱開始儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a54e14cef24ecb1","term":"chant","forms":["chant","chants","chanting","chanted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"齊聲反覆喊","explanation":"指一個人或一群人用強烈而整齊的節奏反覆說同一句話，常見於球迷、示威者或集體活動；這就是把“反覆吟唱”的核心擴充套件到口號。","examples":[{"en":"The supporters chanted the team's name after the goal.","zh":"進球后，支持者們反覆齊聲喊著球隊的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The protesters chanted for equal rights.","zh":"抗議者們齊聲呼喊，要求平等權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d5bddb577102d0a960b","word":"chaos","forms":["chaos"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4656a684caa604b","term":"chaos","forms":["chaos","chaoses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混亂；無秩序狀態","explanation":"chaos 指人、事物或環境完全失去秩序，彼此混雜，局面難以控制。它可以形容房間、交通、組織、計劃或社會局勢等。","examples":[{"en":"After the power went out, the station descended into chaos.","zh":"停電後，車站陷入了一片混亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing files created chaos in the office.","zh":"檔案丟失使辦公室陷入了混亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chaos","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0dc1f56cb0b8dc3","term":"chaos","forms":["chaos","chaoses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原始混沌","explanation":"在古代宇宙起源觀念中，chaos 指物質尚未形成秩序以前的混沌狀態，是神話義向普通“混亂”義發展的早期含義。","examples":[{"en":"The myth describes the universe as rising from chaos.","zh":"這個神話描述宇宙從混沌中誕生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Before the gods imposed order, chaos filled the mythical universe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chaos","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b2c852b2a2d5eea5715","word":"chapel","forms":["chapel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb2b3d76a07f05ea","term":"chapel","forms":["chapel","chapels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小型或附屬禮拜堂","explanation":"chapel 最核心的意思是比 church 小，或在組織上附屬於 church 的基督教禮拜場所。它可以是一座獨立的小建築，也可以只是大教堂、莊園或學校中的一個禮拜空間。","examples":[{"en":"We stopped at a small chapel on the hill to light a candle.","zh":"我們在山上的一座小禮拜堂停下來點了一支蠟燭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chapel stands beside the old parish church.","zh":"這座禮拜堂坐落在老教區教堂旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chapel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f32b3c96eaebc32f","term":"chapel","forms":["chapel","chapels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構內的禮拜室","explanation":"它也指設在學校、機場、醫院、監獄、修道院或其他大型建築中的禮拜場所，通常供內部人員祈禱或舉行小型禮拜。重點不在建築獨立存在，而在它附著於某個機構。","examples":[{"en":"Passengers can pray in the airport chapel before their flight.","zh":"乘客可以在登機前到機場禮拜室祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors may pray in the hospital chapel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chapel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-667b9327cc0b3ab64f0b","word":"chapter","forms":["chapter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9cbd5f61bc3b8a00","term":"chapter","forms":["chapter","chapters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書中的一章","explanation":"指書籍、小說或其他較長作品中相對獨立的一大部分，通常有自己的編號或標題。它像整本書這條長路上的一段，讀者可以按章閱讀。","examples":[{"en":"I finished the first chapter before dinner.","zh":"我在晚飯前讀完了第一章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final chapter explains what happened to everyone.","zh":"最後一章解釋了每個人後來發生了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chapter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-501f15f1f39348df","term":"chapter","forms":["chapter","chapters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人生或事件的一個階段","explanation":"指一連串經歷或事件中的一個階段，暗示這段經歷屬於更長的發展過程，後面可能還會有新的階段。它把人生或歷史想成一本正在展開的書。","examples":[{"en":"Moving to the city began a new chapter in her life.","zh":"搬到這座城市開啟了她人生的新篇章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This difficult chapter will eventually come to an end.","zh":"這段艱難的經歷最終會結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chapter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4bcef3de76eaf574c6ba","word":"character","forms":["character"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb9a249ccabee8ad","term":"character","forms":["character","characters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事人物","explanation":"指故事、小說、戲劇或電影中參與行動的人物；這個人物就像被作者刻進故事裡的一個形象。","examples":[{"en":"The main character learns to trust her friends.","zh":"主人公學會了信任朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each character in the novel has a different goal.","zh":"這部小說中的每個人物都有不同的目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/character","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-826d9a25e96a7687","term":"character","forms":["character","characters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特徵；特點","explanation":"指某人、某物或某種生物身上可辨認的單一特徵，就像刻在它身上的一個標記；它不一定涉及道德評價。","examples":[{"en":"Bright feathers are a striking character of this bird.","zh":"鮮豔的羽毛是這種鳥很醒目的一個特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers identified a character linked to flower color.","zh":"研究人員發現了一個與花色有關的性狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/character","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6081e6d6e286199d","term":"character","forms":["character","characters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"性格；品格","explanation":"指一個人或一類人的整體性格和品格，也就是長期表現出來的一組特徵；它可以包含誠實、勇敢等道德品質。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm character helped the team through the crisis.","zh":"她沉著的性格幫助團隊渡過了危機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book explores the character of the young leader.","zh":"這本書探討了這位年輕領導者的性格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/character","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f7a0de467f7e37b","term":"character","forms":["character","characters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文字或印刷符號","explanation":"指書寫、印刷或顯示出來的一個字母、數字或其他符號；它就是被刻在文字系統中的一個小標記。","examples":[{"en":"Type one character in each box.","zh":"每個方框裡輸入一個字元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The password must contain at least eight characters.","zh":"密碼必須至少包含八個字元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/character","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd70eb35e7aa71d746bc","word":"characteristic","forms":["characteristic"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa0c13c5a6113404","term":"characteristic","forms":["characteristic","more characteristic","most characteristic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"典型的；有特徵的","explanation":"指某人或某物表現出很能代表它的特徵，使人一看或一聽就容易聯想到它。這個特徵可以是外表、說話方式、行為或性質，也可以是令人不快的特點。","examples":[{"en":"Her characteristic patience helped the team finish the difficult project.","zh":"她一貫的耐心幫助團隊完成了這個困難的專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This warm, dry climate is characteristic of the region.","zh":"這種溫暖乾燥的氣候是該地區的典型特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/characteristic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab2c1f5b5efc98da","term":"characteristic","forms":["characteristic","characteristics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特徵；特點","explanation":"指能幫助我們認識、描述或區別某人某物的特點，也可以指一個人的行為方式等較穩定的表現。它就是“識別標記”這個核心概念本身。","examples":[{"en":"Curiosity is one of the most important characteristics of a good scientist.","zh":"好科學家最重要的特點之一是好奇心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Patience is an essential characteristic of a good teacher.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/characteristic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9bf86920ceaf8314f8df","word":"characterize","forms":["characterize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25e83d5ece869e1a","term":"characterize","forms":["characterize","characterizes","characterizing","characterized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……描述為","explanation":"把某人、某事或某種行為描述成某種性質或型別，常常是在作出帶評價的判斷，尤其可能是負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"The report characterized the policy as unfair.","zh":"這份報告把這項政策描述為不公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She characterized his silence as a sign of anger.","zh":"她把他的沉默看作憤怒的表現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/characterize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbf6c3172eaa0fd0","term":"characterize","forms":["characterize","characterizes","characterizing","characterized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"構成……的典型特徵","explanation":"某種性質、現象或細節反覆出現在某事物中，因此成為它的典型標誌；這裡不是誰主動給它貼標籤，而是說某特點本來就能代表它。","examples":[{"en":"Bright colors characterize the town's old houses.","zh":"鮮豔的色彩是這座小鎮老房子的典型特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Long dry summers characterize this coastal region.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/characterize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97488fbab3282166738a","word":"charge","forms":["charge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ce02f17ecc3590a","term":"charge","forms":["charge","charges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服務費用","explanation":"指為某項服務而加上的、需要支付的錢，可以理解為服務給你帶來的費用負擔。","examples":[{"en":"There is no extra charge for delivery.","zh":"配送不另收費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel added a service charge to the bill.","zh":"酒店在賬單上加收了服務費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-816328a315006dca","term":"charge","forms":["charge","charges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指控","explanation":"指正式加在某人身上的犯罪指控，也就是把某項罪名交由法律程式處理。","examples":[{"en":"He faces two charges of fraud.","zh":"他面臨兩項欺詐指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charges were dropped for lack of evidence.","zh":"由於證據不足，這些指控被撤銷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dd00d426ec11584","term":"charge","forms":["charge","charges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"責任範圍","explanation":"指某人負責管理、照料或保護的範圍，也就是一項被交付給他承擔的責任。","examples":[{"en":"The children were left in the teacher's charge.","zh":"孩子們被交給老師照管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is in charge of the evening shift.","zh":"她負責晚班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c11f79318fd5fbc9","term":"charge","forms":["charge","charges","charging","charged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收費；收取費用","explanation":"要求別人為商品、服務或某項行為支付一定金額，也就是給所提供的東西加上一筆費用。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic charges patients thirty dollars for a consultation.","zh":"這家診所向病人收取三十美元的諮詢費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They do not charge for delivery within the city.","zh":"他們在市內配送不收取費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea0c999046858f9d154b","word":"charitable","forms":["charitable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5fdb3ce8d9c2794","term":"charitable","forms":["charitable","more charitable","most charitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與慈善有關的","explanation":"指和捐助、救濟、幫助有需要的人等慈善活動有關，常修飾組織、活動、專案或捐款。","examples":[{"en":"She works for a charitable organization that provides meals to homeless people.","zh":"她在一家為無家可歸者提供餐食的慈善組織工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company made a charitable donation to the local hospital.","zh":"這家公司向當地醫院捐了一筆慈善款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7d1a3ee5613b4ce","term":"charitable","forms":["charitable","more charitable","most charitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慷慨善良的","explanation":"形容一個人或其行為願意幫助別人、寬厚體諒，不吝惜給予支援或資源；這裡的“慈善”從具體事業擴充套件成了人的善意。","examples":[{"en":"It was charitable of her to give the new employee another chance.","zh":"她願意再給那名新員工一次機會，真是很寬厚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her charitable neighbors brought meals throughout her recovery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb0b9c61cefd62358850","word":"charity","forms":["charity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8cacd4170dfbb35e","term":"charity","forms":["charity","charities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慈善機構","explanation":"指以慈善為目的、專門幫助有需要者的組織。這裡 charity 是一個具體機構，因此常可以數，也可以像普通組織名稱一樣談到它的工作、捐款和管理。","examples":[{"en":"The local charity provides meals for homeless families.","zh":"當地的慈善機構為無家可歸的家庭提供飯食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works for a charity that supports disabled children.","zh":"她在一家幫助殘疾兒童的慈善機構工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff444ca4d3854f9e","term":"charity","forms":["charity","charities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"救濟物資或錢","explanation":"指送給有需要者的錢、食物、衣物等具體幫助。這裡的 charity 不是提供幫助的機構，而是被送出去的那份援助本身。","examples":[{"en":"After the flood, thousands of families depended on charity.","zh":"洪水過後，成千上萬的家庭依靠救濟生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shelter received charity from businesses across the city.","zh":"這家收容所得到了全城企業捐贈的物資和資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4f6565d5f5392f6","term":"charity","forms":["charity","charities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慈善行為；救助","explanation":"指為了幫助處境較差的人而提供錢物或其他幫助這一行為本身。它強調“施以援手”的做法，而不是機構或某一件具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"Many people give to charity during the holiday season.","zh":"許多人在節日期間向慈善事業捐款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Volunteering at the food bank was an act of charity.","zh":"在食物銀行做志願者是一種慈善行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3a927cf63131517aecb","word":"charm","forms":["charm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-129841fa34095c32","term":"charm","forms":["charm","charms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"護身符；魔法","explanation":"指被認為具有魔力、能帶來好運或抵禦邪惡的物件、行為或話語，核心形象就是“用魔力保護人”。","examples":[{"en":"She kept a small charm against bad luck in her pocket.","zh":"她把一枚防止厄運的小護身符放在口袋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old woman whispered a charm over the sick child.","zh":"老婦人對著生病的孩子低聲唸了一段咒語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef8a24d030d825dc","term":"charm","forms":["charm","charms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"魅力；吸引力","explanation":"指一個人或事物使別人喜歡、信服或讚歎的吸引力；這是從“施加吸引力”發展出來的非魔法義。","examples":[{"en":"Her warmth and charm made everyone feel welcome.","zh":"她的親切和魅力讓每個人都感到受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He used his charm to persuade the manager to reconsider.","zh":"他用自己的魅力說服經理重新考慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee1b39e18cd6dc4d","term":"charm","forms":["charm","charms","charming","charmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使著迷；討人喜歡","explanation":"指用個人魅力、動人的話語或舉止讓某人喜歡、信服或被吸引，是名詞“魅力”變成動詞後的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"The guide charmed the children with funny stories.","zh":"導遊用有趣的故事逗得孩子們很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was charmed by his quiet confidence.","zh":"她被他沉靜的自信所吸引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc57fc1903e444cf6a72","word":"chart","forms":["chart"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-15c6577bf71c987e","term":"chart","forms":["chart","charts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地圖","explanation":"表示把地點、海域、道路等位置畫出來的地圖，重點是幫助人看清地理位置和方向。","examples":[{"en":"The captain unfolded a chart of the coastline.","zh":"船長展開了一張海岸線地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reefs marked on the nautical chart forced us to change course.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32c3ed8614bf4fd5","term":"chart","forms":["chart","charts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料圖表","explanation":"表示用表格、線條、柱形等非敘述方式系統展示資料的圖表；它把分散的資訊整理成一眼能比較的形式。","examples":[{"en":"This chart shows how household spending changed over the year.","zh":"這張圖表顯示了家庭支出在一年中的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chart compares rainfall across twelve months.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b3d7e7a15e0c5ffbdf7","word":"chase","forms":["chase"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-796be1ff215cc8fe","term":"chase","forms":["chase","chases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"追逐；追趕","explanation":"指一個人或事物持續跟在另一個目標後面，試圖追上或抓住它。這個詞強調“跟在目標後面”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The police car was involved in a high-speed chase.","zh":"那輛警車參與了一場高速追逐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a long chase, the dog finally caught the ball.","zh":"追了很久後，狗終於接住了球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cd7a13e271a2ad3","term":"chase","forms":["chase","chases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狩獵；打獵","explanation":"指對野獸或獵物的狩獵過程，也可以泛指為了捕獲獵物而進行的追逐。這裡的“跟在目標後面”具體變成了追捕獵物。","examples":[{"en":"The hunters returned from the chase before sunset.","zh":"獵人們在日落前結束狩獵回來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fox disappeared into the woods during the chase.","zh":"狩獵過程中，那隻狐狸消失在樹林裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caa6edbf77b380f7","term":"chase","forms":["chase","chases","chasing","chased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"追趕；追逐","explanation":"指持續跟在某人或某物後面，想要追上、抓住或趕走它，是記憶鉤子中“跟在目標後面”的核心動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children chased the pigeons across the square.","zh":"孩子們追著鴿子跑過了廣場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chased her hat down the street after the wind blew it away.","zh":"風把她的帽子吹走後，她沿街追趕那頂帽子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31e06f7d89feb99a0e6c","word":"chat","forms":["chat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e408668019930a8","term":"chat","forms":["chat","chats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕鬆交談","explanation":"指不太正式、氣氛輕鬆的談話，通常是朋友或熟人之間聊一會兒。","examples":[{"en":"We had a quick chat after lunch.","zh":"午飯後我們簡短地聊了一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We enjoyed a quiet chat over coffee.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be94ba5513c3ebe2","term":"chat","forms":["chat","chats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"即時文字或語音交流","explanation":"指透過電腦網路即時交換文字或語音，感覺像面對面聊天一樣。","examples":[{"en":"We had a video chat with our cousins last night.","zh":"昨晚我們和表親們進行了影片聊天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our project team keeps a chat open during meetings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba5822a8f9cf06e1","term":"chat","forms":["chat","chats","chatting","chatted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聊天","explanation":"指進行輕鬆、非正式的交談，核心就是和別人隨意地聊一聊。","examples":[{"en":"She chatted with her friend in the café.","zh":"她在咖啡館和朋友聊天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We chatted while waiting for the bus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86bb43fecdd67270","term":"chat","forms":["chat","chats","chatting","chatted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"線上聊天","explanation":"指透過社交媒體、聊天應用或聊天室即時交換文字或語音，像面對面交談一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Do you want to chat online later?","zh":"你晚點想線上聊聊嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They chat online most evenings after school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6f556046e0c00469fe2","word":"cheap","forms":["cheap"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-499abfc29355bbeb","term":"cheap","forms":["cheap","cheaper","cheapest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"價格低的","explanation":"指價格低，買東西或使用服務所需的錢少，是 cheap 最基本、最常用的意思。它只說明花費低，不一定說明東西划算或質量好。","examples":[{"en":"This shop sells fresh vegetables cheap.","zh":"這家店的新鮮蔬菜賣得很便宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a cheap hotel near the station.","zh":"我們找到了車站附近一家價格便宜的酒店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8468470e51272849","term":"cheap","forms":["cheap","cheaper","cheapest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"質量差的","explanation":"指製作粗糙、材料差或看起來不耐用；這裡的重點不是價格本身，而是低價帶來的低質量印象。","examples":[{"en":"The bag looks cheap and will probably break soon.","zh":"這個包看起來很廉價，可能很快就會壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cheap hinges snapped within a week.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a1b45d4778cc8a6e074","word":"cheat","forms":["cheat"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48e0e79f92ed39dd","term":"cheat","forms":["cheat","cheats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"欺騙；欺詐行為","explanation":"指透過隱瞞、虛假資訊或其他不正當手段欺騙別人，或指這種欺騙本身。","examples":[{"en":"The deal turned out to be a cheat designed to take our money.","zh":"這筆交易後來證明是一個騙錢的騙局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The supposed discount was a deliberate cheat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc17fb930820f480","term":"cheat","forms":["cheat","cheats","cheating","cheated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"作弊；違規取利","explanation":"指為了取得優勢而違反考試、比賽或其他活動的規則，例如偷看答案或使用不允許的幫助。","examples":[{"en":"He cheated on the exam by looking at his neighbor's answers.","zh":"他偷看旁邊同學的答案，在考試中作弊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you cheat in this game, you will be disqualified.","zh":"如果你在這場比賽中作弊，就會被取消資格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a5b2cd0d13ed8bc","term":"cheat","forms":["cheat","cheats","cheating","cheated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欺騙；騙取","explanation":"指故意誤導某人，尤其是用不誠實的辦法騙走對方的錢、權利或其他東西。","examples":[{"en":"The salesman cheated me out of my savings.","zh":"那個推銷員騙走了我的積蓄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They cheated customers by hiding the extra fees.","zh":"他們隱瞞額外費用，欺騙了顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20f65c28671b40937c5b","word":"check","forms":["check"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a81ad8708e7aa56","term":"check","forms":["check","checks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檢查，核對","explanation":"對人、事物或結果進行檢查，以確認它是否正確、完整或符合要求；這正是“確認並控制”記憶鉤子中的第一步。","examples":[{"en":"Let's do one final check before we send the report.","zh":"我們發出報告前再最後檢查一遍吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic gave the brakes a careful check.","zh":"修理工仔細檢查了剎車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/check","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fcd5e7fffc4d763f","term":"check","forms":["check","checks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制，制止","explanation":"指對某種力量、行為或發展加以限制，使它不能無限擴大；也就是發現問題後進行控制。","examples":[{"en":"Independent courts provide a check on government power.","zh":"獨立的法院可以制約政府的權力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new rules put a check on excessive spending.","zh":"新規定限制了過度支出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/check","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-186888a7d0802560","term":"check","forms":["check","checks","checking","checked","checkest","checkedst","checketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"檢查","explanation":"按照一定步驟檢視物品、情況或狀態，確認有沒有問題；這正是“先確認”的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please check the door before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請檢查一下門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the address before sealing the envelope.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/check","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c2e9f556bf44abe","term":"check","forms":["check","checks","checking","checked","checkest","checkedst","checketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打勾標記","explanation":"在清單上用勾號或劃掉的方式標記已經選定、處理或確認無誤的專案，把“確認”留下可見的記號。","examples":[{"en":"Check the names of everyone who has arrived.","zh":"請把已經到達的人的名字勾出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I checked off each task as I finished it.","zh":"我每完成一項任務就把它勾掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/check","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c3878832bc188aee2a2","word":"checkup","forms":["checkup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b63731d347251d42","term":"checkup","forms":["checkup","checkups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體檢","explanation":"指按計劃去醫生、牙醫等處做一次健康檢查，重點是確認身體狀況是否正常，並不暗示本人已經生病。","examples":[{"en":"I have a checkup with my dentist next month.","zh":"我下個月要去牙醫那裡做例行檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor said the checkup showed no problems.","zh":"醫生說這次體檢沒有發現問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/checkup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2aa373c574ebd29a","term":"checkup","forms":["checkup","checkups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"例行檢查","explanation":"把同一個“定期檢查一遍”的概念用於汽車、裝置等物品，目的是確認它們執行正常或及時發現隱患。","examples":[{"en":"The truck needs a checkup before the long trip.","zh":"這輛卡車長途出發前需要做一次例行檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dentist recommends a checkup every six months.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/checkup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3549b2a205e694bb3089","word":"cheek","forms":["cheek"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d6720f47151cea6","term":"cheek","forms":["cheek","cheeks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臉頰","explanation":"指眼睛下方、嘴部兩側的柔軟面部區域，也就是通常說的臉頰；它既可以指一邊，也可以泛指臉頰這一部位。","examples":[{"en":"The cold wind made her cheeks turn red.","zh":"冷風吹得她的臉頰變紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wiped a spot of paint from his cheek.","zh":"他擦掉了臉頰上的一小塊油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e9a84533fd836db","term":"cheek","forms":["cheek","cheeks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臀部的一側","explanation":"指臀部左右兩邊的一塊，尤其是短小衣物露出的部分；這個意思通常用複數表示整個臀部。","examples":[{"en":"He slipped on the wet step and landed on one cheek.","zh":"他在溼臺階上滑了一跤，臀部一側著了地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injection went into his left buttock cheek.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19051351bb6df8bf1e98","word":"cheer","forms":["cheer"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d2e326aa030218d","term":"cheer","forms":["cheer","cheers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愉快的精神","explanation":"指一種輕鬆、愉快、積極的精神狀態，也可以指一個人當時的好心情。它是“把心情提起來”這條主線的內在一面。","examples":[{"en":"Despite the bad weather, everyone was in good cheer.","zh":"儘管天氣很糟，大家的心情仍然很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her kindness brought cheer to the whole office.","zh":"她的善意給整個辦公室帶來了愉快的氣氛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d8941ae048ae9f2","term":"cheer","forms":["cheer","cheers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歡呼聲","explanation":"指表達喜悅、贊同或支援的喊聲，通常是多人一起喊出的聲音。它是把內在的好心情透過聲音提起來、傳出去。","examples":[{"en":"Three cheers for the winners!","zh":"為獲勝者歡呼三聲！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tremendous cheer greeted the winning goal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-433d318b2893902f","term":"cheer","forms":["cheer","cheers","cheering","cheered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使高興；使振作","explanation":"指讓某人的心情變好、從低落中振作起來，常常只是帶來一點安慰或好訊息。它是“把心情提起來”作為動作的一面。","examples":[{"en":"I brought her some flowers to cheer her up.","zh":"我給她帶了些花，想讓她振作起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The good news cheered everyone up.","zh":"這個好訊息讓大家的心情都好了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a92fffaf83fb537","term":"cheer","forms":["cheer","cheers","cheering","cheered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"歡呼助威","explanation":"指用喊聲、掌聲或口號為某人、隊伍或運動員加油。這是把支援和熱情透過聲音提起來的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of fans cheered for the home team.","zh":"成千上萬的球迷為主隊加油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd cheered the runners on to the finish line.","zh":"人群一路為跑步者加油，鼓勵他們衝過終點線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9e20626ae2a25e8e6aa","word":"cheerful","forms":["cheerful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4abd17c9724ada5d","term":"cheerful","forms":["cheerful","more cheerful","cheerfuler","cheerfuller","most cheerful","cheerfulest","cheerfullest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愉快樂觀的","explanation":"形容一個人明顯心情愉快、態度開朗，並且習慣用樂觀的眼光看事情；這就是那張“帶著陽光笑容的臉”的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"She stayed cheerful even after a long and tiring day.","zh":"即使忙碌又疲憊了一整天，她仍然保持著愉快樂觀的心情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our cheerful neighbor always greets everyone with a smile.","zh":"我們那位開朗的鄰居總是微笑著向每個人打招呼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheerful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f243bed7ee9fb432","term":"cheerful","forms":["cheerful","more cheerful","cheerfuler","cheerfuller","most cheerful","cheerfulest","cheerfullest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明亮宜人的","explanation":"形容房間、色彩、氣氛等帶有明亮輕快的感覺，能讓人心情愉悅；這是把人的好心情延伸到了周圍環境。","examples":[{"en":"The café has a cheerful room filled with yellow chairs and fresh flowers.","zh":"這家咖啡館有一個明亮宜人的房間，裡面擺著黃色椅子和鮮花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Yellow curtains made the kitchen cheerful even in winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheerful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-873ac9ffea4dd04fa719","word":"cheese","forms":["cheese"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f3480de4ff404da","term":"cheese","forms":["cheese","cheeses","cheesen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乳酪","explanation":"用凝結或培養過的牛奶等乳製成的食品，通常可切片、切塊或融化食用。","examples":[{"en":"We put some cheese on the warm bread.","zh":"我們在熱麵包上放了一些乳酪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soup tastes better with grated cheese.","zh":"這湯加上磨碎的乳酪味道更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheese","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d05f652e5cc054cf","term":"cheese","forms":["cheese","cheeses","cheesen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種乳酪","explanation":"指乳酪的某一個品種或型別，而不是乳酪這種食品的總稱。","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells several local cheeses.","zh":"這家店賣好幾種本地乳酪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This mild cheese melts beautifully on toast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheese","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f59ac0828b9a32293b34","word":"chef","forms":["chef"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8fd7501ddc963b3a","term":"chef","forms":["chef","chefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餐館主廚","explanation":"指餐館或其他餐飲機構中負責廚房、帶領廚師並掌管烹飪工作的主廚，這是現代英語裡最重要的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The chef at this restaurant changes the menu every season.","zh":"這家餐館的主廚每個季節都會更換選單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We asked the chef to recommend a vegetarian dish.","zh":"我們請主廚推薦一道素食菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chef","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d2d5954a0702c7e","term":"chef","forms":["chef","chefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大戶人家的主廚","explanation":"指大型家庭廚房中統領烹飪、安排宴席的負責人；這裡仍然是“廚房裡的領頭人”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The chef of the estate prepared dinner for all the guests.","zh":"這座莊園的主廚為所有客人準備了晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The household chef inspected deliveries before planning the evening menu.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chef","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6850ca355247469531b9","word":"chemical","forms":["chemical"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-214e4d79591c9d97","term":"chemical","forms":["chemical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"化學的；與化學有關的","explanation":"表示和化學這門學科、化學性質或化學過程有關，範圍很廣，不限於實驗室裡的危險物質。","examples":[{"en":"The students carried out a simple chemical experiment in class.","zh":"學生們在課堂上做了一個簡單的化學實驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chemical reaction released enough heat to melt wax.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chemical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de895f48a41316ee","term":"chemical","forms":["chemical","chemicals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化學物質","explanation":"指一種具體的化學元素、化合物或合金，也就是可以被單獨識別的化學成分；它不一定是人工製造的。","examples":[{"en":"The factory tests the chemicals in the water every week.","zh":"這家工廠每週檢測水中的化學物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep cleaning chemicals away from children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chemical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c0826a6f9096b2f2408","word":"chemist","forms":["chemist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11926d7f87c4cc6c","term":"chemist","forms":["chemist","chemists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化學家","explanation":"專門研究化學、物質及其變化的人，通常指受過專業訓練並以此為職業的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is a chemist who studies how medicines react in the body.","zh":"她是一名研究藥物如何在人體內發生反應的化學家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A chemist analyzed the powder recovered from the bottle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chemist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f07d438fc52e9195","term":"chemist","forms":["chemist","chemists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥劑師","explanation":"在英國、澳大利亞、紐西蘭等地，以及部分其他地區的英語中，chemist 可以指配藥、提供藥物諮詢的藥劑師。這裡指的是人，不是賣藥的地點。","examples":[{"en":"Ask the chemist whether this medicine is safe for children.","zh":"問問藥劑師這種藥對兒童是否安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chemist checked the label before handing over my tablets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chemist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de0152f952776f09f537","word":"chemistry","forms":["chemistry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bbf6a5bdb3863a86","term":"chemistry","forms":["chemistry","chemistries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化學；化學科學","explanation":"指研究物質由什麼組成、具有怎樣的結構，以及它們如何發生變化的自然科學。這裡的核心畫面是研究“不同成分相遇後會發生什麼作用”。","examples":[{"en":"She studies chemistry at university.","zh":"她在大學學習化學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chemistry helps us understand how medicines work.","zh":"化學幫助我們理解藥物如何發揮作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chemistry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-870c3b6190d1b948","term":"chemistry","forms":["chemistry","chemistries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"默契；來電","explanation":"指兩個人之間自然產生的吸引力、協調感和默契，好像彼此的“成分”一接觸就產生了良好作用。常用於演員、朋友、搭檔或戀愛物件之間。","examples":[{"en":"The two actors have great chemistry on screen.","zh":"這兩位演員在銀幕上很有默契。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our new team has good chemistry.","zh":"我們新組建的團隊配合得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chemistry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70f31781c0a0488d7d96","word":"cherish","forms":["cherish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa67fb61a219ab09","term":"cherish","forms":["cherish","cherishes","cherishing","cherished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"悉心珍愛","explanation":"指像照料珍貴之物一樣，用關愛和溫柔去養育、保護或照顧某人或某物。重點不只是照料，還包含深厚的感情。","examples":[{"en":"She cherishes her children and protects them fiercely.","zh":"她深愛並悉心保護自己的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They cherished the old tree in their garden.","zh":"他們十分珍愛花園裡的那棵老樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b50f3c45918e7322","term":"cherish","forms":["cherish","cherishes","cherishing","cherished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"珍惜；珍藏在心","explanation":"指把某人、某段關係、某個回憶或某種願望看得非常珍貴，並在心裡長久珍藏。它強調深切的重視和感情，而不一定包含實際照料。","examples":[{"en":"I cherish our friendship more than I can say.","zh":"我對我們的友誼珍視得難以言表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She will always cherish the memory of that summer.","zh":"她永遠會珍藏那個夏天的回憶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2daf0e6c79009f9234ed","word":"cherry","forms":["cherry"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-049208775d216a2f","term":"cherry","forms":["cherry","cherrier","more cherry","cherriest","most cherry"],"pos":"adj","zh":"櫻桃味的；含櫻桃的","explanation":"表示某種食物、飲料或其他東西含有櫻桃，或嚐起來像櫻桃。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered a cherry pie to share.","zh":"我們點了一份櫻桃派一起吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered a cherry milkshake with her sandwich.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b266e78274a02bf","term":"cherry","forms":["cherry","cherrier","more cherry","cherriest","most cherry"],"pos":"adj","zh":"櫻桃紅的","explanation":"表示顏色鮮亮、接近成熟櫻桃的紅色，通常就是“櫻桃紅”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a cherry dress to the party.","zh":"她穿了一條櫻桃紅的裙子去參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He drove a cherry convertible along the seafront.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b83400f3dcebfc2","term":"cherry","forms":["cherry","cherries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"櫻桃","explanation":"一種通常呈紅色、黑色或黃色的小水果，裡面有堅硬的核，果梗較短。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a bag of fresh cherries at the market.","zh":"我在市場買了一袋新鮮櫻桃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to bite the cherry stone.","zh":"小心別咬到櫻桃核。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac739dccd121f71261d8","word":"chess","forms":["chess"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10f0866dec547c06","term":"chess","forms":["chess","chesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國際象棋","explanation":"chess 是兩個人在棋盤上移動各自棋子、設法將死對方王的棋類遊戲；這個詞通常指整項遊戲，而不是某一個棋子。","examples":[{"en":"My grandfather taught me to play chess when I was six.","zh":"我六歲時，祖父教我下國際象棋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She plays chess online every evening.","zh":"她每天晚上都在網上下國際象棋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ca0d7019158ccd92de4","word":"chest","forms":["chest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43098febe02ccf31","term":"chest","forms":["chest","chests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"箱子","explanation":"指有蓋、通常結實而且較大的箱子，用來存放衣物等物品；“能裝東西的凸起容器”是這個詞最直觀的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The old chest was full of winter clothes.","zh":"那個舊箱子裡裝滿了冬衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An iron chest held the ship's navigation charts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-848b6c8990dddc27","term":"chest","forms":["chest","chests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胸部","explanation":"指從頸根到腹部上緣的身體部分，也可指相應動物身體的這一部位；可以把它想成身體前方鼓起的“箱體”。","examples":[{"en":"He felt a sharp pain in his chest and called a doctor.","zh":"他感到胸部一陣劇痛，於是叫了醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He held the sleeping child against his chest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06d92f17a33b28585d90","word":"chestnut","forms":["chestnut"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1680987ec43abbd","term":"chestnut","forms":["chestnut"],"pos":"adj","zh":"栗色的","explanation":"指像栗子外殼那樣的深紅棕色，尤其用於描述頭髮、毛髮或其他外觀。","examples":[{"en":"She has long chestnut hair that shines in the sun.","zh":"她有一頭在陽光下閃閃發亮的栗色長髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The horse had a glossy chestnut coat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf7b9ce09cf98785","term":"chestnut","forms":["chestnut","chestnuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慄樹","explanation":"指慄屬的樹或灌木，也就是結栗子的植物；這是理解其他字面義的起點。","examples":[{"en":"A tall chestnut tree grows beside the old stone wall.","zh":"一棵高大的慄樹長在古老石牆旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An old chestnut shaded the village well.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0024270382ccdfc5","term":"chestnut","forms":["chestnut","chestnuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"栗子","explanation":"指慄樹結的堅果，也可泛指外形或性質相近的這類堅果；這是日常生活中最常見的字面義之一。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a bag of chestnuts and roasted them over the fire.","zh":"我們買了一袋栗子，在火上把它們烤熟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They roasted chestnuts over a small charcoal fire.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3550d5c93f93da8","term":"chestnut","forms":["chestnut","chestnuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"栗色","explanation":"指栗子那樣的深紅棕色，和形容詞義相同，但名詞形式把這種顏色本身當作物件來談。","examples":[{"en":"The painter used chestnut to warm up the background.","zh":"畫家用栗色讓背景顯得更溫暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her hair faded from chestnut to pale brown.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82434ef4d1aa1d1efd91","word":"chew","forms":["chew"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9eb9d3b38efd1f58","term":"chew","forms":["chew","chews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咀嚼動作","explanation":"chew 指用嘴和牙齒反覆咬動的動作，即“咀嚼”；它是動詞 chew 所表示動作的名詞化說法。","examples":[{"en":"I gave the tough piece of meat a careful chew before swallowing.","zh":"我把那塊難嚼的肉仔細咀嚼後才嚥下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Give each mouthful a thorough chew before swallowing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d4879aef17e7efe","term":"chew","forms":["chew","chews","chewing","chewed","chewn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"咀嚼食物","explanation":"chew 表示用牙齒反覆咬動食物，使食物變軟、變碎後再吞下。這是這個詞最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Chew your food slowly before you swallow it.","zh":"把食物慢慢咀嚼後再嚥下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was chewing a piece of bread while reading.","zh":"她一邊看書，一邊嚼著一片面包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4cfb34f4722c837","term":"chew","forms":["chew","chews","chewing","chewed","chewn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反覆思考","explanation":"在非正式語境中，chew 可以表示把問題像食物一樣在腦中反覆“咀嚼”，也就是認真考慮、琢磨。它不是字面上的咬，而是從身體動作自然引申出的思考義。","examples":[{"en":"I need a few days to chew over your proposal.","zh":"我需要幾天時間好好考慮你的提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sat quietly, chewing on the difficult question.","zh":"他安靜地坐著，反覆琢磨那個難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-811eb81b9d11d65a36c5","word":"chicken","forms":["chicken"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d09e446b00fec61","term":"chicken","forms":["chicken","chickens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雞；家雞","explanation":"指人類飼養的雞，尤其可以指還年幼的雞。這個基本義也是其他許多引申義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer keeps chickens in a fenced yard.","zh":"農夫把雞養在有圍欄的院子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some chickens lay eggs almost every day.","zh":"有些雞幾乎每天都下蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicken","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7179f2435e5b59fc","term":"chicken","forms":["chicken","chickens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雞肉","explanation":"指作為食物吃的雞肉，而不是活著的雞。這裡的 chicken 通常把雞肉看作一種食材或菜餚。","examples":[{"en":"We had grilled chicken with rice for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐吃了烤雞肉配米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like some chicken in your soup?","zh":"你的湯裡要不要加點雞肉？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chicken","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9285827b8031a1dbe7d1","word":"chief","forms":["chief"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2bc0af9d0992c76","term":"chief","forms":["chief","chiefer","more chief","chiefest","most chief"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最主要的","explanation":"指在多個原因、人物或事項中最重要、起決定作用的那個，相當於站在最前面的“頭”。","examples":[{"en":"The chief reason for the delay was bad weather.","zh":"延誤的主要原因是天氣惡劣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Safety is our chief concern.","zh":"安全是我們最關心的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3bbeeb70e7b00d3c","term":"chief","forms":["chief","chiefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"首領；負責人","explanation":"指一個部落、組織、公司部門或其他群體中處在最上位、負責帶領大家的人，就是群體的“頭”。","examples":[{"en":"The chief of police spoke to the reporters.","zh":"警察局長向記者發表了講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became the chief of the research team.","zh":"她成了研究團隊的負責人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ddc9e669194254cef019","word":"child","forms":["child"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3a7565ac7eb9407","term":"child","forms":["child","children","childer"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孩子；兒童","explanation":"child最基本的意思是尚未成年的孩子，重點在年齡或社會、法律上的未成年身份，而不只是在說嬰兒。","examples":[{"en":"Every child deserves a safe place to grow up.","zh":"每個孩子都應該有一個安全的成長環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are playing in the garden.","zh":"孩子們正在花園裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/child","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-371ce1c129234aab","term":"child","forms":["child","children","childer"],"pos":"noun","zh":"子女","explanation":"child也可以沿著“從父母那裡生長出來的生命”這一概念，指某人的親生子女，不論這個子女現在是否已經成年。","examples":[{"en":"Their youngest child has just started university.","zh":"他們最小的孩子剛開始上大學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their youngest child now works in another country.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/child","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2d1ba57ddbb39205c04","word":"childhood","forms":["childhood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24c1b126383fd433","term":"childhood","forms":["childhood","childhoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兒童狀態","explanation":"指一個人處於孩子身份、尚未長大的狀態，重點在“作為孩子”這一狀態本身，而不只是某一段時間。","examples":[{"en":"Childhood self-control can affect success later in life.","zh":"童年時期的自控力可能會影響日後的生活成就。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Illness had robbed him of much of his childhood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/childhood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b22bdc53304207b3","term":"childhood","forms":["childhood","childhoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"童年時期","explanation":"指一個人從嬰兒期之後到進入青春期前的那段人生時間，也就是通常所說的童年。","examples":[{"en":"She spent her childhood in a small town by the sea.","zh":"她在海邊的一個小鎮度過了童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent her childhood on a remote sheep farm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/childhood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74d4fb11dc159c3dbda0","word":"childish","forms":["childish"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51458296463d43d5","term":"childish","forms":["childish","more childish","most childish"],"pos":"adj","zh":"幼稚的；不成熟的","explanation":"形容成年人或較大孩子的想法、脾氣和行為還像小孩一樣，缺乏成熟和剋制，通常含有責備意味。","examples":[{"en":"Your childish temper tantrums are not going to change my decision.","zh":"你這種幼稚的大發脾氣不會改變我的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was childish of me to refuse to apologize.","zh":"我拒絕道歉，實在是很幼稚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/childish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26b5f057c71687d78f33","word":"chili","forms":["chili"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b7a6b7f5d13238a","term":"chili","forms":["chili","chilis","chilies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辣椒","explanation":"指辣椒這種帶有刺激性辣味的果實，可以是新鮮的，也可以是乾的，常用於烹飪。它強調的是辣椒這一種食材，而不是已經做好的菜。","examples":[{"en":"Add two chopped chilies to the sauce.","zh":"把兩隻切碎的辣椒加入醬汁中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She grows red chilies in her garden.","zh":"她在花園裡種紅辣椒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chili","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-300ccd61d1202745","term":"chili","forms":["chili"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辣味燉菜","explanation":"這裡的 chili 是一道完整的燉菜，通常把辣椒和肉、豆類等配料一起煮；它從“辣椒帶來辣味”這一核心概念發展而來。","examples":[{"en":"The chili has beans, beef, and tomatoes in it.","zh":"這道辣味燉菜裡有豆子、牛肉和番茄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I made a big pot of chili for dinner.","zh":"我做了一大鍋辣味燉菜當晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chili","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fe5e0a43712f0578500","word":"chill","forms":["chill"],"officialPos":"n./v./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-db72bc8b14a3035c","term":"chill","forms":["chill","more chill","most chill"],"pos":"adj","zh":"微冷的","explanation":"表示溫度有些低、讓人感到涼或冷，但通常不如嚴寒那麼強烈。它保留了 chill 最基本的“冷”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"A chill wind was blowing down the street.","zh":"一陣寒風正沿著街道吹來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A chill wind slipped through the doorway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-569eebc5c190ed44","term":"chill","forms":["chill","more chill","most chill"],"pos":"adj","zh":"放鬆隨和的","explanation":"俚語中表示一個人不緊張、不愛計較、容易相處；它可以看作把“冷”引申成把緊張和壓力降下來的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"My new roommate is really chill.","zh":"我的新室友特別隨和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Just be chill and give her some time.","zh":"放輕鬆，給她一點時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-046e1ad1a6877290","term":"chill","forms":["chill","chills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寒意","explanation":"指令人不舒服、從空氣或環境中感到的涼冷，通常比普通的低溫更強調身體上的寒意。","examples":[{"en":"There was a chill in the air after sunset.","zh":"日落後空氣中帶著寒意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden chill made us reach for our jackets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92765bab7b93b78b","term":"chill","forms":["chill","chills","chilling","chilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變冷","explanation":"表示降低某物的溫度，例如把飲料、食物或容器冷卻；這是動詞最直接的“冷”義。","examples":[{"en":"Chill the juice before serving.","zh":"飲用前把果汁冰鎮一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I chilled the bottles in the fridge.","zh":"我把瓶子放進冰箱冷藏了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e549c93526e3994","term":"chill","forms":["chill","chills","chilling","chilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變冷","explanation":"表示人或物自身逐漸變冷，不強調有人主動把它冷卻；它和名詞的“寒意”屬於同一條核心詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We chilled quickly in the cold wind.","zh":"我們在寒風中很快就冷了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the sauce until it chills to room temperature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-782ffc5a89ec5b3a","term":"chill","forms":["chill","chills","chilling","chilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放鬆；別緊張","explanation":"俚語中表示放鬆下來、不要過度反應或把事情看得太緊張；它把“降溫”變成了降低情緒壓力。","examples":[{"en":"Chill, we still have plenty of time.","zh":"放輕鬆，我們還有很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need to chill out after work.","zh":"下班後我需要放鬆一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0b889633adb992bd412","word":"chilly","forms":["chilly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51b833e4d3c0c40f","term":"chilly","forms":["chilly","chillier","chilliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冷得不舒服的","explanation":"形容天氣、空氣或環境帶著讓人不舒服的寒意，重點是這種冷會影響人的感受。它像一陣鑽進衣服裡的冷風，但不一定表示極其寒冷。","examples":[{"en":"It was a chilly morning, so I wore a jacket.","zh":"那天早晨冷颼颼的，所以我穿了件夾克。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room feels chilly after the rain.","zh":"下雨後房間裡感覺冷颼颼的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chilly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b55ae2ca8d711243","term":"chilly","forms":["chilly","chillier","chilliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到冷的","explanation":"描述人自己感到冷，通常是冷得不舒服、想加衣服或關窗。這裡的寒意落在人的身體感受上，而不是單純說明外界溫度。","examples":[{"en":"I'm getting chilly—could you close the window?","zh":"我有點冷，你能把窗戶關上嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I feel chilly even with this sweater on.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chilly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d88912fd0946113bc92","word":"chimney","forms":["chimney"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8e151e136c2a15c","term":"chimney","forms":["chimney","chimneys","chimnies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煙囪；排煙管","explanation":"建築物中把燃燒產生的煙和氣體向上排出的豎直通道，通常從屋頂伸出可見。","examples":[{"en":"Smoke was coming out of the chimney.","zh":"煙正從煙囪裡冒出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to clean the chimney before winter.","zh":"我們需要在冬天前清掃煙囪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chimney","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a591e02f5d7f5a13","term":"chimney","forms":["chimney","chimneys","chimnies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蒸汽火車煙囪","explanation":"在英國英語中，可指蒸汽機車上把煙氣排到空中的高大煙囪。","examples":[{"en":"The old steam locomotive had a tall chimney.","zh":"那輛老式蒸汽機車有一根高高的煙囪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Black smoke poured from the locomotive's chimney.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chimney","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a318e93f5a443952b2b","word":"chimpanzee","forms":["chimpanzee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1346683a6a194f83","term":"chimpanzee","forms":["chimpanzee","chimpanzees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑猩猩","explanation":"通常意義上的黑猩猩，是生活在非洲森林和草原中的大型類人猿；它與人類親緣關係很近，常因聰明和複雜的社會行為出現在科普或動物紀錄片中。","examples":[{"en":"The chimpanzee used a stick to reach the fruit.","zh":"那隻黑猩猩用一根棍子夠到了水果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chimpanzees live in close-knit social groups.","zh":"黑猩猩生活在關係緊密的群體中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chimpanzee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-003e4e1941935fbb","term":"chimpanzee","forms":["chimpanzee","chimpanzees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑猩猩屬動物的泛稱","explanation":"在較寬泛的分類用法中，chimpanzee 可以指黑猩猩屬的成員，包括有時被單獨稱為倭黑猩猩的動物；這是把同一屬的類人猿放在一起說。","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists use the term chimpanzee for both species in the genus Pan.","zh":"一些科學家用這個詞指代潘屬中的兩個物種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers compare the behavior of chimpanzees and bonobos.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chimpanzee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4beeb72de58b9de8213c","word":"chin","forms":["chin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2595c14a53455a96","term":"chin","forms":["chin","chins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下巴","explanation":"指嘴巴下面、臉部最下方通常向前突出的部位。它是 chin 最基本、最值得先掌握的意義，也構成許多引申義的核心意象。","examples":[{"en":"He rested his chin on his hand and looked out the window.","zh":"他用手託著下巴，望向窗外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut her chin when she fell.","zh":"她摔倒時劃傷了下巴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50c0152c2952082aeaf4","word":"china","forms":["china"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7af663ffd95111d7","term":"china","forms":["china","chinas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓷器；精美瓷製品","explanation":"指堅硬、潔白、較薄而有半透明感的瓷器，尤其常指精美的餐具或裝飾品；這個意思正是把“中國”聯想到瓷器的核心延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a delicate china doll.","zh":"博物館展出了一尊精緻的瓷娃娃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps the fine china for special occasions.","zh":"她把精美瓷器留到特殊場合才使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e89fa810e4746da7","term":"china","forms":["china","chinas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓷制餐具","explanation":"專指用瓷製成的一套餐具或餐桌用品，仍然保留了“China”與瓷器之間的聯想。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the china on the table before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人到達前，請把瓷餐具擺到桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel uses simple white china in its dining room.","zh":"這家酒店的餐廳使用樸素的白色瓷餐具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7cea7305a333d5c9ceb","word":"chip","forms":["chip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80a458bf4db17a22","term":"chip","forms":["chip","chips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碎片；小塊","explanation":"它指從較大的石頭、木頭、玻璃等固體上碎裂或削下來的小塊，正是“切下或碎裂出小塊”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A chip of paint fell from the old door.","zh":"一小片油漆從那扇舊門上剝落下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The carpenter brushed the wood chips off the floor.","zh":"木匠把木屑從地板上掃掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-931d18785a63cef2","term":"chip","forms":["chip","chips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺口；崩掉的一小處","explanation":"它指物體表面因碎掉一小塊而留下的損壞處，所以杯子、瓷磚或傢俱邊緣都可以有一個chip。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small chip in the rim of this bowl.","zh":"這個碗的邊緣有一處小缺口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The table is still usable despite a few chips in the paint.","zh":"儘管漆面有幾處掉漆，這張桌子仍然可以使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-516bf6b813b681db","term":"chip","forms":["chip","chips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"積體電路晶片","explanation":"它指在很小的基片上整合電子電路的部件，也就是通常所說的晶片；這是把“小塊”縮小並整合後的技術義。","examples":[{"en":"A tiny chip controls the temperature in the oven.","zh":"一塊小晶片控制著烤箱的溫度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new phone uses a faster processor chip.","zh":"這部新手機採用了速度更快的處理器晶片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc0c24002766b781","term":"chip","forms":["chip","chips","chipping","chipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"削下一小塊","explanation":"指從物體表面或邊緣弄掉一小塊，使原物出現一個小缺口；這正是“切下或碎裂出小塊”的典型動作。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful not to chip the edge of the glass.","zh":"小心別把玻璃杯邊磕掉一塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A falling branch chipped a piece off the statue.","zh":"一根掉下來的樹枝從雕像上砸掉了一小塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94b4a9f92e452b538dfc","word":"chirp","forms":["chirp"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-848f33a15d8a64a6","term":"chirp","forms":["chirp","chirps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啾啾聲；短促尖聲","explanation":"指鳥、昆蟲等發出的短促而尖細的聲音，也可以指類似的電子提示聲。它就是記憶中那聲突然出現的“啾”。","examples":[{"en":"A soft chirp came from the bushes.","zh":"灌木叢裡傳來一聲輕柔的啾啾聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The phone gave a cheerful chirp when the message arrived.","zh":"訊息到達時，手機發出了一聲歡快的提示音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chirp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d07e80611817581","term":"chirp","forms":["chirp","chirps","chirping","chirped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"啾啾叫；發出短促尖聲","explanation":"指鳥、昆蟲等發出短促尖細的聲音，也可指裝置發出類似聲音。重點是“發出一聲啾”，而不是單純表示大聲或連續叫喊。","examples":[{"en":"The crickets chirped all night outside my window.","zh":"窗外的蟋蟀整夜都在啾啾叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tiny bird chirped from the branch above us.","zh":"一隻小鳥在我們頭頂的樹枝上啾啾叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chirp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7499aced43869b27f505","word":"chocolate","forms":["chocolate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f296b45d32ce0cc","term":"chocolate","forms":["chocolate","chocolates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巧克力食品","explanation":"指用烘烤後研磨的可可豆製成的食品，是 chocolate 最基本的名詞意義；它可以是巧克力塊、巧克力原料或泛指巧克力這種食物。","examples":[{"en":"I bought some chocolate to make cookies.","zh":"我買了一些巧克力來做餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This chocolate has a rich, slightly bitter flavor.","zh":"這種巧克力味道濃郁，帶一點苦味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf83f0f9828551b6247b","word":"choice","forms":["choice"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96e1e9e1fdd975d5","term":"choice","forms":["choice","choices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇；可選擇的機會","explanation":"choice是站在岔路口時“挑哪一條路”的過程或結果，也可以泛指面臨選擇的機會。","examples":[{"en":"You have a choice of three colors for the walls.","zh":"牆面有三種顏色可供你選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had to make a choice before the store closed.","zh":"我們得在商店關門前作出選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6585b270e4f7c9bc","term":"choice","forms":["choice","choices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇權","explanation":"這裡不是指某個具體選項，而是指一個人能不能自己決定、挑選道路的權力。","examples":[{"en":"The storm left us no choice but to turn back.","zh":"暴風雨逼得我們只能返回，別無選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone should have a choice about where to live.","zh":"每個人都應該有權選擇住在哪裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2ceeb551694b777","term":"choice","forms":["choice","choices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選中的東西；選擇結果","explanation":"在岔路口挑定一條路後，那條被挑中的路就是你的choice；因此它可以指一個具體的選項、偏好或決定。","examples":[{"en":"This model is a popular choice for small families.","zh":"這款型號是小家庭很受歡迎的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee's choice surprised even the winning architect.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1be0686a785a469ecfeb","word":"choir","forms":["choir"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f37f0c56bf35f0bf","term":"choir","forms":["choir","choirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合唱團","explanation":"一群經過訓練、一起唱歌的人組成的團體；重點是許多聲音合在一起形成一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The school choir performs at the spring concert.","zh":"學校合唱團在春季音樂會上演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined the choir last year.","zh":"她去年加入了合唱團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f07d989f1acc093b83de","word":"choke","forms":["choke"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7ae151c630c32f8","term":"choke","forms":["choke","chokes","choking","choked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"窒息；被噎住","explanation":"指氣管被食物、異物或煙塵等堵住，因而無法正常呼吸；重點是“通道被卡住”而不是普通咳嗽。","examples":[{"en":"She began to choke on a piece of bread.","zh":"她被一塊麵包噎住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child choked on a small toy.","zh":"那個孩子被一個小玩具堵住了氣管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a5ca09563ace881","term":"choke","forms":["choke","chokes","choking","choked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使窒息；勒住","explanation":"指透過勒壓、堵住氣道等方式讓某人難以呼吸或說話，也可用於衣領等東西太緊而讓人感到喘不過氣。","examples":[{"en":"The tight scarf was choking him.","zh":"那條緊圍巾勒得他喘不過氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The attacker tried to choke the guard.","zh":"襲擊者試圖勒住保安使他窒息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49de7bc82bd33a24","term":"choke","forms":["choke","chokes","choking","choked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"阻礙；抑制","explanation":"把“通道被堵住”的畫面擴充套件到抽象事物：阻礙增長、擴張或進展，也可以因隔絕氧氣而使植物或火熄滅。","examples":[{"en":"Too many regulations can choke small businesses.","zh":"過多的規定可能會限制小企業的發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Weeds choked the young plants in the garden.","zh":"雜草抑制了花園裡幼苗的生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-366993077ce453b4b9b0","word":"cholesterol","forms":["cholesterol"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9c0cf4ea12ee4a6","term":"cholesterol","forms":["cholesterol","cholesterols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膽固醇這種脂質","explanation":"cholesterol 是動物體內的一種脂質，由肝臟合成並在血液中運輸，也是細胞組成和許多生理過程的一部分。醫學語境常關注血液中膽固醇過高與心血管疾病風險的關係。","examples":[{"en":"The liver makes most of the cholesterol in our bodies.","zh":"肝臟會製造我們體內的大部分膽固醇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some foods contain a lot of cholesterol.","zh":"有些食物含有大量膽固醇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cholesterol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f04c029a58df08f0","term":"cholesterol","forms":["cholesterol","cholesterols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膽固醇水平","explanation":"在談論檢查結果、健康狀況或治療目標時，cholesterol 可以指一個人的膽固醇水平，也就是體內這種物質的含量高低。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise can help improve your cholesterol.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於改善你的膽固醇水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her cholesterol dropped after she changed her diet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cholesterol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-725fed9d1ae909982052","word":"choose","forms":["choose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17440c692103d65f","term":"choose","forms":["choose","chooses","choosing","chose","choosed","chosen","choosest","chosest","choosedst","chooseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"挑選；選擇","explanation":"從兩個或多個物件中挑出一個或幾個，重點是實際作出取捨。它可以用於物品、地點、方案或人選。","examples":[{"en":"I chose the blue jacket because it was warmer.","zh":"我選了那件藍色夾克，因為它更暖和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can choose between tea and coffee.","zh":"你可以在茶和咖啡之間選一種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21c878b45fb90b86","term":"choose","forms":["choose","chooses","choosing","chose","choosed","chosen","choosest","chosest","choosedst","chooseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"決定做；選擇採取","explanation":"在幾種行動可能中決定採用某一種，強調“我決定這樣做”，不一定涉及具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"She chose to stay home and finish her work.","zh":"她決定待在家裡完成工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose to apologize in person.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/choose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5744323314533d2583cc","word":"chop","forms":["chop"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-142946e92e642426","term":"chop","forms":["chop","chops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶骨肉排","explanation":"chop 可以指從動物身上切下、通常還帶著一段骨頭的一塊肉，常見於羊排、豬排等。它體現的是“用力切下的一塊肉”這一主線。","examples":[{"en":"We grilled pork chops with garlic and rosemary.","zh":"我們用大蒜和迷迭香烤了豬排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut the chop away from the bone before eating it.","zh":"她吃之前把肉排從骨頭上切了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbc12581ac0e227e","term":"chop","forms":["chop","chops","chopping","chopped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"切成小塊","explanation":"用短促而有力的連續動作把食物、木頭等切成較小的塊，這正是記憶中“帶力道的短促切斷動作”的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"Chop the carrots into small pieces before adding them to the soup.","zh":"把胡蘿蔔切成小塊後再放進湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chopped some firewood in the backyard.","zh":"她在後院砍了一些柴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7a02985b232c33d","term":"chop","forms":["chop","chops","chopping","chopped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用斧等砍斷","explanation":"用斧頭或類似工具一下下用力砍，使某物，尤其是較粗硬的東西，斷開；這是“帶力道的短促切斷動作”在砍伐場景中的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"They chopped down the dead tree before it fell on the house.","zh":"他們在那棵枯樹倒到房子上之前把它砍倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He chopped off a thick branch with one swing.","zh":"他一揮斧頭就砍掉了一根粗樹枝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7151dcd91b34589d2809","word":"chopstick(s)","forms":["chopsticks"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"chopsticks","forms":["chopsticks","chopstick"],"pos":"n.","zh":"筷子","examples":[{"en":"She picked up a piece of tofu with her chopsticks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"I am learning to use chopsticks without dropping the food.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-25735baaa5b4e4cc238f","word":"chord","forms":["chord"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c6cdf5804419b6f5","term":"chord","forms":["chord","chords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"和絃","explanation":"幾個不同的音同時響起，並且被聽成一個整體，這個整體就是和絃。可以把它想成把分散的音連成一塊聲音。","examples":[{"en":"The pianist played a bright chord at the end of the song.","zh":"鋼琴家在歌曲結尾彈了一個明亮的和絃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She changed the chord just before the singer came in.","zh":"歌手開始演唱前，她換了一個和絃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-643eba5971c54a10","term":"chord","forms":["chord","chords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"弦","explanation":"在幾何中，chord 是曲線上兩點之間的直線段；它把曲線上的兩個點直接連起來，而不是沿著曲線走。","examples":[{"en":"The chord of the circle is shorter than the arc between the same two points.","zh":"這個圓的弦比同樣兩個點之間的弧短。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Draw a chord connecting the two marked points.","zh":"畫一條連線這兩個標記點的弦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87806434b1b0497155db","word":"chore","forms":["chore"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9239a4da51fcd9fd","term":"chore","forms":["chore","chores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家務；日常雜事","explanation":"指為了維持家庭或類似場所正常運轉而需要反覆做的事情，例如打掃、洗碗、洗衣或做飯。它強調這些事情是日常生活中必須輪流承擔的“活兒”。","examples":[{"en":"We take turns doing the chores on weekends.","zh":"我們週末輪流做家務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My son is responsible for the laundry and two other chores.","zh":"我兒子負責洗衣服和另外兩項家務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2909882e76644d51","term":"chore","forms":["chore","chores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麻煩而單調的任務","explanation":"指一件困難、令人不快或重複得讓人厭煩的任務。它不一定是家務，也可以指工作、手續或其他讓人覺得很累贅的事情。","examples":[{"en":"Filling out the same forms every month has become a chore.","zh":"每個月填寫同樣的表格已經變成了一件煩人的差事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sorting years of receipts proved a tedious chore.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca6e99a67a7a8aa26bc0","word":"chorus","forms":["chorus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-417c91e1792e82fa","term":"chorus","forms":["chorus","choruses","chorusses","chori"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合唱團；合唱隊","explanation":"指一起唱歌的一群人，尤其是在音樂劇、歌劇中與獨唱者相對的合唱隊。核心畫面就是許多人把聲音合在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The chorus entered quietly and began to sing behind the soloist.","zh":"合唱隊安靜地上臺，開始在獨唱者身後歌唱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chorus rehearsed in the church every Wednesday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chorus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb399e65d913463f","term":"chorus","forms":["chorus","choruses","chorusses","chori"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一致表達意見的一群人","explanation":"指許多人同時表達相同或相近的看法，像許多聲音匯成一個共同立場。","examples":[{"en":"More scientists joined the chorus calling for faster action on climate change.","zh":"更多科學家加入了呼籲加快應對氣候變化的一致聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A chorus of residents demanded safer pedestrian crossings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chorus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-883b51b2dbe12475","term":"chorus","forms":["chorus","choruses","chorusses","chori"],"pos":"noun","zh":"副歌；反覆段","explanation":"指歌曲中夾在各段主歌之間、反覆出現並突出歌曲內容的部分。它仍然是“許多聲音或音樂元素聚在一起後形成的核心段落”。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone in the car sang along to the chorus.","zh":"車裡的每個人都跟著副歌一起唱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone joined in when the chorus returned.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chorus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-238a314cb3737af198eb","word":"chronic","forms":["chronic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ba2653d02f18b9f","term":"chronic","forms":["chronic","more chronic","most chronic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"長期存在的","explanation":"指問題、困境或情緒持續很長時間，始終沒有真正消失。它強調“拖得久”，不單獨說明問題有多嚴重。","examples":[{"en":"The town has been struggling with chronic unemployment for years.","zh":"這個城鎮多年來一直受到長期失業問題的困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chronic anger can damage a person's relationships.","zh":"長期的憤怒可能會損害一個人的人際關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chronic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cce312066300f6de","term":"chronic","forms":["chronic","more chronic","most chronic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慢性的；久治不愈的","explanation":"用於疾病或症狀時，指持續時間很長、反覆出現，或恢復得很慢。它和表示短期、突然發作的概念相對。","examples":[{"en":"She has suffered from a chronic cough since the winter.","zh":"她從冬天開始就一直受到慢性咳嗽的困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular treatment helps people manage chronic pain.","zh":"定期治療能幫助人們控制慢性疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chronic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca20fb682feb5e81bc1a","word":"chubby","forms":["chubby"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c08283fcc34ca1dc","term":"chubby","forms":["chubby","chubbier","chubbiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"略胖而圓潤的","explanation":"形容人的體形像軟乎乎的小糰子，略微超重，顯得圓潤、豐滿而不瘦削。這個詞常比直接說“肥胖”更柔和，但是否討人喜歡要看語境和說話物件。","examples":[{"en":"The chubby boy smiled and waved at us.","zh":"那個圓乎乎的男孩朝我們微笑著揮手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was a chubby child, but she became very slim as a teenager.","zh":"她小時候有些圓潤，但到了青少年時期就變得很苗條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chubby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3d93a77bb29fba5","term":"chubby","forms":["chubby","chubbier","chubbiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"肉嘟嘟的","explanation":"形容身體某個部位含有適量脂肪，呈現圓鼓、柔軟的樣子；最常讓人想到嬰兒圓圓的臉頰。","examples":[{"en":"The baby has such chubby cheeks that everyone wants to kiss them.","zh":"這個寶寶的臉頰肉嘟嘟的，大家都忍不住想親一口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toddler reached out with chubby hands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chubby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c87f68371b28954707e","word":"chunk","forms":["chunk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cff9416680394e2f","term":"chunk","forms":["chunk","chunks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"厚實的一塊","explanation":"指從整體中分離出來的、通常較厚實且形狀不規則的一塊東西，例如木頭、石頭或食物。核心畫面就是一個整體被掰成幾塊。","examples":[{"en":"She cut a large chunk of cheese from the wheel.","zh":"她從整塊乳酪上切下了一大塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old wall fell apart in huge chunks.","zh":"那堵舊牆碎成了幾大塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chunk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-badb8f127e03a5f5c635","word":"church","forms":["church"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e79d6f0cc9cdecb5","term":"church","forms":["church","churches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教堂","explanation":"指基督教徒舉行禮拜的建築或場所，是最直接、最常見的意思；可以把它想成信徒聚集的那棟房子。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small church in the valley.","zh":"山谷裡有一座小教堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We passed the old church on our way home.","zh":"我們回家路上經過了那座老教堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/church","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd08aae43a8d955b","term":"church","forms":["church","churches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基督徒共同體","explanation":"指所有基督徒組成的精神共同體，而不是某一座建築；這就是從“聚集的地方”擴充套件到“聚集的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The Church welcomes people from many different backgrounds.","zh":"基督教會接納來自不同背景的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These worshippers are part of the Church of Christ.","zh":"這些禮拜者屬於基督教會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/church","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0beca1c4f3e61feb51b4","word":"cigar","forms":["cigar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78a9345bbf932c5a","term":"cigar","forms":["cigar","cigars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雪茄","explanation":"一種捲成圓柱形、外面包著菸草葉並用來抽的菸草製品，通常比普通香菸更厚、更完整。","examples":[{"en":"He sat on the porch and smoked a cigar after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，他坐在門廊上抽了一支雪茄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room smelled strongly of cigar smoke.","zh":"房間裡有濃重的雪茄煙味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cigar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bdda87ebc8009dc86073","word":"cigarette","forms":["cigarette"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-62e2aba9b1d65d09","term":"cigarette","forms":["cigarette","cigarettes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香菸","explanation":"一種細小的菸捲，通常把菸草或其他可吸食的物質包在薄紙裡，點燃後吸食。","examples":[{"en":"He went outside to smoke a cigarette.","zh":"他到外面去抽了一支香菸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She offered me a cigarette, but I said no.","zh":"她遞給我一支香菸，但我拒絕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cigarette","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b815843425f6ac6c018e","word":"cinema","forms":["cinema"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bd5b6f500d2e69f","term":"cinema","forms":["cinema","cinemas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電影院","explanation":"指放映電影、供觀眾觀看的電影院，也就是人們坐在銀幕前看電影的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The cinema is just across the street from the restaurant.","zh":"電影院就在餐館的街對面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cinema sells tickets until the final showing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cinema","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f46218e9616baf8","term":"cinema","forms":["cinema","cinemas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電影作品總稱","explanation":"把許多電影作品作為一個整體來談，強調電影這種創作成果，而不是某一家電影院。","examples":[{"en":"She has loved cinema since she was a child.","zh":"她從小就喜歡電影藝術和電影作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course explores Italian cinema of the postwar years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cinema","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e86df1590a54389","term":"cinema","forms":["cinema","cinemas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電影藝術","explanation":"指拍攝電影這門藝術及其表現手法，關注電影如何透過畫面、剪輯和敘事來創作。","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition explores how technology changed the art of cinema.","zh":"這場展覽探討了技術如何改變電影藝術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival celebrates the visual language of cinema.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cinema","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a39178d327e72a92d3b","word":"circle","forms":["circle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ba278510824a4d4","term":"circle","forms":["circle","circles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓（幾何邊界）","explanation":"由平面上所有到同一個中心點距離相等的點組成的幾何圖形；重點是外圍那條邊界線。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a circle with a radius of five centimeters.","zh":"畫一個半徑為五釐米的圓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The points lie on a circle around the center.","zh":"這些點位於圍繞中心的同一個圓上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e003e8694fe293d4","term":"circle","forms":["circle","circles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓形區域；圓盤","explanation":"由圓的邊界和內部組成的整個圓形區域；日常說“一個圓”時常用這個較寬泛的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She placed a small circle of paper under the glass.","zh":"她在玻璃杯下面放了一小片圓形紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sat in a circle on the floor.","zh":"孩子們在地板上圍成一圈坐著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d604121a57cb43ee","term":"circle","forms":["circle","circles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓形；圍成的圈","explanation":"任何近似圓形的形狀，或人、物圍成的圓圈；共同點是形成了環狀的排列。","examples":[{"en":"The students formed a circle around the speaker.","zh":"學生們圍在演講者周圍站成一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a circle of stones around the fire.","zh":"火堆周圍擺著一圈石頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-518fd1e003cdef9f","term":"circle","forms":["circle","circles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圈子；關係群體","explanation":"一群彼此有聯絡、尤其是有共同興趣或身份的人；就像人們圍成一個社交圈。","examples":[{"en":"She has a wide circle of friends in the city.","zh":"她在這座城市有很廣的朋友圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her circle includes several painters and musicians.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10eb1dbf1d448490","term":"circle","forms":["circle","circles","circling","circled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繞著移動","explanation":"沿彎曲路線繞著某個目標移動，像在目標周圍畫圓。","examples":[{"en":"The hawk circled the field before landing.","zh":"那隻鷹在田地上空盤旋了一會兒才降落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporters circled the building looking for an entrance.","zh":"記者們繞著大樓尋找入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-245dff7ffb66b8c4","term":"circle","forms":["circle","circles","circling","circled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包圍","explanation":"從四周圍住某物，使它處在一個封閉或近似封閉的圈中。","examples":[{"en":"A stone wall circles the old garden.","zh":"一堵石牆圍著那座老花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police circled the building to prevent an escape.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d90a9a938debd0f0","term":"circle","forms":["circle","circles","circling","circled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"圈出；用圈標記","explanation":"在文字、圖片或名單上畫圈標出某項，使它從其他專案中顯眼地分離出來。","examples":[{"en":"Circle the answer that best completes the sentence.","zh":"圈出最適合完成這個句子的答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please circle the dates you are available.","zh":"請圈出你有空的日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4666a3f66bc600ad9f11","word":"circuit","forms":["circuit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92ef787497924b0f","term":"circuit","forms":["circuit","circuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繞行一週；一週運動","explanation":"指某物繞著中心或沿著圓形軌道走完一圈，重點是“繞行並完成一週”的動作或過程。","examples":[{"en":"The satellite makes one circuit of the Earth every ninety minutes.","zh":"這顆衛星每九十分鐘繞地球一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The satellite completed another circuit of the planet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28a6c159428f2c4d","term":"circuit","forms":["circuit","circuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電路；閉合電流通路","explanation":"指供電流沿著迴路流動的一組相互連線的電氣部件；它像一條繞回起點的閉合路線，斷開時電流通常無法正常透過。","examples":[{"en":"The switch breaks the circuit when you turn the light off.","zh":"關燈時，開關會斷開電路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineer tested the circuit before installing it.","zh":"工程師在安裝前測試了這條電路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5060d458702a74ce89c","word":"circular","forms":["circular"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b16d80ba94a7723","term":"circular","forms":["circular","more circular","most circular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"圓形的；與圓有關的","explanation":"指形狀是圓的，或內容與圓、圓周有關。這是最直接的“圓環”義。","examples":[{"en":"The building has a circular design.","zh":"這座建築採用圓形設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They sat around a circular table.","zh":"他們圍坐在一張圓桌旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2754d0ea0c0f526c","term":"circular","forms":["circular","more circular","most circular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"環形的；繞圈移動的","explanation":"指某物呈環形，或運動軌跡繞著一箇中心轉圈，而不是直線前進。","examples":[{"en":"The runners completed a circular route around the lake.","zh":"跑步者沿著湖邊的環形路線跑完了一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A circular beam of light moved across the ceiling.","zh":"一道環形光束在天花板上繞圈移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-812970b7af47b456","term":"circular","forms":["circular","more circular","most circular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迴圈論證的；自我回指的","explanation":"指一個說法繞回它自己，把需要證明的結論反過來當作依據，因此看似完整，實際上沒有提供獨立證明。","examples":[{"en":"Saying the rule is fair because it is the rule is circular reasoning.","zh":"說這條規則公平只是因為它就是規則，這是迴圈論證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The argument is circular because its premise assumes its conclusion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-510a60e068117bf45046","word":"circulate","forms":["circulate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70961ff2b279211a","term":"circulate","forms":["circulate","circulates","circulating","circulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迴圈移動","explanation":"指人、物體或某種流體沿著一個範圍、路線或系統不斷移動，形成迴圈。核心畫面是“沿著圓圈或迴路走”。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh air circulates through the building.","zh":"新鮮空氣在大樓內迴圈流通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People began to circulate around the room after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，人們開始在房間裡走動交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-202b422dc731dde2","term":"circulate","forms":["circulate","circulates","circulating","circulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在人群中走動","explanation":"指人在聚會等場合從一個人或一群人身邊走到另一邊，與不同的人交談，像在人群中繞圈傳遞。","examples":[{"en":"She circulated among the guests and introduced herself.","zh":"她在客人中間走動，並逐一作了自我介紹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager circulated between the tables during lunch.","zh":"午餐時，經理在各張桌子之間走動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-379f5f86d7694737","term":"circulate","forms":["circulate","circulates","circulating","circulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳播；傳閱","explanation":"指把訊息、檔案、傳聞或金錢等在許多人之間傳遞，使它們不斷“繞圈”到達更多人手中。","examples":[{"en":"Please circulate the meeting notes to everyone on the team.","zh":"請把會議記錄傳給團隊裡的每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone circulated a false story about the company.","zh":"有人傳播了一則關於這家公司的假訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70f1947047c98353bf96","word":"circulation","forms":["circulation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d237d9880c0cb217","term":"circulation","forms":["circulation","circulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"迴圈流動","explanation":"指某物沿著一條路線移動，最後回到起點，重點是形成一個迴圈的流動過程。","examples":[{"en":"Good circulation of air keeps the room comfortable.","zh":"空氣良好地迴圈流動，能讓房間保持舒適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pump maintains circulation through the heating pipes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-025541de6fb78c86","term":"circulation","forms":["circulation","circulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳播；流通","explanation":"指東西從一個地方或一個人傳到另一個地方或另一個人，形成持續的傳播和流通。","examples":[{"en":"The circulation of false information caused unnecessary concern.","zh":"虛假資訊的傳播引起了不必要的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please stop the circulation of this document until it has been checked.","zh":"這份檔案檢查完畢前，請停止傳閱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac455671cf7f38cfe638","word":"circumstance","forms":["circumstance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24cd94c3f5033dd4","term":"circumstance","forms":["circumstance","circumstances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影響事情的條件","explanation":"指與某個事實或事件有關、並會影響其發展或結果的條件和情形；重點是“圍繞這件事的外在因素”。","examples":[{"en":"The team changed its plan because of the circumstances.","zh":"團隊因為當時的情況改變了計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We must judge her decision in the circumstances.","zh":"我們必須結合當時的情況來判斷她的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circumstance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-179ca5669b11f74f","term":"circumstance","forms":["circumstance","circumstances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生活或經濟狀況","explanation":"指一個人或家庭所處的生活、財產和經濟條件，例如富裕、拮据或舒適的生活處境；這裡的“周圍條件”變成了包圍個人生活的現實處境。","examples":[{"en":"They lived in modest circumstances for many years.","zh":"他們多年來一直過著不寬裕的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their circumstances improved when her father found work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circumstance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acd8d61b6983eb358899","word":"circus","forms":["circus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0fa028abea5f2ff","term":"circus","forms":["circus","circuses","circusses","circi"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬戲團；馬戲演出","explanation":"指由雜技演員、小丑、馴獸員等組成的巡迴表演團體，也可以指他們進行的整場演出。它保留了“在圓形場地中觀看錶演”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The circus will be in town next week.","zh":"馬戲團下週會來到鎮上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were excited to see the circus.","zh":"孩子們很興奮，期待去看馬戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22f2ff319d3c9ac2","term":"circus","forms":["circus","circuses","circusses","circi"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混亂喧鬧的場面","explanation":"比喻某件事引起了像馬戲場一樣吵鬧、擁擠、失控的局面，也可以指一個混亂不堪的地方。這個意思是從“表演場里人多、聲音雜、場面熱鬧”發展出來的。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting turned into a circus when everyone started shouting.","zh":"大家開始吵起來後，會議變得一團糟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The press conference quickly turned into a circus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be385d45dcaf7b6484f2","word":"cite","forms":["cite"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05a09a5edf27d361","term":"cite","forms":["cite","cites","citing","cited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引用原話","explanation":"把書中、文章中或別人說過的話再次說出或寫出，突出內容本身被拿來使用。","examples":[{"en":"The report cites several experts who warned about the risk.","zh":"這份報告引用了幾位曾警告風險的專家的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cited a passage from the novel in her presentation.","zh":"她在演講中引用了小說中的一段話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b600571c01595ec9","term":"cite","forms":["cite","cites","citing","cited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"註明來源","explanation":"列出獲取資訊、詞語或思想的書籍、文章等來源，讓讀者知道材料出自哪裡。","examples":[{"en":"Please cite every source you use in the final paper.","zh":"請在最終論文中註明你使用的每一個來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cite the original study beneath the quotation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e5f6170d4e1f2560ecb","word":"citizen","forms":["citizen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb9614045c17c173","term":"citizen","forms":["citizen","citizens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城市居民；市民","explanation":"指居住在某個城市或城鎮的人，尤其強調他在當地擁有得到法律承認的權利或承擔相應義務。這個義項體現了“屬於一個地方並參與其中”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The citizens of the town voted on the new park.","zh":"這個城鎮的市民投票決定是否修建新公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every citizen should have access to clean water.","zh":"每位市民都應當能夠獲得清潔的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citizen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3b33e8898989ce1","term":"citizen","forms":["citizen","citizens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公民","explanation":"指依法屬於某個國家的人，通常擁有相應的權利，也承擔相應的義務。這是現代英語中最重要的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"She became a citizen after living in the country for ten years.","zh":"她在這個國家生活了十年後成為了公民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Citizens have the right to vote in national elections.","zh":"公民有權在全國選舉中投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citizen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1757d2fb9628c1340a1b","word":"citizenship","forms":["citizenship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1738e7842250ad88","term":"citizenship","forms":["citizenship","citizenships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公民身份；公民資格","explanation":"指一個人依法成為某國公民的身份或資格。這個身份通常與護照、投票權以及對國家的法律歸屬有關，也可以同時屬於多個國家。","examples":[{"en":"She applied for Canadian citizenship after living there for five years.","zh":"她在那裡生活了五年後申請了加拿大公民身份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He holds dual citizenship in France and Brazil.","zh":"他擁有法國和巴西的雙重公民身份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citizenship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11a62c23412b77477a71","word":"city","forms":["city"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a5065bfc5288c01","term":"city","forms":["city","cities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城市","explanation":"city 是比 town 更大的城市聚居地，通常人口、建築、商業和公共服務都較集中。它可以指一座具體城市，也可以泛指城市生活或城市地區。","examples":[{"en":"São Paulo is the largest city in South America.","zh":"聖保羅是南美洲最大的城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Millions of people move to the city every year.","zh":"每年有數百萬人搬到城市裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a613987b35069028","term":"city","forms":["city","cities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"市中心","explanation":"在澳大利亞英語中，the city 常指一座城市的中心商業區，也就是人們購物、辦公和辦事的市中心。","examples":[{"en":"I'm going into the city today to do some shopping.","zh":"我今天要去市中心購物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We caught the train into the city for dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bea359bea8f7d88ecff2","word":"civic","forms":["civic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97764d630d39bd53","term":"civic","forms":["civic","more civic","most civic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"城市或市政的","explanation":"指與城市、城市公共機構或市政生活有關的事物。它關注的是一個城市作為共同生活空間的公共層面，例如公共中心、城市活動或市政服務。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of people gathered at the civic center for the festival.","zh":"成千上萬的人聚集在市民中心參加節日活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city is investing in new civic buildings.","zh":"這座城市正在投資建設新的市政建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3265052d35c23f68","term":"civic","forms":["civic","more civic","most civic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公民責任的","explanation":"指公民身份帶來的權利、義務以及為公共社會負責的態度。它把“城市中的共同生活”進一步延伸到公民應如何參與和履行責任。","examples":[{"en":"Voting is an important civic duty.","zh":"投票是一項重要的公民責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Jury service forms part of our civic responsibilities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1272dcc42dbfeb2af89e","word":"civil","forms":["civil"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-997b360b7e1ed271","term":"civil","forms":["civil","more civil","civiler","most civil","civilest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公民社會或政府事務的","explanation":"指與普通公民、政府公共事務有關，而不是軍事或宗教事務的。它體現的是“公民社會如何運作”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She joined the civil service after graduating from university.","zh":"她大學畢業後加入了公務員隊伍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The army handed control back to the civil authorities.","zh":"軍隊把控制權交還給了文職當局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35f398c487b80295","term":"civil","forms":["civil","more civil","civiler","most civil","civilest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"禮貌而剋制的","explanation":"形容人在爭執或緊張場合仍保持理性、客氣，不表現出敵意。它更接近“保持基本禮貌”，不一定表示親切或友好。","examples":[{"en":"Please try to be civil during the meeting.","zh":"請儘量在會議期間保持禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Although they disagreed, they remained civil to each other.","zh":"雖然意見不同，他們對彼此仍保持了禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":3,"counts":{"111":2,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-748f556ff0b046ce31fa","word":"civilian","forms":["civilian"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bad4a05253f89911","term":"civilian","forms":["civilian"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平民的；非軍警等職業的","explanation":"指不屬於軍隊、警察或其他政府特殊職業的，或與這類職業相對的平民性質。核心畫面是脫下制服、回到普通社會生活中。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers changed into civilian clothes before leaving the base.","zh":"士兵們離開基地前換上了便服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy is meant to protect civilian workers.","zh":"這項新政策旨在保護平民工作人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civilian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fdb33ffb91ee0c11","term":"civilian","forms":["civilian","civilians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平民","explanation":"指不在軍隊服現役的人，廣義上也指不屬於軍警等特殊職業的普通社會成員。它和 adjective 用法共享同一畫面：沒有穿制服、不是執行特殊任務的那一方。","examples":[{"en":"Several civilians were injured when the building was hit.","zh":"大樓遭到襲擊時，幾名平民受了傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After ten years in the army, he found civilian life difficult.","zh":"在軍隊待了十年後，他覺得平民生活很難適應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civilian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6b15713240e87af20429","word":"civilization","forms":["civilization"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c77bfdccef1c03cb","term":"civilization","forms":["civilization","civilizations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文明；文明社會","explanation":"指由許多共同體組成、具有組織結構和一定政治、社會或技術發展水平的文化社會，也可以指這樣一種社會發展階段或體系。它既能說一個具體歷史文明，也能概括某種社會形態。","examples":[{"en":"The Maya civilization developed a complex calendar.","zh":"瑪雅文明發展出了複雜的歷法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several ancient civilizations flourished along the river.","zh":"幾種古代文明曾沿著這條河繁榮發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civilization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5af365e9bffdd323","term":"civilization","forms":["civilization","civilizations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人類社會；文明社會","explanation":"泛指人類共同生活所形成的社會世界，尤其強調有組織的社會生活；離開這種社會的人，可能會被描述為遠離文明。這裡不一定指某一種具體文化。","examples":[{"en":"After years in the forest, she found it difficult to return to civilization.","zh":"在森林裡生活多年後，她覺得很難重新適應人類社會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruins remind us how fragile civilization can be.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/civilization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35ef9d54eb00cf588561","word":"civilize","forms":["civilize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"civilize","forms":["civilize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使文明化；使較有禮貌","examples":[{"en":"The reformers believed education could civilize society.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"He joked that table manners might civilize his noisy guests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd1b3c312cf7d8161303","word":"claim","forms":["claim"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e72cd4281136c354","term":"claim","forms":["claim","claims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"所有權主張","explanation":"指某人提出自己擁有某物，或認為某物應歸自己所有的要求；重點是“站出來主張擁有”。","examples":[{"en":"She made a claim to the family business after her father's death.","zh":"父親去世後，她提出了對家族企業的所有權主張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two cousins asserted a claim to the land.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-690717f25e565f3c","term":"claim","forms":["claim","claims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未經證實的說法","explanation":"指有人提出一個新的事實判斷，但尚未提供足夠證據，或其真實性仍有爭議。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper published claims of corruption but offered little evidence.","zh":"這家報紙刊登了腐敗指稱，但沒有提供多少證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The advertisement's claim lacked any scientific evidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b261c9270157231","term":"claim","forms":["claim","claims","claiming","claimed","claimest","claimedst","claimeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"主張擁有","explanation":"指聲稱某物屬於自己，或堅持自己擁有某種權利；這是“站出來說這是我的”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Two companies claim ownership of the same patent.","zh":"兩家公司都聲稱擁有同一項專利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She claims the copyright to every illustration in the book.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51ed6c6c7e72df94","term":"claim","forms":["claim","claims","claiming","claimed","claimest","claimedst","claimeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聲稱某事為真","explanation":"指提出一個新的事實說法，通常還沒有給出足夠證據證明它是真的。","examples":[{"en":"The company claims that its new filter removes all harmful chemicals.","zh":"這家公司聲稱其新型過濾器能去除所有有害化學物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He claims he never received the original invoice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09f20eb14937cacb327f","word":"clam","forms":["clam"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1af8aededc0a0d3","term":"clam","forms":["clam","clams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛤蜊；蛤類","explanation":"一種有兩片貝殼的雙殼貝類，許多種類可以食用；在海鮮或海灘語境中通常就是指蛤蜊。","examples":[{"en":"We found dozens of clams buried in the wet sand.","zh":"我們在溼沙裡找到幾十只蛤蜊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant serves clams with garlic and white wine.","zh":"這家餐館供應用大蒜和白葡萄酒烹製的蛤蜊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-530ed40c7ae86639","term":"clam","forms":["clam","clams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美元","explanation":"美國俚語中指一美元，複數可泛指錢。","examples":[{"en":"Those concert tickets cost me fifty clams.","zh":"那些音樂會門票花了我五十美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs cost me fifty clams.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8cceaf5c89e63591aea2","word":"clap","forms":["clap"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bde63f767a24d825","term":"clap","forms":["clap","claps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拍手聲；拍擊","explanation":"clap 可以指兩隻手或兩個表面碰在一起的動作，也可以指由此產生的一聲清脆響聲。它是整組詞義的核心：先有“啪地碰撞”，再引申出鼓掌和各種拍擊。","examples":[{"en":"He called the dog with a loud clap.","zh":"他用一聲響亮的拍手聲把狗叫了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The door shut with a sharp clap.","zh":"門啪的一聲關上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-788ba76a58c6a4d9","term":"clap","forms":["clap","claps","clapping","clapped","clapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拍手","explanation":"作動詞時，clap 最基本的意思是拍手，使兩隻手碰撞併發出清脆聲音。它是“啪地碰在一起”這一核心畫面的直接動作表達。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone clapped along with the song.","zh":"大家都跟著歌曲打拍子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children clapped their hands excitedly.","zh":"孩子們興奮地拍著手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6d540c96cacc963","term":"clap","forms":["clap","claps","clapping","clapped","clapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鼓掌","explanation":"clap 也表示為表演者或發言者鼓掌，是日常英語中表達讚賞的常用動詞。它仍然透過“拍手”這一動作表達支援或認可。","examples":[{"en":"The audience clapped for the young singer.","zh":"觀眾為那位年輕歌手鼓掌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone clapped when she finished speaking.","zh":"她講完話時，大家都鼓起了掌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c010d5892545f57eb436","word":"clarify","forms":["clarify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1bb3d89c28b57a63","term":"clarify","forms":["clarify","clarifies","clarifying","clarified","clarifiest","clarifiedst","clarifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解釋清楚","explanation":"把原本含糊、容易誤解的意思或情況說明白，從而消除疑問；這是現代英語中最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could you clarify what you meant in your email?","zh":"你能解釋一下你在郵件裡是什麼意思嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager clarified the new travel policy for the team.","zh":"經理向團隊說明了新的出差政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clarify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-053873bd31b6b184","term":"clarify","forms":["clarify","clarifies","clarifying","clarified","clarifiest","clarifiedst","clarifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"澄清液體","explanation":"把酒、油、糖漿等液體中的雜質或渾濁成分去掉，使它變得清亮；也可以表示液體自行變清。","examples":[{"en":"This filter helps clarify the cooking oil.","zh":"這個濾網有助於澄清食用油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used egg whites to clarify the stock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clarify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-261b152862d1d6140144","word":"clarity","forms":["clarity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-382a842f036af7b8","term":"clarity","forms":["clarity","clarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"清晰程度","explanation":"指事物呈現得清楚、明白的狀態或程度，可以說視覺上清楚，也可以說思想或表達清楚。它是這個詞最基本的概念，其他意思都像是把“霧散開”延伸到不同領域。","examples":[{"en":"The mountain lake appeared with remarkable clarity after the rain.","zh":"雨後，山間的湖泊顯得格外清澈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She remembered the dream with surprising clarity.","zh":"她對那個夢記得異常清晰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2da508ec3cd8c9fd","term":"clarity","forms":["clarity","clarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"易於理解","explanation":"指說話、寫作或說明讓人一聽就懂、一讀就明白的程度。這裡的“清楚”主要針對資訊的表達方式，而不是資訊本身是否真實。","examples":[{"en":"The instructions need more clarity before we send them to customers.","zh":"這些說明在發給顧客前還需要寫得更清楚一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her presentation was praised for its clarity.","zh":"她的演講因表達清楚而受到稱讚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15a5a49734b740ad0226","word":"clash","forms":["clash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20f4356eee704c71","term":"clash","forms":["clash","clashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碰撞聲","explanation":"指金屬、鍋碗等物體撞在一起時發出的響亮而刺耳的聲音，是“撞在一起”這一核心畫面的直接體現。","examples":[{"en":"A loud clash came from the garage.","zh":"車庫裡傳來一聲巨響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A clash of cymbals ended the performance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-616fed115fa53baa","term":"clash","forms":["clash","clashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"武力衝突","explanation":"指兩方發生短暫或區域性的敵對交鋒；雙方像物體一樣猛烈“撞上”，但這裡撞上的是人或隊伍。","examples":[{"en":"Several clashes broke out between protesters and police.","zh":"示威者和警方之間爆發了幾次衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several soldiers were injured in the border clash.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbbbd9fb79667d04","term":"clash","forms":["clash","clashes","clashing","clashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出碰撞聲","explanation":"指物體相撞而發出響亮的聲音，是“撞在一起”這一核心畫面的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The cymbals clashed at the end of the song.","zh":"歌曲結束時，鈸發出一聲碰撞聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Steel blades clashed as the fighters met.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae94dae07705540b","term":"clash","forms":["clash","clashes","clashing","clashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發生激烈衝突","explanation":"指人群、團體或支援不同一方的人發生激烈對抗，把人與人之間的敵對行為看成正面相撞。","examples":[{"en":"Rival fans clashed outside the stadium.","zh":"rival球隊的球迷在體育場外發生了衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Protesters clashed with police outside the courthouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4daa258350543c622ef","word":"clasp","forms":["clasp"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b87b251aeb7411f8","term":"clasp","forms":["clasp","clasps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"扣件；搭扣","explanation":"指用互相扣合的部分把東西固定在一起的裝置，例如項鍊、手鐲或包上的扣子；它就是“把兩端扣住”的那一部分。","examples":[{"en":"I can't open the clasp on this bracelet.","zh":"我打不開這條手鍊的搭扣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The necklace has a small silver clasp.","zh":"這條項鍊有一個小銀扣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1b42e085154a711","term":"clasp","forms":["clasp","clasps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緊握；擁抱","explanation":"指緊緊握住某人的手，或以擁抱的方式緊緊抱住；畫面仍然是“把對方牢牢握在一起”。","examples":[{"en":"She welcomed me with a warm clasp of the hand.","zh":"她熱情地握住我的手歡迎我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strength of his clasp reassured the frightened passenger.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85639d5f87424c7c","term":"clasp","forms":["clasp","clasps","clasping","clasped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緊緊握住；抱住","explanation":"指用手緊緊抓住、握住或抱住某人或某物；例如 clasp hands 就是讓兩隻手緊緊握在一起。","examples":[{"en":"They clasped hands before saying goodbye.","zh":"他們在道別前緊緊握了握手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He clasped his daughter in his arms.","zh":"他把女兒緊緊抱在懷裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30e92185b3b005a1","term":"clasp","forms":["clasp","clasps","clasping","clasped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"扣緊；扣合","explanation":"指把兩個部分扣在一起，或使它們像用扣件一樣合攏；重點是讓東西牢牢固定在一起。","examples":[{"en":"She clasped the two ends of the necklace together.","zh":"她把項鍊的兩端扣在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clasp the bracelet before pulling on your gloves.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0889113e04d3203f0c40","word":"class","forms":["class"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a95061be17627d29","term":"class","forms":["class","classes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"類別；一組相似事物","explanation":"class 可以是按共同特徵歸在一起的一組人或物，也就是一個類別。這個最基本的“分組”概念也連線到班級、艙位和其他專業分類。","examples":[{"en":"This phone belongs to a different class of devices.","zh":"這部手機屬於另一類裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both paintings are in the same class.","zh":"這兩幅畫屬於同一類別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/class","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d5eea7527dd3ac9","term":"class","forms":["class","classes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會階層","explanation":"class 也指按財富、職業或社會地位形成的人群分層，例如上層、中產階層和工人階層。這裡的“分組”不是課堂分組，而是社會結構中的層次。","examples":[{"en":"Her family moved into the middle class over two generations.","zh":"她的家庭經過兩代人的努力進入了中產階層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel explores tensions between different social classes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/class","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e4e09d7ce9dbeb4","term":"class","forms":["class","classes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"班級；一群一起上課的學生","explanation":"class 可以指在固定時間跟同一位老師上課的學生群體，也就是一個班。這裡仍然是“被分在一起的一組人”。","examples":[{"en":"Our class stayed after school to finish the project.","zh":"我們班放學後留下來完成了專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The class became quiet when the teacher entered.","zh":"老師進來時，全班安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/class","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b002a634647c3350c37b","word":"classic","forms":["classic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46a7ef514fdf34e9","term":"classic","forms":["classic","more classic","most classic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"典型的；典範的","explanation":"指某個例子非常符合一類事物的特點，甚至可以作為這類事物的代表；它不一定真的很優秀，重點是“很典型”。","examples":[{"en":"That is a classic example of poor planning.","zh":"那是計劃不周的典型例子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He made the classic mistake of ignoring the instructions.","zh":"他犯了一個常見的典型錯誤：忽略了說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5e1016d006c8bf9","term":"classic","forms":["classic","more classic","most classic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"經久不衰的；經典的","explanation":"指作品雖然可能並不古老，卻因質量高、影響持久而一直受到認可，成為值得反覆欣賞的經典。","examples":[{"en":"Many people consider this film a classic.","zh":"許多人認為這部電影是經典之作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel remains a classic because its characters still feel real.","zh":"這部小說仍是經典，因為其中的人物至今仍讓人覺得真實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f181d12ad6f1fdf","term":"classic","forms":["classic","classics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"典範；經典範例","explanation":"指某種風格或類別中很早期、很完美或最具代表性的例子；它可以是作品，也可以是某種設計或做法。","examples":[{"en":"This chair is a classic of modern design.","zh":"這把椅子是現代設計的典範。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His speech was a classic of political understatement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71216b607cdae58d","term":"classic","forms":["classic","classics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經典作品","explanation":"指電影、書、歌曲等具有持久價值、長期受到欣賞的藝術作品；不要求作品來自古代。","examples":[{"en":"The song has become a classic among jazz fans.","zh":"這首歌已經成為爵士樂迷心中的經典。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her next book became an instant classic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25d9548a80c751e28218","word":"classical","forms":["classical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42697b269b7375ea","term":"classical","forms":["classical","more classical","most classical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"經典的；一流典範的","explanation":"指在文學、藝術等領域被視為高水平、值得長期學習或模仿的作品、風格或人物。它強調“成為典範”，不只是年代久遠。","examples":[{"en":"She enjoys reading classical literature.","zh":"她喜歡閱讀經典文學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film has become a classical example of suspense.","zh":"這部電影已經成為懸疑作品的經典範例。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f07998dd7f374c47","term":"classical","forms":["classical","more classical","most classical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古希臘羅馬的；古典時代的","explanation":"指古希臘、古羅馬及其文學、藝術、歷史和相關地點，尤其指這些文明中最重要、最具典範性的時期和作品。","examples":[{"en":"She is taking a course in classical Greek history.","zh":"她正在學習古希臘歷史課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displays classical sculptures from Rome.","zh":"博物館展出了來自古羅馬的古典雕塑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f0c8aa526579f4dbde0","word":"classification","forms":["classification"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff1f3308795fdf0c","term":"classification","forms":["classification","classifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分類；分類體系","explanation":"指根據共同的特徵、關係或屬性，把事物分成不同類別的過程；也可以指這樣形成的類別安排或分類體系。想象把許多東西放進不同格子裡，決定“哪些放在一起、哪些分開”的規則就是 classification。","examples":[{"en":"The classification of animals is based on their shared characteristics.","zh":"動物的分類依據它們共同的特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This library uses a clear classification system for its books.","zh":"這家圖書館用一套清晰的分類體系整理書籍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc1f263d32b8ed4a3a77","word":"classify","forms":["classify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c41bbd485f2852b","term":"classify","forms":["classify","classifies","classifying","classified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分類；歸類","explanation":"按照某種標準把人、物、詞語或行為放進不同類別中，就像給它們貼上類別標籤。","examples":[{"en":"The museum classifies its paintings by period and style.","zh":"這家博物館按年代和風格給畫作分類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people classify this book as a mystery novel.","zh":"許多人把這本書歸類為懸疑小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b50a0c317a8032ed","term":"classify","forms":["classify","classifies","classifying","classified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"定為機密","explanation":"把資訊、檔案等正式標記為不能公開的機密內容，相當於給它貼上“秘密”標籤。","examples":[{"en":"The agency classified the report after the investigation.","zh":"調查結束後，該機構將這份報告定為機密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Officials classified the satellite images, preventing newspapers from printing them.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66f9b98dde76ccbaceba","word":"classmate","forms":["classmate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10caf51c671303da","term":"classmate","forms":["classmate","classmates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同班同學","explanation":"指和自己在同一個班級裡學習的學生，重點是“同一個班”，不只是同校。","examples":[{"en":"I ran into an old classmate at the library yesterday.","zh":"我昨天在圖書館偶遇了一位老同學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My classmate helped me prepare for the exam.","zh":"我的同班同學幫我準備了考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classmate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d96e17fd46eb91085fe","word":"clause","forms":["clause"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-67560033c16b0b87","term":"clause","forms":["clause","clauses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"從句；分句","explanation":"指包含主語和謂語的一組詞，可以獨立構成句子，也可以嵌在更大的句子中。它像一個被邊界圈起來的語言單位。","examples":[{"en":"The sentence contains two clauses joined by “and.”","zh":"這個句子包含兩個由“and”連線的從句。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The opening clause gives the reason for the decision.","zh":"開頭的從句說明了作出這一決定的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3662c941e5b960e7","term":"clause","forms":["clause","clauses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨立或從屬從句","explanation":"這裡特別強調從句能否表達完整意思：能獨立表達完整意思的是 independent clause，不能獨立使用、必須依附於其他部分的是 dependent clause。兩者都屬於被邊界圈出的語言單位。","examples":[{"en":"Because it was raining is a dependent clause, not a complete sentence.","zh":"“Because it was raining”是從屬從句，不是完整句子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Underline the subordinate clause in the second sentence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06deac5b8d4a128e257b","word":"claw","forms":["claw"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a83dc76f3704e230","term":"claw","forms":["claw","claws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的爪","explanation":"指哺乳動物、爬行動物或鳥類腳趾末端彎曲而尖的硬質部分。這個最基本的形象也是其他許多義項的來源。","examples":[{"en":"The cat extended its claws when it saw the dog.","zh":"貓看到那條狗時伸出了爪子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eagle's claws were strong enough to carry a fish.","zh":"這隻鷹的爪子強壯得足以抓起一條魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11d8800a867c00d6","term":"claw","forms":["claw","claws","clawing","clawed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓撓；撕抓","explanation":"指用爪或手指反覆抓、撓或撕扯某物，動作通常比普通的 scratch 更有力、更急切。","examples":[{"en":"The frightened cat clawed at the door.","zh":"受驚的貓不停地抓撓房門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child clawed the paint off the wall.","zh":"那個孩子用手把牆上的油漆抓掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cfa344848240898","term":"claw","forms":["claw","claws","clawing","clawed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用爪抓住","explanation":"指動物用爪把目標牢牢抓住；也可形容人費力地抓住某物，核心仍是“像爪一樣扣住”。","examples":[{"en":"The hawk clawed the rabbit and carried it away.","zh":"那隻鷹用爪抓住兔子，把它帶走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat clawed the curtain to steady itself.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/claw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06363555054de198a87c","word":"clay","forms":["clay"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2062a1fac82e2b6","term":"clay","forms":["clay","clays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黏土；陶土","explanation":"clay 是溼潤時可以塑形、燒製後可做陶器的一類細密土質材料，是這個詞最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children made small animals from clay.","zh":"孩子們用黏土捏了些小動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This bowl is made of baked clay.","zh":"這個碗是用燒製的陶土做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da0b7e4afe9cadc8","term":"clay","forms":["clay","clays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紅土網球場","explanation":"在網球語境中，clay 指由碎石、磚或其他鬆散礦物鋪成的紅土場地，而不是一小塊黏土。","examples":[{"en":"She plays best on clay.","zh":"她在紅土場上發揮得最好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tournament is held on clay courts.","zh":"這項賽事在紅土場地上舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b066804f6d1d077173c","word":"clean","forms":["clean"],"officialPos":"adj./v./adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3250dcc07de9eba1","term":"clean","forms":["clean","cleaner","cleanest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"乾淨的","explanation":"去掉灰塵、汙漬和雜質後，東西看起來或摸起來不髒；這正是“去掉雜質、恢復清爽”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the clean plates on the table.","zh":"請把乾淨的盤子放到桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children changed into clean clothes after playing outside.","zh":"孩子們在外面玩後換上了乾淨的衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad7dd396a9dd880a","term":"clean","forms":["clean","cleaner","cleanest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"完全地","explanation":"表示某個動作一直進行到底、完全穿過或徹底達到結果；這是“把障礙全部去掉”的程度引申。","examples":[{"en":"The nail went clean through the thin board.","zh":"釘子完全穿透了那塊薄木板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ball flew clean over the fence.","zh":"球直接飛過了圍欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa523b86e0537e29","term":"clean","forms":["clean","cleans","cleaning","cleaned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"清潔，擦乾淨","explanation":"沿著“去掉雜質，讓東西恢復清爽”的核心畫面，clean 表示清除物品或地方上的灰塵、汙漬等，使其變乾淨。","examples":[{"en":"I clean the kitchen every evening.","zh":"我每天晚上打掃廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please clean your shoes before coming inside.","zh":"進來之前請把鞋子擦乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13535c92204c2e18","term":"clean","forms":["clean","cleans","cleaning","cleaned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"整理，收拾整齊","explanation":"這裡仍然是“去掉雜質”的畫面，不過去掉的是雜亂物品；clean 表示把房間、桌面等收拾得整潔有序。","examples":[{"en":"The children cleaned their room before dinner.","zh":"孩子們在晚飯前把房間收拾整齊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cleaned the table and put the books away.","zh":"她收拾了桌子，把書放了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11336bc0d91358ca2d11","word":"cleaner","forms":["cleaner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d9efbeb835231e3","term":"cleaner","forms":["cleaner","cleaners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"清潔工","explanation":"指以打掃房間、地面、窗戶等為工作的人，是“讓東西變乾淨的人”這一核心概念的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The cleaner comes in twice a week to do the floors.","zh":"清潔工每週來兩次清掃地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hired a cleaner after moving into the new house.","zh":"搬進新房子後，我們僱了一名清潔工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cleaner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-913a4cb91be20332f355","word":"clear","forms":["clear"],"officialPos":"adj./v./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d8908ec1c787241","term":"clear","forms":["clear","clearer","clearest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"透明的","explanation":"把遮擋物拿開後，光線可以穿過，東西看起來透明而清澈。","examples":[{"en":"The lake was so clear that we could see the stones on the bottom.","zh":"湖水清澈得能看見水底的石頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched fish swimming through the clear water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f36018561d79ea0a","term":"clear","forms":["clear","clearer","clearest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清楚易懂的","explanation":"把疑惑拿開後，意思、說明或表達沒有歧義，別人容易理解。","examples":[{"en":"Please give me clear instructions before I start the job.","zh":"請在我開始工作前給我清楚的指示。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made it clear that she would not change her decision.","zh":"她明確表示不會改變自己的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b73069d32d8aed25","term":"clear","forms":["clear","clears","clearing","cleared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"清除障礙","explanation":"把道路、房間或其他地方的實體障礙拿開，使其暢通或可用。","examples":[{"en":"The workers cleared the fallen branches from the road.","zh":"工人們清除了路上的落枝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you clear the entrance before the guests arrive?","zh":"客人到達前，你能把入口清理出來嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9423ccd277d1a914","term":"clear","forms":["clear","clears","clearing","cleared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"澄清疑問","explanation":"把問題中的疑惑和歧義拿開，使事實、意思或責任變得清楚。","examples":[{"en":"I called her to clear up a misunderstanding.","zh":"我給她打電話是為了澄清一個誤會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report cleared up several questions about the project.","zh":"這份報告澄清了幾個關於該專案的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-213f67768585260948e5","word":"clearance","forms":["clearance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ff56433deb9f1b0","term":"clearance","forms":["clearance","clearances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"清除；清空出的空間","explanation":"指清除障礙、物品或人員的行為，也可指清除之後空出來的地方。重點不是“洗乾淨”，而是把東西移走，使空間變得暢通。","examples":[{"en":"The clearance of the old warehouse took three days.","zh":"清空那座舊倉庫用了三天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road is closed for snow clearance.","zh":"這條路因清除積雪而封閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clearance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dadaf7f9b5c9001d","term":"clearance","forms":["clearance","clearances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"間隙","explanation":"指兩個運動物體、尤其是機器部件之間必須保留的距離。可以把它看成“清開”的安全空間，距離太小就可能相撞或摩擦。","examples":[{"en":"The gears need a small clearance between their teeth.","zh":"這些齒輪的齒之間需要留出一小段間隙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the clearance before the wheels start turning.","zh":"車輪開始轉動前要檢查間隙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clearance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23a76f91b27fecc2","term":"clearance","forms":["clearance","clearances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"淨空；可透過的高度或寬度","explanation":"指隧道、橋下或其他通道能容許車輛和物體透過的高度或寬度，也可指車輛與頂部、側壁之間的距離。它就是“清出一條能透過的空間”。","examples":[{"en":"This truck is too tall for the bridge's clearance.","zh":"這輛卡車太高，橋下的淨空容不下它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave enough clearance for the gate to open.","zh":"要留出足夠的空間讓大門開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clearance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4a78e88a22116d8","term":"clearance","forms":["clearance","clearances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通行許可","explanation":"指車輛、飛機或人員獲准繼續前進或出行的許可。原本是把道路或程式“清出來”，所以引申為“放行”。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot waited for clearance to take off.","zh":"飛行員等待起飛許可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We cannot enter until we get security clearance.","zh":"我們得到安全許可後才能進入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clearance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c40dc72b0228e5850d8b","word":"clerk","forms":["clerk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cfd9536c22a908e5","term":"clerk","forms":["clerk","clerks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職員；文員","explanation":"指以處理記錄、賬目、檔案、信件等事務為主要工作的人，通常譯為“職員”或“文員”。這個詞強調文書和事務性工作，不專指某一種行業。","examples":[{"en":"The clerk filed the invoices before leaving the office.","zh":"那名職員離開辦公室前把發票歸檔了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please ask the clerk at the front desk for a visitor badge.","zh":"請向前臺職員索取訪客證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clerk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e895c323cc786e17547","word":"clever","forms":["clever"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d27568344aa0c3e9","term":"clever","forms":["clever","cleverer","more clever","cleverest","most clever"],"pos":"adj","zh":"手巧；動作靈活","explanation":"指使用雙手或身體做事很靈巧，尤其適合需要手藝、準確動作或協調性的工作。這個意思像是“手也很會思考”，強調實際操作能力。","examples":[{"en":"My dad is clever with his hands and can repair almost anything.","zh":"我爸爸手很巧，幾乎什麼東西都會修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is clever with scissors and scrap fabric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b235bbc6d859648e","term":"clever","forms":["clever","cleverer","more clever","cleverest","most clever"],"pos":"adj","zh":"理解快；學得快","explanation":"指人很快理解、學習或運用想法，能夠迅速抓住問題的關鍵。它強調反應和學習上的敏捷，不單單表示考試成績好。","examples":[{"en":"Lina is clever enough to understand the new system after one lesson.","zh":"莉娜很聰明，只上一節課就能理解這個新系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clever apprentice mastered the technique within days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5c7ffac26fed654fe62","word":"click","forms":["click"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b056a374c557c71a","term":"click","forms":["click","clicks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咔嗒聲","explanation":"指一個短促、清脆而不太響的聲音，通常像小而硬的東西碰到硬物，或鎖、開關扣合時發出的“咔嗒”。這正是 memory hook 裡手指一按、聲音隨即響起的那一聲。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a click as the window lock closed.","zh":"窗鎖釦上時，我聽到了一聲咔嗒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box opened with a soft click.","zh":"盒子伴著輕輕一聲咔嗒開啟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/click","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86be65e8ad0f632d","term":"click","forms":["click","clicks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑鼠點選","explanation":"指按下滑鼠或類似輸入裝置按鈕的動作，以及軟體因這次按下而作出的反應。就像 memory hook 裡手指一按，聲音和選擇同時發生。","examples":[{"en":"A single click on the icon opened the file.","zh":"單擊圖示後，檔案就開啟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can select the answer with one click.","zh":"點選一下就可以選中答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/click","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d251c36dc885572","term":"click","forms":["click","clicks","clicking","clicked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"點選選擇","explanation":"指用滑鼠點選電腦介面中的專案、圖示或連結，從而選中或開啟它；就像手指一按，選擇立刻完成。","examples":[{"en":"Click the blue icon to start the program.","zh":"點選藍色圖示啟動程式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Click on your name to view your account.","zh":"點選你的姓名檢視賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/click","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd83cf844a2bca17","term":"click","forms":["click","clicks","clicking","clicked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然明白","explanation":"表示思路突然接上，某件事一下子變得明白，就像腦中也清脆地“咔嗒”一聲。","examples":[{"en":"Then it clicked: I had left my keys at work.","zh":"這時我突然明白了：我把鑰匙落在單位了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It finally clicked that the two stories were connected.","zh":"我終於突然明白，這兩個故事是有關聯的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/click","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-948fe603f61dc036b5c5","word":"client","forms":["client"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a033ae60ff757dbe","term":"client","forms":["client","clients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顧客；客戶","explanation":"指購買商品或接受服務的人或組織。核心概念是“接受別人提供的東西”，所以既可以是商店的顧客，也可以是公司的客戶。","examples":[{"en":"The agency has clients all over the country.","zh":"這家機構的客戶遍佈全國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We always put our clients first.","zh":"我們始終把客戶放在第一位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/client","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1940b10355ead0b6","term":"client","forms":["client","clients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"客戶端","explanation":"在計算機系統中，指向伺服器請求或使用服務的程式、裝置或系統。它就像一個向伺服器“求助”的客戶，伺服器提供資料或功能，客戶端負責請求和使用。","examples":[{"en":"The client sends a request to the server.","zh":"客戶端向伺服器傳送請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need to install a client to access the service.","zh":"你需要安裝客戶端才能訪問這項服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/client","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a2643bb2922fb4229ad","word":"cliff","forms":["cliff"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c91e3ba9a39009fa","term":"cliff","forms":["cliff","cliffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懸崖；峭壁","explanation":"cliff是一面很陡、幾乎垂直的岩石表面，通常位於海邊、山邊或峽谷邊。核心畫面就是站在邊緣後，下面突然沒有可以緩慢走下去的坡，而是直接墜落。","examples":[{"en":"We stood at the edge of a cliff and watched the waves below.","zh":"我們站在懸崖邊，望著下面的海浪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow path leads down from the cliff to the beach.","zh":"一條狹窄的小路從懸崖通向海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cliff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3c300dca11f3786","term":"cliff","forms":["cliff","cliffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斷崖式下跌；突然失效的臨界點","explanation":"比喻某種表現、價值或數量像從懸崖邊掉下去一樣突然下降，或越過某個點後迅速失效。它強調變化突然、幅度大，而不是普通的逐漸減少。","examples":[{"en":"After the scandal, the company's sales fell off a cliff.","zh":"醜聞發生後，這家公司的銷量斷崖式下跌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Battery output drops off a cliff in extreme cold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cliff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10db699812d02cc570ad","word":"climate","forms":["climate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f051eefdd3e0976f","term":"climate","forms":["climate","climates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氣候","explanation":"climate 是一個地方經過很長時間形成的總體天氣模式，包括溫度、降水等穩定特徵，而不是某一天的天氣。","examples":[{"en":"The island has a warm, humid climate all year round.","zh":"這個島全年氣候溫暖而潮溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Climate change is affecting farming in many regions.","zh":"氣候變化正在影響許多地區的農業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfec7f81d36198e3","term":"climate","forms":["climate","climates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氛圍；環境","explanation":"climate 可以把一個地方長期的“空氣感”比作政治、社會或道德環境，表示某個時期人們普遍感受到的整體氛圍。","examples":[{"en":"The current political climate makes cooperation difficult.","zh":"當前的政治氛圍使合作變得困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The merger created a climate of uncertainty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcc43fc8a425bedac5f8","word":"climax","forms":["climax"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae4f7355981ddbdb","term":"climax","forms":["climax","climaxes","climaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遞進修辭","explanation":"一種把一連串詞句或觀點按強度逐步提高的修辭方式，就像沿梯子一層層向上走，最後達到最高處。","examples":[{"en":"The speech builds to a climax by moving from personal loss to a call for national action.","zh":"這篇演講透過從個人的失去逐步推進到號召全國行動，形成了遞進的高潮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speaker used climax to build from inconvenience to disaster.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b467e6c789618d9","term":"climax","forms":["climax","climaxes","climaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事高潮","explanation":"故事或戲劇中，逐漸上升的衝突達到最高強度併發生關鍵轉折的部分。它通常是讀者最期待、情節變化最集中的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The climax of the film comes when the two sisters finally confront their father.","zh":"這部電影的高潮出現在兩姐妹終於面對父親的時候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everything in the novel leads up to the climactic courtroom scene.","zh":"小說中的一切都逐步引向那場高潮性的法庭戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce6729e8cf30b19c","term":"climax","forms":["climax","climaxes","climaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頂點；最高程度","explanation":"某種發展、狀態或荒謬程度逐步升高後達到的最高處，也就是“頂點”。它不只用於故事，也可以描述行為、成就或某種程度。","examples":[{"en":"The argument reached its climax when both teams accused each other of cheating.","zh":"兩隊互相指責作弊時，這場爭論達到了頂點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival reached a climax with a spectacular fireworks display.","zh":"煙花表演令這場節慶活動達到了高潮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d73d3e7a7e1d181671a5","word":"climb","forms":["climb"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7b6273e2bd550b6","term":"climb","forms":["climb","climbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次攀登","explanation":"指攀登這件事本身，通常強調過程以及其中的安全、難度或經歷。","examples":[{"en":"The climb took us nearly three hours.","zh":"這次攀登花了我們將近三個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our final climb began beside the glacier and ended above the clouds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbfaa6d1da6d4bae","term":"climb","forms":["climb","climbs","climbing","climbed","clomb","clumb","climbest","climbedst","climbeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上升；上漲","explanation":"表示人、物或數值從較低處逐步向高處移動；價格、溫度等也可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"Temperatures climbed above thirty degrees by noon.","zh":"到中午時，氣溫升到了三十多度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The balloon climbed slowly into the sky.","zh":"氣球慢慢升入天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9dbc6f0b28c60597","term":"climb","forms":["climb","climbs","climbing","climbed","clomb","clumb","climbest","climbedst","climbeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攀登；爬上","explanation":"表示沿著某個物體或表面向上移動，例如爬樹、爬梯子或登上車輛。","examples":[{"en":"The children climbed the old stone wall.","zh":"孩子們爬上了那堵舊石牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She climbed into the truck and closed the door.","zh":"她爬進卡車，關上了車門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c899599a6054828d","term":"climb","forms":["climb","climbs","climbing","climbed","clomb","clumb","climbest","climbedst","climbeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"登上；攀登到頂","explanation":"強調成功到達某個高處或大型目標的頂部，常用於山峰、建築物和高塔。","examples":[{"en":"They climbed the highest peak on the island.","zh":"他們登上了島上最高的山峰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We climbed to the top of the tower before sunset.","zh":"日落前我們爬到了塔頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/climb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4151dc4c63622213d3dc","word":"cling","forms":["cling"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9becb84ec2c1fed5","term":"cling","forms":["cling","clings","clinging","clung","clinged","clong"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緊緊抓住","explanation":"為了不掉下去或不被甩開而牢牢抓住某物，就像手緊扣住樹枝一樣。它強調抓得很緊、很難鬆開。","examples":[{"en":"The child clung to his father's hand as they crossed the busy street.","zh":"過繁忙的街道時，孩子緊緊抓住父親的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child clung to his father's jacket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9e2cb4ee82e8f48","term":"cling","forms":["cling","clings","clinging","clung","clinged","clong"],"pos":"verb","zh":"貼著表面","explanation":"某種布料、薄膜或其他柔軟物貼在物體表面，並隨著表面的輪廓貼合；它不一定是被膠水永久固定的。","examples":[{"en":"After the rain, her shirt clung to her back.","zh":"下雨後，她的襯衫貼在背上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wet leaves clung to the soles of our shoes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81d997f6c2a0c673","term":"cling","forms":["cling","clings","clinging","clung","clinged","clong"],"pos":"verb","zh":"依戀並依賴","explanation":"表示在感情或心理上緊緊依附某人、某種關係、記憶或希望，不願意放下；這就是把“抓住不放”從身體動作延伸到內心。","examples":[{"en":"Even after the failure, she clung to the hope of starting again.","zh":"即使失敗了，她仍緊緊抱著重新開始的希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She clung to her grandmother after the funeral.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbfeb74a4b4216dfd0f7","word":"clinic","forms":["clinic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1163548169c48aba","term":"clinic","forms":["clinic","clinics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"診所；門診機構","explanation":"指為病人提供檢查、診斷或治療的醫療機構，通常主要接待門診病人，不一定提供住院服務。","examples":[{"en":"I went to a clinic near my office for a routine checkup.","zh":"我去了辦公室附近的一家診所做常規檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic treats children with asthma.","zh":"這家診所為患哮喘的兒童提供治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clinic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-768019d77e41f55a","term":"clinic","forms":["clinic","clinics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門診；診療時段","explanation":"指醫生或醫療團隊集中為病人進行診斷或治療的一次門診活動，而不只是那個固定地點。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital holds a diabetes clinic every Thursday.","zh":"這家醫院每週四安排糖尿病門診。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Patients without appointments can attend the walk-in clinic on Saturday mornings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clinic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98569e7e9080addd9e38","word":"clinical","forms":["clinical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18f24f2afdd0b8bb","term":"clinical","forms":["clinical","more clinical","most clinical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"臨床的；實際診療中的","explanation":"指直接面對真實患者、在實際診療現場進行的工作或專業活動，而不是隻停留在課堂、實驗室或理論層面。","examples":[{"en":"She gained valuable clinical experience during her final year.","zh":"她在最後一年獲得了寶貴的臨床經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment is now being tested in clinical practice.","zh":"這種治療方法目前正在臨床實踐中接受檢驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clinical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c6be7e1778165d7","term":"clinical","forms":["clinical","more clinical","most clinical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"診所的；與診所相關的","explanation":"指屬於診所或發生在診所這一醫療服務場所中的事物；它比“臨床的”更直接地指向診所這個場所。","examples":[{"en":"Most patients now receive care in a clinical setting rather than at home.","zh":"如今大多數患者都在診所或臨床環境中接受護理，而不是在家裡接受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clinical staff must disinfect every examination room.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clinical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67905ad3cc2dd52b1f5f","word":"clip","forms":["clip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5079892050871d9","term":"clip","forms":["clip","clips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夾子；夾具","explanation":"clip是把物品夾住、抓住或連線起來的小裝置，正如記憶鉤子裡的“夾住一小段”，常用來固定紙張、照片或檔案。","examples":[{"en":"Use this clip to attach the receipt to the form.","zh":"用這個夾子把收據夾在表格上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small clip keeps the papers together.","zh":"一個小夾子把這些紙夾在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1acea98c1f6ed785","term":"clip","forms":["clip","clips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剪下的部分","explanation":"clip可以指從較大整體上剪下來的那一小部分，例如剪下的毛、材料或其他東西，正對應記憶鉤子裡的“切下一小段”。","examples":[{"en":"The sweater was made from a clip of angora wool.","zh":"這件毛衣是用一批剪下來的安哥拉羊毛製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She saved a clip of the fabric for repairs.","zh":"她留了一小塊剪下來的布料以備修補。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c375710ff2245fcd","term":"clip","forms":["clip","clips","clipping","clipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用夾子固定","explanation":"clip表示用夾子或類似裝置把東西固定起來，就像用夾子把一小段材料夾在指定位置。","examples":[{"en":"Please clip the photos to the pages where they will go.","zh":"請把照片夾到它們應放的頁面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She clipped her ID badge to her jacket.","zh":"她把身份牌夾在外套上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73017756e73f36f5","term":"clip","forms":["clip","clips","clipping","clipt","clipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剪下","explanation":"用剪刀或剪刀狀工具把東西剪下來，重點是“夾住或切下一小段”中的切下一段，而不是用刀割開。","examples":[{"en":"She clipped the loose threads from the hem.","zh":"她把衣襬上鬆掉的線頭剪掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The barber clipped his hair short for the summer.","zh":"理髮師把他的頭髮剪短了，適合夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d8198efa3604d1648534","word":"clock","forms":["clock"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c68f5baa1e701c5","term":"clock","forms":["clock","clocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鍾；時鐘","explanation":"測量並顯示一天中時間的裝置，是 clock 最核心的意思。它可以是牆上的鐘、桌上的鐘，也可以泛指計時裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The clock says it is nearly noon.","zh":"鍾顯示快到中午了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a clock on the wall.","zh":"牆上有一隻鍾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-469baa511b0da92ee293","word":"clockwise","forms":["clockwise"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b05d4f3bd95de341","term":"clockwise","forms":["clockwise"],"pos":"adj","zh":"順時針的","explanation":"指物體的旋轉方向與鐘錶指標通常轉動的方向一致，也就是從鐘面上方往右、再往下、往左繞行的方向。","examples":[{"en":"The wheel makes a clockwise turn when the machine starts.","zh":"機器啟動時，輪子會順時針轉動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The arrows show the clockwise direction.","zh":"這些箭頭顯示順時針方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clockwise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0abd1e3fe36191e7","term":"clockwise","forms":["clockwise"],"pos":"adv","zh":"順時針地","explanation":"說明轉動、旋轉或擰動的動作沿著鐘錶指標的方向進行；可以把它理解為“朝順時針方向”。","examples":[{"en":"Turn the knob clockwise to tighten it.","zh":"順時針轉動旋鈕，把它擰緊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Turn the dial clockwise until the arrow aligns.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clockwise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5d61dc89a35d2c924b2","word":"clone","forms":["clone"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b20eddc817cdddd0","term":"clone","forms":["clone","clones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"克隆生物","explanation":"指由一個祖先無性產生、因而在遺傳上幾乎相同的活生物；最初主要用於植物，後來也用於動物等。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists cloned a sheep from an adult cell.","zh":"科學家用一個成年細胞克隆出了一隻羊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This plant is a clone of the original rose.","zh":"這株植物是原始玫瑰的克隆體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8103fcd60f176a12","term":"clone","forms":["clone","clones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"仿製品；模仿品","explanation":"指按照已有物件製作、用來模擬它的複製品，常見於產品、電腦、軟體或其他技術物件。","examples":[{"en":"The company released a cheaper clone of the popular game console.","zh":"這家公司推出了一款更便宜的熱門遊戲機仿製品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app looks like a clone of an older service.","zh":"這款應用看起來像是某個舊服務的仿製品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f99fb8c4b428640c","term":"clone","forms":["clone","clones","cloning","cloned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"克隆；製造克隆體","explanation":"指以某個生物、細胞或其他物件為原型，製造出遺傳上相同或高度相似的克隆體。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists were able to clone a sheep.","zh":"科學家成功克隆出了一隻羊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lab cloned the cells from a single sample.","zh":"實驗室從一個樣本中克隆出了這些細胞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-310ff200149b44a32f12","word":"close","forms":["close"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f43a3a4db898af5","term":"close","forms":["close","closer","closest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"接近的","explanation":"把距離收攏到很小，就是 close：地點、人物、時間或抽象差異彼此接近。","examples":[{"en":"The station is close to our hotel.","zh":"車站離我們住的酒店很近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are close in age.","zh":"我們的年齡相近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/close","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d381a31762200fec","term":"close","forms":["close","closes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結束","explanation":"事情一步步收攏到最後，就是 close：它表示專案、會議或活動的結束、收尾。","examples":[{"en":"The conference came to a close with a final speech.","zh":"會議以最後一場演講結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We thanked the team at the close of the project.","zh":"專案結束時，我們向團隊表示了感謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/close","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eef3652b873d06a6","term":"close","forms":["close","closes","closing","closed","closest","closedst","closeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"關上；封閉","explanation":"指把門、窗或其他開口合上，使通道不再敞開；也可以泛指把某個開口堵住。它最直接地體現了“把開口收攏起來”。","examples":[{"en":"Please close the window before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請把窗戶關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shopkeeper closed the door at the end of the day.","zh":"店主在一天結束時關上了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/close","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-784304f88c91dc66e336","word":"closet","forms":["closet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5cf2a51345f7e641","term":"closet","forms":["closet","closets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壁櫥；小儲藏室","explanation":"房屋裡用來放衣物、食物或其他生活用品的小空間，常有門，也可以是嵌在牆裡的儲藏處；這是現代最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The hallway closet is full of coats and umbrellas.","zh":"走廊的壁櫥裡放滿了外套和雨傘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We keep the vacuum cleaner in the closet.","zh":"我們把吸塵器放在儲藏室裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/closet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d4cb937d6d22521566b","word":"closure","forms":["closure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a0a337496da5600","term":"closure","forms":["closure","closures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結束；收尾","explanation":"指某件事、某個階段或某項活動結束這一事件，重點是事情被正式收束，而不只是暫時停止。","examples":[{"en":"The ceremony marked the closure of the investigation.","zh":"這場儀式標誌著調查正式結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project is nearing closure after three years of work.","zh":"經過三年的工作，這個專案即將收尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/closure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cd4217d5559f9ee","term":"closure","forms":["closure","closures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情感了結","explanation":"指人在痛苦經歷、失去或衝突之後，獲得完整感和心理上的結束感，不再一直被這件事牽掛。","examples":[{"en":"Writing the letter helped her find emotional closure.","zh":"寫那封信幫助她獲得了情感上的了結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He never got closure after his friend disappeared.","zh":"朋友失蹤後，他始終沒有得到情感上的了結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/closure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6e28ffb3b198d85e47d","word":"cloth","forms":["cloth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-312c295c52538654","term":"cloth","forms":["cloth","cloths","clothes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"布料；織物","explanation":"指由纖維織成、編成或氈合成的材料，可用於做衣服、裝飾、清潔等。它是 cloth 最基本的意思，重點在材料本身，而不是某一件成品。","examples":[{"en":"She wiped the table with a soft cloth.","zh":"她用一塊柔軟的布擦桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This jacket is made of thick cloth.","zh":"這件夾克是用厚布料做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2aff935c3b4bd92","term":"cloth","forms":["cloth","cloths","clothes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餐桌布","explanation":"特指吃飯時鋪在桌上的布，尤其是在正式用餐的語境中。它是“用於覆蓋桌面的布”這一具體化用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please remove the cloth after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後請把桌布收起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spread a clean cloth over the dining table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2c2c859125b3d5e158c","word":"clothe","forms":["clothe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c6bd57c416b168e","term":"clothe","forms":["clothe","clothes","clothing","clothed","clad"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……穿衣；供給衣物","explanation":"指給某人穿上衣服，或為某人提供足夠的衣物。它把“衣物披到身體上”和“讓某人有衣服可穿”這兩個意思連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The charity helps feed and clothe families in need.","zh":"這個慈善機構幫助為有需要的家庭提供食物和衣物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She clothed herself in a simple black dress.","zh":"她給自己穿上了一條樸素的黑色連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clothe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a1cedfa642089bf","term":"clothe","forms":["clothe","clothes","clothing","clothed","clad"],"pos":"verb","zh":"賦予抽象的外衣","explanation":"指像給人披上一件外衣那樣，賦予某人權力、權威、尊嚴或其他抽象特徵。這裡不是實際穿衣，而是把某種身份或力量加到某人身上。","examples":[{"en":"The new law clothed the agency with greater authority.","zh":"這項新法律賦予了該機構更大的權力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister clothed his refusal in diplomatic language.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clothe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c5f9b87778cfb103aa0","word":"clothes","forms":["clothes"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86ef1819f770bbcc","term":"clothes","forms":["clothes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣服","explanation":"指人穿在身上的衣物，通常把上衣、褲子、裙子等作為整體或多件來稱呼。這個詞本身通常是複數形式，強調各種穿戴用的覆蓋物。","examples":[{"en":"I need to buy some warm clothes for winter.","zh":"我需要買些過冬的暖和衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put your dirty clothes in the basket.","zh":"請把你的髒衣服放進籃子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clothes","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37e3ee86524a3215","term":"clothes","forms":["clothes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"床上被褥","explanation":"指鋪在床上或蓋在身上的床單、毯子等床上覆蓋物，也就是“床上的衣物”。這個意思仍然來自“覆蓋”這一核心概念，但通常要靠上下文判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The child hid under the clothes on the bed.","zh":"孩子躲在床上的被褥下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pulled the bedclothes up against the cold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clothes","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12d264de09a571d6851d","word":"clothing","forms":["clothing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-634532370293e6ac","term":"clothing","forms":["clothing","clothings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣物；服裝","explanation":"指穿在人體外面、用來保暖、遮體或裝飾的各種衣物，也可以把各種衣服作為一個整體或類別來談。","examples":[{"en":"The store sells affordable clothing for the whole family.","zh":"這家商店出售全家人都買得起的服裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her clothing brand focuses on simple, comfortable designs.","zh":"她的服裝品牌專注於簡約、舒適的設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clothing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56681010b753e1abe52c","word":"cloud","forms":["cloud"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5603cc277c02fa51","term":"cloud","forms":["cloud","clouds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雲","explanation":"指懸浮在空中的水滴或冰晶形成的可見雲團，也就是天空中的雲。","examples":[{"en":"Dark clouds gathered over the town before the storm.","zh":"暴風雨前，城鎮上空聚起了烏雲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small cloud drifted across the moon.","zh":"一小片雲飄過月亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81987dea608ed7c1","term":"cloud","forms":["cloud","clouds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使人困惑或陰鬱的事物","explanation":"表示像雲一樣遮住清晰視線的東西，因此可指讓人感到陰沉、困惑或看不清問題的因素。","examples":[{"en":"The argument cast a cloud over the family celebration.","zh":"這場爭吵給家庭慶祝活動蒙上了陰影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cloud of doubt hung over the plan.","zh":"這個計劃一直籠罩著疑雲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-213bb92144ab7e06","term":"cloud","forms":["cloud","clouds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雲端","explanation":"the cloud 指由網路連線的遠端伺服器和儲存、處理空間；使用者不必知道裝置具體放在哪裡，就能透過網際網路使用它。","examples":[{"en":"I keep my photos in the cloud so I can access them anywhere.","zh":"我把照片存放在雲端，這樣在哪裡都能訪問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app backs up your files to the cloud.","zh":"這個應用會把你的檔案備份到雲端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e9562c786d9ca040985","word":"cloudy","forms":["cloudy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-038a1190bc20f596","term":"cloudy","forms":["cloudy","cloudier","cloudiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多雲的","explanation":"指天空中有云，雲層遮住了部分陽光，但不一定完全陰暗；這是最直接、最常見的天氣含義。","examples":[{"en":"It will be cloudy this afternoon, but it should stay dry.","zh":"今天下午天氣多雲，但應該不會下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We woke up to a cloudy sky.","zh":"我們醒來時看到天空佈滿了雲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloudy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1af18538e1334f4b","term":"cloudy","forms":["cloudy","cloudier","cloudiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"渾濁的；不透明的","explanation":"指光線不能清楚地穿過某種材料，或透過它看東西時不清晰，就像視線被一層雲擋住。它可以描述液體、玻璃、塑膠等。","examples":[{"en":"The water in the vase turned cloudy after a few days.","zh":"花瓶裡的水幾天後變渾濁了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cloudy glass lets in light but hides the details behind it.","zh":"這種不透明的玻璃能透光，卻看不清後面的細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloudy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d664efb369e2bf5","term":"cloudy","forms":["cloudy","cloudier","cloudiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含糊的；不確定的","explanation":"指事實、想法、記憶、計劃或判斷像被雲遮住一樣不清楚，難以確定或理解。重點不是看不見，而是意義、真相或結果不明朗。","examples":[{"en":"My memory of that evening is still cloudy.","zh":"我對那天晚上的記憶仍然很模糊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company has a cloudy plan for next year.","zh":"這家公司對明年的計劃還不明確。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloudy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd8cc779bce474283c3e","word":"clown","forms":["clown"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33c2db897085a8cd","term":"clown","forms":["clown","clowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬戲團小丑","explanation":"指穿著誇張服裝、化著彩妝、用滑稽表演逗觀眾發笑的表演者，最典型的形象就是馬戲團裡的小丑。","examples":[{"en":"The children laughed when the clown came into the circus ring.","zh":"小丑走進馬戲團的表演場地時，孩子們都笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clown squeezed a stream of water from his flower.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34ac99e54bee3aef","term":"clown","forms":["clown","clowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑稽的人","explanation":"指總是做傻事、惡作劇或故意逗笑別人的人；重點在他的行為像小丑一樣滑稽。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone knew Jake as the class clown because he was always playing pranks.","zh":"大家都知道傑克是班裡的活寶，因為他總是在搞惡作劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My uncle is a clown who makes every meal entertaining.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc2585df74ecdb8b43e3","word":"club","forms":["club"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76128f31c425d80a","term":"club","forms":["club","clubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棍棒；打擊用的粗重物體","explanation":"指粗重的棍棒，通常用於擊打，也可以指類似棍棒的玩具或器械。這個義項體現了“粗重的一團東西”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The guard carried a wooden club at the gate.","zh":"守衛在門口帶著一根木棍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Archaeologists uncovered a stone club beside the ancient hunting tools.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/club","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac800fa0c55da452","term":"club","forms":["club","clubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"俱樂部；社團","explanation":"指一群因為體育、興趣、娛樂或共同目的而組成的組織。它把“人聚在一起”變成了一個固定的團體。","examples":[{"en":"My sister joined a local tennis club.","zh":"我姐姐加入了當地的網球俱樂部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The club meets every Thursday evening.","zh":"這個俱樂部每週四晚上聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/club","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f14053d4010cc7f","term":"club","forms":["club","clubs","clubbing","clubbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用棍棒擊打","explanation":"指用棍棒或類似的粗重物體擊打某人或某物，是名詞“棍棒”直接發展出的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The attacker clubbed him with a metal bar.","zh":"襲擊者用金屬棒打了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The attackers clubbed him with wooden sticks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/club","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad01ba3652264c05","term":"club","forms":["club","clubs","clubbing","clubbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聯合成團","explanation":"指人或事物聚在一起組成一個團體，強調把分散的部分合到一起。","examples":[{"en":"Several small businesses clubbed together to share delivery costs.","zh":"幾家小企業聯合起來分攤配送費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children clubbed together to build a model plane.","zh":"孩子們一起合作製作了一架模型飛機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/club","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c424a68bbc374bc8aa7","word":"clue","forms":["clue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19713f6f3ab425e4","term":"clue","forms":["clue","clues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提示；線索","explanation":"指能把人引向答案、結論或下一步行動的資訊，既可以是直接提示，也可以是需要自己推斷的線索。","examples":[{"en":"Can you give me a clue? I don't know how to solve this puzzle.","zh":"你能給我一點提示嗎？我不知道怎麼解這道謎題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map gave us a clue about where to look next.","zh":"這張地圖給了我們下一步該去哪裡找的線索。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-923f968c9be9b2b0","term":"clue","forms":["clue","clues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭緒；瞭解","explanation":"表示對某事有一定認識或理解，常用於否定句；“have no clue”就是完全不知道、毫無頭緒。","examples":[{"en":"I have no clue where my keys are.","zh":"我完全不知道我的鑰匙在哪兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had little clue about what was happening.","zh":"她對正在發生的事情幾乎不瞭解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-637308e949738d377835","word":"clumsy","forms":["clumsy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de5ba913205ccfec","term":"clumsy","forms":["clumsy","clumsier","clumsiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"動作笨拙；手腳不協調","explanation":"形容人動作不協調、缺少靈巧，容易碰倒或弄壞東西；也可以直接形容某個動作不自然、不熟練。這裡的重點是身體控制不夠好，不一定是在說這個人笨。","examples":[{"en":"I’m clumsy with chopsticks, so I often drop things.","zh":"我用筷子不太靈巧，所以經常把東西掉下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was clumsy and knocked over the glass.","zh":"他手腳笨拙，把玻璃杯碰倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clumsy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76e1058b0a6d4481","term":"clumsy","forms":["clumsy","clumsier","clumsiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"做法笨拙；不夠巧妙","explanation":"形容解決問題、表達意見或安排事情的方式不夠優雅周全，顯得生硬、繞遠或缺少策略。它未必完全不能用，只是讓人覺得處理得不漂亮。","examples":[{"en":"It was a clumsy attempt to change the subject.","zh":"那是一次很生硬的轉移話題的嘗試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His clumsy attempt at flattery embarrassed us both.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clumsy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-164cf1ca8391532e4f23","word":"cluster","forms":["cluster"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5fab8e9e6eee830e","term":"cluster","forms":["cluster","clusters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一簇；一組","explanation":"指幾個或許多個彼此靠近的、可以分辨開的事物組成的一組，例如靠得很近的島嶼、星星或房屋。重點是“聚在一起形成一團”，而不是一個整體物件。","examples":[{"en":"A cluster of small islands appeared on the horizon.","zh":"地平線上出現了一簇小島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She planted a cluster of bright flowers beside the gate.","zh":"她在門旁種了一簇鮮豔的花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cluster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f3811a6f15c4c7d","term":"cluster","forms":["cluster","clusters","clustering","clustered","clusterest","clusteredst","clustereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使聚成組","explanation":"表示把人、動物、物體或資料點集中安排，使它們形成一個或多個cluster。重點是“讓分散的東西聚到一起”，而不是單純發現它們已經在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The survey responses were clustered into four main groups.","zh":"調查回答被歸成了四個主要群組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmers clustered the pots near the wall to protect them from the wind.","zh":"農民把花盆集中放在牆邊，以免受風吹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cluster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-323fdbf5b7ee4744","term":"cluster","forms":["cluster","clusters","clustering","clustered","clusterest","clusteredst","clustereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聚攏；聚集","explanation":"表示人、動物或物體自己聚到一起，形成一群或一團；也就是cluster作為名詞所表示的狀態發生了。","examples":[{"en":"The children clustered around the guide to hear the story.","zh":"孩子們圍到導遊身邊聽故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors clustered around the newly unveiled sculpture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cluster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0f167bc84b881bc06f6","word":"coach","forms":["coach"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6905f172d98e8ef3","term":"coach","forms":["coach","coaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教練；指導者","explanation":"指負責帶人練習、提高技能或準備比賽和考試的人；他就像把學習者一路帶到目標的人。","examples":[{"en":"Her coach helped her prepare for the national championship.","zh":"她的教練幫助她準備全國錦標賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hired a vocal coach before the audition.","zh":"試演前，他請了一位聲樂教練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b07146ac801067b","term":"coach","forms":["coach","coaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機或火車普通艙","explanation":"在美國英語中，指商業飛機或火車中票價較低的標準艙位；它和“教練”沒有關係，而是把人運往目的地的普通空間。","examples":[{"en":"There were no first-class seats left, so we booked coach.","zh":"頭等艙已經沒有座位了，所以我們訂了普通艙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach seats were narrow but inexpensive.","zh":"普通艙座位很窄，但價格便宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-755021267f53076f","term":"coach","forms":["coach","coaches","coaching","coached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指導；訓練某人","explanation":"表示帶著某人反覆練習、糾正方法並提高表現，也可用於幫助某人準備比賽、演出或考試；這就是“把人帶到目標”的核心動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The mentor coached me through several difficult interviews.","zh":"那位導師帶著我練習並應對了幾次困難的面試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He coaches young players in basic football skills.","zh":"他指導年輕球員練習基本的足球技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d114c95fbf5208dd6cf","word":"coal","forms":["coal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0c0845afb663b0a","term":"coal","forms":["coal","coals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煤","explanation":"指由遠古植物遺骸形成的黑色或褐黑色岩石，主要成分是碳，常被開採並用作燃料。","examples":[{"en":"The region was once famous for its coal mines.","zh":"這個地區曾以煤礦聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many power stations have reduced their use of coal.","zh":"許多發電站已經減少了煤的使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14abb3d3cac42d20","term":"coal","forms":["coal","coals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一塊煤；煤塊","explanation":"把煤看作可以單獨拿取、放入爐火的一塊或一份時使用這個可數義。","examples":[{"en":"He put another coal on the fire.","zh":"他又往火裡添了一塊煤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A glowing coal rolled out of the fireplace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5640f1bb0da680912561","word":"coalition","forms":["coalition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df9fa2f517cc0ac2","term":"coalition","forms":["coalition","coalitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯盟；聯合體","explanation":"coalition是幾個政黨、組織或國家為了共同利益或特定目標而暫時組成的聯盟。成員仍然各自獨立，只是在某件事上聯合行動。","examples":[{"en":"Several environmental groups formed a coalition to oppose the new highway.","zh":"幾個環保組織組成了一個聯盟，反對修建這條新公路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country is governed by a coalition of three parties.","zh":"這個國家由三個政黨組成的聯合政府執政。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coalition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-152397e39cbd1ca8d0be","word":"coarse","forms":["coarse"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1887562027aa931","term":"coarse","forms":["coarse","coarser","coarsest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粗糙的；不光滑的","explanation":"指表面摸起來不平滑、纖維或質地較粗的東西，重點是觸感上的“不細膩”。","examples":[{"en":"This coarse fabric feels rough against the skin.","zh":"這塊粗布貼著皮膚感覺很磨人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The table was covered with coarse, unfinished wood.","zh":"這張桌子用的是粗糙的未加工木材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coarse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c153e230e8175b37","term":"coarse","forms":["coarse","coarser","coarsest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粗俗的；不文雅的","explanation":"把“質地不細膩”引申到人的行為、語言或玩笑，表示缺乏禮貌、品位或 delicacy，聽起來令人不舒服。","examples":[{"en":"His coarse jokes made everyone at the dinner table uncomfortable.","zh":"他那些粗俗的玩笑讓餐桌上的每個人都感到不舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She apologized for her coarse language.","zh":"她為自己粗俗的言語道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coarse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23c075a035f388971803","word":"coast","forms":["coast"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e585584ee12b283","term":"coast","forms":["coast","coasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海岸","explanation":"指陸地與海洋、海灣或大型湖泊相接的地帶，也就是從陸地轉向大片水域的邊緣。","examples":[{"en":"The rocky coast of Maine has few beaches.","zh":"緬因州的岩石海岸很少有沙灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We drove along the coast at sunset.","zh":"我們在日落時沿著海岸開車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0dffa3b5d008608bef81","word":"coastline","forms":["coastline"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-024dfc02e2563cd8","term":"coastline","forms":["coastline","coastlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海岸線","explanation":"指陸地和海洋交界處形成的輪廓或邊界，就像沿著海邊畫出的線；它通常是大範圍觀察下的大致界線，而不是精確不變的線。","examples":[{"en":"We walked along the coastline until sunset.","zh":"我們沿著海岸線走到日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm damaged several towns along the coastline.","zh":"暴風雨損壞了海岸線沿線的幾個城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coastline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8218f3d6780abf45a5a4","word":"coat","forms":["coat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-965c67241bae5e7a","term":"coat","forms":["coat","coats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外套","explanation":"穿在上身外面、覆蓋軀幹和手臂的衣服，通常用於保暖或擋風。它是 coat 最常見、最需要優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She grabbed her coat before leaving the house.","zh":"她出門前拿上了外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His new coat keeps him warm on windy days.","zh":"他的新外套讓他在颳風天也很暖和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-413b389f20d2869d","term":"coat","forms":["coat","coats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"塗層；覆蓋層","explanation":"指覆蓋在物體表面的一層材料，例如油漆、保護材料或其他塗層。它和“外套”共享同一個核心形象：在外面再加一層。","examples":[{"en":"The walls need another coat of paint.","zh":"這些牆還需要再刷一層油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Apply a thin coat of oil to the pan.","zh":"在鍋上塗一層薄薄的油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06554fe0f66220c3","term":"coat","forms":["coat","coats","coating","coated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……塗上覆蓋層","explanation":"把油漆、油、保護材料等均勻覆蓋到某物表面，使它形成一層外部材料。","examples":[{"en":"Coat the vegetables with olive oil before roasting them.","zh":"烘烤蔬菜前，先給它們均勻裹上一層橄欖油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The metal was coated with a rust-resistant finish.","zh":"這塊金屬塗了一層防鏽塗層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39c7ad800c5792108f33","word":"cocaine","forms":["cocaine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e7820fe01600e09","term":"cocaine","forms":["cocaine","cocaines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可成癮的古柯類藥物","explanation":"一種從古柯植物中提取或人工製成的可成癮藥物，能刺激神經；醫學上有時用於區域性麻醉，但非醫療使用通常違法且有嚴重風險。","examples":[{"en":"The patient was warned about the risks of using cocaine.","zh":"醫生提醒這名患者使用可卡因的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cocaine can cause serious health problems.","zh":"可卡因可能導致嚴重的健康問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocaine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-796e43a5a8cdb73b92b5","word":"cock","forms":["cock"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d34e7cee02fba76","term":"cock","forms":["cock","cocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公雞","explanation":"指成年雄性鳥，尤其指公雞；可以把它記成昂首“豎起”的鳥。","examples":[{"en":"The cock began crowing before sunrise.","zh":"公雞在日出前就開始打鳴了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bright-red cock stood on the fence.","zh":"一隻鮮紅的公雞站在籬笆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09c31a3148cdb488","term":"cock","forms":["cock","cocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男性性器官","explanation":"指陰莖，是男性的生殖器官；這是一個粗俗、非正式的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The medical article uses a clinical term instead of this vulgar word.","zh":"這篇醫學文章使用了醫學術語，而不是這個粗俗詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dictionary labels cock as a vulgar term for the penis.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-381462626c1e446dc999","word":"cockroach/roach","forms":["cockroach","roach"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41ee80521491a86a","term":"cockroach","forms":["cockroach","cockroaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蟑螂","explanation":"指蟑螂，即一種通常為黑色或棕色、行動迅速的昆蟲；日常英語中這是最主要、最應先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"There was a cockroach under the sink.","zh":"水槽下面有一隻蟑螂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had to call an exterminator because the kitchen was full of cockroaches.","zh":"廚房裡到處都是蟑螂，我們只好叫滅蟲人員來處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cockroach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f114808e849b6d90","term":"cockroach","forms":["cockroach","cockroaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人厭惡的人","explanation":"把蟑螂那種令人厭惡、難以擺脫的形象移到人身上，指被說話者視為討厭或不受歡迎的人，也可指被這樣看待的一群人。","examples":[{"en":"The dictator called his opponents cockroaches and ordered them arrested.","zh":"那個獨裁者把反對者罵作蟑螂，並下令逮捕他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The landlord called the dishonest broker a cockroach.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cockroach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-599825ed36378090","term":"roach","forms":["roach","roaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蟑螂","explanation":"在美國英語中，roach 可以指蟑螂；這個義項和“蟑螂躲在角落裡”的形象最容易聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"There was a roach hiding under the sink.","zh":"水槽下面藏著一隻蟑螂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A roach scurried behind the refrigerator.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d7a42cf8a9046ff","term":"roach","forms":["roach","roaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鯉科魚","explanation":"roach 可指鯉科中的某些魚，常見於關於河流、湖泊和釣魚的語境。","examples":[{"en":"We caught a roach while fishing in the river.","zh":"我們在河裡釣魚時釣到了一條鯉科魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A silver roach flashed beneath the still water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3db051c8db8ab33407bc","word":"cocktail","forms":["cocktail"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b75818f82f50ddd","term":"cocktail","forms":["cocktail","cocktails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雞尾酒","explanation":"指把酒、果汁、糖漿或其他配料調在一起製成的飲料；這是 cocktail 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She ordered a cocktail before dinner.","zh":"她在晚餐前點了一杯雞尾酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This bar makes excellent fruit cocktails.","zh":"這家酒吧調製的水果雞尾酒很棒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocktail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dec7bd9b1d9fc3fc","term":"cocktail","forms":["cocktail","cocktails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合物；混合組合","explanation":"這裡不一定指飲料，而是把幾種物質、因素或事物混在一起形成的組合；它保留了“調進同一杯”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The river contained a cocktail of industrial chemicals.","zh":"這條河裡含有多種工業化學品的混合物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cleaning product contains a cocktail of solvents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocktail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-740d9472155d310672c7","word":"cocoa","forms":["cocoa"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7af4ee66f35ac1b","term":"cocoa","forms":["cocoa","cocoas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可可豆","explanation":"指從可可樹上得到、經過乾燥並部分發酵的種子，是製作巧克力的原料。可以把它看作整條“可可→粉末→飲料”鏈條的起點。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers dried the cocoa beans in the sun.","zh":"農民們把可可豆放在陽光下晾乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers spread the cocoa in the sun to dry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocoa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-465fb87284337a81","term":"cocoa","forms":["cocoa","cocoas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可可粉","explanation":"指把烘烤後的可可豆磨成的棕色粉末，通常不加糖，用來製作巧克力或烘焙食品。它是從可可豆到飲料之間的中間形態。","examples":[{"en":"Add two tablespoons of cocoa powder to the cake mixture.","zh":"在蛋糕麵糊中加入兩湯匙可可粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sift the cocoa into the flour before mixing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocoa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-772bcd4a16a506ce","term":"cocoa","forms":["cocoa","cocoas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱可可","explanation":"指用牛奶、可可粉和糖調成的熱飲，是可可粉進一步加工後的日常飲品。","examples":[{"en":"The children drank cocoa after playing outside.","zh":"孩子們在外面玩耍後喝了熱可可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We warmed our hands around mugs of cocoa.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocoa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23ebce72c4424e81ef48","word":"coconut","forms":["coconut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-635acd2a6c71b145","term":"coconut","forms":["coconut","coconuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"椰子果實","explanation":"指椰子樹結出的整個果實，外面有纖維狀外殼，裡面包著堅硬的種子。日常說到買、摘或開啟的椰子，通常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a fresh coconut at the market.","zh":"她在市場上買了一個新鮮椰子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children found coconuts under the palm trees.","zh":"孩子們在椰子樹下發現了幾個椰子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coconut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1459602a7b5a36c","term":"coconut","forms":["coconut","coconuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶硬殼的椰子種子","explanation":"特指椰子果實裡面那顆堅硬的種子，通常包括硬殼、白色部分和中間的液體。","examples":[{"en":"He cracked the coconut open with a heavy knife.","zh":"他用一把厚重的刀把椰子劈開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She drilled a hole through the coconut's hard shell.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coconut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5694d08a2e53ffcae0c3","word":"code","forms":["code"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09528cc1b62268cd","term":"code","forms":["code","codes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"程式碼；編號","explanation":"指用短字母、數字或其他符號代表某個物品、類別或狀態的一套標記。它與所代表的物件不一定有直觀關係，重點是大家約定這樣讀懂它。","examples":[{"en":"The shipment was assigned the code WRT-9.","zh":"這批貨被分配了編號 WRT-9。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Enter the product code before checking out.","zh":"結賬前請輸入產品程式碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/code","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cba9a953c508e539","term":"code","forms":["code","codes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"規範；行為準則","explanation":"指圍繞某一主題形成的一套原則、規定或行為標準。它把人們應當如何做整理成可遵循的規則，因此和“程式碼”一樣都建立在共同約定上。","examples":[{"en":"Every employee must follow the company's code of conduct.","zh":"每名員工都必須遵守公司的行為準則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team agreed on a simple code for sharing credit.","zh":"團隊約定了一套分配功勞的簡單準則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/code","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9953a5f8f23aa3c9","term":"code","forms":["code","codes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"編碼規則","explanation":"指把資訊從一種形式轉換成另一種形式時所遵循的一套規則。例如，某種符號可以按約定代表數字、文字或聲音，轉換後再按同一規則還原。","examples":[{"en":"The sensor uses a binary code to represent the temperature.","zh":"這個感測器用二進位制編碼表示溫度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The message was stored in a compact code.","zh":"這條資訊以一種緊湊的編碼形式儲存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/code","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0e0be0a82d44fa2","term":"code","forms":["code","codes","coding","coded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"程式設計","explanation":"指用程式語言寫出讓計算機執行的指令，也就是把解決問題的想法寫成計算機能執行的程式碼。它與名詞“計算機程式碼”直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"He learned to code by building simple games.","zh":"他透過製作簡單的遊戲學會了程式設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I code in Python at work.","zh":"我在工作中用 Python 程式設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/code","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37290d74ac4d186e3a8e","word":"coffee","forms":["coffee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-658139973d751d38","term":"coffee","forms":["coffee","coffees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咖啡飲料","explanation":"指把咖啡樹的種子處理後用熱水衝出的飲料，是coffee最核心的意思；在一般語境中不加數量詞時通常就是這種飲料。","examples":[{"en":"I drink coffee every morning before work.","zh":"我每天上班前早上都喝咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coffee is still too hot to drink.","zh":"這咖啡還是太燙，喝不了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f718e102686027a7","term":"coffee","forms":["coffee","coffees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一杯咖啡；一份咖啡","explanation":"指一份已經點好或端上的咖啡，通常可以具體理解為一杯，但不一定強調容器本身。它是從“咖啡飲料”延伸出的可數用法。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have a coffee and a glass of water, please?","zh":"請給我一杯咖啡和一杯水，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ordered two coffees and shared a piece of cake.","zh":"我們點了兩杯咖啡，分著吃了一塊蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e22665cad68137f2ddcd","word":"coffin","forms":["coffin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e754e9271d3a601","term":"coffin","forms":["coffin","coffins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棺材","explanation":"裝放死者遺體、準備埋葬的封閉盒子，就是棺材。這個義項體現了“封閉的盒子”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The family chose a simple wooden coffin for the burial.","zh":"家人為這次下葬選了一口簡樸的木棺材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coffin was carried into the church.","zh":"棺材被抬進了教堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f744584c7c7e68b68f1a","word":"cognitive","forms":["cognitive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a5e6cba1cce4b63","term":"cognitive","forms":["cognitive","more cognitive","most cognitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"認知的；思維的","explanation":"指與大腦處理資訊、理解、推理、記憶或判斷有關的方面，重點是理智活動，而不是情緒反應。它常用來說明某個過程或研究物件屬於“認知這盞燈”照亮的範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of sleep can affect cognitive performance.","zh":"睡眠不足會影響認知表現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course focuses on cognitive development in young children.","zh":"這門課程重點講幼兒的認知發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cognitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3505d43e9a488e9a","term":"cognitive","forms":["cognitive","more cognitive","most cognitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"智力上的；理智的","explanation":"強調與思考、理解和知識活動有關，而不是與感情或身體活動有關；可以把它理解為“認知的”在更寬泛的“智力方面”上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Reading provides both emotional and cognitive benefits.","zh":"閱讀既能帶來情感上的益處，也能帶來智力上的益處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puzzles measure cognitive skills such as reasoning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cognitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e972546000b214f35e6a","word":"coherent","forms":["coherent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-640fcb6ce23ade2b","term":"coherent","forms":["coherent","more coherent","most coherent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"統一成整體的","explanation":"各部分不是孤立或互相沖突的，而是連線在一起，構成一個完整的整體；這是“連貫、有條理”這些意義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The book presents a coherent picture of life in the city.","zh":"這本書連貫地呈現了城市生活的整體面貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The essays combine into a coherent account of the rebellion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coherent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fef47f6621ab229","term":"coherent","forms":["coherent","more coherent","most coherent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"連貫而合乎邏輯的","explanation":"用於觀點、解釋、敘述或論證時，表示內容前後銜接，容易理解，能組成合理的思路。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a coherent explanation of what had happened.","zh":"她對發生的事情作出了連貫而合乎邏輯的解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness was too upset to give a coherent account.","zh":"證人情緒太激動，無法作出連貫的敘述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coherent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3a1984ba0b1d8ad7f9d","word":"coin","forms":["coin"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cafbf7a38802e816","term":"coin","forms":["coin","coins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"硬幣","explanation":"coin 最基本的意思是作為貨幣使用的金屬片，通常是圓形，也可能有其他形狀或中間有孔。它強調的是具體的一枚硬幣，而不是紙鈔。","examples":[{"en":"I found a coin under the sofa.","zh":"我在沙發下面找到了一枚硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She put a few coins into the vending machine.","zh":"她把幾枚硬幣投進了自動售貨機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aeeaa6dc83d951f3","term":"coin","forms":["coin","coins","coining","coined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鑄造硬幣","explanation":"coin 作動詞時，最具體的意思是把金屬加工並製成正式硬幣，就像把金屬壓入模具使其具有固定價值。","examples":[{"en":"The mint coins new dollars every year.","zh":"造幣廠每年鑄造新的美元硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mint coins commemorative pieces for the anniversary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce142d6991e17c23","term":"coin","forms":["coin","coins","coining","coined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"創造詞語","explanation":"coin a word 或 coin a phrase 表示像鑄造硬幣一樣創造出一個新詞或新說法，使它進入使用和流通。","examples":[{"en":"A journalist coined the phrase during the election.","zh":"一名記者在選舉期間創造了這個說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The term was coined to describe the new technology.","zh":"這個術語是為了描述這項新技術而創造的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7836790352e86b98665f","word":"coincidence","forms":["coincidence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74d21cd7a77dd154","term":"coincidence","forms":["coincidence","coincidences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重合；同時發生","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物恰好出現在同一時間、地點，或處於相同狀態，重點是它們在某一點上重疊，而不一定有共同原因。","examples":[{"en":"The coincidence of the two festivals made the city unusually busy.","zh":"兩個節日重合，使這座城市格外繁忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By coincidence, we arrived at the station at exactly the same time.","zh":"真巧，我們恰好在同一時間到達車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coincidence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cfc63225d4f6d76","term":"coincidence","forms":["coincidence","coincidences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巧合","explanation":"指兩件彼此沒有明顯共同原因的事情恰好同時發生或有相似之處，因此看起來像存在某種聯絡，但這種聯絡可能只是偶然的。","examples":[{"en":"It was a coincidence that both of us chose the same book.","zh":"我們倆都選了同一本書，這只是個巧合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Meeting my old roommate there was pure coincidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coincidence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03cdabc88a4848c52345","word":"cola/Coke","forms":["cola","Coke"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-188a986e6a62c0bb","term":"cola","forms":["cola","colas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可樂飲料","explanation":"cola 指以可樂果風味、焦糖和碳酸水等製成的深色碳酸飲料。它是這個詞在現代日常英語中最重要、最容易遇到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have a cola with my sandwich?","zh":"我可以要一杯可樂配三明治嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She does not drink cola very often.","zh":"她不常喝可樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cola","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-545cf54b587a5a6e","term":"cola","forms":["cola","colas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可樂果；可樂果樹","explanation":"cola 可以指可樂果樹屬的植物，也可以指這種樹結出的果實。可樂飲料的名稱正是和這種果實的風味聯絡在一起的。","examples":[{"en":"The cola tree produces nuts with a bitter, stimulating flavor.","zh":"可樂果樹結出的果實帶有苦味和提神作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cola trees thrive in this humid tropical climate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cola","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f1b695a2ca23e9b","term":"Coke","forms":["Coke"],"pos":"noun","zh":"焦炭","explanation":"coke 是煤經過高溫處理後留下的堅硬含碳殘餘物，既能作燃料，也能在鍊鋼過程中提供熱量和碳。可以把它記成煤被燒煉後留下的“黑色核心”。","examples":[{"en":"The factory uses coke to produce steel.","zh":"這家工廠用焦炭鍊鋼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Coke burns hot enough for the furnace.","zh":"焦炭燃燒時能達到足夠高的溫度，供爐子使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Coke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f98fd02064ab8444","term":"Coke","forms":["Coke","cokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可樂飲料","explanation":"在飲料語境中，coke 可以指可口可樂，或更寬泛地指可樂類碳酸飲料。這個畫面是餐館或商店裡的深色汽水，與焦炭和可卡因沒有關係。","examples":[{"en":"She usually drinks coke with her lunch.","zh":"她通常午餐時喝可樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like some coke?","zh":"你想喝點可樂嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Coke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b640b93443908768","term":"Coke","forms":["Coke","Cokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可樂","explanation":"coke 可以泛指可樂類軟飲料，尤其是可口可樂。它和“焦炭”只是拼寫相同，學習時應把餐館裡的飲料畫面單獨記住。","examples":[{"en":"We bought some coke for the party.","zh":"我們為聚會買了一些可樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered a Coke without ice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Coke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e272deecde720ffc773d","word":"cold","forms":["cold"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3fa21edc8345e4f","term":"cold","forms":["cold","colder","coldest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"溫度低的","explanation":"表示某物的溫度低，核心就是“熱度降低了”，通常讓人感覺涼或冷。","examples":[{"en":"The water in the lake was cold even in July.","zh":"湖水即使在七月也很冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I put on a jacket before going outside because the air was cold.","zh":"我出門前穿上了夾克，因為外面的空氣很冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fe435d9c25b082c","term":"cold","forms":["cold","colder","coldest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冷淡的；不友好的","explanation":"把“缺少熱度”用於人際關係，表示一個人的態度疏遠、不友好，讓人感到沒有溫情。","examples":[{"en":"He gave me a cold smile and returned to his desk.","zh":"他冷冷地對我笑了一下，就回到自己的辦公桌前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her cold reply made it clear that she did not want to talk.","zh":"她冷淡的回答表明她不想談話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d25d31e67231cd0","term":"cold","forms":["cold","colds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感冒","explanation":"指一種通常不嚴重的常見疾病，常伴有鼻塞、流鼻涕，有時還會發燒；身體受到寒冷後，可能會出現這種不適。","examples":[{"en":"I caught a cold and stayed home from work.","zh":"我感冒了，只好請假在家休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He caught a cold on the camping trip.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d5a011050205b392ce2","word":"collaboration","forms":["collaboration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a0bec9d125644ef","term":"collaboration","forms":["collaboration","collaborations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合作；協作","explanation":"指兩個人或多個團體共同工作、共同解決問題或共同創作的過程，重點在“一起出力”這一行為本身。","examples":[{"en":"Collaboration can make a difficult project much easier.","zh":"合作可以讓困難的專案容易得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two universities are working in collaboration on a new study.","zh":"這兩所大學正在合作開展一項新研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collaboration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b8f7cd78c60a2bf","term":"collaboration","forms":["collaboration","collaborations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合作作品；合作成果","explanation":"指由雙方或多方合作製作、創作或完成的具體作品、產品或專案；這裡說的是“合作做出來的東西”，而不是合作過程。","examples":[{"en":"Their latest collaboration combines fashion and modern art.","zh":"他們最新的合作作品融合了時尚與現代藝術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The album is their first collaboration in twenty years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collaboration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93bc5d02dc2a24b53653","word":"collapse","forms":["collapse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6c61af390ec1c6a","term":"collapse","forms":["collapse","collapses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倒塌；崩潰；昏倒事件","explanation":"指突然塌下、失去正常支撐或突然倒下這一事件，既可以是建築物倒塌，也可以是人的身體垮掉或某個系統崩潰。","examples":[{"en":"The collapse of the old bridge closed the road for weeks.","zh":"那座舊橋倒塌後，這條路封閉了好幾個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His sudden collapse worried everyone in the office.","zh":"他突然昏倒讓辦公室裡的每個人都很擔心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collapse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c6e5aeaa4784a7e","term":"collapse","forms":["collapse","collapses","collapsing","collapsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然塌下；倒塌","explanation":"指建築、結構或物體失去支撐，突然向下塌掉或散開；核心畫面就是“撐不住了，整個塌下去”。","examples":[{"en":"Part of the ceiling collapsed during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，天花板的一部分塌了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mine collapsed under the weight of the rock.","zh":"礦井承受不住岩石的重量而塌陷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collapse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9e8d0e88f41f044","term":"collapse","forms":["collapse","collapses","collapsing","collapsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然崩潰；徹底失靈","explanation":"指計劃、企業、系統或經濟狀況突然失去運轉能力，徹底失敗；它把“塌下去”的畫面用於抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The project collapsed after its main funder withdrew.","zh":"主要資助方撤資後，這個專案就崩潰了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without quick repairs, the power system could collapse.","zh":"如果不及時維修，電力系統可能會徹底失靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collapse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a46854926e5416bae46","word":"collar","forms":["collar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab95ad860252f349","term":"collar","forms":["collar","collars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣領","explanation":"衣服圍在脖子周圍的部分，尤其是襯衫、外套等上端的衣領。它是“圍住脖子的一圈”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"His shirt collar was folded neatly.","zh":"他的襯衫領子疊得很整齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a coat with a wide collar.","zh":"她穿著一件寬領外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90b6d3e9b7a3df10","term":"collar","forms":["collar","collars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"環狀部件","explanation":"圍住軸、螺栓或其他物體的一圈裝置，用來固定、限制位置或保護表面。它是“衣領圍住脖子”這一形象在機械結構中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"A metal collar holds the pipe in place.","zh":"一個金屬環把管子固定在原位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tighten the collar around the drill bit before switching the machine on.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fdbbefdb4a4607cd42a","word":"colleague","forms":["colleague"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ffec8eeff42a11cf","term":"colleague","forms":["colleague","colleagues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同事；同業夥伴","explanation":"指和自己從事相同或相關職業、在同一單位或組織中工作的人。這個詞的核心不是“朋友”，而是大家在同一個工作圈子裡並肩做事。","examples":[{"en":"I asked a colleague to check the report before I sent it.","zh":"我請一位同事在發出報告前幫我檢查了一遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several of her colleagues attended the conference.","zh":"她的幾位同事參加了那場會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colleague","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81824c90f8a5276bc87e","word":"collect","forms":["collect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-47cd79237ccf8948","term":"collect","forms":["collect","collects","collecting","collected","collectest","collectedst","collecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收集；聚攏","explanation":"把原本分散的東西拿到一起並集中起來，是 collect 最基礎的意思。重點不在於物品是否珍貴，而在於把它們聚到一處。","examples":[{"en":"Please collect all the receipts before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請把所有收據收齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She collected the papers from the three desks.","zh":"她把三張桌子上的檔案都收集到了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa7496e4ae840306df41","word":"collection","forms":["collection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a64ad25285ddb453","term":"collection","forms":["collection","collections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一組收集在一起的東西","explanation":"指被收集、整理或放在一起的一批物品或材料，可以是珍貴收藏，也可以只是雜物。重點不在物品本身，而在它們被看作一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a collection of hand-painted maps from the nineteenth century.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了一批十九世紀的手繪地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a strange collection of boxes and broken tools in the garage.","zh":"車庫裡堆著一批奇怪的箱子和壞掉的工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66a801c3c6d0f6a3","term":"collection","forms":["collection","collections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收集這一行為","explanation":"指把某類東西集中收走或收集起來的活動，重點是過程，而不是最後形成的那一批東西。","examples":[{"en":"Garbage collection starts early on Monday mornings in this neighborhood.","zh":"這個社群週一一大早就開始收垃圾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Weekly collection of food waste begins on Monday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d867c55b793d0858a464","word":"collective","forms":["collective"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0a325a23739913e","term":"collective","forms":["collective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"集體的；合成整體的","explanation":"指許多個體聚攏、合併後形成的整體，重點是“作為一個整體來看”，而不是分別看每個成員。","examples":[{"en":"The team made a collective decision to continue.","zh":"團隊共同作出了繼續下去的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their collective effort solved the problem.","zh":"他們的共同努力解決了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d4fde457a866136","term":"collective","forms":["collective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"集合的（語法）","explanation":"在語法中，collective 表示用一個單數形式指一群人或一組事物；形式上是一個詞，意義上卻包含許多個體。","examples":[{"en":"“Family” is a collective noun for related people.","zh":"“家庭”是表示有親屬關係的一群人的集合名詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The word “team” is collective, even though it is singular in form.","zh":"“隊伍”這個詞雖然形式是單數，卻表示一個群體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d0731bdaa35e411","term":"collective","forms":["collective","collectives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共同體；團體","explanation":"指因共同的事業、興趣或目標而聚在一起的團體；成員仍各自存在，但整體以一個 collective 的身份行動。","examples":[{"en":"The artists formed a collective to share a studio.","zh":"這些藝術家組成了一個團體，共同使用一間工作室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each member of the farming collective receives an equal share of the profits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0736fd5b7cc7ab7dfe82","word":"collector","forms":["collector"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95edc39afa54edeb","term":"collector","forms":["collector","collectors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收集者；收藏者","explanation":"指收集某類物品的人，也可以泛指負責收集、整理某種東西的人或物。重點不在物品是否珍貴，而在於把分散的東西持續收攏起來。","examples":[{"en":"She is an avid collector of vintage postcards.","zh":"她是一個熱衷收藏老式明信片的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum hired a collector to find local folk art.","zh":"博物館聘請了一名蒐集當地民間藝術品的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collector","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5857a3bacb1a2e0d","term":"collector","forms":["collector","collectors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收款員；徵收員","explanation":"指受僱向別人收取款項的人，例如稅款、車費或賬單費用。這裡收集的不是物品，而是應付的錢。","examples":[{"en":"The utility company sent a collector to discuss the overdue bill.","zh":"公用事業公司派了一名收款員來處理這筆逾期賬單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ticket collector moved slowly through the crowded train.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collector","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-776af9401679287d8d33","word":"college","forms":["college"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b068965141f04d63","term":"college","forms":["college","colleges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學院或大學","explanation":"指提供高等教育的學校或教育機構，是college最核心、最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"She applied to three colleges last year.","zh":"她去年申請了三所大學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He studied engineering at a college near home.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/college","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01c5a180d1b18074","term":"college","forms":["college","colleges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美國的大學教育或大學","explanation":"在美國英語中，college既可以指提供本科教育的大學，也可以泛指大學階段或大學生活。","examples":[{"en":"My brother is still in college.","zh":"我哥哥還在上大學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her oldest daughter starts college in September.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/college","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9550e70a7c3619220570","word":"collision","forms":["collision"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed38af64fbdbe649","term":"collision","forms":["collision","collisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相撞；碰撞事故","explanation":"指兩個或多個真實的人、車輛或物體相撞這一事件，尤其常用於交通事故；重點是“撞在一起”這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"The collision blocked traffic for nearly an hour.","zh":"這起相撞事故導致交通堵塞了將近一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two cyclists were injured in the collision.","zh":"兩名騎腳踏車的人在相撞事故中受了傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9de12492f101fee8","term":"collision","forms":["collision","collisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物理學中的碰撞","explanation":"物理學中指兩個或多個物體在很短時間內相互施力的事件；它不一定要求兩個物體真正接觸，所以比日常所說的“撞上”範圍更寬。","examples":[{"en":"The particles change direction after the collision.","zh":"這些粒子在碰撞後改變了方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists measured the energy released during the collision.","zh":"科學家測量了碰撞過程中釋放的能量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fe82d1c2d9c2abeca43","word":"colloquial","forms":["colloquial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea873f9cce0b0360","term":"colloquial","forms":["colloquial","most colloquial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"口語的；非正式的","explanation":"指日常交談中常用、聽起來親切自然的語言或表達，而不是正式書面語。它強調使用場合和語氣，不表示這種說法本身有錯誤。","examples":[{"en":"This phrase is quite colloquial, so avoid it in a formal report.","zh":"這個短語很口語化，所以不要在正式報告中使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used colloquial language to make the explanation feel friendly.","zh":"她使用口語化的語言，讓解釋聽起來更親切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colloquial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1bde35e6a83b9b1","term":"colloquial","forms":["colloquial","most colloquial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"會話式的；聊天般的","explanation":"強調說話或文字帶有交談的感覺，像人在面對面聊天，而不只是單純說明它不正式。這個意義和“口語的”相連，但更突出交流的語氣和風格。","examples":[{"en":"The article has a relaxed, colloquial tone.","zh":"這篇文章的語氣輕鬆，像是在聊天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The letter's colloquial tone made it feel unusually personal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colloquial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16b8bf238bac841d7eeb","word":"colonial","forms":["colonial"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18e724c2150e8dd3","term":"colonial","forms":["colonial","more colonial","most colonial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"殖民地的","explanation":"表示某事物屬於殖民地，或直接與殖民地的制度、生活和管理有關，是理解 colonial 的基礎含義。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displays colonial maps and documents.","zh":"這家博物館展出了殖民地時期的地圖和檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city still has several colonial buildings.","zh":"這座城市仍保留著幾座殖民時期的建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colonial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00c1388bc61cef3a","term":"colonial","forms":["colonial","more colonial","most colonial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"殖民時期的","explanation":"特指某個國家或地區處於殖民統治時期的事物，例如殖民時期的建築、法律或社會生活。","examples":[{"en":"Many colonial streets have been preserved in the old town.","zh":"老城區保留了許多殖民時期的街道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum occupies a restored colonial courthouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colonial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7786e1f40e8a5784ded","word":"colony","forms":["colony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-077841d956fd80ae","term":"colony","forms":["colony","colonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殖民地","explanation":"指受另一個國家政治控制、通常由該國移民及其後代居住的地區。這個意義保留了“從原處遷出，在另一處建立聚居地”的核心圖景，常用於歷史和政治語境。","examples":[{"en":"The island was once a Spanish colony.","zh":"這座島曾經是西班牙的殖民地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The former colony became independent in 1962.","zh":"這個前殖民地於1962年獲得獨立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de7335e735607466","term":"colony","forms":["colony","colonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海外同胞社群","explanation":"指生活在另一個國家、城市或地區的一群同國籍、同族或使用同一種語言的人，也可指他們所居住的區域。它是“聚居地”概念從殖民歷史擴充套件到普通社群的用法，不一定包含政治統治關係。","examples":[{"en":"A large colony of Indian families lives in the city.","zh":"這個城市裡住著一個規模很大的印度家庭社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small Polish colony grew around the factory.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86b5829593bf1c9b","term":"colony","forms":["colony","colonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物群體","explanation":"指同種或不同種生物在一起緊密生活、彼此形成關聯的群體，例如螞蟻、珊瑚等。這裡的“聚居地”不再是人類建立的地方，而是生物共同形成的群落。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers found a colony of ants beneath the stones.","zh":"研究人員在石頭下面發現了一個螞蟻群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coral colony is damaged by rising water temperatures.","zh":"這個珊瑚群落受到水溫升高的破壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74284d9dcbcc09928ca5","word":"color","forms":["color"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cebcd5073fc2817e","term":"color","forms":["color","colors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顏色；色彩","explanation":"指可見光呈現給眼睛的色彩，是“給事物增添色彩”這一記憶的最基本含義；這裡說的是顏色這種現象，而不是某一個具體色調。","examples":[{"en":"Humans can see color, but some animals see it differently.","zh":"人類能看見顏色，但有些動物看到的顏色與我們不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room felt warmer after we added more color.","zh":"增添更多色彩後，房間讓人感覺更溫暖了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/color","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-081db512617bbfd5","term":"color","forms":["color","colors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表現力；豐富細節","explanation":"指語言、故事、人物描寫或評論中豐富而有趣的細節和特色，使表達更生動、更能吸引人。就像給普通表達添上色彩一樣，這裡的color不是視覺顏色，而是感染力。","examples":[{"en":"Her stories bring color to everyday life.","zh":"她的故事為日常生活增添了豐富的色彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interviews add color to the report.","zh":"這些採訪讓這篇報道更加生動豐富。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/color","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fe69ab623228a24","term":"color","forms":["color","colors","coloring","colored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給某物上色","explanation":"把color記成“給事物增添色彩”：它可以表示用顏料或其他方式給物體加上某種顏色，重點是改變物體的外觀。","examples":[{"en":"We decided to color the bedroom walls pale green.","zh":"我們決定把臥室的牆壁塗成淺綠色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She colored the wooden box bright blue.","zh":"她把木盒塗成了鮮藍色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/color","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3bee16cda595108b","term":"color","forms":["color","colors","coloring","colored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給圖畫塗色","explanation":"指在已經畫好輪廓的圖畫中填入顏色，就像孩子用彩筆或蠟筆把圖畫增添色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The children sat at the table and colored for an hour.","zh":"孩子們坐在桌邊塗了一個小時的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He colored a picture of a dragon with his new crayons.","zh":"他用新蠟筆給一幅龍的圖畫塗了色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/color","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22040cde5778d72e2ab8","word":"colorful","forms":["colorful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e889a262947e3baa","term":"colorful","forms":["colorful","more colorful","most colorful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"色彩鮮明多樣的","explanation":"指包含多種醒目顏色，整體看起來鮮豔、豐富或富有視覺變化。它可以形容衣物、裝飾、圖畫、市場等有明顯色彩的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The market was full of colorful umbrellas.","zh":"市場裡到處都是色彩鮮豔的雨傘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a colorful scarf with her plain coat.","zh":"她穿著一件樸素的外套，配了一條色彩豐富的圍巾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colorful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49bfee82bd15f25b","term":"colorful","forms":["colorful","more colorful","most colorful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"豐富多彩、引人注意的","explanation":"把“顏色豐富、容易吸引目光”的感覺引申到人、生活、經歷或寫作上，表示內容複雜有趣、個性鮮明、充滿活力或與眾不同。","examples":[{"en":"She has led a colorful life, traveling to many countries and changing careers several times.","zh":"她一生豐富多彩，去過許多國家，還幾次轉換過職業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His colorful career included sailing, acting, and gold mining.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colorful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-881d5fb60090f59aabba","word":"column","forms":["column"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9d634d3d5943a58","term":"column","forms":["column","columns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築支柱","explanation":"指直立的柱子，通常用來支撐屋頂、橫樑等上方結構，有時也只是作為裝飾。它是“豎直支撐物”這一核心影象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The stone columns support the roof of the old temple.","zh":"這些石柱支撐著古廟的屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two marble columns stand at the entrance.","zh":"入口處立著兩根大理石柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/column","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-627079c8f76219d0","term":"column","forms":["column","columns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表格豎列","explanation":"指表格中從上到下排列的一列資料或專案。它保留了“豎直排列成柱狀”的形象，是現代資訊處理中最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"Enter each student's name in the first column.","zh":"把每個學生的姓名填在第一列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Click the column heading to sort the results.","zh":"點選列標題即可對結果排序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/column","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3b6d035a034aaa8","term":"column","forms":["column","columns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"版面文字欄","explanation":"指頁面上從上到下排版、需要逐行閱讀的一欄文字，尤其是在同一頁並排排出多欄文字時。它是“把內容豎著分成一列”的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The article is printed in two narrow columns.","zh":"這篇文章排成兩欄窄窄的文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the text from the top of the left column.","zh":"請從左欄頂部開始閱讀文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/column","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27b598187519c346900b","word":"columnist","forms":["columnist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-266ec61e853ae3c3","term":"columnist","forms":["columnist","columnists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專欄作家","explanation":"指定期為報紙、雜誌或其他媒體的固定專欄撰寫文章的人，通常有相對穩定的寫作主題和讀者。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper hired a new sports columnist.","zh":"這家報紙聘請了一位新的體育專欄作家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A local columnist questioned the proposed road expansion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/columnist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef4e3f50798387464764","word":"comb","forms":["comb"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7434327804a0d700","term":"comb","forms":["comb","combs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"梳子","explanation":"有許多細齒、用來整理頭髮或其他纖維的工具；這是comb最基本、最容易聯想到的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I keep a small comb in my bag.","zh":"我在包裡放著一把小梳子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ran a comb through her hair before the meeting.","zh":"開會前，她用梳子把頭髮梳了一遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49506e9a6eab21f2","term":"comb","forms":["comb","combs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜂巢","explanation":"指蜜蜂用許多六邊形小室連成的蜂巢；這些整齊重複的隔室讓人聯想到梳子的齒和格狀結構。","examples":[{"en":"The beekeeper lifted a heavy comb filled with honey.","zh":"養蜂人提起了一塊裝滿蜂蜜的沉重蜂巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wild bees built a comb under the roof.","zh":"野蜂在屋簷下築了一個蜂巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7fc82869c58f8569","term":"comb","forms":["comb","combs","combing","combed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"梳理","explanation":"用有齒的梳子整理頭髮、鬍鬚或類似纖維；這是由名詞“梳子”直接發展來的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I comb my hair before I leave the house.","zh":"我出門前會梳頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He combed the knots out of the child's hair.","zh":"他把孩子頭髮裡的結梳開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ebb9b7ed9f3a7f74","term":"comb","forms":["comb","combs","combing","combed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徹底搜查","explanation":"像梳子一遍遍掃過頭髮那樣，把一個地方或範圍細緻地查遍，以尋找人、物品或證據。","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers combed the beach for the missing child.","zh":"志願者徹底搜查了海灘，尋找失蹤的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor combed through the report for errors.","zh":"編輯仔細查閱了報告，尋找其中的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d988fa37098528770f0","word":"combat","forms":["combat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39f87879334ebac3","term":"combat","forms":["combat","combats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戰鬥；交戰","explanation":"combat指雙方正面交鋒的戰鬥，常讓人聯想到有組織的作戰或使用武器的戰鬥，但也可以泛指激烈的對抗。","examples":[{"en":"Several soldiers were injured in combat.","zh":"幾名士兵在戰鬥中受了傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two warriors met in single combat.","zh":"兩名武士進行了一對一的決鬥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f0ffa431120b11c","term":"combat","forms":["combat","combats","combating","combatting","combated","combatted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對抗；遏制","explanation":"作動詞時，combat就是主動迎上去與問題或對手鬥爭，努力削弱或消除它；它特別常用於對抗疾病、犯罪、貧困等問題。","examples":[{"en":"The new program aims to combat drug addiction.","zh":"這項新計劃旨在遏制毒癮問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trees can help combat air pollution.","zh":"樹木有助於對抗空氣汙染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f3258eaa1979a8be032","word":"combination","forms":["combination"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a9241a4b0a11a017","term":"combination","forms":["combination","combinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組合；結合","explanation":"指把兩個或多個不同的東西放在一起的行為、狀態，或這種結合本身；重點是“合在一起”這個過程。","examples":[{"en":"The combination of fresh air and exercise helped her sleep better.","zh":"新鮮空氣和鍛鍊結合起來，讓她睡得更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This medicine works best in combination with a healthy diet.","zh":"這種藥和健康飲食結合使用效果最好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbc32c7b03b41ae2","term":"combination","forms":["combination","combinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組合物；搭配","explanation":"指由多個元素組合成的具體結果，例如顏色、味道、材料或風格的搭配；這裡關注的是“組合出來的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The soup has an unusual combination of sweet and spicy flavors.","zh":"這道湯把甜味和辣味搭配得很特別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Blue and yellow make a bright combination.","zh":"藍色和黃色搭配起來很明亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f895893037cecd0c","term":"combination","forms":["combination","combinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"密碼；密碼組合","explanation":"指用來開啟密碼鎖、保險箱等的數字或字母序列；這些符號按照規定排列，組成一把“組合盒”的鑰匙。","examples":[{"en":"I forgot the combination to my locker.","zh":"我忘了儲物櫃的密碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write down the safe combination somewhere secure.","zh":"把保險箱密碼記在安全的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bd1454e4848ba9ec483","word":"combine","forms":["combine"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d79faa78425214bc","term":"combine","forms":["combine","combines","combining","combined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……結合起來","explanation":"表示有意把兩個或更多的人、物或活動放到一起，使它們成為一個整體。這是 combine 最基本、最值得先掌握的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Combine the flour and water in a large bowl.","zh":"把麵粉和水在大碗裡混合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school combined the two classes for the afternoon.","zh":"學校把兩個班合併起來上下午的課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe84027367627f1e","term":"combine","forms":["combine","combines","combining","combined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"兼具；把特點結合起來","explanation":"表示某人或某物同時擁有兩種或更多能共同發揮作用的特點，重點不是把東西物理地混在一起，而是“兼有這些特性”。","examples":[{"en":"The new design combines comfort with a modern look.","zh":"這種新設計兼具舒適性和現代外觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The design combines elegance with practical storage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-129db52cf52bcfc3","term":"combine","forms":["combine","combines","combining","combined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結合在一起","explanation":"表示兩個或更多事物自行合到一起，形成共同的狀態或結果；這裡不突出誰把它們合起來。","examples":[{"en":"When the two chemicals combine, they produce heat.","zh":"這兩種化學物質結合時會產生熱量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ingredients combine to form a thick paste.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/combine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c19636ddea25f0a1335","word":"come","forms":["come"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a8d81231a813a1b","term":"come","forms":["come","comes","coming","came","comen","comed","comest","camest","camedst","cometh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向這裡來","explanation":"表示從別處朝說話者或所關注的地點移動，重點是“來到這個參照點”。","examples":[{"en":"Come into the kitchen and see this.","zh":"到廚房來看看這個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She came toward us when she heard her name.","zh":"她聽到自己的名字後朝我們走來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/come","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae6f363f00a38376","term":"come","forms":["come","comes","coming","came","comen","comed","comest","camest","camedst","cometh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到達","explanation":"表示抵達某地或某個目的地，強調移動已經結束併到達了那裡。","examples":[{"en":"We came home just before midnight.","zh":"我們在午夜前剛回到家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several guests came late to the wedding.","zh":"幾位客人很晚才到婚禮現場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/come","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90e710e7eb274bbd","term":"come","forms":["come","comes","coming","came","comen","comed","comest","camest","camedst","cometh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出現","explanation":"表示疼痛、問題、機會等現象出現或顯現出來，也可表示這種現象反覆出現。","examples":[{"en":"A strange smell came from the basement.","zh":"一股奇怪的氣味從地下室傳來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The headache comes and goes.","zh":"頭痛時有時無。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/come","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff83e66c1a61a2a71711","word":"comedian","forms":["comedian"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-864cd2dec43e1a0d","term":"comedian","forms":["comedian","comedians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜劇演員","explanation":"指透過講笑話、說逗趣的話或進行幽默表演來娛樂觀眾的人，通常是這種表演的職業從業者。","examples":[{"en":"The comedian had the whole audience laughing within minutes.","zh":"那位喜劇演員幾分鐘內就逗得全場觀眾大笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to become a professional comedian.","zh":"她希望成為一名職業喜劇演員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comedian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db88ebfec813090f","term":"comedian","forms":["comedian","comedians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"很逗的人","explanation":"泛指某人很幽默、很會逗人笑，不一定以此為職業；有時只是說某一次表現得特別有趣。","examples":[{"en":"My brother is such a comedian when he tells stories about school.","zh":"我哥哥講學校裡的故事時特別逗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your little brother is quite a comedian at breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comedian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03fefb8d091a480a00e0","word":"comedy","forms":["comedy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95b3f5c646cb23b0","term":"comedy","forms":["comedy","comedies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕鬆的喜劇作品","explanation":"指情調輕鬆、令人發笑，並且通常以圓滿結局收尾的戲劇作品；重點是這部具體的作品，而不是整個體裁。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a romantic comedy after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們看了一部浪漫喜劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The play begins sadly but ends as a comedy.","zh":"這部戲開頭很悲傷，但最後變成了喜劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68f403fcee806efc","term":"comedy","forms":["comedy","comedies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幽默或諷刺的戲劇作品","explanation":"指一部以輕鬆、幽默或諷刺為主要風格的戲劇、電影或電視作品；它不一定像傳統喜劇那樣有圓滿結局。","examples":[{"en":"The new film is a sharp political comedy.","zh":"這部新電影是一部尖銳的政治諷刺喜劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That comedy deals with grief as well as laughter.","zh":"那部喜劇既寫悲傷，也寫歡笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1bc8020660c12da8","term":"comedy","forms":["comedy","comedies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜劇表演或幽默娛樂","explanation":"指由笑話、諷刺或幽默表演構成的娛樂內容，尤其指觀看或從事喜劇表演這件事。這裡關注的是表演活動或娛樂形式，不是某一部作品。","examples":[{"en":"My sister performs comedy at a small club on weekends.","zh":"我姐姐週末在一家小俱樂部做喜劇表演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An evening of comedy helped everyone relax.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d51f791051c2e5f9112c","word":"comet","forms":["comet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b778b3c2eb9e9aee","term":"comet","forms":["comet","comets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彗星天體","explanation":"彗星是主要由冰、塵埃和岩石顆粒組成的小型太陽系天體。它沿著偏心軌道繞太陽執行，靠近太陽時冰物質氣化，形成周圍的彗發，有時還出現明亮的彗尾。","examples":[{"en":"The comet will pass close to the Sun next year.","zh":"這顆彗星明年將近距離經過太陽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists detected ice and dust around the comet.","zh":"科學家在這顆彗星周圍探測到了冰和塵埃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-889b9e3739f8bc2c","term":"comet","forms":["comet","comets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彗星現象","explanation":"comet 也可以指天空中呈現出彗星外觀的可見天象，重點在於人們看到的明亮天體和彗尾，而不只是它作為物質天體的組成。","examples":[{"en":"A bright comet appeared above the northern horizon.","zh":"一顆明亮的彗星出現在北方地平線上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The comet was visible just before dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e9498bf9ee96ee667bc","word":"comfort","forms":["comfort"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73edec4709c21f04","term":"comfort","forms":["comfort","comforts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舒適；安逸","explanation":"comfort指身體或生活處於輕鬆、方便、沒有明顯不適的狀態，就像得到了一層讓人放鬆的保護。","examples":[{"en":"The new chair lets me work in comfort for hours.","zh":"這把新椅子讓我能舒舒服服地工作好幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the hike, we welcomed the comfort of clean beds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comfort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92d2a068d53d1030","term":"comfort","forms":["comfort","comforts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安慰；慰藉","explanation":"comfort指在悲傷、痛苦或擔憂中減輕壓力、讓人好受一些的安慰；它可以來自一句話、一個人或一件事。","examples":[{"en":"Her kind words were a great comfort to me.","zh":"她的貼心話給了我很大的安慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His daughter's letters brought comfort during his illness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comfort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70a454583ce31c0a","term":"comfort","forms":["comfort","comforts","comforting","comforted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安慰；撫慰","explanation":"comfort作動詞時，表示用陪伴、話語或行動減輕某人的悲傷、恐懼或痛苦，把“安心的力量”給到對方。","examples":[{"en":"She comforted her brother after he lost his job.","zh":"哥哥失業後，她安慰了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She comforted the frightened child until his father arrived.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comfort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46fd05f35b5591e22afa","word":"comfortable","forms":["comfortable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d365e68d0e3e3041","term":"comfortable","forms":["comfortable","comfortabler","more comfortable","comfortablest","most comfortable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"舒適的；讓人舒服的","explanation":"指物品、環境或身體感受讓人覺得輕鬆、舒服，沒有明顯的不適。它是這個詞最直接、最基礎的意思。","examples":[{"en":"This is the most comfortable bed I’ve ever slept in.","zh":"這是我睡過的最舒適的床。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wear comfortable shoes for the long walk.","zh":"長途步行時要穿舒適的鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comfortable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d594c49e64e4a486","term":"comfortable","forms":["comfortable","comfortabler","more comfortable","comfortablest","most comfortable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到自在的；過得舒服的","explanation":"指人在某個地方或處境中覺得安心、自在，能夠舒舒服服地待著。這裡強調人的狀態，而不只是某件物品本身柔軟或舒適。","examples":[{"en":"Make yourself comfortable while I finish cooking.","zh":"我做完飯以前，你先隨意坐著，別拘束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt comfortable speaking honestly to her mentor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comfortable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05c50735d306e9742849","word":"comic(s)","forms":["comic","comics"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14dd5e02e1f77fc8","term":"comic","forms":["comic","more comic","most comic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"喜劇的；與喜劇有關的","explanation":"表示和喜劇這種文學、戲劇或表演型別有關，重點是“屬於喜劇這一類”，不一定單獨說明某個場面很好笑。","examples":[{"en":"Her comic talent was obvious from the first scene.","zh":"從第一場戲就能看出她的喜劇才華。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel combines comic scenes with serious moments.","zh":"這部小說把喜劇場面和嚴肅時刻結合在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7956d3d48a27e3ce","term":"comic","forms":["comic","more comic","most comic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"逗笑的；喜劇性的","explanation":"表示作品、表演者或表達方式使用了喜劇技巧，目的是讓人覺得好笑、輕鬆或有娛樂性。","examples":[{"en":"The actor gave a brilliant comic performance.","zh":"這名演員帶來了一場精彩的喜劇表演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film uses comic details to keep the story light.","zh":"這部電影用一些逗笑的細節讓故事保持輕鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d189d640b39ff48","term":"comic","forms":["comic","comics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜劇演員","explanation":"指以講笑話、表演喜劇或製造幽默效果為職業的人，尤其常指單口喜劇演員。","examples":[{"en":"The comic had the audience laughing within minutes.","zh":"這名喜劇演員幾分鐘內就把觀眾逗笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked as a comic before appearing in films.","zh":"她在出演電影前曾是一名喜劇演員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-79b5e231f23312ab","term":"comics","forms":["comics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漫畫媒介","explanation":"指由連續畫面、文字和畫格等組成的漫畫媒介或藝術形式，涵蓋漫畫書、連環漫畫以及其他連續影象敘事作品；重點是這種表達方式本身，而不是某一個具體物件。","examples":[{"en":"She studies how comics tell stories through pictures and words.","zh":"她研究漫畫如何透過影象和文字講故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Comics have become an important form of modern art.","zh":"漫畫已經成為現代藝術的一種重要形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f36a4e58670569181595","word":"comma","forms":["comma"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"comma","forms":["comma"],"pos":"n.","zh":"逗號","examples":[{"en":"Put a comma after the introductory phrase.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A missing comma can change the meaning of a sentence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d347fd948b66308f502","word":"command","forms":["command"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1fc1a4d9f12e61d","term":"command","forms":["command","commands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"命令；指示","explanation":"指要求別人做某事的話，重點是說話者有權要求對方服從。","examples":[{"en":"The officer gave the soldiers a clear command.","zh":"軍官向士兵下達了明確的命令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone stopped when they heard the command.","zh":"所有人聽到命令後都停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/command","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-449fd123761cb780","term":"command","forms":["command","commands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指揮權；控制權","explanation":"指有權下令、管理或支配某人某物的資格；這就是“伸出的手”進一步變成握在手裡的權力。","examples":[{"en":"She took command of the rescue team.","zh":"她接管了救援隊的指揮權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She assumed command when the captain was injured.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/command","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8db6bae93b516697","term":"command","forms":["command","commands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"掌控；駕馭能力","explanation":"指對局勢、技能或資源有很強的控制和駕馭能力，不一定意味著正式職位上的權力。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot kept command of the aircraft during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，飛行員仍然牢牢控制著飛機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her command of French impressed the visiting delegation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/command","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d80e3a834e40af4","term":"command","forms":["command","commands","commanding","commanded","commandest","commandedst","commandeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"命令；下令","explanation":"指以權威要求某人做某事，是“伸出的手”最直接的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The guard commanded us to leave the building.","zh":"警衛命令我們離開大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge commanded the room to remain silent.","zh":"法官命令在場人員保持安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/command","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65a28b5fb85a479f","term":"command","forms":["command","commands","commanding","commanded","commandest","commandedst","commandeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指揮；統率","explanation":"指掌握並行使對軍隊、船隻或其他組織的最高控制權。","examples":[{"en":"He commanded a small naval unit for three years.","zh":"他指揮一支小型海軍部隊達三年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The admiral commanded the fleet during the evacuation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/command","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc2dff6ac3e4ca52fece","word":"commander","forms":["commander"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d72bfacd59a8fc1","term":"commander","forms":["commander","commanders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍事指揮官","explanation":"指負責指揮和管理軍隊、艦隊或軍事組織的人，核心概念就是“掌握命令權並帶隊的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The commander ordered the troops to move before dawn.","zh":"指揮官命令部隊在黎明前出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became the commander of the base last year.","zh":"她去年成為這座基地的指揮官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commander","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-724b1563768c1887","term":"commander","forms":["commander","commanders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海軍少校級軍銜","explanation":"在一些英語海軍體系中，這是高於 lieutenant commander、低於 captain 的軍官軍銜；它既可指軍銜，也可指擁有該軍銜的人。","examples":[{"en":"Commander Lee briefed the crew before departure.","zh":"李指揮官在出發前向船員作了簡報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commander inspected the ship in the afternoon.","zh":"這名海軍軍官下午檢查了軍艦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commander","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c44bb2fd516909dab78a","word":"comment","forms":["comment"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c3f4b6f2efe847e","term":"comment","forms":["comment","comments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"評論；意見","explanation":"指對人、事或觀點所作的口頭或書面說明，可以只是表達看法，不一定是在批評。","examples":[{"en":"She made a helpful comment on my draft.","zh":"她對我的草稿提了一條很有幫助的意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have no comment on the decision.","zh":"我對這個決定無可奉告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49251d88789c26df","term":"comment","forms":["comment","comments","commenting","commented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"評論；說出看法","explanation":"指標對某人或某事說出或寫下自己的看法，就是把“說明”這個核心概念變成一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The minister declined to comment on the report.","zh":"部長拒絕對這份報告發表評論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She commented that the room was unusually quiet.","zh":"她說這個房間異常安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af6b51b395e68b29","term":"comment","forms":["comment","comments","commenting","commented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發表意見；談論","explanation":"強調進行評論或表達觀點這一行為，可以不點明具體評論內容。","examples":[{"en":"Several readers commented on the new policy.","zh":"幾位讀者對這項新政策發表了意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mayor declined to comment on the allegations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1a0c11a728e36ab0181","word":"commentary","forms":["commentary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18bd3638fc232b52","term":"commentary","forms":["commentary","commentaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"評論；註釋；評述","explanation":"指圍繞一篇作品、文章或某個主題所作的系統解釋和評論，常常幫助讀者理解原文的意思、背景或價值。它可以是一段評述，也可以是專門解釋整部作品的書。","examples":[{"en":"She wrote a thoughtful commentary on the film.","zh":"她寫了一篇很有見地的電影評論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book includes a detailed commentary on the poem.","zh":"這本書收錄了對這首詩的詳細註釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commentary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca577dacf07c4274","term":"commentary","forms":["commentary","commentaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現場解說","explanation":"指比賽或其他事件進行時，由解說員透過電視、廣播或網路實時講述現場情況。它就像把正在發生的事情即時說給觀眾聽。","examples":[{"en":"We turned on the radio to hear the live commentary.","zh":"我們開啟收音機收聽現場解說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commentator's commentary kept the match exciting.","zh":"解說員的現場解說讓這場比賽一直很精彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commentary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a4a210547932b9fcc47","word":"commentator","forms":["commentator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ad53b6d5c8a5bfe","term":"commentator","forms":["commentator","commentators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解說員；評論員","explanation":"指在比賽、節目或公共事件中持續說明情況、分析進展並把資訊傳達給觀眾或聽眾的人，最常見的是體育比賽解說員，也可以指新聞或社會話題評論員。","examples":[{"en":"She worked as a football commentator for ten years.","zh":"她當了十年的足球解說員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commentator explained why the team changed its strategy.","zh":"解說員解釋了這支球隊改變策略的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commentator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cfb240efa8670bfe5c76","word":"commerce","forms":["commerce"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46004041e9958d91","term":"commerce","forms":["commerce","commerces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業貿易","explanation":"指貨物或商品在不同地方、群體或國家之間進行的大規模買賣和交換，重點是商業活動，而不只是一次普通購物。","examples":[{"en":"The port has been a center of international commerce for centuries.","zh":"這座港口幾個世紀以來一直是國際商業中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement opened new opportunities for commerce between the two countries.","zh":"這項協議為兩國之間的商業貿易帶來了新的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commerce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c9d30f4cbbc7e56","term":"commerce","forms":["commerce","commerces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交往；往來","explanation":"表示人與人或社會群體之間的接觸、交往和來往，是從“彼此交換、往來”這一核心概念引申出來的舊式用法。","examples":[{"en":"He avoided commerce with the local nobles.","zh":"他避免與當地貴族交往。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The remote settlement had little commerce with neighboring towns.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commerce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-d01acdec3a3b87b33882","word":"commercial","forms":["commercial"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ac369073f34e364","term":"commercial","forms":["commercial","more commercial","most commercial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"商業的；與商業有關的","explanation":"表示某事物與買賣、貿易、營利活動或商業機構有關。它抓住的是“圍繞商業運轉”這一核心，而不一定表示已經成功或價格很高。","examples":[{"en":"The town grew into an important commercial center.","zh":"這個城鎮逐漸發展成了重要的商業中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The property is zoned for commercial use.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commercial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa9f3e9d7b83795d","term":"commercial","forms":["commercial","commercials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業廣告","explanation":"指廣播、電視等常見媒體中播放的一則廣告。它就是把商業資訊做成短片或音訊，供觀眾或聽眾收看、收聽。","examples":[{"en":"She appeared in a commercial for a new breakfast cereal.","zh":"她出演了一則新早餐麥片的廣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That commercial always interrupts the most exciting scene.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commercial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22c2ada68577df8a7c9b","word":"commission","forms":["commission"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8eb5efddb1cd767","term":"commission","forms":["commission","commissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式職權或任命","explanation":"指官方授予某人的職務、權力或任命，尤其常用於軍官獲得正式軍職；它仍然保留“被正式派去辦事”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She received her commission as a naval officer after completing her training.","zh":"她完成訓練後獲任命為海軍軍官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He received his commission as a lieutenant in June.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2ee14996cf8ff07","term":"commission","forms":["commission","commissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受託完成的工作","explanation":"指替別人完成的具體委託，尤其是藝術品、設計或公共工程等需要專門製作的專案。","examples":[{"en":"The architect is working on a commission for a new library.","zh":"這位建築師正在承接一個新圖書館的委託專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mural was her largest commission that year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4ec21c44b1f4c1d","term":"commission","forms":["commission","commissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代理佣金","explanation":"指代理人、經紀人或銷售人員替別人完成交易後得到的費用，是“替別人辦成事”的報酬。","examples":[{"en":"The agent earns a five percent commission on every sale.","zh":"這名代理每筆銷售都能獲得百分之五的佣金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without the sale, the broker would receive no commission at all.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a73fc90b0f750e0","term":"commission","forms":["commission","commissions","commissioning","commissioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式派遣或授權","explanation":"指正式派某人或某機構去完成任務，或授予其執行任務的權力，就是把任務正式送給對方。","examples":[{"en":"The government commissioned a team to inspect the bridge.","zh":"政府委託一個團隊檢查這座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council commissioned her to investigate the missing funds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d12a8014a2d16ca3","term":"commission","forms":["commission","commissions","commissioning","commissioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"委託訂作","explanation":"指付費請藝術家、設計師或工匠製作某件作品或物品，是把具體作品作為任務交給對方。","examples":[{"en":"They commissioned a local artist to paint a portrait of their dog.","zh":"他們委託一位當地藝術家為他們的狗畫肖像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library commissioned a sculpture for its entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9505cacb7c710ed17125","word":"commit","forms":["commit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fae8f2fb01c824e9","term":"commit","forms":["commit","commits","committing","committed","committest","committedst","committeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"犯下；實施","explanation":"指做出通常被認為錯誤、違法或有罪過的事，尤其是犯罪、過失或罪行；這裡是把一個行為“交出去”，讓它真正發生。","examples":[{"en":"He was arrested for committing fraud.","zh":"他因實施欺詐而被捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gang committed several robberies before being caught.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cefafd2620f002c","term":"commit","forms":["commit","commits","committing","committed","committest","committedst","committeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承諾；使自己投入","explanation":"指透過一個明確決定把自己約束在某個行動、目標或關係上，也可表示某個行動使人承擔風險或陷入不利處境。","examples":[{"en":"She committed herself to training every morning.","zh":"她承諾每天早晨訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company committed to reducing its waste.","zh":"公司承諾減少廢棄物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f18125416ba21b7","term":"commit","forms":["commit","commits","committing","committed","committest","committedst","committeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提交併永久儲存","explanation":"在資料庫中，指確認一組事務改動，使它們正式成為資料庫的一部分，通常不能再被當作未完成的暫存操作。","examples":[{"en":"The application commits the transaction only after all checks pass.","zh":"應用程式只有在所有檢查透過後才提交事務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Commit the changes before closing your development session.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a19f0fb4be54511524b","word":"commitment","forms":["commitment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fb5143e36b7f681","term":"commitment","forms":["commitment","commitments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未來承諾","explanation":"指答應將來做某事的承諾或協議，重點是已經把未來的行動交給自己承擔。它可以是個人對他人的保證，也可以是雙方約定要履行的事項。","examples":[{"en":"She made a commitment to finish the project by Friday.","zh":"她承諾在星期五前完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We cannot take on another financial commitment right now.","zh":"我們現在無法再承擔一項財務承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commitment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e16d69edf3d66472","term":"commitment","forms":["commitment","commitments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投入和忠誠","explanation":"指在感情或思想上堅定地投入某項行動、事業或某段關係，並願意持續承擔其中的責任。這裡不只是說“答應”，而是已經把自己與目標或他人聯絡在一起。","examples":[{"en":"A strong relationship requires trust and commitment.","zh":"牢固的關係需要信任和投入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His commitment to helping the community inspired others.","zh":"他致力於幫助社群的態度鼓舞了其他人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commitment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1bb3894443fd9088c9c","word":"committee","forms":["committee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f96d587b1c31802e","term":"committee","forms":["committee","committees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"委員會；專門小組","explanation":"指為完成某項明確任務而召集起來的一群人，通常有較正式的組織方式和議事程式。它可以負責制定計劃、審查問題或作出決定，重點是“共同受託辦事的一組人”。","examples":[{"en":"My uncle is on the committee.","zh":"我叔叔是委員會成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee will review the proposal next week.","zh":"委員會下週將審查這份提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/committee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25206cd612b1f2dcce99","word":"commodity","forms":["commodity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6843b4eda0643cf","term":"commodity","forms":["commodity","commodities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可買賣的商品","explanation":"指可以買進、賣出的東西，重點在於它作為商品進入市場交換，而不只是在於它本身是什麼物品。可以是具體的一件商品，也可以泛指商品這一類別。","examples":[{"en":"The company imports commodities from several countries.","zh":"這家公司從幾個國家進口商品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Coffee is an important commodity in the region.","zh":"咖啡是這個地區的一種重要商品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commodity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54feb25fc3b10608","term":"commodity","forms":["commodity","commodities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有用而寶貴的東西","explanation":"把某種東西看成值得珍惜、能夠帶來價值的資源，不一定真的能在市場上買賣；時間、耐心和信任都可以這樣比喻。","examples":[{"en":"In a busy office, patience is a rare commodity.","zh":"在忙碌的辦公室裡，耐心是一種稀缺資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Privacy became a precious commodity in the crowded dormitory.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commodity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37fa60da9a520a0a","term":"commodity","forms":["commodity","commodities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大宗原材料","explanation":"特指在專業市場上大量交易的原材料、農產品等基礎產品，例如原油、金屬或穀物；價格通常受整體市場交易影響。","examples":[{"en":"Oil and wheat are traded as commodities around the world.","zh":"石油和小麥作為大宗商品在世界各地交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Copper is a major commodity on international markets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commodity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92a5dc04bd6f9fb8f29f","word":"common","forms":["common"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d88cc1f4c0e6217","term":"common","forms":["common","commoner","most common","commonest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"共同的；共有的","explanation":"指兩個或更多人、團體共同擁有、共同面對或共同追求的東西，重點是“大家有一份”。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams share a common goal.","zh":"兩支隊伍有一個共同的目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have a common interest in music.","zh":"我們都對音樂有共同的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/common","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57deeb6a769a8ddf","term":"common","forms":["common","commoner","most common","commonest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"普遍的；人人都有的","explanation":"指某種品質、知識或行為幾乎存在於所有人身上，強調範圍非常廣。","examples":[{"en":"It is common knowledge that water freezes at zero degrees Celsius.","zh":"水在攝氏零度結冰是常識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A little common sense would have prevented the mistake.","zh":"有一點常識就能避免這個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/common","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c1647cd31ac4da0","term":"common","forms":["common","commoner","most common","commonest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"常見的；經常發生的","explanation":"指某事經常發生，或某種事物在某個地方、群體中很容易遇到。","examples":[{"en":"It is common to see cyclists on this road.","zh":"在這條路上經常能看到騎腳踏車的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Colds are common in winter.","zh":"冬天感冒很常見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/common","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c09c49345962148832e0","word":"commonplace","forms":["commonplace"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cd08b5104a08744","term":"commonplace","forms":["commonplace","more commonplace","most commonplace"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平淡無奇的","explanation":"形容人或事物太普通，沒有值得注意的特點，像人人都見過的東西一樣平淡。","examples":[{"en":"The film's story is predictable and commonplace.","zh":"這部電影的故事可預測，而且平淡無奇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What once seemed exciting soon became commonplace.","zh":"曾經看起來令人興奮的事，很快就變得司空見慣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commonplace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33cb756e4eef4ebe","term":"commonplace","forms":["commonplace","commonplaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"老生常談；套話","explanation":"指聽起來正確卻沒有新內容的話，像人人都能說出的現成說法，因此顯得空泛或陳腐。","examples":[{"en":"His speech was full of commonplaces about hard work.","zh":"他的演講充滿了關於努力工作的老生常談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His speech repeated the commonplace that patience is a virtue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commonplace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a8074574193735fc6ce","word":"commonwealth","forms":["commonwealth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b66b6ef402d038e","term":"commonwealth","forms":["commonwealth","commonwealths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治共同體","explanation":"指由共同法律、制度和公共生活組成的整個世俗社會或政治共同體。可以把它理解為“共同福祉”從抽象利益擴充套件到承載這種利益的社會和國家。","examples":[{"en":"The reform was intended to benefit the whole commonwealth.","zh":"這項改革旨在造福整個政治共同體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stable commonwealth depends on shared laws.","zh":"穩定的政治共同體依賴共同遵守的法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commonwealth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fa8c11816a035ba","term":"commonwealth","forms":["commonwealth","commonwealths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共和國","explanation":"指由人民或其代表治理、沒有國王或女王作為統治者的國家或政體，常作為正式政治名稱使用。這個意義體現了“共同福祉由共同體管理”的核心觀念。","examples":[{"en":"The new government declared the country a Commonwealth.","zh":"新政府宣佈該國成為共和國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Commonwealth was governed without a king.","zh":"這個共和國在沒有國王的情況下治理國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commonwealth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d22d390ec67d1aa03ec","word":"communicate","forms":["communicate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-630c06f287855040","term":"communicate","forms":["communicate","communicates","communicating","communicated","communicatest","communicatedst","communicateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳達；傳遞","explanation":"把資訊、想法或事實傳給別人，使對方知道或理解。這個意思是現代英語中最核心、最常用的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please communicate the results to everyone on the team.","zh":"請把結果傳達給團隊裡的每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor communicated the risks clearly.","zh":"醫生清楚地說明了風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4e16994df9002e53294","word":"communication","forms":["communication"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f37d629ac9a858a","term":"communication","forms":["communication","communications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資訊傳遞","explanation":"指把某種資訊、事實或內容傳給別人這一行為或事實，重點在“傳過去”這個過程，而不在具體訊息本身。","examples":[{"en":"The communication of the test results was delayed by the outage.","zh":"檢測結果的傳達因停電而延誤了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clear communication prevented confusion during the evacuation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ddc3fef58b4db4e8","term":"communication","forms":["communication","communications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溝通與資訊交換","explanation":"指雙方或多個實體交換資料、思想或資訊這一整體概念，也就是廣義的“溝通”。","examples":[{"en":"Clear communication between the patient and the doctor prevented a serious mistake.","zh":"患者和醫生之間清楚的溝通避免了一次嚴重錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good communication is essential when a team works remotely.","zh":"團隊遠端工作時，良好的溝通至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5bf2e8a62c47369","term":"communication","forms":["communication","communications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一條訊息","explanation":"指在一次溝通中傳遞的具體訊息、通知或核心資訊；這裡的 communication 更像“有人發來的內容”。","examples":[{"en":"I received a communication from the school about the schedule change.","zh":"我收到學校發來的一則關於日程變更的通知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The investigators intercepted several private communications.","zh":"調查人員截獲了幾條私人通訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":3,"counts":{"113":2,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-e7d73f5f1cbd785b0b4f","word":"communicative","forms":["communicative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40e9ee7bba6457dc","term":"communicative","forms":["communicative","more communicative","most communicative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樂於交流的；健談的","explanation":"指一個人很願意開口說話、回應別人並分享資訊或想法，就像主動把交流的大門開啟；不一定表示說個不停，而是表示有交流的意願。","examples":[{"en":"Mia is very communicative and is happy to explain her ideas.","zh":"米婭很善於交流，也樂意解釋自己的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new student was quiet at first but soon became more communicative.","zh":"那個新同學一開始很安靜，但很快就變得願意交流了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communicative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9201d3705a24a4fe403","word":"communism","forms":["communism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2043e5e28e90e4b4","term":"communism","forms":["communism","communisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共產主義思想","explanation":"一種主張把生產資源共同掌握、共同分配的政治思想，常設想透過激進的社會變革來實現這種安排。","examples":[{"en":"The movement was founded on the belief that communism would end exploitation.","zh":"這個運動建立在共產主義能夠終結剝削的信念之上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied communism before writing about revolutionary politics.","zh":"她在撰寫革命政治文章前研究了共產主義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5f681844a35966d","term":"communism","forms":["communism","communisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共產主義制度","explanation":"指把共產主義思想落實為政治和社會安排的制度；重點從“主張什麼”轉向“社會怎樣組織”。","examples":[{"en":"The novel imagines how families might live under communism.","zh":"這部小說設想了家庭在共產主義制度下可能怎樣生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country adopted communism after the revolution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a610285bb690048","term":"communism","forms":["communism"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共產黨的意識形態","explanation":"指名稱中含有“共產黨”的政黨所奉行的政治思想，通常與馬克思主義、列寧主義傳統相聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The party claimed that communism offered a fairer social order.","zh":"該黨宣稱共產主義能帶來更加公平的社會秩序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lectures examine communism as a revolutionary political doctrine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d7c4738117f8e165531","word":"communist","forms":["communist"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7acf74413b5a82ae","term":"communist","forms":["communist","more communist","most communist"],"pos":"adj","zh":"共產主義的","explanation":"指與共產主義有關，或支援以財產共同擁有、社會共同管理為核心的思想和制度。","examples":[{"en":"The book examines communist ideas about social equality.","zh":"這本書研究了共產主義關於社會平等的思想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They formed a communist movement in the 1930s.","zh":"他們在20世紀30年代成立了一個共產主義運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bbd4ec62ab101a7","term":"communist","forms":["communist","communists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共產主義者","explanation":"指支援建立以財產共同擁有、社會共同管理為基礎的社會的人；不一定說明他屬於某個正式政黨。","examples":[{"en":"She became a communist after reading political philosophy.","zh":"她讀了政治哲學後成了一名共產主義者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many communists opposed private ownership of major industries.","zh":"許多共產主義者反對主要工業實行私有制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/communist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f354ee99e2bc863ce19d","word":"community","forms":["community"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46e4f38eabcf5941","term":"community","forms":["community","communities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共同特徵形成的群體","explanation":"指因語言、法律、宗教、傳統或其他共同特徵而聯絡在一起的一群人。重點不一定是住在同一個地方，而是他們擁有某種共同身份或生活聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The city has a large immigrant community.","zh":"這座城市有一個規模很大的移民群體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farming community worked together to repair the bridge.","zh":"當地農民群體齊心協力修好了橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fed20667af68b85","term":"community","forms":["community","communities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共同聯絡或共同認同","explanation":"指人們在態度、興趣、價值觀或生活方式上具有共同點，並因此產生的共同聯絡或共同生活狀態。這裡community不是一群人的名稱，而是“共同在一起”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The festival gave neighbors a strong sense of community.","zh":"這個節日讓鄰居們產生了強烈的共同體歸屬感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project brought students together in community.","zh":"這個專案讓學生們以共同體的方式團結在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":3,"counts":{"114":2,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-1a6674898edecd10d181","word":"commute","forms":["commute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1369bb0999a456a9","term":"commute","forms":["commute","commutes","commuting","commuted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"通勤；往返上班或上學","explanation":"指按固定規律從家到工作地點或學校，再返回原處；核心畫面就是每天在兩點之間反覆往返。","examples":[{"en":"I commute from Brooklyn to Manhattan by bicycle.","zh":"我每天騎腳踏車從布魯克林通勤到曼哈頓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many students commute to campus by bus.","zh":"許多學生坐公交車往返於學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e9f29349fc1e5365ef7","word":"commuter","forms":["commuter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7a558e221dbb2f3","term":"commuter","forms":["commuter","commuters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通勤者","explanation":"指經常在居住地和工作、學習地點之間往返的人，核心是有規律地“來回跑”。","examples":[{"en":"She is a daily commuter between Brighton and London.","zh":"她每天往返於布萊頓和倫敦之間通勤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train is crowded with commuters in the morning.","zh":"早高峰時，火車裡擠滿了通勤者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commuter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce73ea5a23e69964","term":"commuter","forms":["commuter","commuters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"定期往返兩地的人","explanation":"強調某人長期、規律地在兩個地點之間出行，最常見的是住處與工作地點之間的往返。","examples":[{"en":"Many commuters leave home before sunrise.","zh":"許多通勤者在日出前就離開家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ferry is crowded with commuters every morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/commuter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6b54201f23d00f5b719","word":"compact","forms":["compact"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69a07b0f8a6dd3dd","term":"compact","forms":["compact","more compact","compacter","most compact","compactest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"緊密密實的","explanation":"指材料或物體內部排列得很緊，單位體積中包含的物質很多，突出“緊緊擠在一起”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The soil becomes compact after heavy rain and repeated traffic.","zh":"大雨和車輛反覆碾壓後，土壤會變得很密實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Compact soil prevented the roots from spreading.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2fd7bed46e0f3a0","term":"compact","forms":["compact","more compact","compacter","most compact","compactest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"小巧實用的","explanation":"指東西佔用空間小，卻把必要的功能整齊地放在一起；例如小型電腦或小型裝置。","examples":[{"en":"This compact camera is easy to carry on a long trip.","zh":"這臺小巧的相機很適合長途旅行攜帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought a compact dishwasher for our narrow kitchen.","zh":"我們為狹窄的廚房買了一臺小型洗碗機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fcd05a7a9c370e18","term":"compact","forms":["compact","compacts","compacting","compacted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓實；壓緊","explanation":"指透過擠壓減少空隙，讓材料變得更密實；這是把東西“緊緊收攏在一起”的直接動作。","examples":[{"en":"Workers compacted the gravel before laying the pavement.","zh":"鋪路面前，工人把碎石壓實了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please compact the soil around the new tree.","zh":"請把新樹周圍的土壓實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c989edf18246e9c8cdd6","word":"companion","forms":["companion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5893d5266bc453fe","term":"companion","forms":["companion","companions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同伴；陪伴者","explanation":"指和某人一起度過時間、同行或相互陪伴的人，也可以指陪伴人的動物；不一定是最親密的朋友。","examples":[{"en":"Her cat has been a loyal companion through many difficult years.","zh":"她的貓陪她度過了許多艱難的歲月，一直是她忠實的夥伴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was glad to have a companion on the long train journey.","zh":"漫長的火車旅途中有個同伴，我很高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/companion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8c42368b73eea2d","term":"companion","forms":["companion","companions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相伴事物","explanation":"指與另一個事物、現象或人緊密聯絡、經常一起出現的物件；這裡的“陪伴”從人擴充套件到了抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"Stress is often a close companion to major life changes.","zh":"壓力常常伴隨著人生中的重大變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibition catalog makes an excellent companion to the photographs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/companion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81d1b4bf0946fbff","term":"companion","forms":["companion","companions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"配套指南或資料","explanation":"指為配合主要書籍、課程、作品或產品而附加的資料，幫助使用者更深入地理解或使用主要內容。","examples":[{"en":"The publisher released a companion guide with maps and background notes.","zh":"出版社推出了一本配套指南，裡面有地圖和背景說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the illustrated companion alongside the main textbook.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/companion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f168ccdd91548c5a8c87","word":"company","forms":["company"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8201a7a148ef39a7","term":"company","forms":["company","companies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"團隊；團體","explanation":"指為了工作或共同任務而聚在一起的一群人，重點是“結伴合作”的團體，而不一定是正式的公司。","examples":[{"en":"A company of actors traveled from town to town.","zh":"一群演員從一個城鎮巡演到另一個城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A company of dancers toured the coastal villages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/company","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2b7b9b0777d0e43","term":"company","forms":["company","companies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業企業","explanation":"泛指製造或銷售商品、提供服務並以商業經營為目的的企業，無論是否正式註冊為法人。","examples":[{"en":"She started a company that designs kitchen tools.","zh":"她創辦了一家設計廚房用具的企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company manufactures replacement parts for bicycles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/company","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2d7e4f06cd3a351","term":"company","forms":["company","companies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陪伴；相伴","explanation":"指和別人待在一起所帶來的陪伴感，核心仍是“有人結伴同行”，不一定涉及交談或共同活動。","examples":[{"en":"I enjoyed your company during the long journey.","zh":"長途旅行中有你陪伴，我很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you keep me company while I wait?","zh":"我等候的時候，你能陪陪我嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/company","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8751a3fcac50b3ba5e32","word":"comparable","forms":["comparable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ecedf8b9e5cfbc0","term":"comparable","forms":["comparable","more comparable","most comparable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可拿來比較的","explanation":"指兩個物件能夠放在同一標準下衡量，因此可以進行有意義的比較。重點不是它們完全相同，而是它們在相關方面處於可以對照的範圍內。","examples":[{"en":"The two hospitals are comparable in size and quality.","zh":"這兩家醫院在規模和質量上具有可比性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her work is comparable to that of experienced professionals.","zh":"她的工作水平可以和有經驗的專業人士相比。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comparable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8491d455674fb40","term":"comparable","forms":["comparable","more comparable","most comparable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相近的；相當的","explanation":"指兩個事物在某個重要方面相似或程度相當，所以可以用一個來幫助理解另一個。它常用於大小、風險、價格、質量和影響等方面的比較。","examples":[{"en":"The stress of moving can be comparable to the stress of starting a new job.","zh":"搬家帶來的壓力可能與開始一份新工作的壓力相當。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This laptop offers comparable performance at a lower price.","zh":"這款膝上型電腦價格更低，卻能提供相當的效能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comparable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-382439e6f1baad6961e0","word":"comparative","forms":["comparative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93a969695699f5ee","term":"comparative","forms":["comparative","more comparative","most comparative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與比較有關的","explanation":"表示某事物涉及把兩個或多個物件放在一起比較，而不是單獨描述其中一個物件。","examples":[{"en":"The report offers a comparative analysis of the two education systems.","zh":"這份報告對兩個教育體系進行了比較分析。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her comparative study examines education in three countries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comparative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1241626eb8ca542931d7","word":"compare","forms":["compare"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84e1546f8705589a","term":"compare","forms":["compare","compares","comparing","compared","comparest","comparedst","compareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"比較異同","explanation":"把兩個或多個事物放在一起，仔細衡量它們在哪些方面相同、不同或各有優劣。這是 compare 最基本、最常用的意思，重點是進行分析，而不只是說它們相似。","examples":[{"en":"Compare the two plans before you make a decision.","zh":"作出決定前，比較一下這兩個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report compares living costs in three major cities.","zh":"這份報告比較了三個大城市的生活成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b248cdaee12aa7ea","term":"compare","forms":["compare","compares","comparing","compared","comparest","comparedst","compareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……比作……","explanation":"把一個事物說成像另一個事物，突出某個方面的相似之處，常常帶有形象化說明或修辭意味。這裡不一定是在逐項分析差異，而是在建立一個便於理解的類比。","examples":[{"en":"The guide compared the old city to a living museum.","zh":"導遊把這座古城比作一座活的博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The poet compared grief to an endless winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c271f2bb931810eef633","word":"comparison","forms":["comparison"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5168e0275858d544","term":"comparison","forms":["comparison","comparisons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比較；對照這一過程","explanation":"指把兩個或多個事物放在一起觀察、衡量，以便看出它們之間關係的行為或過程。重點在“進行對照”這一動作，而不一定已經得出結論。","examples":[{"en":"A comparison between the two plans will help us choose the better one.","zh":"比較這兩個方案將有助於我們選出更好的一個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report brings the two cities into comparison.","zh":"這份報告把這兩座城市放在一起比較。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comparison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f12c05b861b65a22","term":"comparison","forms":["comparison","comparisons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比較；比較結果","explanation":"指比較多個事物的相似點和不同點後形成的分析或判斷，也可以指這份具體的比較結果。例如購物前把不同產品的價格、效能和質量放在一起衡量，就是這種 comparison。","examples":[{"en":"I made a careful comparison of the three phones before buying one.","zh":"買手機前，我仔細比較了這三款手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The comparison revealed striking differences in fuel consumption.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comparison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1068beeb96a6a799376","word":"compass","forms":["compass"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-726d5cd23bdc7b77","term":"compass","forms":["compass","compasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指南針；羅盤","explanation":"一種幫助人確定方向的儀器，傳統上利用磁性指向北方，也可以是電子裝置。它把“尋找方向”這一概念固定在一個可旋轉的方向盤面上。","examples":[{"en":"We used a compass to find our way back to the trail.","zh":"我們用指南針找回了通往小路的方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The compass points north even when the sky is cloudy.","zh":"即使天空陰雲密佈，指南針也會指向北方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6704ad5ee9fb6327","term":"compass","forms":["compass","compasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓規","explanation":"一種有兩條腿的繪圖工具，一端固定，另一端移動，用來畫圓或轉移長度。它直接體現了“圍出一個圓”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a circle with a compass and a ruler.","zh":"用圓規和直尺畫一個圓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a compass to draw a perfect circle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b260e1abb566eb8b1ea8","word":"compassion","forms":["compassion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53b69b7e1a199355","term":"compassion","forms":["compassion","compassions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對他人的悲苦懷有深切同情並想幫助","explanation":"指看見別人正在受苦時，產生深切而持久的同情，並希望採取行動減輕對方的痛苦；重點不只是覺得對方可憐，而是願意關懷和幫助。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers showed compassion for families who had lost their homes.","zh":"志願者對失去家園的家庭表示了深切的同情和關懷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her compassion for the injured animals led her to open a shelter.","zh":"她對受傷動物的憐憫和關懷促使她開辦了一所收容所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compassion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-385c9f1ae4a4d2fc","term":"compassion","forms":["compassion","compassions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理解並關懷自己或他人的痛苦","explanation":"指認真理解某人，包括自己，正在經歷的痛苦，並以關懷而不是責備的態度回應；“自我慈悲”就是把這種態度用於自己。","examples":[{"en":"Practicing self-compassion can help people recover from mistakes.","zh":"練習自我慈悲可以幫助人們從犯錯的挫折中恢復過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed compassion toward the frightened new arrival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compassion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22ed0a6501b892bf2657","word":"compassionate","forms":["compassionate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2aef6723eeab80d5","term":"compassionate","forms":["compassionate","more compassionate","most compassionate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有同情心的；體恤的","explanation":"指能感受到他人的痛苦或困難，並表現出關懷和體諒；既可以形容人，也可以形容他的言行或態度。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse was compassionate toward every patient.","zh":"那名護士體恤每一位病人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a more compassionate response to people in crisis.","zh":"我們需要以更體恤的方式回應身處危機的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compassionate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d2b30c023cf65a7","term":"compassionate","forms":["compassionate","more compassionate","most compassionate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"因特殊困境而酌情給予的","explanation":"指機構因為某人遭遇家庭急事、親人去世等嚴重困難，破例給予休假、簽證等安排；這裡強調的是出於體恤而作出的特殊處理。","examples":[{"en":"She took compassionate leave after her father died.","zh":"父親去世後，她請了體恤假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee approved her transfer on compassionate grounds because her child was ill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compassionate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1613be9e3df6e9a2d9f","word":"compatible","forms":["compatible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1cec75b9a34c4719","term":"compatible","forms":["compatible","more compatible","most compatible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相容的；可配合執行的","explanation":"指裝置、軟體或系統能夠連線、協同工作，不會因為規格或介面不同而無法使用；重點是“接在一起能正常運作”。","examples":[{"en":"This printer is compatible with most home computers.","zh":"這臺印表機相容大多數家用電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check whether the new software is compatible with your phone.","zh":"請檢查這款新軟體是否相容你的手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compatible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42a1b01aca6c493c","term":"compatible","forms":["compatible","more compatible","most compatible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合得來；相處融洽的","explanation":"指人與人之間的性格、生活方式或價值觀能夠協調，適合長期相處；並不要求兩個人完全相同。","examples":[{"en":"They are very compatible and rarely argue about money.","zh":"他們很合得來，很少為錢爭吵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roommates were compatible despite their different backgrounds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compatible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-179151bcc55466461e65","word":"compel","forms":["compel"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89df1617328432b9","term":"compel","forms":["compel","compels","compelling","compelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迫使；使不得不","explanation":"表示外在壓力、權威、事實或充分理由使某人不得不做某事，是 compel 最核心、最常用的意思之一。力量不一定來自人，也可以來自證據、邏輯或局勢。","examples":[{"en":"The evidence compelled the jury to reconsider its decision.","zh":"證據迫使陪審團重新考慮裁決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Financial difficulties compelled her to leave the city.","zh":"經濟困難迫使她離開了這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d709c8989c5649c1","term":"compel","forms":["compel","compels","compelling","compelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強烈促使採取行動","explanation":"表示某種力量、故事、情感或願望強烈推動人採取特定行動，重點不一定是命令或壓迫，而是讓人幾乎停不下來。它可以看作“驅趕”從外在壓力延伸到內在動力。","examples":[{"en":"The mystery compelled me to read the novel in one sitting.","zh":"這個懸念讓我忍不住一口氣讀完了那部小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sense of responsibility compelled him to speak up.","zh":"責任感促使他站出來發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7a02876a32b93a28f81","word":"compensate","forms":["compensate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a305779537bab97","term":"compensate","forms":["compensate","compensates","compensating","compensated","compensatest","compensatedst","compensateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"付錢酬謝或賠償","explanation":"表示因工作、服務、時間或受到的損失而給某人報酬或補償。這裡的“平衡”體現為用金錢或其他有價值的東西回報對方的付出或損失。","examples":[{"en":"The company compensated the workers for the extra hours.","zh":"公司就加班時間向工人支付了補償。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They compensate her well for managing the project.","zh":"他們為她管理這個專案支付了很好的報酬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compensate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d86c104e9fe91fea","term":"compensate","forms":["compensate","compensates","compensating","compensated","compensatest","compensatedst","compensateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"彌補不足；抵消影響","explanation":"表示用一個方面的優勢、行動或結果去彌補另一個方面的缺點、損失或不足，使整體重新接近平衡。它不一定涉及錢，常用於評價能力、條件和結果之間的抵消。","examples":[{"en":"A friendly attitude cannot compensate for poor service.","zh":"友好的態度無法彌補糟糕的服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The extra storage space compensates for the phone's higher price.","zh":"更大的儲存空間彌補了這部手機較高的價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compensate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b66ecab57861b7224199","word":"compensation","forms":["compensation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e381281ab8dd4f69","term":"compensation","forms":["compensation","compensations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"補償行為；補償原則","explanation":"指用相應的東西彌補損失、付出或不平衡這一行為或原則，重點在“補回來”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The company offered compensation for the delay.","zh":"公司為延誤提供了補償。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No amount of compensation can undo the damage.","zh":"再多的補償也無法挽回這次損害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compensation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12ebab1a3df6d879","term":"compensation","forms":["compensation","compensations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"補償物；賠償金","explanation":"指被看作等價物、用來彌補損失的具體東西，尤其常指賠償金或補償款。","examples":[{"en":"She received compensation for the injury.","zh":"她因受傷獲得了賠償。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The passengers demanded compensation for the canceled flight.","zh":"乘客要求為航班取消獲得賠償。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compensation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e328207c5fd1102b57b","word":"compete","forms":["compete"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c98b420fb3f4dc6","term":"compete","forms":["compete","competes","competing","competed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與人競爭","explanation":"指兩個或多個個人、團隊或機構為了同一個職位、獎項、名次或機會彼此較量，爭取勝出。","examples":[{"en":"Several teams are competing for the championship this year.","zh":"今年有幾支隊伍在爭奪冠軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is competing against experienced candidates for the position.","zh":"她正在和經驗豐富的候選人競爭這個職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a08ef52cce5a3d0","term":"compete","forms":["compete","competes","competing","competed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加競賽","explanation":"指作為選手或隊伍參加比賽、競賽或類似活動；重點是加入這場爭奪，而不一定說明最後是否獲勝。","examples":[{"en":"More than one hundred athletes will compete in the marathon.","zh":"一百多名運動員將參加這場馬拉松比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He competed in his first national swimming event last month.","zh":"他上個月參加了自己的第一場全國游泳比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5c8ed2c5b63d1f504d21","word":"competence","forms":["competence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e616e7135034d655","term":"competence","forms":["competence","competences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勝任力；能力","explanation":"指一個人具備做好某種一般工作或擔任某種角色所需要的能力，重點是“夠資格、能勝任”。","examples":[{"en":"The training aims to improve cultural competence among healthcare workers.","zh":"這項培訓旨在提高醫護人員的文化勝任力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her competence as a manager was never in doubt.","zh":"她作為經理的勝任能力從未受到懷疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa28457a9d61d43c","term":"competence","forms":["competence","competences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完成特定任務的能力","explanation":"指做好某一項具體工作、技能或任務的能力，比一般的勝任力更明確地對應某個目標。","examples":[{"en":"The course tests students' competence in basic first aid.","zh":"這門課程檢驗學生掌握基本急救的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has the technical competence to lead the project.","zh":"她具備領導這個專案所需的技術能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9923e7741b8d8c822759","word":"competent","forms":["competent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-836bffde24c2a94e","term":"competent","forms":["competent","more competent","most competent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有能力的；能勝任的","explanation":"指一個人擁有完成某項工作或活動所需的技能、知識、能力或資格，因此能夠可靠地把事情做好。它強調“夠格並能勝任”，不一定表示水平頂尖。","examples":[{"en":"She is a competent manager who keeps the team focused.","zh":"她是一位能幹的經理，能讓團隊保持專注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need to be competent at handling basic repairs.","zh":"你需要具備處理基本維修工作的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58e39f07006baab7","term":"competent","forms":["competent","more competent","most competent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有管轄權的；有權處理的","explanation":"在法律語境中，指法院、機構或其他權力主體依法有資格審理、決定或處理某個問題。這裡的“有能力”不是一般技能，而是指法律許可權足夠。","examples":[{"en":"The dispute must be brought before a competent court.","zh":"這項爭議必須提交給有管轄權的法院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a competent court can authorize that search.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4721819b2bf3e332787f","word":"competition","forms":["competition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d09d1b56f030f5ad","term":"competition","forms":["competition","competitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"競爭活動","explanation":"指人或團體為了同一個職位、目標或資源而互相爭先的過程，重點在“競爭”本身，而不是某一場具體比賽。","examples":[{"en":"There is fierce competition for places at the best universities.","zh":"爭取頂尖大學名額的競爭非常激烈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The competition for this job is strong.","zh":"爭奪這份工作的競爭很激烈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9bdd8a6e5e363b8c","term":"competition","forms":["competition","competitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽；競賽","explanation":"指為了贏得獎品、獎項或榮譽而舉辦的一場具體競賽，可以是體育比賽，也可以是答題、抽獎等活動。","examples":[{"en":"She entered a photography competition and won first prize.","zh":"她參加了一個攝影比賽，並獲得了一等獎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baking competition attracted thirty local cooks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-020dae383219bf785518","word":"competitive","forms":["competitive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95f85e05050ba990","term":"competitive","forms":["competitive","more competitive","most competitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"競爭性的；與競爭有關的","explanation":"表示某種環境、活動、關係或做法涉及競爭，重點是“處在爭奪名次或優勢的賽道上”，不一定說明誰更強。","examples":[{"en":"The job market is highly competitive this year.","zh":"今年的就業市場競爭非常激烈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Schools create a competitive environment for young athletes.","zh":"學校為年輕運動員創造了競爭性的環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-836891f81409eb57","term":"competitive","forms":["competitive","more competitive","most competitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好勝的；喜歡競爭的","explanation":"描述人的性格或態度，表示這個人願意參加競爭，並且很在意勝負，是“站上賽道、想爭第一”的傾向。","examples":[{"en":"She is very competitive and hates losing.","zh":"她非常好勝，討厭輸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My competitive sister hates losing at chess.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28f72c841366c5be","term":"competitive","forms":["competitive","more competitive","most competitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有競爭力的","explanation":"表示產品、企業、價格、技能或方案能夠有效地與對手抗衡，具有成功競爭的條件；這裡強調結果上的優勢，而不只是參加競爭。","examples":[{"en":"The company offers competitive prices and reliable service.","zh":"這家公司提供有競爭力的價格和可靠的服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her skills make her competitive in the international market.","zh":"她的技能使她在國際市場上具有競爭力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c378ee41c2783d081fb4","word":"competitor","forms":["competitor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-adb7bf9d34204d8c","term":"competitor","forms":["competitor","competitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"競爭對手","explanation":"指和某人或某個組織爭奪同一目標的人或組織，重點是雙方處於競爭關係中。商業、體育、考試等語境都可以使用。","examples":[{"en":"Our biggest competitor lowered its prices last week.","zh":"我們最大的競爭對手上週降價了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a serious competitor for the national title.","zh":"她是全國冠軍的有力競爭者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cb93be660b7d158","term":"competitor","forms":["competitor","competitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參賽者","explanation":"指參加比賽的人，尤其常指參加體育比賽的運動員。這裡重點不一定是他和誰競爭，而是他作為選手出現在比賽中。","examples":[{"en":"Every competitor must check in before the race begins.","zh":"每位參賽者都必須在比賽開始前報到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A competitor from Kenya crossed the finish line first.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/competitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eba8dcd606bd0014b899","word":"compile","forms":["compile"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-152103dacc8292cd","term":"compile","forms":["compile","compiles","compiling","compiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"彙編整理","explanation":"把來自不同地方的材料收集起來並整理成一部完整的書、清單或報告，核心仍是“把零散部分拼成整體”。","examples":[{"en":"She compiled a guide from notes written by several teachers.","zh":"她把幾位教師寫的筆記整理成了一份指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researcher compiled the results into a clear report.","zh":"研究人員把結果彙編成了一份清晰的報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6571647cbb6eaf2b","term":"compile","forms":["compile","compiles","compiling","compiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編譯原始碼","explanation":"使用編譯器處理原始碼，把人編寫的程式轉換成計算機可以執行的程式碼；這正是“把許多程式碼部分整理成成品”的計算機版本。","examples":[{"en":"I need to compile the program before I can run it.","zh":"我得先編譯這個程式，才能執行它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The compiler compiled the source code without errors.","zh":"編譯器順利編譯了原始碼，沒有報錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41aa311d555b8ad087f8","word":"complain","forms":["complain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c90dc47522afc123","term":"complain","forms":["complain","complains","complaining","complained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抱怨；發牢騷","explanation":"指把疼痛、不滿意或受到的不公平說出來，重點是表達自己的不滿或怨氣。這是最常見、最需要先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"My brother is always complaining about the food.","zh":"我弟弟總是在抱怨飯菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several passengers complained that the train was too hot.","zh":"幾名乘客抱怨火車裡太熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb48be88a449a4ea","term":"complain","forms":["complain","complains","complaining","complained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式投訴；提出指控","explanation":"指把對某人的嚴重不滿正式告訴警方、管理機構等，並要求對方處理，語氣比普通抱怨更正式。","examples":[{"en":"The customer complained to the manager about the rude waiter.","zh":"那位顧客向經理投訴那個態度粗魯的服務員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Residents complained to the council about the nightclub.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d08b02d678fc068788c","word":"complaint","forms":["complaint"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e50dba0356716b75","term":"complaint","forms":["complaint","complaints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抱怨或投訴這一行為","explanation":"指把自己的不滿或問題說出來、報告給有關人員的行為，重點在“提出不滿”這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"Several passengers made complaints about the delayed train.","zh":"幾名乘客就火車晚點提出了投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The office received a complaint about the noisy construction work.","zh":"辦公室收到了一起關於施工噪聲的投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complaint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ea46081f1e0fb70","term":"complaint","forms":["complaint","complaints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不滿的問題或意見","explanation":"指一個人認為不對勁、令人不滿意或需要解決的具體事情，也就是被拿出來抱怨的那個問題，而不只是抱怨的動作。","examples":[{"en":"I have no complaints about the food or the service.","zh":"我對食物和服務都沒有什麼不滿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My main complaint concerns the unreliable heating.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complaint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-724f43823fc243f1c77c","word":"complement","forms":["complement"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c60f77995e70579","term":"complement","forms":["complement","complements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完整所需的全部數量","explanation":"指為了使某個整體正常或完整而需要的全部數量，既可以說人、物，也可以說抽象專案；重點是“數量已經湊齊”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is operating with a full complement of staff.","zh":"這家酒店的員工已經全部到位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The orchestra now has its full complement of musicians.","zh":"這支樂團現在已經配齊了全部樂手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0659349053e5bc13","term":"complement","forms":["complement","complements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使整體完整或和諧的補足物","explanation":"指與另一事物結合後使整體更完整、更協調的部分；它可以是實際物品，也可以是能力、風格或其他抽象特徵。","examples":[{"en":"The bright cushions are a perfect complement to the dark sofa.","zh":"這些明亮的靠墊正好襯托並補足了深色沙發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their different skills make them a strong complement to each other.","zh":"他們不同的技能使雙方形成了很好的互補。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85b52946fd51e169","term":"complement","forms":["complement","complements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"補語","explanation":"在語法中，complement 是補足句子結構的詞或片語，常在謂語後說明主語或賓語是什麼、處於什麼狀態，或補充動詞所需要的資訊。","examples":[{"en":"In the sentence “She became a doctor,” “a doctor” is the complement.","zh":"在“She became a doctor”這個句子中，“a doctor”是補語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The adjective “tired” is a complement in “The children seem tired.”","zh":"在“The children seem tired”中，形容詞“tired”是補語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93ec778ad7da26a1","term":"complement","forms":["complement","complements","complementing","complemented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"補足並使完整","explanation":"指加入缺少的部分，使某個整體更完整、更完善；重點是填上缺口，而不是單純增加數量。","examples":[{"en":"A short break will complement the training session.","zh":"短暫休息會讓這次培訓安排更加完整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new evidence complements the original report.","zh":"新證據補充並完善了原來的報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eebbf6457e46a7f63acd","word":"complete","forms":["complete"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e7912c10565e896","term":"complete","forms":["complete","more complete","completer","most complete","completest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完整的；齊全的","explanation":"指某物的所有部分都在，沒有缺少或遺漏；重點是“整體已經齊了”。","examples":[{"en":"This guide gives a complete list of local restaurants.","zh":"這份指南列出了當地餐館的完整名單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My collection is finally complete.","zh":"我的收藏終於齊全了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f2831c3f34afc71","term":"complete","forms":["complete","more complete","completer","most complete","completest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完成的；結束的","explanation":"指任務、工作或過程已經做完，最後一步也已經結束；這裡強調“事情到頭了”。","examples":[{"en":"When the report is complete, send it to the manager.","zh":"報告完成後，把它發給經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building is complete, but the offices are not open yet.","zh":"大樓已經完工了，但辦公室還沒有開門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11e99945760e9f72","term":"complete","forms":["complete","completes","completing","completed","completest","completedst","completeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"完成；做完","explanation":"指把一項任務、作業或過程做到最後，使它結束；重點是從未完成狀態走到完成狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She completed the application before the deadline.","zh":"她在截止日期前填完了申請表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team completed the project in three months.","zh":"團隊用了三個月完成了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a5e397914450730","term":"complete","forms":["complete","completes","completing","completed","completest","completedst","completeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使完整；補齊","explanation":"指加入最後缺少的部分，使某個整體齊全；可以把它看成是“把容器填滿”。","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph completes the article.","zh":"最後一段使這篇文章完整了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One missing tile would complete the mosaic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea4b35e8f83279eab1e6","word":"complex","forms":["complex"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7597e3a064b9a0ae","term":"complex","forms":["complex","more complex","complexer","most complex","complexest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由多部分組成的","explanation":"指一個事物包含許多相互關聯的部分，不是單一、簡單的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The human brain is a complex organ.","zh":"人腦是一個由許多部分組成的複雜器官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are studying a complex social problem.","zh":"他們正在研究一個涉及許多因素的社會問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complex","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9fbb0d52aa126b1","term":"complex","forms":["complex","more complex","complexer","most complex","complexest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"複雜難懂的","explanation":"指事情的步驟、關係或解決方法很多，因此不容易理解、處理或說明。","examples":[{"en":"The legal process is too complex for most people to understand.","zh":"這個法律程式太複雜，大多數人都難以理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Finding a solution to the problem is complex.","zh":"找到這個問題的解決辦法很複雜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complex","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc6318258d3c9989","term":"complex","forms":["complex","complexes","complices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"綜合系統","explanation":"指許多彼此連線、共同運作的系統或機構組成的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The airport is part of a large transport complex.","zh":"這個機場是大型交通綜合系統的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The military-industrial complex has influenced national policy.","zh":"軍工綜合體影響了國家政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complex","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-734a4147e73041cfa51d","word":"complexion","forms":["complexion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58f3546657c72853","term":"complexion","forms":["complexion","complexions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面部膚色與狀態","explanation":"指臉部皮膚呈現出的顏色、光澤和總體狀態，可以是健康、粗糙、蒼白等外觀。它關注的是整張臉給人的皮膚印象，而不只是某一小塊皮膚。","examples":[{"en":"She has a clear, healthy complexion.","zh":"她的面色清透而健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cold wind left his complexion pale and dry.","zh":"寒風讓他的臉色變得蒼白乾燥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complexion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e629da4cb180731","term":"complexion","forms":["complexion","complexions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物的外在面貌","explanation":"把“臉的外觀”比喻到事情或局勢上，表示某事呈現出來的整體樣子、色彩或性質。重點不是內部真實結構，而是它給人留下的外部印象。","examples":[{"en":"The new evidence changed the complexion of the case.","zh":"新的證據改變了這個案件的整體面貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discovery changed the complexion of the investigation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complexion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fff2d310ad659f6e05c","word":"complexity","forms":["complexity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7faeed5460f3690","term":"complexity","forms":["complexity","complexities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"複雜性；複雜程度","explanation":"指一件事交織、難以簡單理解或處理的狀態，強調整體有多少層次和關係，而不是某一個具體問題。","examples":[{"en":"The complexity of the human brain still surprises scientists.","zh":"人腦的複雜性至今仍讓科學家感到驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We underestimated the complexity of moving the entire office.","zh":"我們低估了搬遷整個辦公室的複雜程度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complexity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f14acd55335b82b","term":"complexity","forms":["complexity","complexities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"複雜之處；複雜因素","explanation":"指構成複雜局面的具體環節、關係或難題，就像交織線團中的一根根線頭；常常用複數表示一個系統裡有多個這樣的部分。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer explained the complexities of the new tax rules.","zh":"律師解釋了新稅收規則中的各種複雜之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Another complexity is that the two permits expire separately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complexity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29a3e14798aa2363dc0c","word":"compliance","forms":["compliance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d334dd9c60d767c","term":"compliance","forms":["compliance","compliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遵從；遵守","explanation":"指按照規定、要求或命令去做這一行為，重點是“把行動調到要求的方向上”。既可以談一般的遵守，也可以指某次具體的服從行為。","examples":[{"en":"The company requires strict compliance with its safety rules.","zh":"公司要求嚴格遵守安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inspection was carried out in compliance with the new law.","zh":"這次檢查是按照新法律進行的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b76acce6556defe","term":"compliance","forms":["compliance","compliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合規狀態","explanation":"指個人、機構或系統已經處於符合規定的狀態，不只是某一次遵守動作，而是持續滿足法律、政策或標準的要求。","examples":[{"en":"The software helps hospitals maintain compliance with data protection laws.","zh":"這款軟體幫助醫院遵守資料保護法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular audits are needed to ensure compliance.","zh":"需要定期審計來確保合規。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a6f294bbedda649442f","word":"complicate","forms":["complicate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48a9e8cef6e2b681","term":"complicate","forms":["complicate","complicates","complicating","complicated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使複雜化","explanation":"把原本較清楚的事情加入更多條件、問題或相互影響，使它像纏在一起的線一樣更難理解或處理。","examples":[{"en":"Adding too many rules will only complicate the process.","zh":"增加太多規則只會讓這個過程變得更復雜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His absence complicated our plans.","zh":"他的缺席使我們的計劃複雜起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f65eb6e52fc30d9b4ee5","word":"complication","forms":["complication"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68174e1359a8a7b4","term":"complication","forms":["complication","complications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"複雜化；使事情變複雜","explanation":"指把原本較簡單的事情弄得更復雜的過程，或這種複雜化本身。重點不只是“難”，而是增加了新的環節、問題或關係。","examples":[{"en":"The complication of the approval process delayed the project.","zh":"審批過程的複雜化推遲了專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His unexpected arrival added a further complication.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e57fc8cbd6d0ece","term":"complication","forms":["complication","complications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"複雜情況；複雜性","explanation":"指許多部分或關係交織在一起、難以理清的狀態，也可以指造成這種局面的具體複雜因素。它就像一根越纏越亂的線。","examples":[{"en":"We need a simple plan without unnecessary complications.","zh":"我們需要一個沒有不必要複雜情況的簡單計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The negotiations were delayed by several complications.","zh":"談判因幾個複雜問題而推遲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59354ba20a377991","term":"complication","forms":["complication","complications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"併發症","explanation":"醫學上指在主要疾病之外出現、並改變病情或治療過程的其他疾病或狀況。它就是原有疾病這根線上又纏上的一根問題線，不一定和原病直接相關。","examples":[{"en":"The infection caused serious complications after surgery.","zh":"手術後，這種感染引發了嚴重的併發症。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She recovered without any complications.","zh":"她康復了，沒有出現任何併發症。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/complication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c4fbffdee7b06191ac5","word":"compliment","forms":["compliment"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de11504936eba2c2","term":"compliment","forms":["compliment","compliments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讚美；恭維；稱讚的話","explanation":"指為了讚美、祝賀或表示尊重而對某人說的話，就像遞給對方一朵口頭上的花。可以是一句具體的稱讚，也可以是對成就或表現的認可。","examples":[{"en":"She paid me a lovely compliment on my presentation.","zh":"她稱讚我的演講很精彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave the chef a compliment after dinner.","zh":"晚餐後，他稱讚了廚師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compliment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ddf36605876429d","term":"compliment","forms":["compliment","compliments","complimenting","complimented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"讚美；恭維某人","explanation":"表示把那朵“口頭上的花”遞給某人，也就是直接說出對其外表、能力、行為或成就的肯定看法。它比單純覺得某人不錯更強調把讚美表達出來。","examples":[{"en":"Several guests complimented her on the way she handled the meeting.","zh":"幾位客人稱讚她處理會議的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I complimented him for helping the new students.","zh":"我稱讚他幫助了新來的學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compliment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a55a1b23f2710974cdc","word":"comply","forms":["comply"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-407de621bd717fe9","term":"comply","forms":["comply","complies","complying","complied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵從；照辦","explanation":"表示面對要求、命令、規定或他人的意願時，調整自己的行為並照著做。重點不是單純“同意”這個想法，而是實際順應並執行。","examples":[{"en":"All visitors must comply with the safety rules.","zh":"所有訪客都必須遵守安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company refused to comply with the court order.","zh":"這家公司拒絕遵從法院命令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6985ca1f4daa5a584a28","word":"component","forms":["component"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9cb2bb43cff22fb","term":"component","forms":["component"],"pos":"adj","zh":"構成整體的","explanation":"表示某物是更大整體的一部分，重點在於它參與構成那個整體。","examples":[{"en":"Each component part must be checked before assembly.","zh":"組裝前必須檢查每個組成部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report explains how component words form the phrase.","zh":"這份報告解釋了組成詞如何構成這個短語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/component","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ddc854ae141a3bc","term":"component","forms":["component","components"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組成部分；部件","explanation":"指一個較大裝置、系統或整體中可以單獨辨認的部分，尤其常指機器中能拆換或獨立工作的部件。","examples":[{"en":"The CPU is an important component of a computer.","zh":"中央處理器是計算機的一個重要組成部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A faulty component caused the machine to stop.","zh":"一個有故障的部件導致機器停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/component","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db669af634b75c7f2984","word":"compose","forms":["compose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d436659f02ac90e5","term":"compose","forms":["compose","composes","composing","composed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組合成；創作出","explanation":"把不同的部分組合起來，形成一件完整的東西；也可指創作文字、音樂等作品。重點是“從零散材料中組織出整體”。","examples":[{"en":"She composed a short piece of music for the ceremony.","zh":"她為典禮創作了一首短曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor composed the report from interviews and public records.","zh":"編輯把採訪和公開記錄整理成了這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f120831d241768cb","term":"compose","forms":["compose","composes","composing","composed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組成；構成","explanation":"表示若干部分共同構成一個整體，主語通常是整體，後面說明它由什麼組成。這是“把部分放到一起”這一核心概念的反向表達。","examples":[{"en":"The committee is composed of teachers, parents, and students.","zh":"這個委員會由教師、家長和學生組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Five elected representatives compose the executive council.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4d9d953eff69773","term":"compose","forms":["compose","composes","composing","composed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"創作；構思","explanation":"透過思考和安排，把想法組織成演講、文章、音樂等作品；它突出的是創作過程中的構思和組織。","examples":[{"en":"He composed his speech over several evenings.","zh":"他花了幾個晚上構思自己的演講稿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She composed a short melody for the ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42cc848a9f5ec37abc5b","word":"composer","forms":["composer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e577ee09f3bb51d1","term":"composer","forms":["composer","composers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作曲家；創作者","explanation":"指創作音樂的人，尤其是寫出樂曲、交響樂、歌曲或電影配樂的人；在較寬的語境中，也可以泛指創作者。","examples":[{"en":"The composer wrote the music for several famous films.","zh":"這位作曲家為幾部著名電影創作了音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mozart is one of the most influential composers in Western music.","zh":"莫扎特是西方音樂史上最具影響力的作曲家之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/composer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-730d725c8a59d3a7303d","word":"composition","forms":["composition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59c5560f289d878f","term":"composition","forms":["composition","compositions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組合；組裝","explanation":"指把不同部分放在一起、組成一個整體這一動作或過程，重點在“組合”本身。","examples":[{"en":"The composition of the team took several weeks.","zh":"這支隊伍的組建花了好幾周。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We studied the composition of the committee.","zh":"我們研究了這個委員會的組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/composition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b79010709dcfb26","term":"composition","forms":["composition","compositions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合物；組合物","explanation":"指已經組合出來的混合物或複合物，也就是由若干成分合在一起形成的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The composition of this cleaning product is listed on the label.","zh":"這種清潔產品的成分列在標籤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists tested the composition of the soil.","zh":"科學家檢測了土壤的成分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/composition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-203b202757948a99","term":"composition","forms":["composition","compositions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術作品；創作","explanation":"指由組合和安排產生的一件音樂、文學或藝術作品，也可指創作這種作品的活動。","examples":[{"en":"The orchestra performed a beautiful composition by a young composer.","zh":"樂團演奏了一位年輕作曲家的優美作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This composition combines traditional instruments with electronic sounds.","zh":"這部作品把傳統樂器和電子音效結合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/composition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee0df97cece494b174c6","word":"compound","forms":["compound"],"officialPos":"n./v./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fca22e054dd6cdcd","term":"compound","forms":["compound"],"pos":"adj","zh":"複合的；由多部分組成的","explanation":"指一個東西不是單一成分，而是由兩個或多個部分組合而成；例如一個詞由多個詞根或詞素組成時，就是 compound。","examples":[{"en":"“Toothpaste” is a compound word.","zh":"“牙膏”是一個複合詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine has a compound design with three connected parts.","zh":"這臺機器採用複合設計，由三個相連的部分組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-726f87bc700a27d6","term":"compound","forms":["compound","compounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築群；院落","explanation":"指彼此靠近、通常由同一機構或群體使用的一組建築；把多座建築圍或聚在一起，就是一個 compound。","examples":[{"en":"The embassy compound has offices, apartments, and a garden.","zh":"這座使館院落裡有辦公室、公寓和花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The embassy compound has two guarded entrances.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e525f320b84861e9","term":"compound","forms":["compound","compounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組合物；合成物","explanation":"指把幾個不同東西組合起來形成的整體，是“放在一起”這一核心概念最寬泛的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The artist created a compound of metal, glass, and wood.","zh":"這位藝術家用金屬、玻璃和木材製成了一件組合物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chemist separated the compound into its constituent elements.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68211aa0627b7d1a","term":"compound","forms":["compound","compounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化合物","explanation":"化學中，指兩種或更多元素按固定質量比例發生化學結合後形成的物質；它不是簡單把材料混在一起。","examples":[{"en":"Water is a compound made from hydrogen and oxygen.","zh":"水是由氫和氧形成的化合物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laboratory identified the unknown compound.","zh":"實驗室鑑定出了這種未知化合物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a413ab167af09610","term":"compound","forms":["compound","compounds","compounding","compounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"混合配製","explanation":"指把不同成分混合起來，製成一種新的混合物或製劑；它是“把東西放在一起”這一核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"The pharmacist compounded a cream for the patient.","zh":"藥劑師為病人配製了一種藥膏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician compounds the ingredients in a sterile room.","zh":"技術員在無菌室裡混合配製這些成分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5eb9b11984bdbc41973","word":"comprehend","forms":["comprehend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e84ecd48866cbc56","term":"comprehend","forms":["comprehend","comprehends","comprehending","comprehended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"充分理解","explanation":"指把一件複雜、難懂的事情從整體上理解透徹，而不只是聽說過或知道其中一部分。它常帶有“實在難以想明白”的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"I still can't comprehend how the machine works.","zh":"我還是無法理解這臺機器是怎麼運作的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is difficult to comprehend the scale of the disaster.","zh":"這場災難的規模很難讓人完全理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comprehend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ab9dc11d7d020249c69","word":"comprehension","forms":["comprehension"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e72207c6688b36ed","term":"comprehension","forms":["comprehension","comprehensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理解；領會","explanation":"指對文字、話語、情況或思想的充分理解，也可以指這種理解的能力或程度；核心畫面就是把資訊抓到一起並看懂。","examples":[{"en":"The course is designed to improve students' comprehension of spoken English.","zh":"這門課程旨在提高學生對英語口語的理解能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her comprehension of the problem was clear from her answer.","zh":"從她的回答可以看出，她充分理解了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comprehension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6563ca5bd29e40a6","term":"comprehension","forms":["comprehension","comprehensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"概念的內涵","explanation":"在邏輯、哲學或科學討論中，指一個概念所包含的全部特徵、屬性和條件，也就是這個概念“裡面裝著什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"The comprehension of a concept consists of the properties that define it.","zh":"一個概念的內涵由界定它的各種屬性構成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The concept's comprehension includes all its defining attributes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comprehension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4994ad9e4f40b39e4773","word":"comprehensive","forms":["comprehensive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7a63607344c1117","term":"comprehensive","forms":["comprehensive","more comprehensive","most comprehensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全面的；綜合性的","explanation":"指一個研究、計劃、說明或處理方式覆蓋了某個主題的大部分重要方面，而不是隻看其中一小部分；重點是範圍廣、內容較完整。","examples":[{"en":"The report provides a comprehensive review of the city's transport system.","zh":"這份報告全面評估了這座城市的交通系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need comprehensive research before making such an important decision.","zh":"在作出如此重要的決定前，我們需要進行全面研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comprehensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15385eb4bd7f86378fcf","word":"comprise","forms":["comprise"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25b9140c7ba07629","term":"comprise","forms":["comprise","comprises","comprising","comprised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"由……組成；包括","explanation":"主語是一個整體，後面列出構成它的成員或部分，強調這個整體可以由這些專案完整地說明。","examples":[{"en":"The committee comprises five members.","zh":"這個委員會由五名成員組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course comprises three short modules.","zh":"這門課程由三個短模組組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comprise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6633cab0c30d82e","term":"comprise","forms":["comprise","comprises","comprising","comprised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組成；構成","explanation":"這裡把組成整體的部分放在主語位置，表示這些部分共同構成某個整體；這種方向與核心用法相反。","examples":[{"en":"The course is comprised of three short modules.","zh":"這門課程由三個短模組組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Twelve villages comprise the district.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comprise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1caece2e3bd1aa695359","word":"compromise","forms":["compromise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58ed74693146ec04","term":"compromise","forms":["compromise","compromises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"妥協；和解","explanation":"指有分歧的雙方各自作出一些讓步，從而達成共同接受的解決辦法。這個意思就是“談判桌兩邊都向中間走一步”。","examples":[{"en":"After several hours of discussion, the two sides reached a compromise.","zh":"經過幾個小時的討論，雙方達成了妥協。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final plan was a compromise between speed and safety.","zh":"最終方案是在速度和安全之間取得的折中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compromise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab6453f42f876c95","term":"compromise","forms":["compromise","compromises","compromising","compromised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"透過讓步解決","explanation":"指雙方調整各自立場、互相讓步，把爭議解決下來。它把名詞的“妥協方案”變成了“透過妥協來處理問題”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The two groups compromised to avoid a long legal battle.","zh":"兩方作出了妥協，以避免曠日持久的法律爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They compromised on the wording of the agreement.","zh":"他們就協議的措辭達成了折中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compromise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fc2ddcd5c204976","term":"compromise","forms":["compromise","compromises","compromising","compromised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"折中；取中間辦法","explanation":"指不完全採取任何一個極端立場，而是在兩端之間找一個可接受的辦法。重點是找到中間路線，不一定明確說雙方已經達成正式協議。","examples":[{"en":"We had to compromise between keeping costs low and improving quality.","zh":"我們只能在降低成本和提高質量之間尋找折中辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both sides compromised and agreed on a shorter trial.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compromise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c3437d8af2d52ec9a6a","word":"compulsory","forms":["compulsory"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-284f460872f30c19","term":"compulsory","forms":["compulsory","more compulsory","most compulsory"],"pos":"adj","zh":"必須的；強制性的","explanation":"指按照規定、法律或制度，某件事必須做，不能只憑個人意願決定。","examples":[{"en":"Attendance at the safety briefing is compulsory.","zh":"參加安全說明會是強制性的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ten-dollar fee was compulsory.","zh":"這筆十美元的費用是必須繳納的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compulsory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15fe891bb3892814","term":"compulsory","forms":["compulsory","more compulsory","most compulsory"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有強制力的；起約束作用的","explanation":"指某種措施、力量或做法會迫使人服從，而不只是提出建議；它是“必須做”的規定義向施加壓力的一面延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The government introduced compulsory measures to reduce water use.","zh":"政府採取了強制措施來減少用水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court issued a compulsory order requiring disclosure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compulsory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b04a12f6483ea24a706b","word":"compute","forms":["compute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6de7b6f6478070ef","term":"compute","forms":["compute","computes","computing","computed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"計算；算出","explanation":"compute 是把數字或已知資訊按規則處理，得到一個結果，重點在“經過計算得出”。它既可以指人算數學題，也可以指程式或裝置完成計算。","examples":[{"en":"Can you compute the total cost before we place the order?","zh":"下單前你能算出總費用嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program computes the average automatically.","zh":"這個程式會自動算出平均值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa97302150fce811425c","word":"computer","forms":["computer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50216afa97f819a9","term":"computer","forms":["computer","computers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機；電腦","explanation":"指能按照程式進行數學計算和邏輯處理，並能快速處理、儲存和讀取大量資料的電子裝置；日常也常指個人電腦。","examples":[{"en":"I saved the report on my computer.","zh":"我把報告儲存在電腦上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The computer can store thousands of photos.","zh":"這臺電腦可以儲存數千張照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/computer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0932ce40d217697d5019","word":"computerize","forms":["computerize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"computerize","forms":["computerize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使電腦化","examples":[{"en":"The library plans to computerize its borrowing records.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We can computerize the booking system to reduce paperwork.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-3deac8e2aa21b78a9570","word":"comrade","forms":["comrade"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6d414cd9b33b266","term":"comrade","forms":["comrade","comrades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同伴；夥伴","explanation":"指和某人一起行動、共同經歷事情，或彼此陪伴的人，重點是“並肩同行”的關係，不一定表示親密的私人友誼。","examples":[{"en":"She stayed beside her comrade throughout the difficult journey.","zh":"在整個艱難的旅途中，她一直陪在同伴身邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every soldier trusted the comrade who stood next to him.","zh":"每名士兵都信任站在自己身旁的戰友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comrade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32246950080aae50","term":"comrade","forms":["comrade","comrades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治同志","explanation":"指與自己屬於同一社會主義、共產主義或其他相近政治陣營的人；這裡的“同伴”從共同相處擴充套件成了共同信念和立場上的夥伴。","examples":[{"en":"The speaker thanked his comrades for supporting the campaign.","zh":"發言人感謝同志們支援這場運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She met several comrades at the party meeting.","zh":"她在黨派會議上見到了幾位同志。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comrade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fb137e027d85dc84ebd","word":"conceal","forms":["conceal"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03c71fd7b5ff4461","term":"conceal","forms":["conceal","conceals","concealing","concealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隱藏；隱瞞","explanation":"把某物擋住或藏好，使別人看不見；也可以把真相、資訊等壓在“幕布”後面，使別人不知道。","examples":[{"en":"He concealed the key under the flowerpot.","zh":"他把鑰匙藏在花盆下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She concealed the truth from her parents.","zh":"她對父母隱瞞了真相。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conceal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b31ef75d8a6019e573de","word":"concede","forms":["concede"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5625a95da46fcd17","term":"concede","forms":["concede","concedes","conceding","conceded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"讓步；認輸","explanation":"指在爭論、競爭或衝突中不再堅持原來的立場，承認自己處於下風，或把某一點讓給對方。","examples":[{"en":"After a long debate, she finally conceded the argument.","zh":"經過長時間的辯論，她最後還是在這場爭論中讓步了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team conceded defeat after the final round.","zh":"最後一輪結束後，這支隊伍承認失敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concede","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eadbc22c8f097e95","term":"concede","forms":["concede","concedes","conceding","conceded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承認屬實","explanation":"指承認某個事實、觀點或對方的判斷是正確的，即使自己原先不願意承認，或仍然不完全贊同。","examples":[{"en":"He conceded that the plan had serious risks.","zh":"他承認這項計劃存在嚴重風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I concede that you were right about the timing.","zh":"我承認你對時機的判斷是對的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concede","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d774ea6c0add29b76656","word":"conceive","forms":["conceive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1d97e95c0e05dc8","term":"conceive","forms":["conceive","conceives","conceiving","conceived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懷孕；受孕","explanation":"指身體裡開始孕育孩子，也就是懷孕或受孕。這個義項和“在身體裡孕育某物”的核心畫面直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"They have been trying to conceive for over a year.","zh":"他們已經備孕一年多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She conceived her first child at the age of thirty.","zh":"她三十歲時懷上了第一個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conceive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43adc7de1ca7a93e","term":"conceive","forms":["conceive","conceives","conceiving","conceived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"構想；想出","explanation":"指在頭腦中孕育出一個想法、計劃或作品，從無到有地形成它。","examples":[{"en":"The team conceived a plan to reduce food waste.","zh":"團隊構想出了一個減少食物浪費的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She conceived the idea while walking home.","zh":"她在回家路上構想出了這個主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conceive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e92261c4445c0ed9402","word":"concentrate","forms":["concentrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3884518dd878ce1a","term":"concentrate","forms":["concentrate","concentrates","concentrating","concentrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"集中注意力；專心","explanation":"把思緒從其他事情上收攏，專注於眼前的一件事；注意力就像被拉向一箇中心。","examples":[{"en":"I can't concentrate on my work with all this noise.","zh":"這麼吵，我沒法專心工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She concentrated hard on solving the problem.","zh":"她努力集中注意力解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concentrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bdc4f42527047f250096","word":"concentration","forms":["concentration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f40165d1c387f885","term":"concentration","forms":["concentration","concentrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"集中；專注","explanation":"指把注意力、力量或許多事物收攏到一起的過程、能力或狀態。說人的注意力時，就是“專心”；說人口、建築等時，則強調它們聚集在某個地方。","examples":[{"en":"I can't work without complete concentration.","zh":"沒有全神貫注，我就無法工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The greatest concentration of restaurants is near the station.","zh":"餐館最集中的地方在車站附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concentration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fce1b3d43ab50c1e","term":"concentration","forms":["concentration","concentrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學習方向；專業方向","explanation":"在大學或學院中，指學生主要集中學習的領域，相當於所選的專業方向或主攻方向。它不是一般意義上的“專心程度”，而是長期把學習資源集中到某個學科。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a concentration in environmental policy.","zh":"她選擇了環境政策作為自己的專業方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His degree includes a concentration in environmental economics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concentration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da5e11efa36720a4211a","word":"concept","forms":["concept"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2638d8ed149e6afe","term":"concept","forms":["concept","concepts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽象概念","explanation":"指用一個較一般的想法來概括一類具體事物、性質或關係，例如“自由”“時間”這樣的抽象概念。重點不在某一個具體物件，而在把許多物件共同的特點提煉出來。","examples":[{"en":"Children gradually learn the concept of time.","zh":"孩子們逐漸理解時間這一概念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The concept of fairness is important in a healthy society.","zh":"公平這一概念在健康的社會中很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concept","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fafe0d32a273f509","term":"concept","forms":["concept","concepts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一般化的理解","explanation":"指人在經驗、推理和想象的基礎上形成並保留在頭腦中的一般理解。它把許多不同的具體例項看成同一類東西，是“從具體例子抽出共同模式”的結果。","examples":[{"en":"He has a clear concept of what good leadership means.","zh":"他對優秀領導力意味著什麼有清晰的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children gradually develop a concept of fairness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concept","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"114":2}}},{"id":"ceec-3ea6bca8e7bab208e773","word":"conception","forms":["conception"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6b0c6a1ee745f4d","term":"conception","forms":["conception","conceptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受精","explanation":"在生物學語境中，指精子與卵子結合並形成受精卵的過程；這是生命孕育真正開始的階段。","examples":[{"en":"The embryo begins to develop soon after conception.","zh":"胚胎在受精後不久開始發育。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medication is taken before conception, under medical guidance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63e55c0565a55700","term":"conception","forms":["conception","conceptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭腦中的想法或構想","explanation":"指在頭腦中孕育出來的具體想法、形象、計劃或設計，是“孕育成形”這一核心意象在思想領域的結果。它可以是一個作品的總體構想，也可以是對某事的觀念。","examples":[{"en":"The film began with her original conception of a divided city.","zh":"這部電影源於她對一座分裂城市的最初構想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final building is very different from the architect's original conception.","zh":"最終建成的建築與建築師最初的構想大不相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f1b86bf5531b8e8545e","word":"concern","forms":["concern"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba66ebcc2f1584e0","term":"concern","forms":["concern","concerns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牽涉利益的事情","explanation":"指會影響某人的生活、利益或幸福，因此值得他在意的一件事或一類事。它可以是實際問題，也可以是某人的健康、未來等重要方面。","examples":[{"en":"Her safety is our main concern.","zh":"她的安全是我們最關心的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rising cost of food is a serious concern for many families.","zh":"食品價格上漲是許多家庭非常關切的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89054cde9d1975e4","term":"concern","forms":["concern","concerns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擔憂；憂慮","explanation":"指認為可能出了問題，或擔心將來會有不好的結果時產生的憂慮；也可以指一個具體的令人擔心的問題。","examples":[{"en":"Several parents expressed concerns about the new school bus schedule.","zh":"幾位家長表達了對新校車時刻表的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have one concern about this plan.","zh":"我對這個計劃有一個擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33e8bd4a521e4caa","term":"concern","forms":["concern","concerns","concerning","concerned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"涉及；關係到","explanation":"表示某件事與某人、某群體或某主題有關係，影響到他們的利益，或屬於他們需要處理的範圍。這裡的重點是“牽涉到”，不一定有擔憂的感情色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The new rule concerns everyone who works in this building.","zh":"這項新規定關係到在這棟樓裡工作的每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This question concerns the future of the whole community.","zh":"這個問題關係到整個社群的未來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ec05326f6ea797d","term":"concern","forms":["concern","concerns","concerning","concerned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使擔心","explanation":"表示某人覺得可能有問題或會出現壞結果，因此心裡不安。常見於表達個人憂慮，也可用來委婉地提出一個問題。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor was concerned that the pain had not gone away.","zh":"醫生擔心疼痛一直沒有消失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m concerned about how quickly the river is rising.","zh":"我擔心河水上漲得太快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f29d4daaaae5947243c6","word":"concerning","forms":["concerning"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d1ca08a43941ee1","term":"concerning","forms":["concerning"],"pos":"prep","zh":"關於；涉及","explanation":"表示某句話、問題或行動與某個主題有關，相當於把注意力放到該主題上；這裡不一定含有擔憂的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I have a question concerning your application.","zh":"我有一個關於你申請的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We received several inquiries concerning the missing shipment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concerning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5359565a1aca1516be11","word":"concert","forms":["concert"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-542fefb7e060dcff","term":"concert","forms":["concert","concerts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂會","explanation":"指通常向公眾開放的現場音樂表演，由多位演奏者或多種樂器共同參加；這裡“共同配合”具體變成了一場演出。","examples":[{"en":"We bought tickets for a jazz concert next Saturday.","zh":"我們買了下週六爵士音樂會的票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She performed her new song at the concert.","zh":"她在音樂會上演唱了自己的新歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9aca78e330a930b0012","word":"concession","forms":["concession"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f940221dabc36593","term":"concession","forms":["concession","concessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式授予","explanation":"指把某項權利、許可或利益正式授予別人，重點是“讓出並允許對方擁有或使用”。","examples":[{"en":"The concession gave the company the right to operate the railway.","zh":"這項特許授予該公司經營鐵路的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government granted a concession to build the new bridge.","zh":"政府授予了修建這座新橋的特許權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ea5b664114ee82f","term":"concession","forms":["concession","concessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讓步；承認","explanation":"指在爭論或談判中承認對方有道理，或放棄一部分要求；核心畫面就是“向對方讓出一步”。","examples":[{"en":"After hours of negotiation, both sides made important concessions.","zh":"經過數小時談判，雙方都作出了重要讓步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister's concession helped bring the two groups back to the table.","zh":"部長的讓步幫助兩個團體重新回到談判桌前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e7fbe4df65775d0a6e97","word":"concise","forms":["concise"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abc4824b847a7130","term":"concise","forms":["concise","more concise","most concise"],"pos":"adj","zh":"簡明扼要的","explanation":"形容表達或文字篇幅不長，卻把最重要的資訊交代清楚；重點是“去掉多餘內容，但不犧牲要點”。","examples":[{"en":"The report is concise but still covers the key risks.","zh":"這份報告簡明扼要，但仍涵蓋了主要風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please give me a concise summary of the proposal.","zh":"請給我一份這項提案的簡明摘要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf4531359e01ef216604","word":"conclude","forms":["conclude"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8731502a26e2621","term":"conclude","forms":["conclude","concludes","concluding","concluded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結束；告終","explanation":"某件事走到盡頭並結束，強調過程被收束起來。它可以描述故事、會議、活動等自然結束的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The conference concluded with a short closing speech.","zh":"會議以一段簡短的閉幕致辭結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story concludes happily.","zh":"這個故事以圓滿結局收尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3340102540651a8","term":"conclude","forms":["conclude","concludes","concluding","concluded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結束；完成","explanation":"主動把某項活動、講話或文章收束到終點，相當於“為……作結”。重點是有人負責把它結束，而不是事情自行結束。","examples":[{"en":"The chair concluded the meeting by thanking everyone.","zh":"主席感謝大家後結束了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I will conclude my remarks with one final point.","zh":"我將用最後一點來結束我的發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6796c117a07b91a1","term":"conclude","forms":["conclude","concludes","concluding","concluded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"得出結論","explanation":"把證據、觀察或推理收束到一個最終判斷上，也就是“由此認定……”。這裡關閉的是思考過程，而不是一場活動。","examples":[{"en":"From the test results, we concluded that the machine was unsafe.","zh":"根據測試結果，我們得出結論，認為這臺機器不安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor concluded that the symptoms were caused by stress.","zh":"醫生得出結論，認為這些症狀是壓力造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-852408bfbc8333513e7c","word":"conclusion","forms":["conclusion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45ae16a6a01d0437","term":"conclusion","forms":["conclusion","conclusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結束；收尾","explanation":"指某件事、某個階段或某項活動的最後部分，也就是事情像合上門一樣完成收尾。它強調結束這一時刻或階段本身，而不一定強調結束後得到的結果。","examples":[{"en":"At the conclusion of the meeting, everyone agreed to meet again next week.","zh":"會議結束時，大家都同意下週再見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The concert ended with a short speech at its conclusion.","zh":"音樂會在最後以一段簡短的講話結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a1e1d7bce5423d8","term":"conclusion","forms":["conclusion","conclusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結果；後果","explanation":"指一個過程、行動或事件最後產生的結果，是從前面的發展中收攏出來的東西。這裡關注的是“發生了什麼結果”，不一定是某個人主動作出的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The conclusion of the investigation surprised everyone.","zh":"調查的結果讓所有人都感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The predictable conclusion of such neglect was equipment failure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e68c102a8ce9f40c","term":"conclusion","forms":["conclusion","conclusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結論；決定","explanation":"指一個人或團體仔細考慮事實後形成的判斷或決定，是把各種線索收攏成一個明確看法。它通常可以由某人或某個機構作出，而不是自然發生的結果。","examples":[{"en":"After reviewing the evidence, the committee reached the conclusion that the plan was unsafe.","zh":"委員會審查證據後得出結論，認為這項計劃不安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The investigators reached the same conclusion independently.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff298e4c4f975caa2511","word":"concrete","forms":["concrete"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f8666355f27c798","term":"concrete","forms":["concrete","concreter","concretest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真實具體的","explanation":"指確實存在、可以透過事實或感官加以確認的事物，而不是猜測、傳聞或空泛說法。它強調內容有現實依據，像可以拿在手裡檢查的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation found no concrete evidence of fraud.","zh":"調查沒有發現欺詐的確鑿證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need concrete facts before making a decision.","zh":"我們需要確鑿的事實後再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concrete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09a0fe73301bbb81","term":"concrete","forms":["concrete","concreter","concretest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"針對實際事物的","explanation":"指用於實際事物、物件或其性質，而不是隻討論抽象類別或抽象品質的。比如描述某個具體的人、物或可觀察性質時，就可以用這個意義。","examples":[{"en":"The report uses concrete terms instead of vague labels.","zh":"這份報告使用具體的術語，而不是含糊的標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children often understand concrete examples more easily than abstract ideas.","zh":"孩子通常比起抽象想法，更容易理解具體例子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concrete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9125fea5ccda50a8","term":"concrete","forms":["concrete","concreter","concretest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"具體明確的","explanation":"指已經落實到特定行動、細節或方案的，而不是籠統的目標、建議或願望。它把“真實存在”的概念進一步推進到“可以照著執行”。","examples":[{"en":"She offered a concrete plan to reduce waiting times.","zh":"她提出了一項減少等待時間的具體計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you give me a concrete example?","zh":"你能給我一個具體的例子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concrete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-abef6125763d8a37","term":"concrete","forms":["concrete","concretes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混凝土","explanation":"由水泥、水和砂石等混合後凝固形成的建築材料，用來修路、建牆、鋪地面等。這個意義與形容詞“混凝土製的”直接相連，是名詞最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The path is made of concrete and should last for years.","zh":"這條小路是用混凝土做的，應該能用很多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fresh concrete was poured around the posts.","zh":"工人把新拌的混凝土澆在柱子周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concrete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab99e5c4c300ecabe4fe","word":"condemn","forms":["condemn"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d436af92a78ac23","term":"condemn","forms":["condemn","condemns","condemning","condemned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強烈譴責","explanation":"表示公開而強烈地指責某人或某事，認為其行為錯誤、不可接受或應受責備。這是“給壞行為蓋上否定印章”的最常見用法。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor condemned the violent attack.","zh":"市長強烈譴責了這起暴力襲擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several groups condemned the company’s decision.","zh":"幾個團體強烈批評了這家公司的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condemn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4df8dd8ecb1d8bbb","term":"condemn","forms":["condemn","condemns","condemning","condemned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"判刑","explanation":"表示法院在認定有罪後正式宣佈刑罰，尤其強調被判處某種刑期或極刑；也就是從“蓋章有罪”進一步決定“要受什麼懲罰”。","examples":[{"en":"The judge condemned him to ten years in prison.","zh":"法官判處他十年監禁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rebels were condemned to death after the trial.","zh":"審判後，這些叛亂者被判處死刑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condemn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82e3e6a868647bf7","term":"condemn","forms":["condemn","condemns","condemning","condemned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"註定遭受壞處","explanation":"表示某人或某事被命運、環境或某種條件推向糟糕的結果，彷彿已經被蓋章判定只能經歷貧困、失敗或其他壞處。","examples":[{"en":"A lack of education can condemn people to a life of poverty.","zh":"缺乏教育可能使人一生陷入貧困。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury condemned him to months on the sidelines.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condemn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33a0189af06aabaf3198","word":"condense","forms":["condense"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"condense","forms":["condense"],"pos":"v.","zh":"濃縮；精簡","examples":[{"en":"Please condense the report into a one-page summary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The editor asked me to condense the introduction without losing its main idea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"condense","forms":["condense"],"pos":"v.","zh":"凝結","examples":[{"en":"Water vapor can condense on a cold window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Steam will condense into tiny drops when it touches the lid.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-596d40a4ed24c02a31b1","word":"condition","forms":["condition"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a4ea119adb5474a","term":"condition","forms":["condition","conditions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狀態；狀況","explanation":"指人、物或事情在某一時刻所處的狀態或質量水平。它可以描述身體、裝置、環境、社會狀況等，核心都是“現在處於怎樣的狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"The condition of the old bridge is getting worse.","zh":"那座老橋的狀況越來越差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car is still in excellent condition.","zh":"這輛車的狀況仍然非常好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0ec29b85db5ab09","term":"condition","forms":["condition","conditions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"條件；要求","explanation":"指某件事要成立、發生或繼續進行，必須先滿足的要求。這個意思仍然保留“事情能否處於某種狀態取決於什麼”的核心。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise is a condition for staying healthy.","zh":"經常鍛鍊是保持健康的條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You may borrow the equipment on condition that you return it tomorrow.","zh":"你可以借用這件裝置，條件是明天歸還。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39d263c0ca25af4a","term":"condition","forms":["condition","conditions","conditioning","conditioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使適應","explanation":"指透過反覆接觸某種環境或情況，使人或動物逐漸習慣並能夠適應它。它把“處於某種 condition”發展成“讓某人進入並習慣這種狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"Years in the desert conditioned her to extreme heat.","zh":"多年的沙漠生活使她適應了極端炎熱的天氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became conditioned to working long hours.","zh":"他逐漸習慣了長時間工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00abf05aa4e05017","term":"condition","forms":["condition","conditions","conditioning","conditioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使形成固定反應","explanation":"指透過反覆訓練、獎勵、懲罰或經歷，使某人形成在特定條件下自動做某事的行為模式。它是“置於某種條件中”進一步發展出的心理或行為意義。","examples":[{"en":"The training conditioned the dog to wait by the door.","zh":"訓練使這隻狗形成了在門邊等待的習慣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were conditioned to check their work carefully.","zh":"孩子們被訓練成會認真檢查自己的作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85ca6d6d291c070dbcb2","word":"conduct","forms":["conduct"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53b285acc32bbdfe","term":"conduct","forms":["conduct","conducts","conducting","conducted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"領導；主持；管理","explanation":"指負責帶領人員、組織工作或掌管一項任務，讓它按計劃進行。它保留了“帶著事情向前走”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She conducted the team through a difficult negotiation.","zh":"她帶領團隊完成了一場艱難的談判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The director conducted the meeting efficiently.","zh":"主任高效地主持了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conduct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74ce85be02d852ef","term":"conduct","forms":["conduct","conducts","conducting","conducted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表現；舉止","explanation":"指一個人管理自己的言行，也就是“帶著自己以某種方式表現”。通常用來評價舉止是否得體。","examples":[{"en":"He conducted himself calmly during the interview.","zh":"他在面試中表現得很鎮定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The players conducted themselves professionally after the loss.","zh":"球員們在失利後表現得很專業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conduct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86bafd9f59e86c1c","term":"conduct","forms":["conduct","conducts","conducting","conducted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳導；傳輸","explanation":"指物質把熱量、光、電等能量從一處傳到另一處，就像把某種東西沿通道帶過去。","examples":[{"en":"Copper conducts electricity better than most metals.","zh":"銅的導電性比大多數金屬好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This material conducts heat very slowly.","zh":"這種材料傳熱非常慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conduct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0380db97ec507816cb24","word":"conductor","forms":["conductor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cf959b51aa8a946","term":"conductor","forms":["conductor","conductors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂指揮","explanation":"指站在樂隊、合唱團或其他音樂團體前面，統一節拍、速度和表現方式的專業人員。","examples":[{"en":"The conductor raised her baton, and the orchestra began to play.","zh":"指揮舉起指揮棒，樂隊開始演奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young conductor is leading the school choir tonight.","zh":"這位年輕指揮今晚將帶領學校合唱團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conductor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed8f273c205d9add","term":"conductor","forms":["conductor","conductors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"導體；傳導體","explanation":"指能讓電、熱、光或聲音透過並傳遞的物質或物體，核心仍是“把某種東西傳過去”。例如，金屬通常可作為電和熱的導體。","examples":[{"en":"Copper is a good conductor of electricity.","zh":"銅是良好的電導體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The metal handle is a conductor of heat.","zh":"這個金屬把手是熱的傳導體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conductor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cff179e7721e503c090c","word":"cone","forms":["cone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1655b0e68b350dbc","term":"cone","forms":["cone","cones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓錐曲面","explanation":"在幾何學中，cone 可以指繞著一條相交的直線旋轉另一條線段所形成的曲面。它強調的是圓錐的外部曲面，不一定包括內部實體。","examples":[{"en":"The curve rotates around the axis to form a cone.","zh":"這條曲線繞軸旋轉形成一個圓錐曲面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plane can intersect a cone to form an ellipse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8c1250ccd01caa2","term":"cone","forms":["cone","cones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓錐體","explanation":"在幾何學中，cone 也指由三角形繞其中一條高旋轉形成的實體，也就是通常所說的圓錐體。它有一個圓形底面和一個尖端。","examples":[{"en":"The volume of a cone is one-third the volume of a cylinder with the same base and height.","zh":"底面和高相同的圓錐體，其體積是圓柱體積的三分之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cone has one circular base and a pointed top.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0d08181ff814e94b68d","word":"confederation","forms":["confederation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-908ad1bb8ac4953c","term":"confederation","forms":["confederation","confederations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治聯盟","explanation":"confederation 是多個國家或政治組織組成的聯盟；成員聯合行動，但通常仍保留相當程度的獨立性。它強調“各自為政的一些組織結成一個整體”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The neighboring states formed a confederation to defend their borders.","zh":"鄰近的幾個國家結成了一個聯盟來保衛邊境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The confederation allows each member state to keep its own laws.","zh":"這個聯盟允許每個成員國保留自己的法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confederation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f37023dbd73d95de","term":"confederation","forms":["confederation","confederations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結成聯盟","explanation":"confederation 也可以指多個國家或政治組織建立聯盟這一行為或過程，重點在“聯合起來”這一步，而不只是聯合後的組織。","examples":[{"en":"The formation of the confederation took several years of negotiation.","zh":"這個聯盟的建立經歷了數年的談判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Confederation brought the previously independent colonies together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confederation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea728840d371e1a556f5","word":"conference","forms":["conference"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32cd3eef03062f93","term":"conference","forms":["conference","conferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式商談","explanation":"指人們正式坐下來交換意見、認真討論或協商的過程，重點在“聚在一起談”。","examples":[{"en":"The two sides held a conference to discuss the new agreement.","zh":"雙方舉行了一次會議，討論新的協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge requested a conference with both lawyers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dedfeba4120b0c31","term":"conference","forms":["conference","conferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學術會議","explanation":"指科學家或研究人員展示研究成果的正式活動，可以有演講、研討會、海報展示等不同環節。","examples":[{"en":"She presented her latest research at an international conference.","zh":"她在一次國際學術會議上展示了自己最新的研究成果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She presented her findings at a chemistry conference.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b33f0f602057e9cc4489","word":"confess","forms":["confess"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-400328e0f90d786a","term":"confess","forms":["confess","confesses","confessing","confessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承認過錯或罪行","explanation":"指承認某件確實做過、通常又不太願意公開的錯事，尤其是罪行或嚴重過錯；重點是把真相說出來，而不只是表示後悔。","examples":[{"en":"She confessed to taking the money from the drawer.","zh":"她承認拿走了抽屜裡的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He finally confessed that he had broken the window.","zh":"他終於承認是自己打碎了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-721bdde6ae7598e7","term":"confess","forms":["confess","confesses","confessing","confessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭示隱藏的事實","explanation":"指某人或某物把原本隱藏的事實、特徵或資訊顯露出來，彷彿替它把秘密說了出來；常帶有較正式或文學性的色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The old photograph confessed more than the family intended to reveal.","zh":"那張老照片透露出的資訊，比這家人原本想公開的更多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His nervous smile confessed that he already knew the answer.","zh":"他緊張的笑容表明，他早就知道答案了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae714c76abba41e031af","word":"confession","forms":["confession"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f4af0523b915af2","term":"confession","forms":["confession","confessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承認過錯","explanation":"指一個人公開承認自己做過某件事，尤其是壞事或違法的事；重點在於把原本隱瞞的事實說出來。","examples":[{"en":"The police were waiting for a full confession.","zh":"警方在等待一份完整的認罪供述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her confession shocked everyone in the room.","zh":"她的坦白讓房間裡的所有人都大為震驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93bc610b68bad8a0","term":"confession","forms":["confession","confessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認罪書；書面供認","explanation":"指把認錯或認罪內容寫下來的正式檔案，通常由當事人簽署或交給警方、法庭等機構。","examples":[{"en":"The suspect refused to sign the confession.","zh":"嫌疑人拒絕在認罪書上簽字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The detective placed the signed confession before the jury.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff0139d07c592e9ae929","word":"confidence","forms":["confidence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d446c8634234e926","term":"confidence","forms":["confidence","confidences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自信；信心","explanation":"指相信自己的能力，因此敢於行動或面對挑戰；也可泛指做某事時心裡有底、有信心。","examples":[{"en":"He entered the ring with confidence.","zh":"他滿懷信心地走進了拳擊場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has confidence in her ability to solve the problem.","zh":"她相信自己有能力解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confidence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51005c091c926081","term":"confidence","forms":["confidence","confidences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"把握；信任","explanation":"指對某件事會發生、某個判斷正確，或某人值得信賴的堅定相信；重點不一定是相信自己，而是相信物件或結果。","examples":[{"en":"She had confidence that the problem would soon end.","zh":"她相信這個問題很快就會結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team has confidence in its new leader.","zh":"團隊信任它的新領導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confidence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26c8cca6e668df65cc08","word":"confident","forms":["confident"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-075d62f482fd54d5","term":"confident","forms":["confident","more confident","most confident"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有把握的","explanation":"表示說話人相信某件事是真的、會發生或能成功，心裡沒有太多懷疑。這裡的“信任”指對事實或結果的信任，不一定表示證據絕對充分。","examples":[{"en":"I'm confident that we can finish the project on time.","zh":"我有把握我們能按時完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sounded confident about the result.","zh":"她說起結果時顯得很有把握。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae64596f9ef77a8b","term":"confident","forms":["confident","more confident","most confident"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自信的","explanation":"表示一個人相信自己的能力、判斷或表現，因此做事說話比較鎮定，不容易退縮。它描述的是人的心理狀態或外在表現，不只是對某個具體事實的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"He felt confident speaking in front of a large audience.","zh":"他在大庭廣眾面前講話時很自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach wants the players to be more confident.","zh":"教練希望隊員們更加自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3151084286f59511ce11","word":"confidential","forms":["confidential"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ae7f20933eeb680","term":"confidential","forms":["confidential","more confidential","most confidential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"機密的；不公開的","explanation":"指只允許特定的人知道、不能向公眾公開的資訊或材料；秘密的範圍通常由某個組織、政府或小團體規定。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep this confidential until the announcement is made.","zh":"在正式宣佈之前，請對這件事保密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lawyer showed me a confidential document.","zh":"律師給我看了一份機密檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confidential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c64bc36dfe56ce798e5f","word":"confine","forms":["confine"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-204fcb3a8b1f3a41","term":"confine","forms":["confine","confines","confining","confined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"限制；使侷限於","explanation":"指把人或事物圍在某個範圍、地點或活動領域內，使其不能超出界線；既可以是實際關住，也可以是抽象地限制範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor confined him to bed for several days.","zh":"醫生讓他臥床休息了幾天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please confine your comments to the main issue.","zh":"請把你的評論限制在主要問題上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f267c2ab422e502bad8","word":"confirm","forms":["confirm"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b345026eb60e86a4","term":"confirm","forms":["confirm","confirms","confirming","confirmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使堅定；加強","explanation":"把原本可能動搖的人、信念或決心變得更穩固，就像把它釘牢一樣。重點是增強堅定性，不只是讓別人知道某個訊息。","examples":[{"en":"The coach's words confirmed her resolve to keep trying.","zh":"教練的話堅定了她繼續努力的決心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The successful trial confirmed her faith in the treatment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confirm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3106a9da705f3b9f","term":"confirm","forms":["confirm","confirms","confirming","confirmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"證實；確認屬實","explanation":"用新的證據或資訊把先前的說法、猜測或懷疑釘實，說明它確實如此。它通常不是從零開始發現事實，而是對已有判斷作出確認。","examples":[{"en":"The follow-up test confirmed that the treatment was working.","zh":"後續檢查證實了這種治療正在起作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please confirm your booking by Friday.","zh":"請在星期五前確認你的預訂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confirm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa9e1d22205ad852b0dc","word":"conflict","forms":["conflict"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1eda9e0d92986adb","term":"conflict","forms":["conflict","conflicts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衝突；對立；爭端","explanation":"指兩個或多個彼此對立的人、群體或勢力發生的衝突，可以是意見、利益上的對抗，也可以發展成暴力爭鬥。重點是雙方像迎面相撞一樣無法和平共處。","examples":[{"en":"The conflict between the two communities lasted for years.","zh":"這兩個社群之間的衝突持續了多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy caused a conflict between workers and managers.","zh":"新政策引發了工人和管理層之間的衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conflict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-956c3f8d7eebe2b2","term":"conflict","forms":["conflict","conflicts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不相容；安排衝突","explanation":"指兩件事、兩項要求或兩個安排碰到一起，不能同時實現或進行。它不一定有人爭吵，而是像兩條路在同一時間佔用了同一個位置。","examples":[{"en":"There is a conflict in my schedule on Friday afternoon.","zh":"我的日程在週五下午有衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rehearsal conflicts with my evening class.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conflict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c28d4804cfa499bb","term":"conflict","forms":["conflict","conflicts","conflicting","conflicted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與……不合；與……衝突","explanation":"指某人、某團體、觀點或目標彼此對立、不一致，無法順利共存。它是名詞“衝突”變成動作或狀態的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Her personal values conflict with the company's policy.","zh":"她的個人價值觀與公司的政策相沖突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two witnesses' accounts conflict with each other.","zh":"兩名證人的說法彼此矛盾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conflict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7693628103f401d6b976","word":"conform","forms":["conform"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-168fe40db02f9232","term":"conform","forms":["conform","conforms","conforming","conformed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調整自己以相符合","explanation":"指一個人或事物改變自己的形狀、行為或方式，使自己更像某個既定物件或標準；重點是主動適應、靠攏。","examples":[{"en":"Plants often conform themselves to the shape of the trellis as they grow.","zh":"植物生長時常常會使自己的形狀適應棚架的形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child quickly conformed to the routine of the new school.","zh":"這個孩子很快適應了新學校的日常安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d2b963ee313c3d0","term":"conform","forms":["conform","conforms","conforming","conformed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵從習俗或規範","explanation":"指人在行為、穿著或外在儀式上按照某種社會規範或習俗行事，是“把自己塑造成符合規範的樣子”的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"She conformed to the local custom and removed her shoes at the door.","zh":"她遵循當地習俗，在門口脫下了鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students need not conform to every passing fashion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-199c48140d2be4278289","word":"confront","forms":["confront"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4aa7b6b9d6fe974","term":"confront","forms":["confront","confronts","confronting","confronted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正面對抗","explanation":"指與某人迎面相對，尤其是在敵意、爭執或挑戰的情況下進行對抗；重點是雙方都被置於正面衝突中。","examples":[{"en":"The protesters confronted the police outside the building.","zh":"抗議者在大樓外與警察正面對抗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tenants confronted their landlord over the unsafe wiring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confront","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a89b0a689df88a42","term":"confront","forms":["confront","confronts","confronting","confronted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處理問題","explanation":"指不再回避某個問題、困難或不愉快的事實，而是主動把它拿出來處理；這裡不一定有人與人之間的衝突。","examples":[{"en":"The committee must confront the budget problem before making a decision.","zh":"委員會在作出決定前必須處理預算問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We must confront the shortage before winter arrives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confront","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69979eac5bbca588","term":"confront","forms":["confront","confronts","confronting","confronted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"讓某人面對事實","explanation":"指把某件事擺到某人面前，迫使或要求對方正視它，常常包含當面質問的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She confronted her roommate about the unpaid rent.","zh":"她就未付的房租當面質問室友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She confronted him with copies of the missing receipts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confront","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2167d5a2193dbcc701fd","word":"confrontation","forms":["confrontation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a89d1f72ac86c7c2","term":"confrontation","forms":["confrontation","confrontations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正面對抗；衝突","explanation":"指雙方直接相對並互相挑戰或對抗，可以是人與人之間的衝突，也可以是不同觀點、群體或立場之間的公開較量。核心畫面是“兩方迎面碰上，誰也不輕易讓步”。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting ended in a confrontation between the manager and the workers.","zh":"會議最後演變成經理和工人之間的正面衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tried to avoid a direct confrontation with her neighbor.","zh":"她儘量避免和鄰居發生直接衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confrontation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a4bb7098103c148","term":"confrontation","forms":["confrontation","confrontations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"武裝衝突","explanation":"特指軍隊或武裝力量之間的交戰和衝突，是“正面對抗”這一核心畫面在戰爭場景中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The border dispute led to a brief armed confrontation.","zh":"邊境爭端導致了一場短暫的武裝衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The border confrontation left several soldiers wounded.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confrontation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41364e7a52d1d83f8a2f","word":"confuse","forms":["confuse"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-418fa6c933278e35","term":"confuse","forms":["confuse","confuses","confusing","confused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使困惑","explanation":"把事情攪得難以理解，使某人想不明白、摸不清情況。重點不是單純“難”，而是原本應有的線索或條理被打亂了。","examples":[{"en":"The unfamiliar map confused me.","zh":"這張不熟悉的地圖把我弄糊塗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden change in plans confused everyone.","zh":"計劃突然改變，把大家都弄得不知所措。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78dcf89bba70c999","term":"confuse","forms":["confuse","confuses","confusing","confused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"混淆；誤認","explanation":"把兩個本來不同的事物攪在一起，因而把一個誤認為另一個。這是“界線被攪亂”這一核心畫面在辨認關係上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I confused the north entrance with the main entrance.","zh":"我把北門誤認成了正門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People often confuse the two similar-looking birds.","zh":"人們常常把這兩種長得相像的鳥混淆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32c870923fced53850ca","word":"confusion","forms":["confusion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23ec9548483886ea","term":"confusion","forms":["confusion","confusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺乏清晰或秩序的混亂","explanation":"指資訊、安排、局面等沒有清楚的結構或方向，讓人或整個場面變得混亂。這是最寬泛、最常用的核心義，重點在“外部不清楚、不整齊”。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden change caused confusion at the airport.","zh":"突然的變化在機場造成了混亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is still confusion about the new rules.","zh":"人們對新規定仍然感到困惑，規定本身也不夠清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3c47b56e66d1555","term":"confusion","forms":["confusion","confusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"困惑或誤解的狀態","explanation":"指一個人因為沒有理解清楚而感到困惑，或因此產生誤解。它和“外部局面混亂”相連，但焦點轉到了人的思路和理解上。","examples":[{"en":"After reading the instructions twice, I was still in confusion.","zh":"我把說明讀了兩遍，還是感到困惑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His silence led to confusion about what he really meant.","zh":"他的沉默讓人誤解了他的真正意思。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/confusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7985d6d17717a2608e6","word":"congratulate","forms":["congratulate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-003a19fbdea90026","term":"congratulate","forms":["congratulate","congratulates","congratulating","congratulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人道賀","explanation":"為某人的成功、好訊息或人生喜事感到高興，並把這份喜悅表達給對方；也就是“恭喜、祝賀”。","examples":[{"en":"I called to congratulate Maya on her promotion.","zh":"我打電話向瑪雅祝賀她升職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone congratulated the team on winning the final.","zh":"大家都祝賀這支隊伍贏得了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congratulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd20fa4e50be4daf","term":"congratulate","forms":["congratulate","congratulates","congratulating","congratulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"慶幸自己；自我稱許","explanation":"把道賀的喜悅轉向自己：因為自己的判斷、計劃或行動取得好結果，而覺得自己很幸運或做得不錯。","examples":[{"en":"She congratulated herself on saving enough money for the trip.","zh":"她慶幸自己攢夠了旅行所需的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He congratulated himself for spotting the forged banknote.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congratulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2604ec8329e7e605894d","word":"congratulation(s)","forms":["congratulations"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"congratulations","forms":["congratulations","congratulation"],"pos":"n.","zh":"恭賀；祝賀的話","examples":[{"en":"Please accept my congratulations on your graduation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The winner received congratulations from friends around the world.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-3db20e1df89a35eacd11","word":"congress","forms":["congress"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d17f464d5401dfe4","term":"congress","forms":["congress","congresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表大會；正式會議","explanation":"指為討論或決定某個具體問題而舉行的正式集會，通常有來自不同團體或地區的代表參加。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists from around the world attended the annual congress.","zh":"來自世界各地的科學家參加了年度大會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The congress will discuss new treatments for the disease.","zh":"大會將討論這種疾病的新療法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9964d914354da15","term":"congress","forms":["congress","congresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立法機構；國會","explanation":"指國家或州的立法機關，尤其常指由兩個議院組成的美國國會。","examples":[{"en":"Congress is debating a new climate bill.","zh":"國會正在辯論一項新的氣候法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bill must be approved by Congress.","zh":"這項法案必須得到國會批准。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86e496830021280d44e5","word":"congressman/congresswoman","forms":["congressman","congresswoman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49e0cf4bc4e1c3ba","term":"congressman","forms":["congressman","congressmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男國會議員","explanation":"指美國國會中的男性議員，也就是代表選民參與聯邦立法和政治事務的人。記住“進入國會、代表選民發言”這一核心形象即可。","examples":[{"en":"The congressman from Ohio spoke at the town meeting.","zh":"那位來自俄亥俄州的國會議員在市民會議上發了言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The congressman met with local voters before the election.","zh":"那位國會議員在選舉前會見了當地選民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congressman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4915149315056440","term":"congressman","forms":["congressman","congressmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男眾議員","explanation":"在美國語境中，它還常特指眾議院的男性議員；這是“國會議員”這一核心意義的更具體範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The congressman introduced a bill in the House of Representatives.","zh":"這位眾議員在眾議院提出了一項法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The congressman visited schools throughout his district.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congressman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66509c366410351b","term":"congresswoman","forms":["congresswoman","congresswomen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女國會議員","explanation":"指女性國會議員，也就是在國家立法機構中任職的女性；在美國英語裡通常指美國國會議員。","examples":[{"en":"The congresswoman spoke about the need for better public transportation.","zh":"這位女國會議員談到了改善公共交通的必要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A young congresswoman introduced the new education bill.","zh":"一位年輕的女國會議員提出了新的教育法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congresswoman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c0a2bf61b198783","term":"congresswoman","forms":["congresswoman","congresswomen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眾議院女議員","explanation":"在美國語境中，有時專指美國眾議院的女性議員；這是“女國會議員”這一概念的更具體範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The congresswoman from Ohio announced her retirement from the House.","zh":"來自俄亥俄州的那位眾議院女議員宣佈將退出眾議院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The congresswoman introduced a bill protecting coastal wetlands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congresswoman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a638a128ca67348f107","word":"connect","forms":["connect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b396022b909658b0","term":"connect","forms":["connect","connects","connecting","connected","connectest","connectedst","connecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"接到；連線到","explanation":"表示一個物體接到另一個物體上，或本來就是設計來與另一個物體接合的。重點是“某物連到另一物上”。","examples":[{"en":"This cable connects to the back of the monitor.","zh":"這根電纜接在顯示器後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Does this hose connect to the faucet?","zh":"這根軟管能接到水龍頭上嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/connect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e453fc0864eb45e5","term":"connect","forms":["connect","connects","connecting","connected","connectest","connectedst","connecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相連；連通","explanation":"表示兩個或多個事物彼此相連，尤其用於道路、房間或線路等能連成一體的事物。這裡強調它們之間是否存在通路，而不是某人正在進行連線動作。","examples":[{"en":"The two walking paths connect behind the library.","zh":"這兩條步道在圖書館後面相連。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These rooms connect through a narrow hallway.","zh":"這些房間透過一條狹窄的走廊相通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/connect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-701e76edf713f23e","term":"connect","forms":["connect","connects","connecting","connected","connectest","connectedst","connecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連線兩者；使相通","explanation":"表示某條道路、鐵路、橋樑或其他事物充當紐帶，把兩個地點或物體連在一起。重點是“一個東西讓兩邊建立連線”。","examples":[{"en":"A new bridge will connect the island to the mainland.","zh":"一座新橋將把這座島和大陸連線起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The subway connects the airport with the city center.","zh":"地鐵把機場和市中心連線起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/connect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4ddc6c3e4ec3a8f","term":"connect","forms":["connect","connects","connecting","connected","connectest","connectedst","connecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……接上","explanation":"表示親手拿起一個物體，把它安裝或接到另一個物體上。與s4相比，這裡強調的是人進行的具體連線動作。","examples":[{"en":"I connected the speakers to the television.","zh":"我把揚聲器接到了電視上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Connect the charger to the phone before turning it on.","zh":"開機前先把充電器接到手機上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/connect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b38d9d168c3aedf156f4","word":"connection","forms":["connection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-399b8bd71fc39557","term":"connection","forms":["connection","connections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連線這一動作或過程","explanation":"connection 可以表示把兩個或多個事物系在一起、建立聯絡這一過程，而不一定指具體的連線點或關係。","examples":[{"en":"The connection of the two systems took several hours.","zh":"把這兩個系統連線起來花了幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A secure connection is essential for sharing these files.","zh":"共享這些檔案必須建立安全連線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/connection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1367b6b57869df19","term":"connection","forms":["connection","connections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連線點；兩者之間的聯絡","explanation":"connection 也指兩件事實際接上的地方，或它們之間存在的因果、邏輯等聯絡；這就是“線把兩個點系在一起”的具體關係。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers found a connection between poor sleep and memory problems.","zh":"研究人員發現睡眠不足與記憶問題之間存在聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the connection between the cable and the monitor.","zh":"檢查一下電纜和顯示器之間的連線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/connection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fab2c4aa0b632cf1","term":"connection","forms":["connection","connections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人與人之間的默契和親近感","explanation":"在人際交往中，connection 指雙方感到彼此理解、交流自然而且相處舒服的紐帶，不只是認識對方。","examples":[{"en":"I felt an instant connection with my new colleague.","zh":"我馬上就覺得自己和新同事很合得來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Music created a connection between the performers and the audience.","zh":"音樂在表演者和觀眾之間建立了默契。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/connection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ba89aa561f58111edf8","word":"conquer","forms":["conquer"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-927f86d5961b900c","term":"conquer","forms":["conquer","conquers","conquering","conquered","conquerest","conqueredst","conquereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"制服；戰勝","explanation":"指在戰鬥或對抗中擊敗對方，使其失去抵抗能力。這裡的核心畫面是把一個正在阻擋自己的敵人攻下來。","examples":[{"en":"The army conquered its strongest rival after a long battle.","zh":"這支軍隊經過長期戰鬥，征服了最強大的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked hard to conquer the doubts that held her back.","zh":"她努力克服了那些阻礙自己的疑慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conquer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20662a53a818f28b","term":"conquer","forms":["conquer","conquers","conquering","conquered","conquerest","conqueredst","conquereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"克服；戰勝","explanation":"指經過努力戰勝恐懼、困難、習慣等抽象障礙。雖然沒有真正的戰場，但仍然把它們當作需要攻克的對手。","examples":[{"en":"He finally conquered his fear of speaking in public.","zh":"他終於克服了在公眾面前講話的恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With practice, you can conquer this difficult skill.","zh":"透過練習，你可以攻克這項困難的技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conquer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c97c184615c9da4c9e90","word":"conquest","forms":["conquest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-172d97648be913a5","term":"conquest","forms":["conquest","conquests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"征服；戰勝","explanation":"指透過戰鬥擊敗敵人並取得其土地、政權或控制權，核心畫面就是把對方的領域拿下來。","examples":[{"en":"The conquest of the city took several months.","zh":"征服這座城市花了好幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book describes the Roman conquest of Britain.","zh":"這本書講述了羅馬征服不列顛的過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conquest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-933a98a0fd7a6b5e","term":"conquest","forms":["conquest","conquests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"征服；克服","explanation":"指透過努力克服障礙並取得對某個領域的掌控，不一定涉及武力，例如征服太空或困難。","examples":[{"en":"The conquest of space required new technology.","zh":"征服太空需要新的技術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Climbing the mountain was her greatest conquest.","zh":"登上這座山是她最偉大的挑戰征服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conquest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0abf920cbcf2b571b6ce","word":"conscience","forms":["conscience"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a31ad2434fe7a124","term":"conscience","forms":["conscience","consciences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"良心；道德感","explanation":"指人心中判斷自己行為是對是錯的能力和感覺。它像一盞內在的道德燈：做錯事時可能讓人內疚，做了正確的事時則讓人感到心安。","examples":[{"en":"Her conscience would not let her keep the money.","zh":"她的良心不允許她留下那筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had a guilty conscience after lying to my friend.","zh":"我對朋友撒謊後感到良心不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conscience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-575bfabbfc054b64","term":"conscience","forms":["conscience","consciences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擬人化的良心","explanation":"在小說、戲劇或寓言中，conscience 可以被寫成一個聲音、人物或神秘存在，專門提醒角色什麼是對的、什麼是錯的；它仍然來自“內在道德燈”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"In the story, his conscience appeared as a quiet voice beside him.","zh":"在故事中，他的良心以身旁一個安靜聲音的形象出現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His conscience whispered that keeping the money was wrong.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conscience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4203e108f89147918c4","word":"conscientious","forms":["conscientious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eff4ee6a6c41d742","term":"conscientious","forms":["conscientious","more conscientious","most conscientious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"認真負責的","explanation":"指做事特別仔細、盡責，願意花時間檢查細節，確保任務按要求完成；這裡體現的是“良知監督員”對工作質量的要求。","examples":[{"en":"She is conscientious about checking every report before sending it.","zh":"她很認真負責，每份報告發出前都會仔細檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was a conscientious worker who never ignored small problems.","zh":"他是個認真負責的員工，從不忽視小問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conscientious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8dd4506c52360529","term":"conscientious","forms":["conscientious","more conscientious","most conscientious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有良知、守原則的","explanation":"指一個人做決定時聽從內心的良知，認真遵守自己認可的是非原則；這不僅是辦事仔細，更是道德上的自律。","examples":[{"en":"A conscientious manager refused to hide the mistake from the public.","zh":"一位有良知的經理拒絕向公眾隱瞞這個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a conscientious objector, he refused military service.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conscientious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db6e2c6375d091cce686","word":"conscious","forms":["conscious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d54982341490df67","term":"conscious","forms":["conscious","more conscious","most conscious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清醒的","explanation":"指人已經醒來，頭腦恢復活動，能夠正常感知和思考。它強調從昏睡、失去知覺等狀態中恢復清醒。","examples":[{"en":"She was conscious again a few minutes after the accident.","zh":"事故發生幾分鐘後，她又恢復了意識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He remained conscious throughout the ambulance journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conscious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf116d79647aa666","term":"conscious","forms":["conscious","more conscious","most conscious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有自我意識的","explanation":"指人不僅清醒，還能意識到自己的存在、想法和正在經歷的事情；這是“意識之燈照向自己”。","examples":[{"en":"As children grow older, they become more conscious of themselves as individuals.","zh":"孩子長大後，會越來越意識到自己是獨立的個體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The philosopher asks whether machines can become conscious.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conscious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e94fbd2db76bc97674c3","word":"consecutive","forms":["consecutive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba03efaf67dd1bbc","term":"consecutive","forms":["consecutive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"連續的；接連的","explanation":"指同類事件一個接著一個發生，中間沒有中斷；重點是連續性和相鄰性。","examples":[{"en":"The team won three consecutive games.","zh":"這支球隊連續贏了三場比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It rained for five consecutive days.","zh":"連續五天都下了雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consecutive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e7888534571a541","term":"consecutive","forms":["consecutive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"按順序相接的","explanation":"指幾個部分在時間或邏輯上有清楚的先後關係，後一個自然接在前一個之後；不一定強調完全沒有中斷。","examples":[{"en":"The two chapters describe consecutive stages of the experiment.","zh":"這兩章描述了實驗中前後相接的兩個階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Number the pages in consecutive order.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consecutive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c983c585ac3c40d92083","word":"consensus","forms":["consensus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-285ac8e747e954cc","term":"consensus","forms":["consensus","consensuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"協商形成共識的過程","explanation":"指一個群體透過討論、協調和相互讓步，努力形成廣泛一致意見的決策過程。重點在“形成共識”這一過程，而不只是最後的結論。","examples":[{"en":"The committee used a consensus-building process to choose the new director.","zh":"委員會透過建立共識的過程來選出新主任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council works by consensus, allowing everyone to discuss objections.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consensus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4fb1558acfd01d0","term":"consensus","forms":["consensus","consensuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"群體共識","explanation":"指某個群體成員普遍認可的意見或決定。它不要求每個人完全贊成，但表示大家已經接受一個共同方向，並願意據此採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"After two hours of discussion, the team reached consensus on the project plan.","zh":"經過兩個小時的討論，團隊就專案計劃達成了共識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is broad consensus among scientists that the method is reliable.","zh":"科學家普遍認為這種方法是可靠的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consensus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-12423e0482f3e81cb1d2","word":"consent","forms":["consent"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b23866f5026f4b7c","term":"consent","forms":["consent","consents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同意；許可","explanation":"指某人自願表示可以，因而允許某件事發生；重點是“得到許可”，而不是被迫接受。","examples":[{"en":"The school needs written consent from the parents.","zh":"學校需要得到家長的書面許可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined the project with her manager's consent.","zh":"她在得到經理許可後參加了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50d8184596b1b345","term":"consent","forms":["consent","consents","consenting","consented","consentest","consentedst","consenteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"同意；准許","explanation":"表示某人經過考慮後自願說“可以”，接受某件事或允許某件事發生。","examples":[{"en":"He finally consented to the surgery.","zh":"他最終同意接受手術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They consented to share the information.","zh":"他們同意分享這份資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84bb160039a7955385c4","word":"consequence","forms":["consequence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-909ee12001f75ff5","term":"consequence","forms":["consequence","consequences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結果；後果","explanation":"某個行為、事件或原因之後出現的結果就是 consequence。它可以是好結果，也可以是壞結果，但語境常常特別關注需要承擔的後果。","examples":[{"en":"Every action has a consequence, so think before you speak.","zh":"每個行動都會帶來結果，所以說話前要先想一想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The consequence of missing the last train was a long walk home.","zh":"錯過末班車的結果是不得不走很久回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consequence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6bea20318cab723","term":"consequence","forms":["consequence","consequences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要性；影響力","explanation":"如果某人或某事的結果、影響很有分量，就可以說它 is of consequence，意思是“重要、值得重視”。相反，of no consequence 表示“不重要、無關緊要”。","examples":[{"en":"Her decision could be of great consequence for the whole team.","zh":"她的決定可能會對整個團隊產生重大影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His remarks were of little consequence to the decision.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consequence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b92bacd14cca69abd48","word":"consequent","forms":["consequent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fbb18c2bbba5c1a","term":"consequent","forms":["consequent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"隨之而來的；由此產生的","explanation":"指某件事在另一件事之後自然發生，或是前一件事造成的結果，重點是“跟在前因後面”。","examples":[{"en":"The factory closed, and the consequent job losses affected the whole town.","zh":"工廠關閉，隨之而來的失業影響了整個城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her consequent fatigue made it difficult to concentrate.","zh":"由此產生的疲勞使她很難集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consequent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4873b35ecfe7c16121c","word":"conservation","forms":["conservation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c3c664b24d652d1","term":"conservation","forms":["conservation","conservations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護；儲存","explanation":"指把某物保護好，使它不受損、不丟失，或繼續保持完整狀態。它是全詞“把珍貴的東西留住”的基礎意義。","examples":[{"en":"The conservation of the old bridge will begin next year.","zh":"這座老橋的保護修繕將於明年開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Careful conservation kept the painting in good condition.","zh":"細緻的保護使這幅畫保持了良好狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a3f085b212cd542","term":"conservation","forms":["conservation","conservations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資源節約；資源保護","explanation":"指合理使用水、能源、森林等自然資源，避免浪費，讓它們能夠長期使用。這裡的核心不是完全不使用，而是控制使用、把資源留到以後。","examples":[{"en":"The city introduced new rules for water conservation.","zh":"這座城市出臺了新的節水規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Energy conservation can lower household bills.","zh":"節約能源可以降低家庭開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c152d5bbb379c3f94e74","word":"conservative","forms":["conservative"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-db58c2cfcbf5fd33","term":"conservative","forms":["conservative","more conservative","most conservative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"謹慎的；穩妥的","explanation":"表示採取較安全、適度的做法，不冒不必要的風險，例如分量、速度或計劃安排都留有餘地。這是“把事情穩穩保住”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The chef added a conservative amount of salt to the soup.","zh":"廚師往湯裡只加了適量的鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Taking a conservative approach, we tested the machine before increasing its speed.","zh":"我們採取穩妥的做法，先測試機器，再提高速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11d47ae8040d8d09","term":"conservative","forms":["conservative","more conservative","most conservative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"保守的；抗拒改變的","explanation":"表示不願迅速接受新觀念、制度或做法，更傾向於維持熟悉的傳統和現狀。它是從“保住原來的東西”延伸出來的核心政治和社會含義。","examples":[{"en":"The university has a conservative approach to changing its curriculum.","zh":"這所大學在修改課程方面採取保守的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her parents are quite conservative about social customs.","zh":"她的父母對社會習俗相當保守。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b05fe6c2d390ed81","term":"conservative","forms":["conservative","more conservative","most conservative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"支援保守主義的","explanation":"在政治、經濟或社會議題中，表示傾向維護傳統制度、限制快速變化，或支援保守主義的一系列主張。它把“不輕易改變、保住現有秩序”的核心概念用於政治立場。","examples":[{"en":"The region has elected a conservative government.","zh":"這個地區選出了一個保守派政府。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He joined a conservative party that favored traditional institutions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-694ee77e39a54838","term":"conservative","forms":["conservative","conservatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保守派人士","explanation":"指傾向維持現狀、支援傳統制度或不贊成快速改變的人。這個名詞直接把“保住原有秩序”的核心概念變成了人的稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"Conservatives often argue that traditions should be protected.","zh":"保守派人士常認為傳統應該得到保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is a conservative who prefers gradual reform.","zh":"他是一個傾向於漸進改革的保守派人士。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conservative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ffd29b0b05afb86693e3","word":"conserve","forms":["conserve"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a9cea536ed4d8ebc","term":"conserve","forms":["conserve","conserves","conserving","conserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"儲存；節約使用","explanation":"指透過妥善處理或減少浪費，把食物、能源等留到以後使用。這個意思直接體現了“把東西守住，不讓它白白消失”。","examples":[{"en":"Turning off the lights helps conserve energy.","zh":"關燈有助於節約能源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers conserve fruit by cooking it with sugar.","zh":"村民把水果加糖煮制來儲存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45e39496dcafb311","term":"conserve","forms":["conserve","conserves","conserving","conserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；保全","explanation":"指採取措施保護自然環境、歷史建築、傳統或其他有價值的事物，使它們不被破壞或消失。","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to conserve the area's historic buildings.","zh":"這個專案旨在保護該地區的歷史建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local groups are working to conserve the wetland.","zh":"當地團體正在努力保護這片溼地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2181584795ff55116093","word":"consider","forms":["consider"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5c254872e1af766","term":"consider","forms":["consider","considers","considering","considered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認真考慮","explanation":"指把某件事放在心上，認真思考它的情況、後果或重要性，而不是隨便想一想。","examples":[{"en":"Please consider the possible risks before you sign the contract.","zh":"籤合同前，請認真考慮可能存在的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Consider that we still have two months to finish the project.","zh":"請認真想想，我們還有兩個月來完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consider","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-966f096f34e71de3","term":"consider","forms":["consider","considers","considering","considered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細權衡","explanation":"不帶直接賓語時，指停下來認真想、比較不同選擇或後果，強調思考過程。","examples":[{"en":"Take a few days to consider before you give me your answer.","zh":"你先花幾天仔細考慮一下，再給我答覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Consider the maintenance costs before buying the boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consider","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9e06fddd0dc30d3","term":"consider","forms":["consider","considers","considering","considered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"考慮做某事","explanation":"指把某個動作當作可能的選擇來衡量，表示“在想要不要做”，並不表示已經決定。","examples":[{"en":"We are considering moving to a smaller apartment.","zh":"我們正在考慮搬到一套更小的公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is considering taking a year off after graduation.","zh":"她正在考慮畢業後休學一年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consider","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18b263dcdea6a8a081d4","word":"considerable","forms":["considerable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9eddb173d8f748d6","term":"considerable","forms":["considerable","more considerable","most considerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"重要的；值得重視的","explanation":"形容某人或某事有相當的影響、地位或價值，重要到不能被忽略。這裡的“值得考慮”通常已經引申為“值得認真對待、值得重視”。","examples":[{"en":"She became a considerable figure in the music industry.","zh":"她後來成了音樂界一位舉足輕重的人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became a considerable figure in local politics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/considerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-533ca972ee5cae77","term":"considerable","forms":["considerable","more considerable","most considerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相當大的；數量可觀的","explanation":"形容數量、金額、程度或規模很大，已經達到值得注意的程度。它強調“分量不小”，但不表示一個精確的數值。","examples":[{"en":"The repairs cost a considerable amount of money.","zh":"修理花了相當大一筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A considerable crowd gathered to hear the returning explorer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/considerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-640efab2b9280f3b4862","word":"considerate","forms":["considerate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-962ab244065de23d","term":"considerate","forms":["considerate","more considerate","most considerate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"體貼周到","explanation":"指一個人注意到別人的需要、感受和方便，並主動採取不會給別人添麻煩的做法；重點是“替別人著想”。","examples":[{"en":"It was very considerate of you to give up your place for your friend.","zh":"你把位置讓給朋友，真是太替人著想了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please be considerate of the people who are sleeping.","zh":"請顧及正在睡覺的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/considerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a13c16ac39b6b58f","term":"considerate","forms":["considerate","more considerate","most considerate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"考慮周全","explanation":"指做決定、提出建議或設計做法時認真權衡，顯得謹慎而周全；這種“想得周到”常常也會讓別人感到被照顧。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a considerate response after listening to both sides.","zh":"她聽取雙方意見後，給出了一個考慮周全的答覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was considerate to warn us before arriving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/considerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6195048f9ca4906f9fad","word":"consideration","forms":["consideration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13486f18ada32c6c","term":"consideration","forms":["consideration","considerations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考慮；思量","explanation":"指把多個因素放在一起認真思量，以便作出決定或形成判斷。它強調的是思考和權衡的過程，而不只是短暫地想到某件事。","examples":[{"en":"After careful consideration, we decided to accept the offer.","zh":"經過慎重考慮，我們決定接受這份提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan needs further consideration before it is approved.","zh":"這個計劃在獲批前還需要進一步考慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consideration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96949c7ae84909b3","term":"consideration","forms":["consideration","considerations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考慮因素；理由","explanation":"指作決定時被納入權衡的一件事或一個理由。這裡不是“考慮”這個過程本身，而是“需要考慮的因素”。","examples":[{"en":"Cost was the main consideration when we chose the new supplier.","zh":"我們選擇新供應商時，成本是主要考慮因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cost is only one consideration when choosing a school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consideration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cac787df74af316ac86d","word":"consist","forms":["consist"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"consist","forms":["consist"],"pos":"v.","zh":"由…組成（consist of）","examples":[{"en":"These teams consist of students from different schools.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A balanced meal should consist of more than just bread.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-206b5ec743f4c4871bc4","word":"consistent","forms":["consistent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73e740794041c653","term":"consistent","forms":["consistent","more consistent","most consistent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"穩定可靠的","explanation":"指某種行為、表現或情況反覆出現而且大致可靠，不會忽好忽壞。重點不是每次都完全相同，而是總體保持穩定。","examples":[{"en":"She is consistent about checking every detail before sending a report.","zh":"她每次發報告前都會檢查每個細節，做得很穩定可靠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team has produced consistent results all season.","zh":"這支隊伍整個賽季的表現都很穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consistent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d44597b8183c328","term":"consistent","forms":["consistent","more consistent","most consistent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相符的；一致的","explanation":"指一個說法、行為或結果與另一個事物相吻合，放在一起不會顯得矛盾。它強調彼此之間的關係，而不一定表示兩者完全相同。","examples":[{"en":"Her account is consistent with what the other witnesses told us.","zh":"她的說法與其他證人告訴我們的情況相符。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These fingerprints are consistent with those found upstairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consistent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e6013c7dbe4e386f222","word":"consolation","forms":["consolation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b24992737b21066","term":"consolation","forms":["consolation","consolations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安慰；慰藉","explanation":"指在悲傷、失望或遭受損失時，使人心裡好受一些的安慰，也可以指安慰人的行為或得到安慰的狀態。它是“失敗以後遞來的安慰”這一核心概念的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"She found some consolation in her friends' support.","zh":"朋友們的支援給了她一些安慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His family offered him consolation after the loss.","zh":"失去親人後，他的家人給了他安慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consolation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c88e586297af933d","term":"consolation","forms":["consolation","consolations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安慰獎","explanation":"指比賽或競賽中沒有獲勝者得到的獎品或好處，用來稍微彌補失敗，因此是“安慰”從抽象感受變成具體獎勵的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Although Mia finished second, she received a consolation prize.","zh":"雖然米婭獲得了第二名，她還是拿到了一份安慰獎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every runner-up received a small consolation prize.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consolation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93d8874c8c86f0fc893d","word":"console","forms":["console"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25adf54451680552","term":"console","forms":["console","consoles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家用裝置櫃；遊戲機","explanation":"指放在地面上的獨立櫃體，通常整合電視、音響或其他家庭娛樂裝置；在遊戲語境中也可指遊戲機。它體現了“承載裝置的櫃子”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The film's music blared from the console.","zh":"電影的音樂從那臺音響櫃裡震耳欲聾地傳出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My brother bought a new console for the living room.","zh":"我哥哥為客廳買了一臺新的遊戲機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/console","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a523f69f3b2836a4","term":"console","forms":["console","consoles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子系統控制檯","explanation":"指帶有顯示屏和輸入裝置的裝置，操作人員用它監測和控制電子系統。這裡的重點不是櫃體本身，而是“透過一個集中介面掌控系統”。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer monitored the railway signals from the operating console.","zh":"工程師透過操作控制檯監測鐵路訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The operator adjusted the settings on the control console.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/console","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e5a5ebd3fe8aab7","term":"console","forms":["console","consoles","consoling","consoled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安慰；慰藉","explanation":"指在別人悲傷、失望或遭遇打擊時給予安慰，讓對方的痛苦得到情緒上的支撐。這裡的“支撐”與名詞的承託義形成另一條記憶線。","examples":[{"en":"Her friends consoled her after she lost the match.","zh":"她輸掉比賽後，朋友們安慰了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was consoled by the thought that he had tried his best.","zh":"想到自己已經盡了最大努力，他得到了一些安慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/console","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b05a85b32ccc06be8dbf","word":"consonant","forms":["consonant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2288ad7e30699d8e","term":"consonant","forms":["consonant","consonants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"子音","explanation":"consonant 是發音時氣流在口腔中受到某種阻礙的聲音，例如英語中的許多非母音音。記住它就是“發聲時不是順暢流出，而是受到阻擋的聲音”。","examples":[{"en":"The first sound in “book” is a consonant.","zh":"“book”的第一個音是子音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"English syllables often begin with a consonant.","zh":"英語音節常常以子音開頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consonant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42109aaebde50d1056f3","word":"conspiracy","forms":["conspiracy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73bc64a288348e66","term":"conspiracy","forms":["conspiracy","conspiracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰謀；串通","explanation":"指多人暗中達成安排，共同做有害、不道德或顛覆性的事情；重點在於“聯手策劃不正當目標”。","examples":[{"en":"The police uncovered a conspiracy to attack the courthouse.","zh":"警方揭露了一起襲擊法院的陰謀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several officials were involved in the conspiracy.","zh":"幾名官員參與了這場陰謀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conspiracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e5b98c9e70f32aa","term":"conspiracy","forms":["conspiracy","conspiracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秘密協議","explanation":"較寬泛地指兩人或多人秘密約定一起做某事；事情本身不一定違法，但秘密聯手這一點很突出。","examples":[{"en":"The friends formed a conspiracy to surprise her on her birthday.","zh":"朋友們秘密商量，要在她生日時給她一個驚喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The intercepted letters revealed a conspiracy to sabotage the bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conspiracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96f6549c6b97a641e4d1","word":"constant","forms":["constant"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f97f7232565f5b0","term":"constant","forms":["constant","more constant","most constant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"始終不變的","explanation":"指在一段時間或一定範圍內保持原樣，沒有改變，突出穩定和持久。","examples":[{"en":"The temperature in this room remains constant all day.","zh":"這個房間裡的溫度一整天都保持不變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The solution must remain at a constant temperature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-135a1f34bc6ec815","term":"constant","forms":["constant","more constant","most constant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"持續不斷的","explanation":"指某事一次又一次地出現，幾乎沒有停歇，因此讓人感到一直存在或持續發生。","examples":[{"en":"The constant noise from the construction site kept me awake.","zh":"施工現場持續不斷的噪聲讓我無法入睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Constant drilling made concentration almost impossible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-130cb7dc324c7764","term":"constant","forms":["constant","more constant","most constant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"始終如一的","explanation":"指人在目的、行動或感情上不動搖，長期保持忠誠、堅定或可靠。","examples":[{"en":"She has been a constant friend through every difficult year.","zh":"在每一個艱難的年頭裡，她始終都是可靠的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her constant loyalty sustained the family through exile.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6297d02b6b7bfd5","term":"constant","forms":["constant","constants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固定不變之物","explanation":"指長期保持不變、不會隨情況改變的事物或因素，是形容詞“始終不變”名詞化後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Trust has been a constant in their long partnership.","zh":"信任一直是他們長期合作關係中不變的因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her kindness was the one constant in his childhood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c097b19679a817e5e02","word":"constitute","forms":["constitute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6947600d0496db41","term":"constitute","forms":["constitute","constitutes","constituting","constituted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式建立；制定","explanation":"指依據正式權力把法律、制度、機構或安排建立起來，使它們具有確定的效力。這個意思保留了“把東西放到位並確定下來”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The new act constituted an independent regulatory body.","zh":"這項新法正式設立了一個獨立的監管機構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement constituted a major change in policy.","zh":"這項協議正式確立了政策上的重大變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constitute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-941f44943e168d24","term":"constitute","forms":["constitute","constitutes","constituting","constituted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"構成；組成","explanation":"指若干部分、人或因素合在一起，形成一個整體或情況。想象把多個部分放在一起，整體便由它們構成。","examples":[{"en":"These three departments constitute the core of the organization.","zh":"這三個部門構成了該組織的核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Women constitute more than half of the workforce.","zh":"女性佔勞動力總數的一半以上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constitute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb9a7650cd532b61ca9f","word":"constitution","forms":["constitution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebd3c7f434da5714","term":"constitution","forms":["constitution","constitutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"構成；結構","explanation":"指某個事物由什麼組成、怎樣形成的整體結構，也可以指建立或形成這種結構的過程。它保留了“把東西立起來並組合成形”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists studied the physical constitution of the planet.","zh":"科學家研究了這顆行星的物質構成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chemical constitution of the sample remains uncertain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constitution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-665645d012967820","term":"constitution","forms":["constitution","constitutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政體；政治制度","explanation":"指一套組織政府或其他機構的基本原則、法律和執行安排，也就是把權力和規則“搭起來”的制度框架。","examples":[{"en":"The country's constitution divides power among three branches of government.","zh":"這個國家的憲法把權力分配給政府的三個分支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The revolution replaced the kingdom's constitution with a republic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constitution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab2ba181112374be7771","word":"constitutional","forms":["constitutional"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ebd06298ffc4e49","term":"constitutional","forms":["constitutional","more constitutional","most constitutional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"構成上根本的","explanation":"指某個特點屬於事物的基本構成或核心性質，缺少它，事物就不再是原來的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The two proposals differ in their constitutional principles.","zh":"這兩項提案在根本原則上有所不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His constitutional dislike of conflict made negotiations difficult.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constitutional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-248e6d9b06557ddc","term":"constitutional","forms":["constitutional","more constitutional","most constitutional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"憲法的","explanation":"指與國家或機構的憲法、基本法律制度及其規定的權利和原則有關。","examples":[{"en":"The proposed reform would strengthen constitutional protections for privacy.","zh":"擬議中的改革將加強憲法對隱私的保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal raises serious constitutional questions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constitutional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd00a996380547acaa70","word":"constraint","forms":["constraint"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-340dc3b52131a516","term":"constraint","forms":["constraint","constraints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制；約束條件","explanation":"指限制行動、設計或解決辦法的規則、條件或邊界；重點不是事情本身有多困難，而是你必須在這條“繩子”規定的範圍內行動。","examples":[{"en":"The budget constraint means we cannot hire more staff this year.","zh":"預算限制意味著我們今年不能再僱用更多員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a design that works within the space constraints.","zh":"我們需要一種能適應空間限制的設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constraint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a27cdf09a3eafd0","term":"constraint","forms":["constraint","constraints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強迫；不得不服從的壓力","explanation":"指一種強到讓人無法自由選擇的壓力或力量，人在這種 constraint 下做某事，往往不是出於自己的意願。","examples":[{"en":"She agreed to the deal only under considerable constraint.","zh":"她是在很大的壓力下才同意這項交易的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He signed under constraint, with armed guards behind him.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constraint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b252d4eb5acf5aeaef1e","word":"construct","forms":["construct"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ab4a99def1196d6","term":"construct","forms":["construct","constructs","constructing","constructed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組合建造","explanation":"指把零散部件裝配起來，形成一個完整的物體；核心畫面就是把東西一件件搭起來。","examples":[{"en":"We constructed the radio from spare parts.","zh":"我們用備用零件組裝出了這臺收音機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers constructed a bridge across the river.","zh":"工人們在河上建起了一座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/construct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a01adea4b8a1084a7ae","word":"construction","forms":["construction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abed5b7662d5ead0","term":"construction","forms":["construction","constructions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建造過程","explanation":"指把橋樑、房屋等東西建起來的過程，重點在“正在搭建”這一行動，而不是最後的建築物。","examples":[{"en":"Construction on the new hospital will begin next month.","zh":"新醫院的建設將於下個月開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road is closed because of construction.","zh":"這條路因施工而封閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/construction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af8fa059ea426f35","term":"construction","forms":["construction","constructions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詞語結構","explanation":"指按照一定規則排列起來、能夠表達完整意義的一組詞，也就是一種語言結構。","examples":[{"en":"The construction “the more you practice, the better you become” is common in English.","zh":"“你練習得越多，進步就越大”這一結構在英語中很常見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The construction 'used to' describes a former habit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/construction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2af288ba5b1b854","term":"construction","forms":["construction","constructions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對行為的看法","explanation":"指觀察者怎樣理解或評價某人的話、行為或事情，也就是從這些材料中“搭出”的意義和印象。","examples":[{"en":"Try not to put the worst construction on her silence.","zh":"儘量不要把她的沉默往最壞的方面理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She put a generous construction on his awkward remark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/construction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":5,"counts":{"111":4,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-521bdd8056bf0c57b8f6","word":"constructive","forms":["constructive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a824f67e14ecd869","term":"constructive","forms":["constructive","more constructive","most constructive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有建設性的；有助於改進的","explanation":"形容意見、批評或行動不是隻指出問題，而是能幫助人找到改進辦法，像是在問題上繼續搭建解決方案。因此，尖銳但具體、能帶來改善的批評也可以是 constructive。","examples":[{"en":"Please give me some constructive feedback on my presentation.","zh":"請對我的演講提一些有建設性的反饋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting was difficult, but the discussion remained constructive.","zh":"會議很艱難，但討論仍然是有建設性的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constructive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4d191c39d952bef","term":"constructive","forms":["constructive","more constructive","most constructive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有實際用途的","explanation":"表示某事能產生實際效果、幫助完成目標，而不是隻停留在空談或表達態度上。它和“搭建”這一核心影象相連：這種做法能為下一步提供有用的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"She played a constructive role in finding a solution.","zh":"她在尋找解決辦法的過程中發揮了實際作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put your energy into something constructive, like repairing the fence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/constructive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89fc0f6aa4921aac940a","word":"consult","forms":["consult"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1eae24326cf369d2","term":"consult","forms":["consult","consults","consulting","consulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"共同商量；徵求意見","explanation":"指把問題拿出來，向別人徵求意見，或和別人一起認真討論後再決定。它強調尋求判斷和建議的過程。","examples":[{"en":"We consulted with the engineer before changing the design.","zh":"我們在修改設計前和工程師商量過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She consulted her parents before accepting the offer.","zh":"她接受這份工作邀請前徵求了父母的意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af8dfaa6fad77d76","term":"consult","forms":["consult","consults","consulting","consulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人徵求意見","explanation":"指直接向某人請教、尋求其判斷或建議，是“共同商量”這一核心最常見的具體用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"You should consult a doctor if the pain continues.","zh":"如果疼痛持續，你應該去諮詢醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager consulted an expert before making the decision.","zh":"經理在作出決定前向一位專家徵求了意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48c82481ffda771a","term":"consult","forms":["consult","consults","consulting","consulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"查閱資料","explanation":"指為了獲得資訊而檢視詞典、手冊、檔案等資料，相當於把問題拿給資料來“請教”。","examples":[{"en":"Please consult the map before setting out.","zh":"出發前請查閱地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Consult the manual before adjusting the pressure valve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-217e43bae67e18ca","term":"consult","forms":["consult","consults","consulting","consulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"考慮；顧及","explanation":"指在判斷或採取行動時把某種需要、願望或條件納入考慮。它仍然保留“認真參考某個因素”的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The plan was revised to consult the needs of local residents.","zh":"這項計劃經過修改，以顧及當地居民的需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We must consult our budget before choosing a venue.","zh":"選擇場地前，我們必須考慮預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4087b6426d9adf2bd519","word":"consultant","forms":["consultant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81b5aea4de24dfdd","term":"consultant","forms":["consultant","consultants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專業顧問","explanation":"這是最常用的義項：consultant 是以專業知識、建議或服務為他人解決問題的人，可以為公司、機構或個人工作。核心畫面就是“被請來一起商量的專業人士”。","examples":[{"en":"We hired a financial consultant to review the company's budget.","zh":"我們聘請了一名財務顧問來審查公司的預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The consultant advised us to simplify the reporting process.","zh":"顧問建議我們簡化報告流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consultant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9507af385afa4238","term":"consultant","forms":["consultant","consultants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被徵求意見的人","explanation":"consultant 最基本的概念是“別人來找他商量的人”。這個義項可以泛指任何因判斷、經驗或知識而受到諮詢的一方，不一定把諮詢當作職業。","examples":[{"en":"The committee invited her as a consultant on environmental issues.","zh":"委員會邀請她擔任環境問題方面的顧問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They called her in as a consultant on pronunciation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consultant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-725949a1f8218e8d1997","word":"consultation","forms":["consultation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6b1d43b1652d4b2","term":"consultation","forms":["consultation","consultations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"徵求意見；商量","explanation":"指向別人請教、徵求意見或共同商量的行為，重點是透過交流來作出判斷或決定。它可以只表示這一過程，不一定指一場正式會議。","examples":[{"en":"The policy was changed after consultation with local teachers.","zh":"這項政策是在徵求當地教師的意見後修改的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No major decision should be made without consultation.","zh":"任何重大決定都不應在未經協商的情況下作出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consultation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-960958a29200e9fb","term":"consultation","forms":["consultation","consultations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資訊和建議交流會","explanation":"指專門組織起來的會議或討論會，讓參與者交換資訊、經驗和建議。與前一義相比，這裡更強調一個有多個參與者的正式活動。","examples":[{"en":"The city held a public consultation on the proposed transport plan.","zh":"市政府就擬議中的交通規劃舉行了一次公眾諮詢會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Public consultations will help shape the transport plan.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consultation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96f39e3569ec878ecb0b","word":"consume","forms":["consume"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fce58a71b3d83aab","term":"consume","forms":["consume","consumes","consuming","consumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用盡；消耗","explanation":"指把資源、燃料、時間等逐漸或完全用掉，重點是可用的東西被消耗了。","examples":[{"en":"This machine consumes a lot of electricity.","zh":"這臺機器耗電量很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project consumed most of our time.","zh":"這個專案佔用了我們大部分時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f973fdd595af42f2","term":"consume","forms":["consume","consumes","consuming","consumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃掉；食用","explanation":"指把食物吃下並吸收，常用於較正式的說明、報告或討論飲食的語境。","examples":[{"en":"Adults should consume less salt.","zh":"成年人應該少攝入鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The animal consumed the entire fish.","zh":"那隻動物把整條魚都吃掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98355afa5e1ff6d8","term":"consume","forms":["consume","consumes","consuming","consumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"完全佔據（思想或注意力）","explanation":"把人的心思或注意力比作會被某種情感、慾望或問題“全部吃掉”，表示人幾乎無法再關注別的事。","examples":[{"en":"She was consumed by jealousy.","zh":"嫉妒完全佔據了她的心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mystery consumed his thoughts for weeks.","zh":"這個謎團幾周來一直佔據著他的全部思緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bfbd709d5fdc0618ab5","word":"consumer","forms":["consumer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb515865fe6075b6","term":"consumer","forms":["consumer","consumers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消耗者","explanation":"指消耗某種物品、能源或資源的人、動物，甚至機器等事物；重點是“把某物用掉”，不一定涉及購買。","examples":[{"en":"This old heater is a heavy consumer of electricity.","zh":"這臺老式取暖器耗電量很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Data centers have become major consumers of cooling water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consumer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-879857c45eec6b64","term":"consumer","forms":["consumer","consumers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消費者","explanation":"指以個人身份花錢購買商品或服務的人，與生產者相對，是商業和經濟語境中最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Consumers can compare prices online before they buy.","zh":"消費者可以在購買前線上比較價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law gives consumers more protection.","zh":"這項法律為消費者提供了更多保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consumer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad8c6f6e417a6d2db992","word":"consumption","forms":["consumption"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96e2747119c1b733","term":"consumption","forms":["consumption","consumptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消費；消耗","explanation":"指吃、喝、使用某物這一消耗行為，重點在“把東西用掉或攝入”的過程，不只限於花錢購買。","examples":[{"en":"The consumption of electricity rises sharply in winter.","zh":"冬季的用電量會大幅上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The consumption of raw fish is common in this region.","zh":"這個地區常吃生魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consumption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a4a9db078433b92","term":"consumption","forms":["consumption","consumptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消耗量；消費量","explanation":"指在一段時間內被吃掉、用掉或消耗的總量，是“消耗”這個動作所產生的數量。","examples":[{"en":"Household water consumption has fallen this year.","zh":"今年家庭用水量下降了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Electricity consumption peaks during the hottest afternoons.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/consumption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114,115],"total":7,"counts":{"113":1,"114":5,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-093e7d5fdbaacfa92448","word":"contact","forms":["contact"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f10a2f7334712714","term":"contact","forms":["contact","contacts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體或物體的接觸","explanation":"指兩個身體或物體碰到一起，或處在緊密相連的狀態；這就是“接觸”這條核心概念的本義。","examples":[{"en":"Avoid direct contact between the cleaner and your skin.","zh":"避免清潔劑直接接觸皮膚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two wires must remain in contact.","zh":"這兩根電線必須保持接觸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5dd462893d4c955f","term":"contact","forms":["contact","contacts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建立聯絡","explanation":"指透過說話、電話、郵件等方式與某人或某組織建立溝通；這是從“碰到對方”引申出的“聯絡上對方”。","examples":[{"en":"Please contact me if you have any questions.","zh":"如有任何問題，請聯絡我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have stayed in contact since college.","zh":"我們從大學起一直保持聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ddae38c3337503f","term":"contact","forms":["contact","contacts","contacting","contacted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"接觸、碰到","explanation":"指一個物體或身體部分碰到另一個物體；它把名詞“接觸”變成了一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The falling branch contacted the roof.","zh":"掉下來的樹枝碰到了屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The probe must not contact the surrounding tissue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f13c2052bf28fc2","term":"contact","forms":["contact","contacts","contacting","contacted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聯絡某人或機構","explanation":"指主動透過電話、郵件或其他方式與某人或機構溝通，是名詞“取得聯絡”的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"I contacted the school about the missing documents.","zh":"我就檔案缺失一事聯絡了學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Contact the organizer if you need wheelchair access.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fc2fa3b48768edf9eb0","word":"contagious","forms":["contagious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d2fd519a6e7c590","term":"contagious","forms":["contagious","more contagious","most contagious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易傳播的","explanation":"指疾病、病毒等很容易從一個人或地方傳播到另一個人或地方，強調傳播起來不困難、範圍可能迅速擴大。","examples":[{"en":"The new flu virus is highly contagious, so please stay home.","zh":"這種新型流感病毒傳染性很強，所以請待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her contagious enthusiasm soon spread throughout the group.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contagious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d89832a1f53902c6","term":"contagious","forms":["contagious","more contagious","most contagious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有感染力的","explanation":"把“容易傳出去”的概念用於非疾病事物，表示一個人的熱情、笑聲或情緒很容易感染周圍的人。","examples":[{"en":"Her excitement was contagious, and soon everyone was cheering.","zh":"她的興奮情緒很有感染力，很快大家都歡呼起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His contagious laughter soon spread around the table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contagious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd9245cc1ddc69c88a8a","word":"contain","forms":["contain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22005198475faf33","term":"contain","forms":["contain","contains","containing","contained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝有；容納","explanation":"指某個容器、空間或物品裡面裝著某些東西，重點是內容物處在它的範圍之內。這個畫面是其他用法的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"This bottle contains enough water for the hike.","zh":"這瓶水足夠這次徒步使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sealed envelope contains your examination results.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4da95cee35986d1","term":"contain","forms":["contain","contains","containing","contained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包含；含有","explanation":"指一個整體把某種成分、部分或專案納入其中，不一定是實體容器在裝東西。比如食物含有某種成分，文章包含某項資訊，都可以用這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"The snack contains nuts, so it is not safe for her.","zh":"這種零食含有堅果，所以她吃了不安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box contains spare screws and a small wrench.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0942e3937b4df3b5","term":"contain","forms":["contain","contains","containing","contained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"控制住；抑制","explanation":"把情緒、衝動或行為想象成想衝出容器的東西；contain 就是把它壓在界限之內。因此“控制住自己”常表示沒讓激動、笑聲或怒氣表現出來。","examples":[{"en":"She could hardly contain herself when she heard the good news.","zh":"聽到這個好訊息時，她幾乎抑制不住自己的興奮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took a deep breath to contain his anger.","zh":"他深吸一口氣，努力壓住怒火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a42d519714d616e9411d","word":"container","forms":["container"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1412a046cec187cc","term":"container","forms":["container","containers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"容器","explanation":"指用來存放或運輸物品、材料或資料的東西，可以是盒子、瓶子、箱子，也可以是計算機中的資料容器。","examples":[{"en":"Keep the rice in an airtight container.","zh":"把米放在密封容器裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app stores each message in a separate container.","zh":"這個應用把每條訊息存放在單獨的容器中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/container","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e386b8af56652644","term":"container","forms":["container","containers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"集裝箱","explanation":"指運輸貨物用的特別大的金屬箱子，能夠在船、火車和卡車之間轉運而不必重新拆裝貨物。","examples":[{"en":"The goods were loaded into a container at the port.","zh":"貨物在港口被裝進了集裝箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The container arrived on a truck from the warehouse.","zh":"這個集裝箱由卡車從倉庫運到了這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/container","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a161c36bda594c573b59","word":"contaminate","forms":["contaminate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a66935fbc6e71b56","term":"contaminate","forms":["contaminate","contaminates","contaminating","contaminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"汙染，使有毒或有害","explanation":"把細菌、化學物質或其他有害成分帶入水、食物、土壤等，使它們不再安全。重點不是表面變髒，而是混入了可能造成危險的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The factory contaminated the river with toxic chemicals.","zh":"這家工廠用有毒化學物質汙染了河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eggs may have been contaminated with salmonella.","zh":"這些雞蛋可能受到了沙門氏菌汙染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contaminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13005862ffcd96ba","term":"contaminate","forms":["contaminate","contaminates","contaminating","contaminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"玷汙，敗壞","explanation":"把不良影響帶入原本清白、純正或受尊重的事物，使它在名譽、道德或象徵意義上受到玷汙。","examples":[{"en":"The scandal contaminated his reputation for honesty.","zh":"這起醜聞玷汙了他一向誠實的名聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bribery had contaminated every level of the administration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contaminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0439cc4746fb3ca71444","word":"contemplate","forms":["contemplate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c203e3f463aa7d08","term":"contemplate","forms":["contemplate","contemplates","contemplating","contemplated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細觀察並沉思","explanation":"指把某人或某事放在注意力中心，持續、認真地觀察它的各個方面，或深入思考它的意義和性質。它既可以是實際上的凝視，也可以是心裡的沉思。","examples":[{"en":"She stood by the window, contemplating the changing sky.","zh":"她站在窗邊，專注地凝望著不斷變化的天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent the evening contemplating the meaning of the painting.","zh":"他整個晚上都在沉思那幅畫的含義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contemplate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3f55f1c37f2ccc7","term":"contemplate","forms":["contemplate","contemplates","contemplating","contemplated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"考慮某種可能性","explanation":"指認真考慮某件事是否可能、是否值得做，尤其是在作決定之前進行權衡。這裡不一定表示已經決定，只表示把這個方案納入了考慮。","examples":[{"en":"They are contemplating moving to a smaller apartment.","zh":"他們正在考慮搬到一套更小的公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are contemplating a move to the countryside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contemplate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33b5c4fa571787bdc33a","word":"contemporary","forms":["contemporary"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da719654074fae71","term":"contemporary","forms":["contemporary","more contemporary","most contemporary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"同時代的","explanation":"指某人或某事物與另一人或另一事物處在同一個時代，重點是它們在時間線上相重合，不一定表示兩者見過面或同時發生。","examples":[{"en":"The cathedral is contemporary with the castle.","zh":"這座大教堂與那座城堡屬於同一時代。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two poets were contemporary with each other.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contemporary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5125e18f3e2952d6","term":"contemporary","forms":["contemporary","more contemporary","most contemporary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"當代的","explanation":"表示屬於現在這個時代，強調現代社會或今天的人們所處的時期，是“與現在同時代的”這一概念的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"She studies contemporary art at university.","zh":"她在大學學習當代藝術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gallery specializes in contemporary African painting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contemporary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d0739a192cf9396","term":"contemporary","forms":["contemporary","contemporaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同時代的人或事物","explanation":"指與另一個人或事物處在同一時代的物件，尤其常指同一時期生活或創作的人。","examples":[{"en":"The painter was a contemporary of the novelist.","zh":"這位畫家是那位小說家的同時代人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her contemporaries dismissed a theory later generations would accept.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contemporary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f7e11fc32d9dcd056ee","word":"contempt","forms":["contempt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf99c60496e6319c","term":"contempt","forms":["contempt","contempts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕蔑；鄙視","explanation":"指因為認為某人或某事低劣、卑微或毫無價值，而產生的強烈輕蔑態度；這種態度往往比普通的不喜歡更尖銳。","examples":[{"en":"She spoke about the proposal with open contempt.","zh":"她公開以不屑的口吻談論那項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has nothing but contempt for people who abuse their power.","zh":"他對那些濫用權力的人只有鄙視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contempt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1e34fbf82b63396","term":"contempt","forms":["contempt","contempts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受鄙視；恥辱","explanation":"指某人或某事處於被人看不起、被羞辱或失去尊嚴的狀態；重點從“輕蔑別人的態度”轉向“受到輕蔑、因此蒙受的恥辱”。","examples":[{"en":"The scandal brought contempt on the entire organization.","zh":"這起醜聞使整個組織蒙受了恥辱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His betrayal brought him into contempt among former allies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contempt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51ef2ad77766cb6e735b","word":"contend","forms":["contend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aac8d436e1bee81e","term":"contend","forms":["contend","contends","contending","contended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與人對抗、爭鬥","explanation":"指雙方處在對立狀態，為了勝負或立場而較量；可以是比賽中的競爭，也可以是激烈的衝突。","examples":[{"en":"Several teams are contending for the championship.","zh":"幾支隊伍正在爭奪冠軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two groups contended with each other over control of the company.","zh":"兩個團體為了公司的控制權相互爭鬥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c285c455d8a461c7","term":"contend","forms":["contend","contends","contending","contended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"努力爭取或保住","explanation":"強調為了得到、保住或捍衛某樣東西而持續用力競爭，重點在“爭取目標”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Three candidates are contending for the party leadership.","zh":"三名候選人正在爭奪黨內領導職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several manufacturers contend for a share of this growing market.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed7002b439e9ac845f22","word":"content","forms":["content"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-907f49b46f010740","term":"content","forms":["content","more content","contenter","most content","contentest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"滿足的；滿意的","explanation":"表示一個人覺得現在擁有的已經夠了，對生活、結果或處境感到滿意。它連線著“容器已經裝滿”的核心畫面：心裡已經裝得夠多，不再急著要更多。","examples":[{"en":"She is content with her quiet life in the countryside.","zh":"她對自己在鄉下的寧靜生活感到滿足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was content to wait until the next morning.","zh":"他願意安心等到第二天早上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/content","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c97c1db5f6a1f583","term":"content","forms":["content"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滿足；滿意","explanation":"指一種已經得到滿足、心情安定的狀態，和形容詞“感到滿足”是同一條意義主線的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"After the meal, a warm sense of content filled the room.","zh":"飯後，一種溫暖的滿足感充滿了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He found content in a quiet life by the sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/content","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb74550a330cd755","term":"content","forms":["content","contents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文章、演講等的內容","explanation":"指文字、講話、書籍、電影或影片所傳達的主題和資訊，也就是作品“裡面裝著”的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The article is easy to read, but its content is surprisingly deep.","zh":"這篇文章很容易讀，但內容出人意料地深刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher asked us to discuss the content of the documentary.","zh":"老師讓我們討論這部紀錄片的內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/content","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5400030e472542c7249d","word":"content(ment)","forms":["content","contentment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f242ff455d1deb84","term":"content","forms":["content"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滿足；滿意","explanation":"指一種已經得到滿足、心情安定的狀態，和形容詞“感到滿足”是同一條意義主線的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"After the meal, a warm sense of content filled the room.","zh":"飯後，一種溫暖的滿足感充滿了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sighed with content beside the warm fire.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/content","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86d40512cd71578a","term":"content","forms":["content","contents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文章、演講等的內容","explanation":"指文字、講話、書籍、電影或影片所傳達的主題和資訊，也就是作品“裡面裝著”的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The article is easy to read, but its content is surprisingly deep.","zh":"這篇文章很容易讀，但內容出人意料地深刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher asked us to discuss the content of the documentary.","zh":"老師讓我們討論這部紀錄片的內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/content","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3876481a23debc1","term":"content","forms":["content","contents","contenting","contented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使滿足；滿足於","explanation":"表示給某人足夠的東西使其滿意，或讓自己接受現有條件、不再要求更多。它把“容器裝滿”的畫面從狀態變成動作：把心裡的空缺填到夠用為止。","examples":[{"en":"For now, she contented herself with a simple meal and a good book.","zh":"目前，她滿足於一頓簡單的飯和一本好書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small gift contented the child for the rest of the afternoon.","zh":"這件小禮物讓孩子在下午剩下的時間裡感到滿足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/content","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cee18a6f87159b44","term":"contentment","forms":["contentment","contentments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滿足狀態","explanation":"指感到滿足或心滿意足的狀態，重點是這種滿足感本身，而不是某個具體結果。它可以來自生活條件、關係或眼前的處境。","examples":[{"en":"She felt a deep sense of contentment after a quiet evening at home.","zh":"在家安靜地度過一個晚上後，她感到深深的滿足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He found contentment in a simple life close to nature.","zh":"他在親近自然的簡單生活中找到了滿足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contentment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ca6bfc06abf7ae7","term":"contentment","forms":["contentment","contentments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對處境感到知足","explanation":"強調一個人對自己的生活處境感到滿意和知足，不一定擁有很多東西，但覺得現狀已經足夠好。這是日常理解中最重要的用法。","examples":[{"en":"For many people, contentment comes from spending time with family.","zh":"對許多人來說，滿足感來自與家人共度時光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found contentment in a quieter life by the sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contentment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6015011e7423f36d4f9e","word":"contention","forms":["contention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff9213846a3c9b54","term":"contention","forms":["contention","contentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭執；衝突；競爭","explanation":"指雙方或多方彼此對抗、爭奪或發生激烈爭執的狀態，重點是“互相拉扯”，不一定只靠語言進行。","examples":[{"en":"The dispute led to fierce contention between the two groups.","zh":"這場爭議導致兩個團體之間發生了激烈衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After weeks of contention over the plan, the committee postponed the vote.","zh":"圍繞這項計劃爭執了幾周後，委員會推遲了表決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da1301a99c77d294","term":"contention","forms":["contention","contentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"論點；主張","explanation":"指一個人在爭論中堅持的具體觀點，或用來支援該觀點的一整套論證；它是“拉扯的一端”，也就是一方明確站住的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Her central contention is that public transport should be free.","zh":"她的核心主張是公共交通應當免費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her contention is that the survey excluded younger residents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c59d0c160a320ec0179","word":"contest","forms":["contest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ed257af6b3af999","term":"contest","forms":["contest","contests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽；競賽","explanation":"指按照一定規則爭奪勝負的正式活動，例如拼寫、歌唱或體育比賽；這是日常最容易遇到的名詞義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"The child entered the spelling contest.","zh":"那個孩子參加了拼寫比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She won a cooking contest at the community fair.","zh":"她在社群集市的烹飪比賽中獲勝了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-455405655bbc651e","term":"contest","forms":["contest","contests","contesting","contested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"質疑；反對","explanation":"指站出來否認、反對或質疑某項決定、說法或結果，像是在一場爭論中向對方發起挑戰。","examples":[{"en":"The opposition party contested the election results.","zh":"反對黨對選舉結果提出了異議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lawyer contested the accuracy of the report.","zh":"律師質疑了這份報告的準確性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df9f5b30be92fe4631b8","word":"contestant","forms":["contestant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f55f672191012575","term":"contestant","forms":["contestant","contestants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參賽者","explanation":"指參加比賽、競賽或遊戲的人，重點是這個人已經站到競爭場上，準備爭奪名次、獎品或勝利。","examples":[{"en":"The contestants waited nervously for the final question.","zh":"參賽者們緊張地等待最後一個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each contestant has two minutes to complete the task.","zh":"每位參賽者有兩分鐘完成這項任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contestant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a619ba5d4caa220","term":"contestant","forms":["contestant","contestants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律挑戰者","explanation":"指在法律程式中站出來反對某項決定、權利或法律主張，並請求法院處理的人；這裡的“競爭”變成了法律上的挑戰。","examples":[{"en":"The contestant challenged the decision in court.","zh":"這名異議提出者在法庭上挑戰了這項決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The will's contestant argued that the signature was forged.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contestant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea7792a26f405e2ae9c6","word":"context","forms":["context"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b65c55adc9f14f9a","term":"context","forms":["context","contexts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"背景；處境","explanation":"指圍繞一件事的人際關係、歷史情況、環境等背景資訊。瞭解這些周邊情況，才能準確判斷事件的原因、意義或某人的行為。","examples":[{"en":"You need to understand the historical context before judging her decision.","zh":"在評價她的決定之前，你需要了解歷史背景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His remark sounds rude when taken out of context.","zh":"他的話脫離上下文來看聽起來很無禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/context","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-878d11eb011a5b03","term":"context","forms":["context","contexts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上下文","explanation":"指一個詞、短語或句子前後的文字。透過這些文字，可以判斷某個詞在當前段落中究竟是哪一種意思。","examples":[{"en":"Read the sentence in context to see what the word means.","zh":"把這個句子放在上下文中讀，才能看出這個詞是什麼意思。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Read the whole paragraph to understand the word's context.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/context","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbb2210166f26142af32","word":"continent","forms":["continent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4fcf4d1e225eb86","term":"continent","forms":["continent","continents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大陸","explanation":"指地球表面由海洋或地質特徵分隔開的主要連續陸地。核心畫面是許多陸地連成一整片。","examples":[{"en":"Africa is the second-largest continent in the world.","zh":"非洲是世界第二大洲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The species evolved on a separate continent.","zh":"這個物種是在一塊獨立的大陸上進化出來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e69cb522579fb6d","term":"continent","forms":["continent","continents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洲","explanation":"指傳統上把地球陸地劃分成的主要區域，如亞洲、歐洲、非洲、北美洲和南極洲等。它是對“大陸”這一大片連續陸地的常規地理分類。","examples":[{"en":"She has traveled on every continent except Antarctica.","zh":"除了南極洲，她去過每一個洲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Antarctica is the coldest continent on Earth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad21acb889da17fe038f","word":"continental","forms":["continental"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af1b1a00e48e305d","term":"continental","forms":["continental","more continental","most continental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大陸的","explanation":"表示與大陸或大陸地區有關，範圍可以是地理、地質等方面。它抓住的是“屬於大陸這一大片陸地”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are still studying continental drift.","zh":"科學家仍在研究大陸漂移。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The region has a dry continental climate.","zh":"這個地區屬於乾燥的大陸性氣候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dce84bfbebfb5fe3","term":"continental","forms":["continental","more continental","most continental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大陸本土的","explanation":"表示大陸本土一側的，與附近的島嶼相對。說 continental Europe 時，通常就是“歐洲大陸”，不把英國、愛爾蘭等島嶼算在內。","examples":[{"en":"The ferry connects the island with continental Europe.","zh":"這艘渡船連線該島和歐洲大陸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Goods are shipped from the island to the continental mainland.","zh":"貨物從島上運往大陸本土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6b2aa290a9e2ee4adecf","word":"continual","forms":["continual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9772953a1f8e0f9a","term":"continual","forms":["continual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"反覆不斷的","explanation":"指同類事情以穩定而快速的節奏一再發生，像珠子接連被放上一樣；重點是重複出現，不是整個過程毫無間斷。","examples":[{"en":"The continual noise made it hard for everyone to concentrate.","zh":"噪聲接連不斷，讓大家很難集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old building needs continual repairs.","zh":"這座老建築需要不斷維修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e256ee8e7aff6957a781","word":"continue","forms":["continue"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e26089d41cc3ab4c","term":"continue","forms":["continue","continues","continuing","continued","continuest","continuedst","continueth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續進行","explanation":"表示沿著原來的活動或程序接著做，沒有把它中斷；這就是讓事情沿著那條連續的線繼續向前。","examples":[{"en":"She continued working after everyone else had gone home.","zh":"其他人都回家後，她還繼續工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please continue reading the next paragraph.","zh":"請繼續讀下一段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19766da7b6bcbb3d","term":"continue","forms":["continue","continues","continuing","continued","continuest","continuedst","continueth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"恢復；接著進行","explanation":"表示活動暫停後重新接上原來的程序，也就是把中斷的線接回來，而不是從頭開始。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting will continue after lunch.","zh":"會議將在午餐後繼續進行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film continued from the moment the power came back.","zh":"停電恢復後，電影從中斷的地方繼續播放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0adc36057cef79f8a7b8","word":"continuity","forms":["continuity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-253e7725d49f9c59","term":"continuity","forms":["continuity","continuities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不中斷；連續性","explanation":"指事物在時間、空間或連線關係上沒有斷開，前後保持相連。例如電路正常閉合卻出現斷點，就可以說缺少 continuity。","examples":[{"en":"The new cable restored continuity in the circuit.","zh":"新電纜恢復了電路的連續性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lack of continuity in the power supply caused the computer to shut down.","zh":"電源供應不連續，導致電腦關機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continuity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9302bce091d15027","term":"continuity","forms":["continuity","continuities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"函式的連續性","explanation":"在數學中，continuity 指函式在某一點附近平滑銜接：當自變數逐漸接近該點時，函式值也接近該點應有的函式值，不會突然跳斷。","examples":[{"en":"The graph has continuity at every point in this interval.","zh":"這條曲線在這個區間的每一點都連續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proof establishes continuity at every interior point.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continuity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7496f1fc9731f2ed7dd","word":"continuous","forms":["continuous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3387bcb6abd69b46","term":"continuous","forms":["continuous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"連續不斷的","explanation":"指某個過程從開始到結束一直進行，中間沒有停止、暫停或其他中斷。它強調時間上的連線，就像一條沒有斷開的線。","examples":[{"en":"The machine has been running continuously for twelve hours.","zh":"這臺機器已經連續運轉了十二個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Continuous rain caused the river to rise.","zh":"持續不斷的降雨使河水上漲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continuous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e114341ad152d80d","term":"continuous","forms":["continuous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沒有空隙的","explanation":"指事物在空間上首尾相接，中間沒有空白或間隔；也可以指一系列部分連在一起，沒有被隔開。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a continuous line from the top of the page to the bottom.","zh":"從頁面頂部到底部畫一條不間斷的線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A continuous line of hedges enclosed the garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/continuous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc8321d6375c494d043f","word":"contract","forms":["contract"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49215361172e4061","term":"contract","forms":["contract","contracts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合同；協議","explanation":"雙方或多方把工作、責任和承諾正式拉到一起形成的協議，常常有固定期限並寫成檔案。","examples":[{"en":"The company signed a two-year contract with the university.","zh":"這家公司與那所大學簽訂了為期兩年的合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the contract carefully before you sign it.","zh":"簽字前請仔細閱讀這份合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1811311d86ed3e8","term":"contract","forms":["contract","contracts","contracting","contracted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收縮；縮小","explanation":"把身體、肌肉、範圍或距離向一起拉，使它變短、變窄或變小。","examples":[{"en":"The metal contracts as it cools.","zh":"金屬冷卻時會收縮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The snake contracted its body before striking.","zh":"那條蛇在攻擊前收縮了身體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cf512ada1a6b4cb","term":"contract","forms":["contract","contracts","contracting","contracted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"簽訂協議","explanation":"透過雙方同意，把承諾和責任拉到一起，達成合同或協議。","examples":[{"en":"The city contracted with a local firm to repair the bridge.","zh":"市政府與一家當地公司簽約維修這座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They contracted to supply the school with fresh vegetables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c7e34291dba41872286","word":"contractor","forms":["contractor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d221832076860d2","term":"contractor","forms":["contractor","contractors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築承包商","explanation":"指按合同負責建造或改造房屋、辦公樓等建築物的個人或公司，重點是“把整個建築專案承接下來”。","examples":[{"en":"We hired a contractor to renovate our kitchen.","zh":"我們請了承包商翻修廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contractor says the new office will be ready in June.","zh":"承包商說新辦公室六月就能完工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contractor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85b86fb56b377472","term":"contractor","forms":["contractor","contractors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專業工程承包商","explanation":"指在建築專案中承接某一類具體工作的個人或公司，例如電氣、管道或暖通工程承包商；這裡強調“包下某個專門環節”。","examples":[{"en":"The plumbing contractor replaced all the old pipes.","zh":"管道承包商更換了所有舊管道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hired an electrical contractor to rewire the aging warehouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contractor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b49415474163a330ca4","word":"contradict","forms":["contradict"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-831efeef5a153fe8","term":"contradict","forms":["contradict","contradicts","contradicting","contradicted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反駁；否認……屬實","explanation":"指明確否認某個陳述的真實性或有效性，也就是把對方的話頂回去，表示那句話不成立。","examples":[{"en":"The new evidence contradicts his account of what happened.","zh":"新證據與他對事情經過的說法相矛盾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She contradicted the report during the meeting.","zh":"她在會議上反駁了那份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contradict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7b100e726478ffb","term":"contradict","forms":["contradict","contradicts","contradicting","contradicted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反駁某人","explanation":"指透過否認對方所說的話來反駁這個人；重點在於當面頂回對方的說法，而不只是內心不同意。","examples":[{"en":"He contradicted me in front of everyone.","zh":"他當著所有人的面反駁了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nobody dared contradict the furious director.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contradict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-456cf73c569be56c8591","word":"contradiction","forms":["contradiction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3f5848040728ff8","term":"contradiction","forms":["contradiction","contradictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自相矛盾的說法","explanation":"指同一個說法內部同時肯定和否定同一件事，因而不能在同樣條件下都成立；它像一句話自己撞上自己。","examples":[{"en":"The statement contains a contradiction: it says the rule applies to everyone but also says that no one has to follow it.","zh":"這段話自相矛盾：它說這條規則適用於所有人，卻又說沒有人必須遵守。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a contradiction in his claim that the machine is both essential and unnecessary.","zh":"他說這臺機器既不可或缺又沒有必要，這個說法自相矛盾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contradiction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcf0c88749bca171","term":"contradiction","forms":["contradiction","contradictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀點或事物之間的矛盾","explanation":"指兩個或多個觀點、事實或事物彼此衝突，不能順利放在一起理解；矛盾不一定存在於單獨的一句話內部。","examples":[{"en":"The report reveals a contradiction between the company's promises and its actions.","zh":"這份報告揭示了公司承諾與行動之間的矛盾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His cheerful manner seemed a contradiction of his gloomy words.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contradiction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-112d857213723ac1e1a9","word":"contrary","forms":["contrary"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b1da324376d78ba","term":"contrary","forms":["contrary","more contrary","most contrary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相反的；逆向的","explanation":"表示方向、立場或作用與另一方相反，像本來向前卻迎面而來的風一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The boat struggled against contrary winds.","zh":"船在逆風中艱難前行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Contrary to our expectations, the meeting ended early.","zh":"與我們的預期相反，會議提前結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contrary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12ed30237d74e508","term":"contrary","forms":["contrary","more contrary","most contrary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相沖突的；不一致的","explanation":"表示兩種說法、證據或觀點彼此矛盾，不能自然地同時成立。","examples":[{"en":"The new evidence is contrary to the original report.","zh":"新的證據與最初的報告相矛盾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Contrary winds forced the sailing crew to change course.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contrary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3426125bf109d4bb9ab5","word":"contrast","forms":["contrast"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7df1308664fb0f59","term":"contrast","forms":["contrast","contrasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顏色反差","explanation":"指兩種顏色在明暗、亮度或色調上的差別；差別越明顯，就越容易把它們區分開。","examples":[{"en":"The black text has good contrast against the white background.","zh":"黑色文字與白色背景之間的反差很明顯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There isn't enough contrast between these two shades.","zh":"這兩種色調之間的反差不夠明顯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contrast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-388ef64ccffeaafc","term":"contrast","forms":["contrast","contrasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物之間的差異","explanation":"指兩個或多個物件、人物或觀念在特徵上的明顯不同；這些不同放在一起看，就形成鮮明對照。","examples":[{"en":"The quiet village is a sharp contrast to the busy city.","zh":"安靜的村莊與繁忙的城市形成鮮明對比。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contrast between the twins' personalities amused their teachers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contrast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44874655173f9a51","term":"contrast","forms":["contrast","contrasts","contrasting","contrasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對比兩個物件","explanation":"指主動把兩個物件並列或比較，以顯示它們之間的不同；核心仍是讓差異變得清楚。","examples":[{"en":"The article contrasts life in the city with life in the countryside.","zh":"這篇文章把城市生活和鄉村生活作了對比。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer contrasted warm colours with cool ones.","zh":"設計師把暖色和冷色作了對比。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contrast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8aa73cb60552b99f7d6b","word":"contribute","forms":["contribute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ebb408818889021","term":"contribute","forms":["contribute","contributes","contributing","contributed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為整體貢獻一部分","explanation":"把錢、時間、想法、勞動等一部分投入更大的專案、團體或共同目標中，使它成為整體的一部分，或幫助整體取得結果。","examples":[{"en":"Many residents contributed money to the neighborhood library.","zh":"許多居民為社群圖書館捐了錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her careful research contributed to the team's success.","zh":"她細緻的研究促成了團隊的成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contribute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7b4dc56dac9faf3fec9","word":"contribution","forms":["contribution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa27a4aa1a1001c2","term":"contribution","forms":["contribution","contributions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對整體的投入或貢獻","explanation":"指某人提供的想法、努力、時間、物品等，它們加入一個更大的計劃、活動或成果，並使整體有所增加或改善。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone made a contribution to the team project.","zh":"每個人都為團隊專案作出了貢獻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her ideas were an important contribution to the discussion.","zh":"她的想法是對這次討論的重要貢獻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contribution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2eedc8060a3d1c62","term":"contribution","forms":["contribution","contributions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捐款或支付的一筆錢","explanation":"指為了幫助某人、某項活動或某個目標而提供的一筆錢，是“投入資源”這個核心概念中最具體、最常見的一種。","examples":[{"en":"She made a small contribution to the local food bank.","zh":"她向當地食物銀行捐了一小筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their contribution paid for three new library computers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contribution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fcd568a5cb9bdb4677b","word":"control","forms":["control"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebcf7b6b0359c777","term":"control","forms":["control","controls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"控制權；支配","explanation":"指對某人、某事或某種局面擁有影響、決定或管理的權力；也可指這種支配狀態本身。這是“把事情握在手裡”的最基本含義。","examples":[{"en":"The government has complete control over the situation.","zh":"政府完全控制了局勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wants more control over her own schedule.","zh":"她希望更能掌控自己的日程安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/control","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e16561ca79e468f","term":"control","forms":["control","controls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"操縱裝置；控制部件","explanation":"指用來讓機器或系統按要求執行的方式、裝置或操作部件，例如按鈕、手柄或操縱桿。它仍然是“把機器的動作握在手裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The remote control has a button for each function.","zh":"這個遙控器的每項功能都有一個按鈕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pilot checked the controls before starting the engine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/control","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51f8bad83bc9d753","term":"control","forms":["control","controls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自制；約束能力","explanation":"指約束自己的動作、身體或情緒的能力；沒有 control 就是無法按住自己的反應。這既可以說一個人的自制力，也可以說身體動作不受控制。","examples":[{"en":"He lost control of his temper during the argument.","zh":"爭論時他沒能控制住自己的脾氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had no control over her legs after the accident.","zh":"事故後她無法控制自己的雙腿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/control","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c762e690a59efcc","term":"control","forms":["control","controls","controlling","controlled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"控制；操縱","explanation":"指影響、支配或操縱某人、機器或局面，使其行為按照自己的要求進行。這是動詞最常見的“把事情握在手裡”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"With a simple remote, he could control the toy truck.","zh":"他用一個簡單的遙控器就能操縱那輛玩具卡車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one can control everything that happens.","zh":"沒有人能控制所有發生的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/control","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaca40961d759a4d","term":"control","forms":["control","controls","controlling","controlled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抑制；剋制","explanation":"指把動作、衝動或情緒按住，使它不再失控。它與名詞的自我控制相對應，重點是限制反應而不是操縱外部裝置。","examples":[{"en":"She took a deep breath to control her anger.","zh":"她深吸了一口氣來控制自己的怒火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He could not control his hands because they were shaking.","zh":"他的手一直髮抖，無法控制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/control","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1472135b14c77c8bef9","word":"controller","forms":["controller"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e81ab9799bebed03","term":"controller","forms":["controller","controllers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"控制者","explanation":"controller 的基本形象是“掌控方向的人”：它指控制某人、某事或某個過程的人。這個義項也構成了其他義項的核心，即某種東西負責讓系統按特定方式執行。","examples":[{"en":"She became the controller of the entire operation.","zh":"她成了整個行動的掌控者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The controller of the machine stopped it immediately.","zh":"這臺機器的控制者立即把它停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/controller","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02f50f5f1c93bcf8","term":"controller","forms":["controller","controllers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電路或系統控制器","explanation":"在電氣、電子或機械系統中，controller 是調節電流、動力或執行狀態的裝置。它把“控制者”這個核心形象從人變成了裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The temperature controller keeps the room at a steady level.","zh":"溫度控制器讓房間保持穩定的溫度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A faulty controller prevented the motor from starting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/controller","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-188aa6ae3ca8746e36e1","word":"controversial","forms":["controversial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1d7da6170af8e58","term":"controversial","forms":["controversial","more controversial","most controversial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有爭議的；引發爭論的","explanation":"形容某個觀點、決定、人物或作品容易引起強烈分歧和討論。它只強調存在爭議，不直接判斷物件是對是錯。","examples":[{"en":"The committee made a controversial decision.","zh":"委員會作出了一個有爭議的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her controversial book sparked a heated debate.","zh":"她那本有爭議的書引發了激烈的辯論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/controversial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8856504c33a8cafac148","word":"controversy","forms":["controversy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71ffbb45c290636c","term":"controversy","forms":["controversy","controversies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭議；論戰；紛爭","explanation":"指人們圍繞某個問題持有相反意見，並因此展開爭論或發生衝突。它既可以強調意見對立的過程，也可以指已經引起廣泛關注的爭議事件。","examples":[{"en":"The new law has sparked controversy among parents and teachers.","zh":"這項新法律在家長和教師之間引發了爭議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The decision remains a source of controversy.","zh":"這項決定仍然是爭議的來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/controversy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b12837c5c23ec8e5bf1","word":"convene","forms":["convene"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1fcba859f6b145c1","term":"convene","forms":["convene","convenes","convening","convened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"集合開會","explanation":"指一個團體、委員會或其他組織成員聚在一起，通常是為了正式討論公共事務或作出決定。","examples":[{"en":"The committee will convene next Monday to review the proposal.","zh":"委員會將於下週一開會審議這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parliament convened after the election.","zh":"選舉結束後，議會召開了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03262db3dfc5eee0","term":"convene","forms":["convene","convenes","convening","convened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"召集開會","explanation":"指某人或某機構把一群人召集到一起開會、討論或處理事務，重點是“發出召集並促成集合”。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor convened an emergency meeting of city officials.","zh":"市長召集了一次市政府官員緊急會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The principal convened a meeting of department heads.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7ae368c14991b808b08","word":"convenience","forms":["convenience"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4aea8a1018715baa","term":"convenience","forms":["convenience","conveniences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方便；便利","explanation":"指某種安排或條件讓人少花時間、少費力，因此做事更方便。它常說的是一種整體的便利，而不一定是某一件具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"Many people choose online shopping for convenience.","zh":"許多人為了方便而選擇網上購物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel was chosen for its location and convenience.","zh":"選擇這家酒店是因為它的位置和便利性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convenience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3320956b836c53b726d1","word":"convenient","forms":["convenient"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-729ec9e93d80cdd6","term":"convenient","forms":["convenient","more convenient","most convenient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"方便的；省事的","explanation":"指某種時間、地點、方式或安排能減少麻煩，讓人容易完成事情。它的核心畫面是把需要的東西放在手邊，因此行動不費勁。","examples":[{"en":"It's convenient to shop online when I work late.","zh":"我加班到很晚時，網上購物很方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The station is convenient for people who live nearby.","zh":"這個車站對住在附近的人很方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convenient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65e40b52bb0fa7a2","term":"convenient","forms":["convenient","more convenient","most convenient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巧得可疑的","explanation":"指事情恰好符合某人的需要或說法，巧得讓人懷疑這只是藉口或有意安排。它仍然來自“方便”這個核心，只是方便得過了頭。","examples":[{"en":"How convenient that your phone died just before I asked about the message.","zh":"我剛要問那條訊息，你的手機就沒電了，真是太巧了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His sudden illness was rather convenient, considering the unpaid bill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convenient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37806e80c15b91408f5e","word":"convention","forms":["convention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56dcaf753bdad152","term":"convention","forms":["convention","conventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大會；大型會議","explanation":"指許多人，尤其是來自同一行業、組織或興趣群體的人聚在一起舉行的正式會議或大型集會。這是日常新聞和活動語境中最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of fans attended the annual science-fiction convention.","zh":"數千名愛好者參加了年度科幻大會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The convention was held in Geneva.","zh":"這次大會在日內瓦舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-232d2c7775053a5b","term":"convention","forms":["convention","conventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式協議；約定","explanation":"指經過正式協商而形成的協議、契約或共同遵守的規則。它仍然保留“聚在一起達成一致”的核心畫面，因此常用於國家、組織或群體之間的正式安排。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries signed a convention on cultural cooperation.","zh":"兩國簽署了一項文化合作公約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement follows an international convention on workers' rights.","zh":"這項協議遵循一項關於工人權利的國際公約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3eecf34c9e6463f0","term":"convention","forms":["convention","conventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慣例；約定俗成的做法","explanation":"指一個群體普遍接受並遵守的做法或規則，未必寫成正式法律。它可以看作“大家聚在一起形成共識”之後，逐漸固定下來的行為方式。","examples":[{"en":"By convention, the youngest member speaks first.","zh":"按照慣例，最年輕的成員先發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By convention, north appears at the top of maps.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2676e6e68a8ebfb925a7","word":"conventional","forms":["conventional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-061dda9c42bc3887","term":"conventional","forms":["conventional","more conventional","most conventional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傳統的；按慣例的","explanation":"指遵循社會、行業或某種體系中普遍接受的原則、方法和行為方式，而不是特別新穎或另類的做法。","examples":[{"en":"The company chose a conventional approach to solve the problem.","zh":"這家公司選擇了傳統的辦法來解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Conventional schools still play an important role in education.","zh":"傳統學校在教育中仍然發揮著重要作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conventional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-567f3e213349d599","term":"conventional","forms":["conventional","more conventional","most conventional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"普通的；尋常的","explanation":"強調某人或某物沒有特別之處，符合大多數人的日常習慣和標準。","examples":[{"en":"He leads a conventional life in a quiet town.","zh":"他在一個安靜的小鎮過著普通的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Conventional wisdom favors buying rather than renting here.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conventional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b34dbc2c05eb4d7e25d","word":"conversation","forms":["conversation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17e410c7399ba3aa","term":"conversation","forms":["conversation","conversations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"談話；交談","explanation":"指人們透過說話來交換想法、資訊或感受，也可以指這樣的一次具體談話。這是conversation在現代英語中最常見、最應優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We had a long conversation about our plans for next year.","zh":"我們就明年的計劃進行了長時間的交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conversation became more relaxed after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，談話變得更加輕鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conversation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a930006ef296ea04b81","word":"converse","forms":["converse"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b9477cd269ec6df","term":"converse","forms":["converse","converses","conversing","conversed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交談","explanation":"指與別人說話、交換想法，核心畫面是雙方面對面交流。","examples":[{"en":"The two scientists conversed about the new discovery.","zh":"兩位科學家就這項新發現進行了交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We conversed for hours beneath the hotel awning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/converse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b236a746870a6b86461","word":"conversion","forms":["conversion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31c1e64543fb44e8","term":"conversion","forms":["conversion","conversions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轉變；改信","explanation":"指把人或事物從一種狀態轉成另一種狀態，尤其常用於人的信仰、立場或身份發生轉變。重點不是短暫改變，而是進入了新的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Her conversion to Buddhism surprised her family.","zh":"她改信佛教讓家人感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conversion from paper records to digital files took several months.","zh":"從紙質記錄轉換為電子檔案花了幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conversion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be7f089d3f8e734f","term":"conversion","forms":["conversion","conversions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軟體移植；平臺轉換版","explanation":"指把軟體或電子遊戲改寫、調整到另一種平臺，使它能在新的系統或裝置上執行；也可指這樣得到的產品。","examples":[{"en":"The new conversion of the game runs well on modern consoles.","zh":"這款遊戲的新移植版在現代遊戲機上執行得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The studio released a conversion for mobile devices.","zh":"這家工作室推出了適用於移動裝置的移植版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conversion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c47579671ec3e9f349f9","word":"convert","forms":["convert"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33d269235ee31890","term":"convert","forms":["convert","converts","converting","converted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉變成","explanation":"把某物變成另一種形式、物質、狀態或產品，核心是完成一次從 A 到 B 的轉變。","examples":[{"en":"The machine converts sunlight into electricity.","zh":"這臺機器把陽光轉化為電能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old warehouse was converted into apartments.","zh":"那座舊倉庫被改造成了公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee854add935bc3db","term":"convert","forms":["convert","converts","converting","converted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"換成等值物","explanation":"把一種等值的東西換成另一種，常用於貨幣、積分或其他具有對應價值的物件。","examples":[{"en":"We converted our dollars into euros at the airport.","zh":"我們在機場把美元換成了歐元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Convert the total from euros into dollars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0af415c6e250260","term":"convert","forms":["convert","converts","converting","converted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變成","explanation":"某物自身變成另一種形式或用途，突出結果自然或經過改造後發生了轉換。","examples":[{"en":"This sofa converts into a comfortable bed.","zh":"這張沙發可以變成一張舒適的床。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spare room converted easily into a small studio.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4728b0c37dc84206db31","word":"convey","forms":["convey"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90d7d027fa817033","term":"convey","forms":["convey","conveys","conveying","conveyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"運送；輸送","explanation":"表示把物品、聲音等從一個地方帶到另一個地方，重點是內容透過某種路徑或媒介被送過去。","examples":[{"en":"The pipes convey water from the reservoir to the fields.","zh":"這些管道把水從水庫輸送到田地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Air conveys sound through the room.","zh":"空氣把聲音傳遍房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1251a67536c7e44b","term":"convey","forms":["convey","conveys","conveying","conveyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳達；表達","explanation":"表示把資訊、意思、感情或印象“送”到聽者或讀者那裡，使對方理解或感受到某種內容。","examples":[{"en":"Her expression conveyed a sense of relief.","zh":"她的表情傳達出一種如釋重負的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diagram clearly conveys how the machine works.","zh":"這張圖清楚地說明了機器的工作原理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a15ed74fb2ce1451cad","word":"convict","forms":["convict"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a68a6f3abb8a9e37","term":"convict","forms":["convict","convicts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被判有罪的人","explanation":"指經法院或其他司法機構判定犯有罪行的人，也就是被法律蓋上“有罪”印章的人。它可以泛指這類人的身份，不專指某一種罪行。","examples":[{"en":"The convict was released after serving ten years in prison.","zh":"這名罪犯服刑十年後獲釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program helps former convicts find work.","zh":"這個專案幫助刑滿釋放人員找工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25bb070faded05cc","term":"convict","forms":["convict","convicts","convicting","convicted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"判定有罪","explanation":"指經過審判等法律程式，正式認定某人犯了罪。核心畫面仍是法庭給某人蓋下“有罪”印章，通常比單純懷疑或指控更進一步。","examples":[{"en":"The jury convicted him of fraud.","zh":"陪審團判定他犯有欺詐罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was convicted of stealing from her employer.","zh":"她因偷竊僱主財物被判有罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80ee6e99b2e164533f52","word":"conviction","forms":["conviction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25f0f2ae505b95a5","term":"conviction","forms":["conviction","convictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅定的信念","explanation":"指一個人經過思考後牢牢記住、並且不容易動搖的看法或信念。它比一般的想法更有把握，也更能影響人的判斷和行動。","examples":[{"en":"She has a strong conviction that everyone deserves a second chance.","zh":"她堅定地認為每個人都應該有重新開始的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His convictions guided him through the difficult decision.","zh":"他的堅定信念指引著他作出了這個艱難的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conviction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-201100856244c079","term":"conviction","forms":["conviction","convictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有罪判決","explanation":"指法院對某人作出的“有罪”判決，或這樣一項判決本身。它關注的是具體的一次法律裁決，因此常可以數出有幾項判決。","examples":[{"en":"The court overturned his conviction after new evidence was found.","zh":"發現新證據後，法院推翻了對他的有罪判決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has no previous convictions.","zh":"她沒有此前的犯罪定罪記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conviction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61b0a3c4d28279aa8d7a","word":"convince","forms":["convince"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-867fe6f51997098f","term":"convince","forms":["convince","convinces","convincing","convinced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使相信；使確信","explanation":"用事實、邏輯或證據把對方從懷疑帶到確信，重點是改變對方對某件事的看法。","examples":[{"en":"The evidence convinced me that she was telling the truth.","zh":"這些證據使我相信她說的是實話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m not convinced that this plan will work.","zh":"我還不能確信這個計劃會成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convince","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a951806c34a85bc0","term":"convince","forms":["convince","convinces","convincing","convinced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說服","explanation":"讓某人接受你的建議並願意採取行動；它和“使相信”相連，但結果更偏向行動上的同意。","examples":[{"en":"She convinced me to try the new restaurant.","zh":"她說服我去試試那家新餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They convinced the owner to extend the deadline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/convince","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03fb94180aa0ff2c583d","word":"cook","forms":["cook"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f06b66ced2a354d7","term":"cook","forms":["cook","cooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廚師；做飯的人","explanation":"cook是準備食物的人，可以是職業廚師，也可以只是負責做飯的人。重點是“人”，不是烹調這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"I'm a terrible cook, so I eat a lot of frozen dinners.","zh":"我做飯很差，所以經常吃冷凍餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cook prepared soup for forty hungry guests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bca0ddc747f87649","term":"cook","forms":["cook","cooks","cooking","cooked","cooken","cookest","cookedst","cooketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"烹調","explanation":"cook表示透過加熱準備食物，常包括把不同食材組合起來，使其適合食用。這是動詞最基本、最常用的義項。","examples":[{"en":"I'm cooking dinner for the whole family tonight.","zh":"今晚我為全家做晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cooked the vegetables with garlic and oil.","zh":"她用大蒜和油炒了蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-135237345460e00f","term":"cook","forms":["cook","cooks","cooking","cooked","cooken","cookest","cookedst","cooketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續推進計劃","explanation":"現代俚語中，cook表示讓某人繼續把想法、計劃或行動做下去，哪怕結果可能很好笑、成功或越來越糟。它把“在火上繼續加工”變成“讓事情繼續發展”。","examples":[{"en":"The idea sounds strange, but let her cook.","zh":"這個主意聽起來很奇怪，但讓她繼續做下去吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Give him a few more minutes—he's cooking.","zh":"再給他幾分鐘——他正在把這件事做起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0eed4ace4f636b30def4","word":"cooker","forms":["cooker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff90cc9f9ad839ed","term":"cooker","forms":["cooker","cookers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爐灶","explanation":"在英國和愛爾蘭英語中，cooker 可以指用來加熱和烹調食物的廚房爐灶，通常包括爐面，有時也包括烤箱部分。","examples":[{"en":"The soup is simmering on the cooker.","zh":"湯正在爐灶上慢慢燉著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please turn off the cooker before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請把爐灶關掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47df477a4339c4d0","term":"cooker","forms":["cooker","cookers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烹飪器具","explanation":"在英國和愛爾蘭英語中，cooker 也可以泛指用來烹飪食物的裝置或器具；具體是哪一種，要由上下文決定。","examples":[{"en":"We need a small cooker for the camping trip.","zh":"我們需要一臺小型烹飪器具帶去露營。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The electric cooker has four rings and an oven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7e83e28a04b537e6442","word":"cookie","forms":["cookie"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75dd56940fd821cb","term":"cookie","forms":["cookie","cookies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餅乾","explanation":"指一塊小而扁的烘焙食品，可以是酥脆的，也可以是柔軟但成形的；巧克力豆、果乾或堅果都可能烤在裡面。","examples":[{"en":"She packed two cookies in her lunch.","zh":"她在午餐盒裡裝了兩塊餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These cookies are soft in the middle.","zh":"這些餅乾中間是軟的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cookie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-424109e8854bacac","term":"cookie","forms":["cookie","cookies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路識別資料","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指網站存放在瀏覽器中的一小段資料，用來記住使用者、登入狀態或網站偏好等資訊；它就像網路世界裡的“小餅乾”。","examples":[{"en":"This website uses cookies to remember your language preference.","zh":"這個網站使用網路資料來記住你的語言偏好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can clear your cookies in the browser settings.","zh":"你可以在瀏覽器設定中清除這些網路資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cookie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c34045c1a1db8d1b3fca","word":"cool","forms":["cool"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb9af256bd725baf","term":"cool","forms":["cool","cooler","coolest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"涼的；溫度適中偏低","explanation":"指溫度不高、讓人感到涼，但通常還沒有冷到不舒服。它是整個詞義網路的起點：熱度降下來，就有了 cool 的基本感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The evening air is cool, so bring a light jacket.","zh":"晚上的空氣很涼，帶一件薄外套吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sleep better in a cool room.","zh":"房間涼爽一些，我睡得更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93c85429a256eed9","term":"cool","forms":["cool","cooler","coolest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冷靜的；鎮定的","explanation":"指人在緊張或困難情況下不慌亂，能夠控制情緒和行動。就像身體的熱度降下來一樣，情緒也降下來，保持清醒和從容。","examples":[{"en":"Stay cool and tell us exactly what happened.","zh":"保持冷靜，把事情經過完整地告訴我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stayed cool when the computer suddenly stopped working.","zh":"電腦突然停止工作時，她仍然很鎮定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a03a8210ef016ef3","term":"cool","forms":["cool"],"pos":"noun","zh":"涼爽；涼意","explanation":"指介於炎熱和寒冷之間、讓人感到舒適的涼爽狀態。它仍然保留了“熱度降下來”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We went for a walk in the cool of the early morning.","zh":"我們在清晨的涼爽空氣中散了步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We rested in the cool of the stone cellar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48e71b7e659b8103","term":"cool","forms":["cool","cools","cooling","cooled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變涼；冷卻","explanation":"指物體自身失去熱量，溫度變低。這是動詞形式對基本“熱度降低”畫面的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Let the soup cool before you taste it.","zh":"先讓湯涼一涼再嘗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let the bread cool before slicing it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30a9caa9170d230fa6b5","word":"cooperate","forms":["cooperate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e18e6b163399f44f","term":"cooperate","forms":["cooperate","cooperates","cooperating","cooperated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"共同合作","explanation":"指兩個或多個個人、團體為了共同目標一起行動，重點是彼此配合，而不是一方單獨提供幫助。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams cooperated to finish the project on time.","zh":"兩個團隊相互合作，按時完成了專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two laboratories cooperated on the vaccine study.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooperate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43c4490616fee47e","term":"cooperate","forms":["cooperate","cooperates","cooperating","cooperated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"配合以使行動暢通","explanation":"強調各方的配合讓彼此能夠順利行動，重點在於減少阻礙、避免互相妨礙。","examples":[{"en":"The traffic lights cooperate to keep cars moving safely.","zh":"這些交通訊號燈相互配合，讓車輛安全通行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please cooperate by keeping the entrance clear.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooperate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8f405cbf1381a8cb07c","word":"cooperation","forms":["cooperation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8acaa3bdac6e8c96","term":"cooperation","forms":["cooperation","cooperations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合作；協作","explanation":"指人或團體為了共同目標而一起行動、互相配合的過程，重點在“共同做事”本身。","examples":[{"en":"International cooperation is essential for solving climate problems.","zh":"解決氣候問題離不開國際合作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project succeeded through close cooperation between the two teams.","zh":"這個專案在兩個團隊的密切合作下取得了成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooperation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbdcdc11efca89ee","term":"cooperation","forms":["cooperation","cooperations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"配合；幫助","explanation":"指某個人、組織等主動提供幫助，使事情能夠順利進行，常常帶有“請你配合”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"We appreciate your cooperation in keeping the entrance clear.","zh":"感謝您配合保持入口暢通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inquiry depends on the full cooperation of local witnesses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooperation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-975a0c6243cb25756fb2","word":"cooperative","forms":["cooperative"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb4ef73531655159","term":"cooperative","forms":["cooperative","more cooperative","most cooperative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"願意配合的","explanation":"形容人願意聽取意見、提供幫助或按要求一起做事；說某人不 cooperative，就是說對方不肯配合。這個意思把“共同出力”的畫面放在一個人的態度上。","examples":[{"en":"The new student was cooperative and helped us organize the materials.","zh":"那個新生很配合，還幫我們整理了材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness was cooperative during the interview.","zh":"證人在採訪過程中很配合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooperative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b50cc4a4cf67c02","term":"cooperative","forms":["cooperative","more cooperative","most cooperative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合作進行的","explanation":"形容一項活動、計劃或關係需要兩方或多方共同參與，而不是由一方單獨完成。這裡的“合作”從人的態度擴充套件到了事情本身。","examples":[{"en":"The two schools started a cooperative research project.","zh":"這兩所學校啟動了一個合作研究專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue required a cooperative effort across several agencies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooperative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85d9d29685d929bc","term":"cooperative","forms":["cooperative","cooperatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合作社；合作企業","explanation":"一種由成員共同擁有或控制的公司，成員可以是員工、顧客、住戶或生產者。大家共同投入、共同參與管理，正是“共同出力”這個核心畫面的組織化形式。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers formed a cooperative to sell their produce.","zh":"這些農民成立了一個合作社來銷售農產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dairy cooperative buys milk from neighboring farms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cooperative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-ac7f1c227985687b4b72","word":"coordinate","forms":["coordinate"],"officialPos":"v./n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43e7cb772b46e38f","term":"coordinate","forms":["coordinate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"同等的；並列的","explanation":"指兩個事物在等級、地位或作用上相同，誰也不從屬於誰；它們像被放在同一層秩序中。","examples":[{"en":"The two clauses are coordinate, not subordinate.","zh":"這兩個分句是並列的，不是從屬的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sentence contains two coordinate clauses joined by and.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coordinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d79193b943a69887","term":"coordinate","forms":["coordinate","coordinates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"座標；位置資料","explanation":"座標是用來確定點在一條線、弧線或其他位置系統中的資料；它把某個點放進一套有秩序的定位框架裡。","examples":[{"en":"Send me the coordinates of the campsite.","zh":"把營地的座標發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue crew radioed our precise coordinates to the helicopter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coordinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a02b8bd95d103656","term":"coordinate","forms":["coordinate","coordinates","coordinating","coordinated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"協調；使同步","explanation":"指安排不同的人、動作或活動，使它們按照相互配合的節奏進行；核心畫面就是把多個部分放進同一套行動秩序。","examples":[{"en":"We need to coordinate our schedules before the meeting.","zh":"我們需要在會議前協調好各自的日程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancers coordinated their movements with the drumbeat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coordinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99628a6e64c7224791bc","word":"cope","forms":["cope"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0aabcae37fd6ce63","term":"cope","forms":["cope","copes","coping","coped","copest","copedst","copeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"應對，撐過","explanation":"指面對困難、壓力或不利局面時設法維持下去並處理它，是現代英語最常用的義項。","examples":[{"en":"She is learning to cope with the pressure of her new job.","zh":"她正在學習應對新工作的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He coped well after the accident.","zh":"事故發生後，他應對得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d16f06fe255d801e0639","word":"copper","forms":["copper"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a78fb0abcdbd940","term":"copper","forms":["copper","more copper","most copper"],"pos":"adj","zh":"銅製的","explanation":"表示某物由銅製成，重點是材料，而不是顏色。","examples":[{"en":"The craftsman used a copper wire to repair the lamp.","zh":"工匠用銅線修理了這盞燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A copper kettle hung beside the fireplace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98898f80d251d546","term":"copper","forms":["copper","coppers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銅（金屬）","explanation":"指一種紅棕色、容易加工且導電導熱效能好的金屬，是這個詞最基本的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Copper is widely used in electrical wiring.","zh":"銅廣泛用於電線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The statue is made of copper and has turned green with age.","zh":"這座雕像是銅製的，年代久了已經變綠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26b0b256c87e1176","term":"copper","forms":["copper","coppers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銅紅色","explanation":"指類似銅的紅棕色，是從金屬外觀發展出的顏色義。","examples":[{"en":"The artist mixed orange and brown to get a warm copper.","zh":"畫家把橙色和棕色調在一起，調出了溫暖的銅紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The setting sun turned the water a deep copper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f5a6034e770acbfb3f7","word":"copy","forms":["copy"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01ac60f26f32130c","term":"copy","forms":["copy","copies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"副本；複製品","explanation":"指根據原件複製出的、與原件相同或幾乎相同的一份東西，可以是紙張、檔案、影象或其他物品。","examples":[{"en":"Could you send me a copy of the contract?","zh":"你能給我發一份合同副本嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I made two copies of the form before the meeting.","zh":"開會前我把這張表格影印了兩份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee0b1d441a90fcff","term":"copy","forms":["copy","copies","copying","copied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"複製；影印","explanation":"把一個物件再製作出相同或幾乎相同的一份，動作上對應名詞“副本”。物件可以是檔案、文字、圖片，也可以是紙質材料。","examples":[{"en":"Please copy these pages for everyone in the class.","zh":"請把這些頁面影印給班上的每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I copied the address into my phone.","zh":"我把地址複製到了手機裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9cf5a55f690ba3e","term":"copy","forms":["copy","copies","copying","copied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"複製；複製到另一處","explanation":"在電腦或其他技術操作中，把資料保留一份並放到記憶體、資料夾或另一處，以便之後使用；它仍然是“做出一個副本”。","examples":[{"en":"Copy the photos to a new folder before deleting anything.","zh":"刪除任何內容前，先把照片複製到一個新資料夾裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Copy the photographs onto an external drive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b73c3b708ac6036","term":"copy","forms":["copy","copies","copying","copied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"模仿；照著做","explanation":"不再是製作物品副本，而是照著另一個人的動作、說話方式或做法來做；這就是從“複製原樣”引申出的行為義。","examples":[{"en":"The little boy copied his sister's way of speaking.","zh":"小男孩模仿姐姐說話的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toddler copied her sister's funny dance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2fca2aa3a976ccd7b98","word":"copyright","forms":["copyright"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e00c9ad3e3dd8d98","term":"copyright","forms":["copyright","copyrights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"版權；著作權","explanation":"指法律賦予創作者或其他權利人的控制權，權利人可以決定誰能複製、出版、發行或傳播一部作品。它保護的物件可以是文字、音樂、影象等創作成果。","examples":[{"en":"This photograph is protected by copyright.","zh":"這張照片受版權保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Copyright gives the author control over how the book is published.","zh":"版權讓作者能夠決定這本書如何出版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copyright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7e20b070b14165c","term":"copyright","forms":["copyright","copyrights","copyrighting","copyrighted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取得版權；為作品登記版權","explanation":"指為文字、音樂或其他創作作品取得或登記版權，相當於給作品加上法律保護。這一義延續了“掌握複製鑰匙”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The publisher copyrighted the new textbook before releasing it.","zh":"出版商在發行這本新教材前為它登記了版權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She copyrighted the illustrations for her website.","zh":"她為自己網站上的插圖登記了版權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/copyright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f39fd9073457c8ee4582","word":"coral","forms":["coral"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc8a325362888bdc","term":"coral","forms":["coral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"珊瑚色的","explanation":"指顏色接近珊瑚，通常是帶有粉色或橙色的柔和色調。","examples":[{"en":"The room looked brighter after we painted one wall coral.","zh":"我們把一面牆刷成珊瑚色後，房間看起來更明亮了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a coral dress for the summer wedding.","zh":"她為夏日婚禮選了一條珊瑚色連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46419a753ca41ce3","term":"coral","forms":["coral","corals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珊瑚生物或珊瑚群體","explanation":"指生活在海中的珊瑚動物及其形成的群體；它們常分泌堅硬的碳酸鈣骨骼，逐漸形成珊瑚礁。這裡的 coral 可以指一個珊瑚個體，也可以泛指珊瑚群落。","examples":[{"en":"Bright fish moved between the corals in the shallow water.","zh":"鮮豔的魚在淺水中的珊瑚之間遊動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers found a healthy coral colony near the island.","zh":"研究人員在島附近發現了一個健康的珊瑚群落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cfbf792eb2ad26f","term":"coral","forms":["coral","corals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珊瑚骨骼；珊瑚材料","explanation":"指珊瑚生物留下的堅硬骨骼，也就是常被加工成裝飾品的珊瑚材料。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed jewelry made from red coral.","zh":"博物館展出了用紅珊瑚製成的首飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The antique necklace was carved from pink coral.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19dbaf77a5ecfc85a6af","word":"cord","forms":["cord"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff93f39af243bdbe","term":"cord","forms":["cord","cords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細繩；線繩","explanation":"指由纖維等絞成的細長、柔韌的繩線，可以用來捆紮或連線物品。這是 cord 最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"She tied the package with a strong cord.","zh":"她用一根結實的細繩把包裹捆好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cord was hanging from the old gate.","zh":"舊門上垂著一根繩線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1805715230468096","term":"cord","forms":["cord","cords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電源線","explanation":"指包有絕緣層、用來傳導電流的柔性電線，尤其是燈、吸塵器等家用電器連線插座的線。它仍然保留了“柔韌的線”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The lamp's cord is too short to reach the outlet.","zh":"這盞燈的電源線太短，夠不到插座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unplug the cord before cleaning the machine.","zh":"清潔機器前先拔掉電源線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d45f5fd462b8c70bffb","word":"core","forms":["core"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8c3c1f6f448cd06","term":"core","forms":["core","cores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"果核；內部的核心部分","explanation":"本義是蘋果等水果中間不能吃的硬核，後來也可泛指被其他部分包圍的內部關鍵部分。這個具體的“硬核”形象是理解其他詞義的入口。","examples":[{"en":"She cut the apple in half and removed the core.","zh":"她把蘋果切成兩半，去掉了果核。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At the core of the problem is a lack of trust.","zh":"這個問題的核心是缺乏信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/core","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-796ad2a3d23c0ab1","term":"core","forms":["core","cores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"核心；本質","explanation":"指一個事物、問題或群體中最重要、最能代表其本質的部分，不一定處在實際空間的正中央。","examples":[{"en":"The core of her argument is easy to understand.","zh":"她論點的核心很容易理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These three lessons form the core of the course.","zh":"這三課構成了這門課程的核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/core","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63b0490d4736e740f26e","word":"corn","forms":["corn"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b52fd9bb54bcdd2","term":"corn","forms":["corn","corns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穀物；主食作物","explanation":"在英國等語境中，corn 可泛指一個國家或地區主要種植、食用的穀物；具體是哪種穀物要看當地習慣。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers stored the corn in a dry barn.","zh":"農民把穀物儲存在乾燥的穀倉裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The region's main crop is corn.","zh":"這個地區的主要作物是穀物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-628cfc9bec14eb55","term":"corn","forms":["corn","corns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玉米","explanation":"在美國、加拿大、澳大利亞和紐西蘭英語中，corn 通常特指玉米這種穀物作物。","examples":[{"en":"We grilled corn on the cob for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐烤了玉米棒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Corn grows well in warm, sunny fields.","zh":"玉米在溫暖、陽光充足的田地裡長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45d227c4b297a0ba4ce4","word":"corner","forms":["corner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32bfce1b8aaa349d","term":"corner","forms":["corner","corners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"角；角落","explanation":"兩條線、兩面牆或兩個方向相交的地方，就是一個 corner；在房間等空間中，通常譯為“角落”。","examples":[{"en":"A small spider was hiding in the corner of the room.","zh":"一隻小蜘蛛藏在房間的角落裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The corners of the frame are reinforced with metal.","zh":"框架的四個角用金屬加固了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c87474186b384e9","term":"corner","forms":["corner","corners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊遠處；一角","explanation":"從具體的角引申為離中心較遠的部分、方向或區域，所以可以說某個地方的一角，也可以說心靈深處的某個角落。","examples":[{"en":"People came from every corner of the country.","zh":"人們來自這個國家的各個角落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found the letter in a dark corner of my memory.","zh":"我在記憶的一個黑暗角落裡找到了那封信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18242921abdbd0e4","term":"corner","forms":["corner","corners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隱蔽處；僻靜處","explanation":"指遠離人群、安靜或不容易被發現的地方，可以把它想成躲進空間邊角的地方。","examples":[{"en":"She found a quiet corner to read during lunch.","zh":"午餐時她找了個安靜的角落看書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog sleeps in a warm corner by the window.","zh":"那隻狗睡在窗邊一個溫暖的角落裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58183295053782726462","word":"corporate","forms":["corporate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-330629fbc3761667","term":"corporate","forms":["corporate","more corporate","most corporate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公司的；法人組織的","explanation":"表示與公司、法人團體或其經營活動有關，重點是“屬於公司這一組織或由公司負責”。","examples":[{"en":"The company is revising its corporate governance rules.","zh":"這家公司正在修改其公司治理規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She moved from a local office to the corporate headquarters.","zh":"她從地方辦事處調到了公司總部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corporate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-abb61f037a217332","term":"corporate","forms":["corporate","more corporate","most corporate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"組成法人；已註冊為公司","explanation":"表示某個組織已經被組成或登記為具有法人資格的公司，而不是僅僅由個人或非正式團體組成。","examples":[{"en":"The charity later became a corporate entity.","zh":"這個慈善機構後來成為了一個法人實體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The association acquired corporate status after registration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corporate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65a07093bf150e987976","word":"corporation","forms":["corporation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a31ce55b8b963cb9","term":"corporation","forms":["corporation","corporations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法人團體","explanation":"指依法成立、具有獨立法律身份的團體：它可以持續存在，不會因為成員更換而消失，並且擁有與成員分開的權利、責任和債務。這個詞的核心畫面就是“許多人組成一個獨立的身體”。","examples":[{"en":"The corporation is legally separate from its shareholders.","zh":"這個法人團體在法律上獨立於其股東。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The corporation is responsible for maintaining the public park.","zh":"這個法人團體負責維護那座公共公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corporation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a897ebf025528327","term":"corporation","forms":["corporation","corporations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"市政管理機構","explanation":"指負責管理自治市或城市的正式機構，可以代表當地政府處理公共事務。它仍然保留“代表一個共同體行動的獨立身體”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The corporation approved a new plan for public transport.","zh":"市政機構批准了新的公共交通計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city corporation approved new drainage works.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corporation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42c75396af1d6fe60613","word":"corpse","forms":["corpse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ee747b3b48d7e4a","term":"corpse","forms":["corpse","corpses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的屍體","explanation":"指已經死亡的人的身體，常用於犯罪、戰爭、災難或醫學調查等語境；這是 corpse 最核心的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The police found a corpse in the abandoned house.","zh":"警方在那所廢棄的房子裡發現了一具屍體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers buried the corpses after the battle.","zh":"戰鬥結束後，士兵們掩埋了屍體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corpse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-477f8d059dc13d4f","term":"corpse","forms":["corpse","corpses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物屍體","explanation":"也可指有肉的動物死後留下的屍體，意思接近“動物屍體”或“殘骸”；在這種用法中，重點仍是死亡後不再活動的身體。","examples":[{"en":"A fox dragged the corpse of a rabbit into the woods.","zh":"一隻狐狸把一隻兔子的屍體拖進了樹林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They found the fox's corpse beside the railway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corpse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15a596e3c98c407e0437","word":"correct","forms":["correct"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-07748e131c720931","term":"correct","forms":["correct","more correct","most correct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正確的；準確無誤的","explanation":"表示答案、判斷、資訊或做法沒有錯誤，符合事實或正確標準。","examples":[{"en":"Your answer is correct.","zh":"你的答案是正確的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check that all the information is correct.","zh":"請檢查所有資訊是否正確。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae0983a0ed95bc7b","term":"correct","forms":["correct","corrects","correcting","corrected","correctest","correctedst","correcteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"糾正；改正","explanation":"把原來錯誤的東西改成正確的狀態，就像把偏離標準的做法拉回正確的線。","examples":[{"en":"The coach corrected my posture.","zh":"教練糾正了我的姿勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please correct any mistakes before you submit the form.","zh":"提交表格前請改正所有錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-577bf0c4f4ee4f887ec9","word":"correlation","forms":["correlation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1d44b263224d0bb","term":"correlation","forms":["correlation","correlations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相互聯絡；對應關係","explanation":"指兩個或多個可以比較的事物之間存在相互對應、平行或互補的關係。它強調事物之間有聯絡，但不一定說明誰造成了誰。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers found a clear correlation between regular exercise and better sleep.","zh":"研究人員發現，定期鍛鍊與更好的睡眠之間有明顯的聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a strong correlation between the two changes.","zh":"這兩項變化之間有很強的對應關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correlation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a5336b612215426","term":"correlation","forms":["correlation","correlations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統計相關；相關係數","explanation":"在統計學中，correlation 指用資料描述兩個隨機變數如何一起變化的關係，通常包括關係的強弱和方向。正相關表示二者大致同向變化，負相關表示一方增加時另一方大致減少。","examples":[{"en":"The study found a strong negative correlation between stress levels and sleep quality.","zh":"這項研究發現，壓力水平與睡眠質量之間存在很強的負相關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A high correlation between the two measurements does not prove that one causes the other.","zh":"兩個測量值之間的高度相關並不能證明其中一個導致了另一個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correlation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c59e6d6725012feb6571","word":"correspond","forms":["correspond"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9abddb8aa8cd2b9f","term":"correspond","forms":["correspond","corresponds","corresponding","corresponded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對應；相符","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物在性質、數量、結構、來源或作用等方面彼此相符，好像能夠一一對上。它不一定表示完全相同，而是強調存在相應關係。","examples":[{"en":"The two maps correspond closely to each other.","zh":"這兩張地圖彼此高度對應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her account does not correspond to the facts.","zh":"她的敘述與事實不符。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correspond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f2f35bd92306340","term":"correspond","forms":["correspond","corresponds","corresponding","corresponded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"通訊；通訊往來","explanation":"指兩個人或兩方在一段時間內透過信件或其他書面訊息持續聯絡，重點不是單次回覆，而是來回交流。","examples":[{"en":"Maya has corresponded with her former teacher for years.","zh":"瑪雅多年來一直和她以前的老師通訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sisters corresponded regularly for nearly fifty years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correspond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14654bf2b7733e0f1c97","word":"correspondence","forms":["correspondence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-722f82b524cd5f6f","term":"correspondence","forms":["correspondence","correspondences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書信往來","explanation":"指雙方透過寫信、寄信來保持聯絡的過程或關係，重點是持續的通訊往來，而不是某一封具體的信。","examples":[{"en":"Their correspondence continued for many years.","zh":"他們的書信往來持續了許多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their lively correspondence reveals a friendship built on shared jokes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correspondence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ba5d44437937e27","term":"correspondence","forms":["correspondence","correspondences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相似；對應關係","explanation":"指不同的人、事物或特徵之間存在相似、吻合或相互對應的關係；這裡不再是寫信，而是兩邊在某些方面“對得上”。","examples":[{"en":"There is a clear correspondence between the two designs.","zh":"這兩種設計之間有明顯的相似之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Matching dates established a correspondence between the diary and the ship's log.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correspondence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-198bcf9a7fe59f1e1797","word":"correspondent","forms":["correspondent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b200f6f3d6e2196a","term":"correspondent","forms":["correspondent","correspondents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特派記者；駐外記者","explanation":"指從遠方、外地或海外向報紙、廣播或電視臺發回報道的記者。這個人不僅報道新聞，還承擔把遠方訊息傳回媒體的“通訊”角色。","examples":[{"en":"Our correspondent in Berlin sent back a report on the election.","zh":"我們的柏林特派記者發回了一篇關於選舉的報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our foreign correspondent reported live from the capital.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correspondent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b2fb307802a9977","term":"correspondent","forms":["correspondent","correspondents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對應物；對應者","explanation":"指與另一事物相對應、相匹配的事物，相當於另一邊的對應項；重點仍是“彼此對得上號”。","examples":[{"en":"The custom has a correspondent in several neighboring cultures.","zh":"這種習俗在幾個鄰近文化中都有對應的形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each symbol has a correspondent in the other writing system.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/correspondent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd09da605e5804b35ee4","word":"corridor","forms":["corridor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ec0f39ae78299a2","term":"corridor","forms":["corridor","corridors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"走廊","explanation":"指建築物或車廂裡連線各個房間、座位區的狹長通道，是這個詞最直接、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting room is at the end of the corridor.","zh":"會議室在走廊盡頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I saw her walking quickly down the corridor.","zh":"我看見她快步走過走廊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corridor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06b894d5cd6f617c","term":"corridor","forms":["corridor","corridors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狹長通行地帶","explanation":"指專門保留下來、讓人或交通工具從一個地方通往另一個地方的狹長土地。它把室內“走廊”的通道概念擴充套件到了室外。","examples":[{"en":"The new rail corridor will connect the two cities.","zh":"新的鐵路通道將連線這兩座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The corridor connects the reserve to a larger forest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corridor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11d510e067d2cdcd7559","word":"corrupt","forms":["corrupt"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e7d7303b8ff84e7","term":"corrupt","forms":["corrupt","more corrupt","most corrupt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貪腐的；收受賄賂的","explanation":"指為了個人利益而不誠實行事，尤其是接受賄賂或利用職權謀私。這個意思把“正直的人或制度”想成從內部壞掉了。","examples":[{"en":"The corrupt official accepted money from the company.","zh":"那名貪腐官員收了那家公司的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People are tired of living under a corrupt government.","zh":"人們厭倦了生活在一個腐敗的政府之下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cabfc2420810afb7","term":"corrupt","forms":["corrupt","more corrupt","most corrupt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"道德敗壞的；墮落的","explanation":"指一個人、群體或機構在道德上已經敗壞、墮落，不一定具體涉及賄賂。它仍然體現“從正直狀態變壞”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The novel portrays a corrupt society ruled by greed.","zh":"這部小說描繪了一個由貪婪支配的腐敗社會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel portrays a corrupt aristocracy obsessed with pleasure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b9df60f70dd5974","term":"corrupt","forms":["corrupt","corrupts","corrupting","corrupted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使墮落；使敗壞","explanation":"指把人從正直或健康的道路上帶偏，使其變得不道德、貪婪或墮落。它可以指誘惑，也可以指持續的壞影響。","examples":[{"en":"Power can corrupt even honest people.","zh":"權力甚至會使誠實的人墮落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tried to corrupt the young athlete with easy money.","zh":"他試圖用輕鬆賺來的錢使那名年輕運動員墮落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e152d866bc85450b7c1c","word":"corruption","forms":["corruption"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55c987b122c27bf1","term":"corruption","forms":["corruption","corruptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敗壞；墮落","explanation":"指人的品德、制度或某種原則受到破壞，失去原本應有的正直和純潔；這是本詞最寬泛的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"The novel explores the corruption of power.","zh":"這部小說探討了權力如何使人敗壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He believed that wealth had led to the corruption of his values.","zh":"他認為財富導致了自己價值觀的敗壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corruption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4aaea67f9680cee9","term":"corruption","forms":["corruption","corruptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治或商業腐敗","explanation":"指政府或企業中利用職權謀私的制度性不正當行為，包括收受賄賂、利益衝突、任人唯親和侵吞公款等。","examples":[{"en":"The new law aims to reduce corruption in public offices.","zh":"新法律旨在減少公職機構中的腐敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister resigned after a corruption investigation.","zh":"這名部長在接受腐敗調查後辭職了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corruption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05a9df1166f88123a556","word":"cosmetic","forms":["cosmetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afe8bd5ee768012f","term":"cosmetic","forms":["cosmetic","more cosmetic","most cosmetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"美容的；化妝用的","explanation":"指用來改善人的外表，尤其是皮膚、臉部外觀的；可以修飾產品、處理方式或其他美容相關事物。","examples":[{"en":"The store sells cosmetic products made for sensitive skin.","zh":"這家商店出售為敏感肌膚製作的美容產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company sells cosmetic brushes and skin creams.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12589f00e648cded","term":"cosmetic","forms":["cosmetic","more cosmetic","most cosmetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表面的；治標的","explanation":"指影響外觀或表層、卻沒有改變核心結構或實際功能的。它把“裝飾表面”的概念擴充套件到了房屋、制度、方案和問題等領域。","examples":[{"en":"The scratches are only cosmetic and do not affect the phone's performance.","zh":"這些劃痕只是表面問題，不影響手機的效能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fresh coat of paint is merely a cosmetic fix.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b62d138a858bbb5eb07","word":"cosmetics","forms":["cosmetics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56811ccec2125a5d","term":"cosmetics","forms":["cosmetics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化妝品","explanation":"指塗抹或使用在皮膚、頭髮、指甲、嘴唇、眼睛等外部部位上的產品，用來改善或增強外表美感。核心畫面是“把外表整理、裝飾得更好看”。","examples":[{"en":"She bought some cosmetics for her skin and hair.","zh":"她買了一些用於皮膚和頭髮的化妝品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cosmetics are made from natural ingredients.","zh":"這些化妝品由天然成分製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmetics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-123322c17461a39e","term":"cosmetics","forms":["cosmetics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外在效果；表面包裝","explanation":"指一件事呈現出來的外表、包裝或視覺效果，往往暗示這些外在因素可能比實際內容更受重視。它是從“裝飾外表”這個核心意思引申出來的。","examples":[{"en":"The cosmetics of the presentation were impressive, but the results were weak.","zh":"這場展示的外在包裝很令人印象深刻，但成果並不理想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Voters wanted genuine reform, not electoral cosmetics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmetics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f82f7b375f4aa1bd7d5","word":"cost","forms":["cost"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1ba69e7f250b850","term":"cost","forms":["cost","costs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"費用；花費","explanation":"cost是為了購買、製作、完成或使用某物而需要付出的錢，也可以指所耗費的時間等資源。它關注的是“完成這件事需要付出多少”。","examples":[{"en":"The cost of repairing the roof was higher than we expected.","zh":"修理屋頂的費用比我們預想的高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to reduce the cost of running the office.","zh":"我們需要降低辦公室的運營成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f732374f425c914","term":"cost","forms":["cost","costs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代價；損失","explanation":"cost也可以是為了得到某種結果而失去的東西，例如時間、健康、機會或安全。這裡的“賬單”不一定能用錢支付，而是強調某種結果帶來的負面付出。","examples":[{"en":"He achieved success at the cost of his personal life.","zh":"他犧牲了個人生活才取得成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The war came at a terrible cost to civilians.","zh":"這場戰爭讓平民付出了慘重代價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c6ac193a3ccdba4c","term":"cost","forms":["cost","costs","costing","costed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"需花費；價格為","explanation":"作動詞時，cost表示某物需要付出多少錢，也可以指需要耗費多少時間或資源。它把“賬單”放在句子裡，說明某件事對誰或需要多少付出。","examples":[{"en":"The new computer cost me nearly a thousand dollars.","zh":"這臺新電腦花了我將近一千美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The journey will cost us three hours.","zh":"這段旅程會耗費我們三個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf9662de9cb86b80","term":"cost","forms":["cost","costs","costing","costed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使失去；使付出代價","explanation":"cost可以表示某件事讓某人失去重要的東西，或迫使某人付出生命、健康、機會等代價。這是名詞“代價”變成動作後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The accident cost her the use of one hand.","zh":"那場事故使她失去了右手的功能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His mistake cost the team a place in the final.","zh":"他的錯誤讓球隊失去了進入決賽的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9025b50887457ff41d5f","word":"costly","forms":["costly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c9041ec4c0889bd","term":"costly","forms":["costly","costlier","more costly","costliest","most costly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"昂貴的；代價高昂的","explanation":"指需要付出很多錢，或會帶來很大的時間、精力、損失等代價；因此既可以說物品價格高，也可以說某件事做起來代價很大。","examples":[{"en":"Replacing the old roof was a costly project.","zh":"更換舊屋頂是一個代價高昂的專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A costly mistake nearly bankrupted the inexperienced builder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/costly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-241562d91defe29a81f4","word":"costume","forms":["costume"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5a0938b7af650ae","term":"costume","forms":["costume","costumes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特定風格的服飾","explanation":"指一套能體現某個國家、時代、民族或群體特色的服裝及配飾、髮型等整體裝束。重點不在某一件衣服，而在這種裝束所代表的身份或風格。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a collection of traditional costumes from around the world.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了來自世界各地的傳統服飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancers wore colorful costumes inspired by the region's history.","zh":"舞者穿著受當地歷史啟發的色彩鮮豔的服飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/costume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0887f3883908e8d","term":"costume","forms":["costume","costumes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝扮服或偽裝服","explanation":"指為了扮成某個角色、動物或人物而穿的一整套服裝，常見於派對、節日、舞臺表演或化裝活動。它可以是有趣的裝扮，也可以用於隱藏真實身份。","examples":[{"en":"The children wore superhero costumes for the school party.","zh":"孩子們穿著超級英雄服參加學校聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He arrived at the party in a pirate costume.","zh":"他穿著海盜裝扮來參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/costume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11102e6ea692987aa635","word":"cottage","forms":["cottage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e209fb2946d93fd1","term":"cottage","forms":["cottage","cottages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小屋；小住宅","explanation":"指規模較小、通常讓人聯想到鄉間生活的房子。重點是“小而獨立的住宅”這一形象，不一定真的很簡陋。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a small cottage by the lake.","zh":"他們在湖邊買了一座小屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old cottage has a thatched roof.","zh":"那座老小屋有一頂茅草屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cottage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ca8679c3805fe9a","term":"cottage","forms":["cottage","cottages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鄉間住宅；度假屋","explanation":"也可以指季節性居住的房子、度假屋或偏遠住宅，面積和裝修不一定小；名稱保留了鄉間住宅的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"We rented a cottage in the mountains for the summer.","zh":"我們租了一棟山裡的度假屋過夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They rented a cottage beside the lake for August.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cottage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69e399851c8419993d46","word":"cotton","forms":["cotton"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64576af8200967f9","term":"cotton","forms":["cotton","cottons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棉花纖維","explanation":"指棉花中可紡織的柔軟纖維，是製造棉布和許多棉製品的原料；通常不可數。","examples":[{"en":"Cotton is widely used to make soft, breathable fabric.","zh":"棉花廣泛用於製作柔軟、透氣的布料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer grows cotton on several fields.","zh":"這位農民在幾塊田裡種植棉花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"113":2}}},{"id":"ceec-2990bbc26a23f41e4778","word":"couch","forms":["couch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1957b34d13cc4b7e","term":"couch","forms":["couch","couches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙發","explanation":"指供兩人或多人舒適坐著的軟墊傢俱，通常就是客廳裡的沙發。這是現代日常英語中最重要的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We sat on the couch and watched a movie.","zh":"我們坐在沙發上看了一部電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children built a fort with cushions on the couch.","zh":"孩子們用沙發上的靠墊搭了一個堡壘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/couch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ccb2e85149a0727","term":"couch","forms":["couch","couches","couching","couched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"措辭；表述","explanation":"表示把一個想法、請求或事實“放進”特定的語言形式中，也就是用某種方式來措辭或表述。","examples":[{"en":"She couched her criticism as a helpful suggestion.","zh":"她把批評措辭成了一個有益的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report couched the warning in polite language.","zh":"這份報告用禮貌的措辭表達了警告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/couch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-866ab33b8463db1b3906","word":"cough","forms":["cough"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bb4854065ffd694","term":"cough","forms":["cough","coughs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咳嗽；一次咳嗽聲","explanation":"指肺部突然把氣推出、發出短促聲音的動作，也可以指聽到的那一聲咳嗽。它是 cough 最基本的名詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a dry cough behind me.","zh":"我聽見身後傳來一聲乾咳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She covered her mouth during a cough.","zh":"她咳嗽時捂住了嘴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80d849dc0e562318","term":"cough","forms":["cough","coughs","coughing","coughed","coughest","coughedst","cougheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"咳嗽","explanation":"指肺部把氣推出、發出短促聲音，通常是為了清除刺激物或堵塞氣道。這是動詞 cough 最基本的意義。","examples":[{"en":"I breathed in smoke and started to cough.","zh":"我吸進了煙，開始咳嗽起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child coughed all night.","zh":"那個孩子咳了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0c7ec73f6d7f2b4f3e6","word":"council","forms":["council"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d57b41c2ec507ac","term":"council","forms":["council","councils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"委員會；理事會","explanation":"council 是一群被組織起來、負責領導、管理或共同作決定的人，常譯為“委員會”“理事會”或“議會”。它的核心畫面就是一群人圍坐議事，並代表某個城市、機構或團體行使管理職責。","examples":[{"en":"The city council approved a new park for the neighborhood.","zh":"市議會批准在這個社群修建一座新公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The student council organized a charity event.","zh":"學生會組織了一場慈善活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/council","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13b3fc1ecfd1a941","term":"council","forms":["council","councils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"（委員會的）管理機構","explanation":"這裡是“委員會”義的轉指用法，不強調委員會成員，而是把委員會當作一個管理機關或它所作出的決定來談。上下文通常仍能看出它代表某個正式機構。","examples":[{"en":"The council has closed the road for safety reasons.","zh":"地方政府出於安全原因封閉了這條道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university council approved the new laboratory building.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/council","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff9a0c76596a5d3c658f","word":"counsel","forms":["counsel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-234bd8c5d7f91790","term":"counsel","forms":["counsel","counsels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勸告；建議","explanation":"指別人針對某件事提出的意見或指導，通常暗示這意見經過認真考慮，值得聽取；它是“商議”這一核心概念最常見的結果。","examples":[{"en":"She took her mentor’s counsel and waited before replying.","zh":"她聽從導師的建議，等了一會兒再回復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His counsel helped me make a difficult decision.","zh":"他的建議幫助我作出了一個艱難的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counsel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16385ae8d98268d1","term":"counsel","forms":["counsel","counsels","counseling","counselling","counseled","counselled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勸告；提供專業意見","explanation":"指以審慎或專業的方式給某人建議，幫助對方作出決定；在法律場景中尤其常指律師為當事人提供諮詢。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer counselled her to remain silent during the interview.","zh":"律師建議她在詢問過程中保持沉默。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor counselled the patient to reduce his workload.","zh":"醫生建議病人減少工作量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counsel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a8c1d77579d8c6d127a","word":"counselor","forms":["counselor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b83bc20e5a7ad48","term":"counselor","forms":["counselor","counselors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輔導員；諮詢師","explanation":"指受過專業訓練、幫助人處理個人困難和生活問題的人，通常透過傾聽、交談和提出建議來幫助對方。","examples":[{"en":"She spoke with a counselor after the breakup.","zh":"分手後，她找輔導員談了談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school counselor helped him plan his courses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counselor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02dd8ac1c50988b8","term":"counselor","forms":["counselor","counselors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學校輔導員","explanation":"指在學校幫助學生處理學習、選課、升學、職業規劃或健康問題的工作人員，是學校環境中的專門輔導員。","examples":[{"en":"The school counselor helped me choose my courses.","zh":"學校輔導員幫我選擇了課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school counselor helped her explore career options.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counselor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c35493a2b937829c981","word":"count","forms":["count"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05de4f23fe291dfa","term":"count","forms":["count","counts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計數","explanation":"指把一組東西逐個數一遍這一動作，也就是“數一下”。","examples":[{"en":"Give the chairs a quick count before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人到來前快速數一下椅子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child can count to fifty without help.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/count","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44f5c50ff12eb5e6","term":"count","forms":["count","counts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計數結果；數量","explanation":"指把東西數完後得到的總數，也就是“數出來有多少”。","examples":[{"en":"The final count was  forty-two votes.","zh":"最終統計結果是四十二票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final count showed twenty-seven missing boxes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/count","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa15c1986496b652","term":"count","forms":["count","counts","counting","counted","countest","countedst","counteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"數數","explanation":"指按順序說出數字，或從一個數字連續數到另一個數字。","examples":[{"en":"Can you count to twenty?","zh":"你會數到二十嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toddler can count from one to twenty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/count","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d12857b84f149e95","term":"count","forms":["count","counts","counting","counted","countest","countedst","counteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"數出……的數量","explanation":"指逐個清點一組物品，確定它總共有多少個。","examples":[{"en":"Please count the plates before dinner.","zh":"請在晚餐前數一下盤子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Count the chairs before setting out the plates.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/count","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97769992112cae45","term":"count","forms":["count","counts","counting","counted","countest","countedst","counteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重要；算數","explanation":"表示某人或某事會影響結果、值得考慮，也就是“起作用”或“算數”。這是從“納入計算”引申出來的抽象意思。","examples":[{"en":"Every small effort counts.","zh":"每一點小小的努力都很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your opinion counts when we choose the next project.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/count","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d71021338af54164a72","word":"countable","forms":["countable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"countable","forms":["countable"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"可數的","examples":[{"en":"The word chair is a countable noun.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Use many with countable nouns such as books and apples.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-efe899c74558f20b08bb","word":"counter","forms":["counter"],"officialPos":"n./v./adj./adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3789675df3a9e974","term":"counter","forms":["counter"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相反的；對立的","explanation":"它表示某事與另一件事相反或形成對抗，正對應記憶鉤子裡“相反”這一分支。","examples":[{"en":"His decision was counter to the team's plan.","zh":"他的決定與團隊的計劃相沖突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Strong counter currents pushed the swimmers toward shore.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23057af7723c7beb","term":"counter","forms":["counter","counters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計數籌碼；標記片","explanation":"指用來計數、保持數目或在遊戲中表示位置的小物件，正是“數”這條分支中的籌碼。","examples":[{"en":"Move your counter three spaces forward.","zh":"把你的籌碼向前移三格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each player gets five counters at the start of the game.","zh":"遊戲開始時，每位玩家得到五個籌碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95761467f259247c","term":"counter","forms":["counter","counters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"櫃檯","explanation":"指商店或辦理業務時用來收款、交接物品和辦理交易的檯面，連線了記憶鉤子中“櫃檯”這一含義。","examples":[{"en":"Please leave the package at the counter.","zh":"請把包裹放在櫃檯那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She paid for the tickets at the counter.","zh":"她在櫃檯買票付款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa958613853fb157","term":"counter","forms":["counter","counters","countering","countered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反駁；對抗","explanation":"表示提出相反意見、行動或立場來反駁、阻止對方，正對應記憶鉤子中“相反”這一分支。它既可以針對言論，也可以針對計劃或策略。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer countered the accusation with evidence from the report.","zh":"律師用報告中的證據反駁了這項指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy was designed to counter rising housing costs.","zh":"這項新政策旨在應對不斷上漲的住房成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-9b828e2f3cec3b60d126","word":"counterpart","forms":["counterpart"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-556647070e78ae48","term":"counterpart","forms":["counterpart","counterparts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相配的另一部分","explanation":"指與另一部分彼此配合、互相補足的部分，就像兩塊能夠接合的拼圖。重點是兩者合在一起才能完整發揮作用。","examples":[{"en":"The two panels fit together with their counterparts.","zh":"這兩塊面板和各自相配的部分嚴絲合縫地接在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This glove's counterpart was lying under the bench.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counterpart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea7f89f0d976ed41","term":"counterpart","forms":["counterpart","counterparts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職能或特點相對應的人或物","explanation":"指在職位、職責、功能或重要特點上與另一方相對應的人或事物。比如一個國家的部長可以有另一個國家的對應部長；兩者未必相同，但承擔的角色相近。","examples":[{"en":"The minister spoke with her counterpart from Canada.","zh":"這位部長與她的加拿大對應部長進行了交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our sales team met its counterpart in the European office.","zh":"我們的銷售團隊和歐洲辦事處的對應團隊見了面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/counterpart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aff64e4fd520bd185cb0","word":"country","forms":["country"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1631d0957bfc781","term":"country","forms":["country","countries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家；國土","explanation":"指由政府和邊界組成的國家，也可指這個國家的國土或全國範圍。country強調一個國家作為一片有邊界的土地和共同體。","examples":[{"en":"She has lived in three different countries.","zh":"她在三個不同的國家生活過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"News from all parts of the country was reported that evening.","zh":"那天晚上報道了來自全國各地的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/country","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65ba445507f1fe34","term":"country","forms":["country","countries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鄉村；鄉下","explanation":"指與城鎮或城市相對的農村地區，包括田野、村莊和較為開闊的自然環境。它把country看成城市之外的那片土地，是“國家”一義之外最重要的用法。","examples":[{"en":"My grandparents still live in the country.","zh":"我的祖父母仍然住在鄉下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We go to the country for fresh air at weekends.","zh":"我們週末去鄉下呼吸新鮮空氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/country","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f2f4a9cec4509121498","word":"countryside","forms":["countryside"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee2f687b7e8477b7","term":"countryside","forms":["countryside","countrysides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城市以外的鄉村地區","explanation":"指不屬於城鎮、城市或其密集郊區的鄉村區域，也就是人們通常所說的鄉下。","examples":[{"en":"My grandparents live in the countryside.","zh":"我的祖父母住在鄉下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many young people leave the countryside to find work in the city.","zh":"許多年輕人離開鄉村，到城市找工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/countryside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cc8b0b8698569f6","term":"countryside","forms":["countryside","countrysides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"較大地區中的鄉村部分","explanation":"強調某個國家、州或更大區域裡相對於城市而言的那一部分鄉村地帶。","examples":[{"en":"We spent a week exploring the French countryside.","zh":"我們花了一週探索法國鄉村地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eastern countryside contains orchards and scattered farms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/countryside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50f5d3a0117236c1735f","word":"county","forms":["county"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d68912681a6bbc87","term":"county","forms":["county","counties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行政區、郡或縣","explanation":"指國家內部由政府管理、通常有明確邊界的地區，是現代最重要的含義。不同國家的制度不同，所以它可能相當於“郡”“縣”或類似的地方行政區。","examples":[{"en":"The county government is repairing the road near our town.","zh":"縣政府正在維修我們鎮附近的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The county maintains these rural roads.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/county","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d83d8b50d5953957","term":"county","forms":["county","counties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳統地理區域","explanation":"有時county只表示一個約定俗成、邊界明確的地區，不強調它現在是否直接承擔行政職能；它仍然保留“有邊界的一塊地方”這個核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She grew up in a traditional county known for its old villages.","zh":"她在一個以古老村莊聞名的傳統郡區長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmhouse stands in the historic county of Yorkshire.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/county","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cf382fca2a10c63b223","word":"couple","forms":["couple"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-637a2a74569daffb","term":"couple","forms":["couple","couples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一對；兩個","explanation":"指兩個同類的人或物被放在一起、被看作一個組合。","examples":[{"en":"A couple of birds landed on the fence.","zh":"兩隻鳥落在了籬笆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought a couple of tickets for the show.","zh":"我買了兩張演出的票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/couple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ffedfb66f0769c1","term":"couple","forms":["couple","couples","coupling","coupled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連線；接合","explanation":"把兩個原本分開的東西扣在一起，使它們發生連線或協同作用。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer coupled the new engine to the train.","zh":"工程師把新發動機接到了火車上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two systems are closely coupled.","zh":"這兩個系統連線得很緊密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/couple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72309c04a62543846322","word":"coupon","forms":["coupon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49878735c0e43db6","term":"coupon","forms":["coupon","coupons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"票券；憑證","explanation":"指票上的一部分，持票人可以憑它獲得指定的交通、座位、住宿或其他服務。核心形象是“交出這張小票，就能換到已經承諾的權益”。","examples":[{"en":"The travel coupon includes a seat reservation and one checked bag.","zh":"這張旅行票券包含座位預訂和一件托執行李。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Present this coupon to collect your reserved meal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coupon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a27deeaea953809","term":"coupon","forms":["coupon","coupons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"優惠券；折扣券","explanation":"指商家或製造商發放的小票，使用時可以讓指定商品減價。它是“剪下或拿出一小張票，換取更低價格”的日常用法。","examples":[{"en":"I used a coupon to save two dollars on the cereal.","zh":"我用了一張優惠券，買麥片省了兩美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This coupon expires at the end of the month.","zh":"這張優惠券月底到期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coupon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4492aabd733f37cb76fc","word":"courage","forms":["courage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ae2e3135d03770c","term":"courage","forms":["courage","courages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不怯懦的自信","explanation":"指人在面對威脅、壓力或令人畏懼的人事物時，仍然自信堅定、不容易退縮，同時並不等於粗心或不顧後果。","examples":[{"en":"She showed great courage when she spoke up against the unfair decision.","zh":"她勇敢地站出來反對那個不公平的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found the courage to introduce herself to the panel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6bd2f05946107d6","term":"courage","forms":["courage","courages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"克服恐懼去行動","explanation":"指明明覺得害怕，仍然鼓起力量去做那件令人害怕的事。重點不在於沒有恐懼，而在於沒有讓恐懼阻止自己的行動。","examples":[{"en":"He finally found the courage to apologize to his friend.","zh":"他終於鼓起勇氣向朋友道歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It took courage to move to a new country alone.","zh":"獨自搬到一個新國家生活需要勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aa5c18a621487a5","term":"courage","forms":["courage","courages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"逆境中的堅定","explanation":"指在失敗、挫折、痛苦或長期困難中仍不放棄自己的目標和原則。這裡的勇氣像一顆經受壓力仍不動搖的心，不一定表現為一次大膽行動。","examples":[{"en":"She had the courage to admit her mistake and start again.","zh":"她有勇氣承認自己的錯誤，並重新開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed great courage throughout the difficult recovery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22eafa27fd2cd5628cbc","word":"courageous","forms":["courageous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-922aeb011fa6c871","term":"courageous","forms":["courageous","more courageous","most courageous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"勇敢的；有勇氣的","explanation":"形容一個人在困難、危險或恐懼面前仍然敢於行動，突出這個人的勇氣。","examples":[{"en":"She was courageous enough to speak out against the unfair decision.","zh":"她很勇敢，敢於公開反對這個不公平的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone admired the courageous firefighter.","zh":"所有人都很敬佩那位勇敢的消防員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courageous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7d831aa7323507c","term":"courageous","forms":["courageous","more courageous","most courageous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"需要勇氣的；勇敢的","explanation":"形容一個行為、決定或做法本身需要面對困難和風險，因此體現出勇氣。","examples":[{"en":"Admitting the mistake was a courageous decision.","zh":"承認錯誤是一個需要勇氣的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her courageous refusal to sign the false confession inspired the other prisoners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courageous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a908043ed469f361cd51","word":"course","forms":["course"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24c95972dd2b81df","term":"course","forms":["course","courses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過程；程序","explanation":"指事情按時間逐步展開的程序，也就是事情沿著一條路線發展，而不強調某一個單獨的事件。","examples":[{"en":"The course of the meeting changed when the manager arrived.","zh":"經理到來後，會議的程序發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the course of the afternoon, the rain stopped.","zh":"下午進行到一半時，雨停了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/course","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e17159b6755c065","term":"course","forms":["course","courses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"路線；行進方向","explanation":"指人、物體、河流或疾病等沿著的實際或抽象路徑；說某事 run its course，就是讓它沿自己的程序發展到結束。","examples":[{"en":"The river changed course after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，這條河改變了流向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let the investigation run its course.","zh":"讓調查按自己的程序進行下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/course","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db93ae96293dbf43","term":"course","forms":["course","courses","coursing","coursed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"流經；奔流","explanation":"指液體等沿著某條路徑快速流動，正是“沿路線前進”這一核心概念在動詞中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Warm water coursed through the pipes.","zh":"溫水流過了管道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tears coursed down her cheeks.","zh":"淚水順著她的臉頰流下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/course","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2f89e6fe92debe338cf","word":"court","forms":["court"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38c0b2c33a6d3f62","term":"court","forms":["court","courts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"院落；圍合的空地","explanation":"指建築物之間被圍起來的露天空地、院子，或幾乎被房屋包圍的小巷；這是“圍合空間”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children were playing in the small court behind the house.","zh":"孩子們正在房子後面的小院子裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fountain stood in the center of the paved court.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/court","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ec132c2f6ba4a3f","term":"court","forms":["court","courts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法庭；法院","explanation":"指負責審理案件、執行司法的機構或場所；原來的聚集空間變成了法律權力集中、作出裁決的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The witness gave evidence in court yesterday.","zh":"證人昨天在法庭上作了證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court ruled that the company had broken the law.","zh":"法院裁定這家公司違法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/court","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6629e9c50e64156a631f","word":"courteous","forms":["courteous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64303e98941c6e35","term":"courteous","forms":["courteous","more courteous","most courteous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有禮貌的；體貼周到的","explanation":"指待人時顧及對方感受，遵守禮節，表現得客氣而得體。它可以形容一個人的長期表現，也可以形容某個具體的動作、語氣或舉動。","examples":[{"en":"The courteous gentleman held the door open for the elderly woman.","zh":"那位有禮貌的紳士為老婦人扶住了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a courteous gesture by letting the other driver go first.","zh":"她禮貌地讓另一位司機先走，表現得很體貼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courteous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae8e0e940a94d02552e2","word":"courtesy","forms":["courtesy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-580023ee9d519887","term":"courtesy","forms":["courtesy","courtesies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禮貌；客氣","explanation":"指遵守禮節、尊重他人的行為方式，或對別人應有的客氣。它把“禮貌”看作人與人相處時應給予的一種尊重。","examples":[{"en":"Please show courtesy to the other guests.","zh":"請對其他客人保持禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He had the courtesy to call and explain what happened.","zh":"他還算有禮貌，打電話解釋了事情經過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courtesy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2af4c4b12cba8676","term":"courtesy","forms":["courtesy","courtesies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"客氣表示；善意舉動","explanation":"指一次具體的、出於禮貌或好意而做的事情，尤其是對方並沒有權利要求你這樣做時。比如主動送人一程、代為通知或提供一點方便，都可以是一種 courtesy。","examples":[{"en":"I offered her a ride as a courtesy.","zh":"我出於好意提出送她一程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Offering visitors a drink is a simple courtesy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courtesy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-953ff581e859b90bbcf5","word":"courtyard","forms":["courtyard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-165f4501cd9f22a3","term":"courtyard","forms":["courtyard","courtyards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"露天圍合院落","explanation":"指四周有牆或建築物、但上方露天的空間，可以是住宅中的院子，也可以是學校、酒店等建築內部的庭院。","examples":[{"en":"We ate lunch in the quiet courtyard.","zh":"我們在安靜的庭院裡吃了午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel has a small courtyard with trees.","zh":"這家酒店有一個種著樹的小庭院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/courtyard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42e20cbe942249d85888","word":"cousin","forms":["cousin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff1e6e9115c39a67","term":"cousin","forms":["cousin","cousins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堂兄弟姐妹或表兄弟姐妹；遠親","explanation":"指不是直系祖先、後代或親兄弟姐妹，而屬於同一家族旁系的親屬，最常見的是堂兄弟姐妹和表兄弟姐妹。","examples":[{"en":"My cousin is coming to stay with us this weekend.","zh":"我的堂兄弟（或表兄弟姐妹）這個週末要來和我們一起住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She grew up with several cousins nearby.","zh":"她從小就和幾位住在附近的堂兄弟姐妹或表兄弟姐妹一起長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cousin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42f1184f8ad4d973","term":"cousin","forms":["cousin","cousins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"較遠的旁系親屬","explanation":"在帶有表示遠近或輩分的限定詞時，也可指比通常所說的堂親、表親更遠的旁系親屬。","examples":[{"en":"I met my second cousin at a family reunion.","zh":"我在家庭聚會上見到了我的再從兄弟姐妹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We discovered a distant cousin living in Argentina.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cousin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fa405a8301ace34d11c","word":"cover","forms":["cover"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bea62daa23269cc4","term":"cover","forms":["cover","covers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"掩護；遮蔽處","explanation":"指能把人或物擋住、使其不容易被看見或受到攻擊的地方或情形；正如一塊布蓋住東西，這裡的cover提供的是保護。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers took cover under a rocky overhang during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，徒步者躲到岩石突出處下面避難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wall gave us enough cover to cross the yard safely.","zh":"那堵牆為我們提供了足夠的掩護，讓我們能安全穿過院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bff245f351c4037","term":"cover","forms":["cover","covers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書刊封面；外封","explanation":"指書、雜誌、唱片包裝等最外面的前面和後面部分，用來保護內容，也因此成為展示內容的“蓋子”。","examples":[{"en":"Her photograph appeared on the cover of the magazine.","zh":"她的照片登上了那本雜誌的封面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book has a bright red cover with gold lettering.","zh":"這本書有一個鮮紅色的封面，上面印著金色字樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29f1155c3caa23d3","term":"cover","forms":["cover","covers","covering","covered","coverest","coveredst","covereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蓋住；遮住","explanation":"把某物放在另一物的上面，使其被遮住或受到保護，就像用一塊布把東西蓋起來。","examples":[{"en":"She covered the bowl with a clean towel.","zh":"她用一條幹淨的毛巾蓋住了碗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please cover the plants before the frost arrives.","zh":"霜凍來之前，請把這些植物蓋好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53518f99c91f0410","term":"cover","forms":["cover","covers","covering","covered","coverest","coveredst","covereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支付；承擔費用","explanation":"為某人或某事提供錢，支付賬單、費用或所需開支；可以把它理解成把費用“蓋住”，讓別人不必承擔。","examples":[{"en":"My employer covered the cost of the training course.","zh":"我的僱主承擔了培訓課程的費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't worry about dinner—I’ll cover it.","zh":"晚飯不用擔心，我來買單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3a3091b9d32267d0b31","word":"coverage","forms":["coverage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4deb0c96b28d6b09","term":"coverage","forms":["coverage","coverages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人員或服務保障","explanation":"指為了讓工作或服務持續進行而安排的人員、時間或其他保障，重點是“有人頂上、事情不會中斷”。例如午休時留下足夠人員接聽電話，就是足夠的coverage。","examples":[{"en":"We need more coverage during the evening shift.","zh":"晚班時我們需要更多人員保障。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you find coverage for my shift tomorrow?","zh":"你能找人替我頂明天的班嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coverage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f444e5343cffd23","term":"coverage","forms":["coverage","coverages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"媒體報道","explanation":"指新聞媒體或其他媒體對某個事件、人物或話題給予的報道數量和程度。報道越多、涉及的媒體越廣，就可以說coverage越充分。","examples":[{"en":"The election received extensive media coverage.","zh":"這次選舉得到了廣泛的媒體報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Listeners criticized the station's limited coverage of the strike.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coverage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-beb134754910a4b4790c","word":"cow","forms":["cow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2049f15a30628c58","term":"cow","forms":["cow","cows","cattle","kye","kine"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成年母牛","explanation":"最嚴格的基本義是已經生過小牛的成年母牛。日常英語裡，人們也常用cow較寬泛地指一頭牛，所以具體含義要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer milked the cow before breakfast.","zh":"農夫在早餐前給那頭母牛擠了奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cow and her calf were standing near the fence.","zh":"一頭母牛和她的小牛站在籬笆旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a193d2c99fb91367ec8e","word":"coward","forms":["coward"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-addefed3435cfa5e","term":"coward","forms":["coward","cowards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膽小鬼；懦夫","explanation":"指遇到危險、衝突或困難時不敢面對、容易退縮的人；“夾著尾巴後退”的形象在這裡變成了對人的稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"He called me a coward, but I knew leaving was the safest choice.","zh":"他罵我是懦夫，但我知道離開是最安全的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nobody wants to be remembered as a coward.","zh":"沒人希望自己被記作一個懦夫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a08785f96ff45f77fb62","word":"cowardly","forms":["cowardly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecc02b82090aa917","term":"cowardly","forms":["cowardly","cowardlier","more cowardly","cowardliest","most cowardly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"膽小的；怯懦的","explanation":"形容一個人缺乏面對危險或困難的勇氣，遇到事情容易退縮；也可以形容這種退縮表現出來的行為。","examples":[{"en":"It was cowardly to blame someone who could not defend himself.","zh":"把責任推給一個無法為自己辯護的人，是很怯懦的做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cowardly soldier ran away when the fighting began.","zh":"戰鬥開始時，那個膽小計程車兵逃走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cowardly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d1173c424c75d203bbc","word":"cowboy","forms":["cowboy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09467f24dfd35339","term":"cowboy","forms":["cowboy","cowboys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"放牧牛群的牛仔","explanation":"指在開放牧場等地方照料、驅趕牛群的人，尤其讓人聯想到美國西部的牧牛工作。這是 cowboy 最基本、最具體的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The cowboy rode out early to check the cattle.","zh":"那名牛仔一早騎馬出去檢視牛群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandfather worked as a cowboy on a ranch in Texas.","zh":"她的祖父曾在得克薩斯州的一座牧場當牛仔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cowboy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2aee789db5620b402b48","word":"cozy","forms":["cozy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"cozy","forms":["cozy"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"溫暖舒適的","examples":[{"en":"We spent the evening in a cozy room beside the fire.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"This small cafe has a cozy corner for reading.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-3349a915f7cd0c2ff25e","word":"crab","forms":["crab"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4506b2a14a93ed0","term":"crab","forms":["crab","crabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螃蟹","explanation":"一種有硬殼和五對足的甲殼動物，最前面的一對足通常變成了螯；“橫著走、帶鉗子”的形象就是這個詞最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a crab hiding under a rock at the beach.","zh":"我們在海灘看見一隻螃蟹躲在岩石下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children spent the afternoon catching crabs in the shallow water.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在淺水裡捉螃蟹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f96baaf4d24c5c59","term":"crab","forms":["crab","crabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蟹肉","explanation":"指從螃蟹身上取出的肉，作為食物食用；這裡說的是螃蟹的肉，不是整隻螃蟹。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves fresh crab with garlic butter.","zh":"這家餐館供應配蒜香黃油的新鮮蟹肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered a sandwich filled with crab meat.","zh":"她點了一份夾滿蟹肉的三明治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5154e1a1b42f0126","term":"crab","forms":["crab","crabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脾氣壞的人","explanation":"指性情暴躁、愛發火或不容易被取悅的人，把螃蟹的鉗子和令人不快的形象聯想到人的壞脾氣。","examples":[{"en":"He may seem like a crab in the morning, but he is friendly after breakfast.","zh":"他早上看起來脾氣很壞，但吃過早飯後就很友善。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old crab complained about every neighborhood celebration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94f94c9c97bfa92bd267","word":"crack","forms":["crack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-747d65b671fd5d46","term":"crack","forms":["crack","cracks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裂縫","explanation":"硬的、原本完整的材料裂開後形成的細長縫隙，通常邊緣不規則；這正是“咔嚓”裂開後留下的痕跡。","examples":[{"en":"A crack has appeared in the kitchen wall.","zh":"廚房的牆上出現了一道裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineer found several cracks in the bridge.","zh":"工程師發現橋上有幾處裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c6a90d6068f49c3","term":"crack","forms":["crack","cracks","cracking","cracked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"受力破裂","explanation":"物體承受不了力量、壓力或重量而裂開或斷開，正如“咔嚓”一聲失去完整性。","examples":[{"en":"The old wooden step cracked under his weight.","zh":"那塊老木踏板在他的體重下裂開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ice cracked beneath our feet.","zh":"冰層在我們腳下裂開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c21e770548b3ab53","term":"crack","forms":["crack","cracks","cracking","cracked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解決難題","explanation":"經過思考終於找到困難問題的答案或方法，像“咔嚓”一下突破了卡住自己的難關。","examples":[{"en":"The research team finally cracked the problem after months of testing.","zh":"研究團隊經過幾個月的測試，終於解決了這個難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I think we have cracked the mystery.","zh":"我想我們已經解開這個謎團了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63c07aaa768024214658","word":"crackdown","forms":["crackdown"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5f6fc57fa936c18","term":"crackdown","forms":["crackdown","crackdowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴厲整治；強力打擊","explanation":"指執法或管理突然收緊，對某類違法、違規或不受歡迎的行為採取更嚴厲、更密集的措施；重點在於“加強執行力度”，而不只是提出新規定。","examples":[{"en":"The city launched a crackdown on illegal parking.","zh":"這座城市開展了嚴厲整治違章停車的行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crackdown on counterfeit goods forced several shops to close.","zh":"對假冒商品的嚴厲打擊迫使幾家商店關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crackdown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22f3ae2927952fc2fb44","word":"cracker","forms":["cracker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0a775567d8ad13c","term":"cracker","forms":["cracker","crackers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄脆餅乾","explanation":"指烤得幹、薄、脆的餅乾，通常是鹹味的，可單吃，也常配乳酪、湯或塗抹食物；這是現代最重要的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"I had some crackers and cheese before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前我吃了些薄脆餅乾和乳酪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These whole-grain crackers are surprisingly filling.","zh":"這些全穀物薄脆餅乾吃起來很頂飽，令人意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cracker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e06d84db405699c","term":"cracker","forms":["cracker","crackers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爆竹","explanation":"指點燃後會爆響的火藥小物件，重點在“突然裂響”的感覺；在節慶語境中尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"The children set off firecrackers in the street.","zh":"孩子們在街上燃放爆竹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could hear crackers going off all night.","zh":"我們整晚都能聽到爆竹不斷炸響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cracker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b61fa5d01281d1d","term":"cracker","forms":["cracker","crackers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"破碎器；夾碎工具","explanation":"泛指用來把某物弄裂、弄碎的人或工具，例如夾碎堅果、甲殼的器具；它直接保留了“使東西裂開”的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"Use the shell cracker to open the lobster claws.","zh":"用甲殼夾碎器開啟龍蝦的鉗子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This nutcracker can handle even the hardest shells.","zh":"這個堅果夾碎器連最硬的殼也能夾開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cracker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1a704873bce26f990e5","word":"cradle","forms":["cradle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-096deffc40500c0f","term":"cradle","forms":["cradle","cradles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搖籃","explanation":"供嬰兒躺臥的床，通常可以前後搖動，或懸掛起來輕輕擺動。","examples":[{"en":"The baby fell asleep in the cradle.","zh":"嬰兒在搖籃裡睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gently rocked the cradle with one hand.","zh":"她用一隻手輕輕搖著搖籃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cradle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4714adc41d56aad","term":"cradle","forms":["cradle","cradles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發源地","explanation":"比喻某種思想、文化、產業或現象最早產生並得到培育的地方，就像事物被放在搖籃中成長。","examples":[{"en":"The valley is often called the cradle of modern science.","zh":"這座山谷常被稱為現代科學的發源地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The region is considered the cradle of that civilization.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cradle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39bc5732cd857137","term":"cradle","forms":["cradle","cradles","cradling","cradled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放入搖籃式承託","explanation":"把人或物放在搖籃裡，或放在形狀、作用像搖籃的承託物中。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse cradled the newborn in a soft blanket.","zh":"護士用柔軟的毯子小心托住新生兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box cradled the fragile instrument.","zh":"這個盒子穩穩托住了那件易碎儀器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cradle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8df37bb5fb7544f","term":"cradle","forms":["cradle","cradles","cradling","cradled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"溫柔托住並保護","explanation":"用手臂或身體的一部分輕柔地托住、包圍並保護某人或某物，常用於受傷者或身體部位。","examples":[{"en":"He cradled the injured bird in his hands.","zh":"他用雙手小心地托住那隻受傷的鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cradled his head in her arms.","zh":"她把他的頭溫柔地託在臂彎裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cradle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-355543f790a3b210ecf3","word":"craft","forms":["craft"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45831f55577003c9","term":"craft","forms":["craft","crafts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專業技藝","explanation":"指某項工作或專業中需要長期訓練的精細技能。它把 craft 的核心形象保留下來：靠經驗和技巧把事情做得好。","examples":[{"en":"Good storytelling depends on the craft of choosing the right details.","zh":"好的講故事能力取決於選擇恰當細節的技巧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has mastered the craft of making violins.","zh":"他已經掌握了製作小提琴的技藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/craft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91db13c52fc24fa2","term":"craft","forms":["craft","crafts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手藝行業；專業","explanation":"指一種需要熟練操作、創造力或專門訓練的工作和行業，也可以泛指某人的職業領域。它強調“一個人靠這套本領從事的行當”。","examples":[{"en":"Carpentry is a craft that rewards patience.","zh":"木工是一門需要耐心、也會回報耐心的手藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned the craft of bookbinding from her mother.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/craft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-128c2622f546b0c06fb6","word":"cram","forms":["cram"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9eef4815e6df361","term":"cram","forms":["cram","crams","cramming","crammed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"硬塞；塞滿","explanation":"指把一個東西用力塞進另一個東西里，或把某處塞得滿滿的；重點是空間不夠卻仍然強行裝入。","examples":[{"en":"She crammed all her clothes into one small suitcase.","zh":"她把所有衣服都硬塞進了一個小行李箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train was crammed with commuters.","zh":"火車上擠滿了通勤者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa04fb00364be8d8","term":"cram","forms":["cram","crams","cramming","crammed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"臨時突擊學習","explanation":"指為了考試等緊急任務，在短時間內把大量知識強行記進腦子；它是“硬塞”知識的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"I had to cram for the biology test all weekend.","zh":"我整個週末都不得不為生物考試突擊複習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She crammed three chapters into one afternoon.","zh":"她一個下午突擊記完了三章內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b0962194517caa93836","word":"cramp","forms":["cramp"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4560e9c04ac5ad0d","term":"cramp","forms":["cramp","cramps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽筋；肌肉痙攣","explanation":"肌肉突然不受控制地收緊，並伴有疼痛；有時也可只表示類似的疼痛，即使看不出明顯收縮。","examples":[{"en":"I got a cramp in my calf after the long run.","zh":"長跑後我的小腿抽筋了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She woke up with a painful cramp in her foot.","zh":"她醒來時腳抽筋了，疼得厲害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cramp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56cc7ecf9d7f588e","term":"cramp","forms":["cramp","cramps","cramping","cramped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抽筋；痙攣","explanation":"肌肉突然疼痛地收緊，而且無法控制；這是“夾子收緊在肌肉上”的動詞表現。","examples":[{"en":"My toes cramped while I was swimming.","zh":"我游泳時腳趾抽筋了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His leg cramped halfway through the game.","zh":"比賽進行到一半時，他的腿抽筋了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cramp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c6ac23e4ffdf95f08f3","word":"crane","forms":["crane"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10ad584e2c4c99b7","term":"crane","forms":["crane","cranes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鶴","explanation":"指鶴科的大型鳥類，特點是腿長、脖子長，飛行時常把脖子伸直。這是 crane 最基本的形象，也是其他主要義項的來源。","examples":[{"en":"A crane stood quietly in the shallow water.","zh":"一隻鶴靜靜地站在淺水中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched cranes flying over the wetlands.","zh":"我們看著鶴群飛過溼地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5038857433edfa95","term":"crane","forms":["crane","cranes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"起重機","explanation":"指用長臂、鋼索等把重物吊起或移動的機器。這個義項來自它的形狀像鶴一樣伸出長頸或長臂。","examples":[{"en":"The crane lifted the steel beam onto the building.","zh":"起重機把鋼樑吊到了建築物上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tall crane stood beside the new bridge.","zh":"一臺高大的起重機立在新橋旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dbbc3d54bf4cc28","term":"crane","forms":["crane","cranes","craning","craned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"伸長脖子；探頭","explanation":"指像鶴一樣把脖子或身體向前伸，以便看得更清楚、夠到東西，或努力越過障礙觀察。","examples":[{"en":"She craned her neck to see over the crowd.","zh":"她伸長脖子，想看清人群后面的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He craned forward to read the small sign.","zh":"他探身向前，想看清那塊小標牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8470d663c02f37ab","term":"crane","forms":["crane","cranes","craning","craned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用起重機吊起或降下","explanation":"指用起重機，或像用起重機那樣，把重物吊起或放下；這是從“起重機”這個名詞發展出的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Workers craned the generator into the truck.","zh":"工人用起重機把發電機吊進卡車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The damaged boat was craned out of the water.","zh":"受損的船被起重機吊出了水面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cdb2e0d0f873ce5326e8","word":"crash","forms":["crash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad8ebc24a98c9d57","term":"crash","forms":["crash","crashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車禍；撞毀事故","explanation":"指汽車、飛機等交通工具發生的嚴重碰撞或事故，通常會造成損壞或人員受傷。","examples":[{"en":"Two people were injured in the car crash.","zh":"兩人在這場車禍中受傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plane crash closed the airport for several hours.","zh":"這起飛機墜毀事故使機場關閉了幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f654f04826afd74b","term":"crash","forms":["crash","crashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電腦崩潰","explanation":"指軟體或硬體突然停止正常工作，使電腦或程式部分或完全無法使用。","examples":[{"en":"The game froze after a crash, so I had to restart my computer.","zh":"遊戲崩潰後卡住了，所以我只好重啟電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crash erased three hours of unsaved work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4749e38e8771f889","term":"crash","forms":["crash","crashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴跌；崩盤","explanation":"指商業活動或股票價格突然大幅下降，嚴重時會引發更多企業或市場參與者失敗。","examples":[{"en":"Many investors lost money in the market crash.","zh":"許多投資者在市場崩盤中虧了錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Share prices crashed after the fraud became public.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9955d8ef7baf36a1","term":"crash","forms":["crash","crashes","crashing","crashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撞毀；猛撞","explanation":"指人或物猛烈地撞上某物，或猛烈墜落、倒下，通常會造成損壞或傷害。","examples":[{"en":"The truck crashed into a wall during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，那輛卡車撞上了一堵牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclist crashed on the wet road.","zh":"騎腳踏車的人在溼滑的路上摔倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6305cdf38b8fd554","term":"crash","forms":["crash","crashes","crashing","crashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使猛烈撞上","explanation":"指主動讓某物撞上另一物，通常結果是損壞、破裂或受傷。","examples":[{"en":"He crashed the bicycle into a parked car.","zh":"他把腳踏車撞上了一輛停著的汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The driver crashed the van into a concrete barrier.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b45695450a3ba414","term":"crash","forms":["crash","crashes","crashing","crashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"程式崩潰","explanation":"指程式因異常而停止執行，導致軟體或整個系統無法繼續正常執行。","examples":[{"en":"The app crashes whenever I open a large file.","zh":"我每次開啟大檔案時，這個應用都會崩潰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The browser crashes whenever I open that attachment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-e659dcb12b0fe2190bda","word":"crater","forms":["crater"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-079debe065554685","term":"crater","forms":["crater","craters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"撞擊坑","explanation":"指隕石或其他物體撞擊地面後留下的近似半球形大坑；核心畫面就是地面被重重砸出一個碗狀凹陷。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists found a large crater beneath the ice.","zh":"科學家在冰層下面發現了一個巨大的撞擊坑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meteorite left a crater in the desert.","zh":"那顆隕石在沙漠裡砸出了一個坑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e53c954bd0f1df3d","term":"crater","forms":["crater","craters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火山口","explanation":"指火山頂部或噴發通道的碗狀開口，熔岩、火山灰等主要從這裡噴出；類似的開口也可指間歇泉的噴口周圍形成的凹陷。","examples":[{"en":"Smoke rose from the volcano's crater.","zh":"煙霧從火山口升起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors stood near the crater but kept behind the barrier.","zh":"遊客站在火山口附近，但都留在護欄後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17270d91e6253b7f","term":"crater","forms":["crater","craters","cratering","cratered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"災難性崩潰","explanation":"指經濟、市場、計劃或局面突然徹底垮掉，彷彿被巨力炸出一個大坑；這是從“形成大坑”引申出的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company's sales cratered after the scandal.","zh":"醜聞發生後，這家公司的銷售額暴跌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The local economy cratered when the factory closed.","zh":"工廠關閉後，當地經濟災難性地崩潰了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81a60f2038a06bd1346b","word":"crawl","forms":["crawl"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1f93d75a32287bb","term":"crawl","forms":["crawl","crawls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爬行；匍匐","explanation":"指用手和膝蓋等貼著地面移動的動作，也可指拖著身體緩慢前進的過程。這是 crawl 最直接、最容易延伸出其他意思的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The baby made a slow crawl across the living room.","zh":"嬰兒慢慢爬過了客廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We reached the cave entrance on a crawl.","zh":"我們匍匐著到了洞口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crawl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f5733530baf05a2","term":"crawl","forms":["crawl","crawls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極慢的速度","explanation":"指慢得像人在地上爬一樣的速度，常用於交通、工作進度或電腦執行速度。它把身體爬行的緩慢感轉成了抽象的“進展很慢”。","examples":[{"en":"Traffic moved at a crawl after the accident.","zh":"事故發生後，車流緩慢得幾乎爬不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The approval process has slowed to a crawl.","zh":"審批流程已經慢得幾乎停滯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crawl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c77c6b47be46b8d3","term":"crawl","forms":["crawl","crawls","crawling","crawled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"爬行；匍匐前進","explanation":"指用手和膝蓋、腹部等貼著地面移動，或拖著身體慢慢向前。這是動詞的本義，也是“進展緩慢”等比喻義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The child crawled under the table to find the toy.","zh":"孩子爬到桌子下面去找玩具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injured man crawled toward the door.","zh":"受傷的人朝門口匍匐爬去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crawl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d8b1858e24ae617677d5","word":"crayon","forms":["crayon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01911ec2318c0d8e","term":"crayon","forms":["crayon","crayons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彩色蠟筆","explanation":"指一根用來畫畫或塗色的彩色蠟筆，通常由蠟或類似的固體材料製成，是crayon最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children drew a bright sun with crayons.","zh":"孩子們用蠟筆畫了一個鮮豔的太陽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the red crayon back in the box.","zh":"請把紅色蠟筆放回盒子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crayon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-389ec5f1112d5e956ad2","word":"crazy","forms":["crazy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b8a455962747065","term":"crazy","forms":["crazy","crazier","craziest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精神失常的","explanation":"指一個人的思想或行為嚴重偏離正常，到了令人害怕或難以理解的程度；這裡是“失去理智”的原始核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"His ideas were both frightening and crazy.","zh":"他的想法既令人害怕，又很瘋狂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You must be crazy to drive that fast.","zh":"你開得這麼快，一定是瘋了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crazy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0700b058aa70ee2","term":"crazy","forms":["crazy","crazier","craziest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"失控的","explanation":"指人、行動或局面不再受控制，發展得過猛、過亂，未必真的涉及精神失常。","examples":[{"en":"When she gets on the motorcycle, she goes crazy.","zh":"她一騎上摩托車就變得無法控制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd went crazy after the goal.","zh":"進球后人群徹底沸騰了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crazy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3a22c1ce8e0a5a96393","word":"cream","forms":["cream"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa9a4f1b7efcd0da","term":"cream","forms":["cream"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奶油色的","explanation":"指接近奶油的淺黃白色，顏色比純白略暖。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a cream sweater for the interview.","zh":"她為面試選了一件奶油色毛衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cream curtains softened the room's dark wooden walls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c49494533612801","term":"cream","forms":["cream","creams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"奶油；乳脂","explanation":"指牛奶中脂肪含量較高、分離後浮在上面的部分，也就是通常所說的奶油。","examples":[{"en":"Add a little cream to the soup before serving.","zh":"上桌前在湯里加一點奶油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fresh cream made the dessert much richer.","zh":"鮮奶油讓這道甜點濃郁多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-233014e2055abb82","term":"cream","forms":["cream","creams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精華；最優秀的部分","explanation":"從奶油浮在牛奶上層、較為精華這一形象引申，指某個群體或事物中最好、最有價值的部分。","examples":[{"en":"The program attracts the cream of young scientists.","zh":"這個專案吸引了年輕科學家中的精英。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only the cream of the crop made it to the final round.","zh":"只有最優秀的人進入了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa8847b0c33183273f59","word":"create","forms":["create"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3182224c878c41d","term":"create","forms":["create","creates","creating","created","createst","createdst","createth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"創造；創立","explanation":"指把原本不存在的東西帶到現實中，例如創造產品、作品、方法或解決方案。它抓住了“讓某物出現”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The team created a simple tool for new employees.","zh":"團隊為新員工創造了一個簡單的工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She created a new character for her novel.","zh":"她為自己的小說創作了一個新角色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/create","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-801cc8d67b547be8","term":"create","forms":["create","creates","creating","created","createst","createdst","createth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"造成；引起","explanation":"指某個行為、事件或條件帶來一種原本沒有的局面，尤其常用於困難、需求、壓力、機會等抽象結果。這裡不是“創造出一個物品”，而是“造成一個情況”。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden storm created serious problems for travelers.","zh":"突如其來的暴風雨給旅行者造成了嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fallen tree created a dangerous obstruction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/create","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-965abb254b10e268bd85","word":"creation","forms":["creation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16f50c8e739b28dd","term":"creation","forms":["creation","creations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創造出來的東西；作品或發明","explanation":"指已經被創造出來的具體成果，例如一件藝術作品、一項發明或一種產品。它強調“從無到有”後的成品，而不是創造的過程本身。","examples":[{"en":"The designer proudly showed us her latest creation.","zh":"那位設計師自豪地向我們展示了她最新的作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This robot is the company’s most impressive creation.","zh":"這臺機器人是這家公司最令人印象深刻的成果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2aed05a738e941f6","term":"creation","forms":["creation","creations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創造；創立或設立","explanation":"指創造某物或建立某事的行為和過程，重點在“把原本沒有的東西做出來或設立起來”。它可以用於作品、制度、職位、部門等。","examples":[{"en":"The project led to the creation of hundreds of new jobs.","zh":"這個專案創造了數百個新的就業崗位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The creation of the museum took several years.","zh":"這座博物館的建立花了好幾年時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-828febb7609afd5e728e","word":"creative","forms":["creative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88b183c62d096eb7","term":"creative","forms":["creative","more creative","most creative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有創造力的","explanation":"指一個人有能力創造新東西，尤其能用新穎而有效的方式完成創作或解決問題。重點在“能創造”，不一定限於藝術領域。","examples":[{"en":"She is a creative designer who always finds fresh ways to present information.","zh":"她是一位很有創造力的設計師，總能用新鮮的方式呈現資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need to be creative when the usual solution does not work.","zh":"通常的辦法不起作用時，你需要發揮創造力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-896da4879fa99672","term":"creative","forms":["creative","more creative","most creative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"新穎有想象力的","explanation":"指想法、方案或作品不是照搬舊有做法，而是表達獨特、富有想象力，能為老問題提供新的方向。","examples":[{"en":"The team came up with a creative solution to the parking problem.","zh":"團隊為停車難題想出了一個新穎的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her creative solution turned broken tiles into a mosaic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a59225b5aa6af6cc550","word":"creativity","forms":["creativity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-12036aa16dbdb97c","term":"creativity","forms":["creativity","creativities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創造力；創意","explanation":"指運用想象力產生新穎想法、方法或作品的能力。它既可以說一個人很會想出新東西，也可以指這種能力在藝術、學習或工作中的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"Her creativity helped the team find a simple solution to the problem.","zh":"她的創造力幫助團隊找到了一個簡單的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children showed great creativity when they built toys from old boxes.","zh":"孩子們用舊盒子製作玩具時展現了很強的創造力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creativity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc6bfd848ebd7819c9a8","word":"creator","forms":["creator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41dcac6068788f5f","term":"creator","forms":["creator","creators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創造者；創作者","explanation":"指創造、設計或製作某種事物的人，例如作品、產品、軟體或某個想法的創造者。它保留了“把某種東西做出來”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She is the creator of a popular language-learning app.","zh":"她是一款熱門語言學習應用的創作者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The creator explained how the game was designed.","zh":"這款遊戲的創作者解釋了它是如何設計出來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be651d6c5134f29e","term":"creator","forms":["creator","creators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內容創作者","explanation":"在社交媒體語境中，creator常是content creator的省略，指持續製作併發布影片、文章、直播等內容，通常也可能透過這些內容獲利的人。","examples":[{"en":"The platform helps creators earn money from their videos.","zh":"這個平臺幫助內容創作者從影片中賺錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The creator posts a new cooking video every Friday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df8eb42b37df4f774564","word":"creature","forms":["creature"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28c5d27b0bfef429","term":"creature","forms":["creature","creatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物；動物","explanation":"指有生命的存在，最常用於動物，也可以指想象中的生物、外星生物或其他非人的生命體。這是 creature 最基本、最值得先掌握的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The pond is full of tiny creatures.","zh":"池塘裡滿是微小的生物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists discovered a new creature living deep under the ice.","zh":"科學家發現了一種生活在冰層深處的新生物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01d5bac2376b541c","term":"creature","forms":["creature","creatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神秘或怪異的生物","explanation":"特指身份、外形或性質不明，常常令人害怕或覺得奇怪的生物。這個含義仍然來自“某種生物”的核心概念，只是說話人更強調它的神秘和異常。","examples":[{"en":"A strange creature appeared in the garden at night.","zh":"夜裡有個奇怪的生物出現在花園裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strange creature emerged from the misty lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-844a6074dcc0f8a431d1","word":"credibility","forms":["credibility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35764f70515e1795","term":"credibility","forms":["credibility","credibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某人的公信力或可信度","explanation":"指一個人、組織或訊息來源長期積累的“讓別人相信自己的資格”。如果一個人經常誇大事實、失信或被揭穿，他的 credibility 就會下降；如果他一貫誠實可靠，credibility 就會上升。","examples":[{"en":"The company lost credibility after denying a problem that everyone could see.","zh":"這家公司否認一個大家都看得見的問題後，失去了公信力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has built credibility with her team by admitting mistakes and fixing them quickly.","zh":"她透過承認錯誤並迅速改正，在團隊中建立了可信度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1966961c4fb8c6c3","term":"credibility","forms":["credibility","credibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"證人或證詞的可信性","explanation":"在法律語境中，指法庭認為某位證人或其證詞有多可信。判斷的不只是證人是否誠實，也包括證詞是否前後一致、是否符合證據和一般常理。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer challenged the credibility of the witness by showing that her story had changed several times.","zh":"律師指出這名證人的說法多次改變，從而質疑了她的可信性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conflicting dates damaged the witness's credibility.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51eddb3ebf3a7a3eee16","word":"credible","forms":["credible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-964731c648d71f94","term":"credible","forms":["credible","more credible","most credible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可信的；合理的","explanation":"用於說法、解釋、藉口或證據等，表示它聽起來合理，有足夠根據讓人相信。它不一定已經被證明為真，但至少不是荒唐或牽強的。","examples":[{"en":"The witness gave a credible explanation for being late.","zh":"這名證人為遲到給出了一個令人信服的解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The detective finally found a credible alibi.","zh":"偵探最終找到了一個可信的不在場證明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da242734b0c48f5f","term":"credible","forms":["credible","more credible","most credible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可靠的；值得信賴的","explanation":"用於人、機構、新聞來源或資訊來源時，表示它們一貫可靠，提供的資訊值得信任。這裡的重點從“某個說法合理”擴充套件到了“說話或提供資訊的人、來源可靠”。","examples":[{"en":"We should check the report against several credible sources.","zh":"我們應該用幾個可靠的來源來核對這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The investigator found a credible witness to the accident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecc4873a1694eb0de0b3","word":"credit","forms":["credit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad5341a7ff3f8f66","term":"credit","forms":["credit","credits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信任；相信","explanation":"指對某人所說或所做的事情抱有信任，認為它真實可靠。這是其他許多詞義的起點：既然相信對方，就可能給對方榮譽、賒賬或記上一筆價值。","examples":[{"en":"I gave no credit to the rumor.","zh":"我完全不相信那則傳聞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She deserves credit for telling the truth.","zh":"她因為說了實話而值得肯定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c06a418dfd265dca","term":"credit","forms":["credit","credits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認可；尊重","explanation":"指因為一個人的努力、能力或誠實而給予他認可和尊重，相當於把這份功勞記在他名下。","examples":[{"en":"Give her credit for solving the problem so quickly.","zh":"她這麼快解決了問題，應該得到肯定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Give the volunteers credit for organizing everything.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-edb8d5bf1c109d44","term":"credit","forms":["credit","credits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賒賬；信用付款","explanation":"指賣方或貸款方基於對買方會還款的信任，先提供商品或錢，允許對方以後付款。這裡仍然是“把信任記在賬上”。","examples":[{"en":"The store lets regular customers buy on credit.","zh":"這家商店允許老顧客賒賬購買。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bank refused to extend credit to the company.","zh":"銀行拒絕向這家公司提供信貸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/credit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-6e8fe4702048181b4881","word":"creek","forms":["creek"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce4dfe0f3d6f1613","term":"creek","forms":["creek","creeks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小溪；小河","explanation":"最常見的意思是比 river 小的自然水道，通常指淡水小溪。它和“小水灣”義可以用同一個畫面記憶：水流沿著彎曲的細小通道向前延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The children spent the afternoon playing beside the creek.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在小溪邊玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow creek runs through the forest.","zh":"一條狹窄的小溪流過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-facb06d37b22ccda","term":"creek","forms":["creek","creeks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小水灣；河口小汊","explanation":"在英式英語中，creek 常指海岸或河口向內凹入、與海洋或主河道相通的小水灣；可以把它想成水道向陸地彎進去的一段。","examples":[{"en":"Small boats were moored in the quiet creek.","zh":"小船停泊在寧靜的河口小水灣裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At high tide, fishing boats sheltered in the narrow creek.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2617708489831f17c7b6","word":"creep","forms":["creep"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da1540f523c89edc","term":"creep","forms":["creep","creeps","creeping","crept","creeped","crope","cropen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"貼地爬行","explanation":"指身體腹部貼近地面，緩慢地向前爬，常用於蛇、蜥蜴或人。","examples":[{"en":"The lizard crept across the warm stones.","zh":"那隻蜥蜴貼著溫暖的石頭爬過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby crept along the floor toward the toy.","zh":"嬰兒貼著地板朝玩具爬去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8872316e61be7636","term":"creep","forms":["creep","creeps","creeping","crept","creeped","crope","cropen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"悄悄慢慢移動","explanation":"指為了不被發現而緩慢、安靜地朝某個方向移動，核心畫面仍是“像爬行一樣悄悄靠近”。","examples":[{"en":"She crept past the sleeping dog.","zh":"她悄悄地從熟睡的狗旁邊走過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He crept into the kitchen after midnight.","zh":"午夜後他悄悄走進廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6012a1a40508e903","term":"creep","forms":["creep","creeps","creeping","crept","creeped","crope","cropen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸上升或變化","explanation":"指價格、數量或問題一點一點朝某個方向變化，像在緩慢爬行一樣逐步累積。","examples":[{"en":"Food prices have been creeping up since spring.","zh":"食品價格從春天以來一直在一點點上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature crept above thirty degrees by noon.","zh":"到中午時，溫度逐漸升到了三十度以上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9cae07a2e9ceea5b8860","word":"crew","forms":["crew"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3400ebbea207b34a","term":"crew","forms":["crew","crews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"團隊；工作人員","explanation":"crew的核心意思是共同完成一項工作或任務的一群人，例如船員、拍攝人員或維修人員。重點不是他們只是“在一起”，而是他們作為一個工作團隊協作。","examples":[{"en":"The film crew arrived before sunrise.","zh":"電影劇組在日出前就到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crew worked through the night to finish the repairs.","zh":"維修團隊連夜工作以完成修理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":7,"counts":{"111":1,"115":6}}},{"id":"ceec-1134e4f4a13b06aeaa84","word":"cricket","forms":["cricket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ab51cc527b03aab","term":"cricket","forms":["cricket","crickets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蟋蟀","explanation":"一種會鳴叫的小昆蟲，通常透過摩擦翅鞘發出連續的唧唧聲。日常英語裡說到這種昆蟲，cricket 通常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"We could hear crickets chirping outside the window.","zh":"我們能聽見窗外蟋蟀在鳴叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cricket jumped out of the pile of leaves.","zh":"一隻蟋蟀從那堆樹葉裡跳了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cricket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f42c27e928c0bfd","term":"cricket","forms":["cricket"],"pos":"noun","zh":"板球運動","explanation":"一種兩隊各有十一人的戶外球類運動，球員用球棒擊球並爭取得分，在英國及許多英聯邦國家很流行。它是從“板球比賽”這幅核心畫面延伸出其他比喻義的來源。","examples":[{"en":"My brother plays cricket for his local club.","zh":"我哥哥為當地俱樂部打板球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We played cricket on the village green.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cricket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acff1b6da9fafbdc","term":"cricket","forms":["cricket"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公平正派","explanation":"在英國英語中，cricket 可借板球重視公平競爭的形象，表示某人的做法光明正大、符合規矩。","examples":[{"en":"Hiding the rules from the other team isn't cricket.","zh":"把規則瞞著另一支隊伍並不公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Blaming your absent colleague simply isn't cricket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cricket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-54bd8ea967e56d02f7e2","word":"crime","forms":["crime"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bbd75980c98ed81","term":"crime","forms":["crime","crimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體罪行","explanation":"指違反法律、尤其是刑法的具體行為。重點是某一件可以明確指出的違法行為，而不是實施行為的人。","examples":[{"en":"He was arrested for a serious crime.","zh":"他因一項嚴重罪行被捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court found her guilty of the crime.","zh":"法院判定她犯了這項罪行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b54eb86b30c41576","term":"crime","forms":["crime","crimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會上的犯罪活動","explanation":"把許多罪行作為一個整體來談，指某個社會、地區或時期普遍存在的犯罪現象。","examples":[{"en":"The city is investing more money to fight crime.","zh":"這座城市正在投入更多資金打擊犯罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Street lighting helped reduce crime around the station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fab862fc97dbb716f555","word":"criminal","forms":["criminal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f406a9239865c6a4","term":"criminal","forms":["criminal","more criminal","most criminal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"違法的；法律禁止的","explanation":"指行為、活動或做法越過了法律紅線，因此受到法律禁止或可能受到懲罰。它強調違法性質，不只是一般意義上的不妥或不道德。","examples":[{"en":"The court ruled that the company had engaged in criminal activity.","zh":"法院裁定這家公司從事了犯罪活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is criminal to sell these medicines without a license.","zh":"無證出售這些藥品屬於違法行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criminal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cda886a88b4fb38a","term":"criminal","forms":["criminal","more criminal","most criminal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"刑事的；與犯罪或刑法有關的","explanation":"指研究、處理或記錄犯罪及刑罰的事物，例如刑事案件、刑法程式或犯罪記錄。這裡不一定是在說某個人已經犯罪，而是在說明所屬領域與刑事法律有關。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer specializes in criminal law.","zh":"這名律師專門從事刑法工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prosecutor initiated criminal proceedings after reviewing the evidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criminal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c36d7cb44de9231f","term":"criminal","forms":["criminal","criminals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"罪犯","explanation":"指越過法律紅線、犯下罪行的人；這個名詞把“犯罪的”這一性質直接落在具體的人身上。","examples":[{"en":"The police arrested a criminal who had escaped from prison.","zh":"警方逮捕了一名從監獄逃脫的罪犯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The escaped criminal was captured near the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criminal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b18aefe826adf558cdc","word":"cripple","forms":["cripple"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fcc5ec6c0057095f","term":"cripple","forms":["cripple","cripples","crippling","crippled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嚴重損害；重創","explanation":"比喻地說，使計劃、經濟、組織或個人的發展能力受到重創，像被削弱到難以繼續行動。","examples":[{"en":"The long strike crippled the local economy.","zh":"長期罷工重創了當地經濟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lack of funding crippled the project.","zh":"資金不足使這個專案難以推進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cripple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd05e33232896330","term":"cripple","forms":["cripple","cripples","crippling","crippled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使無法正常運作","explanation":"指嚴重損害某人的能力或某個系統的功能，使其無法像平常那樣運作；焦慮等情緒也可以“使人動彈不得”。","examples":[{"en":"He was crippled by fear when the alarm sounded.","zh":"警報響起時，他因恐懼而幾乎無法行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The power failure crippled the hospital's communication system.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cripple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34d6231c09aa82a5a446","word":"crisis","forms":["crisis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80017e3949dd256c","term":"crisis","forms":["crisis","crises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關鍵轉折點","explanation":"指事情發展到了必須作出重要判斷或選擇的關頭，結果可能因此改變；這裡強調的是“決定性時刻”，不一定已經是災難。","examples":[{"en":"The negotiations have reached a crisis point.","zh":"談判已經到了關鍵轉折點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The illness reached a crisis on the fifth night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crisis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb5e78996f7157f5","term":"crisis","forms":["crisis","crises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴重危機","explanation":"指政治、社會、經濟或軍事等領域中不穩定而緊張的局面，往往預示著可能突然惡化或發生重大變化。這是日常新聞和公共議題中最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"The government is trying to prevent a new energy crisis.","zh":"政府正努力防止新的能源危機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drought has triggered a severe food crisis.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crisis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-127c2817bd9e778721d5","word":"crispy","forms":["crispy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f32b253ef8b3ec8","term":"crispy","forms":["crispy","crispier","crispiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"酥脆的","explanation":"指食物表面形成脆殼，咬起來容易碎，但裡面可以仍然柔嫩；這就是“脆殼”這一核心意象。","examples":[{"en":"The fried chicken stayed crispy even after it cooled down.","zh":"炸雞即使涼了，表面仍然很酥脆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bake the potatoes until the edges are crispy.","zh":"把土豆烤到邊緣酥脆為止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crispy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-918ed1f97b526520a865","word":"criterion/criteria","forms":["criterion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c998c4e699ee3a8","term":"criterion","forms":["criterion","criteria","criterions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"判斷標準","explanation":"criterion 是一把用來衡量或篩選的“尺子”：面對不同的人或事物時，用它檢查誰更合適、什麼算合格，或某項要求是否滿足。這個標準可以是質量、價格、年齡等具體條件，也可以是較抽象的評價尺度。","examples":[{"en":"Price is an important criterion when we choose a hotel.","zh":"選擇酒店時，價格是一個重要標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The main criterion for admission is previous experience.","zh":"錄取的主要標準是以往的經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criterion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db113508c7cb409c8ea4","word":"critic","forms":["critic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-367be79f91cda4ee","term":"critic","forms":["critic","critics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作品評論家","explanation":"指評價別人作品的人，通常透過分析作品的優點、缺點和價值來發表評論。","examples":[{"en":"Several critics praised the novel for its vivid characters.","zh":"幾位評論家稱讚這部小說塑造的人物生動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film was well received by critics and audiences.","zh":"這部電影受到評論家和觀眾的好評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/critic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-149e3d6de2da3eb2","term":"critic","forms":["critic","critics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術評論家","explanation":"特指專門判斷和評價藝術、文學、電影等作品的人，是“評論家”這一核心形象中更專業的一類。","examples":[{"en":"The art critic admired the painting's unusual use of color.","zh":"那位藝術評論家很欣賞這幅畫對色彩的不尋常運用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The critic praised the film's restrained performances.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/critic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfba7033571d606f3c2f","word":"critical","forms":["critical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-704a784f920b9588","term":"critical","forms":["critical","more critical","most critical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"關鍵轉折的；危急的","explanation":"指事情正處在可能決定後果的轉折點，稍有變化就可能向更壞或更好的方向發展。它連線著“判斷臨界點”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"This is a critical moment for the team.","zh":"這是這個團隊的關鍵時刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The political situation became critical overnight.","zh":"政治局勢一夜之間變得危急起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/critical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30f02b678d808fd1","term":"critical","forms":["critical","more critical","most critical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其重要的","explanation":"指某件事對結果成敗不可缺少，不能耽誤或忽略。這是“處在關鍵點上”進一步引申出的高頻義。","examples":[{"en":"It's critical that you deliver this on time.","zh":"你按時交付這件事至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clear communication is critical to the project's success.","zh":"清晰的溝通對專案成功至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/critical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c35a9a90c0f99214f570","word":"criticism","forms":["criticism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cddad315e0d38996","term":"criticism","forms":["criticism","criticisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"批評；指責","explanation":"指指出某人或某事的問題、缺點的行為，或社會、公眾等提出的總體批評；重點是那一束“照向目標”的批評之光，而不是某一條單獨意見。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy has drawn widespread criticism from parents.","zh":"這項新政策受到了家長們的廣泛批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor faced criticism for ignoring the safety rules.","zh":"這名演員因無視安全規定而受到批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criticism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f2d871bab994d9b","term":"criticism","forms":["criticism","criticisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體的批評意見；評論","explanation":"指從總體批評中分出來的一條具體意見，通常詳細指出某個作品、報告或做法的問題；也可指對作品的分析性評論。","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer made one useful criticism of the report.","zh":"評論者對這份報告提出了一條有用的批評意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her main criticism concerned the study's tiny sample.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criticism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3bd933a3238b7a98bfbd","word":"criticize","forms":["criticize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9958698a25e8ff78","term":"criticize","forms":["criticize","criticizes","criticizing","criticized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"批評；指責","explanation":"把注意力放在錯誤、缺點或不當行為上，並明確表示不贊同，常常帶有責備意味。物件可以是人，也可以是決定、行為或制度。","examples":[{"en":"The coach criticized the player for ignoring the safety rules.","zh":"教練批評那名隊員無視安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several residents criticized the city for delaying the repairs.","zh":"幾位居民批評市政府拖延了維修工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criticize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-793235709a712f0c","term":"criticize","forms":["criticize","criticizes","criticizing","criticized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"評價；評論優缺點","explanation":"不只是找錯，而是認真分析某個作品、觀點或做法的長處和不足，作出有根據的評價。這裡的 criticize 不一定表示全盤否定。","examples":[{"en":"The review criticizes the film for its weak ending but praises its acting.","zh":"這篇評論指出這部電影結尾薄弱，但稱讚了它的表演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workshop teaches students to criticize paintings thoughtfully.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/criticize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02766f3002eaa501317f","word":"crocodile","forms":["crocodile"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e8f77dfe437f2e7","term":"crocodile","forms":["crocodile","crocodiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鱷魚","explanation":"指鱷科的捕食性兩棲爬行動物；日常使用中也常寬泛地指鱷目動物，包括某些近似的鱷類。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a crocodile lying beside the river.","zh":"我們看見一條鱷魚躺在河邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Crocodiles can remain still for a very long time.","zh":"鱷魚可以長時間一動不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocodile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5b94ef182047ed1","term":"crocodile","forms":["crocodile","crocodiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排成長隊的人群","explanation":"把一群人，尤其是孩子，想象成鱷魚一個接一個地向前走，因此指排成一長列、一起行進的人群。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher led a crocodile of children across the playground.","zh":"老師帶著一長隊孩子穿過操場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A crocodile of schoolchildren followed their teacher.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocodile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-375676bd26868505668f","word":"crop","forms":["crop"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93bcf4237c54e3d0","term":"crop","forms":["crop","crops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作物","explanation":"指為了收穫食物、飼料、燃料或其他經濟用途而種植的植物，例如小麥、燕麥或棉花。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers planted a new crop of wheat this spring.","zh":"農民們今年春天種了一季新的小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This crop needs plenty of sunshine and little rain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17b616496dedc159","term":"crop","forms":["crop","crops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收成","explanation":"指某種作物在某一季或某一年收穫的總量；重點從“種什麼”轉為“收了多少、收得好不好”。","examples":[{"en":"The apple crop was smaller than usual this year.","zh":"今年的蘋果收成比往年少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Last year's wheat crop exceeded all expectations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a53465e79be7f8a","term":"crop","forms":["crop","crops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裁剪後的影象","explanation":"指去掉照片或其他影象外圍部分後留下的影象，通常是為了突出主體或適應版面。","examples":[{"en":"The editor chose a tighter crop of the family photo.","zh":"編輯選用了這張家庭照片裁剪得更緊的版本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tighter crop removes the distracting background.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd70423d48b3642b","term":"crop","forms":["crop","crops","cropping","cropped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剪掉頂端","explanation":"指去掉植物或其他物體的頂部，正是“削掉最上面一段”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"The gardener cropped off the dead tips of the roses.","zh":"園丁剪掉了玫瑰花枝頂端的枯梢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener cropped the hedge to shoulder height.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46f8f722511a1798","term":"crop","forms":["crop","crops","cropping","cropped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剪短","explanation":"指把頭髮、動物的尾巴或耳朵等剪得很短；仍然是把多餘長度削掉。","examples":[{"en":"He cropped his hair short for the summer.","zh":"他把頭髮剪得很短來迎接夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cropped her hair above her ears.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61d7b3ce602e9167","term":"crop","forms":["crop","crops","cropping","cropped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裁剪影象","explanation":"指去掉照片或影象外圍的部分，使主體更突出或畫面符合需要。","examples":[{"en":"Please crop the photo so that the sign is out of the frame.","zh":"請把照片裁剪一下，讓那個標牌不出現在畫面裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Crop the photograph just below her shoulders.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3986952b145da5f0e4b","word":"cross","forms":["cross"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06f0b13204cfa955","term":"cross","forms":["cross","crosses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"十字形；交叉記號","explanation":"“cross”最基本的畫面是兩條線相交成十字形，也可以泛指這種十字形的記號。例如答題時可用它標出錯誤。","examples":[{"en":"Put a cross beside the answer you think is wrong.","zh":"在你認為錯誤的答案旁邊打一個叉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two paths form a cross in the middle of the field.","zh":"兩條小路在田地中央交叉成十字形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cross","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa11991bfbc809c2","term":"cross","forms":["cross","crosses","crossing","crossed","crossest","crossedst","crosseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穿過；越過","explanation":"從一邊移動到另一邊，通常穿過道路、河流、房間或邊界。“兩條線交叉”的畫面在這裡變成了你從一側穿到另一側。","examples":[{"en":"Look both ways before you cross the street.","zh":"過馬路前要向兩邊看看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers crossed the river before dark.","zh":"徒步旅行者在天黑前渡過了河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cross","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d916ba52b3f83d67fd25","word":"crossing","forms":["crossing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-629b58f4140c7c0d","term":"crossing","forms":["crossing","crossings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交叉處","explanation":"指道路、線路或軌道彼此交叉的地點，就像兩條線在同一點相遇。","examples":[{"en":"Turn left at the next crossing.","zh":"在下一個交叉口左轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train slowed down near the railway crossing.","zh":"火車在鐵路道口附近減速了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crossing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b89fe74e4b67988a","term":"crossing","forms":["crossing","crossings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"渡口或通行處","explanation":"指可以穿過河流、鐵路或公路的地點，重點是“從這一邊到另一邊的通道”。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers used the old bridge as a river crossing.","zh":"村民們把那座舊橋當作過河的通道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crossing closes whenever the river rises.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crossing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6912718b85f83cfc","term":"crossing","forms":["crossing","crossings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穿越","explanation":"指跨過地形、道路或某片區域這一動作或過程，突出從一側到另一側。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers began their crossing of the desert at dawn.","zh":"徒步者在黎明開始穿越沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our crossing of the Atlantic took twelve days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crossing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-851d49d3087657e97153","word":"crow","forms":["crow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eacc6233aba74d0a","term":"crow","forms":["crow","crows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烏鴉","explanation":"指一種通常羽毛深色、叫聲粗啞的鳥。它是全詞最基本的畫面，也是“鳴叫”和“誇耀”等引申義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"A crow landed on the fence and called loudly.","zh":"一隻烏鴉落在籬笆上，大聲叫了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A crow perched on the chimney pot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b4535bdd79ff9cd7894","word":"crowd","forms":["crowd"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd4bf866d5913513","term":"crowd","forms":["crowd","crowds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人群","explanation":"指許多人聚集在一起，通常擠得比較近，未必有整齊的組織。這個義項是最常見的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"A crowd gathered outside the stadium after the game.","zh":"比賽結束後，一群人聚集在體育場外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd cheered when the singer came on stage.","zh":"歌手登臺時，人群歡呼起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crowd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d71e04875b70643b","term":"crowd","forms":["crowd","crowds","crowding","crowded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擠進去；推著前進","explanation":"指人用身體或壓力向前擠，進入原本已經很滿的地方。它把“推、壓”的核心動作放在移動者身上。","examples":[{"en":"We crowded into the elevator before the doors closed.","zh":"電梯門關上前，我們擠進了電梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans crowded into the small café after the show.","zh":"演出結束後，粉絲們擠進了那家小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crowd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf858a4f18886b21","term":"crowd","forms":["crowd","crowds","crowding","crowded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聚攏；擠在一起","explanation":"指許多人聚到一起或成群移動，重點是彼此靠近，而不一定明確表示把誰塞進某處。它和名詞“人群”共享同一個“越聚越緊”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"People crowded around the street performer.","zh":"人們聚在街頭藝人周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children crowded around the magician's table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crowd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-192e8c1edd6e8052","term":"crowd","forms":["crowd","crowds","crowding","crowded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……擠進；塞滿","explanation":"指用力把太多的人或物壓進一個有限空間，常常帶有“塞得過滿”的感覺。這裡的壓力施加在賓語上。","examples":[{"en":"They crowded all the chairs into one corner.","zh":"他們把所有椅子都擠到一個角落裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children crowded themselves into the tent.","zh":"孩子們把自己都擠進了帳篷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crowd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0dcfafab5f8035e779d7","word":"crown","forms":["crown"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9557f7c13ce1739","term":"crown","forms":["crown","crowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王冠","explanation":"指君主或王室成員戴在頭上的王冠，是最直接體現權力和榮譽的“王冠”。","examples":[{"en":"The queen wore a gold crown at the ceremony.","zh":"女王在儀式上戴著一頂金王冠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crown was kept in a heavily guarded room.","zh":"這頂王冠被儲存在一間戒備森嚴的房間裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0e2c77b7946b0d9","term":"crown","forms":["crown","crowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頂部","explanation":"指某物最上面的部分，因為王冠戴在頭頂，所以 crown 可以表示物體的頂部或頂端。","examples":[{"en":"Snow covered the crown of the mountain.","zh":"積雪覆蓋了山頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small flag stood at the crown of the tower.","zh":"塔頂立著一面小旗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17d3a0a3548dc33b","term":"crown","forms":["crown","crowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牙冠","explanation":"指牙齦以上、露在口腔中的牙齒部分；它是牙齒最上方的部分，就像牙齒的王冠。","examples":[{"en":"The dentist examined the crown of each tooth.","zh":"牙醫檢查了每顆牙齒的牙冠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Acid can damage the crown of a tooth.","zh":"酸會損傷牙齒的牙冠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-889eb372b29a7cbf","term":"crown","forms":["crown","crowns","crowning","crowned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式宣佈為君主","explanation":"指透過正式儀式宣佈某人為國王、女王或皇帝等。","examples":[{"en":"They crowned the young prince during a solemn ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The archbishop crowned her queen before the assembled nobles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26dd7517f5ecee31f5df","word":"crucial","forms":["crucial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e21fbdef80a467b","term":"crucial","forms":["crucial","more crucial","most crucial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"至關重要的；決定性的","explanation":"形容某人、某事或某個時刻對結果、計劃或未來起決定作用，缺少它就可能改變最終走向。它就像分岔路口的關鍵路標：一旦選錯，後面的方向也會不同。","examples":[{"en":"Good communication is crucial to a successful team.","zh":"良好的溝通對團隊取得成功至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her advice was crucial in helping me make the decision.","zh":"她的建議對幫助我作出這個決定起了關鍵作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crucial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3ccedf562d9529001d8","word":"crude","forms":["crude"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e53deb5350a7086","term":"crude","forms":["crude","cruder","crudest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未經加工的","explanation":"指物質仍處於天然狀態，沒有經過提煉、處理或精製。這是 crude 最基礎的意思，重點是“還沒有被加工好”。","examples":[{"en":"Crude oil must be refined before it can be used in cars.","zh":"原油必須經過精煉後才能用於汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers built a crude bridge from wooden boards.","zh":"村民用木板搭了一座簡陋的橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e238f55b5c711e1","term":"crude","forms":["crude","cruder","crudest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粗糙簡陋的","explanation":"從“沒有加工”進一步引申為做得簡單、粗糙，缺少熟練技巧或精細設計。它可以形容工具、建築、方法或作品。","examples":[{"en":"They used a crude map to find their way through the forest.","zh":"他們靠一張粗略的地圖穿過了森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His first machine was crude but surprisingly effective.","zh":"他的第一臺機器很粗糙，但出奇地有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4ca32d7b0dbfc0fe269","word":"cruel","forms":["cruel"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f93521b223dd93f","term":"cruel","forms":["cruel","crueler","crueller","more cruel","cruelest","cruellest","most cruel"],"pos":"adj","zh":"殘忍的；無情的","explanation":"指明知會給別人造成痛苦，卻仍然這樣做，或對痛苦毫不在意；這種“硬冷無情”是 cruel 的核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"It was cruel of him to leave the injured dog outside.","zh":"他把受傷的狗留在外面，實在太殘忍了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cruel bully laughed while the younger boy cried.","zh":"那個殘忍的惡霸在小男孩哭泣時還大笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cruel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f32b555455866ebd","term":"cruel","forms":["cruel","crueler","crueller","more cruel","cruelest","cruellest","most cruel"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴酷的；難熬的","explanation":"把“無情地讓人受苦”的感覺用於天氣、環境、命運或經歷，表示它們異常嚴厲、艱難，並不一定涉及有意傷害人的人。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers lost their crops after a cruel winter.","zh":"經過一個嚴酷的冬天，農民們的莊稼都損失了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cruel winter left many families hungry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cruel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7dca86b841d087fe91a0","word":"cruelty","forms":["cruelty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c236619fcf545ebe","term":"cruelty","forms":["cruelty","cruelties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殘忍；殘酷","explanation":"指對別人的痛苦漠不關心，或主動讓別人受苦的殘忍態度和行為。這是 cruelty 最常見的抽象意義，重點在一種持續或總體的殘酷性，而不是某一次單獨的事件。","examples":[{"en":"The report exposed the cruelty of the guards toward the prisoners.","zh":"這份報告揭露了看守對囚犯的殘酷行徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is no excuse for cruelty to animals.","zh":"虐待動物沒有任何藉口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cruelty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e76bbd638d9b00a","term":"cruelty","forms":["cruelty","cruelties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殘酷行為；暴行","explanation":"指一件具體的殘酷行為，也就是把抽象的 cruelty 落實為一個可單獨指出的事件。複數 cruelties 則表示多件殘酷行為或一連串暴行。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers remembered the cruelties committed during the war.","zh":"村民們記得戰爭期間發生的種種暴行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Witnesses described terrible cruelties committed against the prisoners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cruelty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fddbb38a8c0c18b628a0","word":"cruise","forms":["cruise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b469ba28737f6112","term":"cruise","forms":["cruise","cruises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乘船遊覽","explanation":"指乘船在海上或湖上旅行，尤其是為了休閒娛樂而進行的航行；重點是“悠閒地向前航行”這一畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We went on a cruise around the Greek islands.","zh":"我們乘船遊覽了希臘群島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are planning a cruise down the river this summer.","zh":"他們計劃今年夏天乘船沿河遊覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cruise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a0134c5c588afd2","term":"cruise","forms":["cruise","cruises","cruising","cruised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"乘船遊覽","explanation":"指為了休閒而乘船航行，或在水上悠閒地航行；這是“平穩向前移動”這一核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"We cruised along the coast all afternoon.","zh":"我們整個下午都沿著海岸悠閒航行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They cruised around the bay in a small boat.","zh":"他們乘小船在海灣裡四處遊覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cruise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0eaa452a864c304a6c96","word":"crunchy","forms":["crunchy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a9e4398ea40b8828","term":"crunchy","forms":["crunchy","crunchier","crunchiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"脆的；吃起來咔嚓作響的","explanation":"指食物等咬起來會發出清脆聲響，重點是實際的口感和聲音，而不只是“硬”。例如新鮮生菜、脆餅可能都可以用這個詞描述。","examples":[{"en":"The fresh carrots are sweet and crunchy.","zh":"這些新鮮胡蘿蔔又甜又脆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I added some crunchy onions to the sandwich.","zh":"我在三明治里加了一些脆洋蔥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crunchy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3d15d80780ac6dc","term":"crunchy","forms":["crunchy","crunchier","crunchiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"崇尚自然健康的；樸素環保的","explanation":"形容人、地方或生活方式重視自然、健康、環保和樸素生活。這是從天然、脆麥片等食品的形象引申出來的俚語義，常常帶一點輕鬆或調侃色彩。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents are quite crunchy and grow most of their own food.","zh":"她的父母很崇尚自然，自己種了大部分食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their crunchy lifestyle includes composting and homemade soap.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crunchy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-daecc0bd2864ecc50093","word":"crush","forms":["crush"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fe610534c42b4dda","term":"crush","forms":["crush","crushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強力擠壓或撞擊","explanation":"指猛烈的撞擊、擠壓，或這種力量造成的損壞、毀壞；重點是東西被外力壓得變形或受損。","examples":[{"en":"The accident left him with a crush injury to his leg.","zh":"這起事故使他的腿受到擠壓傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His ribs hurt after the crush against the barrier.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dedab0a0827ab53","term":"crush","forms":["crush","crushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擁擠和擠壓","explanation":"指移動的人群帶來的強烈擠壓，強調人被擠在一起、幾乎沒有活動空間。","examples":[{"en":"We were caught in the crush outside the stadium.","zh":"我們被困在體育場外擁擠的人群中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We lost each other in the crush near the exit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aebbe703e6ca1f0c","term":"crush","forms":["crush","crushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"單戀物件","explanation":"指自己迷戀但尚未交往、通常也未必得到回應的人；這個意思來自“心裡被某人壓住、佔滿了空間”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"I have a crush on someone in my history class.","zh":"我暗戀歷史課上的一個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her old crush sent her a message yesterday.","zh":"她以前暗戀的人昨天給她發了訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68d501cb1d618dd7","term":"crush","forms":["crush","crushes","crushing","crushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓碎或擠變形","explanation":"指用兩個硬物之間的壓力把東西壓壞、擠扁或壓成一團，是全詞最基本的動作畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Crush the garlic before adding it to the pan.","zh":"把大蒜壓碎後再放進鍋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heavy box crushed the flowers.","zh":"沉重的箱子把花壓壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5faa222b8f32815a","term":"crush","forms":["crush","crushes","crushing","crushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"以壓力壓倒","explanation":"引申為用強大力量、優勢或壓力徹底壓倒某人或某個組織，像把對方壓得無法反抗。","examples":[{"en":"The home team crushed its rivals 5–0.","zh":"主隊以五比零徹底擊敗了對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The news crushed her hopes of returning home.","zh":"這個訊息徹底打碎了她回家的希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27d7ada5e344cd43","term":"crush","forms":["crush","crushes","crushing","crushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暗戀","explanation":"表示對某人產生迷戀或單戀，彷彿心思被對方壓住、佔滿；通常暗含兩人尚未交往。","examples":[{"en":"She's been crushing on her neighbor for months.","zh":"她暗戀鄰居已經好幾個月了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I think he has a crush on you.","zh":"我覺得他暗戀你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74abd8c158701f5d118b","word":"crutch","forms":["crutch"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1cd64cdf02143018","term":"crutch","forms":["crutch","crutches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"柺杖","explanation":"幫助人行走、支撐身體並減輕受傷腿部負擔的器具，通常是腋下柺杖。","examples":[{"en":"She had to walk on crutches after she injured her ankle.","zh":"她腳踝受傷後不得不拄柺杖走路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse showed him how to adjust the crutches.","zh":"護士教他怎樣調節柺杖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crutch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aab09e33aea821df","term":"crutch","forms":["crutch","crutches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"依賴性的支撐物","explanation":"指在困難中提供心理或實際支援的人或事物，常暗示這種依賴是不健康的，甚至讓人無法獨立。","examples":[{"en":"He used video games as a crutch whenever he felt stressed.","zh":"他每當感到壓力大時，就把電子遊戲當作逃避的依賴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her friends helped her without becoming a crutch.","zh":"她的朋友幫助了她，卻沒有讓她形成依賴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crutch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58a69b8bb1f5e666c354","word":"cry","forms":["cry"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65e10f54fe8c1054","term":"cry","forms":["cry","cries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"哭泣；一陣眼淚","explanation":"指流淚這件事，或一次因悲傷、憤怒等情緒而哭泣的經歷。它仍然保留了“情緒向外湧出”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"After the breakup, she went home for a good cry.","zh":"分手後，她回家痛痛快快地哭了一場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A good cry helped her release the tension.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec03cd0e23bbc308","term":"cry","forms":["cry","cries","crying","cried","cryed","criest","cryest","criedst","cryedst","crieth","cryeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"哭；流淚","explanation":"指因悲傷、疼痛、憤怒等而流淚或哭泣，是“情緒向外湧出”最直接的表現。","examples":[{"en":"The film always makes me cry.","zh":"這部電影總是讓我哭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He cried over the unfair decision.","zh":"他為那個不公平的決定哭了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63f5f513fea56b71","term":"cry","forms":["cry","cries","crying","cried","cryed","criest","cryest","criedst","cryedst","crieth","cryeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喊叫；尖叫","explanation":"指發出響亮、強烈的聲音，可以是喊、叫或尖叫；它和哭泣一樣，都是把強烈情緒或訊號衝向外界。","examples":[{"en":"She cried out when she touched the hot pan.","zh":"她碰到熱鍋時尖叫了一聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child cried for help from the upstairs window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60a0f78b507f6249a6e2","word":"crystal","forms":["crystal"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98c1eb6097a39d4f","term":"crystal","forms":["crystal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非常清楚的","explanation":"像透過透明水晶一樣一眼看清；可形容表達、解釋或意思非常清楚、明白。","examples":[{"en":"Her instructions were crystal clear.","zh":"她的說明清楚得沒有任何歧義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"“Do you understand?” “Crystal.”","zh":"“你明白了嗎？”“完全明白。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crystal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ec6a600311f2b7a","term":"crystal","forms":["crystal","crystals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"晶體","explanation":"指內部原子或分子按規則、週期性方式排列的固體；水晶就是日常可見的一類晶體。這個義項連線了“堅硬、像冰一樣透亮、結構整齊”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The salt formed small crystals as the water evaporated.","zh":"水分蒸發後，鹽形成了小晶體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists examined the crystal structure of the mineral.","zh":"科學家研究了這種礦物的晶體結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crystal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50f610210b17093bef6a","word":"cub","forms":["cub"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aee01a4fee16f3a4","term":"cub","forms":["cub","cubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大型食肉動物的幼崽","explanation":"指熊、狼、狐、獅、虎等大型食肉動物的幼崽，核心形象就是“還沒長大的小獸”。","examples":[{"en":"The lion cub stayed close to its mother.","zh":"那隻獅子幼崽一直緊挨著母獅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw two bear cubs near the river.","zh":"我們在河邊看到了兩隻熊幼崽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d58d1a43b603dfb7","term":"cub","forms":["cub","Cubs","cubs","CUBs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"童子軍成員","explanation":"指參加童子軍幼年組的成員；這裡的cub沿用了“幼小成員”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"Her son became a Cub last year.","zh":"她的兒子去年加入了童子軍幼年組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cubs practiced tying knots at their weekly meeting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f3c4172a4fe308cebc8","word":"cube","forms":["cube"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76a7de69316313c9","term":"cube","forms":["cube","cubes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立方體","explanation":"六個面完全相同、每個面都是正方形的立體圖形；寬、長和高相等的盒子就是直觀例子。","examples":[{"en":"The students built a cube from six square pieces of cardboard.","zh":"學生用六塊正方形紙板拼出了一個立方體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child stacked a red cube on a blue one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cube","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2731d0aff1e4ff9","term":"cube","forms":["cube","cubes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"三次方","explanation":"一個數、數值或表示式連續乘自己兩次所得的結果；例如 2 的三次方是 8。","examples":[{"en":"The cube of four is sixty-four.","zh":"四的三次方是六十四。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cube of three is twenty-seven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cube","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eeb779070640837d","term":"cube","forms":["cube","cubes","cubing","cubed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"求三次方","explanation":"把一個數連續乘自己兩次，求出它的三次方；例如把 3 變成 27。","examples":[{"en":"Cube five and then add two to the result.","zh":"先求五的三次方，再把結果加二。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cube three to obtain twenty-seven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cube","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd832404e8eeb90793f0","word":"cucumber","forms":["cucumber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a43428fccf5ab683","term":"cucumber","forms":["cucumber","cucumbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黃瓜植株","explanation":"指黃瓜這種藤本植物本身，而不是它摘下來的果實；這裡關注的是會生長、開花並結出黃瓜的整株植物。","examples":[{"en":"We planted cucumbers along the fence.","zh":"我們沿著籬笆種了幾株黃瓜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tie the cucumber to a stake as it grows.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cucumber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-123c96ba73d381b6","term":"cucumber","forms":["cucumber","cucumbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黃瓜果實","explanation":"指黃瓜藤結出的綠色、清脆、可以食用的果實，既可以是一整根，也可以是切片或作為菜餚的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"I sliced a cucumber for the salad.","zh":"我切了一根黃瓜做沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cucumber in our garden grew longer than my forearm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cucumber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14da5d70daaa665ecfed","word":"cue","forms":["cue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1942bc9bd6ffc50b","term":"cue","forms":["cue","cues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動訊號","explanation":"cue 是一個訊號，告訴某人該開始做某事、改變做法或進入下一步。它可以來自人的動作、事件或環境變化。","examples":[{"en":"The lights going off were our cue to leave.","zh":"燈熄滅就是我們該離開的訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"When the music starts, that is your cue to begin.","zh":"音樂一響，就是你開始的訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d950704f4ebfc45","term":"cue","forms":["cue","cues","cueing","cuing","cued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給出提示","explanation":"cue 作動詞時，是向某人發訊號，讓對方開始說話、行動或進入下一環節。","examples":[{"en":"The director cued the actors to start the scene.","zh":"導演示意演員開始這一場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cue the lights when the singer raises her hand.","zh":"歌手抬手時就給燈光發訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2753cb15f1d6d34c2d6e","word":"cuisine","forms":["cuisine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af3fd541c21b1629","term":"cuisine","forms":["cuisine","cuisines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烹飪風格","explanation":"指某個地方、民族或群體形成的有代表性的烹飪方式和風格，通常包括常用食材、調味和做法等整體特點。","examples":[{"en":"Japanese cuisine is known for its fresh ingredients and delicate flavors.","zh":"日本料理以新鮮食材和細膩的味道聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant specializes in traditional coastal cuisine.","zh":"這家餐廳專門供應傳統的沿海菜系。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cuisine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a2eb4fa691708ef","term":"cuisine","forms":["cuisine","cuisines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"菜系食物","explanation":"指按照某種烹飪風格做出來的食物總稱；這裡關注的是一類菜餚，而不是形成這類菜餚的方法本身。","examples":[{"en":"We tried several kinds of Middle Eastern cuisine during our trip.","zh":"旅行期間，我們嘗試了好幾種中東菜系。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sampled regional cuisine at the night market.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cuisine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f1fd9f37ede108fb49f","word":"cultivate","forms":["cultivate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e19463617cca547","term":"cultivate","forms":["cultivate","cultivates","cultivating","cultivated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"種植；耕作","explanation":"指耕種土地、種植作物，使其能夠生長並收穫。這是 cultivate 最直接、最原始的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Most farmers in this region cultivate maize.","zh":"這個地區的大多數農民都種植玉米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family cultivates a small plot behind the house.","zh":"這家人在房子後面耕種一小塊地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cultivate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-259b5f1f1dbb899d","term":"cultivate","forms":["cultivate","cultivates","cultivating","cultivated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"培養；培育","explanation":"指有意識地投入時間和精力，使興趣、能力、習慣或關係逐漸形成和發展。它和培育作物的畫面相同，只是物件換成了抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher used games to cultivate an interest in reading.","zh":"老師用遊戲培養學生對閱讀的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has worked hard to cultivate strong relationships with her clients.","zh":"她一直努力與客戶培養牢固的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cultivate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e2215a75ae991148f95","word":"cultural","forms":["cultural"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71810e9d5ba26164","term":"cultural","forms":["cultural","more cultural","most cultural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"文化的；與文化有關的","explanation":"指屬於文化領域，或與一個群體的藝術、習俗、思想、身份認同等有關。它強調“文化留下的印記”，範圍比單指傳統習俗更廣。","examples":[{"en":"The festival has great cultural importance for the local community.","zh":"這個節日對當地社群具有重要的文化意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum explores the cultural history of the region.","zh":"這家博物館探討這個地區的文化歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cultural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1947f79fdfb80461509","word":"culture","forms":["culture"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c235a209dbc657b","term":"culture","forms":["culture","cultures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文化；社會生活方式","explanation":"culture 是一個社會或群體長期培育出來的整體生活方式，包括藝術、習俗、背景和日常習慣。它既可以指全人類的文化，也可以指某個國家、地區或群體的文化。","examples":[{"en":"Every culture has its own ways of celebrating important events.","zh":"每種文化都有自己慶祝重大事件的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Traveling helps people understand cultures different from their own.","zh":"旅行有助於人們理解與自己不同的文化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/culture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-261abceab933b09b","term":"culture","forms":["culture","cultures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信念與價值觀體系","explanation":"這裡的 culture 更具體地指一個人民族或社群共同的信念、價值觀、行為方式以及物質生活，強調“人們怎樣生活和看待世界”。","examples":[{"en":"The company is trying to build a culture of trust.","zh":"這家公司正在努力建立一種信任文化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company's culture rewards cooperation over individual competition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/culture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2dfda8e4279bdadbcdfc","word":"cumulative","forms":["cumulative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-835132a5ef984849","term":"cumulative","forms":["cumulative","more cumulative","most cumulative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"累計的；合計至今的","explanation":"指計算某一時點的結果時，把截至該時點的當前資料和以前的資料全部包括進去。重點是“前面的也沒有丟掉”，例如累計銷售額會不斷加入新的銷售資料。","examples":[{"en":"The chart shows the cumulative number of visitors since January.","zh":"這張圖顯示了自一月以來的累計訪客人數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her cumulative score was high enough to win the scholarship.","zh":"她的累計分數高到足以贏得獎學金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cumulative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd41f9e97c862dcb","term":"cumulative","forms":["cumulative","more cumulative","most cumulative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"逐次加成形成的","explanation":"指某個結果不是一次產生的，而是由一系列連續的增加逐步形成。它和前一義都圍繞“把每一次新增接到已有部分上”，但這裡更強調形成過程或最終效果。","examples":[{"en":"The cumulative effect of small delays made us miss the train.","zh":"許多小延誤累積起來，導致我們沒趕上火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course offers cumulative benefits as students practice each week.","zh":"學生每週練習，這門課程的益處會逐步累積。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cumulative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2acaebc6830e176af15e","word":"cunning","forms":["cunning"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20743a74752cbccc","term":"cunning","forms":["cunning","more cunning","most cunning"],"pos":"adj","zh":"狡猾機靈的","explanation":"形容人或行為很會暗中謀劃，用不顯眼或不誠實的辦法達到目的；既有“聰明”的成分，也常帶“不光明正大”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The cunning thief distracted the guard before taking the jewels.","zh":"那個狡猾的竊賊先分散警衛的注意力，然後偷走了珠寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She came up with a cunning plan to avoid paying the fee.","zh":"她想出了一個巧妙而帶有算計的計劃來逃避付費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cunning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76e9124c89016b84","term":"cunning","forms":["cunning","cunnings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巧計；詭計","explanation":"指把技巧用於隱秘或欺騙性的辦法，藉此操縱別人、取得利益或解決問題；這是“有能力”進一步變成“會耍手段”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"He escaped the trap by using cunning rather than force.","zh":"他沒有靠武力，而是靠詭計逃出了陷阱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fox used its cunning to steal food from the camp.","zh":"狐狸利用自己的狡猾從營地偷走了食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cunning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6171781d65f3ccce113","word":"cup","forms":["cup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10182b727860bb23","term":"cup","forms":["cup","cups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飲水杯","explanation":"指通常有柄、內部凹進去、用來喝水或飲料的杯子；這個意思最直接體現了“像杯子一樣承接”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She poured hot tea into the cup and waited for it to cool.","zh":"她把熱茶倒進杯子裡，等它涼下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a small cup beside each plate.","zh":"每個盤子旁邊都有一個小杯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3f401a5edc7a92c","term":"cup","forms":["cup","cups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一杯的內容物","explanation":"也可以指杯子裡裝著的飲料或其他內容物，重點從凹形容器轉移到了它所承接的東西。","examples":[{"en":"I had a cup of coffee before leaving home.","zh":"我出門前喝了一杯咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like another cup of soup?","zh":"你想再來一碗湯嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8781277bfb33e9ac","term":"cup","forms":["cup","cups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美國杯量單位","explanation":"在美國習慣用法中，指一種烹飪和飲料配方常用的容量單位；具體容量會因測量體系和語境而異。","examples":[{"en":"Add one cup of rice and two cups of water to the pot.","zh":"往鍋里加入一杯米和兩杯水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe calls for half a cup of sugar.","zh":"這個食譜需要半杯糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-928ae8cdaf7937ae8a8b","word":"cupboard","forms":["cupboard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23a7c3fdb5b6636f","term":"cupboard","forms":["cupboard","cupboards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"櫥櫃；壁櫃","explanation":"指有架層、用來收放炊具、餐具或食物的櫃子，也可泛指存放其他物品的類似櫃櫥。這是現代最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I put the clean plates back in the cupboard.","zh":"我把乾淨的盤子放回櫥櫃裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a jar of rice in the cupboard.","zh":"櫥櫃裡有一罐米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cupboard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c1fd92053dc3bc19c25","word":"curb","forms":["curb"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9059b83ba5f58c8","term":"curb","forms":["curb","curbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"路緣石","explanation":"指道路和人行道交界處凸起的邊緣，通常由混凝土等材料製成，用來分隔並保護兩邊。","examples":[{"en":"Please park close to the curb, but don't block the driveway.","zh":"請把車停在路緣石旁，但不要擋住車道入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bicycle hit the curb and the rider fell.","zh":"腳踏車撞上了路緣石，騎車人摔倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db6ddd9cfcd812dc","term":"curb","forms":["curb","curbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制；約束","explanation":"指能擋住或壓住某種行為、力量或發展勢頭的東西，既可以是規則，也可以是自我控制或外部壓力。","examples":[{"en":"Higher taxes were introduced as a curb on reckless spending.","zh":"提高稅收是為了遏制不負責任的消費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Self-discipline can be a useful curb on anger.","zh":"自律可以有效抑制憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7aadced757b8eca6","term":"curb","forms":["curb","curbs","curbing","curbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抑制；控制","explanation":"指把某種行為、情緒、力量或發展勢頭壓住，使它不再繼續擴大；核心形象就是在它前面設一道“擋邊”。","examples":[{"en":"The new rules are meant to curb online fraud.","zh":"新規定旨在遏制網路詐騙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a deep breath to curb her anger.","zh":"她深吸了一口氣來壓住怒火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15152e5a69166f0958db","word":"cure","forms":["cure"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-778febe86ebc2175","term":"cure","forms":["cure","cures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"治療方法；療法；藥物","explanation":"指能把疾病或健康問題治好的方法、裝置或藥物，重點是它有望帶來恢復，而不只是暫時緩解。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are still looking for a cure for the disease.","zh":"科學家仍在尋找這種疾病的療法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new drug may provide a cure for some patients.","zh":"這種新藥可能會治好一些患者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e65159c5afc015c","term":"cure","forms":["cure","cures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"治癒；痊癒","explanation":"指疾病或傷勢被消除、身體恢復健康這一過程或結果，核心仍是從壞狀態回到正常狀態。","examples":[{"en":"There is no quick cure for a serious injury.","zh":"嚴重傷勢沒有快速的治癒辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rest and time were the only cure for his exhaustion.","zh":"休息和時間是他疲憊狀態唯一的療愈辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26f015dad3fd3994","term":"cure","forms":["cure","cures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解決辦法","explanation":"在比喻意義上，cure 是能消除某個困難、壞習慣或社會問題的辦法，就像治病一樣把問題處理掉。","examples":[{"en":"There is no easy cure for loneliness.","zh":"孤獨沒有簡單的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise can be a good cure for stress.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以是緩解壓力的好辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fa3843d2962ea0b","term":"cure","forms":["cure","cures","curing","cured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"治好；使恢復健康","explanation":"指透過治療或其他辦法使某人從疾病、傷勢或不適中恢復健康，直接體現“把壞狀態處理回正常”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The treatment cured her completely.","zh":"這種治療徹底治好了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor cured him of the infection.","zh":"醫生治好了他的感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d9987591ed42267","term":"cure","forms":["cure","cures","curing","cured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消除疾病或不良影響","explanation":"指使一種疾病、症狀或其不良後果結束；賓語可以是疾病本身，而不只是患病的人。","examples":[{"en":"This medicine can cure the infection.","zh":"這種藥能治好感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing seemed to cure his constant headaches.","zh":"似乎沒有什麼能消除他持續的頭痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19a1ac64d330d833a4e8","word":"curfew","forms":["curfew"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7cc7a26f037794d","term":"curfew","forms":["curfew","curfews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宵禁規定","explanation":"指要求人們在規定時間前離開街道、回到家中，或在規定時間後不得外出的制度。它把“晚上蓋住城市的活動”變成一條正式規定。","examples":[{"en":"The city imposed a curfew after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，該市實行了宵禁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Teenagers under sixteen must be home before the curfew.","zh":"十六歲以下的青少年必須在宵禁時間前回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curfew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e37abbb0e918ffad","term":"curfew","forms":["curfew","curfews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宵禁開始的時間","explanation":"指宵禁規定正式開始的那個時刻，而不是整條規定本身。比如規定晚上十點後不得外出，晚上十點就是 curfew。","examples":[{"en":"We need to get back to the hotel before curfew.","zh":"我們得在宵禁時間前回到酒店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be home before curfew at ten.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curfew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8950aeb7bd2ed1fa44e3","word":"curiosity","forms":["curiosity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bb59dbb290ddfa6","term":"curiosity","forms":["curiosity","curiosities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"好奇心","explanation":"指因為某事陌生、有趣或難以解釋，而想透過提問、觀察和調查把它弄明白的心理傾向。它強調主動探索，而不只是覺得事情奇怪。","examples":[{"en":"She opened the old box with curiosity.","zh":"她帶著好奇心開啟了那個舊盒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Out of curiosity, I asked how the machine worked.","zh":"我出於好奇，問了問這臺機器是怎麼運轉的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curiosity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c73445c724229af","term":"curiosity","forms":["curiosity","curiosities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"稀奇物件","explanation":"指因為外形、來源或用途特別而引起人們興趣的獨特物件。它就像把“吸引好奇心的東西”本身單獨拿出來命名。","examples":[{"en":"The shop was filled with curiosities from around the world.","zh":"那家店裡擺滿了來自世界各地的稀奇物件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop displayed mechanical curiosities from Victorian workshops.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curiosity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9e7a8af89a3e21f6b9e","word":"curious","forms":["curious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-416f51058f42ee3a","term":"curious","forms":["curious","more curious","curiouser","most curious","curiousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好奇的；求知的","explanation":"形容一個人想提問、瞭解或親自探索某件事，通常強調積極的求知慾；在特定語境中也可能暗示打聽過多、侵犯隱私。","examples":[{"en":"Young children are naturally curious about the world.","zh":"幼兒天生對世界充滿好奇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m curious to know what happened next.","zh":"我很好奇接下來發生了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d77672a30959b2c","term":"curious","forms":["curious","more curious","curiouser","most curious","curiousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇特的；不同尋常的","explanation":"形容某人或某物與通常情況不同，奇特到會讓人想追問或進一步觀察；它和“好奇”這條主線相連，因為奇特的事物會引起好奇。","examples":[{"en":"We found a curious mark on the old door.","zh":"我們在那扇舊門上發現了一個奇特的標記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A curious silence followed the announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-427e4b79b1f0fc90306c","word":"curl","forms":["curl"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6d278e0bae5de2b","term":"curl","forms":["curl","curls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捲髮；捲曲的一縷","explanation":"指頭髮彎成的卷或一縷捲髮，是“彎曲成卷”這個核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"A curl fell across her cheek.","zh":"一縷捲髮垂到了她的臉頰上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dark curl escaped from beneath her hat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f342ca8ec7defddb","term":"curl","forms":["curl","curls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彎曲的線條或形狀","explanation":"指畫面、裝飾或物體上的弧形線條，也就是直線彎起來後留下的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The vine made a graceful curl around the window.","zh":"藤蔓沿著窗邊形成了一道優美的弧線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A curl of smoke rose from the chimney.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91967617e360cd24","term":"curl","forms":["curl","curls","curling","curled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使沿弧線運動","explanation":"指讓球或其他物體不走直線，而是沿著弧線移動；這是把“彎曲”延伸到運動軌跡上。","examples":[{"en":"She curled the ball around the defender and into the net.","zh":"她讓球繞過防守隊員，沿弧線飛進了球網。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A gust curled the drifting smoke back toward the windows.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2a7cc8213683ff6","term":"curl","forms":["curl","curls","curling","curled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使捲曲或盤旋","explanation":"指把頭髮、身體或其他東西弄成卷狀或螺旋狀。","examples":[{"en":"She curled the ribbon into a neat spiral.","zh":"她把絲帶捲成了整齊的螺旋形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She curled the ribbon with the edge of her scissors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ba72c5de18e6bee","term":"curl","forms":["curl","curls","curling","curled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"呈捲曲狀","explanation":"指嘴唇、煙霧、植物等自身呈現出彎曲或捲起的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The corner of his mouth curled into a faint smile.","zh":"他的嘴角捲起一絲淡淡的笑意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dry leaves curled at the edges.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-466e5b9cd57fa444ccea","word":"currency","forms":["currency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99818dc6dd5eaff4","term":"currency","forms":["currency","currencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貨幣；交易媒介","explanation":"指買賣雙方普遍接受、用來交換商品或服務的錢，也可以指錢以外的交換媒介。重點不只是“錢”，而是“能夠在交易中流通並被認可的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The euro is the currency used in many European countries.","zh":"歐元是許多歐洲國家使用的貨幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In some villages, goods are still exchanged without using currency.","zh":"在一些村莊，人們仍然不用貨幣交換商品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/currency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c1efa2838e74258","term":"currency","forms":["currency","currencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流行；通行；被接受","explanation":"引申指某種詞語、觀點或說法在群體中被廣泛使用和認可，就像貨幣在人群中流通一樣。它強調的是社會上的通行程度，不一定表示這個觀點正確。","examples":[{"en":"The term gained currency after the new technology became popular.","zh":"這項新技術流行起來後，這個術語也變得通用了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theory gained currency among younger scholars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/currency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97b0560280ed60a5a1ea","word":"current","forms":["current"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-819965625287a330","term":"current","forms":["current","currenter","more current","currentest","most current"],"pos":"adj","zh":"當前的；現時的","explanation":"指現在正在發生、存在或適用的事情，重點是時間上“就在目前”。它像一股正在向前流的水，所處的就是當前這一段。","examples":[{"en":"We need to understand the current situation before making a decision.","zh":"我們需要先了解當前情況，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is happy with her current job.","zh":"她對目前的工作很滿意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/current","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6766d1f8840f37f0","term":"current","forms":["current","currenter","more current","currentest","most current"],"pos":"adj","zh":"現行的；通行的","explanation":"指在某個時期被普遍接受、使用或實行的東西。它從“正在流通”引申出“大家都在採用、認可”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The current policy does not cover this type of expense.","zh":"現行政策不涵蓋這類費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This view is still current among many experts.","zh":"許多專家仍然認可這種觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/current","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8acfbf264cbf04dd","term":"current","forms":["current","currents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流體的流動","explanation":"指氣體或液體持續朝某個方向移動的現象，例如空氣流動或地幔中的對流。這裡 current 就是“不斷向前流”的東西本身。","examples":[{"en":"A strong current of air came through the open window.","zh":"一股強勁的氣流從開著的窗戶吹了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experiment shows how heat moves through the liquid current.","zh":"這項實驗顯示了熱量如何透過液體流動傳播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/current","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7379826c42a7794c","term":"current","forms":["current","currents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電流","explanation":"指電荷單位時間內的流動量，也就是電路中電流的大小。它把“流動”的形象轉到了電荷上，雖然看不見，卻仍可測量。","examples":[{"en":"The device shuts off when the electric current becomes too strong.","zh":"電流過強時，這臺裝置會自動關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This wire can carry a large current safely.","zh":"這根電線可以安全地承載較大的電流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/current","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d54eb7dce184bf90f597","word":"curriculum","forms":["curriculum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25a19ddd42d0be51","term":"curriculum","forms":["curriculum","curricula","curriculums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學校提供的課程體系","explanation":"在美國英語中，curriculum 常指一所學校或大學為學生提供的整套課程、作業內容和教學安排，而不是其中某一門課。","examples":[{"en":"The university revised its curriculum to include more courses on data science.","zh":"這所大學修改了課程體系，增加了更多資料科學課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parents want the school curriculum to give students more time for music and art.","zh":"家長希望學校課程體系能給學生更多學習音樂和美術的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curriculum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77173416101a2937","term":"curriculum","forms":["curriculum","curricula","curriculums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統一規定的教學內容","explanation":"在英國、加拿大和澳大利亞等英語用法中，curriculum 還常指教育部門規定學校必須教給所有學生的知識、技能和標準，重點不只是某校自己開設什麼課。","examples":[{"en":"All primary schools must follow the national curriculum in science and mathematics.","zh":"所有小學都必須遵循國家規定的科學和數學課程標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The national curriculum now includes basic programming.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curriculum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b8e0d9bc8319e36a0da","word":"curry","forms":["curry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08337b0f5b4bf540","term":"curry","forms":["curry","curries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咖哩菜","explanation":"以香料濃醬調味的一類菜餚，通常與南亞飲食聯絡在一起；這裡既可以指整道菜，也可以泛指這一類菜。","examples":[{"en":"We had chicken curry with rice for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐吃了雞肉咖哩配米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This restaurant makes a mild vegetable curry.","zh":"這家餐館做溫和不辣的蔬菜咖哩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-53422065450f754912fc","word":"curse","forms":["curse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22a8c9d8c6a955af","term":"curse","forms":["curse","curses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"超自然的禍害","explanation":"指被認為會給某人或某物帶來厄運、傷害或阻礙的超自然力量或狀態；重點是“降下來的禍害”，不只是說出的一句話。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers believed that a curse had fallen on the old house.","zh":"村民們相信那座老房子中了詛咒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witch placed a curse on the king's family.","zh":"女巫對國王一家施了詛咒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69b1775a9df2deda","term":"curse","forms":["curse","curses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詛咒禱告","explanation":"指祈求神靈或超自然力量傷害某人的話語或行為；它強調“發出讓對方遭殃的願望”，不一定表示詛咒真的生效。","examples":[{"en":"In the story, the queen's curse brought misfortune to anyone who betrayed her.","zh":"故事裡，王后的詛咒會給任何背叛她的人帶來厄運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witch uttered a curse over the stolen jewels.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f6c4247e992fffa","term":"curse","forms":["curse","curses","cursing","cursed","curst"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對……施詛咒","explanation":"表示把超自然的禍害施加到某人、某物或某個地方上，重點是“讓物件承受詛咒”。","examples":[{"en":"The sorcerer cursed the village and its fields.","zh":"巫師詛咒了這個村莊和它的田地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witch cursed the prince to sleep for years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e7a73435856236e","term":"curse","forms":["curse","curses","cursing","cursed","curst"],"pos":"verb","zh":"祈求降禍於","explanation":"表示呼求神靈或超自然力量傷害某人；它可以只是憤怒的詛咒，也可以是宗教或傳說中的正式行為。","examples":[{"en":"The old man cursed the thieves who had stolen his horse.","zh":"老人詛咒了偷走他馬的那些賊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witch cursed anyone who opened the forbidden chest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05e884950dccb9aad080","word":"curtain","forms":["curtain"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b965683af0ab377","term":"curtain","forms":["curtain","curtains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"窗簾；簾子","explanation":"指掛在窗戶、床鋪等處，用來擋光、遮擋視線或保護隱私的布簾。這是 curtain 最常見的具體意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please close the curtains before you turn on the light.","zh":"開燈前請把窗簾拉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Morning light came through the thin curtains.","zh":"晨光透過薄薄的窗簾照了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curtain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95fce1b83862ae25","term":"curtain","forms":["curtain","curtains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舞臺幕布","explanation":"指劇院裡隔開觀眾和舞臺的大簾子。它仍然是“遮擋、分隔”的那塊布，只是地點從窗戶變成了舞臺。","examples":[{"en":"The audience became quiet as the curtain rose.","zh":"幕布升起時，觀眾安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actors came back onstage after the curtain fell.","zh":"幕布落下後，演員們又回到了舞臺上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curtain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcb7f265cb52727e","term":"curtain","forms":["curtain","curtains","curtaining","curtained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掛上窗簾；用簾遮住","explanation":"指給窗戶等掛上 curtain，或用簾子把它遮住。這個動詞意思就是把記憶中的“遮擋布”放到相應位置上。","examples":[{"en":"They curtained the windows to keep the afternoon sun out.","zh":"他們給窗戶掛上窗簾，以擋住下午的陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small room was curtained with a faded sheet.","zh":"這個小房間用一條褪色的床單隔了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curtain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80c1018a4c8f1d7fe750","word":"curve","forms":["curve"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ccc0ee08c172c6a","term":"curve","forms":["curve","curves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彎道","explanation":"指道路、軌道等從一個方向彎向另一個方向的部分，重點是可以實際經過的彎路。","examples":[{"en":"Slow down before the sharp curve.","zh":"在急彎前減速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road bends sharply after the curve.","zh":"過了這個彎道，道路急劇轉彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af17741a1205e11e","term":"curve","forms":["curve","curves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"曲線","explanation":"指沒有直線段和尖角、整體呈彎曲形狀的線或圖形；也可以泛指紙上畫出的弧線。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a smooth curve between the two points.","zh":"在這兩個點之間畫一條平滑的曲線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The graph rises in a gentle curve.","zh":"這條圖線沿著平緩的曲線升高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-afe83ab0a7086484","term":"curve","forms":["curve","curves","curving","curved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使彎曲","explanation":"表示把原本較直的東西彎成弧形或彎折的形狀，動作直接作用於某個物體。","examples":[{"en":"She curved the wire into a small loop.","zh":"她把鐵絲彎成了一個小環。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Curve the wire gently around the wooden form.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb7903696a896cde","term":"curve","forms":["curve","curves","curving","curved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使偏轉","explanation":"表示讓球、箭或其他運動中的東西偏離原來的直線方向，形成弧形軌跡。","examples":[{"en":"The pitcher curved the ball away from the batter.","zh":"投手讓球偏離擊球手飛去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spin curved the ball past the defender.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab4e12f7dfdafb9d","term":"curve","forms":["curve","curves","curving","curved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸轉彎","explanation":"表示道路、河流、線條等不突然改變方向，而是沿著弧線慢慢轉向。","examples":[{"en":"The trail curves gently around the lake.","zh":"小路沿著湖邊緩緩轉彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The path curves to the left at the bridge.","zh":"小路在橋邊向左轉彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0eae8d194776727906d","word":"cushion","forms":["cushion"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d3b7419b103086d","term":"cushion","forms":["cushion","cushions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"坐墊；靠墊","explanation":"裝在布套裡的柔軟填充物，用來讓人坐得舒服，或支撐身體、物品。它可以是沙發上的坐墊，也可以是椅子上的靠墊。","examples":[{"en":"I put a cushion behind my back because the chair was uncomfortable.","zh":"椅子坐著不舒服，所以我在背後放了一個靠墊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat curled up on the window cushion.","zh":"貓蜷縮在窗邊的坐墊上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cushion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f54f871f5679c153","term":"cushion","forms":["cushion","cushions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緩衝物；減震層","explanation":"指像軟墊一樣吸收衝擊、壓力或碰撞的東西，不一定是真正的布墊。例如保護層、空氣層或其他材料都可以起 cushion 的作用。","examples":[{"en":"The thick mat provides a cushion if the child falls.","zh":"孩子摔倒時，厚墊子能起到緩衝作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A layer of foam cushions the equipment during transport.","zh":"運輸時，一層泡沫能緩衝裝置受到的衝擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cushion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba54d400cd79a3b6","term":"cushion","forms":["cushion","cushions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緩衝餘量；安全餘地","explanation":"指為防止意外而預留的分數、時間、金錢或其他資源；即使之後損失一部分，也不至於影響最終目標。它是把“軟墊吸收衝擊”引申到計劃和結果上。","examples":[{"en":"We need a cushion of two days in case the shipment is delayed.","zh":"我們需要預留兩天的緩衝時間，以防貨物延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team built a comfortable cushion of points before the final quarter.","zh":"球隊在最後一節前已經建立了充足的分差優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cushion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39732a08f44f4911","term":"cushion","forms":["cushion","cushions","cushioning","cushioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緩和；減輕衝擊","explanation":"像軟墊吸收碰撞一樣，減輕打擊、影響或損失的程度。它既可以說實際的撞擊，也可以說價格上漲、裁員等抽象的不利影響。","examples":[{"en":"The emergency fund cushioned the impact of the sudden repair bill.","zh":"應急資金減輕了突如其來的維修賬單帶來的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lower taxes may cushion families from rising costs.","zh":"降低稅收可能減輕物價上漲對家庭造成的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cushion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21a7f61c15cef4ddedae","word":"custody","forms":["custody"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e87462ab46b10a90","term":"custody","forms":["custody","custodies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監護權；照管權","explanation":"指依法負責照料和決定某人，尤其是孩子的權利或安排。重點不是普通的陪伴，而是法院或法律認可的照管責任。","examples":[{"en":"After the divorce, both parents agreed to share custody of their daughter.","zh":"離婚後，雙方父母同意共同監護女兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court gave the grandmother custody of the two children.","zh":"法院把兩個孩子的監護權判給了祖母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-842a911eb65455f5","term":"custody","forms":["custody","custodies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拘留；羈押狀態","explanation":"指一個人被警方或其他執法機構控制並關押，通常是在審判前；它強調被看守的狀態，不等於已經被判有罪。","examples":[{"en":"The suspect was taken into custody after questioning.","zh":"審問結束後，嫌疑人被拘留了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The suspect remains in custody awaiting trial.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cdfd271da635d491e37","word":"custom","forms":["custom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d84e2663c3da28df","term":"custom","forms":["custom","customs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"習慣；慣例","explanation":"指個人或群體反覆採用的行為方式，也可以指一個社會普遍認可的做事習慣。它把“重複做某事”逐漸變成了大家熟悉的做法。","examples":[{"en":"It is a local custom to leave shoes by the door.","zh":"把鞋放在門邊是當地的一種習俗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By custom, the oldest child opens the ceremony.","zh":"按照慣例，由年齡最大的孩子主持儀式開場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02ccb8c7d1d6bebc","term":"custom","forms":["custom","customs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳統習俗；儀式","explanation":"指一個文化、民族或群體長期保留下來的信仰、儀式和行為方式，通常可以和其他社會的傳統相區別。","examples":[{"en":"Visitors should learn the local customs before the festival.","zh":"遊客應在節日前瞭解當地的習俗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Removing shoes at the door is a local custom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c01133678253ccc98d59","word":"customary","forms":["customary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b27858aab353797","term":"customary","forms":["customary","more customary","most customary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慣常的；按慣例的","explanation":"指某種做法因為長期習慣或共同約定而成為通常做法；重點不是“剛剛發生”，而是“大家一向如此”。","examples":[{"en":"It is customary to shake hands when you meet someone for the first time.","zh":"第一次見面時握手是一種慣例。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guests followed the customary greeting before entering the hall.","zh":"客人們在進入大廳前按慣例行了問候禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/customary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ca01c95012e3aac","term":"customary","forms":["customary","more customary","most customary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"習慣上享有或承擔的","explanation":"強調某種權利、身份或安排是由長期習慣賦予或保持的，而不一定來自成文規定；本質上仍是“老規矩帶來的”。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers claimed a customary right to use the forest.","zh":"村民們聲稱自己按照習俗享有使用這片森林的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers defended their customary grazing rights.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/customary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6c45863875e34487ca3","word":"customer","forms":["customer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2b776454ca5aa73","term":"customer","forms":["customer","customers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顧客；客戶","explanation":"指從商家購買商品、接受服務，或有可能購買、接受服務的人或公司。它覆蓋從路過並可能消費的人，到已經長期使用某項服務的客戶，是最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The store offers free delivery to every customer.","zh":"這家商店為每位顧客提供免費送貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a customer after trying the free sample.","zh":"她試用免費樣品後成了這家店的顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/customer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ebe5f5b5d89b677","term":"customer","forms":["customer","customers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某種人；傢伙","explanation":"非正式地指一個在相處或互動中表現出某種特點的人，前面通常用形容詞說明他是什麼樣的人。例如，冷靜的人、強硬的人或難對付的人都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"He looks quiet, but he is a tough customer in negotiations.","zh":"他看起來很安靜，但在談判中是個難對付的傢伙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That negotiator is a particularly slippery customer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/customer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45e285133b891bc3bc02","word":"customs","forms":["customs"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2de3771139c4b03","term":"customs","forms":["customs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關稅","explanation":"指國家對進口或出口貨物徵收的錢，是“海關門口要交的費用”。它通常和貨物、金額以及繳納關稅的動作一起出現。","examples":[{"en":"We had to pay customs on the watches we imported.","zh":"我們不得不為進口的手錶繳納關稅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The customs on this shipment are higher than expected.","zh":"這批貨的關稅比預想的高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/customs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bad47de046f72a0a","term":"customs","forms":["customs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海關機構","explanation":"指負責檢查進出口物品並徵收相關稅費的政府部門或工作人員。“海關攔下我們”就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"Customs checked our bags at the airport.","zh":"海關在機場檢查了我們的行李。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Customs held the package for further inspection.","zh":"海關扣留了這個包裹，準備進一步檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/customs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-378bfce5cda2599a6cda","word":"cut","forms":["cut"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad2ed54fe273ed12","term":"cut","forms":["cut","cuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"切割動作","explanation":"指用刀或其他工具切割的動作本身，也可泛指一次切割。","examples":[{"en":"He made a careful cut through the paper.","zh":"他小心地把紙切開了一道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One clean cut separated the rope.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-949353aee2ea08fb","term":"cut","forms":["cut","cuts","cutting","cutted","cutten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"切入；割開","explanation":"用刀或其他鋒利工具切入某物的表面，使其出現一道切口；這正是“一刀造成分開或變化”的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"She cut into the loaf with a sharp knife.","zh":"她用一把鋒利的刀切入麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The broken glass cut into his palm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00f424f25256b690","term":"cut","forms":["cut","cuts","cutting","cutted","cutten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剔除；刪減","explanation":"把人或事物從團隊、名單、計劃等中移除，或減少其數量；像一刀把它從原來的整體中分開。","examples":[{"en":"Maya was cut from the team before the final match.","zh":"瑪雅在決賽前被球隊剔除了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had to cut two pages from the report.","zh":"我們不得不從報告中刪去兩頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-17550e2bb9ff2c26dcce","word":"cute","forms":["cute"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e2ee9edc5a6bcc0","term":"cute","forms":["cute","cuter","cutest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"像幼崽一樣可愛","explanation":"指具有嬰兒或小動物常見的特點，例如圓潤、柔軟、眼睛大、動作頑皮、害羞或惹人憐愛，因此讓人自然地產生喜愛之情。","examples":[{"en":"That puppy is so cute that everyone wants to hold it.","zh":"那隻小狗太可愛了，大家都想抱抱它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a cute dress with tiny pockets.","zh":"她穿了一條帶有小口袋的可愛連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb58885f59d02beb","term":"cute","forms":["cute","cuter","cutest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"討人喜歡；迷人","explanation":"指某人或某物有吸引力、討人喜歡，帶有年輕、精巧、俏皮或有趣的感覺；它不一定真的像嬰兒或小動物。","examples":[{"en":"Your idea is cute, but we need a more practical plan.","zh":"你的想法很有趣討喜，但我們需要一個更實際的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave me a cute little note with my coffee.","zh":"他和咖啡一起給了我一張討人喜歡的小紙條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c501935a6b2b247d007e","word":"cycle","forms":["cycle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fc4252c77da6afd","term":"cycle","forms":["cycle","cycles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"週期；一輪","explanation":"指一段完整的時間或空間過程，在這段過程中，一組事件或現象從開始發展到結束；重點是“走完一圈”。","examples":[{"en":"The cycle of the seasons affects many animals.","zh":"季節的迴圈影響許多動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are starting a new work cycle next week.","zh":"我們下週開始新一輪工作週期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e72c5057918d2c9","term":"cycle","forms":["cycle","cycles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一整圈；完整旋轉","explanation":"指某個物體完整轉動一週，回到原來的方向或位置，強調一次完整的圓周運動。","examples":[{"en":"The wheel makes one complete cycle before the machine stops.","zh":"機器停止前，輪子完整轉了一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wheel completes one cycle every second.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24feb7bb9fd96a1d","term":"cycle","forms":["cycle","cycles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"迴圈過程","explanation":"指一個按一定順序進行、結束後又回到開頭並重復的過程；選舉、月經和新聞都可以有這樣的迴圈。","examples":[{"en":"The news cycle moves very quickly these days.","zh":"如今新聞迴圈的變化非常快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The election cycle begins again next year.","zh":"選舉週期明年又會開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ced52170ee661c0d","term":"cycle","forms":["cycle","cycles","cycling","cycled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"騎車","explanation":"指騎腳踏車或其他這類車輛出行，就是沿著路線用車輛完成一段移動。","examples":[{"en":"I cycle to the station every day.","zh":"我每天騎車去車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They cycled along the river on Sunday.","zh":"他們星期天沿著河邊騎車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d98cb1c5d40c84ef","term":"cycle","forms":["cycle","cycles","cycling","cycled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迴圈執行","explanation":"指某事物經歷一個完整迴圈，或讓某事物按一輪程式執行；重點是從一個階段走完又回到起點。","examples":[{"en":"The system cycles through several checks before it starts.","zh":"系統啟動前會依次完成幾項檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pump cycles on and off automatically.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a07a76a357cf6ed5daf8","word":"cynical","forms":["cynical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af4542402e9ee491","term":"cynical","forms":["cynical","more cynical","most cynical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"認為人性自私的","explanation":"這種看法認為人的行動主要不是出於善意或原則，而是出於利益、慾望等較低階的動機；它是 cynical 最根本的觀念。","examples":[{"en":"He has a cynical view of human nature.","zh":"他對人性持一種認為人都很自私的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her cynical explanation was that the company donated money only for publicity.","zh":"她的說法很憤世嫉俗，認為公司捐錢只是為了宣傳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cynical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d579fff1387daf57","term":"cynical","forms":["cynical","more cynical","most cynical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不相信他人真誠的","explanation":"指懷疑別人是否誠實、善良或真心幫助他人，總覺得對方可能另有自私的目的。","examples":[{"en":"Many voters are cynical about the politician's promises.","zh":"許多選民不相信這位政治家的承諾是真心的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of broken promises made voters cynical.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cynical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f31304cdfd0a3a6362b","word":"daily","forms":["daily"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf774105581cd6bf","term":"daily","forms":["daily"],"pos":"adj","zh":"每天的；每日的","explanation":"它把“每天翻一頁日曆”的概念放在名詞前，說明某事每天發生，或每個工作日規律發生。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps a daily record of her expenses.","zh":"她每天記錄自己的開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team has a daily meeting at nine.","zh":"團隊每天九點開會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daily","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0216706dbf84536","term":"daily","forms":["daily"],"pos":"adv","zh":"每天；每日地","explanation":"它把“日曆每天翻一頁”變成動作的頻率，說明某個動作每天發生。","examples":[{"en":"The plants should be watered daily in hot weather.","zh":"天氣炎熱時，這些植物應該每天澆水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He checks the figures daily.","zh":"他每天核對這些數字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daily","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc780484d99134f0","term":"daily","forms":["daily","dailies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"每日產生或使用的東西","explanation":"把“每天翻一頁日曆”的概念名詞化，指每天製作、消費、使用或進行的某種東西。","examples":[{"en":"The editor reviews the dailies before lunch.","zh":"編輯午飯前會檢查當天的日常材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please file each daily by date.","zh":"請按日期歸檔每一份每日材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daily","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7881eddfe386c9831f86","word":"dairy","forms":["dairy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86aae106523dbb43","term":"dairy","forms":["dairy","dairies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乳製品加工場","explanation":"指在農場或附近把牛奶加工成黃油、乳酪等產品的地方。它是“牛奶生產鏈”中實際處理牛奶的場所。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer takes the fresh milk to the dairy every morning.","zh":"農民每天早晨把鮮奶送到乳製品加工場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Milk arrives at the dairy before sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dairy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a2cbb6206b2d663","term":"dairy","forms":["dairy","dairies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乳製品","explanation":"不可數地指牛奶及由牛奶製成的食物這一整類，尤其常見於飲食、健康和食品成分語境。","examples":[{"en":"She stopped eating dairy for a month to see whether she felt better.","zh":"她停止吃乳製品一個月，想看看自己是否感覺更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She avoids dairy but enjoys almond milk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dairy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2fcb6465ee5cbfa35673","word":"dam","forms":["dam"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e56d07bc8836dfe5","term":"dam","forms":["dam","dams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水壩","explanation":"dam 是橫跨河流或其他流水通道的建築物，用來攔水、調節水量或防止洪水突然下洩。記住“先有一道攔水的牆”，就是這個核心義。","examples":[{"en":"The new dam will provide water for nearby farms.","zh":"這座新水壩將為附近的農場供水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Engineers built the dam to control flooding.","zh":"工程師修建這座水壩是為了控制洪水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e45f9f4176e7d43d","term":"dam","forms":["dam","dams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壩形成的水庫","explanation":"這裡指水壩攔住水後形成的蓄水區域。它仍然沿用“把水攔在一道牆後面”的畫面，但重點從牆轉到了牆後的水。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon fishing at the dam.","zh":"我們一下午都在水庫邊釣魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cattle drank from the farm dam.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a1185c2c3f27e70","term":"dam","forms":["dam","dams","damming","dammed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"築壩攔水","explanation":"dam 作動詞就是用壩把水流攔住或限制住：名詞是“攔水的牆”，動詞是“建起這道牆來攔水”。","examples":[{"en":"The town dammed the river to store water for the summer.","zh":"這個城鎮在河上築壩，以儲存夏季用水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Beavers dam streams with branches and mud.","zh":"海狸用樹枝和泥巴攔壩截住溪流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f5a5c61ccdbd8ff2a62","word":"damage","forms":["damage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c15e0b40cd140b9","term":"damage","forms":["damage","damages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"損壞；損害","explanation":"指某物、某人的狀況、價值或名譽受到破壞，或這種破壞所造成的損失。重點不是“動作”本身，而是東西已經不再完好，或者受到的傷害可以被觀察、評估。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused serious damage to several houses.","zh":"暴風雨給幾所房屋造成了嚴重損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is still trying to repair the damage to its reputation.","zh":"這家公司仍在努力挽回對其聲譽造成的損害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44e486246cf75a38","term":"damage","forms":["damage","damages","damaging","damaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"損壞；損害","explanation":"指使物品、建築、身體、名譽或價值受到損害，使它不再完好或不如以前。它強調造成損害的動作，與名詞damage表示的損害結果相連。","examples":[{"en":"Please pack the glasses carefully so you don’t damage them.","zh":"請把玻璃杯仔細包裝好，以免把它們弄壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leak damaged the ceiling and the wooden floor.","zh":"漏水損壞了天花板和木地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b0cf192c14f7e5c25e1","word":"damp","forms":["damp"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-932845168cdad472","term":"damp","forms":["damp","damper","dampest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"潮溼的","explanation":"指含有一定水分、溼度較高但沒有溼透的狀態，例如牆面、衣物、土壤或空氣都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"The towels stayed damp after a night in the bathroom.","zh":"毛巾在浴室裡放了一夜後仍然是潮溼的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a damp patch on the wall.","zh":"我們發現牆上有一塊潮溼的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43b1038be4d01b52","term":"damp","forms":["damp","damps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溼氣；潮溼","explanation":"指空氣、環境或物體中存在的水分，也可以泛指潮溼這種狀態；它是形容詞所描述狀態的名詞化表達。","examples":[{"en":"The damp in this old house is damaging the books.","zh":"這所老房子裡的潮氣正在損壞書籍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Opening the windows helped clear the damp.","zh":"開啟窗戶有助於散去潮氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-926b1747c62e4e40","term":"damp","forms":["damp","damps","damping","damped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"減弱振動；阻尼","explanation":"指把機械振動或電氣波動中的能量消耗掉，使運動或變化逐漸變小、變平穩；可以把它看成“潮氣壓低力量”的技術化延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The rubber mounts damp the engine vibrations.","zh":"橡膠支架能減弱發動機的振動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This filter damps sudden changes in the signal.","zh":"這個濾波器能減弱訊號的突然變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/damp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c371c2ada73a02e26e1","word":"dance","forms":["dance"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-79b9a9b49ca6be6f","term":"dance","forms":["dance","dances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舞蹈；跳舞動作","explanation":"dance 是隨著音樂或節奏做的一連串動作，也可以指一次跳舞。它是這個詞最核心的畫面：身體有節奏地動起來。","examples":[{"en":"The children made up a silly dance for the school show.","zh":"孩子們為學校演出編了一段滑稽的舞蹈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We danced in the kitchen while dinner was cooking.","zh":"做飯的時候，我們在廚房裡跳起了舞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55c0e6663bf5c26a","term":"dance","forms":["dance","dances","dancing","danced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跳舞","explanation":"dance 作動詞時最常表示隨著音樂或節奏跳舞，重點是身體自己有節奏地移動。","examples":[{"en":"They danced together to their favorite song.","zh":"他們隨著自己最喜歡的歌一起跳舞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I danced with my grandmother at the wedding.","zh":"我在婚禮上和祖母跳了舞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc332d001e2c163ab0ea","word":"dancer","forms":["dancer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a293fed0e7aaae67","term":"dancer","forms":["dancer","dancers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳舞的人；舞者","explanation":"dancer 就是跳舞的人，可以是把跳舞當作愛好的人，也可以是表演或以此為職業的人。它直接來自“跳舞”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is a talented dancer.","zh":"我姐姐是一名很有天賦的舞者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm a terrible dancer.","zh":"我跳舞跳得很差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dancer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11db2e7b8976bb2b","term":"dancer","forms":["dancer","dancers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脫衣舞者","explanation":"在特定語境中，dancer 可以委婉地指脫衣舞者；這是普通“舞者”義之外的語境義。","examples":[{"en":"The club hired several dancers for the late-night show.","zh":"這傢俱樂部為深夜演出聘請了幾名脫衣舞者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nightclub hired three new dancers for its adult show.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dancer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-123fd666aa39d376690c","word":"danger","forms":["danger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5967e310dc8f1d8a","term":"danger","forms":["danger","dangers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"危險；危險處境","explanation":"指一個人、動物或事物暴露在很可能受到傷害、損失或破壞的處境中。它強調前方存在真實的威脅，就像警告標誌提醒你不要繼續前進。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers were in danger after the bridge collapsed.","zh":"橋塌了以後，徒步旅行者處於危險之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a real danger of flooding after the heavy rain.","zh":"大雨過後確實有發生洪水的危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/danger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3b452933faebfa5","term":"danger","forms":["danger","dangers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"危險因素；風險","explanation":"指可能造成傷害、損失或嚴重後果的某件事、某種情況或某個來源。這裡關注的是“什麼東西會帶來危險”，而不只是處於危險中的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Loose wires are a danger to children in the building.","zh":"建築物裡鬆動的電線會對孩子造成危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Loose electrical wires present a danger to children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/danger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7eaa968417c5dbde7932","word":"dangerous","forms":["dangerous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cd27ab4c889da57","term":"dangerous","forms":["dangerous","more dangerous","dangerouser","most dangerous","dangerousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有危險的","explanation":"指某種事物、環境或行為本身包含很大的風險，可能導致受傷、損失或其他嚴重後果。這是日常使用中最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Swimming in this river after heavy rain is dangerous.","zh":"大雨後在這條河裡游泳很危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is dangerous to drive when you are tired.","zh":"疲勞時開車很危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dangerous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc789abafcbef8c1","term":"dangerous","forms":["dangerous","more dangerous","dangerouser","most dangerous","dangerousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"會造成傷害的","explanation":"強調某個人、動物或行為具有傷害他人的可能性，彷彿危險會從它那裡主動向外擴散。它可以描述攻擊性，也可以描述某種可能造成損害的做法。","examples":[{"en":"The dog may look friendly, but it can be dangerous to strangers.","zh":"這條狗看起來很友好，但可能會傷害陌生人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mixing these cleaners produces dangerous fumes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dangerous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-827a02fd76a37fa49c71","word":"dare","forms":["dare"],"officialPos":"aux./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-12604ce570bab5f7","term":"dare","forms":["dare","dares","dast","daring","dared","durst"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敢於做某事","explanation":"表示自己有足夠膽量去做某事，就是把記憶中的那一步真正邁出去。","examples":[{"en":"I wouldn't dare question her decision.","zh":"我可不敢質疑她的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you dare to go in alone?","zh":"你敢一個人進去嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6b103bb52305b08","term":"dare","forms":["dare","dares","dast","daring","dared","durst"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人挑戰做某事","explanation":"表示故意向別人叫板，要求對方證明自己敢做某事；這是“讓別人邁出那一步”。","examples":[{"en":"I dare you to ask him yourself.","zh":"我就不信你敢親自問他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dared her brother to jump into the pool.","zh":"她激她哥哥跳進游泳池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6bb5689beec52c4672b","word":"dark","forms":["dark"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dd912c432bfeb53","term":"dark","forms":["dark","darker","darkest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"黑暗的；光線不足的","explanation":"指光線很少，因而看不清周圍的東西，是 dark 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The room was too dark to read in.","zh":"房間太暗了，沒法在裡面看書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dark hallway had no working lights.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4442eb5fb93d64de","term":"dark","forms":["dark","darker","darkest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顏色深的","explanation":"指顏色的明度較低、比另一種同色調更深，例如深藍、深棕或深綠色。","examples":[{"en":"My sister has darker hair than I do.","zh":"我姐姐的頭髮顏色比我的深。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She painted the shutters a dark green.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51e7d2cde85c20e1","term":"dark","forms":["dark","darks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑暗","explanation":"指缺少光線的狀態，即“黑暗”本身，而不是某個黑色物體。","examples":[{"en":"We waited in the dark until the lights came back on.","zh":"我們在黑暗中等到燈重新亮起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We searched for the lost keys in the dark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb609bdcdece3f067149","word":"darling","forms":["darling"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5110560a9dcfb69c","term":"darling","forms":["darling","more darling","darlinger","most darling","darlingest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親愛的；珍愛的","explanation":"指某人受到深厚感情和珍愛，是說“親愛的、心愛的”。它既可以描述伴侶，也可以描述家人或其他關係親近的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is my darling wife of twenty-two years.","zh":"她是我深愛了二十二年的妻子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their darling son came home for the holidays.","zh":"他們心愛的兒子回家度假了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef9e63ddfb7bf8e6","term":"darling","forms":["darling","darlings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親愛的；親暱稱呼","explanation":"用於直接稱呼自己很親愛的人，相當於“親愛的”。它也可以作為對伴侶、家人或親密朋友的暱稱。","examples":[{"en":"Pass the wine, would you, darling?","zh":"親愛的，請把酒遞給我，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Darling, I saved you the last piece of cake.","zh":"親愛的，我把最後一塊蛋糕留給你了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af9d2c92ddc38ca77b3c","word":"dash","forms":["dash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-636bb0b234a33764","term":"dash","forms":["dash","dashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橫線；破折號","explanation":"指書寫或排版中橫向的線狀符號，包括不同長度的連線號、短橫線和破折號。它像動作留下的一道迅速劃過的痕跡。","examples":[{"en":"Use an em dash to show a sudden change in the sentence.","zh":"用破折號表示句子中的突然轉折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a dash to mark the interruption.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2ef774f8933e5de","term":"dash","forms":["dash","dashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短跑；疾奔","explanation":"指一段很短但很快的奔跑，重點是突然加速、迅速衝出去。","examples":[{"en":"She made a dash for the bus before the doors closed.","zh":"車門關上前，她趕緊衝向公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He made a desperate dash for the departing bus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cff757d5f32a83d7","term":"dash","forms":["dash","dashes","dashing","dashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"飛快跑；衝","explanation":"指快速跑一小段路，突出突然加速和迅速向前。","examples":[{"en":"He dashed across the field to catch the ball.","zh":"他飛快跑過球場去接球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dashed upstairs to answer the telephone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e690dab310a5c93d","term":"dash","forms":["dash","dashes","dashing","dashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"趕緊離開","explanation":"口語中表示馬上走、得趕緊離開，是“快速跑開”義的日常引申。","examples":[{"en":"I have to dash now, or I’ll miss my train.","zh":"我得趕緊走了，不然要趕不上火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I must dash; my train leaves shortly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9d4cca615bbb66f","term":"dash","forms":["dash","dashes","dashing","dashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"毀掉；使落空","explanation":"指某件事突然受到打擊而失敗，尤其常說希望、計劃或機會被徹底破壞。它把“猛撞造成損壞”的畫面轉到抽象事物上。","examples":[{"en":"The bad news dashed our hopes of winning.","zh":"這個壞訊息使我們獲勝的希望破滅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rejection dashed her hopes of studying abroad.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a6eb0790f39ac87c94f","word":"data","forms":["data"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cade43606b407140","term":"data","forms":["data"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機中的資訊資料","explanation":"data 是電腦能夠儲存、處理或傳輸的資訊，形式可以是符號、數量、聲音、影象或影片。它對應記憶中的“被記錄下來、可以流動的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The device stores data on a small memory card.","zh":"這臺裝置把資料儲存在一張小儲存卡上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camera sends image data to the computer.","zh":"相機把影象資料傳送到電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/data","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af7fc7b9741601cd","term":"data","forms":["data"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作為依據的事實材料","explanation":"data 也指已經記錄、知道或假定為事實，並用來進行推理、討論或計算的材料，尤其常見於統計和研究。它仍然是“被收集起來、支援判斷的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers collected data from more than a thousand students.","zh":"研究人員收集了一千多名學生的資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The historian gathered data from parish records and letters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/data","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3549b0028b75d981cdda","word":"database","forms":["database"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1879be9e22fd65e","term":"database","forms":["database","databases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料庫；資料庫","explanation":"指按照一定方式組織起來、可以儲存和查詢的資訊集合，例如聯絡人、書目或研究資料。重點不只是“有很多資訊”，而是這些資訊被整理成了便於檢索的結構。","examples":[{"en":"I keep a database of all the books I have read.","zh":"我把讀過的所有書整理成一個資料庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a database of photographs from the nineteenth century.","zh":"這家博物館有一個收錄十九世紀照片的資料庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/database","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e528353c1783bc96","term":"database","forms":["database","databases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結構化資料庫","explanation":"在計算機技術中，指由表格等結構化物件組成的資料集；不同部分之間可以按規則關聯，並供查詢和處理。","examples":[{"en":"The customer database contains separate tables for orders and payments.","zh":"客戶資料庫為訂單和付款分別設有表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We designed a database with one table for each type of record.","zh":"我們設計了一個資料庫，為每種記錄分別設定一個表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/database","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e87632cd46bd4907c51","word":"date","forms":["date"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d194a44c8f1d1cf","term":"date","forms":["date","dates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日期標註","explanation":"date 可以是寫在信件、契約、硬幣等物品上的日期，用來說明它何時寫成、簽署或製作。它把一件物品和具體時間聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"Please write the date at the top of the application.","zh":"請在申請表頂部寫上日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The date on the certificate is hard to read.","zh":"證書上的日期很難看清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/date","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5571b1dc4224bb5f","term":"date","forms":["date","dates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"定好的日期","explanation":"date 可以指某項交易、活動或事件發生或預定發生的具體日期，也就是給事情釘上的時間點。","examples":[{"en":"We set a date for the school festival in June.","zh":"我們把校慶日期定在了六月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hearing date was moved to Friday.","zh":"聽證會日期改到了星期五。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/date","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-821e519f5395fca3","term":"date","forms":["date","dates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戀愛約會","explanation":"date 可以指和戀人或可能發展成戀人的物件進行的一次見面或外出活動。這是“把兩個人釘在同一個約定時間”的具體延伸。","examples":[{"en":"They went on their first date at a small bookstore café.","zh":"他們第一次約會是在一家小書店咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our date lasted longer than we expected.","zh":"我們的約會比預想的持續得更久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/date","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-226a00a737f5d159","term":"date","forms":["date","dates","dating","dated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確定事件日期","explanation":"date 可以表示確定某件事發生的時間，或說明它的日期，相當於給事件釘上時間點。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers dated the temple to the ninth century.","zh":"研究人員確定這座寺廟建於九世紀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inscription dates the bridge to 1820.","zh":"碑文表明這座橋建於1820年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/date","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1efc5c8e8c601ba9","term":"date","forms":["date","dates","dating","dated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與某人交往","explanation":"date 可以表示和某人保持戀愛關係或處於浪漫交往中，重點是持續的關係，而不是某一次約會。","examples":[{"en":"Maya has been dating Daniel since last spring.","zh":"瑪雅從去年春天起就一直和丹尼爾交往。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you dating anyone at the moment?","zh":"你現在在和誰交往嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/date","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-176b4bccaa6bd538","term":"date","forms":["date","dates","dating","dated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"彼此交往","explanation":"date 也可用不及物或相互關係的方式，表示兩個人正在談戀愛或交往。","examples":[{"en":"They started dating after working together on the project.","zh":"他們一起做完這個專案後開始交往。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They dated for two years before marrying.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/date","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ed28f82ca96c3342a5c","word":"daughter","forms":["daughter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a130d16fa71a1aa3","term":"daughter","forms":["daughter","daughters","daughtren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女兒","explanation":"指一個人的女性子女，是 daughter 最基本、最常用的意思；無論年齡多大，只要是某人的女性子女，都可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"Their daughter is studying at university.","zh":"他們的女兒正在上大學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have one son and two daughters.","zh":"我們有一個兒子和兩個女兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ccc6d780a6e78e6","term":"daughter","forms":["daughter","daughters","daughtren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女性後代","explanation":"泛指家族、民族或某個祖先的女性後代，不一定是在說說話人的親生女兒；重點仍是家譜中從上一代延續下來的女性一支。","examples":[{"en":"She is a daughter of a family that has lived here for generations.","zh":"她是一個世代居住在這裡的家族的後代。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inscription honors the daughters of this ancient dynasty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/daughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8326e09ce4e90a419a51","word":"dawn","forms":["dawn"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1ef417674e333cf","term":"dawn","forms":["dawn","dawns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黎明；破曉前後","explanation":"指太陽昇起前後天色開始變亮的時段，也就是夜晚向白天過渡的黎明。這個意義抓住了dawn“第一束光出現”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We left the house before dawn.","zh":"我們在黎明前離開了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The birds began singing at dawn.","zh":"鳥兒在黎明時開始歌唱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d13cca688571916","term":"dawn","forms":["dawn","dawns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開端；初期","explanation":"用於比喻某個時代、思想或發展過程剛剛出現的最初階段，就像黑暗中第一束光剛剛出現。常見於“某事物的開端”這一概念。","examples":[{"en":"The invention marked the dawn of a new age.","zh":"這項發明標誌著一個新時代的開端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At the dawn of aviation, flying remained a dangerous experiment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb6d198bc0bb4fa3","term":"dawn","forms":["dawn","dawns","dawning","dawned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"天開始亮","explanation":"表示天色從黑暗中開始變亮，新的一天開始出現。這裡就是“第一束光出現”這一核心畫面的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"A new day dawned over the quiet town.","zh":"新的一天在這座寧靜的小鎮上開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The day dawned clear after the storm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-852e123927d8380d","term":"dawn","forms":["dawn","dawns","dawning","dawned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸意識到","explanation":"表示某個事實、想法或真相逐漸在某人心中變得清楚，就像天色慢慢亮起來。重點是“開始明白”，而不是突然得知。","examples":[{"en":"It finally dawned on me that I had taken the wrong train.","zh":"我終於意識到自己坐錯了火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The seriousness of the situation began to dawn on her.","zh":"她開始意識到事態的嚴重性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-944c27e5b97ab7793e4b","word":"day","forms":["day"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e19ddbf6364fd471","term":"day","forms":["day","days"],"pos":"noun","zh":"白天","explanation":"day最基本的畫面是太陽在地平線以上、天空明亮的時段，也就是與night相對的“白天”。它強調光照時段，不一定等於嚴格的二十四小時。","examples":[{"en":"The streets are busy during the day and quiet at night.","zh":"白天街道很熱鬧，晚上則很安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Owls sleep by day and hunt at night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52e823ee34f43460","term":"day","forms":["day","days"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一天；二十四小時左右","explanation":"day也可以把從某一時刻到下一次相同時刻看作一個完整時間單位，通常約等於二十四小時。這是安排活動、計算時間和談論期限時最常用的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"We need two more days to finish the project.","zh":"我們還需要兩天才能完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I check my messages several times a day.","zh":"我每天檢視幾次訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e88ecf834fa37e5ae687","word":"dazzle","forms":["dazzle"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6bad260ca642139","term":"dazzle","forms":["dazzle","dazzles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耀眼強光","explanation":"指強烈到使眼睛難以看清的光，重點不只是亮，而是亮得令人目眩。","examples":[{"en":"The dazzle of the morning sun made it hard to read the map.","zh":"早晨陽光的耀眼光芒讓人很難看清地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dazzle of headlights briefly hid the cyclist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dazzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5db27a6e99b3ec97","term":"dazzle","forms":["dazzle","dazzles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人目眩的華麗光彩","explanation":"指外表、表演、才華或場面華麗得令人目不暇接，甚至暫時無法清醒地判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The dazzle of the stage show left the audience speechless.","zh":"舞臺表演的華麗光彩讓觀眾一時說不出話來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dazzle of the jewels filled the display case.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dazzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fb4a166e8abfc2f","term":"dazzle","forms":["dazzle","dazzles","dazzling","dazzled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使看不清","explanation":"指強光直射，使人的眼睛或某種感應裝置被壓倒而暫時無法正常看見或辨認。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden flash dazzled the driver, who slowed down at once.","zh":"突然的閃光晃得司機看不清，他立刻減慢了車速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The headlights dazzled me as I crossed the road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dazzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76e30c17c5e4f293","term":"dazzle","forms":["dazzle","dazzles","dazzling","dazzled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使眼花繚亂","explanation":"指某人的外表、表現、才華或論據過於出眾，使別人驚歎之餘暫時難以冷靜思考或判斷。","examples":[{"en":"Her confidence dazzled the investors, even though the plan was incomplete.","zh":"她的自信氣度讓投資者眼花繚亂，儘管計劃還不完整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The polished mirrors dazzled visitors entering the gallery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dazzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28a3a5e81d1e89f0efc7","word":"dead","forms":["dead"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ccdd25f65287236","term":"dead","forms":["dead","deader","deadest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"死的；去世的","explanation":"指人或動物已經不再有生命，也可以把死者稱為 dead。它體現了記憶鉤子中“生命被徹底切斷”的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"All of my grandparents are dead.","zh":"我的祖父母都已經去世了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog was found dead beside the road.","zh":"那條狗被發現死在路邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d784ff034291b249","term":"dead","forms":["dead","deader","deadest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"斷電的；無訊號的","explanation":"指裝置、電路或訊號當前完全不工作、沒有電或沒有傳輸狀態，正是“力量被徹底切斷”的機器用法。","examples":[{"en":"The phone is dead, so I can’t call you.","zh":"手機沒電了，所以我沒法給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The circuit is dead, so the technician can repair it safely.","zh":"電路已經斷電，所以技術人員可以安全維修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dfc8aeb39828e31c4cf8","word":"deadline","forms":["deadline"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27255bd4d2f55c6c","term":"deadline","forms":["deadline","deadlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最後期限；截止日期","explanation":"指必須在某個日期或時間之前完成、提交或處理某事的最後界限；一旦超過，通常就算遲了。","examples":[{"en":"Please send me the report before the deadline on Friday.","zh":"請在週五的截止日期前把報告發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We worked late to meet the deadline.","zh":"為了趕上最後期限，我們工作到很晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deadline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27ec4ab2cc3f87a8c160","word":"deadly","forms":["deadly"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6732b716461567c2","term":"deadly","forms":["deadly","deadlier","more deadly","deadliest","most deadly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"致命的","explanation":"指某種武器、疾病、傷害或力量足以造成死亡，就像那支能一擊致命的箭。","examples":[{"en":"The snake has a deadly bite.","zh":"這種蛇的咬傷可能致命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firefighters were warned about the deadly smoke.","zh":"消防員被提醒要當心致命的煙霧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deadly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62e932c1a38df6da","term":"deadly","forms":["deadly","deadlier","more deadly","deadliest","most deadly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"懷有毀滅性敵意的","explanation":"形容人或群體的敵意堅決到想徹底毀掉對方，因此 deadly enemies 就是勢不兩立的死敵。","examples":[{"en":"The two politicians became deadly enemies after the scandal.","zh":"那場醜聞之後，兩名政治家成了勢不兩立的死敵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They were deadly enemies throughout the bitter campaign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deadly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9828c99a3600906","term":"deadly","forms":["deadly","deadlier","more deadly","deadliest","most deadly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其準確的","explanation":"形容瞄準、射擊或投擲準得幾乎必然擊中；它保留了“致命箭矢”的畫面，因此 deadly aim 既是“準”，也常帶有危險意味。","examples":[{"en":"Her deadly accurate throw hit the center of the target.","zh":"她精準得驚人的投擲擊中了靶心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her deadly aim won the archery contest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deadly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-820effb874a485bf6151","word":"deaf","forms":["deaf"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d3c0466bac521c5","term":"deaf","forms":["deaf","deafer","deafest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聽不見的；失聰的","explanation":"指聽覺完全或部分受損，因而聽不見或不容易聽見聲音。這個意義就是“耳朵的門關上了”，但不一定表示完全沒有聽力。","examples":[{"en":"She has been deaf in one ear since childhood.","zh":"她從小就一隻耳朵聽不見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The alarm was too quiet for my deaf grandfather to hear.","zh":"警報聲太小，我失聰的祖父聽不見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deaf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db9f2755339c9e1d","term":"deaf","forms":["deaf","deafer","deafest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對勸告充耳不聞的","explanation":"把“聽不見”引申為“不肯讓意見進入耳朵”，指一個人固執地不聽勸告、不接受說服。","examples":[{"en":"He was deaf to every warning from his friends.","zh":"朋友們的每一次警告他都充耳不聞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister remained deaf to repeated warnings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deaf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5010f8a6b4a31894f5a","word":"deafen","forms":["deafen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"deafen","forms":["deafen"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使暫時聽不見；使震耳欲聾","examples":[{"en":"A sudden explosion can deafen anyone standing nearby.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The noise from those giant speakers could deafen the audience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-f96c94f287038f69433b","word":"deal","forms":["deal"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-692564319d6c5c99","term":"deal","forms":["deal","deals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"划算的交易","explanation":"指對買方或賣方有利、價格或條件很划算的一筆交易；可以把它想成把資源分配到一個特別合算的安排上。","examples":[{"en":"We got a good deal on a nearly new washing machine.","zh":"我們很划算地買到了一臺幾乎全新的洗衣機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family ticket is a better deal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93fc5066fb7528d9","term":"deal","forms":["deal","deals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"協議；安排","explanation":"指雙方談妥並接受的一項協議或安排，把各方的責任和結果都安排妥當；這正是記憶中“談成一筆”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"After two weeks of talks, the union and the company reached a deal.","zh":"經過兩週談判，工會和公司達成了一項協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team celebrated after sealing the deal with its new sponsor.","zh":"球隊與新贊助商敲定協議後慶祝了一番。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bfdd503f1d81447","term":"deal","forms":["deal","deals","dealing","dealt","dealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"應對；處理；設法解決","explanation":"指著手處理人或事，想辦法應付並把局面安排妥當，是“把事情處理好”這一核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"She is learning how to deal with stressful situations.","zh":"她正在學習如何應對有壓力的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician dealt with the problem quickly.","zh":"技術人員很快處理了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e321a4f4fcdcbe581ab","word":"dealer","forms":["dealer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2faab1895436e86","term":"dealer","forms":["dealer","dealers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經銷商；中間商","explanation":"指買進並轉賣商品、促成交易的人或企業，尤其常指汽車經銷商。核心概念是把商品從賣方遞到買方，並從中促成或完成交易。","examples":[{"en":"We bought the car from a local dealer.","zh":"我們從當地經銷商那裡買了這輛車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dealer offered us a better price.","zh":"經銷商給了我們一個更優惠的價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dealer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8619071ce03ea13","term":"dealer","forms":["dealer","dealers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發牌者","explanation":"指紙牌遊戲中負責把牌分發給各位玩家的人。它最直接地體現了“把東西一個個遞給別人”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The dealer gave each player five cards.","zh":"發牌者給每位玩家發了五張牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dealer shuffled the cards before the next round.","zh":"發牌者在下一輪開始前洗了牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dealer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f4d44dfaa1b1ed72a8a","word":"dear","forms":["dear"],"officialPos":"adj./n./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-896b9ac0cd74996e","term":"dear","forms":["dear","dearer","more dear","dearest","most dear"],"pos":"adj","zh":"昂貴的","explanation":"價格高，需要花很多錢；這是“被看重所以代價高”這一核心意思的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh fruit is very dear in winter.","zh":"冬天的新鮮水果很貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fresh fruit becomes dear during the winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f7a8456897d449a","term":"dear","forms":["dear","dearer","more dear","dearest","most dear"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親愛的；惹人喜愛的","explanation":"表示一個人受到喜愛，或本身可愛、值得疼愛；不一定表示戀愛關係。","examples":[{"en":"Our old teacher is still very dear to us.","zh":"我們仍然非常敬愛以前的老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy is dear to everyone in the family.","zh":"這隻小狗受到全家人的喜愛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-671c4fd065b41742","term":"dear","forms":["dear","dearer","more dear","dearest","most dear"],"pos":"adj","zh":"信件開頭的正式稱呼","explanation":"放在信件或郵件開頭，表示對收信人的正式稱呼，相當於中文信件中的“尊敬的……”。","examples":[{"en":"Dear Ms. Lee, thank you for your message.","zh":"尊敬的李女士：感謝您的來信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dear Professor Chen, thank you for your thoughtful reply.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52c8e02987ccb1b0eef9","word":"death","forms":["death"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8c25df83a89af3c","term":"death","forms":["death","deaths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生命終止","explanation":"death是生命過程徹底停止，生物不再作為有生命的個體存在。它可以泛指“死亡”，也可以指某個人具體的一次死亡或死法。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden death of her father shocked the whole family.","zh":"她父親的突然去世震驚了全家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldier died a peaceful death after a long life.","zh":"那名士兵一生漫長，最後安詳地去世了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/death","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6112283351a1f5fe","term":"death","forms":["death","deaths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"死神形象","explanation":"這裡把死亡擬人化為一個通常戴兜帽、手持鐮刀的人物，也就是常說的“死神”。這個意思和大寫的Death相近，但普通名詞用法可以不大寫。","examples":[{"en":"In the old painting, death carries a long, silver scythe.","zh":"在那幅古畫中，死神拿著一把長長的銀色鐮刀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Death appears as a cloaked figure in the painting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/death","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f7a9000cccc11b52237","word":"debate","forms":["debate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6fdecd8a29807e3","term":"debate","forms":["debate","debates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式辯論；有組織的討論","explanation":"指在有規則或較正式的場合，圍繞一個議題讓不同立場展開討論，通常還會透過表決或其他方式作出決定。","examples":[{"en":"After a long debate, the council approved the new parking rules.","zh":"經過長時間的辯論，委員會批准了新的停車規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school held a debate on whether students should wear uniforms.","zh":"學校就學生是否應該穿校服舉行了一場辯論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e2139f7881c9b9c","term":"debate","forms":["debate","debates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"友好的觀點交鋒","explanation":"指雙方或多人圍繞相反觀點進行熱烈但通常文明的討論，不一定有正式規則，也不一定要表決。","examples":[{"en":"The debate over the best way to teach children is still going on.","zh":"關於教孩子的最佳方式，爭論仍在繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dinner ended with a lively debate about detective novels.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e401c9d569387ab7","term":"debate","forms":["debate","debates","debating","debated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加辯論；爭論","explanation":"指公開參加不同觀點的交鋒，或與他人就某個問題進行辯論；核心仍是把不同立場擺出來比較。","examples":[{"en":"The candidates debated the proposed tax changes on television.","zh":"幾位候選人在電視上就擬議中的稅收變化展開了辯論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I enjoy debating ideas with people who disagree with me.","zh":"我喜歡和不同意我的人討論各種想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27f7340b5bceb6ab6e5f","word":"debris","forms":["debris"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2e78627ee5bea68","term":"debris","forms":["debris"],"pos":"noun","zh":"破壞後的殘骸和碎片","explanation":"指建築物、車輛、物品等被破壞後散落的碎片和殘骸，重點是原來的整體已經碎掉，只剩下零散部分。","examples":[{"en":"Workers cleared the debris from the damaged house.","zh":"工人清理了受損房屋的殘骸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Debris covered the road after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，路上滿是殘骸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debris","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-066f33abc294a13c","term":"debris","forms":["debris"],"pos":"noun","zh":"散落的垃圾和廢棄物","explanation":"指被人丟棄、散落在環境中的廢物，尤其常用于海洋、海灘或其他汙染語境；這裡仍然保留“散落的殘留物”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers collected plastic debris from the beach.","zh":"志願者從海灘上收集了塑膠廢棄物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm drains were clogged with leaves and other debris.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debris","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-652d75f9bafb25e55c0e","word":"debt","forms":["debt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0fabcbbdfc903c7","term":"debt","forms":["debt","debts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"應盡的義務或應還的人情","explanation":"指一個人欠另一個人的責任、義務、人情，或本來應該為對方做、對待對方或給對方的東西；它不一定涉及金錢。","examples":[{"en":"We owe a debt of gratitude to the volunteers who helped us.","zh":"我們應該感謝那些幫助過我們的志願者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt he had a debt to repay to his old teacher.","zh":"他覺得自己欠老老師一份應該報答的人情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b735b46253d5d56","term":"debt","forms":["debt","debts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"欠下的錢","explanation":"指個人、公司或政府因借款或其他金融交易而必須償還的錢，是日常和財經語境中最常見的具體含義。","examples":[{"en":"The company is trying to reduce its debt before expanding.","zh":"這家公司正努力在擴大業務前減少債務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He paid off his remaining debt last month.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-583999dcd2af5df33a28","word":"debut","forms":["debut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bdaccd3631901f48","term":"debut","forms":["debut","debuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"首次公開登場","explanation":"指表演者、運動員或其他人在公眾面前的第一次正式出場。重點不是單純第一次做某事，而是第一次被正式介紹給觀眾或公眾。","examples":[{"en":"The young striker made his debut for the national team last night.","zh":"這名年輕前鋒昨晚首次代表國家隊出場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her stage debut received warm applause.","zh":"她的舞臺首演贏得了熱烈掌聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44c114375cb51366","term":"debut","forms":["debut","debuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作品首次公開呈現","explanation":"指戲劇、電影、歌曲、舞蹈、節目等作品第一次向公眾正式展示。這裡的“亮相者”不是人，而是一個作品或專案。","examples":[{"en":"The director's new film made its debut at the festival.","zh":"這位導演的新電影在電影節上首次公開放映。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The opera received mixed reviews on its London debut.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/debut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59cd793c05f0e9e7ff8c","word":"decade","forms":["decade"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab41f25378d9e1e5","term":"decade","forms":["decade","decades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"十年；十年時期","explanation":"指連續十年的一段時間，例如從2010年到2019年這一整段。它也可以泛指從某個時間點開始或結束的任意十年，而不只限於日曆年代。","examples":[{"en":"The decade from 2010 to 2019 brought rapid changes in technology.","zh":"2010年至2019年這十年給技術領域帶來了迅速的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent a decade working on the same research project.","zh":"她花了十年時間從事同一個研究專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2db681579fbe43e8e0d7","word":"decay","forms":["decay"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-acbd58ae7aca37ac","term":"decay","forms":["decay","decays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腐壞；腐爛","explanation":"指物質，尤其是有機物，隨著時間逐漸分解、腐爛，最後失去原來的狀態。這個義項就是“往下掉成腐壞”的最具體畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The smell of decay filled the abandoned house.","zh":"腐爛的氣味充滿了那座廢棄的房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cold temperatures slow the decay of food.","zh":"低溫會減緩食物的腐壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d91895e575f6e6d","term":"decay","forms":["decay","decays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衰退；衰敗","explanation":"指健康、質量、力量、地位、財富或社會狀況一點點變差，是從“物質腐壞”擴充套件到抽象事物的用法。它強調持續下降，而不是普通的一次性失敗。","examples":[{"en":"Years of neglect led to the decay of the historic town.","zh":"多年的疏於維護導致這座歷史小鎮逐漸衰敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The abandoned district showed signs of urban decay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd863a04894d78b4","term":"decay","forms":["decay","decays","decaying","decayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸惡化；衰退","explanation":"指人、事物或狀況逐漸變差，失去力量、健康、質量或原有價值。它是“往下掉”的一般動詞用法，範圍比單純的腐爛更廣。","examples":[{"en":"The old building began to decay after years without repairs.","zh":"這座老建築多年沒有維修後開始逐漸破敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Public trust can decay quickly when leaders lie.","zh":"領導人撒謊時，公眾的信任可能會迅速衰退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-746794e88d634285","term":"decay","forms":["decay","decays","decaying","decayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"腐爛；變質","explanation":"指有機物或屍體逐漸腐爛、變壞，是動詞最具體的“失去原狀”用法。與表示抽象狀況惡化的 s1 相比，它通常有明確的物質物件。","examples":[{"en":"The fruit will decay quickly in the summer heat.","zh":"水果在夏季高溫下會很快腐爛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fallen apples decayed beneath the trees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f2224ca4f0897e66c0b","word":"deceive","forms":["deceive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b82c6eba28de9b5","term":"deceive","forms":["deceive","deceives","deceiving","deceived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欺騙；誤導","explanation":"指故意用謊言、假象或其他手段把別人帶偏，讓對方相信不真實的事情；重點在於對方的判斷被改變或被矇蔽。","examples":[{"en":"They deceived us into believing that the tickets were genuine.","zh":"他們騙得我們相信那些票是真的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don’t let flashy advertisements deceive you.","zh":"別讓花哨的廣告把你騙了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deceive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9359bba1538105d98652","word":"decent","forms":["decent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c414d8594fe810ab","term":"decent","forms":["decent","more decent","most decent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合適的；恰當的","explanation":"表示某事符合當時的場合、目的或要求，做得合乎分寸。它是“達到應有標準”這條核心意思的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"This is a decent place to have lunch.","zh":"這裡是個適合吃午飯的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found a decent way to solve the problem.","zh":"她找到了一個合適的辦法來解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e02a540f403bb213","term":"decent","forms":["decent","more decent","most decent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正派的；有道德的","explanation":"形容人或行為符合基本的道德標準，表現出誠實、公平和正直等品質，也就是沒有越過“應有的分寸線”。","examples":[{"en":"He was decent enough to return the money he had found.","zh":"他人很正派，把撿到的錢還了回去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A decent employer treats everyone fairly.","zh":"正派的僱主會公平對待每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34d15a1ac4a1c731","term":"decent","forms":["decent","more decent","most decent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"尚可的；還不錯的","explanation":"表示質量或能力達到可以接受的水平，通常比“差”好，但未必優秀。這是日常評價中很常見的“過得去、還不錯”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is simple, but the rooms are decent.","zh":"這家酒店很簡單，但房間還不錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a decent meal near the station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5589aa5863c2d85622d0","word":"decide","forms":["decide"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4948bb3ad05ff8a0","term":"decide","forms":["decide","decides","deciding","decided","decidest","decidedst","decideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"決定結果；解決爭議","explanation":"指經過判斷後確定比賽、問題、爭議或其他事情的結果，也就是把幾種可能性分開並定下一種結果。","examples":[{"en":"The committee will decide the winner tomorrow.","zh":"委員會明天將決定獲勝者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to decide on a date for the meeting.","zh":"我們需要確定會議日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-111756e57ff0b497","term":"decide","forms":["decide","decides","deciding","decided","decidest","decidedst","decideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"作出判斷；決定怎麼做","explanation":"指一個人在考慮之後自己作出判斷或選擇，重點在“作決定”這個過程，而不是替別人確定結果。","examples":[{"en":"After thinking it over, Maya decided to stay.","zh":"仔細考慮後，瑪雅決定留下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We must decide whether to repair or replace it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86ae35d58a6aa3b5742d","word":"decision","forms":["decision"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97cfbbb073b52a65","term":"decision","forms":["decision","decisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作出決定","explanation":"指從幾個可能性中進行判斷並作出決定這一過程，重點在“定下來”的動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"We need to make a decision before Friday.","zh":"我們需要在星期五之前作出決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After careful discussion, the committee reached a decision.","zh":"經過仔細討論，委員會作出了決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a985388e8768c8f","term":"decision","forms":["decision","decisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"決定；判斷","explanation":"指經過考慮後得到的具體選擇或判斷，也可指法院、委員會等權威機構作出的正式裁定。","examples":[{"en":"The judge's decision changed the course of the case.","zh":"法官的裁定改變了案件的發展方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee announced its decision after lunch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-171cd9969103f91b3289","word":"decisive","forms":["decisive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c0fb00aa79698d6","term":"decisive","forms":["decisive","more decisive","most decisive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"決定性的","explanation":"指某個因素、行動或決定足以決定爭議或最終結果，讓雙方不再懸而未決。例如一票、證據或時刻可能成為決定勝負的關鍵。","examples":[{"en":"The chair's decisive vote settled the dispute.","zh":"主席的決定性一票解決了這場爭議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The goalkeeper made a decisive save in extra time.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decisive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b4d7312372abf6f","term":"decisive","forms":["decisive","more decisive","most decisive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"果斷的；迅速堅決的","explanation":"形容人、態度或行動面對選擇時迅速作出明確決定，不拖延、不猶豫。這裡的核心仍是“切開僵局”，只是切開的是行動上的猶豫。","examples":[{"en":"The manager took decisive action when the problem appeared.","zh":"問題出現後，經理果斷採取了行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her decisive leadership ended weeks of uncertainty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decisive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d830325906c3d540ae21","word":"deck","forms":["deck"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45c8a905bf32758a","term":"deck","forms":["deck","decks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平臺；露臺","explanation":"指高出地面的平坦區域，人可以在上面走動或停留，例如房屋旁的木平臺、門廊或平屋頂。","examples":[{"en":"We ate breakfast on the deck behind the house.","zh":"我們在房子後面的露臺上吃了早飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children ran out onto the wooden deck.","zh":"孩子們跑到木平臺上去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35d38ba3ebacb6db","term":"deck","forms":["deck","decks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"甲板","explanation":"指船或艇上像地板一樣的水平部分，人可以在上面行走；大型船通常有不止一層甲板。","examples":[{"en":"Passengers gathered on the deck to watch the sunset.","zh":"乘客聚集在甲板上觀看日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crew carried the boxes down to the lower deck.","zh":"船員把箱子搬到了下層甲板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caeaf78202d8ee93","term":"deck","forms":["deck","decks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一副牌","explanation":"指一整套用來玩紙牌遊戲的牌；這裡的核心畫面仍是把許多東西整齊疊放成一組。","examples":[{"en":"She shuffled the deck and dealt five cards to each player.","zh":"她洗了洗牌，然後給每位玩家發了五張牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Shuffle the deck before dealing the next hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-abcd0ee1fc2cdf511d8a","word":"declaration","forms":["declaration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03febc1815c4ca77","term":"declaration","forms":["declaration","declarations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式宣告；鄭重宣告","explanation":"指用說話或書面形式鄭重地表達、確認或宣佈某件事，重點是態度明確而且具有正式性。它可以是個人的堅定表態，也可以是組織或國家釋出的正式宣言。","examples":[{"en":"The minister made a declaration of support for the new policy.","zh":"部長正式宣告支援這項新政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her declaration that she would resign surprised everyone.","zh":"她宣佈自己將辭職，這讓所有人都很吃驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/declaration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a408b719dd66f5f","term":"declaration","forms":["declaration","declarations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"申報單；申報","explanation":"指為法律、海關或其他正式手續而列出物品、收入、事實等內容的申報，既可以指申報行為，也可以指填好的檔案。這裡的重點不是表達觀點，而是把規定的資訊正式交給機構。","examples":[{"en":"You must complete a customs declaration before collecting your luggage.","zh":"領取行李前，你必須填寫海關申報單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His customs declaration listed three bottles of imported perfume.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/declaration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7012df7548775c20321","word":"declare","forms":["declare"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-552ca0e1cc616b6c","term":"declare","forms":["declare","declares","declaring","declared","declarest","declaredst","declareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式宣佈；明確聲稱","explanation":"表示以正式、明確或帶強調的方式說出一個決定、事實或判斷，把它公開確定下來。它既可以宣佈某事，也可以說明某人被認定為某種狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The company declared that the project would begin in June.","zh":"公司正式宣佈專案將在六月開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court declared him innocent.","zh":"法院宣佈他無罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/declare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b547f55a8a536a2","term":"declare","forms":["declare","declares","declaring","declared","declarest","declaredst","declareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"申報","explanation":"表示按照法律或規定，主動向海關、稅務機關等說明自己帶入的物品、收入或相關情況。這裡的重點不是隨口告知，而是履行正式申報義務。","examples":[{"en":"You must declare all food when entering the country.","zh":"入境時必須申報所有食品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Declare these imported goods at customs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/declare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd5f8cbed3d05d63b307","word":"decline","forms":["decline"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05f59bfadf517405","term":"decline","forms":["decline","declines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下降；下落","explanation":"表示從較高位置、水平或狀態向下移動或降低，是“向下”這條核心意象最直接的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The report shows a sharp decline in sales.","zh":"報告顯示銷售額大幅下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The graph shows a steady decline in exports.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f8dc9ecd6a22035","term":"decline","forms":["decline","declines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下坡；向下的斜坡","explanation":"表示地面、道路或山路向下傾斜的部分，正是“向下傾斜的線”這一記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The road has a steep decline after the bridge.","zh":"過橋後道路有一段很陡的下坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cart gathered speed on the gentle decline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b295588f5b1f3bba","term":"decline","forms":["decline","declines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"惡化；衰退","explanation":"表示健康、能力、質量或整體狀況逐漸變弱、變壞，是“向下”從位置變化擴充套件到狀態變化。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor noticed a gradual decline in her health.","zh":"醫生注意到她的健康狀況逐漸惡化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town's population entered a prolonged decline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f8f0fdcd935874a","term":"decline","forms":["decline","declines","declining","declined","declinest","declinedst","declineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下降；下落","explanation":"表示價格、數量、水平等向下變化，是動詞最基本的“向下”用法。","examples":[{"en":"The currency declined by five percent this month.","zh":"這種貨幣本月下跌了百分之五。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Temperatures are expected to decline overnight.","zh":"預計氣溫會在夜間下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de8a239bc4b4d17d","term":"decline","forms":["decline","declines","declining","declined","declinest","declinedst","declineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"惡化；變弱","explanation":"表示健康、能力、質量或局勢逐漸變差，是“向下”用於抽象狀態的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"His eyesight began to decline after the injury.","zh":"受傷後，他的視力開始變差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His health declined rapidly after the operation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc6bbd48780b5d78","term":"decline","forms":["decline","declines","declining","declined","declinest","declinedst","declineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拒絕；不願做","explanation":"表示選擇不接受某事或不去做某事，就像把請求從自己面前轉開。","examples":[{"en":"She politely declined to answer the question.","zh":"她禮貌地拒絕回答這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had to decline their invitation.","zh":"我不得不謝絕他們的邀請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-567fa2572b1787bf0a75","word":"decorate","forms":["decorate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a73e88e2632df55","term":"decorate","forms":["decorate","decorates","decorating","decorated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝飾；點綴","explanation":"把裝飾品加到某個物體上，使它更漂亮、更有節日氣氛或更有特色。核心畫面就是給原本樸素的東西添上外在裝飾。","examples":[{"en":"The children decorated the cookies with colorful icing.","zh":"孩子們用彩色糖霜裝飾了餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We decorated the front door with a wreath.","zh":"我們在前門上掛了一個花環作裝飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decorate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11163b1853b4eaed","term":"decorate","forms":["decorate","decorates","decorating","decorated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"粉刷或貼桌布改善室內外觀","explanation":"特指透過刷漆、貼桌布等方式改善房間或房屋內部的外觀。它仍然是“讓空間變得更好看”的意思，只是裝飾手段偏向牆面處理。","examples":[{"en":"They decorated the living room before moving into the house.","zh":"他們搬進房子前粉刷並佈置了客廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We're decorating the bedroom with blue wallpaper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decorate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6ebfb432bfd40c53f71","word":"decoration","forms":["decoration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43f43f8481d94f5f","term":"decoration","forms":["decoration","decorations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝飾；裝點","explanation":"指給地方、物品或場合增添美感、氣氛或象徵意義的行為，也可以泛指這種裝點過程。重點是“進行裝飾”這一動作，而不是某一件裝飾品。","examples":[{"en":"The decoration of the hall took two days.","zh":"大廳的裝飾花了兩天時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We used bright colors for decoration.","zh":"我們用鮮豔的顏色來裝飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decoration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7f3386cff91f31c","term":"decoration","forms":["decoration","decorations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝飾物；裝飾品","explanation":"指被加到房間、物品或場合中、用來美化或增添特色的東西，例如花環、擺件或佈置物。它是“加上以美化”的具體結果。","examples":[{"en":"The children made paper decorations for the party.","zh":"孩子們為聚會製作了紙質裝飾品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wreath was the only decoration on the door.","zh":"門上唯一的裝飾是一隻花環。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decoration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2dc971f4895ca1f298f","word":"decrease","forms":["decrease"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5e34a7c48aec03c","term":"decrease","forms":["decrease","decreases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"減少量；下降幅度","explanation":"它不是“變少”這個動作本身，而是水位線往下後所呈現出的減少幅度或減少量，可以用於銷售額、人口、溫度等數量或程度。","examples":[{"en":"The company reported a slight decrease in sales last year.","zh":"公司報告稱，去年銷售額略有下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There has been a sharp decrease in the number of visitors.","zh":"遊客人數出現了大幅減少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decrease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0aa013bde537d244","term":"decrease","forms":["decrease","decreases","decreasing","decreased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變少；降低","explanation":"水位線自己往下就是這種用法：某個數量、程度或水平從較高狀態變得更小，不強調是誰造成的。","examples":[{"en":"The quality of the products has decreased since the main designer left.","zh":"首席設計師離開後，這些產品的質量下降了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature will decrease overnight.","zh":"氣溫將在夜間下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decrease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f267388a08785d36","term":"decrease","forms":["decrease","decreases","decreasing","decreased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變少；減少","explanation":"有人擰低閥門讓水位線下降，就是讓某個數量、程度或水平變小；重點在於主語主動造成了減少。","examples":[{"en":"Please decrease the volume so we can hear each other.","zh":"請把音量調小一點，這樣我們才能聽見彼此說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new lights decrease our electricity costs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/decrease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d232f6a3a44c379b1e7b","word":"dedicate","forms":["dedicate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b53b1b3046ddc6ac","term":"dedicate","forms":["dedicate","dedicates","dedicating","dedicated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"專門用於","explanation":"把錢、時間、空間或其他資源專門留給某種用途，核心仍是“從一般用途裡分出來，交給一個目標”。","examples":[{"en":"They dedicated part of the budget to improving public transport.","zh":"他們把一部分預算專門用於改善公共交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dedicates two hours every evening to study.","zh":"她每天晚上拿出兩個小時專門學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dedicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c49bea4e77352502","term":"dedicate","forms":["dedicate","dedicates","dedicating","dedicated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"全心投入","explanation":"把自己、自己的時間和精力堅定地投入某種行動、事業或思想方向，表示長期而認真的承諾。","examples":[{"en":"After graduating, he dedicated himself to helping rural children.","zh":"畢業後，他全心投入幫助農村兒童的事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team has dedicated its efforts to finding a safer solution.","zh":"團隊一直致力於尋找更安全的解決方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dedicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30754e64c313955b21ea","word":"dedication","forms":["dedication"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba89462cdf5f7a1a","term":"dedication","forms":["dedication","dedications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投入；奉獻","explanation":"指把時間、精力或注意力持續投入某項工作、事業或目標的態度和狀態，也就是把自己鄭重地交給某個目的。","examples":[{"en":"She completed the project with remarkable dedication.","zh":"她以非凡的投入完成了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His dedication to helping young musicians is widely admired.","zh":"他致力於幫助年輕音樂家，這一點廣受讚賞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dedication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c0dbb98512a2d7c","term":"dedication","forms":["dedication","dedications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獻詞","explanation":"指寫在書籍、音樂作品或其他藝術作品開頭、獻給某位親友或贊助人的短文，以表達敬意、感激或 affection。","examples":[{"en":"The novel begins with a dedication to the author's mother.","zh":"這部小說開頭有一篇獻給作者母親的獻詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dedication thanks her parents for their encouragement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dedication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd889c661913abe1819d","word":"deduct","forms":["deduct"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19e82c280ed8d080","term":"deduct","forms":["deduct","deducts","deducting","deducted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"扣除；減去","explanation":"把一部分從總額、數量或應得之物中拿掉，使剩下的數額變小。例如從工資中扣稅，就是先有一筆工資總額，再從中 deduct 一部分。","examples":[{"en":"The company will deduct the repair cost from my final payment.","zh":"公司會從我的最後一筆款項中扣除維修費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can deduct the discount from the original price.","zh":"你可以從原價中減去折扣金額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deduct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df75f3ea1d63370ba642","word":"deed","forms":["deed"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c4dc0ec6f694146","term":"deed","forms":["deed","deeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行為；行動","explanation":"deed 指已經做出的某個行為或行動，重點在“事情確實被做出來了”，而不只是計劃或想法。","examples":[{"en":"One kind deed can brighten someone's whole day.","zh":"一個善意的舉動可以讓某人的一整天都變得明亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her quiet deeds helped many people.","zh":"她默默做出的許多善舉幫助了很多人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a154b827bfe507d9","term":"deed","forms":["deed","deeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實際行動","explanation":"在強調行動而不是說法、承諾或思考時，deed 指真正做出的事實，核心是“用行動證明”。","examples":[{"en":"She showed her support in word and deed.","zh":"她在言語和行動上都表示了支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His deeds showed more generosity than his speeches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98b8e7d4f9e60929","term":"deed","forms":["deed","deeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房產契據","explanation":"在房地產語境中，deed 是證明房屋、土地等不動產權利或轉移的正式檔案；它把“做出的法律行為”記錄並證明下來。","examples":[{"en":"The deed to the house is kept in a safe place.","zh":"這所房子的產權契據被儲存在一個安全的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She received the deed to the land after the sale.","zh":"交易完成後，她拿到了這塊土地的產權契據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3bc826833fd649047fa","word":"deem","forms":["deem"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ecec047c5166b05","term":"deem","forms":["deem","deems","deeming","deemed","deemest","deemedst","deemeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認定為；視為","explanation":"deem 表示經過判斷後把某人或某事認定為某種狀態或性質，相當於把判斷結果明確地歸到一個類別中。","examples":[{"en":"The committee deemed the proposal impractical.","zh":"委員會認定這項提議不切實際。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The equipment was deemed safe for use.","zh":"這套裝置被認定可以安全使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab1eefb3b8f4f979","term":"deem","forms":["deem","deems","deeming","deemed","deemest","deemedst","deemeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為；想；判斷","explanation":"deem 也可以表示經過考慮後認為某事如此，重點在於形成一個判斷或意見，而不只是瞬間的感覺。它和“認定為……”相連，但有時後面直接接從句或不明確說出判斷結果。","examples":[{"en":"Experts deem the plan unlikely to succeed.","zh":"專家認為這項計劃不太可能成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The change was deemed necessary after careful review.","zh":"經過仔細審查後，這項改變被認為是必要的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74611c1d6455b534323a","word":"deep","forms":["deep"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c54ed5d87ca6d7d7","term":"deep","forms":["deep","deeper","more deep","deepest","most deep"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深的；深入的","explanation":"表示從表面、邊緣或某個參照點向下或向內延伸很遠。既可說湖水、洞穴等實際空間，也可用於抽象內容。","examples":[{"en":"The lake is extremely deep.","zh":"這個湖深得不得了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful—the snow is deep near the trees.","zh":"小心，樹旁的雪很深。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2965488507e608d6","term":"deep","forms":["deep","deeper","more deep","deepest","most deep"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深刻的；複雜的","explanation":"表示思想、感情或問題不在表面，包含需要認真理解的內容；有時也表示關係或社會情況盤根錯節。","examples":[{"en":"That simple question led to a surprisingly deep conversation.","zh":"那個簡單的問題竟然引出了非常深入的談話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a deep understanding of the problem.","zh":"她讓我對這個問題有了深入的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e81b1dce34c18508","term":"deep","forms":["deep","deeper","more deep","deepest","most deep"],"pos":"adj","zh":"低沉的","explanation":"形容聲音或嗓音的音調低，不是說音量小；人的聲音、樂器聲或其他聲響都可以這樣描述。","examples":[{"en":"His deep voice carried across the room.","zh":"他低沉的聲音傳遍了整個房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A deep drumbeat echoed through the hall.","zh":"低沉的鼓聲在大廳裡迴盪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf1b275e4930a808","term":"deep","forms":["deep","deeper","more deep","deepest","most deep"],"pos":"adv","zh":"深入地；在深處","explanation":"表示動作向地下、內部或遠處延伸很深，保留了“往深處去”的空間畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The roots grow deep underground.","zh":"這些根在地下向深處生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roots extend deep beneath the house.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46854e82a3ccdcfd916d","word":"deepen","forms":["deepen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93e7edecb33cef11","term":"deepen","forms":["deepen","deepens","deepening","deepened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變深","explanation":"把井、洞、水域等實際空間向下加深，就是讓它們有更大的深度；這是“往更深處延伸”這一核心概念的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"They deepened the pond to store more water.","zh":"他們把池塘挖深，以便儲存更多的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dredger deepened the channel for larger ships.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deepen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9bc47dd031444535","term":"deepen","forms":["deepen","deepens","deepening","deepened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使感情更強烈","explanation":"讓悲傷、擔憂、同情等情緒變得更強、更難以忽視，就像情緒向內加深了一層。","examples":[{"en":"The unexpected news deepened her anxiety.","zh":"這個意外訊息加重了她的焦慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their shared hardships deepened their friendship.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deepen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-937228f8e0558949","term":"deepen","forms":["deepen","deepens","deepening","deepened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使理解更深入","explanation":"透過學習或經歷，讓理解、知識、研究等從表面走向更全面、更透徹的層次。","examples":[{"en":"The workshop deepened my understanding of local history.","zh":"這次研討會加深了我對當地歷史的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The visit deepened our understanding of island life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deepen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-566aed6514feea3b","term":"deepen","forms":["deepen","deepens","deepening","deepened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變深","explanation":"水域、洞穴或其他實際空間隨著延伸而變得更深，是“往更深處發展”的不及物用法。","examples":[{"en":"The river deepens near the bridge.","zh":"這條河在橋附近變深。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The snow deepened as the storm continued.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deepen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acf5bfd986de639d820d","word":"deer","forms":["deer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20ec3312dab9bf44","term":"deer","forms":["deer","deers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鹿","explanation":"指鹿科動物，通常有蹄，成年雄鹿常有角；有時也泛指外形相近的相關動物。記住森林裡的“鹿”這個畫面，就能抓住這個詞最主要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw three deer near the edge of the forest.","zh":"我們在森林邊緣看到了三隻鹿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A deer crossed the road in front of my car.","zh":"一隻鹿從我的車前穿過了馬路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37a8eec1ce19687d132f","word":"default","forms":["default"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04615f3acef05457","term":"default","forms":["default","defaults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"違約；未履行義務","explanation":"指本來應該履行付款、還款或其他義務，卻沒有按要求完成的狀態。重點是“該做的事沒做”，常見於金融和商業語境。","examples":[{"en":"The company is in default on its loan.","zh":"這家公司沒有按期償還貸款，已經違約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bank sent a warning after the borrower went into default.","zh":"借款人違約後，銀行發出了警告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/default","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3dbe1aef1bc7d2b","term":"default","forms":["default","defaults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出廠預設設定","explanation":"指裝置或軟體在使用者沒有改動之前預先設定的原始設定，也就是系統一開始自動採用的安排。","examples":[{"en":"You can restore the phone to its factory defaults.","zh":"你可以把手機恢復為出廠預設設定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The printer's default settings use ordinary paper.","zh":"這臺印表機的預設設定使用普通紙張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/default","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ec1a62d0b7f5cc1","term":"default","forms":["default","defaults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沒有其他選擇時的結果","explanation":"指沒有人或沒有選項主動作出選擇，於是某人或某方案自然成了結果。這個意義把“沒有另行選擇”延伸成“因缺少替代方案而被採用”。","examples":[{"en":"With no one else willing to lead, Maya became the leader by default.","zh":"沒有其他人願意帶頭，瑪雅就這樣成了預設的領導者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Toast became our dinner by default when the oven failed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/default","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8ebfada440b0a7b","term":"default","forms":["default","defaults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預設值；預設標準","explanation":"指使用者沒有提供具體數值或選項時，系統、程式或規則暫時採用的值或標準。它是“沒有另行選擇，就自動採用”的最典型技術用法。","examples":[{"en":"If you do not enter a number, the default is 10.","zh":"如果你不輸入數字，預設值就是十。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program saves files in this folder by default.","zh":"這個程式預設把檔案儲存在這個資料夾裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/default","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27540cca1bcc8fb4","term":"default","forms":["default","defaults","defaulting","defaulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"違約；未履行義務","explanation":"指沒有履行付款、還款或其他正式義務。它把 default 的核心“該做的事沒有做”直接用作動詞。","examples":[{"en":"The borrower defaulted on the loan after losing his job.","zh":"借款人失業後無力償還貸款，因而違約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several customers defaulted on their payments this month.","zh":"這個月有幾名客戶沒有履行付款義務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/default","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fdfc721b3d33453","term":"default","forms":["default","defaults","defaulting","defaulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"自動採用預設值","explanation":"指在沒有給出具體值時，程式、裝置或規則自動採用某個預設值。它就是“沒有另行選擇，系統替你選擇”的動詞表達。","examples":[{"en":"If no color is specified, the background defaults to white.","zh":"如果沒有指定顏色，背景就預設顯示為白色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The system defaults to the smallest available size.","zh":"系統預設採用可用的最小尺寸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/default","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5fff5b4eec6c48b6a82d","word":"defeat","forms":["defeat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1802b289faf23407","term":"defeat","forms":["defeat","defeats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"失敗；敗北","explanation":"指一方在比賽、鬥爭或競爭中輸掉，也就是被對手壓倒的結果。它強調“輸掉這一次”的結果，而不只是一般意義上的不成功。","examples":[{"en":"The team suffered a narrow defeat in the final.","zh":"這支隊伍在決賽中惜敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team accepted defeat with remarkable grace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defeat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3d8bcb2a1a3bcd9","term":"defeat","forms":["defeat","defeats","defeating","defeated","defeatest","defeatedst","defeateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打敗；戰勝","explanation":"指在戰爭、比賽、爭論或其他競爭中戰勝對手，讓對方失去取勝的機會。它是“把對手壓倒”的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Our school defeated its biggest rival by two points.","zh":"我們學校以兩分之差擊敗了最大的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our team defeated the visitors by three goals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defeat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00a6009aac697f11c40f","word":"defect","forms":["defect"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b9efbf530078729","term":"defect","forms":["defect","defects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺陷；瑕疵","explanation":"指某物本身存在的毛病、損壞或不完美之處，像物品上實際出現的一個缺口。","examples":[{"en":"The inspector found a defect in the electrical wiring.","zh":"檢查員發現電線系統中有一處缺陷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The table was rejected because of a defect in the wood.","zh":"這張桌子因為木材有瑕疵而被拒收。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16e92f71cae5854e","term":"defect","forms":["defect","defects","defecting","defected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"叛離；轉投另一方","explanation":"指一個人離開原來的組織或政治陣營，不再效忠原來的一方，甚至轉而支援另一方；這裡的核心畫面是“從隊伍中抽身”。","examples":[{"en":"Several members defected from the party after the leadership change.","zh":"領導層變動後，幾名成員背離了該黨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer defected to the opposing side.","zh":"這名軍官投向了對立的一方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff1f017072ccd92fb1db","word":"defend","forms":["defend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1acbf0a22b180584","term":"defend","forms":["defend","defends","defending","defended","defendest","defendedst","defendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；抵禦攻擊","explanation":"站在防線前擋住攻擊，保護人、地方、國家或其他物件。這是 defend 最基本、最容易擴充套件出的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers defended the town against the invading army.","zh":"士兵們抵禦入侵軍隊，保衛了這座城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She defended her friend when everyone else blamed him.","zh":"大家都責怪她的朋友時，她站出來保護他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13869c815de1c193","term":"defend","forms":["defend","defends","defending","defended","defendest","defendedst","defendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……辯護；支援","explanation":"把 defend 從身體上的防守擴充套件到言語上：當別人批評某人、某個決定或某種觀點時，公開站出來支援它。","examples":[{"en":"The manager defended the new policy during the meeting.","zh":"經理在會議上為新政策辯護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She defended the policy against accusations of unfairness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94cbd591bdfbeb1170ae","word":"defendant","forms":["defendant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd479e8d0fa460c3","term":"defendant","forms":["defendant","defendants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"民事案件中的被告","explanation":"在民事訴訟中，defendant 是被另一方起訴、需要對訴狀或賠償要求作出回應的人。可以把它記成站在法庭“防守方”的人。","examples":[{"en":"The defendant denied causing the damage and asked the court to dismiss the case.","zh":"被告否認造成了損失，並請求法院駁回案件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The defendant disputed the homeowner's claim for damages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defendant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3817728b5adaddf","term":"defendant","forms":["defendant","defendants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刑事案件中的被告人","explanation":"在刑事訴訟中，defendant 是被控犯罪、需要在法庭上回應指控的人；這仍然是“站在防守方應對指控”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The defendant pleaded not guilty at the first hearing.","zh":"被告人在第一次聽證會上表示不認罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"During the trial, the defendant sat quietly beside her lawyer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defendant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b0b7e51ee5d8e25cc87","word":"defense","forms":["defense"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-105c2b06578cb718","term":"defense","forms":["defense","defenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"防禦；保護","explanation":"指抵禦攻擊、危險或傷害的行動或過程，就像用盾牌把危險擋在外面。","examples":[{"en":"The walls provided defense against the invading army.","zh":"城牆為抵禦入侵軍隊提供了防護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise helps strengthen the body's natural defenses.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於增強身體的自然防禦力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bed004fa05e4782","term":"defense","forms":["defense","defenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支援；辯護","explanation":"指支援某人、某個觀點或某件事的理由和說法，相當於為對方豎起一面看不見的盾。","examples":[{"en":"Her brother came to her defense when the criticism became unfair.","zh":"批評變得不公平時，她哥哥站出來替她說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spoke in defense of the dismissed workers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3385036fb565b6059bc0","word":"defensible","forms":["defensible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4b63d0f122e6993","term":"defensible","forms":["defensible","more defensible","most defensible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"站得住腳的","explanation":"指觀點、決定、政策或行為有足夠的理由，可以面對批評和質疑而得到辯護。它不一定表示人人都同意，只表示支援它的理由足夠合理。","examples":[{"en":"Her decision was defensible given the information available at the time.","zh":"考慮到當時掌握的資訊，她的決定是站得住腳的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report presents a defensible argument for changing the policy.","zh":"這份報告提出了一個有充分理由支援修改政策的論點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defensible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-487848b7fffcc3e2","term":"defensible","forms":["defensible","more defensible","most defensible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易於防守的","explanation":"指地點、陣地或建築的地形和佈局使它不容易被武力攻佔，因此可以有效守住。它強調防守條件有利，不一定表示已經有人在那裡防守。","examples":[{"en":"The hill was defensible because attackers could approach from only one side.","zh":"這座山易於防守，因為進攻者只能從一側接近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow entrance made the hilltop fortress defensible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defensible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cf2c255b068bb691498","word":"defensive","forms":["defensive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ef2f8817af0d2ae","term":"defensive","forms":["defensive","more defensive","most defensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"防禦性的；保護性的","explanation":"指某物的目的在於保護人、地點或系統，使其免受攻擊或傷害；重點是把盾牌立在前面。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers built a defensive perimeter around the village.","zh":"士兵們在村子周圍建立了防禦圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The helmet is part of the team's defensive equipment.","zh":"這頂頭盔是隊伍防護裝備的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3cc16aab085017b","term":"defensive","forms":["defensive","more defensive","most defensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"用於威懾攻擊的","explanation":"指某種武器、系統或部署雖然屬於防禦一方，卻透過顯示反擊能力來阻止對方發動攻擊。","examples":[{"en":"The country developed a defensive missile system to protect its cities.","zh":"這個國家研發了防禦性導彈系統來保護城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fortress had formidable defensive walls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e7438a12be07638","term":"defensive","forms":["defensive","more defensive","most defensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"以儘量降低風險的","explanation":"指行動時優先避免事故、損失或失敗，而不是追求最快、最激進的結果；這也是把盾牌用於提前避險。","examples":[{"en":"Defensive driving can help you avoid accidents in heavy traffic.","zh":"防禦性駕駛能幫助你在車流量大的路上避免事故。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fund follows a defensive investment strategy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3557268ebbd59cdd90c9","word":"defiance","forms":["defiance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a4137567b205e8d","term":"defiance","forms":["defiance","defiances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反抗精神","explanation":"指一個人不願屈服、面對權威或壓力仍堅持抗拒的內在態度或精神。它強調“不後退”的心理狀態，是後面各種公開反抗行為的根源。","examples":[{"en":"She faced the pressure with quiet defiance.","zh":"她以一種安靜而堅定的反抗精神面對壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers' defiance inspired others to speak out.","zh":"工人們不肯屈服的精神鼓舞了其他人站出來發聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defiance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4885997444e20cc","term":"defiance","forms":["defiance","defiances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公開抗拒","explanation":"指公開、強硬地抵抗權威、命令、對手或強大力量，甚至拒絕放棄。相比單純心裡不服，它更強調已經表現為行動或明確立場。","examples":[{"en":"They continued the protest in defiance of the court order.","zh":"他們公然違抗法院命令，繼續舉行抗議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He refused to leave in defiance of the manager's request.","zh":"他公然不顧經理的要求，拒絕離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defiance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b172744548c9b2b03302","word":"deficit","forms":["deficit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-366454f29669c948","term":"deficit","forms":["deficit","deficits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不足；缺口","explanation":"指數量、質量或資源沒有達到應有或需要的水平，也就是留下了一個缺口。這個缺口可以出現在降雨、產量、資金等許多方面。","examples":[{"en":"The region is facing a serious deficit in water supplies.","zh":"這個地區正面臨嚴重的供水缺口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A deficit of skilled workers is slowing the project.","zh":"熟練工人的短缺正在拖慢這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deficit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c66b44798616669","term":"deficit","forms":["deficit","deficits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財政赤字；收支缺口","explanation":"特指一段時期內支出超過收入所形成的金額缺口，常見於政府預算、公司賬目或個人財務。這裡的 deficit 就是“花出去的比收進來的多”。","examples":[{"en":"The government is trying to reduce its budget deficit.","zh":"政府正努力減少預算赤字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government borrowed money to cover the deficit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deficit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecd38f260821a09a8fd4","word":"define","forms":["define"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-278e66cbdec12f1f","term":"define","forms":["define","defines","defining","defined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"明確界定","explanation":"指把某個事物的特徵或範圍劃得很清楚，使人能夠準確辨認它。它強調從模糊變得清晰，而不只是隨便描述幾句。","examples":[{"en":"The sharp contrast defines the edges of the image.","zh":"鮮明的對比清楚地勾勒出了影象的邊緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement clearly defines each partner's responsibilities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/define","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7889113daad9b46e","term":"define","forms":["define","defines","defining","defined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說明本質或身份","explanation":"指說明某人或某物最重要的特徵，也可以表示一個人如何界定自己、把自己看成什麼。這裡是在給“我是誰”畫出核心輪廓。","examples":[{"en":"She defines herself as a teacher and a lifelong learner.","zh":"她把自己看作教師和終身學習者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her dedication to teaching defined her professional life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/define","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3a4108dae265fe4","term":"define","forms":["define","defines","defining","defined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說明詞義","explanation":"指明確說出一個詞、短語、符號或概念是什麼意思，相當於給它畫出清楚的意義邊界。","examples":[{"en":"The dictionary defines this word as a formal expression of agreement.","zh":"這本詞典把這個詞解釋為表示正式同意的說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you define the term in simple language?","zh":"你能用簡單的話解釋這個術語嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/define","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bd0bb132fad95b7","term":"define","forms":["define","defines","defining","defined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"劃定邊界","explanation":"指明確劃出一個地區、物體或抽象概念的邊界，讓它和周圍或相近的東西分開。它是“用筆畫出輪廓”這一核心畫面的直接體現。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement clearly defines the boundaries of the two properties.","zh":"這份協議清楚地劃定了兩處房產的邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stone wall defines the property's northern boundary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/define","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b63ac47336bc7d8aa75","word":"definite","forms":["definite"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d836b9f8874d7aaa","term":"definite","forms":["definite","more definite","most definite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明確的；有確定範圍的","explanation":"某個東西的邊界、數量、時間或尺寸已經說清楚，不是模糊或大概的。它就像在事物周圍畫出一條清楚的線。","examples":[{"en":"We need a definite date for the meeting.","zh":"我們需要確定一個會議日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project has a definite end date.","zh":"這個專案有明確的結束日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/definite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4a65b2fcb39d418","term":"definite","forms":["definite","more definite","most definite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"確定無疑的","explanation":"表示沒有明顯疑問或猶豫，事實、答案或知識已經足夠確定。這裡的“確定”不是範圍清楚，而是對真實性或結論有把握。","examples":[{"en":"There is no definite answer yet.","zh":"目前還沒有明確答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dark clouds are a definite sign of rain.","zh":"烏雲是明顯的下雨跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/definite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71c1c178191a5d90","term":"definite","forms":["definite","more definite","most definite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特指的","explanation":"在語法中，表示說話人和聽話人都能確定所指物件，或物件已經在語境中被識別出來。它仍然延續“邊界清楚”的核心：不是泛指某一類，而是指向一個明確物件。","examples":[{"en":"The definite article points to a specific person or thing.","zh":"定冠詞指向特定的人或事物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We use the definite article when the listener knows which book we mean.","zh":"當聽話人知道我們指的是哪本書時，我們使用定冠詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/definite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c4ed1afbfdaa1e4c3bf","word":"definition","forms":["definition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a64555a2cbb263f","term":"definition","forms":["definition","definitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詞語或符號的定義","explanation":"指說明一個詞、片語、符號或概念是什麼意思的表述，尤其指字典中的釋義。它是在給這個物件畫出含義的邊界。","examples":[{"en":"The dictionary gives a clear definition of the word.","zh":"這本詞典給出了這個詞的清晰定義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your definition of an elephant needs to be more precise.","zh":"你對“大象”的定義需要更準確。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/definition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7faf8bf2c3b1b888","term":"definition","forms":["definition","definitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本質的表述","explanation":"指用一句話或一種表述說明某事物最重要的性質和本質。它比普通的詞典釋義更寬，可以用於人物、行為、制度或抽象概念。","examples":[{"en":"The essay offers a new definition of leadership.","zh":"這篇文章提出了對領導力的新表述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His definition of courage includes acting despite reasonable fear.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/definition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a67a0b358c7ac203499b","word":"definitive","forms":["definitive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c9f72137ec1e8a2","term":"definitive","forms":["definitive","more definitive","most definitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"決定性的；最終定案的","explanation":"指某個行動、證據或結果能夠決定事情的最後走向，相當於給爭議蓋上最終印章。重點不是“很重要”本身，而是它能使結果基本確定下來。","examples":[{"en":"The final vote was definitive.","zh":"最後的投票決定了結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We still need definitive evidence before making a public statement.","zh":"在公開發表宣告前，我們仍需要決定性的證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/definitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53e00fe00f491e40","term":"definitive","forms":["definitive","more definitive","most definitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"權威而完整的；定論性的","explanation":"指內容全面、可靠，並且足以被當作最終權威依據的事物。它把“定案”的印章擴充套件為“完整且值得信賴的標準版本”。","examples":[{"en":"This book is considered the definitive guide to the region.","zh":"這本書被認為是介紹該地區最權威、最完整的指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers have not yet reached a definitive conclusion.","zh":"研究人員還沒有得出最終而明確的結論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/definitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98c73bd75ba63d2d930c","word":"defy","forms":["defy"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-217c34dc34013f21","term":"defy","forms":["defy","defies","defying","defied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"挑戰；蔑視","explanation":"表示迎著某個人、危險、力量或反對意見而上，公開表示自己不怕、不會退縮。它可以挑戰具體的人，也可以挑戰一種力量或觀點。","examples":[{"en":"She defied the critics and released the film anyway.","zh":"她無視批評者的反對，還是發行了這部電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The climber defied the danger and continued upward.","zh":"那名登山者迎著危險繼續向上攀登。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20aa4b032ef83f19","term":"defy","forms":["defy","defies","defying","defied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"違抗；拒不服從","explanation":"表示明知某人有權發出要求，卻故意不聽從，帶有公然抗命的意味。重點不是普通地“拒絕”，而是把命令或權威頂回去。","examples":[{"en":"The student defied the teacher's instructions and left the room.","zh":"那名學生違抗老師的指示，離開了教室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was punished for defying the court's order.","zh":"他因違抗法院命令而受到懲罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/defy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b308a7f43bba8e7a366b","word":"degree","forms":["degree"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72a850fa53779160","term":"degree","forms":["degree","degrees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學位","explanation":"指大學或學院授予的學位，表示完成了某一階段的學習並取得相應資格。常見的 bachelor’s degree 是學士學位，master’s degree 是碩士學位。","examples":[{"en":"She earned a degree in biology last year.","zh":"她去年獲得了生物學學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is working toward a master's degree.","zh":"他正在攻讀碩士學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/degree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59a52398d53da55f","term":"degree","forms":["degree","degrees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"角度單位","explanation":"指角度的單位；一個圓分成 360 個 degree，所以直角是 90 degrees。這個義項仍然保留了“把整體分成一格格”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Turn the handle ninety degrees to the right.","zh":"把把手向右轉九十度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A full circle has 360 degrees.","zh":"一個整圓有 360 度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/degree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5aa6a3ce74bf611","term":"degree","forms":["degree","degrees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溫度單位","explanation":"指溫度刻度上的一度，用於攝氏、華氏等溫標。具體是哪一種溫標通常由上下文或 Celsius、Fahrenheit 等詞說明。","examples":[{"en":"The temperature reached 35 degrees yesterday.","zh":"昨天氣溫達到了 35 度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius.","zh":"水在攝氏零度結冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/degree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e16db102267e6e7de7f","word":"delay","forms":["delay"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af3226e1d9d2f3a6","term":"delay","forms":["delay","delays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"延誤；耽擱","explanation":"指事情沒有按原定時間發生，或指這段被拖出來的等待時間；核心畫面就是事情被暫時按住了。","examples":[{"en":"The flight arrived after a two-hour delay.","zh":"航班延誤了兩個小時後才到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We apologize for the delay in replying.","zh":"很抱歉回覆晚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a05f88e8825c0ce","term":"delay","forms":["delay","delays","delaying","delayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推遲；延期","explanation":"指主動把某件事安排到更晚的時候做，也就是把事情按住而不讓它現在發生。","examples":[{"en":"They delayed the launch until next month.","zh":"他們把釋出推遲到了下個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't delay making a decision.","zh":"請不要拖著不作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d563f94c1046404","term":"delay","forms":["delay","delays","delaying","delayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使耽擱；使受阻","explanation":"指某種天氣、故障或其他原因讓人或事情暫時無法按計劃前進，相當於把它拖住。","examples":[{"en":"Heavy snow delayed the buses this morning.","zh":"今天早上的大雪使公交車晚點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Roadworks delayed the ambulance by several minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e80f7b8f93bcb8c0","term":"delay","forms":["delay","delays","delaying","delayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拖延；遲遲不行動","explanation":"指自己不馬上行動，停留或猶豫太久；這裡不是外界把你按住，而是你自己一直沒有向前走。","examples":[{"en":"Don't delay—apply before the deadline.","zh":"別再拖了——請在截止日期前申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't delay; the final bus leaves soon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f216e33c5cf9add9d70","word":"delegate","forms":["delegate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-961aaafd2841dd4f","term":"delegate","forms":["delegate","delegates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表；代理人","explanation":"delegate 是被授權替別人處理事務、作決定或表達意見的人，核心畫面就是“替別人接過權力去辦事”。","examples":[{"en":"She attended the meeting as the director's delegate.","zh":"她作為主任的代表參加了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The delegate was authorized to sign the agreement.","zh":"這名代表獲授權簽署協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delegate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0c3b15dd290c7a4","term":"delegate","forms":["delegate","delegates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"會議代表","explanation":"在會議、集會或大會中，delegate 指代表某個組織、地區或群體出席並參與討論的人。","examples":[{"en":"More than two hundred delegates attended the annual conference.","zh":"兩百多名代表參加了年度會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each school sent a delegate to the conference.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delegate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-204eb9d3a75744a1","term":"delegate","forms":["delegate","delegates","delegating","delegated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"進行委派","explanation":"delegate 表示管理者把工作分給別人處理，讓對方承擔相應的執行責任；核心仍是“把手裡的事交出去”。","examples":[{"en":"A good manager knows when to delegate.","zh":"優秀的經理知道什麼時候該委派工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She delegates well and gives her team room to work.","zh":"她很善於委派工作，也給團隊留下了發揮空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delegate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3bedb97c55c45a07","term":"delegate","forms":["delegate","delegates","delegating","delegated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把任務交給某人","explanation":"表示把某項任務、職責或許可權正式交給某人，通常是為了讓對方負責完成。","examples":[{"en":"The supervisor delegated the report to Maya.","zh":"主管把報告交給瑪雅負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He delegated responsibility for the project to his deputy.","zh":"他把專案責任交給了副手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delegate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5214bf637717ddb480ec","word":"delegation","forms":["delegation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1cdbf8b9d2f81ac","term":"delegation","forms":["delegation","delegations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"委派；授權","explanation":"指把任務、權力或處理某事的責任交給別人，而不是自己親自完成；重點在“交出去”這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"Good delegation gives team members clear responsibilities.","zh":"良好的任務委派會讓團隊成員清楚自己的責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager is responsible for the delegation of daily tasks.","zh":"經理負責分配日常任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delegation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e1ebd8e9e76369a","term":"delegation","forms":["delegation","delegations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表團","explanation":"指代表某個國家、組織或團體參加會議、訪問或談判的一群人；這裡 delegation 不是“委派動作”，而是被派出的代表們。","examples":[{"en":"A trade delegation from Japan will visit the factory next week.","zh":"一個來自日本的貿易代表團下週將訪問這家工廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A trade delegation arrived to discuss agricultural exports.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delegation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2277d8c05881e3c9bbc5","word":"deliberate","forms":["deliberate"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ab942386e4ff3ce","term":"deliberate","forms":["deliberate","more deliberate","most deliberate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"故意的；有意為之的","explanation":"指某人明知自己在做什麼，特意採取某種行動，而不是偶然發生。這個意義像是在天平上掂量過後，明確選擇了要做這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The damage was a deliberate act, not an accident.","zh":"這次損壞是故意造成的，不是意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a deliberate attempt to include everyone.","zh":"她特意努力讓每個人都參與進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deliberate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1cbb63ab46e689fa","term":"deliberate","forms":["deliberate","more deliberate","most deliberate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"經過審慎考慮的","explanation":"指決定、意見或措施不是倉促產生的，而是在比較理由、後果或不同選擇之後形成的。這裡的重點不是“故意”，而是行動前已經認真掂量過。","examples":[{"en":"After reviewing the evidence, the board made a deliberate decision.","zh":"審查證據後，董事會作出了經過審慎考慮的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her deliberate choice of words avoided unnecessary offense.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deliberate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f709b58f9fad6d4d","term":"deliberate","forms":["deliberate","deliberates","deliberating","deliberated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細權衡某事","explanation":"指把某個問題放在心裡反覆稱量，認真考慮它的事實、理由和後果。它是形容詞“經過權衡的”背後的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The committee deliberated on the proposal before voting.","zh":"委員會在投票前認真權衡了這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The panel deliberated over the evidence for hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deliberate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ebe2f078effe96c3","term":"deliberate","forms":["deliberate","deliberates","deliberating","deliberated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"權衡利弊；反覆思考","explanation":"指把支援和反對某個選擇的理由放在一起比較，並思考應該採取什麼行動。重點是來回衡量，而不是漫無目的地發呆。","examples":[{"en":"They deliberated over whether to accept the offer.","zh":"他們反覆權衡是否接受這份提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jury deliberated for six hours before returning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deliberate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-447f7f5c325ea17e635b","word":"delicate","forms":["delicate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23429be9fe026e47","term":"delicate","forms":["delicate","more delicate","delicater","most delicate","delicatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易損的；需小心處理的","explanation":"指材質或狀態很容易被弄壞、撕裂或損傷，因此需要輕柔、謹慎地處理，就像薄瓷器或蕾絲一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Please wash this delicate fabric by hand.","zh":"請手洗這塊容易損壞的精細布料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glass ornaments are delicate, so pack them carefully.","zh":"這些玻璃裝飾品很易碎，所以要小心包裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54af433b3abfa031","term":"delicate","forms":["delicate","more delicate","delicater","most delicate","delicatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"纖細的；線條精巧的","explanation":"指外形、結構或線條細而精巧，給人輕盈、柔美的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The artist drew delicate lines around the flowers.","zh":"畫家在花朵周圍畫出了纖細的線條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sketch captures the bird's delicate wing bones.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c29fc3464377a28ffe2","word":"delicious","forms":["delicious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-121f9e956b1c613f","term":"delicious","forms":["delicious","more delicious","most delicious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"美味的；好吃的","explanation":"指食物或飲料的味道非常好，讓人吃得滿足、想繼續享用，是這個詞最常見也最應該先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The soup was delicious, so I asked for another bowl.","zh":"湯非常好喝，所以我又要了一碗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had delicious dumplings after the hike.","zh":"徒步後我們吃了美味的餃子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a55e13956b2ee834","term":"delicious","forms":["delicious","more delicious","most delicious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人愉快的；賞心悅目的","explanation":"這裡不是說真的能吃，而是把“好吃得讓人享受”的感覺借來形容幽默、諷刺、畫面或想法特別過癮、討人喜歡。","examples":[{"en":"The film has a deliciously unexpected ending.","zh":"這部電影有一個出人意料而且很過癮的結尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She enjoyed the delicious coolness of the evening breeze.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-315393e576685d59a397","word":"delight","forms":["delight"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02fa5fc49e9c388d","term":"delight","forms":["delight","delights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜悅；快樂","explanation":"指因某人、某事或某種經歷而產生的強烈喜悅，是一種被某事點亮的心情。","examples":[{"en":"The children listened to the story with delight.","zh":"孩子們興致勃勃地聽著這個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child's delight was impossible to miss.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56ca01d7a93546e6","term":"delight","forms":["delight","delights","delighting","delighted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人非常高興","explanation":"指某人或某事把另一個人的心情點亮，使其產生強烈喜悅；主語是帶來喜悅的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The surprise gift delighted my daughter.","zh":"這份意外的禮物讓我的女兒非常高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unexpected visit delighted her elderly father.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee5dce7139fc7558a7dc","word":"delightful","forms":["delightful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43bf534a0938e6e7","term":"delightful","forms":["delightful","more delightful","delightfuler","delightfuller","most delightful","delightfulest","delightfullest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人愉快的","explanation":"指某件事、某個地方、某種體驗或某個人讓你感到快樂、滿足或享受。它強調“能帶來愉悅”，就像一段美好時光把快樂傳遞給人。","examples":[{"en":"We had a delightful afternoon by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個令人愉快的下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small garden is delightful in spring.","zh":"這座小花園在春天格外令人愉快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delightful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa2dcc238152c8737597","word":"deliver","forms":["deliver"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-455ab23db7bf86c9","term":"deliver","forms":["deliver","delivers","delivering","delivered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解救；使脫離危險","explanation":"把人從束縛、俘虜狀態或危險中解救出來，也就是把他送回安全和自由之中。這個意思體現了 deliver “把某人帶離困境”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team delivered the hikers from the storm.","zh":"救援隊把徒步者從暴風雨中救了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rescuers delivered the stranded climbers from certain death.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deliver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ceb4cc20d431d5f","term":"deliver","forms":["deliver","delivers","delivering","delivered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"送達；運送","explanation":"把包裹、貨物、郵件等從傳送者處送到預定地點或收件人手中。這是最典型的“把東西送到目標處”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The courier delivered the package to our office this morning.","zh":"快遞員今天早上把包裹送到了我們辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This service delivers fresh meals every evening.","zh":"這項服務每天晚上配送新鮮餐食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deliver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b262a767bca9af2a","term":"deliver","forms":["deliver","delivers","delivering","delivered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"兌現；達到要求","explanation":"把別人期待的結果實際做出來，尤其指兌現承諾、完成任務或達到要求。可以把它理解為“把答應的成果交出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The new manager promised better results and delivered on that promise.","zh":"新經理承諾會取得更好的成績，而且兌現了這個承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a plan that delivers real savings.","zh":"我們需要一個能真正節省開支的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deliver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4af39d5b65a14849e88","word":"delivery","forms":["delivery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e9d27693b2a158f","term":"delivery","forms":["delivery","deliveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"送達；配送","explanation":"指把信件、貨物等從一處送到另一處的過程，重點是“送到”這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The delivery will arrive before noon.","zh":"這批貨會在中午前送到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We offer free delivery on orders over $50.","zh":"訂單金額超過五十美元即可免費配送。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delivery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e64cf195d7aadca","term":"delivery","forms":["delivery","deliveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"送來的貨物；包裹","explanation":"指已經被送到的東西，尤其是外賣、包裹或訂購的貨物；這裡 delivery 不是過程，而是“送到的那件東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Your delivery is waiting at the front desk.","zh":"你的包裹在前臺等著領取。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A delivery of fresh linen arrived this morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delivery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dffc177fd0bbfd674906","word":"demand","forms":["demand"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03c2309b9d808e36","term":"demand","forms":["demand","demands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈要求","explanation":"指帶有壓力、堅持甚至權利意識的要求，好像把手伸出去，明確表示對方必須給出某物或採取某種行動。","examples":[{"en":"The workers made demands for safer conditions.","zh":"工人們要求改善安全條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His demands were impossible to meet.","zh":"他的要求根本無法滿足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd0ea0310de2b020","term":"demand","forms":["demand","demands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"要求或負擔","explanation":"指工作、生活或某項任務向人提出的條件，尤其是它要消耗你的時間、精力、能力或注意力。","examples":[{"en":"The new project is placing heavy demands on our time.","zh":"這個新專案正大量佔用我們的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Caring for twins places heavy demands on new parents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87288416324ea5ed","term":"demand","forms":["demand","demands","demanding","demanded","demandest","demandedst","demandeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強硬要求","explanation":"指不接受含糊答覆、以強硬態度要求某人做某事或交出某物，就像把手伸出去並堅持對方必須回應。","examples":[{"en":"She demanded to speak to the manager.","zh":"她強烈要求和經理談話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The customer demanded a full refund.","zh":"顧客強硬地要求全額退款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b48a0b1a0c6794bc","term":"demand","forms":["demand","demands","demanding","demanded","demandest","demandedst","demandeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人必須具備或付出","explanation":"指某項工作、任務或情況客觀上需要某種能力、時間或努力；不是人在發命令，而是事情向你提出了要求。","examples":[{"en":"Caring for young children demands patience.","zh":"照顧年幼的孩子需要耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The climb demands stamina and careful preparation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":3,"counts":{"111":2,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5138a960e3e13f6079c2","word":"democracy","forms":["democracy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4e46dd8838d7ed8","term":"democracy","forms":["democracy","democracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人民掌權的制度","explanation":"指人民掌握政治權力的治理方式，可以由人民直接作決定，也可以透過選出的代表來作決定；這是 democracy 的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Democracy gives citizens a voice in how their country is run.","zh":"民主讓公民能夠參與決定國家如何治理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A free press is important to democracy.","zh":"自由媒體對民主制度很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/democracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecf894700ade52cc","term":"democracy","forms":["democracy","democracies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"民主政體","explanation":"指一個由當地人民直接或透過代表來統治的政府或政體，重點在於它的權力執行方式。","examples":[{"en":"In a democracy, citizens can hold their leaders accountable.","zh":"在民主政體中，公民可以要求領導人對自己的行為負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island became a democracy after military rule ended.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/democracy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61e81a50ea9de3c9a48c","word":"democrat","forms":["democrat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f92a27b0f5e7a32","term":"democrat","forms":["democrat","democrats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"民主支持者","explanation":"指支援民主制度或主張民主政治的人，核心概念是“站在民主一邊”。它不一定表示此人屬於某個具體政黨。","examples":[{"en":"She has always been a democrat and opposed authoritarian rule.","zh":"她一直支援民主，並反對專制統治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The democrats called for fair elections.","zh":"民主支持者呼籲舉行公平選舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a democrat, she supports free and fair elections.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"As a democrat, he believes that citizens should choose their leaders.","zh":"作為一名民主支持者，他認為公民應該選擇自己的領導人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/democrat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9070e8db0018ad670e8","word":"democratic","forms":["democratic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4a4e0aee61f21af","term":"democratic","forms":["democratic","more democratic","most democratic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"民主的","explanation":"指國家、制度或決定方式讓人民透過參與或投票選擇領導人、表達意願，權力不是隻掌握在少數人手中。","examples":[{"en":"The country held its first democratic election in decades.","zh":"這個國家舉行了幾十年來第一次民主選舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A democratic system gives citizens a voice in government.","zh":"民主制度讓公民能夠在政府事務中表達意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/democratic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2358d183f8afd676","term":"democratic","forms":["democratic","more democratic","most democratic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平等的；不擺等級架子的","explanation":"指人與人相處時強調社會平等，不因為身份、財富或地位而把某些人看得更高貴；它從“人民共同參與”的核心意思自然擴充套件而來。","examples":[{"en":"Her democratic management style makes everyone feel included.","zh":"她平等的管理方式讓每個人都覺得自己被包括在內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her democratic manner put even the youngest intern at ease.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/democratic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a65dd3628de58bb9f3ee","word":"demonstrate","forms":["demonstrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2f19901cac54a16","term":"demonstrate","forms":["demonstrate","demonstrates","demonstrating","demonstrated","demonstratest","demonstratedst","demonstrateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"演示用法","explanation":"指實際做給別人看，說明某件工具、裝置或方法應該怎樣使用。重點是透過現場操作讓對方看懂，而不只是口頭介紹。","examples":[{"en":"The instructor demonstrated the safety equipment to the new workers.","zh":"教員向新工人演示了安全裝置的使用方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you demonstrate how to use this camera?","zh":"你能演示一下這臺相機怎麼用嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demonstrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a752b20a11560312","term":"demonstrate","forms":["demonstrate","demonstrates","demonstrating","demonstrated","demonstratest","demonstratedst","demonstrateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯示或證明","explanation":"指某個事實、行動或證據把結論清楚地顯示出來，使人能夠看出或相信某件事為真。它仍然保留“擺出證據讓人看見”的核心畫面，但不一定需要現場操作。","examples":[{"en":"The results demonstrate that the new treatment is effective.","zh":"這些結果表明這種新療法有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm response demonstrated great professional judgment.","zh":"她冷靜的回應顯示出很強的專業判斷力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demonstrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69f02b772af161fdf75d","word":"demonstration","forms":["demonstration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d555a4805ff23317","term":"demonstration","forms":["demonstration","demonstrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演示；說明","explanation":"指把做法、過程或道理展示出來，使別人看見並理解，既可以是課堂上的講解，也可以是實際操作的示範。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gave a demonstration of how to use the new software.","zh":"老師演示瞭如何使用這款新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The demonstration made the process much easier to understand.","zh":"這次演示讓這個過程更容易理解了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demonstration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fda8be3c48acb6d5","term":"demonstration","forms":["demonstration","demonstrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演示活動","explanation":"指專門安排的一場展示活動，演示者會在現場向觀眾說明某種方法、產品或過程。","examples":[{"en":"I have to give a demonstration to the class tomorrow.","zh":"我明天得給全班做一場演示。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chef gave a demonstration of knife techniques.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demonstration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b8d8a784eb61b7c6b43","word":"denial","forms":["denial"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42de150e992f7fd7","term":"denial","forms":["denial","denials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"否認某事屬實","explanation":"指明確聲稱某個說法、傳聞或指控不是真的。重點是把一個外界提出的事實或說法擋回去，因此既可以是口頭回應，也可以是正式宣告。","examples":[{"en":"The company issued a denial of the allegations.","zh":"公司發表宣告，否認這些指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His denial did little to calm the reporters.","zh":"他的否認並沒有怎麼讓記者們平靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/denial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db2cb49256a7e34b","term":"denial","forms":["denial","denials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拒絕承認問題存在","explanation":"指一個人面對明顯的問題，卻堅持說問題不存在或沒那麼嚴重。它是把事實擋在心理之外，常用於健康、成癮、關係和個人困境。","examples":[{"en":"She is in denial about how serious the problem is.","zh":"她不願承認這個問題有多嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His friends think he is in denial about his drinking.","zh":"他的朋友認為他不願承認自己的飲酒問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/denial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6a98598212ed729f5b9","word":"dense","forms":["dense"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1e4a4cce0f766e0","term":"dense","forms":["dense","denser","densest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"密度大的；稠密的","explanation":"指同樣大小的空間裡含有較多物質，或物質本身壓得很緊，因此顯得分量大、密度高。","examples":[{"en":"Lead is much denser than aluminum.","zh":"鉛的密度比鋁大得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dense metal sank immediately in water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eba0b4046d0f2e52","term":"dense","forms":["dense","denser","densest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難懂的；晦澀的","explanation":"像東西塞得太滿一樣，文字、論證或資訊過於集中，讀者很難迅速理解。","examples":[{"en":"The article is dense, but the final section is very useful.","zh":"這篇文章很難懂，但最後一部分非常有用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The professor gave us a dense chapter to read.","zh":"教授讓我們讀一章內容很密集、很難懂的材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06f8382071a4109d1a10","word":"density","forms":["density"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2ba0a1144313896","term":"density","forms":["density","densities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"質量密度","explanation":"指單位體積中包含的物質質量，也就是固定大小的空間裡物質塞得有多“實”。例如，同樣大小的盒子裡，裝有更多質量的材料，density 就更高。","examples":[{"en":"The density of this metal is twice that of aluminum.","zh":"這種金屬的密度是鋁的兩倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists measured the density of the rock sample.","zh":"科學家測量了這塊岩石樣本的密度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/density","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-155f9407a5fc7fa8","term":"density","forms":["density","densities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分佈密度","explanation":"指某種東西相對於它所佔空間、面積或其他範圍的數量，即固定大小的區域裡分佈了多少。人口、粒子、樹木或資訊都可以有這種 density。","examples":[{"en":"The city has a high population density near the coast.","zh":"這座城市沿海地區的人口密度很高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Population density increases sharply near the railway stations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/density","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d138e4e2606d9c58caab","word":"dental","forms":["dental"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee99422423b143ec","term":"dental","forms":["dental","more dental","most dental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"牙齒的","explanation":"表示直接與牙齒有關，尤其常見於牙齒護理、檢查和治療等話題。","examples":[{"en":"Regular dental care can prevent many problems.","zh":"定期進行牙齒護理可以預防許多問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a dental appointment for next week.","zh":"她預約了下週的牙齒檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81d342c357b7fa65","term":"dental","forms":["dental","more dental","most dental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"牙科的","explanation":"表示與牙科這一醫療領域或牙科診療工作有關，是“圍繞牙齒”這一意義向專業領域的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The town has a new dental clinic.","zh":"這個鎮上新開了一家牙科診所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular dental examinations can detect problems early.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f62e610834f27439cddf","word":"dentist","forms":["dentist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6165dffe9d74794","term":"dentist","forms":["dentist","dentists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牙醫","explanation":"牙醫是專門檢查、治療和護理牙齒及相關口腔問題的醫生。記住“維護牙齒這排房屋的人”這一形象，就能把它和普通醫生區分開。","examples":[{"en":"I have an appointment with the dentist tomorrow.","zh":"我明天預約了看牙醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dentist told me to brush more carefully.","zh":"牙醫告訴我要更認真地刷牙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dentist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3026a0ca485e5831657b","word":"deny","forms":["deny"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8ffa77674e2fde5","term":"deny","forms":["deny","denies","denying","denied","denyed","deniest","denieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拒絕許可","explanation":"指不允許某人做某事，或不批准某項請求，像把人擋在門外一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The airline denied him boarding because he arrived too late.","zh":"他到得太晚，航空公司拒絕讓他登機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guard denied them entry without identification.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c863c46a51116a87","term":"deny","forms":["deny","denies","denying","denied","denyed","deniest","denieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"否認事實","explanation":"指堅稱某件事不是真的，尤其是在別人指責或提出某種說法時拒不承認。","examples":[{"en":"She denied taking the money from the drawer.","zh":"她否認拿了抽屜裡的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company denied that the product was unsafe.","zh":"公司否認該產品不安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a43ac7b069a33fe30bf3","word":"depart","forms":["depart"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1242251fb7877103","term":"depart","forms":["depart","departs","departing","departed","departest","departedst","departeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離開","explanation":"表示人或動物離開所在的地方，是“depart”的最基本意思：從原來的位置走開。","examples":[{"en":"The train will depart from platform three at noon.","zh":"火車將在中午從三號站臺出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please depart quietly when the meeting ends.","zh":"會議結束後請安靜離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-009025176b23e58e","term":"depart","forms":["depart","departs","departing","departed","departest","departedst","departeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出發；啟程","explanation":"強調離開某地並開始一段行程，因此可理解為“動身、啟程”。","examples":[{"en":"We depart for Rome early tomorrow morning.","zh":"我們明天一早出發前往羅馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ferry departs at half past seven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ad29f65743a0524d916","word":"department","forms":["department"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a0d7a04e744245d","term":"department","forms":["department","departments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"部分；分部","explanation":"指從一個較大的整體中分出來的一部分，可以是物體、活動或組織中的一塊。這個意義是其他意義的基礎：先有“分出來的部分”，才會有專門的領域和部門。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen is a separate department of the house.","zh":"廚房是這棟房子中單獨的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store's furniture department occupies the second floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/department","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3b34fdb0ecc74e2","term":"department","forms":["department","departments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領域；專長","explanation":"指某種專門的活動、知識或工作領域。說某事是某人的 department，就是說那是對方擅長、負責或熟悉的領域。","examples":[{"en":"Planning trips is really her department.","zh":"安排旅行確實是她的專長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can fix the printer, but design is not my department.","zh":"我會修印表機，但設計不是我的專長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/department","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3b239e43cbcac5a","term":"department","forms":["department","departments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政府或機構部門","explanation":"指政府、公共機構或大型組織中負責某一事務的正式部門，例如負責財政、農業或警務的部門。這是“把工作分成不同部分並分別管理”的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The Department of Agriculture issued new safety guidelines.","zh":"農業部發布了新的安全指導方針。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please contact the police department if you need help.","zh":"如果你需要幫助，請聯絡警察部門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/department","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a70712f49d7d1d9cc551","word":"departure","forms":["departure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8eb2a24768abcfd","term":"departure","forms":["departure","departures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"離開；出發","explanation":"指人、車輛、船或飛機離開某地的行為，也可以指已經離開的那一班次或事件。這是departure最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Our train's departure has been delayed by twenty minutes.","zh":"我們的火車出發時間推遲了二十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We arrived at the airport well before the departure.","zh":"我們在起飛前很早就到了機場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/departure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-384c1f67887e1cdb","term":"departure","forms":["departure","departures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偏離；不同做法","explanation":"指某種做法、計劃、規則或標準沒有按原來的方向進行，而是離開了原先的軌道。這裡不是人或交通工具離開，而是思想或行動發生了改變。","examples":[{"en":"The new design is a clear departure from the company's usual style.","zh":"這種新設計明顯不同於公司一貫的風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new album is a departure from her earlier work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/departure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d05c4354368a975e2d9a","word":"depend","forms":["depend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b2c6a611dd05943","term":"depend","forms":["depend","depends","depending","depended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取決於","explanation":"表示某件事的結果或能否實現，要看另一個條件；這個條件就像把結果懸在上面，條件變化，結果也可能變化。","examples":[{"en":"Whether we eat outside depends on the weather.","zh":"我們是否在外面吃飯取決於天氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It depends on how much time you have.","zh":"這取決於你有多少時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40348ac39a3c383a","term":"depend","forms":["depend","depends","depending","depended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"信賴；依靠","explanation":"表示相信某人或某物會可靠地提供幫助、履行承諾或發揮作用，相當於把自己的希望掛在對方身上。","examples":[{"en":"You can depend on Mia to keep the secret.","zh":"你可以相信米婭會保守這個秘密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village depends on volunteers to keep its library open.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75846e529667722d646a","word":"dependent","forms":["dependent"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89756f5ddf138c99","term":"dependent","forms":["dependent","more dependent","most dependent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"依賴的；靠他人供養的","explanation":"指不能完全獨立，需要依靠某人、某機構或某種資源生活、學習或行動。重點是“支援來自外部”，例如經濟上依賴家人或援助。","examples":[{"en":"Many young adults are still dependent on their parents for financial support.","zh":"許多年輕人仍然依靠父母提供經濟支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At that point I was dependent on financial aid for my tuition.","zh":"那時我靠經濟援助支付學費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dependent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dab24331341f8cd4","term":"dependent","forms":["dependent","dependents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受供養的人","explanation":"指在生活費用或其他基本支援方面依靠別人、通常依靠家庭成員供養的人，常包括子女或無法自立的親屬。","examples":[{"en":"She listed her two children as dependents on the form.","zh":"她在表格上把兩個孩子列為受供養人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His health insurance also covers his dependents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dependent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-354f190a9506fed206f5","word":"depict","forms":["depict"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13f93e78062fc4ed","term":"depict","forms":["depict","depicts","depicting","depicted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"描繪；呈現","explanation":"指用文字、影象、聲音等方式，把某人、某物或某種情景清楚地呈現給別人看或感受。它不侷限於繪畫，也可以是小說描寫人物、電影呈現生活或音樂表現情緒。","examples":[{"en":"The novel depicts life in a small coastal town.","zh":"這部小說描繪了一個海濱小鎮的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mural depicts daily life in the fishing village.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ce80ada046fb23c8ea3","word":"deplete","forms":["deplete"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"deplete","forms":["deplete"],"pos":"v.","zh":"耗盡；大量消耗","examples":[{"en":"Years of drought can deplete the region's water supply.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Do not deplete your savings on things you do not need.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7bd55c11b781b0ccc43","word":"deploy","forms":["deploy"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3dd14a540614638b","term":"deploy","forms":["deploy","deploys","deploying","deployed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"部署人員或資源","explanation":"指把軍隊、人員或其他資源有計劃地安排到合適的位置，以便立即發揮作用；重點不是簡單地“放置”，而是為了任務而進行部署。","examples":[{"en":"The agency deployed extra staff to the affected area.","zh":"該機構向受影響地區增派了工作人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commander deployed the units along the northern border.","zh":"指揮官把這些部隊部署在北部邊境一帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deploy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f766c1a83c1dba15","term":"deploy","forms":["deploy","deploys","deploying","deployed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"展開並準備使用","explanation":"指摺疊、收攏或隱藏的東西展開，進入可以發揮作用的狀態；主語可以是人主動展開的物體，也可以是物體自行展開。","examples":[{"en":"The parachute deployed seconds after he jumped.","zh":"他跳下幾秒後，降落傘展開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The airbags deployed when the car hit the wall.","zh":"汽車撞上牆時，安全氣囊彈開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deploy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd47ad6ac9a08e85","term":"deploy","forms":["deploy","deploys","deploying","deployed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"部署軟體；上線系統","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指把軟體或系統安裝到目標環境，完成必要的配置和測試，並正式投入使用；可以理解為把程式“放到該執行的位置並展開其功能”。","examples":[{"en":"The team will deploy the new version to production tonight.","zh":"團隊今晚會把新版本部署到生產環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We tested the update before deploying it to all users.","zh":"我們先測試了更新，然後才把它部署給所有使用者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deploy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3b9fb78a452ce2fc90c","word":"deposit","forms":["deposit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac95cd09b656bc0f","term":"deposit","forms":["deposit","deposits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銀行存款","explanation":"指存入銀行賬戶、由銀行保管並可能產生利息的錢。這裡的錢被“放進”賬戶並留在那裡。","examples":[{"en":"She made a deposit into her savings account.","zh":"她把一筆錢存入了儲蓄賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The deposit earns interest every month.","zh":"這筆存款每個月都會產生利息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deposit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52c32857a8e69f64","term":"deposit","forms":["deposit","deposits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"定金；預付款","explanation":"指為表示誠意、預訂某物或開始購買而先交的一筆錢。它是把錢先放下，之後通常用於總價支付，是否退還要看約定。","examples":[{"en":"We paid a deposit on the apartment yesterday.","zh":"我們昨天為這套公寓交了定金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop asks for a 20 percent deposit before starting the work.","zh":"這家店要求先交百分之二十的定金才開始工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deposit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1564abdca84982d","term":"deposit","forms":["deposit","deposits","depositing","deposited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放下；放置","explanation":"指把某物放到一個地方，強調有意地放下並留下。它是其他動詞義項的基礎：錢、貨物或其他東西都可以被放置到指定地點。","examples":[{"en":"The turtle deposited her eggs in the warm sand.","zh":"這隻海龜把蛋產在溫暖的沙子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please deposit your luggage at the front desk.","zh":"請把行李放在前臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deposit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4fc9513e14c1420","term":"deposit","forms":["deposit","deposits","depositing","deposited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把錢存入賬戶","explanation":"指把錢存進銀行或其他賬戶。可以把它直接記成“把錢放進賬戶並留在那裡”。","examples":[{"en":"I deposited my paycheck into my account this morning.","zh":"我今天早上把工資支票存入了賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please deposit the rent by Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前把房租存入賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deposit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7d680f4aa63059ca89d","word":"depress","forms":["depress"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b4940c327dbbbb0","term":"depress","forms":["depress","depresses","depressing","depressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓下；按下","explanation":"指用力把某物從較高位置按到較低位置，通常是為了操作機器、按鈕或操縱桿。這是 depress 最直接的“向下壓”含義，也是其他用法的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"Depress the brake pedal slowly.","zh":"慢慢踩下剎車踏板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Depress the upper lever to start the machine.","zh":"按下上方的操縱桿來啟動機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c892d2c4e36a0fbd","term":"depress","forms":["depress","depresses","depressing","depressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使沮喪；使情緒低落","explanation":"把人的精神狀態“往下壓”，表示某件事使人難過、失望、提不起興趣或感到壓抑。它強調外部的人或事情造成這種低落情緒。","examples":[{"en":"The long, gray winter depresses me.","zh":"漫長而陰沉的冬天讓我情緒低落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The news really depressed him.","zh":"這條訊息讓他非常沮喪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74fd2e753c4e2cd9afca","word":"depression","forms":["depression"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28cead0166fbc04e","term":"depression","forms":["depression","depressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抑鬱；抑鬱症","explanation":"指人的情緒長期陷入低谷，生活樂趣明顯減少，也可能指以這種狀態為主要特徵的精神障礙。這裡不是短暫的不開心，而是較嚴重、持續時間較長的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She sought help after months of depression.","zh":"她經歷了幾個月的抑鬱後尋求了幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I used to suffer from depression, but now I am mostly content with my life.","zh":"我以前患有抑鬱症，但現在對生活大體感到滿意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23a72a04a74fa1e6","term":"depression","forms":["depression","depressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低窪地","explanation":"指比周圍地面低的地方，就像地形向下陷了一塊。","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater collected in a shallow depression beside the road.","zh":"雨水積在路邊一個淺淺的低窪地裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The surveyors found a circular depression where a pond once stood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c9947e245059292","term":"depression","forms":["depression","depressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟衰退","explanation":"指經濟活動明顯向下收縮的時期，通常表現為生產、就業或消費減少。","examples":[{"en":"The country entered a deep depression after the banking crisis.","zh":"銀行危機後，這個國家陷入了嚴重的經濟衰退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The depression forced thousands of factories to close.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9168392bbe50088ad09","word":"deprive","forms":["deprive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab0b4b0a44c2998a","term":"deprive","forms":["deprive","deprives","depriving","deprived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剝奪；使失去","explanation":"指把某種東西、權利、機會或資源從某人身邊拿走，並使他無法繼續擁有。重點不只是“拿走”這個動作，而是某人因此被置於缺少某物的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The decision deprived many families of access to clean water.","zh":"這項決定使許多家庭失去了獲得清潔飲水的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Working all night deprived her of the sleep she needed.","zh":"整夜工作使她失去了所需要的睡眠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deprive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ded32129b05bfc16ce50","word":"depth","forms":["depth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1fa5521481c153c","term":"depth","forms":["depth","depths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表面以下的深度","explanation":"指從表面垂直向下量到某一點的距離，也可泛指某物有多深。測量水、井、洞或其他空間時，這是最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We measured the depth of the pool before diving.","zh":"跳水前，我們測量了泳池的深度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lake reaches a depth of thirty meters here.","zh":"這個湖在這裡深達三十米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e988617a9cb2d9af","term":"depth","forms":["depth","depths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前後方向的深度","explanation":"指抽屜、櫃子、房間等從前面到後面的距離。雖然不是向地下延伸，它仍然表示“從外向內有多遠”。","examples":[{"en":"Check the depth of the cabinet before you order it.","zh":"訂購之前先確認一下櫃子的進深。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Measure the cabinet's depth before buying the shelves.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a08839451a6ce92","term":"depth","forms":["depth","depths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"程度、強度或內涵","explanation":"把情緒、處境、思想等想成可以向下探測的東西：越往深處，感情越強烈，處境越嚴重，內容越豐富。因此它可以表示痛苦、危機的嚴重程度，也可以表示思想或作品的深度。","examples":[{"en":"No one understood the depth of her grief.","zh":"沒有人理解她悲痛的程度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book has surprising depth for such a short story.","zh":"這樣一篇短篇小說竟然有出人意料的思想深度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00652261d8f5e7a4521d","word":"deputy","forms":["deputy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5123b4796ced009f","term":"deputy","forms":["deputy","deputies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"副手；代理人","explanation":"指受某人委託，在對方缺席或授權範圍內代表對方辦事的人，核心就是“替別人站崗”。","examples":[{"en":"She serves as the director's deputy when he is away.","zh":"主任不在時，她擔任代理主任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prince appointed a deputy to manage the province.","zh":"王子任命了一名代理人來管理這個省。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deputy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef9860714bf186bd","term":"deputy","forms":["deputy","deputies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"議員","explanation":"在一些國家，deputy是議會成員的稱呼，強調這個人作為代表參與立法和公共事務。","examples":[{"en":"The parliament has 450 deputies.","zh":"這個議會有450名議員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newly elected deputy addressed the national assembly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deputy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46023b2bfb8ba6dc6fdc","word":"derive","forms":["derive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9972cc532afdce71","term":"derive","forms":["derive","derives","deriving","derived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從……獲得","explanation":"表示從某個來源、經歷或活動中得到知識、好處、快樂等。重點是“所得之物從來源中引出”，不只是一般的擁有。","examples":[{"en":"She derives great satisfaction from helping others.","zh":"幫助別人讓她獲得了極大的滿足感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students can derive useful ideas from this example.","zh":"學生可以從這個例子中得到有用的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/derive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8b009269bd8c9db","term":"derive","forms":["derive","derives","deriving","derived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推匯出結論","explanation":"表示根據事實、資料或已有條件，透過推理引出結論；結論像是從證據這條“源流”中流出來的。","examples":[{"en":"From these results, we can derive an important conclusion.","zh":"我們可以從這些結果中推匯出一個重要結論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers derived the formula from basic principles.","zh":"研究人員從基本原理推匯出了這個公式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/derive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3b16735d016e42e","term":"derive","forms":["derive","derives","deriving","derived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"源自","explanation":"表示某種特徵、結果或情況的根源在於另一段經歷、原因或來源；這裡不是主動“取得”，而是說明它從哪裡生長出來。","examples":[{"en":"Her confidence derives from years of experience.","zh":"她的自信源自多年的經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The name derives from an ancient river goddess.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/derive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e424ec88ff49966434a9","word":"descend","forms":["descend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bfb3362b45de1ff6","term":"descend","forms":["descend","descends","descending","descended","descendest","descendedst","descendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使沿路向下；順流而下","explanation":"表示讓人或物從較高處向較低處移動，尤其可指船沿河流向下行駛；重點是“沿著某條路線下去”。","examples":[{"en":"The boats descended the river before sunset.","zh":"船隻在日落前順流而下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The canoeists descended the river toward the coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/descend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-113ced508622812c","term":"descend","forms":["descend","descends","descending","descended","descendest","descendedst","descendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向下走；下降","explanation":"表示主語自己從高處向低處移動，或沿斜坡、通道逐漸降低；可以指人、液體或其他自然事物。","examples":[{"en":"We descended into the valley before dark.","zh":"天黑前我們下到了山谷裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers descended carefully into the ravine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/descend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b806ea8d9c0d617","term":"descend","forms":["descend","descends","descending","descended","descendest","descendedst","descendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"是……的後代；源自","explanation":"表示某人或某家族從某位祖先傳下來，也可表示事物從某個來源發展而來；“向下”在這裡變成沿血緣或來源向後傳遞。","examples":[{"en":"She descends from a family of artists.","zh":"她出身於一個藝術家家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several local families descend from the original settlers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/descend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bec4ffaa14c6316d298b","word":"descent","forms":["descent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2c36689d97ac2ce","term":"descent","forms":["descent","descents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下降；下行","explanation":"指從較高處向較低處移動的過程，也就是“下來”這一動作本身。它可以用於下山、下樓等具體情景。","examples":[{"en":"The descent from the ridge took nearly two hours.","zh":"從山脊下行花了將近兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We began our descent as the sun was setting.","zh":"太陽落山時，我們開始下行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/descent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2529356f74f19591","term":"descent","forms":["descent","descents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"血統；出身","explanation":"指一個人的家族來源或祖先傳下來的血統。它把“從上一代傳下來”的方向感用於家族關係，而不是表示身體真的向下移動。","examples":[{"en":"She is of Irish descent but grew up in Canada.","zh":"她有愛爾蘭血統，但在加拿大長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is of Polish descent on her father's side.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/descent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c52028f34e378d1e07b4","word":"describe","forms":["describe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c47106d784bad263","term":"describe","forms":["describe","describes","describing","described"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用語言描述","explanation":"用語言把人、事物、經歷或感受的特點描出來，讓別人能夠形成較清楚的認識；物件不一定是看得見的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The feeling is difficult to describe, but it is not unpleasant.","zh":"這種感覺很難描述，但並不令人不舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you describe the person you saw at the station?","zh":"你能描述一下你在車站看到的那個人嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/describe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c381392018b5120","term":"describe","forms":["describe","describes","describing","described"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用線條描出","explanation":"不用語言，而是用畫線、標記或幾何工具把圓、弧線、路線等輪廓描出來；這仍然是“把輪廓描清楚”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Use a compass to describe a circle around the point.","zh":"用圓規以這個點為中心畫一個圓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The compass describes a perfect circle on paper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/describe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9046f7a37ad0ea7cee7","word":"description","forms":["description"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6796bbb67de6cbe6","term":"description","forms":["description","descriptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文字描寫；文字畫像","explanation":"指用語言把人、事物或事件的樣子、情況和重要特點講清楚，讀者彷彿能從文字中看到一幅畫像。","examples":[{"en":"The witness gave a detailed description of the accident.","zh":"目擊者詳細描述了這起事故。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her description of the village made me want to visit it.","zh":"她對那個村子的描寫讓我想去那裡看看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/description","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3a75a7fa6735877","term":"description","forms":["description","descriptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"描述這一行為","explanation":"指把事物用文字、圖形或其他符號表現出來這一行為本身，重點在“進行描寫”這個過程，而不只是最後形成的文字。","examples":[{"en":"Accurate description of the scene took several hours.","zh":"準確描繪現場花了好幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Description alone cannot convey the music's emotional power.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/description","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-167441da6a3a58c07396","word":"descriptive","forms":["descriptive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-308461fe419d4402","term":"descriptive","forms":["descriptive","more descriptive","most descriptive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"描述性的；說明性的","explanation":"表示用於描寫或說明某人、某物或某種情況，而不是隻作簡單命名或評價。它可以修飾文字、報告、方法等，核心都是把物件的樣子和情況呈現出來。","examples":[{"en":"The report gives a descriptive account of life in the village.","zh":"這份報告描述了村民的生活狀況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide is clear and descriptive.","zh":"這份指南清楚而且說明得很具體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/descriptive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a89d67655cbbf82","term":"descriptive","forms":["descriptive","more descriptive","most descriptive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表示名詞屬性的","explanation":"在語法中，descriptive 形容詞是用來說明名詞具有何種屬性的形容詞，例如說明某本詞典很厚。這裡關注的是形容詞對名詞的描述作用。","examples":[{"en":"In “a heavy dictionary,” “heavy” is a descriptive adjective.","zh":"在“a heavy dictionary”中，heavy 是說明屬性的形容詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In that phrase, golden is a descriptive adjective.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/descriptive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-237ab3365842e475721a","word":"desert","forms":["desert"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37cd74a9678a0d26","term":"desert","forms":["desert","deserts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙漠；荒地","explanation":"指水分和植被都很少的大片荒地，是“被拋棄、難以生存的地方”這一核心畫面的具體化。","examples":[{"en":"The camel carried water across the desert.","zh":"駱駝馱著水穿過了沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Few plants can survive in this desert.","zh":"很少有植物能在這片荒漠中生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68c250e6e1c67357","term":"desert","forms":["desert","deserts","deserting","deserted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拋棄；遺棄","explanation":"指在別人或某件事依賴你時離開，使對方失去支援；這是“把別人留在荒地裡”的動詞化畫面。","examples":[{"en":"He deserted his family when they needed him most.","zh":"他的家人最需要他的時候，他卻拋棄了他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You cannot desert your friends in the middle of a crisis.","zh":"你不能在危機中途拋下朋友不管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7f8d3e72469ce6887d0","word":"deserve","forms":["deserve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5dad8695b5c9db11","term":"deserve","forms":["deserve","deserves","deserving","deserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"應得；值得得到","explanation":"由於先前的表現、行為或付出，某人或某事合理地應當得到某種結果。這個結果可以是獎勵、成功和尊重，也可以是懲罰、批評或失敗；關鍵是結果被認為與其行為相稱。","examples":[{"en":"After working so hard, she deserves a break.","zh":"她這麼辛苦地工作，應該休息一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The players deserved to win the match.","zh":"這些球員的表現配得上贏得這場比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a77de8a6daa1129516b1","word":"design","forms":["design"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91a4dac539377814","term":"design","forms":["design","designs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解決問題的設計方案","explanation":"指為滿足某些要求、解決某個問題而制定的整體方案，重點不只是外觀，還包括需要達到的條件和功能。","examples":[{"en":"The design of the new water system saves both time and energy.","zh":"這套新供水系統的設計既節省時間，也節省能源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a better design for this crowded classroom.","zh":"我們需要為這間擁擠的教室設計一個更好的方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/design","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f8f94d3bed4666e","term":"design","forms":["design","designs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結構和功能的規劃","explanation":"指建築、裝置、系統或其他人工製品在製作前的結構與功能規劃，也就是通常所說的“藍圖”或“設計方案”。","examples":[{"en":"The initial design of the park was too expensive to build.","zh":"公園最初的設計建造成本太高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineers changed the design to make the bridge safer.","zh":"工程師修改了設計，使這座橋更加安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/design","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7840c204b751814","term":"design","forms":["design","designs","designing","designed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設計並製作","explanation":"指先構思、規劃，再把影象、藝術品、建築或其他物品做出來，是名詞“設計方案”變成行動的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The team designed a lighter helmet for cyclists.","zh":"團隊為騎行者設計了一種更輕的頭盔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She designs websites for small businesses.","zh":"她為小企業設計網站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/design","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e4f52a959f00546bff6","word":"designer","forms":["designer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99dbe6c4763f73d9","term":"designer","forms":["designer","designers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"設計者；設計師","explanation":"指負責構思、規劃並確定某種產品、空間、服裝或系統樣式的人；既可以是職業設計師，也可以只是某個專案的設計者。","examples":[{"en":"The designer changed the layout after talking to the client.","zh":"設計師和客戶溝通後改了版面佈局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works as a designer for a small furniture company.","zh":"她在一家小型傢俱公司擔任設計師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/designer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":3,"counts":{"113":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-1ac4d7fa2f743996c470","word":"desirable","forms":["desirable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef1c271400a79b8d","term":"desirable","forms":["desirable","more desirable","most desirable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得想要的；令人滿意的","explanation":"如果一個人或事物具備人們看重的特點，因而值得爭取或選擇，就可以說它是 desirable。它不只表示外表討喜，也可以表示條件、結果或品質合乎期望。","examples":[{"en":"Flexible working hours are a highly desirable benefit for many employees.","zh":"對許多員工來說，靈活的工作時間是一項非常令人滿意的福利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ideal candidate should have several desirable qualities, including patience and reliability.","zh":"理想的人選應具備幾項值得看重的品質，包括耐心和可靠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desirable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83fa74e70278e5b9ff3f","word":"desire","forms":["desire"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9264f57e66c50737","term":"desire","forms":["desire","desires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"渴望；慾望","explanation":"指心裡強烈想得到某物、實現某事或經歷某種情況的感覺，是 desire 最核心的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Her desire for adventure led her to travel alone.","zh":"她對冒險的渴望促使她獨自旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Too much desire for success can cloud your judgment.","zh":"對成功過度的渴望可能會影響你的判斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7977fd08cf87625f","term":"desire","forms":["desire","desires","desiring","desired","desirest","desiredst","desireth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"渴望；強烈想要","explanation":"表示強烈地想得到某物、實現某事或經歷某種情況，是動詞 desire 的核心含義。","examples":[{"en":"I desire to learn more about the history of this place.","zh":"我渴望進一步瞭解這個地方的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people desire a peaceful life.","zh":"許多人渴望過平靜的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-49be417ad74080a0031b","word":"desk","forms":["desk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7612b2a44edf7712","term":"desk","forms":["desk","desks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書桌；辦公桌","explanation":"一種供人讀、寫或辦公的桌子，通常帶抽屜或收納空間；現代最常見的是平頂書桌或辦公桌。","examples":[{"en":"I left the report on my desk before going home.","zh":"我下班前把報告留在辦公桌上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She organized her notes neatly on her desk before starting the project.","zh":"開始專案之前，她把筆記整齊地整理在書桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1cc3e30d50b07989","term":"desk","forms":["desk","desks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專門部門；工作臺","explanation":"指機構中負責某一主題或業務的部門，尤其常見於報社、新聞機構和金融交易機構；它從“一個固定工作位置”擴充套件成了“承擔某項工作的團隊或崗位”。","examples":[{"en":"The sports desk is preparing a report on the championship.","zh":"體育編輯部正在準備一篇關於這次冠軍賽的報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ask the travel desk to arrange your transfer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e7684586cdf724494932","word":"despair","forms":["despair"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f807a00e80fad485","term":"despair","forms":["despair","despairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"絕望","explanation":"指希望徹底消失後的情緒或精神狀態，好像心裡的燈完全熄滅，覺得事情已經沒有挽回的可能。","examples":[{"en":"She stared at the empty room in despair.","zh":"她絕望地望著空蕩蕩的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sense of despair spread through the village after the flood.","zh":"洪水過後，一種絕望感在村子裡蔓延開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/despair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63f431672ea7373a","term":"despair","forms":["despair","despairs","despairing","despaired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"陷入絕望","explanation":"表示自己完全失去希望，認為某事或某種處境已經無法挽回；它就是“心裡的希望之燈熄滅”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"After months without work, he began to despair of finding a job.","zh":"幾個月找不到工作後，他開始對找到工作不抱希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not despair; we still have one more chance.","zh":"不要絕望，我們還有最後一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/despair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d3082f6a1fd718c68ec","word":"desperate","forms":["desperate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-964b799188a6846a","term":"desperate","forms":["desperate","more desperate","desperater","most desperate","desperatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"急需；非常渴望","explanation":"表示某人對食物、幫助、錢等有強烈而緊迫的需要，彷彿已經被逼到不得不馬上得到它的地步。","examples":[{"en":"We were desperate for water after the long hike.","zh":"長途徒步後，我們急需水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was desperate to find a job.","zh":"她急切地想找到一份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desperate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66ecd569e22d096d","term":"desperate","forms":["desperate","more desperate","desperater","most desperate","desperatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"絕望的；陷入絕境的","explanation":"表示一個人或其處境充滿絕望，覺得正常辦法已經沒有用，因此心情極其無助。","examples":[{"en":"By midnight, he felt desperate and called his old friend.","zh":"到了午夜，他感到十分絕望，於是給老朋友打了電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The desperate survivors signaled with a broken mirror.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desperate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9272459bf48061da35d1","word":"despise","forms":["despise"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70ff31c310d179cb","term":"despise","forms":["despise","despises","despising","despised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鄙視；看不起","explanation":"指因為認為某人、某種行為或某件事低劣、可恥或不值得尊重，而帶著輕蔑的態度看待它；重點不是單純不喜歡，而是“從高處往下看”。","examples":[{"en":"She despises people who lie to get ahead.","zh":"她鄙視那些靠撒謊來取得成功的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He despised his former boss for treating workers unfairly.","zh":"他看不起以前的老闆，因為那人對待工人不公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/despise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6dbefb4fe02322df7aa4","word":"despite","forms":["despite"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-361f2aaf71ff1046","term":"despite","forms":["despite"],"pos":"prep","zh":"儘管；不顧","explanation":"把某個不利情況當作阻礙，但結果並沒有因此改變：儘管有它，後面的事情仍然發生。它保留了“迎著阻力照樣做”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Despite the heavy rain, the children continued playing outside.","zh":"儘管下著大雨，孩子們還是繼續在外面玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finished the report despite feeling exhausted.","zh":"儘管感到筋疲力盡，她還是完成了報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/despite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113,114],"total":3,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-6084392347f92be9ce89","word":"dessert","forms":["dessert"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7613c87f6641b4f8","term":"dessert","forms":["dessert","desserts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餐後甜點這一道","explanation":"指一餐最後上的甜點餐程，強調它在整頓飯中的位置；這裡的重點是“收尾的一道”，而不只是某一種甜食。","examples":[{"en":"We had fruit for dessert after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們吃水果作餐後甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I ordered hummus for a starter, a steak as the main course, and chocolate cake for dessert.","zh":"我點了鷹嘴豆泥作開胃菜、牛排作主菜，還點了巧克力蛋糕作餐後甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dessert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2b7f694d8b952e4","term":"dessert","forms":["dessert","desserts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體的甜食","explanation":"指作為餐後收尾的一種具體甜食，例如蛋糕、布丁或水果甜點；可以把它看成“dessert 這一餐程裡端上的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Cheesecake is my favorite dessert.","zh":"芝士蛋糕是我最喜歡的甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a lemon dessert from the trolley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dessert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5c755aaab1038b3d562","word":"destination","forms":["destination"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7614b923fe9a4e16","term":"destination","forms":["destination","destinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目的地；終點","explanation":"指旅程、運輸或傳送行為最後要到達的地點或位置，也就是人或物被送往的終點。這個終點可以是具體地址，也可以是地圖上要抵達的地方。","examples":[{"en":"We finally arrived at our destination just before sunset.","zh":"我們終於在日落前到達了目的地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The package reached its destination two days later.","zh":"包裹兩天後到達了目的地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86b88ea99333b0c4","term":"destination","forms":["destination","destinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最終目標；用途；歸宿","explanation":"從“旅程終點”引申而來，指某人或某物預先被安排要達到的最終目標、用途或歸宿；這裡的終點不一定是地理位置，也可以是人生目標、計劃結果或物品用途。","examples":[{"en":"The final destination of the project is to provide clean water to every village.","zh":"這個專案的最終目標是讓每個村莊都用上乾淨的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The money's destination remains a matter for investigation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":5,"counts":{"112":3,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-198896b3682c08695419","word":"destined","forms":["destined"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b194a551801b2b2c","term":"destined","forms":["destined"],"pos":"adj","zh":"註定的；命中註定會……的","explanation":"形容某種結果彷彿早已由命運決定，事情很難偏離這條路。它可以表示成功、成名等好結果，也可以表示失敗或其他不可避免的結局。","examples":[{"en":"She was destined for greatness from an early age.","zh":"她從小就註定會成就非凡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They believed the two friends were destined to meet again.","zh":"他們相信這兩個朋友註定會再次相遇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destined","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b01774366b2bea90002f","word":"destiny","forms":["destiny"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5163af99ac3586a","term":"destiny","forms":["destiny","destinies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"註定的狀態","explanation":"指一個人或事物被認為註定會達到的狀態或結局，重點是未來彷彿早已被安排好。它可以指個人的命運，也可以指某類事物共同的結局。","examples":[{"en":"She believed that her destiny was to help people.","zh":"她相信自己的命運就是幫助別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one can escape their destiny forever.","zh":"沒有人能永遠逃脫自己的命運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destiny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12d6dba78e7ed3eb","term":"destiny","forms":["destiny","destinies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不可避免的命運","explanation":"強調事情隨著時間推移終究會發生，像一條無法避開的路；這裡突出的是“不可避免”，不一定說明誰預先安排了它。","examples":[{"en":"The old king accepted his destiny and gave up the throne.","zh":"老國王接受了自己的命運，放棄了王位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He believed it was his destiny to explore space.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destiny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f61ec5c7a0ab645b7b9","word":"destroy","forms":["destroy"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c94f796eb968b551","term":"destroy","forms":["destroy","destroys","destroying","destroyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徹底摧毀","explanation":"把建築、物品或其他事物破壞到無法繼續使用、修復，或者實際上不再存在。這是 destroy 最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake destroyed several apartment buildings.","zh":"地震摧毀了好幾棟公寓樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fire destroyed everything in the garage.","zh":"大火燒燬了車庫裡的一切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destroy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83fc5a0ebccb5d07","term":"destroy","forms":["destroy","destroys","destroying","destroyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"破壞某種特性","explanation":"使某種性質、效果或狀態消失或變差，而不一定破壞整個物體。例如，某種行為可能破壞食物原有的味道。","examples":[{"en":"Too much heat can destroy the delicate flavor of the sauce.","zh":"溫度過高會破壞這種醬汁的細膩味道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Excessive heat destroys the fabric's elasticity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destroy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9507b2daa0419d7e57b2","word":"destruction","forms":["destruction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed8d6a2bf9f27265","term":"destruction","forms":["destruction","destructions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摧毀；破壞行為","explanation":"指把建築、設施、自然環境等毀掉的行為或過程，重點在“正在進行的破壞”這一動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The destruction of the old bridge will begin next week.","zh":"舊橋的拆除工作將於下週開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm caused the destruction of several homes.","zh":"暴風雨摧毀了好幾所房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destruction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d76627fa4fd5e0a","term":"destruction","forms":["destruction","destructions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毀壞；破壞造成的結果","explanation":"指破壞事件留下的毀壞景象、廢墟或嚴重損失，重點從“摧毀的動作”轉向“被毀後的局面”。","examples":[{"en":"The town was surrounded by destruction after the earthquake.","zh":"地震過後，小鎮四周都是一片毀壞的景象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fire left a trail of destruction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destruction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b933329d22a42d5507d","word":"destructive","forms":["destructive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73a6cabec73ea56e","term":"destructive","forms":["destructive","more destructive","most destructive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"造成破壞的","explanation":"指某種行為、力量或事物會損壞物件、破壞環境，或對人的生活和發展造成傷害；這是最一般、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The storm was destructive to homes and crops.","zh":"這場暴風雨對房屋和農作物造成了破壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Constant criticism can be destructive to a person's confidence.","zh":"不斷的批評可能會損害一個人的自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destructive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d7b6423c8271f1a","term":"destructive","forms":["destructive","more destructive","most destructive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"使整體分解的","explanation":"指把原本完整的東西拆開、分解成更小的部分；它仍然保留“拆壞或拆散”的核心畫面，但重點在過程本身。","examples":[{"en":"The body uses a destructive process to break down old cells.","zh":"身體透過分解過程來處理舊細胞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Destructive distillation breaks coal into several useful products.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/destructive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e544618d1e7e57eee3e9","word":"detach","forms":["detach"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58a0c5a4c0274b43","term":"detach","forms":["detach","detaches","detaching","detached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……取下；使……脫離","explanation":"指把一個原本貼著、連著或附著的東西取下來，使它與另一物分開。重點是解除連線，而不一定意味著損壞被分開的東西。","examples":[{"en":"Please detach the label from the box before recycling it.","zh":"回收盒子前，請先把標籤從盒子上取下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She detached the cable from the back of the monitor.","zh":"她把電纜從顯示器背面拔了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06957dd6bf4874b4","term":"detach","forms":["detach","detaches","detaching","detached"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……調離整體；分派出去","explanation":"指把一個人、小組、船隻或其他單位從原來的組織、隊伍或任務中分出來，安排它去執行特殊任務或承擔獨立用途。這裡不是簡單的物理拆開，而是從原有整體中抽調出去。","examples":[{"en":"Two officers were detached from the main team to investigate the report.","zh":"兩名軍官被從主隊抽調出去調查這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commander detached two officers to escort the supplies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c0211c51d04574fdaee","word":"detail","forms":["detail"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c0e73e52eebdb76","term":"detail","forms":["detail","details"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個容易忽略的小細節","explanation":"指整體中的一個小部分，通常不仔細看就會漏掉；它像從大圖中單獨剪出來的一小塊。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small detail in the photograph that most people miss.","zh":"照片裡有一個大多數人都會忽略的小細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One telling detail undermined his entire account.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bbf7e6d0f99d7c89","term":"detail","forms":["detail","details"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細節整體；注重細節","explanation":"指許多容易漏掉的小部分的總稱，常強調認真處理這些小部分的態度或能力。","examples":[{"en":"Her attention to detail makes her a reliable editor.","zh":"她對細節的關注使她成為一名可靠的編輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The model's remarkable detail impressed the museum curator.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d048596a4adb025e","term":"detail","forms":["detail","details","detailing","detailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"詳細說明","explanation":"把一個過程、計劃或事件拆成許多具體小部分，逐項講清楚；也就是把“細節”說出來。","examples":[{"en":"The guide detailed the steps for repairing the bicycle.","zh":"指南詳細說明了修理這輛腳踏車的步驟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report details every stage of the investigation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0b5009d200e50247322","word":"detain","forms":["detain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a29de7451512bde6","term":"detain","forms":["detain","detains","detaining","detained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使耽擱；拖住","explanation":"指某件事、某段談話或某種要求把人暫時拖住，使他不能按原計劃繼續前進，不一定涉及法律或強制拘禁。","examples":[{"en":"A long conversation detained me, so I missed the last train.","zh":"一場冗長的談話把我耽擱住了，所以我沒趕上末班車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A phone call detained her at the office.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5f56823f27627ef","term":"detain","forms":["detain","detains","detaining","detained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拘留；扣押","explanation":"指警察或其他有權機構把人留置起來，限制其自由，通常是為了調查、訊問或處理法律事務。","examples":[{"en":"The police detained him for questioning at the station.","zh":"警方把他拘留在警察局接受訊問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police detained the driver for questioning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cfacfd3ec33b9608b59a","word":"detect","forms":["detect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f9a2d916654c396","term":"detect","forms":["detect","detects","detecting","detected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"查出；檢測到","explanation":"指經過仔細搜尋、檢查、測量或分析，把原本不明顯或隱藏的東西發現出來。可以查出氣味、疾病、訊號、錯誤，也可以發現某人正在做某事。","examples":[{"en":"The test can detect the virus before symptoms appear.","zh":"這種檢測能在症狀出現前查出病毒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sensor detected a small movement near the door.","zh":"感測器檢測到門附近有輕微的移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5448f2e81d8402bd06f1","word":"detective","forms":["detective"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c690cfe7da64835","term":"detective","forms":["detective","detectives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偵探；警察偵查員","explanation":"指負責蒐集證據、詢問相關人員並解決犯罪案件的警察偵查員，也可泛指專門調查案件的人。","examples":[{"en":"The detective found a new clue at the scene.","zh":"偵查員在現場發現了一個新線索。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has worked as a detective for ten years.","zh":"她當偵查員已經十年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0e6b41842747a9a","term":"detective","forms":["detective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"偵查的；偵探的","explanation":"表示某件事與尋找證據、追查線索、解決案件有關，也可以指偵探故事或偵查工作本身。","examples":[{"en":"Good detective work helped the police identify the suspect.","zh":"出色的偵查工作幫助警方確認了嫌疑人的身份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The detective unit examined the abandoned warehouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39c547ad619da631a328","word":"detention","forms":["detention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dab46ad8f9b316c5","term":"detention","forms":["detention","detentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"扣留；留置狀態","explanation":"指把人或物暫時扣住，或者指這種扣留本身及持續狀態；物件不一定是人，也可以是貨物、車輛等。","examples":[{"en":"The detention of the cargo delayed its delivery.","zh":"貨物被留置，導致交付延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report examined the detention of several vehicles at the border.","zh":"這份報告調查了幾輛車在邊境被留置的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b67f86989e2ece93","term":"detention","forms":["detention","detentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臨時拘押；拘禁狀態","explanation":"指一個人暫時被官方或其他有權機構控制、限制自由的狀態，也可以指一次這樣的拘押。","examples":[{"en":"The suspect remained in detention while the investigation continued.","zh":"調查繼續進行期間，嫌疑人一直被拘押。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lawyers challenged the legality of her detention at the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f46dc62af3171f09b098","word":"deter","forms":["deter"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86d3d9d75faf531d","term":"deter","forms":["deter","deters","deterring","deterred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"阻止某事發生","explanation":"指某種風險、懲罰或困難使一件事無法發生，重點是產生了阻止作用，而不一定表示有人直接下令禁止。","examples":[{"en":"Stricter safety rules may deter accidents at the factory.","zh":"更嚴格的安全規定可能會防止工廠發生事故。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new fence did little to deter theft.","zh":"新圍欄幾乎沒有起到防止盜竊的作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59bdf93893418098","term":"deter","forms":["deter","deters","deterring","deterred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勸阻某人做某事","explanation":"指透過提醒後果、增加成本或製造顧慮，讓某人打消做某事的念頭，也就是把人“嚇退”或勸退。","examples":[{"en":"The high cost deterred many students from studying abroad.","zh":"高昂的費用讓許多學生打消了出國留學的念頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing could deter her from reporting the problem.","zh":"沒有什麼能阻止她報告這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-958d4f64abe96c80a448","word":"detergent","forms":["detergent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-828df68d820d868a","term":"detergent","forms":["detergent","detergents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洗滌劑；清潔劑","explanation":"指用來洗掉汙垢、油汙或其他髒東西的清潔用品，通常不是傳統肥皂，而是洗衣液、洗衣粉、洗潔精等產品。這個詞的核心畫面就是藉助一種清潔劑把汙垢“擦掉”。","examples":[{"en":"Add some detergent before starting the washing machine.","zh":"啟動洗衣機前加一些洗滌劑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This detergent is gentle on delicate fabrics.","zh":"這種洗滌劑對精細織物比較溫和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detergent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-95f1a23373195c7816d7","word":"determination","forms":["determination"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0aad3c8ef5afd55","term":"determination","forms":["determination","determinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"決心；堅定不移","explanation":"指一個人把意志定住後，即使遇到困難也繼續行動的品質，也就是“決心”和“堅韌”。","examples":[{"en":"With determination, she finished the course despite the injury.","zh":"她憑著堅定的決心，儘管受了傷還是完成了課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His determination to improve kept him practicing every morning.","zh":"他堅持提高自己的決心讓他每天早晨都練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/determination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e53cab4013694d1","term":"determination","forms":["determination","determinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"確定的決定；意圖或結論","explanation":"指經過考慮後定下來的意圖、方案或結論，即“已經決定要什麼或怎麼做”的結果；它是“把事情定下來”的最終產物。","examples":[{"en":"After reviewing the evidence, the panel reached a determination.","zh":"審查證據後，評審小組作出了明確結論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The board announced its determination to close the branch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/determination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3d8eefab379df52272c2","word":"determine","forms":["determine"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa7a5d58a842c8cd","term":"determine","forms":["determine","determines","determining","determined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"查明；確定事實","explanation":"透過分析、計算、調查或觀察，把原本不確定的答案弄清楚。這裡的 determine 不是“決定要做什麼”，而是“找出真實答案”。","examples":[{"en":"The test will determine whether the water is safe to drink.","zh":"這項檢測將確定這些水是否可以安全飲用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need more evidence to determine the cause of the problem.","zh":"我們需要更多證據來查明問題的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/determine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82dcb7aa61e45577","term":"determine","forms":["determine","determines","determining","determined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下定決心；決定做","explanation":"指經過考慮後把意圖固定下來，決定採取某個行動。它仍然保留“把事情定下來”的核心畫面，但重點落在行動者的決心上。","examples":[{"en":"She determined to finish the project before Friday.","zh":"她下定決心在星期五以前完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was determined to solve the problem himself.","zh":"他決心自己解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/determine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a55f1f69192f6e514d26","word":"develop(ment)","forms":["develop","development"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecc94d54db5216f1","term":"develop","forms":["develop","develops","developing","developed","developt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸發展；演變","explanation":"表示事情或局勢沿著某種方向逐漸變化，重點是過程自然展開，而不是某個人直接製造結果。","examples":[{"en":"Let's see how things develop before we make a decision.","zh":"我們先看看事情如何發展，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The situation developed differently from what we expected.","zh":"事態的發展和我們預想的不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/develop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eacd78bd80bace4a","term":"develop","forms":["develop","develops","developing","developed","developt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐階段發展成","explanation":"表示人、動物、事物經過一連串階段逐步成長或轉變，常強調從一種狀態進入下一種狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The small idea developed into a successful business.","zh":"這個小想法逐漸發展成了一項成功的業務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young plant developed several strong branches.","zh":"這株幼苗逐漸長出了幾根粗壯的枝條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/develop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d21a7325faa3bea0","term":"develop","forms":["develop","develops","developing","developed","developt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促進發展；培育","explanation":"表示主動投入時間、資源或努力，使某種能力、資源、業務等得到成長和充分利用。","examples":[{"en":"The company is developing new skills among its staff.","zh":"這家公司正在培養員工的新技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to develop local resources more carefully.","zh":"我們需要更合理地開發當地資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/develop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b1199c5519f995c","term":"development","forms":["development","developments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展；展開過程","explanation":"指某事物逐步成長、變化或展開的過程，既可以是故事的發展，也可以是能力、局勢或社會狀況的變化。","examples":[{"en":"The development of the story became more exciting after the first chapter.","zh":"這部故事在第一章之後發展得更加精彩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city has seen rapid development in recent years.","zh":"這座城市近年來經歷了快速發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/development","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43fbac2e1f8e11de","term":"development","forms":["development","developments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進展；新情況","explanation":"指已經發展出來、值得報告或注意的具體結果，尤其常指事情的新進展或局勢的新變化。","examples":[{"en":"We will share the latest developments as soon as we have more information.","zh":"一有更多資訊，我們就會公佈最新進展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is an unexpected development in the case.","zh":"這是這起案件中一個意想不到的新情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/development","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-263a4dbe41488fb87214","word":"device","forms":["device"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d84f9784ea38d1f","term":"device","forms":["device","devices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝置；裝置","explanation":"為某種特定目的製造或設計的裝置，尤其是機械或電氣裝置。它可以很簡單，如鈴，也可以很複雜。","examples":[{"en":"This device measures the temperature every five minutes.","zh":"這個裝置每五分鐘測量一次溫度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The alarm device stopped working during the storm.","zh":"警報裝置在暴風雨中停止工作了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/device","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9db36fe0de1aa2e6","term":"device","forms":["device","devices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"硬體裝置；外設","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指電腦系統中的硬體，特別是連線到電腦、幫助輸入、輸出或處理資訊的外設。","examples":[{"en":"The computer cannot recognize the new device.","zh":"電腦無法識別這個新裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Connect the device to an available USB port.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/device","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":4,"counts":{"111":2,"113":2}}},{"id":"ceec-68da4167b0cd79b79da4","word":"devil","forms":["devil"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0752b72051670849","term":"devil","forms":["devil","devils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邪惡的魔鬼","explanation":"指被想象成敵視人類、帶來破壞和邪惡的魔鬼，是這個詞最基本的普通名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers believed that a devil lived in the dark forest.","zh":"村民們相信黑暗的森林裡住著一個魔鬼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting shows a devil with red wings.","zh":"這幅畫畫著一個長著紅翅膀的魔鬼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a323dce101ba039","term":"devil","forms":["devil","devils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"淘氣鬼；調皮孩子","explanation":"形容人，尤其是孩子精力旺盛、頑皮愛鬧，但往往帶有親暱或半開玩笑的語氣，並不一定表示真正邪惡。","examples":[{"en":"Those two little devils emptied the toy box in minutes.","zh":"那兩個小淘氣鬼幾分鐘就把玩具箱倒空了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You little devil, you've hidden my slippers again!","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d0f7f57107df31df742","word":"devise","forms":["devise"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-934e4852ef6d6dff","term":"devise","forms":["devise","devises","devising","devised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設計出；想出","explanation":"指運用智力和計劃，設計出一個方案、方法、論點、機器或制度。它不僅是突然想到，更強調經過思考後把解決辦法構思出來。","examples":[{"en":"The engineers devised a simpler way to store energy.","zh":"工程師們設計出了一種更簡單的儲能方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to devise a plan before the meeting.","zh":"我們需要在會議前想出一個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e84eafd39ee49502","term":"devise","forms":["devise","devises","devising","devised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在遺囑中把不動產留給某人","explanation":"指按照遺囑把土地、房屋等不動產指定留給某人。這是“安排、設計歸屬”在法律中的專門用法。","examples":[{"en":"She devised the family farm to her eldest daughter.","zh":"她在遺囑中把家族農場留給了大女兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The will devises the riverside cottage to a local charity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2483f281f1555930244a","word":"devote","forms":["devote"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-866464f9e2232987","term":"devote","forms":["devote","devotes","devoting","devoted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投入；獻身於","explanation":"把自己的時間、精力、注意力或整個人生交給某個目標，表示持續而專注地投入。物件可以是工作、研究、事業、信仰或他人，因此比普通的“花時間”更強調全心全意。","examples":[{"en":"She devoted her weekends to caring for her elderly parents.","zh":"她把週末都用來照顧年邁的父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He devoted himself to improving the local school.","zh":"他全心投入到改善當地學校的工作中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67acf560e238730acee3","word":"devotion","forms":["devotion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b033672d7717f952","term":"devotion","forms":["devotion","devotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投入與奉獻","explanation":"強調把時間、精力或心思持續交給某項事業、某個人或某種責任；重點在“全心投入”這一狀態，而不一定突出具體的感情。","examples":[{"en":"Her devotion to the project kept the team motivated.","zh":"她對這個專案的投入一直鼓舞著團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her devotion to teaching inspired generations of students.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f323988efb29fb24","term":"devotion","forms":["devotion","devotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"深厚的感情與忠誠","explanation":"當持續投入背後有強烈的愛、關心或忠誠時，devotion 就表示對家人、朋友、伴侶或事業的深厚感情，並常透過實際行動表現出來。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone admired his devotion to his children.","zh":"大家都很佩服他對孩子們深厚的愛與付出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her devotion to her patients was evident every day.","zh":"她對病人的關愛和盡心盡力每天都顯而易見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e11386019db8168f8ee","word":"devour","forms":["devour"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ce50bf6a4ca7f7b","term":"devour","forms":["devour","devours","devouring","devoured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"狼吞虎嚥地吃","explanation":"指快速、貪婪或非常飢餓地把食物吃下去，畫面像張大嘴把食物整個吞掉。它比普通的“吃”更有力度。","examples":[{"en":"The hungry children devoured the pizza in minutes.","zh":"飢餓的孩子們幾分鐘就把披薩狼吞虎嚥地吃完了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He devoured his breakfast before catching the train.","zh":"他在趕火車前把早餐迅速吃光了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fd4c33066428157","term":"devour","forms":["devour","devours","devouring","devoured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迅速吞沒；毀掉","explanation":"把火災、戰爭、時間等強大力量描寫成一張大口，迅速吞掉、毀壞或覆蓋某物。","examples":[{"en":"Within an hour, the flames had devoured the old warehouse.","zh":"不到一小時，火焰就吞沒了那座舊倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The expanding city is devouring farmland around it.","zh":"不斷擴張的城市正在吞噬周圍的農田。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0db2f4202a5d361f","term":"devour","forms":["devour","devours","devouring","devoured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"如飢似渴地讀看","explanation":"把讀書、看資料或觀察事物比作把內容吞進眼睛和頭腦裡，表示非常投入、急切地吸收。","examples":[{"en":"She devoured the mystery novel during the weekend.","zh":"她週末如飢似渴地讀完了那本懸疑小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She devoured three detective novels over the weekend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-872f0076c7e4835f34d8","word":"dew","forms":["dew"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cedee62aac80d55f","term":"dew","forms":["dew","dews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凝結的露水","explanation":"指空氣中的水汽遇到較冷的物體表面後凝結成的溼氣或水分，是“露水”這一現象的總稱。","examples":[{"en":"Dew covered the windows before sunrise.","zh":"日出前，窗戶上凝結了一層露水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dew sparkled on the spiderweb at sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46454972cc9a72b1","term":"dew","forms":["dew","dews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"清晨或傍晚植物上的露水","explanation":"特指清晨或傍晚落在草、葉子等植物上的露水，常能看到一顆顆小水滴。它是核心義“空氣中的水汽凝結在表面”的典型場景。","examples":[{"en":"The morning dew made the grass sparkle.","zh":"清晨的露水讓草地閃閃發亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her shoes were wet with dew after the walk.","zh":"散步後，她的鞋子被露水打溼了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a5d28d69b8b05a62cae","word":"diabetes","forms":["diabetes"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b10de0cf3558600c","term":"diabetes","forms":["diabetes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"糖尿病","explanation":"一種代謝性疾病：身體不能正常產生或利用胰島素，導致血糖長期過高。這是 diabetes 最主要、最需要優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Her doctor said she may have diabetes.","zh":"她的醫生說她可能患有糖尿病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise can help people with diabetes control their blood sugar.","zh":"規律運動可以幫助糖尿病患者控制血糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diabetes","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fea5dd8170f453b7c7ca","word":"diagnose","forms":["diagnose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1619a7e92dc6775d","term":"diagnose","forms":["diagnose","diagnoses","diagnosing","diagnosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"診斷疾病","explanation":"醫生根據一個人的症狀和體徵，判斷他患有什麼疾病；重點是查明病情，而不是進行治療。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor diagnosed her with pneumonia after examining her lungs.","zh":"醫生檢查了她的肺部後，診斷她患有肺炎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The condition is difficult to diagnose in its early stages.","zh":"這種病在早期很難診斷出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diagnose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-336c9a37af17ed6e","term":"diagnose","forms":["diagnose","diagnoses","diagnosing","diagnosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"查明問題原因","explanation":"把“診斷”這一思路用於醫學以外的情況，指根據表現找出機器、系統、計劃或其他問題的具體原因。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer quickly diagnosed the cause of the network failure.","zh":"工程師很快查明瞭網路故障的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician diagnosed a fault in the cooling system.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diagnose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b54e2b152c2135f45dfc","word":"diagnosis","forms":["diagnosis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71667bdb7b49b8ff","term":"diagnosis","forms":["diagnosis","diagnoses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫學診斷","explanation":"指醫生根據症狀、檢查結果等判斷疾病的性質和原因，也可以指最終得到的診斷結果。這是 diagnosis 最核心、最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor made a diagnosis after reviewing all the test results.","zh":"醫生檢視了所有檢查結果後作出了診斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was relieved to finally receive a diagnosis.","zh":"她最終得到診斷後鬆了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diagnosis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ae4e5638220599a","term":"diagnosis","forms":["diagnosis","diagnoses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對問題或故障的判斷","explanation":"把“透過線索找出本質”的思路擴充套件到醫學之外，表示判斷汽車、機器、系統或其他事情出了什麼問題以及為什麼出問題。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic made a quick diagnosis of the engine problem.","zh":"修理工很快判斷出了發動機的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic's diagnosis was a worn fuel pump.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diagnosis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c20a6b064ee805c6863","word":"diagram","forms":["diagram"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c0858baf1838253","term":"diagram","forms":["diagram","diagrams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"示意圖；結構圖","explanation":"用線條、符號或簡化的圖形說明某個東西怎樣工作，或說明整體中的各部分怎樣相互聯絡。它的重點不是畫得像，而是讓結構或過程更容易看懂。","examples":[{"en":"The manual includes a diagram of the water filter.","zh":"說明書裡有一張水過濾器的示意圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This diagram shows how the two systems are connected.","zh":"這張圖示說明了這兩個系統是怎樣連線的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diagram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8ea109519c2e8be","term":"diagram","forms":["diagram","diagrams","diagramming","diagraming","diagrammed","diagramed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用圖表示","explanation":"把某個物件、過程或關係畫成diagram，使別人能夠看出它的結構或運作方式。它就是名詞“圖示”轉成動詞後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher diagrammed the process on the board.","zh":"老師把這個過程畫在黑板上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you diagram how the parts fit together?","zh":"你能把這些部件如何組合在一起畫出來嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diagram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2144607a0ceef0303ff3","word":"dial","forms":["dial"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3b0ef86300a11fc","term":"dial","forms":["dial","dials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儀表錶盤","explanation":"dial是儀器上帶有刻度的圓盤，指標在刻度上移動，用來顯示速度、壓力等測量結果。它的核心形象是“圓盤上的指標指向某個數值”。","examples":[{"en":"The speedometer dial showed that we were driving too fast.","zh":"速度表的錶盤顯示我們開得太快了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red needle moved across the dial.","zh":"一根紅色指標在錶盤上移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-865f8f62e0ed093a","term":"dial","forms":["dial","dials","dialing","dialling","dialed","dialled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉動調節","explanation":"dial作動詞時，表示用旋鈕或類似方式控制、選擇某物；也可以比喻性地把某種程度調高或調低。它把“轉動圓盤讓指標或設定移動”的動作擴充套件到了抽象程度。","examples":[{"en":"The company dialled down its advertising budget this year.","zh":"公司今年減少了廣告預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please dial the heat down before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請把暖氣調低一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12aa29ccefb0b9f7","term":"dial","forms":["dial","dials","dialing","dialling","dialed","dialled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撥號呼叫","explanation":"dial表示在電話上輸入或選擇號碼，從而給某人或某個號碼打電話。它把轉動撥號盤選擇數字的動作概括成了“撥號”。","examples":[{"en":"Dial 911 if anyone is in danger.","zh":"如果有人處於危險中，請撥打911。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I dialled the office but nobody answered.","zh":"我撥了辦公室的電話，但沒人接。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3606d0cfb0802522626","word":"dialect","forms":["dialect"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-377f05d7ae5739b6","term":"dialect","forms":["dialect","dialects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某地區、社群或社會群體的語言變體","explanation":"這是最常用的核心意思：同一種語言在不同地方或不同群體中會長出不同的枝條，在語法、發音和詞彙上有一些差別，這樣的變體就是 dialect。","examples":[{"en":"She speaks a dialect of English that is common in the north.","zh":"她說的是北部常見的一種英語方言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel uses the local dialect to make the characters sound natural.","zh":"這部小說使用當地方言，讓人物說話聽起來更自然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dialect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fce0c28b2442ec1d","term":"dialect","forms":["dialect","dialects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語言家族中的一種方言或語言變體","explanation":"指一個語言群體內部相對獨立的地方性或少數群體語言變體，尤其是在它被看作某種共同語言的一部分，或被拿來與標準語比較時使用。它強調的是語言分類和社會認定，不表示這種變體本身低人一等。","examples":[{"en":"Many people consider the local variety a dialect of the national language.","zh":"許多人認為當地的語言變體是民族通用語的一種方言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The islands have developed a distinctive local dialect.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dialect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-abe0ba24dae6eb854ba2","word":"dialogue","forms":["dialogue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5050f6373419c650","term":"dialogue","forms":["dialogue","dialogues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對話；交流","explanation":"指兩個或多個個人之間有來有往的談話或討論，重點是雙方透過說話互相回應、交換看法。它也可以指較正式、持續進行的溝通，而不只是幾句隨口聊天。","examples":[{"en":"The two sides opened a dialogue about the new agreement.","zh":"雙方就這項新協議展開了對話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tried to maintain a dialogue with her neighbors.","zh":"她努力和鄰居保持溝通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dialogue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c01f0c73884de62","term":"dialogue","forms":["dialogue","dialogues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臺詞；對白","explanation":"指戲劇、電影、電視節目或其他敘事作品中由演員或角色說出的文字。這裡的 dialogue 不是現實中的交談，而是作品裡被寫出來、說出來的語言部分。","examples":[{"en":"The film has beautiful music, but the dialogue feels unnatural.","zh":"這部電影的音樂很美，但臺詞聽起來不自然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film's witty dialogue kept the audience laughing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dialogue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00a02fc515ab4e3f18e3","word":"diameter","forms":["diameter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-920e622039232820","term":"diameter","forms":["diameter","diameters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穿過圓心的直線","explanation":"在圓上取兩個點，若連線它們的線段正好穿過圓心，這條線段就是直徑；它可以看作把圓從一邊“橫穿”到另一邊的線。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a diameter through the center of the circle.","zh":"畫一條穿過圓心的直徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diameter of the wheel is easy to measure.","zh":"這個輪子的直徑很容易測量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diameter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7205ee5cc6fe39d","term":"diameter","forms":["diameter","diameters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直徑的長度","explanation":"這裡說的不是那條線本身，而是量出這條線有多長的數值；因此描述圓形物體大小時，diameter 後面通常會接具體單位或尺寸。","examples":[{"en":"This pipe has a diameter of five centimeters.","zh":"這根管子的直徑是五釐米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Measure the diameter before choosing a lid.","zh":"選蓋子前先量一下直徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diameter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81c9d6128b5fcd7bbe4b","word":"diamond","forms":["diamond"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d69746eb1f9184c","term":"diamond","forms":["diamond","diamonds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鑽石這種材料","explanation":"指由碳構成、非常堅硬並能閃光的鑽石礦物本身，常用於切割或製造工具。這裡強調的是材料，而不是一件首飾。","examples":[{"en":"The cutting blade is coated with diamond.","zh":"這把切割刀的表面覆有鑽石塗層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Diamond can scratch almost every other natural material.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diamond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8158e06b76e948d6","term":"diamond","forms":["diamond","diamonds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鑽石寶石","explanation":"指經過加工、可佩戴或收藏的一顆鑽石寶石。它是“鑽石材料”經過切割和打磨後成為的具體物件。","examples":[{"en":"The jeweler showed us three loose diamonds.","zh":"珠寶商給我們看了三顆散裝鑽石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small diamond was set in the pendant.","zh":"吊墜上鑲著一顆小鑽石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diamond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8cf49ca3d8f0a884e24","word":"diaper","forms":["diaper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94ceb62712b8e1c0","term":"diaper","forms":["diaper","diapers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尿布","explanation":"包在嬰兒或失禁者胯部、用來吸收尿液和糞便的用品，也就是通常說的尿布。","examples":[{"en":"We need to buy more diapers before the baby wakes up.","zh":"我們得在寶寶醒來前再買些尿布。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse showed me how to change an adult diaper.","zh":"護士教我怎樣給成年人換尿布。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diaper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c328ea261f18913","term":"diaper","forms":["diaper","diapers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶重複花紋的織物","explanation":"指一種織物：透過改變經緯線的方向織出反覆出現的菱形、花朵等圖案。這是比“尿布”更早的織物義。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a piece of diaper woven with small diamonds.","zh":"博物館展出了一塊織有小菱形圖案的這種織物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The linen diaper displayed a delicate diamond pattern.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diaper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d7fe146fad64b8833cd","word":"diary","forms":["diary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46ab493b28c018cc","term":"diary","forms":["diary","diaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日記；日記本","explanation":"指按天記錄個人經歷、感受、想法或事件的本子，也可以指其中寫下的內容。核心畫面是“每天翻一頁，把當天的生活留下來”。","examples":[{"en":"I write in my diary before I go to bed.","zh":"我睡覺前會寫日記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found an old diary in a box in the attic.","zh":"她在閣樓的一個箱子裡發現了一本舊日記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-625938ffb2dface3","term":"diary","forms":["diary","diaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日程本；約會記錄本","explanation":"指用來提前寫下約會、任務、課程或工作安排的本子。它仍然是“按日期儲存資訊”的本子，只是記錄的重點從已經發生的經歷變成將要做的事情。","examples":[{"en":"Let me check my diary to see whether I am free on Friday.","zh":"讓我查一下日程本，看看星期五有沒有空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I checked my diary before accepting the invitation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18a1083a0d0630915959","word":"dictate","forms":["dictate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df34b5714d16cb5b","term":"dictate","forms":["dictate","dictates","dictating","dictated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"命令；控制","explanation":"指以權力、地位或強勢態度要求別人照辦，或控制事情應當怎樣進行；重點是說話者在施加支配。","examples":[{"en":"You cannot dictate how other people should live.","zh":"你不能規定別人應該怎樣生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contract dictates the terms of payment.","zh":"合同規定了付款條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dictate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36aacef1891e66329201","word":"dictation","forms":["dictation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"dictation","forms":["dictation"],"pos":"n.","zh":"聽寫；口述記錄","examples":[{"en":"We had a short dictation test in English class.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The secretary wrote the letter from the manager's dictation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e2482a1a4258925aa56","word":"dictator","forms":["dictator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c29d6d5966056ca","term":"dictator","forms":["dictator","dictators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨裁者","explanation":"指以個人或少數人的絕對權力統治國家、壓制反對意見的領導人。這個意義保留了“一個人說了算”的核心畫面，通常含有明顯的貶義。","examples":[{"en":"The dictator silenced anyone who criticized his government.","zh":"這名獨裁者壓制了所有批評其政府的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country remained under the dictator's rule for decades.","zh":"這個國家在那名獨裁者的統治下持續了幾十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dictator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffd35e2ee82dad22","term":"dictator","forms":["dictator","dictators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"古羅馬獨裁官","explanation":"在古羅馬共和國時期，指由元老院授予最高行政權、通常為了處理戰爭等緊急事務而任職的一名官員。這是歷史制度中的專門義項，不等同於現代通常所說的暴君。","examples":[{"en":"In times of war, the Roman Senate could appoint a dictator for a limited term.","zh":"在戰爭時期，羅馬元老院可以任命一名任期有限的獨裁官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rome appointed a dictator during the military emergency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dictator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a6e2c2657c0434748a6","word":"dictatorship","forms":["dictatorship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f7197e1c3c3d64b","term":"dictatorship","forms":["dictatorship","dictatorships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨裁製度","explanation":"指國家的最高權力集中在一個人或少數人手中，民眾和其他政治力量缺少真正的制約與決定權。重點是“權力被牢牢攥在少數人手裡”這一制度狀態。","examples":[{"en":"A dictatorship may silence the press and restrict public debate.","zh":"獨裁製度可能壓制新聞自由，限制公眾討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country moved from a fragile democracy to a dictatorship.","zh":"這個國家從脆弱的民主制度轉變成了獨裁製度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dictatorship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a911ef662f844790","term":"dictatorship","forms":["dictatorship","dictatorships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨裁政權","explanation":"指實際實行專制統治的政府或政權，常用於歷史和新聞語境中，強調這個政權如何控制國家，而不只是說明一種政治制度。","examples":[{"en":"The dictatorship arrested thousands of people without trial.","zh":"這個獨裁政權未經審判就逮捕了數千人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dictatorship banned opposition newspapers and independent unions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dictatorship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-177ca70f42def1238e36","word":"dictionary","forms":["dictionary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eef77025df1d3f8f","term":"dictionary","forms":["dictionary","dictionaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詞典；字典","explanation":"一種按字母順序排列詞語並解釋其意義的參考書或工具，常常還提供發音、詞源、用法和翻譯等資訊。遇到不認識的詞時，人們會在其中查詢詞義。","examples":[{"en":"If you don't know the meaning of a word, look it up in the dictionary.","zh":"如果你不知道一個詞的意思，就去詞典裡查一查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I keep a small dictionary beside my desk.","zh":"我在書桌旁放著一本小詞典。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dictionary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8d79f40ddb79de569d7","word":"die","forms":["die"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bb95d6be09c8f52","term":"die","forms":["die","dies","dying","died","diest","diedst","dieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"死亡","explanation":"生命停止，不再活著；這是把 die 記成“停止”的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"Her grandfather died peacefully in his sleep.","zh":"她的祖父在睡夢中安詳地去世了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thousands of people die from air pollution every year.","zh":"每年有數千人死於空氣汙染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/die","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f83cff8066af378d5939","word":"diesel","forms":["diesel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60938f639f882e7c","term":"diesel","forms":["diesel","diesels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"柴油","explanation":"一種主要從石油等油料中提煉的較重燃料，柴油發動機透過壓縮空氣產生的熱量來點燃它。","examples":[{"en":"This truck runs on diesel.","zh":"這輛卡車使用柴油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Diesel is usually cheaper than petrol in this country.","zh":"在這個國家，柴油通常比汽油便宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diesel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19df5dceb558f6f8","term":"diesel","forms":["diesel","diesels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"柴油車","explanation":"指由柴油發動機驅動的車輛，尤其常用於卡車、公共汽車和轎車等語境。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a diesel because she drives long distances every week.","zh":"她買了一輛柴油車，因為她每週都要開車跑很遠的路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their old diesel struggles to start in winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diesel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a36c443337b53097a1ba","word":"diet","forms":["diet"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9c0b6ccffbd4201","term":"diet","forms":["diet","diets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日常飲食","explanation":"指一個人或動物平時吃的食物和喝的飲料的總體。重點不在某一次飯，而在一段時間內形成的攝入內容。","examples":[{"en":"The panda's diet consists mainly of bamboo.","zh":"大熊貓的飲食主要由竹子組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fish and vegetables form most of her diet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f4da2147b552db2","term":"diet","forms":["diet","diets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"控制飲食的計劃","explanation":"指為了減輕或增加體重，或影響健康，而有意識地安排吃什麼、喝什麼的一套計劃。它是把“飲食安排表”明確設定成健康目標。","examples":[{"en":"He's been on a diet since his doctor advised him to lose weight.","zh":"自從醫生建議他減重後，他一直在控制飲食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She followed a special diet recommended by her clinician.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5110a1d592d8ffd9","term":"diet","forms":["diet","diets","dieting","dieted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"控制飲食","explanation":"指主動改變自己的吃喝方式，以減輕或增加體重，或改善健康。它就是把原來的“飲食安排表”重新調整。","examples":[{"en":"I've been dieting for six months and have lost some weight.","zh":"我控制飲食已經六個月了，也減輕了一些體重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He dieted for months before the competition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-599fc58fd0f76984b4a8","word":"differ","forms":["differ"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddf6f6d41945c13e","term":"differ","forms":["differ","differs","differing","differed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"彼此不同","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物在性質、外形、特點等方面不一樣，重點是客觀比較它們的差別，而不一定包含好壞評價。","examples":[{"en":"The two designs differ in size but use the same materials.","zh":"這兩個設計的大小不同，但使用了相同的材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children of the same age can differ greatly in reading ability.","zh":"同齡兒童的閱讀能力可能有很大差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/differ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1071368f06e9d9c","term":"differ","forms":["differ","differs","differing","differed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"意見不同","explanation":"當主語是人或群體時，表示雙方對某件事的看法或判斷不一樣，也就是意見不同；它把“彼此不同”這個核心概念用到了觀點上。","examples":[{"en":"The two experts differ on how quickly the policy should be introduced.","zh":"兩位專家對於這項政策應多快實施意見不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I differ from my colleague on this question.","zh":"我和同事在這個問題上的看法不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/differ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-69ea741e98fdc758a781","word":"difference","forms":["difference"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d19ab7e84c404b7d","term":"difference","forms":["difference","differences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不同這一事實","explanation":"指兩個或多個人、事物不相同這一抽象事實，重點在“存在不同”，而不一定指出具體是哪一點不同。","examples":[{"en":"People should respect difference.","zh":"人們應該尊重差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The difference between their approaches became clear immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7fd86946a571133","term":"difference","forms":["difference","differences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體差異","explanation":"指使一個東西區別於另一個東西的具體特點，也就是可以找出來、列出來的不同之處。","examples":[{"en":"Can you spot the difference between these two photos?","zh":"你能看出這兩張照片的不同之處嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The main difference is the width of the handle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19fc0aa3a4a93d16","term":"difference","forms":["difference","differences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影響；作用","explanation":"指某個行動或變化使情況變好、變壞或發生改變的程度，也就是它和結果之間拉開的差距。","examples":[{"en":"A few extra minutes can make a big difference.","zh":"多幾分鐘就可能產生很大的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your support made a difference to my decision.","zh":"你的支援影響了我的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d6f965ac832e40a5df6","word":"different","forms":["different"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06d2709fbbccdecf","term":"different","forms":["different","more different","most different"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不一樣的","explanation":"表示某人或某物與另一個人、物或情況不相同，是 different 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"This answer is different from mine.","zh":"這個答案和我的不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Things are different now.","zh":"現在情況不一樣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/different","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86b961fcbeca50c9","term":"different","forms":["different","more different","most different"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別的；不尋常的","explanation":"表示某人或某物偏離通常樣子或一般做法，因此顯得特別；它仍然和“與常態不一樣”這一核心概念相連。","examples":[{"en":"She wanted to try something different for dinner.","zh":"她晚餐想嘗試點不一樣的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unusual entrance gives the house something different.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/different","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d53caf87c9ac4e7189e","word":"differentiate","forms":["differentiate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f444e95e720ec662","term":"differentiate","forms":["differentiate","differentiates","differentiating","differentiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使產生差別","explanation":"透過改變形式、特點或用法，把原本相近的事物拉開，使它們變得不同或更容易區分。","examples":[{"en":"The redesign differentiated the new phone from its cheaper competitors.","zh":"重新設計使這款新手機區別於價格更低的競爭產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Its waterproof shell differentiates this camera from earlier models.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/differentiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a464900646477a75","term":"differentiate","forms":["differentiate","differentiates","differentiating","differentiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯示兩者的差別","explanation":"說明或體現某個特徵如何把兩個事物區分開，重點在於指出“差別在哪裡、由什麼造成”。","examples":[{"en":"What differentiates this soup from the others is its smoky flavor.","zh":"這道湯區別於其他湯的地方，是它帶有煙燻味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diagram differentiates the two species by wing shape.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/differentiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8614929c866e504","term":"differentiate","forms":["differentiate","differentiates","differentiating","differentiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辨認出差別","explanation":"透過觀察或判斷，認出兩個相似事物之間的不同，從而知道哪個是真、哪個是假，或哪個屬於哪一類。","examples":[{"en":"With practice, you can differentiate a real signature from a forgery.","zh":"經過練習，你就能辨認出真簽名和偽造簽名的區別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you differentiate the genuine signature from the forgery?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/differentiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e4453a98c9d741737a0","word":"difficult","forms":["difficult"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e15ca835d1dd597","term":"difficult","forms":["difficult","more difficult","most difficult"],"pos":"adj","zh":"困難的；不容易的","explanation":"指事情、任務或情況不容易處理，需要較多時間、能力或努力才能完成。它可以描述實際操作上的難度，也可以描述局面讓人難以應付。","examples":[{"en":"It was difficult to find a quiet place to work.","zh":"找一個安靜的地方工作很難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The difficult conditions delayed the rescue team.","zh":"惡劣而困難的條件耽擱了救援隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difficult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0f6157b2cbecb4d","term":"difficult","forms":["difficult","more difficult","most difficult"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難應付的；不配合的","explanation":"形容人或動物不容易管理、說服或相處，常帶有“故意不合作、愛找麻煩”的意味；也可形容某種局面很棘手。","examples":[{"en":"Our new customer is difficult and complains about everything.","zh":"我們的新客戶很難應付，什麼都要抱怨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The difficult passenger refused to fasten his seat belt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difficult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b129ae4200d2244c056b","word":"difficulty","forms":["difficulty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b56ce34c9e9d848","term":"difficulty","forms":["difficulty","difficulties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"做某事有困難","explanation":"指某件事難以完成，或某人做這件事時感到吃力；重點是“路本身不好走”或“行動不容易”。","examples":[{"en":"I had difficulty finding the right address.","zh":"我很難找到正確的地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has difficulty sleeping when she is worried.","zh":"她擔心時很難入睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difficulty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5faa3cf2c2be2cdd","term":"difficulty","forms":["difficulty","difficulties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"妨礙目標的具體障礙","explanation":"指在實現目標的過程中擋住去路的具體問題或障礙；它不是泛泛地說“很難”，而是指出讓計劃無法順利進行的阻力。","examples":[{"en":"We ran into a difficulty while preparing the report.","zh":"我們準備報告時遇到了一個難處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of transport was their greatest difficulty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/difficulty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebbde58a4bbe357e599b","word":"dig","forms":["dig"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-070d67a295186373","term":"dig","forms":["dig","digs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考古挖掘；挖掘現場","explanation":"指為了尋找和研究古代遺物、化石等而進行的挖掘活動，也可指正在進行這種工作的地點。它可以看作動詞“挖”的名詞化結果。","examples":[{"en":"The students spent a week helping at an archaeological dig.","zh":"這些學生花了一週時間在一個考古挖掘現場幫忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dig uncovered the remains of an ancient house.","zh":"這次挖掘發現了一座古代房屋的遺蹟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a65bc42f91cf513","term":"dig","forms":["dig","digs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戳；捅","explanation":"指用手指、手肘等快速而有力地推或戳某人，常常是為了引起對方注意，或帶著玩笑意味。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a dig in the ribs to stop me talking.","zh":"她戳了戳我的肋部，讓我別再說了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a playful dig in the ribs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e17ad7a78d42b8db","term":"dig","forms":["dig","digs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"挖苦；諷刺話","explanation":"指故意說出的帶刺評論，好像用語言戳對方一下，因此和“戳”的基本意象相連。","examples":[{"en":"His comment sounded like a dig at my new job.","zh":"他的話聽起來像是在挖苦我的新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her remark about punctuality was a dig at me.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3d150a1be02b13e","term":"dig","forms":["dig","digs","digging","dug","digged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"挖；掘出一個洞","explanation":"指把土、石頭等材料移開，通常是為了向下挖洞，也可泛指在堅硬材料中挖出通道或孔洞。","examples":[{"en":"We dug a small hole for the new tree.","zh":"我們為新樹挖了一個小坑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers dug through the rock to reach the tunnel.","zh":"工人們挖穿岩石，抵達了隧道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e38b98e85b7f7d47","term":"dig","forms":["dig","digs","digging","dug","digged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"深入調查；找出","explanation":"把“挖”引申為向資訊深處挖掘，指認真查詢事實、證據或資料，常常要把隱藏的內容找出來。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter dug into the company's financial records.","zh":"記者深入調查了這家公司的財務記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dug up some useful information about the school.","zh":"她查到了一些關於那所學校的有用資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc74fc91d58be90f","term":"dig","forms":["dig","digs","digging","dug","digged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"戳；用肘推","explanation":"指用手指、手肘或其他身體部位突然推、戳某人，和名詞“戳”來自同一個核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"He dug his elbow into my side when the teacher turned around.","zh":"老師轉身時，他用肘部戳了我一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dug him in the ribs with her elbow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bf474896363505e5ea5","word":"digest","forms":["digest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40b53cea175a754d","term":"digest","forms":["digest","digests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整理後的摘要或彙編","explanation":"指把較多材料篩選、歸類並整理成便於查閱的內容，重點不在逐字收錄，而在有條理地呈現要點。","examples":[{"en":"The report is a useful digest of recent research.","zh":"這份報告是近期研究成果的一份實用匯編。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newsletter provides a digest of recent court decisions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/digest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a6db5e9ef5886e1","term":"digest","forms":["digest","digests","digesting","digested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消化食物","explanation":"指身體把吃下的食物分解並吸收，使其中可利用的部分被身體利用；這是最直接的生理意義。","examples":[{"en":"Some people digest beans more easily than others.","zh":"有些人比其他人更容易消化豆類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soup is light and easy to digest.","zh":"這湯清淡，容易消化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/digest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-105cc76536a739bd","term":"digest","forms":["digest","digests","digesting","digested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在頭腦中消化、理解","explanation":"指把聽到或讀到的複雜資訊在頭腦中慢慢整理、思考並弄明白，就像頭腦在“消化”資訊一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Give me a moment to digest everything you have explained.","zh":"給我一點時間，讓我消化一下你解釋的全部內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She read the proposal twice before she could digest it.","zh":"她把提案讀了兩遍才真正理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/digest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c165a933df05102b00b","word":"digestion","forms":["digestion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89233cd94697ec37","term":"digestion","forms":["digestion","digestions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消化過程","explanation":"指食物進入胃腸道後，被分解並轉化為身體可以利用的物質的過程。它強調的是從食物到可吸收養分的整體處理過程。","examples":[{"en":"Digestion begins in the mouth when we chew our food.","zh":"消化從我們咀嚼食物時在口腔中開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water is important for healthy digestion.","zh":"水分對正常消化很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/digestion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cda3c373f19f1c5114f0","word":"digital","forms":["digital"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42837b15f3de0d24","term":"digital","forms":["digital"],"pos":"adj","zh":"用離散數字表示的","explanation":"表示資訊不是以連續變化的形式儲存，而是被分成一個個離散的數值，通常以二進位制數字表示。這就像把連續的資訊切分成許多明確的數字格子。","examples":[{"en":"The sensor converts the signal into digital data.","zh":"感測器把訊號轉換成數字資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This digital computer can process huge amounts of information.","zh":"這臺數字計算機可以處理大量資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/digital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-249bf690ae9703ea","term":"digital","forms":["digital"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與計算機和資訊時代有關的","explanation":"在現代英語中，digital 常進一步泛指與計算機、網際網路和資訊時代有關的事物。它由“用數字表示資訊”擴充套件成了“依靠數字技術運作”的整體概念。","examples":[{"en":"Many people now use digital services to pay their bills.","zh":"現在許多人使用數字服務來支付賬單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is investing heavily in digital technology.","zh":"這家公司正在大力投資數字技術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/digital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-dcddf1ef3dad105ca96e","word":"dignity","forms":["dignity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb3453caa8bacfb2","term":"dignity","forms":["dignity","dignities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尊嚴；人格價值","explanation":"指一個人內在值得尊重的品質，以及由此產生的自重和體面。它常用於強調即使處境困難，人也應被當作有價值、有尊嚴的人來對待。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone deserves to live with dignity.","zh":"每個人都應該有尊嚴地生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kept her dignity despite the public criticism.","zh":"儘管受到公開批評，她仍維護了自己的尊嚴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dignity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54bce24e5ecf1257","term":"dignity","forms":["dignity","dignities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"莊重；體面","explanation":"指舉止、場面或環境表現出的莊重、正式和有分寸的氣度。它是尊嚴在外表和行為上的體現，使人或場合顯得不輕浮、不隨便。","examples":[{"en":"The ceremony was conducted with dignity.","zh":"儀式舉行得莊重而得體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She accepted the defeat with quiet dignity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dignity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ea607f9a01e62d1531a","word":"dilemma","forms":["dilemma"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d5deed5d70abf81","term":"dilemma","forms":["dilemma","dilemmas","dilemmata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兩難困境","explanation":"指必須在兩個或多個選擇之間作決定，而這些選擇看起來都不理想、都可能帶來麻煩。重點不是“有選擇”，而是每個選擇都讓人不舒服或難以接受。","examples":[{"en":"She faced a dilemma: tell the truth or protect her friend.","zh":"她陷入了兩難：說出真相，還是保護朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The decision left me in a difficult dilemma.","zh":"這個決定讓我陷入了艱難的兩難困境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dilemma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29a47f1d77b7b349","term":"dilemma","forms":["dilemma","dilemmas","dilemmata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棘手的問題","explanation":"也可以泛指讓人難以處理的複雜問題，不一定嚴格包含兩個明確的選項；不過它仍然保留“很難找到好辦法”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The company is facing a dilemma over how to reduce costs without cutting jobs.","zh":"這家公司正面臨一個棘手問題：如何降低成本而不裁員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing keys left us with a dilemma.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dilemma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a61e4090fce75bfbd76","word":"diligence","forms":["diligence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4fff5e17104c1cc","term":"diligence","forms":["diligence","diligences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勤勉；持續努力","explanation":"指為了完成目標而穩定、持續並認真地投入時間和精力，不是隻在一時興起時努力。它強調長期堅持和做事紮實。","examples":[{"en":"Her diligence in preparing the reports earned the team's trust.","zh":"她認真持續地準備報告，贏得了團隊的信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With diligence, he eventually mastered the difficult skill.","zh":"他靠持續努力，最終掌握了這項困難的技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diligence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76f58b9a55d87f01","term":"diligence","forms":["diligence","diligences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勤奮認真的品質","explanation":"指一個勤奮者身上體現出的認真、堅定和堅持不懈等品質。這裡關注的是人的做事品格，而不只是某一次具體的努力。","examples":[{"en":"The manager praised the new assistant for her diligence.","zh":"經理稱讚新助理勤奮認真。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His diligence ensured that every document was checked.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diligence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf08fccd9d8bfd57d4e6","word":"diligent","forms":["diligent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61d0b1cbacf2fd44","term":"diligent","forms":["diligent","more diligent","most diligent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"勤奮專注的","explanation":"形容一個人做事時持續下功夫，並且集中注意力、認真負責；重點不只是花時間，而是帶著專心和自覺把事情做好。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is diligent in preparing for her final exams.","zh":"瑪雅認真勤奮地準備期末考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our most diligent intern checks every report twice.","zh":"我們最勤奮認真的實習生會把每份報告檢查兩遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diligent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5d4b45934fe1d9c636d","word":"dim","forms":["dim"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc7943f32afffdce","term":"dim","forms":["dim","dimmer","dimmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"昏暗的","explanation":"表示光線很弱，因而看不清楚；也可指顏色不鮮明。","examples":[{"en":"The hallway was dim, so I switched on the light.","zh":"走廊裡很昏暗，所以我開啟了燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ate dinner in a dim restaurant.","zh":"我們在一家燈光昏暗的餐館吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1179f95a149759b","term":"dim","forms":["dim","dims","dimming","dimmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變暗","explanation":"使燈光或其他發光物變得不那麼亮，就是把“逐漸變暗”施加到某個物件上。","examples":[{"en":"Please dim the lights during the movie.","zh":"電影開始時請把燈光調暗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dimmed her phone screen before bed.","zh":"睡前她把手機螢幕調暗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4f72e459c6833675d7b","word":"dime","forms":["dime"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f545cb7a81ae4fe8","term":"dime","forms":["dime","dimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"十美分硬幣","explanation":"美國或加拿大貨幣中價值一美元十分之一的硬幣，也就是十美分。它是 dime 最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I found a dime under the sofa.","zh":"我在沙發下面找到了一枚十美分硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine costs a dime to use.","zh":"使用這臺機器要花十美分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48eb632fe16ae19550af","word":"dimension","forms":["dimension"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b0aba2453b52ac8","term":"dimension","forms":["dimension","dimensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方面；維度","explanation":"指理解一個事物時可以單獨考察的一個方面或角度。一個電影既可以從劇本、表演等不同 dimension 來評價，意思就是它在多個方面都值得考察。","examples":[{"en":"The project has succeeded in several dimensions, not just financially.","zh":"這個專案在多個方面都取得了成功，不只是財務方面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her research adds a new dimension to the debate.","zh":"她的研究為這場爭論增加了一個新的角度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dimension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ff4af1b4c9e2223","term":"dimension","forms":["dimension","dimensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空間尺寸；維度","explanation":"指物體在某個空間方向上的尺度，如長度、寬度、高度或深度。說一個空間有三個 dimensions，通常是指可以沿三個獨立方向移動或定位。","examples":[{"en":"Please check the dimensions of the table before you buy it.","zh":"買這張桌子之前，請先檢查它的尺寸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We live in a world with three spatial dimensions.","zh":"我們生活在一個具有三個空間維度的世界裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dimension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef527ccc32ee6df974d0","word":"diminish","forms":["diminish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ada86b8040684b3","term":"diminish","forms":["diminish","diminishes","diminishing","diminished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變小、變少或變弱","explanation":"表示主動讓某物的大小、數量、程度或力量降低，重點是“使它不如原來”。不一定是物理尺寸變小，也可以是影響、自由或風險等抽象事物減少。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise can diminish the risk of heart disease.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以降低患心臟病的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new rules diminished the workers' freedom to choose their hours.","zh":"新規定減少了工人選擇工作時間的自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diminish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-502b186b20f0ce0b","term":"diminish","forms":["diminish","diminishes","diminishing","diminished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸減少或減弱","explanation":"表示某種數量、程度或力量自己慢慢變少、變弱，不強調有人主動使它下降。可以形容噪聲、興趣、信心、資源等逐步減退。","examples":[{"en":"Her excitement diminished as the long wait continued.","zh":"隨著漫長的等待繼續，她的興奮感逐漸減退了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The noise diminished as the train entered the distance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diminish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e21032adbefc5cfc779e","word":"dine","forms":["dine"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd3cdce8a2aa5517","term":"dine","forms":["dine","dines","dining","dined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用餐；吃正餐","explanation":"dine 的核心畫面是坐下來吃一天中的正餐，尤其是晚餐或較正式的一餐。它比普通的 eat 更有“用餐、赴宴”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"We dined at a small restaurant near the harbor.","zh":"我們在港口附近的一家小餐館用餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guests dined together after the ceremony.","zh":"賓客們在儀式結束後一起用餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9a5e786827ceef6","term":"dine","forms":["dine","dines","dining","dined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"招待吃飯；供給正餐","explanation":"這裡的畫面從“自己吃正餐”擴充套件為“讓別人有正餐可吃”：某人或某處為客人提供一頓飯，或招待客人用餐。","examples":[{"en":"The host dined the visiting scholars in his garden.","zh":"主人在花園裡設宴招待來訪的學者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ambassador wined and dined the visiting delegation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dda209044ad44962b012","word":"dinner","forms":["dinner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bdb852f534b16bf8","term":"dinner","forms":["dinner","dinners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一天中的主餐","explanation":"指一天中最重要、最正式的一頓飯，現代英語裡通常在晚上吃。重點是“主餐”這一概念，而不只是鐘點。","examples":[{"en":"What are we having for dinner tonight?","zh":"今晚我們吃什麼正餐？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our family eats dinner at noon on Sundays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dinner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aab875886279a4af","term":"dinner","forms":["dinner","dinners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"晚餐","explanation":"特指晚上吃的那頓飯，是dinner在日常英語中最常見的具體時間用法。","examples":[{"en":"We usually have dinner together at seven.","zh":"我們通常七點一起吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We're having vegetable curry for dinner tonight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dinner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-300908b9d3815e2d3ba5","word":"dinosaur","forms":["dinosaur"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50a0b95c1740c489","term":"dinosaur","forms":["dinosaur","dinosaurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恐龍","explanation":"指屬於恐龍類的動物，尤其是生活在三疊紀、侏羅紀和白堊紀、後來滅絕的動物。現代鳥類在科學分類上也屬於恐龍類，因此嚴格的科學用法不一定把鳥排除在外。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a full-size model of a Tyrannosaurus rex.","zh":"這家博物館有一具按霸王龍真實大小製作的模型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists believe that birds are living dinosaurs.","zh":"科學家認為鳥類是仍然存活的恐龍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dinosaur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b19b2701e748f4e","term":"dinosaur","forms":["dinosaur","dinosaurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"非鳥類恐龍","explanation":"日常口語中常用來指恐龍類中不包括鳥類的成員，也就是人們通常想象的那些已經滅絕的陸地恐龍。","examples":[{"en":"Children dug up what looked like a dinosaur bone in the garden.","zh":"孩子們在花園裡挖出了一個看起來像恐龍骨頭的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum reconstructed the skeleton of a giant dinosaur.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dinosaur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6813f3af2d45fbfc768","word":"dip","forms":["dip"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8ae4ccbbc4ead85","term":"dip","forms":["dip","dips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低窪處","explanation":"dip 可以指道路、地面或地質地形中向下凹的一段，也就是“向下”形成的低處。","examples":[{"en":"There is a dip in the road ahead.","zh":"前面的路上有一處低窪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rainwater collected in a dip beside the road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cc0219efdd2d7b3","term":"dip","forms":["dip","dips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蘸醬","explanation":"dip 可以指用來蘸食物的濃稠醬料，例如搭配薯片、蔬菜或麵包的醬。它把食物“向下、再出來”地浸入醬中。","examples":[{"en":"We made a spicy dip for the vegetables.","zh":"我們給蔬菜做了一種辣味蘸醬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Serve the crackers with a spicy bean dip.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2be688a0544b60eb","term":"dip","forms":["dip","dips","dipping","dipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"浸入液體","explanation":"把某物短暫地放入液體中，通常還會再拿出來，正是“向下、再出來”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"She dipped the strawberries into melted chocolate.","zh":"她把草莓蘸進融化的巧克力裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dip the brush in water before you start painting.","zh":"開始畫畫前，把畫筆蘸一下水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bcad958c53a54bc","term":"dip","forms":["dip","dips","dipping","dipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"小幅下降","explanation":"表示價格、溫度、利率、支援率等數值向下變動一點，通常不是大幅下跌。","examples":[{"en":"Sales dipped slightly in January.","zh":"一月份的銷量小幅下降了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature dipped below zero overnight.","zh":"夜間氣溫降到了零度以下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81e901b4262cabd9caa6","word":"diploma","forms":["diploma"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de3fea77a354b258","term":"diploma","forms":["diploma","diplomas","diplomata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文憑；畢業證書","explanation":"指學校、學院等教育機構頒發的正式檔案，證明持有人已經完成某項課程，或已經取得相應學位。重點是這張檔案代表並證明學習成果，而不是學習成果本身。","examples":[{"en":"She got her diploma after two years of study.","zh":"她學習兩年後拿到了畢業證書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He framed his diploma and put it above his desk.","zh":"他把文憑裝框，掛在了書桌上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diploma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1cb74e23f5ffd0793b6","word":"diplomacy","forms":["diplomacy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-954d9062b67248b6","term":"diplomacy","forms":["diplomacy","diplomacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外交；國際談判","explanation":"指國家或國際組織之間透過談判來處理關係、建立聯盟、簽訂條約或達成協議的實踐。它的核心畫面是各方坐在談判桌邊，不靠武力，而靠協商爭取本方利益並維持關係。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries used diplomacy to avoid a trade war.","zh":"兩國透過外交手段避免了一場貿易戰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Successful diplomacy led to a new peace agreement.","zh":"成功的外交談判促成了一項新的和平協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diplomacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c6e20832e1dafe02","term":"diplomacy","forms":["diplomacy","diplomacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓融處事；避免衝突的技巧","explanation":"指與人相處時運用委婉、機智和分寸感，避免激化矛盾或幫助雙方和解的能力。它仍然像談判桌上的 diplomacy，只是談判物件從國家換成了家人、同事或朋友。","examples":[{"en":"She handled the disagreement with great diplomacy.","zh":"她非常圓融地處理了這次分歧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Resolving their quarrel required patience and diplomacy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diplomacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-372c74ea8827080c2e9d","word":"diplomat","forms":["diplomat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a87814163a3de67","term":"diplomat","forms":["diplomat","diplomats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外交官","explanation":"指被正式授權代表本國政府，與其他國家或國際組織打交道的人，例如大使或參與國際談判的官員。這個義項體現了“代表一方、謹慎處理關係”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The diplomat met with officials from three neighboring countries.","zh":"這名外交官會見了來自三個鄰國的官員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked as a diplomat for more than ten years.","zh":"她做了十多年的外交官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diplomat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-450224c64986921b","term":"diplomat","forms":["diplomat","diplomats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓融處事的人","explanation":"指處理人際關係時很有分寸、善於避免衝突並讓各方都能接受的人。這裡不一定真的從事外交工作，而是把外交官在談判中的謹慎和圓融用來形容普通人。","examples":[{"en":"You were a real diplomat when you settled the argument between them.","zh":"你調解他們的爭吵時真是圓融又有分寸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It takes a diplomat to keep those siblings peaceful.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diplomat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-76658a7ce8e6114a3121","word":"diplomatic","forms":["diplomatic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6fede013c3809732","term":"diplomatic","forms":["diplomatic","more diplomatic","most diplomatic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外交的；國家間關係的","explanation":"指國家政府之間的關係、工作或活動，核心是透過外交渠道處理國與國之間的事務。","examples":[{"en":"She spent thirty years working for Canada's diplomatic service.","zh":"她在加拿大外交部門工作了三十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two countries restored diplomatic relations last spring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diplomatic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-902912d78abe5152","term":"diplomatic","forms":["diplomatic","more diplomatic","most diplomatic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"圓融得體的；善於避免衝突的","explanation":"形容說話或處理問題時顧及他人的感受，用委婉而有分寸的方式提出意見，從而避免爭吵或傷害感情。","examples":[{"en":"He was diplomatic when he told me that my first draft needed more work.","zh":"他很委婉地告訴我，我的初稿還需要進一步修改。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her diplomatic reply avoided embarrassing either colleague.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diplomatic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d15690f08a575024650b","word":"direct","forms":["direct"],"officialPos":"adj./v./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7684e6ffc1e1bd42","term":"direct","forms":["direct","more direct","most direct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不繞道地進行","explanation":"表示行動或過程沿著目標推進，中間沒有偏離、繞行或被打斷，重點是“直奔目標”。","examples":[{"en":"The train goes direct to the city center.","zh":"這趟火車直達市中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a direct flight from here to Rome.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ed7f5536ed91ab1","term":"direct","forms":["direct","more direct","most direct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直達的；最短的","explanation":"形容路線、方向或方法不彎曲、不繞遠，能夠以較短或最簡單的路徑到達終點。","examples":[{"en":"This is the most direct route to the museum.","zh":"這是去博物館最直接的路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We booked a direct flight to Seoul.","zh":"我們訂了直飛首爾的航班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03ac86c113656af2","term":"direct","forms":["direct","more direct","most direct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"坦率的","explanation":"形容說話或態度不繞圈子、真誠坦率，直接表達自己的想法或要求。","examples":[{"en":"She was direct with me about the problem.","zh":"她坦率地告訴了我這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’ll be direct: we need more time.","zh":"我就直說吧：我們需要更多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-021e070b1864bc30","term":"direct","forms":["direct","directs","directing","directed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"管理；操控","explanation":"表示負責把一個組織、事務、行動或力量朝著目標安排和控制，像把整體執行方向握在手中。","examples":[{"en":"She directs a team of engineers.","zh":"她負責管理一個工程師團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He directed the rescue operation.","zh":"他指揮了這次救援行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71a7dfcb55f0eb75","term":"direct","forms":["direct","directs","directing","directed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指引；指向","explanation":"表示告訴某人應走哪條路、去哪裡，或把某人引向正確的資訊來源；核心是為對方指出方向。","examples":[{"en":"A volunteer directed us to the nearest exit.","zh":"一名志願者指引我們去最近的出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The receptionist directed me to the right office.","zh":"前臺把我指引到正確的辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93c4abe27cf169610253","word":"direction","forms":["direction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-85d621ac455b140b","term":"direction","forms":["direction","directions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方向；朝向","explanation":"指從某個起點出發、朝向某處或沿著某條路線移動時所指的方向，可以是上下、左右、南北，也可以是相對於某個物體的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Keep going in the same direction until you reach the bridge.","zh":"繼續朝同一個方向走，直到你到達那座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind suddenly changed direction.","zh":"風向突然變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff345b3318b6b991","term":"direction","forms":["direction","directions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展方向；趨勢","explanation":"把“方向”從空間中的箭頭引申到抽象事務，表示一個計劃、行動或局勢將來大體朝哪裡發展。","examples":[{"en":"The company is moving in a more sustainable direction.","zh":"這家公司正朝著更加可持續的方向發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The debate signals a new direction in housing policy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bab8bf75440add4","term":"direction","forms":["direction","directions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指導；指示","explanation":"指有人替你把行動的“箭頭”指清楚，告訴你該怎麼做，或在工作、表演中給出引導。","examples":[{"en":"The new manager gave the team clear direction.","zh":"新經理為團隊指明瞭清晰的方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apprentices worked under the direction of a master carpenter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/direction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16bdd7451e20a9b0eee4","word":"directive","forms":["directive"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c7fddfee64ca01e","term":"directive","forms":["directive","directives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指示；指南","explanation":"指告訴人們如何行動或怎樣達到目標的說明，可以是工作指南，也可以是較正式的行動要求；它就是“指路牌”這個核心形象本身。","examples":[{"en":"The new directive requires all staff to complete safety training.","zh":"新指示要求所有員工完成安全培訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please follow the directive posted beside the machine.","zh":"請遵守機器旁張貼的操作指示。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/directive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef7d74898c22a4bf0be4","word":"director","forms":["director"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c489401d08f41ffa","term":"director","forms":["director","directors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負責人；導演","explanation":"指負責給某項工作、部門、專案或製作活動確定方向並組織執行的人。在電影、戲劇等語境中，通常譯為“導演”；在機構或公司中，通常譯為“主管”或“負責人”。","examples":[{"en":"She was appointed director of the research department.","zh":"她被任命為研究部門主管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The director asked the actors to repeat the scene.","zh":"導演讓演員們把這一場戲再演一遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/director","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e3779ddef268c01","term":"director","forms":["director","directors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"董事","explanation":"指公司董事會中的成員，負責參與公司的重大決策和監督，而不一定負責日常管理。","examples":[{"en":"The directors approved the company's new budget.","zh":"董事們批准了公司的新預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The board appointed two new directors this quarter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/director","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-333178788eae3e0b14c9","word":"directory","forms":["directory"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ab0eda77f244e28","term":"directory","forms":["directory","directories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名單目錄","explanation":"按字母順序或其他分類方式整理的名單，通常列出某類人的姓名、地址或某些機構的資訊，方便查詢。","examples":[{"en":"I found her number in the online directory.","zh":"我在網上名錄裡找到了她的電話號碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her number appears in the staff directory.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/directory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fba62e8ca22e42d","term":"directory","forms":["directory","directories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料夾","explanation":"計算機檔案系統中的虛擬容器，裡面可以存放檔案和其他資料夾；可以把它想成電腦裡用來整理檔案的抽屜。","examples":[{"en":"Create a new directory for your photos.","zh":"為你的照片新建一個資料夾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing documents had been moved into the archive directory.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/directory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3838a8256696f47188d","word":"dirt","forms":["dirt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4f2209e34986317","term":"dirt","forms":["dirt","dirts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"泥土","explanation":"指地面上的土、泥土等自然物質，尤其是沾到鞋子或物品上的土。","examples":[{"en":"The children were playing in the dirt behind the house.","zh":"孩子們在房子後面的泥土裡玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wipe the dirt off your shoes.","zh":"請把鞋上的泥土擦掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f2e1230f4a08485","term":"dirt","forms":["dirt","dirts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汙漬","explanation":"指沾在衣服、物品或表面上的髒東西，使外觀變差；它仍然是“沾上的髒東西”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"There was dirt on the white shirt.","zh":"白襯衫上有汙漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A damp cloth will remove the dirt.","zh":"溼布可以擦掉這些汙漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0c92c764c5647d43d71","word":"dirty","forms":["dirty"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f88c7cd117e71584","term":"dirty","forms":["dirty","dirtier","dirtiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"髒的；沾有汙物的","explanation":"指表面有泥、灰塵、油汙等令人不舒服的東西，和“乾淨”相反。這是 dirty 最直接、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"My shoes got dirty on the walk home.","zh":"我走回家時鞋子弄髒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wash your dirty hands before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前請把髒手洗乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ecbfef1448badfc","term":"dirty","forms":["dirty","dirtier","dirtiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"下流的；淫穢的","explanation":"指笑話、語言、圖片或行為帶有性方面的不雅內容，因而令人覺得冒犯或不適。","examples":[{"en":"He told a dirty joke at the dinner table.","zh":"他在餐桌上講了一個下流笑話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That magazine has some dirty pictures in it.","zh":"那本雜誌裡有一些淫穢圖片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad67fa18be421a0d","term":"dirty","forms":["dirty","dirtier","dirtiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不光彩的；卑鄙的","explanation":"指行為或手段違反公平、誠信等通常認可的標準，讓人覺得卑鄙或不講道德。","examples":[{"en":"Using a fake injury to win was a dirty trick.","zh":"用假裝受傷來獲勝是個卑鄙的手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They played dirty during the final match.","zh":"他們在決賽中使用了不公平的手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a77473a193b0ddd4","term":"dirty","forms":["dirty","dirties","dirtying","dirtied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄髒","explanation":"指使某物沾上汙物，使它從乾淨狀態變髒。","examples":[{"en":"The children dirtied their clothes in the mud.","zh":"孩子們在泥裡把衣服弄髒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take off your boots before you dirty the carpet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dirty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d296add506bba3096a4f","word":"disability","forms":["disability"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3292c3f678915418","term":"disability","forms":["disability","disabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種具體的殘障或能力障礙","explanation":"指一個人的身體或智力能力受到明顯限制的具體狀況，例如影響行動、感知、學習或處理資訊的障礙。這是把 disability 看成個人所具有的一種具體情況。","examples":[{"en":"She has a disability that affects her mobility.","zh":"她有一種影響行動能力的殘障。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school provides support for students with disabilities.","zh":"這所學校為有殘障的學生提供支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83ec5acae5ffe990","term":"disability","forms":["disability","disabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殘障狀態","explanation":"指一個人處於能力受限的總體狀態，而不是某一種具體障礙。它把重點放在“處於殘障狀態”這一事實，以及這種狀態對生活和活動的影響上。","examples":[{"en":"The program helps people living with disability find work.","zh":"這個專案幫助殘障人士尋找工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Disability can affect access to education and healthcare.","zh":"殘障可能影響人們獲得教育和醫療服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8914c3b4aa997c7","term":"disability","forms":["disability","disabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"由障礙和社會環境共同造成的功能限制","explanation":"這裡不只看個人有什麼身體或認知障礙，還看環境是否有足夠的無障礙設施和合理安排。比如，行動不便本身是一種障礙，而沒有電梯的建築可能把這種障礙進一步變成無法進入的實際限制。","examples":[{"en":"Better public transport can reduce disability by removing barriers.","zh":"更好的公共交通可以透過消除障礙來減少功能受限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building was redesigned to improve disability access.","zh":"這座建築經過重新設計，以改善殘障人士的無障礙通行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9d8992f348162fd95ac","word":"disable","forms":["disable"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-753c7449a7c6e4f7","term":"disable","forms":["disable","disables","disabling","disabled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停用功能","explanation":"指把裝置、軟體或其中某項功能關掉，使它暫時不能執行。這裡不是把裝置弄壞，而是主動把它的“能力之燈”關閉，通常之後還可以重新啟用。","examples":[{"en":"You can disable notifications in the settings.","zh":"你可以在設定中停用通知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pilot disabled the automatic control system.","zh":"飛行員停用了自動控制系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56bc61b1f9464924","term":"disable","forms":["disable","disables","disabling","disabled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使失去能力","explanation":"指透過傷害或其他外力，使某人失去原有的行動或完成事情的能力。它突出的是“把能力之燈關掉”的結果，而不只是暫時做不到某事。","examples":[{"en":"The accident disabled him for life.","zh":"那場事故使他終身喪失了行動能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury disabled him for several months.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28c03d30bb4ff66961b9","word":"disadvantage","forms":["disadvantage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cb5d0ed349afe50","term":"disadvantage","forms":["disadvantage","disadvantages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺點；不便之處","explanation":"指某件事本身不理想、會帶來額外麻煩或讓人覺得不方便的地方，就像天平的一端多了負擔。","examples":[{"en":"The main disadvantage of working from home is that it can feel lonely.","zh":"在家工作的主要缺點是可能會讓人感到孤單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One disadvantage of this phone is its short battery life.","zh":"這部手機的一個缺點是電池續航時間短。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disadvantage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f97312c7e3dbbc86","term":"disadvantage","forms":["disadvantage","disadvantages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劣勢；不利條件","explanation":"指某人的身高、資源、處境等使其在競爭或完成任務時比別人少一份優勢，因此更難達到目標。","examples":[{"en":"Without a car, she was at a disadvantage when applying for jobs outside the city.","zh":"沒有汽車，她申請城外的工作時處於劣勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The steep rent put smaller shops at a disadvantage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disadvantage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7faf32d6cfc6607a","term":"disadvantage","forms":["disadvantage","disadvantages","disadvantaging","disadvantaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使處於不利地位","explanation":"指某種做法讓某人少了一份優勢，像把他放到了比賽中更靠後的位置；不一定是故意傷害，也可能只是規則或條件造成的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The new system may disadvantage people who do not have reliable internet access.","zh":"新系統可能會讓無法穩定上網的人處於不利地位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rule disadvantages applicants with caring responsibilities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disadvantage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3d454cba432588ba4f5a","word":"disagree(ment)","forms":["disagree","disagreement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d5814ecb7d03713","term":"disagree","forms":["disagree","disagrees","disagreeing","disagreed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不同意；持不同看法","explanation":"當兩個人的想法沒有對齊時，表示其中一方不贊同另一方的意見或信念。它可以只是客觀地說明看法不同，不一定表示發生了爭吵。","examples":[{"en":"I disagree with your conclusion, but I understand how you reached it.","zh":"我不同意你的結論，但我理解你是怎麼得出這個結論的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two researchers disagreed about the best way to solve the problem.","zh":"兩位研究人員在解決這個問題的最佳方法上意見不一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disagree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9868fec6c96e5078","term":"disagree","forms":["disagree","disagrees","disagreeing","disagreed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不一致；不相符","explanation":"當資料、結果、證據或說法彼此對不上時，也可以說它們 disagree。這裡不是“爭論”，而是把兩條沒有對齊的資訊進行比較。","examples":[{"en":"The figures in the two reports disagree with each other.","zh":"兩份報告中的資料彼此不一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two thermometers disagree by three degrees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disagree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffe8b558996d18de","term":"disagreement","forms":["disagreement","disagreements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次爭論或分歧","explanation":"指雙方因為看法、選擇或決定不同而發生的一次具體爭論；重點是“這件事上的分歧”，不一定是激烈的吵架。","examples":[{"en":"They had a disagreement about where to hold the meeting, but they settled it quickly.","zh":"他們因會議地點發生了分歧，但很快就解決了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had a disagreement with my neighbor about the noise.","zh":"我和鄰居因噪聲問題發生了爭執。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disagreement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbb224fc17091f0f","term":"disagreement","forms":["disagreement","disagreements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意見不一致的狀態","explanation":"指人們、觀點或結論之間缺乏一致，不一定已經發生面對面的爭論；它強調的是一種持續或普遍存在的分歧狀態。","examples":[{"en":"There is still considerable disagreement over how the policy should be implemented.","zh":"對於這項政策應如何實施，人們仍存在很大分歧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was widespread disagreement over the revised timetable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disagreement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed142ddaa38e131ca699","word":"disappear","forms":["disappear"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-748fa0ac43ef26e0","term":"disappear","forms":["disappear","disappears","disappearing","disappeared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消失；不見","explanation":"指人或事物從視線、原處或可感知範圍中不見了，重點是“原本在那裡，後來看不到了”。","examples":[{"en":"The cat disappeared under the bed.","zh":"那隻貓在床底下不見了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fog disappeared by noon.","zh":"到中午時霧散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disappear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e11ca4e89c0c745b","term":"disappear","forms":["disappear","disappears","disappearing","disappeared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"失蹤","explanation":"專指人突然不見、去向不明，因而成為失蹤者；這是“從畫面中消失”用於人的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"A young man disappeared after leaving work.","zh":"一名年輕男子下班後失蹤了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hiker disappeared during a sudden snowstorm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disappear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04573b636e8ea22e2ad6","word":"disappoint(ment)","forms":["disappoint","disappointment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43a45ec5f5d55978","term":"disappoint","forms":["disappoint","disappoints","disappointing","disappointed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人失望","explanation":"某人的表現、結果或行為沒有達到他人的期待，從而使那個人難過或不滿意。這裡的核心畫面是期待的包裹沒有按希望送到。","examples":[{"en":"The final result disappointed everyone on the team.","zh":"最終結果讓團隊裡的每個人都失望了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hope I won't disappoint you.","zh":"我希望不會讓你失望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disappoint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e70694e8f7482f95","term":"disappoint","forms":["disappoint","disappoints","disappointing","disappointed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"未達到預期","explanation":"主語可以是人或事物，意思是沒有實現某個希望、目標或預期；重點放在“期待落空”本身，而不一定強調某個人的情緒。","examples":[{"en":"The new model disappointed our expectations.","zh":"這款新型號沒有達到我們的預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The much-advertised restaurant disappointed us.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disappoint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-474697c7b3d1d842","term":"disappointment","forms":["disappointment","disappointments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"失望情緒","explanation":"指期待沒有實現時產生的悲傷、沮喪或不滿，是“氣球落下”時人的內在感受。這裡通常說的是一種抽象情緒，而不是某個具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"She felt deep disappointment when the concert was canceled.","zh":"音樂會取消時，她感到深深的失望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His disappointment was obvious after the interview.","zh":"面試結束後，他的失望顯而易見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disappointment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67234230f732057f","term":"disappointment","forms":["disappointment","disappointments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人失望的情況","explanation":"指一次沒有達到預期的經歷、結果或情況，也就是讓人產生失望情緒的那件事本身。它強調“發生了什麼令人失望的事”，而不只是心裡的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The delay was a disappointment for everyone waiting at the station.","zh":"這次延誤讓所有在車站等候的人都很失望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long-awaited sequel was a serious disappointment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disappointment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05be8129a9d540d579a9","word":"disapprove","forms":["disapprove"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8062160d9c471ea","term":"disapprove","forms":["disapprove","disapproves","disapproving","disapproved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不贊成；認為不妥","explanation":"指認為某人、某事錯誤、不合適或令人不滿，重點是表達明確的反對態度，常常帶有批評意味。","examples":[{"en":"My parents disapprove of me staying out so late.","zh":"我這麼晚還不回家，我父母很不贊成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people disapprove of wasting food.","zh":"許多人不贊成浪費食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disapprove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff736a5da5ad7dc0","term":"disapprove","forms":["disapprove","disapproves","disapproving","disapproved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拒絕批准；否決","explanation":"指有權作決定的人或機構不接受正式申請、計劃或提案，因此不予批准；這裡不是單純表達個人不喜歡。","examples":[{"en":"The committee disapproved the request for extra funding.","zh":"委員會拒絕批准追加資金的請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city disapproved the building plan because it violated safety rules.","zh":"市政府因該建築方案違反安全規定而拒絕批准它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disapprove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6af308d5ad701d4b9fe0","word":"disaster","forms":["disaster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b7848982f22904c","term":"disaster","forms":["disaster","disasters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重大災難","explanation":"指突然發生、規模較大並造成嚴重破壞、人員傷亡或環境長期改變的自然災害或人為災害。它對應記憶中的“壞星星墜落”，強調後果嚴重，而不只是普通的不順利。","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake was one of the worst natural disasters in the country's history.","zh":"這場地震是該國歷史上最嚴重的自然災害之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Volunteers arrived quickly to provide food and shelter after the disaster.","zh":"災難發生後，志願者迅速趕來提供食物和住所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disaster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-492aaafe4c13155c","term":"disaster","forms":["disaster","disasters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慘敗；糟糕的事情","explanation":"泛指帶來巨大損失、煩惱、混亂或失望的事件，不一定達到真正災害的規模。一次計劃、演出、旅行或個人經歷只要糟到幾乎完全失敗，也可以被形容為 disaster。","examples":[{"en":"The party was a complete disaster because nobody had brought enough food.","zh":"因為沒人帶夠食物，這次聚會徹底搞砸了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our first rehearsal was a complete disaster.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disaster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c02ff7ef091ae7871ca0","word":"disastrous","forms":["disastrous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42498c3d43575d6b","term":"disastrous","forms":["disastrous","more disastrous","most disastrous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"災難性的；後果極其嚴重的","explanation":"形容某件事本身或它造成的結果糟糕到足以引發重大損失、失敗或災難。它比“糟糕”語氣強得多，常用於批評決定、計劃、政策、行動或局面。","examples":[{"en":"The company made a disastrous decision to ignore the safety warnings.","zh":"這家公司無視安全警告，作出了災難性的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm had disastrous consequences for the coastal villages.","zh":"這場暴風雨給沿海村莊帶來了災難性的後果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disastrous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cd067b8c8d94de8712e","word":"disbelief","forms":["disbelief"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba615ddcfa12a6b8","term":"disbelief","forms":["disbelief","disbeliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"難以相信；不相信","explanation":"指一個人面對某個事實時，心裡不願或無法把它當真，常常因為事情太意外、太嚴重或太不可思議。","examples":[{"en":"She shook her head in disbelief when she saw the final bill.","zh":"她看到最後的賬單時難以置信地搖了搖頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers listened in disbelief as the company announced the closure.","zh":"公司宣佈關閉時，工人們難以置信地聽著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disbelief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c0cd8947e6383da","term":"disbelief","forms":["disbelief","disbeliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"震驚","explanation":"這裡突出“不敢相信”帶來的驚愕：看到或聽到出乎意料的事情時，人會因為震驚而一時難以接受。","examples":[{"en":"He read the message twice and stared at the screen in disbelief.","zh":"他把訊息讀了兩遍，難以置信地盯著螢幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stared in disbelief at the winning numbers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disbelief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-109fa9f54c849bb7c2e9","word":"discard","forms":["discard"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-976d3426ed6c9f0b","term":"discard","forms":["discard","discards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被丟棄的東西","explanation":"discard是已經被丟掉、不要或捨棄的東西，重點在於它從原來的使用範圍中被拿開了。","examples":[{"en":"The discard was still on the table.","zh":"那件被丟棄的東西還在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist fashioned sculptures from industrial discards.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7508455bef57771e","term":"discard","forms":["discard","discards","discarding","discarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"丟掉；捨棄","explanation":"discard表示主動把不需要的東西、想法或方案排除掉，不再繼續使用或考慮；這就是“把它甩到一邊”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"She discarded the old plan and started again.","zh":"她放棄了舊計劃，重新開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please discard any damaged batteries.","zh":"請把所有損壞的電池丟掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4ac536145d6649da1b8","word":"discharge","forms":["discharge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee374d4be7f1953d","term":"discharge","forms":["discharge","discharges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"釋放；出院","explanation":"表示把人或某物放出、釋放的行為；在醫療語境中尤其常指病人出院。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor arranged her discharge from the hospital.","zh":"醫生安排她出院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient went home the day after discharge.","zh":"病人出院後的第二天回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discharge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93dbb2ca0e92756b","term":"discharge","forms":["discharge","discharges","discharging","discharged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"履行義務","explanation":"表示完成自己應承擔的義務、職責或任務，也就是把責任履行完、卸下來。","examples":[{"en":"He worked hard to discharge his responsibilities as a manager.","zh":"他努力履行經理的職責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company failed to discharge its legal obligations.","zh":"這家公司沒有履行法律義務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discharge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74a3899833d87fa0","term":"discharge","forms":["discharge","discharges","discharging","discharged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解除債務或責任","explanation":"表示使某人不再承擔債務、索賠、指控或其他責任；可以理解為把壓在身上的負擔卸掉。","examples":[{"en":"The settlement discharged him from all further claims.","zh":"這項和解使他免於承擔今後的所有索賠責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The payment discharged the company from its debt.","zh":"這筆付款使公司清償了債務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discharge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a55bdc40c7ab6172","term":"discharge","forms":["discharge","discharges","discharging","discharged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"釋放；排出","explanation":"表示把人、液體、氣體或其他東西放出去，是 discharge 最基本的“卸下並放走”用法。","examples":[{"en":"The valve discharges excess pressure from the tank.","zh":"閥門把多餘壓力從罐中釋放出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital discharged him after two days.","zh":"住院兩天後，醫院讓他出院了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discharge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea76abe985499b53","term":"discharge","forms":["discharge","discharges","discharging","discharged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放出；排出","explanation":"表示管道、裝置或其他來源把水、氣體、熱量等向外放出，是“釋放”主線在物質上的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The pipe discharges clean water into the channel.","zh":"這根管子把清水排入水道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine discharges heat through the side vents.","zh":"這臺機器透過側面的通風口散熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discharge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e25d68d5b755714fdd95","word":"disciple","forms":["disciple"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5e2e5b603b8e097","term":"disciple","forms":["disciple","disciples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門徒；弟子","explanation":"指向某位老師、思想家或宗教人物學習的人，通常還會繼續實踐並傳播對方的教導，所以不只是短期上課的學生。","examples":[{"en":"She became a disciple of the famous painter.","zh":"她成了那位著名畫家的弟子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The disciple later taught the same method to others.","zh":"這名弟子後來把同樣的方法教給了別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disciple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b7f7417c3d5d5a7","term":"disciple","forms":["disciple","disciples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"追隨者；信徒","explanation":"強調積極擁護並跟隨某人的思想、事業或生活方式；這種人未必正在接受面對面的教學。","examples":[{"en":"He was a devoted disciple of the reformer's ideas.","zh":"他是那位改革者思想的忠實追隨者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A disciple of Gandhi, he rejected violent protest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disciple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f4d06395c0c6e56","term":"disciple","forms":["disciple","Disciples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耶穌的門徒","explanation":"特指跟隨耶穌、接受其教導的人，是“門徒、追隨者”核心形象在基督教語境中的具體化。","examples":[{"en":"The Disciples traveled with Jesus and listened to his teaching.","zh":"門徒們跟隨耶穌旅行，聆聽他的教導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Peter was a disciple of Jesus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disciple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72b9eb08b2fd254e2144","word":"disciplinary","forms":["disciplinary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28c518e33794422d","term":"disciplinary","forms":["disciplinary","more disciplinary","most disciplinary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"紀律方面的","explanation":"指與紀律、規則的維持或紀律訓練有關；它可以強呼叫規則促成良好行為，不一定涉及懲罰。這個意思正是“圍繞紀律的一圈”的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"Clear disciplinary rules helped the team work more efficiently.","zh":"明確的紀律規則幫助團隊更高效地工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager believes that deadlines can have a disciplinary effect on the project.","zh":"經理認為，截止期限可以對專案起到約束作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disciplinary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a005ac01a7ee1f1","term":"disciplinary","forms":["disciplinary","more disciplinary","most disciplinary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"處分用的","explanation":"指為了處理違規行為、施加懲罰或正式處分而採取的措施。它是“紀律”這條主線向懲罰一端發展的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company may take disciplinary action against employees who repeatedly ignore safety rules.","zh":"公司可能會對一再忽視安全規定的員工採取紀律處分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repeated lateness may lead to disciplinary action.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disciplinary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d43c8bd5797aa43a56f5","word":"discipline","forms":["discipline"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cf0bd8272dbcc2a","term":"discipline","forms":["discipline","disciplines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自律；行為控制","explanation":"指一個人能夠控制自己的衝動和行為，按要求或目標持續行動；這種“把自己收攏好”的能力可以來自訓練，也可以靠自己培養。","examples":[{"en":"Learning a language takes discipline and regular practice.","zh":"學習一門語言需要自律和規律的練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed great discipline and finished the project on time.","zh":"她表現出很強的自律，按時完成了專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discipline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16d370e3512fb040","term":"discipline","forms":["discipline","disciplines","disciplining","disciplined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"訓練；教導","explanation":"指透過反覆指導和練習，使某人獲得技能、習慣或受控的行為方式；重點是把人逐步訓練上軌道。","examples":[{"en":"The coach disciplined the young players to follow the team's routine.","zh":"教練訓練年輕隊員遵守球隊的日常安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program disciplines students in careful laboratory work.","zh":"這個專案訓練學生進行嚴謹的實驗室工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discipline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99d79cff2cb32aac8428","word":"disclose","forms":["disclose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a25e6d72dfd7371b","term":"disclose","forms":["disclose","discloses","disclosing","disclosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"披露；透露","explanation":"指把原本不為別人所知的資訊、事實或秘密公開出來，就像把藏著的東西揭開給人看。這是現代英語中最重要、最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company disclosed the results of its safety investigation.","zh":"公司公開了安全調查的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refused to disclose where she had found the document.","zh":"她拒絕透露自己在哪裡找到那份檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disclose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63decf29699b6595","term":"disclose","forms":["disclose","discloses","disclosing","disclosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭開；使顯露","explanation":"指移除遮擋或外殼，讓原來藏在裡面、看不見的實物顯露出來，例如揭開覆蓋物後露出某個物體。","examples":[{"en":"Removing the top layer disclosed a narrow passage beneath it.","zh":"移去頂層後，下面露出了一條狹窄的通道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The retreating tide disclosed a line of ancient posts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disclose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8187135faead31889255","word":"disclosure","forms":["disclosure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55fb82d15fd38581","term":"disclosure","forms":["disclosure","disclosures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公開；透露","explanation":"指把原本隱藏或不為人知的資訊告訴別人這一行為，重點在“掀開遮擋、讓別人知道”的動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The disclosure of the report surprised everyone.","zh":"這份報告的公開讓所有人都感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company refused to make a full disclosure.","zh":"該公司拒絕作出完整披露。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disclosure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed22bfa4cd3367f8","term":"disclosure","forms":["disclosure","disclosures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式披露","explanation":"指把一項原本隱藏的事實或一組事實正式告知另一方，常見於法律、合同、調查或商業往來中；這裡更強調“向特定物件作出公開”這一過程。","examples":[{"en":"The contract requires full disclosure of all financial interests.","zh":"合同要求完整披露所有財務利益關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lawyer requested disclosure of the relevant documents.","zh":"律師要求披露相關檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disclosure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4577e0d592336abb8897","word":"discomfort","forms":["discomfort"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d8ab0b8e852ddb4","term":"discomfort","forms":["discomfort","discomforts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不適；難受","explanation":"指身體或心理上失去舒適狀態後的難受感覺，例如疼痛、緊張、焦慮或坐得不舒服。重點是“舒適感被打破”，不一定嚴重到生病。","examples":[{"en":"She felt considerable discomfort after sitting in the same position for hours.","zh":"她連續幾個小時保持同一個姿勢後感到很不舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bright light caused discomfort in his eyes.","zh":"強光使他的眼睛感到不適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discomfort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cf6b4e591905acd","term":"discomfort","forms":["discomfort","discomforts","discomforting","discomforted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使不適；使煩惱","explanation":"表示某人或某事打破了另一個人的舒適感，使其身體難受、心理不安或感到尷尬。它是名詞核心義的動作形式：把人帶入不舒服的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer’s personal question visibly discomforted the guest.","zh":"採訪者的私人問題明顯讓嘉賓感到不自在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tight collar discomforted him throughout the meeting.","zh":"整個會議期間，緊領子一直讓他很不舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discomfort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f935a0f03deea2fa71a","word":"disconnect","forms":["disconnect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d9d372b4e1aacf1","term":"disconnect","forms":["disconnect","disconnects","disconnecting","disconnected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"斷開連線","explanation":"指把網路、線路、裝置或其他原本相連的東西斷開，也可以表示連線本身中斷。它直接體現了“把連著的東西拆開”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please disconnect the printer from the computer before moving it.","zh":"移動印表機前，請先把它與電腦斷開連線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My phone disconnected from the car's Bluetooth.","zh":"我的手機與汽車的藍芽斷開了連線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disconnect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-221617318bcf512885af","word":"discount","forms":["discount"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5cfcdbb52fde4ea0","term":"discount","forms":["discount","discounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"折扣；減價","explanation":"指從原價中減去的一部分金額，買方因此少付錢，是最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Students can get a ten percent discount on train tickets.","zh":"學生買火車票可以享受九折優惠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students receive a discount on museum admission.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f52f56f460f4f54c","term":"discount","forms":["discount","discounts","discounting","discounted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……打折；降價出售","explanation":"指把商品原來的售價扣掉一部分後出售，也就是“給商品打折”。","examples":[{"en":"The shop discounted all winter coats by thirty percent.","zh":"這家商店把所有冬季外套都打了七折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They discounted the damaged boxes before putting them on sale.","zh":"他們先給有損壞的箱子降價，然後才拿出來賣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e80cef8c4479e9f0bb5","word":"discourage(ment)","forms":["discourage"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-767317d56e1c3692","term":"discourage","forms":["discourage","discourages","discouraging","discouraged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使洩氣；打擊信心","explanation":"指把某人的勇氣和信心壓低，使對方感到灰心、沮喪，甚至不再相信自己能完成某事。","examples":[{"en":"One bad result shouldn't discourage you from trying again.","zh":"一次糟糕的結果不應該讓你失去再次嘗試的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long wait discouraged many volunteers.","zh":"漫長的等待讓許多志願者洩了氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discourage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29a9be799ef0a4a1","term":"discourage","forms":["discourage","discourages","discouraging","discouraged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勸阻；使不願做","explanation":"指把某個行動的念頭壓下去，勸某人不要做某事；重點不是讓人難過，而是讓人放棄或避免一項行動。","examples":[{"en":"The high cost discouraged us from buying a new car.","zh":"高昂的費用使我們打消了買新車的念頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The signs discourage visitors from feeding wildlife.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discourage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfcf44328d2b807c8cfd","word":"discourse","forms":["discourse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c28fab550bb98cb","term":"discourse","forms":["discourse","discourses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"言語或文字論述","explanation":"指用語言表達思想的過程或整體，可以是口頭表達，也可以是文章、學術寫作等書面表達。","examples":[{"en":"Images play an important role in scientific discourse.","zh":"影象在科學論述中發揮著重要作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article examines how language shapes public discourse.","zh":"這篇文章考察語言如何塑造公共討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discourse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a42540a167a6651","term":"discourse","forms":["discourse","discourses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式長篇論述","explanation":"指圍繞某個主題進行的正式而較長的演講、講解或文章；它是“思想在語言中充分展開”的典型形式。","examples":[{"en":"The professor gave a detailed discourse on climate policy.","zh":"教授就氣候政策作了一篇詳細的論述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His discourse on architecture lasted nearly an hour.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discourse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b90071aea261a5b8380","word":"discover","forms":["discover"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ceb73af6e7b76100","term":"discover","forms":["discover","discovers","discovering","discovered","discoverest","discoveredst","discovereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發現；瞭解到","explanation":"原先不知道某人、某物或某個事實，後來透過觀察、經歷或調查第一次知道了它。重點不是單純把東西拿到手，而是讓新的資訊進入自己的認識範圍。","examples":[{"en":"We discovered a quiet beach behind the village.","zh":"我們發現村子後面有一片安靜的海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I discovered that the shop was closed on Mondays.","zh":"我發現那家商店週一不營業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa44132b238e67958fb1","word":"discovery","forms":["discovery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf16219f5f579014","term":"discovery","forms":["discovery","discoveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發現成果","explanation":"指被發現出來的人、事物、事實或資訊，重點是“揭開之後露出的東西”。它既可以指一個具體的新發現，也可以泛指發現成果。","examples":[{"en":"The team made an important discovery while studying the old maps.","zh":"研究舊地圖時，這個團隊有了一項重要發現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This latest discovery could lead to better treatments for the disease.","zh":"這項最新發現可能帶來更好的疾病治療方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discovery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0c7f8686aef4776","term":"discovery","forms":["discovery","discoveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發現活動","explanation":"指探索未知、尋找新事物的過程或活動本身，強調“不斷掀開未知之處”，而不是某一個已經找到的成果。","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of the voyage was discovery.","zh":"這次航行的目的是探索和發現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientific discovery often begins with an unexpected observation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discovery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c2733abf54ccb0f4186","word":"discreet","forms":["discreet"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6dcda0b2aaf32188","term":"discreet","forms":["discreet","more discreet","discreeter","most discreet","discreetest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"謹慎體貼；尊重隱私","explanation":"指說話或做事顧及別人的隱私和體面，不把敏感事情公開，也不讓對方難堪；這種謹慎通常帶有圓融、外交式的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She gave him a discreet warning before the meeting.","zh":"開會前，她委婉而謹慎地提醒了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel arranged a discreet meeting for the two families.","zh":"酒店為兩家人安排了一次低調而私密的會面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discreet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d4cbd219a386306","term":"discreet","forms":["discreet","more discreet","discreeter","most discreet","discreetest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不顯眼；低調","explanation":"指某人、某物或某種行動不吸引注意，不刺激別人，也不顯得張揚；它仍然保留“把自己或事情壓低存在感”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The new sign is small and discreet, so it does not spoil the building's appearance.","zh":"新招牌又小又不顯眼，不會破壞建築的外觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Discreet lighting highlighted the paintings without distracting visitors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discreet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-988c29be3757f1931211","word":"discriminate","forms":["discriminate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45028217d5b56cb9","term":"discriminate","forms":["discriminate","discriminates","discriminating","discriminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辨別；區分","explanation":"指根據顏色、形狀、聲音等差異認出兩個或多個物件並把它們分開看待。這裡沒有“不公平”的意思，只是準確地分辨不同之處。","examples":[{"en":"Can you discriminate between these two shades of blue?","zh":"你能分辨出這兩種藍色的差別嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sensor can discriminate between real and artificial smoke.","zh":"這個感測器能分辨真實煙霧和人造煙霧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discriminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26ae8f205a82d0aa","term":"discriminate","forms":["discriminate","discriminates","discriminating","discriminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"區別對待；歧視","explanation":"指因為人的身份、特徵或背景不同而對其採取不同待遇，通常暗示這種區別不公平。它把“分辨差異”從事物擴充套件到了對人的行為或影響。","examples":[{"en":"The company must not discriminate against older workers.","zh":"公司不得歧視年長的員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Employers must not discriminate against applicants because of age.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discriminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7615f6d756e69c3","term":"discriminate","forms":["discriminate","discriminates","discriminating","discriminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"歧視某人或群體","explanation":"與 s2 同屬“因差異而區別對待”的意思，強調主動對某個群體或個人採取不平等待遇。重點仍是這種區別對待，而不是單純發現差別。","examples":[{"en":"It is illegal to discriminate against applicants because of their religion.","zh":"因為宗教信仰而歧視求職者是違法的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Employers must not discriminate against disabled applicants.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discriminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e93ced725763a701ffea","word":"discrimination","forms":["discrimination"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd185319b5cd6128","term":"discrimination","forms":["discrimination","discriminations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辨別；分辨能力","explanation":"指仔細看出事物之間的差異，並據此作出正確判斷的行為或能力。它強調的不只是“看見不同”，還包括理解這些差異的重要性。","examples":[{"en":"Good discrimination is essential when choosing reliable information online.","zh":"在網上選擇可靠資訊時，良好的辨別力至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The job requires discrimination between useful evidence and misleading claims.","zh":"這項工作要求能夠辨別有用的證據和誤導性的說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discrimination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3371a1a1b289683d","term":"discrimination","forms":["discrimination","discriminations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歧視；不公平區別對待","explanation":"指僅僅因為一個人屬於某個群體，就給予他較差或不公平的待遇，而不是根據其個人表現來判斷。這是現代英語中非常常見的義項。","examples":[{"en":"The company has a policy against discrimination based on age or disability.","zh":"這家公司有一項禁止基於年齡或殘疾進行歧視的政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reported discrimination at work after being denied promotion for no clear reason.","zh":"她因為在沒有明確理由的情況下被拒絕晉升，報告了工作場所的歧視問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discrimination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6a919ef536282bf60c0","word":"discuss","forms":["discuss"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13370938fd034609","term":"discuss","forms":["discuss","discusses","discussing","discussed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"討論；商議","explanation":"圍繞一個話題交換看法、分析情況或權衡選擇，重點是把問題拆開來共同思考，而不只是隨意聊天。","examples":[{"en":"We need to discuss the plan before we make a final decision.","zh":"我們需要先討論一下這個計劃，再作最後決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They discussed whether to move to a larger apartment.","zh":"他們討論了要不要搬到更大的公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discuss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3cc610240ec72ccfbf16","word":"discussion","forms":["discussion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1172a7fb032862f4","term":"discussion","forms":["discussion","discussions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"討論；商談","explanation":"指人們圍繞一個明確話題交換意見、分析問題或進行辯論，重點是把話題展開，而不一定要有衝突。","examples":[{"en":"There was a lively discussion about how to reduce food waste.","zh":"大家熱烈討論瞭如何減少食物浪費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a short discussion of the plan before the meeting ended.","zh":"會議結束前，我們簡短討論了一下這個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discussion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e5ce2e74725e6dc","term":"discussion","forms":["discussion","discussions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"論述；討論部分","explanation":"指書籍、論文、報告等文字中圍繞某個主題展開的進一步說明，像是把口頭討論整理成了書面內容。","examples":[{"en":"The final discussion explains why the experiment produced different results.","zh":"最後的論述解釋了為什麼這項實驗得出了不同的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discussion of limitations appears after the results.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/discussion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8e8c313b6712eb77272","word":"disease","forms":["disease"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-429141d4aba43fa0","term":"disease","forms":["disease","diseases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疾病","explanation":"指人、動物或植物身體出現的異常狀態，會造成不適、功能失常或健康受損；它通常強調生病這一狀態，而不是一次突然造成的外傷。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor said the cough was caused by a lung disease.","zh":"醫生說，這種咳嗽是由肺部疾病引起的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tomato plants developed a disease that turned their leaves brown.","zh":"這些番茄植株患了一種使葉子變褐的病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac38bdecc7047c9e","term":"disease","forms":["disease","diseases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有害的社會問題","explanation":"把“身體生病”的概念推廣到社會、制度、態度或生活方式，指其中持續存在並造成損害的嚴重問題。","examples":[{"en":"Many people see corruption as a disease that weakens society.","zh":"許多人把腐敗看作一種會削弱社會的病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He described corruption as a disease infecting public life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcf0b9529a4450ad686b","word":"disgrace","forms":["disgrace"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d59b1826fae96c5","term":"disgrace","forms":["disgrace","disgraces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"失寵；失去尊重","explanation":"指一個人或團體從原來受信任、受尊重的位置跌落，因而不再受歡迎或被重視，重點是“失去他人的好感和尊敬”。","examples":[{"en":"After the scandal, the minister fell into disgrace.","zh":"醜聞之後，這位部長失去了公眾的信任和尊重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scandal left the former director in disgrace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disgrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d22b97311c112c0c","term":"disgrace","forms":["disgrace","disgraces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蒙羞；受辱","explanation":"指一個人因為嚴重錯誤或不光彩的行為而處於羞恥、名譽受損的狀態，也就是“跌到讓人抬不起頭的位置”。","examples":[{"en":"He lived in disgrace after betraying his closest friends.","zh":"背叛最親密的朋友後，他一直揹負著恥辱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scandal brought disgrace upon the entire institution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disgrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ecc8d97857468ee","term":"disgrace","forms":["disgrace","disgraces","disgracing","disgraced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使蒙羞；使失去聲譽","explanation":"指某人的行為或某件事把人、團體或名聲從受尊敬的位置拉下來，使其受到羞辱或失去社會認可。","examples":[{"en":"His lies disgraced the company and damaged its reputation.","zh":"他的謊言使公司蒙羞，也損害了公司的聲譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was disgraced by the corruption scandal.","zh":"她因腐敗醜聞而身敗名裂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disgrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83180b745cbfaa82c9d0","word":"disguise","forms":["disguise"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ae0a962b7d15ccd","term":"disguise","forms":["disguise","disguises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偽裝裝扮","explanation":"指用衣服、化妝、假髮等改變外貌的東西，使人難以認出真實身份，或讓人看起來像另一個人。","examples":[{"en":"The detective wore a disguise to enter the building.","zh":"偵探戴著偽裝進入了那棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wig and dark glasses completed her disguise.","zh":"假髮和墨鏡使她的偽裝完整了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disguise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7546d46aa56acb30","term":"disguise","forms":["disguise","disguises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"掩蓋真相的外表","explanation":"指事物表面呈現出的樣子，用來遮住裡面真正的性質、原因或內容；這裡不一定涉及人的身份。","examples":[{"en":"The friendly offer was a disguise for a plan to control the company.","zh":"這個友好的提議其實是控制公司的計劃的掩飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her polite smile was a disguise for growing anger.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disguise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-320e31368dd81bed","term":"disguise","forms":["disguise","disguises","disguising","disguised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偽裝身份或外表","explanation":"指改變某人或某物的外表，使其不容易被認出，或使其呈現出另一種身份。最常見的是某人主動把自己偽裝起來。","examples":[{"en":"She disguised herself as a delivery worker.","zh":"她把自己偽裝成一名送貨員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The costume disguised his face completely.","zh":"這套服裝完全遮掩了他的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disguise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c5a8d802eb1eba6","term":"disguise","forms":["disguise","disguises","disguising","disguised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掩飾真實情況","explanation":"指用假象隱藏秘密、真實感情、目的或意圖，使別人看不出事情的真相；這裡被掩飾的可以完全不是外貌。","examples":[{"en":"He disguised his disappointment with a smile.","zh":"他用微笑掩飾了自己的失望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company disguised the problem as a temporary delay.","zh":"公司把這個問題掩飾成一次暫時的延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disguise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2dfe878c689fbabdddf","word":"disgust","forms":["disgust"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae4eff8137b5364e","term":"disgust","forms":["disgust"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈厭惡","explanation":"指因某事令人噁心、卑劣或非常不快而產生的強烈反感，程度明顯高於普通的不喜歡。","examples":[{"en":"She pushed the dirty plate away with disgust.","zh":"她厭惡地把那隻髒盤子推開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He watched the cruel prank with disgust.","zh":"他厭惡地看著那個殘忍的惡作劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disgust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bec04a7ec71f13e8","term":"disgust","forms":["disgust","disgusts","disgusting","disgusted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使厭惡","explanation":"指某種行為、事物或情況讓人產生強烈反感；可以把它理解為“把厭惡的感覺推給某人”。","examples":[{"en":"The smell of spoiled milk disgusted everyone in the kitchen.","zh":"變質牛奶的氣味讓廚房裡的每個人都感到厭惡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It disgusts me to see people throw food away while others are hungry.","zh":"看到有人在別人捱餓時把食物扔掉，我感到非常厭惡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disgust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-edcf27a66a5453a89e3b","word":"dish","forms":["dish"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3bee75fbf1c9877","term":"dish","forms":["dish","dishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盤子、碗等容器","explanation":"指用來盛放或端上食物的器皿，通常像盤子一樣中間略凹，也可以泛指某些碗狀容器。","examples":[{"en":"She placed the warm bread on a clean dish.","zh":"她把熱麵包放在一個乾淨的盤子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sauce came in a small dish.","zh":"醬汁裝在一個小碟子裡端了上來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0aff6a57f4441db","term":"dish","forms":["dish","dishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盤中的食物","explanation":"由“盛食物的盤子”轉指盤子裡所盛的那份食物，重點在一盤或一碗的內容物。","examples":[{"en":"He finished the dish of rice before the soup arrived.","zh":"湯端來之前，他已經吃完了那盤米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was still some fruit in the dish.","zh":"盤子裡還剩一些水果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a982422411d8b95e","term":"dish","forms":["dish","dishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一道菜","explanation":"指一種經過準備、可以作為一餐中一部分的具體食物；這是從“盤中的內容物”進一步發展出的常用義。","examples":[{"en":"This spicy noodle dish is popular with students.","zh":"這道辣面很受學生歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prepared a simple vegetable dish for dinner.","zh":"她為晚餐做了一道簡單的蔬菜菜餚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a51199cca0819ac","term":"dish","forms":["dish","dishes","dishing","dished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝盤、上菜","explanation":"把食物放進盤子或其他餐具中並端上桌，正是名詞 dish“盤子”義的直接動詞化。","examples":[{"en":"She dished the soup into four bowls.","zh":"她把湯分裝到四個碗裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dinner is ready, so I'll dish up the pasta.","zh":"晚飯好了，我來把義大利麵裝盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3734f204b6669b3125d0","word":"dishonest","forms":["dishonest"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5832e8abe177fc9b","term":"dishonest","forms":["dishonest","more dishonest","most dishonest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不誠實的；騙人的；粗劣的","explanation":"指一個人不講真話、隱瞞事實或故意欺騙別人；形容交易、做法或產品時，也可指它不可靠、不光明正大，甚至做工粗劣。核心畫面就是偏離了誠實那條直路。","examples":[{"en":"He was dishonest about how much money he had taken.","zh":"他沒有如實說明自己拿了多少錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop sold dishonest goods that broke after one day.","zh":"那家店賣的商品質量很差，用了一天就壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dishonest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec6d8f8717e6d81bbed4","word":"disk/disc","forms":["disk","disc"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9289dcab3cd59059","term":"disk","forms":["disk","disks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"扁平圓片","explanation":"指薄而平、通常呈圓形的片狀物，重點在它的形狀和扁平外觀；硬幣就是典型例子。","examples":[{"en":"The child cut a disk of paper for the craft project.","zh":"孩子為手工專案剪了一張圓形紙片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A coin is a small metal disk.","zh":"硬幣是一枚小小的金屬圓片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1996394f9fc0ab95","term":"disk","forms":["disk","disks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幾何圓盤","explanation":"在幾何學中，disk不是隻有圓周，而是指圓周裡面的整個平面區域，也就是一個實心圓形區域。","examples":[{"en":"The shaded disk has a radius of three centimeters.","zh":"陰影圓盤的半徑是三釐米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All the points inside the circle form a disk.","zh":"圓內的所有點構成一個圓盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7417101415a18fc","term":"disc","forms":["disc","discs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄圓盤","explanation":"disc最基本的意思是薄而扁的圓形物體，例如金屬、塑膠或其他材料製成的圓盤。","examples":[{"en":"The machine cuts a thin disc of metal.","zh":"這臺機器切出一片薄薄的金屬圓盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A coin is a small metal disc.","zh":"硬幣是一種小型金屬圓盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disc","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2643519037872904","term":"disc","forms":["disc","discs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"椎間盤","explanation":"在解剖和醫學語境中，disc常指位於脊椎骨之間、起緩衝作用的椎間盤。","examples":[{"en":"The scan showed a slipped disc in his lower back.","zh":"掃描顯示他的下背部有椎間盤突出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A damaged disc pressed against a nerve in her back.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disc","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4d14bef7aa0668546bc","word":"dislike","forms":["dislike"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ac86ca6de9087f6","term":"dislike","forms":["dislike","dislikes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不喜歡；反感","explanation":"指心裡對某人、某事的拒絕感或反感，也就是“喜歡”這盞燈沒有亮起來，甚至亮起了拒絕燈。","examples":[{"en":"Her dislike of crowded places is well known.","zh":"她不喜歡擁擠的地方，這是眾所周知的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a strong dislike of unfair rules.","zh":"他非常反感不公平的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dislike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc54c761c5c1a6ff","term":"dislike","forms":["dislike","dislikes","disliking","disliked","dislikest","dislikedst","disliketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不喜歡；反感","explanation":"表示對某人、某事或某種行為有反感，也就是心裡的“拒絕燈”對著這個物件亮了起來。","examples":[{"en":"I dislike waiting in long lines.","zh":"我不喜歡排很長的隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dislikes people who interrupt others.","zh":"她不喜歡打斷別人說話的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dislike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2fa2b5b1eb2d78544dba","word":"dismay","forms":["dismay"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6050d3ac8893894e","term":"dismay","forms":["dismay"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚懼與沮喪","explanation":"指人在面對危險、損失或嚴重麻煩時，勇氣突然下沉，既害怕又感到無力、沮喪。重點不只是受到驚嚇，還包括精神受到打擊、難以振作。","examples":[{"en":"She stared at the broken window in dismay.","zh":"她驚懼而沮喪地盯著那扇破窗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"To my dismay, the last train had already left.","zh":"令我沮喪的是，末班車已經開走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dismay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80845309bd925754","term":"dismay","forms":["dismay","dismays","dismaying","dismayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使驚懼沮喪","explanation":"指某件壞事、危險或令人失望的訊息使人勇氣下沉，變得害怕、悲傷或沒有力氣。它描述的是對方被精神上壓倒的結果，不只是讓對方感到意外。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden increase in rent dismayed many students.","zh":"房租突然上漲使許多學生感到沮喪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was dismayed by how quickly the project failed.","zh":"專案這麼快就失敗了，這讓他既驚懼又沮喪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dismay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5880072b27d45f5845c0","word":"dismiss","forms":["dismiss"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-965d53f0c8521e3a","term":"dismiss","forms":["dismiss","dismisses","dismissing","dismissed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解僱；免職","explanation":"把某人的工作或服務關係結束，讓他不再任職；這就是把人“送走”到不再屬於這個崗位。","examples":[{"en":"The company dismissed her for repeatedly missing deadlines.","zh":"公司因為她屢次錯過截止日期而解僱了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was dismissed from his position last month.","zh":"他上個月被免去了職務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dismiss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6111b6a90bc074c6","term":"dismiss","forms":["dismiss","dismisses","dismissing","dismissed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"讓……離開；解散","explanation":"有權者命令某人或一群人離開，或宣佈一場集合、課程等結束；重點是把人送走。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher dismissed the class ten minutes early.","zh":"老師提前十分鐘讓全班下課了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The troops were dismissed after the ceremony.","zh":"儀式結束後，部隊被解散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dismiss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94e5a52236a4d507","term":"dismiss","forms":["dismiss","dismisses","dismissing","dismissed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"駁回；拒絕受理","explanation":"有權機構把案件、請求或指控推開，不再繼續接受或處理；法院駁回案件就是讓它離開審理程式。","examples":[{"en":"The judge dismissed the case for lack of evidence.","zh":"法官因證據不足而駁回了案件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court dismissed his appeal.","zh":"法院駁回了他的上訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dismiss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4dbaa586691a70d88207","word":"disorder","forms":["disorder"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc2ffd2b92d99b29","term":"disorder","forms":["disorder","disorders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雜亂；無秩序","explanation":"指事物沒有按應有的方式排列或組織，呈現雜亂、失序的狀態；重點是原本應有的秩序不見了。","examples":[{"en":"The papers were left in disorder after the meeting.","zh":"會議結束後，檔案被弄得一片雜亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Opening the suitcase revealed an astonishing disorder of loose clothes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disorder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5db713f0c9c898c","term":"disorder","forms":["disorder","disorders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"功能障礙；疾病","explanation":"在醫學或心理健康語境中，指身體或心理某個系統的正常功能出現持續性問題，因此是一種具體的障礙或疾病，而不是普通的凌亂。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic offers treatment for sleep disorders.","zh":"這家診所提供睡眠障礙治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The specialist diagnosed a rare sleep disorder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disorder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a04b5ec7361d98b","term":"disorder","forms":["disorder","disorders","disordering","disordered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使陷入混亂","explanation":"指主動破壞某個場面或系統原有的組織狀態，使它變得混亂；也就是把原本排好的“佇列”弄亂。","examples":[{"en":"The alarm disordered the carefully planned ceremony.","zh":"警報打亂了精心安排的儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The invasion disordered the country's transport network.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disorder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9879919f35aef0381a7","word":"dispensable","forms":["dispensable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"dispensable","forms":["dispensable"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"非必要的；可省去的","examples":[{"en":"Decorative lights are dispensable when we need to cut costs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The extra paragraph is dispensable because it repeats the introduction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-43f38f92424a702d2b6e","word":"dispense","forms":["dispense"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecd65e439297365d","term":"dispense","forms":["dispense","dispenses","dispensing","dispensed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分發；發放","explanation":"指把某物分給一個人或一群人，強調有秩序地從手裡發出去，而不只是隨意給出。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers dispensed food and water to the crowd.","zh":"志願者向人群分發食物和水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine dispenses tickets automatically.","zh":"這臺機器會自動發放票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2910a4e33a68d031","term":"dispense","forms":["dispense","dispenses","dispensing","dispensed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"配發藥物","explanation":"指藥劑師或藥房按照處方準備並交付藥物，是“按規定分發”在醫療場景中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The pharmacist dispensed the medicine after checking the prescription.","zh":"藥劑師核對處方後配發了藥物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a pharmacist may dispense this medicine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dfbb889cf19bda82ed8d","word":"display","forms":["display"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35c208bbba6495a9","term":"display","forms":["display","displays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"展示；表演","explanation":"指為了讓別人觀看而呈現出來的一場表演、場面或明顯的行為；重點不在某件物品，而在“展示給人看”這個場面。","examples":[{"en":"The dancers put on a spectacular display for the crowd.","zh":"舞者為觀眾獻上了一場精彩的表演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team showed a remarkable display of courage.","zh":"這支隊伍展現出了非凡的勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/display","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ca23c696d098a55","term":"display","forms":["display","displays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子螢幕","explanation":"指手機、電腦、儀器等裝置上顯示文字、影象或資料的螢幕；這是“把資訊展開給人看”的具體裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The phone's display is difficult to read in bright sunlight.","zh":"陽光很強時，這部手機的螢幕很難看清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The display flashes red when the battery runs low.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/display","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9428b1f6744e776e","term":"display","forms":["display","displays","displaying","displayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"展示；顯露","explanation":"指有意或明顯地把某種物品、情緒、品質、技能或行為呈現出來，讓別人注意到；就是把帷幕後面的東西展開給人看。","examples":[{"en":"She displayed great patience while answering the questions.","zh":"她在回答問題時表現出了極大的耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displays paintings by young artists.","zh":"這家博物館展出年輕藝術家的畫作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/display","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75b5da28aed80ed02132","word":"disposable","forms":["disposable"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-564449f579e27e03","term":"disposable","forms":["disposable","more disposable","most disposable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"一次性使用的","explanation":"指產品從設計上就是用完後丟棄，而不是拿來反覆使用、補充內容或修理；紙杯、口罩和某些剃鬚刀都可以這樣描述。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic keeps disposable masks ליד the entrance for visitors.","zh":"診所在入口處放著供訪客使用的一次性口罩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought disposable plates for the picnic.","zh":"我們為野餐買了一次性餐盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disposable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae27930ce4d7bb6d","term":"disposable","forms":["disposable","more disposable","most disposable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可支配的","explanation":"指收入、資金或時間等在滿足必要開支後，可以由個人自行決定怎樣使用；這裡不是“用完就扔”，而是“可以自由安排”。","examples":[{"en":"With less disposable income this year, we are eating out less often.","zh":"今年可支配收入變少後，我們外出就餐的次數減少了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rising rents leave families with less disposable income.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disposable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f0724ffee1368766c72","word":"disposal","forms":["disposal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4676f5f1a4432248","term":"disposal","forms":["disposal","disposals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"處理；清除","explanation":"指把不需要的東西、廢物或危險物品處理掉。這是“把東西放到它最終去處”的最常見延伸，重點是清除或妥善處理，而不是單純移動。","examples":[{"en":"The safe disposal of old batteries is important.","zh":"妥善處理舊電池很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company pays for the disposal of medical waste.","zh":"這家公司負責支付醫療廢物的處理費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disposal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31a3277f8ac17cf4","term":"disposal","forms":["disposal","disposals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可支配使用權","explanation":"表示某人有權使用、安排或調動某物或某人；最常見的畫面是資源已經“放在你手邊，任你支配”。它不是“被處理掉”，而是“可供你使用”。","examples":[{"en":"Our technical team is at your disposal.","zh":"我們的技術團隊隨時聽候你的調遣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You have the whole afternoon at your disposal.","zh":"整個下午的時間都由你支配。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disposal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09d3036c1462ad51929f","word":"dispose","forms":["dispose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bea84b8000b2863f","term":"dispose","forms":["dispose","disposes","disposing","disposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處理掉；清除","explanation":"把不再需要的東西送走、丟棄或以適當方式處理掉，重點是讓它離開當前的佔有或使用範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Please dispose of the empty bottles in the recycling bin.","zh":"請把空瓶子放進回收箱處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company must dispose of the chemical waste safely.","zh":"這家公司必須安全處理化學廢物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-102f39750eb27ad0","term":"dispose","forms":["dispose","disposes","disposing","disposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使傾向於；傾向於","explanation":"表示心態或性格被引向某種態度或行動，例如傾向於謹慎、樂觀或接受某個建議。","examples":[{"en":"After hearing both sides, she was disposed to forgive him.","zh":"聽完雙方的說法後，她傾向於原諒他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His kindness disposed me to trust him.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-caea47fa084a8512bbe1","word":"dispute","forms":["dispute"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-974f87039918d596","term":"dispute","forms":["dispute","disputes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭議；爭端","explanation":"指雙方在某件事上意見不一致，因而產生需要解決的爭議或爭端，常常涉及權利、責任、金錢或安排。","examples":[{"en":"The two companies are in a dispute over the delivery date.","zh":"兩家公司因交貨日期發生了爭議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dispute was settled without going to court.","zh":"這場爭端沒有經過訴訟就解決了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b0ae8e455009a9b","term":"dispute","forms":["dispute","disputes","disputing","disputed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與人爭辯","explanation":"指和另一個人或一方針鋒相對地爭論，反駁對方的觀點；核心是人與人之間的言語交鋒。","examples":[{"en":"She often disputes with her brother about how to run the shop.","zh":"她經常因為如何經營這家店而和哥哥爭辯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They disputed with the neighbors about the boundary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1d6aee934e3cf23","term":"dispute","forms":["dispute","disputes","disputing","disputed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"就某事爭論；討論正反意見","explanation":"指把一個問題拿出來討論，分別提出贊成和反對的理由；重點在對問題本身進行辯論。","examples":[{"en":"The committee disputed whether the plan was safe enough to approve.","zh":"委員會就這項計劃是否足夠安全、能否批准展開了爭論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scholars disputed whether the letter was authentic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dispute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bee0164d53b0209abcb2","word":"disrupt","forms":["disrupt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cbf4904ffc4235a","term":"disrupt","forms":["disrupt","disrupts","disrupting","disrupted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打亂；擾亂","explanation":"指把原本有秩序的活動或局面攪亂，使人無法按原計劃進行；重點是秩序被打散，而不一定完全停止。","examples":[{"en":"A group of protesters disrupted the meeting.","zh":"一群抗議者擾亂了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The loud alarm disrupted everyone’s concentration.","zh":"刺耳的警報聲打亂了所有人的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50e76e6794fe7b25","term":"disrupt","forms":["disrupt","disrupts","disrupting","disrupted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使中斷；妨礙","explanation":"指正在進行的工作、服務或程序被迫停頓、延誤或無法順利繼續，是“把執行中的東西拆開”的進一步表現。","examples":[{"en":"Train services were disrupted by heavy snow.","zh":"大雪導致列車服務中斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A burst water main disrupted the morning traffic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d736c1fff71027df1d49","word":"dissent","forms":["dissent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-290a66aa21079b0d","term":"dissent","forms":["dissent","dissents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反對意見；異議","explanation":"指不接受某個政黨、政府、宗教或其他組織的思想、教義、決定等。它強調從被要求接受的立場中站出來表示反對。","examples":[{"en":"The government has tried to silence political dissent.","zh":"政府試圖壓制政治異議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Religious dissent led to the formation of a new group.","zh":"宗教上的異議導致了一個新團體的成立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dissent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-524e94dfcb4c4965","term":"dissent","forms":["dissent","dissents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對權威的異議","explanation":"指某人不贊成掌權者、機構或多數人的看法，或者拒絕按照他們的意見行事。核心畫面是從大家認定的答案旁邊站出來，明確表示“我不同意”。","examples":[{"en":"She was praised for her courage in expressing dissent.","zh":"她因勇於表達異議而受到稱讚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dissent from the committee’s decision was not tolerated.","zh":"委員會不容許有人反對這一決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dissent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8364d8645a7cd75ee0f3","word":"dissolve","forms":["dissolve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"dissolve","forms":["dissolve"],"pos":"v.","zh":"溶解；使溶解","examples":[{"en":"Dissolve the salt in a little warm water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Sugar will dissolve more quickly if you stir the tea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"dissolve","forms":["dissolve"],"pos":"v.","zh":"解散；終止組織或法律關係","examples":[{"en":"The board voted to dissolve the partnership.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The court has the power to dissolve the marriage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-3","term":"dissolve","forms":["dissolve"],"pos":"v.","zh":"逐漸消失；消除","examples":[{"en":"A friendly conversation can dissolve tension between neighbors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"His anger began to dissolve when he heard her explanation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-63e6ce93e1bcb5122b14","word":"distance","forms":["distance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a929107f0c092ad","term":"distance","forms":["distance","distances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空間距離","explanation":"指兩個地點、物體或點之間相隔的空間長度，也就是空間上“站開一點”有多遠。","examples":[{"en":"What is the distance between the two stations?","zh":"這兩個車站之間的距離是多少？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked a short distance along the river.","zh":"我們沿著河邊走了一小段路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91e9eb0536f005ff","term":"distance","forms":["distance","distances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遙遠；遠離","explanation":"指處於遠方、與某物相隔很遠的狀態，強調空間上真正“站開一點”的程度，而不只是計算出來的長度。","examples":[{"en":"The guide asked us to watch the wild animals from a safe distance.","zh":"導遊要求我們從安全距離觀察野生動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At a distance, the old building looked almost new.","zh":"從遠處看，那座老建築幾乎像新的一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01943b7e9dff74f6","term":"distance","forms":["distance","distances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關係疏遠","explanation":"指人與人不再親近、友好或親密的狀態，也可指原本親近的人後來彼此疏遠；就是關係上“站遠一點”。","examples":[{"en":"The long separation created distance between the sisters.","zh":"長期分離使姐妹倆之間產生了隔閡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt a growing distance between himself and his old friends.","zh":"他感到自己和老朋友之間的隔閡越來越深。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c5777c1c66d4e25a037","word":"distant","forms":["distant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6770c5ff8268b9f4","term":"distant","forms":["distant","more distant","most distant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遙遠的；相隔很遠的","explanation":"指在空間、時間、親屬關係或心理聯結上隔得很遠。它的核心不是單純“看不見”，而是強調兩者之間存在明顯距離，因此 distant relative 是“遠親”，distant look 則表示心思像飄到了別處。","examples":[{"en":"We could hear a distant train whistle late at night.","zh":"深夜裡，我們能聽見遠處火車的汽笛聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She discovered that the new neighbor was a distant relative.","zh":"她發現新鄰居竟是自己的遠親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-357579a410cfc91e","term":"distant","forms":["distant","more distant","most distant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冷淡疏遠的","explanation":"形容一個人不願親近他人，也不太表達真實感情，像主動在彼此之間拉開了一段心理距離。它常描述一段關係中的態度變化，而不只是這個人的外貌或所在位置。","examples":[{"en":"After the disagreement, he became distant toward his sister.","zh":"爭執之後，他對姐姐變得很冷淡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became distant after their argument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-54c9e847ed79c5c2d4a4","word":"distinct","forms":["distinct"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04edfbd44259d3b6","term":"distinct","forms":["distinct","distincter","more distinct","distinctest","most distinct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清楚可辨","explanation":"指聲音、形狀、氣味等很清楚，能夠從背景中被辨認出來；核心畫面就是輪廓分明、不會混在一起。","examples":[{"en":"Her voice was distinct despite the noise outside.","zh":"儘管外面很吵，她的聲音仍然清晰可辨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A distinct outline appeared in the fog.","zh":"霧中出現了一個清晰的輪廓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fa7d40eeddb1f6c","term":"distinct","forms":["distinct","distincter","more distinct","distinctest","most distinct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與……不同","explanation":"表示兩個或幾組事物有明確差別，彼此不是同一種；這是“界線清楚、分得開”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"This kind of tea is distinct from ordinary black tea.","zh":"這種茶不同於普通紅茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two problems are distinct from each other.","zh":"這兩個問題彼此不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b72f4a8521c34d14f2ff","word":"distinction","forms":["distinction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdcca20c26cecf3b","term":"distinction","forms":["distinction","distinctions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"區別；區分開的界線","explanation":"指把兩個或多個事物分開來看的區別，或這種區別本身。重點不是它們完全不同，而是指出某個特徵，使它們能夠被辨認和區分。","examples":[{"en":"There is an important distinction between being busy and being productive.","zh":"忙碌和高效之間有一個重要區別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report makes a clear distinction between fact and opinion.","zh":"這份報告清楚地區分了事實和觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-402b2affe6e2c47f","term":"distinction","forms":["distinction","distinctions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辨別；區分的行為","explanation":"指主動辨認事物之間不同之處的過程或做法。可以把它理解為“畫出那條界線”的動作，而不是界線本身。","examples":[{"en":"We need to draw a distinction between honest mistakes and deliberate lies.","zh":"我們需要區分誠實的錯誤和故意的謊言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The distinction between observation and interpretation requires care.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ac76c88949b07226004","word":"distinctive","forms":["distinctive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1aa5a0958d1161c","term":"distinctive","forms":["distinctive","more distinctive","most distinctive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有辨識度的","explanation":"表示某種設計、外觀或特徵很醒目，能幫助人把物件和其他物件區分開；重點是“容易認出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The shop is easy to recognize because of its distinctive red sign.","zh":"這家店因為醒目的紅色招牌而很容易辨認。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The watch has a distinctive design that sets it apart from cheaper models.","zh":"這塊手錶的設計很有辨識度，能把它和更便宜的型號區別開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinctive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7898fd5e0262c5b9","term":"distinctive","forms":["distinctive","more distinctive","most distinctive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"典型鮮明的","explanation":"表示某種特徵很能代表某人、某物或某群體，讓人一聽、一看就聯想到它；它是“能區分”進一步形成的典型標誌。","examples":[{"en":"Her distinctive laugh filled the room.","zh":"她那獨特的笑聲充滿了整個房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bird has a distinctive white throat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinctive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39d5ef92ac20ece1c585","word":"distinguish","forms":["distinguish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d474bab523953361","term":"distinguish","forms":["distinguish","distinguishes","distinguishing","distinguished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辨別差異","explanation":"指根據特徵認出某人或某物與其他物件的不同，就像在相似事物之間畫出界線。這是 distinguish 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The two species are difficult to distinguish from each other.","zh":"這兩個物種很難彼此區分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you distinguish fact from opinion in this article?","zh":"你能分辨出這篇文章中的事實和觀點嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinguish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64d82641ae4592e9","term":"distinguish","forms":["distinguish","distinguishes","distinguishing","distinguished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使自己突出","explanation":"指某人憑藉勇氣、能力或成就表現得特別突出，從眾人中脫穎而出；字面上像是把自己清楚地標記出來。","examples":[{"en":"She distinguished herself by remaining calm during the crisis.","zh":"她在危機中始終保持鎮定，表現得十分突出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She distinguished herself through her meticulous fieldwork.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinguish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f71c113b389fd3ddf977","word":"distinguished","forms":["distinguished"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40966bb4cf117b09","term":"distinguished","forms":["distinguished","more distinguished","most distinguished"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傑出的；有聲望的","explanation":"指某人因長期成就、貢獻或地位而受到尊重，在群體中顯得特別突出。它強調“被認可的傑出”，不只是能力不錯。","examples":[{"en":"The award honored several distinguished researchers.","zh":"這項獎項表彰了幾位傑出的研究人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a distinguished author with decades of experience.","zh":"她是一位經驗數十年的知名作家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinguished","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8d4eb11085f44fb","term":"distinguished","forms":["distinguished","more distinguished","most distinguished"],"pos":"adj","zh":"莊重體面的","explanation":"指一個人的外表、氣質或舉止顯得端莊、穩重而有分量，讓人感到體面和值得尊敬。這裡不一定表示這個人真的有很高成就，重點在給人的整體印象。","examples":[{"en":"An elderly gentleman with a distinguished air welcomed us at the door.","zh":"一位氣質莊重的老先生在門口迎接了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The distinguished gentleman bowed before taking his seat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distinguished","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f6457b362b766c70011","word":"distract","forms":["distract"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21e083a4bdda73bf","term":"distract","forms":["distract","distracts","distracting","distracted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分散注意力","explanation":"把人的注意力從正在關注的事情上拉開，使他轉而看、聽或想別的東西。這是現代英語中最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please turn off your phone so it doesn't distract you from your work.","zh":"請關掉手機，免得它讓你無法專心工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The loud music distracted everyone from the speaker.","zh":"吵鬧的音樂分散了大家對演講者的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e3dad469b92dd33a4d4","word":"distraction","forms":["distraction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b099bdac00a7c115","term":"distraction","forms":["distraction","distractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讓人分心的事物","explanation":"指把人的注意力從原來的事情上引開的物件、活動或情況。它可以是具體的人或事，也可以是為了暫時轉移注意力而做的事情。","examples":[{"en":"My phone is a constant distraction from my work.","zh":"手機總是讓我無法專心工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A short walk can be a welcome distraction from the pain.","zh":"短暫散步可以讓人暫時從疼痛中分心，感覺好一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a62ff034e02defa3","term":"distraction","forms":["distraction","distractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分心的過程或狀態","explanation":"指注意力被帶離當前任務的過程，或這種分心現象本身。重點不在某一個干擾物，而在注意力沒有保持在應做的事情上。","examples":[{"en":"The students worked better after the teacher removed sources of distraction.","zh":"老師移除分心的因素後，學生們學習得更好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Constant interruptions left him in a state of distraction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16e601ed6c846b43154e","word":"distress","forms":["distress"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf83af9967d45f77","term":"distress","forms":["distress","distresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈的痛苦或焦慮","explanation":"指身體或情緒上強烈而急迫的難受、痛苦或驚慌，通常比一般的不舒服或擔心更嚴重。","examples":[{"en":"She was in obvious distress after hearing the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息後，她顯然十分痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child cried out in distress.","zh":"孩子因痛苦而哭喊起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-417f76c4a9a137f6","term":"distress","forms":["distress","distresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"危急狀態","explanation":"指人、船隻或其他物件處在嚴重危險中，需要立即得到幫助；它強調“被逼到危險邊緣”。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers were in distress and needed to be rescued before dark.","zh":"這些徒步者處於危急中，需要在天黑前獲救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain sent a distress signal as water poured in.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-708396193ecad14b","term":"distress","forms":["distress","distresses","distressing","distressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使人痛苦或焦慮","explanation":"指某件事給某人造成強烈的情緒痛苦、焦慮或不安，即把對方“拉緊、逼得難受”。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden change deeply distressed her.","zh":"這次突然的變化讓她深感痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was distressed by the loss of his job.","zh":"失去工作讓他非常難受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2ef5060da5b83a9ca06","word":"distribute","forms":["distribute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb1c4b6bc5f01d46","term":"distribute","forms":["distribute","distributes","distributing","distributed","distributest","distributedst","distributeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分發；分配","explanation":"把一個整體分成若干份，再分別給不同的人或群體。這是 distribute 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers distributed blankets among the families.","zh":"志願者把毯子分發給各個家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please distribute the worksheets to the students.","zh":"請把練習紙發給學生們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distribute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1a334b20551051a","term":"distribute","forms":["distribute","distributes","distributing","distributed","distributest","distributedst","distributeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發放；傳遞","explanation":"把傳單、資料、物品等逐一送到許多人手中或許多地點。它和“分配”相近，但更突出實際遞送、發放的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Students distributed flyers outside the station.","zh":"學生們在車站外發放傳單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity distributes blankets to families without heating.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distribute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93354845030274cd4bf1","word":"distribution","forms":["distribution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b60cf108496787c","term":"distribution","forms":["distribution","distributions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分配；分佈","explanation":"指把東西分給不同的人或地點的行為，也指東西已經被分開的狀態。重點是“一個整體被拆開並鋪到各處”。","examples":[{"en":"The distribution of food began early in the morning.","zh":"食物的分發一大早就開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map shows the distribution of rainfall across the country.","zh":"這張地圖顯示了全國各地的降雨分佈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distribution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6997d95729f8d3a","term":"distribution","forms":["distribution","distributions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商品流通","explanation":"在商業中，指商品從生產者經過儲存、運輸和銷售，最終到達消費者的整套過程；也可指覆蓋這些環節的渠道。","examples":[{"en":"The company is expanding its distribution network in Asia.","zh":"這家公司正在擴大其在亞洲的分銷網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firm handles distribution to supermarkets nationwide.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distribution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c7b58b2dfd058d8","term":"distribution","forms":["distribution","distributions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分佈範圍和頻率","explanation":"指某種事物在不同地點、群體或時間中出現得多不多、廣不廣，即它的分佈情況。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying the distribution of the species across the island.","zh":"科學家正在研究這種物種在島上的分佈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map shows the distribution of wolves across Europe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distribution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c4483cece55839512ff","word":"district","forms":["district"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5014ee5db7fe0407","term":"district","forms":["district","districts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行政區；轄區","explanation":"district 是被政府或其他管理機構劃定出來的區域，通常有明確邊界和管理職能。它可以是城市、郡或其他更大區域中的一個分割槽。","examples":[{"en":"The new library serves several districts.","zh":"這座新圖書館為幾個行政區提供服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works in the central district.","zh":"她在中心區工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/district","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-deef09bea24ba811","term":"district","forms":["district","districts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有共同特徵的地區","explanation":"district 不一定是行政單位，也可以是因湖泊、山地、產業或其他明顯特徵而被看作一個整體的地區；重點是“這片地方有共同特點”。","examples":[{"en":"The historic district is full of small bookstores.","zh":"這片歷史街區有許多小書店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater district comes alive after sunset.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/district","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2fba0a7b100e7a96cb72","word":"disturb","forms":["disturb"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84725b956057dfb4","term":"disturb","forms":["disturb","disturbs","disturbing","disturbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打擾；擾亂平靜狀態","explanation":"使原本安靜、穩定或連續的狀態不再平穩，例如打斷休息、考試時的專注，或攪亂液體的平靜流動。核心畫面是把一條順暢的流攪亂。","examples":[{"en":"The noisy ventilation disturbed me during the exam.","zh":"考試時，嘈雜的通風裝置打擾了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please do not disturb the water while the paint settles.","zh":"油漆沉澱時，請不要攪動這桶水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disturb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fad14393e97ea1cd","term":"disturb","forms":["disturb","disturbs","disturbing","disturbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使不安；使困擾","explanation":"使人產生強烈的不適、擔憂、困惑或情緒上的不安，好像內心原本平穩的狀態被攪亂了。這個義項常用於令人不安的訊息、行為或想法。","examples":[{"en":"I was deeply disturbed by the cruelty in the video.","zh":"影片中的殘酷場面讓我深感不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children's prolonged silence began to disturb her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disturb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbc373091fe0f09a5ebb","word":"disturbance","forms":["disturbance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-83cab58c9ba3e42b","term":"disturbance","forms":["disturbance","disturbances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擾動；受干擾","explanation":"指打亂原本平靜、穩定或正常狀態的行為，或這種被打亂的情況，重點在“發生了擾動”。","examples":[{"en":"The construction work caused a major disturbance to the neighborhood.","zh":"施工給附近社群造成了很大的干擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Any disturbance of the peace will be reported to the police.","zh":"任何擾亂治安的行為都會被報告給警方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disturbance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f50756415f29c35","term":"disturbance","forms":["disturbance","disturbances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喧鬧；騷亂","explanation":"指引起喧譁、混亂或中斷的公開騷動，是“水面被劇烈攪動”這一形象在公共場合中的表現。","examples":[{"en":"The customer was asked to leave after causing a disturbance in the restaurant.","zh":"那名顧客在餐館裡製造騷亂後被要求離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A disturbance outside interrupted the ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disturbance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ac8dad60a3b83251ad5","word":"ditch","forms":["ditch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df9d7b20fb447bc3","term":"ditch","forms":["ditch","ditches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溝渠；壕溝","explanation":"指地面上狹長而較淺的凹溝，通常用來排水、灌溉或分隔土地；它就是記憶中那條把土地切開的溝。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer dug a ditch along the edge of the field.","zh":"農夫沿著田邊挖了一條溝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rainwater flowed quickly into the drainage ditch.","zh":"雨水很快流進了排水溝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ditch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ad4848b3268d7ac","term":"ditch","forms":["ditch","ditches","ditching","ditched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拋棄；甩掉","explanation":"指把某物、某人或某件事丟到一邊，不再繼續使用或處理，就像把它扔進溝裡一樣。這個義項也常表示放棄原來的安排。","examples":[{"en":"We ditched the old plan and started again.","zh":"我們放棄了原來的計劃，重新開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ditched her heavy coat at the station.","zh":"她在車站把厚外套甩在一邊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ditch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f8897661f150233e7e2","word":"dive","forms":["dive"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d16fc7c0250d6155","term":"dive","forms":["dive","dives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳水；扎入水中","explanation":"指頭朝下跳入水中的動作，是“向下扎入”這一核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She took a deep breath before making the dive.","zh":"她在跳水前深深吸了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dived from the rocks into clear water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd92e8d67c4a1dcc","term":"dive","forms":["dive","dives","diving","dived","dove","doven","diven","divest","divedst","diveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"潛入水下","explanation":"表示人進入水中並在水下游動，是“向下扎入”畫面的基本動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"He dived into the water to save the child.","zh":"他潛入水中去救那個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The divers dived beneath the anchored boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fca8bb2de0943946","term":"dive","forms":["dive","dives","diving","dived","dove","doven","diven","divest","divedst","diveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"頭朝下跳入水中","explanation":"強調以頭朝下的姿勢跳進水裡，比一般的進入水中更突出動作姿態。","examples":[{"en":"The children dived into the pool one after another.","zh":"孩子們一個接一個地頭朝下跳進游泳池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He dived from the rock into the deep pool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-664f07b130bf0942","term":"dive","forms":["dive","dives","diving","dived","dove","doven","diven","divest","divedst","diveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"熱情投入","explanation":"把身體扎入某處的動作借來表示全身心投入工作、任務或新活動，常有馬上行動、不猶豫的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"After a short break, she dived into the new project.","zh":"短暫休息後，她馬上投入了新專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come on in and dive right in!","zh":"來吧，馬上加入進來！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-773267c0c4d894d4","term":"dive","forms":["dive","dives","diving","dived","dove","doven","diven","divest","divedst","diveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"深入探究；全力投入","explanation":"表示深入一個問題、主題、工作或領域，像整個人扎進去一樣認真探索；這是 dive into 抽象用法的核心。","examples":[{"en":"Let's dive into the main problem before lunch.","zh":"我們午飯前深入研究一下主要問題吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I dived into the report as soon as I got it.","zh":"我一拿到報告就認真研究起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db2a30692ef93bfc4ce2","word":"diverse","forms":["diverse"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-977d132a3f515a23","term":"diverse","forms":["diverse","more diverse","most diverse"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多種多樣的","explanation":"指一個整體由許多不同型別、成分或特點組成，重點是內部的多樣性，而不只是數量多。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a diverse collection of modern art.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了多種多樣的現代藝術品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course attracts students with diverse interests.","zh":"這門課程吸引了興趣各不相同的學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0ea872245a5057b","term":"diverse","forms":["diverse","more diverse","most diverse"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不同的；不相似的","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物彼此不一樣、各自有明顯區別；這是“多樣”這一核心概念中最直接的比較用法。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used diverse methods to study the problem.","zh":"研究人員採用了各不相同的方法來研究這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two paintings are diverse in style and mood.","zh":"這兩幅畫在風格和情緒上各不相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d78ea052554398dd33a3","word":"diversify","forms":["diversify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92d2d86193babeae","term":"diversify","forms":["diversify","diversifies","diversifying","diversified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……更多樣","explanation":"指主動改變某項活動、某類產品或某個群體的構成，讓其中出現更多不同型別、特點或方向，從而不再單一。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is trying to diversify its exhibitions by featuring more local artists.","zh":"這家博物館正嘗試透過展出更多本地藝術家的作品來豐富展覽的多樣性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library diversified its collection with more translated novels.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diversify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3726f4e1b55ef216","term":"diversify","forms":["diversify","diversifies","diversifying","diversified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得更多樣","explanation":"指一個活動、組織或事物的範圍和構成逐漸出現更多差異，不再集中於單一型別；也可以帶賓語表示讓它朝多個方向發展。","examples":[{"en":"Over time, the festival diversified and attracted people with different interests.","zh":"隨著時間推移，這個節慶活動變得更加多樣，吸引了興趣各不相同的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The local economy diversified as tourism expanded.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diversify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cddf86d3bca49414da1a","word":"diversion","forms":["diversion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebfd0ea8ace24c42","term":"diversion","forms":["diversion","diversions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轉移注意力的行動","explanation":"指故意把別人對真正目標、威脅或行動的注意力引開，使對方關注另一個方向。它可以是軍事上的佯攻，也可以是政治或日常行動中的掩護手段。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers created a diversion while the rescue team entered the building.","zh":"士兵們製造佯動，救援隊則趁機進入大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The false report was intended as a diversion.","zh":"這份假報告是為了轉移注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diversion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad7111135ac7cf8d","term":"diversion","forms":["diversion","diversions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消遣；娛樂活動","explanation":"指把自己的注意力從煩惱或日常事務上引開的活動，也就是用來放鬆和娛樂的愛好或消遣。這個意思和“轉移注意力”的核心概念相同，只是被引開的物件變成了自己的思緒。","examples":[{"en":"Gardening is a welcome diversion after a stressful week.","zh":"忙碌又有壓力的一週後，園藝是很好的消遣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found diversion in reading mystery novels.","zh":"她從閱讀推理小說中得到消遣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diversion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f277b1934a3bf105a7d2","word":"diversity","forms":["diversity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82601202ba432a6f","term":"diversity","forms":["diversity","diversities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"差異；不相同","explanation":"指人或事物之間存在明顯不同的狀態，重點在於彼此不一樣，而不一定強調種類很多。","examples":[{"en":"The diversity of opinions made the discussion more interesting.","zh":"觀點的多樣性讓討論更加有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum reflects the cultural diversity of the city.","zh":"這座博物館體現了這座城市的文化多樣性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diversity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bac3018925385a7c","term":"diversity","forms":["diversity","diversities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"多種型別；豐富多樣","explanation":"指一個範圍內包含許多不同的型別、例子或風格；這裡的重點從“彼此不同”擴充套件到“種類豐富”。","examples":[{"en":"The festival offers a diversity of music from around the world.","zh":"這個節日提供來自世界各地的多種音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rainforest supports an astonishing diversity of insects.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diversity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3edab1ff7eb6bf33f108","word":"divert","forms":["divert"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01b7de00233568f0","term":"divert","forms":["divert","diverts","diverting","diverted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改道；使轉向","explanation":"指把水流、車輛、交通或其他事物從原來的路線引到另一條路上，也就是讓它“離開原道”。","examples":[{"en":"The workers diverted the stream away from the road.","zh":"工人把溪流引離了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police diverted traffic to a side street.","zh":"警察把車輛引到了一條支路上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2911cd66132b1fd","term":"divert","forms":["divert","diverts","diverting","diverted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分散注意力","explanation":"指把人的注意力從正在關注的目標上帶開；注意力原本在一處，被轉到了別處。","examples":[{"en":"Don't let the noise divert your attention from the presentation.","zh":"別讓噪音分散你對演講的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She asked a quick question to divert him from the real issue.","zh":"她問了一個簡短的問題，想把他對真正問題的注意力引開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-895479bfaa22d9f56567","word":"divide","forms":["divide"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63a242e903b7455d","term":"divide","forms":["divide","divides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分界；隔開兩邊的東西","explanation":"指把兩個區域、群體或部分隔開的界線、障礙或事物。它可以是真實的牆、邊界，也可以是抽象的分隔。","examples":[{"en":"The river forms a natural divide between the two villages.","zh":"這條河成了兩個村莊之間的天然分界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow road marks the divide between the old town and the new one.","zh":"一條狹窄的道路標出了老城區和新城區之間的分界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-186f7bc35b1c77c5","term":"divide","forms":["divide","divides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分歧；鴻溝","explanation":"指人與人、群體與群體之間在感情、利益或觀點上的距離。它把抽象的分歧想象成一道難以跨越的鴻溝。","examples":[{"en":"There is a growing divide between the two generations.","zh":"這兩代人之間的分歧越來越大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project helped bridge the divide between the communities.","zh":"這個專案幫助彌合了兩個社群之間的鴻溝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0b76233c780ed36","term":"divide","forms":["divide","divides","dividing","divided","dividest","dividedst","divideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……分開","explanation":"把一個整體、區域或物件切分成兩個或更多部分，也可指某物把其他東西隔開。這是divide最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The fence divides the garden into two sections.","zh":"籬笆把花園分成了兩部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wall divides the kitchen from the dining room.","zh":"一面牆把廚房和餐廳隔開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1868627761fa3001","term":"divide","forms":["divide","divides","dividing","divided","dividest","dividedst","divideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分配；分攤","explanation":"把食物、錢、工作或其他東西分成幾份，分給不同的人或承擔者。它強調公平或有計劃地把整體分開。","examples":[{"en":"We divided the bill equally among the four of us.","zh":"我們四個人平攤了賬單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please divide the cake into eight pieces.","zh":"請把蛋糕分成八塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7b2b487f74c42f4","term":"divide","forms":["divide","divides","dividing","divided","dividest","dividedst","divideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"除；用……除","explanation":"在數學中表示把一個數按另一個數分成若干等份，求商。例如divide 6 by 3就是用3除6，結果是2。","examples":[{"en":"Divide 24 by 6 to get 4.","zh":"用6除24，結果是4。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher asked us to divide 81 by 9.","zh":"老師讓我們用9除81。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7539a338b962fd3ba51","word":"dividend","forms":["dividend"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d14d5bffd4f8412","term":"dividend","forms":["dividend","dividends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"股息；紅利","explanation":"公司把利潤的一部分按持股情況分給股東，這筆定期或不定期發放的錢叫 dividend。它強調的是公司分配給股東的收益，不是股票本身的價格。","examples":[{"en":"The company paid a dividend to its shareholders.","zh":"這家公司向股東發放了股息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company paid shareholders a modest dividend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dividend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87fdc1195ed5efbf","term":"dividend","forms":["dividend","dividends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被除數","explanation":"在除法中，dividend 是被另一個數分開的數。例如在 42 ÷ 3 中，42 是 dividend，3 是除數。它體現了“把一份數值分開計算”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"In 84 ÷ 7, 84 is the dividend.","zh":"在 84 除以 7 中，84 是被除數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In twelve divided by three, twelve is the dividend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dividend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8647ed424daa9acffd1f","word":"divine","forms":["divine"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2326c63770373177","term":"divine","forms":["divine","more divine","most divine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"神的；與神有關的","explanation":"指屬於神、來自神，或與神和宗教信仰直接有關的事物；這是理解其他義項的起點。","examples":[{"en":"Many people believe that the temple has divine protection.","zh":"許多人相信這座寺廟受到神的庇佑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shrine was believed to possess divine protection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c42dfe89de53239","term":"divine","forms":["divine","more divine","most divine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"神聖的；如神一般的","explanation":"強調某人或某物具有神聖、永恆或近乎神一般的性質，不一定只是在說它屬於某位具體的神。","examples":[{"en":"The painting shows the saint surrounded by divine light.","zh":"這幅畫描繪了聖徒被神聖的光芒環繞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shrine was believed to possess divine protection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-990b23e81455c9812dfd","word":"division","forms":["division"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f7396b9c1806b05","term":"division","forms":["division","divisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劃分；分開","explanation":"指把一個整體分成幾個部分的動作或過程，重點在“分開”本身。","examples":[{"en":"The division of the project into three stages made it easier to manage.","zh":"把專案分成三個階段後，管理起來更容易了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The division of the land caused a long dispute.","zh":"土地的劃分引發了長期爭議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/division","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7aea3629630adc1f","term":"division","forms":["division","divisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分開的部分；分割槽","explanation":"指整體被分開後形成的某一個部分，或這些部分中的一個。它和“劃分”是同一幅圖景的另一面：前者看動作，後者看結果。","examples":[{"en":"The building is divided into four divisions, each with its own entrance.","zh":"這棟樓分成四個區域，每個區域都有自己的入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country is organized into twelve administrative divisions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/division","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4028526b9f838989","term":"division","forms":["division","divisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分歧；意見不合","explanation":"指人們的觀點被分到彼此對立的兩邊，因而產生的分歧或不和；這裡分開的不是物體，而是立場。","examples":[{"en":"The issue has caused deep divisions within the community.","zh":"這個問題在社群內部造成了嚴重分歧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The debate revealed a division between younger and older voters.","zh":"這場辯論暴露了年輕選民和年長選民之間的分歧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/division","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6b2aa44123280902bcf","word":"divorce","forms":["divorce"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f917170ac34e613","term":"divorce","forms":["divorce","divorces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"離婚；婚姻解除","explanation":"指夫妻透過法律程式解除婚姻關係。它強調正式的法律結果，而不只是感情上的分手。","examples":[{"en":"They decided to get a divorce after years of trying to save the marriage.","zh":"他們努力挽救婚姻多年後，決定離婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She filed for divorce last month.","zh":"她上個月提出了離婚申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divorce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e08a17b863e2eab5","term":"divorce","forms":["divorce","divorces","divorcing","divorced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與某人離婚","explanation":"表示一個人依法結束自己與配偶的婚姻關係，重點是“把配偶從婚姻中分開”。","examples":[{"en":"Maya divorced her husband after discovering the hidden debts.","zh":"瑪雅發現丈夫隱瞞的債務後，與他離婚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She divorced her husband after years of separation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divorce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d810e252392052537915","word":"dizzy","forms":["dizzy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27a96cf3ca8d9242","term":"dizzy","forms":["dizzy","dizzier","dizziest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"頭暈的；眩暈的","explanation":"指人感到周圍或自己的身體像在旋轉，站立不穩、發飄或頭腦發昏，常由突然起身、疲勞等情況引起。","examples":[{"en":"I felt dizzy after standing in the hot room for too long.","zh":"我在悶熱的房間裡站太久後感到頭暈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gets dizzy whenever she rides in the back seat.","zh":"她每次坐在後排都會頭暈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dizzy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c449bec92938f37","term":"dizzy","forms":["dizzy","dizzier","dizziest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人眩暈的","explanation":"指高度、速度或強烈的視覺體驗讓人產生頭暈、發飄的感覺；它把“頭暈”從人的感受轉到了引起這種感受的事物上。","examples":[{"en":"We looked down from a dizzy height and held on to the railing.","zh":"我們從令人眩暈的高處向下看，緊緊抓住欄杆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dizzy height made her grip the railing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dizzy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac0b52a2ae6ef99999bc","word":"do","forms":["do"],"officialPos":"aux./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24ee807d54b7c8ef","term":"do","forms":["do","does","doing","did","done","doest","dost","didst","doeth","doth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"構成疑問句","explanation":"作為助動詞，do 幫助把一般現在時的陳述句變成疑問句，把“把事情落實下來”的支撐作用用於句子結構，而不是表示額外的具體動作。","examples":[{"en":"Do you need any help with this task?","zh":"你需要有人幫你完成這項任務嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do these shoes belong to your brother?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/do","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e81713be22530d3","term":"do","forms":["do","does","doing","did","done","doest","dost","didst","doeth","doth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做；執行","explanation":"do 最基本的實義動詞用法是親自把某件事做出來、執行某項任務，正是“把事情落實下來”的核心記憶點。","examples":[{"en":"I have a few important things to do today.","zh":"我今天有幾件重要的事情要做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you want it done properly, do it yourself.","zh":"如果你想把它做好，就自己來做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/do","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a864ed013d128c9c908c","word":"dock","forms":["dock"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ceb6d4f23e5a4a81","term":"dock","forms":["dock","docks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碼頭","explanation":"dock 是岸邊供船隻停靠、裝貨和卸貨的固定設施，也就是常說的碼頭。","examples":[{"en":"The ferry is waiting at the dock.","zh":"渡船正在碼頭等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers loaded the boxes onto the dock.","zh":"工人把箱子裝到了碼頭上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-392f92a5e4fe6946","term":"dock","forms":["dock","docks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擴充套件塢或充電座","explanation":"在電子裝置中，dock 是用來放置並連線便攜裝置的底座，通常能充電或增加介面和功能。","examples":[{"en":"I left my tablet in the dock to charge.","zh":"我把平板電腦放在擴充套件塢裡充電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This dock adds two extra monitors.","zh":"這個擴充套件塢可以連線兩臺額外的顯示器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cda6e3e5a15de068","term":"dock","forms":["dock","docks","docking","docked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"扣減工資","explanation":"dock wages 或 dock someone’s pay 表示從工資中扣掉一部分錢，正如從整體上截去一小段。","examples":[{"en":"The company docked her pay by $50 for the missed shift.","zh":"公司因她缺勤一次而扣了她50美元工資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His wages were docked for being late.","zh":"他因為遲到而被扣了工資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9eafe93acc732e9d","term":"dock","forms":["dock","docks","docking","docked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"扣某人的工資","explanation":"dock someone 表示扣減某人的工資或報酬，重點放在被扣錢的人身上。","examples":[{"en":"They docked me twenty dollars for returning the equipment late.","zh":"他們因為我晚歸還裝置而扣了我20美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The employer docked his pay for leaving early.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9eca7210e9b78808","term":"dock","forms":["dock","docks","docking","docked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"船隻進港停靠","explanation":"船 dock 表示駛入港口並停靠在碼頭，正是“接到停靠處”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The ferry docked at noon.","zh":"渡船中午進港停靠了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our ship will dock in Boston tonight.","zh":"我們的船今晚將在波士頓停靠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ab67d7500fd6ca8","term":"dock","forms":["dock","docks","docking","docked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使兩個運動物體對接","explanation":"dock 可表示讓兩個正在運動的物體連線起來，例如讓兩艘飛船或兩個航天器完成對接。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot docked the two spacecraft safely.","zh":"駕駛員讓兩艘航天器安全完成了對接。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The supply ship docked with the station.","zh":"補給船與空間站完成了對接。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a49436b8b4557fb9a345","word":"doctor/doc","forms":["doctor","doc"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1cf0ea9af045b45c","term":"doctor","forms":["doctor","doctors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫生","explanation":"指受過訓練並獲准為病人診斷、治療疾病或處理傷病的醫學專業人員。日常說“去看醫生”時，通常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"If you still feel unwell tomorrow, see your doctor.","zh":"如果你明天還是不舒服，就去看醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor listened carefully to my breathing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doctor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4d21616dae87e44","term":"doctor","forms":["doctor","doctors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"博士","explanation":"指獲得博士學位的人，例如哲學博士或神學博士。這裡強調的是學術資格，不一定從事醫學工作。","examples":[{"en":"She became a doctor of philosophy after years of research.","zh":"她經過多年的研究，獲得了哲學博士學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a doctor of medieval history.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doctor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51f880fd3b0017b2","term":"doc","forms":["doc","docs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫生","explanation":"doc是doctor的非正式短稱，指給病人診斷和治療的醫生；它和稱呼用法共享“能提供醫療幫助的人”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"I need to call my doc about these headaches.","zh":"我得給我的醫生打電話，問問這些頭痛的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doc said my ankle would heal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doc","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e22cab44677d02c","term":"doc","forms":["doc","docs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檔案；文件","explanation":"doc是document的非正式短稱，指承載資訊的檔案；在工作和技術語境中，常特指說明操作方法的文件或可作為證據的材料。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the docs before installing the software.","zh":"安裝軟體前，請先閱讀文件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Save the doc before closing your laptop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doc","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6747a6bee7c5008ef84","word":"doctrine","forms":["doctrine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5214d4db12534daa","term":"doctrine","forms":["doctrine","doctrines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體教義或信條","explanation":"指關於宗教、哲學等問題的一條明確而重要的信念或主張，強調它被某個傳統或群體正式接受和教導。","examples":[{"en":"The Trinity is a central doctrine of the church.","zh":"三位一體是該教會的核心教義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The denomination rejected the doctrine of predestination.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doctrine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20f501d1efa2b52f","term":"doctrine","forms":["doctrine","doctrines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成套教義或思想體系","explanation":"指一個宗教、意識形態、思想家、組織或經典所包含的一整套相互關聯的教導；重點從單條信條擴充套件到了完整體系。","examples":[{"en":"Students studied the doctrine of nonviolence in the course.","zh":"學生們在課程中學習了非暴力主義的思想體系。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The group developed a doctrine of nonviolent resistance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doctrine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-43cc23fa52b87b4cc1d0","word":"document","forms":["document"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24699001ad4b56e3","term":"document","forms":["document","documents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式檔案；憑證","explanation":"指原件、官方檔案或其他具有憑證作用的書面材料，用來支援、證明或核實某件事。這是日常和正式場合中最重要的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"The signed document proves that the payment was made.","zh":"這份簽署的檔案證明款項已經支付。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep the original document in a safe place.","zh":"請把原始檔案放在安全的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/document","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c516072ba04d7b21","term":"document","forms":["document","documents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機文件","explanation":"指包含文字內容的計算機檔案，通常可以建立、儲存、編輯或傳送。它把“承載資訊的檔案”這個核心概念延伸到了電子環境中。","examples":[{"en":"I saved the report as a separate document.","zh":"我把這份報告另存成了一個單獨的文件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The document contains several embedded photographs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/document","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d539fc63d44f1cff","term":"document","forms":["document","documents","documenting","documented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"記錄；記載","explanation":"指把過程、事實或變化正式記錄下來，使它以後能夠被檢視、核對或作為證據。這正是“把資訊固定成document”的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The researcher documented every change in the patient's condition.","zh":"研究人員記錄了病人狀況的每一項變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film documents how the village recovered after the storm.","zh":"這部影片記錄了這個村莊在暴風雨後如何恢復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/document","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3708de487b319b4faf2e","word":"documentary","forms":["documentary"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-babb0d1c5e986c20","term":"documentary","forms":["documentary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非虛構的；以事實呈現的","explanation":"表示作品不靠編造情節來講述，而是以現實中的人物、事件或資料為基礎，儘量直接呈現事實；這正是“紀錄片”這一名詞義的核心。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a documentary film about coral reefs.","zh":"我們看了一部關於珊瑚礁的紀錄片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film takes a documentary approach to factory life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/documentary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d245ae0d5bbef4a","term":"documentary","forms":["documentary","documentaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紀錄片；紀錄節目","explanation":"指以真實的社會、政治、科學或歷史主題為物件，透過資料、採訪、現場畫面等方式進行事實性介紹的作品。它就是“以記錄現實為目的的作品”這一核心概念的具體名稱。","examples":[{"en":"She made a documentary about families living near the river.","zh":"她製作了一部關於住在河邊的家庭的紀錄片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary follows migrating birds across three continents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/documentary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-784109ed21a6f7c669ea","word":"dodge","forms":["dodge"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2a8427532b494e6","term":"dodge","forms":["dodge","dodges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"閃避；躲閃","explanation":"指為了避開迎面而來的東西、碰撞或攻擊而突然移動身體。它是動詞“突然閃開”所對應的動作名詞。","examples":[{"en":"With a quick dodge, she avoided the falling box.","zh":"她迅速一閃，躲開了掉下來的箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A quick dodge saved him from the swinging branch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68757302d4d36e6a","term":"dodge","forms":["dodge","dodges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"規避手段；詭計","explanation":"指為了逃避責任、費用或直接回答而採用的辦法，常暗含不誠實或取巧。它仍然保留了“避開某件事”的核心，只是避開的物件變成了責任或規則。","examples":[{"en":"The company used a tax dodge to reduce its bill.","zh":"這家公司用稅務規避手段減少了應繳的稅款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Using a false address was a dodge to avoid tax.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34a5487c5dfb18b6","term":"dodge","forms":["dodge","dodges","dodging","dodged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閃避；躲開","explanation":"指透過突然改變方向或位置，避開迎面而來的物體、人或危險。這個具體動作是整個詞義網路的起點。","examples":[{"en":"He dodged a bicycle on his way home.","zh":"他回家路上閃開了一輛腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The goalkeeper dodged the ball at the last second.","zh":"守門員在最後一刻躲開了球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b839de9fe58731c","term":"dodge","forms":["dodge","dodges","dodging","dodged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迴避；規避","explanation":"指故意不直接面對問題、責任或要求，轉而用含糊回答或其他辦法避開。這裡的“閃開”從身體動作引申到了談話和處理事情。","examples":[{"en":"She dodged my question and changed the subject.","zh":"她迴避了我的問題，把話題岔開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report dodges the main issue.","zh":"這份報告迴避了主要問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd6357efdd966de8c0cb","word":"dog","forms":["dog"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a4d238cb087c57e","term":"dog","forms":["dog","dogs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狗","explanation":"指犬科中的一種哺乳動物，也就是通常飼養在人類身邊的狗。","examples":[{"en":"Our dog waits by the door every morning.","zh":"我們的狗每天早上都在門邊等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dog followed me home from the park.","zh":"一隻狗從公園一路跟著我回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1608dad64802b623","term":"dog","forms":["dog","dogs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人討厭的人","explanation":"俚語且帶貶義地指某個人，常表示這個人令人厭煩、討厭或不受尊重。","examples":[{"en":"That dog kept shouting at everyone in the queue.","zh":"那個討厭鬼一直對排隊的人大喊大叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That selfish dog left us to do all the work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44c3e574dac5455e6749","word":"doll","forms":["doll"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7e30d2d6e3c7b91","term":"doll","forms":["doll","dolls","dollz"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洋娃娃；玩偶","explanation":"doll 是做成小人樣子的玩具，尤其指供兒童玩耍的洋娃娃。這個“精緻的小人兒”形象也是其他許多意義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"The little girl carried her favorite doll everywhere.","zh":"那個小女孩走到哪裡都帶著她最喜歡的洋娃娃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought a doll for the baby.","zh":"我們給寶寶買了一個洋娃娃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-588d2c1d1f23963e1647","word":"dollar","forms":["dollar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ee82c31cc4f3f0e","term":"dollar","forms":["dollar","dollars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"元；美元","explanation":"指美國、加拿大、澳大利亞、紐西蘭、新加坡、香港等地使用的貨幣單位；沒有上下文限定時，英語中尤其常讓人想到美元。","examples":[{"en":"The ticket costs twenty dollars.","zh":"這張票要二十美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Canadian dollar fell slightly today.","zh":"加拿大元今天略有下跌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dollar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f92d6302033e947f","term":"dollar","forms":["dollar","dollars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錢；金錢","explanation":"在較寬泛的用法中，dollar可以不強調具體幣種，而是借“錢”來表示金錢、花費或經濟利益。","examples":[{"en":"Every dollar matters when you are saving for a house.","zh":"攢錢買房時，每一塊錢都很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He puts profit first and worships the dollar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dollar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-532f011ec89ff0e2e1be","word":"dolphin","forms":["dolphin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b42a2d02e4c652af","term":"dolphin","forms":["dolphin","dolphins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海豚","explanation":"海豚是一種生活在水中的肉食性哺乳動物，以聰明、活潑以及有時願意接近人類而聞名。這是 dolphin 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a dolphin swimming beside the boat.","zh":"我們看見一隻海豚在船邊游泳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dolphins followed the fishing boat for several minutes.","zh":"那些海豚跟著漁船遊了幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dolphin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cd75536b7a1074c","term":"dolphin","forms":["dolphin","dolphins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鯕鰍魚","explanation":"在魚類語境中，dolphin 也指鯕鰍魚，即 mahi-mahi 或 dorado；它是魚，不是海豚這種哺乳動物。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves grilled dolphin with rice.","zh":"這家餐館供應配米飯的烤鯕鰍魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fisherman landed a dolphin with brilliant blue-green scales.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dolphin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2ff83860a4dc203988e","word":"domain","forms":["domain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48ef00a4a8ee0255","term":"domain","forms":["domain","domains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領地；管轄範圍","explanation":"指由一個人、組織或政權擁有或控制的地理範圍，重點是這塊地方屬於某個權力主體的“地盤”。","examples":[{"en":"The king ruled his domain harshly.","zh":"國王殘酷地統治著自己的領地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island remained within the duke's domain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/domain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43b6291a0639e315","term":"domain","forms":["domain","domains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領域；專長範圍","explanation":"指某人、組織或活動所涉及的範圍，尤其是一個人有責任、影響力或專業知識的領域。它是“地盤”概念的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"Customer complaints are outside my domain.","zh":"客戶投訴不屬於我的職責範圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Medicine is her domain.","zh":"醫學是她的專業領域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/domain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23b6ac8d08a9c29887fa","word":"dome","forms":["dome"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9c24469f3e290ce","term":"dome","forms":["dome","domes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓頂；穹頂","explanation":"dome最常指像半個空心球一樣覆蓋在建築物頂部的結構，中文常譯為“圓頂”或“穹頂”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a huge glass dome.","zh":"這座博物館有一個巨大的玻璃穹頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors stood beneath the dome and looked up.","zh":"遊客們站在穹頂下抬頭仰望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d8287fc46b7c314","term":"dome","forms":["dome","domes","doming","domed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使呈圓頂形","explanation":"dome作動詞時，可以把某物塑造成圓頂或拱起的形狀，就是“使……呈穹頂狀”。","examples":[{"en":"The architect domed the entrance hall with a glass roof.","zh":"建築師用玻璃屋頂把入口大廳做成了穹頂形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ceiling is domed to improve the acoustics.","zh":"天花板做成穹頂形，以改善音響效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfb9e6d725a09bd166dd","word":"domestic","forms":["domestic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b33c3e1136e29817","term":"domestic","forms":["domestic","more domestic","most domestic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"家庭的；家裡的","explanation":"表示屬於家庭、家中生活或家務範圍的事物，也就是“家門以內的”。","examples":[{"en":"She is responsible for all the domestic work in the house.","zh":"她負責家裡所有的家務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Domestic life can be stressful when both parents work full-time.","zh":"父母雙方都全職工作時，家庭生活可能會有壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/domestic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd51fd47524ee438","term":"domestic","forms":["domestic","more domestic","most domestic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"家庭事務相關的","explanation":"表示與家庭中常見的活動、服務或問題有關，即使這些活動實際發生在別處，也仍可歸入家庭生活範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The city has opened a center for victims of domestic violence.","zh":"這座城市為家庭暴力受害者開設了一處中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel uses solar energy to provide domestic hot water.","zh":"這家酒店利用太陽能供應生活熱水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/domestic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04731bc4ce6b2c9826a0","word":"dominant","forms":["dominant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2d164b7ba992aba","term":"dominant","forms":["dominant","more dominant","most dominant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"佔統治地位的","explanation":"指掌握權力、控制局面或對其他成員有明顯支配作用的。這個意義直接體現了“站在最前面、壓過別人”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The dominant party controlled the government.","zh":"占主導地位的政黨控制了政府。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One company has become dominant in the local market.","zh":"一家公司已經在當地市場佔據主導地位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dominant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc6afaa2bdb2044d","term":"dominant","forms":["dominant","more dominant","most dominant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最常見的；最重要的","explanation":"指在某個地方、時期或範圍內數量最多、最普遍，或影響和重要性最大。它不一定真的控制別人，而是“在整體中最突出”。","examples":[{"en":"Cars remain the dominant form of transportation in the region.","zh":"汽車仍是該地區最主要的交通方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One dominant brand accounts for nearly half the market.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dominant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e892aeb42e69a534a2c3","word":"dominate","forms":["dominate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f729d1e4efda08c4","term":"dominate","forms":["dominate","dominates","dominating","dominated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"統治；控制","explanation":"憑藉更強的權力或力量控制某人、團體、地區或局面，像站在高處把其他人壓在自己的支配範圍內。","examples":[{"en":"For decades, the company dominated the local market.","zh":"幾十年來，這家公司一直控制著當地市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One family dominated the island's politics for generations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dominate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0491a1be83dd600","term":"dominate","forms":["dominate","dominates","dominating","dominated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對……產生壓倒性的影響","explanation":"某種思想、因素、形式或問題強烈地影響整體，使其他可能性被壓到次要位置；這裡不一定有一個真正的統治者。","examples":[{"en":"One question dominated the meeting from beginning to end.","zh":"從頭到尾，有一個問題一直主導著這場會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Memories of the accident dominated her thoughts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dominate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97462ff138ca8576","term":"dominate","forms":["dominate","dominates","dominating","dominated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在某領域或比賽中佔據優勢","explanation":"在比賽、行業或其他領域裡表現得遠勝對手，長時間掌握主動權，因此成為最有影響力的一方。","examples":[{"en":"The home team dominated the second half and won easily.","zh":"主隊在下半場完全佔據優勢，輕鬆贏下了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The same two clubs dominated the tournament.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dominate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b3e2278234d0e5fe5a4","word":"donate","forms":["donate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08b2cdaf6b56e3a9","term":"donate","forms":["donate","donates","donating","donated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"捐贈；捐出","explanation":"指把錢、物品或其他有價值的東西交出去，用來支援某項事業、機構或需要幫助的人。核心畫面是“把自己的東西捐出去”，而不只是普通地把東西給別人。","examples":[{"en":"Many people donate money to local food banks every winter.","zh":"每年冬天，許多人都會向當地的食物銀行捐款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She donated her old books to the school library.","zh":"她把自己的舊書捐給了學校圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/donate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3433844a443e80708d70","word":"donation","forms":["donation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-296255c570b28ffb","term":"donation","forms":["donation","donations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捐贈；捐款","explanation":"指自願捐給某個人、組織或公益事業的錢、物品或其他貢獻，重點是把自己的東西遞出去幫助某個目標。","examples":[{"en":"They collected donations for families affected by the flood.","zh":"他們為受洪災影響的家庭募集捐款和物資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a generous donation to the local hospital.","zh":"她向當地醫院慷慨捐贈了一筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/donation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-731b30e6b272618b","term":"donation","forms":["donation","donations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"贈與；授予","explanation":"指把財產、權利或某項利益正式給予別人的行為；這裡關注的是“給予”這個過程，而不只是最後收到的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The donation of the land allowed the town to build a new library.","zh":"這塊土地的贈與使該鎮得以建造一座新圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The donation of the property required a formal deed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/donation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d22f115abd6b44f99850","word":"donkey","forms":["donkey"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ffa04d2e4e4f6558","term":"donkey","forms":["donkey","donkeys","donkies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驢","explanation":"一種家養的、外形像馬但體型通常較小的動物，常用於馱運或拉車。這是donkey最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer keeps two donkeys behind the barn.","zh":"農夫在穀倉後面養了兩頭驢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We rode donkeys up the narrow mountain path.","zh":"我們騎著驢走上狹窄的山路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/donkey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed46e0d5c1bf1df7","term":"donkey","forms":["donkey","donkeys","donkies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固執的人","explanation":"借用驢不肯改變方向的形象，指一個頑固、怎麼勸都不改主意的人，通常含有批評或調侃意味。","examples":[{"en":"Don't be such a donkey—listen to what everyone is telling you.","zh":"別這麼固執，聽聽大家都在勸你什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be such a donkey; admit you took the wrong road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/donkey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07ac1859d93f93fc","term":"donkey","forms":["donkey","donkeys","donkies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蠢人","explanation":"也可把donkey用於指愚蠢或做事很不明智的人，仍然來自對驢的擬人化聯想，通常是非正式的責備或玩笑。","examples":[{"en":"I left my keys in the door again—what a donkey I am!","zh":"我又把鑰匙忘在門上了，我真是個大傻瓜！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt like a donkey after that foolish mistake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/donkey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07a7c43357c379b3ae9e","word":"donor","forms":["donor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c33ca4f9800e259","term":"donor","forms":["donor","donors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捐贈者；捐贈機構","explanation":"指主動把錢、物品、血液、器官等交給他人或某個專案的人或組織，重點是“提供資源的一方”。","examples":[{"en":"The charity thanked every donor for their support.","zh":"這家慈善機構感謝每一位捐贈者的支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a blood donor after learning how many patients needed help.","zh":"得知有許多病人需要幫助後，她成了一名獻血者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/donor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-910ecd3e43c7d241425a","word":"doom","forms":["doom"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a64d94b5919f04f","term":"doom","forms":["doom","dooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可怕的命運；厄運","explanation":"doom 指一種尤其糟糕、彷彿早已被判定的命運；它把“判決錘”落下後的結局呈現為無法逃避的厄運。","examples":[{"en":"The hero knew that he was riding toward his doom.","zh":"英雄知道自己正騎向註定的厄運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They could not escape their doom.","zh":"他們無法逃脫自己的厄運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cba3377395451b2b","term":"doom","forms":["doom","dooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"註定會發生的災難","explanation":"doom 也指看起來必然會發生的嚴重壞事或危險，例如一個專案、城市或社會即將走向毀滅的前景。","examples":[{"en":"A sense of doom hung over the failing factory.","zh":"一種大難臨頭的感覺籠罩著那家瀕臨倒閉的工廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The warning signs made the crisis seem like inevitable doom.","zh":"這些警示訊號讓這場危機看起來像是不可避免的災難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ce1258845b68b2c","term":"doom","forms":["doom","dooms","dooming","doomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使註定失敗或遭殃","explanation":"doom 作動詞最常見的主線義是使某人或某事註定走向壞結局，例如失敗、毀滅或長期困境。","examples":[{"en":"That careless decision doomed the rescue mission to failure.","zh":"那個草率的決定使救援行動註定失敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of funding doomed the small theater to closing.","zh":"資金不足使這家小劇院註定要關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2534e2de1dec24fedab4","word":"door","forms":["door"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec2061f959aa37d5","term":"door","forms":["door","doors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門；房門","explanation":"指建築物、房間或車輛上的可開合出入口，通常帶有門把手、門閂或鎖。它既可以是實體門板，也可以泛指人實際進出的那扇門。","examples":[{"en":"Please close the door behind you.","zh":"請把你身後的門關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone knocked on the front door.","zh":"有人敲了前門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/door","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4649326518dfb0a5","term":"door","forms":["door","doors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"途徑；通向某事物的入口","explanation":"把實體門的“透過它進入裡面”這層意思抽象化，表示獲得知識、成功或某種結果的途徑。它強調一條可通向目標的路徑，而不是真正的門。","examples":[{"en":"Reading opened the door to a whole new world for her.","zh":"閱讀為她開啟了通往全新世界的大門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scholarship opened the door to a scientific career.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/door","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d42b056108f7e48","term":"door","forms":["door","doors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機會；可能性","explanation":"一扇尚未關上的門意味著仍有路可走，所以 door 可以表示一個還存在的機會或選擇。所謂“開啟門”就是讓可能性出現，“關門”則是讓可能性消失。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement leaves the door open for future cooperation.","zh":"這項協議為未來合作留下了可能性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That scholarship opened the door to university study.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/door","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ace8f89851d1e64d3be3","word":"doorway","forms":["doorway"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81ecb8ca62703845","term":"doorway","forms":["doorway","doorways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門口；門道","explanation":"指門所在的出入口，尤其強調人或物透過的那一段開口，而不是門板本身。","examples":[{"en":"Please leave your shoes beside the doorway.","zh":"請把鞋放在門口旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stood in the doorway and waved goodbye.","zh":"她站在門口揮手告別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doorway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b60045a3a9744ac8","term":"doorway","forms":["doorway","doorways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開口；通道；比喻性的入口","explanation":"在擴大或比喻的用法中，doorway可以指一般的開口、通道，或通向某種新經驗、新領域的入口；核心仍是“從這裡通往別處”。","examples":[{"en":"For many students, education is a doorway to a wider world.","zh":"對許多學生來說，教育是通向更廣闊世界的一扇門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Literacy opens a doorway to further education.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doorway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74adf004b923da463d0c","word":"dormitory/dorm","forms":["dormitory","dorm"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf1cf14cda176513","term":"dormitory","forms":["dormitory","dormitories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"多人宿舍房間","explanation":"指擺放多張床、供多人睡覺的房間，常見於學校、旅舍等住宿場所。它把“睡覺的地方”從私人臥室變成了多人共用的空間。","examples":[{"en":"I share a dormitory with three other students.","zh":"我和另外三名學生合住一間宿舍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dormitory has eight beds and two showers.","zh":"這間宿舍有八張床和兩個淋浴間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dormitory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2722697a3d8ae94","term":"dormitory","forms":["dormitory","dormitories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宿舍樓；集體住宿建築","explanation":"指整棟或部分建築，裡面住著學生、士兵、僧侶等群體，並共同使用一些設施。這裡的“睡覺的地方”已經從一個房間擴大成了完整的集體居住區。","examples":[{"en":"The university built a new dormitory for first-year students.","zh":"這所大學為一年級學生建了一棟新宿舍樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university built another dormitory beside the library.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dormitory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa16f617bb77fc67","term":"dorm","forms":["dorm","dorms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學生宿舍","explanation":"指學校裡供學生居住的宿舍或宿舍樓，是 dormitory 的簡短、非正式說法。","examples":[{"en":"I met my best friend in the dorm during my first year.","zh":"我大一時在宿舍認識了我最好的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dorm is quieter during the weekend.","zh":"週末宿舍裡更安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dorm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-daf81fe9648c6ae09439","word":"dose","forms":["dose"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-acb73ed48f614aa8","term":"dose","forms":["dose","doses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一劑藥","explanation":"指某人在一次服用或接受治療時所用的規定份量，尤其是藥物的一劑。重點不是藥物種類，而是這一次應給多少。","examples":[{"en":"Take one dose of this medicine after breakfast.","zh":"早餐後服用一劑這種藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor lowered my dose because it made me dizzy.","zh":"這種藥讓我頭暈，所以醫生減少了我的劑量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a13a4766cf60f5fc","term":"dose","forms":["dose","doses","dosing","dosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……服用一劑","explanation":"指給人或動物施用一劑藥，把“給出一份規定的量”變成動作。重點是施藥行為，而不是藥物本身。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse dosed the patient with a mild sedative.","zh":"護士給病人用了一劑溫和的鎮靜劑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The veterinarian dosed the calf with the prescribed medicine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e392dad8b08599f74d48","word":"dot","forms":["dot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-886934e3eb3caa50","term":"dot","forms":["dot","dots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小圓點；小斑點","explanation":"指很小的圓形斑點或色點，就像紙上、衣服上或圖畫中的一個小圓點。它是理解其他許多詞義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"There was a bright red dot on the white wall.","zh":"白牆上有一個鮮紅的小點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"From the hill, the houses looked like tiny dots.","zh":"從山上看，房子像一個個小點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-413ae252eb6ed92a","term":"dot","forms":["dot","dots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"句號；縮寫點","explanation":"指句末表示結束的句號，或縮寫中使用的點號。它仍然是“用一個點標出邊界”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"Put a dot after the abbreviation.","zh":"在這個縮寫後面加一個點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sentence ends with a dot.","zh":"這個句子以句號結尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ce06a9e7f8c3e6bf85a","word":"double","forms":["double"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0d0051c7b4e003f","term":"double","forms":["double"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由兩個部分組成","explanation":"表示某物由兩個相配或互補的部分組成，就像一件東西出現了兩份。","examples":[{"en":"The closet has double doors.","zh":"這個壁櫥有兩扇門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cupboard has a double door with brass handles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/double","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2db969e1ba06a538","term":"double","forms":["double"],"pos":"adj","zh":"兩倍的","explanation":"表示數量、分量或程度是通常情況的兩倍，也就是兩份合在一起。","examples":[{"en":"She ordered a double portion of rice.","zh":"她點了雙份米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new system offers double the storage.","zh":"新系統提供兩倍的儲存空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/double","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47bca7b4ec26a7ff","term":"double","forms":["double"],"pos":"adv","zh":"兩倍地；加倍地","explanation":"表示某個數量、程度或年齡是原來的兩倍，就像同一份東西出現了兩份。","examples":[{"en":"This bag costs double what I paid last year.","zh":"這個包的價格是我去年支付的兩倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs took double as long as we expected.","zh":"維修花的時間是我們預想的兩倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/double","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44b41d93a287e35e","term":"double","forms":["double","doubles","doubling","doubled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使翻倍","explanation":"把原來的數量變成兩份，也就是增加到原來的兩倍。這裡可以把它想成同樣的東西又出現了一份。","examples":[{"en":"The company doubled its profits in three years.","zh":"這家公司在三年內使利潤翻了一倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to double the recipe for twelve guests.","zh":"我們需要把食譜的用量加倍，才能供十二位客人食用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/double","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6760e80e3327f820f2e","word":"doubt","forms":["doubt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fc68d6a365c9bf0","term":"doubt","forms":["doubt","doubts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疑慮；不確定","explanation":"指你無法確定某件事是否真實、正確或會發生，心裡因此產生疑慮。它既可以表示一般的不確定，也可以表示某一次具體的懷疑。","examples":[{"en":"There was some doubt as to who the child's real father was.","zh":"大家有些疑慮，不確定這個孩子的親生父親是誰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her explanation removed all doubt about what had happened.","zh":"她的解釋消除了人們對事情經過的所有疑慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6536808f18910e30","term":"doubt","forms":["doubt","doubts","doubting","doubted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懷疑；拿不準","explanation":"表示你對某件事是否真實、正確或會發生沒有把握，因而不完全相信或無法作出判斷。這是 doubt 作動詞時最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I doubt that he will arrive before noon.","zh":"我懷疑他能否在中午前到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She doubted her own judgment after hearing the criticism.","zh":"聽到批評後，她開始懷疑自己的判斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c154724d389e4bf89ffe","word":"doubtful","forms":["doubtful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d74718ee118913ee","term":"doubtful","forms":["doubtful","more doubtful","most doubtful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有疑問的；令人懷疑的","explanation":"某件事缺少足夠證據，或者本身讓人無法確定真假，因此使人產生疑問。它既可以說“對某事有疑問”，也可以說“某事令人懷疑”。","examples":[{"en":"I am doubtful about the accuracy of these figures.","zh":"我對這些數字的準確性有疑問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is doubtful whether the plan will work.","zh":"這個計劃能否奏效很值得懷疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubtful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc5a335a8e8e980c","term":"doubtful","forms":["doubtful","more doubtful","most doubtful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"持懷疑態度的","explanation":"形容人或人的表情、語氣表現出不相信、不確定或不願輕易接受的態度；疑雲不是落在事情上，而是落在人的判斷上。","examples":[{"en":"She was doubtful about his explanation.","zh":"她對他的解釋持懷疑態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave me a doubtful look when I suggested the idea.","zh":"我提出這個想法時，他用懷疑的目光看著我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubtful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc5f83b389624c3f","term":"doubtful","forms":["doubtful","more doubtful","most doubtful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結果未定的；沒有把握的","explanation":"事情的結果還被疑雲遮住，暫時無法判斷會怎樣，尤其常用於比賽、計劃或能否成功等結果。","examples":[{"en":"The outcome of the election is still doubtful.","zh":"選舉結果仍未確定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their chances of reaching shore looked doubtful.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doubtful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb9db87912c07db92304","word":"dough","forms":["dough"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-812238ca99bb2493","term":"dough","forms":["dough","doughs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麵糰","explanation":"把麵粉和水、雞蛋、黃油等材料混合後形成的厚實、柔軟而能塑形的團狀物，通常還會被做成某種形狀再烘烤。","examples":[{"en":"Pizza dough is very stretchy.","zh":"披薩麵糰很有彈性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the dough to rise for an hour.","zh":"把麵糰放著發酵一小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d14d4b75cdf408a","term":"dough","forms":["dough","doughs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錢","explanation":"俚語中把錢想成一團可以拿來使用和週轉的東西，因此用 dough 指錢，尤其常指手頭可用的錢。","examples":[{"en":"I need more dough to fix my car.","zh":"我需要更多錢來修車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He earned enough dough to buy a bicycle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6f8ff77a4786fdb7ba7","word":"doughnut","forms":["doughnut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f497e436b767fd24","term":"doughnut","forms":["doughnut","doughnuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"甜甜圈；油炸麵點","explanation":"一種用麵糰或麵糊油炸而成的甜點，通常呈環形，也可以填入果醬、奶油或其他餡料。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a doughnut and a coffee on my way to work.","zh":"我上班路上買了一個甜甜圈和一杯咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bakery fills its doughnuts with raspberry jam.","zh":"這家麵包店在甜甜圈裡填入覆盆子果醬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doughnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0d4acef7465f8ca","term":"doughnut","forms":["doughnut","doughnuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"甜甜圈形的環狀物","explanation":"形狀像甜甜圈、中央有孔的物體；這裡強調的是環形外觀，而不是食物本身。","examples":[{"en":"A doughnut-shaped raft floated beside the boat.","zh":"一隻甜甜圈形的救生筏漂在船旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine has a doughnut-shaped ring around its center.","zh":"這臺機器的中心周圍有一個甜甜圈形的環。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/doughnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-184c926681179fdf7098","word":"dove","forms":["dove"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95048183f1748466","term":"dove","forms":["dove","doves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鴿子","explanation":"指鴿科的一種鳥，通常特指體形較小、顏色偏白的鴿子。記住“溫和的白鴿”這個形象，就能把它和後面的和平、純潔等引申義聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"A white dove landed on the garden wall.","zh":"一隻白鴿落在了花園的牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the doves gather near the fountain.","zh":"我們看著鴿子聚集到噴泉旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b043154c32ba223c","term":"dove","forms":["dove","doves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主張和解的人","explanation":"比喻主張透過談判、妥協和和平手段解決衝突的人，常用於政治或政府討論。它沿用了白鴿溫和、和平的形象，與主張強硬行動的人相對。","examples":[{"en":"The new minister is considered a dove in the peace talks.","zh":"這位新部長被認為是和平談判中的鴿派。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The negotiator was a dove who favored compromise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-908aec4512d80ff4fefb","word":"down","forms":["down"],"officialPos":"adv./prep./adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-400934322c6b4250","term":"down","forms":["down","more down","most down"],"pos":"adj","zh":"情緒低落的","explanation":"表示人因為難過、失望或壓力而情緒落到低谷，接近“沮喪、悶悶不樂”。這是把“向下”用於人的情緒狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She has been feeling down since her dog died.","zh":"她的狗去世後一直情緒低落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You look a little down today.","zh":"你今天看起來有點悶悶不樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/down","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbd949928a02c914","term":"down","forms":["down","further down","farther down","furthest down","farthest down"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向下","explanation":"沿著“向下”的線，從較高處到較低處；可以指人、動物或物體實際往下移動。","examples":[{"en":"The cat jumped down from the table.","zh":"貓從桌子上跳了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The loose tile slid down the roof.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/down","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d21c36254be14fa2","term":"down","forms":["down","downs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"絨毛；羽絨","explanation":"順著“向下”的記憶線想，鳥身上貼近身體、蓬鬆而細軟的羽毛就是 down；它也常被用來填充被子、睡袋和羽絨服。","examples":[{"en":"This sleeping bag is filled with light duck down.","zh":"這個睡袋填充的是輕柔的鴨絨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chick was covered in soft yellow down.","zh":"這隻雛鳥身上 covered with 柔軟的黃色絨毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/down","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6d431f30318a3f2","term":"down","forms":["down","downs","downing","downed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擊倒；打落","explanation":"沿著“向下”的線把人或物打到地上，或使其從直立狀態倒下；也常用於砍倒樹木。","examples":[{"en":"The storm downed several trees near the road.","zh":"暴風雨刮倒了路邊的幾棵樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A defender downed the striker just outside the penalty area.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/down","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68ff63fb82e0e5dfec2a","word":"download","forms":["download"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a4885b5f5982c05","term":"download","forms":["download","downloads","downloading","downloaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下載資料","explanation":"指透過網路把程式、檔案或其他資料從遠端位置傳到自己的電腦、手機等裝置。可以把它想成沿通道“向下裝入”本地裝置。","examples":[{"en":"You can download the guide from our website.","zh":"你可以從我們的網站下載這份指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She downloaded the photos to her phone.","zh":"她把照片下載到了手機上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/download","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8eeafca9de6477b81d0f","word":"downstairs","forms":["downstairs"],"officialPos":"adv./n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-584d7193aaa2994d","term":"downstairs","forms":["downstairs","further downstairs","farther downstairs","furthest downstairs","farthest downstairs"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樓下的","explanation":"表示位於較低樓層的，通常就是“樓下的”。它把“向下、在下面”的空間概念直接用來修飾房間或其他地方。","examples":[{"en":"The children are sleeping in the downstairs bedroom.","zh":"孩子們正在樓下的臥室裡睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The downstairs bathroom needs a new mirror.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downstairs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ac6a88d5de107d2","term":"downstairs","forms":["downstairs","further downstairs","farther downstairs","furthest downstairs","farthest downstairs"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向樓下；在樓下","explanation":"表示沿樓梯向下，或已經在較低樓層。它既能描述移動方向，也能描述所在位置，是 downstairs 最常見的副詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"I left my keys downstairs, so I have to go back for them.","zh":"我把鑰匙落在樓下了，所以得回去拿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wait downstairs while I get my coat.","zh":"我去拿外套時，請在樓下等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downstairs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fcb4ef76dbcd164","term":"downstairs","forms":["downstairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樓下；樓下的一層","explanation":"表示房屋中較低的那一層，通常是地面層，有時也指地下層。這裡“樓下”從位置副詞變成了一個可以被談論的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The downstairs is bright, but the bedrooms upstairs are small.","zh":"樓下很明亮，但樓上的臥室很小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The downstairs needs painting before we move in.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downstairs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-308301fb06e9ac280c30","word":"downtown","forms":["downtown"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-107086e2ff570b08","term":"downtown","forms":["downtown","further downtown","farther downtown","more downtown","furthest downtown","farthest downtown","most downtown"],"pos":"adj","zh":"市中心的","explanation":"指與城市中心商業區有關，或坐落在該區域。這個意義直接來自“城鎮中心”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She found a small café near her downtown office.","zh":"她在市中心的辦公室附近找到了一家小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Downtown shops stayed open late for the festival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downtown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-848cb2141963fa43","term":"downtown","forms":["downtown","further downtown","farther downtown","more downtown","furthest downtown","farthest downtown","most downtown"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在或往市中心","explanation":"表示人在市中心，或移動的方向是市中心。這裡是“朝城鎮中心走”的動態用法。","examples":[{"en":"We took the train downtown for dinner.","zh":"我們坐火車去市中心吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I ran into Maya downtown this morning.","zh":"我今天早上在市中心碰到了瑪雅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downtown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25729de2012a6c43","term":"downtown","forms":["downtown","downtowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"市中心商業區","explanation":"指城市中主要的商業區域，通常位於城市中心或中心附近。它是“城鎮中心”這條記憶主線的名詞化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The new library is in downtown Toronto.","zh":"新圖書館位於多倫多市中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Downtown was crowded with shoppers after work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downtown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21161a7aaac1e6e45130","word":"downward","forms":["downward"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-873933037981a6ee","term":"downward","forms":["downward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"向下的","explanation":"表示方向、傾斜或動作朝向下方；這個“向下”也可以引申為趨勢變差或降低。","examples":[{"en":"She gave him a downward glance.","zh":"她低頭看了他一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road has a sharp downward slope.","zh":"這條路有一段很陡的下坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-378458b50f5581328c78","word":"downward/downwards","forms":["downward","downwards"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c69f133dcca5d0b","term":"downward","forms":["downward"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向下；下降","explanation":"表示朝較低處移動，或某種數量、地位、價值沿著向下的方向發展。","examples":[{"en":"The prices continued to move downward.","zh":"價格繼續下跌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He walked downward toward the valley.","zh":"他向下朝山谷走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5abb236741316b4d","term":"downwards","forms":["downwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向下；朝低處","explanation":"表示人或物朝較低的地方移動，重點是方向向下，而不是已經處在下面。","examples":[{"en":"The stone rolled downwards along the slope.","zh":"石頭沿著斜坡向下滾去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gravity pulls everything downwards.","zh":"重力把一切物體都往下拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-890d0eddda240177","term":"downwards","forms":["downwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向較低水平發展","explanation":"把“向下”的方向用於抽象變化，表示數量、經濟狀況、質量或等級逐漸降低，或朝更差的方向發展。","examples":[{"en":"After the rise in oil prices, the economy headed downwards.","zh":"油價上漲後，經濟開始走下坡路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Prices continued downwards after the holiday season.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0d83d75603db30f99e1","word":"doze","forms":["doze"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"doze","forms":["doze"],"pos":"v./n.","zh":"打瞌睡；小睡","examples":[{"en":"I sometimes doze on the train after a long day.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Grandpa settled into his chair for a short doze.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-bed7ef56035a9e4e09f1","word":"dozen","forms":["dozen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fdb63afe3d196884","term":"dozen","forms":["dozen","dozens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一打；十二個","explanation":"指由十二個同類物品組成的一組，相當於“一打”。它強調的是一個完整的十二個單位，而不只是數字十二本身。","examples":[{"en":"Can I have a dozen eggs, please?","zh":"請給我一打雞蛋，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought a dozen eggs at the farm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dozen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16e16d732e7802a5","term":"dozen","forms":["dozen","dozens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"許多；幾十個","explanation":"在 dozens of 中，它不再強調精確的十二個，而是把數量想成一組組十二個，因此表示“許多、幾十個”，通常數量明顯超過十幾個但沒有明確說出總數。","examples":[{"en":"There were dozens of people waiting outside.","zh":"外面有幾十個人在等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dozens of sparrows crowded the feeder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dozen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7743ce348d9284d677a1","word":"draft","forms":["draft"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-baafaab48e3257ee","term":"draft","forms":["draft","drafts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穿堂風；氣流","explanation":"指進入房間、車輛等處的一股空氣流動，常讓人感到冷；可以把它記成空氣被“拉進來”。","examples":[{"en":"Close the window—there's a cold draft coming in.","zh":"把窗戶關上，有一股冷風吹進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt a draft under the door.","zh":"我感覺到門底下有風吹進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4736d642b5117fdc","term":"draft","forms":["draft","drafts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"初稿；草稿；草圖","explanation":"指作品、文章或圖畫尚未定稿的版本，是先“拉出一個雛形”供修改的東西。它可以是寫作初稿，也可以是繪圖草圖。","examples":[{"en":"I finished the first draft of my report last night.","zh":"我昨晚完成了報告的初稿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The architect showed us a draft of the new layout.","zh":"建築師給我們看了新佈局的草圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b21d1ae18d2a2ff6","term":"draft","forms":["draft","drafts","drafting","drafted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起草初稿；畫出草圖","explanation":"把draft理解為先把想法“拉出”一個雛形：寫作時先寫出初稿，繪圖時先畫出草圖或大致方案，之後還可以繼續修改。它強調的是初步版本，不一定是最終成品。","examples":[{"en":"I drafted a short proposal for the new project.","zh":"我為這個新專案起草了一份簡短的提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She drafted a floor plan before meeting the architect.","zh":"她在會見建築師之前先畫了一張平面草圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ac5248b70ac338b760f","word":"drag","forms":["drag"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-625516579abb0306","term":"drag","forms":["drag","drags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煩人的人或事","explanation":"指讓人厭煩、失望，或妨礙事情順利進行的人或事物。可以把它記成“拖後腿”的東西：它讓原本的行動變得費力、掃興。","examples":[{"en":"Waiting for the bus in the rain is such a drag.","zh":"在雨裡等公交車真讓人煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Having to redo the whole report was a real drag.","zh":"不得不把整份報告重做一遍，真是件煩人的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b411035ecde9f169","term":"drag","forms":["drag","drags","dragging","dragged","drug"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拖著移動","explanation":"用力拉著某物，使它沿地面或其他介質移動，通常暗示移動不輕鬆，就像“拖著走”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We dragged the broken sofa out of the room.","zh":"我們把那張壞沙發拖出了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dragged the heavy suitcase up the stairs.","zh":"她把沉重的手提箱拖上了樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-578783875c4dae5a","term":"drag","forms":["drag","drags","dragging","dragged","drug"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緩慢進行","explanation":"指事情、時間或行動進行得很慢、很費力，彷彿被什麼東西拖著走。","examples":[{"en":"The last hour of the lecture dragged.","zh":"講座最後一個小時過得特別慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting dragged on until midnight.","zh":"會議一直拖到午夜才結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f7f8342570bb07f","term":"drag","forms":["drag","drags","dragging","dragged","drug"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拖動專案","explanation":"在電腦上按住滑鼠或其他指點裝置的按鈕，把檔案、圖示等專案拖到另一個位置；這仍是“拖著走”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Drag the photo into the message box to upload it.","zh":"把照片拖到訊息框裡上傳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can drag the icon to the desktop.","zh":"你可以把這個圖示拖到桌面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9c43be948c5cabd56ef","word":"dragon","forms":["dragon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b578208e6868b146","term":"dragon","forms":["dragon","dragons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳說中的龍","explanation":"指傳說中像巨蛇或大型爬行動物一樣的生物，常被描寫為會飛、噴火或擁有強大力量。不同文化中的dragon形象不完全相同，但都帶有神秘、危險和強大的核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The knight rode into the cave to face the dragon.","zh":"騎士騎馬進入山洞去面對那條龍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story says that the dragon guarded a treasure.","zh":"故事說那條龍守護著一批寶藏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fc102b2bffac53c","term":"dragon","forms":["dragon","dragons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極難對付的事物","explanation":"指某個非常強大、危險或難以解決的人或事物，是從“強大的龍”引申出的比喻義。它可以形容競爭者、問題、制度或其他令人畏懼的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The small team took on the dragon of online fraud.","zh":"這個小團隊迎戰了網路詐騙這個難纏的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unfinished thesis became a dragon she feared facing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2ca6aec52558fcc0431","word":"dragonfly","forms":["dragonfly"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac46881535e6bd1d","term":"dragonfly","forms":["dragonfly","dragonflies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜻蜓","explanation":"一種身體細長、長著四片透明翅膀的昆蟲；它停在物體上時，翅膀通常向身體兩側張開，這正是記憶中那隻會飛的小“龍”。","examples":[{"en":"A dragonfly landed on the garden fence.","zh":"一隻蜻蜓落在花園的籬笆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched several dragonflies flying over the pond.","zh":"我們看著幾隻蜻蜓在池塘上方飛來飛去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragonfly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-510345478efc1edf0c92","word":"drain","forms":["drain"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f83402dac71dba9","term":"drain","forms":["drain","drains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排水管；下水口","explanation":"指讓水或其他液體流出水槽、浴缸等容器的管道或出口；核心畫面就是液體從這裡被排空。","examples":[{"en":"The drain in the kitchen sink is clogged.","zh":"廚房水槽的下水口堵住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hair can block the shower drain.","zh":"頭髮可能會堵住淋浴下水口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-158ec7a84bf49cef","term":"drain","forms":["drain","drains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資源消耗源","explanation":"指不斷消耗金錢、時間、精力等，卻沒有相應回報的人或事物；就像一個把資源慢慢排空的出口。","examples":[{"en":"The old building has become a drain on the charity's budget.","zh":"那棟舊建築已經成了這個慈善機構預算上的一個無底洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That unreliable car is a drain on our savings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5dd9dc26e37c6d2","term":"drain","forms":["drain","drains","draining","drained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"液體流走","explanation":"指容器或區域裡的液體自行流出、變少；重點在液體離開原來的地方，而不強調誰讓它流走。","examples":[{"en":"The clogged sink drained slowly.","zh":"堵塞的水槽排水很慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the storm, the flooded street finally drained.","zh":"暴雨後，被淹的街道終於排幹了水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-841832bd0a33d431","term":"drain","forms":["drain","drains","draining","drained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排出液體","explanation":"指使容器、土地或其他地方里的液體流出去；可以理解為主動開啟“排空出口”。","examples":[{"en":"Please drain the sink before you wash the dishes.","zh":"洗碗前請先把水槽裡的水排掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She drained the pasta and added the sauce.","zh":"她把義大利麵的水瀝掉後加上了醬汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acee9b097b1e842a","term":"drain","forms":["drain","drains","draining","drained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"耗盡精力或資源","explanation":"指某件事逐漸抽走人的精力，或耗盡金錢、時間等資源；這是“液體被排空”這一畫面的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The long meeting drained everyone’s energy.","zh":"長時間的會議耗盡了所有人的精力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Constant repairs are draining our savings.","zh":"不斷的維修正在耗盡我們的積蓄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87da8bbbea6db324c6f7","word":"drama","forms":["drama"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e79d840791789b9","term":"drama","forms":["drama","dramas","dramata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戲劇作品","explanation":"指為演員表演而寫的故事作品，通常以人物對話和行動來展開；它可以是舞臺劇，也可以泛指一部戲劇性很強的作品。","examples":[{"en":"The author released her latest drama last month.","zh":"那位作者上個月推出了她最新的戲劇作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a historical drama about the royal family.","zh":"我們看了一部關於王室的歷史劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drama","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ccc304023dbf7485","term":"drama","forms":["drama","dramas","dramata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生活中的戲劇性場面","explanation":"指現實生活中像舞臺劇情一樣有強烈衝突、麻煩或情緒起伏的情況；它不一定是真正的戲劇作品。","examples":[{"en":"After the argument, nobody wanted any more drama.","zh":"爭吵之後，誰也不想再惹出更多麻煩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting turned into a family drama.","zh":"那場會議變成了一出家庭鬧劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drama","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c51288ab4f6ae0ce906","word":"dramatic","forms":["dramatic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b24907085ff81700","term":"dramatic","forms":["dramatic","more dramatic","most dramatic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"戲劇性的；與戲劇有關的","explanation":"表示和戲劇、舞臺表演有關，或具有戲劇作品的特點。它強調錶演、情節和舞臺效果這一整類事物，是其他幾個義項的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"She studied dramatic writing at university.","zh":"她在大學學習戲劇創作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film uses dramatic music to build tension.","zh":"這部電影用戲劇性的音樂來營造緊張氣氛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dramatic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6241ed921012c831","term":"dramatic","forms":["dramatic","more dramatic","most dramatic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"引人注目的；顯著的","explanation":"表示某種變化、效果或外觀非常醒目，像舞臺上突然加強的燈光或音效一樣能立刻吸引注意。它不一定和真正的戲劇或表演有關。","examples":[{"en":"The new treatment led to a dramatic improvement in her health.","zh":"新的治療使她的健康狀況有了顯著改善。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sunset made a dramatic change to the appearance of the mountains.","zh":"日落讓群山的外觀發生了極其醒目的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dramatic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-150f7f1e560ba8bae36f","word":"drastic","forms":["drastic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64b1504a4b33b32e","term":"drastic","forms":["drastic","more drastic","most drastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"強烈而徹底的","explanation":"指某種措施、改變或行動力度很大，影響範圍廣，甚至會徹底改變原來的狀況；可以把它理解為“下重手”。","examples":[{"en":"The company took drastic measures to avoid bankruptcy.","zh":"這家公司採取了強硬措施來避免破產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a drastic change in our study habits.","zh":"我們需要徹底改變學習習慣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae019a01b9d9076b545b","word":"draught","forms":["draught"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-914bb2013c749026","term":"draught","forms":["draught","draughts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氣流；穿堂風","explanation":"指從門、窗或牆縫等處突然進入室內的空氣，常讓人感到冷。這個意義體現了“有東西從外面被引進來”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I could feel a cold draught coming from under the door.","zh":"我能感覺到一股冷風從門底下鑽進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a draught in this room, so please close the window.","zh":"這個房間裡有穿堂風，請把窗戶關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draught","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3de795f262f64015","term":"draught","forms":["draught","draughts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳棋棋子","explanation":"在英國英語裡，指玩跳棋時使用的一枚棋子；這裡的意義已經從“被移動、被牽引的東西”分化成了遊戲術語。","examples":[{"en":"She moved one draught forward and forced her opponent to jump.","zh":"她把一枚跳棋棋子向前移動了一格，迫使對手跳吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She moved a draught diagonally across the board.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draught","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50f7becde477bb509c77","word":"draw","forms":["draw"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7675bb49d165f021","term":"draw","forms":["draw","draws","drawing","drew","drawn","drawest","drewest","draweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拉出；拖動","explanation":"表示用力把某物拉動，尤其是把它從某處拉出來；記住“把東西拉出來或拉過來”這一基本動作即可。","examples":[{"en":"She drew a small notebook from her bag.","zh":"她從包裡拿出一個小筆記本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He drew the curtain across the window.","zh":"他把窗簾拉到窗戶另一邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-087589ac85e3b98f","term":"draw","forms":["draw","draws","drawing","drew","drawn","drawest","drewest","draweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸引注意力","explanation":"表示把人的目光、興趣或注意力“拉過來”，也就是吸引某人關注某物。","examples":[{"en":"The bright sign drew everyone’s attention.","zh":"那塊醒目的招牌吸引了所有人的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unusual design drew many visitors to the shop.","zh":"獨特的設計吸引了許多遊客來到這家商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6771164ecb2665b2","term":"draw","forms":["draw","draws","drawing","drew","drawn","drawest","drewest","draweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抽取；抽選","explanation":"表示從一組東西中抽出、取出或隨機選出一個；這就是把某物“拉出來”的抽取義。","examples":[{"en":"Each player drew a card from the deck.","zh":"每位玩家都從牌堆裡抽了一張牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The winning number was drawn at random.","zh":"中獎號碼是隨機抽取的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a674132295d42b46","term":"draw","forms":["draw","draws","drawing","drew","drawn","drawest","drewest","draweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"畫出或描繪","explanation":"這是把線條、形狀或影象“拉”到紙面、牆面等表面上，也就是用筆畫出或描繪出來。","examples":[{"en":"Mia drew a small house in the corner of the page.","zh":"米婭在頁面的一角畫了一座小房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He drew a straight line across the map.","zh":"他在地圖上畫了一條直線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d329f11d9a60de9b6f26","word":"drawer","forms":["drawer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc217e7a38130d9b","term":"drawer","forms":["drawer","drawers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽屜","explanation":"傢俱裡可以向外拉出、向內推回的盒狀空間，用來收納衣物或其他物品。","examples":[{"en":"I keep my spare keys in the top drawer.","zh":"我把備用鑰匙放在最上面的抽屜裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drawer is stuck, so pull it gently.","zh":"抽屜卡住了，所以請輕輕地拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drawer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a814fa3fba17c37b","term":"drawer","forms":["drawer","drawers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"側邊補充面板","explanation":"在軟體介面或某些技術結構中，指從側面滑出、用來顯示額外內容的面板。","examples":[{"en":"Tap the icon to open the drawer with more settings.","zh":"點選這個圖示，開啟顯示更多設定的側邊面板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tap the menu icon to open the navigation drawer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drawer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27f3282691613a41f159","word":"drawing","forms":["drawing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-036db74657c5ab3f","term":"drawing","forms":["drawing","drawings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圖畫；示意圖","explanation":"指用線條畫出的影象，可以是藝術作品，也可以是用來說明事物的示意圖、草圖或圖表。它強調“畫出來的成品”，不一定追求藝術性。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer showed us a drawing of the new bridge.","zh":"工程師給我們看了一張新橋的設計圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a pencil drawing of a cat on the wall.","zh":"牆上有一幅鉛筆畫的貓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drawing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89fff7585118dbcb","term":"drawing","forms":["drawing","drawings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繪畫這一動作","explanation":"指製作圖畫的動作本身，而不是完成後的那張圖。重點在“畫的過程或行為”。","examples":[{"en":"The drawing of the portrait took several hours.","zh":"畫這幅肖像花了好幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Drawing from life sharpened her observation skills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drawing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d689d2a8f5ef2f05089","word":"dread","forms":["dread"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41954256f6e8cfe5","term":"dread","forms":["dread","dreads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈的預先恐懼","explanation":"指壞事尚未發生，但因為預料到它可能發生而產生的沉重、強烈的恐懼。","examples":[{"en":"She felt a growing dread as the plane began to shake.","zh":"飛機開始搖晃時，她感到越來越強烈的恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thought of telling his parents filled him with dread.","zh":"一想到要告訴父母這件事，他就充滿恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77498dfc18277d51","term":"dread","forms":["dread","dreads","dreading","dreaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"非常害怕","explanation":"指對某人或某事感到強烈恐懼，恐懼程度通常明顯高於普通的擔心。","examples":[{"en":"Many people dread speaking in front of a large audience.","zh":"許多人都害怕在大庭廣眾面前講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I dread the long drive home after dark.","zh":"我很害怕天黑後開很長時間的車回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9953e0536dc9b92","term":"dread","forms":["dread","dreads","dreading","dreaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"害怕地等待","explanation":"指因為預料到某個結果可能很糟，而一邊等待、一邊害怕它到來；這是“恐懼提前壓來”的典型動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"They are dreading hearing the doctor's decision tomorrow.","zh":"他們害怕明天聽到醫生的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dreaded opening the letter.","zh":"她害怕開啟那封信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5e9214462bbae548f98","word":"dreadful","forms":["dreadful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28cc4e4190d3f554","term":"dreadful","forms":["dreadful","more dreadful","most dreadful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可怕的；糟糕透頂的","explanation":"指某事物會引起強烈恐懼，或糟糕、嚴重得讓人覺得難以忍受。它可以描述真實的危險，也可以只是強烈地評價某種不好的情況或體驗。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a dreadful noise coming from the basement.","zh":"我們聽到地下室傳來一陣可怕的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The weather was dreadful, so we stayed indoors all day.","zh":"天氣糟透了，所以我們一整天都待在室內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreadful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33285f22f73f40a7","term":"dreadful","forms":["dreadful","more dreadful","most dreadful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其嚴重或強烈的","explanation":"表示某種程度大得驚人，常帶有讓人害怕或震驚的意味；它強調“嚴重、過分或強烈”，不一定具體說明害怕的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The accident caused dreadful damage to the old bridge.","zh":"這場事故給那座老橋造成了極其嚴重的損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He suffered dreadful pain whenever he moved his shoulder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreadful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30fde358b34772de141e","word":"dream","forms":["dream"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-822126dd0a35129c","term":"dream","forms":["dream","dreams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夢","explanation":"指人在睡覺時腦海中出現的虛構場景、人物或經歷。","examples":[{"en":"I had a strange dream about flying last night.","zh":"我昨晚做了一個夢，夢見自己在飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She woke up and wrote the dream in her notebook.","zh":"她醒來後把那個夢寫在了筆記本上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14187fcf1ed9459c","term":"dream","forms":["dream","dreams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夢想；願望","explanation":"指一個人希望將來實現的目標或生活狀態；它不是睡眠中的畫面，而是醒著時心中的嚮往。","examples":[{"en":"Her dream is to open a bakery by the sea.","zh":"她的夢想是在海邊開一家麵包店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has always dreamed of becoming a pilot.","zh":"他一直夢想成為一名飛行員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5fc3268da95b6e5f","term":"dream","forms":["dream","dreams","dreaming","dreamed","dreamt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做夢","explanation":"指人在睡覺時腦海中經歷虛構的場景或事件。","examples":[{"en":"I dreamed that I was walking through a city made of glass.","zh":"我夢見自己走在一座玻璃做的城市裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Did you dream about your old school?","zh":"你夢見你的舊學校了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7eeb50bcff642329","term":"dream","forms":["dream","dreams","dreaming","dreamed","dreamt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"夢想；希望","explanation":"指懷抱某個願望，希望將來成為某種人或實現某件事。","examples":[{"en":"Maya dreams of studying medicine abroad.","zh":"瑪雅夢想去國外學醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They dream about building a home in the countryside.","zh":"他們夢想在鄉下建一所房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b612edb571c479d1a33","word":"dress","forms":["dress"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a34bacc2d91885bc","term":"dress","forms":["dress","dresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連衣裙","explanation":"指從上身一直覆蓋到腰部以下、連著裙襬的一件衣服，通常指女性或女孩穿的連衣裙。這個義項最直接地體現了把外表整理得得體的記憶線索。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a blue dress to the wedding.","zh":"她穿了一條藍色連衣裙去參加婚禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a comfortable dress for the summer.","zh":"我需要一條適合夏天穿的舒適連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f58222722bbb2733","term":"dress","forms":["dress","dresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服裝；裝束","explanation":"指服裝或整體穿著，尤其強調它是否適合某個場合、職業或身份。它把“整理到合適、得體的狀態”從一件衣服擴充套件到了整套裝束。","examples":[{"en":"The guests arrived in formal dress.","zh":"賓客們穿著正式服裝到場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers were inspected in full dress.","zh":"士兵們穿著全套禮服接受檢閱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4600fd20513c01b","term":"dress","forms":["dress","dresses","dressing","dressed","drest","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……穿衣","explanation":"指給自己、別人或擬人化的物件穿上衣服，把外表整理得合適、得體。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse dressed the child in warm clothes.","zh":"護士給孩子穿上了暖和的衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was dressed in a simple blue suit.","zh":"她穿著一套樸素的藍色套裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-338854e077e19e8a","term":"dress","forms":["dress","dresses","dressing","dressed","drest","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"準備以供使用","explanation":"指整理、安裝或處理某物，使它達到預定用途所需的狀態；記住它就是把東西收拾妥當、準備好。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic dressed the machine for its first test.","zh":"機械師把機器準備好，等待第一次測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kitchen staff dressed the vegetables for the meal.","zh":"廚房工作人員把蔬菜處理好，準備做這頓飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-351c77d371856ff10934","word":"dresser","forms":["dresser"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6dd0863c6e94322f","term":"dresser","forms":["dresser","dressers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廚房碗櫃（英）","explanation":"在英國英語中，dresser 是廚房裡的櫃子，通常有架子或櫃格，用來擺放和收納盤子、杯子等餐具。它體現了“把東西整理好、放整齊”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The blue plates are displayed on the kitchen dresser.","zh":"藍色的盤子擺在廚房碗櫃上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The antique dresser has deep cupboards below its open display shelves.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dresser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5591061980336c0","term":"dresser","forms":["dresser","dressers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臥室梳妝櫃（美）","explanation":"在美國英語中，dresser 通常是臥室裡較矮的抽屜櫃，常用於收放衣物，有時配有鏡子。它把“整理衣物”的概念變成了一件傢俱。","examples":[{"en":"I keep my socks in the top drawer of the dresser.","zh":"我把襪子放在梳妝櫃的最上層抽屜裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cracked mirror hung above the antique dresser in her bedroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dresser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f393752ab3da8f60daea","word":"dressing","forms":["dressing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f944c1d9619c1c2","term":"dressing","forms":["dressing","dressings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傷口敷料","explanation":"指覆蓋傷口、保護傷口或幫助治療的材料，如紗布或其他醫用覆蓋物；它正是“給傷口加一層保護”的 dressing。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse changed the dressing on my arm.","zh":"護士給我換了手臂上的敷料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the dressing clean and dry.","zh":"保持敷料清潔乾燥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dressing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-688cd697c3158a60","term":"dressing","forms":["dressing","dressings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙拉醬；調味汁","explanation":"指澆在沙拉等食物上的醬汁，尤其常指冷的沙拉調味汁；它是“給食物加上一層味道”。","examples":[{"en":"Would you like the dressing on the side?","zh":"你想把沙拉醬另外放嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This salad needs a lighter dressing.","zh":"這份沙拉需要清淡一點的醬汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dressing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ca0c3c357388609","term":"dressing","forms":["dressing","dressings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穿衣；著裝","explanation":"指穿衣服這一活動或過程，是 dress 加上 -ing 後形成的動名詞義；這裡不是衣服本身，而是“給自己穿上一層外表”。","examples":[{"en":"The child needs help with dressing.","zh":"這個孩子穿衣需要幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She listened to the radio while dressing.","zh":"她穿衣時聽著收音機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dressing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b7a461fefbb68e518e5","word":"drift","forms":["drift"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6906e6d2ce7b960c","term":"drift","forms":["drift","drifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主旨；大意；意圖","explanation":"指一段話、一個論證或一項行動逐漸顯出的總體走向和想表達的意思，就像葉子漂移後呈現出的方向。","examples":[{"en":"I did not understand every detail, but I got the drift of her argument.","zh":"我沒有聽懂每個細節，但明白了她論證的大意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drift of the report is that we need to act sooner.","zh":"這份報告的總體意思是，我們需要更早採取行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1022eb438072f65","term":"drift","forms":["drift","drifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"逐漸變化；漂移","explanation":"指某種狀態、數值或特徵經過較長時間一點點改變，逐漸偏離原來的位置或範圍，就像葉子被水流慢慢帶走。","examples":[{"en":"Small changes in the policy led to a gradual drift away from its original purpose.","zh":"政策中的細小變化使它逐漸偏離了最初的目的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team noticed a drift in customer preferences over several years.","zh":"團隊注意到，幾年間顧客偏好逐漸發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28d97966a748fbaa","term":"drift","forms":["drift","drifts","drifting","drifted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隨水流或氣流緩慢移動","explanation":"像被水流或風推著走的葉子一樣，緩慢地離開原來的位置，沒有明顯的主動控制。","examples":[{"en":"The boat drifted away from the shore.","zh":"小船慢慢漂離了岸邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several leaves drifted downstream with the current.","zh":"幾片樹葉隨水流漂向下游。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de8a404dbfb21b04","term":"drift","forms":["drift","drifts","drifting","drifted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漫無目的地走動或生活","explanation":"指人像沒有固定方向的葉子一樣，到處走動或輾轉生活，沒有明確目的地，也沒有穩定下來。","examples":[{"en":"He drifted from city to city for years, never really settling down.","zh":"他這些年一直從一個城市漂到另一個城市，從未真正安定下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After graduating, she had no clear plan and drifted from place to place.","zh":"畢業後，她沒有明確計劃，只是在各地漂著生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b76419d9ad059fdfdc06","word":"drill","forms":["drill"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bdd3646bb9fb918","term":"drill","forms":["drill","drills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鑽孔工具","explanation":"一種帶旋轉鑽頭、用來在木材、金屬等材料上打孔的工具，也可指相應的電動機器。","examples":[{"en":"I used a drill to make two holes in the wall.","zh":"我用電鑽在牆上打了兩個孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wear safety glasses when operating an electric drill.","zh":"操作電鑽時要戴護目鏡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d67496511a7f904b","term":"drill","forms":["drill","drills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演習；操練","explanation":"為應對未來可能發生的情況而反覆練習的一項活動，尤其常見於軍事操練、消防演習或應急演練。","examples":[{"en":"The school held a fire drill on Monday.","zh":"學校星期一舉行了消防演習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular emergency drills help staff react quickly.","zh":"定期的應急演練有助於員工迅速作出反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e84d3f0d7ee9ae44","term":"drill","forms":["drill","drills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育訓練專案","explanation":"體育訓練中為提高某項具體技能而反覆進行的短練習，例如射門、傳球或守門訓練。","examples":[{"en":"The players did passing drills before the game.","zh":"球員們在比賽前做了傳球訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach devised a catching drill using brightly colored tennis balls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e98fefd16d91ad3","term":"drill","forms":["drill","drills","drilling","drilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鑽出孔","explanation":"用鑽頭去除材料，從而在某物上形成孔；這是名詞“鑽孔工具”直接發展出的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Drill a small hole before inserting the screw.","zh":"先鑽一個小孔，再擰入螺釘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They drilled three holes in the wooden board.","zh":"他們在木板上鑽了三個孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6bd344b35e8ab135","term":"drill","forms":["drill","drills","drilling","drilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反覆操練","explanation":"為了把動作或程式練得準確而反覆練習，尤其可用於軍事操練或有固定步驟的訓練。","examples":[{"en":"The recruits drilled every morning before breakfast.","zh":"新兵們每天早飯前操練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We drilled for the evacuation exercise all week.","zh":"我們整個星期都在為疏散演習訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41adefc07f5f0993","term":"drill","forms":["drill","drills","drilling","drilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反覆灌輸","explanation":"透過不斷重複某個觀念或要點，使別人牢牢記住它；這裡保留了“反覆鑽入腦中”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents drilled into her the importance of honesty.","zh":"她的父母反覆向她灌輸誠實的重要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher drilled the safety rules into us.","zh":"老師把安全規則反覆灌輸給我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-218ae6b44966c8a9913e","word":"drink","forms":["drink"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5e16dcbc02a485b","term":"drink","forms":["drink","drinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飲料","explanation":"指可以喝的液體，如水、茶、果汁或其他飲品；重點是“供人喝的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"I’d like another drink, please.","zh":"請再給我一杯飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a cold drink waiting for each guest.","zh":"每位客人面前都放著一杯冷飲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-424fa447dd3f72bf","term":"drink","forms":["drink","drinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某種飲品","explanation":"指一種有特定配方或名稱的飲料，尤其常指調製飲品；這裡關注的是“哪一類飲料”。","examples":[{"en":"Her favourite drink is iced tea with lemon.","zh":"她最喜歡的飲品是檸檬冰茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What hot drinks does the café serve?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c16e1ca8d5c92b8e","term":"drink","forms":["drink","drinks","drinking","drank","drunk","drinked","drunken","drinken","dranken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喝液體","explanation":"把水、茶等液體透過嘴喝進身體，是最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"He drank the water I gave him.","zh":"他喝了我給他的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please drink plenty of water in hot weather.","zh":"天氣炎熱時請多喝水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3eeddeda3cb49b6e","term":"drink","forms":["drink","drinks","drinking","drank","drunk","drinked","drunken","drinken","dranken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喝酒","explanation":"不帶具體賓語時，常指飲用酒精飲料；核心仍是“把液體喝進去”，只是語境把液體限定為酒。","examples":[{"en":"You’ve been drinking, haven’t you?","zh":"你喝酒了，對吧？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My uncle stopped drinking last year.","zh":"我叔叔去年戒酒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66780f1fb0171bd83d64","word":"drip","forms":["drip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80e1dd62667b6a21","term":"drip","forms":["drip","drips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一滴液體","explanation":"指單獨的一滴液體，也可泛指液體滴落形成的少量液體。它和動詞的核心畫面相同：液體從某處一滴滴出現。","examples":[{"en":"I added a drip of vanilla extract to my hot cocoa.","zh":"我在熱可可里加了一滴香草精。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A drip of paint landed on my shoe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5fcbf63c06f2ecb","term":"drip","forms":["drip","drips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穿搭風格；派頭","explanation":"俚語中指時髦、顯眼或昂貴的服裝和整體穿搭，也可引申為由此體現出的派頭。可以把它想成身上“滴滿了”風格和好東西。","examples":[{"en":"Her drip was the best outfit at the party.","zh":"她的這身穿搭是聚會上最有派頭的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His new jacket adds serious drip to that outfit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ccf4cb450da9d1a","term":"drip","forms":["drip","drips","dripping","dripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"一滴滴落下","explanation":"指液體從某處連續地一滴滴落下，是 drip 最基本的動作畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Water was dripping from the old tap.","zh":"水正從舊水龍頭上一滴滴落下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paint dripped onto the floor.","zh":"油漆一滴滴滴到了地板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48fc693e4a4e7a18","term":"drip","forms":["drip","drips","dripping","dripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"慢慢漏出","explanation":"指容器、管道或水龍頭有小量液體緩慢漏出，強調持續而不猛烈的洩漏。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen tap is dripping again.","zh":"廚房的水龍頭又在漏水了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water dripped from a crack in the tank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7062520c5a0ea9deac82","word":"drive","forms":["drive"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01aa8a18e29909d9","term":"drive","forms":["drive","drives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動力；進取心","explanation":"這裡的 drive 是推動一個人持續努力、實現目標的內在動力，通常包含抱負、決心和行動力；它就像把人不斷推向前方的力量。","examples":[{"en":"She has the drive to build her own business.","zh":"她有創辦自己事業的進取心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His drive and determination helped the team succeed.","zh":"他的動力和決心幫助團隊取得了成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-973f8c7ba1dbbd35","term":"drive","forms":["drive","drives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"駕車出行；車程","explanation":"指乘坐或駕駛車輛進行的一次出行，也可以指這次出行所花的車程；車輛把人從一個地方推動到另一個地方。","examples":[{"en":"We went for a drive along the coast.","zh":"我們沿著海岸駕車出行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The airport is a thirty-minute drive from here.","zh":"機場距這裡有三十分鐘車程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7fbcaddd9a5ed1a","term":"drive","forms":["drive","drives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驅動器","explanation":"指計算機中負責從大容量儲存裝置讀寫資料的裝置，例如讀寫磁碟的裝置；它體現了“推動資料讀寫”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Save the files to an external drive.","zh":"把這些檔案儲存到外接驅動器中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The computer cannot detect the disk drive.","zh":"這臺計算機無法檢測到磁碟驅動器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5410aa624e5f42a","term":"drive","forms":["drive","drives","driving","drove","drave","driv","driven","druv","drivest","drovest","dravest","driveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"駕駛車輛使人或物透過某處","explanation":"抓住“推動、使前進”這個核心，指駕駛車輛，讓車載著人或物透過某個地點或路段；有時也可把所載的人或物放在括號所示的位置。","examples":[{"en":"She drove the children across the bridge before the storm arrived.","zh":"暴風雨到來前，她開車載孩子們過了橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide drove the visitors through the old town.","zh":"導遊開車載遊客穿過了老城區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4def8217cadae26d4da","word":"driver","forms":["driver"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de1b7c4e59049e57","term":"driver","forms":["driver","drivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"駕駛者；驅動者","explanation":"driver是駕駛汽車、馬車、船等交通工具，或操縱某種裝置使其執行的人。這個詞的核心概念是“讓某物動起來的人”，所以不只限於汽車司機。","examples":[{"en":"The bus driver stopped to let an elderly passenger get on.","zh":"公交車司機停車讓一位老人上車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The driver checked the truck before leaving.","zh":"駕駛員出發前檢查了卡車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/driver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ecffbc550b449b3","term":"driver","forms":["driver","drivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推動因素","explanation":"driver也可以不是人，而是促成某件事發生、發展或改變的因素。它把“推動某物前進”的具體動作擴充套件成了“推動社會、經濟或結果變化”的抽象力量。","examples":[{"en":"Lower prices have become a major driver of online shopping.","zh":"價格降低已成為網上購物增長的重要推動因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tourism is the main driver of the island's economy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/driver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da023587974e543ea8b3","word":"driveway","forms":["driveway"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e2a41bbacf3d3afe","term":"driveway","forms":["driveway","driveways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"住宅或車庫前的私人車道","explanation":"指從街道通向房屋、車庫或停車處的一小段私人道路，通常是住戶開車進出自家房產的地方。","examples":[{"en":"I left my bicycle in the driveway.","zh":"我把腳踏車放在了自家車道上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were playing in the driveway.","zh":"孩子們正在住宅前的車道上玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/driveway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e226fb022f64c23b","term":"driveway","forms":["driveway","driveways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通往特定區域的內部道路","explanation":"指進入或穿行於某個機構、院落或土地範圍內的道路，主要用於私人通行、維護或安全管理；它仍然保留了“讓車輛進入某個區域”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow driveway leads from the main road to the research center.","zh":"一條狹窄的內部道路從主幹道通往研究中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The driveway winds through the estate to the stables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/driveway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d90ee9ccf6bea1d2942a","word":"drop","forms":["drop"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31471d1317b65fec","term":"drop","forms":["drop","drops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一滴","explanation":"指一小滴液體，通常是從液體來源落下、並因表面張力保持成團的形狀；這正是“向下掉一點”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"A drop of water fell from the leaf.","zh":"一滴水從葉子上落了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add one drop of lemon juice to the tea.","zh":"往茶里加一滴檸檬汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b3075eef3b14efb","term":"drop","forms":["drop","drops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下降；減少","explanation":"指程度、質量、數量或比率向下變小，也就是把“從原來的位置向下掉一點”引申到價格、需求、溫度等數值或水平上。","examples":[{"en":"There was a sharp drop in the temperature overnight.","zh":"夜間氣溫大幅下降了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company reported a drop in sales this quarter.","zh":"公司報告說本季度銷售額有所下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd29a3e7df1f9257","term":"drop","forms":["drop","drops","dropping","dropped","dropt","droppest","droppedst","droppeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"落下","explanation":"人或物受重力影響，從空中或較高處直直地向下落；核心畫面就是從原來的位置向下掉一點。","examples":[{"en":"The glass slipped from her hand and dropped onto the floor.","zh":"玻璃杯從她手裡滑落，掉到了地板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaves dropped from the tree in the wind.","zh":"樹葉在風中從樹上飄落下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90a8723979346abf","term":"drop","forms":["drop","drops","dropping","dropped","dropt","droppest","droppedst","droppeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使落下或放下","explanation":"表示鬆手、失去抓握，或主動把某物放開，讓它向下掉；也可用於命令某人放下武器。核心仍是讓東西從原來的位置向下。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful not to drop the phone.","zh":"小心別把手機掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer told him to drop the knife.","zh":"警察叫他放下刀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-caaed8c4eb8dfedde10e","word":"drought","forms":["drought"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-face43d2cee5e040","term":"drought","forms":["drought","droughts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乾旱期","explanation":"指一段異常少雨、持續時間較長且比普通短暫乾燥更嚴重的時期。它常影響農田、供水和當地生活，核心畫面就是“土地長時間沒有得到足夠的水”。","examples":[{"en":"The region has suffered a severe drought this year.","zh":"這個地區今年遭遇了嚴重的乾旱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers are struggling to protect their crops during the drought.","zh":"乾旱期間，農民正努力保護莊稼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drought","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-543a259eaf8325d8","term":"drought","forms":["drought","droughts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長期未成功","explanation":"把“長時間沒有水”借來比喻“長時間沒有成功”。在體育等語境中，它尤其常指球隊或運動員很久沒有獲勝、得分或奪冠。","examples":[{"en":"The team ended its five-year drought with a dramatic win.","zh":"這支球隊用一場戲劇性的勝利結束了五年的無冠期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The striker finally ended his scoring drought.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drought","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-476342b3553fe919674e","word":"drown","forms":["drown"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-111e6c892727278e","term":"drown","forms":["drown","drowns","drowning","drowned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"溺水而死","explanation":"指人在水或其他液體中無法呼吸，最後因窒息而死。主語是遭遇溺水的人或動物，重點是“自己沉入其中並因此死亡”。","examples":[{"en":"The child drowned in the lake.","zh":"那個孩子溺死在湖裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I nearly drowned when the boat overturned.","zh":"船翻了以後，我差點溺水身亡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23b08073d881b421","term":"drown","forms":["drown","drowns","drowning","drowned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"被淹沒；被壓垮","explanation":"先是水把人或物完全蓋住，後來也可指人被工作、資訊、問題等大量事物壓得應付不過來。它保留了“陷在太多東西里、幾乎無法脫身”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I’m drowning in emails this morning.","zh":"我今天早上被一大堆郵件壓得應接不暇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The office was drowning in unanswered complaints.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8978c132949a4dba6232","word":"drowsy","forms":["drowsy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a7ce9a5c5c2d4cb","term":"drowsy","forms":["drowsy","drowsier","drowsiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"睏倦的；昏昏欲睡的","explanation":"指人眼皮發沉、注意力變弱，已經很想睡但通常還沒有睡著。這是 drowsy 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I felt drowsy after lunch, so I took a short walk.","zh":"午飯後我感到昏昏欲睡，所以出去走了一小會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medicine may make you drowsy.","zh":"這種藥可能會讓你犯困。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drowsy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41bb8dc7fd7c0185","term":"drowsy","forms":["drowsy","drowsier","drowsiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"使人犯困的；催眠般的","explanation":"形容溫暖、安靜或節奏緩慢的環境和時段，使人自然放鬆併產生睡意。這裡不是說環境自己“困”，而是說它讓人困。","examples":[{"en":"We spent a drowsy summer afternoon by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個令人昏昏欲睡的夏日午後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drowsy hum of the fan lulled me asleep.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drowsy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4a85a7509a0a75611ef","word":"drug","forms":["drug"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8051dc74b0fe771b","term":"drug","forms":["drug","drugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥物","explanation":"用於治療疾病、緩解症狀，或有目的地改變人體內化學過程的物質。它可以是處方藥，也可以是泛指的醫學用藥。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor prescribed a drug to control her blood pressure.","zh":"醫生開了一種控制她血壓的藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This drug can reduce pain and fever.","zh":"這種藥可以緩解疼痛和退燒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0993d0b7423ba034","term":"drug","forms":["drug","drugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毒品；娛樂性精神活性物質","explanation":"指為獲得興奮或其他精神體驗而使用的物質，通常暗含非法、危險或容易成癮的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The police found drugs in his car.","zh":"警察在他的車裡發現了毒品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became addicted to drugs in his twenties.","zh":"他二十多歲時染上了毒癮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-413251444cd784fa","term":"drug","forms":["drug","drugs","drugging","drugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給人下迷藥","explanation":"在對方不知道或不同意的情況下給對方使用會使人產生精神或身體影響的毒品，使其狀態發生改變。","examples":[{"en":"She felt dizzy and realized that someone had drugged her.","zh":"她感到頭暈，意識到有人給她下了藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captors drugged the guard before escaping.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed015c0da936c7fe924d","word":"drugstore","forms":["drugstore"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d362a5415962a4a9","term":"drugstore","forms":["drugstore","drugstores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥店；兼售日用品的商店","explanation":"drugstore 是以藥房為核心、同時出售日常用品的小商店。除了買處方藥或非處方藥，人們也可能在那裡買洗漱用品、化妝品、零食等。","examples":[{"en":"I’m going to the drugstore to pick up some cold medicine.","zh":"我要去藥店買些感冒藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There’s a drugstore across the street that sells snacks and toiletries.","zh":"街對面有一家藥店，也賣零食和洗漱用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drugstore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2752a2b5446f68dd231e","word":"drum","forms":["drum"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9181242f1bf44b13","term":"drum","forms":["drum","drums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼓","explanation":"鼓是一種中空的打擊樂器，至少一端蒙著薄膜，敲擊後讓內部空氣共鳴發聲。","examples":[{"en":"She plays the drums in a jazz band.","zh":"她在爵士樂隊裡打鼓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children took turns beating a drum.","zh":"孩子們輪流敲鼓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51692b6f2badb52f","term":"drum","forms":["drum","drums","drumming","drummed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敲鼓","explanation":"作動詞時，drum 最直接地表示敲鼓、打鼓，即用連續的敲擊讓鼓發聲。","examples":[{"en":"He drummed softly while the singer warmed up.","zh":"歌手開嗓時，他輕輕地打著鼓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She drums in a jazz band every Friday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05b8b79eea5088487f03","word":"drunk","forms":["drunk"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ac15b6927d57807","term":"drunk","forms":["drunk","drunker","drunkest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"喝醉的","explanation":"指因喝了過量酒而失去平時的清醒和控制力；重點是“處於醉酒狀態”，不單指喝過酒。","examples":[{"en":"He was too drunk to find his way home.","zh":"他醉得連回家的路都找不到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I got drunk at the party and apologized the next morning.","zh":"我在聚會上喝醉了，第二天早上道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drunk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71e204e2d212acaa","term":"drunk","forms":["drunk","drunks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醉漢；喝醉的人","explanation":"指當時處於醉酒狀態的人，重點是這個人已經醉了，而不是單純喜歡喝酒的人。","examples":[{"en":"A drunk was sleeping on the bench outside the station.","zh":"一個醉漢睡在車站外的長椅上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bartender refused to serve another drink to the drunk.","zh":"酒保拒絕再給那個醉漢上酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drunk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-b755cb248c3c4a7d94f8","word":"dry","forms":["dry"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-befc1398a1a3c299","term":"dry","forms":["dry","drier","dryer","driest","dryest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"乾的；不溼的","explanation":"東西里的水分被拿走了，或本來就沒有水分，所以摸起來不溼；這是 dry 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please make sure the dishes are completely dry before you put them away.","zh":"請先確認碗碟完全乾了再收起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My shoes are still wet, so I can't wear them until they dry.","zh":"我的鞋還溼著，得等它們幹了才能穿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b750a785296d28f5","term":"dry","forms":["dry","drier","dryer","driest","dryest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不含酒精的；戒酒的","explanation":"酒精這一類“液體”被拿走了：dry 可以形容不供應酒的場所，也可以形容一個人暫時或長期不喝酒。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel has a dry bar, but guests can still order soft drinks.","zh":"這家酒店的酒吧不供應酒，但客人仍可點無酒精飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been dry for two years and feels much healthier.","zh":"她戒酒兩年了，感覺健康多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf121d539cb404e8","term":"dry","forms":["dry","dries","drying","dried","driest","drieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變幹","explanation":"水分被拿走後，物體本身逐漸變得不溼，就是 dry。這個用法強調變化過程或結果，不表示有人主動把它弄乾。","examples":[{"en":"Leave the dishes on the rack until they dry.","zh":"把盤子放在瀝水架上，直到它們變幹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road dried quickly after the rain stopped.","zh":"雨停後，道路很快就幹了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f2c6baa47993a1b","term":"dry","forms":["dry","dries","drying","dried","driest","drieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄乾","explanation":"把水分從某物上拿走，使它變幹，就是 dry something；例如用毛巾擦去眼淚或擦乾身體。","examples":[{"en":"Please dry your hands before you touch the baby.","zh":"請先把手擦乾，再碰寶寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dried the wet floor with a clean towel.","zh":"她用乾淨的毛巾把溼地板擦乾了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-386841164098fe3272c4","word":"dryer","forms":["dryer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec00827083d5e084","term":"dryer","forms":["dryer","dryers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乾燥裝置或乾燥劑","explanation":"指能除去水分或溼氣的人、裝置、設施或物質；太陽和風也可以在較寬泛的語境中被稱為幫助乾燥的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The warm air acts as a dryer for the wet paper.","zh":"暖空氣起到了烘乾溼紙的作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The industrial dryer removes moisture from the grain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dryer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ce3d6ac01370a29","term":"dryer","forms":["dryer","dryers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣物烘乾機","explanation":"在日常生活中，dryer 最常作為 clothes dryer 或 tumble dryer 的簡稱，指用熱風或轉動把衣物烘乾的機器。","examples":[{"en":"I put the wet clothes in the dryer before dinner.","zh":"我在晚飯前把溼衣服放進了烘乾機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The towels are still tumbling in the dryer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dryer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ccf2f9e9cc41e7ad5bf","word":"dual","forms":["dual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f06f264d6e9e3cc3","term":"dual","forms":["dual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由兩個部分組成的","explanation":"表示某個東西由兩個通常相互配合或相等的部分組成，重點是“成對構成一個整體”。","examples":[{"en":"This dual-motor vehicle can climb steep hills.","zh":"這輛雙電機車輛能爬上陡峭的山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camera has a dual-lens system.","zh":"這臺相機採用雙鏡頭系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-977686a0319045e1","term":"dual","forms":["dual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與兩個或一對有關的","explanation":"表示某事涉及兩個物件或一對物件，不一定說明它們組成一個裝置或整體。","examples":[{"en":"The plane suffered a dual engine failure.","zh":"這架飛機的兩個發動機都發生了故障。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She holds dual citizenship through her parents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2da310051c9f4a25c5a8","word":"dubious","forms":["dubious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dffa706adfa10065","term":"dubious","forms":["dubious","more dubious","most dubious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可疑的；難以信服的","explanation":"形容某件事、某種說法或某份證據讓人覺得不可靠，因而無法完全相信。重點不是已經證明它是假的，而是它留下了足夠的疑點。","examples":[{"en":"The report was based on dubious evidence.","zh":"這份報告建立在可疑的證據之上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He made some dubious claims about the product.","zh":"他對這款產品提出了一些令人懷疑的說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dubious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c5fa37a8b5a9481","term":"dubious","forms":["dubious","more dubious","most dubious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"將信將疑的；拿不準的","explanation":"形容人對某個計劃、解釋或結果沒有把握，心裡在相信和懷疑之間搖擺。它強調暫時的猶豫，不表示這個人已經明確反對。","examples":[{"en":"She was dubious about the plan at first.","zh":"她起初對這個計劃將信將疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looked dubious when he promised immediate results.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dubious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d2370db2447ff8cf4f3","word":"duck","forms":["duck"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0757df8b8faec5a7","term":"duck","forms":["duck","ducks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鴨子","explanation":"指有扁嘴和蹼足、生活在水邊或水中的鴨類鳥；記住“鴨子會潛水”，有助於聯絡動詞duck的“低下去、鑽下去”。","examples":[{"en":"A duck was swimming across the pond.","zh":"一隻鴨子正遊過池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children watched the ducks by the lake.","zh":"孩子們看著湖邊的鴨子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c5369213a5a3c32","term":"duck","forms":["duck","ducks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鴨肉","explanation":"指作為食物的鴨子的肉；這是從“鴨子”這一基本概念延伸出的食物用法。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered roast duck with pancakes.","zh":"我們點了烤鴨和薄餅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Duck is often served with a sweet sauce.","zh":"鴨肉常配甜味醬汁食用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-344b08b94523bf33","term":"duck","forms":["duck","ducks","ducking","ducked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"低頭或彎身躲避","explanation":"指為了避開迎面而來的東西而迅速低下頭或彎下身體；可以把它記成“低下去、鑽下去”。","examples":[{"en":"She ducked her head as the branch swung toward her.","zh":"樹枝向她擺來時，她趕緊低下了頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Duck! The ball is coming this way.","zh":"快低頭！球朝這邊飛來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f786f9835a201ce6","term":"duck","forms":["duck","ducks","ducking","ducked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逃避責任","explanation":"引申為設法躲開本應承擔的責任、任務或要求，就像把自己“低下去”藏開一樣。","examples":[{"en":"You cannot duck your responsibilities forever.","zh":"你不可能永遠逃避自己的責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager tried to duck the question about the missing money.","zh":"經理試圖迴避關於那筆失蹤款項的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-458a4770df2b51b57769","word":"due","forms":["due"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b92ba404960b771c","term":"due","forms":["due","more due","most due"],"pos":"adj","zh":"應付的；欠著的","explanation":"表示某人應當支付、歸還或獲得某物，重點是這件事已經成為應盡的義務或應得的權益。","examples":[{"en":"He is due four weeks of back pay.","zh":"他應得四周的補發工資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers are due their wages on Friday.","zh":"工人們應在星期五拿到工資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/due","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28b7dc5f129d8377","term":"due","forms":["due","more due","most due"],"pos":"adj","zh":"預定的；預計要來的","explanation":"表示某事按照安排或預期應該在某個時間發生，常用於交通工具、天氣、付款或其他即將發生的事件。","examples":[{"en":"The train is due at six o’clock.","zh":"火車預計六點到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report is due to be published next month.","zh":"這份報告預計下個月釋出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/due","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9740836d46f3e8cb","term":"due","forms":["due","more due","most due"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由於；歸因於","explanation":"用於說明某種結果或狀態應歸因於某個原因，相當於“由於、因為”。這裡的due不是“欠”，而是把結果歸到一個原因上。","examples":[{"en":"The delay was due to heavy traffic.","zh":"延誤是由於交通擁堵造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plant’s success is largely due to careful planning.","zh":"這家公司的成功很大程度上歸功於周密的規劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/due","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f5b8fed06c1411b","term":"due","forms":["due","dues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"應付之物；債務；責任","explanation":"指某人欠下的東西、依法或按道德應履行的責任，或某人有權要求得到的份額；它延續了“該歸位、該履行”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The company paid what was due under the contract.","zh":"公司支付了合同規定應付的款項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even if you dislike him, you should give the devil his due.","zh":"即使你不喜歡他，也應該承認他應得的那份讚譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/due","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f68ea0282db37900c1a","word":"dull","forms":["dull"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71c6abe81b6598b7","term":"dull","forms":["dull","duller","dullest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不鋒利的","explanation":"指刀、剪刀等邊緣不再容易切開東西，像磨損後失去了原來的鋒利感。","examples":[{"en":"These kitchen knives are too dull to cut the tomatoes cleanly.","zh":"這些廚刀太鈍了，沒法利落地切番茄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sharpened the dull blade before cooking.","zh":"做飯前我把鈍了的刀刃磨利了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85ce5604bf6b76c6","term":"dull","forms":["dull","duller","dullest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無聊乏味的","explanation":"指活動、談話或內容缺少趣味和刺激，讓人難以投入，彷彿燈光變暗後什麼都不吸引人。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting was so dull that several people checked their phones.","zh":"會議無聊得讓好幾個人都拿出手機看了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found the book dull after the first few chapters.","zh":"讀了頭幾章後，我覺得這本書很乏味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04501eb5b9604ed2","term":"dull","forms":["dull","duller","dullest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"暗淡無光的","explanation":"指表面沒有明亮的光澤，呈啞光或灰暗效果；這裡是光澤變弱，而不是顏色一定變成黑色。","examples":[{"en":"The old silver has a dull surface instead of a bright shine.","zh":"這塊舊銀器表面暗淡，沒有明亮的光澤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Polish restored the dull silver to its original shine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c35907f6d12c05e","term":"dull","forms":["dull","dulls","dulling","dulled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變鈍","explanation":"指讓刀刃或其他鋒利邊緣失去切割力，是把“失去鋒利”主動作用到某物上。","examples":[{"en":"Cutting cardboard quickly dulled the scissors.","zh":"剪硬紙板很快就把剪刀弄鈍了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cutting wire dulled the blade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cca69d1534ecb2b8","term":"dull","forms":["dull","dulls","dulling","dulled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"減弱；緩解","explanation":"指把疼痛、情緒或感覺的強度壓低，使它不再那麼尖銳，像把燈光調暗一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The medicine dulled the pain but did not remove it completely.","zh":"藥物減輕了疼痛，但沒有把它完全消除。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He turned on music to dull his anxiety.","zh":"他開啟音樂來緩解焦慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac996ae492f9a987c84f","word":"dumb","forms":["dumb"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c312ae35d24b4748","term":"dumb","forms":["dumb","dumber","dumbest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愚蠢的","explanation":"指人缺乏判斷力或理解力；也常作為直接的侮辱，表示“你真蠢”。它和“沒有思考、沒有反應”的核心形象相連。","examples":[{"en":"I was dumb enough to leave my keys inside the locked car.","zh":"我蠢到把鑰匙留在了鎖上的車裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be dumb—check the address before you leave.","zh":"別犯傻，出發前先檢查地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f14092fbf1455ac","term":"dumb","forms":["dumb","dumber","dumbest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"荒唐的；沒意義的","explanation":"形容計劃、規則或情況缺乏道理和價值，重點不是某個人笨，而是事情本身很蠢、很不合理。","examples":[{"en":"Taking the long way around was a dumb idea.","zh":"繞遠路走是個很荒唐的主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This rule is dumb because it wastes everyone's time.","zh":"這條規定很沒意義，因為它浪費所有人的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6ca0868bca6a2926b70","word":"dump","forms":["dump"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cb2ff132278ebeb","term":"dump","forms":["dump","dumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"垃圾傾倒場","explanation":"指集中傾倒垃圾、灰燼或其他廢棄物的地方，也就是把東西“嘩啦一下倒出去”後堆放的場所。","examples":[{"en":"The city is planning to close the toxic waste dump.","zh":"這座城市計劃關閉那個有毒廢物傾倒場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gulls circled above the dump while trucks unloaded household waste.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3825699a5c9ccc8a","term":"dump","forms":["dump","dumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低落憂鬱的情緒","explanation":"通常用複數表示悲傷、憂鬱、無精打采的狀態；這種情緒像被某種力量一下子“倒落”到低處。","examples":[{"en":"She has been in the dumps since her team lost.","zh":"她支援的隊輸掉後，她一直情緒低落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He's been down in the dumps since the cancellation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70fd7a4fee179aba","term":"dump","forms":["dump","dumps","dumping","dumped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"丟掉；處理掉","explanation":"指把不再想要或不再需要的東西扔掉、處理掉，畫面就是把它倒出去，不再留在手邊。","examples":[{"en":"We dumped the broken furniture before moving into the new apartment.","zh":"我們搬進新公寓前把壞掉的傢俱扔掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't dump your old clothes beside the recycling bins.","zh":"請不要把舊衣服扔在回收箱旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a92244a8d146847","term":"dump","forms":["dump","dumps","dumping","dumped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"甩掉戀人","explanation":"口語中指主動結束戀愛關係、甩掉戀人，帶有把對方從自己生活中推開的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Maya dumped her boyfriend after he lied to her again.","zh":"男朋友再次對瑪雅撒謊後，她和他分手了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was devastated when his partner dumped him by text.","zh":"伴侶發簡訊和他分手時，他受到了沉重打擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32e382dfb93f0f3f26f7","word":"dumpling","forms":["dumpling"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"dumpling","forms":["dumpling"],"pos":"n.","zh":"餃子；麵糰類食物","examples":[{"en":"She placed a steamed dumpling in my bowl.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"This dumpling has a filling of pork and cabbage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-54dab9eb6d3204a0b428","word":"durable","forms":["durable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4433496c271ca62","term":"durable","forms":["durable","more durable","most durable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"耐用的；持久的","explanation":"指某物不容易因使用、時間或自然作用而損壞、衰敗，因此能保持很久；也可以把這個“撐得久”的意思用於關係等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"These boots are durable enough for daily use.","zh":"這雙靴子很耐用，足以應付日常使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They built a durable friendship during their years at school.","zh":"他們在求學期間建立了持久的友誼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/durable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-caa79af4db67695cce51","word":"duration","forms":["duration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26c9e23083ac3c1a","term":"duration","forms":["duration","durations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持續時間；時長","explanation":"指一件事從開始到結束所佔的時間長度，也就是那條“時間帶”有多長。它可以是幾分鐘、幾小時，也可以是更長的時期。","examples":[{"en":"The duration of the flight is about three hours.","zh":"這趟航班的飛行時間大約是三個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course has a duration of six weeks.","zh":"這門課程為期六週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7a9e45e01906e16","term":"duration","forms":["duration","durations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整個持續期間","explanation":"指當前事件、局勢或狀態持續到結束的整段時間，重點不是這段時間具體有多長，而是“在它持續的這段時間裡”。","examples":[{"en":"Visitors must remain inside for the duration of the storm.","zh":"暴風雨持續期間，訪客必須留在室內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge stayed closed for the duration of the repairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-76678e40cf8bdb8a8350","word":"during","forms":["during"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c48b3e725e4122f","term":"during","forms":["during"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在整個期間","explanation":"表示事情發生在所說時間段的全過程或大部分時間裡，相當於把整個時間段當作背景。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is closed during the winter.","zh":"這家博物館冬季期間閉館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep your phone silent during the performance.","zh":"演出期間請將手機調為靜音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/during","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-900d90fafc612052","term":"during","forms":["during"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在期間的某個時候","explanation":"表示某事發生在一個較長時間段中的某個時刻或某些時刻，不必貫穿整個期間。","examples":[{"en":"I received several calls during the afternoon.","zh":"下午期間我接到了幾通電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone called during the final scene.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/during","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29aef83195b27118a6c6","word":"dusk","forms":["dusk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f99dfbff91a4f7b","term":"dusk","forms":["dusk","dusks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黃昏；暮色","explanation":"指太陽落下以後、天空還留有一些光的時段。它正是“光線逐漸褪去”的核心畫面，也是 dusk 最重要、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We reached the village at dusk.","zh":"我們在黃昏時到達了村子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The birds become quiet at dusk.","zh":"鳥兒在黃昏時安靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-abb32701117d50a93f8f","word":"dust","forms":["dust"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-978ac36e3978963a","term":"dust","forms":["dust","dusts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"塵土；細小顆粒","explanation":"dust 是由許多細小、乾燥顆粒組成的塵土或粉末，常落在地面、傢俱或物體表面，也可能飄在空氣中。抓住“細小乾燥顆粒”這個核心，就能理解它為什麼會積在表面或在作業中揚起。","examples":[{"en":"A thick layer of dust covered the old books.","zh":"舊書上覆蓋著厚厚一層塵土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers wore masks because the dry soil created a lot of dust.","zh":"工人們戴著口罩，因為乾燥的土壤揚起了很多塵土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5d9d825105fa78e","term":"dust","forms":["dust","dusts","dusting","dusted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……除塵","explanation":"把傢俱、表面或物品上的細小塵土擦掉，也就是把落下的顆粒清除乾淨。","examples":[{"en":"I dust the bookshelves every Saturday.","zh":"我每週六給書架除塵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She dusted the old lamp before putting it on the desk.","zh":"她把那盞舊檯燈除塵後放到了書桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa5084181807c259","term":"dust","forms":["dust","dusts","dusting","dusted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撒粉或噴灑","explanation":"把細小的粉末或液體覆蓋到某物表面，就像把細小顆粒撒上去或噴上去。","examples":[{"en":"Dust the cake with a little cocoa before serving it.","zh":"上桌前，在蛋糕上撒一點可可粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse dusted the baby's skin with powder.","zh":"護士在嬰兒的皮膚上撒了些粉末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9985c202d7aa32672eb2","word":"dusty","forms":["dusty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce7afce0026ba0c1","term":"dusty","forms":["dusty","dustier","dustiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"蒙著灰塵的","explanation":"指表面覆蓋了灰塵，通常是因為很久沒有清潔或使用。這個意義最直接地保留了“灰塵落在東西上”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The attic was full of dusty boxes.","zh":"閣樓裡堆滿了蒙著灰塵的箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wiped the dusty table before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前我擦了擦滿是灰塵的桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5bd05a8aa8f9f83","term":"dusty","forms":["dusty","dustier","dustiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粉狀的；像灰塵的","explanation":"指質地或外觀像細灰塵一樣，容易散開或呈細粉末狀；重點不一定是表面真的落了灰。","examples":[{"en":"The old road was covered in a dusty white powder.","zh":"那條舊路上覆蓋著一層灰白色的粉末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dusty coating of flour covered the workbench.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9bb09914b117aaa92837","word":"duty","forms":["duty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b674ffe03904c684","term":"duty","forms":["duty","duties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"責任；義務","explanation":"指一個人根據道德、法律、身份或承諾而應該完成的事，也就是“該由你承擔的那份任務”。它可以是抽象的責任，也可以是具體的一項義務。","examples":[{"en":"It is our duty to protect the children.","zh":"保護孩子是我們的責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She did her duty and reported the problem.","zh":"她盡到了自己的責任，報告了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98943b49298a1f6b","term":"duty","forms":["duty","duties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"值班；執勤狀態","explanation":"指正在工作並負責某項任務的狀態。一個人“在 duty 上”就是在值班、執勤或負責當班工作。","examples":[{"en":"A doctor is on duty at the clinic tonight.","zh":"今晚診所有一名醫生值班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please call the officer on duty.","zh":"請聯絡當班的警員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a283fd012b06e2e7d4e","word":"dwarf","forms":["dwarf"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddc69c2e5143d77a","term":"dwarf","forms":["dwarf","dwarfs","dwarves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神話中的矮人","explanation":"指歐洲尤其是北歐、日耳曼傳說中的矮小人形生物，通常被描寫為擅長鍛造和製作工藝品，並擁有某些超自然能力。","examples":[{"en":"The dwarves forged a sword beneath the mountain.","zh":"矮人在山下鍛造了一把劍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young dwarf led the travelers through his underground kingdom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwarf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a715b67188ba6707","term":"dwarf","forms":["dwarf","dwarfs","dwarfing","dwarfed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使顯得很小","explanation":"指某物在大小或規模上遠遠超過另一物，從而把另一物襯得很小，就像巨大的建築把周圍建築變成了“矮小者”。","examples":[{"en":"The new stadium dwarfs every other building nearby.","zh":"新體育場把附近其他建築都襯得很小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child was dwarfed by the huge statue.","zh":"那座巨大的雕像把孩子襯得十分渺小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwarf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72d8d10863238361fc2c","word":"dwell","forms":["dwell"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-483d8008a0a8f3e0","term":"dwell","forms":["dwell","dwells","dwelling","dwelt","dwelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"居住","explanation":"指住在某個地方，強調持續在那裡生活，而不是短暫到訪。現代英語中這個說法偏文學或正式。","examples":[{"en":"The poet dwelled in a small village by the sea.","zh":"那位詩人居住在海邊的一個小村莊裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several families dwell in the valley throughout winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75fd67452ccbea98","term":"dwell","forms":["dwell","dwells","dwelling","dwelt","dwelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反覆糾纏於","explanation":"指人的思想或注意力長時間停留在某件事上，尤其是過去的錯誤、壞訊息或令人煩惱的問題，常帶有“不必再想了”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Try not to dwell on your mistake; focus on what you can do now.","zh":"儘量別再糾結於你的錯誤，把注意力放在現在能做的事上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kept dwelling on the argument long after it was over.","zh":"爭吵結束很久後，她還一直糾結於那件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a280f846c1a56aa8ca00","word":"dwelling","forms":["dwelling"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c6e8ce05c41b8242","term":"dwelling","forms":["dwelling","dwellings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"住所；住宅","explanation":"dwelling 是人實際居住的地方，可以是房屋，也可以泛指居所；它強調“供人住的地方”這一功能。","examples":[{"en":"The small cottage became their first dwelling in the countryside.","zh":"那座小屋成了他們在鄉下的第一處住所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old house served as a dwelling for Albert.","zh":"那棟老房子成了阿爾伯特的住所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwelling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6f82976b5f02c538cd1","word":"dye","forms":["dye"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7bde6986a4499d4","term":"dye","forms":["dye","dyes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"染料","explanation":"dye 是能附著或滲入布料等材料、使其變色的著色物質。它強調“用來染色的東西”，不是染色這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"This dye is made from walnut shells.","zh":"這種染料是用核桃殼製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a dye for synthetic fabric.","zh":"我們需要一種用於合成布料的染料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dye","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1c37d6a8f3503ab","term":"dye","forms":["dye","dyes","dyeing","dying","dyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"染色；染成某色","explanation":"dye 作動詞時，就是把染料用於頭髮、布料等，使它們變成新的顏色；也可以描述彷彿被顏色染上的效果。它和名詞 dye 共享“顏色進入材料”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She dyed her hair red for the summer.","zh":"她把頭髮染成了紅色，準備迎接夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fabric was dyed by hand.","zh":"這塊布是手工染的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dye","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-73c76d56fd4042001a19","word":"dynamic","forms":["dynamic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ec4d70a275942df","term":"dynamic","forms":["dynamic","more dynamic","most dynamic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"動態的；不斷變化的","explanation":"形容環境、局面或系統不是固定不動的，而是在持續運動、發展和改變。它像一臺一直運轉的發動機，變化本身就是特點。","examples":[{"en":"The city has a dynamic arts scene that changes every year.","zh":"這座城市的藝術氛圍充滿活力，而且每年都在變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We work in a dynamic industry where new tools appear constantly.","zh":"我們所在的行業變化不斷，新工具層出不窮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynamic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53e70f912fe51ab6","term":"dynamic","forms":["dynamic","more dynamic","most dynamic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有活力的；富有感染力的","explanation":"形容人、演講或表現時，表示精力充沛、行動有力，能吸引並帶動別人。這裡的“力量”主要體現為氣勢和感染力，而不是體力大小。","examples":[{"en":"She is a dynamic leader who motivates the whole team.","zh":"她是一位充滿活力的領導者，能激勵整個團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dynamic teacher transformed the struggling drama club.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynamic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05f612cafca00ebe","term":"dynamic","forms":["dynamic","more dynamic","most dynamic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能變化並適應的","explanation":"強調某人、組織或系統能夠根據新情況調整自己，而不是固守原來的形式。它是“動態”的進一步含義：不僅在變化，而且能跟著變化運轉下去。","examples":[{"en":"The company needs a dynamic plan that can respond to changing demand.","zh":"公司需要一套能應對需求變化的靈活計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dynamic timetable adjusts when new bookings arrive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynamic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-813cf1ca6462bbb705fb","word":"dynasty","forms":["dynasty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7a60bb60ab8d487","term":"dynasty","forms":["dynasty","dynasties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"世襲統治家族","explanation":"指同一家族連續幾代產生統治者，形成一條延續的統治家系。重點不在某一位君主，而在家族接力般地掌權。","examples":[{"en":"The Tudor dynasty ruled England for more than a century.","zh":"都鐸王朝統治英格蘭長達一個多世紀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Ottoman dynasty produced many powerful sultans.","zh":"奧斯曼王朝產生過許多強大的蘇丹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d750cf348afd4a0b","term":"dynasty","forms":["dynasty","dynasties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王朝時期或政權","explanation":"指某個統治家族掌權時形成的政權或歷史時期，也就是這面家族旗幟覆蓋的整個時代，而不僅是家族成員本身。","examples":[{"en":"During the Ming dynasty, the capital was moved to Beijing.","zh":"明朝時期，首都遷到了北京。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city flourished under the Tang dynasty.","zh":"這座城市在唐朝統治下繁榮起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bec1687971e36be51a29","word":"each","forms":["each"],"officialPos":"pron./adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f92f5bd7de6f787","term":"each","forms":["each"],"pos":"adv","zh":"各自；分別","explanation":"放在複數主語或代詞之後，表示同一個動作或狀態分別適用於群體中的每個成員，強調個體而不是集體一起行動。","examples":[{"en":"We each brought a small gift.","zh":"我們每個人都帶了一份小禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two children each chose a book.","zh":"兩個孩子各自選了一本書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/each","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ddb56b17679c10e7","term":"each","forms":["each"],"pos":"det","zh":"每一個","explanation":"指所說範圍內的所有成員，但把它們看成一個個獨立的個體；因此既包含“全都”的範圍，又強調“逐個”的視角。","examples":[{"en":"Each student received a certificate.","zh":"每個學生都收到了一張證書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check each page carefully.","zh":"請仔細檢查每一頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/each","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5dca96ca80be8dfd","term":"each","forms":["each"],"pos":"pron","zh":"每一個；各自的那個","explanation":"不重複名詞，直接指群體中的每一個人或物，表示它們被一個一個地處理、給予或選擇。","examples":[{"en":"I gave each of them a map.","zh":"我給他們每個人都發了一張地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each received a handwritten letter of thanks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/each","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ca0c5ea4a249dfcba50","word":"eager","forms":["eager"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7dcd7bff19f23fd","term":"eager","forms":["eager","more eager","eagerer","most eager","eagerest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"渴望；迫不及待","explanation":"形容一個人非常想做某事或得到某物，心情積極而急切，彷彿已經向目標衝過去了。","examples":[{"en":"Stacey is eager to go cycling this weekend.","zh":"史泰茜迫不及待地想在這個週末去騎腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were eager for the doors to open.","zh":"孩子們急切地盼著門開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eager","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60115c4f218594bd","term":"eager","forms":["eager","more eager","eagerer","most eager","eagerest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"立即計算的","explanation":"在計算機或數學語境中，指系統馬上計算結果，不等到真正需要結果時才計算；這裡的“急切”變成了“不延遲”。","examples":[{"en":"This language uses eager evaluation for function arguments.","zh":"這種語言會立即計算函式引數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eager evaluation strategy computes each argument immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eager","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e73b48f750be953532c1","word":"eagle","forms":["eagle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0354318a3606e2a","term":"eagle","forms":["eagle","eagles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鷹","explanation":"eagle 指鷹科中體型較大、以肉類或腐肉為食的猛禽，給人的典型印象是喙彎曲有力、視力敏銳。它是這個詞最基本的形象，也構成了許多比喻和專名義項的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"We watched an eagle circle above the valley.","zh":"我們看著一隻鷹在山谷上空盤旋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eagle has sharp eyesight and powerful claws.","zh":"鷹有敏銳的視力和有力的爪子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eagle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa09290ced63cc59","term":"eagle","forms":["eagle","eagles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高爾夫低於標準桿兩杆","explanation":"在高爾夫中，eagle 指一洞打出低於該洞標準桿兩杆的成績。這個詞延續了鷹迅速飛越球場的形象，表示一次非常出色的表現。","examples":[{"en":"Maya made an eagle on the par-five ninth hole.","zh":"瑪雅在標準桿五杆的第九洞打出了低於標準桿兩杆的成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two strokes below par earned her an eagle and the tournament lead.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eagle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c6a36b640fceaa873f0","word":"ear","forms":["ear"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e6297a9ef4b743d","term":"ear","forms":["ear","ears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耳朵","explanation":"指人或動物用來聽聲音的器官，包括外部部分和內部聽覺結構。","examples":[{"en":"The child covered his ears when the alarm went off.","zh":"警報響起時，孩子捂住了耳朵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She whispered something in my ear.","zh":"她在我耳邊低聲說了些什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1450fbf46882a72c","term":"ear","forms":["ear","ears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聽覺；鑑賞力","explanation":"指接收聲音的能力，也可指對音樂或聲音細節的敏銳感覺，因此“有一雙好耳朵”可以表示很會聽、很有音樂鑑賞力。","examples":[{"en":"He has a good ear for accents.","zh":"他很會辨別不同的口音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Maya has an excellent ear for music.","zh":"瑪雅有很強的音樂鑑賞力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f408830bcc7fab370819","word":"early","forms":["early"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a84223ebd82699a4","term":"early","forms":["early","earlier","earliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"提前的；較早的","explanation":"表示某事發生在通常時間或預期時間之前，例如提前吃飯、年紀很小時開始做某事，或過早去世。核心畫面是事件在日程線上向前移。","examples":[{"en":"We had an early dinner because the children were tired.","zh":"孩子們累了，所以我們很早就吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed an early interest in science.","zh":"她很早就對科學產生了興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/early","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-799dad0ad0cb4e36","term":"early","forms":["early","earlier","earliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清早的；一大早的","explanation":"特指一天開始後的早些時候，常表示現在還太早，人還沒有完全清醒。它是“時間線在一天開頭”的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"It’s too early for a phone call; everyone is still asleep.","zh":"現在打電話還太早，大家都還在睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I usually exercise early in the morning.","zh":"我通常一大早鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/early","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc297b5d8c908393","term":"early","forms":["early","earlier","earliest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"提前；早些時候","explanation":"表示動作在預定或通常時間之前完成、發生或結束。核心仍是把動作在時間線上向前移動，例如提前離開、早早完成。","examples":[{"en":"We finished early, so we went home before dark.","zh":"我們提前完成了，所以天黑前就回家了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please come early if you want a good seat.","zh":"如果你想要好座位，請早點來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/early","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf07a76f938476da14a1","word":"earn","forms":["earn"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75df719b6d0bf9d3","term":"earn","forms":["earn","earns","earning","earned","earnt","earnest","earnedst","earneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"憑努力贏得回報","explanation":"指透過實際的工作或努力得到獎勵、成功或認可；回報不一定是錢，重點是“付出換來應得的結果”。","examples":[{"en":"Her careful research earned her the team's respect.","zh":"她認真細緻的研究為她贏得了團隊的尊重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volunteers earned a well-deserved break after the cleanup.","zh":"志願者們清理完畢後，憑努力贏得了應得的休息時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd17f402e83b89e7","term":"earn","forms":["earn","earns","earning","earned","earnt","earnest","earnedst","earneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲得收入或利息","explanation":"指因工作、職位、資金或賬戶而得到錢；這裡強調收入的來源，不一定表示收入與付出的程度相稱。","examples":[{"en":"She earns enough to support her family.","zh":"她賺的錢足以養活全家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The savings account earns interest every month.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb52dd6511002d30d7ab","word":"earnest","forms":["earnest"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34a3ad2596f0ce4e","term":"earnest","forms":["earnest","earnester","more earnest","earnestest","most earnest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"認真而真誠的","explanation":"指一個人或說話、行為不是敷衍或虛假，而是發自內心、態度認真。這是“earnest”最重要的中心義。","examples":[{"en":"She made an earnest request for another chance.","zh":"她真誠地請求再給她一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His earnest apology convinced everyone.","zh":"他真誠的道歉說服了所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earnest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80cba63f4160f4cc","term":"earnest","forms":["earnest","earnester","more earnest","earnestest","most earnest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱切投入的","explanation":"指為了達到目標而認真、熱切地努力，帶有確實想做成某事的意味。祈禱、願望或行動都可以有這種投入的態度。","examples":[{"en":"With earnest effort, he finally passed the exam.","zh":"他經過認真努力，終於透過了考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They offered earnest prayers for the missing hikers.","zh":"他們真誠而熱切地為失蹤的徒步者祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earnest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84a5b242c35ee43a","term":"earnest","forms":["earnest"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認真嚴肅的態度","explanation":"指認真、嚴肅並且確實投入的態度，也就是形容詞“earnest”所描述的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"After years of preparation, she began her research in earnest.","zh":"經過多年的準備，她開始認真開展研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children started arguing in earnest.","zh":"孩子們真的開始爭吵起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earnest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a597f7903e7816d","term":"earnest","forms":["earnest"],"pos":"noun","zh":"當真；現實","explanation":"表示某件事是真實發生的或被認真對待，而不是玩笑、假裝或表演。它體現了“把事情當真”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"What began as a joke soon became earnest.","zh":"起初只是玩笑，後來很快變成了真事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He said it in jest, but she took it in earnest.","zh":"他說那話是開玩笑，但她當真了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earnest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6759ee18fd14a7064dd","word":"earphone","forms":["earphone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"earphone","forms":["earphone"],"pos":"n.","zh":"耳機；耳塞式聽筒","examples":[{"en":"One earphone stopped working during the flight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"He removed an earphone so he could hear the announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-741511f4ee662999ac84","word":"earring(s)","forms":["earring"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30b17d1de07dbd94","term":"earring","forms":["earring","earrings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耳環；耳飾","explanation":"指戴在耳朵上、通常懸掛在耳垂或耳部穿孔處的珠寶或裝飾品。最典型的是一對耳環，但單獨的一隻也可以稱為 earring。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a pair of silver earrings to the party.","zh":"她戴著一對銀耳環去參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found one of my earrings under the sofa.","zh":"我在沙發下面找到了我的一隻耳環。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b74b418a352d6710817","word":"earth","forms":["earth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bc412c8117a3874","term":"earth","forms":["earth","earths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"土壤；泥土","explanation":"earth 可以指植物生長的土壤，也就是腳下鬆散的泥土和土地。它強調的是能種植或挖掘的土，而不是整個地球。","examples":[{"en":"This earth is rich enough to grow vegetables.","zh":"這片土壤肥沃，足以種植蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mix the seeds with a little earth before planting them.","zh":"播種前把種子和一點泥土混合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7ba0ebe58abf662","term":"earth","forms":["earth","earths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地面；陸地","explanation":"earth 也可以指與天空或海洋相對的地面、陸地。這個意義仍然來自“腳下的大地”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"After two hours at sea, we were glad to see earth again.","zh":"在海上航行兩小時後，我們很高興又看到了陸地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaves fell from the tree and settled on the earth.","zh":"樹葉從樹上落下，落在了地面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa7835fc1c74a9e014c7","word":"earthquake","forms":["earthquake"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9c791fbca8d2639","term":"earthquake","forms":["earthquake","earthquakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地震","explanation":"地殼或地下活動使地面發生明顯搖晃的自然現象；這是 earthquake 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A strong earthquake struck the city early this morning.","zh":"今天清晨，一場強烈地震襲擊了這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The earthquake damaged several roads and bridges.","zh":"這場地震損壞了幾條道路和幾座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earthquake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f15fc67e54e4b963","term":"earthquake","forms":["earthquake","earthquakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劇烈動盪","explanation":"比喻某件事突然打破原有穩定狀態，並在經濟、政治或社會等方面造成廣泛而強烈的衝擊。它是從“地面劇烈搖晃”引申出來的。","examples":[{"en":"The merger caused an earthquake in the technology industry.","zh":"這次合併給科技行業帶來了劇烈衝擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scandal caused a political earthquake across the country.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earthquake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-914ff41a2b1acf1c0f9c","word":"ease","forms":["ease"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-874ea625210386be","term":"ease","forms":["ease"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕鬆；不費力","explanation":"指做某事時幾乎沒有困難，動作或任務進行得很輕鬆。重點不是事情本身簡單，而是完成它時沒有明顯阻力。","examples":[{"en":"She solved the puzzle with ease.","zh":"她輕鬆地解開了這道謎題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She climbed the steep path with surprising ease.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9c8cf94d4c9960e","term":"ease","forms":["ease"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舒適；自在","explanation":"指生活或環境讓人感到舒服、沒有不便和壓力，整個人可以從容自在地待著。","examples":[{"en":"The quiet room allowed him to work in ease.","zh":"這間安靜的房間讓他能夠舒適自在地工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The friendly welcome immediately put us at ease.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9c0f79cc7b20605","term":"ease","forms":["ease","eases","easing","eased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消除憂慮；使安心","explanation":"指把人的痛苦、擔心、激動或內疚等心理負擔鬆開，使其不再那麼沉重。","examples":[{"en":"Talking to her friend eased her worries.","zh":"和朋友談過之後，她的憂慮減輕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her reassuring call eased our anxiety.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dce85dbcd8865cba","term":"ease","forms":["ease","eases","easing","eased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"減輕疼痛","explanation":"指讓疼痛或身體不適變弱，就像把壓迫身體的重量慢慢移開。","examples":[{"en":"A pillow under her knees eased the pain.","zh":"膝下墊一個枕頭減輕了疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The warm compress eased the stiffness in his neck.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-afc74cb85a4f9f87","term":"ease","forms":["ease","eases","easing","eased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"自行減弱","explanation":"指疼痛、緊張、風勢等強度逐漸下降，不再像原來那麼強。這是“阻力被鬆開”這一核心概念的不及物用法。","examples":[{"en":"The pain eased after a few minutes.","zh":"幾分鐘後，疼痛減輕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strong wind finally eased.","zh":"強風終於減弱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bdb262b0201799aefb0","word":"east","forms":["east"],"officialPos":"n./adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8c6c99d3e3ec4f2","term":"east","forms":["east"],"pos":"adj","zh":"東邊的；向東的","explanation":"指某物位於東邊，或方向朝向東邊；這是“東門”意象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The village is east of the river.","zh":"這個村子在河的東邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our bedroom has an east window.","zh":"我們的臥室有一扇朝東的窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/east","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82244ca322117939","term":"east","forms":["east"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向東；往東","explanation":"表示動作朝太陽昇起的方向進行，是從“東門”意象自然延伸出的方向用法。","examples":[{"en":"We drove east for two hours.","zh":"我們向東開了兩個小時的車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The birds are flying east.","zh":"鳥兒正向東飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/east","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54eee27a8994e9c2","term":"east","forms":["east","easts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"東；東方","explanation":"指地球上的東這一方向，即太陽昇起的大致方向，是整組詞義的中心。","examples":[{"en":"Portsmouth is to the east of Southampton.","zh":"樸次茅斯在南安普敦的東邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sun rises in the east.","zh":"太陽從東方升起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/east","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4221a8f26bb25551c649","word":"eastern","forms":["eastern"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c71f2c2e215361f","term":"eastern","forms":["eastern","more eastern","most eastern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"東方的；東部的","explanation":"指位於東方、朝向東方，或與某個地區的東部有關。它就像“靠近東方日出的那一邊”，既可以描述地理位置，也可以描述與東部相關的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The eastern side of the island is much quieter.","zh":"這座島的東側安靜得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They live in an eastern suburb of the city.","zh":"他們住在這座城市的一個東部郊區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eastern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3eed5f7fd7b3050c","term":"eastern","forms":["eastern","more eastern","most eastern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"來自東方的（風）","explanation":"描述從東方吹來的風，也就是風的來源在東方。這裡仍然保留“來自東方”這條核心方向意義，只是修飾物件變成了風。","examples":[{"en":"An eastern wind brought cooler air overnight.","zh":"一夜之間，一股東風帶來了更涼的空氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An eastern wind carried cold air across the plain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eastern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97c10efe01d5c9c88704","word":"easy","forms":["easy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bd9c92fec45a5eb","term":"easy","forms":["easy","easier","more easy","easiest","most easy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易的；不費力的","explanation":"表示完成某件事不需要很多技能、努力或時間，是 easy 最核心的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"This recipe is easy to follow.","zh":"這個食譜很容易照著做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exam was easier than I expected.","zh":"這場考試比我預想的容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/easy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e57bd924047ef39d2a20","word":"eat","forms":["eat"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d346911ddae3d16","term":"eat","forms":["eat","eats","eating","ate","et","eaten","etten","eatest","atest","eateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃；攝入","explanation":"最基本的意思是把食物放入口中並攝入體內，也可以泛指某物被人吃掉。它是 eat 其他“消耗”類引申義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"I usually eat a light breakfast before work.","zh":"我通常在上班前吃一頓清淡的早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are eating apples in the kitchen.","zh":"孩子們正在廚房裡吃蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f99bba4493844c26","term":"eat","forms":["eat","eats","eating","ate","et","eaten","etten","eatest","atest","eateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃飯","explanation":"不帶賓語時，eat 可以只表示進行一頓飯或進餐這一活動，重點不是吃什麼，而是吃飯這件事。","examples":[{"en":"What time do we eat tonight?","zh":"我們今晚幾點吃飯？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you eaten, or shall I make lunch?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86cbcc120c9f41bc","term":"eat","forms":["eat","eats","eating","ate","et","eaten","etten","eatest","atest","eateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消耗；耗掉","explanation":"這裡把錢、時間、能源等抽象資源想成會被“吃掉”的東西：專案或活動不斷吸收資源，使剩餘量減少。","examples":[{"en":"The repairs ate up most of our savings.","zh":"維修費用耗掉了我們大部分積蓄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This task is eating up all my time.","zh":"這項任務佔用了我全部的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9dbf2334803fd989b05","word":"eccentric","forms":["eccentric"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41b60c0e0d7fdda4","term":"eccentric","forms":["eccentric","more eccentric","most eccentric"],"pos":"adj","zh":"偏離中心","explanation":"指位置不在中心，或在思想、立場等抽象空間中明顯偏離通常的中心位置。核心畫面就是一個點沒有落在圓心上。","examples":[{"en":"The new office occupies an eccentric position far from the center of town.","zh":"新辦公室的位置偏離市中心很遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An eccentric shaft makes the piston move back and forth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0e098adc9e6f588","term":"eccentric","forms":["eccentric","more eccentric","most eccentric"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古怪的；不合常規的","explanation":"指一個人的行為、習慣或想法偏離大家通常的方式，顯得特別甚至有些古怪。這裡是把“偏離中心”從空間轉到社會規範上。","examples":[{"en":"Her eccentric habits made her memorable to everyone in the village.","zh":"她古怪的習慣讓村裡的每個人都對她印象深刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The professor is eccentric, but his students admire his creativity.","zh":"這位教授有些古怪，但學生們很欣賞他的創造力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76ded05f57bb7d27","term":"eccentric","forms":["eccentric","eccentrics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"古怪的人","explanation":"指行為、習慣或想法明顯偏離常規的人。這個名詞直接把“偏離中心”的畫面放到社會行為上。","examples":[{"en":"The old artist was an eccentric who painted all night.","zh":"那位老藝術家是個古怪的人，總是在夜裡作畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village eccentric wore a top hat to breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eccentric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-092c79e8f80e559e404b","word":"echo","forms":["echo"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06267d32304a0266","term":"echo","forms":["echo","echoes","echos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"回聲","explanation":"聲音碰到牆壁、山谷等表面後返回，過一會兒又被原來的人聽見，這個返回的聲音就是echo。它是“聲音回來”這一核心畫面的直接意義。","examples":[{"en":"We heard an echo when we shouted across the canyon.","zh":"我們朝峽谷對面喊叫時聽到了回聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our shouts produced an echo across the valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/echo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f6064b4760dba34","term":"echo","forms":["echo","echoes","echoing","echoed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出回聲","explanation":"聲音或聲波從表面反射回來並再次響起，就是echo。它是“聲音返回”這個核心畫面在動詞中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Our footsteps echoed through the empty station.","zh":"我們的腳步聲在空蕩蕩的車站裡迴響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A shout echoed back from the cliffs on the opposite shore.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/echo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80b1509ea37643250da6","word":"eclipse","forms":["eclipse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f420a5189dc4387","term":"eclipse","forms":["eclipse","eclipses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天體遮擋","explanation":"指一個天體移動到觀察者和另一個天體之間，使後者的一部分或全部被遮住的現象。這是最寬的天文學含義，日食和月食都屬於它。","examples":[{"en":"The observatory will broadcast the eclipse tonight.","zh":"天文臺今晚將直播這次天文食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several planets can appear close together during an eclipse.","zh":"在天體發生食的過程中，幾顆行星可能看起來彼此很近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eclipse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d59056338502df5e","term":"eclipse","forms":["eclipse","eclipses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日食或月食","explanation":"特指一個行星天體擋在太陽和另一個行星天體之間，並把影子投到後者上，最常見的就是月亮擋住太陽形成日食。","examples":[{"en":"People travelled north to watch the solar eclipse.","zh":"人們前往北方觀看日食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lunar eclipse gave the moon a reddish colour.","zh":"月食使月亮呈現出偏紅的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eclipse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a4bea39ed005fb1","term":"eclipse","forms":["eclipse","eclipses","eclipsing","eclipsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遮住天體","explanation":"指一個天體擋住另一個天體，使後者的光或形象暫時看不見。這是名詞天文義轉成的動作表達。","examples":[{"en":"The Moon will eclipse the Sun for a few minutes.","zh":"月亮將遮住太陽幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Io briefly eclipsed the sunlight reaching another Jovian moon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eclipse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-294a1d5ec8f7b60ad2c2","word":"ecological","forms":["ecological"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dab17a1d5c372b93","term":"ecological","forms":["ecological","more ecological","most ecological"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生態學的；生態的","explanation":"指生物、環境以及它們之間相互作用的性質或研究內容，重點是那張“生態關係網”本身，而不一定表示某種做法更環保。","examples":[{"en":"The study examines the ecological relationships among insects, plants, and soil.","zh":"這項研究考察昆蟲、植物和土壤之間的生態關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Drought can have serious ecological effects on local bird populations.","zh":"乾旱可能會對當地鳥類種群產生嚴重的生態影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecological","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbe693c7e1358e9c","term":"ecological","forms":["ecological","more ecological","most ecological"],"pos":"adj","zh":"環保的；對環境危害較小的","explanation":"指某種產品、材料或做法能減少對自然環境的傷害，也就是更符合生態平衡的要求；這裡的重點從“描述生態關係”轉為“保護生態環境”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel has adopted more ecological practices to reduce waste.","zh":"這家酒店採用了更環保的做法來減少浪費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel uses ecological cleaning products.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecological","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d45d1ea845efb8a8a7c","word":"ecology","forms":["ecology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37ba3c55b0cf3851","term":"ecology","forms":["ecology","ecologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生態學","explanation":"生態學是生物學的一個分支，研究生物與周圍環境之間，以及不同生物彼此之間如何相互影響。它關注的不是某一種生物孤立的特徵，而是它們共同生活在“同一個家”中的關係。","examples":[{"en":"She studied ecology at university.","zh":"她在大學學習生態學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ecology of the wetland has changed dramatically.","zh":"這片溼地的生態狀況發生了巨大變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a929d80082a8911","term":"ecology","forms":["ecology","ecologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某系統的相互關係研究","explanation":"這個義項把“共同的家”從自然界擴充套件到社會、組織或其他系統，指研究其中各部分如何相互影響以及如何受環境影響。例如，社會生態學研究個人、群體和社會環境之間的聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The report examines the social ecology of the city.","zh":"這份報告考察了這座城市的社會生態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study examines the ecology of online communities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11c45871e9f8b9dfd5a7","word":"economic","forms":["economic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-004f4c16bd689b46","term":"economic","forms":["economic","more economic","most economic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"經濟的","explanation":"指整個經濟系統、經濟活動或經濟狀況有關的事物，例如生產、就業、增長和政策。這裡的重點是資源和金錢在社會中的執行，而不是某一件商品是否便宜。","examples":[{"en":"The country is facing serious economic problems.","zh":"這個國家正面臨嚴重的經濟問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Economic growth has slowed this year.","zh":"今年的經濟增長放緩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/economic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7feb1fadf2233043c02","word":"economical","forms":["economical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5eff91facec30908","term":"economical","forms":["economical","more economical","most economical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"節儉的；花錢謹慎的","explanation":"形容人花錢和使用東西很謹慎，儘量避免不必要的開支；重點是這個人會把錢和資源省下來。","examples":[{"en":"She is economical with her money and rarely buys things on impulse.","zh":"她花錢很節儉，很少衝動購物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was an economical person by nature.","zh":"他天生就是個節儉的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/economical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfbd0f2bc105cbd0","term":"economical","forms":["economical","more economical","most economical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"省錢的；節省資源的；划算的","explanation":"形容某種物品、做法或選擇能減少花費或資源消耗，因此長期來看更划算；不只是價格便宜，也可以是省油、省電或省材料。","examples":[{"en":"This small car is economical to run.","zh":"這輛小汽車使用起來很省錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new bicycle was an economical purchase.","zh":"買這輛新腳踏車很划算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/economical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e9ad751b5e6102bb17b","word":"economics","forms":["economics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e03db424145ce4ec","term":"economics","forms":["economics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟學","explanation":"經濟學研究有限的資源應當怎樣分配，以及商品和服務怎樣生產、交換、消費；也研究資本、投資、勞動等因素如何共同影響社會執行。","examples":[{"en":"Mary studied economics for five years before going into banking.","zh":"瑪麗學習了五年經濟學，之後進入銀行業工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Economics helps us understand why prices change.","zh":"經濟學幫助我們理解價格為什麼會變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/economics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-829af112ee3cdf7f8306","word":"economist","forms":["economist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25b06d9a422030af","term":"economist","forms":["economist","economists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟學家","explanation":"指以經濟學為專業，研究生產、消費、就業、價格等現象，分析資料並提出解釋或理論的人。這個意義就是“觀察社會如何管理資源的人”，是現代最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The economist explained why prices had risen so quickly.","zh":"這位經濟學家解釋了價格為什麼上漲得這麼快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several economists expect unemployment to fall next year.","zh":"幾位經濟學家預計明年失業率會下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/economist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a44bf5642d9c085","term":"economist","forms":["economist","economists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治經濟學家","explanation":"指特別關注政治制度、政府決策與經濟活動之間關係的經濟學家。它仍然屬於現代“研究資源如何在社會中分配”的核心概念，只是研究範圍更集中在政治與經濟的交界處。","examples":[{"en":"The economist examined how elections affected government spending.","zh":"這位政治經濟學家研究了選舉如何影響政府支出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The economist studied taxation and public expenditure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/economist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6fda2b8252b6d5ea9d19","word":"economy","forms":["economy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-784324acf3d2c8c6","term":"economy","forms":["economy","economies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟體系","explanation":"指一個國家、地區或社會中生產、分配和消費商品與服務的整體系統，也可泛指這套系統的執行狀況。這是現代新聞和日常討論中最重要的名詞義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"The national economy is slowly recovering.","zh":"國民經濟正在逐步復甦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strong economy can create more jobs.","zh":"強勁的經濟可以創造更多就業機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/economy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-570dd38dc5baf3112a7c","word":"ecosystem","forms":["ecosystem"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b406026b57856864","term":"ecosystem","forms":["ecosystem","ecosystems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生態系統","explanation":"由生物群落和周圍環境共同組成、彼此作用並作為一個整體運作的系統。例如，一片森林中的植物、動物、土壤、水和氣候可以共同構成一個 ecosystem。","examples":[{"en":"The forest ecosystem is under pressure from prolonged drought.","zh":"這個森林生態系統正受到長期乾旱的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Protecting the river ecosystem requires cleaner water.","zh":"保護河流生態系統需要更清潔的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecosystem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca025f3d374718f3","term":"ecosystem","forms":["ecosystem","ecosystems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物與環境的相互聯絡","explanation":"強調生態系統中植物、動物、微生物和環境彼此連線、互相影響的關係，而不只是這些事物的簡單集合；一個環節變化，其他環節也可能受到影響。","examples":[{"en":"Removing one species can disrupt the balance of the entire ecosystem.","zh":"移除一個物種可能會破壞整個生態系統的平衡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Removing the predators changed the entire ecosystem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecosystem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1cb100f57e971cacf26","word":"edge","forms":["edge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c9a857b262a0cfd","term":"edge","forms":["edge","edges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊緣；邊界線","explanation":"指一個表面最外側、與周圍部分分開的那條邊界線。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your name along the edge of the page.","zh":"請沿著頁面邊緣寫下你的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small crack appeared at the edge of the window.","zh":"窗戶邊緣出現了一條小裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09e3c0861d4e323a","term":"edge","forms":["edge","edges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"優勢","explanation":"表示相對於對手或競爭者的一點優勢，好像站在競爭的邊緣位置上，更容易獲勝。","examples":[{"en":"Her experience gives her an edge over the other candidates.","zh":"她的經驗使她比其他候選人略佔優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The home team has the edge in defense.","zh":"主隊在防守方面佔有優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e8d82eb2cda6c35","term":"edge","forms":["edge","edges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刀刃；切割邊","explanation":"指刀、斧、劍等工具或武器上用來切割或造成深傷的薄而鋒利的一側。","examples":[{"en":"The knife has a sharp edge, so handle it carefully.","zh":"這把刀的刃很鋒利，所以要小心拿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sharp edge of his words hurt her.","zh":"他話語中的尖刻傷害了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45ff13156be1d290","term":"edge","forms":["edge","edges","edging","edged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"小心地推移","explanation":"指把物體沿某個方向一點一點、緩慢而小心地移動。","examples":[{"en":"She edged the chair closer to the window.","zh":"她小心地把椅子一點點挪近窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He edged the box across the floor.","zh":"他小心地把箱子一點點推過地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1bf079ba51fcac1","term":"edge","forms":["edge","edges","edging","edged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緩慢移動","explanation":"指人或物自己朝某個方向慢慢而謹慎地移動，彷彿沿著邊緣前進。","examples":[{"en":"The dog edged away from the noisy crowd.","zh":"那條狗慢慢躲開了喧鬧的人群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She edged closer to the door.","zh":"她小心地一點點靠近門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60cd85012b2dbd4ee1a0","word":"edible","forms":["edible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0db6b3f68753e480","term":"edible","forms":["edible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可安全食用的","explanation":"表示某種食物或植物可以安全地吃，適合供人食用，重點是不會因食用本身而造成傷害，不保證味道好。","examples":[{"en":"These berries are edible, but they are not very sweet.","zh":"這些漿果可以食用，但不是很甜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide showed us which mushrooms were edible.","zh":"嚮導告訴我們哪些蘑菇可以食用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-262121c5372be8af3ae6","word":"edit","forms":["edit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abda9315f14991bb","term":"edit","forms":["edit","edits","editing","edited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修改文字","explanation":"指修改文章、演講稿或其他文字檔案，使內容更準確、清楚、簡潔或合適。","examples":[{"en":"Your report is too long, so please edit it before Friday.","zh":"你的報告太長了，請在週五前把它修改一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She edited the letter to make the tone more polite.","zh":"她修改了這封信，使語氣更禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70c8c7c2db8750bd","term":"edit","forms":["edit","edits","editing","edited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剪輯照片或錄音錄影","explanation":"指對照片、聲音或影片進行剪下、調整、刪減和重新組合，做出更合適的媒體版本。","examples":[{"en":"We edited the interview down to twenty minutes.","zh":"我們把這段採訪剪輯到了二十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you edit these photos before we share them?","zh":"你能在我們分享這些照片前先修整一下嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a3be761036549131b35","word":"edition","forms":["edition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d2be59ad9c82ce1","term":"edition","forms":["edition","editions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"版本；版次","explanation":"指經過特定編輯、以特定方式製作，或在特定時間出版的作品版本。一本書可能有精裝版、刪節版、修訂版或不同年份的 edition，它們通常內容或編排有所不同。","examples":[{"en":"I bought the latest edition of the dictionary.","zh":"我買了這本詞典的最新版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This edition includes a new introduction.","zh":"這個版本附有一篇新的導言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a59312f030b3388","term":"edition","forms":["edition","editions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一版印刷品；一批出版物","explanation":"指某一版作品在同一時間印刷並出版的全部副本，也就是這一版的整批書。這裡關注的不是某一本具體的書，而是同一次印刷發行的數量或整體。","examples":[{"en":"The first edition sold out within a week.","zh":"第一版在一週內就售罄了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only fifty copies of this limited edition were printed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/edition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1553cc62ff246044c683","word":"editor","forms":["editor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34352727b0664d1c","term":"editor","forms":["editor","editors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"編輯內容的人","explanation":"指修改、整理檔案或其他內容，使其更清楚、準確、適合使用或發表的人。這是最寬泛的核心意思，具體工作可以包括改文字、刪改結構和檢查內容。","examples":[{"en":"The editor changed several sections of the report.","zh":"編輯修改了報告中的幾個部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works as an editor for a science magazine.","zh":"她在一家科學雜誌社當編輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/editor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f33a48dfc6110d92","term":"editor","forms":["editor","editors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"媒體機構中的編輯或選稿負責人","explanation":"指報紙、出版社或類似機構中負責修改報道、決定發表哪些內容，或統籌某個版面的人。這裡的“整理成品”進一步包括篩選和安排內容，而不只是改句子。","examples":[{"en":"The city editor chose the main story for tomorrow's paper.","zh":"城市新聞編輯為明天的報紙選定了頭條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor selected three letters for publication.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/editor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-004a8606fe4bb266","term":"editor","forms":["editor","editors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"編輯檔案的軟體","explanation":"指用於建立、開啟和修改檔案的程式，尤其常指編輯文字檔案的軟體。這裡“編輯者”從人擴充套件成了能整理內容的工具。","examples":[{"en":"I opened the file in a text editor and removed the extra lines.","zh":"我用文字編輯器開啟檔案，刪掉了多餘的行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This editor lets you search and replace words quickly.","zh":"這個編輯器可以讓你快速查詢和替換文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/editor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-405b1a1fadc27ffb5aa6","word":"editorial","forms":["editorial"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4d47e98dd70d4e2","term":"editorial","forms":["editorial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"編輯的；社論的","explanation":"指與編輯、編輯工作或編輯部表達的意見有關。它可以描述編輯所做的工作，也可以描述帶有媒體立場的評論。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper changed its editorial policy after the election.","zh":"這家報紙在選舉後改變了編輯方針。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has several years of editorial experience.","zh":"她有多年的編輯工作經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/editorial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec065263fed3b392","term":"editorial","forms":["editorial","editorials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社論","explanation":"指報紙、雜誌等出版物以編輯部名義，就某個議題或時事表達立場、進行評論的文章。它不是單純報道事實，而是媒體在“拿著筆定調”。","examples":[{"en":"The paper published an editorial criticizing the new law.","zh":"這家報紙發表了一篇社論，批評這項新法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I read the editorial before forming my own opinion.","zh":"我在形成自己的看法前讀了那篇社論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/editorial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f98fa2c08464cdb4ec33","word":"educate","forms":["educate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-47c0cb219f5927d4","term":"educate","forms":["educate","educates","educating","educated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"教育；培訓；使瞭解","explanation":"指透過講解、訓練或引導，把知識、技能或認識傳給別人，幫助對方“被培養出來”。物件既可以是學生，也可以是公眾、員工或訪客等群體。","examples":[{"en":"The museum uses interactive displays to educate visitors about climate change.","zh":"這家博物館利用互動展板讓訪客瞭解氣候變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program educates young workers to handle workplace emergencies.","zh":"這個專案培訓年輕員工應對工作場所的緊急情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/educate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68bf0109c6f8a87bfa96","word":"education","forms":["education"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fdbd9809e299dbd6","term":"education","forms":["education","educations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教育過程","explanation":"指系統地傳授知識、培養技能和判斷力的過程，重點在“培養人”這一行動本身，而不只是上課。","examples":[{"en":"Every child has the right to a good education.","zh":"每個孩子都有權接受良好的教育。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Education can change the way people understand the world.","zh":"教育可以改變人們理解世界的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/education","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f068b61507d3c43","term":"education","forms":["education","educations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"所受教育；學識","explanation":"指一個人透過學習和正式教學獲得的知識、技能與觀念，重點從“培養過程”轉向“培養出來的成果”。也可以指一個人接受過的完整教育經歷。","examples":[{"en":"Her education prepared her well for the demands of the job.","zh":"她所受的教育使她很好地應對了這份工作的要求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her education enabled her to read several ancient languages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/education","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbedbde861ac4af28bac","word":"educational","forms":["educational"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93028a683ecf1db2","term":"educational","forms":["educational","more educational","most educational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"教育的；與教育有關的","explanation":"表示某人或某事物屬於教育領域，或與學習、教學和學校等有關。它強調所屬關係，不一定表示這個東西本身很有啟發性。","examples":[{"en":"The city is investing in new educational facilities.","zh":"這座城市正在投資建設新的教育設施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works for an educational charity.","zh":"她在一家教育慈善機構工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/educational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-081ed9141211929d","term":"educational","forms":["educational","more educational","most educational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有教育意義的；啟發性的","explanation":"表示某種材料、活動或經歷能教給人知識，幫助人理解某個問題，或帶來有益的啟發。這裡重點不是它屬於教育系統，而是它確實能讓人學到東西。","examples":[{"en":"The museum visit was both enjoyable and educational.","zh":"這次博物館參觀既有趣又有教育意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visiting the restoration workshop was surprisingly educational.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/educational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcb576426a17b7df1390","word":"effect","forms":["effect"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28afb199d65fea3e","term":"effect","forms":["effect","effects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結果；影響","explanation":"指某個原因、行動或事件造成的結果，尤其強調它對人、事物或環境產生的改變。這是effect最基本、最常用的名詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"The new schedule had a positive effect on team morale.","zh":"新的日程安排對團隊士氣產生了積極影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are still studying the long-term effects of the accident.","zh":"我們仍在研究那起事故的長期影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/effect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18086d9cfe513b3b","term":"effect","forms":["effect","effects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印象；感染力","explanation":"指某種言語、動作、外表或藝術手法在人的心裡造成的感覺和印象，重點不在實際後果，而在“給人什麼感覺”。","examples":[{"en":"She paused before the final sentence for dramatic effect.","zh":"她在最後一句之前停頓了一下，以增強戲劇效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The simple lighting creates a calm effect.","zh":"簡潔的燈光營造出一種平靜的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/effect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aafa0f5d8a1429c6","term":"effect","forms":["effect","effects","effecting","effected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促成；實現","explanation":"表示透過行動或安排主動把某件事做成、使某種改變發生。它強調“把結果實現出來”，而不是僅僅對某事產生影響。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy is intended to effect major changes in healthcare.","zh":"這項新政策旨在促成醫療保健領域的重大改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee effected a peaceful transfer of power.","zh":"委員會促成了權力的和平交接。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/effect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46e0876178516073c5ae","word":"effective","forms":["effective"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2c7c8f90e130b3d","term":"effective","forms":["effective","more effective","most effective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有效的；能產生預期效果的","explanation":"指某種方法、藥物、措施等確實能夠達到想要的結果，就像一把真的能開門的鑰匙。","examples":[{"en":"This medicine is effective against common colds.","zh":"這種藥對普通感冒有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise is an effective way to reduce stress.","zh":"經常鍛鍊是減輕壓力的有效方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/effective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8fa1f2960a60393","term":"effective","forms":["effective","more effective","most effective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"效果顯著的；有說服力的","explanation":"指某種行動、講話或表現能產生明顯而有決定性的影響，不只是形式上完成了。","examples":[{"en":"She gave an effective presentation that convinced the team.","zh":"她做了一場很有說服力的演示，說服了團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her effective use of silence held the audience's attention.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/effective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3b8ab66b02ea5faa90b","word":"efficiency","forms":["efficiency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d83cf3859a1aa32","term":"efficiency","forms":["efficiency","efficiencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"效率；資源利用率","explanation":"指用一定的時間、金錢、能源或其他資源去完成目標時，利用得有多好、浪費有多少。效率高不一定只是做得快，也可以是用更少資源達到同樣或更好的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The new software has greatly improved the efficiency of our office.","zh":"新軟體大大提高了我們辦公室的工作效率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are looking for ways to reduce costs without losing efficiency.","zh":"我們正在尋找既能降低成本又不損失效率的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/efficiency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9a7e9c2383b4497","term":"efficiency","forms":["efficiency","efficiencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"單間公寓","explanation":"在美國英語中，指把起居、睡眠和通常的廚房空間安排在一個房間裡的小型公寓；重點是空間緊湊、設施集中。","examples":[{"en":"She rented an efficiency near the university for the summer.","zh":"她租了一間大學附近的單間公寓，住一個夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The efficiency had a foldaway bed beside its tiny kitchenette.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/efficiency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-480e4f1d08e9079c05c0","word":"efficient","forms":["efficient"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e39bb3990144d0a","term":"efficient","forms":["efficient","more efficient","most efficient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高效的；節省資源的","explanation":"指完成工作時少花時間、精力、材料或金錢，卻能得到需要的結果。它關注的是投入和過程中的浪費少，而不只是最後有沒有成功。","examples":[{"en":"The new system is much more efficient than the old one.","zh":"新系統比舊系統高效得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found an efficient way to organize the files.","zh":"她找到了整理檔案的高效方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/efficient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-694ce01f0fd052f8","term":"efficient","forms":["efficient","more efficient","most efficient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能量利用率高的","explanation":"用於機器、發動機或其他過程時，表示輸入的能量中有較大比例轉化成了有用輸出；這裡的重點是一個可計算的利用比例。","examples":[{"en":"This refrigerator is highly efficient and uses very little electricity.","zh":"這臺冰箱能量利用率很高，用電量很少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An efficient boiler uses less fuel for the same heat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/efficient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-a4f12c3895258d0b6e32","word":"effort","forms":["effort"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9263e8c671a49c05","term":"effort","forms":["effort","efforts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"努力；付出","explanation":"指為了完成活動、解決問題或達到目標而投入的力氣、時間和精力，重點在“推門時用上的勁”，不一定表示最後成功。","examples":[{"en":"She made a real effort to arrive on time.","zh":"她確實努力按時到達了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A little effort can make a big difference.","zh":"稍微努力一點就能帶來很大的改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/effort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b17845a1e7aa919","term":"effort","forms":["effort","efforts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘗試；成果","explanation":"指某人為了實現目標而進行的一次具體嘗試，也可以泛指這次行動本身及其表現；即使沒有成功，也能稱為一番努力。","examples":[{"en":"Her first effort at painting impressed everyone.","zh":"她第一次嘗試畫畫就給大家留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His first effort at pottery was a crooked bowl.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/effort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34707c3f40dfa20c3902","word":"egg","forms":["egg"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-531912daeff16dc2","term":"egg","forms":["egg","eggs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的卵、蛋","explanation":"指鳥類、昆蟲、爬行動物等動物產下的、通常由膜或外殼包住並孕育胚胎的身體結構。","examples":[{"en":"The duck laid three eggs in the nest.","zh":"那隻鴨子在巢裡下了三個蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The turtle buried its eggs in the sand.","zh":"那隻海龜把蛋埋在沙子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f4bd96f4576c113","term":"egg","forms":["egg","eggs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作為食物的雞蛋","explanation":"在日常飲食中，通常指人們烹飪和食用的雞蛋，也可以泛指可食用的蛋。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a dozen eggs for breakfast.","zh":"我買了一打雞蛋當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Crack an egg into the mixing bowl.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5c27db0dada30212f6a","word":"ego","forms":["ego"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95035ec9838cd817","term":"ego","forms":["ego","egos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自我意識；自我中心感","explanation":"指心裡強烈的“我”意識，尤其是把自己的想法、感受和重要性看得很重。它可以只是對自我的認同，也常暗示一個人過分關注自己。","examples":[{"en":"His ego makes it hard for him to admit when he is wrong.","zh":"他的自我意識太強，很難承認自己錯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned to put her ego aside and listen to the advice.","zh":"她學會放下自我，聽取別人的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ego","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-daa137951b7d1159","term":"ego","forms":["ego","egos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理學中的自我","explanation":"在弗洛伊德心理學中，ego 是心智中負責在內在慾望、道德要求和現實環境之間進行調節的部分。這裡的 ego 是專業概念，不單純表示一個人的驕傲或自負。","examples":[{"en":"In Freud's theory, the ego helps a person deal with the demands of reality.","zh":"在弗洛伊德的理論中，自我幫助人應對現實的要求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Freud described the ego as mediating conflicting demands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ego","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94f106e0117354cedb9e","word":"either","forms":["either"],"officialPos":"adv./pron./adj./conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be4e315a4a1153cc","term":"either","forms":["either"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也不","explanation":"在否定句末，either 表示前面提到的否定情況同樣適用於另一個人或事物，相當於“也不”。","examples":[{"en":"I don't want coffee, and I don't want tea either.","zh":"我不想喝咖啡，茶也不想喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wasn't invited, and I wasn't either.","zh":"她沒有被邀請，我也沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/either","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f4c018c3a12ca3e","term":"either","forms":["either"],"pos":"det","zh":"兩者任一","explanation":"放在單數名詞前，表示兩個選項中的任何一個，重點是“二選一”，而不是兩個都要。","examples":[{"en":"You can choose either seat.","zh":"你可以選兩個座位中的任意一個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Either answer is acceptable.","zh":"兩個答案中的任意一個都可以接受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/either","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c4864fe64303c2b","term":"either","forms":["either"],"pos":"pron","zh":"兩者之一","explanation":"不帶後面的名詞時，either 代替“兩者中的一個”，強調二選一或任取其一。","examples":[{"en":"I tried both routes, but I didn't like either.","zh":"兩條路線我都試過，但哪一條我都不喜歡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Either would fit through the narrow opening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/either","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-730375e4de9f5e78524f","word":"elaborate","forms":["elaborate"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cad9cf2217359568","term":"elaborate","forms":["elaborate","more elaborate","most elaborate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"複雜而詳細的","explanation":"形容內容、計劃、說明等包含許多細節，結構周密，不是簡單幾句話就能概括的。這個意思體現了把事情充分展開、做得完整的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The committee prepared an elaborate plan for the festival.","zh":"委員會為這次節日活動制定了一份周密詳細的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave an elaborate explanation of how the machine worked.","zh":"她詳細解釋了這臺機器的工作原理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elaborate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe073c646d977ebd","term":"elaborate","forms":["elaborate","elaborates","elaborating","elaborated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"詳細發展；使更完善","explanation":"把一個原本較粗略的想法、計劃或方案繼續加工，補充更多細節，使它變得更完整、更復雜。它和形容詞的“詳細複雜”是同一條記憶線索：把內容充分展開。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers elaborated their theory after reviewing the new evidence.","zh":"研究人員研究了新證據後，進一步完善了他們的理論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The architect elaborated the original design to include a larger garden.","zh":"建築師在原有設計的基礎上進一步完善方案，加入了更大的花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elaborate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-986051385feae5b98508","word":"elastic","forms":["elastic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6eb798df0022fda","term":"elastic","forms":["elastic","more elastic","most elastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可拉伸並回彈的","explanation":"指物體受到拉、壓等外力時可以改變形狀，外力消失後又大致恢復原來的形狀或大小。這是 elastic 最基本、最容易擴充套件出的意思。","examples":[{"en":"This fabric is elastic enough to fit comfortably.","zh":"這種布料彈性足夠好，穿起來很舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rope is elastic, so it stretches when you pull it.","zh":"這根繩子有彈性，所以你拉它時會伸長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-abf2a2e8dac00f4a","term":"elastic","forms":["elastic","elastics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鬆緊材料","explanation":"指能拉伸和回彈、用於衣物腰部或袖口等位置的材料。它就是“有彈性的”這一核心概念在名詞形式下所指的實際東西。","examples":[{"en":"These shorts use elastic instead of a belt.","zh":"這條短褲用鬆緊帶代替了腰帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The elastic in my sleeve has become loose.","zh":"我袖口裡的鬆緊帶變鬆了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e85ebe7458309e1e39f","word":"elbow","forms":["elbow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98f53dff05750b03","term":"elbow","forms":["elbow","elbows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肘部","explanation":"elbow最基本的意思是上臂和前臂連線處的肘部，也就是手臂中間能夠彎曲的關節。","examples":[{"en":"She cut her elbow when she fell off her bike.","zh":"她從腳踏車上摔下來時擦傷了肘部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sleeves of this jacket reach just below my elbows.","zh":"這件夾克的袖子剛好到我的肘部以下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elbow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a459fabdc2390bce","term":"elbow","forms":["elbow","elbows","elbowing","elbowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用肘擠著前進","explanation":"elbow表示藉助肘部推開周圍的人或障礙，艱難地擠出一條路向前走；重點是“用肘開路”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We elbowed our way through the crowd to reach the exit.","zh":"我們用肘擠過人群，走到了出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She elbowed her way to the front of the line.","zh":"她一路推擠著到了隊伍最前面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elbow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4bad2eaec5cd6571264f","word":"elder","forms":["elder"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-058881e7f6ca4cc9","term":"elder","forms":["elder"],"pos":"adj","zh":"較年長的","explanation":"指在年齡、輩分或資歷上比另一個人更大，核心感覺是“更老、更資深”。","examples":[{"en":"My elder sister lives in Canada.","zh":"我姐姐住在加拿大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The elder son took over the family business.","zh":"大兒子接管了家族生意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-880e811c5dcb52b8","term":"elder","forms":["elder","elders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長老；社群領袖","explanation":"指因年長、經驗豐富而在部落、村莊或社群中受尊敬、能提供建議的人，核心仍是“資深的年長者”。","examples":[{"en":"The village elder helped settle the dispute.","zh":"村裡的長老幫助解決了這場爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The elders met to discuss the future of the community.","zh":"長老們開會討論社群的未來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-839e757698e9a5bb","term":"elder","forms":["elder","elders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"年長者；長輩","explanation":"指比另一個人年長的人，常常是家庭中的長輩或社會關係中的前輩，複數時尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"Children should listen to their elders.","zh":"孩子應該聽長輩的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children greeted their elders respectfully at the celebration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-457020499ea391ea3c56","word":"elderly","forms":["elderly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08364e5ad5115b7e","term":"elderly","forms":["elderly","more elderly","most elderly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"上了年紀的","explanation":"形容人已經進入較年長的階段，通常譯為“年長的、上了年紀的”。這個詞常用於禮貌而客觀地談論老年人。","examples":[{"en":"The program provides free meals for elderly people.","zh":"這個專案為老年人提供免費餐食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An elderly woman helped me find the right bus.","zh":"一位老婦人幫我找到了正確的公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elderly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0b92f54e6e7d356f826","word":"elect","forms":["elect"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8dbbc59c24d59aaf","term":"elect","forms":["elect"],"pos":"adj","zh":"當選待任職","explanation":"指已經被選上某個職位、但還沒有正式開始任職的人，畫面就是“被挑出來了，正在等著接任”。","examples":[{"en":"The president-elect will take office next month.","zh":"總統當選人將在下個月就職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The president-elect met the outgoing administration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a44cd606c20e9eda","term":"elect","forms":["elect","elects","electing","elected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"選擇；決定","explanation":"指在幾個可能性中挑出一個，或決定採取某種行動；就是把某個選項從其他選項中挑出來。","examples":[{"en":"She elected to work from home for the rest of the week.","zh":"她決定本週剩下的時間在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several employees elected to work from home.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e668503bf7b35642","term":"elect","forms":["elect","elects","electing","elected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"選舉選出","explanation":"指透過投票或正式選舉把某位候選人挑出來，讓他獲得某個職位。","examples":[{"en":"Voters elected Maria mayor by a wide margin.","zh":"選民以很大的優勢選舉瑪麗亞擔任市長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The members elected a new treasurer by secret ballot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b9e99d2bd5e48d9a569","word":"election","forms":["election"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b57ccc9c677e30e","term":"election","forms":["election","elections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選舉過程","explanation":"指公眾透過投票，從候選人中選出領導人、議員、地方議員或其他代表的過程。這是 election 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The parliamentary election will be held in March.","zh":"議會選舉將於三月舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Millions of people voted in the national election.","zh":"數百萬人在全國選舉中投了票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/election","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d6eb34e27d13b43","term":"election","forms":["election","elections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"當選；選出的結果","explanation":"強調某位領導人或代表被公眾投票選中的事實或結果，而不是選舉活動本身。可以理解為“從投票中產生的那個選擇結果”。","examples":[{"en":"Her election as mayor surprised many people.","zh":"她當選市長讓許多人感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her election to the council surprised local commentators.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/election","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44b3c5003d93c5f1623b","word":"electric","forms":["electric"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-669f72fc1540fbdd","term":"electric","forms":["electric"],"pos":"adj","zh":"用電的；與電有關的","explanation":"指由電產生、靠電執行、使用電力，或總體上與電有關的事物。這是 electric 最基本、最常見的意思，電動汽車、電燈和電器都可以用它來說明。","examples":[{"en":"More people are choosing electric cars to reduce fuel costs.","zh":"越來越多人選擇電動汽車來降低燃料費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old building still has electric heating.","zh":"那棟老建築仍然使用電暖氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4224b4537ef3ea08","term":"electric","forms":["electric"],"pos":"adj","zh":"電聲樂器的","explanation":"指本來可以用原聲方式演奏、現在改用電力放大或處理聲音的樂器，例如電吉他或電鋼琴。重點仍是“透過電來執行或增強效果”。","examples":[{"en":"She learned to play electric guitar in a small band.","zh":"她在一個小樂隊裡學會了彈電吉他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He plugged his electric guitar into the amplifier.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed157486b875d92c25c9","word":"electrical","forms":["electrical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b5d62b2b1f397c1","term":"electrical","forms":["electrical","more electrical","most electrical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"電氣的；電子的","explanation":"表示某物與電、電子裝置或電氣工程有關，重點是“屬於電氣領域”這一屬性。","examples":[{"en":"She is studying electrical engineering at university.","zh":"她正在大學學習電氣工程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building has serious electrical problems.","zh":"這棟樓存在嚴重的電氣問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electrical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2a955255f249d33f04a","word":"electrician","forms":["electrician"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f63f22e59e81b6a","term":"electrician","forms":["electrician","electricians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電工","explanation":"指安裝、檢查、修理和維護電線、電路及各種電氣裝置的技術工人。記住“處理實際電氣系統的人”這條主線，就能和只研究電或設計大型系統的職業區分開。","examples":[{"en":"We called an electrician to fix the faulty socket.","zh":"我們叫來一名電工修理壞掉的插座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The electrician installed new lights in the kitchen.","zh":"電工在廚房安裝了新燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electrician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae80c184961f8640e6de","word":"electricity","forms":["electricity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a37fdeff45b10030","term":"electricity","forms":["electricity","electricities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電；電現象","explanation":"指由帶電粒子的分佈和運動產生的自然現象，也就是我們所說的“電”。它是後面“電力”和“電學”等意義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"Electricity can pass through some materials more easily than others.","zh":"電在某些材料中的傳導比在其他材料中更容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are still finding new ways to use electricity.","zh":"科學家仍在尋找利用電的新方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electricity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d0ccc6313e4137a","term":"electricity","forms":["electricity","electricities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電力；供電產生的功率","explanation":"指發電站或發電機提供、用來讓裝置工作的電力。記作“看不見的力量在做功”，重點是裝置正在使用的供電能力。","examples":[{"en":"This machine uses a lot of electricity.","zh":"這臺機器耗電量很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village now has enough electricity to run the water pumps.","zh":"這個村現在有足夠的電力執行水泵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electricity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-73e4c51456c25bab5458","word":"electronic","forms":["electronic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7473b0c1765adc8c","term":"electronic","forms":["electronic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"電子裝置產生的","explanation":"指由電子裝置製作、處理或播放出來的內容；裝置把看不見的電子訊號變成聲音、影象或其他可感知的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The band is famous for its electronic music.","zh":"這個樂隊以電子音樂聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An electronic beep signaled that the scan was complete.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electronic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a48ea13e43c22a7","term":"electronic","forms":["electronic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"網路上的；電子化的","explanation":"指透過電腦、網路或其他電子通訊手段完成的事物；這是從“電子裝置傳遞資訊”進一步延伸出的日常義。","examples":[{"en":"You can submit the form through the electronic payment system.","zh":"你可以透過電子支付系統提交這份表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep an electronic copy of the receipt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electronic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a848a87fec458f1f61a3","word":"electronics","forms":["electronics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b587e8e4cc709ec8","term":"electronics","forms":["electronics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子學；電子技術","explanation":"指研究和應用如何控制電子或其他帶電粒子流動的學科與技術，包括把電能轉換成其他形式能量的相關方法。這裡強調的是知識、原理和技術，而不是某一件裝置。","examples":[{"en":"Electronics is a popular subject at this college.","zh":"電子學是這所大學裡很受歡迎的一門學科。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied electronics before designing the circuit.","zh":"她先學習了電子學，然後才設計這個電路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electronics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de6d98724904e67f","term":"electronics","forms":["electronics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子裝置","explanation":"指靠電子在導體和半導體中流動來工作的裝置總稱，例如需要電池或插座供電的各種電子產品。這個意思關注的是看得見、可以使用的一組裝置，而不是研究它們的學科。","examples":[{"en":"Please unplug all the electronics in the room before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請把房間裡的所有電子裝置都拔掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep sensitive electronics away from moisture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electronics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4c3858f5f1e123198e8","word":"elegant","forms":["elegant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e633113e2a2e24d","term":"elegant","forms":["elegant","more elegant","most elegant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"優雅的；精緻得體的","explanation":"形容人、衣著、動作、語言、氣味、設計等具有自然、得體而令人欣賞的美感。它通常暗示不誇張、不過分裝飾，卻顯得有品位。","examples":[{"en":"She wore an elegant black dress to the ceremony.","zh":"她穿著一條優雅的黑色禮服參加典禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant has an elegant but relaxed atmosphere.","zh":"這家餐廳的氛圍優雅，卻又很輕鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elegant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-742cfd0679d921f5","term":"elegant","forms":["elegant","more elegant","most elegant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"簡潔而精準的","explanation":"形容解決辦法、論證、設計或程式沒有多餘步驟，卻能準確地達到目的。這裡的“優雅”不是外表好看，而是思路清楚、結構簡練、效果可靠。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer found an elegant solution to the problem.","zh":"這名工程師為這個問題找到了一個簡潔而精準的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proof offers an elegant solution using simple geometry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elegant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-445929267209c034d1e3","word":"element","forms":["element"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-022cc9ece39e4be5","term":"element","forms":["element","elements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基本組成部分","explanation":"指構成某個整體、體系或原則的基本部分；字母是書面語言的基本組成部分，正是這個核心義的直接例子。","examples":[{"en":"Letters are the basic elements of written language.","zh":"字母是書面語言的基本組成部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trust is an essential element of their partnership.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/element","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b87f0a66a58cc7f","term":"element","forms":["element","elements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最適合的環境","explanation":"把人或物想成回到最適合自己的那一塊環境：be in one's element就是“如魚得水、做得特別自在”。","examples":[{"en":"She was in her element during the cooking class.","zh":"上烹飪課時，她如魚得水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Surrounded by old books, she was in her element.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/element","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f06c64ed51a565c6b1c3","word":"elementary","forms":["elementary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce8c84b644ba8c24","term":"elementary","forms":["elementary","more elementary","most elementary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基礎的；基本的","explanation":"表示某事物處在最基礎、最重要的層面，是理解或構成更復雜內容所必需的部分。","examples":[{"en":"This book explains the elementary principles of economics.","zh":"這本書解釋了經濟學的基本原理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone should understand the elementary rules of safety.","zh":"每個人都應該瞭解最基本的安全規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elementary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f19717cbdb18a0e2","term":"elementary","forms":["elementary","more elementary","most elementary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非常簡單的","explanation":"表示某件事只需要很少的知識或技巧就能完成，簡單到幾乎不構成困難。","examples":[{"en":"The solution is elementary once you see the pattern.","zh":"一旦看出規律，這個解法就非常簡單了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experiment uses only elementary equipment.","zh":"這個實驗只使用最基本的裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elementary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd08c4c4316df20d9c30","word":"elephant","forms":["elephant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65402b44816d9072","term":"elephant","forms":["elephant","elephants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"象；大象","explanation":"指生活在非洲和亞洲的大型哺乳動物，最顯著的特徵是長鼻子和巨大的體形。這個詞既可以指一頭具體的大象，也可以泛指大象這一類動物。","examples":[{"en":"We saw an elephant near the river.","zh":"我們在河邊看見了一頭大象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Elephants use their trunks to pick up food.","zh":"大象用長鼻子撿起食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elephant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6dd02611ba74732","term":"elephant","forms":["elephant","elephants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"龐大笨重的東西","explanation":"由大象體形巨大、行動不便的形象引申，指某個物體、機構或計劃大得笨重、難以移動或處理。它不一定真的像動物，只要強調“過於龐大”即可。","examples":[{"en":"That old machine is an elephant to move around the office.","zh":"那臺舊機器太龐大笨重，在辦公室裡很難搬動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unused printing press became an elephant in our storeroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elephant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25508c0d59c3ca443b08","word":"elevate","forms":["elevate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2103474dd8876136","term":"elevate","forms":["elevate","elevates","elevating","elevated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抬高；升高","explanation":"把某物從較低位置抬到較高位置，是“向上託”的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Elevating your legs may help reduce the swelling.","zh":"抬高雙腿可能有助於減輕腫脹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The platform was elevated above the stage.","zh":"平臺被抬高到舞臺上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elevate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f3768209f469fc6","term":"elevate","forms":["elevate","elevates","elevating","elevated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提升價值或品質","explanation":"把原本普通的事物加工或呈現得更出色、更有價值，就像把它託到更高的層次。","examples":[{"en":"A good sauce can elevate a simple meal.","zh":"好的醬汁能讓一頓簡單的飯菜提升一個檔次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lighting elevated the entire performance.","zh":"燈光提升了整場演出的效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elevate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8244539b2ea5ca09","term":"elevate","forms":["elevate","elevates","elevating","elevated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提高程度或數值","explanation":"把某種水平、強度或數值往上推，例如提高血糖、風險或溫度。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of sleep can elevate your blood pressure.","zh":"睡眠不足可能會使血壓升高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discovery elevated the risk of further delays.","zh":"這項發現提高了進一步延誤的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elevate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41762bcf88c5e7148181","word":"elevator","forms":["elevator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b204b33d825b3140","term":"elevator","forms":["elevator","elevators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電梯","explanation":"指安裝在建築物中的轎廂或平臺，用來把人和貨物運送到不同樓層，是現代英語中最常見的含義之一。","examples":[{"en":"We took the elevator to the eighth floor.","zh":"我們乘電梯到了八樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The elevator is out of order, so we have to use the stairs.","zh":"電梯壞了，所以我們得走樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elevator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc99c152d84713fe276d","word":"eligible","forms":["eligible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5182b361f93d98c2","term":"eligible","forms":["eligible","more eligible","most eligible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"符合條件；有資格","explanation":"指某人或某物滿足參加、申請、領取或被選中的必要條件，就拿到了進入下一步的“通行證”。這隻說明具備資格，不保證最後一定成功或被選中。","examples":[{"en":"You may be eligible for a tax refund.","zh":"你可能有資格獲得退稅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only members who are over eighteen are eligible to vote.","zh":"只有年滿十八歲的會員才有資格投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eligible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea83ea4ec241a478","term":"eligible","forms":["eligible","more eligible","most eligible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"適合被選擇結婚","explanation":"指某人被認為條件合適、值得成為結婚物件，是“可以被選中”這一核心意思在婚姻選擇中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The magazine described him as one of the city's most eligible bachelors.","zh":"這本雜誌把他稱為城裡最適合結婚的單身漢之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wealthy bachelor was considered highly eligible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eligible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a60353a3fd8b779765b","word":"eliminate","forms":["eliminate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d132c6f8691127e","term":"eliminate","forms":["eliminate","eliminates","eliminating","eliminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徹底去掉","explanation":"把某種問題、物質、危險或不需要的東西完全清除，使它不再存在或不再造成影響。這是 eliminate 最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The new filter eliminates most of the dust in the room.","zh":"新過濾器能清除房間裡的大部分灰塵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to eliminate unnecessary steps from the process.","zh":"我們需要刪去流程中不必要的步驟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eliminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64274de4f16d8999","term":"eliminate","forms":["eliminate","eliminates","eliminating","eliminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排除或淘汰","explanation":"把某人或某隊從調查、選擇範圍或比賽中趕出去，使其不能繼續參與。例如，警方排除某人是嫌疑人，比賽中淘汰一支隊伍，都是把目標移出門檻外。","examples":[{"en":"The team was eliminated from the tournament in the first round.","zh":"這支隊伍在第一輪就被淘汰出比賽了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One loss will eliminate them from the tournament.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eliminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b89f45bfe540e1a97fc7","word":"eloquent","forms":["eloquent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-792e76833e294193","term":"eloquent","forms":["eloquent","more eloquent","most eloquent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能言善辯的；有說服力的","explanation":"形容一個人表達流暢、措辭準確，而且能讓聽者信服或受到感染。重點不只是“會說”，還包括說得清楚、有力量。","examples":[{"en":"She is an eloquent speaker who can explain complex ideas clearly.","zh":"她是一位很有說服力的演講者，能把複雜的想法解釋得很清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave an eloquent defense of the new policy.","zh":"他為這項新政策作了有力而清晰的辯護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eloquent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b321839da9b0c730","term":"eloquent","forms":["eloquent","more eloquent","most eloquent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表達效果強的；很能說明問題的","explanation":"形容言語、文章、影象或行動等把某種意思表達得特別清楚、有力，甚至不需要很多解釋。這裡的重點是表達本身產生了強烈效果，不一定涉及會說話的人。","examples":[{"en":"The empty chairs were an eloquent reminder of everyone who was absent.","zh":"那些空椅子有力地提醒人們，還有許多人沒有出席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her empty chair was an eloquent reminder of their loss.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eloquent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7dd530c4d36da47cd333","word":"else","forms":["else"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-634955ee9bd0a247","term":"else","forms":["else"],"pos":"adv","zh":"另外地；否則","explanation":"它表示從現有辦法之外尋找另一種辦法，或說明“不這樣做就會怎樣”。how else 可理解為“還能用什麼別的方法”，or else 則是“否則、不然”。","examples":[{"en":"How else can we get to the station?","zh":"我們還可以怎麼去車站？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hurry up, or else we'll miss the train.","zh":"快一點，不然我們會趕不上火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/else","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b1b763ee8f62eb88e47","word":"elsewhere","forms":["elsewhere"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-79054d93a838e1df","term":"elsewhere","forms":["elsewhere"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在別處；到別處","explanation":"指不在這裡、不到這裡，而是在另一個地方或前往另一個地方。它可以描述人或物的所在，也可以表示把注意力、行動轉向其他地方。","examples":[{"en":"If this shop is closed, we can eat elsewhere.","zh":"如果這家店關門了，我們可以去別處吃飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing files may be stored elsewhere.","zh":"丟失的檔案可能存放在別的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elsewhere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82244417f956ac7c599f","word":"email","forms":["email"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4175d2aa5afc1d14","term":"email","forms":["email","emails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子郵件系統","explanation":"指利用聯網計算機傳送和接收電子郵件的整套方式或系統，重點在“傳送電子信件的渠道”。","examples":[{"en":"Please send the documents by email.","zh":"請透過電子郵件傳送這些檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Email has replaced most internal paper memos.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/email","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d56e1a80a21b348e","term":"email","forms":["email","emails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一封電子郵件","explanation":"指透過電子郵件系統傳送的一條具體訊息，也就是可以單獨開啟、閱讀和轉發的一封電子信。","examples":[{"en":"I received an email confirming the appointment.","zh":"我收到了一封確認預約的郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sent me an email about the new schedule.","zh":"她給我發了一封關於新日程的郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/email","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a8d38ae779058ea","term":"email","forms":["email","emails","emailing","emailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給某人發郵件","explanation":"表示把一封或多封電子郵件傳送給某人，核心畫面就是把電子信件寄到對方的郵箱。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll email you when the results are ready.","zh":"結果出來後我會給你發郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager emailed everyone about the change.","zh":"經理給每個人發了郵件，說明這項變更。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/email","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-284a3b146dc7c03b","term":"email","forms":["email","emails","emailing","emailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"透過郵件傳送內容","explanation":"表示把連結、檔案、資訊等內容裝進電子郵件發給某人，重點是“把某物寄過去”。","examples":[{"en":"Please email me the final version tonight.","zh":"請今晚把最終版本透過郵件發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Email the completed form to the admissions office.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/email","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e3a7f2008954abd6c82","word":"embarrass(ment)","forms":["embarrass","embarrassment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5180cf9812ed7b5","term":"embarrass","forms":["embarrass","embarrasses","embarrassing","embarrassed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使人難堪","explanation":"指某人的言行讓另一個人在公開場合失去從容、感到羞窘或不自在，就像體面被“纏住”了一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The crowd's laughter embarrassed him.","zh":"人群的笑聲讓他感到很難堪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His loud complaints embarrassed everyone at the table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embarrass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d07238661dac413","term":"embarrassment","forms":["embarrassment","embarrassments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尷尬；難堪","explanation":"指因為害羞、失禮、出錯或意識到自己違反了社交規則而感到不自在、丟臉的狀態。它可以是輕鬆打趣帶來的臉紅，也可以是真正的受辱和難堪。","examples":[{"en":"She tried to hide her embarrassment by looking down at the table.","zh":"她低頭看著桌子，試圖掩飾自己的尷尬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"To his embarrassment, everyone heard his stomach growl during the meeting.","zh":"讓他尷尬的是，開會時所有人都聽到了他的肚子咕咕叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embarrassment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3deb0685104763e2","term":"embarrassment","forms":["embarrassment","embarrassments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人難堪的人或事","explanation":"指使別人丟臉、難堪或感到羞辱的人或事。這裡不是“感到尷尬”，而是“造成尷尬的物件”。","examples":[{"en":"His rude behavior was an embarrassment to his entire family.","zh":"他的粗魯行為讓全家人都感到難堪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That repeatedly malfunctioning machine became an embarrassment to its manufacturer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embarrassment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-667e55d79f7d12a07956","word":"embassy","forms":["embassy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92dfe3e26789453c","term":"embassy","forms":["embassy","embassies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"常駐使館；外交代表機構","explanation":"指一個國家在另一個國家長期設立的官方代表機構及其工作人員，負責外交聯絡和相關事務；也可泛指這一整套代表組織。","examples":[{"en":"The embassy in Tokyo issued a safety warning.","zh":"駐東京使館釋出了一則安全警告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works at the Canadian embassy in Beijing.","zh":"她在加拿大駐北京使館工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embassy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e783f142c07ca89","term":"embassy","forms":["embassy","embassies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臨時外交使團","explanation":"指為完成一次特定外交任務而臨時派出的代表團；重點不在固定辦公地點，而在“代表國家出發執行任務”。","examples":[{"en":"The president sent an embassy to negotiate a peace agreement.","zh":"總統派出一個外交使團去談判和平協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An embassy arrived bearing gifts from the neighboring king.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embassy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3962ce683c81e928fff5","word":"embrace","forms":["embrace"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0016a82ab8f58565","term":"embrace","forms":["embrace","embraces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擁抱","explanation":"指用雙臂抱住某人，把對方拉近自己的胸前，通常表達親近、安慰或喜愛。","examples":[{"en":"She greeted her old friend with a warm embrace.","zh":"她用一個熱情的擁抱迎接老朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child ran into his father's embrace.","zh":"孩子跑進父親的懷抱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c67caac8fb89a02","term":"embrace","forms":["embrace","embraces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接納","explanation":"指對某種信念、變化或生活方式完全接受，彷彿把它主動抱進自己的懷裡。","examples":[{"en":"Her embrace of change helped the team move forward.","zh":"她對變化的接納幫助團隊繼續向前發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city's embrace of cycling reduced traffic considerably.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8305026a010604ea","term":"embrace","forms":["embrace","embraces","embracing","embraced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擁抱","explanation":"指用雙臂抱住某人，把對方拉近自己，通常帶有感情或親近意味。","examples":[{"en":"The sisters embraced after years apart.","zh":"這對姐妹分離多年後擁抱在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He embraced his son and welcomed him home.","zh":"他擁抱了兒子，歡迎他回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2eeabf954f1a674c","term":"embrace","forms":["embrace","embraces","embracing","embraced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欣然接納","explanation":"指主動、熱情地接受機會、變化、想法或新事物，彷彿把它們抱進自己的範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The company embraced new technology to serve customers better.","zh":"這家公司欣然採用新技術，以便更好地服務客戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She embraced the opportunity to study abroad.","zh":"她欣然接受了出國學習的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15275743f9d383469da7","word":"emerge","forms":["emerge"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78eeae2b766b3150","term":"emerge","forms":["emerge","emerges","emerging","emerged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯現出來","explanation":"某人或某物原先被遮擋、隱藏或看不見，後來進入視線，就可以說它 emerge 了；重點是“從隱藏狀態中顯現出來”。","examples":[{"en":"As the fog lifted, the old tower emerged.","zh":"霧散去後，那座古塔顯現了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dark shape emerged from the fog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emerge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d8d722c103f4eb4","term":"emerge","forms":["emerge","emerges","emerging","emerged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從某處或處境中出來","explanation":"某人或某物從洞穴、液體、事故或困難處境中出來，強調從裡面或其中脫離出來，仍然保留著“從下方或隱藏處浮現”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She emerged from the cave covered in mud.","zh":"她從洞穴裡出來時渾身都是泥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After months of rehabilitation, she emerged stronger and more confident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emerge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e98460da93654c2","term":"emerge","forms":["emerge","emerges","emerging","emerged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸為人所知","explanation":"事實、真相或某種情況原先不清楚，經過調查、討論或時間推移後逐漸顯露出來，就是 emerge；這裡浮現的不是物體，而是資訊。","examples":[{"en":"After several interviews, a clearer picture of the accident emerged.","zh":"幾次採訪之後，人們逐漸更清楚地瞭解了事故的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New evidence emerged during the final week of the trial.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emerge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-b955e6cd0808744cf5cb","word":"emergency","forms":["emergency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7db8e24a21283369","term":"emergency","forms":["emergency","emergencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緊急情況","explanation":"指眼下有明顯危險、必須馬上處理的情況，例如嚴重受傷、火災或突發的醫療問題。這個義項保留了“紅色警報突然亮起”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Call an ambulance—this is a medical emergency.","zh":"叫救護車——這是醫療緊急情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep this number in case of an emergency.","zh":"請記住這個號碼，以備發生緊急情況時使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emergency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be1041adccf0fc8c","term":"emergency","forms":["emergency","emergencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"急診部門","explanation":"指醫院裡專門接收和處理急症的部門，也就是遇到需要立即救治的問題時要去的地方。它是“處理紅色警報的地方”，不是一般的醫院。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse told us to take him straight to emergency.","zh":"護士叫我們直接把他送到急診。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They took the injured cyclist straight to emergency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emergency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc20e299ed57ac6cdc16","word":"emigrant","forms":["emigrant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"emigrant","forms":["emigrant"],"pos":"n.","zh":"移出本國的人；移民者","examples":[{"en":"The museum displays letters written by an emigrant who left Ireland in 1850.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Each emigrant carried documents needed to begin a new life overseas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-b77b7bd9a4bcde4d32bf","word":"emigrate","forms":["emigrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1701c9bce6afbacc","term":"emigrate","forms":["emigrate","emigrates","emigrating","emigrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"移居國外","explanation":"指離開自己原來居住的國家，尤其是離開祖國，到另一個國家長期生活。這個詞把重點放在“從哪裡遷出”，不只是泛指搬到別處。","examples":[{"en":"Many families emigrated from Europe to Canada after the war.","zh":"戰後，許多家庭從歐洲移居到了加拿大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandparents emigrated when they were young.","zh":"她的祖父母年輕時移居到了國外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emigrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-184dff82ee6944b4744f","word":"emigration","forms":["emigration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2808ada03a76a096","term":"emigration","forms":["emigration","emigrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遷出；移居國外","explanation":"指一個人或一群人離開本國或本地區，到別處長期改變居住地的行為或過程；重點在“從這裡出去”。","examples":[{"en":"High unemployment has led to increased emigration from the region.","zh":"高失業率導致該地區的遷出人數增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government is studying the causes of emigration.","zh":"政府正在研究人口遷出的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emigration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06964dd2fac36383601c","word":"emission","forms":["emission"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aafaeed388d400be","term":"emission","forms":["emission","emissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排放物；發出的東西","explanation":"指從某處被送出來、散發出來或排出去的東西，例如光、氣體、聲音，或醫學語境中的血液。重點是“被送到外面來的結果”。","examples":[{"en":"The factory's emissions are damaging the local air quality.","zh":"這家工廠排放的廢氣正在損害當地的空氣質量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The emission was mostly blood.","zh":"排出的東西主要是血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9494c7efe345d0e1","term":"emission","forms":["emission","emissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發出；排放這一行為","explanation":"指把光、熱、氣體等從某處送出來的動作或過程。它關注的是“送出”本身，而不是最後被送出的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The emission of light from the sun warms the Earth.","zh":"太陽發出的光使地球變暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New rules aim to reduce the emission of greenhouse gases.","zh":"新規定旨在減少溫室氣體的排放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b9c4346fbead3ae18ec","word":"emotion","forms":["emotion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33c33d9e13e57c1c","term":"emotion","forms":["emotion","emotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情緒；情感","explanation":"指人在某種事情、感覺或處境影響下產生的內在感受，以及伴隨出現的身體和心理反應，例如喜悅、恐懼、悲傷或激動。它關注的是“被某事觸動後，內心和身體發生了什麼變化”。","examples":[{"en":"She tried to hide her emotion during the farewell.","zh":"告別時，她努力掩飾自己的情緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The music brought a strong emotion of sadness.","zh":"這首音樂帶來了一種強烈的悲傷情感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-edef7647443644bf","term":"emotion","forms":["emotion","emotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物的情緒反應","explanation":"指動物或其他非人類生物受到刺激時產生的、在行為和身體狀態上類似人類情緒的反應。這裡仍然是“被某事攪動並作出反應”的核心概念，只是主體不一定是人。","examples":[{"en":"The study suggests that dogs can show emotion through their facial expressions.","zh":"這項研究表明，狗可以透過面部表情表現出情緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers studied emotion in dogs separated from their owners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcab7f7d07fb2ac50991","word":"emotional","forms":["emotional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9a20542ea5ec3f2","term":"emotional","forms":["emotional","more emotional","most emotional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與情緒有關的","explanation":"表示某件事屬於情緒或感情這一方面，而不是身體、技術或純理性方面。它通常只是客觀分類，不一定含有負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"The family needed emotional support after the accident.","zh":"這家人在事故後需要情感上的支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The counselor offered emotional support during the transition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emotional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3171b7534d4775b7","term":"emotional","forms":["emotional","more emotional","most emotional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感情用事的","explanation":"表示決定或行動主要由強烈情緒推動，而不是經過冷靜、純理性的權衡。這裡常帶有“可能不夠理智”的暗示。","examples":[{"en":"He made an emotional decision and regretted it later.","zh":"他一時感情用事作了決定，後來後悔了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try not to send an emotional reply while you are angry.","zh":"生氣時儘量不要立刻發出感情用事的回覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emotional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5846d60018319b9e7970","word":"emperor","forms":["emperor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7b07b7cb55f55ad","term":"emperor","forms":["emperor","emperors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皇帝；帝王","explanation":"指統治帝國的男性君主，是 emperor 最基本、最常見的意思。這個詞強調他處在帝國政治權力的最高位置。","examples":[{"en":"The emperor ordered the army to return before winter.","zh":"皇帝下令軍隊在冬天前返回。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors can see the palace where the emperor once lived.","zh":"遊客可以看到皇帝曾經居住的宮殿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emperor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b0889bafaf77dc6","term":"emperor","forms":["emperor","emperors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帝國君主；皇帝（不限性別）","explanation":"也可以泛指統治帝國的君主，不論其性別；因此女性統治者在某些歷史或政治語境中也能稱為 emperor。這裡說的是君主本人的帝位，而不是君主的配偶。","examples":[{"en":"She became emperor after leading the country through the civil war.","zh":"她率領國家度過內戰後成為了皇帝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The emperor ruled through a network of provincial governors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emperor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd8c171b30ddda660f98","word":"emphasis","forms":["emphasis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2a0c3b4429e0848","term":"emphasis","forms":["emphasis","emphases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強調；著重","explanation":"指說話或寫作時有意給某個資訊加上更強的力量，讓聽者或讀者明顯感到它很重要，就像給這句話打上一束強光。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher put emphasis on clear pronunciation.","zh":"老師特別強調了清晰的發音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She repeated the warning for emphasis.","zh":"她重複了一遍警告，以加強語氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emphasis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3623a26c00d35fc6","term":"emphasis","forms":["emphasis","emphases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重點；著重關注","explanation":"指某個計劃、組織或討論把主要注意力放在某一方面；這裡不一定有強烈語氣，而是說“光”主要照在什麼地方。","examples":[{"en":"The course places emphasis on practical skills.","zh":"這門課程側重實用技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In planning the exhibition, we put greater emphasis on local artists.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emphasis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-c21f0c94db79d75f83d3","word":"emphasize","forms":["emphasize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9eeac6a573a4698","term":"emphasize","forms":["emphasize","emphasizes","emphasizing","emphasized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強調；著重指出","explanation":"把某個觀點、事實或特點特別突出，讓聽者或讀者注意到它的重要性，就叫強調。它不一定表示提高音量，也可以透過重複、特別說明或突出某個特點來實現。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher emphasized the importance of checking the figures carefully.","zh":"老師強調了仔細核對數字的重要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She emphasized that everyone should arrive on time.","zh":"她強調每個人都應該準時到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emphasize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d602bf8f470bc67ca7fa","word":"empire","forms":["empire"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2513e3867a3bb5f8","term":"empire","forms":["empire","empires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帝國","explanation":"指透過征服周邊領土、城市或國家而不斷擴大，形成的龐大政治國家，通常帶有統治和擴張的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The Roman Empire controlled much of Europe for centuries.","zh":"羅馬帝國幾個世紀以來控制著歐洲的大部分地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The empire expanded rapidly after the victory.","zh":"這 個帝國在勝利後迅速擴張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6301937576a8d335","term":"empire","forms":["empire","empires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"龐大事業集團","explanation":"比喻某個人或集團透過不斷擴充套件，建立起來的規模巨大、影響力很強的企業或事業版圖；這裡的“帝國”不一定是政治國家。","examples":[{"en":"She built a publishing empire from a small local magazine.","zh":"她從一家小地方雜誌起步，建立了一個出版帝國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The siblings inherited an empire of hotels and shopping centers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51a1f0ea765a801583e6","word":"employ(ment)","forms":["employ","employment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f536fae20f95286","term":"employ","forms":["employ","employs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受僱狀態","explanation":"指作為僱員為某人或某機構工作的狀態，也就是“在某人的僱用之下”。","examples":[{"en":"The school district has six thousand teachers in its employ.","zh":"這個學區僱用了六千名教師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent ten years in the employ of a large publisher.","zh":"她受一家大型出版社僱用了十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/employ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bc63d97cb3964bf","term":"employ","forms":["employ","employs","employing","employed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"僱用","explanation":"指正式僱某人為僱員，讓這個人進入某個工作崗位並持續為僱主工作。","examples":[{"en":"Our company employs hundreds of people.","zh":"我們公司僱用了數百人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital employs her as a laboratory technician.","zh":"這家醫院聘用她擔任實驗室技術員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/employ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c7a03f2e0ad5e99","term":"employ","forms":["employ","employs","employing","employed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使用","explanation":"指把某人、工具、方法或資源投入某項工作，以達到特定目的；核心仍是“讓它進入任務”。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer employed a simple tool to open the cover.","zh":"工程師使用一個簡單工具開啟了蓋子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laboratory employs lasers to measure tiny movements.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/employ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b04a494a0ddb8c19","term":"employment","forms":["employment","employments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工作；職業；就業","explanation":"指一個人從事的工作或職業，通常暗含這種工作帶來收入或正式的職業關係；也可泛指就業本身。","examples":[{"en":"After months of searching, she finally found employment at a small design firm.","zh":"經過幾個月的尋找，她終於在一家小型設計公司找到了工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory provides employment for hundreds of local residents.","zh":"這家工廠為數百名當地居民提供了就業機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/employment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c416a9b21820e75a","term":"employment","forms":["employment","employments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"僱用；聘用","explanation":"指僱主把某人安排來工作這一行為或過程，重點在“招人、聘人”這個動作，而不是員工已經處於工作的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The company has strict rules governing the employment of temporary workers.","zh":"這家公司對臨時工的僱用有嚴格規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The employment of minors is strictly regulated.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/employment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2fdc0177057d3a5c6c2c","word":"employee","forms":["employee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-246a55505ac0bfe8","term":"employee","forms":["employee","employees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"員工；僱員","explanation":"employee 是受公司、組織或個人僱用、為其完成工作並通常獲得報酬的人。記住“被僱來工作的人”這一核心形象，就能和僱主一方區分開。","examples":[{"en":"The company has more than five hundred employees.","zh":"這家公司有五百多名員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every employee receives health insurance.","zh":"每名員工都享有醫療保險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/employee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8efdf55724c97710333b","word":"employer","forms":["employer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-479d0d2764b6af41","term":"employer","forms":["employer","employers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"僱主","explanation":"僱主是提供工作、僱用他人並支付工資的一方，可以是一個人，也可以是公司或其他組織。","examples":[{"en":"The employer provides health insurance for all full-time workers.","zh":"這家僱主為所有全職員工提供醫療保險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works for a small employer near her home.","zh":"她為家附近的一家小型僱主工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/employer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e1cfa82b035c26cbbbd","word":"empty","forms":["empty"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6ddbf5ef2d6454e","term":"empty","forms":["empty","emptier","emptiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空的；裡面沒有東西","explanation":"指容器、房間或某個位置中沒有物品或人，是 empty 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The cupboard was empty, so we ordered dinner.","zh":"櫥櫃裡什麼也沒有，所以我們點了晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the empty box by the door.","zh":"請把空盒子放在門邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f361ff775c0d79a3","term":"empty","forms":["empty","emptier","emptiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空洞的；沒有誠意或效果的","explanation":"形容話語、承諾、威脅等表面上像有內容，實際上沒有真正的誠意、依據或作用。","examples":[{"en":"We are tired of empty promises.","zh":"我們已經厭倦了空洞的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His apology sounded like empty words.","zh":"他的道歉聽起來只是空話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44a25de3c6a59fdd","term":"empty","forms":["empty","empties","emptying","emptied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"清空；倒出","explanation":"表示把容器或空間裡的內容物拿走、倒出，使它變成 empty；也可指容器中的東西逐漸被用完。","examples":[{"en":"Could you empty the trash before you leave?","zh":"你離開前能把垃圾倒掉嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He emptied the water from the bucket.","zh":"他把桶裡的水倒了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e97166b54500da3a32ea","word":"enable","forms":["enable"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bfc5a59cbd893c7b","term":"enable","forms":["enable","enables","enabling","enabled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使能夠；賦予能力","explanation":"指給某人足夠的能力、力量或條件，使其能夠做某事或處於某種狀態。它正像是給人一把能開啟門的鑰匙，重點在於“具備做到的能力”。","examples":[{"en":"The new software enables employees to work from home.","zh":"這款新軟體使員工能夠在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A scholarship enabled her to study abroad.","zh":"一項獎學金使她能夠出國留學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-940f2c4e3b05400f","term":"enable","forms":["enable","enables","enabling","enabled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使成為可能；提供條件","explanation":"指提供機會、資源或必要條件，讓某件事得以發生，即使沒有直接教會某人具體怎麼做。它是“開啟一扇門”的最寬泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"The internet enables people to share information instantly.","zh":"網際網路使人們能夠即時分享資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The grant enabled the museum to remain open.","zh":"這筆撥款使博物館得以繼續開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7e45b6c390a26b23a7b","word":"enclose","forms":["enclose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e3733fe09104371","term":"enclose","forms":["enclose","encloses","enclosing","enclosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"圍住；圈起","explanation":"用牆、柵欄或其他邊界把土地、建築物等包圍起來，使它們處在一個限定範圍內。這裡的重點是形成“外邊有界線、裡面被包住”的空間。","examples":[{"en":"A low stone wall encloses the garden.","zh":"一堵低矮的石牆圍住了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farm is enclosed by a wooden fence.","zh":"這座農場四周用木柵欄圍了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enclose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27d75f7f73a0393b","term":"enclose","forms":["enclose","encloses","enclosing","enclosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隨信附上；裝入","explanation":"把檔案、支票或其他物品放進信封、包裹等容器中，使它隨信或包裹一起寄出。這裡仍然是“把東西封在一個範圍裡”，只是邊界從牆或柵欄變成了容器。","examples":[{"en":"I enclose a copy of my passport with this application.","zh":"隨本申請附上我的護照影印件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please enclose the receipt with your return.","zh":"請將收據隨退貨一併寄回。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enclose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f70b7769ae02a76af966","word":"encounter","forms":["encounter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-751566a7859adf80","term":"encounter","forms":["encounter","encounters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意外相遇","explanation":"指沒有事先安排、偶然發生的一次見面或相遇，重點在於事情出乎意料。","examples":[{"en":"I had a chance encounter with my old teacher at the station.","zh":"我在車站偶然遇到了以前的老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their first encounter happened during a power cut.","zh":"他們第一次相遇發生在一次停電時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc1c10e39364d6cb","term":"encounter","forms":["encounter","encounters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對抗；衝突","explanation":"指帶有敵意或暴力的一次正面碰撞，例如敵對雙方之間的交鋒。它是從“迎面相遇”發展出的更緊張的情形。","examples":[{"en":"The patrol had a brief encounter with armed robbers.","zh":"巡邏隊與武裝劫匪發生了短暫交鋒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The encounter left both sides with several injuries.","zh":"這次衝突導致雙方都有幾人受傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-feadac34f723e786","term":"encounter","forms":["encounter","encounters","encountering","encountered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"意外遇到","explanation":"指沒有預先安排就遇到某人，或在過程中發現、碰上某件事。它可以用於人，也可以用於問題、困難等事物。","examples":[{"en":"We encountered a strange dog on the mountain path.","zh":"我們在山路上遇到了一隻奇怪的狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team encountered several delays during the project.","zh":"團隊在專案期間遇到了幾次延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-421816f204eff3ac","term":"encounter","forms":["encounter","encounters","encountering","encountered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正面面對","explanation":"指與某人或某個困難、威脅面對面地相遇，需要直接處理對方或問題。這個意義比單純“碰見”更突出壓力和對峙感。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers encountered a bear near the river.","zh":"徒步旅行者在河邊正面遇到了一頭熊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She encountered strong opposition from the committee.","zh":"她遇到了委員會的強烈反對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bc416d34d81c38e2551","word":"encourage(ment)","forms":["encourage","encouragement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b406c94f1123cb8d","term":"encourage","forms":["encourage","encourages","encouraging","encouraged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給人打氣","explanation":"表示透過安慰、支援或肯定，讓某人更有勇氣和信心去面對困難或繼續努力。","examples":[{"en":"Her friends encouraged her when she felt like giving up.","zh":"她想放棄時，朋友們給了她鼓勵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher encouraged the shy student to speak up.","zh":"老師鼓勵那個害羞的學生大膽發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encourage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40f8f4e6a04992e6","term":"encourage","forms":["encourage","encourages","encouraging","encouraged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鼓勵採取行動","explanation":"表示積極推動某人或某群體去做某事，常帶有建議、提倡或強烈支援的意味；這裡推動的是具體行動，而不只是安慰對方。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign encourages people to use public transport.","zh":"這項宣傳活動鼓勵人們使用公共交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her mentor encouraged her to enter the competition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encourage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04edd295ebdb9ef8","term":"encouragement","forms":["encouragement","encouragements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼓勵這一行為","explanation":"指主動給別人信心、支援或動力的行為，也就是“鼓勵”這個過程本身，而不是某一句具體的話。","examples":[{"en":"The team needs encouragement after the disappointing result.","zh":"這個隊在令人失望的結果之後需要鼓勵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her encouragement helped him return to painting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encouragement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8f06c827004c240","term":"encouragement","forms":["encouragement","encouragements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼓勵人的話或行動","explanation":"指具體能讓人恢復信心、繼續努力的言語或行動，例如加油的話、陪伴和實際幫助；它是“推你一把”的具體內容。","examples":[{"en":"Her kind words gave me the encouragement to try again.","zh":"她親切的話給了我再次嘗試的勇氣和動力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The players heard encouragement from the crowd throughout the match.","zh":"整場比賽中，運動員不斷聽到觀眾的鼓勵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encouragement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93e42dd48381e964b79f","word":"encyclopedia","forms":["encyclopedia"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59f8d9d98c8ee776","term":"encyclopedia","forms":["encyclopedia","encyclopedias","encyclopediae","encyclopediæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"百科全書（紙質參考書）","explanation":"指系統介紹許多主題、通常篇幅很大的參考書或書套，內容可以按字母順序，也可以按主題分類編排。它像一個裝滿各類知識的圓圈，讀者可以從中查詢某個主題的基本資料。","examples":[{"en":"I found a clear explanation of the solar system in an encyclopedia.","zh":"我在一本百科全書裡找到了對太陽系的清楚解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library has a complete encyclopedia of world history.","zh":"這家圖書館有一套完整的世界歷史百科全書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encyclopedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9fc3d4a03996e980","term":"encyclopedia","forms":["encyclopedia","encyclopedias","encyclopediae","encyclopediæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"線上百科全書","explanation":"也可以指以網站、資料庫或其他數字形式存在的百科全書。雖然沒有紙書的外形，它仍然承擔著集中整理和解釋知識的作用。","examples":[{"en":"Students often use an online encyclopedia before checking more specialized sources.","zh":"學生們常常先查線上百科全書，再查更專業的資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She checked the dates in an online encyclopedia.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encyclopedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-361e48d0308f20e32dba","word":"end","forms":["end"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c65538fc7943d8f8","term":"end","forms":["end","ends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"終點；盡頭","explanation":"指某物在空間或時間上延伸到的最後一點，也就是從這裡繼續下去就沒有原來那一段了。它是“盡頭”這個核心畫面的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"We sat at the end of the long table.","zh":"我們坐在長桌的一端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop is at the end of this street.","zh":"那家店在這條街的盡頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/end","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a03707a261140ccb","term":"end","forms":["end","ends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結束；終止","explanation":"指一項活動、努力、狀態或運動停止，過程走到了盡頭；“Is there no end to...?”還可表示某事似乎沒完沒了。","examples":[{"en":"The noise finally came to an end.","zh":"噪音終於停下來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There seemed to be no end to the delays.","zh":"這些延誤似乎沒完沒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/end","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50d2f8fcf89b7539","term":"end","forms":["end","ends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目的；目標","explanation":"指行動想要達到的最終點，也就是努力最終要指向的目標；這是從“終點”自然發展出的抽象意義。","examples":[{"en":"We saved money to this end.","zh":"我們存錢就是為了這個目的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The end of the plan is to make travel cheaper.","zh":"這個計劃的目的是讓出行更便宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/end","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23b701e12adce4bef230","word":"endanger","forms":["endanger"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-588b4462bb479555","term":"endanger","forms":["endanger","endangers","endangering","endangered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……陷入危險","explanation":"指某人的行為、某種情況或某件事把人或事物置於可能受到傷害或損失的處境中。重點是“造成危險”，不一定表示傷害已經發生。","examples":[{"en":"Careless driving can endanger everyone on the road.","zh":"粗心駕駛可能使路上的每個人都陷入危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smoke endangered the health of nearby residents.","zh":"煙霧危及了附近居民的健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endanger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1cd38b20bf937895efff","word":"endeavor","forms":["endeavor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-396c7fc95816a668","term":"endeavor","forms":["endeavor","endeavors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認真努力；艱苦嘗試","explanation":"指朝著明確目標認真而持續地努力，也可以指需要投入心力的具體嘗試或事業。重點不只是“試”，而是為成功而不斷用力。","examples":[{"en":"Building a community garden was a demanding endeavor, but everyone was proud of the result.","zh":"建設社群花園是一項艱苦的努力，但大家都為成果感到自豪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Restoring the frescoes was a painstaking endeavor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endeavor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cce24da0d0858649","term":"endeavor","forms":["endeavor","endeavors","endeavoring","endeavored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"努力嘗試去做","explanation":"指為完成某事而認真用力地嘗試，強調行動者投入了相當的努力，而不是隻抱著試一試的態度。","examples":[{"en":"We will endeavor to answer all customer questions by Friday.","zh":"我們將努力在星期五之前回答所有客戶的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She endeavored to remain calm during the interview.","zh":"她努力在面試期間保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endeavor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-063a4c32864519ab1ced","word":"ending","forms":["ending"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1abb4e55e10e44ae","term":"ending","forms":["ending","endings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結束；收尾","explanation":"指一件事情或一個過程走到盡頭、完成收尾的階段，重點在“結束這一結果或過程”。","examples":[{"en":"The ending of the meeting was delayed by a long discussion.","zh":"會議的結束因為一次長時間的討論而推遲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stayed to watch the ending of the ceremony.","zh":"我們留下來看完了儀式的收尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ending","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03194b395a020327","term":"ending","forms":["ending","endings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結尾；最後部分","explanation":"指故事、電影、書或其他作品最後呈現出來的部分；它可以決定整個作品給人的最終感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The film has a surprising ending.","zh":"這部電影有一個出人意料的結尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel's ending explains the mysterious disappearance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ending","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf54be634e6a4dfd5901","word":"endorse(ment)","forms":["endorse","endorsement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11ede01271fc26c6","term":"endorse","forms":["endorse","endorses","endorsing","endorsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"公開支援；認可","explanation":"endorse 表示公開、正式地站在某人或某事一邊，表明自己認可並願意支援它。政治人物可以支援候選人，公司也可以認可某種產品或計劃；這正是“在背後留下支援印記”的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor endorsed her campaign for governor.","zh":"市長公開支援她競選州長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several doctors endorsed the new treatment.","zh":"幾位醫生認可了這種新療法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endorse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c47bbd3ca2b4aa29","term":"endorse","forms":["endorse","endorses","endorsing","endorsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在票據背面簽名轉讓","explanation":"在支票等可轉讓票據上，endorse 指持票人在背面簽名，以便把票據轉給別人或兌現。這裡仍然保留“在背面留下自己的印記”這一畫面，但不是表示贊成。","examples":[{"en":"Please endorse the cheque before giving it to the bank.","zh":"把支票交給銀行前，請先在背面簽名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Endorse the check before depositing it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endorse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47253a790c923ec4","term":"endorsement","forms":["endorsement","endorsements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支援；認可；背書","explanation":"指個人、團體或機構公開表示支援某項政策、產品、人物或主張，相當於在它後面蓋上“我認可”的章。這種支援通常帶有一定正式性或公開性。","examples":[{"en":"The association announced its endorsement of the new safety rules.","zh":"該協會宣佈支援新的安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal gained strong endorsement from local businesses.","zh":"這項提案得到了當地企業的大力支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endorsement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6374adef6f1b0f2","term":"endorsement","forms":["endorsement","endorsements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險或官方檔案的附加條款","explanation":"指加在保險合同、駕駛執照等正式檔案上的條款或備註。它就像把“認可”這個章具體寫進檔案中，用來增加、修改或說明某項保障或許可權。","examples":[{"en":"We added a flood-damage endorsement to our home insurance policy.","zh":"我們在房屋保險單上加了一項洪水損害附加條款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An endorsement extended the policy to cover flood damage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endorsement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e5d6d0adeb4a1952980","word":"endowment","forms":["endowment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25fea1b02735479a","term":"endowment","forms":["endowment","endowments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天賦；才能","explanation":"指一個人天生或獲得的特殊能力、品質或才華，也可以說某種事物所具有的特性。它強調“被賦予的能力”，比一般的 skill 更接近天賦或稟賦。","examples":[{"en":"Her musical endowment was clear from an early age.","zh":"她從小就顯露出音樂方面的天賦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Education can help children develop their natural endowments.","zh":"教育可以幫助孩子發展自己的天賦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endowment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3b2027922917327","term":"endowment","forms":["endowment","endowments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捐贈基金；資助財產","explanation":"指捐給個人或非營利機構、用於長期支援其工作的財產或資金，尤其常指由投資收益持續提供經費的基金。這裡的“資源”不是交給個人消費的一筆普通捐款，而是為了長期發揮作用。","examples":[{"en":"The university used the endowment to fund scholarships.","zh":"這所大學用捐贈基金資助獎學金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university's endowment funds several student scholarships.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endowment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be95e048ff6aaae6e320","word":"endurance","forms":["endurance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2269da19e7abbff1","term":"endurance","forms":["endurance","endurances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耐力；持久力","explanation":"指一個人持續進行體力或腦力活動、長時間堅持而不疲憊或不放棄的能力。馬拉松、長時間工作和持續訓練都可以體現這種耐力。","examples":[{"en":"She has the endurance to run for three hours without stopping.","zh":"她有連續跑三個小時而不停下來的耐力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular swimming has greatly improved my endurance.","zh":"經常游泳大大提高了我的耐力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endurance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd4ec1cdad799fd5","term":"endurance","forms":["endurance","endurances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承受困難的能力","explanation":"指人在痛苦、壓力或長期困難中仍能堅持下去的能力。這裡的重點不一定是身體強壯，而是面對艱難處境時能夠撐住、不輕易放棄。","examples":[{"en":"The long journey tested his endurance, but he never gave up.","zh":"這段漫長的旅程考驗了他的承受力，但他從未放棄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long trek tested everyone's endurance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endurance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93a80394715c57d83b03","word":"endure","forms":["endure"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49b2be27e21ec3ca","term":"endure","forms":["endure","endures","enduring","endured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堅持下去","explanation":"指人在障礙、壓力或困境中仍繼續做下去，沒有輕易放棄；重點是“扛住並堅持”。","examples":[{"en":"She endured through years of uncertainty and kept working toward her goal.","zh":"她熬過了多年的不確定，仍繼續朝著目標努力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The singer's popularity endured for decades.","zh":"這位歌手的受歡迎程度持續了幾十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cf16cdb6bc57fad","term":"endure","forms":["endure","endures","enduring","endured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忍受；熬過","explanation":"指接受並熬過令人痛苦、煩惱或不愉快的事情，通常暗含“雖然難受，但還是承受住了”。","examples":[{"en":"I could not endure the constant noise any longer.","zh":"我再也無法忍受持續不斷的噪音了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers endured the cold rain until they reached the shelter.","zh":"徒步者們忍受著冰冷的雨，直到抵達避難處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed1347b1c242f01f","term":"endure","forms":["endure","endures","enduring","endured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持續；長存","explanation":"指某種關係、影響、名聲、傳統或狀態經過很長時間仍然存在；這裡不是“忍受”，而是“經得住時間”。","examples":[{"en":"Their friendship endured for more than fifty years.","zh":"他們的友誼持續了五十多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our love will endure forever.","zh":"我們的愛將永遠長存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6610cc55246908a68b83","word":"enemy","forms":["enemy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ddb59bdfe741f12","term":"enemy","forms":["enemy","enemies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敵人；仇敵","explanation":"指對某人懷有敵意、反對其利益，或打算傷害某人的人。這個詞的核心畫面是“站在你對面的人”，可以是公開的對手，也可以是懷有仇恨的人。","examples":[{"en":"He refused to share the information with his enemy.","zh":"他拒絕把這條資訊告訴他的敵人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had made an enemy of a powerful local businessman.","zh":"她得罪了一位很有勢力的當地商人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enemy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40f6ccb09faa0d8b","term":"enemy","forms":["enemy","enemies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敵對勢力；敵軍成員","explanation":"指與己方敵對的國家、軍隊或其他武裝力量，也可以指其中的一名戰鬥人員。這裡的“敵人”從個人擴大成了整支站在對立面的力量。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers joined forces against a common enemy.","zh":"士兵們聯合起來對抗共同的敵人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The enemy crossed the river before dawn.","zh":"敵軍在黎明前渡過了河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enemy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa3531b78ac7cfc4a0cc","word":"energetic","forms":["energetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbe2f9ef85dc338a","term":"energetic","forms":["energetic","more energetic","most energetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精力旺盛的","explanation":"形容人或動物充滿活力、喜歡行動，像電量充滿一樣停不下來；也可形容行動或表達很有衝勁。","examples":[{"en":"Our new puppy is so energetic that it runs around the house all morning.","zh":"我們的小狗精力特別旺盛，整個上午都在屋裡跑來跑去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave an energetic speech that kept everyone interested.","zh":"她發表了一場充滿活力的演講，讓大家始終很感興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/energetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56199d06bf227013","term":"energetic","forms":["energetic","more energetic","most energetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能量高的","explanation":"在科學語境中，energetic 表示某種粒子、輻射或其他現象具有較高能量，而不是說它“很有活力”。","examples":[{"en":"The detector recorded a stream of energetic particles from the sun.","zh":"探測器記錄到了一股來自太陽的高能粒子流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Energetic particles struck the instrument's protective shield.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/energetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-381cfb6e1e428419d5d6","word":"energy","forms":["energy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f3661eb3921f977","term":"energy","forms":["energy","energies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推動力；勁頭","explanation":"指推動運動、行動或某種活動發生的力量，是“讓事情動起來”的廣義說法；既可以說機器，也可以說計劃、社會活動或人的行動。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy gave the project fresh energy.","zh":"這項新政策給這個專案注入了新的活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Braking the heavy train takes a lot of energy.","zh":"讓這列重型列車剎車需要消耗大量能量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/energy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb3c6d9dc23cc6c7","term":"energy","forms":["energy","energies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精力；做事的勁頭","explanation":"指人或動物能夠投入行動的精力和體力。它仍然保留“推動行動”的核心形象，但重點從外部運動轉向一個人當下有多少勁頭去做事。","examples":[{"en":"I don't have enough energy to cook tonight.","zh":"我今晚沒有足夠的精力做飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children still had plenty of energy after the hike.","zh":"孩子們徒步之後仍然精力充沛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/energy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-905c294018a2d0815f23","word":"enforce(ment)","forms":["enforce","enforcement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d5bfe17ae535cc5","term":"enforce","forms":["enforce","enforces","enforcing","enforced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"執行；實施（法律、規定）","explanation":"透過執法、檢查或處罰等手段讓法律、規定或禁令真正得到遵守，也就是給規則加上使其落地的力量。","examples":[{"en":"The police are working hard to enforce the new traffic laws.","zh":"警方正在努力執行新的交通法規。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school strictly enforces its no-smoking policy.","zh":"這所學校嚴格執行禁菸規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enforce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a444c9f99013259","term":"enforcement","forms":["enforcement","enforcements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強制執行；監督落實","explanation":"指透過監督、處罰或其他強制手段，使人遵守法律、規則或命令。這是最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思，重點在“讓人照做”。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy will require stricter enforcement of safety rules.","zh":"新政策將要求更嚴格地落實安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without consistent enforcement, the ban will have little effect.","zh":"如果不能持續執行，這項禁令將很難發揮作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enforcement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-951d8ea077202a2f","term":"enforcement","forms":["enforcement","enforcements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使規定生效；付諸實施","explanation":"指把法律、政策或決定真正落實到現實中，使它不只是紙面上的規定。和 s1 相比，這一義更突出“讓規定產生實際效力”，不一定強調具體的強制行為。","examples":[{"en":"The enforcement of the new regulations begins next month.","zh":"新規定將於下個月開始實施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Consistent enforcement of the rules improved road safety.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enforcement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cddc2b01a83ae16c3e0e","word":"engage(ment)","forms":["engage","engagement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ce3fe9b81e6606c","term":"engage","forms":["engage","engages","engaging","engaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸引並使人投入","explanation":"把某人的注意力、興趣或關心接到某件事上，使其投入其中；重點不只是“接觸”，還常含有“吸引住”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The story engaged the children's imagination.","zh":"這個故事激發了孩子們的想象力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speaker quickly engaged the audience.","zh":"演講者很快吸引了觀眾的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-738c1fb93701612a","term":"engage","forms":["engage","engages","engaging","engaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人參與交談","explanation":"把某人接入談話或社交活動中，通常表示主動找對方說話，讓對方參與進來。","examples":[{"en":"She engaged the shy student in conversation.","zh":"她主動和那個害羞的學生交談，讓他參與進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to engage your guests in a light discussion.","zh":"試著讓客人參與輕鬆的討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b9d936f7f11f646","term":"engage","forms":["engage","engages","engaging","engaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聘請或僱用","explanation":"把某人接入一項工作或服務關係中，即正式聘請、僱用某人；也可指按約定請人提供服務。","examples":[{"en":"The company engaged a consultant to review its accounts.","zh":"公司聘請了一名顧問來審查賬目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They engaged a local guide for the expedition.","zh":"他們為這次探險聘請了一名當地嚮導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-326e2ba1b0f221ec","term":"engagement","forms":["engagement","engagements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連線；齧合","explanation":"指兩個部件、裝置或力量彼此接上並開始有效配合。它保留了“接到一起”的核心影象，例如齒輪完全齧合後，轉動才能傳過去。","examples":[{"en":"Check the gears for full engagement before turning the handle.","zh":"轉動手柄前，檢查齒輪是否完全齧合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanism prevents accidental engagement of the gears.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engagement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-696c96f2fec80808","term":"engagement","forms":["engagement","engagements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投入感；參與度","explanation":"指人被某件事吸引、持續關注，並覺得自己和正在發生的事情有聯絡。它不只是“參加過”，而是注意力和興趣真正接上了活動、內容或過程。","examples":[{"en":"The interactive workshop kept the students' engagement high.","zh":"這場互動式研討課讓學生始終保持很高的參與度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game uses short challenges to increase player engagement.","zh":"這款遊戲用簡短的挑戰來提高玩家的投入感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engagement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed9f6f25068608efd412","word":"engine","forms":["engine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98cacb9c60e01bf2","term":"engine","forms":["engine","engines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機械動力裝置","explanation":"指把能量轉化為運動或其他有用效果的複雜機械裝置。汽車發動機屬於這個大類，但這個義項本身不只限於汽車。","examples":[{"en":"The machine is powered by a small diesel engine.","zh":"這臺機器由一臺小型柴油發動機驅動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Engineers designed an engine that uses less fuel.","zh":"工程師設計了一種耗油更少的發動機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18c9ffa984abf2bc","term":"engine","forms":["engine","engines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽車發動機","explanation":"特指汽車或其他車輛中提供行駛動力的部分，是現代日常英語裡最常見的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"The car's engine stopped at the traffic lights.","zh":"那輛車的發動機在紅綠燈處熄火了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took the car to a garage because the engine was making a strange noise.","zh":"她把車送到修車廠，因為發動機發出了奇怪的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7826b958b79c70626801","word":"engineer","forms":["engineer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-267b91fe2699e23b","term":"engineer","forms":["engineer","engineers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工程師；工程專業人員","explanation":"指受過工程訓練、從事機器或其他工程領域設計、建造、維護，或正在學習這些工作的專業人員。這是現代最基本、最廣的職業意思。","examples":[{"en":"The engineers are testing a safer design for the new train.","zh":"工程師們正在測試新列車更安全的設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I studied engineering before becoming an engineer.","zh":"我先學了工程學，後來成為了一名工程師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engineer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c85b6639e62e10b8330","word":"engineering","forms":["engineering"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36ea9f8796622a2a","term":"engineering","forms":["engineering","engineerings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工程學；工程技術","explanation":"指運用數學、物理等科學知識，設計和建造裝置、系統或基礎設施，以解決人類實際需要的學科和實踐。它既可以指整個工程領域，也可以指其中的技術工作。","examples":[{"en":"She studied engineering at university and now designs water-treatment systems.","zh":"她在大學學習工程學，現在設計水處理系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good engineering can make a building safer and more efficient.","zh":"優秀的工程設計能讓建築更安全、更高效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engineering","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c18fb018bd690f8","term":"engineering","forms":["engineering","engineerings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有計劃地操控或設計","explanation":"指透過技術、設計或安排，主動控制某個物體的運動、形狀或成分，使它達到預期狀態。這裡強調的不是工程學這門學科，而是“把物件按計劃加工或操控”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The engineering of the device allows it to change shape in seconds.","zh":"這臺裝置的設計使它能在幾秒鐘內改變形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Social engineering can manipulate people into revealing passwords.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engineering","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-17a75bc41da46ee2e7f3","word":"enhance(ment)","forms":["enhance","enhancement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-047628cdd0382ac9","term":"enhance","forms":["enhance","enhances","enhancing","enhanced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"增強；提高","explanation":"指讓某種程度、價值、影響力或效果變得更大、更強。它不一定表示數量增加，也可以表示聲譽、吸引力或作用得到提升。","examples":[{"en":"Good lighting can enhance the colors in the room.","zh":"良好的照明可以增強房間裡的色彩效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The award enhanced her reputation as a researcher.","zh":"這項獎項提升了她作為研究人員的聲譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enhance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78d6d0e8fe13b2e2","term":"enhance","forms":["enhance","enhances","enhancing","enhanced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"透過新增細節改善","explanation":"指在原有基礎上加入裝飾、功能或其他細節，使某物看起來更好、用起來更方便，或整體效果更突出。這仍然是把東西“提升一格”，但重點在改善品質和表現。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow frame enhances the beauty of the painting.","zh":"窄邊框提升了這幅畫的美感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app was updated to enhance the user experience.","zh":"這個應用經過更新，以改善使用者體驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enhance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d463fd3b4a5274b3","term":"enhancement","forms":["enhancement","enhancements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"改進；提升","explanation":"指給產品、服務、設計或體驗增加改進或補充，使它更好、更有吸引力或更受重視。它既可以指具體增加的一項功能，也可以指整體提升這一結果。","examples":[{"en":"The new safety features are a major enhancement to the original design.","zh":"新的安全功能是對原設計的一項重大改進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The software has received several enhancements since its release.","zh":"這款軟體釋出以來已經進行了多項改進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enhancement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6efe7f663fcd0046b46","word":"enjoy(ment)","forms":["enjoy","enjoyment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a695e6bf0082486c","term":"enjoy","forms":["enjoy","enjoys","enjoying","enjoyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"享受；從……中獲得快樂","explanation":"指從食物、活動、旅行、陪伴等事物中得到快樂或滿足，是這個詞最常見、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We really enjoyed the concert last night.","zh":"我們昨晚非常享受那場音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She enjoys cooking for her friends.","zh":"她喜歡為朋友做飯，也很享受這個過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enjoy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d96d0c742ff7719","term":"enjoy","forms":["enjoy","enjoys","enjoying","enjoyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"享有；擁有並受益於","explanation":"指擁有並能夠使用或受益於某種條件、權利或好處，重點不一定是當下的快樂，而是“享有”這種有利狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Older residents enjoy free bus travel in this city.","zh":"這座城市的老年居民享有免費乘坐公交車的待遇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Employees enjoy free access to the swimming pool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enjoy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21d2c2e801101853","term":"enjoyment","forms":["enjoyment","enjoyments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"享受；愉悅","explanation":"指從某件事、某種經歷或某種陪伴中得到的快樂和滿足，重點是“享受的感覺”本身。","examples":[{"en":"The enjoyment of a good meal is even greater when you share it with friends.","zh":"和朋友一起分享時，享用一頓美餐的樂趣更大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Music adds to the enjoyment of the journey.","zh":"音樂增加了旅途中的樂趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enjoyment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cfb3fd600cef8f4","term":"enjoyment","forms":["enjoyment","enjoyments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愉快的心境","explanation":"指一個人處在滿足、快樂的心理狀態中；它關注的是內在心情，而不只是某項活動帶來的瞬間樂趣。","examples":[{"en":"She read the novel slowly, taking great enjoyment in every chapter.","zh":"她慢慢讀著這部小說，每一章都讀得十分快樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He works in the garden for the sheer enjoyment of it.","zh":"他在花園裡勞作，純粹是因為其中的樂趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enjoyment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f77470ce4f1959e59348","word":"enjoyable","forms":["enjoyable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5199f2110b71034c","term":"enjoyable","forms":["enjoyable","more enjoyable","most enjoyable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人愉快的","explanation":"指某件事或某段經歷能帶來快樂，讓人覺得舒服、有趣並願意享受其中。它可以形容一天、旅行、電影、活動等，而不是專門描述人的感受。","examples":[{"en":"We had an enjoyable evening by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個愉快的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The class was enjoyable because everyone took part.","zh":"這堂課很有趣，因為每個人都參與了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enjoyable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a1b393694e567075d04","word":"enlarge(ment)","forms":["enlarge","enlargement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0ae7d1cdfe2525d","term":"enlarge","forms":["enlarge","enlarges","enlarging","enlarged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……變大","explanation":"表示主動把某個具體或抽象物件做得更大，例如擴大房間、照片、預算或計劃的規模。重點是“讓某物變大”，所以後面通常要有被擴大的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The museum plans to enlarge the main gallery next year.","zh":"博物館計劃明年擴建主展廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had to enlarge the budget to cover the extra repairs.","zh":"我們不得不增加預算來支付額外的維修費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enlarge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e829d860b7a46cf3","term":"enlarge","forms":["enlarge","enlarges","enlarging","enlarged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變大","explanation":"表示某物自身逐漸變大，不強調誰主動把它擴大。它可以描述實際尺寸，也可以描述問題、影響或某種範圍逐漸增加。","examples":[{"en":"The crack in the wall began to enlarge after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，牆上的裂縫開始變大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The image enlarges when you click the thumbnail.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enlarge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88d4b53b3a52b46f","term":"enlarge","forms":["enlarge","enlarges","enlarging","enlarged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擴大容量、範圍或思想空間","explanation":"在抽象語境中，表示讓某種能力、範圍或容納空間變得更寬廣，例如擴大知識帶來的思想空間。這裡不一定是物理尺寸變大，而是可容納、可理解或可發展的範圍增加。","examples":[{"en":"Travel can enlarge our understanding of other cultures.","zh":"旅行可以拓展我們對其他文化的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The debate enlarged his ideas about what democracy could achieve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enlarge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1994c3d12ea5dca","term":"enlargement","forms":["enlargement","enlargements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擴大；增大","explanation":"指把某物做得比原來更大，或這一變化本身。它可以指實際尺寸的增加，也可以指某種身體部位、空間或物件的擴大。","examples":[{"en":"The enlargement of the storage room gave us much more space.","zh":"儲藏室擴大後，我們多出了很多空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose surgery for breast enlargement.","zh":"她選擇了隆胸手術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enlargement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31f25f062d4bb2697eba","word":"enlighten(ment)","forms":["enlighten","enlightenment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45971cc6e5cb64a1","term":"enlighten","forms":["enlighten","enlightens","enlightening","enlightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使明白；增長見識","explanation":"透過解釋、事實或知識把“理解之光”帶給某人，使對方明白某件事或獲得新的認識。重點不只是傳遞資訊，而是幫助對方真正理解。","examples":[{"en":"Could you enlighten me about the new safety rules?","zh":"你能給我講講新的安全規定嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide enlightened us about the history of the old town.","zh":"導遊向我們介紹了這座老城的歷史，使我們增長了見識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enlighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2532f5e9cebdcb90","term":"enlightenment","forms":["enlightenment","enlightenments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啟發；理解","explanation":"指接受教育、解釋或啟發後，原來不明白的事情變得清楚，也可以指這種“被點亮”的狀態。重點不只是得到一條資訊，而是形成了更清晰、更成熟的認識。","examples":[{"en":"Reading the book gave her a new enlightenment about how memory works.","zh":"讀完這本書後，她對記憶如何運作有了新的認識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His explanation brought enlightenment to a problem we had struggled with for weeks.","zh":"他的解釋讓困擾我們幾周的問題變得清楚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enlightenment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7e5fe1ab2a1098f","term":"enlightenment","forms":["enlightenment","enlightenments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"覺悟；開悟","explanation":"指透過反思、修行或深入思考，獲得對自我、現實和真相的深層清晰認識。這裡的“光”不只是知識增加，而是看穿表面迷惑、改變看待世界的方式。","examples":[{"en":"The monk spent many years seeking enlightenment through meditation.","zh":"這位僧人花了許多年透過冥想尋求開悟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monk sought enlightenment through years of meditation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enlightenment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c354eb166766cbcb08ae","word":"enormous","forms":["enormous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49bb02d28604a28a","term":"enormous","forms":["enormous","more enormous","most enormous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巨大的；極其多的","explanation":"這是現代英語的核心義：某個東西、數量或影響大到遠遠超出通常尺度。它既能形容具體物體，也能強調工作量、費用、壓力或影響等抽象事物的驚人程度。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused enormous damage to the coastal towns.","zh":"這場暴風雨給沿海城鎮造成了極其嚴重的破壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made an enormous effort to finish the project on time.","zh":"她付出了巨大的努力，按時完成了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enormous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,114],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-6f6465f9dd0685853e76","word":"enough","forms":["enough"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bfbb51dd17445e1","term":"enough","forms":["enough"],"pos":"adv","zh":"足夠地；達到所需程度","explanation":"表示某種性質或動作的程度已經達到要求，常常隱含“足以完成某事”的意思。它強調的是越過某個必要的程度門檻，而不只是程度比較高。","examples":[{"en":"The soup isn't cool enough to drink.","zh":"這湯還不夠涼，不能喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke slowly enough for everyone to follow.","zh":"她說得足夠慢，大家都能聽懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f75915767d72d786","term":"enough","forms":["enough"],"pos":"det","zh":"足夠的","explanation":"表示某種東西的數量達到實際需要，重點是“夠用”，並不表示數量特別多。它可以修飾不可數名詞，也可以修飾可數名詞複數。","examples":[{"en":"We have enough chairs for everyone.","zh":"我們有足夠的椅子，人人都有座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There isn't enough time to finish the report.","zh":"沒有足夠的時間完成這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30678dea2d9417c16f15","word":"enrich(ment)","forms":["enrich","enrichment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0b4e7f805743d05","term":"enrich","forms":["enrich","enriches","enriching","enriched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提升；使更豐富","explanation":"表示改善某人或某物的質量、內容或價值，使它比原來更豐富、更有意義；不一定涉及金錢。","examples":[{"en":"Travel can enrich your understanding of other cultures.","zh":"旅行可以加深你對其他文化的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reading has enriched her life in many ways.","zh":"閱讀從許多方面豐富了她的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enrich","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2b46ece4e1f8360","term":"enrich","forms":["enrich","enriches","enriching","enriched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變富或更富有","explanation":"表示讓人、生活或某種經歷變得更富足；既可以指經濟上的富裕，也可以指生活內容和精神收穫變多。","examples":[{"en":"The experience enriched him more than he had expected.","zh":"這段經歷帶給他的收穫比他預想的更多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new business greatly enriched the family.","zh":"這項新生意讓這個家庭富裕了許多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enrich","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91b201e731a130d5","term":"enrichment","forms":["enrichment","enrichments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豐富、增益","explanation":"指在原有基礎上增加有價值的內容、成分或體驗，使某物變得更豐富、更充實。這是最寬泛的含義，其他專門含義都可以看作對某種物件“加料”或“增益”。","examples":[{"en":"Travel can bring great enrichment to a person's life.","zh":"旅行可以給人的生活帶來很大的充實和提升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum's new programs offer enrichment for visitors of all ages.","zh":"博物館的新專案為各個年齡段的參觀者提供了豐富體驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enrichment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6018211521361c8c","term":"enrichment","forms":["enrichment","enrichments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鈾濃縮","explanation":"在核技術語境中，指提高鈾中某種特定同位素比例的過程。這裡的“豐富”不是一般意義上的變好，而是對材料成分進行濃度提升。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement places limits on uranium enrichment.","zh":"這項協議對鈾濃縮設定了限制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plant conducts uranium enrichment under international inspection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enrichment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b182aa29355c7398f39","word":"enroll(ment)","forms":["enroll","enrollment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b223a99ee623eaf","term":"enroll","forms":["enroll","enrolls","enrolling","enrolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"登記入冊","explanation":"把某人的姓名或資料正式寫入名冊、登記表或名單中，重點是完成記錄這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The office enrolled every new voter in the local register.","zh":"辦公室把每位新選民都登記進了當地選民名冊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please enroll your child in the school database before Friday.","zh":"請在星期五前把孩子登記到學校資料庫中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enroll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73cb6ffc82f3d459","term":"enroll","forms":["enroll","enrolls","enrolling","enrolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"招收為成員","explanation":"讓某人加入組織、隊伍或專案，使其成為正式成員；這裡更突出“招收或吸納”這個結果。","examples":[{"en":"The club hopes to enroll more young members this year.","zh":"這個俱樂部希望今年招收更多年輕成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity enrolled several volunteers in its training program.","zh":"這家慈善機構招收了幾名志願者參加培訓專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enroll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62a10b55bd80079d","term":"enroll","forms":["enroll","enrolls","enrolling","enrolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"報名加入","explanation":"自己正式報名參加課程、專案、組織或其他活動，也就是把自己的名字寫進相關名單。","examples":[{"en":"I enrolled in an evening photography course last month.","zh":"我上個月報名參加了一門晚間攝影課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you enrolled in the summer program yet?","zh":"你報名參加暑期專案了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enroll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e65ef4b41a9052e","term":"enrollment","forms":["enrollment","enrollments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報名；註冊；在冊狀態","explanation":"指把名字登記進去的行為，也指登記完成後處於在冊狀態。重點是“進入名單”這一過程或結果，而不是名單上的具體人數。","examples":[{"en":"Enrollment for the summer course closes on Friday.","zh":"暑期課程的報名於週五截止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her enrollment at the university was confirmed yesterday.","zh":"她在這所大學的註冊情況昨天得到了確認。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enrollment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4c56ae6acff5a8f","term":"enrollment","forms":["enrollment","enrollments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報名者；在冊人員","explanation":"把已經報名或註冊的人看作一個整體，強調名單上的這群人，而不是報名這一行為。","examples":[{"en":"The program's enrollment includes students from twelve countries.","zh":"這個專案的在冊學生來自十二個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Enrollment at the college now exceeds three thousand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enrollment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27ce252594811401f987","word":"ensure","forms":["ensure"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa3fb16b0416dc49","term":"ensure","forms":["ensure","ensures","ensuring","ensured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確保；保證發生","explanation":"指採取行動或作出安排，使預期的事情確實發生，像把結果牢牢固定住一樣。重點在結果得到保障，而不只是口頭表達信心。","examples":[{"en":"I set two alarms to ensure that I wake up on time.","zh":"我設了兩個鬧鐘，以確保自己準時起床。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check the address to ensure safe delivery.","zh":"請核對地址，以確保貨物安全送達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ensure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e08d706b3e4ce964b632","word":"enter","forms":["enter"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-552b9d2ba12fb62a","term":"enter","forms":["enter","enters","entering","entered","entred","enterest","entrest","enteredst","entredst","entres","-","entring"],"pos":"verb","zh":"進入（空間）","explanation":"指人或物從外面進入房間、建築物等封閉或半封閉空間，是“跨過門進入裡面”的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please knock before you enter the office.","zh":"進辦公室前請先敲門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She entered the building through the side door.","zh":"她從側門進入了大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a16f08a3143af570","term":"enter","forms":["enter","enters","entering","entered","entred","enterest","entrest","enteredst","entredst","entres","-","entring"],"pos":"verb","zh":"進入某種狀態或階段","explanation":"把抽象的狀態、年齡階段、職業或活動看成一扇門，表示開始處於其中。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter will enter high school next year.","zh":"我女兒明年將進入高中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He entered politics after working as a lawyer.","zh":"他當了幾年律師後進入了政界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f82abbe4cf4abfa8","term":"enter","forms":["enter","enters","entering","entered","entred","enterest","entrest","enteredst","entredst","entres","-","entring"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輸入","explanation":"表示把姓名、密碼、數字等內容送進電腦或其他系統，就像把資訊跨過螢幕上的門送進去。","examples":[{"en":"Enter your email address and click Continue.","zh":"輸入你的電子郵箱地址，然後點選“繼續”。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please enter the code into the box below.","zh":"請在下面的框中輸入程式碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b97ac5e767e5393cd0e","word":"enterprise","forms":["enterprise"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e28749c8d7623c0","term":"enterprise","forms":["enterprise","enterprises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"企業；事業組織","explanation":"指為某個明確目的而運作的公司、商業組織或其他正式事業。重點不只是“公司”這個實體，還包括它持續開展的有組織活動。","examples":[{"en":"The family turned the small farm into a successful enterprise.","zh":"這家人把小農場經營成了一項成功的事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new enterprise provides affordable housing for students.","zh":"這家新企業為學生提供價格可負擔的住房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enterprise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac4076e40de3121f","term":"enterprise","forms":["enterprise","enterprises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事業；大膽的專案","explanation":"指被接下並努力完成的一項任務、計劃或事業，尤其強調它規模大、難度高或帶有冒險性。它可以是科學、公益或其他非商業專案。","examples":[{"en":"Building a research station in the desert was a challenging enterprise.","zh":"在沙漠中建造研究站是一項頗具挑戰的事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue enterprise lasted through the night.","zh":"這項救援行動持續了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enterprise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c7fe001fb04640c3fc2","word":"entertain(ment)","forms":["entertain","entertainment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8007cef5ebeb1f39","term":"entertain","forms":["entertain","entertains","entertaining","entertained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使人開心；娛樂","explanation":"透過有趣的談話、表演或活動吸引並保持某人的注意力，使對方感到愉快。核心畫面就是把人的注意力留在一段愉快的體驗中。","examples":[{"en":"The magician entertained the children with a funny story.","zh":"魔術師用一個有趣的故事逗得孩子們很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She entertained us while we waited for dinner.","zh":"我們等晚餐時，她一直逗我們開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entertain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8bb3044c0a880635","term":"entertain","forms":["entertain","entertains","entertaining","entertained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"招待客人；請人到家裡做客","explanation":"指邀請客人到家裡或某個場所，併為他們安排吃飯、聊天等活動。這裡仍然是把人接到自己的圈子裡，讓他們愉快地待著。","examples":[{"en":"We often entertain friends at home on Saturday evenings.","zh":"我們週六晚上經常在家招待朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their dining room is too small to entertain more than six guests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entertain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbf58d9afcc1b869","term":"entertain","forms":["entertain","entertains","entertaining","entertained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"考慮；接受某個想法","explanation":"指把一個想法、可能性或建議留在腦中，認真考慮它是否可行，而不一定表示已經同意。它把“留住某物”的畫面從人和注意力擴充套件到了思想。","examples":[{"en":"The team is entertaining the idea of moving the office.","zh":"團隊正在考慮搬遷辦公室的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I never entertained the possibility that he was lying.","zh":"我從未考慮過他可能在撒謊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entertain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f74e028b3c71b47d","term":"entertainment","forms":["entertainment","entertainments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"娛樂活動","explanation":"指以帶來快樂、消遣或放鬆為目的的活動，既可以是觀眾觀看，也可以是參與者親自參加；電影、音樂、遊戲等都包括在內。","examples":[{"en":"The children found plenty of entertainment at the science museum.","zh":"孩子們在科學博物館裡找到了許多有趣的娛樂活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel offers entertainment for guests of all ages.","zh":"這家酒店為各個年齡段的客人提供娛樂活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entertainment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67d4f9cb66193dc6","term":"entertainment","forms":["entertainment","entertainments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"娛樂節目；演出","explanation":"特指為別人安排或呈現的一場娛樂節目、演出或表演，是“娛樂活動”中較具體的一項。","examples":[{"en":"There will be live entertainment after dinner.","zh":"晚餐後將有現場娛樂節目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cruise included evening entertainment in the lounge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entertainment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87a738aed26af0059fee","word":"enthusiasm","forms":["enthusiasm"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0baad903e634cfd0","term":"enthusiasm","forms":["enthusiasm","enthusiasms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈熱情；興奮投入","explanation":"指因某事而產生的強烈興奮、熱情和積極投入，彷彿心裡的火被點燃了。它既可以形容對某件事的興趣很濃，也可以強調做事時的興奮勁頭。","examples":[{"en":"Her enthusiasm for the project encouraged the whole team.","zh":"她對這個專案的熱情鼓舞了整個團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children shouted with enthusiasm when the show began.","zh":"演出開始時，孩子們興奮地喊了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enthusiasm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d5ce483ac66beae","term":"enthusiasm","forms":["enthusiasm","enthusiasms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱衷的興趣；愛好","explanation":"指一個人特別熱衷、願意持續投入的具體事情，也就是能點燃其熱情的物件。它可以是某項活動、主題或收藏領域。","examples":[{"en":"Gardening has become one of my main enthusiasms.","zh":"園藝已經成了我最主要的愛好之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Birdwatching is his newest enthusiasm; he never leaves without binoculars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enthusiasm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d847aaec1929ff04439","word":"enthusiastic","forms":["enthusiastic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5603de60889dbe71","term":"enthusiastic","forms":["enthusiastic","more enthusiastic","most enthusiastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱情投入的","explanation":"形容人對某項活動、想法或領域非常有興趣，並且願意積極投入時間和精力；也可以形容這種積極熱烈的態度。","examples":[{"en":"She is enthusiastic about learning new languages.","zh":"她熱衷於學習新語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students gave an enthusiastic response to the idea.","zh":"學生們對這個想法作出了熱烈的回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enthusiastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-260b27ca3018bc10add7","word":"entire","forms":["entire"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19b257fde84b49c8","term":"entire","forms":["entire"],"pos":"adj","zh":"整個的；全部的","explanation":"指一個有明確邊界的物件從頭到尾都包括在內，沒有被分開、刪去或遺漏。它把注意力放在“一個完整整體”上，例如整棟建築、整段時間或全部內容。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the entire afternoon by the lake.","zh":"我們整個下午都待在湖邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The entire building lost power during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，整棟樓都停電了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f7185b2e31704c414df","word":"entitle","forms":["entitle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"entitle","forms":["entitle"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使有權享有","examples":[{"en":"This ticket will entitle you to a free drink.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Membership does not entitle anyone to break the club's rules.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"entitle","forms":["entitle"],"pos":"v.","zh":"為…命名；給…題名","examples":[{"en":"She decided to entitle her poem A Quiet Morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"What will you entitle your new collection of essays?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-bca3685fea8acd4e4b5c","word":"entity","forms":["entity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17de5d3942fb8862","term":"entity","forms":["entity","entities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨立單位；實體","explanation":"指一個能夠同其他部分割槽分開、作為整體單獨存在或被討論的單位，尤其常指組織、機構等沒有具體身體的抽象單位。","examples":[{"en":"The two departments now operate as a single entity.","zh":"這兩個部門現在作為一個整體運作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity is a separate legal entity.","zh":"這個慈善機構是一個獨立的法人實體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-178d425f9f534c62","term":"entity","forms":["entity","entities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料庫物件","explanation":"在資料庫和相關技術中，指可以單獨儲存資訊的物件，例如一個人、一家公司或一件商品；它通常對應一類資料中的一個具體成員。","examples":[{"en":"Each customer is stored as a separate entity in the database.","zh":"資料庫把每位客戶儲存為一個獨立的資料物件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An invoice entity links the customer record to several purchased items.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3902eb874fcc6c8a1dbf","word":"entrance","forms":["entrance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff0fbb291b13da3f","term":"entrance","forms":["entrance","entrances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進入；入場","explanation":"指人走進某處或進入某個場合的動作，常帶有“出場、登場”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She made a quiet entrance and sat at the back.","zh":"她安靜地進場，坐在後排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor made a dramatic entrance.","zh":"那位演員氣勢十足地登場了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entrance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28d7573d7b4437e2","term":"entrance","forms":["entrance","entrances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入口；門口","explanation":"指供人進入建築物、道路或其他地方的門、通道或位置，也就是“門”這一具體入口。","examples":[{"en":"I'll meet you at the main entrance.","zh":"我在正門口等你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a small entrance to the garden behind the house.","zh":"房子後面有一個通往花園的小入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entrance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98b9b7f3410c5235","term":"entrance","forms":["entrance","entrances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入場權；進入資格","explanation":"指被允許進入某處或參加某項活動的權利，不是入口本身，而是“能不能進去”的資格。","examples":[{"en":"You need a ticket for entrance to the exhibition.","zh":"你需要買票才能進入展覽會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guard denied him entrance to the building.","zh":"警衛不讓他進入那棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entrance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4594a1dfbd0c1151f890","word":"entrepreneur","forms":["entrepreneur"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56818d0ad0eca0b9","term":"entrepreneur","forms":["entrepreneur","entrepreneurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"企業家；創業者","explanation":"指創辦企業、經營事業，或擁有並管理企業，同時承擔資金和經營風險的人。核心畫面是一個人主動把事業做起來，而不只是受僱替別人管理工作。","examples":[{"en":"She became an entrepreneur after starting a small online clothing business.","zh":"她創辦了一家小型網上服裝店後，成了一名創業者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young entrepreneur is looking for investors to expand his company.","zh":"這位年輕企業家正在尋找投資者來擴大自己的公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entrepreneur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-923fe53966c6cd9343e1","word":"entry","forms":["entry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0009307cd1ec340d","term":"entry","forms":["entry","entries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進入；入場","explanation":"指進入某個地方、場合或領域這一動作，重點在“走進去”本身，也可指引人注目的入場方式。","examples":[{"en":"Her entry into the competition surprised everyone.","zh":"她參加這場比賽讓所有人都感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor made a dramatic entry onto the stage.","zh":"那名演員以很有戲劇性的方式登上舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53a5a705f9f0d9f5","term":"entry","forms":["entry","entries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進入許可；入場資格","explanation":"指獲准進入某地或參加某項活動的權利，不是進入動作本身，而是“被允許走進去”。","examples":[{"en":"Entry to the museum is free on Sundays.","zh":"星期日進入這家博物館免費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your ticket permits entry to all exhibition rooms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95890d3147f2b434","term":"entry","forms":["entry","entries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入口；門廳入口","explanation":"指供人進入建築物的門、門口或入口空間，是“走進去”這條主線中的具體通道。","examples":[{"en":"Please wait for me at the front entry.","zh":"請在前門入口等我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel has a separate entry for staff.","zh":"這家酒店為員工設有單獨的入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bc5798c57eb62c7","term":"entry","forms":["entry","entries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詞條；列表專案","explanation":"指被“放進”名單、詞典、百科全書等有組織材料中的一項，例如一個詞典詞條或一篇收錄文章。","examples":[{"en":"Look up the word in the dictionary entry for “light”.","zh":"請在“light”的詞典詞條中查詢這個詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her name was the first entry on the list.","zh":"她的名字是名單上的第一項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/entry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c503ca67761e5c4aaec","word":"envelope","forms":["envelope"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f01ced027d2bed3","term":"envelope","forms":["envelope","envelopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信封","explanation":"裝信件或其他扁平小物、通常可以封口寄出的紙質或紙板外套。","examples":[{"en":"She put the invitation in an envelope and added a stamp.","zh":"她把邀請函放進信封，貼上了郵票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was no return address on the envelope.","zh":"信封上沒有寄件人地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envelope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88c131fd0e28f675","term":"envelope","forms":["envelope","envelopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"包裹物；外套","explanation":"泛指把某物包住或圍住的一層東西；信封只是這種“外層”的一個具體例子。","examples":[{"en":"A thin envelope of ice covered the surface of the pond.","zh":"池塘表面覆蓋著一層薄冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A delicate envelope surrounds each developing seed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envelope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fea767fd43539609","term":"envelope","forms":["envelope","envelopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安全效能範圍","explanation":"指技術系統能夠安全而有效執行的限制範圍；它把系統的能力包在一個可接受的邊界內。push the envelope 就是試著把這條邊界往外推。","examples":[{"en":"The new aircraft can fly faster while staying within its safety envelope.","zh":"這架新飛機能在安全效能範圍內飛得更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is pushing the envelope with its new battery design.","zh":"這個團隊的新電池設計正在挑戰現有的效能極限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envelope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74c4a5de72fc1bbaed63","word":"envious","forms":["envious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f56ab6a35dc90d2","term":"envious","forms":["envious","more envious","most envious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嫉妒的；眼紅的","explanation":"指因為別人擁有自己想要的優點、成就、財富或好運而感到不滿，或表現出這種不滿；有時還帶有想貶低、阻礙對方的惡意。","examples":[{"en":"She felt envious of her friend's new job.","zh":"她很羨慕又嫉妒朋友的新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His envious comments made the celebration uncomfortable.","zh":"他那些嫉妒的評論讓慶祝活動變得很不自在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba5285161ba6eed0085f","word":"environment","forms":["environment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf7c731118e17116","term":"environment","forms":["environment","environments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"周圍環境；外部條件","explanation":"指圍繞某個物件、並對它產生影響的各種人、事物、條件和因素。它是最基礎、最寬泛的意思，其他許多用法都可以看作這個“包圍並影響”的概念延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Children learn best in a safe and supportive environment.","zh":"孩子在安全、有人支援的環境中學習效果最好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new design fits well into its urban environment.","zh":"這個新設計很適合周圍的城市環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/environment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19e83abe017c584e","term":"environment","forms":["environment","environments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自然環境；生態環境","explanation":"指自然界及其中的空氣、水、土地、植物、動物等整體。這裡的 environment 不是某個人身邊的一般環境，而是人類和其他生物共同生活的自然系統。","examples":[{"en":"We need to reduce plastic waste to protect the environment.","zh":"我們需要減少塑膠垃圾來保護自然環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Plastic waste threatens the marine environment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/environment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cb948126bc7cece459e","word":"environmental","forms":["environmental"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0713d40e0d741b4","term":"environmental","forms":["environmental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"環境相關的","explanation":"表示某事物和周圍的自然或物理環境有關，重點是“涉及環境”，不一定表示它對環境有好處。","examples":[{"en":"The factory faces strict environmental regulations.","zh":"這家工廠面臨嚴格的環境法規。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report examines the environmental impact of the new road.","zh":"這份報告考察了這條新公路對環境的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/environmental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9cb37d19e87c4b4b","term":"environmental","forms":["environmental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"環保的","explanation":"當它修飾產品、技術或做法，並且上下文強調減少汙染、節約資源等好處時，表示“對環境友好的、環保的”。這是從“與環境有關”發展出來的評價性用法。","examples":[{"en":"More customers are choosing environmental cleaning products.","zh":"越來越多的顧客選擇環保清潔產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The group campaigns for stronger environmental protections.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/environmental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e03ff190d15d63a6fb97","word":"envision","forms":["envision"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eddab6a5aa5de1f4","term":"envision","forms":["envision","envisions","envisioning","envisioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想象；設想","explanation":"envision 就是在腦海中先“看見”一個還不存在的東西：可以是一個具體畫面，也可以是未來的計劃、目標或結果。它強調想象得相對清楚，而不只是隨便想到。","examples":[{"en":"She envisions a small house by the sea.","zh":"她設想將來住在海邊的一所小房子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team envisions creating a safer way to travel.","zh":"這個團隊設想創造一種更安全的出行方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc91368f2036677b48a4","word":"envy","forms":["envy"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-123e82f4171276a2","term":"envy","forms":["envy","envies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嫉妒；羨慕不滿","explanation":"指看到別人擁有自己沒有的好運、能力或物品時，產生的帶有不甘和渴望的情緒；它不只針對物質東西。","examples":[{"en":"She felt a flash of envy when her colleague received the award.","zh":"同事獲獎時，她心裡閃過一陣嫉妒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He watched his friend's new bicycle with envy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-132f13dc9be5fd57","term":"envy","forms":["envy","envies","envying","envied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嫉妒某人","explanation":"表示因為某人擁有好運、優勢或令人羨慕的處境而對其感到不滿，心裡希望自己也有同樣的東西。","examples":[{"en":"I envy you for having so much time to travel.","zh":"我真羨慕你有這麼多時間去旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I envy her ability to stay calm under pressure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-685c25f2d7613ae1","term":"envy","forms":["envy","envies","envying","envied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想要別人擁有的東西","explanation":"表示不甘地想要別人擁有而自己沒有的東西，例如財富、能力、機會或生活狀態；焦點落在被渴望的東西上。","examples":[{"en":"Many people envy her confidence and independence.","zh":"許多人都羨慕她的自信和獨立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I envy your ability to sleep on airplanes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4ce996f70c5e989845d","word":"epidemic","forms":["epidemic"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d649cdfd2aecdb66","term":"epidemic","forms":["epidemic","more epidemic","most epidemic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"流行病的；流行的","explanation":"描述疾病在人群中廣泛傳播，或與這種大規模疾病傳播有關。它把“在人群中擴散”這個核心畫面直接放在名詞前面。","examples":[{"en":"The region is facing an epidemic outbreak of dengue fever.","zh":"該地區正面臨登革熱的大規模流行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Epidemic disease spread rapidly through the crowded camps.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dec4ca565b933379","term":"epidemic","forms":["epidemic","epidemics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流行病","explanation":"指一種疾病在一個人群中大範圍傳播，使許多人在相近時期患病。它是“某種東西像傳染一樣在人群中鋪開”這一核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"An epidemic of measles swept through the villages.","zh":"一場麻疹流行病席捲了這些村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An influenza epidemic closed schools across the region.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epidemic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e414e6ac41ac7a0658c","word":"episode","forms":["episode"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0645f138d759e712","term":"episode","forms":["episode","episodes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段事件或經歷","explanation":"指一連串事情中能夠單獨拿出來講的一段事件、行動或時期，通常與整體經歷有關，但本身有比較清楚的界限。","examples":[{"en":"That embarrassing episode stayed with her for years.","zh":"那段尷尬的經歷讓她多年難以忘懷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book describes an episode from his childhood.","zh":"這本書講述了他童年時期的一段經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/episode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71bedf4de6693b2f","term":"episode","forms":["episode","episodes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續劇的一集","explanation":"指電視連續劇、廣播劇或其他分集講述的作品中的一集；這一集通常既屬於整個故事，又能作為一個單獨單元觀看。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the final episode together last night.","zh":"昨晚我們一起看了最後一集。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tonight's episode reveals who stole the necklace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/episode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9d6cd1ed5cf1ead7b54","word":"equal","forms":["equal"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-822218e2ae5908c1","term":"equal","forms":["equal","more equal","most equal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相等的；相同的","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物在數量、價值、大小、地位等某一個或幾個方面相同，不一定所有方面都一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams are equal in strength.","zh":"這兩支隊伍實力相當。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each child received an equal share of the cake.","zh":"每個孩子都分到了同樣多的蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-165c3f3213480671","term":"equal","forms":["equal","equals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同等地位的人；匹敵者","explanation":"指在地位、能力或其他重要方面與另一個人相同的人，也就是站在同一高度上的人或事物。","examples":[{"en":"In this field, she has few equals.","zh":"在這個領域，幾乎沒人能與她匹敵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"On the chessboard, she finally met her equal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb0ccb07fe61c9b4","term":"equal","forms":["equal","equals","equaling","equalling","equaled","equalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"等於；相當於","explanation":"表示一個數量、價值或結果與另一個相同，就像天平兩邊完全平衡。","examples":[{"en":"Three times four equals twelve.","zh":"三乘四等於十二。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One hour of driving equals about sixty kilometers on this road.","zh":"在這條路上開車一小時大約相當於六十公里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc3dd57e3c5b074bb4da","word":"equality","forms":["equality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c4c44c86deaa255","term":"equality","forms":["equality","equalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相等；平等狀態","explanation":"指雙方或多個物件處在相同的狀態、地位或水平，沒有一方高於另一方。它是最寬泛的意義，可以用於社會關係，也可以用於一般性的比較。","examples":[{"en":"The movement fought for equality between all citizens.","zh":"這場運動爭取所有公民之間的平等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"True equality means that no one is treated as less important.","zh":"真正的平等意味著沒有人會被當作不那麼重要的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06c99f7e18e1b5f1","term":"equality","forms":["equality","equalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人人平等；平等待遇","explanation":"特指不因性別、種族、文化背景或社會身份不同，就給予不同的權利、機會和尊重。這裡的核心不是每個人完全一樣，而是每個人都應處在同等的地位上。","examples":[{"en":"The school has a clear policy on gender equality.","zh":"這所學校有明確的性別平等政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign demands equality in pay and promotion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-401b59e35a5a1bc2399a","word":"equalize","forms":["equalize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"equalize","forms":["equalize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使相等；使均衡","examples":[{"en":"The new policy aims to equalize access to education.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Open the valve slowly to equalize the pressure on both sides.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb273c8b634624978d75","word":"equate","forms":["equate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a45d5bf59dbbf1b2","term":"equate","forms":["equate","equates","equating","equated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……等同於……","explanation":"指認為兩個事物在價值、意義或性質上相等或等價，把它們放在同一架天平上看待；不一定表示它們在每個方面都完全相同。","examples":[{"en":"It is a mistake to equate popularity with quality.","zh":"把受歡迎等同於質量，是一種錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report equates longer working hours with greater productivity.","zh":"這份報告把更長的工作時間等同於更高的生產率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9bf099e737199a1c","term":"equate","forms":["equate","equates","equating","equated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設為相等","explanation":"指在數學、科學或計算中明確規定兩個量相等，或透過計算使它們相等；這裡不是主觀地把兩件事看成相當，而是進行明確的等式設定。","examples":[{"en":"To solve the equation, equate the two sides and simplify.","zh":"要解這個方程，先令兩邊相等，再進行化簡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Equate the two expressions and solve for x.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-edfc47701c055a12d3e7","word":"equation","forms":["equation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08a2fd33ea6da0eb","term":"equation","forms":["equation","equations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方程；等式","explanation":"指用等號連線兩個相等的數學表示式，例如左邊和右邊雖然寫法不同，但數值相同。它常用來表示問題中的已知關係，並透過求解找出未知數。","examples":[{"en":"Solve the equation 3x + 2 = 14.","zh":"解方程 3x + 2 = 14。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This equation shows how pressure changes with temperature.","zh":"這個方程表示壓力如何隨溫度變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c807b474205f2a4a","term":"equation","forms":["equation","equations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相等關係；平衡","explanation":"指把兩個或多個事物相互比較並使它們處於相等、平衡的關係，也可以指這種相等狀態本身。核心畫面是把等號兩邊調平。","examples":[{"en":"The talks aimed to bring the two sides into equation.","zh":"會談旨在讓雙方達到平衡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The equation between effort and reward is imperfect.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99cad685f03c7103ca02","word":"equip(ment)","forms":["equip","equipment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ca8cf8f624c8b47","term":"equip","forms":["equip","equips","equipping","equipped","equipt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"配備必需品","explanation":"指給人、車輛、船隻、團隊或其他事物配上完成特定任務所需要的工具、物資或武器；核心畫面就是“出發前把裝備配齊”。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team was equipped with ropes, radios, and medical kits.","zh":"救援隊配備了繩索、無線電和醫療包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workshop is equipped with modern tools.","zh":"這間工坊配備了現代工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6157a5c95acea611","term":"equip","forms":["equip","equips","equipping","equipped","equipt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使具備技能","explanation":"不僅可以給人配物品，也可以給人配上知識、訓練或能力，使其能夠完成某項任務；這就是把“裝備”從工具擴充套件到能力。","examples":[{"en":"The course equips students with the skills they need for the job.","zh":"這門課程使學生掌握工作所需的技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course equips graduates to manage complex emergencies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3237d4c0995a4376","term":"equipment","forms":["equipment","equipments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝備；裝置","explanation":"指為某項工作、運動、旅行或活動所使用的一整套物品，例如工具、器材和裝置。重點不是某一件東西，而是為完成任務而準備的“成套配備”。","examples":[{"en":"We need more gardening equipment for the backyard.","zh":"我們需要更多園藝裝置來整理後院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue team checked all its equipment before leaving.","zh":"救援隊出發前檢查了所有裝備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equipment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-067a3f0889ee23e9","term":"equipment","forms":["equipment","equipments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"配備；裝備的過程或狀態","explanation":"指為航行、遠征等任務準備並配齊人員、物資或器材的過程，也可指已經處於配備齊全的狀態。這個意思是從“把任務所需東西裝上、備好”這一核心概念發展來的，語氣通常比“裝置”更書面或歷史化。","examples":[{"en":"The equipment of the expedition took several months.","zh":"這次遠征的裝備準備花了幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adequate equipment of the new laboratory depended on outside funding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equipment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30703a5c0fcb28e886e0","word":"equity","forms":["equity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bcff44be4d68369d","term":"equity","forms":["equity","equities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公平；公正","explanation":"指依據公認的正當原則，公正、不偏不倚地對待人或處理事情。它強調結果或判斷是否合乎公平，而不只是形式上完全相同。","examples":[{"en":"The committee questioned the equity of the new admission policy.","zh":"委員會質疑新招生政策是否公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should consider equity as well as efficiency.","zh":"我們既要考慮效率，也要考慮公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ac88397aff88b2a","term":"equity","forms":["equity","equities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"淨值；淨資產","explanation":"在金融和房地產語境中，指一項資產的價值減去相關債務後真正屬於持有人的部分，例如房屋市值減去尚未償還的貸款。這裡的“公平份額”變成了資產中你實際擁有的那一部分。","examples":[{"en":"After five years of payments, they had built substantial equity in their home.","zh":"還款五年後，他們已經積累了相當多的房屋淨值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have little equity in the property because most of the loan remains unpaid.","zh":"由於大部分貸款還沒有還清，我在這處房產中的淨值很少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc73c906e945aa99228f","word":"equivalent","forms":["equivalent"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1b74c7ebaeb67e7","term":"equivalent","forms":["equivalent","more equivalent","most equivalent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相當的；等價的","explanation":"指兩個事物雖然形式可能不同，但在價值、意義、作用或結果上幾乎相等，可以互相替代或比較。","examples":[{"en":"One large apple is roughly equivalent to two small ones.","zh":"一個大蘋果大致相當於兩個小蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new training course is equivalent to six months of practical experience.","zh":"這門新培訓課程相當於六個月的實踐經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/equivalent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49eaab7e75d92ddfe7e7","word":"era","forms":["era"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9d84be51ebfffa8","term":"era","forms":["era","eras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時代；長期時期","explanation":"指持續時間較長、通常超過一年的一段時間，尤其強調這段時間具有某種共同特徵或風貌。它可以指歷史上的時代，也可以泛指社會、科技或生活中的一個階段。","examples":[{"en":"We are living in an era of rapid technological change.","zh":"我們正生活在一個技術迅速變化的時代。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum explores how people dressed in the Victorian era.","zh":"這家博物館探討維多利亞時代人們的穿著方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/era","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acee3df9f21107c6","term":"era","forms":["era","eras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人興趣階段","explanation":"非正式地指一個人在生活中集中表現某種興趣、風格或狀態的一段時期，彷彿進入了自己的“某某時代”。","examples":[{"en":"I'm in my baking era and trying a new recipe every weekend.","zh":"我最近進入了自己的烘焙階段，每個週末都在嘗試新食譜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"During his gardening era, every windowsill held seedlings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/era","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5cf46cd89515601e0d2a","word":"erase","forms":["erase"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e2442fa23573a69","term":"erase","forms":["erase","erases","erasing","erased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦掉文字或痕跡","explanation":"指把紙上、黑板上或其他表面上的字跡、標記擦去，使原來的痕跡不再看得見。這是從“擦掉痕跡”這一核心畫面最直接發展出的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I erased the wrong answer from the page.","zh":"我把頁面上的錯誤答案擦掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please erase the last line on the board.","zh":"請把黑板上的最後一行擦掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b95fab1c1980a3d8","term":"erase","forms":["erase","erases","erasing","erased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"清除儲存介質","explanation":"指把磁帶、磁碟等儲存介質中的內容整體清掉，重點在處理這件“裝著資訊的載體”，而不只是刪除其中某個檔案。","examples":[{"en":"Before reusing the old tape, we erased it completely.","zh":"重新使用那盤舊磁帶前，我們把它徹底清除了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Erase the hard drive before recycling the computer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9010072f85ea54692588","word":"eraser","forms":["eraser"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1bed54d197203f53","term":"eraser","forms":["eraser","erasers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橡皮；擦除工具","explanation":"指擦掉鉛筆字、鉛筆畫或其他可擦書寫痕跡的工具，最常見的形象就是鉛筆上的橡皮或單獨使用的橡皮。","examples":[{"en":"Could I borrow an eraser to fix this smudge?","zh":"我能借一塊橡皮擦掉這個汙跡嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eraser on my pencil is too worn to clean the line.","zh":"我鉛筆上的橡皮磨得太厲害，擦不乾淨這條線了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eraser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2587ea256bf0e87d","term":"eraser","forms":["eraser","erasers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑板擦；白板擦","explanation":"指擦掉黑板上的粉筆字或白板上的可擦記號的工具；它和橡皮的共同點都是把留下的痕跡擦掉，只是使用的表面更大。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher left a large eraser beside the whiteboard.","zh":"老師把一塊大白板擦放在白板旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the eraser to clean the whiteboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eraser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb93e8d7c9f898cb5c75","word":"erect","forms":["erect"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7e1c578cb96d438","term":"erect","forms":["erect","more erect","most erect"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直立的；豎直向上的","explanation":"指人、物體或結構沒有倒下，而是直直地站著或向上延伸。這是 erect 最基礎、最容易擴充套件的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The young trees remained erect despite the strong wind.","zh":"儘管風很大，這些小樹仍然直挺挺地立著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sat erect and listened carefully.","zh":"她挺直身子坐著，認真地聽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f754834e174045ad","term":"erect","forms":["erect","erects","erecting","erected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搭建；建造","explanation":"把材料或部件組合起來，使房屋、堡壘等結構出現並站立起來。這裡保留了“把東西立起來”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Workers erected a temporary shelter beside the road.","zh":"工人在路邊搭建了一個臨時避難所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city plans to erect a new bridge here.","zh":"這座城市計劃在這裡建一座新橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df89624eda2273f2","term":"erect","forms":["erect","erects","erecting","erected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"豎起；豎直放置","explanation":"把柱子、旗杆、紀念碑等從橫放或倒下的位置立到豎直位置上。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers erected a flagpole in front of the school.","zh":"志願者在學校前面豎起了一根旗杆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A monument was erected in memory of the victims.","zh":"人們豎立了一座紀念碑來緬懷遇難者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1bf792ef47f005a","term":"erect","forms":["erect","erects","erecting","erected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建立；創立","explanation":"把組織、制度、國家或其他抽象實體正式“立起來”，也就是建立、創立或設立。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement erected a new system for protecting workers.","zh":"這項協議建立了一套保護工人的新制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The settlers erected a small government of their own.","zh":"定居者建立了一個屬於自己的小型政府。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6522cf7814f326a71cbe","word":"errand","forms":["errand"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bd252e768ba221e","term":"errand","forms":["errand","errands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跑腿辦事的一趟","explanation":"指為了買東西、取東西、送東西或辦理某件小事務而外出的一趟。重點不是旅行本身，而是“帶著明確任務跑一趟”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to run an errand before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前我得出去辦一趟事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent the morning running errands around town.","zh":"她整個上午都在鎮上跑腿辦事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/errand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1629b69454526d8c","term":"errand","forms":["errand","errands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"這趟行程的目的","explanation":"這裡不強調實際走了多遠，而是問或說明“為什麼要去、要去辦什麼”。因此，問某人的 errand，就是在問他此行所肩負的任務。","examples":[{"en":"He explained the purpose of his errand to the manager.","zh":"他向經理說明了自己這趟出行的目的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My errand was to collect the repaired watch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/errand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca00fccfb408989eddc4","word":"error","forms":["error"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cad5a6b0a5ea1bcd","term":"error","forms":["error","errors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錯誤狀態","explanation":"指事情處在不正確的狀態，或某個判斷、做法本身是錯的；重點是“錯誤這一狀態”，而不是某一個具體錯誤。","examples":[{"en":"The report concluded that the original assumption was in error.","zh":"報告得出結論，原先的假設是錯誤的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge admitted that he had been in error.","zh":"法官承認自己當時判斷錯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/error","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-555c55a41d465f10","term":"error","forms":["error","errors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個具體錯誤","explanation":"指一次具體的錯誤行為、錯誤判斷或錯誤陳述，通常不是故意造成的；這是最常用、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"There was an error in the final total.","zh":"最終總數中有一個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She noticed the error and corrected it immediately.","zh":"她發現了這個錯誤，並立即改正了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/error","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df2f18f63c66b2151e04","word":"erupt","forms":["erupt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf641c4d9d69b94f","term":"erupt","forms":["erupt","erupts","erupting","erupted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"噴發；猛烈噴出","explanation":"指火山、噴泉等把熔岩、水或其他物質猛烈地從內部噴出來。這是“從裡面衝出”這一核心畫面最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The volcano erupted without warning.","zh":"那座火山毫無預警地噴發了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hot water erupted from the ground.","zh":"熱水從地面猛烈噴出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7ba21b66f7c9f73","term":"erupt","forms":["erupt","erupts","erupting","erupted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"情緒或反應爆發","explanation":"指原本積壓在內部的憤怒、笑聲、歡呼等突然釋放出來，或指人群突然爆發出強烈反應。這是把“內部壓力衝出來”用於抽象情緒。","examples":[{"en":"The audience erupted in applause.","zh":"觀眾突然爆發出熱烈的掌聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children erupted into laughter.","zh":"孩子們突然大笑起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b0b0c53c761f8e91a08","word":"escalator","forms":["escalator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-790ac032d51521d3","term":"escalator","forms":["escalator","escalators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自動扶梯","explanation":"指由電力驅動、階梯連續迴圈執行的裝置，能自動把人從一層送到另一層。這是最常見、最應該優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Take the escalator to the second floor.","zh":"乘自動扶梯到二樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The escalator is out of order today.","zh":"自動扶梯今天壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/escalator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3140286ac71ad2acf69","word":"escape","forms":["escape"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0488edc253384627","term":"escape","forms":["escape","escapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"逃脫；脫身","explanation":"指從危險、監禁或令人不快的處境中成功離開，重點是從束縛中“出去”。","examples":[{"en":"The prisoners made their escape through a narrow tunnel.","zh":"囚犯們透過一條狹窄的隧道逃了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a narrow escape from the falling tree.","zh":"那真是從倒下的樹下險險逃生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/escape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08ba0b2ec7c4d617","term":"escape","forms":["escape","escapes","escaping","escaped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逃離；逃脫","explanation":"指自己從危險、監禁或限制中成功出去，突出主動擺脫束縛的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers escaped from the burning cabin through a back window.","zh":"徒步旅行者從燃燒的小屋後窗逃了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog escaped while the gate was being repaired.","zh":"大門維修時，那條狗跑掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/escape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b36d340b28f8375","term":"escape","forms":["escape","escapes","escaping","escaped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"躲開；逃避","explanation":"指避開令人不快的人或事，也可以表示避免經歷某種壞結果，重點是成功從它面前脫身。","examples":[{"en":"She escaped paying a fine because the mistake was not hers.","zh":"因為那不是她的錯，她免於繳納罰款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He escaped the noisy crowd by taking a side street.","zh":"他走了一條小路，避開了嘈雜的人群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/escape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a448294a6283de8a4438","word":"escort","forms":["escort"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7d5988c354711fe","term":"escort","forms":["escort","escorts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"護送隊；護衛隊","explanation":"指陪著重要人物或一隊人、車輛同行，並負責保護其安全的人員或車輛組成的隊伍。重點是“同行並護衛”，不一定只有一個人。","examples":[{"en":"The ambassador arrived with a police escort.","zh":"大使在警方護送下抵達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An armed escort accompanied the convoy through the pass.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/escort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4638f9174f7e6c1","term":"escort","forms":["escort","escorts","escorting","escorted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"護送；陪同保護","explanation":"指陪著某人前往某處，並在途中保護其安全，或出於禮儀鄭重陪同。它是名詞“護送者、護衛隊”對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"A staff member escorted the elderly visitor to the exit.","zh":"一名工作人員陪同那位老年訪客走到出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two officers escorted the witness to a waiting car.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/escort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b109a53288ba6ef3ffa8","word":"especially","forms":["especially"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03215d552d5c4197","term":"especially","forms":["especially","more especially","most especially"],"pos":"adv","zh":"尤其；格外","explanation":"表示某種性質或程度比通常更突出，相當於在一大片範圍中把一個特點照得更亮。","examples":[{"en":"This plant grows especially well in warm, wet places.","zh":"這種植物在溫暖潮溼的地方長得格外好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I especially enjoyed the final violin solo.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/especially","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c675382aaf3839d","term":"especially","forms":["especially","more especially","most especially"],"pos":"adv","zh":"尤其是；特別是","explanation":"用來從一組人或事物中單獨突出一個，說明它比同組其他物件更值得注意。","examples":[{"en":"I like all the desserts, especially the mango pudding.","zh":"我喜歡所有甜點，尤其是芒果布丁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I love citrus fruit, especially blood oranges.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/especially","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4231a97ecfd74fdbdde4","word":"essay","forms":["essay"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c84ff7ecdda630c8","term":"essay","forms":["essay","essays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文章；短論","explanation":"指圍繞一個具體問題、主題或觀點展開分析和討論的文章，通常比完整專著短，但不只是簡單羅列事實。它像是把一次對想法的“檢驗”寫下來，讓讀者看到作者怎樣思考這個主題。","examples":[{"en":"She wrote an essay about the impact of social media on education.","zh":"她寫了一篇關於社交媒體對教育影響的文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book is a collection of essays on travel and memory.","zh":"這本書收錄了多篇關於旅行與記憶的文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/essay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-092bd8646cf5c6a62b65","word":"essence","forms":["essence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00d86fcca3c9bb6e","term":"essence","forms":["essence","essences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內在本質","explanation":"指一個事物最核心、最能說明它是什麼的內在性質，而不是外表、附帶特徵或具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"The essence of friendship is trust.","zh":"友誼的本質是信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She explained the essence of the problem in one sentence.","zh":"她用一句話說明了這個問題的本質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/essence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d01a1967a5479f1","term":"essence","forms":["essence","essences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"真實本性","explanation":"強調事物真正的性質，尤其是與表面現象、偶然變化或虛假印象相對的那一面。","examples":[{"en":"The study tries to reveal the essence of human memory.","zh":"這項研究試圖揭示人類記憶的真實本性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The essay captures the essence of her philosophy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/essence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a55751cecd11bad874ef","word":"essential","forms":["essential"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0471b563dd849e5d","term":"essential","forms":["essential","more essential","most essential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"必不可少的","explanation":"指缺少某人或某物，某件事就難以完成、維持或正常運轉；它是不可拿掉的核心部分。","examples":[{"en":"Clean water is essential for good health.","zh":"清潔的水對身體健康是必不可少的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is essential to check the address before sending the package.","zh":"寄出包裹前核對地址是必不可少的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/essential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad8b005df9bf3751","term":"essential","forms":["essential","more essential","most essential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其重要的","explanation":"指某事在一組事情中處於核心位置，重要性很高；不一定是物理上或絕對意義上的必需品，但忽略它會帶來嚴重影響。","examples":[{"en":"Good communication is essential to a successful team.","zh":"良好的溝通對團隊成功至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clean water is essential for the village's survival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/essential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8736a682244d9a4","term":"essential","forms":["essential","essentials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必需品；必要成分","explanation":"指完成某事或維持生活不可缺少的東西；它就是“不能拿掉的核心”本身。","examples":[{"en":"We packed only the essentials for the short trip.","zh":"這次短途旅行我們只帶了必需品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A reliable internet connection is an essential for remote work.","zh":"可靠的網路連線是遠端工作的必備條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/essential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-364710ec39480495168e","word":"establish(ment)","forms":["establish","establishment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97ae9c1cc8d106f4","term":"establish","forms":["establish","establishes","establishing","established"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使穩定；使站穩","explanation":"指讓植物、習慣、關係、地位等逐漸穩定下來並站住腳，不再只是剛剛開始。例如植物成活並適應環境，也可以說它已經“站穩了”。","examples":[{"en":"The young tree became established after a year in the new garden.","zh":"這棵小樹在新花園裡生長一年後站穩了腳跟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young doctor soon established herself in the town.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/establish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbc17e26c8caf689","term":"establish","forms":["establish","establishes","establishing","established"],"pos":"verb","zh":"創立；建立","explanation":"指正式創辦機構、組織、企業或制度，把原本不存在的事物立起來並使其持續運作。","examples":[{"en":"They established a small clinic in the village.","zh":"他們在村裡建立了一家小診所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two countries established diplomatic relations last year.","zh":"兩國於去年建立了外交關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/establish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7e27990b8aaaa96","term":"establish","forms":["establish","establishes","establishing","established"],"pos":"verb","zh":"證實；確立為事實","explanation":"指透過證據、調查或推理證明某個事實、觀點或模式，使它被認為真實可靠。這裡不是“創造”事實，而是把事實穩穩地確立下來。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation established that the fire started in the kitchen.","zh":"調查證實火災是從廚房開始的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study established a clear link between sleep and memory.","zh":"這項研究確立了睡眠與記憶之間的明確聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/establish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48d6371cf2222763","term":"establishment","forms":["establishment","establishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建立；確立","explanation":"指把某個組織、制度或安排建立起來並正式確定的過程。它對應記憶中的“把大樓建起來”這一步，重點在動作或正式確立，而不是建立後的實體。","examples":[{"en":"The establishment of the new museum took nearly three years.","zh":"新博物館的建立花了將近三年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement led to the establishment of a joint committee.","zh":"這項協議促成了聯合委員會的成立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/establishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0f38dd9979d7ee1","term":"establishment","forms":["establishment","establishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構；營業場所","explanation":"指已經固定存在、提供某種服務或開展某種活動的機構、企業或場所，是“建好的大樓”本身。它可以是商店、餐館、企業、軍隊單位或其他長期組織。","examples":[{"en":"This small establishment serves excellent vegetarian food.","zh":"這家小餐館供應很棒的素食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel is one of the oldest establishments in the town.","zh":"這家酒店是鎮上歷史最悠久的機構之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/establishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39a62c9908f12eb7","term":"establishment","forms":["establishment","establishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統治階層；既有權威","explanation":"指社會中已經穩固的權力階層或權威集團，尤其是維護現狀的政治、經濟和文化精英。它是從“已經建成的大樓”進一步引申出的“大樓裡掌權的人”。","examples":[{"en":"Young voters are increasingly skeptical of the political establishment.","zh":"年輕選民越來越不信任政治既得權力集團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became known for criticizing the cultural establishment.","zh":"她因批評文化界的既有權威而出名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/establishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e62377847bbe2117fbea","word":"estate","forms":["estate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c63e89bea6497e0","term":"estate","forms":["estate","estates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遺產；遺產總額","explanation":"指某人，尤其是去世的人，留下的全部財產和債務，不只是房子或金錢。可以把它想成一個完整的“財產包”，由繼承人或法律程式統一處理。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer is helping the family settle their father's estate.","zh":"律師正在幫助這家人處理父親留下的遺產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most of the estate went to his two children.","zh":"這筆遺產的大部分留給了他的兩個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/estate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8ba60a87d590c0e","term":"estate","forms":["estate","estates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"土地權益；土地所有權範圍","explanation":"在法律中指某人對土地享有的權益性質和範圍，不一定等於土地本身；重點是“對這塊土地擁有怎樣的權利”。","examples":[{"en":"The contract explains what estate each buyer will receive in the land.","zh":"合同說明了每位買方將獲得這塊土地上的哪種權益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lease grants an estate for twenty years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/estate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe685ad27c9e143e","term":"estate","forms":["estate","estates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大片地產","explanation":"指歸同一人或同一機構所有、管理的一大片土地，通常包括住宅、農田、園林或其他建築。這裡的重點是“成片土地歸在一個所有權之下”。","examples":[{"en":"They spent the weekend exploring the old estate and its gardens.","zh":"他們週末遊覽了那座古老莊園及其花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The estate includes woodland, pastures, and several cottages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/estate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eaccc3e5305cbcda8f99","word":"esteem","forms":["esteem"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5aade5153528deca","term":"esteem","forms":["esteem","esteems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尊重；敬意；高度評價","explanation":"esteem 是把某人或某事物放在心中的高處，表示由認可和尊重形成的敬意，常帶有“高度評價”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The whole team holds its coach in high esteem.","zh":"整個團隊都非常敬重自己的教練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her colleagues held her in high esteem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/esteem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b28a07fdc6303d16","term":"esteem","forms":["esteem","esteems","esteeming","esteemed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"尊重；敬重","explanation":"esteem 某人，就是把對方放在心中的高處，認為對方值得尊敬或敬仰。","examples":[{"en":"She is widely esteemed for her honesty.","zh":"她因誠實而受到廣泛敬重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her colleagues esteem her for her integrity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/esteem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41e9fd7e41c0ff1e","term":"esteem","forms":["esteem","esteems","esteeming","esteemed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"珍視；看重","explanation":"因為認為某人或某物有價值而 esteem 它，就是珍視、看重它；這是從“放在心中的高處”自然延伸出來的意思。","examples":[{"en":"They esteem the freedom to make their own choices.","zh":"他們很看重自行作出選擇的自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He esteemed her judgment above that of his advisers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/esteem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-79e1d925e79c904a9cf8","word":"estimate","forms":["estimate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d1f6bab8b22aa4c","term":"estimate","forms":["estimate","estimates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"估計值；大概判斷","explanation":"指根據已有資料對數量、大小、價值或費用作出的粗略判斷。它就像把不完整的資訊先整理成一個可用的大概數字。","examples":[{"en":"The builder gave us an estimate of the repair costs.","zh":"建築商給了我們一份維修費用的估價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My estimate was close to the actual number.","zh":"我的估計值和實際數量很接近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/estimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-685b1e92835f6e25","term":"estimate","forms":["estimate","estimates","estimating","estimated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"估算；估計","explanation":"指根據不完整或不完全可靠的資訊，算出一個大概的數量、時間、費用或規模。這個動作就是先“掂量”情況，再給出一個可供計劃使用的數字。","examples":[{"en":"We estimate that the project will take two months.","zh":"我們估計這個專案需要兩個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you estimate how much paint we need?","zh":"你能估算一下我們需要多少油漆嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/estimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7679dfa95094e8a9417","word":"eternal","forms":["eternal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03caff42ae107ab2","term":"eternal","forms":["eternal","more eternal","most eternal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"永恆的；永久的","explanation":"指持續到沒有盡頭、永遠不會結束的狀態或事物，既可以說時間上的永久，也可以說某種觀念或感情被認為不會消失。","examples":[{"en":"Many people hope for eternal peace after death.","zh":"許多人希望死後得到永恆的安寧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their friendship seemed eternal.","zh":"他們的友誼似乎永遠不會消失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1259c95bd6291f4","term":"eternal","forms":["eternal","more eternal","most eternal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"超越時間的","explanation":"指某物不受時間限制，彷彿不在時間之中，而不是僅僅在時間裡無限延續；這是哲學和宗教討論中較嚴格的“永恆”。","examples":[{"en":"The philosopher described God as an eternal being outside time.","zh":"這位哲學家把上帝描述為超越時間的永恆存在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The philosopher imagined eternal truths beyond human history.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c08c0d223af7f43cbf3","word":"eternity","forms":["eternity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff8240834ada2922","term":"eternity","forms":["eternity","eternities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無盡的時間","explanation":"指沒有開始或結束、無限延續的時間，重點是“永遠不會終止”的時間長河。","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe that the soul lives for eternity.","zh":"有些人相信靈魂會永遠存在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monument was built to stand for eternity.","zh":"這座紀念碑的建造目標是永遠屹立不倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14ac33c43107c98f","term":"eternity","forms":["eternity","eternities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"很長時間","explanation":"口語中的誇張用法：實際並非真的無限久，只是說某件事等了或持續了特別長時間，彷彿經歷了永恆。","examples":[{"en":"It feels like an eternity since we last met.","zh":"感覺我們上次見面已經是很久以前的事了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We waited an eternity for the final announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-338e6898edb9f81a0ae9","word":"ethic(s)","forms":["ethic","ethics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fab6160132de280a","term":"ethic","forms":["ethic","ethics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道德準則；行為風氣","explanation":"指指導某個個人、群體、社會或文化判斷對錯、安排行為的一套原則。它像一把共同使用的道德尺子，例如某個群體重視勤奮、誠實或責任，就可以說它有相應的 ethic。","examples":[{"en":"Her strong work ethic makes her reliable under pressure.","zh":"她強烈的工作道德觀使她在壓力下也很可靠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team's ethic is to share credit and take responsibility.","zh":"這個團隊的行為準則是共同分享功勞、共同承擔責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80d25736fa7fa665","term":"ethics","forms":["ethics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道德觀；道德原則","explanation":"指一個人用來判斷行為對錯的內在道德觀和原則，也就是那把屬於個人的“道德尺子”。","examples":[{"en":"Her decision was guided by her strong personal ethics.","zh":"她的決定受到自己堅定的個人道德原則指引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He refused the offer because it went against his ethics.","zh":"他拒絕了這個提議，因為這違背了他的道德原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-082acdfec7f0c677","term":"ethics","forms":["ethics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業或行業道德規範","explanation":"指某個職業、組織或行業共同接受的行為標準，規定從業者應該怎樣做、哪些事不能做。","examples":[{"en":"The company expects all employees to follow its business ethics.","zh":"公司要求所有員工遵守商業道德規範。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Medical ethics requires respect for patient confidentiality.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a683592454edd4fc001","word":"ethical","forms":["ethical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5cd25216cc9e00ca","term":"ethical","forms":["ethical","more ethical","most ethical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"道德規範的","explanation":"指依據某個組織、行業或職業所認可的對錯原則制定的規範。它把道德指南針放進位制度中，例如公司或醫生群體需要共同遵守的行為準則。","examples":[{"en":"All employees must follow the company's ethical guidelines.","zh":"所有員工都必須遵守公司的道德準則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers discussed the ethical issues involved in the study.","zh":"研究人員討論了這項研究涉及的倫理問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed7281d3f763350d","term":"ethical","forms":["ethical","more ethical","most ethical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合乎道德的","explanation":"指某種行為、決定或做法在道德上值得認可，被認為是正確、負責或正當的。它是把道德指南針用於現實選擇：比較不同做法時，判斷哪一條路更正當。","examples":[{"en":"We are trying to choose the most ethical course of action.","zh":"我們正努力選擇最合乎道德的做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was ethical to tell the customer about the mistake.","zh":"把錯誤告訴顧客是合乎道德的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f9a8fab481f42436ccd","word":"ethnic","forms":["ethnic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78f52fc36ac793d9","term":"ethnic","forms":["ethnic","more ethnic","most ethnic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"族群的；民族的","explanation":"指與一群擁有共同祖先、國家、宗教、語言或文化傳統的人有關的事物，重點是共同的群體身份，而不只是一種國籍。","examples":[{"en":"The city has a large ethnic minority population.","zh":"這座城市有很多少數族群人口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey examined ethnic differences in access to health care.","zh":"這項調查研究了不同族群在獲得醫療服務方面的差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethnic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d3fc4631119698b","term":"ethnic","forms":["ethnic","more ethnic","most ethnic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"具有族群特色的；異國文化的","explanation":"指某個族群或少數族群特有的文化形式，尤其常說食物、商店、服裝或藝術等；在英語中有時也泛指與主流文化不同的傳統文化。","examples":[{"en":"We found a small restaurant serving ethnic food from the region.","zh":"我們找到了一家供應該地區族群傳統食物的小餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The market sells ethnic textiles from several regions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethnic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2342909968ca928ce57a","word":"evacuate","forms":["evacuate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-325945860961ee24","term":"evacuate","forms":["evacuate","evacuates","evacuating","evacuated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撤離某地","explanation":"指離開或撤出某個地點，尤其是因為戰爭、火災或其他危險而撤離。這裡的重點是“從一個空間裡撤走”，不一定表示慌亂逃跑。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers evacuated the fortress before dawn.","zh":"士兵們在黎明前撤出了要塞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Residents were told to evacuate the area immediately.","zh":"居民被告知要立即撤離該地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evacuate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4dcccd04e1fe9d88","term":"evacuate","forms":["evacuate","evacuates","evacuating","evacuated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"疏散某人","explanation":"指把人從危險或受威脅的地點帶走，使他們撤離。它仍然是“把空間清空”的畫面，只是動作的物件變成了人。","examples":[{"en":"Firefighters evacuated the residents from the apartment building.","zh":"消防員把居民從公寓樓裡疏散了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide helped evacuate the hikers to safety.","zh":"嚮導幫助把徒步者疏散到安全處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evacuate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10aca1d8b724381a8cbe","word":"evaluate","forms":["evaluate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1f5d891762c1d46","term":"evaluate","forms":["evaluate","evaluates","evaluating","evaluated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"評估；評價","explanation":"透過檢查資料、表現或結果，判斷某事物的價值、質量、效果或重要性；重點是先考察，再作出有根據的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The team will evaluate the new training program after three months.","zh":"團隊將在三個月後評估新的培訓專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An independent panel will evaluate the proposals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evaluate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-efe77b201dc216c0edf4","word":"evaluation","forms":["evaluation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-658cd14e039f4dd5","term":"evaluation","forms":["evaluation","evaluations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"評估；評價","explanation":"指根據一定標準考察人、事物或整體情況，並形成判斷或總結，例如評價員工表現、課程成績或某項計劃的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The manager gave me a positive evaluation at the end of the year.","zh":"經理在年底對我作出了積極的評價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The evaluation of the new course will include feedback from students.","zh":"對這門新課程的評估將包括學生的反饋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evaluation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85262adf74518bbb70c7","word":"eve","forms":["eve"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e96244497d3d837e","term":"eve","forms":["eve","eves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前夕","explanation":"eve 指某個節日或重要日子到來之前的那一天或那一夜，重點是“正在臨近的門檻”。例如 Christmas Eve 就是聖誕節前夕。","examples":[{"en":"We usually have a family dinner on Christmas Eve.","zh":"我們通常在聖誕節前夕舉行家庭晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The streets were crowded on the eve of the festival.","zh":"節日前夕，街道上人很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ebbf97a523cbdc1","term":"eve","forms":["eve","eves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某事發生前夕","explanation":"比喻使用時，eve 指某件事即將發生、某種變化即將到來的階段，像站在事件門口的“前夜”。","examples":[{"en":"The country stood on the eve of a major political change.","zh":"這個國家正處在一次重大政治變革的前夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town was unusually quiet on the eve of battle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec38063c881f0a5edfef","word":"even","forms":["even"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2333d6c822aa0379","term":"even","forms":["even","more even","most even"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平的；平整的","explanation":"指表面沒有高低不平，像被抹平的地面一樣平整。","examples":[{"en":"Clear away the stones so the surface is even.","zh":"把石頭清走，讓表面變得平整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place the machine on a firm, even surface.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/even","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29c7e508016ae15c","term":"even","forms":["even","more even","most even"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平穩的；變化不大的","explanation":"指程度、情緒、聲音或表現沒有明顯起伏，保持在較穩定的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She answered in an even voice despite the bad news.","zh":"儘管聽到了壞訊息，她仍用平穩的聲音回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the temperature even throughout the baking process.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/even","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6af3b54b2616ad08","term":"even","forms":["even","more even","most even"],"pos":"adj","zh":"均勻的；相等的","explanation":"指數量、比例、大小或分配沒有明顯偏差，彼此大致相等。","examples":[{"en":"Make sure the paint is spread in an even layer.","zh":"要確保油漆鋪成均勻的一層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spread an even layer of icing over the cake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/even","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6763529a8cb11f0a","term":"even","forms":["even"],"pos":"adv","zh":"甚至","explanation":"用於突出一個通常不容易被想到、卻也包括在內的例子，表示“連……都”。","examples":[{"en":"Even my little brother understood the joke.","zh":"連我弟弟都聽懂了這個笑話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She didn’t even look at the message.","zh":"她甚至都沒有看那條訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/even","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf058af3be5a631d","term":"even","forms":["even","evens","evening","evened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄平；整平","explanation":"指主動把不平的表面弄平，或把高低差異調整掉。","examples":[{"en":"We need to even the ground before putting up the tent.","zh":"搭帳篷前，我們得先把地面弄平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even the soil before scattering the grass seed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/even","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5bd0801d10e59653546","word":"evening","forms":["evening"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3eaa44db37528cc6","term":"evening","forms":["evening","evenings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傍晚；晚上","explanation":"指下午過後、夜晚開始前後的一段時間，通常是天色漸暗、一天活動逐漸收尾的時候。日常談論時間、見面或安排活動時，這是最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We usually take a walk in the evening.","zh":"我們通常在晚上散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked beside the river in the evening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evening","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ffee287b2b4afec","term":"evening","forms":["evening","evenings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"晚間；下班後的晚上","explanation":"指從大約冬季黃昏到午夜之間，或通常工作時間結束後的晚間時段。這個意思特別適合描述晚上進行的社交、休閒和日常活動。","examples":[{"en":"The library stays open late on Thursday evenings.","zh":"圖書館每週四晚上都會開到很晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent the evening sorting old photographs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evening","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8e1f80bd70ae0784c78","word":"event","forms":["event"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-872fb7c77ec1d898","term":"event","forms":["event","events"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發生的事情","explanation":"event 可以指任何發生的事情，不論是日常小事、重大歷史事件，還是可能發生的情況。它強調“事情發生了”這一事實，不一定帶有好壞評價。","examples":[{"en":"In the event of heavy rain, the outdoor concert will be canceled.","zh":"如果下大雨，露天音樂會就會取消。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discovery was an important event in medical history.","zh":"這項發現是醫學史上的一件大事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11ce06d7b4a6e28d","term":"event","forms":["event","events"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安排好的活動","explanation":"event 也指人們事先安排、準備參加或觀看的活動，例如聚會、展覽、演出或公益活動。這個意思把“發生的事情”變成了一個有組織、有人參與的場合。","examples":[{"en":"Our school is hosting a charity event this Saturday.","zh":"我們學校本週六要舉辦一場慈善活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I met her at a local art event.","zh":"我是在當地的一場藝術活動上認識她的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aad1308c0f67203f","term":"event","forms":["event","events"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽專案","explanation":"在由多個專案組成的比賽中，event 指其中一個專案，例如游泳比賽中的某個泳姿或田徑比賽中的某個專案。這裡仍然保留“一個可單獨識別的發生事項”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She won the 100-meter freestyle event at the national championships.","zh":"她在全國錦標賽的100米自由泳專案中奪冠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She entered three swimming events at the championships.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/event","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bd8ad9f5d83f47c612f","word":"eventual","forms":["eventual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eaa87908787de490","term":"eventual","forms":["eventual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最終的；最後發生的","explanation":"指某事經過一段時間或一連串發展後最終發生、形成或成為不可避免的結果，強調“最後落到這裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The team celebrated their eventual victory after a difficult season.","zh":"這個隊經歷了艱難的賽季後，慶祝了最終取得的勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became the company's eventual leader.","zh":"她後來成了公司的最終領導人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eventual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63212655f2e25a8f89ee","word":"ever","forms":["ever"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b16a42d8ccca180","term":"ever","forms":["ever"],"pos":"adv","zh":"曾經；在任何時候","explanation":"表示時間範圍中的任意一點，常用於詢問或否定某事是否發生過，也可表示“到目前為止曾經”。","examples":[{"en":"Have you ever visited a desert?","zh":"你曾經去過沙漠嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you ever seen a shooting star?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-484846e6154f0b71","term":"ever","forms":["ever"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不斷地；持續地","explanation":"表示某種變化或狀態一直持續，就像時間線不停向前延伸；例如價格持續上漲。","examples":[{"en":"The ever-changing weather makes planning difficult.","zh":"不斷變化的天氣讓計劃變得困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ever-increasing noise drove the neighbors indoors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ccc5212a30a1256c10c","word":"evergreen","forms":["evergreen"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74fe6cc28c8dce78","term":"evergreen","forms":["evergreen"],"pos":"adj","zh":"常綠的","explanation":"像記憶鉤子裡那樣，植物始終保持綠色，不會隨著季節更替而落葉，尤其常指樹木。","examples":[{"en":"Evergreen trees keep their leaves through the winter.","zh":"常綠樹木整個冬天都保留著葉子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Evergreen shrubs keep the garden green in winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evergreen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e86fbc0386c2fc1","term":"evergreen","forms":["evergreen"],"pos":"adj","zh":"長期保持新鮮的","explanation":"由樹木始終“保持綠色”引申而來，表示內容、想法或產品能夠不斷更新，長期不過時，仍然有吸引力或實用價值。","examples":[{"en":"The website relies on evergreen articles that remain useful for years.","zh":"這個網站依靠多年後仍然有用的常青文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her advice about saving money has become an evergreen topic.","zh":"她關於省錢的建議已經成了一個長期不過時的話題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evergreen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-483eb02510a9fdef","term":"evergreen","forms":["evergreen","evergreens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"常綠植物","explanation":"指不會隨著季節脫落全部葉子或針葉的灌木或樹木，也就是“始終保持綠色”的植物。","examples":[{"en":"We planted two evergreens beside the front door.","zh":"我們在前門旁種了兩棵常綠樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden stays green in winter because of the evergreens.","zh":"因為有常綠植物，這座花園冬天仍保持綠色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evergreen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1a278be8132a269","term":"evergreen","forms":["evergreen","evergreens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可隨時播出的新聞","explanation":"指不受特定時效限制、可以在需要時發表或播出的新聞報道；它就像內容也能“始終保持新鮮、隨時可用”。","examples":[{"en":"The editor saved the interview as an evergreen for a quiet news day.","zh":"編輯把這次採訪作為一則可隨時播出的新聞，留給新聞較少的日子使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Travel tips are often treated as evergreen content by the website.","zh":"這個網站常把旅行建議當作可以長期使用的內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evergreen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66a424a9a958b152c1c3","word":"every","forms":["every"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7640a818242c57f1","term":"every","forms":["every"],"pos":"det","zh":"每一個；人人","explanation":"指一個可數群體中的每個成員，一個也不漏，重點是把成員逐個納入範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Every person in the room stood and cheered.","zh":"房間裡的每個人都站起來歡呼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every passenger must present a valid ticket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/every","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42afa2e2906dbc41","term":"every","forms":["every"],"pos":"det","zh":"每隔；每逢","explanation":"把“逐個納入”的感覺延伸到時間、距離或其他單位上，表示每經過相同的一段間隔就發生一次。","examples":[{"en":"The bus leaves every twenty minutes.","zh":"這班公共汽車每隔二十分鐘發一班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take a short break every hour to rest your eyes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/every","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36ec78685c6b0ffc05e7","word":"everyone/everybody","forms":["everyone","everybody"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2bbc152838445c6b","term":"everyone","forms":["everyone"],"pos":"pron","zh":"每個人；人人","explanation":"表示群體中的每一個人，沒有遺漏，重點是“人人都包括在內”。雖然意義上指許多人，everyone 在語法上通常按單數處理。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone enjoyed the party.","zh":"每個人都很享受這次聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone in our class has finished the test.","zh":"我們班的每個人都做完了測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/everyone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3b51faac44c5415","term":"everybody","forms":["everybody"],"pos":"pron","zh":"大家；每個人","explanation":"指某個範圍內的所有人，一個也不漏；根據上下文可以譯成“大家”或“每個人”。","examples":[{"en":"Everybody is ready to leave.","zh":"大家都準備好出發了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Does everybody have their ticket?","zh":"大家都有自己的票嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/everybody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0a44ed8cfc32b7e61be","word":"everything","forms":["everything"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-513825995127d07d","term":"everything","forms":["everything"],"pos":"pron","zh":"一切；所有相關事物","explanation":"指當前談論範圍內的全部事物或事情，把它們看成一個整體。範圍可以是物品、任務、資訊，也可以是正在發生的各種事情。","examples":[{"en":"I checked the list again, and everything is ready.","zh":"我又檢查了一遍清單，一切都準備好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pack everything before dinner.","zh":"請在晚飯前把所有東西都收拾好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/everything","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03b19d21974d76b2","term":"everything","forms":["everything"],"pos":"pron","zh":"最重要的因素","explanation":"當某件事被說成 everything 時，意思是它對結果或成功極其重要，幾乎決定一切。它是“整體”概念的另一種延伸：某一個關鍵部分被看成整個結果的核心。","examples":[{"en":"In a close race, timing is everything.","zh":"在勢均力敵的比賽中，時機最重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For a touring musician, reliable transport is everything.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/everything","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee8250fb76e094b34b47","word":"evidence","forms":["evidence"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cdd4e80ef14ff4e","term":"evidence","forms":["evidence","evidences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支援說法的事實材料","explanation":"指用來支援某個說法、判斷或懷疑的事實、觀察結果或其他材料；重點在於它幫助人判斷某事是否可信。","examples":[{"en":"There is no evidence that anyone was here earlier.","zh":"沒有證據表明之前有人來過這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new evidence supports her explanation.","zh":"新的證據支援她的解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evidence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-486d18ff891241c2","term":"evidence","forms":["evidence","evidences","evidencing","evidenced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"證明或顯示","explanation":"指提供事實材料，使某個判斷顯得真實或可信；也可指某人的行為、表現直接顯示出其情緒或狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Her silence evidenced her disappointment.","zh":"她的沉默表明她很失望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs evidence a considerable investment in the property.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evidence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":3,"counts":{"112":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-ed11c288ac874f1064a0","word":"evident","forms":["evident"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-971aadbd23d2a9f5","term":"evident","forms":["evident","more evident","most evident"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯而易見的","explanation":"就像被陽光照亮的東西一樣，事實已經清楚地顯露出來，普通觀察或簡單判斷就能看出它是真的。它既可以說某件事本身很明顯，也可以說明某個結論是從跡象中直接看出的。","examples":[{"en":"It was evident that she was upset after she left the room.","zh":"她離開房間後，顯然很不高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The damage was evident from the broken window.","zh":"從破碎的窗戶就能明顯看出受到了損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5c1fb2efc6d6b4674c2","word":"evil","forms":["evil"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd814c1d57104e3b","term":"evil","forms":["evil","eviller","eviler","more evil","evillest","evilest","most evil"],"pos":"adj","zh":"存心害人的","explanation":"指一個人、團體或計劃有意傷害無辜者，帶有強烈的道德譴責；這是“越過善良界線”的典型表現。","examples":[{"en":"The villain carried out an evil plot against the village.","zh":"那個反派實施了一個要傷害村莊的邪惡計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They believed the stranger had an evil purpose.","zh":"他們認為那個陌生人別有邪惡的目的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c2187163a68f1bd","term":"evil","forms":["evil","eviller","eviler","more evil","evillest","evilest","most evil"],"pos":"adj","zh":"道德敗壞的","explanation":"指行為、選擇或事物本身在道德上極其錯誤，代表善的對立面，不一定強調某一次具體的傷害。","examples":[{"en":"The story asks whether a person can choose good over evil.","zh":"這個故事探討人能否選擇善而不是邪惡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refused to support an evil system.","zh":"她拒絕支援一個道德敗壞的制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e68895d0512f2d02","term":"evil","forms":["evil","evils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邪惡","explanation":"指道德上的壞、惡意以及與善相對立的力量或行為；它把“越過善良界線”的特徵概括成一個抽象概念。","examples":[{"en":"The novel presents a long struggle between good and evil.","zh":"這部小說描寫了善與惡之間的長期鬥爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people believe that evil grows when good people remain silent.","zh":"許多人認為，善良的人保持沉默時，邪惡就會滋長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-720e5d3327634e73","term":"evil","forms":["evil","evils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禍害；傷害","explanation":"指使人失去幸福、遭受痛苦或受到損害的具體事物、情況或後果；它可以是某種社會問題，也可以是行為造成的傷害。","examples":[{"en":"The report examines the evils caused by extreme poverty.","zh":"這份報告研究了極端貧困造成的各種禍害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good laws can prevent many social evils.","zh":"良好的法律可以防止許多社會禍害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a04e52d895fe5248b939","word":"evoke","forms":["evoke"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-161d170e328ed889","term":"evoke","forms":["evoke","evokes","evoking","evoked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喚起記憶、情感或畫面","explanation":"指某人、某物或某種經歷使腦海中浮現出記憶、畫面、情感或聯想，好像把它們從心裡喚了出來。","examples":[{"en":"The smell of pine trees evoked memories of family holidays.","zh":"松樹的氣味喚起了我對家庭假期的記憶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her painting evokes a feeling of quiet loneliness.","zh":"她的畫喚起了一種安靜的孤獨感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-508cb3e3712c0f61","term":"evoke","forms":["evoke","evokes","evoking","evoked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引發反應","explanation":"指某件事促使別人產生某種反應、回應或表現；這裡被“叫出來”的不是記憶，而是人的反應。","examples":[{"en":"The speaker's joke evoked laughter from the audience.","zh":"演講者的笑話引起了聽眾的笑聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The melody evoked memories of summer holidays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-970eaf0d4dc9bec3d741","word":"evolution","forms":["evolution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5086a24ad008961c","term":"evolution","forms":["evolution","evolutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"逐步發展；演變","explanation":"指某種事物隨著時間逐步變化、成熟並形成現在的樣子，重點是連續的過程，而不是突然發生的一次改變。它可以用於文化、技術、思想、風格、制度等許多事物。","examples":[{"en":"The evolution of online shopping has changed the way people buy everyday goods.","zh":"網上購物的發展改變了人們購買日常用品的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We traced the evolution of the city's architecture over three centuries.","zh":"我們追溯了這座城市建築風格在三個世紀中的演變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-136abab300cc4b03","term":"evolution","forms":["evolution","evolutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隊形調動；軍事演練動作","explanation":"指軍隊或一隊人按照安排移動、變換位置或隊形，強調一連串有組織的動作。這個意思保留了“展開、變換”的具體畫面，現代日常英語中主要出現在軍事或歷史語境裡。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers practiced complex evolutions on the parade ground.","zh":"士兵們在閱兵場上練習複雜的隊形變換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The review described the fleet's coordinated evolutions in unusually precise detail.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b200897121bfd4012645","word":"evolve","forms":["evolve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f600e5618c13b02f","term":"evolve","forms":["evolve","evolves","evolving","evolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐步改變或發展","explanation":"表示把某事物經過一段時間逐步改造成新的樣子，例如故事、制度或產品不斷發展變化。","examples":[{"en":"The small project evolved into a useful online service.","zh":"這個小專案逐步發展成了一項有用的線上服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She evolved the original idea into a practical design.","zh":"她把最初的想法逐步發展成了一個實用的設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9dc5037eef894833","term":"evolve","forms":["evolve","evolves","evolving","evolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸變成","explanation":"表示某事物本身經過時間逐步發展，最後變成另一種狀態或形式，這是 evolve 最重要的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The conversation evolved into a serious discussion about trust.","zh":"這場談話逐漸變成了關於信任的嚴肅討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app has evolved considerably since its first release.","zh":"這款應用自首次釋出以來已經有了很大的發展變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa79d4746c21cd960a17","word":"exact","forms":["exact"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-531bf6a52c1de517","term":"exact","forms":["exact","exacter","more exact","exactest","most exact"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精確的；完全一致的","explanation":"表示某個時間、數量、答案或事實與標準完全吻合，既沒有多一點，也沒有少一點。它正是“刻度完全對齊”的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"Please tell me the exact address.","zh":"請告訴我確切的地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train arrived at the exact time shown on the ticket.","zh":"火車在票上寫明的準確時間到達了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a76d5874ce043d7c824","word":"exaggerate","forms":["exaggerate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c878f5eeedd02518","term":"exaggerate","forms":["exaggerate","exaggerates","exaggerating","exaggerated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"誇大；言過其實","explanation":"把事實像越堆越高一樣說得超過實際程度，例如把數量、困難或經歷描述得更大、更嚴重。這不一定是故意撒謊，但會讓資訊失真。","examples":[{"en":"Don't exaggerate the problem; we can fix it this afternoon.","zh":"別把問題說得太嚴重；我們今天下午就能解決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tends to exaggerate when he tells stories.","zh":"他講故事時往往會誇大其詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exaggerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c0013cee81ff71d4795","word":"exaggeration","forms":["exaggeration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30910ce708a94944","term":"exaggeration","forms":["exaggeration","exaggerations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誇大；言過其實","explanation":"指把事實、數量或程度說得比實際更大、更嚴重，超出了真實、合理或公正的範圍；也可以指這種誇大的說法本身。","examples":[{"en":"Calling the short delay a disaster was an exaggeration.","zh":"把這次短暫的延誤說成災難，實在是誇大了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The claim that she never makes mistakes is a clear exaggeration.","zh":"說她從不犯錯，顯然是誇大其詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exaggeration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e80506d5654cc154","term":"exaggeration","forms":["exaggeration","exaggerations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術誇張","explanation":"指在繪畫、文學或表演中，故意把外貌、力量、動作等表現得超過自然狀態，以增強視覺效果或感染力。","examples":[{"en":"The cartoon uses exaggeration to make the character's huge muscles look funny.","zh":"這部漫畫用誇張手法把人物的大塊肌肉畫得很滑稽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The portrait uses exaggeration to emphasize his enormous eyebrows.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exaggeration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e29b2eeb0bb989f0c0a","word":"examination/exam","forms":["examination","exam"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a88da301713c12a4","term":"examination","forms":["examination","examinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檢查；查驗","explanation":"指為了弄清某人或某事的情況而進行的系統、仔細的檢視，是其他幾個意思的共同基礎。它可以是一次具體的檢查，也可以泛指檢查這一行為。","examples":[{"en":"The examination of the machine found several small cracks.","zh":"對這臺機器的檢查發現了幾處小裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Examination of the lock revealed signs of forced entry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/examination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc316a42a9950313","term":"examination","forms":["examination","examinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式考試","explanation":"指在規定時間內回答書面或口頭問題的正式測驗，通常考查一段課程中學過的內容，往往不能查閱教材；它是把“檢查”轉向檢查學習成果。","examples":[{"en":"She is studying every evening for her final examination.","zh":"她每天晚上都在為期末考試學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You must pass the examination before applying for the license.","zh":"申請許可證前，你必須透過這項考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/examination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caf8b746e1eaccee","term":"exam","forms":["exam","exams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考試；測驗","explanation":"指用來檢查學習成果或知識掌握情況的考試、測驗。它可以是一次重要的正式考試，也可以是課程中的普通小測驗。","examples":[{"en":"I have a math exam tomorrow, so I need to study tonight.","zh":"我明天有數學考試，所以今晚得學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She passed the final exam on her first try.","zh":"她第一次參加期末考試就透過了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ccb261d43dccffa74758","word":"examine","forms":["examine"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c8eb1ef4991ef0a","term":"examine","forms":["examine","examines","examining","examined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細檢查","explanation":"表示為了發現細節、問題或線索而仔細觀察或檢查某人或某物，是這個詞最基本的“看清楚”用法。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic examined the car for signs of damage.","zh":"修理工仔細檢查汽車是否有損壞的跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She examined the map before choosing a route.","zh":"她仔細檢視地圖後才選擇路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/examine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5eb05dd259fb208c","term":"examine","forms":["examine","examines","examining","examined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"檢查健康狀況","explanation":"表示專業人員檢視人或物的健康、狀態或身體情況，以判斷是否正常；醫生檢查病人就是把“仔細看清狀況”用在醫療場景中。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor examined my ankle and ordered an X-ray.","zh":"醫生檢查了我的腳踝，並安排了X光檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse examined the cut for signs of infection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/examine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-225a0d0db8eb37f93c4c","word":"examinee","forms":["examinee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"examinee","forms":["examinee"],"pos":"n.","zh":"應試者；考生","examples":[{"en":"Each examinee must bring a valid identification card.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The examiner gave the nervous examinee a glass of water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-064807585e6f79206eeb","word":"examiner","forms":["examiner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65c50190cf260955","term":"examiner","forms":["examiner","examiners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檢查或調查人員","explanation":"指透過檢視、核對或調查來判斷某人或某物情況的人，例如檢查行李、檔案或案件的人。這是從“仔細檢視的人”這一核心形象直接發展出來的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The customs examiner opened the suitcase and checked the contents.","zh":"海關檢查員開啟行李箱，檢查裡面的物品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The examiner asked several questions about the company's records.","zh":"調查人員就公司的記錄提出了幾個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/examiner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dffe716e273cc1d","term":"examiner","forms":["examiner","examiners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"命題考官","explanation":"指負責設計、擬定或組織考試的人；他把需要考查的內容安排成試題，供考生作答。","examples":[{"en":"The examiner set a difficult final examination for the students.","zh":"考官為學生安排了一場很難的期末考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The examiner prepared questions covering every required topic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/examiner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50d858e0985ecc7f6041","word":"example","forms":["example"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48202c8cb6d72116","term":"example","forms":["example","examples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表性例子","explanation":"從一類事物中挑出的一個具體物件，用來代表這整類事物；重點在於它能讓人看出這一類事物通常是什麼樣。","examples":[{"en":"This painting is a fine example of modern art.","zh":"這幅畫是現代藝術的一個典型例子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The blue whale is an example of a very large mammal.","zh":"藍鯨是大型哺乳動物的一個例子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/example","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-851bf5d78db2a635","term":"example","forms":["example","examples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說明規則的示例","explanation":"一個具體事例，用來把較抽象的規則、解釋或觀點講清楚，讓人看到它在實際中怎樣體現。","examples":[{"en":"Can you give an example of how this rule works?","zh":"你能舉個例子說明這條規則是怎麼運作的嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This mistake is a good example of the problem.","zh":"這個錯誤很好地說明了問題所在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/example","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b7595d8bdf2f907","term":"example","forms":["example","examples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"榜樣；行為範例","explanation":"某人的行為被看作一種模式，別人可以照著做，也可能把它當作反面教材而避免效仿；因此可以是好的榜樣，也可以是不好的榜樣。","examples":[{"en":"She set a good example for the younger students.","zh":"她為年紀較小的學生樹立了好榜樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His honesty is an example we should follow.","zh":"他的誠實是我們應該效仿的榜樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/example","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a12b051e0416dc3217e","word":"exceed","forms":["exceed"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e0933d1577412a7","term":"exceed","forms":["exceed","exceeds","exceeding","exceeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"超過數量或大小","explanation":"某個數量、金額、尺寸或程度比另一個物件更大，重點是客觀數值或規模越過了比較物件。","examples":[{"en":"This year's sales exceeded last year's total.","zh":"今年的銷售額超過了去年的總額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new stadium can hold more than 50,000 people, exceeding the old one by 10,000.","zh":"新體育場可容納五萬多人，比舊體育場多一萬人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exceed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b52cc52262b85ea1","term":"exceed","forms":["exceed","exceeds","exceeding","exceeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勝過標準或預期","explanation":"某人的表現、質量或結果比原先設定的標準更好，因此可以理解為“越過了期待的那條線”。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant exceeded all our expectations.","zh":"這家餐館完全超出了我們的預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Demand exceeded the warehouse capacity within three days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exceed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50b44ab00082e524","term":"exceed","forms":["exceed","exceeds","exceeding","exceeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"超出限制","explanation":"某事物越過規定的最大範圍、時長或數量，常用於說明規則、容量和技術限制。","examples":[{"en":"The file size must not exceed 10 megabytes.","zh":"檔案大小不得超過十兆位元組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your answer should not exceed 200 words.","zh":"你的回答不應超過兩百詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exceed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-faba1e00af8e6c89837f","word":"excel","forms":["excel"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5926ee61f668aca4","term":"excel","forms":["excel","excels","excelling","excelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勝過某人或某物","explanation":"表示某人在成績、能力或表現上超過另一個人或事物，重點是比較結果。這個用法把“站得更高”的畫面具體化為勝過對手。","examples":[{"en":"She excelled her classmates in the final examination.","zh":"她在期末考試中勝過了同班同學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new design excels the old one in both speed and safety.","zh":"新設計在速度和安全性方面都勝過舊設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4644f0ab5dd9b8ff","term":"excel","forms":["excel","excels","excelling","excelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在某方面表現出色","explanation":"表示某人或某事在某個領域特別突出，不一定明確指出勝過誰；可以理解為自己在某方面站到了更高處。","examples":[{"en":"He excels at explaining difficult ideas clearly.","zh":"他特別擅長把複雜的想法解釋清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He excels in endurance events but struggles with sprinting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87409b1c5a34910b1e75","word":"excellence","forms":["excellence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b044915f55fb843d","term":"excellence","forms":["excellence","excellences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"卓越；優秀","explanation":"指某項工作、表現或能力達到非常高的水平，強調“出色”這一整體品質，而不是某一個具體成果。","examples":[{"en":"The school is known for excellence in science education.","zh":"這所學校以科學教育方面的卓越表現而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The award recognizes excellence in public service.","zh":"這項獎項表彰公共服務領域的卓越表現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excellence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ece2c059fc81492b","term":"excellence","forms":["excellence","excellences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專長；拿手之處","explanation":"指某人特別擅長的方面，也就是他的能力優勢；這裡的“出色”從一種總體品質具體落到了某個領域或技能上。","examples":[{"en":"Her excellence in design helped the team win the competition.","zh":"她在設計方面的特長幫助團隊贏得了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clarity of expression is one of her excellences.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excellence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d785acc7d4ce49fe4e4","word":"excellent","forms":["excellent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64f4541e913165df","term":"excellent","forms":["excellent","more excellent","most excellent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"質量上乘；極好的","explanation":"表示質量高、水平高，或整體令人稱讚，是最核心、最常用的意思。它可以形容物品、工作、想法、服務和機會等。","examples":[{"en":"This is an excellent book for beginners.","zh":"這是一本非常適合初學者的優秀書籍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You did an excellent job on the presentation.","zh":"你的演講做得非常出色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excellent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fc8a9ee8be895a6","term":"excellent","forms":["excellent","more excellent","most excellent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別好；出色的","explanation":"表示某事物在同類中格外好，尤其適合評價一次經歷、一個計劃或某種表現。它常常只是強烈地說“很好”，不必進行嚴格比較。","examples":[{"en":"We had an excellent time at the museum.","zh":"我們在博物館玩得特別開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel serves an excellent breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excellent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b11279547bc49510a81a","word":"except","forms":["except"],"officialPos":"prep./conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01d0646d5dad3ad5","term":"except","forms":["except"],"pos":"prep","zh":"除……之外；……除外","explanation":"它把一個物件劃出前面說的整體範圍，說明這個物件是例外。例如說“櫃子裡什麼都沒有，除了豆子罐頭”，就是其他東西都沒有，只有豆子罐頭在裡面。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone finished the test except Maya.","zh":"除了瑪雅，所有人都完成了測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is nothing in the box except a note.","zh":"盒子裡除了便條什麼也沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/except","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2104e56ef446302ca000","word":"exception","forms":["exception"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8afea5129de3a363","term":"exception","forms":["exception","exceptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排除；不納入","explanation":"指把原本會被包括在某個類別、宣告或規則中的內容排除出去，強調“從一般範圍裡拿掉”這一動作或限制。","examples":[{"en":"The exception of weekends from the policy was clearly stated.","zh":"該政策明確說明不包括週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone was invited, with the exception of former members.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e77147112a2e82d6","term":"exception","forms":["exception","exceptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"例外；特殊情況","explanation":"指不符合通常規則、被單獨看待的人、事物或情況。它就是“從規則圈子裡拿出來的一個特殊點”，是日常最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is open every day, with the exception of Monday.","zh":"這家博物館每天開放，星期一除外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are always a few exceptions to this rule.","zh":"這條規則總會有幾個例外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14930a90c71a8711f252","word":"exceptional","forms":["exceptional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2af621675e68d9b9","term":"exceptional","forms":["exceptional","more exceptional","most exceptional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非同尋常的；罕見的","explanation":"它表示某人或某物跳出了平常範圍，因而少見、特別或不尋常；重點是“不同於通常情況”，不一定表示更好。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is open on exceptional occasions.","zh":"這家博物館只在特殊情況下開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What an exceptional meal!","zh":"這頓飯真是非同尋常！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exceptional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98baa00cdbace2fb","term":"exceptional","forms":["exceptional","more exceptional","most exceptional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別優秀的","explanation":"它表示某人的能力或某物的質量明顯高於平均水平，是“超出通常範圍”這一核心概念在正面評價中的發展。","examples":[{"en":"The quality of the beer was exceptional.","zh":"這種啤酒的質量非常出色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her exceptional skill earned immediate recognition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exceptional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df50f680326679347d55","word":"excerpt","forms":["excerpt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bc5286f19d22369","term":"excerpt","forms":["excerpt","excerpts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摘錄；片段","explanation":"指從一篇文章、一本書、電影或其他較大作品中挑出來的一小段內容；這段內容通常仍保留原作的形式。","examples":[{"en":"The magazine published an excerpt from her new novel.","zh":"這本雜誌刊登了她新小說的一段節選。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a short excerpt from the documentary.","zh":"我們觀看了這部紀錄片的一個短片段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excerpt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25a03287fdfe9381","term":"excerpt","forms":["excerpt","excerpts","excerpting","excerpted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"摘錄；節選","explanation":"指從完整作品中挑出一部分內容並複製、引用或發表，強調“把片段挑出來”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The editor excerpted two paragraphs from the report for the newsletter.","zh":"編輯從報告中摘錄了兩段文字用於簡報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newspaper excerpted several passages from her memoir.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excerpt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ddd36ae5e6900effb789","word":"excess","forms":["excess"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f3e3f218e2a446c","term":"excess","forms":["excess"],"pos":"adj","zh":"過多的；額外的","explanation":"指數量或程度越過了正常、必要或規定的範圍；它強調“超過夠用線”的部分。","examples":[{"en":"Passengers must pay for excess baggage.","zh":"乘客必須為超額行李付費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory has excess capacity this year.","zh":"這家工廠今年有過剩產能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adc46f6c6519a2d5","term":"excess","forms":["excess","excesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過量；超出限度","explanation":"指某物超過了正常、必要、適當或規定的程度，也可指這種超出的狀態或數量。","examples":[{"en":"An excess of salt can raise your blood pressure.","zh":"鹽攝入過量可能會升高血壓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shipment weighs in excess of two tons.","zh":"這批貨物的重量超過兩噸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f47e627c6b9894b2c6b","word":"excessive","forms":["excessive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9c910bee3141f0f","term":"excessive","forms":["excessive","more excessive","most excessive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"過度的；過量的","explanation":"指某種數量、程度或行為超過通常、合理的範圍，因此顯得太多、太強或太誇張。重點不只是“多”，而是“多到不合適”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel charged an excessive fee for a short taxi ride.","zh":"這家酒店為一小段計程車行程收取了過高的費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His excessive use of his phone kept him awake all night.","zh":"他過度使用手機，結果整晚都沒睡著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excessive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab27b729d9cc4cb1c009","word":"exchange","forms":["exchange"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-662e58d9b165ece9","term":"exchange","forms":["exchange","exchanges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交換；互換","explanation":"指雙方把物品、位置、服務或價值相近的東西互相換給對方，重點在來回交換這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams agreed to an exchange of players.","zh":"兩隊同意互換球員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me her old camera in exchange for my tablet.","zh":"她用她的舊相機換了我的平板電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exchange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-793cd77792dc31d9","term":"exchange","forms":["exchange","exchanges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交談；言語交鋒","explanation":"指雙方來回說話、提問或爭論的一段互動；交換的不是物品，而是話語。","examples":[{"en":"I had a brief exchange with the receptionist before the meeting.","zh":"開會前我和接待員簡短交談了幾句。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their heated exchange attracted everyone's attention.","zh":"他們激烈的爭執吸引了所有人的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exchange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe87dcb3e5e0ffd7","term":"exchange","forms":["exchange","exchanges","exchanging","exchanged","exchangest","exchangedst","exchangeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交換；互換","explanation":"指雙方把物品、位置或價值互相換給對方，是名詞“交換”變成動作後的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"I'll exchange my seat for yours if you prefer the window.","zh":"如果你更喜歡靠窗的座位，我可以和你換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children exchanged gifts after the party.","zh":"聚會後孩子們互相交換了禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exchange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca6cc42a27f1e249","term":"exchange","forms":["exchange","exchanges","exchanging","exchanged","exchangest","exchangedst","exchangeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"更換；換成","explanation":"指把原來的物品退回或拿走，再換取另一件作為替代品；畫面仍是把舊物遞迴、把新物接回來。","examples":[{"en":"Can I exchange this jacket for a smaller size?","zh":"我可以把這件夾克換成小一號的嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He exchanged his ticket for one on an earlier train.","zh":"他把車票換成了更早一班火車的票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exchange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68570e4081a38d045eb9","word":"excite(ment)","forms":["excite","excitement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58b1085579ee949c","term":"excite","forms":["excite","excites","exciting","excited","excitest","excitedst","exciteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使興奮；使激動","explanation":"指某件事讓人產生強烈的興奮、激動或期待，就像按下了人的“興奮鍵”。","examples":[{"en":"The surprise concert excited everyone in the crowd.","zh":"這場突然宣佈的音樂會讓人群中的每個人都興奮不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were excited about seeing the animals.","zh":"孩子們想到要看那些動物就興奮不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f531e2d06d765fa9","term":"excite","forms":["excite","excites","exciting","excited","excitest","excitedst","exciteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"激起；引發感情","explanation":"指某種行為、處境或訊息把某種具體感情喚起，感情不一定是愉快的，例如嫉妒、憤怒或興趣。","examples":[{"en":"Her sudden promotion excited jealousy among her coworkers.","zh":"她突然升職在同事之間激起了嫉妒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discovery excited considerable interest among astronomers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d8d5e0231bd36ce","term":"excitement","forms":["excitement","excitements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"興奮；激動","explanation":"指人因為期待、刺激、快樂或緊張而產生的興奮狀態，重點是心裡的感覺，而不是引起感覺的具體事情。","examples":[{"en":"The crowd got caught up in the excitement of the final minute.","zh":"觀眾都沉浸在最後一分鐘的激動氣氛中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You could hear the excitement in her voice.","zh":"從她的聲音裡都能聽出興奮之情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excitement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e7fd04224ac78e3","term":"excitement","forms":["excitement","excitements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人興奮的事；刺激","explanation":"指能點燃這種興奮情緒的具體事情、活動或經歷，例如比賽、旅行中的新鮮體驗或特別的節目。","examples":[{"en":"One of the excitements of travel is meeting people from different cultures.","zh":"旅行的樂趣之一，就是能遇到來自不同文化的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The parade provided plenty of excitement for the children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excitement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d1c8a7a12c3739bb3b9","word":"excited","forms":["excited"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb5f77503268ea50","term":"excited","forms":["excited","more excited","most excited"],"pos":"adj","zh":"興奮的；激動的","explanation":"指人因期待、好訊息或強烈興趣而情緒高漲、充滿熱情和精力。這個意義就是“能量被激發起來”的日常用法。","examples":[{"en":"I’m excited about starting my new job next week.","zh":"我很期待下週開始新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were excited when they saw the presents.","zh":"孩子們看到禮物時都興奮起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excited","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ae666e5b1a641b37709","word":"exciting","forms":["exciting"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9964b6034feb0500","term":"exciting","forms":["exciting","more exciting","most exciting"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人興奮的；激動人心的","explanation":"指某件事、某個活動或某種經歷能把人的情緒“按亮”，使人感到興奮、激動或很有興趣。","examples":[{"en":"The final match was one of the most exciting games of the season.","zh":"決賽是本賽季最激動人心的比賽之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have some exciting news to share with you.","zh":"我們有一些令人興奮的訊息要告訴你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exciting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-344a3011262cf46429b9","word":"exclaim","forms":["exclaim"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d8a3f100d5a403c","term":"exclaim","forms":["exclaim","exclaims","exclaiming","exclaimed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然喊叫","explanation":"指因為驚訝、害怕、憤怒或興奮等強烈情緒，突然喊出聲，但不特別強調喊出了什麼具體內容。","examples":[{"en":"She exclaimed in surprise when the lights suddenly went out.","zh":"燈突然熄滅時，她驚訝地喊了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"'Look out!' she exclaimed as the branch fell.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclaim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80ffd06da4d74b49","term":"exclaim","forms":["exclaim","exclaims","exclaiming","exclaimed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"激動地說出","explanation":"指在強烈情緒推動下突然說出一句話或一個判斷，重點是說話方式很激動，而不只是內容本身。","examples":[{"en":"“That is unbelievable!” he exclaimed.","zh":"“這簡直難以置信！”他激動地說道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She exclaimed that the ring was missing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclaim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35443277fe297662cfc3","word":"exclude","forms":["exclude"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9a7b2e200a60a0e","term":"exclude","forms":["exclude","excludes","excluding","excluded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不讓進入；擋在外面","explanation":"把某人或某物擋在一個地方、活動或範圍之外，使其不能進入或參與。這是“把門關上”的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The club excludes anyone under sixteen from its evening events.","zh":"這個俱樂部不讓十六歲以下的人參加晚間活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please close the door to exclude the cold air.","zh":"請關上門，把冷空氣擋在外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-060e275b1a4c3e4a","term":"exclude","forms":["exclude","excludes","excluding","excluded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不計入；不考慮","explanation":"把某項內容有意放在計算、統計或討論範圍之外，因此它不會影響最後的結果。這裡的“門”變成了一個抽象範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The total excludes delivery and installation costs.","zh":"總價不包括配送和安裝費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The estimate excludes the cost of replacement windows.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-180a26f2655f92f654a1","word":"exclusion","forms":["exclusion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5937f13caec9a088","term":"exclusion","forms":["exclusion","exclusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排除；不讓參加","explanation":"指把某人或某事排除在某個群體、活動、權利或考慮範圍之外，也可以指這種排除行為或結果。核心畫面就是關上門，不讓物件進入或參與。","examples":[{"en":"The exclusion of local residents from the meeting caused widespread anger.","zh":"不讓當地居民參加這次會議引起了廣泛的憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The policy aims to prevent the exclusion of children with disabilities.","zh":"這項政策旨在防止殘障兒童被排除在外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb5e20d06d84c2fd","term":"exclusion","forms":["exclusion","exclusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險除外專案","explanation":"在保險中，指保單明確不承擔、不賠付的風險、情況或損失，也就是被擋在保險保障範圍之外的專案。","examples":[{"en":"Damage caused by flooding is a common exclusion in home insurance policies.","zh":"洪水造成的損失是家庭保險保單中常見的除外專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The policy's exclusions include damage caused by flooding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-433cd7fc8060e0821280","word":"exclusive","forms":["exclusive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16ea97722d9e6614","term":"exclusive","forms":["exclusive","more exclusive","most exclusive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"排除不符合條件者的","explanation":"指按照某些條件把不符合要求的人或事物排除在外，只保留符合條件的物件；這是 exclusive 最基本的“關在圈外”含義。","examples":[{"en":"This offer is exclusive to members.","zh":"這項優惠僅限會員享用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The price is exclusive of tax.","zh":"這個價格不含稅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclusive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c357fbef05669cd","term":"exclusive","forms":["exclusive","more exclusive","most exclusive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"專屬而高檔的","explanation":"形容只向少數有資格、有錢或有地位的人開放的俱樂部、品牌、服務等，因此常帶有高檔、知名或勢利的意味。","examples":[{"en":"They booked an exclusive hotel on the island.","zh":"他們預訂了島上一家高檔的專屬酒店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gallery hosted an exclusive dinner for its donors.","zh":"這家畫廊為捐贈者舉辦了一場僅限特定人士參加的晚宴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exclusive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b76c1db1f24b29fe617b","word":"excuse","forms":["excuse"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae367a9a058341db","term":"excuse","forms":["excuse","excuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藉口；辯解理由","explanation":"為了減輕過錯帶來的責備，或避免別人負面評價而提出的理由；它可以是真實解釋，也可以被聽者認為是在推卸責任。","examples":[{"en":"Being tired is no excuse for speaking rudely to your parents.","zh":"疲憊不能成為你對父母出言不遜的藉口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave an excuse for missing the meeting, but nobody believed it.","zh":"她為錯過會議找了個藉口，但沒人相信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85e410c179dc2bc5","term":"excuse","forms":["excuse","excuses","excusing","excused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"准許免除；允許離開","explanation":"把某人從一項義務、活動或場合中放出來，使他不必繼續參加或履行；也可以禮貌地請求離開。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher excused Maya from practice because she was ill.","zh":"瑪雅生病了，所以老師准許她不參加訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"May I be excused from practice tomorrow?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f6c6474852c1780","term":"excuse","forms":["excuse","excuses","excusing","excused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……開脫；為……辯護","explanation":"提出理由來減輕某個行為的錯誤或責任，好像把它從應受責備的範圍中推開；不一定表示說話者真的認同這個行為。","examples":[{"en":"Nothing can excuse his decision to lie to the whole team.","zh":"他決定對整個團隊撒謊，這件事無論如何都無法開脫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her difficult childhood may explain her anger, but it does not excuse it.","zh":"她艱難的童年或許能解釋她為什麼憤怒，但不能為這種憤怒開脫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/excuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be6bdfe81ec4a456a537","word":"execute","forms":["execute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb246e6056cdf8f1","term":"execute","forms":["execute","executes","executing","executed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"執行；實施","explanation":"指把命令、計劃、決定或行動真正做出來，強調從要求到落實的完整過程。","examples":[{"en":"The team executed the plan exactly as discussed.","zh":"團隊完全按照討論的內容執行了計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officers executed the search warrant at dawn.","zh":"警員在黎明時執行了搜查令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/execute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68fb980d66f5db4e","term":"execute","forms":["execute","executes","executing","executed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"執行；啟動","explanation":"在計算機等技術語境中，指讓程式開始執行並執行其中的指令，是“把程式落實為實際運作”。","examples":[{"en":"The system will execute the program automatically.","zh":"系統會自動執行這個程式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need administrator permission to execute this file.","zh":"你需要管理員許可權才能執行這個檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/execute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a402c4336ebfd78227de","word":"execution","forms":["execution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d0b2aa434f40c12","term":"execution","forms":["execution","executions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"執行方式；實施","explanation":"指把計劃、動作、任務或表演真正做出來的過程，也可以強調做這件事時採用的方式和技巧。它連線著“貫徹到底”這條核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The plan was good, but its execution was poor.","zh":"這個計劃很好，但執行得很差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancer impressed us with the precision of her execution.","zh":"這位舞者執行動作時的精準度給我們留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/execution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd474ade1aee1df4","term":"execution","forms":["execution","executions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實施完成；完成情況","explanation":"指某項任務、計劃或使命已經被落實並完成的狀態或過程，重點是“做成了”。","examples":[{"en":"The successful execution of the mission raised the team's confidence.","zh":"任務的成功完成增強了團隊的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan was ambitious but poor in execution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/execution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-180b988a36f655a375c5","word":"executive","forms":["executive"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3d357adc2c807c1","term":"executive","forms":["executive","more executive","most executive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"行政管理的；管理層的","explanation":"指與組織、公司或國家的日常執行和管理有關，強調由負責落實和作決定的管理層來處理事務。","examples":[{"en":"The board approved the executive team's plan.","zh":"董事會批准了管理團隊的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made an executive decision to close the office early.","zh":"她以管理者的許可權決定提前關閉辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/executive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d9ba13471b4ba83","term":"executive","forms":["executive","executives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高管；行政主管","explanation":"指在公司或其他組織中擁有較大自主決策權、負責重要事務和日常執行的管理人員。它強調“能作決定並推動落實”，不只是普通員工或一般主管。","examples":[{"en":"Several senior executives joined the meeting.","zh":"幾名高階管理人員參加了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chief executive announced the new strategy.","zh":"執行長宣佈了新戰略。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/executive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42d8a7ea9cafaebde853","word":"exempt","forms":["exempt"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-045fe793708408a3","term":"exempt","forms":["exempt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"免於；獲准不受……約束","explanation":"某人或某事被從一項義務、規則或法律的適用範圍中拿開，因此不必承擔該義務或不受該規則約束。","examples":[{"en":"Children under six are exempt from the entrance fee.","zh":"六歲以下兒童免收入場費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new rule exempts small businesses from filing this report.","zh":"新規定使小型企業免於提交這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exempt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f55101cb5e7453c770d2","word":"exercise","forms":["exercise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ef283f90b7730bc","term":"exercise","forms":["exercise","exercises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"練習；訓練題","explanation":"指為了提高某種技能而安排的活動，尤其可以指課本、課堂或訓練中的一道練習題。","examples":[{"en":"Please complete exercise three before tomorrow.","zh":"請在明天之前完成第三道練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This writing exercise will help you organize your ideas.","zh":"這項寫作練習會幫助你整理思路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exercise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8196d8e07966a95b","term":"exercise","forms":["exercise","exercises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鍛鍊；運動","explanation":"指為了保持或提高身體健康、力量和體能而進行的活動，也可以泛指這種鍛鍊本身。","examples":[{"en":"Swimming is excellent exercise for your whole body.","zh":"游泳是非常好的全身鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I try to get some exercise after work.","zh":"我儘量在下班後鍛鍊一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exercise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ebdcb763358b628","term":"exercise","forms":["exercise","exercises","exercising","exercised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"訓練；練習","explanation":"指透過反覆使用和訓練來提高某人的技能、能力或思考能力，也可以指訓練動物或隊伍。","examples":[{"en":"These puzzles exercise your memory and concentration.","zh":"這些謎題能訓練你的記憶力和注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach exercises the horses every morning.","zh":"教練每天早上訓練馬匹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exercise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaa51b268ce1dddf","term":"exercise","forms":["exercise","exercises","exercising","exercised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鍛鍊身體","explanation":"指進行體育活動或身體活動，以保持健康、增強力量或改善體能。","examples":[{"en":"I exercise for thirty minutes every morning.","zh":"我每天早上鍛鍊三十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She exercises at home when the weather is bad.","zh":"天氣不好時，她在家鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exercise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4eac0cdd1fd7916e14da","word":"exert","forms":["exert"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fdd8b1cf1cee9586","term":"exert","forms":["exert","exerts","exerting","exerted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"施加影響或力量","explanation":"把某種力量、影響、壓力或控制作用到人或事情上；這裡的“力量”不一定是身體力量，也可以是職位、關係等帶來的影響力。","examples":[{"en":"The manager exerted considerable influence over the final decision.","zh":"經理對最終決定施加了相當大的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The group tried to exert pressure on the company to change its policy.","zh":"這個團體試圖向公司施壓，要求它改變政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cc3687991c1dd42","term":"exert","forms":["exert","exerts","exerting","exerted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使自己全力行動","explanation":"把自己的體力、精力或意志充分用出來，努力完成某項任務；可以理解為把力量伸回自己身上，讓自己竭盡全力。","examples":[{"en":"She exerted herself to finish the report before lunch.","zh":"她竭盡全力，爭取在午飯前完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't exert yourself while you're recovering.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3592f48abb9339b4558c","word":"exhaust","forms":["exhaust"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1dadc424471dedb6","term":"exhaust","forms":["exhaust","exhausts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排氣系統","explanation":"指發動機中燃燒後的氣體排出的整套部件和通道，也就是汽車的排氣系統。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic replaced the car's exhaust system.","zh":"修理工更換了這輛車的排氣系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic found a hole in the exhaust.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhaust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e778834bc01c91b0","term":"exhaust","forms":["exhaust","exhausts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廢氣","explanation":"指發動機或其他燃燒過程排出的氣體，通常帶有汙染物。","examples":[{"en":"The factory releases toxic exhaust into the air.","zh":"這家工廠把有毒廢氣排入空氣中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Diesel exhaust filled the narrow garage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhaust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-243e5aef1caee9c9","term":"exhaust","forms":["exhaust","exhausts","exhausting","exhausted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"耗盡；用光","explanation":"把供應、資源、耐心或其他可用的東西用到一點不剩，正是“把容器抽空”這一核心畫面的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The long drought exhausted the town's water supply.","zh":"長期乾旱耗盡了這個城鎮的供水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She never seems to exhaust her patience.","zh":"她的耐心似乎永遠也用不完。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhaust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73aa5e2643566c61","term":"exhaust","forms":["exhaust","exhausts","exhausting","exhausted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使精疲力竭","explanation":"把一個人的體力或精力消耗到幾乎沒有，像把能量完全抽空一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The overnight flight exhausted me.","zh":"這次通宵航班讓我精疲力竭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Caring for the baby exhausted both parents.","zh":"照顧嬰兒把父母倆都累得筋疲力竭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhaust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2cc7e7e9e251522b627a","word":"exhibit","forms":["exhibit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1e9124db770e318","term":"exhibit","forms":["exhibit","exhibits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"展品","explanation":"指被拿出來供人觀看的具體物品，例如博物館中的一件物品、藝術品或歷史文物。","examples":[{"en":"This exhibit is one of the oldest tools in the museum.","zh":"這件展品是博物館裡最古老的工具之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The oldest exhibit is a carved wooden spoon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhibit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a609cdb8e42f241","term":"exhibit","forms":["exhibit","exhibits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"展覽","explanation":"指面向公眾安排的一組展示或一次公開展出，通常在博物館、畫廊或其他公共場所舉行。","examples":[{"en":"The museum's new exhibit opens on Saturday.","zh":"博物館的新展覽週六開幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibit runs until the end of June.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhibit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fcba4eb44eac274","term":"exhibit","forms":["exhibit","exhibits","exhibiting","exhibited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"展示物品","explanation":"指把物品擺出來或帶到展覽、比賽等場合供別人觀看，核心仍是“拿出來給人看”。","examples":[{"en":"She will exhibit her photographs at the summer festival.","zh":"她將在夏季節慶活動上展出自己的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum will exhibit the restored armor next month.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhibit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9169b461a4fdaa4e","term":"exhibit","forms":["exhibit","exhibits","exhibiting","exhibited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯露出","explanation":"指透過行為或表現讓別人看出某種能力、品質、情緒或特徵，相當於把內在的東西“顯露”到外面。","examples":[{"en":"The young players exhibited remarkable teamwork.","zh":"這些年輕運動員表現出了出色的團隊協作能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient exhibited no signs of distress.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhibit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83a2bff84b1d599d9eed","word":"exhibition","forms":["exhibition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4af2c15850dbfd5","term":"exhibition","forms":["exhibition","exhibitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"展示；展出","explanation":"泛指把某物、某種能力或某種現象展示給別人看，也可以指被展示出來的東西本身。","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition of rare books attracted many visitors.","zh":"珍稀書籍的展出吸引了許多參觀者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm exhibition of confidence reassured the team.","zh":"她鎮定自信的表現讓團隊安下心來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhibition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d8803a4b24a4e98","term":"exhibition","forms":["exhibition","exhibitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公開展覽；展覽會","explanation":"指在公共場所集中展示藝術品、產品或其他物品的大型活動，通常可供公眾參觀。","examples":[{"en":"There is a photography exhibition at the town hall this weekend.","zh":"本週末市政廳有一個攝影展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent the afternoon walking around the exhibition.","zh":"我們整個下午都在展覽會上參觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhibition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-55ab75d85a136dfe0c7a","word":"exile","forms":["exile"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7121599ca5094559","term":"exile","forms":["exile","exiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流放；流亡","explanation":"指一個人被迫離開自己的家鄉或祖國，並持續處於不能回去或不便回去的狀態。重點是這種被迫離開的處境，而不只是地理上的離開。","examples":[{"en":"He lived in exile for many years.","zh":"他在流亡中生活了很多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the coup, the president went into exile.","zh":"政變後，總統流亡國外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-201dc34fbfb60698","term":"exile","forms":["exile","exiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流亡者；被流放的人","explanation":"指被迫離開自己的家鄉或祖國、因此身處流亡狀態的人。這個意義把注意力從“處境”轉到“處於這種處境的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The writer became an exile after criticizing the government.","zh":"這位作家批評政府後成了一名流亡者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exile dreamed of returning to his homeland.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-678b1a5cfe646a53","term":"exile","forms":["exile","exiles","exiling","exiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"流放；放逐","explanation":"指當權者或某個機構強迫某人離開家鄉、祖國或原來的生活地點，使其成為流亡者。這個動詞就是記憶圖景中“把人趕出去”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The king exiled his rival to a distant island.","zh":"國王把他的對手流放到一個遙遠的島上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The regime exiled many of its critics.","zh":"這個政權流放了許多批評者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d68838bddc6082b8d3d","word":"exist","forms":["exist"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e6e949390ca358f","term":"exist","forms":["exist","exists","existing","existed","existest","existedst","existeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"存在；真實存在","explanation":"表示某人、某物或某種抽象情況確實存在於現實中，而不是隻存在於想象或說法裡。","examples":[{"en":"Small differences exist between the two versions.","zh":"這兩個版本之間存在一些小差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A real solution may exist, but we have not found it yet.","zh":"可能確實存在一個解決辦法，只是我們還沒有找到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22669e38dc308a78af3e","word":"existence","forms":["existence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-415ad4bf290dc9d3","term":"existence","forms":["existence","existences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"存在；存在狀態","explanation":"表示某人、某物或某事確實存在，或表示“存在”這一狀態本身。它可以用於事實、問題、威脅等抽象事物，強調它們不是空想，而是在某種意義上真實存在。","examples":[{"en":"The report confirms the existence of a serious problem.","zh":"這份報告證實了一個嚴重問題的存在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people still doubt the existence of life on other planets.","zh":"許多人仍然懷疑其他行星上是否存在生命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/existence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1e75d849541c1ac","term":"existence","forms":["existence","existences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現實；物質世界","explanation":"在哲學或較抽象的討論中，existence 可以指實際存在的整體，也就是與思想、幻想相對的現實世界。這裡的重點不是某一個東西“有沒有”，而是“現實本身是什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"The novel explores the meaning of human existence.","zh":"這部小說探討了人類存在的意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The philosopher distinguished imagination from material existence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/existence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e596899f114b51624023","word":"exit","forms":["exit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f1c687cbdcc5c50","term":"exit","forms":["exit","exits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"離開；退場","explanation":"指從某處或某種情境中離開的動作，重點是“走出去”這一行為，而不是離開的具體通道。","examples":[{"en":"She made a quiet exit before the meeting ended.","zh":"會議結束前，她悄悄離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor made his exit as the lights went down.","zh":"燈光暗下時，那名演員退場了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53e9d36b452ab88c","term":"exit","forms":["exit","exits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出口","explanation":"指可以從建築物、道路或其他空間出去的通道或門，是“走出去”這一核心概念的具體地點。","examples":[{"en":"The nearest exit is at the end of the hallway.","zh":"最近的出口在走廊盡頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take the second exit at the roundabout.","zh":"在環島駛出第二個出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31f7918225e1c77e","term":"exit","forms":["exit","exits","exiting","exited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離開；出去","explanation":"指人從某處或某種情境中走出去，是“從裡面到外面”這一核心動作的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please exit the building through the rear door.","zh":"請從後門離開這棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He exited quietly when the discussion became heated.","zh":"討論變得激烈時，他悄悄離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4d6cb99915dfaa46ca7","word":"exotic","forms":["exotic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1519eb666e980bf9","term":"exotic","forms":["exotic","more exotic","most exotic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"異國的；異域風情的","explanation":"指來自外國或陌生環境的事物，因不同於本地常見事物而顯得新奇、特別，常帶有吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"The market sells exotic fruits from Southeast Asia.","zh":"這個市場出售來自東南亞的異國水果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her exotic appearance attracted everyone's attention.","zh":"她的異域外貌吸引了所有人的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exotic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a61586aa4bbf3e41","term":"exotic","forms":["exotic","exotics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外來者；外來生物","explanation":"指對某個環境來說來自外部的生物或人，也就是不屬於當地常見群體的物件；核心仍是“從外面來到這裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The reserve is home to several exotics that were brought in from overseas.","zh":"這片保護區裡有幾種從海外引入的外來生物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener removed invasive exotics from the reserve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exotic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d78de925a87867319201","word":"expand","forms":["expand"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdb7ca47efc282d5","term":"expand","forms":["expand","expands","expanding","expanded","expandest","expandedst","expandeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"展開；使變大","explanation":"把原本收攏、壓縮或較小的東西向外攤開，使它佔據更大的空間或呈現更大的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"You can expand this compact umbrella to cover a large table.","zh":"你可以把這把摺疊傘展開，讓它遮住一張大桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Expand the folded frame before attaching the fabric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aec9ea87e97e70d9","term":"expand","forms":["expand","expands","expanding","expanded","expandest","expandedst","expandeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變大；膨脹","explanation":"自身從較小、收攏的狀態變成更大的形狀、體積或數量，常常不需要外力直接使它改變。","examples":[{"en":"Many materials expand when heated.","zh":"許多材料受熱時會膨脹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The balloon expanded until it pressed against the ceiling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-167f448f11f389abcfaa","word":"expansion","forms":["expansion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49c0e5ab0a2d4b6e","term":"expansion","forms":["expansion","expansions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擴大；擴張；膨脹","explanation":"指規模、數量、範圍或體積向外變大，重點是“變大”這一過程，也可以指這種變化本身。","examples":[{"en":"The expansion of the city has put pressure on local roads.","zh":"城市的擴張給當地道路帶來了壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heat causes the expansion of most materials.","zh":"熱量會導致大多數材料膨脹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expansion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19987cbd32c0053a","term":"expansion","forms":["expansion","expansions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擴建部分；擴建工程","explanation":"指在原有建築物旁邊或其基礎上增加出來的建築空間，也可以指這項擴建工程。","examples":[{"en":"The library's new expansion includes three study rooms.","zh":"圖書館新擴建的部分包括三個自習室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new expansion houses the children's ward.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expansion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77f2f036726eaa17f75c","word":"expect","forms":["expect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a4da528ed7e0ca9","term":"expect","forms":["expect","expects","expecting","expected","expectest","expectedst","expecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預料；預計","explanation":"指根據已有資訊或通常情況，認為某事將會發生。它像站在門口向外看，心裡已經把將來的情況放在眼前，但不表示事情一定會發生。","examples":[{"en":"We expect the train to arrive on time.","zh":"我們預計火車會準時到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Call me when you least expect it.","zh":"在你最意想不到的時候給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e453c74e68ddfb32","term":"expect","forms":["expect","expects","expecting","expected","expectest","expectedst","expecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"要求；認為有義務","explanation":"指某個規則、機構或有權力的人認為某人必須做某事。這裡不是預測未來，而是把某種行為看作應盡的責任。","examples":[{"en":"The school expects every student to wear a uniform.","zh":"學校要求每名學生都穿校服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I expect you to honor your commitments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40d1f6b8dd815d77515f","word":"expectation","forms":["expectation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f54ccdae4157080","term":"expectation","forms":["expectation","expectations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預期；期待","explanation":"指等待某件事發生時的心理狀態，重點在“認為它將要發生”或“盼著它發生”這一過程，而不一定表示結果已經確定。","examples":[{"en":"The crowd waited in expectation of the singer's arrival.","zh":"人群滿懷期待地等待歌手到來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She opened the letter with the expectation that it would bring good news.","zh":"她開啟信，預期裡面會帶來好訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expectation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5926597c36cfa013","term":"expectation","forms":["expectation","expectations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預期的事；期待的結果","explanation":"指人所預料或期待會出現的具體事情、結果或表現；這裡的重點從“等待的心理”轉向“心裡等著的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The new restaurant did not live up to our expectations.","zh":"這家新餐館沒有達到我們的預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His expectations of the job were higher than the reality.","zh":"他對這份工作的預期高於實際情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expectation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-232303b2a70c9b71cbb3","word":"expedition","forms":["expedition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da8f6dc086be00d6","term":"expedition","forms":["expedition","expeditions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍事遠征","explanation":"指軍隊為攻擊、佔領或執行軍事任務而進行的行動，尤其是進入敵方領地的遠征。這是 expedition 最典型的歷史和軍事用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The army launched an expedition against the rebels.","zh":"軍隊對叛軍發起了一次遠征。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The naval expedition returned without capturing the enemy port.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expedition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ee99140bcec6aff","term":"expedition","forms":["expedition","expeditions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有明確目的的遠行","explanation":"指個人或團體為特定目的進行的旅行，常包括探險、科學考察、搜救或海上行動。它不是隨意遊玩，而是“帶著任務出發”的遠行。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists went on an expedition to study the rainforest.","zh":"科學家們進行了一次考察雨林的遠征。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined an expedition to find the lost temple.","zh":"她參加了一次尋找失落神廟的探險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expedition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":3,"counts":{"113":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-e7d78e39e8ccc66caf71","word":"expenditure","forms":["expenditure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-282f53a10264c6a0","term":"expenditure","forms":["expenditure","expenditures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支出行為；花費","explanation":"指把金錢、時間或其他資源花出去這一行為，重點在“正在付出或消耗資源”這個過程，而不只是最後的數字。","examples":[{"en":"The expenditure of time and effort was necessary to complete the research.","zh":"完成這項研究必須投入時間和精力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project required a large expenditure of public resources.","zh":"這個專案需要大量投入公共資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expenditure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-734b76157f9310e6","term":"expenditure","forms":["expenditure","expenditures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支出額；花費的金額","explanation":"指已經花掉或計劃花掉的資源數量，尤其是錢；這裡的重點從“花費的過程”轉向“花了多少”。","examples":[{"en":"The city plans to reduce its annual expenditure on public transport.","zh":"這座城市計劃減少公共交通的年度支出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Annual expenditure on heating has doubled.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expenditure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23b18e504dd45960690a","word":"expense","forms":["expense"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74cb01c1ab80fc05","term":"expense","forms":["expense","expenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開支；花費","explanation":"指為了購買、完成或維持某件事而付出的錢，也可以泛指這種花費本身。它既能指一筆具體費用，也能指為某個目標投入的大量金錢。","examples":[{"en":"They went to considerable expense to repair the old house.","zh":"他們花了很大一筆錢修繕那棟老房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company will cover my travel expenses.","zh":"公司會承擔我的差旅費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9d863961f1999ca","term":"expense","forms":["expense","expenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代價；以……為代價","explanation":"表示為了得到某種結果，消耗、犧牲或損害了另一方。這裡付出的不一定是錢，也可以是機會、利益、健康或他人的處境。","examples":[{"en":"The team won the match at the expense of several key players' health.","zh":"這支隊伍贏了比賽，卻犧牲了幾名主力隊員的健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He advanced his career at his family's expense.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3cca575ff7e90bd5ef3","word":"expensive","forms":["expensive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-566eeb22f4bb4700","term":"expensive","forms":["expensive","more expensive","most expensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"昂貴的；價格高的","explanation":"表示購買、使用或完成某件事需要花很多錢，因此價格或總成本很高。這是 expensive 最常見、最需要優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"That restaurant is too expensive for us.","zh":"那家餐廳對我們來說太貴了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is expensive to repair an old car.","zh":"修理一輛舊車花費很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-901048bb148f9e36","term":"expensive","forms":["expensive","more expensive","most expensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"耗費大量時間或資源的","explanation":"表示某種演算法、操作或方案雖然不一定花很多錢，但會佔用大量計算時間、記憶體、能源等系統資源，因此代價高。","examples":[{"en":"This method is accurate, but it is expensive in terms of memory.","zh":"這種方法很準確，但佔用的記憶體資源很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Searching every possible combination is computationally expensive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-53e5e7c5a884893739c4","word":"experience","forms":["experience"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2791876944f2bf9","term":"experience","forms":["experience","experiences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親身經歷；體驗","explanation":"指親自遇到、參與或感受到的事情，以及這件事帶來的直接感受。它既可以指一次具體而難忘的經歷，也可以泛指個人親身接觸過的生活體驗。","examples":[{"en":"Moving to a new country was a challenging experience for her.","zh":"搬到一個新國家對她來說是一次很有挑戰的經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trip gave me my first experience of working with children.","zh":"這次旅行讓我第一次親身體驗了和孩子們一起工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84f861b33a22a831","term":"experience","forms":["experience","experiences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經驗；經歷積累","explanation":"指一個人或團體透過長期參與各種事情而積累的知識、判斷力和實際技能，尤其常用於工作或專業領域。","examples":[{"en":"She has five years of experience in software design.","zh":"她有五年的軟體設計經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of experience taught her to recognize faulty stitching.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0471ee5c564cca40","term":"experience","forms":["experience","experiences","experiencing","experienced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經歷；體驗；遭遇","explanation":"指親自觀察、感受或參與某個事件、過程或行動，並因此受到影響或獲得認識。它既可用於主動體驗，也可用於被動遭遇某種變化或困難。","examples":[{"en":"Many families experienced serious difficulties during the flood.","zh":"洪水期間，許多家庭遭遇了嚴重困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students can experience different ways of learning through the project.","zh":"學生可以透過這個專案體驗不同的學習方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a530c507fd893f520b97","word":"experiment","forms":["experiment"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2755c653072013d3","term":"experiment","forms":["experiment","experiments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實驗；試驗","explanation":"指在較受控的條件下進行測試，用來驗證一個想法、假設，或判斷某種方法是否有效。它強調有目的地試驗並觀察結果，而不是一般性的經歷。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists conducted an experiment to test the new drug.","zh":"科學家進行了一項實驗來測試這種新藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our first experiment failed, but we learned something useful.","zh":"我們的第一次實驗失敗了，但我們學到了有用的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experiment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6eca036095c4bc3","term":"experiment","forms":["experiment","experiments","experimenting","experimented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做實驗；進行試驗","explanation":"指親自進行實驗或測試，透過觀察結果來判斷某個想法或方法是否可行。這個動詞把“嘗試—觀察—判斷”的過程集中在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The team is experimenting with a cheaper way to make the product.","zh":"團隊正在嘗試一種更便宜的產品製造方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She likes to experiment with different recipes.","zh":"她喜歡嘗試不同的食譜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experiment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-748be63c87c9fad252fb","word":"experimental","forms":["experimental"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86c445f7e68477d1","term":"experimental","forms":["experimental","more experimental","most experimental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"實驗的；以實驗為基礎的","explanation":"指某種知識、方法或學科建立在觀察和實驗的結果上，而不是隻靠理論推測。它強調“用實驗來驗證或形成”。","examples":[{"en":"Chemistry is an experimental science.","zh":"化學是一門實驗科學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The claim lacks experimental evidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experimental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e36147864ea15ad2","term":"experimental","forms":["experimental","more experimental","most experimental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"試驗性的；探索新路的","explanation":"指作品、團隊或方法故意嘗試不同於傳統的做法，處在探索和試驗階段。這裡的“實驗”從科學實驗延伸到了創作和實踐。","examples":[{"en":"The band is known for its experimental sound.","zh":"這支樂隊以其探索性的聲音風格而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The troupe is known for experimental approaches to theater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experimental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7d253870ab8de3825e3","word":"expert","forms":["expert"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9fde1862271fb781","term":"expert","forms":["expert","more expert","most expert"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熟練而專業的","explanation":"表示某人在某方面能力特別強，或者某種做法顯示出很高的專業水平。它強調知識、訓練和實踐結合後的熟練程度，而不只是一般的“會做”。","examples":[{"en":"She is expert at repairing old cameras.","zh":"她很擅長修理老相機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need expert advice before changing the design.","zh":"在修改設計前，我們需要專業建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39b251c2fced412a","term":"expert","forms":["expert","experts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專家","explanation":"指在某一學科、職業或技能方面擁有廣泛知識和較強實踐能力的人。這個詞強調長期學習和經驗積累，而不只是某一次表現很好。","examples":[{"en":"They asked an expert in child development to review the study.","zh":"他們請一位兒童發展專家審閱這項研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you are unsure, consult an expert.","zh":"如果你不確定，就諮詢專家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b3bcb2b7d1d97cec0bf","word":"expertise","forms":["expertise"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f2232b8b2fb0910","term":"expertise","forms":["expertise","expertises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專業知識和能力","explanation":"指人在某一特定領域中積累的深入知識、技能和判斷能力，也就是專家工具箱裡的內容。它可以來自職業，也可以來自長期鑽研某種興趣。","examples":[{"en":"She has considerable expertise in repairing old cameras.","zh":"她在修理老式相機方面有很豐富的專業知識和經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need someone with expertise in data security.","zh":"我們需要一位具備資料安全專業能力的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expertise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd20c653820e498d","term":"expertise","forms":["expertise","expertises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專家意見或建議","explanation":"指專家把自己的專業能力用於某個具體問題後給出的判斷、建議或專業支援；重點不在專家這個人，而在他提供出來的意見。","examples":[{"en":"The committee called on her expertise before making the decision.","zh":"委員會在作出決定前徵求了她的專業意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sought legal expertise before signing the lease.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expertise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2eea88ac2baa11e3a746","word":"expiration","forms":["expiration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6047f83144ee0275","term":"expiration","forms":["expiration","expirations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"呼氣","explanation":"指把空氣從肺部撥出的過程，核心畫面就是氣息向外排出。","examples":[{"en":"The device measures airflow during expiration.","zh":"這臺裝置測量呼氣時的氣流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Slow expiration can help relax the body.","zh":"緩慢呼氣有助於放鬆身體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expiration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10a34aaf2a7af76d","term":"expiration","forms":["expiration","expirations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"期限屆滿；到期","explanation":"指某項有效期、合同期限或許可期限走到盡頭，因而不再有效；這是“時間走到盡頭”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please renew your passport before its expiration.","zh":"請在護照到期前續辦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the expiration date before using the medicine.","zh":"使用藥物前請檢視有效期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expiration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2dae5aed5b773b62caa","word":"expire","forms":["expire"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d88e15c0de0bf86f","term":"expire","forms":["expire","expires","expiring","expired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到期；失效","explanation":"指證件、合同、優惠券、密碼或有效期等走到規定的終點，因而不再有效。這裡不是“東西壞了”，而是“使用許可到期了”。","examples":[{"en":"My passport expires in six months.","zh":"我的護照六個月後到期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This discount code has expired.","zh":"這個折扣碼已經失效了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0818ab2593f5cb6c2daa","word":"explain","forms":["explain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-010857692a3ca728","term":"explain","forms":["explain","explains","explaining","explained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解釋；說明","explanation":"把一件事的內容、意義或經過講清楚，讓原本不明白的人能夠理解。重點是消除疑惑、使事情變得清楚。","examples":[{"en":"Could you explain this rule to me?","zh":"你能給我解釋一下這條規則嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide explained how the machine worked.","zh":"導遊說明了這臺機器是怎樣工作的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efe4c1cc2e98fcd0","term":"explain","forms":["explain","explains","explaining","explained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解釋原因；說明緣由","explanation":"說明某件事為什麼發生，或某人的行為、結果是由什麼原因造成的。這裡不是單純介紹內容，而是把背後的原因講清楚。","examples":[{"en":"Can you explain why the meeting was canceled?","zh":"你能解釋一下會議為什麼取消嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This result may explain her decision.","zh":"這個結果或許能說明她為什麼這樣決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f78fcae67d4aa99819ff","word":"explanation","forms":["explanation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c451043113fc3e9","term":"explanation","forms":["explanation","explanations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解釋這一行為或過程","explanation":"指把複雜、陌生或不清楚的事情講清楚的行為或過程，重點在“解釋”本身，而不一定強調最後得到的答案。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a clear explanation of how the machine works.","zh":"她清楚地解釋了這臺機器是怎樣工作的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The explanation was so long that everyone lost track of the main point.","zh":"這個解釋太長了，大家都忘了重點是什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explanation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-567a9549951725c4","term":"explanation","forms":["explanation","explanations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解釋、說明或理由","explanation":"指能夠說明某件事、讓人理解它的內容，也可以指事情發生的原因或理由；這裡重點是“解釋出來的東西”，而不是解釋的動作。","examples":[{"en":"We still have no explanation for the sudden change in the weather.","zh":"我們仍然無法解釋天氣為什麼突然變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her explanation accounted for every missing receipt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explanation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b283e93debf035e990d","word":"explicit","forms":["explicit"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5450dbd789be9fc","term":"explicit","forms":["explicit","more explicit","most explicit"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明確具體的","explanation":"指把意思、要求或細節直接說清楚，不需要聽者自己猜測；這是 explicit 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gave us explicit instructions about how to submit the assignment.","zh":"老師明確告訴我們該怎樣提交作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contract is explicit about who is responsible for repairs.","zh":"合同明確說明了由誰負責維修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explicit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92d488600e5c1b87","term":"explicit","forms":["explicit","more explicit","most explicit"],"pos":"adj","zh":"露骨直白的","explanation":"指表達得非常直接，直白到包含可能令人不適或被認為冒犯的性、暴力或粗俗內容；這是“毫不遮掩地說出來”從一般明確義發展出的語境義。","examples":[{"en":"The album carries a warning because some of the lyrics are explicit.","zh":"這張專輯帶有提示，因為其中一些歌詞內容很露骨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film contains explicit scenes unsuitable for children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explicit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fecb036594866077d7f3","word":"explode","forms":["explode"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bcba5562f929ec60","term":"explode","forms":["explode","explodes","exploding","exploded","explodest","explodedst","explodeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"炸燬","explanation":"指用爆炸摧毀某個物體，重點是讓目標被爆炸力量破壞。","examples":[{"en":"The attackers exploded the bridge at midnight.","zh":"襲擊者在午夜炸燬了那座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bomb exploded the locked gate.","zh":"炸彈炸燬了那扇上鎖的大門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a2f14cbe60024af","term":"explode","forms":["explode","explodes","exploding","exploded","explodest","explodedst","explodeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"爆炸","explanation":"指炸彈、氣體或其他物體突然猛烈地向四周釋放力量，發生爆炸、爆裂或引爆。","examples":[{"en":"The fireworks exploded above the stadium.","zh":"煙花在體育場上空爆炸開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone ran when the gas tank began to explode.","zh":"煤氣罐開始爆炸時，所有人都跑開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75143bb6875f2b9b","term":"explode","forms":["explode","explodes","exploding","exploded","explodest","explodedst","explodeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"情緒爆發","explanation":"指一個人積累的強烈情緒突然衝出來，尤其是突然發怒並激烈表達出來。","examples":[{"en":"She exploded when her brother broke the lamp.","zh":"她弟弟打壞檯燈時，她一下子大發雷霆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He exploded at the unfair accusation.","zh":"面對這項不公平的指責，他突然勃然大怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04da09655d48e4920ce5","word":"exploit","forms":["exploit"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0155404fd0fa53e","term":"exploit","forms":["exploit","exploits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漏洞利用程式","explanation":"指利用其他軟體安全漏洞的程式、程式碼或技術，使攻擊者能夠進入系統、執行操作或取得不應有的許可權；這裡的“利用”是技術上的利用，不是普通的軟體工具。","examples":[{"en":"The company released a patch after researchers found a serious browser exploit.","zh":"研究人員發現一個嚴重的瀏覽器漏洞利用程式後，公司釋出了補丁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Attackers used an exploit to gain access to the server.","zh":"攻擊者利用一個漏洞利用程式進入了伺服器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exploit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d4b1255d4c3ad88","term":"exploit","forms":["exploit","exploits","exploiting","exploited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"利用資源或機會","explanation":"指充分利用某種資源、條件、機會或技術，使自己、他人或社會得到好處；這個義項本身不一定帶有負面色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to exploit solar energy without damaging the environment.","zh":"這個專案旨在利用太陽能，同時不破壞環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She exploited the opportunity to learn from an experienced engineer.","zh":"她利用這個機會向一位經驗豐富的工程師學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exploit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a7b0e67aaa00ba3","term":"exploit","forms":["exploit","exploits","exploiting","exploited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剝削；佔便宜","explanation":"指利用他人的勞動、弱勢處境、身體或財產來為自己謀利，通常暗含不公平和道德上的批評；這是中文“剝削”最接近的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company was accused of exploiting temporary workers.","zh":"這家公司被指控剝削臨時工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He exploited her trust to take her money.","zh":"他利用她的信任騙走了她的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exploit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c6f6840875e87c7ce76","word":"exploration","forms":["exploration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f9b9d5071cd6bb5","term":"exploration","forms":["exploration","explorations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"探索；考察","explanation":"指為了瞭解某個地方、領域或問題而進行的探索過程，重點是主動查探未知內容。它可以是實地行動，也可以是對思想、可能性或新領域的深入研究。","examples":[{"en":"The book is an exploration of how people adapt to life in extreme climates.","zh":"這本書探討了人們如何適應極端氣候下的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her exploration of local traditions changed the way she understood the town.","zh":"她對當地傳統的探索改變了她理解這座城鎮的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exploration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1edd58f58aefcb7","term":"exploration","forms":["exploration","explorations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地理探索；探測未知區域","explanation":"特指進入、穿越或考察尚未充分了解的地區，以發現新的地理資訊。它是“探索”這一核心概念在地圖和未知地域上的具體延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The exploration of the polar region required careful planning and specialized equipment.","zh":"對極地地區的探索需要周密的計劃和專門的裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Space exploration has given scientists new ways to study Earth.","zh":"太空探索為科學家研究地球提供了新的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exploration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":4,"counts":{"112":2,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-6f281157ab246f0e1f35","word":"explore","forms":["explore"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8fb66d266e62268a","term":"explore","forms":["explore","explores","exploring","explored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"系統調查；深入研究","explanation":"把未知的問題、方案或可能性逐步查清楚，就像把一個尚未看清的地方仔細走遍一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The team is exploring several ways to reduce travel costs.","zh":"團隊正在研究幾種降低出行成本的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let's explore whether a later meeting would work better.","zh":"我們來研究一下把會議推遲是否會更合適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32a8c0db758e2550","term":"explore","forms":["explore","explores","exploring","explored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到某處探索","explanation":"親自前往陌生或不熟悉的地方，透過走訪和觀察發現那裡有什麼；這裡的“查詢”變成了實際的空間探索。","examples":[{"en":"They spent the afternoon exploring the narrow streets of the village.","zh":"他們整個下午都在探索村子裡狹窄的街道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers explored the island before choosing a campsite.","zh":"研究人員在選定營地前考察了這座島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e33d57d8955b3138a0c","word":"explosion","forms":["explosion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-619d6ac3ffb00008","term":"explosion","forms":["explosion","explosions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爆炸","explanation":"指化學、機械或核能等在很短時間內猛烈釋放，造成爆裂、衝擊或破壞的事件；也可指發生這樣一次爆炸。","examples":[{"en":"The explosion damaged several nearby buildings.","zh":"爆炸損壞了附近的幾棟建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police are investigating an explosion at the factory.","zh":"警方正在調查工廠發生的一起爆炸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explosion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e4891467a37f5bd","term":"explosion","forms":["explosion","explosions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突然激增；大量湧現","explanation":"從“能量向外猛烈釋放”引申而來，指人口、物種、資訊、興趣等在短時間內快速而大規模地增加、擴張或湧現。","examples":[{"en":"The city has seen an explosion of new restaurants.","zh":"這座城市新開了大量餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discovery triggered an explosion of related research.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explosion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33a5c8e80138e5f89435","word":"explosive","forms":["explosive"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b65a8d3dd425bffd","term":"explosive","forms":["explosive","more explosive","most explosive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"會爆炸的；易爆的","explanation":"指物體或物質能夠爆炸，或很可能爆炸，核心畫面是裡面積聚的能量突然釋放。","examples":[{"en":"The workers found an explosive device near the railway.","zh":"工人在鐵路附近發現了一個爆炸裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the explosive materials away from heat.","zh":"要把易爆材料遠離熱源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explosive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ec8ad50604913a6","term":"explosive","forms":["explosive","more explosive","most explosive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"爆炸般猛烈的","explanation":"形容火、聲音或其他現象呈現出爆炸那樣突然而猛烈的特點，重點不一定是它真的會爆炸。","examples":[{"en":"An explosive fire spread through the old warehouse.","zh":"一場猛烈的火災蔓延過了那座舊倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The explosive growth of algae depleted the lake's oxygen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explosive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d46aee08cc49f6d1eb41","word":"export","forms":["export"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a40520f575d022b","term":"export","forms":["export","exports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出口商品","explanation":"指從本國或本地運到國外出售的商品；它是“被帶到外面”的具體東西。","examples":[{"en":"Coffee is one of the region's main exports.","zh":"咖啡是這個地區的主要出口商品之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Falling demand for steel hurt the country's exports.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/export","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d215ee17a043c67","term":"export","forms":["export","exports","exporting","exported"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出口；銷往國外","explanation":"指把商品從本國或本地運到外國出售，是“把商品向外帶”的最常用動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company exports tea to several European countries.","zh":"這家公司把茶葉出口到幾個歐洲國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local farmers export their fruit around the world.","zh":"當地農民把他們的水果出口到世界各地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/export","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3b96e66bb86f3750f42","word":"expose","forms":["expose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ca6a0d6f03243b61","term":"expose","forms":["expose","exposes","exposing","exposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭露；使顯現","explanation":"把原本隱藏、未被注意或被掩蓋的事實、問題、秘密等呈現出來，讓別人看見或知道。常常帶有揭穿不實、腐敗或錯誤行為的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation exposed serious problems in the company.","zh":"這項調查揭露了這家公司存在的嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report exposed his claim as a lie.","zh":"這份報告揭穿了他的說法是謊言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1dda6dcd6c141ff6","term":"expose","forms":["expose","exposes","exposing","exposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使接觸；使暴露於","explanation":"有意或無意地讓人或物接觸某種物質、環境或壓力，以觀察反應、測試抵抗力，或說明其可能受到影響。常見物件包括過敏原、化學物質、危險環境和壓力。","examples":[{"en":"The test exposed the material to extreme heat.","zh":"這項測試讓這種材料經受了高溫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not expose the film to direct sunlight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b40356e6d1c6948bcb05","word":"exposure","forms":["exposure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54ba09b2d66a2843","term":"exposure","forms":["exposure","exposures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴露；無遮蔽狀態","explanation":"指人或物沒有遮擋或保護，直接面對外界的人、物質或影響；也可指這種狀態本身。這是 exposure 從“開啟給外界看或碰到”發展出的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"Workers should wear gloves to reduce their exposure to harmful chemicals.","zh":"工人應該戴手套，以減少接觸有害化學品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Long exposure to loud music can damage your hearing.","zh":"長時間暴露在高音量音樂中可能損害聽力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exposure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8d7bf910e75e61d","term":"exposure","forms":["exposure","exposures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揭露；曝光","explanation":"指把原本隱藏的事實、醜聞或問題公開給別人知道。核心畫面仍是把某物開啟，直接放到公眾面前。","examples":[{"en":"The exposure of the corruption scandal led to several resignations.","zh":"這起腐敗醜聞被揭露後，有幾名官員辭職了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporter's investigation resulted in a shocking exposure of the company's practices.","zh":"記者的調查揭露了這家公司令人震驚的做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exposure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9456d2b55c74b2b","term":"exposure","forms":["exposure","exposures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次攝影曝光","explanation":"在攝影中，指感光材料或相機感測器接受一次光線的過程，也可指由此拍出的一張照片或一次拍攝。這是“開啟感光面讓光進入”這一核心畫面的直接應用。","examples":[{"en":"The photographer took several exposures of the moon.","zh":"攝影師拍了幾張月亮的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A long exposure captured the lights of the moving cars.","zh":"長時間曝光拍下了行駛中汽車的燈光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exposure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-008231aaf99956982ffb","word":"express","forms":["express"],"officialPos":"v./adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-874c86809bea7e9b","term":"express","forms":["express","more express","most express"],"pos":"adj","zh":"快速直達的","explanation":"指車輛或交通服務行駛很快，通常因為沿途不停或少停，直接到達目的地。","examples":[{"en":"We took the express train and arrived before noon.","zh":"我們坐了快車，中午前就到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An express elevator carries visitors to the observation deck.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94b66f52c102fab7","term":"express","forms":["express","more express","most express"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明確的；明說的","explanation":"指某個意思、要求或許可被直接說出來，而不是讓人根據暗示自己推斷。","examples":[{"en":"The manager gave us express instructions to lock the door.","zh":"經理明確吩咐我們要鎖門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not enter without the owner's express permission.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7aeb18c913711e2a","term":"express","forms":["express"],"pos":"adv","zh":"乘快車；直達地","explanation":"表示列車或其他交通工具以快車方式行駛，通常不在所有站點停留。","examples":[{"en":"This train runs express to the airport.","zh":"這趟列車直達機場，中途少停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Send the package express so it arrives tomorrow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26a2ec78af1a9623","term":"express","forms":["express","expresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"快車","explanation":"指快速或直達的交通工具，最常見的是途中跳過一些車站的列車。","examples":[{"en":"I took the express into the city.","zh":"我坐快車進了城。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We caught the morning express to Edinburgh.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-592035edaa281fe8","term":"express","forms":["express","expresses","expressing","expressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表達；傳達","explanation":"指把思想、感情、意見等從心裡或頭腦中明確傳達出來，讓別人知道。","examples":[{"en":"She found it difficult to express her feelings.","zh":"她覺得很難表達自己的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Words cannot express how grateful I am.","zh":"言語無法表達我有多麼感激。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8bc0e4f01a0ebdbfe99","word":"expression","forms":["expression"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1491965af7ef9353","term":"expression","forms":["expression","expressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表達；表現","explanation":"指把思想、意見、感情或身份顯現出來的行為或結果，重點是“讓內在的東西被別人看見或聽見”。","examples":[{"en":"Her music is a powerful expression of grief.","zh":"她的音樂有力地表達了悲傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clothing can be an expression of personal identity.","zh":"服裝可以是個人身份的一種表達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e520a5728890a12a","term":"expression","forms":["expression","expressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"措辭；表達方式","explanation":"指用語言說出或寫出一個意思的具體說法，也就是“這個意思是怎樣被措辭表達出來的”。","examples":[{"en":"Is there a more polite expression for this idea?","zh":"這個意思有沒有更禮貌的說法？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That expression sounds old-fashioned now.","zh":"那個說法現在聽起來過時了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1bb74d5d86e87401","term":"expression","forms":["expression","expressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表情；神情","explanation":"指臉上顯露出的、通常能讓人聯想到某種情緒的樣子，是感情從內在“顯現”到臉上的結果。","examples":[{"en":"A worried expression appeared on his face.","zh":"他臉上露出了擔憂的神情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me an expression of surprise.","zh":"她露出了驚訝的表情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-339f68b4394a8503f177","word":"expressive","forms":["expressive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce43f4cdbae4056b","term":"expressive","forms":["expressive","more expressive","most expressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富有表現力的","explanation":"指某種動作、藝術形式、聲音或文字能有效地把思想或感情表現出來，讓別人清楚感受到其中的內容。","examples":[{"en":"Her expressive eyes showed that she was worried.","zh":"她富有表現力的眼睛流露出擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancer used expressive movements to tell the story.","zh":"舞者用富有表現力的動作講述這個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85643c29c36df64b","term":"expressive","forms":["expressive","more expressive","most expressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能傳達說話人的感情或態度的","explanation":"指語言或表達方式除了傳達字面資訊，還讓人聽出說話人的情緒、立場或態度；這裡的 expressive 關注“話是以什麼態度說出來的”。","examples":[{"en":"Her expressive language made her excitement clear.","zh":"她富有表現力的語言清楚地傳達了她的興奮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her expressive sigh revealed exactly how she felt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf0bb4ee60e2cd5a1a52","word":"extend","forms":["extend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-077d11fc2d0199e2","term":"extend","forms":["extend","extends","extending","extended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"延伸；擴大","explanation":"某物自身向外變長、變大或覆蓋得更廣，重點是變化自然發生，而不是誰主動把它拉長。","examples":[{"en":"The road extends beyond the village.","zh":"這條路一直延伸到村外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their farm extends to the edge of the woods.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e97f4075a870692","term":"extend","forms":["extend","extends","extending","extended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"延伸至；佔據","explanation":"強調某個地方、區域或物體實際覆蓋了一段空間，常用於說明它延伸了多遠。","examples":[{"en":"The beach extends for several miles.","zh":"這片海灘綿延數英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vineyard extends from the road to the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f5bbb9757479f2d","term":"extend","forms":["extend","extends","extending","extended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擴大；擴充套件","explanation":"某人或某事物把已有的範圍、長度或影響力向外擴大，是“向外伸展”這一核心動作的主動形式。","examples":[{"en":"The company plans to extend the railway to the airport.","zh":"這家公司計劃把鐵路延伸到機場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hope to extend the service to more villages.","zh":"我們希望把這項服務擴充套件到更多村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c498af0c53115235","term":"extend","forms":["extend","extends","extending","extended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"延長時間","explanation":"把一段已經存在的時間向後拉長，使期限、合同、假期或活動持續更久。","examples":[{"en":"The library has extended its opening hours.","zh":"圖書館延長了開放時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can we extend the deadline by two days?","zh":"我們能把截止日期延後兩天嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26f1de33979d065ba8d8","word":"extension","forms":["extension"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34e5b12da4d856a8","term":"extension","forms":["extension","extensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"延伸；擴大；延長","explanation":"指把某物向外拉長、擴大，或把持續時間延長；也可指這一變化本身。建築、空間、範圍和時間都能使用這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"We asked for an extension of the deadline.","zh":"我們申請延長截止期限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The extension of the road will reduce traffic in the village.","zh":"道路的延伸將減少村裡的交通擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71c39e734a60f320","term":"extension","forms":["extension","extensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築擴建部分","explanation":"指在原有建築旁邊或其基礎上加建出來的部分。它是“向外延伸”在建築中的具體結果。","examples":[{"en":"The family added a kitchen extension to the back of the house.","zh":"這家人在房子後面加建了一個廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They added an extension behind the kitchen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cbd267ae49b3a1b","term":"extension","forms":["extension","extensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擴充套件部分；能力延伸","explanation":"指從某個主體長出來、附加上去，並讓主體擁有更多功能或影響範圍的部分。人、組織、裝置和軟體都可以有這種“延伸”。","examples":[{"en":"The mobile app is a useful extension of the company’s online service.","zh":"這款手機應用是該公司線上服務的一個實用擴充套件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The telescope acts as an extension of human sight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9e9ef157670b0cfd8a42","word":"extensive","forms":["extensive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc6969269fda988b","term":"extensive","forms":["extensive","more extensive","most extensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"範圍廣闊的","explanation":"指覆蓋的空間、地域或範圍非常大，就像一張向四面鋪開的地圖。它既可以描述國家、土地等具體範圍，也可以描述影響所及的廣大區域。","examples":[{"en":"The extensive forest stretches across three countries.","zh":"這片廣闊的森林橫跨三個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program has extensive coverage in rural areas.","zh":"這項計劃在農村地區覆蓋範圍很廣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-425336b74a8071fc","term":"extensive","forms":["extensive","more extensive","most extensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量或程度很大的","explanation":"從“鋪開的範圍很大”引申為某件事涉及的數量、規模或程度很大。它常用於研究、損害、準備、討論等抽象事物，強調廣泛或大量，而不一定強調深入。","examples":[{"en":"She conducted extensive research before writing the report.","zh":"她在寫報告前進行了廣泛的研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report draws on extensive archival research.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b4a5bdd6f71c4a7fad0","word":"extent","forms":["extent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53290872eaced942","term":"extent","forms":["extent","extents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"範圍；數值區間","explanation":"指一組數值、地點或可能性的跨度，也就是某事物從一個端點延伸到另一個端點的範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The survey measured the extent of the damage across the region.","zh":"這項調查測量了該地區受損的範圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map shows the full extent of the floodplain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6bd76601aec1eac3","term":"extent","forms":["extent","extents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"程度；規模","explanation":"指某事物實際延伸到的空間、數量或抽象程度，常表示“達到什麼程度”或“規模有多大”。","examples":[{"en":"I agree with you to some extent, but we need more evidence.","zh":"我在某種程度上同意你的看法，但我們還需要更多證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report revealed the full extent of the problem.","zh":"這份報告揭示了這個問題的全部嚴重程度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a123a777ca1a5b437abf","word":"exterior","forms":["exterior"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8cd2c29a0ed3d1e6","term":"exterior","forms":["exterior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外部的；外表的","explanation":"表示某物在另一個物體的外面，或屬於它朝外的一面，重點是盒子或邊界的“外殼”。","examples":[{"en":"The exterior walls need a fresh coat of paint.","zh":"外牆需要重新刷一層油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exterior of the phone is made of metal.","zh":"這部手機的外殼是金屬製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exterior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97af9519c4a0d9cd","term":"exterior","forms":["exterior","exteriors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外部；外表","explanation":"名詞直接把某物朝外的部分看作一個整體，也就是盒子的外殼或建築的外觀。","examples":[{"en":"We cleaned the exterior of the car before the trip.","zh":"出發前我們清洗了汽車外部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building has a plain exterior but a colorful interior.","zh":"這座建築外表樸素，內部卻色彩鮮豔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exterior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c4623849a49a53911c4","word":"external","forms":["external"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-852d6a04c4f37d1a","term":"external","forms":["external","more external","most external"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外部的；外表的","explanation":"指位於某物外側或外表面的部分，重點是和內部相對的外部位置。","examples":[{"en":"The external walls need to be repaired before winter.","zh":"入冬前需要修繕外牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An external staircase leads to the upper rooms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/external","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a4f669504e16c8d","term":"external","forms":["external","more external","most external"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外部提供的；外來的","explanation":"指力量、幫助、權威或資源不是由當前物件自身產生，而是由外部個人、團體或機構提供。","examples":[{"en":"The project cannot continue without external funding.","zh":"沒有外部資金，這個專案就無法繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The decision was challenged by an external authority.","zh":"這一決定受到了外部機構的質疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/external","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-588f98bd492a5d969985","word":"extinct","forms":["extinct"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7bb8bab3d0c001a5","term":"extinct","forms":["extinct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不再存在的；已廢止的","explanation":"指觀念、習俗、法律、權利、職位或組織等已經不再存在、不再使用或被廢止。它們不像火焰那樣真的燃燒過，但都像被一口氣吹滅後不再發揮作用。","examples":[{"en":"The old custom is now extinct in most towns.","zh":"這種舊習俗如今在大多數城鎮已經不復存在了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ideas that support slavery should be extinct in modern society.","zh":"支援奴隸制的觀念在現代社會應當已經絕跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extinct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-995c8a89968ae1d9","term":"extinct","forms":["extinct"],"pos":"adj","zh":"滅絕的","explanation":"指一個動物或植物物種，或某一類生物，已經全部消失，世上不再有活著的成員。這是現代英語中最重要、最容易遇到的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists believe this bird has been extinct for centuries.","zh":"科學家認為這種鳥已經滅絕了幾個世紀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The species went extinct after its habitat disappeared.","zh":"這種物種的棲息地消失後滅絕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extinct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8dee78f8c7b466c8818","word":"extra","forms":["extra"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ff85711d194b6b4","term":"extra","forms":["extra","more extra","most extra"],"pos":"adj","zh":"額外的；多出來的","explanation":"指超出原本應有、通常需要或已經安排好的數量，因此可以譯為“額外的”“附加的”或“多餘的”。它既能說多做的事，也能說另外支付的費用或多出的物品。","examples":[{"en":"Could you give me an extra day to finish the report?","zh":"你能多給我一天時間完成報告嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We brought extra chairs in case more guests arrived.","zh":"我們多準備了一些椅子，以防有更多客人到來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9334ea97cb14045e","term":"extra","forms":["extra"],"pos":"adv","zh":"格外地；特別地","explanation":"表示某種性質或動作達到比平常更高的程度，也就是在通常程度上“再加一層”。","examples":[{"en":"Please be extra careful near the wet floor.","zh":"靠近溼地板時請格外小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She arrived extra early for the interview.","zh":"她為了面試到得特別早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d2dcb95f5f01d92","term":"extra","forms":["extra","extras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"額外專案；附加費用","explanation":"指在通常內容、課程、服務或價格之外再增加的東西；它是形容詞“額外的”名詞化後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Breakfast is included, but fresh juice costs extra.","zh":"早餐包含在內，但鮮榨果汁要另外收費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel offers several extras, including airport pickup.","zh":"這家酒店提供幾項附加服務，包括機場接送。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1cf2fd5c86895128d55","word":"extract","forms":["extract"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f0376e441973363","term":"extract","forms":["extract","extracts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"取出的東西","explanation":"泛指從某個整體中取出或抽出的東西，是名詞 extract 最寬的基本概念；具體可以是被拔出的物體，也可以是經過處理後得到的成分。","examples":[{"en":"The laboratory tested the extract for harmful chemicals.","zh":"實驗室檢測了這份提取物中是否含有有害化學物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jar contained a concentrated extract of seaweed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b69801c84f99134f","term":"extract","forms":["extract","extracts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書面摘錄","explanation":"指從書籍、文章或檔案中單獨取出並引用的一段文字，重點是它原本屬於較大的文字。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher read an extract from the novel to the class.","zh":"老師給全班朗讀了這部小說的一段摘錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This extract from the report explains the main problem clearly.","zh":"報告中的這段摘錄清楚地解釋了主要問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc3ed7dad4114dea","term":"extract","forms":["extract","extracts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提取物；濃縮液","explanation":"指從植物、食物或其他材料中提取出的、保留其主要味道或功效的製劑，例如香草提取物。","examples":[{"en":"Add a teaspoon of vanilla extract to the cake mixture.","zh":"在蛋糕麵糊中加入一茶匙香草提取物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The perfumer experimented with concentrated lavender extract.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7bc27bd1dda7b05f","term":"extract","forms":["extract","extracts","extracting","extracted","extraught"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拔出；取出","explanation":"指把原本固定在某處的東西用拉、吸或其他力量取出來，核心畫面就是把它從整體中硬生生拉出。","examples":[{"en":"The dentist had to extract the broken tooth.","zh":"牙醫不得不拔掉那顆斷裂的牙齒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor extracted a small piece of glass from her finger.","zh":"醫生從她的手指裡取出了一小片玻璃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff6b0c5ee524d60c","term":"extract","forms":["extract","extracts","extracting","extracted","extraught"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提取成分","explanation":"指透過擠壓、蒸餾或化學、機械處理，把某種材料中的成分取出來；畫面仍是從來源中“拉出”有效部分。","examples":[{"en":"The company extracts oil from the seeds and sells it as a cooking product.","zh":"這家公司從種子中提取油，並把它作為烹飪產品銷售。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The process extracts oil from crushed seeds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f245f700b94c63f0886a","word":"extracurricular","forms":["extracurricular"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6acf371307d7451","term":"extracurricular","forms":["extracurricular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"課外的","explanation":"指不屬於學校正常課程、但通常由學生參加的活動或專案，也就是從正規課程這條“主軌道”延伸出去的部分。","examples":[{"en":"She spends most of her free time on extracurricular activities.","zh":"她大部分空閒時間都用來參加課外活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school offers several extracurricular programs for younger students.","zh":"這所學校為年紀較小的學生提供了幾個課外專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extracurricular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ce1449767372eac10ce","word":"extraordinary","forms":["extraordinary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2671f61ebb0d62e5","term":"extraordinary","forms":["extraordinary","more extraordinary","most extraordinary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非同尋常的；異常的","explanation":"指明顯超出平常情況或通常標準的事物，可以是罕見、異常，也可以只是非常特殊。它強調“不同於一般”，不單純表示數量更多。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team showed extraordinary courage during the storm.","zh":"救援隊在暴風雨中表現出了非同尋常的勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum is closed today because of extraordinary circumstances.","zh":"博物館今天因特殊情況閉館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extraordinary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d0f6f09e71c5923","term":"extraordinary","forms":["extraordinary","more extraordinary","most extraordinary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別出色的","explanation":"指好得遠遠超過一般水平，常用於稱讚人的才華、作品、成就或表現。這裡的“超出常規”具體體現為優秀、卓越。","examples":[{"en":"She is an extraordinary teacher who inspires every student.","zh":"她是一位特別出色的老師，能激勵每一名學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young cellist gave an extraordinary performance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extraordinary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-3393b41eeeea1c11dc97","word":"extreme","forms":["extreme"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-714c896ae19a37e4","term":"extreme","forms":["extreme","extremer","more extreme","extremest","most extreme"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最邊緣的","explanation":"指位置在一組範圍的最遠處、最外側，例如一塊區域的邊緣。","examples":[{"en":"A small cabin stood at the extreme edge of the forest.","zh":"一間小木屋坐落在森林的最邊緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lighthouse stands at the island's extreme northern tip.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extreme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a25168ed9103f89d","term":"extreme","forms":["extreme","extremer","more extreme","extremest","most extreme"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極度的","explanation":"指某種感受、態度或性質達到非常高、非常強的程度。","examples":[{"en":"She felt extreme anxiety before the interview.","zh":"面試前她感到極度焦慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers faced extreme heat on the open plain.","zh":"徒步者在開闊平原上遭遇了極端高溫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extreme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-896ba533b85bd304","term":"extreme","forms":["extreme","extremer","more extreme","extremest","most extreme"],"pos":"adj","zh":"過度的；超出常態的","explanation":"指某種行為、愛好或程度遠遠超過一般標準，顯得不尋常甚至過火。","examples":[{"en":"His extreme devotion to the hobby left little time for his family.","zh":"他對這項愛好的過度投入幾乎沒有給家人留下時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Extreme heat forced the cancellation of the marathon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extreme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ceb568945f692e8","term":"extreme","forms":["extreme","extremes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極端；極限","explanation":"指某個尺度、程度或狀態能達到的最遠、最高或最強位置。","examples":[{"en":"The design is simple in the extreme.","zh":"這個設計極其簡單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The climate swings between extremes of heat and cold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extreme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-47c215b5f70eb9c9b4bc","word":"eye","forms":["eye"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c30792b4a3a4f3b3","term":"eye","forms":["eye","eyes","eyen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眼睛","explanation":"動物用來感受光線、看見周圍事物的器官，是“看與被看見的中心”最直接的含義。","examples":[{"en":"Bright lights really hurt my eyes.","zh":"強光真的刺痛我的眼睛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She closed one eye and looked through the camera.","zh":"她閉上一隻眼睛，從相機裡觀察。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e753c4a9923974fc","term":"eye","forms":["eye","eyes","eyen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"視覺；觀感","explanation":"指透過眼睛獲得的視覺感受，也可以表示某物在視覺上給人的整體觀感。","examples":[{"en":"The garden is a pleasure to the eye in spring.","zh":"這個花園在春天賞心悅目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The design is simple but pleasing to the eye.","zh":"這個設計很簡單，但看起來很舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8d0d13f38182380","term":"eye","forms":["eye","eyes","eyen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"注意；關注","explanation":"注意力像目光一樣落到某人或某物上，因此 eye 可引申為“看見並留意”。","examples":[{"en":"A red scarf caught my eye in the shop window.","zh":"櫥窗裡的一條紅圍巾吸引了我的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep an eye on the soup while I answer the phone.","zh":"我接電話時請幫忙看著湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16bc6b91c29a305189d5","word":"eyebrow/brow","forms":["eyebrow","brow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cbb5cc7146502679","term":"eyebrow","forms":["eyebrow","eyebrows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眉毛","explanation":"指長在眼窩上方骨脊處的毛髮，也就是眼睛上方那道通常呈弧形的毛。它是這個詞最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She raised one eyebrow when she heard the strange excuse.","zh":"聽到這個奇怪的藉口時，她抬起了一邊眉毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He raised an eyebrow at the surprising price.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyebrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-139dee57ccd53036","term":"brow","forms":["brow","brows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眉骨","explanation":"指眼睛上方托住眉毛的骨性隆起，也就是眉毛所在的那條突起部位。它是“眼睛上方一道隆起”這一核心意象最直接的身體義。","examples":[{"en":"A deep line appeared on his brow as he read the letter.","zh":"他讀信時，眉骨上出現了一道深深的皺紋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The helmet pressed against her brow.","zh":"頭盔壓在她的眉骨上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c89d94d4f14de184","term":"brow","forms":["brow","brows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眉毛","explanation":"也可直接指眉毛本身，尤其常見於文學描寫或描述眉部外觀。它仍然保留著“眼睛上方”的核心位置概念。","examples":[{"en":"She raised her brows in surprise.","zh":"她驚訝地揚起眉毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His dark brows stood out against his pale face.","zh":"他烏黑的眉毛在蒼白的臉上格外醒目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a834a9781c3d459e","term":"brow","forms":["brow","brows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"額頭","explanation":"指眉毛上方的額頭，常用於描寫汗水、皺紋或其他表情痕跡。這裡仍是從眼睛和眉毛上方的區域自然擴充套件出來的。","examples":[{"en":"Sweat gathered on the runner’s brow.","zh":"汗水聚集在那名跑步者的額頭上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wiped her brow after carrying the boxes upstairs.","zh":"她把箱子搬上樓後擦了擦額頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-654ffbb22e2bb7262376","word":"eyelash/lash","forms":["eyelash","lash"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8bcc6d5a66772b5","term":"eyelash","forms":["eyelash","eyelashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"睫毛","explanation":"指沿著眼瞼邊緣生長的一根毛；把許多根合起來看，就是通常所說的睫毛。它們像眼睛邊上的細小刷子，構成了這個詞的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"I got an eyelash in my eye.","zh":"我的眼睛裡進了一根睫毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her eyelashes are very long.","zh":"她的睫毛很長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyelash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3784bbbb8fc6fc4","term":"lash","forms":["lash","lashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞭梢","explanation":"指鞭子末端柔韌的皮條、繩帶或編織繩，真正抽打到物體的部分。它是“甩出力量”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The old whip was missing its lash.","zh":"那條舊鞭子沒有鞭梢了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The whip's lash curled around a fence post.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3db18f7382011d63","term":"lash","forms":["lash","lashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞭打；抽打","explanation":"指用鞭子或類似柔韌物體抽打，也可指一次鞭打。畫面就是鞭梢甩出去並打在目標上。","examples":[{"en":"The horse flinched after a lash from the whip.","zh":"馬被鞭子抽了一下後瑟縮起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoner received several lashes as punishment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5816007d24311217","term":"lash","forms":["lash","lashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"睫毛","explanation":"指長在眼瞼邊緣的毛髮；它們細長、成排，形狀像許多小鞭梢。","examples":[{"en":"A tear hung from her lower lash.","zh":"一滴淚掛在她下眼瞼的睫毛上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A loose lash had fallen into her eye.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a060386b07e23220c55f","word":"eyelid","forms":["eyelid"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f8b4ab0d093b9af","term":"eyelid","forms":["eyelid","eyelids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眼瞼","explanation":"眼睛外面可以上下開合的薄皮膚，像保護眼睛的小簾子；眨眼時它會移動，閉眼時則遮住眼睛。","examples":[{"en":"Her eyelids were swollen after she cried all night.","zh":"她哭了一整夜後，眼瞼腫了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tiny insect landed on her eyelid.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyelid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3662c1bb251060291469","word":"eyesight","forms":["eyesight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b834c5895d928d89","term":"eyesight","forms":["eyesight","eyesights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"視力；視覺能力","explanation":"指眼睛看清東西的能力，也就是一個人視物清楚與否的視覺能力；這是 eyesight 最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She has excellent eyesight.","zh":"她的視力非常好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reading in poor light can damage your eyesight.","zh":"在光線不足的地方閱讀可能會損害視力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyesight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09cf980b5ff304ac11b7","word":"fable","forms":["fable"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d89bb54aada1a219","term":"fable","forms":["fable","fables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寓言","explanation":"指用虛構的故事，常讓動物或其他事物作為角色，來傳達某種道理或勸誡的作品；典型例子是伊索寓言。","examples":[{"en":"The children read a fable about a fox and a crow.","zh":"孩子們讀了一則關於狐狸和烏鴉的寓言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fable teaches us not to trust appearances.","zh":"這則寓言教導我們不要相信表面現象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-938ed89c0d5f0c5a","term":"fable","forms":["fable","fables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳聞；引人談論的故事","explanation":"可泛指被人講來講去、能引起好奇或議論的故事，不一定像典型寓言那樣明確包含道德教訓。","examples":[{"en":"Over time, the explorer's courage became a fable in the village.","zh":"隨著時間過去，那位探險家的勇氣成了村裡廣為流傳的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mysterious visitor soon became the subject of village fable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad2a542c84c7060f1f2e","word":"fabric","forms":["fabric"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b18a38fb39f9911","term":"fabric","forms":["fabric","fabrics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體結構；基礎框架","explanation":"這仍然是“許多纖維交織成整體”的比喻：fabric指一個社會、生活或制度中彼此連線、共同支撐整體的基礎框架。它不只是某個單獨部分，而是整體賴以運作的組織。","examples":[{"en":"Trust is part of the fabric of a healthy community.","zh":"信任是健康社群整體結構的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The railway became an essential part of the region's economic fabric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-739667698d2b5752","term":"fabric","forms":["fabric","fabrics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"織物；布料","explanation":"這是現代最核心的意思：fabric是由纖維製成、可用來做衣服、窗簾或其他物品的布料。它強調材料本身，不一定指一件已經做好的衣物。","examples":[{"en":"This jacket is made from a light, breathable fabric.","zh":"這件夾克用輕薄透氣的布料製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choose a durable fabric for the sofa covers.","zh":"給沙發套選擇耐用的布料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"113":2}}},{"id":"ceec-4b1ee48af1e0bd5e301d","word":"fabulous","forms":["fabulous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72f9966043f06189","term":"fabulous","forms":["fabulous","more fabulous","most fabulous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"神奇非凡的","explanation":"表示像寓言或傳奇一樣神奇、非同尋常，強調事情令人驚歎，甚至有點難以相信。這個意義連線了“寓言般神奇”和現代“好得驚人”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"They told us a fabulous story about a hidden city under the sea.","zh":"他們給我們講了一個關於海底隱藏城市的神奇故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found a fabulous old theater in the middle of the town.","zh":"她在鎮中心發現了一座非凡的老劇院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabulous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e16f773ebe1eff4e","term":"fabulous","forms":["fabulous","more fabulous","most fabulous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"棒極了；極好的","explanation":"在現代非正式英語中，fabulous 常直接表示“非常好、精彩極了”。可以把它理解為：某件事好得像寓言或傳奇中才會出現的奇蹟。","examples":[{"en":"The concert was fabulous from beginning to end.","zh":"這場音樂會從頭到尾都精彩極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You did a fabulous job on the presentation.","zh":"你的演示做得棒極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabulous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0282d9b79f42c74c1550","word":"face","forms":["face"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55dcf87b9f03716e","term":"face","forms":["face","faces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臉；面部","explanation":"指人或動物頭部的正面，通常包括眼睛、鼻子、嘴及其周圍部分；這正是“朝向外界的正面”這個記憶鉤子的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"The baby has a round face and bright eyes.","zh":"這個嬰兒臉圓圓的，眼睛很明亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She covered her face with both hands.","zh":"她用雙手捂住了臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/face","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0aeb224a652505eb","term":"face","forms":["face","faces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面子；名譽；尊嚴","explanation":"指一個人在別人眼中的好名聲、地位和尊嚴；因為臉代表外在形象，所以“face”也能表示一個人不能輕易丟掉的“面子”。","examples":[{"en":"He apologized publicly to save face after the mistake.","zh":"犯錯後，他公開道歉以挽回面子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She did not want to lose face in front of her colleagues.","zh":"她不想在同事面前丟臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/face","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e70f540816d9e35","term":"face","forms":["face","faces","facing","faced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"面向；朝向","explanation":"把“臉”想成朝向外界的“正面”：人轉身讓臉朝著某個方向，就是面向那個方向或物體。","examples":[{"en":"Face the window so you can see the garden.","zh":"面向窗戶，這樣你就能看到花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bedrooms face the quiet courtyard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/face","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fc1da2c8c70250d","term":"face","forms":["face","faces","facing","faced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"面對並處理","explanation":"把“臉”轉向不想看的東西，表示不再躲避，而是承認事實並正面處理困難、責任或現實。","examples":[{"en":"She finally faced the truth about her mistake.","zh":"她終於正視了自己犯錯這一事實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to face the problem before it gets worse.","zh":"我們需要在問題惡化前正面處理它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/face","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd6fdc9a04bb5d7e3afe","word":"facial","forms":["facial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38f4842bd85b7c27","term":"facial","forms":["facial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"臉部的；面部的","explanation":"指屬於臉部、位於臉部或直接影響臉部的事物。把注意力放在臉這一區域，就能理解 facial expression（面部表情）和 facial muscles（面部肌肉）等用法。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor checked her facial muscles for signs of weakness.","zh":"醫生檢查了她的面部肌肉，看是否有無力的跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His facial expression changed when he heard the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息時，他的面部表情變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/facial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c3184ba2d30a35caa0e","word":"facilitate","forms":["facilitate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a271a99764937240","term":"facilitate","forms":["facilitate","facilitates","facilitating","facilitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使更容易","explanation":"表示透過工具、安排或條件，讓某件事更容易、更快或更順利地完成。重點是降低阻礙，而不是代替別人完成任務。","examples":[{"en":"The new software facilitates communication between remote teams.","zh":"這款新軟體使遠端團隊之間的溝通更加方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clear instructions will facilitate the application process.","zh":"清晰的說明會讓申請流程更加順利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/facilitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39004fd3acbe6373","term":"facilitate","forms":["facilitate","facilitates","facilitating","facilitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促成；推動實現","explanation":"表示某人或某事幫助一個結果、計劃或變化發生，把事情向目標方向推進。它不一定是唯一原因，也不表示結果必然成功。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement facilitated closer cooperation between the two countries.","zh":"這項協議促進了兩國之間更密切的合作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mediator helped facilitate an agreement between the neighbors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/facilitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87c597285cce41492615","word":"facility","forms":["facility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31cfeb15f5e73cf0","term":"facility","forms":["facility","facilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"設施；便利條件","explanation":"指使某項活動或公共服務能夠進行的裝置、基礎設施、地點或其他條件。它可以是具體的建築和器材，也可以泛指為某件事提供便利的條件。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel has excellent conference facilities.","zh":"這家酒店有很好的會議設施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city needs better public transport facilities.","zh":"這座城市需要更完善的公共交通設施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/facility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad1cf7266e29b5a1","term":"facility","forms":["facility","facilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專門場所；設施建築","explanation":"指為特定目的專門設計的建築、園區或場所，例如科研、軍事、監獄或醫療場所。這裡強調的是承載某項活動的完整地點，而不只是其中的一件裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The research facility is closed to visitors.","zh":"這座科研設施不對訪客開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recycling facility accepts broken household appliances.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/facility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e7dc6d6c16565406afd","word":"fact","forms":["fact"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d547720e34a3f9a","term":"fact","forms":["fact","facts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"與虛構相對的事實","explanation":"fact 是故事、想象或編造之外，確實發生或確實存在、可以被當作真實內容的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The book mixes historical facts with fiction.","zh":"這本書把歷史事實和虛構內容混在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is a fact that she was there.","zh":"她當時在那裡，這是事實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2704de8949339aa","term":"fact","forms":["fact","facts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"真實存在的情況","explanation":"這裡強調某件事確實是真的，而不是隻是一種猜測、說法或假設；它是“現實本身”這條主線的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The fact is that we do not have enough money.","zh":"事實是，我們沒有足夠的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fact of her resignation surprised nobody.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96fd268e8250feb2","term":"fact","forms":["fact","facts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可作為判斷依據的具體事實","explanation":"一條 fact 像一枚證據釘：它不是空泛看法，而是能拿來分析、解釋或決定下一步的具體情況。","examples":[{"en":"Let us look at the facts before we decide.","zh":"我們先看看事實，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jury must base its verdict on the facts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff926d04864c233ef09c","word":"faction","forms":["faction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bdafd8fd971648b","term":"faction","forms":["faction","factions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組織內的派別","explanation":"一群人在較大的政治組織或其他團體內部，因為共同的信念、利益或立場而結成一派，並與組織中的其他人有所區別。重點不只是“幾個人在一起”，而是他們形成了相對明確的內部陣營。","examples":[{"en":"A powerful faction within the party opposed the new policy.","zh":"黨內一個有影響力的派別反對這項新政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several factions are competing for control of the organization.","zh":"幾個派別正在爭奪這個組織的控制權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f1b5c360bbaadc1","term":"faction","forms":["faction"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事實與虛構的混合作品","explanation":"一種把真實人物、事件或背景當作材料，卻用小說、電影等虛構形式來講述的作品。它既不是單純的事實記錄，也不是完全脫離現實的虛構，而是讓事實穿上虛構敘事的外衣。","examples":[{"en":"The film is a work of faction based on a real political scandal.","zh":"這部電影是一部以真實政治醜聞為基礎的事實與虛構混合作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her new novel blends biography and invention in a striking faction.","zh":"她的新小說把傳記材料和虛構創作結合起來，形成了鮮明的事實與虛構混合寫法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41a093100bbbb59e31dc","word":"factor","forms":["factor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65bac94530dc27f8","term":"factor","forms":["factor","factors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影響結果的因素","explanation":"指會促成、改變或影響某個結果的元素、情況或力量，是日常和學術英語中最重要的意義之一。","examples":[{"en":"Cost was a major factor in our decision.","zh":"成本是我們作出決定時的一個重要因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Weather can be a factor in the delay.","zh":"天氣可能是造成延誤的一個因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/factor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-304e85c63b43627f","term":"factor","forms":["factor","factors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數學因子","explanation":"在數學中，factor 是能與其他數相乘、共同組成一個整體的數或物件；例如 3 是 12 的因子，因為 3 乘以 4 等於 12。","examples":[{"en":"Six is a factor of eighteen.","zh":"6 是 18 的因子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students listed all the factors of 24.","zh":"學生們列出了 24 的所有因子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/factor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06c8aaa93d80a768829b","word":"factory","forms":["factory"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e4d734ca86c8433","term":"factory","forms":["factory","factories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工廠","explanation":"指集中使用機器和工人制造產品的建築物或場所，是 factory 最基本的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"My aunt works at a factory that makes medical equipment.","zh":"我姨媽在一家生產醫療裝置的工廠工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory produces thousands of batteries daily.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/factory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3dbd9cd5e1fb3e4f7854","word":"faculty","forms":["faculty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-650be533f6c8d464","term":"faculty","forms":["faculty","faculties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學教師群體","explanation":"指學校、學院、大學或非營利研究機構中負責教學或學術工作的教師群體，用來和學生及行政、後勤人員區分開。在美國、加拿大和菲律賓英語中尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"The faculty at this college are known for their close work with students.","zh":"這所學院的教師以和學生密切合作而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The faculty voted to revise the graduation requirements.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faculty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-434ad81ec4c30d42","term":"faculty","forms":["faculty","faculties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學院系","explanation":"指大學中按學科或專業劃分的一個教學單位，例如科學、醫學或法律等院系。這裡強調的是組織結構，而不是該院系裡的教師個人。","examples":[{"en":"She transferred from the Faculty of Science to the Faculty of Medicine.","zh":"她從理學院轉到了醫學院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined the faculty of engineering last autumn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faculty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57f5fe2f81d1bfef","term":"faculty","forms":["faculty","faculties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"能力；心智慧力","explanation":"指一個人擁有的能力、力量或技能，尤其可以指記憶、判斷等心智慧力。這個義項常用複數 faculties，表示一個人的各種能力整體。","examples":[{"en":"Even at ninety, she still had all her faculties.","zh":"她即使到了九十歲，仍然頭腦清楚、各項能力完好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a remarkable faculty for remembering names.","zh":"他有非凡的記名能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faculty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-009978b8c24f47f63fbb","word":"fade","forms":["fade"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38705cc9d5b76ee7","term":"fade","forms":["fade","fades","fading","faded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸變弱、衰敗","explanation":"fade 表示力量、生命力或狀態慢慢減弱，進而衰敗、枯萎甚至逐漸消亡；這是“慢慢退去”這一核心畫面的擴充套件。","examples":[{"en":"Without rain, the young plants began to fade.","zh":"沒有雨水，幼苗開始漸漸枯萎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her confidence faded after several failures.","zh":"幾次失敗後，她的信心逐漸減弱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-765f7f2e154d17cb","term":"fade","forms":["fade","fades","fading","faded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"褪色、變淡","explanation":"fade 也表示顏色、光澤或鮮明程度逐漸減弱，變得不再鮮豔；這正是“畫面慢慢退色”的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The red curtains faded in the afternoon sun.","zh":"紅色窗簾在午後的陽光下褪色了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ink on the old letter has faded.","zh":"那封舊信上的墨跡已經變淡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-743d7e7150692f98","term":"fade","forms":["fade","fades","fading","faded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸消失、變得聽不見或看不見","explanation":"fade 表示聲音、影像、光線或身影逐漸退遠、變暗或消失；它強調過程是慢慢發生的，而不是一下子不見。","examples":[{"en":"The sound of the train faded into the distance.","zh":"火車的聲音漸漸消失在遠方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lights faded as the sun rose.","zh":"太陽昇起時，燈光逐漸暗了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02041e85dd20f641b85b","word":"Fahrenheit","forms":["Fahrenheit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"Fahrenheit","forms":["Fahrenheit"],"pos":"n.","zh":"華氏溫標；華氏","examples":[{"en":"Water freezes at thirty-two degrees Fahrenheit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The thermometer reads seventy degrees Fahrenheit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-51280dabfbc880cdc5f9","word":"fail","forms":["fail"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ee63dd9d1427fb2","term":"fail","forms":["fail","fails","failing","failed","failest","failedst","faileth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"失敗；未成功","explanation":"表示人、計劃或行動沒有成功，也就是沒有越過預期的目標線；這是 fail 最基本、最值得先掌握的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Our first attempt failed, but we learned a lot from it.","zh":"我們的第一次嘗試失敗了，但我們從中學到了很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan failed because nobody checked the details.","zh":"這個計劃失敗了，因為沒有人核對細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d69cd6dd46028366","term":"fail","forms":["fail","fails","failing","failed","failest","failedst","faileth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"未能做到","explanation":"表示沒有實現某個明確目標，尤其是沒有完成後面的動作；重點不是完全沒有嘗試，而是結果沒有達到要求。","examples":[{"en":"The truck failed to start on the coldest morning of the year.","zh":"卡車在一年中最冷的早晨沒能啟動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She failed to notice the warning sign.","zh":"她沒有注意到警告標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a676d1e16585f1b","term":"fail","forms":["fail","fails","failing","failed","failest","failedst","faileth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"失靈；停止正常運轉","explanation":"說機器、系統或部件 fail，表示它沒有繼續按預期工作；機器沒有越過“正常執行”的目標線。","examples":[{"en":"The heating system failed during the night.","zh":"供暖系統在夜間失靈了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My brakes failed just as I reached the steepest bend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16d34b5e7bcb341ee6cb","word":"failure","forms":["failure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0604906c978dace7","term":"failure","forms":["failure","failures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"失敗；未達到目標","explanation":"指某項行動、計劃或努力沒有達到預期目標，也就是沒有走到原本想去的終點。它既可以指一次具體的失敗，也可以指總體上的失敗狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The project was a failure because it never reached its main goal.","zh":"這個專案沒有達到主要目標，因此是一次失敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Failure is often part of the process of learning.","zh":"失敗往往是學習過程的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/failure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9b34c9a50b17607","term":"failure","forms":["failure","failures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未履行；沒有做應做的事","explanation":"指某人沒有完成本來應該完成的行動或責任，重點在“該做的事沒有做到”，不一定表示這件事嘗試過但沒有成功。","examples":[{"en":"His failure to reply caused a serious delay.","zh":"他沒有回覆，導致了嚴重的延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Failure to submit identification will delay your application.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/failure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4acfccfbec10ea281d05","word":"faint","forms":["faint"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-075bbdf6beb244d5","term":"faint","forms":["faint","fainter","faintest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"虛弱得頭暈","explanation":"指身體缺乏力量，感到頭暈，甚至快要失去意識；這是“力量弱到人要斷電”的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"I felt faint after standing in the hot sun for an hour.","zh":"在炎熱的陽光下站了一個小時後，我感到頭暈乏力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became faint when she saw the blood.","zh":"她看到血時感到一陣頭暈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c34980978e998ba","term":"faint","forms":["faint","fainter","faintest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"微弱而隱約","explanation":"指光、聲音、氣味、顏色或遠處的跡象很弱，幾乎要察覺不到；這是“訊號變淡”的直接畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a faint light near the top of the hill.","zh":"我們看見山頂附近有一絲微弱的光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A faint smell of smoke filled the room.","zh":"房間裡瀰漫著一絲淡淡的煙味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2348dd35d2b8e2f2","term":"faint","forms":["faint","faints","fainting","fainted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暈倒；失去意識","explanation":"指身體供給大腦的力量突然不足，因而短暫失去意識；這是“人弱到燈滅”的動作版本。","examples":[{"en":"She fainted from the heat but soon woke up.","zh":"她因炎熱而暈倒，但很快就醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I thought I was going to faint when the room started spinning.","zh":"房間開始旋轉時，我以為自己要暈倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1869c9d2a11e8ecde889","word":"fair","forms":["fair"],"officialPos":"adj./n./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-907367252ee055e0","term":"fair","forms":["fair","fairer","fairest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"美麗的；好看的","explanation":"表示外表漂亮、清秀，帶有清新或純潔的感覺；這是“令人滿意”的記憶鉤子在外表上的延伸，但現代日常英語中常帶文學色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The fair maiden smiled at the children.","zh":"那位美麗的少女對孩子們微笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prince fell in love with a fair maiden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1330501692dd01c1","term":"fair","forms":["fair","fairer","fairest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公平的；公正的","explanation":"表示對各方按照合理、平等的標準處理，不偏袒任何一方；這正是記憶鉤子中“對人和規則是公平”。","examples":[{"en":"The judge promised the defendant a fair trial.","zh":"法官承諾被告會得到公正的審判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is only fair to give everyone a chance to speak.","zh":"讓每個人都有機會發言才公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a10f4d9f680eb2c2","term":"fair","forms":["fair","fairer","fairest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"尚可的；合理的","explanation":"表示達到基本要求、還算令人滿意，但沒有特別出色；這是記憶鉤子中“對錶現是還不錯”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel was clean, and the price was fair.","zh":"這家酒店很乾淨，價格也合理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her exam results were fair, but she wanted to improve.","zh":"她的考試成績還不錯，但她想繼續提高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90875fa69161da69","term":"fair","forms":["fair","fairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"集市；交易會","explanation":"指面向公眾的集市或市場，人們可以在那裡買賣商品、觀看攤位和參加活動；這正對應記憶鉤子中的“集市”。","examples":[{"en":"We bought fresh bread at the village fair.","zh":"我們在村裡的集市買了新鮮麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children spent the afternoon at the fair.","zh":"孩子們在集市上度過了一個下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cdbb10488cec6e732113","word":"fairly","forms":["fairly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7dac80bfd4367cd","term":"fairly","forms":["fairly","more fairly","fairlier","most fairly","fairliest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"公平地","explanation":"表示不偏袒任何一方、按照公平原則做某事；這是 fairly 最重要的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The judge promised to treat both sides fairly.","zh":"法官承諾會公平地對待雙方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone deserves to be fairly judged.","zh":"每個人都應該受到公正的評判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14439b28c0609422","term":"fairly","forms":["fairly","more fairly","fairlier","most fairly","fairliest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"相當；頗為","explanation":"放在形容詞或副詞前，表示程度不低但還沒有達到“非常”，是現代英語中非常常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The instructions are fairly easy to follow.","zh":"這些說明相當容易理解和操作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was fairly cold outside this morning.","zh":"今天早上外面相當冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a81e6aa7556585ba7c5","word":"fairy","forms":["fairy"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3285e3c56cdaa2f","term":"fairy","forms":["fairy","more fairy","most fairy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精靈般的；奇幻的","explanation":"形容某人、某物或某種氛圍像精靈世界一樣，顯得奇幻、輕盈、精巧或帶有幻想色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The garden looked fairy-like in the early morning mist.","zh":"清晨的薄霧中，這座花園看起來像精靈的世界一樣奇幻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She decorated the room with fairy lights and tiny stars.","zh":"她用串燈和小星星把房間裝飾得很有奇幻氣息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06a42fd75eb5edb8","term":"fairy","forms":["fairy","fairies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精靈；仙女","explanation":"神話和民間傳說中擁有魔法力量、具有人形的生物；現代插畫常把它畫成帶薄翅膀的小型精靈，但不同傳統中的外形和大小並不相同。","examples":[{"en":"The children believed that a fairy lived under the old oak tree.","zh":"孩子們相信那棵老橡樹下面住著一個精靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story tells of fairies who protect the forest.","zh":"這個故事講述了一群保護森林的精靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b93b177b55445f513d7","word":"faith","forms":["faith"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-409a5737239ba24f","term":"faith","forms":["faith","faiths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信任；信心","explanation":"這裡的 faith 是把心交給某人或某物的信任，通常來自過去的表現、經驗或可靠證據。","examples":[{"en":"I have faith in her ability to solve the problem.","zh":"我相信她有能力解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team's recent wins restored my faith in them.","zh":"球隊最近的勝利讓我重新對他們有了信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faith","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f163d04f263b4b2f","term":"faith","forms":["faith","faiths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信念；信仰","explanation":"faith 也可以是即使沒有直接證據，仍然對某種想法、理想或結果抱有堅定相信。","examples":[{"en":"She kept faith that things would improve.","zh":"她始終相信情況會好轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has faith in the power of education.","zh":"他相信教育的力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faith","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34d26b9eaba5f74b","term":"faith","forms":["faith","faiths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宗教信仰","explanation":"當 faith 指一整套宗教或精神信仰時，它不只是個人的一次相信，而是包含教義、傳統和信仰群體的體系。","examples":[{"en":"The museum welcomes visitors of every faith.","zh":"這座博物館歡迎各種宗教信仰的訪客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her faith guides many of her daily decisions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faith","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b63a9017b09f194f6c0","word":"faithful","forms":["faithful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-882d6731e64978a0","term":"faithful","forms":["faithful","more faithful","most faithful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"忠誠的；忠貞的","explanation":"指對某個人、團體、事業或原則堅定支援，不輕易離開或改變立場；這正是“不會偏航”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She remained faithful to her team even after they lost the final.","zh":"即使球隊輸掉了決賽，她仍然忠於自己的球隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has always been a faithful friend.","zh":"他一直是個忠誠的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faithful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b5d064c976238d3","term":"faithful","forms":["faithful","more faithful","most faithful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有信仰的；堅定信奉的","explanation":"指對宗教或某種信念持有堅定信心並遵循它；可以看作“沿著信念的路不偏離”。","examples":[{"en":"The faithful gathered at the temple before sunrise.","zh":"信徒們在日出前聚集到寺廟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The faithful gathered for evening prayers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faithful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81b5b1da7196812c","term":"faithful","forms":["faithful","more faithful","most faithful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可靠的；值得信賴的","explanation":"指人會履行職責、不會讓人失望，或事物能穩定按預期工作；這是“不會偏航”從忠誠擴充套件到可靠。","examples":[{"en":"Our old car has been a faithful companion on many road trips.","zh":"我們的舊車在許多次公路旅行中一直是可靠的夥伴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The faithful assistant never missed an important deadline.","zh":"這位可靠的助理從未錯過重要截止日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faithful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5d54c39e66671c9731b","word":"fake","forms":["fake"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e97c775b75312a43","term":"fake","forms":["fake","faker","more fake","fakest","most fake"],"pos":"adj","zh":"假的；偽造的","explanation":"指看起來像真的、實際上並非真品，或為了欺騙而製造出來的東西。它可以形容材料、證件、身份、新聞等被偽造或不真實的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The painting looked expensive, but it was fake.","zh":"這幅畫看起來很貴，但其實是假的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The website was selling fake concert tickets.","zh":"那個網站在賣假演唱會門票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbff21aeb4aea6d9","term":"fake","forms":["fake","fakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"假貨；偽造品","explanation":"指看起來像真品、實際上不是正品的東西，或被冒充成真品出售的物品。它是形容詞“假的”所描述的物件化結果。","examples":[{"en":"The museum discovered that the statue was a fake.","zh":"博物館發現那座雕像是一件贗品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Experts identified the supposedly ancient coin as a fake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f38fbcf83836de3","term":"fake","forms":["fake","fakes","faking","faked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偽造；仿造","explanation":"指故意製造假貨、假檔案或虛假資訊，使它看起來像真的。這個動作義直接對應形容詞“假的”和名詞“假貨”。","examples":[{"en":"Someone tried to fake my signature on the form.","zh":"有人試圖在表格上偽造我的簽名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He faked his father's signature on the note.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c70daebc9f506f45","term":"fake","forms":["fake","fakes","faking","faked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"假裝；裝出","explanation":"指明明不是某種狀態，卻故意表現得像是那樣；也可以指裝作會做某事或裝出某種感情。它仍然是用表面表現去影響別人判斷。","examples":[{"en":"He faked surprise when he saw the birthday cake.","zh":"他看到生日蛋糕時裝出一副驚訝的樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I did not know the answer, so I faked confidence.","zh":"我不知道答案，所以裝出很有把握的樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2dc46af1b78c32dfe99d","word":"fall","forms":["fall"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80ed656e4433121b","term":"fall","forms":["fall","falls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下落；跌落","explanation":"指物體受重力影響從較高位置向下移動，也可指人跌倒這一動作或事件。它是記憶畫面中最直接的“從高處向下”。","examples":[{"en":"The fall of snow covered the road by morning.","zh":"一夜之間落下的雪蓋住了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had a bad fall while climbing the stairs.","zh":"她上樓梯時重重摔了一跤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e8dc186bed4c40d","term":"fall","forms":["fall","falls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秋天；秋季","explanation":"指樹葉通常落下的季節，也就是秋季；這是由“樹葉落下”的畫面引申來的用法。","examples":[{"en":"We plan to visit the mountains in the fall.","zh":"我們計劃秋天去山區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trees turn bright red every fall.","zh":"每年秋天，樹木都會變成鮮紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c9249ae73c50ccc","term":"fall","forms":["fall","falls","falling","fell","fallen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"落下","explanation":"表示人或物從較高處向下移動，正是記憶中“從高處向下”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The glass fell from the table and broke.","zh":"玻璃杯從桌上掉下來摔碎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Snow fell throughout the night.","zh":"雪下了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcbcf165908dd18a9e49","word":"false","forms":["false"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60a65e5523a7a574","term":"false","forms":["false","falser","falsest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不真實的","explanation":"指陳述、訊息或事實與真實情況不相符，也就是表面像真的“假印章”。","examples":[{"en":"The report contained several false claims.","zh":"這份報告包含幾項不實的說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rumor turned out to be false.","zh":"這個傳聞後來被證明是假的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/false","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9895d63dd6137f31","term":"false","forms":["false","falser","falsest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"建立在錯誤前提上的","explanation":"指法律、判斷或決定等從一開始就建立在不正確的事實或理由上，因此整體不可靠。","examples":[{"en":"The policy was based on a false assumption.","zh":"這項政策建立在一個錯誤的假設之上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The argument rests on a false assumption about demand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/false","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8309254b6979d771f140","word":"falter","forms":["falter"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c3426964ebfcf2c","term":"falter","forms":["falter","falters","faltering","faltered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得不穩；變弱","explanation":"指腿腳、動作、機器運轉或某個過程失去原來的穩定，開始搖晃、減弱或斷續；核心畫面就是“腳下一晃”。","examples":[{"en":"His legs began to falter after the long climb.","zh":"長時間爬山後，他的雙腿開始發軟不穩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old engine faltered but started again a few seconds later.","zh":"那臺舊發動機運轉不穩，但幾秒後又重新啟動了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/falter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-723d08f165672c7d","term":"falter","forms":["falter","falters","faltering","faltered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說話結巴；聲音發抖","explanation":"指說話時因為緊張、激動或虛弱而停頓、結巴，或用發抖而微弱的聲音說出話來；這和腳步不穩是同一個“失去穩定”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"“I don't know,” she faltered, looking down at the floor.","zh":"她低頭看著地板，結結巴巴地說：“我不知道。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His voice faltered as he tried to explain what had happened.","zh":"他試圖解釋事情經過時，聲音開始發抖、斷續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/falter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ef09098aa7d919d","term":"falter","forms":["falter","falters","faltering","faltered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"信心或決心動搖","explanation":"把“腳步失穩”的畫面轉到內心：指失去信心、精力或勇氣，開始懷疑目標，甚至想放棄。","examples":[{"en":"She never faltered in her determination to finish the project.","zh":"她完成這個專案的決心從未動搖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our confidence faltered when the first plan failed.","zh":"第一個方案失敗後，我們的信心動搖了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/falter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4ce4b23fe50330234d0","word":"fame","forms":["fame"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5ba43ab9c935878","term":"fame","forms":["fame","fames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名聲；聲譽","explanation":"fame 是別人長期談論某人或某事後形成的名聲，也就是“在別人心中的聲譽”。它關注的是被廣泛知道和談論，不單純表示道德意義上的好壞。","examples":[{"en":"Her fame grew after the film won several awards.","zh":"那部電影獲得多個獎項後，她的名聲越來越大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discovery brought him fame beyond academic circles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eff48ac3c88bb71a","term":"fame","forms":["fame","fames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成名；廣為人知","explanation":"這個意思強調處於“人人都知道、人人都在談論”的狀態，通常可譯為“成名”或“名聲大”。它和 s2 緊密相連：s2 是擁有的名聲，s3 更突出廣泛知名的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"He found fame as a young actor.","zh":"他年輕時就作為演員成名了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The singer avoided fame and preferred a quiet life.","zh":"那位歌手避開名聲，更喜歡安靜的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a419467866c1174426c","word":"familiar","forms":["familiar"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ffc12effd73b7c0","term":"familiar","forms":["familiar","more familiar","most familiar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熟悉的；常見的","explanation":"像那張見過多次的臉一樣，familiar 表示某人或某事讓人覺得認識、眼熟，或者因為經常出現而不顯得陌生。","examples":[{"en":"That name sounds familiar, but I can't remember where I saw it.","zh":"這個名字聽起來很熟悉，但我想不起在哪裡見過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smell of fresh bread was familiar from her childhood.","zh":"新鮮麵包的香味讓她想起童年，那是她很熟悉的味道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/familiar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf39c728d29681b7","term":"familiar","forms":["familiar","more familiar","most familiar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熟悉；瞭解","explanation":"familiar with 表示對某個系統、主題、方法或活動有了解，已經知道它大致怎樣運作，但不一定精通。","examples":[{"en":"Are you familiar with the new ticketing system?","zh":"你熟悉新的售票系統嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm familiar with the route, so we won't need a map.","zh":"我熟悉這條路線，所以我們不需要地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/familiar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114,115],"total":3,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-a8f60840bfec84375721","word":"familiarity","forms":["familiarity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0934be3aec0a5ea","term":"familiarity","forms":["familiarity","familiarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親密；熟稔","explanation":"指人與人之間非常親近、相處自然的狀態，像彼此已經熟到不必拘謹。這個親近本身不一定是負面的，關鍵看上下文是否暗示越過了合適的距離。","examples":[{"en":"The familiarity between the two neighbors grew after they began walking their dogs together.","zh":"兩位鄰居一起遛狗後，彼此變得越來越親近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their easy familiarity made newcomers feel welcome.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/familiarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62a5c363e35be929","term":"familiarity","forms":["familiarity","familiarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過分親暱；冒犯性的隨便","explanation":"這裡的“門開得太近”帶出了負面意味：對方表現得過於隨便，彷彿已經親近到可以不顧禮貌和界限。它常用於提醒某種言行超過了合適的分寸。","examples":[{"en":"The assistant’s familiarity with the director made several visitors uncomfortable.","zh":"這名助理對主任過分隨便的態度讓幾位來訪者感到不舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her unwanted familiarity made the new employee uncomfortable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/familiarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b8a38d27caedf14","term":"familiarity","forms":["familiarity","familiarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熟悉；瞭解","explanation":"指因為反覆接觸、使用或經歷而對某人或某事物有了認識和把握，像一扇門被走過很多次後不再陌生。它既可表示認識某人，也可表示瞭解主題、環境、工具或流程。","examples":[{"en":"Her familiarity with the software helped the team solve the problem quickly.","zh":"她對這款軟體很熟悉，幫助團隊迅速解決了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her familiarity with mountain weather kept us from taking unnecessary risks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/familiarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d34a569ab7aaa54dacd7","word":"family","forms":["family"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-87e2ac94faeb2d71","term":"family","forms":["family","families"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家庭；家人","explanation":"指由血緣、婚姻或收養聯絡起來的人，最常見的是父母和子女組成的家庭，也可泛指親屬。記住它是一個“共同歸屬的家人圈”，不只是一棟房子。","examples":[{"en":"My family eats dinner together on Sundays.","zh":"我們家人星期天一起吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are starting a family next year.","zh":"他們計劃明年組建家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/family","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-79b1bc81314de30fec0e","word":"famous","forms":["famous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdf95d7ec8660443","term":"famous","forms":["famous","more famous","most famous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"廣為人知的","explanation":"指名字或事蹟傳得很廣，很多人知道這個人、地方、作品或事件。它就像名字被廣泛傳開，重點是知名範圍大，而不一定帶有褒義。","examples":[{"en":"The city is famous for its beautiful old buildings.","zh":"這座城市因美麗的古建築而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became famous after writing her first novel.","zh":"她寫完第一部小說後出名了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/famous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c395b10efeb403a","term":"famous","forms":["famous","more famous","most famous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"受到公眾關注的","explanation":"強調某人或某事進入公眾視線，成為大家正在關注或議論的物件；知名範圍可以侷限在某個城市、群體或領域，不一定是全世界都知道。","examples":[{"en":"The chef is famous in our neighborhood for his spicy noodles.","zh":"這位廚師因為辣麵條在我們這一帶很有名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The famous actor could hardly walk outside unnoticed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/famous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e29a7f31cac05abc97e1","word":"fan","forms":["fan"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-932afedec3165ecc","term":"fan","forms":["fan","fans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"扇子","explanation":"指拿在手裡、可以展開並來回揮動以送風的扇子。它保留了 fan“推動空氣”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She opened her hand fan and waved it slowly.","zh":"她開啟手中的扇子，慢慢地扇著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paper fan is small enough to fit in my bag.","zh":"這把紙扇很小，可以放進我的包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d8c5b80e6261570","term":"fan","forms":["fan","fans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"風扇","explanation":"指用電力或機械力推動空氣的裝置，可以給人降溫，也可以給機器通風。","examples":[{"en":"Please turn on the fan; the room is too hot.","zh":"請開啟風扇，房間太熱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The computer fan keeps the machine cool.","zh":"電腦風扇讓機器保持涼爽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-383ca088a43aab48","term":"fan","forms":["fan","fans","fen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"粉絲；愛好者","explanation":"指喜歡並支援某位表演者、球隊、運動或其他事物的人。這個意思可以和“扇旺熱情”的畫面聯絡起來：粉絲把自己的興趣和熱情扇得更旺。","examples":[{"en":"I'm a big fan of this band.","zh":"我是這個樂隊的忠實粉絲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many fans traveled to see the final game.","zh":"許多球迷趕去觀看決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0abeb765241b2ef8","term":"fan","forms":["fan","fans","fanning","fanned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"扇風；吹拂","explanation":"指用扇子、風扇或其他氣流吹向某物，核心仍是“讓空氣流動起來”。也可以說風自然地吹拂某人或某物。","examples":[{"en":"A cool breeze fanned our faces as we walked.","zh":"我們走路時，涼爽的微風吹拂著臉龐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He fanned the fire to make it burn brighter.","zh":"他扇動空氣，讓火燒得更旺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed541aab68a44e6e71b9","word":"fancy","forms":["fancy"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a99cea5c233093e1","term":"fancy","forms":["fancy","fancier","fanciest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"裝飾華麗的","explanation":"指裝飾很多、做工講究，或樣式顯得特別華麗的東西。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a fancy shawl to the wedding.","zh":"她戴了一條華麗的披肩參加婚禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We don't need a fancy dinner tonight.","zh":"我們今晚不需要吃什麼講究的大餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28da77b53ba8352a","term":"fancy","forms":["fancy","fancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"想象力","explanation":"指在頭腦中形成影象、場景或念頭的能力，即想象力。","examples":[{"en":"Her fancy turned the empty room into a castle.","zh":"她的想象力把空房間變成了一座城堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The magical landscape sprang entirely from the artist's fancy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5349fcc4a629594e","term":"fancy","forms":["fancy","fancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一時興起的念頭","explanation":"指突然想做某事的念頭或小願望，通常不表示長期計劃。","examples":[{"en":"I had a fancy to walk along the river after lunch.","zh":"我午飯後突然想沿著河邊走走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"On a fancy, she bought a bright red hat.","zh":"她一時興起，買了一頂鮮紅的帽子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58b327b90d314170","term":"fancy","forms":["fancy","fancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜歡；愛慕","explanation":"指對某人產生喜歡或愛慕之情，是“特別偏愛某人”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"He took a fancy to the new teacher.","zh":"他喜歡上了那位新老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children took a fancy to the gentle dog.","zh":"孩子們喜歡上了那隻溫順的狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-171ff9820d9e291f","term":"fancy","forms":["fancy","fancies","fancying","fancied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想要","explanation":"在英國英語中表示想吃、想喝或想做某事，是一種隨意的願望。","examples":[{"en":"Do you fancy a walk after dinner?","zh":"你想不想晚飯後散散步？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I fancy some tea before bed.","zh":"我睡前想喝點茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-659c6e8d11873dbc6794","word":"fantastic","forms":["fantastic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1306c0a8d580103","term":"fantastic","forms":["fantastic","more fantastic","most fantastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極好的；棒極了","explanation":"形容某人、某物或某段經歷好得特別突出，常帶有興奮和讚歎的語氣，相當於“太棒了、精彩極了”。","examples":[{"en":"We had a fantastic time at the beach.","zh":"我們在海灘玩得特別開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a fantastic idea.","zh":"那真是個棒極了的主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fantastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c4dc4c43413e769","term":"fantastic","forms":["fantastic","more fantastic","most fantastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇幻的；幻想中的","explanation":"形容內容來自想象而不是現實，常用於龍、魔法、異世界等奇幻題材，也可以泛指富有幻想色彩的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The children loved the fantastic world in the movie.","zh":"孩子們喜歡電影裡的奇幻世界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fantastic creatures filled the pages of her sketchbook.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fantastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5292f27501324087b9dc","word":"fantasy","forms":["fantasy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dfc5b8b805cd4376","term":"fantasy","forms":["fantasy","fantasies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幻想；想象中的事物","explanation":"指主要存在於人的想象中的事物、情景或願望，不一定是真實發生的事情。它可以是個人腦中的畫面，也可以是脫離現實的設想。","examples":[{"en":"For years, owning a small house by the sea was only a fantasy.","zh":"多年來，擁有一座海邊小屋只是一個幻想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He built his whole plan on the fantasy that nothing could go wrong.","zh":"他把整個計劃建立在“一切都不會出問題”的幻想上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fantasy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5412191cdec0e076","term":"fantasy","forms":["fantasy","fantasies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"奇幻文學或影視型別","explanation":"指以魔法、超自然力量、虛構世界或想象中的生物為主要內容的文學、電影、遊戲等型別。這裡的 fantasy 不是某個角色的個人幻想，而是一種創作型別。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter is reading a fantasy novel about a kingdom ruled by dragons.","zh":"我女兒正在讀一本關於龍統治的王國的奇幻小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bookshop keeps fantasy beside science fiction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fantasy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-512eea46ceb3921dff43","word":"far","forms":["far"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce3c999f667ac0be","term":"far","forms":["far","farther","further","farthest","furthest","farthermost","furthermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遙遠的","explanation":"指在空間上距離很大、離說話者或某個參照點很遠。它是 far 最基本、最容易擴充套件的意思。","examples":[{"en":"They moved to a far corner of the country.","zh":"他們搬到了這個國家一個遙遠的角落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A far mountain rose above the morning mist.","zh":"一座遠山聳立在晨霧之上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/far","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-282e7c2dc6f12856","term":"far","forms":["far","farther","further","farthest","furthest","farthermost","furthermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遙遠的（時間）","explanation":"把空間上的“距離遠”轉用於時間，表示離現在或某個時間點很久、很遙遠。","examples":[{"en":"People may live on Mars in the far future.","zh":"在遙遠的未來，人們或許會生活在火星上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the far future, these islands may disappear.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/far","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-333b78cfde692aa6","term":"far","forms":["far","farther","further","farthest","furthest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"遠遠地；到很遠的程度","explanation":"表示動作、進展或範圍延伸到很遠的地方、時間或程度，也可表示某人已經取得了很大進展。","examples":[{"en":"You have come far, but there is still work to do.","zh":"你已經取得了很大進展，但還有工作要做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sound carried far across the valley.","zh":"聲音傳遍了整個山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/far","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2b23f0df81ab91a","term":"far","forms":["far","farther","further","farthest","furthest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"遠遠地；大大地","explanation":"放在比較級、某些形容詞或副詞前，表示程度遠遠超過普通水平，相當於“很大幅度地”。","examples":[{"en":"This solution is far better than the one we tried before.","zh":"這個解決辦法比我們之前試過的好得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The replacement is far cheaper than the original.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/far","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eaa8b6e89fcb020dc966","word":"fare","forms":["fare"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8bd6f6e3a7170633","term":"fare","forms":["fare","fares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交通費；車票錢","explanation":"fare 是為了完成一段乘車、乘船或乘飛機旅程而支付的錢，也就是交通費用。","examples":[{"en":"The train fare has gone up again.","zh":"火車票價又上漲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I paid the fare with my phone.","zh":"我用手機付了車費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-418437ef1acfe630916f","word":"farewell","forms":["farewell"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b977154bcfc488b7","term":"farewell","forms":["farewell","farewells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"告別；臨別道別","explanation":"指人在分別時作出的告別，尤其適用於鄭重、感傷或可能長期不見的離別場景。","examples":[{"en":"The graduates bid farewell to their teachers after the ceremony.","zh":"畢業生在典禮後向老師們道別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her farewell to the village was deeply emotional.","zh":"她向這個村莊作的告別充滿了感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/farewell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8cf701f30ad11d3ee87","word":"farm","forms":["farm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebe5ccf6281b28e4","term":"farm","forms":["farm","farms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農場；農莊","explanation":"種植莊稼或飼養牲畜、並進行相關農業活動的地方。它通常不只是一塊田地，還包括建築、裝置和經營活動。","examples":[{"en":"Her family runs a small farm outside the town.","zh":"她家在城外經營一個小農場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent the summer working on a sheep farm.","zh":"我們整個夏天都在一個養羊場工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/farm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36fab2b9eb335735","term":"farm","forms":["farm","farms","farming","farmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從事農業","explanation":"指在農場工作，尤其是種植和收穫莊稼。這裡強調人的農業勞動，而不是農場這個地點。","examples":[{"en":"After college, he moved to the countryside to farm.","zh":"大學畢業後，他搬到鄉下務農。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many families still farm along the river.","zh":"許多家庭仍在河邊務農。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/farm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51bf5502a7102c96f3ff","word":"farmer","forms":["farmer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb3a37de992ed214","term":"farmer","forms":["farmer","farmers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農民；農場經營者","explanation":"farmer 指從事種植、養殖或其他農業經營的人；重點是“經營農業”，不一定只做某一種農活，也不一定只是僱工。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer grows vegetables and keeps chickens.","zh":"這位農民種蔬菜，還養雞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many farmers sell their produce at the local market.","zh":"許多農民在當地市場出售自己的農產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/farmer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d757055d1027fc5d407","word":"farther","forms":["farther"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"farther","forms":["farther"],"pos":"adv./adj.","zh":"更遠地；更遠的","examples":[{"en":"We walked farther than we had planned.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The farther shore was hidden by thick fog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-50ab16562d1212d9f8ea","word":"fascinate","forms":["fascinate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"fascinate","forms":["fascinate"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使著迷；深深吸引","examples":[{"en":"Stories about distant planets fascinate many children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The tiny details in this painting never fail to fascinate me.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-e55eb0745a11ff1c638c","word":"fascination","forms":["fascination"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c34abdd994dd788","term":"fascination","forms":["fascination","fascinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"著迷感；被吸引的狀態","explanation":"指人面對某個事物時產生的強烈吸引和著迷感，重點在於“被吸住”的心理狀態，而不只是普通的興趣。","examples":[{"en":"To my fascination, the old machine still worked perfectly.","zh":"令我著迷的是，那臺老機器仍然運轉得十分完美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her fascination with the night sky began when she was a child.","zh":"她對夜空的著迷始於童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fascination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f40ae9abea22bf63","term":"fascination","forms":["fascination","fascinations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人著迷的事物","explanation":"指本身能夠持續吸引人、讓人產生強烈興趣的物件，例如某個主題、活動或現象；也就是“吸引人的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Space travel has been a lifelong fascination for her.","zh":"太空旅行一直是她一生著迷的事物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ancient maps were one of his lifelong fascinations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fascination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-309d267f086d5fe5433d","word":"fashion","forms":["fashion"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-355bd69c9c435bba","term":"fashion","forms":["fashion","fashions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流行趨勢","explanation":"指某一時期受到人們追捧的樣式或觀念，重點在於它會隨著時間改變，過一陣子可能就不再流行。","examples":[{"en":"Bright colors are back in fashion this year.","zh":"今年鮮豔的顏色又流行起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That style went out of fashion decades ago.","zh":"那種風格幾十年前就過時了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fashion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d516e6a39392e702","term":"fashion","forms":["fashion","fashions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時尚與服裝行業","explanation":"泛指服裝和外表方面的流行樣式，也可以指設計、生產和推廣這些服裝的整個時尚行業。","examples":[{"en":"She hopes to work in fashion after college.","zh":"她希望大學畢業後從事時尚行業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to build a career in fashion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fashion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02a50dce377961bb","term":"fashion","forms":["fashion","fashions","fashioning","fashioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"製作；塑造","explanation":"指把材料、工具或想法親手做成某種樣子，常帶有臨時製作、巧手拼制或因地制宜的意味。它正是“把東西做出某種樣子”這一核心概念的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"They fashioned a shelter from branches and leaves.","zh":"他們用樹枝和樹葉搭出了一個 shelter。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fashioned a simple tool from a piece of wire.","zh":"她用一段金屬線做成了一個簡單工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fashion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-862f3a0809f9b9f60a74","word":"fashionable","forms":["fashionable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0444a6f3c0fd231","term":"fashionable","forms":["fashionable","more fashionable","most fashionable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"時髦的；流行的","explanation":"指符合當前流行趨勢或風格的，常用於衣服、髮型、場所、生活方式等。它的核心畫面是“貼著當下潮流標籤”，所以不只可以形容外表，也可以形容一種受到追捧的選擇。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a fashionable dress for the party.","zh":"她買了一條時髦的裙子參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That neighborhood has become fashionable among young professionals.","zh":"那個社群在年輕的專業人士中變得很流行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fashionable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1c83bd7adc56218","term":"fashionable","forms":["fashionable","more fashionable","most fashionable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"當時流行的；盛行的","explanation":"指某個特定時期被普遍接受、採用或認可的思想、做法或觀點。這裡不一定是在說外表時髦，而是在說它代表了那個時代的主流風尚。","examples":[{"en":"At the time, this was the fashionable theory among historians.","zh":"在當時，這一理論是歷史學家中流行的觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wide collars were fashionable during that decade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fashionable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-115dc3606fbf8691fb69","word":"fast","forms":["fast"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e62146ee12a65bd","term":"fast","forms":["fast","faster","fastest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"快速的","explanation":"表示移動速度很快，或本身能夠快速移動。可以把它想成動作緊緊向前推進，因此又快又有力。","examples":[{"en":"This is the fastest train on the line.","zh":"這是這條線路上最快的火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a fast car for her daily commute.","zh":"她買了一輛速度很快的汽車來通勤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c523307854987c4a","term":"fast","forms":["fast","faster","fastest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"快速地","explanation":"表示以很快的速度做某事，或在很短時間內完成。它和形容詞的“快”一樣，帶有動作緊緊向前推進的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Please walk fast or we will miss the bus.","zh":"請走快一點，不然我們要趕不上公共汽車了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river is flowing fast after the rain.","zh":"下雨後河水流得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e5138f7dba1f26f4609","word":"fasten","forms":["fasten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-259a78128d7691bb","term":"fasten","forms":["fasten","fastens","fastening","fastened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繫牢；扣緊；固定連線","explanation":"把兩個物體連線起來，或把某物扣好、繫好，使它不容易鬆開或脫落。核心畫面就是“讓東西變得牢固並保持連線”。","examples":[{"en":"Please fasten your seat belt before the plane takes off.","zh":"飛機起飛前請繫好安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fastened the package to the bicycle with a strong strap.","zh":"她用一條結實的帶子把包裹固定在腳踏車上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fasten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be07f5139a61ebb919cc","word":"fat","forms":["fat"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-260f72323cfdb35a","term":"fat","forms":["fat","fatter","fattest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"肥胖的","explanation":"形容人的身體脂肪比通常更多，整體顯得胖；這正是“脂肪堆在人身上”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The dog is getting fat because we keep giving it treats.","zh":"這隻狗越來越胖，因為我們總是不停地給它零食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was fat as a child, but became very active in high school.","zh":"他小時候很胖，但上高中後變得非常愛運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-062be1c9ab3a0095","term":"fat","forms":["fat","fatter","fattest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"油膩的；脂肪多的","explanation":"形容食物含有較多油脂，吃起來油膩或肥；這是“脂肪堆在食物裡”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"This soup is too fat for me, so I will remove some of the oil.","zh":"這湯對我來說太油膩了，所以我會撇掉一些油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe uses a fat cut of pork for extra flavor.","zh":"這道菜譜用了一塊肥肉較多的豬肉來增加風味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f86fd3538e93178a","term":"fat","forms":["fat","fats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脂肪","explanation":"指動物體內儲存能量、也能幫助保溫的脂肪組織，是“脂肪堆在人或動物身上”的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"Bears store fat before they settle down for the winter.","zh":"熊在進入冬眠前會儲存脂肪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise can help reduce body fat.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於減少體脂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-79e216f9ba0184b79f34","word":"fatal","forms":["fatal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53104eda856af763","term":"fatal","forms":["fatal","more fatal","most fatal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"致命的；導致毀滅的","explanation":"指某物會造成死亡、毀滅或無法挽回的結果，像給人或事情造成決定性的一擊；fatal wound 是“致命傷”，fatal mistake 是“致命錯誤”。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor said that the injury was fatal.","zh":"醫生說這處傷是致命的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ignoring the warning proved to be a fatal mistake.","zh":"無視警告最終成了一個致命的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fatal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c94defcda218cdfb","term":"fatal","forms":["fatal","more fatal","most fatal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"使程式終止的","explanation":"在計算機語境中，fatal 描述嚴重到足以讓程式突然停止執行的錯誤或異常；它仍然保留“造成無法繼續的結果”這一核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The application closed after a fatal error.","zh":"應用程式在發生致命錯誤後關閉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fatal error stopped the program before completion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fatal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-774a13da8cfe47716460","word":"fate","forms":["fate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-965981de5378550f","term":"fate","forms":["fate","fates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"決定事情走向的命運力量","explanation":"指被認為會預先決定事件發生方式和結果的力量、原則或神意。它像一條看不見的路線，解釋人們為什麼覺得某些事情早已被安排好。","examples":[{"en":"She believed that fate had brought them together.","zh":"她相信是命運讓他們走到了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fate of the village depended on the result of the vote.","zh":"這個村莊的命運取決於投票結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de1b4c4bbdfefaf3","term":"fate","forms":["fate","fates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"命運，尤指不幸的遭遇","explanation":"指一個人註定要經歷的命運，尤其是死亡、毀滅或其他不幸的結局。說“接受自己的命運”時，fate 常帶有無法逃脫的沉重意味。","examples":[{"en":"After the defeat, the soldiers knew they had to accept their fate.","zh":"戰敗後，士兵們知道自己只能接受命運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hero tried to escape his fate, but the prophecy came true.","zh":"英雄試圖逃脫命運，但預言還是應驗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-88a1881f0025cf711750","word":"father","forms":["father"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbc8ff1fce44510d","term":"father","forms":["father","fathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"父親","explanation":"father 指男性父母，即生育、收養、寄養或實際承擔父親職責的人。核心不是單純的血緣，而是“作為父親來養育或承擔責任”。","examples":[{"en":"My father was a strong influence on me.","zh":"我的父親對我影響很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a father figure to her younger cousins.","zh":"她成了年幼表親們的父輩榜樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/father","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97ac064bc39d0544","term":"father","forms":["father","fathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孩子的生父","explanation":"father 也可專門指生育了某個孩子的男性，強調他與孩子之間的生物學父子關係。","examples":[{"en":"My friend Tony just became a father.","zh":"我的朋友託尼剛剛當上了父親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The birth certificate identifies his biological father.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/father","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4064e6a9a434b058fcae","word":"fatigue","forms":["fatigue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d33a54a7eae58f8","term":"fatigue","forms":["fatigue","fatigues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疲勞；疲憊","explanation":"指體力或腦力持續消耗後產生的疲憊狀態，也可以指一次辛苦的勞累過程。重點不是普通的短暫睏倦，而是“被消耗得很累”。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, she felt severe fatigue in her legs.","zh":"長途徒步後，她感到雙腿極度疲勞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can lead to mental fatigue.","zh":"睡眠不足可能導致精神疲勞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fatigue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6420d3bba4ce75ea","term":"fatigue","forms":["fatigue","fatigues","fatiguing","fatigued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使疲勞","explanation":"指體力或腦力活動把某人消耗得很累，強調造成疲勞的動作。它把名詞的“疲勞狀態”變成了“使人疲勞”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The demanding schedule fatigued the young athletes.","zh":"緊張的日程使年輕運動員疲憊不堪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long meeting fatigued everyone in the room.","zh":"長時間的會議讓房間裡的每個人都感到疲憊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fatigue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5050d866cb43920b","term":"fatigue","forms":["fatigue","fatigues","fatiguing","fatigued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得疲勞","explanation":"指人因持續活動而逐漸失去力氣，變得疲憊、虛弱或筋疲力盡；這裡強調主體自己被消耗。","examples":[{"en":"Workers quickly fatigued in the intense summer heat.","zh":"工人在酷熱的夏天很快就感到疲憊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her muscles fatigued quickly during the final set.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fatigue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-f40b4c5241c68cafc72d","word":"faucet","forms":["faucet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ca2f61b7e4a7e86e","term":"faucet","forms":["faucet","faucets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水龍頭；出水閥","explanation":"安裝在水管或容器出口處、用來開啟、關閉或調節水流的裝置。這個詞強調的是人可以操作的出水口，而不只是裡面的管道。","examples":[{"en":"Please turn off the faucet when you finish washing your hands.","zh":"洗完手後請把水龍頭關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kitchen faucet is leaking again.","zh":"廚房的水龍頭又漏水了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faucet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb6eb714c535500a","term":"faucet","forms":["faucet","faucets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊戲經濟的貨幣注入口","explanation":"在遊戲開發語境中，faucet 是不斷把遊戲貨幣注入經濟系統的一個或多個來源；設計者會調節它，以免貨幣流入過多而造成通貨膨脹。它沿用了“控制液體流量”的核心畫面，只是流出的東西變成了遊戲貨幣。","examples":[{"en":"The developers reduced the currency faucet to slow inflation.","zh":"開發者減少了貨幣注入量，以減緩通貨膨脹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Daily quests act as a currency faucet in the game.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/faucet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1c562eae32f9cc2a97d","word":"fault","forms":["fault"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa722e6aa61dd6f8","term":"fault","forms":["fault","faults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"責任；過錯","explanation":"指某件壞事發生時應由誰承擔責任，重點是“這件事是某人的過錯”，不一定表示這個人故意造成了它。","examples":[{"en":"It wasn't your fault that the train was late.","zh":"火車晚點不是你的錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accident happened through no fault of her own.","zh":"這場事故的發生完全不是她的責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fault","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7801da6aac2e73af","term":"fault","forms":["fault","faults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"品格上的缺點","explanation":"指一個人性格或行為中值得批評的弱點，通常比一般的小瑕疵更嚴重，但有這個缺點並不等於這個人整體很壞。","examples":[{"en":"Her impatience is one of her biggest faults.","zh":"缺乏耐心是她最大的缺點之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Impatience is his most obvious fault.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fault","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df2fc6e9c627881ad80d","word":"favor","forms":["favor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-818f1ee6a1617104","term":"favor","forms":["favor","favors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫忙；善意的幫助","explanation":"指一個人出於善意，主動為別人做的一件有幫助的事，也可以泛指這種幫助本身。它既可以是一次具體行動，也可以是不限定次數的善意相助。","examples":[{"en":"Could you do me a favor and watch my bag for a minute?","zh":"你能幫我個忙，替我看一分鐘包嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I owe you a favor for helping me move.","zh":"你幫我搬家，我欠你一個人情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/favor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eff473cd8fe81afb","term":"favor","forms":["favor","favors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"好感；恩寵","explanation":"指掌權者或某人對另一個人的善意、信任和偏愛；得到這種 favor，就意味著受到特別的認可或照顧。","examples":[{"en":"The young adviser quickly won the mayor’s favor.","zh":"這位年輕顧問很快贏得了市長的好感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ambitious courtier hoped to win the queen's favor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/favor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-417127d94df47e08","term":"favor","forms":["favor","favors","favoring","favored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偏愛；看重","explanation":"指對某人或某事物抱有特別好感，因而更喜歡它或優先選擇它。這是名詞“好感、恩寵”轉成動詞後的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"The committee favored the simpler proposal.","zh":"委員會更傾向於採用那份較簡單的提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has always favored quiet places.","zh":"她一直偏愛安靜的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/favor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3576f2205122c75877cc","word":"favorable","forms":["favorable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b2dd1e90659b17d","term":"favorable","forms":["favorable","more favorable","most favorable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"favourable 的美式拼寫","explanation":"favorable 是 favourable 的美式標準拼寫，意思包括“有利的、適宜的、令人滿意的”以及“表示贊成的”。無論說條件有利，還是說某人的態度支援，核心都是事情朝好的方向發展。","examples":[{"en":"The warm weather created favorable conditions for growing tomatoes.","zh":"溫暖的天氣為種植番茄創造了有利條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee gave a favorable response to the proposal.","zh":"委員會對這項提案作出了贊成的回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/favorable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ff3a3c1830a1531cde6","word":"favorite","forms":["favorite"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f533b64bcf321114","term":"favorite","forms":["favorite","more favorite","most favorite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最喜歡的；偏愛的","explanation":"指在多個選擇中被某人特別喜歡、最願意選擇的事物。它就是“放在心上、被優先挑出來”的那個物件。","examples":[{"en":"Blue is my favorite color.","zh":"藍色是我最喜歡的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is my favorite restaurant in town.","zh":"這是我在城裡最喜歡的餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/favorite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b36c28e11f9db16","term":"favorite","forms":["favorite","favorites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最喜歡的人或事物","explanation":"指在一組人或事物中最受某人偏愛的那個，也就是被放在心上、優先選擇的物件。它可以指人、食物、作品、選項等。","examples":[{"en":"That song has become one of my favorites.","zh":"那首歌已經成了我最喜歡的歌曲之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Of all the desserts, this one is my favorite.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/favorite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4af4e217c06a9b00b977","word":"fax","forms":["fax"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39aea56db61ce210","term":"fax","forms":["fax","faxes","faxxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳真機","explanation":"fax 可以指傳送和接收傳真檔案的裝置，也可以順帶指傳真這種通訊方式。","examples":[{"en":"The fax is in the office next door.","zh":"傳真機在隔壁辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our fax jams whenever someone feeds in several pages together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59183324952768a7","term":"fax","forms":["fax","faxes","faxxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳真檔案","explanation":"fax 也指已經透過傳真傳送、或由傳真機接收並列印出來的檔案。","examples":[{"en":"I received the contract by fax this morning.","zh":"我今天早上透過傳真收到了合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fax confirming the reservation arrived this morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d447eadd4f408b88","term":"fax","forms":["fax","faxes","faxxes","faxing","faxxing","faxed","faxxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳真傳送","explanation":"作動詞時，fax 就是把檔案透過傳真機傳送給某人或某機構；它把“傳送傳真”這個動作壓縮成一個詞。","examples":[{"en":"Please fax the signed form to this number.","zh":"請把簽好字的表格傳真到這個號碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The receptionist faxed our booking details to the remote office.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58d54e7c7553ce1fd758","word":"fear","forms":["fear"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a96507fcbfd7564","term":"fear","forms":["fear","fears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恐懼","explanation":"fear 是面對真實或想象中的危險、威脅時產生的強烈不安情緒；它可以是當下的害怕，也可以是對未來壞結果的擔憂。","examples":[{"en":"Fear spread through the village when the fire came closer.","zh":"大火逼近時，恐懼在村子裡蔓延開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke calmly, although fear was growing inside her.","zh":"雖然內心的恐懼越來越強烈，她說話仍然很平靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39f2f16d411be1c4","term":"fear","forms":["fear","fears","fearing","feared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"害怕；擔心會發生","explanation":"fear 某人或某事，表示把它看成危險、威脅，或擔心它會帶來壞結果；fear 後面也可接一個說明擔憂內容的從句。","examples":[{"en":"Many residents fear that the storm will destroy their homes.","zh":"許多居民擔心暴風雨會毀掉他們的家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fears the dog because it has bitten someone before.","zh":"她害怕那條狗，因為它以前咬過人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-331b049e72fbf94f8b7c","word":"fearful","forms":["fearful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-703cdaf2703a043b","term":"fearful","forms":["fearful","more fearful","most fearful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人害怕的","explanation":"恐懼充滿了某個場面、聲音或事物，所以它會讓人感到害怕。這個義項強調“引起恐懼”，不是說事物自己感到害怕。","examples":[{"en":"The storm made a fearful noise all night.","zh":"暴風雨整晚都發出令人害怕的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They faced a fearful danger in the dark forest.","zh":"他們在黑暗的森林裡遇到了可怕的危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fearful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63d2152392499e6a","term":"fearful","forms":["fearful","more fearful","most fearful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"膽小的；容易害怕的","explanation":"恐懼容易充滿一個人的內心，因此這個人總是擔心、退縮或容易被嚇到。它說的是一種傾向或性格，不一定表示此刻已經受驚。","examples":[{"en":"The fearful child held his father's hand tightly.","zh":"那個膽小的孩子緊緊抓住父親的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fearful puppy hid behind the sofa.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fearful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-208a1228bf9d0e8da86e","word":"feasible","forms":["feasible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d994a78315a6fe1f","term":"feasible","forms":["feasible","more feasible","most feasible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可行的；做得到的","explanation":"指某件事不只是理論上可能，而且在現實的時間、資源或條件下確實有機會完成。它常用來說明一個計劃或方案“走得通”。","examples":[{"en":"The committee considered the proposal feasible after the costs were reduced.","zh":"費用降低後，委員會認為這個提議是可行的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is it feasible to finish the repairs before winter?","zh":"在冬天到來前完成維修可行嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feasible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d8dec1a06b9459fef2f","word":"feast","forms":["feast"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1670d4103ccf1052","term":"feast","forms":["feast","feasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盛宴；豐盛大餐","explanation":"feast 是為慶祝某件事而準備的豐盛大餐，通常比普通的一頓飯更隆重，賓客也常常較多。","examples":[{"en":"They prepared a feast to celebrate their daughter's graduation.","zh":"他們準備了一桌盛宴來慶祝女兒畢業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the ceremony, the guests sat down to a feast.","zh":"儀式結束後，賓客們坐下來享用盛宴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8c50ae4dc8a4c86","term":"feast","forms":["feast","feasts","feasting","feasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"享用盛宴","explanation":"feast 作動詞時，可以表示像參加盛宴一樣盡情吃喝，尤其強調食物豐盛、享受充分。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, we feasted on roast chicken and fresh bread.","zh":"長途徒步後，我們盡情享用了烤雞和新鮮麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children feasted on the desserts at the party.","zh":"孩子們在聚會上大吃各種甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b52115ea553c55b7f70c","word":"feather","forms":["feather"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9848d1a302d3319f","term":"feather","forms":["feather","feathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羽毛","explanation":"鳥身上生長的輕而有分枝的結構，用於飛行、游泳、保護或展示。","examples":[{"en":"A white feather fell from the bird.","zh":"一根白色的羽毛從鳥身上掉了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bird spread its feathers in the sun.","zh":"那隻鳥在陽光下展開了羽毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ad562319767157087dd","word":"feature","forms":["feature"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-591d67cc8df5d82a","term":"feature","forms":["feature","features"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要專案；主要內容","explanation":"指某件事中被特別看重、佔主要位置的一項內容或事項，是“突出部分”這一核心概念的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Safety is a key feature of the new design.","zh":"安全性是新設計的一項主要特點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden's best feature is its quiet pond.","zh":"這個花園最突出的部分是那座安靜的池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91647543df2e763b","term":"feature","forms":["feature","features"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面部特徵","explanation":"指眼睛、鼻子、嘴等構成面部外觀的部分；這些是臉上最容易被辨認的突出部分。","examples":[{"en":"Her delicate features made her easy to recognize.","zh":"她精緻的面部特徵讓人很容易認出她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sketch captures her delicate facial features.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9e83d2127eeed62","term":"feature","forms":["feature","features"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軟體功能","explanation":"指軟體、裝置或系統提供的一項有用能力，也就是產品中被設計出來、可以使用的突出部分。","examples":[{"en":"The latest update adds a useful search feature.","zh":"最新更新增加了一項實用的搜尋功能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This feature lets users share files securely.","zh":"這個功能可以讓使用者安全地共享檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e289c8fdd1875cc6","term":"feature","forms":["feature","features"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顯著特徵；特色","explanation":"指景觀、圖畫、文章、條約等事物中具有辨識度的構造、性質或突出特點，是“顯眼部分”這一核心概念最廣的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The river is the most striking feature of the landscape.","zh":"這條河是這片景觀中最醒目的特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A winding staircase is the house's most striking feature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7dae6e638fede12f","term":"feature","forms":["feature","features","featuring","featured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"以……出演；包含","explanation":"表示作品、節目或活動安排某人出演，或把某項內容作為突出組成部分包含進去。","examples":[{"en":"The film features two well-known comedians.","zh":"這部電影由兩位知名喜劇演員出演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The menu features fresh vegetables from nearby farms.","zh":"這份選單主打附近農場供應的新鮮蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b74e6b8e7391a61cba6b","word":"federal","forms":["federal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a8eb11e12acc42c9","term":"federal","forms":["federal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聯邦中央政府的","explanation":"指聯邦制國家中全國性的中央政府層級，與州、省、縣、市或城鎮等地方層級相對。","examples":[{"en":"Federal funds helped repair the old bridge.","zh":"聯邦政府的資金幫助修復了那座舊橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Federal funding helped rebuild the damaged highway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/federal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b80cdaae9b322bba2a38","word":"fee","forms":["fee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2091b36df6d956d","term":"fee","forms":["fee","fees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"權利或手續費用","explanation":"指為了獲得某項權利、許可、入場資格或使用機會而支付的錢，例如入場費、牌照費或啟用費。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small admission fee for the museum.","zh":"這家博物館收取一小筆入場費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You must pay the license fee before using the equipment.","zh":"你必須先支付許可證費用，才能使用這臺裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aab9dce833849bf6","term":"fee","forms":["fee","fees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專業服務費","explanation":"指律師、顧問、會計師等專業人士因提供專業服務而收取的錢。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer explained her fees before taking the case.","zh":"律師在接手這個案子前說明了她的服務費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our consulting fee includes the final report.","zh":"我們的諮詢費包括最終報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81362274717173b4ea1b","word":"feeble","forms":["feeble"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32134a65747e0711","term":"feeble","forms":["feeble","feebler","feeblest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體虛弱的","explanation":"指人或身體缺乏體力，顯得虛弱、衰弱，常用於年老、生病或體能很差的情況。","examples":[{"en":"The old man looked feeble, but he still walked to the market every morning.","zh":"那位老人看起來很虛弱，但他仍然每天早晨走路去市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the illness, she was too feeble to lift the box.","zh":"生病後，她虛弱得連那個箱子都搬不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feeble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5aef6bef89537914","term":"feeble","forms":["feeble","feebler","feeblest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"微弱無力的；無效的","explanation":"把“沒力氣”的概念用於非身體物件：聲音、努力、行動、理由或藉口缺少力度，因此效果很差或沒有說服力。","examples":[{"en":"His apology sounded feeble and did not convince anyone.","zh":"他的道歉聽起來很無力，沒能說服任何人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He offered a feeble excuse for missing the deadline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feeble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8bc2586cdd87cd6f970","word":"feed","forms":["feed"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ad42e8b2fd258de","term":"feed","forms":["feed","feeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物飼料","explanation":"指專門給動物，尤其是食草動物吃的食物。它把“喂”這個動作中的食物單獨拿出來，成為可供動物食用的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer stores the feed in a dry shed.","zh":"農夫把飼料存放在乾燥的棚子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Drought forced the ranchers to buy expensive supplementary feed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51762e5dc9397a25","term":"feed","forms":["feed","feeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續供應的內容或訊號","explanation":"指不斷送來的資訊、畫面、聲音或訊號；重點不在某一條內容，而在持續輸入的通道。","examples":[{"en":"The news channel received a live feed from the scene.","zh":"新聞頻道收到了現場的實時訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camera feed disappeared during the storm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e20bb71d0be983e","term":"feed","forms":["feed","feeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網站內容流","explanation":"指網站或部落格按時間不斷彙集、推送新內容的列表；使用者訂閱後，可以在一個地方看到更新。","examples":[{"en":"I subscribed to the museum's feed to hear about new exhibitions.","zh":"我訂閱了博物館的內容流，以便了解新的展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her feed is full of photographs of rescue dogs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55ed8f3fe8b57fff","term":"feed","forms":["feed","feeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社交媒體資訊流","explanation":"指社交媒體中按順序顯示、不斷更新的帖子和其他內容組成的資訊流；向下滾動通常會看到更早的內容。","examples":[{"en":"A photo from our trip appeared in my feed.","zh":"我們旅行時拍的一張照片出現在我的資訊流裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I muted that account to keep advertisements out of my feed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd33cf87c267e378","term":"feed","forms":["feed","feeds","feeding","fed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……餵食","explanation":"指主動給人、動物或其他生物食物吃，是 feed 最基本的“把食物送過去”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"Please feed the cat before you leave.","zh":"你走之前請給貓餵食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse fed the baby a little soup.","zh":"護士給嬰兒餵了一點湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4084900b46a2717b","term":"feed","forms":["feed","feeds","feeding","fed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取食；以……為食","explanation":"指動物自己吃東西，強調它從某種食物或獵物那裡取得營養，而不是有人把食物遞給它。","examples":[{"en":"These birds feed on insects and small seeds.","zh":"這些鳥以昆蟲和小種子為食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The larvae feed on decaying wood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1503ce4f46e6b203","term":"feed","forms":["feed","feeds","feeding","fed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把材料送入機器","explanation":"指把紙張、材料或物體送進機器，讓機器繼續加工；這裡仍然是“把東西送入通道”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Feed the card slowly into the reader.","zh":"把卡片慢慢送入讀取器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Feed one sheet at a time into the scanner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59bda3f8ee98128d5435","word":"feedback","forms":["feedback"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aba2aafa11fa0ae6","term":"feedback","forms":["feedback","feedbacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反饋意見；評價","explanation":"指別人對某項工作、活動或其結果提出的評價、建議和反應，重點是這些資訊可以幫助你改進下一步。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gave us useful feedback on our presentations.","zh":"老師對我們的演講提出了有用的反饋意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer welcomed feedback on her first sketches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23e17f5eb58c27cb","term":"feedback","forms":["feedback","feedbacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"回饋訊號","explanation":"在控制論和工程中，指輸出的一部分被送回輸入端的訊號；系統據此調整或改變自己的執行狀態，就像把結果重新送回過程。","examples":[{"en":"The machine uses feedback to keep the temperature stable.","zh":"這臺機器利用反饋訊號保持溫度穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The controller uses sensor feedback to adjust speed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feedback","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-116c49130f14f514b810","word":"feel","forms":["feel"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8748c83985aeb18","term":"feel","forms":["feel","feels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觸感","explanation":"指物體被摸到時給人的具體感覺，例如粗糙、光滑、柔軟或堅硬。它是“用手摸到的感覺”，也是其他抽象意義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"I like the soft feel of this sweater.","zh":"我喜歡這件毛衣柔軟的觸感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stone has a smooth, cool feel.","zh":"這塊石頭摸起來光滑而冰涼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad15dfa93ea71495","term":"feel","forms":["feel","feels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"模糊印象","explanation":"指人透過接觸環境、觀察情況或親身體驗形成的整體印象。這種印象通常說不出精確依據，卻能幫助人判斷某個地方或局面的特點。","examples":[{"en":"Spend a few days here to get a feel for the neighborhood.","zh":"在這裡待幾天，熟悉一下這個社群的氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The quiet streets give the town a friendly feel.","zh":"安靜的街道讓這座城鎮給人一種友好的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-467503e354f0040d","term":"feel","forms":["feel","feels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直覺和把握","explanation":"指不完全依靠規則或明確計算，而是憑經驗直接把握某種活動、藝術或情境的能力。它仍然來自“摸到門道”的核心形象，但已經變成一種穩定的直覺。","examples":[{"en":"She has a natural feel for rhythm.","zh":"她對節奏有一種天生的直覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a good feel for what customers want.","zh":"他很能憑直覺把握顧客想要什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02b51abc99c634f0","term":"feel","forms":["feel","feels","feeling","felt","feelest","feltst","feltest","feeleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用觸覺感知","explanation":"指用身體接觸來察覺某物，例如摸到脈搏、溫度或形狀。這是 feel 最具體的動詞意義，其他許多意義都從這裡引申出來。","examples":[{"en":"I could feel the baby's heartbeat under my fingers.","zh":"我能感覺到手指下嬰兒的心跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt the wall carefully in the dark.","zh":"她在黑暗中小心地摸著牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cf002ca288e1543","term":"feel","forms":["feel","feels","feeling","felt","feelest","feltst","feltest","feeleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感受到情緒","explanation":"指從言語、行為或作品中感受到情緒，也可以表示自己對某件事有強烈的情感態度。這裡的“感受”已經從皮膚上的觸覺擴充套件到了內心。","examples":[{"en":"I can feel the sadness in her voice.","zh":"我能感受到她聲音裡的悲傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people feel strongly about protecting the river.","zh":"許多人強烈支援保護這條河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73f4ec92f5d3d214","term":"feel","forms":["feel","feels","feeling","felt","feelest","feltst","feltest","feeleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感覺上像","explanation":"指某物給人的整體感覺呈現為某種性質或樣子，常用於比較外觀與實際觸感、質地或氛圍。它仍然保留“接觸後得到印象”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"This fabric feels like silk but costs much less.","zh":"這種布料摸起來像絲綢，但便宜得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room feels warmer with the curtains open.","zh":"窗簾拉開後，這個房間感覺暖和多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e8abffb973c275e041e","word":"feeling","forms":["feeling"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9a83eb94bd8d617","term":"feeling","forms":["feeling","feelings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情緒；感受","explanation":"指心裡產生的情緒或對某件事的整體感受，例如害怕、安心或不安。","examples":[{"en":"The empty street gave me a feeling of unease.","zh":"那條空蕩蕩的街道讓我感到不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had a strong feeling that someone was watching us.","zh":"我強烈感覺有人在看著我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feeling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-643845c222927ef3","term":"feeling","forms":["feeling","feelings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情緒狀態；感情","explanation":"複數 feelings 指一個人的內心狀態，尤其是受到傷害、安慰或尊重時的情緒和感情。","examples":[{"en":"Please be careful with her feelings when you discuss the mistake.","zh":"你討論這個錯誤時，請顧及她的感受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was upset, but I did not want to hurt his feelings.","zh":"我很難過，但不想傷害他的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feeling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a57c4e7933ced6b6d227","word":"fellow","forms":["fellow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25f627325efec50b","term":"fellow","forms":["fellow","fellows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同伴；夥伴","explanation":"指和自己一起行動、共同經歷某件事的人，重點是雙方處在同一個圈子裡並有陪伴或合作關係。它既可以指朋友，也可以只表示同行者，不一定關係親密。","examples":[{"en":"She traveled with a fellow from her language class.","zh":"她和語言班的一位同伴一起旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two fellows helped each other carry the boxes.","zh":"這兩個夥伴互相幫忙搬箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fellow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-864cdc8944a3df73","term":"fellow","forms":["fellow","fellows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學術機構成員；研究員","explanation":"大寫為 Fellow 時，指學院、大學或專業團體中經過選拔的成員、研究員或資助者，表示正式加入某個學術或專業圈子。具體職責會因機構而不同。","examples":[{"en":"She was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society.","zh":"她當選為皇家學會會員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university appointed him a research Fellow.","zh":"這所大學任命他為研究員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fellow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-861d00478c693234","term":"fellow","forms":["fellow","fellows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男人；傢伙","explanation":"非正式地指一個男人，中文裡可根據語氣譯成“夥計、傢伙、老兄”或“某個男的”。它有時只是隨意稱呼，有時會因為修飾詞而帶一點親暱、調侃或責備。","examples":[{"en":"I met a friendly fellow at the station who gave me directions.","zh":"我在車站遇到一位友善的老兄，他給我指了路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come on, old fellow, we still have work to do.","zh":"好了，老夥計，我們還有工作要做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fellow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-946510653218f787","term":"fellow","forms":["fellow","fellows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同事；合作伙伴","explanation":"指與自己共同工作、合作或承擔同一任務的人，核心仍是和自己處在同一個工作或行動圈子裡。這個義項在現代英語中多由 colleague 或 partner 表達，但在固定或歷史語境中仍可能見到。","examples":[{"en":"He discussed the problem with a fellow worker before making a decision.","zh":"他在作決定前和一位同事討論了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two fellows worked together on the same project.","zh":"這兩位合作伙伴一起完成了同一個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fellow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f165139a8c2894a47ae","word":"female","forms":["female"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f52d96efee31a5e0","term":"female","forms":["female","femaler","more female","femalest","most female"],"pos":"adj","zh":"女性的；雌性的","explanation":"指屬於通常能夠產生卵細胞的性別，或通常與這一性別相關的性別身份。它既可修飾人，也可修飾動物等生物。","examples":[{"en":"The female bird stayed near the nest.","zh":"那隻雌鳥待在巢附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study included both male and female athletes.","zh":"這項研究包括男性和女性運動員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/female","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7501b091096867a5","term":"female","forms":["female","femaler","more female","femalest","most female"],"pos":"adj","zh":"女性的；雌性特徵的","explanation":"指通常被認為與女性或雌性有關的外貌、行為、活動或其他特徵；重點不是身份本身，而是“具有這類特徵”。","examples":[{"en":"The insect has distinctive female coloration.","zh":"這種昆蟲有明顯的雌性體色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The costume was designed for a female audience.","zh":"這套服裝是為女性觀眾設計的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/female","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65d14cdab71175b9","term":"female","forms":["female","females"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女性；雌性個體","explanation":"指屬於女性或雌性的一方，可以指人，也可以指動物等生物。談論人時，它是一個帶有分類色彩的名詞，日常語境通常用 woman 指成年女性。","examples":[{"en":"The female stayed close to her young.","zh":"那隻雌性動物待在幼崽身邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey compared responses from males and females.","zh":"這項調查比較了男性和女性的回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/female","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-584a6898b0a5a6131f4e","word":"feminine","forms":["feminine"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39361fb4d34b8740","term":"feminine","forms":["feminine","more feminine","most feminine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"女性相關的","explanation":"表示與女性或女性身份有關，是最寬泛、最常用的一層意思，可以修飾名字、服裝、聲音、風格等。","examples":[{"en":"The brand uses feminine colors and delicate details.","zh":"這個品牌採用女性風格的色彩和精緻的細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her handwriting has a distinctly feminine style.","zh":"她的字跡有一種明顯的女性風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feminine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87346eb282352fda74ad","word":"fence","forms":["fence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93890072393e5104","term":"fence","forms":["fence","fences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圍欄；柵欄","explanation":"用來分隔兩塊土地、圍住房屋或劃出範圍的人工屏障，就是fence。它通常由木頭、金屬等材料製成，比牆更強調“圍起來”而不一定完全擋住視線。","examples":[{"en":"We put a new fence around the garden.","zh":"我們在花園四周裝了一道新圍欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog slipped through a gap in the fence.","zh":"那條狗從圍欄的縫隙裡鑽了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9087d0b20d80d3e12bc","word":"ferry","forms":["ferry"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1581e99865fca27","term":"ferry","forms":["ferry","ferries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"渡船","explanation":"指按固定路線在水面兩岸之間往返、運送乘客、車輛或貨物的船。記住“來回擺渡的船”這個核心畫面即可。","examples":[{"en":"We took the ferry across the river with our bicycles.","zh":"我們帶著腳踏車乘渡船過了河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The last ferry leaves the island at ten.","zh":"最後一班渡船十點離開這個島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ferry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be86797186a7fa8f","term":"ferry","forms":["ferry","ferries","ferrying","ferried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"運送；帶到","explanation":"指把人或物從一個地方運到另一個地方，核心仍是“把物件帶過去”。不一定真的使用渡船，也可以泛指有組織的接送或運輸。","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers ferried the families to safety after the flood.","zh":"洪水過後，志願者把這些家庭運送到了安全處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A shuttle bus ferries guests from the hotel to the airport.","zh":"接駁車把客人從酒店運送到機場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ferry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2760077b45c8e4a3","term":"ferry","forms":["ferry","ferries","ferrying","ferried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用船渡過","explanation":"指乘船或靠渡船把人、車輛或貨物送過河流、海峽等水面。這個義項最直接地保留了“在兩岸之間擺渡”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The boat ferried the workers across the narrow channel.","zh":"這艘船把工人送過了狹窄的海峽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They ferry cars from the mainland to the island every day.","zh":"他們每天把汽車從大陸運到島上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ferry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bcc370ad4e87a561544c","word":"fertile","forms":["fertile"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a27859cb17f78c76","term":"fertile","forms":["fertile","more fertile","most fertile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"土地肥沃；高產","explanation":"形容土地、土壤等適合生長植物，能夠產出大量莊稼或其他農作物。這裡的重點是“產出能力強”，不只是土壤本身含有養分。","examples":[{"en":"The river valley has fertile soil and produces wheat every year.","zh":"這條河谷土壤肥沃，每年都出產小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers moved to the fertile plain in search of better harvests.","zh":"農民們搬到肥沃的平原，尋找更好的收成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fertile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bf9ba2857dc6363","term":"fertile","forms":["fertile","more fertile","most fertile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"想象力豐富；創意多","explanation":"形容想象力、思想或頭腦能夠不斷產生新想法，強調創意和構思源源不斷。它把土地豐產的形象轉用於抽象事物：不是“想象得真實”，而是“能產出很多想法”。","examples":[{"en":"Her fertile imagination turned a simple walk into a thrilling story.","zh":"她豐富的想象力把一次普通的散步變成了驚險的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His fertile imagination supplied a new story every evening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fertile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d053f74eb1b74874efb1","word":"fertility","forms":["fertility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e298f04ffeffb33","term":"fertility","forms":["fertility","fertilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肥沃度；生育能力","explanation":"指土地、土壤或生物孕育和產生新生命的能力。土地的fertility高，就能更好地長出作物；談生物時，則指繁殖能力強。","examples":[{"en":"Adding compost can improve the fertility of poor soil.","zh":"加入堆肥可以提高貧瘠土壤的肥力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study examined how age affects female fertility.","zh":"這項研究考察了年齡如何影響女性的生育能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fertility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaaa25b4c7536434","term":"fertility","forms":["fertility","fertilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人口出生率","explanation":"指一個人口或地區在一定時期內出生得多不多，通常按每一千人每年的活產數來統計。這裡的“生出多少”從土地的產出能力擴充套件成了整個社會的出生水平。","examples":[{"en":"The region's fertility rose slightly after the policy was introduced.","zh":"這項政策實施後，該地區的出生率略有上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study compares fertility across three generations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fertility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee3a336aa6fb6f0d259c","word":"fertilizer","forms":["fertilizer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-622be5452701700c","term":"fertilizer","forms":["fertilizer","fertilizers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天然肥料","explanation":"指天然形成或來源於天然材料、用來改善土壤並幫助植物生長的物質，例如來自農場或其他自然來源的肥料；核心意思就是給土地補充營養。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer spread fertilizer across the fields before planting.","zh":"農民在播種前把肥料撒遍了田地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Compost can be used as a natural fertilizer for vegetables.","zh":"堆肥可以用作蔬菜的天然肥料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fertilizer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4180dc9188464bb2","term":"fertilizer","forms":["fertilizer","fertilizers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化學肥料","explanation":"指專門製成、具有施肥作用的化學化合物；它不是天然材料本身，但能像天然肥料一樣為土壤或植物提供所需作用。","examples":[{"en":"The company developed a fertilizer that releases nutrients slowly.","zh":"這家公司開發了一種能緩慢釋放養分的化學肥料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runoff contained fertilizer from nearby fields.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fertilizer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ffaaf97add883ad7d02","word":"festival","forms":["festival"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ea9705f05a0a9d1","term":"festival","forms":["festival","festivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主題節慶活動；節展","explanation":"指圍繞音樂、電影、藝術、食物等主題舉辦的特別活動，往往持續數天，包含一系列演出、展覽或比賽；這是現代最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the weekend at a film festival in the city.","zh":"我們在城裡的一場電影節上度過了週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city hosts a documentary film festival each spring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/festival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cca9c7216da39db6","term":"festival","forms":["festival","festivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"節日；節慶日","explanation":"指為宗教、傳統或特定紀念日而慶祝的節日，重點在“過節的日子”或節慶本身，而不一定是現代意義上的大型主題活動。","examples":[{"en":"The town holds a festival every spring to celebrate the harvest.","zh":"這個城鎮每年春天都會舉行慶祝豐收的節慶活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lanterns fill the streets during the spring festival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/festival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e7d3799ecc09f5cbc446","word":"fetch","forms":["fetch"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35f547155223fe6a","term":"fetch","forms":["fetch","fetches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"取回；取來","explanation":"指去遠處把某物帶回來這一動作，既可以按字面理解，也可以用於抽象的“調取、取來”。","examples":[{"en":"The fetch of fresh water took nearly an hour.","zh":"取回淡水花了將近一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog enjoyed a game of fetch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fetch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-746137ff104ae9de","term":"fetch","forms":["fetch","fetches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"取回遊戲","explanation":"指人把物品扔出去、狗跑去把它叼回來的一種遊戲，也可泛指這種活動本身。","examples":[{"en":"The children played fetch with the dog in the yard.","zh":"孩子們在院子裡和狗玩取回遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our dog never tires of playing fetch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fetch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6b6ce58c4ad72e6","term":"fetch","forms":["fetch","fetches","fetching","fetched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取來；取回","explanation":"指到別處取得某物並帶回來，常用於請求別人去拿東西，也可以指狗把扔出的物品叼回來。","examples":[{"en":"Could you fetch me a glass of water?","zh":"你能幫我取一杯水來嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog fetched the ball and dropped it at my feet.","zh":"那隻狗把球叼了回來，放在我的腳邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fetch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e44a1c45388c81c1a4b","word":"fever","forms":["fever"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4d41c89a18fd632","term":"fever","forms":["fever","fevers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發燒；發熱","explanation":"指人的體溫高於正常水平，通常是疾病引起的發熱狀態。它強調身體“燒起來”，不一定等同於某一種具體疾病。","examples":[{"en":"I have a fever and need to rest.","zh":"我發燒了，需要休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her fever finally went down during the night.","zh":"她的燒終於在夜裡退了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e017c7c072602625","term":"fever","forms":["fever","fevers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發熱性疾病","explanation":"指以發熱為特徵的某種疾病，通常出現在疾病名稱或固定搭配中，而不是單獨泛指所有發燒。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor tested her for scarlet fever.","zh":"醫生給她做了猩紅熱檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old record lists her death as a fever.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa95e5080882f52bd40c","word":"few","forms":["few"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-846815507ad06a17","term":"few","forms":["few","fewer","less","fewest","least"],"pos":"det","zh":"一些，但不多","explanation":"放在可數名詞複數前，表示有一小部分，但數量不多，通常語氣比單獨的 few 更中性。","examples":[{"en":"I have a few questions about the plan.","zh":"我對這個計劃有幾個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stayed there for a few days.","zh":"我們在那裡待了幾天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/few","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-601aa5923044ba42","term":"few","forms":["few","fewer","less","fewest","least"],"pos":"det","zh":"很少，沒幾個","explanation":"表示數量少，常常帶有和預期或另一數量相比“少得明顯”的意味；它仍然修飾可數名詞複數。","examples":[{"en":"Few people understood the warning.","zh":"很少有人聽懂了這個警告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Very few students finished the test early.","zh":"很少有學生提前完成了考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/few","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6496ede18bcb3166","term":"few","forms":["few"],"pos":"pron","zh":"少數人或事物","explanation":"不帶名詞時，few 指前文語境中的少數人或少數事物，核心仍是“數量很少”。","examples":[{"en":"Many wanted to join, but few were accepted.","zh":"很多人想加入，但只有少數人被接受了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Few knew the truth at the time.","zh":"當時很少有人知道真相。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/few","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77c3e615d715acdbb049","word":"fiber","forms":["fiber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4958014f0edf8e60","term":"fiber","forms":["fiber","fibers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一根纖維","explanation":"指材料中一根細長、通常近似圓截面的絲狀部分，許多這樣的 fiber 可以擰在一起形成線。","examples":[{"en":"A single red fiber was caught on the edge of the bag.","zh":"一根紅色纖維掛在包的邊緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The test found a cotton fiber on the jacket.","zh":"檢測在夾克上發現了一根棉纖維。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-303d5a27225b8ea9","term":"fiber","forms":["fiber","fibers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膳食纖維","explanation":"指食物中不容易被人體消化、但有助於正常消化和排便的纖維成分，蔬菜、水果和全穀物都是常見來源。","examples":[{"en":"Beans and whole grains are excellent sources of fiber.","zh":"豆類和全穀物是很好的膳食纖維來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to eat more fiber if your meals contain few vegetables.","zh":"如果你的飯菜蔬菜很少，儘量多攝入一些膳食纖維。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6aae12031a990478","term":"fiber","forms":["fiber","fibers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅韌和意志力","explanation":"這是從“纖維不容易斷”的形象發展出的比喻義，指人在困難或考驗中保持勇氣、原則和堅持的內在力量。","examples":[{"en":"The long recovery was a test of her fiber.","zh":"漫長的康復過程考驗了她的堅韌意志。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He showed real fiber when the project failed.","zh":"專案失敗時，他表現出了真正的堅韌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d778b673710a7c96d31c","word":"fiction","forms":["fiction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cb6dc6273b4ffe4","term":"fiction","forms":["fiction","fictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"虛構文學","explanation":"指不是在陳述真實事實、而是憑想象創作出來的文學作品，通常包括小說等以敘事為主的作品；重點在於“創作出來的故事”，不一定帶有欺騙意味。","examples":[{"en":"I read a lot of fiction before going to bed.","zh":"我睡前常讀很多虛構文學作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel is a work of fiction, not a memoir.","zh":"這部小說是虛構作品，不是回憶錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d485556132c505d","term":"fiction","forms":["fiction","fictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"編造的說法","explanation":"指沒有真實依據的口頭或書面敘述，常帶有隱瞞、欺騙或為自己辯解的意味；這裡虛構的是“說法”，而不一定是文學作品。","examples":[{"en":"The report was full of fictions designed to hide the truth.","zh":"這份報告充滿了為了掩蓋真相而編造的說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His heroic account was mostly fiction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0d2856b74d0df05b9d4","word":"field","forms":["field"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21ceb9b4ec8190ae","term":"field","forms":["field","fields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"田野；開闊地","explanation":"field 是沒有森林、城市或建築物遮滿的開闊土地，通常讓人聯想到鄉間的一片地。它是“某種活動發生在一塊空間裡”這一核心形象的起點。","examples":[{"en":"We walked across the field to reach the village.","zh":"我們穿過田野去村子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several wildflowers were growing in the field.","zh":"田野里長著幾種野花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70316608973b8091","term":"field","forms":["field","fields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農田；牧場","explanation":"field 也可以是圍起來種莊稼或放牲畜的一片地；牛在裡面吃草的地方同樣可以叫 field。","examples":[{"en":"The cows are grazing in the field behind the house.","zh":"牛正在房子後面的田地裡吃草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They planted corn in the field this spring.","zh":"他們今年春天在這塊田裡種了玉米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a29f095ea854740","term":"field","forms":["field","fields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽場地","explanation":"比賽場地也是一塊被劃出來、讓運動員競爭的 field；因此 field 可從自然土地延伸到體育活動的空間。","examples":[{"en":"The players ran onto the field before the match began.","zh":"比賽開始前，球員們跑上了場地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans cheered when the captain returned to the field.","zh":"隊長回到場上時，球迷們歡呼起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0eb0109f31b701a019a","word":"fierce","forms":["fierce"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16f108ff28dc77d9","term":"fierce","forms":["fierce","fiercer","more fierce","fiercest","most fierce"],"pos":"adj","zh":"猛烈的；兇猛的","explanation":"指力量或行為強到危險、殘酷或難以抵擋，常形容暴風雨、戰鬥、攻擊等。核心畫面就是“未被馴服的力量猛烈衝來”。","examples":[{"en":"A fierce storm damaged several houses along the coast.","zh":"一場猛烈的暴風雨損壞了海岸邊的幾所房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two teams fought a fierce battle for the final place.","zh":"兩支隊伍為最後一個名額展開了激烈的爭奪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fierce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35d25316c9a409eb","term":"fierce","forms":["fierce","fiercer","more fierce","fiercest","most fierce"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅決有力的；拼命的","explanation":"指人不是被動地承受，而是用很強的決心和能量去做某事，例如奮力爭取、強烈反對或努力逃脫。這裡的“兇猛”從外在攻擊力轉成了行動上的衝勁。","examples":[{"en":"She made a fierce effort to finish the project on time.","zh":"她拼盡全力，爭取按時完成專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He faced fierce opposition from his former allies.","zh":"他遭到了前盟友的強烈反對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fierce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23b6a8f399dd913a23fa","word":"fight","forms":["fight"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43c49efef437f2a2","term":"fight","forms":["fight","fights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"打鬥；衝突","explanation":"指發生在某個時間和地點的一次打鬥或衝突，通常涉及身體上的攻擊，也可以泛指一場激烈爭鬥。","examples":[{"en":"The police arrived just after the fight ended.","zh":"警察在打鬥剛結束後趕到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They got into a fight outside the restaurant.","zh":"他們在餐館外打了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a00473cf302c80b","term":"fight","forms":["fight","fights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鬥爭；對抗","explanation":"把身體上的對抗延伸到思想、利益或力量之間的衝突，表示為了保護、改變或爭取某事而持續抗爭。","examples":[{"en":"She joined the fight for equal education.","zh":"她加入了爭取教育平等的鬥爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is in a fight to stay in the league.","zh":"這支隊伍正在為留在聯賽中而奮力拼搏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dabcb3ee4c7dfeb9","term":"fight","forms":["fight","fights","fighting","fought","foughten","fightest","foughtest","fighteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與某人或某方戰鬥","explanation":"指主動與人、軍隊或其他對手進行身體上的戰鬥；核心畫面就是迎著對手上前對抗。","examples":[{"en":"My grandfather fought the enemy during the war.","zh":"我祖父在戰爭期間與敵人作戰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers fought bravely to defend the town.","zh":"士兵們英勇作戰，保衛這座城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b73ddb1ae7203897","term":"fight","forms":["fight","fights","fighting","fought","foughten","fightest","foughtest","fighteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為某事奮鬥","explanation":"把迎戰對手的動作用於抽象目標，表示努力爭取成功、權利、機會或政治目標。","examples":[{"en":"They are fighting for better working conditions.","zh":"他們正在爭取更好的工作條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fought to keep her small business open.","zh":"她努力爭取讓自己的小企業繼續營業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-794abe4382b236102732","word":"fighter","forms":["fighter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6304ef61583bb5e0","term":"fighter","forms":["fighter","fighters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戰鬥者","explanation":"指實際參加戰鬥、與敵人交手的人，是 fighter 最直接、最基礎的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The fighters moved through the forest before dawn.","zh":"戰鬥人員在黎明前穿過了森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every fighter needs courage and discipline.","zh":"每個戰鬥者都需要勇氣和紀律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fighter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84289c3c17254cbf","term":"fighter","forms":["fighter","fighters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頑強抗爭的人","explanation":"指面對重病、長期困難或嚴重逆境仍堅持抵抗、不輕易放棄的人，是從“迎戰”這個核心形象自然延伸出來的比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"The doctors say she is a fighter and has a good chance of recovering.","zh":"醫生說她非常頑強，康復的希望很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He remained a fighter throughout his long illness.","zh":"在漫長的病痛中，他始終沒有放棄抗爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fighter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-889393fb69a5b3051884","word":"figure","forms":["figure"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a769dfca0b677fff","term":"figure","forms":["figure","figures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身材","explanation":"指人的身體外形和體態，尤其是整體的身材曲線。這裡的 figure 是人體形成的清晰外在形象。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise helped her maintain a healthy figure.","zh":"經常鍛鍊幫助她保持了健康的身材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dress was designed to flatter the wearer’s figure.","zh":"這條連衣裙的設計能襯托穿著者的身材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/figure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4eaf5470375cc03f","term":"figure","forms":["figure","figures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數字","explanation":"指表示數量的單個數字或數碼，例如 7、0 或電話號碼中的某一位。它是把數量寫成清晰符號的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The answer must be written in figures, not words.","zh":"答案必須用數字書寫，不能用文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature fell to single figures overnight.","zh":"夜間氣溫降到個位數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/figure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-556a593be5739643","term":"figure","forms":["figure","figures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數額","explanation":"指一個具體的數字、數量或金額，尤其用於統計、價格、收入和估計結果。它是已經算出或列出的清晰結果。","examples":[{"en":"The final figure was higher than the original estimate.","zh":"最終數額高於最初的估計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company reported record sales figures this year.","zh":"公司報告稱今年的銷售額創下了紀錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/figure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce317c249b29e6ec","term":"figure","forms":["figure","figures","figuring","figured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄懂","explanation":"經過思考或查詢線索後，把原來不清楚的事情想明白，形成清晰的理解。","examples":[{"en":"I finally figured out why the printer was not working.","zh":"我終於弄明白印表機為什麼不工作了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to figure out how to get home before dark.","zh":"我們得想辦法弄清楚天黑前怎麼回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/figure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b9c358f36f0a31b6ad3","word":"file","forms":["file"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0496ae3b54685eba","term":"file","forms":["file","files"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檔案；資料夾中的材料","explanation":"指把相關檔案、信件或記錄集中整理並儲存起來的一組材料，重點是“歸在一起、以後查詢”。","examples":[{"en":"I found the contract in the client’s file.","zh":"我在客戶的檔案裡找到了合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please add these receipts to the file.","zh":"請把這些收據放進檔案裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f5b23b32ad0cb92","term":"file","forms":["file","files"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電腦檔案","explanation":"指儲存裝置或電腦中以名稱標識的一組資料，例如文件、圖片或程式資料；它仍然保留了“把內容集中儲存起來”的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The report is saved as a PDF file.","zh":"這份報告儲存成了 PDF 檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sent the file to my colleague.","zh":"我把這個檔案發給了同事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb37b2136b532c1d","term":"file","forms":["file","files"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一列；縱隊","explanation":"指人或物一個接一個，或在規則網格中沿同一豎線排列；這和檔案義共享“沿線整理”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers moved in single file along the narrow path.","zh":"徒步者沿著狹窄的小路排成一列前進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoners stood in a single file.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44a1d99c849c8ed5","term":"file","forms":["file","files"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銼刀","explanation":"指表面粗糙的硬金屬工具，用來磨平邊緣、修整形狀或削去材料；可以把它想成沿表面反覆走線的工具。","examples":[{"en":"Use a small file to smooth the sharp edge.","zh":"用一把小銼刀把鋒利的邊緣磨平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kept a metal file in his toolbox.","zh":"他在工具箱裡放著一把金屬銼刀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6daf820814e432b4","term":"file","forms":["file","files","filing","filed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提交官方檔案","explanation":"指把正式檔案交給有關機構，使其進入官方記錄或辦理流程；核心仍是把材料沿著規定的線整理進去。","examples":[{"en":"The company filed its annual report with the regulator.","zh":"這家公司向監管機構提交了年度報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They filed a complaint with the housing authority.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b73a176a78e5748","term":"file","forms":["file","files","filing","filed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"儲存電腦檔案","explanation":"指把資料檔案儲存到磁碟、電腦或其他儲存介質中，使它成為可按名稱找到的檔案。","examples":[{"en":"Remember to file the photos on the external drive.","zh":"記得把照片儲存到外接硬碟上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"File the scanned receipts in the shared folder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b561eb729291a727","term":"file","forms":["file","files","filing","filed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排成一列移動","explanation":"指人們一個接一個地進入、離開或經過某處，就像沿著一根線移動。","examples":[{"en":"The guests filed into the dining room.","zh":"客人們依次走進餐廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students filed quietly into the examination hall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54c65280e63689dc","term":"file","forms":["file","files","filing","filed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用銼刀磨削","explanation":"指用銼刀反覆摩擦材料，使其變平、變薄、成形或去掉鋒利部分；這是名詞“銼刀”直接變成的動詞。","examples":[{"en":"She filed down the rough edge of the shelf.","zh":"她把架子的粗糙邊緣銼平了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"File the sharp edge until it feels smooth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/file","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcd32479a72e55b29a03","word":"fill","forms":["fill"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2bce3931d57d0db3","term":"fill","forms":["fill","fills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"足量；盡情滿足的量","explanation":"指足以滿足需要、甚至超過需要的量，尤其常說吃喝到滿足為止。","examples":[{"en":"After the hike, we had our fill of hot soup.","zh":"徒步後，我們喝了足量的熱湯，喝得很滿足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children had their fill of games before dinner.","zh":"孩子們在晚飯前盡情玩了個夠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f336848e9dd1059a","term":"fill","forms":["fill","fills","filling","filled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝滿；填滿","explanation":"把東西放入容器或空間，使它達到滿的狀態。這是“fill”最核心、最具體的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She filled the glass with cold water.","zh":"她把玻璃杯裝滿了冷水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please fill the box with packing paper.","zh":"請在箱子裡裝滿包裝紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0366f6f913758743","term":"fill","forms":["fill","fills","filling","filled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變滿","explanation":"容器、洞穴或其他空間自行變滿，重點是從空到滿的狀態變化，而不是誰主動裝入東西。","examples":[{"en":"The bucket slowly filled with rain.","zh":"桶裡慢慢裝滿了雨水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bucket filled slowly beneath the dripping tap.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4125ba729fe542fd","term":"fill","forms":["fill","fills","filling","filled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"充滿（情感等）","explanation":"某種情感或感覺在心中逐漸變得滿滿的，例如喜悅、希望或恐懼充滿內心。","examples":[{"en":"Her heart filled with relief when she heard the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息時，她的心裡充滿了寬慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Relief filled her when the missing child appeared.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dfc3376b8266c66e8c24","word":"filter","forms":["filter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e45e0b6d011ca97f","term":"filter","forms":["filter","filters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過濾器；濾網","explanation":"把液體、氣體或其他物質中的雜質分離出來的裝置；重點是讓某些成分透過，同時攔住另一些成分。","examples":[{"en":"The coffee filter kept the grounds out of my cup.","zh":"咖啡濾紙把咖啡渣擋在了杯子外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Replace the air filter every six months.","zh":"每六個月更換一次空氣濾芯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/filter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3e37d25c6ecfe55","term":"filter","forms":["filter","filters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"篩選機制","explanation":"泛指任何能把目標與非目標分開、把不想要的東西攔下來的專案、程式或步驟，例如郵件自動分類規則。","examples":[{"en":"I set up a filter to send newsletters to a separate folder.","zh":"我設定了一個篩選規則，把新聞郵件放進單獨的資料夾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The age filter excludes unsuitable search results.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/filter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7e9db3a6145fc0b","term":"filter","forms":["filter","filters","filtering","filtered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"過濾；篩出","explanation":"把大顆粒、噪聲、資訊或其他不需要的部分篩掉，留下想要的部分；這是“過濾器”這個核心形象對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"This program filters out messages from unknown senders.","zh":"這個程式會篩掉來自未知發件人的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We filtered the water before drinking it.","zh":"我們先把水過濾後再喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/filter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a383bcb77c832a8ff52c","word":"fin","forms":["fin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad825bb7a968bd28","term":"fin","forms":["fin","fins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"魚鰭","explanation":"魚身體兩側或背部的鰭幫助魚推進、轉向和控制遊動方向；這是 fin 最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The fish moved its fins and turned sharply.","zh":"那條魚擺動鰭，猛地轉了個彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fish spread its fins to maintain balance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cba2fd7e28f4ab2","term":"fin","forms":["fin","fins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機垂直安定面","explanation":"飛機機身上細長、豎直的鰭狀結構，用來幫助飛機保持穩定並控制方向；它是魚鰭“幫助定向”作用的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The aircraft fin keeps the plane stable in strong winds.","zh":"飛機的垂直安定面讓飛機在強風中保持穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The aircraft's tall fin carries the airline's emblem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2443630b4620165c8b17","word":"final","forms":["final"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc9ab7bff6329879","term":"final","forms":["final","more final","most final"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最後的；最終的","explanation":"指在一系列事物中排在末尾，或某個過程已經走到終點的。它可以說最後一天、最終版本，也可以說最終解決方案。","examples":[{"en":"Friday is the final day of the school term.","zh":"星期五是本學期的最後一天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We submitted the final version of the report yesterday.","zh":"我們昨天提交了報告的最終版本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/final","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cab16cb3fd89376d","term":"final","forms":["final","more final","most final"],"pos":"adj","zh":"決定性的；不可更改的","explanation":"指某個判斷、決定或結果已經起決定作用，之後通常不會再改變；重點不只是“排在最後”，而是它把事情定下來了。","examples":[{"en":"The judge's final decision ended the dispute.","zh":"法官的最終裁決結束了這場爭議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee's decision is final.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/final","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f61051a988a2dedf","term":"final","forms":["final","finals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"期末考試","explanation":"指課程或學期結束時進行的考試；複數 finals 常泛指一段時間內的多門期末考試。","examples":[{"en":"I have a final in chemistry tomorrow.","zh":"我明天有一門化學期末考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent the weekend studying for finals.","zh":"她整個週末都在準備期末考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/final","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-205c3e16c66ff0b84570","word":"finally","forms":["finally"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26f9bbfacb030483","term":"finally","forms":["finally"],"pos":"adv","zh":"終於；最終","explanation":"表示經過一段時間、努力或延誤後，事情終於發生或達到結果，重點在“過程拖得較久，但結果出現了”。","examples":[{"en":"After months of repairs, the old theater finally reopened.","zh":"經過幾個月的維修，那座老劇院終於重新開放了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing parcel finally arrived on Friday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30fbcf435cb3d1f5","term":"finally","forms":["finally"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最後；最後一點","explanation":"用於列舉或組織講話內容，表示前面的事項都說完後，現在講最後一項；它是話語順序上的“最後”，不強調等待。","examples":[{"en":"Finally, I would like to thank everyone who helped with the event.","zh":"最後，我想感謝所有幫助籌辦這次活動的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Finally, I'd like to thank our generous hosts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eab762a03fd979a04cc4","word":"finance","forms":["finance"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45f60177ded5806e","term":"finance","forms":["finance","finances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資金管理","explanation":"指管理錢、投資和其他資產的活動；個人、公司和政府都可以有自己的finance。","examples":[{"en":"She works in finance for a large technology company.","zh":"她在一家大型科技公司的金融部門工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good finance is essential to the success of any business.","zh":"良好的財務管理對任何企業的成功都至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-528f1aed499af205","term":"finance","forms":["finance","finances","financing","financed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……提供資金","explanation":"指為某人、專案、交易或活動籌集並提供資金；例如出錢供某人上學，或為一個專案提供經費。","examples":[{"en":"A local foundation financed the renovation of the community center.","zh":"一家當地基金會為社群中心的翻修提供了資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her parents financed her education abroad.","zh":"她的父母資助了她在國外的教育。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fed0e4820af42571c936","word":"financial","forms":["financial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad3bd1999e4267f8","term":"financial","forms":["financial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"財務的；金融的","explanation":"表示某事與錢、資金、收入、支出或財務管理有關，是 financial 最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The company is facing serious financial problems.","zh":"這家公司正面臨嚴重的財務問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need financial support to complete the project.","zh":"我們需要資金支援來完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/financial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6640de835ad09fb0a73","word":"find","forms":["find"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b59f0bfa7eba8a9","term":"find","forms":["find","finds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有價值的發現","explanation":"指找到的物品、遺址、人才等，通常帶有“這次發現很有價值或很令人興奮”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The old coins were an exciting find for the children.","zh":"這些舊硬幣對孩子們來說是一次令人興奮的發現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This little shop is a great find.","zh":"這家小店真是個意外發現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/find","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-458a85b1ec66cf8e","term":"find","forms":["find","finds","finding","found","fand","founden","findest","foundest","findeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"找到；定位到","explanation":"經過尋找後發現某個物品、人或地點，是真正“找到目標”的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"I found this shell on the beach.","zh":"我在海灘上找到了這個貝殼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you found your keys yet?","zh":"你找到鑰匙了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/find","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d057f634d5f269d","term":"find","forms":["find","finds","finding","found","fand","founden","findest","foundest","findeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為；覺得","explanation":"在思考或體驗之後形成看法，表示“覺得某人或某事具有某種性質”。這仍然像是從經驗中“發現”一個判斷。","examples":[{"en":"I find this book very helpful.","zh":"我覺得這本書很有幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many students find it difficult to speak in public.","zh":"許多學生覺得當眾講話很難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/find","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d14a58bae804a2b80b5b","word":"fine","forms":["fine"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97386e4e6873cd96","term":"fine","forms":["fine","finer","finest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好的；優秀的","explanation":"表示某人或某物質量高、令人滿意，符合“達到很高標準”的記憶。根據上下文，也可以譯為“漂亮的、出色的”。","examples":[{"en":"She is a fine musician.","zh":"她是一位出色的音樂家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a fine performance.","zh":"那是一場精彩的表演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83544f5e80939c49","term":"fine","forms":["fine","fines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"罰款","explanation":"指因違反法律、規章或規定而必須繳納的錢，是法律語境中需要付出的“罰款”。","examples":[{"en":"He had to pay a fine for parking illegally.","zh":"他因違法停車而必須繳納罰款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court imposed a heavy fine on the company.","zh":"法院對這家公司處以了高額罰款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34ba4844d32e841c","term":"fine","forms":["fine","fines","fining","fined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對……處以罰款","explanation":"因為違反法律、規定或公共秩序而要求某人繳納罰款；這正是記憶鉤子中“罰款”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The city fined the restaurant for dumping oil into the river.","zh":"市政府因這家餐館把油倒入河裡而對其處以罰款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council fined the company for illegal dumping.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-400b181c878493867e72","word":"finger","forms":["finger"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3c5e1cc870ae89a","term":"finger","forms":["finger","fingers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手指","explanation":"手指是手上細長、分節、用來觸碰、抓握和指向的部分；通常不包括拇指。它正是“手指的指向和觸碰”這一核心概念的直接含義。","examples":[{"en":"Humans have ten fingers, but only two thumbs.","zh":"人有十根手指，但只有兩個拇指。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pricked her finger while sewing the hem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48e6333a1d3813af","term":"finger","forms":["finger","fingers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豎中指手勢","explanation":"指把手掌朝內並豎起中指，向別人表示侮辱或強烈不滿的手勢；這是“伸出手指指向他人”發展出的冒犯性用法。","examples":[{"en":"He got angry and gave the driver the finger.","zh":"他生氣了，朝那名司機豎起了中指。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The furious driver gave him the finger.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d745e884b5843de5","term":"finger","forms":["finger","fingers","fingering","fingered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指出；歸咎於","explanation":"像手指指向一個目標一樣，表示明確指出某人或某事，也可以表示把責任歸咎於某人或某事。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation fingered two employees as the likely source of the leak.","zh":"調查指出兩名員工很可能是洩密源頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report fingered poor planning for the project’s failure.","zh":"報告把專案失敗歸咎於規劃不周。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-afee601c36b97136","term":"finger","forms":["finger","fingers","fingering","fingered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用手指觸碰或探查","explanation":"由手指的觸碰動作引申而來，表示用一個或多個手指戳、摸、探查或輕輕觸碰某物。","examples":[{"en":"She fingered the loose thread on her sleeve.","zh":"她用手指撥弄袖子上的松線頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He fingered the buttons on the old radio until it started working.","zh":"他用手指撥弄那臺舊收音機上的按鈕，直到它開始運轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42af43e3616eba4a133a","word":"finish","forms":["finish"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-acc3dee896d7647e","term":"finish","forms":["finish","finishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結束；結局","explanation":"指某件事、某段經歷或某個人生階段走到最後，也可以指最終結局。","examples":[{"en":"The story has a surprising finish.","zh":"這個故事有一個出人意料的結局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The race had an unexpectedly dramatic finish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed3fff6251f76692","term":"finish","forms":["finish","finishes","finishing","finished","finishest","finishedst","finisheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"完成；做完","explanation":"指把任務、工作、活動或一件事做到最後，使它完整結束。","examples":[{"en":"I need to finish my report before lunch.","zh":"我得在午飯前完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finished reading the book on the train.","zh":"她在火車上讀完了那本書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e9b521b480d1e1b","term":"finish","forms":["finish","finishes","finishing","finished","finishest","finishedst","finisheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結束；告終","explanation":"指活動、演出、會議或其他過程自然進行到終點。它描述事情自己結束，而不是某人把它做完。","examples":[{"en":"The concert finished just after ten.","zh":"音樂會剛過十點就結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lesson finishes at three o'clock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4f568b800c6a61b3ba2","word":"finite","forms":["finite"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2fc8d600cc5aa9b","term":"finite","forms":["finite","more finite","most finite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有限的；有界的","explanation":"指某種事物有終點，或數量、範圍受到明確限制。有限集合的元素個數是有限的，但有限並不表示一定很少。","examples":[{"en":"We have only a finite amount of time to finish the project.","zh":"我們只有有限的時間來完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every finite set has a definite number of elements.","zh":"每個有限集合都有確定數量的元素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f969d6a2d813546d","term":"finite","forms":["finite","more finite","most finite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"限定人稱或數的（動詞形式）","explanation":"在語法中，finite 形容動詞形式受到主語的人稱或數等語法資訊限定，通常能在句子中充當謂語；例如第三人稱單數現在時形式帶有這種限定。","examples":[{"en":"In “She walks to work”, “walks” is a finite verb.","zh":"在“She walks to work”中，“walks”是限定動詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unlike the infinitive, a finite form can mark past tense.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/finite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc9f28b12dd1818ee42f","word":"fire","forms":["fire"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a98722b3dd990a7","term":"fire","forms":["fire","fires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火；燃燒","explanation":"指燃料與氧氣發生反應而產生熱和火焰的燃燒現象，是fire最基本的意義，正如某種力量從燃燒中爆發出來。","examples":[{"en":"Keep away from the fire; it is very hot.","zh":"離火遠一點，它很燙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fire needs oxygen to keep burning.","zh":"火需要氧氣才能繼續燃燒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27723fc877bd1f04","term":"fire","forms":["fire","fires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火災","explanation":"指意外發生在某處、可能造成損害和危險的火，重點是破壞性和失控性；這也是“力量爆發”變成災害的情況。","examples":[{"en":"A fire broke out in the apartment building last night.","zh":"昨晚那棟公寓樓發生了火災。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firefighters quickly put out the fire.","zh":"消防員很快撲滅了火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8bbdf3eab3a15db","term":"fire","forms":["fire","fires","firing","fired","firest","firedst","fireth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"點燃","explanation":"表示把某物點著，使火焰爆發出來，常用於房屋、紙張等可燃物。","examples":[{"en":"The old shed was fired during the night.","zh":"那座舊棚屋在夜裡被點燃了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He fired the pile of leaves and watched the flames rise.","zh":"他點燃了那堆樹葉，看著火焰升起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f07fc2db298e182","term":"fire","forms":["fire","fires","firing","fired","firest","firedst","fireth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解僱","explanation":"表示僱主終止某人的工作，通常因為表現差、違規或其他工作原因；也就是把某人從職位上“趕出去”。","examples":[{"en":"The company fired him for repeatedly missing deadlines.","zh":"公司因他一再錯過截止期限而解僱了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was fired from her first job after three months.","zh":"她工作三個月後被第一份工作解僱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2d872a13438b3768c94","word":"firecracker","forms":["firecracker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"firecracker","forms":["firecracker"],"pos":"n.","zh":"鞭炮；爆竹","examples":[{"en":"A firecracker exploded in the street outside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Never hold a firecracker after lighting it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-11f41bf8c1d74ab1a150","word":"fireman/firewoman","forms":["fireman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-328e616c63efdb13","term":"fireman","forms":["fireman","firemen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消防員","explanation":"指專門撲滅火災、救援人員並處理火災現場的人，通常就是日常所說的消防員。這個詞保留了“與火打交道、控制火勢”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The fireman carried the child out of the burning house.","zh":"消防員把孩子從著火的房子裡抱了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her brother works as a fireman in the city.","zh":"她哥哥在這座城市當消防員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73b61e06ccb1e94f","term":"fireman","forms":["fireman","firemen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蒸汽鍋爐司爐工","explanation":"在蒸汽機車或蒸汽船上，指負責向鍋爐添煤、維持爐火的人。這裡不是撲滅火，而是守住並控制產生動力所需的火。","examples":[{"en":"The fireman shoveled coal into the locomotive's boiler.","zh":"蒸汽機車的司爐工把煤鏟進鍋爐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sweat soaked the fireman's shirt as he tended the liner's enormous furnaces.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9e00cabae41376d7891","word":"fireplace","forms":["fireplace"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c444b8b33cecbc82","term":"fireplace","forms":["fireplace","fireplaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壁爐；爐膛","explanation":"指房間裡固定的生火處，通常位於牆邊或牆內，下面放木柴生火，上方連線煙囪。它的核心概念就是“房間裡專門放火的地方”。","examples":[{"en":"We sat by the fireplace and drank hot chocolate.","zh":"我們坐在壁爐旁喝熱巧克力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old fireplace still works well in winter.","zh":"那座老壁爐冬天仍然很好用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireplace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-366b6ac67e1209751d21","word":"fireproof","forms":["fireproof"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c767bbc16787c4bc","term":"fireproof","forms":["fireproof","more fireproof","most fireproof"],"pos":"adj","zh":"防火的；耐火的","explanation":"指物品或材料經過設計或處理後，遇到火時不容易被燒壞，能夠在一定程度上保護裡面的東西。","examples":[{"en":"We keep the important papers in a fireproof box.","zh":"我們把重要檔案放在防火箱裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building has fireproof doors on every floor.","zh":"這棟樓每層都有防火門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fireproof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd2db00b68d692183fa4","word":"firework","forms":["firework"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d222ef0e4752e51","term":"firework","forms":["firework","fireworks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煙火裝置","explanation":"一種裝有火藥等化學物質的裝置，點燃後會噴出彩色火焰和火花，發出哨聲或爆響，有些還會升到空中再爆炸，常用於慶祝或娛樂。","examples":[{"en":"The city set off a firework over the river to celebrate the festival.","zh":"這座城市在河上空燃放了一枚煙火來慶祝節日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a firework explode high above the stadium.","zh":"我們看到一枚煙火在體育場上空爆炸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firework","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f62550731d942f8bb6b","word":"firm","forms":["firm"],"officialPos":"n./adj./v./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3cd34d0393e868a","term":"firm","forms":["firm","firmer","firmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"牢牢穩住的","explanation":"表示位置穩、不容易移動或鬆開；它把“穩固”的核心形象直接用於握力、支撐等情境。","examples":[{"en":"Keep a firm grip on the railing as you go down the stairs.","zh":"下樓梯時要牢牢抓住扶手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep a firm grip on the ladder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e083350bdc44e2b0","term":"firm","forms":["firm","firmer","firmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結實不軟的","explanation":"表示材料或身體組織有支撐力、不鬆軟；土地 firm 則表示不泥濘、踩上去穩。","examples":[{"en":"Choose peaches that are firm but not completely hard.","zh":"挑選結實但不是完全堅硬的桃子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choose a firm peach rather than a mushy one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e29e53279591b7f","term":"firm","forms":["firm","firms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業企業","explanation":"表示一個經營業務的企業，重點在於它作為商業組織進行活動；這是從“以固定名稱開展業務”發展來的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Several firms are competing for the same contract.","zh":"幾家企業正在爭奪同一份合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her firm specializes in environmental consulting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c8b4bcc64a9f73f","term":"firm","forms":["firm","firms","firming","firmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使穩固、加強","explanation":"表示採取行動讓某物更牢固，或讓某人的決心更加堅定，是“穩固”核心義的使動用法。","examples":[{"en":"The criticism only firmed her resolve to finish the project.","zh":"這些批評反而堅定了她完成專案的決心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Press gently to firm the soil around the roots.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7937b64b8caa58f0372","word":"first","forms":["first"],"officialPos":"n./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55f6a6a3b1c04d0d","term":"first","forms":["first","firstmost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"第一個；最先的","explanation":"指在一系列人或事物中排在最前面的，也就是序數“第一”。","examples":[{"en":"Maya was the first person to arrive.","zh":"瑪雅是第一個到達的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our first meeting will be on Monday.","zh":"我們的第一次會議將在星期一舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0b070d9f8d14459","term":"first","forms":["first","firstmost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最重要的；最優秀的","explanation":"從“站在最前面”引申為地位最高、最重要或質量最好的。","examples":[{"en":"Safety is our first priority.","zh":"安全是我們的首要任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Passenger safety is our first concern.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3136da58e56598fd","term":"first","forms":["first"],"pos":"adv","zh":"首先；先","explanation":"表示在其他事情之前先做某事，延續了“排在最前面”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"First, check the address before you leave.","zh":"首先，出發前檢查一下地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Finish your homework first.","zh":"先把作業做完。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51b5cff73d425b70","term":"first","forms":["first"],"pos":"adv","zh":"第一次","explanation":"表示某人以前沒有經歷過，而這次是首次經歷。","examples":[{"en":"I first visited the city when I was a child.","zh":"我第一次到這座城市是在小時候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We first met on a rainy afternoon in Lisbon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c8c87e188f49a48","term":"first","forms":["first","firsts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"第一名；最前者","explanation":"指排在最前面的人或事物，通常是某個順序中的第一項。","examples":[{"en":"She was the first to finish the race.","zh":"她是第一個跑完比賽的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The first is usually the hardest step.","zh":"第一步通常是最難的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b65bf95cc4f9b4b3a52f","word":"fiscal","forms":["fiscal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d4042dfa19eaacb","term":"fiscal","forms":["fiscal","more fiscal","most fiscal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"財政的","explanation":"指國家、地方政府或機構的收入、支出、稅收和預算等財政事務。它把注意力放在“公共或組織的錢怎樣收進來、怎樣花出去”上。","examples":[{"en":"The government is under pressure to improve its fiscal policy.","zh":"政府正面臨改善財政政策的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report examines the country's fiscal position.","zh":"這份報告分析了該國的財政狀況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiscal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5085ddacef384b34","term":"fiscal","forms":["fiscal","more fiscal","most fiscal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"財政年度的","explanation":"表示按政府或機構的會計週期計算的年度。這個年度用於編制預算和統計收支，起止時間可以不同於一月至十二月的自然年。","examples":[{"en":"The new budget will take effect in fiscal 2027.","zh":"新預算將在2027財政年度生效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sales increased during the last fiscal year.","zh":"銷售額在上一財政年度有所增長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiscal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b474a99a2705e23cf905","word":"fish","forms":["fish"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b6639b1c51133f3","term":"fish","forms":["fish","fishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"魚","explanation":"一種生活在水中、用鰓呼吸並靠鰭遊動的脊椎動物；也就是從水裡撈出來的典型東西。","examples":[{"en":"A bright fish swam past the boat.","zh":"一條色彩鮮豔的魚從船邊遊過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw hundreds of fish in the clear water.","zh":"我們在清澈的水裡看到了數百條魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a9892ce6d4bd3d3","term":"fish","forms":["fish","fishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"魚肉","explanation":"指可供食用的魚肉，也就是從水裡撈出的魚被做成食物後的部分。","examples":[{"en":"We had grilled fish with rice for dinner.","zh":"我們晚飯吃了烤魚配米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soup contains fish and vegetables.","zh":"這道湯裡有魚肉和蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-274fa910e31c00cc","term":"fish","forms":["fish","fishes","fishing","fished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"捕魚；捕撈水中動物","explanation":"指在河、湖、海等水域捕魚，也可以捕捉螃蟹等其他水生動物，或從海底採集珊瑚、珍珠等；就是把水裡的東西“撈出來”。","examples":[{"en":"We fish for salmon in the river every summer.","zh":"我們每年夏天都在這條河裡捕鮭魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children went fishing for crabs by the pier.","zh":"孩子們到碼頭邊捕螃蟹去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23c24f69df2a87d9","term":"fish","forms":["fish","fishes","fishing","fished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"旁敲側擊套取資訊","explanation":"指透過試探、迂迴提問或其他辦法，讓別人說出自己想知道的資訊，像用話把資訊“撈出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter was fishing for details about the new policy.","zh":"記者在旁敲側擊地套取有關新政策的細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kept fishing around for information about the merger.","zh":"他一直旁敲側擊地打聽合併的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da8cc7909055a96967f8","word":"fisherman","forms":["fisherman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d6ba95d4524d7f2","term":"fisherman","forms":["fisherman","fishermen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捕魚者；漁民","explanation":"指以捕魚為職業或正在從事捕魚的人，是這個詞在現代日常語境中的主要意思。記住海上捕魚的畫面：船上撒網、收網的人就是這個詞所指的人。","examples":[{"en":"The fisherman repaired his net before sunrise.","zh":"那名漁民在日出前修好了自己的漁網。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several fishermen returned to the harbor after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，幾名漁民回到了港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fisherman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2e3839afef367a6867b","word":"fishery","forms":["fishery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-371884e704f2f9b4","term":"fishery","forms":["fishery","fisheries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捕魚業；漁業","explanation":"指捕撈魚類或其他海產品，以及隨後進行加工、銷售的整個行業或活動。這是fishery最基礎的意思，重點不在某一條魚，而在圍繞捕魚形成的完整產業。","examples":[{"en":"The local fishery provides jobs for thousands of coastal families.","zh":"當地漁業為數千個沿海家庭提供了工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New rules are needed to protect the fishery from overfishing.","zh":"需要制定新規定，保護漁業免受過度捕撈的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fishery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c73066db2fa31a5d","term":"fishery","forms":["fishery","fisheries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漁場；漁業資源區","explanation":"指適合捕魚、並與捕魚活動相關的特定地點或水域。這裡的fishery像是捕魚業所依託的那片“地方和資源”，所以可以說有一個漁場，也可以說多個漁場。","examples":[{"en":"The storm damaged several fisheries along the northern coast.","zh":"暴風雨損壞了北部海岸沿線的幾個漁場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The estuary supports a valuable oyster fishery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fishery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91f49598ac3a9ff6bdeb","word":"fist","forms":["fist"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc0b4b79d6bf7eb4","term":"fist","forms":["fist","fists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拳頭","explanation":"指五指收攏、握緊的手。它是“用拳頭打”和“握緊某物”等義項的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She held the key tightly in her fist.","zh":"她把鑰匙緊緊攥在拳頭裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He raised his fist in anger.","zh":"他憤怒地舉起了拳頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cfb3cb95c6c0ae2","term":"fist","forms":["fist","fists","fisting","fisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用拳頭擊打","explanation":"指用拳頭打擊某人或某物，是從“拳頭”這一核心形象直接發展出的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The player was sent off for fisting the other team's striker.","zh":"這名球員因用拳頭擊打對方前鋒而被罰下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He fisted the ball away from the goal.","zh":"他用拳頭把球擊離了球門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da4270e3735a3418c9d4","word":"fit","forms":["fit"],"officialPos":"v./adj./n./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff9d07440a113eda","term":"fit","forms":["fit","fitter","fittest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合適；恰當","explanation":"指某個選擇、做法或判斷與情況相配，認為這樣做最合適。","examples":[{"en":"Choose whichever option you see fit.","zh":"請選擇你認為合適的方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This explanation is fit for beginners.","zh":"這個解釋適合初學者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70eb87edba3f1906","term":"fit","forms":["fit","fitter","fittest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"健康強健","explanation":"指身體狀況良好，有足夠體力應對某項活動或要求。這個意思仍然可以理解為身體狀態“配得上”任務。","examples":[{"en":"She is fit enough to hike all day.","zh":"她身體很好，足以徒步一整天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I swim twice a week to keep fit.","zh":"我每週游泳兩次來保持健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0626c926bb222ad","term":"fit","forms":["fit","fits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合身程度","explanation":"指衣物或其他穿戴物與身體尺寸、形狀的匹配程度，也可泛指某物是否適合某人或某種用途。","examples":[{"en":"This jacket is a perfect fit for me.","zh":"這件夾克我穿著非常合身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shoes have a comfortable fit.","zh":"這雙鞋穿起來很合腳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2a3ae683d8ca6ce","term":"fit","forms":["fit","fits","fitting","fitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"適合；適用於","explanation":"某事物或做法與某個目的、場合或需要相配，正好“配得上”。","examples":[{"en":"This solution fits our needs perfectly.","zh":"這個解決方案完全符合我們的需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The schedule fits the purpose of the training.","zh":"這個日程安排適合培訓的目的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c6e6c4c02e55178e858","word":"fix","forms":["fix"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d24052739b0b87df","term":"fix","forms":["fix","fixes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"修理；解決辦法","explanation":"fix 是為壞掉或出問題的事物採取的修理措施，也可以指解決問題的辦法；它體現了把事情重新“固定”到正常狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic found a quick fix for the noisy engine.","zh":"修理工很快找到了修好這臺吵鬧發動機的辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Restarting the router provided a temporary fix.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fix","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce4eb8ed6ded1aed","term":"fix","forms":["fix","fixes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被操縱的結果","explanation":"a fix 指本應公平競爭的比賽、選舉、審判或交易，其結果已被事先安排；結果彷彿被牢牢“釘死”了。","examples":[{"en":"The fans suspected that the match was a fix.","zh":"球迷懷疑這場比賽的結果是被操縱的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans suspected the championship result was a fix.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fix","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a3d8404f789fd6a","term":"fix","forms":["fix","fixes","fixing","fixt","fixed","fixest","fixedst","fixeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"固定；粘住","explanation":"fix something 是把東西固定在某處，或把某個時間、狀態定下來；這正是“釘牢”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please fix this notice to the door.","zh":"請把這張通知固定在門上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fix the label to the jar with glue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fix","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ccf4776743d021a7","term":"fix","forms":["fix","fixes","fixing","fixt","fixed","fixest","fixedst","fixeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修理；修復","explanation":"fix something 是把壞掉的東西恢復到能正常使用的狀態，也就是把它重新“固定好”。","examples":[{"en":"Can you fix the broken lamp before dinner?","zh":"你能在晚飯前把壞掉的燈修好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician fixed the faulty door latch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fix","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-807d0fbcae7c4b20518d","word":"flag","forms":["flag"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-448ca572f81d13e7","term":"flag","forms":["flag","flags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旗幟；旗子","explanation":"旗幟是醒目的布制標記，用來表示國家、組織或身份，也可以傳遞訊號。記住“醒目的標記”這個核心形象，就能理解它為什麼常被升起、揮動或懸掛。","examples":[{"en":"The school raised its flag at the start of the ceremony.","zh":"學校在儀式開始時升起了校旗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red flag warned hikers not to enter the beach.","zh":"一面紅旗警告徒步者不要進入海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db7305da2ffd76217710","word":"flake","forms":["flake"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89b418d5992e74b1","term":"flake","forms":["flake","flakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄片；碎屑","explanation":"指從較大物體表面脫落或被削下來的薄而鬆散的一層，常見於油漆、皮膚、雪或其他片狀物。這個意義保留了“從整體上掉下一小片”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"There were a few flakes of paint on the floor after we painted the wall.","zh":"我們刷完牆後，地板上有幾片掉下來的油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Flakes of old paint fell from the ceiling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-770f3c7c290a8db4","term":"flake","forms":["flake","flakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不可靠的人","explanation":"非正式地指做事輕浮、缺乏實際安排，或常常不能按約定完成事情的人；重點不是能力差，而是讓別人無法依靠。","examples":[{"en":"She is friendly, but she is a flake when it comes to keeping appointments.","zh":"她人很友好，但一到遵守約定時間就不太可靠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't rely on him; he's a complete flake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fcfcd87d6ec96473","term":"flake","forms":["flake","flakes","flaking","flaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剝落；脫片","explanation":"指某物表面破裂或碎成薄片並脫落，通常是油漆、塗層、乾燥物等一層層掉下來。它就是“薄片”這個核心畫面變成了一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The old paint started to flake off around the window.","zh":"窗戶周圍的舊油漆開始剝落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Old paint flaked from the window frame.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3be757090691efb","term":"flake","forms":["flake","flakes","flaking","flaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"失約；不兌現","explanation":"非正式地指原本答應做某事，後來沒有出現、沒有完成，或臨時放棄了承諾。它和名詞“不可靠的人”相連，像人從原定計劃中“掉了出去”。","examples":[{"en":"He said he would help us move, but he flaked at the last minute.","zh":"他說會幫我們搬家，但最後一刻卻臨時不來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He promised to help, then flaked at the last minute.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd9dc5f78dac9fad83a6","word":"flame","forms":["flame"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6843ac20cb3b8ad4","term":"flame","forms":["flame","flames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火焰","explanation":"火燃燒時可見的發光部分，既帶來熱量，也會不斷跳動、變大或熄滅。","examples":[{"en":"The candle flame flickered whenever the door opened.","zh":"每當門開啟時，燭火就一閃一閃的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flames quickly spread across the dry grass.","zh":"火焰很快蔓延到了乾燥的草地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c934cbc5e1e1319","term":"flame","forms":["flame","flames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短暫熱烈的戀人或戀情","explanation":"像火焰一樣熱烈、但通常不會長久的戀愛物件或戀情，常帶有回憶舊情的意味。","examples":[{"en":"He ran into an old flame at the train station.","zh":"他在火車站偶遇了一位舊情人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His latest flame is a painter he met in Paris.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c10eb69d76bd85aa","term":"flame","forms":["flame","flames","flaming","flamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"燃燒；冒火焰","explanation":"產生火焰或像火焰一樣燃燒，常強調火勢出現、恢復或繼續燃燒。","examples":[{"en":"A spark made the dry leaves flame again.","zh":"一顆火星讓幹樹葉又燃燒起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The torch flamed brightly in the cold wind.","zh":"火炬在冷風中燒得很旺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-851e43bd44a2c3d30e5f","word":"flash","forms":["flash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5aacc1205df5dc0","term":"flash","forms":["flash","flashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"閃光","explanation":"指突然出現、很快消失的一陣強光，正是“一道突然亮起、馬上消失的光”。","examples":[{"en":"A flash lit up the sky during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，一道閃光照亮了天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I saw a flash through the window.","zh":"我透過窗戶看見了一道閃光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6246c43f555c1a9","term":"flash","forms":["flash","flashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一瞬間","explanation":"指極其短暫的一段時間，像閃光一樣轉眼就過去。","examples":[{"en":"The bird disappeared in a flash.","zh":"那隻鳥轉眼間就消失了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In a flash, the children ran across the yard.","zh":"孩子們一轉眼就跑過了院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8dc3e4239f19eb4","term":"flash","forms":["flash","flashes","flashing","flashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使閃爍；使短暫發光","explanation":"指讓燈光或其他光源短暫地亮起，或有間歇地發光。可以把它想成主動讓“一道突然亮起、馬上消失的光”出現。","examples":[{"en":"He flashed his torch at the dark window.","zh":"他用手電筒朝黑暗的窗戶閃了幾下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The driver flashed his headlights to warn us.","zh":"司機閃了幾下車燈來警告我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b982eabb1680523bf098","word":"flashlight","forms":["flashlight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f747bc6061db46a","term":"flashlight","forms":["flashlight","flashlights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手電筒","explanation":"一種靠電池供電、可以拿在手裡照明的小型燈，常用於停電、夜間行走或尋找東西。","examples":[{"en":"I used a flashlight to find my keys under the sofa.","zh":"我用手電筒找沙發底下的鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please bring a flashlight when we go camping.","zh":"我們去露營時請帶一把手電筒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flashlight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5dc27af287fa554aa10f","word":"flat","forms":["flat"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-083cd390c003e235","term":"flat","forms":["flat","flatter","flattest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平坦的","explanation":"指表面沒有明顯的高低起伏，像被壓平了一樣；這是 flat 最基本的空間含義。","examples":[{"en":"The land around here is flat.","zh":"這一帶的土地很平坦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We pitched our tent on flat ground.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7eb71ad65c4be43","term":"flat","forms":["flat","flatter","flattest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沉悶乏味的","explanation":"指聚會、故事、表演或氣氛缺少活力和變化，讓人覺得無趣或洩氣；這也是“失去起伏”從具體狀態到抽象狀態的引申。","examples":[{"en":"The party felt flat after the band left.","zh":"樂隊離開後，聚會的氣氛變得很沉悶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interview felt flat until the final question.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6faa753603a0a0cc","term":"flat","forms":["flat","flats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漏氣的輪胎","explanation":"指輪胎漏氣或已經癟掉的情況，輪胎被壓扁，正是“失去起伏”的 flat 狀態。","examples":[{"en":"I got a flat on the way to work.","zh":"我上班路上車胎漏氣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you help me change this flat?","zh":"你能幫我換這條漏氣的輪胎嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08a32335dda33fe0","term":"flat","forms":["flat","flats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公寓；套房","explanation":"指建築物中的一套獨立住宅，通常包括臥室、廚房和衛生間等空間，常用於出租或居住。","examples":[{"en":"They rented a small flat near the train station.","zh":"他們在火車站附近租了一套小公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They share a small flat above the bakery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d92d2c2d4bb1810fda33","word":"flatter","forms":["flatter"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f956a0cc2f1e34f","term":"flatter","forms":["flatter","flatters","flattering","flattered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"奉承；討好","explanation":"用誇獎或好聽的話讓某人高興，常常帶有討好、取悅或不完全真誠的意味。","examples":[{"en":"He flattered his boss by praising every decision she made.","zh":"他誇獎老闆作出的每個決定，以此討好她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He flattered the manager to obtain better shifts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flatter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5d2f4515ba34f2f83f3","word":"flavor","forms":["flavor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b8522394b7895aa","term":"flavor","forms":["flavor","flavors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"味道；風味","explanation":"指食物或飲料嚐起來、聞起來綜合形成的味道，是flavor最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The flavor of this soup is rich and comforting.","zh":"這道湯的味道濃郁而令人感到舒心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fresh herbs give the dish a brighter flavor.","zh":"新鮮香草讓這道菜的風味更加清新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flavor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-beaeca0d5e3d289c","term":"flavor","forms":["flavor","flavors","flavoring","flavored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……調味","explanation":"指向食物或飲料中加入調味物，讓它產生特定風味；這是名詞“味道”轉成的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Flavor the rice with garlic and ginger.","zh":"用大蒜和姜給米飯調味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sauce is flavored with roasted peppers.","zh":"這道醬汁用烤甜椒調過味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flavor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-031a0427b237efb39953","word":"flaw","forms":["flaw"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-807beb5afb90a233","term":"flaw","forms":["flaw","flaws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裂縫；斷口","explanation":"指物體表面或結構中出現的裂縫、缺口，使原本連續完整的東西斷開；這個具體形象也引出了“缺陷、破綻”的抽象義。","examples":[{"en":"There is a flaw in the blade of this knife.","zh":"這把刀的刀刃上有一道裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tiny flaw in the crystal caught the light.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61a982f6ecf44ef3","term":"flaw","forms":["flaw","flaws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺點；瑕疵；破綻","explanation":"指人、物品、計劃或論證中隱藏的缺點或不完美之處，往往會削弱整體的價值、可靠性或說服力。","examples":[{"en":"The plan has a serious flaw that could cost us time.","zh":"這個計劃有一個嚴重的缺陷，可能會讓我們浪費時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His impatience is a flaw, but it does not define him.","zh":"他的急躁是一個缺點，但不能因此概括他這個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e1b6072c029f89695a2e","word":"flea","forms":["flea"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c01de9bbf608b74","term":"flea","forms":["flea","fleas","fleen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳蚤","explanation":"一種很小的無翅寄生昆蟲，會吸食人或動物的血，並能跳得很遠；這是 flea 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The dog has fleas, so we need to wash its bedding.","zh":"這隻狗身上有跳蚤，所以我們得把它的 bedding 洗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flea jumped onto my sock.","zh":"一隻跳蚤跳到了我的襪子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d15a1edfb23cdba76277","word":"flee","forms":["flee"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9555ffcd22201c7e","term":"flee","forms":["flee","flees","fleeing","fled","fleed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逃跑；逃走","explanation":"指人或動物為了躲避危險、追捕或不利處境而迅速離開，重點是“逃走”這一動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers fled when the fire reached the edge of the town.","zh":"大火燒到城邊時，村民們紛紛逃走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fled from the building after hearing the alarm.","zh":"聽到警報後，她逃離了那棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4b8d44c9a7c594f","term":"flee","forms":["flee","flees","fleeing","fled","fleed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逃離；逃避","explanation":"指主動離開某個地方、國家或危險處境，以躲避即將發生或正在發生的威脅。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of families fled the region before the fighting began.","zh":"戰鬥開始前，成千上萬的家庭逃離了這個地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He fled the burning hotel through a ground-floor window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5eb2ce291c7d227dd684","word":"fleet","forms":["fleet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94853d8c3a3f9d9a","term":"fleet","forms":["fleet","fleets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船隊；車隊","explanation":"把許多船或車輛想成一起在水面或道路上移動的編隊，就是“fleet”。它們通常屬於同一組織，或被統一管理、排程。","examples":[{"en":"The company operates a fleet of electric buses.","zh":"這家公司運營著一支電動公交車隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fleet of fishing boats returned to the harbor before the storm.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，一支漁船船隊回到了港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fleet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb8db7f3aeeb5b2730b5","word":"flesh","forms":["flesh"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74a3bf7c1a76d558","term":"flesh","forms":["flesh","fleshes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體的柔軟肉組織","explanation":"指人或動物身體裡柔軟的組織，主要包括肌肉和脂肪，是“肉”這一核心意象在身體上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The flesh of the fish was firm and white.","zh":"這種魚的肉緊實而潔白。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thorn cut deep into the flesh of his hand.","zh":"這根刺深深扎進了他的手部肌肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flesh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98fee11994ff0524","term":"flesh","forms":["flesh","fleshes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可食用的動物肉","explanation":"指作為食物的動物組織，也就是肉；在一些語境中通常不包括魚肉。這是“柔軟的肉質”在餐桌上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The bird feeds mainly on the flesh of small animals.","zh":"這種鳥主要以小動物的肉為食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Remove the flesh from the cooked crab shell.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flesh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91ab4d276f2433107b47","word":"flexibility","forms":["flexibility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4418b265437aaabb","term":"flexibility","forms":["flexibility","flexibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"柔韌性；靈活變通","explanation":"指人、物或做法不僵硬，能夠彎曲、適應或改變。它可以是身體上的柔韌，也可以是對規則、立場或處理方式的變通；共同點是“不會一碰就斷，而是可以調整”。","examples":[{"en":"The manager showed flexibility towards employees who needed to change their shifts.","zh":"經理對需要調班的員工表現出了靈活和體諒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular stretching can improve flexibility in your legs and back.","zh":"經常拉伸可以提高腿部和背部的柔韌性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flexibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a4e8c6bc89b8f99","term":"flexibility","forms":["flexibility","flexibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇餘地；調整空間","explanation":"指安排、計劃或條件沒有被完全固定，因此可以在幾個選項之間選擇，或根據情況作出調整。這裡的“彎曲”不是身體動作，而是給未來留下轉向的空間。","examples":[{"en":"This job gives me some flexibility in choosing my working hours.","zh":"這份工作讓我在選擇工作時間方面有一定的餘地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Remote work gives parents greater flexibility over their schedules.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flexibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-800ad6207fe609eac8f8","word":"flexible","forms":["flexible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c23860fd95751a84","term":"flexible","forms":["flexible","more flexible","most flexible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能彎曲而不斷裂","explanation":"指物體有彈性，可以彎、扭或改變形狀，卻不容易折斷；這是“有彈性、不僵硬”這一核心畫面的字面意義。","examples":[{"en":"This flexible tube can bend around tight corners.","zh":"這根柔韌的管子可以繞過狹窄的拐角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soles are flexible enough for walking on uneven ground.","zh":"鞋底足夠柔韌，走在不平的地面上也合適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flexible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5adfcd92e2901f6","term":"flexible","forms":["flexible","more flexible","most flexible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能適應變化，能夠變通","explanation":"表示計劃、安排、制度或人的做法可以隨著新情況調整，不必一成不變；這是現代日常使用中非常重要的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"I need a flexible schedule because my children sometimes get sick.","zh":"我需要一份靈活的時間安排，因為孩子有時會生病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be flexible and change the plan if the weather gets worse.","zh":"要靈活一些，如果天氣變差就調整計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flexible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03b6b3e9163de296faeb","word":"flight","forms":["flight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8cea2280b60f9fd","term":"flight","forms":["flight","flights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛行","explanation":"指飛在空中的動作或狀態，重點是“飛行”這一過程，而不是某一次具體旅程。","examples":[{"en":"Most birds are capable of flight.","zh":"大多數鳥都有飛行能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eagle stayed in flight for nearly an hour.","zh":"那隻鷹在空中飛了將近一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20680fa3b9638a99","term":"flight","forms":["flight","flights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次飛行","explanation":"指某隻鳥、某架飛機或其他飛行物完成的一次具體飛行。","examples":[{"en":"The migrating birds' flight took them to Africa.","zh":"候鳥的一次飛行把它們帶到了非洲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The short flight across the lake lasted ten minutes.","zh":"飛過湖面的這次短途飛行持續了十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-731689552ae5d1fd","term":"flight","forms":["flight","flights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"航班","explanation":"指飛機從一個地點飛往另一個地點的一次行程，通常是已經安排或預訂好的商業飛行。","examples":[{"en":"Our flight to Seoul leaves at nine tonight.","zh":"我們飛往首爾的航班今晚九點起飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I booked a direct flight from Madrid to Rome.","zh":"我訂了一趟從馬德里直飛羅馬的航班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b9107c01615ac65","term":"flight","forms":["flight","flights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段樓梯","explanation":"指兩層平臺之間連續的一段樓梯；它是由“通向另一處的路線”從飛行引申出來的空間用法。","examples":[{"en":"We climbed one flight of stairs to reach the office.","zh":"我們爬了一段樓梯才到辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a narrow flight of stairs behind the kitchen.","zh":"廚房後面有一段狹窄的樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e448897946ead9e39e8","word":"flip","forms":["flip"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-125c1d355dbdeead","term":"flip","forms":["flip","flips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"翻轉；翻面動作","explanation":"指物體繞著自身翻過去、從一面變成另一面，或完成一次這樣的動作。","examples":[{"en":"We will decide who goes first with a flip of a coin.","zh":"我們用擲硬幣來決定誰先開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gymnast landed after one clean flip.","zh":"體操運動員完成一個漂亮的翻轉後落地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24e251badf62ab75","term":"flip","forms":["flip","flips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"徹底轉變","explanation":"指方向、決定、立場或行動突然完全改變，像原來的面被翻到了另一面。","examples":[{"en":"The team made a sudden flip in its public position.","zh":"這個團隊突然徹底改變了公開立場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The announcement caused a sudden flip in public opinion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a375c50b559f749","term":"flip","forms":["flip","flips","flipping","flipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……翻過來","explanation":"把物體從一面翻到另一面，通常是為了翻面、檢查背面或讓它落在另一面。","examples":[{"en":"Flip the pancake when the edges start to turn brown.","zh":"煎餅邊緣開始變棕時，把它翻過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She flipped the card over to read the message.","zh":"她把卡片翻過來，讀上面的留言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49a13482517af5b6","term":"flip","forms":["flip","flips","flipping","flipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"彈動；快速轉動","explanation":"用手指一彈，使物體快速轉動或翻轉，最典型的是擲硬幣來隨機決定。","examples":[{"en":"If we cannot agree, let's flip a coin.","zh":"如果我們無法達成一致，就擲硬幣決定吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He flipped the switch with one finger.","zh":"他用一根手指撥動了開關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-76a7e234dc54e9c605b2","word":"float","forms":["float"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6418c4cff2f31f23","term":"float","forms":["float","floats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"浮具","explanation":"指幫助人或物在水或其他液體上保持漂浮的裝置，正是“浮在表面、不被固定”的具體工具。","examples":[{"en":"Attach a float to the fishing line so you can see when a fish bites.","zh":"把浮漂系在魚線上，這樣魚咬鉤時你就能看見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children held on to a float while they learned to swim.","zh":"孩子們學游泳時抓著一個浮具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/float","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dfdf384e2a1c810d","term":"float","forms":["float","floats","floating","floated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漂浮","explanation":"物體停留在液體或空氣的表面或其中，不沉下去，也沒有被固定住；這正是“浮在表面、不被固定”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The leaves floated on the surface of the pond.","zh":"樹葉漂浮在池塘水面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Helium balloons float in the air.","zh":"氦氣球漂浮在空中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/float","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a518542eb7145fe","term":"float","forms":["float","floats","floating","floated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漫無目的地飄動","explanation":"人、物體或注意力沒有明確目的地到處移動、遊蕩，像沒有被固定在某處一樣。","examples":[{"en":"After lunch, I floated around the city with no particular plan.","zh":"午飯後，我漫無目的地在城裡閒逛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children floated around the garden while the adults talked.","zh":"大人聊天時，孩子們在花園裡四處閒逛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/float","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0ecdb2fc8a09ac8","term":"float","forms":["float","floats","floating","floated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提出想法","explanation":"把一個想法或方案提出來，放給別人考慮，就像把東西放到水面上供人觀察。","examples":[{"en":"I floated the idea of working four days a week.","zh":"我提出了每週工作四天的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She floated a possible solution at the meeting.","zh":"她在會上提出了一個可能的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/float","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a1eb3d0b3d5c74a5ef7","word":"flock","forms":["flock"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73a1cd507292ebc4","term":"flock","forms":["flock","flocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鳥群","explanation":"flock 可指聚在一起活動或遷徙的一群鳥，重點是它們像一個整體一起行動。","examples":[{"en":"A flock of birds crossed the evening sky.","zh":"一群鳥飛過傍晚的天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flock of geese settled on the lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-113496fd4b434100","term":"flock","forms":["flock","flocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羊群；動物群","explanation":"flock 也指成群的動物，最常見的是羊；在較舊的用法中還可指山羊或其他飼養動物。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer led his flock back to the field.","zh":"農夫把他的羊群帶回了田裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flock of sheep blocked the narrow road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9019f51e7e188948","term":"flock","forms":["flock","flocks","flocking","flocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成群湧向","explanation":"flock 作動詞時，表示許多人或動物像一群一樣聚集起來，或成群趕往某個地方；它把名詞的“一群”變成了“成群行動”。","examples":[{"en":"Fans flocked to the store for the product launch.","zh":"產品釋出時，粉絲們成群湧向商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Birds flock to the lake at sunset.","zh":"日落時，鳥兒成群飛向湖邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d8864644c15d33be9c0a","word":"flood","forms":["flood"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-adba1f664c7dadbb","term":"flood","forms":["flood","floods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洪水；水災","explanation":"大量水突然越過河流、湖泊或其他水體的邊界，淹沒原本乾燥的地方；重點是水量失控並造成氾濫。","examples":[{"en":"The village was cut off by a flood after three days of heavy rain.","zh":"連續三天暴雨後，洪水使這個村莊與外界隔絕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flood damaged hundreds of homes along the river.","zh":"洪水毀壞了河岸沿線數百所房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e3b0ed34a85eb80","term":"flood","forms":["flood","floods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量湧來的事物","explanation":"這裡沒有真的水，而是把突然出現、數量大到難以應付的投訴、訊息或請求比作洪水。","examples":[{"en":"The company received a flood of complaints after the update.","zh":"更新後，公司收到了一大堆接踵而來的投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The appeal brought a flood of donations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1312e322e48af18e","term":"flood","forms":["flood","floods","flooding","flooded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"氾濫；湧入","explanation":"水量過大而溢位時，水會 flood 某地；人群也可以像洪水一樣湧入某處，因此該詞還能描述大批人突然進入。","examples":[{"en":"Fans flooded into the stadium before the final match.","zh":"決賽前，大批球迷湧進了體育場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rainwater flooded into the basement through the broken window.","zh":"雨水從破窗湧進了地下室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-273c40024fd0175a","term":"flood","forms":["flood","floods","flooding","flooded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使大量充斥；使應接不暇","explanation":"把大量請求、資訊或投訴像洪水一樣傾倒給某人或某處，使其難以及時處理。","examples":[{"en":"The help desk was flooded with calls after the service went down.","zh":"服務中斷後，客服臺被大量來電淹沒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The announcement flooded our inbox with questions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3e1f4935b0919b346c2","word":"floor","forms":["floor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6d7ad7e543aa9e0","term":"floor","forms":["floor","floors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房間的地面","explanation":"指房屋或建築內部供人行走、承託傢俱的平面，通常就是“地板”或“地面”。","examples":[{"en":"The children were playing on the floor.","zh":"孩子們正在地板上玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We replaced the old floor with pale wooden boards.","zh":"我們用淺色木板換掉了舊地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9901669234a1f322","term":"floor","forms":["floor","floors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自然空間的底部","explanation":"指洞穴、森林、海洋或其他自然空間最下面的表面，也就是這些地方的“底”。它仍然保留了“平坦承託面”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The divers found shells on the ocean floor.","zh":"潛水員在海底發現了貝殼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sunlight barely reached the forest floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-479eb2bff5985fb3","term":"floor","forms":["floor","floors","flooring","floored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給建築鋪地面","explanation":"指給房屋或房間安裝、鋪設地面材料，把建築變成有可行走底面的空間。","examples":[{"en":"They floored the cottage with wide pine boards.","zh":"他們用寬鬆木板給小屋鋪了地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We plan to floor the balcony in weather-resistant tiles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac2599379ec2678e","term":"floor","forms":["floor","floors","flooring","floored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擊倒在地","explanation":"指把人打倒，使其倒在地面上；這是把名詞“地面”直接變成動作的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The boxer floored his opponent in the second round.","zh":"那名拳擊手在第二回合擊倒了對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A punch to the jaw floored the champion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f55f97cfa0dd5f18c1ac","word":"flour","forms":["flour"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89cbbb1d53eb1efa","term":"flour","forms":["flour","flours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麵粉；食用細粉","explanation":"把小麥等穀物磨成的細粉，最常用於製作麵包、蛋糕、麵條和糕點；也可以泛指由其他食材磨成、用於烹飪的粉。","examples":[{"en":"Add two cups of flour to the bowl and mix well.","zh":"把兩杯麵粉倒進碗裡，攪拌均勻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a bag of flour for the weekend baking.","zh":"她買了一袋麵粉，準備週末烘焙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f445fa0e787c44f9","term":"flour","forms":["flour","flours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標準小麥粉","explanation":"在食品標準或配料語境中，特指經過清理、研磨和篩分、達到規定細度與成分要求的小麥粉；日常說的普通烘焙用麵粉通常也屬於這個範圍。","examples":[{"en":"This recipe calls for all-purpose flour rather than bread flour.","zh":"這個食譜要求用通用麵粉，而不是高筋麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dust the board with flour before rolling dough.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e49a740aa8f7a42150b","word":"flourish","forms":["flourish"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbcddeb5428d8ca8","term":"flourish","forms":["flourish","flourishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝飾性筆觸","explanation":"指附加在簽名、書寫或設計上的華麗線條或裝飾，使整體顯得更醒目。","examples":[{"en":"He added a flourish to the last letter of his name.","zh":"他在自己名字的最後一個字母上添了一筆華麗的裝飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chef finished the dish with a flourish of herbs.","zh":"廚師用一撮香草為這道菜作了醒目的點綴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60e8efa54f962da9","term":"flourish","forms":["flourish","flourishes","flourishing","flourished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蓬勃生長","explanation":"指植物或其他有生命的東西生長旺盛、狀態良好，像花朵盛放一樣。","examples":[{"en":"These herbs flourish in the warm, sunny garden.","zh":"這些香草在溫暖、陽光充足的花園裡長得很旺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young trees flourished after the rainy season.","zh":"雨季過後，這些小樹長勢很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57945a3d36866562","term":"flourish","forms":["flourish","flourishes","flourishing","flourished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"興盛繁榮","explanation":"指城市、企業、行業或群體發展順利、越來越繁榮，是“花朵盛放”這一意象對社會事物的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses flourished after the new market opened.","zh":"新市場開張後，小企業蓬勃發展起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The port flourished under her careful management.","zh":"這個港口在她的精心管理下日益繁榮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flourish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b21278178ed3463f3bd","word":"flow","forms":["flow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28c0792c988405e9","term":"flow","forms":["flow","flows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續流動","explanation":"指人、物或大量事物連續不斷地向前移動，重點是“不斷流動”這一整體過程，不一定是液體。","examples":[{"en":"The police redirected the flow of traffic.","zh":"警方改變了交通流向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A steady flow of visitors entered the museum.","zh":"參觀者持續不斷地進入博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0045472e030bcac","term":"flow","forms":["flow","flows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"液體或比喻之物的流動","explanation":"指液體實際流動，也可比喻語言、話語等連續湧出；核心仍是某種東西不斷向外展開。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden flow of water filled the basement.","zh":"突然湧入的水流填滿了地下室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flow of angry words came from the audience.","zh":"觀眾中傳來一連串憤怒的話語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d614a72b5216cdc","term":"flow","forms":["flow","flows","flowing","flowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"流動","explanation":"指液體從一個地方連續移動到另一個地方，是flow最直接的動詞義，也是其他抽象用法的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The river flows into the sea.","zh":"這條河流入大海。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tears flowed down her cheeks.","zh":"淚水順著她的臉頰流下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-812686d9dca28480","term":"flow","forms":["flow","flows","flowing","flowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"順暢進行","explanation":"指文字、談話、動作或活動銜接自然、連續進行，沒有讓人感到卡頓；彷彿它們自己向前流動。","examples":[{"en":"The conversation flowed easily after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，談話很自然地進行下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final scene does not flow well.","zh":"最後一幕銜接得不太順暢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c06b0cfe0cc5e900c577","word":"flower","forms":["flower"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af1ce11423b573e4","term":"flower","forms":["flower","flowers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"花","explanation":"flower 最基本的意思是植物上顯眼、通常有顏色並能吸引昆蟲的花。","examples":[{"en":"She picked a yellow flower from the garden.","zh":"她從花園裡摘了一朵黃色的花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flowers attract bees in spring.","zh":"這些花在春天會吸引蜜蜂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2b2170cc217503f","term":"flower","forms":["flower","flowers","flowering","flowered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開花","explanation":"植物 flower，就是像花朵盛放一樣長出花來。","examples":[{"en":"This plant flowers in June.","zh":"這種植物在六月開花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roses flowered early this year.","zh":"這些玫瑰今年開花較早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92f75a33d5898073e05d","word":"flu","forms":["flu"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c88735239b318654","term":"flu","forms":["flu","flus"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流感","explanation":"指由流感病毒引起的疾病，通常讓人發燒、咳嗽並感到全身不適；這是 flu 最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I caught flu and had to stay home for three days.","zh":"我得了流感，只好在家待了三天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several students have flu this week.","zh":"這周有幾個學生得了流感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flu","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78ce2fc61d9030de","term":"flu","forms":["flu","flus"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腸胃型流感","explanation":"在非正式說法 stomach flu 中，flu 可指一類主要表現為嘔吐、腹瀉等胃腸不適的疾病；這裡不一定是在嚴格指真正的流感。","examples":[{"en":"The children stayed home with stomach flu.","zh":"孩子們因為腸胃型流感待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stomach flu kept him home for two days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flu","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-129df964b701d0b8e72f","word":"fluency","forms":["fluency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3532db6c201709fe","term":"fluency","forms":["fluency","fluencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流暢性","explanation":"指某種流動、表達或過程進行得平穩順暢，沒有明顯的停頓、阻滯或生硬感。它是“水流得順”這一核心畫面的直接用法，也可以描述寫作、動作或整體表現。","examples":[{"en":"The fluency of her writing made the difficult ideas easy to follow.","zh":"她的文章很流暢，讓人容易理解那些難懂的觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancers moved with surprising fluency.","zh":"舞者的動作流暢得令人驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-985e4d788c43ae98","term":"fluency","forms":["fluency","fluencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語言流利程度","explanation":"指一個人運用某種語言時能自然、連貫地聽說或讀寫的能力和程度。說某人有某種語言的 fluency，就是說他能較順暢地使用這門語言，而不只是認識一些詞。","examples":[{"en":"The job requires fluency in English and Spanish.","zh":"這份工作要求能流利使用英語和西班牙語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her fluency in Japanese improved quickly after she moved to Tokyo.","zh":"她搬到東京後，日語流利程度提高得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cebbec9619efd343f958","word":"fluent","forms":["fluent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27053690c28fa49b","term":"fluent","forms":["fluent","more fluent","most fluent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"語言流利的","explanation":"表示一個人能準確、快速而有信心地使用某種語言，表達通常連貫自然。這就像詞語在說話者腦中順暢地流出來；它不必表示完全沒有語法錯誤，也不等於一定是母語者。","examples":[{"en":"She is fluent in French and can handle business meetings with ease.","zh":"她法語很流利，可以輕鬆應對商務會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After living abroad for two years, he became fluent in Spanish.","zh":"在國外生活兩年後，他的西班牙語變得很流利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b39453c77af48d5","term":"fluent","forms":["fluent","more fluent","most fluent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"流暢的；流動自然的","explanation":"表示線條、筆跡或其他東西連續而自然地流動，沒有生硬或停頓的感覺。它和“語言流利”共享同一個核心形象：某種東西能夠順暢地向前流動。","examples":[{"en":"Her fluent handwriting was easy to read.","zh":"她流暢的筆跡很容易讀懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her fluent movements made the difficult dance look effortless.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e0502adfb96f1f1544d","word":"fluid","forms":["fluid"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29a6e52afbab279d","term":"fluid","forms":["fluid","more fluid","most fluid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"流體的；流動的","explanation":"指與能夠流動的物質有關，或具有流體性質；重點是它不會保持固定形狀，而會流動、變形。","examples":[{"en":"The experiment measures fluid pressure at different depths.","zh":"這項實驗測量不同深度的流體壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancer moved with fluid grace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ce59313115d9395","term":"fluid","forms":["fluid","more fluid","most fluid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易變的；尚未確定的","explanation":"把“能流動、沒有固定形狀”的特點用於計劃、局勢或安排，表示它們還在變化，不能當作最終確定的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The project schedule is still fluid, so the launch date may change.","zh":"專案日程還沒有確定，因此釋出日期可能會變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our plans are fluid until we hear from the client.","zh":"在得到客戶的訊息前，我們的計劃都還可能調整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67b815c6d1bbfd20","term":"fluid","forms":["fluid","more fluid","most fluid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"流暢的；動作連貫的","explanation":"形容動作像液體流動一樣連續、自然，不顯得僵硬或突然停頓，尤其常用於身體動作、舞蹈和表達。","examples":[{"en":"The dancer's fluid movements made the routine look effortless.","zh":"舞者流暢的動作讓整套舞步看起來毫不費力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The swimmer's fluid stroke barely disturbed the surface.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd3959a721e5dd15","term":"fluid","forms":["fluid","fluids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流體","explanation":"指容易流動、會隨容器形狀變化的物質，科學上包括液體、氣體和等離子體。","examples":[{"en":"Air is a fluid, even though we cannot see it.","zh":"空氣是一種流體，儘管我們看不見它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Air behaves as a fluid around the wing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e7305a30288688934e9","word":"flunk","forms":["flunk"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"flunk","forms":["flunk"],"pos":"v.","zh":"考試不及格；使不及格","examples":[{"en":"You might flunk the course if you miss the final exam.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The instructor will flunk anyone caught cheating.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-f56175f2116fbf22b394","word":"flush","forms":["flush"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6160c0b32bd3cf4c","term":"flush","forms":["flush","flushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沖廁所","explanation":"水一下子湧入並把廁所裡的東西衝走，這個flush就是一次沖廁所或沖水。","examples":[{"en":"The toilet needs another flush.","zh":"這個廁所還需要再衝一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I heard the flush while I was brushing my teeth.","zh":"我刷牙時聽到了沖廁所的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e3eb0c7097f9423","term":"flush","forms":["flush","flushes","flushing","flushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"沖廁所","explanation":"向馬桶中放入大量水，把裡面的排洩物沖走；這是 flush 在日常生活中最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"Please flush the toilet after you use it.","zh":"用完廁所後請沖水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toilet won't flush because the tank is empty.","zh":"水箱是空的，所以馬桶無法沖水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8eb4c314f3226542","term":"flush","forms":["flush","flushes","flushing","flushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"臉紅","explanation":"血液、熱氣或強烈情緒突然湧到臉上，使臉變紅；這與“湧動並鋪滿”這一核心畫面相符。","examples":[{"en":"She flushed with embarrassment when everyone looked at her.","zh":"大家看著她時，她尷尬得臉紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His face flushed after he ran up the stairs.","zh":"他跑上樓梯後，臉漲紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c52c4fb88926f84bcbc3","word":"flute","forms":["flute"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f200832c84df0e97","term":"flute","forms":["flute","flutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長笛","explanation":"一種有指孔、透過氣流發聲的木管樂器；現代英語中通常首先指橫吹的西方長笛。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter has been learning to play the flute.","zh":"我女兒一直在學吹長笛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The musician lifted the flute and began the solo.","zh":"音樂家舉起長笛，開始獨奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4debdb7ab7dd958e95c","word":"fly","forms":["fly"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55e9258cabbed84b","term":"fly","forms":["fly","flies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雙翅目昆蟲","explanation":"泛指雙翅目昆蟲，也就是通常只有一對翅膀、能在空中飛行的一大類昆蟲；蒼蠅、蚊子和蚋等都屬於這一大類。","examples":[{"en":"A fly landed on the window and rubbed its legs together.","zh":"一隻飛蟲落在窗戶上，不停地搓動腿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many flies are attracted to bright lights at night.","zh":"許多雙翅目昆蟲在夜間會被明亮的燈光吸引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed77172c6290f49a","term":"fly","forms":["fly","flies","flying","flew","flown","fliest","flyest","flewest","flieth","flyeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"飛；飛行","explanation":"表示人、鳥或其他事物離開地面，在空中移動；也可以泛指乘坐飛行器前往某地。這正對應“離開地面、在空中移動”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Many birds fly south before winter arrives.","zh":"許多鳥在冬天到來前飛往南方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We flew to Shanghai for the holiday.","zh":"我們乘飛機去了上海度假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8cc2cd79785b73d701b8","word":"foam","forms":["foam"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88c1e10c76cd983f","term":"foam","forms":["foam","foams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"泡沫；泡沫團","explanation":"指許多氣泡聚集在一起形成的物質，常見於液體表面，也可以指氣泡凝固或聚集後留下的泡沫狀物。","examples":[{"en":"A thick layer of foam covered the surface of the soup.","zh":"湯的表面覆蓋著一層厚厚的泡沫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soap made a lot of foam in the sink.","zh":"肥皂在水槽裡產生了很多泡沫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8e2eb0bd7e6b0e1","term":"foam","forms":["foam","foams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"泡沫材料","explanation":"指在液體或固體內部封住許多氣體小孔而形成的輕質、多孔材料，例如泡沫墊或泡沫塑膠。","examples":[{"en":"A foam mat made the hard floor more comfortable.","zh":"泡沫墊讓堅硬的地面坐起來舒服多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Foam padding protected the delicate glass ornaments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59b68f501812da6f","term":"foam","forms":["foam","foams","foaming","foamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起泡；冒泡沫","explanation":"表示液體或其他表面形成、產生泡沫，是名詞 foam 的直接動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The river foamed as it rushed over the rocks.","zh":"河水衝過岩石時泛起了泡沫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The milk began to foam when I heated it.","zh":"牛奶加熱後開始起泡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c51faa148557a08cbf79","word":"focus","forms":["focus"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eee1298f1c27b34f","term":"focus","forms":["focus","foci","focuses","focusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光學焦點","explanation":"指光線經過反射或折射後匯聚到的點。放大鏡把陽光集中到一點時，這一點就是 focus。","examples":[{"en":"The sunlight was hot enough to burn the paper at the focus of the lens.","zh":"透鏡焦點處的陽光熱到足以燒著紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lens brings sunlight to a single focus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/focus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57b6903c10873e68","term":"focus","forms":["focus","foci","focuses","focusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"注意力集中","explanation":"指把注意力集中起來的狀態或能力。一個人能夠長時間專心工作，就可以說他有很好的 focus。","examples":[{"en":"You need great focus to finish this difficult task.","zh":"完成這項困難的任務需要高度的專注力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The noise made sustained focus almost impossible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/focus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d810d43ec4c1e8d2","term":"focus","forms":["focus","foci","focuses","focusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關注重點","explanation":"指某項活動、討論或興趣主要指向的人或事，也就是當前最重要的中心。","examples":[{"en":"Improving public transport is the main focus of the new plan.","zh":"改善公共交通是新計劃的主要重點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Affordable housing became the focus of the campaign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/focus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0c135f122c9ffaa","term":"focus","forms":["focus","focuses","focusses","focusing","focussing","focused","focussed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把注意力或精力集中於","explanation":"指把注意力、努力或精力有意識地指向某個物件、任務或人群，就像把光線匯到一箇中心點。","examples":[{"en":"The team focused its efforts on reducing waiting times.","zh":"團隊把精力集中在縮短等待時間上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Focus your attention on the speaker's main argument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/focus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85586d0f51f14dfc","term":"focus","forms":["focus","focuses","focusses","focusing","focussing","focused","focussed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"集中注意力","explanation":"指讓自己的注意力集中起來，保持專心。","examples":[{"en":"Take a short break, then try to focus again.","zh":"短暫休息一下，然後再試著集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Focus on the rhythm before increasing your speed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/focus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc2ec41096438914","term":"focus","forms":["focus","focuses","focusses","focusing","focussing","focused","focussed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"專注於某事","explanation":"指把注意力集中在某件具體事情上，或讓某事成為自己最主要的關注物件。","examples":[{"en":"I need to focus on finishing this report today.","zh":"我需要專心在今天完成這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let's focus on solving the immediate problem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/focus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4608c52cd46a96450a48","word":"foe","forms":["foe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c56e189d9b7c41d","term":"foe","forms":["foe","foes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敵人；對手","explanation":"指與某人或某方敵對的人，也可以較寬泛地指競爭中站在對立面的一方。核心畫面就是“站在你對面的人”，由此可以理解它和過時形容詞義“敵對的”的聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The hero finally defeated his greatest foe.","zh":"主人公最終擊敗了自己最大的敵人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even a former foe can become an ally.","zh":"即使曾經的敵人也可能成為盟友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b04216546057e8659fec","word":"fog","forms":["fog"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1508a1b6df71f53","term":"fog","forms":["fog","fogs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"濃霧","explanation":"指貼近地面、濃得會遮擋視線的霧；核心畫面就是一層把遠處景物遮住的雲霧。","examples":[{"en":"A thick fog covered the road before sunrise.","zh":"日出前，一場濃霧籠罩了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plane was delayed because of fog.","zh":"飛機因大霧晚點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fd0dc9717ecbc35","term":"fog","forms":["fog","fogs","fogging","fogged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起霧","explanation":"指某處被霧覆蓋，或像被霧覆蓋一樣變得看不清，是名詞“霧”變成動作的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The road fogged over as evening fell.","zh":"天黑下來時，道路被霧遮住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mirror fogged when she opened the shower door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22f44dee8d6e393f6a46","word":"foggy","forms":["foggy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13b39f00b8e64603","term":"foggy","forms":["foggy","foggier","foggiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"霧濛濛的；模糊不清的","explanation":"指空氣中有霧，使景物、道路或視線變得模糊，看不清楚；也可引申為事情或畫面不夠清楚。","examples":[{"en":"The road was foggy, so we drove slowly.","zh":"路上霧很大，所以我們開得很慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a foggy morning by the river.","zh":"我們在河邊度過了一個霧濛濛的早晨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foggy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5817ca383d1080f","term":"foggy","forms":["foggy","foggier","foggiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"頭腦昏沉的；糊里糊塗的","explanation":"把“被霧遮住”的感覺用於人的頭腦，表示剛睡醒、疲倦或身體不適時思路不清、反應遲鈍。","examples":[{"en":"I felt foggy after sleeping for only four hours.","zh":"我只睡了四個小時，醒來後覺得頭腦昏沉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the sleepless night, my thinking felt foggy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foggy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-255541b1d8c6185596fd","word":"fold","forms":["fold"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0d61e9b82183fba","term":"fold","forms":["fold","folds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摺疊一下","explanation":"指把紙、布等東西摺疊這一下，重點是這個動作形成的摺疊，而不是摺疊的物件本身；這和記憶中的“向內折”直接相關。","examples":[{"en":"Give the blanket a fold before you put it away.","zh":"把毯子折一下再收起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One more fold will make the sheet fit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8522aea238f81831","term":"fold","forms":["fold","folds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牲畜圈","explanation":"指圈養羊或其他家畜的圍欄或封閉場地；這是把動物向內圍住的“摺疊、收攏”概念具體化了。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer led the sheep back into the fold before dark.","zh":"天黑前，農夫把羊趕回了羊圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shepherd led the lambs into the fold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f99277b6b251960","term":"fold","forms":["fold","folds","folding","folded","folden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"摺疊","explanation":"把紙、布等薄而柔韌的東西向內彎折，使它的一部分接觸或貼近另一部分，就像把平面收攏起來形成摺痕。","examples":[{"en":"She folded the letter and put it in her pocket.","zh":"她把信摺好，放進了口袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fold the blanket neatly over the chair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed88a83307fe1d42","term":"fold","forms":["fold","folds","folding","folded","folden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"失敗；垮掉；解散","explanation":"指個人、計劃、組織或活動因為缺乏支撐而徹底失敗、垮掉或解散；這是把“折下去”的畫面引申到事情上。","examples":[{"en":"The small project folded after its main sponsor pulled out.","zh":"主要贊助方退出後，這個小專案失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The magazine folded after losing its main advertiser.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcbbae7c00b4d07dc1e4","word":"folk","forms":["folk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa1067a91f42957b","term":"folk","forms":["folk","folks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人們；普通人","explanation":"指一群人，常帶有親切、非正式的語氣；它把一群普通人看成一個共同體。","examples":[{"en":"There were plenty of folk at the market this morning.","zh":"今天早上市集上有很多人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival attracts folk from neighboring villages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/folk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48bdab03a9a997f9c435","word":"folklore","forms":["folklore"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-986d0013f1e34fb3","term":"folklore","forms":["folklore","folklores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"民族或地區的民間傳統","explanation":"指某個民族或人口群體共同流傳的故事、傳說、迷信和傳統，是“民間記憶包”最典型的內容。它不只包括故事，也包括人們相信什麼、怎樣慶祝和怎樣傳承習俗。","examples":[{"en":"The museum explores the folklore of the mountain villages.","zh":"這家博物館介紹山區村莊的民間傳統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many local festivals grew out of ancient folklore.","zh":"許多地方節日都源自古老的民間傳說和習俗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/folklore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10ce3891ed04b6e9","term":"folklore","forms":["folklore","folklores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某個群體的共同傳說和說法","explanation":"把核心概念從民族擴大到任何共同體：一個社群、行業、興趣圈或網路群體都可能有自己的 folklore。這裡強調的是群體內部反覆流傳、大家都聽過或認可的故事、笑話、迷信和習慣說法。","examples":[{"en":"That story has become part of the folklore of the film industry.","zh":"那個故事已經成了電影業內部廣為流傳的一部分傳說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing portrait became part of the school's folklore.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/folklore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3ce0b6106cdb3982d7b","word":"follow","forms":["follow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-199f9fd1e3fb7fe4","term":"follow","forms":["follow","follows","following","followed","followest","followedst","followeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跟隨；追趕","explanation":"沿著另一個人、車輛或物體的路線在後面走或移動，常帶有想追上對方的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Follow me and stay close.","zh":"跟著我，別離得太遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police followed the car for several miles.","zh":"警察跟著那輛車走了好幾英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/follow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da3a682fb1691369","term":"follow","forms":["follow","follows","following","followed","followest","followedst","followeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵照；執行","explanation":"沿著別人給出的步驟或路線去做，因此表示按照命令、建議、規則或說明執行。","examples":[{"en":"Please follow the instructions on the package.","zh":"請按照包裝上的說明操作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He followed his doctor's advice and rested at home.","zh":"他聽從醫生的建議，在家休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/follow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-837f152eb60b0863","term":"follow","forms":["follow","follows","following","followed","followest","followedst","followeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"理解；聽懂","explanation":"表示思路跟得上，所以能理解別人正在解釋的內容；“Do you follow me?”就是在問對方是否聽懂了。","examples":[{"en":"I understand the first step, but I don't follow the rest.","zh":"第一步我明白，但後面的內容我沒聽懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you following what I'm saying?","zh":"你聽得懂我在說什麼嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/follow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-074cdde4132a64f0abe7","word":"follower","forms":["follower"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce3738f0b9d321d2","term":"follower","forms":["follower","followers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跟隨者","explanation":"指跟在另一個人後面、隨著對方行動的人，重點是實際的身體跟隨。這是 follower 最直接的“跟在後面的人”這一基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"The guide walked ahead, with several followers behind him.","zh":"嚮導走在前面，身後跟著幾個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The king entered the hall with his followers.","zh":"國王帶著跟隨者走進了大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/follower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9cde97a84784d0c","term":"follower","forms":["follower","followers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擁護者；信徒","explanation":"指在思想、信仰、政治立場或行動上跟隨某個人、團體或運動的人。這裡的“跟隨”從身體行動擴充套件到了思想和立場上的認同。","examples":[{"en":"She is a devoted follower of the environmental movement.","zh":"她是環保運動的忠實擁護者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many followers of the teacher gathered outside the school.","zh":"那位老師的許多追隨者聚集在學校外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/follower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cf9aec78649c28a","term":"follower","forms":["follower","followers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社交媒體關注者","explanation":"在社交媒體上，指訂閱某個賬號、從而可以看到該賬號內容的人。它是“線上跟著某個賬號”的現代用法，中文常譯為“關注者”或“粉絲”。","examples":[{"en":"Her travel account gained thousands of followers this year.","zh":"她的旅行賬號今年獲得了數千名關注者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a few followers saw his latest post.","zh":"只有少數關注者看到了他最新發布的內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/follower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d0288f434f2ff12a3dd","word":"following","forms":["following"],"officialPos":"adj./prep./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eecf50533f447ef4","term":"following","forms":["following"],"pos":"adj","zh":"接下來的；下面的","explanation":"指在順序或時間上緊接著前面內容出現的事物，也就是“後面的、接下來的”。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the following instructions carefully.","zh":"請仔細閱讀以下說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The following day, we returned to the village.","zh":"第二天，我們回到了村子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/following","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34856ebcba4f9358","term":"following","forms":["following","followings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"追隨者群體","explanation":"指支援、欣賞或跟隨某人的一群人，可以是公眾人物、藝術家、思想家等的擁護者。","examples":[{"en":"The singer has a large following among young people.","zh":"這位歌手在年輕人中擁有一大批支持者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her online following grew quickly after the video went viral.","zh":"那段影片走紅後，她在網上的追隨者迅速增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/following","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-922a80e5382ae15a","term":"following","forms":["following","followings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下列內容；下文","explanation":"the following 可以把後面馬上出現的一項或多項內容整體當作名詞，意思是“下列內容”或“下面這段話”。","examples":[{"en":"The following is a summary of the report.","zh":"以下是這份報告的摘要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please bring the following: gloves, boots, and a torch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/following","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3c7f93158f6e98a4a3e","word":"fond","forms":["fond"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-378da25651025053","term":"fond","forms":["fond","fonder","fondest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"喜愛；喜歡","explanation":"表示對某人或某物有明顯的好感，心裡願意親近它；這是 fond 最常見、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I'm very fond of this old photograph.","zh":"我很喜歡這張老照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is fond of walking by the river after work.","zh":"她喜歡下班後沿著河邊散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9500f5b69b74d65d","term":"fond","forms":["fond","fonder","fondest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親切的；充滿感情的","explanation":"形容一個動作、語氣或告別帶著溫柔和感情，讓人感到親暱，而不只是單純表示喜歡。","examples":[{"en":"They shared a fond goodbye before he left for college.","zh":"他去上大學前，他們溫情地道了別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave his old teacher a fond smile.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1f026582fe6e8cb620d","word":"food","forms":["food"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c638286412230460","term":"food","forms":["food","foods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"食物；吃的東西","explanation":"指人或動物為了維持生命而吃下的東西，是 food 最基本、最常用的意思。它強調“可供食用的養料”這一整體概念，通常不數單個單位。","examples":[{"en":"The innkeeper brought us food and drink.","zh":"客棧老闆給我們送來了食物和飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Make sure the dog has enough food.","zh":"要確保這隻狗有足夠的食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/food","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2534ff0766d7644e","term":"food","forms":["food","foods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種食品；食品種類","explanation":"指可以單獨區分的一種食品或一類食品。這時 food 可以用複數，表示多種食品或不同種類的食物。","examples":[{"en":"The market sells foods from many different countries.","zh":"這家市場出售來自許多不同國家的食品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fermented foods are popular in many cultures.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/food","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18679f10e50678804a44","word":"fool","forms":["fool"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0227eff2cb9b86fb","term":"fool","forms":["fool","fools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傻瓜；判斷力差的人","explanation":"指判斷力差、做事不明智或智力不高的人，是fool最基本的名詞形象。它通常帶有批評或貶低意味，但有時也可用於自嘲。","examples":[{"en":"You were a fool to drive so fast in the rain.","zh":"你在雨裡開得這麼快，真是太不明智了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt like a fool after I missed the obvious clue.","zh":"錯過那個明顯的線索後，我覺得自己像個傻瓜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd1999059ddb8ed2","term":"fool","forms":["fool","fools","fooling","fooled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欺騙；愚弄","explanation":"指透過假象、騙局或誤導使某人相信錯誤的事情，讓對方暫時處在“傻瓜”位置上。","examples":[{"en":"The fake email fooled several customers into sharing their passwords.","zh":"那封假郵件騙了好幾位顧客，讓他們交出了密碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't let the simple design fool you.","zh":"別被簡單的設計騙了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d305fd473f327e1003d","word":"foolish","forms":["foolish"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2a3541fedf3af3e","term":"foolish","forms":["foolish","more foolish","most foolish"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不明智的","explanation":"形容某個行動、決定或做法缺乏常識和良好判斷，結果可能給自己帶來麻煩。重點是“這件事做得不對或不值得”，不一定是在斷言當事人天生愚笨。","examples":[{"en":"It was foolish to ignore the warning.","zh":"無視那個警告是不明智的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Buying the car without checking the price was foolish.","zh":"沒查價格就買下那輛車，實在不明智。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foolish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15162953febebf99","term":"foolish","forms":["foolish","more foolish","most foolish"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傻氣的；愚笨的","explanation":"形容人、表情、語氣或行為帶有傻瓜般的特點，顯得傻乎乎或不夠機靈。這裡的重點從“做錯了判斷”擴充套件到“整體表現像個傻瓜”。","examples":[{"en":"His foolish grin made everyone laugh.","zh":"他那傻乎乎的笑容把大家都逗笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was foolish to ignore the warning signs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foolish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22e4f6912a6980d6fd59","word":"foot","forms":["foot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c8e7ece7c8b49bf","term":"foot","forms":["foot","feet"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的腳","explanation":"指腳踝以下、用來站立和行走的人體部分；記憶時可以把它看成身體最下面、負責支撐身體的“承託物”。","examples":[{"en":"I stepped on a sharp stone and hurt my left foot.","zh":"我踩到一塊尖石頭，左腳受傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stood on one foot while tying her shoe.","zh":"她單腳站著繫鞋帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0247f7df68f1d08e","term":"foot","forms":["foot","feet"],"pos":"noun","zh":"底部；根部","explanation":"指物體最下面、起支撐或邊界作用的部分，就像物體也有一個“腳下”位置。","examples":[{"en":"A small café stands at the foot of the hill.","zh":"山腳下有一家小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave your boots at the foot of the stairs.","zh":"把你的靴子放在樓梯腳下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-951978930b47d74b","term":"foot","forms":["foot","feet"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英尺","explanation":"英美製長度單位，等於十二英寸，也就是準確的30.48釐米；可以把它記成由“腳的長度”引申出來的單位。","examples":[{"en":"The room is twelve feet wide and eight feet long.","zh":"這個房間寬十二英尺，長八英尺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A six-foot fence surrounds the garden.","zh":"花園四周圍著一堵六英尺高的圍牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc320197803a380a","term":"foot","forms":["foot","foots","footing","footed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支付賬單","explanation":"表示承擔並支付一筆賬單或費用，就像“承擔腳下的賬”一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The company footed the bill for our train tickets.","zh":"公司承擔了我們的火車票費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Who is going to foot the repair costs?","zh":"誰來承擔維修費用？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6382deaf1f5dc6e792b7","word":"football","forms":["football"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b60803558be2e9a","term":"football","forms":["football","footballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"足球運動","explanation":"泛指在場上用腳踢球、讓球進入對方球門或得分割槽域的團隊運動；它是football最基本的概念。","examples":[{"en":"My children play football after school.","zh":"我的孩子們放學後踢足球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Football brings people together in many countries.","zh":"在許多國家，足球把人們團結在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/football","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aeb75f5a48fbdf85","term":"football","forms":["football","footballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英式足球","explanation":"在英國、非洲部分地區、加勒比地區和南亞等地，football通常特指兩隊主要用腳把圓球踢進對方球門的英式足球，也就是很多地方所說的soccer。","examples":[{"en":"We watched football at the pub last night.","zh":"我們昨晚在酒吧看了英式足球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wants to become a professional football player.","zh":"她想成為一名職業足球運動員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/football","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-040dafb74672be47","term":"football","forms":["football","footballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美式橄欖球","explanation":"在美國，football通常指美式橄欖球：兩隊爭取得分，把橢圓形球推進到對方場地的底線區域。","examples":[{"en":"My brother plays football for his college team.","zh":"我哥哥在大學校隊打美式橄欖球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The football season starts in September.","zh":"美式橄欖球賽季從九月開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/football","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10c22bcf4c768b515be4","word":"for","forms":["for"],"officialPos":"prep./conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a0e41bc03cfb6fa","term":"for","forms":["for"],"pos":"prep","zh":"給；面向","explanation":"箭頭指向某人，表示某物是給這個人的，或某個動作、資訊是面向這個人的。","examples":[{"en":"I saved the last piece of cake for you.","zh":"我把最後一塊蛋糕留給你了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a message for you at the front desk.","zh":"前臺有一條給你的留言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f6f71f973ec35f9","term":"for","forms":["for"],"pos":"prep","zh":"為了某人的利益","explanation":"箭頭指向某人的利益，表示做某事是為了幫助、取悅、尊重或造福某人或某物。","examples":[{"en":"She worked late for her family.","zh":"她為了家人工作到很晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I made this card for my teacher.","zh":"我為老師做了這張卡片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dee36e1fb136347f","term":"for","forms":["for"],"pos":"prep","zh":"因為；由於","explanation":"箭頭指向一個原因，說明某種行為或結果是由這個原因引起的。","examples":[{"en":"He missed the bus, and for that reason he was late.","zh":"他沒趕上公共汽車，因此遲到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers were praised for their courage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc29d16b9552909d","term":"for","forms":["for"],"pos":"prep","zh":"引出不定式的主語","explanation":"箭頭指向接下來要做的動作，並明確指出是誰來做這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"It is important for everyone to listen carefully.","zh":"每個人認真聽都很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was no time for us to discuss the issue.","zh":"我們沒有時間討論這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-76626ec9e79c1c457cae","word":"forbid","forms":["forbid"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5edcbdb6087a3c3","term":"forbid","forms":["forbid","forbids","forbidding","forbade","forbad","forbidded","forbidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"禁止；不準","explanation":"指以規則、命令或權威明確規定某事不可以做，就像在某個入口立下“禁止通行”的命令。這是 forbid 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The school forbids students from using phones during exams.","zh":"學校禁止學生在考試期間使用手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parking is forbidden in front of the emergency exit.","zh":"緊急出口前禁止停車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forbid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a039a5d076292005","term":"forbid","forms":["forbid","forbids","forbidding","forbade","forbad","forbidded","forbidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"禁止某人進入或接近","explanation":"強呼叫明確命令把某人排除在某處或某件事之外，相當於不準某人進入、參加或接觸。現代英語通常把它表達為禁止某人做某事，而不是直接說禁止某人某物。","examples":[{"en":"The manager forbade him from entering the building.","zh":"經理禁止他進入那棟大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His mother forbade him the house after their quarrel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forbid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32500d7500ce0755c1a0","word":"force","forms":["force"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7fedb9b36dfcc367","term":"force","forms":["force","forces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影響力；力量","explanation":"指推動人或事物發生改變的力量，可以來自身體、思想、論點、呼籲或規則等；重點是它能產生影響或效果。","examples":[{"en":"The force of her argument persuaded the committee.","zh":"她的論點很有說服力，最終說服了委員會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pushed the door with all his force.","zh":"他用盡全力推門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/force","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0d0dfb49af52220","term":"force","forms":["force","forces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物理學中的力","explanation":"在物理學中，force 是能推動、拉動、扭轉或加速物體的有方向的力，單位通常是牛頓。它仍然體現“推動事物改變的力量”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The force of gravity keeps the Moon in orbit.","zh":"引力使月球保持在軌道上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A force of 10 newtons pushed the box forward.","zh":"一個十牛頓的力把箱子向前推。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/force","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47b4995b13e2c37f","term":"force","forms":["force","forces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強制力；暴力","explanation":"指違揹他人意願或未經同意而施加的力量，可能表現為強迫、威脅或暴力。它是“推動改變的力量”轉為壓制他人意願的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The protesters were removed by force.","zh":"抗議者被強行帶走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one should be forced to sign a contract by force.","zh":"任何人都不應被強迫簽署合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/force","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcdae8cfc185d4f2","term":"force","forms":["force","forces","forcing","forced","forcest","forcedst","forceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迫使某人做某事","explanation":"把“推動事物改變的力量”施加到人身上，使對方即使不願意也不得不做某事。","examples":[{"en":"The storm forced us to cancel the picnic.","zh":"暴風雨迫使我們取消了野餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one can force you to accept the offer.","zh":"沒有人能強迫你接受這份提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/force","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59f0db478528b4c446cf","word":"forecast","forms":["forecast"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46fb290f612f2346","term":"forecast","forms":["forecast","forecasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預測；預報","explanation":"對未來可能出現的情況作出的估計，就是一份“先看未來”的判斷；天氣預報、經濟預測和銷售預測都可以用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"The weather forecast says it will rain tomorrow.","zh":"天氣預報說，明天會下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The latest sales forecast is more optimistic.","zh":"最新的銷售預測更加樂觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forecast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc4b6a3b235009d2","term":"forecast","forms":["forecast","forecasts","forecasting","forecasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預測；預報","explanation":"根據已有資訊判斷未來會怎樣，尤其常用於天氣、經濟、需求和結果等話題。","examples":[{"en":"Experts forecast higher demand for electric cars next year.","zh":"專家預測明年對電動汽車的需求會增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app forecasts storms several hours in advance.","zh":"這個應用會提前幾小時預報暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forecast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-656771905e1ef731f65c","word":"foreign","forms":["foreign"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18e04ef45e7e521d","term":"foreign","forms":["foreign","more foreign","most foreign"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外國的；在外地的","explanation":"指位於本國、本地或所討論範圍之外的地方或事物，核心感覺是“在外面”。","examples":[{"en":"The company is expanding into foreign markets.","zh":"這家公司正在拓展外國市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers were ordered to remain on foreign soil.","zh":"士兵奉命留在外國土地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foreign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcf97708c3eafb9a","term":"foreign","forms":["foreign","more foreign","most foreign"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外國的；來自別處的","explanation":"指來自、屬於或具有另一個國家或地方特點的人、物或活動，重點是來源或歸屬不同。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a foreign car because it was more reliable.","zh":"她買了一輛外國車，因為它更可靠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum exhibits pottery from foreign countries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foreign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9391007239d7d05cdaa","word":"foreigner","forms":["foreigner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69dbdde21ebfad15","term":"foreigner","forms":["foreigner","foreigners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外國人","explanation":"指來自另一個國家、目前處在所談國家之外或其中的人。這個詞的核心畫面就是“從外國跨過邊界來到這裡的人”。","examples":[{"en":"She has lived here for years, but people still treat her as a foreigner.","zh":"她已經在這裡生活多年了，但人們仍把她當作外國人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum offers information in several languages for foreign visitors.","zh":"這座博物館為外國遊客提供多種語言的資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foreigner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-619a2ccf126ce837dc7c","word":"forest","forms":["forest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c6ec502a0bcfdcf","term":"forest","forms":["forest","forests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"森林；大片林地","explanation":"指由大量樹木和下層植物密集組成、規模通常比普通樹林更大的自然區域。它是forest最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"They spent the afternoon walking through the forest.","zh":"他們整個下午都在森林裡散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow path leads deep into the forest.","zh":"一條小路通向森林深處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be4c56b3eb01883f","term":"forest","forms":["forest","forests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"密集的一大片","explanation":"可把任何事物比作密密麻麻、鋪展開來的一大片，例如大量建築、標誌或批評意見。重點不是樹木，而是“數量很多並形成一片”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"A forest of antennas covered the rooftops.","zh":"屋頂上密密麻麻地佈滿了天線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Raised hands formed a forest around the visiting singer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2070f725ff1c765b73c4","word":"forever","forms":["forever"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-665afb72b0dc79cf","term":"forever","forms":["forever"],"pos":"adv","zh":"永遠；永恆地","explanation":"表示某個動作或狀態持續到沒有盡頭，強調“始終如此”。它可以用於承諾、感情、記憶等持續時間很長的事情。","examples":[{"en":"I will remember this day forever.","zh":"我永遠會記得這一天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They promised to stay together forever.","zh":"他們承諾永遠在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-71b41d6dd48dc58eba8f","word":"forge","forms":["forge"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d51e06f57562ffda","term":"forge","forms":["forge","forges","forging","forged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鍛造金屬","explanation":"forge 表示把金屬加熱後反覆敲打，使它變成所需的形狀；這是名詞“鍛造爐”所對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The craftsman forged the blade by hand.","zh":"工匠手工鍛造了這把刀刃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smith forged the hot iron into a horseshoe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6630c3e33905164","term":"forge","forms":["forge","forges","forging","forged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"努力建立","explanation":"forge 可引申為透過持續努力“打造”關係、聯盟、道路或計劃，強調從無到有地形成穩固成果。","examples":[{"en":"The two groups forged a strong partnership.","zh":"這兩個團體建立了牢固的合作關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She forged a new path for young artists.","zh":"她為年輕藝術家開闢了一條新道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-babc1bd8ec812c742b45","word":"forget","forms":["forget"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f59aefa4f964ba3a","term":"forget","forms":["forget","forgets","forgetting","forgot","forgat","forgotten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忘記；記不起","explanation":"指記憶從腦中滑脫，想不起原本知道的人、事或資訊。重點是“記不住了”，不一定表示從來沒有接觸過。","examples":[{"en":"I forgot her name as soon as she introduced herself.","zh":"她一介紹自己的名字，我馬上就忘了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't forget what I told you.","zh":"別忘了我告訴你的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forget","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3e04dda34944ca2","term":"forget","forms":["forget","forgets","forgetting","forgot","forgat","forgotten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忘了做；疏忽漏做","explanation":"指本來應該做某事，卻因為忘記而沒有做。這裡滑脫的是“要做這件事”的記憶，所以常帶有疏忽意味。","examples":[{"en":"I forgot to call my mother yesterday.","zh":"我昨天忘了給媽媽打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't forget to lock the door.","zh":"請別忘了鎖門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forget","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b06b788c4234e67fac9","word":"forgive","forms":["forgive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9659c1b80e7a5304","term":"forgive","forms":["forgive","forgives","forgiving","forgave","forgiven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"原諒某人","explanation":"不再因為某人的錯誤而生氣、懲罰或要求報復，相當於把這件事放下。既可用於嚴重過錯，也常用於遲到、打擾等日常小事。","examples":[{"en":"Please forgive me for arriving so late.","zh":"請原諒我來得這麼晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She forgave him after he gave a sincere apology.","zh":"他真誠道歉後，她原諒了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forgive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fa9443e9d20512c","term":"forgive","forms":["forgive","forgives","forgiving","forgave","forgiven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"原諒某事","explanation":"把某個錯誤、冒犯或令人不快的行為放下，不再因此責怪或追究相關的人。","examples":[{"en":"Can you forgive my careless remark?","zh":"你能原諒我那句不經意的話嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She forgave his thoughtless remark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forgive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d0c7ac992af2f4913b4","word":"fork","forms":["fork"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8311d4fcb9c43437","term":"fork","forms":["fork","forks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"叉子；叉狀工具","explanation":"有尖齒、用於叉取或挖掘等用途的叉狀工具，餐叉是最常見的一種。","examples":[{"en":"She picked up a fork and tasted the salad.","zh":"她拿起叉子嚐了嚐沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener used a fork to loosen the soil.","zh":"園丁用叉狀工具鬆了鬆土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fork","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da6c9f990ab95b14","term":"fork","forms":["fork","forks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道路分岔處","explanation":"道路分成兩個或多個方向的地方，就像叉子的齒從一個柄處分開。","examples":[{"en":"At the fork in the road, take the left path.","zh":"到了岔路口，走左邊那條路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stopped at the fork to check the map.","zh":"我們在岔路口停下來檢視地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fork","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e78e4314d1c7e389","term":"fork","forms":["fork","forks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人生岔路口；選擇時刻","explanation":"在比喻中，人生到了必須在兩條道路或兩種方向之間作選擇的時刻，也被看作一個 fork。","examples":[{"en":"After college, she reached a fork in the road.","zh":"大學畢業後，她到了人生的岔路口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At this fork in my career, I chose teaching.","zh":"在職業生涯的這個岔路口，我選擇了教書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fork","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07397d633f25a7101990","word":"form","forms":["form"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-15c2c82b577cc4ae","term":"form","forms":["form","forms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"形狀；外形","explanation":"指人或物呈現出來的形狀、外觀或整體樣子，是 form 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The sculpture has a simple, elegant form.","zh":"這座雕塑的形狀簡潔而優雅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clouds began to form strange forms above the hills.","zh":"雲朵開始在山上空形成奇特的形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/form","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e209519122662a6","term":"form","forms":["form","forms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"形式；結構；組織方式","explanation":"指事物被組織起來的結構或運作方式；它把“外形”推廣到了制度、活動和社會關係。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting took the form of an open discussion.","zh":"會議採取了公開討論的形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The disease can appear in several forms.","zh":"這種疾病可能以幾種形式出現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/form","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39b48f67b6075e9a","term":"form","forms":["form","forms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表格；填寫用的檔案","explanation":"指預先排好專案、留出空白讓人填寫的檔案；這是現代日常英語中非常重要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please fill in this form before your appointment.","zh":"請在預約前填寫這張表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I submitted the application form yesterday.","zh":"我昨天提交了申請表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/form","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-263045b8cd857cb8","term":"form","forms":["form","forms","forming","formed","formest","formedst","formeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"形成某種形狀","explanation":"指人或物呈現出某種具體形狀或排列方式，是名詞“形狀”義直接變成動詞。","examples":[{"en":"Please form a line behind the counter.","zh":"請在櫃檯後面排成一隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancers formed a circle on the stage.","zh":"舞者們在舞臺上圍成了一個圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/form","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91a35b51f4494217","term":"form","forms":["form","forms","forming","formed","formest","formedst","formeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塑造；使成形","explanation":"指主動把某物塑造成特定形狀，也可以引申為塑造人的性格或能力。","examples":[{"en":"Roll the dough to form a thin circle.","zh":"把麵糰擀成薄薄的圓形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Early experiences form a child's character.","zh":"早期經歷會塑造孩子的性格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/form","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8df7b62c8ef6fb3e","term":"form","forms":["form","forms","forming","formed","formest","formedst","formeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"形成；成形","explanation":"指某物自行逐漸出現或成形，主語通常是雲、冰、佇列、想法等。","examples":[{"en":"Ice began to form on the lake overnight.","zh":"湖面上的冰在一夜之間開始形成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plan is beginning to form in my mind.","zh":"一個計劃正在我的腦海中逐漸成形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/form","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b92231fc15698337333b","word":"formal","forms":["formal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0736d6a364a311d","term":"formal","forms":["formal","more formal","most formal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正式的；合乎規範的","explanation":"指語言、表達方式或行為符合公認的正式規範，不帶明顯的方言、口語或隨意色彩。它就像把說話放進一套規定好的形式裡，顯得莊重而有規矩。","examples":[{"en":"Please use formal language in your application.","zh":"請在申請中使用正式的語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report is written in a formal style.","zh":"這份報告採用正式的文體撰寫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd0efbf67b885b79","term":"formal","forms":["formal","more formal","most formal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"官方的；正式提出的","explanation":"指得到正式承認、按官方程式提出或辦理的事情，而不是私下說說或非正式安排。它把一個要求或行動放進了可以被記錄和處理的制度程式中。","examples":[{"en":"We filed a formal complaint about the delay.","zh":"我們就這次延誤提出了正式投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She submitted a formal request for access to the archived letters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de3a45b71a4f6bfe","term":"formal","forms":["formal","more formal","most formal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"拘謹的；不隨意的","explanation":"形容人的態度、舉止或交往方式嚴格遵守禮節，不像熟人之間那樣輕鬆隨意。核心畫面仍是把互動放進固定規矩裡，所以有時會讓人覺得拘謹。","examples":[{"en":"Our new manager is very formal with visitors.","zh":"我們的新經理接待訪客時非常拘謹正式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His formal manner relaxed after the introductions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e904c9ccfa425ff0b055","word":"format","forms":["format"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e269496211f6335f","term":"format","forms":["format","formats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"版式；開本","explanation":"指書籍、報刊或檔案的頁面外形和編排方式，例如頁面大小、文字安排和整體版式。它體現的是內容被“塑造”成什麼樣子。","examples":[{"en":"The report is available in both printed and digital formats.","zh":"這份報告有印刷版和數字版兩種形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The magazine changed to a smaller format last year.","zh":"這本雜誌去年改成了更小的開本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/format","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8138b78b5cf6f8af","term":"format","forms":["format","formats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"呈現形式","explanation":"指某種內容被組織和展示的方式，範圍比頁面版式更廣；節目、會議、課程或活動都可以有不同的 format。","examples":[{"en":"The conference will use a more informal format this year.","zh":"今年的會議將採用更輕鬆的形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workshop uses a question-and-answer format.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/format","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0aea32e3eb83bd3","term":"format","forms":["format","formats","formatting","formatted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排版；編排","explanation":"指安排或修改檔案、文件的版式，讓文字、圖片和頁面以指定的形式呈現。","examples":[{"en":"I formatted the document so that the headings were easier to read.","zh":"我給文件重新排了版，讓標題更容易閱讀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Format the headings consistently throughout the report.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/format","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3eb95cbef2662002788a","word":"formation","forms":["formation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c102b0bba5a50c4a","term":"formation","forms":["formation","formations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聚攏成形","explanation":"指把人、物或各個部分集合、組織起來，形成一個群體或結構，強調“組裝起來”的動作或過程。","examples":[{"en":"The formation of the committee took several weeks.","zh":"這個委員會的組建花了好幾個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The formation of clouds covered the mountain peaks.","zh":"雲層的形成遮住了山頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-899c9642c34ad770","term":"formation","forms":["formation","formations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"形成後的結構","explanation":"指某物已經呈現出的形狀、構造或有組織的樣子，是“聚成形”後的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The ice formation at the edge of the lake looked like a bridge.","zh":"湖邊的冰層結構看起來像一座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cave contains remarkable limestone formations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1cdf7af59bff046d","term":"formation","forms":["formation","formations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"形成過程","explanation":"指某事物逐漸產生並獲得自己的特徵的過程，例如湖泊、習慣、性格或社會組織慢慢形成。","examples":[{"en":"The formation of the lake took thousands of years.","zh":"這個湖泊的形成經歷了數千年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Early friendships play a role in the formation of character.","zh":"早期的友誼會影響性格的形成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a36430635e7505479f0","word":"former","forms":["former"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-177c31dc65ad0ef7","term":"former","forms":["former"],"pos":"adj","zh":"以前的","explanation":"指過去曾經是某種身份、擔任某個職務或處於某種狀態，但現在已經不是；核心畫面是“時間上排在現在前面”。","examples":[{"en":"A former president spoke at the ceremony.","zh":"一位前總統在典禮上發了言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She met her former classmates for dinner.","zh":"她和以前的同學見面吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/former","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14f303573fe5b01d","term":"former","forms":["former"],"pos":"adj","zh":"前者的；前者","explanation":"在前面剛提到的兩個物件中，former 指排在前面的那個，也就是“前者”；它把“在前面”的空間或順序概念延伸到了談話中的兩個選項。","examples":[{"en":"We can travel by train or bus; the former is faster.","zh":"我們可以坐火車或公共汽車去；前者更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Of the two plans, I prefer the former.","zh":"在這兩個計劃中，我更喜歡前一個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/former","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62bcdf5181440bb18c86","word":"formidable","forms":["formidable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-599c60907dc0ded6","term":"formidable","forms":["formidable","more formidable","most formidable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人敬畏的；氣勢強大的","explanation":"形容某人或某事物因為規模、力量、能力或氣勢突出而讓人感到敬畏、尊重，甚至驚歎；不一定只表示負面的害怕。","examples":[{"en":"The company has become a formidable force in the industry.","zh":"這家公司已經成為行業中一股令人敬畏的力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She built a formidable reputation as a scientist.","zh":"她作為科學家樹立了令人敬畏的聲譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formidable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44aa59f520345668","term":"formidable","forms":["formidable","more formidable","most formidable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難以戰勝的；難以克服的","explanation":"強調對手、任務或問題強大到不容易擊敗、處理或解決，就像面對一座難以翻越的高山。","examples":[{"en":"Our team will face a formidable opponent in the final.","zh":"我們隊將在決賽中面對一個難以戰勝的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The steep climb presented a formidable challenge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formidable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7374df08a7a6cf109af4","word":"formula","forms":["formula"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-227fb127147dca3b","term":"formula","forms":["formula","formulas","formulae","formulæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數學公式","explanation":"用符號寫出的固定數學規則，按照它代入或運算，就能得到某個結果，例如求方程的根。它體現了 formula“按模板計算”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"This formula calculates the area of a circle.","zh":"這個公式計算圓的面積。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students used a formula to solve the equation.","zh":"學生們用一個公式解這道方程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formula","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83380d5c7b0cba23","term":"formula","forms":["formula","formulas","formulae","formulæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化學式","explanation":"用元素符號表示一種物質由哪些元素組成，以及它們之間的固定比例；它像是物質的“成分模板”。","examples":[{"en":"H2O is the chemical formula for water.","zh":"H2O 是水的化學式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write a chemical formula beside each substance in the table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formula","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2111b9552696cd9","term":"formula","forms":["formula","formulas","formulae","formulæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成功方法","explanation":"處理問題或取得結果的一套可重複方法，好像一份不一定寫出具體材料的“成功配方”。","examples":[{"en":"There is no simple formula for success.","zh":"成功沒有簡單的固定方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They found a reliable formula for attracting customers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formula","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfdb264e14b3a34a95f7","word":"formulate","forms":["formulate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1d7c56bc90680f3","term":"formulate","forms":["formulate","formulates","formulating","formulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"明確表達；擬定","explanation":"指把原本零散、模糊的想法整理好，形成清楚而有條理的話、計劃或主張。重點不只是“說出來”，而是先把內容定下來、組織清楚。","examples":[{"en":"The team formulated a clear plan for the next stage.","zh":"團隊為下一階段擬定了一項清晰的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She struggled to formulate her ideas clearly.","zh":"她費了很大力氣才把自己的想法清楚地表達出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/formulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8864d7816bab46230668","word":"forsake","forms":["forsake"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9fb571a74366f65d","term":"forsake","forms":["forsake","forsakes","forsaking","forsook","forsaken","forsakest","forsookest","forsaketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拋棄；背棄；放棄","explanation":"指永久離開或不再支援某人、某物、某種責任或信念，常帶有背棄和決絕放手的意味。","examples":[{"en":"He forsook his comfortable life to care for his sick mother.","zh":"他放棄了舒適的生活，去照料生病的母親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She would never forsake her friends in a time of need.","zh":"她絕不會在朋友需要幫助時拋棄他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forsake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-150e9de319eb46ab4dbc","word":"fort","forms":["fort"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-553f15e5dc72cc5c","term":"fort","forms":["fort","forts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"防禦堡壘","explanation":"fort最核心的意思是為防守而建、通常有士兵駐守的堅固建築；它就是“把一個地方圍得很強”的實體形式。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers defended the fort all night.","zh":"士兵們守衛那座堡壘守了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruined fort once guarded the river crossing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-350a23b615e6df84","term":"fort","forms":["fort","forts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊戲堡壘","explanation":"孩子用椅子、毯子、枕頭等臨時搭出的藏身小空間也叫fort，因為它像一個供人躲進去的簡易堡壘；這是兒童語境中很常見的延伸義。","examples":[{"en":"The children built a fort under the dining table.","zh":"孩子們在餐桌下面搭了一個堡壘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children built a fort from sofa cushions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58190a849fa33f10a8d3","word":"forth","forms":["forth"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc98c1d5423ade86","term":"forth","forms":["forth"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從此以後；向前發展","explanation":"把時間想成不斷向前延伸：forth 可表示從某個時刻起繼續往後，最常見於“從今以後”這一類正式表達。","examples":[{"en":"From this day forth, we will work as one team.","zh":"從今天起，我們將作為一個團隊共同工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She promised to be more careful from then forth.","zh":"她答應從那以後會更加小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32ec07823e8949ba3309","word":"forthcoming","forms":["forthcoming"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82b3880c7c7aaa49","term":"forthcoming","forms":["forthcoming","more forthcoming","most forthcoming"],"pos":"adj","zh":"即將發生的","explanation":"指某件事已經臨近，很快就會發生，重點是它正從未來走到眼前。","examples":[{"en":"The forthcoming conference will focus on clean energy.","zh":"即將舉行的會議將重點討論清潔能源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Details of the forthcoming election will be announced tomorrow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forthcoming","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e2938ed5c049a8a","term":"forthcoming","forms":["forthcoming","more forthcoming","most forthcoming"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可得到的；會提供的","explanation":"指錢、幫助、資訊等在需要時會來到手邊，處於可以獲得或已經準備好的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The extra funding was not forthcoming, so the project was delayed.","zh":"額外資金沒有到位，因此專案被推遲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No explanation was forthcoming from the directors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forthcoming","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a58c6bdbbf52d5d3d7a","word":"fortify","forms":["fortify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4736a2e36f3f352d","term":"fortify","forms":["fortify","fortifies","fortifying","fortified","fortifiest","fortifiedst","fortifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"增強；使更有力量","explanation":"把人、身體、能力或事物變得更強、更有活力，就像給城牆加厚一樣。它既可以指實際增強，也可以指增強效果或抵抗力。","examples":[{"en":"A good breakfast fortified her for the long day ahead.","zh":"一頓豐盛的早餐讓她有力量應對接下來漫長的一天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He fortified himself with a cup of tea before the meeting.","zh":"開會前，他喝了一杯茶給自己提神打氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73d6de9a7e728b23","term":"fortify","forms":["fortify","fortifies","fortifying","fortified","fortifiest","fortifiedst","fortifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用證據支援；證實","explanation":"給一個觀點或說法“加上磚塊”，也就是提供證據，使它更牢靠、更可信。","examples":[{"en":"The report fortified her argument with data from three independent studies.","zh":"這份報告用三項獨立研究的資料進一步支援了她的論點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His conclusion was fortified by several eyewitness accounts.","zh":"幾名目擊者的敘述使他的結論更有說服力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05cecc98ad2e1e5b3266","word":"fortunate","forms":["fortunate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49043b2be74c06a1","term":"fortunate","forms":["fortunate","more fortunate","most fortunate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"因好運而發生的；碰巧有利的","explanation":"形容一件事或一個結果是在有利的偶然條件下發生的，帶有“運氣幫了忙”的意味。它通常說明結果不錯，但過程未必完全靠實力或計劃。","examples":[{"en":"The team secured a fortunate victory after the ball took a strange bounce.","zh":"球出現一次奇怪的彈跳後，這支球隊幸運地贏得了勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fortunate delay saved them from the storm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortunate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c73ee910a25521fe","term":"fortunate","forms":["fortunate","more fortunate","most fortunate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"幸運的；走運的","explanation":"形容某人受到好運眷顧，處在有利或令人慶幸的處境中。常常不是說這個人擁有特殊能力，而是說事情本來可能更糟，卻幸運地有了好的結果。","examples":[{"en":"We were fortunate to find a doctor so quickly.","zh":"我們很幸運，很快就找到了醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was fortunate that no one was injured in the accident.","zh":"她很幸運，事故中沒有人受傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortunate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27a0113e9ce8bfd5ba29","word":"fortune","forms":["fortune"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6969ed721731c261","term":"fortune","forms":["fortune","fortunes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"命運，尤其是好運","explanation":"fortune 可以指支配一個人未來遭遇的命運，尤其強調結果有利、走運的一面。這裡的重點是“未來會怎樣”，不單是當下的一次好運。","examples":[{"en":"She believed that fortune had finally turned in her favor.","zh":"她相信命運終於開始對她有利了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He never knows what fortune will bring next.","zh":"他永遠不知道命運接下來會帶來什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1445ef22e7d5fc2f","term":"fortune","forms":["fortune","fortunes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"好運","explanation":"這裡的 fortune 直接指有利的運氣或成功機會，是“命運對人有利”的簡潔說法。","examples":[{"en":"After years of hard work, fame and fortune finally came.","zh":"多年的努力之後，名望和財富終於到來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good fortune helped the small team win the final.","zh":"好運幫助這支小隊贏得了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-254eb088ac9808c8","term":"fortune","forms":["fortune","fortunes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財富，個人擁有的錢","explanation":"fortune 可以指一個人擁有的財富，尤其是數量很大、經過積累或足以改變生活的財產。","examples":[{"en":"She made a fortune by building affordable homes.","zh":"她靠建造價格實惠的住房積累了鉅額財富。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family lost most of its fortune during the war.","zh":"這個家族在戰爭期間失去了大部分財產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4eb41a2a9dfe70722ee4","word":"forum","forms":["forum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5de26145d124aad","term":"forum","forms":["forum","forums","fora"],"pos":"noun","zh":"討論場所","explanation":"forum 可以是人們公開交換意見、提出問題或討論某一主題的場所，不一定是實體房間，也可以是一個抽象的交流平臺。","examples":[{"en":"The website provides a forum for local residents to share their concerns.","zh":"這個網站為當地居民分享自己的關切提供了一個交流平臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library has become an important forum for debate about the new plan.","zh":"這座圖書館已經成為人們討論新計劃的重要場所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc44ba53f28af0b3","term":"forum","forms":["forum","forums","fora"],"pos":"noun","zh":"討論活動","explanation":"forum 也指為討論某個主題而組織的一次聚會或活動，參加者通常可以聽取意見並進行交流。","examples":[{"en":"The city held a public forum on the future of public transportation.","zh":"市政府舉行了一場討論公共交通未來發展的公開論壇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library hosted a forum on neighborhood development.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89271704f4bb9f6f","term":"forum","forms":["forum","forums","fora"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路論壇","explanation":"在網際網路語境中，forum 是使用者圍繞一個或多個主題釋出帖子、回覆他人並持續交流的網路空間。","examples":[{"en":"I found the answer in an online forum for amateur gardeners.","zh":"我在一個業餘園藝愛好者的網路論壇裡找到了答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She posted her question on a gardening forum.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9dc08e4033827c93f48c","word":"forward","forms":["forward"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cab9c249ec61a044","term":"forward","forms":["forward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"前面的；前部的","explanation":"表示某物位於另一個物體的前方或前部，就像朝前移動時最先到達的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Please sit in the forward section of the bus.","zh":"請坐在公共汽車的前部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The forward compartment contains the emergency equipment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04ad10798150d3c5","term":"forward","forms":["forward","forwards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"足球前鋒","explanation":"在足球中，forward 是靠近對方球門、主要負責創造和攻入進球的球員。","examples":[{"en":"The young forward scored twice in the final.","zh":"這名年輕前鋒在決賽中進了兩個球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The forward scored twice before halftime.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68c021e8dab8ce2f","term":"forward","forms":["forward","forwards","forwarding","forwarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉發；轉寄","explanation":"把收到的信件、電子郵件或其他資訊繼續送給另一個人，就像把資訊沿著路線向前傳給下一個人。","examples":[{"en":"Could you forward this email to the rest of the team?","zh":"你能把這封電子郵件轉發給團隊其他成員嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Forward the invoice to our finance department.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2c61b1ed28a64e864d0","word":"forward/forwards","forms":["forward","forwards"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ef2ab432bc0f137","term":"forward","forms":["forward"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向前；繼續推進","explanation":"表示實際向前移動，也表示計劃、工作或事情繼續取得進展。","examples":[{"en":"The project can move forward after we approve the budget.","zh":"預算獲批後，專案就可以繼續推進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are looking forward to meeting you.","zh":"我們期待與您見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e481a59744d01c3","term":"forwards","forms":["forwards","further forwards","farther forwards","furthest forwards","farthest forwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向前；朝前方","explanation":"表示人或事物朝前方移動，也可以引申為事情繼續向前發展；核心畫面就是從當前位置往前走。","examples":[{"en":"She took two steps forwards and opened the door.","zh":"她向前走了兩步，開啟了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project is finally moving forwards.","zh":"這個專案終於在向前推進了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d735fb5e9f2f61a33e8d","word":"fossil","forms":["fossil"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-87f2cafe2d832feb","term":"fossil","forms":["fossil","fossils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物遺骸化石","explanation":"指動物或植物死後，身體的一部分經過漫長時間被礦物替代或儲存下來的遺骸。它像是從地下挖出的遠古生命實體，讓人看到已經消失的生命曾經存在過。","examples":[{"en":"The children found a fossil of a small shell near the cliff.","zh":"孩子們在懸崖附近發現了一塊小貝殼化石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fossil preserved the outline of an ancient fish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fossil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c903c7f5eb6f4af","term":"fossil","forms":["fossil","fossils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遠古生命的儲存證據","explanation":"範圍比單純的遺骸更廣，凡是儲存下來的遠古生命證據都可以包括在內，例如貝殼印痕、足跡、洞穴痕跡，或生命活動留下的其他痕跡。重點不在於它是不是完整的身體，而在於它儲存了遠古生命存在或活動的線索。","examples":[{"en":"The fossil record shows that these animals lived in the region millions of years ago.","zh":"化石記錄顯示，這些動物數百萬年前生活在這個地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fossil preserves the delicate outline of a fern.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fossil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-17c3a324486be8f84436","word":"foster","forms":["foster"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97f5c6b90e430e0f","term":"foster","forms":["foster"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寄養的；提供寄養照護的","explanation":"指成年人或家庭照料並撫養與自己沒有親生關係的孩子，最常見於foster parent或foster parents。","examples":[{"en":"The foster parents welcomed the child into their home.","zh":"這對寄養父母把孩子接納到家中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Foster parents receive training before caring for children.","zh":"寄養父母在照顧孩子前會接受培訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-859b31941739d158","term":"foster","forms":["foster"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寄養的","explanation":"指正在接受非親生家庭照料的孩子，即寄養兒童。","examples":[{"en":"The foster child stayed with the same family for two years.","zh":"這個寄養兒童在同一個家庭住了兩年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a foster child after her parents could no longer care for her.","zh":"父母無法繼續照顧她後，她成了一名寄養兒童。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37b050567a857ded","term":"foster","forms":["foster","fosters","fostering","fostered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寄養；養育","explanation":"指照料、養育自己的孩子，或為非親生孩子提供類似父母的照護；核心畫面就是把孩子接過來並幫助他成長。","examples":[{"en":"The couple fostered three children over the course of a decade.","zh":"這對夫婦在十年間寄養過三個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They opened their home to foster a teenager.","zh":"他們敞開家門，寄養一名青少年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd64cca7c84242d9","term":"foster","forms":["foster","fosters","fostering","fostered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促進；培養","explanation":"把“養育孩子使其成長”的畫面擴充套件到抽象事物，表示創造條件、給予支援，使興趣、能力、關係或發展逐漸壯大。","examples":[{"en":"The program fosters creativity through hands-on projects.","zh":"這個專案透過實踐活動培養創造力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good communication fosters trust between team members.","zh":"良好的溝通能促進團隊成員之間的信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-772b56fcd499960d9709","word":"foul","forms":["foul"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39ef124de1b9b999","term":"foul","forms":["foul","fouler","foulest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"髒的；汙穢的","explanation":"表示表面沾有髒東西，或含有不潔物質，髒到不適合使用或接觸。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen towel was too foul to use.","zh":"這條廚房毛巾太髒了，沒法用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Foul water collected beneath the damaged sewer pipe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98d1489cfd5cee59","term":"foul","forms":["foul","fouls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"犯規","explanation":"指比賽中違反規則的動作，尤其是為了取得優勢而與對手發生不當身體接觸。這個名詞把“越過乾淨的規則界線”具體化了。","examples":[{"en":"The defender was given a foul for pushing the striker.","zh":"防守隊員因推搡前鋒而被判犯規。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The referee blew for a foul near the goal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c53d8dcf5cb43751","term":"foul","forms":["foul","fouls","fouling","fouled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄髒","explanation":"表示使某物沾上汙物，或變得不潔；這是“髒”這一核心概念的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The oil fouled the river near the factory.","zh":"油汙汙染了工廠附近的河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Oil fouled the birds' feathers after the spill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73efc43c2ef1c3b9","term":"foul","forms":["foul","fouls","fouling","fouled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堵塞；妨礙","explanation":"表示某物堵住、擋住或干擾另一物，使其不能正常透過、執行或發揮作用；這與“髒東西造成阻塞”的畫面相連。","examples":[{"en":"Leaves fouled the drain after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，樹葉堵住了下水道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Weeds fouled the boat's propeller.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bcc649cfdb8cc557053d","word":"found","forms":["found"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f04365b448747d87","term":"found","forms":["found","founds","founding","founded","foundest","foundedst","foundeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建立組織或機構","explanation":"found 表示從無到有地建立一個組織、機構或事業，好像先為它打下基礎。","examples":[{"en":"She founded a small charity after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，她創辦了一個小型慈善機構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sisters founded a charity supporting young musicians.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/found","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f72a13c265992fee","term":"found","forms":["found","founds","founding","founded","foundest","foundedst","foundeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"以……為依據","explanation":"表示把判斷、計劃或行動建立在某個事實、證據或原則之上，也就是以它為基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The report is founded on interviews with local residents.","zh":"這份報告以對當地居民的訪談為依據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her argument is founded on careful archival research.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/found","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bd8b7b0d83e0ec92abd","word":"foundation","forms":["foundation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-616803e07aac5eaf","term":"foundation","forms":["foundation","foundations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地基；支撐物","explanation":"指直接托住建築或其他結構的最底層部分；從“在下面支撐住東西”的畫面出發，它是foundation最具體、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The builders found a crack in the foundation of the house.","zh":"建築工人在房子的地基上發現了一條裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strong foundation keeps the building safe during storms.","zh":"堅固的地基能讓建築在暴風雨中保持安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f30adca2c2bfeaa6","term":"foundation","forms":["foundation","foundations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基礎；根基","explanation":"指使事業、計劃、制度或發展能夠穩定展開的準備、條件或成果；它把建築的“地基”引申成抽象事物賴以成立的根本。","examples":[{"en":"Good reading habits provide a strong foundation for learning.","zh":"良好的閱讀習慣為學習打下堅實基礎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement laid the foundation for closer cooperation.","zh":"這項協議為更密切的合作奠定了基礎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foundation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59458508a0827cff5f80","word":"founder","forms":["founder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1ca605493003855","term":"founder","forms":["founder","founders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創始人","explanation":"指創立並建立起公司、專案、組織、國家或其他事業的人，重點是“把某件事立起來的人”。","examples":[{"en":"She is the founder of a small technology company.","zh":"她是一家小型科技公司的創始人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The founder stepped down as CEO last year.","zh":"這位創始人去年辭去了執行長職務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/founder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0be1f30623191572183","word":"fountain","forms":["fountain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bb83a19f2066cd4","term":"fountain","forms":["fountain","fountains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噴泉","explanation":"指公園、庭院或公共場所中由裝置噴出水流的水景，通常具有裝飾作用。","examples":[{"en":"The children played beside the fountain.","zh":"孩子們在噴泉旁邊玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fountain lights up at night.","zh":"這座噴泉晚上會亮燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c3dc4989feb54d0","term":"fountain","forms":["fountain","fountains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"來源","explanation":"指某種事物不斷產生或流出的源頭，例如知識、幫助、恩惠或資訊的來源。","examples":[{"en":"Her grandmother was a fountain of practical wisdom.","zh":"她的祖母是實用智慧的源泉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library became a fountain of new ideas.","zh":"這座圖書館成了新思想的源泉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-406fd99bd8240af80ed2","word":"fowl","forms":["fowl"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-049787b4017fe64b","term":"fowl","forms":["fowl","fowls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"供捕獵或食用的鳥","explanation":"fowl把鳥看作人們捕獵、飼養或食用的物件，常包括雞鴨鵝等家禽，也包括某些獵鳥和水禽。它強調的是鳥與人的食物或狩獵關係，而不是單純說明“這是一隻鳥”。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer kept several fowl in a pen behind the house.","zh":"農夫在屋後的圈裡養了幾隻家禽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wild fowl gathered near the marsh at sunset.","zh":"日落時，野禽聚集在沼澤附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fowl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-776cb326ab0cd5f0a974","word":"fox","forms":["fox"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3ace84a72f72317","term":"fox","forms":["fox","foxes","foxen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狐狸","explanation":"一種體形較小到中等、長著尖嘴、三角形直耳和蓬鬆長尾的犬科動物。記住“靠機敏取勝的動物”，就能把這個具體義項和後面的比喻義聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"A fox crossed the road just before dawn.","zh":"一隻狐狸在黎明前穿過了馬路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw two foxes near the edge of the forest.","zh":"我們在森林邊緣附近看到了兩隻狐狸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-808af0447b665a0e","term":"fox","forms":["fox","foxes","foxen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狡猾的人","explanation":"借狐狸機敏、善於躲避和取勝的形象，指一個很會算計、機靈而可能不誠實的人。這個詞可以是讚賞其聰明，也可以是批評其狡猾，要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"That old fox found a way to win without breaking the rules.","zh":"那個老狐狸找到了一個不違反規則就能獲勝的辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a clever fox when it comes to negotiations.","zh":"談判時她可是個很精明的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c0f0f4581aa813bfe2e","word":"fraction","forms":["fraction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81275e43719851da","term":"fraction","forms":["fraction","fractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一部分","explanation":"它把整體想成一個完整的東西，fraction就是從中分出來的一塊，通常暗示這部分相對較小。","examples":[{"en":"Only a fraction of the students completed the survey.","zh":"只有一小部分學生完成了調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This information represents a fraction of the total cost.","zh":"這項資訊只代表總成本的一小部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d64432f545236532","term":"fraction","forms":["fraction","fractions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分數","explanation":"在數學裡，整體被分成若干等份，其中取了幾份，就可用fraction表示，通常寫成分子在上、分母在下的形式。","examples":[{"en":"Three quarters is a fraction equal to 0.75.","zh":"四分之三這個分數等於0.75。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write the answer as a fraction.","zh":"把答案寫成分數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fraction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7935748bd98de23e6ed","word":"fracture","forms":["fracture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e55ae6e8f199b533","term":"fracture","forms":["fracture","fractures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斷裂處；破裂","explanation":"指某物斷開的事實，或斷開的具體位置；重點是原本完整的結構被分開了。它可以用於材料、物體，也可以較抽象地指關係或結構出現裂痕。","examples":[{"en":"The impact left a fracture in the metal support.","zh":"撞擊使金屬支架出現了一處斷裂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fracture runs diagonally across the stone slab.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fracture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-789661f410f54864","term":"fracture","forms":["fracture","fractures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"骨折","explanation":"指骨頭或軟骨發生斷裂，是 fracture 最重要的醫學用法之一。它既可以指輕微裂紋，也可以指明顯的斷裂，不一定意味著骨頭完全斷成兩截。","examples":[{"en":"The X-ray showed a small fracture in her wrist.","zh":"X 光片顯示她的手腕有一處小骨折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was taken to the hospital after suffering a leg fracture.","zh":"他腿部骨折後被送往醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fracture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-184c6c36488dbd4c","term":"fracture","forms":["fracture","fractures","fracturing","fractured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"斷裂；使斷裂","explanation":"表示某物自己裂開或斷掉，也表示外力使某物裂開；核心仍是從完整狀態變成斷裂狀態。用於骨頭時，就是“使骨折”或“發生骨折”。","examples":[{"en":"The thin ice fractured under his weight.","zh":"薄冰在他的體重下裂開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fall fractured her ankle.","zh":"那次跌倒使她的腳踝骨折了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fracture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb8771659e9fb622424b","word":"fragile","forms":["fragile"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-155b76ef351d8642","term":"fragile","forms":["fragile","fragiler","more fragile","fragilest","most fragile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易碎的；不結實的","explanation":"指材料或物品經不起碰撞、壓力或摔落，很容易破碎。它把“經不起輕輕一碰”的玻璃杯形象直接用於具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"Please handle this box carefully—the contents are fragile.","zh":"請小心搬運這個箱子，裡面的東西很容易碎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fragile glass ornament fell off the shelf.","zh":"那個易碎的玻璃裝飾品從架子上掉了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ce43f915d820070","term":"fragile","forms":["fragile","fragiler","more fragile","fragilest","most fragile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"脆弱的；容易被破壞的","explanation":"指和平、協議、關係、經濟或局勢等雖然暫時存在，卻經不起一點衝擊，很容易被打亂或毀掉。這裡保留了玻璃杯“輕輕一碰就會碎”的核心畫面，只是被碰壞的是抽象狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The two sides are trying to protect the fragile peace.","zh":"雙方正努力維護來之不易而又脆弱的和平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fragile ceasefire lasted only three days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7587669ca42e19e8a9aa","word":"fragment","forms":["fragment"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65d11a550df58710","term":"fragment","forms":["fragment","fragments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碎片；片段","explanation":"指從較大或完整的東西上斷裂、脫離出來的一小部分，也可指不完整的文字、記憶或資訊片段。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a fragment of an ancient vase.","zh":"博物館展出了一塊古代花瓶的碎片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I only remember a fragment of the conversation.","zh":"我只記得那段談話的一小部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efcfcb5126e8dd92","term":"fragment","forms":["fragment","fragments","fragmenting","fragmented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"破碎；分裂","explanation":"指一個原本完整的東西自行分成彼此分離、不再統一的部分，也可用於組織或社會力量的分裂。","examples":[{"en":"The old alliance began to fragment after the election.","zh":"那個舊聯盟在選舉後開始分裂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ice fragmented under the pressure.","zh":"冰在壓力下碎裂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bcf9a9a604831d8ec020","word":"fragrance","forms":["fragrance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04e60be718ae6e2c","term":"fragrance","forms":["fragrance","fragrances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"怡人的氣味","explanation":"指聞起來令人愉快的氣味，可以來自花、食物、木材或其他物品。重點不只是“氣味”本身，還包含“香、宜人”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The fragrance of jasmine filled the evening air.","zh":"茉莉花的香氣充滿了夜晚的空氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I love the fresh fragrance of newly cut grass.","zh":"我喜歡新割青草散發出的清新香味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-617ba2c83313b210","term":"fragrance","forms":["fragrance","fragrances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香水；香氛產品","explanation":"指用來散發香味的香水或香氛產品，尤其常用於美容和個人護理語境。這裡關注的是裝在瓶子裡、可以購買和使用的產品，而不只是空氣中的香味。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a light floral fragrance for the summer.","zh":"她為夏天選了一款清淡的花香香水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store sells fragrances made from local flowers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e138157efe3a1a4cb30","word":"fragrant","forms":["fragrant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e65531c36e95d78d","term":"fragrant","forms":["fragrant","more fragrant","most fragrant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"芬芳的；芳香的","explanation":"指散發出令人愉悅的香味，常讓人聯想到花朵、香草或清新的植物氣息；帶有這種香味的東西也可以這樣形容。","examples":[{"en":"The garden was filled with fragrant flowers.","zh":"花園裡開滿了芬芳的花朵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fragrant herbs grew along the path.","zh":"小路旁長著散發香氣的香草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9dff50df08c635815f4b","word":"frame","forms":["frame"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed0abe60887201ef","term":"frame","forms":["frame","frames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結構框架","explanation":"frame可以指建築物或其他構造物中支撐整體的骨架；先搭好這個“框架”，再加上牆面或其他部分。","examples":[{"en":"The builders finished the frame of the house before winter.","zh":"建築工人在冬天前完成了房子的框架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The metal frame keeps the machine steady.","zh":"金屬框架使機器保持穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dfd5da4f3d528a3","term":"frame","forms":["frame","frames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"畫框","explanation":"frame可以指裝裱圖片、畫布或其他柔性材料的堅硬邊框，把內容固定幷包在裡面。","examples":[{"en":"She put the family photograph in a wooden frame.","zh":"她把全家福放進了木製相框。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This frame is too small for the painting.","zh":"這個畫框對這幅畫來說太小了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6789383d933f458","term":"frame","forms":["frame","frames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理解語境","explanation":"frame還可以指理解或解釋某件事時所採用的語境和角度；換一個“框架”，同一事實可能會顯得不同。","examples":[{"en":"In this frame, the decision looks much less surprising.","zh":"在這樣的語境下，這個決定看起來就不那麼令人意外了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article frames the debate as a choice between safety and freedom.","zh":"這篇文章把這場爭論呈現為安全與自由之間的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4da249129c4057b4","term":"frame","forms":["frame","frames","framing","framed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組合構建","explanation":"把不同部分按一定方式組合起來，形成一個完整的結構；記住“框架”就是把各部分支撐、連線在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The team framed the shelter from wood and canvas.","zh":"團隊用木材和帆布搭出了這個避難所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of training framed her into a disciplined performer.","zh":"多年的訓練塑造了她，使她成為一名自律的表演者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06a61df042ad775e8bdd","word":"framework","forms":["framework"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a7357f3d0132025","term":"framework","forms":["framework","frameworks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築骨架","explanation":"特指建築物中由梁、柱等組成的支撐骨架，它先確定建築的大致形狀和大小，牆面等部分隨後再加上去。","examples":[{"en":"The steel framework of the new stadium is nearly complete.","zh":"新體育場的鋼結構骨架快完工了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers put up the framework before installing the walls.","zh":"工人在安裝牆體前先搭起了骨架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/framework","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a16c781bf46e2327","term":"framework","forms":["framework","frameworks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基本概念結構","explanation":"指組織思想、觀點或論證的一套基本結構。它像建築骨架一樣把主要部分連線起來，但裡面填入的是概念和關係，而不是磚石。","examples":[{"en":"The course gives students a useful framework for understanding climate change.","zh":"這門課為學生理解氣候變化提供了有用的基本框架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a clear framework before we can compare the two proposals.","zh":"在比較這兩項提議之前，我們需要一個清晰的基本框架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/framework","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fe8ef24525db81848e6","word":"franchise","forms":["franchise"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0fac2a82aac5f2e","term":"franchise","forms":["franchise","franchises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業經營授權","explanation":"指公司允許另一方在特定地區銷售或分銷自己的商品或服務的授權；這就是現代商業中最重要的 franchise 義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a franchise to run a coffee shop near the station.","zh":"她買下了一項經營授權，在車站附近開了一家咖啡店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is looking for new franchise partners in Asia.","zh":"這家公司正在亞洲尋找新的加盟合作伙伴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22022ff667a0bfb8","term":"franchise","forms":["franchise","franchises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獲授權經營的店或企業","explanation":"指在公司授權下經營的具體企業或店鋪，也就是“拿到那張經營通行證後實際開起來的業務”。","examples":[{"en":"He runs three fast-food franchises in the suburbs.","zh":"他在郊區經營三家快餐加盟店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant franchise employs thirty local residents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77646f5a4f3166637627","word":"frank","forms":["frank"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a8efdbab9972333","term":"frank","forms":["frank","franker","frankest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"坦率的；直言不諱的","explanation":"指不拐彎、不隱藏真實想法，直接把事實或意見說出來；這種直接有時會讓人覺得略微生硬。","examples":[{"en":"May I be frank with you?","zh":"我可以跟你直說嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was frank about why she left the company.","zh":"她坦率地說明了自己離開公司的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad25f5a155010d50e5f3","word":"frantic","forms":["frantic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8eb9e23b614bf7b8","term":"frantic","forms":["frantic","more frantic","most frantic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慌亂焦急的","explanation":"形容一個人因為恐慌、擔憂或緊急情況而手忙腳亂、情緒失控，常讓人聯想到急著尋找、呼喊或採取行動的人。","examples":[{"en":"The frantic parents searched every street for their son.","zh":"焦急萬分的父母搜遍了每一條街，尋找他們的兒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a frantic call for help.","zh":"她慌慌張張地打電話求助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frantic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ce6a3f4fdc37348","term":"frantic","forms":["frantic","more frantic","most frantic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極度活躍的","explanation":"形容音樂、活動或動作充滿猛烈而快速的能量，彷彿節奏快到幾乎無法控制；重點不一定是害怕，而是強烈、急促和失控感。","examples":[{"en":"The band played at a frantic pace.","zh":"樂隊以極快而瘋狂的節奏演奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Frantic trading continued until the exchange closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frantic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f02b95ed0b00ce453359","word":"fraud","forms":["fraud"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d609c10d61394489","term":"fraud","forms":["fraud","frauds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"欺詐罪；騙錢","explanation":"指透過欺騙手段偷取或非法取得錢財的行為，通常涉及法律上的欺詐。重點不只是說謊，而是藉此獲得錢或其他財物。","examples":[{"en":"The company was accused of committing fraud against its customers.","zh":"這家公司被指控欺詐客戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Online payment fraud has become a serious problem.","zh":"網上支付欺詐已經成為一個嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fraud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00d86f6663804950","term":"fraud","forms":["fraud","frauds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"為不當獲利而欺騙","explanation":"泛指為了得到不應得或不合法的利益而採取的欺騙行為，不一定只涉及錢，也可以涉及地位、機會或其他好處。這是“用謊言織網來獲利”的最寬泛核心義。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation uncovered fraud in the hiring process.","zh":"調查發現招聘過程中存在欺詐行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The auditor uncovered fraud in the expense accounts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fraud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7653097b0a56851e687b","word":"freak","forms":["freak"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce8deddba70b8097","term":"freak","forms":["freak","freaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"古怪的人或異常事物","explanation":"指明顯不尋常、難以預測的人或事物；用於人時常帶“怪人”的意味。現代普通交流中，這個義項往往被更中性的詞替代。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a freak of nature with two heads.","zh":"博物館展出了一種長著兩個頭的異常生物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People treated him like a freak because he looked different.","zh":"因為外表不同，人們把他當成怪人一樣對待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1d7a756fae670c9","term":"freak","forms":["freak","freaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狂熱愛好者","explanation":"指對某件事極度著迷、投入很多時間，甚至擁有異常豐富知識的人。這裡的“異常”從負面偏離常態轉成了對興趣的強烈專注。","examples":[{"en":"My brother is a real history freak.","zh":"我哥哥是個十足的歷史迷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fitness freak, she exercises even on holiday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-094e877a512ddb8b","term":"freak","forms":["freak","freaks","freaking","freaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"情緒失控；反應過度","explanation":"指人在壓力、驚嚇或不安下突然反應得非常激烈，表現得不理智或失去鎮定。它正是“跳出正常軌道”這一核心概念在動詞上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"I freaked out when I realized I had lost my passport.","zh":"我發現護照丟了以後，整個人都慌了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't freak out; we still have plenty of time.","zh":"別慌，我們還有很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad95d5fa651ba86d8923","word":"free","forms":["free"],"officialPos":"adj./v./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb9d4aba00ac7e78","term":"free","forms":["free","freer","more free","freest","most free"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自由的；不受約束的","explanation":"指人或行動沒有受到控制、限制或強迫，可以按自己的意願行事。這是從“擺脫束縛、門被開啟”的核心畫面直接發展出來的意思。","examples":[{"en":"You are free to leave whenever you want.","zh":"你想什麼時候離開都可以。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were given free rein to choose the games.","zh":"孩子們可以完全自主地選擇遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/free","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9076bc825a9c2e38","term":"free","forms":["free","freer","more free","freest","most free"],"pos":"adj","zh":"免費的","explanation":"指獲得某物或使用某項服務不需要付款，好像它沒有被“付款條件”拴住。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is free on the first Sunday of every month.","zh":"這家博物館每月第一個星期日免費開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They gave me a free ticket with my purchase.","zh":"他們在我購買商品時送了我一張免費票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/free","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb9c644c3a0c5824","term":"free","forms":["free","freer","more free","freest","most free"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沒有；免於","explanation":"指某物不含有指定成分，或某人不受某種煩惱、責任和限制影響。門被開啟後，裡面沒有那種東西或負擔，就是 free of/from。","examples":[{"en":"This soap is free of artificial colors.","zh":"這種肥皂不含人工色素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wants a life free from unnecessary stress.","zh":"她想過一種沒有不必要壓力的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/free","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0023442e7acc9c9c","term":"free","forms":["free","frees","freeing","freed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"釋放；使自由","explanation":"指把人或動物從囚禁、控制或其他束縛中放出來，也就是替它開啟那扇門。","examples":[{"en":"The firefighters freed the child from the locked room.","zh":"消防員把孩子從鎖著的房間裡救了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new law freed thousands of workers from unfair restrictions.","zh":"新法律使數千名工人擺脫了不公平的限制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/free","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13b1f7ec5beaefc781e4","word":"freedom","forms":["freedom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-977ef0250791f58d","term":"freedom","forms":["freedom","freedoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自由狀態","explanation":"指一個人不再被關押、控制或強迫，能夠按照自己的意願生活和行動。這是 freedom 最基本、最廣泛的意思。","examples":[{"en":"After years of strict control, she finally felt a sense of freedom.","zh":"經過多年的嚴格控制，她終於感受到了一種自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoner was released and began to enjoy his freedom.","zh":"那名囚犯獲釋後開始享受自己的自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freedom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a123999bae86000c","term":"freedom","forms":["freedom","freedoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不受某項限制","explanation":"指沒有某種具體約束，或總體上不受限制的狀態。它強調的是“沒有攔住你的條件”，而不一定涉及法律或政治上的自由。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone should have the freedom to choose where to live.","zh":"每個人都應該有選擇居住地點的自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Residents demanded freedom from arbitrary searches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freedom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bac816c9cb0330a07e17","word":"freeway","forms":["freeway"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b1512c596efbd8b","term":"freeway","forms":["freeway","freeways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高速公路","explanation":"主要指一種為高速機動車設計的公路：往返方向各有獨立車道，並透過立交橋或其他方式避免與普通道路平面交叉。這個詞主要用於美國，在加拿大和澳大利亞的部分地區也使用。","examples":[{"en":"We took the freeway to get to the airport faster.","zh":"我們走高速公路，這樣能更快到機場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Traffic slowed where the freeway narrowed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freeway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca49679528521ca4","term":"freeway","forms":["freeway","freeways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不收費的公路","explanation":"這裡強調的是道路不收通行費，而不一定強調它是否符合嚴格的高速公路標準；因此它可以泛指一條免費的公路。","examples":[{"en":"The new freeway gives drivers a toll-free route between the two cities.","zh":"這條新公路為兩座城市之間的駕車者提供了一條不收費的路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Travelers chose the freeway to avoid the expensive toll road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freeway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12dd9774cc96e18b5b1b","word":"freeze","forms":["freeze"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01e750fc3cd92dd8","term":"freeze","forms":["freeze","freezes","freezing","froze","frore","frozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結冰","explanation":"指液體因溫度降低而變成固體，核心畫面就是水被凍成冰。","examples":[{"en":"The lake froze solid overnight.","zh":"湖水一夜之間結成了堅冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water expands when it freezes into ice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d76e135e3cc6c27c","term":"freeze","forms":["freeze","freezes","freezing","froze","frore","frozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"機器或程式卡住","explanation":"指機器、程式或系統突然停止工作並且不再響應輸入，就像被凍住一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The app freezes whenever I open a large file.","zh":"我每次開啟大檔案，這個應用就會卡死。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My laptop froze in the middle of an important video call.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e76fd4fea5384d0","term":"freeze","forms":["freeze","freezes","freezing","froze","frore","frozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"因害怕或驚訝而僵住","explanation":"指人或動物因恐懼、緊張、驚訝或高度注意而突然停止動作，身體像被凍住一樣。","examples":[{"en":"I froze when everyone turned to look at me.","zh":"所有人轉過來看我時，我一下子僵住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She froze when she heard footsteps behind her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de0660ea5a8bfb8ffc92","word":"freezer","forms":["freezer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f1fbe7b0d6525e8","term":"freezer","forms":["freezer","freezers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冷凍櫃；冰櫃","explanation":"指專門把食物或其他易腐物品保持在零攝氏度以下的裝置，通常比普通冰箱的冷凍格更像一個獨立的冷凍空間。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a small freezer for the garage.","zh":"我們給車庫買了一個小冷凍櫃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the extra meat in the freezer.","zh":"把多餘的肉放進冷凍櫃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freezer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-428b250d06e64395","term":"freezer","forms":["freezer","freezers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冷凍室；冷凍格","explanation":"指冰箱內部專門低溫冷凍食物的部分，不一定是一臺獨立裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","zh":"冰淇淋在冷凍室裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Defrost the freezer before ice blocks the upper compartment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freezer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58467d4070997eb48ecb","word":"freight","forms":["freight"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d255241b8eccb24","term":"freight","forms":["freight","freights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貨運；貨物運輸","explanation":"指把貨物從一個地方運到另一個地方的運輸活動，也可以指為這種運輸而租用車輛或船隻。核心畫面是“裝滿貨物並把它運走”。","examples":[{"en":"We sent the machinery by freight because it was too heavy for air travel.","zh":"我們用貨運把這臺機器送走，因為它太重，不能空運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company arranged freight for the entire shipment.","zh":"公司為整批貨物安排了運輸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e2239b9b5b2c493","term":"freight","forms":["freight","freights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貨物；運輸中的物品","explanation":"指正在運輸或準備運輸的貨物，重點是“車、船或拖車裡裝著的東西”，而不是運輸這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"The truck carried freight from the port to the warehouse.","zh":"卡車把貨物從港口運到倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The driver checked that the freight was secured before leaving.","zh":"司機出發前檢查了貨物是否固定牢靠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15a5cd7f058d333e","term":"freight","forms":["freight","freights","freighting","freighted","freightest","freightedst","freighteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給運輸工具裝貨；租用其運貨","explanation":"指把貨物裝進船、車等運輸工具，或租用運輸工具來裝運貨物。核心畫面就是“把貨裝上去並讓它承擔運輸任務”。","examples":[{"en":"The company freighted three trucks with construction materials.","zh":"公司給三輛卡車裝上了建築材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They freighted a vessel to carry the equipment overseas.","zh":"他們租了一艘船把裝置運到海外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e9089fefc7aaa5c45a2","word":"frequency","forms":["frequency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b69f03668388fce6","term":"frequency","forms":["frequency","frequencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發生率；發生頻率","explanation":"指某件事在特定時間段內出現或發生的次數與快慢。時間段相同，出現次數越多，frequency 就越高；時間段不同，比較時要注意不能只看總次數。","examples":[{"en":"The frequency of power cuts has increased this winter.","zh":"今年冬天停電發生得更頻繁了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We recorded the frequency of visitors during each hour.","zh":"我們記錄了每個小時訪客出現的次數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frequency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f973cd98ee6333d","term":"frequency","forms":["frequency","frequencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頻率（每秒振動次數）","explanation":"在物理學中，frequency 是週期性振動在單位時間內重複的次數。聲音或無線電波每秒振動得越多，數值越高，通常用赫茲表示。","examples":[{"en":"The radio is tuned to a frequency of 100 megahertz.","zh":"這臺收音機調到了 100 兆赫的頻率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tuning fork vibrates at a fixed frequency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frequency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-403b8dc9df0dc3ced2f5","word":"frequent","forms":["frequent"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a387f16232513a8b","term":"frequent","forms":["frequent","more frequent","frequenter","most frequent","frequentest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"經常的；頻繁的","explanation":"指某件事反覆發生，次數很多，因此給人“總是遇到”的感覺。它可以修飾事件、行為、問題或短暫的停頓等。","examples":[{"en":"I take frequent breaks so I don't get too tired.","zh":"我經常休息一下，這樣就不會太累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Frequent mistakes made the report difficult to trust.","zh":"反覆出現的錯誤讓這份報告很難令人信服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frequent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ad39c68cca8a82b","term":"frequent","forms":["frequent","frequents","frequenting","frequented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"常去；常光顧","explanation":"指反覆去某個地方，尤其是餐館、商店、酒吧等，也可以指經常拜訪某人；它把“頻繁出現”變成了“自己頻繁出現在某處”。","examples":[{"en":"She frequents a small café near her office.","zh":"她經常光顧辦公室附近的一家小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tourists frequently visit the market, but local artists also frequent it.","zh":"遊客經常參觀這個市場，但當地藝術家也常來這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frequent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d098ab5e44b9aabb755f","word":"fresh","forms":["fresh"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32d5c01cf10737ca","term":"fresh","forms":["fresh","fresher","freshest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"剛有的；最近的","explanation":"指剛剛產生、製作、獲得或發生的，還沒有經過很長時間的事物。重點是“時間很近”，不一定只用於食物。","examples":[{"en":"The police found fresh tracks in the snow.","zh":"警方在雪地裡發現了剛留下的足跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a fresh plan after the first one failed.","zh":"第一個計劃失敗後，我們需要一個新方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e969e142fefc6d36","term":"fresh","forms":["fresh","fresher","freshest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"新鮮的；未變質的","explanation":"指沒有曬乾、冷凍或腐壞，仍保持原本狀態的食物或材料；這裡的核心仍是“沒有被時間破壞”。","examples":[{"en":"I bought fresh vegetables for dinner.","zh":"我買了新鮮蔬菜做晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This bread is fresh from the oven.","zh":"這麵包剛從烤箱裡出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc66f365af2dbfbf","term":"fresh","forms":["fresh","fresher","freshest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清爽的；涼爽宜人的","explanation":"指空氣、風或感覺帶來涼意和活力，讓人覺得舒服、清新。","examples":[{"en":"A fresh breeze came through the open window.","zh":"一陣清爽的微風從開著的窗戶吹了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the stuffy carriage, the fresh mountain air felt wonderful.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10ffb1a844318e53985e","word":"freshman","forms":["freshman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7fa11ac87b46003b","term":"freshman","forms":["freshman","freshmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大一新生；第一年成員","explanation":"指剛進入高中、大學或某個機構、處於第一年的人。在美國英語中尤其常指高中或大學一年級學生，也可指剛當選進入立法機構的第一年成員。","examples":[{"en":"She moved into the dorm as a freshman.","zh":"她作為大一新生搬進了宿舍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The freshman class elected two representatives.","zh":"新生班選出了兩名代表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freshman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0de598f2e8e4753650e","word":"friction","forms":["friction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5837e487543eb2c","term":"friction","forms":["friction","frictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表面相互摩擦","explanation":"指兩個物體或表面相互接觸並來回蹭動的過程；這是“摩擦”這個詞最基本的畫面，也為其他義項提供了核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Rubbing two dry sticks together can create enough friction to start a fire.","zh":"把兩根幹木棍相互摩擦，可能產生足夠的熱量來生火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine makes a strange noise because of friction between the moving parts.","zh":"這臺機器發出奇怪的聲音，是因為運動部件之間有摩擦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f5d956d4f7c093d","term":"friction","forms":["friction","frictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"阻礙運動的摩擦力","explanation":"指接觸中的物體相對運動時，阻礙它們繼續運動的力。它是從“表面相互蹭動”發展出的物理概念，常解釋為什麼物體會逐漸減速或停下。","examples":[{"en":"Friction between the tires and the road helps the car stop safely.","zh":"輪胎和路面之間的摩擦力有助於汽車安全停下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Oil is used to reduce friction between the metal parts.","zh":"人們用油來減少金屬部件之間的摩擦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69a0a6d422e4bb9e","term":"friction","forms":["friction","frictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意見或利益衝突","explanation":"比喻不同的人、團體或機構彼此“蹭撞”，表示因想法、利益或權力不一致而產生的緊張和不和。它通常不一定是公開爭吵，而是關係中持續存在的阻力。","examples":[{"en":"There has been growing friction between the two departments over the new policy.","zh":"兩個部門因這項新政策產生的摩擦越來越多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small disagreements can create friction in a close friendship.","zh":"小小的分歧也可能在親密友誼中造成摩擦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cde48537ca2c28084ff5","word":"friend","forms":["friend"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2bd05be910a7702","term":"friend","forms":["friend","friends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"朋友","explanation":"指通常不是家人、配偶或戀人，但彼此喜歡相處、關係親近的人。這是friend最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She is a close friend of mine.","zh":"她是我的一位親密朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I met some old friends for dinner.","zh":"我和幾位老朋友見面吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-404db65abf92f900","term":"friend","forms":["friend","friends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫助者；支持者","explanation":"這裡的friend不一定是私人朋友，而是願意幫助、保護或支援某個人的人，也可以指贊助者或導師。","examples":[{"en":"The local charity has been a good friend to many families.","zh":"當地慈善機構一直幫助著許多家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been a faithful friend to the museum.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c448a406dcdf064f726","word":"friendly","forms":["friendly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9159438f39a9888","term":"friendly","forms":["friendly","friendlier","more friendly","friendliest","most friendly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親切友好","explanation":"形容一個人或動物容易接近、態度親切，讓別人感到相處輕鬆。","examples":[{"en":"The new neighbor is very friendly.","zh":"新鄰居非常友好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our dog is friendly to children.","zh":"我們的狗對孩子很友好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friendly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f1c72724aabbd9b","term":"friendly","forms":["friendly","friendlier","more friendly","friendliest","most friendly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"友好的、親切的","explanation":"形容笑容、語氣、問候等帶有朋友般的親切感，而不一定說明這個人已經是朋友。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a friendly smile.","zh":"她朝我友好地笑了笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His friendly tone made the conversation easier.","zh":"他親切的語氣讓談話變得更輕鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friendly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b529ac375b4217be17f","word":"friendship","forms":["friendship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3b8c2269d50d24e","term":"friendship","forms":["friendship","friendships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"友誼；友情","explanation":"friendship 是朋友之間建立並維持的友好聯絡，強調這種關係或狀態本身，而不是某一個朋友。","examples":[{"en":"Their friendship grew stronger after they worked together.","zh":"他們一起工作後，友誼更加深厚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"True friendship takes time and trust.","zh":"真正的友誼需要時間和信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friendship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c88dbb41b8bfed3","term":"friendship","forms":["friendship","friendships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段朋友關係","explanation":"friendship 也可以指人與人之間的一段具體友情，也就是“他們之間的朋友關係”。這種用法把抽象的友誼看成一條具體的關係紐帶。","examples":[{"en":"She has formed several lasting friendships at university.","zh":"她在大學裡建立了幾段持久的友誼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their friendship survived years of living apart.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friendship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1fce31d9b8cd02f4fa1","word":"fries","forms":["fries"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20c1277f773b3639","term":"fries","forms":["fries","fry"],"pos":"noun","zh":"炸薯條","explanation":"fries 指切成條後炸熟的土豆，通常就是餐館裡作為配菜或小吃的炸薯條。這裡的複數形式是固定常用說法，不必按一根一根的數量去理解。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a burger and fries for lunch.","zh":"我午餐點了漢堡和炸薯條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These fries are crispy and hot.","zh":"這些炸薯條又脆又熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fries","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c3cc494be55f4863031","word":"fright","forms":["fright"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e03ea25143b0222","term":"fright","forms":["fright","frights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚嚇；恐懼","explanation":"指危險或可怕的事情突然出現時產生的一陣強烈害怕，通常來得突然、持續時間不長。重點是“心裡猛地一震”這一感覺，而不只是長時間的擔憂。","examples":[{"en":"The loud bang gave me a fright.","zh":"那聲巨響把我嚇了一跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ran out of the room in fright.","zh":"她嚇得跑出了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04794b1d687f6aee","term":"fright","forms":["fright","frights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚇人的醜東西；嚇人相貌的人","explanation":"指外表、打扮或狀態難看得讓人吃驚甚至害怕的人或物；這裡的 fright 不是“感到害怕”，而是“本身讓別人害怕或反感”。這種說法通常很不客氣。","examples":[{"en":"After the storm, the old house was a fright.","zh":"暴風雨過後，那座老房子難看得嚇人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I look a fright after sleeping on the train.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52d8a8577f39e45e78fc","word":"frighten","forms":["frighten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28dd073d86b98cb6","term":"frighten","forms":["frighten","frightens","frightening","frightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……害怕；嚇到","explanation":"指某人、某物或某個動作讓另一個人或動物產生恐懼，重點是“把恐懼帶給別人”。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden crash frightened everyone in the room.","zh":"突然的一聲巨響把房間裡的所有人都嚇了一跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't frighten the cat with that loud noise.","zh":"別用那麼大的聲音嚇貓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-605e595d277ca44e","term":"frighten","forms":["frighten","frightens","frightening","frightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"受驚；變得害怕","explanation":"指人或動物自己受到驚嚇、變得害怕，是前一個意義的另一面：恐懼落到了主語身上。","examples":[{"en":"The horse frightens easily in crowded places.","zh":"這匹馬在人多的地方很容易受驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pony frightens easily around unfamiliar dogs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74fa5327cc0f4e947789","word":"frog","forms":["frog"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5234817254d1057","term":"frog","forms":["frog","frogs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"青蛙","explanation":"一種沒有尾巴、通常會跳躍的小型兩棲動物；這是 frog 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A frog jumped out of the pond.","zh":"一隻青蛙從池塘裡跳了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard frogs singing after the rain.","zh":"雨後我們聽見青蛙在叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a961101c68c843b2","term":"frog","forms":["frog","frogs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"弓根","explanation":"小提琴、中提琴、大提琴等弓上供演奏者握住的一端，弓毛連線在那裡。","examples":[{"en":"Keep your thumb near the frog of the bow.","zh":"把拇指放在弓根附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adjust the screw at the frog to tighten the bow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75857a45899985be4c4d","word":"from","forms":["from"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e7fae61a80285dc","term":"from","forms":["from"],"pos":"prep","zh":"來自；源於","explanation":"表示人、物或資訊的來源，也就是“從哪裡來”或“出自哪裡”。","examples":[{"en":"My new colleague is from Brazil.","zh":"我的新同事來自巴西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This message is from my manager.","zh":"這條訊息來自我的經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/from","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-321d45f1ea80b891","term":"from","forms":["from"],"pos":"prep","zh":"從……移開；從……取下","explanation":"表示某人或某物離開、被拿走的地點或物件，突出“從起點向外分離”。","examples":[{"en":"Please take the plates from the table.","zh":"請把盤子從桌子上拿走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She removed the jacket from the chair.","zh":"她把夾克從椅子上拿了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/from","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d256c89ec88beb9b","term":"from","forms":["from"],"pos":"prep","zh":"使免於；排除在外","explanation":"表示某人被阻止參與某事，或某物被排除在某個行動之外；可以看作把物件擋在某個範圍外面。","examples":[{"en":"The injury kept him from playing in the final.","zh":"這次受傷使他無法參加決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing can prevent her from trying again.","zh":"沒有什麼能阻止她再次嘗試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/from","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d8d693177ac44895fc0","word":"front","forms":["front"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-514542c41a92cab5","term":"front","forms":["front","further front","farther front","furthest front","farthest front"],"pos":"adj","zh":"前面的；最前方的","explanation":"指位於一組事物最前面或靠近最前面的，就像站在隊伍最前面的那張臉。","examples":[{"en":"We found two empty seats in the front row.","zh":"我們在前排找到了兩個空座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The front runner crossed the finish line first.","zh":"領先者第一個衝過了終點線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/front","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9e72f308ed9a4b3","term":"front","forms":["front","fronts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前面；前端","explanation":"指物體最前面的那一面，或物體正常移動方向的前端，就是站在最前面的那張臉。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small scratch on the front of the car.","zh":"汽車前面有一道小劃痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please sit at the front of the bus.","zh":"請坐在公共汽車前部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/front","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb8b12495fa1a533","term":"front","forms":["front","fronts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門面人物；掩護組織","explanation":"指替另一個隱秘團體或活動出面的人或機構，站在最前面充當公眾看得見的那張臉。","examples":[{"en":"The small shop was reportedly a front for an illegal operation.","zh":"據報道，那家小店是某項非法活動的掩護門面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She acted as the public front for the group.","zh":"她充當了這個團體對外的門面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/front","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7575274a20d035b5a72","word":"frontier","forms":["frontier"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-656fa5a2ba40ecc0","term":"frontier","forms":["frontier","frontiers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊疆；邊界地帶","explanation":"指一個國家面對另一個國家、荒野或尚未開發地區的邊疆地帶。它像地圖上通向未知的最外緣，常帶有開拓和開發中的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Many families moved to the frontier in search of land.","zh":"許多家庭為了尋找土地搬到了邊疆地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The frontier of civilization shifted westward.","zh":"文明的邊疆向西推進了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frontier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f377ce240beefd24","term":"frontier","forms":["frontier","frontiers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前沿；尖端領域","explanation":"從地理上的最外緣引申而來，指某個知識、技術或事業目前推進到的最前沿，也就是最先進、最接近未知的部分。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are working at the frontier of artificial intelligence.","zh":"科學家們正在人工智慧的前沿開展研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers are exploring new frontiers in brain imaging.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frontier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7bf0c9ea6ea590ff1a4","word":"frost","forms":["frost"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-351436d037fa5284","term":"frost","forms":["frost","frosts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"霜；霜層","explanation":"指空氣中的水汽在低於冰點的物體表面形成的細小冰晶，常見於草地、窗戶和汽車上。它就是“清晨物體上薄薄的一層冰”。","examples":[{"en":"There was a thin layer of frost on the car windshield.","zh":"汽車擋風玻璃上有一層薄薄的霜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The morning frost made the grass sparkle.","zh":"清晨的霜讓草地閃閃發光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-236a2ac1de367774","term":"frost","forms":["frost","frosts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"霜凍天氣；嚴寒","explanation":"指使物體結霜的寒冷天氣，尤其是夜間或清晨的低溫。這裡關注的不是霜層本身，而是造成霜的那段寒冷天氣。","examples":[{"en":"The gardeners covered the plants because a frost was expected overnight.","zh":"園丁們把植物蓋了起來，因為預計夜間會有霜凍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The late frost damaged many young tomatoes.","zh":"晚來的霜凍毀壞了許多幼小的番茄植株。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a4a2f4d0085abe6","term":"frost","forms":["frost","frosts","frosting","frosted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……覆霜","explanation":"指使某個表面形成霜狀覆蓋層，是“霜附著到物體上”這一畫面的主動形式。","examples":[{"en":"The cold air frosted the windows overnight.","zh":"冷空氣使窗戶在夜間結了一層霜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glass was frosted with a delicate white pattern.","zh":"玻璃上覆著精緻的白色霜狀圖案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8025f1ac36394530","term":"frost","forms":["frost","frosts","frosting","frosted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結霜","explanation":"指物體自身因為寒冷而覆上一層霜，是 frost 作不及物動詞時的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The fields frosted before sunrise.","zh":"太陽昇起前，田野結了霜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It frosted lightly during the night.","zh":"夜裡下了輕霜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-426d6ea425e6c2c940db","word":"frown","forms":["frown"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c955dcd399c414b","term":"frown","forms":["frown","frowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皺眉；蹙眉的表情","explanation":"眉頭皺起、眉毛靠攏形成的表情，常讓人看起來嚴肅、專注或不高興。這是名詞 frown 最核心、最值得先掌握的意義。","examples":[{"en":"A deep frown appeared on her forehead.","zh":"她的額頭上出現了深深的皺紋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He listened with a frown.","zh":"他皺著眉聽著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb4e5332cd1ef1af","term":"frown","forms":["frown","frowns","frowning","frowned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"皺眉；蹙眉","explanation":"指人把眉頭皺起來，通常因為不高興、驚訝、擔心或正在認真思考。這是動詞 frown 最基本的意義，核心畫面就是“臉上的門關緊了”。","examples":[{"en":"She frowned when I told her the news.","zh":"我告訴她這個訊息時，她皺了皺眉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He frowned at the confusing question.","zh":"面對這個令人困惑的問題，他皺起了眉頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d0fe7f8abc270e9","term":"frown","forms":["frown","frowns","frowning","frowned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對……不贊成；不以為然","explanation":"由“皺眉表示不悅”引申而來，表示某種行為或做法不被認可、不受歡迎。這裡不一定真的有人皺眉，而是說這種做法在態度上被否定。","examples":[{"en":"Loud conversations are frowned upon in the reading room.","zh":"閱覽室裡不贊成大聲交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Skipping the safety check is frowned upon at work.","zh":"在工作中，跳過安全檢查是不被認可的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9209526aaa61b0709dbb","word":"fruit","forms":["fruit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-934741e583af02ba","term":"fruit","forms":["fruit","fruits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可食的水果或類似部分","explanation":"日常生活中指植物上甜或酸、可以食用、外形像有種子的果實的部分；這裡的範圍比嚴格植物學定義更寬。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh fruit is a healthy snack.","zh":"新鮮水果是健康的零食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought some fruit for the picnic.","zh":"我們為野餐買了一些水果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fruit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29bd26c826597ddd","term":"fruit","forms":["fruit","fruits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成果；結果","explanation":"把植物結出果實的畫面引申到人的行動：長期努力最終“結出”的東西，就是成果或結果，可能是好的，也可能是壞的。","examples":[{"en":"Years of careful work finally bore fruit.","zh":"多年的認真工作終於結出了成果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their patience bore fruit when the project succeeded.","zh":"他們的耐心在專案成功時終於取得了成果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fruit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b59cbd080973d9eb039","word":"frustrate","forms":["frustrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2179536b07f42f86","term":"frustrate","forms":["frustrate","frustrates","frustrating","frustrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使未能如願","explanation":"指某人原本期待得到某物或實現某事，卻被結果打敗、失望，目標因此落空。重點是“期待的結果沒有實現”。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden cancellation frustrated our plans for the weekend.","zh":"突然取消的安排使我們的週末計劃落了空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repeated injuries frustrated her ambition to become a dancer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frustrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4ed4e4a1bf258de","term":"frustrate","forms":["frustrate","frustrates","frustrating","frustrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"阻礙，妨礙","explanation":"指某種困難擋住行動或進展，使人難以完成原本想做的事；這裡突出“路被堵住”這一過程，不一定已經徹底失敗。","examples":[{"en":"A poor internet connection frustrated my attempt to submit the form.","zh":"網路連線很差，妨礙了我提交表格的嘗試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A locked gate frustrated our attempt to reach the beach.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frustrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1748ba31e26277da728a","word":"frustration","forms":["frustration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37f3a3d06e7d70fa","term":"frustration","forms":["frustration","frustrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"挫敗感；懊惱","explanation":"事情不斷受阻、自己又無法實現目標時產生的惱怒和挫敗感，就是 frustration。它既可以來自一次失敗，也可以來自長期無法推進的處境。","examples":[{"en":"After three failed attempts, I felt a lot of frustration.","zh":"連續嘗試三次都失敗後，我感到非常挫敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her frustration with the slow internet was obvious.","zh":"她對網速太慢的惱火顯而易見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frustration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-104c30b4d03b939a","term":"frustration","forms":["frustration","frustrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使受挫的行為或受挫狀態","explanation":"這個意思把注意力放在“受阻這件事本身”上：可以指某人阻止計劃、願望實現的行為，也可以指目標處於無法實現的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The frustration of his efforts left him discouraged.","zh":"他的努力受到阻撓，這讓他很灰心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injunction ensured the frustration of their original plan.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frustration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f23c707b474c45bdcbd","word":"fry","forms":["fry"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-67736489b43a0f49","term":"fry","forms":["fry","fries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"炸薯條","explanation":"在加拿大和美國，fry 通常指一根炸好的土豆條，但實際使用中幾乎總用複數 fries 指一份薯條。","examples":[{"en":"Could we get two orders of fries with the burgers?","zh":"我們可以要兩份漢堡配薯條嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fries are crispy and lightly salted.","zh":"這些薯條很酥脆，鹽放得不多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57abf1781cd4bf7a","term":"fry","forms":["fry","fries","frying","fried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"煎、炸食物","explanation":"fry 表示把食物放在熱油或高溫表面上煮熟，使表面變脆或變色；它比“油炸”更寬，也可以指煎。","examples":[{"en":"Fry the onions until they turn golden brown.","zh":"把洋蔥煎到金黃色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fried the fish in a little oil.","zh":"她用少量油煎了魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acbe4bfc77e55c071db3","word":"fuel","forms":["fuel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b59143219500cdbe","term":"fuel","forms":["fuel","fuels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燃料；能量來源","explanation":"指被消耗來產生能量的物質，最典型的是煤、木材、汽油和天然氣；在更寬的科學語境中，也可以指透過化學或核反應提供能量的物質。","examples":[{"en":"Wood is still used as fuel in some rural homes.","zh":"一些農村家庭仍然把木材當作燃料使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The aircraft carried enough fuel for the long flight.","zh":"這架飛機攜帶了足夠完成長途飛行的燃料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2386c2387e60cd9a","term":"fuel","forms":["fuel","fuels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"助長因素；推動力","explanation":"把憤怒、謠言、新聞或某種想法想成添進火裡的東西：它們不一定直接造成事件，卻會使行動、爭論或情緒持續並增強。","examples":[{"en":"The rumor provided fuel for public anger.","zh":"這則謠言助長了公眾的憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her comments became fuel for the online debate.","zh":"她的評論成了網上爭論進一步升級的材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-574309ca14afb809","term":"fuel","forms":["fuel","fuels","fueling","fuelling","fueled","fuelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"助長；加劇","explanation":"指給某種情緒、衝突、擔憂或行動添火，使它變得更嚴重、更強烈或持續更久；它強調推動和放大，不一定表示說話者有意為之。","examples":[{"en":"The misleading report fueled fears about the new policy.","zh":"這篇誤導性的報道加劇了人們對新政策的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Personal attacks only fueled the conflict.","zh":"人身攻擊只會進一步加劇衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12f9706499405c5c12fd","word":"fulfill(ment)","forms":["fulfill","fulfillment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19792b7ceefbb599","term":"fulfill","forms":["fulfill","fulfills","fulfilling","fulfilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"履行；完成","explanation":"把自己答應的事、承擔的責任或必須完成的任務真正做到，使這項義務不再有空缺。它常帶有“圓滿兌現”的意味，而不只是做過某個動作。","examples":[{"en":"She worked hard to fulfill her promise to the community.","zh":"她努力工作，以兌現自己對社群的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company fulfilled its obligation to repair the damaged equipment.","zh":"公司履行了修理受損裝置的義務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fulfill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9ef2a60e14e68a2","term":"fulfill","forms":["fulfill","fulfills","fulfilling","fulfilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使滿足；實現自我","explanation":"把內心的願望、才能或人生潛能充分發揮出來，因此感到滿足和充實；也可以說某項經歷或工作給人這種滿足感。","examples":[{"en":"Teaching allows him to fulfill his potential and help others.","zh":"教書讓他能夠發揮自己的潛能，同時幫助別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Teaching fulfills her more than any previous job.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fulfill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-febf40663696d3a0","term":"fulfillment","forms":["fulfillment","fulfillments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完成；履行；滿足","explanation":"指某件事終於落實：承諾被履行、任務被完成，或願望得到滿足。在商業語境中，它尤其常指訂單從下單到處理、發貨並完成交付的過程；這裡的美式拼寫是 fulfillment，英式英語常寫 fulfilment。","examples":[{"en":"The company handles order fulfillment from its warehouse in Texas.","zh":"這家公司在得克薩斯州的倉庫處理訂單履約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found a deep sense of fulfillment in helping her community.","zh":"她在幫助社群的過程中獲得了深深的滿足感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fulfillment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a18b869b2e81c0c52955","word":"full","forms":["full"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e8f45d7e3514dfe","term":"full","forms":["full","fuller","more full","fullest","most full"],"pos":"adj","zh":"裝滿的","explanation":"表示空間中的東西已經達到所能容納的最大量，幾乎沒有空餘；這是“填到邊緣”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The glass is full of ice.","zh":"這個杯子裡裝滿了冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train was full, so we had to wait for the next one.","zh":"這趟火車滿員了，所以我們只好等下一趟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/full","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92087ca437a5c230","term":"full","forms":["full","fuller","more full","fullest","most full"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完整的；詳盡的","explanation":"表示內容沒有重要遺漏，像一個容器被完整填充，因而可譯為“完整的、詳盡的”。","examples":[{"en":"The report gives a full account of what happened.","zh":"這份報告完整地說明了事情的經過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please give me your full name.","zh":"請告訴我你的全名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/full","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f50f8b1b1b8a206","term":"full","forms":["full","fuller","more full","fullest","most full"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全部的；整個的","explanation":"表示範圍達到整體，沒有省略或缺少部分；它是“裝滿”從空間延伸到範圍的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The trip took a full three hours.","zh":"這次行程整整花了三個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You must pay the full price before delivery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/full","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab9eb089b7bb0bb2e40f","word":"fume","forms":["fume"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"fume","forms":["fume","fumes"],"pos":"n.","zh":"煙氣；有害氣體","examples":[{"en":"Toxic fumes escaped from the damaged pipe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The worker stepped back when strong fumes rose from the mixture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"fume","forms":["fume","fumes"],"pos":"v.","zh":"發怒；生悶氣","examples":[{"en":"He would fume whenever someone parked in front of his gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Do not sit and fume about the mistake; ask how to correct it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-00c4285274fcc5d6fba2","word":"fun","forms":["fun"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dbbb394488ed6a0","term":"fun","forms":["fun"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂趣；開心","explanation":"指參加活動或做某事時獲得的快樂和享受，也就是“好玩”所帶來的那種感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The children had a lot of fun at the beach.","zh":"孩子們在海灘上玩得很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I joined the class just for fun.","zh":"我參加這門課只是為了好玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78f9ac018e5543650691","word":"function","forms":["function"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a14951cecebc69ed","term":"function","forms":["function","functions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"功能；作用","explanation":"指某個東西承擔的工作，或它被設計來發揮的作用。這是 function 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The main function of this button is to lock the screen.","zh":"這個按鈕的主要功能是鎖定螢幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lungs have an important function in keeping the body supplied with oxygen.","zh":"肺部在為身體供應氧氣方面發揮著重要作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/function","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c750187605d4603","term":"function","forms":["function","functions","functioning","functioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起作用；發揮功能","explanation":"表示人或事物確實承擔了某種工作或作用，是名詞“功能、作用”轉為動作的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The old bridge still functions as the main road into the village.","zh":"這座老橋仍然充當進村的主要道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The backup pump functions without mains electricity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/function","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec7a66642321488e","term":"function","forms":["function","functions","functioning","functioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"運轉；在起作用","explanation":"強調某人或某物處於工作狀態，正在執行應有的任務；也可指某個系統正常執行。","examples":[{"en":"The backup system continued to function during the power cut.","zh":"停電期間，備用系統仍繼續運轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pump won't function without a steady power supply.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/function","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b637864e75ab14ebba7","word":"functional","forms":["functional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fff66ed436caf47","term":"functional","forms":["functional","more functional","most functional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"運轉正常的","explanation":"指裝置、系統或身體部位等能夠正常發揮應有作用，沒有失靈。重點是“能工作”，不一定表示效能特別好。","examples":[{"en":"The old printer is still functional, although it works slowly.","zh":"那臺舊印表機雖然執行很慢，但仍然能正常使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to make sure the alarm system is fully functional before opening the building.","zh":"大樓開放前，我們必須確認報警系統能夠完全正常工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/functional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adf9683255e6fb9f","term":"functional","forms":["functional","more functional","most functional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"實用的；有用途的","explanation":"指某物不只是好看或有象徵意義，還能完成明確的實際任務。設計、傢俱和建築中常用這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"The room has a simple but functional design.","zh":"這個房間的設計簡潔而實用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a functional bag with enough space for her laptop.","zh":"她選了一個實用的包，裡面有足夠空間放膝上型電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/functional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-639f78fb7729d09dc606","word":"fund","forms":["fund"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1a23b5c8be0977e","term":"fund","forms":["fund","funds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資金；資金來源","explanation":"指為某種用途準備的一筆錢，或能夠提供這筆錢的資金來源。它強調錢被集中起來、可以按需要使用，就像一個資金池。","examples":[{"en":"The school created a fund for new computers.","zh":"學校設立了一筆購買新電腦的資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity is running out of funds.","zh":"這家慈善機構的資金快用完了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fund","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f65c8cd920ac50e","term":"fund","forms":["fund","funds","funding","funded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"資助；為……提供資金","explanation":"指從資金池中拿出錢，支援某項活動、計劃、組織或個人。重點是錢被實際提供給某個目標，因此也可以理解為“給……撥款”。","examples":[{"en":"The government funded a project to improve public transport.","zh":"政府資助了一個改善公共交通的專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The research is funded by a private foundation.","zh":"這項研究由一傢俬人基金會資助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fund","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c215cc7ced6a185b5bec","word":"fundamental","forms":["fundamental"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04e487afa7cf130f","term":"fundamental","forms":["fundamental","more fundamental","most fundamental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"根本的；極其重要的","explanation":"表示某事物重要到不可缺少，是其他事情能夠成立或正常發展的根本條件；這是日常閱讀中最常見的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"Freedom of speech is a fundamental right.","zh":"言論自由是一項基本權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a fundamental difference between the two approaches.","zh":"這兩種方法之間存在根本差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fundamental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1168799173f89c2","term":"fundamental","forms":["fundamental","fundamentals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基本原則；基本概念","explanation":"指一條可以作為其他想法或規則出發點的基本原則，就像搭建複雜體系時的一塊基礎材料。它既可以是抽象真理，也可以是構成某個體系的基本規則。","examples":[{"en":"Honesty is a fundamental of a fair society.","zh":"誠實是公平社會的一項基本原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course explains the fundamentals of electrical circuits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fundamental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60e04706c43421be4c68","word":"funeral","forms":["funeral"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e36003fbd0979ff7","term":"funeral","forms":["funeral","funerals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葬禮；喪禮","explanation":"為已經去世的人舉行的送別、悼念儀式，通常由親友和其他悼念者參加；通常能見到逝者遺體，因此和只紀念逝者、未必有遺體在場的紀念儀式有所區別。","examples":[{"en":"We attended her funeral on Saturday.","zh":"我們週六參加了她的葬禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people came to the funeral to pay their respects.","zh":"許多人來到葬禮上表達哀悼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/funeral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b22d1d8fe57525339540","word":"funny","forms":["funny"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-57a4ba3bf9b9326e","term":"funny","forms":["funny","funnier","funniest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好笑的；滑稽的","explanation":"指能讓人發笑、具有幽默效果的事物或人。這是 funny 最常見、最容易首先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"That comedian is really funny.","zh":"那個喜劇演員真的很搞笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a funny movie after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們看了一部搞笑的電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/funny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbe22d032e99d507","term":"funny","forms":["funny","funnier","funniest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇怪的；不對勁的","explanation":"指某種感覺、氣味、聲音、行為等和平常不同，讓人覺得奇怪，甚至有些不安。這裡不是“好笑”，而是“不尋常”。","examples":[{"en":"This milk smells funny, so don't drink it.","zh":"這牛奶聞起來不對勁，所以別喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There's something funny about that message.","zh":"那條訊息有點不對勁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/funny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be1130b77b9d58d66a21","word":"fur","forms":["fur"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f4bf07542b7ea78","term":"fur","forms":["fur","furs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的毛","explanation":"指某些哺乳動物身上柔軟、濃密的毛，強調它像一層保暖外套。","examples":[{"en":"The cat has thick, soft fur.","zh":"這隻貓的毛又厚又柔軟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bear's fur kept it warm in winter.","zh":"熊的毛讓它在冬天保持溫暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c505befa4d258620","term":"fur","forms":["fur","furs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毛皮材料","explanation":"指從動物身上取得、用於製作衣物或裝飾的毛皮材料，是“動物外套”被拿來使用的形態。","examples":[{"en":"The shop stopped selling clothing made of fur.","zh":"這家商店停止銷售毛皮製成的衣物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people object to the use of fur in fashion.","zh":"許多人反對在時裝中使用毛皮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab8e1efe40afa48721fe","word":"furious","forms":["furious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bed48b3de4667e62","term":"furious","forms":["furious","more furious","most furious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"暴怒的","explanation":"形容人憤怒到了幾乎無法控制的程度，重點不是普通的不高興，而是怒火強烈、反應激烈。","examples":[{"en":"She was furious with her brother for breaking her laptop.","zh":"她因弟弟弄壞了自己的膝上型電腦而對他大發雷霆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach was furious about the team's careless mistake.","zh":"教練對球隊那個粗心的錯誤怒不可遏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71ee972427abb3df","term":"furious","forms":["furious","more furious","most furious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"猛烈的；來勢洶洶的","explanation":"形容風、暴風雨、水流等自然力量衝得很快、很猛，彷彿帶著暴怒的力量向前衝。","examples":[{"en":"A furious wind drove the rain against the windows.","zh":"猛烈的風把雨狠狠地吹打在窗戶上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A furious storm battered the exposed coastline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2355401ce9b52d24dea4","word":"furnish","forms":["furnish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56cf8f6be6146c72","term":"furnish","forms":["furnish","furnishes","furnishing","furnished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給場所配傢俱裝置","explanation":"把 furnish 想成把一個空房間“填充到可以使用”：給住宅、辦公室等配上傢俱、器材或其他必要裝置。","examples":[{"en":"They furnished the apartment with simple wooden furniture.","zh":"他們給這套公寓配了簡單的木製傢俱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new office is fully furnished.","zh":"這間新辦公室傢俱和裝置齊全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furnish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c191bab497c3bf3","term":"furnish","forms":["furnish","furnishes","furnishing","furnished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提供事物","explanation":"從“把房間填滿所需物品”引申為“提供所需的東西”，賓語可以是資訊、材料、證據、理由等抽象或具體事物。","examples":[{"en":"The report furnished useful information about the local market.","zh":"這份報告提供了有關當地市場的有用資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness furnished the police with additional evidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furnish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a5a9bb73d93fca87ae1","word":"furniture","forms":["furniture"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4300f98e9b344f07","term":"furniture","forms":["furniture","furnitures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傢俱","explanation":"指房間裡用來坐、睡、儲物或裝飾的桌椅、床、櫃子等可移動物品。這是 furniture 在現代英語中的核心義，畫面就是把空房間一點點佈置起來。","examples":[{"en":"We still need to buy some furniture for the new apartment.","zh":"我們還需要為新公寓買些傢俱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room was empty except for one old piece of furniture.","zh":"房間裡除了一箇舊傢俱之外空無一物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furniture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f084f550a2551648","term":"furniture","forms":["furniture","furnitures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門等物品的配件","explanation":"指門、棺材或其他木製品上加裝的把手、鎖件、護板等五金配件。這裡的核心不是整件物品，而是給它補齊功能和外觀的附屬部分。","examples":[{"en":"The brass door furniture matched the lights in the hallway.","zh":"黃銅門配件與走廊裡的燈很相配。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The carpenter fitted new brass door furniture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furniture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a20d00f82196c319bac9","word":"further","forms":["further"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-123c1cde61516d58","term":"further","forms":["further"],"pos":"adj","zh":"更遠的","explanation":"指在空間、距離或位置上比另一個物件更遠，是“向前再走一點”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Of the two cafés, the further one is quieter.","zh":"兩家咖啡館中，較遠的那家更安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The further shore was barely visible through the mist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/further","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e37961e21cd7263","term":"further","forms":["further"],"pos":"adv","zh":"更遠地","explanation":"表示移動、延伸或持續到更遠的距離，也可用於時間或範圍的延伸；仍然是“再向前走一步”的空間畫面。","examples":[{"en":"If you walk further, you will see the lake.","zh":"你再往前走一點，就會看到湖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked further along the shoreline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/further","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91ed7430f3bf06d0","term":"further","forms":["further","furthers","furthering","furthered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"幫助推進；助長","explanation":"表示採取行動讓某件事繼續向前發展，重點是提供幫助或推動，而不是自己移動得更遠。","examples":[{"en":"The partnership will further our shared goals.","zh":"這次合作將推動我們共同目標的實現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scholarship furthered her studies in marine biology.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/further","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-533ce8ef5fb43253e512","word":"furthermore","forms":["furthermore"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be4f34b4ee2021b8","term":"furthermore","forms":["furthermore"],"pos":"adv","zh":"此外；而且","explanation":"說完一個事實後，再把論述向前推進一步，補充另一個相關事實，尤其常用於補充支援前面觀點的理由。","examples":[{"en":"The plan is affordable; furthermore, it can be completed in a week.","zh":"這個計劃負擔得起；而且，它一週內就能完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She speaks three languages and is furthermore an excellent writer.","zh":"她會說三種語言，而且還是一位出色的作家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furthermore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114,115],"total":4,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-f44a052a0ececd804438","word":"fury","forms":["fury"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48608a4141108109","term":"fury","forms":["fury","furies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狂怒","explanation":"指極其強烈的憤怒，彷彿怒火衝破控制、猛烈爆發。它比普通的生氣強得多，常暗示情緒已經接近失控。","examples":[{"en":"She flew into a fury when she saw the broken window.","zh":"她看到破窗後勃然大怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left the room in a fury.","zh":"他怒氣衝衝地離開了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5dae3763f66a6c3","term":"fury","forms":["fury","furies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈的力量","explanation":"表示行動、風暴、火焰等爆發時的強度和衝擊力；這裡是把“怒火的猛烈”擴充套件到其他力量上。","examples":[{"en":"The small boat could not withstand the fury of the storm.","zh":"那條小船經受不住暴風雨的猛烈衝擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sea struck the wall with terrifying fury.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-125c521a95b22c848b64","word":"fuse","forms":["fuse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f95385df8bf0a13e","term":"fuse","forms":["fuse","fuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引信","explanation":"引信是一條或一種會把火傳到爆炸裝置的部件；它本身不是炸彈，而是負責把點火過程傳過去。","examples":[{"en":"Someone had lit the fuse, but the device did not explode.","zh":"有人點燃了引信，但裝置沒有爆炸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bomb's fuse had been carefully removed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a858042cfb3a00f7","term":"fuse","forms":["fuse","fuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險絲","explanation":"保險絲是一段會在電流過大時熔化的金屬部件；它熔斷後切斷電流，防止線路或裝置繼續受損。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen lights went out because a fuse had blown.","zh":"廚房的燈滅了，因為一根保險絲熔斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A blown fuse left the workshop dark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be388e19247b4157","term":"fuse","forms":["fuse","fuses","fusing","fused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使熔化","explanation":"表示用熱使某種物質變成液態；它和保險絲“因過熱而熔斷”的核心畫面相連。","examples":[{"en":"The heat fused the thin wires together.","zh":"高溫把細電線熔接在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Intense heat fused the glass fragments together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64067bc5ef89bb38","term":"fuse","forms":["fuse","fuses","fusing","fused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使融合","explanation":"表示把不同部分熔在一起或混合到難以區分；重點是原本分開的東西形成一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The designer fused traditional patterns with modern materials.","zh":"設計師把傳統圖案和現代材料融合在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jeweler fused two pieces of silver together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-839be58134876f459a5e","word":"fuss","forms":["fuss"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fab6453cf4efad2","term":"fuss","forms":["fuss","fusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大驚小怪；過度操心","explanation":"指為某件事投入過多的活動、擔心、麻煩或討論，常暗示事情本身沒有嚴重到需要如此反應。","examples":[{"en":"The children made a huge fuss about having to leave the park.","zh":"孩子們因為必須離開公園而大吵大鬧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She fixed the mistake without any fuss.","zh":"她不聲不響地把錯誤改好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c520b2407897a52d","term":"fuss","forms":["fuss","fusses","fussing","fussed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"過分操心；過度興奮","explanation":"指對某事過分擔心、激動或忙亂，程度常被認為超過實際需要。","examples":[{"en":"There is no need to fuss about a little rain.","zh":"下點小雨，沒必要這麼大驚小怪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My father still fusses over every detail of the trip.","zh":"我父親仍然對旅行的每個細節都過分操心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fuss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebb3de8a3d9a40366132","word":"future","forms":["future"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-efc048910f495eeb","term":"future","forms":["future"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未來的；將來的","explanation":"指時間上還沒有到來的，或屬於將來的人、事。它把某個名詞放到“那條還沒走到的路”上，例如未來的世代、未來的計劃。","examples":[{"en":"Future generations may judge our choices very differently.","zh":"未來的世代也許會以完全不同的方式評價我們的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is already thinking about her future career.","zh":"她已經在考慮自己未來的職業了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/future","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d442c96f26fbbf2","term":"future","forms":["future","futures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未來；將來","explanation":"指現在之後、還沒有經歷的那段時間，是“前方那條還沒走到的路”本身。它可以泛指人的未來，也可以指整個社會或世界的未來。","examples":[{"en":"We cannot know exactly what the future will bring.","zh":"我們無法確切知道未來會帶來什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is saving money for the future.","zh":"她正在為未來存錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/future","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2da5aa4f38b53d97","term":"future","forms":["future","futures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前景；命運走向","explanation":"指某人、團體或事物今後可能走向的結果，是“沿著這條路繼續走會到哪裡”。它強調對發展狀況的判斷，例如前景光明或前景不佳。","examples":[{"en":"The company has a promising future if it keeps improving its product.","zh":"如果這家公司繼續改進產品，它會有很好的發展前景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village faces an uncertain economic future.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/future","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66dd231befc8120d323e","word":"gain","forms":["gain"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-135e2f54ea42f181","term":"gain","forms":["gain","gains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獲得；收益","explanation":"表示獲得某種好處、利益或成果的過程，重點是“得到並因此有所收穫”。","examples":[{"en":"The company saw a gain in efficiency after the changes.","zh":"改動後，這家公司在效率方面有所提高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a steady gain in confidence.","zh":"她的自信心穩步提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-111869b898182cb9","term":"gain","forms":["gain","gains","gaining","gained","gain'd","gainest","gainedst","gaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲得；取得","explanation":"表示得到原來沒有的東西、關係、機會或地位，核心畫面是把某物收入自己這邊。","examples":[{"en":"She gained valuable experience during the internship.","zh":"她在實習期間獲得了寶貴的經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He quickly gained the trust of his colleagues.","zh":"他很快贏得了同事們的信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c519f581cedb3fb1","term":"gain","forms":["gain","gains","gaining","gained","gain'd","gainest","gainedst","gaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲益；取得進展","explanation":"表示獲得優勢、利益，或在健康、能力、事業等方面逐漸進步；也可指變得富有或幸福。","examples":[{"en":"The team gained confidence after winning the first game.","zh":"球隊贏下第一場比賽後信心增強了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small businesses can gain from better online services.","zh":"小企業可以從更好的線上服務中獲益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eba4ae33f54ae0f96bed","word":"galaxy","forms":["galaxy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a20150e24a274f35","term":"galaxy","forms":["galaxy","galaxies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"星系","explanation":"星系是由數以百萬或數十億計的恆星，以及星際塵埃、黑洞等組成的巨大天體系統；銀河系只是其中一個例子。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists discovered a distant galaxy with a powerful telescope.","zh":"科學家用一臺強大的望遠鏡發現了一個遙遠的星系。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our galaxy contains billions of stars.","zh":"我們的星系包含數十億顆恆星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/galaxy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7f935933690781a","term":"galaxy","forms":["galaxy","galaxies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"群星般耀眼的一群人或事物","explanation":"這裡把許多出色、引人注目的人或事物比作聚成一片的星光，強調它們數量多而且個個耀眼。","examples":[{"en":"The festival brought together a galaxy of young musicians.","zh":"這場節日活動匯聚了一群才華橫溢的年輕音樂家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A galaxy of celebrated actors attended the premiere.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/galaxy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce387d5e0a2972dea9e5","word":"gallery","forms":["gallery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0070e06cb9ee056","term":"gallery","forms":["gallery","galleries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"畫廊；展館","explanation":"指展示、儲存藝術品或其他重要物件的機構、建築或房間。它可以是專門的美術館，也可以是較小的展覽空間。","examples":[{"en":"The gallery is displaying paintings by local artists this month.","zh":"這家畫廊本月正在展出當地藝術家的畫作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent the afternoon exploring the new gallery.","zh":"我們整個下午都在參觀新開的展館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gallery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3245895fe54e08fb","term":"gallery","forms":["gallery","galleries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劇院樓座","explanation":"指劇院、音樂廳或禮堂後方、側面較高處伸出的座席區，通常票價較低、離舞臺較遠。","examples":[{"en":"We bought gallery seats because they were cheaper.","zh":"我們買了樓座的座位，因為票價更便宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"From the gallery, the stage looked very small.","zh":"從樓座看下去，舞臺顯得很小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gallery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf8df08393fe40177c2a","word":"gallon","forms":["gallon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b58caf557bb0d7d","term":"gallon","forms":["gallon","gallons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"加侖；體積單位","explanation":"gallon是一個體積單位，尤其常用於表示汽油、牛奶和水等液體的容量。它的具體大小要看採用英國標準還是美國標準。","examples":[{"en":"We bought two gallons of milk for the week.","zh":"我們買了兩加侖牛奶，夠這周喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This tank holds ten gallons of water.","zh":"這個水箱能裝十加侖水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gallon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca457924fcac2c3a","term":"gallon","forms":["gallon","gallons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英制加侖","explanation":"在英國和加拿大語境中，gallon通常指英制加侖，恰好等於4.54609升。","examples":[{"en":"The car uses about one gallon of fuel every forty miles.","zh":"這輛車每行駛四十英里大約耗油一英制加侖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An imperial gallon holds about four and a half liters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gallon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ee616488dbedb0c34c2","word":"gallop","forms":["gallop"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed00b5e9afc3190e","term":"gallop","forms":["gallop","gallops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬的賓士","explanation":"指馬最快的一種步態：馬在奔跑過程中會有一瞬間四條腿同時離地。它也可以泛指這種高速賓士的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The horse broke into a gallop as soon as the gate opened.","zh":"大門一開啟，那匹馬就飛奔起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard the gallop of horses in the distance.","zh":"我們聽見遠處傳來馬匹賓士的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gallop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a622abdefad0a5e","term":"gallop","forms":["gallop","gallops","galloping","galloped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"賓士","explanation":"指馬以最快步態奔跑，畫面就是四蹄騰空、一路向前衝。","examples":[{"en":"The horse galloped past the finish line.","zh":"那匹馬賓士著衝過了終點線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The riders galloped across the field at sunset.","zh":"日落時，騎手們騎馬賓士著穿過田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gallop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-377d648d65f2dbfe7e3e","word":"gamble","forms":["gamble"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c96ef8ba25eb9a35","term":"gamble","forms":["gamble","gambles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下注；賭博","explanation":"gamble 可以指一次下注或賭博行為：你把錢押在某個結果上，希望贏得更多。","examples":[{"en":"I had a small gamble on the horse race last weekend.","zh":"上週末我在賽馬上小賭了一把。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He lost his savings on a reckless gamble.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gamble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8aac2d27fa51da6","term":"gamble","forms":["gamble","gambles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冒險行為","explanation":"這裡的 gamble 是一次有明顯風險的選擇：結果可能帶來很大好處，也可能失敗，不一定真的涉及賭博或金錢。","examples":[{"en":"Starting a business was a gamble, but it paid off.","zh":"創業是一場冒險，但最後成功了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Opening a restaurant there was a considerable gamble.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gamble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45f21a3097256ce0","term":"gamble","forms":["gamble","gambles","gambling","gambled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒險","explanation":"gamble 作動詞時，表示為了可能得到好結果而承擔風險，就像把選擇押在一個不確定的結果上。","examples":[{"en":"She gambled on a new approach and won the team’s support.","zh":"她冒險採用了一種新方法，贏得了團隊的支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gambled his savings on opening a restaurant.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gamble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ca5cab77e702c787b4c","word":"game","forms":["game"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77258af218de6690","term":"game","forms":["game","games"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊戲；比賽活動","explanation":"指為了娛樂或競爭而進行的、有一定規則的活動，是 game 最基本的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We played a game after dinner.","zh":"我們晚飯後玩了一個遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children spent the afternoon playing games.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在玩遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/game","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2546dd17b0e8c2df","term":"game","forms":["game","games"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一項具體遊戲","explanation":"指一種具體設計出來供人玩的遊戲，例如課堂遊戲、棋盤遊戲或電子遊戲。","examples":[{"en":"This game helps students learn new words.","zh":"這個遊戲能幫助學生學習新單詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chess is a game that rewards patient planning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/game","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e17c0d0d0bf52527df9","word":"gang","forms":["gang"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c921e2733c4057b","term":"gang","forms":["gang","gangs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一群人；團伙","explanation":"指因為一起行動、交往或共同目標而聚在一起的一群人，語氣可以中性，也可以帶有不太正式的色彩。","examples":[{"en":"A gang of students gathered outside the library.","zh":"一群學生聚集在圖書館外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The whole gang is coming over for dinner tonight.","zh":"大家今晚要一起過來吃飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-651101b4b283a4c7","term":"gang","forms":["gang","gangs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫派","explanation":"指有共同身份、地盤或標誌，並經常一起活動的犯罪性團體，尤其常指街頭青年幫派。","examples":[{"en":"The police believe the gang controls several blocks.","zh":"警方認為這個幫派控制著好幾個街區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gang controlled several streets near the station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a869c1ff4397a5b1d91","word":"gangster","forms":["gangster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-855851397c0c9a50","term":"gangster","forms":["gangster","gangsters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫派成員；歹徒","explanation":"指屬於犯罪團伙或街頭幫派的人，通常讓人聯想到暴力、非法活動或幫派生活。","examples":[{"en":"The police arrested a gangster near the warehouse.","zh":"警方在倉庫附近逮捕了一名歹徒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film follows a young gangster trying to leave the gang.","zh":"這部電影講述了一個想離開幫派的年輕歹徒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gangster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-54d5dbf0124e59afba31","word":"gap","forms":["gap"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04f1ceb683251b45","term":"gap","forms":["gap","gaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺口；破口","explanation":"原本完整的東西被弄開或損壞後出現的開口，重點是“連續表面被開啟了一個空處”。","examples":[{"en":"He made a gap in the fence by kicking at a weak spot.","zh":"他朝圍欄的薄弱處踢了幾腳，踢出了一個缺口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rabbit escaped through a gap in the fence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7cde183f8439f9d9","term":"gap","forms":["gap","gaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可透過的空隙","explanation":"兩個物體或位置之間留下了足以讓人或物透過的空間，核心仍是“開啟一條通道”。","examples":[{"en":"We can slip through that gap between the buildings.","zh":"我們可以從那兩棟樓之間的空隙溜過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mouse slipped through a gap beneath the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c29d7eb28b1cd1cd","term":"gap","forms":["gap","gaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空檔；空閒時間","explanation":"連續安排中暫時空出來的一段時間，就像日程表上出現了一個空處。","examples":[{"en":"I have a gap in my schedule next Tuesday.","zh":"我下週二的日程中有一段空檔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found a gap between appointments for lunch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21b747de22dbb757fde3","word":"garage","forms":["garage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e2f369f86a375feb","term":"garage","forms":["garage","garages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車庫","explanation":"指用來停放汽車、工具和雜物的建築或其中一部分，最常見的畫面就是住宅旁邊可以把車關在裡面的空間。","examples":[{"en":"I left my bicycle in the garage overnight.","zh":"我把腳踏車放在車庫裡過了一夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garage is full of old boxes.","zh":"車庫裡堆滿了舊箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-795b6904e54f82411df4","word":"garbage","forms":["garbage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e918d95d0cb630aa","term":"garbage","forms":["garbage"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廢棄物；生活垃圾","explanation":"泛指不再需要、準備丟棄或處理的材料，包括家庭和市政產生的各種垃圾。","examples":[{"en":"The garbage truck comes every Tuesday morning.","zh":"垃圾車每週二早上來收垃圾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to take out the garbage before dinner.","zh":"我們得在晚飯前把垃圾拿出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garbage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e4ff9ba16da45af","term":"garbage","forms":["garbage"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胡說八道；無意義的話","explanation":"把沒有道理、沒有價值或無法信任的資訊看成語言垃圾，因此可指胡說八道、荒謬內容或糟糕的資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The article is full of garbage.","zh":"這篇文章裡滿是胡說八道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't listen to that garbage online.","zh":"別聽信網上那些胡說八道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garbage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23eeb69c681dfdb8eacc","word":"garden","forms":["garden"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf7f6d67cb82cdcb","term":"garden","forms":["garden","gardens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"花園；園地","explanation":"指戶外一塊種植植物的地方，可以種蔬菜、水果、花卉或觀賞植物，是 garden 最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We grow tomatoes and herbs in our garden.","zh":"我們在自家花園裡種西紅柿和香草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are playing in the garden.","zh":"孩子們正在花園裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b1a389110cb30b4","term":"garden","forms":["garden","gardens","gardening","gardened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做園藝；打理花園","explanation":"指種植、照料花園中的植物，或負責建立和維護一塊花園；它把名詞 garden 變成了“照料這塊園地”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"My grandmother gardens every morning.","zh":"我祖母每天早上都做園藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I started gardening after moving to the country.","zh":"搬到鄉下後，我開始做園藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9416a9df5328046b781b","word":"gardener","forms":["gardener"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b094f3bc99f3bbb","term":"gardener","forms":["gardener","gardeners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"園藝工；園丁","explanation":"指種植植物、修剪花木或照料花園的人。核心畫面就是一個長期守護花園、讓植物生長起來的人。","examples":[{"en":"The gardener planted roses along the path.","zh":"園藝工沿著小路種下了玫瑰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hired a gardener to look after the large backyard.","zh":"我們僱了一名園藝工照料這座大後院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gardener","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41024084d2e27b7db742","word":"garlic","forms":["garlic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b7a3b23e74b6528","term":"garlic","forms":["garlic","garlics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大蒜；蒜頭","explanation":"指大蒜這種植物，尤其可指地下的蒜頭；它和洋蔥相近，味道辛辣，常用於烹飪。","examples":[{"en":"She planted garlic in the garden last autumn.","zh":"她去年秋天在花園裡種了大蒜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He bought a bulb of garlic at the market.","zh":"他在市場上買了一頭蒜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garlic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c083081ab7128244","term":"garlic","forms":["garlic","garlics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蒜；蒜味","explanation":"指剝下、切碎或加工後作為食材使用的大蒜，也可以指食物帶有的蒜味；這裡重點不是整株植物，而是進鍋裡的蒜。","examples":[{"en":"Add some chopped garlic to the pan before the onions.","zh":"把切碎的蒜加進鍋裡，放在洋蔥之前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Crush the garlic before adding it to the sauce.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garlic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a8b166e62b835fc5547","word":"garment","forms":["garment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a112be4099572b41","term":"garment","forms":["garment","garments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一件衣服","explanation":"指可以穿在身上的一件具體衣物，重點是把衣服看作一個獨立的物件，而不是泛指穿衣這件事。","examples":[{"en":"Each garment is checked for loose buttons before it is packed.","zh":"每件衣服在打包前都要檢查是否有鬆動的紐扣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a warm garment for the cold journey.","zh":"她為寒冷的旅程選了一件保暖衣物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-64ef59378ce76b7531d0","word":"gasoline/gas","forms":["gasoline","gas"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e2749cfd0090548c","term":"gasoline","forms":["gasoline","gasolines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽油","explanation":"一種從石油中提煉出的易燃液體，主要給汽車等發動機提供動力；這是 gasoline 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We need to buy gasoline before the long drive.","zh":"長途開車前，我們得先買汽油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This truck runs on diesel, not gasoline.","zh":"這輛卡車用柴油，不用汽油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gasoline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb083ba945c55e78","term":"gas","forms":["gas","gases","gasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氣體","explanation":"gas 是物質的一種狀態：它不像液體那樣固定形狀，會擴散並充滿可用空間，例如空氣、氧氣或水蒸氣。","examples":[{"en":"The gas escaped through a small crack.","zh":"氣體從一道小裂縫中洩漏了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water vapor is a gas.","zh":"水蒸氣是一種氣體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44314e0cf86bc786","term":"gas","forms":["gas","gases","gasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽油","explanation":"在部分英語地區，gas 是 gasoline 的簡稱，指給汽車發動機使用的汽油。","examples":[{"en":"I need to stop for gas before the trip.","zh":"出發前我得停下來加點汽油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stopped for gas before leaving the highway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ac7f69ea53de68a0662","word":"gasp","forms":["gasp"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11861f0a0e8d2531","term":"gasp","forms":["gasp","gasps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突然吸氣；驚呼聲","explanation":"指人在震驚、害怕或驚訝時突然吸進的一口氣，也可以指這一下吸氣發出的聲音。它把“吸氣的動作”和“驚訝的聲音”合在了同一個核心畫面裡。","examples":[{"en":"A gasp of surprise came from the back of the room.","zh":"房間後面傳來一聲驚訝的吸氣聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An audible gasp greeted the surprising announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bad4c4f2bac0950","term":"gasp","forms":["gasp","gasps","gasping","gasped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"驚訝得突然吸氣","explanation":"指人因震驚、害怕或意外而突然吸進一口氣，是 gasp 最典型的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"She gasped when the lights suddenly went out.","zh":"燈突然熄滅時，她驚得倒吸了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audience gasped when the acrobat slipped.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcf29b3546e88e83","term":"gasp","forms":["gasp","gasps","gasping","gasped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喘氣；呼吸急促","explanation":"指運動、爬坡或過度用力後呼吸又快又費力，是“突然吸氣”在持續體力負擔下的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"He was gasping for breath after running up the stairs.","zh":"跑上樓梯後，他喘得上氣不接下氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gasped for air after the steep climb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c974e17b8e7321ce8c12","word":"gate","forms":["gate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b5bc489c8ab8cc1","term":"gate","forms":["gate","gates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房屋外的門","explanation":"它是房屋外面、像門一樣可以開合的結構，是“控制通行的開口”這一記憶中的最基本實物。","examples":[{"en":"Please close the gate to the yard.","zh":"請把院子的門關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are waiting outside the gate.","zh":"孩子們在門外等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61495284411900cb","term":"gate","forms":["gate","gates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可移動的閘門","explanation":"它是能夠升起、降下或移動的屏障，用來暫時阻斷或放行交通，仍然體現“控制通行”的記憶。","examples":[{"en":"The gate at the railway crossing went up after the train passed.","zh":"火車透過後，鐵路道口的閘門升了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gate at the entrance is still closed.","zh":"入口的閘門仍然關閉著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0860df80f25f4cbe","term":"gate","forms":["gate","gates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機場登機口","explanation":"在機場等交通場所，它指乘客登機或下機所經過的通道口，是公共場所中的“控制通行的開口”。","examples":[{"en":"Our flight boards at Gate 12.","zh":"我們的航班從十二號登機口登機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wait near the gate.","zh":"請在登機口附近等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9da0bd78f29fd838d1a","word":"gather","forms":["gather"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90b211a50f76e67c","term":"gather","forms":["gather","gathers","gathering","gathered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收集；蒐集","explanation":"把原本分散的東西、人們的意見或資訊收集到一起。重點是主動把許多零散物件集中起來。","examples":[{"en":"She gathered ideas from everyone on the team.","zh":"她收集了團隊每個人的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to gather more information before deciding.","zh":"我們需要收集更多資訊後再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c813298f9266988","term":"gather","forms":["gather","gathers","gathering","gathered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聚集；集合","explanation":"指人或事物從分散狀態聚到同一個地方。這裡不一定有一個人負責收集，重點是大家自己聚攏起來。","examples":[{"en":"A small crowd gathered around the musician.","zh":"一小群人聚在那位音樂家周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students gathered outside the library.","zh":"學生們聚集在圖書館外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a6990e6ccf4b1ca","term":"gather","forms":["gather","gathers","gathering","gathered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攏起；收攏","explanation":"把一個整體的各部分向一起拉近或攏住，例如把披肩攏在身上、把布料抽出褶皺。它仍然是“讓分散部分靠攏”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She gathered her coat around her in the cold wind.","zh":"寒風中，她把外套攏緊在身上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gathered her skirt above the muddy ground.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45441664c0ba6a9d6afb","word":"gathering","forms":["gathering"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1d3abbe8c98b472","term":"gathering","forms":["gathering","gatherings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聚會；集會","explanation":"指人們為了社交、討論或共同活動而聚到一起的場合，既可以是輕鬆的聚會，也可以是較正式的集會。","examples":[{"en":"We had a small family gathering on Sunday.","zh":"星期天我們舉行了一次小型家庭聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke at a gathering of local artists.","zh":"她在當地藝術家的集會上發了言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gathering","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a90fd9a9a1e66597ae12","word":"gauge","forms":["gauge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42498c9d2bfe4c57","term":"gauge","forms":["gauge","gauges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"測量標準或工具","explanation":"指用來測量大小、距離、容量等的標準或工具，也可以泛指衡量某種程度的尺度。這是從“測量桿”發展出來的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"Public opinion is an important gauge of how people feel about the policy.","zh":"公眾輿論是衡量人們如何看待這項政策的重要標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pilot checked the fuel gauge before takeoff.","zh":"飛行員在起飛前檢視了燃油表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gauge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5cdcbe8e3746b06","term":"gauge","forms":["gauge","gauges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"估計；判斷","explanation":"指根據已有資訊估計數量、程度或情況，是從“用尺度測量”引申出的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The number of visitors is a useful gauge of the event's success.","zh":"訪客數量是衡量活動是否成功的一個有用指標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ticket sales provide a gauge of public interest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gauge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8e66e50dfcb13d7","term":"gauge","forms":["gauge","gauges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"測量儀表","explanation":"指用來測定或調節液位、狀態、尺寸或形狀的具體儀器，例如壓力錶、溫度表或液位計。這個意思仍然保留了“藉助工具衡量”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"A warning light comes on when the temperature gauge gets too high.","zh":"溫度表讀數過高時，警示燈就會亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pressure gauge showed a dangerous rise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gauge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7689eadd98e727a","term":"gauge","forms":["gauge","gauges","gauging","gauged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"測量；確定容量","explanation":"指用儀表或其他標準測量某物的大小、距離、程度或容量，是“測量桿”這一核心形象最直接的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer gauged the depth of the hole before ordering the pipe.","zh":"工程師先測量了孔的深度，然後才訂購管子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to gauge the tank's capacity accurately.","zh":"我們需要準確測出這個罐子的容量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gauge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3c58783ae34d2f8","term":"gauge","forms":["gauge","gauges","gauging","gauged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"估計","explanation":"指根據觀察或已有資訊估計數量、程度或可能結果，不一定使用實際儀器。它是把“測量”擴充套件到無法直接量出的事物。","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to gauge how much support the proposal has.","zh":"很難估計這項提案獲得了多少支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gauged the distance and chose a safer route.","zh":"她估計了一下距離，選擇了更安全的路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gauge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-586acb3c6bac489308c0","word":"gay","forms":["gay"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-145214d8d51e2ae2","term":"gay","forms":["gay","gayer","gayest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"同性戀的","explanation":"指對同性產生情感或性吸引的人，或與同性戀者有關的事物；這是現代最核心的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Cliff is gay, but his twin brother is straight.","zh":"克利夫是同性戀者，但他的雙胞胎兄弟是異性戀者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city opened a gay community center.","zh":"這座城市開設了一家同性戀者社群中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf77058e73b87927","term":"gay","forms":["gay","gayer","gayest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"同性戀的（嚴格指同性戀者）","explanation":"強調 gay 直接指同性戀者或同性戀群體，而不是泛指所有性少數群體。","examples":[{"en":"The program offers support to gay and lesbian students.","zh":"這項計劃為同性戀男女學生提供支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel follows a gay couple raising their daughter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8b0e7effd208c1e2e3e","word":"gaze","forms":["gaze"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3e24dff36ce8841","term":"gaze","forms":["gaze","gazes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凝視；目光","explanation":"指長時間、專注地看，也指這種帶有好奇、驚歎、欣賞或強烈注意的目光。它不是輕輕掃過，而是把目光固定在物件上。","examples":[{"en":"Her curious gaze followed the bright kite across the sky.","zh":"她好奇的目光隨著那隻明亮的風箏劃過天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I could feel his gaze on me while I was speaking.","zh":"我說話時能感覺到他的目光一直落在我身上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gaze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a24631719aa7cc9e","term":"gaze","forms":["gaze","gazes","gazing","gazed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"凝視；專注地看","explanation":"指持續而認真地看著某人或某物，目光像固定的光束一樣停在那裡。它可以表達好奇、驚歎、欣賞，也可以只是高度專注。","examples":[{"en":"We gazed at the stars until the fire went out.","zh":"我們一直凝望著星星，直到篝火熄滅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child gazed at the snow falling outside the window.","zh":"孩子凝視著窗外飄落的雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gaze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70ad3de50a55e77d300b","word":"gear","forms":["gear"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d6068f0cfe35f84","term":"gear","forms":["gear","gears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝備","explanation":"gear 指為某項運動、活動或工作準備的一整套用品和器材，重點是“做某事所需的裝備”。","examples":[{"en":"We need to buy some camping gear before the trip.","zh":"旅行前我們需要買些露營裝備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All his climbing gear was packed in one bag.","zh":"他的所有攀巖裝備都裝在一個包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cfc63ab1750c702","term":"gear","forms":["gear","gears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"齒輪","explanation":"gear 指外緣有齒、能與另一個齒輪咬合並傳遞運動的輪狀部件；這裡的核心畫面是兩個齒輪互相咬住，讓機器運轉。","examples":[{"en":"A broken gear stopped the machine from working.","zh":"一個損壞的齒輪使機器無法運轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two gears turn together inside the clock.","zh":"這兩個齒輪在鐘的內部一起轉動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-671c771142ea3cc0","term":"gear","forms":["gear","gears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擋位","explanation":"gear 還指一組相互配合的齒輪所形成的擋位；換擋就是選擇不同的齒輪組合，從而改變車輛或腳踏車的傳動比例。","examples":[{"en":"Shift into a lower gear before going down the hill.","zh":"下坡前換到低擋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car was still in first gear.","zh":"這輛車還在一擋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce125c92cf13271c","term":"gear","forms":["gear","gears","gearing","geared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使適合；面向","explanation":"gear something toward someone or something 表示按照目標物件來設計或調整某物，使它適合那類人或那種用途；就像把機器的配置調到合適的擋位。","examples":[{"en":"The course is geared toward beginners.","zh":"這門課程是為初學者設計的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company geared its advertising toward young families.","zh":"公司把廣告定位在年輕家庭這一群體上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de9feaea8b66f7ba7484","word":"gender","forms":["gender"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d40bcb6ffd51df41","term":"gender","forms":["gender","genders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會性別；性別身份","explanation":"指一個人對自身性別的認同，以及與這種認同相關的社會角色、行為、服裝和表達方式。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone should be free to express their gender in their own way.","zh":"每個人都應該可以用自己的方式表達性別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her gender identity is an important part of her life.","zh":"她的性別身份是她生活中的重要部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1eea0826725bc61","term":"gender","forms":["gender","genders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語法性","explanation":"語言學中，指名詞、代詞等被分為陽性、陰性、中性或其他類別的語法系統；這種分類不一定對應真實的生理性別。","examples":[{"en":"German nouns can have masculine, feminine, or neuter gender.","zh":"德語名詞可以有陽性、陰性或中性語法性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pronoun changes according to the gender of its antecedent.","zh":"代詞會根據先行詞的語法性而變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ac52c67c10a6cea6daa","word":"gene","forms":["gene"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-372935ce5cd5a591","term":"gene","forms":["gene","genes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遺傳單位","explanation":"gene可以理解為遺傳“說明書”中的一個資訊單元：它可能以不同形式存在，並在原則上決定或影響生物的某種特徵，例如頭髮顏色。這是較抽象的遺傳學概念。","examples":[{"en":"She inherited a gene for curly hair from her mother.","zh":"她從母親那裡遺傳了一個與捲髮有關的基因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are studying genes linked to eye color.","zh":"科學家正在研究與眼睛顏色相關的基因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f64f904830bba626","term":"gene","forms":["gene","genes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"DNA或RNA片段","explanation":"在分子生物學中，gene更具體地指基因組中的一段DNA或RNA序列；這段序列可以有不同形式，並參與規定某種生物過程，例如蛋白質的結構。也就是說，前一個意義偏向“資訊單位”，這裡更強調承載資訊的實際片段。","examples":[{"en":"This gene encodes a protein involved in cell growth.","zh":"這個基因編碼一種參與細胞生長的蛋白質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A mutation changed the sequence of the gene.","zh":"一次突變改變了這個基因的序列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0feae16d55365acf07fe","word":"general","forms":["general"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be888df98f2c08db","term":"general","forms":["general","more general","most general"],"pos":"adj","zh":"總體的；普遍的","explanation":"指涉及某個整體的每一部分或每個成員，而不是隻針對其中一小部分；核心感覺是“大家都包括在內”。","examples":[{"en":"The general rule is that visitors must sign in.","zh":"總的規定是訪客必須登記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a general feeling of relief after the announcement.","zh":"公告發布後，大家普遍感到如釋重負。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/general","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a92e7591359d7b20","term":"general","forms":["general","more general","most general"],"pos":"adj","zh":"普遍的；常見的","explanation":"指某種情況在一群人、一個地區或一個時期內廣泛存在，是大家通常會遇到的情況。","examples":[{"en":"There is general agreement that the plan needs changes.","zh":"大家普遍同意這個計劃需要修改。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Concern about the factory closure became general throughout the town.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/general","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd58a23df22d80db","term":"general","forms":["general","more general","most general"],"pos":"adj","zh":"概括的；籠統的","explanation":"只說明最重要的輪廓，不展開次要細節，因此資訊比較寬泛、不具體。","examples":[{"en":"I understand the general idea, but I need the exact steps.","zh":"我明白大致思路，但還需要具體步驟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report gives only a general description of the problem.","zh":"這份報告只對問題作了概括性描述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/general","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7c5ffdcd68e51a1","term":"general","forms":["general","generals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"將軍","explanation":"指軍隊中的高階指揮官，核心形象是掌握全域性並負責指揮大規模軍事行動的人。","examples":[{"en":"The general ordered the soldiers to withdraw.","zh":"將軍命令士兵撤退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a general after decades in the army.","zh":"她在軍隊服役數十年後成為將軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/general","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24cacf5004bf68ae9daa","word":"generate","forms":["generate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7abebb7abba4234","term":"generate","forms":["generate","generates","generating","generated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引起；產生結果","explanation":"指某件事把一種結果、反應或情緒帶出來，讓原本沒有的東西出現。它既能用於具體結果，也能用於騷動、興趣、支援等抽象結果。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign generated a great deal of public interest.","zh":"這項活動引起了公眾的極大興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her remark generated an angry response from the audience.","zh":"她的話引起了聽眾的憤怒回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81538c2561f27165","term":"generate","forms":["generate","generates","generating","generated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"產生能量或物質","explanation":"指裝置、反應或其他物理過程生成熱量、電力、氣體等可觀察的產物；仍然是“讓某物出現”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"These panels generate enough electricity to power the whole house.","zh":"這些面板產生的電力足以供應整棟房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bacteria in the compost generate enough heat to produce steam.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e661f4c935e8a5a83349","word":"generation","forms":["generation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1e2faa62a87b5ce","term":"generation","forms":["generation","generations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生成；產生","explanation":"指把某種東西創造出來或使其出現的過程。它是整組詞義的起點：有東西被“產生”出來，才會進一步談到新的一代或新階段。","examples":[{"en":"The generation of clean energy is becoming more affordable.","zh":"清潔能源的生產正變得越來越負擔得起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine is designed for the generation of steam.","zh":"這臺機器用於產生蒸汽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffc5a6322c1dd01b","term":"generation","forms":["generation","generations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一代；家族世代","explanation":"指家族延續中的一個層次，或由同一對父母產生、處在同一層次的家庭成員。它把“產生”具體化為父母產生子女、家族一代代向下延續。","examples":[{"en":"Three generations of the family live under one roof.","zh":"這個家庭的三代人住在同一屋簷下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is the first generation in her family to attend university.","zh":"她是家裡第一代上大學的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7f35a93786518cc","term":"generation","forms":["generation","generations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一代人的時間","explanation":"指從一代人成長到生育下一代所需的大致時間，通常約三十年；也可藉此表示相隔多少代、多少個這樣的時間段。","examples":[{"en":"The village changed completely in just one generation.","zh":"這個村莊僅僅一代人的時間就徹底變了樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two generations later, the family still runs the shop.","zh":"兩代人之後，這家人仍然經營著這家店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9123dcbb0b42652b0e10","word":"generator","forms":["generator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20faa8c4922814f0","term":"generator","forms":["generator","generators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發電機；能量轉換裝置","explanation":"指把一種形式的能量轉化為另一種形式的裝置，最常見的是把機械能轉化為電能的發電機。它仍然符合“產出器”的影象，只是產出的物件變成了能量，尤其是電。","examples":[{"en":"We used a portable generator during the power cut.","zh":"停電期間，我們使用了一臺行動式發電機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind turns the generator and produces electricity.","zh":"風帶動發電機併產生電力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97ccbe07926e22c6","term":"generator","forms":["generator","generators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"產生者；來源","explanation":"指產生、促成或製造某種事物的人或事物，可以是具體的生產者，也可以是某種結果的來源。這裡的核心不是機器，而是“帶來某種產出”。","examples":[{"en":"Tourism is an important generator of local income.","zh":"旅遊業是當地收入的重要來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory became a major generator of employment in the valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b284e5fb60aba4fb16d","word":"generosity","forms":["generosity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7a27c9f5e570774","term":"generosity","forms":["generosity","generosities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慷慨；大方","explanation":"指一個人願意拿出錢、物品、時間或幫助來分享的品質，重點不在給了多少，而在於願意向外給予。它可以用於捐贈，也可以用於日常幫助和待人寬厚。","examples":[{"en":"Her generosity helped the family get through a difficult winter.","zh":"她的慷慨幫助這家人熬過了一個艱難的冬天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We were touched by his generosity with both his time and money.","zh":"他在時間和金錢上的慷慨讓我們很感動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generosity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-daf73fd60aca6732","term":"generosity","forms":["generosity","generosities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慷慨之舉","explanation":"指一次具體的慷慨行為，比如一筆捐款、一次幫助或某種善意的給予；也可以泛指多次這樣的行為。","examples":[{"en":"The shelter will remember her generosity for many years.","zh":"這家收容所很多年都會記得她的那次慷慨相助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her many generosities included paying a neighbor's rent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generosity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8aef9b5ddede4f620d83","word":"generous","forms":["generous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70e333f8474f754d","term":"generous","forms":["generous","more generous","most generous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬厚大方的","explanation":"形容一個人待人寬厚、心胸開闊，不愛計較，也願意給予幫助或體諒；重點是品格上的大方，而不只是物質上的富有。","examples":[{"en":"Thank you for your generous words.","zh":"謝謝你那些寬厚而充滿善意的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was generous enough to give me another chance.","zh":"她非常寬厚，願意再給我一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a80aafc71ee5bc1","term":"generous","forms":["generous","more generous","most generous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慷慨給予的","explanation":"表示願意不吝惜地給予或分享，給出的數量、金錢、時間或幫助通常比別人預期的更多。","examples":[{"en":"She's been extremely generous with her winnings.","zh":"她一直非常慷慨，願意分享自己的獎金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our neighbors were generous with their time and help.","zh":"我們的鄰居很慷慨，投入了很多時間並提供了大量幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/generous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05cf69408f5a187965c2","word":"genetic","forms":["genetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23f920d83b4ac945","term":"genetic","forms":["genetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基因的；遺傳學的","explanation":"表示某事物與基因、遺傳資訊或遺傳學研究有關，例如遺傳差異、基因變異等。","examples":[{"en":"The two varieties show considerable genetic diversity.","zh":"這兩個品種表現出相當大的遺傳多樣性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A genetic test confirmed the inherited condition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef80ba84641dd4e7","term":"genetic","forms":["genetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由基因造成的","explanation":"強調某種特徵、疾病或傾向的成因在基因，而不只是說它與基因研究有關；這仍然是“家譜樹上由上一代傳下來的特徵”這一核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"Doctors suspect that the condition is genetic.","zh":"醫生懷疑這種病症是由基因造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The condition has a genetic cause.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-3b096ab7467aff69376a","word":"genetics","forms":["genetics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b3aea3d89b0a08c","term":"genetics","forms":["genetics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遺傳學","explanation":"指研究遺傳資訊如何從親代傳給後代，以及這些遺傳特徵為什麼會發生差異的生物學分支，涉及染色體、DNA等內容。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to study genetics at university.","zh":"她決定在大學學習遺傳學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Advances in genetics are helping scientists understand inherited diseases.","zh":"遺傳學的進展正在幫助科學家瞭解遺傳性疾病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genetics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-840ae0e38ffd7d72","term":"genetics","forms":["genetics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遺傳構成","explanation":"指某個個體或物種從親代繼承而來的整體遺傳特徵和遺傳資訊，也就是它那套“生物說明書”。","examples":[{"en":"Her genetics may make her more likely to develop the condition.","zh":"她的遺傳構成可能使她更容易患上這種疾病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their similar appearance reflects their shared genetics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genetics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ed142d60c4571b67f14","word":"genius","forms":["genius"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-348c134bb8644e20","term":"genius","forms":["genius","geniuses","genii"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天才人物","explanation":"指智力、技能或創造力遠超常人的人，尤其是已經透過科學、音樂、藝術等原創成果證明自己的人。這個人就是點亮某個領域的“天才火花”。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone recognized her as a musical genius.","zh":"大家都承認她是音樂天才。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young genius designed a safer bridge.","zh":"那位年輕天才設計了一座更安全的橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genius","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecb567da7d35dfd3","term":"genius","forms":["genius","geniuses","genii"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天才般的創意或靈感","explanation":"指突然產生的非凡創意、靈感或創造過程，強調作品或想法中閃現的那一點天才火花。","examples":[{"en":"The sculpture is a work of genius.","zh":"這座雕塑是天才般的作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adding wheels to the base was a stroke of genius.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genius","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4856d20b49bcdfe182b9","word":"genre","forms":["genre"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a02e356037ac6757","term":"genre","forms":["genre","genres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"型別；體裁","explanation":"genre 是給文學、電影、音樂或繪畫貼上的“型別標籤”，用來說明作品屬於哪一類、遵循哪種常見風格或表達方式。","examples":[{"en":"Science fiction is my favorite genre of film.","zh":"科幻片是我最喜歡的電影型別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The still life is an important genre in painting.","zh":"靜物畫是繪畫中的一種重要體裁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genre","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dca13388cd38b5da22c8","word":"gentle","forms":["gentle"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-541a4948932d39d4","term":"gentle","forms":["gentle","gentler","more gentle","gentlest","most gentle"],"pos":"adj","zh":"性情溫和體貼","explanation":"形容人的性情溫和、友善、體貼，不會故意傷害或粗暴對待別人。這是 gentle 最重要的核心義之一。","examples":[{"en":"Stuart is a gentle man; he would never hurt you.","zh":"斯圖爾特是個溫和的人，他絕不會傷害你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gentle nurse reassured the frightened child.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98eb374ac669f627","term":"gentle","forms":["gentle","gentler","more gentle","gentlest","most gentle"],"pos":"adj","zh":"輕柔而不強烈","explanation":"形容觸碰、動作或感覺柔和輕緩，不堅硬、不猛烈，也不會給人明顯的不適或衝擊。它和“溫和的性情”共享同一個核心：不施加太大力量。","examples":[{"en":"I felt something touch my shoulder; it was gentle and a little slimy.","zh":"我感覺有什麼東西碰了碰我的肩膀，動作很輕柔，還有點滑膩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A gentle massage eased the tension in her shoulders.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-617c062d7b882381c7b4","word":"gentleman","forms":["gentleman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa16fdce754238a0","term":"gentleman","forms":["gentleman","gentlemen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有教養的男子；紳士","explanation":"指舉止有禮、待人得體，或給人溫和迷人印象的男子。這裡的重點是行為和氣質上的“體面”，不一定表示貴族身份。","examples":[{"en":"He was a perfect gentleman throughout the dinner.","zh":"整個晚餐期間，他都表現得彬彬有禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A gentleman always treats others with respect.","zh":"有教養的人總是尊重他人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentleman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b3f7ed94a79563a","term":"gentleman","forms":["gentleman","gentlemen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先生；這位男士","explanation":"在禮貌或較正式的場合，gentleman可以泛指一名男子，不特別強調他的性格，只是讓稱呼聽起來客氣。","examples":[{"en":"Could you ask that gentleman to wait outside?","zh":"您能請那位先生在外面等候嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would this gentleman like a seat near the window?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentleman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dfec22473777f0ddaea9","word":"genuine","forms":["genuine"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0dc114627a95a19e","term":"genuine","forms":["genuine","more genuine","most genuine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真的；正品的；真誠的","explanation":"指東西不是仿造、偽造或摻假的；用於人的感情、友誼或態度時，則表示發自內心，不是為了做樣子。","examples":[{"en":"She showed genuine concern for the injured dog.","zh":"她真心關心那隻受傷的狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop guarantees that every watch is genuine.","zh":"這家商店保證每塊手錶都是正品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genuine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e91354ec09771c141a3f","word":"geographical","forms":["geographical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd7109c3259f920b","term":"geographical","forms":["geographical","more geographical","most geographical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"地理上的","explanation":"指與地理學、地區、邊界或地理位置有關的事物。它把注意力放在“地圖上的位置和範圍”上，而不一定涉及具體的地貌知識。","examples":[{"en":"The report compares geographical differences in access to healthcare.","zh":"這份報告比較了不同地區在醫療服務獲取方面的差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river forms a natural geographical boundary.","zh":"這條河構成了一條天然的地理邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geographical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf8e5ca0b2d5abd3393e","word":"geography","forms":["geography"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19d9e62829f4383a","term":"geography","forms":["geography","geographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地理學","explanation":"研究地球的自然特徵、各地的人類活動，以及人和環境如何相互影響的學科。它既可以指學校裡的地理課程，也可以指正式的學術領域。","examples":[{"en":"Geography was my favorite subject at school.","zh":"地理是我上學時最喜歡的科目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is studying geography at university.","zh":"她正在大學裡學習地理學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a78ecb0ede0e676e","term":"geography","forms":["geography","geographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某地的地形環境","explanation":"指一個地區的山地、平原、河流等自然條件，以及這些條件對交通、居住或發展的影響。這裡的 geography 不是學科，而是“這片地方是什麼樣”。","examples":[{"en":"The geography of the island makes travel difficult.","zh":"這座島的地形使出行很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The region's mountainous geography makes road construction difficult.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8148b7fefaf89ebf8e79","word":"geometry","forms":["geometry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eacae086a83289a0","term":"geometry","forms":["geometry","geometries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幾何學","explanation":"指研究空間關係的數學分支，包括形狀、大小、角度、距離、位置等內容。這是 geometry 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She is studying geometry this semester.","zh":"她這學期正在學習幾何學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Geometry helps us understand the properties of shapes.","zh":"幾何學幫助我們理解各種圖形的性質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geometry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70000f6cf17a58fa","term":"geometry","forms":["geometry","geometries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幾何體系","explanation":"指建立在一組特定公理或規則上的幾何系統。它仍然研究空間關係，但採用的基本規則可以不同，因此可以有不同的幾何體系。","examples":[{"en":"The course introduces several different geometries.","zh":"這門課介紹幾種不同的幾何體系。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In spherical geometry, a triangle can have three right angles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geometry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff3663688727bbb077e6","word":"germ","forms":["germ"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f9ced5d2c54571c","term":"germ","forms":["germ","germs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"萌芽；胚種","explanation":"指一個新生命開始發育時最早的那一小團細胞，也可泛指種子、芽、孢子或受精卵等具有生長潛力的起點。它就像一顆藏著未來生命的“小種子”。","examples":[{"en":"The germ develops into a new plant under the right conditions.","zh":"在適宜的條件下，這個胚種會發育成一株新植物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tiny germ is already growing inside the seed.","zh":"種子裡面已經有一個微小的胚芽在生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/germ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9d6f67030e36a6e","term":"germ","forms":["germ","germs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"病菌；病原微生物","explanation":"指能引起疾病的微生物，例如某些細菌或病毒。這裡仍然保留“會在某處生長、擴散的起點”這一種子般的形象，只是它會在人體或環境中造成感染。","examples":[{"en":"Wash your hands often to keep germs from spreading.","zh":"要經常洗手，防止病菌傳播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor thinks a germ caused the infection.","zh":"醫生認為是某種病菌引起了感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/germ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6b1243a8947f257da1a0","word":"gesture","forms":["gesture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-371d89340961c83a","term":"gesture","forms":["gesture","gestures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體手勢","explanation":"指手、頭或身體其他部位做出的動作，常用來加強說話內容、表達情緒或傳遞不用語言說出的資訊。","examples":[{"en":"She made a small gesture with her hand to emphasize the last point.","zh":"她用手做了個小手勢來強調最後一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He waved in a friendly gesture as the train pulled away.","zh":"火車開走時，他友好地揮了揮手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gesture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-734e9a279af6206f","term":"gesture","forms":["gesture","gestures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表示態度的舉動","explanation":"指一個具體的行為或話語，用來表示某種態度、情感或禮節，即使它本身未必能解決實際問題。比如送花可以是同情或慰問的表示。","examples":[{"en":"The flowers were a thoughtful gesture of sympathy.","zh":"這些花是體貼的慰問表示。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He offered to pay for the broken window as a gesture of goodwill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gesture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-295dd9dba52b2caf","term":"gesture","forms":["gesture","gestures","gesturing","gestured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做手勢","explanation":"指用手、頭或身體做出動作，通常是在說話時加強表達，或不用語言傳遞資訊。","examples":[{"en":"She tends to gesture with both hands when explaining an idea.","zh":"她解釋想法時常常會用雙手做手勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't gesture at people while you're angry.","zh":"生氣時請不要對著別人做手勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gesture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2998b3232d29e8dc5a78","word":"get","forms":["get"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30c40d1219e3bb51","term":"get","forms":["get","gets","getting","got","gat","gotten","getten","gettest","gottest","gattest","getteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"得到；獲得","explanation":"把某樣東西帶到自己這裡，強調取得或獲得它，通常不說明它原來是否已經答應給你。","examples":[{"en":"I need to get a new phone before my trip.","zh":"我得在旅行前買一部新手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She got a place at the university she wanted.","zh":"她被自己心儀的大學錄取了一個名額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/get","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6096d61744245d82","term":"get","forms":["get","gets","getting","got","gat","gotten","getten","gettest","gottest","gattest","getteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收到；接收","explanation":"東西、訊息或禮物從別人那裡到了自己這裡，重點是“接到”或“收到”。","examples":[{"en":"I got a message from my sister this morning.","zh":"我今天早上收到了姐姐發來的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He got a gift from his neighbors.","zh":"他收到了鄰居送的禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/get","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ada964d6a4f1ce32","term":"get","forms":["get","gets","getting","got","gat","gotten","getten","gettest","gottest","gattest","getteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得；開始處於","explanation":"某種狀態到了自己身上，因此表示逐漸變成某種狀態或開始有某種感受。","examples":[{"en":"I get nervous before big meetings.","zh":"大型會議前我會緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It gets dark very early in winter.","zh":"冬天很早天就黑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/get","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4524f59cd611558e","term":"get","forms":["get","gets","getting","got","gat","gotten","getten","gettest","gottest","gattest","getteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"理解；明白","explanation":"意思進入腦中，因此表示聽懂、看懂或明白某人的意圖。","examples":[{"en":"I don't get this question.","zh":"我不明白這道題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Oh, now I get what you mean.","zh":"哦，我現在明白你的意思了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/get","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ead6ef03d61ee60c533d","word":"ghost","forms":["ghost"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc9017e937c087e9","term":"ghost","forms":["ghost","ghosts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幽靈；鬼魂","explanation":"指死者留下的靈魂，或被認為死後仍出現的靈體；這是“人留下幽靈般痕跡”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"They said a ghost appeared in the old house.","zh":"他們說那座老房子裡出現了一個幽靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt as if her grandmother’s ghost were watching over her.","zh":"她覺得祖母的靈魂彷彿在守護著她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06c59a27083f0821","term":"ghost","forms":["ghost","ghosts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"模糊的影像；淡淡的輪廓","explanation":"指某物留下的若有若無的影像、輪廓或相似痕跡，像幽靈一樣不清晰、不實在。","examples":[{"en":"A ghost of a smile appeared on his face.","zh":"他的臉上浮現出一絲若有若無的笑意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hills were only a ghost through the morning fog.","zh":"晨霧中，山巒只剩下模糊的輪廓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b132ea2f6cd37dd630d","word":"giant","forms":["giant"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb0adf2aa7206ad3","term":"giant","forms":["giant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非常大的","explanation":"表示某人、動物、植物或物體的大小遠遠超過通常水平，是“巨人”這一核心形象在形容詞上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"A giant wave crashed over the small fishing boat.","zh":"一個巨大的海浪打過了那艘小漁船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They found a giant mushroom under the old oak tree.","zh":"他們在那棵老橡樹下發現了一朵巨大的蘑菇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/giant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ad72306e2b564ff","term":"giant","forms":["giant","giants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神話中的巨人","explanation":"指神話、傳說或幻想故事中身材極其高大的類人存在，是“巨大的人”這一核心形象最直接的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"In the old legend, a giant guarded the bridge to the castle.","zh":"在那個古老傳說中，一個巨人守護著通往城堡的橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children read a story about giants living in the mountains.","zh":"孩子們讀了一個關於住在山裡的巨人的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/giant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5394f5a4da7edd61","term":"giant","forms":["giant","giants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大型組織；行業巨頭","explanation":"指規模、市場影響力或資源遠超一般競爭者的大型公司或組織，是“巨大”從物理尺寸向社會規模的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The online retail giant opened a new warehouse near the airport.","zh":"這家網路零售巨頭在機場附近開設了一座新倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several technology giants are competing to develop better batteries.","zh":"幾家科技巨頭正在競爭開發更好的電池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/giant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1954b15a7459a2f7f6c","word":"gift","forms":["gift"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ed45bb9e3a86c4b","term":"gift","forms":["gift","gifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禮物；贈品","explanation":"指自願送給別人、通常不要求對方付款的東西，可以是生日禮物、捐贈物或其他贈品。這是 gift 最直接、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I bought my sister a small gift for her birthday.","zh":"我給姐姐買了一件小小的生日禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum received a gift of several old maps.","zh":"博物館收到了一批舊地圖的捐贈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb2e61cb73428707","term":"gift","forms":["gift","gifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天賦；才能","explanation":"指一個人天生或很早就表現出來的特殊才能，彷彿不是自己掙來的，而是得到的一份禮物。","examples":[{"en":"Mina has a gift for explaining difficult ideas clearly.","zh":"米娜很有把難懂的想法講清楚的天賦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a gift for remembering unfamiliar names.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dbdc7bf49b2282178cab","word":"gifted","forms":["gifted"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2118d9f566140235","term":"gifted","forms":["gifted","more gifted","most gifted"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有天賦的；才華出眾的","explanation":"指某人在某一方面天生或明顯特別擅長，能力超過一般水平，例如藝術、音樂、寫作或學術。重點是“能力特別突出”，不侷限於智力。","examples":[{"en":"She is a gifted artist who can capture a person’s character in a few lines.","zh":"她是一位很有天賦的藝術家，幾筆就能畫出一個人的特點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our gifted math teacher made difficult ideas feel simple.","zh":"我們那位很有才華的數學老師把難懂的概念講得很簡單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gifted","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9a1905d513825b7","term":"gifted","forms":["gifted","more gifted","most gifted"],"pos":"adj","zh":"資優的；具有超常認知能力的","explanation":"在心理學和教育語境中，指一個人的資訊處理、學習、記憶或推理能力明顯超過大多數人，因此能更快理解概念並建立複雜聯絡。這是“有天賦”在認知能力方面的更專門用法。","examples":[{"en":"The school offers a separate program for gifted students who need more challenging work.","zh":"這所學校為需要更有挑戰性作業的資優學生開設了專門課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gifted child taught herself algebra at eight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gifted","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de917bf06f5843e21554","word":"gigantic","forms":["gigantic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b2da97f78b1e4ff","term":"gigantic","forms":["gigantic","more gigantic","most gigantic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巨大得驚人","explanation":"指大小、數量、規模或程度遠遠超過通常水平，彷彿大到需要用“巨人”來作比較。它既可以描述具體物體，也可以描述任務、費用、差距等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"They built a gigantic stadium on the edge of the city.","zh":"他們在城市邊緣建了一座規模巨大的體育場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project faces a gigantic financial problem.","zh":"這個專案面臨著一個巨大的財務問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gigantic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c50a11249e1b221eed96","word":"giggle","forms":["giggle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-511de518fc102b8d","term":"giggle","forms":["giggle","giggles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咯咯笑聲","explanation":"指輕聲、細碎、略顯傻氣或淘氣的笑聲，常出現在人害羞、緊張或覺得好玩時。它不是單純的笑，而是帶有一種忍不住發出的輕快聲音。","examples":[{"en":"A few giggles came from the back of the room.","zh":"教室後面傳來幾聲咯咯的笑聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tried to hide her giggle behind her hand.","zh":"她試圖用手捂住自己的咯咯笑聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/giggle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a98c559a285423f","term":"giggle","forms":["giggle","giggles","giggling","giggled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"咯咯地笑","explanation":"指發出細碎、輕快的笑聲，常帶有玩鬧、害羞或緊張的意味。這個動作義和名詞義的“咯咯笑聲”直接相連：人發出這種笑聲，就是 giggle。","examples":[{"en":"The children giggled when the magician pulled out the silly hat.","zh":"魔術師拿出那頂滑稽的帽子時，孩子們咯咯地笑了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He giggled nervously before answering the question.","zh":"他回答問題前緊張地咯咯笑了幾聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/giggle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08ddff4ebe39249a9208","word":"ginger","forms":["ginger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70ccf0e22e9503a3","term":"ginger","forms":["ginger","gingers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"姜；姜根","explanation":"指姜科植物的辛辣芳香根莖，常用作調味料或飲品原料。","examples":[{"en":"Add some fresh ginger to the soup.","zh":"往湯里加一些鮮姜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I grated ginger into the tea.","zh":"我把姜磨碎後放進茶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ginger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bb7e067447139b18f60","word":"giraffe","forms":["giraffe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-124de603d3ddfa9a","term":"giraffe","forms":["giraffe","giraffes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長頸鹿","explanation":"一種生活在非洲草原上的大型反芻動物，以異常長的脖子和腿、帶斑紋的皮毛以及頭頂的小角狀突起為特徵，是現存最高的陸生動物。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a giraffe reaching for leaves above the trees.","zh":"我們看見一隻長頸鹿伸長脖子去夠樹頂上方的葉子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were excited when the giraffes came close to the fence.","zh":"長頸鹿走近圍欄時，孩子們都很興奮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/giraffe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-431ba1c6936744f65928","word":"girl","forms":["girl"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-47e55f051129df91","term":"girl","forms":["girl","girls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女孩","explanation":"指女性兒童，是“girl”最基本、最安全的用法，通常對應還沒有成年的女孩。","examples":[{"en":"A little girl was drawing pictures by the window.","zh":"一個小女孩正在窗邊畫畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The girls played together after school.","zh":"女孩們放學後一起玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/girl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e4e913def547bed","term":"girl","forms":["girl","girls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"年輕女性","explanation":"在非正式語境中可指年輕女性，尤其是說話者覺得年輕、有吸引力或與自己關係較近的女性；對成年女性使用時可能帶有輕浮或居高臨下的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"He met a girl from his office for coffee after work.","zh":"他下班後和辦公室裡的一位年輕女同事喝了咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The girl at reception showed us upstairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/girl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0895a532e404a5c9ea96","word":"give","forms":["give"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b734a9b24a32bca","term":"give","forms":["give","gives","giving","gave","given","givest","gavest","giveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給予；提供","explanation":"表示把具體物品、抽象事物或幫助遞給某人、某處或某個物件，是 give 最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a useful piece of advice.","zh":"她給了我一條有用的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please give the keys to David.","zh":"請把鑰匙給大衛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-79a7026834332227","term":"give","forms":["give","gives","giving","gave","given","givest","gavest","giveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在壓力下鬆動；塌陷","explanation":"這裡是“向壓力讓開”的 give：柱子、地面或其他結構承受不住時發生彎曲、鬆動或坍塌。","examples":[{"en":"The old wooden floor gave under his weight.","zh":"那塊舊木地板承受不住他的體重，塌了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rusty bolt finally gave with a sharp crack.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29f0274900445b32","term":"give","forms":["give","gives","giving","gave","given","givest","gavest","giveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發表；宣佈","explanation":"表示把訊息、意見、決定、判斷或聲音公開遞出，讓別人聽到或知道。","examples":[{"en":"The judge gave his decision after a short break.","zh":"法官短暫休庭後宣佈了決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The professor will give a lecture after lunch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9149a4a2c2c78eacd782","word":"glacier","forms":["glacier"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b4384a9bdbb2a7b","term":"glacier","forms":["glacier","glaciers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冰川","explanation":"指由大量冰雪形成、在自身重量作用下通常緩慢向下流動的巨大冰體。它像一條非常慢的冰河，會改變山谷地貌，也可能因氣候變暖而融化。","examples":[{"en":"The glacier is retreating faster than scientists expected.","zh":"這座冰川退縮的速度比科學家預期的更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Meltwater from the glacier feeds the river in summer.","zh":"這座冰川融化形成的水在夏季匯入河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glacier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6aa1595f76142b8020e","word":"glad","forms":["glad"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0dc82b0dbd775ab8","term":"glad","forms":["glad","gladder","more glad","gladdest","most glad"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高興的；欣慰的","explanation":"表示因為某個結果、訊息或可能發生的事情而感到高興、放心或慶幸。它常把“心裡亮起來”的感覺和具體原因連線起來。","examples":[{"en":"I'm glad you found your keys.","zh":"我很高興你找到了鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was glad to hear that everyone was safe.","zh":"聽說大家都平安，她感到很欣慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-525ec4aec327df9d022c","word":"glamorous","forms":["glamorous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1a9439d0bf3b428","term":"glamorous","forms":["glamorous","more glamorous","most glamorous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迷人時髦的；有光彩的","explanation":"指某人、某地、某種工作或生活方式看起來特別有吸引力、時髦而令人嚮往，彷彿被聚光燈照亮。它強調整體印象，不只是在說價格高或物質奢華。","examples":[{"en":"She dreamed of a glamorous life in Paris.","zh":"她夢想在巴黎過一種迷人而時髦的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel looked glamorous in the evening light.","zh":"這家酒店在暮色中顯得格外迷人而有光彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glamorous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec7922138fb98dc571cc","word":"glamour","forms":["glamour"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7faeecf59aedff3","term":"glamour","forms":["glamour","glamours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"迷人的美貌；華麗魅力","explanation":"指讓人覺得美麗、華貴並受到吸引的外表或氣質，常常還帶有一定的性感和明星般的光彩。這是現代英語中最核心的含義之一。","examples":[{"en":"The actress brought old Hollywood glamour to the awards ceremony.","zh":"這位女演員把老派好萊塢的華麗魅力帶到了頒獎典禮上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The magazine is known for its glamour and fashion photography.","zh":"這本雜誌以華麗風格和時尚攝影而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glamour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d6de90c3520710d","term":"glamour","forms":["glamour","glamours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸引力；令人嚮往的光彩","explanation":"指某個人、地方、職業或事物讓人覺得有趣、刺激或值得嚮往的特質，不一定只來自外貌。比如電影明星生活的 glamour，就是這種生活方式在人們心中的迷人光彩。","examples":[{"en":"After years on the road, she no longer saw any glamour in touring.","zh":"在路上奔波多年後，她已經不再覺得巡演有什麼吸引力了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glamour of overseas travel fascinated her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glamour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e776a070909341e9f27f","word":"glance","forms":["glance"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c171b7254ceff7c5","term":"glance","forms":["glance","glances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一瞥；看一眼","explanation":"短暫而不仔細地看一下，重點是動作很快，通常沒有深入觀察。","examples":[{"en":"I took a quick glance at the clock.","zh":"我迅速看了一眼時鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At a glance, the report looks complete.","zh":"乍一看，這份報告似乎很完整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0010c2d05c0e79fa","term":"glance","forms":["glance","glances","glancing","glanced","glancest","glancedst","glanceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉眼看向","explanation":"把視線迅速轉向某個物件，強調視線方向的改變，通常動作很短。","examples":[{"en":"She glanced at the door when she heard a noise.","zh":"聽到聲音時，她迅速朝門看了一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He glanced toward the clock above the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5881c7165048c42","term":"glance","forms":["glance","glances","glancing","glanced","glancest","glancedst","glanceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"快速瀏覽；看一眼","explanation":"快速看某物，通常只獲取大致資訊而不仔細研究；這是日常使用中最重要的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Could you glance over my email before I send it?","zh":"我發郵件前，你能幫我快速看一下嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He glanced at the menu and ordered soup.","zh":"他看了一眼選單，就點了湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf3ed277bc4b4c22","term":"glance","forms":["glance","glances","glancing","glanced","glancest","glancedst","glanceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"瞥一眼","explanation":"快速地看某人或某物一下，是最常見、最值得優先掌握的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I glanced at my phone during the meeting.","zh":"開會時我瞥了一眼手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She glanced at him and smiled.","zh":"她瞥了他一眼，笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28574c1e4364eea84190","word":"glare","forms":["glare"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10f2c6d093592ff8","term":"glare","forms":["glare","glares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刺眼的強光","explanation":"指強烈、耀眼到使人難以直視的光，常由金屬、太陽或其他明亮表面反射出來。","examples":[{"en":"The glare from the wet road made it hard to see.","zh":"溼路面反射的強光讓人很難看清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We lowered the blinds against the afternoon glare.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6714abd6936e5518","term":"glare","forms":["glare","glares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"怒視","explanation":"指帶著憤怒、敵意或威嚇意味的盯視，好像目光本身在逼迫對方。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a sharp glare when I interrupted.","zh":"我打斷她時，她狠狠地瞪了我一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her glare silenced the whispering students.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59d4e9e7e74668d4","term":"glare","forms":["glare","glares","glaring","glared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"怒視，瞪著","explanation":"帶著憤怒或敵意盯著某人看，目光像強光一樣具有壓迫感。","examples":[{"en":"The coach glared at the players who arrived late.","zh":"教練怒視著那些遲到的隊員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He glared at the stranger blocking his driveway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-132a1a391cce181c490a","word":"glass","forms":["glass"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2a056dda521b3a6","term":"glass","forms":["glass","glasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玻璃材料","explanation":"glass 最基本的意思是玻璃：一種通常透明、由熔化的砂和其他材料製成的非晶體固體。","examples":[{"en":"The tabletop is made of glass.","zh":"這張桌面是玻璃做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Recycled glass gives these green bottles their uneven texture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0adcadfc6394111","term":"glass","forms":["glass","glasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玻璃杯；杯子","explanation":"glass 也指用玻璃、塑膠等製成的飲水容器，即一個玻璃杯或類似的杯子。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have a glass of water?","zh":"可以給我一杯水嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She left her glass on the kitchen table.","zh":"她把杯子落在廚房桌上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-266550babbb7bd394ab6","word":"glasses","forms":["glasses"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-427c9ac814ccd084","term":"glasses","forms":["glasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眼鏡","explanation":"戴在眼睛前面的鏡片和鏡架，用來幫助看清東西。它通常以複數形式出現，即使說的是一副眼鏡。","examples":[{"en":"I can't read the menu without my glasses.","zh":"沒有眼鏡我看不清選單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She left her glasses on the bedside table.","zh":"她把眼鏡落在床頭櫃上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glasses","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d25d5ca9b02d480","term":"glasses","forms":["glasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雙筒望遠鏡","explanation":"拿在手裡、用來觀察遠處物體的雙筒望遠鏡；它和眼鏡一樣，都是藉助鏡片改善視線，只是使用距離不同。","examples":[{"en":"We used the glasses to watch the birds on the far shore.","zh":"我們用雙筒望遠鏡觀察遠岸的鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Through the glasses, we could see birds on the distant cliff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glasses","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-027dcc20c7ede0fca28a","word":"gleam","forms":["gleam"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-456aaeba399b0e68","term":"gleam","forms":["gleam","gleams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一絲微光；閃光","explanation":"指短暫、微弱或不太清楚的一點光，常像光線在黑暗中或物體表面閃了一下。","examples":[{"en":"A gleam of sunlight slipped through the curtains.","zh":"一縷陽光從窗簾縫裡透了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A gleam of sunlight crossed the polished floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gleam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1d06bb7163f09d8","term":"gleam","forms":["gleam","gleams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一線跡象；一點希望","explanation":"指某件事隱約顯露出的跡象或希望，就像黑暗中剛剛看見的一點光。","examples":[{"en":"The first test results offered a gleam of hope.","zh":"第一次測試結果帶來了一線希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unexpected donation offered a gleam of hope.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gleam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32c7abcabf31a1aa","term":"gleam","forms":["gleam","gleams","gleaming","gleamed","gleamest","gleamedst","gleameth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閃耀；閃閃發光","explanation":"指物體發出微弱、間歇或不穩定的光，像光線短暫地從表面閃出來。","examples":[{"en":"The wet stones gleamed in the morning sun.","zh":"溼漉漉的石頭在晨光中閃閃發亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Raindrops gleamed on the spiderweb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gleam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e97c382099fe40dd562b","word":"glide","forms":["glide"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e119e2dd47154fb5","term":"glide","forms":["glide","glides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑行；平穩移動","explanation":"glide 作名詞時可以指平穩、輕柔地滑行這一動作，重點是移動過程順暢而幾乎不費力。","examples":[{"en":"The swan crossed the lake in a graceful glide.","zh":"天鵝優雅地滑過湖面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The skater ended with a long backward glide.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a2ebae7da6ea3e9","term":"glide","forms":["glide","glides","gliding","glided","glid","glode","glidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"平穩滑行","explanation":"glide 作動詞時，表示人、動物、車輛或物體平穩而輕柔地移動，彷彿沒有受到明顯阻力。","examples":[{"en":"The boat glided quietly across the calm water.","zh":"小船安靜地滑過平靜的水面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She glided across the room to greet her guests.","zh":"她輕盈地走過房間去迎接客人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62c4ea25a12240685372","word":"glimpse","forms":["glimpse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f9bd6e752fbf0a3","term":"glimpse","forms":["glimpse","glimpses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短暫的一瞥","explanation":"指很快、很不完整地看到某人或某物，只獲得片段資訊，就像從門縫裡看了一眼。","examples":[{"en":"I caught a glimpse of the singer as she left the building.","zh":"歌手離開大樓時，我瞥見了她一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary gives us a glimpse of life in the village.","zh":"這部紀錄片讓我們一窺村裡的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glimpse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44f728206c74d05e","term":"glimpse","forms":["glimpse","glimpses","glimpsing","glimpsed","glimpsest","glimpsedst","glimpseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"短暫瞥見","explanation":"指快速而不完整地看見某人或某個具體事物，只掌握到一部分外觀或資訊。","examples":[{"en":"I glimpsed a deer between the trees.","zh":"我從樹縫間瞥見了一隻鹿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She glimpsed her friend in the crowd but lost sight of him.","zh":"她在人群中瞥見了朋友，但很快又看不見他了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glimpse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-209d0f47fedd5133","term":"glimpse","forms":["glimpse","glimpses","glimpsing","glimpsed","glimpsest","glimpsedst","glimpseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"初步瞭解到","explanation":"指對抽象事物短暫而片面地有所認識，好像只從門縫裡看到了問題的一角。","examples":[{"en":"We are beginning to glimpse the scale of the challenge.","zh":"我們開始初步瞭解到這項挑戰的規模。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Through her letters, we glimpse the pressures of royal life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glimpse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce2bf1f4ddd4bda4885b","word":"glitter","forms":["glitter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e8e437e45bb2808","term":"glitter","forms":["glitter","glitters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"閃耀的光澤","explanation":"指光線以斷續、跳動的方式反射出來，形成明亮的閃光或光澤；可以是金屬、珠寶、水面等發出的光。","examples":[{"en":"The glitter of sunlight danced on the surface of the lake.","zh":"陽光的閃光在湖面上跳動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw the glitter of gold in the display case.","zh":"我們看見展櫃裡黃金閃耀的光澤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glitter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e636786cea506d30","term":"glitter","forms":["glitter","glitters","glittering","glittered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閃耀；閃閃發光","explanation":"指某物反射出斷續、跳動的明亮光線，正是“碎光在表面上跳動”這個核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The wet leaves glittered in the morning sun.","zh":"溼樹葉在晨光中閃閃發亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A glittering sword hung above the fireplace.","zh":"壁爐上方掛著一把閃閃發光的劍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glitter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8001c27439650c5c5a6b","word":"global","forms":["global"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4948732715754e3f","term":"global","forms":["global","more global","most global"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全球的","explanation":"指涉及世界各地、面向整個世界，而不是只限於一個國家或地區。它保留了“覆蓋整個地球”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Climate change is a global problem.","zh":"氣候變化是一個全球性問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is building a global network.","zh":"這家公司正在建立一個全球網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/global","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-452675a5e7835d6c","term":"global","forms":["global","more global","most global"],"pos":"adj","zh":"整體的；全域性的","explanation":"指涉及某個事物的全部，而不是其中一個區域性；因此可以不涉及世界，只表示“整個系統或整體範圍”。","examples":[{"en":"We need a global solution, not a temporary fix.","zh":"我們需要整體性的解決方案，而不是臨時修補。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The review takes a global view of the entire project.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/global","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2a1fc043243f36ba9b7","word":"globe","forms":["globe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b23e004e58e5af72","term":"globe","forms":["globe","globes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球形物體","explanation":"指任何呈球形或接近球形的物體。它抓住了這個詞最基本的“完整的球”形象，眼球、燈罩等也可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"The globe of the eye is protected by the eyelids.","zh":"眼球受到眼瞼的保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A glass globe covered the old lamp.","zh":"一隻玻璃燈罩罩住了那盞舊燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/globe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f87478aabe4bcd28","term":"globe","forms":["globe","globes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地球","explanation":"指我們居住的整個地球，把地球看作一個漂浮在宇宙中的球體。這裡強調的是行星本身，而不是桌上的模型。","examples":[{"en":"The story was reported across the globe.","zh":"這則報道傳遍了全世界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Satellite signals can travel around the globe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/globe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42fd50a8a1ef753a","term":"globe","forms":["globe","globes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地球儀","explanation":"指按比例縮小、用來展示地球或其他行星的球形模型。它把“球形”這個核心形象變成了可以觀察和使用的模型。","examples":[{"en":"The children gathered around the globe to find Brazil.","zh":"孩子們圍在地球儀旁尋找巴西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a globe of Mars.","zh":"博物館裡有一個火星儀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/globe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-910ae8258000041a6ff4","word":"gloom","forms":["gloom"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2777076581accc16","term":"gloom","forms":["gloom","glooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"昏暗；幽暗","explanation":"指光線很弱、視野不清的狀態，像一層陰影籠罩著地方。它可以指森林、房間或夜晚的實際黑暗。","examples":[{"en":"We could barely see the path in the gloom of the forest.","zh":"在森林的昏暗中，我們幾乎看不清小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room was filled with gloom after the curtains were closed.","zh":"窗簾拉上後，房間裡一片昏暗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gloom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cbbbca1f3c42bcb","term":"gloom","forms":["gloom","glooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰沉氣氛；悲觀情緒","explanation":"指一種籠罩環境或人群的壓抑、悲觀氣氛，好像昏暗的光線從四周壓下來。它常用於壞訊息、失敗或不確定局勢造成的整體低落感。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden job losses cast a gloom over the whole town.","zh":"突然出現的失業讓整個城鎮籠罩在陰沉的氣氛中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the gloomy news, the team refused to give up.","zh":"儘管訊息令人悲觀，這支隊伍還是不肯放棄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gloom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f695f6db85ce1d2a06c2","word":"gloomy","forms":["gloomy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f5480325df1df9c","term":"gloomy","forms":["gloomy","gloomier","gloomiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"昏暗而壓抑的","explanation":"指光線不足、顯得陰暗的地方或環境，通常還帶有令人不安、壓抑或可怕的感覺。它不只是說“看不清”，還暗示整體氣氛不明快。","examples":[{"en":"The old house felt gloomy even in the afternoon.","zh":"那座老房子即使在下午也讓人覺得陰暗壓抑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked through a gloomy tunnel with only one weak lamp.","zh":"我們走過一條昏暗的隧道，裡面只有一盞微弱的燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gloomy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d08c9f80df572e5","term":"gloomy","forms":["gloomy","gloomier","gloomiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"憂鬱悲觀的","explanation":"指人情緒低落、神情陰鬱，或對未來和結果持悲觀看法。這裡的“陰暗”從環境轉到了人的心情和想法上。","examples":[{"en":"She looked gloomy after hearing the disappointing news.","zh":"聽到令人失望的訊息後，她看起來很憂鬱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report gives a gloomy outlook for the economy.","zh":"這份報告對經濟前景持悲觀態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gloomy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8748cb435202bd382f34","word":"glorious","forms":["glorious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d6505e67a3b0940","term":"glorious","forms":["glorious","more glorious","gloriouser","most glorious","gloriousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"光榮的；值得讚頌的","explanation":"形容人、行為或成就具有值得讚美的品質，或者已經贏得了榮耀；核心畫面是被榮耀的光環照亮。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers were honored for their glorious deeds.","zh":"這些士兵因英勇而光榮的功績受到表彰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She led the team to a glorious victory.","zh":"她帶領團隊取得了光榮的勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glorious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19585868a4e3b8b2","term":"glorious","forms":["glorious","more glorious","gloriouser","most glorious","gloriousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極好的；令人愉快的","explanation":"表示某件事美好、成功或讓人非常享受，像是被榮耀的光環照亮，因此比普通的 good 更有感染力。","examples":[{"en":"We had a glorious afternoon by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個美妙的下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden looks glorious in spring.","zh":"這座花園在春天看起來美極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glorious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-409a14887e0958f1efcd","word":"glory","forms":["glory"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7b6c5db1f26c58c","term":"glory","forms":["glory","glories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壯麗；輝煌","explanation":"指景色、建築、音樂等極其美麗、宏偉、耀眼的狀態，彷彿發出奪目的光。","examples":[{"en":"We arrived just in time to see the mountain in all its glory.","zh":"我們及時趕到，看到了山脈最壯麗的景象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old theater has lost much of its former glory.","zh":"這座老劇院已經失去了許多昔日的輝煌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0aaec891b6a27b5d","term":"glory","forms":["glory","glories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"榮譽；聲望","explanation":"指一個人或事物因為傑出成就而得到公眾的尊敬、讚美和好名聲。","examples":[{"en":"The medal brought glory to the whole team.","zh":"這枚獎牌為整個團隊贏得了榮譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked hard, not for money or glory, but to help people.","zh":"她努力工作不是為了金錢或聲望，而是為了幫助別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e13571ffb2bbd21a","term":"glory","forms":["glory","glories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勝利；成功","explanation":"指透過比賽、競爭或努力取得勝利，從而獲得眾人注目的榮耀。","examples":[{"en":"The young striker scored the winning goal and grabbed the glory.","zh":"這名年輕前鋒打進位制勝球，贏得了勝利的榮光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After years of practice, she finally achieved Olympic glory.","zh":"經過多年的練習，她終於取得了奧運會的輝煌成就。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba18df1f84e06020794c","word":"glove(s)","forms":["glove"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bf478a983b0e4ba","term":"glove","forms":["glove","gloves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手套","explanation":"戴在手上、覆蓋全部或部分手指的衣物，通常讓各根手指能夠分別活動。這是 glove 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I wore gloves to keep my hands warm.","zh":"我戴了手套來保暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took off her gloves before washing the dishes.","zh":"她洗碗前摘下了手套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3ebdb431e13292a","term":"glove","forms":["glove","gloves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棒球手套","explanation":"棒球運動員用來接球的厚手套，通常比普通手套大得多，並有專門的兜。","examples":[{"en":"The young player brought his new glove to practice.","zh":"那名年輕球員帶著他的新棒球手套來訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The catcher held his glove above his shoulder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d27608cca9b65f91aef2","word":"glow","forms":["glow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8fc41762c6f8e618","term":"glow","forms":["glow","glows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"柔和的光","explanation":"指發光物體持續散出的光，常像火焰、燈或餘燼在暗處形成的一層柔和亮光。","examples":[{"en":"A warm glow came from the lamp by the window.","zh":"窗邊的燈發出溫暖的光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stove cast a warm glow across the kitchen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b90ce0803df5c7a5","term":"glow","forms":["glow","glows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內在的熱情","explanation":"指人因熱愛、興奮或強烈感情而顯出的溫暖熱烈狀態，彷彿心裡在發光發熱。","examples":[{"en":"She spoke about her students with a glow of pride.","zh":"她帶著自豪而熱烈的神情談起自己的學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The welcome rekindled a glow of affection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77575c393052da03","term":"glow","forms":["glow","glows","glowing","glowed","glew","glown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出柔光","explanation":"指火、燈或餘燼等像被加熱一樣持續發光，重點是光從物體內部透出。","examples":[{"en":"The embers were still glowing after midnight.","zh":"午夜過後，餘燼還在發著紅光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The embers glowed softly in the fireplace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99552de9998a2b8267df","word":"glue","forms":["glue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1533e3c0a2fb129","term":"glue","forms":["glue","glues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膠水；黏合劑","explanation":"指能把兩個表面粘在一起的黏性物質，通常是液體或半液體，幹後形成牢固的連線；日常也可泛指各種黏合劑。","examples":[{"en":"I used glue to fix the broken handle.","zh":"我用膠水把壞掉的把手粘好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let the glue dry before you move the box.","zh":"先讓膠水乾了，再移動箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c110c7a35f3fdfa6","term":"glue","forms":["glue","glues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紐帶；凝聚力","explanation":"把“粘在一起”的畫面引申到抽象關係上，指使兩個人、兩個團體或若干事物保持聯絡的共同因素或力量。","examples":[{"en":"Shared memories were the glue that held the family together.","zh":"共同的回憶是維繫這個家庭的紐帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their shared love of music was the glue holding them together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62a1cd054aa513cf","term":"glue","forms":["glue","glues","gluing","glueing","glued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用膠粘住","explanation":"表示用膠把一個物體連線或固定在另一個物體上，就是把“膠水”這個名詞變成實際的粘合動作。","examples":[{"en":"She glued the photo to the front of the card.","zh":"她把照片粘在卡片正面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need to glue the chair leg back into place.","zh":"我得把椅子腿粘回原來的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cd0e21a9a0795a14ec9","word":"go","forms":["go"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d24e08e79350c8f1","term":"go","forms":["go","goes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘗試","explanation":"指為完成某事而進行的一次嘗試；既然“去做”是向前推進，這個名詞就表示向目標推進的一次機會。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll give it a go after lunch.","zh":"午飯後我來試一試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Why don’t you have a go at fixing the lamp?","zh":"你為什麼不試著修修這盞燈？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7f84e70c5371e78","term":"go","forms":["go","goes","going","went","yode","gone","goest","wentest","goeth","-","goand"],"pos":"verb","zh":"去；移動","explanation":"表示人或物從當前位置向另一個地方移動，也可以泛指向前推進。這裡的“去”是整個詞義網路的起點。","examples":[{"en":"Why don't you go with us?","zh":"你為什麼不和我們一起去？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I usually go to work by bus.","zh":"我通常坐公交車去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1294b06892bf491","term":"go","forms":["go","goes","going","went","yode","gone","goest","wentest","goeth","-","goand"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開始","explanation":"表示某個動作、比賽或過程現在開始，像是發出“向前推進”的訊號。","examples":[{"en":"The timer has started—go!","zh":"計時器已經開始了——開始！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"When I say go, open the box.","zh":"我說“開始”時，開啟盒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0304523efff53f243d76","word":"goal","forms":["goal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6aef42f7f1bfde63","term":"goal","forms":["goal","goals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目標；目的","explanation":"指一個人或團體希望透過努力實現的結果，也就是自己想抵達的“終點”。可以是長期人生方向，也可以是一次具體任務的預期結果。","examples":[{"en":"Her goal is to become a doctor.","zh":"她的目標是成為一名醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We set a clear goal for the project.","zh":"我們為這個專案設定了明確的目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2d698d91acf24db","term":"goal","forms":["goal","goals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球門；終點區域","explanation":"在許多體育比賽中，指運動員試圖把球或其他物體送入的區域；它是比賽中的實際“終點”。在某些比賽中也可以指賽道或比賽要抵達的終點。","examples":[{"en":"The striker kicked the ball into the goal.","zh":"前鋒把球踢進了球門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ball rolled just wide of the goal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c224b5e99ac5e12c044","word":"goalkeeper","forms":["goalkeeper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05a2a1353d5c2d2a","term":"goalkeeper","forms":["goalkeeper","goalkeepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"守門員","explanation":"指站在本方球門前守門的球員，主要任務是撲擋或攔截對方的射門，防止對方得分。","examples":[{"en":"The goalkeeper made an excellent save in the final minute.","zh":"守門員在最後一分鐘完成了一次精彩撲救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their goalkeeper kept the score at 0–0.","zh":"他們的守門員讓比分保持在零比零。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goalkeeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5480f08f35968440ebe8","word":"goat","forms":["goat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d103183648c66f6f","term":"goat","forms":["goat","goats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"山羊","explanation":"指山羊這種有蹄類動物，是 goat 最基本、最容易和記憶影象連線的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A goat was standing on the wall.","zh":"一隻山羊正站在牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer keeps goats on the hillside.","zh":"農夫在山坡上養山羊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7e22e1776c2fa99","term":"goat","forms":["goat","goats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"史上最偉大者","explanation":"這是大寫縮寫 GOAT 的小寫替代形式，指某個領域中公認最偉大的人或事物，與普通動物 goat 沒有意義上的聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"Many fans call her the goat of tennis.","zh":"許多球迷稱她為網球史上最偉大的選手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans called her the GOAT after her fifth championship.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce42b647777efb89","term":"goat","forms":["goat","GOATs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"史上最偉大","explanation":"GOAT 是“史上最偉大”的首字母縮寫，用來稱讚某人在一個領域中達到最高水平。","examples":[{"en":"Messi is widely regarded as the GOAT of football.","zh":"梅西被廣泛認為是足球史上最偉大的球員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She may be the GOAT, but the debate is not over.","zh":"她也許是史上最偉大的選手，但爭論還沒有結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-974c95a7d9a84f49d7cc","word":"god/goddess","forms":["god","goddess"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9a353300340f929","term":"god","forms":["god","gods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神祇；至高神","explanation":"god指被認為擁有超自然力量、通常不死並受到崇拜的神祇，也可以指某個宗教中的至高神。這個普通名詞既可指一位神，也可泛指神這一類存在。","examples":[{"en":"The ancient temple was built for a sun god.","zh":"這座古老的神廟是為一位太陽神建造的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the story, the gods control the weather.","zh":"在這個故事裡，眾神控制著天氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/god","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4abbd26525484bf6","term":"goddess","forms":["goddess","goddesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女性神祇","explanation":"goddess 是具有神性、被人崇拜的女性神祇，與 god 相對。它可以指神話、宗教或幻想作品中的女性神明。","examples":[{"en":"The ancient people prayed to the goddess of the harvest.","zh":"古人向掌管豐收的女神祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the story, the goddess protects the village from the storm.","zh":"在這個故事中，女神保護村莊免受暴風雨侵襲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goddess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb9443e140c05caa","term":"goddess","forms":["goddess","goddesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女神般的女性","explanation":"比喻一個女性非常漂亮、迷人，或被人仰慕得像女神一樣；重點是她在別人眼中的魅力和受崇拜程度。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone at the party thought she looked like a goddess.","zh":"參加聚會的人都覺得她美得像女神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"To her devoted fans, the singer was a goddess.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goddess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24d7f03d8dc3c3666969","word":"gold","forms":["gold"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e8e8b75a5739b39","term":"gold","forms":["gold","golder","goldest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"金制的","explanation":"表示物品的材料是金子，例如金項鍊、金戒指等；重點是材質，而不是僅僅像金子的顏色。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a gold bracelet to the ceremony.","zh":"她戴著一隻金手鐲參加儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wore a gold wedding ring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ddfe956fa206614f","term":"gold","forms":["gold","golds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金；黃金","explanation":"指一種價值很高的黃色貴金屬，化學符號是 Au，原子序數為 79。這裡說的是材料本身，不是由它製成的一枚硬幣或一件首飾。","examples":[{"en":"Gold has been used to make jewelry for thousands of years.","zh":"幾千年來，人們一直用黃金製作首飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The price of gold rose sharply this month.","zh":"本月黃金價格大幅上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7d16a957c1fd8ca","term":"gold","forms":["gold","golds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極有價值的人或物","explanation":"比喻某人、某物或某件事像金子一樣有用、可靠或寶貴；這是從金子的高價值自然引申出的口語義。","examples":[{"en":"That old map was gold when we got lost in the mountains.","zh":"我們在山裡迷路時，那張舊地圖幫了大忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That patient receptionist is pure gold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd56de4137951d9c9268","word":"golden","forms":["golden"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2301c1bdcf0740a","term":"golden","forms":["golden","more golden","goldener","most golden","goldenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"金制的；與金有關的","explanation":"指由金子製成，或直接與金子有關的事物，是“金光”這一核心畫面的最字面用法。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a golden crown from the ancient kingdom.","zh":"博物館展出了一個古王國的金王冠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A golden bracelet glittered on her wrist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83686c2cc5800bbd","term":"golden","forms":["golden","more golden","goldener","most golden","goldenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"金色的；呈金黃色的","explanation":"指顏色像金子一樣明亮、溫暖或有光澤，例如陽光、頭髮和麥田的顏色。","examples":[{"en":"Golden light filled the room at sunset.","zh":"日落時的金色光線灑滿了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fields turned golden in late summer.","zh":"夏末，田野變成了一片金色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-808e2d9611ea3266","term":"golden","forms":["golden","more golden","goldener","most golden","goldenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"輝煌繁榮的","explanation":"由金子的珍貴和光輝引申，形容一個時期、社會或領域特別繁榮、富有創造力或成就突出。","examples":[{"en":"Many artists worked in the city during its golden era.","zh":"這座城市的黃金時期有許多藝術家在那裡創作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city entered a golden age of trade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-204258f45b3f1ffe","term":"golden","forms":["golden","more golden","goldener","most golden","goldenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極有利的；難得的","explanation":"形容機會、條件或建議非常好，值得把握，就像發現了一塊金子。","examples":[{"en":"This scholarship is a golden opportunity for young researchers.","zh":"這項獎學金對年輕研究人員來說是一個難得的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The internship offers a golden opportunity to learn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-625fe74cad4600b5e8b7","word":"golf","forms":["golf"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a55d7e5d6f68e9bd","term":"golf","forms":["golf"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高爾夫球運動","explanation":"一種用球杆擊球、設法用儘可能少的擊球次數把球打入一系列球洞的運動。日常說golf時，通常就是指這項運動，而不是某一個球洞或球杆。","examples":[{"en":"My parents play golf every Sunday.","zh":"我父母每個星期天都打高爾夫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took up golf after moving to the countryside.","zh":"她搬到鄉下後開始打高爾夫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a22f46d2ca542a38","term":"golf","forms":["golf","golfs","golfing","golfed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打高爾夫","explanation":"指進行高爾夫運動，也就是用球杆擊球、爭取用較少的擊球次數完成球洞。這裡強調的是人的活動，因此可以直接說某人golf。","examples":[{"en":"We often golf with our neighbors in the summer.","zh":"夏天我們經常和鄰居一起打高爾夫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They golf together on Sunday mornings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-770e607624d689265ca6","word":"good","forms":["good"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-faada458beb64c67","term":"good","forms":["good","better","gooder","best","goodest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"品德好；有益的","explanation":"表示一個人的意圖、行為或選擇符合道德標準，或者是在為他人和整體利益著想；也就是“符合期待、帶來好處”中的道德和正面價值。","examples":[{"en":"She had good intentions, even though the plan failed.","zh":"她的出發點是好的，雖然計劃失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is good to help people who are in trouble.","zh":"幫助有困難的人是有益且正確的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa1d9cfc86fe86ac","term":"good","forms":["good","better","gooder","best","goodest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有能力的；擅長的","explanation":"表示某人在某項活動、技能或工作上能力強、表現出色，符合對能力的期待。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is good at solving difficult puzzles.","zh":"我妹妹很擅長解決難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is a good swimmer and rarely gets tired.","zh":"他很會游泳，很少感到疲累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e530b5476b81e948","term":"good","forms":["good","better","best"],"pos":"adv","zh":"充分地；徹底地","explanation":"這裡的good不是“好的”這個形容詞，而是說某個動作做得足夠充分、徹底，達到了期待的效果。","examples":[{"en":"Please clean the corners good before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人到來前，請把角落徹底打掃乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hose soaked his shoes good and proper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72df19e3666d0fed","term":"good","forms":["good","goods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"好處；積極結果","explanation":"這裡的good指某件事帶來的具體好處或積極結果，也就是它如何讓人受益、讓情況變好。","examples":[{"en":"A short walk will do you good.","zh":"散散步對你有好處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy has done a lot of good for local families.","zh":"新政策給當地家庭帶來了許多好處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82e35a63ceba37e96464","word":"goodbye","forms":["goodbye"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4164428c683c8d20","term":"goodbye","forms":["goodbye","goodbyes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"告別","explanation":"goodbye 作名詞時，指分別這一行為，或分別時說出的“再見”這句話；重點從“說再見”轉成了“一次告別”。","examples":[{"en":"They said a quiet goodbye at the station.","zh":"他們在車站安靜地道了別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their goodbye lasted longer than expected.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goodbye","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-089857f9c407941715fa","word":"goods","forms":["goods"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd8074a3d6751dc2","term":"goods","forms":["goods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商品；貨品","explanation":"指生產出來、隨後被交易、購買並最終使用或消費的東西，是商業語境中最常見的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The company exports goods to several countries.","zh":"這家公司向多個國家出口商品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Goods are cheaper online than in the shop.","zh":"網上的商品比店裡的便宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goods","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29b29c3f20d52f09","term":"goods","forms":["goods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"真東西；關鍵資訊；真本事","explanation":"the goods 指真正重要、可靠或能揭示事實的東西，也可以指某人確實拿得出手的本事；它延續了“有價值、值得拿出來看”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter says she has the goods on the corrupt official.","zh":"那名記者說她掌握了這名腐敗官員的確鑿證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He looked nervous, but the new player has the goods.","zh":"他看起來很緊張，但這名新隊員確實有實力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goods","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-47b2d9943b23501cbe74","word":"goodwill","forms":["goodwill"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16b6dce8536ae285","term":"goodwill","forms":["goodwill","goodwills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"善意；友好支援","explanation":"指對某人、團體或事物抱有友好、支援和信任的態度。它可以來自個人，也可以來自公眾或客戶，是 goodwill 最基本的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The company offered a refund to preserve goodwill with its customers.","zh":"這家公司主動退款，以維護客戶對它的信任和支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her generous help earned the goodwill of the whole neighborhood.","zh":"她慷慨相助，贏得了整個社群的好感和支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goodwill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-299f0ea4d96d5ac8","term":"goodwill","forms":["goodwill","goodwills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商譽","explanation":"在會計和商業中，goodwill 是企業因品牌聲譽、客戶忠誠和良好關係等獲得的無形價值，不能直接歸入廠房、裝置等有形資產。它可以理解為企業長期積累的“信任餘額”。","examples":[{"en":"The buyer paid extra for the restaurant's established goodwill.","zh":"買方為這家餐館積累已久的商譽支付了額外費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The purchase price includes the business's established goodwill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goodwill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2d37dd0575766e4deed","word":"goose","forms":["goose"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b88481af3211b528","term":"goose","forms":["goose","geese"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鵝","explanation":"指鵝這種有羽毛和蹼、能飛、游泳並在陸地上行走的水鳥；既可以指一隻鵝，也可以泛指這種動物。","examples":[{"en":"There is a flock of geese on the pond.","zh":"池塘上有一群鵝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A goose followed us across the field.","zh":"一隻鵝跟著我們走過了田地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba62e103218be28b","term":"goose","forms":["goose","geese"],"pos":"noun","zh":"母鵝","explanation":"在嚴格區分公鵝和母鵝時，goose 專指母鵝；公鵝叫 gander。日常語境中，goose 也常泛指鵝，不一定強調性別。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer keeps one gander with three geese.","zh":"農夫養了一隻公鵝和三隻母鵝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The goose guarded her eggs while the gander watched nearby.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6c4fa47fc72bd2570e9","word":"gorgeous","forms":["gorgeous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc9445a37b724985","term":"gorgeous","forms":["gorgeous","more gorgeous","most gorgeous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其漂亮的","explanation":"表示美得令人驚豔，常形容人，也能形容風景、物品或外觀。這是這個詞最核心、最常用的意思，比普通的“漂亮”帶有更強的讚歎語氣。","examples":[{"en":"The lake looks gorgeous at sunset.","zh":"這座湖在日落時美得驚豔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You look absolutely gorgeous tonight.","zh":"你今晚漂亮極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gorgeous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7b73059712d0976","term":"gorgeous","forms":["gorgeous","more gorgeous","most gorgeous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"穿著華麗的","explanation":"形容一個人穿戴得非常講究、華麗，顯得醒目而有氣派。這是“華麗得讓人注意到”的具體表現，和後來表示“極其漂亮”的意思相連。","examples":[{"en":"She looked gorgeous in a long red dress.","zh":"她穿著一條紅色長裙，顯得華麗極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gorgeous courtiers wore embroidered robes and jewels.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gorgeous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-541f42d7542b70062fa4","word":"gorilla","forms":["gorilla"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd28ccfe1c8aede1","term":"gorilla","forms":["gorilla","gorillas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大猩猩","explanation":"一種生活在非洲中部森林中的大型類人猿，是現存體型最大的靈長類動物之一；“體型巨大、力量強”的形象構成了這個詞其他比喻義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a gorilla calmly eating leaves at the zoo.","zh":"我們看見一隻大猩猩在動物園裡平靜地吃樹葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gorillas usually avoid people when they can.","zh":"大猩猩通常會盡量避開人類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gorilla","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e173d15c406fac9e","term":"gorilla","forms":["gorilla","gorillas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"粗野兇悍的人","explanation":"把人比作大猩猩，突出其身材魁梧、舉止粗魯或具有威脅性，常常含有侮辱意味；重點不是單純說這個人強壯。","examples":[{"en":"The bouncer looked like a gorilla, but he was surprisingly polite.","zh":"那名保鏢看起來像個粗野大漢，但意外地很有禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two gorillas in dark suits blocked the doorway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gorilla","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61814ec78c5df056943a","word":"gospel","forms":["gospel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5430ae3650374d46","term":"gospel","forms":["gospel","gospels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"《福音書》；新約四福音","explanation":"gospel首先指《新約》開頭的四部福音書，即《馬太福音》《馬可福音》《路加福音》和《約翰福音》，內容圍繞耶穌的出生、傳道、受難和復活。","examples":[{"en":"The four Gospels tell the story of Jesus in different ways.","zh":"四部福音書從不同角度講述了耶穌的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was reading the Gospel of John before breakfast.","zh":"她早餐前正在讀《約翰福音》。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gospel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c8ba38de242aa52","term":"gospel","forms":["gospel","gospels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關於耶穌生平的福音記述","explanation":"在較寬的意義上，gospel也可以指早期基督教時期寫成的、記述耶穌生平及教導的福音書或相關記述，而不只強調它在新約中的書名地位。","examples":[{"en":"This ancient gospel describes several events from Jesus' ministry.","zh":"這部古老的福音記述了耶穌傳道時期的幾件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The class read the Gospel of Luke.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gospel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd73a2f7c7982c61006b","word":"gossip","forms":["gossip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af3b5d772cd26c18","term":"gossip","forms":["gossip","gossips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愛傳閒話的人","explanation":"指喜歡談論、傳播別人私事的人，常含有“不太守口如瓶”的批評意味。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful what you tell Maya—she's a bit of a gossip.","zh":"你告訴瑪雅的話要小心——她有點愛傳閒話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our neighbor is a notorious gossip.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gossip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b45c14a048c7111","term":"gossip","forms":["gossip","gossips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關於私事的閒話","explanation":"指關於某人私生活的未經正式證實的談論，尤其是當事人不在場時流傳的訊息。","examples":[{"en":"According to the latest gossip, their relationship is in trouble.","zh":"據最近的傳聞說，他們的關係遇到了麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't want to spread gossip about my coworkers.","zh":"我不想傳播關於同事的閒話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gossip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b596a06091c2e522","term":"gossip","forms":["gossip","gossips","gossiping","gossipping","gossiped","gossipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳播他人私事","explanation":"指談論並傳播別人的私生活，尤其是把訊息告訴更多人；它就是名詞“閒話”變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"They were gossiping about their manager after the meeting.","zh":"會議結束後，他們在議論經理的私事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't gossip about people who aren't here.","zh":"請不要議論不在場的人的私事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gossip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0acb4d236dc4d40335f7","word":"govern","forms":["govern"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b824c4e082b22bd","term":"govern","forms":["govern","governs","governing","governed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"治理；統治","explanation":"指以政治權力制定並執行公共政策，掌管國家或地區；就是握住國家的方向盤。","examples":[{"en":"The new leader governed the country with patience.","zh":"這位新領導人耐心地治理這個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one can govern a city by fear alone.","zh":"沒有人能單靠恐懼來治理一座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/govern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efbf83d6c3ca11bb","term":"govern","forms":["govern","governs","governing","governed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"約束；控制行為","explanation":"指控制某人或某物的行為，使其遵守規則或保持在可接受範圍內；也可以要求人自我約束。","examples":[{"en":"Children must learn to govern their impulses.","zh":"孩子必須學會控制自己的衝動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please govern yourselves while the teacher is away.","zh":"老師不在時，請大家自覺遵守規矩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/govern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a26da2e0101cc6c7","term":"govern","forms":["govern","governs","governing","governed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"決定；支配結果","explanation":"指某個因素對結果起決定性影響，好像它握住了結果的方向盤。","examples":[{"en":"Several factors govern the final price.","zh":"幾個因素決定了最終價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In this game, luck governs the outcome.","zh":"在這個遊戲中，運氣決定結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/govern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab5e9e376f9539179e46","word":"government","forms":["government"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-414f74ce45ee24e1","term":"government","forms":["government","governments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政府機構","explanation":"指有權制定或執行法律、管理國家、地區、人民或組織的政府機構。這是最常見、最基本的用法，重點在“掌握管理和立法權力的機構”。","examples":[{"en":"The government has announced new measures to reduce pollution.","zh":"政府宣佈了減少汙染的新措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The local government repaired the damaged bridge.","zh":"地方政府修復了受損的橋樑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/government","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9406f48eafa1eba0","term":"government","forms":["government","governments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統治性的國家行政權力","explanation":"指把國家及其行政機構看作一種統治性的政治力量，強調“誰在掌權並負責治理”，而不只是某個辦公機構。它和“政府機構”相近，但視角更偏國家的統治與行政體系。","examples":[{"en":"People expect the government to protect their basic rights.","zh":"人們希望政府保障他們的基本權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Government must remain accountable to the people.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/government","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3f6a67e041389bbd013","word":"governor","forms":["governor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac883d35882f9bc1","term":"governor","forms":["governor","governors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行政區最高長官","explanation":"指一個國家一級行政區的最高行政負責人，例如州或省的長官。這個人像“掌舵者”一樣負責領導和管理整個行政區。","examples":[{"en":"The governor announced new measures to improve public transport.","zh":"州長宣佈了改善公共交通的新措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was elected governor of the state last year.","zh":"她去年當選為該州州長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/governor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6a2f9e6783bd8aa","term":"governor","forms":["governor","governors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自動調節裝置","explanation":"指機器中根據執行情況自動調節速度、功率或其他動作的裝置。它不是人在管理，而是像一個自動掌舵者一樣讓機器保持合適的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The engine governor keeps the motor running at a steady speed.","zh":"發動機調速器使電動機保持穩定轉速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"When the governor failed, the turbine accelerated dangerously.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/governor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ce8f3a30b319c93","term":"governor","forms":["governor","Governors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"州長等職位名稱","explanation":"指“governor”這一官職或擔任該職務的人，通常對應某個州、省或其他一級行政區的最高行政長官。它與普通名詞義相同，但更強調正式的職位稱謂。","examples":[{"en":"She is the leading candidate for Governor of the state.","zh":"她是該州州長職位的主要候選人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The governor signed the bill at noon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/governor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b447a850b890144660c","word":"gown","forms":["gown"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aaa008aa48228245","term":"gown","forms":["gown","gowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬鬆長袍","explanation":"指寬鬆、下襬較長、從身體上方垂落下來的外衣，是 gown 各種含義的基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"The dancer wore a loose white gown that moved with every step.","zh":"舞者穿著一件寬鬆的白色長袍，每一步都隨之飄動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge entered wearing a long black gown.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6cb7c96b8878ae7","term":"gown","forms":["gown","gowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女式長裙","explanation":"指女性穿的外衣或連衣裙，可以是普通布料製成，也可以是絲綢等較講究的材料。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a blue silk gown for the evening reception.","zh":"她為晚間招待會選了一件藍色絲綢長裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actress stepped onto the stage in a long black gown.","zh":"那位女演員穿著一襲黑色長裙走上舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f543e8cabc2bdceb","term":"gown","forms":["gown","gowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業或學術禮袍","explanation":"指法官、律師、牧師、大學教師或學生等在特定職業、宗教或學術場合穿的正式長袍。它仍然是“套在身上的寬鬆袍服”，只是用途更正式。","examples":[{"en":"The graduates put on their gowns before the ceremony.","zh":"畢業生們在典禮開始前穿上了學位袍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge entered the courtroom wearing a black gown.","zh":"法官穿著黑色法袍走進法庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-234afbd5f044f3636494","word":"grab","forms":["grab"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0005ce45e6c5ccd5","term":"grab","forms":["grab","grabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突然一抓","explanation":"指突然伸手去抓某物的一下動作，重點是動作迅速、帶有撲抓或搶抓的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"She made a grab for the falling phone.","zh":"她伸手去抓正在掉落的手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His first grab missed the ball.","zh":"他第一次伸手抓球沒有抓到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be7566ba5d482dd2","term":"grab","forms":["grab","grabs","grabbing","grabbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然抓住","explanation":"指迅速而突然地抓住某人或某物，通常是為了阻止、拉回、拿住或不讓它逃走。","examples":[{"en":"I grabbed her hand before she stepped into the road.","zh":"她走進馬路前，我抓住了她的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He grabbed the cup before it fell.","zh":"杯子掉下來前，他抓住了它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1e56aa722c2ce2c","term":"grab","forms":["grab","grabs","grabbing","grabbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"趕緊拿取","explanation":"指快速拿來、取回或找個地方坐下，常帶有“順手、馬上”的語氣；這是日常最實用的引申義之一。","examples":[{"en":"Grab a chair and join us.","zh":"拿把椅子過來，和我們一起吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need to grab my keys from the office.","zh":"我得趕緊去辦公室拿鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e010fd1ce1acc173e3b4","word":"grace","forms":["grace"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95d10a291a7e94da","term":"grace","forms":["grace","graces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"優雅的魅力","explanation":"指一個人或事物使人感到愉悅、得體而有魅力的品質；這種“光彩”可以來自外表、舉止或整體氣質。","examples":[{"en":"She handled the difficult question with grace.","zh":"她優雅而得體地應對了這個難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His quiet grace made everyone feel welcome.","zh":"他安靜而從容的氣質讓每個人都感到受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32cc260430d22927","term":"grace","forms":["grace","graces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動作的優美與從容","explanation":"指身體動作自然、平衡而優美的狀態，尤其常用於舞蹈、運動或走路；這是“讓動作更美”的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"The dancer moved across the stage with grace.","zh":"舞者優雅地穿過舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She crossed the icy stage with surprising grace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-411647b734dfa783","term":"grace","forms":["grace","graces","gracing","graced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……增添光彩","explanation":"指用自己的出現、氣質或裝飾使某個地方、場合或事物更美、更有分量；也就是把名詞意義中的“優雅和光彩”帶給物件。","examples":[{"en":"A famous chef graced the opening ceremony.","zh":"一位著名廚師為開幕式增添了光彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bright flowers graced the entrance.","zh":"鮮豔的花朵裝點了入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da8b2af143753f86a0a8","word":"graceful","forms":["graceful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-396f792e541cedfb","term":"graceful","forms":["graceful","more graceful","most graceful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"動作或形態優美","explanation":"指動作輕盈流暢，或形狀、比例自然協調，給人優雅美觀的感覺。這是 graceful 最常見、最容易聯想到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The young dancer moved across the stage with graceful steps.","zh":"年輕舞者邁著優雅的舞步走過舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The swan made a graceful turn on the water.","zh":"天鵝在水面上優雅地轉了個身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graceful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-636e45aa5c013433","term":"graceful","forms":["graceful","more graceful","most graceful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬厚而得體","explanation":"形容人在受挫、被批評或處於不利情形時仍然從容體面，不傲慢，也不抱怨；這裡的優雅更多是品格和態度上的。","examples":[{"en":"She was graceful in defeat and congratulated the winner.","zh":"她輸得體面，還向獲勝者表示祝賀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a graceful concession after losing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graceful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8ddd88d2ee60bda3057","word":"gracious","forms":["gracious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b129f1f8a1d28c63","term":"gracious","forms":["gracious","more gracious","most gracious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親切有禮","explanation":"形容一個人待人溫和、親切而有禮貌，讓別人感到受到尊重和歡迎。這是 gracious 最常用、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Our host was gracious to everyone, even when the dinner ran late.","zh":"主人對每個人都很親切有禮，即使晚餐推遲了也沒有改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our gracious hostess welcomed even the unexpected guests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gracious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-99ce87ad600dd796","term":"gracious","forms":["gracious","more gracious","most gracious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"優雅迷人","explanation":"形容外表、動作、舉止或整體氣質自然流暢、優美而有魅力。它和前面“待人親切”的意思相通，都帶有一種不勉強、不粗魯的得體感。","examples":[{"en":"Her gracious movements made the dance look effortless.","zh":"她優雅的動作讓這支舞看起來毫不費力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their gracious hostess welcomed each guest personally.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gracious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ffe97bba510b9f5cf1bb","word":"grade","forms":["grade"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26edf183bd560bce","term":"grade","forms":["grade","grades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"等級；評級","explanation":"grade 可以是對物品質量、狀況或價值作出的等級評定，也就是把它放在某個質量檔次上。","examples":[{"en":"This is a high-grade steel used in aircraft.","zh":"這是一種用於飛機制造的高等級鋼材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inspector assigned the hotel a higher grade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6acb0323d4d10116","term":"grade","forms":["grade","grades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考試成績；分數","explanation":"grade 是考試、作業或其他評價給出的分數、字母等級或類似符號，表示表現有多好。","examples":[{"en":"She got an excellent grade on her final exam.","zh":"她的期末考試成績非常好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher posted our grades online.","zh":"老師把我們的成績釋出到了網上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51aa3fa6ebbb26cc","term":"grade","forms":["grade","grades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"程度；檔次","explanation":"grade 表示某物在一條質量、強度或用途標準上的位置，因此可以指某種檔次或等級。","examples":[{"en":"Make sure you buy food-grade containers for this recipe.","zh":"做這個食譜時，要確保買的是食品級容器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop sells several grades of olive oil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f910788e3a559fc","term":"grade","forms":["grade","grades","grading","graded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……評分","explanation":"grade 作動詞時，最常見的意思是給考試、作業或整體學習表現打分或定等級。","examples":[{"en":"The professor graded our essays over the weekend.","zh":"教授週末批改並給我們的文章打了分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each project was graded on accuracy and clarity.","zh":"每個專案都按準確性和清晰度評分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68fc24ccdb4e48c7cee8","word":"gradual","forms":["gradual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bff6be544ec236c3","term":"gradual","forms":["gradual","more gradual","most gradual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"逐漸的；漸進的","explanation":"指某種變化像沿臺階前進一樣，一點一點、按一定過程發生，而不是突然完成。它既可以描述增加、減少，也可以描述知識、能力或狀態的發展。","examples":[{"en":"The gradual increase in sunlight helped the plants grow.","zh":"陽光逐漸增加，幫助植物生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made gradual progress after practicing every day.","zh":"她每天練習後取得了逐步的進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gradual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ec0375ea56387e5c8f0","word":"graduate","forms":["graduate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-557c1ea7b9d7b65c","term":"graduate","forms":["graduate","graduates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學畢業生","explanation":"指完成大學學位要求、被學校正式認可的人，也就是走完高等教育這段臺階的人。","examples":[{"en":"The company is looking for recent university graduates.","zh":"這家公司正在招聘剛畢業的大學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Recent graduates often struggle to find affordable housing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graduate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f36c869ec73bb5ea","term":"graduate","forms":["graduate","graduates","graduating","graduated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"畢業","explanation":"指完成學校或大學規定的學習要求並正式畢業，就是走完一個教育階段的臺階。","examples":[{"en":"My sister graduated from college last spring.","zh":"我姐姐去年春天從大學畢業了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He graduated in 2022 with a degree in biology.","zh":"他於2022年畢業，獲得了生物學學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graduate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-415473a357d9d696222e","word":"graduation","forms":["graduation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5e89724d1871c34","term":"graduation","forms":["graduation","graduations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"畢業；畢業過程","explanation":"指完成學校或課程的學習要求並取得文憑的行為或過程，重點在“完成學業、正式畢業”這一階段。","examples":[{"en":"Her graduation from medical school was a proud moment for the whole family.","zh":"她從醫學院畢業是全家都感到驕傲的時刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He found a job soon after graduation.","zh":"他畢業後不久就找到了一份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graduation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16002c50dc1da23b","term":"graduation","forms":["graduation","graduations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"畢業典禮","explanation":"指為慶祝學生完成學業而舉行的正式典禮或相關活動，是“畢業”這一終點的公開慶祝。","examples":[{"en":"My parents are coming to my graduation next month.","zh":"我父母下個月要來參加我的畢業典禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandparents traveled overnight to attend her graduation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graduation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c2240217b64aa2d2b96","word":"grain","forms":["grain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0efb27b52e978e3","term":"grain","forms":["grain","grains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穀物；糧食","explanation":"指收穫後作為糧食使用的穀物籽粒，如小麥、玉米或大麥；從“一粒穀物”可以擴充套件到這類糧食的總稱。通常作不可數名詞。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers stored grain in a dry warehouse for the winter.","zh":"農民把糧食儲存在乾燥的倉庫裡過冬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rising grain prices have affected the cost of bread.","zh":"糧食價格上漲影響了麵包的成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f91a56413863cbf","term":"grain","forms":["grain","grains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紋理方向","explanation":"像許多穀粒排列出方向一樣，木材、皮革等材料表面也會有由纖維或紋路形成的方向，這就是 grain。","examples":[{"en":"Always sand the table along the grain of the wood.","zh":"給桌子打磨時，要始終順著木材的紋理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The knife cut through the leather against the grain.","zh":"刀子逆著皮革的紋理劃了過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52c98f3552df2667","term":"grain","forms":["grain","grains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微小顆粒","explanation":"由“一粒穀物”引申而來，指沙子、鹽等物質中的一個很小的顆粒。","examples":[{"en":"A grain of sand got into my eye at the beach.","zh":"在海邊時，一粒沙子進了我的眼睛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She added a grain of salt to the sauce.","zh":"她在醬汁里加了一粒鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-caa75103c53be0b30302","word":"gram","forms":["gram"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa70405f905ecdac","term":"gram","forms":["gram","grams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"克","explanation":"gram 是質量單位“克”，一克等於一千克的千分之一。買食品、稱材料或說明藥物劑量時都可能用到它。","examples":[{"en":"Add 200 grams of flour to the bowl.","zh":"把兩百克麵粉加入碗中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This tablet contains five grams of sugar.","zh":"這片藥含有五克糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c82b4c91a9fa5467","term":"gram","forms":["gram","grams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豆科植物","explanation":"這裡的 gram 指一種為種子而栽培的豆科植物，尤其可以指鷹嘴豆一類的植物。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers grow gram in the dry region.","zh":"農民在這個乾旱地區種植這種豆科植物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers plant gram after the monsoon rains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e05eb8a4a255743e051d","word":"grammar","forms":["grammar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a8c4c1859909182","term":"grammar","forms":["grammar","grammars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種語言的語法系統","explanation":"指一門語言中詞語、短語和句子如何組合的規則系統，強調某一種具體語言或某一套獨立的規則。","examples":[{"en":"The grammar of this language is quite different from English.","zh":"這種語言的語法和英語很不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A good grammar helps learners understand how sentences are built.","zh":"一本好的語法書能幫助學習者理解句子是怎樣構成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grammar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ac65144327b2373","term":"grammar","forms":["grammar","grammars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語法；語言結構規則","explanation":"泛指語言中支配詞語排列和句子構成的規則整體，不特指某一種語言。","examples":[{"en":"Grammar is often harder to learn than vocabulary.","zh":"語法往往比詞彙更難學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The textbook explains the grammar of spoken Japanese.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grammar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b732997dc9a5a73e16b","word":"grammatical","forms":["grammatical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecb73e8649adbf9e","term":"grammatical","forms":["grammatical","more grammatical","most grammatical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合乎語法的","explanation":"指一個片語、句子或整段表達符合該語言的語法和句法規則，結構上沒有明顯違規。它強調“搭建方式正確”，不一定表示內容有意義、表達自然或適合正式發表。","examples":[{"en":"This sentence is grammatical, but it sounds rather formal.","zh":"這個句子合乎語法，但聽起來相當正式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please make the paragraph grammatical without changing its meaning.","zh":"請在不改變原意的情況下，把這段話改得合乎語法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grammatical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-846bd33c5ca22f06","term":"grammatical","forms":["grammatical","more grammatical","most grammatical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"語法的；與語法有關的","explanation":"指某件事涉及語言的語法規則或語法結構，例如分析句子的複雜程度、準確性或結構特點。這裡不是說某個表達本身“正確”，而是說明它屬於語法這一方面。","examples":[{"en":"The study compares grammatical complexity in spoken and written language.","zh":"這項研究比較了口語和書面語中的語法複雜程度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher explained the grammatical function of each word.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grammatical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4361cc01e665e9d5dfa0","word":"grand","forms":["grand"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a742a03ef469c420","term":"grand","forms":["grand","grander","more grand","grandest","most grand"],"pos":"adj","zh":"宏大的；等級高的；程度強的","explanation":"表示事物規模很大、地位很高、氣勢宏大，或程度特別強、出眾。它不是單純說尺寸大，還常讓人感到重要、壯觀或非同一般。","examples":[{"en":"We stood quietly and admired the grand mountain.","zh":"我們靜靜地站著，欣賞那座宏偉的山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has grand plans for its new exhibition.","zh":"這家博物館對新展覽有宏大的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ab7049973595a7f3568","word":"grandfather","forms":["grandfather"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afe13fcc060ee8cc","term":"grandfather","forms":["grandfather","grandfathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祖父；外祖父","explanation":"指父親或母親的父親，也就是自己上一代男性長輩中的父親。這個詞不區分父系和母系，因此既可以譯為“爺爺”，也可以譯為“外公”。","examples":[{"en":"My grandfather taught me how to repair bicycles.","zh":"我爺爺教會了我怎麼修腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandfather lives with the family.","zh":"她的外公和家人住在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grandfather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c04d87aa70a7d16530de","word":"grandmother","forms":["grandmother"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0f93fa8ab915927","term":"grandmother","forms":["grandmother","grandmothers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祖母；外祖母","explanation":"指父親或母親的母親，也就是自己的祖母或外祖母。英語的 grandmother 不像漢語那樣單獨區分父系和母系，具體是哪一位要看語境。","examples":[{"en":"My grandmother lives with us and makes wonderful soup.","zh":"我的外祖母和我們住在一起，而且很會煲湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandmother taught her how to sew.","zh":"她的祖母教她縫紉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grandmother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-609991bb611a48aa","term":"grandmother","forms":["grandmother","grandmothers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女性祖先","explanation":"在較寬泛的說法中，grandmother 不一定只指仍在世或能明確認出的祖母，也可以泛指家族譜系中更早的一位女性祖先或創始者。","examples":[{"en":"She was the grandmother of a family that had lived in the valley for generations.","zh":"她是一個世代居住在那座山谷裡的家族的女性先祖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our grandmothers endured hardships we can scarcely imagine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grandmother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3492ad65d05a973fef8c","word":"grant","forms":["grant"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-839b12fa58d2fe36","term":"grant","forms":["grant","grants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資助金；授予物","explanation":"指被授予的具體東西，尤其是政府、學校或機構為某個專案提供的一筆資助金；也可以泛指一項恩惠或好處。","examples":[{"en":"The university gave her a grant for field research.","zh":"大學給了她一筆田野研究資助金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We received a small grant to repair the community center.","zh":"我們獲得了一筆小額資助，用來修繕社群中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-168a72b978bd45cf","term":"grant","forms":["grant","grants","granting","granted","grantest","grantedst","granteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"准許；批准","explanation":"指正式同意某人的請求，允許其做某事或擁有某項許可；也就是把“可以做”的權利遞給對方。","examples":[{"en":"The committee granted her permission to join the study.","zh":"委員會批准她參加這項研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His request for leave was granted.","zh":"他的休假請求獲准了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f78fcc486f5315418fb","word":"grape","forms":["grape"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1426872854f268a","term":"grape","forms":["grape","grapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葡萄","explanation":"一種圓而光滑、通常成串長在藤上的水果，顏色可為綠色、紅色或紫色；這是 grape 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I packed a bunch of grapes for lunch.","zh":"我帶了一串葡萄當午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These grapes are sweet and seedless.","zh":"這些葡萄很甜，而且沒有籽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e30970665ed2e34594c2","word":"grapefruit","forms":["grapefruit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f95a007324a83e45","term":"grapefruit","forms":["grapefruit","grapefruits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葡萄柚","explanation":"指葡萄柚樹結出的較大的圓形果實，味道通常酸甜，果肉有白色、粉紅色或紅色等。它是這個詞最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I had half a grapefruit for breakfast.","zh":"我早餐吃了半個葡萄柚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She squeezed a grapefruit into a glass of juice.","zh":"她把一個葡萄柚榨成了一杯果汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grapefruit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f085f21d4a0939b","term":"grapefruit","forms":["grapefruit","grapefruits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葡萄柚樹","explanation":"指結葡萄柚的樹，即葡萄柚這種植物本身；可以把它看成“葡萄柚”從果實延伸到整棵樹。","examples":[{"en":"They planted a grapefruit in the corner of the garden.","zh":"他們在花園角落種了一棵葡萄柚樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The grapefruit outside our window blooms in spring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grapefruit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eef93e1d14482804277f","word":"graph","forms":["graph"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64a8e9f68ae0cd59","term":"graph","forms":["graph","graphs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料圖表","explanation":"把一組或多組數量、測量值等與另一組參照資料對應起來的圖形，用來直觀看出變化、差異或關係。它可以是折線圖、柱狀圖等資料表示方式。","examples":[{"en":"The graph shows how temperatures changed during the week.","zh":"這張圖顯示了一週內氣溫是怎樣變化的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please include a graph of the survey results in your report.","zh":"請在報告中加入一張調查結果圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc7be04ce41eff2e","term":"graph","forms":["graph","graphs","graphing","graphed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繪製成圖","explanation":"把資料、變化或觀察結果畫成 graph，使其中的關係能夠被看見和比較；也可以指用圖形記錄這些資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers graphed the results from all three experiments.","zh":"研究人員把三次實驗的結果都繪成了圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine graphs the patient's heart rate over time.","zh":"這臺機器會把病人的心率隨時間的變化記錄成圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c465a314b76283674757","word":"graphic","forms":["graphic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa4bf96e693907a2","term":"graphic","forms":["graphic","more graphic","most graphic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"圖畫的；影象的","explanation":"指以圖畫、插圖或其他視覺影象呈現的，而不是單靠文字表達的。它可以修飾作品、表示方式或資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The report includes graphic illustrations of the machine.","zh":"這份報告附有這臺機器的圖解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Graphic symbols helped visitors follow the evacuation route.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graphic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-961993c3a74af576","term":"graphic","forms":["graphic","more graphic","most graphic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"描寫生動而直白的","explanation":"指描寫具體到彷彿能直接看見現場，因而畫面感很強；用於性或暴力內容時，常強調其直白、露骨，可能令人不適。","examples":[{"en":"The article contains a graphic description of the accident.","zh":"這篇文章對事故作了非常直白、具體的描述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His graphic account of the injury upset the audience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graphic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8fd43d2f50aada6","term":"graphic","forms":["graphic","graphics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圖畫；影象","explanation":"指一幅用來傳達資訊、裝飾或說明內容的圖畫或影象，是“刻畫出來的畫面”這一核心概念最直接的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The designer made a simple graphic for the event poster.","zh":"設計師為活動海報製作了一幅簡潔的影象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report includes a graphic showing regional rainfall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graphic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60d8888af8808f1f2b59","word":"grasp","forms":["grasp"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2b60031c4119b21","term":"grasp","forms":["grasp","grasps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抓力；掌握","explanation":"指手抓住東西時的力量或控制；有時也可泛指對某物的牢牢控制。核心畫面就是把東西抓在手裡。","examples":[{"en":"The strong wind pulled the umbrella out of my grasp.","zh":"大風把雨傘從我手裡拽走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grasp weakened as her fingers grew numb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93b21451019db0d7","term":"grasp","forms":["grasp","grasps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理解；領會","explanation":"指對一個概念、問題或情況真正理解並掌握住，而不只是聽說過或記住表面資訊。就像腦子把一個難懂的東西抓牢了。","examples":[{"en":"She has a clear grasp of the basic rules.","zh":"她清楚地掌握了基本規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She quickly grasped the principle behind the machine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e513c77ea7139bb8","term":"grasp","forms":["grasp","grasps","grasping","grasped","graspest","graspedst","graspeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓住；握住","explanation":"指用手牢牢拿住或控制某物，動作重點是從接觸到抓牢。這個實際的“抓住”畫面也是其他抽象義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"He grasped the rail as the bus started moving.","zh":"公交車啟動時，他抓住了扶手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Grasp the rail firmly before stepping aboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-285ecfb650c42953","term":"grasp","forms":["grasp","grasps","grasping","grasped","graspest","graspedst","graspeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"理解；領會","explanation":"指在頭腦中把一個概念、事實或問題弄明白，能夠掌握它的要點。這裡不是用手抓，而是讓思維把內容“抓牢”。","examples":[{"en":"It took me a while to grasp how the new system works.","zh":"我花了一段時間才理解新系統是如何運作的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He quickly grasped the significance of the discovery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grasp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f6cc5b085b61387ac2c1","word":"grass","forms":["grass"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18248bde2e8170ef","term":"grass","forms":["grass","grasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"草；草本植物","explanation":"指禾本科植物，通常有細長的葉子，常成片覆蓋地面；這是grass最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The grass is wet after the rain.","zh":"雨後草地是溼的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children were playing in the tall grass.","zh":"孩子們在高高的草叢裡玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39e72f2f31c1b677","term":"grass","forms":["grass","grasses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"草坪","explanation":"指經過修剪和維護、供庭院或公園使用的草地；也就是“草”鋪成的一整片地面。","examples":[{"en":"We sat on the grass and ate lunch.","zh":"我們坐在草坪上吃午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep off the grass while the new seed establishes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7f22419aacf0eae9563","word":"grasshopper","forms":["grasshopper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c720d0ef3022f6d5","term":"grasshopper","forms":["grasshopper","grasshoppers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蚱蜢；蝗蟲類昆蟲","explanation":"一種主要吃植物的昆蟲，擅長跳躍；有些種類還會透過摩擦身體部位發出聲音。它和蟋蟀相近，但不是同一種昆蟲。","examples":[{"en":"A grasshopper landed on the garden fence.","zh":"一隻蚱蜢落在了花園的柵欄上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children watched grasshoppers leap through the tall grass.","zh":"孩子們看著蚱蜢在高高的草叢中跳躍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grasshopper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4317174f35620177","term":"grasshopper","forms":["grasshopper","grasshoppers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蚱蜢雞尾酒","explanation":"一種以薄荷奶油酒為主要成分的雞尾酒，通常呈綠色；這個名稱是固定的飲品名稱，不是指飲料裡真的有蚱蜢。","examples":[{"en":"She ordered a grasshopper after dinner.","zh":"晚餐後她點了一杯蚱蜢雞尾酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered a grasshopper instead of her usual martini.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grasshopper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-309fd2d254161060a48e","word":"grassy","forms":["grassy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-020930edcbc76309","term":"grassy","forms":["grassy","grassier","grassiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"長滿草的","explanation":"形容地面、山坡、空地等被草覆蓋，呈現出一片草地的樣子。這是 grassy 最常見、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children ran across the grassy field.","zh":"孩子們跑過那片長滿草的田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sat on a grassy bank beside the river.","zh":"我們坐在河邊長滿草的堤岸上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grassy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aaa8c4b1d63fd4a2","term":"grassy","forms":["grassy","grassier","grassiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"像草的","explanation":"形容某物在外觀、觸感或整體特徵上像草；這裡不一定真的覆蓋著草，而是從“帶有草的樣子”延伸出來的比喻性描述。","examples":[{"en":"The fabric has a soft, grassy texture.","zh":"這種布料有柔軟、像草一樣的質感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fresh olive oil sometimes has a pleasantly grassy aroma.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grassy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8652b6b8e1b1f91280c9","word":"grateful","forms":["grateful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f1f69f36e2b28d8","term":"grateful","forms":["grateful","gratefuller","more grateful","gratefullest","most grateful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感激的；感謝的","explanation":"形容一個人因為得到幫助、善意或好處而心懷感謝，強調“認出別人給自己的好意並對此感到感激”。","examples":[{"en":"I’m grateful that you helped me out.","zh":"我很感激你幫助了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We’re deeply grateful to everyone who supported the project.","zh":"我們由衷感謝所有支援這個專案的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grateful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9c32f41256156344970","word":"gratitude","forms":["gratitude"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49cabb067ac1caad","term":"gratitude","forms":["gratitude","gratitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感激；感謝之情","explanation":"指因為受到幫助、支援或善待而產生的感激心情，也可以指把這種心情表達出來的謝意。它比單說“謝謝”更像一種持續的內在情感或較正式的感謝。","examples":[{"en":"She showed deep gratitude for the support she received.","zh":"她對自己得到的支援表現出了深深的感激。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I want to express my gratitude to everyone who helped us.","zh":"我想向所有幫助過我們的人表達謝意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gratitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebefe184171f13e8bf0f","word":"grave","forms":["grave"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91de39d4da1aca9b","term":"grave","forms":["grave","graver","gravest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴肅莊重的","explanation":"像面對墳墓時那樣安靜而莊重，表示一個人的神情、態度或場合嚴肅，不輕鬆也不歡快。","examples":[{"en":"The judge gave the defendant a grave look.","zh":"法官嚴肅地看了被告一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone became grave when the news was announced.","zh":"訊息宣佈後，所有人都變得嚴肅起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fbd3ea48def545d","term":"grave","forms":["grave","graver","gravest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴重的；重大的","explanation":"引申自“墳墓”的沉重感，表示問題、後果或威脅非常嚴重，可能造成重大損害。","examples":[{"en":"The accident caused grave damage to the bridge.","zh":"這起事故給橋樑造成了嚴重損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report raises grave concerns about safety.","zh":"這份報告引發了人們對安全問題的嚴重擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31917c06cf4e1cd2","term":"grave","forms":["grave","graves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"墳墓","explanation":"指挖在地下、用來埋葬一個人的具體墳墓，是 grave 最基本的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"They placed flowers on her grave.","zh":"他們把鮮花放在她的墳墓上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old grave was hidden under the trees.","zh":"那座舊墳墓隱藏在樹下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4e3fc7b0477747da28f","word":"gravity","forms":["gravity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3912cf21a83e81a9","term":"gravity","forms":["gravity","gravities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴重性；嚴肅性","explanation":"把問題想象成沉重到不能輕輕放下：因此 gravity 表示情況、決定或後果的嚴重性，以及應當認真對待的程度。","examples":[{"en":"We did not understand the gravity of the warning at first.","zh":"起初我們沒有意識到這個警告的嚴重性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge stressed the gravity of the crime.","zh":"法官強調了這項罪行的嚴重性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gravity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-216d90b50045e360","term":"gravity","forms":["gravity","gravities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重力","explanation":"指地球或其他天體使物體具有重量並向其表面下落的現象；這是“向下拉”這一核心意象在自然界中的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"Without gravity, rain would not fall to the ground.","zh":"沒有重力，雨水就不會落到地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Astronauts float because they are in very weak gravity.","zh":"宇航員會漂浮，是因為他們處在非常微弱的重力環境中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gravity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e92d69f9b951b18299f","word":"gray","forms":["gray"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68e63d4cc83379b3","term":"gray","forms":["gray","grayer","more gray","grayest","most gray"],"pos":"adj","zh":"灰色的","explanation":"指介於黑色和白色之間的顏色，是 gray 最基本的意義。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a gray sweater to work.","zh":"她穿了一件灰色毛衣去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sky turned gray before the storm.","zh":"暴風雨前，天空變成了灰色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25e0126038843f8f","term":"gray","forms":["gray","grays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"灰色","explanation":"指黑白之間的這種無彩色本身，相當於把形容詞 gray 當作顏色名稱使用。","examples":[{"en":"Gray goes well with almost every color.","zh":"灰色幾乎和所有顏色都很相配。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They painted the hallway a warm gray.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffe9f5d0585b9ec2","term":"gray","forms":["gray","grays","graying","grayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變灰","explanation":"表示頭髮或其他事物逐漸變成灰色，最常見的是說人的頭髮因年齡增長而變灰。","examples":[{"en":"His hair began to gray in his thirties.","zh":"他的頭髮在三十多歲時開始變灰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His beard grayed before his hair did.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f1eb0b9138370bffeef","word":"graze","forms":["graze"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-883cd434ff6f313c","term":"graze","forms":["graze","grazes","grazing","grazed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃草；在草地上覓食","explanation":"指牛、羊、馬等動物貼著地面一點點吃正在生長的草，這也是這個詞最基本的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Cows were grazing quietly in the meadow.","zh":"奶牛正在草地上安靜地吃草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The goats graze on weeds beside the road.","zh":"山羊在路邊吃雜草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e115a95625fc03bd","term":"graze","forms":["graze","grazes","grazing","grazed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦著表面經過","explanation":"指某物沒有正面撞上，而是貼著另一物的表面輕輕掠過；子彈擦牆就是典型畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The ball grazed the top of the fence and rolled away.","zh":"球擦過籬笆的頂部後滾開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stone grazed my shoulder as I walked past.","zh":"我走過時，一塊石頭擦過了我的肩膀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38e3607df174e5f398b0","word":"grease","forms":["grease"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78eb5f4090d56bbe","term":"grease","forms":["grease","greases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物油脂","explanation":"指動物脂肪融化後或處於柔軟狀態的油脂，常見於烹飪或食品語境。","examples":[{"en":"The recipe calls for bacon grease.","zh":"這道菜譜要求使用培根油脂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She saved the grease from the roast for cooking.","zh":"她把烤肉滲出的油脂留著做飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c96b55a2dc622d8","term":"grease","forms":["grease","greases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"油脂；油汙","explanation":"泛指有油性或脂性的物質，包括食物上的油和機器上的潤滑油脂；核心仍是“滑滑的一層油”。","examples":[{"en":"There was grease all over the kitchen floor.","zh":"廚房地板上到處都是油汙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put some grease on the gears before you close the cover.","zh":"蓋上蓋子前，在齒輪上塗些潤滑脂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23a8b86640f8a162","term":"grease","forms":["grease","greases","greasing","greased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塗油；潤滑","explanation":"給某物塗上油脂，使它減少摩擦、運轉更順暢；這是名詞“油脂”自然發展出的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Grease the hinges so the door stops squeaking.","zh":"給門鉸鏈上點油，這樣門就不會吱吱響了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Grease the pan before adding the batter.","zh":"倒入麵糊前先給烤盤塗油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5c46d70e8a33f661cef","word":"greasy","forms":["greasy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-768644f1535d4223","term":"greasy","forms":["greasy","greasier","greasiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表面油滑的","explanation":"指物體表面沾著油脂，因此摸起來滑，或看起來有一層油。這個義項最直接地體現了“沾油”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The pan left a greasy mark on the table.","zh":"這口鍋在桌上留下了一塊油漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My hands are greasy after fixing the bike.","zh":"修完腳踏車後，我的手上沾滿了油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greasy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89b3a6db7098a8f8","term":"greasy","forms":["greasy","greasier","greasiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"油脂很多的","explanation":"指食物或其他東西本身含有很多油脂，吃起來或感覺上很油膩。它和 s1 都來自同一個“油”的畫面，但這裡重點是內容物油多，而不只是表面沾油。","examples":[{"en":"The fried chicken was too greasy for me.","zh":"這份炸雞對我來說太油膩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I try not to eat greasy food late at night.","zh":"我儘量不在深夜吃油膩的食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greasy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87765da6ccf0668238c1","word":"great","forms":["great"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-079af7c58ceccff0","term":"great","forms":["great","greater","greatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大的","explanation":"表示在大小、容量或數量上明顯超過一般程度，佔據很多空間或包含很多東西，是“很大”的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"A great cloud covered the whole sky.","zh":"一大片雲遮住了整個天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They faced a great wall of ice.","zh":"他們面對著一堵巨大的冰牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/great","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26653cd38e3627cc","term":"great","forms":["great","greater","greatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很棒的","explanation":"表示某事物質量高、令人滿意或讓人開心，是日常英語裡非常常見的“很棒、很好”。","examples":[{"en":"We had a great time at the beach.","zh":"我們在海邊玩得很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a great idea.","zh":"那真是個好主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/great","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f89feead0b91741f","term":"great","forms":["great","greater","greatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"重要的","explanation":"表示某人、某事的影響、後果或意義很大，因此值得特別重視，不一定帶有讚美意味。","examples":[{"en":"This decision will have a great effect on our future.","zh":"這個決定將對我們的未來產生重大影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a great risk to help her friend.","zh":"她冒著很大的風險去幫助朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/great","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fba7b30e1dec7eba0ed","word":"greed","forms":["greed"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9ef8446107947eb","term":"greed","forms":["greed","greeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過度貪求","explanation":"指已經擁有或得到足夠的東西，卻因為自私而繼續想要更多，尤其常指對金錢、財富、食物或其他佔有物的過度慾望。它強調的是“不滿足”和“超過應得”，不只是普通的想要。","examples":[{"en":"His greed for money cost him his friends.","zh":"他對金錢的貪慾讓他失去了朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company's greed led it to ignore safety rules.","zh":"這家公司的貪婪使它無視安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-370aed697dc503aecee7","word":"greedy","forms":["greedy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac197f4ccc9c25a0","term":"greedy","forms":["greedy","greedier","greediest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貪婪的；貪得無厭的","explanation":"形容一個人過分想得到錢、權力、資源或好處，只顧滿足自己的慾望，不願適可而止。這是 greedy 最核心、最常見的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The greedy investor wanted to control the entire company.","zh":"那個貪婪的投資者想控制整家公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be greedy—leave some cake for the others.","zh":"別太貪心，給別人留點蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cf9f8ec4b95f578","term":"greedy","forms":["greedy","greedier","greediest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貪吃的","explanation":"形容人或動物總想吃得更多，或者已經吃得不少卻還不滿足。它可以是責備，也可以帶一點輕鬆、玩笑的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"Our greedy puppy grabbed another biscuit before anyone noticed.","zh":"我們那隻貪吃的小狗趁沒人注意又叼走了一塊餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The greedy puppy swallowed both treats at once.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba4788b226aa8dc2e6dc","word":"green","forms":["green"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c3fff197340d2fe","term":"green","forms":["green","greener","greenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"綠色的","explanation":"指顏色像草木、樹葉那樣的綠色，這是“green”最直接、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"He is wearing a green shirt.","zh":"他穿著一件綠色的襯衫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaves turn green in spring.","zh":"樹葉在春天變綠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a43d27559ff76485","term":"green","forms":["green","greener","greenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"缺乏經驗的","explanation":"指人像尚未成熟的植物一樣生澀，缺少實際經驗，尤其是剛開始做某件事時。","examples":[{"en":"She is still green at the job, so give her time to learn.","zh":"她做這份工作還缺乏經驗，給她一點時間學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team hired a few green graduates this year.","zh":"這個團隊今年聘用了幾名缺乏經驗的畢業生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9155b12b665500ff","term":"green","forms":["green","greens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"綠色","explanation":"指草葉等植物通常呈現的顏色，也可以泛指這種顏色本身；這個詞的核心畫面就是生長中的綠色植物。","examples":[{"en":"The hills are bright green after the rain.","zh":"雨後山坡呈現出鮮亮的綠色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose green for the kitchen walls.","zh":"她為廚房牆壁選擇了綠色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7a887acd1e128d4","term":"green","forms":["green","greens","greening","greened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變綠","explanation":"指使某物變成綠色，或使原有的綠色更加明顯；可以把它理解為讓事物靠近生長中的綠色植物所呈現的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Spring rain greened the bare fields.","zh":"春雨使光禿的田野變綠了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Algae slowly greened the neglected pond's concrete rim.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f300f10844ecfc75f12a","word":"greenhouse","forms":["greenhouse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3318e6b5b16a92c","term":"greenhouse","forms":["greenhouse","greenhouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溫室","explanation":"指用玻璃或塑膠圍起來、利用陽光保溫以種植植物的建築。它就像把適合生長的溫度留在一座房子裡。","examples":[{"en":"We grow herbs and tomatoes in the greenhouse.","zh":"我們在溫室裡種香草和番茄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school built a small greenhouse behind the science building.","zh":"學校在科學樓後面建了一座小溫室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greenhouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-231bf89d726826891c15","word":"greet","forms":["greet"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e1f3def88bd2543","term":"greet","forms":["greet","greets","greeting","greeted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迎接；問候","explanation":"指見到某人時以友好的方式迎接、問候或打招呼，是 greet 最重要、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The host greeted every guest at the door.","zh":"主人在門口迎接每一位客人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She greeted me with a warm smile.","zh":"她帶著溫暖的笑容向我打招呼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77fdb9b66430a16d","term":"greet","forms":["greet","greets","greeting","greeted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"映入眼簾；被感受到","explanation":"把某種景象、聲音或感覺寫成“迎面而來”，表示它被某人注意到或感受到；核心仍是某物主動來到感知者面前。","examples":[{"en":"A bright sunrise greeted us as we opened the curtains.","zh":"我們拉開窗簾時，明亮的日出映入眼簾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A magnificent sea view greeted us at the summit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6963a96c3b64a8a9f00","word":"greeting(s)","forms":["greeting"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1d0d992aecaca46","term":"greeting","forms":["greeting","greetings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問候語","explanation":"指人在見面、開始交談、寫信或承認對方到來時說出或寫下的禮貌用語。它可以是簡單的招呼，也可以是書信或電子郵件開頭的正式問候。","examples":[{"en":"She opened the email with a warm greeting.","zh":"她用一句親切的問候語開始了這封電子郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her cheerful greeting immediately put us at ease.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greeting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95b2ecdc71905e47","term":"greeting","forms":["greeting","greetings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問候，致意","explanation":"指向別人打招呼、表示歡迎或承認對方到來這一動作本身，而不是具體說出的那句話。可以把它看成從“問候語”延伸出來的“進行問候”。","examples":[{"en":"He raised his hand in greeting when he saw us.","zh":"他看到我們時舉手表示問候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their greeting consisted of a handshake and a shy smile.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greeting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63145a8fb4f0d9324290","word":"grief","forms":["grief"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66b7017c3120a1e6","term":"grief","forms":["grief","griefs","grieves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"悲痛；哀傷","explanation":"這是最核心的意思：人在重大失去或不幸之後，心裡產生的深切、沉重的悲痛，尤其常與親人去世等經歷有關。","examples":[{"en":"She struggled with grief after her father's death.","zh":"父親去世後，她一直在悲痛中掙扎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Time did not immediately ease his grief.","zh":"時間並沒有立即減輕他的悲痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bbb09b0b7b0109fd","term":"grief","forms":["grief","griefs","grieves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"困苦；麻煩","explanation":"這裡的 grief 是壓在人身上的麻煩或困境，不一定專指喪親之痛；它強調某件事持續給人帶來煩惱和壓力。","examples":[{"en":"The noisy neighbours have been giving us a lot of grief.","zh":"吵鬧的鄰居一直給我們帶來很多麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The faulty printer caused us endless grief.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c5bcc35ba843b536c7f","word":"grieve","forms":["grieve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a761bb89a0ab574","term":"grieve","forms":["grieve","grieves","grieving","grieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使悲痛","explanation":"某件事使人心裡承受沉重的痛苦，使這個人悲傷或苦惱。這裡的重點是悲痛落在被影響的人身上。","examples":[{"en":"The news of her brother's death grieved the whole family.","zh":"她哥哥去世的訊息使全家人悲痛不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It grieved her to sell the house where the children grew up.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2604b3e03aada23b","term":"grieve","forms":["grieve","grieves","grieving","grieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……悲痛；哀悼","explanation":"人因為某個失去、不幸或命運而感到深切悲傷，並把這份悲痛作為自己的情感來承受。","examples":[{"en":"She is still grieving for her father.","zh":"她仍在哀悼父親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The whole village grieved the loss of its doctor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5f71a452c036115","term":"grieve","forms":["grieve","grieves","grieving","grieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經歷悲痛","explanation":"人處在悲痛之中，經歷失去親人或其他重大不幸帶來的哀傷；這裡不一定明確說出悲痛的物件。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone grieves in a different way after a loss.","zh":"失去重要的人或事物後，每個人的悲痛方式都不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She needed time to grieve after her father's death.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d6c1f3fa3c69d96c4b1","word":"grill","forms":["grill"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9048af34de238441","term":"grill","forms":["grill","grills","grillz"],"pos":"noun","zh":"格柵；柵欄罩","explanation":"指帶有規則孔洞或縫隙的金屬等材料製成的格柵，用來讓空氣或液體透過，同時擋住手指、物體或攻擊。","examples":[{"en":"Keep your fingers away from the fan grill.","zh":"別把手指靠近風扇的防護格柵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A metal grill protects the ventilation opening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49b8d0a784c01b31","term":"grill","forms":["grill","grills","grillz"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燒烤裝置（英式）","explanation":"在英式英語中，指利用上方輻射熱烤制食物的爐具或烤箱功能。","examples":[{"en":"Put the cheese toast under the grill for two minutes.","zh":"把乳酪吐司放到烤箱上方的燒烤檔下烤兩分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place the sausages under a hot grill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e58bdd0fad0408c3","term":"grill","forms":["grill","grills","grillz"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燒烤架（美式）","explanation":"在美式英語中，指把食物放在上方、利用輻射熱和熱空氣進行烹調的燒烤裝置，常用於戶外燒烤。","examples":[{"en":"We put chicken and corn on the grill for dinner.","zh":"我們把雞肉和玉米放在燒烤架上做晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place the skewers on the hot grill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-131e2152323ee1d5","term":"grill","forms":["grill","grills","grilling","grilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"燒烤；烤制","explanation":"指把食物放在高溫烤架上烤熟；引申上仍保留“讓熱力直接作用於食物”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We grilled some burgers in the backyard.","zh":"我們在後院烤了幾個漢堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Grill the vegetables until they are slightly charred.","zh":"把蔬菜烤到表面微微焦黃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dff0404e2a8bd0a","term":"grill","forms":["grill","grills","grilling","grilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嚴厲盤問","explanation":"指像用高溫反覆烘烤一樣，連續而尖銳地追問某人，通常是為了查清事實或逼出答案。","examples":[{"en":"The reporters grilled the minister about the missing funds.","zh":"記者們就失蹤的資金嚴厲盤問那位部長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My parents grilled me about where I had been.","zh":"父母追問我剛才去了哪裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd228270ce068e3301ec","word":"grim","forms":["grim"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49dd325f5a20e7ab","term":"grim","forms":["grim","grimmer","grimmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陰沉嚴峻的","explanation":"形容環境、生活或前景陰沉、艱苦而缺乏希望，常讓人感到寒冷或壓抑。這是把“冷硬的烏雲”用於現實處境。","examples":[{"en":"The workers faced a grim future after the factory closed.","zh":"工廠關閉後，工人們面臨著黯淡而艱難的未來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave us a grim look before leaving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-692069ec6ff6f42a","term":"grim","forms":["grim","grimmer","grimmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冷硬而不屈的","explanation":"形容態度、決心或表情堅定得近乎冷酷，表示不退讓、不放鬆。這是同一張冷硬麵孔從“陰沉”轉向“咬牙堅持”。","examples":[{"en":"With grim determination, she continued the climb through the storm.","zh":"她帶著冷硬而不屈的決心，在暴風雨中繼續攀登。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With grim determination, she began the climb again.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fa6c2d2e923a33a93af","word":"grin","forms":["grin"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-494aaa72137dde39","term":"grin","forms":["grin","grins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"露齒的笑容","explanation":"指嘴唇分開、牙齒露出來的笑容；這種笑容可以是開心的，也可以帶有尷尬、得意或調皮的意味。","examples":[{"en":"A huge grin spread across her face when she saw the surprise.","zh":"她看到這個驚喜時，臉上立刻露出了燦爛的笑容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A broad grin spread across his face.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43a3fb965a96b303","term":"grin","forms":["grin","grins","grinning","grinned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"露齒笑","explanation":"指嘴唇分開、露出牙齒地笑，重點在可見的面部動作，不一定說明心情單純愉快。","examples":[{"en":"He grinned at me as if he already knew the answer.","zh":"他朝我咧嘴一笑，好像早就知道答案了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Why are you grinning? Did something funny happen?","zh":"你為什麼咧嘴笑？發生什麼有趣的事了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3026fac023c67598797c","word":"grind","forms":["grind"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9636f19c1e452a8","term":"grind","forms":["grind","grinds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"研磨；磨削","explanation":"指透過摩擦把東西磨成粉、磨利或加工成形的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The grind of the mill could be heard from the village.","zh":"村裡都能聽到磨坊研磨的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final grind produced a fine powder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-516a2acab9bd9dba","term":"grind","forms":["grind","grinds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"枯燥苦差事","explanation":"把一項需要長時間費力完成、又很無聊的任務比作持續研磨，因此表示苦差事。","examples":[{"en":"Sorting all these old files is a real grind.","zh":"整理這些舊檔案真是一件枯燥又費力的苦差事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The daily grind of commuting left him exhausted.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df20e5440fb2c7e2","term":"grind","forms":["grind","grinds","grinding","ground","grinded","grindest","groundst","groundest","grindeth","-","grounden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"磨碎","explanation":"透過橫向的擠壓和摩擦，把東西磨成較小的碎片或粉末。","examples":[{"en":"Grind the beans just before you make the coffee.","zh":"在煮咖啡前再把咖啡豆磨碎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine grinds wheat into flour.","zh":"這臺機器把小麥磨成麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4742543d50bf9c4c","term":"grind","forms":["grind","grinds","grinding","ground","grinded","grindest","groundst","groundest","grindeth","-","grounden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"磨製成形或磨利","explanation":"用摩擦力把物體加工成需要的形狀，或把邊緣磨利。","examples":[{"en":"The craftsman ground the lens to the right shape.","zh":"工匠把鏡片磨成了合適的形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ground the chisel to a sharper edge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8312def9ce627de","term":"grind","forms":["grind","grinds","grinding","ground","grinded","grindest","groundst","groundest","grindeth","-","grounden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"努力工作或學習","explanation":"把工作、學習或訓練看成持續不斷的研磨，表示長時間辛苦投入、埋頭完成目標。","examples":[{"en":"She grinds every evening to prepare for the exam.","zh":"她每天晚上都刻苦學習，為考試做準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm grinding through my final project this weekend.","zh":"這個週末我正埋頭苦幹，完成我的畢業專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-994dc8440a6b8c0627ca","word":"grip","forms":["grip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5378224736fdf15d","term":"grip","forms":["grip","grips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抓握；握法","explanation":"指用手抓住或握住某物的動作、方式或力度。重點是手牢牢接觸並控制住物體。","examples":[{"en":"Keep a firm grip on the railing as you go down the stairs.","zh":"下樓梯時要緊緊抓住扶手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grip tightened when the bus suddenly stopped.","zh":"公共汽車突然停下時，她的手握得更緊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9233fbd8c7c75b1c","term":"grip","forms":["grip","grips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摩擦力；抓地力","explanation":"指兩個表面接觸時防止滑動的力量。它不是人的動作，而是輪胎、鞋底或材料本身提供的“抓住表面”的能力。","examples":[{"en":"These hiking boots have excellent grip on wet rocks.","zh":"這雙登山靴在溼滑岩石上有很好的抓地力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soles lose their grip once the tread wears smooth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e1b759153794621","term":"grip","forms":["grip","grips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"控制；掌控","explanation":"指對人、局面或問題擁有牢固的控制，不讓它失控。它是把“手抓牢某物”擴大到抽象事物上。","examples":[{"en":"The new manager quickly got a grip on the budget.","zh":"新經理很快就控制住了預算情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is losing its grip on the competition.","zh":"這支隊伍正在失去對比賽局面的控制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23cce1d9596d5c19","term":"grip","forms":["grip","grips","gripping","gripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓緊；握牢","explanation":"指用手牢牢抓住某物，防止它掉落或滑走。它是 grip 各種比喻義的最直接來源。","examples":[{"en":"Grip the handle firmly before lifting the box.","zh":"抬箱子前要緊緊抓住把手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child gripped her father's hand in the crowd.","zh":"在人群中，孩子緊緊抓住父親的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e76c74073b5eb5b2","term":"grip","forms":["grip","grips","gripping","gripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"控制；著手處理","explanation":"指像抓住物體一樣牢牢抓住一個問題或局面，開始控制並處理它。","examples":[{"en":"We need to grip the problem before it gets worse.","zh":"我們得在問題惡化前控制住它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new manager must grip this problem immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c94177dd9b5bd1d30ba","word":"groan","forms":["groan"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8cb996878cdef41","term":"groan","forms":["groan","groans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痛苦或悲傷的呻吟","explanation":"指人因疼痛、悲傷或身體不適而發出的低沉、拖長的聲音，彷彿壓力被壓在喉嚨裡，只能沉沉地洩露出來。","examples":[{"en":"He gave a groan as he lifted the heavy box.","zh":"他搬起那個沉重的箱子時呻吟了一聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A quiet groan came from the dark room.","zh":"黑暗的房間裡傳來一聲低沉的呻吟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/groan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0e06425c8adbeae","term":"groan","forms":["groan","groans","groaning","groaned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"呻吟；發出低沉的聲音","explanation":"表示人發出低沉的呻吟聲，原因可以是疼痛，也可以是煩惱、不滿或聽到令人失望的事情。這是“壓力從喉嚨裡變成低沉聲音”的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"We groaned at his terrible joke.","zh":"聽到他糟糕的笑話，我們都發出了無奈的呻吟聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She groaned with pain when she stood up.","zh":"她站起來時疼得呻吟了一聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/groan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7aa5eb472a5562e3b021","word":"grocery","forms":["grocery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39745943df3944f9","term":"grocery","forms":["grocery","groceries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"食品和日用品等雜貨","explanation":"指家庭日常購買的食品以及其他生活用品，重點是“雜貨店裡的一批日常用品”，而不只是某一種食物。","examples":[{"en":"I need to buy some groceries for dinner.","zh":"我得買些雜貨準備晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carried the groceries into the kitchen.","zh":"她把買來的雜貨提進了廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grocery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e50946ff7682c2a0","term":"grocery","forms":["grocery","groceries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雜貨店","explanation":"指出售食品和家庭日用品的商店，也就是人們購買這些日常雜貨的地方；現代英語裡常見的完整說法是 grocery store。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small grocery near my apartment.","zh":"我住處附近有一家小雜貨店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little grocery sells excellent fresh bread.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grocery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6914401398f629ac563f","word":"gross","forms":["gross"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-995d7a163e8b7300","term":"gross","forms":["gross","grosser","more gross","grossest","most gross"],"pos":"adj","zh":"惡劣的；嚴重失當的","explanation":"指行為、錯誤、不公或侮辱等嚴重違反標準，壞得很明顯。這裡的“粗糙”從物質層面擴充套件到了道德和行為層面。","examples":[{"en":"The report contained a gross error in the final figures.","zh":"這份報告的最終數字有一個嚴重錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company was fined for gross negligence.","zh":"這家公司因嚴重疏忽而被罰款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gross","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90584d2d36597360","term":"gross","forms":["gross","grosser","more gross","grossest","most gross"],"pos":"adj","zh":"總的；未扣除的","explanation":"指金額、重量或統計數值在扣除稅費、成本或其他專案之前的總數；也就是那“一大團”尚未被削減的數值。","examples":[{"en":"Her gross income was higher than she expected.","zh":"她的總收入比預想的高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What is the gross weight of this package?","zh":"這個包裹的總重量是多少？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gross","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92d3350637b37bcc","term":"gross","forms":["gross","grosser","more gross","grossest","most gross"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人噁心的","explanation":"指外表、氣味、行為或場面讓人產生強烈的厭惡感；可以把它記成“粗糙得讓人不想碰”。","examples":[{"en":"That smell is gross—please open the window.","zh":"那個味道太噁心了，請把窗戶開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was gross to leave dirty dishes in the sink for days.","zh":"把髒盤子在水槽裡放好幾天，真讓人噁心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gross","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fd71a90a490a094","term":"gross","forms":["gross","grosses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總額；毛額","explanation":"指稅費、成本等尚未扣除前的全部金額或數量，是未經削減的“一大團”總數。","examples":[{"en":"The film's gross was ten million dollars in its first week.","zh":"這部電影第一週的總票房是一千萬美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film's opening-weekend gross exceeded expectations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gross","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ece7f2352a37af5f","term":"gross","forms":["gross","grosses","grossing","grossed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收入總額達到","explanation":"指電影、活動或商品在扣除成本前賺得某個總金額；核心仍是“得到一大團未經扣除的收入”。","examples":[{"en":"The new film grossed more than fifty million dollars worldwide.","zh":"這部新電影在全球的總票房超過了五千萬美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film grossed millions during its opening weekend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gross","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dbb3b50e59c7326b2ff7","word":"ground","forms":["ground"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61a14f9b27c20344","term":"ground","forms":["ground","grounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地面","explanation":"指人或物腳下的地表，與天空、水面或地下相對；這是把名詞 ground 記成“底部”時最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I found a ten-dollar bill on the ground outside the station.","zh":"我在車站外的地上發現了一張十美元鈔票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sat on the ground and ate their lunch.","zh":"孩子們坐在地上吃午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ground","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96944c4a12e29c9c","term":"ground","forms":["ground","grounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基礎；依據","explanation":"表示支撐某個想法、制度或工作的基礎，好像把抽象事物放在一個穩固的“底部”上。","examples":[{"en":"The training gave her solid ground for making the decision.","zh":"這次培訓為她作出決定提供了堅實的基礎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their early research laid the ground for a new treatment.","zh":"他們早期的研究為一種新療法奠定了基礎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ground","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d8c0645a3de9f0e","term":"ground","forms":["ground","grounds","grounding","grounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"罰禁外出","explanation":"把孩子或青少年“壓回家裡這個底部”，透過禁止外出或取消娛樂活動來懲罰他們。","examples":[{"en":"My parents grounded me for a week after I missed curfew.","zh":"我因為超過規定時間回家，被父母罰了一週不許外出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you keep arguing with your sister, I’ll ground you.","zh":"如果你一直和妹妹吵架，我就罰你不許出門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ground","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad936fcbed631fa67e05","word":"group","forms":["group"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99520aa7782305be","term":"group","forms":["group","groups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組；群；一組人或物","explanation":"指因為位置、特徵、活動或其他關係而被看作整體的一些人或事物。這是 group 最基本的意思：原本分散的物件被“攏”成一組。","examples":[{"en":"A group of students gathered outside the library.","zh":"一群學生聚集在圖書館外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide divided us into three groups.","zh":"導遊把我們分成了三組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/group","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ac6b4e7b6af169a","term":"group","forms":["group","groups","grouping","grouped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……分組","explanation":"指按照顏色、用途、特徵等標準，把原本分開的物件放進不同的組裡。動作重點是“把東西攏到一起並分類”。","examples":[{"en":"Please group the books by subject.","zh":"請按主題給這些書分組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher grouped the children according to age.","zh":"老師按年齡給孩子們分了組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/group","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-adca5146416ee41992ac","word":"grow","forms":["grow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ed599b79ba659c1","term":"grow","forms":["grow","grows","growing","grew","growed","grown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變大；增加","explanation":"主語本身逐漸變大、變高或增加，不一定只指人的身高，也可以指數量、規模等增長。","examples":[{"en":"The puppy grew very quickly during its first year.","zh":"這隻小狗在第一年長得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company grew from ten employees to more than a hundred.","zh":"這家公司從十名員工發展到了一百多人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6210d25efbda2358","term":"grow","forms":["grow","grows","growing","grew","growed","grown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成長；成熟","explanation":"指人隨著年齡、經歷或時間發展，逐漸成熟，也可以指能力、理解力和性格不斷發展。","examples":[{"en":"She grew more confident after joining the team.","zh":"加入團隊後，她變得更加自信了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children grow through play, practice, and relationships.","zh":"孩子透過玩耍、練習和人際關係逐漸成長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91269d49d16a819b","term":"grow","forms":["grow","grows","growing","grew","growed","grown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"種植；培育","explanation":"表示人讓植物在土地或其他環境中長起來，也就是栽種、培育某種作物。","examples":[{"en":"We grow tomatoes and herbs on our balcony.","zh":"我們在陽臺上種西紅柿和香草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This farmer grows rice without chemical pesticides.","zh":"這位農民種植水稻時不用化學農藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d61e39e75b05dab92cb","word":"growl","forms":["growl"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2e7505976ae5564","term":"growl","forms":["growl","growls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的低吼","explanation":"指動物從喉嚨裡發出的低沉、粗啞並帶有警告或威脅意味的聲音，最典型的就是狗準備攻擊前的低吼。","examples":[{"en":"The dog gave a warning growl when I reached for its food.","zh":"我伸手去拿它的食物時，那條狗發出了一聲警告性的低吼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A deep growl came from behind the gate.","zh":"大門後傳來一陣低沉的吼聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/growl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b56a701021f506d3","term":"growl","forms":["growl","growls","growling","growled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"低吼","explanation":"指動物或人發出低沉、粗啞、帶威脅或憤怒意味的聲音，核心畫面就是喉嚨裡的低沉咕嚕聲。","examples":[{"en":"The dog growled at me when I came near its bowl.","zh":"我靠近它的碗時，那條狗衝我低吼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He growled, “Stay away from my car.”","zh":"他低吼道：“離我的車遠點。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/growl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19c64195eb8f22c39b4b","word":"growth","forms":["growth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b0d3b6ba4e884cc","term":"growth","forms":["growth","growths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"增長；增加","explanation":"指規模、數量、價值或力量比原來更大，是 growth 最基本、最寬泛的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The company has seen strong growth in recent years.","zh":"這家公司近年來增長很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rapid population growth is putting pressure on housing.","zh":"人口快速增長正在給住房帶來壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/growth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ceece960da2ef51","term":"growth","forms":["growth","growths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理成長","explanation":"指人在挫折、批評或困難中獲得的心理力量、成熟度和應對逆境的能力，是“內在變得更強”的 growth。","examples":[{"en":"Moving abroad became an important part of her personal growth.","zh":"出國生活成了她個人成長的重要部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Failure can lead to growth if you learn from it.","zh":"如果能從失敗中吸取教訓，失敗也能帶來成長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/growth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02b3da21780e1038a798","word":"grumble","forms":["grumble"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c477c51ed7f7b1a","term":"grumble","forms":["grumble","grumbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牢騷；不滿的抱怨","explanation":"指用悶悶不樂、帶不滿情緒的方式說出的抱怨；這裡“低沉的聲音”進一步變成了“低沉地表達不滿”。","examples":[{"en":"After another delay, there was a grumble about the service.","zh":"又一次延誤後，有人抱怨起服務來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There were grumbles about the reduced lunch break.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88dba6427092ba76","term":"grumble","forms":["grumble","grumbles","grumbling","grumbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出低沉的咕隆聲","explanation":"指肚子、雷聲或某些動物發出低沉的咕隆聲，是最直接的“悶聲作響”。","examples":[{"en":"The thunder grumbled all night.","zh":"雷聲整夜都在低沉地隆隆作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thunder grumbled beyond the hills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-439ad56e3f893d6a","term":"grumble","forms":["grumble","grumbles","grumbling","grumbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抱怨；發牢騷","explanation":"指人用低聲、悶悶不樂的語氣表達不滿，往往是一再的小抱怨，而不是正式提出強烈抗議。","examples":[{"en":"She grumbled about the long wait.","zh":"她抱怨等候的時間太長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Passengers grumbled about the delayed departure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47032622e20b741b293b","word":"guarantee","forms":["guarantee"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1780107a4b1ea9a9","term":"guarantee","forms":["guarantee","guarantees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保證；承諾","explanation":"指讓人相信某個結果一定會出現的承諾或保障，重點是“結果有把握”。","examples":[{"en":"Can you give me a guarantee that the plan will work?","zh":"你能保證這個計劃會奏效嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company gave a written guarantee of replacement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guarantee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00339d0094143bb7","term":"guarantee","forms":["guarantee","guarantees","guaranteeing","guaranteed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保證會做到","explanation":"表示明確承諾某事會正確完成或某個結果會出現，相當於給這件事蓋上“保證印章”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel guarantees a full refund if you cancel within 24 hours.","zh":"酒店保證，如果你在二十四小時內取消，就會全額退款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We guarantee to replace any defective item.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guarantee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-298d99f3882af617","term":"guarantee","forms":["guarantee","guarantees","guaranteeing","guaranteed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……確定","explanation":"表示某種條件或行動幾乎必然帶來某個結果，因此可理解為“確保、註定會造成”。主語不一定是人，也可以是事實、條件或行為。","examples":[{"en":"Regular practice guarantees better performance.","zh":"經常練習能確保表現更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That error virtually guaranteed our defeat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guarantee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9d4034da07d8ef31db1","word":"guard","forms":["guard"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a9b5157ee35a51d5","term":"guard","forms":["guard","guards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"守衛；護衛人員或物件","explanation":"指負責保護、看守某人或某物的人，也可以指起保護作用的物件。它體現的是“站在危險和目標之間”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"A guard stood outside the museum all night.","zh":"一名警衛整晚站在博物館外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine has a guard over the moving belt.","zh":"這臺機器的傳送帶上方有一個防護罩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-561aeacc8a75264d","term":"guard","forms":["guard","guards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"警戒；防備狀態","explanation":"指為了避免危險而保持警惕、採取防守姿態的狀態。它不是一個具體的人或部件，而是“把自己置於保護狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden noise put everyone on guard.","zh":"突然的聲響讓所有人都警惕起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You must be on guard against online scams.","zh":"你必須提防網路詐騙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53dadecf04d35b7f","term":"guard","forms":["guard","guards","guarding","guarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；防衛","explanation":"指主動保護某人或某物，使其免受危險、攻擊或傷害。這是“在危險和目標之間形成防線”的動詞版本。","examples":[{"en":"Two soldiers guarded the entrance all night.","zh":"兩名士兵整晚守衛著入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This case guards the phone against water damage.","zh":"這個保護殼能防止手機受到水損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2a5adb57029ffac","term":"guard","forms":["guard","guards","guarding","guarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提防；保持警惕","explanation":"指保持謹慎或採取防守姿態，避免錯誤、危險或意外發生；也可以表示主動防範某種風險。","examples":[{"en":"Always guard against mistakes when entering the figures.","zh":"輸入數字時一定要防止出錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She guarded against giving away too much information.","zh":"她很謹慎，避免透露過多資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dde6e8974b46a1eddcd7","word":"guardian","forms":["guardian"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23edb78fda59a989","term":"guardian","forms":["guardian","guardians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"守護者；保護人","explanation":"指負責看守、照料或保護某人、某物的人，是這個詞“站在門口守護”的核心意義。它既可以指現實中的保護者，也可以較寬泛地指承擔守護職責的人。","examples":[{"en":"She became the child's guardian after his parents died.","zh":"孩子的父母去世後，她成了孩子的監護人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old trees are guardians of the village's history.","zh":"這些老樹守護著這個村莊的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guardian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7a91f2c830521e7","term":"guardian","forms":["guardian","guardians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未成年人的法定監護人","explanation":"指依法對未成年人負責的人，通常在父母不能履行職責時代表未成年人處理生活或法律事務。這是“守護者”在法律制度中的具體化意義。","examples":[{"en":"The court appointed her as the boy's legal guardian.","zh":"法院指定她為這個男孩的法定監護人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A guardian must give permission for the child to travel abroad.","zh":"監護人必須同意孩子出國旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guardian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e27150cb1fc10c8366e","word":"guava","forms":["guava"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"guava","forms":["guava"],"pos":"n.","zh":"芭樂；番石榴","examples":[{"en":"She sliced a ripe guava and shared it with us.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"This guava has pink flesh and a sweet smell.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1abe1b083d12d181ae1","word":"guess","forms":["guess"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1d48288ce79b202","term":"guess","forms":["guess","guesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猜測；估計","explanation":"指在不知道確切答案時，憑已有資訊或直覺提出一個可能的答案或結果。它強調答案尚未得到事實充分支援，而不表示這個答案一定錯誤。","examples":[{"en":"If you don't know the answer, take a guess.","zh":"如果你不知道答案，就猜一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My guess is that the train will be late.","zh":"我猜火車會晚點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-baf0782d8677f28b","term":"guess","forms":["guess","guesses","guessing","guessed","guessest","guessedst","guesseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猜測；推測","explanation":"指面對未知情況時，試著從不完整的資訊中推斷出一個可能的解釋或結果。這個動作就是把霧中的目標先估出一個位置，不保證結論正確。","examples":[{"en":"We can only guess at what was going through her mind.","zh":"我們只能猜測她當時在想什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you guess why the door is locked?","zh":"你能猜出門為什麼鎖著嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84983c60f7daadc1cb86","word":"guest","forms":["guest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1907823672c803c","term":"guest","forms":["guest","guests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受邀的客人","explanation":"guest首先指被主人邀請到家中或其他場所、接受招待的人，重點是對方處在被接待的關係中。","examples":[{"en":"We have two guests staying with us this weekend.","zh":"這個週末有兩位客人住在我們這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She welcomed every guest with a smile.","zh":"她微笑著迎接每一位客人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93b7f5457f927701","term":"guest","forms":["guest","guests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒店住客；顧客","explanation":"在酒店、旅館等提供住宿或服務的地方，guest指付費入住或接受服務的顧客，不一定是私人意義上被邀請來的客人。","examples":[{"en":"Hotel guests can use the gym until midnight.","zh":"酒店住客可以使用健身房直到午夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A guest in room twelve requested another pillow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f8aac527f9c928fcec7b","word":"guidance","forms":["guidance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-79798c26bb694c0d","term":"guidance","forms":["guidance","guidances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引導過程","explanation":"指把人、行動或事物帶向某個方向或目標的引導過程。重點不在某一句具體的話，而在持續幫助其走對路。","examples":[{"en":"The new employees worked under the guidance of an experienced manager.","zh":"新員工在一位有經驗的經理指導下工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With proper guidance, children can learn to solve problems on their own.","zh":"有適當的引導，孩子們就能學會獨立解決問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guidance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a945c7aff7e9f76","term":"guidance","forms":["guidance","guidances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建議與諮詢","explanation":"指標對某個問題提供的建議、意見或諮詢，幫助別人判斷該怎麼做。它可以來自老師、專家、機構，也可以被理解為較系統的一套建議。","examples":[{"en":"Please seek professional guidance before making a major investment.","zh":"在進行重大投資前，請尋求專業指導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her guidance helped me choose a suitable training course.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guidance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83ca68be6227af2feb15","word":"guide","forms":["guide"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-202438a3b40117e4","term":"guide","forms":["guide","guides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚮導；導遊","explanation":"guide 可以是帶人參觀某個地方、講解相關資訊，或帶人穿越危險地形的人；核心形象是走在前面替別人指路。","examples":[{"en":"Our guide showed us around the old castle.","zh":"我們的導遊帶我們參觀了那座古堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hired a guide for the mountain crossing.","zh":"我們僱了一名嚮導帶我們翻越那座山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f25d5e05da80319c","term":"guide","forms":["guide","guides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指南；指導手冊","explanation":"guide 也可以是幫助讀者瞭解某個地方、主題或操作方法的書或檔案，就像把路線和要點寫下來的“嚮導”。","examples":[{"en":"This guide explains how to use the new software.","zh":"這份指南說明了如何使用這款新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought a guide to the city before our trip.","zh":"旅行前我們買了一本城市指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01f0f09d15d34338","term":"guide","forms":["guide","guides","guiding","guided","guidest","guidedst","guideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"帶領；引導","explanation":"guide 表示帶著某人或某物沿著路線、過程或目標前進，是“走在前面幫別人找到方向”的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse guided the patient through the registration process.","zh":"護士引導病人完成了登記流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map guided us to the village.","zh":"地圖指引我們找到了那個村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03ce8b95eb32632192ca","word":"guideline","forms":["guideline"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dcbc237cf9849b1d","term":"guideline","forms":["guideline","guidelines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指導原則","explanation":"它像一條給行動定方向的線，告訴人通常應當怎樣做，但往往仍留有判斷和調整的餘地，因此不一定等同於強制性規定。","examples":[{"en":"These guidelines are intended to help new staff handle customer complaints.","zh":"這些指導原則旨在幫助新員工處理客戶投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school treats the dress code as a guideline, not a strict rule.","zh":"這所學校把著裝規範視為指導原則，而不是嚴格規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guideline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dc6e4f8f60b52bc","term":"guideline","forms":["guideline","guidelines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動指引","explanation":"這裡更強調一份較具體的計劃、說明或框架：它把目標轉化為選擇標準和操作方向，幫助人決定下一步怎麼做。","examples":[{"en":"The report provides guidelines for choosing a suitable research method.","zh":"這份報告為選擇合適的研究方法提供了指引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The handbook provides guidelines for handling customer complaints.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guideline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bde7dd741c3844cc33a2","word":"guilt","forms":["guilt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24e148170ffb7062","term":"guilt","forms":["guilt","guilts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過錯責任","explanation":"guilt 是一個人因做錯事而應承擔的責任；重點在“這件錯事算在誰身上”，不一定涉及法律或犯罪。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation placed the guilt on the company.","zh":"調查認定責任在這家公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refused to accept the guilt for the mistake.","zh":"她拒絕為這次錯誤承擔責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guilt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e910cb6da159f700","term":"guilt","forms":["guilt","guilts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內疚感","explanation":"guilt 也指做錯事後心裡感到不安、後悔，彷彿那塊“做錯事的石頭”一直壓在心上；這種感覺可以促使人道歉或改正。","examples":[{"en":"He felt intense guilt after lying to his parents.","zh":"他對父母撒謊後感到非常內疚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Talking to a friend helped her let go of her guilt.","zh":"和朋友談過後，她逐漸放下了內疚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guilt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51997f8a8db2530ecb0d","word":"guilty","forms":["guilty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c74ea1d8fbc2d210","term":"guilty","forms":["guilty","guiltier","more guilty","guiltiest","most guilty"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對不誠實行為負有責任","explanation":"指某人確實做了欺騙、作弊等不誠實的事，因此要為這件事負責；這裡的重點是“過錯落在這個人身上”。","examples":[{"en":"He was guilty of cheating at cards.","zh":"他打牌時作弊了，應為此負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt guilty about hiding the truth.","zh":"她因隱瞞真相而感到內疚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guilty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8541d895d240de58","term":"guilty","forms":["guilty","guiltier","more guilty","guiltiest","most guilty"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到內疚的","explanation":"指人心裡覺得自己做錯了事，產生不安、慚愧或想補償的感覺；不一定涉及犯罪或正式責備。","examples":[{"en":"I feel guilty about missing her birthday.","zh":"我因為錯過她的生日而感到內疚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He had a guilty conscience after lying to his parents.","zh":"他對父母撒謊後一直心裡有愧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guilty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d081f5e402980b267f1f","word":"guitar","forms":["guitar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb9d51f12bed631d","term":"guitar","forms":["guitar","guitars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吉他","explanation":"一種通常有六根弦、琴頸上帶品格的絃樂器，可以用手指或撥片撥絃演奏；日常說guitar時，通常就是指這種樂器。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps her guitar beside the sofa.","zh":"她把吉他放在沙發旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My brother plays the guitar every evening.","zh":"我哥哥每天晚上都彈吉他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guitar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-682e9763d43140d8f6c0","word":"gulf","forms":["gulf"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ca3657b3a9e212ca","term":"gulf","forms":["gulf","gulfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海灣","explanation":"gulf 指海洋的一部分向陸地深入、四周部分被陸地包圍的大片水域，也就是較大的海灣。海岸線像向內張開的空隙，因此和“深陷、凹入”的核心意象相連。","examples":[{"en":"Fishing communities line the coast of the gulf.","zh":"許多漁業社群分佈在這片海灣沿岸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river flows into a broad gulf before reaching the ocean.","zh":"這條河在入海前流入一片寬闊的海灣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9907b7ee123d1d3f","term":"gulf","forms":["gulf","gulfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鴻溝；間隔","explanation":"gulf 可以指兩個地方、事物或人之間寬闊而難以跨越的空隙；它把物理上的深大裂口轉成了抽象的“隔開”。","examples":[{"en":"A wide gulf now separates the two former friends.","zh":"如今一道巨大的鴻溝隔開了這兩位昔日的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a gulf between what the law promises and what people experience.","zh":"法律所承諾的與人們實際經歷的之間存在巨大差距。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00fb0b9e3ab096cb","term":"gulf","forms":["gulf","gulfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巨大差距","explanation":"在比喻用法中，gulf 特別指不同群體、階層或立場之間懸殊的差別；這個差別大到像一道無法輕易跨過的海溝。","examples":[{"en":"The report reveals a growing gulf between rich and poor.","zh":"這份報告揭示了貧富之間日益擴大的差距。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A gulf separates their incomes and living conditions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e46c8846ec5016c238d","word":"gum","forms":["gum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee0f5239efc41711","term":"gum","forms":["gum","gums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牙齦","explanation":"gum 是包圍並支撐牙齒的口腔軟組織，也就是牙齒周圍的牙齦。這個義項和“口腔裡包住東西的一層”這一核心形象相連。","examples":[{"en":"My gums bleed when I brush my teeth.","zh":"我刷牙時牙齦會出血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dentist says my gums look healthy.","zh":"牙醫說我的牙齦看起來很健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30493a0d31ffb84b","term":"gum","forms":["gum","gums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口香糖","explanation":"gum 也指可以放在嘴裡咀嚼、通常不吞下去的口香糖。這是“黏性樹膠”進入日常食品後的常見用法。","examples":[{"en":"I like chewing gum after lunch.","zh":"我喜歡午飯後嚼口香糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't stick your gum under the table.","zh":"請不要把口香糖粘在桌子下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3eed0f33297699415de5","word":"gun","forms":["gun"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-923f92de11fc52d7","term":"gun","forms":["gun","guns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"槍；炮","explanation":"指能把硬物高速發射出去的裝置，通常是槍，也可以是大炮。它是全詞最核心的“把力量射向目標”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The guard kept a gun under his jacket.","zh":"警衛把一把槍放在夾克下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old ship fired its guns at dawn.","zh":"那艘舊船在黎明時開炮了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5dd956df890bca43","term":"gun","forms":["gun","guns","gunning","gunned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使加速","explanation":"指用力踩油門或提高機器轉速，讓某物快速運轉；可以理解為把機器的力量“射”出去。","examples":[{"en":"She gunned the engine and pulled onto the highway.","zh":"她轟了一下發動機，駛上了高速公路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gunned the motorcycle up the hill.","zh":"他加大摩托車油門衝上山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77562953d4c8dc074e55","word":"gut","forms":["gut"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-87467021d931e312","term":"gut","forms":["gut","guts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腸道；腸胃","explanation":"指消化道，尤其是腸子；也可泛指身體內部的腸胃部分。","examples":[{"en":"A healthy gut helps your body absorb nutrients.","zh":"健康的腸道有助於身體吸收營養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The infection irritated the lining of his gut.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d1cc842ac7ed554","term":"gut","forms":["gut","guts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內在直覺","explanation":"指人的情緒、本能和身體化的內在感受，尤其是難以用理由說明的直覺。","examples":[{"en":"My gut tells me that something is wrong.","zh":"我的直覺告訴我，有些地方不對勁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My gut told me the offer was suspicious.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87ff6834290b1727","term":"gut","forms":["gut","guts","gutting","gutted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"摧毀內部；掏空核心","explanation":"比喻把建築、計劃或組織中最重要的內部部分毀掉，使其只剩外殼或失去原有功能。","examples":[{"en":"The fire gutted the old theater.","zh":"大火燒燬了這座老劇院的內部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Vandals gutted the abandoned warehouse, leaving only the outer shell.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3379feb6ae9fed3b9894","word":"guy","forms":["guy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c855f5cc93fb54e","term":"guy","forms":["guy","guys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男人；傢伙","explanation":"Guy最常見的口語義項之一是“男人、傢伙”，通常指一個具體的人，語氣比man更隨意。","examples":[{"en":"A guy at work helped me fix my bike.","zh":"單位裡有個傢伙幫我修好了腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guy next door lent me a ladder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-778d72becf7ad79e","term":"guy","forms":["guy","guys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人；大家","explanation":"複數Guys常可泛指一群人，甚至包括女性，意思接近“大家”或“各位”；但這種用法會因語境和聽者而有爭議。","examples":[{"en":"Are you guys ready to leave?","zh":"大家準備好出發了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You guys can leave your bags here.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2aa6cc2d16576ef2615e","word":"gymnasium/gym","forms":["gymnasium","gym"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-412a2e737cd6ca60","term":"gymnasium","forms":["gymnasium","gymnasia","gymnasiums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"室內體育館","explanation":"指供籃球、體操等室內運動使用的大型房間或建築物。它保留了“集中鍛鍊的場所”這一核心概念，但重點是現代室內運動場館。","examples":[{"en":"The students played basketball in the school gymnasium.","zh":"學生們在學校體育館裡打籃球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town built a new gymnasium for indoor sports.","zh":"鎮上為室內運動修建了一座新的體育館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gymnasium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-382cad1adb87666f","term":"gymnasium","forms":["gymnasium","gymnasia","gymnasiums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歐洲的升學中學","explanation":"在一些歐洲國家，指一種以學術課程為主、通常幫助學生準備大學學習的中學。這一義項把“訓練場所”從身體訓練擴充套件到了系統的學術訓練。","examples":[{"en":"After gymnasium, she plans to study medicine at university.","zh":"她讀完這類中學後，打算在大學學習醫學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He studied Latin at a German gymnasium.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gymnasium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e17d515fae125a4","term":"gym","forms":["gym","gyms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學校體育館","explanation":"指學校裡用於打球、做體操等活動的大型室內體育場所，尤其是學校體育館。","examples":[{"en":"Because of the rain, the students practiced basketball in the gym.","zh":"因為下雨，學生們在體育館裡練習籃球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The assembly moved into the gym because of rain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gym","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87dcaaf5686e5b0f","term":"gym","forms":["gym","gyms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"健身房","explanation":"指專門用於力量訓練、有氧運動和其他鍛鍊的運動設施，通常是商業健身房，不是學校體育館。","examples":[{"en":"I go to the gym three times a week before work.","zh":"我每週上班前去健身房三次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gym gets crowded after office hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gym","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09aee23b1fd4f638918d","word":"habit","forms":["habit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-528e9a7d7ed89857","term":"habit","forms":["habit","habits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日常習慣","explanation":"habit 是一個人反覆做的事情，做久了就成為穩定的日常習慣，不一定是壞事。","examples":[{"en":"Reading before bed has become a habit for me.","zh":"睡前閱讀已經成了我的一個習慣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a habit of checking the door twice.","zh":"她有反覆檢查兩遍門的習慣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/habit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7d97e9bf27c9419","term":"habit","forms":["habit","habits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不自覺的慣性行為","explanation":"這裡強調行為因為重複太多而變得自動化，即使當時沒有特別想做，也會按照老習慣做出來。","examples":[{"en":"Out of habit, I reached for my phone when I woke up.","zh":"我醒來時出於習慣就伸手去拿手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He opened the old app by force of habit.","zh":"他習慣性地開啟了那個舊應用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/habit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a831f1ff1a6c6f0ec602","word":"habitat","forms":["habitat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98bfdc79dbdee0e3","term":"habitat","forms":["habitat","habitats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生存條件與環境","explanation":"指一套能讓某種生物或某個生物群體生活、繁殖和維持下去的環境條件，重點不只是地點，還包括水、食物、溫度等適宜條件。","examples":[{"en":"The wetland provides vital habitat for many birds.","zh":"這片溼地為許多鳥類提供了重要的生存環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pollution is destroying the habitat of freshwater fish.","zh":"汙染正在破壞淡水魚的生存環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/habitat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fcc41d3b8175201","term":"habitat","forms":["habitat","habitats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物種自然分佈地","explanation":"指某個物種在自然狀態下出現和生活的地理範圍或具體地方；這裡更像是在地圖上指出“它通常在哪裡生活”。","examples":[{"en":"The panda's natural habitat is shrinking.","zh":"大熊貓的自然棲息地正在縮小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These frogs are found in a forest habitat.","zh":"這些青蛙生活在森林環境中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/habitat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc854d485a3fab487d5b","word":"habitual","forms":["habitual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-551360b63c4169a1","term":"habitual","forms":["habitual","more habitual","most habitual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"習慣性的；反覆的","explanation":"指某種行為已經反覆發生，像走熟了一條路，因此成了固定習慣或一再出現的事情。","examples":[{"en":"Her habitual lateness began to frustrate the whole team.","zh":"她習慣性遲到，開始讓整個團隊感到沮喪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He checked his phone in a habitual motion.","zh":"他下意識地做著檢視手機的習慣性動作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/habitual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91c7e8861db9d76f","term":"habitual","forms":["habitual","more habitual","most habitual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慣常做某事的","explanation":"形容一個人反覆做某種行為，已經把這種行為變成了自己的習慣，常可譯為“慣於……的”或“老是……的”。","examples":[{"en":"He was a habitual gambler who often lost more than he could afford.","zh":"他是個慣於賭博的人，經常輸掉超過自己承受能力的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The habitual offender was given another chance to change.","zh":"這個慣犯又獲得了一次改過的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/habitual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e7d3685715939842749c","word":"hacker","forms":["hacker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-124cc713259c51ac","term":"hacker","forms":["hacker","hackers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入侵計算機系統的人","explanation":"這是現代最需要優先掌握的義項：hacker指試圖進入、控制或獲取計算機、賬戶、手機等系統的人，尤其是未經許可時。它正是“把系統切開、改動”的核心畫面在網路世界中的發展。","examples":[{"en":"A hacker broke into the company's computer network last night.","zh":"昨晚有駭客入侵了這家公司的計算機網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hacker stole thousands of customers' passwords.","zh":"駭客竊取了數千名客戶的密碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hacker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7621a99764f4e5b","term":"hacker","forms":["hacker","hackers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進行改動或破解的人","explanation":"這是“做hack的人”的概括說法，指用不尋常或技術性的方式改動、拆解或處理某個物件的人。在現代語境中常常需要結合上下文，才能知道是在說計算機、裝置還是別的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The hacker changed the software to make it run faster.","zh":"那個駭客改動了軟體，讓它執行得更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hardware hacker replaced the console's original processor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hacker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f6639a8a51c6f74348c","word":"hail","forms":["hail"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f7a9b0aace64c7c","term":"hail","forms":["hail","hails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冰雹","explanation":"hail 是從雷雨雲中落下的冰粒，通常比雨滴硬，可能砸壞作物、車輛或窗戶。這是這個詞最重要的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Hail damaged the farmer's crops last night.","zh":"昨晚的冰雹損壞了農民的莊稼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm brought heavy rain and hail.","zh":"這場暴風雨帶來了大雨和冰雹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-139ec9d0098bda00","term":"hail","forms":["hail","hails","hailing","hailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下冰雹","explanation":"表示天空正在或將要降下冰雹，核心畫面就是冰粒從天上落下來。天氣主語通常是 it，而不是具體的人或物。","examples":[{"en":"It started to hail just as we left the house.","zh":"我們剛離開房子，天就開始下冰雹了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They say it will hail tonight.","zh":"據說今晚會下冰雹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8da98097b6d0bf8","term":"hail","forms":["hail","hails","hailing","hailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"大聲叫住","explanation":"表示為了引起注意而大聲喊某人或某種交通工具，就像在遠處揮手並喊出聲來。","examples":[{"en":"She hailed a taxi outside the hotel.","zh":"她在酒店外叫了一輛計程車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hailed my friend across the street.","zh":"我在街對面大聲叫住了朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4dc2159bba05da394c3b","word":"hair","forms":["hair"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78b7cca90d5e4390","term":"hair","forms":["hair","hairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一根毛髮","explanation":"指人或動物皮膚上長出的一根毛，通常是細長的角蛋白絲。它可以是頭髮中的一根，也可以是眉毛、體毛或動物毛中的一根。","examples":[{"en":"I found a long hair on my jacket.","zh":"我在外套上發現了一根長頭髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a cat hair on the sofa.","zh":"沙發上有一根貓毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b84315e42bc5125","term":"hair","forms":["hair","hairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭髮或體毛的整體","explanation":"指頭部或身體上成片、成團的毛髮；說人的髮型、長短、顏色時，最常用的就是這個意義。","examples":[{"en":"She has thick, curly hair.","zh":"她的頭髮濃密而捲曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His hair is still wet from the shower.","zh":"他洗完澡後頭發還是溼的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a9c59afb7e7cb408b27","word":"haircut","forms":["haircut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d6bbacffc92ea54","term":"haircut","forms":["haircut","haircuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理髮","explanation":"指剪頭髮這件事，通常是在理髮店由理髮師完成；重點是“剪髮的過程”，而不是剪完後的樣式。","examples":[{"en":"I need to get a haircut before the interview.","zh":"我得在面試前去理個髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My brother gave me a haircut at home.","zh":"我哥哥在家給我理了發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haircut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ad5bfec1baad46c","term":"haircut","forms":["haircut","haircuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"髮型","explanation":"指頭髮被剪成的樣式，即理髮後呈現出來的“剪法”或整體造型；它和s1的理髮過程有關，但強調結果。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a short haircut for the summer.","zh":"她為夏天選了一個短髮髮型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her short haircut suits her face.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haircut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8842c5c5e22730a50403","word":"hairdresser","forms":["hairdresser"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-485c0851692d0fed","term":"hairdresser","forms":["hairdresser","hairdressers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理髮師；髮型師","explanation":"指以剪髮、修剪、染髮或設計髮型為職業的人，也就是專門把頭髮整理和打扮得更合適的人。","examples":[{"en":"I have an appointment with my hairdresser tomorrow.","zh":"我明天和我的髮型師約好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hairdresser cut my hair shorter than I expected.","zh":"理髮師把我的頭髮剪得比我預想的短。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hairdresser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a11ae06469c63740d7b0","word":"half","forms":["half"],"officialPos":"n./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9b7cb3cba6719c2","term":"half","forms":["half"],"pos":"adj","zh":"一半的","explanation":"表示正好由二等分中的一份構成，即百分之五十。","examples":[{"en":"I drank half a bottle of water.","zh":"我喝了半瓶水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe needs half a kilo of flour.","zh":"這個食譜需要半公斤麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/half","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f59ad22cc9abaa5","term":"half","forms":["half"],"pos":"adv","zh":"一半地","explanation":"表示某件事在兩個相等部分或同等程度上發生了一半。","examples":[{"en":"The door was half open.","zh":"門半開著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bottle was only half full.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/half","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23c5811a4ba4fcd2","term":"half","forms":["half","halves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一半；兩個部分之一","explanation":"指一個整體被分成兩個大致相等的部分後，其中的一個部分。","examples":[{"en":"I ate half of the apple.","zh":"我吃了這個蘋果的一半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me one half of the sandwich.","zh":"她給了我三明治的一半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/half","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72a1b218fe5f8963","term":"half","forms":["half","halves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"二分之一","explanation":"指把一除以二得到的分數，也就是 0.5。","examples":[{"en":"Three quarters minus a quarter equals a half.","zh":"四分之三減去四分之一等於二分之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cut the melon in half.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/half","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3cbaeb57c64020ee4df4","word":"hall","forms":["hall"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b6bc708238ea072","term":"hall","forms":["hall","halls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"走廊；門廳","explanation":"指建築物內部連線房間或出入口的通道，通常比普通房間狹長，人們從這裡經過。","examples":[{"en":"I left my umbrella in the hall by the front door.","zh":"我把傘落在前門旁的門廳裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children ran laughing down the hall.","zh":"孩子們笑著沿走廊跑了過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55effdd52877a5f1","term":"hall","forms":["hall","halls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大廳；會議廳","explanation":"指能容納許多人、用於會議、演出、典禮或其他集體活動的大房間；這裡保留了“公共大房間”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The awards ceremony will take place in the main hall.","zh":"頒獎典禮將在主廳舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We booked a hall for the community meeting.","zh":"我們為社群會議預訂了一個大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ceb04a698ebb3a692774","word":"hallway","forms":["hallway"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9948b1c45363d5df","term":"hallway","forms":["hallway","hallways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"走廊；過道","explanation":"建築物內部供人通行、連線不同房間的狹長空間，就像房間之間的一條室內通道。","examples":[{"en":"I left my umbrella in the hallway.","zh":"我把傘落在走廊裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children ran down the hallway.","zh":"孩子們沿著走廊跑了過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hallway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fd07d7b4ee9ae634cc2","word":"halt","forms":["halt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fa8e6830c1b5064","term":"halt","forms":["halt","halts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"停止；中止","explanation":"a halt 是程序暫時或永久停下的狀態；它既可以是自然停下，也可以是某人或某事造成的中止。","examples":[{"en":"The new safety rules brought a halt to the dangerous work.","zh":"新的安全規定使這項危險工作停止了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After three hours, the machine came to a halt.","zh":"三個小時後，機器停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b738ce228c5e2aa","term":"halt","forms":["halt","halts","halting","halted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停下；停止","explanation":"表示人、車輛、活動或程序停下來；它直接體現 halt 的核心畫面：原本向前的東西在某一點停住。","examples":[{"en":"The bus halted outside the school.","zh":"公共汽車在學校外停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Work halted when the alarm sounded.","zh":"警報響起後，工作停止了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0eccfe263668d171bd19","word":"ham","forms":["ham"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bcab0f4db3ed2293","term":"ham","forms":["ham","hams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火腿，醃製豬腿肉","explanation":"指經過醃製等處理、作為食物食用的豬腿肉，通常就是中文所說的“火腿”。這是日常閱讀和會話中最重要的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We had ham and eggs for breakfast.","zh":"我們早餐吃了火腿和雞蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put some ham in my sandwich.","zh":"請在我的三明治裡放些火腿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ham","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89bde9913f4fd3e2","term":"ham","forms":["ham","hams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表演過火的人","explanation":"指表演過分誇張、情緒外放或顯得業餘做作的演員，也可泛指喜歡這樣表演的人。這個義項連線著“把腿和動作擺得很醒目”的誇張形象。","examples":[{"en":"He is a talented actor, but he turns into a ham on stage.","zh":"他是個有才華的演員，但一上臺就表演得過於誇張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He's such a ham whenever a camera appears.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ham","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18753f75d8e978fa4ee0","word":"hamburger/burger","forms":["hamburger","burger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fdcc42dd2ab1f375","term":"hamburger","forms":["hamburger","hamburgers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漢堡","explanation":"指把煎熟的碎牛肉肉餅夾在切開的圓麵包中，通常還加蔬菜、醬料等的一份食物；也可用肉類替代品製作。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a hamburger and fries for lunch.","zh":"我午飯點了一個漢堡和薯條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This restaurant makes hamburgers with beans instead of beef.","zh":"這家餐館用豆類代替牛肉做漢堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hamburger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb0622f194bb492b","term":"hamburger","forms":["hamburger","hamburgers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漢堡肉餅","explanation":"指夾在麵包裡的那塊肉餅本身，不包括麵包和配料；它可以由牛肉或其他替代材料製成。","examples":[{"en":"The hamburger was still pink in the middle.","zh":"那塊漢堡肉餅中間還是粉紅色的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cook the hamburger thoroughly before serving it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hamburger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85eb093f05904e1e","term":"burger","forms":["burger","burgers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漢堡包","explanation":"最常見的意思是漢堡包，通常指把肉餅夾在兩半圓麵包之間的食物。這裡的重點是“麵包夾著一個餡料”，不一定限定為牛肉。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a burger and fries for lunch.","zh":"我午飯點了一個漢堡和薯條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This restaurant makes a great chicken burger.","zh":"這家餐廳做的雞肉漢堡很好吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e2a7f828df70dbd","term":"burger","forms":["burger","burgers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"類似漢堡的夾餡食物","explanation":"這個意思把核心形象擴大了：只要是把類似餡餅或成形餡料夾在兩半面包之間的食物，也可以叫burger，即使餡料不是傳統的牛肉。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a spicy bean burger for dinner.","zh":"她晚餐選了一個辣味豆餅漢堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered a mushroom burger with fries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3ef81cb18bdaac2f67a1","word":"hammer","forms":["hammer"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed31ec02fc8ca0af","term":"hammer","forms":["hammer","hammers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錘子","explanation":"一種有沉重錘頭和手柄、用來敲打物體的工具。它是 hammer 最基本、最容易聯想到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She used a hammer to fix the loose chair.","zh":"她用錘子把鬆動的椅子修好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the hammer in the toolbox when you are finished.","zh":"用完後把錘子放回工具箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hammer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df69acd4cd905e76","term":"hammer","forms":["hammer","hammers","hammering","hammered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反覆敲打","explanation":"指用錘子、工具、拳頭等連續而用力地打，就像錘子一次次落下。這是動詞 hammer 的基本動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Someone was hammering on the front door late at night.","zh":"深夜有人不停地敲前門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hammered the metal flat with a heavy tool.","zh":"他用重工具把金屬反覆敲平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hammer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c30b30005a1335a77f2","word":"hamper","forms":["hamper"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9dd6d55db9240cf7","term":"hamper","forms":["hamper","hampers","hampering","hampered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"妨礙；拖累","explanation":"指讓行動、工作或進展變得更困難、更緩慢，但不一定完全阻止它；就像一個礙事的大籃子拖住了人的腳步。","examples":[{"en":"Bad weather hampered the rescue effort.","zh":"惡劣天氣妨礙了救援工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lack of funds has hampered the project.","zh":"資金不足拖累了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hamper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b001706a418bdfca353","word":"hand","forms":["hand"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8cf2fd9dcbc6bac","term":"hand","forms":["hand","hands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手","explanation":"指人的手，即腕部以下、用來抓握和傳遞東西的部位；這正是“用手掌握並傳遞”這一核心概念的起點。","examples":[{"en":"Wash your hands before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前洗手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She held the child's hand tightly.","zh":"她緊緊握住孩子的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a064ea36f4cfb96","term":"hand","forms":["hand","hands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"能力；手藝","explanation":"指做某件事的能力、技巧或實際掌控力：有一雙“能掌握事情的手”，就有做好它的本事。","examples":[{"en":"She tried her hand at baking a cake.","zh":"她試著做了一次蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a good hand with young children.","zh":"他很會照顧小孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bda0195a52752666","term":"hand","forms":["hand","hands","handing","handed","handest","handedst","handeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遞給；傳給","explanation":"把東西親手遞給某人，或把機會、訊息等抽象事物傳給別人；它體現了“用手掌握並傳遞”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Please hand me the salt.","zh":"請把鹽遞給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She handed the documents to her manager.","zh":"她把檔案遞給了經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b164d4d7d347d0da010","word":"handful","forms":["handful"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cec26c8fdfccdb99","term":"handful","forms":["handful","handfuls","handsful"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一把的量","explanation":"指一隻手能夠抓住或裝下的量，重點是“手裡的一把”，不要求精確計量。","examples":[{"en":"She added a handful of nuts to the salad.","zh":"她往沙拉里加了一把堅果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He scooped a handful of sand from the riverbed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3d8738b909819e4","term":"handful","forms":["handful","handfuls","handsful"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少數，約五個","explanation":"由“一把”的概念引申為一小撮人或物，通常表示數量不多，大約五個，但並非嚴格數字。","examples":[{"en":"Only a handful of students stayed after class.","zh":"只有少數幾個學生留在課後沒有離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a handful of spectators remained after midnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49b17b5d1003ee09a40a","word":"handicap","forms":["handicap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80047def8bf7446a","term":"handicap","forms":["handicap","handicaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"妨礙因素","explanation":"handicap 可以是年齡、傷病、經驗不足等使人或事情更難成功的因素，也就是前面記憶影象中的“包袱”。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of experience was a serious handicap in the interview.","zh":"經驗不足是這次面試中的一個嚴重不利因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her small size was not a handicap in the competition.","zh":"她個子小並沒有成為比賽中的障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handicap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9bf83f2ccada0f48","term":"handicap","forms":["handicap","handicaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽讓步","explanation":"在比賽中，handicap 是為了拉平雙方機會而給弱者的時間、距離等優勢，或給強者增加的重量等負擔；它不一定表示真正的缺陷，而是規則安排。","examples":[{"en":"The younger runner was given a handicap of ten seconds.","zh":"那名年紀較小的跑步者獲准提前十秒出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The champion started with a five-kilogram handicap.","zh":"這位冠軍帶著五公斤的額外負重出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handicap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a4bc5efdb30651b","term":"handicap","forms":["handicap","handicaps","handicapping","handicapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使處於不利地位","explanation":"handicap someone/something 就是給它加上“包袱”，使其更難成功；handicap 也常用於抽象原因造成的阻礙。","examples":[{"en":"The project was handicapped by a shortage of staff.","zh":"人員短缺使這個專案受到阻礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His lack of training handicapped him in the final round.","zh":"缺乏訓練使他在最後一輪中處於不利地位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handicap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d7906c798c9f8a7d1e2","word":"handicraft","forms":["handicraft"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"handicraft","forms":["handicraft"],"pos":"n.","zh":"手工藝；手工製品","examples":[{"en":"The village is known for its traditional handicraft.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We bought a local handicraft made from bamboo.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a324108508a69447776","word":"handkerchief","forms":["handkerchief"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1076d086e119a3f","term":"handkerchief","forms":["handkerchief","handkerchiefs","handkerchieves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手帕","explanation":"指一塊通常為方形的布巾，隨身帶著，用來擦臉、眼睛、鼻子或手；核心形象就是“手邊的一小塊擦拭用布”。","examples":[{"en":"She always carries a clean handkerchief in her bag.","zh":"她總是在包裡帶著一塊乾淨的手帕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He covered his mouth with a handkerchief when he coughed.","zh":"他咳嗽時用手帕捂住了嘴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handkerchief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2a116aa910d147bd5bd","word":"handle","forms":["handle"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fb961b9ea07382b","term":"handle","forms":["handle","handles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"把手；柄","explanation":"物體上專門讓人用手握住、提起或移動的部分，例如門、杯子、刀或工具的把手。","examples":[{"en":"The mug has a wide handle that is easy to hold.","zh":"這個杯子有一個很寬、很好握的把手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The suitcase handle broke on the stairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b0dc8b8f437ea77","term":"handle","forms":["handle","handles","handling","handled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"觸控；握住","explanation":"用手碰、摸或拿住某物，是所有引申義中最直接的“把東西放在手裡”。","examples":[{"en":"Please handle the glass carefully.","zh":"請小心拿這個玻璃杯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please handle the fragile plates with clean hands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58931e023c3ab290","term":"handle","forms":["handle","handles","handling","handled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"操縱；使用","explanation":"用手熟練地操作、使用或揮動工具、武器等，就像把它穩穩掌握在手中。","examples":[{"en":"She handles the camera with remarkable skill.","zh":"她操作這臺相機非常熟練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only trained staff may handle the cutting equipment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d29c3073bb7d1ed0","term":"handle","forms":["handle","handles","handling","handled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"管理；控制","explanation":"把人、局面或任務掌握在手中，負責管理、控制或安排它。","examples":[{"en":"Our manager handled the emergency calmly.","zh":"我們的經理冷靜地處理了這場緊急情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She handles complaints with patience and tact.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4623f30b926198d4284b","word":"handsome","forms":["handsome"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb065825c8032998","term":"handsome","forms":["handsome","more handsome","handsomer","most handsome","handsomest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好看的；漂亮的","explanation":"形容樹、建築、動物等非人的事物外表漂亮、令人欣賞，重點是整體看起來很有吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"That is one handsome tree in your garden.","zh":"你花園裡的那棵樹真漂亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book has a handsome leather binding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handsome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1d11a9cfa42a4f9","term":"handsome","forms":["handsome","more handsome","handsomer","most handsome","handsomest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"英俊的；有吸引力的","explanation":"形容人的外貌好看，尤其常用於男性，也可以形容女性或其他有鮮明吸引力的人。","examples":[{"en":"A handsome man was waiting by the door.","zh":"一個英俊的男人正在門口等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is handsome in a confident, elegant way.","zh":"她有一種自信而優雅的美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handsome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-668b22024c177562274e","word":"handwriting","forms":["handwriting"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-103675e7c9397e49","term":"handwriting","forms":["handwriting","handwritings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手寫這一行為","explanation":"指不用鍵盤或文書處理軟體，而是親手寫字的過程或方式，重點在“寫”這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"Handwriting takes longer than typing for me.","zh":"對我來說，手寫比打字花的時間更長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Handwriting notes helps her remember important information.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handwriting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97e95fcc29fe1198","term":"handwriting","forms":["handwriting","handwritings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人筆跡","explanation":"指某個人特有的寫字樣式，包括字形、大小和書寫習慣等；看到這種痕跡，別人可能認出是誰寫的。","examples":[{"en":"I recognized my sister’s handwriting on the envelope.","zh":"我認出了信封上我姐姐的筆跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His handwriting is small but very clear.","zh":"他的字很小，但非常清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handwriting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97858c3f5e63db2c1eef","word":"handy","forms":["handy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a73ccb7efdaa6dfe","term":"handy","forms":["handy","handier","handiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"方便好用","explanation":"指某物容易使用、能解決問題，因此很方便；重點是它像隨手可用的工具一樣實用。","examples":[{"en":"This little flashlight is handy when the power goes out.","zh":"停電時，這個小手電筒很方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A notebook is handy for recording quick ideas.","zh":"筆記本很適合隨手記錄想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f4c68b99f4c7f67","term":"handy","forms":["handy","handier","handiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"在手邊","explanation":"指某物就在附近，伸手或稍加尋找就能拿到；它從“方便使用”進一步強調了位置。","examples":[{"en":"Keep your passport handy while you go through security.","zh":"過安檢時把護照放在手邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you have a pen handy?","zh":"你手邊有筆嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-102fe46e9f0c5138","term":"handy","forms":["handy","handier","handiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"手巧能幹","explanation":"形容人動手能力強、操作靈活，能自己修理或製作東西；仍然保留“手很有用、很靈活”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is handy with tools and fixes most things herself.","zh":"我姐姐很會用工具，大多數東西都自己修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is handy around the house.","zh":"他很會做家裡的維修和雜活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/handy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3ccbe1f95156325c612","word":"hang","forms":["hang"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0671b0275f882581","term":"hang","forms":["hang","hangs","hanging","hung","hanged","hangest","hungest","hangedst","hangeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懸掛著","explanation":"某人或某物處於被支撐、吊著而離開地面的狀態，正像記憶鉤子裡“懸在半空中”。","examples":[{"en":"Several lanterns hung from the ceiling.","zh":"幾盞燈籠懸掛在天花板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A portrait hangs above the fireplace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b960d4688e429632","term":"hang","forms":["hang","hangs","hanging","hung","hanged","hangest","hungest","hangedst","hangeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掛起","explanation":"把某物吊在鉤子、牆、天花板或其他支撐物上，使它懸在半空中。","examples":[{"en":"We hung the picture above the sofa.","zh":"我們把畫掛在了沙發上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please hang your coat by the door.","zh":"請把你的外套掛在門邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c604996597da280","term":"hang","forms":["hang","hangs","hanging","hung","hanged","hangest","hungest","hangedst","hangeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閒待；閒逛","explanation":"沒有明確事情要做，只是在某處消磨時間，像時間懸著一樣過去。","examples":[{"en":"We hung around the park after school.","zh":"放學後我們在公園裡閒逛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m just hanging at home tonight.","zh":"我今晚只想待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39f8b7c01c72a5bf","term":"hang","forms":["hang","hangs","hanging","hung","hanged","hangest","hungest","hangedst","hangeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停止響應","explanation":"電腦或程式像卡在半空中一樣不再響應鍵盤、滑鼠等輸入。","examples":[{"en":"My laptop hung when I opened the large file.","zh":"我開啟那個大檔案時，膝上型電腦卡住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game keeps hanging after the update.","zh":"更新後，這個遊戲一直停止響應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d248cfe618cea15bbd95","word":"hanger","forms":["hanger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-370d6ce33b1d1e89","term":"hanger","forms":["hanger","hangers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懸掛裝置；衣架","explanation":"hanger 是把衣物或其他物品掛起來的裝置，最常見的就是衣架；核心畫面就是“讓東西掛住”。","examples":[{"en":"Please put your coat on a hanger.","zh":"請把你的外套掛到衣架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are several empty hangers in the closet.","zh":"衣櫃裡有幾個空衣架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hanger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e8ecb38de5fd6a5","term":"hanger","forms":["hanger"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餓到發火","explanation":"hanger 把 hunger（飢餓）和 anger（憤怒）合在一起，表示因為太餓而煩躁、發脾氣；核心畫面是“肚子空了，情緒也被點著了”。","examples":[{"en":"I need lunch soon because I'm getting hanger.","zh":"我得趕緊吃午飯了，因為我餓得開始發火了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She becomes hanger when she skips breakfast.","zh":"她不吃早飯時就會餓得脾氣暴躁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hanger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ecfb3a042a271f4389e","word":"happen","forms":["happen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7db7ed8746f5336","term":"happen","forms":["happen","happens","happening","happened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發生；出現","explanation":"表示某件事發生或某種情況出現，重點是事件從無到有地來到現實中。它常用來詢問或敘述事情的經過。","examples":[{"en":"What happened after the meeting?","zh":"會議結束後發生了什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing serious happened.","zh":"沒發生什麼嚴重的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9220123a68715d0d","term":"happen","forms":["happen","happens","happening","happened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"碰巧；恰好","explanation":"在 happen to do something 中，表示“碰巧做某事”或“恰好處於某種情況”；也可以用於自然發生的事情，強調它並非事先安排。","examples":[{"en":"I happened to see your brother at the station.","zh":"我碰巧在車站看到了你哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It happened to rain on the day of the picnic.","zh":"野餐那天碰巧下雨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-489f719cadf919094ddb","word":"happy","forms":["happy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e5f621e09b254f2","term":"happy","forms":["happy","happier","more happy","happiest","most happy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"快樂的；滿足的","explanation":"指因為感覺良好、生活舒適或事情令人愉快而產生滿足和快樂的心情。這是happy最基本、最常用的意思，可以從短暫的開心擴充套件到總體上過得滿意。","examples":[{"en":"Music makes me feel happy.","zh":"音樂讓我感到快樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looks happy in her new home.","zh":"她住進新家後看起來很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b2dcd0d124dbd76","term":"happy","forms":["happy","happier","more happy","happiest","most happy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"幸運的；順利的","explanation":"指受到好運照顧，結果比預期順利，接近“幸運的”或“走運的”。這裡的happy不是心情快樂，而是事情碰巧朝有利的方向發展。","examples":[{"en":"We were happy to find a taxi so quickly.","zh":"我們很幸運，很快就找到了計程車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By a happy coincidence, we caught the last ferry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c23dcbe6792e4c3c2ce","word":"harass(ment)","forms":["harass","harassment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23551ab9ed4b9744","term":"harass","forms":["harass","harasses","harassing","harassed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反覆煩擾；糾纏","explanation":"指一再做令人煩惱的事來打擾或糾纏某人，重點是行為反覆發生，讓對方無法輕鬆應對。","examples":[{"en":"Several companies kept calling to harass him about the unpaid bill.","zh":"幾家公司不斷打電話糾纏他，催他支付未繳的賬單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please stop harassing me with the same question.","zh":"請不要再用同一個問題反覆煩我了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a57ac953dbd2d67f","term":"harass","forms":["harass","harasses","harassing","harassed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人承受過重負擔","explanation":"強調反覆的要求、困難或擔憂壓在某人身上，使其精神緊張或難以承受；這裡不一定有直接糾纏者。","examples":[{"en":"The constant demands of the job were harassing him.","zh":"這份工作的不斷要求讓他壓力重重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family was harassed by debt and constant demands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d925db8dc1042fc","term":"harassment","forms":["harassment","harassments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持續攻擊或批評造成的困擾","explanation":"指反覆受到攻擊、責難或負面批評，久而久之使人擔憂、痛苦或精神上不堪其擾。重點不只是一次批評，而是持續不斷的壓力。","examples":[{"en":"The journalist received constant harassment after publishing the investigation.","zh":"這名記者發表調查報道後不斷受到騷擾和攻擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reported months of harassment from her neighbors.","zh":"她舉報說自己幾個月來一直受到鄰居的騷擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harassment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a210156b81c20686","term":"harassment","forms":["harassment","harassments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故意糾纏或恐嚇","explanation":"指有意反覆糾纏、騷擾或恐嚇某人，讓對方感到害怕、難受或無法正常生活。性騷擾、職場騷擾等都屬於這一類。","examples":[{"en":"The company fired the manager for sexual harassment.","zh":"公司因這名經理實施性騷擾而解僱了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repeated threatening calls constituted harassment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harassment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1d64b2d4cb30f1be788","word":"harbor","forms":["harbor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9c0a6308f56333e","term":"harbor","forms":["harbor","harbors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"避難處；藏身處","explanation":"它可以泛指任何能讓人或其他東西躲避危險、獲得保護的地方，不一定是海邊的港口。","examples":[{"en":"The abandoned warehouse became a harbor for stray cats.","zh":"那座廢棄倉庫成了流浪貓的藏身處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The abandoned barn offered a harbor from the storm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harbor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1ac164e28ecb030","term":"harbor","forms":["harbor","harbors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"港口；避風港","explanation":"指受到陸地或其他屏障保護、供船隻停泊或裝卸貨物的水域，是 harbor 最典型的具體形象。","examples":[{"en":"The fishing boats returned to the harbor before the storm.","zh":"漁船在暴風雨來臨前回到了港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several ships were waiting in the harbor.","zh":"幾艘船正在港口裡等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harbor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88a5f81c7d8273e5","term":"harbor","forms":["harbor","harbors","harboring","harbored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收容；為……提供藏身處","explanation":"表示讓人、船或其他東西進入安全處或藏在受保護的地方；物件可以是需要保護的人，也可以是被秘密藏匿的人。","examples":[{"en":"The small island harbored the sailors until the storm passed.","zh":"暴風雨過去前，那座小島為水手們提供了避難處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The house was accused of harboring fugitives.","zh":"那所房子被指控窩藏逃犯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harbor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed5465b9220df9ce176d","word":"hard","forms":["hard"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10704e40c524fda8","term":"hard","forms":["hard","harder","more hard","hardest","most hard"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅硬的","explanation":"表示物體質地堅硬，受到壓力時不容易變形；也可以指雨等帶來明顯衝擊的強烈特徵。","examples":[{"en":"The ground was hard after a week without rain.","zh":"一週沒有下雨後，地面變得很硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This bread is too hard to cut.","zh":"這麵包太硬了，切不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e7a72650359304c","term":"hard","forms":["hard","harder","more hard","hardest","most hard"],"pos":"adj","zh":"困難的","explanation":"表示事情、問題或處境有很大阻力，不容易完成、理解或處理。","examples":[{"en":"This is a hard question, but we can solve it together.","zh":"這是個難題，但我們可以一起解決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was hard for her to leave her family.","zh":"離開家人對她來說很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51d8bdee02bf96ff","term":"hard","forms":["hard","harder","hardest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"費力地；困難地","explanation":"表示完成某事時需要付出很多努力，過程並不容易。","examples":[{"en":"He worked hard to earn enough money for college.","zh":"他努力工作，為上大學掙夠了錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their success was hard earned.","zh":"他們的成功來之不易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f7f561ef6ac74ed6687","word":"harden","forms":["harden"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc5e0d1dc5ed0273","term":"harden","forms":["harden","hardens","hardening","hardened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變硬","explanation":"指原本較軟的東西逐漸變硬，例如液體凝固、材料變得堅硬，也可描述人的表情或態度變得僵硬。它是從“形成硬殼”這一核心畫面自然發展出的不及物用法。","examples":[{"en":"The cement will harden overnight.","zh":"水泥一夜之間就會變硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paint hardens as it dries.","zh":"油漆變干時會變硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-524196113c048751","term":"harden","forms":["harden","hardens","hardening","hardened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變硬","explanation":"指透過加熱、冷卻、乾燥或其他處理，讓某物變得更硬；也可以泛指讓某種狀態更加堅固。這裡是“形成硬殼”畫面的使動版本。","examples":[{"en":"The treatment hardens the metal.","zh":"這種處理會使金屬變硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clay is hardened in a kiln.","zh":"黏土在窯中被燒硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85db6c2962471c3c","term":"harden","forms":["harden","hardens","hardening","hardened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加強；使更堅強","explanation":"從材料變硬引申到力量、制度或防禦能力變強，表示讓某人或某物更能承受壓力和衝擊。它不一定涉及真實的硬度，而是強調“更堅固、更強韌”。","examples":[{"en":"The experience hardened her against criticism.","zh":"這段經歷使她更能經受批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The army hardened its defenses along the border.","zh":"軍隊加強了邊境防禦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-626c0884ac7ef99a8d86","word":"hardly","forms":["hardly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53ed414821fbaa1d","term":"hardly","forms":["hardly","hardlier","more hardly","hardliest","most hardly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"幾乎不；僅僅勉強","explanation":"表示某事發生的程度非常低，接近於沒有發生，或只是勉強達到；它強調“差一點就不行了”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"They hardly ever watch television.","zh":"他們幾乎從來不看電視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I could hardly hear her over the noise.","zh":"聲音太吵了，我幾乎聽不見她說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hardly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fec4a1ab659fada","term":"hardly","forms":["hardly","hardlier","more hardly","hardliest","most hardly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不大可能；才不是","explanation":"用於否定一個判斷或推測，意思接近“不太認為”“當然不是”，常帶有對所說內容的懷疑或反駁。","examples":[{"en":"I hardly think this plan will solve the problem.","zh":"我不太認為這個計劃能解決問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can hardly expect praise after arriving so late.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hardly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae82d9e9ec75475d1c87","word":"hardship","forms":["hardship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bda7218e6791855e","term":"hardship","forms":["hardship","hardships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"艱難困苦；苦日子","explanation":"指生活中持續或較嚴重的困難、困苦處境，常涉及經濟壓力、生活條件或長期的艱難經歷。它強調人正在承受的苦難，而不只是某件小麻煩。","examples":[{"en":"After losing his job, he went through a period of financial hardship.","zh":"失業後，他經歷了一段經濟困難時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family showed great strength during years of hardship.","zh":"這個家庭在多年的困苦中表現出了巨大的堅韌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hardship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-448af5e380f04246","term":"hardship","forms":["hardship","hardships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負擔；障礙","explanation":"指某件具體事情會給人帶來沉重負擔，甚至使人難以參加、完成或承擔某事；它是“路上的一塊擋路石”，不一定表示整段人生都很艱難。","examples":[{"en":"The extra fee would be a hardship for many students.","zh":"這項額外費用會給許多學生造成負擔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The extra fee imposes a hardship on poorer families.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hardship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26787dd2f72cc993706e","word":"hardware","forms":["hardware"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a64897faa0215bd","term":"hardware","forms":["hardware"],"pos":"noun","zh":"五金、工具和修理裝置","explanation":"指建造、安裝或修理房屋及其他物品時使用的實體器材，如錘子、釘子、螺絲和螺栓，也可泛指五金店出售的這類貨物。","examples":[{"en":"We need some hardware to fix the kitchen cabinet.","zh":"我們需要一些五金件來修理廚房櫥櫃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought the screws and other hardware at the local hardware store.","zh":"她在當地五金店買了螺絲和其他五金件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hardware","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cbee09e27c3afb2","term":"hardware","forms":["hardware"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機硬體","explanation":"指計算機中實際存在的部件，例如主機板、擴充套件卡等；它是可以觸控和更換的實體部分，與控制計算機執行的software相對。","examples":[{"en":"The new software runs well, but the computer hardware is too old.","zh":"新軟體執行得很好，但電腦硬體太舊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You may need to upgrade the hardware to play this game.","zh":"你可能需要升級硬體才能執行這款遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hardware","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af3ce03f6874c53162b7","word":"harm","forms":["harm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4b2846be38cf4ba","term":"harm","forms":["harm","harms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體損傷或物質損壞","explanation":"指身體受到傷害，或物品、財產遭到損壞。重點不只是“疼”，而是某人或某物留下了實際的損害。","examples":[{"en":"The firefighters rescued everyone without serious harm.","zh":"消防員救出了所有人，沒有造成嚴重傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm did considerable harm to the old bridge.","zh":"暴風雨對那座老橋造成了相當大的損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af765f72c59dd679","term":"harm","forms":["harm","harms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理或抽象傷害","explanation":"指對人的感情、心理或名譽等造成的傷害，即使身體沒有受傷，也可能受到 harm。","examples":[{"en":"Constant criticism can cause lasting emotional harm.","zh":"不斷的批評可能造成持久的心理傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The false rumor caused lasting harm to her confidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca9011ef7bd5eb6c","term":"harm","forms":["harm","harms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不利後果、損失或禍害","explanation":"指某種會讓人或事物處於更糟狀態的不利後果，常常不強調具體傷在哪裡。wish someone no harm 就是希望某人平安、不遭禍害。","examples":[{"en":"I meant no harm; I was only trying to help.","zh":"我沒有惡意，只是想幫忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child came to no harm after getting lost.","zh":"那個孩子走失後沒有遭遇不幸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ccc94f9dde861a46","term":"harm","forms":["harm","harms","harming","harmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傷害或損害","explanation":"表示使某人或某物受到身體、心理、物質或其他方面的損害。它強調把“傷害的痕跡”留在物件上，不限於打傷或弄壞。","examples":[{"en":"Too much screen time may harm children's sleep.","zh":"螢幕時間過長可能損害兒童的睡眠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chemical can harm plants and animals.","zh":"這種化學品會傷害植物和動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58904effcb30c04e5daf","word":"harmful","forms":["harmful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9efb30f1cf42e76","term":"harmful","forms":["harmful","harmfuller","more harmful","harmfullest","most harmful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有害的；會造成傷害的","explanation":"指某種東西、行為或影響會傷害身體、破壞事物，或帶來不良後果；重點是它具有造成損害的可能性。","examples":[{"en":"Too much sugar can be harmful to your teeth.","zh":"攝入過多糖分可能會損害牙齒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some cleaning products contain harmful chemicals.","zh":"有些清潔用品含有有害化學物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harmful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2940f4354ebd1ab721cf","word":"harmonica","forms":["harmonica"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61b46e19f084afd1","term":"harmonica","forms":["harmonica","harmonicas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口琴","explanation":"最常見的意思是口琴：樂器上有一排小孔，吹入或吸出氣流時，不同的孔會發出不同的音。它體積小，常用於獨奏、民謠和藍調等音樂。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps a harmonica in her coat pocket.","zh":"她把一把口琴放在外套口袋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He played the harmonica while his friends sang.","zh":"朋友們唱歌時，他吹起了口琴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harmonica","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2be663431f0072506a04","word":"harmony","forms":["harmony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3c2be6371fdf9e5","term":"harmony","forms":["harmony","harmonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"和諧；協調","explanation":"指不同的人、群體或事物相處、配合得很好，彼此沒有明顯衝突，就像各部分被放到了合適的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The two communities have lived in harmony for generations.","zh":"這兩個社群幾代人以來一直和睦相處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy aims to restore harmony between workers and managers.","zh":"這項新政策旨在恢復工人與管理者之間的和諧關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harmony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce1f6c408fa42d4a","term":"harmony","forms":["harmony","harmonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"協調的組合；和諧效果","explanation":"指顏色、形狀、聲音或其他元素搭配在一起很協調，整體聽起來或看起來令人愉悅。","examples":[{"en":"The room achieves a calm harmony of light, color, and texture.","zh":"這個房間把光線、色彩和質感組合成了寧靜和諧的整體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The colors blend into a pleasing harmony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harmony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49f756463ad9dcfb9b6a","word":"harness","forms":["harness"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f940f6429ee3f94","term":"harness","forms":["harness","harnesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"挽具；安全帶式裝備","explanation":"指套在馬等工作動物身上、用來約束動物並把它的力量傳給車輛或農具的一套帶子、繩子或支撐物，也可泛指類似的承託或約束裝備。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer checked the horse's harness before starting the cart.","zh":"農夫在讓馬拉車前檢查了馬的挽具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The climber wore a safety harness before going up the wall.","zh":"攀巖者上牆前穿戴了安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1117cb475a1085b3","term":"harness","forms":["harness","harnesses","harnessing","harnessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……套上挽具；拴住","explanation":"指把挽具套到動物或其他物件上，或用帶子、繩索將其固定起來，使它能夠被牽引、控制或承擔工作。","examples":[{"en":"They harnessed the pony to a small wagon.","zh":"他們把小馬套在一輛小車上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide harnessed the child before the climbing lesson.","zh":"攀巖課開始前，嚮導給孩子繫好了安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8804799308aa2b6","term":"harness","forms":["harness","harnesses","harnessing","harnessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"控制並利用","explanation":"指把原本分散、難以控制的力量或資源組織起來，使其為某個目的發揮作用；它保留了“套住並調動”的挽具意象。","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to harness solar energy for clean electricity.","zh":"這個專案旨在利用太陽能生產清潔電力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good leaders harness the team's creativity.","zh":"優秀的領導者會調動團隊的創造力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd878fa2293de72e9c87","word":"harsh","forms":["harsh"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee9887d6c233f6d8","term":"harsh","forms":["harsh","harsher","more harsh","harshest","most harsh"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粗糙或令人不適","explanation":"指觸感或其他感官體驗不舒服，像粗糙的表面一樣讓人難受；也可以形容刺耳的聲音、刺眼的光線或惡劣的環境。","examples":[{"en":"The harsh sunlight made it difficult to see the road.","zh":"刺眼的陽光讓人很難看清道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The harsh fabric scratched against his skin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harsh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb3b1de6d81a485d","term":"harsh","forms":["harsh","harsher","more harsh","harshest","most harsh"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴厲而苛刻","explanation":"形容批評、待遇、懲罰或決定過於嚴厲，給人不公平、殘酷或難以接受的感覺；它是從“讓人不舒服”擴充套件到心理和社會層面的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The judge was criticized for making such a harsh decision.","zh":"那名法官因作出如此嚴厲的決定而受到批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge delivered a harsh criticism of their conduct.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harsh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-d087ee8196afa2ff461a","word":"harvest","forms":["harvest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c415dd04ef62ac9","term":"harvest","forms":["harvest","harvests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收割；收穫過程","explanation":"指把已經成熟的莊稼或果實收集起來的過程，也可以泛指一次收穫活動。","examples":[{"en":"The constant rain made the harvest a nightmare this year.","zh":"今年連綿不斷的雨讓收穫工作變得非常艱難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers began the harvest as soon as the wheat was dry.","zh":"小麥一干，工人們就開始收割了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harvest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17443272475fe20c","term":"harvest","forms":["harvest","harvests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收成；收穫物","explanation":"指收割後得到的莊稼、果實或其他農產品，也就是一次收穫的產量或成果。","examples":[{"en":"This year's apple harvest was smaller than expected.","zh":"今年的蘋果收成比預期少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmers stored their harvest in stone barns.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harvest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46a54d715fd8d77f","term":"harvest","forms":["harvest","harvests","harvesting","harvested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收割；採收","explanation":"指把成熟的莊稼、果實等從田地或樹上收集起來。","examples":[{"en":"We harvested the apples in September.","zh":"我們在九月採收了蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmers are harvesting the rice by hand.","zh":"農民們正在手工收割水稻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harvest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49fa6d753c7ad75b524c","word":"haste","forms":["haste"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02bf7c95d83a35c5","term":"haste","forms":["haste","hastes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"匆忙；迅速","explanation":"haste 指為了趕時間而加快行動的狀態，重點不只是快，還包含急著完成、來不及從容處理的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"She packed her bag in haste and ran for the train.","zh":"她匆忙收拾好包，跑去趕火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report was written in haste and contains several errors.","zh":"這份報告寫得很倉促，裡面有幾處錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbbfc16798711395b027","word":"hasten","forms":["hasten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-393af8de5a600e7c","term":"hasten","forms":["hasten","hastens","hastening","hastened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使加快","explanation":"指催促某人，或推動某件事更快發生；這裡的“加速”物件是別人或一項正在進行的事情。","examples":[{"en":"The warning hastened the team's response.","zh":"這則警告促使團隊更快作出回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Warm weather hastened the melting of the snow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hasten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20a232caf0b58e1c","term":"hasten","forms":["hasten","hastens","hastening","hastened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使提前","explanation":"指讓原本安排在某個時間發生的事件提前發生，是“加快程序”進一步具體化的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Extra funding hastened the completion of the project.","zh":"額外的資金使專案得以提前完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scandal hastened the minister's resignation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hasten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0963cbca2986d4e9bf8","word":"hasty","forms":["hasty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-210486681cf940d9","term":"hasty","forms":["hasty","hastier","hastiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"倉促的；草率的","explanation":"事情做得太快，幾乎沒有充分考慮，因而顯得倉促或草率。它正是“被時間推著衝”的典型用法。","examples":[{"en":"I made a hasty decision and regretted it the next day.","zh":"我倉促地做了決定，第二天就後悔了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They left after a hasty breakfast.","zh":"他們匆匆吃過早飯就離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfceeac2e2efe7e5","term":"hasty","forms":["hasty","hastier","hastiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易怒的；性急的","explanation":"人的情緒像動作一樣衝得很快，容易突然生氣，所以 hasty 也可形容脾氣急、容易發火的人。","examples":[{"en":"His hasty temperament made small disagreements difficult.","zh":"他容易發火的脾氣讓小小的分歧也很難處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His hasty temper often led to needless arguments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18e1dd392168f601d0e5","word":"hat","forms":["hat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ea2bd5a2ed289c1","term":"hat","forms":["hat","hats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帽子","explanation":"戴在頭上的覆蓋物，通常有帽頂，有些還帶帽簷或裝飾；這是 hat 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a wide-brimmed hat to protect her face from the sun.","zh":"她戴了一頂寬邊帽來保護臉部免受陽光照射。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please take off your hat when you enter the room.","zh":"請進房間時摘下帽子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f3697e986fd3dfd","term":"hat","forms":["hat","hats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"角色；身份","explanation":"把一個人承擔的職位、職責或身份想成他“戴著的一頂帽子”；同一個人可以在不同場合戴不同的“帽子”。","examples":[{"en":"In my hat as team leader, I need to make the final decision.","zh":"作為團隊負責人，我需要作出最後決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Today I'm wearing my teacher's hat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eea8ec0d450873055807","word":"hatch","forms":["hatch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7220ddc591ad075e","term":"hatch","forms":["hatch","hatches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"艙口；地板或天花板上的活板門","explanation":"hatch 是裝在地板或天花板上的可開合小門，開啟後可以通往下面或上面。","examples":[{"en":"We found a hatch in the floor under the carpet.","zh":"我們在地毯下面的地板上發現了一個活板門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please close the hatch before you go upstairs.","zh":"你上樓前請把活板門關好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b640302e646c4745","term":"hatch","forms":["hatch","hatches","hatching","hatched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"孵化；破殼而出","explanation":"蛋裡的幼鳥開啟蛋殼、從裡面出來，就是 hatch；主語通常是幼鳥或蛋。","examples":[{"en":"The ducklings hatched early this morning.","zh":"小鴨子們今天清晨就孵出來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three chicks hatched from the blue eggs.","zh":"三隻小雞從那些藍色的蛋裡孵了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b86823c1650dd64","term":"hatch","forms":["hatch","hatches","hatching","hatched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"破殼","explanation":"也可以把蛋作為主語，表示蛋裂開，幼鳥即將或正在從裡面出來。","examples":[{"en":"The egg hatched while the children were watching.","zh":"孩子們觀看時，蛋破殼了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chicks began to hatch before sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11ad0e78018aab4a","term":"hatch","forms":["hatch","hatches","hatching","hatched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"策劃；醞釀計劃","explanation":"就像幼鳥在蛋裡慢慢形成，計劃或陰謀也可以在腦中“孵出來”，所以 hatch 可表示秘密地想出並策劃某事。","examples":[{"en":"They hatched a plan to surprise their teacher.","zh":"他們策劃了一個給老師驚喜的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone has hatched a clever way to save money.","zh":"有人想出了一個巧妙的省錢辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2e9a23ac36c4b227b16","word":"hate","forms":["hate"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff50f9d0509df267","term":"hate","forms":["hate","hates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"討厭的物件","explanation":"指一個人特別討厭的人、事或行為，也就是會引起強烈厭惡的物件。","examples":[{"en":"One of my biggest hates is being interrupted.","zh":"我最討厭的事情之一就是被人打斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ironing is one of my pet hates.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7c07649d68098d3","term":"hate","forms":["hate","hates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"仇恨","explanation":"指強烈的敵意或憎恨這種情緒本身，是把人或事推開的那種強烈感受。","examples":[{"en":"His voice was full of hate when he spoke about the betrayal.","zh":"他談到那次背叛時，聲音裡充滿了仇恨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of hate divided the two families.","zh":"多年的仇恨使兩個家庭彼此分裂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec9663d4e40840d5","term":"hate","forms":["hate","hates","hating","hated","hatest","hatedst","hateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"非常不喜歡；憎恨","explanation":"表示對某人、某物或某種行為有強烈厭惡，是“把它推開”的動作化表達。","examples":[{"en":"I hate waiting in long lines.","zh":"我討厭排很長的隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hates dishonest people.","zh":"她憎恨不誠實的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8730915c627248915c0","word":"hateful","forms":["hateful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1028b83cc16ebe44","term":"hateful","forms":["hateful","hatefuller","more hateful","hatefullest","most hateful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人憎恨的","explanation":"指某人或某事物讓人產生強烈的憎恨感，是“帶來仇恨”的一面，而不一定表示它本身有仇恨。","examples":[{"en":"The hateful policy caused suffering for thousands of families.","zh":"這項令人憎恨的政策讓成千上萬的家庭遭受了痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone condemned the hateful attack.","zh":"所有人都譴責那場令人憎恨的襲擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hateful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16936a6c2b9adc67","term":"hateful","forms":["hateful","hatefuller","more hateful","hatefullest","most hateful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人討厭的","explanation":"指某人或某物很惹人厭煩、讓人不想接近；這裡的情感可以比“令人憎恨的”弱一些，重點是強烈的不喜歡。","examples":[{"en":"That hateful noise kept me awake all night.","zh":"那討厭的噪聲讓我整夜睡不著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That hateful alarm wakes everyone before sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hateful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15b45021ccf8ed60039e","word":"hatred","forms":["hatred"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e000829c49560901","term":"hatred","forms":["hatred","hatreds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"憎恨；仇恨","explanation":"指非常強烈的厭惡感，往往不是短暫情緒，而是對某人、某群體或某件事形成的深重反感。它可以看作“不喜歡”不斷加深、變成一道難以消除的情緒之牆。","examples":[{"en":"Years of conflict created deep hatred between the two communities.","zh":"多年的衝突在兩個社群之間造成了深重的仇恨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke with hatred of the people who had betrayed her.","zh":"她談到那些背叛自己的人時充滿了憎恨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hatred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67f9b93a7abbb27fa8c5","word":"haul","forms":["haul"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1538883074b157bf","term":"haul","forms":["haul","hauls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漫長的路程","explanation":"指把人或物拉運、搬運所要經過的距離，常強調路遠或過程辛苦。","examples":[{"en":"The trip to the mountain village was a long haul.","zh":"去那個山村的路程很漫長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It's a long haul from here to the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc9e35544bdaa86b","term":"haul","forms":["haul","hauls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一大批收穫或所得","explanation":"指一次拿到、捕到或買到的一批東西，常常數量不少；可以是魚、贓物，也可以是購物所得。","examples":[{"en":"She came home with a huge haul of books.","zh":"她帶著一大批書回到了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fishermen showed us their morning haul.","zh":"漁民們給我們看了他們早上的收穫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a64873966e57965a","term":"haul","forms":["haul","hauls","hauling","hauled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拉運到某處","explanation":"指用車輛、牲畜或其他牽引方式，把沉重的東西拉到指定地點；重點是運輸過程費力。","examples":[{"en":"The trucks haul timber from the forest to the mill.","zh":"卡車把木材從森林運到鋸木廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They hauled the broken boat back to shore.","zh":"他們把那條壞掉的船拖回了岸邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9c28587d47e5186","term":"haul","forms":["haul","hauls","hauling","hauled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用力拉或拖重物","explanation":"指把重物從原處拉動、拖動，不一定強調把它運到很遠的地方。","examples":[{"en":"We hauled the sofa up the stairs together.","zh":"我們一起把沙發拖上了樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hauled the anchor onto the deck.","zh":"他用力把錨拖到了甲板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a18e5dc26ce0c647","term":"haul","forms":["haul","hauls","hauling","hauled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"費力搬運或運輸","explanation":"泛指把重的、笨的或難移動的東西搬走或運走，強調搬運本身很辛苦。","examples":[{"en":"The company hauls fresh fruit across the country every night.","zh":"這家公司每天晚上把新鮮水果運往全國各地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They hauled the damaged boat onto the beach.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c8d4a2c6cde265e4aff","word":"haunt","forms":["haunt"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d717aa880e771bb","term":"haunt","forms":["haunt","haunts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"常去的地方","explanation":"指某人或某一類人經常出現、活動或消磨時間的地方，核心畫面就是“總會回去的地方”。","examples":[{"en":"This café has become a favorite haunt of local artists.","zh":"這家咖啡館成了當地藝術家最喜歡的聚集地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old library was once a quiet haunt for students.","zh":"那座老圖書館曾是學生們常去的安靜去處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3e97172d5eaf336","term":"haunt","forms":["haunt","haunts","haunting","haunted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鬼魂反覆出沒","explanation":"指鬼魂反覆出現在某個地方，彷彿總會回來；也可理解為某處被鬼魂纏住。","examples":[{"en":"People say that a ghost haunts the abandoned hotel.","zh":"人們說那家廢棄的旅館鬧鬼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruined chapel is said to be haunted by a restless spirit.","zh":"據說那座殘破的小教堂被一個不得安寧的幽靈糾纏著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6886c3a7f2c1f1bf","term":"haunt","forms":["haunt","haunts","haunting","haunted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持續困擾","explanation":"指過去的記憶、失敗、恐懼或創傷像揮不去的影子一樣長期影響某人，使人不安或難以平靜。","examples":[{"en":"The memory of the accident still haunts her.","zh":"那場事故的記憶至今仍困擾著她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was haunted by the mistakes he had made as a young man.","zh":"他一直被年輕時犯下的錯誤所困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-193c45b5281908d2d9c8","word":"have","forms":["have"],"officialPos":"aux./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8340bad404b461ab","term":"have","forms":["have","has","having","had","hast","hadst","hath","-","haveing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擁有","explanation":"表示某人手裡有某物，或擁有某種財產、關係和特點，是“手裡有”的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"I have a small apartment near the station.","zh":"我在車站附近有一套小公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has two older brothers.","zh":"她有兩個哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/have","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-731bf1958cac31b2","term":"have","forms":["have","has","having","had","hast","hadst","hath","-","haveing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包含","explanation":"表示某個物體、地方或事物裡面有某種部分、成分或特徵，是“身上有”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"This jacket has a hidden pocket.","zh":"這件夾克有一個隱藏口袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soup has a lot of garlic in it.","zh":"這湯裡有很多大蒜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/have","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a692e69dc8ba2c3","term":"have","forms":["have","has","having","had","hast","hadst","hath","-","haveing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經歷","explanation":"表示經歷某段時期、事件或處境，即“身上經歷著”某種事情。","examples":[{"en":"We had a wonderful time at the beach.","zh":"我們在海邊玩得很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had a difficult experience at her first job.","zh":"她在第一份工作中經歷了一段艱難時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/have","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f1b9b47374e5c87","term":"have","forms":["have","has","having","had","hast","hadst","hath","-","haveing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"構成完成時","explanation":"作助動詞時，have 表示某件事已經發生並與相關時間或現在狀態相連，用來構成完成時。","examples":[{"en":"I have already finished the report.","zh":"我已經完成報告了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They had left before we arrived.","zh":"我們到達之前，他們已經離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/have","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0139bc5debaaa4b84e93","word":"hawk","forms":["hawk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33c8cd943d2cf5b9","term":"hawk","forms":["hawk","hawks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鷹科猛禽","explanation":"hawk是一類白天活動、捕食其他動物的鷹科猛禽，體型通常比鷹小。這個具體的鳥類義是其他比喻義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"A hawk circled above the meadow before diving toward the trees.","zh":"一隻鷹在草地上空盤旋，隨後向樹林俯衝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw a hawk perched on the fence at dawn.","zh":"黎明時我們看到一隻鷹停在籬笆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hawk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4371b1d60a759fab","term":"hawk","forms":["hawk","hawks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外形相近的猛禽","explanation":"hawk也可以泛指體型和外形類似鷹科hawk的日行性陸地猛禽，例如某些獵鷹；這裡強調的是外形和捕獵方式相近，而不一定是嚴格的分類名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The guide pointed out a hawk-like falcon flying over the cliffs.","zh":"導遊指出了一隻飛過懸崖的鷹形獵鷹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hawk circled above the meadow searching for prey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hawk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e30ea25cda1c18cfc42","word":"hay","forms":["hay"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-809728dea373508c","term":"hay","forms":["hay","hays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乾草；牲畜飼料","explanation":"hay是割下後曬乾的草，主要用來餵馬、牛等牲畜；核心畫面就是一堆曬乾的飼料草。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer put fresh hay in the horses' stall.","zh":"農夫把新幹草放進了馬廄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stacked the hay under the barn roof.","zh":"我們把乾草堆在穀倉屋頂下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac647a8a7ce5086d","term":"hay","forms":["hay","hays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飼料植物混合物","explanation":"hay也可以泛指用於喂牲畜的多種綠色葉狀植物混合物，不一定只由一種草製成。","examples":[{"en":"This hay contains clover and several kinds of grass.","zh":"這種飼料草含有三葉草和好幾種草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hay contained clover, timothy, and meadow grass.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-652607e181622fd24a78","word":"hazard","forms":["hazard"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1034fc6b8b77ecb","term":"hazard","forms":["hazard","hazards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"危險；風險","explanation":"hazard 指可能造成傷害、損失或嚴重麻煩的危險因素，也可以指處於這種危險中的風險。它保留了“把結果押在不確定事情上”的核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Loose wires are a serious fire hazard.","zh":"鬆動的電線是嚴重的火災隱患。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Driving in heavy rain is a hazard to other road users.","zh":"在大雨中駕駛會給其他道路使用者帶來危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a048711c62c99708","term":"hazard","forms":["hazard","hazards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"危險障礙；危險源","explanation":"hazard 也可以具體指路上、遊戲中或某個環境裡會造成風險的障礙或設施。它是“危險”這個抽象概念在現實中的具體落點。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers had to cross the road carefully because of several hazards.","zh":"由於路上有幾個危險障礙，徒步者必須小心過馬路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game is full of hazards that can slow you down.","zh":"這個遊戲裡到處都是會讓你減速的危險障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f639b511cf599d1c","term":"hazard","forms":["hazard","hazards","hazarding","hazarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒險；承擔風險","explanation":"hazard 作動詞時，表示明知結果不確定，仍把自己或某物置於風險之中去做某事。它和名詞“危險”的聯絡在於：行動者主動把自己放到了骰子般不可控的結果面前。","examples":[{"en":"She would not hazard her reputation on an untested plan.","zh":"她不會拿自己的名譽去冒險押在一個未經檢驗的計劃上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hazarded his life to save the child.","zh":"他冒著生命危險去救那個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b85f1592a5abdb89","term":"hazard","forms":["hazard","hazards","hazarding","hazarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒險提出；大膽猜測","explanation":"hazard 也可以表示冒險說出一個猜測、答案或意見，相當於把一個不確定的判斷先押出來。這是“承擔猜錯風險”這一核心概念在說話中的引申。","examples":[{"en":"I would hazard a guess that the meeting will be postponed.","zh":"我大膽猜測會議會被推遲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can I hazard an answer?","zh":"我可以試著猜一個答案嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0cbc64478f47cc4493a6","word":"he (him, his, himself)","forms":["he"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3706684b1630786","term":"he","forms":["he"],"pos":"pron","zh":"他","explanation":"“he”代替已經提到或聽者知道的一個男性，通常放在句首作主語；這是最重要、最常見的意義。","examples":[{"en":"He lives near the station and walks to work.","zh":"他住在車站附近，走路去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I called David, and he answered immediately.","zh":"我給大衛打了電話，他馬上接了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/he","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f2e6d33a3717ee82635","word":"head","forms":["head"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1caf3f3b9409872a","term":"head","forms":["head","heads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭部","explanation":"指人或動物身體最上方、包含大腦、嘴和主要感覺器官的部位；這是 head 最基本的“頭”義。","examples":[{"en":"The child bumped his head on the door.","zh":"那個孩子的頭撞到了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She nodded her head and smiled.","zh":"她點了點頭，笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/head","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b135fd5c71f37ce6","term":"head","forms":["head","heads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頂部；最前端","explanation":"指某物位於最上方、最前方或起始位置的部分，體現了“頭”在空間上向上、向前的引申。","examples":[{"en":"The title appears at the head of the page.","zh":"標題出現在頁面頂部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small flag flew at the head of the parade.","zh":"遊行隊伍最前面飄著一面小旗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/head","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed56bd464c732849","term":"head","forms":["head","heads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負責人；主管","explanation":"指負責領導某個部門、機構或群體的人，把身體最重要、負責指揮的“頭”引申為負責人。","examples":[{"en":"I spoke to the head of the department about the problem.","zh":"我就這個問題和部門負責人談過了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The head of the school welcomed the new students.","zh":"校長歡迎了新生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/head","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b8736ad35301b8f","term":"head","forms":["head","heads","heading","headed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"領導；負責","explanation":"表示擔任負責人並帶領一個組織、團隊或機構，就像“頭”負責思考和指揮一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Who heads the research team?","zh":"誰負責領導這個研究團隊？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Maya heads the local charity.","zh":"瑪雅負責這家當地慈善機構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/head","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cfa9ac1e084975b5d646","word":"headache","forms":["headache"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f34e27671f317a4b","term":"headache","forms":["headache","headaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭痛","explanation":"指頭部出現疼痛或不舒服的感覺，是“讓頭難受”的字面義。","examples":[{"en":"I have a headache, so I’m going to bed early.","zh":"我頭痛，所以要早點睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bright lights gave me a terrible headache.","zh":"刺眼的燈光讓我頭痛得厲害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headache","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d93ce88321db1383","term":"headache","forms":["headache","headaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麻煩事；令人頭疼的問題","explanation":"比喻某件事像頭痛一樣讓人煩惱、操心或難以處理，重點不在身體疼痛，而在問題帶來的困擾。","examples":[{"en":"Finding a parking space in this area is a real headache.","zh":"在這個地方找停車位真是件讓人頭疼的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing paperwork became a major headache.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headache","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25b1ed9615a0b6b815b4","word":"headline","forms":["headline"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b912f0f853a95d0","term":"headline","forms":["headline","headlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新聞標題；文章標題","explanation":"headline是頁面最上方、用醒目文字概括新聞或文章內容的標題，正是“頭部的一行”。","examples":[{"en":"The headline on today's newspaper reads \"John Doe Wins Wood-Splitting Competition.\"","zh":"今天報紙上的標題寫著：“約翰·多伊贏得劈柴比賽。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That shocking headline made everyone want to read the story.","zh":"那個令人震驚的標題讓所有人都想讀這篇報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26e840ab971d7de6","term":"headline","forms":["headline","headlines","headlining","headlined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擔任主打；領銜演出","explanation":"headline表示讓某人或某個專案站在演出的最顯眼位置，成為觀眾最期待的主打內容；也可以說某人自己擔任活動的主角。","examples":[{"en":"The singer will headline the festival on Saturday night.","zh":"這位歌手將在週六晚上領銜音樂節演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three local bands are headlining the concert.","zh":"三支本地樂隊將擔任這場音樂會的主打樂隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd14d23c5b078c544ecf","word":"headphone(s)","forms":["headphone","headphones"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cfff0b9252c8e912","term":"headphone","forms":["headphone","headphones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耳機","explanation":"一種貼在耳朵上、罩住耳朵，或放進耳道里的揚聲器裝置，把聲音直接送到耳邊；日常說一副耳機時通常用複數形式 headphones。","examples":[{"en":"I put on my headphones before the flight.","zh":"登機前我戴上了耳機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wears headphones when she studies in the library.","zh":"她在圖書館學習時戴著耳機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headphone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33ceaf76852dbaf3","term":"headphones","forms":["headphones","headphone"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耳機","explanation":"一種戴在耳朵上或放入耳內的發聲裝置，聲音主要由佩戴者自己聽到；它可以覆蓋耳朵，也可以貼在耳朵上或塞入耳道。","examples":[{"en":"I put on my headphones and listened to music on the train.","zh":"我戴上耳機，在火車上聽音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please take off your headphones when someone is talking to you.","zh":"有人和你說話時，請摘下耳機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headphones","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-582a5164e20a5be0f93b","word":"headquarters","forms":["headquarters"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03b9a8e2f30b2ed6","term":"headquarters","forms":["headquarters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍事指揮部","explanation":"指軍隊中負責釋出命令、指揮部隊，並由指揮官及其輔助人員組成的地點或機構。它是“把命令傳出去的中心”，是記憶這個詞最具體的起點。","examples":[{"en":"The commander returned to headquarters after the battle.","zh":"戰鬥結束後，指揮官回到了指揮部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Orders came from army headquarters before dawn.","zh":"黎明前，軍隊指揮部下達了命令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headquarters","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a01df7b58575ac48","term":"headquarters","forms":["headquarters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組織總部","explanation":"指公司、政府機構、非營利組織等負責日常管理和運營的中心。它是“組織的頭部駐地”，通常也是辦公、決策和行政活動集中的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The company’s headquarters is in Singapore.","zh":"這家公司的總部在新加坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity moved its headquarters to a larger building.","zh":"這家慈善機構把總部搬到了更大的大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/headquarters","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-599f8341fe3e0fd23de7","word":"heal","forms":["heal"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11b578ed3e8479bb","term":"heal","forms":["heal","heals","healing","healed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"治癒；使恢復","explanation":"heal表示使疾病、傷口或受傷的身體狀況變好，直到恢復健康。它的核心畫面是把受損的部分重新變完整。","examples":[{"en":"The medicine helped heal the infection.","zh":"這種藥幫助治好了感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor says the treatment will heal her damaged lung.","zh":"醫生說這種治療會治好她受損的肺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1fba8160b7fc7a2","term":"heal","forms":["heal","heals","healing","healed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"恢復健康；癒合","explanation":"heal也表示人或傷口自己逐漸恢復健康，不強調是誰進行治療。這裡是“受損的東西重新變完整”這一核心畫面的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The cut should heal in a few days.","zh":"這道傷口應該幾天後就會癒合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With rest, his body began to heal.","zh":"經過休息，他的身體開始恢復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92e6d7c4350a5194","term":"heal","forms":["heal","heals","healing","healed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修復關係；彌合分歧","explanation":"heal還可以比喻修復人與人之間的裂縫，例如緩和衝突、彌合分歧，使關係重新完整。","examples":[{"en":"They need time and honest conversation to heal their relationship.","zh":"他們需要時間和坦誠的交流來修復關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apology helped heal the rift between them.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62484e22a6a5ade1ba25","word":"health","forms":["health"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19c1c05484e80b77","term":"health","forms":["health","healths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"健康；身心無恙","explanation":"指沒有疾病或功能障礙、身心處於良好狀態；這是 health 最基本的意思。它既包括身體健康，也包括心理健康。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of sleep can seriously affect your health.","zh":"睡眠不足會嚴重影響你的健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is taking a short break to protect her mental health.","zh":"她正在短暫休息，以保護自己的心理健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/health","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7b636251f11891e","term":"health","forms":["health","healths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體狀況；運轉情況","explanation":"把“健康”這個概念從人和身體擴充套件到專案、經濟、組織等系統，表示它們目前是否穩定、強健、運轉良好。","examples":[{"en":"The report examines the financial health of the company.","zh":"這份報告考察了公司的財務狀況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report assesses the health of the banking system.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/health","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bde7a8b6346c071ae993","word":"healthful","forms":["healthful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97938ea9330a7022","term":"healthful","forms":["healthful","healthfuller","more healthful","healthfullest","most healthful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有益健康的","explanation":"指某種活動、食物、環境或習慣能夠促進身體健康，就像把健康帶給人一樣。重點是“有助於健康”，而不只是看起來沒有疾病。","examples":[{"en":"Swimming is a healthful activity for people of many ages.","zh":"游泳是適合許多年齡段人群的有益健康的活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She replaced sugary snacks with more healthful foods.","zh":"她用更有益健康的食物替代了含糖零食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healthful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b228539d362a99cf","term":"healthful","forms":["healthful","healthfuller","more healthful","healthfullest","most healthful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有益身心或道德發展的","explanation":"這個義項把“促進健康”的想法從身體擴充套件到心靈、品格或精神生活，表示某種影響能讓人的內心或道德狀態變得更好。","examples":[{"en":"The honest conversation had a healthful effect on their friendship.","zh":"這次坦誠的談話對他們的友誼產生了有益的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school encourages healthful outdoor recreation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healthful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87695fdac81728b9d7f2","word":"healthy","forms":["healthy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-549634f95e5844ae","term":"healthy","forms":["healthy","healthier","more healthy","healthiest","most healthy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體健康的","explanation":"指人或動物身體狀況良好，沒有疾病或明顯的身體障礙。這是 healthy 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor said that the baby was healthy.","zh":"醫生說這個嬰兒很健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wants to stay healthy as he gets older.","zh":"他希望隨著年齡增長仍然保持健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healthy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea7e78ce40633b60","term":"healthy","forms":["healthy","healthier","more healthy","healthiest","most healthy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有利於健康的","explanation":"指食物、飲食、習慣或生活方式等能夠幫助身體保持良好狀態，對健康有益。","examples":[{"en":"We are trying to make healthier meals at home.","zh":"我們正努力在家裡做更健康的飯菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise is part of a healthy lifestyle.","zh":"經常鍛鍊是健康生活方式的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healthy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-103a360f285151bfda3f","word":"heap","forms":["heap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-805694b423d07af0","term":"heap","forms":["heap","heaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一堆；堆積物","explanation":"這是最具體、最核心的意思：許多東西被放在一起，形成一個隆起的堆。","examples":[{"en":"There was a heap of leaves beside the gate.","zh":"門旁有一堆樹葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the dirty towels in a heap.","zh":"請把髒毛巾堆在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf34998c6e38726b","term":"heap","forms":["heap","heaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量；許多","explanation":"從“堆”引申出來，heap 可以表示數量多到像堆起來一樣，既可指具體事物，也可指抽象內容。","examples":[{"en":"We still have a heap of work to finish.","zh":"我們還有一大堆工作要完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We've got heaps of blankets in the cupboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04dc31b394e328e0","term":"heap","forms":["heap","heaps","heaping","heaped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堆放；堆成一堆","explanation":"heap 作動詞時，就是主動把東西集中放在一起，使它們形成一堆。","examples":[{"en":"She heaped the blankets on the sofa.","zh":"她把毯子堆在沙發上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He heaped the fallen branches into a corner.","zh":"他把掉落的樹枝堆到角落裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-915f919652f6cb59","term":"heap","forms":["heap","heaps","heaping","heaped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"大量給予","explanation":"從把東西堆起來引申，heap 可以把讚美、批評等抽象內容大量“堆”到某人身上，表示給予很多。","examples":[{"en":"The coach heaped praise on the young team.","zh":"教練對這支年輕隊伍大加讚揚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reviewers heaped praise on her debut novel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49000c4444d51233fa10","word":"hear","forms":["hear"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aab96ca437be0aa6","term":"hear","forms":["hear","hears","hearing","heard"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聽見聲音","explanation":"指耳朵接收到聲音，強調“聽到了”這一結果，而不是主動把注意力集中在聲音上。","examples":[{"en":"I could hear rain tapping on the window.","zh":"我能聽見雨點敲打窗戶的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you hear the music from outside?","zh":"你能聽見外面的音樂嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23d18c6065685029","term":"hear","forms":["hear","hears","hearing","heard"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聽見並辨認出","explanation":"不僅是聽到聲音，還能辨認出是誰、是什麼，或聽到某人正在說什麼、做什麼。","examples":[{"en":"We heard someone knock at the door.","zh":"我們聽見有人敲門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I heard her voice above the crowd.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-918edf8f60082cf7","term":"hear","forms":["hear","hears","hearing","heard"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聽取；聽某人說","explanation":"表示主動把注意力放到某人的話或某段內容上，認真聽取，而不只是碰巧聽見聲音。","examples":[{"en":"Please hear me out before you make a decision.","zh":"請先聽我把話說完，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager agreed to hear our concerns.","zh":"經理同意聽取我們的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3cb968a982080be1d7a5","word":"heart","forms":["heart"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0365d33d4e0e4033","term":"heart","forms":["heart","hearts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心臟","explanation":"heart 首先是把血液泵遍全身的肌肉器官；英語裡也常把它看作感情所在的身體中心。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor listened to my heart.","zh":"醫生聽了我的心臟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise helps keep your heart healthy.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於保持心臟健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-492e2d9f5083b4de","term":"heart","forms":["heart","hearts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內心感情","explanation":"從跳動的心臟引申而來，heart 可以指一個人的感情和情緒，尤其是被看作性格一部分的內心。","examples":[{"en":"She has a warm heart and always helps her neighbors.","zh":"她心地熱誠，總是幫助鄰居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In his heart, he knew the decision was right.","zh":"他心裡知道這個決定是對的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ee79e09cf095cd5","term":"heart","forms":["heart","hearts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中心與核心","explanation":"心臟位於身體的中心並維持生命，所以 heart 可比喻某件事最重要、最本質的部分，即“核心”或“中心”。","examples":[{"en":"Trust is at the heart of a good friendship.","zh":"信任是良好友誼的核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This question goes to the heart of the problem.","zh":"這個問題觸及了問題的核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac5f83a355e1274fb64a","word":"hearty","forms":["hearty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de9594c1290377ab","term":"hearty","forms":["hearty","heartier","heartiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱情真摯的","explanation":"形容對別人熱情、誠懇而真摯，尤其常表示熱烈歡迎、支援或祝賀。它讓人感覺這種態度不是客套，而是發自內心的。","examples":[{"en":"The new students received a hearty welcome from the whole class.","zh":"新生們受到了全班同學的熱烈歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave her hearty support to the community project.","zh":"她全心全意地支援這個社群專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hearty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59808d9ba6f4fec0","term":"hearty","forms":["hearty","heartier","heartiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精力充沛的；熱切的","explanation":"形容人或身體狀態很有活力、積極主動，也可以表示胃口很旺盛。核心感覺是“有足夠的心力和體力去做事或享用食物”。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, everyone had a hearty appetite.","zh":"長途徒步後，大家的胃口都很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hearty volunteers worked until sunset.","zh":"這些精力充沛的志願者一直工作到日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hearty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1b50705383a1794","term":"hearty","forms":["hearty","heartier","heartiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"豐盛有營養的","explanation":"形容食物分量足、能補充體力，通常讓人覺得吃完後更有力氣。它強調滋養和飽足，不只是味道好或熱量高。","examples":[{"en":"We prepared a hearty meal for the tired workers.","zh":"我們為疲憊的工人準備了一頓豐盛有營養的飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A hearty stew awaited the returning hikers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hearty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a2a0ed9aa3ab7d82b53","word":"heat","forms":["heat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-465e09c6ea9bf150","term":"heat","forms":["heat","heats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱能","explanation":"指能夠使物體升溫的熱能，是物理學中的“熱”，不等同於溫度本身。","examples":[{"en":"The metal absorbs heat from the fire.","zh":"這種金屬從火中吸收熱能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heat moves from the warmer object to the cooler one.","zh":"熱能會從較熱的物體傳向較冷的物體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be5aee1401feba7a","term":"heat","forms":["heat","heats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高溫；炎熱","explanation":"指處於很熱的狀態，尤其指天氣、陽光或環境帶來的炎熱。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed inside to escape the afternoon heat.","zh":"我們待在室內躲避下午的炎熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heat from the pavement made the walk exhausting.","zh":"路面的熱氣讓這次步行累人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-028932fb49689d7b","term":"heat","forms":["heat","heats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情緒或局勢的激烈狀態","explanation":"指情緒、爭論或行動達到很強烈、很緊張的程度；“在熱頭上”也可表示人在衝動狀態中。","examples":[{"en":"In the heat of the argument, she said something she regretted.","zh":"爭論最激烈時，她說了句後來後悔的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team kept playing well despite the heat of the competition.","zh":"儘管競爭激烈，這支隊伍仍然發揮得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b11311dbee7401d","term":"heat","forms":["heat","heats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暖氣系統","explanation":"指給房間或建築物升溫的供暖系統，尤其是家中或建築裡的暖氣裝置。","examples":[{"en":"Could you turn on the heat? The baby is cold.","zh":"你能把暖氣開啟嗎？寶寶冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heat stopped working last night.","zh":"暖氣昨晚壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5a62014297d31ab","term":"heat","forms":["heat","heats","heating","heated","het"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加熱；使變熱","explanation":"指讓物體或空間升高溫度，常常讓它變熱起來。","examples":[{"en":"Heat the oil in a large pan before adding the onions.","zh":"加入洋蔥前，先在大鍋裡把油加熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’ll heat up the leftovers for lunch.","zh":"我會把剩菜加熱一下當午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbe81278780d62460410","word":"heater","forms":["heater"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74a33f179fe1db72","term":"heater","forms":["heater","heaters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"取暖器；加熱器","explanation":"heater 是把熱量產生並散發出來、用來提高房間或建築溫度的裝置，例如電暖器、暖氣裝置等。日常對話裡說“開 heater”，通常就是讓室內暖起來。","examples":[{"en":"Turn on the heater; I'm cold.","zh":"把暖氣開啟，我冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heater in my office stopped working.","zh":"我辦公室裡的取暖器壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f846d7683994b395","term":"heater","forms":["heater","heaters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高速球","explanation":"在棒球俚語中，heater 指速度特別快、令擊球手難以應對的快速球；球像一股猛衝過來的“熱力”。","examples":[{"en":"The pitcher threw a heater past the batter.","zh":"投手投出一個高速球，球從擊球手身旁掠過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pitcher surprised him with a high heater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-818efe46a6c2ddb95df1","word":"heaven","forms":["heaven"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3e0aaf34143bd1a","term":"heaven","forms":["heaven","heavens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天空","explanation":"heaven 最早的核心畫面就是頭頂上高遠的天空，尤其是太陽、月亮和星星所在的廣闊空間。現代英語中說普通天空更常用 sky，因此 heaven 的這個義項常帶有詩意、古舊或較正式的色彩。","examples":[{"en":"Bright stars filled the evening heaven.","zh":"明亮的星星佈滿了傍晚的天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dark clouds gathered across the heavens.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heaven","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-451fa2080230ae77","term":"heaven","forms":["heaven","heavens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神或諸神的居所","explanation":"在宗教想象中，頭頂的高天被看成神或諸神居住的地方，於是 heaven 從“天空”發展出“天堂”這一核心宗教義。","examples":[{"en":"The painting shows angels rising toward heaven.","zh":"這幅畫描繪了天使向天堂升去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prayed that her father would go to Heaven.","zh":"她祈禱父親能進入天堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heaven","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11db49793cf4e896","term":"heaven","forms":["heaven","heavens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"死後有福者的居所","explanation":"heaven 也專指善者或蒙福者死後的幸福歸宿，通常與 hell 形成對照。這是“神聖居所”義進一步聚焦到來世的用法。","examples":[{"en":"They believe that the faithful will meet again in heaven.","zh":"他們相信虔誠的人會在天堂再次相聚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were taught that heaven is the opposite of hell.","zh":"孩子們被教導說，天堂與地獄相對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heaven","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22d5925ed64680ab5f3f","word":"heavy","forms":["heavy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff08a16e5b24280e","term":"heavy","forms":["heavy","heavier","heaviest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"重量大的","explanation":"核心是“重量很大”：物體拿起來費力，或需要較大力氣才能搬動、支撐。","examples":[{"en":"This suitcase is too heavy for me to lift alone.","zh":"這個手提箱太重了，我一個人搬不起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box looked small, but it was surprisingly heavy.","zh":"這個箱子看起來不大，卻出奇地重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heavy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a07cf506f4a0f5b","term":"heavy","forms":["heavy","heavier","heaviest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難以承受的；負擔重的","explanation":"事情或責任像有很大重量一樣壓在人身上，表示難以承受、負擔沉重或令人壓迫。","examples":[{"en":"The heavy cost of treatment put the family under great pressure.","zh":"高昂的治療費用給這個家庭帶來了很大壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carried the heavy responsibility of caring for her younger brothers.","zh":"她承擔著照顧弟弟們的沉重責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heavy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2216ac9a9d8efe5","term":"heavy","forms":["heavy","heavier","heaviest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聲音大而強烈的","explanation":"把“重量很大”引申為聲音、音樂或效果衝擊力強，可能音量大、失真重或整體強烈。","examples":[{"en":"My brother listens to heavy metal, but I prefer quiet acoustic music.","zh":"我哥哥喜歡聽重金屬音樂，但我更喜歡安靜的原聲音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band’s heavy sound filled the small room.","zh":"樂隊強烈的聲音充滿了這個小房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heavy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97fe21bcd36ae81c1cb0","word":"hedge","forms":["hedge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c4ae0b05be5c442","term":"hedge","forms":["hedge","hedges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樹籬；灌木圍欄","explanation":"指種在土地邊界或花園分隔處的一排灌木，作用像一道植物圍欄。這是 hedge 最具體、最容易連線到其他義項的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We trim the hedge every Saturday.","zh":"我們每週六修剪樹籬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tall hedge separates the two gardens.","zh":"一道高高的樹籬把兩個花園隔開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hedge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-481db509346da5ad","term":"hedge","forms":["hedge","hedges","hedging","hedged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用樹籬圍住","explanation":"表示給田地、花園等周圍種上或設定樹籬，把它們圍起來。它是名詞“樹籬”直接變成動作的用法。","examples":[{"en":"They hedged the garden to keep the dogs out.","zh":"他們用樹籬把花園圍起來，不讓狗進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They hedged the vegetable plot to keep animals out.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hedge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-760ec6dee3a069ba","term":"hedge","forms":["hedge","hedges","hedging","hedged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"含糊其辭；避免承諾","explanation":"表示說話時故意不把立場說死，用模糊或保留的措辭給自己留出迴旋空間。這裡的“圍”從現實邊界變成了圍住自己的承諾範圍。","examples":[{"en":"When asked about the deadline, the manager hedged and gave no firm date.","zh":"經理被問到截止日期時含糊其辭，沒有給出確切日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hedged her answer by saying that the plan was still under review.","zh":"她說計劃仍在審查中，以此讓自己的回答留有餘地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hedge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aee12eebcac8ca0bab74","word":"heel","forms":["heel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2e201d677388d88","term":"heel","forms":["heel","heels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腳後跟","explanation":"腳和小腿連線處後方、承受身體重量的部位；可以把它想成身體後方用來支撐和帶動方向的點。","examples":[{"en":"My left heel hurts after the long walk.","zh":"走了很久以後，我的左腳後跟疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She landed heavily on her heels.","zh":"她重重地用腳後跟著地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adffb7518f4e8e90","term":"heel","forms":["heel","heels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞋跟","explanation":"鞋底支撐腳後跟的部分；它正是把腳的“後跟”托住的鞋子部位。","examples":[{"en":"The heel of my right shoe is coming loose.","zh":"我右腳鞋子的鞋跟快要脫落了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These boots have low, sturdy heels.","zh":"這雙靴子的鞋跟低而結實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51c56780806c72d2","term":"heel","forms":["heel","heels","heeling","heeled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緊跟在後面","explanation":"讓人或動物緊緊跟在某人的後跟後面，突出距離很近、幾乎不離開。也常用於對狗下達“跟著我、別亂跑”的指令。","examples":[{"en":"The puppy was trained to heel beside its owner.","zh":"這隻小狗被訓練得緊跟在主人身邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heel, Max!","zh":"麥克斯，跟上！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4213651dff2c989","term":"heel","forms":["heel","heels","heeling","heeled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向一側傾斜","explanation":"指船或其他整體向左、右一側歪斜，就像後部的支撐點帶偏了整個物體。它強調姿態發生傾斜，不一定表示物體已經倒下。","examples":[{"en":"The boat heeled sharply when a strong gust hit the sails.","zh":"一陣強風吹動船帆時，船身猛地向一側傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The yacht heeled sharply in the gust.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39e0f5efdc39ec109928","word":"height","forms":["height"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e2d38a9480a6850","term":"height","forms":["height","heights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"從底部到頂部的距離","explanation":"height 是沿豎直方向從物體底部量到頂部的距離，也就是通常所說的“高度”。它既可以描述建築物、樹木等實體，也可以描述某個物體本身有多高。","examples":[{"en":"The height of the tower is nearly one hundred meters.","zh":"這座塔的高度將近一百米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We measured the height of the doorway before buying the furniture.","zh":"買傢俱前，我們測量了門口的高度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/height","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a73dda52babfac6b","term":"height","forms":["height","heights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高於基準面的高度","explanation":"這裡關注的不是物體本身有多高，而是某人、某物或飛機離地面、海平面等選定基準面有多高。它仍然是“豎直距離”這個核心概念，只是起點換成了一個基準面。","examples":[{"en":"The aircraft was flying at a height of ten thousand meters.","zh":"飛機正在一萬米的高度飛行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village stands at a height of two thousand meters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/height","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3967aaa26326d629","term":"height","forms":["height","heights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高峰；頂峰","explanation":"從豎直線的頂端，height 進一步引申為某件事達到的最高點或最興盛階段，例如事業、權力、成功或情緒的頂峰。這個義項保留了“向上達到最高處”的核心畫面，但物件變成了抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"At the height of his career, he was performing to packed theaters every night.","zh":"在事業巔峰時期，他每晚都在座無虛席的劇院裡演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She left the company at the height of her success.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/height","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-948ad152cccd31975dd6","word":"heighten","forms":["heighten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb2ff6595e489cff","term":"heighten","forms":["heighten","heightens","heightening","heightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"增強；加劇","explanation":"把某種感覺、情緒、效果或特徵推向更高的程度，使它變得更強烈、更明顯。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden silence heightened the tension in the room.","zh":"突然的寂靜加劇了房間裡的緊張氣氛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The music heightened the emotional impact of the final scene.","zh":"音樂增強了最後一幕的情感衝擊力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0522a7c161e6a97","term":"heighten","forms":["heighten","heightens","heightening","heightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加高；抬高","explanation":"把牆、橋或其他實體結構再向上加高，使它達到更高的位置或高度。","examples":[{"en":"The city plans to heighten the flood walls before the rainy season.","zh":"這座城市計劃在雨季前加高防洪牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They heightened the wall to improve security.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f85ba2b6d876dfc4a2e2","word":"heir","forms":["heir"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9406b3e9a796c821","term":"heir","forms":["heir","heirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財產繼承人","explanation":"指依法或按遺囑繼承他人財產的人，也可以指已經被指定為未來繼承人的人。重點不在財產多少，而在“接過別人留下的東西”這一關係。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is the heir to our grandmother's house.","zh":"我姐姐是祖母那所房子的繼承人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became the sole heir to his uncle's estate.","zh":"他成了叔叔遺產的唯一繼承人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a81750df7c2e9452","term":"heir","forms":["heir","heirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭銜或職位的繼承人","explanation":"指將要繼承世襲頭銜、王位或類似職位的人。這裡繼承的不是普通財產，而是一個具有身份和權力的家族或制度位置。","examples":[{"en":"The young prince is heir to the throne.","zh":"這位年輕王子是王位繼承人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As heir to the dukedom, she inherited extensive ceremonial duties.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbde83173a31f4f2f91f","word":"helicopter","forms":["helicopter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b91258723237ece1","term":"helicopter","forms":["helicopter","helicopters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直升機","explanation":"一種靠旋轉葉片升空、能懸停並向前後左右移動的飛行器。這是 helicopter 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We flew over the city in a helicopter.","zh":"我們乘直升機飛過了這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue helicopter landed near the mountain hut.","zh":"救援直升機降落在山間小屋附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/helicopter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ebdc3317b75839f6433","word":"hell","forms":["hell"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d4473cc0c50499b","term":"hell","forms":["hell","hells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極度痛苦的處境","explanation":"把現實中的生活、工作或某個地方比作地獄，表示那裡令人極其痛苦或難以忍受。","examples":[{"en":"The last few weeks at work have been hell.","zh":"最近幾周的工作簡直像地獄一樣難熬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long journey became a living hell.","zh":"這段漫長的旅程變成了活生生的地獄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e8","word":"hello","forms":["hello"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bfbf63e8d38d0e3b","term":"hello","forms":["hello","hellos","helloes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次問候","explanation":"作為名詞，hello 指說出 hello 這樣的一次招呼或問候，例如“向某人打個招呼”。它把“問候”看成一個具體的交流動作。","examples":[{"en":"Please say hello to your family for me.","zh":"請代我向你的家人問好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He waved a friendly hello from across the street.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hello","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-115584860cd5620e40fd","word":"helmet","forms":["helmet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6acb344896ec4604","term":"helmet","forms":["helmet","helmets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭盔","explanation":"一種堅硬的頭部覆蓋物，用來保護頭部；它可以是盔甲的一部分，也可以是騎車、施工或運動時使用的安全裝備。","examples":[{"en":"You must wear a helmet when riding a bicycle.","zh":"騎腳踏車時必須戴頭盔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firefighter put on his helmet before entering the building.","zh":"消防員進入大樓前戴上了頭盔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/helmet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dece39a4ac61f50a","term":"helmet","forms":["helmet","helmets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭盔狀的東西","explanation":"指形狀、位置或覆蓋方式像頭盔的東西：它不一定真能保護頭部，但看起來像一個扣在上面的硬殼或罩子。","examples":[{"en":"Her thick black hair formed a smooth helmet around her head.","zh":"她濃密的黑髮在頭部周圍形成了一個光滑的頭盔狀輪廓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flower's upper petal forms a purple helmet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/helmet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-106a5842fc5fce6f6631","word":"help","forms":["help"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4e88c5d6bcfa75d","term":"help","forms":["help","helps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫助；援助","explanation":"為了讓某人完成事情、擺脫困難或解決問題而提供的援助，是名詞 help 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I need some help with my homework.","zh":"我的家庭作業需要一些幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your help made the move much easier.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/help","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9230dc8e661a9027","term":"help","forms":["help","helps","helping","helped","holp","holpen","helpest","helpedst","helpeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"幫助某人或某物","explanation":"主動提供力量、時間、知識或行動，使某人或某物更容易完成任務或解決問題。","examples":[{"en":"Can you help me carry these boxes?","zh":"你能幫我搬這些箱子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you help my father carry these bags?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/help","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc1560162a8e60eb","term":"help","forms":["help","helps","helping","helped","holp","holpen","helpest","helpedst","helpeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"幫忙","explanation":"不說明具體幫助物件或內容，只表示主動提供援助；常用於回應請求或提出幫忙。","examples":[{"en":"I saw her carrying too many bags and offered to help.","zh":"我看到她提著太多袋子，就主動提出幫忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you help carry these boxes upstairs?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/help","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77f13b846efe9402","term":"help","forms":["help","helps","helping","helped","holp","holpen","helpest","helpedst","helpeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忍不住；無法避免","explanation":"在否定或疑問語境中，表示人無法控制自己不去做某事，或無法避免注意到某事；核心仍是“無法把反應控制住”。","examples":[{"en":"I couldn't help laughing at his impression of the teacher.","zh":"我忍不住笑了，因為他模仿老師的樣子太逗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I couldn't help laughing at the puppy's antics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/help","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8678e47531eae3d20215","word":"helpful","forms":["helpful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65e77dc1849bc249","term":"helpful","forms":["helpful","more helpful","most helpful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有幫助的；有用的","explanation":"指某人提供了實際幫助，或某個資訊、建議、工具能讓事情更容易完成、讓問題更容易解決。它既可以形容人，也可以形容線索、說明、建議等具體內容。","examples":[{"en":"This guide was very helpful when I was setting up the printer.","zh":"我設定印表機時，這份指南幫了很大的忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a helpful clue about where to look.","zh":"她給了我一個很有用的線索，告訴我該去哪裡找。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/helpful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04195d8a8cbcfd0a6855","word":"hemisphere","forms":["hemisphere"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-941c47f4ec3de8c3","term":"hemisphere","forms":["hemisphere","hemispheres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地球半球","explanation":"指地球被某條經過中心的分界線分成的一半，例如北半球、南半球、東半球和西半球。日常和新聞中最常見的是表示地理區域的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Australia lies mainly in the Southern Hemisphere.","zh":"澳大利亞大部分位於南半球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Summer begins in the Northern Hemisphere in June.","zh":"北半球在六月開始進入夏季。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hemisphere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-566bedea8adae629","term":"hemisphere","forms":["hemisphere","hemispheres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幾何半球","explanation":"在幾何學中，指一個平面經過球心，把球切成的任意一半。這個定義是其他許多用法的基礎：重點是“從球心切開的半邊”。","examples":[{"en":"The bowl is shaped like a hemisphere.","zh":"這個碗呈半球形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plane through the center divides the sphere into two hemispheres.","zh":"經過球心的平面把球分成兩個半球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hemisphere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d44a08de3981889dae0f","word":"hen","forms":["hen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2ebdbab81e9191f","term":"hen","forms":["hen","hens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"母雞","explanation":"指成年雌性雞，尤其是飼養來下蛋的母雞。這是hen最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The hens are laying eggs in the coop.","zh":"母雞正在雞舍裡下蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We keep six hens in the backyard.","zh":"我們在後院養了六隻母雞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec758eedf4a9ddf8","term":"hen","forms":["hen","hens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雌鳥","explanation":"可泛指某些鳥類中已經成年的雌性個體，尤其用於和雄鳥作比較。","examples":[{"en":"The hen stayed near the nest while the male searched for food.","zh":"雄鳥尋找食物時，雌鳥一直守在巢附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hen pheasant hid her chicks in the grass.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44a53f8fca870ba0619e","word":"hence","forms":["hence"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a71a34b4f251be7","term":"hence","forms":["hence"],"pos":"adv","zh":"因此，由此","explanation":"表示前面的事實或原因自然推出後面的結果，相當於“因此、由此”。這是現代英語中最值得優先掌握的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The roads were flooded, hence the delay.","zh":"道路被水淹了，因此耽擱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She missed the train and hence arrived late.","zh":"她沒趕上火車，因此遲到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a476eb71d4b3a03c","term":"hence","forms":["hence"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從現在起……以後","explanation":"表示從現在起經過某段時間之後，仍然保留了“向前走”的時間意象。","examples":[{"en":"Five years hence, the town may look completely different.","zh":"五年以後，這座城鎮可能會完全不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ten years hence, this sapling will shade the terrace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25852c87d6e47fb8d7d5","word":"herb","forms":["herb"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdb44914c343a1f1","term":"herb","forms":["herb","herbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調味香草","explanation":"指用新鮮或乾燥的葉子、莖等給食物增加味道的綠色植物，例如羅勒、薄荷、歐芹等。這裡重點是廚房中的調味用途，不一定有藥用作用。","examples":[{"en":"Add fresh herbs to the soup just before serving.","zh":"上桌前再把新鮮香草加入湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sauce gets its flavor from basil and other herbs.","zh":"這種醬汁的味道來自羅勒和其他香草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c400e8ace8ff2ae","term":"herb","forms":["herb","herbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥草","explanation":"指根、葉、種子等部分被用於藥物或傳統治療的植物。它強調植物的醫療用途，不只是指普通的綠色植物。","examples":[{"en":"The village healer used several herbs to treat the fever.","zh":"村裡的治療者用幾種藥草治療發燒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The healer cultivated herbs beside her cottage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5527e537a2771ec638e8","word":"herd","forms":["herd"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b839335196920a0","term":"herd","forms":["herd","herds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獸群；畜群","explanation":"herd 指聚在一起、由人照看或所有的一群家畜，尤其常指牛、羊等。核心畫面就是許多動物聚成一團一起行動。","examples":[{"en":"A herd of cattle was resting near the river.","zh":"一群牛正在河邊休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer counted his herd before sunset.","zh":"農夫在日落前數了數自己的牛群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b3eda44ae90e365","term":"herd","forms":["herd","herds","herding","herded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成群驅趕；被集中帶走","explanation":"herd 還可表示讓動物或人以群體形式移動，常常是把他們集中起來並帶到某個地方。說人時通常暗示他們缺少自主選擇，像被趕著走一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The passengers were herded through a narrow gate.","zh":"乘客們被集中趕過一道狹窄的門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The keeper herded the elephants back to their enclosure.","zh":"飼養員把大象群趕回了圍欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcec91509759ad995c2c","word":"here","forms":["here"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de3a41eb366fcaf7","term":"here","forms":["here"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在這裡","explanation":"指人或物位於說話者認為靠近自己的這個地方，和表示另一處的 there 相對。","examples":[{"en":"Your keys are here on the table.","zh":"你的鑰匙就在這張桌子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wait here until I come back.","zh":"請在這裡等我回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/here","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5586d4ce4109c9b","term":"here","forms":["here"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到這裡為止","explanation":"把“這裡”擴大為當前的程序或位置，表示事情在這一點停下，不再繼續。","examples":[{"en":"I think we should stop here for today.","zh":"我覺得我們今天就到這裡吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The evidence takes us here, but no further.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/here","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33840d062eb05df1","term":"here","forms":["here"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到這裡來","explanation":"表示朝說話者所在的地方移動，也就是從別處來到“這個圈子”裡。","examples":[{"en":"Come here and look at this picture.","zh":"到這裡來看看這張照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you bring the boxes here?","zh":"你能把這些箱子拿到這裡來嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/here","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67a7743cdaba48d61305","word":"heritage","forms":["heritage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0decfe9dd427d28","term":"heritage","forms":["heritage","heritages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可繼承的財產；遺產","explanation":"heritage 可以指一個人從前輩那裡繼承來的財產，強調這些東西原本屬於上一代，後來傳給了後代。","examples":[{"en":"She used her family heritage to restore the old house.","zh":"她利用家族留下的遺產修復了那座老房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum protects the heritage of the local community.","zh":"這座博物館保護著當地社群的遺產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heritage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0e6462c0f249452","term":"heritage","forms":["heritage","heritages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳統；傳承下來的價值","explanation":"heritage 也指家庭、群體或機構代代傳下來的傳統、做法和價值觀；這裡繼承的不是物品，而是共同保留的生活方式或記憶。","examples":[{"en":"The festival celebrates the musical heritage of the region.","zh":"這個節日慶祝該地區傳承下來的音樂文化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school is proud of its long educational heritage.","zh":"這所學校為自己悠久的教育傳統感到自豪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heritage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d02ce19b52553f55b301","word":"hero/heroine","forms":["hero","heroine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18036b1ad153131c","term":"hero","forms":["hero","heroes","heros"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英雄；勇者","explanation":"指具有很大勇氣，並做出非凡或高尚行為的人。這個詞強調擔當和行動，不一定表示有超能力。","examples":[{"en":"The firefighter became a hero after rescuing the family.","zh":"這名消防員救出那家人後成了英雄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was hailed as a hero for speaking up.","zh":"她因為勇敢發聲而被譽為英雄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hero","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f2d2eeb96d3e52a","term":"hero","forms":["hero","heroes","heros"],"pos":"noun","zh":"榜樣","explanation":"指值得別人尊敬和學習的人，不一定做過驚天動地的事情；重點是他的品格或行為具有示範作用。","examples":[{"en":"My grandmother has always been a hero to me.","zh":"我的祖母一直是我心中的榜樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My grandmother is my hero for returning to school at sixty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hero","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7826484fd286259","term":"hero","forms":["hero","heroes","heros"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主角","explanation":"指小說、電影、戲劇或其他虛構作品中推動故事發展的主要人物。這個人未必真正勇敢或品德高尚，只是故事圍繞他展開。","examples":[{"en":"The hero of the novel must choose between love and duty.","zh":"這部小說的主角必須在愛情和責任之間作出選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In this film, the hero is far from perfect.","zh":"在這部電影中，主角遠非完美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hero","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38a1ba41f01c01ac","term":"heroine","forms":["heroine","heroines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女英雄","explanation":"指因勇敢、犧牲或傑出行動而被視為英雄的女性。她可以是真實人物，也可以是虛構人物；重點是她具有英雄性的行動或品質。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse was hailed as a heroine after saving three children.","zh":"這名護士救了三個孩子後，被譽為女英雄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a national heroine for her courage.","zh":"她因勇敢而成為民族女英雄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heroine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-759da93a20396270","term":"heroine","forms":["heroine","heroines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女主角","explanation":"指故事、電影、戲劇或小說中最重要的女性角色。這裡的重點是她處於故事中心，不一定表示她本人英勇，所以她也可能是普通人、受害者或反英雄式人物。","examples":[{"en":"The heroine of the novel leaves her village to find her missing brother.","zh":"這部小說的女主角離開村子去尋找失蹤的哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel's heroine refuses the arranged marriage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heroine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b141a9e490f34259fb9","word":"heroic","forms":["heroic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f726f74cc9255601","term":"heroic","forms":["heroic","more heroic","most heroic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"英雄的；高尚非凡的","explanation":"指與英雄或女英雄有關，或者體現出英雄應有的高尚品質；重點在身份、形象或行為所具有的崇高意味。","examples":[{"en":"The museum tells the story of her heroic deeds.","zh":"這座博物館講述了她的英雄事蹟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel presents him as a heroic figure.","zh":"這部小說把他塑造成一個英雄式人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heroic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8c002b1c0f74a42","term":"heroic","forms":["heroic","more heroic","most heroic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"英勇的；表現出英雄氣概的","explanation":"指人在危險、困難或重大責任面前表現出非凡勇氣；它強調實際行動中的勇敢，而不只是“像英雄”這一形象。","examples":[{"en":"It was heroic of her to return to the burning house to save the child.","zh":"她冒險返回著火的房子救孩子，表現得十分英勇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volunteers made a heroic effort to keep the shelter open.","zh":"志願者們竭盡全力，英勇地維持收容所開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heroic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee6f01a92dd8063b3236","word":"heroin","forms":["heroin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59eb4a8f31d4f0e4","term":"heroin","forms":["heroin","heroins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海洛因","explanation":"一種由鴉片製成的強效毒品，會帶來強烈快感，但也很容易使人產生嚴重依賴；在世界大多數地方都屬於非法麻醉品。","examples":[{"en":"He became addicted to heroin after several years of drug use.","zh":"他吸毒幾年後染上了海洛因成癮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic offers treatment for people who are dependent on heroin.","zh":"這家診所為海洛因依賴者提供治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heroin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce8a390a4a5b7c85047f","word":"hesitate","forms":["hesitate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c173a6991de54cf0","term":"hesitate","forms":["hesitate","hesitates","hesitating","hesitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猶豫；遲疑","explanation":"人在決定或行動前像被卡住一樣，暫時邁不出下一步，因為不確定、擔心後果或拿不定主意。它不一定表示拒絕，只表示決定或行動被暫緩了。","examples":[{"en":"She hesitated before opening the letter.","zh":"她在開啟信之前猶豫了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you need help, don't hesitate to ask.","zh":"如果你需要幫助，儘管開口，不要猶豫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hesitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3883f1d2f94567e7","term":"hesitate","forms":["hesitate","hesitates","hesitating","hesitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說話結巴；吞吞吐吐","explanation":"“卡住”也可以發生在嘴上：說話者不能流暢地說下去，出現停頓、遲疑或吞吞吐吐的情況。","examples":[{"en":"He hesitated over the unfamiliar name and then pronounced it slowly.","zh":"他念到那個不熟悉的名字時遲疑了一下，然後慢慢把它讀了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hesitated over the unfamiliar name while reading aloud.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hesitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3e5918c39441096100c","word":"hesitation","forms":["hesitation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3a4415bf603b969","term":"hesitation","forms":["hesitation","hesitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猶豫的行為","explanation":"指人在採取行動前停下來考慮、沒有馬上做決定的行為，重點是“遲疑這一動作本身”。","examples":[{"en":"After a brief hesitation, Maya opened the door.","zh":"短暫猶豫後，瑪雅開啟了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her brief hesitation suggested that she had doubts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hesitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5c366ad3b4ebda8","term":"hesitation","forms":["hesitation","hesitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疑慮；舉棋不定","explanation":"指因為不確定、擔心或缺乏信心而在幾個選擇之間搖擺不定，常常暗示沒有堅定地採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"She accepted the offer without hesitation.","zh":"她毫不猶豫地接受了這個提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His hesitation made us wonder whether he agreed.","zh":"他的猶豫讓我們懷疑他是否同意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hesitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-445dec4377f02c1e594c","word":"heterosexual","forms":["heterosexual"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba9e5f5db8228a16","term":"heterosexual","forms":["heterosexual","more heterosexual","most heterosexual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"異性戀的","explanation":"指一個人在性方面被異性吸引，或與異性戀取向有關。這是描述性取向時最核心的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She identifies as heterosexual.","zh":"她認同自己是異性戀者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey asked about heterosexual and homosexual relationships.","zh":"這項調查詢問了異性戀和同性戀關係的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heterosexual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9195719226d3a990","term":"heterosexual","forms":["heterosexual","heterosexuals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"異性戀者","explanation":"指性方面主要被異性吸引的人；它是形容詞“heterosexual”名詞化後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Heterosexuals should also support equal rights for everyone.","zh":"異性戀者也應支援人人享有平等權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey included both heterosexuals and homosexuals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heterosexual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f5bb9791a310e136d15","word":"hide","forms":["hide"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef0f441cacbc2651","term":"hide","forms":["hide","hides","hiding","hid","hidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"藏起某物","explanation":"把東西放到不顯眼、不容易被發現的地方，就是給它找一個“遮住”的位置。","examples":[{"en":"She hid the spare key under a flowerpot.","zh":"她把備用鑰匙藏在了花盆下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please hide the gift before the children arrive.","zh":"孩子們到之前，請把禮物藏起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54760688f7b0e227","term":"hide","forms":["hide","hides","hiding","hid","hidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"躲起來","explanation":"把自己放到別人看不見或找不到的地方，就是讓自己被環境遮住。","examples":[{"en":"The child hid behind the curtain during the game.","zh":"遊戲時，孩子躲在窗簾後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hid from her brother in the garden.","zh":"她躲在花園裡，不讓哥哥找到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff88bf24065193426262","word":"hierarchy","forms":["hierarchy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a37e26402080894d","term":"hierarchy","forms":["hierarchy","hierarchies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"等級制度","explanation":"指社會、宗教、經濟、政治或組織中按地位、權力等把人或群體分成高低等級的制度或結構；這裡強調整套上下有別的安排，而不只是其中的成員。","examples":[{"en":"The company is trying to reduce its strict hierarchy.","zh":"這家公司正努力減少其森嚴的等級制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The army maintains a strict hierarchy of command.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hierarchy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5cca78ece1566dd","term":"hierarchy","forms":["hierarchy","hierarchies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物層級","explanation":"指把事物按上下級關係排列的結構：除最上層外，每一項都從屬於上面的某一項。例如資料夾可以分成主資料夾、子資料夾和更深的子資料夾。","examples":[{"en":"The website uses a clear hierarchy of menus and submenus.","zh":"這個網站採用了清晰的選單和子選單層級結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Organize the files in a clear hierarchy of folders.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hierarchy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ef7c9b15ecdd6908372","word":"high","forms":["high"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d12895678b2e6bc","term":"high","forms":["high","higher","highest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高的；在上方的","explanation":"表示人或物在空間中向上，位置高於地面、底部或通常水平；這就是把 high 記成“向上”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"A bright balloon floated high above the city.","zh":"一個鮮豔的氣球飄在城市上空很高的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shelves are too high for the children to reach.","zh":"這些架子太高，孩子們夠不著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6d9006a2dc02140","term":"high","forms":["high","higher","highest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"地位高的；重要的","explanation":"把空間上的“向上”引申到社會地位、聲望、重要性或發展水平，表示處於較高層次。","examples":[{"en":"She holds a high position in the company.","zh":"她在公司裡擔任要職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The award brought him high praise from critics.","zh":"這項獎讓他贏得了評論家的高度讚譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f458e36d8e0e1234","term":"high","forms":["high","highs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高點；高峰","explanation":"指實際位置上的高處，也指事業、成就或某段經歷中向上達到的高點，即最成功、最精彩的時刻。","examples":[{"en":"Winning the championship was one of the highs of her career.","zh":"贏得冠軍是她職業生涯中的高光時刻之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trail climbs to a high above the valley.","zh":"這條小路向上攀升到山谷上方的一處高地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc2c5be187f6f31e70a8","word":"highlight","forms":["highlight"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd5595c4e6c90a35","term":"highlight","forms":["highlight","highlights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"亮部；高光","explanation":"在畫、照片或其他影象中，受到強光照射、比周圍更亮的那一小塊就是highlight。它像畫面裡被光圈出來的部分，通常用來表現光澤或立體感。","examples":[{"en":"The highlights on the water made the photograph look alive.","zh":"水面上的高光讓這張照片顯得栩栩如生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A white highlight made the painted apple seem glossy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highlight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4996789ae7b9ec35","term":"highlight","forms":["highlight","highlights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"亮點；最精彩的部分","explanation":"某段經歷中最值得注意、最令人滿意的部分，也像被光照出來一樣，是highlight。它可以是一次活動、一個時刻、一件事，甚至是某段時期。","examples":[{"en":"The highlight of our weekend was the small concert in the park.","zh":"我們週末最精彩的部分是在公園裡聽那場小型音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The waterfall was the highlight of our trip.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highlight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd6d851c6631b7a9","term":"highlight","forms":["highlight","highlights","highlighting","highlighted","highlit"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強調；突出","explanation":"highlight某件事，就是把它像放在強光下一樣凸顯出來，讓讀者或聽者特別注意。賓語可以是事實、問題、特點、差異或某個重要部分。","examples":[{"en":"The report highlights the need for safer roads.","zh":"這份報告強調了建設更安全道路的必要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report highlights gaps in the training program.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highlight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-cbae973f3f0bc8203746","word":"highly","forms":["highly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2bbeb07d4bf4b02","term":"highly","forms":["highly","highlier","more highly","highliest","most highly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"高度地；很讚賞地","explanation":"指把某人或某事評價得很高，帶有明顯的讚賞或認可意味；也就是把評價“抬到高處”。","examples":[{"en":"The director spoke highly of her work.","zh":"導演高度評價了她的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is highly respected by her colleagues.","zh":"她深受同事們尊敬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43e5573eb41d0b4e","term":"highly","forms":["highly","highlier","more highly","highliest","most highly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"非常；極其","explanation":"表示程度被抬得很高，相當於“非常”或“極其”，常用來加強形容詞或過去分詞所表達的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"This position is highly visible within the organization.","zh":"這個職位在組織內部非常受關注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment is highly effective for many patients.","zh":"這種治療對許多患者非常有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5fa896b2fbacdfc6676d","word":"highway","forms":["highway"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1721bc1d52f85791","term":"highway","forms":["highway","highways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主要公路；高速公路","explanation":"指供公眾通行的主要道路，通常比普通街道更寬、更長，可能有多條車道並允許高速行駛。它是 highway 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We took the highway to the coast and arrived before sunset.","zh":"我們走沿海高速公路，在日落前到了那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Traffic is heavy on the highway this morning.","zh":"今天早上這條公路上的交通很擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64e3330f81d00548","term":"highway","forms":["highway","highways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通向目標的道路","explanation":"這裡把現實中的道路用作比喻，表示通往某種成就、結果或命運的途徑。","examples":[{"en":"Hard work can be a highway to success.","zh":"努力可以成為通往成功的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Education offered him a highway out of poverty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07a36500aabab91be1f8","word":"hijack","forms":["hijack"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce2b853374651da7","term":"hijack","forms":["hijack","hijacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劫持交通工具","explanation":"指非法強行奪取飛機、汽車、卡車或船隻等交通工具的控制權，通常為了搶劫或迫使其駛向指定地點。","examples":[{"en":"The hijacking of the bus ended when the police arrested the gunman.","zh":"警方逮捕持槍者後，這起公交車劫持事件結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gunmen attempted to hijack a passenger bus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hijack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c3e47f206320d03","term":"hijack","forms":["hijack","hijacks","hijacking","hijacked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"劫持交通工具","explanation":"指以武力或威脅強行控制飛機、汽車、卡車或船隻等交通工具，以便搶劫或將其駛往另一個地點。","examples":[{"en":"The criminals hijacked a truck carrying electronics.","zh":"罪犯劫持了一輛運送電子產品的卡車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Armed men hijacked a passenger bus near the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hijack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f98e3e40d3a565d5","term":"hijack","forms":["hijack","hijacks","hijacking","hijacked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強行把事情帶偏","explanation":"指奪取某個過程、節目、計劃或資源的控制權，使它不再服務於原本的目的，而改為服務自己的目的。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't hijack the discussion with a completely different issue.","zh":"請不要用一個完全不同的問題把討論帶偏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A personal crisis hijacked her plans for the summer.","zh":"一場個人危機打亂並改變了她夏天的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hijack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c02d7803a91c395845d5","word":"hike","forms":["hike"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3dfe02359d3aef2","term":"hike","forms":["hike","hikes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"徒步，遠足","explanation":"指為了鍛鍊或享受風景而進行的一段較長步行，通常比普通散步更有目的性或距離更遠。","examples":[{"en":"We went on a hike through the forest.","zh":"我們去森林裡徒步了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We planned a short hike around the lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6790c443dfebf079","term":"hike","forms":["hike","hikes","hiking","hiked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徒步，遠足","explanation":"指為了鍛鍊或消遣而走較長的路，強調持續移動和戶外步行活動。","examples":[{"en":"We’re hiking along the coast this weekend.","zh":"這個週末我們要沿著海岸徒步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hiked through pine forests all morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f77fcbb21ddefc82222a","word":"hill","forms":["hill"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2dfea4137459c16","term":"hill","forms":["hill","hills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小山丘","explanation":"hill指比山低小的自然隆起地形，核心畫面就是地面鼓起的一座小土丘。","examples":[{"en":"A wooded hill rises behind the village.","zh":"村子後面有一座長滿樹木的小山丘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stopped at the top of the hill to enjoy the view.","zh":"我們在山丘頂上停下來欣賞風景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0901484393b843f8","term":"hill","forms":["hill","hills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"坡道","explanation":"hill也可以指道路上的上坡或下坡，重點不在整座地形，而在道路的傾斜段。","examples":[{"en":"The bicycle slowed down as we climbed the hill.","zh":"我們騎車上坡時，車速慢了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclist struggled up the long hill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b80e0af617d0f8ff54ab","word":"hint","forms":["hint"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6270f56c8df7c41","term":"hint","forms":["hint","hints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"線索；提示","explanation":"能幫助你找到答案或理解事情方向的一點資訊，就像輕輕把你推向正確答案，而不是直接把答案說出來。","examples":[{"en":"Could you give me a hint for the last crossword clue?","zh":"你能給我最後一道填字遊戲線索的提示嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map gave us a hint about which road to take.","zh":"這張地圖給了我們該走哪條路的線索。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7d98e00037f8fb2","term":"hint","forms":["hint","hints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暗示","explanation":"說話人不把意思直接說出來，只透露一點，讓聽者自己領會。例如不直接說對方口氣不好，而是委婉地讓他注意。","examples":[{"en":"She dropped a hint that she wanted a quieter room.","zh":"她暗示自己想要一間更安靜的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her pointed glance was a hint to leave.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e8a7a767000da89","term":"hint","forms":["hint","hints","hinting","hinted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暗示；提示","explanation":"透過一句不完整的話、一個細節或間接說法，把方向透露給別人，讓對方自己推出真正意思。","examples":[{"en":"He hinted that the meeting might be canceled.","zh":"他暗示會議可能會取消。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach hinted at changes to the starting lineup.","zh":"教練暗示首發陣容會有變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd805812f2fd7ff1476c","word":"hip","forms":["hip"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96ad3a622efb8c71","term":"hip","forms":["hip","hips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"髖部","explanation":"身體兩側骨盆與大腿相接的部位，外面通常能摸到向外突出的髖骨；日常語境中也常泛指這一帶。","examples":[{"en":"I hurt my left hip while playing tennis.","zh":"我打網球時傷到了左髖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carried the baby on her hip.","zh":"她把嬰兒抱在髖部旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aadc9b93941caf82bc2d","word":"hippopotamus/hippo","forms":["hippo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad847f3358e0f038","term":"hippo","forms":["hippo","hippos","HiPPOs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"河馬的簡稱","explanation":"這是 hippopotamus 的常用非正式簡稱，指生活在水邊、體型很大的河馬。它保留了原詞的核心動物意義，只是說法更短、更口語化。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a hippo resting in the river.","zh":"我們看見一頭河馬在河裡休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hippo opened its mouth wide.","zh":"那頭河馬張大了嘴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hippo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf90ace460be66498a91","word":"hire","forms":["hire"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-470179afbef13a37","term":"hire","forms":["hire","hires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新僱員","explanation":"hire 可以指被僱來工作的人，尤其常指剛加入團隊的新員工；這是“付錢請人來工作”這個核心概念的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The manager introduced the new hires to the team.","zh":"經理把新員工介紹給了團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The latest hire joins our design team on Monday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1f4b0c54fe4f682","term":"hire","forms":["hire","hires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"租用費","explanation":"hire 可以指臨時使用某物所付的費用，也就是“付錢借用一段時間”的費用。它和動詞“租用”來自同一個核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Bicycles are available for hire near the station.","zh":"車站附近有腳踏車出租。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bicycle hire includes a helmet and lock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a53d340b2f41466","term":"hire","forms":["hire","hires","hiring","hired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"租用物品","explanation":"hire 可以表示付錢臨時取得汽車、裝置等物品的使用權，也就是“租用”。這和“付錢請來一段時間”的核心畫面完全一致。","examples":[{"en":"We hired a van for the weekend.","zh":"我們租了一輛麵包車過週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hired bicycles to explore the island.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10096c396ad0f482","term":"hire","forms":["hire","hires","hiring","hired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"僱用人","explanation":"hire 最核心的動詞義之一是付錢請某人工作，即“僱用、錄用”。僱主取得的是對方一段時間的勞動服務，而不是擁有這個人。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant hired two cooks before summer.","zh":"那家餐館在夏季前僱用了兩名廚師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hired a technician to fix the machine.","zh":"我們請了一名技術員來修理機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-604c00db87b22994f944","word":"historian","forms":["historian"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0c0775d0aa4b806","term":"historian","forms":["historian","historians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歷史撰寫者","explanation":"指把過去的事件和社會整理、分析並寫成歷史的人，重點在正式記錄和解釋歷史。","examples":[{"en":"The historian spent ten years writing about the city's medieval past.","zh":"這位歷史學家花了十年時間撰寫這座城市的中世紀曆史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A respected historian challenged the traditional account of the war.","zh":"一位受尊敬的歷史學家對這場戰爭的傳統敘述提出了質疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35a0cbfee7d8f17c","term":"historian","forms":["historian","historians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歷史研究者","explanation":"泛指研究歷史資料、人物和社會變化的人；不一定已經出版歷史著作，強調的是對歷史的系統研究。","examples":[{"en":"Historians are still debating why the empire collapsed.","zh":"歷史學家們仍在爭論這個帝國為什麼會崩潰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The historian compared diaries with official military records.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c4824ae8bb216f860ca4","word":"historic","forms":["historic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-301b24824339a3d7","term":"historic","forms":["historic","more historic","most historic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"歷史性的；重大而值得紀念的","explanation":"指一件事重要到可能被寫進歷史、被後人記住。它不只是發生在過去，而是強調這件事本身具有重大意義。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement was a historic step toward peace.","zh":"這項協議是邁向和平的歷史性一步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team made a historic comeback in the final.","zh":"這支隊伍在決賽中完成了一次載入史冊的逆轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dafa9c530767d46","term":"historic","forms":["historic","more historic","most historic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"歷史上的；與過去有關的","explanation":"在較少見或較正式的用法中，historic 可近似 historical，表示與有記錄的歷史或一般過去有關。它不一定表示事件本身特別重大。","examples":[{"en":"The museum preserves historic records of the region.","zh":"這座博物館儲存著該地區的歷史記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive preserves historic photographs of the harbor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5dbf9fe930c4f499bc6","word":"historical","forms":["historical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab65331e6f9f30b5","term":"historical","forms":["historical","more historical","most historical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與已記錄的歷史有關","explanation":"表示某人、某事或某項研究屬於真實記錄中的歷史，而不是傳說、神話或虛構。","examples":[{"en":"The museum contains many historical documents.","zh":"這座博物館收藏著許多歷史文獻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers are checking the historical record.","zh":"研究人員正在查閱歷史記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42fbf640b13b9b93","term":"historical","forms":["historical","more historical","most historical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與過去一般有關","explanation":"把範圍從正式的歷史記錄擴大到過去發生的事情；凡是用於談論過去及其背景的內容，都可能用 historical 修飾。","examples":[{"en":"The tour gives visitors some historical background.","zh":"這次參觀為遊客介紹了一些歷史背景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building has great historical importance.","zh":"這座建築具有很大的歷史重要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-259aa8ef98a8b91de574","word":"history","forms":["history"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd9eb9ec3a261393","term":"history","forms":["history","histories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過去發生的一切","explanation":"指已經發生過的全部事件，重點在“過去的事情本身”，不一定強調誰來研究或記錄。它可以涵蓋個人、社會乃至全人類的過去。","examples":[{"en":"The history of this city reaches back more than a thousand years.","zh":"這座城市的歷史可以追溯到一千多年前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People often repeat the same mistakes throughout history.","zh":"縱觀歷史，人們常常重複同樣的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/history","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26c631e756af8a59","term":"history","forms":["history","histories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歷史學；對過去的研究","explanation":"指透過資料和證據研究、判斷並說明過去事件的學科，不只是把故事講出來，也區別於神話或純文學作品。","examples":[{"en":"She is studying the history of migration at university.","zh":"她正在大學裡研究移民史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good history depends on careful use of evidence.","zh":"紮實的歷史學依靠對證據的謹慎使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/history","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63d04dee7c50f6fb1202","word":"hit","forms":["hit"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-291599497fa43e4d","term":"hit","forms":["hit","hits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擊打；碰撞","explanation":"指一次擊打、拳打，或兩個物體相互碰撞；核心畫面就是某物碰上了目標。","examples":[{"en":"The boxer landed a clean hit on his opponent's shoulder.","zh":"這名拳擊手乾淨利落地擊中了對手的肩膀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vase broke after a hard hit against the wall.","zh":"花瓶狠狠撞到牆上後碎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-209f117308621980","term":"hit","forms":["hit","hits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱門成功作品","explanation":"指歌曲、電影、遊戲等非常成功並廣受認可的作品，就像它“命中”了大眾口味。","examples":[{"en":"The singer's first single was an unexpected hit.","zh":"這位歌手的第一首單曲意外地大獲成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That comedy became a hit with families.","zh":"那部喜劇很受家庭觀眾歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-139971e06aedcec7","term":"hit","forms":["hit","hits","hitting","hat","het","hitten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擊打","explanation":"表示用手、拳頭或其他物體碰撞並打到某人或某物，是“碰上並命中”這一記憶線索最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The ball hit the window and broke it.","zh":"球撞上窗戶，把窗戶打碎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hit his brother during the argument.","zh":"爭吵時他打了他的弟弟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e5a08c2bdd2c6ba","term":"hit","forms":["hit","hits","hitting","hat","het","hitten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開關燈","explanation":"在口語中表示開啟或關閉燈，動作上可理解為碰一下開關就讓燈亮起或熄滅。","examples":[{"en":"Please hit the lights when you leave the room.","zh":"你離開房間時請把燈關掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is getting dark, so I will hit the lights.","zh":"天快黑了，所以我來把燈開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7640da40298286a6e462","word":"hive","forms":["hive"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99d7baa8755f2a14","term":"hive","forms":["hive","hives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜂巢","explanation":"蜜蜂居住、儲存蜂蜜並共同活動的巢，可以是天然形成的，也可以是人造的。它是整組詞義的核心畫面：一個容納蜂群的“容器”。","examples":[{"en":"The beekeeper moved the hive to a sunnier part of the garden.","zh":"養蜂人把蜂巢移到了花園裡陽光更充足的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the bees return to the hive at dusk.","zh":"我們看著蜜蜂在黃昏時飛回蜂巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b5f68891aed16a7","term":"hive","forms":["hive","hives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜂群","explanation":"也可以把住在同一個蜂巢裡的蜜蜂整體稱為 hive，強調的是蜂群這個集體，而不是巢本身。","examples":[{"en":"A hive of bees settled in the old apple tree.","zh":"一群蜜蜂在那棵老蘋果樹上安了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The entire hive followed the queen into the box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-881df5708c30cfeda67a","word":"hoarse","forms":["hoarse"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"hoarse","forms":["hoarse"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"聲音沙啞的","examples":[{"en":"Her voice was hoarse after cheering at the concert.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"I sounded hoarse because I had a bad cold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-0834a044f52ddbed8d49","word":"hobby","forms":["hobby"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0cfade221390814","term":"hobby","forms":["hobby","hobbies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"業餘愛好","explanation":"hobby是人在空閒時間反覆做、並且從中得到樂趣的活動，例如集郵、園藝或繪畫。它強調這是工作和日常義務以外的個人興趣。","examples":[{"en":"Photography started as a hobby, but it soon became his full-time job.","zh":"攝影一開始只是他的業餘愛好，但很快成了他的全職工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took up gardening as a hobby after moving to the countryside.","zh":"搬到鄉下後，她開始把園藝當作愛好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hobby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6976798cc640523","term":"hobby","forms":["hobby","hobbies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偏愛反覆談論的話題","explanation":"hobby可以表示一個人總愛談論或堅持討論的話題，就像騎著一匹木馬反覆繞圈一樣。這個義通常帶有輕微調侃意味，強調對方反覆回到同一觀點。","examples":[{"en":"Whenever we discuss education, his hobby is the need for stricter exams.","zh":"每當我們討論教育時，他總要反覆談考試必須更嚴格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Railway timetables were his hobby; he mentioned them constantly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hobby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-308738b8195da46d65c9","word":"hockey","forms":["hockey"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dfc7e4be0c48b94b","term":"hockey","forms":["hockey"],"pos":"noun","zh":"曲棍球類運動","explanation":"泛指使用曲棍球杆、把球或球餅打進球門的一類運動；場地曲棍球和冰球都屬於這個大類。記住“球杆把目標趕向球門”這一核心畫面即可。","examples":[{"en":"My children started playing hockey at school this year.","zh":"我的孩子們今年開始在學校打曲棍球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hockey is popular in many parts of the world.","zh":"曲棍球在世界許多地方都很受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hockey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f85be979715117f","term":"hockey","forms":["hockey"],"pos":"noun","zh":"場地曲棍球","explanation":"指在堅實場地或草地球場上進行的團隊運動，隊員用球杆擊球，目標是把球打進對方球門。單說“hockey”時，在英國及英聯邦語境中常指這個專案。","examples":[{"en":"Our school team won its field hockey match on Saturday.","zh":"我們校隊星期六贏了場地曲棍球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She plays hockey on the school's outdoor pitch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hockey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e8b22d83b417e85ba4f2","word":"hold","forms":["hold"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5813d8302af2566","term":"hold","forms":["hold","holds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抓握；握住","explanation":"指用手或其他部位抓住某物的動作或抓住後的握力，核心畫面就是把東西抓住並讓它留在手裡。","examples":[{"en":"She lost her hold on the wet railing.","zh":"她沒能抓穩那根溼欄杆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child kept a tight hold of his mother's hand.","zh":"孩子緊緊抓著媽媽的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9bf96b87970f7d9","term":"hold","forms":["hold","holds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拿著；抱著的動作","explanation":"指一次把人或物拿在手裡、抱在懷裡的動作，也可表示請求別人讓自己拿一會兒。","examples":[{"en":"Can I have a hold of your camera for a moment?","zh":"我能拿一下你的相機嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave the baby a gentle hold while she tied her shoe.","zh":"她繫鞋帶時，他輕輕抱著嬰兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4df9b83a62bf8823","term":"hold","forms":["hold","holds","holding","held","holden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓住；拿住","explanation":"用手抓住某物，使它留在手中；這是“把某物抓住並讓它留在那裡”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Hold the handle firmly when you open the door.","zh":"開門時要牢牢抓住把手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you hold my bag while I tie my shoe?","zh":"我繫鞋帶時，你能幫我拿一下包嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5f2ae0d120f4b3a","term":"hold","forms":["hold","holds","holding","held","holden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拿著；保持","explanation":"表示替別人拿著某物，或讓某物、某種狀態繼續留在那裡；這正是“抓住並讓它留在那裡”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Please hold my coat while I wash my hands.","zh":"我洗手時請幫我拿著外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hold the door open for the delivery driver.","zh":"替送貨員把門保持開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e45386daeb0b86da1ac","word":"holder","forms":["holder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5de6173d3bd126e","term":"holder","forms":["holder","holders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"容納或固定物品的器具","explanation":"holder 可以是用來放置、承託或固定某件物品的東西，重點是它把東西穩穩“托住”。例如，雨傘架就是專門承載雨傘的 holder。","examples":[{"en":"Put your umbrella in the umbrella holder by the door.","zh":"把你的雨傘放進門邊的雨傘架裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place the candle securely in its holder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a3800986e40fa2c","term":"holder","forms":["holder","holders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持有某物的人","explanation":"holder 也指依法或事實上擁有某項賬戶、證件、票據等的人，也就是“持有人”。這裡的核心仍是某人把某樣東西或某種資格握在手中。","examples":[{"en":"Only the account holder can change the mailing address.","zh":"只有賬戶持有人可以更改郵寄地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ticket holders may enter through the side gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39ee4551970726c324df","word":"hole","forms":["hole"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-973dcf6bf411c864","term":"hole","forms":["hole","holes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凹坑；坑洞","explanation":"指地面、牆面或其他表面上的凹陷、坑或空腔，不一定貫穿整個物體。","examples":[{"en":"We dug a hole in the garden for the new tree.","zh":"我們在花園裡挖了一個坑，好種下那棵新樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child fell into a hole in the ground.","zh":"孩子掉進了地上的一個坑裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2986d94e0da181cc","term":"hole","forms":["hole","holes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穿孔；破洞","explanation":"指穿透固體、布料等的開口，例如鞋、襪子或牆上被穿出的洞。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small hole in my sock.","zh":"我的襪子上有一個小洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drill made a hole in the wall.","zh":"電鑽在牆上打了一個孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b063441b9161e43","term":"hole","forms":["hole","holes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漏洞；缺陷","explanation":"把實體上的洞比作論證或計劃中缺失的一塊，因此指推理、計劃或規則中的漏洞、缺陷或含糊之處。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer found a hole in the contract.","zh":"律師發現了合同中的一個漏洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prosecutor found a hole in his alibi.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81c16d337a1b73144ebf","word":"holiday","forms":["holiday"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6d897cbcfd379c8","term":"holiday","forms":["holiday","holidays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"節日","explanation":"holiday是為了宗教活動、傳統慶典或國家慶祝而特別紀念的日子。它的核心感覺是：這一天從普通日曆中被劃出來，用來慶祝或紀念某件重要的事。","examples":[{"en":"Today is a national holiday, so the banks are closed.","zh":"今天是法定節日，所以銀行關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival is an important holiday for the local community.","zh":"這個節日是當地社群的重要節慶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holiday","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4b5d42308f8d309","term":"holiday","forms":["holiday","holidays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法定休息日","explanation":"holiday也指政府宣佈的不上班日；這一天不一定有宗教意義，重點是國家或地方規定人們可以休息。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is closed on public holidays.","zh":"博物館在法定節假日閉館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Monday was declared a holiday by the government.","zh":"政府宣佈星期一為休息日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holiday","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b21b17b4ecc60cdbfa7b","word":"hollow","forms":["hollow"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6545cb60ec5a616e","term":"hollow","forms":["hollow","hollower","hollowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空心的；內部有空腔的","explanation":"裡面不是實心的，而是有一個空的空間；這正是 hollow 最基本的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A hollow tree stood beside the path.","zh":"小路旁立著一棵空心樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ball is hollow but surprisingly strong.","zh":"這個球是空心的，但出人意料地結實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hollow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d821317ac48e8be","term":"hollow","forms":["hollow","hollower","hollowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空洞的；沒有實際意義的","explanation":"表面上似乎有成果或價值，實際上缺少真正的內容，就像一個空心物體一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Winning the argument felt like a hollow victory.","zh":"贏了這場爭論卻感覺是一場空洞的勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without her family there, the award seemed hollow.","zh":"沒有家人在身邊，這個獎似乎失去了實際意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hollow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5e5bed422341255","term":"hollow","forms":["hollow","hollower","hollowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空口的；不真誠的","explanation":"話聽起來像承諾或保證，實際上沒有誠意、依據或兌現的可能，因此是“空的”。","examples":[{"en":"People are tired of hearing hollow promises from politicians.","zh":"人們已經厭倦了聽政客們說空頭承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His hollow promises no longer reassured anyone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hollow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf195da459c81f40","term":"hollow","forms":["hollow","hollows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空腔；凹洞","explanation":"實心物體內部或表面形成的空的空間，可以是天然的，也可以是人為挖出的。","examples":[{"en":"A family of birds nested in a hollow in the old tree.","zh":"一窩鳥在那棵老樹的樹洞裡築了巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A squirrel nested in a hollow inside the trunk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hollow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1551d1eb020a113540d8","word":"holy","forms":["holy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41f661d4e80a1bdf","term":"holy","forms":["holy","holier","holiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"神聖的","explanation":"指專門獻給神、用於宗教活動，或因宗教意義而被視為神聖的事物。它強調某個地方、物品或時間已經被劃出日常生活範圍，受到特別尊重。","examples":[{"en":"The pilgrims walked quietly through the holy city.","zh":"朝聖者們安靜地走過那座聖城。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They gathered in a holy place to pray.","zh":"他們聚集在一處聖地祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72527c8741ab5b2a","term":"holy","forms":["holy","holier","holiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"受宗教敬仰的","explanation":"指某個物件在一種宗教或文化中被尊為神聖、值得敬拜或敬重。重點不一定是它用於宗教儀式，而是人們賦予它神聖地位。","examples":[{"en":"The river is holy to the people who live nearby.","zh":"這條河對附近居民來說是神聖的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pilgrims traveled to the holy city each spring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ea140588150773ce3aa","word":"home","forms":["home"],"officialPos":"n./adv./v./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d81a594a9df949b1","term":"home","forms":["home"],"pos":"adj","zh":"本國的；本地的；家裡的","explanation":"表示屬於自己的家、本國或本地，而不是外國或外來的。它把“家”這個中心概念擴充套件到個人所屬的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The company is trying to sell more products in the home market.","zh":"這家公司正努力在國內市場銷售更多產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Home production cannot meet the growing demand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/home","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5b4b6f68d59de02","term":"home","forms":["home"],"pos":"adv","zh":"回家","explanation":"表示朝自己的家回去，突出“回到安頓之處”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"I usually go home by bus after work.","zh":"我通常下班後坐公交車回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come home before it gets dark.","zh":"天黑以前回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/home","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bedda10387d4d5e3","term":"home","forms":["home"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在家；在通常所在地","explanation":"表示人在自己的住所，或處在平時、正式所屬的位置上；它仍然圍繞“安頓在自己的地方”這一概念。","examples":[{"en":"She stayed home to look after her sick child.","zh":"她待在家裡照顧生病的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please make yourself at home.","zh":"請別拘束，就把這裡當自己家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/home","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-031d3d5a9129e590","term":"home","forms":["home","homes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家；住宅","explanation":"指人居住並有歸屬感的地方，重點不只是房屋本身，也包括“這是我安頓下來的地方”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a small home near the river.","zh":"他們在河邊買了一所小房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After years abroad, she finally made a home in the city.","zh":"在國外多年後，她終於在這座城市安頓下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/home","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5a996ad1b63f6fb","term":"home","forms":["home","homes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家鄉；祖國","explanation":"表示一個人出生、成長或祖先居住的地方，可以是家鄉，也可以是自己的國家；這裡的“家”從住宅擴大到了更大的歸屬地。","examples":[{"en":"She hopes to return home after studying abroad.","zh":"她希望留學後回到家鄉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After years abroad, she longed to return home.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/home","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04053db001d229f34efc","word":"homeland","forms":["homeland"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ea1206f3f608484","term":"homeland","forms":["homeland","homelands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祖國；故土","explanation":"指一個人心裡認作“家”的國家或土地，常包含深厚的歸屬感；人在國外生活多年後仍可能把某地稱為 homeland。","examples":[{"en":"After years abroad, she finally returned to her homeland.","zh":"在國外多年後，她終於回到了自己的祖國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He still feels a deep connection to his homeland.","zh":"他仍然與自己的故土有著深厚的聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homeland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f820a8f9ec115de","term":"homeland","forms":["homeland","homelands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"居住國；生活的家園","explanation":"可指一個人目前居住並把它當作家的國家，重點在現實生活中的歸屬，而不一定是出生地。","examples":[{"en":"She has made this country her homeland.","zh":"她已經把這個國家當成了自己的家園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They made Canada their adopted homeland.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homeland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50d88b8404f266a8761b","word":"homesick","forms":["homesick"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb1ada47ec5483ee","term":"homesick","forms":["homesick","more homesick","most homesick"],"pos":"adj","zh":"想家；思鄉","explanation":"人在外地或離開家人後，因非常想念熟悉的家、家鄉或家人而感到難受；重點是強烈的思念，不只是普通的懷念。","examples":[{"en":"After two weeks abroad, I was homesick for my parents.","zh":"在國外待了兩週後，我開始非常想念父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The homesick student called home every night.","zh":"那個想家的學生每天晚上都給家裡打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homesick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14a78db18a9fbb57b004","word":"hometown","forms":["hometown"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94abd3a48fab5c51","term":"hometown","forms":["hometown","hometowns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家鄉","explanation":"指一個人出生、長大，或長期居住過並有熟悉感的地方。它把“家”和“城鎮”連在一起，重點是這個地方對個人來說像家一樣熟悉。","examples":[{"en":"I visit my hometown every summer to see my family.","zh":"我每年夏天都回家鄉看望家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She grew up in a small hometown near the coast.","zh":"她在海邊附近的一個小城鎮長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hometown","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"113":2}}},{"id":"ceec-404355522396b9295308","word":"homework","forms":["homework"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb179f458b46f45f","term":"homework","forms":["homework","homeworks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"課後作業","explanation":"指老師佈置給學生、用來複習課堂所學內容的課後練習，是這個詞最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I have to finish my homework before dinner.","zh":"我得在晚飯前完成作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher gave us too much homework this week.","zh":"老師這周給我們佈置了太多作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homework","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3f7c687d585ac7a","term":"homework","forms":["homework","homeworks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事先調查和準備","explanation":"從“完成作業”引申為在做重要事情前認真查資料、瞭解情況並做好準備，常用於演講、談判或作決定等場合。","examples":[{"en":"She did her homework before meeting the client.","zh":"她在見客戶前做了充分的調查和準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do your homework before negotiating the purchase.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homework","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-304bf48b8274c460d990","word":"homosexual","forms":["homosexual"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"homosexual","forms":["homosexual"],"pos":"adj./n.","zh":"同性戀的；同性戀者","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses the rights of homosexual people.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Some people describe themselves as homosexual, while others prefer the word gay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf5b6382c2ea46ede311","word":"honest","forms":["honest"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c825511f55437734","term":"honest","forms":["honest","more honest","honester","most honest","honestest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"誠實的；不欺騙的","explanation":"指一個人堅持說真話，不靠撒謊、欺詐或耍手段獲利，是 honest 最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She is honest with her customers, even when the news is bad.","zh":"即使訊息不好，她也會對顧客說實話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I trust him because he is honest.","zh":"我信任他，因為他很誠實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-033358df8608b24e","term":"honest","forms":["honest","more honest","honester","most honest","honestest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真實的；公正的","explanation":"指說法或記錄儘可能符合事實，不故意偏袒或歪曲；重點從“這個人不騙人”擴充套件到“這件事說得真實、公平”。","examples":[{"en":"The report gives an honest account of what happened.","zh":"這份報告如實說明了事情的經過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can I ask for your honest opinion?","zh":"我可以聽聽你的真實意見嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-203e303a50269f3d533d","word":"honesty","forms":["honesty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0b9ea7187eed854","term":"honesty","forms":["honesty","honesties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誠實；正直","explanation":"指一個人不說假話、不欺騙，也願意坦誠面對事實和自己的想法；它既可以指誠實的行為，也可以指這種品質本身。","examples":[{"en":"Her honesty about the mistake earned everyone's respect.","zh":"她坦誠地承認錯誤，贏得了大家的尊重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report was written with complete honesty.","zh":"這份報告完全如實撰寫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honesty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a55e2e3846a51f6ad0ab","word":"honey","forms":["honey"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f740b27d9e084779","term":"honey","forms":["honey","honeys","honies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜂蜜","explanation":"指蜜蜂從植物花蜜中釀成的甜、黏稠、金黃色食物，是這個詞最基本的意義。","examples":[{"en":"I put a little honey in my tea.","zh":"我在茶裡放了一點蜂蜜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The honey in this jar came from a local farm.","zh":"這罐蜂蜜來自當地農場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0db55574ab5ebf1e","term":"honey","forms":["honey","honeys","honies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親暱稱呼","explanation":"用來稱呼親近的人，意思接近“親愛的”或“寶貝”，把對方比作甜蜜可愛的人。","examples":[{"en":"Honey, could you close the window?","zh":"親愛的，你能把窗戶關上嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thanks for helping me, honey.","zh":"謝謝你幫我，親愛的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d58905e0342217b1fa5","word":"honeymoon","forms":["honeymoon"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09ac28d266b96c49","term":"honeymoon","forms":["honeymoon","honeymoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"婚後蜜月期","explanation":"指結婚後最初的一段甜蜜、親密的時間，不一定強調去了哪裡旅行；它是“蜜月旅行”背後的時間概念。","examples":[{"en":"They are still on their honeymoon and spend every evening together.","zh":"他們還在蜜月期，每晚都一起度過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The couple enjoyed a quiet honeymoon at home.","zh":"這對夫妻在家安靜地享受了蜜月期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honeymoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48abaa0faaa6b5da","term":"honeymoon","forms":["honeymoon","honeymoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜜月旅行","explanation":"指新婚夫婦在婚後這段時間裡安排的旅行，重點是一次具體的出行，而不是整個婚後時期。","examples":[{"en":"We went to Bali for our honeymoon.","zh":"我們去巴厘島度蜜月了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The couple spent their honeymoon in a mountain cabin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honeymoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-343cc4426bef4f48","term":"honeymoon","forms":["honeymoon","honeymoons","honeymooning","honeymooned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"去度蜜月","explanation":"指新婚夫婦進行蜜月旅行，強調“去度蜜月”這一行動，而不是婚後的一整段時期。","examples":[{"en":"They honeymooned in Italy after the wedding.","zh":"他們婚禮後去義大利度蜜月了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They honeymooned in a quiet village beside the sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honeymoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ab4ca2f83725a04752a","word":"honor","forms":["honor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0606d5ad02bc801d","term":"honor","forms":["honor","honors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尊重；敬意","explanation":"指人因為重要、有成就或品德好而得到的尊重。它強調別人對這個人的看重，而不一定是一個具體獎項。","examples":[{"en":"The town held a parade in honor of the firefighters.","zh":"鎮上舉行了遊行，以表達對消防員的敬意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ceremony paid honor to the rescue workers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d5e6f06dd5697b1","term":"honor","forms":["honor","honors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名譽；尊嚴","explanation":"指一個人正直、高尚、守信所形成的名譽和尊嚴，也可以指這種高尚品格本身。它把“受人尊重”推進到“值得受尊重的品格”。","examples":[{"en":"She refused to lie because her honor mattered more than the money.","zh":"她拒絕撒謊，因為她覺得自己的名譽比錢更重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The false accusation threatened both his livelihood and his honor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33ec238bacdb2411","term":"honor","forms":["honor","honors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"榮幸；特殊待遇","explanation":"指某人因受到特別邀請或信任而獲得的榮幸和待遇。它仍然來自“別人把你看得很重要”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"It was an honor to meet the award-winning scientist.","zh":"能見到這位獲獎科學家是我的榮幸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our team was given the honor of opening the anniversary celebrations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0a4c7ff034c842e","term":"honor","forms":["honor","honors","honoring","honored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"尊重；紀念","explanation":"表示認真看重某人、某種價值或某人的貢獻，並以尊敬或紀念的方式表達出來。","examples":[{"en":"The museum honors local artists with a yearly exhibition.","zh":"這家博物館每年舉辦展覽，以表彰當地藝術家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The memorial honors those who died at sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-638ac34b84528316","term":"honor","forms":["honor","honors","honoring","honored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵守；履行","explanation":"表示按照承諾、協議、請求或約定去做，使自己說過的話得到兌現。這是“維護名譽”在行動上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"The company promised to honor its agreement.","zh":"公司承諾會履行協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company honored its promise to refund customers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c1970d8d12c4c1f8593","word":"honorable","forms":["honorable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d27be7a12b8a427","term":"honorable","forms":["honorable","more honorable","most honorable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正直體面；有品格","explanation":"指一個人的行為符合正直、誠實和體面的標準，表現出值得信賴的品格。它強調“做事有原則”，不一定表示這個人已經獲得了某種正式榮譽。","examples":[{"en":"She kept her promise even when it was difficult, which was honorable.","zh":"即使很困難，她仍然信守承諾，這種做法很有品格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is an honorable man who admits his mistakes.","zh":"他是個有正直品格、願意承認錯誤的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honorable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be7a7d191cbef501","term":"honorable","forms":["honorable","more honorable","most honorable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得尊敬的；體面的","explanation":"指某人、職業、選擇或做法本身值得別人尊重，給人正面而體面的印象。重點是社會評價上的“值得尊敬”，不只限於個人道德。","examples":[{"en":"Teaching is an honorable profession that helps shape the future.","zh":"教師是一種值得尊敬的職業，能幫助塑造未來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Helping his injured opponent was an honorable act.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honorable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-278204674761b2498777","word":"honorary","forms":["honorary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c19fe8edd94d1efa","term":"honorary","forms":["honorary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"榮譽性的","explanation":"指某個稱號、學位或身份是為了表彰一個人的貢獻而授予的，持有者通常不需要履行該職位的正式職責，也沒有相應薪酬。它就像一枚表示認可的榮譽徽章。","examples":[{"en":"The university awarded her an honorary degree.","zh":"這所大學授予她榮譽學位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was made an honorary citizen of the town.","zh":"他被授予該鎮的榮譽公民稱號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honorary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-030b813a5267d76c","term":"honorary","forms":["honorary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"義務性的；無償參與的","explanation":"指某人出於榮譽、善意或自願而參與某項工作，通常沒有正式報酬或固定的職業責任。這個意思仍然來自“戴著榮譽徽章幫忙”，而不是把它當作正式工作。","examples":[{"en":"She serves as an honorary guide at the museum on weekends.","zh":"她週末在博物館擔任義務導覽員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She serves as honorary treasurer without receiving payment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honorary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0648298b48be03199627","word":"hook","forms":["hook"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2dbceceae45fdb4c","term":"hook","forms":["hook","hooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鉤子；掛鉤","explanation":"指一端固定、另一端彎曲並可鉤住東西的桿狀物，是“彎曲並鉤住”這一核心畫面的實體形式。它可以用來懸掛、連線或固定物品。","examples":[{"en":"She hung her coat on a hook by the door.","zh":"她把外套掛在門邊的掛鉤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rope was fastened to a metal hook.","zh":"繩子固定在一個金屬掛鉤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f48e1c643684844","term":"hook","forms":["hook","hooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸引注意力的開場","explanation":"指演講、文章、書、節目或影片開頭用來立刻吸引受眾、讓人繼續聽讀看的短句或開場內容。它就是把聽眾注意力“鉤住”的抽象鉤子。","examples":[{"en":"The speaker opened with a surprising question as her hook.","zh":"演講者用一個令人意外的問題作為吸引注意力的開場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The first sentence is a strong hook that makes readers want to continue.","zh":"第一句話是一個很有吸引力的開場，讓讀者想繼續讀下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d739845498f43337","term":"hook","forms":["hook","hooks","hooking","hooked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鉤住；釣到","explanation":"指用鉤子把魚或其他東西鉤住，尤其常用於釣魚；也可指意外鉤到某物。","examples":[{"en":"She hooked a large trout near the bank.","zh":"她在岸邊釣到了一條大鱒魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hooked my coat on a nail as I walked past.","zh":"我走過時，外套被釘子鉤住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0be7a2613df998b8","term":"hook","forms":["hook","hooks","hooking","hooked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使上癮；使著迷","explanation":"指某物像鉤子一樣牢牢抓住人的興趣或慾望，使人著迷、離不開，常表示上癮。","examples":[{"en":"I got hooked on that mystery series after one episode.","zh":"我看了一集那部懸疑劇後就上癮了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many teenagers become hooked on short videos.","zh":"許多青少年會沉迷於短影片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87a0acaec00fa34a3166","word":"hop","forms":["hop"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e133b075e70f7297","term":"hop","forms":["hop","hops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短促的一跳","explanation":"hop 是一次幅度不大、時間很短的跳躍，重點是“輕輕跳一下”，而不是跳得很高或很遠。","examples":[{"en":"The rabbit reached the garden in three hops.","zh":"兔子跳了三下就到了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rabbit disappeared with one enormous hop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a6db1978ef268ec","term":"hop","forms":["hop","hops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"單腳跳","explanation":"它也特指只用一隻腳連續跳，這正是“輕輕跳一下”這一核心動作的具體形式。","examples":[{"en":"The children hopped across the room on one foot.","zh":"孩子們單腳跳著穿過了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One quick hop carried her over the puddle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40681380a1444c88","term":"hop","forms":["hop","hops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啤酒花植物","explanation":"hop 還指啤酒花，一種在釀造啤酒時用來增加苦味和香氣的植物；這是與“跳”完全不同的一條詞義線。","examples":[{"en":"The brewer grows hops behind the small brewery.","zh":"這位釀酒師在小型啤酒廠後面種植啤酒花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hops climbed the wires beside the brewery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a33da06f7ba05b35","term":"hop","forms":["hop","hops","hopping","hopped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跳一小段","explanation":"作動詞時，hop 表示向前跳一小段，動作輕快而距離短。","examples":[{"en":"The bird hopped from the fence to the path.","zh":"那隻鳥從籬笆跳到了小路上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopped across the puddle on one foot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c074861ffba40d7","term":"hop","forms":["hop","hops","hopping","hopped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"單腳跳","explanation":"它也表示用一隻腳跳著移動，是名詞“單腳跳”的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"He hopped on one foot while tying his shoe.","zh":"他繫鞋帶時單腳跳著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injured child hopped to the bench.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c29277f55fb31aeb8d40","word":"hope","forms":["hope"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c12c6dc71170b41a","term":"hope","forms":["hope","hopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"希望；期待","explanation":"指相信某件想要的事可能或將會發生的感覺，重點是願望中帶著信心和期待。","examples":[{"en":"There is still hope that the missing hikers will be found.","zh":"仍然有希望找到失蹤的徒步者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All hope of an early recovery disappeared.","zh":"早日康復的希望破滅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf49310444dd3866","term":"hope","forms":["hope","hopes","hoping","hoped","hopest","hopedst","hopeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"希望；盼望","explanation":"表示希望某件事發生，並認為它有可能發生，常帶有願望和期待。","examples":[{"en":"I hope you feel better soon.","zh":"我希望你很快好起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They hope it will stop raining by noon.","zh":"他們希望中午前雨能停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4709ff721c95599","term":"hope","forms":["hope","hopes","hoping","hoped","hopest","hopedst","hopeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"希望做；期待做","explanation":"表示打算做某事，並期待將來有機會實現它，常用於談自己的計劃或願望。","examples":[{"en":"We hope to visit Japan next year.","zh":"我們希望明年去日本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hope to reopen the museum in April.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ad2e0351be5fbd48cac","word":"hopeful","forms":["hopeful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0d1d8441ea6e972","term":"hopeful","forms":["hopeful","more hopeful","most hopeful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"抱有希望的","explanation":"指一個人相信事情仍可能朝好的方向發展，心裡保持期待，但不表示結果已經確定。","examples":[{"en":"I’m hopeful about finding a new job soon.","zh":"我對很快找到新工作抱有希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Doctors remained hopeful about his recovery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hopeful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40454a5d314d766a","term":"hopeful","forms":["hopeful","more hopeful","most hopeful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"帶來希望的；前景有望的","explanation":"指跡象、局面或結果顯示事情可能變好，因而給人希望；這裡不是說某個人有這種心情，而是事情本身顯得有希望。","examples":[{"en":"The latest test results look hopeful.","zh":"最新的檢測結果看起來很有希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A hopeful development in the peace talks encouraged investors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hopeful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4726a1bce9706083939a","word":"horizon","forms":["horizon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18b8c17ae183e09f","term":"horizon","forms":["horizon","horizons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地平線","explanation":"指從某個地方看出去，遠處天空彷彿與大地或海面相接的那條線。它是最具體、最容易想象的本義。","examples":[{"en":"A red sun was sinking below the horizon.","zh":"一輪紅日正在地平線下沉落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dark clouds gathered on the horizon.","zh":"烏雲聚集在地平線上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horizon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5bcc8c37bf04bd6","term":"horizon","forms":["horizon","horizons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"視野；眼界","explanation":"把人的知識、經歷、興趣或可能性看成一片可以望到的範圍；horizon 越寬，表示眼界越開闊，能接觸和考慮的東西越多。","examples":[{"en":"Traveling abroad broadened her horizons.","zh":"出國旅行開闊了她的眼界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reading widely can expand your horizons.","zh":"廣泛閱讀可以拓寬你的視野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horizon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69b273a2e991006f8526","word":"horizontal","forms":["horizontal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d54b12f32323c96","term":"horizontal","forms":["horizontal","more horizontal","most horizontal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"水平的；平的","explanation":"指與垂直方向成直角、與地平線平行的狀態，也就是像平坦地面或一條水平線那樣展開。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a horizontal line across the page.","zh":"在頁面上畫一條水平線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shelf must be perfectly horizontal.","zh":"這個架子必須完全水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horizontal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a47bd61af75003ff","term":"horizontal","forms":["horizontal","horizontals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水平結構部分","explanation":"指結構物中沿水平方向延伸或承受水平作用的部分，具體所指要看工程或建築上下文。","examples":[{"en":"The bridge has a strong horizontal supporting member.","zh":"這座橋有一根堅固的水平支撐構件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The horizontal was reinforced before the roof was added.","zh":"加屋頂之前，那根水平構件得到了加固。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horizontal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a63ccce91a1b685fa06","word":"hormone","forms":["hormone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a03dcf0f59cc2f9","term":"hormone","forms":["hormone","hormones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體內天然激素","explanation":"指由某種組織產生、經血液等途徑送到另一處並調節其生理活動的化學信使；重點是“組織之間傳遞調節指令”。","examples":[{"en":"The hormone is produced by the thyroid gland and carried through the blood.","zh":"這種激素由甲狀腺產生，並透過血液輸送。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stress can change the body's hormone levels.","zh":"壓力會改變體內的激素水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hormone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d23db6169d7d89b1","term":"hormone","forms":["hormone","hormones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合成激素藥物","explanation":"指人工製造、但能產生與天然激素相同或相近生理作用的化合物；它是對天然“化學信使”的仿製。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor prescribed a synthetic hormone to replace the one the body could not make.","zh":"醫生開了一種合成激素，用來替代身體無法產生的激素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor prescribed hormones to treat the deficiency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hormone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9543098f1704584b8edd","word":"horn","forms":["horn"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4be3cacb1450bcdf","term":"horn","forms":["horn","horns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的角","explanation":"指某些動物頭頂長出的堅硬角狀結構，通常成對出現。它是“向外伸出的硬尖角”這一核心意象的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The goat has two sharp horns.","zh":"這隻山羊有兩隻尖角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bull lowered its horns and charged.","zh":"公牛低下角衝了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7acb9c19190006d2","term":"horn","forms":["horn","horns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"號角類樂器","explanation":"指用嘴吹奏的管樂器，外形或發聲方式與角狀管子有關；具體可指多種號角類樂器。","examples":[{"en":"She learned to play the horn at school.","zh":"她在學校學會了吹號角類樂器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The horn player joined the orchestra.","zh":"圓號手加入了樂團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b739ed39cbf14040","term":"horn","forms":["horn","horns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽車喇叭","explanation":"指汽車等車輛上的喇叭，也可指按喇叭發出的響亮警報聲；它是“號角發聲”在現代交通中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't honk the horn outside the hospital.","zh":"請不要在醫院外按喇叭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I heard a car horn behind me.","zh":"我聽到身後有汽車喇叭聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a26d8b8ab63b75c458fd","word":"horrible","forms":["horrible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4feddba7aae35988","term":"horrible","forms":["horrible","horribler","more horrible","horriblest","most horrible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可怕的；令人震驚的","explanation":"指某事物造成強烈恐懼、震驚或厭惡，讓人覺得可怕得難以接受。它可以形容事件、行為、景象或後果。","examples":[{"en":"The accident was horrible, and several people were badly injured.","zh":"那場事故很可怕，有幾個人受了重傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They heard a horrible scream coming from the empty house.","zh":"他們聽見空屋裡傳來一聲可怕的尖叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horrible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3895bd1ec6099307","term":"horrible","forms":["horrible","horribler","more horrible","horriblest","most horrible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"糟糕透頂的","explanation":"表示某事物質量極差、令人非常不滿意；這裡不一定真的讓人害怕，而是把“糟糕”說得很重，彷彿糟糕到了可怕的程度。","examples":[{"en":"The food was horrible, so we left without ordering dessert.","zh":"食物糟糕透頂，所以我們沒點甜點就離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had a horrible day at work.","zh":"我今天上班過得糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horrible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ad032d4cb6bc4d300a2","word":"horrify","forms":["horrify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"horrify","forms":["horrify"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使驚恐；使震驚","examples":[{"en":"Scenes of animal cruelty horrify many viewers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The thought of losing all those records would horrify the researcher.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-9e96274abcf3df0dfcd1","word":"horror","forms":["horror"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c215ba1f2640c97","term":"horror","forms":["horror","horrors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈的恐懼或厭惡","explanation":"指面對危險、死亡、暴力或極其令人反感的事物時產生的強烈恐懼，也可以同時帶有噁心和排斥感。這是horror最基本的抽象意義，重點不只是“害怕”，而是反應特別強烈、令人難以承受。","examples":[{"en":"She looked at the damage with horror.","zh":"她驚恐地看著造成的損害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt horror at the thought of losing his family.","zh":"想到要失去家人，他感到極度恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a578e701695ffa5","term":"horror","forms":["horror","horrors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恐怖題材","explanation":"指專門透過危險、怪異、暴力或超自然情節制造恐懼和懸念的文學、電影或其他藝術型別。它和“恐懼”這個核心義相連：作品的目的就是讓觀眾產生horror。","examples":[{"en":"I enjoy horror, but I dislike films with realistic violence.","zh":"我喜歡恐怖題材，但不喜歡有真實暴力場面的電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel combines horror with a family mystery.","zh":"這部小說把恐怖題材和家庭謎案結合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd62862b6dc213bee77c","word":"horse","forms":["horse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e6fe4638a2a0e5a","term":"horse","forms":["horse","horses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬","explanation":"指馬這種有蹄哺乳動物，歷史上常被人騎乘、馱運或拉車；這是horse最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The children took turns riding the horse.","zh":"孩子們輪流騎那匹馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Horses once carried people and supplies across the mountains.","zh":"過去，馬曾馱著人和物資翻越山脈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41d12df274ffaef654ea","word":"hose","forms":["hose"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55d9dd96f4c82b3d","term":"hose","forms":["hose","hoses","hosen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軟管","explanation":"hose 是一根柔軟、可以彎曲的管子，用來輸送水、空氣、燃油或其他液體。它的核心形象就是“把液體從一處送到另一處的軟管”。","examples":[{"en":"Please connect the hose to the outdoor faucet.","zh":"請把軟管接到室外水龍頭上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fire crew pulled a long hose across the street.","zh":"消防隊員把一條長軟管拖過了街道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc497aead501ee4d","term":"hose","forms":["hose","hoses","hosing","hosed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用軟管沖洗","explanation":"hose 作動詞時最基本的意思是用軟管向某物噴水，常用於澆花、沖洗地面或清潔裝置。","examples":[{"en":"We hosed down the patio after the muddy party.","zh":"泥濘的聚會結束後，我們用水管沖洗了露臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hosed the plants before leaving for work.","zh":"他上班前用水管給植物澆了水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1552f59d213e755fce02","word":"hospitable","forms":["hospitable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c66cf3eca45a299","term":"hospitable","forms":["hospitable","more hospitable","most hospitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱情好客的","explanation":"形容主人、家庭或地方願意熱情接待客人，讓人感到受歡迎、受到照顧；這是 hospitable 最直接、最常見的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The hospitable family invited us to stay for dinner.","zh":"這家人熱情好客，邀請我們留下來吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our hosts were extremely hospitable during the visit.","zh":"我們訪問期間，主人招待得非常熱情周到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hospitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b41ae78a3e9eede","term":"hospitable","forms":["hospitable","more hospitable","most hospitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樂於接納的；思想開放的","explanation":"把“歡迎客人”的形象延伸到抽象事物上，表示願意接受不同的人、意見或新想法，不排斥新事物。","examples":[{"en":"The committee was hospitable to new ideas.","zh":"委員會樂於接受新想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university is hospitable to unconventional research ideas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hospitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8afe3c83decffdf6dc48","word":"hospital","forms":["hospital"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a1c47d2ad6138e0","term":"hospital","forms":["hospital","hospitals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫院","explanation":"醫院是為病情嚴重或受傷的人提供檢查、治療、手術和住院照護的大型醫療機構。這是hospital在現代英語中最重要、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She was taken to hospital after breaking her leg.","zh":"她摔斷腿後被送進了醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital treated hundreds of patients during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，這家醫院救治了數百名患者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hospital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d61d74587224c86ab5c1","word":"hospitality","forms":["hospitality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec12c090c65d983c","term":"hospitality","forms":["hospitality","hospitalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱情待客","explanation":"指歡迎、接待和款待客人的行為，也指對客人開放、尊重、慷慨的態度。重點不只是提供東西，而是讓客人感到受到歡迎。","examples":[{"en":"Thank you for your warm hospitality during our visit.","zh":"感謝你在我們來訪期間的熱情款待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They showed great hospitality to everyone who came to the village.","zh":"他們對所有來到村裡的人都表現出極大的熱情和好客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hospitality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-273d77110eb17d5c","term":"hospitality","forms":["hospitality","hospitalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"款待業","explanation":"指圍繞迎接和服務客人而形成的商業行業，主要包括酒店、餐館以及類似的住宿、餐飲和娛樂服務。","examples":[{"en":"After college, he started a career in hospitality.","zh":"大學畢業後，他開始在款待業發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He found work in hospitality after leaving school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hospitality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-891c3a58b7dcabc33b84","word":"hospitalize","forms":["hospitalize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"hospitalize","forms":["hospitalize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使住院","examples":[{"en":"Doctors may hospitalize patients who have severe breathing problems.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The infection was serious enough to hospitalize him for several days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-9aa83e4dd1f2adf26129","word":"host/hostess","forms":["host","hostess"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8d0445c9218a50f","term":"host","forms":["host","hosts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主人；接待者","explanation":"指接待客人、訪客或顧客並照料其需要的人，也可以指負責接待的機構。它體現了 host“為別人提供空間和照料”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Our host welcomed everyone with a warm smile.","zh":"我們的主人帶著親切的微笑歡迎每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel was a gracious host to the visiting team.","zh":"這家酒店熱情接待了來訪團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/host","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d7d3fbcf700dbfd","term":"hostess","forms":["hostess","hostesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女主人；女性接待者","explanation":"指在家中、聚會或活動中迎接並照料客人的女性，是 hostess 最基本、最容易遷移到其他場景的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The hostess welcomed everyone with a warm smile.","zh":"女主人面帶親切的微笑歡迎每一個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our hostess showed us to our seats.","zh":"接待我們的女士把我們帶到了座位旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ce3fece38f73c58","term":"hostess","forms":["hostess","hostesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女客棧老闆","explanation":"指經營旅店並接待住客的女性；這裡的“主人”具體落實為旅店的經營者。","examples":[{"en":"The hostess of the small inn prepared breakfast for the guests.","zh":"那家小旅店的女老闆為客人準備了早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inn's hostess brought fresh towels upstairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ae3cf7d4c49da7e4ff2","word":"hostage","forms":["hostage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40bc837100e8ca81","term":"hostage","forms":["hostage","hostages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被扣押的人質","explanation":"指被抓住並用來威脅、逼迫另一方採取某種行動或停止某種行動的人；對方通常以傷害人質相威脅。","examples":[{"en":"The gunman took two workers hostage during the robbery.","zh":"持槍歹徒在搶劫過程中劫持了兩名工人作為人質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hostages were released after several hours.","zh":"幾小時後，人質獲釋了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f47ef6bdc295085e","term":"hostage","forms":["hostage","hostages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受到風險牽制的事物","explanation":"這裡不是說真的有人被抓，而是說某件事因為自身處於風險中，導致人不得不限制行動；它像被拿在別人手裡的籌碼。","examples":[{"en":"The project is hostage to a lack of funding.","zh":"這個專案受資金不足的牽制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their savings remained hostage to the unstable currency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6188622aab1dfdbcd13","word":"hostel","forms":["hostel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-181d4e1f73763b7d","term":"hostel","forms":["hostel","hostels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅舍；青年旅舍","explanation":"指商業經營的過夜住宿處，常有多人合住的宿舍房間和共用浴室、廚房等設施，尤其常指青年旅舍。它的重點是以較低成本提供“共同住宿”的空間。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed at a hostel near the train station.","zh":"我們住在火車站附近的一家旅舍裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hostel has a shared kitchen and a quiet garden.","zh":"這家旅舍有共用廚房和一個安靜的花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb2ba8efc7bfdeaa","term":"hostel","forms":["hostel","hostels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臨時收容處","explanation":"指為無家可歸者提供臨時床位的地方，有時還提供食物等基本幫助。這裡的核心仍是“給人一個可以暫住的共同空間”，但重點不在旅行住宿，而在臨時安置和援助。","examples":[{"en":"The charity runs a hostel for people without homes.","zh":"這家慈善機構為無家可歸者經營一所臨時收容處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity runs a hostel for homeless teenagers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f383ccddc6f17eb57a9","word":"hostile","forms":["hostile"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afc4b82ecc61763b","term":"hostile","forms":["hostile","more hostile","most hostile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"敵意的；不友好的","explanation":"表示把對方當成敵人，態度明顯不友好，帶有惡意或阻撓、傷害對方的意圖；既可形容人，也可形容言語、行動或局面。","examples":[{"en":"The committee adopted a hostile attitude toward the proposal.","zh":"委員會對這項提議採取了敵意的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers were hostile to the strangers at first.","zh":"村民起初對那些陌生人充滿敵意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab184b1b0df6eaac","term":"hostile","forms":["hostile","more hostile","most hostile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"攻擊性的；對抗的","explanation":"強調敵意已經表現為強烈的對抗或攻擊傾向，比單純冷淡、不友好更有主動衝突的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The protest became hostile when the police arrived.","zh":"警察到達後，抗議活動變得具有攻擊性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He faced hostile questions from an angry crowd.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3e55073268ce2f157a5","word":"hostility","forms":["hostility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb9df3e7c5ead596","term":"hostility","forms":["hostility","hostilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敵意；敵對狀態","explanation":"指人與人、群體與群體之間持續的不友好、對立或敵視態度，也可以指這種關係造成的緊張氣氛。它強調的是“敵對之牆”本身，不一定已經發生了實際攻擊。","examples":[{"en":"There was growing hostility between the two communities.","zh":"兩個群體之間的敵意越來越強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She faced hostility from some of her coworkers.","zh":"她受到一些同事的敵視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16a4f3d0d95b9252","term":"hostility","forms":["hostility","hostilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敵對行動；戰事","explanation":"指把敵意變成實際行動，尤其是軍事上的攻擊、交戰或戰爭行動。常用複數 hostilities 表示一系列持續或反覆發生的敵對行動。","examples":[{"en":"The two sides agreed to suspend hostilities for a week.","zh":"雙方同意暫停敵對行動一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hostilities resumed along the disputed border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hostility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f5d1618e7d28cc7bf32","word":"hot","forms":["hot"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cae78044119f61e","term":"hot","forms":["hot","hotter","hottest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"溫度高的","explanation":"表示溫度高，會使人感到熱，或可能因高溫而受傷；這是把 hot 記成“熱度很高”的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful—the pan is still hot.","zh":"小心，這口鍋還很燙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was too hot to sit outside at noon.","zh":"中午太熱了，沒法坐在外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-330e50e8e9aa57f4","term":"hot","forms":["hot","hotter","hottest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"情緒激烈的","explanation":"表示脾氣、爭論或情緒很強烈，像“熱度很高”一樣難以平靜。","examples":[{"en":"His hot temper often causes problems at work.","zh":"他的暴脾氣經常在工作中引發問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hot tempers made agreement increasingly unlikely.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7132add2dc71ccd9","term":"hot","forms":["hot","hotter","hottest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱門的；受關注的","explanation":"表示人、作品、產品或話題很受歡迎、很有前景，關注度和熱度都很高。","examples":[{"en":"She is one of the hottest young designers in the city.","zh":"她是這座城市最受關注的年輕設計師之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Solar energy became a hot topic during the campaign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d53a3e3672946bd802c","word":"hotel","forms":["hotel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8016421c1282f473","term":"hotel","forms":["hotel","hotels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒店；旅館","explanation":"指向付費客人提供房間住宿，並通常提供餐飲、清潔等服務的場所。它可以是獨立經營的旅館，也可以是連鎖酒店，是hotel最常見、最重要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed at a small hotel near the train station.","zh":"我們住在火車站附近的一家小旅館裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I booked a hotel room for three nights.","zh":"我訂了一間住三晚的酒店客房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hotel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ac0add475dd38e6ab3a","word":"hour","forms":["hour"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2133be07d623c38a","term":"hour","forms":["hour","hours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小時；六十分鐘","explanation":"一天的二十四分之一，也就是六十分鐘，是 hour 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting lasted two hours.","zh":"會議持續了兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I will call you in an hour.","zh":"我一小時後給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30b15f5db73ab3b1","term":"hour","forms":["hour","hours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時刻；時段","explanation":"不一定精確指六十分鐘，而是指某個特別的時刻、時期或不尋常的時間段。","examples":[{"en":"We arrived at a very late hour.","zh":"我們在很晚的時候到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dawn is my favorite hour for walking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b2a51df70a161c58c62","word":"hourly","forms":["hourly"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3afa7edaac92bc8d","term":"hourly","forms":["hourly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"每小時發生的","explanation":"指某項服務、活動或事件每隔一小時發生一次，重點在固定的時間間隔。","examples":[{"en":"There are hourly express buses to the airport.","zh":"有每小時一班的機場快線公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hourly weather reports kept the sailing crews informed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hourly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfb8a24de870d599","term":"hourly","forms":["hourly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"每小時一次","explanation":"表示某個動作或服務以一小時為間隔反覆進行。","examples":[{"en":"The shuttle departs hourly from the station.","zh":"班車每小時從車站發出一班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"During the trial, technicians recorded the tank's temperature hourly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hourly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6e21286621a8586f7e5","word":"house","forms":["house"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63de8e60012c9f16","term":"house","forms":["house","houses","housen","hice"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房屋；住宅","explanation":"指為人提供遮蔽和居住空間的建築，即通常所說的房子或住宅。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a small house near the river.","zh":"他們在河邊買了一所小房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave your shoes outside the house.","zh":"請把鞋放在房子外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/house","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-162a2cbcb120579e","term":"house","forms":["house","houses","housen","hice"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一家人；家庭成員","explanation":"指住在同一所房子裡、共同組成一個家庭的人；這裡從“容納人的房屋”轉而強調被房屋容納的家庭。","examples":[{"en":"The whole house gathered around the table for dinner.","zh":"一家人聚在餐桌旁吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is respected by everyone in the house.","zh":"家裡的每個人都尊敬她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/house","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca31dcdb7d66d3b7","term":"house","forms":["house","houses","housing","housed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……安置在結構或容器內","explanation":"指把車、裝置或其他物品放進並留在房屋、車庫、容器等有遮蔽的結構裡，突出“提供空間來容納”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum houses a large collection of ancient coins.","zh":"這座博物館收藏著大量古錢幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bicycles are housed in a locked shed.","zh":"腳踏車存放在一間上鎖的棚屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/house","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30a45cfbb560f032","term":"house","forms":["house","houses","housing","housed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收容；給……提供住處","explanation":"指為人提供住處、收留或安置某人，體現房屋為人提供遮蔽和容納的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The charity housed fifty families after the flood.","zh":"洪水過後，這家慈善機構為五十個家庭提供了住處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel can house up to three hundred guests.","zh":"這家酒店最多可以容納三百名客人住宿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/house","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbcd628c07a0e35a5a86","word":"household","forms":["household"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43530ccc600c67f7","term":"household","forms":["household","households"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一家人；一戶人家","explanation":"指住在同一所房子裡、作為一個生活單位共同生活的人，可以包括家庭成員以及長期在其中服務或居住的人；核心畫面就是“同一個家裡的一群人”。","examples":[{"en":"The survey included 2,000 households.","zh":"這項調查包括兩千戶家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several households shared the same well.","zh":"幾戶人家共用同一口井。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/household","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-414360a5214ca1a5e3e7","word":"housekeeper","forms":["housekeeper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-efb4a270d28196ef","term":"housekeeper","forms":["housekeeper","housekeepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受僱管理家務的人","explanation":"指受僱照料和管理一個家庭的人，通常負責安排家務、管理家中的其他工作人員，使家庭日常運轉有序；在酒店或機構中也可指承擔類似管理職責的人。","examples":[{"en":"They hired a housekeeper to manage the large family's daily affairs.","zh":"他們僱了一位管家來管理這個大家庭的日常事務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel housekeeper checked every room before the guests arrived.","zh":"客人到達前，酒店的客房管理員檢查了每個房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/housekeeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f2f5639f795b9e1","term":"housekeeper","forms":["housekeeper","housekeepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理家庭的人","explanation":"指負責讓一個家庭正常運轉的人，重點在家庭管理者的角色，不一定表示受僱於別人；傳統上常指家中的女性主人。","examples":[{"en":"As the housekeeper of the household, she organized meals and household expenses.","zh":"作為家裡的管理者，她安排飯菜和家庭開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A careful housekeeper, he planned meals and tracked expenses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/housekeeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a73b2a9532398fc23ba","word":"housewife","forms":["housewife"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-006555a847f86e9b","term":"housewife","forms":["housewife","housewives","housewifes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家庭主婦","explanation":"指把料理家務、照料孩子或維持家庭日常運轉作為主要工作的女性，尤其指沒有把有薪工作作為主要職業的女性。這個義項的核心畫面就是“主要守著家、打理家的人”。","examples":[{"en":"After the children were born, she decided to become a housewife.","zh":"孩子出生後，她決定做一名家庭主婦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was a housewife for many years, but now she runs a small shop.","zh":"她做了很多年家庭主婦，但現在經營一家小店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/housewife","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbf62822b7360e34dbf8","word":"housework","forms":["housework"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-befb264136f3ad0c","term":"housework","forms":["housework"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家務","explanation":"指在家中維持日常生活所做的事務，尤其包括打掃、洗衣、做飯和整理等。這個詞強調的是一整類家庭勞動，而不是某一件具體工作。","examples":[{"en":"We share the housework on weekends.","zh":"我們週末分擔家務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I usually do the housework after dinner.","zh":"我通常晚飯後做家務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/housework","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d005d6c459a8a9f40f64","word":"housing","forms":["housing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da91b3930aed2850","term":"housing","forms":["housing","housings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提供住所；容納","explanation":"指為人提供住處，或把某物安置、容納在一個空間裡這一行為。它突出“讓物件進入並有地方待著”的過程，與“房子”這一核心形象相連。","examples":[{"en":"The shelter is responsible for housing dozens of families.","zh":"這個收容所負責安置幾十個家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Proper housing of the cables prevents damage.","zh":"妥善容納電纜可以防止損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/housing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3efb36bed8b18fd","term":"housing","forms":["housing","housings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"住房；住宅（總稱）","explanation":"指一批住宅或住房這一整體概念，而不是某一棟具體房屋。它常用於談住房供應、公共住房和不同收入群體的居住條件。","examples":[{"en":"Many students struggle to find affordable housing near campus.","zh":"許多學生很難在校園附近找到負擔得起的住房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city urgently needs more affordable housing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/housing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c8b29e7dc08862f3ec4","word":"hover","forms":["hover"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-378d259078af1609","term":"hover","forms":["hover","hovers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懸停狀態","explanation":"指人、鳥、飛機等停在空中或某處而暫時不移動的動作或狀態，核心畫面就是“懸著不動”。","examples":[{"en":"The drone held a steady hover above the field.","zh":"無人機穩定地懸停在田地上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The helicopter maintained a steady hover above the clearing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec8fdbe21604c7f6","term":"hover","forms":["hover","hovers","hovering","hovered","hoverest","hoveredst","hovereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在空中懸停","explanation":"指鳥、昆蟲、飛機等停在空中或漂浮在某處，位置基本不變。這是“hover”最直接的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"A hummingbird hovered beside the red flowers.","zh":"一隻蜂鳥在紅花旁懸停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The helicopter hovered over the roof.","zh":"直升機懸停在屋頂上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a03c0e1b8f42477e","term":"hover","forms":["hover","hovers","hovering","hovered","hoverest","hoveredst","hovereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在附近徘徊","explanation":"引申指人在某處附近逗留、徘徊，尤其帶有不確定、遲遲不離開的感覺；筆尖停在紙上方也是同一個“懸著不落下”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Several customers hovered around the entrance, waiting for the store to open.","zh":"幾位顧客在入口附近徘徊，等著商店開門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her finger hovered over the send button.","zh":"她的手指停在傳送按鈕上方，遲遲沒有按下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8044aae1f86875d993f2","word":"how","forms":["how"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a8e868b3bd2f24d","term":"how","forms":["how"],"pos":"adv","zh":"多大程度；多頻繁","explanation":"how 放在形容詞或副詞前，詢問某種性質、數量或頻率達到什麼程度，核心感覺是“有多……”。","examples":[{"en":"How often do you practice speaking English?","zh":"你多久練習一次英語口語？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"How difficult was the exam?","zh":"這場考試有多難？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/how","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b577d799dc6ffa4","term":"how","forms":["how"],"pos":"adv","zh":"以什麼方式","explanation":"how 詢問事情是透過什麼方式完成、發生或被解釋的，重點在“怎麼做、怎麼運作”。","examples":[{"en":"How do you solve this puzzle?","zh":"你怎麼解這道謎題？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"How did you get the door open?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/how","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47951833ecf6211793c0","word":"however","forms":["however"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e7285038c7cea7d","term":"however","forms":["however"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不過；然而","explanation":"前面的情況本來會讓人期待某個結果，但後面的事實卻沒有按這個期待發展，因此用 however 表示“儘管如此，還是……”。","examples":[{"en":"The weather was bad. However, we went hiking.","zh":"天氣很糟，不過我們還是去徒步了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was tired; I finished the work, however.","zh":"我很累，不過我還是完成了工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/however","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4ef78672d872a1a","term":"however","forms":["however"],"pos":"adv","zh":"相比之下；然而","explanation":"這裡的 however 把前後兩個情況放在一起比較，指出後一個情況與前一個形成反差。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel was comfortable. The location, however, was inconvenient.","zh":"這家酒店很舒適，不過位置不太方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rooms are small; however, the location is excellent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/however","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1542ab0048c80ebc9a3a","word":"howl","forms":["howl"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c00f0a848f8a06a","term":"howl","forms":["howl","howls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的嚎叫聲","explanation":"指狗、狼、狐狸等犬科動物發出的拖長、響亮而哀鳴般的叫聲；這是 howl 最典型的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We heard the howl of a wolf in the distance.","zh":"我們聽見遠處傳來狼的嚎叫聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog let out a long howl when the siren started.","zh":"警報器響起時，那條狗發出了一聲長長的嚎叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/howl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e76f4f42bce98f94","term":"howl","forms":["howl","howls","howling","howled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出動物般的嚎叫","explanation":"指狗、狼等發出拖長、響亮而哀鳴般的聲音；這是動詞 howl 的核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"The wolves howled together under the full moon.","zh":"滿月下，狼群一起發出嚎叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our dog always howls when it hears the piano.","zh":"我們的狗每次聽到鋼琴聲都會嚎叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/howl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-628fecb264d2e97260ac","word":"hug","forms":["hug"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c46a8ea58638893f","term":"hug","forms":["hug","hugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擁抱","explanation":"指兩個人用手臂緊緊抱住彼此的動作或擁抱本身，通常表達親情、喜悅、安慰、激動等感情，也可能帶有強烈情緒。","examples":[{"en":"She gave her brother a hug before leaving.","zh":"她離開前擁抱了哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the good news, they shared a long hug.","zh":"聽到這個好訊息後，他們緊緊擁抱了很久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f603f2d73f4b8491","term":"hug","forms":["hug","hugs","hugging","hugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擁抱，抱緊","explanation":"指用手臂把某人緊緊抱住，常用於表達親近、安慰、喜悅或激動。這是名詞“擁抱”變成動作後的最常見用法。","examples":[{"en":"Billy hugged Danny until he felt better.","zh":"比利一直抱著丹尼，直到他感覺好些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hugged my mother when I got home.","zh":"我回家時擁抱了媽媽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e580eee1a39851ef636","word":"huge","forms":["huge"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c27e7f0d5615fe39","term":"huge","forms":["huge","huger","more huge","hugest","most huge"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巨大的","explanation":"像一座大到佔滿視野的山一樣，表示實際體積、數量或範圍非常大，明顯超過通常標準。","examples":[{"en":"They built a huge new sports center near the station.","zh":"他們在車站附近建了一座很大的新體育中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A huge crowd gathered outside the theater.","zh":"劇院外聚集了一大群人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/huge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e1cb04d80431802","term":"huge","forms":["huge","huger","more huge","hugest","most huge"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非常有力的；極其投入的","explanation":"由“規模很大”引申為力量或投入程度很大；例如某人是某項事業的堅定支持者，表示支援十分強烈。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is a huge supporter of free public libraries.","zh":"我姐姐非常支援免費公共圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm a huge supporter of community libraries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/huge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04fb78ddc42ed5b74614","word":"hum","forms":["hum"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c500ec09bd61a34","term":"hum","forms":["hum","hums","humming","hummed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"哼唱","explanation":"hum 作動詞時，表示閉著嘴發出連續的旋律聲，通常沒有真正說出歌詞。","examples":[{"en":"She hummed along with the song while she cooked.","zh":"她做飯時跟著歌曲輕聲哼唱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hummed a familiar tune while making tea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7676651158210c99","term":"hum","forms":["hum","hums","humming","hummed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"哼出曲調","explanation":"hum 也可以帶賓語，表示把一首歌、一段曲調或旋律用哼唱的方式表現出來。","examples":[{"en":"Can you hum the melody for me?","zh":"你能為我哼一下這段旋律嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hummed a lullaby while washing the dishes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-79a5478768d2447431a9","word":"human","forms":["human"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8618c8280185772c","term":"human","forms":["human","more human","most human"],"pos":"adj","zh":"人類的；人的","explanation":"指屬於人類這一物種，或與人類有關的事物，重點是“和人相對的其他生物或事物”這一分類關係。","examples":[{"en":"Human beings need clean water to survive.","zh":"人類需要清潔的水才能生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum explores human history.","zh":"這座博物館探討人類歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/human","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33786bc55a7949d4","term":"human","forms":["human","humans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人；人類成員","explanation":"指一個具體的人，或把人看作一種靈長類動物成員；核心概念仍是“屬於人類這一類的個體”。","examples":[{"en":"Humans share common ancestors with other apes.","zh":"人類與其他類人猿擁有共同的祖先。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The robot was designed to help humans.","zh":"這個機器人被設計用來幫助人類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/human","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1db76b4d70514fe4e7aa","word":"humanity","forms":["humanity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdc653c269772c1e","term":"humanity","forms":["humanity","humanities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全人類","explanation":"指所有人組成的整體，強調人類這個群體，而不是某一個具體的人。","examples":[{"en":"Technology should serve humanity as a whole.","zh":"科技應當服務於全人類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The disease poses a serious threat to humanity.","zh":"這種疾病對全人類構成嚴重威脅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humanity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce4bdd1415c0792b","term":"humanity","forms":["humanity","humanities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人類處境或本性","explanation":"指人類共同的生活處境、情感侷限和行為本性，常用於討論人為什麼會這樣生活、思考或犯錯。","examples":[{"en":"The novel explores the complexity of humanity.","zh":"這部小說探討了人類處境的複雜性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The play asks what our failures reveal about humanity.","zh":"這部戲劇追問我們的失敗揭示了人類怎樣的本性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humanity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-851d3fcf9fe60976956b","word":"humble","forms":["humble"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a22bfa9597fa3306","term":"humble","forms":["humble","humbler","more humble","humblest","most humble"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樸素的；不張揚的","explanation":"形容物品、住所、生活方式或出身時，表示簡單樸素、不奢華，也不刻意顯擺。它抓住的是“貼近地面、不往高處炫耀”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"They built a humble home near the river.","zh":"他們在河邊建了一座樸素的房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She came from humble beginnings.","zh":"她出身普通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bc08ea8a1941155","term":"humble","forms":["humble","humbler","more humble","humblest","most humble"],"pos":"adj","zh":"謙遜的；不自大的","explanation":"形容人不把自己看得過高，不炫耀成就，也願意承認自己的侷限。它仍然延續“把自己放低、貼近地面”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Even after winning the award, he remained humble.","zh":"即使獲了獎，他仍然很謙遜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is humble about her achievements.","zh":"她對自己的成就很謙遜，不張揚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9656ef3ddd36b9516237","word":"humid","forms":["humid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0919470f35609d75","term":"humid","forms":["humid","humider","more humid","humidest","most humid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"潮溼的；溼熱悶溼的","explanation":"指空氣或周圍環境中含有較多水分，感覺潮、悶，常用於天氣、氣候或空氣；也可形容帶有潮氣的土地等環境。","examples":[{"en":"The air feels humid after the rain.","zh":"雨後空氣感覺很潮溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The region has a hot, humid climate.","zh":"這個地區氣候炎熱而潮溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba3fb020c49e34898954","word":"humidity","forms":["humidity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5b95872ae776d67","term":"humidity","forms":["humidity","humidities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空氣的潮溼感","explanation":"指空氣潮溼的狀態，尤其強調人感受到的悶、黏和不舒服。空氣裡的水分越多，通常就越容易產生這種感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The high humidity made the room feel hot and stuffy.","zh":"高溼度讓房間感覺又熱又悶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sleep badly when the humidity is high.","zh":"溼度高時，我睡不好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humidity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0ca98227174ec56","term":"humidity","forms":["humidity","humidities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空氣中的水蒸氣含量","explanation":"指空氣中含有多少水蒸氣，是可以測量或用百分比表示的量。溫室、氣象和室內環境控制中常用這個意義。","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse maintains a humidity of 70 percent.","zh":"溫室保持百分之七十的溼度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"High humidity made the afternoon feel even hotter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humidity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2722a61f27b08f78ec3b","word":"humiliate","forms":["humiliate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4587139044e4ec6e","term":"humiliate","forms":["humiliate","humiliates","humiliating","humiliated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使蒙羞；傷害尊嚴","explanation":"指透過言語、行為或公開場面讓某人感到非常難堪，彷彿把他的尊嚴壓到了地上。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher apologized after humiliating the student in front of the class.","zh":"老師在全班同學面前羞辱了那名學生，之後為此道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt humiliated when her mistake was laughed at by everyone.","zh":"自己的錯誤被所有人嘲笑時，她感到非常丟臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humiliate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c50a5e4de8983f75ee4c","word":"humor","forms":["humor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c50ba7c1c3cd4a6e","term":"humor","forms":["humor","humors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心情；幽默感","explanation":"humor 的核心概念是人的“情緒或幽默頻道”。在談心情時，它表示一個人當時的情緒狀態；在談表達方式時，它表示讓人發笑的幽默感。","examples":[{"en":"She was in a good humor after hearing the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息後，她心情很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His humor makes even difficult meetings easier.","zh":"他的幽默感讓即使很難熬的會議也變得輕鬆一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-283deba1f3a5b4a86fb0","word":"humorous","forms":["humorous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25b6ca4dde1507f5","term":"humorous","forms":["humorous","more humorous","most humorous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"幽默的；逗人發笑的","explanation":"指某人、某句話或某種行為帶有幽默感，能夠讓人發笑或感到有趣。這是現代英語中最主要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The waiters were so humorous that the whole table kept laughing.","zh":"服務員們非常幽默，整桌人一直笑個不停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote a humorous story about life in a crowded city.","zh":"她寫了一個關於擁擠城市生活的幽默故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humorous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53017b1a592e45f7","term":"humorous","forms":["humorous","more humorous","most humorous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"詼諧的；機智的","explanation":"強調說話或寫作中有機智、打趣的風格，不一定讓人放聲大笑，但能以輕鬆方式表達觀點。","examples":[{"en":"He added a humorous comment to make the serious discussion less tense.","zh":"他加了一句詼諧的評論，讓嚴肅的討論不那麼緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His humorous observations enlivened the long journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humorous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-977ef51fa0b115429630","word":"hunch","forms":["hunch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef6c656099501bb6","term":"hunch","forms":["hunch","hunches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直覺；預感","explanation":"指沒有完整證據，卻覺得某件事可能如此的直覺判斷；它像心裡突然拱出一個方向，但不等於事實已經確定。","examples":[{"en":"I have a hunch that the missing keys are in the kitchen.","zh":"我預感那串丟失的鑰匙在廚房裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her hunch turned out to be right.","zh":"她的直覺後來證明是對的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f481f267212b4e17","term":"hunch","forms":["hunch","hunches","hunching","hunched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弓著上身","explanation":"指把上身向前彎、同時縮起或抬起肩膀，使身體呈現拱起的姿勢。","examples":[{"en":"Try not to hunch over your phone for hours.","zh":"儘量不要一連幾個小時弓著背看手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hunched over the tiny computer screen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97fe8a374906993133a2","word":"hundred","forms":["hundred"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f51d608c27262b31","term":"hundred","forms":["hundred","hundreds"],"pos":"num","zh":"一百","explanation":"表示數值100，位於99之後，是十的平方。它是所有相關擴充套件義的核心：錢的面額、板球得分和某些歷史區劃都圍繞這個數量展開。","examples":[{"en":"There were a hundred people at the concert.","zh":"音樂會上有一百人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The package weighs one hundred kilograms.","zh":"這個包裹重一百公斤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hundred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1da3efe89dc79d9","term":"hundred","forms":["hundred","hundreds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面額為100的錢","explanation":"指一張面額為100的鈔票，或任何貨幣中面額為100的紙幣；具體是美元、歐元等要看上下文。它是把“100”這個數量直接用在錢的面額上。","examples":[{"en":"I found a hundred in my coat pocket.","zh":"我在外套口袋裡發現了一張面額為100的鈔票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cashier checked the hundred for signs of forgery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hundred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5baba4fb94157978d3d2","word":"hunger","forms":["hunger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b50ffb245f288de","term":"hunger","forms":["hunger","hungers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飢餓；飢餓感","explanation":"指身體需要食物的狀態或感覺，也可以指這種需要本身。它是hunger最基本的意思，所有引申義都可以理解為“身體裡有一個迫切的空缺”。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, we felt a deep hunger.","zh":"長途徒步後，我們感到非常飢餓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smell of fresh bread made my hunger worse.","zh":"新鮮麵包的香味讓我更餓了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb921219d9feb4b9","term":"hunger","forms":["hunger","hungers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈渴望；迫切需要","explanation":"把身體對食物的強烈需要比喻性地用於目標、成就、愛等事物，表示一種迫切而持續的渴望。它比普通的“想要”語氣更強，彷彿內心有一個必須填補的空缺。","examples":[{"en":"She has a hunger for knowledge and asks questions constantly.","zh":"她對知識有強烈的渴望，總是不停地提問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students showed a hunger for new ideas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca4176138ea4086faada","word":"hungry","forms":["hungry"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72768a1754ad1301","term":"hungry","forms":["hungry","hungrier","hungriest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到飢餓的","explanation":"指身體需要食物、肚子感到空或餓的狀態，是 hungry 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I'm hungry, so let's find somewhere to eat.","zh":"我餓了，我們找個地方吃飯吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children came home hungry after school.","zh":"孩子們放學回家時都餓了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hungry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-357cb5463860f048","term":"hungry","forms":["hungry","hungrier","hungriest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"渴望得到的","explanation":"把身體對食物的強烈需要引申為對成功、機會或某種結果的強烈渴望，表示一個人很有衝勁、很想得到某物。","examples":[{"en":"The young players are hungry for a chance to prove themselves.","zh":"這些年輕球員非常渴望得到證明自己的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is hungry for new challenges.","zh":"她非常渴望迎接新的挑戰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hungry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18c3bc28bde14691d7ce","word":"hunt","forms":["hunt"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-694318df83c55fb7","term":"hunt","forms":["hunt","hunts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狩獵行為","explanation":"hunt可以指為了捕殺獵物而進行的打獵行為；它把動詞hunt“打獵”變成了一個活動名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The hunt began before sunrise.","zh":"狩獵在日出前開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hunt for the missing fox lasted all morning.","zh":"尋找那隻失蹤狐狸的行動持續了一整個上午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-170821efc30c3853","term":"hunt","forms":["hunt","hunts","hunting","hunted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打獵","explanation":"hunt最基本的動詞義是到野外追蹤並捕殺動物，通常為了獲取肉食或娛樂。","examples":[{"en":"They hunt deer in the mountains every autumn.","zh":"他們每年秋天都在山裡獵鹿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers hunt for food during the winter.","zh":"村民冬天靠打獵獲取食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37c00ddd244efb51","term":"hunt","forms":["hunt","hunts","hunting","hunted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"尋找","explanation":"hunt也可以把目標換成貝殼、工作或答案，表示費力地尋找某物；這裡保留了“不斷追蹤目標”的感覺，但不一定涉及動物。","examples":[{"en":"The children hunted for shells along the beach.","zh":"孩子們沿著海灘尋找貝殼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is hunting for a new apartment.","zh":"她正在到處尋找新公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9a63a4eb15738ae85cd","word":"hunter","forms":["hunter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23a34698f6deace4","term":"hunter","forms":["hunter","hunters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獵人","explanation":"hunter指為了運動或獲取食物而追蹤、捕捉獵物的人，是這個詞最直接的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The hunter followed the deer through the forest.","zh":"獵人跟著鹿穿過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hunters returned before sunset.","zh":"獵人們在日落前回來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41313a7cc8ab2ffb","term":"hunter","forms":["hunter","hunters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"追逐者","explanation":"在比喻意義上，hunter指追逐或尋找某個目標的人，不限於真正追捕動物；因此也可以說追逐機會、資訊或其他物件的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is a careful hunter of new opportunities.","zh":"她善於謹慎地尋找新的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hunter became the hunted.","zh":"獵人變成了獵物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b441e730bdaeeafb4f06","word":"hurdle","forms":["hurdle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ce251f3bd5fe954","term":"hurdle","forms":["hurdle","hurdles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽欄架","explanation":"指跑步或馬術比賽中設定的欄架，運動員或馬匹必須跳過去。","examples":[{"en":"The runners cleared every hurdle with ease.","zh":"這些跑步者輕鬆跳過了每一道欄架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runner clipped the last hurdle with her foot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurdle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8ab13a0c020549f","term":"hurdle","forms":["hurdle","hurdles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"障礙","explanation":"指擋在人或事情前面的實際障礙，也可以是資金不足、規則限制等抽象困難。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of funding remains the biggest hurdle for the project.","zh":"資金不足仍是這個專案面臨的最大障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of reliable transport remains a major hurdle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurdle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c35c9b3e953a031a","term":"hurdle","forms":["hurdle","hurdles","hurdling","hurdled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跳過","explanation":"指人在奔跑或匆忙移動時跳過某個物體或障礙，動作重點是越過去。","examples":[{"en":"She hurdled the fallen branch and kept running.","zh":"她跳過倒下的樹枝，繼續跑去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A startled deer hurdled the fence and vanished into the trees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurdle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e55d48ebbef06fc","term":"hurdle","forms":["hurdle","hurdles","hurdling","hurdled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"克服障礙","explanation":"把抽象困難看成需要跳過去的欄，表示成功克服問題、限制或阻礙。","examples":[{"en":"The team hurdled several legal obstacles before launching the service.","zh":"這個團隊克服了幾項法律障礙後才推出這項服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The startup hurdled its funding problems with help from local investors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurdle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fb312f8c4f8ecac0a05","word":"hurricane","forms":["hurricane"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ed2f2f05bca7c4b","term":"hurricane","forms":["hurricane","hurricanes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈熱帶氣旋","explanation":"指圍繞中心旋轉、風力極強並常伴有暴雨的熱帶風暴；日常語境中通常譯為“颶風”。它的核心形象就是猛烈旋轉、席捲周圍環境的巨大風暴。","examples":[{"en":"A powerful hurricane is moving toward the coast.","zh":"一場強烈的颶風正向海岸移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hurricane damaged hundreds of homes.","zh":"這場颶風損壞了數百所房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurricane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7da36783fe37be58","term":"hurricane","forms":["hurricane","hurricanes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特定海域的颶風","explanation":"在北大西洋、加勒比海、墨西哥灣以及東太平洋部分海域，達到規定強度的熱帶氣旋稱為hurricane；它通常伴隨雷雨，並可能向溫帶地區移動。","examples":[{"en":"The hurricane brought heavy rain and winds over 120 kilometers per hour.","zh":"這場颶風帶來了大雨，風速超過每小時一百二十公里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Atlantic hurricane damaged hundreds of coastal homes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurricane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f6002cbceb8c0327d974","word":"hurry","forms":["hurry"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a3cf972bdc435b7","term":"hurry","forms":["hurry","hurries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"匆忙；趕時間","explanation":"指為了儘快完成或到達而處於匆忙狀態，重點是動作很快、沒有多少從容時間。","examples":[{"en":"I left home in a hurry and forgot my keys.","zh":"我匆匆離開家，忘了帶鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There's no hurry; the shop stays open late.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4f7285cf24851c4","term":"hurry","forms":["hurry","hurries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緊迫；急著要做","explanation":"表示某件事需要儘快處理，或沒有必要立刻處理；核心是“時間壓力的大小”。","examples":[{"en":"There is no hurry, so you can finish the report tomorrow.","zh":"不著急，你明天完成報告也可以。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There's no hurry; the museum stays open late.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-567a757e8e44dd82","term":"hurry","forms":["hurry","hurries","hurrying","hurried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"趕快；加快行動","explanation":"指自己做事、移動或趕路的速度變快，通常因為遲到、時間不夠或需要儘快完成。","examples":[{"en":"She's hurrying to catch the last train.","zh":"她正趕著去乘最後一班火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hurry or we'll miss the curtain rising.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7cf5840674606c8","term":"hurry","forms":["hurry","hurries","hurrying","hurried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加快速度","explanation":"強調把做某事的速度提高，常常是為了在限定時間內完成。","examples":[{"en":"Hurry up, or we'll miss the beginning of the movie.","zh":"快點，不然我們會錯過電影開頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conductor hurried the musicians through the final rehearsal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49002d515d1605d8e492","word":"hurt","forms":["hurt"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01a5c5787fa56ff8","term":"hurt","forms":["hurt","hurts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心傷；情感上的痛苦","explanation":"指被欺騙、拒絕、羞辱或失望後留下的感情傷痛；它像身體受傷一樣，會持續一段時間並需要恢復。","examples":[{"en":"Talking about it helped her heal an old hurt.","zh":"談論這件事幫助她治癒了舊日的心傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years later, she still remembered the hurt of his betrayal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-333c7f6c8cb43ce5","term":"hurt","forms":["hurt","hurts","hurting","hurtest","hurtedst","hurteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使受傷；弄疼","explanation":"表示某人、動物或行為造成身體疼痛或實際傷害，是“把撞擊和痛傳給別人”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The sharp edge could hurt your hand.","zh":"這個鋒利的邊緣可能會弄傷你的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hurt his ankle while playing football.","zh":"他踢足球時弄傷了腳踝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1cd342388f1ecd8b","term":"hurt","forms":["hurt","hurts","hurting","hurtest","hurtedst","hurteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使感情受傷","explanation":"表示某人的言語或行為讓另一個人在感情上感到痛苦、被冒犯或失望；身體疼痛的影象在這裡轉成了心裡的疼痛。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't mean to hurt your feelings.","zh":"我不是故意要傷你的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was hurt by his careless comment.","zh":"他那句不經意的話讓她很受傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d595537cdb27149","term":"hurt","forms":["hurt","hurts","hurting","hurtest","hurtedst","hurteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"疼；感到疼痛","explanation":"表示身體某處正在疼痛，也可用於較抽象的情感痛苦；這裡重點不是誰造成了傷害，而是痛苦本身存在。","examples":[{"en":"My shoulder hurts when I lift my arm.","zh":"我抬起手臂時肩膀會疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Does it hurt when you walk?","zh":"你走路時會疼嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hurt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fee8f88b93ae8b399f5","word":"husband","forms":["husband"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-818b6f2ed3a64daa","term":"husband","forms":["husband","husbands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"丈夫","explanation":"指處於婚姻關係中的男性配偶，通常是相對於他的妻子或伴侶而言的“丈夫”。這是 husband 最常見、最應優先掌握的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Her husband works at the hospital.","zh":"她的丈夫在醫院工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She introduced me to her husband at dinner.","zh":"她在晚餐時把我介紹給了她的丈夫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/husband","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc8331bcb2283e89d275","word":"hush","forms":["hush"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4dcf40cae2053b7e","term":"hush","forms":["hush"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寂靜","explanation":"指喧鬧或聲音停止後留下的安靜狀態，常帶有夜晚、等待或突然靜下來的氛圍。","examples":[{"en":"We walked home in the hush of the early morning.","zh":"我們在清晨的寂靜中走回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A hush fell over the room before the announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f376e034ef3d961b","term":"hush","forms":["hush","hushes","hushing","hushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變安靜","explanation":"指人、聲音或環境從有聲狀態變得安靜下來，就是“噓”之後聲音逐漸停下的狀態變化。","examples":[{"en":"The children hushed when the teacher entered.","zh":"老師進來時，孩子們安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audience hushed as the lights dimmed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad6d28970c106bb8","term":"hush","forms":["hush","hushes","hushing","hushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使安靜","explanation":"指讓人、聲音或場面安靜下來，就像用手勢示意別人“噓”一樣。","examples":[{"en":"She raised a finger to hush the noisy crowd.","zh":"她豎起一根手指，讓喧鬧的人群安靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher hushed the class with a raised hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d07204fbfa65400b1da","word":"hut","forms":["hut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a48e2a1901438f6","term":"hut","forms":["hut","huts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簡陋小屋","explanation":"指只有一層、通常只有一個房間的簡陋住所或遮蔽處，往往用當地容易取得的材料搭建。它的核心畫面就是“用簡單材料蓋起來的小屋”。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the night in a small hut by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊的一間小屋裡過了一夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shepherd returned to his hut before the storm.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，牧羊人回到了自己的小屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b56c4d5cc05d2350","term":"hut","forms":["hut","huts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小木棚","explanation":"指用木頭搭成的小型棚屋，通常供工作人員看守、儲物或臨時工作使用，而不是供人長期居住。","examples":[{"en":"The park keeper was sitting in a wooden hut near the gate.","zh":"公園管理員正坐在大門附近的一間小木棚裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener keeps his tools in a wooden hut.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0deac0a26c0d846d7869","word":"hybrid","forms":["hybrid"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04b1d1164730eb2b","term":"hybrid","forms":["hybrid","more hybrid","most hybrid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"混合來源或成分的","explanation":"指一個事物由不同來源、風格、材料或型別結合而成，核心就是“兩種不同東西合在一起”。例如音樂同時吸收爵士和朋克風格，就可以說它是 hybrid。","examples":[{"en":"The band created a hybrid sound that blends jazz with punk.","zh":"這支樂隊創造了一種融合爵士和朋克的混合音色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course uses a hybrid teaching model with online and classroom lessons.","zh":"這門課程採用線上與課堂教學相結合的混合教學模式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hybrid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c92f1a4a6985321","term":"hybrid","forms":["hybrid","more hybrid","most hybrid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"混合動力的","explanation":"特指汽車同時使用燃油發動機和電力系統來行駛，因此 hybrid car 就是“混合動力汽車”。這是日常新聞和汽車語境中非常常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a hybrid because we wanted to use less fuel.","zh":"我們買了一輛混合動力車，因為希望少用一些燃油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their hybrid car switches between petrol and electricity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hybrid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87b82f3875a25e51","term":"hybrid","forms":["hybrid","hybrids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雜交後代；混合體","explanation":"指不同物種、品種或純種親本交配後產生的後代，也可泛指由不同型別事物結合形成的混合體。在生物學中，它突出“來自不同親本或來源”。","examples":[{"en":"The mule is a hybrid of a horse and a donkey.","zh":"騾是馬和驢雜交產生的後代。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gardeners prize this hybrid for its large, unusually fragrant flowers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hybrid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e7f90b0310363d697e83","word":"hydrogen","forms":["hydrogen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35fc750168e61239","term":"hydrogen","forms":["hydrogen","hydrogens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氫元素","explanation":"指原子序數為1的化學元素，是所有元素中最輕的一個。這裡強調的是元素這一基本類別，不一定是在說一瓶或一團氫氣。","examples":[{"en":"Hydrogen is the most abundant element in the universe.","zh":"氫是宇宙中含量最豐富的元素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stars produce helium by fusing hydrogen.","zh":"恆星透過氫聚變生成氦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hydrogen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6aafd38e8fadc7e","term":"hydrogen","forms":["hydrogen","hydrogens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氫氣","explanation":"指由氫分子組成的無色、無味、易燃氣體，是氫元素在常溫下常見的一種物質形態。這個意義關注的是可以儲存、洩漏或燃燒的氣體。","examples":[{"en":"The tank is filled with hydrogen.","zh":"這個儲罐裡裝滿了氫氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hydrogen burns quickly in air.","zh":"氫氣在空氣中燃燒得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hydrogen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51cc6dfe4d3c65f6f461","word":"hygiene","forms":["hygiene"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88de543c8962197a","term":"hygiene","forms":["hygiene","hygienes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衛生學","explanation":"指研究如何促進和保持健康的知識或學科，是“衛生防護網”背後的系統理論。","examples":[{"en":"Hygiene plays a central role in public health.","zh":"衛生學在公共健康中發揮著核心作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied hygiene as part of her public-health training.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hygiene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6261f40c11e03319","term":"hygiene","forms":["hygiene","hygienes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衛生措施與條件","explanation":"指有助於促進和保持健康的衛生條件、規則和實際做法，例如處理食物時遵守清潔和安全規範。","examples":[{"en":"Good hygiene is essential when preparing food.","zh":"準備食物時，良好的衛生習慣至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic has strict hygiene standards.","zh":"這家診所實行嚴格的衛生標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hygiene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-857bb592535889733c36","word":"hypocrite","forms":["hypocrite"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03bbed8a96f2c059","term":"hypocrite","forms":["hypocrite","hypocrites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偽君子；表裡不一的人","explanation":"指表面上聲稱相信某種原則、要求別人這樣做，自己卻不按同一標準行事的人。核心不是普通的犯錯，而是把自己裝成某種樣子，同時用另一套方式生活。","examples":[{"en":"He tells everyone to save money, but he spends thousands on clothes every month. What a hypocrite!","zh":"他叫大家都要省錢，自己卻每個月花幾千塊買衣服，真是個偽君子！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She called him a hypocrite for criticizing others while breaking the same rules himself.","zh":"她罵他是偽君子，因為他自己違反同樣的規定，卻還批評別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hypocrite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7beb7f4a57251263ca5d","word":"hypothesis","forms":["hypothesis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35dd6d52b0ab7f73","term":"hypothesis","forms":["hypothesis","hypotheses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可檢驗的假說","explanation":"這是為解釋某個觀察結果或現象而提出的暫時性觀點，必須能透過進一步的觀察、調查或實驗來檢驗。它像是先放在證據下面的一塊支撐板，檢驗結果可以支援它，也可以推翻它。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers designed an experiment to test their hypothesis about sleep.","zh":"研究人員設計了一項實驗，來檢驗他們關於睡眠的假說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The results did not support the original hypothesis.","zh":"結果並不支援原來的假說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hypothesis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9dc09e7330c7555a","term":"hypothesis","forms":["hypothesis","hypotheses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"論證中的假設","explanation":"這裡不一定是科學假說，而是為了展開論證或調查，暫時把某件事當作真的前提。推理完成後，這個前提仍可能需要驗證或被否定。","examples":[{"en":"For the sake of argument, let us accept the hypothesis that the witness was mistaken.","zh":"為了展開論證，我們暫且接受證人弄錯了這一假設。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For this proof, take the hypothesis as given.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hypothesis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63b10fe34084556a64e6","word":"I (me, my, mine, myself)","forms":["I"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b0d94c933290403","term":"I","forms":["I"],"pos":"pron","zh":"我（主語）","explanation":"I 表示說話者或作者本人，作句子的主語，相當於“我”。它是第一人稱單數代詞，並且在英語中始終寫成大寫 I。","examples":[{"en":"I need a little more time.","zh":"我還需要一點時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I saw your message this morning.","zh":"我今天早上看到了你的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/I","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cb0b250c6250d528f3e","word":"ice","forms":["ice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0160aa50bc146e72","term":"ice","forms":["ice","ices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冰","explanation":"ice 最基本的意思是凍結的水，也就是水冷下來後形成的固體；它正對應記憶中的“冷而凝固的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Please put some ice in my tea.","zh":"請在我的茶里加些冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lake was covered with ice after the cold night.","zh":"經過寒冷的一夜，湖面結滿了冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3df2151b4a7a502b64c4","word":"iceberg","forms":["iceberg"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e6b5bed9dadf36f","term":"iceberg","forms":["iceberg","icebergs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漂浮的巨大冰體","explanation":"指冰川或冰架斷裂後漂浮在海面上的巨大冰塊，露出水面的部分通常只是整體的一小部分。","examples":[{"en":"The ship changed course after the crew spotted an iceberg ahead.","zh":"船員發現前方有一座冰山後，船就改變了航向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A large iceberg broke away from the ice shelf and drifted south.","zh":"一座巨大的冰山從冰架上斷裂下來，向南漂去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iceberg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c6e8e9233c06ff6","term":"iceberg","forms":["iceberg","icebergs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隱患初現的災難","explanation":"比喻一種即將造成嚴重損失的災難或危機，目前只顯露出一小部分，真正的影響還沒有完全出現；就像水下隱藏著更大的冰體。","examples":[{"en":"The budget shortfall may be only the tip of a much larger iceberg.","zh":"預算缺口可能只是一個大得多的隱患露出水面的一角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing payment was only the tip of the iceberg.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iceberg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2d4b446a44ce54fab8e","word":"icon","forms":["icon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc39cb0b8cbe5327","term":"icon","forms":["icon","icons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標誌性人物或事物","explanation":"指某個領域中極具代表性、幾乎可以成為該領域象徵的人或事物。這裡的“影象”從實際畫面擴充套件成了“代表整個領域的形象”。","examples":[{"en":"She became an icon of modern fashion.","zh":"她成了現代時尚的標誌性人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old theater is an icon of the city.","zh":"這座老劇院是這座城市的標誌性建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/icon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e741338e2047d3dd","term":"icon","forms":["icon","icons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機圖示","explanation":"指介面上用來代表程式、檔案、裝置或操作的小圖片。它正是“用一幅小圖代表某個功能或物件”的最常見現代用法。","examples":[{"en":"Click the speaker icon to adjust the volume.","zh":"點選揚聲器圖示來調節音量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The file icon is missing from my desktop.","zh":"我的桌面上找不到檔案圖示了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/icon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6393507a33556ff93929","word":"icy","forms":["icy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f92ca57aeb4f81f","term":"icy","forms":["icy","icier","iciest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冰冷的；嚴寒的","explanation":"表示溫度很低，像冰一樣冷，也可以表示環境帶有嚴寒、霜凍的感覺。這是 icy 最基本的字面義。","examples":[{"en":"An icy wind blew through the open window.","zh":"一陣刺骨的寒風從開著的窗戶吹進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lake was icy even in early autumn.","zh":"即使在初秋，湖水也冷得像冰一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/icy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15c53d5e0a5ed803","term":"icy","forms":["icy","icier","iciest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結冰的；被冰覆蓋的","explanation":"表示某個表面或物體上有冰，全部或部分被冰覆蓋。重點不是單純溫度低，而是確實形成了冰層。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful—the steps are icy.","zh":"小心，臺階結冰了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The icy pavement made every step uncertain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/icy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae0a9ad3227c5420c07d","word":"idea","forms":["idea"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbab1e9a57d7f92d","term":"idea","forms":["idea","ideas","ideæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"想法；看法","explanation":"這是最核心的意思：idea 是頭腦裡形成的一個想法、觀點或念頭。那盞燈只是告訴你“我這樣想”，並不一定意味著你已經有了具體行動計劃。","examples":[{"en":"I have an idea for making the room brighter.","zh":"我有個讓房間更明亮的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That is an interesting idea, but I am not sure it will work.","zh":"這是個有意思的想法，但我不確定它能不能奏效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f0ef05fb8596b9e","term":"idea","forms":["idea","ideas","ideæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計劃；打算","explanation":"當腦中的想法已經指向要做的事情時，idea 就表示計劃或打算，也就是“這盞燈照出了下一步怎麼做”。","examples":[{"en":"Do you have any idea how we can solve this problem?","zh":"你有沒有想過我們可以怎樣解決這個問題？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My idea is to leave early and avoid the traffic.","zh":"我的計劃是早點出發，避開交通擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbc8a8ffa86a593fb890","word":"ideal","forms":["ideal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c92c34e557115700","term":"ideal","forms":["ideal","more ideal","most ideal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最合適的；最佳的","explanation":"表示在當前目標和條件下最合適、最能達到效果的選擇，是“完美藍圖”在現實選擇中的應用。","examples":[{"en":"This quiet room is ideal for studying.","zh":"這間安靜的房間最適合學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spring is the ideal time to visit the garden.","zh":"春天是參觀這座花園的最佳時節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14c16137f16a78e6","term":"ideal","forms":["ideal","more ideal","most ideal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完美無缺的","explanation":"表示某人或某事完全符合心目中的標準，沒有明顯缺點，是“完美藍圖”最直接的現實對應。","examples":[{"en":"She would be an ideal candidate for the position.","zh":"她會是這個職位的理想人選。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experiment was conducted under ideal conditions.","zh":"這項實驗是在完美的條件下進行的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-372b130c9d65b636","term":"ideal","forms":["ideal","ideals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理想；完美標準","explanation":"指心中認為值得追求的完美標準或目標，是把“完美藍圖”當作行動方向。它可以是外貌、品格、社會狀態等方面的標準。","examples":[{"en":"Her ideal is to build a kinder and fairer community.","zh":"她的理想是建立一個更友善、更公平的社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He refused to abandon his ideals for money.","zh":"他不願為了金錢放棄自己的理想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-319e2ba078f51cfad133","word":"identical","forms":["identical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73f70b89234a342a","term":"identical","forms":["identical","more identical","most identical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完全相同","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物擁有完全一樣的一組特徵，實際觀察中無法區分；這是 identical 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The two keys are identical to each other.","zh":"這兩把鑰匙彼此完全相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They bought identical jackets in different sizes.","zh":"他們買了完全一樣、只是尺寸不同的夾克。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6433caf08dcc5f0","term":"identical","forms":["identical","more identical","most identical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"就是同一個；並非另一個","explanation":"強調某人或某物與先前提到的物件是同一個，而不是另一個類似物件；它把“相同”推進到“身份也相同”。","examples":[{"en":"That is the identical chair I saw in the shop yesterday.","zh":"那正是我昨天在商店裡看到的那把椅子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The identical mistake appeared in both reports.","zh":"兩份報告中出現的是同一個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd3dfa76050e048e229d","word":"identification","forms":["identification"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37ad2ee3487e2f0b","term":"identification","forms":["identification","identifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辨認；確定是什麼","explanation":"指透過觀察、檢查等方式弄清楚某人是誰，或某物究竟是哪一種、哪一個。重點在於把物件和正確的名稱或類別對應起來。","examples":[{"en":"Accurate identification of the plant took several hours.","zh":"準確辨認出這種植物花了幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The software helps with the identification of unusual sounds.","zh":"這款軟體有助於辨認不尋常的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a978477014e2c069","term":"identification","forms":["identification","identifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辨認並核實身份","explanation":"在較寬的意義上，不僅要判斷物件是誰或是什麼，還要檢查這個判斷是否可靠；因此它把“辨認”和“確認身份”看作一個完整過程。","examples":[{"en":"Early identification of the disease can improve treatment.","zh":"及早識別並確認這種疾病，有助於改善治療效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Identification of the victim took several days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e23ac1e6f5b01ae","term":"identification","forms":["identification","identifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身份證明檔案","explanation":"指能證明一個人身份的證件或證件資料，例如身份證、護照等。這裡的 identification 是“用來證明你是誰的東西”，不是辨認過程。","examples":[{"en":"Please show identification before entering the building.","zh":"進入大樓前請出示身份證明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I left my identification at home.","zh":"我把身份證明檔案落在家裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f780b5c735e70251a83","word":"identify","forms":["identify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bd510332b657e7e","term":"identify","forms":["identify","identifies","identifying","identified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確認身份；認出","explanation":"透過證據、外表或其他線索確認某人是誰、某物是什麼。它是“給物件貼上正確身份標籤”的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"The witness identified the man in the photograph.","zh":"證人認出了照片中的那名男子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists identified the source of the contamination.","zh":"科學家確認了汙染源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63817583d627b16c","term":"identify","forms":["identify","identifies","identifying","identified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"覺得自己像；與……產生認同","explanation":"把自己看作與某人相似，或覺得自己的經歷、感受與對方相連，彷彿把對方的身份標籤部分貼到了自己身上。","examples":[{"en":"Many readers identify with the character's loneliness.","zh":"許多讀者都能體會這個角色的孤獨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She identified herself with the young artist in the novel.","zh":"她覺得自己和小說中的年輕藝術家很相像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb39457bb0c4be79","term":"identify","forms":["identify","identifies","identifying","identified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認同某群體或立場","explanation":"把自己看作某個群體的一員，或認為自己與該群體共享相同的價值觀、感受或立場。","examples":[{"en":"He identifies with people who have moved to a new country.","zh":"他認同那些移居到新國家的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She identifies with the environmental movement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-689f6a627384c7dcb2dc","word":"identity","forms":["identity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23fcb63e81ced15a","term":"identity","forms":["identity","identities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同一性；相同這一事實","explanation":"identity 可以指兩個或多個物件實際上是同一個，或具有完全相同的身份與本質。重點不在外表相似，而在確認“它們就是同一個”這一事實。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are still investigating the identity of the two samples.","zh":"科學家仍在調查這兩個樣本是否屬於同一物種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The identity of the two samples was confirmed chemically.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d14a5ab518653861","term":"identity","forms":["identity","identities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身份；個性認同","explanation":"identity 是一個人、群體或事物區別於其他同類的特徵，也指一個人對“我是誰”的穩定認識。經歷重大變化時，人可能會覺得自己的身份或自我認同變得模糊。","examples":[{"en":"Moving to a new country made her question her identity.","zh":"搬到一個新的國家讓她開始質疑自己的身份認同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team has developed a strong identity over the years.","zh":"這個團隊這些年來形成了鮮明的集體特色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e435b8219f449ac4a7c9","word":"ideology","forms":["ideology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18538bb44bed3446","term":"ideology","forms":["ideology","ideologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意識形態；思想體系","explanation":"指個人、群體或組織用來理解世界、判斷對錯並指導行動的一整套觀念、信念或原則。它像一副共同佩戴的思想眼鏡，因此既可以影響政治，也可以影響社會運動、宗教團體或其他組織。","examples":[{"en":"The movement was built on an ideology of equality.","zh":"這場運動建立在平等思想體系的基礎上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People with different political ideologies can still work together.","zh":"政治意識形態不同的人仍然可以合作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ideology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15626af7abddf6321e27","word":"idiom","forms":["idiom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33f75c72d73598d2","term":"idiom","forms":["idiom","idioms","idiomata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語言特有的表達方式","explanation":"指一個語言、語言家族或群體特有的說話和表達習慣；重點不在某一個短語，而在整套表達方式。","examples":[{"en":"The translation sounds awkward because it follows the idiom of the original language too closely.","zh":"這個譯文聽起來不自然，因為它過分照搬了原語言的表達方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The translation preserves the idiom of everyday Spanish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idiom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cd46ef87abae57f","term":"idiom","forms":["idiom","idioms","idiomata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固定習語","explanation":"指由幾個片語成、約定俗成的固定表達，其整體意思不能只把各個詞的字面意思相加來推斷。比如表示“下傾盆大雨”的固定說法，實際並不是說天上真的在掉小動物。","examples":[{"en":"“Break the ice” is an idiom meaning to make people feel more relaxed when they first meet.","zh":"“打破僵局”是一個習語，意思是讓初次見面的人放鬆下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You should learn this idiom as a whole rather than translate each word separately.","zh":"你應該把這個習語整體記住，而不是分別翻譯每個詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idiom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48fab7a56479b7ec15bd","word":"idiot","forms":["idiot"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-304d3afd60858ae9","term":"idiot","forms":["idiot","idiots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傻瓜；作蠢事的人","explanation":"指作出明顯愚蠢決定的人，不一定真的智力低下；重點是他這次的行為或判斷像個傻瓜。","examples":[{"en":"I was an idiot and left my keys on the train.","zh":"我真是個傻瓜，竟然把鑰匙落在火車上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt like an idiot after locking myself out.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idiot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4fb62348858c2f6fbd6d","word":"idle","forms":["idle"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fad5a459ed126b59","term":"idle","forms":["idle","more idle","most idle"],"pos":"adj","zh":"閒置的；未使用的","explanation":"東西或時間沒有被充分使用，處在“停在一旁”的狀態；時間閒著也可指沒有重要活動。","examples":[{"en":"The factory has several idle machines.","zh":"這家工廠有幾臺閒置的機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I spent a few idle hours reading by the window.","zh":"我在窗邊讀書，消磨了幾個空閒小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9168a06d334e03c","term":"idle","forms":["idle","more idle","most idle"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無所事事的；不工作的","explanation":"人沒有從事工作或其他明確活動，只是閒著；也可以指暫時沒有工作的工人或僱員。","examples":[{"en":"The workers were idle while they waited for new instructions.","zh":"工人們在等待新指示時無所事事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent the afternoon idle instead of finishing the report.","zh":"他整個下午都在閒著，沒有完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-678be429bff5b95d","term":"idle","forms":["idle","idles","idling","idled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閒著；無所事事","explanation":"沒有工作或明確任務，只是待著消磨時間；可以是暫時閒著，也可以是在某處無目的地逗留。","examples":[{"en":"We idled around the station until the train arrived.","zh":"火車到來前，我們一直在車站附近閒逛消磨時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He idled in the café instead of going back to work.","zh":"他待在咖啡館裡閒著，沒有回去工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cde5eea74b81768","term":"idle","forms":["idle","idles","idling","idled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發動機怠速運轉","explanation":"發動機以較低轉速執行，但沒有帶動裝置或車輛正常行駛，像是機器處於“半閒置”狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The car idled outside while I ran into the shop.","zh":"我進商店時，汽車在外面怠速運轉著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not leave the truck idling for too long.","zh":"不要讓卡車長時間怠速運轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e614f65efb0fdb09af60","word":"idol","forms":["idol"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d314919b8a237adb","term":"idol","forms":["idol","idols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神像；偶像","explanation":"指被人當作具有神聖力量而加以膜拜的雕像或形象，常見於宗教或批評偶像崇拜的語境中。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers were warned not to worship idols made of wood and stone.","zh":"村民們被告誡不要膜拜用木頭和石頭製成的偶像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ancient temple once held a golden idol.","zh":"那座古老的神廟裡曾經供奉著一尊金色偶像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a8df18346aa78ee","term":"idol","forms":["idol","idols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文化偶像；崇拜物件","explanation":"指在某個社會、時代或領域中極具代表性、受到大眾推崇的人物，也可以泛指被人高度崇拜的物件。這是從“被仰望的形象”發展出來的現代用法。","examples":[{"en":"For many young athletes, she is an idol who represents courage and discipline.","zh":"對許多年輕運動員來說，她是一位代表勇氣和自律的偶像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The singer became an idol for a generation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/idol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-935f68319d4f227e02bf","word":"if","forms":["if"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"if","forms":["if"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"如果；假如","examples":[{"en":"If you leave now, you can catch the early train.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We will play outside if the rain stops.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"if","forms":["if"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"是否","examples":[{"en":"Please ask if the store offers free delivery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"I wonder if she has already received the letter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5dfc5900a1d1569667a","word":"ignorance","forms":["ignorance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d772f33614c734b","term":"ignorance","forms":["ignorance","ignorances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無知；不瞭解","explanation":"指一個人缺少某方面的知識或資訊，因此不瞭解相關事實、規則或主題。重點是“沒有知道”，不一定表示這個人沒有能力學習。","examples":[{"en":"His ignorance of local customs caused several awkward moments.","zh":"他不瞭解當地習俗，造成了好幾次尷尬的場面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course is designed to replace ignorance with basic knowledge.","zh":"這門課程旨在用基礎知識消除無知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ignorance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3192a0b4ddbf6259d7c8","word":"ignorant","forms":["ignorant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68a5e1547ea45a07","term":"ignorant","forms":["ignorant","ignoranter","more ignorant","ignorantest","most ignorant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無知的；缺乏知識的","explanation":"指一個人整體上缺少知識或教育，對許多本應瞭解的事情並不瞭解；重點是“知識不足”，不一定表示智力低下。","examples":[{"en":"He was ignorant of basic history.","zh":"他連基本的歷史知識都不瞭解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is unfair to call her ignorant just because she has not studied science.","zh":"僅僅因為她沒有學過科學，就說她無知是不公平的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ignorant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-175029d4d5606fa4","term":"ignorant","forms":["ignorant","ignoranter","more ignorant","ignorantest","most ignorant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不知道的；未意識到的","explanation":"指某人不知道某個事實或沒有意識到某種情況，範圍可以很小，常常只涉及一件具體的事。","examples":[{"en":"We were ignorant of the change in schedule.","zh":"我們不知道日程已經改變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was ignorant of the danger nearby.","zh":"她沒有意識到附近有危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ignorant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f0af516936c6ab13dfc","word":"ignore","forms":["ignore"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-85efd49c1288933e","term":"ignore","forms":["ignore","ignores","ignoring","ignored","ignorest","ignoredst","ignoreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"故意不理會","explanation":"指明明知道某人或某事，卻有意不聽、不回應或不給它注意力，就像主動把注意力的門關上。","examples":[{"en":"She ignored my advice and made the same mistake again.","zh":"她沒有理會我的建議，又犯了同樣的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you ignore the warning, the problem may get worse.","zh":"如果你不理會這個警告，問題可能會變得更嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ignore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8e8b317ee8309d5","term":"ignore","forms":["ignore","ignores","ignoring","ignored","ignorest","ignoredst","ignoreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝作沒看見","explanation":"指看見或意識到某人、某事的存在，卻故意表現得像沒看見一樣，常常因此不打招呼、不回應。","examples":[{"en":"He saw me at the door but ignored me.","zh":"他在門口看見了我，卻裝作沒看見我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ignored her wave and crossed the street.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ignore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c426a5fe614fcd11a22e","word":"ill","forms":["ill"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-83ddd401eac487b3","term":"ill","forms":["ill","iller","more ill","illest","most ill"],"pos":"adj","zh":"惡意的；刻薄的","explanation":"指某人的意圖或行為帶著傷害、欺負或不友善的傾向，是“壞”這一核心概念在人際關係中的表現。","examples":[{"en":"The workers complained about ill treatment from their manager.","zh":"工人們抱怨經理對他們惡劣相待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bear him no ill will despite our disagreement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa3221be6a8845fd","term":"ill","forms":["ill","iller","more ill","illest","most ill"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生病的；身體不適的","explanation":"指健康狀況不好或患病，是現代英語中最重要的基本義之一；身體被“壞”的狀態影響，就表現為生病。","examples":[{"en":"She has been seriously ill for several weeks.","zh":"她已經重病幾個星期了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He fell ill during the trip.","zh":"他在旅途中病倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f358d2ed6b845be","term":"ill","forms":["ill","ills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疾病；病痛","explanation":"指一種身體疾病或長期病痛，是形容詞“生病的”轉化出的名詞義；複數可泛指多種病痛。","examples":[{"en":"The treatment relieved several of his long-term ills.","zh":"這種治療減輕了他幾種長期的病痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The herbalist claimed her tea cured every ill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f63a8387f34cb135de24","word":"illuminate","forms":["illuminate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd0483c1f8019f29","term":"illuminate","forms":["illuminate","illuminates","illuminating","illuminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"照亮","explanation":"把光投到某物上，使它從黑暗中顯現出來；這是 illuminate 最直接的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The streetlights illuminated the narrow road.","zh":"路燈照亮了那條狹窄的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lantern illuminated the faces around the table.","zh":"一盞燈籠照亮了桌邊每個人的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illuminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3dd9f5b0ea5e4ae","term":"illuminate","forms":["illuminate","illuminates","illuminating","illuminated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"闡明","explanation":"像把光照進一個難懂的問題，使其中的關係、原因或細節變得清楚易懂。","examples":[{"en":"The report illuminates the causes of the housing shortage.","zh":"這份報告闡明瞭住房短缺的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her example illuminated a difficult idea.","zh":"她舉的例子使一個難懂的概念變得清楚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illuminate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-171aac72c04f6eaa2516","word":"illusion","forms":["illusion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1cc62392d3f35fbc","term":"illusion","forms":["illusion","illusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"假象；錯覺","explanation":"某個東西看起來像另一種東西，實際上並不是；它可以來自光線、影子、距離等造成的視覺誤判，也可以泛指令人誤認的表象。","examples":[{"en":"The fog created the illusion of a lake in the distance.","zh":"霧氣造成了遠處有一片湖的假象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The moving lights gave the illusion that the wall was breathing.","zh":"移動的燈光讓人產生牆壁在呼吸的錯覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cebb0612b5b251c3","term":"illusion","forms":["illusion","illusions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錯誤信念；誤解","explanation":"指一個人相信某件事是真的，但事實並非如此；這裡的“假象”從眼睛看到的東西延伸到了頭腦中的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"He lives under the illusion that money can solve every problem.","zh":"他一直錯誤地以為錢能解決所有問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They were under the illusion that admission was free.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illusion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2ec3e85b72ddfae1c31","word":"illustrate","forms":["illustrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c9c4316b077c48b","term":"illustrate","forms":["illustrate","illustrates","illustrating","illustrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用例子或比較說明","explanation":"透過具體例子、故事、比較或圖示，把抽象的觀點講得更清楚；這裡的“圖”也可以只是聽者腦中形成的形象。","examples":[{"en":"This case illustrates why small changes can have large effects.","zh":"這個案例說明了為什麼微小的變化可能帶來巨大的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She illustrated her point with a short story.","zh":"她用一個小故事說明了自己的觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illustrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a2b48bd1630c765","term":"illustrate","forms":["illustrate","illustrates","illustrating","illustrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給書刊配圖或圖表","explanation":"為書、文章或其他出版物加入照片、插圖、地圖、圖表等，使內容更直觀，也可能兼有裝飾作用。","examples":[{"en":"The new edition is illustrated with maps and photographs.","zh":"新版配有地圖和照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sister illustrated the children's book with watercolor paintings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illustrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-498cc84b29cb560e15b4","word":"illustration","forms":["illustration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04e188335e0743b8","term":"illustration","forms":["illustration","illustrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"例證；說明性的事例","explanation":"指用來讓人理解某個觀點、情況或抽象概念的具體例子、比較或事件。它就像給抽象意思打上一束光，讓讀者透過一個看得見的事例弄明白。","examples":[{"en":"Her kindness was an illustration of the team's true spirit.","zh":"她的善意體現了這個團隊真正的精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This case is a useful illustration of how quickly rumors spread.","zh":"這個案例很好地說明了謠言傳播得有多快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illustration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ae48f2ba9aa4c0e","term":"illustration","forms":["illustration","illustrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"插圖；說明圖","explanation":"指書籍、雜誌或其他出版物中的圖畫，用來裝飾文字，或幫助讀者理解文字內容。它仍然是在“把意思畫出來”，只是說明工具從語言變成了影象。","examples":[{"en":"The book has colorful illustrations of animals.","zh":"這本書有色彩鮮豔的動物插圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The illustration showing the water cycle helped the students understand it.","zh":"展示水迴圈的插圖幫助學生理解了這個過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illustration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6105d6cc76af400325e9","word":"image","forms":["image"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3749447fa24a646a","term":"image","forms":["image","images"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影象；形象","explanation":"指用繪畫、雕刻、攝影或其他方式呈現某物外形的影象，是“把東西呈現出來”的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed an image of the ancient king.","zh":"博物館展出了一幅古代國王的畫像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The satellite sent back clear images of the coast.","zh":"衛星傳回了海岸的清晰影象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/image","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f7faeefc3ceac00","term":"image","forms":["image","images"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腦海中的形象；印象","explanation":"指不在眼前的事物在人腦中形成的畫面或概念；它不是實際物體，而是心裡“浮現出的影像”。","examples":[{"en":"The poem creates a vivid image of a quiet village.","zh":"這首詩生動地描繪出了一個寧靜村莊的畫面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"When I hear that song, an image of my childhood comes to mind.","zh":"我聽到那首歌時，童年的畫面就會浮現在腦海中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/image","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-835a7b97400b906b","term":"image","forms":["image","images"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公眾形象；風格印象","explanation":"指別人對某個人、團體或公司的整體看法，包括其表現出來的風格、穿著和氣質；這是“呈現給別人看的形象”。","examples":[{"en":"The company is trying to improve its image among younger customers.","zh":"這家公司正努力改善自己在年輕顧客中的形象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He carefully chose his clothes to create a professional image.","zh":"他仔細挑選衣服，以塑造專業的形象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/image","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0c4a7ff52c65c773e24","word":"imaginary","forms":["imaginary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3eff6e93d9f7a73","term":"imaginary","forms":["imaginary","more imaginary","most imaginary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"想象中的；虛構的","explanation":"指只存在於人的想象、故事或頭腦中的事物，現實中並沒有對應的實體。例如兒童想象出的朋友就是 imaginary。","examples":[{"en":"The child had an imaginary friend named Leo.","zh":"這個孩子有一個名叫利奧的想象中的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel takes place in an imaginary country.","zh":"這部小說發生在一個虛構的國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imaginary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fd3d60ce9d3c5f5","term":"imaginary","forms":["imaginary","more imaginary","most imaginary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"虛數的","explanation":"數學中指沒有實數部分、與虛數單位相乘形成的數或相關概念。它仍然是數學中有明確定義的物件，並不是日常意義上的“虛假數字”。","examples":[{"en":"The equation has an imaginary solution.","zh":"這個方程有一個虛數解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The square root of minus one is an imaginary number.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imaginary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec3d00212250fb995d08","word":"imagination","forms":["imagination"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d5a215c89d82f7b","term":"imagination","forms":["imagination","imaginations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"想象力","explanation":"指人在腦中構造或再現畫面的能力，即使眼前沒有這個事物，也能設想它的樣子、情景或可能性。這是 imagination 最基礎的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Children use their imagination to turn a cardboard box into a spaceship.","zh":"孩子們用想象力把一個紙箱變成宇宙飛船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good stories give your imagination room to grow.","zh":"好的故事會給你的想象力留下成長的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imagination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57fd9ccdca223813","term":"imagination","forms":["imagination","imaginations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創造力","explanation":"指把腦中的新點子變成有用、獨特方案的能力。它是想象力在實際工作、設計或解決問題中的積極表現。","examples":[{"en":"Her imagination helped the team find a simple solution to a difficult problem.","zh":"她的創造力幫助團隊找到了一個難題的簡單解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her imagination transformed cardboard boxes into castles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imagination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25299588df215e5ac15c","word":"imaginative","forms":["imaginative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d376b06f5c3303b1","term":"imaginative","forms":["imaginative","more imaginative","most imaginative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富有想象力的","explanation":"形容一個人腦中能形成豐富、新穎的畫面或想法，通常表示這個人有創造力，而不只是愛做白日夢。","examples":[{"en":"She is an imaginative child who invents games for everyone.","zh":"她是個很有想象力的孩子，總能為大家 придум出各種遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need to be imaginative to solve this problem.","zh":"要解決這個問題，你需要有豐富的想象力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imaginative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92620d4922ef0bb2","term":"imaginative","forms":["imaginative","more imaginative","most imaginative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有創意的；新奇巧妙的","explanation":"形容故事、設計、計劃或解決辦法等，不是普通地重複已有做法，而是藉助想象力產生新穎、有趣的構思。","examples":[{"en":"The book offers an imaginative way to explain science to children.","zh":"這本書用一種富有創意的方式向孩子解釋科學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The architect proposed an imaginative use of the narrow site.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imaginative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fdd65bbaaa687d48dc8","word":"imagine","forms":["imagine"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b720885a1d105b7b","term":"imagine","forms":["imagine","imagines","imagining","imagined","imaginest","imaginedst","imagineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想象出畫面","explanation":"指在腦中形成某個事物、人物或場景的畫面，即使眼前並沒有它；這是 imagine 最基本的意義。","examples":[{"en":"Can you imagine living on a small island?","zh":"你能想象住在一個小島上嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Imagine a room filled with sunlight.","zh":"想象一下有一間灑滿陽光的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imagine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12fda0156b21c7f6","term":"imagine","forms":["imagine","imagines","imagining","imagined","imaginest","imaginedst","imagineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"料想、認為","explanation":"表示根據現有情況作出一個不太確定的判斷，相當於“我想、我料想、我認為”；這裡不一定真的在腦中構造畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I imagine she'll be tired after the trip.","zh":"我想她旅行之後會很累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I imagine the shops will be crowded tomorrow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imagine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9cfdfe79dbd192f3","term":"imagine","forms":["imagine","imagines","imagining","imagined","imaginest","imaginedst","imagineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設想","explanation":"把一個並不存在或尚未發生的情境放進腦中來考慮，例如設想“如果我們是兄弟姐妹”這樣的假設；它是“腦內投影”的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Imagine that we had to start over tomorrow.","zh":"設想一下，如果我們明天必須重新開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Imagine living somewhere without roads or electricity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imagine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-003c443ef2785c0937de","word":"imitate","forms":["imitate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5eb2a1f90dfba30","term":"imitate","forms":["imitate","imitates","imitating","imitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"模仿；仿照","explanation":"把某人、某物或某種樣式當作樣板，照著複製它的聲音、動作、外表或做法。重點不是單純受到影響，而是主動做出相似的表現。","examples":[{"en":"Young children often imitate their parents.","zh":"小孩子常常模仿父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor can imitate the singer's voice perfectly.","zh":"這名演員能把那位歌手的聲音模仿得惟妙惟肖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f921321aaedb0bb53398","word":"imitation","forms":["imitation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c12efe22caa4b947","term":"imitation","forms":["imitation","imitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"模仿行為","explanation":"指照著某人或某物去做、去表現的行為，也就是把原來的樣子或方式複製過來。這個意義強調“模仿的過程”，而不是最後做出的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The child gave a funny imitation of his teacher.","zh":"那個孩子滑稽地模仿了他的老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her imitation of the singer's voice was remarkably accurate.","zh":"她對那位歌手嗓音的模仿非常逼真。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4dba16a3b926707","term":"imitation","forms":["imitation","imitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"仿製品；仿造物","explanation":"指模模擬品做出來的東西，或看起來像真品但並不是真品的替代物。這裡的 imitation 是模仿行為留下的具體結果，常帶有“不是真正的那個東西”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The sofa is covered in imitation leather.","zh":"這張沙發包著仿皮革材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The necklace was an imitation of a famous royal jewel.","zh":"這條項鍊是一件仿製的著名王室珠寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-251ce3daf88ff66915c6","word":"immediate","forms":["immediate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbde54de0dbe926e","term":"immediate","forms":["immediate","more immediate","most immediate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"立即的；馬上發生的","explanation":"表示事情中間沒有等待，馬上發生或馬上得到結果。這是日常和工作語境中最重要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We need an immediate response to this problem.","zh":"我們需要立即回應這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medicine brought immediate relief.","zh":"這種藥馬上緩解了症狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immediate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e2c56b7a3e8380c","term":"immediate","forms":["immediate","more immediate","most immediate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"緊鄰的；直接的","explanation":"表示人與人、地點或關係之間沒有隔著別人或別的層級，距離很近或聯絡很直接。例如 immediate family 指最親近的直系家人。","examples":[{"en":"Only her immediate family knew about the decision.","zh":"只有她的直系家人知道這個決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are no shops in the immediate vicinity.","zh":"附近緊鄰的地方沒有商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immediate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07f33781121e176596b3","word":"immense","forms":["immense"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e490e78fb3b5fbfe","term":"immense","forms":["immense","immenser","immensest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巨大無比的","explanation":"表示體積、距離、數量或程度大得驚人，彷彿大到難以測量；它比普通的“大”更有震撼感。","examples":[{"en":"The project required an immense amount of time and money.","zh":"這個專案需要投入巨量的時間和金錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An immense wall stood between the two towns.","zh":"兩座城鎮之間矗立著一堵巨大無比的牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7847617cb587526","term":"immense","forms":["immense","immenser","immensest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極好的；棒極了的","explanation":"在非正式口語中，immense 可以把“巨大”的強烈感覺轉成誇讚，表示某人或某事好得不得了、令人非常滿意。","examples":[{"en":"The band was absolutely immense last night.","zh":"昨晚那支樂隊簡直棒極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drummer was immense throughout the final set.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-353e5d16112c5f1bfb5e","word":"immigrant","forms":["immigrant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93b5b2b2c5166c62","term":"immigrant","forms":["immigrant","immigrants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"移民；移居者","explanation":"指從一個國家來到另一個國家，並打算在那裡永久或長期定居的人。這個詞把重點放在“從外地遷入並紮根”，而不只是“不是本地人”。","examples":[{"en":"Her grandparents were immigrants from Italy.","zh":"她的祖父母是從義大利來的移民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many immigrants build new lives in the city.","zh":"許多移民在這座城市建立了新的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immigrant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de41e5c8b23a3d008474","word":"immigrate","forms":["immigrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"immigrate","forms":["immigrate"],"pos":"v.","zh":"移居外國；移入","examples":[{"en":"Her parents decided to immigrate to Canada in search of work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"People who immigrate often need time to adjust to a new language.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ecfc652f6b09c9facb7","word":"immigration","forms":["immigration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1290dd8353bede3b","term":"immigration","forms":["immigration","immigrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遷入別國定居","explanation":"指原本不是該國出生的人進入這個國家，並以長期或永久居住為目的；重點是“遷進去”，而不是短期旅行。它既可以說這種社會現象，也可以說某一批人的遷入。","examples":[{"en":"Immigration to the city has grown rapidly in recent years.","zh":"近年來，遷入這座城市的人數迅速增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country is reviewing its immigration policy.","zh":"這個國家正在審查其移民政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immigration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cd3450aeeb4272e","term":"immigration","forms":["immigration","immigrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入境檢查","explanation":"指人在機場或邊境透過移民官檢查、核驗證件並辦理入境手續的過程；這裡說的不是遷居本身，而是抵達後要透過的那一關。","examples":[{"en":"We waited at immigration for nearly an hour after landing.","zh":"我們落地後在入境檢查處等了將近一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We passed through immigration before collecting our luggage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immigration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9323c87c2e56962f17f","word":"imminent","forms":["imminent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f072585fd925cf4d","term":"imminent","forms":["imminent","more imminent","most imminent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迫在眉睫的；即將發生的","explanation":"指某件事已經近在眼前，很快就會發生，彷彿懸在頭頂、隨時可能落下；重點是發生時間非常近，而不只是將來某個時候會發生。","examples":[{"en":"The arrival of the storm is imminent.","zh":"暴風雨很快就要來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company’s closure now seems imminent.","zh":"這家公司現在看來很快就要關閉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imminent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-808a374d01599f57dd4f","word":"immune","forms":["immune"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4af71d3b390d5cb0","term":"immune","forms":["immune","more immune","most immune"],"pos":"adj","zh":"豁免的；免於承擔的","explanation":"指某人依法不受某種追究、懲罰或義務約束，就像有一道保護層把責任擋在外面。最常見的是免於起訴或其他法律後果。","examples":[{"en":"As a diplomat, she was immune from prosecution.","zh":"作為外交官，她享有免於被起訴的豁免權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Diplomats are immune from certain forms of prosecution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c1bd5544ce567ef","term":"immune","forms":["immune","more immune","most immune"],"pos":"adj","zh":"免疫的","explanation":"指身體已經透過接種或自身抵抗力形成保護，因此不容易感染某種疾病。這是醫學和日常健康話題中最重要的含義之一。","examples":[{"en":"After the vaccination, she became immune to the disease.","zh":"接種疫苗後，她對這種疾病產生了免疫力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most children are immune to chickenpox after vaccination.","zh":"大多數兒童接種疫苗後都對水痘有免疫力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c4f992dfe6d3201","term":"immune","forms":["immune","more immune","most immune"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不受影響的；不為所動的","explanation":"把“保護層”擴大到非醫學領域，表示某人或某物經得住誘惑、批評、勸說或其他影響，怎麼刺激都不起作用。","examples":[{"en":"He seemed immune to their criticism.","zh":"他似乎完全不受他們批評的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is immune to his charm.","zh":"她完全不為他的魅力所動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/immune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f61f46c23a66607af75","word":"impact","forms":["impact"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d8d084196af371a","term":"impact","forms":["impact","impacts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重大影響","explanation":"指某人或某事像一次強烈撞擊一樣，對決定、生活或結果造成明顯而有力的改變。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy will have a major impact on small businesses.","zh":"新政策將對小企業產生重大影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her decision had a lasting impact on the whole team.","zh":"她的決定對整個團隊產生了持久影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6438e55d5483c94","term":"impact","forms":["impact","impacts","impacting","impacted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強烈影響","explanation":"指某事物像強烈撞擊一樣，明顯改變某人的決定、某項計劃或某種結果。","examples":[{"en":"The delay could impact our travel plans.","zh":"這次延誤可能會影響我們的旅行計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The closure had a devastating impact on the village.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114,115],"total":5,"counts":{"111":1,"114":3,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-e7735f86642e2f00514b","word":"imperative","forms":["imperative"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad6840048f9102b9","term":"imperative","forms":["imperative","more imperative","most imperative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"必須的；至關重要的","explanation":"某件事重要到不能拖延或省略，帶有“非做不可”的壓力。它比普通的“重要”語氣更強，常暗示不這樣做就會造成嚴重後果。","examples":[{"en":"It is imperative that we leave before the storm arrives.","zh":"我們必須在暴風雨到來前離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is imperative to check the pressure first.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c992a38f0a8a6469","term":"imperative","forms":["imperative","more imperative","most imperative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"命令式的；強制性的","explanation":"表示話語、要求或行動帶有直接命令的力量，要求別人服從，而不是僅僅提出建議。","examples":[{"en":"The officer spoke in an imperative tone.","zh":"那名軍官用命令式的口吻說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer's imperative tone left no room for discussion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61c31f70a91c6dfc","term":"imperative","forms":["imperative","imperatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祈使語氣","explanation":"一種用來表達命令、請求或指示的語氣；在英語裡，祈使句中的動詞通常採用動詞原形形式。","examples":[{"en":"“Open the window” is an example of the imperative.","zh":"“開啟窗戶”是一個祈使語氣的例子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sentence uses the imperative to give an order.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd74f1ce3ba0720d","term":"imperative","forms":["imperative","imperatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必須做的事","explanation":"指一項不能迴避、必須完成的行動或任務。這裡保留了“命令”的核心感覺，只是命令可能來自形勢、責任或現實需要，而不一定來自某個人。","examples":[{"en":"Protecting clean water is an imperative for every community.","zh":"保護清潔水源是每個社群都必須承擔的任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Protecting the water supply became an urgent imperative.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a5b8990e60ffa74e154","word":"imperial","forms":["imperial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-406fb43afeb7b853","term":"imperial","forms":["imperial","more imperial","most imperial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"帝國的；皇帝的","explanation":"指屬於帝國、皇帝或女皇，或與他們有關的事物；可以把它記成“帝國宮殿裡的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displays an imperial crown from the nineteenth century.","zh":"博物館展出了一頂十九世紀的帝國王冠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The palace once housed the imperial family.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9429ac489d006688","term":"imperial","forms":["imperial","more imperial","most imperial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"宏大的；壯麗的","explanation":"形容規模、外觀或氣勢非常宏大、華美，像帝國建築一樣有壓倒性的氣派。","examples":[{"en":"They walked through an imperial hall covered with gold decorations.","zh":"他們走過一座飾有金色裝飾的宏偉大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The palace rose above the gardens in imperial splendor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9bb818d84838e08127b","word":"implement","forms":["implement"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-513f266085681293","term":"implement","forms":["implement","implements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工具；器具","explanation":"它是填補工作需要的實物工具，通常有明確用途，例如耕作、修理或手工製作所用的器具。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer keeps his gardening implements in the shed.","zh":"農民把園藝工具放在工具棚裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archaeologists uncovered several wooden farming implements.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/implement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c424bcd8427b4051","term":"implement","forms":["implement","implements","implementing","implemented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"實施；落實","explanation":"作動詞時，是把紙面上的計劃或想法填進現實行動中，按照決定真正執行起來。","examples":[{"en":"The school will implement a new safety policy next month.","zh":"學校將於下個月實施一項新的安全政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council will implement the new parking rules next month.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/implement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c8dc148912ef0688116","word":"implication","forms":["implication"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b1c6916d2675f08","term":"implication","forms":["implication","implications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可能產生的後果","explanation":"指一個決定、行動或事件可能帶來的影響和後果，常常不止一個，因此談論具體影響時很常用複數。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy could have serious implications for small businesses.","zh":"這項新政策可能會給小企業帶來嚴重後果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We discussed the implications of canceling the contract.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/implication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ebda96286b35460","term":"implication","forms":["implication","implications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暗含的意思","explanation":"指話語沒有直接說出、卻可以根據上下文合理推知的意思；它像是藏在話語背後的那根線，把聽者引向一個結論。","examples":[{"en":"Her silence carried the implication that she disagreed.","zh":"她的沉默暗含著她並不同意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The implication was that our services were unnecessary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/implication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a8f7b6c00a3d17deeef","word":"implicit","forms":["implicit"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24f02d90b794fdf6","term":"implicit","forms":["implicit"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未明說但可推知的","explanation":"某個意思沒有直接說出來，但聽者或讀者可以根據上下文、語氣或內容推知；重點是“存在這個意思，卻沒有明講”。","examples":[{"en":"Her silence carried an implicit warning.","zh":"她的沉默中含有一個未明說的警告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article makes an implicit criticism of the policy.","zh":"這篇文章含蓄地批評了這項政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/implicit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29d79ff084b7469e","term":"implicit","forms":["implicit"],"pos":"adj","zh":"本質上含有但未顯露的","explanation":"某種性質或結果已經包含在事物本身之中，只是沒有公開表現出來；它更強調“內在包含”，不一定是某人有意暗示。","examples":[{"en":"There is an implicit assumption that everyone will agree.","zh":"其中含有一個未明說的前提，即所有人都會同意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A promise of fairness is implicit in the agreement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/implicit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3b290f1c5ba865dbcea","word":"imply","forms":["imply"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e78618e0c6b03c01","term":"imply","forms":["imply","implies","implying","implied","impliest","impliedst","implieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"必然意味著","explanation":"某個事實、條件或行動把另一個結果“折”在裡面，因此前者成立時，後者會作為必要後果被推出。這裡強調邏輯上的必然聯絡，不只是可能相關。","examples":[{"en":"A rise in prices does not imply that every shop is overcharging.","zh":"價格上漲並不意味著每家商店都在漫天要價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Correlation does not imply causation.","zh":"相關性並不意味著因果關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30d44b70b6a47072","term":"imply","forms":["imply","implies","implying","implied","impliest","impliedst","implieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"由邏輯推斷出","explanation":"說話者給出一個事實或判斷，讓聽者根據其中的邏輯關係推出另一個意思；重點是推理能得到的含義，不一定是說話者有意暗示。","examples":[{"en":"Her silence implied that she had already made up her mind.","zh":"她的沉默讓人推斷出她已經拿定了主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A falling temperature does not imply that snow is certain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d942f64886578d874731","word":"import","forms":["import"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-847f571f9574e0f2","term":"import","forms":["import","imports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進口商品","explanation":"指從外國或其他外部地區帶進來、通常用於銷售或貿易的商品。它強調的是被帶進來的東西，而不是進口這一行為本身。","examples":[{"en":"The store sells imported cars, but its wine import is small.","zh":"這家商店銷售進口汽車，但葡萄酒進口量很小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cheap imports crowded the shelves of local shops.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/import","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b452952e4ea50b5","term":"import","forms":["import","imports","importing","imported"],"pos":"verb","zh":"進口","explanation":"指把商品從外國帶入本國，通常為了銷售或貿易；這是“從外部帶進來”這一核心概念的直接應用。","examples":[{"en":"The country imports most of its coffee from Brazil.","zh":"這個國家的大部分咖啡都從巴西進口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country imports most of its medical equipment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/import","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1ec49df3bf4c283a28f","word":"importance","forms":["importance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a17c301758c48f7","term":"importance","forms":["importance","importances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要性","explanation":"指某人或某事具有重要價值、值得注意的性質，也就是“重要”這一點本身。它可以說明為什麼某件事需要被重視。","examples":[{"en":"The importance of regular sleep is often underestimated.","zh":"規律睡眠的重要性常常被低估。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stressed the importance of checking the figures twice.","zh":"她強調了把數字核對兩遍的重要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/importance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c28a84592e70cb0","term":"importance","forms":["importance","importances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意義；分量","explanation":"指某件事在某個問題、領域或局勢中的意義和分量，強調它會帶來多大影響或應受到多大關注。","examples":[{"en":"The map's importance became clear when we lost our way.","zh":"我們迷路後，才明白這張地圖有多重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old bridge has considerable historical importance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/importance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34a989eb3e220e6b0b19","word":"important","forms":["important"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e11be1457619f1c5","term":"important","forms":["important","more important","importanter","most important","importantest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"重要的；關鍵的","explanation":"指某人或某事很有分量，對結果、決定或生活有明顯影響，因此值得特別重視。它不只表示“有用”，還可以表示在某個情境中不可忽視或起關鍵作用。","examples":[{"en":"It is important for new drivers to check their mirrors regularly.","zh":"新司機定期檢查後視鏡很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This small detail is important to the success of the project.","zh":"這個小細節對專案的成功很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/important","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0734bf93ed06c9169956","word":"impose","forms":["impose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42fad91d0eeb9de2","term":"impose","forms":["impose","imposes","imposing","imposed","imposest","imposedst","imposeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"施加；強制實行","explanation":"把某項規定、限制、稅費或責任正式加到某人、某群體或某事物上，通常帶有權威施加負擔的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The government imposed a new tax on imported goods.","zh":"政府對進口商品徵收了一項新稅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court imposed a heavy fine on the company.","zh":"法院對這家公司處以重罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1b25fae4728563b","term":"impose","forms":["impose","imposes","imposing","imposed","imposest","imposedst","imposeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把負擔或影響強加於","explanation":"把某種主要是抽象的負擔、限制、壓力或影響放到某人或某事物上；也可以表示某人或某事強行佔據、壓制對方。這個用法正是“把沉重的東西放到別人身上”這一核心畫面的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The long journey imposed a great strain on everyone.","zh":"這段漫長的旅程給每個人都帶來了很大壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new rules impose extra costs on small businesses.","zh":"新規定給小企業增加了額外成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14a597b3268c192faccf","word":"imposing","forms":["imposing"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a85c164decbc7446","term":"imposing","forms":["imposing","more imposing","most imposing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"氣勢宏大，令人印象深刻","explanation":"指某人、某物或某個場面憑藉高大、莊嚴的外表、規模或氣勢給人很強的印象，常讓人感到敬畏。","examples":[{"en":"The mountain looked imposing against the evening sky.","zh":"傍晚的天空映襯下，那座山顯得氣勢恢宏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old courthouse has an imposing entrance.","zh":"那座老法院的入口氣勢宏大，令人印象深刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imposing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b87169a483e64f360504","word":"impress","forms":["impress"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dcbfb407136f1979","term":"impress","forms":["impress","impresses","impressing","impressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使人讚歎","explanation":"指某人的表現、能力或品質強烈影響了別人，通常讓對方覺得出色、佩服或滿意。","examples":[{"en":"The young designer impressed the judges with her bold ideas.","zh":"這位年輕設計師大膽的想法給評委們留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was impressed by how calmly he handled the problem.","zh":"他處理問題時的冷靜讓我很佩服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60e94711a6eb1955","term":"impress","forms":["impress","impresses","impressing","impressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在心裡留下鮮明印象","explanation":"指某個景象、聲音或經歷深深進入人的記憶，好像把一道痕跡壓進了心裡。","examples":[{"en":"The sight of the empty village impressed itself on my memory.","zh":"那個空無一人的村莊景象深深印在我的記憶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tragedy impressed upon him the fragility of life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00d89c6761d9ad962549","word":"impression","forms":["impression"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64600198d41078df","term":"impression","forms":["impression","impressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壓出的凹痕；印記","explanation":"某物受到壓力後，在另一個物體表面留下的凹痕或形狀痕跡，就是 impression；這是“留下印記”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The keys left a clear impression in the soft clay.","zh":"鑰匙在柔軟的黏土上留下了清晰的印記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wax retained a detailed impression of the stolen ring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1e5397f48c51051","term":"impression","forms":["impression","impressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總體印象；影響","explanation":"某人的言行或某件事在別人心中留下的總體感覺或評價，稱為 impression；它就像心理上留下的痕跡。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm answer made a strong impression on the interview panel.","zh":"她鎮定的回答給面試小組留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to make a good impression on your new colleagues.","zh":"要努力給新同事留下好印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b98fecba93fd4a7fb31e","word":"impressive","forms":["impressive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4a58190ca0ceaec","term":"impressive","forms":["impressive","more impressive","most impressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人印象深刻的","explanation":"指某人或某事物效果突出、水平很高或規模很大，因而給人留下強烈而通常正面的印象。","examples":[{"en":"Her speech was impressive despite its simplicity.","zh":"她的演講雖然簡潔，卻給人留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team achieved an impressive result in its first season.","zh":"這支隊伍在第一個賽季就取得了令人矚目的成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d52f60f52adbd8bd","term":"impressive","forms":["impressive","more impressive","most impressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有吸引力的","explanation":"指某人或某事物具有讓人喜歡、欣賞或願意接近的特點；重點不一定是規模大，而是整體效果討人喜歡。","examples":[{"en":"The small house has an impressive, welcoming design.","zh":"這座小房子的設計很有吸引力，給人溫馨的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apartment boasts an impressive view of the harbor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-258f953a9e65b478ffa3","word":"imprison(ment)","forms":["imprison","imprisonment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74a5ee6239d5ee3e","term":"imprison","forms":["imprison","imprisons","imprisoning","imprisoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"監禁；關押","explanation":"指把某人關進監獄，或強行限制在某個地方，使其不能自由離開。這裡的核心畫面就是把人鎖進一個封閉空間；在比喻用法中，也可表示彷彿把人困住。","examples":[{"en":"The authorities imprisoned him in a small cell.","zh":"當局把他關進了一個小牢房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt imprisoned in a job she hated.","zh":"她覺得自己彷彿被困在一份討厭的工作裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imprison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f2d40882a734680","term":"imprisonment","forms":["imprisonment","imprisonments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監禁；入獄","explanation":"指把人關在監獄或其他封閉場所中，限制其自由，尤其是作為犯罪後的懲罰；也可泛指被關押的狀態或經歷。","examples":[{"en":"He was sentenced to five years' imprisonment for fraud.","zh":"他因詐騙罪被判處五年監禁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Long imprisonment had changed her view of freedom.","zh":"長期監禁改變了她對自由的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imprisonment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e48397b37fd1f537dad1","word":"improve(ment)","forms":["improve","improvement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22262062a1d3d6c5","term":"improve","forms":["improve","improves","improving","improved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改善；提高","explanation":"表示主動讓某個東西變得更好，或提高它的價值、質量、效率和成果。物件既可以是具體事物，也可以是技能、方法、成績等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"A new website could improve our customer service.","zh":"新網站可以改善我們的客戶服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is taking a course to improve her writing.","zh":"她正在上課，以提高自己的寫作能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/improve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f70baed4453b67b0","term":"improve","forms":["improve","improves","improving","improved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變好；改善","explanation":"表示某人的健康、能力、表現或某種情況自行朝更好的方向發展，重點是“變得更好”，而不是強調誰主動做了改善。","examples":[{"en":"Her English has improved a lot this year.","zh":"她的英語今年進步了很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His condition improved after a few days of rest.","zh":"休息幾天後，他的情況有所好轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/improve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-838d49d6544ea964","term":"improvement","forms":["improvement","improvements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"改善；改進","explanation":"指讓某事物變得更好這一過程，強調從原來的狀態向更好的狀態發展。它可以用於能力、制度、環境、成績等抽象物件，也可以用於具體事物。","examples":[{"en":"There has been a clear improvement in her English.","zh":"她的英語有了明顯進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new system has brought a major improvement in safety.","zh":"新系統大幅提高了安全性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/improvement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a4e6414ce7762ac","term":"improvement","forms":["improvement","improvements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"改善後的狀態；進步","explanation":"指事物已經變得更好的狀態或程度，重點不在“做改善”的動作，而在改善所帶來的結果。它和 s1 緊密相連：s1 更像“變好的過程”，s3 更像“變好之後的狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"The patient is showing steady improvement.","zh":"病人正在穩步好轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can see a real improvement in your writing.","zh":"我能看出你的寫作確實有了進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/improvement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d490624d0f219289f998","word":"impulse","forms":["impulse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a2a43ba0dcbfb08","term":"impulse","forms":["impulse","impulses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推動力；推力","explanation":"指把物體向前推、使它開始運動或改變運動狀態的力量。它也可以較抽象地表示促使某件事發生的推動因素，是“推動”這一核心概念的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden impulse sent the cart rolling down the slope.","zh":"突然的一股推力使小車沿著斜坡滾了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The explosion gave the spacecraft a brief forward impulse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impulse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c2be8acce8f9f7d","term":"impulse","forms":["impulse","impulses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衝動；突然的慾望","explanation":"指突然冒出來、促使人立刻做某事的慾望或念頭。它可以是消極的衝動，例如突然想買東西，也可以是積極的內在推動，例如想學習或幫助別人。","examples":[{"en":"On impulse, I bought the bright red jacket.","zh":"我一時衝動，買下了那件鮮紅色的夾克。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She resisted the impulse to check her phone during the meeting.","zh":"她忍住了開會時檢視手機的衝動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impulse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-582967534d0f909d196b","word":"in","forms":["in"],"officialPos":"prep./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afcf19754b7fe18e","term":"in","forms":["in","more in","most in"],"pos":"adj","zh":"在室內；在家或工作地點","explanation":"表示某人就在室內，通常是在家、辦公室或自己的工作地點；記住它就是“進入一個範圍並處於其中”。","examples":[{"en":"Is Anna in?","zh":"安娜在嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m in all afternoon if you need me.","zh":"你要找我的話，我整個下午都在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e84368c161dc56cd","term":"in","forms":["in"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向裡面；進來","explanation":"表示朝某個室內空間或內部移動，重點是從外面進入範圍之內。","examples":[{"en":"Come in and take a seat.","zh":"進來坐吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog ran in when the door opened.","zh":"門一開，狗就跑了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58036cefc552bb3f","term":"in","forms":["in"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……裡面；處於……範圍內","explanation":"表示人或事物已經進入某個範圍並處於其中，可以是具體空間、時間範圍，也可以是抽象的情況或領域。","examples":[{"en":"The dog is in the kennel.","zh":"狗在狗舍裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spare key is in the kitchen drawer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a09fc71725e9911","term":"in","forms":["in"],"pos":"prep","zh":"進入；到裡面去","explanation":"表示從外部向某個範圍內部移動，重點是“進入”這個方向；這正是“進入一個範圍並處於其中”的動態用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please come in and take a seat.","zh":"請進來坐吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the folded receipt in your pocket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba66450affc4547b40d2","word":"incentive","forms":["incentive"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf0a684d7a75cac0","term":"incentive","forms":["incentive","more incentive","most incentive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有激勵作用的","explanation":"表示某事物能像火星一樣點燃行動的意願，使人更願意去做某事。","examples":[{"en":"The tax break was an incentive for companies to hire more workers.","zh":"減稅政策鼓勵企業僱用更多員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers receive incentive payments for meeting production targets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incentive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34052ecb731dfd21","term":"incentive","forms":["incentive","incentives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動力；誘因","explanation":"指促使人採取行動的事物，可以是獎勵、好處、壓力之外的吸引力，或任何能點燃行動意願的因素。","examples":[{"en":"People have little incentive to save money when prices keep rising.","zh":"物價持續上漲時，人們幾乎沒有存錢的動力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discount provides an incentive to book early.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incentive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1cf6e72a3b6db4bc509c","word":"inch","forms":["inch"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31ba1013fd26d0dd","term":"inch","forms":["inch","inches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英寸","explanation":"inch是英制長度單位，一英寸等於2.54釐米，傳統上可粗略想成成年人大拇指的寬度。","examples":[{"en":"The picture is eight inches wide.","zh":"這幅畫寬八英寸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cut the rope into twelve-inch pieces.","zh":"把繩子剪成每段十二英寸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7189cfb30dc01cb","term":"inch","forms":["inch","inches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一點點距離","explanation":"在比喻用法中，inch不強調精確的單位，而是強調距離非常短，幾乎一點也沒有。","examples":[{"en":"She refused to move an inch on the issue.","zh":"在這個問題上，她一點也不肯讓步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat was only an inch from the edge.","zh":"那隻貓離邊緣只有一點點距離。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4191834714542dcf3e5","word":"incident","forms":["incident"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f4e71afc01531da","term":"incident","forms":["incident","incidents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事件","explanation":"指發生過的一件事情，尤其是值得提起、回憶或說明的事情。它可以是普通事件，也可以是意外事件，不自動錶示嚴重事故。","examples":[{"en":"She told us about an incident on her way home.","zh":"她告訴我們一件回家路上發生的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The incident was reported to the police.","zh":"這起事件被報告給了警方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-622128caf9c860eda024","word":"incline","forms":["incline"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bd437581c08c703","term":"incline","forms":["incline","inclines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斜坡","explanation":"指向上或向下傾斜的地面或道路，也就是一條偏離水平線的坡。坡度越大，通常越難走或越難爬。","examples":[{"en":"To reach the station, we had to climb a steep incline.","zh":"為了到達車站，我們不得不爬上一段陡坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wheelchair ramp has a gentle incline.","zh":"輪椅坡道的坡度很緩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-552c303ccabbf971","term":"incline","forms":["incline","inclines","inclining","inclined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使傾斜","explanation":"指把身體或物體從原來的水平或垂直方向推向一邊，使它偏離原來的直線。核心畫面就是“讓一條線朝某個方向歪過去”。","examples":[{"en":"She inclined her head toward the speaker.","zh":"她把頭朝說話的人微微側過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He inclined his body against the strong wind.","zh":"他讓身體向強風吹來的反方向傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c416b5361b4c5922","term":"incline","forms":["incline","inclines","inclining","inclined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傾斜；呈斜面","explanation":"指物體本身偏離水平線或垂直線，處於斜著的狀態。它和名詞“斜坡”共享同一個核心畫面，只是這裡強調發生傾斜的狀態或變化。","examples":[{"en":"The old wall inclines slightly toward the road.","zh":"那面舊牆向道路一側略微傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The path inclines sharply toward the summit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0cbff04cc90f5b4cd53","word":"include","forms":["include"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae7e40e6c9ba1d8e","term":"include","forms":["include","includes","including","included"],"pos":"verb","zh":"納入；把……算入","explanation":"指主動把某人、某物或某項內容放進一個群體、清單、範圍或總數中，使它成為整體的一部分。記住“把東西關進整體”的畫面，就能理解“把費用也算進去”這類用法。","examples":[{"en":"The tour price includes breakfast and airport transfer.","zh":"這次旅行的價格包括早餐和機場接送。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please include my name in the guest list.","zh":"請把我的名字列入賓客名單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/include","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7fd2483ebb07e604","term":"include","forms":["include","includes","including","included"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包含；包括在內","explanation":"指一個整體裡面已經有某個部分，或某個範圍把某項內容算在其中。它仍然來自“關進整體”的核心畫面，但重點從“放進去”轉為“裡面有”。","examples":[{"en":"The course includes six practical workshops.","zh":"這門課程包括六次實踐工作坊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fee includes all materials.","zh":"這筆費用包括所有材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/include","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-031af55b1821e721e588","word":"including","forms":["including"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c4c01fc7e11653f","term":"including","forms":["including"],"pos":"prep","zh":"包括；其中有","explanation":"把後面的一個或多個物件放進前面所說的整體範圍裡，既可以表示明確包含，也可以用來舉出其中的例子。它的畫面就是先有一個大框，再指出框中的幾項。","examples":[{"en":"The price includes breakfast, including fresh fruit and coffee.","zh":"這個價格包括早餐，其中有新鮮水果和咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone was invited, including my next-door neighbor.","zh":"每個人都受到了邀請，包括我隔壁的鄰居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/including","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":4,"counts":{"111":1,"113":3}}},{"id":"ceec-1b5541ff45ff5f9c7457","word":"inclusive","forms":["inclusive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24803d5b4237afcf","term":"inclusive","forms":["inclusive","more inclusive","most inclusive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"範圍廣泛且儘量全部包含","explanation":"指某個清單、範圍或安排把其中幾乎所有相關內容都納入，不把重要專案排除在外。它強調“覆蓋面完整”，而不只是內容數量多。","examples":[{"en":"The report provides an inclusive list of possible causes.","zh":"這份報告列出了幾乎所有可能的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need an inclusive plan that considers small businesses as well as large companies.","zh":"我們需要一項兼顧小企業和大公司的全面計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inclusive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c5acf51093daf91","term":"inclusive","forms":["inclusive","more inclusive","most inclusive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"包括起點和終點","explanation":"用於數字、日期或其他範圍時，表示範圍兩端的值也算在內；例如從一數到十，十也包括在內。","examples":[{"en":"The course runs from September 1 to September 15, inclusive.","zh":"課程從九月一日持續到九月十五日，包括這兩天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Read pages ten to twenty inclusive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inclusive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00cf141f881d4b5572d4","word":"income","forms":["income"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d1e46ee747d8099","term":"income","forms":["income","incomes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收入","explanation":"指個人、家庭或機構透過工作、經營、投資等方式獲得的錢，是 income 最常見的意思。它強調錢進入某人的經濟生活，不限於工資。","examples":[{"en":"Her income comes from teaching and freelance design.","zh":"她的收入來自教學和自由職業設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family needs a higher income to cover rising costs.","zh":"這個家庭需要更高的收入來應付不斷上漲的開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/income","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d058d61344f1cd52","term":"income","forms":["income","incomes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資金流入；收益","explanation":"指進入基金、賬戶、保單或其他金融安排的錢，重點不在誰工作賺錢，而在資金作為收益或收入流入某個地方。","examples":[{"en":"The fund generates enough income to support the project.","zh":"這隻基金產生的收益足以支援這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rental income covered most of her living expenses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/income","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd4b5d65b6a2c33af6d5","word":"incorporate","forms":["incorporate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9521c337d41fcf6b","term":"incorporate","forms":["incorporate","incorporates","incorporating","incorporated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"納入；包含","explanation":"把某個部分、想法或特徵放進一個更大的整體，使它成為整體的一部分。這是 incorporate 最常用、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The new plan incorporates several suggestions from the staff.","zh":"新計劃納入了員工提出的幾項建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kitchen design incorporates plenty of storage space.","zh":"廚房設計中融入了充足的儲物空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incorporate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d0e336180572a56","term":"incorporate","forms":["incorporate","incorporates","incorporating","incorporated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"混入；調和","explanation":"把一種成分加入另一種成分，並透過攪拌或處理使它們均勻地結合在一起。這裡仍然是“讓東西進入同一個整體”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Gradually incorporate the melted butter into the sauce.","zh":"把融化的黃油逐漸拌入醬汁中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Incorporate the melted butter gradually into the mixture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incorporate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e20a548f23fa36bc8d5b","word":"increase","forms":["increase"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc1a4d407c2e72a6","term":"increase","forms":["increase","increases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"增加的量","explanation":"指某個數量比原來多出來的部分，重點是“增加了多少”。例如風險、價格或人數的上升幅度都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"There was a sharp increase in food prices this year.","zh":"今年食品價格大幅上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They received an increase of twenty pounds per week.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/increase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f032e0e862a3ab15","term":"increase","forms":["increase","increases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"增加過程","explanation":"指數量、程度或規模逐漸變大的過程，重點是“變大這件事”，而不只是最後多出來的數額。","examples":[{"en":"The increase in traffic has made the roads much noisier.","zh":"交通量的增加使道路變得吵鬧多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The steady increase in noise disturbed nearby residents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/increase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6399189534e861ec","term":"increase","forms":["increase","increases","increasing","increased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得更多或更大","explanation":"指數量、程度或規模自己變大，畫面是東西沿著“往上長”的方向發展。主語是發生變化的事物，而不是使它變化的人。","examples":[{"en":"Her confidence increased after she passed the exam.","zh":"她透過考試後信心增強了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature increased by five degrees overnight.","zh":"一夜之間氣溫升高了五度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/increase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-391b6bb746758692","term":"increase","forms":["increase","increases","increasing","increased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變得更多或更大","explanation":"指主動讓某個數量、程度或規模變大，也就是把“往上長”施加到另一個物件上。主語是造成變化的人、組織或事物。","examples":[{"en":"The company increased production to meet demand.","zh":"公司提高了產量以滿足需求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to increase the budget by ten percent.","zh":"我們需要把預算增加百分之十。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/increase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bf67200c28902770671","word":"incredible","forms":["incredible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5eaee42a0232c0f","term":"incredible","forms":["incredible","more incredible","most incredible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難以置信的","explanation":"指事情離常理或預期太遠，讓人覺得幾乎不可能相信；這裡保留了“衝擊大到不敢相信”的基本畫面，通常不一定是在誇獎。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden disappearance of the island seemed incredible.","zh":"那座島突然消失，令人難以置信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is incredible that nobody was hurt in the accident.","zh":"事故中竟然沒有人受傷，實在難以置信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incredible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aac80ee985af0bd2","term":"incredible","forms":["incredible","more incredible","most incredible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"驚人的；令人震撼的","explanation":"指某個場面、效果或經歷帶來的衝擊非常強，讓人驚歎甚至說不出話；它是從“難以相信”發展出來的積極用法。","examples":[{"en":"The incredible fireworks lit up the whole harbor.","zh":"那場令人震撼的煙花照亮了整個港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave an incredible performance at the concert.","zh":"她在音樂會上呈現了令人驚歎的表演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incredible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-1703e69d5070324f9040","word":"incur","forms":["incur"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2188b44428813689","term":"incur","forms":["incur","incurs","incurring","incurred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"招致並承擔","explanation":"指由於自己的行為或某種情況，使費用、債務、損失、責任等落到自己身上，並因此需要承擔它。它常常帶有“招來麻煩或負擔”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The company incurred heavy losses after the factory closed.","zh":"工廠關閉後，公司遭受了重大損失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You may incur extra charges if you cancel the booking late.","zh":"如果你臨近預訂日期才取消，可能會產生額外費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/incur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d888a3e4ea95d4043e8c","word":"indeed","forms":["indeed"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9395c462a2a103c3","term":"indeed","forms":["indeed"],"pos":"adv","zh":"確實；事實上","explanation":"用於確認前面或後面的內容符合事實，相當於“確實如此”或“事實上”。它常把一句話牢牢釘在事實層面上。","examples":[{"en":"Indeed, the plan had several serious problems.","zh":"事實上，這個計劃確實有幾個嚴重的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She did indeed keep her promise.","zh":"她確實遵守了諾言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indeed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f48cd173e65c9a2e","term":"indeed","forms":["indeed"],"pos":"adv","zh":"非常；確實很","explanation":"放在表示性質或程度的詞後面，表示該性質達到了很明顯的程度，相當於“確實很……”。這裡不是補充新事實，而是在事實基礎上進一步加重語氣。","examples":[{"en":"That was a difficult journey indeed.","zh":"那確實是一段非常艱難的旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a generous offer indeed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indeed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fbb6337a2ba75d089e1e","word":"independence","forms":["independence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2ea38e2b25a2549","term":"independence","forms":["independence","independences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨立；自主","explanation":"指不再依賴別人，也不再受別人控制的狀態，可以用於個人、組織或國家。核心畫面是自己站穩、自己作決定。","examples":[{"en":"The country gained independence from colonial rule in 1960.","zh":"這個國家在1960年擺脫殖民統治，獲得了獨立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Moving out gave her a stronger sense of independence.","zh":"搬出去住讓她有了更強的獨立感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/independence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38fab45eb4ac16fc","term":"independence","forms":["independence","independences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟自立","explanation":"指擁有足夠的收入或經濟來源，可以舒適地維持生活，不必依靠別人供養。這是“自己站穩”在經濟方面的具體體現。","examples":[{"en":"She hopes to achieve financial independence before turning forty.","zh":"她希望在四十歲以前實現經濟獨立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A steady salary gave her financial independence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/independence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0275fca08c216c77b2a1","word":"independent","forms":["independent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c351b1c42faef85","term":"independent","forms":["independent","more independent","most independent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獨立的；不依賴的","explanation":"指一個人、國家或組織不靠別的物件維持或決定自己的行動，能夠自己作主。這是 independent 最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The country became independent after years of struggle.","zh":"這個國家經過多年的鬥爭後實現了獨立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is financially independent and supports herself.","zh":"她在經濟上獨立，能夠養活自己。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/independent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc9dfebebac56886","term":"independent","forms":["independent","more independent","most independent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有獨立判斷的","explanation":"指不輕易受他人意見、權威或壓力左右，能夠自己思考和判斷。它把“自己站穩”的概念從生活安排擴充套件到了思想和判斷。","examples":[{"en":"She has an independent mind and asks difficult questions.","zh":"她很有獨立思考能力，總會提出一些難回答的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An independent thinker may question even popular assumptions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/independent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bc04b5291c26a46d918","word":"index","forms":["index"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0697994bb5c5b2d","term":"index","forms":["index","indexes","indices","index's"],"pos":"noun","zh":"索引；索引頁","explanation":"書末或資料中的索引把詞語、主題等和它們出現的頁碼對應起來，幫助讀者迅速找到內容。它就像一根指向相關頁面的手指。","examples":[{"en":"I found the article by checking the index at the back of the book.","zh":"我查閱書後的索引找到了那篇文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The index lists important names and the pages where they appear.","zh":"索引列出了重要人物的姓名及其出現的頁碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/index","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d2c1128ed2a7e63","term":"index","forms":["index","indexes","indices","index's"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顯示某事的指標","explanation":"任何能夠指出、顯示或暴露某種情況的事物都可以是 index；它不一定是數字，也可以是一個現象或特徵。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden drop in sales can be an index of falling demand.","zh":"銷售額突然下降可能是需求下滑的一個指標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Bird diversity serves as an index of habitat health.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/index","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d293513ff3e69706","term":"index","forms":["index","indexes","indexing","indexed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編索引","explanation":"為書籍、長文件或資料整理出索引，使讀者能夠按詞語或主題找到對應位置。","examples":[{"en":"The editor indexed the book by subject and author.","zh":"編輯按主題和作者為這本書編制了索引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The database indexes the most frequently searched fields.","zh":"資料庫會為最常檢索的欄位建立索引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/index","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4932c716f725df5e480e","word":"indicate","forms":["indicate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5221626bee6bb1bf","term":"indicate","forms":["indicate","indicates","indicating","indicated","indicatest","indicatedst","indicateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指出；表明","explanation":"把某個資訊、事實或方向明確地指給別人看，使對方知道它是什麼或接下來會發生什麼。這是最基本的“指出並讓人瞭解”之意。","examples":[{"en":"The sign indicates the way to the station.","zh":"這個標誌指明瞭去車站的路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She indicated that the meeting would start soon.","zh":"她表示會議很快就要開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-218d8e93c37296ca","term":"indicate","forms":["indicate","indicates","indicating","indicated","indicatest","indicatedst","indicateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"由症狀顯示","explanation":"症狀、體徵或檢查結果像是在替病情“指出”某件事：它們顯示身體可能處於某種狀態。這種用法常見於醫學和科學說明。","examples":[{"en":"These symptoms may indicate an infection.","zh":"這些症狀可能表明有感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Persistent thirst may indicate a medical problem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indicate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e27f26c157e65145f4f3","word":"indication","forms":["indication"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cbe67334e72351b2","term":"indication","forms":["indication","indications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指出；表明的動作","explanation":"指把某件事明確指出來或表明出來的行為，重點在“指出”這個動作本身，而不是之後留下的跡象。","examples":[{"en":"His indication of the safest route saved us a lot of time.","zh":"他指出最安全路線的做法為我們節省了很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With a brief indication of the exit, he dismissed us.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e0f7fde7b2f9fa9","term":"indication","forms":["indication","indications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跡象；表明某事的證據","explanation":"指某個事實、變化或現象所發出的訊號，讓人看出另一件事可能存在或即將發生，但它本身通常還不等於確鑿證明。","examples":[{"en":"There is no indication that the storm will reach the city tonight.","zh":"沒有跡象表明這場暴風雨今晚會到達這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm voice was an indication that she had a plan.","zh":"她平靜的聲音表明她已經有了計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01d3fa047699b1fa6234","word":"indifference","forms":["indifference"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6b483e0e7a1f656","term":"indifference","forms":["indifference","indifferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漠不關心的狀態","explanation":"指心裡沒有特別在意某人或某事，不會因它而產生關心或行動。這是全詞最寬的核心義，其他許多義項都可以看作“不被牽動”的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"Her indifference to the problem worried everyone.","zh":"她對這個問題漠不關心，這讓所有人都很擔心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He watched the argument with complete indifference.","zh":"他對這場爭論完全無動於衷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indifference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-317153dc6c31a32b","term":"indifference","forms":["indifference","indifferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冷漠、麻木","explanation":"指情感上沒有反應，尤其是面對他人的困難、痛苦或重要事件時也不表現出同情和關切。它比一般的“不感興趣”更突出情感上的冷淡。","examples":[{"en":"His indifference to the victims shocked his friends.","zh":"他對受害者的冷漠讓朋友們感到震驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke about the tragedy with an unsettling indifference.","zh":"她談起那場悲劇時表現出的冷漠令人不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indifference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37825ceb9b7e3e1d5bb6","word":"indifferent","forms":["indifferent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8cface6924dda926","term":"indifferent","forms":["indifferent","more indifferent","most indifferent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不在乎；漠不關心","explanation":"表示對某人、某事沒有興趣或情感投入，結果怎樣都不太在意；重點是“這件事對我沒有影響，所以我不關心”。","examples":[{"en":"He was indifferent to the criticism and continued working.","zh":"他對這些批評毫不在意，繼續工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She seemed indifferent to what happened next.","zh":"她似乎不在乎接下來發生什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indifferent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ef134318db39dd0","term":"indifferent","forms":["indifferent","more indifferent","most indifferent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冷淡的；漠不關心的","explanation":"表示某人的表情、回答或動作顯出不在乎的態度，是“不關心”在外表或行為上的表現。","examples":[{"en":"He gave an indifferent shrug and walked away.","zh":"他冷淡地聳了聳肩，轉身走開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He seemed indifferent to the outcome of the vote.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indifferent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50bbcf6ff4a9294b","term":"indifferent","forms":["indifferent","more indifferent","most indifferent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沒有偏好；哪個都可以","explanation":"表示在幾個選擇之間不作取捨，任何一個都可以；這裡不是“不關心一切”，而是“沒有特別喜歡哪一個”。","examples":[{"en":"I am indifferent between tea and coffee this morning.","zh":"今天早上喝茶還是喝咖啡對我來說都一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm indifferent between the two colors; choose whichever you prefer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indifferent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f6caccb363435739c40","word":"indigenous","forms":["indigenous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24f62c6d019b401e","term":"indigenous","forms":["indigenous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"本土的；原生的","explanation":"指某人、某族群、動物、植物或文化原本就在某地形成或生活，而不是後來遷入的；常隱含“在外來者進入以前就已存在”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Several plant species are indigenous to this island.","zh":"有幾種植物原生於這座島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum works closely with indigenous communities.","zh":"這家博物館與當地原住社群保持密切合作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indigenous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-723ee610f975e85f","term":"indigenous","forms":["indigenous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"本土的；原住的（大寫寫法）","explanation":"這是 indigenous 的首字母大寫形式，表示與某地原住居民及其身份、歷史或社群有關的“本土的、原住的”。","examples":[{"en":"The festival was organized with advice from Indigenous leaders.","zh":"這個節慶是在原住民領袖的建議下組織的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum consulted Indigenous communities about the exhibition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indigenous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e6cdeb0a858ed246973","word":"indignant","forms":["indignant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75c47a4b98a2f670","term":"indignant","forms":["indignant","more indignant","most indignant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"因不公而義憤","explanation":"形容一個人因為看到不公正、錯誤或不應有的行為而感到憤怒，心裡認為“這不應該這樣”。這種憤怒通常帶有明確的道德判斷，不只是個人脾氣不好。","examples":[{"en":"She was indignant at the unfair decision.","zh":"她對這個不公平的決定感到義憤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sounded indignant when he was accused of cheating.","zh":"有人指責他作弊時，他聽起來非常憤怒和不平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indignant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8042c6d16511690e7d32","word":"indispensable","forms":["indispensable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-089ea4512eb52291","term":"indispensable","forms":["indispensable","more indispensable","most indispensable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"必不可少的","explanation":"表示某人、某物或某條件絕對必要，少了它就無法順利完成或維持某件事，是這個詞最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A reliable internet connection is indispensable for remote work.","zh":"可靠的網路連線是遠端工作的必備條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has become an indispensable member of the team.","zh":"她已經成了團隊中不可或缺的一員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indispensable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da15caaee9de1b0dc60a","word":"individual","forms":["individual"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9784431697b23ffe","term":"individual","forms":["individual","more individual","most individual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"單獨的；單個的","explanation":"強調一個人或一個事物被單獨看待，而不是作為一群人或一批事物的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"The needs of individual students vary widely.","zh":"每個學生的需求差別很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report examines each individual case.","zh":"這份報告逐一考察每個個案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/individual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d38ce6d2872592c","term":"individual","forms":["individual","individuals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人；個體","explanation":"指單獨的一個人，尤其強調這個人不是作為群體成員，而是作為獨立單位被看待。","examples":[{"en":"She is a thoughtful individual who listens carefully.","zh":"她是一個善於思考、認真傾聽的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program gives individuals more control over their data.","zh":"這個專案讓個人更能控制自己的資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/individual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fabe40e86f8364ba20d","word":"indoor","forms":["indoor"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89350e02edf01df9","term":"indoor","forms":["indoor"],"pos":"adj","zh":"室內的","explanation":"指位於建築物裡面，或專門在建築物內部使用、進行的事物。核心畫面就是“從門外移到門內”，所以室內運動、室內裝置和室內用途都可以用 indoor 修飾。","examples":[{"en":"The children moved the game indoors because it started to rain.","zh":"因為開始下雨，孩子們把遊戲移到了室內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This plant is best kept in bright indoor light.","zh":"這種植物最好放在明亮的室內光線下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indoor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb0343b30bd2d644df61","word":"indoors","forms":["indoors"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63e7ca886f6032f2","term":"indoors","forms":["indoors"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在室內；到室內","explanation":"表示人在建築物裡面，或從外面進入建築物內部。核心畫面就是從“門外”來到“門內”，並待在這個室內空間中。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed indoors to avoid the brutal heat.","zh":"我們待在室內，以避開酷熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children went indoors when it started to rain.","zh":"開始下雨後，孩子們進了屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indoors","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5c8a5d68cdcc4647af4","word":"induce","forms":["induce"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a96d9ea98d3eb125","term":"induce","forms":["induce","induces","inducing","induced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勸使；誘使","explanation":"透過勸說、影響或某種手段，使某人願意或決定做某事；重點在於把人引向一個行動，而不一定帶有負面意味。","examples":[{"en":"The discount induced many shoppers to buy the larger package.","zh":"折扣使許多購物者買下了更大的包裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing could induce her to change her mind.","zh":"沒有任何事情能勸她改變主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/induce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cb61621c89e7997","term":"induce","forms":["induce","induces","inducing","induced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"導致；促成","explanation":"使某種事件、狀態或結果出現，強調一個原因把結果“引出來”；這裡不一定涉及人的意願或勸說。","examples":[{"en":"The treatment induced a rapid improvement in his symptoms.","zh":"這種治療使他的症狀迅速好轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long discussion induced both sides to accept a compromise.","zh":"長時間的討論促使雙方接受了妥協。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/induce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21feae6bc4428b5c0ad8","word":"indulge","forms":["indulge"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4efbe380b365e7a1","term":"indulge","forms":["indulge","indulges","indulging","indulged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放縱自己；滿足慾望","explanation":"指順從自己的食慾、興趣或其他慾望，暫時不去剋制；重點是“給自己鬆開韁繩”，常含有偶爾放縱或明知不該仍去做的意味。","examples":[{"en":"I usually eat healthy food, but I indulge in ice cream on weekends.","zh":"我平時吃得健康，但週末會放縱自己吃冰淇淋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was tired, so she indulged in a long afternoon nap.","zh":"她很累，於是放縱自己睡了一個長長的午覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indulge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-beb89c9e22bc3977","term":"indulge","forms":["indulge","indulges","indulging","indulged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遷就；縱容某人","explanation":"指為了滿足某人的願望或任性而順著他，像把韁繩替對方鬆開；既可以是疼愛，也可能暗示過分寵溺。","examples":[{"en":"His parents indulge him by letting him stay up late.","zh":"他的父母很縱容他，讓他熬夜到很晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandfather indulged her with an extra bedtime story.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indulge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ff09c475dc48a3f9c16","word":"industrial","forms":["industrial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0acd67feb80bb91f","term":"industrial","forms":["industrial","more industrial","most industrial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"工業的；製造業的","explanation":"指與工業，尤其是製造業和工廠生產有關的事物。可以把它想成工廠周圍的一整套活動：生產部門、工業經濟和製造業發展都可以用這個詞描述。","examples":[{"en":"The industrial sector is recovering after a difficult year.","zh":"工業部門正在艱難的一年後逐步復甦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city has a long industrial history.","zh":"這座城市有著悠久的工業歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/industrial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac7928776d02bfe6","term":"industrial","forms":["industrial","more industrial","most industrial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"工業生產的","explanation":"指由工廠或大規模工業流程生產出來的，而不是主要靠手工製作的。核心畫面仍是工廠流水線：產品因此更標準化、更容易大量生產。","examples":[{"en":"The store sells both handmade goods and industrial products.","zh":"這家商店既賣手工製品，也賣工業產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The area contains several industrial warehouses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/industrial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":3,"counts":{"113":2,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-059d90a2718d1580c720","word":"industrialize","forms":["industrialize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"industrialize","forms":["industrialize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使工業化；工業化","examples":[{"en":"The government tried to industrialize the region by building factories.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Some countries began to industrialize much earlier than others.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-14d24f98ae39d2990b27","word":"industry","forms":["industry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1071d0c3bab39db8","term":"industry","forms":["industry","industries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勤奮；勤勞","explanation":"指一個人長期堅持做事、願意付出努力的品質。這裡的重點不是某一次辛苦，而是持續不斷地投入。","examples":[{"en":"Her industry and patience helped her build a successful business.","zh":"她的勤奮和耐心幫助她建立起了成功的企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With industry, he learned the craft in just a few years.","zh":"憑著勤奮，他只用了幾年就學會了這門手藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/industry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ce768189ac77587","term":"industry","forms":["industry","industries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行業；產業","explanation":"指從事同一種或相近商業活動的企業整體，例如軟體行業、旅遊業或鋼鐵行業。它把許多企業看成一個共同領域，而不是指某一家企業。","examples":[{"en":"The renewable-energy industry is creating many new jobs.","zh":"可再生能源行業正在創造許多新的就業機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fishing industry supports most families along this coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/industry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d10dd510c72ea24edc79","word":"inevitable","forms":["inevitable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-136deea623fa9cb4","term":"inevitable","forms":["inevitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不可避免的","explanation":"指某件事無論怎樣都很難躲開、阻止或預防，最後註定會發生。","examples":[{"en":"After years of disagreement, a major change seemed inevitable.","zh":"多年的分歧之後，重大改變似乎已經不可避免。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without more support, failure was inevitable.","zh":"如果得不到更多支援，失敗就是不可避免的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inevitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-178d7b0f65569cb9","term":"inevitable","forms":["inevitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"註定會出現的","explanation":"指某種結果或反應按照一貫的情況幾乎總會出現，所以讓人覺得早已可以預料。","examples":[{"en":"The inevitable questions came at the end of the meeting.","zh":"會議結束時，那些意料之中的問題果然出現了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As usual, the meeting ended with the inevitable argument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inevitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c81409883fdefbb3fffa","word":"infant","forms":["infant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-152c8d5e068c0cc9","term":"infant","forms":["infant","infants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嬰兒","explanation":"指出生後不久、通常還需要幾乎持續照料的人類幼兒；年齡界限會因語境而變，但核心形象就是需要照顧、還不能獨立生活的小生命。","examples":[{"en":"The infant slept peacefully in her mother's arms.","zh":"那個嬰兒安靜地睡在母親懷裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic offers advice on feeding infants.","zh":"這家診所提供嬰兒餵養方面的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b396bd3ffb8908df7505","word":"infect","forms":["infect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-040588ecb80b134c","term":"infect","forms":["infect","infects","infecting","infected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感染身體","explanation":"指病原體進入身體或身體的一部分並開始起作用，也就是使某人感染疾病。重點是“把病原體染到身體上”。","examples":[{"en":"The virus can infect people through close contact.","zh":"這種病毒可以透過密切接觸感染人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several workers were infected with the virus.","zh":"幾名工人感染了這種病毒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8ddfa5f01873d50","term":"infect","forms":["infect","infects","infecting","infected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"汙染物品","explanation":"指病原體附著或進入物品、液體等，使它們帶有可能造成感染的病原體。","examples":[{"en":"The water was infected with harmful bacteria.","zh":"這水被有害細菌汙染了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dirty needles can infect the equipment with dangerous microorganisms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f36e4307cf5d409bb92","word":"infection","forms":["infection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9242e37fe8e94d6e","term":"infection","forms":["infection","infections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"病原體在體內繁殖","explanation":"指有害的細菌、病毒或其他病原體進入宿主體內並失去控制地繁殖；這裡的重點是病原體正在身體裡佔據和擴散。","examples":[{"en":"The cut became red because it had developed an infection.","zh":"這道傷口因為發生了感染而變紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Doctors are testing for infection in his lungs.","zh":"醫生正在檢查他的肺部是否有感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a924fea476839c4","term":"infection","forms":["infection","infections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感染性疾病","explanation":"指病原體存在並繁殖後造成的疾病，也就是患者實際患上的一種感染；此時重點從病原體的活動轉向人的患病狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She was given antibiotics to treat a serious ear infection.","zh":"她接受了抗生素治療嚴重的耳部感染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She developed a chest infection after the flu.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae0279441ec1a649061d","word":"infectious","forms":["infectious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-460f14773adfbae4","term":"infectious","forms":["infectious","more infectious","most infectious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傳染性的；由病原體引起的","explanation":"指疾病或病症由細菌、病毒等病原體進入身體而引起，並且通常可以透過某種途徑在宿主之間傳播。它強調這種疾病具有傳染性質，不表示所有疾病都是如此。","examples":[{"en":"Cancer is usually not infectious.","zh":"癌症通常沒有傳染性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor tested him for an infectious disease.","zh":"醫生給他做了傳染病檢測。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infectious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e17f823c8ccd80f9","term":"infectious","forms":["infectious","more infectious","most infectious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能傳染給別人的","explanation":"通常形容人或動物，表示其體內的病原體仍能傳給其他人，因此即使本人感覺好轉，也可能繼續把疾病傳播出去。","examples":[{"en":"Despite feeling better, the patient is still infectious.","zh":"儘管感覺好多了，這名患者仍然具有傳染性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His infectious laugh made everyone else smile.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infectious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8df983505fb54b2","term":"infectious","forms":["infectious","more infectious","most infectious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易感染他人的；迅速傳開的","explanation":"把“病原體傳播”的畫面擴大到非醫學場景，表示一個人的情緒、態度或行為很快影響周圍的人，使別人也產生類似反應。","examples":[{"en":"Her enthusiasm for the project was infectious.","zh":"她對這個專案的熱情感染了大家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His laughter is infectious.","zh":"他的笑聲很有感染力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infectious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92bc2e412115876270c8","word":"infer","forms":["infer"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1701bdfba6d7f52","term":"infer","forms":["infer","infers","inferring","inferred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推斷；推論得出","explanation":"根據證據、事實或前提，把資訊一步步帶到一個合理結論上；重點在於結論是推理出來的，而不是原話直接說出的。","examples":[{"en":"From the muddy footprints, we can infer that someone came in through the back door.","zh":"從這些泥腳印可以推斷，有人是從後門進來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It would be a mistake to infer too much from one bad result.","zh":"僅憑一次糟糕的結果就作出過多推斷，是不妥的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d67a02ebcf174379d24d","word":"inferior","forms":["inferior"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0eeca61cb9dccf5b","term":"inferior","forms":["inferior","more inferior","most inferior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"較差的；低人一等的","explanation":"指某人的地位、能力或某件事物的質量低於另一個人或事物，常含有“比不上”的意味。它既可以描述客觀質量，也可以描述一個人因比較而產生的自卑感。","examples":[{"en":"This material is inferior to the one we used before.","zh":"這種材料不如我們以前用的那種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt inferior to her classmates after failing the exam.","zh":"考試不及格後，她覺得自己比同學低人一等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inferior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7eae482400b70d6e","term":"inferior","forms":["inferior","more inferior","most inferior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"位於下方的","explanation":"在醫學、解剖學等語境中，指某個部位處在另一個部位的下方。這裡強調的是空間位置，不一定表示質量差。","examples":[{"en":"The stomach lies inferior to the heart.","zh":"胃位於心臟的下方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inferior surface of the leaf is pale green.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inferior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-704b7acbacf9cd963218","word":"infinite","forms":["infinite"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2df1cccf4d65b99","term":"infinite","forms":["infinite","more infinite","most infinite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無邊無際；沒有盡頭","explanation":"形容某物沒有終點、邊界或限制，就像那條永遠走不到盡頭的路；也可用於抽象的時間、空間、愛或可能性。","examples":[{"en":"The night sky seemed to open onto infinite space.","zh":"夜空彷彿通向無邊無際的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are infinite ways to solve this problem.","zh":"解決這個問題的方法有無窮多種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infinite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe659d694fbec66a","term":"infinite","forms":["infinite","more infinite","most infinite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大得無法估量","explanation":"形容數量、規模或程度大到難以估量，重點是“多得幾乎數不清”，不一定嚴格表示真的沒有上限。","examples":[{"en":"She showed infinite patience while teaching the children.","zh":"教孩子們時，她表現出了極大的耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project demands almost infinite patience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infinite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d731a5ed145ab6d2e88","word":"inflation","forms":["inflation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd03bc3ae4034731","term":"inflation","forms":["inflation","inflations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膨脹；充氣","explanation":"指物體因充入氣體或液體而變大，或這一變大的過程；核心畫面就是“被吹大”。","examples":[{"en":"The inflation of the giant balloon took nearly an hour.","zh":"給這個巨型氣球充氣花了將近一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Complete inflation of the mattress takes five minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inflation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d8eda96c2766b00","term":"inflation","forms":["inflation","inflations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通貨膨脹","explanation":"指貨幣數量增加或購買力下降，導致商品和服務的總體價格水平上升；可以把它理解為“錢變多了，但每一單位錢被吹薄了”。","examples":[{"en":"Inflation has made groceries much more expensive this year.","zh":"今年的通貨膨脹讓食品雜貨貴了很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many families are cutting back because of rising inflation.","zh":"由於通貨膨脹加劇，許多家庭正在削減開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inflation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5389d89891805202bdad","word":"inflict","forms":["inflict"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a8384d1bca56ca23","term":"inflict","forms":["inflict","inflicts","inflicting","inflicted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強加痛苦或傷害","explanation":"指把痛苦、傷害、損失或懲罰強加給某人或某物，使對方承受負面後果。這個詞帶有“把打擊落到對方身上”的感覺，通常不是中性地施加某種東西。","examples":[{"en":"The storm inflicted serious damage on several coastal towns.","zh":"暴風雨給幾個沿海城鎮造成了嚴重損失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The attackers inflicted terrible pain on their prisoners.","zh":"襲擊者給囚犯施加了極大的痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inflict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22fefa8cf4bda9184634","word":"influence","forms":["influence"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10ca601b07ae738e","term":"influence","forms":["influence","influences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影響力","explanation":"指能夠改變某人的想法、行為、發展方向或決定的力量，重點是“有多大能力讓事情發生變化”。","examples":[{"en":"She has considerable influence over the team.","zh":"她對這個團隊有相當大的影響力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Money still has a strong influence on people's choices.","zh":"金錢仍然強烈影響著人們的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/influence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7354ea3078f667eb","term":"influence","forms":["influence","influences","influencing","influenced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"影響；左右","explanation":"指把一股力量流進別人的想法、行為或決定中，使其發生改變；可以是輕微影響，也可以是明顯左右。","examples":[{"en":"Friends can influence the way we make decisions.","zh":"朋友可能影響我們作決定的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary influenced him to change his habits.","zh":"這部紀錄片影響了他，使他改變了習慣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/influence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2411f90645028dcc347","word":"influential","forms":["influential"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-699561d7167b9914","term":"influential","forms":["influential","more influential","most influential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有影響力的","explanation":"形容某人或某事物能讓很多人的想法、行為或文化發展發生變化，影響範圍或作用都比較明顯。","examples":[{"en":"She became an influential voice in environmental policy.","zh":"她成了環境政策領域一個有影響力的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This book was influential in shaping modern design.","zh":"這本書對現代設計的形成產生了重要影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/influential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea07dcc807ffe0d65325","word":"inform","forms":["inform"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b09b44f01f924cd7","term":"inform","forms":["inform","informs","informing","informed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"通知；告知","explanation":"指把具體訊息、事實或決定傳達給某人，使對方知道某件事。","examples":[{"en":"Please inform all members of the change in schedule.","zh":"請通知所有成員日程有所變更。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We will inform you about the results next week.","zh":"我們下週會通知你結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09d8cd50076c0402","term":"inform","forms":["inform","informs","informing","informed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塑造；深刻影響","explanation":"沿著“把某種東西放進去並塑造它”的主線，指思想、信念或經驗滲透到作品、行為或制度中，影響其內容和特點。","examples":[{"en":"Her experience informs every decision she makes.","zh":"她的經歷影響著她所作的每一個決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strong sense of fairness informs the new policy.","zh":"強烈的公平意識塑造了這項新政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dea7111a8406e27cfc8b","word":"information","forms":["information"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6d1dc5c8a59254f","term":"information","forms":["information","informations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消除未知的資訊","explanation":"指能回答“這是什麼”或解決疑問的內容，也就是把原本不清楚的地方照亮的資訊。重點不在內容屬於哪個主題，而在它能讓人從不知道變為知道。","examples":[{"en":"The map gives us enough information to find the village.","zh":"這張地圖給了我們足夠的資訊，讓我們能找到那個村子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without more information, we cannot decide what to do.","zh":"沒有更多資訊，我們無法決定該怎麼辦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/information","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80be878434d5994a","term":"information","forms":["information","informations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關於某主題的資料和知識","explanation":"指人們關於某個話題已經知道、能夠查到或能夠傳達的資料和知識。它可以由事實、數字、說明等組成，範圍比一條具體訊息更廣。","examples":[{"en":"I need some more information about this issue.","zh":"我還需要一些關於這個問題的資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaflet contains information about local bus services.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/information","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114,115],"total":7,"counts":{"113":3,"114":3,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-57d4604818e24600a017","word":"informative","forms":["informative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d5e1d7911b31e5a","term":"informative","forms":["informative","more informative","most informative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"資訊豐富且有幫助的","explanation":"指某種內容提供了很多有用、具體或有趣的資訊，使人更瞭解一個主題。它常用來稱讚文章、報告、講座、紀錄片或談話等內容，而不只是說明其中“有資訊”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum's website has an informative guide to the city's history.","zh":"這家博物館的網站有一份介紹這座城市歷史的實用指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary was short but very informative.","zh":"這部紀錄片雖然很短，但資訊量很大，也很有幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/informative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72cf4eb4b2abda74","term":"informative","forms":["informative","more informative","most informative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"僅供說明的，不規定要求的","explanation":"在標準、規範或技術檔案中，指某一部分只是幫助讀者瞭解背景或解釋內容，不是在規定必須滿足的條件。它強調“提供說明”與“提出要求”之間的區別。","examples":[{"en":"This appendix is informative and does not set any requirements.","zh":"本附錄僅供說明，不規定任何要求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This informative annex provides examples without imposing requirements.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/informative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fec08e4574bcb96d535","word":"infrastructure","forms":["infrastructure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e98933f11f7932db","term":"infrastructure","forms":["infrastructure","infrastructures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"底層基礎；支撐結構","explanation":"指位於下面、支撐建築、組織或系統的基礎結構，也可抽象地指讓某個系統能夠成立和執行的底層條件。重點不在表面上看到的部分，而在承託整體的“骨架”。","examples":[{"en":"Reliable data infrastructure is essential for the new system.","zh":"可靠的資料基礎設施對這個新系統至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge needs stronger infrastructure beneath the road.","zh":"這座橋的道路下方需要更堅固的基礎結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infrastructure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d53a76f662a8994a","term":"infrastructure","forms":["infrastructure","infrastructures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會基礎設施","explanation":"指社群或社會正常運作所需的設施、服務和裝置，例如道路、鐵路、供水、電力、通訊等。它們共同構成托住日常生活和經濟活動的“底座”。","examples":[{"en":"The city is investing in public infrastructure to reduce traffic.","zh":"這座城市正在投資建設公共基礎設施，以緩解交通擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reliable water infrastructure is essential for public health.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infrastructure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d8178aae87b9a429761b","word":"ingredient","forms":["ingredient"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cc165ecf4303964","term":"ingredient","forms":["ingredient","ingredients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"食材；成分","explanation":"指加入食物或其他混合物、並構成整體的一種材料，不只限於調味料，也可以是麵粉、雞蛋等主要材料。","examples":[{"en":"Garlic is an essential ingredient in this sauce.","zh":"大蒜是這道醬汁不可缺少的一種材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check every ingredient for possible allergens.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ingredient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-330cb24f43fab82b","term":"ingredient","forms":["ingredient","ingredients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必要因素；組成部分","explanation":"把“加入鍋裡並構成整體”的畫面用於抽象目標：某種品質、行動或條件進入一個結果，併成為成功所需要的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"The right team is a key ingredient in a successful project.","zh":"合適的團隊是專案成功的關鍵因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Patience is a crucial ingredient in successful teaching.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ingredient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a362454abeb021598052","word":"inhabit","forms":["inhabit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0871f1d29e06cf2e","term":"inhabit","forms":["inhabit","inhabits","inhabiting","inhabited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"居住在；棲息於","explanation":"表示人、動物或某個群體住在某地，把那裡作為生活或棲息的空間。這個意義就是“住進一座地方的房子裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The Inuit inhabit the Arctic.","zh":"因紐特人居住在北極地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many birds inhabit this wetland.","zh":"許多鳥類棲息在這片溼地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inhabit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d5adf3d0f95da0f","term":"inhabit","forms":["inhabit","inhabits","inhabiting","inhabited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"存在於；佔據","explanation":"把“居住”擴充套件到抽象空間：想法、感覺或其他無形事物彷彿住在人的頭腦、內心或某個空間中。重點不是物理上的住所，而是持續存在並佔據那裡。","examples":[{"en":"Doubt still inhabits her mind.","zh":"懷疑仍然存在於她的腦海中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spirit of optimism inhabits her early paintings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inhabit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78254e8528eed7d0ca06","word":"inhabitant","forms":["inhabitant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41f4b8c6501b6199","term":"inhabitant","forms":["inhabitant","inhabitants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"居民；居住者","explanation":"指實際生活在某個地方的人或生物：城市、島嶼、森林甚至其他星球都可以有 inhabitant。記住“住在某處的物件”這條主線，就能同時理解它對人和動物的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The island has fewer than five hundred inhabitants.","zh":"這個島上的居民不到五百人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The forest's inhabitants became active after sunset.","zh":"森林裡的生物在日落後活躍起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inhabitant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96c842ee0d60fa41d518","word":"inherent","forms":["inherent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73a7d05e723f0eaf","term":"inherent","forms":["inherent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"固有的；內在的","explanation":"某種性質像根一樣紮在事物內部，是事物本來就帶有的，或由其本身自然產生的，而不是外部後來加上的。它既可以指中性的內在特點，也常用於說明某種問題、風險或侷限難以從事物本身分離。","examples":[{"en":"Every plan has inherent risks.","zh":"每個計劃都有其固有的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The design has an inherent weakness that makes repairs difficult.","zh":"這種設計有一個固有的缺陷，使維修變得困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inherent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-035300f3afee55ae79b7","word":"inherit","forms":["inherit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ca6e74808a36ca6e","term":"inherit","forms":["inherit","inherits","inheriting","inherited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼承遺產或頭銜","explanation":"指前任或親屬去世後，按照法律繼承或遺囑接收房屋、金錢、土地、頭銜等財產或身份。核心畫面是前一個人留下東西，後一個人依法接過來。","examples":[{"en":"She inherited a small house from her aunt.","zh":"她從姨媽那裡繼承了一棟小房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He inherited his father's business after the funeral.","zh":"葬禮後，他繼承了父親的生意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inherit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd77a883c6a34a9b","term":"inherit","forms":["inherit","inherits","inheriting","inherited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遺傳得到特徵","explanation":"指子女從祖先那裡透過遺傳獲得外貌、體質或其他生物特徵；傳下來的不再是房產，而是身體和基因中的特徵。","examples":[{"en":"The twins inherited their mother's curly hair.","zh":"這對雙胞胎遺傳了母親的捲髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She inherited a tendency to migraines from her father.","zh":"她從父親那裡遺傳了偏頭痛的傾向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inherit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b033a1ba098d3eea","term":"inherit","forms":["inherit","inherits","inheriting","inherited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承接前代留下的影響","explanation":"指一個人、社會或機構接過前一時期已經存在的制度、傳統、問題或局面；這裡傳下來的不是具體物品，而是過去造成的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The new government inherited a serious housing shortage.","zh":"新政府接手了嚴重的住房短缺問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new administration inherited a severe budget deficit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inherit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac1b5c0961a7269b6a05","word":"initial","forms":["initial"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-014f96ad175ffa47","term":"initial","forms":["initial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最初的；起始的","explanation":"指某件事開始時的狀態、反應或階段，強調它發生在後續變化之前。例如最初的計劃後來可能被修改，最初的好感也可能轉為失望。","examples":[{"en":"Our initial plan was to stay for two weeks.","zh":"我們最初的計劃是待兩週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her initial reaction was surprise.","zh":"她最初的反應是驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/initial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9721761e88025d86","term":"initial","forms":["initial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"開頭的；首位的","explanation":"指在空間、順序或書寫位置上排在最前面的部分，尤其常指一個詞的第一個字母。","examples":[{"en":"Write your initial letter in the first box.","zh":"請把你的首字母寫在第一個方框裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The poem's initial word sets its melancholy tone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/initial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4b1e0f3f3f7d670dd87","word":"initiate","forms":["initiate"],"officialPos":"v./adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e283cb8b59a53926","term":"initiate","forms":["initiate","initiates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新成員","explanation":"指剛加入某個組織、團體或圈子的人，也就是剛走進那扇門的人。重點在於“新加入”，不一定表示能力不足。","examples":[{"en":"Each initiate receives a badge at the welcome ceremony.","zh":"每位新成員都會在歡迎儀式上領取一枚徽章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The initiates attended a special welcoming ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/initiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59bb981ccb318bd2","term":"initiate","forms":["initiate","initiates","initiating","initiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"啟動；開始","explanation":"指正式開啟一項行動、程式或變化，相當於把事情推過起點。它對應記憶畫面中“開啟那扇門”的第一步。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy initiated a series of changes in the department.","zh":"這項新政策啟動了該部門的一系列變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee initiated an investigation into the complaint.","zh":"委員會啟動了對這起投訴的調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/initiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-063fe4bf363353a767e9","word":"initiative","forms":["initiative"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4eab3b8f0cae7af4","term":"initiative","forms":["initiative","initiatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開端；第一步","explanation":"指一件事開始時邁出的第一步或最初行動，重點是“先啟動起來”。它可以是一個具體動作，也可以泛指事情的起頭。","examples":[{"en":"She took the initiative and called the client first.","zh":"她主動採取了第一步，先給客戶打了電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His initiative brought the two teams together.","zh":"他的主動行動讓兩支團隊走到了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/initiative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-205e8c6b63e4cf2b","term":"initiative","forms":["initiative","initiatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新計劃；新舉措","explanation":"指為解決問題或推動變化而提出的一項新計劃、新辦法或新行動。它是“第一步”進一步發展成的具體方案。","examples":[{"en":"The school launched an initiative to reduce food waste.","zh":"學校啟動了一項減少食物浪費的新舉措。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her recycling initiative persuaded every café on the street to participate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/initiative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db690957bf329893","term":"initiative","forms":["initiative","initiatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主動性；獨立行動能力","explanation":"指一個人不等別人安排，就能自己發現事情、先採取行動並推動進展的能力。這裡的“第一步”不再是一次行動，而是一個人的穩定特質。","examples":[{"en":"Her manager praised her for showing initiative.","zh":"經理表揚她很有主動性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed initiative by organizing the files without being asked.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/initiative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-e6f2ad814692e3f553d6","word":"inject","forms":["inject"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c074e29e3e5220d9","term":"inject","forms":["inject","injects","injecting","injected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把液體注入某處","explanation":"指用針、泵等把液體或藥物推入身體、管道或其他空腔。重點是“東西被打進一個內部空間”，而不是單純把東西放在表面。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor injected the medicine into the patient's shoulder.","zh":"醫生把藥物注入了病人的肩部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine injects water into the tank at high pressure.","zh":"這臺機器用高壓把水注入水箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inject","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-010c9af782ca46b3","term":"inject","forms":["inject","injects","injecting","injected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"注入新的力量或特點","explanation":"指突然或強有力地把某種感覺、思想、活力或特點帶進原有的環境、活動或文化中。這裡投入的不是液體，而是抽象的影響。","examples":[{"en":"The new coach injected fresh energy into the team.","zh":"新教練為球隊注入了新的活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her joke injected some warmth into the formal meeting.","zh":"她的玩笑為嚴肅的會議注入了一絲輕鬆氣氛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inject","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94c5e3f12f124417","term":"inject","forms":["inject","injects","injecting","injected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給某人或某物打針","explanation":"指對人或動物實施注射，尤其是注射藥物。這個義項關注的是接受治療的物件，而不是藥物被推進身體的具體部位。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse injected the child with a local anesthetic.","zh":"護士給孩子注射了區域性麻醉劑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They injected the dog before the operation.","zh":"他們在手術前給那隻狗打了針。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inject","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-545a70019936cf887441","word":"injection","forms":["injection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be2452aff945cc2f","term":"injection","forms":["injection","injections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"注入；注射；注入物","explanation":"指把液體、藥物或其他物質送入某處的動作，也可指被送入的東西。醫學語境中常指注射，但範圍比“打針”更廣。","examples":[{"en":"The treatment begins with an injection of the medicine into the muscle.","zh":"這種治療先要把藥物注射進肌肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician checked the injection before starting the machine.","zh":"技術員在啟動機器前檢查了注入物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a79f5944e93a23c9","term":"injection","forms":["injection","injections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資金注入","explanation":"指向個人、企業或專案補充資金，把急需的資源“打進去”；這是由物質注入引申出的常見比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"The small company survived after receiving a large cash injection.","zh":"這家小公司獲得大筆現金注入後渡過了難關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An injection of fresh capital kept the factory open.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df73cf99ee6e85954a09","word":"injure","forms":["injure"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f7a8ce068702aed","term":"injure","forms":["injure","injures","injuring","injured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使受傷","explanation":"指透過碰撞、事故、暴力等使人或動物的身體受到傷害。說某人自己受傷時，常用 be injured 或 get injured，突出“受到傷害”的結果。","examples":[{"en":"Two players were injured during the match.","zh":"兩名運動員在比賽中受傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The falling branch injured a man in the park.","zh":"掉下來的樹枝使公園裡的一名男子受了傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a6269f7642f1755","term":"injure","forms":["injure","injures","injuring","injured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"損害；破壞","explanation":"把“身體受傷”的畫面擴充套件到事物：裝置、經濟、計劃或關係等受到損害，功能、狀態或發展因此變差。","examples":[{"en":"The scandal seriously injured the company's reputation.","zh":"這起醜聞嚴重損害了公司的聲譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unfair ruling injured his chances of reaching the final.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a945a02a044c3286e670","word":"injury","forms":["injury"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f61cdf4a44888819","term":"injury","forms":["injury","injuries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體傷害","explanation":"指生物的身體受到損傷，例如事故、運動或打鬥造成的傷口、骨折等。這是 injury 最常見、最應先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She suffered a serious knee injury during the match.","zh":"她在比賽中膝蓋嚴重受傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The driver sustained minor injuries in the crash.","zh":"司機在撞車事故中受了輕傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04147c580f4a1be8","term":"injury","forms":["injury","injuries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理或其他損害","explanation":"指身體以外的傷害，尤其是心理、情感等方面受到創傷。它仍然沿用“某種東西被傷到”的核心形象，只是被傷害的物件變得抽象了。","examples":[{"en":"The bullying caused lasting emotional injury.","zh":"這種欺凌造成了持久的心理傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accusation inflicted a serious injury on his reputation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":4,"counts":{"112":1,"113":3}}},{"id":"ceec-6f45ce2b3b594f16328d","word":"injustice","forms":["injustice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-854d842682da82a4","term":"injustice","forms":["injustice","injustices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正義缺失","explanation":"指整體上沒有公正原則或公正待遇的狀態，也就是“正義不在場”。它可以描述社會制度、處理方式或某種做法本身的不公。","examples":[{"en":"She spoke passionately about the injustice of the system.","zh":"她慷慨激昂地談到了這個制度的不公。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their campaign challenged the injustice of unequal voting rights.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injustice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-026cd642a82b5980","term":"injustice","forms":["injustice","injustices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"侵犯權利","explanation":"指某人或某群體沒有得到應有的權利、尊重或保護，因而受到不公正對待。重點不只是結果不理想，而是有人被虧待或被剝奪了應得之物。","examples":[{"en":"The report exposed a serious injustice against migrant workers.","zh":"這份報告揭露了對移民工人的嚴重不公。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent years trying to correct the injustice done to his family.","zh":"他用了多年時間，試圖糾正加在家人身上的不公。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/injustice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b728b7e775f708faf513","word":"ink","forms":["ink"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fb7a8c7721d5fb2","term":"ink","forms":["ink","inks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"墨水","explanation":"用於書寫、繪畫、列印等的液體顏料或染料；它會在紙張或其他表面留下顏色和字跡。","examples":[{"en":"Please fill out the form in blue ink.","zh":"請用藍色墨水填寫這張表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ink is still wet, so be careful.","zh":"墨水還沒幹，所以小心一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62c4f296f8360251","term":"ink","forms":["ink","inks","inking","inked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用墨水塗寫","explanation":"在紙張、版面或其他表面上施加墨水，使其留下墨跡；核心就是“把墨水印上去”。","examples":[{"en":"The printer inks the plates before each run.","zh":"印刷工在每次印刷前給印版上墨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He inked the drawing with a fine brush.","zh":"他用細毛筆給這幅畫描上了墨線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08fcfc1755fa52b6","term":"ink","forms":["ink","inks","inking","inked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"簽署","explanation":"把名字“寫進”合同或協議中，因此表示正式簽署檔案，常暗示雙方已經達成並落實了協議。","examples":[{"en":"The two companies inked a five-year agreement.","zh":"兩家公司簽署了一項為期五年的協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The player inked a new contract with the club.","zh":"這名球員與俱樂部簽下了一份新合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9628d7750ebfd53e041a","word":"inland","forms":["inland"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fad06cdd38ff1334","term":"inland","forms":["inland","more inland","most inland"],"pos":"adj","zh":"內陸的；遠離海岸的","explanation":"指位於陸地內部、離海岸或開闊水域較遠的地方或事物。它把注意力從海邊移到國家或大陸的內部。","examples":[{"en":"They moved to an inland town after living by the coast.","zh":"他們住在海邊之後，搬到了一個內陸城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inland lake is surrounded by mountains.","zh":"這座內陸湖四周都是山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11ca3745fa8304d0","term":"inland","forms":["inland","more inland","most inland"],"pos":"adj","zh":"內陸運輸的；只經陸路的","explanation":"由“遠離海上、在土地內部進行”引申，指交通、路線或商業只在陸地上進行，不經過海路。","examples":[{"en":"The company specializes in inland transport between the ports and the capital.","zh":"這家公司專門經營港口和首都之間的內陸運輸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Inland freight travels by rail from the coastal port.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-265617d4fe82c18b","term":"inland","forms":["inland","more inland","most inland"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向內陸；向陸地內部","explanation":"指從海岸或開闊水域向陸地內部移動，核心畫面就是路線離開海邊、朝國家腹地延伸。","examples":[{"en":"After the storm, the fishing boats moved inland along the river.","zh":"暴風雨過後，漁船沿河向內陸駛去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road continues inland for another fifty kilometres.","zh":"這條路還向內陸延伸五十公里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0dc0ad7ac4bba718029","word":"inn","forms":["inn"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e95885010d49c4f","term":"inn","forms":["inn","inns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅店","explanation":"指旅行者可以住宿、吃飯和喝酒的旅店，核心畫面就是人在旅途中找到一個可以住下來的地方。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed at a small inn near the mountain trail.","zh":"我們住在山路附近的一家小旅店裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inn offers simple rooms and a warm dinner.","zh":"這家旅店提供簡樸的房間和熱乎乎的晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17b8ffa3990beb2f","term":"inn","forms":["inn","inns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒館","explanation":"指旅店中的酒館，或本身主要作為供人喝酒、吃飯的傳統小酒館；這是從“旅途中停下來歇腳”這一核心畫面發展出來的義項。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers met at the inn after the market closed.","zh":"集市結束後，村民們在酒館碰了面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The travelers stopped at an inn for ale.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33bf6fbd7cd8379785a2","word":"inner","forms":["inner"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36cc9e001b5808e6","term":"inner","forms":["inner","innermore","inmore","innermost","inmost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"更裡面的；內部的","explanation":"指位於某物內部，或比另一個部分更靠裡面的位置；這是 inner 最基本的空間義。","examples":[{"en":"Please close the inner door before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請關上裡面那扇門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inner room has no windows.","zh":"裡面的房間沒有窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c54977666a339c0","term":"inner","forms":["inner","innermore","inmore","innermost","inmost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"內心的；精神上的","explanation":"把“更裡面”的概念轉到人的心靈：指不直接顯露的感受、精神狀態或內在力量。","examples":[{"en":"Meditation gives her a sense of inner peace.","zh":"冥想讓她獲得了內心的平靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He drew on his inner strength during the crisis.","zh":"危機期間，他依靠了自己的內在力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7419c0d117c6b3e91ca","word":"inning","forms":["inning"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38aeaccbef6528b2","term":"inning","forms":["inning","innings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棒球一局","explanation":"棒球比賽中，客隊和主隊依次進攻、直到規定數量的擊球手出局，這樣的一輪叫一局。正規比賽通常有九局或更多，因此它表示的是比賽中的一段完整程序，而不是一次擊球。","examples":[{"en":"The home team scored three runs in the fifth inning.","zh":"主隊在第五局得了三分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game was still tied after nine innings.","zh":"九局結束後，比賽仍然平局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f2ce6776168a43012f1","word":"innocence","forms":["innocence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5acc5b8c5eae3e71","term":"innocence","forms":["innocence","innocences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無罪；無過錯","explanation":"指一個人沒有實施犯罪、侵權或其他應負責任的行為，尤其常用於法庭和法律討論中。它強調的是“沒有做錯事”，而不只是看起來單純或天真。","examples":[{"en":"The evidence was enough to prove his innocence.","zh":"這些證據足以證明他無罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She continued to insist on her innocence throughout the trial.","zh":"整個審判期間，她一直堅持自己是無罪的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innocence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c55e71bfb1275949","term":"innocence","forms":["innocence","innocences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天真無知","explanation":"指一個人不瞭解性、犯罪等敏感或複雜事情，因此沒有意識到某種行為的風險或不妥。這裡的 innocence 更接近“未經世事、缺乏相關知識”，不一定表示道德上的純潔。","examples":[{"en":"In her innocence, she shared the password with a stranger.","zh":"她由於天真無知，把密碼告訴了一個陌生人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In her innocence, she trusted every advertisement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innocence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c95538022f8a2eaa5cf","word":"innocent","forms":["innocent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2620756e6e8a6f19","term":"innocent","forms":["innocent","more innocent","most innocent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無罪的；清白的","explanation":"指沒有做錯事、沒有罪過，尤其強調道德或宗教意義上的清白。它對應“手上沒有傷害別人的東西”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She insisted that she was innocent and had never taken the money.","zh":"她堅持說自己是無辜的，從來沒有拿過那筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child looked completely innocent after the vase broke.","zh":"花瓶打碎後，那個孩子看起來完全無辜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innocent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0506347eced8ab2c","term":"innocent","forms":["innocent","more innocent","most innocent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無心的；非故意的","explanation":"指言語、行為或錯誤沒有惡意，也沒有傷害別人的意圖。這裡“沒有傷害”從人的品格延伸到了具體行為。","examples":[{"en":"It was an innocent mistake, so nobody blamed her.","zh":"那是一個無心的錯誤，所以沒有人責怪她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His innocent question made everyone realize that the plan was unclear.","zh":"他那句沒有惡意的問題讓大家意識到計劃並不清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innocent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6611032577e5a7b3a146","word":"innovation","forms":["innovation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43155c5b75b5aba2","term":"innovation","forms":["innovation","innovations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創新活動；引入新事物","explanation":"指把新的想法、方法、技術或做法引入某個領域的行為和過程，重點在“進行創新”這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"Medical innovation has helped doctors treat diseases that were once considered incurable.","zh":"醫療創新幫助醫生治療了過去被認為無法治癒的疾病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company invests heavily in innovation to keep up with its competitors.","zh":"這家公司大力投資創新，以跟上競爭對手的步伐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innovation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef6f54623445ab6b","term":"innovation","forms":["innovation","innovations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創新帶來的改變或新成果","explanation":"指透過創新產生的具體改變、新做法或新事物，重點在“創新之後出現了什麼”。它可以是一個產品、制度、流程，也可以是對原有習慣的改變。","examples":[{"en":"Online booking was a useful innovation that saved customers a great deal of time.","zh":"網上預訂是一項實用的創新，為顧客節省了大量時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibition showcases recent innovations in battery technology.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innovation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113,114],"total":4,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1,"114":2}}},{"id":"ceec-d42a5821ba1507a63696","word":"innovative","forms":["innovative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da674f724ee89daa","term":"innovative","forms":["innovative","more innovative","most innovative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富有創新的","explanation":"指能創造新想法、發明或做法，而不是簡單重複已有模式；常用來讚揚設計、技術、產品或解決問題的方法。","examples":[{"en":"The team developed an innovative way to reduce food waste.","zh":"這個團隊開發了一種創新的方法來減少食物浪費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum is known for its innovative use of digital technology.","zh":"這家博物館因創新地運用數字技術而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innovative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-339241c70d9d1ced","term":"innovative","forms":["innovative","more innovative","most innovative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"思路超前的","explanation":"強調思想、計劃或方向走在當前普遍做法之前，已經在考慮未來的需要和可能性；它和“創造新辦法”相連，但重點更偏向前瞻性。","examples":[{"en":"The city adopted an innovative plan for future public transport.","zh":"這座城市採用了一項面向未來的創新公共交通計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The innovative teacher replaced lectures with student investigations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innovative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114,115],"total":3,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-977f457d5fe5e02ad973","word":"innumerable","forms":["innumerable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04af124549a47feb","term":"innumerable","forms":["innumerable","more innumerable","most innumerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無法計數的","explanation":"數量大到不能逐一清點、編號或準確計算，重點是“數不清”這一事實。","examples":[{"en":"The victims of the disaster were innumerable.","zh":"這場災難的受害者多得無法統計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Innumerable stars filled the night sky.","zh":"無數星星佈滿了夜空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innumerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab0785a8a9d19097","term":"innumerable","forms":["innumerable","more innumerable","most innumerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其眾多的","explanation":"不一定真的完全無法計數，而是數量極大，給人多得數不清的感覺；這是“無法計數”這一核心概念在一般描述中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The forest is home to innumerable insects.","zh":"這片森林裡生活著數量極其龐大的昆蟲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Innumerable stars shone above the desert camp.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innumerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c96c6d5be8d08a12e7b5","word":"input","forms":["input"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c40ff532760b3020","term":"input","forms":["input","inputs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意見；建議；貢獻","explanation":"指一個人提供的意見、資訊或實際工作，這些內容會幫助討論、計劃或決定形成結果；它仍然保留“把東西放進過程裡”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We need your input on the new schedule.","zh":"我們需要你對新日程安排的意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her input helped us make a better decision.","zh":"她的意見幫助我們作出了更好的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/input","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a27bab30e0c5f8c","term":"input","forms":["input","inputs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輸入資料；過程的輸入內容","explanation":"指送入程式、機器或其他處理過程的資料或訊號，目的是讓它影響後續輸出；文字、聲音和影象都可以成為 input。","examples":[{"en":"The system checks the input before producing an answer.","zh":"系統會在生成答案前檢查輸入資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clear sound input makes the recording easier to understand.","zh":"清晰的聲音輸入會讓錄音更容易聽懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/input","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdd4418aedb335bc","term":"input","forms":["input","inputs","inputting","inputted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輸入資料","explanation":"指把資料輸入程式、裝置或系統，讓它繼續處理；這裡正是“從入口放進去”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Please input your email address into the form.","zh":"請把你的電子郵件地址輸入表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The operator input the figures into the system.","zh":"操作員把這些數字輸入了系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/input","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e6073ea718e40e588da","word":"inquire","forms":["inquire"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a829a0c18c81223d","term":"inquire","forms":["inquire","inquires","inquiring","inquired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"詢問；打聽","explanation":"向別人詢問某件事，以獲得資訊或確認情況，語氣通常比日常的“問”更正式。","examples":[{"en":"I am writing to inquire about the status of my application.","zh":"我寫信是想詢問我的申請目前進展如何。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She called to inquire whether the museum was open.","zh":"她打電話詢問博物館是否開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inquire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-755105ff87140e59","term":"inquire","forms":["inquire","inquires","inquiring","inquired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調查；查究","explanation":"不只是提出一個問題，而是持續蒐集資訊、查詢原因或核實事實；這是“尋找答案”進一步深入後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company is inquiring into the cause of the security breach.","zh":"公司正在調查這次安全漏洞的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commission will inquire into the prisoner's death.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inquire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84d7466427d6e8c1747e","word":"inquiry","forms":["inquiry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-092fda6648492bd4","term":"inquiry","forms":["inquiry","inquiries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詢問；提問","explanation":"指為了得到資訊而提出問題，既可以是一次具體的詢問，也可以泛指提問這一行為；核心畫面是把問題伸向未知處，等待答案。","examples":[{"en":"I am writing to make an inquiry about the delivery date.","zh":"我寫信是想詢問送貨日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The office received several inquiries from local residents.","zh":"辦公室收到了當地居民的幾次詢問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inquiry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e135fea38deaca4","term":"inquiry","forms":["inquiry","inquiries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調查；探究","explanation":"指為了弄清真相、事實或知識而進行的較系統的查詢和檢查；它是從一個問題出發，持續向未知處探進去，接近“調查”或“探究”。","examples":[{"en":"The committee opened an inquiry into the cause of the accident.","zh":"委員會開始調查這起事故的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The senator demanded a public inquiry into the missing funds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inquiry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ea748b09b117e6cc691","word":"insane","forms":["insane"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-755aff6fce0a583a","term":"insane","forms":["insane","more insane","insaner","most insane","insanest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精神失常的","explanation":"指人的精神狀態嚴重失常，已經不能正常判斷或思考；這是最接近字面核心的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The illness left him insane and unable to care for himself.","zh":"這場疾病使他精神失常，無法照顧自己。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one knew what had caused her to go insane.","zh":"沒人知道是什麼導致她精神失常的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cf07d734f6e4844","term":"insane","forms":["insane","more insane","insaner","most insane","insanest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"荒唐離譜的","explanation":"形容計劃、價格、數量或行為誇張到失去尺度，幾乎不可能認真執行；這裡不是說真的精神失常，而是把“失去理智”用於評價事情。","examples":[{"en":"That is an insane plan; we would never finish it on time.","zh":"那是個離譜的計劃，我們絕不可能按時完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Driving all night after that shift would be insane.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db7304319ed7d941faf3","word":"insect","forms":["insect"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb0eb0d410ee9808","term":"insect","forms":["insect","insects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"昆蟲","explanation":"指身體通常分為頭、胸、腹三部分、長有六條腿的節肢動物，如螞蟻、黃蜂和甲蟲。是否會飛不是判斷標準，所以螞蟻也屬於 insect。","examples":[{"en":"A small insect landed on my hand.","zh":"一隻小昆蟲落在了我的手上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many insects are active at night.","zh":"許多昆蟲在夜間活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54e65fa41c22278b","term":"insect","forms":["insect","insects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"卑微可鄙的人","explanation":"把人比作微小、令人厭惡而且沒有力量的蟲子，表示說話者認為對方卑微、可鄙或無足輕重。這是從“小蟲”的形象發展出的強烈貶義。","examples":[{"en":"He treated the powerless workers like insects.","zh":"他把那些無權無勢的工人當作卑微的蟲子一樣對待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tyrant treated his servants as insignificant insects.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e22560cee2c4b727c6a","word":"insert","forms":["insert"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e7ab8703dc154eb","term":"insert","forms":["insert","inserts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"插圖或插入的圖片","explanation":"指放進文字內容中的圖片或影象，重點是它被安排在原有文字之中。","examples":[{"en":"The article includes an insert showing the new bridge.","zh":"這篇文章中插入了一張展示新橋的圖片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newspaper's insert showed the route in color.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fdccb550acde823","term":"insert","forms":["insert","inserts","inserting","inserted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"插入；放入","explanation":"表示把一個物體或一段內容放進另一個東西里面，使它處在其中或成為其中的一部分。這是insert所有主要用法的動作核心。","examples":[{"en":"Insert the card into the reader and wait for the light.","zh":"把卡插入讀卡器，然後等待指示燈亮起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She inserted a note between the pages of the book.","zh":"她把一張便條夾進了書頁之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insert","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-106b086224a4d945eae2","word":"inside","forms":["inside"],"officialPos":"prep./adv./n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ebf43f906454f31","term":"inside","forms":["inside"],"pos":"adj","zh":"內部的；裡面的","explanation":"指位於某物內表面、內界或內部的部分，重點是“在邊界裡面”。","examples":[{"en":"The inside surface of the bowl is smooth.","zh":"這個碗的內表面很光滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wipe the inside surface with a clean cloth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8a3ef5c886c2936","term":"inside","forms":["inside"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到裡面；在裡面","explanation":"表示人或物向某個內部空間移動，或已經處在其中，尤其常用於建築物內部。","examples":[{"en":"It started to rain, so we went inside.","zh":"開始下雨了，所以我們進了屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come inside and warm up.","zh":"進來暖和一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-839516ad23c0d39a","term":"inside","forms":["inside","insides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內部；裡面","explanation":"指建築物、容器或其他事物的內部部分，是 inside 最基本的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The inside of the old house needs a lot of work.","zh":"這所老房子的內部需要進行大量修繕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please clean the inside before you close the lid.","zh":"蓋上蓋子前，請先把裡面清理乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-658a310107c9d499","term":"inside","forms":["inside"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……裡面；進入……內部","explanation":"表示某人或某物處在一個空間的邊界內，或移動到該空間內部。","examples":[{"en":"She put the key inside the drawer.","zh":"她把鑰匙放進了抽屜裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The note was hidden inside the book.","zh":"那張紙條藏在書裡面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e43ba08557cbb4f19ed7","word":"insight","forms":["insight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e30c4a2aae1f1a4","term":"insight","forms":["insight","insights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"深入瞭解；洞察","explanation":"指看進某個事物的內部，從而獲得比表面資訊更深的理解，常用於對問題、過程或主題的深入認識。","examples":[{"en":"The report offers valuable insight into why the project failed.","zh":"這份報告讓人深入瞭解了專案失敗的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Talking to local residents gave us insight into the history of the town.","zh":"和當地居民交談讓我們深入瞭解了這座城鎮的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e00087bd0a56d0ea","term":"insight","forms":["insight","insights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敏銳的觀察和推理能力","explanation":"指能夠從細節中迅速看出關鍵關係，並透過觀察和推理得到別人不容易發現的結論；也可指這樣得到的一條深刻認識。","examples":[{"en":"Her insight helped the team identify the real cause of the problem.","zh":"她敏銳的洞察力幫助團隊找到了問題的真正原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He had the insight to see that the two events were connected.","zh":"他敏銳地看出這兩件事彼此有關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-509c40394c0eaa8580dc","word":"insist","forms":["insist"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1c9ee8818725f86","term":"insist","forms":["insist","insists","insisting","insisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堅持自己的說法","explanation":"指堅定、明確地維護某個說法或立場，即使別人不相信或提出反對，也不改變自己的說法。","examples":[{"en":"She insisted on telling the truth.","zh":"她堅持要說實話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He insisted that he had locked the door.","zh":"他堅持說自己已經鎖了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1262e942714556e2","term":"insist","forms":["insist","insists","insisting","insisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堅持要求某事發生","explanation":"指不斷、堅決地要求某件事被做成，即使別人勸阻，也不願放棄這個要求。","examples":[{"en":"My parents insisted on paying for dinner.","zh":"我父母堅持要付晚餐的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She insisted that the damaged bridge be closed immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e677cd4db5d505aabbb6","word":"insistence","forms":["insistence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9b16c9462a8bd78","term":"insistence","forms":["insistence","insistences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅持不退讓","explanation":"指一個人持續堅持自己的觀點、要求或做法，不因為阻力而輕易改變。這個意義強調“不斷頂住阻力”的狀態，不一定已經提出了具體要求。","examples":[{"en":"Her insistence on checking every detail saved us from a costly mistake.","zh":"她堅持檢查每一個細節，使我們避免了一次代價高昂的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the criticism, he continued with quiet insistence.","zh":"儘管受到批評，他仍然安靜而堅定地繼續下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insistence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69f6726109c67c82","term":"insistence","forms":["insistence","insistences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"急切要求","explanation":"指帶有壓力的、要求對方必須接受或照辦的話語或行動。它是“堅持”向外施加壓力後的表現，通常比普通請求更強硬、更緊迫。","examples":[{"en":"At her insistence, we postponed the trip until the weather improved.","zh":"在她的堅決要求下，我們把旅行推遲到天氣好轉之後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At her insistence, we checked every window again.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insistence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14a60637758cb026afd2","word":"inspect","forms":["inspect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa7727113d4b9f99","term":"inspect","forms":["inspect","inspects","inspecting","inspected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細檢查並找問題","explanation":"指有目的地把某物仔細檢視一遍，重點是找出故障、漏洞或其他問題，或者判斷它目前的狀況。可以想象把目光“伸進去”，不放過可能出問題的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer inspected the pipes for cracks.","zh":"工程師仔細檢查管道是否有裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please inspect the package before signing for it.","zh":"簽收包裹前請仔細檢查一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc84e82fab29542c","term":"inspect","forms":["inspect","inspects","inspecting","inspected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式檢查","explanation":"指官員、檢查人員或上級按照職責和規定，正式檢視人員、建築、設施等。這仍然是“認真看進去”，但更突出檢查者的官方身份和程式性。","examples":[{"en":"The safety officer inspected the factory before it reopened.","zh":"安全檢查員在工廠重新開業前檢查了它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An officer inspected the ship before departure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b1957f394d1b896c806","word":"inspection","forms":["inspection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27cc8299991102d1","term":"inspection","forms":["inspection","inspections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"仔細檢查","explanation":"指對某物、某處或某種情況進行較為仔細、正式的檢視，以發現問題或確認事實；重點在“檢視得很仔細”這一過程。","examples":[{"en":"Upon closer inspection, the crack was only a layer of paint.","zh":"仔細一看，那道裂縫其實只是一層油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building passed its annual inspection.","zh":"這棟樓透過了年度檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98fe442255035a1459bb","word":"inspector","forms":["inspector"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-331e54196475e583","term":"inspector","forms":["inspector","inspectors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檢查員","explanation":"指受僱檢視、核查某項工作、機構、裝置或情況的人，重點是透過檢查發現是否符合要求或是否存在問題。","examples":[{"en":"The building inspector found several safety problems.","zh":"建築檢查員發現了幾處安全問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An inspector visits the school every year.","zh":"一名檢查員每年都會到這所學校檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspector","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21b9a2ef0f6f6e60","term":"inspector","forms":["inspector","inspectors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"警察督察","explanation":"指警察系統中的一種職級，通常負責監督警員或調查案件，級別低於 superintendent。具體職責和對應的中文職稱可能因國家或地區而不同。","examples":[{"en":"Inspector Patel is leading the investigation.","zh":"帕特爾督察正在負責這起調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Inspector Davies interviewed the missing child's neighbors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspector","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be2c9ce17278c9311853","word":"inspiration","forms":["inspiration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6673d5208da6e20","term":"inspiration","forms":["inspiration","inspirations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啟發過程","explanation":"指某種力量提升或刺激人的思考、情感和創造力的過程，也就是“受到啟發”或“獲得創作靈感”。它像把新的力量吸進心裡，讓原本停滯的思想重新運轉起來。","examples":[{"en":"She is waiting for inspiration to finish her novel.","zh":"她正在等待靈感來完成自己的小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The quiet garden gave him inspiration for his paintings.","zh":"安靜的花園給了他繪畫上的靈感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspiration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4001ad8700d6c777","term":"inspiration","forms":["inspiration","inspirations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"靈感來源","explanation":"指能夠激發人的思想、感情或創造力的人、物或情境，也就是“啟發人的來源”。它不是心裡產生的靈感本身，而是把這種靈感帶來的人或事。","examples":[{"en":"Her grandmother was the inspiration for the main character.","zh":"她的祖母是這個主要人物的靈感來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An abandoned railway station provided inspiration for the architect's design.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspiration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00b4490ebffb1da9","term":"inspiration","forms":["inspiration","inspirations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突然想到的妙點子","explanation":"指突然出現的新想法，尤其是聰明、有創意、能解決問題的點子。它可以看作“吸收了啟發”之後，靈感在腦中凝結成的具體結果。","examples":[{"en":"I had an inspiration while walking home.","zh":"我回家路上突然想到了一個妙點子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her inspiration solved the problem in minutes.","zh":"她突然想到的妙點子幾分鐘就解決了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspiration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113,114,115],"total":4,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1,"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-1cb6508098e9e5955ef7","word":"inspire","forms":["inspire"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d28badaabe5449b","term":"inspire","forms":["inspire","inspires","inspiring","inspired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"激勵；啟發","explanation":"把勇氣、熱情、想法或崇高感注入人的心裡，使對方受到鼓舞，產生行動的願望或新的想法。這是現代最重要的用法，既可以由人激勵人，也可以由故事、作品或榜樣帶來啟發。","examples":[{"en":"Her courage inspired me to keep going.","zh":"她的勇氣激勵我繼續堅持下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher inspired a love of reading in her students.","zh":"那位老師激發了學生對閱讀的熱愛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70199f676427073d","term":"inspire","forms":["inspire","inspires","inspiring","inspired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸入","explanation":"指把空氣吸進肺裡，也就是“氣息進入身體”這一最直接的字面意義；它與表示撥出的詞相對。","examples":[{"en":"The lungs inspire air and then expel it.","zh":"肺部吸入空氣，然後把它排出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient inspired slowly through the mouthpiece.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e142e6277b12b7e1110","word":"install","forms":["install"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18012de9aa2dcfc9","term":"install","forms":["install","installs","installing","installed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安裝並準備使用","explanation":"指把軟體、裝置或其他東西連線、放置並設定好，使它能夠正常使用。這是 install 最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We installed the new printer in the office.","zh":"我們在辦公室安裝了新印表機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please install the latest version before opening the file.","zh":"請先安裝最新版本，再開啟檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/install","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-561f0a3d84e3c5cf22f3","word":"installation","forms":["installation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d808db7e8323433","term":"installation","forms":["installation","installations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安裝過程","explanation":"指把軟體、裝置或系統裝上並設定好這一過程，重點在“裝好”這件事本身，而不是裝好的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The installation of the new software took only a few minutes.","zh":"安裝新軟體只花了幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Installation took longer because several parts were missing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/installation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c8705fcb197e687","term":"installation","forms":["installation","installations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成套裝置","explanation":"指已經安裝並安排妥當、能夠實際執行的一整套裝置和附屬部件，強調“裝好的系統整體”。","examples":[{"en":"The solar installation now supplies power to the entire building.","zh":"這套太陽能裝置現在為整棟大樓供電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The solar installation powers the entire research station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/installation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e8c03a94c7835b87dd8","word":"instance","forms":["instance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-098fb801630e436a","term":"instance","forms":["instance","instances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"例子；個案","explanation":"指拿來說明某種觀點、規則或情況的一個具體例子。它把抽象的一類事物變成眼前可以觀察的一個樣本，因此常用於論證或解釋。","examples":[{"en":"This is a clear instance of how small changes can make a big difference.","zh":"這清楚地說明了微小的變化如何產生巨大的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report gives several instances of discrimination in the workplace.","zh":"這份報告列舉了工作場所中發生歧視的幾個例子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-618dc58379dda348eba0","word":"instant","forms":["instant"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31f820fe9e8bc63e","term":"instant","forms":["instant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"立即發生的","explanation":"表示某事就在眼前發生，幾乎沒有等待時間，和“站在現在旁邊”的核心畫面相連。","examples":[{"en":"The medicine gave him instant relief.","zh":"這種藥讓他立刻得到了緩解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her instant reaction was to call her parents.","zh":"她的第一反應是給父母打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4481fa182b5c90c","term":"instant","forms":["instant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"速成的","explanation":"指食物、飲料或照片等已經預先處理好，使用時幾乎馬上就能得到結果；這是“離現在很近”延伸出的現代常用義。","examples":[{"en":"I keep instant noodles in the cupboard for busy nights.","zh":"我在櫥櫃裡放著泡麵，忙的時候晚上可以吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made instant coffee before the meeting.","zh":"開會前她衝了一杯速溶咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6bbe67eb75266588","term":"instant","forms":["instant","instants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一瞬間","explanation":"指非常短的一段時間，像眼睛眨一下那麼長；這是“靠近現在的一小段時間”的名詞化表達。","examples":[{"en":"He hesitated for an instant before answering.","zh":"他猶豫了一瞬間才回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lights went out for an instant.","zh":"燈光熄滅了一瞬間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ec743a1d44c0a4a","term":"instant","forms":["instant","instants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某一時刻","explanation":"指時間線上一個明確的點，尤其用於說明兩件事幾乎同時發生的時刻。","examples":[{"en":"The instant the door opened, the dog ran out.","zh":"門一開啟，狗就跑了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At that instant, the lights went out.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99262a0284ae7670f20f","word":"instead","forms":["instead"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ac2381693bd92e6","term":"instead","forms":["instead"],"pos":"adv","zh":"代替；改而","explanation":"表示原先考慮、計劃或正在做的事情被另一個選擇替代，意思是“改做這個，而不是那個”。它既可以指行動上的替換，也可以指選擇上的改變。","examples":[{"en":"I was going to cook, but we ordered pizza instead.","zh":"我本來打算做飯，但後來改成點披薩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took the train instead of driving.","zh":"她沒有開車，而是坐了火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26e59d6a3c92de802760","word":"instinct","forms":["instinct"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b59cfa6aa1c4f90b","term":"instinct","forms":["instinct","instincts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本能；天性","explanation":"指生來就有、通常不需要學習或思考便會出現的行為傾向，常用於動物，也可以用於人。","examples":[{"en":"The baby reached for her mother by instinct.","zh":"嬰兒憑本能伸手去找母親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some birds instinctively fly south before winter.","zh":"有些鳥會憑本能在冬天來臨前飛往南方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instinct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7dedea79d4235d3d","term":"instinct","forms":["instinct","instincts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直覺；直覺反應","explanation":"指沒有經過清楚的有意識推理，就立刻產生的判斷或反應；它像本能一樣迅速，但物件通常是人的判斷、選擇或感覺。","examples":[{"en":"My instinct told me that something was wrong.","zh":"我的直覺告訴我事情有些不對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My instinct told me to avoid the deserted alley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instinct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb9e4598c6785820fa4c","word":"instinctive","forms":["instinctive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e14db0c9507832f","term":"instinctive","forms":["instinctive","more instinctive","most instinctive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"本能的","explanation":"指某種反應、行為或感覺由人的本能引起，而不是主要靠後天學習或有意識推理產生。重點是它像身體自帶的反應機制一樣自然。","examples":[{"en":"A baby's instinctive reaction is to cry when it feels uncomfortable.","zh":"嬰兒感到不舒服時，本能的反應就是哭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made an instinctive movement to protect her face.","zh":"她本能地做了個動作來保護自己的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instinctive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dadc50c994cf4d3","term":"instinctive","forms":["instinctive","more instinctive","most instinctive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"下意識的；衝動的","explanation":"指人受到一瞬間的衝動驅使，未經充分思考就自發做出某個動作或反應。這是“本能的”在具體行為中的表現，突出速度和不假思索。","examples":[{"en":"Her instinctive reaction was to protect the child.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"The sudden noise caused an instinctive movement of his hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instinctive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3165df34fcec14548163","word":"institute","forms":["institute"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc29ecc780f5b8f8","term":"institute","forms":["institute","institutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構","explanation":"指為研究、教育、公益或其他明確目標而正式成立的組織。它和“把目標立起來”的畫面相連，強調這是一個有固定目的的機構。","examples":[{"en":"She works at a medical research institute.","zh":"她在一家醫學研究機構工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The institute funds research on endangered languages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/institute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e50b6f59113c0f63","term":"institute","forms":["institute","institutes","instituting","instituted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"創立；實行","explanation":"指正式開始一項政策、制度、程式或做法，或把某個組織創立起來。它就是“把一個目標立起來並讓它開始存在”的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The school instituted a new safety policy this year.","zh":"這所學校今年實行了一項新的安全政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city instituted a program to help homeless people.","zh":"這座城市創立了一項幫助無家可歸者的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/institute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-822fe3679c9dbb1c8a56","word":"institution","forms":["institution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df2e26e226d376e5","term":"institution","forms":["institution","institutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會制度或習俗","explanation":"指一個社會或群體長期建立並普遍遵循的做法、制度或習俗。這裡的institution不是具體建築，而是被社會固定下來的規則和生活安排。","examples":[{"en":"The institution of marriage has changed in many societies.","zh":"婚姻制度在許多社會中都發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Family remains an important social institution.","zh":"家庭仍然是一項重要的社會制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/institution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13582048570f9c5c","term":"institution","forms":["institution","institutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構；組織","explanation":"指已經建立並持續運作、通常受到社會認可的組織，尤其是教育、公共服務或慈善機構。大學、醫院、基金會等都可能是institution。","examples":[{"en":"The university is a respected institution in the region.","zh":"這所大學是該地區受人尊敬的機構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity is a vital institution for local families.","zh":"這家慈善機構對當地家庭非常重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/institution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1c58eabfe7be8974c54","word":"instruct","forms":["instruct"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94673ed7c6a5276b","term":"instruct","forms":["instruct","instructs","instructing","instructed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指導；教會","explanation":"指透過說明步驟、方法或規則，讓某人學會怎樣完成一件事。重點是把“怎麼做”的知識交給對方，而不只是表達個人看法。","examples":[{"en":"The technician instructed me how to reset the machine.","zh":"技術員教我怎樣重置這臺機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New staff are instructed in basic safety procedures.","zh":"新員工會接受基本安全操作的指導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instruct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d182f612cc5adf1d","term":"instruct","forms":["instruct","instructs","instructing","instructed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指示；吩咐","explanation":"指明確告訴某人應該或必須做什麼。它仍然保留“把行動方向交給對方”的核心畫面，但重點從教方法轉為規定行動。","examples":[{"en":"The manager instructed everyone to leave the building immediately.","zh":"經理指示所有人立即離開大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse instructed him to remain still.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instruct","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a92f6f089f63f0d476b","word":"instruction","forms":["instruction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-863b27b35ecdf6df","term":"instruction","forms":["instruction","instructions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教學；教導","explanation":"指向別人傳授知識或技能、使對方獲得資訊的過程，重點是“教人”這一行為，而不是某一條具體要求。","examples":[{"en":"The children receive instruction in music twice a week.","zh":"孩子們每週接受兩次音樂課教學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course provides instruction in basic first aid.","zh":"這門課程教授基礎急救知識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instruction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ad3e91a2cb58171","term":"instruction","forms":["instruction","instructions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指導；說明","explanation":"指傳給某人的一項具體資訊或做事方法，是從“教人”發展出來的一條可供參考的指導。","examples":[{"en":"The guide gives clear instructions on how to assemble the shelf.","zh":"這份指南清楚說明了如何組裝架子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Read the instructions before assembling the shelves.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instruction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf2eb894cc40f5c6e781","word":"instructor","forms":["instructor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94ff97e0a57d3c7c","term":"instructor","forms":["instructor","instructors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"授課者；教師","explanation":"指實際負責教課、講解內容並指導學習的人。它不侷限於某一教育階段，大學教師、培訓師或其他課程的授課者都可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"The instructor explained the exercise step by step.","zh":"授課者一步一步講解了這道練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ask the instructor if you have any questions.","zh":"有問題就問授課者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instructor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3e43f83d066d0cc621c","word":"instrument","forms":["instrument"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32e3504f1676204a","term":"instrument","forms":["instrument","instruments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂器","explanation":"指用來演奏音樂的器具，如小提琴、鋼琴或長笛；這是最常見、最容易先掌握的意思。它體現了instrument作為“讓某種作用發生的工具”這一核心。","examples":[{"en":"She practices her instrument for an hour every evening.","zh":"她每天晚上練習自己的樂器一小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trumpet is a difficult instrument to master.","zh":"小號是一種很難掌握的樂器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instrument","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bacbc415f506596b","term":"instrument","forms":["instrument","instruments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手段；工具","explanation":"指用來達到目的或產生某種結果的手段，不一定是有形物品。一個計劃、制度甚至某種力量，只要被用來推動結果，都可以被看作instrument。","examples":[{"en":"Education can be a powerful instrument for social change.","zh":"教育可以成為推動社會變革的有力手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treaty became an instrument of peace.","zh":"這項條約成了維護和平的手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instrument","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95f1789aee78e51f","term":"instrument","forms":["instrument","instruments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"測量儀器；顯示儀表","explanation":"指用來測量、記錄或顯示數值和變化的裝置，例如實驗室或控制檯上的儀器。它仍然是“幫助人獲得資訊的工具”。","examples":[{"en":"The instrument detected a small change in temperature.","zh":"這臺儀器檢測到了溫度的輕微變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The instrument measures tiny changes in air pressure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instrument","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38d9baa7eb7c73fba9af","word":"insult","forms":["insult"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-925dd1260c9b8cd4","term":"insult","forms":["insult","insults"],"pos":"noun","zh":"侮辱；辱罵","explanation":"指故意用無禮、輕蔑的言語或行為傷害、貶低某人；既可以指這種行為，也可以指一次具體的辱罵。","examples":[{"en":"Calling her work worthless was a serious insult.","zh":"說她的作品一文不值是一種嚴重的侮辱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took the remark as an insult.","zh":"他把那句話當成了侮辱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-907a98cb9add8274","term":"insult","forms":["insult","insults","insulting","insulted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"侮辱；辱罵","explanation":"指用無禮、輕蔑或貶低的言語、態度對待某人，使對方感到受辱；它強調對人的冒犯和貶低。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't mean to insult you with that question.","zh":"我問那個問題不是想侮辱你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt insulted when they laughed at her accent.","zh":"他們嘲笑她的口音時，她覺得受到了侮辱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insult","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-64e8937abc6d71cf2d2f","word":"insurance","forms":["insurance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42e2cc9c0dc6e87a","term":"insurance","forms":["insurance","insurances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險保障","explanation":"指為未來可能發生的意外、損失或其他不確定事件提供經濟補償的安排，也就是為風險撐起的一把保護傘。","examples":[{"en":"The car was badly damaged, but luckily we had insurance.","zh":"汽車損壞得很嚴重，但幸運的是我們買了保險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought insurance against theft before the trip.","zh":"她在旅行前買了防盜保險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insurance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3290ef000718f49f","term":"insurance","forms":["insurance","insurances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險業","explanation":"指為客戶提供保險保障、管理風險並處理理賠等業務的整個行業。","examples":[{"en":"After working in banking for years, he moved into insurance.","zh":"在銀行業工作多年後，他轉到了保險業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent twenty years working in insurance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insurance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6d7ddd8f414a22d8935","word":"intact","forms":["intact"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-606f078bb2c2e0a9","term":"intact","forms":["intact","more intact","most intact"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完整無損；原封不動","explanation":"指某物雖然經歷了搬運、變化或可能的危險，仍然保持完整，沒有被損壞、玷汙或改動。這是 intact 最常見、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The vase arrived intact after the long journey.","zh":"這隻花瓶經過長途運輸後仍然完好無損。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We managed to keep the original design intact.","zh":"我們設法保留了原設計，沒有改動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4736bc313525a831796b","word":"intake","forms":["intake"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc1912a91fcc5c1d","term":"intake","forms":["intake","intakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入口；進水口或進氣口","explanation":"指水、空氣等進入管道、裝置或系統的地方，重點是“從外面往裡面收進來”的入口，通常和出口相對。","examples":[{"en":"Leaves were blocking the air intake.","zh":"樹葉堵住了進氣口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the water intake for gravel before starting the pump.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07caa6c00d7b8764","term":"intake","forms":["intake","intakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攝入量；吸入量","explanation":"指在一段時間內被身體或系統收進去的數量，例如空氣、食物、水或能量的量。","examples":[{"en":"You should reduce your salt intake.","zh":"你應該減少鹽的攝入量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her daily water intake is about two liters.","zh":"她每天的飲水量大約是兩升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da7703ae48fe0462","term":"intake","forms":["intake","intakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新招收的一批人","explanation":"指某個組織、學校或機構在同一時期接收進來的一批人，核心仍是“收進來”。","examples":[{"en":"The new intake of students starts next Monday.","zh":"新招收的這批學生下週一開始上課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are preparing rooms for the autumn intake.","zh":"我們正在為秋季招收的這批人準備房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad9b338ab555c072a213","word":"integrate","forms":["integrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7c2f82e498c446f","term":"integrate","forms":["integrate","integrates","integrating","integrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……整合進整體","explanation":"把新知識、功能或部分放進已有系統，使它成為系統的一部分；重點是“納入一個整體”。","examples":[{"en":"The team integrated the new software into its existing system.","zh":"團隊把這款新軟體整合進了現有系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Integrate these records into the existing database.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67ad154596961ee3","term":"integrate","forms":["integrate","integrates","integrating","integrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"融入；適應群體","explanation":"指人或群體順利成為某個社群、團隊或環境的一部分，不再顯得格格不入；也可以表示讓自己融入其中。","examples":[{"en":"It took her several months to integrate into the new community.","zh":"她花了幾個月才融入這個新社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new pupils integrated quickly into the class.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fc3369ee44cc1ef","term":"integrate","forms":["integrate","integrates","integrating","integrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使完整；重新整合","explanation":"把破碎、分散或不完整的部分重新組織起來，使整體恢復完整；既可用於實際事物，也可用於生活、經歷等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"After the crisis, he slowly integrated the different parts of his life.","zh":"危機過後，他慢慢重新整合了生活的各個方面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment helps integrate memories into a coherent personal story.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb92cc52a766c500e001","word":"integration","forms":["integration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a00f1f0fc8c09246","term":"integration","forms":["integration","integrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整合成整體","explanation":"指把原本分散或不完整的部分合在一起，使其成為一個完整、統一的整體。這是 integration 最基礎的概念，其他許多意義都可以看作“合成整體”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The integration of the two databases will make the system more efficient.","zh":"兩個資料庫的整合將使系統執行得更高效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Successful integration takes time and careful planning.","zh":"成功的整合需要時間和周密的規劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5bec28b86818a17","term":"integration","forms":["integration","integrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相容合併","explanation":"指把彼此相容的元素組合起來並納入同一個系統，重點是不同部分合並後能夠共同發揮作用。它是“整合成整體”在技術、組織或功能層面的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The new software allows seamless integration with existing tools.","zh":"這款新軟體可以與現有工具無縫整合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The update improves integration between the two applications.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78587c41ed99a3375022","word":"integrity","forms":["integrity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43e0ea306184b304","term":"integrity","forms":["integrity","integrities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道德正直","explanation":"指一個人始終遵守明確的道德原則，即使沒人監督或這樣做並不方便，也不輕易違背自己的原則。","examples":[{"en":"Her integrity was never in doubt, even when the decision was unpopular.","zh":"即使這個決定不受歡迎，她的正直也從未受到懷疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A leader must act with integrity when no one is watching.","zh":"領導者必須在無人監督時也堅持正直行事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d592ef0cb279643","term":"integrity","forms":["integrity","integrities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"守信可靠","explanation":"強調一個人值得信賴，會履行承諾、說到做到；它是“道德原則完整”在與他人相處時最直接的表現。","examples":[{"en":"People trust him because he keeps his promises and has integrity.","zh":"人們信任他，因為他信守承諾，而且為人正直。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clients trusted her because of her professional integrity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/integrity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-718b3ba4d288a23b8fdb","word":"intellect","forms":["intellect"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f66bde6c5756c5d","term":"intellect","forms":["intellect","intellects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"思維能力","explanation":"指人進行思考、判斷、抽象推理和理解概念的心智慧力，也就是“思維中樞”本身。","examples":[{"en":"Education should develop both the intellect and the imagination.","zh":"教育應該同時培養思維能力和想象力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book challenges the intellect without becoming difficult to follow.","zh":"這本書挑戰人的思維能力，但並不難讀懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intellect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94a08e39efcfef4c","term":"intellect","forms":["intellect","intellects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某人的出眾智力","explanation":"指某一個人所擁有的思考和理解能力，尤其強調這種能力很強、很出眾。","examples":[{"en":"Her remarkable intellect made her a natural leader of the research team.","zh":"她出眾的智力使她自然成為研究團隊的領導者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her formidable intellect impressed even her harshest critics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intellect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ec9f882d11037b9c833","word":"intellectual","forms":["intellectual"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0de67018bd6f3b8","term":"intellectual","forms":["intellectual","more intellectual","most intellectual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"智力的；與思考有關的","explanation":"表示某件事依靠人的理解、推理或思考能力，而不是主要依靠體力或感官。它可以描述智力、活動、工作等。","examples":[{"en":"Reading widely develops your intellectual abilities.","zh":"廣泛閱讀能培養你的智力能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The job is physically tiring but intellectually rewarding.","zh":"這份工作雖然消耗體力，但在智力上很有收穫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intellectual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c619627c81010a1f","term":"intellectual","forms":["intellectual","more intellectual","most intellectual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聰明的；有知識的","explanation":"形容一個人理解力強，能夠進行較高層次的思考，或受過良好教育、對知識有興趣。重點不只是反應快，還包括思考和理解的能力。","examples":[{"en":"She is an intellectual person who enjoys difficult questions.","zh":"她是個有思想的人，喜歡思考難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discussion attracted intellectual people from many disciplines.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intellectual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fdfe97d2d38849a","term":"intellectual","forms":["intellectual","intellectuals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"知識分子；有學問的人","explanation":"指受過較多教育、長期從事思考或學術活動，並常談論文化、社會或政治問題的人。它描述的是一種知識和思想身份，而不只是個人智力高。","examples":[{"en":"Several young intellectuals spoke at the public meeting.","zh":"幾位年輕知識分子在公開會議上發了言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several prominent intellectuals signed the open letter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intellectual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f80a5e14017ccc05ab0","word":"intelligence","forms":["intelligence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7771dc5ae4fe4c5","term":"intelligence","forms":["intelligence","intelligences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"智力；理解和學習能力","explanation":"指理解事實、原則或意義，獲取知識，並把知識用於實際的思維能力。它強調一個人或有感知能力的存在能否理解和學習，而不只是知識儲備的多少。","examples":[{"en":"The test measures a child's intelligence and ability to learn.","zh":"這項測試衡量孩子的智力和學習能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Human intelligence allows us to solve problems in new ways.","zh":"人類的智力使我們能夠用新的方式解決問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intelligence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2db12eaedf102e5","term":"intelligence","forms":["intelligence","intelligences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聰明；理解力強","explanation":"指一個人實際表現出的理解深度和思維敏捷程度，也就是運用智力時顯得有多聰明、反應有多快。它更強調能力的質量或表現，而不是智力這一抽象能力本身。","examples":[{"en":"She handled the difficult question with remarkable intelligence.","zh":"她以非凡的理解力處理了這個難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His intelligence was clear from the way he adapted to the situation.","zh":"從他應對局勢的方式可以看出他的聰明才智。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intelligence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e71ab401bdd58c1b","term":"intelligence","forms":["intelligence","intelligences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情報；秘密資訊","explanation":"指透過觀察、調查或其他渠道獲得的、尤其涉及敵人或敵對活動的重要資訊。這裡的核心不再是“理解能力”，而是運用判斷力找出的關鍵訊息。","examples":[{"en":"The scouts returned with valuable intelligence about the enemy's movements.","zh":"偵察員帶回了有關敵軍動向的寶貴情報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need more intelligence before deciding what to do.","zh":"我們需要更多情報後再決定怎麼做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intelligence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-040eb379271f55d0ddbc","word":"intelligent","forms":["intelligent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b238e2cc1288824d","term":"intelligent","forms":["intelligent","more intelligent","intelligenter","most intelligent","intelligentest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聰明的；有智慧的","explanation":"形容人理解快、判斷力強，或具有較高的認知能力。這是最基本的意思，就像一盞燈能迅速照清複雜的問題。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is intelligent enough to solve the problem on her own.","zh":"瑪雅很聰明，能夠獨自解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is an intelligent student who asks difficult questions.","zh":"他是個聰明的學生，總會提出有難度的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intelligent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc616e88d4362eb8","term":"intelligent","forms":["intelligent","more intelligent","intelligenter","most intelligent","intelligentest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"經過周密思考的","explanation":"形容計劃、設計或決定考慮得很周到、很合理。這裡不是說物品本身會思考，而是說人的思考讓它顯得聰明。","examples":[{"en":"The team came up with an intelligent solution to the problem.","zh":"團隊為這個問題想出了一個周密而有效的解決方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was an intelligent decision to delay the launch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intelligent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4044ea11082e5a0c","term":"intelligent","forms":["intelligent","more intelligent","intelligenter","most intelligent","intelligentest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有思想內容的","explanation":"形容談話、討論或交流不是空泛閒聊，而是有思考、有見解、能推動理解的交流。那盞“分辨資訊的燈”從人的頭腦延伸到了語言中。","examples":[{"en":"We had an intelligent discussion about how to improve the neighborhood.","zh":"我們就如何改善社群進行了一次有深度的討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film offers intelligent commentary on family relationships.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intelligent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eec4c34a8bcdb24bde1f","word":"intend","forms":["intend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3b7d898f5464e88","term":"intend","forms":["intend","intends","intending","intended","intendest","intendedst","intendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打算；有意","explanation":"表示心裡已經把注意力和計劃指向某個目標，即“打算做某事”或“有意做某事”。","examples":[{"en":"She intends to study medicine after graduation.","zh":"她打算畢業後學醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I didn't intend to upset anyone with my comment.","zh":"我沒想因為那句話讓任何人不高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0d092b83d4aefab43b6","word":"intense","forms":["intense"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e34bb403dff2f3e3","term":"intense","forms":["intense","intenser","more intense","intensest","most intense"],"pos":"adj","zh":"程度極高","explanation":"形容某種性質或感受達到非常高、非常強的程度，例如熱、痛苦、壓力或競爭都可能是 intense。這個意思抓住了“繃得很緊、力量集中到很高”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The heat was so intense that we had to leave.","zh":"炎熱太強烈了，我們只好離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt intense pain in her shoulder.","zh":"她感到肩膀劇烈疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b81c1c857ad78bf5","term":"intense","forms":["intense","intenser","more intense","intensest","most intense"],"pos":"adj","zh":"專注而熱烈的","explanation":"形容感情、思想或學習等投入得很深、很集中，帶有熱烈和認真的意味。這裡的“強”不一定是外在聲音或力量大，而是內在的注意力和情感非常集中。","examples":[{"en":"After weeks of intense study, she passed the exam.","zh":"經過幾周高度專注的學習，她透過了考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He watched the chessboard with intense concentration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-17a4d9f8cf4ccfb87f9e","word":"intensify","forms":["intensify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dd223aa92e4c260","term":"intensify","forms":["intensify","intensifies","intensifying","intensified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使更強烈","explanation":"指主動讓某種感覺、狀態、力量或影響變得更強，像把音量旋鈕向上擰。例如，可以讓熱度、壓力或衝突進一步增強。","examples":[{"en":"The new measures may intensify pressure on small businesses.","zh":"新措施可能會加大小企業面臨的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They intensified their efforts before the deadline.","zh":"他們在截止日期前加大了努力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intensify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-385ba36d83e45a14","term":"intensify","forms":["intensify","intensifies","intensifying","intensified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得更強烈","explanation":"指某種情緒、局勢、現象或力量自身逐漸變強，不強調是誰主動使它增強。也可以理解為音量旋鈕自己繼續向上轉。","examples":[{"en":"As the storm intensified, the streets became empty.","zh":"隨著暴風雨加劇，街道變得空無一人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind intensified as we approached the coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intensify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0854ad1c7e25944fb52","word":"intensity","forms":["intensity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d17b82538fe7a75","term":"intensity","forms":["intensity","intensities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈性","explanation":"指某種感覺、表現或狀態具有強烈性質這一點，重點在“很強烈”這種特徵本身，而不一定是在測量具體數值。","examples":[{"en":"The intensity of her gaze made everyone fall silent.","zh":"她目光的強烈程度讓所有人都安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The music builds slowly, then releases its intensity in the final passage.","zh":"音樂逐漸增強，最後一段釋放出強烈的感染力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intensity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54d519a3de7fe44c","term":"intensity","forms":["intensity","intensities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強度；強烈程度","explanation":"指某種力量、感覺或現象處在什麼程度，強調可以在較弱和較強之間比較或變化。它是日常使用中最實用的中心義。","examples":[{"en":"You can adjust the intensity of the light with this switch.","zh":"你可以用這個開關調節燈光的強度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The intensity of the storm increased during the night.","zh":"夜間暴風雨的強度增強了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intensity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6745418a4852c85652dc","word":"intensive","forms":["intensive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-efbe34b852cf8bb7","term":"intensive","forms":["intensive","more intensive","most intensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深入徹底的","explanation":"表示投入很多時間、精力或注意力，因而做得深入、細緻而不是浮於表面。它把“強度很高”體現為徹底的研究、訓練或工作。","examples":[{"en":"The team carried out an intensive study of the local river.","zh":"團隊對這條當地河流進行了深入研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She began intensive training before the competition.","zh":"她在比賽前開始了高強度訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66b5b2ff2ba725d2","term":"intensive","forms":["intensive","more intensive","most intensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"短期高強度的","explanation":"表示把很多活動集中安排在很短的時間內，因此過程緊湊、強度很高。課程、訓練和治療尤其常見這種用法。","examples":[{"en":"I enrolled in an intensive three-week language course.","zh":"我報名參加了為期三週的高強度語言課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He attended an intensive language course over the summer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-282bcbc3f0a34a8a4ac6","word":"intent","forms":["intent"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6ba26c05d95a246","term":"intent","forms":["intent","more intent","most intent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"專心於","explanation":"指一個人的注意力和心思牢牢集中在某件事上，幾乎不被其他事情分散；就像一束光只照向一個目標。","examples":[{"en":"She was intent on improving her English before the exam.","zh":"她一心想在考試前提高英語水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Intent on her reading, she missed the announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-743d756f115e3477","term":"intent","forms":["intent","intents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意圖；目的","explanation":"指某人或某件事原本想實現的目標，也就是那束“心意之光”所對準的方向；它可以是個人的打算，也可以是制度或文字的目的。","examples":[{"en":"The intent of the new rule is to make the process fairer.","zh":"新規定的目的是讓這一過程更加公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His intent was to prevent another costly misunderstanding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74a11fdc7152e4924918","word":"intention","forms":["intention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cbc59a2b7020963d","term":"intention","forms":["intention","intentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"打算；意圖","explanation":"指一個人心裡已經形成、準備去做的行動計劃，重點是“想做什麼、準備怎麼做”，不表示事情一定會發生。","examples":[{"en":"Her intention is to study abroad next year.","zh":"她打算明年出國留學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had no intention of hurting anyone.","zh":"我並沒有傷害任何人的意圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87e35b8d28005e0e","term":"intention","forms":["intention","intentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目的；意旨","explanation":"指一項行動、計劃、法律或設計想要達到的結果，也就是“這樣做是為了什麼”。這裡的主體不一定是人。","examples":[{"en":"The intention of the new law is to protect consumers.","zh":"這項新法律的目的是保護消費者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He joined the course with the intention of improving his writing.","zh":"他參加這門課程是為了提高寫作能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-110c08f1fbfc058d8000","word":"interact","forms":["interact"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0399b5c0de149e96","term":"interact","forms":["interact","interacts","interacting","interacted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"互動；相互作用","explanation":"指雙方或多方彼此交流、影響或產生作用；物件可以是人和人，也可以是事物和事物。重點不只是單方面行動，而是雙方之間形成了來回的作用。","examples":[{"en":"Students interact with one another during group activities.","zh":"學生在小組活動中彼此互動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two chemicals interact when they are heated.","zh":"這兩種化學物質加熱後會相互作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interact","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-167d4b09d014f218c42a","word":"interaction","forms":["interaction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd82d00584e37bf1","term":"interaction","forms":["interaction","interactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相互作用；相互影響","explanation":"指兩個或多個物件、事件或因素彼此作用，因而產生新的效果或結果。重點不在單方面影響，而在雙方或多方相互作用的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful about the interaction between these two medicines.","zh":"要注意這兩種藥物之間的相互作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study examines the interaction of light and water.","zh":"這項研究考察光與水之間的相互作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37e8c04389c4cc3d","term":"interaction","forms":["interaction","interactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交流；互動","explanation":"指人與人之間透過交談、回應或共同活動而產生的交流和聯絡。它可以指一次具體的交流，也可以泛指人與人互動的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The workshop encouraged interaction among the participants.","zh":"這次研討會鼓勵參加者彼此互動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Daily interaction helped the two communities build trust.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-828408e40d4fe651488b","word":"interest","forms":["interest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc75b47ad2a10d06","term":"interest","forms":["interest","interests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"利息","explanation":"借錢的一方為使用這筆錢而支付的額外金額，或放貸的一方因提供資金而獲得的額外金額，通常按本金的一定比例計算。","examples":[{"en":"The bank charges five percent interest on personal loans.","zh":"這家銀行對個人貸款收取百分之五的利息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you leave the money in the account, it will earn interest.","zh":"如果你把錢留在賬戶裡，就會產生利息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff786438333bb883","term":"interest","forms":["interest","interests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"興趣","explanation":"對某個主題、活動或事物產生的好奇和關注，也就是把自己的注意力投入進去。","examples":[{"en":"She has a strong interest in traditional cooking.","zh":"她對傳統烹飪很感興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His interest in astronomy began when he was a child.","zh":"他對天文學的興趣始於童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04832d2b352ad463","term":"interest","forms":["interest","interests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"利益；權益","explanation":"指某人在企業、計劃或其他事業中擁有的利益、權利、份額或切身關係，因此該事業的結果會影響到他。","examples":[{"en":"The investor has a financial interest in the company.","zh":"這名投資者在這家公司擁有經濟利益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager declared a conflict of interest before the vote.","zh":"經理在投票前宣告瞭利益衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5a3831742c60500","term":"interest","forms":["interest","interests","interesting","interested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使感興趣","explanation":"使某人願意注意、瞭解或參與某件事，也就是把對方的注意力吸引到某個物件上。","examples":[{"en":"The science exhibition interested children and adults alike.","zh":"這場科學展覽讓孩子和成年人都很感興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It may interest you to know that the museum is free on Sundays.","zh":"你可能會感興趣：這家博物館星期日免費開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a30d5f870e0bcb30005d","word":"interested","forms":["interested"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-878093c113cf8bae","term":"interested","forms":["interested","more interested","most interested"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感興趣的","explanation":"表示某人的注意力、好奇心或參與意願被某事吸引，想了解、觀看或做這件事。","examples":[{"en":"I'm very interested in going to see that play.","zh":"我很想去看那場戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became interested in astronomy when she was a child.","zh":"她小時候就開始對天文學感興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interested","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e658d85a4c20614","term":"interested","forms":["interested","more interested","most interested"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有利害關係的","explanation":"表示某人或某方在某件事中有自己的利益、責任或得失，因此是相關方；這裡不一定表示喜歡或好奇。","examples":[{"en":"All interested parties will be invited to the meeting.","zh":"所有相關方都會被邀請參加會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Interested parties must disclose any financial connection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interested","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-637ab2808704d851a93b","word":"interesting","forms":["interesting"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff6fc52501bbf201","term":"interesting","forms":["interesting","more interesting","most interesting"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有趣的；引人注意的","explanation":"表示某人或某事能勾住注意力，讓人想繼續聽、看或瞭解；重點在於事物本身具有吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"The documentary was so interesting that I watched it twice.","zh":"這部紀錄片很有趣，我看了兩遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is this book interesting to children?","zh":"這本書對孩子來說有趣嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interesting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a3cf84a74842bfa4b07","word":"interfere","forms":["interfere"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc7057f3420292a8","term":"interfere","forms":["interfere","interferes","interfering","interfered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"干涉；妨礙","explanation":"指未經歡迎或不必要地介入別人的事務，從而打擾、妨礙對方。這個義項延續了“碰到一起、彼此擋路”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please do not interfere with my decision.","zh":"請不要干涉我的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The neighbors asked us not to interfere in their dispute.","zh":"鄰居請求我們不要插手他們的爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interfere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ac656986f40c308","term":"interfere","forms":["interfere","interferes","interfering","interfered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"波相互干涉","explanation":"在物理學中，指兩列或多列波疊加後相互影響，使合成波出現增強、減弱或其他圖樣。這裡不是有人故意插手，而是“疊在一起後改變結果”的技術意義。","examples":[{"en":"The two light waves interfere and form a pattern of bright and dark bands.","zh":"兩列光波相互干涉，形成明暗相間的條紋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sound waves interfere, making some seats much quieter than neighboring ones.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interfere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3b1f58e9bd1e8b95067","word":"interference","forms":["interference"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40f88053b9044707","term":"interference","forms":["interference","interferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"干涉；妨礙","explanation":"指某人或某事插手原本正在進行的事情，使其受到阻礙或不能按計劃發展；重點在於這種外來介入本身或它造成的妨礙。","examples":[{"en":"The project was delayed by political interference.","zh":"這個專案因政治干涉而延期了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parents should avoid interference in their children's friendships.","zh":"父母應避免干涉孩子的友誼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84d2c1ec1d3cca27","term":"interference","forms":["interference","interferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"波的干涉效應","explanation":"指兩列或多個波疊加後彼此增強或抵消，從而形成新的強弱分佈。這不是人為插手，而是不同波相遇後產生的物理干擾。","examples":[{"en":"The bright and dark bands are caused by interference between the light waves.","zh":"這些明暗相間的條紋是光波相互干涉造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists used wave interference to measure the distance accurately.","zh":"科學家利用波的干涉來精確測量距離。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6b6b85aed8adda90f7a7","word":"interior","forms":["interior"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49a1c54ccfe1cf2f","term":"interior","forms":["interior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"內部的；裡面的","explanation":"指位於某個邊界、封閉空間或物體裡面的部分，與外部相對。它可以描述房屋內部、容器內壁或其他空間的裡面。","examples":[{"en":"The interior walls of the cabin were covered with warm wooden panels.","zh":"小木屋的內牆鋪著溫暖的木質板材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent the afternoon cleaning the interior of the car.","zh":"我們整個下午都在清潔汽車內部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a82a26da03855b51","term":"interior","forms":["interior","interiors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內部；裡面","explanation":"指建築物、容器、洞穴等有邊界結構的裡面，和外部相對。可以把它想成“盒子裡真正佔據的空間或部分”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum looks plain outside, but its interior is beautifully decorated.","zh":"這座博物館外觀看起來很樸素，但內部裝飾得很漂亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow staircase leads into the interior of the cave.","zh":"一段狹窄的樓梯通向洞穴內部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94e6f02a5aca51e44a2c","word":"intermediate","forms":["intermediate"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b2847405264cac0","term":"intermediate","forms":["intermediate","more intermediate","most intermediate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"中間的；中等的","explanation":"指不在兩端，而處於兩個極端或一個範圍中間的位置、程度或階段。這個“中間”可以是空間上的，也可以是難度、大小或發展過程上的。","examples":[{"en":"This course is suitable for intermediate learners.","zh":"這門課程適合中級學習者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village lies at an intermediate point between the two cities.","zh":"這個村莊位於兩座城市之間的中間位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intermediate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfd750e6aed73026","term":"intermediate","forms":["intermediate","intermediates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中間位置的事物","explanation":"指處在兩個端點、等級或階段之間的事物；它是“中間的東西”本身，而不是用來修飾別的名詞的形容詞。","examples":[{"en":"The program offers an intermediate between the basic and advanced levels.","zh":"這個專案提供了基礎級和高階之間的中間等級。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reaction produces an unstable intermediate before the final compound.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intermediate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3bed2cb3a3acf7b6a8ef","word":"internal","forms":["internal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2187b15968c8cf64","term":"internal","forms":["internal","more internal","most internal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"內部的；裡面的","explanation":"指位於某個物體、系統或空間裡面的部分，與外部相對。想象把東西從外殼剖開，看到的裡面部分就是 internal。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic checked the car's internal components.","zh":"修理工檢查了汽車的內部零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scan showed damage to her internal organs.","zh":"掃描顯示她的內臟受到了損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/internal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15909b1339dccbe2","term":"internal","forms":["internal","more internal","most internal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"內心的；未表達出來的","explanation":"指發生在人的思想和感情裡面、沒有直接表現出來的內容。它仍然沿著“在裡面”的核心意象，只是裡面變成了人的心理世界。","examples":[{"en":"She hid her internal feelings behind a calm smile.","zh":"她用平靜的微笑掩飾內心的感受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He faced an internal conflict about leaving his job.","zh":"他在是否辭職的問題上經歷了內心的衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/internal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e3bb894756f8d62b575","word":"international","forms":["international"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8bf2e2b094e9be5","term":"international","forms":["international","more international","most international"],"pos":"adj","zh":"國際的；跨國的","explanation":"指涉及兩個或更多國家，或由不同國家共同參與的事物。核心畫面就是不同國家之間搭起了一座橋。","examples":[{"en":"The university hosts an international conference every year.","zh":"這所大學每年都會舉辦一次國際會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"International cooperation is essential to solve this problem.","zh":"國際合作對於解決這個問題至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/international","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5aa4891eabc30569","term":"international","forms":["international","more international","most international"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全世界共同的；不受國界限制的","explanation":"強調某個問題、原則或群體超越單個國家，屬於全人類共同面對或共同擁有的範圍。這是“國家之間的橋”進一步擴大到全球的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The international community must work together to protect the oceans.","zh":"國際社會必須共同努力保護海洋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency promotes international cooperation across all borders.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/international","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45fc4d92419dedc7c5e0","word":"Internet/internet","forms":["Internet","internet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6757269bb8b76f3d","term":"Internet","forms":["Internet","internets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路接入","explanation":"這裡的 internet 指你家、辦公室或裝置獲得的網際網路連線和服務，所以“沒有 internet”就是沒有網路可用。","examples":[{"en":"Our internet is down, so I can't send the report.","zh":"我們這兒斷網了，所以我沒法發報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campsite has electricity but no Internet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Internet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9251003f147ac77","term":"Internet","forms":["Internet","internets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機網路","explanation":"指任何使用網際網路協議彼此通訊的計算機網路，不一定專指面向全世界開放的全球網際網路，也可以是一個內部網路。","examples":[{"en":"The research center built an internet connecting all of its laboratories.","zh":"這家研究中心建了一個連線所有實驗室的計算機網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Internet connects researchers around the globe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Internet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2abd924b4579bac8","term":"internet","forms":["internet","internets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路接入","explanation":"這裡的 internet 指你家、辦公室或裝置獲得的網際網路連線和服務，所以“沒有 internet”就是沒有網路可用。","examples":[{"en":"Our internet is down, so I can't send the report.","zh":"我們這兒斷網了，所以我沒法發報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cottage has electricity but no internet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/internet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4bbc6c597820b0293ac","word":"interpret","forms":["interpret"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-794580c33d9b4627","term":"interpret","forms":["interpret","interprets","interpreting","interpreted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"理解並判斷含義","explanation":"指先弄清某個主題、資訊或現象的含義，再據此決定如何理解、行動或向別人說明。它突出的是從表面材料中讀出意義，而不只是複述字面內容。","examples":[{"en":"We need to interpret these results before making a decision.","zh":"我們需要先解讀這些結果，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We interpreted his silence as agreement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interpret","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12a85955bcff8536","term":"interpret","forms":["interpret","interprets","interpreting","interpreted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解釋或翻譯意義","explanation":"指把語言、夢、跡象、行為或神秘難懂的內容解釋成別人能理解的意義；在語言場景中，也可以指把一種語言口頭轉成另一種語言。","examples":[{"en":"How do you interpret her silence?","zh":"你如何理解她的沉默？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide interpreted the speaker's words for the visitors.","zh":"導遊把發言人的話口頭翻譯給訪客聽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interpret","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e0534af16e1fe990db0","word":"interpretation","forms":["interpretation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8bc18e4f2499439c","term":"interpretation","forms":["interpretation","interpretations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解釋；理解版本；口譯","explanation":"指把原本含糊、難懂的內容解釋清楚，也可以指解釋後形成的某種理解或版本；在語言服務語境中，還可指把口頭或手語內容轉換成另一種語言的行為。","examples":[{"en":"Her interpretation of the dream was completely different from mine.","zh":"她對這個夢的解釋和我的完全不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conference provided interpretation for international guests.","zh":"會議為國際來賓提供了口譯服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interpretation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc3c5d46b7d456ba","term":"interpretation","forms":["interpretation","interpretations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理解；解釋","explanation":"指解釋者賦予某段話、某個事件或某部作品的具體含義；同一物件可以有多個 interpretation，因為不同人可能形成不同理解。","examples":[{"en":"There are several interpretations of the final scene.","zh":"人們對最後一幕有好幾種不同的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your interpretation of the final scene differs from mine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interpretation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9666d9e8899447735cb9","word":"interpreter","forms":["interpreter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf5a9b8ca247e279","term":"interpreter","forms":["interpreter","interpreters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解釋事物的人或工具","explanation":"指幫助別人理解某種含義的人或事物，尤其可以是解釋夢境、符號或其他難懂內容的人。","examples":[{"en":"She became an interpreter of dreams after studying psychology.","zh":"她學習心理學後成了一名解夢者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide acted as an interpreter of the ancient symbols.","zh":"這名導遊充當了古代符號的解釋者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interpreter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf1faec590c69be0","term":"interpreter","forms":["interpreter","interpreters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口譯員","explanation":"指在說不同語言的人之間進行口頭翻譯、幫助雙方交流的人。","examples":[{"en":"The patient asked for an interpreter before speaking to the doctor.","zh":"病人在和醫生交談前要求安排一名口譯員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An interpreter helped the visitors communicate with the local officials.","zh":"一名口譯員幫助訪客與當地官員溝通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interpreter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2090fd63782e9c30ddc","word":"interrupt","forms":["interrupt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34db6c433b6a2554","term":"interrupt","forms":["interrupt","interrupts","interrupting","interrupted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打斷","explanation":"突然介入正在進行的談話、行動或工作，使它暫時停下或無法順利繼續；也可以指用說話、提問等方式打斷某人。","examples":[{"en":"Please do not interrupt me while I am explaining the plan.","zh":"我解釋計劃時請不要打斷我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The phone rang and interrupted our conversation.","zh":"電話響了，打斷了我們的談話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a927d433c2a71ec","term":"interrupt","forms":["interrupt","interrupts","interrupting","interrupted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打斷連續狀態","explanation":"使原本平穩、連續或單調的狀態出現間隔、變化或不連貫，好像從中間掰開一樣。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden shower interrupted the long afternoon of sunshine.","zh":"一場突然的陣雨打斷了持續了一下午的陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden announcement interrupted the silence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interrupt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbc3d30b2a88d68fe0e8","word":"interruption","forms":["interruption"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d381df932662239a","term":"interruption","forms":["interruption","interruptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"打斷；中斷","explanation":"指原本連續進行的事情被外來的行動或事件打斷，重點是“原來的流程被截斷”。打斷可以來自別人，也可以來自電話、噪聲、故障等事情。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting was delayed by several interruptions.","zh":"會議因幾次意外打斷而推遲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need an hour of quiet without interruption.","zh":"我需要一小時不受打擾的安靜時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interruption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef82572a1965c784","term":"interruption","forms":["interruption","interruptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中斷期間；停頓時段","explanation":"指某件事停止進行後、恢復之前的那段時間。這裡關注的不是“誰打斷了它”，而是打斷造成的空檔本身。","examples":[{"en":"There was a brief interruption in the service.","zh":"服務曾短暫中斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Service resumed after an interruption of forty minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interruption","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6fda7451bc6b4a595141","word":"intersection","forms":["intersection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9319e8b8eab89ce0","term":"intersection","forms":["intersection","intersections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"路口；交叉口","explanation":"兩條或多條道路、街道或通道相交的地方，就是一個 intersection。它強調不同行進路線匯合的地點。","examples":[{"en":"Turn left at the next intersection.","zh":"在下一個路口左轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a small café at the intersection of Pine Street and Third Avenue.","zh":"松樹街和第三大道的交叉口有一家小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intersection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9608c756d45f9150","term":"intersection","forms":["intersection","intersections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交叉；交集；重疊處","explanation":"這裡的 intersection 不一定是實際地點，而是指兩個或多個領域、事物或群體相互交叉、重合的部分。它保留了“幾條路在同一點匯合”的畫面，只是把道路換成了思想、文化或利益等抽象物件。","examples":[{"en":"Her research focuses on the intersection of technology and education.","zh":"她的研究重點是技術與教育的交叉領域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shaded area represents the intersection of both sets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intersection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fe1406a8254afd471de","word":"interval","forms":["interval"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cde03509fd9c7c15","term":"interval","forms":["interval","intervals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空間間隔","explanation":"指兩個地點、物體或人之間留下的距離或空隙，也就是兩道“牆”之間的空間。","examples":[{"en":"There was only a narrow interval between the two buildings.","zh":"兩棟樓之間只有一條很窄的空隙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trees were planted at regular intervals along the road.","zh":"道路兩旁每隔一段距離就種著樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2da3a2c0140343c2","term":"interval","forms":["interval","intervals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時間間隔","explanation":"指兩件事情發生之間經過的一段時間，例如兩次事件、兩次動作或兩個時刻之間的間隔。","examples":[{"en":"The interval between trains is about fifteen minutes.","zh":"兩班火車之間的間隔大約是十五分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take the medicine at six-hour intervals.","zh":"每隔六小時服一次藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-95661f9fc2c369e58745","word":"intervene","forms":["intervene"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd14324794f81b9a","term":"intervene","forms":["intervene","intervenes","intervening","intervened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"介入並改變局面","explanation":"指主動進入衝突、爭執或其他正在發生的局面，試圖制止、調解或改變事情的發展。重點不是旁觀，而是出手影響結果。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher intervened in the argument before anyone was hurt.","zh":"老師在有人受傷之前介入了這場爭執。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Neighbors intervened to stop the fight.","zh":"鄰居們出手制止了打鬥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-862f43964a3a49f1","term":"intervene","forms":["intervene","intervenes","intervening","intervened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"介於兩個時間或事件之間","explanation":"指某段時間、某件事或某個階段落在兩個時間點或事件之間；這裡沒有人主動干預，而是某物“來到中間”。","examples":[{"en":"Several quiet weeks intervened between the two meetings.","zh":"兩次會議之間隔了幾個平靜的星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several years intervened between the expedition and publication.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-375fc6f699c45970","term":"intervene","forms":["intervene","intervenes","intervening","intervened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處在兩者之間","explanation":"指一個地方、物體或人位於另外兩者之間，形成空間上的間隔或阻隔；這是“來到中間”最直觀的空間用法。","examples":[{"en":"A low wall intervenes between the garden and the road.","zh":"花園和道路之間隔著一堵矮牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strip of woodland intervenes between the two farms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77f4c0b60ee93a5cb1e5","word":"intervention","forms":["intervention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9bbb7c426355d7c0","term":"intervention","forms":["intervention","interventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"介入；干預","explanation":"指主動插入某個正在發展的過程，試圖阻止、糾正或改變結果。這個詞本身不一定帶有負面評價，既可以是多管閒事式的干涉，也可以是為了解決問題而及時出手。","examples":[{"en":"The referee's quick intervention stopped the argument from becoming a fight.","zh":"裁判及時介入，避免了爭吵升級為打架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child's intervention helped the two friends make peace.","zh":"孩子的介入幫助兩個朋友和好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-623d86d0a7599545","term":"intervention","forms":["intervention","interventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律介入","explanation":"在美國法律語境中，指原本不是案件當事人的個人或機構申請加入案件，並請求法院允許自己成為當事方。","examples":[{"en":"The charity filed for intervention because the court's decision could affect its members.","zh":"這個慈善機構申請介入訴訟，因為法院的裁決可能會影響其成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge allowed the charity's intervention in the proceedings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intervention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02540942346fdfbf21a9","word":"interview","forms":["interview"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74132be3e48b88a6","term":"interview","forms":["interview","interviews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"採訪","explanation":"指記者或主持人與某人交談，透過提問記錄對方的觀點、經歷或說法，準備發表或播出；談話也可以透過電話或網路進行。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter interviewed the mayor about the new plan.","zh":"記者就這項新計劃採訪了市長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave an interview to a local newspaper.","zh":"她接受了當地報紙的採訪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25124f64b024e4a2","term":"interview","forms":["interview","interviews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面試","explanation":"指僱主或招聘方透過正式談話評估求職者是否適合某項工作；也可泛指申請學校、專案等時的正式評估會談。","examples":[{"en":"I have an interview for the marketing job on Friday.","zh":"我星期五要參加市場營銷職位的面試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interview went better than I expected.","zh":"這次面試比我預想的順利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7411c3159e6eebf8","term":"interview","forms":["interview","interviews","interviewing","interviewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"採訪或面試某人","explanation":"指主動向某人提問並透過正式談話瞭解對方，可用於記者採訪，也可用於招聘方對求職者進行面試。","examples":[{"en":"The company interviewed six candidates for the position.","zh":"公司面試了六名這個職位的候選人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The journalist interviewed the scientist after the lecture.","zh":"講座結束後，記者採訪了那位科學家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/interview","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a427b3cbc38e5ca8ee49","word":"intimacy","forms":["intimacy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-821bb2857058ed2c","term":"intimacy","forms":["intimacy","intimacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親密與坦誠","explanation":"指人與人之間感到親近、信任並願意敞開心扉的狀態或氛圍；這種親密有時包含性關係，但並不一定包含。","examples":[{"en":"Honest conversations can create a sense of intimacy between friends.","zh":"坦誠的談話可以在朋友之間營造親密感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small room gave the dinner a feeling of intimacy.","zh":"這個小房間讓這頓晚餐帶有一種親密的氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intimacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e071141641e8eb0","term":"intimacy","forms":["intimacy","intimacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親密關係","explanation":"指一段具體的、建立在親近和信任之上的關係；重點是“關係本身”，而不只是親密的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Over the years, she formed several close intimacies at work.","zh":"這些年來，她在工作中建立了幾段親密的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their intimacy grew through years of mutual support.","zh":"他們在多年的相互支援中逐漸建立了親密關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intimacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c370f4e5287e29eef416","word":"intimate","forms":["intimate"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f360904bcac05307","term":"intimate","forms":["intimate","more intimate","most intimate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親密的；熟識的","explanation":"指彼此非常熟悉、關係親近，通常比普通朋友更深入。這個“走進對方內心”的核心意思是 intimate 最重要的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is one of my most intimate friends.","zh":"瑪雅是我最親密的朋友之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two artists became intimate after working together for years.","zh":"這兩位藝術家合作多年後變得非常親密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e01598a2febf4549","term":"intimate","forms":["intimate","more intimate","most intimate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"私人的；私密的","explanation":"指只適合少數人參與或瞭解的事物，像是進入一個人的私人空間，而不是公開場合。","examples":[{"en":"They held an intimate dinner at home with only six guests.","zh":"他們在家舉行了一場只有六位客人參加的私密晚宴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shared some intimate details about her childhood.","zh":"她分享了一些關於自己童年的私密細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114,115],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-ffa53c9adaffb4da5cc5","word":"intimidate","forms":["intimidate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a33e876b86a28e7b","term":"intimidate","forms":["intimidate","intimidates","intimidating","intimidated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使害怕；震懾","explanation":"指用威脅、強硬態度或令人畏懼的氣勢，使某人感到害怕、緊張或膽怯，因而不敢繼續做某事或不敢反抗。","examples":[{"en":"The aggressive questions intimidated the young witness.","zh":"咄咄逼人的問題讓年輕證人感到害怕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't let the size of the task intimidate you.","zh":"不要被任務的規模嚇倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intimidate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6b847a0ed0b2c484c73f","word":"into","forms":["into"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01d4d15e6bde84b3","term":"into","forms":["into"],"pos":"prep","zh":"進入……裡面","explanation":"表示人或物朝某個空間的內部移動，重點是“從外面進去”。","examples":[{"en":"The children ran into the garden when it started to rain.","zh":"開始下雨時，孩子們跑進了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stepped into the elevator just before the doors closed.","zh":"門快關上時，她走進了電梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/into","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-320536522dc5728b","term":"into","forms":["into"],"pos":"prep","zh":"撞向；撞上","explanation":"表示運動中的人或物以力量碰到某個目標，畫面仍然是朝目標“進去”或衝上去。","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist lost control and crashed into a parked van.","zh":"騎車人失去了控制，撞上了一輛停著的麵包車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wasn't looking and walked into a glass door.","zh":"我沒注意，撞上了一扇玻璃門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/into","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6138a816cac1a0f9","term":"into","forms":["into"],"pos":"prep","zh":"變成；製成","explanation":"表示把某物改變成另一種形式、狀態或物質，像是讓它“進入”新的形態。","examples":[{"en":"The artist turned an old door into a dining table.","zh":"那位藝術家把一扇舊門改成了餐桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The caterpillar changed into a butterfly.","zh":"毛毛蟲變成了蝴蝶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/into","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d53ca01b678bb06d261f","word":"intonation","forms":["intonation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f7c68e76f5e156d","term":"intonation","forms":["intonation","intonations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語調；聲調起伏","explanation":"說話時聲音沿著一條高低曲線變化，這種上升、下降和停頓形成的整體效果就是 intonation。它可以幫助聽者判斷一句話是在提問、陳述，還是帶有某種態度。","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of the question changes with the intonation.","zh":"這個問題的意思會隨著語調變化而改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm intonation made the announcement less alarming.","zh":"她平靜的語調讓這則通知聽起來沒那麼令人不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intonation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5287a3e7642ecda0","term":"intonation","forms":["intonation","intonations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用語調加強情感","explanation":"說話者透過提高、壓低或改變聲音的力度和走勢，讓話語更有感染力、更顯得諷刺、憤怒、驚訝等；這裡強調的是語調所產生的情感力量。","examples":[{"en":"He used a sharp intonation to show that he was annoyed.","zh":"他用尖銳的語調錶示自己很惱火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her rising intonation conveyed disbelief rather than curiosity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intonation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-111f44a7032e2ea46031","word":"intrigue","forms":["intrigue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96aa28ab184c3bb2","term":"intrigue","forms":["intrigue","intrigues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰謀；秘密策劃","explanation":"指為了達到某種目的而暗中設計的複雜計劃，通常帶有隱瞞、欺騙或操縱意味；也可以泛指一連串秘密活動。","examples":[{"en":"The minister was caught in an intrigue to remove his rival.","zh":"那名部長卷入了一場企圖排擠對手的陰謀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The palace was full of political intrigue.","zh":"宮廷裡充滿了政治陰謀和暗鬥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intrigue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca6942aa562e16fd","term":"intrigue","forms":["intrigue","intrigues","intriguing","intrigued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引起興趣；使著迷","explanation":"指某件事讓人產生好奇心，想進一步瞭解；就像複雜線索把人的注意力纏住一樣。這是現代英語中最常見的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The strange message intrigued Maya, so she began to investigate.","zh":"那條奇怪的資訊引起了瑪雅的興趣，於是她開始調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was intrigued by the scientist's unusual explanation.","zh":"那位科學家不同尋常的解釋引起了我的好奇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intrigue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fee7196f6817d6f81e7","word":"introduce","forms":["introduce"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-12755e18241b4dab","term":"introduce","forms":["introduce","introduces","introducing","introduced","introducest","introducedst","introduceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"介紹某人認識","explanation":"把一個人帶到另一個人或一群人面前，讓他們彼此認識。這裡的“帶到面前”最接近日常中文裡的“介紹”。","examples":[{"en":"May I introduce you to my sister?","zh":"我可以把你介紹給我妹妹嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She introduced herself to the new neighbors.","zh":"她向新鄰居作了自我介紹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/introduce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8272f8a5e9249ffb","term":"introduce","forms":["introduce","introduces","introducing","introduced","introducest","introducedst","introduceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式提出或推薦","explanation":"把法案、計劃、觀點或新人正式帶到公眾或某個機構面前，使其被大家知道、討論或考慮。","examples":[{"en":"The committee introduced a proposal to improve public transport.","zh":"委員會提出了一項改善公共交通的提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The senator introduced a bill limiting industrial pollution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/introduce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3db5338aae140c5cc04","word":"introduction","forms":["introduction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-415af784f54baf21","term":"introduction","forms":["introduction","introductions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"介紹或引入的過程","explanation":"指把某人、某物或某種做法帶到新的場合中，使別人開始認識、接觸或使用它；重點在“引入”這個過程。","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of electric buses has reduced noise in the city center.","zh":"電動公交車的引入減少了市中心的噪音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school is planning the introduction of a new language program next year.","zh":"這所學校計劃明年引入一項新的語言課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/introduction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8bd3f7b0d8eca797","term":"introduction","forms":["introduction","introductions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書文章的導言","explanation":"指書、文章或報告開頭用來引出主題、背景和後續內容的部分，也就是讀者進入正文前的導言。","examples":[{"en":"The main argument is explained clearly in the introduction.","zh":"主要論點在導言中得到了清楚的說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The introduction explains how the interviews were conducted.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/introduction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78777adf53d87ea7d72d","word":"intrude","forms":["intrude"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2172f6f0b3c21e50","term":"intrude","forms":["intrude","intrudes","intruding","intruded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"未經允許闖入或干涉","explanation":"指人在沒有得到邀請或許可、也不受歡迎的情況下進入某處，或插入別人的談話、私人生活和活動中；也可指某物越界佔入別人的空間。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't mean to intrude on your family dinner.","zh":"我不是故意要打擾你們一家吃飯的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new road intrudes on the quiet landscape.","zh":"這條新公路侵入了這片寧靜的景觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intrude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-023b54a361b6b0e5","term":"intrude","forms":["intrude","intrudes","intruding","intruded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把某物強行塞入","explanation":"指把物體、意見或其他東西硬推到某個空間、談話或範圍裡；重點是“外力推入”，而不是它自己進入。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't intrude your personal opinions into our discussion.","zh":"請不要把你的個人意見強行塞進我們的討論中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He intruded irrelevant political opinions into every conversation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intrude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aedad4dfac4747d17e5d","word":"intruder","forms":["intruder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f42601e6bf711db6","term":"intruder","forms":["intruder","intruders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"闖入者；侵入者","explanation":"指未經允許進入某處，或不受歡迎地打擾、干涉他人的人。它突出“越過界限、闖進不屬於自己的地方”這一層意思。","examples":[{"en":"The alarm went off when an intruder entered the house.","zh":"有闖入者進入房子時，警報響了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The alarm frightened away the intruder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intruder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-207dcab2fa481014e6bc","word":"intuition","forms":["intuition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84e017978c3da384","term":"intuition","forms":["intuition","intuitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直覺能力","explanation":"指人在沒有有意識地一步步分析或推理時，仍能直接形成判斷的能力；這種判斷過程就像腦中的燈先亮了，但本人未必馬上說得出理由。","examples":[{"en":"Young children often rely on intuition before they can explain their choices.","zh":"幼兒還不能解釋自己的選擇時，常常會依靠直覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She trusted her intuition when selecting promising recruits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intuition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b52f311e58bdf1fc","term":"intuition","forms":["intuition","intuitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直覺洞察","explanation":"指直覺能力具體照亮的一個想法、預感或判斷，也就是人在還沒有充分分析時，對某件事突然產生的洞察。","examples":[{"en":"Her intuition told her not to take the shortcut.","zh":"她的直覺告訴她不要走那條近路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her intuition told her the painting was older.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intuition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59ab84ee2e3e9d75f6d7","word":"invade","forms":["invade"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f96e77ba142c5b8","term":"invade","forms":["invade","invades","invading","invaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"侵犯隱私或空間","explanation":"指未經允許進入或干涉某人的私人範圍，重點是越過了本來應受尊重的界限，例如檢視私生活或打擾個人空間。","examples":[{"en":"Constant questions from strangers can invade your privacy.","zh":"陌生人不斷提問可能會侵犯你的隱私。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reporters invaded the family's privacy after the accident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f0407b2cbc28f9d","term":"invade","forms":["invade","invades","invading","invaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"武力入侵併佔領","explanation":"指軍隊或國家以武力進入另一個國家或地區，通常帶有徵服、佔領或發動戰爭的目的。","examples":[{"en":"The army invaded the neighboring country at dawn.","zh":"軍隊在黎明時入侵了鄰國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island was invaded and occupied for several years.","zh":"這座島遭到入侵併被佔領了好幾年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-860df3df27fb58bbfc79","word":"invaluable","forms":["invaluable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9aa3243feefe44fa","term":"invaluable","forms":["invaluable","more invaluable","most invaluable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其寶貴的；不可或缺的","explanation":"形容某人或某物的重要性和價值大到難以計算，常常帶有“對完成某事特別有幫助、不可替代”的意思。它不是說價值無法確定為零，而是說價值高得難以估量。","examples":[{"en":"Her advice was invaluable when I was preparing for the interview.","zh":"我準備面試時，她的建議極其寶貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volunteers provided invaluable help after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，志願者提供了不可或缺的幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invaluable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44a43b475350a5f18dbd","word":"invariably","forms":["invariably"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3e64ad0b54e36cf","term":"invariably","forms":["invariably"],"pos":"adv","zh":"總是；每次都如此","explanation":"它表示某件事每次或幾乎每次都按同樣方式發生，就像沿著固定軌道執行一樣。根據語境可以譯為“總是”“一貫”“無一例外地”，但核心是反覆發生而且沒有變化。","examples":[{"en":"She invariably arrives early for work.","zh":"她上班總是很早到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their plans invariably change at the last minute.","zh":"他們的計劃總是在最後一刻改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invariably","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb117886e6c1026a3e65","word":"invasion","forms":["invasion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c9748d780f86383","term":"invasion","forms":["invasion","invasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍事入侵","explanation":"指一個國家或政治實體的武裝力量進入另一個實體控制的領土，通常意在征服土地或改變當地政權。這是 invasion 最典型、最核心的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The invasion of the island began at dawn.","zh":"對該島的入侵在黎明時開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country prepared for a possible invasion.","zh":"這個國家為可能發生的入侵做好了準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-491ee178ec0e86a3","term":"invasion","forms":["invasion","invasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不受歡迎的闖入","explanation":"指個人或群體未經同意進入不歡迎他們的地方，也可引申為某種事物大量進入並干擾一個空間或領域。核心仍是“外來的東西越過邊界闖進來”。","examples":[{"en":"The beach was overwhelmed by an invasion of tourists.","zh":"這片海灘被大批湧入的遊客弄得不堪重負。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constant messages felt like an invasion of privacy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e2f4f54c7a1c494162b","word":"invent","forms":["invent"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de8109ef744a4192","term":"invent","forms":["invent","invents","inventing","invented","inventest","inventedst","inventeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發明；創造新方法或裝置","explanation":"指設計並創造出以前沒有的裝置、方法、過程或解決辦法，重點是產生新的東西，而不只是找到已經存在的東西。","examples":[{"en":"She invented a simple tool that saves gardeners a lot of time.","zh":"她發明了一種簡單的工具，能為園丁節省很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team invented a faster way to sort the files.","zh":"團隊發明了一種更快的檔案分類方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cd861f8b7e12d87","term":"invent","forms":["invent","invents","inventing","invented","inventest","inventedst","inventeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編造；捏造說法或藉口","explanation":"指為了某種目的臨時創造出一個並非事實的藉口、故事或解釋，就像把腦中沒有的說法帶到現實對話中。","examples":[{"en":"He invented an excuse for being late, but nobody believed him.","zh":"他為遲到編了個藉口，但沒人相信他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He invented an excuse to avoid the meeting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bebe4b948683362feab","word":"invention","forms":["invention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a39af35c2643df7d","term":"invention","forms":["invention","inventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發明物","explanation":"指人新造出來的東西、裝置、方法或想法，重點是已經被提出或做出來的成果。它可以是很具體的產品，也可以是解決問題的新辦法。","examples":[{"en":"Her latest invention uses less electricity than older machines.","zh":"她最新的發明比舊機器耗電少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young engineer showed us an invention for sorting recyclable materials.","zh":"那位年輕工程師給我們看了一項用於分類可回收材料的發明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15587e13d9ca4c7d","term":"invention","forms":["invention","inventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發明行為","explanation":"指創造某種新東西或新方法這一行為本身，尤其常用於說明某項技術、工具或制度何時出現，以及它帶來的影響。","examples":[{"en":"The invention of the telephone changed the way people communicated.","zh":"電話的發明改變了人們交流的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The invention of refrigeration made it easier to transport fresh food.","zh":"製冷技術的發明使運輸新鮮食品變得更容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":3,"counts":{"113":2,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-78921cb5cc3ef08ee9dd","word":"inventor","forms":["inventor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e26475efa308c8f8","term":"inventor","forms":["inventor","inventors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發明者","explanation":"指發明新產品、工具、裝置或方法的人，既可以是出於興趣進行發明的人，也可以是以發明為職業的人。","examples":[{"en":"The inventor of this device wanted to make cooking easier.","zh":"這個裝置的發明者希望讓做飯變得更容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became an inventor after building a machine for her school project.","zh":"她為學校專案製作了一臺機器後，成了一名發明者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inventor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b11a85b296a90afc4604","word":"inventory","forms":["inventory"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3cc7d253cdad460","term":"inventory","forms":["inventory","inventories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"庫存；現貨","explanation":"指某家商店、倉庫或其他地點當下擁有、可以提供的貨物總量。重點是“手頭實際有多少”，不只是記錄這些貨物的檔案。","examples":[{"en":"The store has a limited inventory of winter coats.","zh":"這家商店的冬衣庫存有限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to order more chairs because our inventory is running low.","zh":"我們需要再訂些椅子，因為庫存快用完了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inventory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea9d751596b81f85","term":"inventory","forms":["inventory","inventories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"存貨清單；物品清單","explanation":"指把某處所有物品逐項列出的詳細記錄。它回答的是“有哪些東西、各有多少”，而不是單純表示這些東西本身。","examples":[{"en":"The manager checked the inventory before placing a new order.","zh":"經理在下新訂單前核對了存貨清單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inventory lists every painting in the collection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inventory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-314fb3b5264f9545","term":"inventory","forms":["inventory","inventories","inventorying","inventoried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"盤點；登記庫存","explanation":"指逐項檢查手頭的貨物或資源，並把結果記錄成清單。它就是名詞“盤點過程”的動詞形式，通常還暗含發現缺貨後採取補充措施的工作背景。","examples":[{"en":"The night crew inventories the shelves every Friday.","zh":"夜班員工每週五盤點貨架上的商品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We inventoried all the equipment before the trip.","zh":"出發前我們盤點了所有裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inventory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a2cc603b75c1cfc9a2d","word":"invest(ment)","forms":["invest","investment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d894f67ffca5c32","term":"invest","forms":["invest","invests","investing","invested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投入時間、金錢或精力","explanation":"表示把時間、金錢、精力等資源投入某件事，通常暗含希望達到某個目的或獲得某種回報。這裡的“投入”不一定是金融投資，也可以是投入精力或長期關注。","examples":[{"en":"She invested a lot of time in learning Spanish.","zh":"她在學習西班牙語上投入了很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is investing heavily in renewable energy.","zh":"這家公司正在大力投資可再生能源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-556ccd5619465c22","term":"invest","forms":["invest","invests","investing","invested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投資以獲取收益","explanation":"表示把錢或資本投入某項資產、企業或計劃，希望將來獲得經濟收益。這是 s1“投入資源”在金融領域的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"Many people invest in property as a long-term strategy.","zh":"許多人把房地產投資作為長期策略。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He invested his savings in a small technology company.","zh":"他把積蓄投資到一家小型科技公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2589b65007ef34c","term":"investment","forms":["investment","investments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投入；投資行為","explanation":"指投入資金、時間、精力等，或指這種投入所處的狀態，重點是為了將來獲得某種好處。教育、訓練和健康方面的投入也可以用這個詞表示，不限於賺錢。","examples":[{"en":"Giving your children a good education is a wise long-term investment.","zh":"給孩子良好的教育是一項明智的長期投資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Learning a new skill is an investment in your future.","zh":"學習一項新技能是在為自己的未來投資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/investment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4790cf17878074c","term":"investment","forms":["investment","investments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投資專案；資本投入","explanation":"指把資本放入某個專案、企業或資產中，期待透過收入或價值上漲獲得利潤。它既可以指投資這件事，也可以指具體投進去的一筆錢或一個專案。","examples":[{"en":"The company made a large investment in renewable energy.","zh":"這家公司對可再生能源進行了大筆投資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The solar farm represents a substantial long-term investment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/investment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29ba6947875fa4dbc743","word":"investigate","forms":["investigate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2627ab2910cfdc1","term":"investigate","forms":["investigate","investigates","investigating","investigated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調查事實或原因","explanation":"為了弄清事實、獲得資訊或找出原因而進行有條理的研究和調查。它可以用於科學現象，也可以用於日常問題。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists are investigating why the river became polluted.","zh":"科學家們正在調查這條河受到汙染的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to investigate the problem before making a decision.","zh":"我們需要先調查清楚這個問題，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/investigate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25b16354c431e9c3","term":"investigate","forms":["investigate","investigates","investigating","investigated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"查究秘密或案件","explanation":"專門查詢被隱藏的事實、線索或秘密，尤其常用於調查尚未解決的犯罪案件。這裡仍然是“拿著手電筒往事情裡面照”，只是物件更隱秘、更需要追查。","examples":[{"en":"The police are investigating the robbery at the corner shop.","zh":"警方正在調查那家街角商店的搶劫案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee will investigate the allegations carefully.","zh":"委員會將仔細調查這些指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/investigate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57794bdeddd908748d80","word":"investigation","forms":["investigation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03b61d1bf3a905b1","term":"investigation","forms":["investigation","investigations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調查；研究","explanation":"指為了弄清事實、原因或問題而進行的有步驟的調查和查證，通常包含蒐集資料、詢問相關人員以及仔細檢查等過程。它可以是對案件的調查，也可以是對科學問題、事故原因或工作情況的研究。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation into the accident is still under way.","zh":"對這起事故的調查仍在進行中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university launched an investigation into the student's complaint.","zh":"這所大學針對該學生的投訴展開了調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/investigation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea077ff913f0f89b0fb8","word":"investigator","forms":["investigator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-44233c540c35a91a","term":"investigator","forms":["investigator","investigators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調查員；調查人員","explanation":"指透過查閱資料、詢問人員和核對證據來調查某件事、查明事實的人。這個詞強調“負責調查的人”，不限定其一定屬於警察或專門偵探。","examples":[{"en":"The investigator interviewed everyone who had witnessed the accident.","zh":"調查員詢問了所有目睹事故的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several investigators are examining the company’s financial records.","zh":"幾名調查人員正在審查這家公司的財務記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/investigator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3013c082c75edc91359","word":"invitation","forms":["invitation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4183c810c0442bfc","term":"invitation","forms":["invitation","invitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邀請；邀請行為","explanation":"指邀請某人參加聚會、用餐、訪問等活動這一行為，也可以泛指對某人的正式或非正式邀請。核心畫面是把門向別人敞開，請對方加入。","examples":[{"en":"We received an invitation to her birthday dinner.","zh":"我們收到了參加她生日晚餐的邀請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thank you for the invitation, but I cannot come.","zh":"謝謝你的邀請，但我不能來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42293555013a99bc","term":"invitation","forms":["invitation","invitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"請帖；邀請函；邀請資訊","explanation":"指把邀請內容傳達給別人的東西或話語，例如請帖、邀請函、電子邀請或口頭通知。它是“敞開的門”留下來的具體形式。","examples":[{"en":"She sent us an invitation to the opening ceremony.","zh":"她給我們發了一份開幕式邀請函。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The invitation lists the address and starting time.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5014f9af3a684fdd64a7","word":"invite","forms":["invite"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37ed00ff77939fc4","term":"invite","forms":["invite","invites","inviting","invited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"邀請參加","explanation":"請某人到某處，或請某人參加某項活動；這是 invite 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We invited our neighbors to dinner on Saturday.","zh":"我們邀請鄰居星期六來吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She invited me to join the team.","zh":"她邀請我加入這個團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6477b7c51a2248c31e90","word":"involve(ment)","forms":["involve","involvement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-714bd12bba5cda53","term":"involve","forms":["involve","involves","involving","involved","involvest","involvedst","involveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包括；涉及內容","explanation":"某件工作、活動或情況把某項內容作為其中的一部分，也就是“包含某項內容”。","examples":[{"en":"The project involves careful planning and regular testing.","zh":"這個專案包括周密的計劃和定期測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her new role involves working with children.","zh":"她的新職務包括和孩子們一起工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92daecddc2a27f65","term":"involve","forms":["involve","involves","involving","involved","involvest","involvedst","involveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使參與；使捲入","explanation":"讓某人或某物與一項活動、事件或情況發生聯絡，尤其是讓某人參加其中。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher involved the students in planning the class trip.","zh":"老師讓學生參與策劃班級旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Volunteering involved me in many local projects.","zh":"做志願者使我參與了許多當地專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2e7df22a3dd8368","term":"involvement","forms":["involvement","involvements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參與；投入","explanation":"指參與某項活動、事務或領域，或處於這種參與狀態；重點是一個人已經投入其中，而不是隻在旁邊觀看。","examples":[{"en":"Her involvement in the local library has grown steadily over the past year.","zh":"過去一年裡，她對當地圖書館工作的參與逐漸加深。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project succeeded because of the strong involvement of the whole team.","zh":"這個專案之所以成功，是因為整個團隊都積極參與。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involvement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04e9c0db87e7eebbf812","word":"iron","forms":["iron"],"officialPos":"n./v./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d2e738c120b63d3","term":"iron","forms":["iron"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鐵製的","explanation":"指物品由鐵這種金屬製成，例如鐵門、鐵架等。","examples":[{"en":"The old bridge has an iron railing.","zh":"這座舊橋有鐵製欄杆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An iron gate protected the entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5f938e9e3413c7f","term":"iron","forms":["iron"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅強堅定的","explanation":"把鐵的堅硬和不易彎曲引申到人的意志或性格，表示非常堅定、堅強。","examples":[{"en":"She showed iron discipline during the difficult training.","zh":"在艱苦訓練中，她表現出了鋼鐵般的自律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She maintained iron discipline throughout the long campaign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85a0a1c48fe4df20","term":"iron","forms":["iron","irons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵","explanation":"一種銀灰色、容易生鏽並會被磁鐵吸引的金屬，也是鍊鋼的重要材料。","examples":[{"en":"Iron is widely used to make steel.","zh":"鐵被廣泛用於鍊鋼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gate is made of iron.","zh":"這扇門是鐵製的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-491936170bb99c0e","term":"iron","forms":["iron","irons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熨斗","explanation":"指用來加熱並壓平衣物褶皺的電器或工具。","examples":[{"en":"I left the iron on the ironing board.","zh":"我把熨斗放在熨衣板上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unplug the iron before filling its water tank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a4f61ba28b799f8","term":"iron","forms":["iron","irons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅強、力量","explanation":"借鐵堅硬耐用的形象，表示強大的力量、堅韌性或非常堅強的品質。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team showed an iron determination.","zh":"救援隊表現出了鋼鐵般的決心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was iron in her voice when she refused.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e99b39556821b72","term":"iron","forms":["iron","irons","ironing","ironed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"熨平","explanation":"用熨斗在衣服或布料上壓過，去掉褶皺。","examples":[{"en":"Please iron this shirt before dinner.","zh":"請在晚飯前把這件襯衫熨平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ironed the curtains while they were still damp.","zh":"窗簾還沒完全乾時，她把它們熨平了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d8dc711aa796d4af8ba","word":"ironic","forms":["ironic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1db11d716ee2364a","term":"ironic","forms":["ironic","more ironic","most ironic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"反諷的；具有出人意料反差的","explanation":"指事情的實際結果與通常預期形成有意味的反差，因而顯得反諷。例如，在本應倡導環保的日子裡卻出現嚴重霧霾，這種反差就是 ironic。","examples":[{"en":"It was ironic that the environmental conference was held during a record heat wave.","zh":"環保會議恰好在創紀錄的熱浪期間舉行，這很有反諷意味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firefighter's house burning down was deeply ironic.","zh":"消防員自己的房子被燒燬，實在是極具反諷意味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ironic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0eabb4c3d95cef90","term":"ironic","forms":["ironic","more ironic","most ironic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"故意戲謔的；不當真的","explanation":"指說話或做事時故意採取不認真、帶玩笑的方式，讓別人不要按字面或當成真正的冒犯來理解。","examples":[{"en":"Don't worry about her comment—she was just being ironic.","zh":"別在意她那句話——她只是在故意開玩笑，並不是認真的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His ironic bow made the children laugh.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ironic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e10bb5d3b091d32bb91a","word":"irony","forms":["irony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc969fcc8b53fa3d","term":"irony","forms":["irony","ironies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反話；反諷","explanation":"說話表面上表達一種意思，實際卻借語境讓人理解成另一種、甚至相反的意思，常帶有幽默或批評意味。例如嘴上稱讚一個明顯做得很糟的人，真正意圖可能是在諷刺。","examples":[{"en":"Calling the broken printer a model of efficiency was pure irony.","zh":"把那臺壞掉的印表機稱為效率典範，純粹是在反諷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used irony to criticize the company without naming it directly.","zh":"她用反諷批評那家公司，卻沒有直接點名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab4940a945f34431","term":"irony","forms":["irony","ironies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反常意味；表面與實際的矛盾","explanation":"指一種值得注意的反差：某個地方、制度或情況表面上代表某種東西，實際卻不符合人們對它的期待。這裡不一定有人故意說反話，而是現實本身形成了諷刺意味。","examples":[{"en":"There is an irony in the fact that the quietest street has the most traffic signs.","zh":"最安靜的街道反而有最多的交通標誌，這件事頗有反諷意味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The irony of a fire station burning down escaped nobody.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f55cd5699ebc2767851","word":"irritable","forms":["irritable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ca88e9f965ebcf68","term":"irritable","forms":["irritable","more irritable","most irritable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易受刺激的","explanation":"它表示某人、某個身體部位或事物很容易被碰到、影響或刺激，從而產生不適或反應；“容易煩躁”這一常見含義就是這個核心概念在人身上的表現。","examples":[{"en":"After the illness, his stomach became irritable.","zh":"生病後，他的胃變得很容易受到刺激。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rash left her skin irritable and sensitive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irritable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d2087748bb2f656","term":"irritable","forms":["irritable","more irritable","most irritable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易怒的；煩躁的","explanation":"形容人一點小事就容易不高興、發火或感到厭煩，強調這個人像繃緊的弦一樣很容易被惹惱。","examples":[{"en":"He gets irritable when he has not slept well.","zh":"他睡不好時就容易煩躁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The irritable customer complained about every small delay.","zh":"那個脾氣暴躁的顧客對每一點小延誤都抱怨不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irritable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2588a942de826f3f7bb","word":"irritate","forms":["irritate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-542925a18c8c1a03","term":"irritate","forms":["irritate","irritates","irritating","irritated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"惹惱；使煩躁","explanation":"指某人的行為、聲音或情況不斷刺激情緒，使人感到不耐煩、惱怒或不高興。核心畫面是“碰到了情緒上的敏感點”。","examples":[{"en":"The constant noise irritates my neighbors.","zh":"持續不斷的噪音讓我的鄰居們很煩躁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It irritates me when people interrupt.","zh":"別人插話時，我會覺得很惱火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irritate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4646b3f5bced205","term":"irritate","forms":["irritate","irritates","irritating","irritated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刺激而引起疼痛或不適","explanation":"指某種物質、摩擦或環境因素刺激身體的某個部位，使它疼痛、發癢或不舒服。這裡不是刺激情緒，而是刺激身體這個“敏感點”。","examples":[{"en":"This soap irritates my skin.","zh":"這種肥皂會刺激我的皮膚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Smoke irritates the eyes and throat.","zh":"煙會刺激眼睛和喉嚨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irritate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28cd2c5c15d13978a6bc","word":"island","forms":["island"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc270442b7b48017","term":"island","forms":["island","islands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"島嶼","explanation":"指四面被水包圍、面積小於大陸的一片連續陸地。它可以位于海洋、湖泊或河流中，是 island 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"They spent a week on a small island in the Mediterranean.","zh":"他們在地中海的一座小島上待了一個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island is famous for its white beaches.","zh":"這座島以白色沙灘聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36b9faea09a43eee","term":"island","forms":["island","islands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孤立的一塊","explanation":"借用“島嶼被周圍水域隔開”的形象，指在一片完全不同的環境中獨立存在的人、地方或狀態，例如喧鬧中的一小塊寧靜。","examples":[{"en":"The quiet garden was an island of peace in the crowded city.","zh":"這座安靜的花園是擁擠城市中的一片寧靜之地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt like an island of calm during the crisis.","zh":"危機期間，她彷彿成了鎮定自持的一方孤島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d937f01b7daf50dce79e","word":"isle","forms":["isle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6deba508a094c793","term":"isle","forms":["isle","isles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小島","explanation":"指通常面積很小、四面環水的島。可以把它想成水面上的一小塊陸地；與更中性的 island 相比，isle 常讓人聯想到文學描寫、地名或較正式的表達。","examples":[{"en":"A small isle appeared beyond the waves.","zh":"海浪的遠處出現了一座小島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They spent the summer on a quiet isle.","zh":"他們在一座寧靜的小島上度過了夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-014aadadffadbb5cd719","word":"isolate","forms":["isolate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9341ff0cae43046d","term":"isolate","forms":["isolate","isolates","isolating","isolated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使分開；隔離","explanation":"把某人、某物或某個問題從其他物件中單獨分出來，使它不再與周圍混在一起。這是 isolate 最基本、最能延伸出其他意思的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The study isolated the main cause of the problem.","zh":"這項研究找出了這個問題的主要原因，並把它單獨區分出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue team isolated the damaged section of the bridge.","zh":"救援隊把橋樑受損的部分隔離開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8080202007116225","term":"isolate","forms":["isolate","isolates","isolating","isolated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使隔離；實行隔離","explanation":"把可能傳播疾病或造成危險的人、動物或區域單獨隔離，避免與其他物件接觸。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital isolated the patient until the test results arrived.","zh":"醫院把這名病人隔離起來，直到檢測結果出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Staff isolated the infected patients in a separate ward.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3624d3181d5c4f8abf2f","word":"isolation","forms":["isolation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9935ce03e6643c29","term":"isolation","forms":["isolation","isolations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孤立；與人隔絕","explanation":"指一個人或群體與其他人分開、缺少接觸，強調一種持續的孤立狀態。它既可以是外界造成的，也可以是當事人主動選擇的。","examples":[{"en":"After moving to the remote island, she began to suffer from isolation.","zh":"搬到那座偏遠的島上後，她開始受到孤立生活的困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent years in isolation and rarely spoke to anyone.","zh":"他多年與世隔絕，很少和任何人說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e10e1d1646374ed","term":"isolation","forms":["isolation","isolations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隔離行為","explanation":"指把人或事物從其他人或事物中分開這一動作，而不是分開之後形成的狀態。可以用於實際隔開，也可以用於抽象地把某個因素單獨處理。","examples":[{"en":"The isolation of the infected animals helped protect the rest of the herd.","zh":"把受感染的動物隔離起來有助於保護畜群中的其他動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Isolation of infected animals prevented further spread.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a502846d070e2088b70","word":"issue","forms":["issue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3cabf0e8758beb7","term":"issue","forms":["issue","issues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問題；爭議點","explanation":"指需要解決、討論或決定的問題、情況或故障；某件事被“向外提出來”後，就成了大家需要處理的事項。","examples":[{"en":"We are having an issue with the online payment system.","zh":"我們的線上支付系統出了點問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee will discuss this issue at its next meeting.","zh":"委員會將在下次會議上討論這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/issue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbe157f338aefc91","term":"issue","forms":["issue","issues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結果；結局","explanation":"指一件事或一連串事件最後得到的結果、結局或後果；事情向外展開後，最終顯現出來的就是它的 issue。","examples":[{"en":"No one could predict the issue of the negotiations.","zh":"沒人能預測談判的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The issue of the election will affect the whole country.","zh":"這次選舉的結果將影響整個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/issue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8eba63260a08fbc","term":"issue","forms":["issue","issues","issuing","issued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"導致；結果是","explanation":"表示某種行動、情況或發展向外展開後，最終產生某個結果；也就是事情“出來”的結局。","examples":[{"en":"Poor planning issued in delays and extra costs.","zh":"計劃不周最終導致了延誤和額外費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The negotiations issued in an agreement acceptable to both sides.","zh":"談判最終達成了一項雙方都能接受的協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/issue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c7df19d9c6e4779","term":"issue","forms":["issue","issues","issuing","issued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"釋出；發行","explanation":"表示政府、銀行、機構或其他有權主體把資訊、檔案、貨幣等正式向外發出或投入流通，正體現了“向外出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The central bank issued new banknotes last month.","zh":"中央銀行上個月發行了新鈔票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school issued a notice about the schedule change.","zh":"學校釋出了關於日程變更的通知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/issue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":3,"counts":{"113":2,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-caa0a2170ba32fe60a50","word":"it (its, itself)","forms":["it"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4281141a4292e67b","term":"it","forms":["it","they","them"],"pos":"pron","zh":"它；這件事","explanation":"it 是把一個非人的物件、抽象概念或非人動物放到句子裡的指代牌，通常指前面已經提到的單數事物。","examples":[{"en":"Take this book and put it on the shelf.","zh":"拿上這本書，把它放到書架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine is old, but it still works well.","zh":"這臺機器很舊，但它仍然運轉良好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/it","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6055a09f672d171c","term":"it","forms":["it","they","them"],"pos":"pron","zh":"無指代的形式主語","explanation":"it 可以不指任何具體物件，只是先佔住主語位置，用於天氣、時間、日期、距離等表達；真正要表達的是後面的情況。","examples":[{"en":"It is nearly ten o’clock.","zh":"快十點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was raining when we left.","zh":"我們離開時正在下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/it","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7cfd9a45042c2c5","term":"it","forms":["it","they","them"],"pos":"pron","zh":"形式主語或形式賓語","explanation":"it 可以先佔住主語或賓語位置，把真正較長的內容放到後面；這個後置內容常是不定式、動名詞或從句。它就像為後面的完整意思預留位置。","examples":[{"en":"It is easy to see why she was upset.","zh":"很容易看出她為什麼不高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I find it difficult to explain the idea clearly.","zh":"我覺得很難把這個想法解釋清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/it","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f668d7185e0fd2ddcfa","word":"itch","forms":["itch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3f254ad056d6b4b","term":"itch","forms":["itch","itches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"癢感","explanation":"指身體某處產生的癢感，讓人想用手抓或摩擦；重點是這種感覺，而不是造成它的皮膚問題。","examples":[{"en":"I have an itch on my back that I can't reach.","zh":"我背上有一處癢，可我夠不著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mosquito bite gave me a terrible itch.","zh":"蚊子叮的地方癢得厲害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/itch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32ad64beb041ee1c","term":"itch","forms":["itch","itches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揮之不去的衝動","explanation":"比喻心裡像有一個不斷催促你的“癢點”，表示持續、煩人而且很想滿足的願望，常指想做某件事或得到某樣東西。","examples":[{"en":"After saving enough money, she had an itch to travel again.","zh":"攢夠錢後，她又按捺不住想去旅行了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By spring, she felt the familiar itch to travel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/itch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-788b06fcb01660c2","term":"itch","forms":["itch","itches","itching","itched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發癢","explanation":"指身體某處感到癢，需要抓或摩擦來緩解；它強調正在產生這種感覺。","examples":[{"en":"My eyes itch whenever the air is dry.","zh":"空氣乾燥時，我的眼睛就會發癢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This wool sweater makes my neck itch.","zh":"這件羊毛衫讓我的脖子發癢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/itch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6dd0532bd6f7297d","term":"itch","forms":["itch","itches","itching","itched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迫切想做","explanation":"表示心裡有一個持續催促自己的衝動，因而非常想做某事；這是由“癢得想抓”發展來的比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"He is itching to show everyone his new invention.","zh":"他迫不及待想把自己的新發明展示給大家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After months at home, I was itching for a change.","zh":"在家待了幾個月後，我渴望有所改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/itch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a33eacd5fa65f2b2e28","word":"item","forms":["item"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5adead91bbf925b4","term":"item","forms":["item","items"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物件；單獨的一件東西","explanation":"指一個可以單獨拿取、辨認或處理的具體物件，是“清單上一格”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please put each item in a separate box.","zh":"請把每件物品分別放進一個盒子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found a useful item at the back of the drawer.","zh":"我在抽屜後面找到了一件有用的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/item","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55fdbfd1904ad8ad","term":"item","forms":["item","items"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賬目或文字中的一項","explanation":"指賬單、清單或正式文字中可以單獨列出的一個條目，因此可以是費用、規定或其他具有獨立意義的內容。","examples":[{"en":"The delivery fee was listed as a separate item on the bill.","zh":"運費在賬單上被列為單獨的一項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final item on the agenda concerns parking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/item","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c679da09e353a34552b7","word":"ivory","forms":["ivory"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3523a2e9ec6b6753","term":"ivory","forms":["ivory"],"pos":"adj","zh":"象牙色的","explanation":"表示顏色像象牙，通常是柔和、偏暖的乳白色。這正是從“象牙這種白色材料”自然發展出的顏色義。","examples":[{"en":"She chose ivory curtains for the bedroom.","zh":"她為臥室選了象牙色的窗簾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The walls were painted ivory to make the room feel warmer.","zh":"牆壁刷成了象牙色，讓房間顯得更溫暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83afe8aa5f1edf2f","term":"ivory","forms":["ivory","ivories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"象牙","explanation":"指大象、海象等動物獠牙中的堅硬白色牙質，是 ivory 最基本的材料義。由這層“堅硬而潔白的材料”又產生了顏色和製品等其他義項。","examples":[{"en":"The old comb was carved from ivory.","zh":"那把舊梳子是用象牙雕刻的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many countries restrict the sale of ivory.","zh":"許多國家限制象牙的銷售。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-daf8988ae45566cb","term":"ivory","forms":["ivory","ivories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"象牙色","explanation":"指像象牙一樣的柔和乳白色，通常比純白更暖一些。它把象牙這種材料最醒目的外觀提取成了顏色名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The bride wore a simple dress in ivory.","zh":"新娘穿了一條簡潔的象牙色禮服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This paint comes in white and ivory.","zh":"這種塗料有白色和象牙色兩種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-254ac4523be56a1a724c","word":"ivy","forms":["ivy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c39620c9fe71475d","term":"ivy","forms":["ivy","ivies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"常春藤","explanation":"ivy通常指常春藤屬的木質攀援或匍匐常綠植物，常沿牆壁、樹幹或地面生長。記住“纏繞並攀附”的畫面，就能掌握這個最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Ivy covered the old stone wall.","zh":"常春藤爬滿了那堵舊石牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener removed the ivy before repairing the roof.","zh":"園丁在修屋頂前清除了常春藤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98d2dedc80c85ba5","term":"ivy","forms":["ivy","ivies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"類似常春藤的藤本植物","explanation":"在較寬泛的用法中，ivy也可以指其他屬中外形或生長方式類似常春藤的植物；核心仍是“攀爬、蔓生、像常春藤”。","examples":[{"en":"This garden has several kinds of ivy growing along the fence.","zh":"這個花園裡有幾種沿著籬笆生長的常春藤類植物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Boston ivy covered the brick wall by autumn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ivy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-554f4d3dafc80844871a","word":"jacket","forms":["jacket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-79613ebc8d2fb3d1","term":"jacket","forms":["jacket","jackets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夾克；短外套","explanation":"穿在襯衫或上衣外面的上身衣物，通常長度到腰部至大腿之間，用來保暖或遮擋。它是 jacket 最常見、最基礎的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Take a jacket—the evening air is getting cold.","zh":"帶件夾克吧，晚上的空氣越來越冷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hung her jacket on the back of the chair.","zh":"她把夾克掛在椅背上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jacket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a4412714ddcac39","term":"jacket","forms":["jacket","jackets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"西裝上衣","explanation":"指一套西裝中穿在上身的那一件，通常和 trousers 一起構成 suit；這裡不一定是日常意義上的休閒夾克。","examples":[{"en":"He wore a dark jacket with matching trousers to the interview.","zh":"他穿著深色西裝上衣和配套的褲子去面試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hung his suit jacket over the back of the chair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jacket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-213442e866fc76f6","term":"jacket","forms":["jacket","jackets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護套；包覆層","explanation":"指包在物體外面的覆蓋層，用來保護物體、隔熱或增強安全性；這個意思仍然保留了“外面套一層”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The tank has an insulating jacket to keep the water hot.","zh":"這個水箱有隔熱包覆層，可以讓水保持溫熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Remove the jacket before replacing the damaged cable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jacket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5db6810e7cf9ff073c27","word":"jade","forms":["jade"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b74bf5123b04459","term":"jade","forms":["jade","jades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玉石","explanation":"指可用於製作飾品或雕刻品的玉石，通常是綠色或白色；這裡說的是材料本身，而不是玉石的顏色。","examples":[{"en":"The pendant is carved from a single piece of jade.","zh":"這枚吊墜由一整塊玉石雕刻而成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave her mother a jade bracelet.","zh":"她送給母親一隻玉手鐲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d72fa8065e24a58a3c5","word":"jail","forms":["jail"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd0b7b37014a8e42","term":"jail","forms":["jail","jails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監獄；拘留所","explanation":"指依法關押不願自行離開的人或等待司法處理的機構、場所，尤其常指關押輕罪犯人或等待審判人員的地方。","examples":[{"en":"He was sent to jail for stealing a car.","zh":"他因偷車被送進了監獄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is waiting in jail for her trial.","zh":"她正在拘留所裡等待審判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd8080a3a25d140d","term":"jail","forms":["jail","jails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監禁；坐牢","explanation":"指人被關在jail裡的處境或懲罰本身，不強調關押地點，而強調失去自由的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"A short jail sentence would be better than a large fine.","zh":"短期監禁可能比高額罰款更合適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent six months in jail for fraud.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4991fcb10db66792","term":"jail","forms":["jail","jails","jailing","jailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"關進監獄；監禁","explanation":"指依法剝奪某人的自由，把這個人關進jail；它就是名詞“監獄、拘禁”這一核心畫面的動作化表達。","examples":[{"en":"The court jailed him for three years.","zh":"法院判處他三年監禁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several protesters were jailed after the demonstration.","zh":"示威活動後，幾名抗議者被關進了監獄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7152e6ec048e24fadb10","word":"jam","forms":["jam"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f8a09357c141d7a","term":"jam","forms":["jam","jams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"果醬","explanation":"水果加糖熬煮並濃縮成的甜稠食品，通常抹在麵包或吐司上，也可用於甜點。它和“擠在一起”的主線不同，是由水果熬煮、濃縮形成的另一條常用記憶支線。","examples":[{"en":"I spread strawberry jam on my toast every morning.","zh":"我每天早上都在吐司上抹草莓果醬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought a jar of homemade jam at the market.","zh":"我們在市場上買了一罐自制果醬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-885775f7398926d6","term":"jam","forms":["jam","jams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堵塞；擁堵","explanation":"指車輛、道路、人群或其他事物擠在一起，造成通行受阻或無法移動。交通擁堵是最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"A truck overturned and caused a huge traffic jam.","zh":"一輛卡車翻倒了，造成了嚴重的交通擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We left early to avoid the morning jam.","zh":"我們很早就出發了，以避開早高峰擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fbec3beace7cf2e","term":"jam","forms":["jam","jams","jamming","jammed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"硬塞","explanation":"指用力把某物擠進並不寬敞的空間，常常帶有粗暴、勉強塞入的感覺，正像把東西硬擠進去。","examples":[{"en":"He jammed the wet towels into the small suitcase.","zh":"他把溼毛巾硬塞進小行李箱裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She jammed a piece of cardboard into the broken window.","zh":"她把一塊硬紙板硬塞進破窗戶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e903caeacd464f1a","term":"jam","forms":["jam","jams","jamming","jammed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"即興合奏","explanation":"指音樂人不按完整預先排練的安排，尤其是多人在一起即興演奏；許多人和聲音擠在一起合作，形成了音樂上的即興活動。","examples":[{"en":"After dinner, the musicians jammed together in the living room.","zh":"晚飯後，音樂家們在客廳裡一起即興合奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She often jams with her brother on weekends.","zh":"她週末經常和哥哥一起即興演奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5dbcd1efbd0acbc0ae60","word":"janitor","forms":["janitor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65b1b64e3ffc3ae7","term":"janitor","forms":["janitor","janitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築清潔和維護人員","explanation":"指在學校、辦公樓等公共建築中負責打掃、簡單維修和日常照看的人。可以把他想成守著建築、讓建築正常運轉的人，這是 janitor 最核心、最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"The school janitor fixed the broken door before classes started.","zh":"學校的維修清潔人員在上課前修好了壞掉的門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She got a job as a janitor at a large office building.","zh":"她在一棟大型辦公樓找到了一份清潔維護人員的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/janitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb7ec255b7a02514","term":"janitor","forms":["janitor","janitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築看護和清潔人員","explanation":"同樣指負責公共建築清潔、維修和日常照看的人；這個義項主要反映部分地區的英語用法，與 s1 的核心概念基本相同。區別主要在使用地區，而不是工作內容。","examples":[{"en":"Please tell the janitor that the lights in the hallway are out.","zh":"請告訴負責大樓維護的人，走廊裡的燈壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The janitor unlocked the school before sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/janitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0163f1eea78943500606","word":"jar","forms":["jar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c65531907a44682","term":"jar","forms":["jar","jars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"罐子；罈子","explanation":"一種通常用玻璃或陶土製成的容器，用來裝水、油、酒、食物等；古義也可指較大的陶製容器或墓葬用的罐。","examples":[{"en":"She kept the homemade jam in a glass jar.","zh":"她把自制果醬放在一個玻璃罐裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pass me the jar of honey.","zh":"請把那罐蜂蜜遞給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d1c5859550824d403d8","word":"jasmine","forms":["jasmine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee66c5bd10706c57","term":"jasmine","forms":["jasmine","jasmines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"茉莉；茉莉花","explanation":"指一類通常開白色或黃色花、並散發濃郁香味的植物，最常見的理解就是茉莉花。這裡的 jasmine 是花或植物本身，不是單指香水。","examples":[{"en":"The jasmine flowers filled the garden with a sweet fragrance.","zh":"茉莉花讓整個花園充滿了甜美的香氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She planted jasmine beside the bedroom window.","zh":"她在臥室窗邊種了茉莉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jasmine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64cbc339112de01a","term":"jasmine","forms":["jasmine","jasmines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"茉莉香水；茉莉香味","explanation":"指從茉莉花中取得的香水或香味，重點從植物本身轉到了它所提供的香氣。","examples":[{"en":"This perfume has a delicate jasmine scent.","zh":"這款香水帶有淡雅的茉莉香味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A trace of jasmine lingered after she left.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jasmine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f695e71ab38157263ecb","word":"jaw","forms":["jaw"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ace4850741751dac","term":"jaw","forms":["jaw","jaws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頜骨","explanation":"指構成口腔框架、通常長著牙齒的上頜或下頜骨，是“嘴”這個核心形象的骨架。","examples":[{"en":"The dentist said that the bone in her lower jaw had healed well.","zh":"牙醫說她的下頜骨已經癒合得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He broke his jaw in a cycling accident.","zh":"他在一次騎車事故中摔斷了頜骨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95848da5c19eb88a","term":"jaw","forms":["jaw","jaws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下巴；嘴下方的臉部","explanation":"指嘴下面、臉的下半部，偏向外表可見的部位，而不是內部的骨頭。","examples":[{"en":"She rested her chin on her hand and rubbed her aching jaw.","zh":"她把下巴擱在手上，揉著疼痛的頜部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His jaw dropped when he saw the final bill.","zh":"他看到最後的賬單時驚得目瞪口呆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d89a7053d2804a5","term":"jaw","forms":["jaw","jaws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"像嘴一樣的入口或包圍處","explanation":"把動物張開的嘴這個形象移到別處，指兩側張開、彷彿要吞入或包圍東西的入口、峽口或危險處，通常用複數。","examples":[{"en":"The narrow road disappeared into the jaws of the canyon.","zh":"那條狹窄的道路消失在峽谷的入口處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They escaped from the jaws of death.","zh":"他們從死亡的魔爪中逃了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c301f75ab52fa076c827","word":"jazz","forms":["jazz"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5632894e2b7d1d51","term":"jazz","forms":["jazz","jazzes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爵士樂","explanation":"jazz是一種重視即興、節奏變化和樂手互動的音樂型別，源於西非音樂傳統與非裔美國人布魯斯傳統，並不斷吸收其他音樂元素。","examples":[{"en":"She listens to jazz while she works.","zh":"她工作時聽爵士樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band played jazz until midnight.","zh":"樂隊演奏爵士樂一直演到午夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jazz","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2f5e2e21758c5c25bdc","word":"jealous","forms":["jealous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41acea242d8c61dd","term":"jealous","forms":["jealous","jealouser","more jealous","jealousest","most jealous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"吃醋；懷疑伴侶變心","explanation":"指擔心自己在伴侶心中的位置被別人取代，因此對伴侶與他人的關係感到不安、懷疑或不滿。","examples":[{"en":"She gave him a jealous look when he started talking to his ex.","zh":"他開始和前任說話時，她吃醋地看了他一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm not jealous, but I do want to know who keeps texting you.","zh":"我不是在吃醋，只是想知道一直給你發簡訊的人是誰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01bbf3a4b71d2b90","term":"jealous","forms":["jealous","jealouser","more jealous","jealousest","most jealous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嫉妒；眼紅","explanation":"因為別人擁有自己想要的成功、機會或物質優勢而感到不滿，甚至希望對方失去這種優勢。它和戀愛中的吃醋有關，都是害怕自己在比較中失去位置。","examples":[{"en":"He was jealous of his friend’s success and stopped inviting him out.","zh":"他嫉妒朋友的成功，後來不再邀請朋友一起出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be jealous of her new job; you can apply for similar positions too.","zh":"別嫉妒她的新工作，你也可以申請類似的職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a245672087ced1cdb19","word":"jealousy","forms":["jealousy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0fefc9877edc1322","term":"jealousy","forms":["jealousy","jealousies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嫉妒；吃醋；猜忌","explanation":"指因為擔心自己失去他人的愛、關注、地位或某種優勢而產生的強烈不安和嫉妒。它可以發生在戀愛關係中，也可以發生在朋友、同事或群體之間。","examples":[{"en":"Her jealousy grew when her partner started spending more time with a coworker.","zh":"伴侶開始更多地和一位同事相處後，她的嫉妒和不安越來越強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager's praise of one employee aroused jealousy among the others.","zh":"經理對一名員工的表揚引起了其他人的嫉妒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealousy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3eb874ba01490ab92db6","word":"jeans","forms":["jeans"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f976ad5d584559a","term":"jeans","forms":["jeans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牛仔褲","explanation":"指用牛仔布製成的長褲，通常呈藍色，但也可以有其他顏色；英語裡通常把整條褲子作為 jeans 來說，形成固定的複數形式。","examples":[{"en":"I wear jeans to work on Fridays.","zh":"我星期五穿牛仔褲上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She patched the knees of her favorite jeans.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jeans","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d254fa846ea7252ec95b","word":"jeep","forms":["jeep"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-676e5fe5623c38e9","term":"jeep","forms":["jeep","Jeeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吉普車；越野車","explanation":"指一種適合泥地、山路等崎嶇地形的車輛，通常讓人聯想到四輪驅動的吉普車。","examples":[{"en":"They rented a Jeep to explore the mountain roads.","zh":"他們租了一輛吉普車去探索山路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our Jeep handled the muddy trail surprisingly well.","zh":"我們的吉普車在泥濘的小路上行駛得出奇地好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jeep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04a43181b13a2381","term":"jeep","forms":["jeep","jeeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小型軍用越野車","explanation":"指一種外形較方正、配有四輪驅動、適合崎嶇地形的小型軍用風格車輛；這是 Jeep 這一詞形的核心車輛概念。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers loaded their supplies into a small jeep.","zh":"士兵們把補給裝進了一輛小型越野車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A jeep carried us across the rocky ground.","zh":"一輛越野車載著我們穿過了崎嶇的地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jeep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67b4154851853fc0","term":"jeep","forms":["jeep","jeeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"越野型多用途車","explanation":"在品牌名稱泛化後，也可泛指運動型多用途車或其他相似的四輪驅動車，重點仍是能夠應對較差路況。","examples":[{"en":"We took a jeep along the unpaved coastal road.","zh":"我們開著一輛越野車沿著未鋪路面的海岸公路行駛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jeep carried supplies along the rocky track.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jeep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22d8ec27fc129158128c","word":"jelly","forms":["jelly"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9db33c767ec1f29","term":"jelly","forms":["jelly","jellies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"果凍","explanation":"用明膠或植物凝固劑、糖和調味料製成的凝固甜點，質地柔軟而有彈性，通常作為甜品食用。","examples":[{"en":"We had jelly and ice cream for dessert.","zh":"我們甜點吃了果凍和冰淇淋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children ate raspberry jelly with ice cream.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jelly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a64f46febefb8eca968e","word":"jet","forms":["jet"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68074496094b87c7","term":"jet","forms":["jet","jets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噴流；噴出的一股液體或氣體","explanation":"指受壓力推動、從容器、發動機或地面噴口中高速噴出的一股液體或氣體。核心畫面就是“集中成束地噴出去”。","examples":[{"en":"A jet of water shot from the broken pipe.","zh":"一股水流從破裂的管道里噴了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Steam jets rose from the cracks in the ground.","zh":"蒸汽流從地面的裂縫中噴湧而出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3def60643689aea2","term":"jet","forms":["jet","jets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噴氣式飛機","explanation":"指用噴氣發動機而不是螺旋槳推進的飛機，是“噴流”這一核心概念在航空中的應用。","examples":[{"en":"We flew there on a private jet.","zh":"我們乘坐私人噴氣式飛機飛到了那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jet landed safely despite the strong winds.","zh":"儘管風很大，那架噴氣式飛機還是安全降落了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0810ade5e250d89c","term":"jet","forms":["jet","jets","jetting","jetted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"噴出","explanation":"指液體或氣體從容器、管道等處形成一股噴流衝出來，是名詞“噴流”的動作形式。","examples":[{"en":"Water jetted out of the cracked hose.","zh":"水從裂開的軟管裡噴了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Steam jetted from the machine.","zh":"蒸汽從機器裡噴了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ddc6af1a32422cb2d518","word":"jewel","forms":["jewel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5912c191887de183","term":"jewel","forms":["jewel","jewels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寶石","explanation":"指有價值、可切割和打磨的寶石或半寶石，例如鑽石、紅寶石等。這裡強調的是石頭本身，不一定已經制成首飾。","examples":[{"en":"A small blue jewel was set in the center of the ring.","zh":"戒指中央鑲著一顆小小的藍色寶石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displays jewels from several ancient cultures.","zh":"這家博物館展出了幾個古代文明的寶石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jewel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e311c7c6e0d4c978","term":"jewel","forms":["jewel","jewels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珍寶；珍貴的人或事物","explanation":"比喻某個人、地方或事物極其珍貴、出色，像值得珍藏的寶石一樣。它既可以說具體的地方或物品，也可以稱讚某個人。","examples":[{"en":"The old library is the jewel of the university.","zh":"那座老圖書館是這所大學的瑰寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone on the team considers Maya a real jewel.","zh":"團隊裡的每個人都認為瑪雅是個真正的寶貝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jewel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d68ebe3c27c836bfffdd","word":"jewelry","forms":["jewelry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55c5a2c51d053408","term":"jewelry","forms":["jewelry","jewelries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珠寶；首飾","explanation":"指用金、銀、寶石等製成、佩戴在身上的裝飾品，也可以泛指首飾這一類物品。這裡的 jewelry 是美國英語拼寫，對應英國英語的 jewellery。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps her jewelry in a small wooden box.","zh":"她把首飾放在一個小木盒裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave his mother a beautiful piece of jewelry.","zh":"他送給母親一件漂亮的首飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jewelry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":3,"counts":{"111":2,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-ed121aec34f231b951ac","word":"jingle","forms":["jingle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b07745903ae4db6","term":"jingle","forms":["jingle","jingles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"叮噹聲","explanation":"指金屬或玻璃相互碰撞時發出的清脆、連續的聲音，比如鑰匙、硬幣或玻璃片碰撞的聲音。","examples":[{"en":"I heard the jingle of keys outside the door.","zh":"我聽見門外傳來鑰匙的叮噹聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jingle of coins in his pocket grew louder as he ran.","zh":"他跑起來時，口袋裡硬幣的叮噹聲越來越響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jingle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c5d570058e1a775","term":"jingle","forms":["jingle","jingles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣告短歌","explanation":"指廣告中為了讓人記住商品或服務而反覆播放的簡短歌曲或旋律，通常歌詞很簡單、很上口。","examples":[{"en":"That catchy jingle made the company’s phone number easy to remember.","zh":"那段上口的廣告短歌讓人很容易記住公司的電話號碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new cereal commercial has a jingle that children sing at school.","zh":"新麥片廣告裡的短歌孩子們在學校都會唱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jingle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a689182a08a6b4d6","term":"jingle","forms":["jingle","jingles","jingling","jingled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出叮噹聲","explanation":"指鑰匙、珠子、硬幣等物體相互碰撞，自己發出清脆的叮噹聲。","examples":[{"en":"The beads jingled as she walked down the stairs.","zh":"她走下樓梯時，珠子發出叮噹聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bells jingled softly in the wind.","zh":"鈴鐺在風中輕輕作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jingle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e8c9902207afaeb7120","word":"job","forms":["job"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3dbf4188fc4b0fe","term":"job","forms":["job","jobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"任務；要做的事","explanation":"job 可以是一件交給某人完成的具體任務，不一定是有薪工作。它把“要處理的一件事”這個核心概念直接表現出來。","examples":[{"en":"I've got a job for you: could you wash the dishes?","zh":"我有件事要你做：你能洗洗碗嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cleaning the garage was a bigger job than I expected.","zh":"清理車庫比我想象的任務量大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/job","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3f30e18bb839203","term":"job","forms":["job","jobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業；有薪工作","explanation":"job 也指一個人透過勞動獲得報酬的職位或職業，是日常英語中“工作”的常用說法。","examples":[{"en":"She found a job at a small design company.","zh":"她在一家小型設計公司找到了一份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His job requires him to travel every week.","zh":"他的工作要求他每週出差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/job","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60f51d969903e3d8f143","word":"jockey","forms":["jockey"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32a9469e0cfeacb9","term":"jockey","forms":["jockey","jockeys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賽馬騎手","explanation":"指參加賽馬比賽、騎著賽馬競技的人，是 jockey 最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The young jockey won the final race.","zh":"那名年輕的賽馬騎手贏得了最後一場比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jockey fell from the horse near the finish line.","zh":"那名騎手在終點線附近從馬上摔了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jockey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-994424cf2fdb5a75","term":"jockey","forms":["jockey","jockeys","jockeying","jockeyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"騎馬參賽","explanation":"指騎著馬參加賽馬比賽，和名詞“賽馬騎手”直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"She jockeyed professionally for ten years.","zh":"她做了十年的職業賽馬騎手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She jockeyed professionally before becoming a trainer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jockey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22e62e97fb3a821a","term":"jockey","forms":["jockey","jockeys","jockeying","jockeyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"靈活周旋以謀利","explanation":"比喻像騎手操控坐騎一樣，憑技巧調整局面、爭取有利位置或結果，常含有競爭和為自己謀利的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Several companies are jockeying for control of the market.","zh":"幾家公司正在爭奪市場控制權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The candidates jockeyed for a place on the committee.","zh":"候選人們競相爭取委員會中的一個席位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jockey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c30b983b5860e0481288","word":"jog","forms":["jog"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71d144cef00f711e","term":"jog","forms":["jog","jogs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慢跑","explanation":"指速度介於走路和正式跑步之間、通常為了鍛鍊而進行的輕鬆跑動，可以把它想成身體有節奏地上下顛動著向前。","examples":[{"en":"I go for a jog around the lake every Saturday morning.","zh":"我每週六早上都繞湖慢跑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He jogs around the park before breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7e6f93fa2a729c7","term":"jog","forms":["jog","jogs","jogging","jogged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喚起；激起","explanation":"指用一個提示、問題或刺激把沉睡的記憶、興趣或情緒輕輕“推醒”，最常見的是幫助某人想起忘記的事情。","examples":[{"en":"That old photograph jogged my memory about our first trip.","zh":"那張舊照片使我想起了我們第一次旅行的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A quick look at the notes should jog her memory.","zh":"快速看一眼筆記應該能幫助她想起那件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29c26ceb5054b763","term":"jog","forms":["jog","jogs","jogging","jogged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"慢跑","explanation":"指以介於走路和跑步之間的輕鬆速度跑動，通常是為了鍛鍊或休閒，正是身體反覆輕微顛動著向前的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"He jogs in the park before work three times a week.","zh":"他每週上班前在公園慢跑三次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They jogged along the beach as the sun came up.","zh":"太陽昇起時，他們沿著海灘慢跑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58393216032be6257784","word":"join","forms":["join"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-043c5980aeafe806","term":"join","forms":["join","joins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連線處；連線","explanation":"指把兩個部分接在一起的動作，或接好後形成的連線處。它可以是實際物體的接縫，也可以泛指兩個部分之間的連線。","examples":[{"en":"The join between the two pieces of wood is barely visible.","zh":"兩塊木頭之間的接縫幾乎看不出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water began leaking at the join where the new pipe met the old one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/join","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-921461c8446d337a","term":"join","forms":["join","joins","joining","joined","joinest","joinedst","joineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連線；接合","explanation":"把兩個或多個東西接在一起，使它們成為一個整體。這是 join 最基礎的畫面，也能延伸到把資訊、系統或計劃接起來。","examples":[{"en":"Join the two pieces of paper with a strip of tape.","zh":"用一條膠帶把這兩張紙粘在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge joins the two sides of the river.","zh":"這座橋連線著河的兩岸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/join","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e07e20ae4536a81","term":"join","forms":["join","joins","joining","joined","joinest","joinedst","joineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加入；聯合","explanation":"從“站到一起”引申為加入某個群體，和別人為了共同目標聯合起來。重點是一起成為一個行動整體。","examples":[{"en":"Several small groups joined together to protect the local park.","zh":"幾個小團體聯合起來保護當地公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined with her neighbors to raise money for the shelter.","zh":"她和鄰居們聯合起來為收容所籌款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/join","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34d1602264805752","term":"join","forms":["join","joins","joining","joined","joinest","joinedst","joineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成為成員；加入組織","explanation":"表示正式進入俱樂部、團隊、機構或其他群體，成為其中的一員。這是“走進一個群體並和它連在一起”的常用延伸。","examples":[{"en":"He joined the school basketball team last year.","zh":"他去年加入了學校籃球隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He joined the local rowing club last autumn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/join","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0a613ed6eebe40f33ab","word":"joint","forms":["joint"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa367e23f162864a","term":"joint","forms":["joint"],"pos":"adj","zh":"共同的；聯合的","explanation":"表示兩個或更多人、團體或機構一起做某事，而不是由其中一方單獨完成。它延續了“連線在一起”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The two universities launched a joint research project.","zh":"這兩所大學啟動了一個聯合研究專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They opened a joint account for household expenses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2967420021193864","term":"joint","forms":["joint","joints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關節","explanation":"指動物身體中兩塊骨頭或外骨骼相接的部位，通常可以讓身體彎曲或伸直。它是最常見、最容易聯想到的“連線處”之一。","examples":[{"en":"My knee joint hurts after the long hike.","zh":"長途徒步後我的膝關節很疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise helps keep your joints flexible.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於保持關節靈活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2fa4cfad054c30de64a","word":"joke","forms":["joke"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48926596b05b13c6","term":"joke","forms":["joke","jokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"笑話","explanation":"指一個為了逗人發笑而講出的故事、說法或機智的話，通常有鋪墊和笑點。","examples":[{"en":"She told a funny joke at dinner.","zh":"她在晚餐時講了一個有趣的笑話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I know a joke that will make you laugh.","zh":"我知道一個能把你逗笑的笑話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ff59fe1b2c81d3b","term":"joke","forms":["joke","jokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玩笑；不是認真的話或事","explanation":"指為了逗樂而說或做的事，並不打算讓別人按字面或嚴肅的方式理解。","examples":[{"en":"Don't be angry—I was only joking.","zh":"別生氣，我只是開個玩笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He played a harmless joke on his brother.","zh":"他和弟弟開了一個無傷大雅的玩笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4dca60e54f17077","term":"joke","forms":["joke","jokes","joking","joked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開玩笑；並非認真地說或做","explanation":"指為了逗樂而說話或做事，所表達的內容不應被當成嚴肅的真實意思。","examples":[{"en":"I was joking when I said I would quit.","zh":"我說要辭職時是在開玩笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you joking, or do you really mean it?","zh":"你是在開玩笑，還是確實是這個意思？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9780d47478787498c88","word":"jolly","forms":["jolly"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bbfac2171803c713","term":"jolly","forms":["jolly","jollier","jolliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"快活的；興高采烈的","explanation":"形容一個人情緒高漲、愛笑愛玩，或整體氣氛充滿歡樂；這是 jolly 最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Our jolly host kept everyone laughing all evening.","zh":"我們那位興致勃勃的主人讓大家笑了一晚上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children came back from the party in a jolly mood.","zh":"孩子們參加聚會回來時心情特別愉快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jolly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ad162a7e2408495","term":"jolly","forms":["jolly","jollier","jolliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很棒的；令人愉快的","explanation":"形容某件事、某個地方或某種體驗讓人覺得很好、很舒服，帶有“真不錯”的輕鬆語氣。","examples":[{"en":"We had a jolly good time at the seaside.","zh":"我們在海邊玩得非常開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a jolly evening playing cards.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jolly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81dd6b775afcccb6dbb8","word":"journal","forms":["journal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c9e4f2423752793","term":"journal","forms":["journal","journals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日記；日誌","explanation":"指個人、組織、船隻等按時間順序寫下的日常記錄。重點不在文學形式，而在持續記錄每天發生的事情，因此既可以是個人日記，也可以是工作日誌。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps a journal of her travels.","zh":"她記錄旅行日記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain checked the ship's journal before leaving port.","zh":"船長離港前查閱了航海日誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b61549231b447d0f","term":"journal","forms":["journal","journals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"期刊；專業雜誌","explanation":"指圍繞某一學科或主題定期出版的報刊，尤其常指學術期刊。它是把許多人的研究或文章按期整理出來公開發行的“記錄冊”。","examples":[{"en":"The university library subscribes to several medical journals.","zh":"這所大學圖書館訂閱了幾種醫學期刊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study appeared in a respected medical journal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-683eb347788051362646","word":"journalism","forms":["journalism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9dc98863dcb2c79d","term":"journalism","forms":["journalism","journalisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新聞業；新聞報道工作","explanation":"指為了讓公眾瞭解事實或事件，把新聞收集、核實、撰寫、編輯並透過報紙、廣播、電視或網路等渠道傳播出去的整套工作，也指從事這項工作的行業和專業領域。","examples":[{"en":"She studied journalism before joining a local newspaper.","zh":"她先學習了新聞專業，後來加入了一家地方報紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good journalism helps people understand what is happening in their community.","zh":"優秀的新聞報道能幫助人們瞭解社群里正在發生的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journalism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-563773f188ec7d279331","word":"journalist","forms":["journalist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6efbb495d30d9d9","term":"journalist","forms":["journalist","journalists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新聞記者","explanation":"指以採訪、核實並報道新聞和時事為職業的記者。這是現代最常見的意義：把現實中的事件寫下來並傳播給公眾。","examples":[{"en":"The journalist interviewed several witnesses at the scene.","zh":"那名記者在現場採訪了幾位目擊者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A journalist traveled with the expedition to report its discoveries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journalist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d99381f112ae386c","term":"journalist","forms":["journalist","journalists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新聞工作者","explanation":"指以新聞寫作或新聞報道為職業的人，最初尤其指為印刷媒體寫新聞的人。這個意義把“記錄自己的生活”擴充套件成了“為公眾記錄現實”。","examples":[{"en":"She worked as a journalist for a local newspaper after college.","zh":"大學畢業後，她在一家地方報紙當新聞工作者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The journalist interviewed residents affected by the closure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journalist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cde56892bbebbf6c5fe5","word":"journey","forms":["journey"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60c241d7c5a61075","term":"journey","forms":["journey","journeys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段旅行","explanation":"journey指被看作一個完整單位的一段旅行，通常有明確的起點和終點，可以乘火車、汽車或其他交通工具完成。","examples":[{"en":"The journey to London takes two hours by train.","zh":"坐火車去倫敦的旅程需要兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a long journey home after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，我們回家走了很長一段路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44b7ddb52e523ec6","term":"journey","forms":["journey","journeys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展歷程","explanation":"這裡把現實中的旅程借來比喻一個需要時間、努力或克服困難的發展過程，例如追求自由、學習成長或實現目標。","examples":[{"en":"Her journey to becoming a doctor took many years.","zh":"她成為醫生的歷程經歷了許多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her journey from apprentice to master took twenty years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f466bdc9465b8579","term":"journey","forms":["journey","journeys","journeying","journeyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"旅行","explanation":"作動詞時，journey表示親自進行一段旅行或長途行程，就是沿著一條路從一個地方前往另一個地方。","examples":[{"en":"They journeyed through the mountains for three days.","zh":"他們在山中跋涉了三天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We journeyed westward through dusty mountain villages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/journey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b113405b6f9114b2abac","word":"joy","forms":["joy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61d5e306fb1510f6","term":"joy","forms":["joy","joys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜悅；快樂","explanation":"joy是因得到、期待或經歷美好事物而產生的強烈快樂，像心裡突然亮起的一團光。它比一般短暫的高興更有感染力，也可以指某個具體時刻的快樂。","examples":[{"en":"The children shouted with joy when the gates opened.","zh":"大門開啟時，孩子們高興得喊了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt great joy at the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息，她感到非常喜悅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15c44c10ae950ea8","term":"joy","forms":["joy","joys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂事；令人快樂的人或事","explanation":"joy也可以指帶來喜悅的具體人、事或經歷，也就是“快樂的來源”。因此，養育孩子既可能帶來辛勞，也可能是生活中的許多joy。","examples":[{"en":"The joys of travel include meeting people from different cultures.","zh":"旅行的樂趣包括結識來自不同文化的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Watching her grandson learn to read was a joy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1483e88be8eb83821b55","word":"joyful","forms":["joyful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06719083727dad17","term":"joyful","forms":["joyful","joyfuller","more joyful","joyfullest","most joyful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"充滿喜悅的","explanation":"用於描述人因某事感到強烈而明顯的快樂，也可描述把這種快樂傳遞出來的笑聲、氣氛、場合等。它比一般的“開心”更有“喜悅洋溢、令人感受到”的色彩。","examples":[{"en":"She felt joyful when her family surprised her with a birthday cake.","zh":"家人為她準備生日蛋糕給她驚喜時，她感到非常喜悅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The joyful music filled the room.","zh":"歡快喜悅的音樂充滿了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joyful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a039a3e2654d716dc2a","word":"joyous","forms":["joyous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2472cbee54d504f9","term":"joyous","forms":["joyous","more joyous","most joyous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"充滿喜悅的；歡樂的","explanation":"指內心或周圍充滿強烈而明顯的喜悅，彷彿快樂向外散發出來。它可以形容人，也可以形容音樂、節日、慶典或某個歡樂的時刻。","examples":[{"en":"The wedding was a joyous occasion for the whole family.","zh":"這場婚禮是全家人都感到無比喜悅的時刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sang a joyous song around the fire.","zh":"我們圍著篝火唱了一首充滿歡樂的歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joyous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10e86c6514d40f2a3e86","word":"judge","forms":["judge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3dc752c9b6034d97","term":"judge","forms":["judge","judges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法官","explanation":"法官是在法院主持審判、解釋和執行法律並作出裁決的公職人員。這是judge最重要的名詞義，也是“作最終判斷的人”這一核心形象最直接的體現。","examples":[{"en":"The judge listened carefully before making a decision.","zh":"法官在作出決定前認真聽取了意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge dismissed the case.","zh":"法官駁回了這起案件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8db68083d807dbe7","term":"judge","forms":["judge","judges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"善於評價的人","explanation":"在“a good judge of...”中，judge指能夠準確評價某種品質、價值或人的人，例如懂酒、識人或判斷性格的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is a good judge of character.","zh":"她很會判斷一個人的品格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He's an excellent judge of antique furniture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-223e0ff03f5f4e90","term":"judge","forms":["judge","judges","judging","judged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裁判、判決","explanation":"judge某人或某事，就是以裁判者身份作出正式決定或判決，尤其用於法律或最終裁定的語境。","examples":[{"en":"The court judged him responsible for the damage.","zh":"法院判定他應對這起損失負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The panel judged the proposal unacceptable.","zh":"評審小組裁定這項提議不可接受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aed1c998dc55894b","term":"judge","forms":["judge","judges","judging","judged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"判斷、評價","explanation":"judge某人或某事可以是根據證據、經驗或外表形成評價，不一定涉及法院。這是日常英語中非常常見的“作判斷”用法。","examples":[{"en":"You should not judge people by their appearance.","zh":"你不應該以外表來判斷別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We can judge the quality by the results.","zh":"我們可以根據結果判斷質量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4dea58a058380897ff6","word":"judgment/judgement","forms":["judgment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e252104bcdfc9681","term":"judgment","forms":["judgment","judgments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"判斷過程","explanation":"指對情況、價值或可能結果進行衡量並作出判斷的過程，也就是“在心裡稱量”的動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"Good judgment of the risks helped the team avoid a costly mistake.","zh":"對風險的正確判斷幫助團隊避免了一次代價高昂的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choosing a safe crossing requires careful judgment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judgment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fb089efc412ac65","term":"judgment","forms":["judgment","judgments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"判斷力","explanation":"指一個人正確、明智地判斷和決定的能力；它像一把能把事情稱量清楚的內在尺度。","examples":[{"en":"She showed good judgment by checking the figures before signing the contract.","zh":"她在籤合同前核對了數字，表現出了良好的判斷力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The job requires patience and sound judgment.","zh":"這份工作需要耐心和可靠的判斷力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judgment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-136217482eb37e86","term":"judgment","forms":["judgment","judgments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意見；判斷結果","explanation":"指經過衡量後形成的看法、結論或決定，也就是“稱量”之後得到的結果。","examples":[{"en":"In my judgment, the proposal is practical but too expensive.","zh":"依我判斷，這項提議很實際，但費用太高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee reserved judgment until it had heard both sides.","zh":"委員會聽取雙方意見後才作出判斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judgment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ab7ab8937c8bd23548d","word":"judicial","forms":["judicial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27e09428123c25e7","term":"judicial","forms":["judicial","more judicial","most judicial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"司法的；司法行政的","explanation":"指與法律的執行、司法程式或司法行政有關的事物，是 judicial 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The case is still under judicial review.","zh":"這起案件仍在接受司法審查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister called for judicial reform.","zh":"部長呼籲進行司法改革。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judicial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-959517decc5ffb1b","term":"judicial","forms":["judicial","more judicial","most judicial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"法院體系的；司法部門的","explanation":"特指與法院體系或政府的司法分支有關，關注的是法院和司法機關這一整套制度。","examples":[{"en":"The constitution protects the independence of the judicial branch.","zh":"憲法保護司法部門的獨立性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reform strengthens judicial independence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/judicial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44b2255326ec1b073f52","word":"jug","forms":["jug"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14c5c8cd5c31c168","term":"jug","forms":["jug","jugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壺；有把手的盛液體容器","explanation":"一種通常有把手、壺嘴或較小開口的容器，主要用來盛放並倒出水、牛奶等液體。","examples":[{"en":"She poured a jug of lemonade for the guests.","zh":"她為客人倒了一壺檸檬水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the milk back in the jug.","zh":"請把牛奶放回壺裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ec1b3028d351a62","term":"jug","forms":["jug","jugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一壺的量","explanation":"指一個 jug 容器能夠裝下的那一份液體或其他內容物，重點在“這一壺的量”，而不是容器本身。","examples":[{"en":"We finished one jug of iced tea during lunch.","zh":"午飯時我們喝完了一壺冰茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you make another jug of water?","zh":"你能再準備一壺水嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5ad895656074bb12930","word":"juice","forms":["juice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18fde9ffb0310f56","term":"juice","forms":["juice","juices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物或水果的汁液","explanation":"指從水果或其他植物中流出或榨出的液體，最典型的是果汁。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh orange juice tastes best in the morning.","zh":"新鮮橙汁早上喝味道最好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Squeeze the lemon over the fish to add some juice.","zh":"把檸檬汁擠在魚上，增加一些汁水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85335a4038ff91ae","term":"juice","forms":["juice","juices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"果汁飲料","explanation":"指一杯、一份或一瓶用果汁製成的飲料；這時說的是飲品，而不只是其中的液體成分。","examples":[{"en":"Could we get two apple juices for the children?","zh":"可以給孩子們來兩杯蘋果汁嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like orange juice with your breakfast?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c17109d20746ad75bc1","word":"juicy","forms":["juicy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59c2a1a43d822837","term":"juicy","forms":["juicy","juicier","juiciest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"汁水豐富的","explanation":"指水果、食物等含有很多汁水，吃起來通常溼潤多汁；這是最直接、最容易掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"This peach is sweet and juicy.","zh":"這個桃子又甜又多汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought some juicy tomatoes for the salad.","zh":"我們買了一些汁水豐富的西紅柿做沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juicy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb191ece554f6941","term":"juicy","forms":["juicy","juicier","juiciest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"刺激有趣的","explanation":"把“汁水足、很有滋味”的感覺用於比喻，表示訊息、故事、八卦或細節很精彩、刺激，能引起強烈興趣；有時也帶一點煽情或曖昧意味。","examples":[{"en":"She told us a juicy story about what happened at the party.","zh":"她給我們講了一個關於聚會上發生的事的勁爆故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The memoir promises juicy details about backstage rivalries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juicy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bdaf554e42029bd0dbe","word":"jump","forms":["jump"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6a037097c20f243","term":"jump","forms":["jump","jumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳躍；一躍","explanation":"指身體突然越過原來的高度或位置所做的跳躍動作，也可以指向前躍進一段距離。","examples":[{"en":"The cat made a jump onto the windowsill.","zh":"貓一躍跳上了窗臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With one jump, he cleared the puddle.","zh":"他一躍就跨過了水窪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f85d750418ccb2a","term":"jump","forms":["jump","jumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘗試；冒險一試","explanation":"指為達到某個結果而邁出的一步，尤其帶有不確定性或風險，因此可理解為“冒險嘗試”。","examples":[{"en":"Starting her own business was a big jump, but she was ready.","zh":"自己創業是一次很大的冒險嘗試，但她已經準備好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took a jump into a new career after years in finance.","zh":"他在金融行業工作多年後，冒險嘗試了一個全新的職業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c62c19e93da5858f","term":"jump","forms":["jump","jumps","jumping","jumped","jumpest","jumpedst","jumpeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跳躍；躍起","explanation":"指身體藉助力量突然離開地面，向上、向下或向某個方向躍起，也可泛指跳過一段距離。這是把身體突然越過某個位置或高度的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"The dog jumped over the low wall.","zh":"那隻狗跳過了矮牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She jumped when she heard her name.","zh":"她聽到有人叫自己的名字時跳了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52794fef4e747173","term":"jump","forms":["jump","jumps","jumping","jumped","jumpest","jumpedst","jumpeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猛增；驟升","explanation":"表示價格、數量、溫度等在短時間內突然大幅上升，像一下子越到了更高的位置。常用於資料、市場和新聞語境。","examples":[{"en":"Online sales jumped by 30% in December.","zh":"十二月份的網上銷售額猛增了百分之三十。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature jumped to 35 degrees by noon.","zh":"到中午時，氣溫驟升到三十五度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fbfdf186038f834c76c8","word":"junction","forms":["junction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27fc068f537d513b","term":"junction","forms":["junction","junctions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連線；接合","explanation":"表示把東西連在一起的動作，或已經連在一起的狀態。它強調“從分開到接上”這一連線關係，是全詞“幾條線碰頭”的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The junction of the two pipes was leaking.","zh":"兩根管子的接合處漏水了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A clean junction is essential for a strong connection.","zh":"整潔的接合對於形成牢固的連線至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcd0c6eb14d6cbce","term":"junction","forms":["junction","junctions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道路交匯處；路口","explanation":"指兩條道路相遇、連線或分開的地方。可以把它想成地圖上幾條線碰頭的那個點。","examples":[{"en":"Turn left at the junction and follow the signs for the station.","zh":"在路口左轉，然後按照車站的指示牌走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Traffic was heavy near the junction this morning.","zh":"今天早上路口附近交通很擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91ed2ef15eee7102873d","word":"jungle","forms":["jungle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a64329939f664dd","term":"jungle","forms":["jungle","jungles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱帶叢林；熱帶雨林","explanation":"指面積很大、溼熱、植物茂密且有許多野生動物的森林，尤其是熱帶地區難以開發和穿行的森林。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers spent three weeks in the jungle studying rare frogs.","zh":"研究人員在熱帶叢林裡待了三週，研究稀有的青蛙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow path led through the jungle to the river.","zh":"一條狹窄的小路穿過叢林，通向那條河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ffa838a12b4abe2","term":"jungle","forms":["jungle","jungles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"弱肉強食的環境","explanation":"比喻一個缺少規則、法律或道德約束的地方，在那裡人們為了自身利益而殘酷競爭，像在野外叢林中求生一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Finding a good job is a jungle out there, so prepare for fierce competition.","zh":"找一份好工作就像置身弱肉強食的叢林，得做好激烈競爭的準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inexperienced lawyer struggled in the corporate jungle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fdd880f097cddfef868","word":"junior","forms":["junior"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d9a247047e3c855","term":"junior","forms":["junior","more junior","most junior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"職位較低的","explanation":"指在組織或工作中職位、級別或資歷低於別人，處於較初級的角色。它仍然圍繞“年輕或經驗較少的一方”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She started her career as a junior editor.","zh":"她以初級編輯的身份開始了自己的職業生涯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is junior to me in the company.","zh":"他在公司裡的職位比我低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a875eecd95a4a71","term":"junior","forms":["junior","more junior","most junior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"較年輕的","explanation":"指年齡比另一個人小，常用於兩個人之間的比較，尤其是談到親屬、同事或上下級關係時。","examples":[{"en":"He is five years her junior.","zh":"他比她小五歲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My junior colleagues helped me learn the new system.","zh":"比我年輕或資歷較淺的同事幫助我瞭解了新系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ec3f86728c527d5","term":"junior","forms":["junior","juniors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"較年輕的人","explanation":"指在年齡、資歷或家庭輩分上較年輕的那個人，常常需要結合上下文才能確定比較物件。","examples":[{"en":"She is three years his junior.","zh":"她比他小三歲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is my junior by three years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef875a1705a5fdac206b","word":"junk","forms":["junk"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d166e65a7edcaa27","term":"junk","forms":["junk","junks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雜物；廢品","explanation":"指沒有什麼價值、被丟棄或不想要的各種雜物，常常是一堆說不清具體名稱的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The garage is full of junk we never use.","zh":"車庫裡堆滿了我們從來不用的雜物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I cleared out a box of old junk from the attic.","zh":"我從閣樓清理出了一箱舊雜物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55b2e5fac3a3b61c","term":"junk","forms":["junk","junks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低質量的；低價值的","explanation":"指質量差、價值低，尤其是沒有多少商業價值的材料、產品或資源；它常用來批評某類東西。","examples":[{"en":"He is trying to cut down on junk food.","zh":"他正在努力少吃垃圾食品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drawer was full of broken junk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30f3d8f20c57025d","term":"junk","forms":["junk","junks","junking","junked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"丟棄","explanation":"把某物當作沒有價值的廢物扔掉或處理掉；這個動詞義直接來自“junk”作為廢品的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"We should junk this broken printer.","zh":"我們應該把這臺壞掉的印表機扔掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We junked the broken printer rather than repairing it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/junk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e79db8f9719a84b11d0","word":"jury","forms":["jury"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f69b0d31d1873a14","term":"jury","forms":["jury","juries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陪審團","explanation":"指從普通人中選出、在法庭上聽取證據並判斷案件事實的一組人。他們不是通常意義上的法官，而是根據證據決定被告是否有罪等事實問題。","examples":[{"en":"The jury found the defendant not guilty.","zh":"陪審團認定被告無罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge asked the jury to consider all the evidence.","zh":"法官要求陪審團考慮全部證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2c66dfd45dd07f58d22","word":"just","forms":["just"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3dee06b495bbef10","term":"just","forms":["just","juster","more just","justest","most just"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公正正當","explanation":"表示在道德、法律或利益分配上公平正當，既不偏袒，也不虧待應得的人。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone deserves a just and peaceful society.","zh":"每個人都應享有一個公正而和平的社會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge made a just decision.","zh":"法官作出了公正的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/just","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-285ed99bd9a62a97","term":"just","forms":["just"],"pos":"adv","zh":"只是；僅僅","explanation":"表示範圍很小或沒有更多內容，相當於“只是、僅僅”，把所說的事情限制在一個較窄的範圍內。","examples":[{"en":"I just need a few minutes to finish this.","zh":"我只需要幾分鐘就能做完這件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She just wanted to help.","zh":"她只是想幫忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/just","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8be993f93f301335","term":"just","forms":["just"],"pos":"adv","zh":"剛剛","explanation":"表示動作在不久前發生，時間上離現在非常近，相當於“剛剛、才”。","examples":[{"en":"They have just left the office.","zh":"他們剛剛離開辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I just saw your message.","zh":"我剛剛看到你的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/just","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b07136d6781847d0","term":"just","forms":["just"],"pos":"adv","zh":"正好；恰恰","explanation":"表示時間、數量、位置或狀態完全吻合，達到準確的點，相當於“正好、恰恰、完全合適”。","examples":[{"en":"The jacket is just right for this weather.","zh":"這件夾克正適合這樣的天氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We arrived just in time for the show.","zh":"我們到達時正好趕上演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/just","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-468c7b6449dd928f2dda","word":"justice","forms":["justice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-243ed43979d7365a","term":"justice","forms":["justice","justices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公正；公平","explanation":"justice 是讓人和事受到公平、合理對待的狀態或原則，重點在於“不偏袒、合乎公道”。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone questioned the justice of the decision.","zh":"每個人都質疑這個決定是否公正。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She believes that justice requires equal treatment for all.","zh":"她認為，公正要求平等對待所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2212a32a99f80bd","term":"justice","forms":["justice","justices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正義；應有的公道","explanation":"這裡的 justice 不只是公平原則，還帶有讓錯誤受到應有處理、讓受害者得到公道的理想。","examples":[{"en":"The victim's family felt that justice had finally been served.","zh":"受害者家屬覺得正義終於得到了伸張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People marched through the city to demand justice.","zh":"人們走過城市街道，要求得到公道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b578cbff1f54fa92825","word":"justify","forms":["justify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3d01b0216bb7be0","term":"justify","forms":["justify","justifies","justifying","justified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為行為提出合理解釋","explanation":"指給出理由，說明自己的行為、決定或花費為什麼可以接受，重點是讓這件事在別人眼中“站得住”。","examples":[{"en":"How can you justify spending so much money on clothes?","zh":"你怎麼能為花這麼多錢買衣服辯解呢？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tried to justify his decision with a long explanation.","zh":"他試圖用一大段解釋來說明自己的決定是合理的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d7cbdef74ee44fd","term":"justify","forms":["justify","justifies","justifying","justified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"足以成為合理理由","explanation":"指某件事本身足以支援另一個行為或決定，常用於判斷某種理由是否真的夠充分。","examples":[{"en":"Nothing can justify the way he spoke to his parents.","zh":"沒有任何理由能為他說話那樣對待父母辯護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The emergency justified delaying the flight.","zh":"這場緊急情況足以說明延誤航班是合理的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d4fc934c35ccb21","term":"justify","forms":["justify","justifies","justifying","justified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為自己辯解","explanation":"指一個人主動說明自己的行為或決定為什麼合理，常帶有“沒有必要向別人證明自己”的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"She felt no need to justify herself for leaving early.","zh":"她覺得自己沒必要為提前離開而辯解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You do not have to justify yourself to anyone.","zh":"你不必向任何人證明自己是有道理的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/justify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5fd4f2f653e28dc2d201","word":"juvenile","forms":["juvenile"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c973fc3ae0b069bd","term":"juvenile","forms":["juvenile","more juvenile","most juvenile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"年輕的；未成熟的","explanation":"指年齡尚小，或身體、心理、事物的發展還沒有完成；核心畫面就是“還在長大”。","examples":[{"en":"The juvenile birds stayed close to their mother.","zh":"幼鳥一直待在母鳥身邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study examines juvenile behavior in young mammals.","zh":"這項研究考察幼年哺乳動物的行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juvenile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4924a600b568135c","term":"juvenile","forms":["juvenile","more juvenile","most juvenile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"幼稚的；孩子氣的","explanation":"指言行、幽默或態度像小孩子一樣，缺少成熟和穩重；這裡“年輕”從年齡延伸到了行為方式。","examples":[{"en":"His juvenile jokes made the meeting uncomfortable.","zh":"他那些幼稚的笑話讓會議氣氛很尷尬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stop being so juvenile and talk to her calmly.","zh":"別這麼幼稚，平靜地和她談談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juvenile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e82bd4c8e3a1067","term":"juvenile","forms":["juvenile","juveniles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未成年人","explanation":"泛指尚未達到法定成年年齡的人；重點是法律或社會身份上的“還未成年”。","examples":[{"en":"The program offers counseling to juveniles and their families.","zh":"這個專案為未成年人及其家人提供諮詢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law limits the detention of juveniles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juvenile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a3484b3bf2fcb0ff5f7","word":"kangaroo","forms":["kangaroo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ec8e636960226e2","term":"kangaroo","forms":["kangaroo","kangaroos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"袋鼠","explanation":"一種原產於澳大利亞的大型有袋動物，後腿強壯，主要靠跳躍移動，雌性腹部有育兒袋。","examples":[{"en":"We saw three kangaroos near the road at sunrise.","zh":"日出時我們在路邊看到了三隻袋鼠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby kangaroo stayed close to its mother.","zh":"小袋鼠一直待在媽媽身邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kangaroo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7471bdb1765a28da268a","word":"keen","forms":["keen"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2067fb6a93aef7a1","term":"keen","forms":["keen","keener","more keen","keenest","most keen"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱切的；很有興趣的","explanation":"表示對某事反應積極、很感興趣或很願意做某事，像注意力和熱情都被尖銳地集中到目標上。","examples":[{"en":"I’m keen on computers.","zh":"我對電腦很感興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She’s keen to join the hiking club.","zh":"她很想加入徒步俱樂部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52542c63b2153717","term":"keen","forms":["keen","keener","more keen","keenest","most keen"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鋒利的；尖銳的","explanation":"表示刀、刃或尖端很容易切入或刺入，直接體現了“能穿透”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The carpenter tested the keen edge of the new chisel.","zh":"木匠試了試新鑿子鋒利的刃口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A keen knife cut through the rope easily.","zh":"一把鋒利的刀很容易割斷了繩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5a51a1c294f09cf","term":"keen","forms":["keen","keener","more keen","keenest","most keen"],"pos":"adj","zh":"敏銳的；洞察力強的","explanation":"表示頭腦反應快、判斷深入，能像鋒利的刀一樣迅速穿透表面看清問題。","examples":[{"en":"Her keen eye spotted the mistake immediately.","zh":"她敏銳的眼光立刻發現了錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a keen understanding of local history.","zh":"他對當地歷史有著敏銳而深入的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ca7ea2feefc88ecb5ed","word":"keep","forms":["keep"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ca8258a1726dd99d","term":"keep","forms":["keep","keeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城堡主塔","explanation":"在城堡或堡壘內部、城牆保護之中的主要高塔，通常是防守和居住的核心部分。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers gathered in the castle keep.","zh":"士兵們聚集在城堡主塔裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The castle's keep rises above the outer walls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fdf4e1858f42d582","term":"keep","forms":["keep","keeps","keeping","kept","keepest","keptst","keptest","keepeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保持；繼續","explanation":"讓某種行為、狀態或做法持續下去，不中斷或不放棄；這是 keep 最核心的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep the door closed.","zh":"請讓門保持關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kept her room tidy all week.","zh":"她整個星期都保持房間整潔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f8b1b57f1bb7657","term":"keep","forms":["keep","keeps","keeping","kept","keepest","keptst","keptest","keepeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵守承諾","explanation":"按自己說過的話去做，不違背諾言或約定。","examples":[{"en":"He always keeps his promises.","zh":"他總是信守承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We kept our agreement despite receiving a more profitable offer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12217c800f6cd16e","term":"keep","forms":["keep","keeps","keeping","kept","keepest","keptst","keptest","keepeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持續做某事","explanation":"表示某個動作反覆或連續進行，常帶有“一直做下去”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She kept asking the same question.","zh":"她一直在問同一個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep practicing and you will improve.","zh":"繼續練習，你就會進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00aa8942525b763cbe72","word":"keeper","forms":["keeper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff3ba8f4208e1ead","term":"keeper","forms":["keeper","keepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保留某物的人","explanation":"keeper可以指把某物留下、不交出去或繼續持有的人，核心是“把東西留住”。","examples":[{"en":"You found it, so you’re the keeper.","zh":"是你找到的，所以它歸你留著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum is the keeper of these old records.","zh":"博物館負責儲存這些舊檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eeb5b6897d180449","term":"keeper","forms":["keeper","keepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"值得留下的人或物","explanation":"口語中，keeper指值得保留、繼續使用或認真對待的人或東西，好像“應該把它留下”。","examples":[{"en":"This recipe is a keeper.","zh":"這個食譜值得保留下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That old jacket is still a keeper.","zh":"那件舊夾克仍然值得留下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5fee6e3b804637f","term":"keeper","forms":["keeper","keepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看守或照料者","explanation":"指受託守護、照料、儲存或維護某物的人，例如動物管理員、守門人或保管員；共同點是負責把物件安全地留住。","examples":[{"en":"The zoo keeper feeds the pandas every morning.","zh":"動物園管理員每天早上給熊貓餵食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is the keeper of the family archives.","zh":"他負責保管家族檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6120675e395477c5","term":"keeper","forms":["keeper","keepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"守門員","explanation":"在足球、冰球等運動中，keeper是負責守住球門、阻止對方得分的隊員。它仍然體現“把球守住”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The keeper made a brilliant save in the final minute.","zh":"守門員在最後一分鐘完成了一次精彩撲救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The keeper saved the penalty with one hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bc3a5ae30466de3d77b","word":"ketchup","forms":["ketchup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-62695704907b7a4e","term":"ketchup","forms":["ketchup","ketchups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"番茄醬","explanation":"最常見的意思是番茄製成的調味醬，通常帶有酸甜味，和薯條、漢堡等一起吃。這裡的 ketchup 就是人們通常說的“番茄醬”。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have some ketchup with my fries?","zh":"可以給我的薯條來點番茄醬嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children put ketchup on almost everything.","zh":"孩子們幾乎什麼東西都要加番茄醬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ketchup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20cd4732ae60507a2e2e","word":"kettle","forms":["kettle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c40d0201afb0fab","term":"kettle","forms":["kettle","kettles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燒水壺；煮食鍋","explanation":"kettle是用來把液體燒開或煮食物的容器，通常是金屬製成並帶有蓋子。它可以是廚房裡的燒水壺，也可以是較大的煮食鍋。","examples":[{"en":"Put the kettle on while I get the cups.","zh":"我去拿杯子，你先把水壺燒上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used a large kettle to cook the soup.","zh":"她用一口大鍋煮湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kettle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d95473aca2fbb44","term":"kettle","forms":["kettle","kettles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燒水器具","explanation":"在日常生活中，kettle尤其常指專門把水燒開的器具，用來準備茶、咖啡或其他熱飲，也可以用來燒烹飪用水。","examples":[{"en":"Stick the kettle on and we'll have some tea.","zh":"把水壺燒上，我們喝點茶吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the kettle on for a cup of tea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kettle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c70e12b7a0646f92279","word":"key","forms":["key"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c8a37b1ee9e30d4","term":"key","forms":["key","keyer","more key","keyest","most key"],"pos":"adj","zh":"關鍵的；極其重要的","explanation":"表示某人或某事對結果起決定作用，缺少它就很難完成目標，就像鑰匙能開啟鎖一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Her advice was key to solving the problem.","zh":"她的建議是解決這個問題的關鍵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clear communication is a key part of good teamwork.","zh":"清晰的溝通是良好團隊合作的關鍵部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cdccae10902218b","term":"key","forms":["key","keys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鑰匙","explanation":"用來開鎖或鎖門的物件，是“開啟或控制某物的關鍵裝置”最直接的含義。","examples":[{"en":"I left my house key on the kitchen table.","zh":"我把家門鑰匙落在廚房桌上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used the spare key to open the back door.","zh":"她用備用鑰匙開啟了後門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b9dd6e0daf32d66","term":"key","forms":["key","keys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關鍵","explanation":"某個問題中最能決定結果的步驟、條件或辦法；它像一把開啟難題的鑰匙。","examples":[{"en":"The key to learning a language is regular practice.","zh":"學習一門語言的關鍵是經常練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good communication was the key to their success.","zh":"良好的溝通是他們成功的關鍵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66e27749ed41a0d3","term":"key","forms":["key","keys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鍵；按鍵","explanation":"鍵盤上按下後會觸發某項輸入或操作的小按鈕，是控制裝置的“關鍵裝置”。","examples":[{"en":"Press the space bar to start the video.","zh":"按空格鍵開始播放影片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hold down the Shift key while you select the files.","zh":"選擇檔案時按住 Shift 鍵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/key","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91f060a9ad4b39eb228d","word":"keyboard","forms":["keyboard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82d50257d955f1ab","term":"keyboard","forms":["keyboard","keyboards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電腦鍵盤","explanation":"由許多按鍵排列成的輸入裝置，用來在打字機、電腦等裝置上輸入文字、數字或符號；核心形象就是“按鍵組成的板”。","examples":[{"en":"I spilled coffee on my keyboard and several keys stopped working.","zh":"我把咖啡灑在鍵盤上了，幾個按鍵因此失靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This keyboard is quiet and comfortable to use.","zh":"這款鍵盤聲音很小，用起來很舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keyboard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d27b208b1eef34b","term":"keyboard","forms":["keyboard","keyboards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂器的琴鍵","explanation":"鋼琴、管風琴等樂器上由黑白琴鍵組成的部分；按下不同的鍵，就會產生不同的音高。","examples":[{"en":"The pianist moved her hands quickly across the keyboard.","zh":"鋼琴家的雙手快速地在琴鍵上移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The piano's keyboard needs careful cleaning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keyboard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0db10f2c2f332cd27cf1","word":"kick","forms":["kick"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-388331e4d08eef38","term":"kick","forms":["kick","kicks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"踢擊；一腳","explanation":"指用腿、腳或膝蓋用力擊打的一下，正是“用力踢出去”的基本畫面；也可以泛指這種踢擊動作。","examples":[{"en":"He took a hard kick to the shin during the game.","zh":"比賽中他的脛部被狠狠踢了一腳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One well-placed kick broke the door open.","zh":"恰到好處的一腳把門踢開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d10a4969d20781f","term":"kick","forms":["kick","kicks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂趣；刺激","explanation":"指某件事帶來的強烈樂趣、興奮或覺得好玩，像“踢出去”後產生的一陣帶勁感。","examples":[{"en":"I get a real kick out of watching my dog chase bubbles.","zh":"看我的狗追泡泡，我覺得特別有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She got a kick out of surprising everyone at the party.","zh":"她喜歡在聚會上給所有人一個驚喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-214388afd1ae6eef","term":"kick","forms":["kick","kicks","kicking","kicked","kickest","kickedst","kicketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"踢；用腳擊打","explanation":"用腳或腿的末端用力擊打某人或某物，這是“用力踢出去”的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"The boy kicked the ball across the yard.","zh":"男孩把球踢過了院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kicked the door when it would not open.","zh":"門打不開時，他踢了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ea099c0d9216108","term":"kick","forms":["kick","kicks","kicking","kicked","kickest","kickedst","kicketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"趕走；開除","explanation":"強行把某人從工作、住所、組織或活動中趕出去，就像把人“踢出去”。","examples":[{"en":"The manager kicked him out of the meeting for shouting.","zh":"經理因為他大喊大叫，把他趕出了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They kicked her off the team after she broke the rules.","zh":"她違反規定後，他們把她踢出了球隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c77d7fd8f51ed0c2a91","word":"kid","forms":["kid"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e294c9c7a663e84","term":"kid","forms":["kid","kids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孩子；年輕人","explanation":"kid 是對兒童的親切、非正式稱呼，也可以寬泛地指青少年或年輕人；重點是“還年輕的人”，不一定是嬰兒。","examples":[{"en":"The kids are playing in the garden.","zh":"孩子們正在花園裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I learned to swim when I was a kid.","zh":"我小時候學會了游泳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18ae13660405821d","term":"kid","forms":["kid","kids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小山羊","explanation":"kid 最初的核心形象就是幼小的山羊，因此也直接表示“小山羊”。這個意義把“幼小”這一共同概念和“孩子”的意義連線起來。","examples":[{"en":"A small kid followed its mother across the field.","zh":"一隻小山羊跟著母羊穿過田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children wanted to feed the baby goats, or kids.","zh":"孩子們想給小山羊餵食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a68c1c917f165e2","term":"kid","forms":["kid","kids","kidding","kidded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欺騙；戲弄","explanation":"kid 作動詞時可以表示故意讓某人相信不是真的事情，也就是把人騙住或戲弄；它和“開玩笑”有聯絡，但語氣可能更像在捉弄對方。","examples":[{"en":"Are you kidding me, or is that really the price?","zh":"你是在逗我嗎，還是那真的是價格？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was only kidding me about the broken computer.","zh":"他只是在拿電腦壞了這件事逗我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea0e2816fedee66b","term":"kid","forms":["kid","kids","kidding","kidded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開玩笑","explanation":"kid 也可以單純表示說笑，並不是真的要欺騙別人；這就是“孩子互相逗弄”發展出的日常口語義。","examples":[{"en":"Relax, I'm just kidding.","zh":"別緊張，我只是開玩笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You're kidding! We won the game?","zh":"不會吧！我們贏了比賽？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11b9608684bb5563ed6b","word":"kidnap","forms":["kidnap"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bff5cb32a90ee444","term":"kidnap","forms":["kidnap","kidnaps","kidnapping","kidnaping","kidnapped","kidnaped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"綁架；劫持","explanation":"指把某人強行抓走並限制其自由，隨後扣押或藏匿起來；這就是記憶中的“抓走並控制住”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The gang kidnapped a businessman and demanded money.","zh":"這夥人綁架了一名商人，並索要錢財。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police rescued the kidnapped child from an isolated farmhouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kidnap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1df1fcc3cb5ad1d75993","word":"kidney","forms":["kidney"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38f26666b13376d9","term":"kidney","forms":["kidney","kidneys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腎臟","explanation":"腎臟是身體裡的器官，負責過濾血液並生成尿液；人和動物都有腎臟。這是 kidney 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Drinking enough water helps your kidneys work properly.","zh":"喝足夠的水有助於腎臟正常工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is waiting for a kidney transplant.","zh":"她正在等待腎臟移植。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kidney","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1acadc4fde1723e5","term":"kidney","forms":["kidney","kidneys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物腎臟作食物","explanation":"在談論烹飪或選單時，kidney 還可以指動物的腎臟，重點不是身體器官本身，而是經過烹調後食用的內臟。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves steak and kidney pie on Fridays.","zh":"這家餐館每週五供應牛排腎臟派。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pie contains diced kidney and tender beef.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kidney","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bda9b4dfbabfdb17cd7","word":"kill","forms":["kill"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd9250048968af0e","term":"kill","forms":["kill","kills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殺戮；殺死這一行為","explanation":"指殺死某人或某物這一行為本身，強調“致死”這個動作或結果。","examples":[{"en":"The hunter wanted a quick, clean kill.","zh":"獵人希望迅速、乾淨利落地完成獵殺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lioness dragged her kill into the shade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c94b47b560202c4","term":"kill","forms":["kill","kills","killing","killed","killest","killedst","killeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"殺死","explanation":"使人、動物或其他有生命的目標死亡，是 kill 最基本、最直接的意義。","examples":[{"en":"Smoking can kill people slowly.","zh":"吸菸可能會慢慢奪走人的生命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The falling tree killed two people.","zh":"倒下的樹砸死了兩個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7f6fcfbf3197798","term":"kill","forms":["kill","kills","killing","killed","killest","killedst","killeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使停止運轉","explanation":"把機器、發動機、燈光或程式等變得不再執行，核心仍是“讓它徹底停下來”。","examples":[{"en":"He killed the engine and checked the map.","zh":"他熄滅發動機，然後檢視地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Kill the engine before inspecting the propeller.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65d614fc9f43450d","term":"kill","forms":["kill","kills","killing","killed","killest","killedst","killeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取消；終止","explanation":"使計劃、專案、報道或提議停止並不再繼續，相當於把它“扼殺”掉。","examples":[{"en":"The editor killed the story before publication.","zh":"編輯在報道發表前把它撤掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Budget cuts killed the proposed extension before construction began.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8b9ab59d73ced9d","term":"kill","forms":["kill","kills","killing","killed","killest","killedst","killeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消磨；浪費","explanation":"把時間、機會或資源一點點用掉，尤其常指為了等待而消磨時間。","examples":[{"en":"We played cards to kill time at the airport.","zh":"我們在機場打牌來消磨時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We killed an hour browsing the station bookshop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16db10b2848943982d5d","word":"kilogram","forms":["kilogram"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74c58138f8ee8634","term":"kilogram","forms":["kilogram","kilograms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"千克；公斤","explanation":"kilogram 是國際單位制中的質量基本單位，等於一千克，也就是一千克的質量；符號是 kg。它是“標準的一袋重量”這個核心概念，常用於稱量食物、行李、貨物等。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a kilogram of apples at the market.","zh":"我在市場買了一公斤蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This suitcase weighs eight kilograms.","zh":"這個行李箱重八公斤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kilogram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61fba1c74f781423","term":"kilogram","forms":["kilogram","kilograms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一公斤的重量","explanation":"在日常買賣或談論物品重量時，kilogram 也可以指“一公斤重的量”，重點從抽象的計量單位轉到實際稱出來的重量。例如買一公斤肉時，kilogram 指這份肉的重量。","examples":[{"en":"A kilogram of beef costs more than a kilogram of chicken.","zh":"一公斤牛肉比一公斤雞肉貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The parcel weighs exactly one kilogram.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kilogram","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9d9454da28129a7c683","word":"kilometer","forms":["kilometer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b13aa3eb5fe0ac8","term":"kilometer","forms":["kilometer","kilometers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"千米（美國拼寫）","explanation":"指一千米的長度單位，用來表示兩個地點之間的距離或某段路程；這個詞本身只是美國英語的拼寫形式。","examples":[{"en":"The station is about two kilometers from my apartment.","zh":"車站離我的公寓大約兩千米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cabin is one kilometer from the lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kilometer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1d6b0ba57d78fec8689","word":"kin","forms":["kin"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93fe59fd75c60b06","term":"kin","forms":["kin","kins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親屬；家人","explanation":"泛指一個人或一群人的親戚，通常包括兄弟姐妹、堂表親等，不限於直系家人；這是“kin”最值得先掌握的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Her kin gathered at the family home after the news.","zh":"聽到訊息後，她的親屬聚集到了家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her kin gathered from across the country for the funeral.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6823f6fc772a824","term":"kin","forms":["kin","kins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親緣關係；密切關聯","explanation":"表示人與人或事物之間的親近聯絡，可以是共同血緣，也可以是像親緣一樣緊密的關係；這使“kin”的核心從“人”擴充套件到“關係”。","examples":[{"en":"Her anger was a near kin to fear.","zh":"她的憤怒與恐懼有著非常接近的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His bitter jealousy was close kin to fear.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b27c158feb36ab18a10","word":"kind","forms":["kind"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a8d843e804ba4543","term":"kind","forms":["kind","kinder","kindest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"友善體貼的","explanation":"指一個人願意體諒、幫助或溫和地對待別人，重點是善意和關懷。","examples":[{"en":"It was kind of you to help me move.","zh":"你幫我搬家，真是太體貼了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please be kind to the new student.","zh":"請對新同學友善一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-794db2d8ffaf3cdc","term":"kind","forms":["kind","kinds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"種類；型別","explanation":"指擁有共同特徵、可以歸在一起的一組人或事物，是 kind 最核心的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"What kind of music do you usually listen to?","zh":"你通常聽哪種音樂？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This kind of plant needs a lot of sunlight.","zh":"這種植物需要很多陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e48b820f4c8f67210bf","word":"kindergarten","forms":["kindergarten"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-276a9bfc3f77b614","term":"kindergarten","forms":["kindergarten","kindergartens","kindergärten"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幼兒園；學前教育機構","explanation":"指主要面向幼兒的教育機構，通常接收大約四至六歲的孩子，重點是為入小學做準備。這裡的重點是“孩子學習和成長的地方”，而不只是照看孩子的場所。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter starts kindergarten next month.","zh":"我女兒下個月開始上幼兒園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kindergarten has a large outdoor play area.","zh":"這所幼兒園有一大片戶外活動區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kindergarten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-094ae246eafd30d0","term":"kindergarten","forms":["kindergarten","kindergartens","kindergärten"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小學一年級前的年級","explanation":"在一些英語地區，kindergarten 不是泛指一所學校，而是指小學一年級之前的那個正式年級；孩子通常在這一年後進入 first grade。","examples":[{"en":"He is in kindergarten and will start first grade next year.","zh":"他現在讀幼兒園大班，明年將開始上一年級。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her son will enter kindergarten this autumn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kindergarten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b77065060d98eaa3657","word":"kindle","forms":["kindle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64da8e3271564b3c","term":"kindle","forms":["kindle","kindles","kindling","kindled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"點燃","explanation":"表示把火、火炬、火柴或煤等點著，讓原本沒有火或尚未燃燒的東西出現火焰。它是“點燃小火苗”的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She kindled a fire before the sun went down.","zh":"太陽落山前，她生起了一堆火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kindled the torch with a match.","zh":"他用火柴點燃了火炬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kindle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f41a240e6180fa81","term":"kindle","forms":["kindle","kindles","kindling","kindled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"激起；點燃熱情","explanation":"把“點燃火焰”引申為在某人心中點燃熱情、興趣、希望或其他強烈感情，使它們開始活躍起來。","examples":[{"en":"The story kindled her interest in astronomy.","zh":"這個故事激起了她對天文學的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lecture kindled her interest in marine biology.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kindle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e81dfe69841ad2f7b579","word":"king","forms":["king"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f9d8906e1b1e1f4","term":"king","forms":["king","kings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國王","explanation":"king是男性君主，即統治君主制國家的國王；在傳統王室語境中，他通常是王位上的男性統治者。","examples":[{"en":"The king greeted the visitors at the palace.","zh":"國王在宮殿裡迎接了來訪者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The king of Norway opened the new museum.","zh":"挪威國王為新博物館揭幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85f66e739a22c76e","term":"king","forms":["king","kings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某領域的第一人","explanation":"king可以比喻某人在一個領域裡最有影響力、最成功或地位最高，重點不是真正擁有王位，而是“稱王”。","examples":[{"en":"She is known as the king of street food in the city.","zh":"她被稱為這座城市街頭美食界的王者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He remains the king of late-night television.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76b26679f49f6330","term":"king","forms":["king","kings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棋類中的王","explanation":"在國際象棋等棋類遊戲中，king是王這一棋子或角色；保護它通常是遊戲目標的重要部分。","examples":[{"en":"Protect your king before you attack.","zh":"進攻之前先保護好你的王。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The player moved his king out of danger.","zh":"這名棋手把自己的王移出了危險位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6038ac4d789347a54e09","word":"kingdom","forms":["kingdom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-802c880b350fe394","term":"kingdom","forms":["kingdom","kingdoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王國","explanation":"指由國王或女王實際統治，或名義上由其作為最高統治者的國家或領地。這裡的重點是“君主掌管的一塊範圍”，不只是宮廷或王室。","examples":[{"en":"The kingdom was ruled by a young queen.","zh":"這個王國由一位年輕的女王統治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Kingdom of Bhutan is known for its mountain landscapes.","zh":"不丹王國以山地景觀聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kingdom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9eb80325e05b984a","term":"kingdom","forms":["kingdom","kingdoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主導領域","explanation":"指某種事物最有影響力、占主導地位的範圍或領域。它把現實中的“王國”比作一個由某種力量“統治”的空間，例如思想、想象或商業活動的天地。","examples":[{"en":"In the kingdom of fashion, old styles often return.","zh":"在時尚領域，舊式樣常常會重新流行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the kitchen, grandmother ruled her little kingdom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kingdom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89d19d63941a517f4921","word":"kiss","forms":["kiss"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5483001b6ca72179","term":"kiss","forms":["kiss","kisses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親吻","explanation":"指用嘴唇輕輕接觸某人，通常表示愛意、親近或問候；它也可以單純指這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"She gave her son a kiss before he went to bed.","zh":"兒子睡覺前，她親了他一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kissed her daughter on the forehead.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a10121df8d50888b","term":"kiss","forms":["kiss","kisses","kissing","kissed","kist"],"pos":"verb","zh":"親吻","explanation":"指用嘴唇接觸某人或某物，通常表達愛意、親近、激情或問候，是 kiss 最核心的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"He kissed his wife goodbye at the station.","zh":"他在車站親吻妻子道別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little girl kissed the puppy on the nose.","zh":"小女孩親了親小狗的鼻子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb241deb0c8aa119","term":"kiss","forms":["kiss","kisses","kissing","kissed","kist"],"pos":"verb","zh":"互相親吻","explanation":"指兩個人的嘴唇互相接觸，通常表達愛意、激情或親近；重點是動作由雙方共同完成。","examples":[{"en":"They kissed each other in the rain.","zh":"他們在雨中互相親吻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reunited couple kissed beside the arrivals gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbc8a597a67c46549755","word":"kit","forms":["kit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-609d986015ab9258","term":"kit","forms":["kit","kits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某種用途的一整套物品","explanation":"kit 最常見的核心意思之一是為特定任務準備好的一整套物品，例如急救用品、工具或旅行用品。","examples":[{"en":"Keep a first-aid kit in the car.","zh":"在車裡放一套急救用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She packed a sewing kit for the trip.","zh":"她為這次旅行帶了一套針線用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b6632c26b0bb3a1","term":"kit","forms":["kit","kits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"供組裝的零件套裝","explanation":"kit 也指已經配齊、但需要買家自己組裝的零件套裝；重點從“裝備齊全”轉為“部件齊全”。","examples":[{"en":"The children built the model plane from a kit.","zh":"孩子們用一套模型零件組裝出了飛機模型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This kit contains everything you need to make a bookshelf.","zh":"這套零件包含製作書架所需的一切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3171d89ad00530ffa19a","word":"kitchen","forms":["kitchen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dac50c87c33ffccb","term":"kitchen","forms":["kitchen","kitchens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廚房","explanation":"指準備和烹飪食物的房間或區域，是 kitchen 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children were playing in the kitchen while I made dinner.","zh":"我做晚飯時，孩子們在廚房裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a small table next to the kitchen window.","zh":"廚房窗戶旁邊有一張小桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitchen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e8c7d42b456c9e4ec52","word":"kite","forms":["kite"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50ec1e03590a1bb9","term":"kite","forms":["kite","kites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛禽","explanation":"指一種在空中滑翔、常藉助上升氣流飛行的猛禽；它和“風箏”共享“被風托起、在空中滑翔”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A kite circled above the meadow, looking for prey.","zh":"一隻鳶在草地上空盤旋，尋找獵物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw two kites gliding over the river.","zh":"我們看見兩隻鳶在河面上空滑翔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6963a658286edeb","term":"kite","forms":["kite","kites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"風箏","explanation":"指由輕質材料製成、借風升空並由地面上的一根或多根線牽引控制的玩具或裝置；核心就是“被風托起、由線牽引”。","examples":[{"en":"The children flew kites on the beach all afternoon.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在海灘上放風箏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hold the line tightly, or the kite may blow away.","zh":"把線拉緊，不然風箏可能會被吹走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69ef5a88b0273f586588","word":"knee","forms":["knee"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b2a0656c2752f20","term":"knee","forms":["knee","knees","kneen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膝蓋","explanation":"指人腿中部連線大腿和小腿的關節，也常泛指這個關節附近的部位。它是 knee 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I fell and scraped both my knees.","zh":"我摔倒了，兩個膝蓋都擦破了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My left knee hurts when I climb stairs.","zh":"我爬樓梯時左膝會疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-922f451b8c03d3e1","term":"knee","forms":["knee","knees","kneen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膝形彎角；轉折點","explanation":"凡是呈現膝蓋般彎折形狀的東西，或一條線、曲線突然改變方向的地方，都可以叫 knee。圖表中的 knee 就是趨勢發生明顯轉折的點。","examples":[{"en":"The graph has a sharp knee before the curve flattens out.","zh":"這張圖在曲線變平之前有一個明顯的轉折點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The response curve has a knee at higher temperatures.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61edd1ff3a5d95f887f1","word":"kneel","forms":["kneel"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d04e976dbfdd4c00","term":"kneel","forms":["kneel","kneels","kneeling","knelt","kneeled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跪下；跪著","explanation":"指把一條或兩條腿彎曲，讓膝蓋支撐身體，或移動到這種姿勢。重點是身體從站立狀態降低到膝蓋著地或接近地面的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She knelt beside the child to tie his shoe.","zh":"她跪在孩子旁邊給他繫鞋帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He knelt down and picked up the broken cup.","zh":"他跪下來，撿起了摔碎的杯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kneel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3d4d101cd7ea9e5effe9","word":"knife","forms":["knife"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5cd0f1dc739252a9","term":"knife","forms":["knife","knives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"切割用的刀","explanation":"一種帶鋒利刀刃和握柄的工具，用來切、削或分割食物及其他材料；刀尖有時也可用於刺入。","examples":[{"en":"Could you pass me a knife to cut the bread?","zh":"你能把刀遞給我切面包嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a sharp knife to chop the onions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c739791ac2013f40","term":"knife","forms":["knife","knifes","knifing","knifed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用刀切","explanation":"用刀的鋒刃切開或分割某物，是名詞“刀”最直接的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"He knifed the apple into thin slices.","zh":"他用刀把蘋果切成薄片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He knifed a thin slice from the loaf.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knife","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce1d801d152db837c0fc","word":"knight","forms":["knight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad12f3614a8233bb","term":"knight","forms":["knight","knights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中世紀的披甲騎士","explanation":"這是最典型的歷史形象：騎馬、披甲併為領主或國王作戰的武士；故事中的圓桌騎士就是這種形象。","examples":[{"en":"The knight rode through the forest in shining armor.","zh":"騎士穿著閃亮的盔甲騎馬穿過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The knight lowered his visor before charging.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85630814035754ca","term":"knight","forms":["knight","knights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獲君主授予騎士爵位的人","explanation":"現代語境中，它可以指被君主正式授予騎士爵位的人，尤其是英國稱號體系中的“爵士”。","examples":[{"en":"The king knighted the scientist for her public service.","zh":"國王因這位科學家對公共事業的貢獻而授予她騎士爵位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a knight, he may place Sir before his first name.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a9a750a1f5f4207","term":"knight","forms":["knight","knights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國際象棋中的馬","explanation":"在國際象棋中，它是通常畫成馬頭的棋子，走日字形，能越過中間的棋子。","examples":[{"en":"Move the knight to the center of the board.","zh":"把馬移到棋盤中央。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her knight jumped over two pieces and captured the queen.","zh":"她的馬跳過兩個棋子，吃掉了對方的後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b56e72e957c16786a0c","word":"knit","forms":["knit"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1027902de8322211","term":"knit","forms":["knit","knits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"針織衣物","explanation":"指用針織方法制成的衣物，尤其是毛衣、開衫等，也可以泛指一件針織服裝。它保留了“線圈彼此扣合成布料”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a soft wool knit for the winter.","zh":"她買了一件柔軟的羊毛針織衫過冬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fold delicate knits rather than hanging them.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1ca466622c82f9d","term":"knit","forms":["knit","knits","knitting","knitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編織成布料或衣物","explanation":"指用針或機器把紗線形成相互穿過的線圈，織成布料、衣物等。這是最直接的本義：把一根線不斷變成相互扣住的結構。","examples":[{"en":"My aunt knitted me a warm scarf.","zh":"我姨媽給我織了一條暖和的圍巾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She knits sweaters for her children every winter.","zh":"她每年冬天都給孩子們織毛衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57c5d9be08b96bac","term":"knit","forms":["knit","knits","knitting","knitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使緊密團結","explanation":"指把人、關係或群體牢牢聯絡在一起，使其形成更緊密的整體，常用於比喻。就像線圈互相扣住一樣，重點是連線牢固。","examples":[{"en":"The difficult journey knitted the whole team together.","zh":"這段艱難的旅程使整個團隊緊密團結起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Shared memories have knitted the two families closely together.","zh":"共同的回憶把兩個家庭緊緊聯絡在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-741094f66e2c146a26a8","word":"knob","forms":["knob"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5e2db826dd96db0","term":"knob","forms":["knob","knobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓形凸起","explanation":"指從平面或身體表面圓鼓鼓地突出來的一小塊；它是“圓鼓凸起”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small knob on the wooden board.","zh":"木板上有一個小小的圓凸塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The door had a strange metal knob sticking out of it.","zh":"門上有一個奇怪的金屬圓凸塊凸了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-191a9f9a54537622","term":"knob","forms":["knob","knobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旋鈕","explanation":"指用手指轉動的圓形控制開關，例如調節音量、溫度或火力的旋鈕。","examples":[{"en":"Turn the knob to lower the heat.","zh":"把旋鈕往下調，以降低火力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volume knob is broken.","zh":"音量旋鈕壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1f16971b489e31d","term":"knob","forms":["knob","knobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球形把手","explanation":"指門、抽屜、槓桿等把手末端供手抓握的圓球形部件；它把“圓鼓凸起”變成了可抓住的握柄。","examples":[{"en":"She grabbed the brass knob and pulled the drawer open.","zh":"她抓住黃銅球形把手，把抽屜拉開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old cupboard has a wooden knob.","zh":"那個舊櫥櫃有一個木製球形把手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-392245974134021aa670","word":"knock","forms":["knock"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4124a53415d19db3","term":"knock","forms":["knock","knocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敲擊聲","explanation":"指硬物敲在木頭等表面上發出的短促、有力的聲音，是“敲”這條主線最直接的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a knock on the front door.","zh":"我們聽見前門傳來一陣敲門聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sharp knock interrupted our conversation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b619f99b88b0a82","term":"knock","forms":["knock","knocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"撞擊","explanation":"指身體或物體受到的一次突然撞擊，也就是“敲”從聲音延伸到實際打擊。","examples":[{"en":"He took a knock on the shoulder during the game.","zh":"他在比賽中肩膀捱了一下撞擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sharp knock against the wall cracked the plaster.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0800744f53a0b335","term":"knock","forms":["knock","knocks","knocking","knocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敲","explanation":"用手指或其他物體連續擊打表面，尤其是木門，發出敲擊聲。","examples":[{"en":"Please knock on the door before you come in.","zh":"進來前請先敲門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone knocked twice on the wooden door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e40a5cdd8519a72","term":"knock","forms":["knock","knocks","knocking","knocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"批評、貶低","explanation":"用言語“敲打”某人或某事，表示批評、貶低或認為其不值得。","examples":[{"en":"Don’t knock the job until you’ve tried it.","zh":"沒試過這份工作之前，別急著貶低它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It's easy to knock someone else's hard work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec580d1e235cba2089cc","word":"knot","forms":["knot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-801445bb647be538","term":"knot","forms":["knot","knots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繩結","explanation":"繩子、線或其他細長柔軟材料繞成的結，通常不能直接拉開，必須讓一端穿過圈才能解開。","examples":[{"en":"Tie a knot in the rope so it will not come loose.","zh":"在繩子上打個結，這樣它就不會鬆開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The climber checked every knot before going up.","zh":"登山者上去前檢查了每一個繩結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d9ad0a0ac04c2c5","term":"knot","forms":["knot","knots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"節（海里每小時）","explanation":"航海和航空中表示速度的單位，等於每小時一海里；它的名稱來自測量航海繩上結數的傳統。","examples":[{"en":"The boat was moving at twelve knots.","zh":"這艘船正以十二節的速度航行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vessel maintained a speed of twelve knots.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8416e894f50e7ce","term":"knot","forms":["knot","knots","knotting","knotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打結","explanation":"把繩子或其他柔軟細長材料做成一個結，使它不容易散開。","examples":[{"en":"She knotted the two ends of the string together.","zh":"她把繩子的兩端打了個結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Knot the rope securely around the post.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd1bb3012bcfaa0c50e9","word":"know","forms":["know"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-87cbb782611c1a48","term":"know","forms":["know","knows","knowing","knew","knowed","known","knowest","knewest","knoweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確定；知道事實","explanation":"表示心裡已經確認某件事是真的，或對事實有把握；這是 know 最基本、最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I know that she is telling the truth.","zh":"我知道她說的是真話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you know where the station is?","zh":"你知道車站在哪裡嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18103976f7a4f7e4","term":"know","forms":["know","knows","knowing","knew","knowed","known","knowest","knewest","knoweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"得知；意識到","explanation":"表示從不知道到知道，或意識到某件事；在敘述過去情況時常用 knew 表示“當時得知或意識到”。","examples":[{"en":"I knew something was wrong when he stopped answering.","zh":"他不再回復時，我就意識到出了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I knew immediately that something had gone wrong.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e75acfbe87810e15","term":"know","forms":["know","knows","knowing","knew","knowed","known","knowest","knewest","knoweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"意識到；知道","explanation":"強調某人對某個事實或情況有所意識，和“知道某件事”相近，但賓語通常是具體的資訊或情況。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't know you had moved to another city.","zh":"我不知道你已經搬到另一座城市了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I know the road is closed today.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fddf00dcdfb934f1","term":"know","forms":["know","knows","knowing","knew","knowed","known","knowest","knewest","knoweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懂得；會","explanation":"表示透過學習或經驗掌握了某種方法或原理，尤其常譯為“知道怎麼做”或“會做”。","examples":[{"en":"He knows how to fix the printer.","zh":"他會修這臺印表機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you know how this app works?","zh":"你知道這個應用是怎麼執行的嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/know","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0f895872d65b2528fee","word":"knowledge","forms":["knowledge"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36bfac4e03f71e70","term":"knowledge","forms":["knowledge","knowledges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對某事的瞭解","explanation":"指一個人對某個主題、地方或情況所具有的總體瞭解和熟悉程度，也就是腦中那張已經畫出的“已知地圖”。","examples":[{"en":"His knowledge of local history impressed the visitors.","zh":"他對當地歷史的瞭解給遊客留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need some knowledge of the area before planning the hike.","zh":"規劃徒步旅行前，你需要對這個地區有一些瞭解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knowledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce92d1d6a8f6f69c","term":"knowledge","forms":["knowledge","knowledges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"得知；知情","explanation":"指意識到某個具體事實或情況，重點不是深入理解，而是已經被告知或已經知道這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The change was made without my knowledge.","zh":"這項變更是在我不知情的情況下進行的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"To my knowledge, nobody has reported the problem.","zh":"據我所知，還沒有人報告這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knowledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d5538376b03422f","term":"knowledge","forms":["knowledge","knowledges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理解和認識","explanation":"指對資訊或真理的智力理解，即不只是聽說過，還能認識其中的意義和區別。","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge helps us make better decisions.","zh":"知識能幫助我們作出更好的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Real knowledge comes from testing ideas, not just repeating them.","zh":"真正的理解來自檢驗想法，而不只是重複它們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knowledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db9ab3081e9fa8ac830a","word":"knowledgeable","forms":["knowledgeable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f121f05a401e0fe9","term":"knowledgeable","forms":["knowledgeable","more knowledgeable","most knowledgeable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對某領域很有知識","explanation":"指某人掌握了某個特定主題的大量知識，能夠較可靠地解釋、判斷或提供建議；記住“腦中的知識燈照亮一個領域”即可。","examples":[{"en":"She is knowledgeable about traditional medicine.","zh":"她很瞭解傳統醫學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a knowledgeable guide for the mountain trip.","zh":"我們需要一位熟悉山區情況的嚮導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knowledgeable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28bde7a8ea849925","term":"knowledgeable","forms":["knowledgeable","more knowledgeable","most knowledgeable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"受過教育且訊息靈通","explanation":"可不限定某一專門領域，表示一個人總體上有教養、見多識廣，而且對相關情況瞭解得很充分；這是“知識燈”從一個領域擴充套件到更廣範圍。","examples":[{"en":"He is a knowledgeable and thoughtful teacher.","zh":"他是一位博學而且善於思考的老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our knowledgeable guide answered every question about local history.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knowledgeable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c88cf9468f1701ff059a","word":"koala","forms":["koala"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c789bad3c29eef55","term":"koala","forms":["koala","koalas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考拉","explanation":"考拉是一種主要生活在澳大利亞東部樹上的有袋動物，頭寬、耳朵大、爪子尖，外形有點像小熊。記憶時可以想象它抱著樹枝休息的樣子。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a koala resting in a tree.","zh":"我們看見一隻考拉在樹上休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Koalas spend much of their time in trees.","zh":"考拉大部分時間都待在樹上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/koala","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1aca80e8b55c802f7b43","word":"label","forms":["label"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e15efae90c7ae99","term":"label","forms":["label","labels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標籤；標牌","explanation":"貼在衣服、商品、容器等物品上的小紙條或標牌，用來提供名稱、價格、成分等資訊。它就像附在物品上的說明牌。","examples":[{"en":"I checked the label before buying the jacket.","zh":"買這件夾克前，我檢視了標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The price label fell off the jar.","zh":"罐子上的價格標籤掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/label","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09e01a803454c12d","term":"label","forms":["label","labels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"稱呼；分類標籤","explanation":"給某人或某事物加上的分類名稱，常暗含別人據此形成的看法；它是把人或事物歸入某一類的“標籤”。","examples":[{"en":"She dislikes being given the label of a troublemaker.","zh":"她不喜歡被貼上“惹麻煩的人”這個標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is unfair to label the whole group as lazy.","zh":"把整個群體都貼上懶惰的標籤是不公平的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/label","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8073a4ad2f8ac81","term":"label","forms":["label","labels","labeling","labelling","labeled","labelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……貼標籤","explanation":"把標籤貼到物品上，或在物品上寫明名稱、價格等資訊；也就是把說明牌附到物件上。","examples":[{"en":"The staff labelled every box with its destination.","zh":"工作人員給每個箱子都貼上了目的地標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please label your lunch before putting it in the fridge.","zh":"請在把午餐放進冰箱前貼好標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/label","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d0e7b92a3bff1ab","term":"label","forms":["label","labels","labeling","labelling","labeled","labelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……貼上分類標籤","explanation":"把某人或某事物歸入某一類，或用某種名稱評價它；這個動作像是在人的身上貼上一張看不見的標籤。","examples":[{"en":"The article labelled him as a careless manager.","zh":"那篇文章把他貼上了粗心經理的標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should not label children as failures after one bad test.","zh":"我們不該因為一次考試沒考好就把孩子貼上失敗者的標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/label","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3236c2112dab28cc4189","word":"labor","forms":["labor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d00056650f6bb8c","term":"labor","forms":["labor","labors","laboring","labored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辛苦勞動；費力做某事","explanation":"作為動詞，labor 表示持續而辛苦地工作，或費力完成某件事；它是美國英語中 labour 的標準拼寫。","examples":[{"en":"The team labored through the night to finish the report.","zh":"團隊辛苦工作了一整夜，才完成了報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She labored to explain the difficult idea clearly.","zh":"她費了很大力氣，努力把這個難懂的想法解釋清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/labor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2f7232a95df56d54215","word":"laboratory/lab","forms":["laboratory","lab"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19b83ef04b831194","term":"laboratory","forms":["laboratory","laboratories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"科學實驗室","explanation":"指配有專門儀器和裝置、供科學家或技術人員進行研究、實驗、檢測和分析的房間、建築或機構，是這個詞最核心的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The samples were examined in a laboratory.","zh":"這些樣本在實驗室裡接受了檢測。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spends most of her time working in the laboratory.","zh":"她大部分時間都在實驗室裡工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laboratory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fb433e4af6e2443","term":"laboratory","forms":["laboratory","laboratories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"製備場所","explanation":"指專門製備或生產化學品、藥物、微生物等物質的場所；重點不只是做實驗，還包括按照技術流程把東西做出來。","examples":[{"en":"The drug was first prepared in a small laboratory.","zh":"這種藥最初是在一個小型實驗室裡製備的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pharmacy's laboratory prepares custom ointments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laboratory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72ee260ad9744c0a","term":"lab","forms":["lab","labs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實驗室","explanation":"lab 是 laboratory 的口語短稱，指進行科學研究、實驗或檢測的房間、場所或部門。","examples":[{"en":"I left my notebook in the lab.","zh":"我把筆記本落在實驗室了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works in a medical lab.","zh":"她在一家醫學實驗室工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd9d08382bfca485","term":"lab","forms":["lab","labs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實驗或檢測","explanation":"lab 也可以指在實驗室完成的一項實驗、檢測、調查，或這項工作的結果；這裡重點不是地點，而是做出來的實驗任務。","examples":[{"en":"We have to finish the lab before Friday.","zh":"我們必須在星期五之前完成這個實驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lab showed that the water was safe.","zh":"檢測結果表明這水是安全的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97eb1d6128536a2628d9","word":"lace","forms":["lace"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-436258204c62fce0","term":"lace","forms":["lace","laces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蕾絲；花邊織物","explanation":"指用線織成、帶有許多孔洞和花紋的輕薄裝飾性織物，常用於衣服、窗簾或內衣。","examples":[{"en":"The bride wore a simple dress with lace sleeves.","zh":"新娘穿著一條袖子帶蕾絲的簡潔婚紗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strip of lace edged her wedding veil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f342de654a4da627","term":"lace","forms":["lace","laces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞋帶；繫帶","explanation":"指穿過鞋子或衣物上的孔眼、拉緊後用來固定的繩帶，最常見的是鞋帶。","examples":[{"en":"Your laces are untied—be careful not to trip.","zh":"你的鞋帶鬆開了，小心別絆倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tied her laces before going for a run.","zh":"她跑步前繫好了鞋帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bdf15f84127acfe4","term":"lace","forms":["lace","laces","lacing","laced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用帶子繫緊","explanation":"指用鞋帶或其他繫帶穿過孔眼並拉緊，把鞋子或衣物固定好。","examples":[{"en":"He laced up his boots and headed outside.","zh":"他繫好靴子，走到外面去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The costume was laced tightly at the back.","zh":"那套服裝的後背系得很緊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f15846b16dba201","term":"lace","forms":["lace","laces","lacing","laced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交織；交叉編在一起","explanation":"指把幾樣東西穿插、編織或交叉在一起，形成互相連線的結構。","examples":[{"en":"She laced her fingers together and waited.","zh":"她十指交叉，等在那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reeds were laced together to form a mat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3f315ea36abca8f80be","word":"lack","forms":["lack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ab6bb0d787c0d6b","term":"lack","forms":["lack","lacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺少；不足","explanation":"指需要或希望有的東西沒有，或數量不夠，核心畫面就是貨架上留下了一個空缺。","examples":[{"en":"The project failed because of a lack of funding.","zh":"這個專案因缺少資金而失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His lack of experience made the task difficult.","zh":"他缺乏經驗，使這項任務變得困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-980824f19099490e","term":"lack","forms":["lack","lacks","lacking","lacked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"缺少；沒有","explanation":"表示某人或某物沒有所需的東西，或本來應有的條件不足；也就是把“貨架上的空缺”直接說成某處缺著某物。","examples":[{"en":"This room lacks enough natural light.","zh":"這個房間缺少足夠的自然光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report lacks clear evidence.","zh":"這份報告缺乏明確的證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5f02630dd666a73979b","word":"lad","forms":["lad"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0dff3634ad6c940c","term":"lad","forms":["lad","lads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男孩；年輕男子","explanation":"指男孩或年輕男子，是lad最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。它通常比單純的“男性”更突出年輕感，也常帶有隨意、親近的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"He was a quiet lad who loved reading.","zh":"他是個安靜的男孩，很喜歡讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lads went down to the beach after work.","zh":"那幫小夥子下班後去了海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2d7a074916ed6ab","term":"lad","forms":["lad","lads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對年輕男子的熟悉稱呼","explanation":"可以直接用來叫一位年輕男子，類似親切地說“小夥子”。說話人不一定是在正式描述他的年齡，而是在用熟悉、隨意的方式招呼他。","examples":[{"en":"Lad, could you give me a hand with this door?","zh":"小夥子，你能幫我扶一下這扇門嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good work, lad; you've repaired it perfectly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5605a516a7ebf33bbfc1","word":"ladder","forms":["ladder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64f6a97bbf3c0f5a","term":"ladder","forms":["ladder","ladders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"梯子","explanation":"一種通常可以搬動的架子，由兩根縱向支撐和若干橫檔組成，人可以踩著橫檔上下攀爬。","examples":[{"en":"He climbed the ladder to clean the upstairs windows.","zh":"他爬上梯子去擦樓上的窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please hold the ladder while I come down.","zh":"我下來時請扶住梯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ladder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d3f982c13ef0f23","term":"ladder","forms":["ladder","ladders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"逐級上升的途徑","explanation":"把人生、事業或競爭中的進步想成一格一格往上爬的梯子，表示通向更好位置的一連串階段。","examples":[{"en":"She worked hard and slowly climbed the career ladder.","zh":"她努力工作，逐步在事業上向上發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apprenticeship provided a ladder into skilled employment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ladder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49547872a664dd8e6328","word":"lady","forms":["lady"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d5fc257d9b8ea39","term":"lady","forms":["lady","ladies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女士；成年女性","explanation":"禮貌地指一位成年女性，相當於較客氣的“這位女士”或“女性”，不一定表示她有貴族身份。","examples":[{"en":"A lady is waiting for you at the front desk.","zh":"前臺有一位女士在等你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lady in the blue coat is my manager.","zh":"穿藍色外套的那位女士是我的經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a00f5d8c2fc2de1f","term":"lady","forms":["lady","ladies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對女性的禮貌稱呼","explanation":"複數ladies常用於禮貌地稱呼一群女性，也常與gentlemen並列，表示“女士們”。","examples":[{"en":"Ladies and gentlemen, the show will begin shortly.","zh":"女士們、先生們，演出馬上開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ladies, please take your seats.","zh":"女士們，請就座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b2319dc1ccf78038936","word":"ladybug","forms":["ladybug"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"ladybug","forms":["ladybug"],"pos":"n.","zh":"瓢蟲","examples":[{"en":"A red ladybug landed on my sleeve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The ladybug ate tiny insects on the rose bush.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d0042b2b8a5540b4313","word":"lag","forms":["lag"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a131e3d5f7f17857","term":"lag","forms":["lag","lags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"延遲間隔；空檔","explanation":"指某件事沒有跟上另一件事而形成的時間差或空檔，例如研究與發表之間的間隔。","examples":[{"en":"There is a long lag between ordering the equipment and receiving it.","zh":"訂購裝置和收到裝置之間有很長的延遲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A short lag separated each flash from the thunder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75717e7e0a4ec457","term":"lag","forms":["lag","lags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"延遲；反應遲緩","explanation":"泛指資料、訊號或行動傳遞得慢，造成系統反應不及時；網路卡頓就是這種 lag。","examples":[{"en":"The game is unplayable because of the network lag.","zh":"網路延遲太高，遊戲根本沒法玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Network lag made the game difficult to play.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2a101742e95db6e","term":"lag","forms":["lag","lags","lagging","lagged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"落後；跟不上","explanation":"指速度、進度或位置沒有跟上別人或整體，落在後面；這正是 lag 的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Our team is lagging behind the others in productivity.","zh":"我們的團隊在生產效率上落後於其他團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She lagged behind because she had hurt her ankle.","zh":"她因為腳踝受傷而落在了後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e5dc801ffd74510","term":"lag","forms":["lag","lags","lagging","lagged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反應遲緩；卡頓","explanation":"指手機、電腦、遊戲或網路反應慢，操作和結果之間出現明顯延遲；這是“跟不上”在技術裝置上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"My phone starts to lag when I open too many apps.","zh":"我開啟太多應用時，手機就開始卡頓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The video is lagging because the signal is weak.","zh":"訊號太弱，影片播放出現了卡頓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f021f0268d5dd0d4e28","word":"lake","forms":["lake"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93282b74996f34ff","term":"lake","forms":["lake","lakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"湖泊","explanation":"指被陸地包圍的大面積內陸水域，是 lake 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We rented a cabin beside the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊租了一間小木屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lake freezes every winter.","zh":"這座湖每年冬天都會結冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-021f7d058130cc72","term":"lake","forms":["lake","lakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量液體","explanation":"把液體想象成像湖一樣聚成一大片，用來誇張地表示某種液體數量很多。","examples":[{"en":"A lake of paint covered the garage floor.","zh":"車庫地板上鋪滿了一大片油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lake of spilled milk covered the counter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d23384be3fd6cce0529","word":"lamb","forms":["lamb"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-368847f56d3d2d3b","term":"lamb","forms":["lamb","lambs","lamber","lambren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小綿羊","explanation":"lamb 最基本的意思是幼小的綿羊，通常指還沒有長成的羊。它常讓人聯想到柔軟、無害和需要照料的小動物。","examples":[{"en":"The little lamb followed its mother across the field.","zh":"那隻小綿羊跟著媽媽走過田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer found two lambs sleeping in the barn.","zh":"農夫發現兩隻小綿羊正在穀倉裡睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lamb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-325aabd04ccf4bb1","term":"lamb","forms":["lamb","lambs","lamber","lambren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羊肉","explanation":"lamb 也指小羊或羊的肉，尤其是作為食物出售或食用的肉。這個意思把“小羊”延伸到了由它製成的食物。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered grilled lamb with rice for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐點了烤羊肉配米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lamb is often served with mint sauce.","zh":"羊肉常常配薄荷醬食用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lamb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c98e85f249002f03068e","word":"lamp","forms":["lamp"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0d8ebea613506c6","term":"lamp","forms":["lamp","lamps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燈；發光裝置","explanation":"lamp是能產生光、熱或其他輻射的裝置，日常最常指電燈、燈泡或燈具。","examples":[{"en":"Could you turn off the lamp before you leave?","zh":"你離開前能把燈關掉嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small lamp lit the desk beside her bed.","zh":"一盞小燈照亮了她床邊的書桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e938c7b110ab2b8","term":"lamp","forms":["lamp","lamps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"油燈","explanation":"lamp也可以特指裝有油、靠燈芯燃燒來照明的油燈，這是傳統或歷史語境中的燈。","examples":[{"en":"They used an oil lamp when the power went out.","zh":"停電時，他們用了一盞油燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She filled the lamp with oil before nightfall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-90eae63487cae2df5b79","word":"land","forms":["land"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec30977b59249096","term":"land","forms":["land","lands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陸地","explanation":"指地球上沒有被海洋或其他水體覆蓋的部分，也就是人和動物可以在上面生活、行走的陸地。這個含義最直接地體現了“落腳點”的意象。","examples":[{"en":"Most insects live on land.","zh":"大多數昆蟲生活在陸地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat finally reached land after two days at sea.","zh":"那艘船在海上航行兩天後終於抵達陸地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07229dca380425a3","term":"land","forms":["land","lands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家；地區","explanation":"指一個國家或較大的地區，把它看成一片有邊界、能讓人們在那裡生活的土地。這個含義也常帶有故事性或文學色彩。","examples":[{"en":"She dreamed of traveling to a faraway land.","zh":"她夢想去一個遙遠的國度旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People from many lands now live in this city.","zh":"來自許多國家的人如今生活在這座城市裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8cf14df8995a041","term":"land","forms":["land","lands","landing","landed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"降落；著陸","explanation":"從空中下降並落到地面、跑道或其他表面上；這個用法最直接地體現了“落到土地上”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The plane landed safely just before the storm began.","zh":"飛機在暴風雨開始前安全降落了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small bird landed on the balcony railing.","zh":"一隻小鳥落在陽臺欄杆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75481b2cec3b8d63","term":"land","forms":["land","lands","landing","landed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲得；爭取到","explanation":"成功得到工作、合同、機會或其他目標，好像把想要的東西穩穩落到手裡。","examples":[{"en":"Maya landed a summer internship at a design studio.","zh":"瑪雅成功獲得了一家設計工作室的暑期實習機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small company landed a major contract overseas.","zh":"這家小公司成功拿到了一份海外大合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07c0f59d7003e2f69476","word":"landlady","forms":["landlady"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1857a3dde59ed8b2","term":"landlady","forms":["landlady","landladies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女房東","explanation":"指擁有或管理出租房屋、並與房客打交道的女性房東；她可以出租整套房子，也可以只出租其中的房間。","examples":[{"en":"Our landlady fixed the broken shower the next day.","zh":"我們的女房東第二天修好了壞掉的淋浴器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I paid the rent to the landlady at the beginning of the month.","zh":"我在月初把房租交給了女房東。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landlady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c4a11b3a02a7908b51ba","word":"landlord","forms":["landlord"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e4e31828f79cb15","term":"landlord","forms":["landlord","landlords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房東","explanation":"landlord 是把房屋或其他不動產出租給別人使用、並向租客收取租金的人。重點不是單純擁有土地，而是以出租和管理房產為主要關係中的“主人”。","examples":[{"en":"Our landlord fixed the leaking roof within two days.","zh":"我們的房東在兩天內修好了漏水的屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tenants asked the landlord if they could keep a cat.","zh":"租客們問房東是否可以養貓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landlord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bc04e4367534c5d","term":"landlord","forms":["landlord","landlords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒吧老闆","explanation":"在英國英語中，landlord 還可以指酒吧的老闆或經營者。這裡的“掌管一處地方”從出租房產轉到了管理一家供公眾飲酒的酒吧。","examples":[{"en":"The pub landlord welcomed the musicians before the evening crowd arrived.","zh":"晚上的客人到來前，那家酒吧的老闆歡迎了樂手們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The landlord poured two pints behind the bar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landlord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7200ba2827444d683cb3","word":"landmark","forms":["landmark"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb636e5a7f3eb01b","term":"landmark","forms":["landmark","landmarks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辨路地標","explanation":"landmark是沿途或周圍一眼就能認出的自然物或建築，人們可以靠它判斷自己在哪裡或該往哪裡走；它就像土地上醒目的“標記”。","examples":[{"en":"The old bridge is a useful landmark when you are driving into town.","zh":"開車進城時，那座老橋是一個很有用的辨路標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You will see the tower as a landmark on the left.","zh":"你會看到左邊那座塔，它就是辨路的標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landmark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa633442e72adf51","term":"landmark","forms":["landmark","landmarks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"著名地標","explanation":"landmark也指因歷史、文化或地理意義而值得記住的地點，通常是城市或地區的代表性景觀；它由“醒目的標記”進一步變成“值得專門記住的地方”。","examples":[{"en":"The cathedral is one of the city's most famous landmarks.","zh":"這座大教堂是這座城市最著名的地標之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clock tower is the town's best-known landmark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landmark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acb955df82b85f26ecc8","word":"landscape","forms":["landscape"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-890841b28415b896","term":"landscape","forms":["landscape","landscapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"土地景觀","explanation":"指一片由地形、自然環境和建築等共同構成的土地區域，重點是這片地方整體呈現出來的樣子。","examples":[{"en":"The road winds through a dramatic mountain landscape.","zh":"這條路蜿蜒穿過壯麗的山地景觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New buildings have changed the landscape of the town.","zh":"新建築改變了這座城鎮的面貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landscape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33f3214483d6374e","term":"landscape","forms":["landscape","landscapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眼前的整體景色","explanation":"指從一個視野中可以同時看到的整片景色，包括其中的山、樹、房屋、水面等各種物件。","examples":[{"en":"From the hilltop, we could see a wide landscape below.","zh":"從山頂上，我們可以看到下面一大片景色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Snow transformed the familiar landscape into something magical.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landscape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e58ac0d02d2cecdc7400","word":"landslide","forms":["landslide"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd05ee8f0a682d91","term":"landslide","forms":["landslide","landslides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"山體滑坡","explanation":"指岩石、泥土和水等從山坡或斜坡上大規模向下滑落，並可能沖毀沿途的東西；重點是“成片地往下衝”的自然災害畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A landslide blocked the only road to the village.","zh":"山體滑坡堵住了通往村莊的唯一一條路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rain triggered a landslide near the mountain tunnel.","zh":"暴雨在山間隧道附近引發了山體滑坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landslide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a1997af83362d09","term":"landslide","forms":["landslide","landslides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壓倒性勝利","explanation":"指在選舉或表決中以懸殊票數獲勝，勝勢像山坡上的泥石一樣一口氣壓過對手；不只是“贏了”，而是贏得非常徹底。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor won the election in a landslide.","zh":"市長以壓倒性優勢贏得了選舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The referendum produced a landslide in favor of independence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landslide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d93244e7b08131ef10ed","word":"lane","forms":["lane"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31c8bc46516dc0da","term":"lane","forms":["lane","lanes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道路或街道","explanation":"lane最基本的畫面是一條供人或車輛通行的道路，既可以是街道，也可以是較小的道路。","examples":[{"en":"We turned into a quiet lane behind the village.","zh":"我們轉入了村子後面一條安靜的小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their house is on Green Lane.","zh":"他們的房子在格林巷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a773f7682e3db17e","term":"lane","forms":["lane","lanes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"籬牆之間的窄路","explanation":"當lane夾在圍欄、牆、樹籬或樹木之間時，它就是一條狹窄而有邊界的小路，常帶有鄉間或住宅區的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A leafy lane leads from the garden to the river.","zh":"一條綠樹成蔭的小路從花園通向河邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow lane winds between tall hedges.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea2ef2808fdd94c4","term":"lane","forms":["lane","lanes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公路車道","explanation":"lane把“細長的通道”這個概念延伸到公路上，指供一列車輛行駛的分隔區域。","examples":[{"en":"Please stay in the middle lane until the next exit.","zh":"請一直待在中間車道，直到下一個出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She moved into the left lane to turn.","zh":"她駛入左側車道準備轉彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4ef304ba42a200bafd7","word":"language","forms":["language"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4e47e6a7a8da5a7","term":"language","forms":["language","languages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語言系統","explanation":"指一個社群共同理解並使用的一整套詞語和組合規則，例如英語、德語等；它是“傳遞意思的訊號系統”這一核心概念最典型的體現。","examples":[{"en":"She speaks three languages fluently.","zh":"她能流利地說三種語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sign language has its own complex grammar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/language","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a526f6dc29ce5ed0","term":"language","forms":["language","languages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語言能力","explanation":"指人運用詞語交流和表達意思的能力，而不是某一種具體語言；可以把它理解成“使用這套訊號系統的能力”。","examples":[{"en":"The child is beginning to develop language.","zh":"這個孩子開始發展語言能力了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury affected the brain areas responsible for language.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/language","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14908849b5b83ab1","term":"language","forms":["language","languages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表達方式或溝通訊號","explanation":"指用某種形式傳達意義的方式，不限於詞語本身；因此肢體動作、眼神等也可以被比作一種“語言”。","examples":[{"en":"His body language showed that he was nervous.","zh":"他的肢體語言顯示他很緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dance became a language for expressing her grief.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/language","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5220b3c4266890f0471","word":"lantern","forms":["lantern"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3eed69533ec28d06","term":"lantern","forms":["lantern","lanterns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燈籠；燈具","explanation":"一種用半透明或透明材料保護火焰或燈光的外殼，讓光照向周圍；可以是傳統燈籠，也可以是現代燈具。","examples":[{"en":"We hung a lantern outside the tent after sunset.","zh":"日落後，我們在帳篷外掛了一盞燈籠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old lantern still gave enough light to read by.","zh":"那盞舊燈仍然亮得足以讓人借光閱讀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lantern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94a94a90115890c9","term":"lantern","forms":["lantern","lanterns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舞臺燈具","explanation":"特指舞臺上用金屬外殼和鏡片控制光線的燈具，例如聚光燈或泛光燈。","examples":[{"en":"The lighting crew adjusted a lantern to brighten the actor's face.","zh":"燈光組調節了一盞舞臺燈具，把演員的臉照亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician focused a lantern on the empty chair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lantern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-066addf6741e4a75b484","word":"lap","forms":["lap"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b48a34b0eb5777e1","term":"lap","forms":["lap","laps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腿上；膝上","explanation":"指人坐下時從腰部到膝蓋之間的大腿上方區域，也可指覆蓋在這個部位的衣物。記住“貼著並覆蓋一部分”的畫面：物體放在腿上，就像貼著身體並覆蓋其中一部分。","examples":[{"en":"The child fell asleep on his mother's lap.","zh":"孩子在媽媽腿上睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I put the book on my lap during the train ride.","zh":"坐火車時，我把書放在腿上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-709c15fc3ec7499d","term":"lap","forms":["lap","laps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搭接部分","explanation":"指一塊材料或固定裝置伸出並壓在另一部分上面的區域，也就是兩部分相互覆蓋形成的部分。","examples":[{"en":"Apply glue to the lap of the two pieces of paper.","zh":"把膠水塗在兩張紙的搭接部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave a small lap where the roofing sheets meet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a308e537a029c9a2","term":"lap","forms":["lap","laps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賽道一圈","explanation":"指繞跑道、賽車場等一週的完整距離或一次完整繞行。記住記憶鉤子裡的“一圈”：跑步者多繞出的一個完整迴圈，就是一圈。","examples":[{"en":"She completed five laps around the track.","zh":"她繞跑道跑了五圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclists began their final lap.","zh":"腳踏車手們開始了最後一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d35c416a85b807e9b538","word":"large","forms":["large"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00fc07fb1ef8941d","term":"large","forms":["large","larger","largest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大的；規模大的","explanation":"表示某人或某物的尺寸、範圍、規模或數量明顯較大，是large最基本、最常用的意思；具體“大”到什麼程度要由比較物件或語境決定。","examples":[{"en":"They live in a large house near the park.","zh":"他們住在公園附近的一所大房子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a large collection of photographs.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了大量照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/large","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aeb49aff33a262d5","term":"large","forms":["large","larger","largest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大號的","explanation":"用於食物、飲料、衣物等已經約定好規格的商品，表示其中較大的標準尺寸，而不只是臨時描述物體很大。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a large coffee for the long drive.","zh":"我為這段長途駕駛點了一杯大杯咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This shirt is available in large.","zh":"這件襯衫有大號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/large","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4696521ee51a3ce45828","word":"largely","forms":["largely"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d428d5e0d4c95f53","term":"largely","forms":["largely","largelier","more largely","largeliest","most largely"],"pos":"adv","zh":"主要地；在很大程度上","explanation":"表示某種情況佔了大部分，或某個結論在很大程度上成立，但通常不表示全部如此。這是 largely 在現代英語中最重要、最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The project was largely successful.","zh":"這個專案大體上是成功的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town's economy is largely dependent on tourism.","zh":"這個城鎮的經濟主要依賴旅遊業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/largely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113,114,115],"total":4,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1,"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-94d8fe2cffbe16b26a3a","word":"laser","forms":["laser"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61b8e746e1d82d68","term":"laser","forms":["laser","lasers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐳射器","explanation":"鐳射器是一種產生方向集中、顏色較單一且彼此協調的強光裝置。它是“被壓緊的光”這條記憶主線的起點，裝置本身發出鐳射。","examples":[{"en":"The technician used a laser to measure the distance.","zh":"技術員用鐳射器測量距離。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This laser can cut through thin metal.","zh":"這臺鐳射器可以切割薄金屬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b22d0c829860052d","term":"laser","forms":["laser","lasers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐳射束","explanation":"laser也可以不指發光的機器，而指機器射出的那一道集中而精確的光。也就是從“產生光的裝置”延伸到“被產生出來的光”。","examples":[{"en":"A red laser swept across the stage.","zh":"一道紅色鐳射掃過舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laser traced a red line across the wall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3547cb112ac4489af231","word":"last","forms":["last"],"officialPos":"n./v./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac02cc3852a59290","term":"last","forms":["last"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最後的","explanation":"指在同類事物中排在所有其他事物之後的那個，位於順序或時間的末端。","examples":[{"en":"She was the last person to leave the office.","zh":"她是最後一個離開辦公室的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is the last train to the city tonight.","zh":"這是今晚開往市區的最後一班火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb29af3e924e4d82","term":"last","forms":["last"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最近的；上一次的","explanation":"指截至現在最近發生的那一次，尤其常用於談過去最近的一段時間或事件。","examples":[{"en":"I saw her last week.","zh":"我上週見過她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The last time we spoke, he was working in London.","zh":"我們上次談話時，他在倫敦工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d56ec76f89ed9005","term":"last","forms":["last"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最近一次","explanation":"指某個動作或事件在過去最近發生的那一次。","examples":[{"en":"When we last met, she was studying medicine.","zh":"我們上次見面時，她正在學醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"When did you last visit your grandparents?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c844a145dc3b09e","term":"last","forms":["last"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最後；最後才","explanation":"表示在其他事情都完成之後才做某事，或在一系列行動中位於末尾。","examples":[{"en":"Add the eggs last so the mixture stays smooth.","zh":"最後加入雞蛋，這樣混合物會保持順滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She arrived last of all.","zh":"她最後才到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12e265e997c9f502","term":"last","forms":["last"],"pos":"det","zh":"上一個；最近的","explanation":"限定緊挨現在之前的那段時間或那一天，例如“上週”“去年”。","examples":[{"en":"We moved here last year.","zh":"我們去年搬到了這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge reopened last Friday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24b8b032217bb6c3","term":"last","forms":["last","lasts","lasting","lasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持續","explanation":"表示某件事或某種狀態從開始一直存在到一段時間之後，強調延續到末端。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting lasted for two hours.","zh":"會議持續了兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This battery should last all day.","zh":"這塊電池應該能用一整天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a7f15441f09ba2b","term":"last","forms":["last","lasts","lasting","lasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撐住；堅持下去","explanation":"表示在困難、壓力或競爭中繼續存在、保持完整或不被擊敗，像把事情撐到最後。","examples":[{"en":"I don't know how long we can last without help.","zh":"我不知道沒有幫助我們還能撐多久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't last another hour without some water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/last","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-089001a35679a33ef3db","word":"late","forms":["late"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fee1e6d7c38241af","term":"late","forms":["late","later","latest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"接近某段時間末尾的","explanation":"指某事發生在一段時間的後面，而不是開始或中間。例如某個季節快結束時出現的霜，可以說是“晚霜”。","examples":[{"en":"A late frost damaged the young plants.","zh":"一場晚霜損壞了幼苗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm arrived in late September.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/late","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c4d8117de846337","term":"late","forms":["late","later","latest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"晚於預期的","explanation":"指某事沒有在通常或預期的時間發生，拖到後來才發生。植物“開花晚”，就是開花時間比原先預期的遲。","examples":[{"en":"The train was late because of heavy snow.","zh":"火車因為大雪晚點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trees were late in blooming this year.","zh":"今年這些樹開花晚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/late","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8da9ff8e8c206aac","term":"late","forms":["late","later","latest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"已故的","explanation":"用於談論已經去世的人，語氣委婉，指這個人在世時的身份或行為。它把人的生命也看成已經走完的時間段。","examples":[{"en":"Her late father was a skilled carpenter.","zh":"她已故的父親是一名手藝精湛的木匠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her late husband had planted the apple trees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/late","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7a4edbaae515f6d","term":"late","forms":["late","later","latest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"遲到地；晚於規定時間地","explanation":"表示動作發生在預定或期待的時間之後，例如人到達、車輛抵達或活動開始得太晚。它是“晚”的動作狀態。","examples":[{"en":"We arrived late and missed the opening speech.","zh":"我們到晚了，錯過了開場講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He often stays up late on weekends.","zh":"他週末常常熬夜到很晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/late","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91dc940996806d7e7841","word":"lately","forms":["lately"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49aaba5893137869","term":"lately","forms":["lately","latelier","more lately","lateliest","most lately"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最近；近來","explanation":"指離現在不久的這段時間，強調某事近期發生，或某種情況近來一直如此。這是 lately 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I've been feeling tired lately.","zh":"我最近一直覺得很累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you seen Maya lately?","zh":"你最近見過瑪雅嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lately","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d9283d848ea941ace1f","word":"later","forms":["later"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd718a272b21600d","term":"later","forms":["later"],"pos":"adv","zh":"更晚地；更遲地","explanation":"這是 late 作副詞時的比較級，表示動作發生得比另一個動作或時間更晚。它仍然圍繞時間線上的相對後移。","examples":[{"en":"You came in late yesterday, and today you came in even later.","zh":"你昨天來晚了，今天來得更晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They arrived later than the invitation suggested.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/later","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d720636eed8bb82","term":"later","forms":["later"],"pos":"adv","zh":"後來；隨後","explanation":"它表示某件事在另一件事之後發生，強調事件的先後順序。參照事件可以在前一句中，也可以放在 than 後面明確說明。","examples":[{"en":"My roommate arrived first, and I arrived later.","zh":"我的室友先到了，我後來才到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years later, they met again in Paris.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/later","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e1e2bcac305958b2707","word":"latest","forms":["latest"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ad9f35e9284ce88","term":"latest","forms":["latest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最新的；最近的","explanation":"latest 表示截至現在或某個參照時間，最近發生、剛出現或剛釋出的事物，也就是資訊或產品沿時間線走到最靠後的那個。","examples":[{"en":"Have you read the latest report from the committee?","zh":"你看過委員會最新的報告嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The latest version of the app runs much faster.","zh":"這個應用的最新版本執行快得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ff87f6b41ccc0c3936c","word":"latitude","forms":["latitude"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e63f919ef90f97ef","term":"latitude","forms":["latitude","latitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緯度數值","explanation":"表示某地位於赤道以北或以南多遠的角距離，通常用度數表示。它回答的是“這個地方在地球南北方向上的位置有多遠”。","examples":[{"en":"Crops grow differently at high latitudes.","zh":"農作物在高緯度地區的生長狀況不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island lies at a latitude of about thirty degrees south.","zh":"這座島位於南緯約三十度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de2f2f76cf1ed5ff","term":"latitude","forms":["latitude","latitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自由空間；迴旋餘地","explanation":"比喻一個人可以自行決定的範圍，或規則允許的靈活空間。它仍然保留了“範圍很寬”的核心畫面：限制沒有把選擇空間壓得很窄。","examples":[{"en":"The manager gave her plenty of latitude to design the project.","zh":"經理給了她很大的自主空間來設計這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Teachers need some latitude when dealing with unusual cases.","zh":"教師處理特殊情況時需要有一定的靈活餘地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c17c036604f660ca5f75","word":"latter","forms":["latter"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50c1d857be32e22a","term":"latter","forms":["latter"],"pos":"adj","zh":"後者","explanation":"在明確提到的兩個物件中，latter 指第二個，也就是後者。可以把它想成順序線上的後一個點。","examples":[{"en":"Of the two proposals, the latter would cost less.","zh":"在這兩個提案中，後一個花費會更少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mia chose tea rather than coffee, and I agreed with the latter choice.","zh":"米婭選了茶而不是咖啡，我也贊成後一個選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4df62a253889741","term":"latter","forms":["latter"],"pos":"adj","zh":"後半段；末期","explanation":"用於一段時間時，latter 指靠近末尾的部分，不一定就是最後一刻。它仍然保留了“線上上位於後面”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The latter part of the meeting was devoted to questions.","zh":"會議的後半段用於回答問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rain dominated the latter half of our holiday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3787ac36c4ac14f","term":"latter","forms":["latter"],"pos":"adj","zh":"晚年；較近的後期","explanation":"用於人生或過去的一段時間時，latter 指其中較晚、較接近現在的階段，例如某人的晚年。它不是單純說“以後”，而是回看一條時間線上的後段。","examples":[{"en":"In his latter years, he spent more time with his grandchildren.","zh":"他晚年時花更多時間陪伴孫輩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent his latter years restoring old clocks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31e289f536683cb9ce6c","word":"laugh","forms":["laugh"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d29f7a9481b2c3d8","term":"laugh","forms":["laugh","laughs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"笑聲","explanation":"指人因開心、覺得有趣或受到刺激而發出的笑，也可以指這種聲音本身。","examples":[{"en":"Her laugh filled the quiet room.","zh":"她的笑聲充滿了安靜的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I recognized him by his loud laugh.","zh":"我憑他響亮的笑聲認出了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laugh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e92fb50771093e5f","term":"laugh","forms":["laugh","laughs","laughing","laughed","laughest","laughedst","laugheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"笑","explanation":"指因為開心、覺得有趣或感到滿足而發笑，動作通常伴隨面部和喉嚨的明顯變化。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone laughed when the dog stole the sandwich.","zh":"狗叼走三明治時，大家都笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She laughed with relief after hearing the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息後，她如釋重負地笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laugh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb1f72e53d8496fe","term":"laugh","forms":["laugh","laughs","laughing","laughed","laughest","laughedst","laugheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嘲笑；取笑","explanation":"指把笑聲對準某人或某事，以表示覺得對方可笑、荒唐，或故意挖苦對方。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't laugh at my accent.","zh":"請不要嘲笑我的口音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children laughed at his old hat.","zh":"孩子們嘲笑他那頂舊帽子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laugh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11d819b7d17daa649144","word":"laughter","forms":["laughter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5652337d9d02aad3","term":"laughter","forms":["laughter","laughters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"笑聲","explanation":"指人笑時從口中發出的聲音，重點是能聽見、能傳開的那一部分；笑聲很大時，旁人甚至可以靠聲音發現有人在笑。","examples":[{"en":"Their loud laughter gave away their hiding place.","zh":"他們響亮的笑聲暴露了藏身之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A burst of laughter came from the next room.","zh":"隔壁房間突然傳來一陣笑聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7e95218d9066dbb","term":"laughter","forms":["laughter","laughters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發笑狀態","explanation":"指笑時臉部、嘴唇和身體不由自主地運動，並伴隨顯示開心、滿足或嘲弄的表情；它不只是一種聲音，也包括整個發笑的反應。","examples":[{"en":"Her laughter relaxed everyone at the table.","zh":"她的笑讓桌邊的所有人都放鬆下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child's laughter quickly spread through the group.","zh":"孩子的笑很快感染了整群人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-abfc412ce6e530df63b0","word":"launch","forms":["launch"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00520071fd83c3ec","term":"launch","forms":["launch","launches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啟動；釋出","explanation":"指正式開始一個專案、活動或產品的公開使用，也可以指新書等正式面世。它保留了“把東西送出去、讓它開始執行”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The launch of the new service attracted thousands of users.","zh":"這項新服務的釋出吸引了數千名使用者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company delayed the product launch by two weeks.","zh":"公司把產品釋出推遲了兩週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/launch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0b07e394de54b83","term":"launch","forms":["launch","launches","launching","launched","launcht"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發射升空","explanation":"指使火箭、氣球或其攜帶的裝置從地面開始向上飛行。它是把“送出去”延伸到空中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The agency will launch a weather satellite next month.","zh":"該機構下個月將發射一顆氣象衛星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rocket launched successfully at dawn.","zh":"火箭在黎明時成功發射升空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/launch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63817b8f3ca50180","term":"launch","forms":["launch","launches","launching","launched","launcht"],"pos":"verb","zh":"啟動；開展","explanation":"指正式開始一項任務、計劃或專案，把它推向實際執行。這是“把東西送上軌道”的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The city launched a campaign to reduce plastic waste.","zh":"這座城市啟動了一項減少塑膠垃圾的宣傳活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team launched an investigation into the error.","zh":"團隊對此次錯誤展開了調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/launch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95b3bd96688a3462","term":"launch","forms":["launch","launches","launching","launched","launcht"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推出；上市","explanation":"指把新產品、服務或品牌正式推向市場或公眾。它仍然是把某物“送出去”，只是送進市場和公眾視野。","examples":[{"en":"The company plans to launch its new app in July.","zh":"公司計劃在七月推出新應用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They launched the shoes in three colors.","zh":"他們推出了三種顏色的這款鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/launch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba29c6b70b275f61afcf","word":"laundry","forms":["laundry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c282411b7b59ec51","term":"laundry","forms":["laundry","laundries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洗衣；洗滌活動","explanation":"指洗衣服這件事或整個洗衣過程，也就是把衣物洗乾淨的家務活動。","examples":[{"en":"I usually do the laundry on Saturday mornings.","zh":"我通常在星期六上午洗衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have a lot of laundry to do before the trip.","zh":"旅行前我們有很多衣服要洗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laundry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55636ab94767ab56","term":"laundry","forms":["laundry","laundries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"待洗或已洗的衣物","explanation":"指需要洗、正在洗或已經洗過的衣物，重點是衣物本身，而不是洗衣這個活動。","examples":[{"en":"Please put your dirty laundry in the basket.","zh":"請把你的髒衣服放進籃子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clean laundry is still on the bed.","zh":"洗乾淨的衣服還在床上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/laundry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-695d8a635e7168052998","word":"lavish","forms":["lavish"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76d76b57431e283c","term":"lavish","forms":["lavish","lavisher","more lavish","lavishest","most lavish"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慷慨大量的","explanation":"形容花錢、給予或表達感情時非常大方，數量多得像不斷傾瀉出來；根據語境，既可能是讚美慷慨，也可能暗示揮霍。","examples":[{"en":"She was lavish with praise after the successful performance.","zh":"演出成功後，她毫不吝惜地大加讚美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave his guests a lavish welcome.","zh":"他以非常隆重而熱情的方式迎接客人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-641f84788396d871","term":"lavish","forms":["lavish","lavisher","more lavish","lavishest","most lavish"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其豐富的","explanation":"形容某物數量極多、供應過於充足，像水流一樣氾濫出來；這種“豐富”有時帶有奢華或過度的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel prepared a lavish dinner for the visiting team.","zh":"酒店為來訪團隊準備了一頓極其豐盛的晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book contains lavish illustrations on every page.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f1f74adf65864c86d3d","word":"law","forms":["law"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c29fce35ead5ef9","term":"law","forms":["law","laws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律制度","explanation":"指由社會或政府制定、並由有關機構維護和執行的一整套具有約束力的法律規則；這裡可以把 law 記成“立下來並要求遵守的規則”整體。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone is expected to obey the law.","zh":"每個人都應當遵守法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied the law before starting her business.","zh":"她在創業前研究了相關法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/law","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-454d5789b988433a","term":"law","forms":["law","laws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一條法規","explanation":"指由有關機構制定、對某個具體行為作出約束的單條法律或規定；也就是“立下來並要求遵守的規則”中的單條規則。","examples":[{"en":"There is a law against selling alcohol to children.","zh":"法律禁止向兒童出售酒類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new law requires cyclists to use lights.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/law","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-114ece8d992faac0dbff","word":"lawful","forms":["lawful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da9736f95888a971","term":"lawful","forms":["lawful","more lawful","most lawful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合法的；依法的","explanation":"指行為、權利、資金或制度等符合社會法律，並得到法律認可；核心畫面就是“沒有越過法律畫出的界線”。","examples":[{"en":"The company must prove that the transfer was lawful.","zh":"公司必須證明這筆轉賬是合法的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The citizens demanded a lawful investigation.","zh":"公民要求進行依法開展的調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd764bde8c6e5318","term":"lawful","forms":["lawful","more lawful","most lawful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遵循規則或規律的","explanation":"把“法律界線”擴充套件為任何公認的規則、自然規律或基本原則：某種行為或過程按照這套規則執行，因此被稱為 lawful。","examples":[{"en":"The process is lawful according to the principles of nature.","zh":"這個過程遵循自然的基本規律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The model describes lawful behavior in physical systems.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09d67d6e08b83655f52a","word":"lawmaker","forms":["lawmaker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-870f97f5fe4fbd55","term":"lawmaker","forms":["lawmaker","lawmakers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立法者；議員","explanation":"指負責制定、修改或正式透過法律的人，通常是議會中的議員。這個詞的核心畫面就是“製造法律的人”，重點在其立法職責，而不只是一般的政治身份。","examples":[{"en":"Lawmakers approved a bill to improve public transportation.","zh":"立法者透過了一項改善公共交通的法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several lawmakers called for stricter rules on online privacy.","zh":"幾名議員呼籲制定更嚴格的網路隱私規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawmaker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b3e27a4d43770aaa291","word":"lawn","forms":["lawn"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29d2f5974a306b3c","term":"lawn","forms":["lawn","lawns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"草坪","explanation":"lawn 是房屋前後或周圍一片被定期修剪、保持整齊的草地。核心畫面就是“整理出來的一片平整綠地”，公園或其他場所也可以有 lawn。","examples":[{"en":"The children were playing on the lawn behind the house.","zh":"孩子們正在房子後面的草坪上玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need to mow the lawn before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人到之前，我得把草坪修剪一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cc883d6f165ad8d","term":"lawn","forms":["lawn","lawns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"林間空地","explanation":"在較舊或英國英語語境中，lawn 也可以指樹林之間自然或人工形成的一片開闊地，不一定緊挨房屋，也不一定像普通草坪那樣精心修剪。","examples":[{"en":"We stopped for lunch in a sunny lawn between the trees.","zh":"我們在樹林間一片陽光充足的空地上停下來吃午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Deer grazed on a small lawn within the forest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b85b91c53558d46dfdbd","word":"lawsuit","forms":["lawsuit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7be0d8bd7b52cb7","term":"lawsuit","forms":["lawsuit","lawsuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"民事訴訟","explanation":"當雙方發生民事糾紛，其中一方把事情提交法院，請法院裁決時，這個案件就是 lawsuit。它強調的是正式進入法院程式的爭議，而不只是私下爭吵或一般法律諮詢。","examples":[{"en":"The company filed a lawsuit against its former partner.","zh":"這家公司起訴了它以前的合作伙伴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lawsuit was settled before it went to trial.","zh":"這宗訴訟在開庭審理前就和解了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawsuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83a70052504733134861","word":"lawyer","forms":["lawyer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e995fb83cbf2ec4d","term":"lawyer","forms":["lawyer","lawyers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獲准執業的律師","explanation":"指已經取得相應資格並獲准從事法律實務的人，可以代理當事人參加訴訟或審判，也可以提供法律建議。","examples":[{"en":"You should talk to a lawyer before signing the contract.","zh":"你籤合同前應該諮詢律師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lawyer represented her in court.","zh":"這名律師在法庭上代理她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawyer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bec5273c8da7988d","term":"lawyer","forms":["lawyer","lawyers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律專業人士","explanation":"指取得法律專業學位、具備從事法律工作的專業人士；這個義項強調法律教育和專業資格，不一定特別說明其是否獲准出庭執業。","examples":[{"en":"She became a lawyer after graduating from law school.","zh":"她從法學院畢業後成為了一名律師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her lawyer reviewed the contract before she signed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawyer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-360cdbba702f58890c26","word":"lay","forms":["lay"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-497f227a244a6836","term":"lay","forms":["lay","lays","laying","laid","lain","layest","laidst","laidest","layeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放下；擺放","explanation":"把東西放到某個位置，尤其是平放或讓它處於穩定、休息的狀態，正是“把東西放到一個位置上”這條主線。","examples":[{"en":"She laid the keys on the kitchen table.","zh":"她把鑰匙放在廚房桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They laid the child gently in bed.","zh":"他們輕輕地把孩子放到床上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cd2e90bf1d5c390","term":"lay","forms":["lay"],"pos":"verb","zh":"躺著；位於","explanation":"表示某人或某物過去處於平躺狀態，或過去位於某個地方；這裡的 lay 是 lie 的過去式。","examples":[{"en":"The baby lay quietly in the crib.","zh":"嬰兒安靜地躺在嬰兒床裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A thick layer of snow lay across the road.","zh":"厚厚的積雪覆蓋在道路上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dac1d7cfa95021764849","word":"layer","forms":["layer"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a03510d7facfc89c","term":"layer","forms":["layer","layers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一層材料","explanation":"指覆蓋在某個表面上的一層材料，可以是薄膜、食物、衣物或其他物質。重點是“有厚度、覆蓋在外面的一層”。","examples":[{"en":"Spread a thin layer of butter over the toast.","zh":"在烤麵包上抹一層薄薄的黃油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jacket has an extra layer of insulation.","zh":"這件夾克多了一層保溫材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c91cf3ff768a417","term":"layer","forms":["layer","layers","layering","layered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"切分成層","explanation":"表示把一個整體切開或分成若干層，讓各層清楚分離。它把名詞 layer 的“層”變成了一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The machine layers the clay into thin sheets.","zh":"這臺機器把黏土分成薄薄的幾層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Layer the cake horizontally with a sharp knife.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dab584350a04381","term":"layer","forms":["layer","layers","layering","layered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分層鋪放","explanation":"表示把不同東西一層層放置或疊在一起，使它們形成有順序的層。可以是食材、衣物、紙張或影象元素。","examples":[{"en":"Layer the vegetables and sauce in the dish before baking.","zh":"烘烤前，把蔬菜和醬汁一層層鋪在盤子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She layered two sweaters under her coat.","zh":"她在外套裡面疊穿了兩件毛衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db62b6e647942d702177","word":"layman","forms":["layman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fe00f633d549760","term":"layman","forms":["layman","laymen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"非神職人員","explanation":"在宗教語境中，layman指不是受任命神職人員的人，也就是教會組織中的普通訊徒或非神職成員。這裡的重點是宗教身份，而不是這個人的知識水平。","examples":[{"en":"The priest explained the ceremony so that every layman could understand it.","zh":"牧師把儀式解釋得讓每位非神職人員都能聽懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A layman may assist the priest during the service.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d470ad56a2ff7abe","term":"layman","forms":["layman","laymen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"非專業人士","explanation":"在某個專業領域之外的人就是layman：他可能聰明且有經驗，只是沒有該領域的職業身份。這個意義把“站在專業之門外”的核心形象從宗教領域擴充套件到了任何專業領域。","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains complex medical ideas in language that a layman can understand.","zh":"這本指南用外行也能理解的語言解釋複雜的醫學概念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide explains the procedure for the layman.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1dc5ae5b68174891b6aa","word":"layout","forms":["layout"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c60d790a3301c943","term":"layout","forms":["layout","layouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"佈局；佈置","explanation":"指物品、房間或一片空間中各部分實際擺放形成的整體樣子。重點是“東西怎樣被安排在一定範圍內”，例如花園、房屋或辦公室的佈置。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant has a simple layout with tables around the walls.","zh":"這家餐廳的佈局很簡單，桌子都擺在牆邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We changed the office layout to create more space.","zh":"我們調整了辦公室的佈局，以騰出更多空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a910a4d74b805d5","term":"layout","forms":["layout","layouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"佈局方案；平面圖","explanation":"指說明怎樣安排建築、房間或其他空間的計劃或圖紙。它不一定是已經佈置好的現場，也可以是事先用來指導佈置的方案。","examples":[{"en":"The architect showed us the layout for the new house.","zh":"建築師給我們看了新房子的佈局圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The floor layout includes three bedrooms and a large kitchen.","zh":"這張樓層佈局圖包括三間臥室和一個大廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c219c458afb2e73","term":"layout","forms":["layout","layouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頁面排版","explanation":"指雜誌、報紙或其他出版物中，文字、圖片、廣告等內容在頁面上的整體安排。它是“佈局”在出版和視覺設計中的具體應用。","examples":[{"en":"The magazine has a clean layout that is easy to read.","zh":"這本雜誌的版面整潔，讀起來很方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer revised the magazine's layout for easier reading.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/layout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81fd67d02f679b818a4d","word":"lazy","forms":["lazy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4f8cc04d74e3bd3","term":"lazy","forms":["lazy","lazier","laziest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"懶惰的；不願費力的","explanation":"指一個人不願工作、不想付出努力，常常因為嫌麻煩而不行動。這是 lazy 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I'm too lazy to cook tonight.","zh":"我今晚懶得做飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be lazy—get up and help me carry these boxes.","zh":"別偷懶，起來幫我搬這些箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lazy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-427ecbe700552fa0","term":"lazy","forms":["lazy","lazier","laziest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悠閒的；慵懶的","explanation":"指活動或一段時間不緊張、不忙碌，帶有舒緩、放鬆的感覺。這裡的“不費力”不一定是批評，常常是享受輕鬆節奏。","examples":[{"en":"We spent a lazy Sunday reading in the garden.","zh":"我們在花園裡看書，悠閒地度過了星期天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent a lazy afternoon beside the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lazy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3456bc1f4d270f4a979","word":"lead","forms":["lead"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6237d1d50108e60c","term":"lead","forms":["lead","leads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鉛","explanation":"指一種沉重、柔軟的金屬，記憶時不要和“在前面”這一組意義混在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The old building still has lead pipes.","zh":"那座老建築裡仍然有鉛管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lead was once widely used in household pipes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04ac29c523f4f27a","term":"lead","forms":["lead","leads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領先；優勢","explanation":"指比賽或競爭中處於前面的位置，也可以指領先的分數、距離或優勢。想象隊伍跑在前面，就是有 lead。","examples":[{"en":"Our team took the lead early in the second half.","zh":"我們隊在下半場剛開始時取得了領先。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The blue car has a narrow lead over the others.","zh":"那輛藍色汽車只領先其他車一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1025c4cf86ae9745","term":"lead","forms":["lead","leads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主角；主要角色","explanation":"指戲劇或電影中最重要的角色，也就是故事中處在最前面、最受關注的人物。","examples":[{"en":"She won the lead in a new historical drama.","zh":"她獲得了一部新歷史劇的主角角色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film follows two leads whose lives change overnight.","zh":"這部電影講述了兩位主角的生活一夜之間發生變化的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88811f073ba3fd67","term":"lead","forms":["lead","leads","leading","led","leadest","ledst","ledest","leadeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"帶領；引導","explanation":"把“在前面”作為核心畫面：某人走在前面，帶著別人一起走，或負責指揮他們做事。","examples":[{"en":"The guide led us through the old town.","zh":"導遊帶我們走過了老城區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She leads a team of eight engineers.","zh":"她帶領一個由八名工程師組成的團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d5b660943625c0af95e","word":"leader","forms":["leader"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89cdfa50d9418c20","term":"leader","forms":["leader","leaders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領導者；帶頭人","explanation":"leader 是走在前面、決定方向並帶領他人的人，可以是政治人物、團隊負責人，也可以只是某個行動中的帶頭者。","examples":[{"en":"The team leader explained the plan and assigned everyone a task.","zh":"團隊負責人說明了計劃，並給每個人分配了任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a respected leader in her community.","zh":"她成了社群裡受人尊敬的帶頭人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leader","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5184c5028be1d882","term":"leader","forms":["leader","leaders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主要演員；樂隊領隊","explanation":"在娛樂和音樂語境中，leader 可以指帶領表演或樂隊的人，尤其是英國英語中的這種用法。","examples":[{"en":"The band leader counted in the song before the musicians began.","zh":"樂隊領隊在樂手開始演奏前數拍帶入了歌曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band's leader asked the drummer to slow down.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leader","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9e720e53885580b1e0c5","word":"leadership","forms":["leadership"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d587fb3e8d426b8","term":"leadership","forms":["leadership","leaderships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領導能力","explanation":"指帶領、影響並組織他人朝共同目標前進的能力；重點不只是擁有權力，還包括作出方向判斷和帶動他人的本領。","examples":[{"en":"Her leadership helped the team recover after a difficult season.","zh":"她的領導能力幫助團隊在艱難的賽季後重新振作起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm leadership kept the team focused.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leadership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f8f878e73ad476d","term":"leadership","forms":["leadership","leaderships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領導層","explanation":"指一個組織、國家或團體中負責作決定、帶領整體的那群領導者；這裡的“帶隊者”從個人擴充套件成了一個群體。","examples":[{"en":"The company's leadership approved the plan after a long discussion.","zh":"公司領導層經過長時間討論後批准了這項計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leadership announced the restructuring on Monday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leadership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f91161f43433e49a6de","word":"leaf","forms":["leaf"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89b4c409e94957e0","term":"leaf","forms":["leaf","leaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葉子；葉片","explanation":"植物通常綠色而扁平、用來進行生長活動的部分就是leaf；日常說樹葉、花葉時都可用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"The leaves turn red in autumn.","zh":"這些葉子在秋天變紅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A leaf fell onto my shoulder.","zh":"一片葉子落在了我的肩膀上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leaf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d38263e49a941fd0","term":"leaf","forms":["leaf","leaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書頁；雜誌的一張紙","explanation":"書、雜誌等中的一張紙有正反兩面；從裝訂角度看，這整張紙叫leaf，而不是隻指其中一面。","examples":[{"en":"The old book is missing its first leaf.","zh":"這本舊書缺了第一張書頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The advertisement takes up a full leaf of the magazine.","zh":"這則廣告佔了雜誌整整一張書頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leaf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2e0c347e274d2c3b61e","word":"league","forms":["league"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2be4a9b7437afadf","term":"league","forms":["league","leagues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯盟；聯合組織","explanation":"league把不同的國家、團體或個人聯合成一個合作組織，核心仍是“綁在一起共同做事”。它可以是正式機構，也可以只是為共同目標組成的團體。","examples":[{"en":"Several local charities formed a league to support homeless families.","zh":"幾家當地慈善機構組成了一個聯盟來幫助無家可歸的家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined a league of small business owners.","zh":"她加入了一個由小企業主組成的聯盟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/league","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-150a9fcb0874b946","term":"league","forms":["league","leagues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育聯賽","explanation":"在體育中，league是由多支球隊組成、彼此比賽並爭奪冠軍的聯賽；它既可以指整個組織，也可以指這個比賽體系。","examples":[{"en":"The club has played in the national league for twenty years.","zh":"這傢俱樂部參加全國聯賽已經二十年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The league will announce its new schedule next week.","zh":"該聯賽將在下週公佈新的賽程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/league","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a73f424d2b4e39b","term":"league","forms":["league","leagues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水平；檔次","explanation":"由“處在同一個聯賽圈子裡”引申為處於相同水平、地位或檔次。out of one's league尤其常表示對方高不可攀，或某事超出自己的能力範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Our small company is not in the same league as the industry leaders.","zh":"我們這家小公司和行業龍頭不在一個檔次上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That apartment is completely out of my league.","zh":"那套公寓完全超出了我的經濟能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/league","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f537b80f1f2b7d1cc17","word":"leak","forms":["leak"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-711fdfbe04045cad","term":"leak","forms":["leak","leaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"漏洞；漏孔","explanation":"指容器、屋頂、管道等上的裂縫或孔，它讓水、氣體等本來應該被封住的東西漏出去。","examples":[{"en":"We found a leak in the roof after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，我們發現屋頂有個漏孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plumber repaired a leak in the pipe.","zh":"水管工修好了管道上的一個漏點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8d591acef71b36a","term":"leak","forms":["leak","leaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秘密洩露","explanation":"指原本保密的資訊被未經授權地公開，就像秘密從封閉處漏了出去。","examples":[{"en":"The leak revealed details of the new policy.","zh":"這次洩密披露了新政策的細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is investigating a leak to the press.","zh":"公司正在調查向媒體洩露資訊的事件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eac444b4569fd342","term":"leak","forms":["leak","leaks","leaking","leaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使液體或氣體漏出","explanation":"指讓本應封住的液體或氣體透過開口漏出去，強調造成洩漏的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The damaged tank is leaking fuel into the soil.","zh":"受損的儲罐正把燃油漏進土壤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pipe leaked water onto the floor.","zh":"管道把水漏到了地板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ddbea1977866caa1","term":"leak","forms":["leak","leaks","leaking","leaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漏出","explanation":"指液體或氣體自己從本應封住的開口漏出去，重點在洩漏正在發生。","examples":[{"en":"Water is leaking from the ceiling.","zh":"水正從天花板上漏下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gas has been leaking all night.","zh":"煤氣已經漏了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e20fab8db863ee65","term":"leak","forms":["leak","leaks","leaking","leaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洩露秘密","explanation":"指偷偷或匿名地把秘密資訊透露給不該知道的人，讓資訊從保密狀態中“漏出去”。","examples":[{"en":"Someone leaked the plan to the press.","zh":"有人把這項計劃洩露給了媒體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The document was leaked online before the announcement.","zh":"這份檔案在公佈前就被洩露到了網上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92e89a1ed0d392158c91","word":"lean","forms":["lean"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7078c9d4eb68ee06","term":"lean","forms":["lean","leaner","leanest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精瘦的","explanation":"指人的身體苗條而結實，身上沒有很多贅肉；重點是“瘦而有精氣”，不只是體重輕。","examples":[{"en":"She stays lean by swimming three times a week.","zh":"她每週游泳三次來保持精瘦的身材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The distance runner had a lean, muscular build.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1060e6f15afe711","term":"lean","forms":["lean","leans","leaning","leaned","leant"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傾斜","explanation":"指人、物體或身體偏離垂直位置，向一邊歪過去；這是“lean”最基本的動作畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The tower began to lean after the earthquake.","zh":"地震後，這座塔開始傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He leaned forward to hear her better.","zh":"他向前傾身，以便聽清她的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c00e10e8d73ef2c7","term":"lean","forms":["lean","leans","leaning","leaned","leant"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傾向於","explanation":"指在意見、選擇或願望上更偏向某一方，但通常還沒有表示已經作出決定。它是從“身體向一邊傾斜”引申出來的。","examples":[{"en":"I’m leaning toward taking the train instead of driving.","zh":"我傾向於坐火車，不自己開車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm leaning toward the less expensive option.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93ecb473569097c3","term":"lean","forms":["lean","leans","leaning","leaned","leant"],"pos":"verb","zh":"倚靠","explanation":"指把身體或物體靠在某個堅硬表面上，以獲得支撐、休息或書寫時的支撐。這個意義仍然是“向一邊靠過去”。","examples":[{"en":"She leaned against the wall while waiting for the bus.","zh":"她等公交車時靠在牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhausted traveler leaned on his walking stick.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a76f47a688f22080c2f5","word":"leap","forms":["leap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fd75b88c8044697","term":"leap","forms":["leap","leaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳躍；躍起","explanation":"指人或動物從地面躍起並落下的動作，是leap最基本的名詞義。它把身體突然離地、跨過空間的畫面保留下來。","examples":[{"en":"With one leap, the cat reached the wall.","zh":"貓一躍就跳到了牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He made a leap across the narrow stream.","zh":"他一躍跳過了那條窄溪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b29d7e3c4ecd6435","term":"leap","forms":["leap","leaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重大進步；飛躍","explanation":"把向前跳躍的畫面轉用於抽象變化，表示發展或成就突然跨上一個很大的臺階。它常強調進步幅度大，而不只是普通的改善。","examples":[{"en":"The new treatment represents a major leap forward in medicine.","zh":"這種新療法代表了醫學上的重大飛躍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company made a leap in battery technology.","zh":"這家公司在電池技術方面取得了飛躍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d68d5f0c30abd0c","term":"leap","forms":["leap","leaps","leaping","leaped","leapt","lept","lope","lopen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跳；躍起","explanation":"指人或動物從地面躍起，是動詞的核心義。這個動作可以是突然發生的，也可以帶有向前、向上或逃避的方向。","examples":[{"en":"The deer leaped over the fallen tree.","zh":"鹿跳過了倒下的樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She leaped to her feet when she heard the alarm.","zh":"聽到警報後，她猛地站了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a8da52e920664ef15b3","word":"learn","forms":["learn"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6edb5bcf39c7b90c","term":"learn","forms":["learn","learns","learning","learned","learnt","learnest","learnedst","learneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"學習並學會","explanation":"透過練習、觀察或接受指導，逐漸獲得知識或做某件事的能力，重點是從不會到會的過程。","examples":[{"en":"She is learning to play the guitar.","zh":"她正在學習彈吉他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I learned how to fix the bike.","zh":"我學會了怎麼修這輛腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/learn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ede204e6c7d1c45","term":"learn","forms":["learn","learns","learning","learned","learnt","learnest","learnedst","learneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從教訓中學習","explanation":"從錯誤或不好的經歷中得到經驗，以後改進做法；這裡的“學習”來自親身經歷，而不只是課堂或書本。","examples":[{"en":"We all learn from our mistakes.","zh":"我們都會從錯誤中吸取教訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He learned from the mistake and checked more carefully.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/learn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23c8257fce9466b0","term":"learn","forms":["learn","learns","learning","learned","learnt","learnest","learnedst","learneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"得知，獲悉","explanation":"從別人、新聞或某種資訊來源那裡知道一個事實；這裡不是自己去學習，而是資訊進入了自己的認知。","examples":[{"en":"I learned that the meeting had been canceled.","zh":"我得知會議已經取消了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned about the accident from the news.","zh":"她從新聞中得知了那起事故。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/learn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d78e3c38d98d17d7355e","word":"learned","forms":["learned"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e14149b1b1ad3d88","term":"learned","forms":["learned","more learned","most learned"],"pos":"adj","zh":"博學的；有學問的","explanation":"形容人知識豐富、受過良好教育，尤其強調讀書和學術方面的修養。它也可以形容一個人的談吐或身份給人“很有學問”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The learned professor answered every question with patience.","zh":"那位博學的教授耐心地回答了每一個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a learned woman with a deep knowledge of history.","zh":"她是一位博學的女性，對歷史有深厚的知識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/learned","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc0347ea673389ad","term":"learned","forms":["learned","more learned","most learned"],"pos":"adj","zh":"閣下；尊敬的律師或法官","explanation":"在法律語境中，Learned 可作為對律師或法官的正式、禮貌稱呼，表達對其專業知識的尊重。","examples":[{"en":"The learned judge asked both sides to present their evidence.","zh":"尊敬的法官要求雙方提交證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My learned friend has overlooked an important precedent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/learned","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-edd95740e339e6aa0a1d","word":"learning","forms":["learning"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb5a6be66ed27d1e","term":"learning","forms":["learning","learnings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學習過程","explanation":"指學習、掌握新知識或新技能這一過程，重點在“正在把新東西裝進腦子裡”，而不是某一項具體知識。","examples":[{"en":"Learning to cook has made me more independent.","zh":"學做飯讓我變得更加獨立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course uses games to make learning more enjoyable.","zh":"這門課程透過遊戲讓學習變得更有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/learning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9b6a12d3cbbe8ef","term":"learning","forms":["learning","learnings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"知識學問","explanation":"指一個人透過長期學習積累起來的知識、學問和見識，相當於“腦子裡已經裝進去的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone respected her for her great learning.","zh":"大家都因她淵博的學識而尊敬她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His conversation revealed a remarkable breadth of learning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/learning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":3,"counts":{"114":2,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-b544a7686d1186680a9d","word":"lease","forms":["lease"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fc848ab7a04b2cf","term":"lease","forms":["lease","leases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"租賃權","explanation":"指在限定期限內獨佔使用某塊土地或房產的權利，也就是租客獲得的使用權。","examples":[{"en":"The company acquired a long-term lease on the office building.","zh":"公司取得了這棟辦公樓的長期租賃權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their lease on the apartment expires in June.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98c7ca01bf345de3","term":"lease","forms":["lease","leases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某物的租用權","explanation":"也可以指汽車、船等物品在一段時間內專供某人使用的租賃權。","examples":[{"en":"The boat is available for lease throughout the summer.","zh":"這艘船整個夏天都可以租用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company holds a lease on the warehouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a47eb6a24786be93","term":"lease","forms":["lease","leases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"租約","explanation":"指規定租賃雙方權利和義務的合同或契約，說明誰可以使用什麼以及使用多久。","examples":[{"en":"Before moving in, read the lease carefully.","zh":"搬進去以前，要仔細閱讀租約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our lease expires at the end of June.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bab65a2bddec8af5dbc","word":"least","forms":["least"],"officialPos":"adv./pron./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a17a030dc58b767","term":"least","forms":["least"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最不；最……程度最低","explanation":"放在形容詞前，表示某個性質在比較範圍內最弱，也就是“最不……”。","examples":[{"en":"This was the least expensive option.","zh":"這是最便宜的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is the least likely person to complain.","zh":"她是最不可能抱怨的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/least","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e792b49532500cee","term":"least","forms":["least","less"],"pos":"det","zh":"最少的；最小量的","explanation":"放在名詞前，表示幾組數量中最少的一組，通常修飾不可數名詞或表示總量的名詞。","examples":[{"en":"He spends the least money on clothes.","zh":"他花在衣服上的錢最少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have the least free time on weekdays.","zh":"我工作日的空閒時間最少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/least","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5022472b2831c66a63bf","word":"leather","forms":["leather"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f69dc9bd814d9d0b","term":"leather","forms":["leather","leathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮革","explanation":"指經過鞣製等處理、變得結實耐用的動物皮，常用於製作衣物、鞋、包和傢俱等。","examples":[{"en":"These boots are made of soft leather.","zh":"這雙靴子是用柔軟的皮革製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wiped the leather with a clean cloth.","zh":"他用乾淨的布擦拭皮革。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af193190b8d3cd14103e","word":"leave","forms":["leave"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad3bceca507c1219","term":"leave","forms":["leave","leaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"休假","explanation":"leave 可以指得到允許、暫時不工作的一段時間，也就是休假；它把“離開工作崗位”看成一種正式安排。","examples":[{"en":"I'm taking two weeks' leave in July.","zh":"我七月份要休兩週假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is on sick leave this week.","zh":"她這周在休病假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-290aeeaa291b648e","term":"leave","forms":["leave","leaves","leaving","left","leavest","leftest","leaveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"留下某物或造成遺留結果","explanation":"leave 可以表示不帶走某物，把它留在某處；也可以表示某個行為之後留下結果、痕跡或影響。核心畫面是“人走了，但某物或結果還在那裡”。","examples":[{"en":"I left my keys on the kitchen table.","zh":"我把鑰匙落在廚房桌上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm left several streets under water.","zh":"暴風雨過後，有幾條街道還泡在水裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b254fd272f1a6dc3","term":"leave","forms":["leave","leaves","leaving","left","leavest","leftest","leaveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離開某人或某處","explanation":"leave 表示從某個地方、某個人身邊或某種關係中離開，重點是“從這裡走開”。","examples":[{"en":"We left the office at six.","zh":"我們六點離開了辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left his family to find work abroad.","zh":"他離開家人，到國外找工作去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b00c11e50013ce4","term":"leave","forms":["leave","leaves","leaving","left","leavest","leftest","leaveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離開","explanation":"不及物使用時，leave 就是從當前位置出發或走開，常常不說明離開誰或什麼地方。","examples":[{"en":"We should leave before it gets dark.","zh":"我們應該在天黑前出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train leaves at eight.","zh":"火車八點開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6bc636ff0103a2888fb3","word":"lecture","forms":["lecture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac0b1c5aa73843e9","term":"lecture","forms":["lecture","lectures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"講座；講課","explanation":"指老師或其他講授者面向一群人，較正式、較系統地講解某個主題，通常聽眾主要聽講而不是進行大量互動。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is hosting a lecture on ancient Egypt tonight.","zh":"博物館今晚將舉辦一場關於古埃及的講座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our professor gave a clear lecture about climate change.","zh":"我們的教授清楚地講了一堂關於氣候變化的課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lecture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-031d0c2d24111060","term":"lecture","forms":["lecture","lectures","lecturing","lectured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"講授；作講課","explanation":"指透過連續講話向聽眾講解一個主題，通常是教師或專家在正式場合進行教學。","examples":[{"en":"She lectures to medical students at the university.","zh":"她在大學給醫學院學生講課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He will lecture on modern architecture next week.","zh":"他下週將講授現代建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lecture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ca7aaa322fbe8cd8619","word":"lecturer","forms":["lecturer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddf3d6370b6b9986","term":"lecturer","forms":["lecturer","lecturers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"講課者；演講者","explanation":"指站在聽眾面前進行講課或演講的人，尤其是把這件事作為職業的人。重點不在聽眾身處學校還是其他場所，而在於這個人負責系統地講解某個主題。","examples":[{"en":"The lecturer explained the difficult theory with several simple examples.","zh":"講課者用幾個簡單的例子解釋了這個難懂的理論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works as a lecturer in environmental science.","zh":"她是一名環境科學講師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lecturer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd7318051e288b30","term":"lecturer","forms":["lecturer","lecturers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學講師","explanation":"指大學或學院中的一種教學職位，通常級別低於教授；這個人主要負責授課，也可能參與研究或指導學生。具體職位層級會因國家和學校制度而不同。","examples":[{"en":"He became a lecturer at the university after completing his doctorate.","zh":"他完成博士學位後，成為那所大學的講師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lecturer teaches medieval history at the university.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lecturer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-360f84035942243c6a36","word":"left","forms":["left"],"officialPos":"adj./n./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-847cac6104a53650","term":"left","forms":["left","further left","farther left","more left","lefter","furthest left","farthest left","most left","leftmost","leftest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"左邊的","explanation":"指身體或物體位於左側的一邊，也就是通常與 right 相對的方向；對多數人來說，這一側也是心臟所在的一側。","examples":[{"en":"Please raise your left hand.","zh":"請舉起你的左手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pharmacy is on the left side of the street.","zh":"藥店在街道的左側。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/left","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c4e71fdc8af4ab4","term":"left","forms":["left"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在左邊","explanation":"表示某人或某物位於左側，重點是位置，而不是移動方向。","examples":[{"en":"The entrance is left of the main building.","zh":"入口在主樓的左邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Turn left after the stone bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/left","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12fa8b59e0f73708","term":"left","forms":["left"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向左","explanation":"表示朝左側移動或轉向，是日常指路中最常見的副詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Turn left after the traffic light.","zh":"過了紅綠燈後向左轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclist moved left to avoid the car.","zh":"騎車人向左移開，以避開那輛車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/left","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4253992e46c5f11f","term":"left","forms":["left","lefts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"左邊；左方","explanation":"指左側這個位置或向左的方向，是形容詞和副詞空間意義的名詞化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The restroom is on the left.","zh":"洗手間在左邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow canal lies to the left of the walking trail.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/left","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7c8fc91abb8ed76c29a","word":"leg","forms":["leg"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08dd7eef22e19b5d","term":"leg","forms":["leg","legs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的整條腿","explanation":"指人的下肢整體，通常從腹股溝一直到腳踝，包括大腿和小腿，是幫助人站立、行走和移動的身體部分。","examples":[{"en":"She hurt her leg while getting off the bus.","zh":"她下公交車時傷了腿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His legs were tired after the long hike.","zh":"長途徒步後，他的雙腿都累了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8467646065d89dbf","term":"leg","forms":["leg","legs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膝蓋到腳踝的小腿","explanation":"指人的下肢中從膝蓋到腳踝的部分，也就是小腿；它是整條腿中較靠下的一段。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor examined the swelling in his lower leg.","zh":"醫生檢查了他小腿上的腫脹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wound lies halfway down the leg, below the knee.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a00b7ea8aad86be","term":"leg","forms":["leg","legs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"褲腿","explanation":"指褲子等衣物中包住一條腿的部分；它就像從衣物主體向下伸出的部分，包住身體的腿。","examples":[{"en":"There is a tear in the left leg of my jeans.","zh":"我牛仔褲的左邊褲腿破了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One trouser leg was caught in the bicycle chain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-957b0393481405af","term":"leg","forms":["leg","legs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傢俱等的支腿","explanation":"指桌子、椅子等物體底部向下伸出的支撐部分，用來承受物體的重量並保持穩定。","examples":[{"en":"One leg of the table is shorter than the others.","zh":"這張桌子有一條腿比其他幾條短。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The broken chair leg snapped when he sat down.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c49fea7425fa7f869989","word":"legacy","forms":["legacy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e67b02e5926bdf3","term":"legacy","forms":["legacy","legacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"留下的影響或成就","explanation":"指一個人、組織或歷史事件留給後世的思想、成就、制度或精神影響。它不一定是物質財產，但會像遺產一樣繼續影響後來的人。","examples":[{"en":"Her work left a lasting legacy in public health.","zh":"她的工作在公共衛生領域留下了持久的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scholarship fund is her most enduring legacy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a708df92c9e46229e8f1","word":"legal","forms":["legal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b2091110f0d5720","term":"legal","forms":["legal","more legal","most legal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"法律相關的","explanation":"表示事情與法律、律師或法律程式有關，重點是“屬於法律領域”，不一定說明事情本身已經獲法律許可。","examples":[{"en":"She sought legal advice before signing the contract.","zh":"她在籤合同前尋求了法律諮詢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dispute may end in a legal battle.","zh":"這場爭端可能會以法律訴訟收場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d45502952cb521b","term":"legal","forms":["legal","more legal","most legal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有法律依據的","explanation":"強調某項權利、主張或做法的依據來自法律，而不只是碰巧與法律領域有關。","examples":[{"en":"The court found no legal basis for the claim.","zh":"法院認定這項主張沒有法律依據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tenant sought legal grounds to challenge eviction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9b77e726256faee","term":"legal","forms":["legal","more legal","most legal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"法律允許的","explanation":"表示某事由法律建立、許可、要求或規定，因此處在法律認可的範圍內；這是最接近“合法”的常見用法。","examples":[{"en":"It is legal to vote at eighteen in this country.","zh":"在這個國家，十八歲可以合法投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is overnight camping legal on this beach?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba29297b6c4f8486cb3f","word":"legend","forms":["legend"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-200dc8a5da3eb253","term":"legend","forms":["legend","legends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聖徒傳記；傳奇故事","explanation":"最早，legend指講述聖徒生平的故事；這些故事往往經過誇飾，因此後來也可泛指帶有傳奇色彩的故事。","examples":[{"en":"The legend of the old king has been told for centuries.","zh":"老國王的傳說已經流傳了幾個世紀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book retells a legend about a brave young sailor.","zh":"這本書重新講述了一個關於勇敢年輕水手的傳奇故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73f505e22cb0b7f6","term":"legend","forms":["legend","legends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳奇故事","explanation":"legend可以指描述過去事件、但帶有誇張或不現實成分的故事；它不一定完全虛構，也可能包含真實歷史。","examples":[{"en":"The legend of Troy may contain some real history.","zh":"特洛伊的傳說可能包含一些真實的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local children still enjoy the legend of the hidden treasure.","zh":"當地孩子仍然喜歡那個關於隱藏寶藏的傳說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8884711dfe32cbcc","term":"legend","forms":["legend","legends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳奇人物","explanation":"因為一個人常被講述、成就非凡或影響深遠，legend也可指這樣的人，意思接近“傳奇人物”。","examples":[{"en":"The coach is a legend in the world of basketball.","zh":"這位教練是籃球界的傳奇人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a legend after winning the race against all odds.","zh":"她在極其不利的情況下贏得比賽後，成了傳奇人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f61e4e48a0a3ce63d684","word":"legendary","forms":["legendary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdadbb482dfd9d84","term":"legendary","forms":["legendary","more legendary","most legendary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其出色的；傳奇級的","explanation":"在日常口語中常表示“好得不可思議、厲害到會被人講很多年”，是從“足以寫進傳說”發展出來的誇張讚美。","examples":[{"en":"That last-minute goal was legendary.","zh":"那個最後時刻的進球太傳奇了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is legendary for her generosity and courage.","zh":"她因慷慨和勇氣而成為傳奇人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legendary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ed9acb26623db9b","term":"legendary","forms":["legendary","more legendary","most legendary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傳說中的；與傳說有關的","explanation":"指存在於傳說、故事或民間敘述中的人、動物、地方或事件，重點是它與傳說這一類故事有關。","examples":[{"en":"The legendary hero is said to have defeated a whole army alone.","zh":"據說那位傳說中的英雄曾獨自擊敗一整支軍隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sailors searched for a legendary island of gold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legendary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b7b13bc416f7216aeca","word":"legislation","forms":["legislation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23cf061897287dc6","term":"legislation","forms":["legislation","legislations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立法；制定法律","explanation":"指制定、討論和透過法律的整個過程，也就是把社會規則正式寫成法律的活動。","examples":[{"en":"Parliament passed legislation to protect renters.","zh":"議會透過了保護租戶的立法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government is preparing legislation on data privacy.","zh":"政府正在準備有關資料隱私的立法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legislation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-626577f95b6542e2","term":"legislation","forms":["legislation","legislations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"已透過的法律；法律條文總稱","explanation":"指立法機關已經制定並透過的一項法律或一組法律，是“立法過程”產生的正式規則。","examples":[{"en":"The company must comply with environmental legislation.","zh":"這家公司必須遵守環境法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Existing legislation already prohibits dumping waste there.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legislation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07f12cbc2ab5135c72ba","word":"legislative","forms":["legislative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e48cd508929e1c1","term":"legislative","forms":["legislative","more legislative","most legislative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"立法的；制定法律的","explanation":"指制定法律的行為、權力、機構或檔案，核心意思就是“造法律的”。","examples":[{"en":"The committee proposed a legislative act to protect public parks.","zh":"委員會提出了一項保護公共公園的立法法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constitution separates legislative and executive powers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legislative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-43b910c2766295e66ab3","word":"legislator","forms":["legislator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b13459a081eccceb","term":"legislator","forms":["legislator","legislators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立法者；議員","explanation":"指有權提出、制定或透過法律的人，通常是在議會中代表公眾參與立法的議員。記住“把社會規則寫進法律的人”這一形象，就能理解這個詞的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The legislator introduced a bill to improve public transportation.","zh":"這位立法者提出了一項改善公共交通的法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several legislators opposed the new tax proposal.","zh":"幾位議員反對這項新的稅收提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legislator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3ad0ec5b9dd0e5669dd7","word":"legitimate","forms":["legitimate"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90ad64b3c339c355","term":"legitimate","forms":["legitimate","more legitimate","most legitimate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合法的；符合法律要求的","explanation":"指某件事得到法律允許，或按照正式的法律程式和要求進行，就像蓋有法律印章一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The referee ruled that it was a legitimate challenge.","zh":"裁判判定這是一次合法的搶斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company has a legitimate license to operate here.","zh":"這家公司擁有在這裡經營的合法許可證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legitimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6479c76aa34bbb99","term":"legitimate","forms":["legitimate","more legitimate","most legitimate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合理的；有效的；符合規則的","explanation":"指觀點、方法、理由等符合已知原則或公認標準，因此在邏輯或規則上站得住腳，不一定涉及法律。","examples":[{"en":"You have a legitimate reason to be concerned.","zh":"你有充分的理由感到擔心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That is a legitimate question, not a complaint.","zh":"那是一個合理的問題，不是在抱怨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legitimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb77cbf2db98387d","term":"legitimate","forms":["legitimate","more legitimate","most legitimate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真實的；正品的；可信的","explanation":"指某物確實是真的、不是偽造的，也可指某人的身份或說法可信；它從“得到正式承認”進一步發展為“真實可靠”。","examples":[{"en":"Is this a legitimate website or a scam?","zh":"這是正規真實的網站，還是詐騙網站？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dealer provided proof that the painting was legitimate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/legitimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00ed6c583d74e36528fe","word":"leisure","forms":["leisure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2dc2ef219ede8181","term":"leisure","forms":["leisure","leisures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擺脫事務後的自由","explanation":"指工作或其他責任停止後獲得的自由狀態：人不再被事務牽著走，可以自己決定如何安排時間。這是“開啟一扇門、從事務中抽身”的一面，重點在獲得了自由。","examples":[{"en":"After the project ended, she finally had leisure to choose her own schedule.","zh":"專案結束後，她終於有了按自己安排日程的自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Retirement finally gave her leisure to study painting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leisure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa192a9a99d2ec9e","term":"leisure","forms":["leisure","leisures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"閒暇時間","explanation":"指沒有工作或職責佔用的空閒時間，是leisure最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。它可以用來休息，也可以用來讀書、運動或做其他自己選擇的事情。","examples":[{"en":"He spends his leisure time reading in the park.","zh":"他在閒暇時間喜歡在公園裡讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum offers activities for children during their leisure.","zh":"博物館為孩子們的閒暇時間提供活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leisure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d507792dd54a49ce0d0","word":"leisurely","forms":["leisurely"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-159003056c4982a4","term":"leisurely","forms":["leisurely","more leisurely","most leisurely"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悠閒的；從容的","explanation":"形容人、行動或節奏不急不忙，彷彿有充足時間慢慢享受過程；重點是從容的狀態，而不只是沒有事情可做。","examples":[{"en":"We had a leisurely breakfast by the river.","zh":"我們在河邊悠閒地吃了一頓早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We enjoyed a leisurely breakfast beside the pool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leisurely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-602430345f6f7221","term":"leisurely","forms":["leisurely","more leisurely","most leisurely"],"pos":"adv","zh":"悠閒地；從容地","explanation":"說明某個動作是在不趕時間、心情放鬆的狀態下完成的，就像一邊散步一邊享受周圍環境。","examples":[{"en":"She leisurely browsed the stalls at the market.","zh":"她悠閒地逛著市場裡的攤位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They strolled leisurely through the botanical gardens.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leisurely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f464d7d71c06e47a535c","word":"lemon","forms":["lemon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c80f1938a0f2575","term":"lemon","forms":["lemon","lemons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檸檬","explanation":"指一種黃色、味酸的柑橘類水果，也可以泛指這種水果或它產生的汁液。","examples":[{"en":"Cut a lemon in half and squeeze it over the fish.","zh":"把一個檸檬切成兩半，擠汁淋在魚上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like lemon in your tea?","zh":"你的茶裡要加檸檬嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13cc358c604102b8449c","word":"lemonade","forms":["lemonade"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af9da8e82e981065","term":"lemonade","forms":["lemonade","lemonades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檸檬水","explanation":"在加拿大、印度、菲律賓和美國等地，lemonade 通常是用水、檸檬和糖等甜味劑調成的清涼飲料，有時會加冰。","examples":[{"en":"We sat outside and drank cold lemonade after the hike.","zh":"徒步後，我們坐在外面喝冰涼的檸檬水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could I have a glass of lemonade, please?","zh":"請給我一杯檸檬水，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemonade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21df2f4d52a38916","term":"lemonade","forms":["lemonade","lemonades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檸檬味汽水","explanation":"在英國、澳大利亞和紐西蘭等地，lemonade 通常指透明、一般帶氣泡的檸檬味甜飲料，可以由檸檬製成，也可以使用人工檸檬香味。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a can of lemonade from the vending machine.","zh":"她從自動售貨機買了一罐檸檬味汽水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The British pub served lemonade with ice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemonade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d59b2b96755e2c6e7ec","word":"lend","forms":["lend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90e05b6dd61c0789","term":"lend","forms":["lend","lends","lending","lent"],"pos":"verb","zh":"借給；暫時給……使用","explanation":"把自己擁有的東西暫時交給別人使用，並期待東西本身或等價物之後回來。重點是方向：東西從你這裡流向別人，所以 lend 是“借出、借給”。","examples":[{"en":"Could you lend me your umbrella for a few minutes?","zh":"你能把雨傘借給我幾分鐘嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I lent my brother my bike for the weekend.","zh":"我把腳踏車借給哥哥週末用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4a9c1e6b577a32b","term":"lend","forms":["lend","lends","lending","lent"],"pos":"verb","zh":"適合；適用於","explanation":"這裡不是實際把東西借出去，而是把“提供給別人使用”的畫面引申為：某事物很適合某種活動、處理方式或用途。","examples":[{"en":"This simple recipe lends itself to many variations.","zh":"這個簡單的食譜很適合做出各種變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room lends itself to small musical performances.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f82aca66af91493b1ff","word":"length","forms":["length"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0da5f7ffc1299352","term":"length","forms":["length","lengths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長度","explanation":"指物體沿最長方向，從一端到另一端的距離，也就是通常所說的長度。","examples":[{"en":"The length of the table is two meters.","zh":"這張桌子的長度是兩米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Measure the length of the room before buying the carpet.","zh":"買地毯前先量一下房間的長度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/length","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9fc1bed66fdf6ca","term":"length","forms":["length","lengths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持續時間","explanation":"把時間看成從開始延伸到結束的距離，因此 length 也表示某件事持續了多久或一段時間有多長。","examples":[{"en":"The length of the meeting was nearly two hours.","zh":"這次會議持續了將近兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film is enjoyable despite its length.","zh":"這部電影雖然時間很長，但仍然很好看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/length","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fac5bf622ac077a","term":"length","forms":["length","lengths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總體長度或篇幅","explanation":"指某件事物在長度、時間或篇幅上的總體延伸程度；因此可以說書、演講或文章的 length，強調它總體有多長。","examples":[{"en":"The length of the report makes it difficult to read in one sitting.","zh":"這份報告篇幅太長，很難一次讀完。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We were surprised by the length of the discussion.","zh":"我們對討論持續了這麼久感到驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/length","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aeb65b6d2de598b0b537","word":"lengthen","forms":["lengthen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cac7728ed6f4b0c3","term":"lengthen","forms":["lengthen","lengthens","lengthening","lengthened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變長；延長","explanation":"表示主動把某物拉長、延長或增加其篇幅，重點是有一個施動者讓長度發生變化。物件可以是實際的東西，也可以是故事、文章或時間段等抽象物件。","examples":[{"en":"The editor asked me to lengthen the article with more background information.","zh":"編輯讓我補充更多背景資訊，把文章寫長一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They lengthened the table by adding another section.","zh":"他們加上一塊板，把桌子加長了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lengthen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e9a91efccb4c47e","term":"lengthen","forms":["lengthen","lengthens","lengthening","lengthened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變長；延長","explanation":"表示某物自身的長度、篇幅或持續範圍逐漸增加，不強調誰主動使它變化。常見於影子、白晝、道路、故事等隨著時間或發展而變長的情況。","examples":[{"en":"The shadows lengthened across the street as evening approached.","zh":"傍晚臨近時，影子在街道上越拉越長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Summer days lengthen noticeably as the solstice approaches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lengthen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-861c2ae802b8e8cb0a35","word":"lengthy","forms":["lengthy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd9d38833bf2bb44","term":"lengthy","forms":["lengthy","lengthier","lengthiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冗長的；持續很久的","explanation":"表示時間、文章篇幅或某個過程被拉得很長，往往長到讓人覺得不必要或有些拖沓。它的重點通常不是物體的空間尺寸，而是“花的時間多”或“佔的篇幅大”。","examples":[{"en":"The report is accurate but rather lengthy.","zh":"這份報告很準確，但篇幅相當長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a lengthy delay, the train finally arrived.","zh":"經過長時間的延誤，火車終於到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lengthy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e47b154e0b50f73","term":"lengthy","forms":["lengthy","lengthier","lengthiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"說話或寫作冗長的","explanation":"形容一個人說話、佈道或寫作持續很久、內容鋪陳過多，聽者或讀者容易覺得沒完沒了。這是“被拉得很長”的線從時間和篇幅進一步延伸到表達方式。","examples":[{"en":"The speaker was knowledgeable but too lengthy for a short meeting.","zh":"這位發言人很有知識，但對一場短會來說講得太久了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His lengthy reply filled five handwritten pages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lengthy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-812b9215cd2f0e7ea41f","word":"lens","forms":["lens"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc44edd6162fdb9d","term":"lens","forms":["lens","lenses","lentes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光學透鏡","explanation":"指能讓透過的光線聚焦或散開的物體，通常由玻璃等透明材料製成。照相機、眼鏡和顯微鏡等裝置都可能使用不同型別的lens。","examples":[{"en":"This camera has a wide-angle lens for taking landscape photos.","zh":"這臺相機配有一個用於拍攝風景照的廣角鏡頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lens focuses the light onto the sensor.","zh":"透鏡把光線聚焦到感測器上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lens","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3fae7aac7be9b18","term":"lens","forms":["lens","lenses","lentes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀察視角","explanation":"引申義是看待某件事的方式或角度，好像透過一塊透鏡來選擇、放大或改變所看到的內容。它常用於討論媒體、社會問題和個人判斷。","examples":[{"en":"She examines the issue through the lens of public health.","zh":"她從公共衛生的角度審視這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She examines migration through the lens of family history.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lens","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-359f7793cbd65f175164","word":"leopard","forms":["leopard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c415d6be4aca8db","term":"leopard","forms":["leopard","leopards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豹","explanation":"leopard最核心的意思是豹：一種生活在非洲和亞洲、毛皮上有斑點的大型野生貓科動物。記住“斑點的野貓”這個形象，就能自然理解它在故事、新聞和動物介紹中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"A leopard crossed the road just before dawn.","zh":"黎明前，一隻豹穿過了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leopard dragged its prey into a tree.","zh":"那隻豹把獵物拖到了一棵樹上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leopard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33095ce8dc7c2f84","term":"leopard","forms":["leopard","leopards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"以豹命名的相似大型貓科動物","explanation":"在複合名稱中，leopard還可以泛指外形像豹、因而借用“豹”來命名的其他大型野生貓科動物。這裡的重點不是它一定屬於通常所說的豹，而是它有相似的外觀或斑紋。","examples":[{"en":"The snow leopard lives high in the mountains of Central Asia.","zh":"雪豹生活在中亞的高山地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The snow leopard disappeared among the rocks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leopard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f6a9dcb187642124f208","word":"lesbian","forms":["lesbian"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c536994ac4ad230","term":"lesbian","forms":["lesbian","more lesbian","most lesbian"],"pos":"adj","zh":"女同性戀的","explanation":"指女性只或主要以女性為戀愛或性關係物件的；也可描述具有這種性取向的女性。","examples":[{"en":"Many lesbian women find support in local community groups.","zh":"許多女同性戀女性從當地社群組織中獲得支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She came out as lesbian in college.","zh":"她在大學期間公開了自己的女同性戀身份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lesbian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0d68e52e00c436a","term":"lesbian","forms":["lesbian","more lesbian","most lesbian"],"pos":"adj","zh":"女性同性戀之間的","explanation":"描述發生在兩個或多個女性之間、並帶有同性戀性質的關係、婚姻、親吻等。","examples":[{"en":"They have been in a lesbian relationship for five years.","zh":"她們的女性同性戀關係已經維持五年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel portrays a lesbian relationship with warmth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lesbian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4fdd3b6201a22c7814d6","word":"less","forms":["less"],"officialPos":"pron./adv./adj./prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b5dbb320963a705","term":"less","forms":["less"],"pos":"adv","zh":"較少；不如以前多","explanation":"這是 little 的比較形式，表示某種數量或程度比另一時間、另一情況或另一項更少。","examples":[{"en":"I slept less last night than I did the night before.","zh":"我昨晚的睡眠比前晚少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to worry less and enjoy the trip.","zh":"儘量少擔心，多享受這次旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/less","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f08fb7522f43e6f","term":"less","forms":["less"],"pos":"adv","zh":"較不……","explanation":"放在形容詞或副詞前，表示某人或某事具有較低程度的某種特徵，即“不那麼……”。","examples":[{"en":"This route is less dangerous than the old one.","zh":"這條路線沒有舊路線那麼危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He seemed less anxious after hearing the explanation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/less","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33bc3cb17d6909ed","term":"less","forms":["less"],"pos":"det","zh":"較少的；不那麼多的","explanation":"放在不可數名詞前，表示某種物質、時間、金錢或抽象事物的量比另一項少。","examples":[{"en":"We need less time to finish the second task.","zh":"完成第二項任務我們需要的時間更少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent less money this month.","zh":"她這個月花的錢更少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/less","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-542500079b091fb753a6","word":"lessen","forms":["lessen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f502f066a91d20b8","term":"lessen","forms":["lessen","lessens","lessening","lessened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使減輕；使減少","explanation":"把某種數量、痛苦、負擔或影響調低，使它沒有原來那麼強。這就像把音量旋鈕往下擰，重點是“讓它變小”，而不是把它完全消除。","examples":[{"en":"A short walk may lessen your back pain.","zh":"短暫散步可能會減輕你的背痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new rule is intended to lessen the burden on small businesses.","zh":"這項新規定旨在減輕小企業的負擔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lessen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5b7db23866d76a7","term":"lessen","forms":["lessen","lessens","lessening","lessened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變少；減弱","explanation":"某種程度、感覺或影響不需要明確的施動者，自己逐漸變小或變弱。畫面仍然是音量旋鈕慢慢向下，而不是有人主動去擰它。","examples":[{"en":"Her anxiety gradually lessened after she spoke to her doctor.","zh":"她和醫生談過之後，焦慮逐漸減輕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pressure lessened as the aircraft descended.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lessen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b78e58750d4f05fb33ff","word":"lesson","forms":["lesson"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3fb36740b5037db","term":"lesson","forms":["lesson","lessons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一節課","explanation":"把較大的學習內容劃出一段來，由老師講授或由學生學習，這一段就是 lesson。它可以是學校裡按時間安排的一節課，也可以泛指一次有組織的教學活動。","examples":[{"en":"We have an English lesson after lunch.","zh":"我們午飯後有一節英語課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Today's lesson is about healthy eating.","zh":"今天這節課講健康飲食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lesson","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f35669dec69f6db5","term":"lesson","forms":["lesson","lessons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"從經歷中學到的東西","explanation":"lesson 可以是一個人從書本、自然或親身經歷中得到的認識：經歷彷彿又劃出了一“課”，告訴你以後該怎麼做。","examples":[{"en":"The mistake taught me an important lesson about planning.","zh":"這次錯誤讓我明白了計劃的重要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nature can teach us many lessons.","zh":"大自然能教給我們許多道理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lesson","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba0b201fb157cf636bbc","word":"lest","forms":["lest"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"lest","forms":["lest"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"以免；唯恐","examples":[{"en":"She spoke quietly lest she wake the baby.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"He checked the address twice lest the parcel go to the wrong house.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-5654d4106d7025c25788","word":"let","forms":["let"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6125f2360bcbb749","term":"let","forms":["let","lets","letting","leet","letten","lettest","letteth"],"pos":"verb","zh":"允許某人做某事","explanation":"表示不阻止某人做某事，相當於把行動的門開啟；這是 let 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"My parents let me stay up late on weekends.","zh":"我父母允許我週末晚點睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please let the children play outside.","zh":"請讓孩子們在外面玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/let","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9394dad1c83471e","term":"let","forms":["let","lets","letting","leet","letten","lettest","letteth"],"pos":"verb","zh":"別干涉；任其保持原樣","explanation":"表示允許某人或某事按原樣存在，不去打擾、控制或插手；所以 let me be 是“別煩我、讓我待著”。","examples":[{"en":"I'm tired—just let me be for a while.","zh":"我累了——先讓我安靜一會兒，別打擾我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let the sleeping dog be.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/let","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15acd758113abb6f","term":"let","forms":["let","lets","letting","leet","letten","lettest","letteth"],"pos":"verb","zh":"讓我們……；請允許我……","explanation":"用於引出第一人稱或第三人稱的祈使結構：Let's … 通常表示提議“讓我們……”，Let me … 可表示請求“讓我……”。它把“允許”縮成一個直接推動行動的表達。","examples":[{"en":"Let's take a short break before the next meeting.","zh":"我們在下次會議前先休息一會兒吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let me check the address for you.","zh":"我來幫你核對一下地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/let","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6fcba40fce82b7dba02","word":"lethal","forms":["lethal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d7597f96d38c71a","term":"lethal","forms":["lethal","more lethal","most lethal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"致命的","explanation":"指某種東西、行為或情況能夠導致死亡；核心畫面就是“把人帶到死亡邊緣，甚至直接造成死亡”。","examples":[{"en":"Even a small dose can be lethal.","zh":"即使是少量劑量也可能致命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new weapon is far more lethal than the old one.","zh":"這種新武器的殺傷力比舊武器強得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lethal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f80105efab6d863fd8fc","word":"letter","forms":["letter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d453b34d904fdfec","term":"letter","forms":["letter","letters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"字母","explanation":"字母表中的一個符號，用來記錄語言中的聲音或組成單詞；它是“文字”這個核心概念最小的單位。","examples":[{"en":"The word has five letters.","zh":"這個詞有五個字母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write your name in capital letters.","zh":"請用大寫字母寫你的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/letter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5037a520c68efad2","term":"letter","forms":["letter","letters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書信","explanation":"寫給某人的一段較完整、通常比便條正式的文字；它是把許多字母和單片語織起來傳達訊息。","examples":[{"en":"I wrote a letter to my sister about my new job.","zh":"我給姐姐寫了一封信，講了講我的新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her letter arrived two days later.","zh":"她的信兩天後寄到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/letter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27b393a57980d0c2","term":"letter","forms":["letter","letters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"字面含義","explanation":"指一句話或一條規則寫在紙面上的直接意思，不包括說話者更深或更實際的意圖；因此常與“精神”相對。","examples":[{"en":"They followed the letter of the agreement but ignored its purpose.","zh":"他們遵守了協議的字面規定，卻忽視了協議的目的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The policy follows the letter of the law.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/letter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48695422fbc25ad01b63","word":"lettuce","forms":["lettuce"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d666133c7918f4ed","term":"lettuce","forms":["lettuce","lettuces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生菜植物","explanation":"指生菜這一類可食用的綠葉植物，通常有一團層層包裹的葉子，顏色可以是綠色或紫色。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a fresh head of lettuce at the market.","zh":"我在市場買了一棵新鮮的生菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lettuce is growing well in the garden.","zh":"園裡的生菜長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lettuce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f43d1398eca605a3","term":"lettuce","forms":["lettuce","lettuces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生菜葉；生菜這道食物","explanation":"指從生菜植株上取下、作為蔬菜食用的葉子，也可以指用生菜葉做成或拌入其他食材的食物。","examples":[{"en":"Could you add some lettuce to my sandwich?","zh":"你能在我的三明治里加些生菜嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add lettuce after the burgers finish cooking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lettuce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0081779c287d567d9ca6","word":"level","forms":["level"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8df34e6016e4a5de","term":"level","forms":["level","leveler","leveller","levelest","levellest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平的；水平的","explanation":"想象一條水平參考線：物體各處都與這條線齊平，沒有高低傾斜，就是 level。","examples":[{"en":"The shelf is not level, so the books keep sliding to one side.","zh":"這塊擱板不平，所以書總是滑向一邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check that the shelf is level before tightening the screws.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/level","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcec55ede9f7cfd7","term":"level","forms":["level","levels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"程度；數量水平","explanation":"表示某種事物達到的程度或數量，好像它線上上的某個位置；可以是高、低，也可以是不斷變化的中間水平。","examples":[{"en":"The noise level in the office becomes unbearable after lunch.","zh":"辦公室裡的噪聲水平在午飯後變得讓人難以忍受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise can lower your stress levels.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以降低你的壓力水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/level","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb5ade971413a9ab","term":"level","forms":["level","levels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊戲中的等級","explanation":"在角色扮演等遊戲中，表示角色或其他元素的數值等級；等級越高，通常代表能力、挑戰資格或可進行的內容越多。它可以看成角色在遊戲進度線上所處的位置。","examples":[{"en":"My character reached level twenty after completing the mountain quest.","zh":"我的角色完成山地任務後升到了二十級。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reached level forty after defeating the dragon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/level","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5fd94b8c335618802e8","word":"liability","forms":["liability"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6a65982c74e395f","term":"liability","forms":["liability","liabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律或金錢上的責任、債務","explanation":"指某人或某機構必須向別人承擔的責任、債務或賠償義務，像一筆必須背在身上的重量。它既可以指具體的一項債務，也可以泛指承擔責任的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The company accepted liability for the damage.","zh":"這家公司承認對這起損壞負有賠償責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contract limits our liability to the amount paid.","zh":"合同把我們的賠償責任限制在已支付的金額以內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-099517092cea8221","term":"liability","forms":["liability","liabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拖累或增加風險的人、事物","explanation":"指會拖慢進展、增加照料負擔或讓別人承擔更大風險的人或事物。它仍然保留“別人不得不揹負的重量”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"If he cannot keep the information private, he will become a liability to the team.","zh":"如果他不能保守資訊秘密，就會成為團隊的負擔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old equipment is now more of a liability than an asset.","zh":"這套舊裝置如今更像是負擔，而不是資產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6001162b99d373ae52e3","word":"liable","forms":["liable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7fdc73c20ab9d70a","term":"liable","forms":["liable","more liable","most liable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"依法負責","explanation":"指某人或某機構依法必須為債務、損失或其他後果承擔責任，也就是法律上能夠被追責。這個義項體現的是“被法律綁住”。","examples":[{"en":"The company is liable for the damage caused by its contractor.","zh":"這家公司要為承包商造成的損失承擔責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A court will decide whether the manufacturer is liable for the injury.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c37ed64902d22b79","term":"liable","forms":["liable","more liable","most liable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很可能；容易","explanation":"表示某事很可能發生，或某人、某物容易處於某種狀態，通常帶有不好的結果。這裡不是說已經承擔責任，而是說被某種可能性牽引著。","examples":[{"en":"The path is liable to become slippery after rain.","zh":"下雨後這條小路很容易變滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These old pipes are liable to freeze in winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30e9190d7fdfc50d3621","word":"liar","forms":["liar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4d81da98ee65e85","term":"liar","forms":["liar","liars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說謊者","explanation":"指經常說謊的人，也可以指剛剛說了謊、因此被指責的人。這個詞通常暗示說話者不信任對方，或認為對方不誠實。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone knows he is a liar, so nobody trusts his promises.","zh":"大家都知道他是個說謊者，所以沒人相信他的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She called me a liar, but I had the message to prove it.","zh":"她說我是個說謊者，但我有訊息可以證明自己說的是真的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-559359f07850f1bc717d","word":"liberal","forms":["liberal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14206ac82f3c31a7","term":"liberal","forms":["liberal","more liberal","most liberal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"慷慨的；大方的","explanation":"指願意給很多、給得很大方，也可指不吝惜讚美、時間或幫助。核心畫面是那扇門開得很大，別人可以得到充足的東西。","examples":[{"en":"Our neighbor was liberal with her advice when we moved into the area.","zh":"我們搬到這附近時，鄰居毫不吝惜地給了我們許多建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is liberal with praise when someone does a good job.","zh":"有人工作出色時，他總是不吝讚美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-785499673892866c","term":"liberal","forms":["liberal","more liberal","most liberal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"思想開放的；寬容的","explanation":"指願意接受新想法，不拘泥於傳統規範，也較允許他人按不同方式生活。它把“門開得很大”從物質慷慨延伸到了觀念和社會習慣。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents had liberal ideas about education and let her choose her own subjects.","zh":"她的父母在教育問題上思想開放，讓她自己選擇學習科目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a liberal policy on photography.","zh":"這家博物館對拍照採取較為寬鬆的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5475bee3c1057bd","term":"liberal","forms":["liberal","more liberal","most liberal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"支援自由與改革的","explanation":"在政治和社會語境中，指支援個人自由、社會變化或改革的立場。它就是“把舊門開啟，讓更多選擇進入公共生活”的政治化用法，但不同國家對這一標籤的具體理解並不完全相同。","examples":[{"en":"The candidate is known for liberal views on immigration and civil rights.","zh":"這位候選人在移民和公民權利問題上以持自由派觀點而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new law was welcomed by liberal groups.","zh":"自由派團體歡迎這項新法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fb7120ca39aba6119b9","word":"liberate","forms":["liberate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d147ab66a01e266","term":"liberate","forms":["liberate","liberates","liberating","liberated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解放；釋放","explanation":"指使人擺脫監禁、壓迫、控制或其他束縛，回到自由狀態。這是 liberate 最核心、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team liberated the hostages from the abandoned building.","zh":"救援隊把人質從那座廢棄建築中解救了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reform gave workers more freedom and liberated them from unfair rules.","zh":"這項改革給工人更多自由，使他們擺脫了不公平的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a59050636774d4d","term":"liberate","forms":["liberate","liberates","liberating","liberated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解放（奪取敵方地區）","explanation":"在戰爭或政治語境中，指從敵方或佔領者手中奪取城市、地區等人口聚集地，並把這一行動稱為“解放”。這個詞常帶有官方或委婉色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The army claimed that it had liberated the town from the occupying forces.","zh":"軍隊聲稱自己已把這座城鎮從佔領軍手中解放出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Allied troops liberated the town after fierce fighting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4075864ad5e7545961d","word":"liberation","forms":["liberation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-07224a63112fd381","term":"liberation","forms":["liberation","liberations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解放；獲釋","explanation":"指使人或群體擺脫囚禁、統治、控制等束縛的行動，也可以指擺脫束縛後所處的自由狀態；重點是“從鎖住的門後出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The liberation of the prisoners took several months.","zh":"這些囚犯的獲釋花了好幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town celebrated its liberation from military rule.","zh":"這個城鎮慶祝擺脫軍事統治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-737623f6a7daef01","term":"liberation","forms":["liberation","liberations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭取平等與擺脫壓迫","explanation":"指個人或群體爭取平等權利和社會地位、擺脫長期制度性或歷史性壓迫的過程，像是共同把一扇長期鎖住的門開啟。","examples":[{"en":"The movement fought for women's liberation.","zh":"這場運動為婦女解放而鬥爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign for national liberation drew support from workers and students.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f41f2c785e15ca0c3fa8","word":"liberty","forms":["liberty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c615c69a0d9c9c97","term":"liberty","forms":["liberty","liberties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自由狀態","explanation":"liberty表示不受束縛、能夠自主生活和行動的狀態，是“自由”這一核心概念的正式說法。","examples":[{"en":"The new law protects liberty for all citizens.","zh":"這項新法律保護所有公民的自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoners regained their liberty after the peace agreement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa0415bbf25c8585","term":"liberty","forms":["liberty","liberties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"免於監禁和強迫","explanation":"這裡的liberty特指從監禁、奴役或強迫勞動中解脫出來，強調重新獲得人身自由。","examples":[{"en":"After ten years in prison, he finally regained his liberty.","zh":"在監獄裡待了十年後，他終於重新獲得了人身自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoners demanded the restoration of their liberty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8592c6f9d3932917","term":"liberty","forms":["liberty","liberties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自主行動、信仰和表達的自由","explanation":"liberty也指人在法律和社會中按自己的意願行動、相信某種觀點或表達意見的權利，常與權利和安全並列。","examples":[{"en":"The constitution guarantees the liberty to express political opinions.","zh":"憲法保障表達政治觀點的自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constitution protects liberty of belief and expression.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liberty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c445e1c04df4e247c20","word":"librarian","forms":["librarian"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7aa56fe19dc2cc19","term":"librarian","forms":["librarian","librarians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圖書館負責人","explanation":"指負責管理圖書館整體事務的人，包括館藏、服務和日常運營；這是最能代表這個詞的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The librarian showed us how to use the new reading room.","zh":"圖書館員向我們演示瞭如何使用新的閱覽室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chief librarian approved the purchase of new reference books.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/librarian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2da4b54fd32dd22","term":"librarian","forms":["librarian","librarians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"館藏管理人員","explanation":"指在圖書館照料書籍、檔案和其他出版物的人，可以是正式員工，也可以是志願者；重點是維護和管理館藏。","examples":[{"en":"A volunteer librarian sorted the donated books by subject.","zh":"一名志願圖書館員按主題整理了捐贈的書籍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The librarian cataloged the newly donated manuscripts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/librarian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b718f1354f7247312eca","word":"library","forms":["library"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a017d948c6f5538","term":"library","forms":["library","libraries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圖書館","explanation":"供公眾或特定人群查閱、借閱書籍和其他資料的機構，通常還提供閱讀、檢索等服務。","examples":[{"en":"I returned the books to the library before it closed.","zh":"我在圖書館關門前還回了那些書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library offers free computer access to residents.","zh":"這家圖書館為居民提供免費的電腦使用服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/library","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13e485f018734a27","term":"library","forms":["library","libraries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書籍或資料的收藏","explanation":"指集中收藏的一批書或其他資訊資料，不一定是一個機構，也不一定放在專門的建築裡。","examples":[{"en":"She has built a small library of books about local history.","zh":"她收集了一小批關於地方歷史的書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive contains a valuable library of maps.","zh":"這份檔案收藏了大量有價值的地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/library","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc1d3b0234846714b0ae","word":"license","forms":["license"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7c0fb41e0f3b136","term":"license","forms":["license","licenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"許可證；許可","explanation":"指政府或其他有權機構正式發出的許可檔案，拿到它就可以合法做某件事，例如駕駛、捕魚、經營或從事某種職業。","examples":[{"en":"You need a license to sell alcohol in this state.","zh":"在這個州銷售酒類需要許可證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She renewed her fishing license before the season began.","zh":"捕魚季開始前，她更新了自己的捕魚許可證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/license","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-065ab62c69454b19","term":"license","forms":["license","licenses","licensing","licensed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式授權","explanation":"表示由有權機構正式授予某人資格或許可，使其可以合法從事某項活動。","examples":[{"en":"She is licensed to practice medicine in three states.","zh":"她獲准在三個州行醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency licenses inspectors to examine public buildings.","zh":"該機構授權檢查員檢查公共建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/license","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c13f6fd6f97586cbd03","word":"lick","forms":["lick"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9f12d0ef6e3e008","term":"lick","forms":["lick","licks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舔一下","explanation":"指用舌頭舔的一個動作，重點是一次短暫的舔。","examples":[{"en":"The cat gave its paw a quick lick.","zh":"貓迅速舔了一下自己的爪子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took one lick of the spoon.","zh":"他舔了一下勺子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bd362ad1f4a1195","term":"lick","forms":["lick","licks","licking","licked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"舔","explanation":"用舌頭接觸並掃過某物，通常是為了清潔、取食或感受味道。","examples":[{"en":"The dog licked my hand.","zh":"那隻狗舔了我的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child licked the melting ice cream.","zh":"孩子舔著正在融化的冰淇淋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-540cec543c6a8b0b","term":"lick","forms":["lick","licks","licking","licked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"舔食或舔淨","explanation":"用舌頭把液體、食物等一點點舔進去，或把附著在表面的東西舔乾淨。","examples":[{"en":"She licked the honey off the spoon.","zh":"她把勺子上的蜂蜜舔乾淨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy licked up the spilled milk.","zh":"小狗把灑出來的牛奶舔掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98fbb7ef60124ed0c3bb","word":"lid","forms":["lid"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edcacd7a27e04bd9","term":"lid","forms":["lid","lids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"容器蓋","explanation":"指放在盒子、鍋、杯子等容器上面，用來覆蓋或封住容器的部分。這是 lid 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the lid back on the pot.","zh":"請把鍋蓋蓋回去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't find the lid for this box.","zh":"我找不到這個盒子的蓋子了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7e6e1aed04a2848","term":"lid","forms":["lid","lids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制；控制","explanation":"引申義是給某件事蓋上蓋子，使它不能繼續擴大、公開或失控，因此表示壓制、限制或控制某事。","examples":[{"en":"The manager tried to put a lid on the rumors.","zh":"經理試圖壓下這些傳言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to keep a lid on spending this month.","zh":"這個月我們得控制開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8b1a1a3e6bcee8660ad","word":"lie","forms":["lie"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a69cb7dadde74a0d","term":"lie","forms":["lie","lies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"姿勢或相對位置","explanation":"指人或物所處的姿勢、方向或相對位置，也就是“怎樣躺著或處在哪裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The dog changed its lie beside the fire.","zh":"狗在火爐旁換了個躺臥姿勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lie of the fallen tree blocked the footpath.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70de55b60beb100c","term":"lie","forms":["lie","lies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"謊言","explanation":"指明知不真實卻故意說出來、用來欺騙別人的話；它是“說謊”這一行為留下的虛假說法。","examples":[{"en":"She told a lie about where she had been.","zh":"她對自己去過哪裡撒了謊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child admitted that his story was a lie.","zh":"那個孩子承認自己的說法是謊言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea02ed50bcc3b138","term":"lie","forms":["lie","lies","lying","lay","laid","lain","lien","lyest","layst","lyeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"躺著","explanation":"指人或物以水平姿勢停留在某個表面上，是“處在一個躺臥位置”的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"The keys lie on the kitchen table.","zh":"鑰匙放在廚房桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He lay on the sofa all afternoon.","zh":"他整個下午都躺在沙發上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9cc4db458cb89cd","term":"lie","forms":["lie","lies","lying","lay","laid","lain","lien","lyest","layst","lyeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"位於","explanation":"指某個地方、建築或物體處在某一地理位置；這裡不一定真的呈水平姿勢，而是強調“在那裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The village lies north of the river.","zh":"這個村莊位於河的北邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruins lie beneath a modern supermarket car park.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28e01c846ea7e886","term":"lie","forms":["lie","lies","lying","lied","liest","liedst","lieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說謊","explanation":"指明知事實並非如此，卻故意說出虛假資訊來欺騙別人；這是“把事實放到錯誤位置”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"He lied to his parents about the broken window.","zh":"他就窗戶被打破一事對父母撒了謊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't lie to me.","zh":"請不要對我說謊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8349e1b76f7f0b4f43af","word":"lieutenant","forms":["lieutenant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fcfea74bf3bf19e4","term":"lieutenant","forms":["lieutenant","lieutenants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美國軍隊的初級軍官","explanation":"在美國軍隊中，lieutenant 通常指陸軍或海軍陸戰隊等軍種的最低階別初級軍官，具體級別仍要看軍種和上下文。","examples":[{"en":"The lieutenant briefed the soldiers before the patrol.","zh":"那名中尉在巡邏前向士兵們作了簡報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lieutenant reported to the captain before dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lieutenant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d10de89a8669d45","term":"lieutenant","forms":["lieutenant","lieutenants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"二把手","explanation":"它還可以專門指一個團體中的第二負責人，即在首領之下、負責協助領導和統籌事務的人；這個意思延續了“替更高層級辦事”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The gang's lieutenant took charge when the leader disappeared.","zh":"首領失蹤後，這個幫派的二把手接管了事務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His trusted lieutenant supervised the campaign while he traveled.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lieutenant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63bd7065ef1e165a0425","word":"life","forms":["life"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed6bd323ee676b93","term":"life","forms":["life","lives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生命；生活","explanation":"指生物活著的狀態，也可指一個人的日常生活和人生經歷。這是 life 最基本、最常見的意義。","examples":[{"en":"She wants to live a quiet life in the countryside.","zh":"她想在鄉下過安靜的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Life can change unexpectedly.","zh":"人生可能會出人意料地改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/life","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be1286613c879c4a","term":"life","forms":["life","lives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個人的生命","explanation":"指某個具體活著的人，尤其常用於說有人死亡、獲救或受到保護。這裡 life 可以數，複數是 lives。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team saved three lives after the flood.","zh":"洪水過後，救援隊挽救了三條生命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A doctor warned that further delays could cost the patient's life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/life","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afe411584c92d6e7d37c","word":"lifeguard","forms":["lifeguard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-837f3c9d915743a9","term":"lifeguard","forms":["lifeguard","lifeguards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"救生員","explanation":"在游泳池、海灘等水域值守的人，負責監護游泳者，並在有人遇險或快要溺水時進行救援。","examples":[{"en":"The lifeguard blew the whistle when the children swam too far out.","zh":"孩子們遊得太遠時，救生員吹響了哨子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked as a lifeguard at the public pool during the summer.","zh":"她夏天在公共游泳池當救生員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lifeguard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2e84111817d29e4865d","word":"lifelong","forms":["lifelong"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5aabbdc937e135d3","term":"lifelong","forms":["lifelong"],"pos":"adj","zh":"終身的；一生的","explanation":"指某種關係、興趣、習慣或狀態從人生較早階段開始，並持續到生命結束，重點是“貫穿一生”，而不只是時間很長。","examples":[{"en":"Maya and I have been lifelong friends.","zh":"我和瑪雅是一輩子的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His lifelong interest in music began when he was a child.","zh":"他對音樂一生的興趣始於童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lifelong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f6a6d94fb43a9266140","word":"lifetime","forms":["lifetime"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71154389f2466474","term":"lifetime","forms":["lifetime","lifetimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一生；存續期","explanation":"指某人的一生，或某個事物從開始存在到結束的整個時期。它強調的是完整的生命或存在過程，不只是一段普通的時間。","examples":[{"en":"She achieved more in her lifetime than most people do.","zh":"她一生取得的成就比大多數人都多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lifetime of this battery depends on how often you use it.","zh":"這塊電池的使用壽命取決於你使用它的頻率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lifetime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ed0d8b99cf7d152","term":"lifetime","forms":["lifetime","lifetimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"很長時間","explanation":"非正式地把很長的一段時間誇張地說成 lifetime，常用於表示等待、尋找或經歷某事已經久得讓人覺得沒完沒了。","examples":[{"en":"It felt like a lifetime before the doctor finally called my name.","zh":"在醫生終於叫到我的名字之前，我感覺自己等了很久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wait outside the operating room felt like a lifetime.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lifetime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5364b92e50b1944f33d1","word":"lift","forms":["lift"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-299da7e8ed7233ac","term":"lift","forms":["lift","lifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搭便車；乘車","explanation":"指別人用車輛載你一程，也就是讓你藉助車輛向前移動的機會；這裡“向上提起”的感覺變成了把人帶離原地。","examples":[{"en":"Could you give me a lift to the station?","zh":"你能載我去車站嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I got a lift home from a colleague after work.","zh":"下班後我搭同事的車回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e24a71f5582fceee","term":"lift","forms":["lift","lifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電梯","explanation":"指在建築物樓層之間垂直運送人或貨物的裝置，是把人和物向上或向下送到另一層的“看不見的手”的實體化形式。","examples":[{"en":"Take the lift to the fourth floor, then turn left.","zh":"乘電梯到四樓，然後向左轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lift is out of order, so we have to use the stairs.","zh":"電梯壞了，所以我們得走樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-363510ea4b78fac3","term":"lift","forms":["lift","lifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"升力","explanation":"指機翼、旋翼或其他翼面產生的向上力量，它像一隻看不見的手托住飛機，使飛機能夠保持在空中。","examples":[{"en":"The wings generate enough lift to keep the plane in the air.","zh":"機翼產生了足夠的升力，使飛機保持在空中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As the plane slows down, it loses lift.","zh":"飛機減速時，升力會減小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17c942ac96e3d669","term":"lift","forms":["lift","lifts","lifting","lifted","yleft"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提起；升起","explanation":"表示把某物向上提起，或某物自己升起、消散；記住那隻“向上提起”的看不見的手，既能抬起物體，也能讓霧氣等向上散去。","examples":[{"en":"He lifted the box onto the table.","zh":"他把箱子提到桌子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fog lifted before sunrise.","zh":"日出前霧散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99a7026172d42714d029","word":"light","forms":["light"],"officialPos":"n./adj./v./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2df2b28777ce4c0b","term":"light","forms":["light","lighter","lightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明亮的","explanation":"像“發光”這個畫面一樣，表示有足夠的光，因此不暗，也可以表示環境清楚明亮。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen is light and sunny in the morning.","zh":"廚房早上明亮而且陽光充足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choose a light room for painting and drawing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0d286f2c435860d","term":"light","forms":["light","lighter","lightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"輕的","explanation":"像“沒有重量”這個畫面一樣，表示實際重量小，拿著、搬運或攜帶不費力。","examples":[{"en":"This suitcase is light enough to carry with one hand.","zh":"這個手提箱很輕，一隻手就能拎起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I packed light for the weekend trip.","zh":"週末旅行時我只帶了很少的行李。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bf2d2d3c48e3a97","term":"light","forms":["light","lights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光線；可見光","explanation":"指人眼能夠看見的電磁輻射，也就是日光、燈光等形成的光線；這是從“發光”畫面直接想到的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen gets plenty of light in the afternoon.","zh":"廚房下午光線很充足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Light passes through the glass and strikes the sensor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1435aa119f4be4f0","term":"light","forms":["light","lights","lighting","lit","lighted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"點燃","explanation":"把火、爐子或其他可燃物點著，使它開始發光或產生熱量；這是從“發光”這一核心畫面直接延伸出的用法。","examples":[{"en":"We lit a small fire to keep warm.","zh":"我們點了一小堆火來取暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He lit a candle when the electricity failed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e1e47cc739b772bfa7bb","word":"lighten","forms":["lighten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ae9df77c252201b","term":"lighten","forms":["lighten","lightens","lightening","lightened","lightenest","lightenedst","lighteneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變亮；照亮","explanation":"指讓某個地方或物體獲得更多光線，從而看得更清楚。它是“變亮”這條主線的使動形式。","examples":[{"en":"A few lamps lightened the dark room.","zh":"幾盞燈照亮了昏暗的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The candles lightened the hallway.","zh":"蠟燭照亮了走廊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-731e47b56d28b9fc","term":"lighten","forms":["lighten","lightens","lightening","lightened","lightenest","lightenedst","lighteneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變亮；變清楚","explanation":"指光線或景象自己變得更明亮、更清晰，不強調有人主動照亮它。","examples":[{"en":"The sky began to lighten before sunrise.","zh":"日出前天空開始變亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her face lightened when she heard the news.","zh":"她聽到這個訊息後臉色明朗起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8d32091cd2b47c0","term":"lighten","forms":["lighten","lightens","lightening","lightened","lightenest","lightenedst","lighteneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"減輕負擔或痛苦","explanation":"指讓悲傷、責任、壓力等變得不那麼沉重；這是從“變輕”自然發展出的抽象意義。","examples":[{"en":"Talking to a friend helped lighten my worries.","zh":"和朋友談心幫助我減輕了憂慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The extra staff lightened her workload.","zh":"增加人手減輕了她的工作量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b370de14e94142d4a108","word":"lighthouse","forms":["lighthouse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0fc916c300646120","term":"lighthouse","forms":["lighthouse","lighthouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燈塔","explanation":"燈塔是海邊或海上的高大建築，頂部有強光，用來給船隻指引方向，或提醒船員遠離礁石等危險地點。","examples":[{"en":"The lighthouse guided the ship safely into the harbor.","zh":"燈塔引導船隻安全駛入港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could see the lighthouse from the beach.","zh":"我們從海灘上可以看見那座燈塔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lighthouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01db71ab8048f74a4b92","word":"lightning","forms":["lightning"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e447a59edb0fb345","term":"lightning","forms":["lightning","lightnings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"閃電","explanation":"指雲中、雲與雲之間或雲與地面之間發生的強烈電放電，以及由此產生的短暫閃光。日常說天氣時，這是最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw lightning in the distance before the storm arrived.","zh":"暴風雨到來前，我們看見遠處閃起了閃電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flash of lightning illuminated the distant hills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lightning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cab2644828bcc1f22061","word":"like","forms":["like"],"officialPos":"prep./v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-712860ff957972d0","term":"like","forms":["like","likes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜歡的事物","explanation":"指某人喜歡或偏好的事物，通常用複數概括一個人的偏好。它體現的是人的心意與某些事物相合。","examples":[{"en":"The survey asks about your likes and dislikes.","zh":"這份調查詢問你的喜好和厭惡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our shared likes include chess, sailing, and detective stories.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/like","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57fd56f16923a367","term":"like","forms":["like"],"pos":"prep","zh":"像；類似於","explanation":"表示某人或某物在外表、性質或感覺上與另一人或物相似，即兩者彼此“相合”。","examples":[{"en":"This fabric feels like silk, but it is much cheaper.","zh":"這種布料摸起來像絲綢，但便宜得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looks like her mother.","zh":"她長得像她媽媽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/like","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa1c0a8abb8b5e9a","term":"like","forms":["like","likes","liking","liked","likest","likedst","liketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喜歡；喜愛","explanation":"表示對某人、某物或某項活動有好感，覺得它令人愉快，心意與它相合。它可以表示一般性的興趣，也可以表示對具體事物的偏愛。","examples":[{"en":"I like reading books.","zh":"我喜歡讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She likes quiet places.","zh":"她喜歡安靜的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/like","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7d11e18f3d131a54fdd","word":"likelihood","forms":["likelihood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fc38676ce93e0c0","term":"likelihood","forms":["likelihood","likelihoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可能性；機率","explanation":"指某件事發生、某個結果出現的可能程度；可能性越大，事情越容易被認為會發生。","examples":[{"en":"There is a high likelihood that the train will be delayed.","zh":"火車很可能會晚點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In all likelihood, the meeting will be cancelled.","zh":"十有八九，會議會被取消。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/likelihood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eab01b036c00417f","term":"likelihood","forms":["likelihood","likelihoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統計似然","explanation":"在統計學中，它表示：假定某個引數取某個值時，已經觀察到的資料有多“說得通”。這裡重點不是未來結果本身的機率，而是用已有資料比較不同引數或模型的解釋力。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers selected the model with the highest likelihood for the observed data.","zh":"研究人員選擇了對觀測資料具有最高似然的模型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The statistician maximized the likelihood of the observed data.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/likelihood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-442b7af49162a9324e5b","word":"likely","forms":["likely"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0100c47b53f08934","term":"likely","forms":["likely","more likely","likelier","most likely","likeliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很可能的","explanation":"表示某件事發生的可能性較大，通常是根據現有跡象作出的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"Rain is likely later this afternoon.","zh":"今天下午晚些時候很可能會下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is likely to finish the project on time.","zh":"這個團隊很可能會按時完成專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/likely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ba6e1316dc61592","term":"likely","forms":["likely","more likely","likelier","most likely","likeliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"預期會發生的","explanation":"強調按照情況來看，某事似乎註定或很合理地會發生，常用於詢問或說明某種預期。","examples":[{"en":"Do you think there's likely to be snow tonight?","zh":"你覺得今晚可能會下雪嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rain is likely before the match ends.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/likely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14b917e231e68b215944","word":"likewise","forms":["likewise"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c03f8d40d2055ec8","term":"likewise","forms":["likewise"],"pos":"adv","zh":"同樣地；以類似方式","explanation":"指後面的動作或做法與前面提到的相似，像是把前面的方式照搬過來。它強調“做法相同”，不一定表示兩件事完全相同。","examples":[{"en":"The first team trained indoors; likewise, the second team avoided the rain.","zh":"第一支隊伍在室內訓練；同樣，第二支隊伍也避開了雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I apologized, and she did likewise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/likewise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14c9c2002b01b065","term":"likewise","forms":["likewise"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也；同樣如此","explanation":"指前面說過的情況也適用於另一個人或事物，相當於把前面的判斷再加到後者身上。這裡重點不是動作方式，而是“後者也一樣”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is closed on Mondays, and the nearby gallery is likewise closed.","zh":"博物館週一閉館，附近的畫廊也一樣閉館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My brother dislikes celery, and I feel likewise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/likewise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40903c59d19feef1d67c","word":"lily","forms":["lily"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-db583446187b7706","term":"lily","forms":["lily","lilies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"百合花","explanation":"lily最常見的意思是百合屬植物的花，通常讓人聯想到有觀賞價值、花形醒目的百合花。","examples":[{"en":"She placed three white lilies in a glass vase.","zh":"她把三朵白百合插進了一個玻璃花瓶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lilies bloom in our garden every summer.","zh":"我們花園裡的百合每年夏天都會開花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lily","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81b158ceb82d09034036","word":"limb","forms":["limb"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4521a02cdcab6cf","term":"limb","forms":["limb","limbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肢體；四肢","explanation":"指人或動物從軀幹伸出的手臂、腿、翅膀等主要肢體。記住“從主體伸出的部分”這個畫面，就能理解它為什麼既能指手臂，也能指腿或翅膀。","examples":[{"en":"The hiker injured a limb when he slipped on the rocks.","zh":"那名徒步者在岩石上滑倒時弄傷了一條腿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bird spread its limbs and glided over the lake.","zh":"那隻鳥展開肢體，在湖面上滑翔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cda1a854691e36ba","term":"limb","forms":["limb","limbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樹枝","explanation":"指從樹幹或較粗樹枝上伸出的粗大枝條。它和“肢體”共享同一個核心畫面：都是從主體向外伸出的部分。","examples":[{"en":"A heavy limb fell from the old oak during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，那棵老橡樹的一根粗枝掉了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A broken limb hung from the oak.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-55ea09e5715d0a8d9d94","word":"limit","forms":["limit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf27dfb0dc9c0f54","term":"limit","forms":["limit","limits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制；上限","explanation":"指規定了不能超過的範圍或程度，就像給行動畫出一條邊界線。","examples":[{"en":"The law places a limit on how much companies can charge.","zh":"法律限制了公司可以收取的費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a limit to how much stress anyone can handle.","zh":"任何人能承受的壓力都是有限的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f925504a29620631","term":"limit","forms":["limit","limits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極限","explanation":"在數學中，指一個數列或函式不斷接近的目標值；它強調趨近的結果，不一定表示實際到達這個值。","examples":[{"en":"As x approaches zero, the limit of the function is one.","zh":"當 x 趨近於零時，這個函式的極限是 1。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sequence approaches a finite limit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6abf1ef401a0268","term":"limit","forms":["limit","limits","limiting","limited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"限制；限定","explanation":"指給某人的行動、某物的數量或某種權力畫出不能越過的邊界。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy limits access to the building after six o’clock.","zh":"新政策限制了六點以後進入這棟樓的許可權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to limit your screen time before bed.","zh":"睡前儘量限制使用螢幕的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f86e4b17a89f8d27fad4","word":"limitation","forms":["limitation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af55740218e8a8e2","term":"limitation","forms":["limitation","limitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制；受限狀態","explanation":"指限制某人或某事的行為，也指受到限制的狀態；重點是原本可以展開的行動被某條邊界壓住了。","examples":[{"en":"The limitation of public transport makes it hard to travel at night.","zh":"公共交通受到限制，使得夜間出行很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to understand the limitations of the current system.","zh":"我們需要了解現有系統受到的限制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a808d051eacf3cd","term":"limitation","forms":["limitation","limitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體限制；界限","explanation":"指由身體狀況、環境、規則或其他情況造成的實際邊界，說明一個人或一件事能做到什麼、不能做到什麼。","examples":[{"en":"Her physical limitations do not stop her from working.","zh":"她的身體限制並沒有阻止她工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small budget placed serious limitations on the project.","zh":"預算有限給這個專案帶來了很大的限制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e21b6c4d86fc689b69aa","word":"limp","forms":["limp"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b01f13a86686c54","term":"limp","forms":["limp","limps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跛行","explanation":"指因一條腿疼痛、受傷或無力而形成的不規則、明顯不均勻的走路姿勢。","examples":[{"en":"After the accident, she walked with a slight limp.","zh":"事故後，她走路有些跛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He walked with a slight limp after the accident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3218d435a5285891","term":"limp","forms":["limp","limps","limping","limped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跛著走","explanation":"指走路時偏向一條腿，像腿部疼痛或無力一樣一瘸一拐地移動。","examples":[{"en":"He limped off the field after twisting his ankle.","zh":"他扭傷腳踝後，一瘸一拐地離開了球場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injured horse limped painfully back to its stable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38a9c1e721584da284b9","word":"line","forms":["line"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c40b984d650a54c1","term":"line","forms":["line","lines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"線；路徑","explanation":"指連線兩個或多個點的連續痕跡或路徑，可以是直的，也可以是彎的；它正像一根伸展開、留下方向的繩子。","examples":[{"en":"The arrow descended in a curved line.","zh":"箭頭沿著一條彎曲的線向下移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Draw a straight line between the two dots.","zh":"在這兩個點之間畫一條直線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/line","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f721f098fb43d6ec","term":"line","forms":["line","lines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通訊線路；連線","explanation":"指連線兩個地點的電話線、網路線或通訊連線，資訊可以沿著這條“繩子”傳過去。","examples":[{"en":"I tried to call, but the line was dead.","zh":"我試著打電話，但線路斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The internet line went down during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間網路線路斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/line","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61fe15177301e79c","term":"line","forms":["line","lines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"佇列；一排","explanation":"指許多人或物體沿著一條大致直的方向排開，尤其是等待辦理事情的隊伍；大家就像排到那根繩子上。","examples":[{"en":"We stood in line for tickets for nearly an hour.","zh":"我們排了將近一個小時的隊買票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A line of trees stood beside the road.","zh":"路旁排列著一行樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/line","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91acfee9f1015da0","term":"line","forms":["line","lines","lining","lined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排成一列；對齊","explanation":"把“line”想成一根伸展開的繩子：這個義項就是把人或物放到這根繩子上，使它們排成一列或彼此對齊。","examples":[{"en":"Please line the chairs up against the wall.","zh":"請把椅子沿牆排好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher lined the children up before the trip.","zh":"老師在出發前讓孩子們排成一列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/line","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07ad2ef1607d283839af","word":"linen","forms":["linen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbe7e5614fb4090e","term":"linen","forms":["linen","linens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"亞麻布；亞麻線","explanation":"指用亞麻纖維紡成的線或織成的布，是 linen 最基本的名詞義。想象一塊透氣、天然的亞麻布即可。","examples":[{"en":"This dress is made of linen and feels very light.","zh":"這條連衣裙是亞麻布做的，穿起來很輕便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Linen dries quickly in the sun.","zh":"亞麻布在陽光下乾得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c167fcb444faf1de7ad","word":"liner","forms":["liner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92f799e195c9570f","term":"liner","forms":["liner","liners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可拆換的內襯","explanation":"指放在容器、衣物或其他物品裡面、可以取出或更換的覆蓋層；它就是“貼在裡面的一層”。","examples":[{"en":"I put a fresh liner in the kitchen bin.","zh":"我給廚房垃圾桶換了一個新的內袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This jacket has a warm fleece liner.","zh":"這件夾克有一層保暖的抓絨內襯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50706c1cfc8ffc98","term":"liner","forms":["liner","liners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"定期遠洋客輪","explanation":"指沿固定航線執行、主要運送乘客的大型船；可以把它記成“線上路上執行的船”。","examples":[{"en":"The ocean liner sailed between the two ports every week.","zh":"這艘遠洋客輪每週往返於兩個港口之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old liner carried thousands of passengers across the Atlantic.","zh":"那艘老客輪載著數千名乘客橫渡大西洋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d21b3384028efa0e641","word":"linger","forms":["linger"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-802471f736285e44","term":"linger","forms":["linger","lingers","lingering","lingered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逗留；遲遲不走","explanation":"指人在某處或某種情境中繼續待著，往往帶有不願離開、捨不得離開，或行動上難以馬上離開的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"We lingered outside the café after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，我們在咖啡館外遲遲沒有離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She lingered by the door, hoping he would come back.","zh":"她在門邊遲遲不走，希望他會回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22a888a90630a48d","term":"linger","forms":["linger","lingers","lingering","lingered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸消亡；苟延","explanation":"指生命、疾病、感情或某種存在雖然已經走向終結，卻還持續了一段時間，像是慢慢消失而不是突然結束。","examples":[{"en":"The old tree lingered on for another winter.","zh":"那棵老樹又勉強熬過了一個冬天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wounded tree lingered for years before dying.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2eec533c3767f8d10182","word":"lining","forms":["lining"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5a78b6f647a716b","term":"lining","forms":["lining","linings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內襯；襯裡","explanation":"指貼在衣服、容器或其他物體內部的一層覆蓋物，主要作用是保護裡面或讓內部更整齊。它是“裡面那一層”，不是外面的表層。","examples":[{"en":"The jacket's lining is torn near the pocket.","zh":"這件夾克的內襯在口袋附近破了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bag has a soft lining inside.","zh":"這個包裡面有一層柔軟的襯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lining","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de626d93d82527e5","term":"lining","forms":["lining","linings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"襯裡材料","explanation":"指用來製作內襯的布料、紙張、塑膠或其他材料；這裡說的是“做裡面那一層的東西”，不一定已經裝上去了。","examples":[{"en":"Choose a durable lining for the new curtains.","zh":"給新窗簾選一種耐用的襯裡材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tailor chose silk for the jacket's lining.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lining","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1b1bdb480c61d075300","word":"link","forms":["link"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-462a5bf4df6fd64d","term":"link","forms":["link","links"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯絡；紐帶","explanation":"指把兩個或多個地方、人物、事件、事物或想法聯絡起來的關係或紐帶，重點是它讓原本分開的東西彼此相通。","examples":[{"en":"Her research found a link between sleep and memory.","zh":"她的研究發現了睡眠和記憶之間的聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The local guide was our link to the village.","zh":"當地嚮導是我們與那個村莊之間的紐帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/link","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a60504545edbbdf","term":"link","forms":["link","links"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鏈環；連線的一段","explanation":"指鏈條或其他連續連線物中的一個環節；這個具體義正是“聯絡”這一核心形象最直觀的來源。","examples":[{"en":"One link in the old chain has broken.","zh":"舊鏈條有一個鏈環斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The necklace is made of small gold links.","zh":"這條項鍊由小金鍊環製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/link","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8e44216ff543a48","term":"link","forms":["link","links"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連結；超連結","explanation":"在網頁或電子檔案中，指點選後會把人帶到另一個網頁、檔案或位置的超連結。","examples":[{"en":"Please send me the link to the registration page.","zh":"請把報名頁面的連結發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I clicked the link and downloaded the form.","zh":"我點選了連結，下載了表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/link","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-218281dd86ce7f24","term":"link","forms":["link","links","linking","linked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連線；聯絡","explanation":"把兩個或多個地方、人物、事物或想法連在一起，使它們形成聯絡。它是名詞“連線的一環”轉成的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The bridge links the island to the mainland.","zh":"這座橋把島和大陸連線起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two reports are closely linked.","zh":"這兩份報告密切相關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/link","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7cba237207b59720","term":"link","forms":["link","links","linking","linked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連結到另一網頁","explanation":"指一個網頁或頁面包含通往另一個網頁的超連結，或透過連結指向另一頁面。","examples":[{"en":"This article links to several reliable sources.","zh":"這篇文章連結到幾個可靠的來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The homepage links to the full research report.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/link","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc59487712bbe89b4888","word":"lion","forms":["lion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9310b810c18d062c","term":"lion","forms":["lion","lions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獅子","explanation":"指原產於非洲、印度等地的大型貓科動物，雄獅通常有鬃毛，是 lion 最基本、最需要優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a lion resting under a tree.","zh":"我們看見一頭獅子正在樹下休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lions usually live in social groups.","zh":"獅子通常以群體形式生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ac1ef5381caf75418d7","word":"lip","forms":["lip"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-faf591737a65991f","term":"lip","forms":["lip","lips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘴唇","explanation":"嘴巴開口周圍的兩片柔軟肉組織就是lip，通常包括上唇和下唇。","examples":[{"en":"Her lips were dry after the long walk.","zh":"她走了很久後嘴唇都幹了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pressed his lips together and said nothing.","zh":"他抿緊嘴唇，什麼也沒說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5fa90a5036325b38","term":"lip","forms":["lip","lips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口沿；邊緣","explanation":"容器或鍾等開口處向外突出的邊沿，好像一片嘴唇伸在開口上。","examples":[{"en":"Water spilled over the lip of the cup.","zh":"水從杯沿溢了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rested the spoon against the lip of the bowl.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89490cd8a5ad9eb4fb48","word":"lipstick","forms":["lipstick"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00ea484a81999963","term":"lipstick","forms":["lipstick","lipsticks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口紅（化妝品）","explanation":"指塗在嘴唇上、用來增加顏色或修飾嘴唇的化妝品，重點是這種產品本身，而不是某一支具體的口紅。","examples":[{"en":"She put on lipstick before the interview.","zh":"她在面試前塗了口紅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This lipstick stays on for hours.","zh":"這種口紅能保持好幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lipstick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1efda2eeeb80674c","term":"lipstick","forms":["lipstick","lipsticks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一支口紅","explanation":"指裝在管中的一支具體口紅，通常可以按支數計算，也可以按顏色或品牌來區分。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a new lipstick in a darker shade.","zh":"我買了一支顏色更深的新口紅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red lipstick rolled out of her handbag.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lipstick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42110162e06395fd5364","word":"liquid","forms":["liquid"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dba69c17b2700033","term":"liquid","forms":["liquid","liquids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"液體","explanation":"指會流動、沒有固定形狀、會隨著容器改變形狀的物質，例如水、油或果汁。","examples":[{"en":"A liquid takes the shape of its container.","zh":"液體會呈現容器的形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please do not put this liquid near the fire.","zh":"請不要把這種液體放在火邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liquid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0dd258095f14992b824","word":"liquor","forms":["liquor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e02e2baf6368e0cd","term":"liquor","forms":["liquor","liquors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烈性酒","explanation":"這是現代最重要的義項，指經過發酵並蒸餾製成的酒，常見於威士忌、伏特加等烈性酒；在部分英語地區也可泛指酒精飲料。","examples":[{"en":"He rarely drinks liquor, but he enjoys a glass of wine with dinner.","zh":"他很少喝烈性酒，但喜歡晚餐時喝一杯葡萄酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store keeps its liquor behind the counter.","zh":"這家商店把烈性酒放在櫃檯後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liquor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dae1dbd5f056a524","term":"liquor","forms":["liquor","liquors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"湯汁","explanation":"指煮肉或蔬菜後得到的液體，通常含有食材煮出的味道，可理解為菜餚中的湯汁或肉汁。","examples":[{"en":"Strain the liquor from the cooked vegetables before serving.","zh":"上桌前把煮熟蔬菜的湯汁濾出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reserve some cooking liquor before draining the beans.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liquor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a330395cc0a53ad12077","word":"list","forms":["list"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ce9d780024e4fa4","term":"list","forms":["list","lists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"清單；名單；目錄","explanation":"把許多專案一項項排在一起，就形成了一個“list”：它可以列出人名、物品、任務或其他專案。重點是這些專案被集中整理，方便檢視或逐項處理。","examples":[{"en":"I made a list of things to buy before going to the supermarket.","zh":"去超市前，我列了一份要買的東西清單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her name is at the top of the guest list.","zh":"她的名字在賓客名單最上面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/list","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c870572a81024b7c","term":"list","forms":["list","lists","listing","listed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"列出；列舉","explanation":"把東西一項項排在一起並說出來或寫出來，就是把它們列出；這是“list”最核心的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please list everything you need for the trip.","zh":"請列出這次旅行你需要的所有東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She listed the main reasons for leaving the job.","zh":"她列出了離開這份工作的主要原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/list","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f8860eb5103a16b9171","word":"listen","forms":["listen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17fb796979e71c54","term":"listen","forms":["listen","listens","listening","listened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認真聽","explanation":"指主動把耳朵和注意力轉向聲音，認真聽某人說話、某種聲音或即將出現的內容。重點不是聲音是否偶然進入耳朵，而是聽的人有意在注意。","examples":[{"en":"Please listen carefully while I explain the new plan.","zh":"我解釋新計劃時，請認真聽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She listened to the rain from her window.","zh":"她在窗邊聽著雨聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/listen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6743ec81fea6499f","term":"listen","forms":["listen","listens","listening","listened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聽從；聽勸","explanation":"由“認真聽某人的話”進一步發展為接受對方的建議、要求或指示，並願意照著做。這裡關注的不只是耳朵聽到，而是態度上把對方的話當回事。","examples":[{"en":"You should listen to your doctor and get more rest.","zh":"你應該聽醫生的話，多休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He never listens to anyone's advice.","zh":"他從來不聽任何人的勸告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/listen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c4c05d40a8c3ebc0eb0c","word":"listener","forms":["listener"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b47906034016830","term":"listener","forms":["listener","listeners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聽者；聽眾","explanation":"指認真聽講話、故事、廣播或其他聲音內容的人。重點是“正在聽的人”，可以是某次談話中的個人，也可以是一檔節目的聽眾群體。","examples":[{"en":"Every listener in the room stayed quiet until the speaker finished.","zh":"房間裡的每位聽眾都一直保持安靜，直到演講者講完。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The radio show received a message from a regular listener.","zh":"這個廣播節目收到了一位老聽眾的留言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/listener","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03d92a6e2b45e2cff821","word":"liter","forms":["liter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"liter","forms":["liter"],"pos":"n.","zh":"公升","examples":[{"en":"The bottle holds one liter of water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Add half a liter of milk to the mixture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-578756ca4aa16d887261","word":"literacy","forms":["literacy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd2d27dd91462134","term":"literacy","forms":["literacy","literacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讀寫能力","explanation":"指一個人能夠讀懂文字並用文字進行基本書寫的能力；它像開啟文字世界的第一把鑰匙。","examples":[{"en":"The school runs evening classes to improve adult literacy.","zh":"這所學校開設夜校課程，以提高成年人的讀寫能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Early literacy begins with listening to stories and recognizing letters.","zh":"早期讀寫能力的培養始於聽故事和認字母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11bbcbc70dd27431","term":"literacy","forms":["literacy","literacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領域素養","explanation":"由“能讀懂文字”擴充套件而來，指一個人能夠理解、判斷並實際運用某一領域的資訊、工具或規則。","examples":[{"en":"Basic computer literacy is now expected in most office jobs.","zh":"如今大多數辦公室工作都要求具備基本的計算機素養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Financial literacy helps teenagers recognize expensive borrowing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-829f8d848b44fa309819","word":"literal","forms":["literal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d2f2b39be4eb987","term":"literal","forms":["literal","more literal","most literal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"字面上的；按原話的","explanation":"指按照文字本身或原句表面來理解，不加入比喻、引申或額外解釋。一個表達的 literal meaning 可能只是字面意思，而不是人們實際想表達的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The literal meaning of the phrase is quite different from what people usually intend.","zh":"這個短語的字面意思和人們通常想表達的意思很不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That is a literal translation, not the way a native speaker would normally say it.","zh":"那是直譯，不是母語者通常會說的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10b4c11a0178c355","term":"literal","forms":["literal","more literal","most literal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真實的；實實在在的","explanation":"表示某物不是比喻、誇張或想象，而是在現實中確實存在或發生的。它把“按字面理解”進一步落實為“事情真的就是這樣”。","examples":[{"en":"There was a literal storm outside while we were discussing the problem.","zh":"我們討論問題時，外面真的正在颳風暴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He built a literal wall between the two gardens.","zh":"他在兩個花園之間真的砌了一堵牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-458defad73e0f299b5f2","word":"literary","forms":["literary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eeac88a1a04e68a0","term":"literary","forms":["literary","more literary","most literary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與文學有關的","explanation":"指和文學作品、文學創作或文學領域有直接關係的事物，是最基本、最寬的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The university hosts a literary festival every spring.","zh":"這所大學每年春天都會舉辦文學節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her literary fame grew after the novel was translated.","zh":"這部小說被翻譯後，她的文學聲譽越來越高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c972ceabbecc1b6","term":"literary","forms":["literary","more literary","most literary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"適合文學寫作的","explanation":"指語言、表達或風格像文學作品中使用的文字，適合文學創作，而不是普通日常寫作或口語交流。","examples":[{"en":"The translator tried to preserve the novel's literary style.","zh":"譯者努力保留這部小說的文學風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report is clear, but it is not especially literary.","zh":"這份報告很清楚，但並不特別具有文學性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15a89d48a72624f17c4b","word":"literate","forms":["literate"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bb2060c80842cb4","term":"literate","forms":["literate","more literate","most literate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能讀寫的","explanation":"指一個人具備讀懂文字和寫出文字的基本能力，重點是讀寫能力本身，不一定表示受過高等教育。","examples":[{"en":"The program is designed for adults who are not yet literate.","zh":"這個專案是為尚不具備讀寫能力的成年人設計的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program helps adults become literate in their own language.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12246dbce9f6e4c4","term":"literate","forms":["literate","literates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"識字者；會讀寫的人","explanation":"指能夠讀寫的人，是把“具備讀寫能力”這一性質直接當作人的稱呼；現代英語中使用頻率低於形容詞。","examples":[{"en":"The survey compared literates with people who had never learned to read.","zh":"這項調查比較了識字者和從未學會閱讀的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey compared literates and nonreaders of similar ages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac9fa2503ffea8a35ed6","word":"literature","forms":["literature"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f520909048dd460a","term":"literature","forms":["literature","literatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文學作品的總稱","explanation":"它指由文字寫成的作品的總體，重點在於把許多作品看作一個整體，而不是指某一本書。","examples":[{"en":"Literature gives us a way to imagine lives very different from our own.","zh":"文學讓我們能夠想象與自己截然不同的人生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course examines literature from the ancient world to the present.","zh":"這門課程研究從古代到現代的文學作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-391342e225d5e50d","term":"literature","forms":["literature","literatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某國或文化的文學","explanation":"它把一個國家、民族、語言群體或文化傳統中的文學作品看作一個整體，例如英語文學或日本文學。","examples":[{"en":"She studied English literature at university.","zh":"她在大學學習英語文學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She specializes in nineteenth-century Russian literature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/literature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff4a41f6aa62a1c97c05","word":"litter","forms":["litter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b2f4282ea181611","term":"litter","forms":["litter","litters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一窩幼崽","explanation":"指同一時間出生的一群幼崽，通常用於哺乳動物；也可以貶義地指一群令人討厭的人或物。","examples":[{"en":"Our dog had a litter of six puppies.","zh":"我們的狗生了六隻小狗，一窩有六隻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat's latest litter contains five kittens.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/litter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-261907990705bd6b","term":"litter","forms":["litter","litters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地上的垃圾","explanation":"指散落或被丟在地面上的廢紙、瓶子等垃圾，突出“零零散散鋪在一處”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please pick up the litter around the park.","zh":"請把公園周圍的垃圾撿起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was litter all over the beach after the festival.","zh":"節日結束後，海灘上到處都是垃圾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/litter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d841c5a8839626a","term":"litter","forms":["litter","litters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貓砂等寵物墊料","explanation":"指放在貓廁所等寵物排洩區域、用來吸收排洩物的黏土顆粒、木屑等材料，最常見的組合是 cat litter。","examples":[{"en":"I need to change the cat litter tonight.","zh":"我今晚得換貓砂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kitten kicked litter out of the box.","zh":"小貓把貓砂踢出了貓砂盆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/litter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ccc7d0e72206aa15","term":"litter","forms":["litter","litters","littering","littered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"亂丟垃圾","explanation":"指不把垃圾放進垃圾桶，而是隨手丟在公共場所或地面上；畫面上就是把垃圾散落出去。","examples":[{"en":"It is illegal to litter in this park.","zh":"在這個公園裡亂丟垃圾是違法的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone littered bottles along the road.","zh":"有人把瓶子亂丟在路邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/litter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-180ca01b95f0dfdd36fb","word":"little","forms":["little"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7fdc5154c73b83e","term":"little","forms":["little","less","lesser","littler","least","littlest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"小的","explanation":"表示尺寸、體積或規模較小。","examples":[{"en":"A little mouse darted behind the cupboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We used little cups so the children could hold them easily.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c761f5d0d08a1c08","term":"little","forms":["little","less","least"],"pos":"det","zh":"少量的","explanation":"表示某種不可數事物只有少量。","examples":[{"en":"There is little milk left in the jug.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We had little warning before the flood arrived.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b589f62b3fa20328","term":"little","forms":["little","littles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少量","explanation":"表示數量不多的某種事物。","examples":[{"en":"Little remained after the guests finished dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We knew little about the island before arriving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-247610f4dedd4ab7247d","word":"live","forms":["live"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-605142f88efe9ea0","term":"live","forms":["live","more live","most live"],"pos":"adj","zh":"活著的；活的","explanation":"表示人或動物仍然活著，沒有死亡，正體現“保持活著並處於活動狀態”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The zoo keeps live animals in large, carefully designed habitats.","zh":"這家動物園把活的動物飼養在精心設計的大型棲息地中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please do not put live fish in this small tank.","zh":"請不要把活魚放進這個小魚缸裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/live","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d44f365bc30864b5","term":"live","forms":["live","lives","living","lived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"活著","explanation":"表示人或動物仍然活著，也就是保持生命、沒有死去；這是“保持活著並處於活動狀態”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Doctors say he may live for many more years.","zh":"醫生說他可能還能活很多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She lived to see her grandchildren graduate.","zh":"她活到了看到孫輩畢業的那一天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/live","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e47edc54d17b7721","term":"live","forms":["live","lives","living","lived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"居住","explanation":"表示人在某個地方長期居住、把那裡作為住所，而不只是暫時待在那裡。","examples":[{"en":"My sister lives in a small town near the coast.","zh":"我姐姐住在海邊附近的一座小鎮上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They have lived at this address since 2018.","zh":"他們從2018年起就住在這個地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/live","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36b481152ba40f4eec67","word":"lively","forms":["lively"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25e1c43e77d0322c","term":"lively","forms":["lively","livelier","liveliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"充滿活力的；活潑的","explanation":"形容人或動物精力充沛、行動積極，給人活潑有生氣的感覺；也可以形容氣氛或活動熱烈而有活力。","examples":[{"en":"Our new teacher is lively and keeps everyone interested.","zh":"我們的新老師很有活力，總能讓大家保持興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children became lively after lunch.","zh":"孩子們午飯後變得活潑起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lively","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09f2fdcede5cf7a7","term":"lively","forms":["lively","livelier","liveliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鮮明的；生動有力的","explanation":"形容顏色、影象、語言、想法或場面等顯得明亮、強烈、具體而有感染力，彷彿帶著生命力。","examples":[{"en":"The mural uses lively colors to show the city in summer.","zh":"這幅壁畫用鮮明的色彩表現夏日的城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a lively account of her journey.","zh":"她生動地講述了自己的旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lively","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebaf48a9725795ea8b3a","word":"liver","forms":["liver"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bfa46a19d6e000d6","term":"liver","forms":["liver","livers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肝臟","explanation":"指人體或動物體內的大型器官，負責處理營養物質、分解有害物質並製造膽汁等。它是 liver 最基本、最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The doctors said that his liver was badly damaged.","zh":"醫生說他的肝臟受到了嚴重損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is waiting for a liver transplant.","zh":"她正在等待肝臟移植。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc6021af2d4e31f8b731","word":"livestock","forms":["livestock"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc5000e3fc9cdd05","term":"livestock","forms":["livestock","livestocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農場牲畜總稱","explanation":"指農場裡飼養、用於耕作或生產肉、奶等的牲畜整體，例如牛、羊、豬等；重點是農業用途，而不是單純指任何被馴養的動物。","examples":[{"en":"The farm's livestock were moved indoors before the storm.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，農場的牲畜被趕進了棚裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Raising livestock is an important part of the local economy.","zh":"飼養牲畜是當地經濟的重要組成部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/livestock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b95cbcfe0cd25ed09eef","word":"lizard","forms":["lizard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-397af461f9e3e8ab","term":"lizard","forms":["lizard","lizards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜥蜴","explanation":"指蜥蜴這一類爬行動物，通常有四條腿、長尾巴和相對短的頸部；不同種類的外形可以差別很大。","examples":[{"en":"A small lizard was sunning itself on the wall.","zh":"一隻小蜥蜴正在牆上曬太陽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw several lizards hiding in the grass.","zh":"我們看到幾隻蜥蜴躲在草叢裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lizard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b97f752975bd10ec","term":"lizard","forms":["lizard","lizards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜥蜴皮","explanation":"指蜥蜴的皮，常用於談論由這種皮製成的物品；這是由動物義直接轉來的定語用法。","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells handbags made from lizard skin.","zh":"這家商店出售用蜥蜴皮製成的手提包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dealer identified the old belt as genuine lizard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lizard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0cf67fc72b3c86c7a454","word":"load","forms":["load"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51f164fe443fa24e","term":"load","forms":["load","loads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負擔；重量","explanation":"指需要搬運或承受的重量、貨物，也可以指揹包等物品中裝著的一批東西；核心畫面就是把負荷放在身上或由人、動物承受。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers shared the load as they climbed the mountain.","zh":"徒步者們分擔了負重，一起爬上山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The delivery van was carrying a heavy load of furniture.","zh":"那輛送貨車裝著一大批沉重的傢俱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/load","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e16d42092cdbaf66","term":"load","forms":["load","loads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一批貨物；一次處理量","explanation":"指一次能夠運輸、裝載或處理的特定數量的貨物或材料，重點是這一批東西構成了車輛或裝置的一次負荷。","examples":[{"en":"The ship arrived with a load of grain from Canada.","zh":"這艘船載著一批來自加拿大的穀物抵達了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine can process one load of parts in ten minutes.","zh":"這臺機器十分鐘可以處理一批零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/load","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61f62891031f0c36","term":"load","forms":["load","loads","loading","loaded","loaden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝載貨物","explanation":"把貨物或其他負荷放進運輸工具、儲存處或其上面，形成“把負荷放進去”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The dock workers loaded the ship before sunrise.","zh":"碼頭工人在日出前給船裝好了貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers loaded the truck with sacks of flour.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/load","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd2b878dcd14ab71","term":"load","forms":["load","loads","loading","loaded","loaden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把資料讀入記憶體","explanation":"把檔案、程式或其他資料從儲存位置讀入計算機記憶體，像把負荷放進機器裡一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Click the button to load the saved document.","zh":"點選按鈕以載入儲存的文件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The application loads the settings automatically.","zh":"應用程式會自動載入這些設定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/load","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc0ba88f20a66cdc468c","word":"loaf","forms":["loaf"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-055cadf879bcb009","term":"loaf","forms":["loaf","loaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一整塊麵包","explanation":"指烘烤後成形的一整塊麵包，通常還沒有切成片；這是 loaf 最基本、最值得先掌握的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a fresh loaf of bread for breakfast.","zh":"我買了一整條新鮮麵包當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sliced the loaf and put it on the table.","zh":"她把整條麵包切片後放到桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loaf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-472bbf14923e2e7cefd8","word":"loan","forms":["loan"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6b3f6c9d2eb22d5","term":"loan","forms":["loan","loans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"借出行為","explanation":"指把錢或物品暫時交給別人使用、以後再收回的行為，重點在“借出”這個過程。","examples":[{"en":"The bank approved the loan to the small business.","zh":"銀行批准了給這家小企業的貸款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her loan of the car helped us move the furniture.","zh":"她把車借給我們，幫我們搬了傢俱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-474970783eb44703","term":"loan","forms":["loan","loans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貸款；借款","explanation":"指借來、約定在以後歸還的錢或其他財物，通常還可能需要支付利息；這是現代英語中最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"We took out a loan to buy our first home.","zh":"我們貸款買了第一套房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She paid back the loan in monthly installments.","zh":"她按月分期還清了這筆貸款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b5dc076e7b9c122b3c8","word":"lobby","forms":["lobby"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-115de407eb65bb10","term":"lobby","forms":["lobby","lobbies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"入口大廳；接待區","explanation":"指建築物入口附近供人進入、接待或等候的大廳，常見於酒店、醫院、辦公樓等。它保留了“門口的有頂通道”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"I waited in the hotel lobby until my friend arrived.","zh":"我在酒店大堂等到朋友到來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave your coat in the lobby.","zh":"請把外套留在大廳裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lobby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-375541fa36fa9668","term":"lobby","forms":["lobby","lobbies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊說團體","explanation":"指一群有共同利益、試圖影響政府官員或其他公共決策者的人，通常透過表達立場、提供意見或施加政治壓力來影響政策。它可以看作是在議會入口處聚集、接近議員的人群。","examples":[{"en":"The farming lobby opposed the proposed tax increase.","zh":"農業遊說團體反對擬議中的加稅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A powerful business lobby is backing the bill.","zh":"一個強大的商業遊說團體正在支援這項法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lobby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2e1c40da1ae335d4dff","word":"lobster","forms":["lobster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d077e643a1c6f46c","term":"lobster","forms":["lobster","lobsters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"龍蝦","explanation":"一種有堅硬外殼、大螯和多條腿的海生甲殼動物，通常顏色較深，煮熟後會變成鮮紅色，常作為海鮮食用。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered a whole lobster for dinner.","zh":"我們點了一整隻龍蝦當晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lobster turned bright red in the pot.","zh":"鍋裡的龍蝦變成了鮮紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lobster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25bf8e1a2393f1108d37","word":"local","forms":["local"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9124c37d043cd2f5","term":"local","forms":["local","more local","most local"],"pos":"adj","zh":"當地的；本地的","explanation":"指來自某個地方、發生在某個地方，或與該地方直接有關的事物。它可以是“附近的”，也可以是更廣義的“本地區的”。","examples":[{"en":"We buy local vegetables whenever possible.","zh":"只要條件允許，我們就買本地蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The local library is hosting a reading event.","zh":"當地的圖書館正在舉辦閱讀活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/local","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de837af61f3c543b","term":"local","forms":["local","locals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"當地人；本地居民","explanation":"指生活在某個地方或其附近的人，通常與遊客、外來者相對。這是名詞中最常見、最值得先掌握的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The locals recommended a quiet beach outside town.","zh":"當地人推薦了城外一處安靜的海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can learn a lot by talking with the locals.","zh":"和當地人聊天能學到很多東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/local","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c61d02ef654ab458ca50","word":"locate","forms":["locate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7829c4694eb3bc9e","term":"locate","forms":["locate","locates","locating","located"],"pos":"verb","zh":"找出位置","explanation":"透過搜尋、調查或線索確定某人或某物在哪裡；重點是“定位”，不只是籠統地找到它。","examples":[{"en":"Can you help me locate the missing file?","zh":"你能幫我找到那個丟失的檔案嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police located the vehicle near the station.","zh":"警方在車站附近找到了那輛車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/locate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a9945671d989dbf","term":"locate","forms":["locate","locates","locating","located"],"pos":"verb","zh":"選定地點","explanation":"為醫院、工廠、商店等確定建造或設立的地點；這裡是主動“給它選位置”，不一定表示已經建成。","examples":[{"en":"The company plans to locate its new office near the airport.","zh":"公司計劃把新辦公室設在機場附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They located the new plant beside the railway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/locate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-e6eaea18e885e1078829","word":"location","forms":["location"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16f633da4b05f5e2","term":"location","forms":["location","locations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地點；位置","explanation":"指人、物、活動或某件事在現實空間中的具體地點，也就是可以在地圖上標出的那個位置。這是 location 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel is in a convenient location near the station.","zh":"這家酒店位於車站附近一個交通便利的地點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please share your location with the rescue team.","zh":"請把你所在的位置告訴救援隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/location","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfe4dbff8c5d622f","term":"location","forms":["location","locations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"查詢位置；確定位置","explanation":"指透過尋找、調查或測定，把某人、某物或某處所在的點確定下來。它和“地點”這一核心義相連，只是焦點從“那個點”轉向了“找出這個點的過程”。","examples":[{"en":"The location of the missing hikers took the team two days.","zh":"這支隊伍花了兩天才找到失蹤徒步者的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Accurate location of the leak prevented further excavation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/location","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c030586945fe504b604","word":"lock","forms":["lock"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-147c1b2a60913f10","term":"lock","forms":["lock","locks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鎖","explanation":"指用來把門、箱子等關住並固定的裝置，通常需要鑰匙或密碼才能開啟，正是“關住並固定”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I forgot to put a lock on the garden gate.","zh":"我忘了給花園門裝鎖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lock on my suitcase is stuck.","zh":"我行李箱上的鎖卡住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5af81ca34c72adb5","term":"lock","forms":["lock","locks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船閘","explanation":"指運河或其他水道中由閘門圍成的一段水道，用來調節水位，讓船在不同高度的水面之間升降；它同樣體現了用閘門把水和船控制在一定位置。","examples":[{"en":"The boat entered the lock and waited for the water to rise.","zh":"船駛入船閘，等待水位上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It took ten minutes to pass through the next lock.","zh":"透過下一個船閘花了十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6d23707bf1760a8","term":"lock","forms":["lock","locks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一綹頭髮或羊毛","explanation":"指頭髮、羊毛等自然纖維聚成的一綹或一束；這是另一個詞源的lock，不是“關住並固定”的鎖。","examples":[{"en":"A lock of hair fell across her face.","zh":"一綹頭髮垂到了她臉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child had soft curls and thick locks.","zh":"那個孩子有柔軟的捲髮和濃密的發綹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4788c690ca9a61d","term":"lock","forms":["lock","locks","locking","locked","locken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鎖上；鎖住","explanation":"表示用鎖、鑰匙或類似裝置把門、箱子、車等關住並固定，使別人不能直接開啟；這正是“關住並固定”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please lock the door when you leave.","zh":"你離開時請把門鎖上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She locked her bicycle outside the library.","zh":"她把腳踏車鎖在圖書館外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bca6dada231e0fd80bf","word":"locker","forms":["locker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1725d5d3e6c78082","term":"locker","forms":["locker","lockers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲物櫃","explanation":"指學校、車站、工作場所、健身房等公共場所用來存放個人物品的櫃子，通常帶鎖。它就是“把東西關進一個能鎖住的小格子”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The student put her books in her locker before class.","zh":"學生在上課前把書放進了儲物櫃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I left my jacket in the gym locker.","zh":"我把外套放在健身房的儲物櫃裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/locker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8171df63cf574322","term":"locker","forms":["locker","lockers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可上鎖的隔間","explanation":"指一個人可以進入、並且能夠關門上鎖的小隔間；這是從“能鎖住的小空間”這一核心畫面發展出來的義項。","examples":[{"en":"The performer stepped into the locker and closed the door.","zh":"表演者走進那個可上鎖的隔間並關上了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave valuables in a locker before entering the pool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/locker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb610bc1048f7abce1a9","word":"lodge","forms":["lodge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5234c49b40785a3","term":"lodge","forms":["lodge","lodges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"休閒小屋","explanation":"指建在自然環境中、供打獵、度假或短期休息使用的小屋，通常比普通住宅更偏遠、更接近戶外活動。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the weekend in a small mountain lodge.","zh":"我們在一間小山屋裡度過了週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We rented a mountain lodge for the weekend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72c19b32f3d9123e","term":"lodge","forms":["lodge","lodges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鄉間旅館或度假村","explanation":"指鄉村、山地或景區中的小型旅館、客棧或度假住宿處，通常提供親近自然的住宿體驗。","examples":[{"en":"The lodge offers rooms overlooking the lake.","zh":"這家鄉間旅館提供能俯瞰湖泊的客房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stayed at a mountain lodge near the ski slopes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de3aac359fee62e9","term":"lodge","forms":["lodge","lodges","lodging","lodged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"卡在某處","explanation":"指某物進入一個位置後牢牢停住，難以移動出來，常用於子彈、碎屑或異物。","examples":[{"en":"A piece of glass lodged in the tire.","zh":"一塊玻璃碎片卡在了輪胎裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small bone lodged in his throat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-037a2c468004f94d","term":"lodge","forms":["lodge","lodges","lodging","lodged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使卡住或固定","explanation":"指把某物牢牢塞入或固定在某個位置，常見於食物卡在牙縫等情形。","examples":[{"en":"A seed became lodged between my teeth.","zh":"一粒種子卡在了我的牙縫裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The impact lodged a shard of glass in the frame.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8bbf208cba07b637","term":"lodge","forms":["lodge","lodges","lodging","lodged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式提出申訴或申請","explanation":"指把申訴、投訴、異議或正式檔案提交給有權處理的機構，就像把它安置到正確的官方渠道中。","examples":[{"en":"She lodged a complaint with the airline.","zh":"她向航空公司正式提出了投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She lodged a formal complaint about the noise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lodge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3e068d3411d678a1d35","word":"lofty","forms":["lofty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a52e51e99201405","term":"lofty","forms":["lofty","loftier","loftiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高聳的","explanation":"表示實際高度很大，常讓人聯想到高山、高塔等直衝天空的東西，語氣比普通的“高”更有文學性。","examples":[{"en":"Lofty mountains surrounded the quiet valley.","zh":"高聳的群山環繞著寧靜的山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cathedral's lofty arches made the choir seem tiny.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lofty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f375bfe7d93745ff","term":"lofty","forms":["lofty","loftier","loftiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高遠而理想化的","explanation":"把“高”從空間引申到目標和理想：目標聽起來很宏大、很崇高，但有時也暗示它過於樂觀，未必容易實現。","examples":[{"en":"She set a lofty goal of helping every child in the town.","zh":"她定下了幫助鎮上每個孩子的宏大目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His lofty ideals inspired the younger volunteers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lofty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-836ff184e7b41b1e13cb","word":"log","forms":["log"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1dbb290a3a3943a1","term":"log","forms":["log","logs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倒下的樹幹；原木","explanation":"指樹木死去或被砍倒後，去掉樹枝留下的粗大樹幹。這是“log”最基本、最容易聯想到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We crossed the stream on a fallen log.","zh":"我們踩著一根倒下的樹幹過了小溪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sat around the log and shared their lunch.","zh":"孩子們圍坐在原木旁分享午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/log","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c89aa7222df757c0","term":"log","forms":["log","logs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"航海或飛行日誌","explanation":"指記錄船隻或飛機行程、時間、位置等資訊的日誌或記錄簿，是由航海測速記錄發展來的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot entered the weather conditions in the flight log.","zh":"飛行員把天氣狀況記入了飛行日誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain entered our position in the ship's log.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/log","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ccaa92d5a8a3286","term":"log","forms":["log","logs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"活動日誌；記錄","explanation":"泛指按時間順序記錄行動、工作表現、使用情況等的文件或記錄，核心概念是“把事情一條條記下來”。","examples":[{"en":"I keep a log of every repair I make on the car.","zh":"我把自己對汽車做過的每次維修都記錄下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain kept a detailed log of each voyage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/log","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f733b3b003113d1","term":"log","forms":["log","logs","logging","logged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"記錄；寫入日誌","explanation":"指把某件事、某項資料或某次活動正式記入日誌、記錄簿或系統中，是“日誌”名詞義對應的動詞。","examples":[{"en":"Please log the customer's complaint before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請把客戶的投訴記錄下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app logs every change to the document.","zh":"這個應用會記錄文件的每一次更改。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/log","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08e4e1c34e288c718c56","word":"logic","forms":["logic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45600fdd89604796","term":"logic","forms":["logic","logics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推理的條理和方法","explanation":"指按照前提、步驟和結果來思考問題的方式，是從已知內容走向結論的那條“清晰道路”。","examples":[{"en":"There is no logic in blaming the weather for the mistake.","zh":"把這個錯誤歸咎於天氣，完全沒有道理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to explain the problem step by step so we can follow your logic.","zh":"請一步一步解釋這個問題，好讓我們跟上你的思路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/logic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ebbdba0421aa6f1","term":"logic","forms":["logic","logics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邏輯學","explanation":"指研究什麼樣的推理有效、結論如何由前提推出的學科，也就是專門研究那條推理道路是否可靠。","examples":[{"en":"She is taking a course in logic this semester.","zh":"她這學期正在修一門邏輯學課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She teaches logic in the philosophy department.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/logic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac7f39a1e0b7bcd03a4d","word":"logical","forms":["logical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91353cddf9f9f563","term":"logical","forms":["logical","more logical","most logical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合乎邏輯的","explanation":"指觀點、論證或推理遵循清楚的邏輯規則，前提與結論能夠連貫地接起來。它強調“推得出來、說得通”，不單純保證結論一定符合事實。","examples":[{"en":"We need a logical explanation for this change.","zh":"我們需要一個合乎邏輯的解釋來說明這次變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her argument was clear and logical.","zh":"她的論證清楚而且合乎邏輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/logical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-618beca488294067","term":"logical","forms":["logical","more logical","most logical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合理的；講得通的","explanation":"指某個選擇、行為或判斷按照當時掌握的情況來看是合理的、可以理解的。它比 s1 更貼近日常生活中的實際決定，不一定涉及完整的形式推理。","examples":[{"en":"Taking the train was the most logical choice in the heavy rain.","zh":"下大雨時，坐火車是最合理的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It seemed logical to check the address before leaving.","zh":"出發前核對地址似乎是合理的做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/logical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3598ce6f965b2481fe26","word":"logo","forms":["logo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd05384b85381df8","term":"logo","forms":["logo","logos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"品牌或機構標誌","explanation":"logo 是代表公司、機構或品牌、讓人能夠認出它的視覺符號，常見形式包括圖案、字樣或二者的組合。","examples":[{"en":"The new logo appears on the website and all the product boxes.","zh":"新標誌出現在網站和所有產品包裝盒上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They redesigned the company logo last year.","zh":"他們去年重新設計了公司的標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/logo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35af34d731bb1de3","term":"logo","forms":["logo","logos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聲音標誌；品牌短曲","explanation":"logo 也可以是用於識別公司或品牌的短小錄音，例如廣告中一聽就能認出的聲音或短曲。","examples":[{"en":"The app plays a short audio logo when it opens.","zh":"這個應用開啟時會播放一段簡短的聲音標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The station's musical logo played before every news bulletin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/logo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07307784035fdc5cb2e0","word":"lollipop","forms":["lollipop"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93cf08a874925ff0","term":"lollipop","forms":["lollipop","lollipops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棒棒糖","explanation":"一種固定在小棒上的糖或甜食，通常可以拿著棒舔食。","examples":[{"en":"The child was happily licking a red lollipop.","zh":"那個孩子正開心地舔著一根紅色棒棒糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a lollipop for her little brother.","zh":"她給弟弟買了一根棒棒糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lollipop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc4669c3a23754d9","term":"lollipop","forms":["lollipop","lollipops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棒棒糖形物體","explanation":"指外形像棒棒糖的東西：一根細長的杆連線著一個圓形或球形主體。","examples":[{"en":"The sculpture has a lollipop shape, with a round top on a thin stem.","zh":"這座雕塑呈棒棒糖形狀，細杆上頂著一個圓形頂部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road worker raised a stop-sign lollipop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lollipop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86c0173f4f9cb6988a98","word":"lone","forms":["lone"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d9f75dbd07e3c54","term":"lone","forms":["lone"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獨自的；沒有同伴的","explanation":"指某人或某物單獨存在，沒有同伴陪著；重點是“只有它自己在場”。","examples":[{"en":"A lone traveler waited beside the empty station.","zh":"一名獨自旅行的人在空蕩蕩的車站旁等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lone guard heard a noise outside.","zh":"唯一獨自值守的警衛聽見了外面的聲響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d8a3a96fc3dd8f9","term":"lone","forms":["lone"],"pos":"adj","zh":"唯一的；僅有的一個","explanation":"指某一類人或物中只有一個，重點從“獨自存在”轉向“數量上唯一”。","examples":[{"en":"She was the lone woman on the expedition.","zh":"她是這次探險隊裡唯一的女性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lone surviving tree was protected by a fence.","zh":"那棵唯一存活下來的樹被圍欄保護起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1cb0f5a9e3a8e4ddd723","word":"lonely","forms":["lonely"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c187fdbf3d72d0d5","term":"lonely","forms":["lonely","lonelier","loneliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寂寞的","explanation":"指因為缺少朋友、家人或其他人的聯絡和陪伴而感到難過、空虛。這是 lonely 最常見、最需要優先掌握的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I felt lonely after moving to a new city.","zh":"搬到一座新城市後，我感到很寂寞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gets lonely when her children are away.","zh":"孩子們不在身邊時，她會感到寂寞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lonely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-648deef2447ee4f9","term":"lonely","forms":["lonely","lonelier","loneliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"孤單的；獨自的","explanation":"強調一個人沒有同伴、獨自處在某處或做某事；這種狀態常常也會讓人產生寂寞感，但這裡的重點是缺少陪伴這一客觀情形。","examples":[{"en":"The lonely child sat quietly at the back of the bus.","zh":"那個孤單的孩子靜靜地坐在公交車後排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lonely traveler waited beneath the station clock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lonely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1cba997a725e91beb1f4","word":"lonesome","forms":["lonesome"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-129ea4b22cc8d94a","term":"lonesome","forms":["lonesome","more lonesome","most lonesome"],"pos":"adj","zh":"孤單的；寂寞的","explanation":"指因為一個人、缺少陪伴而感到不開心或寂寞；這裡的核心不只是“獨處”，而是獨處帶來的孤單感。","examples":[{"en":"I feel lonesome when everyone else has gone home.","zh":"別人都回家後，我會覺得很孤單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lonesome traveler stopped at a quiet roadside café.","zh":"那個孤單的旅行者在路邊一家安靜的咖啡館停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lonesome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc66f021c67d064c1490","word":"long","forms":["long"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e2aac18d58b3f91","term":"long","forms":["long","longer","more long","longest","most long"],"pos":"adj","zh":"長度大的","explanation":"核心是把空間距離拉開：從一端到另一端的距離很大，就是 long。","examples":[{"en":"We need a long piece of rope.","zh":"我們需要一根長繩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge is long but very sturdy.","zh":"這座橋很長，但非常堅固。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/long","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc9e9149daf392dd","term":"long","forms":["long","longer","more long","longest","most long"],"pos":"adj","zh":"持續時間長的","explanation":"把時間距離拉開，就是持續時間很長；可形容演講、會議、電影等。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting was long but useful.","zh":"會議開了很久，但很有用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was a long journey through the mountains.","zh":"那是一次穿越群山的漫長旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/long","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce483ed740640506","term":"long","forms":["long","longer","longest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"很久以來","explanation":"把時間距離拉開，表示某狀態或動作已經持續很久，常譯為“早已”或“長期以來”。","examples":[{"en":"This place has long been known for its fresh bread.","zh":"這個地方早已因新鮮麵包而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They had long hoped to move closer to the sea.","zh":"他們早就希望搬到離海邊近些的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/long","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-174b1d07348db25f","term":"long","forms":["long","longs","longing","longed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"渴望；盼望","explanation":"long 表示對某人或某事有強烈而持續的願望，彷彿願望把自己和目標之間的距離拉開了。它可以表示盼望某事發生，也可以表示思念某人。","examples":[{"en":"After months abroad, she longed for a quiet evening at home.","zh":"在國外待了幾個月後，她渴望在家安靜地度過一個晚上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He longed to see his family again.","zh":"他盼望再次見到家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/long","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e6609817466dcc418ad","word":"longevity","forms":["longevity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-625b9ee55dc31452","term":"longevity","forms":["longevity","longevities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長壽；壽命長","explanation":"指生命持續了很長時間，尤其用於稱讚某人活得久。它把人的生命想成一條延伸很遠的時間線，因此常譯為“長壽”或“長壽能力”。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying the habits associated with human longevity.","zh":"科學家正在研究與人類長壽有關的習慣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her longevity surprised everyone when she celebrated her 100th birthday.","zh":"她慶祝一百歲生日時，長壽令所有人都感到驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/longevity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec402cb6a9dcfa6e","term":"longevity","forms":["longevity","longevities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"永續性；長久存在","explanation":"指某種事物、做法、傳統或詞語能夠持續存在很久。這裡仍然是“時間線拉得很長”的概念，只是延伸物件從人的生命變成了事物或現象。","examples":[{"en":"Regular maintenance can greatly improve the longevity of the machine.","zh":"定期維護可以大大延長這臺機器的使用壽命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The longevity of that tradition surprised the researchers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/longevity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7dd0c85c947c5e8fe3be","word":"longitude","forms":["longitude"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c26a440e559d91d9","term":"longitude","forms":["longitude","longitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經度","explanation":"經度是一個地點相對於本初子午線向東或向西的位置，用來確定地球上的東西方向位置，通常用度數表示。","examples":[{"en":"The city's longitude is 121 degrees east.","zh":"這座城市的經度是東經121度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"GPS uses latitude and longitude to locate your position.","zh":"全球定位系統用緯度和經度來確定你的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/longitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c01eba119e00d79c82b","word":"look","forms":["look"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7fd733fedc2c55c7","term":"look","forms":["look","looks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看一看","explanation":"指把目光投向某處的一次動作，或為了看清楚而進行的檢視。","examples":[{"en":"Can I have a look at your new phone?","zh":"我可以看一下你的新手機嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have a look at this unusual postage stamp.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/look","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c935bd981db02db","term":"look","forms":["look","looks","looking","looked","lookest","lookedst","looketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看；注視","explanation":"用眼睛把注意力投向某人或某物，是 look 最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Look at that bird on the fence.","zh":"看籬笆上的那隻鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He looked out the window.","zh":"他朝窗外看去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/look","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0445458ff86c4807","term":"look","forms":["look","looks","looking","looked","lookest","lookedst","looketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看起來；似乎","explanation":"根據眼前看到的跡象作出判斷，表示某事似乎會發生或似乎是真的。","examples":[{"en":"It looks like the bus is going to be late.","zh":"看起來這趟公交車要晚點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You look tired after that long journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/look","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ea7d2ae32ce1329","term":"look","forms":["look","looks","looking","looked","lookest","lookedst","looketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看起來是；顯得","explanation":"某人或某物呈現出某種性質或狀態，重點在外觀給人的印象。","examples":[{"en":"You look tired today.","zh":"你今天看起來很累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room looks much brighter now.","zh":"這個房間現在看起來明亮多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/look","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-254637f72efcddb6a545","word":"loop","forms":["loop"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b1561a460bebec0","term":"loop","forms":["loop","loops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繩線形成的環","explanation":"指一段繩、線或繩帶對摺後形成的環，通常中間留有可以穿入或掛住東西的開口；記住“繞一圈又回來”。","examples":[{"en":"She made a loop with the rope and tied it to the post.","zh":"她用繩子打了一個環，把它系在柱子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pull the loop tight so the knot will not come loose.","zh":"把繩環拉緊，這樣結就不會鬆開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac5093aba31a182e","term":"loop","forms":["loop","loops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"迴圈播放的音影片內容","explanation":"指首尾相接、可以不斷重複播放的磁帶、膠片或其中的內容；就像沿著同一條路徑一遍遍繞回起點。","examples":[{"en":"The same short video was playing on a loop in the shop.","zh":"店裡同一個短影片一直在迴圈播放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I put the song on a loop while I was studying.","zh":"我學習時讓這首歌迴圈播放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74d041844d7a2522","term":"loop","forms":["loop","loops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"程式迴圈","explanation":"指一組按照條件反覆執行的程式指令；程式沿同一段步驟不斷“繞回去”，直到條件滿足或不再滿足。","examples":[{"en":"The program uses a loop to check the sensor every second.","zh":"這個程式用迴圈每秒檢查一次感測器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The loop stops when the counter reaches ten.","zh":"計數器達到十時，迴圈就會停止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5e0eee6e28efca6d6ad","word":"loose","forms":["loose"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a155a31ee8b234b","term":"loose","forms":["loose","looser","loosest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鬆動的；未固定牢的","explanation":"指物體沒有被牢牢固定，會晃動、移動，甚至可能脫落；也就是已經部分脫離了束縛。","examples":[{"en":"One of the chair legs is loose.","zh":"這把椅子有一條腿鬆動了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check that the screws are not loose before you use the shelf.","zh":"使用這個架子前，檢查一下螺絲有沒有松。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3e97c9de7b38f47","term":"loose","forms":["loose","looser","loosest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬鬆的；不貼身的","explanation":"指衣物或其他物品不緊貼身體或表面，留有較多空間；它體現的是不受緊束的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"I prefer loose clothes in hot weather.","zh":"天氣熱時，我更喜歡穿寬鬆的衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a loose jacket over her dress.","zh":"她在連衣裙外面穿了一件寬鬆的夾克。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05e5a3fc4552f574","term":"loose","forms":["loose","looser","loosest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"放鬆的；舒展的","explanation":"指身體動作、姿態或整體感覺不僵硬、不受拘束，顯得自然舒展。這個意義仍然是從身體上“脫離緊束”延伸而來。","examples":[{"en":"After a few stretches, his movements became loose and natural.","zh":"做了幾次伸展後，他的動作變得放鬆而自然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She danced with loose, flowing movements.","zh":"她用放鬆而流暢的動作跳舞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33f133e113bb258ee126","word":"loosen","forms":["loosen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eecfd213da319832","term":"loosen","forms":["loosen","loosens","loosening","loosened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變鬆；放鬆","explanation":"把原本繃緊、繫緊或抓緊的東西弄得不那麼緊。除了繩結、螺絲等具體物體，也可以指放鬆對某物的控制或抓握。","examples":[{"en":"She loosened the knot with one hand.","zh":"她用一隻手把繩結弄鬆了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He loosened his grip on the bag.","zh":"他放鬆了對袋子的抓握。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loosen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a2a55bc0bb0f2d8","term":"loosen","forms":["loosen","loosens","loosening","loosened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變鬆","explanation":"原本緊固的東西逐漸變得不緊，重點在狀態發生了變化，而不是誰主動把它弄鬆。","examples":[{"en":"The straps loosened while I was walking.","zh":"我走路時，帶子鬆了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The knot gradually loosened as the rope dried.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loosen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-096b3764d961902778a5","word":"lord","forms":["lord"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2d0640ef44dc774","term":"lord","forms":["lord","Lords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領主頭銜","explanation":"英國貴族制度中的正式稱號，尤其用於領主或莊園主，表示具有貴族身份和相應尊榮。","examples":[{"en":"Lord Ashford opened the new library on his estate.","zh":"阿什福德勳爵在他的莊園裡主持了新圖書館的開館儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The estate belonged to Lord Ashford.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lord","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a57cf9eaf908c5ce5ca0","word":"lose","forms":["lose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40a449f8303b71b0","term":"lose","forms":["lose","loses","losing","lost","losest","lostest","loseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"失去","explanation":"指原本擁有或能夠使用的人、物、能力不再在手中，也可以指把東西弄丟。核心畫面是“手裡原本握著的東西滑走了”。","examples":[{"en":"I lost my keys on the way home.","zh":"我在回家的路上把鑰匙弄丟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She lost her job last month.","zh":"她上個月失去了工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6e6a21bbe9046e6","term":"lose","forms":["lose","loses","losing","lost","losest","lostest","loseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迷路；找不到方向","explanation":"指離開了原本應走的路線，因而找不到方向；也可以說某人迷路了。這裡是把“正確方向”弄丟了。","examples":[{"en":"We lost our way in the old part of town.","zh":"我們在老城區迷路了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you lose your way, call me.","zh":"如果你迷路了，就給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc2afa5f633866f1","term":"lose","forms":["lose","loses","losing","lost","losest","lostest","loseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輸掉比賽","explanation":"指作為參賽者在比賽、競賽或訴訟中落敗，把原本可能得到的勝利“輸掉”。後面接比賽或競賽本身。","examples":[{"en":"Our team lost the final by one goal.","zh":"我們隊以一球之差輸掉了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He lost the case in court.","zh":"他在法庭上輸掉了官司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc8a30ea6faccd1bd350","word":"loser","forms":["loser"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e23dc4e3e35923e7","term":"loser","forms":["loser","losers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輸家；失敗者","explanation":"指在比賽、競爭或某次較量中沒有贏的人；重點是結果上“輸掉了”。","examples":[{"en":"Every contest has a winner and a loser.","zh":"每場比賽都有贏家和輸家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nobody wants to be the loser in this race.","zh":"沒人想成為這場比賽的輸家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80a535516be246be","term":"loser","forms":["loser","losers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"常常失敗的人","explanation":"指一個人在生活、工作或各種嘗試中長期不成功，彷彿總是在“輸”；比只說一次比賽輸了更嚴重。","examples":[{"en":"He calls himself a loser because every business he starts fails.","zh":"他把自己稱為失敗者，因為他創辦的每個生意都失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He unfairly dismissed anyone without money as a loser.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loser","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ea71c18131a7f038329","word":"loss","forms":["loss"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b21f68bc2bd88b8b","term":"loss","forms":["loss","losses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"失去；喪失","explanation":"指由於外部原因或放錯位置，不再擁有某件東西，或不再具備某種功能、能力或特徵。這是 loss 最基礎的意思，重點在於“原來有，後來沒有了”。","examples":[{"en":"The accident caused a loss of hearing in her left ear.","zh":"那場事故導致她左耳失聰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient suffered a sudden loss of appetite.","zh":"這名患者突然失去了食慾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7b2353b17d23569","term":"loss","forms":["loss","losses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"失利；敗北","explanation":"指比賽、選舉或競爭中沒有獲勝的一次經歷。勝利像握住了東西，loss 則表示優勢從手中滑走，結果變成了失敗。","examples":[{"en":"The team suffered its first loss of the season on Saturday.","zh":"這支球隊週六遭遇了本賽季的首次失利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The election loss forced the candidate to rethink her campaign.","zh":"選舉失利迫使那名候選人重新思考競選策略。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3182cfd955c60e3","term":"loss","forms":["loss","losses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"死亡；喪親","explanation":"指某個人或動物的死亡，尤其用於表達留下的人所經歷的失去。它把“某人離開了生命”看作一種無法挽回的 loss。","examples":[{"en":"The community mourned the loss of a beloved teacher.","zh":"社群哀悼一位受人愛戴的老師去世。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We were deeply saddened by the loss of our dog.","zh":"我們的狗去世讓我們深感悲痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7b30d6e4f8c864714bf","word":"lot","forms":["lot"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4b5dd33753ba82e","term":"lot","forms":["lot","lots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量；許多","explanation":"lot 可以把一整堆東西看作一個“大份”，所以 a lot of 表示“許多、大量”。","examples":[{"en":"A lot of people came to the concert.","zh":"很多人來參加了音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We still have a lot of work to do.","zh":"我們還有很多工作要做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fb3c90e678705fd","term":"lot","forms":["lot","lots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一份；分出來的一部分","explanation":"lot 的基本畫面是從整體中分出來的一份，因此可以指一個單獨劃分出來的部分或批次。","examples":[{"en":"The shop received a new lot of notebooks.","zh":"這家商店收到了一批新筆記本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The auctioneer offered the tools as a single lot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-232e40ba34191eee","term":"lot","forms":["lot","lots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽籤用的物件；抽籤","explanation":"如果一份結果不是人直接選擇，而是靠抽取紙條、骰子等決定，這個決定過程就是 lot；因此 cast lots 表示“抽籤”。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams cast lots to decide who would start.","zh":"兩隊透過抽籤決定誰先開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each lot bore a different number, and mine was drawn last.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62b81e10f049a0b757e4","word":"lotion","forms":["lotion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dd5be8a0b3e6511","term":"lotion","forms":["lotion","lotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮膚乳液；外用護理液","explanation":"指塗在沒有破損的皮膚上的較稀液體或乳液，可以用於護膚、防曬，也可以含有外用處理成分。重點是它能較容易地鋪開在皮膚表面。","examples":[{"en":"I put some lotion on my hands after washing them.","zh":"我洗完手後在手上塗了些乳液。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Remember to apply sun-tan lotion before you go outside.","zh":"出門前記得塗防曬乳液。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be7f94bb10c4be7b447f","word":"lottery","forms":["lottery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63d283e1f9823b10","term":"lottery","forms":["lottery","lotteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彩票；抽獎","explanation":"透過抽籤或隨機號碼決定誰能得到獎品的活動，也可以指參加這種活動的彩票。大多數票沒有獎，只有抽中的票獲獎。","examples":[{"en":"She buys a lottery ticket whenever the jackpot gets very large.","zh":"每當頭獎金額很高時，她就會買一張彩票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school held a lottery to give away the last two concert tickets.","zh":"學校透過抽籤送出了最後兩張音樂會門票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lottery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a92e1a7a686fc0e","term":"lottery","forms":["lottery","lotteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全憑運氣的事","explanation":"比喻結果像抽獎一樣無法預測，主要取決於偶然機會，而不是個人能夠完全控制的因素。","examples":[{"en":"Finding a parking space in this neighborhood is a lottery on Saturday nights.","zh":"週六晚上在這個街區找停車位完全得碰運氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Getting a reliable internet connection became a daily lottery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lottery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6013de0381f648b7f215","word":"lotus","forms":["lotus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eaa45c5f94072e9b","term":"lotus","forms":["lotus","lotuses","loti"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蓮花；荷花","explanation":"lotus 最核心的意思是生長在水中的蓮屬植物，通常就是人們熟悉的蓮花或荷花。它突出的是從水中長出、花朵浮在水面上方的植物形象。","examples":[{"en":"A pink lotus opened on the pond this morning.","zh":"今天早晨，池塘裡的一朵粉色蓮花開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temple garden is filled with white lotuses.","zh":"寺廟花園裡開滿了白色蓮花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lotus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1cba38569bab972d","term":"lotus","forms":["lotus","lotuses","loti"],"pos":"noun","zh":"睡蓮","explanation":"在某些植物學或文學語境中，lotus 也可指睡蓮屬植物，尤其是與埃及或印度有關的睡蓮。這個義項與通常所說的蓮花相近，但植物學上並不是同一屬。","examples":[{"en":"The painting shows blue lotuses floating on the Nile.","zh":"這幅畫描繪了漂浮在尼羅河上的藍色睡蓮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pink lotus blossoms floated above the pond.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lotus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db1a60bbff220d0910f0","word":"loud","forms":["loud"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6fd547e1380ffbda","term":"loud","forms":["loud","louder","loudest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聲音很大","explanation":"表示聲音或音量強，達到讓人覺得過大的程度。它可以描述音樂、電視、說話聲等，不一定表示聲音本身難聽。","examples":[{"en":"The music is too loud for this small room.","zh":"這音樂對這個小房間來說太大聲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you speak a little less loudly?","zh":"你能不能說得小聲一點？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd790a17a3b7817e","term":"loud","forms":["loud","louder","loudest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"喧鬧的","explanation":"表示某件事或某個場合持續製造很多噪聲，因而顯得吵鬧。重點不只是音量大，還包括整體環境缺少安靜。","examples":[{"en":"We left the loud party before midnight.","zh":"我們在午夜前就離開了那個喧鬧的聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A loud group of tourists disturbed the quiet café.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da5ac17e0fe584e1","term":"loud","forms":["loud","louder","loudest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"大聲地","explanation":"表示某個動作發出的聲音很大，例如大聲說話、唱歌或敲門。它與形容詞“聲音大”屬於同一個音量畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She called loud enough for everyone to hear.","zh":"她大聲喊，聲音大到所有人都能聽見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audience laughed loud at the comedian's opening joke.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3db9a88c89d760c468e3","word":"loudspeaker","forms":["loudspeaker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7135932d297f085","term":"loudspeaker","forms":["loudspeaker","loudspeakers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揚聲器；喇叭","explanation":"指把電訊號轉換成可以聽見的聲音的裝置，是 loudspeaker 最基本的意義。它可以安裝在收音機、電視、公共廣播系統或其他音響裝置中。","examples":[{"en":"The announcement came through the station loudspeaker.","zh":"車站揚聲器傳來了通知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please turn down the loudspeaker; it is too loud.","zh":"請把揚聲器的音量調低，聲音太大了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loudspeaker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39b97515de0fe542","term":"loudspeaker","forms":["loudspeaker","loudspeakers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外放揚聲器","explanation":"泛指能把聲音直接放到周圍環境中的揚聲器，用來和耳機等只讓個人聽見聲音的裝置相區別。重點在於聲音向外傳播，而不只是裝置本身很響。","examples":[{"en":"I could hear the call clearly after switching to the loudspeaker.","zh":"切換到揚聲器後，我能清楚地聽見通話內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The announcement came through a loudspeaker beside the gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loudspeaker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67d3e22ffdf32bc7b366","word":"lounge","forms":["lounge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-736aa4111446ebc4","term":"lounge","forms":["lounge","lounges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"多人沙發","explanation":"指一張寬大舒適、可以坐兩三個人甚至更多人的沙發；它體現了lounge“讓人放鬆地坐著”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a large lounge for the new apartment.","zh":"我們給新公寓買了一張大沙發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three people squeezed onto the battered lounge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lounge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3233ee23e3897b22","term":"lounge","forms":["lounge","lounges","lounging","lounged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懶洋洋地待著","explanation":"指舒服而懶散地坐著、躺著或消磨時間，正是“在lounge裡放鬆”的動作化表達。","examples":[{"en":"I spent the afternoon lounging on the sofa.","zh":"我整個下午都懶洋洋地窩在沙發上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We like to lounge around at home on Sundays.","zh":"我們喜歡星期天懶洋洋地待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lounge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52f3b71bccfaf6bede5b","word":"lousy","forms":["lousy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7f4f181c064e134","term":"lousy","forms":["lousy","lousier","lousiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很糟的；質量很差的","explanation":"表示某件事物或某種表現非常差，遠低於預期，語氣比一般的“差”更強，常帶有說話人的嫌棄。","examples":[{"en":"No offense, but his cooking is lousy.","zh":"無意冒犯，但他的廚藝糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had lousy weather during the whole trip.","zh":"我們整個旅程的天氣都糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lousy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30703efceb08cb1e","term":"lousy","forms":["lousy","lousier","lousiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體不舒服的","explanation":"表示人感到難受、虛弱或不在狀態，常用於生病、疲憊等情況；它說的是整體感覺，不一定指某一種具體症狀。","examples":[{"en":"I caught a cold and I've been feeling lousy all week.","zh":"我感冒了，整個星期都感覺很難受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt lousy after staying up all night.","zh":"她熬了一整夜後感覺很不舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lousy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4d9cd2a289dfb4c","term":"lousy","forms":["lousy","lousier","lousiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"充斥著的；塞滿的","explanation":"表示某個地方或範圍內某種東西多得擠滿了，通常暗示這種東西令人討厭或不受歡迎；它保留了“蝨子多得滿處都是”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The place was lousy with students after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，那個地方擠滿了學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old house was lousy with mosquitoes.","zh":"那座老房子裡到處都是蚊子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lousy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-686f746a95b6f836d7d7","word":"love","forms":["love"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a963b13178591431","term":"love","forms":["love","loves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愛與關懷","explanation":"指對另一個人的存在和福祉有深切關懷，是“愛”最核心的抽象意義。","examples":[{"en":"Their love for one another grew stronger over the years.","zh":"他們彼此的愛隨著歲月流逝變得更加深厚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A child's love can bring great comfort.","zh":"孩子的愛能帶來巨大的安慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76c6bc3a78093398","term":"love","forms":["love","loves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"深厚感情","explanation":"指強烈而深厚的感情，可以是對人，也可以是對某種事物或理念。","examples":[{"en":"Her love for music began when she was a child.","zh":"她對音樂的熱愛從孩提時代就開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A mother's love is not easily shaken.","zh":"母親的愛不容易動搖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60a6161dae9d263b","term":"love","forms":["love","loves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱愛的事物","explanation":"指一個人特別喜歡並投入熱情的事物或活動，例如某項運動、音樂或工作。","examples":[{"en":"Cooking became her first love.","zh":"烹飪成了她最初也是最熱愛的事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gardening became her greatest love after retirement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf5a1d875310c26a","term":"love","forms":["love","loves","loving","loved","lovest","lovedst","loveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"愛；深切喜歡","explanation":"對某人或某物有強烈而持久的感情或關懷，是動詞“love”的核心用法。物件可以是伴侶、家人、朋友，也可以是事物。","examples":[{"en":"I love my family very much.","zh":"我非常愛我的家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They love each other deeply.","zh":"他們深深地愛著彼此。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c42b170f343c4cbe","term":"love","forms":["love","loves","loving","loved","lovest","lovedst","loveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"非常喜歡","explanation":"表示對某項活動、事物或結果有強烈偏好，比普通的“喜歡”更有熱情。","examples":[{"en":"I love walking barefoot on wet grass.","zh":"我非常喜歡赤腳走在溼草地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We'd love to join the team.","zh":"我們很想加入這個團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f85b43067a280d4cc40f","word":"lovely","forms":["lovely"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-245961f0bc6b3329","term":"lovely","forms":["lovely","lovelier","loveliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"美好的；可愛的","explanation":"指因美麗、和諧、優雅或整體感覺而令人喜歡，既可形容外表，也可形容天氣、景色和時光。","examples":[{"en":"It's a lovely day, so let's eat outside.","zh":"今天真是美好的一天，我們到外面吃吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent a lovely evening by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個愉快的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lovely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-877c506018d9d826","term":"lovely","forms":["lovely","lovelier","loveliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很棒的；太好了","explanation":"泛指某件事令人滿意、令人高興或值得期待，常用於表達溫和而真誠的讚美。","examples":[{"en":"It would be lovely to have a little more time.","zh":"如果能多一點時間就太好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lovely, we can leave as soon as you're ready.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lovely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16a2dd3a872593902a1e","word":"lover","forms":["lover"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3ee7dee6c83224d","term":"lover","forms":["lover","lovers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戀人；愛人","explanation":"指以浪漫方式彼此相愛、關心對方的人，可以是男朋友、女朋友、配偶或其他戀愛伴侶。","examples":[{"en":"She has been my lover for nearly ten years.","zh":"她做我的戀人已經快十年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wrote a poem for his lover.","zh":"他為自己的戀人寫了一首詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-516ac20bead56eda","term":"lover","forms":["lover","lovers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愛好者；熱愛某物的人","explanation":"指非常喜歡某種事物的人，把對人的愛擴充套件為對酒、藝術、音樂等事物的熱愛。","examples":[{"en":"She is a lover of classical music.","zh":"她是古典音樂愛好者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reserve attracts bird lovers from across the country.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c1ff09db3a73dc4a854","word":"low","forms":["low"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-544bc0a65cbfe341","term":"low","forms":["low","lower","lowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"位置低的","explanation":"指處在靠近地面、低於通常參照面的地方，核心就是“處在低處”。","examples":[{"en":"The house stands on low ground.","zh":"這座房子建在低地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The low ceiling made the attic feel cramped.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/low","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3830ff2f42bbbaca","term":"low","forms":["low","lower","lowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"情緒低落的","explanation":"表示心情低落、沮喪或悲傷，彷彿情緒也落到了低處。","examples":[{"en":"I felt low after hearing the bad news.","zh":"聽到這個壞訊息後，我情緒很低落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been in low spirits all week.","zh":"她整個星期都情緒低落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/low","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e951c8c3ca07a2aa","term":"low","forms":["low","lower","lowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量或價格低的","explanation":"表示數量、價格、程度、強度、溫度或數值小於通常水平，核心仍是處在較低的範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells fresh bread at low prices.","zh":"這家商店以低價出售新鮮麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report predicts low temperatures tonight.","zh":"報告預計今晚氣溫較低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/low","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d3a39d0f922e1bd","term":"low","forms":["low","lows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低點；低谷","explanation":"指位置、程度或處境上的最低點；核心仍是“處在低處”，既可以是實際深度，也可以是事情發展到最差的階段。","examples":[{"en":"His behavior reached a new low after he lied to his friends.","zh":"他對朋友撒謊後，行為跌到了新的低谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her confidence reached a new low after the rejection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/low","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c6fb1e9e37a1aea1d30","word":"lower","forms":["lower"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-183067bf94b4804c","term":"lower","forms":["lower","lowers","lowering","lowered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放下；使懸掛物下降","explanation":"把懸掛或舉起的東西慢慢向下放，讓它靠自身重量下降，正是“向下移動”的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"They lowered the basket into the well.","zh":"他們把籃子放進了井裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crew lowered the lifeboat into the water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb5064b6a0d77cb4","term":"lower","forms":["lower","lowers","lowering","lowered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"降低程度或強度","explanation":"讓溫度、音量、速度、強度等變小或變弱，仍然是把某種“高度”往下調。","examples":[{"en":"Please lower the volume; the baby is asleep.","zh":"請把音量調低，寶寶睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lower your voice while the baby sleeps.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5fdae4ca73bd186a","term":"lower","forms":["lower","lowers","lowering","lowered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"降低價格、數額或價值","explanation":"把價格、費用、數量或價值往下調，使它們變少或變低，是“降低”最常見的抽象延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The store lowered the price of the jackets.","zh":"那家商店降低了夾克的價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop lowered prices after the holiday rush.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc03f402b0ece4c6a944","word":"loyal","forms":["loyal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ba4137300710f26","term":"loyal","forms":["loyal","more loyal","most loyal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"忠誠的；始終支援的","explanation":"形容一個人或動物長期、穩定地支援某人或某個團體，不會輕易轉向；這種“不離開、不背棄”的感覺就是它的核心。","examples":[{"en":"Dogs are often loyal companions.","zh":"狗常常是忠誠的夥伴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has always been loyal to her friends.","zh":"她一直忠於自己的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loyal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caabd7b04e20dfa1","term":"loyal","forms":["loyal","more loyal","most loyal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"忠於目標或事業的","explanation":"表示始終堅持某項任務、原則或事業，不因困難而背離；這裡忠誠的物件不一定是人，也可以是一個目標。","examples":[{"en":"Even during difficult times, we must remain loyal to our mission.","zh":"即使在困難時期，我們也必須忠於自己的使命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She remained loyal to the reform movement despite its setbacks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loyal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e931aac0a6a734c2d522","word":"loyalty","forms":["loyalty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b5b56352076f9fa","term":"loyalty","forms":["loyalty","loyalties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"忠誠狀態；持續支援","explanation":"指一個人或群體持續站在某一方、給予支援的狀態；物件可以是人、組織、事業，也可以是品牌。它強調這種支援本身，而不只是一時的選擇。","examples":[{"en":"The shop has built strong customer loyalty over the years.","zh":"這家商店多年來培養了很強的顧客忠誠度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Brand loyalty can keep customers coming back even when prices rise.","zh":"即使價格上漲，品牌忠誠也可能讓顧客繼續回來購買。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loyalty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63f7c892fb0c29bc","term":"loyalty","forms":["loyalty","loyalties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對人、事業或國家的忠貞","explanation":"指對某個人、團隊、事業或國家的堅定情感和投入；即使對方或所屬團體經歷困難，仍然願意支援它。這是“站在某一邊並不輕易離開”這一核心概念最典型的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She showed great loyalty to her team during its difficult season.","zh":"球隊處境艱難的那個賽季，她仍然對球隊表現出極大的忠誠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her loyalty to the club never wavered.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loyalty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7a45ea923c6229b341e","word":"luck","forms":["luck"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4db30afde81e3b9d","term":"luck","forms":["luck","lucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偶然機會","explanation":"luck 指事情並非完全由計劃或能力決定，而是碰巧發生在某人身上的機會或結果。它強調事情的偶然性，例如抽獎能否中獎主要取決於 luck。","examples":[{"en":"Winning the last ticket was pure luck.","zh":"搶到最後一張票純粹是運氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By luck, we found an open table near the window.","zh":"我們靠運氣找到了窗邊的一張空桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87fac1d0745ef718","term":"luck","forms":["luck","lucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶來好運的力量","explanation":"luck 也可指人們相信能帶來好運或避免厄運的神秘力量，因此有人會做某些動作或攜帶某些物品來求 luck。這裡表達的是一種迷信觀念。","examples":[{"en":"She kept the old coin in her pocket for luck.","zh":"她把那枚舊硬幣放在口袋裡，想求個好運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He always wears the same shirt for luck before a big game.","zh":"每逢重要比賽前，他總穿同一件襯衫來求好運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db9fbddbd7caeff7a326","word":"lucky","forms":["lucky"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9db2eecd4d3876b7","term":"lucky","forms":["lucky","luckier","more lucky","luckiest","most lucky"],"pos":"adj","zh":"幸運的","explanation":"指某人受到好運眷顧，事情進展順利，或獲得了本來未必能得到的好結果。","examples":[{"en":"We were lucky to find a taxi so quickly.","zh":"我們很幸運，很快就找到了計程車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a lucky traveler who rarely has problems.","zh":"她是個幸運的旅行者，很少遇到麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22167dca53094b66","term":"lucky","forms":["lucky","luckier","more lucky","luckiest","most lucky"],"pos":"adj","zh":"帶來好運的","explanation":"指某件事本身看起來可能只是偶然，卻產生了好的結果，因此被認為是幸運的或帶來好運的。","examples":[{"en":"Missing that train was a lucky mistake.","zh":"錯過那班火車反而是個幸運的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She always carries her lucky coin to interviews.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19532b5632e2269d3bc3","word":"lucrative","forms":["lucrative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94d785cc924be200","term":"lucrative","forms":["lucrative","more lucrative","most lucrative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有利可圖的","explanation":"指某項生意、工作、投資或機會能夠帶來較多利潤，重點是收入明顯超過投入，因此值得去做。","examples":[{"en":"The company is looking for new and lucrative investment opportunities.","zh":"這家公司正在尋找新的高收益投資機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Selling software to small businesses has become a lucrative business.","zh":"向小企業銷售軟體已經成了一門很賺錢的生意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucrative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c6e46c1c4ed275e","term":"lucrative","forms":["lucrative","more lucrative","most lucrative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得攻擊的目標","explanation":"在軍事或戰略語境中，指一個目標一旦被攻擊、摧毀或控制，就能帶來重要的戰略收益；這裡的“收益”不一定是金錢。","examples":[{"en":"The enemy's fuel depot was considered a lucrative target.","zh":"敵方的燃料庫被認為是一個值得攻擊的重要目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exposed supply depot presented a lucrative target.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucrative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f59e7a4ed324acd6be7a","word":"luggage","forms":["luggage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-478f5509066468bd","term":"luggage","forms":["luggage","luggages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅行行李總稱","explanation":"指旅行者帶在身邊的包、箱等行李的總稱，重點是這些用來裝東西、隨人一起旅行的容器。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep your luggage with you at all times.","zh":"請始終把行李帶在身邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We checked our luggage before boarding the train.","zh":"上火車前我們辦理了行李託運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luggage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78163a9b32a43d0bf9bf","word":"lullaby","forms":["lullaby"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2667548338e4ff5d","term":"lullaby","forms":["lullaby","lullabies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搖籃曲","explanation":"lullaby 是為了安撫孩子、幫助孩子入睡而唱的柔和歌曲，重點不在表演，而在讓孩子平靜下來。","examples":[{"en":"She sang a lullaby to the baby before turning off the light.","zh":"她關燈前給寶寶唱了一首搖籃曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gentle lullaby helped the child fall asleep.","zh":"這首輕柔的搖籃曲幫助孩子睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lullaby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f3991a6127f24880383","word":"lump","forms":["lump"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d731a7eaa5660ae2","term":"lump","forms":["lump","lumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結塊；一團","explanation":"指突出、粘在一起或聚成一團的東西，通常形狀不規則，例如食物、泥土或麵糊中的一塊。這個意思最直接地體現了“聚成一團”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Stir the soup until the lumps disappear.","zh":"把湯攪拌到結塊都消失為止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a small lump of clay on the table.","zh":"桌上有一小團黏土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a9c64f5f1158579","term":"lump","forms":["lump","lumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腫塊；結節","explanation":"指皮下或身體內部鼓起的組織塊。它仍然像是身體裡“多出來的一團”，但常需要結合檢查來判斷原因，不能僅憑這個詞判斷病情。","examples":[{"en":"She found a lump in her neck and made an appointment with her doctor.","zh":"她發現脖子上有個腫塊，於是預約了醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse checked the lump carefully.","zh":"護士仔細檢查了那個腫塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c11901b5d393e6f0","term":"lump","forms":["lump","lumps","lumping","lumped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……歸在一起","explanation":"指不仔細區分，把不同的人或事物粗略地當成同一類。它就像把幾樣東西隨手揉成一團，因此常暗含分類過於簡單或不夠準確。","examples":[{"en":"People often lump all online courses together, but their quality varies widely.","zh":"人們常把所有線上課程一概而論，但它們的質量差別很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't lump beginners with experienced players.","zh":"不要把初學者和有經驗的選手混為一談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9738b6bf3ae32f433b04","word":"lunar","forms":["lunar"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1651b388a899ae21","term":"lunar","forms":["lunar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"月球的；月亮的","explanation":"表示事物屬於月球、發生在月球上，或直接與月亮有關，是 lunar 最核心、最常用的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The telescope recorded several lunar craters.","zh":"這臺望遠鏡記錄下了幾個環形山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mission will study the lunar surface.","zh":"這次任務將研究月球表面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lunar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3bb79e48a7a8af1d028","word":"lunch","forms":["lunch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df986fb58ca2b55d","term":"lunch","forms":["lunch","lunches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"午餐；便餐","explanation":"通常在中午吃的一頓較輕的飯，尤其不是一天中最主要的一餐。它可以是家裡簡單吃的東西，也可以是在外面吃的一頓飯。","examples":[{"en":"I usually have lunch at noon.","zh":"我通常在中午吃午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We went out for lunch after the meeting.","zh":"會議結束後，我們出去吃了午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lunch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2654eef7351173ec","term":"lunch","forms":["lunch","lunches","lunching","lunched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃午餐","explanation":"作不及物動詞時，表示去吃或正在吃午餐；可以把名詞所指的那頓飯直接變成“進行這項活動”。","examples":[{"en":"We lunched together at a small café.","zh":"我們一起在一家小咖啡館吃了午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She often lunches with her colleagues.","zh":"她經常和同事一起吃午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lunch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d08c7b739fee1f2f2d6c","word":"lung","forms":["lung"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91503c1936681856","term":"lung","forms":["lung","lungs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肺","explanation":"肺是脊椎動物體內負責呼吸的器官：空氣進入肺後，肺幫助把氧氣送入血液。它就是“空氣倉”這一核心形象的本義。","examples":[{"en":"Smoking can seriously damage the lungs.","zh":"吸菸會嚴重損害肺部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor listened to her lungs.","zh":"醫生聽了聽她的肺部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lung","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a37644c94aed0a80","term":"lung","forms":["lung","lungs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體力；耐力","explanation":"複數 lungs 可以把肺能持續供氣的能力引申為人的呼吸力和耐力，尤其指長時間運動、比賽或活動所需的體力。","examples":[{"en":"She has the lungs to run the whole race without stopping.","zh":"她有足夠的耐力不停地跑完全程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runner has the lungs to maintain that pace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lung","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65cc63a4e10ee8f05be4","word":"lure","forms":["lure"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b351cd5045987d8","term":"lure","forms":["lure","lures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誘惑；吸引人的東西","explanation":"指能讓人想靠近、接受或追求的事物，通常帶有利益、快樂或某種回報的許諾。它把“吸引目標過來”的具體畫面擴大到了機會、財富和享樂等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The lure of easy money attracted many people to the scheme.","zh":"輕鬆賺錢的誘惑吸引了許多人參加這個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For some visitors, the lure of the quiet beaches is stronger than the city nightlife.","zh":"對一些遊客來說，寧靜海灘的吸引力比城市夜生活更大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7b8fa8a3d7c606b","term":"lure","forms":["lure","lures","luring","lured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"誘使；吸引","explanation":"指用好處、快樂、承諾或策略使某人或某物靠近、加入或採取某種行動。它把名詞義的“誘惑物”變成了主動使用這種吸引物的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement lured customers into signing up for a costly service.","zh":"這則廣告誘使顧客報名購買一項昂貴的服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Warm weather lured us outside after lunch.","zh":"溫暖的天氣吸引我們午飯後到戶外去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7937c4dc4579bfc7c37b","word":"lush","forms":["lush"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48116f3e902fa7f2","term":"lush","forms":["lush","lusher","lushest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"茂盛繁密的","explanation":"形容植物長得密、生命力旺盛，常讓人聯想到水分充足、綠色濃厚的自然環境。","examples":[{"en":"We walked through a lush tropical forest.","zh":"我們穿過了一片茂盛的熱帶森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The valley is lush after the summer rains.","zh":"夏雨過後，這個山谷一片蔥鬱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80d889387e10f4ee","term":"lush","forms":["lush","lusher","lushest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多汁的；鮮嫩豐美的","explanation":"指食物或植物含水豐富、鮮嫩誘人，像被充分滋養過一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The ripe peaches were lush and sweet.","zh":"熟透的桃子多汁又甜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cattle grazed on lush spring grass.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b360321fdc3725cba81","word":"luxurious","forms":["luxurious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd27cf199ee05ded","term":"luxurious","forms":["luxurious","more luxurious","most luxurious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奢華舒適的","explanation":"形容某個地方、物品或生活條件非常精美、舒適，讓人感到享受和奢華。它不只表示質量好，還突出環境和體驗上的富足與講究。","examples":[{"en":"They spent the weekend in a luxurious hotel by the sea.","zh":"他們在海邊一家豪華舒適的酒店裡度過了週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train offers luxurious seats and plenty of legroom.","zh":"這列火車提供舒適豪華的座椅和充足的腿部空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luxurious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd8b20c25fa48b062f1d","word":"luxury","forms":["luxury"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e8d9398d9818968","term":"luxury","forms":["luxury","luxuries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"奢華生活；舒適富裕的環境","explanation":"指由富裕、舒適和高檔環境構成的生活狀態，強調整體的奢華，而不只是某一件物品。","examples":[{"en":"After years of hard work, they finally live in luxury.","zh":"辛苦工作多年後，他們終於過上了奢華的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He enjoys the luxury of a private office.","zh":"他享有一間私人辦公室帶來的舒適便利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luxury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-915c221c6aea19c3","term":"luxury","forms":["luxury","luxuries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"昂貴的非必需品","explanation":"指價格通常較高、令人嚮往但沒有它也能生活的東西，例如高檔物品或服務。","examples":[{"en":"A weekend at the spa is an expensive luxury.","zh":"去水療中心度過週末是一種昂貴的享受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dishwasher once seemed an unimaginable luxury.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luxury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc020a35b7f9cb1382e7","word":"machine","forms":["machine"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec7f8806cfb847bf","term":"machine","forms":["machine","machines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機器；裝置","explanation":"一種利用能量並控制運動、電力等來完成特定任務的裝置。它可以很簡單，也可以是由許多部件組成的複雜裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The washing machine is making a strange noise.","zh":"洗衣機發出一種奇怪的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This machine turns sunlight into electricity.","zh":"這臺機器把陽光轉化成電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/machine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5045cedfe3f1ded1","term":"machine","forms":["machine","machines","machining","machined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用機器製造","explanation":"指藉助機器把材料或零件做成產品，是“讓東西進入機器流程並被做出來”這一核心概念的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The factory machines all the parts on site.","zh":"這家工廠在現場用機器加工所有零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These tools are machined from solid steel.","zh":"這些工具是用整塊鋼材機加工出來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/machine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7cb194d9414fdb990b0e","word":"machinery","forms":["machinery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71116a2a76783f9c","term":"machinery","forms":["machinery","machineries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成套生產裝置","explanation":"指工廠、礦場等生產場所中共同組成生產系統的機器裝置，重點是整套裝置，而不是其中某一臺機器。","examples":[{"en":"The factory replaced its old machinery with more efficient equipment.","zh":"這家工廠用效率更高的裝置替換了舊機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy machinery is not allowed in this part of the building.","zh":"這棟建築的這一區域不允許使用重型機械。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/machinery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c39fc267ad78e20b","term":"machinery","forms":["machinery","machineries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機器內部的運轉部件","explanation":"指一臺機器中彼此配合、使機器能夠運轉的內部部件的整體，例如鐘錶或發動機裡的齒輪和其他活動部件。","examples":[{"en":"Dust had damaged the machinery inside the clock.","zh":"灰塵損壞了鐘錶內部的運轉部件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineer examined the machinery of the engine.","zh":"工程師檢查了發動機的內部機件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/machinery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-079cdc52e64462dfac51","word":"mad","forms":["mad"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc2ba2ded8318bd8","term":"mad","forms":["mad","madder","maddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"瘋的；精神失常的","explanation":"形容人或行為失去通常的理智，顯得瘋狂或精神失常。英國英語中也常用它來質問某人的做法是否太不理智。","examples":[{"en":"Are you mad to drive through that storm?","zh":"你要在那場暴風雨裡開車，瘋了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He must be mad to turn down such a good offer.","zh":"他拒絕這麼好的機會，肯定是不理智。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80775e0776ae6988","term":"mad","forms":["mad","madder","maddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生氣的；惱火的","explanation":"表示對某人或某事感到憤怒、惱火，是現代英語中非常常用的情緒義項。","examples":[{"en":"Are you still mad at me?","zh":"你還在生我的氣嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was mad about the delay.","zh":"她對延誤很惱火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-208be34b55c3475df168","word":"magazine","forms":["magazine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a931fbd646550604","term":"magazine","forms":["magazine","magazines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雜誌；期刊","explanation":"指定期出版、由多位作者寫文章、面向某一類主題或一般讀者的刊物。它像一個把許多文章集中“儲存”起來並一次提供給讀者的容器。","examples":[{"en":"She reads a travel magazine on the train.","zh":"她在火車上讀一本旅遊雜誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I subscribed to a science magazine for my son.","zh":"我給兒子訂了一本科學雜誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magazine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c1b33fa129e04c0","term":"magazine","forms":["magazine","magazines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彈藥庫；彈藥儲存處","explanation":"指集中存放彈藥的倉庫或儲存處，是“儲存東西的地方”在軍事領域的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers guarded the ammunition magazine all night.","zh":"士兵們整夜守衛著彈藥庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The explosion destroyed the fortress's powder magazine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magazine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3be7a505483c0050243c","word":"magic","forms":["magic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70ffbeb6685a5b6f","term":"magic","forms":["magic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有魔法的","explanation":"指被認為具有超自然力量或性質的事物，像巫師施法時使用的力量一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The wizard raised his magic wand.","zh":"巫師舉起了他的魔杖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the story, a magic door opens only at midnight.","zh":"故事裡有一扇魔法門，只有午夜才會開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28c0a4dfbec3ea14","term":"magic","forms":["magic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"神奇有效的","explanation":"形容某件事帶來了非同尋常的結果，彷彿施了魔法，但不一定真的涉及超自然力量。","examples":[{"en":"A little patience worked like magic.","zh":"一點耐心就像施了魔法一樣有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a magic moment for the whole team.","zh":"那是整個團隊都難忘的神奇時刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cea4301b524c9fa0","term":"magic","forms":["magic","magics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"魔法","explanation":"指透過儀式、咒語或神秘知識來影響自然力量或超自然存在，以達到某種目的的力量或實踐。","examples":[{"en":"The witch used magic to protect the village.","zh":"女巫用魔法保護村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book is about ancient magic and forbidden spells.","zh":"這本書講的是古老的魔法和禁忌咒語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95bb26217bb4693d","term":"magic","forms":["magic","magics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神奇效果","explanation":"指某種方法、技能或事物產生了顯著而令人驚歎的效果，即使人們未必完全明白它為什麼有效。","examples":[{"en":"The magic of music brought everyone together.","zh":"音樂的神奇力量把大家凝聚到了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is real magic in the way she tells stories.","zh":"她講故事的方式確實有一種神奇的魅力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ce2d4c7087733c06b10","word":"magical","forms":["magical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c47d6259d40692f5","term":"magical","forms":["magical","more magical","most magical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"魔法的；與魔法有關的","explanation":"指直接涉及魔法、由魔法產生，或需要藉助魔法才能實現的事物。它強調事物和魔法之間的實際聯絡，而不是僅僅讓人覺得美好或驚奇。","examples":[{"en":"In the story, a magical door leads to another world.","zh":"故事裡，一扇魔法之門通向另一個世界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wizard used a magical spell to protect the village.","zh":"巫師用魔法咒語保護了村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4892c4ff3b87e184","term":"magical","forms":["magical","more magical","most magical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"夢幻迷人的；令人陶醉的","explanation":"指某個時刻、地方、氣氛或經歷美好得彷彿有魔法，讓人感到驚喜、著迷或難忘。這裡通常是比喻用法，並不表示真的施了魔法。","examples":[{"en":"We had a magical evening by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個夢幻迷人的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lanterns created a magical atmosphere in the garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bc345e4ff215112b0e9","word":"magician","forms":["magician"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c21e6eedf413463","term":"magician","forms":["magician","magicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"魔法師","explanation":"指施展被認為具有超自然力量的魔法的人，核心形象就是讓普通規則暫時失效、製造奇蹟的人。","examples":[{"en":"The young magician summoned a storm in the old legend.","zh":"在那個古老傳說中，年輕的魔法師召來了一場暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hero must defeat the dark magician.","zh":"主人公必須打敗那位黑暗魔法師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b28639e6df2daeac","term":"magician","forms":["magician","magicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"魔術師","explanation":"指在舞臺或其他表演場合用戲法、錯覺或逃脫術製造奇蹟的表演者；這裡的“魔法”是表演技巧，不是真的超自然力量。","examples":[{"en":"The magician pulled a rabbit out of his hat.","zh":"那位魔術師從帽子裡變出了一隻兔子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a magician perform at the children's party.","zh":"我們在兒童聚會上觀看了一位魔術師表演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed05dd4d068fc00dd223","word":"magnet","forms":["magnet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-12667b1295d56a5b","term":"magnet","forms":["magnet","magnets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"磁鐵；磁石","explanation":"指能透過磁力吸引鐵等某些金屬的物體。它是“把東西吸過來”這一核心概念的字面意義。","examples":[{"en":"The magnet pulled the paper clips across the table.","zh":"磁鐵把回形針從桌子另一邊吸了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This magnet is strong enough to hold the note on the fridge.","zh":"這塊磁鐵的磁力足以把便條固定在冰箱上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d536560cf933b409","term":"magnet","forms":["magnet","magnets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有吸引力的人或事物","explanation":"比喻某人或某物特別能吸引別人、顧客或注意力，就像磁鐵吸引金屬一樣。這個意義保留了“把東西吸引過來”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The new market has become a magnet for young shoppers.","zh":"這個新市場已經成了吸引年輕購物者的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new stadium became a magnet for investment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7674fd90e76d296a31d4","word":"magnetic","forms":["magnetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a30567ba3a51dad","term":"magnetic","forms":["magnetic","more magnetic","most magnetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與磁性有關的","explanation":"指與磁性、磁場或利用磁性工作的裝置有關，不一定表示這個東西本身就是磁鐵。","examples":[{"en":"The device uses magnetic tape to store data.","zh":"這臺裝置使用磁帶儲存資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experiment measures changes in the magnetic field.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b36e1fab0c6f62ed","term":"magnetic","forms":["magnetic","more magnetic","most magnetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有磁性的","explanation":"指物質本身具有磁鐵的性質，尤其能夠吸引鐵等材料。它是從“磁效能夠產生吸引力”這一核心概念直接發展出來的。","examples":[{"en":"This metal is magnetic and attracts iron filings.","zh":"這種金屬有磁性，能吸引鐵屑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The magnetic clasp held the cover closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c6a6a634bef70723","term":"magnetic","forms":["magnetic","more magnetic","most magnetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有強大吸引力的","explanation":"比喻某人的性格、氣質或表現像磁鐵一樣吸引別人，使人願意靠近、關注或信服。這個義項把物理上的“吸引”擴充套件成了社交和心理上的吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"She has a magnetic personality that makes people feel welcome.","zh":"她有一種很有吸引力的性格，讓人感到賓至如歸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor has a magnetic presence on screen.","zh":"那位演員在銀幕上極具吸引力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-beb942513440d063f653","word":"magnificent","forms":["magnificent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ccd51923d745c9a3","term":"magnificent","forms":["magnificent","more magnificent","most magnificent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"壯麗華美的","explanation":"形容外觀、裝飾或整體氣勢華美壯麗，給人強烈的視覺震撼或莊重感。它不一定只表示體積大，重點是顯得非凡、堂皇。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a magnificent sunset over the sea.","zh":"我們欣賞了海上壯麗的日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The palace has a magnificent entrance hall.","zh":"這座宮殿有一間富麗堂皇的門廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnificent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1176eda0da58d63d","term":"magnificent","forms":["magnificent","more magnificent","most magnificent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高尚宏大的","explanation":"形容人的行為、舉動或精神顯得高尚、慷慨而有氣魄，重點不在外表，而在行動體現出的偉大和尊嚴。","examples":[{"en":"Her magnificent gesture brought the two families together.","zh":"她那高尚而慷慨的舉動使兩個家庭重新走到了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her magnificent generosity saved the children's hospital.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnificent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-53020fb01ddf7c7e19b1","word":"magnify","forms":["magnify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb39b5dbc7ca7fb0","term":"magnify","forms":["magnify","magnifies","magnifying","magnified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變大或更重要","explanation":"它可以讓具體物件在尺寸上變大，也可以讓某種影響、作用或重要性增加；後者是把“放大”從外形延伸到了抽象層面。","examples":[{"en":"The crisis magnified the need for reliable public transport.","zh":"這場危機放大了人們對可靠公共交通的需求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The award magnified her influence in the scientific community.","zh":"這項獎項提高了她在科學界的影響力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2553d49a24a2f8db","term":"magnify","forms":["magnify","magnifies","magnifying","magnified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"誇大；加劇","explanation":"這裡是讓某件事顯得比實際更嚴重、更重要或更有影響，常常帶有誇張意味；它可以指人為誇大，也可以指某種情況使問題的影響加重。","examples":[{"en":"The article magnified a minor mistake into a national scandal.","zh":"那篇文章把一個小錯誤誇大成了全國性的醜聞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stress can magnify small problems and make them seem impossible to solve.","zh":"壓力會放大小問題，讓它們看起來根本無法解決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a180cdcb4940723d","term":"magnify","forms":["magnify","magnifies","magnifying","magnified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用鏡頭放大","explanation":"指藉助放大鏡、顯微鏡、望遠鏡等光學裝置，使遠處或微小的物件在觀察中顯得更大。這是“放大”最直接、最具體的用法。","examples":[{"en":"This lens magnifies distant objects without making the image blurry.","zh":"這枚鏡頭能放大遠處的物體，同時不會讓影象變模糊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This lens magnifies the insect's delicate wing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-773106703bdaada919e4","word":"maid","forms":["maid"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df317690e5d65c33","term":"maid","forms":["maid","maids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女傭；女清潔工","explanation":"maid指受僱在私人住宅、旅館等地方做清潔和家務的女性，也可泛指女性清潔工。這是現代最值得優先掌握的普通義項。","examples":[{"en":"The maid cleaned our room while we were out.","zh":"我們外出時，女清潔工打掃了我們的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family hired a maid to help with the housework.","zh":"這家人僱了一名女傭幫忙做家務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad313e758ba53ea287c1","word":"maiden","forms":["maiden"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9810e298ee140c1b","term":"maiden","forms":["maiden"],"pos":"adj","zh":"首次的","explanation":"從“尚未經歷過”引申為某人的第一次、某事物的首次出現，因此表示“首個的、初次的”。","examples":[{"en":"The ship began its maiden voyage in June.","zh":"這艘船於六月開始了首次航行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She scored a century in her maiden international match.","zh":"她在自己的首場國際比賽中就拿到了一百分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maiden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eedfe00d9d63076f","term":"maiden","forms":["maiden","maidens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少女；未婚年輕女子","explanation":"指年輕的女孩或未婚年輕女子，是 maiden 最基本的名詞形象，但現代英語中通常帶文學或古雅色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The old story begins with a maiden living by the sea.","zh":"這個古老故事開頭講的是一位住在海邊的少女。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A village maiden brought flowers to the festival.","zh":"一位村裡的少女把鮮花帶到了節日活動上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maiden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00d8d3f11739d2f35370","word":"mail","forms":["mail"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43bd2240939b5b7e","term":"mail","forms":["mail","mails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝信件的郵件袋","explanation":"mail可以指裝著要投遞的信件、包裹等的郵件，也就是郵政系統正在傳送的那一批東西。","examples":[{"en":"The mail arrived just after breakfast.","zh":"郵件就在早餐後送到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found the letter in the mail this morning.","zh":"我今天早上在郵件裡找到了那封信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9efd6a90aa050242","term":"mail","forms":["mail","mails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"郵政服務","explanation":"mail也可以從“被送出的郵件”擴大為“負責收取和投遞郵件的郵政服務或系統”。","examples":[{"en":"We sent the signed contract by mail.","zh":"我們透過郵政把簽好字的合同寄出去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mail is slower during the holidays.","zh":"節日期間郵政服務會慢一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7473cb47935e29a0","term":"mail","forms":["mail","mails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電子郵件服務","explanation":"mail還可以指透過計算機網路傳送、儲存和轉發電子訊息的服務，重點是整個電子郵件系統或功能。","examples":[{"en":"Our mail service was down for an hour.","zh":"我們的電子郵件服務停了一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I check my mail before work every day.","zh":"我每天上班前都會檢視電子郵件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9a75e2cc658386a","term":"mail","forms":["mail","mails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鎖子甲","explanation":"mail可以指用許多相扣的金屬環織成的盔甲，形成像金屬網一樣的防護層。","examples":[{"en":"The knight wore mail beneath his cloak.","zh":"那名騎士在斗篷下面穿著鎖子甲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sword struck his mail but did not break through.","zh":"劍砍中了他的鎖子甲，卻沒有穿透。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9c657059627cc41","term":"mail","forms":["mail","mails","mailing","mailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"郵寄","explanation":"mail作動詞時，表示把信件、包裹等交給郵政系統寄出去，核心仍是“把東西裝好並送出”。","examples":[{"en":"Please mail the form to the address on the card.","zh":"請把表格寄到卡片上的地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I mailed the package yesterday.","zh":"我昨天把包裹寄出去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d6e4079e36703ebd37c","word":"main","forms":["main"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9beb6ff603c5614","term":"main","forms":["main"],"pos":"adj","zh":"主要的；最重要的","explanation":"指在一組事物中處在中心位置、起決定作用或最值得關注的；這正是“main”所表示的“處在中心、起主要作用”。","examples":[{"en":"The main reason I left was the long commute.","zh":"我離開的主要原因是通勤時間太長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our main goal is to keep the park clean.","zh":"我們的主要目標是保持公園整潔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/main","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55ffd7e714fcf480","term":"main","forms":["main"],"pos":"adj","zh":"主體的；佔最大部分的","explanation":"指在大小、數量、範圍或力量上構成最大部分的東西；也就是“主體”或“佔最大部分”的部分。","examples":[{"en":"The main part of the house was built from local stone.","zh":"這棟房子的主體部分用當地石材建成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most of the damage was to the main beams.","zh":"大部分損壞都發生在主樑上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/main","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9bc5b2707f57e1d0","term":"main","forms":["main","mains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主體；大部分","explanation":"指某個整體中最主要的部分或佔最大比例的部分，也就是記憶鉤子中的“主體”。","examples":[{"en":"The main of the work is already finished.","zh":"這項工作的主體部分已經完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The main of the crowd moved toward the station.","zh":"人群的大部分向車站方向走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/main","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c35b091be3c28b8","term":"main","forms":["main","mains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主幹管線","explanation":"指向某個區域或建築物供應水、電、煤氣等公用服務的大型主幹電纜或管道；它承擔的是“主幹線”的供應作用。","examples":[{"en":"The city shut off the water main after the pipe burst.","zh":"水管爆裂後，市政府關閉了供水主管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers found a gas leak in the main outside the building.","zh":"工人在大樓外的煤氣主管中發現了洩漏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/main","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d46bcc63d0618b41ece4","word":"mainland","forms":["mainland"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-85f46d12a34436e5","term":"mainland","forms":["mainland","mainlands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本土；主要陸地","explanation":"指相對於周圍島嶼或半島而言的主要陸地，常包含大陸或一個國家的本土部分。核心畫面是“海中的島回到那塊更主要、更大的陸地”。","examples":[{"en":"The ferry will take us back to the mainland before dark.","zh":"渡船會在天黑前把我們送回本土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most of the supplies arrive from the mainland.","zh":"大部分物資都從本土運來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mainland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eae1087395bc7fff","term":"mainland","forms":["mainland","mainlands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"群島主島","explanation":"指一組島嶼中最大或最主要的那個島。這裡的“主要陸地”不必是大陸，也可以是在群島內部充當中心的主島。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed on the mainland of the archipelago and took boats to the smaller islands.","zh":"我們住在這個群島的主島上，再乘船前往較小的島嶼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ferry links several smaller islands with the mainland.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mainland","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc9c8f83c36b4179d2a9","word":"mainstream","forms":["mainstream"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ab674d90f1e2cbc","term":"mainstream","forms":["mainstream","mainstreams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主流；普遍規範","explanation":"指一個社會或領域中大多數人接受的想法、習慣、文化或做法，也就是那條“把多數人帶在其中”的社會主流。","examples":[{"en":"Her music has gradually moved from the margins into the mainstream.","zh":"她的音樂逐漸從邊緣進入了主流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The movement gradually entered the political mainstream.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mainstream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91bb720d0df350055e59","word":"maintain","forms":["maintain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51ff7ec57f667ff9","term":"maintain","forms":["maintain","maintains","maintaining","maintained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"維持；保持","explanation":"使某種狀態、水平或條件繼續存在，不讓它明顯變差或改變。重點是“保持住”，而不是把已經損壞的東西修好。","examples":[{"en":"Regular breaks help you maintain your concentration during long meetings.","zh":"定時休息有助於你在長時間開會時保持注意力集中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team worked hard to maintain a positive atmosphere.","zh":"團隊努力維持積極的氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maintain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-569e59d046af47c5","term":"maintain","forms":["maintain","maintains","maintaining","maintained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"維護；保養","explanation":"透過持續照料、檢查或處理，使裝置、道路等保持良好狀態並正常工作。這是“維持狀態”在具體物品上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The building is expensive to maintain because it is so old.","zh":"這座樓太舊了，維護起來費用很高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mechanics maintain the buses throughout the year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maintain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8589c63b0943a62bfda9","word":"maintenance","forms":["maintenance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c44b20fa58ce82d","term":"maintenance","forms":["maintenance","maintenances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"維護；保養","explanation":"指為使機器、裝置、建築或系統繼續正常執行而進行的檢查、保養和必要修理。重點不是把已經壞掉的東西修好，而是持續托住它的正常狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Regular maintenance keeps the elevator running safely.","zh":"定期維護能讓電梯安全執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car needs maintenance before the long trip.","zh":"這輛車在長途出發前需要維護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maintenance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e235d1aea65af5f","term":"maintenance","forms":["maintenance","maintenances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軟體維護","explanation":"指軟體釋出後為修復錯誤、提高穩定性或保持相容而進行的更新，不以增加新功能為主要目的。它是“讓系統繼續正常執行”這一核心概念在軟體中的應用。","examples":[{"en":"The company released a maintenance update to fix several bugs.","zh":"公司釋出了一次維護更新來修復幾個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Software maintenance includes fixing bugs and updating dependencies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maintenance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d54e8c0e9f538b7b268e","word":"majestic","forms":["majestic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3952f2a43fc782a","term":"majestic","forms":["majestic","more majestic","most majestic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"壯麗莊嚴的","explanation":"形容某人、某物或某個場面氣勢宏大、莊嚴尊貴，給人一種王者般的震撼感；它可以說自然景觀、建築，也可以說人的動作和姿態。","examples":[{"en":"The mountains looked majestic in the morning light.","zh":"群山在晨光中顯得壯麗莊嚴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gymnast performed a majestic vault.","zh":"那名體操運動員完成了一個氣勢非凡的跳馬動作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/majestic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-086688a2e3b68ef2079d","word":"majesty","forms":["majesty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa530bbb1ae6ffa2","term":"majesty","forms":["majesty","majesties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宏偉與威嚴","explanation":"指某人、某物或某種場面因宏大、尊貴、強大或莊嚴而令人敬畏的特質。金字塔、山川和莊嚴的儀式都可以展現這種“高大到讓人肅然起敬”的氣勢。","examples":[{"en":"We stood quietly and admired the majesty of the mountains.","zh":"我們靜靜地站著，讚歎群山的雄偉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old cathedral still has a sense of majesty.","zh":"這座古老的大教堂依然帶有莊嚴宏偉的氣勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/majesty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6558a6a3379db4f31039","word":"major","forms":["major"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a0089bb72fa2007","term":"major","forms":["major","more major","most major"],"pos":"adj","zh":"重要的；主要的","explanation":"抓住“更大、更重要”這個核心：major 表示某事物在地位、意義、影響或受關注程度上很突出，常譯為“重要的”或“主要的”。","examples":[{"en":"This is a major decision for the company.","zh":"這是公司的一項重大決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new bridge is a major improvement to the city's transport system.","zh":"這座新橋大大改善了這座城市的交通系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/major","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecf3d6287542558e","term":"major","forms":["major","majors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少校","explanation":"指軍隊中的一種軍官軍銜，通常高於上尉、低於中校；可以把它記成軍銜中“更大、更重要”的一級。","examples":[{"en":"Her father served as a major in the army.","zh":"她的父親曾在軍隊中擔任少校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The major inspected the camp before breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/major","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b0a24030d160239","term":"major","forms":["major","majors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學主修專業","explanation":"指大學生為取得學位而重點學習的主要學科；它是學習經歷中“最重要、最主要”的專業方向。","examples":[{"en":"I chose biology as my major in my second year.","zh":"我在大二時選擇了生物學作為主修專業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her major requires several years of laboratory work.","zh":"她的主修專業要求進行多年的實驗室學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/major","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ed874b1d8c2a6b5","term":"major","forms":["major","majors","majoring","majored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"主修","explanation":"指在大學裡把某一學科作為自己的主要學習方向；也就是把“最重要的專業”作為主修。","examples":[{"en":"She majors in environmental science at a state university.","zh":"她在一所州立大學主修環境科學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I majored in history because I loved working with old documents.","zh":"我因為喜歡研究古老文獻而主修歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/major","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-226f9e95eca7880a1150","word":"majority","forms":["majority"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66d42fec815b7580","term":"majority","forms":["majority","majorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"超過一半的多數","explanation":"指某個群體、數量或票數中超過百分之五十的部分，也就是佔優勢的那一邊。","examples":[{"en":"The majority of students supported the new schedule.","zh":"大多數學生支援新的時間安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A clear majority of voters chose the safer option.","zh":"明顯多數的選民選擇了更安全的方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/majority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63fd9b85c81b42f4","term":"majority","forms":["majority","majorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"議會或選舉中的領先票數","explanation":"指獲勝一方比對手多出的席位或票數，也就是政治競爭中的領先優勢。這個數值可以很小，所以“多數”不一定意味著壓倒性勝利。","examples":[{"en":"The coalition won the vote by a majority of six seats.","zh":"這個聯盟以六個席位的多數贏得了表決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She retained the seat with a majority of ninety votes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/majority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d05aa2a15fb3c40efeeb","word":"make","forms":["make"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f20773a9eaffb54a","term":"make","forms":["make","makes","making","made","maked","makest","madest","maketh","-","makeing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"製作；創造","explanation":"指透過行動把物品、作品或其他東西做出來，體現了“做出某物”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"We made a bird feeder for the garden.","zh":"我們為花園做了一個喂鳥器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She makes most of her clothes herself.","zh":"她的大部分衣服都是自己做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/make","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a774f3a56c9dd79","term":"make","forms":["make","makes","making","made","maked","makest","madest","maketh","-","makeing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使成為；使處於","explanation":"指透過某種原因讓人或事物進入某種狀態，正是“做出某種結果”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The long delay made everyone nervous.","zh":"長時間的延誤讓每個人都緊張起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This change will make the process easier.","zh":"這個改變會讓流程更容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/make","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b1aed21a7353c94","term":"make","forms":["make","makes","making","made","maked","makest","madest","maketh","-","makeing"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到達","explanation":"指設法到達某個地點或在某個時間前趕到，體現了“做成一件事併到達目標”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"We should make the station by six.","zh":"我們應該能在六點前趕到車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hope you can make it to the meeting.","zh":"我希望你能趕到會議現場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/make","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5a5256c1cd3b0c4295f","word":"makeup","forms":["makeup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b61bacc40ea7a4e","term":"makeup","forms":["makeup","makeups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"構成；組成","explanation":"指一個整體由哪些部分、成分或成員組成，強調把許多部分組合成一個整體。它可以用於物質、裝置、群體或抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The makeup of the committee has changed this year.","zh":"這個委員會的構成今年發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to understand the makeup of the material.","zh":"我們需要了解這種材料的組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/makeup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8ae01eaf06ddf6c","term":"makeup","forms":["makeup","makeups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化妝品；妝容","explanation":"指塗在皮膚上、尤其是臉上，用來改變或修飾外觀的各種顏色和物質；在日常語境中也可泛指一個人所化的妝。","examples":[{"en":"She rarely wears makeup to work.","zh":"她很少化妝去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This makeup looks natural in daylight.","zh":"這種妝在日光下看起來很自然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/makeup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d248e82c62c93868783","word":"male","forms":["male"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-739c15bd7a031103","term":"male","forms":["male","maler","more male","malest","most male"],"pos":"adj","zh":"男性的；雄性的","explanation":"指屬於通常產生精子的性別，或與這種性別相關的人、動物和生物體。它可以修飾人，也可以修飾動物、植物或細胞等。","examples":[{"en":"The study included 120 male participants.","zh":"這項研究包括120名男性參與者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The male lion guarded the entrance to the den.","zh":"那頭雄獅守在洞穴入口處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9061ec912ef0f5e5","term":"male","forms":["male","maler","more male","malest","most male"],"pos":"adj","zh":"男性特有的；雄性特徵的","explanation":"指某種外表、行為、興趣或其他特點通常與男性或雄性相關。這個意思強調“具有這種特徵”，不一定是在說明物件本身就是男性。","examples":[{"en":"The bird's male coloration helps it attract a mate.","zh":"這種鳥的雄性體色有助於吸引配偶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The advertisement relies on stereotypically male interests.","zh":"這則廣告依賴人們通常認為屬於男性的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-afdfba87c2186ac2","term":"male","forms":["male","males"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男性；雄性個體","explanation":"指一個屬於通常產生精子的性別的人或動物。它是形容詞 male 的名詞用法，重點是把個體歸入男性或雄性這一類。","examples":[{"en":"A male was seen leaving the building before dawn.","zh":"有人看到一名男性在黎明前離開了大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The zoo moved the young male to a larger enclosure.","zh":"動物園把那隻年輕雄性動物轉移到了更大的圍欄裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-029d33cff213147256c2","word":"mall","forms":["mall"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6c2d5afeb5ec318","term":"mall","forms":["mall","malls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"購物中心","explanation":"指把許多商店、餐館和娛樂設施集中在一起的大型購物中心，通常是現代英語中最重要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon at the mall looking for a birthday gift.","zh":"我們整個下午都在購物中心尋找生日禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mall closes at nine on weekdays.","zh":"這家購物中心工作日晚上九點關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e11337da71c61f1","term":"mall","forms":["mall","malls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業步行街","explanation":"指以步行為主、兩側有許多商店的商業街，通常是城市中供人逛街的開放式空間；它體現了“讓人走動、逛店的地方”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The new mall has cafés, bookstores, and a small playground.","zh":"新的商業步行街有咖啡館、書店和一個小型遊樂場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pedestrian mall contains cafés and small shops.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e645af8e0e4e3646cd24","word":"mammal","forms":["mammal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac97f2bed75eebb5","term":"mammal","forms":["mammal","mammals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"哺乳動物","explanation":"屬於哺乳綱的動物，核心特徵是母體用乳汁哺育幼崽；人、貓、鯨和蝙蝠都屬於 mammal。","examples":[{"en":"The children learned that dolphins are mammals.","zh":"孩子們瞭解到海豚是哺乳動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bat is a mammal capable of sustained flight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mammal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48b676e2b107da679512","word":"man","forms":["man"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-876960e79a44de17","term":"man","forms":["man","men"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成年男子","explanation":"最基本的意思是“成年男性”，也就是一個成年的男性人類，是“人”這一核心概念的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"A man was waiting outside the station.","zh":"一名男子正在車站外等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two men helped carry the table.","zh":"那兩名男子幫忙搬桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/man","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45e36eba39cdee92","term":"man","forms":["man","men"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人；某個人","explanation":"從“成年男性”擴大而來，可泛指一個人或人類中的任何人，通常帶有較正式、傳統或概括性的色彩。","examples":[{"en":"Every man must decide what matters most to him.","zh":"每個人都必須決定對自己最重要的是什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No man can solve this problem alone.","zh":"沒有人能獨自解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/man","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c09821eb3eb7088","term":"man","forms":["man","mans","manning","manned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……配備人員","explanation":"表示給船、崗位、裝置或其他任務安排“人手”，也就是讓某處有人負責工作；這裡的man承接了“人”的核心概念，但工作人員可以是任何性別。","examples":[{"en":"Two technicians man the control room at night.","zh":"兩名技術人員夜間負責值守控制室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The help desk is manned by volunteers on weekends.","zh":"服務檯週末由志願者值守。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/man","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e14f209c084a7384360e","word":"manage(ment)","forms":["manage","management"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61414c2c6c2691f6","term":"manage","forms":["manage","manages","managing","managed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"管理；負責","explanation":"指負責帶領人或掌管組織、團隊等，使它們按目標運作；重點是處在負責人的位置上。","examples":[{"en":"She manages a small design team in London.","zh":"她在倫敦負責管理一個小型設計團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He manages a small hotel by the coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f59a5372da20e74d","term":"manage","forms":["manage","manages","managing","managed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處理；控制局面","explanation":"指把問題、工作或局面控制住並妥善處理，未必意味著你是負責整個組織的人。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse managed the emergency calmly.","zh":"護士冷靜地處理了這場緊急情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't worry; we can manage without another assistant.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-849ec7bb1ef5a3e6","term":"manage","forms":["manage","manages","managing","managed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設法做到","explanation":"指事情並不容易，但某人還是想辦法完成了；它突出“克服困難後成功”。","examples":[{"en":"I managed to catch the last train.","zh":"我設法趕上了末班車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the pain, he managed to finish the race.","zh":"儘管很疼，他還是設法跑完了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06581c551fda0a5a","term":"management","forms":["management","managements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理；經營","explanation":"指為了達到明確目標，對人員、事務和有限資源進行規劃、組織、領導和執行的整個過程。它強調“把事情管起來”，而不只是某一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"Good management is essential for a successful business.","zh":"良好的管理對企業成功至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project requires careful management from start to finish.","zh":"這個專案從頭到尾都需要精心管理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/management","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0af4b8bcbf18a1f3","term":"management","forms":["management","managements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理層；經營者","explanation":"指組織中負責作決定、制定政策和監督運營的領導人員整體。這裡management不是“管理這件事”，而是“負責管理的人”。","examples":[{"en":"Management has agreed to improve working conditions.","zh":"管理層已同意改善工作條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Management rejected the union's latest proposal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/management","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ee4a469cd4e91053847","word":"manager","forms":["manager"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-687fed781bc0b5ff","term":"manager","forms":["manager","managers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理者；負責人","explanation":"指以管理某項事務為工作的人，例如負責公司、餐館、商店或專案運營的人；重點不只是“職位較高”，而是負責把事情組織和推進起來。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant manager changed the schedule for next week.","zh":"餐廳經理調整了下週的排班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works as a manager at a small technology company.","zh":"她在一家小型科技公司擔任經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manager","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b174569d3bf69730","term":"manager","forms":["manager","managers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球隊主教練；球隊負責人","explanation":"在體育語境中，指負責帶領和安排球隊的人，尤其常指足球或棒球隊的主教練。這個意思仍然圍繞“管理一支隊伍、讓它運轉起來”。","examples":[{"en":"The team’s manager announced the starting lineup before the match.","zh":"球隊主教練在比賽前公佈了首發陣容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager changed the formation at halftime.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manager","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d959b638663f9a7de663","word":"mandate","forms":["mandate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae93267227e1828b","term":"mandate","forms":["mandate","mandates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式命令或授權","explanation":"指由政府、法院、機構或有權力的人正式發出的命令，也可以指完成某項任務所獲得的正式許可權。核心感覺是某件事被鄭重地交到某人手裡，並要求按規定執行。","examples":[{"en":"The committee received a clear mandate to investigate the complaint.","zh":"委員會獲得了調查這起投訴的明確授權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court issued a mandate requiring the agency to change its policy.","zh":"法院釋出命令，要求該機構改變政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f37be87c8ee793f","term":"mandate","forms":["mandate","mandates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選民授予的政治授權","explanation":"指選舉結果賦予政治人物或政黨的行動權力，尤其表示選民認為他們有權推行某項政策。這裡的“命令”不是上級發給下級，而是選民把執政任務交給當選者。","examples":[{"en":"The new government claimed a mandate to reform the health-care system.","zh":"新政府聲稱選民授權它改革醫療保健體系。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The election gave the party a mandate for reform.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6815f3c300383519de8e","word":"mango","forms":["mango"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f6572537c14730a","term":"mango","forms":["mango","mangoes","mangos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"芒果樹","explanation":"指結芒果的熱帶果樹；在語境明確時，也可以直接用“mango”指這棵樹。它對應記憶影象中的“結著果實的樹”。","examples":[{"en":"We sat under a mango tree to escape the heat.","zh":"我們坐在一棵芒果樹下乘涼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A mango stood beside the old house.","zh":"老房子旁邊有一棵芒果樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mango","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc08b2a2c0e0612b","term":"mango","forms":["mango","mangoes","mangos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"芒果果實","explanation":"指芒果樹結出的果實，是最常見的日常義。它和樹義共用同一個詞，可以把它記成“樹上結出的果子”。","examples":[{"en":"I bought two ripe mangoes for breakfast.","zh":"我買了兩個熟芒果當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This mango tastes wonderfully sweet.","zh":"這個芒果吃起來特別甜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mango","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05b3abf2579a5eb66403","word":"manifest","forms":["manifest"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5cdfe5ece3ca9a7","term":"manifest","forms":["manifest","more manifest","most manifest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清楚可見的","explanation":"指某物已經清楚地呈現出來，尤其是肉眼可以看見或直接感知到，不再隱藏。","examples":[{"en":"The damage was manifest in the cracked walls.","zh":"牆上的裂縫清楚地顯示出損壞的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her relief was manifest in the smile on her face.","zh":"她臉上的笑容明顯流露出如釋重負的心情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manifest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74d274fc5640cdcd","term":"manifest","forms":["manifest","manifests","manifesting","manifested","manifestest","manifestedst","manifesteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯示；表明","explanation":"指把原本不夠明顯的情緒、特徵或事實清楚地表現出來，使別人能夠看見或確認它。","examples":[{"en":"The child manifested unusual courage during the rescue.","zh":"那個孩子在救援過程中表現出了非同尋常的勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His anxiety manifested itself in constant questions.","zh":"他的焦慮透過不停提問表現了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manifest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-191d560e80e26ef00854","word":"manipulate","forms":["manipulate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73649775f18da548","term":"manipulate","forms":["manipulate","manipulates","manipulating","manipulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用手操作或移動","explanation":"指用手拿、移、擺放或調整某物，重點是對物件進行直接的手上操作，是其他引申義的起點。","examples":[{"en":"She carefully manipulated the small pieces into place.","zh":"她小心地把小零件調整到合適的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician manipulated the controls with one hand.","zh":"技術員用一隻手操控那些控制裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manipulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5094a8af68ca9f00","term":"manipulate","forms":["manipulate","manipulates","manipulating","manipulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"操控資料或局面","explanation":"由“動手調整”引申為有意改變、整理或控制某種資訊、資料或局面，使它按自己的需要呈現或發展。","examples":[{"en":"The report claims that the figures were manipulated to hide the problem.","zh":"報告稱這些數字被人為改動，以掩蓋問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good software lets users manipulate data quickly.","zh":"好的軟體能讓使用者快速處理和調整資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manipulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a03c07a08b59b94f","term":"manipulate","forms":["manipulate","manipulates","manipulating","manipulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暗中操縱他人","explanation":"指利用影響力控制某人，使其在不清楚真實目的的情況下按操縱者的意願行動；通常暗示操縱者從中獲益。","examples":[{"en":"He manipulated his colleagues into supporting the plan.","zh":"他操縱同事，讓他們支援這項計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt that the advertisement was manipulating her emotions.","zh":"她覺得那則廣告在操控她的情緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manipulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52a1f90189a9280a56c9","word":"mankind/humankind","forms":["mankind","humankind"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bde62c7f50fd1451","term":"mankind","forms":["mankind"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全體人類","explanation":"指作為一個整體的所有人，即人類這個物種或全體人類。這個意義最常見，也最適合先掌握；它把每一個人都看作“人類”這一大群體的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are working together for the future of mankind.","zh":"科學家們正在為人類的未來共同努力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This discovery could change the way mankind uses energy.","zh":"這項發現可能改變人類利用能源的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mankind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-536499a526fc6157","term":"humankind","forms":["humankind","humankinds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全人類","explanation":"指地球上所有人組成的人類整體，也就是人類這個物種；重點在“整體”而不是某些具體的人。","examples":[{"en":"Humankind has always tried to understand the world around it.","zh":"人類一直在努力理解周圍的世界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Climate change is a serious threat to humankind.","zh":"氣候變化是對全人類的嚴重威脅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humankind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0425843ebda6f84d5ecf","word":"manner","forms":["manner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32b705165fe207e0","term":"manner","forms":["manner","manners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方式；做法","explanation":"manner 指一件事是怎樣做成或表現出來的方式，重點在“做法和呈現方式”，而不只是達到目標的工具。","examples":[{"en":"She explained the problem in a calm manner.","zh":"她用平靜的方式解釋了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was impressed by the manner in which he handled the complaint.","zh":"他處理投訴的方式給我留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71c50c512cfdfc2b","term":"manner","forms":["manner","manners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舉止；表現出來的樣子","explanation":"manner 也指一個人待人接物時表現出的整體樣子，包括語氣、動作和外在氣質；它像是“一個人做事的方式”長期顯露在人身上。","examples":[{"en":"His quiet manner made everyone feel comfortable.","zh":"他安靜沉穩的舉止讓每個人都感到自在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse spoke to the child in a gentle manner.","zh":"護士用溫和的態度和孩子說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30de4f96dcffa3c04512","word":"mansion","forms":["mansion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a4ff07ac0a28f40","term":"mansion","forms":["mansion","mansions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豪華大宅","explanation":"指規模很大、裝修豪華、通常屬於富人或顯貴的住宅或建築。這是mansion最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The actor bought a mansion in the hills.","zh":"那位演員在山裡買了一座豪宅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old mansion has been turned into a museum.","zh":"那座老宅已經被改成了博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mansion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36bde66f289a35683683","word":"manual","forms":["manual"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8c0ba120923aa23","term":"manual","forms":["manual","more manual","most manual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"人工完成的","explanation":"指由人親自完成，而不是交給機器或軟體自動處理；例如人工檢查能發現自動程式漏掉的問題。","examples":[{"en":"We carried out a manual check after the software finished scanning the files.","zh":"軟體掃描完檔案後，我們又進行了人工檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Manual inspection catches defects the camera sometimes misses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbdea2d14c4be8ea","term":"manual","forms":["manual","manuals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使用說明書","explanation":"指隨機器或產品提供、用來說明安裝、操作和故障處理方法的說明書；日常說 the manual 時，常常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"The printer is making a strange noise, so I checked the manual.","zh":"印表機發出奇怪的聲音，所以我查了說明書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the manual before removing the back panel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46c3ccf1e2a8855d","term":"manual","forms":["manual","manuals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手動擋車","explanation":"在汽車語境中，指需要駕駛員用離合器和換擋桿換擋的手動擋車輛，也可借指手動變速系統。","examples":[{"en":"I learned to drive in a manual, but my current car is automatic.","zh":"我學車時開的是手動擋車，但現在的車是自動擋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned to drive in a manual.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed0a3b494b3cd42a8d03","word":"manufacture","forms":["manufacture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39357b51d9893d8c","term":"manufacture","forms":["manufacture","manufactures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"製造；生產過程","explanation":"指按照一定流程、通常以較大規模製造商品的行動或過程。這裡強調從原料或部件到成品的系統生產。","examples":[{"en":"The factory specializes in the manufacture of electric bicycles.","zh":"這家工廠專門生產電動腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New rules will affect the manufacture of medical equipment.","zh":"新規定將影響醫療裝置的生產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manufacture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dab7d0b1f0009fdf","term":"manufacture","forms":["manufacture","manufactures","manufacturing","manufactured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"製造；生產","explanation":"指使用工具、體力勞動或機器，通常按一定流程大規模生產物品。它突出有計劃的製造活動，而不是偶然做出某件東西。","examples":[{"en":"The company manufactures parts for aircraft engines.","zh":"這家公司生產飛機發動機的零部件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These medicines are manufactured in a facility near the coast.","zh":"這些藥品在海邊附近的一家工廠生產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manufacture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10002859ace9985449d1","word":"manufacturer","forms":["manufacturer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df17785a98931da6","term":"manufacturer","forms":["manufacturer","manufacturers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"製造商；生產者","explanation":"指製造某種產品的人或公司，核心概念是把原材料或零件做成成品的那一方；在商業語境中通常指生產企業。","examples":[{"en":"The manufacturer produces parts for the car industry.","zh":"這家製造商為汽車工業生產零部件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please contact the manufacturer if the machine stops working.","zh":"如果機器停止工作，請聯絡製造商。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manufacturer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f10a68d54a88afcb636","word":"manuscript","forms":["manuscript"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-220054716c75ae9c","term":"manuscript","forms":["manuscript","manuscripts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手稿；手寫檔案","explanation":"指一份用手寫成的書、文章、樂譜或其他檔案，通常強調它是原始的手寫文字，而不是後來印刷的版本。","examples":[{"en":"The historian compared the manuscript with the printed edition.","zh":"歷史學家把這份手稿與印刷版進行了比較。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive preserves her original handwritten manuscript.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manuscript","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1137b15c7797aa84ec24","word":"many","forms":["many"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-544618988ba4800d","term":"many","forms":["many","more","most"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量很多的","explanation":"表示某類人或事物的數量很大，突出“多”這一整體特徵。這裡的 many 本身是形容詞，常用於說明某種情況中存在大量物件。","examples":[{"en":"The reasons for her decision are many.","zh":"她作出這個決定的原因很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dangers of the journey are many.","zh":"這段旅程有很多危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/many","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40d69cc269a65c36","term":"many","forms":["many","more","most"],"pos":"det","zh":"許多；很多","explanation":"放在可數名詞複數前，表示數量很多，但不說明確切數目。它是把“數量堆得很高”直接放到名詞前的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"Many students walk to school every day.","zh":"許多學生每天步行上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"How many tickets do we need?","zh":"我們需要多少張票？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/many","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0c6541855c89c84","term":"many","forms":["many"],"pos":"pron","zh":"許多人；許多事物","explanation":"名詞被省略後，many 自己承擔“很多人或很多東西”的意思。它延續了“數量堆得很高”的核心畫面，但具體指什麼要從上下文判斷。","examples":[{"en":"Many have tried, but few have succeeded.","zh":"許多人嘗試過，但成功的寥寥無幾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many believe that the plan will work.","zh":"許多人認為這個計劃會奏效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/many","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60be9861750facbfad87","word":"map","forms":["map"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24c2458f42ecd78a","term":"map","forms":["map","maps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地圖","explanation":"把一個真實或虛構的區域畫出來，用來顯示各個地點和其他要素相對位置的圖。它不一定是精確的地理測繪圖，也可以是故事世界或想象空間的地圖。","examples":[{"en":"We spread a map of the city across the table.","zh":"我們把一張城市地圖鋪在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children drew a map of the island in their story.","zh":"孩子們為故事中的島嶼畫了一張地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/map","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44eee299b8b35c4f","term":"map","forms":["map","maps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結構圖；關係圖","explanation":"把一個系統、結構或抽象領域的組成部分及其相互位置、聯絡表示出來的圖。這裡的map不一定表示地理位置，而是把複雜資訊整理成一眼能看懂的關係圖。","examples":[{"en":"The report includes a map of the company’s internal structure.","zh":"這份報告包含一張公司內部結構圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diagram provides a map of the organization's hierarchy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/map","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbe54bbc918a8535","term":"map","forms":["map","maps","mapping","mapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繪製成地圖","explanation":"把某個區域用地圖的形式表示出來，重點是完成“畫出地圖”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The atlas maps the entire coastline in detail.","zh":"這本地圖冊詳細繪出了整條海岸線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The surveyors mapped the newly discovered cave system.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/map","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1022b269d2041057","term":"map","forms":["map","maps","mapping","mapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"測繪；勘察","explanation":"為製作地圖而考察、測量或調查一個區域，並收集相關資訊。它強調獲取資訊的過程，不只是最後畫出成圖。","examples":[{"en":"Engineers are mapping the route of the new highway.","zh":"工程師們正在勘察新公路的路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Surveyors mapped the valley before construction began.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/map","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49ead2b1066bda1e127f","word":"maple","forms":["maple"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-413bca803e6932a6","term":"maple","forms":["maple","maples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"楓樹","explanation":"maple 是楓屬樹木的統稱，通常有掌狀葉和帶翅的種子。看到 maple 時，最基本的畫面就是一棵楓樹。","examples":[{"en":"They planted a maple in the front yard.","zh":"他們在前院種了一棵楓樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The maples turn bright red in autumn.","zh":"秋天，楓樹會變成鮮紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59fcea6baf8b6504","term":"maple","forms":["maple","maples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"楓木","explanation":"maple 也可以指楓樹的木材，常用於傢俱等物品；這裡關注的不是樹，而是樹被加工後的材料。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen island is made of maple.","zh":"廚房島臺是用楓木做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cabinet is built from solid maple.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51609286fb7f6089e0a0","word":"mar","forms":["mar"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f3039ba346d95a0","term":"mar","forms":["mar","mars","marring","marred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"損壞；破壞","explanation":"它表示把某物弄壞、弄得不完美，或破壞一件好事的效果。可以把它想成在完整的表面上留下瑕疵，因此既能說實體受損，也能說美好印象被破壞。","examples":[{"en":"A loud argument marred an otherwise pleasant evening.","zh":"一場激烈的爭吵破壞了原本愉快的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scratch marred the new car's finish.","zh":"這道劃痕損壞了新車的漆面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d205806e19dba5306a0","word":"marathon","forms":["marathon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf76267df94a32c9","term":"marathon","forms":["marathon","marathons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬拉松賽","explanation":"馬拉松是一項長距離公路賽，標準全程約為42.195公里；核心感覺就是跑很長的路並堅持到終點。","examples":[{"en":"She trained for six months before running her first marathon.","zh":"她訓練了六個月，才參加自己的第一次馬拉松。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She completed her first marathon in four hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marathon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae7d75af279b276a","term":"marathon","forms":["marathon","marathons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持久進行的活動","explanation":"這裡借用馬拉松路程很長的形象，指某項活動持續很久、規模很大，或在一段時間內連續進行。","examples":[{"en":"We had a movie marathon during the rainy weekend.","zh":"那個下雨的週末，我們連續看了一大串電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The negotiations became a three-day marathon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marathon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9dd98f82c7de3323b17","word":"marble","forms":["marble"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0eb6afe5105f6e2","term":"marble","forms":["marble","marbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大理石","explanation":"一種帶有晶體紋理的石灰岩變質岩，常用於建築、地面和雕刻；這是 marble 最基本的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The museum floor is made of white marble.","zh":"博物館的地面由白色大理石製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The staircase was carved from white marble.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa75b5c25fc089798cf9","word":"march","forms":["march"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc20d834a2341674","term":"march","forms":["march","marches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行進；行軍","explanation":"march 是按穩定節奏、邁著整齊步伐向前走，尤其常說士兵、樂隊或儀仗隊的這種走法。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers began their march at dawn.","zh":"士兵們在黎明時開始行軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band marched in step down the street.","zh":"樂隊邁著整齊的步伐沿街行進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/march","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ad7c36f94226825","term":"march","forms":["march","marches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持續推進","explanation":"從隊伍不斷向前行進引申而來，march 可以表示時間、歷史或某種程序穩定而持續地向前發展。","examples":[{"en":"The march of technology has changed how we work.","zh":"技術的不斷發展改變了我們的工作方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing can stop the march of time.","zh":"沒有什麼能阻擋時間向前流逝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/march","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cdd254bd65e7af8","term":"march","forms":["march","marches","marching","marched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"行進；齊步走","explanation":"march 表示像士兵一樣邁著長而規律的步子向前走，重點是步伐整齊、節奏穩定。","examples":[{"en":"The band marched through the town in the rain.","zh":"樂隊冒雨齊步走過了小鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guards marched in formation.","zh":"衛兵們列隊行進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/march","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4595176a1975c23","term":"march","forms":["march","marches","marching","marched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穩步推進","explanation":"由人或隊伍不斷向前行進引申而來，march 可以表示某個過程持續向前發展，常含有堅定或不可阻擋的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Despite the setbacks, the project marched forward.","zh":"儘管遇到挫折，這個專案仍在穩步推進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Time marches on, whether we are ready or not.","zh":"不管我們是否準備好，時間都在不斷向前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/march","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34e39f662ff56641cc73","word":"margin","forms":["margin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ccb1ae3ea5e72e3e","term":"margin","forms":["margin","margins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊緣；邊界","explanation":"指任何平面或區域的外緣，也就是從內部向外延伸到盡頭的位置；它把“紙邊”這個具體形象擴大到了湖泊、道路和土地等事物。","examples":[{"en":"We sat at the margin of the lake and watched the sunset.","zh":"我們坐在湖邊看日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wild flowers grew along the margin of the field.","zh":"野花沿著田地的邊緣生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/margin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5dd72b2a287a0682","term":"margin","forms":["margin","margins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"差額；差距","explanation":"指兩個結果、分數或特徵之間相差的距離，也就是從一個結果的邊界到另一個結果之間留下的空間。","examples":[{"en":"The team won by a margin of three points.","zh":"這支隊以三分的差距獲勝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was elected by a narrow margin.","zh":"她以微弱優勢當選。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/margin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d684c7eede18e14f","term":"margin","forms":["margin","margins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餘地；允許範圍","explanation":"指在某個界限之內還可以變化或出錯的空間，例如允許的誤差、時間上的寬裕或行動上的自由度。","examples":[{"en":"We left a small margin of error in the budget.","zh":"我們在預算中留出了一點誤差餘地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Allow a margin of ten minutes in case the train is late.","zh":"留出十分鐘的餘地，以防火車晚點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/margin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae4e19fd6a9209da19e1","word":"marginal","forms":["marginal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9d9a48e214c5b2f","term":"marginal","forms":["marginal","more marginal","most marginal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"邊緣的；邊際的","explanation":"指位於某個區域、範圍或事物邊緣附近的，也可以引申為處在主要部分之外但仍與其相鄰。重點是“靠邊”這個空間或抽象位置概念。","examples":[{"en":"Several rare birds live in the marginal areas of the wetland.","zh":"幾種稀有鳥類生活在溼地的邊緣區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The marginal seats could determine the election result.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marginal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2260497d89a94cfe","term":"marginal","forms":["marginal","more marginal","most marginal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"勉強的；差一點的","explanation":"表示某種能力、質量或結果只達到最低要求，雖然不能說完全沒有，但餘地很小、表現不理想。它保留了“只在邊緣線上”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Her qualifications are marginal at best, so she may not get the job.","zh":"她的資歷充其量只是勉強達標，所以可能得不到這份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report provides only marginal evidence for the claim.","zh":"這份報告為這一說法提供的證據十分有限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marginal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fe26efbd6c39984f653","word":"marine","forms":["marine"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6fc21f0d7837882","term":"marine","forms":["marine","more marine","most marine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"海洋的；海里的","explanation":"指屬于海洋、生活在海里，或由海水形成、產生的事物。這是 marine 最基本的含義，重點是“來自海或存在於海中”。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied marine animals near the reef.","zh":"研究人員研究了珊瑚礁附近的海洋動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Marine pollution is harming coastal ecosystems.","zh":"海洋汙染正在破壞沿海生態系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4100fe79306879a1","term":"marine","forms":["marine","more marine","most marine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"海上的；與航運或海軍有關的","explanation":"指與海上運輸、船運、海軍或海軍力量有關的事物。它把“海洋”這個範圍延伸到了人在海上的組織活動。","examples":[{"en":"The company provides insurance for marine transport.","zh":"這家公司為海上運輸提供保險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Marine insurance covers damage to ships and cargo.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb7923a3a43863d1","term":"marine","forms":["marine","marines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海軍陸戰隊員","explanation":"指受過訓練、在船上或從船上執行任務的海軍陸戰隊員。這裡的 marine 不是形容詞，而是指具體的人。","examples":[{"en":"Her brother joined the Marines after college.","zh":"她哥哥大學畢業後加入了海軍陸戰隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A marine helped evacuate the civilians.","zh":"一名海軍陸戰隊員幫助疏散了平民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6201eb4dccc956cc4fa3","word":"mark","forms":["mark"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5ffb785dabf0a1a","term":"mark","forms":["mark","marks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痕跡或特徵","explanation":"mark可以是留下的可見痕跡，也可以是顯示某種品質、關係或經歷的特徵；也就是說，某件事在物體或人身上留下了清晰的“標記”。","examples":[{"en":"There is a dark mark on the wall.","zh":"牆上有一道深色的痕跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her kindness is a mark of her character.","zh":"她的善良體現了她的性格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0763bdcce6e3317","term":"mark","forms":["mark","marks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"位置或目標標誌","explanation":"mark可以是用來指示位置、方向或射擊目標的標誌；它把注意力和行動“標”到一個明確的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The archer took careful aim at the mark.","zh":"那名弓箭手仔細瞄準了靶標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The red flag marks the entrance.","zh":"紅旗標出了入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20f45b2fbca2776e","term":"mark","forms":["mark","marks","marking","marked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……做標記","explanation":"在物品上留下記號、寫上名稱或貼上標籤，使它容易被認出或分類；這正是“留下一個清晰的標記”的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please mark each box with its destination.","zh":"請在每個箱子上標明目的地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She marked the pages she wanted to read again.","zh":"她給想再讀一遍的頁面做了標記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ade77e709c4a21bd","term":"mark","forms":["mark","marks","marking","marked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"注意；留意","explanation":"把注意力“標”到某人或某事上，認真留意並記住它；現代英語中最常保留在習語“mark my words”裡。","examples":[{"en":"Mark my words, this plan will cause trouble.","zh":"記住我的話，這個計劃會惹出麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mark my words: she will win the competition.","zh":"記住我的話：她會贏得比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed5b8120601641c516d0","word":"marker","forms":["marker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4db926697b15ff1","term":"marker","forms":["marker","markers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標記工具或留下記號的人","explanation":"指用來畫線、寫字或留下明顯痕跡的工具，尤其常指馬克筆；也可以泛指負責留下這種標記的人或物。","examples":[{"en":"Don't use the permanent marker on the whiteboard.","zh":"別在白板上用油性馬克筆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used a blue marker to circle the important words.","zh":"她用藍色馬克筆圈出了重要的詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15e4175f8ca01fa9","term":"marker","forms":["marker","markers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標誌；指標","explanation":"指能顯示位置、數量、進展或某種變化的事物。它不一定是實體物品，也可以是一個事件或現象，像一個提醒人們“變化已經發生”的訊號。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy was a marker of changing attitudes.","zh":"這項新政策是觀念正在改變的一個標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rising attendance is a marker of growing interest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4d693d24e646cb78784","word":"market","forms":["market"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54f6fcd7fdb509d6","term":"market","forms":["market","markets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"定期集市","explanation":"指人們在固定時間聚集、買賣商品的市場活動；核心畫面就是買家、賣家和貨物在同一處匯聚。","examples":[{"en":"The town holds a farmers' market every Saturday.","zh":"這個鎮每週六都會舉辦農貿市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought fresh bread at the morning market.","zh":"我們在早市買了新鮮麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/market","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a0477d673a4f9e3","term":"market","forms":["market","markets","marketing","marketed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推廣上市","explanation":"指把產品或服務帶入買賣場景，向目標顧客宣傳並準備銷售；它連線了“市場”這個場所和商業行為。","examples":[{"en":"The company markets its software to small businesses.","zh":"這家公司把自己的軟體推廣給小型企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drink is marketed as a healthy alternative to soda.","zh":"這種飲料被宣傳成汽水的健康替代品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/market","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf929d06a4e69002b7b2","word":"marriage","forms":["marriage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eabb3503ad8beba8","term":"marriage","forms":["marriage","marriages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"婚姻狀態","explanation":"指已婚的狀態或婚姻生活本身，重點是兩人已經處於婚姻關係中，而不是舉行婚禮的那一刻。","examples":[{"en":"She entered marriage with realistic expectations.","zh":"她以切合實際的期待步入婚姻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Marriage requires patience and trust.","zh":"婚姻需要耐心和信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marriage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1e208c397e55348","term":"marriage","forms":["marriage","marriages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"婚姻關係","explanation":"指兩人或多人透過婚姻形成的家庭關係，以及隨之產生的法律、社會或宗教權利和責任；這裡更強調這種結合本身。","examples":[{"en":"Their marriage brought the two families closer together.","zh":"他們的婚姻使兩個家庭更加親近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law recognizes marriage between two consenting adults.","zh":"法律承認兩名自願成年人的婚姻關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marriage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9ce3beb80492facbec3","word":"married","forms":["married"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4c49e29ffe3965d","term":"married","forms":["married"],"pos":"adj","zh":"已婚的","explanation":"指一個人目前處於婚姻關係中，有配偶。它描寫的是婚姻狀態，而不是單純指剛剛完成結婚這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"Are you married or single?","zh":"你結婚了嗎，還是單身？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been married to Daniel for ten years.","zh":"她和丹尼爾結婚十年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/married","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28e96b28d33c1f44","term":"married","forms":["married"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全心投入的","explanation":"把婚姻中牢固的連線關係比作人與某項工作或事物的關係，表示一個人幾乎把全部精力和忠誠都放在它上面。","examples":[{"en":"He is so married to his work that he rarely takes a vacation.","zh":"他全心撲在工作上，幾乎從不休假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was married to his work and rarely took holidays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/married","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d84f13234092bdc60e2","word":"marry","forms":["marry"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cef33baa0cd0caa","term":"marry","forms":["marry","marries","marrying","married"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結婚","explanation":"指一個人進入婚姻，成為某人的丈夫或妻子。這裡的重點是這個人開始處於婚姻關係中，而不是專指舉行婚禮的儀式。","examples":[{"en":"They decided to marry after living together for two years.","zh":"他們一起生活兩年後決定結婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her youngest daughter married last spring.","zh":"她最小的女兒去年春天結婚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0f5ca759d523354","term":"marry","forms":["marry","marries","marrying","married"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與……結婚","explanation":"表示把某人作為自己的丈夫或妻子，也就是“和某人結婚”。它突出結婚物件，而不是婚禮本身。","examples":[{"en":"She married her college sweetheart at the age of twenty-six.","zh":"她二十六歲時和大學戀人結了婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hopes to marry someone who shares his values.","zh":"他希望和一個價值觀相同的人結婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5e390af6083f636548d","word":"martial","forms":["martial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6bfddcd8d25c1da4","term":"martial","forms":["martial","more martial","most martial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"戰爭的；好戰的","explanation":"指與戰爭有關，或帶有戰爭般的激烈、強硬氣息。它可以描述事物的性質，也可以形容整體氛圍像戰爭一樣緊張或有攻擊性。","examples":[{"en":"The film opens with a striking martial display.","zh":"這部電影一開場就是一場氣勢逼人的戰爭場面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speech adopted a martial tone.","zh":"這篇演講採取了強硬而好戰的語調。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/martial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cd3e109f234cf26","term":"martial","forms":["martial","more martial","most martial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"軍事的；軍隊生活的","explanation":"指與武裝部隊、軍職或軍隊生活有關的事物，是“戰爭的”在制度和職業領域中的具體延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers were tried under martial law.","zh":"這些士兵依照戒嚴法接受審判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The academy imposed strict martial discipline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/martial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38868dc905f4d6d6de71","word":"marvel","forms":["marvel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"marvel","forms":["marvel"],"pos":"v.","zh":"感到驚奇；讚嘆","examples":[{"en":"Visitors marvel at the size of the ancient temple.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"I still marvel at how quickly the children learned the song.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"marvel","forms":["marvel"],"pos":"n.","zh":"令人驚嘆的人事物","examples":[{"en":"The bridge is a marvel of modern engineering.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"This tiny camera is a technological marvel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-e7bc37c63185e4ecdd21","word":"marvelous","forms":["marvelous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14c82c9d5605fa5e","term":"marvelous","forms":["marvelous","more marvelous","most marvelous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人驚歎的；精彩的","explanation":"形容某人或某事好得出乎意料、令人驚歎；在日常表達中也就是“非常棒、精彩”。它保留了“像奇蹟一樣讓人驚喜”的核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"We had a marvelous time at the festival.","zh":"我們在節日活動上玩得非常開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She did a marvelous job organizing the event.","zh":"她把這次活動組織得棒極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marvelous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b01cc7b0a6012d960af4","word":"masculine","forms":["masculine"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88c94e92306f1bf6","term":"masculine","forms":["masculine","more masculine","most masculine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"男性的；有男子氣概的","explanation":"表示某人或某物與男性、男子氣概或傳統上被視為男性化的特徵有關，是“站在男性這一邊”的一般說法。","examples":[{"en":"He prefers a more masculine style of clothing.","zh":"他更喜歡偏男性化的服裝風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room has a simple, masculine design.","zh":"這個房間採用了簡潔的男性化設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masculine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb8679ea35033eb9","term":"masculine","forms":["masculine","more masculine","most masculine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"男性的；雄性的","explanation":"專指生理性別屬於男性或雄性，與 female 相對，強調生物學上的性別，而不是性格或外表。","examples":[{"en":"The study compared masculine and feminine patterns in the data.","zh":"這項研究比較了資料中的男性和女性模式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The embryo developed masculine characteristics.","zh":"這個胚胎髮育出了雄性特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masculine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c871175db1eb7961","term":"masculine","forms":["masculine","more masculine","most masculine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陽性的；陽性語法的","explanation":"在有語法性別的語言中，表示某個名詞、代詞或相關形式屬於“陽性”這一語法類別；它不一定說明所指的人或物是男性。","examples":[{"en":"In German, the word for “table” is masculine.","zh":"在德語中，“桌子”這個詞屬於陽性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In Spanish, this noun takes a masculine article.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masculine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c13e8eab33659458","term":"masculine","forms":["masculine","masculines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陽性","explanation":"指語法性別中的陽性類別，即與陰性或中性相對的一類形式。","examples":[{"en":"In this language, the masculine includes several different noun endings.","zh":"在這種語言中，陽性包括幾種不同的名詞詞尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In French, the masculine of blanche is blanc.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masculine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48bf9b4f142ab45cac6f","word":"mask","forms":["mask"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9b1e9d8bcda5c28","term":"mask","forms":["mask","masks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面具；防護面罩","explanation":"遮住臉部的東西，可以用來偽裝身份，也可以保護臉部免受傷害；核心就是“遮住或擋住”。","examples":[{"en":"The fencer adjusted her mask before the match.","zh":"擊劍運動員在比賽前調整了她的面罩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wore a mask to protect his face from the dust.","zh":"他戴著面罩，以保護臉部不受塵土影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9391087c12ffcdb","term":"mask","forms":["mask","masks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"掩飾；偽裝","explanation":"指用某種外表、藉口或行為遮住真實的身份、意圖或感情，就像用面具擋住真正的臉。","examples":[{"en":"His cheerful smile was only a mask for his anxiety.","zh":"他愉快的笑容只是掩飾焦慮的外表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity campaign became a mask for the company's real interests.","zh":"這場慈善活動成了掩蓋公司真實利益的幌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd38d646b5c786e6","term":"mask","forms":["mask","masks","masking","masked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遮住以保護或隱藏身份","explanation":"mask表示把臉或其他部位遮住，通常是為了隱藏身份，或防止受傷、受到傷害；這裡正體現了“遮住或擋住”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The dancers masked their faces before entering the hall.","zh":"舞者們進入大廳前遮住了臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He masked the cut on his cheek with a small dressing.","zh":"他用一小塊敷料遮住了臉頰上的傷口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9446f9b8749f4a77","term":"mask","forms":["mask","masks","masking","masked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掩蓋；隱藏","explanation":"mask表示把事實、問題、情緒或資訊遮起來，使別人看不見或不知道；它把“遮住臉”的概念引申到了抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"A cheerful smile masked her anxiety during the interview.","zh":"面試期間，她用愉快的笑容掩蓋了焦慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strong sales figures masked serious problems in the supply chain.","zh":"強勁的銷售資料掩蓋了供應鏈中的嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mask","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4084a32b9bba4b4a03d0","word":"mass","forms":["mass"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdca29139bf073ec","term":"mass","forms":["mass","masses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量；總量","explanation":"指數量很大的東西，或把許多東西合在一起計算出的總量；許多零散的東西像聚成了一大團。","examples":[{"en":"A mass of paperwork arrived before the deadline.","zh":"截止日期前送來了一大堆檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report summarizes the mass of evidence collected.","zh":"這份報告總結了收集到的大量證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3868f717a39bbb63","term":"mass","forms":["mass","masses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彌撒；聖餐禮","explanation":"指基督教，尤其羅馬天主教中舉行聖餐禮的核心宗教儀式。它與“大量”的 mass 只是拼寫相同，意義來自另一條教會詞源。","examples":[{"en":"She attends Mass every Sunday.","zh":"她每個星期日都參加彌撒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The church was full before Mass began.","zh":"彌撒開始前，教堂裡已經坐滿了人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3aeadbcaafc890ebe45","word":"massage","forms":["massage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8f4207f081951bf","term":"massage","forms":["massage","massages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"按摩","explanation":"指用手揉、按或拍打人的身體，以幫助放鬆、緩解疼痛，或讓肌肉為運動做好準備。它既可以指按摩這種活動，也可以指一次按摩。","examples":[{"en":"I had a massage after the long flight.","zh":"長途飛行後我做了一次按摩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A gentle massage helped relax her shoulders.","zh":"輕柔的按摩幫助她放鬆了肩膀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/massage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-100fe0a997ed55df","term":"massage","forms":["massage","massages","massaging","massaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……按摩","explanation":"指用手揉、按或推某人的身體或身體部位，也就是進行按摩。","examples":[{"en":"She massaged my neck after I worked at the desk all day.","zh":"我在辦公桌前工作了一整天后，她給我按摩了脖子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Massage the sore muscles gently.","zh":"輕輕按摩疼痛的肌肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/massage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c7bbbc199d3b161dca1","word":"massive","forms":["massive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-246cb9348464624c","term":"massive","forms":["massive","more massive","most massive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巨大的；規模龐大的","explanation":"指大小、範圍或規模遠超普通水平，核心畫面就是一件大得驚人的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The company built a massive new warehouse outside the city.","zh":"這家公司在城外建了一座巨大的新倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A massive crowd gathered in the square.","zh":"廣場上聚集了一大群人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/massive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-560b98de5ae80213","term":"massive","forms":["massive","more massive","most massive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巨大而沉重結實的","explanation":"強調物體不僅大，而且給人沉重、厚實、堅固的感覺；巨石、行星或大型裝置都可以這樣描述。","examples":[{"en":"A massive boulder blocked the narrow road.","zh":"一塊巨大而沉重的巨石擋住了狹窄的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has massive wooden doors.","zh":"這家博物館有厚重結實的木門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/massive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc613b4dfd6736a7bd26","word":"master","forms":["master"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc9ed8995d232837","term":"master","forms":["master","masters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"掌控者；主人","explanation":"指能夠控制某人、某物或某種局面的人，核心是擁有支配權或主導權。","examples":[{"en":"After years of practice, she became master of the old technique.","zh":"經過多年的練習，她掌握了這項古老技藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sailors believed they were masters of the sea.","zh":"水手們相信自己能夠駕馭大海。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/master","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b266b6f6752ae39","term":"master","forms":["master","masters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專家；高手","explanation":"指在某一領域擁有極高技能和造詣的人，已經把相關能力掌握到很高水平。","examples":[{"en":"She is a master of negotiation and rarely loses a deal.","zh":"她是談判高手，很少談丟一筆交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chef is a master of delicate flavors.","zh":"這位廚師特別擅長調配細膩的味道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/master","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9c9edbb639be74d","term":"master","forms":["master","masters","mastering","mastered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"熟練掌握","explanation":"表示透過長期學習和練習，把技能、知識或藝術掌握到很高水平，達到近乎能夠自如駕馭的程度。","examples":[{"en":"It took him years to master the violin.","zh":"他花了多年時間才熟練掌握小提琴演奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She quickly mastered the new software.","zh":"她很快就熟練掌握了這款新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/master","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-498a5e52b139091423c8","word":"masterpiece","forms":["masterpiece"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-294a08024ab1081d","term":"masterpiece","forms":["masterpiece","masterpieces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表作；傑作","explanation":"指受到評論界或公眾高度讚譽的作品，尤其強調它可能是某位創作者一生中最出色、最具代表性的一件作品。","examples":[{"en":"Many critics consider this film her masterpiece.","zh":"許多評論家認為這部電影是她的代表作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting is widely regarded as the artist's masterpiece.","zh":"這幅畫被廣泛認為是這位藝術家的傑作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masterpiece","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d37a390acfaf5ecd","term":"masterpiece","forms":["masterpiece","masterpieces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傑出作品","explanation":"泛指在創意、技巧或製作水平上特別出色的作品，不一定是作者一生中最重要或最受讚譽的那一件。","examples":[{"en":"The chef's final dish was a masterpiece of balance and flavor.","zh":"這位廚師最後做出的菜在搭配和風味上堪稱傑作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The symphony is widely considered her masterpiece.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/masterpiece","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38011b43becd198ef78a","word":"mastery","forms":["mastery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-494256dc447a0958","term":"mastery","forms":["mastery","masteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精通；熟練掌握","explanation":"指透過學習和練習把某項技能、學科或語言掌握到很高水平，彷彿已經能夠完全駕馭它。這是現代英語中最重要、最常用的義項。","examples":[{"en":"She achieved mastery of three programming languages.","zh":"她精通三種程式語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mastery of the basics takes time and practice.","zh":"熟練掌握基礎知識需要時間和練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mastery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7673f68f792f6be3","term":"mastery","forms":["mastery","masteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支配；控制權","explanation":"指對某人、某地或某種局勢擁有控制權和主導地位，重點是“掌控在自己手裡”，而不只是暫時獲勝。","examples":[{"en":"The rebels fought for mastery of the mountain passes.","zh":"叛軍爭奪山口的控制權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The victory gave the navy mastery of the channel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mastery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c1c541af9cc252a1c75","word":"mat","forms":["mat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-765079b03372516c","term":"mat","forms":["mat","mats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"墊子；地墊","explanation":"指一塊扁平、通常較粗糙的材料，鋪在地上用來擦腳、裝飾地面或保護地板。","examples":[{"en":"Please wipe your shoes on the mat before coming inside.","zh":"進來之前請在墊子上擦擦鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a rubber mat beside the back door.","zh":"後門旁邊有一張橡膠墊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3012b611e6f6ac31","term":"mat","forms":["mat","mats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隔熱墊；杯墊","explanation":"指放在桌面或其他表面上的小墊子，用來防止熱、硬或粗糙的物品損壞表面。","examples":[{"en":"Put the hot pan on a mat to protect the table.","zh":"把熱鍋放在隔熱墊上，以免弄壞桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put a mat beneath the hot casserole.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-367f17f087f12932","term":"mat","forms":["mat","mats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"糾結成團的一層","explanation":"指許多細長或纖維狀東西糾結在一起，形成像墊子一樣的厚團；這個意思仍然保留了“鋪成一層”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"A thick mat of weeds covered the pond.","zh":"一層厚厚的雜草糾結著，覆蓋了池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her hair had formed a tangled mat after the hike.","zh":"徒步之後，她的頭髮糾結成了一團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4945a70fa7f9c13fe193","word":"match","forms":["match"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4c486710e66afd3","term":"match","forms":["match","matches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽","explanation":"兩方或多方為了勝負而進行的體育比賽，也可指類似的正式較量。","examples":[{"en":"Our team has a match against the school across town on Saturday.","zh":"我們隊星期六要和城另一頭的學校比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She watched the tennis match with her parents.","zh":"她和父母一起觀看了網球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/match","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de63dd5bb150727b","term":"match","forms":["match","matches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對手；敵手","explanation":"某人在某種能力上足以與另一個人抗衡，甚至超過對方；“meet one’s match”就是遇到了強勁對手。","examples":[{"en":"After beating every challenger, she finally met her match.","zh":"她打敗了所有挑戰者後，終於遇到了強勁的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the final, she finally met her match.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/match","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5f34b45f56d879e","term":"match","forms":["match","matches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相配的一對","explanation":"指兩個彼此適合、特點協調的事物或人，放在一起正好成對；這就是“匹配”這條主線的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The blue curtains are a good match for the new sofa.","zh":"藍色窗簾和新沙發很相配。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Those two make a wonderful match.","zh":"他們兩個真是天作之合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/match","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b53cd362c15bcb6b","term":"match","forms":["match","matches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火柴","explanation":"頂端帶有可燃物、擦過粗糙表面就能點燃的小木籤或紙籤。","examples":[{"en":"He struck a match to light the candle.","zh":"他划著一根火柴來點蠟燭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep the matches away from the children.","zh":"請把火柴放在孩子夠不到的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/match","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e048fd2a62f13078660","word":"mate","forms":["mate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-754fb28b2965b996","term":"mate","forms":["mate","mates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夥伴；同伴","explanation":"指和某人一起生活、工作、學習或共同承擔某件事的人，也可以指共同組成某種關係的一方。這個義項是“和另一方連在一起”的基本概念。","examples":[{"en":"She is my classmate and my closest mate at school.","zh":"她既是我的同班同學，也是我在學校最親近的夥伴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My hiking mate carried the spare water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe515590b5ca6f90","term":"mate","forms":["mate","mates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"朋友；夥計","explanation":"在英國、澳大利亞、愛爾蘭等地的口語中，指通常同性別的朋友或熟人，是“夥伴”義在日常交往中的親近用法。","examples":[{"en":"I am meeting a few mates after work.","zh":"我下班後要和幾個朋友見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My old school mate helped me move house.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22aa23c6a5a93713","term":"mate","forms":["mate","mates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夥計；朋友","explanation":"在上述地區的口語中，可把 mate 當作對年齡相仿、通常為男性的陌生人的友好稱呼，語氣類似“夥計”。","examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, mate, could you tell me where the station is?","zh":"不好意思，夥計，你能告訴我車站在哪兒嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thanks, mate; I owe you one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8196e9a10d1e6df","term":"mate","forms":["mate","mates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成對物品中的另一件","explanation":"指與某件物品成套或相配的另一件，例如一隻襪子對應的另一隻。這裡的“夥伴”從人擴充套件到了物品。","examples":[{"en":"I found one earring, but I still cannot find its mate.","zh":"我找到了一隻耳環，但還是找不到它的另一隻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found one glove but lost its mate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e2c5c7d9b2c55b2","term":"mate","forms":["mate","mates","mating","mated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相配；嚴密接合","explanation":"指兩個物件彼此配合得很好，連線後沒有空隙，或正好能夠組成一套。這是從“夥伴在一起”擴充套件出的物品義。","examples":[{"en":"These two pieces mate perfectly.","zh":"這兩塊零件嚴絲合縫地接在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The replacement plug mates perfectly with the original socket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40b30b4e8f0d137056ac","word":"material","forms":["material"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40c8d4ed5b989377","term":"material","forms":["material","materials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"材料；原料","explanation":"指用來製造、建造或組成實體物品的物質，如木材、金屬、塑膠和纖維。這是名詞 material 最基本的意義。","examples":[{"en":"We need stronger material for the bridge.","zh":"我們需要更結實的材料來建這座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toy is made from recycled materials.","zh":"這個玩具由回收材料製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/material","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-352d4bd055e7ccaa","term":"material","forms":["material","materials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料；素材","explanation":"指可用於寫作、教學、研究或形成判斷的資訊、資料、觀察和想法。它把“可加工的物質”引申成“可加工的資訊”。","examples":[{"en":"I gathered enough material for my presentation.","zh":"我收集了足夠的演示資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interviews provided material for her biography.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/material","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d84cbe8b573d0b43acc3","word":"mathematical","forms":["mathematical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14734159cba64a72","term":"mathematical","forms":["mathematical","more mathematical","most mathematical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數學的；與數學有關的","explanation":"表示直接屬於數學、使用數學方法，或和數學研究、計算有關。這是最基本、最應先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers built a mathematical model of the spread of the disease.","zh":"研究人員建立了一個描述疾病傳播的數學模型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The problem requires careful mathematical reasoning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mathematical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4274e0c4e0f9a7a5","term":"mathematical","forms":["mathematical","more mathematical","most mathematical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"像公式一樣精確的","explanation":"形容動作、結構、安排或方法非常精確、整齊而有規律，彷彿每一步都能按公式計算；這裡不一定真的涉及數學。","examples":[{"en":"The dancers moved with mathematical precision.","zh":"舞者的動作精準得像經過公式計算一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The watchmaker positioned the tiny gears with mathematical exactness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mathematical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36b336a1b4cefee92a4e","word":"mathematics/math","forms":["mathematics","math"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-103114f67d65764a","term":"mathematics","forms":["mathematics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數學這門學科","explanation":"指用數、形狀、結構和關係來描述並推理的系統性學科，不僅包括日常算術，也包括更抽象的數學領域。","examples":[{"en":"Mathematics helps us describe patterns in nature.","zh":"數學幫助我們描述自然界中的規律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose to study mathematics at university.","zh":"她選擇在大學學習數學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mathematics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-625610f05aec1243","term":"mathematics","forms":["mathematics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數學能力","explanation":"指一個人計算、理解數學關係以及運用不同數學方法的能力；這裡說的是掌握這套結構的水平，而不是數學學科本身。","examples":[{"en":"My mathematics has improved since I started practicing every day.","zh":"自從我開始每天練習以來，我的數學能力提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His mathematics improved through regular practice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mathematics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1fa4ece1e96347a","term":"math","forms":["math","maths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數學","explanation":"math是mathematics的非正式簡稱，指研究數字、數量、形狀和規律的學科，也可泛指學校裡的數學學習。","examples":[{"en":"I was never very good at math in school.","zh":"我上學時數學一直不太好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studies math and physics at university.","zh":"她在大學學習數學和物理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/math","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1a68c8a4a91ca8e","term":"math","forms":["math","maths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算；算賬","explanation":"這裡的math不再只是學科名稱，而是指為了判斷結果而進行的數字計算；因此do the math常表示“把數字算清楚，你就會明白”。","examples":[{"en":"Do the math before you decide whether the deal is worth it.","zh":"先把賬算清楚，再決定這筆交易是否划算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do the math before agreeing to that loan.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/math","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57523f642f63eabb2a4f","word":"matter","forms":["matter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b54a6f708019abb","term":"matter","forms":["matter","matters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物質；材料","explanation":"matter 指構成物體或存在於自然界中的物質，重點是“東西由什麼構成”。","examples":[{"en":"Water is a form of matter.","zh":"水是一種物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists study how matter changes.","zh":"科學家研究物質如何變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-789edb490408b7aa","term":"matter","forms":["matter","matters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事情；問題","explanation":"matter 也指正在談論或需要處理的事情，尤其常指令人擔憂的情況或麻煩。","examples":[{"en":"What is the matter with your phone?","zh":"你的手機出什麼問題了？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to discuss this matter today.","zh":"我們今天需要討論這件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb0feb2ab4c6b970","term":"matter","forms":["matter","matters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要性","explanation":"matter 還可以表示一件事是否值得在意，也就是它的分量或重要性；這正是動詞 matter“要緊”的名詞對應概念。","examples":[{"en":"Money is not the only matter of importance.","zh":"金錢不是唯一重要的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exact shade is of little matter here.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11a249dfa5c474b4","term":"matter","forms":["matter","matters","mattering","mattered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重要；要緊","explanation":"matter 作動詞時表示某事有分量、會影響結果，因而值得在意；這就是“這件事擺在桌上，而且不能忽略”。","examples":[{"en":"Your opinion really matters to me.","zh":"你的意見對我真的很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What matters is that everyone is safe.","zh":"重要的是每個人都安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-098223b63ef7e402c389","word":"mattress","forms":["mattress"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2abf232d954fd9ca","term":"mattress","forms":["mattress","mattresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"床墊","explanation":"供人躺下和睡覺的厚墊子，通常放在床架上，由彈簧、泡沫等柔軟材料和外層布料組成。","examples":[{"en":"We need to replace the old mattress before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人來之前，我們得把舊床墊換掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This mattress is too firm for me.","zh":"這張床墊對我來說太硬了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mattress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d30726493527b61af2e","word":"mature","forms":["mature"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88a7f1ff8f512caa","term":"mature","forms":["mature","more mature","most mature"],"pos":"adj","zh":"成熟的；穩重的","explanation":"指人在身體、行為或思考方面已經發展得較充分，通常也帶有穩重、懂事的意味；也可以形容達到成熟狀態的事物。","examples":[{"en":"She is quite mature for her age.","zh":"她比同齡人穩重成熟得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young actor gave a remarkably mature performance.","zh":"這位年輕演員的表演成熟得令人印象深刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bbfa09089c3e29ec","term":"mature","forms":["mature","more mature","most mature"],"pos":"adj","zh":"成熟的；準備充分的","explanation":"指計劃、想法或其他事物已經發展完整，達到可以實施或使用的程度。","examples":[{"en":"We need a more mature plan before we ask for funding.","zh":"在申請資金前，我們需要一個更成熟、更完善的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technology is mature enough for everyday use.","zh":"這項技術已經成熟到足以用於日常生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec7314f5a9c2ab6e9aee","word":"maturity","forms":["maturity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-841e0b3a17067f62","term":"maturity","forms":["maturity","maturities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成熟狀態","explanation":"指人、動物、食物、飲料或其他事物發展到充分、完善並能發揮其性質的階段。它強調“走到了成熟的終點”，不只用於人的性格。","examples":[{"en":"The wine develops its richest flavor after years of maturity.","zh":"這款酒經過多年的陳化後，才能發展出最濃郁的風味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her maturity helped her handle the difficult decision calmly.","zh":"她的成熟讓她能夠冷靜地處理這個艱難的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maturity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9ec8cc42618daa8","term":"maturity","forms":["maturity","maturities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體發育完成","explanation":"特指身體生長基本完成、達到成年或具備繁殖能力的階段，是“成熟”在生物發育上的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"Most birds reach maturity within their first year.","zh":"大多數鳥在第一年內達到性成熟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sexual maturity arrives much later in elephants than in mice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maturity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a64ff09886cc35fe5f5","word":"maximum","forms":["maximum"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-482ec0411ddb1d66","term":"maximum","forms":["maximum"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最大的；最高限度的","explanation":"表示某種程度已經達到允許或可能達到的頂端，例如最大效果、最大劑量或最大速度。","examples":[{"en":"Use the proper dose for the maximum effect.","zh":"使用適當的劑量，以達到最大效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not exceed the maximum permitted load.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maximum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4defb694fc7a3ef1","term":"maximum","forms":["maximum","maxima","maximums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最高限度；最大程度","explanation":"指一件事所能達到的頂端，也就是不能再往上增加的限度；它可以指數量，也可以指抽象程度。","examples":[{"en":"The machine can operate at a maximum of 80 degrees.","zh":"這臺機器最高可以在八十度下執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We want to get the maximum from this opportunity.","zh":"我們想充分利用這次機會，取得最大收穫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maximum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee4d988c65de860fabbf","word":"may","forms":["may"],"officialPos":"aux.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22db6bb131efdff1","term":"may","forms":["may","might"],"pos":"verb","zh":"可以；獲准","explanation":"may 表示某人獲准做某事，像是得到一扇可以開啟的門；在疑問句中也常用於禮貌請求許可。","examples":[{"en":"You may leave after the test.","zh":"考試結束後你可以離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"May I use your phone?","zh":"我可以用你的手機嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/may","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbb5bebf9e118491","term":"may","forms":["may","might"],"pos":"verb","zh":"可能","explanation":"may 表示事情有可能發生，但說話人並不確定；這仍然是那扇門“可能開啟，也可能不開啟”。","examples":[{"en":"It may rain this evening.","zh":"今晚可能會下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She may be at home.","zh":"她可能在家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/may","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcfff5eb40423f055a4c","word":"maybe","forms":["maybe"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d03279ebbae2fbb","term":"maybe","forms":["maybe"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也許；可能","explanation":"表示某事有可能發生，但說話人沒有把握，是最基本、最常用的“半開著的門”。","examples":[{"en":"Maybe we can finish the report before lunch.","zh":"也許我們能在午飯前完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Maybe the parcel will arrive tomorrow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maybe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd44ec0c11b6a7dd","term":"maybe","forms":["maybe"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也許吧；暫不表態","explanation":"用於回答或回應時，表示既不明確同意，也不明確反對，意思接近“說不準”或“先看看”。它仍然來自“事情懸而未決”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"“Are you coming with us?” “Maybe—I need to check my schedule.”","zh":"“你要和我們一起去嗎？”“也許吧——我得先看看日程。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"'Maybe,' he replied, unwilling to commit himself.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maybe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd51a825d06aae5299fc","word":"mayor","forms":["mayor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d4ffa9eefd38463","term":"mayor","forms":["mayor","mayors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"市長；鎮長","explanation":"mayor 是城市、城鎮或其他自治市地方政府的主要行政負責人，負責代表並管理這個地方。中文通常譯為“市長”，但在較小的地方也可譯為“鎮長”或類似稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor of the city opened the new library.","zh":"這座城市的市長為新圖書館揭幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Voters elected a new mayor last year.","zh":"選民去年選出了一位新市長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mayor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fae5a4ecd6f6a12f","term":"mayor","forms":["mayor","mayors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禮儀性市長","explanation":"在美國某些地方，mayor 主要主持市議會和代表城市出席活動，而實際行政事務由受聘的城市經理負責，因此這個職位可能偏禮儀性。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor presides over the council, while the city manager runs daily operations.","zh":"市長主持市議會，而城市經理負責日常運作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ceremonial mayor welcomed the visiting delegation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mayor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d02f7d61e02d070944a","word":"meadow","forms":["meadow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cd435f112eb63b7","term":"meadow","forms":["meadow","meadows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"草地；牧草地","explanation":"meadow 是一片長滿草的土地，常用於放牧，或專門讓草長起來以便收割、製成乾草。核心畫面就是開闊的天然或半人工草地。","examples":[{"en":"We walked across the meadow to the old stone bridge.","zh":"我們穿過草地，走到那座古老的石橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Horses were grazing in the meadow.","zh":"馬正在草地上吃草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meadow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-946f39eb3fcc9418","term":"meadow","forms":["meadow","meadows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"河邊或海邊的低溼草地","explanation":"在特定語境中，meadow 指河流附近或海邊沼澤地帶的低窪草地，通常草長得較粗密，也更容易受潮。","examples":[{"en":"Birds gathered in the wet meadow beside the river.","zh":"鳥兒聚集在河邊的溼草地裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spring floods soaked the low river meadow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meadow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aec6c3d03f013562eb39","word":"meal","forms":["meal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9c404ba4de7ef0c","term":"meal","forms":["meal","meals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一餐；一頓飯","explanation":"指在相對固定的時間吃的一頓較完整的飯，而不是隨手吃的少量零食。早餐、午餐和晚餐都可以稱為 meal。","examples":[{"en":"We had a quick meal before the movie.","zh":"看電影前，我們很快吃了一頓飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Breakfast is often the simplest meal of the day.","zh":"早餐通常是一天中最簡單的一餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ae4481097999172","term":"meal","forms":["meal","meals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穀物粉；粗粉","explanation":"指穀物磨碎後的可食用部分，通常比普通麵粉更粗，也可作動物飼料；具體粗細要看語境。","examples":[{"en":"The recipe calls for cornmeal rather than ordinary flour.","zh":"這個食譜要求用玉米粉，而不是普通麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer mixed grain meal into the animal feed.","zh":"農民把穀物粗粉混進了動物飼料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82523faea1b0f2da676a","word":"mean","forms":["mean"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e92754f3190132e","term":"mean","forms":["mean","meaner","meanest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"吝嗇的","explanation":"形容一個人不願意花錢或分享，待人不夠慷慨，像是把一切都緊緊攥在手裡。","examples":[{"en":"He is mean with money and never buys anyone a drink.","zh":"他花錢很吝嗇，從來不請別人喝東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was mean of you not to share the cake.","zh":"你不分蛋糕給別人，真是太小氣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-959b7fe65efa02dc","term":"mean","forms":["mean"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平均的","explanation":"指把一組數字合在一起後得到的中心水平，用來概括整體，而不是表示每個個體都一樣。這個意義正好對應記憶鉤子裡的“指向中間值”。","examples":[{"en":"The mean age of the participants was thirty-two.","zh":"參與者的平均年齡是三十二歲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mean temperature rose by two degrees this month.","zh":"本月的平均氣溫上升了兩度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73e1fb217e454fae","term":"mean","forms":["mean","means","meaning","meant"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打算；有意","explanation":"表示某人心裡計劃或有意做某事，常常還可用於為無意造成的後果道歉或澄清；它指向的是行動背後的意圖。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't mean to interrupt you.","zh":"我不是故意打斷你的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She means to finish the report tonight.","zh":"她打算今晚完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c6971247b5be423","term":"mean","forms":["mean","means","meaning","meant"],"pos":"verb","zh":"意味著；表示","explanation":"表示某個詞、動作、跡象或事實傳達出某種意思，或說明某種情況可能隨之發生；它把資訊指向一個解釋或結論。","examples":[{"en":"What does this warning sign mean?","zh":"這個警告標誌是什麼意思？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dark sky usually means rain is coming.","zh":"天空變暗通常意味著要下雨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e409bfc6fe798c2efaaf","word":"meaning","forms":["meaning"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-52d4ddf854977c63","term":"meaning","forms":["meaning","meanings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"含義","explanation":"指一個詞、表達、符號或動作所指向的內容，也就是我們問“它是什麼意思”時要找的答案。","examples":[{"en":"I looked up the meaning of the word in a dictionary.","zh":"我在詞典裡查了這個詞的含義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What is the meaning of this symbol?","zh":"這個符號是什麼意思？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meaning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-285987147062d53f","term":"meaning","forms":["meaning","meanings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意義；價值","explanation":"指一件事超出“它確實發生了”這一事實之外的價值、重要性或值得追問的目的；它回答的是“這件事為什麼重要”。","examples":[{"en":"For her, caring for others gives meaning to life.","zh":"對她來說，照顧別人賦予生活意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experience gave new meaning to his work.","zh":"這段經歷讓他的工作有了新的意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meaning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5edb6472cf83e3ea3ec","word":"meaningful","forms":["meaningful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a4f2076d31b3435","term":"meaningful","forms":["meaningful","more meaningful","most meaningful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有意義的；重要的","explanation":"形容某件事不只是形式上完成了，而是真正產生了價值、影響，或讓人感到值得、重要。例如，對專案有實際幫助的貢獻，或令人難忘的人生經歷，都可以說是 meaningful。","examples":[{"en":"I think we made a meaningful contribution to this project today.","zh":"我覺得我們今天為這個專案作出了有實際意義的貢獻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her support was deeply meaningful to me.","zh":"她的支援對我來說意義非常深遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meaningful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70332d559269a27a08e8","word":"means","forms":["means"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-85f456a6f74f8398","term":"means","forms":["means"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手段；方法","explanation":"means 是為了達到某個結果而使用的辦法、工具或條件。把目標想成終點，means 就是幫助你到達終點的那條路或所用的工具。","examples":[{"en":"Education is a means of improving your opportunities.","zh":"教育是改善個人機會的一種手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They used peaceful means to solve the dispute.","zh":"他們用和平手段解決了爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/means","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7edb677649f21d5","term":"means","forms":["means"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財力；經濟條件","explanation":"means 可以指一個人擁有的金錢和經濟資源，也就是他能負擔什麼生活方式的財力。這裡仍然保留“幫助達到某種生活目標的資源”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She comes from a family of means.","zh":"她出身於一個家境富裕的家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They lack the means to buy a larger house.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/means","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-208a97abd4d8ce165297","word":"meantime","forms":["meantime"],"officialPos":"n./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3504d1475cdc35dd","term":"meantime","forms":["meantime"],"pos":"adv","zh":"與此同時；在此期間","explanation":"它把注意力放在兩件事之間的那段時間：一件事還沒完成，另一件事就在這段空檔中發生。","examples":[{"en":"The report will be ready tomorrow; in the meantime, please check these figures.","zh":"報告明天才能準備好；在此期間，請先核對這些數字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children played in the garden, and their parents talked in the meantime.","zh":"孩子們在花園裡玩，與此同時，他們的父母在聊天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meantime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74f6a180125ba3ea","term":"meantime","forms":["meantime","meantimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中間等待的時間","explanation":"這裡把兩件事之間的“空檔”當作一段時間來談，重點是等待後續事件期間可以做什麼。","examples":[{"en":"The new office is not ready yet, so we will work from home in the meantime.","zh":"新辦公室還沒準備好，所以在這段等待期間我們會在家辦公。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs take a week; in the meantime, borrow mine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meantime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c044215e7b91f66e5050","word":"meanwhile","forms":["meanwhile"],"officialPos":"n./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94fbfd22a10b9329","term":"meanwhile","forms":["meanwhile"],"pos":"adv","zh":"與此同時","explanation":"一件事正在某處或某種情境中發生時，另一件事也在同時進行，重點是把注意力轉到另一邊。","examples":[{"en":"The children were playing outside; meanwhile, their parents were preparing dinner.","zh":"孩子們在外面玩，與此同時，他們的父母正在準備晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I waited at the station. Meanwhile, my sister was looking for a taxi.","zh":"我在車站等著，而與此同時，我姐姐正在找計程車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meanwhile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e11c1f5f4e281d22","term":"meanwhile","forms":["meanwhile"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在此期間","explanation":"下一件事還沒有發生，或要到將來才發生；在這段等待時間裡，可以先繼續做另一件事。","examples":[{"en":"The repairs will take a week; meanwhile, please use the back entrance.","zh":"維修要花一週時間；在此期間，請使用後門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vegetables roasted; meanwhile, she prepared the sauce.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meanwhile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-f5911999c9d6d6c513ed","word":"measurable","forms":["measurable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d747cb7a0ada9245","term":"measurable","forms":["measurable","more measurable","most measurable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可測量的","explanation":"指某個數量、變化或性質能夠用儀器、數字或明確的標準加以測定。核心畫面就是把它放到尺子或儀表上，能夠得到可靠的結果。","examples":[{"en":"These instruments can detect measurable changes in pressure.","zh":"這些儀器能夠檢測出壓力的可測量變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The test showed a measurable drop in pollution levels.","zh":"檢測結果顯示汙染水平出現了可以測出的下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measurable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e539bc7d6f46836a","term":"measurable","forms":["measurable","more measurable","most measurable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明顯而有影響的","explanation":"指某種影響、差異或進步明顯到足以被清楚看出，因而具有實際意義。它是從“能夠測出”引申來的：如果變化大到測得出來，通常就不再是微不足道的變化。","examples":[{"en":"The new training program made a measurable difference to staff performance.","zh":"新的培訓專案明顯改善了員工的工作表現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign had a measurable effect on recycling habits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measurable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e23536e5c9a91c2bb035","word":"measure(ment)","forms":["measure","measurement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-175f875b632e1fdf","term":"measure","forms":["measure","measures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數量；限度","explanation":"指某物或某種情緒、行為所能達到的數量或程度，也就是用一把想象中的尺子來表示“有多少、到什麼程度”。","examples":[{"en":"Her patience seemed to have no measure.","zh":"她的耐心似乎沒有限度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe calls for one measure of oil.","zh":"這個食譜需要一份油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-438c639e7a27de86","term":"measure","forms":["measure","measures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計量單位；分量","explanation":"指測量這一動作得到的結果，或烹飪、製作時按標準取出的分量；可以把它想成尺子上標出的“一格”。","examples":[{"en":"Add two measures of rice to the pot.","zh":"往鍋里加入兩份米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add equal measures of oil and vinegar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-edc034cc50f20795","term":"measure","forms":["measure","measures","measuring","measured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"測量","explanation":"用尺、儀器或其他標準確定某物的數量、大小、溫度等；就是讓想象中的刻度告訴你“它有多少”。","examples":[{"en":"We measured the room before buying the furniture.","zh":"我們買傢俱前測量了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please measure the water carefully.","zh":"請仔細量取這些水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-435fb84dcf024480","term":"measurement","forms":["measurement","measurements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"測量；測定","explanation":"指用工具、方法或標準去測定某個物件的行為，也就是把原本模糊的大小、數量或程度確定下來。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor took a measurement of my blood pressure.","zh":"醫生測量了我的血壓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Accurate measurement is essential in this experiment.","zh":"準確測量對這個實驗至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measurement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8261d50529d6dfb2","term":"measurement","forms":["measurement","measurements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"測量值；大小或程度","explanation":"指測量動作產生的結果，即某物的數量、大小、範圍或程度所對應的具體數值；它是把模糊物件變成數字後的“結果”。","examples":[{"en":"The measurement of the room is six meters by four meters.","zh":"這個房間的尺寸是六米乘四米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write down each measurement before adjusting the instrument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measurement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f6bf7a2f5924552a3fc","word":"measure(s)","forms":["measure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6438f0d8533b9c30","term":"measure","forms":["measure","measures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數量；限度","explanation":"指某物或某種情緒、行為所能達到的數量或程度，也就是用一把想象中的尺子來表示“有多少、到什麼程度”。","examples":[{"en":"Her patience seemed to have no measure.","zh":"她的耐心似乎沒有限度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe calls for one measure of oil.","zh":"這個食譜需要一份油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-587aff6f38780f32","term":"measure","forms":["measure","measures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計量單位；分量","explanation":"指測量這一動作得到的結果，或烹飪、製作時按標準取出的分量；可以把它想成尺子上標出的“一格”。","examples":[{"en":"Add two measures of rice to the pot.","zh":"往鍋里加入兩份米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add two measures of water for each measure of rice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/measure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59d6d61431fce7d91388","word":"meat","forms":["meat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ffcdf3ea174b4f70","term":"meat","forms":["meat","meats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肉；肉類食品","explanation":"指動物的肌肉組織，經過烹調後作為食物，也可以指模仿肉的味道和口感製成的植物性食品。這裡的重點是“可食用的肉或仿肉食品”這一實物。","examples":[{"en":"We are eating less meat and more beans these days.","zh":"我們最近少吃肉，多吃豆類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This restaurant serves plant-based meat in several dishes.","zh":"這家餐廳有幾道菜使用植物肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5efd21a2d71d268","term":"meat","forms":["meat","meats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實質；最重要的部分","explanation":"指一件事中最有分量、最值得關注的內容，就像一塊東西里真正“厚實”的 meat。它常表示論點、問題或討論的核心。","examples":[{"en":"The meat of her proposal is a plan to cut energy costs.","zh":"她提案的核心是降低能源成本的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a short introduction, the speaker got to the meat of the issue.","zh":"簡短介紹後，演講者開始談這個問題的實質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c8a739536961bcf34dc","word":"mechanic","forms":["mechanic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f31adb93ad8e1a34","term":"mechanic","forms":["mechanic","mechanics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機械維修技師","explanation":"指負責製造、檢查或修理機械的人，現代最常見的是修理汽車及其機械部件的技師，也可用於飛機或工業裝置的維修人員。","examples":[{"en":"I took my car to the mechanic because the engine was making a strange noise.","zh":"我的車發動機發出奇怪的聲音，所以我把車送去了修理工那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works as an aircraft mechanic at the airport.","zh":"她在機場當飛機維修技師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd80afb525c112c7","term":"mechanic","forms":["mechanic","mechanics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝置或運作方法","explanation":"這裡不是指修理工，而是指某個系統如何運作的具體裝置、方法或功能；它是從“讓事情運轉起來的部件”這一核心形象擴充套件來的。","examples":[{"en":"The app uses a simple mechanic to remind users to take breaks.","zh":"這個應用用一種簡單的機制提醒使用者休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game introduces a new trading mechanic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96ae0f875bd9062d5e26","word":"mechanical","forms":["mechanical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd02a10a28014953","term":"mechanical","forms":["mechanical","more mechanical","most mechanical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"機械學的","explanation":"指與機械學有關，即研究力如何作用於物體、使物體運動或保持平衡的領域。","examples":[{"en":"She chose mechanical engineering because she enjoys understanding how forces move objects.","zh":"她選擇了機械工程，因為她喜歡理解力如何使物體運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course covers basic mechanical principles, including torque.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16c1834469c8af13","term":"mechanical","forms":["mechanical","more mechanical","most mechanical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由機器完成的","explanation":"指某項工作、過程或動作是由機器完成，而不是主要靠人的手直接完成。","examples":[{"en":"The factory uses machines for most of the mechanical tasks.","zh":"這家工廠的大多數機械性工作都由機器完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mechanical harvesting replaced much of the manual labor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92bdc0314223e4e2","term":"mechanical","forms":["mechanical","more mechanical","most mechanical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"機械呆板的","explanation":"像機器按固定程式執行一樣，沒有思考、感情或自然反應；這是從“機器”這個核心畫面引申出來的比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"He gave a mechanical reply and continued looking at his phone.","zh":"他機械地回答了一句，然後繼續看手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her apology sounded mechanical rather than sincere.","zh":"她的道歉聽起來很機械，不像是真誠的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3deac28c1e76d856eed0","word":"mechanism","forms":["mechanism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e95926c92f84c196","term":"mechanism","forms":["mechanism","mechanisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機器中的傳動或控制裝置","explanation":"指機器內部把運動轉換、傳遞或控制起來的裝置或方式，例如轉動一個部件後帶動另一個部件的那套結構。重點不在整臺機器，而在讓機器動作的內部機制。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanism for opening the gate is hidden beneath the floor.","zh":"開門的傳動裝置藏在地板下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician examined the mechanism of the lift.","zh":"技術人員檢查了電梯的運作裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b55ba2a2bc665fcc","term":"mechanism","forms":["mechanism","mechanisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"由零件配合成的機械結構","explanation":"特指由齒輪、凸輪、連桿、皮帶或鏈條等零件組合而成的整體機械結構。可以把它想成許多小部件彼此咬合，共同完成一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The locking mechanism is too stiff to turn easily.","zh":"鎖閉機構太緊，不容易轉動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This toy uses a simple mechanism to make the wings move.","zh":"這個玩具用一個簡單的機械結構讓翅膀動起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1189125fa624af4a","term":"mechanism","forms":["mechanism","mechanisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"產生結果的作用過程","explanation":"指某種心理、身體或化學過程，也就是一件事為什麼會發生、又是怎樣一步步產生結果的方式。它把“內部裝置”從看得見的零件擴充套件到了看不見的作用過程。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are investigating the mechanism behind memory loss.","zh":"研究人員正在調查記憶喪失背後的作用機制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The drug works by a different mechanism from older treatments.","zh":"這種藥物透過不同於舊療法的作用機制發揮效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mechanism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b23a57f108a6a63099a6","word":"medal","forms":["medal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b52fd99c1efdf71","term":"medal","forms":["medal","medals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎牌；獎章","explanation":"medal是通常授予比賽或競賽優勝者的金屬獎牌，用來正式記錄成績或表彰成就。","examples":[{"en":"The swimmer won a gold medal in the final.","zh":"這名游泳運動員在決賽中贏得了一枚金牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school displayed her medal in a glass case.","zh":"學校把她的獎牌陳列在玻璃櫃裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-721c9525ade2ea8903d3","word":"media","forms":["media"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c03a2b6982f0b31","term":"media","forms":["media","medias"],"pos":"noun","zh":"媒體與傳播機構","explanation":"指報紙、電視、廣播、網路等傳播資訊的渠道、機構和制度整體，也就是把資訊送給公眾的“通道”。","examples":[{"en":"Social media has changed how people get their news.","zh":"社交媒體改變了人們獲取新聞的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The media reported the story widely.","zh":"媒體廣泛報道了這件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/media","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f75e5ad3427c9663","term":"media","forms":["media","medias"],"pos":"noun","zh":"媒體內容","explanation":"指電視節目、電影、書籍、照片等已經制作並傳播出去的內容；這裡重點不是“通道”，而是通道里傳送的東西。","examples":[{"en":"Popular media often presents pilots as fearless heroes.","zh":"大眾媒體常把飛行員塑造成無所畏懼的英雄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The platform lets users upload several types of media.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/media","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a61fa7f2e880a7a9b256","word":"mediate","forms":["mediate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-968837f690f9a2f8","term":"mediate","forms":["mediate","mediates","mediating","mediated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調解爭端","explanation":"指作為中間人介入有分歧的雙方，幫助他們停止衝突並達成協議。","examples":[{"en":"The manager mediated the dispute between the two teams.","zh":"經理調解了兩個團隊之間的爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A neutral committee was asked to mediate a ceasefire.","zh":"有人請一箇中立委員會出面調解停火事宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f9ffe618bdef44f","term":"mediate","forms":["mediate","mediates","mediating","mediated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"居中斡旋","explanation":"指主動站到發生衝突的雙方之間，努力促成和解，但不一定已經達成結果。","examples":[{"en":"The union leader offered to mediate between the workers and the company.","zh":"工會領導人提出在工人和公司之間進行斡旋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The union asked an independent official to mediate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-948dbde67a8ef961ee8b","word":"medical","forms":["medical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c49bc5c3c40699aa","term":"medical","forms":["medical","more medical","most medical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"醫學的；醫療的","explanation":"表示同醫學實踐、醫生工作或醫學教育有關，是這個詞最寬、最基礎的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She is studying to become a medical doctor.","zh":"她正在學習，準備成為一名醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university offers excellent medical training.","zh":"這所大學提供很好的醫學培訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43bfaf778e5a1719","term":"medical","forms":["medical","more medical","most medical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"醫療用的；有治療作用的","explanation":"表示某種物質、產品或處理方式是為了改善健康、治療疾病而使用的，重點在醫療用途。","examples":[{"en":"The patient needs medical treatment for the infection.","zh":"這名患者需要接受感染的醫療治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shipment contained urgently needed medical supplies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-876636910b597ab4f30f","word":"medication","forms":["medication"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-180b702463c656e2","term":"medication","forms":["medication","medications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥物；所服的藥","explanation":"medication 可以指藥物本身，也可以指病人按照醫囑持續服用的那一套藥。這裡的重點是“用於治療的藥”，而不是普通的保健品或食物。","examples":[{"en":"Have you remembered to take your medication today?","zh":"你記得今天服藥了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This medication may make you feel sleepy.","zh":"這種藥可能會讓你感到睏倦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b157d49938cf2be","term":"medication","forms":["medication","medications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用藥治療","explanation":"medication 也可以把焦點從“藥瓶裡的藥”移到“用藥來治療”的過程上，表示透過服藥或接受藥物處理來控制病情或症狀。","examples":[{"en":"The condition can usually be controlled with medication.","zh":"這種病通常可以透過藥物治療得到控制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her condition requires long-term medication and regular monitoring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a82ce870f999b01b17b9","word":"medicine","forms":["medicine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa1b8c9dc00405f9","term":"medicine","forms":["medicine","medicines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥物","explanation":"medicine 是用來治療疾病、改善身體狀況的藥物，可以指藥品這一類東西，也可以指某一種具體的藥。","examples":[{"en":"Take this medicine after breakfast and dinner.","zh":"早餐和晚餐後服用這種藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new medicine helped reduce her pain.","zh":"這種新藥幫助減輕了她的疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medicine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f00d5fb04654148c","term":"medicine","forms":["medicine","medicines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫學","explanation":"medicine 還指研究疾病的原因、診斷、預後和治療方法的學科，也就是通常所說的醫學。","examples":[{"en":"She is studying medicine at university.","zh":"她正在大學學習醫學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to study medicine after leaving school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medicine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c46cf71604b2c0a7c4f5","word":"medieval","forms":["medieval"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1dc3a24e7606f228","term":"medieval","forms":["medieval","more medieval","most medieval"],"pos":"adj","zh":"中世紀的","explanation":"指公元約500年至1500年間中世紀時期的人、事物或文化，與這一歷史階段有關。它是歷史分類詞，不只是泛指很久以前的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a collection of medieval weapons.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了一批中世紀武器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is studying medieval history at university.","zh":"她在大學學習中世紀曆史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medieval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9118d305513da1d","term":"medieval","forms":["medieval","more medieval","most medieval"],"pos":"adj","zh":"像中世紀般落後的","explanation":"形容現代的人或事物帶有大眾想象中的中世紀特徵，例如粗暴、迷信、殘酷、衛生條件差或技術落後，因此顯得不合現代社會。","examples":[{"en":"The prison's medieval conditions shocked the inspectors.","zh":"監獄中那種中世紀般惡劣的條件令檢查人員震驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoners endured almost medieval conditions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medieval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":5,"counts":{"114":3,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-4b9ffffd2ca646753ab3","word":"meditate","forms":["meditate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8369c860b2a73737","term":"meditate","forms":["meditate","meditates","meditating","meditated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"沉思；專心思索","explanation":"指把注意力長時間集中在某個主題、文字或問題上，安靜而深入地思考，重點是持續專注，而不只是突然想到一下。","examples":[{"en":"He spent the evening meditating on the meaning of the poem.","zh":"他整個晚上都在沉思這首詩的含義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She meditated quietly on the nature of courage.","zh":"她靜靜地思考勇氣的本質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meditate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8dae20d482edebc","term":"meditate","forms":["meditate","meditates","meditating","meditated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認真考慮；權衡","explanation":"指把一個選擇、計劃或行動的利弊和後果放在心裡反覆權衡，常常暗含還沒有作出決定；它是“心思固定在問題上”進一步發展出的籌劃意味。","examples":[{"en":"The board meditated on whether to accept the proposal.","zh":"董事會認真權衡是否接受這項提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He meditated upon the offer for several days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meditate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d19d7f84196d56a6686","word":"meditation","forms":["meditation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0dfb904f5da43e42","term":"meditation","forms":["meditation","meditations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宗教性的冥想或默想","explanation":"指透過祈禱、默想等方式使心神安靜，並進入對宗教內容的專注或默觀。重點不只是“想事情”，而是帶有內省和精神修習的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She began each morning with ten minutes of meditation and prayer.","zh":"她每天早晨都用十分鐘進行冥想和祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The retreat gave him time for quiet meditation.","zh":"這次靜修給了他安靜默想的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meditation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-084431e695d00d42","term":"meditation","forms":["meditation","meditations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"透過專注或放鬆達到特殊意識狀態","explanation":"指有意識地放鬆身體、集中注意力或觀察呼吸和念頭，使心境變得安靜、清明，有時會進入不同於平常的意識狀態。這是現代英語中很常見的非宗教用法。","examples":[{"en":"I use meditation to calm my mind before a difficult meeting.","zh":"我會在重要會議前用冥想讓自己平靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a few weeks of meditation, he found it easier to focus.","zh":"練習了幾周冥想後，他發現自己更容易集中注意力了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meditation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c082456a7766e23a18db","word":"medium","forms":["medium"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3cb8c7835c90c819","term":"medium","forms":["medium"],"pos":"adj","zh":"中等的","explanation":"表示大小、程度、數量或強度處在較低與較高之間，不偏向任何一端。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a medium coffee and a medium sandwich.","zh":"我點了一杯中杯咖啡和一箇中份三明治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room has medium lighting.","zh":"這個房間的燈光亮度中等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f15d3ea43fb78f3","term":"medium","forms":["medium"],"pos":"adj","zh":"肉熟度中等的","explanation":"專指肉煎到比三分熟更熟、但還沒有全熟的程度，通常中心仍帶紅色。它仍然體現“處在兩端之間”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"I'd like the steak cooked medium, please.","zh":"請把牛排做成五分熟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered her burger medium.","zh":"她點的漢堡肉要中等熟度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6fb97d82839afe5e6eab","word":"medium/media","forms":["medium","media"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d90e4dd7ee1041a7","term":"medium","forms":["medium","media","mediums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳播或呈現資訊的媒介","explanation":"指傳遞資訊、故事或觀點的形式或工具，如書籍、廣播、電影等。它把“中間層”擴充套件為連線表達者與受眾的渠道。","examples":[{"en":"Film is a powerful medium for telling stories.","zh":"電影是講述故事的有力媒介。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The message reached people through a new medium.","zh":"這條資訊透過一種新的媒介傳達給了人們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d99dc3175e14052","term":"medium","forms":["medium","media","mediums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手段、渠道或中間人","explanation":"指實現目標或傳遞資訊的手段、渠道，也可以指在雙方之間傳話或促成事情的人。這裡的共同點仍是“連線兩端”。","examples":[{"en":"The website became a medium for sharing local news.","zh":"這個網站成了分享本地新聞的渠道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She acted as a medium between the two groups.","zh":"她充當了兩個團體之間的中間人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9420a9f14efee4a0","term":"medium","forms":["medium","media","mediums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中號規格","explanation":"指商品可選規格中的中號，尤其用於食品、飲料和服裝。它是形容詞“中號的”名詞化後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I'll have a medium, please.","zh":"請給我一份中號的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This shirt comes in small, medium, and large.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ef983916a27e432","term":"media","forms":["media","medias"],"pos":"noun","zh":"媒體與傳播機構","explanation":"指報紙、電視、廣播、網路等傳播資訊的渠道、機構和制度整體，也就是把資訊送給公眾的“通道”。","examples":[{"en":"Social media has changed how people get their news.","zh":"社交媒體改變了人們獲取新聞的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The media reported the story widely.","zh":"媒體廣泛報道了這件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/media","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f113e69618240e1","term":"media","forms":["media","medias"],"pos":"noun","zh":"媒體內容","explanation":"指電視節目、電影、書籍、照片等已經制作並傳播出去的內容；這裡重點不是“通道”，而是通道里傳送的東西。","examples":[{"en":"Popular media often presents pilots as fearless heroes.","zh":"大眾媒體常把飛行員塑造成無所畏懼的英雄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We downloaded educational media for the long flight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/media","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ccb033c0e48b27ff91e","word":"meet","forms":["meet"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2b4b2bf734ff5ba","term":"meet","forms":["meet","meets","meeting","met"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遇見；碰到","explanation":"表示人在同一地點遇到某人，可能是偶然碰見，也可能是專門約見。它是 meet 最基本的“兩個物件碰到一起”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I met Maya at the supermarket this morning.","zh":"我今天早上在超市遇到了瑪雅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was great to meet you in person.","zh":"很高興親自見到你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5049d8a0959e166","term":"meet","forms":["meet","meets","meeting","met"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滿足；達到；承擔","explanation":"表示某事物與要求、標準、需要或費用對得上，因此可以譯為“滿足、達到”；說 meet the cost 時則表示承擔這筆費用。它仍然保留“與目標對上”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"This product meets all the safety requirements.","zh":"這款產品符合所有安全要求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company will meet the cost of repairs.","zh":"公司將承擔維修費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fd924362117d03662f0","word":"meeting","forms":["meeting"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc93e9f5f1abdb0f","term":"meeting","forms":["meeting","meetings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相遇；遇見這件事","explanation":"指人或事物碰到一起這件事，也可泛指“遇見某人”這一活動；這裡強調的是相遇本身，而不是一次正式聚會。","examples":[{"en":"Meeting new people can be difficult at first.","zh":"剛開始認識新朋友可能會很難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Meeting her again made me very happy.","zh":"再次遇見她讓我非常開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meeting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4da252bf63f5ceb5","term":"meeting","forms":["meeting","meetings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"會議；集會","explanation":"指人們為了討論、決定或完成某件事而聚在一起的活動，是日常英語中最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"We have a meeting about the new project tomorrow.","zh":"我們明天要開一個關於新專案的會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting lasted nearly two hours.","zh":"會議持續了將近兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meeting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e14c0387e5c674667224","word":"melancholy","forms":["melancholy"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-206a94845a8546fa","term":"melancholy","forms":["melancholy","more melancholy","most melancholy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"憂鬱的；悲傷的","explanation":"形容一個人或一種情緒被深沉的悲傷籠罩，往往還帶有安靜、內省的感覺。它不是簡單的“心情不好”，而是像一層黑沉沉的情緒壓在心上。","examples":[{"en":"The old song left him in a melancholy mood.","zh":"那首老歌讓他陷入了憂鬱的情緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a melancholy smile and looked out the window.","zh":"她憂鬱地笑了笑，然後望向窗外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melancholy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd71d9351a0f4b8b","term":"melancholy","forms":["melancholy","melancholies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"深沉的憂鬱","explanation":"指一種安靜、深沉而常帶有思索意味的悲傷狀態，就是“黑沉沉的情緒”這一核心形象本身。它可以描述一時的心境，也可以指較長時間籠罩人的憂鬱。","examples":[{"en":"A quiet melancholy filled the room after the guests left.","zh":"客人離開後，一種安靜的憂鬱充滿了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He listened to the rain with a feeling of melancholy.","zh":"他帶著一種憂鬱的心情聽著雨聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melancholy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2db76f21528566a3f39c","word":"melody","forms":["melody"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f398f325c89dedd3","term":"melody","forms":["melody","melodies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旋律","explanation":"melody是音樂中依次展開的一串音符，組合成一個可以聽出、記住、哼唱或演奏的音樂片段。把它想成一條音符線，就能理解為什麼歌手可以唱出旋律，樂器也可以演奏旋律。","examples":[{"en":"She hummed a cheerful melody while making breakfast.","zh":"她做早餐時哼著一段歡快的旋律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The violin carries the melody in this section.","zh":"這一段由小提琴演奏主旋律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a73860a05ec07cb9ce86","word":"melon","forms":["melon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e6d2734d2e7e54a","term":"melon","forms":["melon","melons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓜類植物","explanation":"指結瓜供人食用的一類葫蘆科植物，通常不包括黃瓜；這裡強調的是植物這一整體類別，而不只是摘下來的果實。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers grow melon in this warm, dry region.","zh":"農民在這個溫暖乾燥的地區種植瓜類作物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The melon is flowering earlier than usual this year.","zh":"這種瓜今年開花得比往年早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e88a8ce0c134b89","term":"melon","forms":["melon","melons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓜果","explanation":"指瓜類植物結出的、通常有外皮的圓形或橢圓形果實，也就是人們切開來吃的那個瓜。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a ripe melon at the market.","zh":"我在市場買了一個熟透的瓜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cut the melon into wedges and chill it.","zh":"把瓜切成楔形塊，再冰鎮一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af45b9700bb0b00ef1b2","word":"melt","forms":["melt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4dad5758d72dfbd9","term":"melt","forms":["melt","melts","melting","melted","molt","molten","meltest","meltedst","melteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"融化；熔化","explanation":"指固體在熱量等作用下逐漸變成液體，也可指使某物發生這種變化。主語可以自己融化，也可以由人加熱使它融化。","examples":[{"en":"Melt the butter in a pan before adding the flour.","zh":"加入麵粉前，先在鍋裡把黃油融化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The snow melted by noon.","zh":"積雪到中午就融化了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b59e3eee7b5573e4","term":"melt","forms":["melt","melts","melting","melted","molt","molten","meltest","meltedst","melteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消散；消失","explanation":"把煩惱、恐懼、界限等抽象事物想象成逐漸融化並不見了，強調緩慢地散去或消失。","examples":[{"en":"A quiet walk helped my worries melt away.","zh":"安靜地散了會兒步，我的煩惱漸漸消散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His anger melted when he saw her smile.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e31ab643c44f7a0ec824","word":"member","forms":["member"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50faf56c0bd474c7","term":"member","forms":["member","members"],"pos":"noun","zh":"團體成員","explanation":"指屬於某個團體、組織、俱樂部或機構的人，是“整體裡的一個成員”這一核心概念最常見的人稱用法。","examples":[{"en":"She has been a member of the tennis club for five years.","zh":"她已經是這家網球俱樂部的成員五年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every member of the team must attend the meeting.","zh":"團隊的每一名成員都必須參加會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/member","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63b5f03a1285e0c9","term":"member","forms":["member","members"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體的組成部分","explanation":"指構成某個整體、結構或系統的一個部分；這裡的“整體”不一定是團體，也可以是橋樑、機器或抽象系統。","examples":[{"en":"Each steel member was checked before the bridge was opened.","zh":"這座橋開放前，每個鋼製構件都經過了檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The supporting members of the roof need to be replaced.","zh":"屋頂的承重構件需要更換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/member","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-060de424498b00bd","term":"member","forms":["member","members"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體部位或肢體","explanation":"指動物身體中承擔特定功能的部位，尤其是器官或肢體；它仍然體現“身體整體中的一個部分”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The surgeon carefully examined every member of the injured animal's body.","zh":"外科醫生仔細檢查了這隻受傷動物身體的每個部位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury left him unable to move the affected member.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/member","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf5cf59e356652253268","word":"membership","forms":["membership"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f65cdabfcca448d","term":"membership","forms":["membership","memberships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成員資格；會員身份","explanation":"指成為某個組織、團體或社群成員的狀態，重點是“屬於這個群體的資格或關係”，而不是某一名具體成員。","examples":[{"en":"She applied for membership in the local tennis club.","zh":"她申請加入當地網球俱樂部成為會員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your membership gives you access to the library's online resources.","zh":"你的會員資格讓你可以使用圖書館的線上資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/membership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b0f17335b8054fc","term":"membership","forms":["membership","memberships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全體成員","explanation":"指一個組織或團體中的所有成員，強調“把持有會員身份的人整體看作一個群體”。","examples":[{"en":"The membership voted to elect a new chairperson.","zh":"全體成員投票選出了新主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The membership voted overwhelmingly to support the strike.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/membership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-989c480c77112cffe6ac","word":"memorable","forms":["memorable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3392daafb0a709b","term":"memorable","forms":["memorable","more memorable","most memorable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人難忘的","explanation":"某人或某事在記憶中留下了很深的印記，因此特別值得記住；這種特別可以來自重要性、精彩程度或強烈的情感。","examples":[{"en":"Our first trip together was a memorable experience.","zh":"我們第一次一起旅行是一次令人難忘的經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a memorable speech at the ceremony.","zh":"她在典禮上發表了一場令人難忘的演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memorable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da1c95dd1a2a98702ebf","word":"memorial","forms":["memorial"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b999d81a036facc","term":"memorial","forms":["memorial","more memorial","most memorial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"紀念性的","explanation":"表示某物是為了紀念某人、某件事或某段歷史而設立或製作的，是這個詞最重要的形容詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The city built a memorial garden for the victims.","zh":"這座城市為遇難者建了一座紀念花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They held a memorial service on Sunday.","zh":"他們星期日舉行了紀念儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memorial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dabce9f75ac04a30","term":"memorial","forms":["memorial","memorials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紀念物；紀念碑","explanation":"指用來讓人記住某個人、事件或群體的實物，例如紀念碑、紀念館或其他紀念設施；這是名詞最核心的含義。","examples":[{"en":"A memorial to the soldiers stands in the town square.","zh":"鎮廣場上立著一座紀念士兵的紀念碑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stone memorial honors the villagers lost at sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memorial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61bbff73e058ac87e5b2","word":"memorize","forms":["memorize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0faae67a399752c7","term":"memorize","forms":["memorize","memorizes","memorizing","memorized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"背熟；記住","explanation":"指透過學習、重複或練習，把某項資訊牢牢記在腦中，以後可以不看原文就回想、背出或使用它。","examples":[{"en":"I memorized the first ten lines of the poem for class.","zh":"我為上課背熟了這首詩的前十行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You should memorize these emergency numbers.","zh":"你應該把這些緊急電話號碼記熟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memorize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c064fbca9d9de8dd9bb0","word":"memory","forms":["memory"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eab2833ebd4f6142","term":"memory","forms":["memory","memories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"記憶能力","explanation":"指大腦儲存資訊、印象並在之後回想起來的能力，也就是一個人“記得住東西”的能力。","examples":[{"en":"Memory improves with regular practice.","zh":"經常練習能提高記憶力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her memory is still remarkably sharp.","zh":"她的記憶力仍然非常好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-222a4401131e383a","term":"memory","forms":["memory","memories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段記憶；記憶中的內容","explanation":"指被儲存下來、以後可以回想的某件經歷、印象或事實；這裡的memory像記憶庫裡取出的一個具體檔案。","examples":[{"en":"I have no memory of meeting him before.","zh":"我不記得以前見過他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That photograph brought back a happy memory.","zh":"那張照片勾起了一段美好的回憶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/memory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f1f4f910a8324e2b8d1","word":"mend","forms":["mend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17493563784de18b","term":"mend","forms":["mend","mends","mending","mended","mendest","mendedst","mendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修補損壞物品","explanation":"指把破損、撕裂或損壞的物品修好，使它恢復可用狀態，正體現了“把有缺陷的東西變好”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to mend this coat before winter.","zh":"我得在冬天前把這件外套補好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mended the tear in my backpack.","zh":"她把我揹包上的裂口補好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35ca21157b6c180d","term":"mend","forms":["mend","mends","mending","mended","mendest","mendedst","mendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"糾正錯誤","explanation":"指把錯誤、缺點或問題糾正過來，使事情恢復正常，也就是把出錯的地方“修好”。","examples":[{"en":"We need to mend the mistake before anyone notices.","zh":"我們得在別人發現之前把這個錯誤糾正過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sincere apology may mend the damage to their friendship.","zh":"真誠的道歉或許能彌補對他們友誼造成的損害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a664d44f82ba281","term":"mend","forms":["mend","mends","mending","mended","mendest","mendedst","mendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改善狀況","explanation":"指使某人或某事物處於更好的狀態，例如改善能力、表現、習慣或整體狀況；重點不一定是原來壞了，而是變得更好。","examples":[{"en":"The new treatment mended his speech problem.","zh":"新的治療改善了他的語言障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are trying to mend their relationship.","zh":"他們正努力改善彼此的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9dd12c24710333fc","term":"mend","forms":["mend","mends","mending","mended","mendest","mendedst","mendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"病情或傷勢好轉","explanation":"指疾病、傷口或受傷的身體部位逐漸減輕、恢復或癒合，也就是缺陷狀態自行變好。","examples":[{"en":"Her injured knee is finally beginning to mend.","zh":"她受傷的膝蓋終於開始好轉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cut should mend in a few days.","zh":"這個傷口應該幾天後就會癒合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-888df6d1572d02bc1a80","word":"mental","forms":["mental"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7828c54f3985108a","term":"mental","forms":["mental","more mental","most mental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"心智的；心理的","explanation":"指和人的思考、情緒、意識以及對外界的內在反應有關的事物，也就是“發生在心裡的”或“屬於心智的”。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise can improve your mental health.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以改善你的心理健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The test measures both physical and mental abilities.","zh":"這項測試同時測量身體能力和心智慧力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe618fa8587d2e16","term":"mental","forms":["mental","more mental","most mental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精神疾病相關的","explanation":"指與精神疾病有關，或受到這類疾病影響的人、治療和機構等。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic offers support for mental patients and their families.","zh":"這家診所為精神疾病患者及其家人提供支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic provides mental health services.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-132cacf3339541fd1d4b","word":"mentality","forms":["mentality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ccb01bbb8fa606b","term":"mentality","forms":["mentality","mentalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"思維方式；心態","explanation":"指一個人或一群人慣常看待問題、作出判斷和行動的方式，就像一副長期戴著的“思維眼鏡”。它常包含某些固定信念或態度，並不只是某一刻的情緒。","examples":[{"en":"She has a positive mentality and does not give up easily.","zh":"她有積極的思維方式，不容易放棄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team needs to change its mentality if it wants to win.","zh":"這支隊伍想贏，就需要改變自己的思維方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mentality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68b9c231ac85c9597c7f","word":"mention","forms":["mention"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59781f9d191fe4fe","term":"mention","forms":["mention","mentions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提及；提到","explanation":"指對某人或某事作簡短、順帶的提到，重點在“點到為止”，不表示已經詳細說明。","examples":[{"en":"Her brief mention of the delay made everyone nervous.","zh":"她簡短提到延誤一事，讓大家都緊張起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mentioned your name during the interview.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-498de4a6a0b411ab","term":"mention","forms":["mention","mentions","mentioning","mentioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提到；說起","explanation":"指在說話或寫作中短暫地帶到某人、某事或某個觀點，不一定展開解釋。","examples":[{"en":"She mentioned the broken printer during the team meeting.","zh":"她在團隊會議上提到了那臺壞掉的印表機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mentioned your name during the interview.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9d771df57e86d113220","word":"mentor","forms":["mentor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eca2ff1c5f51c75a","term":"mentor","forms":["mentor","mentors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"導師；指導者","explanation":"mentor是一個有經驗、值得信賴的人，幫助別人學習、作決定並逐漸成長。它不一定是在學校任教，更強調持續的個人指導，就像神話中的Mentor指導忒勒馬科斯一樣。","examples":[{"en":"She found a mentor to help her develop her leadership skills.","zh":"她找到了一位導師，幫助自己培養領導能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My mentor encouraged me to apply for the position.","zh":"我的導師鼓勵我申請這個職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mentor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-398991009da1d251792e","word":"menu","forms":["menu"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e5e253b6b159c06","term":"menu","forms":["menu","menus"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餐館選單","explanation":"這是最常見的含義：餐館、咖啡館或酒吧提供給顧客檢視和選擇食物、飲料的清單，可以印在紙上、展示在牆上，也可以顯示在電子裝置上。","examples":[{"en":"The waiter brought us the menu as soon as we sat down.","zh":"我們一坐下，服務員就把選單拿來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can we see the dessert menu, please?","zh":"請給我們看看甜點選單，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/menu","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c124a36b7a0e562","term":"menu","forms":["menu","menus"],"pos":"noun","zh":"操作選項選單","explanation":"在軟體、遊戲或其他電子介面中，menu是一列可供使用者選擇的操作，例如儲存、設定或退出；它保留了“列出選擇”的核心概念，只是選擇物件從食物變成了功能。","examples":[{"en":"Open the menu and select the sound settings.","zh":"開啟選單，然後選擇聲音設定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game menu lets you save or quit.","zh":"遊戲選單讓你可以儲存或退出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/menu","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-885deb16ec204f038195","word":"merchandise","forms":["merchandise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c848f92cbbd0901","term":"merchandise","forms":["merchandise","merchandises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"待售商品","explanation":"指商店或企業正在出售、準備出售的一批商品或商品總稱，重點是“作為貨物來賣”。","examples":[{"en":"The store received new merchandise this morning.","zh":"這家商店今天早上收到了新貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good merchandise brings customers back.","zh":"優質商品會吸引顧客再次光臨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merchandise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c5f4234e299b041","term":"merchandise","forms":["merchandise","merchandises","merchandising","merchandised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"陳列促銷商品","explanation":"指在商店裡擺放、安排和展示商品，使顧客更容易看到併購買；它正是“把待售商品擺上貨架並推動銷售”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"She spent the weekend merchandising in a busy department store.","zh":"她整個週末都在一家繁忙的百貨商店做商品陳列促銷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop merchandises seasonal goods near the entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merchandise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9e786cce0d95f0f60895","word":"merchant","forms":["merchant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-624647a92a388506","term":"merchant","forms":["merchant","merchants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商人","explanation":"指為了獲利而買賣商品的人，重點在商品交易，而不只是偶爾賣出一件東西。","examples":[{"en":"The merchant bought spices overseas and sold them in the city.","zh":"這名商人從海外購買香料，再在城裡出售。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Merchants from several countries gathered at the port.","zh":"來自幾個國家的商人聚集在港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merchant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d3b58b28c2d33a4","term":"merchant","forms":["merchant","merchants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"零售商；店主","explanation":"指經營零售生意、直接向顧客出售商品的人或企業主，是“商人”概念在店鋪經營中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The online merchant offers free delivery on large orders.","zh":"這家網店商戶對大額訂單提供免費送貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wine merchant recommended a local white.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merchant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d51fd998fd3a724c06a","word":"mercy","forms":["mercy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a29c05a23374c146","term":"mercy","forms":["mercy","mercies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬容；免於傷害","explanation":"指本來可以懲罰、傷害或繼續為難某人，卻選擇停手、放過對方的行為或態度；核心畫面就是“手停下來，不再加害”。","examples":[{"en":"The judge showed mercy to the young offender.","zh":"法官寬恕了那名年輕的違法者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please have mercy on me and let me try again.","zh":"請寬容我一次，讓我再試一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mercy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-415422bf562af3d3","term":"mercy","forms":["mercy","mercies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"憐憫；寬恕","explanation":"指因為同情處境較差或受苦的人，而願意幫助、寬恕或減輕其痛苦；它是“停手不傷害”進一步發展出的同情心。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers had mercy on the injured traveler.","zh":"村民們憐憫那名受傷的旅客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He begged for mercy after admitting his mistake.","zh":"他承認錯誤後懇求寬恕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mercy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7800ffc65778f54d","term":"mercy","forms":["mercy","mercies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幸事；值得慶幸的結果","explanation":"表示某件壞事本來可能造成更嚴重的後果，但幸運地沒有發生，因此這件事本身像是得到了一份“寬免”或恩惠。","examples":[{"en":"It was a mercy that nobody was hurt in the accident.","zh":"值得慶幸的是，事故中沒有人受傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rain stopped, which was a mercy after the long match.","zh":"雨停了，踢了那麼久的比賽後這真是件幸事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mercy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35d3ec98be746911c34b","word":"mere","forms":["mere"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-425020fc9502456b","term":"mere","forms":["mere","merer","merest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"僅僅的；不過是……的","explanation":"指某事物只是所說的這一點，沒有更多內容或更高程度；它把注意範圍縮小到“僅僅如此”。","examples":[{"en":"The mere mention of his name made everyone leave the room.","zh":"僅僅提到他的名字，就讓所有人離開了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was a mere coincidence that we arrived at the same time.","zh":"我們同時到達純粹只是個巧合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-283128acef14943c127f","word":"merge","forms":["merge"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3bc22c8c96ca1e8","term":"merge","forms":["merge","merges","merging","merged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"合併成一體","explanation":"指把兩個或多個組織、部門、檔案或其他部分組合起來，最後作為一個整體存在。","examples":[{"en":"The two companies merged to form one larger business.","zh":"兩家公司合併成了一家更大的企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor merged the two reports into one document.","zh":"編輯把兩份報告合併成了一份檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-429bf78dbd9b95352ba7","word":"merit","forms":["merit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-85d78609bcb2cdf3","term":"merit","forms":["merit","merits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"值得稱讚或獎勵的功勞","explanation":"指某人的品格、行為或成就所具有的價值，足以讓人稱讚或給予獎勵；重點是“憑什麼值得被認可”。","examples":[{"en":"Her proposal has merit, even though it needs more research.","zh":"她的提議有可取之處，雖然還需要更多研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He earned the team's respect through merit rather than luck.","zh":"他靠實力而不是靠運氣贏得了團隊的尊重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caf69cab8bb4fc78","term":"merit","forms":["merit","merits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"應得的價值或功勞","explanation":"指某人或某事本身值得得到的認可、獎勵或好結果，強調“應得的程度”，而不只是擁有某項優點。","examples":[{"en":"The committee recognized the merit of her careful investigation.","zh":"委員會認可了她細緻調查的價值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal deserves consideration on its own merit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fbccedd61528383fcf1","word":"mermaid","forms":["mermaid"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50184d1652aff708","term":"mermaid","forms":["mermaid","mermaids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美人魚；人魚","explanation":"指傳說中上半身像女人、下半身像魚的海中生物。這個詞本身帶有神話和幻想色彩，不是現實動物的正式名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The little girl dressed up as a mermaid for the school play.","zh":"小女孩在學校演出中打扮成了美人魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story says that a mermaid saved the sailor.","zh":"故事裡說，一條美人魚救了那個水手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mermaid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc261a5e3e3c85a41982","word":"merry","forms":["merry"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c84352b928a6fe5c","term":"merry","forms":["merry","merrier","merriest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"快樂的；興高采烈的","explanation":"形容人心情非常好、興致高，彷彿正沉浸在歡樂的聚會中。","examples":[{"en":"The children were merry as they opened their presents.","zh":"孩子們開啟禮物時興高采烈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have a merry Christmas!","zh":"祝你聖誕快樂！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9cf2502ed10f49c0","term":"merry","forms":["merry","merrier","merriest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱鬧歡樂的","explanation":"形容聚會、節日或場面充滿笑聲和樂趣，大家一起玩得很開心。","examples":[{"en":"The neighbors had a merry party in the garden.","zh":"鄰居們在花園裡舉行了一個熱鬧的聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A merry crowd gathered outside the theater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d64084076881eb259d7","word":"mess","forms":["mess"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4d1add279e0486a","term":"mess","forms":["mess","messes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"髒亂的一團；混亂局面","explanation":"指東西堆得凌亂、骯髒，或事情發展得毫無條理、很難收拾；核心畫面就是一張亂掉的桌子。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen is a complete mess after the party.","zh":"聚會後廚房亂成了一團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project became a mess when nobody agreed on the plan.","zh":"大家都沒能就計劃達成一致，這個專案後來變得一團糟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ae801d1ee752dd8","term":"mess","forms":["mess","messes","messing","messed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄髒；弄亂","explanation":"把原本整潔的東西弄得髒亂，正是名詞 mess 所對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The children messed up the living room with paint and toys.","zh":"孩子們用顏料和玩具把客廳弄得亂七八糟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't mess the kitchen while I'm cleaning it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6e2a5a488219512","term":"mess","forms":["mess","messes","messing","messed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄亂；搞砸","explanation":"把事情、安排或局面推入混亂，甚至使它失敗；也就是把原本能運轉的“桌面”徹底攪亂。","examples":[{"en":"I messed up the schedule and made everyone wait.","zh":"我把日程安排搞亂了，讓大家都等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't mess up this opportunity.","zh":"別把這次機會搞砸了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab530a13e45914982b79","word":"message","forms":["message"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18f8b881d2e22e2c","term":"message","forms":["message","messages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"訊息；資訊","explanation":"指傳遞給某人的話、通知或其他資訊，形式可以是口頭、書面、電話留言或電子內容，不限於簡訊。","examples":[{"en":"I left a message for Anna before I left the office.","zh":"我離開辦公室前給安娜留了個口信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We received an important message from the school.","zh":"我們收到了學校的一條重要通知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/message","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-050f993ea2322d4b6940","word":"messenger","forms":["messenger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-198248a96091432c","term":"messenger","forms":["messenger","messengers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信使；傳遞訊息的人","explanation":"指替別人把訊息、檔案或口信送到另一個地方的人。核心畫面就是“帶著訊息去找收件人”。","examples":[{"en":"The messenger delivered the letter before sunset.","zh":"信使在日落前送到了那封信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sent a messenger to tell the village chief.","zh":"我們派了一名信使去通知村長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/messenger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4c0099dbd73c0ab","term":"messenger","forms":["messenger","messengers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"即時通訊軟體","explanation":"指用於即時傳送文字等資訊的軟體或服務；它把“傳遞訊息的人”延伸成了“傳遞訊息的程式”。","examples":[{"en":"I sent the file through an instant messenger.","zh":"我透過即時通訊軟體傳送了那個檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team uses Messenger to discuss small updates.","zh":"團隊用 Messenger 討論一些小的更新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/messenger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-231516be2612fdfa8507","word":"messy","forms":["messy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-727a0e11ab559bfe","term":"messy","forms":["messy","messier","messiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"凌亂的","explanation":"指東西擺放雜亂、環境沒有整理好，像一團攤開的亂攤子；重點是秩序混亂，不一定特別髒。","examples":[{"en":"My desk is so messy that I can't find my keys.","zh":"我的桌子太亂了，我找不到鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children's room got messy after the party.","zh":"聚會後，孩子們的房間變得亂七八糟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/messy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66d13da1096cb3a7","term":"messy","forms":["messy","messier","messiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"棘手的；糾纏不清的","explanation":"把“亂攤子”的形象轉用於抽象事情：局面複雜、牽涉多方，處理起來麻煩，往往還伴隨著不愉快的後果。","examples":[{"en":"Their business dispute turned into a messy legal battle.","zh":"他們的商業糾紛變成了一場棘手的法律爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their separation became a messy legal dispute.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/messy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03ecab669ba200ba17f9","word":"metal","forms":["metal"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29f32ff137af65f1","term":"metal","forms":["metal","more metal","most metal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"金屬音樂風格的","explanation":"指音樂帶有強烈鼓點和失真吉他等金屬音樂的典型特點。這裡的 metal 不是材料，而是音樂型別名稱。","examples":[{"en":"My brother listens to metal music every morning.","zh":"我哥哥每天早上都聽金屬音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band is famous for its fast drums and heavy guitar sound.","zh":"這個樂隊以快速鼓點和厚重的吉他聲而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8e2d8ccf28ebd9e","term":"metal","forms":["metal","metals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金屬；金屬礦物或合金","explanation":"指鐵、銅、銀等化學元素或合金，也可以泛指這些金屬所在的礦石以及開採它們的礦藏。日常最常見的意思是製作物品的金屬材料。","examples":[{"en":"The frame is made of light but strong metal.","zh":"這個框架由輕而堅固的金屬製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Copper is a useful metal for electrical wiring.","zh":"銅是製作電線的實用金屬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-065d74f27665fd459117","word":"metaphor","forms":["metaphor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0469c461e7d577f3","term":"metaphor","forms":["metaphor","metaphors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"借喻這種表達方式","explanation":"指不按字面理解，而是把一個事物的形象或特點借來說明另一個事物的表達方式。比如用“人海”表現人很多，重點不在真的有海，而在借用了海的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “a sea of faces” uses metaphor to show how crowded the hall was.","zh":"“人海”這個說法用借喻表現大廳里人很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speaker relies on metaphor to explain the difficult idea.","zh":"演講者藉助比喻來解釋這個難懂的概念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metaphor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43a97ba3e5747054","term":"metaphor","forms":["metaphor","metaphors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體的比喻說法","explanation":"指一個實際使用的詞或短語，它把某物說成另一種相似的事物。比如“時間是小偷”就是一個具體的 metaphor，因為它把時間寫成會悄悄帶走東西的小偷。","examples":[{"en":"“Time is a thief” is a metaphor for how quickly life passes.","zh":"“時間是小偷”是一個表現生命流逝很快的比喻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Calling memory a library is a useful metaphor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metaphor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5eff322a1bd4164e1db3","word":"meter","forms":["meter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-642afd228e634006","term":"meter","forms":["meter","meters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"測量儀表","explanation":"meter 是用來測量數量、流量、用量等的儀表，通常能顯示讀數。","examples":[{"en":"The electric meter is outside the house.","zh":"電錶在房子外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check the water meter before you leave.","zh":"你離開前請檢視一下水錶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e74ba3653bff4d5","term":"meter","forms":["meter","meters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"米","explanation":"在美國英語中，meter 是長度單位“米”，等於一百釐米。","examples":[{"en":"The table is two meters long.","zh":"這張桌子長兩米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The desk is just over a meter wide.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b7e6bf2dc4a32a6aa47","word":"method","forms":["method"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef1d11fe6b65e9f9","term":"method","forms":["method","methods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方法；做法","explanation":"指完成某項任務或達到某個目的時採用的具體辦法，也就是“做事的路線圖”。重點在於這是一套可以採用、比較或改進的做法。","examples":[{"en":"This method is simple enough for beginners to follow.","zh":"這種方法足夠簡單，初學者也能照著做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a better method for keeping the records organized.","zh":"我們需要一種更好的方法來讓記錄保持井然有序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/method","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f3425e9a2eb982a","term":"method","forms":["method","methods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"條理；有系統","explanation":"這裡不指某一個具體辦法，而指做事時有計劃、有秩序、不是雜亂進行的狀態。它可以形容一個人的做事方式，也可以說某件看似混亂的事其實暗中有條理。","examples":[{"en":"She sorted the files with remarkable method.","zh":"她以非凡的條理整理了這些檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is method in the way she arranges her notes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/method","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-493f17c232e40c8d4cfb","word":"metropolitan","forms":["metropolitan"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-917f89333a5b79b3","term":"metropolitan","forms":["metropolitan","more metropolitan","most metropolitan"],"pos":"adj","zh":"都市的；大城市的","explanation":"指大城市本身、城市生活方式，或與大城市有關的機構和問題；核心畫面就是“以大都市為中心的”。","examples":[{"en":"The metropolitan area has grown rapidly over the past decade.","zh":"過去十年間，這個大都市區發展得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Metropolitan residents often spend a long time commuting.","zh":"大都市居民往往要花很長時間通勤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metropolitan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-047c7b1ecb967ebf","term":"metropolitan","forms":["metropolitan","more metropolitan","most metropolitan"],"pos":"adj","zh":"本土國家的","explanation":"在殖民地或屬地語境中，指與本土國家有關的；例如 metropolitan France 指相對於海外屬地的法國本土。","examples":[{"en":"The law applies both to the overseas territory and to metropolitan France.","zh":"這項法律既適用於海外屬地，也適用於法國本土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Colonial officials answered to the metropolitan government.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metropolitan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cac3826a8b6a3d6d0959","word":"microphone/mike","forms":["microphone","mike"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9141b59b5d44a175","term":"microphone","forms":["microphone","microphones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麥克風；話筒","explanation":"一種接收聲音並把聲音轉換成電訊號的裝置，之後可以用來放大、錄音或透過廣播等方式傳送聲音。","examples":[{"en":"Please speak into the microphone so everyone can hear you.","zh":"請對著麥克風說話，這樣大家都能聽見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporter held a microphone toward the singer.","zh":"記者把麥克風伸向歌手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/microphone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3205867c7e6452a8","term":"mike","forms":["mike","mikes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麥克風","explanation":"指把聲音收集並傳送或錄下來的麥克風；這是mike最重要的普通名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Please speak clearly into the mike.","zh":"請對著麥克風清楚地說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The singer dropped the mike after the final song.","zh":"歌手唱完最後一首歌后放下了麥克風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f09538d0ea075eeabc6","word":"microscope","forms":["microscope"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d9985fc8125925f","term":"microscope","forms":["microscope","microscopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顯微鏡","explanation":"一種把極小物體放大併成像，使人能夠觀察其細節的光學儀器。它是 microscope 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The students used a microscope to examine a drop of pond water.","zh":"學生們用顯微鏡檢查一滴池塘水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw several tiny cells under the microscope.","zh":"我們在顯微鏡下看到了幾個微小的細胞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/microscope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17ad7b858a0ace83","term":"microscope","forms":["microscope","microscopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微小物體成像儀器","explanation":"也可以泛指任何用來成像極小物體的儀器，不限於普通光學顯微鏡，例如電子顯微鏡等。","examples":[{"en":"An electron microscope can reveal details that ordinary microscopes cannot show.","zh":"電子顯微鏡能顯示普通顯微鏡無法顯示的細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The microscope revealed organisms invisible to the naked eye.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/microscope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-d2bedad966f1b52aca5d","word":"microwave","forms":["microwave"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2967957a45a31365","term":"microwave","forms":["microwave","microwaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微波（電磁波）","explanation":"微波是一種電磁波，波長大致處在紅外線和無線電波之間；雷達和通訊等技術會利用它。","examples":[{"en":"Some radar systems use microwaves to detect distant objects.","zh":"一些雷達系統利用微波探測遠處的物體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Microwaves carry signals between the two communication towers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/microwave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b459fd7db306c1df","term":"microwave","forms":["microwave","microwaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微波爐","explanation":"在日常語境中，microwave 常是 microwave oven 的簡稱，指用微波加熱食物的廚房電器。","examples":[{"en":"Put the soup in the microwave for two minutes.","zh":"把湯放進微波爐里加熱兩分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heat the leftovers in the microwave.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/microwave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e7ef8a7bf4d61ee","term":"microwave","forms":["microwave","microwaves","microwaving","microwaved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用微波爐加熱","explanation":"表示把食物放進微波爐中加熱，突出的是快速處理食物這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"I microwaved the leftovers before leaving for work.","zh":"我出門上班前用微波爐熱了剩菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Microwave the soup in a suitable covered bowl.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/microwave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4888af4e46c129c695e","word":"middle","forms":["middle"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-baf0fdf02f446540","term":"middle","forms":["middle","middlemost","middlest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"中間的；位於兩端之間的","explanation":"表示某物正處在兩個端點、兩部分或一段範圍的中間位置，是middle最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a line through the middle point of the circle.","zh":"畫一條線穿過圓的中點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please sit in the middle seat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/middle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc747b680ceeade3","term":"middle","forms":["middle","middlemost","middlest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"中央的","explanation":"強調位於整體的中心區域，而不一定是嚴格測量出的幾何中點；可以指中央位置、中央部分或中間階段。","examples":[{"en":"She chose the middle seat on the train.","zh":"她選了火車中間的座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She occupied the middle seat between her brothers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/middle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1856b22cd357db96","term":"middle","forms":["middle","middles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中心；中點","explanation":"指一個空間、形狀或範圍的中心位置，也就是到周圍邊界大致等距或處在正中央的點。","examples":[{"en":"A small fountain stands in the middle of the square.","zh":"廣場中央有一座小噴泉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the vase in the middle of the table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/middle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-270d9da7786dab44","term":"middle","forms":["middle","middles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中間部分；中段","explanation":"指一件事從開始到結束之間的那一段，尤其常用於一天、夜晚、故事、活動或某個過程的中段。","examples":[{"en":"The lights went out in the middle of the movie.","zh":"電影放到一半時燈熄滅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The middle of the loaf was still doughy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/middle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35af25f5a5fdac6401dd","word":"midnight","forms":["midnight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5843414a02a2ca28","term":"midnight","forms":["midnight","midnights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"深夜；夜半","explanation":"指夜晚最中間的時段，通常圍繞夜裡十二點，但範圍可以比十二點整稍寬。它強調的是夜晚的中點，而不只是一般意義上的“晚上”。","examples":[{"en":"The streets are almost empty at midnight.","zh":"午夜時街道上幾乎空無一人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train finally arrived well after midnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-577b2ea2af9260e4","term":"midnight","forms":["midnight","midnights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夜裡十二點整","explanation":"特指一天中夜間的十二點整，是 midnight 作為時間點的最明確用法。","examples":[{"en":"The new year began at midnight.","zh":"新年在午夜十二點整開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bells rang twelve times at midnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4224c5d7c67e5e5d66c4","word":"midst","forms":["midst"],"officialPos":"n./prep.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3138a188dee9746","term":"midst","forms":["midst","midsts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正中間；當中","explanation":"指某個地方、群體或情境的中心位置；也可以把抽象事件想成一個場景，表示正處在事件或活動的中心。","examples":[{"en":"The speaker stood in the midst of the crowd.","zh":"演講者站在人群中央。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We were in the midst of a difficult negotiation.","zh":"我們正處在一場艱難談判之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6422b12d9831df965e52","word":"mighty","forms":["mighty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2a1df0bec9f8d01","term":"mighty","forms":["mighty","mightier","mightiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"力量強大的","explanation":"指人或動物本身很強壯、有很強的能力，重點是能以力量取勝或產生影響。","examples":[{"en":"The mighty wrestler lifted his opponent with ease.","zh":"那名強壯的摔跤手輕鬆舉起了對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A mighty river carved this deep valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mighty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5dbcc5555a6a750c576","word":"migrant","forms":["migrant"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e0d857689f92344","term":"migrant","forms":["migrant","migrants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遷移者；流動勞動者","explanation":"指從一個地區或國家移動到另一個地區或國家的人，原因可能是工作、生活或暫時旅行。重點是“跨地區移動”，不一定意味著永久定居。","examples":[{"en":"Many migrant workers return home after the harvest.","zh":"許多流動工人在收穫季結束後回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city provides shelter and legal advice for migrants.","zh":"這座城市為遷移者提供住所和法律諮詢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/migrant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2a6d1636cedda14","term":"migrant","forms":["migrant","more migrant","most migrant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遷徙的","explanation":"指會按照季節或環境變化從一個地方遷到另一個地方的，尤其常說動物或鳥類。它體現的是“不斷遷移”的特徵，而不是一次性的搬家。","examples":[{"en":"The lake is an important resting place for migrant birds.","zh":"這個湖是遷徙鳥類重要的棲息地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Migrant birds rest here during their autumn journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/migrant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a6cead4385ed4394247","word":"migration","forms":["migration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-037d7a312beb78e6","term":"migration","forms":["migration","migrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遷居；人口遷移","explanation":"指人離開原來居住的地方，到另一個地方生活一段時間或長期生活，重點是居住地點發生了改變，而不只是去那裡短暫訪問。","examples":[{"en":"The migration of workers to the cities changed the region.","zh":"工人遷往城市改變了這個地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"War caused a large migration of families across the border.","zh":"戰爭導致許多家庭遷移到邊境另一側。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/migration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c01a9a03a89f7e55","term":"migration","forms":["migration","migrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物遷徙","explanation":"指鳥、魚或哺乳動物按照季節、繁殖等規律，在不同地點之間往返移動；它仍然是“從一個位置到另一個位置”的遷移，只是物件換成了動物。","examples":[{"en":"The annual migration of whales attracts visitors to the coast.","zh":"鯨魚每年的遷徙吸引遊客來到海岸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists tracked the birds during their winter migration.","zh":"科學家在這些鳥冬季遷徙期間追蹤了它們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/migration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8290c583738717f6ceea","word":"mild","forms":["mild"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51324d3d3723d25d","term":"mild","forms":["mild","milder","mildest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"性情溫和的","explanation":"形容一個人脾氣平和、不容易生氣或對別人發火。它強調待人柔和，不一定表示這個人軟弱或沒有主見。","examples":[{"en":"Although he looks serious, he is actually very mild.","zh":"他看起來很嚴肅，但其實性情非常溫和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a mild manner and listens patiently to everyone.","zh":"她舉止溫和，耐心地聽每個人說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mild","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3ea4d2598582474","term":"mild","forms":["mild","milder","mildest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不嚴厲的；程度較輕的","explanation":"表示處罰、規定或批評的力度不大，遠沒有達到嚴厲的程度。它仍然可能帶來後果，只是相對寬鬆或較輕。","examples":[{"en":"Because it was his first offense, he received a mild sentence.","zh":"因為這是他第一次犯錯，他受到了較輕的判決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher gave him a mild warning.","zh":"老師只是對他提出了輕微的警告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mild","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11d105f4d731d19b","term":"mild","forms":["mild","milder","mildest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"溫暖而不冷的","explanation":"形容天氣或氣候溫和，尤其表示比預期暖一些、寒意不強。它不一定表示炎熱，只是說明天氣舒適或不太冷。","examples":[{"en":"We had a mild winter, with very little snow.","zh":"我們度過了一個溫和的冬天，幾乎沒下什麼雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mild weather was perfect for a walk.","zh":"這種溫和的天氣非常適合散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mild","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fede2030631728fc75f","word":"mile","forms":["mile"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7faed281c9b37ea8","term":"mile","forms":["mile","miles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英里","explanation":"英里是英語中常用的長度單位，1英里準確等於1.609344公里，也就是5280英尺或1760碼。它常用於說明道路距離、地點之間的遠近或行程長度。","examples":[{"en":"Turn left in 1.2 miles.","zh":"再走1.2英里後左轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel is about three miles from the station.","zh":"這家酒店距離車站大約三英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecd13c50d65d7837","term":"mile","forms":["mile","miles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舊制或其他英里","explanation":"mile有時泛指歷史上不同地區使用的英里單位，不一定嚴格等於現代國際英里。通常需要根據時代、國家或上下文來確定它的實際長度。","examples":[{"en":"The old map marks the village as four miles from the castle.","zh":"這張舊地圖示明該村莊距城堡四英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive uses the old Danish mile in distance records.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f7f85b1e7d5ffd45265","word":"milestone","forms":["milestone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c03b985795e6e5d","term":"milestone","forms":["milestone","milestones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要節點；里程碑式事件","explanation":"比喻人生、事業、國家歷史或專案中具有標誌性意義的重要事件或階段，就像路邊的里程碑一樣，說明事情已經推進到一個值得記住的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Graduating from university was a major milestone in her life.","zh":"大學畢業是她人生中的一個重要里程碑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team reached a major milestone when the first prototype worked.","zh":"第一個原型成功執行時，團隊達成了一個重要階段性成果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milestone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1110ec5adfeb77d7","term":"milestone","forms":["milestone","milestones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"里程碑","explanation":"本義是設定在道路旁、按里程排列的標誌，幫助行路者知道已經走了多遠；它不一定真的由石頭製成。","examples":[{"en":"The old milestone still stands beside the country road.","zh":"那塊古老的里程碑仍然立在鄉間小路旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inscription on the milestone placed the next town seven miles away.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milestone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-71d7575667922ac5c970","word":"military","forms":["military"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-619e0a11b4b821a9","term":"military","forms":["military","more military","most military"],"pos":"adj","zh":"軍人的；軍隊成員的","explanation":"指一個人的行為、經歷或身份帶有軍人或軍隊成員的特點，重點在“這個人屬於或體現軍隊的一方”。","examples":[{"en":"She has extensive military experience.","zh":"她有豐富的軍隊經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His military pension covers most of his expenses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/military","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5517ccd5e401365f","term":"military","forms":["military","more military","most military"],"pos":"adj","zh":"武裝力量的；軍隊的","explanation":"指與陸軍、海軍、空軍、海軍陸戰隊等武裝力量有關的事物，常用來和平民、警察或其他非軍事機構區分。","examples":[{"en":"The country sent military forces to protect the border.","zh":"這個國家派出武裝部隊保護邊境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Military vehicles carried supplies to the isolated villages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/military","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5537ded38e475a6","term":"military","forms":["military","militaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍隊；武裝部隊","explanation":"指一個國家的軍隊這一整體，包括不同軍種及其人員和組織；它不是指單獨的一名士兵。","examples":[{"en":"He spent six years in the military.","zh":"他在軍隊服役了六年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The military established a temporary bridge across the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/military","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8825e76530f87ff5c737","word":"milk","forms":["milk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d537ba38088abf98","term":"milk","forms":["milk","milks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乳汁；牛奶","explanation":"milk 是雌性哺乳動物乳腺產生的白色液體，用來餵養幼崽；人們也常把牛奶直接飲用或製成黃油、乳酪和酸奶。","examples":[{"en":"I drink a glass of milk with breakfast.","zh":"我早餐喝一杯牛奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This cheese is made from sheep's milk.","zh":"這種乳酪是用羊奶製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-901fac08e3b464b12fab","word":"mill","forms":["mill"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-437481b1f8bb67ec","term":"mill","forms":["mill","mills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"研磨機；磨坊","explanation":"mill 可以是把穀物、種子等材料磨碎的機器；由“把材料送進機器反覆加工”這個核心概念，也常讓人聯想到磨坊裡的研磨裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The pepper tastes better when it is ground in a mill.","zh":"胡椒用研磨器磨出來味道更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old water mill still grinds wheat for local farmers.","zh":"那座老水磨坊仍在為當地農民磨小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10252a2e5f146a64","term":"mill","forms":["mill","mills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"磨坊；加工廠","explanation":"mill 也指安置研磨或其他材料加工機器的建築、廠區或企業；因此它不只是一臺機器，還可以是“機器所在的工廠”。","examples":[{"en":"Her family has worked at the flour mill for three generations.","zh":"她家三代人都在這家麵粉廠工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The textile mill closed after the town lost its main customer.","zh":"這座紡織廠在該鎮失去主要客戶後關閉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce88d9c443cca40f","term":"mill","forms":["mill","mills","milling","milled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"磨碎；加工","explanation":"指把材料送進 mill 或其他機器反覆研磨、切削或加工，使它變成需要的形狀或狀態。這是“把材料送進機器反覆加工”這一核心概念最直接的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The factory mills wheat into flour.","zh":"這家工廠把小麥磨成麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These machines mill plastic parts very quickly.","zh":"這些機器加工塑膠零件的速度很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c98aa1222a25d36a","term":"mill","forms":["mill","mills","milling","milled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"機加工成形","explanation":"指用機器對材料或工件進行切削、整形、拋光或最後加工，使其達到規定的外形和表面狀態。這裡仍然是把東西送進機器反覆加工，只是重點從“處理材料”轉向“做出精確成品”。","examples":[{"en":"The workshop mills the metal plate to the required thickness.","zh":"車間用機器把金屬板加工到規定厚度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A computer-controlled machine milled the precise grooves.","zh":"一臺計算機控制的機器加工出了精確的凹槽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8ce96a5ba0d15da2f24","word":"million","forms":["million"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-770f582d01726b1e","term":"million","forms":["million","millions"],"pos":"num","zh":"一百萬","explanation":"它表示準確的數字一百萬，即一千乘以一千；把“一千個一千”看成一大堆，就容易記住這個數值。","examples":[{"en":"The city has a population of one million.","zh":"這座城市有一百萬人口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company sold two million phones last year.","zh":"這家公司去年賣出了兩百萬部手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/million","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8bf0febb220bc05d","term":"million","forms":["million","millions"],"pos":"num","zh":"極多；成百萬地","explanation":"它把“一百萬”這個巨大數量的畫面進一步誇張化，用來強調某物多得驚人，通常不是真的要精確計算。","examples":[{"en":"I've told you a million times to lock the door.","zh":"我都告訴過你無數次要鎖門了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I've got a million things to do before leaving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/million","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-725544de96fa7e38e7c1","word":"millionaire","forms":["millionaire"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b97770c283c0f718","term":"millionaire","forms":["millionaire","millionaires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"百萬富翁；百萬富婆","explanation":"指財富總量至少達到一百萬貨幣單位的人。這裡的“一百萬”通常是對整體財富的概括，不限於銀行賬戶裡的現金；因此，一個人的房產、投資等資產加起來達到這個數量，也可以稱為 millionaire。","examples":[{"en":"She became a millionaire after selling her company.","zh":"她賣掉自己的公司後成了百萬富翁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many millionaires still choose to live modestly.","zh":"許多百萬富翁仍然選擇過樸素的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/millionaire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-692e51978c0e4aa1f130","word":"mimic","forms":["mimic"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c31dcc7f46d9d04","term":"mimic","forms":["mimic","mimics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"模仿者","explanation":"指擅長模仿他人的聲音、動作、表情或說話方式的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is a brilliant mimic and can copy all her friends' accents.","zh":"她非常擅長模仿，能模仿所有朋友的口音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The talented mimic reproduced the principal's voice perfectly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mimic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a0d9a398f6d6b68","term":"mimic","forms":["mimic","mimics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"仿製品；模仿作品","explanation":"指模仿某人的聲音、動作或某件作品而做出的結果，也就是複製出來的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The recording was an almost perfect mimic of her voice.","zh":"這段錄音幾乎完美地模仿了她的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lure is a convincing mimic of a small fish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mimic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-970f1aadf5741c53","term":"mimic","forms":["mimic","mimics","mimicking","mimicked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"模仿；學樣取笑","explanation":"指複製某人的聲音、動作、表情或行為；如果是為了讓對方難堪，就有“學樣取笑”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The children mimicked their teacher's way of speaking.","zh":"孩子們模仿老師說話的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He mimicked my accent to make everyone laugh.","zh":"他學我的口音，想把大家逗笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mimic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c48f6310f1c849b4ac3","word":"mind","forms":["mind"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd7182755e7fd227","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"思考能力","explanation":"指進行推理、理解和思考的心智慧力，也可以指一個人的頭腦是否敏銳。","examples":[{"en":"Her mind is still sharp despite her age.","zh":"儘管年事已高，她的頭腦依然敏銳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puzzle exercises the mind as well as memory.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ceb024e8da443ea","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"記憶","explanation":"指記住和回想事情的能力；說某事不在 mind 裡，常常就是一時想不起來。","examples":[{"en":"The answer suddenly slipped my mind.","zh":"那個答案我突然想不起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The incident remains fresh in my mind.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e34e2aa0cd07bf5","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"注意力","explanation":"指把思想集中在某事上的能力；注意力轉到哪裡，心智之燈就照到哪裡。","examples":[{"en":"I can't keep my mind on my work today.","zh":"我今天無法集中注意力工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep your mind on the road while driving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3280c4a91516a22","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主意；意見","explanation":"指一個人心裡形成的判斷、看法或決定；改變 mind 就是改變原來的主意。","examples":[{"en":"I changed my mind and decided to stay home.","zh":"我改變了主意，決定待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I've changed my mind about selling the boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cded73a5effeab4b","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds","minding","minded","mindest","mindedst","mindeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"注意；留意","explanation":"表示把心智之燈轉向某人或某事，注意到它或觀察它。","examples":[{"en":"Mind the step when you get off the bus.","zh":"下公共汽車時請注意臺階。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mind the uneven stones near the entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-347616aa101983b9","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds","minding","minded","mindest","mindedst","mindeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聽從；當心","explanation":"表示注意某個要求並照做，也可用於提醒某人務必避免某種情況。","examples":[{"en":"Mind you don't touch the hot pan.","zh":"小心別碰那口熱鍋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mind the gap between the platform and the train.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eca4a6024e2e7726","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds","minding","minded","mindest","mindedst","mindeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"照看；照料","explanation":"表示暫時替別人看管人或物，把它放在自己的心上並確保它安全。","examples":[{"en":"Could you mind my bag while I buy a ticket?","zh":"我買票時，你能幫我照看一下包嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you mind the children while I shop?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbfbee08b6768341","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds","minding","minded","mindest","mindedst","mindeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"當心","explanation":"表示對可能造成危險或麻煩的地方保持警覺，常帶有直接提醒的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"Mind the gap between the train and the platform.","zh":"請當心列車和站臺之間的縫隙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mind you don't burn your fingers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dfd6669d7b33e89","term":"mind","forms":["mind","minds","minding","minded","mindest","mindedst","mindeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"介意；在乎","explanation":"表示某事讓自己不舒服、反感或受到影響；否定形式常表示“並不介意”或“願意”。","examples":[{"en":"Would you mind waiting outside for a moment?","zh":"你介意在外面等一會兒嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wouldn't mind a cup of tea.","zh":"我很想來一杯茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fd30542fe3f61b14bd4","word":"mine","forms":["mine"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3aadc79f9652ca38","term":"mine","forms":["mine","mines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"礦；礦井","explanation":"從地下開挖礦石或其他固體資源的地方，通常包括地下通道和作業區。這是“從地下挖出東西”這一核心畫面的直接名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The miners returned to the mine before sunrise.","zh":"礦工們在日出前回到了礦井。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old gold mine is now open to visitors.","zh":"那座舊金礦現在對遊客開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e2f49d73a7fc064","term":"mine","forms":["mine","mines","mining","mined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開採","explanation":"從地下挖出礦石、煤或其他資源，是“從礦井中取出東西”這一核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"The workers mine copper in the mountains.","zh":"工人在山區開採銅礦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are mining for lithium near the lake.","zh":"他們正在湖邊開採鋰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b133a3868993176b613","word":"miner","forms":["miner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e046675755f96fe3","term":"miner","forms":["miner","miners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"礦工","explanation":"指在礦井或礦區中開採煤、金屬等礦物的人。這個詞強調實際進行採礦工作的人，而不是擁有礦山的人。","examples":[{"en":"The miner worked underground for eight hours.","zh":"那名礦工在地下工作了八個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many miners lost their jobs when the coal mine closed.","zh":"煤礦關閉後，許多礦工失去了工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b607fddc95949938","term":"miner","forms":["miner","miners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地雷操作員","explanation":"指佈置、處理或操作地雷等軍用爆炸物的人；這裡的“礦”不是礦石，而是地雷這一類埋藏的爆炸物。","examples":[{"en":"The army sent a trained miner to clear the field.","zh":"軍隊派了一名受過訓練的地雷操作員去清理這片區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The miners carefully laid charges across the approach road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df5878eedaa9a3b2e67e","word":"mineral","forms":["mineral"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6db39f8fca788200","term":"mineral","forms":["mineral","minerals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"礦物","explanation":"指自然形成、具有相對確定化學成分和特徵物理性質的物質，通常特指無機物；可以把它記成地下自然形成的“礦物材料”。","examples":[{"en":"Quartz is one of the most common minerals in the Earth's crust.","zh":"石英是地殼中最常見的礦物之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cave contains several rare minerals.","zh":"這個洞穴裡有幾種稀有礦物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mineral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69a42ae4207453836a98","word":"mingle","forms":["mingle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f112a05b930b55b","term":"mingle","forms":["mingle","mingles","mingling","mingled","minglest","mingledst","mingleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"混合；混雜","explanation":"mingle 表示把某物與其他東西混在一起，混合後通常還能看出原來的不同部分，而不是完全變成均勻的一體。","examples":[{"en":"Mingle the flour and sugar in a large bowl.","zh":"把麵粉和糖在大碗裡混合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smell of coffee mingled with the scent of fresh bread.","zh":"咖啡的香味和新鮮麵包的香氣混在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mingle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e0a8e2e986d1778","term":"mingle","forms":["mingle","mingles","mingling","mingled","minglest","mingledst","mingleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"混合起來","explanation":"不及物的 mingle 表示不同事物自行混在一起或彼此融合，強調混合的過程和結果，而不是某人主動攪拌。","examples":[{"en":"The children's laughter mingled with the music.","zh":"孩子們的笑聲和音樂交織在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smells of coffee and fresh bread mingled.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mingle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89af49d76d2bd29a","term":"mingle","forms":["mingle","mingles","mingling","mingled","minglest","mingledst","mingleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加社交；與人交談","explanation":"在聚會中，mingle 表示在人群中走動並和不同的人隨意交談，也就是讓自己融入社交人群。","examples":[{"en":"Please mingle with the other guests while I finish setting the table.","zh":"我擺好桌子時，請和其他客人聊聊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt nervous, but soon started mingling at the party.","zh":"他本來有些緊張，但很快就開始在聚會上和大家交談了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mingle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-409664d46246de830632","word":"miniature","forms":["miniature"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8707322eeb79b8da","term":"miniature","forms":["miniature","more miniature","most miniature"],"pos":"adj","zh":"微型的；小型的","explanation":"表示比同類事物的通常尺寸小，往往是有意按比例縮小，仍保留原來的外形或用途。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a miniature railway running through the garden.","zh":"博物館裡有一條穿過花園的微型鐵路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibition features miniature models of famous buildings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miniature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f403c8da61b0e6a6","term":"miniature","forms":["miniature","miniatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"縮小的尺寸或形式","explanation":"指事物被縮小後的比例或狀態，重點在“縮小呈現”這一概念，而不一定指某一個具體模型。","examples":[{"en":"The whole village was recreated in miniature for the exhibition.","zh":"整個村莊都按縮小比例重現出來，供展覽使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jeweler painted a detailed portrait in miniature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miniature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1bb91d6b4c257f92","term":"miniature","forms":["miniature","miniatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微型模型；縮小複製品","explanation":"指按照較小比例製作、用來代表真實物體或場景的東西，例如建築、船隻或車輛的模型。","examples":[{"en":"A miniature of the old theater stood inside a glass case.","zh":"一個老劇院的微型模型放在玻璃櫃裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displays a miniature of the entire palace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miniature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a703788f832056626d71","word":"minimal","forms":["minimal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d13aa9e8263229b7","term":"minimal","forms":["minimal","more minimal","most minimal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極少的；最低限度的","explanation":"表示數量、努力、影響或程度少到接近最低限度，常暗示這樣的數量可能不夠完成某件事。它是“只留下必要部分”這一核心概念在數量上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"The repair was completed with minimal damage to the wall.","zh":"修理完成時，牆壁只受到極小的損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even minimal preparation can improve your presentation.","zh":"即使只做最低限度的準備，也能改善你的演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minimal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a31af4ca2e372da9","term":"minimal","forms":["minimal","more minimal","most minimal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極簡的","explanation":"描述藝術、建築、設計或生活方式中刪去裝飾、只保留簡單形狀和結構的風格。這裡的“少”不是數量少，而是視覺或結構元素被壓縮到很少。","examples":[{"en":"The studio has a minimal design with white walls and simple wooden furniture.","zh":"這間工作室採用極簡設計，牆壁是白色的，傢俱是簡單的木製品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her apartment has a minimal design with few decorations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minimal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5879a0f59f728fdfcf8f","word":"minimize","forms":["minimize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5b8957c23767136","term":"minimize","forms":["minimize","minimizes","minimizing","minimized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縮小；減少到最低程度","explanation":"表示把某物的大小、數量、程度或成本變小、變少，重點是實際減少，而不一定完全消除。","examples":[{"en":"We are trying to minimize food waste at home.","zh":"我們正在努力減少家裡的食物浪費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Careful packing minimizes the risk of damage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minimize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c35308f631aa434","term":"minimize","forms":["minimize","minimizes","minimizing","minimized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"淡化；貶低事情的嚴重性","explanation":"表示故意把問題、損失、風險或影響說得沒那麼嚴重，或讓它顯得不那麼重要；這裡縮小的是人們對事情的判斷，而不一定是事情本身。","examples":[{"en":"The company tried to minimize the risks of the new product.","zh":"這家公司試圖淡化新產品的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He minimized his injuries so his parents would not worry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minimize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-692e4e5decffcf5eac86","word":"minimum","forms":["minimum"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6dd52a8039fac1ed","term":"minimum","forms":["minimum"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最低限度的","explanation":"表示程度、數量或要求已經降到最低，不能再低；它強調的是一條最低界線，而不只是數量很少。","examples":[{"en":"The minimum age for entry is eighteen.","zh":"入場的最低年齡是十八歲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need the minimum amount of equipment to complete the job.","zh":"我們需要完成這項工作所必需的最低限度裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minimum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-175f9771caf2cf53","term":"minimum","forms":["minimum","minima","minimums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最低界線","explanation":"指某項要求、標準或數量允許達到的最低界線；實際情況不能低於這個界線。","examples":[{"en":"The course requires a minimum of three years of relevant experience.","zh":"這門課程要求至少有三年的相關經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At a minimum, please bring a valid identification card.","zh":"至少請帶一張有效身份證件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minimum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-830b6857946c3dc23d1a","word":"minister","forms":["minister"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30be08409fa71a44","term":"minister","forms":["minister","ministers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牧師","explanation":"指在新教教會中負責講道、主持宗教儀式並照料會眾的牧師。這個義項體現了“為他人服務、代表教會辦事”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The minister welcomed everyone before the service began.","zh":"禮拜開始前，牧師向大家表示歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our minister visits elderly members of the church every week.","zh":"我們的牧師每週都會探望教會里的年長會眾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minister","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac988d9f489891e5","term":"minister","forms":["minister","ministers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"部長","explanation":"指領導政府某個部門的政治人物，例如內政部長或財政部長。這裡的“服務”從服務會眾擴充套件為代表政府、負責公共事務。","examples":[{"en":"The Minister of Education announced a new school funding plan.","zh":"教育部長宣佈了一項新的學校經費計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became minister after winning the election.","zh":"她贏得選舉後成為了部長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minister","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ec99078e538c33050f7","word":"ministry","forms":["ministry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71608f6ce54ef354","term":"ministry","forms":["ministry","ministries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政府部門","explanation":"指由部長或同等級別官員負責的政府行政部門，例如財政、外交或教育部門。它的核心畫面是“負責公共事務的一套政府服務機構”。","examples":[{"en":"The Ministry of Finance released its annual budget today.","zh":"財政部今天公佈了年度預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ministry announced new funding for rural schools.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ministry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaacfcb9831aa9ea","term":"ministry","forms":["ministry","ministries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宗教牧職","explanation":"指某種宗教中承擔教導、牧養和精神服務的牧職或宗教工作；這裡的“服務”物件從公眾事務轉成了信仰群體。","examples":[{"en":"She felt called to the ministry after years of volunteering.","zh":"她做了多年志願服務後，感到自己受到召喚，應該投身牧職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left the ministry to teach at a university.","zh":"他離開牧職，到一所大學任教。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ministry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cabd786ac52d8cfc81b0","word":"minor","forms":["minor"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3340c289ae3773e","term":"minor","forms":["minor","more minor","most minor"],"pos":"adj","zh":"較小的；次要的","explanation":"表示某事物相較於另一選擇、同類事物或整體來說較小、較不重要或較不嚴重，抓住“較小、次要”這個核心即可。","examples":[{"en":"The report contains a few minor errors.","zh":"這份報告有幾處小錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The delay was only a minor inconvenience.","zh":"這次延誤只造成了小小的不便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77dec7c934b8eef1","term":"minor","forms":["minor","minors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未成年人","explanation":"指尚未達到法定成年年齡、因此通常承擔較少法律責任並享有較少法律權利的人；核心仍是年齡和法律地位相對較小。","examples":[{"en":"A minor cannot sign this contract without a parent or guardian.","zh":"未成年人未經父母或監護人同意不能簽署這份合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel does not allow minors to check in alone.","zh":"這家酒店不允許未成年人單獨辦理入住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-382a26212df69c1a","term":"minor","forms":["minor","minors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小調；小和絃","explanation":"在音樂語境中，是“minor scale”“minor key”或“minor chord”等說法的省略，表示小調、關係小調式或小和絃等。這裡是“較小、次要”發展出的音樂術語。","examples":[{"en":"The song begins in A minor and ends in C major.","zh":"這首歌以A小調開始，以C大調結束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He played a minor chord on the piano.","zh":"他在鋼琴上彈了一個小和絃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c357bba54304c7c","term":"minor","forms":["minor","minors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學輔修專業","explanation":"指大學裡正式認可的第二學習方向，所需學分通常少於主修專業；它就是“學習領域較小的第二方向”。","examples":[{"en":"I got a minor in English literature.","zh":"我輔修了英國文學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose economics as her minor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e48590cc1d30a5602ce","word":"minority","forms":["minority"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7126dc525289f9a4","term":"minority","forms":["minority","minorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少數；少數一方","explanation":"指在一個群體中人數少於多數的一方，重點是數量比例，不一定表示受歧視或處於弱勢。比如大多數人贊成時，反對的人就是 a minority。","examples":[{"en":"A minority of the students opposed the new rule.","zh":"少數學生反對這項新規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most people agreed, but a sizable minority were upset.","zh":"大多數人同意，但相當一部分少數人感到不滿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5795d4854db0d348","term":"minority","forms":["minority","minorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受壓制或受歧視的少數群體","explanation":"指在社會中被視為不同、並且受到從屬對待或歧視的群體。這裡不只是人數較少，還強調社會權力和待遇上的不平等。","examples":[{"en":"The policy aims to protect minorities from discrimination.","zh":"這項政策旨在保護少數群體免受歧視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Members of the minority reported being denied access to public housing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc6f17bbec824fff8f86","word":"mint","forms":["mint"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ce2b87a8400c352","term":"mint","forms":["mint","mints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鑄幣廠","explanation":"指由政府授權制造硬幣或其他貨幣的機構、建築或場所；它正是“把錢鑄造出來”的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The new coins were produced at the national mint.","zh":"這些新硬幣是在國家鑄幣廠製造的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum stands beside the old mint.","zh":"博物館坐落在舊鑄幣廠旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70d5b3924d7f66ba","term":"mint","forms":["mint","mints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄荷植物","explanation":"指一類帶有清涼香氣和味道的植物，常用於飲食、飲料或調味。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh mint grows well in a pot by the window.","zh":"新鮮薄荷在窗邊的花盆裡長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add a few mint leaves to the tea.","zh":"在茶里加幾片薄荷葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-129fa7713adba71e12dc","word":"minus","forms":["minus"],"officialPos":"prep./n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2674998c2b0009e0","term":"minus","forms":["minus"],"pos":"adj","zh":"負的；減少的","explanation":"表示數量為負，或相對於原來的數量有所減少；數學中的負數就是落在零以下的數。","examples":[{"en":"The account showed a minus balance after the payment.","zh":"付款後，賬戶顯示為負餘額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine cannot display a minus number.","zh":"這臺機器無法顯示負數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a0766c219b3383b","term":"minus","forms":["minus"],"pos":"adj","zh":"低於零；負的某個數值","explanation":"表示某個數值在零以下，或比指定的基準低出一定數量，最常見於溫度和其他刻度。","examples":[{"en":"It was minus ten degrees when we left the house.","zh":"我們出門時氣溫是零下十度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature fell to minus three overnight.","zh":"夜間氣溫降到了零下三度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-046dda06e9a0eccb","term":"minus","forms":["minus","minuses","minusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"減號","explanation":"指數學中的符號 −，表示從一個數量中減去另一個數量。","examples":[{"en":"Put a minus sign before the number.","zh":"在這個數字前加一個減號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing minus completely changed the calculation's result.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d264b11e0956d22f","term":"minus","forms":["minus","minuses","minusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負數","explanation":"指小於零的數量，核心仍是“從零以下減少”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"A minus is still a number, even though it is below zero.","zh":"負數雖然低於零，但仍然是一個數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature fell into the minuses overnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c01153f86b414250","term":"minus","forms":["minus"],"pos":"prep","zh":"減去","explanation":"表示從前面的數量中拿走後面的數量，形成減法關係。","examples":[{"en":"Seven minus two is five.","zh":"七減二等於五。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Twelve minus five leaves seven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28cdd20eaf134a05f183","word":"minute","forms":["minute"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-287ba8454fdf3287","term":"minute","forms":["minute","minutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分鐘","explanation":"時間單位，一分鐘等於六十秒，是一小時的六十分之一。","examples":[{"en":"The train will arrive in five minutes.","zh":"火車將在五分鐘後到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wait one minute before opening the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36b61103917424ad","term":"minute","forms":["minute","minutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一會兒；片刻","explanation":"口語中表示一段不明確但通常不長的時間，常用於請求別人稍等或表示馬上回來。","examples":[{"en":"Give me a minute to finish this message.","zh":"給我一點時間把這條訊息寫完。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wait a minute while I find my coat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04e84b3a86c2a0163fba","word":"miracle","forms":["miracle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b5f6ecdfddc7a65","term":"miracle","forms":["miracle","miracles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"超自然奇蹟","explanation":"miracle可以指看起來無法用自然規律解釋、因此被認為來自神或其他超自然力量的事件。","examples":[{"en":"Many people believe that the recovery was a miracle.","zh":"許多人相信這次康復是一個奇蹟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story tells of a miracle that saved the village.","zh":"這個故事講述了一個拯救村莊的奇蹟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miracle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ab5c0ea5922453d","term":"miracle","forms":["miracle","miracles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"奇蹟般的幸運結果","explanation":"miracle也可以指事情本來幾乎不可能成功，卻因為極大的幸運或頑強努力而成功的結果。","examples":[{"en":"By some miracle, everyone escaped the burning building.","zh":"大家不知憑什麼奇蹟般地逃出了著火的大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It would be a miracle if we finished the project by Friday.","zh":"如果我們能在星期五前完成這個專案，那簡直就是個奇蹟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miracle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f30701bcdb4e60a630f","word":"miraculous","forms":["miraculous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dafd6be2a5847b35","term":"miraculous","forms":["miraculous","more miraculous","most miraculous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇蹟般的；超自然的","explanation":"指事情彷彿由神明或其他超自然力量促成，或者按正常規律根本無法解釋。這個意義保留了“奇蹟”的本來含義，常用於宗教敘述或描述不可能的轉機。","examples":[{"en":"The doctors called her recovery miraculous.","zh":"醫生稱她的康復是個奇蹟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child survived the crash in what witnesses described as a miraculous escape.","zh":"那名孩子在事故中倖存下來，目擊者稱這是奇蹟般的逃生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miraculous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d189ae94cd5d1f27","term":"miraculous","forms":["miraculous","more miraculous","most miraculous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"驚人的；奇蹟般的","explanation":"泛指結果或表現驚人得像奇蹟，未必真的涉及神或超自然力量。它常用來形容逆轉、成功或及時發生的好事，強調事情原本幾乎不可能。","examples":[{"en":"Their miraculous comeback stunned everyone in the stadium.","zh":"他們奇蹟般的逆轉讓體育場裡的所有人都驚呆了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her recovery after such a fall seemed miraculous.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miraculous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00154761637ca746c354","word":"mirror","forms":["mirror"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8796da853c87eb0","term":"mirror","forms":["mirror","mirrors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鏡子","explanation":"能反射光線、照出面前影像的光滑表面，通常是玻璃製成的鏡子。","examples":[{"en":"She checked her hair in the mirror before leaving.","zh":"她出門前照了照鏡子，檢查自己的頭髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He checked his reflection in the mirror.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mirror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc29cc54eaad0dd4","term":"mirror","forms":["mirror","mirrors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反映物","explanation":"某個物件、人或事件像鏡子一樣，呈現出另一個物件的特點或真實情況。","examples":[{"en":"The novel is a mirror of life in a changing city.","zh":"這部小說反映了這座不斷變化的城市生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her letters are a mirror of changing social attitudes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mirror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25d9552ecea1a05b","term":"mirror","forms":["mirror","mirrors","mirroring","mirrored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"映出","explanation":"像鏡子一樣把光線、影像或某個物件呈現出來。","examples":[{"en":"The still lake mirrored the snow-covered mountains.","zh":"平靜的湖面映出了白雪覆蓋的群山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every polished window mirrored the flames across the street.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mirror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6644b07bc87bf06e","term":"mirror","forms":["mirror","mirrors","mirroring","mirrored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反映；對應","explanation":"某種佈局、結構或特點與另一個物件相同，或以相反方向對應，就像彼此形成映象。","examples":[{"en":"The new building mirrors the shape of the old station.","zh":"新建築的形狀與舊車站相對應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey results mirror our own experience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mirror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd21059c22fa488ea479","word":"miscellaneous","forms":["miscellaneous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-115a453185c848b8","term":"miscellaneous","forms":["miscellaneous","more miscellaneous","most miscellaneous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由不同種類的部分組成","explanation":"指一個集合裡混有許多不同型別的東西，彼此沒有單一的共同類別；重點是“混在一起、種類雜”。","examples":[{"en":"She found a miscellaneous collection of tools in the old shed.","zh":"她在舊棚子裡發現了一堆各種各樣的工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box contains miscellaneous items from my travels.","zh":"這個箱子裡裝著我旅行時留下的各種雜物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miscellaneous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15c3c641bd2b7a0c","term":"miscellaneous","forms":["miscellaneous","more miscellaneous","most miscellaneous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特點、能力或外觀各不相同","explanation":"強調同一組人或事物之間差異很大：它們可能有不同的特點、能力、外貌或形式，但被放在同一個總體中討論。","examples":[{"en":"The team includes people with miscellaneous skills and backgrounds.","zh":"這個團隊成員的技能和背景各不相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A miscellaneous crowd of traders, artists, and students gathered.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miscellaneous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3cd17514917a9abcccd","word":"mischief","forms":["mischief"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71031e80d3d446e3","term":"mischief","forms":["mischief","mischiefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"淘氣搗亂","explanation":"指帶有玩鬧意味、會給別人造成小麻煩的行為，通常不表示嚴重傷害。","examples":[{"en":"The children got into mischief while their parents were busy.","zh":"父母忙碌時，孩子們淘氣搗亂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A little mischief can make a dull afternoon more fun.","zh":"一點小淘氣能讓無聊的下午變得更有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mischief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9f3bab70facdd36","term":"mischief","forms":["mischief","mischiefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次惡作劇","explanation":"指一個具體的、帶有頑皮意味的搗亂行為，例如把別人的鞋帶系在一起。","examples":[{"en":"His latest mischief was hiding all the remote controls.","zh":"他最近的一次惡作劇是把所有遙控器都藏了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher smiled at the harmless mischief.","zh":"老師對這個無傷大雅的惡作劇笑了笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mischief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52a9afd09cfeb76962f5","word":"mischievous","forms":["mischievous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-12f06bd9e217db24","term":"mischievous","forms":["mischievous","more mischievous","most mischievous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"調皮的；愛惡作劇的","explanation":"形容人或孩子喜歡搞小惡作劇、故意做些不該做但通常不嚴重的事，帶有頑皮、淘氣和愛玩的意味。它常讓人覺得對方令人頭疼，卻未必真正令人討厭或危險。","examples":[{"en":"The mischievous boy hid his sister's shoes as a joke.","zh":"那個調皮的男孩為了開玩笑，把妹妹的鞋藏了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a mischievous smile before pressing the button.","zh":"她按下按鈕前，調皮地衝我笑了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mischievous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1710ebb1f2f69693cbe","word":"miserable","forms":["miserable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6fe4eebbf6548d07","term":"miserable","forms":["miserable","more miserable","most miserable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悲慘難受的","explanation":"表示人處於強烈的不快樂、身體不適或困窘之中，核心感覺是“被痛苦壓著，過得很不好”。它不一定只指貧窮，也可以指情緒低落、身體難受或生活處境糟糕。","examples":[{"en":"I felt miserable after hearing the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息後，我感到非常難受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sick dog looked miserable in the corner.","zh":"那條生病的狗蜷在角落裡，看起來很痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miserable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-64407f4d33e018635aa2","word":"misery","forms":["misery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7726a93a58587f40","term":"misery","forms":["misery","miseries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極度痛苦","explanation":"misery 指非常強烈的身心痛苦、悲慘狀態或深深的苦惱；重點是人彷彿被痛苦整個包圍，而不只是暫時心情不好。","examples":[{"en":"After the accident, he spent weeks in misery.","zh":"事故發生後，他在痛苦中熬了好幾個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You could see the misery on her face.","zh":"你可以看出她臉上的痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/misery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d51ed49eead1bf5","term":"misery","forms":["misery","miseries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"災禍；不幸","explanation":"misery 也可以指造成痛苦的具體災禍或不幸事件，也就是讓人陷入痛苦的事情本身，而不只是內心感受。","examples":[{"en":"The war brought misery to millions of families.","zh":"戰爭給數百萬個家庭帶來了苦難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote about the miseries of wartime displacement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/misery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-698a6a0e8c68690e4f21","word":"misfortune","forms":["misfortune"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dff2b360a6f75c6a","term":"misfortune","forms":["misfortune","misfortunes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壞運氣","explanation":"指事情接連不順、命運不佳的狀態，重點是整體的“運氣不好”，而不是某一件單獨的事故。","examples":[{"en":"I had the misfortune to lose my passport while traveling.","zh":"我旅行時很不幸地把護照弄丟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By misfortune, the train was delayed for three hours.","zh":"真倒黴，火車晚點了三個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/misfortune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9e4f41d9872eccf","term":"misfortune","forms":["misfortune","misfortunes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不幸的事情","explanation":"指一件具體而令人不快的事情，例如事故、損失或其他災禍；它可以看作壞運氣落到現實中的一次結果。","examples":[{"en":"After several misfortunes, the family decided to move to another city.","zh":"經歷了幾次不幸之後，這家人決定搬到另一座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Losing his passport was only the first of several misfortunes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/misfortune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a54754cf13316d475c81","word":"mislead","forms":["mislead"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e934e33c0d42ad2b","term":"mislead","forms":["mislead","misleads","misleading","misled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把人帶錯方向","explanation":"原本是帶路，卻把人引向錯誤的路、地點或方向；也可用於比喻性的指引和資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The broken sign misled us onto a narrow mountain road.","zh":"那塊損壞的路牌把我們引上了一條狹窄的山路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map misled the hikers, who ended up far from the lake.","zh":"地圖誤導了徒步者，結果他們離湖邊很遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mislead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fdc7aad4254eccf","term":"mislead","forms":["mislead","misleads","misleading","misled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用假資訊誤導","explanation":"透過撒謊、隱瞞事實或給出不完整的資訊，使別人相信了錯誤的印象或判斷；不一定要有明確的“帶路”動作。","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement misled customers about the product's safety.","zh":"這則廣告誤導了顧客，使他們對產品的安全性產生錯誤認識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was misled by his confident explanation.","zh":"他那番自信的解釋誤導了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mislead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80688fc3d5f88a06909e","word":"miss","forms":["miss"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1ce36a506baab62","term":"miss","forms":["miss","misses","Misses","Mlles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小姐；女士稱呼","explanation":"Miss 是對女性的禮貌稱呼，通常用於未婚女性，可單獨使用，也可放在姓名前；這裡的 Miss 是另一條獨立用法，不是“錯過”。","examples":[{"en":"Miss Carter, your appointment is ready.","zh":"卡特小姐，您的預約已經準備好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Excuse me, Miss, is this seat free?","zh":"不好意思，小姐，這個座位有人嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2daa056d8d6171aa","term":"miss","forms":["miss","misses","missing","missed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"未命中","explanation":"表示嘗試擊中、接住或抓住某物，卻擦肩而過，沒有碰到目標。","examples":[{"en":"I threw the ball to Sam, but he missed it.","zh":"我把球扔給薩姆，但他沒接住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The arrow missed the target by a few centimetres.","zh":"箭偏離目標幾釐米，沒射中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90658bca1b351b66","term":"miss","forms":["miss","misses","missing","missed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"未達到目標","explanation":"表示沒有達到原定的目標、標準或數值，就像目標從身邊擦過一樣。","examples":[{"en":"We missed our sales target by five percent.","zh":"我們的銷售目標差了百分之五，沒有達到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project missed its deadline by two days.","zh":"這個專案晚了兩天，沒趕上截止日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cba71408a02865cc","term":"miss","forms":["miss","misses","missing","missed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想念","explanation":"表示因為某人或某物不在身邊而感到缺少、思念或難過；這也是把 miss 記成“擦肩而過”後，距離變成情感上的空缺。","examples":[{"en":"I miss my family when I travel for work.","zh":"我出差時會想念家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She misses the quiet life she had in the countryside.","zh":"她懷念自己曾在鄉下過的寧靜生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/miss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fa1d3c4460b7347671e","word":"missile","forms":["missile"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1229e97eae667028","term":"missile","forms":["missile","missiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"導彈","explanation":"指發射後能自行推進、並且可以調整飛行路線的武器。這是現代英語中最常見、最需要優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The country launched a missile at the enemy's base.","zh":"該國向敵方基地發射了一枚導彈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missile can change direction after launch.","zh":"這枚導彈發射後可以改變方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/missile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12c4bb22086c095c","term":"missile","forms":["missile","missiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投射物；飛行武器","explanation":"指被人投擲或發射到空中的武器，例如石頭、箭或子彈。這是“把武器送出去”這一核心概念的寬泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers used stones as missiles.","zh":"士兵把石頭當作投射物使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Protesters hurled stones and other missiles at the barricade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/missile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ffa63583dfa6706b87d2","word":"missing","forms":["missing"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1a0b523def3702b","term":"missing","forms":["missing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"丟失的；找不到的","explanation":"東西原來存在，但現在找不到了，重點是它像從眼前消失了一樣。可以說某件物品丟了，也可以說某個人下落不明。","examples":[{"en":"One of my keys is missing.","zh":"我的一把鑰匙不見了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police are looking for the missing child.","zh":"警方正在尋找失蹤的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/missing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bdbe2b29ed1f3a1","term":"missing","forms":["missing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"缺少的；未出現的","explanation":"某人、某物或某項資訊本來應該在場或出現在某處，卻沒有出現；這裡不一定表示它曾經被找到後又丟失。","examples":[{"en":"There is a missing data point in the table.","zh":"這張表裡缺少一個資料點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missing page contained the crucial signature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/missing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ceb00a91525da64fb171","word":"mission","forms":["mission"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-817a712023696d57","term":"mission","forms":["mission","missions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"任務；使命","explanation":"指為完成某個明確目的而承擔的一組任務，可以是別人交給你的工作，也可以是你自己認定的責任。它比普通的“工作”更強調目的和責任感。","examples":[{"en":"The team was given a mission to restore the old bridge.","zh":"這個團隊接到了一項修復那座舊橋的任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is on a mission to find the perfect birthday gift.","zh":"她下定決心要找到最合適的生日禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dde75d53f42986a9a701","word":"missionary","forms":["missionary"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-079fa4d962662c3f","term":"missionary","forms":["missionary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傳教的；與傳教使命有關的","explanation":"表示某件事、某個組織或某項工作與宗教傳教使命有關，也就是圍繞向他人傳播宗教信仰展開。","examples":[{"en":"She spent ten years doing missionary work in rural communities.","zh":"她在農村社群從事了十年傳教工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The church runs several missionary schools overseas.","zh":"這所教會在海外開辦了幾所傳教學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/missionary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46cc1e159a75dac8","term":"missionary","forms":["missionary","missionaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳教士","explanation":"指到別的地方傳播宗教信仰、勸人接受某種宗教的人，英語語境中尤其常指基督教傳教士。","examples":[{"en":"The missionary spent years learning the local language.","zh":"這名傳教士花了多年時間學習當地語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The missionary learned the local language before opening a school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/missionary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9054966f3df0a88caa5a","word":"mist","forms":["mist"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-014e9d8ea4646a83","term":"mist","forms":["mist","mists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄霧；細小液滴","explanation":"mist是懸浮在空氣中的細小水滴或其他液滴形成的輕霧，通常比濃厚的霧更輕、更細。","examples":[{"en":"A thin mist covered the valley at dawn.","zh":"黎明時，一層薄霧籠罩著山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A light mist settled over the valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6c820ea72de99a8","term":"mist","forms":["mist","mists","misting","misted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"形成薄霧；起霧","explanation":"mist作不及物動詞時，表示空氣中出現一層細霧，也就是名詞mist所表示的霧形成了。","examples":[{"en":"It began to mist as we walked home.","zh":"我們走回家時，天開始下起濛濛細雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bathroom window misted as the shower ran.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b34ffb5e8ddb2c95579","word":"mistake","forms":["mistake"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-668eb0fb1edf97b9","term":"mistake","forms":["mistake","mistakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錯誤；失誤","explanation":"指無意中做錯、想錯或判斷錯的事情，範圍很廣，從拼寫錯誤到人生決定都可以稱為 mistake。","examples":[{"en":"I made a mistake in the last question.","zh":"我最後一道題做錯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone makes mistakes sometimes.","zh":"每個人有時都會犯錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mistake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-194fc69966cbe84a","term":"mistake","forms":["mistake","mistakes","mistaking","mistook","mistaken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……認成……","explanation":"指因為外表、聲音或其他相似之處，把一個人或事物誤認成另一個物件；核心畫面就是“拿錯了物件”。","examples":[{"en":"I mistook her for her sister.","zh":"我把她認成了她姐姐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dark shape was mistaken for a person.","zh":"那個黑影被誤認為是一個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mistake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b4a59fec3e7bcc78e40","word":"mistress","forms":["mistress"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a9d67135e52604e","term":"mistress","forms":["mistress","mistresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女主人；掌權女性","explanation":"指擁有很大控制權、權威或所有權的女性，是“女性掌控者”這一核心形象的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"She was the mistress of the house and made all the important decisions.","zh":"她是這所房子的女主人，所有重要決定都由她作出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The estate's mistress welcomed the guests at the door.","zh":"莊園的女主人在門口迎接客人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mistress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31340af4e43aae8d","term":"mistress","forms":["mistress","mistresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情婦；婚外伴侶","explanation":"現代最重要的特殊義項之一，指與已婚男性保持通常包含性關係的婚外女性伴侶；這裡“掌控者”的形象轉成了親密關係中的女性一方。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper claimed that the actor had a mistress in Paris.","zh":"報紙聲稱那名演員在巴黎有一位情婦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left his wife for his mistress.","zh":"他為了情婦離開了妻子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mistress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c86df9c018ed59ee053","word":"misunderstand","forms":["misunderstand"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5ec86251ecd98f6","term":"misunderstand","forms":["misunderstand","misunderstands","misunderstanding","misunderstood"],"pos":"verb","zh":"錯誤理解；誤會","explanation":"指一個人以為自己已經明白了，但實際上錯誤地理解了某人的話、某件事或某種情況。重點不只是沒有理解，而是形成了一個不正確的理解。","examples":[{"en":"I think you misunderstood my question.","zh":"我想你誤解了我的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She misunderstood what he meant and became upset.","zh":"她誤解了他的意思，因此生氣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/misunderstand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f907a6de331cc77376c","word":"mix","forms":["mix"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d94d27f3e9b2ce9f","term":"mix","forms":["mix","mixes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合物；混合組合","explanation":"指把兩種或更多物質混合後得到的整體，也可泛指由多種成分組成的組合。記住那個共同容器：不同東西進入其中後，形成一個mix。","examples":[{"en":"The salad is a fresh mix of lettuce, tomatoes, and herbs.","zh":"這份沙拉是生菜、西紅柿和香草的新鮮混合物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The birdseed is a mix of millet and sunflower seeds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mix","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47a87081c14c40c5","term":"mix","forms":["mix","mixes","mixing","mixed","mix'd","mixt","mixest","mixedst","mixeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攪拌；混合","explanation":"指把兩種或更多物質實際攪在一起，使它們形成一個整體。想象把食材倒進同一個碗裡並攪勻，這就是mix的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Mix the flour with the water until the dough is smooth.","zh":"把麵粉和水混合，直到麵糰變得光滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mix the two colors on your palette to make green.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mix","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4ae5c6049d2f902","term":"mix","forms":["mix","mixes","mixing","mixed","mix'd","mixt","mixest","mixedst","mixeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把不同事物結合起來","explanation":"指把原本分開或通常不放在一起的事物結合起來，可以是具體物品，也可以是工作、生活等抽象事物。核心仍是把不同部分放進同一個組合中。","examples":[{"en":"She tries not to mix work with her personal life.","zh":"她儘量不把工作和個人生活混在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course mixes classroom instruction with practical fieldwork.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mix","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58c92ee653b56b65bb14","word":"mixture","forms":["mixture"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27be5eaa1dfd0b87","term":"mixture","forms":["mixture","mixtures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合這一過程","explanation":"指把兩種或多種東西混在一起的動作或過程，重點在“正在混合”這件事，而不是最後得到的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The mixture of the two liquids must be done slowly.","zh":"這兩種液體的混合必須慢慢進行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gentle mixture of the ingredients prevents unwanted air bubbles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mixture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d84833dbba41d66a","term":"mixture","forms":["mixture","mixtures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合物","explanation":"指不同物質混合後形成的東西，例如由多種金屬、液體或其他材料組成的混合物；這裡的重點是混合後的結果。","examples":[{"en":"This tea is a mixture of herbs, flowers, and spices.","zh":"這種茶是由草藥、花朵和香料混合而成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add the mixture to the bowl and stir well.","zh":"把混合物倒入碗中並充分攪拌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mixture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52e763ef8e402df2","term":"mixture","forms":["mixture","mixtures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不同事物的混合組合","explanation":"把性質不同的事物放在一起看，表示一個由多種要素共同構成的整體，不一定是真正把物質攪在一起。天氣、情緒、經歷或風格都可以形成這種 mixture。","examples":[{"en":"The film is a mixture of humor and suspense.","zh":"這部電影融合了幽默和懸疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The neighborhood offers a mixture of shops and homes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mixture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b4d25aaa5980b090854","word":"moan","forms":["moan"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41a585a187f24f31","term":"moan","forms":["moan","moans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"呻吟聲","explanation":"指人在疼痛、悲傷或快感中發出的低沉聲音；核心畫面就是從情緒或身體裡拖出的一聲呻吟。","examples":[{"en":"He let out a deep moan when he tried to stand up.","zh":"他試著站起來時發出了一聲低沉的呻吟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A low moan came from the injured cyclist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11017c37a8c32e58","term":"moan","forms":["moan","moans","moaning","moaned","moanest","moanedst","moaneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出呻吟聲","explanation":"指發出低沉、拖長的聲音，通常因為疼痛、悲傷或快感；這裡 moan 直接把名詞 moan 變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"She moaned with pain as the doctor examined her ankle.","zh":"醫生檢查她的腳踝時，她疼得呻吟起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind moaned through the empty house.","zh":"風穿過空屋，發出低沉的嗚鳴聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d0d31889ef9ae20","term":"moan","forms":["moan","moans","moaning","moaned","moanest","moanedst","moaneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抱怨；發牢騷","explanation":"指像拖長呻吟一樣反覆表達不滿，因此從“發出呻吟聲”自然引申為“抱怨、發牢騷”。","examples":[{"en":"He is always moaning about the weather.","zh":"他總是在抱怨天氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He moaned about the traffic all morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a370ebd95136e8b2036","word":"mob","forms":["mob"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ac1ecc791eb93bd","term":"mob","forms":["mob","mobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴亂人群","explanation":"一大群聚在一起、行為混亂甚至準備打砸或攻擊的人。核心畫面就是人群擠成一團並可能失去控制。","examples":[{"en":"A mob gathered outside the courthouse.","zh":"一群鬧哄哄的人聚集在法院外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The angry mob broke through the gate.","zh":"憤怒的人群衝破了大門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6c79de19e403630","term":"mob","forms":["mob","mobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑手黨、犯罪團伙","explanation":"指從事有組織犯罪的團伙，尤其可指黑手黨；這裡的“一團人”不是失控，而是有組織地作惡。","examples":[{"en":"The detective spent years investigating the mob.","zh":"那名偵探花了多年調查這個犯罪團伙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness refused to testify against the mob.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19b22acea3662aa6","term":"mob","forms":["mob","mobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊戲敵人單位","explanation":"電子遊戲中可被玩家攻擊或擊殺的非玩家角色，通常是為了推進任務或劇情而存在的敵人。它延續了“會移動的一團物件”這個畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We need better gear before we fight that mob.","zh":"在挑戰那個敵人之前，我們需要更好的裝備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Defeat the smaller mobs before attacking the boss.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ab05ea75b240122","term":"mob","forms":["mob","mobs","mobbing","mobbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蜂擁圍住某人","explanation":"一群人突然聚攏並圍住某人，常帶有追逐、騷擾或敵意；也可用於粉絲過度圍上名人。","examples":[{"en":"Fans mobbed the actor as he left the theater.","zh":"演員離開劇院時，粉絲們蜂擁圍了上來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd mobbed the reporter with questions.","zh":"人群圍住記者，向他連珠炮似的提問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-372f86064e42e753","term":"mob","forms":["mob","mobs","mobbing","mobbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蜂擁進入或擠滿","explanation":"許多人同時擁入某個地方，使那裡迅速擠滿。它把“聚成一團”的畫面從圍住人擴充套件到圍進一個地點。","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers mobbed the store when the sale began.","zh":"打折開始時，顧客們蜂擁進了商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans mobbed the theater entrance after the performance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d524c1a0811da49592f8","word":"mobile","forms":["mobile"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ae8267b13aad6ae","term":"mobile","forms":["mobile","more mobile","most mobile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可移動的","explanation":"表示某物能夠被搬動、運輸，尤其是裝在輪子上或可以整體遷移的東西。它延續了“能動起來”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a mobile home near the lake.","zh":"他們在湖邊買了一所可移動住宅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic is mobile and visits remote villages.","zh":"這家診所可以移動，併為偏遠村莊提供服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mobile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36c012f42485cf6a","term":"mobile","forms":["mobile","more mobile","most mobile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"手機的；行動通訊的","explanation":"表示與手機、行動電話或行動通訊服務有關，是“能隨身移動”這一概念在通訊領域的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Please leave your mobile number on the form.","zh":"請在表格上留下你的手機號碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is expanding its mobile payment service.","zh":"這家公司正在拓展移動支付服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mobile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61fb11e9a8309acb22cf","word":"mobilize","forms":["mobilize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf96667d58a20197","term":"mobilize","forms":["mobilize","mobilizes","mobilizing","mobilized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調動起來","explanation":"把原本分散或尚未投入行動的人、資金、物資等組織起來，使它們能夠迅速發揮作用；核心畫面是“把力量集中並推向行動”。","examples":[{"en":"The new plan mobilized local resources for emergency relief.","zh":"這項新計劃調動了當地資源，用於緊急救援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The community mobilized volunteers to clean up the river.","zh":"社群組織志願者清理河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mobilize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7880420aa4bdbd66","term":"mobilize","forms":["mobilize","mobilizes","mobilizing","mobilized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"動員部隊和裝備","explanation":"把士兵、武器和其他軍事裝備按統一計劃集中起來，進入隨時可以作戰的狀態；這是“調動力量”在軍事領域的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The government mobilized thousands of troops and their equipment near the border.","zh":"政府在邊境附近動員了數千名士兵及其裝備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country mobilized its reserve forces overnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mobilize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec864fe99b539704b887","word":"mock","forms":["mock"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0c734c8fb2d50b6","term":"mock","forms":["mock"],"pos":"adj","zh":"模擬的；仿製的","explanation":"指按照真實物件做出的替代品或練習版本，功能或外形像真的，但本身不是真正的原物。","examples":[{"en":"We have a mock exam next Friday.","zh":"我們下週五要參加一次模擬考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firefighters practiced inside a mock aircraft cabin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae4937fbc0ce4165","term":"mock","forms":["mock","mocks","mocking","mocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"模仿；模擬","explanation":"指讓某個動作、狀態或物件表現得像另一個真實物件，不一定含有嘲笑意味。","examples":[{"en":"The actor mocked the sound of a train.","zh":"那名演員模仿了火車的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting mocks the style of nineteenth-century portraits.","zh":"這幅畫模仿了十九世紀肖像畫的風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e642b12901a6ee51456f","word":"mode","forms":["mode"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54a233ad382cdc9c","term":"mode","forms":["mode","modes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂調式","explanation":"在音樂中，mode 是一套組織音高的音階模式；現代西方音樂中的大調和自然小調也可以看作其中的兩種調式。","examples":[{"en":"The melody shifts from a major mode to a minor mode.","zh":"這段旋律從大調式轉為小調式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The melody is written in the Dorian mode.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e5af7d5a8776694","term":"mode","forms":["mode","modes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"做事的方式","explanation":"mode 可以表示完成某件事所採用的具體辦法，也就是“以什麼方式做成”。它強調事情采取的形式或途徑，而不是動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The form asks for your preferred mode of payment.","zh":"表格要求填寫你偏好的付款方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to choose the safest mode of transport.","zh":"我們需要選擇最安全的交通方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2db1a5a20a0e78e","term":"mode","forms":["mode","modes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"所處狀態","explanation":"mode 也可以表示人、團隊或系統暫時處於的狀態或應對框架，例如危機狀態、工作狀態。它把一種狀態想成當前正在執行的模式。","examples":[{"en":"After the accident, the whole team went into crisis mode.","zh":"事故發生後，整個團隊進入了危機狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I am in work mode, so I cannot talk right now.","zh":"我現在正處於工作狀態，所以暫時不能聊天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mode","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9372c470eeadd5ecd9c3","word":"model","forms":["model"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82b43916eab643d0","term":"model","forms":["model","models"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術或時裝模特","explanation":"指為繪畫、雕塑或其他藝術創作提供人體形象的人，也可泛指作為創作參照的人體物件。這裡的核心仍是“提供樣板”。","examples":[{"en":"The artist asked her to pose as a model for an hour.","zh":"那位藝術家請她當了一個小時的模特。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He worked as a model before becoming an actor.","zh":"他在成為演員以前做過模特。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/model","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff4cf26fd82fb5c3","term":"model","forms":["model","models"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實物的模型","explanation":"指對真實物體的縮小、簡化或仿製呈現，讓人能夠觀察它的外形、結構或運作方式。它本身不是原物，而是幫助理解原物的樣板。","examples":[{"en":"The students built a model of the bridge from cardboard.","zh":"學生們用硬紙板做了一座橋的模型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a detailed model of the old town.","zh":"博物館裡有一座老城區的精細模型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/model","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-710ce73b2ee2fadb","term":"model","forms":["model","models"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用於分析的模擬模型","explanation":"指用公式、資料或程式對真實系統或事件進行簡化和模擬的工具，用來分析其運作方式或預測可能結果。它像一張抽象的樣板，把複雜現實保留成可研究的結構。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used a computer model to predict flooding.","zh":"研究人員用計算機模型預測洪水情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This model helps us understand how the market changes.","zh":"這個模型幫助我們理解市場如何變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/model","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dff22754ace5cbab4fbb","word":"moderate","forms":["moderate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71023b9f607681a6","term":"moderate","forms":["moderate","more moderate","most moderate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"適度的；不過度的","explanation":"指數量、行為或程度控制在合理範圍內，既不是過量，也沒有走向極端。這是 moderate 最基礎、最能帶出其他含義的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Moderate exercise can improve your health.","zh":"適度運動有助於改善健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company expects moderate growth this year.","zh":"公司預計今年會有適度增長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moderate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-774cdf08f6a80fc9dded","word":"modern","forms":["modern"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3d6506ea34f13fd","term":"modern","forms":["modern","moderner","more modern","modernest","most modern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"現代的；當代的；現代風格的","explanation":"指與現在或不久以前的時代有關，或者在外觀、方法上顯得不像古代而具有現代風格。它可以形容技術和教育方法，也可以形容歷史悠久的建築如今呈現出的樣子。","examples":[{"en":"The museum combines an old stone exterior with a modern interior.","zh":"這座博物館把古老的石頭外牆和現代化的內部設計結合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Modern technology has changed the way we learn.","zh":"現代技術改變了我們的學習方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08fe4e55201124aa","term":"modern","forms":["modern","moderner","more modern","modernest","most modern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"近現代時期的","explanation":"在歷史、社會科學等學術語境中，指從大約十九世紀開始直到當代的近現代時期；這裡的 modern 是一個時期分類詞，不只是日常意義上的“看起來新”。","examples":[{"en":"She is taking a course on modern history this semester.","zh":"她這學期正在修一門近現代史課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course traces European history from medieval to modern times.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a83f8a2ed89bf20f0e92","word":"modernization","forms":["modernization"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aacbb15884972930","term":"modernization","forms":["modernization","modernizations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現代化；現代化改造","explanation":"指把舊的裝置、制度、機構或社會整體改造成更符合現代標準和需要的狀態，重點在“變現代”的過程，而不是最終結果本身。","examples":[{"en":"The modernization of the railway system will take several years.","zh":"鐵路系統的現代化改造需要幾年時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government launched a modernization program for public hospitals.","zh":"政府啟動了公立醫院現代化改造計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modernization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cbbcbb0892c3e82ff12","word":"modernize","forms":["modernize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd136360f5a577f9","term":"modernize","forms":["modernize","modernizes","modernizing","modernized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使現代化","explanation":"指主動改造舊的或過時的事物，例如更換裝置、調整設計或更新系統，使它符合現在的需要。重點是“有人把某物改好”，而不是僅僅說它看起來新。","examples":[{"en":"The city plans to modernize its public transportation system.","zh":"這座城市計劃對公共交通系統進行現代化改造。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory modernized its equipment last year.","zh":"這家工廠去年更新了裝置，使其實現了現代化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modernize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a69d385651720cf2","term":"modernize","forms":["modernize","modernizes","modernizing","modernized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得現代化","explanation":"指某個組織、行業或社會逐漸採用新的外觀、觀念或做法，自己轉向更現代的狀態。這裡不強調誰具體動手改造，而強調主語發生了現代化變化。","examples":[{"en":"The industry is modernizing rapidly as new technology becomes cheaper.","zh":"隨著新技術變得更便宜，這個行業正在迅速實現現代化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rail network modernized rapidly after the war.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modernize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab76588c2a469ca06aa9","word":"modest","forms":["modest"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bff5fbe808ad5de","term":"modest","forms":["modest","more modest","modester","most modest","modestest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"謙遜的；不自誇的","explanation":"形容人不誇耀自己的能力、成就或身份，表現得樸實而謙遜。","examples":[{"en":"Despite winning the award, she remained modest.","zh":"儘管獲了獎，她仍然很謙遜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is modest about his achievements.","zh":"他不愛誇耀自己的成就。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cccf5cab09f6c6c4","term":"modest","forms":["modest","more modest","modester","most modest","modestest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不大的；適度的","explanation":"形容數量、收入、規模或要求等不算大，但通常仍然夠用或可以接受，帶有“適中”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"He earns a modest amount of money.","zh":"他賺的錢不多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project produced modest results in its first year.","zh":"這個專案第一年取得的成果有限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0451dc5daae76d618dd0","word":"modesty","forms":["modesty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6caedbcec7782ea","term":"modesty","forms":["modesty","modesties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"謙遜；不自誇","explanation":"指一個人不會高估自己，也不會過分炫耀自己的能力或成就；核心畫面是把自我評價收得恰到好處。","examples":[{"en":"She accepted the award with modesty and thanked the whole team.","zh":"她謙遜地接受了獎項，並感謝了整個團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His modesty makes it hard to realize how much experience he has.","zh":"他的謙遜讓人很難意識到他其實經驗豐富。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modesty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-121ec0794c365abd","term":"modesty","forms":["modesty","modesties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剋制；含蓄","explanation":"指行為、態度或表達不過度張揚，保持適度和分寸；它把“收一收”的核心概念從自我評價擴充套件到了整體舉止。","examples":[{"en":"The room was decorated with modesty, using simple furniture and soft colors.","zh":"房間佈置得很樸素，使用了簡單的傢俱和柔和的色彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building's architectural modesty suits its quiet surroundings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modesty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9106d6212bb4dfc92844","word":"modify","forms":["modify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a9389d3bc916cbb","term":"modify","forms":["modify","modifies","modifying","modified","modifiest","modifiedst","modifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修改；調整","explanation":"在原有事物的基礎上改動其中一部分，使它更合適、更清楚或更有效；重點是調整，而不是從頭創造一個全新的東西。","examples":[{"en":"We modified the design to make it easier to use.","zh":"我們調整了設計，使它更容易使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher asked me to modify a few sentences in my essay.","zh":"老師讓我修改文章中的幾個句子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e3efa2c376c42e6","term":"modify","forms":["modify","modifies","modifying","modified","modifiest","modifiedst","modifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發生變化；得到調整","explanation":"表示事物本身經過調整而變得不同，或處於不斷被調整的狀態；這裡不突出是誰在改它。","examples":[{"en":"The original plan was modified after the meeting.","zh":"原計劃在會議後作了調整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their behavior modified as they became accustomed to captivity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69c7a3b8ce22ce1feca4","word":"moist","forms":["moist"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fc1ec99f8f9302d","term":"moist","forms":["moist","moister","more moist","moistest","most moist"],"pos":"adj","zh":"溼潤的；略溼的","explanation":"指某物帶有水分、不是乾的，但通常還沒有溼到滴水或浸透的程度。這是 moist 最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Keep the soil moist, but do not let it become waterlogged.","zh":"保持土壤溼潤，但不要讓它積水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The towel was still moist after drying overnight.","zh":"這條毛巾晾了一夜後仍然有些溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ade169be89e9910c","term":"moist","forms":["moist","moister","more moist","moistest","most moist"],"pos":"adj","zh":"潮溼的；溼潤多雨的","explanation":"描述氣候、空氣或天氣中水分較多，給人潮溼、悶溼或多雨的感覺。這是從“帶有水分”自然擴充套件出的常用意思。","examples":[{"en":"This plant grows best in a warm, moist climate.","zh":"這種植物在溫暖潮溼的氣候中生長最好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Moss thrives in this moist woodland climate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31bb9529338de2408874","word":"moisture","forms":["moisture"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b31364886b284cc0","term":"moisture","forms":["moisture","moistures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水分；溼氣","explanation":"指使東西變溼的水分或少量液體，常常是表面上的水珠、凝結水，或材料中含有的水分。重點不是一整片水，而是附著、滲入或散佈在某處的那層水分。","examples":[{"en":"Wipe the moisture off the window before it drips onto the floor.","zh":"在水分滴到地板上之前，把窗戶上的水汽擦掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soil still contains enough moisture for the plants.","zh":"土壤裡仍然含有足夠的水分供植物生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moisture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-449b0eabc7972d01","term":"moisture","forms":["moisture","moistures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溼潤狀態","explanation":"指某物保持溼潤、不幹燥的狀態。這裡關注的不是某一滴水，而是由水分帶來的整體溼潤程度。","examples":[{"en":"This cream helps the skin retain moisture throughout the day.","zh":"這款面霜有助於皮膚一整天保持水分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The seedlings need steady moisture to survive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moisture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd282cd375dcc40a9fa0","word":"molecule","forms":["molecule"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e3f4ea41ba07494","term":"molecule","forms":["molecule","molecules","moleculae","moleculæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分子","explanation":"分子是由兩個或更多原子透過化學鍵結合成的微小單位，並且仍保留某種元素或化合物的化學性質。例如，水分子由氫原子和氧原子組成。","examples":[{"en":"A water molecule contains two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.","zh":"一個水分子含有兩個氫原子和一個氧原子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The molecule breaks apart when heated.","zh":"這種分子受熱時會分解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/molecule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8899c3e565f98935","term":"molecule","forms":["molecule","molecules","moleculae","moleculæ"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極少量","explanation":"在非嚴格的科學語境中，molecule 可以把某物說成小到幾乎不存在的一點點，強調數量極少，而不是在定義真正的化學分子。","examples":[{"en":"There wasn't a molecule of dust left in the room.","zh":"房間裡一點灰塵都沒有留下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He showed not a molecule of sympathy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/molecule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72110207b6499adb0ff6","word":"moment","forms":["moment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-189d6407e7126844","term":"moment","forms":["moment","moments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"片刻；一會兒","explanation":"指很短、但沒有精確規定長度的一段時間，是日常英語中最核心的用法。它可以表示說話者希望對方短暫等待，也可以指某件事發生的那一刻。","examples":[{"en":"Wait a moment while I find my keys.","zh":"等我一會兒，我找找鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She closed her eyes for a moment and took a deep breath.","zh":"她閉了一會兒眼，深深地吸了口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-446be308664e1964b816","word":"momentum","forms":["momentum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71ccd58d412da4a6","term":"momentum","forms":["momentum","momentums","momenta"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動量","explanation":"在物理學中，momentum 是運動物體所具有的動量，取決於物體的質量和速度；物體越重或運動越快，動量通常越大。這個意義是其他抽象意義的基礎：運動中的物體帶有繼續運動的力量。","examples":[{"en":"In physics, momentum is calculated as mass multiplied by velocity.","zh":"在物理學中，動量等於質量乘以速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Doubling the object's mass doubles its momentum at unchanged velocity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/momentum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4b9f27fb2c3f407","term":"momentum","forms":["momentum","momentums","momenta"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運動產生的衝力","explanation":"這裡強調物體運動起來後所帶有的衝力或慣性力量，常常使它難以馬上停下。它比單純描述運動更突出“運動帶來的持續推動作用”。","examples":[{"en":"The heavy cart gathered momentum as it rolled down the hill.","zh":"那輛沉重的推車沿山坡滾下時逐漸獲得了衝力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heavy cart's momentum carried it through the gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/momentum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1ea29a52d796b45","term":"momentum","forms":["momentum","momentums","momenta"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展勢頭","explanation":"這是從物體運動引申出的抽象意義：一個想法、計劃或事件一旦獲得支援和進展，就像滾動起來的物體一樣，會形成繼續向前發展的力量。它強調事情正在變得更有影響力或更難停下來，而不只是表示“進展”。","examples":[{"en":"The community project gained momentum after more volunteers joined.","zh":"更多志願者加入後，這個社群專案獲得了更大的發展勢頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The petition gained momentum after the television report.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/momentum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f27d53a9e09c7a9a80e","word":"monarch","forms":["monarch"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91d5ac7fc4b9a535","term":"monarch","forms":["monarch","monarchs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"君主","explanation":"monarch 是君主制國家的統治者：在絕對君主制中掌握最高權力，在君主立憲制中則可能只是國家元首。這個詞強調的是“處於最高統治位置的人”，不只等於“國王”。","examples":[{"en":"The monarch opened Parliament with a speech.","zh":"這位君主發表演講，宣佈議會開會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country’s monarch has mostly ceremonial duties.","zh":"這個國家的君主主要履行禮儀性職責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monarch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1c758610c008685e0f8","word":"monetary","forms":["monetary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-107d70a60bbedd64","term":"monetary","forms":["monetary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貨幣的；金錢的","explanation":"指與錢或貨幣直接有關的事物，重點可以是錢的價值、數量，也可以是貨幣的發行和管理。它把“錢”這個核心概念擴充套件到圍繞錢展開的制度、政策和評價。","examples":[{"en":"The painting has little monetary value, but it means a lot to my family.","zh":"這幅畫的貨幣價值不高，但對我們家來說意義重大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The central bank announced a change in monetary policy.","zh":"中央銀行宣佈調整貨幣政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monetary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d2ac8b58ead9744d772","word":"money","forms":["money"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-049684ce5827a2a1","term":"money","forms":["money","monies","moneys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錢；交換媒介","explanation":"money 最基本的意思是大家普遍接受、可以用來購買商品或服務的東西。它不只指紙幣和硬幣，也包括社會認可的其他支付形式。","examples":[{"en":"I saved some money to buy a bicycle.","zh":"我攢了一些錢，準備買一輛腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Money makes it easier to trade goods and services.","zh":"錢讓商品和服務的交換變得更容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/money","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-393cb4d9321a743b","term":"money","forms":["money","monies","moneys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財富；有錢","explanation":"當 money 表示財富時，重點不再是某一筆支付用的錢，而是一個人總體擁有的經濟實力和富裕程度。","examples":[{"en":"She grew up with money but learned to live simply.","zh":"她從小家境富裕，但學會了過簡樸的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He never talks about how much money he has.","zh":"他從不談自己有多少財富。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/money","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7de97367c9cdc3c6db31","word":"monitor","forms":["monitor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ded9c9dfe305dc7a","term":"monitor","forms":["monitor","monitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監督者；值班看護人","explanation":"指負責看守、照料或監督某人某事的人，是“觀察哨”這一核心概念在人身上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"The camp monitors look after the children at night.","zh":"營地管理員晚上負責照看孩子們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An examination monitor checked everyone's identification.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0f0d53b69898897","term":"monitor","forms":["monitor","monitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監測器","explanation":"指能持續檢測某種情況、數量或變化並報告結果的裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse checked the patient's heart monitor.","zh":"護士檢查了病人的心臟監測儀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monitor sounds an alarm if oxygen levels drop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0081b6ee8408aaa","term":"monitor","forms":["monitor","monitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顯示器","explanation":"指連線電腦、用於顯示文字、影象或程式輸出的螢幕裝置。它仍然像一個“觀察哨”，把電腦內部的結果呈現給人看。","examples":[{"en":"The error message appeared on my monitor.","zh":"錯誤資訊出現在我的顯示器上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Connect the laptop to a larger monitor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-79a7b21a164410fe","term":"monitor","forms":["monitor","monitors","monitoring","monitored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"監測；監督","explanation":"指持續觀察、檢查或照看某人某事，以確認情況正常或及時發現問題。這是“觀察哨”概念最直接的動作形式。","examples":[{"en":"Doctors monitored her closely after the operation.","zh":"手術後，醫生密切監測她的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We monitor the temperature every hour.","zh":"我們每小時監測一次溫度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b550d15e298bd082ff0","word":"monk","forms":["monk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e60dfb9c486aa7de","term":"monk","forms":["monk","monks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男修道士","explanation":"指加入修道團體、把一生投入宗教服務的男性修士，通常遵守嚴格的宗教生活規則。","examples":[{"en":"The monk spent most of his day in prayer.","zh":"這位修道士一天的大部分時間都在祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young monk lived in a mountain monastery.","zh":"這名年輕修道士住在山間的修道院裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3bfd0408c7a8220c","term":"monk","forms":["monk","monks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隱修士","explanation":"在較早的用法中，monk也可特指離群獨居、專心修行的隱修士，而不是住在共同體中的修士。","examples":[{"en":"The hermit monk lived alone in a cave.","zh":"這位隱修士獨自住在洞穴裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An elderly monk welcomed pilgrims to the secluded monastery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-000c285457fc971f862a","word":"monkey","forms":["monkey"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1f3c446cb3c1745","term":"monkey","forms":["monkey","monkeys","monkies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猴子","explanation":"指通常體形較小、有尾巴或頰囊、但不包括猿類的猴科或類人猿近親動物；日常英語中常泛指猴子。","examples":[{"en":"A monkey grabbed my hat at the zoo.","zh":"動物園裡有隻猴子搶走了我的帽子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the monkeys play in the trees.","zh":"我們看著猴子們在樹上玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monkey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb3b5639a043f55b783e","word":"monopoly","forms":["monopoly"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b6dce5e1cdf7ed6","term":"monopoly","forms":["monopoly","monopolies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"市場壟斷","explanation":"指某一家公司、團體或其他一方成為某種商品或服務的唯一或壓倒性供應者，從而能夠強力影響整個市場。這是“市場入口只有一個賣家”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"The company has a monopoly on electricity in the region.","zh":"這家公司壟斷了該地區的電力供應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small number of firms control a near monopoly over the online market.","zh":"少數幾家公司幾乎壟斷了網路市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monopoly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b5ab781f11d1c51","term":"monopoly","forms":["monopoly","monopolies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對生產或交易的獨佔控制","explanation":"強調對某種商品的生產、供應或交易擁有排他性的控制權；重點不只是市場結果，而是“只有這一方能夠掌控或經營”。","examples":[{"en":"The company built a monopoly over the region's rare minerals.","zh":"這家公司壟斷了該地區稀有礦產的開採和交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company maintained a monopoly over the salt trade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monopoly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-973c99824dc2a1e07bd6","word":"monotony","forms":["monotony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89842cda72786dda","term":"monotony","forms":["monotony","monotonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重複造成的乏味","explanation":"指因為事情一再重複、沒有新鮮變化而產生的單調和厭倦感；重點在於“沒有變化”帶來的乏味，而不只是短暫的無聊。","examples":[{"en":"The monotony of doing the same task every day was exhausting.","zh":"每天做同一項工作所帶來的單調感令人疲憊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Music and conversation helped break the monotony of the long journey.","zh":"音樂和交談幫助打破了漫長旅途的單調。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monotony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fb7d31b909e8071","term":"monotony","forms":["monotony","monotonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音調始終不變","explanation":"指聲音、說話聲或音樂的音高沒有起伏，始終保持同一個調子；這種聲音常會讓聽者覺得單調。","examples":[{"en":"The monotony of his voice made the lecture difficult to follow.","zh":"他聲音的單調讓這場講座很難聽下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monotony of his delivery sent listeners to sleep.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monotony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-beaafa510bcc774b1be0","word":"monster","forms":["monster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d662f64940f9b576","term":"monster","forms":["monster","monsters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可怕的怪物","explanation":"指尤其出現在神話、幻想或恐怖故事中的危險生物，是 monster 最基本的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers hid when the monster came out of the cave.","zh":"怪物從洞裡出來時，村民們躲了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monster emerged from beneath the ruined castle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5a12df66df6947fe90a","word":"monstrous","forms":["monstrous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d40a9ad715cdde58","term":"monstrous","forms":["monstrous","more monstrous","most monstrous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可怕的；醜陋駭人的","explanation":"形容外表、行為或事物像怪物一樣令人害怕、厭惡或震驚，重點是負面的強烈感受。","examples":[{"en":"The monster had a monstrous face and enormous teeth.","zh":"那隻怪物長著一張可怕的臉和巨大的牙齒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was a monstrous act of cruelty.","zh":"那是一種極其殘酷、令人髮指的行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monstrous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f158e3d0e8078658","term":"monstrous","forms":["monstrous","more monstrous","most monstrous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大得驚人的","explanation":"從“怪物般異常”引申而來，形容尺寸、數量或程度大得不正常、令人吃驚。","examples":[{"en":"The project required a monstrous amount of money.","zh":"這個專案需要一大筆驚人的資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A monstrous truck blocked the narrow alley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monstrous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5c7d1719e284f2c9485","word":"month","forms":["month"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce928f82db51447f","term":"month","forms":["month","months"],"pos":"noun","zh":"月份","explanation":"一年被分成若干個固定的日曆單位，每一個單位就是一個 month，例如一月、七月等。這個義項強調它在一年中的位置和名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The school year begins in September, the first month of autumn.","zh":"學年從九月開始，這是秋季的第一個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"February is the shortest month of the year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/month","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85418138f83e9907","term":"month","forms":["month","months"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個月的時間","explanation":"month 也可以表示一段大約三十天的時長，不強調它在日曆中的具體名稱；實際天數會隨月份不同而變化。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed there for a month before moving on.","zh":"我們在那裡待了一個月，之後才繼續前行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repairs should take about a month.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/month","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9169e3ca73eeb47d29e9","word":"monthly","forms":["monthly"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5028295234e9c92","term":"monthly","forms":["monthly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"每月的","explanation":"指每個月都會發生、安排或出現一次的事，重點是固定的月度週期。","examples":[{"en":"The magazine includes a monthly crossword.","zh":"這本雜誌每月都有一道填字遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have a monthly team meeting.","zh":"我們每月開一次團隊會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monthly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cb96996ae5709d1","term":"monthly","forms":["monthly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"每月地","explanation":"說明某個動作每個月重複一次，強調做事的時間間隔。","examples":[{"en":"The fee is billed monthly.","zh":"這項費用按月收取。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our landlord collects the rent monthly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monthly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"113":2}}},{"id":"ceec-6c58160fe1935610171c","word":"monument","forms":["monument"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c24b5cdcd5e56084","term":"monument","forms":["monument","monuments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紀念碑；紀念性建築","explanation":"為紀念某個人、群體或事件而建的建築、雕塑或其他大型紀念物，重點是讓人記住被紀念的物件。","examples":[{"en":"A monument to the firefighters stands in the center of the town.","zh":"鎮中心矗立著一座消防員紀念碑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city unveiled a monument to the victims of the disaster.","zh":"這座城市為災難遇難者揭幕了一座紀念碑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monument","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee0e4f309c9a47317d33","word":"mood","forms":["mood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb3a506e625ed5fd","term":"mood","forms":["mood","moods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心情；情緒狀態","explanation":"指某人在一段時間裡的內在情緒和精神狀態，例如開心、煩躁、悲傷或平靜。它像心裡的氣氛，會影響一個人怎麼看事情以及怎樣回應別人。","examples":[{"en":"She has been in a better mood since the weather improved.","zh":"天氣好轉後，她的心情一直好多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sunshine put everyone in a cheerful mood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3532f45e0764f3c","term":"mood","forms":["mood","moods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有心情；有意願","explanation":"表示當下的精神狀態適合或願意做某事：如果有那個 mood，就會覺得想做；沒有那個 mood，就提不起興趣。","examples":[{"en":"I'm not in the mood for a crowded party tonight.","zh":"我今晚沒心情去參加人多的聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you in the mood to watch a comedy?","zh":"你現在想看喜劇嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5654179bcb95d30b4571","word":"moody","forms":["moody"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-555d31f103611f66","term":"moody","forms":["moody","moodier","moodiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"喜怒無常的","explanation":"形容一個人的情緒、態度或決定容易突然改變，讓人難以預測。它強調這種變化反覆出現，而不只是偶爾心情不好。","examples":[{"en":"My brother gets moody when he is tired.","zh":"我弟弟累的時候就容易喜怒無常。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been moody all week and keeps changing her plans.","zh":"她這整個星期情緒都不穩定，一直改變計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77c408c6978e8819","term":"moody","forms":["moody","moodier","moodiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悶悶不樂的","explanation":"形容人沉默、陰沉，帶著不高興或低落的情緒，常常不願意與別人交流。這個意思比單純的“情緒變化快”更集中在當下的不快狀態上。","examples":[{"en":"Tom looked moody after the meeting.","zh":"湯姆開完會後看起來悶悶不樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became moody and withdrawn after the argument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9e78b43ea00edcac8299","word":"moon","forms":["moon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c716bd968cde30ed","term":"moon","forms":["moon","moons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行星的天然衛星","explanation":"最基本的畫面是繞著行星執行、像月亮一樣的天然衛星。日常談地球時指月球，談木星等行星時也能用複數表示它們各自的衛星。","examples":[{"en":"Jupiter has many moons, including Europa.","zh":"木星有許多衛星，其中包括木衛二。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Europa is one of Jupiter's moons.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-497c2f3d189e408d","term":"moon","forms":["moon","moons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個月或陰曆月","explanation":"月亮的盈虧大約對應一個月，所以moon在文學或古雅表達中可以表示一個月，尤其是一個陰曆月。","examples":[{"en":"They had not seen each other for many moons.","zh":"他們已經好幾個月沒見面了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They waited three moons for the expedition's return.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40685fd53d8eb3b1e921","word":"mop","forms":["mop"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82fdee1581dd972d","term":"mop","forms":["mop","mops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拖把","explanation":"一種裝在長柄上的布條或粗紗清潔工具，用來擦洗地面等表面。","examples":[{"en":"I left the mop by the kitchen door.","zh":"我把拖把放在廚房門旁了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a mop to clean up the muddy floor.","zh":"用拖把把沾滿泥的地板擦乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f35614d92204aabb","term":"mop","forms":["mop","mops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拖地；用拖把清潔","explanation":"指用拖把擦洗地面的行為，也可以指進行這項清潔的一次動作。","examples":[{"en":"A quick mop will remove the spilled coffee.","zh":"簡單拖一下就能把灑出的咖啡擦掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The floor needs a quick mop before guests arrive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31f17217c5f3898c","term":"mop","forms":["mop","mops","mopping","mopped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用拖把拖；擦洗","explanation":"用拖把，或像用拖把那樣擦洗、清潔或擦拭某個表面。它就是從“拖把”這個工具發展出的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"I mop the kitchen floor every Saturday.","zh":"我每週六都拖廚房地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mopped up the water near the sink.","zh":"她把水槽旁的水拖幹了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d11e92bbc4db371a2cf","word":"moral","forms":["moral"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-469de781958a4e92","term":"moral","forms":["moral","more moral","most moral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"道德的；關於對錯的","explanation":"指與判斷行為對錯、建立行為準則或教人如何正確行事有關。它就是那把衡量行為的“對錯尺子”，可用於道德原則、道德判斷和教誨性的作品。","examples":[{"en":"The novel raises difficult moral questions.","zh":"這部小說提出了一些艱難的道德問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children often learn moral lessons from stories.","zh":"孩子們常常從故事中學到道德教訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ec0e919812a9a2c","term":"moral","forms":["moral","morals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寓意；道理","explanation":"指故事、經歷或事件要傳達的關於做人和行為對錯的道理。它就是那把“對錯尺子”給出的結論，告訴人們應該怎樣做。","examples":[{"en":"The moral of the story is that honesty builds trust.","zh":"這個故事的寓意是，誠實能夠建立信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What is the moral of this tale?","zh":"這個故事的道理是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acaaa8c374ca6ea5652c","word":"morale","forms":["morale"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3a438ece0a0f3ea","term":"morale","forms":["morale","morales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"士氣；信心和幹勁","explanation":"指一個人或一群人在困難中仍相信目標、組織或彼此，並願意繼續努力的精神狀態；說團隊時通常譯為“士氣”，說個人時也可譯為“精神狀態”或“幹勁”。","examples":[{"en":"The team’s morale improved after the manager praised their hard work.","zh":"經理表揚團隊的辛勤工作後，大家計程車氣提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Long hours and constant delays have lowered staff morale.","zh":"長時間加班和不斷的延誤降低了員工計程車氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4b81862039491e159dc","word":"morality","forms":["morality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7ba7458d766d97f","term":"morality","forms":["morality","moralities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道德觀念；道德性","explanation":"指心裡能夠分辨善惡、對錯，並願意按照正當行為準則去做的品質或狀態。它既包括對道德規則的認識，也包括按這些規則行動的傾向。","examples":[{"en":"The story raises important questions about morality.","zh":"這個故事提出了一些重要的道德問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Power without morality can be dangerous.","zh":"沒有道德約束的權力可能很危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4b68bb608f9d299","term":"morality","forms":["morality","moralities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會道德規範","explanation":"指一個社會或群體共同接受的行為規則、習俗和觀念，也就是大家認為哪些做法合適、哪些做法不可接受的一整套標準。","examples":[{"en":"The morality of that society was very different from ours.","zh":"那個社會的道德規範與我們的非常不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel challenges conventional Victorian morality.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-187897ce0afcf20b50ba","word":"more","forms":["more"],"officialPos":"adj./pron./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00c7414f10231820","term":"more","forms":["more"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量更多","explanation":"用於可逐個計數的人或物，表示數量比另一方大，例如更多的申請、學生或辦法。","examples":[{"en":"More students joined the club this year than last year.","zh":"今年加入這個社團的學生比去年更多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need more chairs for the extra guests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07d999dbabc13ce4","term":"more","forms":["more"],"pos":"adj","zh":"分量更多","explanation":"用於不能逐個計數的物質、時間或抽象概念，表示數量、分量或比例更大。","examples":[{"en":"This recipe needs more water than the old one.","zh":"這個食譜比舊食譜需要更多水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This jar holds more jam than that one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bbc286ad0015d144","term":"more","forms":["more"],"pos":"adv","zh":"更大程度地","explanation":"放在動詞後，表示對某事的喜歡、需要或做法比另一項更強。","examples":[{"en":"I enjoy reading more than watching television.","zh":"比起看電視，我更喜歡閱讀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became more confident with every performance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70550d79945eef69","term":"more","forms":["more"],"pos":"det","zh":"更多（可數）","explanation":"放在複數可數名詞前，表示人數、物件或事項的數量比另一方多。","examples":[{"en":"We need more chairs for the guests.","zh":"我們需要更多椅子給客人用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are more oranges in the cupboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa52cb4910e01df5","term":"more","forms":["more"],"pos":"det","zh":"更多（不可數）","explanation":"放在不可數名詞前，表示需要或擁有更大的分量、數量或程度。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have more information about the course?","zh":"可以再給我一些關於這門課程的資訊嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need more information before making a decision.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24fd45a9b15bd8a3","term":"more","forms":["more"],"pos":"pron","zh":"更多的東西或人","explanation":"指比已有數量更多的同類事物或人，所指名詞由上下文決定。","examples":[{"en":"We have enough food for now, but we may need more later.","zh":"我們現在的食物夠了，但之後可能還需要更多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like more before I clear the table?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/more","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-215695de89b14c609eb0","word":"moreover","forms":["moreover"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f88900e02ea2713","term":"moreover","forms":["moreover"],"pos":"adv","zh":"此外；而且","explanation":"在已經說過一件事之後，再補充另一件相關的事，通常用來加強說明或增加一個理由。它像是在原有資訊上再疊加一層內容。","examples":[{"en":"The plan is expensive. Moreover, it would take several years to complete.","zh":"這個計劃成本很高，而且還需要幾年才能完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has excellent qualifications; moreover, she has practical experience.","zh":"她的資歷非常出色，而且還有實際工作經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moreover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"112":2}}},{"id":"ceec-c23b31a0179b550f8a18","word":"morning","forms":["morning"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f3049c1f2e54af3","term":"morning","forms":["morning","mornings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"早晨","explanation":"指一天開始的早些時候，通常從午夜到中午之間；在日常交談中，常特指人們起床、開始一天活動的時段。","examples":[{"en":"I usually read the news in the morning.","zh":"我通常早上看新聞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We will leave early tomorrow morning.","zh":"我們明天早上會早點出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morning","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-641f3495279b93bc8a54","word":"mortal","forms":["mortal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8f872df35d3eff1","term":"mortal","forms":["mortal","more mortal","most mortal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"會死亡的；非永生的","explanation":"指會因為衰老、疾病或受傷而死亡的，和“永生的”相反；也常用來強調普通人而非神或超自然存在。","examples":[{"en":"Even the strongest heroes are mortal.","zh":"即使最強大的英雄也會死。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gods looked down on ordinary mortals.","zh":"眾神俯視著普通凡人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc0c02d1dff3b82c","term":"mortal","forms":["mortal","more mortal","most mortal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"致命的","explanation":"表示足以導致死亡的，現代英語尤其常形容傷口、損傷或打擊；它把“凡人會死”這一核心概念轉成了“能把人推向死亡”。","examples":[{"en":"The soldier suffered a mortal wound in the battle.","zh":"那名士兵在戰鬥中受了致命傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The snake's bite can deliver a mortal dose of venom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e85acea50ef848db","term":"mortal","forms":["mortal","mortals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凡人","explanation":"指有生有死的普通人，常用來和神、超人或其他不朽存在對比；這個名詞義直接來自“會死亡的生命”。","examples":[{"en":"Her talent seemed almost supernatural to a mere mortal like me.","zh":"對我這樣的凡人來說，她的才能簡直像超自然力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gods rarely revealed themselves to mortals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b18339675891662b290","word":"mortality","forms":["mortality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2807676fa5ef6a5c","term":"mortality","forms":["mortality","mortalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必死性","explanation":"指人或其他有生命的東西終究會死亡這一狀態或性質，強調“沒有誰能永遠活著”這一事實，而不是某一次具體的死亡。","examples":[{"en":"The novel makes us reflect on human mortality.","zh":"這部小說讓我們思考人類終有一死這一事實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accident reminded him of his own mortality.","zh":"那場事故使他意識到自己也終究難逃一死。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25f52490a6f6be9e","term":"mortality","forms":["mortality","mortalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"死亡人數；死亡率","explanation":"指某一地區、群體或疾病造成的死亡數量，尤其指按一年或其他時間單位計算出的死亡率。它是把“人終會死亡”這一概念轉化成可統計的資料。","examples":[{"en":"The new treatment has reduced mortality among patients with the disease.","zh":"這種新療法降低了該疾病患者的死亡率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Infant mortality has fallen sharply over the past decade.","zh":"過去十年中，嬰兒死亡率大幅下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-adf27cc54e26ca64846f","word":"mortgage","forms":["mortgage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ec6d4cf700e2a35","term":"mortgage","forms":["mortgage","mortgages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房屋抵押貸款","explanation":"一種以房屋、土地等固定財產作擔保的貸款。借款人按約還款；如果不能履行還款義務，貸款方可能依法處置這項財產，貸款還清後，抵押限制通常解除。","examples":[{"en":"They took out a mortgage to buy their first home.","zh":"他們貸款買下了自己的第一套房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hope to pay off the mortgage before we retire.","zh":"我們希望在退休前還清房屋抵押貸款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortgage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d19949c3d422029d0651","word":"mosquito","forms":["mosquito"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c873906389de2a8","term":"mosquito","forms":["mosquito","mosquitoes","mosquitos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蚊子","explanation":"mosquito是一種小型飛蟲，雌蚊會叮咬人和動物並吸血，皮膚上常會留下發癢的小包；有些蚊子還可能傳播疾病。","examples":[{"en":"A mosquito kept buzzing around my ear all night.","zh":"一隻蚊子整晚在我耳邊嗡嗡飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We covered the baby with a net to keep mosquitoes away.","zh":"我們給寶寶罩上蚊帳，防止蚊子靠近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mosquito","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24ea913efda289dc1b17","word":"most","forms":["most"],"officialPos":"adv./pron./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad97d6bc516f5d4b","term":"most","forms":["most"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最……","explanation":"放在許多較長的形容詞或副詞前，most 把它們的程度推到最高，表示“最……”。","examples":[{"en":"This is the most important lesson in the book.","zh":"這是書中最重要的一課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She answered the question most carefully.","zh":"她最認真地回答了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/most","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70e3e326e612f6fb","term":"most","forms":["most"],"pos":"adv","zh":"much 的最高階：最多地","explanation":"它是 much 的最高階副詞，表示在數量、程度或使用頻率等方面達到最高，即“最多地”。","examples":[{"en":"This is the most widely used method.","zh":"這是使用最廣泛的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Of all the gifts, I value your letter most.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/most","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7573f6ca2a316cb","term":"most","forms":["most"],"pos":"det","zh":"最多的數量","explanation":"在名詞前表示某個數量或總量達到比較範圍中的最高點，即“最多的”。","examples":[{"en":"Which project needs the most time?","zh":"哪個專案需要最多時間？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Which orchard produced the most apples?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/most","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfd3e52bb21fcf70","term":"most","forms":["most"],"pos":"det","zh":"最多的（可數物件）","explanation":"與可數名詞連用時，the most 表示數量最大的那一組或那一方。","examples":[{"en":"The team with the most points wins.","zh":"得分最多的隊伍獲勝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whoever collects the most signatures receives a small prize.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/most","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e6433b147a6299d","term":"most","forms":["most"],"pos":"det","zh":"大多數；超過一半的","explanation":"不帶 the 直接放在複數名詞或不可數名詞前時，most 表示“大多數”或“大部分”，重點不是比較誰最多，而是說明整體中的主要部分。","examples":[{"en":"Most students enjoy the summer break.","zh":"大多數學生喜歡暑假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most shops close early on Sundays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/most","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9962aa7709caae3","term":"most","forms":["most"],"pos":"pron","zh":"大多數人；大多數事物","explanation":"most 單獨使用時，代替“大多數人或事物”，把整體中佔主要部分的物件作為一個群體來談。","examples":[{"en":"Most want a better future for their children.","zh":"大多數人都希望自己的孩子有更好的未來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most preferred the earlier version of the proposal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/most","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f65402e247b10d1006e4","word":"mostly","forms":["mostly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-427ed179675b71f0","term":"mostly","forms":["mostly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"主要地；大部分地；通常","explanation":"表示整體中的大多數部分或大多數時候是這樣，但不一定全部如此。它把注意力放在“最大的一部分”上，因此常可理解為“主要是”“大體上”。","examples":[{"en":"The guests were mostly young families.","zh":"客人主要是年輕家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I mostly work from home during the week.","zh":"我平時一週大多在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mostly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,113],"total":4,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1,"113":2}}},{"id":"ceec-70cc7d3c6e9a2a308b25","word":"motel","forms":["motel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf78b5e54c7e11c8","term":"motel","forms":["motel","motels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽車旅館","explanation":"一種常設在公路或主要道路附近的旅館，房間入口通常靠近停車位，駕車者可以把車停在房間附近，進出很方便。","examples":[{"en":"We stopped at a motel for the night after driving for six hours.","zh":"我們開了六個小時的車後，在一家汽車旅館住了一晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The motel room opened onto a small parking lot.","zh":"這家汽車旅館的房間門外就是一個小停車場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19c3d6e4f5c8b0da71e2","word":"moth","forms":["moth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4104af51f575ca8b","term":"moth","forms":["moth","moths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛾","explanation":"一種屬於鱗翅目、通常在夜間活動的飛行昆蟲，外形常與蝴蝶相似，但通常有羽毛狀觸角。日常語境中也常指會損壞衣物的蛾。","examples":[{"en":"A moth flew into the room when we opened the window.","zh":"我們開啟窗戶時，一隻蛾飛進了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found holes in my sweater and realized that moths had eaten it.","zh":"我發現毛衣上有洞，才意識到是蛾把它啃壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf0622ef2a661cd2f11b","word":"mother","forms":["mother"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91085d1782ade140","term":"mother","forms":["mother","mothers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"母親；女性家長","explanation":"指生育、收養或照料孩子的女性家長，是 mother 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I am visiting my mother today.","zh":"我今天要去看望我母親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her mother adopted two children.","zh":"她的母親收養了兩個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d49813b09432508e","term":"mother","forms":["mother","mothers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"來源；孕育者","explanation":"把母親“孕育生命”的形象推廣到事物上，指某物產生、發展或形成的來源。","examples":[{"en":"The forest is the mother of many rivers.","zh":"這片森林孕育了許多河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The valley was the mother of several ancient civilizations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ccf54e6fd0fe643485f","word":"motherhood","forms":["motherhood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3693a6349064c1a","term":"motherhood","forms":["motherhood","motherhoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"母親身份；母親角色","explanation":"指作為母親的狀態、經歷和角色，包括照顧孩子、面對責任以及由此產生的生活體驗；重點不是某個單獨動作，而是“成為母親後所處的整體狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"She found the first year of motherhood both exhausting and rewarding.","zh":"她覺得做母親的第一年既疲憊又充實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book explores how motherhood changes a woman's sense of identity.","zh":"這本書探討了成為母親如何改變女性的身份認同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motherhood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-305238273bb0fac2a73b","word":"motion","forms":["motion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64a06cfa26ddc8ae","term":"motion","forms":["motion","motions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運動；移動狀態","explanation":"指人或物從靜止變為移動，或處在持續移動的狀態。它強調“正在動”這一過程，而不一定強調從哪裡到哪裡。","examples":[{"en":"The train was already in motion when we arrived.","zh":"我們到達時，火車已經開動了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy set a series of changes in motion.","zh":"這項新政策推動了一連串變化的開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae48a9668193bb270207","word":"motivate","forms":["motivate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba4446795af0df99","term":"motivate","forms":["motivate","motivates","motivating","motivated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鼓勵；激發動力","explanation":"透過獎勵、目標、支援或鼓勵等方式給某人動力，使他願意去做某事。重點是讓人產生行動的意願，而不只是暫時安慰或稱讚。","examples":[{"en":"A clear goal can motivate people to work harder.","zh":"明確的目標可以激勵人們更加努力地工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach motivated the team to keep fighting until the end.","zh":"教練激勵球隊堅持戰鬥到最後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motivate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d93e12116064f5b5","term":"motivate","forms":["motivate","motivates","motivating","motivated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促使；驅使","explanation":"指某種內在或外在因素在背後推動人採取行動，例如利益、野心、恐懼或個人目標。這裡不一定含有表揚或鼓勵的意思，只強調行動的原因和推動力。","examples":[{"en":"She was motivated by the desire to help her family.","zh":"幫助家人的願望促使她採取了行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fear of failure motivated him to practice daily.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motivate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4594d493f0fdacdc82a9","word":"motivation","forms":["motivation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09cee8bbfdbf2920","term":"motivation","forms":["motivation","motivations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動意願；動力","explanation":"指一個人願意採取行動並持續做下去的內在動力，重點在“想做、願意做”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"I have plenty of motivation to finish the project on time.","zh":"我有足夠的動力按時完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a long week, she found it hard to keep her motivation.","zh":"忙了一週後，她發現很難保持動力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motivation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1226d929bdbb6bcd","term":"motivation","forms":["motivation","motivations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"做某事的理由或誘因","explanation":"指一個人做某事時所依據的理由、目的或誘因，回答“為什麼要這樣做”。它可以和內在願望重合，但更突出具體的行動依據。","examples":[{"en":"What was your motivation for changing the plan?","zh":"你改變計劃的理由是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report explains the motivation behind the decision.","zh":"這份報告解釋了作出這一決定的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motivation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e17abe0e23f5e2330ad6","word":"motive","forms":["motive"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0967207d09e6ae68","term":"motive","forms":["motive","motives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動動機；理由","explanation":"指促使某人選擇並採取某種行動的原因、願望或情緒，也就是推動人行動的那股力量。","examples":[{"en":"Her main motive for changing jobs was to spend more time with her family.","zh":"她換工作的主要動機是想多花時間陪家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police are still trying to discover his motive.","zh":"警方仍在努力查明他的動機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02983856320b180ca333","word":"motor","forms":["motor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b2b736147d00989","term":"motor","forms":["motor","motors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發動機；電動機","explanation":"指把電能、燃料等其他形式的能量轉化為機械能，從而使機器或交通工具運動的裝置。這是 motor 最基本、最常見的名詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"The washing machine's motor stopped working.","zh":"洗衣機的電動機壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat has a quiet electric motor.","zh":"這艘船裝有一臺安靜的電動機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48a39a331171798c866c","word":"motorcycle","forms":["motorcycle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6dbeac44856d6ecb","term":"motorcycle","forms":["motorcycle","motorcycles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摩托車","explanation":"一種通常有兩個輪子的機動車，騎車人坐在敞開的座位上，用車把控制方向。它的核心特點是靠發動機行駛，而不是靠腳蹬。","examples":[{"en":"He rides his motorcycle to work every day.","zh":"他每天騎摩托車上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A motorcycle was parked outside the store.","zh":"商店外停著一輛摩托車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motorcycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86e8298447b2f332f199","word":"motto","forms":["motto"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8b08adf1d13d4ea","term":"motto","forms":["motto","mottos","mottoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人口號","explanation":"指一個人用來表達自己信念、態度或處世原則的簡短話語，常常是在困難或做決定時提醒自己的口號。","examples":[{"en":"“Keep moving forward” is her motto.","zh":"“繼續向前”是她的座右銘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My motto is to treat every mistake as a lesson.","zh":"我的座右銘是把每一次錯誤都當作教訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a2fa3797d3118c9","term":"motto","forms":["motto","mottos","mottoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指導原則或篇首格言","explanation":"指放在文章、演講、章節或其他作品開頭、用來提示主題的短句，也泛指能夠概括某種指導原則的格言。","examples":[{"en":"The author placed “Know yourself” as a motto at the start of the book.","zh":"作者把“認識你自己”作為格言放在書的開頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their motto is printed above the main entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/motto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ebaceabeedd0b47c67c","word":"mound","forms":["mound"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49891b71ec94f099","term":"mound","forms":["mound","mounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人工土丘；土堤","explanation":"指人為堆起的土丘、土堤或防禦用的隆起地帶，核心畫面就是把土堆高形成一道屏障。","examples":[{"en":"The workers built a mound of earth around the garden.","zh":"工人在花園周圍築起了一圈土堤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A low mound protected the old fort from flooding.","zh":"一道低矮的土堤保護著那座古堡，使它免受洪水侵襲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69e1d5e7e610316c","term":"mound","forms":["mound","mounds","mounding","mounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堆高；堆成丘","explanation":"指把土、食物或其他東西集中堆高，形成一堆隆起的形狀；這是“mound”作為名詞時的動作版本。","examples":[{"en":"She mounded up the rice so everyone could see the vegetables underneath.","zh":"她把米飯堆得高高的，好讓大家都能看見下面的蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener mounded the soil around the new plant.","zh":"園丁把土堆在新植物周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4536f2555836b0b1bdc","word":"mount","forms":["mount"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2751409e2aaa89e0","term":"mount","forms":["mount","mounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"山丘；山","explanation":"mount可以指一座山丘或山，符合“向上隆起”的核心概念，語氣有時比普通的“山”更書面或用於專名。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow path leads to the top of the mount.","zh":"一條小路通向這座山的山頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They watched the sunset from Mount Eden.","zh":"他們在伊甸山上觀看日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7066b235ec97fcdd","term":"mount","forms":["mount","mounts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"坐騎","explanation":"mount可以指供人騎乘的動物，通常是馬；它體現了人“向上並置於其上”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The rider checked his mount before the race.","zh":"騎手在比賽前檢查了自己的坐騎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She climbed onto her mount and rode toward the village.","zh":"她騎上坐騎，朝村莊騎去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f30864b4ebb0ffe3","term":"mount","forms":["mount","mounts","mounting","mounted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"登上；攀登","explanation":"表示向上登到某個地方或物體上，正體現了“向上並置於其上”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"We mounted the narrow steps to the roof.","zh":"我們沿著狹窄的臺階登上了屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mounted the platform and began to speak.","zh":"她登上講臺，開始講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9dbbf13707411f9c","term":"mount","forms":["mount","mounts","mounting","mounted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安裝到支撐物上","explanation":"表示把物體固定或連線到支架、底板、框架等支撐物上，使它被置於其上並能發揮作用。","examples":[{"en":"They mounted the camera on the wall above the door.","zh":"他們把攝像機安裝在門上方的牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician mounted the screen to a metal frame.","zh":"技術人員把螢幕安裝到金屬框架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mount","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b80d38f7686a8b5f8e6","word":"mountain","forms":["mountain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea88d6c1fd07a4a7","term":"mountain","forms":["mountain","mountains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"山；高山","explanation":"mountain 指從地面明顯隆起、規模很大的高地，通常有較突出的山體和山頂。這是這個詞最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Everest is the highest mountain in the world.","zh":"珠穆朗瑪峰是世界上最高的山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could see the mountains from the train.","zh":"我們從火車上可以看到群山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e7a61f100bf27a5","term":"mountain","forms":["mountain","mountains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"艱難的挑戰","explanation":"把困難想成擋在面前、必須翻越的一座山，mountain 就可以指非常艱難的任務、局面或障礙。","examples":[{"en":"After the injury, finishing the race felt like climbing a mountain.","zh":"受傷後完成比賽感覺像是在翻越一座大山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team faces a mountain of debt.","zh":"這支隊伍面臨著鉅額債務的重壓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11d99a7ea7dea3e19b85","word":"mountainous","forms":["mountainous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8c7433135c57786","term":"mountainous","forms":["mountainous","more mountainous","most mountainous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多山的；山地崎嶇的","explanation":"指一個地區有許多山，或者地面像山地一樣高低起伏、岩石眾多，行走或修路往往不容易。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers spent three days crossing the mountainous northern region.","zh":"徒步旅行者花了三天穿越北部的山區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mountainous terrain made the journey much slower.","zh":"崎嶇的山地讓這段旅程慢了許多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountainous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74080dcd7d40fd6d","term":"mountainous","forms":["mountainous","more mountainous","most mountainous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高大如山的；龐大的","explanation":"形容人、物體或體量大得像山一樣，給人高聳、巨大或壓倒性的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"A mountainous defender stood between the striker and the goal.","zh":"一名高大魁梧的防守隊員擋在前鋒和球門之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mountainous waves threatened to overturn the fishing boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountainous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99507470e0a59d41e082","word":"mourn","forms":["mourn"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dea9d0cc3a45b15f","term":"mourn","forms":["mourn","mourns","mourning","mourned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"哀悼；為失去而悲痛","explanation":"指因某人的死亡或某種重大失去而持續悲痛、哀悼。它把“低頭守著失去的東西”的核心畫面變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"The town mourned the loss of its beloved teacher.","zh":"這個鎮上的人哀悼那位深受愛戴的老師的離世。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mourned her brother for many years.","zh":"她為哥哥的去世悲痛了很多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mourn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c1048fa3dc0f6970b4a","word":"mournful","forms":["mournful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"mournful","forms":["mournful"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"悲傷的；哀傷的","examples":[{"en":"A mournful tune drifted from the empty hall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The dog gave a mournful howl when its owner left.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-47c5c28cae2574cdf5a1","word":"mouse","forms":["mouse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41b4a7f48088b498","term":"mouse","forms":["mouse","mice","mouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"老鼠","explanation":"指體形小、尾巴較長的齧齒動物，最常見的基本義就是這種家中或野外的小鼠。","examples":[{"en":"We found a mouse hiding behind the kitchen cabinet.","zh":"我們發現一隻老鼠躲在廚房櫃子後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat chased two mice across the floor.","zh":"貓追著兩隻老鼠跑過地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d371cc314488f6a","term":"mouse","forms":["mouse","mice","mouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑鼠","explanation":"指連線電腦、在平面上移動以控制螢幕指標的輸入裝置；名稱來自它像一隻帶尾巴的小老鼠。","examples":[{"en":"My wireless mouse needs new batteries.","zh":"我的無線滑鼠需要換新電池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Move the mouse to the right and click the icon.","zh":"把滑鼠向右移動，然後點選圖示。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cf35cf87435b1ba3c6d","word":"mouth","forms":["mouth"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10ca34a8e4e24f0a","term":"mouth","forms":["mouth","mouths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘴；口","explanation":"動物用來吃東西、發出聲音和呼吸的身體開口，就是mouth。這個詞也常泛指嘴部，而不只指嘴唇。","examples":[{"en":"Open your mouth so I can check your teeth.","zh":"張開嘴，讓我檢查一下你的牙齒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby put the toy in her mouth.","zh":"那個嬰兒把玩具放進了嘴裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ffd1d3f80c878f7","term":"mouth","forms":["mouth","mouths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"河口","explanation":"河流流入海洋、湖泊或另一條更大的河流的地方叫mouth，因為它是河流向外“張開”的出口。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the boats near the mouth of the river.","zh":"我們在河口附近觀看船隻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many birds gather at the river mouth in winter.","zh":"冬天有許多鳥聚集在河口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f32a6ff9bd2b7ff2","term":"mouth","forms":["mouth","mouths","mouthing","mouthed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說出；講述","explanation":"作動詞時，mouth就是用嘴把意見、詞語或聲音說出來，重點仍然是“從開口發出話語”。","examples":[{"en":"He mouthed his objections during the meeting.","zh":"他在會議上說出了自己的反對意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mouthed a quick apology and left.","zh":"她匆匆說了聲抱歉就離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56efe88bdf6974bc56fb","word":"move(ment)","forms":["move","movement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b0865b85b11a51c","term":"move","forms":["move","moves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"移動；動作","explanation":"指位置、方向或姿態發生的一次移動。它可以很小，例如輕輕轉動方向，也可以是明顯的身體動作。","examples":[{"en":"One wrong move and the ladder could fall.","zh":"一動錯了，梯子就可能倒下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One sudden move could frighten the horse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fce7347182badd78","term":"move","forms":["move","moves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動；步驟","explanation":"指為達到目標而採取的一步行動，常常是計劃中的策略或進展。","examples":[{"en":"Offering her a promotion was a smart move.","zh":"給她升職是一個明智的舉措。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her first move was to call a lawyer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d79cfb9336c68cc4","term":"move","forms":["move","moves","moving","moved","movest","movedst","moveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"移動；動身","explanation":"指人、動物或物體從一個位置、姿勢或地點變到另一個位置。","examples":[{"en":"The train began to move slowly out of the station.","zh":"火車開始緩緩駛出車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't move while I take the photo.","zh":"我拍照時請不要動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6811d17bc0df5de2","term":"move","forms":["move","moves","moving","moved","movest","movedst","moveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"採取行動","explanation":"指開始做某事或在一件事情上採取實際行動，使事情向前推進。","examples":[{"en":"We need to move quickly before the offer expires.","zh":"我們得趕快行動，不然這個報價就失效了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council must move quickly to prevent further damage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb8bec2171a914d7","term":"move","forms":["move","moves","moving","moved","movest","movedst","moveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搬家；遷居","explanation":"指離開原來的住處，到另一個地方生活。","examples":[{"en":"They moved to the coast after retirement.","zh":"他們退休後搬到了海邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m moving out at the end of the month.","zh":"我月底要搬出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb6dc1ecd08402ff","term":"move","forms":["move","moves","moving","moved","movest","movedst","moveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使移動；搬動","explanation":"指讓某人或某物改變位置、姿勢或方向，也可以指推動、搬運或帶到別處。","examples":[{"en":"Could you move the table nearer the window?","zh":"你能把桌子移到窗戶旁邊嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strong wind moved the branches.","zh":"大風吹動了樹枝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bd48f1ef960902b","term":"move","forms":["move","moves","moving","moved","movest","movedst","moveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使振奮；促使行動","explanation":"指透過理由、勸說或呼籲使某人產生行動的動力，像把人的意志向前推動。","examples":[{"en":"The appeal moved many people to donate.","zh":"這份呼籲促使許多人捐款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speech moved hundreds of volunteers to join.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6df0e2585843f8b4","term":"move","forms":["move","moves","moving","moved","movest","movedst","moveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打動；使感動","explanation":"指某件事改變了人的情緒，使人感到感動、憐憫或深受觸動。","examples":[{"en":"Her story moved everyone in the room.","zh":"她的故事打動了房間裡的每一個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was deeply moved by his kindness.","zh":"他的善意讓我深受感動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/move","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6891c02dc03cd499","term":"movement","forms":["movement","movements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"移動；運動","explanation":"指物體或身體從一個位置向另一個位置移動，也可以指被觀察到的一次動作或動靜。這是 movement 最基礎的含義，其他許多義項都從“動起來”引申而來。","examples":[{"en":"I noticed a movement behind the curtain.","zh":"我注意到窗簾後面有動靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden movement made the baby cry.","zh":"突然的動作把嬰兒嚇哭了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/movement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3699014a405d11c6","term":"movement","forms":["movement","movements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會運動；潮流","explanation":"指一群人因共同理念而採取行動、爭取某種社會目標，也可指某個領域中持續發展的思想或潮流。這是“人們一起動起來”從身體動作擴充套件到集體行動。","examples":[{"en":"The environmental movement has changed public attitudes.","zh":"環保運動改變了公眾的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined a movement for equal pay.","zh":"她加入了爭取同工同酬的運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/movement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5353345790461b9f23f","word":"movie/film","forms":["movie","film"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60bcb5ded57cc3f0","term":"movie","forms":["movie","movies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電影","explanation":"指在螢幕上連續播放、看起來像在運動的影象作品，也就是通常所說的電影。這是movie最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a funny movie after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們看了一部有趣的電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you seen the new movie about space travel?","zh":"你看過那部關於太空旅行的新電影嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/movie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75731f74ad9715f7","term":"film","forms":["film","films"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄膜；薄層","explanation":"指覆蓋在某種物質或表面上的很薄一層，像透明包裝膜、油膜或結在表面的薄皮。","examples":[{"en":"A thin film of oil covered the surface of the water.","zh":"水面上覆蓋著一層薄薄的油膜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glass had a film of dust on it.","zh":"玻璃上蒙了一層灰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/film","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a546a0a8d7e1d83","term":"film","forms":["film","films"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電影藝術；電影業","explanation":"指透過連續影像製造運動效果的藝術形式，泛指電影這種媒介或行業，而不是某一部具體作品。","examples":[{"en":"She is studying film at university.","zh":"她在大學學習電影專業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Film has changed dramatically in the digital age.","zh":"在數字時代，電影發生了巨大的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/film","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c4db1a5fb1894a62836","word":"mow","forms":["mow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d984fbdfebe71ce","term":"mow","forms":["mow","mows","mowing","mowed","mown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"割草；收割","explanation":"mow 指用割草機、鐮刀等把草或莊稼從地面割下，畫面就是把一片植物整齊地削平。","examples":[{"en":"I mow the lawn every Saturday morning.","zh":"我每週六早上都割草坪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer mowed the wheat before the rain came.","zh":"農夫在下雨前收割了小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-55d38f7ba3ca48709f2f","word":"Mr./Mister","forms":["Mr.","Mister"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c1d37eda93a5053","term":"Mr.","forms":["Mr.","Messrs."],"pos":"noun","zh":"先生","explanation":"放在男性姓名前時，Mr. 是對男性的禮貌稱呼，相當於“先生”，用來表示尊重或正式稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"Mr. Brown will speak at the meeting.","zh":"布朗先生將在會議上發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good morning, Mr. Lee.","zh":"早上好，李先生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mr.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93e882e1eef25cef","term":"Mister","forms":["Mister","misters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先生；對男子的稱呼","explanation":"這是 Mister 的另一種拼寫，尤其常在沒有說出男子姓名、直接稱呼他時使用，相當於叫對方“先生”。","examples":[{"en":"You may sit here, mister.","zh":"先生，您可以坐這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Excuse me, Mister, you dropped your wallet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mister","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10b7c9307967d15a","term":"Mister","forms":["Mister","Misters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先生；男子尊稱","explanation":"放在成年男子姓名前的正式尊稱，相當於“先生”，是 mister 最核心的正式用法。","examples":[{"en":"This is Mister Smith, our new manager.","zh":"這位是史密斯先生，我們的新經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children politely addressed him as Mister Lewis.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mister","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8dd1f8b55780a03c","term":"Mister","forms":["Mister","Misters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先生；喂，先生","explanation":"單獨使用時，mister 可以稱呼姓名未知的男子；它可以禮貌地引起注意，也可能因語氣而顯得生硬或帶敵意。","examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, mister, did you drop this glove?","zh":"先生，不好意思，這是您掉的手套嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mister, you dropped your wallet!","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mister","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26b341ee55d596e90c1f","word":"Mrs.","forms":["Mrs."],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6254bcaa18c0104b","term":"Mrs.","forms":["Mrs.","Mmes.","Mesdames","Mrses."],"pos":"noun","zh":"已婚女性稱謂","explanation":"Mrs. 是放在女性姓名前的禮貌稱謂，傳統上表示這位女性已婚，中文常譯為“夫人”或“太太”。它是 Mrs 的標準寫法，通常不能脫離姓名單獨使用。","examples":[{"en":"Mrs. Brown will meet us at the school gate.","zh":"布朗夫人會在學校門口和我們見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please give this letter to Mrs. Wilson.","zh":"請把這封信交給威爾遜夫人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mrs.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7cfb46258a6f545f77cc","word":"Ms.","forms":["Ms."],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d67f0aa7a518b7ef","term":"Ms.","forms":["Ms.","Mss.","Mses.","MSS.","mss."],"pos":"noun","zh":"女士；女性稱謂","explanation":"放在女性的姓氏或全名前，是一種不說明婚姻狀況的禮貌稱謂。它可以用於已婚或未婚女性，因此比明確表示“小姐”或“夫人”的稱謂更中性。","examples":[{"en":"Ms. Chen will lead the meeting this afternoon.","zh":"陳女士今天下午將主持會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dear Ms. Rodriguez, thank you for your application.","zh":"羅德里格斯女士，感謝您的申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ms.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-543b1c4bd4f6b184ca2a","word":"much","forms":["much"],"officialPos":"adj./pron./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-903e73d522b8af65","term":"much","forms":["much","more","most"],"pos":"adv","zh":"很大程度地","explanation":"much 放在動詞附近，表示某個動作或感覺達到很大程度，相當於“很、非常”或“在很大程度上”。","examples":[{"en":"I don't much enjoy crowded restaurants.","zh":"我不太喜歡擁擠的餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That decision matters much more than it first seemed.","zh":"那個決定的重要性比一開始看起來大得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/much","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f47ed306b1b49332","term":"much","forms":["much","more","most"],"pos":"adv","zh":"同樣多；同樣程度","explanation":"在比較結構中，much 用來量出兩個動作、感受或性質的程度，表示“這麼多、那麼多”或“同樣程度”。","examples":[{"en":"I don't enjoy winter as much as summer.","zh":"我喜歡冬天不如喜歡夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can take as much as you need.","zh":"你需要多少就可以拿多少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/much","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ecef04a3ff6c441","term":"much","forms":["much","more","most"],"pos":"det","zh":"大量的","explanation":"much 放在不可數名詞前，表示數量很大，例如水、時間、錢或工作等不能直接一個個數的事物。","examples":[{"en":"We don't have much time before the train leaves.","zh":"火車開之前我們沒有多少時間了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"How much information do you need?","zh":"你需要多少資訊？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/much","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b794c280cce331d9","term":"much","forms":["much"],"pos":"pron","zh":"大量；很大程度","explanation":"much 單獨使用時，指前文已經提到的大量不可數事物，或指某件事達到的很大程度，核心仍是“量很大”。","examples":[{"en":"Much of what she said was true.","zh":"她說的大部分內容都是真的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Much has changed since we moved away.","zh":"自從我們搬走以後，變化很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/much","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af07ff91ab7ce2a7d1f9","word":"mud","forms":["mud"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb4a151bfaa50c45","term":"mud","forms":["mud","muds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"泥；泥漿","explanation":"指水和土或細小沉積物混合形成的溼、黏物質，是這個詞最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children came home with mud on their shoes.","zh":"孩子們回家時鞋上都沾滿了泥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rain turned the path into mud.","zh":"大雨把小路變成了一片泥濘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03b4cc3d83b564b99411","word":"muddy","forms":["muddy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc838864fad6c2bc","term":"muddy","forms":["muddy","muddier","muddiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沾滿泥的；泥濘的","explanation":"指表面沾著泥、被泥水濺到，或本身充滿泥的東西，尤其常形容道路、田地、鞋和衣服。","examples":[{"en":"The children came home with muddy shoes.","zh":"孩子們穿著沾滿泥的鞋回家了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The path becomes muddy after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，這條小路會變得泥濘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a547b4861469ef8","term":"muddy","forms":["muddy","muddier","muddiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"渾濁的","explanation":"形容水或其他液體混有泥土、沉澱物，因而不再清澈。","examples":[{"en":"The river was muddy after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，河水變渾濁了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not drink that muddy water.","zh":"別喝那渾濁的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a19ee2577879b76a5b98","word":"mug","forms":["mug"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f1c5bf8c4767e8f","term":"mug","forms":["mug","mugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬克杯；大杯","explanation":"指通常帶柄、用來喝飲料的大杯，尤其是日常使用的陶瓷杯。","examples":[{"en":"I made myself a mug of hot chocolate.","zh":"我給自己衝了一大杯熱巧克力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her favorite mug has a picture of a cat on it.","zh":"她最喜歡的馬克杯上印著一隻貓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbffb90cd0afa3eb","term":"mug","forms":["mug","mugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臉","explanation":"非正式地指人的臉，常常暗含嫌棄、嘲笑或不客氣的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"Get your ugly mug out of my doorway.","zh":"把你那張醜臉從我門口挪開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He grinned until his whole ugly mug creased.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7fadf9f3c25ac26cec0","word":"mule","forms":["mule"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec551198b7c0f943","term":"mule","forms":["mule","mules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"騾子","explanation":"指公驢和母馬交配生出的騾子，通常不能繁殖。它兼有驢和馬的一些特點，常被用於馱運或騎乘。","examples":[{"en":"They rode a mule up the narrow mountain trail.","zh":"他們騎著一頭騾子走上狹窄的山路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mule carried our supplies through the desert.","zh":"那頭騾子馱著我們的補給穿過沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8570166de70cb82","term":"mule","forms":["mule","mules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固執的人","explanation":"把不肯改變主意、怎麼勸也不聽的人比作騾子；語氣通常是不客氣的，也可以帶半開玩笑意味。","examples":[{"en":"He is such a mule that he refuses to ask for directions.","zh":"他固執得很，連問路都不肯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be such a mule; listen to her advice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f8a7e66329a6d6c92ac","word":"multiple","forms":["multiple"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38568982eebfe62e","term":"multiple","forms":["multiple"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多個的；多次的","explanation":"指一個事物中有不止一個部分、例項或功能，或者同一類事情發生了不止一次。重點是“數量超過一個”，不一定表示數量特別多。","examples":[{"en":"The report lists multiple causes of the accident.","zh":"報告列出了這起事故的多個原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She holds multiple citizenships.","zh":"她擁有多重國籍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/multiple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-108fd5c0a552e3ae","term":"multiple","forms":["multiple"],"pos":"det","zh":"多個","explanation":"直接限定名詞，表示同類事物有兩個或更多。它只說明數量超過一個，不說明具體數量。","examples":[{"en":"The device has multiple safety features.","zh":"這臺裝置有多項安全功能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Multiple witnesses confirmed the driver's account.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/multiple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-0d31bc618d289b7eda5d","word":"multiply","forms":["multiply"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ea2fccd1b69fa9b","term":"multiply","forms":["multiply","multiplies","multiplying","multiplied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使增加；使變多","explanation":"表示讓數量、程度、影響或問題變得更多、更大。它延續了“把一份折成許多份”的核心畫面，但不一定真的增加到原來的整數倍。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy could multiply the number of available jobs.","zh":"這項新政策可能會增加可提供的工作崗位數量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small mistake can multiply the difficulty of the task.","zh":"一個小錯誤可能會使任務的難度大大增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/multiply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed5b62be5ae807f8","term":"multiply","forms":["multiply","multiplies","multiplying","multiplied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把數相乘","explanation":"表示對數字進行乘法運算，也就是把一個數按另一個數的數量重複計算。","examples":[{"en":"Multiply 8 by 4, and you get 32.","zh":"8乘以4，結果是32。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She multiplied the length by the width to find the area.","zh":"她用長度乘以寬度來求面積。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/multiply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40d54aacd33273ca","term":"multiply","forms":["multiply","multiplies","multiplying","multiplied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"數量增長；變多","explanation":"表示數量自己逐漸增加，像一份東西不斷產生更多份，而不是某人直接把它增加。","examples":[{"en":"The rumors multiplied after the announcement.","zh":"公告發布後，謠言越來越多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rabbits multiplied rapidly after predators disappeared.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/multiply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2792e2efcb433e305f19","word":"mumble","forms":["mumble"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7724f91a88fdecd4","term":"mumble","forms":["mumble","mumbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"含混的低聲話音","explanation":"指聽起來低沉、含混、難以辨認的說話聲，重點在於聽者聽不清內容。","examples":[{"en":"All I could hear was a mumble from the next room.","zh":"我只能聽到隔壁房間傳來一陣含混的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He answered with a quiet mumble and looked away.","zh":"他含含糊糊地低聲回答了一句，然後移開了視線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29b86d1489bd95b2","term":"mumble","forms":["mumble","mumbles","mumbling","mumbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"含混地說；咕噥","explanation":"指說話時聲音低、吐字不清，使別人難以聽懂；可以是因為緊張、疲倦、不自信，也可以只是說話習慣。","examples":[{"en":"Please try not to mumble so I can hear you better.","zh":"請儘量不要含含糊糊地說，這樣我才能聽清你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mumbled an apology and left the room.","zh":"她含混地道了聲歉，然後離開了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-908e2636911e8764e34b","word":"municipal","forms":["municipal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-812e68d49b30b3d5","term":"municipal","forms":["municipal","more municipal","most municipal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"市政的；地方政府的","explanation":"指屬於城市或地方政府、由地方政府管理或提供的事物。可以把它理解為“市政廳範圍內的”：例如地方消防、道路和公共服務都可能是 municipal 的。","examples":[{"en":"The city is investing more money in municipal services.","zh":"這座城市正在增加對市政服務的投入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Municipal firefighters helped control the forest fire.","zh":"地方消防員幫助控制了這場森林火災。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/municipal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc3086f6d1e06809f75e","word":"murder","forms":["murder"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8989d63d34c78732","term":"murder","forms":["murder","murders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"謀殺罪","explanation":"指非法且通常帶有預謀地殺死他人這一罪行，強調法律上或道德上的嚴重性。","examples":[{"en":"The suspect was charged with murder.","zh":"嫌疑人被控謀殺罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police are investigating a murder.","zh":"警方正在調查一起謀殺案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/murder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a47685dd6f31a868","term":"murder","forms":["murder","murders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次謀殺","explanation":"指具體發生的一次非法殺人行為，因此可以把它看成一個案件或事件來計數。","examples":[{"en":"Three murders were reported in the city last month.","zh":"上個月這座城市報告了三起謀殺案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police are investigating a murder near the station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/murder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b6423c0e47930b5","term":"murder","forms":["murder","murders","murdering","murdered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"謀殺；蓄意殺害","explanation":"指非法且通常有預謀地殺死某人，是名詞 murder 所表示的行為。","examples":[{"en":"The victim was murdered in her own home.","zh":"受害者在自己的家中被謀殺了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was convicted of murdering his business partner.","zh":"他因謀殺自己的生意夥伴而被判有罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/murder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c1d8af3b671c780ba70","word":"murderer","forms":["murderer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89abffabf8386567","term":"murderer","forms":["murderer","murderers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殺人犯；謀殺者","explanation":"指實施謀殺的人，也就是故意非法殺害他人的犯罪者。這個詞把“謀殺”與“做出謀殺行為的人”連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The police arrested the murderer the next morning.","zh":"警方第二天早上逮捕了那名殺人犯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The murderer was sentenced to life in prison.","zh":"那名殺人犯被判處終身監禁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/murderer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6200f53485b683973d0c","word":"murmur","forms":["murmur"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fa866c628deacda","term":"murmur","forms":["murmur","murmurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低沉的聲音","explanation":"指持續而輕柔、聽不清具體內容的低沉聲音，例如水流、風聲或遠處傳來的聲響；重點是聲音本身，而不是說話的人。","examples":[{"en":"We fell asleep to the gentle murmur of the stream.","zh":"我們伴著溪水輕柔的潺潺聲入睡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A murmur of conversation filled the waiting room.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/murmur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a83c147d1c7733ea","term":"murmur","forms":["murmur","murmurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低聲議論","explanation":"指人們壓低聲音說話時形成的含混聲響，通常聽不清每個字，但能感覺到有人在議論。","examples":[{"en":"A murmur went through the crowd when the lights went out.","zh":"燈熄滅時，人群中傳來一陣低聲議論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People murmured nervously at the back of the hall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/murmur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c6b0f3125cd885a","term":"murmur","forms":["murmur","murmurs","murmuring","murmured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"低聲說話","explanation":"指說話聲音很低、吐字不清，聽者往往難以聽明白內容；它描寫的是說話方式，不一定表示不滿。","examples":[{"en":"He murmured to me that he was feeling tired.","zh":"他低聲對我說，他覺得累了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She murmured an apology and left the room.","zh":"她低聲道了歉，然後離開了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/murmur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db875b25b06f03288326","word":"muscle","forms":["muscle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95c6294b988e164f","term":"muscle","forms":["muscle","muscles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肌肉組織","explanation":"指動物體內能夠收縮併產生運動的肌肉組織，是 muscle 最基礎的概念；這裡通常把它看作一種物質或組織，而不是一塊具體的肌肉。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise helps maintain healthy muscle tissue.","zh":"規律鍛鍊有助於保持健康的肌肉組織。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise helps preserve muscle as we age.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muscle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37f9f317e16e1068","term":"muscle","forms":["muscle","muscles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一塊肌肉；肌肉群","explanation":"指由肌肉組織組成的身體器官，也就是可以指認、檢查或感到收縮的某一塊肌肉或一組肌肉。","examples":[{"en":"The physiotherapist gently stretched the muscles in my shoulder.","zh":"理療師輕輕拉伸了我肩膀的肌肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pulled a muscle in her calf.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muscle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94b0a1a34834efaf5e32","word":"muscular","forms":["muscular"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69fc605ea1ae5203","term":"muscular","forms":["muscular","more muscular","most muscular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與肌肉有關的","explanation":"表示某事物屬於肌肉、涉及肌肉，重點是“和肌肉有關係”，不一定表示肌肉很大或很強。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise can improve muscular strength and coordination.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以提高肌肉力量和協調性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury caused severe muscular pain in his shoulder.","zh":"這次受傷使他的肩部出現了嚴重的肌肉疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muscular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fdc07c023e7a5874","term":"muscular","forms":["muscular","more muscular","most muscular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"肌肉發達的","explanation":"形容人或身體部位的肌肉明顯、發展良好，突出外形上的肌肉量和線條。","examples":[{"en":"She has muscular shoulders from years of swimming.","zh":"她多年游泳，肩部肌肉很發達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The muscular athlete easily lifted the heavy bar.","zh":"那名肌肉發達的運動員輕鬆舉起了沉重的槓鈴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muscular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4016c3db3bc3c731a414","word":"muse","forms":["muse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-842cad848b42495c","term":"muse","forms":["muse","muses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"靈感來源","explanation":"muse 可以指激發藝術家、作家或其他創作者創作慾望的人或事物，就像一個具體的“靈感源頭”。它不一定是戀人，也可以是朋友、風景、經歷或其他創作物件。","examples":[{"en":"The quiet lake became the painter's muse.","zh":"那片寧靜的湖成了這位畫家的靈感源泉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was his muse while he wrote the novel.","zh":"他寫那部小說時，她是他的靈感來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4919063719e8c3888b72","word":"museum","forms":["museum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6cbb1630a13ae789","term":"museum","forms":["museum","museums","musea"],"pos":"noun","zh":"博物館","explanation":"專門收藏、儲存和展示有價值物品或資料，並供人學習和參觀的機構或建築；展品可以來自藝術、歷史、科學或其他文化領域。","examples":[{"en":"We visited the history museum during our trip.","zh":"我們旅行期間參觀了歷史博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum closes early on public holidays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/museum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ef2c394d5b63e4175cd","word":"mushroom","forms":["mushroom"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-114d30dee6df5bc4","term":"mushroom","forms":["mushroom","mushrooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蘑菇；真菌子實體","explanation":"指通常從土壤、腐木等地方長出的真菌肉質部分，也就是人們日常所說的蘑菇；有些可食用，有些有毒。","examples":[{"en":"We found several large mushrooms under the old tree.","zh":"我們在那棵老樹下發現了幾朵大蘑菇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Never eat a wild mushroom unless an expert has identified it.","zh":"除非有專家鑑定過，否則不要吃野生蘑菇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mushroom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0533d65efd3b283d","term":"mushroom","forms":["mushroom","mushrooms","mushrooming","mushroomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迅速擴大；暴增","explanation":"指數量、規模或範圍像蘑菇突然冒出並迅速長大一樣，在短時間內大幅增加。","examples":[{"en":"The town's population mushroomed from ten thousand to one hundred thousand.","zh":"這個城鎮的人口從一萬人暴增到十萬人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small disagreement mushroomed into a serious argument.","zh":"一次小小的分歧迅速演變成了嚴重的爭吵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mushroom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80f189984e5ca70287d1","word":"music","forms":["music"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eba333f73bf9f010","term":"music","forms":["music","musics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂","explanation":"指按旋律、節奏、和聲等組織起來的聲音，通常用來表達情緒或營造氛圍；這是music最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I listen to music while I work.","zh":"我工作時聽音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This music makes me feel calm.","zh":"這音樂讓我感到平靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/music","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7943e9e00df46ac6","term":"music","forms":["music","musics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂藝術","explanation":"指把音高、節奏、聲音和演奏或歌唱組織起來的藝術形式；這裡強調“音樂”作為一種藝術。","examples":[{"en":"Music can bring people from different cultures together.","zh":"音樂可以把來自不同文化的人聯絡在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Music has always been central to her life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/music","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70de0f95a234f5685f54","word":"musical","forms":["musical"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-232afba25272821e","term":"musical","forms":["musical","more musical","most musical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"音樂的；與音樂有關的","explanation":"表示某事物屬於音樂領域，或與音樂的演奏、創作、記譜等有關。這是最直接、最基礎的“帶著音樂屬性”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The school is adding more musical activities this year.","zh":"這所學校今年要增加更多音樂活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied musical notation at college.","zh":"她在大學學習了音樂記譜法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/musical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94c4cf7b24101bcc","term":"musical","forms":["musical","more musical","most musical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悅耳的；和諧動聽的","explanation":"形容聲音或說話方式聽起來像音樂一樣順耳、流暢、和諧，重點在聽覺上的美感，而不只是它與音樂有關。","examples":[{"en":"Her musical voice made even the long speech pleasant to hear.","zh":"她悅耳的聲音讓這篇很長的演講聽起來也很舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stream made a musical sound as it ran over the stones.","zh":"溪水流過石頭時發出悅耳的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/musical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c429d1901593baa","term":"musical","forms":["musical","musicals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂劇","explanation":"指把劇情表演與演員的歌唱、舞蹈和音樂節目結合起來的舞臺演出或電影。可以把它記成“音樂走上舞臺並參與講故事”。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a musical about a young inventor last weekend.","zh":"我們上週末看了一部關於年輕發明家的音樂劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school staged a musical for the spring festival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/musical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c5af973f604c186dcbe","word":"musician","forms":["musician"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-810e05d4bedf8281","term":"musician","forms":["musician","musicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂家；音樂人","explanation":"指創作、指揮、演唱或演奏音樂的人。它既可以指以音樂為職業的人，也可以指把唱歌或演奏樂器作為興趣的人。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is a musician who plays the violin in a local orchestra.","zh":"我姐姐是一名音樂人，在當地管弦樂團拉小提琴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became a professional musician after years of playing in small clubs.","zh":"他在小俱樂部演出多年後，成為了一名職業音樂人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/musician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4137b01e139589b7a1d3","word":"must","forms":["must"],"officialPos":"aux./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c38d7bbe24605751","term":"must","forms":["must","musts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必備之物；必做之事","explanation":"這裡的 must 把“必須”這個強制概念變成了名詞：某樣東西或某件事重要到不能缺少。它可以是實際物品，也可以是建議中認為一定要做的事情。","examples":[{"en":"A warm jacket is a must for this trip.","zh":"這次旅行一定要帶一件保暖外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Saving your work regularly is a must.","zh":"定期儲存工作內容是必不可少的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/must","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad73bf611b2df375","term":"must","forms":["must","mote","motest","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"必須；一定要","explanation":"must 表示說話人認為某個要求不可違反：主語必須完成後面的動作，否則會有不良後果。它可以表達規定，也可以表達說話人很強的要求。","examples":[{"en":"You must wear a helmet when riding this bike.","zh":"騎這輛腳踏車時你必須戴頭盔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We must finish the report before Friday.","zh":"我們必須在星期五以前完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/must","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19c01fbecb2ba78f","term":"must","forms":["must","mote","motest","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"一定是；很可能是","explanation":"must 也能把線索推到一個幾乎確定的結論，表示“肯定是”或“想必是”。例如看到燈亮著、聽到屋裡有聲音，就可以推斷人在裡面。","examples":[{"en":"The lights are on, so they must be home.","zh":"燈亮著，所以他們一定在家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This must be the right address.","zh":"這一定是正確的地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/must","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fdcd4bfab1994990306b","word":"mustache","forms":["mustache"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"mustache","forms":["mustache"],"pos":"n.","zh":"上唇的鬍子；八字鬍","examples":[{"en":"He grew a mustache during the summer vacation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A drop of milk was caught in his mustache.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-352b5b6699d83cdc4efd","word":"mustard","forms":["mustard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5fcc9268ee67c315","term":"mustard","forms":["mustard","mustards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"芥末；芥末醬","explanation":"指用芥菜籽磨成的粉或調成的糊狀調味品，味道通常帶有明顯的辛辣刺激感。這是日常生活中最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Could you pass me the mustard for my sandwich?","zh":"請把芥末遞給我，我要給三明治加一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spread a little mustard on the ham sandwich.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mustard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7aa1b9790748b71e5c2","word":"mute","forms":["mute"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ec0455a10567f0b","term":"mute","forms":["mute","muter","mutest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不會說話的","explanation":"指沒有說話能力，或在特定語境中不能用語言發聲的人或動物。這是“嘴巴沒有聲音”這一核心影象的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The mute child communicated with her hands.","zh":"那個不會說話的孩子用手勢交流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story follows a mute child learning sign language.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab11815c16830eaa","term":"mute","forms":["mute","muter","mutest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無聲的；沉默的","explanation":"指沒有發出聲音，或一個人、一個場面完全不作聲。它仍然保留“聲音被關掉”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The room fell mute when the lights went out.","zh":"燈熄滅後，房間裡頓時一片寂靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave him a mute look of disappointment.","zh":"她默默地投給他一個失望的眼神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ea093f2f99adf95","term":"mute","forms":["mute","mutes","muting","muted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使安靜；讓……不出聲","explanation":"指讓人停止說話，或讓一個場面、聲音變得無聲，是“按下靜音鍵”的主動動作。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher muted the noisy class with one raised hand.","zh":"老師舉起一隻手，讓吵鬧的班級安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thick carpet muted the sound of footsteps.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71650caafdf72463","term":"mute","forms":["mute","mutes","muting","muted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使裝置靜音","explanation":"指關閉裝置、軟體、麥克風或音訊訊號的聲音。這是“沒有聲音”最常見的現代操作用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please mute your microphone while someone else is speaking.","zh":"別人發言時，請把你的麥克風靜音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I muted the video but kept watching the subtitles.","zh":"我把影片靜音了，但繼續看字幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d8752e36fab151d74f7","word":"mutual","forms":["mutual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-558890f70d99a225","term":"mutual","forms":["mutual","more mutual","most mutual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"互相的","explanation":"指一種感情、行為或影響從一方指向另一方，同時也從另一方指回這一方；兩邊彼此都有同樣的反應。","examples":[{"en":"Their partnership is built on mutual trust.","zh":"他們的合作建立在相互信任的基礎上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two candidates showed mutual respect during the debate.","zh":"兩位候選人在辯論中表現出了相互尊重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mutual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e57dd98ff0e4a72","term":"mutual","forms":["mutual","more mutual","most mutual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"雙方都認識或擁有的","explanation":"特別常用於 mutual friend，指這個朋友同時是說話雙方的朋友；它強調雙方分別與這個人有聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"We met through a mutual friend at a small dinner.","zh":"我們透過一位共同的朋友在一次小型晚餐上認識了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A mutual friend recommended her for the job.","zh":"一位我們共同認識的朋友推薦她做這份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mutual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da7cc64ae8ad7e0b926b","word":"mysterious","forms":["mysterious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bef4a564ad6ad8b0","term":"mysterious","forms":["mysterious","more mysterious","most mysterious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"來源不明的","explanation":"某件事、某個物品或某種現象出現了，但沒人知道它從哪裡來、為什麼發生，像被霧遮住了來路，因此是 mysterious。","examples":[{"en":"A mysterious package arrived at the office with no return address.","zh":"辦公室收到一個神秘包裹，上面沒有寄件人地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police are investigating a mysterious fire in the old warehouse.","zh":"警方正在調查舊倉庫裡那場來歷不明的火災。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mysterious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b6362ec37f57ed2","term":"mysterious","forms":["mysterious","more mysterious","most mysterious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難以理解的","explanation":"某人的決定、行為或某件事缺少合理解釋，讓人想不明白為什麼會這樣；這裡的“神秘”來自意義被霧遮住，而不一定有未知來源。","examples":[{"en":"It is mysterious why the lights went out just before the meeting.","zh":"會議開始前燈為什麼突然熄滅，實在讓人想不明白。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sudden change of plans remains mysterious to everyone.","zh":"她突然改變計劃的原因對所有人來說仍然難以理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mysterious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f0d9e5f2d159c8bd632","word":"mystery","forms":["mystery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05bb9b2e2119de3e","term":"mystery","forms":["mystery","mysteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"謎；未解之事","explanation":"指某件事的真相、原因或經過仍然不知道，或者目前無法解釋。它是 mystery 最基本的用法，重點是“謎團還沒有被解開”。","examples":[{"en":"Why the lights went out remains a mystery.","zh":"燈為什麼熄滅仍然是個謎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mystery of her sudden departure was never solved.","zh":"她突然離開的原因始終沒有查清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mystery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b943c1289c9c5db","term":"mystery","forms":["mystery","mysteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推理故事；懸疑作品","explanation":"指以犯罪、謀殺或其他謎團為核心的小說、電影、電視劇或戲劇，情節通常會在結尾解釋前面發生的奇怪事情。這裡 mystery 指的是一種作品型別，不是作品中的某一個具體謎團。","examples":[{"en":"I picked up a mystery novel for the train ride.","zh":"我買了一本推理小說，準備在火車上看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reads a mystery every weekend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mystery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":5,"counts":{"111":1,"113":4}}},{"id":"ceec-b50b9b3a45059ef41c4c","word":"myth","forms":["myth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-539310a27b5f28c8","term":"myth","forms":["myth","myths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神話故事","explanation":"指流傳已久、用故事解釋神靈、英雄、世界起源或自然現象的敘事，通常帶有神聖或文化傳統色彩。它不只是普通的虛構故事，而是一個群體長期傳承、賦予意義的故事。","examples":[{"en":"The myth of Icarus warns people not to ignore good advice.","zh":"伊卡洛斯的神話告誡人們不要不聽忠告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This ancient myth explains how the seasons began.","zh":"這個古老的神話解釋了四季是怎樣開始的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/myth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9b201a1493114be","term":"myth","forms":["myth","myths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錯誤的普遍觀念","explanation":"指很多人相信、但實際上不正確的說法或認識。這是從“被群體傳開的故事”發展出來的現代用法，重點不在神話背景，而在這種觀念廣泛流傳卻不真實。","examples":[{"en":"It is a myth that you must drink eight glasses of water every day.","zh":"“每天必須喝八杯水”是一種普遍的錯誤說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article challenges the myth that success comes overnight.","zh":"這篇文章質疑了“成功可以一夜之間到來”這一錯誤觀念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/myth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7811647f8e15ef22a156","word":"nag","forms":["nag"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75fb4e03e26cab33","term":"nag","forms":["nag","nags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愛嘮叨的人","explanation":"nag像一隻不斷啃咬耳朵的人，指反覆催促、抱怨、讓人厭煩的人。","examples":[{"en":"I'm not trying to be a nag, but could you wash the dishes tonight?","zh":"我不是想嘮叨，但你今晚能洗碗嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hate sounding like a nag about the washing-up.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da4c59693207f1cc","term":"nag","forms":["nag","nags","nagging","nagged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嘮叨；反覆催促或抱怨","explanation":"nag表示像不斷啃咬一樣，一遍遍提醒、催促或抱怨，直到對方感到厭煩。","examples":[{"en":"My brother keeps nagging me to clean the garage.","zh":"我哥哥一直嘮叨著要我打掃車庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She nagged him about being late again.","zh":"她不停抱怨他又遲到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ac41a0ec75bfa52ddda","word":"nail","forms":["nail"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abf361393547bed0","term":"nail","forms":["nail","nails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指甲","explanation":"指甲是手指或腳趾末端的堅硬甲片；它就是“尖硬末端”這一核心形象在人體上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"I bite my nails whenever I feel nervous.","zh":"我一緊張就咬指甲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She painted her nails bright red.","zh":"她把指甲塗成了鮮紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d722f6676dc48e27","term":"nail","forms":["nail","nails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金屬釘子","explanation":"金屬釘子是尖頭的固定件，用錘子打入木材等材料，把不同部分牢牢連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"He hammered a nail into the wall to hang the picture.","zh":"他往牆裡釘了一根釘子來掛畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful—there's a rusty nail on the floor.","zh":"小心，地板上有一根生鏽的釘子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ec5f4127c97618e3329","word":"naive","forms":["naive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43ee9003355d3773","term":"naive","forms":["naive","more naive","most naive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"天真而缺少經驗","explanation":"指一個人或他的想法沒有經過世事磨鍊，缺乏實際經驗和判斷力，因此可能把複雜的問題想得過於簡單，或輕易相信別人。","examples":[{"en":"It was naive of me to believe that everyone would keep their promises.","zh":"我以為所有人都會信守承諾，真是太天真了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His naive view of politics changed after he started working in government.","zh":"他開始在政府工作後，對政治的天真看法改變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/naive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a4e4f32ef29b9a0","term":"naive","forms":["naive","more naive","most naive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"尚未接觸過","explanation":"指某人或某種生物以前沒有接觸過某種事物，尤其用於醫學、生物學中表示尚未接觸過某種病原體、抗原或治療。這裡不表示性格天真。","examples":[{"en":"The study followed patients who were naive to this type of treatment.","zh":"這項研究跟蹤了此前未接受過這種治療的患者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experiment used animals naive to the drug.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/naive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12a667c9be6ff8f665d2","word":"naked","forms":["naked"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd0bbf0d8dcbc213","term":"naked","forms":["naked","more naked","most naked"],"pos":"adj","zh":"赤裸的；沒穿衣服的","explanation":"指身體沒有衣物遮蓋，強調完全裸露，正是“沒有任何外層保護”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The baby was naked after his bath.","zh":"嬰兒洗完澡後沒有穿衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ran into the room naked.","zh":"他赤裸著跑進了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/naked","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4d20fa63c86914c","term":"naked","forms":["naked","more naked","most naked"],"pos":"adj","zh":"赤裸裸的；直截了當的","explanation":"把事實像裸露的身體一樣直接攤開，不加修飾或掩飾，因此可表示話說得很直白。","examples":[{"en":"The naked truth is that we cannot afford the project.","zh":"赤裸裸的事實是，我們負擔不起這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave us a naked account of what happened.","zh":"她直截了當地告訴了我們發生的一切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/naked","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82a3537ff0dbce7eec35","word":"name","forms":["name"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb8497b19d5ed8c0","term":"name","forms":["name","names"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名稱；名字","explanation":"name是用來指認某個人、地方、事物或類別的名稱，就像貼在物件上的標籤。","examples":[{"en":"What’s the name of this street?","zh":"這條街叫什麼名字？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She changed her name after getting married.","zh":"她結婚後改了名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/name","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c73126dd421f94d","term":"name","forms":["name","names","naming","named"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……命名","explanation":"name作動詞時，最核心的意思是給人、地方或事物確定一個名稱，把標籤貼到物件上。","examples":[{"en":"They named the puppy Max.","zh":"他們給這隻小狗取名叫馬克斯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The park was named after a local teacher.","zh":"這座公園以一位當地教師的名字命名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/name","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-faa94f91ef29ae160937","word":"namely","forms":["namely"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c9a03eddb51c29b","term":"namely","forms":["namely"],"pos":"adv","zh":"即；具體說就是","explanation":"當先說了一個較寬泛的範圍，隨後要準確指出其中包含的具體人、物或事項時，用 namely 把答案“點出來”。它強調後面的內容就是前面所指的確切物件，而不是隨便舉的例子。","examples":[{"en":"Several people helped organize the event, namely Maria, Tom, and Lee.","zh":"有幾個人幫忙組織了這次活動，具體說就是瑪麗亞、湯姆和李。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repair requires one special tool, namely a torque wrench.","zh":"這項維修需要一種特殊工具，也就是扭力扳手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/namely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82ebadafdeec2df737e5","word":"nap","forms":["nap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c3d96d21345f5ab","term":"nap","forms":["nap","naps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小睡","explanation":"指時間較短的一次睡眠，通常發生在白天或兩段活動之間，就像暫時把自己放下休息一會兒。","examples":[{"en":"I usually take a short nap after lunch.","zh":"我通常午飯後小睡一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby is having a nap upstairs.","zh":"寶寶正在樓上睡午覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f04574a9bcb03f9c","term":"nap","forms":["nap","naps","napping","napped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"小睡","explanation":"指短時間睡一會兒，通常是白天休息；它就是名詞“小睡”所對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"I napped for twenty minutes on the train.","zh":"我在火車上小睡了二十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She likes to nap on quiet weekends.","zh":"她喜歡在安靜的週末小睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9db44611cf4a08a87bfa","word":"napkin","forms":["napkin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b7f6b91087f8e9f","term":"napkin","forms":["napkin","napkins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餐巾；餐巾紙","explanation":"指吃飯時放在腿上或放在桌邊、用來擦嘴和手的一小塊布或紙，是 napkin 最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please put a napkin on your lap before you start eating.","zh":"請在開始吃飯前把餐巾放在腿上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used a napkin to wipe the sauce from her mouth.","zh":"她用餐巾擦掉嘴邊的醬汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/napkin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8236c276682fc55f","term":"napkin","forms":["napkin","napkins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尿布（英國、南非）","explanation":"在英國和南非英語中，napkin 還可以指給嬰兒使用的尿布；這也是“用一小塊東西墊住、保護身體”這一核心概念的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The baby needs a clean napkin before the trip.","zh":"寶寶出發前需要換一塊乾淨的尿布。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse changed the baby's wet napkin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/napkin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3886a8502fbbc810ce92","word":"narrate","forms":["narrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58912581c65b602d","term":"narrate","forms":["narrate","narrates","narrating","narrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"講述故事或事件","explanation":"把故事或一連串事件按時間或情節順序講出來，可以用口頭方式，也可以寫下來；重點在於有條理地呈現過程。","examples":[{"en":"She narrated the story of her journey to the children.","zh":"她向孩子們講述了自己的旅行故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary is narrated by a local journalist.","zh":"這部紀錄片由一名當地記者擔任旁白。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b7c442b5a2cc99f","term":"narrate","forms":["narrate","narrates","narrating","narrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交代事情經過","explanation":"不一定是在講虛構故事，也可以把會議、事故或某項工作的經過按順序說明清楚，讓別人瞭解發生了什麼。","examples":[{"en":"The report narrates what happened during the meeting.","zh":"這份報告敘述了會議期間發生的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She narrated the events leading to the accident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3c903c9c4a4065db673","word":"narrative","forms":["narrative"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ea92ace1552eae3","term":"narrative","forms":["narrative","more narrative","most narrative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"敘述的；敘事的","explanation":"指與敘述行為、敘事結構或故事講法有關，重點在“怎樣把事情講出來”，而不是故事中的某一個事實。","examples":[{"en":"The director gives the film a strong narrative focus.","zh":"導演賦予這部電影鮮明的敘事重點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel shifts between two narrative voices.","zh":"這部小說在兩種敘事聲音之間切換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad675ac55215cdee","term":"narrative","forms":["narrative","narratives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敘述；敘事","explanation":"指按照一定順序系統講述一個事件或一連串事件的過程，也可以指這種講述形成的整體文字。它關注的是如何把經歷組織成一個可理解的故事。","examples":[{"en":"The book provides a detailed narrative of her journey.","zh":"這本書詳細講述了她的旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story is told through a first-person narrative.","zh":"這個故事採用第一人稱敘述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-228188ae8245dcfa","term":"narrative","forms":["narrative","narratives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敘事框架；話語","explanation":"指用某種角度組織和解釋事件的故事框架，往往會突出某些事實、淡化另一些事實，從而支援特定立場。這裡的 narrative 不只是“發生了什麼”，還包括“希望別人怎樣理解這些事”。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign tried to change the public narrative about the company.","zh":"這場宣傳活動試圖改變公眾對這家公司的敘事框架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several witnesses challenged the official narrative.","zh":"幾名目擊者對官方敘事提出了質疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-663ee49c71db7d169dc5","word":"narrator","forms":["narrator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0524f4a5006a7f6","term":"narrator","forms":["narrator","narrators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事講述者","explanation":"指實際把故事講出來的人，可以是在現場講故事的人，也可以是書、電影或有聲作品中的講述者。這個意義抓住了“把故事帶給聽眾”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The narrator tells the story in a calm and gentle voice.","zh":"講述者用平靜而溫和的聲音講述這個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The narrator reveals the secret in the final chapter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5bb05dc1d57f10d","term":"narrator","forms":["narrator","narrators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敘事聲音或視角","explanation":"在文學或敘事分析中，它指負責組織和講述故事的“聲音”或視角；這個聲音可以是故事中的人物，也可以是故事外的敘述者。重點不是現實中誰寫了作品，而是讀者透過誰的眼光聽到這個故事。","examples":[{"en":"The narrator describes the same event very differently from the other characters.","zh":"敘述者對同一事件的描述與其他人物很不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel's unreliable narrator conceals important details.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5eda958e9ddee7721fb7","word":"narrow","forms":["narrow"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3026c3082700b58a","term":"narrow","forms":["narrow","narrower","narrowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"狹窄的","explanation":"指實際寬度小，兩個相對的邊或側面距離很近，通常相對於長度來說尤其明顯。它就是“越走越窄的路”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We walked down a narrow hallway.","zh":"我們沿著一條狹窄的走廊走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village is connected to the town by a narrow road.","zh":"這個村子由一條狹窄的道路與城鎮相連。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c773fc5aae6160ba","term":"narrow","forms":["narrow","narrows","narrowing","narrowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縮小；縮窄","explanation":"指主動把寬度、範圍或候選項變小，讓原本較寬的“路”變得更窄。","examples":[{"en":"We need to narrow the search to three possible causes.","zh":"我們需要把搜尋範圍縮小到三個可能的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new evidence narrowed the gap between the two accounts.","zh":"新的證據縮小了兩種說法之間的差距。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18eee7b2355caf52","term":"narrow","forms":["narrow","narrows","narrowing","narrowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變窄；縮小","explanation":"指道路、通道或抽象範圍自行變得更窄，不強調誰主動造成這種變化。","examples":[{"en":"The path narrows as it climbs into the hills.","zh":"小路進入山地後逐漸變窄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As the deadline approached, our options narrowed.","zh":"隨著截止日期臨近，我們的選擇越來越少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/narrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2271fcf39b42a922de2","word":"nasty","forms":["nasty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afb8698fb8270145","term":"nasty","forms":["nasty","nastier","nastiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"骯髒的；汙穢的","explanation":"指沾滿汙物、很不乾淨的東西，核心感覺是讓人想躲開或清理掉。","examples":[{"en":"The bathroom was in a nasty condition after the party.","zh":"聚會後，浴室髒得不成樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A nasty smell was coming from the kitchen sink.","zh":"廚房水槽裡飄來一股難聞的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f85698a79f5a9a5b","term":"nasty","forms":["nasty","nastier","nastiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"討厭的；兇惡的","explanation":"形容人態度惡劣、讓別人不舒服，或外表神情顯得兇狠。","examples":[{"en":"He was nasty to the waiter for no reason.","zh":"他無緣無故地對服務員很刻薄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That dog looks nasty, but it is actually gentle.","zh":"那隻狗看起來很兇，但其實很溫順。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02b38b86665c822b","term":"nasty","forms":["nasty","nastier","nastiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人反感的；討厭的","explanation":"形容事情、工作、氣味、狀況等讓人不舒服、厭惡或難以接受，是“髒”這一核心感覺向更廣泛物件的擴充套件。","examples":[{"en":"Cleaning the blocked drain was a nasty job.","zh":"清理堵塞的下水道是件令人反感的活兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A nasty smell drifted from the blocked drain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7400ec1250e1475bb7d0","word":"nation","forms":["nation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ae531ed1674cf05","term":"nation","forms":["nation","nations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"民族；民族共同體","explanation":"nation首先可以指一個歷史上形成的、因語言、文化、地域或共同身份而團結起來的人群，不一定擁有自己的主權國家。它強調“我們屬於同一個共同體”這一身份感。","examples":[{"en":"The Kurds are a nation without an independent state.","zh":"庫爾德人是一個沒有獨立國家的民族。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A nation is held together by more than shared borders.","zh":"一個民族共同體的凝聚力不只是來自共同邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f22f6069989b86e4","term":"nation","forms":["nation","nations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家；主權國家","explanation":"nation也指擁有主權、在國際關係中作為整體行動的國家。這時重點從“共同身份的人群”擴充套件到代表這個共同體的政治實體。","examples":[{"en":"Every nation has the right to protect its citizens.","zh":"每個國家都有權保護自己的公民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two nations signed a trade agreement.","zh":"兩國簽署了一項貿易協定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-400464e9e99bb03f0cd9","word":"national","forms":["national"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9ad4ef2a8210abb","term":"national","forms":["national","more national","most national"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全國的；國家層面的","explanation":"指影響全國、遍及全國，或由國家整體組織和承擔的事物，重點是“整個國家”而不是某個地區。","examples":[{"en":"The issue was discussed in the national newspapers.","zh":"全國性報紙都討論了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government announced a new national health program.","zh":"政府宣佈了一項新的全國性醫療計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/national","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a07c5ad5eeeee45","term":"national","forms":["national","more national","most national"],"pos":"adj","zh":"本國的；某國特有的","explanation":"指屬於某個特定國家、體現該國特色的事物，常用來和其他國家作對比。","examples":[{"en":"Rice is a national staple in many Asian countries.","zh":"米飯是許多亞洲國家的主食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The national flag flew above every public building.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/national","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5e1d8a3f58b44e0d60e","word":"nationalism","forms":["nationalism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd2d4ed8ce77c2fc","term":"nationalism","forms":["nationalism","nationalisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈的民族或國家認同","explanation":"指把本國、本民族或本族文化置於特別重要的位置，並強烈支援、維護它的思想或立場。它比一般的愛國情感更強調集體身份，某些語境下還可能帶有排斥他者的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Nationalism can unite people, but it can also exclude minorities.","zh":"民族主義可以團結人們，但也可能排斥少數群體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crisis led to a rise in nationalism.","zh":"這場危機導致民族主義情緒上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nationalism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dd1bd66e50d4a50","term":"nationalism","forms":["nationalism","nationalisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭取建立獨立國家的民族主義","explanation":"指一個尚未擁有自己主權國家的民族或地區，支援建立一個獨立國家的政治思想或運動。這是“高舉自己的旗幟”進一步發展為“要有自己的國家”。","examples":[{"en":"Basque nationalism has shaped politics in the region for decades.","zh":"巴斯克民族主義幾十年來一直影響著該地區的政治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nationalism fueled the colony's struggle for independence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nationalism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f540d3e12e3abb7c31d","word":"nationality","forms":["nationality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-408fc507534648ad","term":"nationality","forms":["nationality","nationalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國籍；法律身份","explanation":"這是最常見的意思，指一個人在法律上屬於哪個國家，以及這種身份如何由出生、血統、入籍或其他法律關係取得。","examples":[{"en":"Please state your nationality on the application form.","zh":"請在申請表上填寫你的國籍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She acquired Canadian nationality after living there for five years.","zh":"她在那裡生活五年後取得了加拿大國籍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nationality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7bff13c70dd1361","term":"nationality","forms":["nationality","nationalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具有共同身份的民族或群體","explanation":"這裡把“歸屬”從個人擴大到群體，指一群共享來源、文化、語言或歷史的人，有時可以構成一個民族或國家。","examples":[{"en":"The region is home to several nationalities with distinct languages and traditions.","zh":"這個地區生活著幾個擁有不同語言和傳統的民族。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The empire contained people of many nationalities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nationality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bef32d2c315a289576f2","word":"native","forms":["native"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb1675888100cf6e","term":"native","forms":["native","more native","most native"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生來屬於某地","explanation":"指一個人出生於某地，因出生而與那裡有天然聯絡；也可指與出生地有關的事物。","examples":[{"en":"She returned to her native country after many years abroad.","zh":"她在國外多年後回到了自己的出生國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is native to this coastal region.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/native","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c0e28d08956739f","term":"native","forms":["native","more native","most native"],"pos":"adj","zh":"當地生長或產生的","explanation":"指人、動物或植物出生、長成或原本存在於所在地區，而不是從別處引進的；這是“土生土長”從人擴充套件到生物和其他事物。","examples":[{"en":"This tree is native to the wet forests of Southeast Asia.","zh":"這種樹原生於東南亞的溼潤森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The park protects native plants from invasive species.","zh":"這座公園保護當地原生植物，防止它們受到入侵物種的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/native","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3a0b5648df735f5","term":"native","forms":["native","natives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"當地出生的人","explanation":"指在某地出生的人，不一定表示此人現在仍住在那裡；它把形容詞“生來屬於某地”變成了人。","examples":[{"en":"He is a native of Dublin but now lives in London.","zh":"他出生於都柏林，但現在住在倫敦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a native of the mountain village.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/native","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ee407eb07a850ac","term":"native","forms":["native","natives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"母語者","explanation":"在語言學習中，指從小自然習得某種語言的人；這裡的“出生於某地”擴充套件成“在某語言環境中土生土長”。","examples":[{"en":"Ask a native speaker to check whether the sentence sounds natural.","zh":"請母語者檢查一下這個句子聽起來是否自然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ask a native if this phrase sounds natural.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/native","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12765295db4f1e7911dd","word":"natural","forms":["natural"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dca6f2113a1b7516","term":"natural","forms":["natural","more natural","most natural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自然的；天然的","explanation":"指存在於自然界中，或沒有經過人為製造、加工和安排的狀態。這個意思抓住“保持本來樣子”這一核心。","examples":[{"en":"The park is designed to protect the natural environment.","zh":"這個公園的設計是為了保護自然環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tried to keep her movements natural during the interview.","zh":"她在面試時儘量讓自己的動作顯得自然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/natural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5697abca7a318e6871d9","word":"nature","forms":["nature"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0136c64faeed6712","term":"nature","forms":["nature","natures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自然界；自然秩序","explanation":"指物理世界及其中的自然力量和秩序，通常與人造的制度、技術或精神領域相對，也可泛指植物、動物和其他自然現象的整體。","examples":[{"en":"Many species live in nature without human protection.","zh":"許多物種沒有人類保護也能在自然界中生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary explores the power of nature.","zh":"這部紀錄片探討了自然的力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df9f0188ac66cbbe","term":"nature","forms":["nature","natures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本性；性質","explanation":"指某個人或某種事物固有的樣子、特點或行為傾向，也就是它“本來是什麼樣”。","examples":[{"en":"The nature of the job requires patience.","zh":"這份工作的性質要求人有耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is generous by nature.","zh":"她天生慷慨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-118011bef6c697f7107c","word":"naughty","forms":["naughty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fa2f75733358270","term":"naughty","forms":["naughty","naughtier","naughtiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"調皮的；淘氣的","explanation":"指孩子或有時指動物愛惡作劇、不聽話或做了不該做的小事，通常不是嚴重的壞行為。","examples":[{"en":"The naughty puppy pulled the towels off the rack.","zh":"那隻淘氣的小狗把毛巾從架子上扯了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be naughty—put the toys back in the box.","zh":"別淘氣，把玩具放回盒子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/naughty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0cda6559bb347db706f","word":"navigate","forms":["navigate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-098089ee73c2f823","term":"navigate","forms":["navigate","navigates","navigating","navigated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掌握航向","explanation":"指在旅途中規劃、控制並記錄船、飛機或其他交通工具的位置和行進路線，也就是親自掌舵，確保它沿著預定方向前進。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot carefully navigated the plane through the storm.","zh":"飛行員小心地操縱飛機穿過暴風雨區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They used the stars to navigate across the desert.","zh":"他們藉助星星確定方向，穿過了沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navigate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b547858a1db673f0","term":"navigate","forms":["navigate","navigates","navigating","navigated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"瀏覽頁面","explanation":"指在網站、應用或選單中透過點選連結、按鈕等方式找到並進入不同頁面；這裡把網頁結構想成一條需要沿路尋找出口的路線。","examples":[{"en":"It took me a few minutes to navigate back to the account page.","zh":"我花了幾分鐘才找到回到賬戶頁面的路徑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new menu makes the website easier to navigate.","zh":"新的選單讓這個網站更容易瀏覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navigate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e94350d2a898acf5","term":"navigate","forms":["navigate","navigates","navigating","navigated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設法應對","explanation":"指在困難的處境、複雜的制度或漫長的過程中摸清方向並逐步處理好它；它把現實中的找路引申成在問題中找到可行辦法。","examples":[{"en":"She had to navigate a complicated visa application process.","zh":"她不得不設法應對複雜的簽證申請流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team is learning to navigate the changes in the industry.","zh":"團隊正在學習如何應對行業變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navigate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-d70d5a7909ed5910fbc6","word":"navigation","forms":["navigation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3175f3199fa9c8b","term":"navigation","forms":["navigation","navigations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"導航；航海與路線規劃","explanation":"指利用地圖、儀器或其他技術確定方向、規劃路線並沿路線到達目的地的知識和實踐，可用於道路交通、船舶、飛機甚至太空飛行。","examples":[{"en":"The crew relied on satellite navigation to avoid the storm.","zh":"船員依靠衛星導航避開了暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good navigation is essential when driving on unfamiliar roads.","zh":"在陌生道路上開車時，良好的導航能力至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navigation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1a6ccc71a53c244","term":"navigation","forms":["navigation","navigations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船舶航運","explanation":"指船隻在水上的往來運輸，尤其常用於商業船運這一整體活動。這裡關注的是船隻交通網路，而不是某艘船的一次航行。","examples":[{"en":"The river has supported commercial navigation for centuries.","zh":"這條河支援商業航運已有數百年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Navigation on the river stops when ice forms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navigation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df108922e732f36d1805","word":"navy","forms":["navy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1fcf57a45ce4c90","term":"navy","forms":["navy","navies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海軍","explanation":"指一個國家全部的海上軍事力量，包括軍艦、其他裝備和海軍人員；記住它不是單獨一艘船，而是整支海上軍事隊伍。","examples":[{"en":"She joined the navy after finishing college.","zh":"她大學畢業後加入了海軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The navy sent two ships to the island.","zh":"海軍派了兩艘軍艦前往那座島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/navy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46ba34770bccfde75670","word":"near","forms":["near"],"officialPos":"prep./adj./adv./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a8cccc57219d690f","term":"near","forms":["near","nearer","nearest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空間上近的","explanation":"表示某人或某物在空間位置上離另一人或另一物很近，就像伸手或走幾步便能接觸到。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small café near my office.","zh":"我辦公室附近有一家小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't see near objects clearly without my glasses.","zh":"不戴眼鏡時，我看不清近處的物體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/near","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04615bdaf2234984","term":"near","forms":["near","nearer","nearest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"時間將近的","explanation":"表示某個時間、事件或階段快要到來或結束，離現在已經不遠。","examples":[{"en":"The deadline is near, so we need to finish the report.","zh":"截止日期快到了，所以我們得完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Summer is near.","zh":"夏天快到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/near","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d84e9182a4ca03f7","term":"near","forms":["near","nearer","nearest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在附近；臨近","explanation":"表示某人或某物處在接近的位置或時間，重點是“靠近著”，而不是修飾一個名詞。","examples":[{"en":"Come near so I can show you the picture.","zh":"靠近一點，我好給你看這張照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As winter drew near, they gathered extra firewood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/near","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-befed8080807f0d4","term":"near","forms":["near"],"pos":"prep","zh":"靠近；在附近","explanation":"表示某人或某物在空間位置上接近另一個地點、物體或人。","examples":[{"en":"They live near the river.","zh":"他們住在河邊附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bright planet was visible near the Moon.","zh":"月亮附近可以看到一顆明亮的行星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/near","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09a05f0a0d4d1c1d","term":"near","forms":["near","nears","nearing","neared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"接近；靠近","explanation":"表示人、船、車輛等向某個地點或物件移動，距離逐漸縮短，但不一定已經到達。它是“靠近”這一核心影象最直接的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The train is nearing the station.","zh":"火車正在接近車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As we neared the village, the road became narrower.","zh":"我們接近村莊時，道路變窄了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/near","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-71ed8bd8993d761cd00d","word":"nearby","forms":["nearby"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-acaa464713361b6b","term":"nearby","forms":["nearby","more nearby","most nearby"],"pos":"adj","zh":"附近的","explanation":"表示某個地方、人或物離說話者或所談物件不遠，就在旁邊或不遠處。","examples":[{"en":"He stopped at a nearby store for some groceries.","zh":"他在附近的一家商店停下來買了些食品雜貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a nearby park where children can play.","zh":"附近有一個孩子們可以玩耍的公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nearby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-540c243ffddce7da","term":"nearby","forms":["nearby","more nearby","most nearby"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在附近","explanation":"表示人或物所在的位置離這裡不遠，方便前往或看見；這是 nearby 最常見的日常用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"I'm glad my friends live nearby where I can visit them.","zh":"我很高興朋友們住在附近，我可以去看望他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We parked nearby and walked to the museum.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nearby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf33e11fa29422274424","word":"nearly","forms":["nearly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-57b414c797573e11","term":"nearly","forms":["nearly","nearlier","more nearly","nearliest","most nearly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"幾乎；差不多","explanation":"表示某人或某事已經非常接近某種狀態、數量或結果，但還沒有完全達到；這是 nearly 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The bottle is nearly empty.","zh":"這個瓶子差不多空了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I nearly missed the bus.","zh":"我差點沒趕上公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nearly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bf722eabef8f47b86e1","word":"nearsighted","forms":["nearsighted"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"nearsighted","forms":["nearsighted"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"近視的","examples":[{"en":"She is nearsighted and needs glasses to read the board.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A nearsighted person may find distant signs difficult to see.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-60f858c0625d7b4100d5","word":"neat","forms":["neat"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cbd453de8b1064be","term":"neat","forms":["neat","neater","neatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"整潔的；乾淨的","explanation":"指沒有雜亂或汙跡，外表收拾得很整齊；房間、衣服、頭髮和書寫都可以這樣形容。","examples":[{"en":"Her desk is always neat and organized.","zh":"她的書桌總是整潔而井然有序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He keeps his notes neat and easy to read.","zh":"他把筆記整理得很整潔，讀起來也很容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3677b909e01246c5","term":"neat","forms":["neat","neater","neatest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"純飲的；不加混合物的","explanation":"說酒或其他飲品保持原樣飲用，不加冰、不加水或其他調和物；重點是“不摻別的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"I usually drink bourbon neat.","zh":"我通常純飲波本威士忌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ordered his whisky neat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80ea8bc4ba2d5f41e0e3","word":"necessary","forms":["necessary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0bed265682eeeb9","term":"necessary","forms":["necessary","necessarier","more necessary","necessariest","most necessary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"必須的；必需的","explanation":"指為了完成某事、達到某個結果，或者避免某種懲罰而不能缺少的東西。它強調“沒有它就不行”，不一定表示這是最方便或最好的選擇。","examples":[{"en":"A passport is necessary for international travel.","zh":"出國旅行必須有護照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is necessary to back up your files regularly.","zh":"定期備份檔案是必要的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/necessary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74bd4cd0bb5fbd2a","term":"necessary","forms":["necessary","necessarier","more necessary","necessariest","most necessary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不可避免的；躲不開的","explanation":"指某件事無論人們願不願意，最終都會發生，或者在特定條件下無法迴避。這個意思從“不得不面對”延伸而來，重點不是需要採取行動，而是結果無法逃避。","examples":[{"en":"Some changes are necessary when a company grows quickly.","zh":"公司快速發展時，有些變化是不可避免的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some discomfort is a necessary consequence of the treatment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/necessary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6451cc6dd815a950de3","word":"necessity","forms":["necessity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac6b863ee8364e40","term":"necessity","forms":["necessity","necessities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必要性；不可避免","explanation":"表示某件事是必須的、無法避免的，或某種情況要求人不得不這樣做。它強調“非這樣不可”的性質，而不一定指具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"Out of necessity, she learned to repair her own bicycle.","zh":"由於不得已，她學會了自己修腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The necessity of regular backups became clear after the computer failed.","zh":"電腦出故障後，定期備份的必要性顯而易見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/necessity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b440798024ffecc","term":"necessity","forms":["necessity","necessities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必需品","explanation":"指某件具體而不可缺少的東西，是“必須有”的物品或條件。它正是“必要性”從抽象要求延伸到具體物件的用法。","examples":[{"en":"A warm coat is a necessity for anyone working outdoors in winter.","zh":"對冬天在戶外工作的人來說，保暖外套是必需品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clean drinking water is a basic necessity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/necessity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f14896d8de9dc78832dd","word":"neck","forms":["neck"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42048c5f0897bd3a","term":"neck","forms":["neck","necks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脖子；頸部","explanation":"連線頭部和軀幹的部位，人和許多動物都有；這是 neck 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I slept badly and now my neck hurts.","zh":"我沒睡好，現在脖子疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The giraffe stretched its long neck toward the leaves.","zh":"長頸鹿把長長的脖子伸向樹葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d99b006219c2a338","term":"neck","forms":["neck","necks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣領；領口部分","explanation":"指衣服上圍繞或貼近脖子的部分，是從“脖子所在的位置”擴充套件出來的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The dress has a high neck and long sleeves.","zh":"這條連衣裙是高領的，而且袖子很長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sweater has a loose, rounded neck.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c029044bd6ff4aad","term":"neck","forms":["neck","necks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓶頸；瓶口下方的細頸","explanation":"指瓶子靠近開口處逐漸變細的部分，因為它像一隻瓶子的脖子。","examples":[{"en":"She tied a ribbon around the neck of the bottle.","zh":"她把一條絲帶系在瓶頸上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A ribbon was tied around the bottle's neck.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-731f46507cc5394513e3","word":"necklace","forms":["necklace"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1753b7d9ce6944ad","term":"necklace","forms":["necklace","necklaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"項鍊","explanation":"圍在脖子上佩戴的首飾，通常由金屬、珍珠、寶石、珠子或貝殼串成，有時帶有吊墜。這是 necklace 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a silver necklace with a small pendant.","zh":"她戴著一條帶小吊墜的銀項鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought my sister a pearl necklace for her birthday.","zh":"我給妹妹買了一條珍珠項鍊作為生日禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/necklace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97e5f4b3e8abdc94","term":"necklace","forms":["necklace","necklaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"項鍊狀的一串東西","explanation":"指一串物體排列成像項鍊一樣的形狀，常用於描寫島嶼、燈光、城市或其他彼此相連的事物。這裡不是說它真的能戴在脖子上，而是借用了“一串圍繞或延伸開來的東西”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"A necklace of small islands stretches along the coast.","zh":"一串小島沿著海岸延展開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A necklace of tiny islands surrounds the lagoon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/necklace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-145ad053dc56aeef0d61","word":"necktie","forms":["necktie"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"necktie","forms":["necktie"],"pos":"n.","zh":"領帶","examples":[{"en":"He chose a blue necktie for the interview.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The child tried to tie his father's necktie.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-be8dff00b0d468b29d80","word":"need","forms":["need"],"officialPos":"v./n./aux.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71463962096db5d8","term":"need","forms":["need","needs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"需要；必要性","explanation":"need指某件事或某樣東西不可缺少的情況，也可以指因此產生的具體需求。它既能表示客觀上的必要，也能表示人意識到自己缺少某物。","examples":[{"en":"There's no need to hurry; we still have plenty of time.","zh":"沒必要著急，我們還有很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project has an urgent need for more staff.","zh":"這個專案急需更多工作人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/need","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fdd99b33b2e8f549","term":"need","forms":["need","needs","needing","needed","needest","neededst","needeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"需要","explanation":"need表示某人或某物要正常存在、運作或完成任務，必須有某樣東西。它強調不可缺少，而不只是一般意義上的想要。","examples":[{"en":"Plants need sunlight and water to grow.","zh":"植物生長需要陽光和水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to check the address before we leave.","zh":"我們出發前需要核對地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/need","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4e7ad35baaa83c3","term":"need","forms":["need","needs","needing","needed","needest","neededst","needeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"必須；不必","explanation":"作為情態動詞，need表示做某事是否有必要，尤其常用於否定式need not，意思是“不必做某事”。它把重點放在行動的必要性上，而不是某個人的具體需求上。","examples":[{"en":"You need not bring anything; dinner is already prepared.","zh":"你不必帶任何東西，晚飯已經準備好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You needn't bring anything to the picnic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/need","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09881f6ed93360a2f6ad","word":"needle","forms":["needle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec320884b7e7e718","term":"needle","forms":["needle","needles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"針","explanation":"needle是細長尖銳、用來刺入或穿過東西的工具，最典型的是縫紉針，也可指注射、針灸、紋身等使用的針。","examples":[{"en":"She threaded the needle and repaired the torn shirt.","zh":"她給針穿上線，縫好了撕破的襯衫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse prepared a needle for the injection.","zh":"護士準備好了注射用的針。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/needle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a0d73f9ab3f941c7219","word":"needy","forms":["needy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d030c841706379f4","term":"needy","forms":["needy","needier","neediest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貧困的；缺少生活所需的","explanation":"指缺錢、缺少食物或其他基本生活用品，因而需要外界幫助的人。這個義項保留了“身上有物質缺口”的核心形象，重點是生活條件困難，而不只是暫時想要某樣東西。","examples":[{"en":"The charity provides meals and warm clothes for needy families.","zh":"這家慈善機構為貧困家庭提供飯菜和保暖衣物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many needy children rely on free school lunches.","zh":"許多生活困難的孩子依靠免費的學校午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/needy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2288709dc57b7fac","term":"needy","forms":["needy","needier","neediest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"情感上過度依賴的","explanation":"指一個人缺乏自信或安全感，不斷要求別人陪伴、回覆、安慰或肯定。這裡的“需要缺口”從物質轉到了感情，通常暗示這種索取已經過多，令身邊的人感到壓力。","examples":[{"en":"He becomes needy when he feels ignored and keeps asking whether I am angry.","zh":"他覺得自己被忽視時就會變得很依賴，不停問我是不是生氣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His needy behavior strained their friendship.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/needy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09f04951af4cd5038778","word":"negative","forms":["negative"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2ddf8c2e7c81819","term":"negative","forms":["negative","more negative","most negative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"負面的；不利的","explanation":"表示某事帶來壞的、不受歡迎的或不利的結果，是日常英語中最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden price increase had a negative effect on sales.","zh":"突然漲價對銷量產生了不利影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can have negative effects on your health.","zh":"睡眠不足可能對健康產生不良影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/negative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa0cc6478be3c30e","term":"negative","forms":["negative","more negative","most negative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"負的；小於零的","explanation":"在數學中表示數值低於零，例如負五就是比零小五。","examples":[{"en":"The temperature fell to a negative five degrees overnight.","zh":"一夜之間氣溫降到了零下五度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A negative number is less than zero.","zh":"負數小於零。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/negative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ce83a10686860c0","term":"negative","forms":["negative","more negative","most negative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"檢測陰性的；未檢出的","explanation":"形容檢測結果沒有檢出所要尋找的疾病、病毒或其他目標，通常譯為“陰性”。","examples":[{"en":"She tested negative for the virus.","zh":"她的病毒檢測結果為陰性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His blood test came back negative.","zh":"他的血液檢查結果為陰性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/negative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84e0c3d153f90f6d5bfd","word":"neglect","forms":["neglect"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8cd6f7c17305075d","term":"neglect","forms":["neglect","neglects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長期疏於照料","explanation":"指習慣性或持續地缺少關心和照料；它不是偶爾漏掉一件事，而是反覆讓某人或某物得不到應有的照顧。","examples":[{"en":"Years of neglect left the garden full of weeds.","zh":"多年的疏於照料使這座花園雜草叢生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The neglected pony had received neither grooming nor proper food.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neglect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ace58eb201d2ab1","term":"neglect","forms":["neglect","neglects","neglecting","neglected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忽視；疏於照料","explanation":"指本來應該照料、關注或處理某人某事，卻沒有這樣做；原因可以是粗心，也可以是長期缺乏關心。","examples":[{"en":"He neglected his health while working two jobs.","zh":"他同時做兩份工作時忽視了自己的健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please do not neglect to check the locks before you leave.","zh":"離開前請不要忘了檢查門鎖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neglect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67c9a9ad709a59ba7747","word":"negotiate","forms":["negotiate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e71d5396c7312dee","term":"negotiate","forms":["negotiate","negotiates","negotiating","negotiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"協商","explanation":"指雙方或多方就分歧和條件進行談判，努力找到彼此都能接受的協議。重點是“談出共同安排”，而不只是交換意見。","examples":[{"en":"The two sides are negotiating with each other to end the dispute.","zh":"雙方正在相互協商，以結束這場爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to negotiate before making a final decision.","zh":"我們需要先協商，再作出最後決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/negotiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c0064b741f4b962","term":"negotiate","forms":["negotiate","negotiates","negotiating","negotiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"談妥；協商安排","explanation":"指透過相互讓步或協調，把合同、價格、條件等具體事項安排並確定下來。這裡的重點從“進行談判”落到了“談出結果”。","examples":[{"en":"The company negotiated a better price with the supplier.","zh":"公司和供應商談出了一個更優惠的價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The union negotiated a shorter working week.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/negotiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c79e1f0e3efc3a43ee11","word":"negotiation","forms":["negotiation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40c2e6998bbcb0ff","term":"negotiation","forms":["negotiation","negotiations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"協商；談判過程","explanation":"指雙方或多方透過討論、讓步和調整條件，努力達成共同協議的過程。它可以涉及價格、合同、工作條件或其他需要雙方同意的事項。","examples":[{"en":"The final price is still under negotiation.","zh":"最終價格仍在協商中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After several rounds of negotiation, both sides reached an agreement.","zh":"經過幾輪談判後，雙方達成了協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/negotiation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c65f1ed1c4f4bf1bc265","word":"neighbor","forms":["neighbor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c4a5e4bb55fd10e","term":"neighbor","forms":["neighbor","neighbors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鄰居；鄰近者","explanation":"neighbor 指住在你附近的人，也可以泛指彼此相鄰的國家、地區或其他事物；它的核心畫面就是“在旁邊”。","examples":[{"en":"Our new neighbor brought us some homemade bread.","zh":"我們的新鄰居送了我們一些自制麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Canada is a close neighbor of the United States.","zh":"加拿大是美國的近鄰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neighbor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b361dfe3a8fc504c982","word":"neighborhood","forms":["neighborhood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1c3f598c61459f5","term":"neighborhood","forms":["neighborhood","neighborhoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"住所附近的社群","explanation":"指住宅周圍的一片區域，通常包括街道、房屋和附近設施，也就是人們所說的一個社群或街區。","examples":[{"en":"He lives in my neighborhood.","zh":"他住在我所在的社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a quiet park in our neighborhood.","zh":"我們社群裡有一個安靜的公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neighborhood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2ee3055be6bcd79","term":"neighborhood","forms":["neighborhood","neighborhoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社群居民","explanation":"把一個社群看作住在其中的人們，強調這一片地方里的居民整體，而不是某一個鄰居。","examples":[{"en":"The fire alarmed the neighborhood.","zh":"這場火災驚動了整個社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The whole neighborhood came out to welcome them.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neighborhood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02566ed5f41493c2adb6","word":"neither","forms":["neither"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./pron./conj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c508da7f26ff6ef","term":"neither","forms":["neither"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也不","explanation":"這裡的 neither 不是在選擇兩個物件，而是接著前面的否定說“同樣也不”。它把“我不做”擴充套件成“另一個人也不做”，就像兩扇門都沒有被選中一樣。","examples":[{"en":"I don't enjoy crowded places, and neither does my sister.","zh":"我不喜歡擁擠的地方，我妹妹也不喜歡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He can't drive, and neither can I.","zh":"他不會開車，我也不會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neither","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eee9a29d12835815","term":"neither","forms":["neither"],"pos":"det","zh":"兩個都不","explanation":"neither 放在名詞前，表示兩個物件中的哪一個都不符合所說的情況。例如說兩種定義都不正確，就是“兩個選項都沒有被選中”。","examples":[{"en":"Neither answer explains the problem clearly.","zh":"兩個答案都沒有清楚地解釋這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Neither answer matches the evidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neither","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca6fda6a8a81f07a","term":"neither","forms":["neither"],"pos":"pron","zh":"兩者都不是","explanation":"neither 單獨使用時，指兩個已經提到或容易確定的物件，表示其中哪一個都不是。它仍然保留“兩扇門都不選”的核心畫面，只是不再重複名詞。","examples":[{"en":"I've tried on both jackets, but neither fits me well.","zh":"兩件夾克我都試過了，但哪一件穿著都不合身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I tried both keys, but neither worked.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neither","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1004e926e8eb10e1f6c","word":"nephew","forms":["nephew"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddcf542ebc158b39","term":"nephew","forms":["nephew","nephews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"侄子；外甥","explanation":"指兄弟或姐妹的兒子：兄弟的兒子是侄子，姐妹的兒子是外甥。英語用同一個 nephew 覆蓋這兩種關係。","examples":[{"en":"My nephew is starting school this year.","zh":"我的侄子（或外甥）今年要開始上學了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She often takes her nephew to the park.","zh":"她經常帶她的侄子（或外甥）去公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nephew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a1c2d155cdc566ea285","word":"nerve","forms":["nerve"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02e05e2a11640b7c","term":"nerve","forms":["nerve","nerves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神經","explanation":"指由神經元及其保護、供血組織組成的身體結構，負責傳遞感覺和行動訊號；它是“傳遞力量和感覺的線”這一核心形象的本義。","examples":[{"en":"The nerves can be seen through the skin.","zh":"透過皮膚可以看到神經。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury damaged a nerve in his hand.","zh":"這次受傷損傷了他手裡的一條神經。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nerve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8574857594d7d1e","term":"nerve","forms":["nerve","nerves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膽量；厚臉皮","explanation":"指讓人敢於採取行動的心理力量，既可以是值得稱讚的勇氣，也可以是令人惱火的大膽或厚臉皮。","examples":[{"en":"He had the nerve to enter my house uninvited.","zh":"他竟敢未經允許就進我家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She almost lost her nerve before going on stage.","zh":"她上臺前差點失去勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nerve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7763f466cd16e5ff","term":"nerve","forms":["nerve","nerves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緊張不安","explanation":"複數形式表示由害怕、壓力或其他負面情緒造成的緊張狀態；身體裡的“線”彷彿被拉緊，於是人變得坐立不安。","examples":[{"en":"I had a bad case of nerves before the interview.","zh":"面試前我緊張得厲害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was a bundle of nerves waiting for the results.","zh":"她等結果時緊張得坐立不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nerve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb3a7850111f293bfc97","word":"nervous","forms":["nervous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-517da6a7c54a1b59","term":"nervous","forms":["nervous","more nervous","nervouser","most nervous","nervousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"神經的","explanation":"指與神經有關，常用於描述神經組織、神經系統或神經活動。這是本詞最值得優先掌握的義項。","examples":[{"en":"The nervous system sends signals throughout the body.","zh":"神經系統把訊號傳遍全身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Damage to nervous tissue can take a long time to heal.","zh":"神經組織受損後可能需要很長時間才能恢復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nervous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75ef2e329bdb50d26a4c","word":"nest","forms":["nest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cfb6cda16a735fa9","term":"nest","forms":["nest","nests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鳥巢","explanation":"鳥搭出來用來產卵、孵蛋和養育幼鳥的結構，就是 nest；這個“讓生命安穩待在裡面的窩”是全詞的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The mother bird returned to the nest with food.","zh":"鳥媽媽帶著食物回到了巢裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a nest hidden in the hedge.","zh":"我們在樹籬裡發現了一個隱藏的鳥巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d83974962e85bd3c","term":"nest","forms":["nest","nests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舒適的居處或處境","explanation":"由“窩”引申為讓人感到舒適、安全的家或工作處境；a cozy nest 就是一個溫馨的小窩。","examples":[{"en":"After years of travel, they finally made a cozy nest by the sea.","zh":"旅行多年後，他們終於在海邊安了一個溫馨的小家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has created a comfortable nest at the back of the office.","zh":"她在辦公室後面佈置出了一個舒適的小天地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0a43a1edd99a4fa","term":"nest","forms":["nest","nests","nesting","nested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"築巢或居巢","explanation":"nest 作動詞時可指鳥築巢，或鳥在巢中安頓；動作核心是建立並使用自己的“窩”。","examples":[{"en":"Swallows nest under the roof every spring.","zh":"燕子每年春天都在屋簷下築巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A pair of owls began nesting in the abandoned chimney.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b1d9aee8fcd50e8","term":"nest","forms":["nest","nests","nesting","nested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安頓在家中","explanation":"nest 也可指人搬進一個地方後很快安頓下來，把那裡變成自己的舒適小窩。","examples":[{"en":"We nested in our new apartment within a week.","zh":"我們一週內就把新公寓安頓成了自己的小窩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newlyweds spent autumn nesting in their little flat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a08a0fcbdeafd3c1b3a4","word":"net","forms":["net"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e36702d88271a8b6","term":"net","forms":["net","nets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網狀物","explanation":"指由線、繩或纖維交織成的網，例如髮網、蚊帳或球網；先想象一張能把東西攔住的網。","examples":[{"en":"She put a net over the bowl to keep the flies away.","zh":"她在碗上罩了一張網，防止蒼蠅靠近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fisherman repaired the torn net before dawn.","zh":"漁夫在天亮前修好了破網。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/net","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c407ed1baa925b5","term":"net","forms":["net","nets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路系統","explanation":"指把多個地點、裝置、使用者或組織連線起來，以便通訊、運輸或共享資源的系統；這就是“把人和地點連成一張網”的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"The bus net connects the villages with the nearest town.","zh":"這套公交網路把各個村莊和最近的城鎮連線起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wireless net links all the devices in the office.","zh":"無線網路把辦公室裡的所有裝置連線起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/net","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e17e6626d68439c0","term":"net","forms":["net","nets","netting","netted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用網捕捉","explanation":"表示用網把魚、昆蟲或其他東西捕獲，正是“網能把東西網住”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"The children netted three small fish by the pier.","zh":"孩子們在碼頭邊用網捕到了三條小魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers netted several small fish for examination.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/net","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3009be769fb8f956e841","word":"network","forms":["network"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d82875bd5eba8bcc","term":"network","forms":["network","networks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相互連線的網路或系統","explanation":"指許多道路、機構、人員或其他要素彼此連線而形成的整體。重點不在單個成員，而在這些成員之間形成了像網一樣的聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"A network of roads connects the villages.","zh":"一個道路網路把這些村莊連線起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has built a strong network of professional contacts.","zh":"她建立了一個穩固的職業人脈網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/network","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28bdf67b8f7a1736","term":"network","forms":["network","networks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電腦或裝置組成的網路","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指彼此連線、能夠交換資料或共享資源的裝置系統。它可以是辦公室裡的區域網絡，也可以是更大的通訊網路。","examples":[{"en":"The printer is connected to the office network.","zh":"這臺印表機連線到了辦公室網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A damaged cable disconnected half the machines from the network.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/network","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b7e54d2f5bcdc0e","term":"network","forms":["network","networks","networking","networked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建立人脈","explanation":"指為了獲得資訊、機會或職業發展而主動認識他人、維持聯絡。它把“進入關係網”的概念變成了一個行動。","examples":[{"en":"He goes to conferences to network with people in the industry.","zh":"他參加會議是為了結識業內人士、建立人脈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She networked for months before finding a new job.","zh":"她花了幾個月建立人脈，後來才找到新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/network","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e2372f4115c43bac724","word":"neutral","forms":["neutral"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5bfdb53c8688abc7","term":"neutral","forms":["neutral","more neutral","most neutral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"衝突中不站隊","explanation":"在戰爭、衝突或國際關係中，neutral 表示不加入任何一方，也不支援其中一方。它強調政治或軍事上的不結盟、保持中立。","examples":[{"en":"The country remained neutral during the war.","zh":"這個國家在戰爭期間保持中立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country remained neutral throughout the conflict.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neutral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67939ea3a7e3ea9d","term":"neutral","forms":["neutral","more neutral","most neutral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對爭議雙方都不支援","explanation":"在爭論或有分歧的話題上，neutral 表示既不贊成支援方，也不贊成反對方，暫時不偏向任何觀點。","examples":[{"en":"I try to stay neutral when my friends argue.","zh":"朋友爭論時，我儘量保持中立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report takes a neutral position on the issue.","zh":"這份報告在這個問題上採取中立立場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neutral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a24808251ff10214","term":"neutral","forms":["neutral","more neutral","most neutral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不正面也不負面","explanation":"對結果、反應或評價來說，neutral 表示既不是積極的，也不是消極的，處在不明顯的中間狀態。比如一個人的反應可能既不是贊成也不是反對，而只是平淡或無明確傾向。","examples":[{"en":"Her reaction to the news was neutral.","zh":"她對這個訊息的反應很平淡，沒有明顯的正面或負面傾向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His expression remained neutral throughout the announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neutral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90a19f1415ddfd20","term":"neutral","forms":["neutral","neutrals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中立狀態或中立國","explanation":"作名詞時，neutral 可指不參加衝突任何一方的中立狀態，也可指採取這種立場的國家或一方。它把“沒有向任一邊傾斜”從形容詞變成了一個立場或實體。","examples":[{"en":"The country declared its neutrality and became a neutral.","zh":"這個國家宣佈中立，併成為一箇中立國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several neutrals offered to host the peace talks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neutral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0950c6ae0e719f25","term":"neutral","forms":["neutral","neutrals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不站隊的人","explanation":"neutral 可以指在爭端中不支援任何一方的人，也就是保持中立的當事人或旁觀者。這個人可能只是拒絕選邊，不一定負責解決爭端。","examples":[{"en":"Both sides asked a neutral to listen to their arguments.","zh":"雙方都請一位中立者聽取各自的論點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Neutrals offered to mediate between the warring factions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/neutral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6497e4b3d7bed16979a3","word":"never","forms":["never"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-910ab1f90f75c3de","term":"never","forms":["never"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從不；絕不","explanation":"指某事在整個相關時間範圍內一次也沒有發生，或說話人表示以後也堅決不會做。它就像那扇門在所有時間點都沒有開啟。","examples":[{"en":"I never drink coffee after dinner.","zh":"我晚飯後從不喝咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She said she would never give up.","zh":"她說她絕不會放棄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/never","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-426d1c082ae6f7a2","term":"never","forms":["never"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從未；以前沒有","explanation":"強調在某個參照時間以前沒有發生過，常用於談論個人經歷或第一次經歷某事；重點是“到那時為止還沒有”。","examples":[{"en":"I have never seen snow before.","zh":"我以前從未見過雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That timid horse has never jumped a fence successfully.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/never","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45ecebb38d4c1fd79a19","word":"nevertheless","forms":["nevertheless"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0041317afe213164","term":"nevertheless","forms":["nevertheless"],"pos":"adv","zh":"儘管如此；然而","explanation":"它先承認前面的事實或困難，再強調後面的情況依然成立，核心感覺就是“雖然這樣，但是仍然……”。","examples":[{"en":"The task was difficult; nevertheless, she finished it on time.","zh":"任務很難，儘管如此，她還是按時完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He knew the risks, but he nevertheless decided to go.","zh":"他知道其中的風險，但還是決定要去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nevertheless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11507a0e2f5e69d5dfa4","word":"new","forms":["new"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e17b17d23bbfe83","term":"new","forms":["new","newer","newest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"剛做成的；剛出現的","explanation":"指最近才製造、創作或出現的東西，重點是它以前還不存在，或最近才以這種形式出現。","examples":[{"en":"The band released a new album last week.","zh":"這個樂隊上週發行了一張新專輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a new scratch on my car.","zh":"我的車上多了一道新的劃痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b55894f9f954ebc8","term":"new","forms":["new","newer","newest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"新增的；新發現的","explanation":"指在原有資訊、證據或選擇之外後來增加，或最近才被發現的內容。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyers found new evidence in the old files.","zh":"律師在舊檔案中找到了新的證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers identified a new species in the cave.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f500e096261a0d3c","term":"new","forms":["new","newer","newest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"現在的；取代原來的","explanation":"指相對於過去的安排、身份、住所或物品而言，現在所擁有或使用的那個，即使它本身並不新造。","examples":[{"en":"My new job is more demanding than my old one.","zh":"我現在的新工作比以前的工作要求更高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had lived in our new house for five years.","zh":"那時我們已經在現在這所房子裡住了五年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2def21009e38043","term":"new","forms":["new","newer","newest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未使用過的；嶄新的","explanation":"指物品處於原始、潔淨、沒有被使用或穿戴過的狀態，常與二手物品相對。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a new coat instead of a second-hand one.","zh":"她買了一件新外套，而不是二手的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore new shoes straight from the box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19fba0e995b9794fc2c2","word":"news","forms":["news"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c497feb546756c8a","term":"news","forms":["news"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新訊息；新資訊","explanation":"指剛得知的、值得關注的新資訊，可以是關於某個人、某件事或某種情況的訊息。核心感覺是“新的東西傳到你這裡來了”，不一定來自新聞媒體。","examples":[{"en":"Is there any news about the storm?","zh":"有關於這場暴風雨的訊息嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you heard any news about the missing hikers?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/news","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5503248df6cf220d","term":"news","forms":["news"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新聞；時事報道","explanation":"指報紙、電視、廣播或網路媒體釋出的當前事件資訊。它仍然是“新訊息傳開”的概念，只是來源和範圍更明確，通常面向公眾。","examples":[{"en":"I watched the evening news before dinner.","zh":"我晚飯前看了晚間新聞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The news led with an update on the coastal flooding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/news","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f29c4511672f1610be08","word":"newspaper","forms":["newspaper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97ee72f121efaead","term":"newspaper","forms":["newspaper","newspapers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報紙；報刊","explanation":"通常指定期出版、刊登新聞和其他文章的報紙，既可以是紙質的，也可以是數字版；重點是它作為一種新聞出版物。","examples":[{"en":"I read the newspaper every morning before work.","zh":"我每天早晨上班前都看報紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newspaper published a detailed report on the election.","zh":"這家報紙發表了一篇關於選舉的詳細報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/newspaper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ea926bcb5293583","term":"newspaper","forms":["newspaper","newspapers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報社；報業機構","explanation":"這裡不是指紙張或具體的一期報紙，而是指製作和出版報紙的新聞機構，是用出版物的名稱來指代其背後的組織。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper said it would launch a new website next month.","zh":"報社表示下個月將推出一個新網站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newspaper hired three additional reporters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/newspaper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6c1c9a9c8543f1e4cd9","word":"next","forms":["next"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31d17460c15dfbf7","term":"next","forms":["next"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相鄰的；緊挨著的","explanation":"指在空間位置上緊挨著某物或某人，中間沒有別的同類事物；就像排隊時站在你旁邊的人。","examples":[{"en":"The woman in the next seat offered me her window seat.","zh":"坐在旁邊座位上的女士把靠窗的座位讓給了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The next house along has a red gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/next","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-447b849a465ffde9","term":"next","forms":["next"],"pos":"adj","zh":"下一個的；緊接著的","explanation":"指在順序、頁碼、步驟、等級等方面緊跟當前物件的那一個；當前物件結束後，就輪到它。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the next paragraph and underline the main idea.","zh":"請閱讀下一段，並畫出中心思想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take the next turning after the bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/next","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e536892c59940915","term":"next","forms":["next"],"pos":"adv","zh":"接下來會怎樣；下一個","explanation":"表示在當前時刻或當前事項之後即將發生的事情，核心就是“現在這個之後輪到什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"We have finished this chapter; what comes next?","zh":"這一章我們已經學完了，接下來是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Who will speak next?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/next","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59df2f242a610f66","term":"next","forms":["next"],"pos":"det","zh":"下一個；接下來的","explanation":"放在名詞前，表示當前這個或最近提到的那個之後緊接著出現的一個。它可以修飾星期、章節、車次、機會等。","examples":[{"en":"Let’s discuss the budget at our next meeting.","zh":"我們下次開會時討論預算吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The next speaker will discuss urban wildlife.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/next","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e186022d0931afe9fe06","word":"nice","forms":["nice"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f85c66aab1191ca7","term":"nice","forms":["nice","nicer","nicest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人愉快；不錯","explanation":"表示某件事、某個地方或某種體驗讓人感到舒服、滿意或愉快，是 nice 最常見的概括性用法。","examples":[{"en":"We had a nice time at the beach.","zh":"我們在海邊玩得很愉快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a nice surprise.","zh":"那真是個令人愉快的驚喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57cc786f439b67e1","term":"nice","forms":["nice","nicer","nicest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"友好的；討人喜歡的","explanation":"形容人待人友善、相處舒服，也可以泛指這個人給人的印象很好；在某些語境中還可表示有吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"Our new neighbor is very nice to everyone.","zh":"我們的新鄰居對每個人都很友好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She seems like a nice person.","zh":"她看起來是個很友善的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1429f4e31e8d9b21","term":"nice","forms":["nice","nicer","nicest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很；令人滿意地","explanation":"在 “nice and + 形容詞” 中，nice 表示說話人認為後面的性質令人滿意，並帶有輕微加強語氣的作用，如“又……又舒服”或“很……”。","examples":[{"en":"The room is nice and warm now.","zh":"房間現在暖和極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the dough somewhere nice and cool.","zh":"把麵糰放在涼爽的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47c4d6406db7b34454aa","word":"nickel","forms":["nickel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edc76d49746c6523","term":"nickel","forms":["nickel","nickels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鎳","explanation":"指一種銀白色的化學元素和金屬，符號為 Ni，原子序數為 28。這是 nickel 最直接的物質義。","examples":[{"en":"This alloy contains nickel and copper.","zh":"這種合金含有鎳和銅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nickel is used in many corrosion-resistant alloys.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nickel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b239817602422abc","term":"nickel","forms":["nickel","nickels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"五美分硬幣","explanation":"在美國和加拿大，a nickel 是面值五美分的硬幣；它的名稱來自硬幣中曾使用的鎳等金屬。","examples":[{"en":"I found a nickel under the sofa.","zh":"我在沙發下面找到了一枚五美分硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine accepts quarters but won't take a nickel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nickel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0fb3f1159c9dfba179a","word":"nickname","forms":["nickname"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58acf4a6eaddc69e","term":"nickname","forms":["nickname","nicknames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外號；別名","explanation":"這是替代真實姓名或正式名稱的非正式稱呼，通常抓住某個人或事物的突出特點，也可以只是大家約定俗成的別名。","examples":[{"en":"\"The Big Apple\" is a common nickname for New York City.","zh":"“大蘋果”是紐約市常見的別稱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His teammates gave him the nickname Rocket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nickname","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7253f46f50513cfb","term":"nickname","forms":["nickname","nicknames","nicknaming","nicknamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……取外號；給……取暱稱","explanation":"表示把一塊熟悉的“替代名字牌子”掛到某人或某事物上，也就是給它取暱稱或外號。","examples":[{"en":"The students nicknamed their science teacher \"Rocket\" because he moved so quickly.","zh":"學生們因為科學老師動作很快，就給他取了“火箭”這個外號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her classmates nicknamed her Rocket because she ran fast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nickname","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbe6181036b5818eb319","word":"niece","forms":["niece"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5ab41335de64ec7","term":"niece","forms":["niece","nieces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兄弟姐妹的女兒","explanation":"指自己兄弟或姐妹的女兒，也包括配偶的兄弟姐妹的女兒。英語通常不進一步區分她是兄弟的女兒還是姐妹的女兒，所以中文可以根據具體家庭關係譯成“侄女”或“外甥女”。","examples":[{"en":"My niece just celebrated her fifteenth birthday.","zh":"我的外甥女剛過完十五歲生日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His niece is starting university this autumn.","zh":"他的侄女今年秋天要開始上大學了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/niece","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-176473d7313395b6e209","word":"night","forms":["night"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e515e79cc09db8e","term":"night","forms":["night","nights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夜晚；夜間","explanation":"指太陽在地平線下、天空變暗的時段，也就是通常所說的夜晚。","examples":[{"en":"Most animals sleep during the day and move around at night.","zh":"大多數動物白天睡覺，晚上活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The streets are very quiet at night.","zh":"夜裡街道非常安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e89931b70bc24fb","term":"night","forms":["night","nights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某個夜晚的活動","explanation":"把“夜晚”看成一次完整的外出或活動時段，表示在某個晚上參加的娛樂、聚會或其他安排。","examples":[{"en":"We had a fun night out in the city.","zh":"我們在城裡度過了一個開心的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We enjoyed a night at the opera.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6dfa5ed997611337144a","word":"nightmare","forms":["nightmare"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0964543e76dcd954","term":"nightmare","forms":["nightmare","nightmares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噩夢","explanation":"指人在睡覺時做的可怕、令人驚醒或極度不安的夢；夜裡的恐懼畫面就是這個詞最直接的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I had a nightmare about being trapped in a burning building.","zh":"我做了一個被困在著火大樓裡的噩夢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She woke up crying after a terrible nightmare.","zh":"她做了一個可怕的噩夢，哭著醒了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightmare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-960bf3e2dfaa3733","term":"nightmare","forms":["nightmare","nightmares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噩夢般的糟糕經歷","explanation":"把現實中極其混亂、痛苦、令人焦慮或難以處理的情況比作噩夢，因此不必真的發生在睡眠中。","examples":[{"en":"The delayed flight turned the whole trip into a nightmare.","zh":"航班延誤讓整個旅程變成了一場噩夢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trying to fix the old computer was a nightmare.","zh":"想修好那臺舊電腦簡直是一場噩夢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nightmare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d34997d1478a12e9bb0","word":"no/nope","forms":["no","nope"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7f93f7d543d88a6","term":"no","forms":["no"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不；一點也不","explanation":"這裡的 no 直接加強否定，表示“完全不”或“一點也不”，常用於比較或評價。","examples":[{"en":"The second plan is no better than the first.","zh":"第二個方案一點也不比第一個好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The replacement felt no lighter than the original.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/no","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-739aa2a76a9ab771","term":"no","forms":["no"],"pos":"det","zh":"沒有任何","explanation":"no 放在名詞前，表示相關的人或事物一個也沒有，範圍相當於“not any”。","examples":[{"en":"There are no clean cups in the kitchen.","zh":"廚房裡沒有乾淨的杯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one answered the door.","zh":"沒有人應門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/no","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8fffacbe7c43c4b","term":"no","forms":["no","noes","nos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"否定或拒絕的回答","explanation":"no 可以把“不同意、拒絕或否認”本身當作一個回答來談論，核心就是那扇關上的門。","examples":[{"en":"He said no to the offer after thinking it over.","zh":"他考慮過後拒絕了這個提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A simple no was enough to end the discussion.","zh":"一句簡單的“不”就足以結束討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/no","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be03c8546b920429","term":"nope","forms":["nope","nopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拒絕；不行","explanation":"nope 作名詞時指明確的否定回答或拒絕，核心感覺是把某個提議、選擇或請求當場關掉。","examples":[{"en":"I asked if he wanted to come, and he gave me a firm nope.","zh":"我問他想不想來，他明確地拒絕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If she doesn't reply, I'll take that as a nope.","zh":"如果她不回覆，我就把那當作拒絕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3a61c684446b22fbc32","word":"noble","forms":["noble"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-451a19c4b179d0ac","term":"noble","forms":["noble","nobler","more noble","noblest","most noble"],"pos":"adj","zh":"品格高尚的","explanation":"指人的品格、行為或努力高尚正直，不帶自私、卑鄙或可疑的動機；也可形容這樣的行為本身。","examples":[{"en":"She made a noble effort to protect the village.","zh":"她為了保護村莊作出了高尚的努力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was noble of him to admit his mistake.","zh":"他能承認錯誤，這種做法很高尚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14fad82f5ae69cae","term":"noble","forms":["noble","nobler","more noble","noblest","most noble"],"pos":"adj","zh":"宏偉莊嚴的","explanation":"指建築、景象或事物規模宏大、氣勢莊嚴，給人壯麗而高貴的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The noble building stood above the old square.","zh":"那座宏偉的建築矗立在老廣場旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A noble avenue led toward the palace gates.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6382b3cc881412b77bfc","word":"nobody","forms":["nobody"],"officialPos":"pron./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-465d1c87cbf1e641","term":"nobody","forms":["nobody"],"pos":"pron","zh":"沒有人","explanation":"nobody 表示一個人都沒有，範圍比“沒人認識”中的“沒人”更明確，指相關範圍內沒有任何人。","examples":[{"en":"Nobody answered when I knocked on the door.","zh":"我敲門時沒有人回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nobody knows the answer yet.","zh":"目前還沒有人知道答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nobody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-849e6801ae0cf9c4","term":"nobody","forms":["nobody","nobodies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無名小卒","explanation":"這裡把“沒有分量的人”稱為 nobody，指沒有名氣、地位或影響力的人，常含輕視或自我貶低的意味。","examples":[{"en":"He was a nobody before his first novel became a bestseller.","zh":"他的第一部小說成為暢銷書之前，他只是個無名小卒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Before her discovery, she was a nobody in scientific circles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nobody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4043d35e7dd415e7a3e1","word":"nod","forms":["nod"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ad6a02c233914be","term":"nod","forms":["nod","nods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"點頭；點頭致意","explanation":"頭部上下輕動的動作，通常用來表示同意，也可以作為簡短的招呼或致意。它是“nod”最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a quick nod before entering the room.","zh":"她進房間前朝我快速點了點頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His nod showed that he agreed with the plan.","zh":"他的點頭表明他同意這個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nod","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2cbab0329782960","term":"nod","forms":["nod","nods","nodding","nodded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"點頭表示同意","explanation":"上下點動頭部來表示同意、接受或確認，是動詞“nod”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"I asked whether he was ready, and he nodded.","zh":"我問他是否準備好了，他點了點頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She nodded in agreement with the suggestion.","zh":"她點頭表示同意這個建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nod","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-efe2a5c09e6d49d7eb73","word":"noise","forms":["noise"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-10071ce9965085ad","term":"noise","forms":["noise","noises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噪聲；嘈雜聲","explanation":"指通常不想聽、令人不舒服或妨礙安靜的聲音，比如機器轟鳴、施工聲或人群喧鬧。這是 noise 最典型的日常意思。","examples":[{"en":"The construction work is making too much noise.","zh":"施工發出的噪聲太大了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you keep the noise down after ten?","zh":"十點以後你能小聲一點嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24becaaaa7fd8e50","term":"noise","forms":["noise","noises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聲音；聲響","explanation":"也可以泛指聽到的任何聲音，不一定令人討厭。突然傳來的聲響、門外的一聲動靜，都可以叫 noise。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a strange noise outside the window.","zh":"我聽見窗外有奇怪的聲響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strange noise came from beneath the hood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acd6beff7c3430bfed5d","word":"noisy","forms":["noisy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f736aa2a6c9ddd3","term":"noisy","forms":["noisy","noisier","noisiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聲音很大而擾人","explanation":"指發出聲音，尤其是很大而且令人不舒服的聲音；可以形容人群、機器或其他會發聲的東西。核心畫面是聲音像噪聲一樣不斷擠進來，讓人難以安靜地聽或思考。","examples":[{"en":"The noisy crowd made it hard to hear the announcement.","zh":"吵鬧的人群讓人很難聽清通知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our noisy neighbors kept us awake until dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noisy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da916c4294f8096e","term":"noisy","forms":["noisy","noisier","noisiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"充滿噪聲的","explanation":"指某個地方或環境裡到處都是聲音，重點在整體環境嘈雜，而不一定強調某一個具體發聲者。它是“噪聲擠滿空間”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We left the noisy bar and found a quiet café nearby.","zh":"我們離開了嘈雜的酒吧，在附近找了一家安靜的咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The noisy workshop makes telephone calls difficult.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noisy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1139859357aeb528b3f9","word":"nominate","forms":["nominate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-637a33c802a3768f","term":"nominate","forms":["nominate","nominates","nominating","nominated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提名；推薦擔任","explanation":"正式把某人的名字提出，作為某個職位、獎項或角色的候選人；核心畫面就是把名字寫進候選名單。","examples":[{"en":"The committee nominated her for chairperson.","zh":"委員會提名她擔任主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Three students were nominated for the award.","zh":"三名學生獲提名角逐這項獎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nominate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db670e30d0246280","term":"nominate","forms":["nominate","nominates","nominating","nominated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預先指定目標","explanation":"在臺球等有明確規則的遊戲中，先說出這一次要擊入哪個球袋，相當於提前把目標名字點出來。","examples":[{"en":"Before taking the shot, he nominated the corner pocket.","zh":"擊球前，他先指定了角袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nominate the account that should receive the payment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nominate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc5d6641e893d4bb6d43","word":"nomination","forms":["nomination"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1cf23ea8e97e0b06","term":"nomination","forms":["nomination","nominations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提名；推薦","explanation":"指把某人的名字正式提交給某個獎項、職位或選舉，建議由其獲得該獎項、擔任該職位或參加競爭；重點在“提出名字”這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"Her nomination for the award came as a pleasant surprise.","zh":"她獲提名參評該獎項讓人感到意外驚喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee announced the nomination of three young scientists.","zh":"委員會宣佈提名了三位年輕科學家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nomination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78cead8fa91f9704","term":"nomination","forms":["nomination","nominations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提名；提名資格或記錄","explanation":"指一次提名完成後留下的正式結果，也就是某人或某物已經進入候選名單、獲得參評資格這一事實。這裡關注的是“這項提名”，而不只是提交名字的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The film received two nominations but did not win either award.","zh":"這部電影獲得了兩項提名，但沒有贏得其中任何一個獎項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her performance earned an award nomination.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nomination","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc7fdf972e1b13b90b7f","word":"nominee","forms":["nominee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c702173c0b6154a9","term":"nominee","forms":["nominee","nominees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被提名者；候選人","explanation":"指被別人正式提名、推薦或指定去擔任職位、參加選舉或競逐獎項的人。重點在於“有人把他列為人選”，並不保證他最後會當選或獲獎。","examples":[{"en":"She was the youngest nominee for mayor in the city's history.","zh":"她是這座城市歷史上最年輕的市長候選人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The award nominees will be announced next week.","zh":"該獎項的提名名單將於下週公佈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nominee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d545ceba2256cf09","term":"nominee","forms":["nominee","nominees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名義持有人","explanation":"指資產或證券登記在其名下、但實際所有權屬於另一方的人或組織。這裡仍有“名字被安排在某個位置上”的感覺，只是這個位置是登記檔案上的所有者。","examples":[{"en":"The shares were registered in the name of a nominee for the overseas investor.","zh":"這些股份登記在一名名義持有人名下，實際投資者是那位海外投資人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shares are registered in a nominee's name.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nominee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-140bedbf9c3f6d56a984","word":"none","forms":["none"],"officialPos":"pron./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1188b62b632542c4","term":"none","forms":["none"],"pos":"adv","zh":"一點也不；絲毫不","explanation":"這裡的 none 把某種程度降到零，表示完全沒有受到某種影響或完全不具備某種程度。例如生病後“並沒有更糟”，就是一點也不比以前糟。","examples":[{"en":"After the long journey, we were none the worse for wear.","zh":"長途旅行後，我們一點也沒有感到更疲憊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The delay left us none the wiser.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/none","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1e33393198d5e54","term":"none","forms":["none"],"pos":"pron","zh":"一個也沒有；沒有任何一個","explanation":"none 把一個給定數量或群體看成空集合，表示其中一個也沒有。它既可以單獨使用，也可以接“of + 群體”，核心畫面始終是“一個都沒留下”。","examples":[{"en":"None of the students remembered the meeting time.","zh":"這些學生沒有一個記得會議時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I checked all the cupboards, but none was large enough.","zh":"我檢查了所有櫥櫃，但沒有一個足夠大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/none","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20b1b5af0cf3ab0a5b45","word":"nonprofit","forms":["nonprofit"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae6bc1bf926a59da","term":"nonprofit","forms":["nonprofit"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非營利的","explanation":"指一個組織或活動的主要目標不是為所有者或投資者創造利潤，而是服務公眾、成員或某種社會目標；它仍然可以有收入。","examples":[{"en":"She works for a nonprofit organization that provides free meals to children.","zh":"她在一家為兒童提供免費餐食的非營利組織工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum operates as a nonprofit and depends on donations.","zh":"這家博物館以非營利機構的形式運營，依靠捐款維持。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nonprofit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-999aaa8645bb72ff599e","word":"nonsense","forms":["nonsense"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc0b6be5b64a01a9","term":"nonsense","forms":["nonsense","nonsenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"荒唐、毫無道理的東西","explanation":"指愚蠢、缺乏邏輯、沒有價值或根本說不通的想法和行為，是日常使用中最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Paying that much for a broken phone is nonsense.","zh":"花那麼多錢買一部壞手機太荒唐了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His excuse was complete nonsense.","zh":"他的藉口完全是胡說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nonsense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49742b4b8dd3a7ff2a2a","word":"noodle","forms":["noodle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21bf68d653d6a744","term":"noodle","forms":["noodle","noodles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麵條","explanation":"指用麵粉或其他麵糰製成的長條或扁條狀食品，通常煮熟後放進湯裡，或拌醬汁和其他食材食用。","examples":[{"en":"We had noodles in soup for lunch.","zh":"我們午飯吃了湯麵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She picked up one noodle with her chopsticks.","zh":"她用筷子夾起了一根麵條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noodle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b198f3cd8e7048e4a523","word":"noon","forms":["noon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7bc41d374fa1a8cc","term":"noon","forms":["noon","noons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中午","explanation":"指一天中太陽看起來升到最高處的時刻，現代日常英語通常約為中午十二點。它是最常見、最應該優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"On Saturdays, I usually wake up at noon.","zh":"星期六我通常中午才醒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please send me the report by noon.","zh":"請在中午前把報告發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72b2d6cef0fbe37d","term":"noon","forms":["noon","noons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頂峰；全盛時期","explanation":"由太陽到達最高處的畫面引申而來，表示生命、事業或某種發展達到最高點，也就是“巔峰”或“全盛時期”。","examples":[{"en":"She was at the noon of her career when the award arrived.","zh":"她正處於事業巔峰時，獲得了這項獎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At the noon of his career, he commanded enormous influence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb14067bfdd0352e77af","word":"nor","forms":["nor"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"nor","forms":["nor"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"也不；亦非","examples":[{"en":"Neither the manager nor the assistant knew the answer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"He did not apologize, nor did he offer an explanation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-733859c1fc6b9331793b","word":"norm","forms":["norm"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2129ab9623bed80","term":"norm","forms":["norm","norms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"常態；通常情況","explanation":"norm 是用來作比較的“通常標準”，所以某種情況成為 the norm，就是說它在某個地方或群體中已經變得很普遍、很典型。","examples":[{"en":"Working from home has become the norm for many employees.","zh":"對許多員工來說，在家辦公已經成了常態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In this industry, long hours are the norm.","zh":"在這個行業，長時間工作是常態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/norm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9e8cee0efacc909","term":"norm","forms":["norm","norms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會規範；行為準則","explanation":"這裡的 norm 是群體用來約束成員行為的標準，可以是明確規定，也可以只是大家預設應當遵守的習慣。","examples":[{"en":"The custom may seem strange, but it is an accepted social norm there.","zh":"這種習俗可能看起來很奇怪，但在那裡卻是被接受的社會規範。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Laughing loudly during the ceremony would violate local norms.","zh":"在儀式上大聲笑會違反當地的規範。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/norm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-317b32c143692b9939c1","word":"normal","forms":["normal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3142d15192f8c9e","term":"normal","forms":["normal","more normal","normaler","normaller","most normal","normalest","normallest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"符合規範的","explanation":"表示按照既定規則、標準或固定模式進行的，不一定只是“常見的”。例如在資料處理或數學中，normal 常表示某種符合正式規範的形式。","examples":[{"en":"The data must be converted into normal form before analysis.","zh":"這些資料在分析前必須轉換成規範形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The results fell within the normal range.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/normal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92cbede3588c4a8f","term":"normal","forms":["normal","more normal","normaler","normaller","most normal","normalest","normallest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正常的；恢復平常的","explanation":"表示身體、精神或日常狀態沒有異常，或者已經回到平時的狀態。它把“符合通常基準”用於人和生活狀態。","examples":[{"en":"After a good night's sleep, I feel normal again.","zh":"好好睡了一晚後，我又感覺恢復正常了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It took a week for her appetite to return to normal.","zh":"她的食慾過了一週才恢復正常。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/normal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-dc365e79d41cfae1c3c0","word":"north","forms":["north"],"officialPos":"n./adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6765aef538a704e","term":"north","forms":["north"],"pos":"adj","zh":"北面的；北部的","explanation":"表示某地、某物位於北方，或與北方有關，是 north 最基本的形容詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"They moved to north London last year.","zh":"他們去年搬到了倫敦北部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The north entrance opens onto the main road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d5bb3d9476c5011","term":"north","forms":["north"],"pos":"adj","zh":"向北的","explanation":"表示路線、位置或移動方向朝向北方，重點在“朝北”而不是“位於北部”。","examples":[{"en":"The northbound train leaves at six.","zh":"這趟開往北方的列車六點出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We maintained a north course until the lighthouse came into view.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2973869206238070","term":"north","forms":["north"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向北地","explanation":"表示朝北移動，或說明某地位於另一地點的北面；這是方向副詞的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"We drove north for three hours before stopping.","zh":"我們向北開了三個小時才停下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The geese flew north as spring approached.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-787929fcbb4e0cec","term":"north","forms":["north","norths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"北方；北面","explanation":"指朝向北極的方向，也指某個地區的北部；這是名詞用法的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"The village lies in the north of the country.","zh":"這個村莊位於該國北部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dark line marks north on the map.","zh":"地圖上用一條深色線標出了北方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a47d5f99b6c94ce8553","word":"northern","forms":["northern"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b96a42a7ee1f959","term":"northern","forms":["northern","more northern","most northern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"北方的；北部的","explanation":"指位於北方、朝向北方、來自北方，或總體上與北方地區有關。它可以描述地點，也可以描述氣候、邊界、地區等和北方相連的事物。","examples":[{"en":"Flooding has affected several towns in northern India.","zh":"洪水影響了印度北部的幾個城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The northern border is closed during the winter.","zh":"北部邊境在冬季關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/northern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-831db72800d62984","term":"northern","forms":["northern","more northern","most northern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"來自北方的（風）","explanation":"專門說風或氣流從北方吹來，重點是來源方向，而不只是它位於北邊。","examples":[{"en":"A cold northern wind swept across the harbor.","zh":"一陣寒冷的北風席捲了港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A northern breeze brought cooler air to the vineyard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/northern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d77e22123e64d3d87f1f","word":"nose","forms":["nose"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d8f8e8134097ddd","term":"nose","forms":["nose","noses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼻子","explanation":"指人臉中央突出的器官，鼻孔透過它呼吸，也用它聞氣味。這是nose最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The child wiped his nose with a tissue.","zh":"孩子用紙巾擦了擦鼻子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her nose turned red in the cold.","zh":"她的鼻子在寒冷中變紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1128a9a8202583e","term":"nose","forms":["nose","noses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖端；前端","explanation":"指物體最前面或向外伸出的尖端，像鼻子從臉上向前伸出一樣。可以說茶壺嘴、飛機頭部等物體的前端。","examples":[{"en":"A small bird was painted on the nose of the plane.","zh":"飛機頭部畫著一隻小鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Steam escaped from the nose of the kettle.","zh":"蒸汽從茶壺嘴冒了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fae353936a40c0d98c79","word":"nostril","forms":["nostril"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa47cafe2daaf021","term":"nostril","forms":["nostril","nostrils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼻孔","explanation":"nostril 指鼻子上的一個開口，空氣可以透過它進出鼻腔；說鳥時，也可以指鳥喙上的相應開口。","examples":[{"en":"He could barely breathe through one nostril because of his cold.","zh":"他感冒了，幾乎無法透過一個鼻孔呼吸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bird flared its nostrils as it flew.","zh":"那隻鳥飛行時張大了鼻孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nostril","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-254bb97b57f12e1608fe","word":"not","forms":["not"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aaf65eb2f7dd3409","term":"not","forms":["not"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不；沒有","explanation":"not 像一個否定開關，把句子中的動作、狀態或判斷變成“不做、不是、沒有”。它可以否定現在、過去或將來的事情，具體時間由句中的助動詞或時態表達。","examples":[{"en":"I did not see your message.","zh":"我沒有看到你的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is not ready yet.","zh":"她還沒有準備好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/not","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e346e7eb06cbb0a","term":"not","forms":["not"],"pos":"adv","zh":"一點也不；並非","explanation":"not 放在性質或程度前，可以把某個特徵完全否定掉，例如說明某物“不是紅的”，而是另一種顏色或性質。","examples":[{"en":"The water is not hot enough to make tea.","zh":"水還不夠熱，泡不了茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That is not the parcel I ordered.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/not","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6adc722e54d82920e3fa","word":"notable","forms":["notable"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-236d1892498fa54a","term":"notable","forms":["notable","more notable","most notable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯著的；值得注意的","explanation":"指因為成就、特點或重要性而值得人們特別注意，常含有“突出、非同一般”的評價。","examples":[{"en":"She made a notable contribution to the project.","zh":"她為這個專案作出了顯著貢獻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum is notable for its collection of modern art.","zh":"這家博物館因其現代藝術收藏而引人注目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df136e87f7f9f492","term":"notable","forms":["notable","more notable","most notable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯眼的；引人注意的","explanation":"指某人或某物很容易被看出或注意到，重點在外觀或表現的突出，不一定表示它有特別的價值。","examples":[{"en":"The most notable feature of the house is its bright red door.","zh":"這所房子最顯眼的特點是那扇鮮紅色的門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His notable absence prompted several awkward questions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-edb465624291e4053c6c","word":"note","forms":["note"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b12c25d8e85e9550","term":"note","forms":["note","notes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"記號；註釋","explanation":"指用文字、符號等留下的標記或說明，重點是幫助人識別、理解或記住某件事。","examples":[{"en":"She added a note beside the difficult word.","zh":"她在那個難詞旁邊加了一條註釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please make a note of the change.","zh":"請記下這項變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/note","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-858c56a9243270a5","term":"note","forms":["note","notes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"便條；書面訊息","explanation":"指寫給某人或留給某人的簡短書面訊息，也可以是表達某種承諾或安排的書面檔案。","examples":[{"en":"I left a note on the kitchen table.","zh":"我在廚房桌上留了一張便條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wrote me a note saying he would be late.","zh":"他給我寫了張便條，說自己會遲到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/note","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20be7acbc1b3d762","term":"note","forms":["note","notes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音符；音","explanation":"指音樂中可辨認、可寫出的一個音，或由這個音形成的聲音標記；它仍然是“留下的聲音標記”。","examples":[{"en":"She played the first note on the piano.","zh":"她在鋼琴上彈出了第一個音符。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I couldn't reach the highest note.","zh":"我唱不上最高的那個音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/note","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f28998d7a8d54775","term":"note","forms":["note","notes","noting","noted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"注意；留意","explanation":"指認真觀察並把某事當作值得重視的標記，常用於提醒別人注意某個事實或細節。","examples":[{"en":"Note the difference between the two pictures.","zh":"請注意這兩幅圖的區別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I noted that the door was unlocked.","zh":"我注意到門沒有鎖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/note","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-069b77227fd2e0fb","term":"note","forms":["note","notes","noting","noted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"記錄；記下","explanation":"指把聽到、看到或想到的資訊寫下來，留下以後可以檢視的標記。","examples":[{"en":"The secretary noted the time of the meeting.","zh":"秘書記下了會議的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please note down your phone number.","zh":"請記下你的電話號碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/note","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b53bcf919f24746d7209","word":"notebook","forms":["notebook"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0228d62087f29612","term":"notebook","forms":["notebook","notebooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"筆記本；記錄本","explanation":"指用來寫筆記、備忘或記錄想法的本子，也就是把資訊“裝”在裡面的紙質本子。","examples":[{"en":"I wrote the address in my notebook.","zh":"我把地址寫在了筆記本里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She always carries a small notebook.","zh":"她總是帶著一個小筆記本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notebook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b396618715fe019","term":"notebook","forms":["notebook","notebooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"互動式程式設計文件","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指一種把可執行的程式碼與文字說明、圖表等放在同一份文件中的“電子筆記本”，常用於分析、教學和分享工作過程。","examples":[{"en":"The students used a notebook to explain and run their code.","zh":"學生們用互動式文件講解並執行他們的程式碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The notebook combines executable code with explanatory text.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notebook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1785cfc3bc6ac7738e8b","word":"nothing","forms":["nothing"],"officialPos":"pron./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b17b3d5fdbf7fde6","term":"nothing","forms":["nothing","nothings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小事；無關緊要的東西","explanation":"指一件輕得幾乎沒有分量的事情，常用來淡化問題、安慰別人，或說明某事不值得擔心。","examples":[{"en":"“Does your hand hurt?” “No, it's nothing.”","zh":"“你的手疼嗎？”“不疼，沒什麼大不了的。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She said the delay was nothing and kept working.","zh":"她說這點耽擱沒什麼，繼續工作了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nothing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de489ed16852d96c","term":"nothing","forms":["nothing"],"pos":"pron","zh":"什麼都沒有","explanation":"表示沒有任何東西、事情或內容；這是最基本的“空空如也”之義，也是其他引申義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"Nothing happened while we were away.","zh":"我們離開時什麼也沒有發生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I opened the box, but there was nothing inside.","zh":"我開啟盒子，裡面什麼都沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nothing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9368a7d21e018f64ae33","word":"notice","forms":["notice"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4aa9569223f5d151","term":"notice","forms":["notice","notices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"注意；留意","explanation":"指把某人、某物或某個變化放進自己的注意範圍，強調察覺到它，而不一定表示長時間觀察。","examples":[{"en":"She took no notice of the loud music and continued reading.","zh":"她沒有理會吵鬧的音樂，繼續看書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unusual signature escaped everyone's notice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50bd040d2f8a47ae","term":"notice","forms":["notice","notices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公告；告示","explanation":"指寫出來或印出來、放在公共場所或發給一群人的資訊，目的是讓別人注意並瞭解某件事。","examples":[{"en":"A notice about the building repairs was posted near the entrance.","zh":"入口附近張貼了一張關於樓房維修的公告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the notice before using the swimming pool.","zh":"使用游泳池前請先閱讀公告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a75dcc54be395d7c","term":"notice","forms":["notice","notices","noticing","noticed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"注意到；察覺","explanation":"指透過看、聽或其他感知發現某人、某物或某個變化，是 notice 最常用的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Did you notice the new sign outside the station?","zh":"你注意到車站外面那塊新標牌了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I noticed that the door was still open.","zh":"我注意到門還開著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34b953d3ca4ee7c462e1","word":"noticeable","forms":["noticeable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8096685f06939f4","term":"noticeable","forms":["noticeable","more noticeable","most noticeable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯眼的；容易察覺的","explanation":"指某物、某種變化或某種效果很容易被看見、聽見或感覺到，因此會從背景中突出出來。它不一定特別重要，只要足夠明顯、難以忽略，就可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"There was a noticeable change in her voice after the long meeting.","zh":"長時間開會後，她的聲音有了明顯變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new sign is noticeable from across the street.","zh":"從街對面就能清楚地看到那個新標牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noticeable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-deee52b601685ce7","term":"noticeable","forms":["noticeable","more noticeable","most noticeable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯著的；值得注意的","explanation":"從“很容易被注意到”進一步發展為“程度很明顯、值得特別提出來”。這裡重點不只是看得見，而是某種差異、成績或影響已經突出到值得一提。","examples":[{"en":"The team has made a noticeable improvement this season.","zh":"這支隊伍本賽季取得了明顯進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There has been a noticeable improvement in water quality.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noticeable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cd6f41455d78245f129","word":"notify","forms":["notify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7e44c549905792e","term":"notify","forms":["notify","notifies","notifying","notified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"通知；告知","explanation":"把某個重要訊息正式傳達給某人或某個機構，尤其是讓對方知道某件事已經發生、需要處理或即將發生。","examples":[{"en":"Please notify the manager of any changes to the schedule.","zh":"如有任何日程變動，請通知經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital notified her that the test results were ready.","zh":"醫院通知她檢查結果已經出來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31f61ed3e6e210c5f3f7","word":"notion","forms":["notion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f3d0d7278402853","term":"notion","forms":["notion","notions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"想法；觀念","explanation":"指腦中對某件事形成的想法、觀念或概念，可以是已經想清楚的理解，也可以只是一個模糊的設想。這是notion最基本、最重要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She has a clear notion of what she wants to achieve.","zh":"她很清楚自己想實現什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The notion that money can solve every problem is unrealistic.","zh":"認為金錢能解決所有問題的想法是不現實的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5880d574f3513173","term":"notion","forms":["notion","notions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看法；意見","explanation":"指一個人對某人或某事的具體看法或意見。它仍然來自腦中的“想法”，但重點從一般觀念轉向個人的判斷，常可帶有贊成、懷疑或批評的語氣。","examples":[{"en":"I don't agree with his notion of success.","zh":"我不同意他對成功的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I disagree with the notion that silence means consent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa7859fadb201f6bb467","word":"notorious","forms":["notorious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d19f1b7b9575d749","term":"notorious","forms":["notorious","more notorious","most notorious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"臭名昭著的","explanation":"指某人或某事因為犯罪、醜聞、殘酷行為等壞事而廣為人知，也就是“臭名昭著”。這是 notorious 在現代英語中的主要意思。","examples":[{"en":"The company is notorious for exploiting its workers.","zh":"這家公司因剝削工人而臭名昭著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became notorious after the scandal.","zh":"那起醜聞之後，他變得臭名昭著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notorious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6ff76d0a02b7af23b0b","word":"nourish(ment)","forms":["nourish","nourishment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ce4533376081a16","term":"nourish","forms":["nourish","nourishes","nourishing","nourished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滋養；餵養","explanation":"給人、動物或植物提供食物和營養，使其長得更健康、更強壯；重點不只是“喂進去”，而是“供給後產生良好成長”。","examples":[{"en":"A balanced diet nourishes the body and supports healthy growth.","zh":"均衡的飲食能滋養身體，促進健康成長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rich soil nourished the young plants.","zh":"肥沃的土壤滋養了這些幼苗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nourish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-440c17345d3347d0","term":"nourish","forms":["nourish","nourishes","nourishing","nourished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支援；維持","explanation":"像持續供給養分一樣，為某人、某個群體或某項事業提供生存和發展的條件，並承擔維持它的責任。","examples":[{"en":"The small business nourishes several families in the village.","zh":"這家小企業養活了村裡的好幾個家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Daily conversations nourished their friendship across the distance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nourish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9dc7164418d5acd6","term":"nourishment","forms":["nourishment","nourishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滋養；營養狀態","explanation":"指給予營養、維持身體或精神的過程，也指接受這種滋養後的狀態。重點不在某一種具體食物，而在“得到支援、得到滋養”這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"Young plants need regular nourishment to grow strong.","zh":"幼苗需要持續的滋養才能茁壯成長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found emotional nourishment in her close friendships.","zh":"她從親密的友誼中獲得了情感上的滋養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nourishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0d8a75153357d32","term":"nourishment","forms":["nourishment","nourishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"營養物；食物","explanation":"指實際能夠滋養身體的東西，尤其是食物或飲料。這裡可以把 nourishment 看成“給身體加油時所用的燃料”，既可以泛指食物，也可以指某種具體的營養來源。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers carried enough nourishment for two days.","zh":"徒步旅行者帶了足夠兩天食用的食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soup provided warmth and nourishment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nourishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2110e6cf92b93ae7b8b","word":"novel","forms":["novel"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-988a652bf1aef903","term":"novel","forms":["novel","more novel","most novel"],"pos":"adj","zh":"新出現的；前所未有的","explanation":"指剛形成、剛發展出來，或過去沒有先例的事物；重點是“以前沒有這種東西或做法”。","examples":[{"en":"The team developed a novel method for cleaning polluted water.","zh":"這個團隊開發了一種清理汙染水的新方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment is novel and has not been tested widely.","zh":"這種治療方法是全新的，尚未得到廣泛測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/novel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-735b219fdf6c95d3","term":"novel","forms":["novel","more novel","most novel"],"pos":"adj","zh":"新穎而引人注意的","explanation":"指想法、方式或設計很有創意，因不同於普通做法而顯得新奇、有吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"She found a novel way to teach children about science.","zh":"她想出了一個新穎的方法來教孩子們科學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel design attracted a lot of attention.","zh":"這個新穎的設計吸引了很多關注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/novel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c45c1736e0355bfd","term":"novel","forms":["novel","novels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小說","explanation":"指以散文寫成、通常比短篇故事更長的虛構文學作品，包含人物、情節和較完整的故事世界。","examples":[{"en":"I stayed up late to finish the novel.","zh":"我熬夜讀完了這部小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her first novel won a major literary prize.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/novel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b905d20cdaf223f8f215","word":"novelist","forms":["novelist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6397191862fd8c5e","term":"novelist","forms":["novelist","novelists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小說家","explanation":"指創作小說的人，通常把小說寫作作為主要工作或身份。這個詞可以指知名作家，也可以指正在寫小說的人。","examples":[{"en":"She became a novelist after publishing her first book.","zh":"她出版第一本書後成了一名小說家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novelist is working on a new mystery.","zh":"這位小說家正在創作一部新的懸疑小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/novelist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d89400074e7763b004d5","word":"novice","forms":["novice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59fc657d4c64ed2b","term":"novice","forms":["novice","novices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新手；初學者","explanation":"指對某個學科、工作或活動還不熟悉、經驗較少的人；他還在“剛加入並學習”的階段，因此可以自然地延伸到各種領域。","examples":[{"en":"I'm a novice at coding, so I still make simple mistakes.","zh":"我是程式設計新手，所以還會犯一些簡單的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even a novice can follow these simple instructions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/novice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed5eb9a37e2d8231af33","word":"now","forms":["now"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-673f7d463378b196","term":"now","forms":["now"],"pos":"adv","zh":"現在；此刻","explanation":"指說話時正在發生或成立的時間點，是 now 最基本的意思。記住“時間線上被按住的此刻”，其他許多用法都從這裡發展出來。","examples":[{"en":"I can't talk now; I'm in a meeting.","zh":"我現在不能說話，我正在開會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Now the store is closed.","zh":"現在商店關門了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/now","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33b4d26e14ae5418","term":"now","forms":["now","nows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現在；當下","explanation":"把“現在”當作一個時間階段或當前時刻來談，而不是隻把它當作修飾動詞的副詞。它延續了核心的“被按住的此刻”這一畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Try to enjoy the now instead of worrying about tomorrow.","zh":"試著享受當下，不要一直擔心明天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Forget next year; let's concentrate on the now.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/now","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac6eb9b28a8c164f8012","word":"nowadays","forms":["nowadays"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f56dcc2040756868","term":"nowadays","forms":["nowadays"],"pos":"adv","zh":"如今；現在","explanation":"表示當前這個時代或現在的情況，常常帶有與過去作對照的意味。例如說如今汽車更高效，就是在把現在的汽車和過去的汽車相比。","examples":[{"en":"Cars nowadays are more efficient.","zh":"如今的汽車更加高效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nowadays, many people work from home.","zh":"如今，許多人在家辦公。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nowadays","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20aeff0494e828d188c7","word":"nowhere","forms":["nowhere"],"officialPos":"adv./pron.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e509354310d748f","term":"nowhere","forms":["nowhere"],"pos":"adv","zh":"哪裡都沒有","explanation":"表示某事沒有發生在任何地方，或某人、某物不在任何地方；核心畫面就是地圖上沒有一個地點符合條件。","examples":[{"en":"My keys are nowhere in the house.","zh":"我的鑰匙在屋裡任何地方都找不到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nowhere did the rules mention popcorn.","zh":"規則裡任何地方都沒有提到爆米花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nowhere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5aef42bb069f3ba3","term":"nowhere","forms":["nowhere"],"pos":"adv","zh":"沒有去處；毫無進展","explanation":"從“沒有目的地”發展而來，表示向哪裡都去不了，也常表示事情沒有進展、努力沒有結果。","examples":[{"en":"We drove for an hour but went nowhere.","zh":"我們開了一個小時的車，卻哪兒也沒去成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Arguing about it will get us nowhere.","zh":"爭論這件事不會讓我們取得任何進展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nowhere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-901ad244ed23ebc2c420","word":"nuclear","forms":["nuclear"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a05433756b5cb304","term":"nuclear","forms":["nuclear"],"pos":"adj","zh":"原子核的","explanation":"指與原子內部的原子核有關的，是 nuclear 最基礎的科學含義。由這個核心可以進一步理解核能和核武器等用法。","examples":[{"en":"The experiment measures nuclear reactions at very high temperatures.","zh":"這項實驗測量極高溫度下的核反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nuclear physics helps us understand how atoms are built.","zh":"核物理學幫助我們理解原子是如何構成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nuclear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-934243c9e928f5f9","term":"nuclear","forms":["nuclear"],"pos":"adj","zh":"核能的","explanation":"指透過裂變、聚變或放射性衰變等核反應釋放能量的事物，如核電站和核能源。它是“原子核釋放巨大能量”這一核心畫面的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The country plans to build a new nuclear power plant.","zh":"這個國家計劃建造一座新的核電站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nuclear energy can produce electricity without burning coal.","zh":"核能可以在不燃燒煤炭的情況下發電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nuclear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c798ac4211f6edb","term":"nuclear","forms":["nuclear"],"pos":"adj","zh":"核武器的","explanation":"指依靠核反應迅速釋放能量來造成破壞的武器或爆炸。它把“原子核釋放巨大能量”這一畫面用於軍事領域。","examples":[{"en":"The treaty limits the development of nuclear weapons.","zh":"這項條約限制核武器的研發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film begins with a nuclear explosion.","zh":"這部電影以一次核爆炸開場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nuclear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b933ef6f1f8c0d87e64b","word":"nucleus","forms":["nucleus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df901a8fdd1bace1","term":"nucleus","forms":["nucleus","nuclei","nucleuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"核心；中心部分","explanation":"指一個事物中最重要、最集中的部分，其他成員、要素或活動圍繞它組織起來。它可以是一個群體、地區、機構，也可以是一個觀點或系統的核心。","examples":[{"en":"The research team became the nucleus of a much larger project.","zh":"這個研究團隊成了一個規模大得多的專案的核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small group of volunteers formed the nucleus of the campaign.","zh":"一小群志願者構成了這場活動的核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nucleus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88500cfeac13f1a0","term":"nucleus","forms":["nucleus","nuclei","nucleuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最初基礎；雛形","explanation":"指一個還不完整的最初部分，後來會在它的基礎上繼續增加成員、內容或功能，逐漸發展成更大的整體。","examples":[{"en":"These books will form the nucleus of the school library.","zh":"這些書將成為學校圖書館的最初基礎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The first three members became the nucleus of the new organization.","zh":"最初的三名成員成了這個新組織的雛形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nucleus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdede6100c4745e5","term":"nucleus","forms":["nucleus","nuclei","nucleuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原子核","explanation":"指原子正中央的緻密部分，由帶正電的質子和不帶電的中子組成；原子的其他部分圍繞它存在。這個意思仍然保留了“位於中心、構成核心”的基本概念。","examples":[{"en":"Most of an atom's mass is concentrated in its nucleus.","zh":"原子的大部分質量集中在原子核中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Protons and neutrons occupy the atom's nucleus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nucleus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d92f4cf1e2d7e8129d75","word":"nude","forms":["nude"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2230ae2bf719db1b","term":"nude","forms":["nude","nuder","nudest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未著衣的；裸露的","explanation":"指身體沒有衣物或其他遮蓋，露出皮膚；這個概念是nude最直接、最核心的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The model stood nude in front of the blank canvas.","zh":"模特裸體站在空白畫布前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting depicts a nude figure beside a window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c679d406b43f4777","term":"nude","forms":["nude","nudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裸體人體藝術作品","explanation":"指以接近全裸或全裸的人體為主題的繪畫、雕塑、照片或其他藝術、媒體作品；這是“把裸露的人體定格下來”的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The gallery recently acquired a bronze nude by a local sculptor.","zh":"這家畫廊最近收藏了一件當地雕塑家的裸體青銅雕像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her first exhibition consisted entirely of expressive watercolor nudes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12886f9d00055adf24c4","word":"number","forms":["number"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af14c2dff3d15d43","term":"number","forms":["number","numbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數量","explanation":"指某類人或物有多少，重點在總量，而不是寫出來的某個數字。","examples":[{"en":"Any number of people can join the discussion.","zh":"許多人都可以參加討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The number of applicants increased sharply this year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/number","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4be234c92a19d40c","term":"number","forms":["number","numbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數；數量概念","explanation":"指用來表示多少的抽象數學物件，例如零、負數、小數或圓周率，而不只是寫出來的符號。","examples":[{"en":"Zero is a number, even though it means nothing is there.","zh":"零也是一個數，雖然它表示那裡什麼都沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Zero is a number, despite representing no quantity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/number","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe78c193a9bcc31b","term":"number","forms":["number","numbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數字；數碼","explanation":"指寫下來或印出來、用來表示非負整數的符號，例如數字8；它是抽象之“數”的外在寫法。","examples":[{"en":"Write the number 8 at the top of the page.","zh":"把數字8寫在紙的頂端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write each number in its own square.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/number","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d00fb01e13ff26f","term":"number","forms":["number","numbers","numbering","numbered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"數到；總數達到","explanation":"表示數出某群體有多少，或說明總數達到某個數量，是名詞“數量”義的動作化表達。","examples":[{"en":"The students number more than five hundred.","zh":"這些學生總數超過五百人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The colony now numbers more than five hundred birds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/number","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50206559c31fd34a","term":"number","forms":["number","numbers","numbering","numbered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編號","explanation":"表示給物品貼上或寫上數字標籤，使它們容易識別、查詢或按順序排列。","examples":[{"en":"Please number the boxes before you move them.","zh":"請先給這些箱子編號，再搬動它們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Number each page before printing the document.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/number","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecc62dd3e8533b5714f0","word":"numerous","forms":["numerous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0c3e2e18b0413b8","term":"numerous","forms":["numerous","more numerous","most numerous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量很多","explanation":"指數量大、數目多，但不說明具體有多少；可以說許多理由、問題、機會等。","examples":[{"en":"There are numerous reasons to protect the old building.","zh":"保護這座老建築有許多理由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Numerous visitors returned to the museum after it reopened.","zh":"博物館重新開放後，許多遊客又來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/numerous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f8a40e9bb0c4188","term":"numerous","forms":["numerous","more numerous","most numerous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"由許多個體或部分組成","explanation":"強調一個群體、集合或整體裡包含很多人、物或組成部分，重點從“數量很多”轉向“成員很多”。","examples":[{"en":"A numerous crowd gathered outside the theater.","zh":"劇院外聚集了一大群人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family was numerous enough to fill three tables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/numerous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e66f9e6444b4e6b13f86","word":"nun","forms":["nun"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7aff46af36a4ef17","term":"nun","forms":["nun","nuns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"修女","explanation":"指加入基督教女性修會、按一定宗教誓願生活的女性；在天主教語境中，通常還暗示她生活在修道院或隱修團體中。","examples":[{"en":"The nun greeted the children at the school gate.","zh":"那位修女在學校門口迎接孩子們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several nuns work at the hospital.","zh":"幾位修女在這家醫院工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d11fef545886835a","term":"nun","forms":["nun","nuns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"其他宗教的女性修行者","explanation":"在較寬泛的用法中，nun也可指其他宗教傳統裡類似修女的女性團體成員，例如佛教尼姑。","examples":[{"en":"The Buddhist nun teaches meditation to visitors.","zh":"那位佛教尼姑教來訪者打坐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A Buddhist nun led the morning meditation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-781e5116a1e14a34eada","word":"nurse","forms":["nurse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a6ffae7689a34bb","term":"nurse","forms":["nurse","nurses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"護士","explanation":"指在醫院、診所等場所直接護理病人的專業人員，是 nurse 最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse checked my temperature and changed the bandage.","zh":"護士給我量了體溫，還換了繃帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A nurse showed us how to use the new medicine.","zh":"一名護士教我們如何使用這種新藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nurse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0b8d5ad7580696d","term":"nurse","forms":["nurse","nurses","nursing","nursed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"護理；照料","explanation":"指在生病或虛弱時照顧某人，幫助其恢復健康；這是從“持續供養和照看”發展出的核心動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"His family nursed him back to health after the accident.","zh":"事故後，他的家人照料他，使他恢復了健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She nursed her sick father through the winter.","zh":"整個冬天她都在照料生病的父親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nurse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a22f4d79b88c12cc874b","word":"nursery","forms":["nursery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14896f9396e366b5","term":"nursery","forms":["nursery","nurseries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"育兒室；托兒場所","explanation":"指家中或機構裡照料、養育嬰幼兒的地方。它體現了 nursery 的核心概念：把需要照料的孩子放在一個安全的地方，讓他們成長。","examples":[{"en":"The baby is sleeping in the nursery.","zh":"嬰兒正在育兒室裡睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We left the children at the nursery while we went shopping.","zh":"我們去購物時把孩子們留在了託兒所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nursery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfdcaea6c956cd3f","term":"nursery","forms":["nursery","nurseries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孕育某物的地方","explanation":"比喻指培育某種事物、促進其成長的地方或環境，例如孕育藝術、思想或事業的城市和機構。這裡的“照料孩子”被擴大成“扶持任何事物成長”。","examples":[{"en":"The university became a nursery of new ideas.","zh":"這所大學成了新思想的孕育地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shallow bay serves as a nursery for young fish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nursery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a47bc2990e8dab02a033","word":"nurture","forms":["nurture"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41528c545f603749","term":"nurture","forms":["nurture","nurtures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滋養；照料","explanation":"指透過餵養、護理和關愛使人或生物得到健康成長的行為，重點是持續提供所需的照料。","examples":[{"en":"Children need love and nurture to grow into confident adults.","zh":"孩子需要愛與悉心照料，才能成長為自信的成年人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Young plants require careful nurture through the winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nurture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1187f2772e884f5b","term":"nurture","forms":["nurture","nurtures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"後天環境與教養","explanation":"指家庭、教育、社會環境等對一個人性格和能力發展的影響，強調後天培養，與先天因素相對。","examples":[{"en":"The debate asks whether talent comes from nature or nurture.","zh":"這場討論探究天賦究竟來自先天因素還是後天環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study examines how nature and nurture shape personality.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nurture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-072c38fe31bed2d6","term":"nurture","forms":["nurture","nurtures","nurturing","nurtured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"養育；滋養","explanation":"指給人或生物提供食物、照料和保護，使其能夠健康成長；也可用於使某物得到充分滋養。","examples":[{"en":"Good parents nurture their children with patience and care.","zh":"好的父母用耐心和關愛養育孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plant needs careful nurture during its first winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nurture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2347b30faa4759a5","term":"nurture","forms":["nurture","nurtures","nurturing","nurtured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"培育；促進發展","explanation":"指有意識地提供支援和條件，鼓勵某種能力、關係、想法或事業逐步發展起來，是“給幼苗澆水施肥”這一形象在抽象領域的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The school works hard to nurture students’ curiosity.","zh":"這所學校努力培養學生的好奇心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trust must be nurtured over time.","zh":"信任必須經過長期培養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nurture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7dfd8928a4a3162bbd66","word":"nut","forms":["nut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1eee8526a23ba7d5","term":"nut","forms":["nut","nuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅果；硬殼種子","explanation":"指許多植物結出的外殼堅硬、裡面可食用的種子或乾果；記住樹上那種堅硬、圓的東西，就是這個詞最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I keep a small bag of nuts in my desk.","zh":"我在辦公桌裡放著一小袋堅果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Peanuts and cashews are popular snack foods.","zh":"花生和腰果是很受歡迎的零食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b38a7eaff371fed","term":"nut","forms":["nut","nuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螺母","explanation":"指套在有螺紋的螺栓或螺桿上、透過旋緊來固定東西的金屬件；它正是“堅硬、能擰緊”的核心影象在五金中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Use a wrench to tighten the nut on the bolt.","zh":"用扳手把螺栓上的螺母擰緊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One of the nuts came loose during the trip.","zh":"旅途中有一個螺母鬆脫了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9a89614b9d06413","term":"nut","forms":["nut","nuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瘋子；魯莽的人","explanation":"口語中指行為瘋狂、魯莽或不理智的人；這是由“腦袋”這一聯想進一步引申出的意思。","examples":[{"en":"That nut drove through the red light.","zh":"那個瘋子闖了紅燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You'd have to be a nut to climb that wall without ropes.","zh":"不帶繩子爬那面牆，簡直得是個瘋子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20d542fc1254ee7428cf","word":"nutrient","forms":["nutrient"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16abac5e259adf86","term":"nutrient","forms":["nutrient","more nutrient","most nutrient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有營養的","explanation":"指能夠為身體或其他生物提供營養、幫助生長或維持活動的。它強調“能滋養身體”這一性質。","examples":[{"en":"This soup is simple but very nutrient.","zh":"這湯雖然簡單，但很有營養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Roots absorb water from the nutrient solution.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutrient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b5fe35da3bf6582","term":"nutrient","forms":["nutrient","nutrients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"營養物質","explanation":"指食物或其他來源中能被生物代謝利用的物質，用來提供能量、幫助生長或構成組織，例如食物中的各種營養成分。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh vegetables provide many important nutrients.","zh":"新鮮蔬菜能提供許多重要的營養物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roots absorb nutrients from the soil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutrient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-257c4a121ae568ba528f","word":"nutrition","forms":["nutrition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29923e49a9acf81d","term":"nutrition","forms":["nutrition","nutritions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"營養過程","explanation":"指生物攝取食物後，消化、吸收並利用其中物質來維持身體和促進生長的整個過程。重點不只是吃進去，而是身體如何把食物轉化為自身需要的養分。","examples":[{"en":"Good nutrition helps children grow strong and stay healthy.","zh":"良好的營養有助於孩子強壯成長並保持健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course explains how nutrition affects the human body.","zh":"這門課程講解營養如何影響人體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutrition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9256e99b9f90002e","term":"nutrition","forms":["nutrition","nutritions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滋養；養分","explanation":"指食物或其他來源所提供的、能滋養身體的東西；這裡關注的是“得到的滋養”，而不是身體處理食物的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The seeds provide nutrition for birds during the winter.","zh":"這些種子在冬天為鳥類提供滋養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roots absorb nutrition from the surrounding soil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutrition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4e986e60a0591bc033b","word":"nutritious","forms":["nutritious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46421bb8e7f50cf3","term":"nutritious","forms":["nutritious","more nutritious","most nutritious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有營養的","explanation":"指食物或飲料含有身體需要的營養，吃下或喝下後有助於保持健康。重點是營養價值，不只是好吃或能填飽肚子。","examples":[{"en":"A nutritious breakfast can help you stay focused all morning.","zh":"營養豐富的早餐能幫助你整個上午保持專注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We packed fruit, nuts, and other nutritious snacks for the trip.","zh":"我們為這次旅行準備了水果、堅果和其他有營養的零食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nutritious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-172cfd242641c055faca","word":"O.K./OK/okay","forms":["OK"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0bbbb778a50be8a","term":"OK","forms":["OK","more OK","OKer","most OK","OKest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可以；沒問題","explanation":"表示某事被允許、可以接受，或沒有造成問題；這是 OK 最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Is it OK if I open the window?","zh":"我開啟窗戶可以嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It’s OK to ask for help.","zh":"尋求幫助沒問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/OK","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c79ac6fa2aa5f882","term":"OK","forms":["OK","OKs","OK's","OKing","OK'ing","OKed","OK'd","OK'ed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"批准；接受","explanation":"作動詞時，表示對某項請求、計劃或安排點頭同意，讓它可以繼續進行。","examples":[{"en":"The director OK’d the new budget yesterday.","zh":"主任昨天批准了新預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you OK this request today?","zh":"你今天能批准這個請求嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/OK","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df877645404747cb7973","word":"oak","forms":["oak"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5313f66f7b2ccd47","term":"oak","forms":["oak","oaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橡樹","explanation":"指一種落葉樹，葉片通常有明顯的深裂，結橡果，木材堅硬；這是 oak 最基本的名詞意思。","examples":[{"en":"An old oak stood beside the farmhouse.","zh":"農舍旁邊有一棵老橡樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children collected acorns under the oak.","zh":"孩子們在橡樹下撿橡果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98244194245abc7c","term":"oak","forms":["oak","oaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橡木","explanation":"指橡樹的木材，常用於傢俱、地板和建築；這是從“橡樹”自然延伸出的材料意義。","examples":[{"en":"The floor is made of oak and has lasted for decades.","zh":"這地板是橡木做的，已經用了幾十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Oak is valued for its strength and durability.","zh":"橡木因堅固耐用而受到重視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e424db8e5664ade7622","word":"oasis","forms":["oasis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3291a8736529577","term":"oasis","forms":["oasis","oases","oasises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙漠綠洲","explanation":"指沙漠中有泉水或淡水、周圍長有植物的一片肥沃地區。它是“荒漠中突然出現的生機之地”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"After three days in the desert, the travelers finally reached an oasis.","zh":"在沙漠裡走了三天後，旅行者們終於到達了一片綠洲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Palm trees marked the location of the oasis.","zh":"棕櫚樹標出了綠洲的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oasis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-762a083cbec229f5","term":"oasis","forms":["oasis","oases","oasises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寧靜之處","explanation":"比喻喧鬧、緊張的周圍環境中一處安靜平和的地方或狀態，就像城市裡的“綠洲”。","examples":[{"en":"The small library is an oasis of calm in the busy station.","zh":"這座小圖書館是繁忙車站裡的一片寧靜之地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her garden became an oasis in the noisy neighborhood.","zh":"她的花園成了喧鬧社群中的一方寧靜天地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oasis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c044f5159556b36e9673","word":"oath","forms":["oath"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd522426c6231dda","term":"oath","forms":["oath","oaths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"莊嚴誓言","explanation":"指人在神明、統治者或其他被視為有權威的物件面前作出的莊嚴保證，表示自己會說真話或履行承諾。","examples":[{"en":"The witness took an oath to tell the truth.","zh":"證人宣誓要如實作證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They swore an oath to protect the village.","zh":"他們發誓要保護這個村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-941c5a140499504a","term":"oath","forms":["oath","oaths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誓言確認的宣告","explanation":"指經過宣誓而得到鄭重確認的具體宣告或承諾，例如就職時正式作出的保證。","examples":[{"en":"The new mayor read the oath of office aloud.","zh":"新市長大聲宣讀了就職誓詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness gave evidence under oath.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ee3dd007932cb1bec91","word":"oatmeal","forms":["oatmeal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1044e72801316ece","term":"oatmeal","forms":["oatmeal","oatmeals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燕麥粥","explanation":"指把燕麥加水或牛奶煮成的早餐食物，也就是最常見的“一碗燕麥粥”。它從燕麥原料進一步發展成了煮熟後的成品。","examples":[{"en":"I usually eat oatmeal with bananas for breakfast.","zh":"我通常早餐吃加香蕉的燕麥粥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He cooked oatmeal in the microwave before work.","zh":"上班前他用微波爐煮了燕麥粥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oatmeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2337a51926e18467d0ad","word":"obedience","forms":["obedience"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0d5561a4b6f3fdc","term":"obedience","forms":["obedience","obediences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服從；遵從","explanation":"指願意並能夠按照權威、規則或命令去做的品質或行為。它不只是聽見指示，而是實際接受並執行指示，是 obedience 的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"Obedience to the law is expected of every citizen.","zh":"每位公民都應當遵守法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer valued discipline and obedience.","zh":"這名軍官看重紀律和服從。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obedience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57e5f2fe0142f3c5cd74","word":"obedient","forms":["obedient"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6719ab3ceb592e3","term":"obedient","forms":["obedient","more obedient","most obedient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聽話的；服從的","explanation":"指一個人願意按照有權威者的命令、要求或指示去做，就像聽到指令便照做一樣。它強調服從行為，不單是態度友好或懂禮貌。","examples":[{"en":"The children were obedient to their teacher and followed the instructions carefully.","zh":"孩子們很聽老師的話，認真按照指示去做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is usually obedient, but he will speak up when he thinks a rule is unfair.","zh":"他通常很聽話，但覺得規則不公平時也會表達意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obedient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3a4871f647842ab36f9","word":"obey","forms":["obey"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3ceba6b837f9f1a","term":"obey","forms":["obey","obeys","obeying","obeyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"服從；遵守","explanation":"按照某個人、機構或規定提出的要求去行動。物件可以是發出命令的人，也可以是規則、法律等要求；重點是把自己的行為調整為符合要求。","examples":[{"en":"All visitors must obey the safety rules.","zh":"所有訪客都必須遵守安全規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child refused to obey his parents.","zh":"那個孩子拒絕聽從父母的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a376d7e9d87a5670","term":"obey","forms":["obey","obeys","obeying","obeyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"服從；聽從安排","explanation":"不明確說出物件時，表示按照別人告訴自己的事情去做，也就是服從、聽話。這裡的核心仍然是“聽到要求後照做”，而不是單純聽見聲音。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers are trained to obey without hesitation.","zh":"士兵們接受訓練，要毫不猶豫地服從命令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy still refuses to obey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2958d416d08aa5a472d7","word":"object","forms":["object"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72f4cdf764ee80e4","term":"object","forms":["object","objects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物體","explanation":"指有實際形體、但不是活物的東西，例如桌子、石頭或工具。這是object最具體、最容易掌握的意義。","examples":[{"en":"A strange object was lying on the road.","zh":"一件奇怪的物體躺在路上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A heavy object blocked the doorway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/object","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8b798ee8f04c9df","term":"object","forms":["object","objects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目標；目的","explanation":"指某個行動希望達到的目標或目的。它把“目標”看成擺在面前、引導行動的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The object of the meeting is to find a practical solution.","zh":"這次會議的目的是找到一個可行的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her main object was to protect the children.","zh":"她的主要目標是保護孩子們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/object","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42e877a890d58f69","term":"object","forms":["object","objects","objecting","objected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反對；提出異議","explanation":"表示不同意某個提議、行為或觀點，並把自己的反對意見明確地擋在對方面前。在法庭上，object還可作為簡短喊話，表示提出異議。","examples":[{"en":"Several residents objected to building the factory near the river.","zh":"幾位居民反對在河邊建廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"“Object!” the lawyer said when the question was asked.","zh":"問題提出後，律師說：“反對！”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/object","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4194b692f5789e4b2236","word":"objection","forms":["objection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bbb5e5f90d9ebc03","term":"objection","forms":["objection","objections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反對意見；反對理由","explanation":"objection 是對某項安排、觀點或行為表示反對的意見，也可以指支援這種反對的具體理由；核心畫面就是“站出來擋一下”。","examples":[{"en":"I have no objection to your working from home on Fridays.","zh":"我不反對你每週五在家辦公。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her main objection to the plan was its high cost.","zh":"她反對這項計劃的主要理由是成本太高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/objection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d454bec656d327234049","word":"objective","forms":["objective"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad27beecc9ad9b25","term":"objective","forms":["objective","more objective","most objective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不帶偏見的","explanation":"指判斷或態度不被強烈情緒、個人好惡或偏見左右，能夠儘量公平地看待事實。","examples":[{"en":"Try to remain objective when reviewing the complaints.","zh":"審查這些投訴時，儘量保持客觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An objective judge should consider all the evidence.","zh":"客觀的法官應當考慮所有證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/objective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b07946f5d0fd94a","term":"objective","forms":["objective","more objective","most objective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基於事實的","explanation":"指結論、標準或評價建立在觀察到的事實和可檢驗的證據上，而不是純粹憑個人感覺作出。","examples":[{"en":"The candidates were evaluated using objective criteria.","zh":"這些候選人是根據客觀標準進行評估的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need objective data before making a decision.","zh":"作出決定前，我們需要客觀資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/objective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f90185ec7caa68b5","term":"objective","forms":["objective","objectives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目標","explanation":"指一個人或組織努力想要實現、達到或完成的結果；也就是“朝著某個物件努力”時所指向的終點。","examples":[{"en":"Our main objective is to reduce waste.","zh":"我們的主要目標是減少浪費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team achieved its objective ahead of schedule.","zh":"團隊提前完成了目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/objective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df9a29a9b49e45d59d53","word":"obligation","forms":["obligation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66e16bbcfbb5b9da","term":"obligation","forms":["obligation","obligations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必須履行的責任或義務","explanation":"指社會、法律、道德、合同或承諾要求某人必須做或不得做的具體事情，是obligation最常用的意思。它可以來自外部規定，也可以來自自己作出的承諾。","examples":[{"en":"I feel under an obligation to tell her the truth.","zh":"我覺得自己有責任把真相告訴她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parents have an obligation to keep their children safe.","zh":"父母有責任保障孩子的安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obligation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f1fd1804b915281bda5","word":"oblige","forms":["oblige"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f462d2595e57a7a4","term":"oblige","forms":["oblige","obliges","obliging","obliged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使不得不；迫使承擔義務","explanation":"表示透過法律、道德、社會壓力或實際情況，使某人受到約束，不得不做某事。它對應記憶中的“義務繩子套在人身上”，不一定表示直接使用暴力。","examples":[{"en":"The new rule obliges all visitors to show identification.","zh":"新規定要求所有訪客出示身份證件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was obliged to cancel the trip because of the storm.","zh":"由於暴風雨，我不得不取消這次旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oblige","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27babeb57b893533","term":"oblige","forms":["oblige","obliges","obliging","obliged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"幫某人一個忙","explanation":"表示為某人做一件有幫助的事，彷彿先替對方承擔了一份“人情義務”。這裡不是迫使別人，而是滿足對方的請求或給對方方便。","examples":[{"en":"She obliged us by opening the shop a little early.","zh":"她幫了我們的忙，提前了一點開店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you oblige me by holding this ladder?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oblige","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-771ddab9b936047a7c44","word":"obscure","forms":["obscure"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bbc6ece18108ee76","term":"obscure","forms":["obscure","obscurer","more obscure","obscurest","most obscure"],"pos":"adj","zh":"昏暗；模糊","explanation":"指光線很弱，或某物的輪廓、細節因昏暗而難以看清。這是“被陰影遮住”的最具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"We walked through an obscure tunnel with only a small lamp.","zh":"我們走過一條昏暗的隧道，只有一盞小燈照明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mountains disappeared into the obscure evening light.","zh":"群山消失在昏暗的暮光中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obscure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7853bfacb578ffd6","term":"obscure","forms":["obscure","obscurer","more obscure","obscurest","most obscure"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難懂的；晦澀的","explanation":"指文字、觀點或說法像被陰影遮住一樣，含義不容易理解。它常用於文章、解釋、引用或表達，而不只是表示“很複雜”。","examples":[{"en":"The article contains several obscure references to medieval history.","zh":"這篇文章有幾處關於中世紀曆史的晦澀引文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His explanation was so obscure that nobody knew what he meant.","zh":"他的解釋太晦澀了，沒人知道他到底是什麼意思。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obscure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2df7808656e33c8","term":"obscure","forms":["obscure","obscures","obscuring","obscured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使模糊；遮暗；掩蓋","explanation":"指主動把光線、視線或含義遮住，使某物變得不清楚。它是形容詞核心畫面的主動版本：原本被遮住，現在有人或某物把它遮住。","examples":[{"en":"Thick smoke obscured the road ahead.","zh":"濃煙遮住了前方的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unnecessary details obscure the main point.","zh":"多餘的細節掩蓋了重點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obscure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-772c6953848bf5b19aed","word":"observation","forms":["observation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d96d543b02bc8f19","term":"observation","forms":["observation","observations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀察；觀察狀態","explanation":"指仔細地看、留意某人或某事這一行為，也可以指某人或某物處在被觀察的狀態。它是整組意思的起點：先看，才有後面的記錄、評論和判斷。","examples":[{"en":"Careful observation of the birds revealed a change in their behavior.","zh":"仔細觀察這些鳥後，我們發現它們的行為發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient remains under observation overnight.","zh":"這名病人整晚仍在接受觀察。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbc43bcd50b6795d","term":"observation","forms":["observation","observations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀察記錄","explanation":"指把觀察到的事件、現象或變化記下來的行為，也可以指記下來的記錄。也就是說，觀察不只停留在“看”，還留下了可以檢查或使用的資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers recorded each observation in a notebook.","zh":"研究人員把每次觀察結果都記在筆記本上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her observations of the children helped the teacher understand the problem.","zh":"她對孩子們的觀察記錄幫助老師理解了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-74e892c91130daa5e9c5","word":"observe","forms":["observe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a446a364e8f249d8","term":"observe","forms":["observe","observes","observing","observed","observest","observedst","observeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細觀察；注意到","explanation":"指帶著注意力去看、研究某人或某物，重點是認真觀察細節，而不只是隨便看一眼。這個意思最直接地保留了“守著看”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers observed the birds for several hours.","zh":"研究人員觀察了這些鳥好幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She observed that the child was unusually quiet.","zh":"她注意到那個孩子異常安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-700a3b0d2caaa53d","term":"observe","forms":["observe","observes","observing","observed","observest","observedst","observeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵守；遵循","explanation":"指像守著某種規定一樣照做，遵守法律、規則、習俗或宗教要求。這裡不是“觀察規則”，而是“按規則行動”。","examples":[{"en":"All visitors must observe the museum's safety rules.","zh":"所有訪客都必須遵守博物館的安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors must observe the monastery's rules of silence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e41f1d834710df8c7bc2","word":"observer","forms":["observer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d636b0df0f926b0","term":"observer","forms":["observer","observers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀察者；留意情況的人","explanation":"指認真觀察、監測或注意某件事的人，重點是透過觀看和留意形成判斷，而不一定承擔正式職務。","examples":[{"en":"Several observers noticed that the team was losing confidence.","zh":"幾位觀察者注意到，這支隊伍正在失去信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As an observer of local politics, she writes a weekly analysis.","zh":"作為地方政治的觀察者，她每週撰寫一篇分析。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6dd796c616ad5821","term":"observer","forms":["observer","observers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀察員；監督代表","explanation":"指被派到會議、選舉或其他活動現場進行監督和了解情況的代表，通常可以旁聽或報告，但不直接參加決策。","examples":[{"en":"The organization sent observers to monitor the election.","zh":"該組織派出觀察員監督這次選舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Observers were allowed to attend the meeting but could not vote.","zh":"觀察員獲准參加會議，但不能投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1190a77216baaa019ea2","word":"obsess","forms":["obsess"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71c571389f9b71e8","term":"obsess","forms":["obsess","obsesses","obsessing","obsessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"被某事佔據心思","explanation":"指某人被一個想法、情緒或事物牢牢佔住注意力，腦子總離不開它；重點是“人被纏住”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Mia is obsessed with collecting old postcards.","zh":"米婭痴迷於收集舊明信片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became obsessed with the idea of moving abroad.","zh":"他開始滿腦子都是搬到國外去的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obsess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa623373572590d3","term":"obsess","forms":["obsess","obsesses","obsessing","obsessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"佔滿某人的思想","explanation":"指某個念頭、問題或事物反過來支配一個人的思想，使對方清醒時幾乎總會想到它；這裡強調“它在影響人”。","examples":[{"en":"The unanswered question obsessed her for weeks.","zh":"那個沒有答案的問題讓她幾個星期都無法釋懷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The idea of finding the lost ship began to obsess her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obsess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b42a5cb0b08bd6351b3b","word":"obstacle","forms":["obstacle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c2c4e9bc8c495ec","term":"obstacle","forms":["obstacle","obstacles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"障礙；阻礙","explanation":"指擋住某人或某事、使行動變慢或難以取得進展的東西。它可以是路上的實物，也可以是糟糕的說明、缺少資金等抽象因素。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of experience was the biggest obstacle to finding a job.","zh":"缺乏經驗是找工作時最大的障礙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fallen tree became an obstacle on the narrow road.","zh":"倒下的樹成了狹窄道路上的障礙物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obstacle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-977b51546403b0ab5777","word":"obstinate","forms":["obstinate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"obstinate","forms":["obstinate"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"固執的；頑固的","examples":[{"en":"The obstinate child refused to put on a coat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We could not persuade the obstinate owner to sell the land.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf3c3437a865359b6bdb","word":"obtain","forms":["obtain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61f7d143b4273c07","term":"obtain","forms":["obtain","obtains","obtaining","obtained","obtainest","obtainedst","obtaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取得；獲得","explanation":"表示透過申請、努力、購買或其他方式把某物拿到手，常用於許可、證件、資訊、資源或機會等。","examples":[{"en":"Applicants must obtain a permit before construction.","zh":"申請人必須在施工前取得許可證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She obtained the information from a public database.","zh":"她從一個公開資料庫中獲取了這條資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obtain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-deda93f8a70667e0","term":"obtain","forms":["obtain","obtains","obtaining","obtained","obtainest","obtainedst","obtaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成立；有效；存在","explanation":"在正式或學術語境中，表示某種情況、規則、條件或觀點成立並持續有效；也可以理解為這種狀態在現實中“站得住”。","examples":[{"en":"The same rules obtain in all three regions.","zh":"同樣的規則在這三個地區都適用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Different rules obtain outside the city boundary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obtain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81dcf73d98053ac41c7b","word":"obvious","forms":["obvious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5dcc592c283a527","term":"obvious","forms":["obvious","more obvious","most obvious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明顯的；顯而易見的","explanation":"某件事就像擺在眼前一樣，很容易被看見、發現或理解，不需要別人再詳細解釋。","examples":[{"en":"It was obvious that she had forgotten the meeting.","zh":"很明顯，她忘了這次會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The answer is obvious from the first paragraph.","zh":"從第一段就能明顯看出答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/obvious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99fd0b148570ac9770e7","word":"occasion","forms":["occasion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-173da360f7999a98","term":"occasion","forms":["occasion","occasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機會；時機","explanation":"指適合做某事、值得抓住的機會，重點在於時機恰當而且有利。","examples":[{"en":"This is a perfect occasion to thank everyone who helped us.","zh":"這是感謝所有幫助過我們的人的絕佳機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reunion gave us occasion to discuss old times.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c585ae34b65b93e","term":"occasion","forms":["occasion","occasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發生某事的時刻；這一次","explanation":"指某件事發生的那個時間或具體情境，也就是“事情落到眼前的節點”。","examples":[{"en":"On this occasion, we decided to stay at home.","zh":"這一次，我們決定待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was unusually quiet on that occasion.","zh":"那一次她異常安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcc4292c3e271e79","term":"occasion","forms":["occasion","occasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特殊場合；特別活動","explanation":"指值得特別對待的活動或場合，例如慶祝、正式聚會或重要家庭事件；因為這個節點特別，所以本身成了“一個場合”。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a cake for the occasion.","zh":"我們為這個特殊場合買了一個蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They hired a photographer for the special occasion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b46253821445b83b9e86","word":"occasional","forms":["occasional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f934644c78755a8f","term":"occasional","forms":["occasional","more occasional","most occasional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"偶爾的；不常發生的","explanation":"指某事不經常發生，只是在一段時間裡偶爾出現。它把“occasion”這個時機的概念擴充套件為：事情不是日常固定發生，而是有時才出現。","examples":[{"en":"We still have the occasional argument, but we get along well.","zh":"我們偶爾還是會爭吵，但相處得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An occasional delay is unavoidable during the winter.","zh":"冬天偶爾出現延誤是無法避免的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occasional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-689e112bc3a0012e","term":"occasional","forms":["occasional","more occasional","most occasional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"為特定場合而作的","explanation":"指某件作品、物品或活動是為了某個特別場合而創作或安排的，而不是平時一般使用的。這裡的重點從“偶爾出現”轉為“由某個場合觸發”。","examples":[{"en":"She wrote an occasional poem for the school's anniversary.","zh":"她為學校週年紀念活動寫了一首專門的詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The composer's occasional music marked royal weddings and public anniversaries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occasional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3d7f19555f1d2f0722c7","word":"occupation","forms":["occupation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f068e7c7844a9208","term":"occupation","forms":["occupation","occupations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業；工作","explanation":"指一個人平時從事、通常以此獲得報酬的工作、行業或職業。它也可以泛指用來打發或安排時間的活動，但在個人資料中通常首先理解為“職業”。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your occupation on the application form.","zh":"請在申請表上填寫你的職業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Painting began as a hobby but became her full-time occupation.","zh":"繪畫起初只是她的愛好，後來成了她的全職工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occupation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a96a3f58b1572a49","term":"occupation","forms":["occupation","occupations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍事佔領","explanation":"指敵對的軍隊或準軍事力量控制並佔據一個國家或地區，通常持續一段時間。它仍然保留“佔住一個地方”的核心畫面，但控制者和政治、軍事背景更加明確。","examples":[{"en":"The city suffered greatly during the enemy occupation.","zh":"這座城市在敵軍佔領期間遭受了嚴重苦難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The occupation lasted until the foreign troops withdrew.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occupation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18e3ae4efaddf07c4780","word":"occupy","forms":["occupy"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2bbb46eb9283bea0","term":"occupy","forms":["occupy","occupies","occupying","occupied","occupiest","occupieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"佔用時間或資源","explanation":"指某件事佔用了某段時間、注意力或其他可用資源，重點是這些資源被它佔住了。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting occupied most of my afternoon.","zh":"這場會議佔用了我下午的大部分時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reading occupied her while she waited.","zh":"她等待時靠閱讀打發時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occupy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c000a94190cd25f","term":"occupy","forms":["occupy","occupies","occupying","occupied","occupiest","occupieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"佔據空間或地點","explanation":"指人、物或建築佔住一定的空間、面積或地點，就像把那塊地方填滿或控制住。","examples":[{"en":"The new desks occupy too much space in the classroom.","zh":"這些新課桌佔用了教室裡太多空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A large oak tree occupies the center of the garden.","zh":"一棵大橡樹佔據了花園中央的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occupy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-def696de03d9fc35566f","word":"occur","forms":["occur"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ea1ebad30de6d68","term":"occur","forms":["occur","occurs","occurring","occurred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發生；發生在","explanation":"某件事情“跑來與你相遇”，也就是在某個時間或地點發生、進行。它常用於事件、變化、事故或過程，而不是表示某人主動做某事。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting will occur next Monday.","zh":"會議將於下週一舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most accidents occur at night.","zh":"大多數事故發生在夜間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55aa38237b6112c7","term":"occur","forms":["occur","occurs","occurring","occurred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想到；出現在腦海中","explanation":"一個想法或記憶像是跑進某人的腦海，因此表示“某人突然想到某事”。重點是想法自己出現，而不是某人主動努力地思考它。","examples":[{"en":"It suddenly occurred to me that I had left my keys at work.","zh":"我突然想到，我把鑰匙落在單位了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A better solution occurred to her during the discussion.","zh":"討論過程中，她突然想到了一個更好的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5363303936b0117594a9","word":"occurrence","forms":["occurrence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f02ff71660a68b68","term":"occurrence","forms":["occurrence","occurrences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次實際發生的事件","explanation":"指某種情況、事件或現象在現實中實際發生的一次。它可以是單獨的一件事，也可以是某種現象反覆出現中的一次，例如停電、事故或季節性霧霾。","examples":[{"en":"Power cuts are a common occurrence during the summer storms.","zh":"夏季暴風雨期間，停電是很常見的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unusual occurrence was reported to the local authorities.","zh":"這起不同尋常的事件已報告給當地政府部門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/occurrence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47afad612b1f9cc8fd0a","word":"ocean","forms":["ocean"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22ba58cc7756a109","term":"ocean","forms":["ocean","oceans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海洋","explanation":"ocean指分隔大陸的巨大水域，如大西洋、太平洋等。它比一般的“海”更強調範圍廣大。","examples":[{"en":"The Atlantic Ocean separates Europe from North America.","zh":"大西洋把歐洲和北美洲分隔開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They sailed across the ocean for two weeks.","zh":"他們橫渡海洋航行了兩週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ocean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-239ef242a0e8d83f","term":"ocean","forms":["ocean","oceans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海水","explanation":"ocean也可以不強調某一片海域，而是指屬于海洋的水，突出周圍全是海水的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The small island is surrounded by ocean.","zh":"這座小島四周都是海水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wave spilled ocean into the little boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ocean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5633c9b8af6d089859af","word":"octopus","forms":["octopus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-809d0570ed7a9065","term":"octopus","forms":["octopus","octopuses","octopusses","octopi","octopii","octopodes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"章魚這種動物","explanation":"指生活在海里的八腕軟體動物，腕上有許多吸盤，通常沒有像貝殼那樣的外部硬殼或骨骼。這是這個詞最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw an octopus hiding under a rock.","zh":"我們看見一隻章魚藏在岩石下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The octopus changed color as it moved across the sand.","zh":"章魚在沙地上移動時改變了顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/octopus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ef2b060b4ca5256","term":"octopus","forms":["octopus","octopuses","octopusses","octopi","octopii","octopodes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"章魚肉","explanation":"指作為食物的章魚肉，重點不在活的動物，而在被烹調或食用的肉。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves grilled octopus with lemon.","zh":"這家餐館供應配檸檬的烤章魚肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tender octopus is the main ingredient in this traditional stew.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/octopus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-990cb8ebd0afb7150da4","word":"odd","forms":["odd"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e966d7483f14382","term":"odd","forms":["odd","odder","oddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇怪的；不尋常的","explanation":"表示某人或某事偏離平常、預期或一般規則，讓人覺得奇怪。它是從“和通常模式不合拍”這一核心概念發展出來的最常見用法。","examples":[{"en":"She slept in, which was very odd.","zh":"她睡過頭了，這很不尋常。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was odd that nobody answered the door.","zh":"沒人來開門，這很奇怪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e45f6d8a0293c22c","term":"odd","forms":["odd","odder","oddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不成對的；落單的","explanation":"指沒有相應同伴、無法和另一個東西組成一對的東西，也可指一對東西彼此不匹配。它直接體現了“偏離成對狀態”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I found an odd sock under the bed.","zh":"我在床底下找到了一隻落單的襪子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gloves are an odd pair.","zh":"這副手套不是一對相配的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f8bfb8c69d8d15e","term":"odd","forms":["odd","odder","oddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"成組後剩下的；落單的","explanation":"指其他東西已經配對或分組後，最後剩下、不能歸入完整組的那個。這裡的“剩下”就是落單概念的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Three children wore blue shirts, and Tom was the odd one out.","zh":"三個孩子穿藍色襯衫，湯姆是唯一不同的那個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An odd sock lay beside three matching pairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67329d5b847d81ff","term":"odd","forms":["odd","odder","oddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇數的","explanation":"在數學中指不能被二整除的整數，如一、三、五。它把“不能被整齊地分成兩組”這一落單概念變成了數字規則。","examples":[{"en":"Seven is an odd number.","zh":"七是奇數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The product of two odd numbers is odd.","zh":"兩個奇數的乘積是奇數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1fd5faa9b5cf91c2156a","word":"odds","forms":["odds"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea341df807cc2e4e","term":"odds","forms":["odds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相對可能性","explanation":"odds 表示某件事發生的可能性與它不發生的可能性之間的相對比例，也就是這架“可能性天平”哪一邊更佔優勢。它不只是說事情“有可能”，而是把兩種相反結果放在一起比較。","examples":[{"en":"The odds of finding a seat on the late train are low.","zh":"在晚班火車上找到座位的可能性很低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The odds are in our favor if the weather stays clear.","zh":"如果天氣保持晴朗，形勢就對我們有利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odds","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffea5d7935d9170a","term":"odds","forms":["odds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下注賠率","explanation":"在博彩中，odds 是按照賭注計算的潛在贏款比例：賠率越高，通常表示結果越不被看好，但押中後的回報也可能更大。這裡仍然保留了“雙方不均衡”的核心畫面，只是天平的一邊變成了賭注，另一邊變成了回報。","examples":[{"en":"The odds on the favorite were too short for me to place a bet.","zh":"熱門選手的賠率太低了，我不值得為此下注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bookmaker offered odds of ten to one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odds","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e180d5acd4e7876ee48","word":"odor","forms":["odor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66399231ea646452","term":"odor","forms":["odor","odors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氣味","explanation":"指任何能被聞到的氣味，不限定是香的還是臭的。它就像從某個物體中散出的看不見的東西，因此可以談某種東西的氣味，也可以單獨談空氣中的氣味。","examples":[{"en":"The odor of fresh bread filled the kitchen.","zh":"新鮮麵包的香味充滿了廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a strange odor coming from the basement.","zh":"地下室裡飄來一股奇怪的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-080ebfbc83b0e32a","term":"odor","forms":["odor","odors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瀰漫的氣息；意味","explanation":"把真實氣味的形象用於抽象事物，表示某種感覺、特徵或氛圍彷彿瀰漫在周圍。例如，欺騙、腐敗或衰敗可以被寫成某處散發出的氣息。","examples":[{"en":"The proposal carried an odor of dishonesty.","zh":"這項提議帶有一種不誠實的意味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An odor of suspicion surrounded the hurried transaction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28391d3bc64ec15cbb09","word":"of","forms":["of"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6f3d3db535cc30a","term":"of","forms":["of"],"pos":"prep","zh":"來自；具有……的來源","explanation":"of表示某人、某物或某個詞從哪裡來，說明來源、出身或起源。它把物件連回其來源地或來源類別。","examples":[{"en":"This custom is of ancient origin.","zh":"這個習俗源自古代。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She comes of a family of skilled weavers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/of","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74dc3c8ad10b507f","term":"of","forms":["of"],"pos":"prep","zh":"由……製成","explanation":"of表示某物的材料或組成成分，說明它是由什麼做成的。這條關係線把成品連到構成它的材料。","examples":[{"en":"The frame is made of lightweight metal.","zh":"這個框架由輕質金屬製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gate was made of solid oak.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/of","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78bcb56928291481","term":"of","forms":["of"],"pos":"prep","zh":"屬於；……的","explanation":"of可以表示所屬、歸屬或某人某物與另一個名詞之間的關係，常相當於漢語的“的”。它把事物連到擁有者、所屬群體或時代等參照物上。","examples":[{"en":"The roof of the house needs repairing.","zh":"這所房子的屋頂需要修理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The handle of my suitcase snapped at the airport.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/of","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4dc66dde806261bdda8","word":"off","forms":["off"],"officialPos":"adv./prep./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc9d0c0bc9eb55e8","term":"off","forms":["off","more off","most off"],"pos":"adj","zh":"關閉的；停止運作的","explanation":"把它理解成從“運作狀態”移開：裝置、燈或電源沒有在工作，處於關閉或停用狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The lights are off, so nobody is in the office.","zh":"燈都關著，所以辦公室裡沒人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Make sure the oven is off before leaving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/off","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af2e464621814cfd","term":"off","forms":["off"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向外；離開","explanation":"表示從說話者或其他參照點移開，核心仍是“從原來的位置離開”。","examples":[{"en":"The train pulled off just as we reached the platform.","zh":"我們剛到站臺，火車就開走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He waved once and hurried off.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/off","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58427e8dbcccc9e6","term":"off","forms":["off"],"pos":"prep","zh":"離開表面或位置","explanation":"表示人或物已經從某個表面、位置或支撐處移開，正體現了“從原來的位置移開”。","examples":[{"en":"Please get off the wet pavement before you slip.","zh":"請先離開溼滑的人行道，免得滑倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat jumped off the kitchen counter.","zh":"貓從廚房操作檯上跳了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/off","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4240ac38a1a57c197a0d","word":"offend","forms":["offend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b15b9054a569fb58","term":"offend","forms":["offend","offends","offending","offended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒犯；惹怒","explanation":"指某人的話、行為或態度傷害了他人的感情，使對方不高興、受辱或生氣。重點是撞上了對方心裡的界線。","examples":[{"en":"I hope my question didn't offend you.","zh":"希望我的問題沒有冒犯你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His rude comments offended several guests.","zh":"他無禮的評論冒犯了幾位客人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72f89f8432e314802936","word":"offense","forms":["offense"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb220b407a030999","term":"offense","forms":["offense","offenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冒犯行為","explanation":"指使別人感到被冒犯的行為，重點在“做了什麼”這一動作本身。它可以是失禮的舉動，也可以泛指越過某種界線、造成冒犯的行為。","examples":[{"en":"His rude joke was an offense to everyone at the table.","zh":"他的粗魯玩笑冒犯了在場的每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She apologized for causing offense with her comment.","zh":"她為自己的話造成冒犯而道歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0050e0cae4e4006e","term":"offense","forms":["offense","offenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不快；被冒犯的感覺","explanation":"指一個人因為受到冒犯而產生的惱怒、不快或不滿，重點在“感覺如何”，而不是冒犯行為本身。可以把它理解為“被撞到界線後心裡產生的反應”。","examples":[{"en":"I hope you won't take offense at my question.","zh":"希望你不會因為我的問題而感到不快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took offense at the suggestion that she was careless.","zh":"有人暗示她粗心，這讓她感到被冒犯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-952be7cef84694e12546","word":"offensive","forms":["offensive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c0b9504fe0a8227","term":"offensive","forms":["offensive","more offensive","most offensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人冒犯的","explanation":"指某種言語、行為或內容衝擊人的感受，使人感到厭惡、憤怒、憎惡、悲傷或義憤；也就是“力量衝到情緒上”。","examples":[{"en":"Many viewers found the advertisement offensive.","zh":"許多觀眾覺得這則廣告很冒犯人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His offensive language prompted several guests to leave.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d3646a44d07f414","term":"offensive","forms":["offensive","more offensive","most offensive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"進攻性的","explanation":"指用於攻擊、主動推進或打擊對手的一方，與防禦性的相對；這裡“向外衝”的力量指向敵人或對手。","examples":[{"en":"The country has increased its offensive capabilities.","zh":"這個國家增強了自己的進攻能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The commander ordered an offensive maneuver at dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offensive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-988180bf0c9328c9e8bd","word":"offer","forms":["offer"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b44dc927c1a4620d","term":"offer","forms":["offer","offers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提議；條件","explanation":"offer 是一方主動遞出的提議或安排，通常等著另一方接受、拒絕或繼續商量；求職、幫助和交易中都很常見。","examples":[{"en":"She received a job offer from a small design studio.","zh":"她收到了一家小型設計工作室的工作邀請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I accepted his offer to drive me home.","zh":"我接受了他送我回家的提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-024d0c3b0f3f30b6","term":"offer","forms":["offer","offers","offering","offered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"主動提出做某事","explanation":"offer to do something 表示主動表示願意做某事，核心是把自己的幫助或行動遞給對方選擇。","examples":[{"en":"Tom offered to carry the heavy box upstairs.","zh":"湯姆主動提出把那個重箱子搬到樓上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I offered to call the restaurant for her.","zh":"我主動提出幫她給餐館打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3bdc3157d51c0e0","term":"offer","forms":["offer","offers","offering","offered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提出意見或建議","explanation":"offer something 可以表示把一句話、一個意見或一個建議遞出來供別人考慮，而不只是遞出實物。","examples":[{"en":"Several students offered useful suggestions during the meeting.","zh":"幾名學生在會議期間提出了有用的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She offered her opinion only after everyone else had spoken.","zh":"她等其他人都發言後才提出自己的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9dc9f65b0c93842","term":"offer","forms":["offer","offers","offering","offered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提供給某人選擇","explanation":"offer 某物給某人，表示把它放到對方面前，讓對方決定接受還是拒絕；物件可以是物品、使用權、機會或善意。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel offered us a free shuttle to the airport.","zh":"那家酒店為我們提供了免費的機場接送車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He offered his seat to an elderly passenger.","zh":"他把座位讓給了一位年長乘客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5691093abe2dd0a51a92","word":"offering","forms":["offering"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af7fba4144584089","term":"offering","forms":["offering","offerings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提供；提出這一動作","explanation":"這裡的 offering 把 offer 的“遞出去、提供或提出”變成一個名詞，指這一動作本身。例如，提供幫助這一行為可以被當作一個整體來談。","examples":[{"en":"The offering of free advice is part of her job.","zh":"提供免費建議是她工作的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The offering of an apology helped calm the dispute.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offering","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5cc3f82838ba7260203e","word":"office","forms":["office"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b20bad9b0483b81","term":"office","forms":["office","offices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負責某事的職務","explanation":"指一個人承擔責任、履行職責的正式職位。它強調“這個職位要負責什麼”，所以和辦公室這一空間義有“工作的載體”這一共同核心。","examples":[{"en":"The office of director carries a great deal of responsibility.","zh":"主任這一職務承擔著很大的責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She accepted the office of treasurer last month.","zh":"她上個月接受了財務主管這一職務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/office","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fa1ae555465fb6c","term":"office","forms":["office","offices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公職或高階職位","explanation":"特指政府或其他正式機構中的職位，以及擔任該職位的任期。它既可以指職位本身，也可以指一個人是否仍在任。","examples":[{"en":"He left office after the election.","zh":"選舉後他離開了公職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several candidates are running for office.","zh":"幾名候選人正在競選公職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/office","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a12fa94b122e341","term":"office","forms":["office","offices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辦公室或辦公場所","explanation":"指人們從事非體力工作的房間、幾間房或一棟建築。它是最常見的現代具體義：工作的職責被放在一個固定空間裡。","examples":[{"en":"I left my notebook at the office.","zh":"我把筆記本落在辦公室了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She goes to the office by train.","zh":"她坐火車去辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/office","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3671f1ce3678c476","term":"office","forms":["office","offices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辦公軟體套裝","explanation":"指把文書處理、電子表格、簡報等辦公程式集中在一起的一套軟體。它是“數字辦公室”：把完成日常辦公職責所需的工具放在同一套系統中。","examples":[{"en":"The school provides office software for all its students.","zh":"學校為所有學生提供辦公軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I use an office suite to write reports and make presentations.","zh":"我用辦公軟體套裝寫報告和製作簡報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/office","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d71f0bd623e5e0b40eb4","word":"officer","forms":["officer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f083007e857d9005","term":"officer","forms":["officer","officers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"官員；軍警人員","explanation":"officer 是組織中被授予一定權力和責任、可以代表組織辦事的人，最常見於軍隊、警察或政府機構。","examples":[{"en":"A police officer stopped us outside the station.","zh":"一名警察在車站外攔住了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer explained the new safety rules.","zh":"那名官員解釋了新的安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/officer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4b49653002dbec0","term":"officer","forms":["officer","officers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對警察等官員的禮貌稱呼","explanation":"在直接對警察或其他執法人員說話時，Officer 可以作為禮貌而正式的稱呼，類似於“警官”。","examples":[{"en":"Officer, I think you dropped your notebook.","zh":"警官，我想您把筆記本掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Officer, someone has broken into my car.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/officer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6896191a14f6c66534ba","word":"official","forms":["official"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-87d0330d97ac9339","term":"official","forms":["official","more official","most official"],"pos":"adj","zh":"官方釋出的","explanation":"表示資訊、檔案或行動來自有權機關，或者由相應負責人正式作出，因此具有權威性。","examples":[{"en":"The ministry issued an official statement this morning.","zh":"該部門今天上午釋出了一份官方宣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are waiting for the official report.","zh":"我們正在等待正式報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/official","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c733440b143f7fed","term":"official","forms":["official","more official","most official"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獲授權的","explanation":"表示某項計劃、版本、名稱或做法已經得到相關機構的認可，可以作為正式標準使用。","examples":[{"en":"This is the official guide to the new software.","zh":"這是這款新軟體的官方指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the official entrance beside the guardhouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/official","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1078c99de9b8b3e","term":"official","forms":["official","officials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"官員；裁判","explanation":"指代表政府、組織或比賽機構履行正式職責的人，例如政府官員、體育裁判或負責執行規則的工作人員。","examples":[{"en":"A government official confirmed the new travel rules.","zh":"一名政府官員確認了新的旅行規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The match officials stopped the game because of the rain.","zh":"比賽裁判因下雨暫停了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/official","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01d4a0fcebc9e5a1a3a8","word":"offshore","forms":["offshore"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c6b1ba8e0abce888","term":"offshore","forms":["offshore"],"pos":"adj","zh":"位於海岸外的","explanation":"指位於離海岸有一段距離的海面上，而不是緊靠岸邊；海上石油平臺就是典型例子。","examples":[{"en":"The company operates an offshore wind farm.","zh":"這家公司經營一個海上風電場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several boats are working in offshore waters.","zh":"幾艘船正在近海以外的海域作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offshore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c9c0b832324cdfa","term":"offshore","forms":["offshore"],"pos":"adj","zh":"設在國外的；境外的","explanation":"指公司、服務或生產活動設在另一個國家，通常是為了利用較低的勞動力成本、稅收或其他經營條件。","examples":[{"en":"The company moved some of its production to an offshore facility.","zh":"這家公司把部分生產轉移到了境外工廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many banks offer offshore accounts to international clients.","zh":"許多銀行為國際客戶提供境外賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offshore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cf5ee09cea1b23e5ea2","word":"offspring","forms":["offspring"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-676e4f9d08e832f3","term":"offspring","forms":["offspring","offsprings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"子女；孩子","explanation":"指某人的兒子或女兒，強調親子關係。它可以泛指一個人的孩子，也可以把多個孩子作為一個整體來談。","examples":[{"en":"The couple brought their offspring to the family gathering.","zh":"這對夫婦帶著他們的孩子參加了家庭聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes her offspring will grow up kind and confident.","zh":"她希望自己的孩子善良而自信地長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offspring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8564a6df463c38c","term":"offspring","forms":["offspring","offsprings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"後代；子孫","explanation":"指某人的後代，可以包括子女、孫輩以及更遠的世代；範圍比只指孩子更廣。","examples":[{"en":"The old explorer left his fortune to his offspring.","zh":"那位老探險家把財產留給了自己的後代。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The couple's offspring settled on three different continents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/offspring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93c68148f4acfe0d7284","word":"often","forms":["often"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f60d07e62763023","term":"often","forms":["often","more often","oftener","most often","oftenest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"經常；常常","explanation":"表示一件事在不同時間發生過很多次，但不一定每次都發生。它是說明頻率的常用副詞，常放在主要動詞前，幫助聽者理解某個動作出現得很頻繁。","examples":[{"en":"I often read before going to bed.","zh":"我經常在睡覺前看書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We often see deer near the stream.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/often","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab7902bcbd91137e09d6","word":"oil","forms":["oil"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3c882983ae2e945","term":"oil","forms":["oil","oils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"液態脂肪","explanation":"oil可以指液態脂肪，常用於烹飪，也包括植物油、動物油等能流動的脂肪。它對應記憶中的“能鋪開、能覆蓋表面的油”。","examples":[{"en":"Heat the oil in a pan before adding the vegetables.","zh":"先把鍋裡的油加熱，再放入蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This salad needs a little olive oil.","zh":"這份沙拉需要加一點橄欖油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f457add3bf35234b","term":"oil","forms":["oil","oils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"石油","explanation":"oil可以專指地下開採的石油，是燃料、塑膠和許多工業產品的重要原料。它把“液體油”這條主線延伸到了能源領域。","examples":[{"en":"Oil prices rose sharply this winter.","zh":"今年冬天石油價格大幅上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country exports oil to several neighbors.","zh":"這個國家向幾個鄰國出口石油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2d7e2467ddcce75","term":"oil","forms":["oil","oils","oiling","oiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……加潤滑油","explanation":"oil作動詞時，最常見的意思是給機器的關節、軸承等部位加潤滑油，使其運轉更順暢。這正是“讓油覆蓋並保護表面”這條記憶主線。","examples":[{"en":"Oil the hinges if the door starts to squeak.","zh":"如果門開始吱吱響，就給合頁加點油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician oiled the machine before testing it.","zh":"技術人員在測試機器前給它加了油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cba06b5736faf67e54b0","word":"old","forms":["old"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8fe071c3db06236","term":"old","forms":["old","older","elder","oldest","eldest","oldermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"老的；古老的","explanation":"表示某物、某種關係或某個概念已經存在了很長時間，不一定強調它被使用過。它是“老、舊”這條核心意義的起點。","examples":[{"en":"They live in an old house near the river.","zh":"他們住在河邊一棟老房子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are old friends from school.","zh":"我們是上學時就認識的老朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3df27ec85fba232e","term":"old","forms":["old","older","elder","oldest","eldest","oldermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"……歲；年齡為……","explanation":"表示某人、動物或事物已經存在或生活了多長時間，常用於詢問和說明年齡。","examples":[{"en":"How old is your daughter?","zh":"你女兒幾歲了？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy is only three months old.","zh":"這隻小狗只有三個月大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-840abd040a7416ed","term":"old","forms":["old","older","elder","oldest","eldest","oldermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"以前的；過去的","explanation":"指屬於過去、現在已經被新的事物取代的那一個；它來自“曾經是老的、熟悉的”這一延伸。","examples":[{"en":"I found a photo of my old apartment.","zh":"我找到了一張我以前住的公寓的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We met some old neighbors at the reunion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa6598317163f260c9f3","word":"olive","forms":["olive"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59e18f9b30b15e8f","term":"olive","forms":["olive","olives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橄欖樹","explanation":"指結橄欖果、可產油的橄欖樹，是這個詞最基本的植物義。記住“樹結出果實”這條主線，就能和果實義自然聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"Several olive trees grow beside the old house.","zh":"老房子旁邊長著幾棵橄欖樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ancient olives grew along the terraced hillside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/olive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a8dedb2ac9e3947","term":"olive","forms":["olive","olives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橄欖果","explanation":"指橄欖樹結出的橢圓形果實，成熟時通常變黑，未成熟時通常為綠色；它可以直接食用或用於制油。","examples":[{"en":"We served bread, cheese, and olives before dinner.","zh":"晚餐前我們端上了麵包、乳酪和橄欖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She removed the stones from the olives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/olive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c266ada2b324936aa923","word":"omit","forms":["omit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4fa83630c13a9b0","term":"omit","forms":["omit","omits","omitting","omitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"省略；不包括","explanation":"指本來應該寫出、提到或列入的內容被排除在外，因此沒有出現在整體中。重點是“把某項漏在外面”，不一定表示有意刪除。","examples":[{"en":"Please do not omit any required information from the form.","zh":"請不要省略表格中的任何必填資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor omitted the final paragraph from the article.","zh":"編輯把文章的最後一段省略了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/omit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a31c9ceebab0b49","term":"omit","forms":["omit","omits","omitting","omitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漏做某事","explanation":"指本來應該完成的動作沒有完成，是把一個行動從應做的事項中漏掉。它和“省略內容”是同一幅清單圖景，只是被漏掉的物件變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"I omitted to attach the file to the email.","zh":"我忘了把檔案附在郵件裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He omitted to mention the extra delivery charge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/omit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8d31e852725afb1e26d","word":"on","forms":["on"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-097ea42a8daa28c9","term":"on","forms":["on"],"pos":"adv","zh":"開啟；使運轉","explanation":"表示把某物貼到“開啟”的狀態上，即開啟並使其開始運轉。","examples":[{"en":"Please turn the radio on.","zh":"請把收音機開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She switched the computer on before breakfast.","zh":"她早餐前開啟了電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/on","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-231c8ccbe4dd318f","term":"on","forms":["on"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……上","explanation":"表示某物貼著、接觸著或位於某個表面上，就像把東西貼在桌面、牆面或其他支撐面上。它也可用於某物沿著表面或處在表面的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Your keys are on the kitchen counter.","zh":"你的鑰匙在廚房檯面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a small label on the back of the box.","zh":"盒子背面貼著一個小標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/on","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-200651a8b2d5912f692d","word":"once","forms":["once"],"officialPos":"adv./conj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08159ad4f442c413","term":"once","forms":["once"],"pos":"adv","zh":"一次；曾經一次","explanation":"表示某件事只發生過一個次數，即“一次”。它強調次數只有一個，而不是反覆發生。","examples":[{"en":"I have only once eaten pizza.","zh":"我只吃過一次披薩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We meet once a month.","zh":"我們每月見一次面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/once","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-194e9c4950d3defa","term":"once","forms":["once"],"pos":"adv","zh":"曾經；從前","explanation":"表示某種身份、狀態或情況在過去存在，但現在通常已經不是這樣了。它就像時間線上已經過去的那個點。","examples":[{"en":"She was once a famous singer.","zh":"她曾經是一位著名歌手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This busy road was once a quiet country lane.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/once","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e0d9b7086c3134bea98","word":"ongoing","forms":["ongoing"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d81ef3a2a18bf1d","term":"ongoing","forms":["ongoing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"持續的；長期進行的","explanation":"指某項工作、計劃或狀況會繼續一段時間，並不是一次性的事情，重點在“持續存在或持續發展”。","examples":[{"en":"The company has an ongoing program to improve public safety.","zh":"這家公司有一項持續開展的公共安全改進計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge requires ongoing maintenance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ongoing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db47c31e4d35b9c7","term":"ongoing","forms":["ongoing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正在進行中的","explanation":"指某件事此刻已經開始、目前還沒有完成，強調“正在發生或進行中”。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation is ongoing, so we cannot release more details yet.","zh":"調查仍在進行中，所以我們還不能公佈更多細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We will update you during the ongoing negotiations.","zh":"談判進行期間，我們會向你通報最新情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ongoing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-288971671685b8da5662","word":"onion","forms":["onion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d12b16c68ef90ff2","term":"onion","forms":["onion","onions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洋蔥植物","explanation":"指洋蔥這種可食用的植物本身，包括它在土裡生長的整株，而不只是收穫後吃的洋蔥頭。","examples":[{"en":"We planted onions along the edge of the garden.","zh":"我們在花園邊上種了一排洋蔥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This onion variety grows well in cool weather.","zh":"這個洋蔥品種在涼爽的天氣里長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/onion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f694616c1e67950","term":"onion","forms":["onion","onions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洋蔥頭；洋蔥鱗莖","explanation":"指洋蔥植物地下的鱗莖，也就是通常買回家切片、切碎或烹調的那一部分。","examples":[{"en":"Chop an onion and add it to the soup.","zh":"切一個洋蔥，把它加進湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fried onions made the kitchen smell wonderful.","zh":"炸洋蔥讓廚房裡香氣四溢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/onion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f6fc84c9f21c24907d6b","word":"online","forms":["online"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69feb364a01d95ae","term":"online","forms":["online","more online","most online"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聯網的；接入系統的","explanation":"指裝置或系統已經接入更大的網路，能夠與網路中的其他部分連線。它是“接上線”這一核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The printer is online and ready to use.","zh":"印表機已聯網，可以使用了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The terminal must remain online during the update.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/online","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68ba6d4a04f3f47a","term":"online","forms":["online","more online","most online"],"pos":"adj","zh":"網上提供的","explanation":"指內容、服務或活動可以透過網際網路獲得或完成，例如網上廣告、網上課程和網上購物。這裡重點是“透過網際網路提供”，不一定是在說裝置此刻是否連線。","examples":[{"en":"She signed up for an online language course.","zh":"她報名參加了一門網上語言課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company sells its products through an online store.","zh":"這家公司透過網上商店銷售產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/online","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f905b19542ed08c9a9c2","word":"only","forms":["only"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b29eb2cda719505","term":"only","forms":["only"],"pos":"adj","zh":"唯一的","explanation":"在某個範圍或類別中，只有這一個符合條件；它把“一個”突出成沒有其他同類者。","examples":[{"en":"She is the only person who knows the password.","zh":"她是唯一知道密碼的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is the only bus that goes to the airport.","zh":"這是唯一一班去機場的公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/only","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1728336f5d89c532","term":"only","forms":["only"],"pos":"adv","zh":"只；僅限於","explanation":"把範圍限制在一個人、一個目的或一種情況內，意思是“除此之外不包括”。這是 only 最核心的“只圈住一項”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The room is used only for meetings.","zh":"這個房間只用於開會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only members can enter this area.","zh":"只有會員可以進入這個區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/only","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86cbd90003afbefa","term":"only","forms":["only"],"pos":"adv","zh":"僅僅；不過","explanation":"表示數量、程度或要求很少，帶有“不過是這麼一點”的意思；它不是排除類別，而是把程度壓低。","examples":[{"en":"It will take only five minutes.","zh":"這只需要五分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a few people knew the answer.","zh":"只有少數人知道答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/only","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a44853642e540dd7777c","word":"onto","forms":["onto"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea7c76840b43e64a","term":"onto","forms":["onto"],"pos":"prep","zh":"移動到……上","explanation":"表示人或物朝著一個表面、位置移動，並最終到了那裡；可以想象物體從別處跳上或落到目標表面上。","examples":[{"en":"The child climbed onto the sofa and reached for the book.","zh":"孩子爬到沙發上，伸手去拿那本書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the boxes onto the table.","zh":"請把這些箱子放到桌子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/onto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-498cb631eca459d5","term":"onto","forms":["onto"],"pos":"prep","zh":"察覺到……的秘密或計劃","explanation":"表示某人已經發現了另一個人的秘密、真實意圖或正在進行的計劃，好像已經順著線索追到了它。","examples":[{"en":"I think Mia is onto our surprise party.","zh":"我覺得米婭已經察覺到我們在籌備驚喜派對了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The detectives were onto his scheme within days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/onto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2348f998744212575d85","word":"open","forms":["open"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69b994d1d0386c31","term":"open","forms":["open","more open","opener","most open","openest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"敞開的；沒有遮擋的","explanation":"指門、窗、蓋子等沒有關上或擋住，處於可以透過、看見或進入的狀態；核心就是“沒有擋住”。","examples":[{"en":"The front door is open, so you can come in.","zh":"前門開著，你可以進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the window open for a while.","zh":"請讓窗戶開一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/open","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea63b8531aebc189","term":"open","forms":["open","more open","opener","most open","openest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公開的；不隱瞞的","explanation":"表示資訊、行為或態度沒有被隱藏，也沒有限制知情範圍；核心仍是“資訊沒有擋住”。","examples":[{"en":"She is open about the challenges she faced.","zh":"她坦率地談到了自己遇到的困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The issue is now open to public discussion.","zh":"這個問題現在公開接受公眾討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/open","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3677db054ede3b8","term":"open","forms":["open","opens","opening","opened","openest","openedst","openeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開啟；變得敞開","explanation":"把門、窗、盒子等原本擋住或合上的東西開啟，使裡面或裡面的通道不再被擋住；也可指東西自己變成敞開的狀態，這正是“沒有擋住”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please open the window; the room is getting stuffy.","zh":"請把窗戶開啟，房間裡越來越悶了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The door opened by itself when the wind blew.","zh":"風一吹，門自己開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/open","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b0f0694c142dc40","term":"open","forms":["open","opens","opening","opened","openest","openedst","openeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開始；拉開序幕","explanation":"open可表示讓活動、演出、會議等從封閉或未進行的狀態轉為進行，也就是“開始”的畫面。它既可指某人或某事開啟活動，也可指活動本身開始。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor opened the festival with a short speech.","zh":"市長用一段簡短的演講拉開了節日活動的序幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new exhibition opens next Friday.","zh":"新展覽下週五開始對公眾開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/open","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f79926c01dc6dfc2c3b5","word":"opera","forms":["opera"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4dfc302b51fbec8","term":"opera","forms":["opera","operas","opere"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歌劇作品","explanation":"指一部把戲劇表演、器樂、歌唱，有時還包括舞蹈結合起來的舞臺作品。它通常有劇情和角色，但主要透過歌唱與音樂推進。","examples":[{"en":"We saw an opera about a queen who loses her kingdom.","zh":"我們看了一部講述一位女王失去王國的歌劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This opera is famous for its final duet.","zh":"這部歌劇因最後的二重唱而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opera","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-223fff5e1c23e3a2","term":"opera","forms":["opera","operas","opere"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歌劇藝術與體裁","explanation":"指歌劇這一整體藝術形式，包括創作和演出歌劇的傳統、方法與作品型別。此時不是某一部具體歌劇，而是把許多作品看成同一種藝術。","examples":[{"en":"Opera combines powerful music with dramatic storytelling.","zh":"歌劇把有感染力的音樂和戲劇性的敘事結合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She developed a love of opera in college.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opera","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c29d39181de8f853de5","word":"operate","forms":["operate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-611d500f0dacff4c","term":"operate","forms":["operate","operates","operating","operated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"操作；使運轉","explanation":"表示人直接控制機器、裝置或系統，使它執行或繼續執行，是“讓某種力量運轉起來”這一核心概念最具體的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Only trained staff may operate this equipment.","zh":"只有受過培訓的員工才能操作這臺裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned how to operate the heating system.","zh":"她學會了如何操作供暖系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25bd44e153072d1e","term":"operate","forms":["operate","operates","operating","operated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"運轉；起作用；行動","explanation":"表示某人或某事物在發揮力量、進行活動或按某種方式運轉，重點是“開始工作或發揮作用”這一過程。","examples":[{"en":"The committee operates independently from the main office.","zh":"這個委員會獨立於總部運作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine operates quietly even at full speed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9bf5a24e4aa779981ac4","word":"operation","forms":["operation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73fc27699fa0ff00","term":"operation","forms":["operation","operations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機器或系統的運作方式","explanation":"指裝置或系統實現功能時的工作過程或運作狀態，重點是它“怎樣動起來”。","examples":[{"en":"The alarm must remain active while the machine is in operation.","zh":"機器執行時，警報必須保持開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manual explains the operation of the cooling system.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cb5ee39590ce914","term":"operation","forms":["operation","operations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有計劃的一次行動","explanation":"指為達到明確目標而組織起來的一次行動，常見於警方、救援、商業或秘密活動。","examples":[{"en":"The police launched an operation to rescue the missing hikers.","zh":"警方發起了一次行動，營救失蹤的徒步者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The operation continued through the night.","zh":"這次行動持續了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3954f246c7cec1a4","term":"operation","forms":["operation","operations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外科手術","explanation":"指醫生為治療或檢查而進行的一次外科處理，是把身體當作需要有計劃處理的物件來“運作”。","examples":[{"en":"He had an operation on his knee last month.","zh":"他上個月做了膝部手術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The operation removed the damaged tissue.","zh":"這次手術切除了受損組織。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5e4f7f12f0e53151a46","word":"operational","forms":["operational"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c882067317b1cee1","term":"operational","forms":["operational","more operational","most operational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與運作或執行有關的","explanation":"表示某事物屬於實際運作、執行或行動這一層面，尤其常用於軍事行動、業務運作和管理工作，而不是隻停留在理論或規劃上。","examples":[{"en":"The commander reviewed the operational plans before the mission.","zh":"任務開始前，指揮官審閱了行動計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was promoted to lead the company's operational team.","zh":"她被提拔去領導公司的運營團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-862dc60a490da3e6","term":"operational","forms":["operational","more operational","most operational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"已啟動並可使用的","explanation":"表示裝置、系統或設施已經準備好，可以正常投入使用；重點是從“尚未能用”變成“已經能運轉”。","examples":[{"en":"The backup generator is fully operational now.","zh":"備用發電機現在已經完全可以使用了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new payment system should become operational next week.","zh":"新的支付系統預計下週啟用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b79264a37f73ce6a7502","word":"operative","forms":["operative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4654e712749d68c7","term":"operative","forms":["operative","more operative","most operative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"關鍵的；起決定作用的","explanation":"指某個詞、事實或因素是理解情況時最關鍵、最能影響結果的部分，也就是“真正起作用的那一點”。","examples":[{"en":"The operative word is \"temporary,\" not \"permanent.\"","zh":"關鍵詞是“臨時”，而不是“永久”。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cost was the operative factor in our decision.","zh":"成本是我們作出決定時的關鍵因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dccd82ef5ea164ab","term":"operative","forms":["operative","more operative","most operative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能運轉的；可使用的","explanation":"指機器、裝置或系統處於正常狀態，能夠實際工作，而不是壞掉或停用。","examples":[{"en":"Only two of the four elevators are operative today.","zh":"今天四部電梯中只有兩部能正常執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The backup generator is now fully operative.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06e55b633481f7bb0729","word":"operator","forms":["operator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ad6c224f11defa4","term":"operator","forms":["operator","operators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"操作員；運營者","explanation":"指負責操作裝置、執行系統或提供某項服務的人，也可以指運營這項服務的機構。核心畫面就是“讓機器、系統或服務正常運轉的人或組織”。","examples":[{"en":"The drone crashed because of operator error.","zh":"無人機因操作員失誤而墜毀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The network operator will upgrade the system tonight.","zh":"網路運營商今晚將升級系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0031a08703f7cd6e","term":"operator","forms":["operator","operators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電話接線員","explanation":"指幫助接通電話、轉接線路或協助打電話的人，尤其常見於傳統電話服務語境。她的工作仍然是“讓一個系統順利運轉”，只是這個系統是電話網路。","examples":[{"en":"To make an international call, you had to go through the operator.","zh":"以前打國際電話必須透過接線員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ask the operator to connect you to the hospital.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-197c502463e9297d","term":"operator","forms":["operator","operators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精於辦事的人；老手","explanation":"非正式地指很會談判、周旋或達成目的的人，有時暗示他手段圓滑甚至不太正當。這裡是“讓事情按自己想要的方式運轉”的人際版本。","examples":[{"en":"She is a clever operator who always gets the best deal.","zh":"她很會辦事，總能談到最划算的條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He's a smooth operator who knows every influential buyer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/operator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4379105aca40fc3c6b7c","word":"opinion","forms":["opinion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9565b7aa568d30b2","term":"opinion","forms":["opinion","opinions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看法；意見","explanation":"指一個人針對某個問題、人或事形成的看法，可以來自事實分析，也可以帶有個人感受。這是 opinion 最常見、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"What is your opinion of the new library?","zh":"你對新圖書館有什麼看法？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In my opinion, we should wait another week.","zh":"在我看來，我們應該再等一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opinion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5603e8939608ba2d","term":"opinion","forms":["opinion","opinions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對人的評價","explanation":"指心裡對某個人或某件事作出的評價，也就是“在別人眼中是什麼樣”。它和普通“看法”相近，但更強調評價結果。","examples":[{"en":"The team's honest response improved my opinion of them.","zh":"這個團隊誠實的回應改善了我對他們的評價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her colleagues have a high opinion of her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opinion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98c4e5a5e476681cd95a","word":"opponent","forms":["opponent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e30c6f1e5cb8681","term":"opponent","forms":["opponent","opponents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對手；反對者","explanation":"opponent 是站在你對面、與你競爭或反對你的人的統稱：比賽中是對手，選舉或爭論中則是與你立場相反的人。這個詞強調對立關係，不一定表示私人敵意。","examples":[{"en":"She studied her opponent carefully before the final match.","zh":"決賽前，她仔細研究了自己的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal faced strong opposition from its opponents.","zh":"這項提案遭到了反對者的強烈抵制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opponent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04b447783afe5bfd4b48","word":"opportunity","forms":["opportunity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-461ade9e08efdf9d","term":"opportunity","forms":["opportunity","opportunities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展或獲益的機會","explanation":"指能讓人取得進步、發展事業或獲得利益的機會，就像一扇開啟後可以讓你向前走的門。","examples":[{"en":"She saw the new position as an opportunity for advancement.","zh":"她把這個新職位看作晉升的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should seize this opportunity to expand the business.","zh":"我們應該抓住這個拓展業務的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opportunity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd0abb2c70aac8f0","term":"opportunity","forms":["opportunity","opportunities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"做某事的有利時機","explanation":"指某種有利的情況或場合，使某件事變得適合或更容易進行；不一定涉及賺錢或職位發展。","examples":[{"en":"The trip was a great opportunity to learn about local culture.","zh":"這次旅行是瞭解當地文化的好機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The internship offers an opportunity to gain practical experience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opportunity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26a0ee5c659ab6a85d59","word":"oppose","forms":["oppose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20ed461e891d3665","term":"oppose","forms":["oppose","opposes","opposing","opposed","opposest","opposedst","opposeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抵抗；阻止","explanation":"指站到對面，設法擋住某人、某行動或某種力量，使它不能順利繼續；這種對抗可以是實際行動，也可以是用理由爭辯。","examples":[{"en":"Several local groups opposed the plan to close the library.","zh":"幾個當地團體反對關閉圖書館的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers opposed the invading army at the river.","zh":"士兵們在河邊抵抗入侵的軍隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oppose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47c6a125038c15cd","term":"oppose","forms":["oppose","opposes","opposing","opposed","opposest","opposedst","opposeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反對；表示異議","explanation":"強調公開表明自己不贊成某個決定、做法或想法，通常是在討論、投票或公共議題中表達立場。","examples":[{"en":"Many parents oppose raising the school fees.","zh":"許多家長反對提高學費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local residents opposed the plan to close the park.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oppose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9f62c2ad0ad79d037d3","word":"opposite","forms":["opposite"],"officialPos":"adj./n./prep./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-546bb373ee4ffa0e","term":"opposite","forms":["opposite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對面的；正對著的","explanation":"指某物位於另一物的正對面，中間通常隔著道路、房間或其他空間。這是從“兩端互相面對”的核心畫面直接發展出來的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"She saw him walking on the opposite side of the road.","zh":"她看見他在馬路對面走著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pharmacy is on the opposite corner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opposite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ac86c3e23d64f94","term":"opposite","forms":["opposite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完全不同的；相反的","explanation":"指觀點、性質、結果或行為與另一者處在相反的一端，甚至彼此衝突。這是由空間上的“兩端相對”抽象出來的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"Her decision had the opposite effect from what she expected.","zh":"她的決定產生了與預期相反的效果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sisters reached opposite conclusions from the same evidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opposite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3bf7f5c7faecee0","term":"opposite","forms":["opposite"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……對面","explanation":"表示某地點或物體位於另一地點或物體的正對面，是最直接的“隔著一條線面對面”用法。","examples":[{"en":"There’s a café opposite the station.","zh":"車站對面有一家咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She lives opposite the village bakery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opposite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f17469d178f0487a711","word":"opposition","forms":["opposition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab06bda3058c42e4","term":"opposition","forms":["opposition","oppositions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反對；對立","explanation":"指反對某項計劃、決定或觀點的行動、態度，或雙方因此形成的衝突關係；核心畫面就是站在對方的另一邊。","examples":[{"en":"There was strong opposition to the new housing plan.","zh":"人們強烈反對這項新的住房計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two politicians are in opposition to the bill.","zh":"這兩位政治家反對這項法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opposition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7fc9f6fa0dceb662","term":"opposition","forms":["opposition","oppositions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反對黨；反對派","explanation":"指在政治上反對現任政府或執政黨的政黨、黨派或政治運動；它就是“站到掌權者對面”的團體。","examples":[{"en":"The leader of the opposition criticized the government's budget.","zh":"反對黨領袖批評了政府的預算案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The opposition demanded an inquiry into the contracts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opposition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-974b5d240842f853911d","word":"oppress","forms":["oppress"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a9cf6584797f639d","term":"oppress","forms":["oppress","oppresses","oppressing","oppressed","oppressest","oppressedst","oppresseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓迫；以不公正力量壓制","explanation":"指掌權者、強勢群體或制度用不公正的力量限制、控制並傷害較弱者，就像把對方長期壓在下面。","examples":[{"en":"The regime oppressed the minority for decades.","zh":"這個政權壓迫少數群體長達數十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers were oppressed by unfair laws.","zh":"工人受到不公平法律的壓迫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oppress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dee3d1b8b0eaa807","term":"oppress","forms":["oppress","oppresses","oppressing","oppressed","oppressest","oppressedst","oppresseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使人鬱悶；使心情沉重","explanation":"指天氣、環境、憂慮或其他沉重因素像壓力一樣壓在人的心上，使人感到悲觀、壓抑或沒有精神。","examples":[{"en":"The endless rain oppressed everyone in the house.","zh":"沒完沒了的雨讓屋裡每個人都感到壓抑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The silence in the empty house oppressed her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oppress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36894e5351c4cd9a99bb","word":"oppression","forms":["oppression"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5989e736b610a97","term":"oppression","forms":["oppression","oppressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殘酷或不公的壓迫","explanation":"指掌權者或有力量的一方，以沉重、殘酷或不公的方式控制、傷害或限制他人；重點在於這種力量使用得不正當。","examples":[{"en":"The movement was founded to resist the oppression of workers.","zh":"這個運動是為了反抗對工人的壓迫而成立的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people spoke out against political oppression.","zh":"許多人公開反對政治壓迫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oppression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adf9b0efd10bbc7b","term":"oppression","forms":["oppression","oppressions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壓迫行為或受壓迫的狀態","explanation":"指壓迫他人的行為本身，或一個人、一個群體長期被壓制、失去自由和尊嚴的處境；它更側重“壓迫這一過程或狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"The community lived under oppression for many years.","zh":"這個群體在壓迫之下生活了許多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The uprising challenged decades of political oppression.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oppression","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f44712b7d71ded71ea9","word":"opt","forms":["opt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-081570780d8b7e68","term":"opt","forms":["opt","opts","opting","opted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"選擇","explanation":"opt 表示從幾個可能性中作出選擇，重點是“選定某個方案”。它常帶有經過考慮後決定採用或不採用某事的意味。","examples":[{"en":"We opted for the cheaper hotel.","zh":"我們選擇了價格較便宜的那家酒店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He opted not to go.","zh":"他選擇不去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/opt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9c3722d768c33938b0a","word":"optimism","forms":["optimism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18f09fefbbebc018","term":"optimism","forms":["optimism","optimisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂觀態度","explanation":"指一個人傾向於期待最好的結果，或至少相信事情會朝有利的方向發展。即使現實有困難，抱有 optimism 的人仍相信最後會有辦法或會出現好轉。","examples":[{"en":"Her optimism helped the team stay calm during the difficult project.","zh":"她的樂觀態度幫助團隊在這個困難的專案中保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the bad news, he remained full of optimism about the future.","zh":"儘管聽到了壞訊息，他仍然對未來充滿樂觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/optimism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2584457d7f394d3a","term":"optimism","forms":["optimism","optimisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"世界本質上最好","explanation":"指一種哲學思想：相信現實世界已經是所有可能世界中最好的，或者總體上存在足夠充分的理由使它呈現為最好的一種狀態。這是日常“樂觀態度”在哲學層面的擴大。","examples":[{"en":"The novel questions the optimism that the world is ultimately arranged for the best.","zh":"這部小說質疑這樣一種樂觀主義：世界最終會以最好的方式執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The philosopher's optimism held that this was the best possible world.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/optimism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65ee89092efbf78ab19a","word":"optimistic","forms":["optimistic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d237f442fee8b911","term":"optimistic","forms":["optimistic","more optimistic","most optimistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樂觀的；抱樂好期待的","explanation":"形容一個人相信事情大機率會有好的結果，或在面對未來時保持積極、充滿希望的態度。它強調“期待最好結果”，不表示結果已經確定。","examples":[{"en":"She is optimistic about finding a new job soon.","zh":"她對很快找到新工作抱有樂觀態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the delay, the team remains optimistic.","zh":"儘管有所延誤，團隊仍然保持樂觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/optimistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b69bae022b4f34f","term":"optimistic","forms":["optimistic","more optimistic","most optimistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樂觀併發的","explanation":"在計算機等技術語境中，指一種“先相信不會衝突”的處理方式：多個操作可以暫時同時進行，等結果準備寫回時才檢查資料是否被其他操作改動。","examples":[{"en":"The application uses optimistic concurrency to handle updates efficiently.","zh":"這個應用採用樂觀併發來高效處理更新操作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Optimistic locking checks for conflicting edits before saving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/optimistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a11a75e0feeecc1a9eff","word":"option","forms":["option"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fdaeaae6efa39b8d","term":"option","forms":["option","options"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可選方案","explanation":"option 可以指在幾種可能性中可以選擇的一種方案或做法，也就是擺在面前的一條可走的路。","examples":[{"en":"Taking the train is our best option.","zh":"坐火車是我們最好的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had no option but to cancel the trip.","zh":"我們別無選擇，只能取消這次旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/option","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e6eb0c4df4512aa","term":"option","forms":["option","options"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇權","explanation":"option 也可以指一個人擁有選擇的自由或權利，重點不在具體方案，而在於“可以自己決定走哪條路”。","examples":[{"en":"Employees have the option to work from home on Fridays.","zh":"員工可以選擇星期五在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your contract gives you the option to renew.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/option","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec91fdd9256cb75ae611","word":"optional","forms":["optional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-006f14174ca25402","term":"optional","forms":["optional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可選的；非必需的","explanation":"指某項要求、活動或東西不是必須的，是否採用完全由個人選擇；不選通常也不會違反規定。","examples":[{"en":"The final project is optional, but it can help improve your grade.","zh":"期末專案不是必做的，但完成它可能有助於提高成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Guests may attend the workshop, but attendance is optional.","zh":"客人可以參加這次研討會，但參加並非強制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/optional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7175517a370b5cd2e664","word":"or","forms":["or"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"or","forms":["or"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"或者；或是","examples":[{"en":"Would you like tea or coffee?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"You can send the form by mail or submit it online.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-81fcbba2c584e6bc656f","word":"oral","forms":["oral"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73155f89263adcbc","term":"oral","forms":["oral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"口腔的；與嘴有關的","explanation":"指身體的嘴或口腔，或者與口腔健康、口腔檢查等有關。可以把它記成“圍繞嘴的”。","examples":[{"en":"Regular brushing is important for good oral hygiene.","zh":"經常刷牙對保持良好的口腔衛生很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic provides routine oral examinations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f396bf2e2d5a055a","term":"oral","forms":["oral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"口頭的；非書面的","explanation":"指透過說話完成，而不是透過書面文字完成。口頭報告、口頭回答和口試都可以用這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"Each student must give a short oral presentation.","zh":"每名學生都必須作一個簡短的口頭報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The instructions were given orally rather than in writing.","zh":"這些說明是口頭給出的，而不是書面給出的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c78445976000e97","term":"oral","forms":["oral","orals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口試；口頭考試","explanation":"指透過當面說話回答來完成的考試，尤其常見於語言學習。它就是“口頭的考試”被縮短成名詞後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"We have our French oral tomorrow.","zh":"我們明天有法語口試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her French oral is scheduled for Tuesday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b4c9133da73a7113224","word":"orange","forms":["orange"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4fb1ad94d06de5b","term":"orange","forms":["orange","oranger","more orange","orangest","most orange"],"pos":"adj","zh":"橙色的","explanation":"像成熟橙子外皮那樣的顏色，通常指紅色和黃色之間的橙色。","examples":[{"en":"She wore an orange sweater to the party.","zh":"她穿著一件橙色毛衣去參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The evening sky turned orange.","zh":"傍晚的天空變成了橙色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c04fb4487ccf6c5c","term":"orange","forms":["orange","oranges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橙子","explanation":"橙樹結出的圓形柑橘類水果，成熟時呈黃紅色，味道酸甜。","examples":[{"en":"I packed an orange in my lunch box.","zh":"我在午餐盒裡放了一個橙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These oranges are sweet and easy to peel.","zh":"這些橙子很甜，也很容易剝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e176ce11eb4da5d9","term":"orange","forms":["orange","oranges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橙色","explanation":"成熟橙子的顏色，位於紅色和黃色之間。","examples":[{"en":"Orange is her favorite color.","zh":"橙色是她最喜歡的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The traffic cones are bright orange.","zh":"那些交通錐是鮮亮的橙色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4fa1a13ac468ac495f33","word":"orbit","forms":["orbit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a839abe7376ff5d","term":"orbit","forms":["orbit","orbits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"執行軌道","explanation":"物體圍繞某個點或另一個天體執行時所走的彎曲路線，例如行星圍繞恆星的軌道。","examples":[{"en":"The satellite has entered a stable orbit around the planet.","zh":"這顆衛星已經進入圍繞該行星的穩定軌道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The moon travels in an orbit around Earth.","zh":"月球沿著繞地球的軌道執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orbit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8834fb583a83590f","term":"orbit","forms":["orbit","orbits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影響圈","explanation":"把“圍繞中心執行”引申到社會關係中，表示某人、團體或勢力能夠影響、吸引或控制的範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Several smaller companies have come into the orbit of the technology giant.","zh":"幾家較小的公司已經進入這家科技巨頭的影響圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rarely lets strangers into her orbit.","zh":"她很少讓陌生人進入自己的交際圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orbit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08f855eb0a35cbbd","term":"orbit","forms":["orbit","orbits","orbiting","orbited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繞著執行","explanation":"指一個天體或物體沿軌道圍繞另一個物體或位置執行。","examples":[{"en":"The Earth orbits the Sun once a year.","zh":"地球每年繞太陽執行一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tiny moon orbits around the distant planet.","zh":"一顆小衛星繞著那顆遙遠的行星執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orbit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16dcefb6f89535cb","term":"orbit","forms":["orbit","orbits","orbiting","orbited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"圍繞……展開","explanation":"比喻地表示把生活、計劃或注意力的中心放在某個人或某件事上，彷彿自己一直繞著那個中心執行。","examples":[{"en":"For years, she orbited her whole life around her family.","zh":"多年來，她把自己的整個人生都圍繞著家人安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team's plans still orbit around one major project.","zh":"團隊的計劃仍然圍繞著一個重大專案展開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orbit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68566dc699f6bb9ea633","word":"orchard","forms":["orchard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef9681f9ab5b6959","term":"orchard","forms":["orchard","orchards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"果園","explanation":"指專門種植蘋果、橙子等果樹，或種植堅果樹的一片土地。記住“整齊排列的果樹地”這個畫面，就能和普通花園區分開。","examples":[{"en":"We picked apples in the orchard yesterday.","zh":"我們昨天在果園裡摘了蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farm has a small peach orchard.","zh":"這個農場有一小片桃園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2626a2d3f1466548","term":"orchard","forms":["orchard","orchards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"果園裡的樹木","explanation":"有時它不強調土地本身，而是把果園中的果樹整體看作一個群體，例如說某個果園的樹木開花或結果。","examples":[{"en":"The orchard is full of blossoms this spring.","zh":"今年春天，果園裡的樹開滿了花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The orchard flowered a week earlier this spring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-613ad991bf2b5079e818","word":"orchestra","forms":["orchestra"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80671694ee8b337a","term":"orchestra","forms":["orchestra","orchestras","orchestrae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管弦樂團","explanation":"指許多音樂家組成的樂團，他們用絃樂器、木管樂器、銅管樂器和打擊樂器等一起演奏。這個詞有時也可泛指這支樂團所使用的樂器。","examples":[{"en":"The orchestra performed Beethoven's Fifth Symphony last night.","zh":"管弦樂團昨晚演奏了貝多芬的《第五交響曲》。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to join the city orchestra after graduation.","zh":"她希望畢業後加入市管弦樂團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchestra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f25a6d2e69a75d0e","term":"orchestra","forms":["orchestra","orchestras","orchestrae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂池；樂手演奏區","explanation":"指劇場或音樂廳中緊挨舞臺、位於舞臺前方下側的區域，樂手通常坐在那裡演奏，有時也供其他表演者使用。","examples":[{"en":"The musicians took their seats in the orchestra before the opera began.","zh":"歌劇開始前，樂手們在樂池裡就座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conductor stepped down into the orchestra pit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchestra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-338d4e3dd450f4a00997","word":"ordeal","forms":["ordeal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34f46ce5a75900c7","term":"ordeal","forms":["ordeal","ordeals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痛苦的經歷","explanation":"ordeal 最常見的現代含義是一次令人痛苦、緊張或筋疲力盡的經歷，重點不只是“難”，而是經歷過程讓人很不好受。漫長的治療、艱難的談判或令人壓力巨大的場合，都可以被稱為 ordeal。","examples":[{"en":"The long journey home was an exhausting ordeal.","zh":"漫長的回家旅程是一場令人精疲力竭的苦難經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stayed calm throughout the ordeal.","zh":"在整個艱難過程中，她始終保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ordeal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3eeb7e96e59ce40f9cb1","word":"order","forms":["order"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f886c226561feb95","term":"order","forms":["order","orders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"順序","explanation":"order表示把人或事物按一定標準排到合適的位置，也就是它們先後或排列的順序；可以把它想成“排到合適的位置”。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the files in alphabetical order.","zh":"請把這些檔案按字母順序排列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children stood in order of age.","zh":"孩子們按年齡順序站好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/order","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-841c07fa17908a0a","term":"order","forms":["order","orders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"命令","explanation":"order可以表示要求別人照辦的正式命令，也就是把事情“按要求進行”；它通常帶有釋出者的權威或明確指示。","examples":[{"en":"The officer gave an order to leave the building.","zh":"那名官員下令離開大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We must obey the court's order.","zh":"我們必須遵守法院的命令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/order","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93526640195ff9f0","term":"order","forms":["order","orders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"訂單；訂購請求","explanation":"order表示向商家或服務方提出的購買、供應請求，讓對方按要求提供東西；這正是把東西“排到合適的位置”並讓供應按要求進行。","examples":[{"en":"I placed an order for two shirts online.","zh":"我在網上下單買了兩件襯衫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop has shipped your order.","zh":"商店已經把你的訂單發出了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/order","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8534b585cc132428","term":"order","forms":["order","orders","ordering","ordered","orderest","orderedst","ordereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"訂購商品或服務","explanation":"向商家提出具體要求，讓對方按要求提供商品或服務；這正是把事情安排好、讓它照要求進行的一種方式。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a new desk online, and it will arrive next week.","zh":"我在網上訂了一張新書桌，下週會送到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ordered two soups and a plate of noodles for lunch.","zh":"我們午飯點了兩份湯和一盤面條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/order","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b81791acd50956478d68","word":"orderly","forms":["orderly"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edfb5fad14388814","term":"orderly","forms":["orderly","more orderly","most orderly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"整齊的；井然有序的","explanation":"指東西擺放整齊、環境不雜亂，彷彿每件東西都排在合適的位置上。它強調整體安排有秩序，不只是表面乾淨。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps her desk orderly even during busy weeks.","zh":"即使在忙碌的幾周裡，她也把書桌保持得整整齊齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The records were stored in an orderly way.","zh":"這些記錄被有條理地存放著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orderly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c1b84f47faa2e3d","term":"orderly","forms":["orderly","more orderly","most orderly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有條理的；系統的","explanation":"指做事或執行方式按照清楚的規則和步驟進行，不是雜亂或隨意的。這裡的“有序”從物品的排列擴充套件到了計劃、過程和體系。","examples":[{"en":"The team made an orderly plan for moving the equipment.","zh":"團隊為搬運裝置制訂了一個有條理的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting ended in an orderly manner.","zh":"會議有條不紊地結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orderly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03822375f2aca5e53d66","word":"ordinary","forms":["ordinary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b052b115ce12c03c","term":"ordinary","forms":["ordinary","more ordinary","most ordinary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平常的；慣常的","explanation":"指符合通常規律、日常習慣或自然秩序的事物，沒有特殊或異常之處。它強調“平時就是這樣”，不一定帶有負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"On an ordinary day, I take the bus to work.","zh":"平常的一天裡，我坐公交車上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took our ordinary route to the station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ordinary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98909b3b7004d503","term":"ordinary","forms":["ordinary","more ordinary","most ordinary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"普通的；平凡的","explanation":"指沒有特別特徵、功能或經歷的事物，也可以形容人的生活平凡日常；根據語氣，有時會含有“平庸、沒什麼看頭”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She leads an ordinary life and enjoys quiet weekends.","zh":"她過著平凡的生活，喜歡安靜的週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was an ordinary Tuesday until the letter arrived.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ordinary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0fb6e6c6305332dbd13","word":"organ","forms":["organ"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b43bca7d26bd593f","term":"organ","forms":["organ","organs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體器官","explanation":"organ 指由多種組織構成、共同完成某項生理功能的身體部分，例如心臟、肺或肝臟。它強調的是“負責某項功能的身體部件”。","examples":[{"en":"The heart is a vital organ that pumps blood around the body.","zh":"心臟是把血液泵送到全身的重要器官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctors checked all her major organs.","zh":"醫生檢查了她的主要器官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c177deadf213042","term":"organ","forms":["organ","organs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管風琴","explanation":"organ 指管風琴，一種透過琴鍵使許多音管發聲的樂器；也可以指模仿這種聲音的電子樂器。它像“由許多功能部件組成、共同完成工作的器官”。","examples":[{"en":"She learned to play the organ at her local church.","zh":"她在當地教堂學習演奏管風琴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The organ filled the hall with a deep, powerful sound.","zh":"管風琴用深沉有力的聲音充滿了大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69f81619d0ef92cbb165","word":"organic","forms":["organic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac05b5813b8522b9","term":"organic","forms":["organic","more organic","most organic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與生命體有關的","explanation":"指屬於生物、由生物產生，或與生命活動有關的事物；核心感覺是“來自一個活的整體”。例如有機物質可以來自植物或動物，也可以泛指生物性材料。","examples":[{"en":"The soil contains a lot of organic matter.","zh":"這片土壤含有大量有機物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Organic remains were preserved beneath the volcanic ash.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36e22b0fe389792e","term":"organic","forms":["organic","more organic","most organic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有機種植的","explanation":"用於食品或農產品時，指按照有機農業標準種植或生產，通常限制使用人工合成的農用化學品，並可能經過認證。","examples":[{"en":"They buy organic vegetables from a local farm.","zh":"他們從當地農場購買有機蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farm grows organic vegetables without synthetic pesticides.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a492dab5c23afc8b","term":"organic","forms":["organic","more organic","most organic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自然漸進形成的","explanation":"指某事不是按僵硬的計劃突然拼出來的，而是在實際發展中逐漸形成；它保留了“從內部生長成形”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The partnership grew organically over several years.","zh":"這段合作關係經過幾年的發展自然形成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The neighborhood's organic growth produced winding, irregular streets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d13dae0e56798384a013","word":"organism","forms":["organism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc922ef587f7db3f","term":"organism","forms":["organism","organisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物；有機體","explanation":"指一個獨立而完整、能夠作為整體存在的生命體，包括動物、植物、真菌和微生物等。重點是“整個活的個體”，而不是其中的某個部分。","examples":[{"en":"Every living organism needs a source of energy.","zh":"每個有生命的生物都需要能量來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists discovered a tiny organism living in the hot spring.","zh":"科學家發現了一種生活在溫泉中的微小生物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f0fed48e3513d1d","term":"organism","forms":["organism","organisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有機系統；統一運作的整體","explanation":"指由許多彼此依賴、相互配合的部分組成的整體；說話人把它看成像生物一樣，會自行運轉並對外作出反應。","examples":[{"en":"The city is a complex organism that changes with its people.","zh":"這座城市是一個會隨著居民而變化的複雜有機系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university functions as a complex social organism.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af3a1bb312bf8430055d","word":"organization","forms":["organization"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-007409ec972d751f","term":"organization","forms":["organization","organizations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"條理；組織性","explanation":"指事物被安排得有條理、結構清楚的狀態。它強調零散內容被排成一個容易理解或運作的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting lacked organization and quickly became confusing.","zh":"這次會議缺乏條理，很快就變得混亂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good organization makes a busy week much easier.","zh":"良好的安排能讓忙碌的一週輕鬆得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6aff13b46faeea2e","term":"organization","forms":["organization","organizations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"編排；結構","explanation":"指一本書、文章、計劃或其他內容具體是怎樣安排和分成各部分的，也就是它的結構和編排方式。","examples":[{"en":"The organization of the report makes the main points easy to find.","zh":"這份報告的結構讓人很容易找到重點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report's clear organization made its argument easy to follow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75f963e200d4190d","term":"organization","forms":["organization","organizations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式組織；機構","explanation":"指一群人為明確目標而成立，並通常有名稱、規則和一定正式結構的團體，例如公益組織、國際機構或行業組織。","examples":[{"en":"She works for an organization that supports local schools.","zh":"她在一個支援當地學校的組織工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The organization has strict rules for its members.","zh":"這個組織對其成員有嚴格的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6ad82a52d2b03768a75","word":"organize","forms":["organize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59234f0e7026ba81","term":"organize","forms":["organize","organizes","organizing","organized","organizest","organizedst","organizeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安排整理","explanation":"把原本零散或混亂的東西按一定次序安排好，使它們更容易使用、理解或運轉。物件可以是材料、資訊、活動，也可以是時間和工作。","examples":[{"en":"I need to organize my notes before the exam.","zh":"考試前我得整理一下筆記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They organized a charity concert for the local hospital.","zh":"他們為當地醫院組織了一場慈善音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e3fc4d02f6922b0","term":"organize","forms":["organize","organizes","organizing","organized","organizest","organizedst","organizeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建立結構","explanation":"不是單純排列現成的東西，而是把一個整體分成有明確作用的部分，讓各部分按照一定關係共同發揮作用。可以用於政府、機構、計劃或其他複雜系統。","examples":[{"en":"The new plan organizes the department into three working teams.","zh":"新計劃把這個部門劃分為三個工作小組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She organized the notes into three broad categories.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bf7ab78559a04941f15","word":"organizer","forms":["organizer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97323cbc7466a928","term":"organizer","forms":["organizer","organizers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"活動組織者","explanation":"指負責安排公共活動各項細節的人，例如聯絡場地、安排流程和協調參與者。這個人把原本分散的事務整理成一個能順利進行的活動。","examples":[{"en":"The event organizer sent everyone the final schedule.","zh":"活動組織者把最終日程發給了所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works as a professional organizer for busy families.","zh":"她為忙碌的家庭提供專業整理服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organizer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-644494312e0d9eff","term":"organizer","forms":["organizer","organizers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紙質日程本","explanation":"指沒有電子功能的記事本、日曆本或日程本，用來記錄約會、任務和個人安排。它和電子工具的共同點是都把生活事務集中整理起來。","examples":[{"en":"I wrote all my appointments in my new organizer.","zh":"我把所有預約都記在了新買的日程本里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She noted the appointment in her leather organizer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/organizer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ded579862da80bf4e463","word":"orient","forms":["orient"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d151197b9ada4016","term":"orient","forms":["orient","orients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"東方","explanation":"指地平線上早晨太陽最先出現的方向，也就是東方；這是“定方向”這一核心概念的起點。","examples":[{"en":"The sun rose in the Orient and lit the valley.","zh":"太陽從東方升起，照亮了山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A pale glow appeared in the Orient before dawn.","zh":"黎明前，東方出現了一片淡淡的光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5df5e49d9b50936","term":"orient","forms":["orient","orients","orienting","oriented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使熟悉並適應","explanation":"幫助自己或他人在新環境、新制度或新任務中找到位置，瞭解該怎麼行動；這就是把“找到方向”從空間方向擴充套件到生活和工作情境。","examples":[{"en":"It took me a week to orient myself to the new job.","zh":"我花了一週才適應這份新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide helped visitors orient themselves in the museum.","zh":"導遊幫助參觀者熟悉博物館裡的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c4a23e0f78beaac4775","word":"oriental","forms":["oriental"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2079b71918f48a4","term":"oriental","forms":["oriental","more Oriental","most Oriental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"珍珠光澤極佳的","explanation":"形容珍珠或其他寶石時，表示表面光澤特別明亮、柔和而有質感；可以把它記成“像東方升起的太陽一樣發光”。","examples":[{"en":"The collector admired the pearl’s oriental lustre.","zh":"收藏家欣賞這顆珍珠出眾的光澤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jeweler admired the oriental luster of the pearl.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oriental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c54de840367898b6","term":"oriental","forms":["oriental","more Oriental","most Oriental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"東方地區的","explanation":"表示與地中海以東、近東、中東或遠東，尤其東亞有關的；具體範圍取決於說話者和時代。","examples":[{"en":"The gallery specializes in oriental art from East Asia.","zh":"這家畫廊專門收藏來自東亞的東方藝術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibition traces trade along ancient Oriental routes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oriental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c59cf32b132c815c214c","word":"orientation","forms":["orientation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b30d27ededa2b087","term":"orientation","forms":["orientation","orientations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實際朝向","explanation":"指某物或某人的實際位置和朝向，例如建築物面向哪邊、裝置朝向哪裡。","examples":[{"en":"The orientation of the solar panels should face south.","zh":"太陽能電池板的朝向應該面向南方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We changed the orientation of the desk to get more sunlight.","zh":"我們改變了書桌的朝向，以獲得更多陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orientation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-749b0e0272d0516d","term":"orientation","forms":["orientation","orientations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傾向或方向","explanation":"從“朝向某個方向”引申為思想、政策、研究或行動所呈現的傾向和發展方向。","examples":[{"en":"The company has a strong customer-oriented orientation.","zh":"這家公司有很強的客戶導向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course has a practical orientation rather than a theoretical one.","zh":"這門課程偏重實踐，而不是理論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orientation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f16b4a6261c0e01d","term":"orientation","forms":["orientation","orientations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"適應新環境","explanation":"指一個人進入新學校、工作場所或社會環境後，逐漸熟悉並適應那裡的過程。","examples":[{"en":"It took me a few weeks to complete my orientation to the new job.","zh":"我花了幾周才適應這份新工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New staff receive a week of orientation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orientation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-181fdd46fc4a7246b9f4","word":"origin","forms":["origin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06989dcb0aded0ee","term":"origin","forms":["origin","origins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"起源；開端","explanation":"指某件事、某種習俗或某個過程開始出現的時間、地點或背景，也就是它從哪裡“冒出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The tradition has its origin in a small village.","zh":"這個傳統起源於一個小村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one knows the origin of the story.","zh":"沒人知道這個故事的起源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/origin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9ac9c8805fd5f8a","term":"origin","forms":["origin","origins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"來源；源頭","explanation":"指河流、訊息、商品等實際或抽象事物從哪裡來；它仍然是“起點”這個核心概念的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The shop cannot confirm the origin of the coffee beans.","zh":"這家店無法確認這些咖啡豆的來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river's origin lies high in the mountains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/origin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0682c5f2076f099c34cf","word":"original","forms":["original"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-efd999584d53bbf2","term":"original","forms":["original","more original","most original"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最初的；原來的","explanation":"指在時間、順序或狀態上最早出現的那個，後來的人、事物或版本都是從它開始的。","examples":[{"en":"The original plan was much simpler.","zh":"原來的計劃簡單得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep the room in its original state.","zh":"請保持房間原來的狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/original","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf127abf0bdc1ecc","term":"original","forms":["original","more original","most original"],"pos":"adj","zh":"原版的；原件的","explanation":"指一系列複製品、改編版或修訂版之前的第一份或最初版本，也就是後來版本所依據的源頭。","examples":[{"en":"The museum keeps the original painting behind glass.","zh":"博物館把原畫儲存在玻璃後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I prefer the original version of the song.","zh":"我更喜歡這首歌的原版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/original","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89e9611987c75804","term":"original","forms":["original","more original","most original"],"pos":"adj","zh":"原創的","explanation":"指作品、設計或內容是自己新創作出來的，不是從別處複製或翻譯來的；它仍然保留“直接從源頭產生”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"She wrote an original song for the film.","zh":"她為這部電影創作了一首原創歌曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gallery is showing original works by young artists.","zh":"畫廊正在展出年輕藝術家的原創作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/original","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfabce11a391c2da","term":"original","forms":["original","originals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原件；原作","explanation":"指所有複製品、改編版或變體所依據的那件最初作品或物品，是“源頭”本身。","examples":[{"en":"The gallery has the original, not a reproduction.","zh":"畫廊裡的是原作，不是複製品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is the original of the document you received.","zh":"這就是你收到的那份檔案的原件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/original","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cb74d43b863c8876b71","word":"originality","forms":["originality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0285da8f0e4ceeb9","term":"originality","forms":["originality","originalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新意；獨創性","explanation":"指某件作品、設計、做法或想法不像已有的東西那樣照搬，而是具有新穎、獨特的特點。重點在於“成果本身顯得新”。","examples":[{"en":"The originality of her design impressed the judges.","zh":"她設計中的獨創性給評委留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel is admired for its originality.","zh":"這部小說因其獨創性而受到讚賞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/originality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15f462be5f52ea08","term":"originality","forms":["originality","originalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨立創新的能力","explanation":"指一個人不只是重複別人看過的事實或答案，而是能獨立思考，從熟悉的材料中想出新的解釋和辦法。重點在於“產生新想法的能力”。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher valued originality in the students' essays.","zh":"老師很重視學生作文中的獨立創意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She solved the problem with remarkable originality.","zh":"她以非同尋常的創新思路解決了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/originality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19bf2c59ada7a9d31503","word":"originate","forms":["originate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fa1e5bfeed3e527","term":"originate","forms":["originate","originates","originating","originated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發起；創造","explanation":"表示某人或某個機構把一個想法、計劃、制度或其他事物創造出來並使其開始存在，就像讓泉水開始流動一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The committee originated the proposal for a citywide recycling program.","zh":"委員會提出了在全市推行回收計劃的提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The idea was originated by a group of local teachers.","zh":"這個想法是由一群當地教師提出的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/originate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4b3383f28278836","term":"originate","forms":["originate","originates","originating","originated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起源於；來自","explanation":"表示某種傳統、想法、問題或事物從某個地方、某個時期、某個人或某個群體開始出現，強調它的源頭。","examples":[{"en":"This style of music originated in the southern United States.","zh":"這種音樂風格起源於美國南部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The custom originated in fishing villages centuries ago.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/originate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3cf04805560a8e140dd","word":"ornament","forms":["ornament"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a46dc86fe38bd595","term":"ornament","forms":["ornament","ornaments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝飾物；裝飾","explanation":"指用來使某物更漂亮、更有特色的裝飾物或裝飾性元素，也可以泛指裝飾本身。","examples":[{"en":"The carved wooden panels are a beautiful ornament to the old house.","zh":"這些雕花木板是這座老房子的漂亮裝飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She placed a small glass ornament on the shelf.","zh":"她把一個小玻璃裝飾品放在架子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ornament","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0ad4c5fbac3b759","term":"ornament","forms":["ornament","ornaments","ornamenting","ornamented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"裝飾；點綴","explanation":"指給某物加上裝飾，使它更漂亮、更華麗。","examples":[{"en":"They ornamented the hall with paper lanterns and flowers.","zh":"他們用紙燈籠和鮮花裝飾大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gold stars ornamented the dark blue ceiling.","zh":"金色星星點綴著深藍色的天花板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ornament","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-88f6811ab5d8fc6d3177","word":"orphan","forms":["orphan"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ce4fb6de172b72b","term":"orphan","forms":["orphan","orphans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孤兒","explanation":"指失去父母的孩子，也可指父母去世的成年人，但最典型的形象是沒有父母照料的未成年人。","examples":[{"en":"The orphan found a safe home with a kind family.","zh":"這個孤兒在一個善良的家庭裡找到了安全的家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The war left thousands of children orphans.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orphan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be6734cbad1a669ceb38","word":"orphanage","forms":["orphanage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b489bffe2b07ffd7","term":"orphanage","forms":["orphanage","orphanages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孤兒院；孤兒收容機構","explanation":"指為失去父母或沒有父母照料的孩子提供居住、照料和保護的機構。它的核心畫面是為孤兒提供一個安全的生活場所。","examples":[{"en":"The children grew up in an orphanage after the war.","zh":"戰爭結束後，這些孩子在一家孤兒院長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity built a new orphanage in the village.","zh":"這家慈善機構在村裡建了一所新的孤兒院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orphanage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61b1716556bbcf1f4c27","word":"orthodox","forms":["orthodox"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a500c18111cf5588","term":"orthodox","forms":["orthodox","more orthodox","most orthodox"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正統的；符合教義的","explanation":"指符合某種宗教、思想體系或信仰團體所認可的正式教義，也就是被視為“正路”的觀點或做法。","examples":[{"en":"The committee rejected the proposal as unorthodox and defended the orthodox teaching.","zh":"委員會認為這項提議不合正統，因此為正統教義辯護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His interpretation is orthodox within this religious tradition.","zh":"他的解釋在這一宗教傳統中屬於正統觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orthodox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47d80bf4a8f02127","term":"orthodox","forms":["orthodox","more orthodox","most orthodox"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傳統的；循規蹈矩的","explanation":"從宗教教義擴大到一般生活，表示遵循習慣、傳統或多數人認可的做法，而不是新奇或非主流的做法。","examples":[{"en":"She took an orthodox approach to solving the problem.","zh":"她用傳統的方法解決了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She preferred an orthodox treatment to experimental remedies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orthodox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9298a10d1b0735837dc","word":"other","forms":["other"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af75b60efb76637e","term":"other","forms":["other"],"pos":"adj","zh":"見下列限定詞用法","explanation":"這裡的形容詞用法與限定詞用法相連，核心概念仍是“不是先前提到的那個，而是另一個或其餘的”。","examples":[{"en":"We tried the other key, and the lock opened immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The other passengers were already waiting on the platform.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/other","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f98eebe586edcf9","term":"other","forms":["other"],"pos":"adj","zh":"第二個；隔一個","explanation":"在兩個或按規律排列的物件中，other 可以指第二個，也可以表示“每隔一個”。例如按周計算時，every other week 就是“每隔一週”。","examples":[{"en":"We meet every other Friday.","zh":"我們每隔一個星期五見一次面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The other door is open.","zh":"另一扇門開著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/other","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1e513e51b597f48","term":"other","forms":["other"],"pos":"det","zh":"另一個；其他的","explanation":"它指前面已經提到的物件以外的人或物：可以是同一組中的其他成員，也可以是兩者中的另一方。","examples":[{"en":"Do you have any other questions?","zh":"你還有其他問題嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have no other source of income.","zh":"我沒有其他收入來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/other","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e48aec36376384325d6","word":"otherwise","forms":["otherwise"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2761be630bc34d10","term":"otherwise","forms":["otherwise"],"pos":"adv","zh":"以另一種方式","explanation":"它表示不按前面提到的方式來，而是換一種看法、做法或結果；核心畫面就是“換一條路”。","examples":[{"en":"I know what the instructions say, but I decided to do otherwise.","zh":"我知道說明上寫了什麼，但我決定換一種做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you think otherwise, please explain your reasons.","zh":"如果你有不同看法，請說明理由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/otherwise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72a234ccbb66bea7","term":"otherwise","forms":["otherwise"],"pos":"adv","zh":"否則；要不然","explanation":"這裡表示條件不變就會有某個結果，換個情況則會不同，通常可譯為“否則”或“要不然”。","examples":[{"en":"Take an umbrella, otherwise you may get soaked.","zh":"帶把傘吧，否則你可能會被淋溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to leave now; otherwise, we will miss the train.","zh":"我們現在得出發了，不然就趕不上火車了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/otherwise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35b749ee397805804b26","word":"ounce","forms":["ounce"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-693310eea6044336","term":"ounce","forms":["ounce","ounces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"常衡盎司","explanation":"最常見的重量義是常衡盎司，十六盎司合一磅，約等於二十八點三五克。它常用於食品、包裹和日常物品的重量。","examples":[{"en":"This package weighs eight ounces.","zh":"這個包裹重八盎司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add two ounces of cheese to the salad.","zh":"在沙拉里加兩盎司乳酪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2f130de5cd64f23","term":"ounce","forms":["ounce","ounces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一丁點","explanation":"從“一小份”的具體概念引申出來，表示非常少的一點，常用於感情、品質或抽象事物。它不再是精確的計量單位，而是強調數量少得幾乎可以忽略。","examples":[{"en":"She showed not an ounce of fear.","zh":"她沒有表現出一絲恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I haven't an ounce of patience left for these delays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-762069bc07a6e1b5df12","word":"out","forms":["out"],"officialPos":"adv./prep./adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd761e385f68b1e2","term":"out","forms":["out"],"pos":"adj","zh":"在外面","explanation":"表示人或物已經越過裡面的邊界，處在外面，不在原來的地方或容器中。","examples":[{"en":"The children are out in the garden.","zh":"孩子們在外面的花園裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The key is out of the lock.","zh":"鑰匙已經從鎖裡拔出來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/out","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ecec8989745d2b9","term":"out","forms":["out"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向外；出來","explanation":"表示人或物從裡面向外移動，越過原來的邊界。","examples":[{"en":"A small bird flew out of the open window.","zh":"一隻小鳥從開著的窗戶飛了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please take the books out of the box.","zh":"請把書從箱子裡拿出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/out","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c29d0959d9d4558","term":"out","forms":["out"],"pos":"prep","zh":"從……裡面出來","explanation":"表示人或物從某個內部空間越過邊界到外面，和記憶中的“向外、在外面”直接對應。它常見於口語中的非標準或受地域影響的表達。","examples":[{"en":"He threw the old newspapers out the window.","zh":"他把舊報紙從窗戶扔了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to get that thought out your mind.","zh":"儘量把那個念頭從腦子裡趕出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/out","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90876a808da78717","term":"out","forms":["out","outs","outing","outed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出來；顯露","explanation":"表示人或物出來、離開原來的範圍，也可指事實或真相最終顯露出來。無論是哪一種，都是某物越過隱蔽或內部的邊界，進入可見範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The truth will out, no matter how carefully they hide it.","zh":"不管他們藏得多嚴，真相終究會大白。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The moon came out after the clouds moved away.","zh":"雲層散開後，月亮露了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/out","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f07b1ea81964e88ad493","word":"outbreak","forms":["outbreak"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4438dacfc599fdee","term":"outbreak","forms":["outbreak","outbreaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疾病等突然爆發","explanation":"指疾病、傳染病或皮疹等原本沒有大規模出現的現象突然爆發，重點是突然出現並可能迅速影響許多人。","examples":[{"en":"The town reported an outbreak of flu in several schools.","zh":"這個城鎮報告說，幾所學校出現了流感暴發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Health workers acted quickly to contain the outbreak.","zh":"衛生工作人員迅速採取行動控制這次疫情暴發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outbreak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25a63e52a98f6fdaa618","word":"outcome","forms":["outcome"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d33e3f6d880acae5","term":"outcome","forms":["outcome","outcomes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結果；結局","explanation":"指某個事件、行動或過程最後產生的結果，是 outcome 最核心、最廣泛的意思。這個結果可以是好的、壞的，也可以只是客觀上發生的情況。","examples":[{"en":"The outcome of the meeting was better than we expected.","zh":"會議的結果比我們預想的更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Good planning can lead to a successful outcome.","zh":"周密的計劃可以帶來成功的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outcome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cc50230c38c4b45","term":"outcome","forms":["outcome","outcomes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機率試驗的可能結果","explanation":"在機率論中，outcome 是一次隨機試驗可能得到的一個具體結果。例如擲骰子時出現三點，就是一個 outcome；所有可能結果合在一起構成樣本空間。","examples":[{"en":"Getting an even number is one possible outcome when you roll a die.","zh":"擲骰子時，得到偶數是一個可能結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rolling a six is one possible outcome of the trial.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outcome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f472b2f2983102a207f","word":"outdoor","forms":["outdoor"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e2213d1dde1a9c47","term":"outdoor","forms":["outdoor"],"pos":"adj","zh":"戶外的；露天的","explanation":"指位於露天、設計成在露天使用，或本身就在戶外進行的事物，和室內環境相對。可以把它記成“走出門、接觸外面的空氣”。","examples":[{"en":"We bought outdoor chairs for the garden.","zh":"我們給花園買了戶外椅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school offers several outdoor activities in spring.","zh":"這所學校春天提供幾項戶外活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outdoor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc722fdb1dad80255de3","word":"outdoors","forms":["outdoors"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd3c68def1d3eded","term":"outdoors","forms":["outdoors"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在戶外；露天","explanation":"指人在房屋或其他有遮蓋的建築外面、露天的空氣中；核心畫面就是從室內走到外面。","examples":[{"en":"We went outdoors after dinner to enjoy the cool air.","zh":"晚飯後我們到戶外去享受涼爽的空氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children spent the afternoon playing outdoors.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在戶外玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outdoors","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-560e3e12b1e0dafa161e","word":"outer","forms":["outer"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-155d36ef05389033","term":"outer","forms":["outer","outermore","outermost","outmost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外部的；外層的","explanation":"指處在某物外面或構成其外部邊界的部分，與內部相對。","examples":[{"en":"The outer door was locked, but the inner door was open.","zh":"外門鎖著，但內門開著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rain began to tap against the outer windows.","zh":"雨開始敲打外側的窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4fd67d85241e3ac","term":"outer","forms":["outer","outermore","outermost","outmost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"更外側的；離中心更遠的","explanation":"在多個同心或相鄰部分中，指距離中心更遠、處在外圍的那一部分。","examples":[{"en":"The children waited beside the outer wall.","zh":"孩子們在外牆旁等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most of the damage was found along the outer edge.","zh":"大部分損壞出現在外緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c7732c423fb9c66a16a","word":"outfit","forms":["outfit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19e992089e521a9b","term":"outfit","forms":["outfit","outfits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一套衣服和配飾","explanation":"指搭配在一起、作為一個完整造型穿著的一套衣服，通常還包括鞋、包或其他配飾。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a simple black outfit to the dinner.","zh":"她穿了一身簡單的黑色衣服去參加晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need an outfit that goes well with these shoes.","zh":"我需要一套和這雙鞋很搭的衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outfit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f05818e10999a216","term":"outfit","forms":["outfit","outfits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一套專用裝備","explanation":"指為某項工作、活動或任務配齊的一組工具、用品或物資；重點不是外觀，而是這些東西共同服務於一個目的。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers carried a lightweight camping outfit.","zh":"這些徒步者帶了一套輕便的露營裝備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diving outfit includes a mask, fins, and an air tank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outfit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f61e95ddcee1df8c","term":"outfit","forms":["outfit","outfits","outfitting","outfitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為某用途配備","explanation":"指按照某項任務或活動的需要，把衣物、工具、食物等必需品配給某人、某地或某個行動，使其準備就緒。","examples":[{"en":"The expedition was outfitted with warm clothes and medical supplies.","zh":"這支探險隊配備了保暖衣物和醫療用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They outfitted the van with beds and a cooker.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outfit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ec7f5066b80e4c0b207","word":"outgoing","forms":["outgoing"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88ea17fe92e6b4a0","term":"outgoing","forms":["outgoing","more outgoing","most outgoing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外向的；善於交際的","explanation":"指一個人願意主動接近別人，尤其是不怕和陌生人交談，顯得友好、健談而合群。這裡的“向外走”是從自己的圈子走向別人。","examples":[{"en":"Mia is outgoing and can start a conversation with almost anyone.","zh":"米婭性格外向，幾乎和誰都能聊起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became much more outgoing after joining the drama club.","zh":"加入戲劇社後，他變得外向多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outgoing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee7825b6d8c26871","term":"outgoing","forms":["outgoing","more outgoing","most outgoing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"發出的；正在外發的","explanation":"指郵件、包裹、航班等已經從某處向外傳送或正在離開。這裡不是說它“很外向”，而是說它正沿著“向外走”的方向移動。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the letter in the outgoing mail tray.","zh":"請把這封信放進待發郵件托盤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place outgoing mail in the tray by the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outgoing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ad6f401d5b53a420b6c","word":"outing","forms":["outing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed9e0a23e6d39ab9","term":"outing","forms":["outing","outings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外出遊玩","explanation":"指為了休閒而進行的一次短途外出或遊玩活動，重點是“走出去的一次活動”，不只是離開房間這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"We planned a family outing to the lake.","zh":"我們計劃了一次去湖邊的家庭郊遊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were excited about their first school outing.","zh":"孩子們對第一次學校郊遊感到很興奮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9043333359039d1e","term":"outing","forms":["outing","outings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公開亮相","explanation":"指演員、運動員等在公眾面前的一次表現，也可指某人參與的一部作品或一次公開活動；核心仍是“走到外介面前”。","examples":[{"en":"Her latest outing as a director has received strong reviews.","zh":"她最近一次以導演身份亮相的作品獲得了很好的評價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new striker scored on his first outing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31c74d4639ab2f1477ee","word":"outlaw","forms":["outlaw"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a93cf02e17d4dd93","term":"outlaw","forms":["outlaw","outlaws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"逃犯；法律之外的人","explanation":"指逃避法律追捕，或被法律排除在正常保護之外的人。核心畫面是這個人被推到了法律圈外，因此不能再像普通人一樣依靠法律保護。","examples":[{"en":"The sheriff warned that the outlaw was still hiding in the hills.","zh":"治安官警告說，那名逃犯仍躲在山裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The outlaw hid in the mountains beyond the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7f0d8568ddc96ac","term":"outlaw","forms":["outlaw","outlaws","outlawing","outlawed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"宣佈違法","explanation":"指正式宣佈某種行為、事物或做法不再合法，把它推出法律允許的範圍。這個義項直接延續了“推到法律圈外”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The new law outlaws the sale of fireworks to children.","zh":"新法律宣佈向兒童出售煙花違法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new law outlaws dumping waste in rivers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6335d111cbfa97f0","term":"outlaw","forms":["outlaw","outlaws","outlawing","outlawed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"禁止","explanation":"指透過法律或正式規定禁止某種行為、產品或做法，使其不能再合法進行。它和“宣佈違法”緊密相連，重點是建立明確的禁令。","examples":[{"en":"The city plans to outlaw parking on this narrow street.","zh":"市政府計劃禁止在這條狹窄的街道上停車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law outlaws dumping waste in rivers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlaw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7647af7af268c583c941","word":"outlet","forms":["outlet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f83f7f5adbad1a4","term":"outlet","forms":["outlet","outlets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出口；排放口","explanation":"指讓空氣、煙、水等從裡面出去的孔、管道或通道，是“向外開的口”這一核心概念的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Make sure the air outlet is not blocked.","zh":"請確保通風口沒有被堵住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pipe has an outlet at the back of the machine.","zh":"這臺機器後面有一個管道出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf9545c5e9849d75","term":"outlet","forms":["outlet","outlets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"品牌直銷店；折扣店","explanation":"指某個製造商或供應商直接銷售自己產品的商店，商品常以較低價格出售；這裡可以把它想成商品走向顧客的“銷售出口”。","examples":[{"en":"We bought these shoes at the company outlet.","zh":"我們在這家公司的直銷店買了這雙鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought discounted coats at a factory outlet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b35ce1b9a17a2d44","term":"outlet","forms":["outlet","outlets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電源插座","explanation":"指牆上或其他表面安裝的電源插孔，電器可以從這裡接取電流；它是電流向外供出的一個“口”。","examples":[{"en":"The lamp is plugged into the outlet beside the sofa.","zh":"檯燈插在沙發旁邊的電源插座上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This adapter lets two appliances share a single outlet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-318678825324247b8176","word":"outline","forms":["outline"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8526909e043f85d1","term":"outline","forms":["outline","outlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輪廓線","explanation":"指沿著物體或圖形邊界畫出的線，用來標出它的外邊緣。","examples":[{"en":"She drew the outline of a tree before adding the leaves.","zh":"她先畫出樹的輪廓，然後再添上樹葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The moonlit outline of the castle appeared above the trees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3e329f3ef0cd172","term":"outline","forms":["outline","outlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外形輪廓","explanation":"指一個物體或建築從外部看呈現出的整體形狀，也就是它的外在輪廓。","examples":[{"en":"The outline of the mountains was clear against the evening sky.","zh":"群山的輪廓映襯在傍晚的天空中，十分清晰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mountain's outline appeared against the pale sky.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9cc158f487f15d9a","term":"outline","forms":["outline","outlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內容提要","explanation":"指把文章、書或報告中的重要觀點和結構列出來的概要，幫助讀者快速看懂主要內容。","examples":[{"en":"Before writing the essay, I made an outline of my main arguments.","zh":"寫文章前，我列出了主要論點的提綱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The outline lists the main stages of the project.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b0a3f5d5a147da0","term":"outline","forms":["outline","outlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"初步計劃","explanation":"指專案、演講或其他工作的初步結構安排，只確定主要步驟和內容，之後還可以繼續修改。","examples":[{"en":"I prepared an outline for my presentation last night.","zh":"我昨晚為演講準備了一個提綱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She submitted an outline of her proposed research.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41aac5f016d873e9","term":"outline","forms":["outline","outlines","outlining","outlined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勾畫輪廓","explanation":"指沿著某個物體或圖形的邊緣畫線，也可引申為清楚地勾勒出它的外形。","examples":[{"en":"The artist outlined the building in black ink.","zh":"畫家用黑墨水勾出了那座建築的輪廓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She outlined the leaf with a fine pencil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15e21a947a718a66","term":"outline","forms":["outline","outlines","outlining","outlined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"概述","explanation":"指用簡潔方式說明某件事的主要內容、要點或步驟，不展開所有細節。","examples":[{"en":"The manager outlined the plan for the next month.","zh":"經理概述了下個月的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She outlined the proposal before discussing the costs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f53c6c301f98610918a","word":"outlook","forms":["outlook"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-970d2f9a94511a85","term":"outlook","forms":["outlook","outlooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"態度；看法","explanation":"把“向外看”的畫面轉到人的內心：outlook 指一個人看待生活、工作或世界的總體態度和角度。","examples":[{"en":"Her cheerful outlook helped the team through a difficult month.","zh":"她樂觀的態度幫助團隊度過了艱難的一個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Travel broadened his outlook on life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd9a07e827443c3f","term":"outlook","forms":["outlook","outlooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前景；預期","explanation":"指根據目前情況向外看、推測未來會怎樣，常用於經濟、天氣、健康或某項計劃的發展前景。","examples":[{"en":"The outlook for the local economy is improving.","zh":"當地經濟的前景正在改善。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The economic outlook improved after exports recovered.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outlook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e4561fb0760e8059d34","word":"outnumber","forms":["outnumber"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c42eb07e77852a25","term":"outnumber","forms":["outnumber","outnumbers","outnumbering","outnumbered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"數量超過","explanation":"指某人群或事物的數量比另一個人群或事物更多，核心是“數目佔優勢”，不一定表示其他方面更強。","examples":[{"en":"In this village, children outnumber adults by nearly two to one.","zh":"在這個村子裡，孩子的人數幾乎是成年人的兩倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors outnumber residents during the summer festival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outnumber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0ee8bb50685e05fa0f4","word":"output","forms":["output"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c883ff1a1c07550f","term":"output","forms":["output","outputs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"產出；產量；成果","explanation":"output 是某個工廠、系統、活動或一段努力向外產生的東西，重點可以是數量，也可以是最終成果。它既能指一個時期的總產量，也能指某項工作做出的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The factory's output rose sharply in the second half of the year.","zh":"這家工廠下半年的產量大幅提高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her research output has grown steadily since she joined the university.","zh":"她加入這所大學以來，科研成果一直穩步增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/output","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ec242e7bd2b85e8","term":"output","forms":["output","outputs","outputting","outputted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"產出；生產","explanation":"作動詞時，output 表示把產品、數量或成果做出來並向外產出，強調產出的結果或規模，而不是製作過程本身。","examples":[{"en":"The plant can output 5,000 batteries a day.","zh":"這家工廠每天可以生產五千塊電池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory outputs thousands of components each day.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/output","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acd8e304dea093e7","term":"output","forms":["output","outputs","outputting","outputted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輸出資料","explanation":"在計算機語境中，output 表示程式或裝置把資料向外傳送，使資料顯示在螢幕上、列印出來，或傳給另一個程式；核心仍是“把東西放出去”。","examples":[{"en":"The program outputs the results to a text file.","zh":"這個程式把結果輸出到一個文字檔案中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program writes its output to a separate file.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/output","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-713d66baefcd7ea248b7","word":"outrage","forms":["outrage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0488de31589c2f0","term":"outrage","forms":["outrage","outrages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴行；殘酷襲擊","explanation":"指嚴重、殘暴而越過正常界限的攻擊或暴行，重點在行為本身的惡劣程度。","examples":[{"en":"The attack was described as an outrage against innocent civilians.","zh":"這次襲擊被稱為針對無辜平民的暴行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report documents several outrages committed during the war.","zh":"這份報告記錄了戰爭期間發生的幾起暴行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outrage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21b83f23deaeb720","term":"outrage","forms":["outrage","outrages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"義憤；憤怒","explanation":"指人們因暴行、不公或嚴重冒犯而產生的強烈、帶有道德譴責的憤怒。","examples":[{"en":"The ruling sparked public outrage across the country.","zh":"這項裁決在全國引發了公憤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She expressed outrage at the unfair treatment of the workers.","zh":"她對工人受到的不公平對待表示憤慨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outrage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-831f5b4d514a120d","term":"outrage","forms":["outrage","outrages","outraging","outraged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使義憤填膺","explanation":"表示某個行為、決定或言論嚴重冒犯道德感，從而使人強烈憤怒和震驚。","examples":[{"en":"The leaked images outraged the public.","zh":"洩露的圖片激起了公眾的義憤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was outraged by the manager's refusal to help.","zh":"經理拒絕幫忙讓她感到非常憤慨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outrage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d560e0630ab7cc86d34b","word":"outrageous","forms":["outrageous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-668df822fda1b50b","term":"outrageous","forms":["outrageous","more outrageous","most outrageous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人憤怒的；有傷風化的","explanation":"形容行為、言論或情形越過了道德和體面的紅線，因此使人感到憤怒、被冒犯或難以接受。","examples":[{"en":"The company made an outrageous decision to cut medical benefits without warning.","zh":"這家公司毫無預警地削減醫療福利，做法令人憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was outrageous to blame the children for the accident.","zh":"把那起事故歸咎於孩子們，實在令人無法接受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outrageous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13c0a7e5b1b7758a","term":"outrageous","forms":["outrageous","more outrageous","most outrageous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其誇張的；離譜的","explanation":"形容某事遠遠超出合理或適度的範圍，誇張得不像正常情況，常譯為“離譜”“過分”。它不一定涉及道德問題，也可以只是數量、價格、要求或說法太過頭。","examples":[{"en":"They charged us an outrageous price for two bottles of water.","zh":"他們兩瓶水竟然收了我們高得離譜的價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His outrageous demand left everyone in the room speechless.","zh":"他那離譜的要求讓房間裡的所有人都說不出話來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outrageous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4086219366ba1a357455","word":"outright","forms":["outright"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0564ff98ca499bfe","term":"outright","forms":["outright"],"pos":"adj","zh":"毫不保留的；明確的","explanation":"指態度、要求或行為完全明確，不留餘地，也沒有試探或保留。它突出的是“說清楚、做到底”的態度。","examples":[{"en":"The company issued an outright denial of the report.","zh":"公司明確否認了這則報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His response was an outright refusal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-220436f94edd5f30","term":"outright","forms":["outright"],"pos":"adj","zh":"徹底的；完全的","explanation":"指某種優勢、勝利或控制達到完整、壓倒性的程度，幾乎沒有留下可爭議的空間。它和“把事情推到盡頭”的核心畫面相連。","examples":[{"en":"Their outright victory surprised everyone.","zh":"他們壓倒性的勝利讓所有人都感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The negotiations ended in outright failure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7856090761ed622a","term":"outright","forms":["outright"],"pos":"adv","zh":"完全地；徹底地","explanation":"表示某事被徹底完成、否定或消除，沒有留下部分或餘地。它是“把事情推到盡頭”作為副詞的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She rejected the accusation outright.","zh":"她完全否認了這一指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought the car outright rather than arranging monthly payments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d0c2002b4b9acc52bc9","word":"outset","forms":["outset"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-065a3dbc50e25620","term":"outset","forms":["outset","outsets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開始；起初","explanation":"指一件事剛剛開始的時刻或最初階段，也就是整件事展開之前的起點。","examples":[{"en":"She understood the plan from the outset.","zh":"她從一開始就明白這個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We agreed on the deadline at the outset.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31207a2065f46a5b948f","word":"outside","forms":["outside"],"officialPos":"prep./adv./adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37225a4d8b9638fb","term":"outside","forms":["outside","more outside","most outside"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外部的；外面的","explanation":"指某物朝向外面或位於邊界外側的部分，例如建築物的外表面。它是“在裡面”這個概念的直接反面。","examples":[{"en":"The outside surface looks clean now.","zh":"外表面現在看起來很乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The outside wall needs a fresh coat of paint.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d265a2a5a68dbd59","term":"outside","forms":["outside","more outside","most outside"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到外面；在外面","explanation":"表示人或物從內部到外部，或已經處在外部位置，是“外”這個核心概念最常見的動態用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children ran outside when the rain stopped.","zh":"雨停後，孩子們跑到了外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I left my shoes outside.","zh":"我把鞋子留在外面了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc31f5c15a83e1ae","term":"outside","forms":["outside","outsides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外部；外表面","explanation":"指物體朝外的那一部分，例如房屋的外面或容器的外表面。","examples":[{"en":"The outside of the house needs a fresh coat of paint.","zh":"這棟房子的外面需要重新刷一層漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Paint the outside before replacing the window frames.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c7c61a9d5450c2d","term":"outside","forms":["outside","outsides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外部空間；外界","explanation":"指某個邊界、建築或封閉範圍之外的空間。","examples":[{"en":"From the outside, the old building looked empty.","zh":"從外面看，那座老建築像是空的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The windows keep much of the outside out.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc9f768898f75088","term":"outside","forms":["outside"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……外面","explanation":"表示某人或某物位於建築物、容器或其他具體邊界之外。","examples":[{"en":"A taxi is waiting outside the hotel.","zh":"一輛計程車正在酒店外面等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We waited outside the locked theater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8977913fcc5dcbc16c9d","word":"outsider","forms":["outsider"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0de984c5a36cfb31","term":"outsider","forms":["outsider","outsiders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圈外人","explanation":"指不屬於某個社群、組織、團體或圈子的人。這個人站在群體的“外面”，因此可能不瞭解內部規則、符號或關係。","examples":[{"en":"As an outsider to the industry, she noticed problems that insiders had ignored.","zh":"作為這個行業的圈外人，她注意到了業內人士忽視的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The club's rules can seem confusing to outsiders.","zh":"這個俱樂部的規則對圈外人來說可能很難理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outsider","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb036e8610cc7314","term":"outsider","forms":["outsider","outsiders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新來者","explanation":"指剛進入某個組織或社群、幾乎沒有內部經驗的人。這個意思仍然來自“站在圈子外面”，只是強調他正在進入、還沒有熟悉圈內做法。","examples":[{"en":"As an outsider in the company, he asked questions that everyone else took for granted.","zh":"作為公司的新來者，他提出了一些其他人習以為常的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As an outsider, she needed time to understand local customs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outsider","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f2e9e1cc05b26ab778f","word":"outskirts","forms":["outskirts"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0d130677f99f900","term":"outskirts","forms":["outskirts","outskirt"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城市外圍","explanation":"想象城市中心外面圍著一圈邊緣地帶，這個外圍區域就是 outskirts；它可以包括住宅、道路或其他城市邊緣地帶。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a small house on the outskirts of the city.","zh":"他們在城市外圍買了一棟小房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A new hospital is being built on the outskirts of town.","zh":"城鎮外圍正在修建一所新醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outskirts","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab39a00236186da7aef1","word":"outstanding","forms":["outstanding"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6df0d7033e4ec654","term":"outstanding","forms":["outstanding","more outstanding","most outstanding"],"pos":"adj","zh":"突出顯眼","explanation":"某人或某物明顯地站在其他事物前面，因此特別引人注意，甚至處於顯著或主導位置。","examples":[{"en":"The red tower is outstanding against the white buildings.","zh":"那座紅色的塔在白色建築中格外顯眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An outstanding rock interrupted the otherwise smooth cliff face.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outstanding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-060dc9ca83ff5f33","term":"outstanding","forms":["outstanding","more outstanding","most outstanding"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傑出的；極出色的","explanation":"某人的能力、成就或某件事的質量遠遠超過一般水平，因此顯得特別優秀、值得注意。","examples":[{"en":"She received an award for her outstanding work in medicine.","zh":"她因在醫學領域的傑出工作而獲獎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is an outstanding teacher who makes difficult ideas clear.","zh":"他是一位傑出的老師，能把難懂的概念講清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outstanding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d16f739f94eddd6300d","word":"outward","forms":["outward"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ab8fc4870d0d82f","term":"outward","forms":["outward","more outward","most outward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外部的；向外的","explanation":"指位於某物外側，或朝著外部的方向；核心畫面就是從中心向外伸展。","examples":[{"en":"The outward wall of the old house needs repair.","zh":"這座老房子的外牆需要修理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The windows open outward.","zh":"這些窗戶向外開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-593b443603456466","term":"outward","forms":["outward","more outward","most outward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"外在可見的","explanation":"指能從外表、行為或明顯跡象中觀察到的，不一定反映真實的內在情況。","examples":[{"en":"Her outward calm hid how worried she was.","zh":"她表面上的平靜掩蓋了她內心的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By all outward signs, the project was a success.","zh":"從各種表面跡象看，這個專案是成功的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd026f964c7c30264dbb","word":"outward/outwards","forms":["outward","outwards"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99942973e744dddc","term":"outward","forms":["outward","more outward","most outward"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向外；離開中心","explanation":"表示動作從中心向外部移動，或離開原來的內部位置；仍然是“箭頭朝外”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The branches spread outward from the trunk.","zh":"樹枝從樹幹向外伸展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are outward bound for the coast.","zh":"我們正出發前往海岸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc033227bcbd7242","term":"outwards","forms":["outwards","more outwards","most outwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向外；朝外","explanation":"表示從內部、中心或某個起點向外部移動、延伸或反射。核心畫面是“從裡往外走”，因此可用於光線、力量、物體或身體動作等。","examples":[{"en":"The doors open outwards.","zh":"這些門向外開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The branches spread outwards from the trunk.","zh":"樹枝從樹幹向外伸展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fb847f1d0c26c90eefa","word":"oval","forms":["oval"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f15f374809aabb4","term":"oval","forms":["oval","more oval","most oval"],"pos":"adj","zh":"橢圓形的；蛋形的","explanation":"表示外形像拉長的圓或雞蛋，兩端通常較圓，中間向外彎曲。它就是記憶主線中的“像蛋一樣的形狀”。","examples":[{"en":"They bought an oval table for the dining room.","zh":"他們為餐廳買了一張橢圓形的桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden has an oval pond in the middle.","zh":"花園中央有一個橢圓形的池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcece2df24750b84","term":"oval","forms":["oval","ovals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橢圓；橢圓形","explanation":"指像雞蛋一樣拉長的圓形本身，是形容詞“橢圓形的”所描述的那個形狀。","examples":[{"en":"Draw an oval around the correct answer.","zh":"在正確答案周圍畫一個橢圓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child colored the oval blue.","zh":"孩子把這個橢圓塗成了藍色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oval","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4908abbcc9666d67bb3e","word":"oven","forms":["oven"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cf71ce35844f143","term":"oven","forms":["oven","ovens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烤箱","explanation":"一種封閉的加熱空間，用來烘烤麵包、蛋糕、肉類等食物，也可以加熱食物。記住“東西放進高溫空間裡變熟”這個核心畫面即可。","examples":[{"en":"The bread is baking in the oven.","zh":"麵包正在烤箱裡烘烤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Preheat the oven to 180 degrees.","zh":"把烤箱預熱到180度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oven","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf358b038bf7479d","term":"oven","forms":["oven","ovens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱得像烤箱的地方","explanation":"比喻某個房間或場所熱得難受、悶得像一個烤箱。這裡不是說那裡真的有烤箱，而是借用烤箱的高溫形象來強調炎熱。","examples":[{"en":"The bus was an oven without any air conditioning.","zh":"沒有空調的公交車裡熱得像烤箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By midday, the parked car was an oven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oven","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5fb6a47e368e12e5d8b1","word":"over","forms":["over"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05fd1666587daaa8","term":"over","forms":["over"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從頭到尾地","explanation":"表示把事情完整地檢查、討論或處理一遍，像沿著一條線從起點越到終點。","examples":[{"en":"Let's go over the plan once more before we start.","zh":"開始前我們再把計劃完整檢查一遍吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She went over the report carefully.","zh":"她仔細地審閱了那份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/over","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-289d38ad6e117329","term":"over","forms":["over"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在上方；越過","explanation":"表示某物位於另一物上方，或從其上方經過。它直接對應“從上方越過去”的記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A lamp hangs over the dining table.","zh":"餐桌上方掛著一盞燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers climbed over the fallen tree.","zh":"徒步者翻過了倒下的樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/over","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1deb3268b977bb92590","word":"overall","forms":["overall"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c28bc91f65c08010","term":"overall","forms":["overall","more overall","most overall"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全面的；總體的","explanation":"指涉及一個事物的全部方面或整體情況，不侷限於其中一個部分。","examples":[{"en":"The overall quality of the service has improved.","zh":"這項服務的總體質量提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need an overall plan before we start.","zh":"我們開始之前需要一個全面的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce4c81f805c46d1e","term":"overall","forms":["overall"],"pos":"adv","zh":"總的來說","explanation":"把各方面情況放在一起考慮後，給出一個總體判斷。","examples":[{"en":"Overall, the meeting was useful, despite a few problems.","zh":"總的來說，儘管有一些問題，這次會議還是很有用的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Overall, the exhibition attracted more visitors than expected.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7524b5d326a2c8b4745","word":"overcoat","forms":["overcoat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-891112aca5efefd5","term":"overcoat","forms":["overcoat","overcoats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"厚外套","explanation":"指穿在其他衣服外面、主要用來保暖或抵擋寒冷天氣的外套。核心畫面就是在衣服外面再蓋上一層保護。","examples":[{"en":"She put on her overcoat before leaving the house.","zh":"她出門前穿上了外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I forgot my overcoat, and the walk home was freezing.","zh":"我忘了帶外套，走回家時冷得不得了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overcoat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e4d65166ca1411d011d","word":"overcome","forms":["overcome"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-374258b19abb0c0c","term":"overcome","forms":["overcome","overcomes","overcoming","overcame"],"pos":"verb","zh":"克服；戰勝障礙","explanation":"把身體上的障礙或抽象的難題壓過去、越過去，從而成功解決或控制它。這裡強調主動付出力量後取得勝利。","examples":[{"en":"She overcame her fear of public speaking.","zh":"她克服了當眾演講的恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With patience, we can overcome this difficulty.","zh":"只要有耐心，我們就能克服這個困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overcome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8ca2b9dfa5620a0","term":"overcome","forms":["overcome","overcomes","overcoming","overcame"],"pos":"verb","zh":"熬過；恢復","explanation":"指經歷困難、疾病、悲傷或打擊後逐漸走出來，恢復正常狀態；這裡的“越過”更像是從難關的另一邊出來。","examples":[{"en":"He eventually overcame the shock of the accident.","zh":"他最終從那場事故的打擊中恢復了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team overcame several setbacks during the season.","zh":"這個團隊在整個賽季中克服了幾次挫折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overcome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-982b2b5ca74ffd828b67","word":"overdo","forms":["overdo"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82c213bb2d795d9c","term":"overdo","forms":["overdo","overdoes","overdoing","overdid","overdone"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做得過頭；過度","explanation":"指做某件事超過合適、真實或自然的程度，常常暗示結果不理想。比如吃得太多、裝飾太誇張，或把某種情緒表現得過火，都可以說是 overdo。","examples":[{"en":"I overdid the decorations and made the room feel crowded.","zh":"我把裝飾弄得太過了，房間顯得很擁擠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can be confident, but don't overdo it.","zh":"你可以自信一點，但別表現得過頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overdo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a09628a87782b8c","term":"overdo","forms":["overdo","overdoes","overdoing","overdid","overdone"],"pos":"verb","zh":"煮過頭","explanation":"專指食物烹調時間太長，導致口感變差；這是“做得過頭”在烹飪中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"Take the fish out now, or you'll overdo it.","zh":"現在把魚拿出來，不然就會煮過頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't overdo the pasta; it should remain slightly firm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overdo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94fa3e5538d57f71937a","word":"overflow","forms":["overflow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46b50d37ae60c725","term":"overflow","forms":["overflow","overflows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溢位的東西","explanation":"指液體或其他物質越過邊界後流出來的部分，重點是“已經溢位來的多餘物”，而不只是溢位的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The overflow from the bathtub spread across the bathroom floor.","zh":"浴缸溢位的水流到了整個浴室地面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sandbags kept the river overflow away from the houses.","zh":"沙袋擋住了河水溢流，沒讓它流到房屋附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overflow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-baf6386f4cf0d2cd","term":"overflow","forms":["overflow","overflows","overflowing","overflowed","overflown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"溢位容器或邊界","explanation":"指液體越過容器、河岸或其他邊界流出，是“超過邊界並流出來”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The soup overflowed the pot and spilled onto the stove.","zh":"湯從鍋裡溢了出來，灑到了爐子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the storm, the river overflowed into the fields.","zh":"暴風雨過後，河水溢進了田地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overflow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4e085068ca561fd5","term":"overflow","forms":["overflow","overflows","overflowing","overflowed","overflown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"溢流到某處","explanation":"指液體或人流越過原來的邊界，繼續流入或擴散到另一個地方，是“溢位後向外延伸”的不及物用法。","examples":[{"en":"Water from the broken pipe overflowed into the hallway.","zh":"破裂水管裡的水溢進了走廊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans overflowed into the streets after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，粉絲多得走到了街上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overflow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-945c8f9d4fe6b4899a55","word":"overhead","forms":["overhead"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59b3596c0775ec49","term":"overhead","forms":["overhead","more overhead","most overhead"],"pos":"adj","zh":"頭頂上方的","explanation":"指位置在人的頭頂上方，通常強調正上方或從上方覆蓋過來。這是 overhead 最基本、最容易延伸出其他義項的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please put your coat in the overhead compartment.","zh":"請把外套放進頭頂上方的行李艙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An overhead lamp lit the narrow hallway.","zh":"一盞頂燈照亮了狹窄的走廊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overhead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b494ea1277db465","term":"overhead","forms":["overhead","more overhead","most overhead"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在頭頂上方","explanation":"表示某物位於說話者頭頂上方，或在頭頂上方飛過、經過。","examples":[{"en":"We heard an airplane passing overhead.","zh":"我們聽見一架飛機從頭頂上方飛過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flock of geese passed overhead.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overhead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8dba3755f1b6ddea","term":"overhead","forms":["overhead","overheads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"間接經營成本","explanation":"指不能直接歸到某件商品或服務上的業務開支，例如辦公場地、管理和日常運營費用。它像覆蓋整個業務的一層成本，而不是某件產品本身的材料成本。","examples":[{"en":"The small business keeps its overhead low by working from home.","zh":"這家小企業透過在家辦公來壓低間接經營成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rent is one of our biggest overhead costs.","zh":"房租是我們最大的一項間接成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overhead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e79924ec4dd30ec690a","word":"overhear","forms":["overhear"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"overhear","forms":["overhear"],"pos":"v.","zh":"無意中聽到","examples":[{"en":"I did not mean to overhear your private conversation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Passengers could overhear the driver talking to the police.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe55bd22d9475bdebec3","word":"overlap","forms":["overlap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa0517f58c92b132","term":"overlap","forms":["overlap","overlaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重疊；交疊部分","explanation":"指兩個物體、範圍或事物部分蓋在一起或部分相同的狀態。它強調“有一部分相交”，不表示全部一致。","examples":[{"en":"There is considerable overlap between the two training programs.","zh":"這兩個培訓專案有相當多的內容重合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We marked the overlap in red so both editors could coordinate revisions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overlap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0994862211b26b0","term":"overlap","forms":["overlap","overlaps","overlapping","overlapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"部分覆蓋","explanation":"指一個物體伸到另一個物體上方，並把它的一部分蓋住；也可以不帶賓語，表示兩個物體彼此交疊。","examples":[{"en":"The edge of the cloth overlapped the table.","zh":"布的邊緣蓋過了桌子的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two circles overlap in the middle.","zh":"這兩個圓在中間部分重疊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overlap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8e5a6f807f7ec9f","term":"overlap","forms":["overlap","overlaps","overlapping","overlapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"時間重合","explanation":"指兩個事件或活動在同一段時間發生，因此時間上有一部分相同。","examples":[{"en":"My morning class overlaps with the staff meeting.","zh":"我的早課和員工會議時間有衝突。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our shifts overlap for an hour at lunchtime.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overlap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-303197632307ae163114","word":"overlook","forms":["overlook"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32f27db4d60f2284","term":"overlook","forms":["overlook","overlooks","overlooking","overlooked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"俯瞰；臨高處看見","explanation":"某建築、房間或地點從較高位置可以看到某個地方，就可以說它 overlooks 那個地方；重點是視線從高處向下。","examples":[{"en":"Our room overlooks the harbor.","zh":"我們的房間俯瞰著港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The café overlooks the old town.","zh":"這家咖啡館可以俯瞰老城區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overlook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba6fdab95300f771","term":"overlook","forms":["overlook","overlooks","overlooking","overlooked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漏看；忽略","explanation":"視線從某件事上方越過去而沒有注意到它，因此 overlook 也表示因為疏忽而漏掉資訊、錯誤或細節。","examples":[{"en":"I overlooked a small error in the report.","zh":"我漏看了報告中的一個小錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor overlooked an important detail.","zh":"編輯忽略了一個重要細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overlook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fc96fd3f6c6be2a00ae","word":"overnight","forms":["overnight"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80ca0d9bcca6865e","term":"overnight","forms":["overnight"],"pos":"adj","zh":"夜間的；過夜的","explanation":"指發生在傍晚到第二天早晨之間，或需要人在外面住一晚的事物。核心畫面就是事情跨過了整夜。","examples":[{"en":"The overnight train arrives in the city before breakfast.","zh":"這趟夜行列車在早餐前抵達這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are going to an overnight camp this weekend.","zh":"孩子們這個週末要去參加一個過夜營。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overnight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-964c869fcac1e0bf","term":"overnight","forms":["overnight"],"pos":"adv","zh":"過夜；整夜","explanation":"表示某人留宿，或某件事從晚上持續到第二天早晨。它直接對應“跨過一夜”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"You can stay overnight at my place if the buses stop running.","zh":"如果公交車停運了，你可以在我家過夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the dough to rise overnight.","zh":"把麵糰放著發酵一夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overnight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4240e31b6a90fc542604","word":"overseas","forms":["overseas"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a6a5e85ca5c5721","term":"overseas","forms":["overseas"],"pos":"adj","zh":"海外的；國外的","explanation":"表示與本國相對的海外或國外，重點是地點在外國，而不一定強調具體隔著哪一片海。","examples":[{"en":"The company is expanding its overseas business.","zh":"這家公司正在拓展海外業務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Overseas branches of the company are doing well.","zh":"這家公司的海外分支機構經營得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overseas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-abd937387685b66a","term":"overseas","forms":["overseas"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在國外；到國外","explanation":"表示人在國外，或從本國前往國外，是副詞中最常用的意義；它把“越過海界”的畫面變成實際的去處或所在位置。","examples":[{"en":"He moved overseas for work.","zh":"他為了工作搬到了國外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has lived overseas for several years.","zh":"她已經在國外生活好幾年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overseas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d77f5f36b728b2bd3c0e","word":"oversee","forms":["oversee"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2777f04d497ab68","term":"oversee","forms":["oversee","oversees","overseeing","oversaw","overseen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"監督並指導","explanation":"表示負責監督某人、團隊、專案或工作，既要了解進展，也可能提出指導、檢查結果或作出管理決定。這是現代英語中最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She oversees a team of designers.","zh":"她負責監督一個設計師團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee oversees the use of public funds.","zh":"委員會負責監督公共資金的使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oversee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fbb8f6fde16b35bb0595","word":"overtake","forms":["overtake"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-403311a3910f843d","term":"overtake","forms":["overtake","overtakes","overtaking","overtook","overtaken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"趕上並超過；超車","explanation":"指原本在後面的車輛、騎手或人趕上前方較慢的一方，並從旁邊超過去。它把“趕上”和“超過”看成一個連續動作。","examples":[{"en":"The blue car overtook us just before the bridge.","zh":"那輛藍色汽車就在橋前超過了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She slowed down because she could not safely overtake the bus.","zh":"她放慢了速度，因為無法安全地超過那輛公共汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overtake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e23033d355f8471a93bb","word":"overthrow","forms":["overthrow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b34b15905583e147","term":"overthrow","forms":["overthrow","overthrows","overthrowing","overthrew","overthrown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推翻政權","explanation":"指透過武力或武力威脅使政府、政權或統治者垮臺，是動詞形式的“把權力扔倒”。","examples":[{"en":"The rebels overthrew the dictator after a long conflict.","zh":"長期衝突後，叛軍推翻了獨裁者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The people united to overthrow the corrupt regime.","zh":"人民團結起來推翻腐敗政權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overthrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0addbb3521001d3d342c","word":"overturn","forms":["overturn"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb05a7152be23f8a","term":"overturn","forms":["overturn","overturns","overturning","overturned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"翻倒；弄翻","explanation":"指物體翻過去或被弄翻，使原來的上下面倒置；這是“把東西徹底翻過來”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The strong waves overturned the fishing boat.","zh":"巨浪把漁船掀翻了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bus overturned on the icy road.","zh":"公共汽車在結冰的路上翻倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overturn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6358f25a3e8575a4","term":"overturn","forms":["overturn","overturns","overturning","overturned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推翻；摧毀","explanation":"指以強力使政府、制度、秩序或原有局面不再成立，相當於把整個局面翻到另一面。","examples":[{"en":"The revolution overturned the old political order.","zh":"這場革命推翻了舊的政治秩序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The invaders overturned centuries of customary land ownership.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overturn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e4fe0f9cec42dc740d1","word":"overwhelm","forms":["overwhelm"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-138591b1a5802bdb","term":"overwhelm","forms":["overwhelm","overwhelms","overwhelming","overwhelmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"淹沒；蓋過","explanation":"指水浪等從上面湧來，把某物整個蓋住並淹沒，直接對應“被一股力量壓過”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The rising river overwhelmed several low-lying houses.","zh":"上漲的河水淹沒了幾座低窪處的房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wall of water overwhelmed the low sea defenses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overwhelm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3c5aa0bdb5230a3","term":"overwhelm","forms":["overwhelm","overwhelms","overwhelming","overwhelmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓倒；擊潰","explanation":"指力量、數量或優勢大到足以擊敗對手，就像巨浪壓過小船一樣；也常表示以壓倒性優勢取勝。","examples":[{"en":"The home team overwhelmed its opponents in the second half.","zh":"主隊在下半場以壓倒性優勢擊敗了對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The larger force quickly overwhelmed the defenders.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overwhelm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc062ec0de2cfcee","term":"overwhelm","forms":["overwhelm","overwhelms","overwhelming","overwhelmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使不堪承受","explanation":"指強烈的情緒、責任、資訊或事務一下子壓過一個人的承受能力，使人感到無法應付；人也可以因喜悅、感激等強烈感情而有這種狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She was overwhelmed by the kindness of the people around her.","zh":"周圍人的善意讓她感動得不知所措。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt overwhelmed by the amount of work waiting for me.","zh":"面對堆積如山的工作，我感到實在應付不過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overwhelm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c4e26c5b58b1cad5a62","word":"overwork","forms":["overwork"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"overwork","forms":["overwork"],"pos":"v./n.","zh":"過度工作；使工作過度","examples":[{"en":"Do not overwork yourself just to meet an unrealistic deadline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Too much overwork can damage your health.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9e482b474d7ac4b3867","word":"owe","forms":["owe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-015cdd96db398d89","term":"owe","forms":["owe","owes","owing","owed","ought","own"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欠某人某物；應為某人做某事","explanation":"表示你有一筆尚未結清的“賬”，這筆賬可以是錢、幫助，也可以是應該為某人做的事。重點不一定是法律上的債務，也可以是道義上的責任或應有回報。","examples":[{"en":"I owe my sister twenty dollars.","zh":"我欠我姐姐二十美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We owe it to our community to keep the park clean.","zh":"我們有責任為社群保持公園整潔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e13655f27461d8f5","term":"owe","forms":["owe","owes","owing","owed","ought","own"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欠債；負債","explanation":"表示處於尚未還清債務的狀態，通常指欠錢，也可以指欠款項。它是“賬還沒有結清”這個核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She still owes the bank a large amount of money.","zh":"她仍然欠銀行一大筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"How much do I owe you for dinner?","zh":"這頓飯我該給你多少錢？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10f7127b980b0b06ef15","word":"owl","forms":["owl"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9da4a85386e4f6cb","term":"owl","forms":["owl","owls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貓頭鷹","explanation":"一種主要在夜間活動的猛禽，眼睛朝前，聽覺敏銳，外形通常給人安靜而警覺的印象。","examples":[{"en":"We heard an owl calling from the trees after dark.","zh":"天黑後，我們聽見一隻貓頭鷹在樹叢裡叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The owl turned its head toward the sound.","zh":"那隻貓頭鷹把頭轉向聲音傳來的方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32ea4860b991bff7","term":"owl","forms":["owl","owls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"像貓頭鷹的人","explanation":"指看起來聰明、嚴肅，或者經常在夜間活動的人；這種用法把人的特點和貓頭鷹的形象聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is a night owl and does her best work after midnight.","zh":"我姐姐是個夜貓子，午夜以後工作效率最高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A night owl, she rarely goes to bed before two.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b3975651c3cab92d044","word":"own","forms":["own"],"officialPos":"adj./pron./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5192651484a3e11","term":"own","forms":["own"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自己的；所屬的","explanation":"表示某物屬於某人，常用來強調它確實是這個人自己的，而不是借來的、別人的或泛指的。","examples":[{"en":"She brought her own lunch to work.","zh":"她帶了自己的午飯去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I want a room of my own.","zh":"我想要一間屬於我自己的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/own","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-904fb988fadc5db2","term":"own","forms":["own","owns","owning","owned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擁有；所有","explanation":"表示某人依法或實際擁有財產、物品或資產，是“這是我的”這一核心概念的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"They own a small restaurant near the station.","zh":"他們在車站附近擁有一家小餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't own a car.","zh":"我沒有車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/own","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c1029697ee358715d3a","word":"owner","forms":["owner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b5de4fa11d9fe4c","term":"owner","forms":["owner","owners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"所有者；物主","explanation":"指擁有某件物品、某項財產、企業或寵物的人，也就是東西在法律或實際意義上歸他所有的人。這是 owner 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The owner of this dog lives next door.","zh":"這條狗的主人住在隔壁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant owner greeted us at the door.","zh":"那家餐館的老闆在門口迎接了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01b8016fdce455c43439","word":"ownership","forms":["ownership"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6adf8e4e9fcbc519","term":"ownership","forms":["ownership","ownerships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"所有權；擁有狀態","explanation":"指某人依法擁有並有權控制某件物品、財產或企業的狀態，就像鑰匙上掛著你的名字牌。它強調正式的權利，不只是暫時拿著或使用某物。","examples":[{"en":"The document proves her ownership of the house.","zh":"這份檔案證明她擁有這棟房子的所有權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ownership of the car was transferred to his daughter.","zh":"這輛車的所有權轉給了他的女兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ownership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0993394b98e18b11","term":"ownership","forms":["ownership","ownerships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"責任承擔；掌控權","explanation":"指主動接過一項任務或專案的“鑰匙”，不僅參與，還要對結果負責並推動事情完成。這裡通常不是法律上的所有權，而是責任和控制權。","examples":[{"en":"Maya took ownership of the problem and kept everyone informed.","zh":"瑪雅主動負責解決這個問題，並持續向大家通報進展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team took ownership of the scheduling problem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ownership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1dd14ffc3c3045741a5e","word":"ox","forms":["ox"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a8e4634ac2161002","term":"ox","forms":["ox","oxen","oxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"役用公牛","explanation":"“ox”最核心的意思是成年閹公牛，通常被訓練來拉車、耕地或承擔其他重活；重點是它作為役畜的身份，而不只是“雄性牛”。","examples":[{"en":"Two oxen pulled the heavy cart up the hill.","zh":"兩頭役牛把沉重的車拉上了山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers once used oxen to plow these fields.","zh":"過去農民用役牛耕種這些田地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b63077805a7452d9","term":"ox","forms":["ox","oxen","oxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牛屬動物","explanation":"在較寬泛或較舊的用法中，“ox”也可以泛指牛屬動物，即牛這一類大型家畜，而不特別強調是否用於拉車。","examples":[{"en":"The village kept oxen, sheep, and goats.","zh":"這個村子飼養牛、羊和山羊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ox pulled the loaded cart across the field.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b982a09b35429d8f8755","word":"oxygen","forms":["oxygen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7975fb25c02eb0d7","term":"oxygen","forms":["oxygen","oxygens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氧元素","explanation":"oxygen 是化學元素“氧”，元素符號為 O，存在於空氣和許多化合物中。這裡強調的是元素這一類物質，而不只是某一瓶氣體。","examples":[{"en":"Plants release oxygen during photosynthesis.","zh":"植物在光合作用過程中釋放氧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The water contains very little oxygen.","zh":"這片水域含氧量很低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxygen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fa2fbc92eb4d8e5","term":"oxygen","forms":["oxygen","oxygens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氧氣","explanation":"oxygen 也指在常溫下呈無色、無味氣態的氧氣，通常由兩個氧原子組成的 O₂ 分子構成。這是人和許多生物呼吸時所利用的那種氣體。","examples":[{"en":"The fish need oxygen-rich water to survive.","zh":"這些魚需要含氧豐富的水才能生存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fish obtain oxygen from water through their gills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxygen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d73aa9bbc6604a72","term":"oxygen","forms":["oxygen","oxygens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展所需的空間或條件","explanation":"比喻地說，oxygen 是讓某人、某個想法或某項活動能夠繼續成長和發揮作用的自由、關注或有利環境，就像生物需要氧氣一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Creative work needs the oxygen of free discussion.","zh":"創造性工作需要自由討論所提供的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small grants provide oxygen for independent community projects.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxygen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f08689f14e3421bb12d7","word":"oyster","forms":["oyster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a270d0b7a2cc020a","term":"oyster","forms":["oyster","oysters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牡蠣","explanation":"指生活在海水或河口附近、常附著在岩石等固定物上的雙殼貝類，也可指這種貝類作為食物。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered a dozen oysters and ate them with lemon.","zh":"我們點了一打牡蠣，配著檸檬吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Oysters attach themselves to rocks in shallow coastal water.","zh":"牡蠣會附著在淺海沿岸的岩石上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oyster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb2bd7ca4a327f84e6cd","word":"ozone","forms":["ozone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23c9a04f127ce707","term":"ozone","forms":["ozone","ozones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臭氧","explanation":"臭氧是由三個氧原子組成的氣體，常在雷電或放電時形成；它有明顯而刺激的氣味，濃度較高時對人體有害。","examples":[{"en":"After the storm, the smell of ozone lingered in the air.","zh":"暴風雨過後，空氣中還殘留著臭氧的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"High levels of ozone can damage the lungs.","zh":"高濃度的臭氧會損傷肺部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ozone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19b87ac5ecb1afe2d7f3","word":"pace","forms":["pace"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc3169f858de5a30","term":"pace","forms":["pace","paces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一步","explanation":"pace 最具體的畫面就是邁出的一步，即腳從一個位置移動到另一個位置的距離或動作。","examples":[{"en":"He took a pace back when the dog barked.","zh":"狗叫起來時，他向後退了一步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box was only a pace from the door.","zh":"箱子離門只有一步遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-606ec32e01101d93","term":"pace","forms":["pace","paces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"步伐；行走節奏","explanation":"許多步連線起來，就形成一個人的步伐或行走節奏；這個節奏可以快、慢、穩定或有變化。","examples":[{"en":"She walked at a steady pace through the forest.","zh":"她以穩定的步伐穿過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We slowed our pace as the trail steepened.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ef13080371c30f1","term":"pace","forms":["pace","paces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"速度；進度","explanation":"步伐的快慢可以推廣為任何移動或事情發展的速度，因此 pace 常指某件事進行得快不快。","examples":[{"en":"Technology is changing at an incredible pace.","zh":"技術正以驚人的速度變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I struggled to keep pace with the rest of the group.","zh":"我很難跟上小組其他人的步伐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97bb77d099678179","term":"pace","forms":["pace","paces","pacing","paced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"來回踱步","explanation":"人沿著一小段距離反覆走動，就像把自己的步伐保持在一條短線上；這通常表示等待、焦慮或思考。","examples":[{"en":"He paced up and down the hallway while waiting for the call.","zh":"他等電話時在走廊裡來回踱步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She paced around the room, trying to think of an answer.","zh":"她在房間裡來回踱步，努力想出答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4862f447f2c7f272fa2f","word":"pack","forms":["pack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ce239d1b4389727","term":"pack","forms":["pack","packs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"便於攜帶的一捆或一包","explanation":"指把物品聚攏、捆好後形成的負載，通常是為了揹著、馱著或搬運；也可以指一捆貨物或一包物品。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers carried heavy packs up the mountain.","zh":"徒步旅行者揹著沉重的行囊上山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The donkey carried a pack of supplies.","zh":"那頭驢馱著一捆補給品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3299ba8226da928b","term":"pack","forms":["pack","packs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一組相同或相關的東西","explanation":"指若干個相同或相關的東西被聚在一起，作為一個整體來考慮或出售。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a pack of colored pencils for the children.","zh":"她給孩子們買了一盒彩色鉛筆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The printer came with a pack of blank paper.","zh":"這臺印表機附帶了一疊空白紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06ab0b7d8f340410","term":"pack","forms":["pack","packs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一整副撲克牌","explanation":"指可用於玩牌的一整副牌，牌通常已經按一套完整的組合聚在一起。","examples":[{"en":"We need a pack of cards for the game.","zh":"我們需要一副撲克牌來玩這個遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shuffled the pack before dealing.","zh":"她發牌前把整副牌洗了洗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b9ca160d4144502","term":"pack","forms":["pack","packs","packing","packed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打包；裝入","explanation":"把物品聚攏起來，裝進箱子、袋子或其他有限空間，通常是為了儲存、運輸或帶走；這正是“把東西裝在一起”的核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"We packed the books into two sturdy boxes.","zh":"我們把這些書裝進了兩個結實的箱子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pack the equipment carefully for transport.","zh":"請把裝置仔細打包，以便運輸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc4a71180870f7945155","word":"package","forms":["package"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2810ddb9a3db9fe3","term":"package","forms":["package","packages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"包裹；包裝好的東西","explanation":"指已經包好、裝好或寄送中的一件東西，可以是盒子、信封或其他包裹；重點是“許多東西被包在一起”。","examples":[{"en":"A package arrived at the front desk this morning.","zh":"今天早上前臺收到一個包裹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrapped the books and sent them as one package.","zh":"她把這些書包在一起，作為一個包裹寄了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/package","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffaedb9121a0c538","term":"package","forms":["package","packages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軟體包；組合套件","explanation":"指由多個相關部分組成、作為一個整體提供的東西，例如一套軟體，也可以泛指組合好的服務或產品。","examples":[{"en":"The new software package includes tools for editing photos and videos.","zh":"這套新軟體包括照片和影片編輯工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Install the package before running the analysis script.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/package","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7426afc489d0eef99a0b","word":"packet","forms":["packet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-beccb725d20612d8","term":"packet","forms":["packet","packets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小包裝；小束","explanation":"指裝有少量物品的小包、小包裝或小束，是“把東西分裝成一小份”這個核心概念在現實生活中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a packet of biscuits for the train journey.","zh":"我買了一小包餅乾，準備在火車上吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the tea bags back in the packet.","zh":"請把茶包放回包裝袋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/packet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbcf2d56c6ac7ec6","term":"packet","forms":["packet","packets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路資料包","explanation":"指網路傳輸時被單獨傳送的一小段資料；複雜資訊會被拆成許多這樣的“小包”，到達後再組合起來。","examples":[{"en":"The router sends each packet to the next network.","zh":"路由器把每個資料包傳送到下一個網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some packets were lost during the video call.","zh":"視訊通話過程中有一些資料包丟失了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/packet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f563fcd3fb8578799b80","word":"pad","forms":["pad"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7215f7485e0c81a8","term":"pad","forms":["pad","pads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"柔軟墊子","explanation":"指由柔軟材料壓成或堆成的平墊，可以坐、躺或放東西；它體現了“柔軟的承託層”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She put a soft pad under the baby’s head.","zh":"她在嬰兒頭下放了一塊柔軟的墊子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a pad to protect the table from the hot pan.","zh":"用一塊墊子保護桌面，免得被熱鍋燙壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89faaf4d28acd108","term":"pad","forms":["pad","pads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衛生巾","explanation":"指用來吸收月經的吸收性衛生用品，是“吸收材料”這一承託層概念的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"She kept a few pads in her bag in case her period started early.","zh":"她在包裡放了幾片衛生巾，以防月經提前來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wrap the used pad before putting it in the bin.","zh":"請把用過的衛生巾包好後再放進垃圾桶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c85c743c82be2542","term":"pad","forms":["pad","pads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書寫本","explanation":"指由許多張紙組成、用來書寫或吸墨的本子，體現了“承託和吸收材料”擴充套件為書寫用紙本。","examples":[{"en":"I wrote the address on a pad beside the phone.","zh":"我把地址寫在電話旁邊的便箋本上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tore a sheet from her writing pad and made a quick list.","zh":"她從書寫本上撕下一張紙，迅速列了個清單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84843beb1c1371f8","term":"pad","forms":["pad","pads","padding","padded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加襯墊；加墊料","explanation":"這是“柔軟的承託層”這一記憶鉤子的直接動詞用法：給物體或身體部位加上墊料，以緩衝、保護或增加舒適度。","examples":[{"en":"We padded the sharp corners of the table to protect the children.","zh":"我們給桌子的尖角加上襯墊，以保護孩子們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse padded his injured arm before putting on the cast.","zh":"護士給他受傷的手臂墊好保護層後才戴上石膏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2afeec49a4a4c3d4cbc","word":"paddle","forms":["paddle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc236c160b5665b3","term":"paddle","forms":["paddle","paddles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"槳；船槳","explanation":"指用雙手操控、沒有固定在船上支點上的槳，用來推動獨木舟、皮划艇或小船前進。核心畫面就是人用寬扁的槳葉反覆撥水。","examples":[{"en":"She grabbed a paddle and climbed into the kayak.","zh":"她拿起一把槳，爬進了皮划艇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We forgot to bring a second paddle.","zh":"我們忘了帶第二把槳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paddle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e632edbfe278d1f","term":"paddle","forms":["paddle","paddles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"划船；划水活動","explanation":"也可以把使用槳在水上前進這一活動本身叫作 paddle，重點從“工具”擴充套件到了“用工具划水的經歷”。","examples":[{"en":"We went for a paddle before breakfast.","zh":"我們早餐前去划了一會兒船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river is perfect for a quiet paddle.","zh":"這條河很適合安靜地划船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paddle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3313de6ddf7abd9","term":"paddle","forms":["paddle","paddles","paddling","paddled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"划動；划船前進","explanation":"指用槳、槳狀物或手在水中推動船、人或其他東西前進。核心仍是反覆撥水、產生向前的力量。","examples":[{"en":"They paddled the canoe across the lake.","zh":"他們划著獨木舟穿過湖面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We paddled along the quiet river.","zh":"我們沿著安靜的河流划船前行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paddle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3660315a9af3df255d8f","word":"page","forms":["page"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba0a3ceb3aae3f0f","term":"page","forms":["page","pages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書或檔案的一頁","explanation":"page 最常見指書、雜誌或檔案中可以按順序定位的一頁，是“可被定位的一頁”這一核心意象。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the first page of the report.","zh":"請讀一下報告的第一頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wrote the address on a page in my notebook.","zh":"我把地址寫在筆記本的一頁上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/page","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-320b9ac57918b5f5","term":"page","forms":["page","pages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網頁","explanation":"在網際網路語境中，page 指網頁，是螢幕上可以透過連結或地址定位的一頁。","examples":[{"en":"The school has a page with information for new students.","zh":"這所學校有一個介紹新生資訊的網頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found the schedule on the event page.","zh":"我在活動網頁上找到了日程安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/page","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c78c8e7160e76ba9b6c","word":"pain","forms":["pain"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-486b3f4e3c4620ee","term":"pain","forms":["pain","pains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體疼痛","explanation":"指受傷、生病或身體功能異常帶來的不舒服感覺，可以泛指疼痛，也可以指一次具體的疼痛。它是 pain 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She has severe pain in her lower back.","zh":"她的下背部疼得很厲害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor asked me to describe the pain.","zh":"醫生讓我描述疼痛的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caa016dde38e9619","term":"pain","forms":["pain","pains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精神痛苦","explanation":"這裡的 pain 不在身體上，而是指悲傷、焦慮或其他強烈的精神折磨；它和身體疼痛共享“難受的痛苦”這個核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"He hid his emotional pain from his family.","zh":"他把自己的精神痛苦隱藏起來，不讓家人知道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Time does not always take away the pain of loss.","zh":"時間並不總能消除失去親人的痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10f318eb6556843c","term":"pain","forms":["pain","pains","paining","pained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使身體疼痛","explanation":"指某個傷口、動作或身體問題使人產生疼痛，是名詞“身體疼痛”的動詞化表達。","examples":[{"en":"The old injury still pains her in cold weather.","zh":"天氣寒冷時，那處舊傷仍然讓她疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His injured shoulder pained him throughout the night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f5f253e21ebcc86a4d2","word":"painful","forms":["painful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-62de8fb2743163be","term":"painful","forms":["painful","painfuller","more painful","painfullest","most painful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人疼痛或難受的","explanation":"指某種動作、情況或經歷會造成身體上的疼痛，或造成強烈的心理痛苦和難受。這是 painful 最常見、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"It was painful to watch her say goodbye to her family.","zh":"看著她和家人告別令人很難受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cut is still painful when I touch it.","zh":"這道傷口碰到時還是很疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1473421bd77d5b5","term":"painful","forms":["painful","painfuller","more painful","painfullest","most painful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"艱難費力的","explanation":"把“痛苦”從身體或情緒延伸到做事過程：某項任務需要很多努力，進行起來很折磨人，因此表示艱難、費力或勞累。","examples":[{"en":"Selling the family home was a painful decision.","zh":"賣掉家裡的房子是一個痛苦而艱難的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Learning to walk again was a painful process.","zh":"重新學走路是一個艱難而痛苦的過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-297e619db5ee855a68d5","word":"paint","forms":["paint"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-681eb1f35b4bd111","term":"paint","forms":["paint","paints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"塗料；顏料","explanation":"一種以液體或糊狀塗到表面、幹後形成固體塗層的材料，既能保護物體，也能給它上色；畫畫用的顏料也可這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"We need a fresh coat of paint on the front door.","zh":"我們需要給前門重新刷一層漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children mixed the paint on a paper plate.","zh":"孩子們在紙盤上調顏料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0b96f0984dee71e","term":"paint","forms":["paint","paints","painting","painted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……刷漆；塗上顏料","explanation":"把塗料或顏料塗到某個表面上，使它受到保護或改變顏色。","examples":[{"en":"They painted the kitchen walls pale yellow.","zh":"他們把廚房的牆刷成了淡黃色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are painting the fence this weekend.","zh":"我們這個週末要給柵欄刷漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e8b43a7ad53af7e","term":"paint","forms":["paint","paints","painting","painted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繪畫","explanation":"用顏料創作影象，例如肖像、風景或其他畫面。這裡的paint連線了“顏料”和“把影象塗繪出來”兩個核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She painted a portrait of her grandmother.","zh":"她畫了一幅祖母的肖像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He likes to paint landscapes by the sea.","zh":"他喜歡在海邊畫風景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7175d41e052114d7e663","word":"painter","forms":["painter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-139ed9ec54e8d271","term":"painter","forms":["painter","painters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"畫家","explanation":"painter是拿顏料在畫布等材料上創作畫作的人，重點是藝術創作，而不只是拿刷子塗東西。","examples":[{"en":"The painter is working on a portrait in her studio.","zh":"這位畫家正在畫室裡創作一幅肖像畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became a famous painter after studying in Paris.","zh":"他在巴黎學習後成了一名著名畫家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55d11f18bebbf45d","term":"painter","forms":["painter","painters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"油漆工","explanation":"painter也指用刷子、滾筒或其他工具給牆、門、房屋等表面上漆的工人；這裡的核心不是創作畫作，而是給表面覆蓋塗料。","examples":[{"en":"We hired a painter to repaint the kitchen.","zh":"我們請了一名油漆工重新粉刷廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painter covered the floor before opening the tin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a54e5638bbc34d80ddd3","word":"painting","forms":["painting"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21cb0bdc3fdada64","term":"painting","forms":["painting","paintings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"畫作","explanation":"顏料落在畫布、牆面等表面後形成的具體作品就是一幅 painting；重點是留下來的成品。","examples":[{"en":"There is a beautiful painting of the lake above the fireplace.","zh":"壁爐上方掛著一幅描繪那座湖的美麗畫作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum bought two paintings by a young local artist.","zh":"博物館買下了當地一位年輕藝術家的兩幅畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56d1dce9db997a7e","term":"painting","forms":["painting","paintings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"塗漆過程","explanation":"這裡說的是把顏料或油漆塗到表面上的過程，關注的是正在進行的工作，而不是最後形成的作品。","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen needs some painting before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人到來前，廚房還需要刷一刷漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Painting the ceiling took most of the afternoon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c95ce435e0ffa60d","term":"painting","forms":["painting","paintings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繪畫藝術","explanation":"當 painting 指一種藝術實踐時，它表示以顏料作畫這一門藝術，而不是某一幅具體作品。","examples":[{"en":"She studied painting at an art school before becoming a teacher.","zh":"她成為教師前曾在藝術學校學習繪畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Painting allows her to explore color without words.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47d8bd46877831ccd61c","word":"pair","forms":["pair"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93ce251bb25dae0c","term":"pair","forms":["pair","pairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一對；兩個成套的東西","explanation":"指兩個相似、相互配套或通常一起出現的東西，重點不是單純的數量“二”，而是它們被看作一個組合。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a pair of comfortable shoes for the trip.","zh":"我為這次旅行買了一雙舒適的鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A pair of birds is nesting in the tree.","zh":"一對鳥正在樹上築巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6bcf9c1a90a2667d","term":"pair","forms":["pair","pairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一對人；搭檔","explanation":"指因戀愛、婚姻、合作或友誼而聯絡在一起的兩個人；這裡的“成對”來自兩人之間的關係。","examples":[{"en":"Those two musicians make a great pair.","zh":"那兩位音樂家是很棒的搭檔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pair walked home together after dinner.","zh":"這兩個人晚飯後一起走回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-118f034faa1ba189","term":"pair","forms":["pair","pairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一件成雙使用的物品","explanation":"用於剪刀、眼鏡、牛仔褲等通常由兩部分組成、英語中常用複數形式的名詞。此時 pair 是計數單位，表示一件完整物品，而不是兩個獨立物件。","examples":[{"en":"She needs a new pair of glasses.","zh":"她需要一副新眼鏡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I packed two pairs of jeans.","zh":"我裝了兩條牛仔褲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1c24cc083ed75e71fc3","word":"pajamas","forms":["pajamas"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7807a9c0713c8200","term":"pajamas","forms":["pajamas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"睡衣","explanation":"指睡覺時穿的寬鬆衣服，通常包括一件寬鬆上衣和一條褲子；這是日常英語中最主要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I put on my pajamas as soon as I got home.","zh":"我一到家就換上了睡衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were already in their pajamas when dinner was ready.","zh":"晚飯準備好時，孩子們已經穿上睡衣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pajamas","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1a38b5bae5866d7d998","word":"pal","forms":["pal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65f955b7eb3e5958","term":"pal","forms":["pal","pals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"朋友；夥伴","explanation":"pal是口語中的“朋友、夥伴”，強調一起相處、玩耍或做事的人；它比正式的“朋友”說法更隨意親近。","examples":[{"en":"I ran into an old pal at the market.","zh":"我在市場碰到了一位老朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kids spent the afternoon playing with their pals.","zh":"孩子們和夥伴們玩了一下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d08833009ea9ab20","term":"pal","forms":["pal","pals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夥計；朋友（可帶諷刺或敵意）","explanation":"pal也能直接用來稱呼對方，表面像“朋友”或“夥計”，但在爭吵、警告等場景中常帶反諷，意思接近“聽著，夥計”。","examples":[{"en":"Take it easy, pal; nobody is trying to blame you.","zh":"放輕鬆，夥計；沒人想怪你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Back off, pal, or I'll call security.","zh":"離我遠點，夥計，不然我就叫保安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee2aa44805b51b108837","word":"palace","forms":["palace"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9135be95c93f7ae3","term":"palace","forms":["palace","palaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"君主或國家領導人的官邸","explanation":"指君主、國家領導人或其他重要人物正式居住或辦公的宏偉官邸，尤其常見於王室或帝國制度。","examples":[{"en":"The king welcomed the foreign delegation at the palace.","zh":"國王在王宮接待了外國代表團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The palace released a statement after the meeting.","zh":"王宮方面在會晤後發表了一份宣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-933ad708fbc563e6","term":"palace","forms":["palace","palaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豪華的大宅","explanation":"泛指規模很大、裝飾華麗的住宅，不一定真的屬於君主或政府。","examples":[{"en":"They built a palace overlooking the sea.","zh":"他們建了一座俯瞰大海的豪華大宅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actress lives in a palace outside the city.","zh":"那位女演員住在城外一座宮殿般豪華的宅邸裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e6805d9e6f7212aec46","word":"pale","forms":["pale"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f56ab60945a7a86","term":"pale","forms":["pale","paler","palest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顏色淺的","explanation":"指顏色不濃、不鮮明，接近白色但不一定是純白色。它可以描述牆面、布料、天空等物體的顏色。","examples":[{"en":"The room was painted a pale blue.","zh":"房間刷成了淺藍色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They chose pale blue curtains for the nursery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f878cd036740c88c","term":"pale","forms":["pale","paler","palest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"臉色蒼白的","explanation":"指人的臉色因為害怕、震驚、生病或疲憊等原因失去血色，看起來很白。","examples":[{"en":"She went pale when she heard the news.","zh":"她聽到這個訊息後臉色變得蒼白。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor noticed how pale he looked beneath the bright lamp.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5afa2b3773eb81b5eb8","word":"palm","forms":["palm"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53ce36350d675d1c","term":"palm","forms":["palm","palms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棕櫚樹","explanation":"一種主要生長在熱帶地區的常綠樹，通常有高直的樹幹和頂部展開的大片葉子。這個義項與“手掌”的聯絡在於棕櫚葉像張開的手掌。","examples":[{"en":"Tall palms lined the beach.","zh":"海灘邊排列著高大的棕櫚樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A coconut fell from the palm beside our tent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f44b2a8bd8ab4ee","term":"palm","forms":["palm","palms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手掌；掌心","explanation":"指從手腕延伸到手指根部、手的內側那一面，也就是可以向上攤開的掌心。它不是整隻手，而是手的扁平內側。","examples":[{"en":"She held the tiny key in the palm of her hand.","zh":"她把那把小鑰匙握在手掌心裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His palm was covered with ink.","zh":"他的手掌沾滿了墨水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00e37ffae0562ab6818d","word":"pan","forms":["pan"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9925aada74925328","term":"pan","forms":["pan","pans","pen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平底鍋；淺鍋","explanation":"一種寬而平、通常用於烹飪的容器；可以把它想成承接食物的平面。","examples":[{"en":"Heat the oil in a large pan before adding the onions.","zh":"先在大鍋里加熱油，再放入洋蔥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pan is still hot, so use an oven mitt.","zh":"鍋還很燙，所以要用隔熱手套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9c1034fb623883b5786","word":"pancake","forms":["pancake"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f726f6001371d98","term":"pancake","forms":["pancake","pancakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄煎餅","explanation":"指把較稀的麵糊倒在鍋或煎盤上，用油或黃油煎成的薄圓餅，通常作為早餐或甜點食用。這是 pancake 最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I made pancakes for the children this morning.","zh":"今天早上我給孩子們做了煎餅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She flipped the pancake and cooked the other side.","zh":"她把煎餅翻了個面，煎另一面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pancake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-637258b977224555","term":"pancake","forms":["pancake","pancakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"厚粉底","explanation":"在化妝語境中，pancake 指壓制成餅狀、質地較厚的粉底或粉餅。這個意思保留了“鋪成一層、看起來較平”的聯想，但不是普通的煎餅。","examples":[{"en":"The actor wore heavy pancake under the stage lights.","zh":"那名演員在舞臺燈光下塗了厚厚的粉底。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor's pancake concealed the small scar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pancake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7cdf5d0586b392473dd","word":"panda","forms":["panda"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eff307b662bad84b","term":"panda","forms":["panda","pandas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大熊貓","explanation":"這是現代最核心的意思，指黑白相間、以竹子為主要食物的大熊貓。它可以看作panda這個名稱如今最常被保留下來的動物物件。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a panda eating bamboo at the zoo.","zh":"我們在動物園看到一隻大熊貓在吃竹子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The panda is one of the country's best-known animals.","zh":"大熊貓是這個國家最知名的動物之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-320e00e73a7d24a9a44c","word":"panel","forms":["panel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c6c59173d51a07ca","term":"panel","forms":["panel","panels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表面上的一塊板面","explanation":"指牆、門、圍欄、覆蓋物等表面中被分隔出來的一塊，通常有清楚的邊界。它是“從整體中取出一塊板塊”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The workers replaced a damaged panel on the garage door.","zh":"工人更換了車庫門上一塊損壞的面板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sunlight came through a glass panel in the roof.","zh":"陽光透過屋頂上的一塊玻璃板照了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1802841a4711276e","term":"panel","forms":["panel","panels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"評審或討論小組","explanation":"指聚在一起進行評判、面試、討論或節目交流的一組人。這裡的“板塊”從物理空間擴充套件到了一個被組織起來、共同完成任務的小組。","examples":[{"en":"A panel of experts will judge the entries tomorrow.","zh":"專家評審小組明天將評判這些參賽作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The panel asked each candidate the same question.","zh":"評審小組向每位候選人都問了同一個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-79631cb1b7b63b6e84ab","word":"panic","forms":["panic"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cfcbf5e243502a77","term":"panic","forms":["panic","panics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恐慌；驚慌","explanation":"指突然而強烈的恐懼狀態，常使一個人、許多人或動物失去冷靜並倉促行動；也可以指一次具體的驚慌事件。","examples":[{"en":"The passengers ran for the exits in panic.","zh":"乘客們驚慌失措地跑向出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden panic swept through the stadium.","zh":"一陣突如其來的恐慌席捲了體育場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-033c043b4be7f444","term":"panic","forms":["panic","panics","panicking","panicked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人恐慌","explanation":"指某人或某件事使另一個人陷入強烈恐懼，並可能因此倉促行動。","examples":[{"en":"The false alarm panicked the residents into leaving their homes.","zh":"虛假警報使居民慌忙離開了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unexpected siren panicked the sleeping campers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40cd4ca93564b0da","term":"panic","forms":["panic","panics","panicking","panicked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"慌起來；失去冷靜","explanation":"指自己突然陷入強烈恐懼，因而慌亂、失去判斷力或不知所措。","examples":[{"en":"Don't panic; we still have plenty of time.","zh":"別慌，我們還有很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She panicked when she could not find her passport.","zh":"她找不到護照時慌了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c50624bea38c570f59f","word":"pants","forms":["pants"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ede40dbf7815416c","term":"pants","forms":["pants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"褲子","explanation":"pants 指從腰部向下覆蓋兩條腿的外穿衣物，也就是通常所說的褲子。在美國英語及一些其他地區，這是最常見的理解。","examples":[{"en":"I need a clean pair of pants for work.","zh":"我需要一條幹淨的褲子去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These pants are too tight around the waist.","zh":"這條褲子的腰部太緊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pants","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98a4f7655958a385a066","word":"papaya","forms":["papaya"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd73a0717377e0b5","term":"papaya","forms":["papaya","papayas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"番木瓜樹","explanation":"指結番木瓜果實的熱帶常綠樹，樹上長著大而寬的葉子和可食用的果實。","examples":[{"en":"There is a papaya tree behind the house.","zh":"房子後面有一棵番木瓜樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The papaya grew rapidly in the sheltered courtyard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/papaya","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7094c8401cff96d8","term":"papaya","forms":["papaya","papayas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"番木瓜果實","explanation":"指番木瓜樹結出的果實，成熟後通常有橙黃色果肉和許多黑色種子，常作為水果食用。","examples":[{"en":"She cut a ripe papaya and removed the seeds.","zh":"她切開一個熟番木瓜，去掉了種子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sliced a ripe papaya for breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/papaya","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-382635c9325bf3273d19","word":"paper","forms":["paper"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c208a201b731c455","term":"paper","forms":["paper","papers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紙","explanation":"紙是一種用來書寫、繪畫、印刷或包裝的薄片材料；這正是把 paper 想成“一張紙”的最基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your name on the paper.","zh":"請把你的名字寫在紙上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a piece of paper to make a note.","zh":"我需要一張紙來記筆記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-780f23d509279823","term":"paper","forms":["paper","papers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檔案；文章；報告","explanation":"寫在紙面上的內容可以成為一份較短的書面檔案，例如學生作業、報告或一般文章。","examples":[{"en":"I have to finish a paper for my history class.","zh":"我得完成歷史課的一篇論文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee released a paper on public transport.","zh":"委員會發布了一份關於公共交通的報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bba1f620dac9a733","term":"paper","forms":["paper","papers","papering","papered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式記錄；寫成檔案","explanation":"把已經談妥或正在進行的事情落到紙面上，形成正式的檔案或記錄。這正對應“把事情落到紙面上”的記憶：不只是說過，而是留下可作為正式依據的文字。","examples":[{"en":"The two companies agreed on the price and papered the deal the next day.","zh":"兩家公司談妥了價格，第二天就把這筆交易正式寫進了檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Before we begin the project, let's paper the arrangement clearly.","zh":"開始專案之前，我們先把這項安排明確寫成正式檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4aa10252d0c3a5437f3","word":"paperback","forms":["paperback"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09ca13c3404dc2d0","term":"paperback","forms":["paperback","paperbacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平裝書；平裝本","explanation":"指用柔軟封面裝訂的書，通常較輕、價格也較低；它是“紙封面版本”這一概念的核心名詞。","examples":[{"en":"She carried a paperback on the train.","zh":"她帶著一本平裝書上了火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paperback is half the price of the hardcover.","zh":"這本平裝書的價格只有精裝書的一半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paperback","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a438450d6ba8f12daa4f","word":"parachute","forms":["parachute"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4b0b34bfe064f4c","term":"parachute","forms":["parachute","parachutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"降落傘","explanation":"降落傘是用布等材料製成的裝置，張開後利用空氣阻力減慢人或物體的下降，使其較安全地落下。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot pulled the emergency parachute and landed safely.","zh":"飛行員拉開了應急降落傘，安全著陸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The parachute opened just before he reached the ground.","zh":"他快到地面時，降落傘才開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parachute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8901c03c766de917","term":"parachute","forms":["parachute","parachutes","parachuting","parachuted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"乘降落傘下降","explanation":"作不及物動詞時，parachute 表示乘降落傘跳下、下降或降落；核心仍是“藉助張開的傘面控制下落”。","examples":[{"en":"The team parachuted into the valley before sunrise.","zh":"這支隊伍在日出前乘降落傘降落到山谷裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned to parachute from an aircraft during her military training.","zh":"她在軍事訓練中學會了從飛機上跳傘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parachute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cae1afc1235b4cfbb42d","word":"parade","forms":["parade"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9aa736cddf116ef9","term":"parade","forms":["parade","parades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊行；閱兵","explanation":"指一群人按照一定安排公開行進、集合或展示，常見於慶典、軍隊、政治活動等場合。重點是“有組織地把一群人展示出來”。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of people watched the parade through the city center.","zh":"數千人觀看了穿過市中心的遊行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers took part in the national day parade.","zh":"士兵們參加了國慶閱兵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ebba4e10014d06a","term":"parade","forms":["parade","parades","parading","paraded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加遊行；列隊","explanation":"指人或隊伍參加遊行、閱兵等有組織的公開展示，核心畫面就是“走進佇列，供人觀看”。","examples":[{"en":"The students paraded through the town carrying flags.","zh":"學生們舉著旗子列隊走過城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band paraded down the main street.","zh":"樂佇列隊走過了主街。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b591cc313c07621780d","word":"paradise","forms":["paradise"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-094b01c509f53f8d","term":"paradise","forms":["paradise","paradises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天堂","explanation":"指人們相信聖潔靈魂死後會居住的地方，是“完美花園”這一核心意象最莊重的來源。","examples":[{"en":"She believes her grandmother is in paradise now.","zh":"她相信祖母現在已經在天堂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hymn describes the soul entering paradise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c87303d7de84ff5","term":"paradise","forms":["paradise","paradises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美好宜人的地方","explanation":"由天堂花園的形象引申，指景色優美、環境舒適、讓人感到特別享受的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The quiet island is a paradise for nature lovers.","zh":"這座寧靜的島嶼是自然愛好者的天堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the rain, the garden looked like paradise.","zh":"雨後，這座花園看起來就像天堂一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39b6d2a392e569cb","term":"paradise","forms":["paradise","paradises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某類人的理想場所","explanation":"指特別適合某種人、興趣或活動的地方，例如購物者、讀書者或衝浪者的理想去處。","examples":[{"en":"This market is a paradise for food lovers.","zh":"這個市場是美食愛好者的天堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new library is a paradise for students.","zh":"這座新圖書館是學生的理想去處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45066dd976d8bf0c05dc","word":"paradox","forms":["paradox"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf7eb5bdb2d3e01d","term":"paradox","forms":["paradox","paradoxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自相矛盾卻有邏輯意義的說法","explanation":"指一個說法表面上自相矛盾，甚至會出現“它為真則為假、它為假則為真”的迴圈。它不是簡單的病句或錯誤，而是透過矛盾暴露出語言或邏輯中的問題。","examples":[{"en":"The statement “This statement is false” is a classic paradox.","zh":"“這句話是假的”是一個經典悖論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paradox arises because either answer seems to make the statement untrue.","zh":"悖論之所以產生，是因為無論哪個答案都好像會使這句話變成假的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-265b0917b3e78411","term":"paradox","forms":["paradox","paradoxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反直覺的結果","explanation":"指結果看起來違反常識，卻確實可能發生，或至少值得認真解釋。這裡的矛盾通常來自“按直覺應當如此”與實際結果之間的衝突。","examples":[{"en":"It is a strange paradox that saving more money can sometimes make people feel less secure.","zh":"一個奇怪的悖論是，存下更多錢有時反而會讓人覺得更沒有安全感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paradox is that the faster we work, the less we seem to get done.","zh":"矛盾之處在於，我們工作得越快，似乎完成的事情反而越少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0061e7ab1e3f914","term":"paradox","forms":["paradox","paradoxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兩個看似矛盾的觀點同時成立","explanation":"指兩個表面衝突的判斷或觀點可以同時成立，重點是它們並非簡單二選一，而是從不同角度共同說明一個更復雜的事實。","examples":[{"en":"There is a paradox in wanting complete freedom while asking others to protect us.","zh":"人們一方面想要完全的自由，另一方面又要求別人保護自己，這本身就是一種悖論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paradox is that having no fixed style can itself become a style.","zh":"悖論在於，沒有固定風格本身也可能變成一種風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradox","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c097a031849cabfc7d0a","word":"paragraph","forms":["paragraph"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9500e521246f33c2","term":"paragraph","forms":["paragraph","paragraphs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"段落","explanation":"文章中另起一行、通常圍繞一個主題展開的一組句子就是一個 paragraph。段落常透過換行或首行縮排與前後文字分開。","examples":[{"en":"The opening paragraph introduces the main idea of the article.","zh":"開頭的段落介紹了這篇文章的主要觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the second paragraph carefully.","zh":"請仔細閱讀第二段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paragraph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83a00300ad6a2502c3fd","word":"parallel","forms":["parallel"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bce5e2a900ee0277","term":"parallel","forms":["parallel"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平行的","explanation":"指兩條線或兩個面在各處都保持相同距離，像鐵軌一樣朝同一方向延伸而不靠攏。","examples":[{"en":"The horizontal lines on my notebook paper are parallel.","zh":"我筆記本上的橫線彼此平行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two walls are parallel to each other.","zh":"這兩面牆彼此平行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parallel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f25ddc17d9b7f8f5","term":"parallel","forms":["parallel"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相似對應的","explanation":"從“方向始終一致”引申而來，表示兩個人、事件或發展過程在結構、經歷或結果上有明顯相似之處，但不必完全相同。","examples":[{"en":"The two writers led parallel lives in different countries.","zh":"這兩位作家在不同國家過著相似的人生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are parallel changes in the two industries.","zh":"這兩個行業出現了相似的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parallel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e14baeeb01735187","term":"parallel","forms":["parallel","parallels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相似物件","explanation":"指在重要方面與另一事物相同或相似、因此可以拿來比較的事物。","examples":[{"en":"Critics have drawn parallels between the two novels.","zh":"評論家指出了這兩部小說之間的相似之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a clear parallel between the two events.","zh":"這兩件事之間有明顯的相似之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parallel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d8c967453a363df2259","word":"paralyze","forms":["paralyze"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"paralyze","forms":["paralyze"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使癱瘓；使無法動彈","examples":[{"en":"A serious spinal injury can paralyze the legs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Fear can paralyze a person even when there is a clear way to escape.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"paralyze","forms":["paralyze"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使停頓；使失去運作能力","examples":[{"en":"The strike could paralyze public transport across the city.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A computer failure might paralyze the entire booking system.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-550a49ead28c8f626c70","word":"parcel","forms":["parcel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97e077e5a946e405","term":"parcel","forms":["parcel","parcels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"包裹","explanation":"指用紙、盒子等包好、準備寄送或已經寄送的一件包裹；它就是把某些東西單獨包成“一份”的結果。","examples":[{"en":"A parcel was waiting for me at the front door.","zh":"門口有一個包裹在等我取。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The courier left a parcel beside the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parcel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6685b89da0f548a5","term":"parcel","forms":["parcel","parcels","parceling","parcelling","parceled","parcelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……包起來","explanation":"指把東西包成一個可以拿取或運輸的包裹，是名詞“包裹”所對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"I parcelled the books up and took them to the post office.","zh":"我把書包好後拿到了郵局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She parceled the fragile cups in tissue paper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parcel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5824ab38ef4c506f753f","word":"pardon","forms":["pardon"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b28c1cc745eecb04","term":"pardon","forms":["pardon","pardons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原諒；寬恕","explanation":"指不再追究某人的過錯或冒犯，也就是把應受的責罰放下。它可以表示某個人給予的寬恕，也可以泛指獲得原諒這件事。","examples":[{"en":"She asked her friend for pardon after speaking so harshly.","zh":"她說話那麼刻薄之後，請求朋友原諒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He begged her pardon for his thoughtless remark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pardon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11c9f2cce1e26f03","term":"pardon","forms":["pardon","pardons","pardoning","pardoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"原諒某人","explanation":"表示不再因為某人的過錯而責怪或懲罰他，也就是把這件事放下、寬恕對方。它可以用於個人之間，也可以用於較正式或莊重的請求。","examples":[{"en":"Please pardon me for arriving so late.","zh":"請原諒我來得這麼晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hope you can pardon my careless remark.","zh":"我希望你能原諒我那句不經意的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pardon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00743498a43f3ea2861d","word":"parent(s)","forms":["parent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1d9f38d0c0c489d","term":"parent","forms":["parent","parents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"父母；家長","explanation":"指養育孩子的人，不限於親生父母，也可以是收養父母、寄養父母或實際照料孩子的家長。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents adopted her when she was three.","zh":"她三歲時被父母收養了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every child needs a caring parent.","zh":"每個孩子都需要一位關愛自己的家長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ba0ee0a62b57289","term":"parent","forms":["parent","parents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生育過孩子的人","explanation":"強調某人與自己所生孩子之間的父母關係，常用於談論生育身份或家庭關係。","examples":[{"en":"They became parents for the first time last year.","zh":"他們去年第一次成為父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every parent worries when a child is seriously ill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2a97de261bb121c","term":"parent","forms":["parent","parents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"來源；起因","explanation":"把某事物看成“生出”另一事物的源頭，因此 parent 可以指某種結果、思想或情況的來源或起因。","examples":[{"en":"Curiosity is often the parent of discovery.","zh":"好奇心往往是發現的源頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The parent company owns several regional newspapers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d3971de62245c94cd3d","word":"park","forms":["park"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01333f7d29f2487f","term":"park","forms":["park","parks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公園","explanation":"供人休閒、運動或保護自然環境而保留的一片土地就是park，即公園。","examples":[{"en":"We walked through the park after lunch.","zh":"午飯後我們穿過了公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are playing in the park.","zh":"孩子們正在公園裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/park","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59d7145aed4d2bab","term":"park","forms":["park","parks","parking","parked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停車；停放","explanation":"park最基本的動詞義是把車輛停在某處，也可泛指把某物放到指定位置。核心畫面就是“讓東西停在一個地方”。","examples":[{"en":"Please park the car behind the house.","zh":"請把車停在房子後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can park here for ten minutes.","zh":"你可以在這裡停車十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/park","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b817af420157e386","term":"park","forms":["park","parks","parking","parked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暫緩處理","explanation":"把問題“停放”起來，就引申為暫時不處理，留到以後再討論；這是會議和工作中的非正式說法。","examples":[{"en":"Let’s park that question until we have more information.","zh":"等我們有更多資訊後，再處理那個問題吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We parked the proposal for next month’s meeting.","zh":"我們把這個提案推遲到下個月的會議再討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/park","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ee162f213ce23422a95","word":"parliament","forms":["parliament"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e80b3fd6dddd591","term":"parliament","forms":["parliament","parliaments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家議會","explanation":"指國家的立法機關，由選舉或任命產生的成員組成，負責辯論公共事務、制定或修改法律，並可能監督政府的財政和行政活動。","examples":[{"en":"The parliament voted to approve the new education law.","zh":"議會投票透過了新的教育法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parliament debated the budget until midnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parliament","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a88195bafa0e8bc6","term":"parliament","forms":["parliament","parliaments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某一屆議會","explanation":"指在某段任期或為某個具體目的而組成的一屆議會，重點不在議會這一制度本身，而在其中一次特定的組成和任期。","examples":[{"en":"She was elected to the country's fifth parliament.","zh":"她當選為該國第五屆議會議員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new parliament assembled for its first session.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parliament","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4488b8b86b1ac061dbe3","word":"parrot","forms":["parrot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d1413bfbca92623","term":"parrot","forms":["parrot","parrots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鸚鵡","explanation":"指鸚鵡這種鳥，許多種類顏色鮮豔，並且能夠模仿人說話的聲音。它是 parrot 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a colorful parrot at the pet store.","zh":"我在寵物店買了一隻色彩鮮豔的鸚鵡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The parrot can mimic several human voices.","zh":"這隻鸚鵡會模仿幾種人的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parrot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2494ad22438d1db1","term":"parrot","forms":["parrot","parrots","parroting","parroted","parrotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鸚鵡學舌般重複","explanation":"指一個人原樣重複剛聽到的話或別人的觀點，卻沒有表現出自己的理解，正像鸚鵡模仿人聲一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The speaker merely parroted the newspaper's opinions.","zh":"那位發言人只是機械地重複報紙上的觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't parrot everything you hear online.","zh":"不要把你在網上聽到的一切都鸚鵡學舌般重複出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parrot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37a680133bd09342f934","word":"part","forms":["part"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16f4b9b9a545f514","term":"part","forms":["part","parts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"部分；組成部分","explanation":"指整體中的一份或構成整體的一個成分，可以是具體物件，也可以是計劃、故事或地區中的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"This room is part of the original house.","zh":"這個房間是原來房子的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small part of the machine needs replacing.","zh":"這臺機器有一個小部件需要更換。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/part","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fff59df558db0b1e","term":"part","forms":["part","parts","parting","parted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離開；分別","explanation":"指原本在一起的人離開彼此，回到不同的地方；它是“部分分開”這一核心畫面的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"We parted after saying goodbye at the station.","zh":"我們在車站道別後分別了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two friends parted ways after the argument.","zh":"那兩個朋友爭吵後各自離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/part","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9834a14ab9bcaa0f6a8d","word":"partial","forms":["partial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ecd945d16eecfba","term":"partial","forms":["partial","more partial","most partial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"部分的；不完整的","explanation":"只完成、包含或說明了一部分，距離完整狀態還有缺失；這裡的“部分”強調不全，而不只是把整體分成幾份。","examples":[{"en":"We only have a partial explanation for the sudden change.","zh":"我們目前只能對這次突然變化作出不完整的解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The eclipse was only partial from our location.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bffe9a55982df46b","term":"partial","forms":["partial","more partial","most partial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"偏袒的","explanation":"面對競爭、爭端或不同立場時，只站在某個人或某一方這邊，因此判斷可能不公平。它正好體現了“只站在一部分這一邊”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The judge seemed partial to the home team.","zh":"裁判似乎偏袒主隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The referee seemed partial to players from his own hometown.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0cde073e7e5fc1c872c","word":"participant","forms":["participant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-466d31343d8500f8","term":"participant","forms":["participant","participants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參與者；參加者","explanation":"指實際加入某項活動、計劃、討論或事件的人，也就是在那張“共同參與的桌子”旁佔有一席的人。","examples":[{"en":"Every participant in the workshop received a feedback form.","zh":"研討會的每位參與者都收到了一份反饋表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each participant received a numbered badge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/participant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48f8106bb7de701e3ec3","word":"participate","forms":["participate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-adc78c20b0e68e45","term":"participate","forms":["participate","participates","participating","participated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加；參與","explanation":"指主動加入一項活動、比賽、討論或專案，而不只是到場觀看；也就是把自己放進共同的事情裡，成為其中一部分。","examples":[{"en":"Students are encouraged to participate in class discussions.","zh":"鼓勵學生參與課堂討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"More than a hundred people participated in the charity run.","zh":"有一百多人參加了這場慈善跑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/participate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3ea38fc3209511ada089","word":"participation","forms":["participation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68e58ddd02129f6b","term":"participation","forms":["participation","participations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參加；參與","explanation":"指實際加入某項活動、討論、比賽或工作，而不是隻在旁邊觀看。這個詞突出“把自己放進事情裡並佔有一份參與”。","examples":[{"en":"The success of the event depends on everyone's participation.","zh":"活動的成功取決於每個人的參與。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Student participation in class has increased this term.","zh":"這學期學生在課堂上的參與度提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/participation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d1d155e75844591220d","word":"particle","forms":["particle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95f5a974cd7b4d6a","term":"particle","forms":["particle","particles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微小碎片","explanation":"指非常小的一塊物質或碎片，強調它只是整體中很小的一部分。也可以用於抽象事物，表示少到幾乎可以忽略的一點。","examples":[{"en":"There wasn't a particle of dust on the clean table.","zh":"乾淨的桌子上一點灰塵也沒有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A particle of glass was stuck in his shoe.","zh":"他鞋裡卡著一小片玻璃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/particle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-243be0d7f586560b","term":"particle","forms":["particle","particles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語法功能詞","explanation":"在語言學中，particle 是一個本身詞彙意義很弱、但能和其他詞結合來表達語法關係、語氣或句法功能的小詞。它就像語言結構中的小零件，單獨看不起眼，卻能改變整個短語或句子的作用。","examples":[{"en":"In this language, a particle marks the topic of the sentence.","zh":"在這種語言中，一個助詞用來標記句子的主題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher explained how the particle changes the meaning of the phrase.","zh":"老師解釋了這個小詞如何改變短語的意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/particle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32182951b85a244a9bf6","word":"particular","forms":["particular"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f81032ad494db96","term":"particular","forms":["particular","more particular","most particular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特定的；具體的","explanation":"它把一類東西中的某一個明確物件挑出來，讓聽者知道你說的不是泛泛的一類，而是這個具體物件。","examples":[{"en":"I'm looking for a particular book, but I can't remember the title.","zh":"我在找一本特定的書，但想不起書名了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is there any particular reason you left so early?","zh":"你這麼早離開有什麼特別具體的原因嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/particular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1650a6fde8472d54","term":"particular","forms":["particular","more particular","most particular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別的；特意區分出來的","explanation":"它表示某個物件因某種原因被單獨挑出來，帶有“特別指定”或“與其他物件不同”的感覺；在否定結構中常用於說明“不按特定順序或方式”。","examples":[{"en":"The guests arrived in no particular order.","zh":"客人們沒有按什麼特定順序到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have nothing particular planned for this weekend.","zh":"這個週末我沒有安排什麼特別的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/particular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f747b89b39c65891","term":"particular","forms":["particular","more particular","most particular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"講究的；挑剔的","explanation":"這裡的人像是在不斷挑出小細節，只有符合自己標準的東西才滿意，所以表示對食物、整潔、質量等要求很高。","examples":[{"en":"She's very particular about how her coffee is made.","zh":"她非常講究咖啡的沖泡方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He's particular about keeping his desk tidy.","zh":"他很講究保持書桌整潔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/particular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13bfaf8f3c4750362fa8","word":"partly","forms":["partly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d13f572d4f1f0dc8","term":"partly","forms":["partly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"部分地；在一定程度上","explanation":"表示某事只發生、完成或成立了一部分，剩下的部分並未發生，或情況並不完全如此。它可以修飾具體結果，如“部分完成”，也可以修飾較抽象的判斷，如“部分因為某個原因”。","examples":[{"en":"The report is only partly finished, so we still need to check the final section.","zh":"這份報告只完成了一部分，所以我們還需要檢查最後一節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The delay was partly caused by the heavy rain.","zh":"這次延誤有一部分是由大雨造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f3fa48ca88567813484","word":"partner","forms":["partner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1302b077aa94207f","term":"partner","forms":["partner","partners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夥伴；搭檔；配對的一方","explanation":"指和另一人或另一物成對、相互配合的一方，可以是生活中的伴侶、活動中的搭檔，也可以是彼此相配的事物。","examples":[{"en":"I asked my partner to check the figures with me.","zh":"我請我的搭檔和我一起核對數字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two gloves are partners in the same pair.","zh":"這兩隻手套是同一雙中的一對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f9a96e0c4261efe","term":"partner","forms":["partner","partners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合作伙伴；共同參與者","explanation":"指因共同的活動、工作或興趣而與另一人建立聯絡的人，重點是一起做某件事或共享某種利益。","examples":[{"en":"She is my business partner, and we run the shop together.","zh":"她是我的商業夥伴，我們一起經營這家店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our research partner supplied the laboratory equipment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-76f9df77e8afeb0caad8","word":"partnership","forms":["partnership"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-560e6efe061996df","term":"partnership","forms":["partnership","partnerships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夥伴關係；合作關係","explanation":"指兩個人或多人作為夥伴聯絡在一起、共同合作的狀態，重點是雙方之間的合作關係，而不一定涉及商業活動。","examples":[{"en":"The project succeeded through a strong partnership between the two teams.","zh":"這個專案透過兩支團隊之間的緊密合作取得了成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum developed a partnership with local schools.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partnership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9f596a29d1c8e44","term":"partnership","forms":["partnership","partnerships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合夥企業；商業合夥關係","explanation":"指兩人或多人為了經營生意而組成的合夥關係，也可以指這項共同經營的事業。","examples":[{"en":"The two designers formed a partnership to open a furniture studio.","zh":"兩位設計師合夥開了一家傢俱工作室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They formed a partnership to open a bakery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/partnership","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d0fea39ec33ff7543f3","word":"party","forms":["party"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd0f76f5ce9101ef","term":"party","forms":["party","parties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律上的一方；合同當事人","explanation":"在訴訟或合同中，party 是承擔權利、義務或參與法律程式的一方，可以是個人或組織。","examples":[{"en":"Both parties must sign the contract before work begins.","zh":"雙方必須在工作開始前簽署合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court invited the injured party to give evidence.","zh":"法院請受害一方作證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/party","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfdb0e1bce5b2a20","term":"party","forms":["party","parties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聚會；一群同行者","explanation":"可指為慶祝、娛樂而聚集的人，也可指為旅行、用餐或其他特定目的暫時聚在一起的一群人。","examples":[{"en":"We're having a small party at home on Saturday.","zh":"我們星期六要在家裡辦一個小型聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A party of four is waiting by the entrance.","zh":"有四個人組成的一組正在入口處等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/party","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b195d4f17c13123c","term":"party","forms":["party","parties","partying","partied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加聚會；盡情玩樂","explanation":"表示參加聚會、社交和娛樂活動，重點是和別人一起放鬆玩樂。","examples":[{"en":"We partied with our friends until midnight.","zh":"我們和朋友一起玩到午夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They spent the weekend partying by the beach.","zh":"他們在海邊參加聚會、玩了整個週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/party","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d74ff0ee8da3b9806b18","word":"pass","forms":["pass"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a50e8b10d0f2b662","term":"pass","forms":["pass","passes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考試透過","explanation":"指在考試或類似測試中達到要求並獲得透過。它把“透過”從空間移動延伸到了成績達到標準。","examples":[{"en":"She got a pass in mathematics on her second attempt.","zh":"她第二次參加數學考試時透過了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A pass in the safety test is required before you can start work.","zh":"透過安全測試後，你才能開始工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-385b4adddf707c17","term":"pass","forms":["pass","passes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通行證；入場券","explanation":"指證明持有人可以通行、往來或入場的檔案、證件或票券，例如交通通行證、工作證或入場證。它把獲得通行許可具體化成了可以出示的東西。","examples":[{"en":"You need a visitor pass to get beyond the reception desk.","zh":"你需要訪客通行證才能透過接待臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival gave us passes for all three days.","zh":"音樂節給了我們三天全程的入場證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-724c1e93de355908","term":"pass","forms":["pass","passes","passing","passed","passest","passedst","passeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經過；移動到另一處","explanation":"表示人或物從一個地方移動到另一個地方，突出“從一邊到另一邊”的經過過程。","examples":[{"en":"We passed from the kitchen into the garden.","zh":"我們從廚房走到了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train passed through the village without stopping.","zh":"火車經過村莊，沒有停下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97b54cdfaab10e81","term":"pass","forms":["pass","passes","passing","passed","passest","passedst","passeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"可以接受；勉強過得去","explanation":"表示某事雖然不理想，但達到最低要求，可以接受或暫時不會造成問題；可以把它記成“這件事順利越過了要求線”。","examples":[{"en":"The room is small, but it will pass for one night.","zh":"這個房間雖然小，但住一晚還過得去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That excuse won't pass with the teacher.","zh":"那個藉口在老師那裡行不通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0886b051075687c18a9a","word":"passage","forms":["passage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bae25d83fe17929","term":"passage","forms":["passage","passages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文字或音樂片段","explanation":"指文章、書籍或音樂中可以單獨拿出來理解的一段內容，就像讀者在整篇作品中“經過”的一個小部分。","examples":[{"en":"I found an interesting passage in the final chapter.","zh":"我在最後一章發現了一段有趣的文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher asked us to read the passage aloud.","zh":"老師讓我們把這段文字朗讀出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26c957dc589cbe2b","term":"passage","forms":["passage","passages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經過的路線或行程","explanation":"指從一個地方到另一個地方時所走過的一段路或一段行程，重點在“穿過、經過”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The passage through the forest took nearly an hour.","zh":"穿過森林的這段路幾乎花了一個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fog delayed our passage from the island to the mainland.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88669dc283aace15","term":"passage","forms":["passage","passages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時間流逝","explanation":"指時間從一個時刻不斷向前經過，強調歲月推移帶來的變化。","examples":[{"en":"The passage of time helped him understand what had happened.","zh":"隨著時間流逝，他逐漸理解了發生的一切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The passage of years softened her anger.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0196538a40ede00","term":"passage","forms":["passage","passages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通道或走廊","explanation":"指供人或物穿過的狹長空間，例如建築物裡的走廊；它是“從一邊透過到另一邊”的最具體形象。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow passage led from the kitchen to the garden.","zh":"一條狹窄的通道從廚房通向花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow passage connects the two courtyards.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf816809a4d8aa98ed09","word":"passenger","forms":["passenger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e03abfbbbcd86f9","term":"passenger","forms":["passenger","passengers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"乘客","explanation":"乘坐汽車、公共汽車、火車、飛機或船等交通工具，但不負責駕駛、操作，也不屬於工作人員的人，就是 passenger。","examples":[{"en":"All passengers must fasten their seat belts before takeoff.","zh":"所有乘客都必須在起飛前繫好安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A passenger on the bus offered me her seat.","zh":"公交車上的一位乘客主動把座位讓給了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passenger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f90c3cafb0092b5a","term":"passenger","forms":["passenger","passengers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"團隊中的搭便車者","explanation":"在團隊或集體中，這個詞可以比喻只享受團隊成果、卻沒有承擔應有工作的人，就像坐車卻不參與駕駛一樣。","examples":[{"en":"He was a passenger in the team and contributed almost nothing.","zh":"他在隊裡只是個搭便車的人，幾乎沒有任何貢獻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone must contribute; this team cannot carry passengers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passenger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-76b1ee582dbd709cf8e9","word":"passion","forms":["passion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-924cb06f7bcb917a","term":"passion","forms":["passion","passions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持久熱愛","explanation":"指對某件事持續很久、願意投入大量時間和精力的強烈願望或熱愛。它比普通的興趣更深、更能推動人的行動。","examples":[{"en":"She has a passion for restoring old houses.","zh":"她熱衷於修復老房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His passion for teaching never faded.","zh":"他對教學的熱愛從未減退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3414b8732429379","term":"passion","forms":["passion","passions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈情感","explanation":"指非常強烈的感情，尤其是熱烈的愛，也可以是極端的恨。這裡強調情感的力量，而不一定表示長期的興趣。","examples":[{"en":"Their passion for each other was obvious to everyone.","zh":"他們彼此之間熾烈的感情對所有人都很明顯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The debate was driven by passion rather than evidence.","zh":"這場辯論更多是由強烈情緒而不是證據推動的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-117621ca9b86ec98e0cf","word":"passionate","forms":["passionate"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebdaebb10d7d9c57","term":"passionate","forms":["passionate","more passionate","most passionate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱烈的；充滿激情的","explanation":"指一個人對愛情、某人或某件事懷有強烈而投入的感情；在親密關係中也可帶有明顯的浪漫或性意味。","examples":[{"en":"She is passionate about protecting local wildlife.","zh":"她熱衷於保護當地的野生動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They shared a passionate kiss before saying goodbye.","zh":"告別前，他們熱烈地吻了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passionate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58341ee0f61ed1ea","term":"passionate","forms":["passionate","more passionate","most passionate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感情強烈的；激動的","explanation":"指情緒、觀點或表達方式帶著很強的感情色彩，像心裡的火一下子燒旺了；不一定與愛情有關。","examples":[{"en":"He gave a passionate speech about equal access to education.","zh":"他發表了一篇情緒飽滿、呼籲教育機會平等的演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The passionate debate continued long after dinner.","zh":"這場激烈的辯論在晚餐後持續了很久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passionate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7f1d7bc2124decc0ebf","word":"passive","forms":["passive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8fe838b6066ede8","term":"passive","forms":["passive","more passive","most passive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"被動承受的","explanation":"指某人或某物只是承受外來的行動、影響或處理，沒有作出相應的主動反應。","examples":[{"en":"The audience remained passive while the speaker answered questions.","zh":"演講者回答問題時，觀眾只是被動地聽著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plant is passive in this process and only receives the treatment.","zh":"在這個過程中，這株植物只是被動接受處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e95342aa38330829","term":"passive","forms":["passive","more passive","most passive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不採取行動的","explanation":"指面對問題或局面時不主動做任何事情，任由事情發展。","examples":[{"en":"He remained passive during the protest.","zh":"抗議期間，他始終沒有採取行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You cannot stay passive when a child is in danger.","zh":"孩子處於危險中時，你不能袖手旁觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5907e9366acb0a65","term":"passive","forms":["passive","more passive","most passive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"被動語態的","explanation":"語法上指使用被動語態的句子或結構：重點放在承受動作的人或事物，而不是動作的執行者。","examples":[{"en":"The report was written in the passive voice.","zh":"這份報告使用了被動語態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Passive sentences often leave the actor unstated.","zh":"被動句常常不說明動作的執行者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbc471ca60092bbe6c63","word":"passport","forms":["passport"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95259e9215012b44","term":"passport","forms":["passport","passports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"護照","explanation":"由政府簽發、證明持有人身份和國籍，通常用於國際旅行的正式證件。它像一張帶有本人身份資訊的國際通行證。","examples":[{"en":"You need a valid passport to travel abroad.","zh":"出國旅行需要有效護照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please show your passport at the border.","zh":"請在邊境出示護照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16ff6d31a2e5c825","term":"passport","forms":["passport","passports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通行憑證","explanation":"泛指允許某人進入某處或透過某處的檔案、證件或許可，是從真實護照“讓人通行”這一作用擴充套件出來的較寬泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"This badge is your passport into the restricted area.","zh":"這張徽章是你進入限制區域的通行憑證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fluency in another language can be a passport to employment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e884898da28047151d0","word":"password","forms":["password"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef1c8f034e27ca33","term":"password","forms":["password","passwords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"登入密碼；訪問密碼","explanation":"這是進入賬戶、電腦、網路或遊戲關卡時輸入的字元組合。雖然名稱中有“word”，現代 password 不一定是單詞，也可以是字母、數字、符號組成的字串，甚至是一整句短語。","examples":[{"en":"I forgot my password and had to reset it.","zh":"我忘記了密碼，只好重置它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Never share your password with anyone.","zh":"永遠不要把你的密碼告訴任何人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/password","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2228bd303b59052","term":"password","forms":["password","passwords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通行口令；暗號","explanation":"這是守門人或組織用來確認來者有權進入某處、接觸某項資訊的秘密詞語。它保留了“說對口令就能透過”的核心畫面，常見於軍事、秘密行動或帶有儀式感的場景。","examples":[{"en":"The guard asked for the password before opening the gate.","zh":"守衛在開啟大門前要求對方說出口令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without the password, even uniformed soldiers could not pass the checkpoint.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/password","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84ccdf8a849ffbc98d3a","word":"past","forms":["past"],"officialPos":"adj./n./prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd112f6d2cd32d54","term":"past","forms":["past","more past","most past"],"pos":"adj","zh":"過去的；已結束的","explanation":"指事情已經發生並結束，或某段經歷已經屬於過去。它把現在和已經走過的時間界線分開，例如過去的輝煌如今不再是現在的現實。","examples":[{"en":"We should learn from our past mistakes.","zh":"我們應該從過去的錯誤中吸取教訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Those past glories cannot be recovered.","zh":"那些昔日的輝煌已經無法重現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/past","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33ca70398ad5521f","term":"past","forms":["past","more past","most past"],"pos":"adv","zh":"經過；從旁邊走過","explanation":"表示人或物從某處、某人旁邊經過並繼續向前，就像沿著路越過一個位置點。重點是經過，而不是到達後停下。","examples":[{"en":"I watched him walk past without saying hello.","zh":"我看著他走過去，連招呼也沒打。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bus drove past our house.","zh":"一輛公共汽車從我們家旁邊駛過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/past","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-634c92a63f64fef1","term":"past","forms":["past","pasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過去；過去的時期","explanation":"指現在以前已經發生的全部時間或其中一段時期，與現在和未來相對。可以把它想成已經走過的路：發生過的事情都留在這條路的後方。","examples":[{"en":"The museum tells the story of the city's past.","zh":"這座博物館講述了這座城市的過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We cannot change the past.","zh":"我們無法改變過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/past","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1edbd68de59be75a","term":"past","forms":["past"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……之外；經過……","explanation":"表示位置或數量已經越過某個參照點，到了它的另一邊或更遠處。空間上可以是某房間之後，數量上也可以是超過某個界限。","examples":[{"en":"The restroom is just past the elevator.","zh":"洗手間就在電梯後面一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Walk past the bakery and turn left.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/past","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4c18ee0ada59e343691","word":"pasta","forms":["pasta"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30874df790963527","term":"pasta","forms":["pasta","pastas","paste"],"pos":"noun","zh":"義大利麵（作食材）","explanation":"指用小麥和水，有時加雞蛋製成的麵糰及其製品，通常做成各種形狀，乾燥後煮熟食用。這裡著重把 pasta 看作一種麵食材料或食品類別，而不是已經裝盤的一份菜。","examples":[{"en":"I bought some pasta for dinner.","zh":"我買了些義大利麵，準備晚飯吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cook the pasta in boiling water for ten minutes.","zh":"把義大利麵放在沸水裡煮十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pasta","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3f685725e3696b2","term":"pasta","forms":["pasta","pastas","paste"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一份麵食","explanation":"指已經做成的一道麵食或一份裝盤的義大利麵，例如煮熟後配上醬汁、蔬菜或其他食材的菜。這裡的 pasta 從“麵食材料”自然延伸到“由它做成的餐食”。","examples":[{"en":"We had pasta with tomato sauce for lunch.","zh":"我們午餐吃了番茄醬義大利麵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pasta was delicious, but the sauce was too salty.","zh":"這道義大利麵很好吃，但醬汁太鹹了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pasta","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2c183d5a12aea35598b","word":"paste","forms":["paste"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb63775ab1567154","term":"paste","forms":["paste","pastes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"糊狀物；糊","explanation":"指由液體和粉末、碎料等混合成的柔軟溼潤物質，通常不易保持清晰形狀，有時還能用來黏合東西。它是這個詞最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"Mix the flour with a little water to make a thick paste.","zh":"把麵粉和少量水混合，調成濃稠的糊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Apply the paste evenly to the back of the paper.","zh":"把糊均勻地塗在紙的背面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a27a3092f70fd1f","term":"paste","forms":["paste","pastes","pasting","pasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"貼上複製的內容","explanation":"在電腦操作中，指把已經複製或剪下的文字、圖片等內容放到另一個位置。它仍然像把東西“黏”進新位置，只是被貼上的物件變成了數字內容。","examples":[{"en":"Copy the address and paste it into the form.","zh":"複製這個地址，然後把它貼上到表格裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pasted the photo into the document.","zh":"他把照片貼上到了文件中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-853dcf4db0705ed7fccc","word":"pastime","forms":["pastime"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e621cdc3d9586f8c","term":"pastime","forms":["pastime","pastimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消遣；娛樂活動","explanation":"指讓人感到愉快、用來打發時間的活動，例如聊天、閱讀、園藝或下棋。重點不在於完成任務，而在於輕鬆享受這段時間。","examples":[{"en":"Reading has become my favorite pastime.","zh":"閱讀已經成了我最喜歡的消遣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Chatting with neighbors is a pleasant pastime.","zh":"和鄰居聊天是一種愉快的消遣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e8a10a5bb2a29d363e3c","word":"pastry","forms":["pastry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31931ba76ce4910d","term":"pastry","forms":["pastry","pastries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一件糕點","explanation":"指用麵粉和油脂製成並烘烤的一件糕點，例如派皮點心、撻、酥皮點心等；重點是看得見、可以數的一件成品。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a pastry and a coffee for breakfast.","zh":"我買了一塊糕點和一杯咖啡當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bakery makes fresh pastries every morning.","zh":"這家麵包店每天早上製作新鮮糕點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e17da53f85c39c4","term":"pastry","forms":["pastry","pastries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"糕點的總稱","explanation":"把各種 pastry 作為一個食品類別來談時，pastry 表示“糕點這一類”，不是某一件具體糕點。","examples":[{"en":"This café is known for its excellent pastry.","zh":"這家咖啡館以優質糕點聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bakery sells freshly made pastry every morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pastry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68d753f055b1a15b3949","word":"pat","forms":["pat"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cdbdbd6841eac79","term":"pat","forms":["pat","pats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕拍聲","explanation":"指輕而短的拍擊或敲擊聲，尤其是腳步或物體輕輕落下時發出的聲音，正是“手掌輕拍”這一核心畫面的聲音版本。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a soft pat on the window.","zh":"我們聽到窗戶上有輕輕的一聲拍響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard the soft pat of slippers in the hall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4acf57b9f973ce78","term":"pat","forms":["pat","pats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕拍；輕拍動作","explanation":"指用手掌輕輕拍一下，通常表達安慰、鼓勵、問候或吸引注意，而不是要造成傷害。","examples":[{"en":"She gave her nervous friend a gentle pat on the back.","zh":"她輕輕拍了拍緊張朋友的背。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave the puppy a gentle pat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b232c53687503444","term":"pat","forms":["pat","pats","patting","patted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕拍","explanation":"用手掌輕輕拍人或物，常用於安慰、鼓勵、表示親近或吸引注意；這就是 pat 最直接的核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"He patted the child on the shoulder and smiled.","zh":"他輕輕拍了拍孩子的肩膀，然後笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He patted the dog's head gently.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8db227eeed930611","term":"pat","forms":["pat","pats","patting","patted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拍平；拍成形","explanation":"反覆輕拍柔軟材料，使它變平、變光滑或形成需要的形狀，仍然是“用輕拍改變表面”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Pat the dough into small rounds before baking.","zh":"烘烤前，把麵糰拍成小圓片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pat each ball of clay flat with your fingertips.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4895eb44afc336fecbb","word":"patch","forms":["patch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00cf5cb7168cf871","term":"patch","forms":["patch","patches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣物補丁","explanation":"指縫在或貼在衣物上的一小塊材料，用來蓋住破洞、磨損處或加強薄弱部位。這是“把一小塊東西貼上去修補”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"There is a patch on the elbow of my old jacket.","zh":"我那件舊夾克的肘部有一塊補丁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sewed a patch over the hole in his jeans.","zh":"她在他牛仔褲的破洞上縫了一塊補丁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1277e372c9754fc","term":"patch","forms":["patch","patches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"修補片","explanation":"指用來堵住或修復水壺、屋頂等物品破損處的一小塊材料。它把衣服上的補丁概念擴充套件到了其他物品。","examples":[{"en":"The plumber put a patch on the leaking pipe.","zh":"水管工在漏水的管子上加了一塊修補片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small patch stopped the leak in the roof.","zh":"一小塊修補片止住了屋頂的漏水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a99143a2b7268ad9","term":"patch","forms":["patch","patches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"區域性；一段時期","explanation":"表示整體中一小塊與周圍不同的部分，也可表示一段與平常不同的時期，例如一段困難時期。這裡的“不同的一小塊”已經從實體材料擴充套件到了地點、時間和狀態。","examples":[{"en":"We went through a rough patch after the move.","zh":"搬家後我們經歷了一段艱難時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bright patch of sunlight fell across the floor.","zh":"一小片明亮的陽光落在地板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a138e534860e063","term":"patch","forms":["patch","patches","patching","patched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縫補","explanation":"指在破損處縫上一塊布、皮革等材料來修補。它是名詞“補丁”對應的最基本動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"I patched my jeans before going to work.","zh":"我上班前把牛仔褲補好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He patched the torn trousers with matching fabric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cd6b391db6a118bee1f","word":"patent","forms":["patent"],"officialPos":"n./adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4f48f0b8b55211d","term":"patent","forms":["patent","more patent","most patent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公開而明顯的","explanation":"指某事清楚地顯露出來，沒有被隱藏或掩飾，別人很容易看出。","examples":[{"en":"The conflict between the two reports was patent.","zh":"兩份報告之間的矛盾顯而易見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her patent reluctance made the meeting awkward.","zh":"她明顯不情願，使會議氣氛很尷尬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17728e1f3c70b0f6","term":"patent","forms":["patent","more patent","most patent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯而易見的","explanation":"強調某個判斷、錯誤或荒謬之處明顯到幾乎不需要解釋，常帶有批評意味。","examples":[{"en":"The claim that water does not freeze is patent nonsense.","zh":"說水不會結冰，顯然是胡說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The explanation was a patent attempt to avoid responsibility.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b774a91d96f21ed","term":"patent","forms":["patent","patents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發明專利","explanation":"指政府確認發明者在規定期限內擁有製造、銷售或使用該發明的專有權，也可指證明這種權利的檔案。這是現代英語中最重要的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer filed a patent for a quieter electric motor.","zh":"這名工程師為一種更安靜的電動機申請了專利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inventor applied for a patent on her device.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9144b25e814d8afa","term":"patent","forms":["patent","patents","patenting","patented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為發明申請專利","explanation":"指向政府機構登記一項新發明，從而在規定期限內取得製造、銷售或使用它的專有權。","examples":[{"en":"The company patented its new water-saving filter.","zh":"這家公司為自己的新型節水過濾器申請了專利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She patented the design before showing it to investors.","zh":"她在把設計展示給投資者之前先為它申請了專利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0af9f865bf637e67368","word":"path","forms":["path"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf6ae1ec2721f2c6","term":"path","forms":["path","paths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小路；步行道","explanation":"指人步行時走的路，通常比公路窄，也可以是人們長期走出來的土路。它是“通向某處的路”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow path leads from the garden to the river.","zh":"一條狹窄的小路從花園通向河邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We followed the path through the woods.","zh":"我們沿著小路穿過樹林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/path","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b7833b2a17acae5","term":"path","forms":["path","paths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展道路；人生軌跡","explanation":"把人的經歷、計劃或事物的發展想象成沿著一條路前進，因此表示一個人或一件事所走的方向和過程。它可以指職業、人生、成長或通向某個結果的路線。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a different path after leaving university.","zh":"大學畢業後，她選擇了另一條發展道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hard work is one path to success.","zh":"努力是通往成功的一條道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/path","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1776e45bf96c145a8e35","word":"pathetic","forms":["pathetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d2538cc30a49207","term":"pathetic","forms":["pathetic","more pathetic","most pathetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人同情的；可憐的","explanation":"形容某人或某種處境令人心酸、想要給予幫助或同情，重點是引發憐憫，而不只是說情況很糟。","examples":[{"en":"Her pathetic cry for help made everyone stop and look back.","zh":"她那令人心酸的求救聲讓所有人都停下來回頭看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lost puppy gave a pathetic little whimper.","zh":"那隻走失的小狗發出令人憐惜的嗚咽聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pathetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ed4eeb0d5577817","term":"pathetic","forms":["pathetic","more pathetic","most pathetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可悲的；糟糕得可鄙的","explanation":"形容表現、能力或結果差得很可憐，已經讓人不只是失望，還產生嘲笑或鄙視。這是現代口語中很常見、也很尖刻的用法。","examples":[{"en":"That was a pathetic attempt to fix the computer.","zh":"那是一次糟糕得可笑的電腦維修嘗試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The excuse was a pathetic attempt to avoid responsibility.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pathetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96d61fe343ddf5e0d8d6","word":"patience","forms":["patience"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99b102819735606c","term":"patience","forms":["patience","patiences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耐心；忍耐","explanation":"指在等待、練習或困難中不急躁，能夠鎮定地堅持下去；它就像安靜地等牌一步步排好一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Learning to play the piano takes patience.","zh":"學習彈鋼琴需要耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She waited with patience while the repairs were completed.","zh":"修理完成時，她耐心地等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80e58b89711d1c7c","term":"patience","forms":["patience","patiences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"單人紙牌遊戲","explanation":"指一種通常由一個人玩的紙牌遊戲，玩家要慢慢按規則排列紙牌；這個名稱也強調了遊戲需要耐心。","examples":[{"en":"My grandfather plays patience every evening.","zh":"我爺爺每天晚上都玩單人紙牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She played patience while waiting for the telephone to ring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patience","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2295ff7a8bd8b3f2884c","word":"patient","forms":["patient"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c84bc88c74a0940","term":"patient","forms":["patient","more patient","most patient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"耐心的","explanation":"指願意等待，遇到拖延或不順利時仍能控制情緒、不急躁。它是 patient 最常見的形容詞義，核心畫面就是安靜地承受等待。","examples":[{"en":"Please be patient while we check your order.","zh":"我們核對訂單時，請耐心等一等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is patient with children who ask many questions.","zh":"她對愛問很多問題的孩子很有耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ffaa2891351aba0","term":"patient","forms":["patient","patients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"病人；患者","explanation":"指正在接受醫生、護士、牙醫或其他醫療人員照料的人。這個名詞義和“接受治療”直接相連，是日常英語中非常重要的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor spoke with each patient before the examination.","zh":"醫生在檢查前和每位患者交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient rested while waiting for the surgeon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1155c23d603d643e73f8","word":"patriot","forms":["patriot"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5119b491a7dc0b4e","term":"patriot","forms":["patriot","patriots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愛國者","explanation":"patriot 指把自己的國家看得很重要，並積極支援、維護或保衛它的人。這個詞的核心畫面是：在國家需要時，願意站出來承擔責任、保護共同家園。","examples":[{"en":"She is a patriot who spends her time helping communities affected by the war.","zh":"她是一位愛國者，把時間花在幫助受戰爭影響的社群上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He called the soldiers patriots for defending their country.","zh":"他稱那些保衛國家計程車兵為愛國者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patriot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28bd2f7fc7affd6b","term":"patriot","forms":["patriot","Patriots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一枚愛國者導彈","explanation":"這裡的 Patriot 是對單個愛國者導彈的非正式稱呼，是導彈系統專名的個體用法。","examples":[{"en":"A Patriot intercepted the incoming missile before it reached the city.","zh":"一枚愛國者導彈在來襲導彈抵達城市前將其攔截。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crew loaded another Patriot onto the missile launcher.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patriot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81b5cc40a8f63ea72b2a","word":"patriotic","forms":["patriotic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae75e8b384821ab2","term":"patriotic","forms":["patriotic","more patriotic","most patriotic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愛國的；體現愛國情感的","explanation":"指一個人真誠熱愛自己的國家，或某種言行、作品和活動表現出這種愛國情感；重點是“出於愛國之心”，而不只是與國家有關。","examples":[{"en":"The school held a patriotic concert before the national holiday.","zh":"學校在國慶節前舉辦了一場愛國主義音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her patriotic speech inspired many young volunteers.","zh":"她的愛國演講激勵了許多年輕志願者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patriotic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e87f314e6f2183a5804f","word":"patrol","forms":["patrol"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1a210b4d80ac6f5","term":"patrol","forms":["patrol","patrols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巡邏；巡邏任務","explanation":"指守衛人員沿著崗哨、邊界或指定路線來回檢視，以防止襲擊或發現危險。重點是“按路線走動並保持警戒”這一行動。","examples":[{"en":"Two officers were on patrol near the station.","zh":"兩名警察正在車站附近巡邏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The night patrol checked every gate before midnight.","zh":"夜間巡邏隊在午夜前檢查了每一道門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patrol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-742f9162ea3b2d5a","term":"patrol","forms":["patrol","patrols","patrolling","patrolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"巡邏；巡視","explanation":"指警察、士兵或保安沿著某個地區或路線來回檢視，以維持安全並及時發現問題。這個動詞就是“巡邏”這一核心行動本身。","examples":[{"en":"Officers patrol the park until late at night.","zh":"警察一直巡邏公園到深夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Soldiers patrol the road along the frontier.","zh":"士兵巡邏邊境沿線的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patrol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e753a6b0a37cd1032c9","word":"patron","forms":["patron"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-893e51aaf5832a19","term":"patron","forms":["patron","patrons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護者；支持者","explanation":"指保護、支援或為某項事業發聲的人，重點是站在別人或某個目標一邊提供幫助。","examples":[{"en":"She has long been a patron of local wildlife projects.","zh":"她長期支援當地的野生動物保護專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The foundation became a major patron of the museum.","zh":"這家基金會成了該博物館的重要支持者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cc620ee9ae5f607","term":"patron","forms":["patron","patrons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術或學術的資助者","explanation":"指有影響力或有錢、長期資助藝術家、工匠、學者等人的人；這個義項是“支持者”在文化領域的具體發展。","examples":[{"en":"A wealthy patron helped the young painter open her first studio.","zh":"一位富有的資助者幫助這位年輕畫家開設了她的第一間工作室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wealthy patron financed the young composer's first opera.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b03821985d36d59","term":"patron","forms":["patron","patrons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顧客；光顧者","explanation":"指到商店、餐館、劇院或其他服務場所消費、使用服務的人，也就是受到該場所接待的顧客。","examples":[{"en":"The café offers free Wi-Fi to all its patrons.","zh":"這家咖啡館為所有顧客提供免費無線網路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular patrons receive a discount at the cafe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patron","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1fd38d5cbd2a997b91f7","word":"pattern","forms":["pattern"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ead2422bdb72b4b0","term":"pattern","forms":["pattern","patterns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"範本；樣板","explanation":"指可以照著製作、安排或模仿的範本。它強調“先有一個樣式，後來者依此形成相似結果”，所以既可以是具體的製作樣板，也可以是抽象的示範。","examples":[{"en":"The tailor used an old coat as a pattern for the new one.","zh":"裁縫把一件舊外套當作新外套的樣板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The first workshop became a pattern for later sessions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pattern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77e4de6b0021781e","term":"pattern","forms":["pattern","patterns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圖案；排列樣式","explanation":"指顏色、線條、形狀或其他元素按照一定方式組成的可見樣式。它可以是布料、牆紙、繪畫上的裝飾圖案，也可以是任何有規律的排列。","examples":[{"en":"The curtains have a simple pattern of blue leaves.","zh":"窗簾上有簡單的藍色葉子圖案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wallpaper has a repeating pattern.","zh":"牆紙上有重複的圖案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pattern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b040add9a1ae7b19","term":"pattern","forms":["pattern","patterns","patterning","patterned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"套用圖樣","explanation":"指把一個圖樣或範本應用到材料、物品或設計上，使它按照該樣式成形。這是名詞“範本、圖案”轉成動詞後的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"She patterned the fabric before cutting the dress.","zh":"她先按圖樣在布料上畫好樣板，再裁剪連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fabric was patterned with tiny blue stars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pattern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7867d5b1dd0c151e","term":"pattern","forms":["pattern","patterns","patterning","patterned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仿照；仿製","explanation":"指以某人或某物為範本來製作、設計或安排另一物，也就是“照著範本做”。它可以用於具體物品，也可以用於制度、建築或整體安排。","examples":[{"en":"The new library was patterned after a famous building.","zh":"這座新圖書館是仿照一座著名建築設計的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The club patterned its rules on a neighboring association's.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pattern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6210c0bf05396716df93","word":"pause","forms":["pause"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a8fc499a2df2639","term":"pause","forms":["pause","pauses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短暫停頓；休息","explanation":"指活動、動作或行進中暫時停下來的一段時間，重點是停頓之後還可能繼續。","examples":[{"en":"After a short pause, the speaker continued.","zh":"短暫停頓後，演講者繼續說了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took a pause halfway up the hill.","zh":"我們走到半山腰時休息了一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-99d88694adae5325","term":"pause","forms":["pause","Pauses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暫停按鈕","explanation":"指按下後讓影片、音樂、遊戲或電腦程式暫時停住，再按一次或使用相應控制即可繼續的按鈕。","examples":[{"en":"He pressed the pause button to answer the phone.","zh":"他按下暫停按鈕來接電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Press pause if you need to take notes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4139dee95159adf","term":"pause","forms":["pause","pauses","pausing","paused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暫時休息","explanation":"指自己經過一段努力後暫時停下來休息，之後通常還會繼續原來的活動。","examples":[{"en":"She paused to catch her breath.","zh":"她停下來喘了口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We paused beside the stream to catch our breath.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-118dca11f265eb63","term":"pause","forms":["pause","pauses","pausing","paused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暫停某項活動","explanation":"指把正在進行的活動暫時停下，但沒有結束它，之後可以重新開始。","examples":[{"en":"The team paused the project during the holidays.","zh":"團隊在假期期間暫時暫停了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pause the recording while I answer the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-faba69526b11c75e","term":"pause","forms":["pause","pauses","pausing","paused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暫停播放或執行","explanation":"指暫時停止歌曲、影片、遊戲或程式的播放、執行，並保留在當前位置，以便稍後繼續。","examples":[{"en":"Can you pause the video for a minute?","zh":"你能把影片暫停一分鐘嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I paused the game when dinner was ready.","zh":"晚飯準備好時，我暫停了遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pause","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb61f1d472962f754f92","word":"pave(ment)","forms":["pave","pavement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab351d37af850cdc","term":"pave","forms":["pave","paves","paving","paved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鋪設堅硬路面","explanation":"指用石頭、混凝土、瀝青等堅硬材料覆蓋地面，通常是為了讓車輛或行人更方便地通行。這是把路面鋪平、鋪牢這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The city paved the road outside our school last summer.","zh":"市政府去年夏天給我們學校外面的道路鋪了路面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They paved the parking area with concrete.","zh":"他們用混凝土鋪設了停車區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-036d84149bdee758","term":"pave","forms":["pave","paves","paving","paved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……鋪平道路","explanation":"指提前創造條件、消除障礙，使某件事更容易發生或成功。它把“把地面鋪平，讓人順利透過”的具體畫面轉成了抽象意義上的“鋪路”。","examples":[{"en":"The new research paved the way for better treatments.","zh":"這項新研究為更好的治療方法鋪平了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her early work paved the way for a successful career.","zh":"她早期的工作為她後來事業成功打下了基礎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc7779c53db6c8d7","term":"pavement","forms":["pavement","pavements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋪設的硬質地面","explanation":"指用石頭、磚、混凝土等鋪成的堅硬表面，是這個詞最基本的“鋪平、壓實的地面”概念，不限於道路。","examples":[{"en":"The old courtyard has a beautiful stone pavement.","zh":"這座老庭院鋪著漂亮的石地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water gathered in cracks in the pavement after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，水積在鋪面裂縫裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pavement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0602c1b2bc58b30","term":"pavement","forms":["pavement","pavements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人行道（英國等地區）","explanation":"在英國、愛爾蘭、南非等英語語境中，特指道路兩旁供行人行走的鋪面，也就是美國英語通常說的 sidewalk。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep to the pavement when the road is busy.","zh":"道路擁擠時，請走人行道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep your bicycle off the pavement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pavement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35cb9009af685e6793de","word":"paw","forms":["paw"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6bcda93940c95cb","term":"paw","forms":["paw","paws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的腳掌","explanation":"動物用來走路、抓取或觸碰東西的帶爪或指甲的腳掌，尤其常指貓、狗等四足動物的腳。","examples":[{"en":"The kitten lifted one paw and touched my hand.","zh":"小貓抬起一隻腳掌，碰了碰我的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog hurt its front paw.","zh":"這隻狗的前爪受傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35191ebcc161e933","term":"paw","forms":["paw","paws","pawing","pawed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用爪碰","explanation":"動物伸出爪子去碰某物，是“腳掌”這個核心概念變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"The puppy pawed at the ball.","zh":"小狗用爪子扒弄那個球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat pawed my face while I was sleeping.","zh":"我睡覺時，貓用爪子碰了碰我的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d12b38b808a9ecec","term":"paw","forms":["paw","paws","pawing","pawed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用爪扒找","explanation":"動物用爪子在一堆東西里翻扒，試圖找出或弄到裡面的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The raccoon pawed through the trash for food.","zh":"浣熊在垃圾裡用爪子扒找食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The terrier pawed through the pile of fallen leaves.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75815ffb2e028c35eed1","word":"pay(ment)","forms":["pay","payment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b19c92c308ca60ef","term":"pay","forms":["pay","pays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工資；報酬","explanation":"指為了工作或提供服務而得到的錢，是“付出勞動後收到的回報”。它可以泛指收入，也可以指不同工作所對應的報酬。","examples":[{"en":"The new job offers better pay and flexible hours.","zh":"這份新工作工資更高，工作時間也更靈活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She negotiated higher pay before accepting the transfer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-753cb0eb66699fee","term":"pay","forms":["pay","pays","paying","paid","payed","payest","paidest","paidst","payedst","payeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"付錢換取","explanation":"指為商品、服務或工作交出錢或其他補償。這是pay最基本的動作：付出應付之物，換來相應的東西或服務。","examples":[{"en":"I paid for the tickets online this morning.","zh":"我今天早上在網上付了票錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company will pay the designer next week.","zh":"公司下週會給設計師付款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9bd121aed3dbb44","term":"pay","forms":["pay","pays","paying","paid","payed","payest","paidest","paidst","payedst","payeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"償還；履行義務","explanation":"指透過付款或採取應有行動來清償債務、賬單或其他義務，也就是把欠下的東西交還清楚。","examples":[{"en":"Please pay the electricity bill before Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前付清電費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She paid her debt in full after getting the new job.","zh":"找到新工作後，她把債務全部還清了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2217b2d75b74948a","term":"payment","forms":["payment","payments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"付款行為","explanation":"指把錢交給對方、完成支付這一行為，重點在“付款”這個過程，而不是某一筆具體金額。","examples":[{"en":"Payment is due within 30 days.","zh":"應在三十天內付款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We received payment for the order yesterday.","zh":"我們昨天收到了這筆訂單的款項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/payment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7272f92aadb16486","term":"payment","forms":["payment","payments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一筆付款；已付金額","explanation":"指一次具體的付款、付出的一筆錢，或完成這筆錢的支付交易；這是“付款行為”落到實際金額上的結果。","examples":[{"en":"I made the final payment on my car loan today.","zh":"我今天付清了汽車貸款的最後一筆款項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final payment cleared the outstanding balance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/payment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d906f667d8010733648","word":"pea","forms":["pea"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2085131f48d2c061","term":"pea","forms":["pea","peas","pease"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豌豆類植物","explanation":"pea可以指豌豆屬的一類植物，也就是結出豌豆的植株。這個意義強調的是整株植物，而不是摘下來的種子。","examples":[{"en":"We grow peas in the garden every spring.","zh":"我們每年春天都在花園裡種豌豆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pea plants are beginning to flower.","zh":"豌豆植株開始開花了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbda3ba34c9df389","term":"pea","forms":["pea","peas","pease"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通常所說的豌豆植物","explanation":"不加其他限定時，pea通常就是日常所說的豌豆這種植物；它與上一個義項接近，但更強調普通語境中的常用名稱。","examples":[{"en":"Peas grow well in cool weather.","zh":"豌豆在涼爽的天氣里長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The peas needed taller supports as they grew.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05d31899ea99d3d7","term":"pea","forms":["pea","peas","pease"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豌豆種子","explanation":"pea也指從豌豆植株上取下、可以食用的圓形種子。這是餐桌和食譜中最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"She added a handful of peas to the soup.","zh":"她往湯里加了一把豌豆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was one pea left on his plate.","zh":"他的盤子裡還剩一顆豌豆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2e10c20bf46daf0ba03","word":"peace","forms":["peace"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c14d88d5e09dcd2b","term":"peace","forms":["peace","peaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安寧；平靜","explanation":"peace的核心畫面是衝突和喧鬧停下來，環境恢復安靜、有秩序、讓人感到安穩。它既可以說公共環境，也可以說某段生活狀態。","examples":[{"en":"After the storm, the quiet garden gave everyone a feeling of peace.","zh":"暴風雨過後，安靜的花園讓每個人都感到一陣寧靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I enjoy the peace of the garden at dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20b3298079fc276f","term":"peace","forms":["peace","peaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"和平；非戰爭狀態","explanation":"peace也專門指國家、地區或群體之間沒有戰爭，仍然保留“放下衝突、恢復安寧”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The leaders met to discuss how to build lasting peace in the region.","zh":"領導人會面討論如何在該地區建立持久和平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement brought peace after years of fighting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a4baa647f524b2a9e19","word":"peaceful","forms":["peaceful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9bad0e7d7f2918ca","term":"peaceful","forms":["peaceful","more peaceful","peacefuller","peacefuler","most peaceful","peacefullest","peacefulest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"和平的；沒有紛爭的","explanation":"指國家、社會或某項行動沒有戰爭、暴力和嚴重衝突；和平抗議雖然表達反對意見，但方式本身不使用暴力。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands joined a peaceful protest outside the city hall.","zh":"數千人在市政廳外參加了和平抗議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two countries reached a peaceful agreement.","zh":"兩國達成了和平協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peaceful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31bf5fb0fbeb9791","term":"peaceful","forms":["peaceful","more peaceful","peacefuller","peacefuler","most peaceful","peacefullest","peacefulest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平靜安寧的","explanation":"指景色、地方或時刻安靜而平和，幾乎沒有讓人不安的活動或聲音；就像沒有紛爭的和平狀態擴充套件到周圍環境。","examples":[{"en":"We spent a peaceful afternoon by the lake.","zh":"我們在湖邊度過了一個寧靜的下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The peaceful courtyard offered an escape from the busy market.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peaceful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85356064d03872ac4bed","word":"peach","forms":["peach"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3602828845f2d090","term":"peach","forms":["peach","peaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"桃；桃子","explanation":"指桃樹結出的柔軟多汁的核果，通常有絨毛狀外皮和中間的大核；這是 peach 最基本、最常見的含義。","examples":[{"en":"I sliced a ripe peach and put it on my cereal.","zh":"我把一個熟桃切片，放在麥片上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These peaches are sweet and very juicy.","zh":"這些桃子很甜，汁水也很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95f223879079a883","term":"peach","forms":["peach","peaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特別討喜的人或事物","explanation":"從桃子甜美可愛的形象引申而來，指某人非常討人喜歡，或某件事物特別出色、令人滿意。","examples":[{"en":"Your neighbor is a peach for bringing us dinner.","zh":"你的鄰居真是個大好人，還給我們送來了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thanks for repairing my bike; you are an absolute peach.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a095c7713e337faa7c39","word":"peacock","forms":["peacock"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6dceb17bf03ba89","term":"peacock","forms":["peacock","peacocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雄孔雀","explanation":"peacock 首先指雄孔雀，最顯眼的特徵是能展開色彩鮮豔、帶眼狀斑紋的尾羽來展示自己。","examples":[{"en":"A peacock spread its tail beside the garden pond.","zh":"一隻雄孔雀在花園池塘邊展開了尾羽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the peacock walk across the lawn.","zh":"我們看著那隻雄孔雀走過草坪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peacock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ee9e606474e322872c8","word":"peak","forms":["peak"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d918da5083cbaa04","term":"peak","forms":["peak","peaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖端；尖頂","explanation":"指物體末端尖銳或突出的部分，是“山峰”和“最高點”這些義項的具體形象來源。","examples":[{"en":"The foam formed soft peaks on top of the cake.","zh":"泡沫在蛋糕頂部形成了柔軟的小尖峰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Snow covered the peak of the steep roof.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b38c6cc2f2cf5176","term":"peak","forms":["peak","peaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"峰值；最高點","explanation":"指某個數量或現象在一段時間內達到的最高數值或最強程度。","examples":[{"en":"Sales reached a peak in December.","zh":"銷售額在十二月達到峰值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Electricity demand reaches its peak in the early evening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcb967daa645bab0","term":"peak","forms":["peak","peaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"山峰；頂峰","explanation":"指山、山丘或山脈中尖尖的最高處，最直接地體現了“峰頂”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"We reached the mountain peak before sunset.","zh":"我們在日落前到達了山峰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clouds concealed the mountain's highest peak.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb5d2523463872cf","term":"peak","forms":["peak","peaks","peaking","peaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"達到頂峰","explanation":"指某事物發展到最高程度或最大值，隨後可能趨於下降。","examples":[{"en":"The company peaked in the early 2000s.","zh":"這家公司在二十一世紀初達到鼎盛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Electricity demand peaks shortly after sunset.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5509840d0873adb04055","word":"peanut","forms":["peanut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f673fb7c9dba85af","term":"peanut","forms":["peanut","peanuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"花生","explanation":"花生是一種豆科植物的種子，外殼堅硬，通常作為零食或食材食用。雖然名稱裡有nut，但植物學上它屬於豆科。","examples":[{"en":"She ate a handful of peanuts with her tea.","zh":"她喝茶時吃了一把花生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sauce contains peanuts.","zh":"這種醬汁含有花生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peanut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80ab1acc2b52fe55","term":"peanut","forms":["peanut","peanuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極少量；微不足道的錢","explanation":"複數peanuts把花生“又小又不值錢”的形象引申為極少的錢、報酬或數量，強調少得可憐、幾乎不值得一提。","examples":[{"en":"They paid me peanuts for all that work.","zh":"他們給我的那點報酬，根本配不上那麼多工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They paid peanuts for that beautiful antique desk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peanut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97cfbe87531abe0c6bac","word":"pear","forms":["pear"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c0b94241c12b70a","term":"pear","forms":["pear","pears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"梨","explanation":"指梨樹結出的可食用果實，通常比蘋果更向果梗一端拉長。它既可以指一個梨，也可以泛指這種水果。","examples":[{"en":"I packed a pear for my lunch.","zh":"我給午餐帶了一個梨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These pears are sweet and juicy.","zh":"這些梨又甜又多汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3a51bd2cb3f292e","term":"pear","forms":["pear","pears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"梨樹","explanation":"指結梨的樹，尤其是栽培的梨樹。這裡關注的不是果實，而是產生果實的整株樹。","examples":[{"en":"A pear tree grows beside the old fence.","zh":"老籬笆旁邊長著一棵梨樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pear beside the gate produces fruit every autumn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26e3b2a5dc54dd5812fe","word":"pearl","forms":["pearl"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fafd8f4107b0bd6c","term":"pearl","forms":["pearl","pearls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珍珠","explanation":"指貝類體內形成的圓潤、有光澤的硬質小珠，常被用作首飾；它正是“圓潤、發光而珍貴”這一記憶形象的本義。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a pearl necklace to the wedding.","zh":"她戴著一條珍珠項鍊參加婚禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diver found a small pearl inside the oyster.","zh":"潛水員在牡蠣裡面發現了一顆小珍珠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pearl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f92b0545eb88034","term":"pearl","forms":["pearl","pearls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珍貴的人或物","explanation":"比喻特別珍貴、難得或令人喜愛的人、事物或品質，就像一顆珍貴的小珠。","examples":[{"en":"That book is a pearl of wisdom for new teachers.","zh":"那本書對新教師來說是一份寶貴的智慧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her kindness is a pearl in a difficult world.","zh":"在這個艱難的世界裡，她的善良是一種珍貴的品質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pearl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-757982d77738f2a4e3fd","word":"peasant","forms":["peasant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5c03c8577795b4e","term":"peasant","forms":["peasant","peasants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農民","explanation":"指主要靠耕種土地謀生的人，尤其是小農、佃農或農業僱工；這是 peasant 最核心的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The peasants worked in the fields from sunrise to sunset.","zh":"農民們從日出一直在田裡幹活到日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The king promised land to the peasants.","zh":"國王答應把土地分給農民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peasant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2b2e5ddebda4dc3cfa7","word":"pebble","forms":["pebble"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02ffb468a07cc445","term":"pebble","forms":["pebble","pebbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小圓石；鵝卵石","explanation":"指一塊小石頭，尤其是經過水流沖刷、表面變得圓滑的石子，常見於河灘、海灘或小路上。","examples":[{"en":"She picked up a smooth pebble from the riverbank.","zh":"她從河岸邊撿起了一顆光滑的小石子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children skipped pebbles across the lake.","zh":"孩子們讓小石子在湖面上打水漂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pebble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-974aaac18031d81c","term":"pebble","forms":["pebble","pebbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地質學中的礫石","explanation":"在地理學和地質學中，指直徑約為 4 至 64 毫米的一類顆粒，比沙粒大，但還沒有大到通常所說的石塊程度。","examples":[{"en":"The stream carried sand, pebbles, and larger stones downstream.","zh":"這條溪流把沙子、礫石和更大的石塊帶向下遊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sample contains rounded pebbles embedded in sandstone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pebble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f7439aa4e2b5d340bf3","word":"peculiar","forms":["peculiar"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-014ffe36a310e0d6","term":"peculiar","forms":["peculiar","more peculiar","most peculiar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇怪的；不尋常的","explanation":"表示和通常情況不同，因而讓人覺得奇怪、古怪或不大尋常。它可以描述外表、聲音、行為、氣味或氣氛，重點是“異乎尋常”，不一定表示非常嚴重。","examples":[{"en":"There was a peculiar smell in the empty room.","zh":"空房間裡有一股奇怪的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a peculiar look when I mentioned his name.","zh":"我提到他的名字時，她用一種奇怪的眼神看著我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peculiar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28e2f283c48e3b2a","term":"peculiar","forms":["peculiar","more peculiar","most peculiar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"某地或某情境特有的","explanation":"表示某種事物特別屬於某個地方、群體或情況，在那裡常見或具有代表性；這裡的重點不是“奇怪”，而是“專屬於某處或某種條件”。","examples":[{"en":"This species of bird is peculiar to the northern islands.","zh":"這種鳥是北部群島特有的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bird has markings peculiar to this island.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peculiar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4bb2d2d7f23cc2595531","word":"pedal","forms":["pedal"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4090fcca8ef56b64","term":"pedal","forms":["pedal","pedals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"踏板","explanation":"指用腳操作、用來控制或驅動機器的槓桿式部件，例如汽車的踏板、腳踏車的腳蹬或鋼琴的踏板。它就是記憶影象中腳下的那個裝置。","examples":[{"en":"She pressed the brake pedal when the light turned red.","zh":"紅燈亮時，她踩下了剎車踏板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One of my bike pedals fell off.","zh":"我的腳踏車有一個腳蹬掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07cf8ff32e732dac","term":"pedal","forms":["pedal","pedals","pedaling","pedalling","pedaled","pedalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蹬車","explanation":"指騎腳踏車時連續蹬動腳蹬，使車向前行進。它把“腳踩踏板”這一核心動作直接變成了騎車動作。","examples":[{"en":"He pedaled up the steep hill and stopped for a rest.","zh":"他蹬車上了陡坡，然後停下來休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children pedaled around the park all afternoon.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在公園裡騎車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-750cfe5c94c6b2f63d3b","word":"pedestrian","forms":["pedestrian"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-119e3bcd97032e6f","term":"pedestrian","forms":["pedestrian","more pedestrian","most pedestrian"],"pos":"adj","zh":"行人的；步行的","explanation":"指與步行者有關，或專門供步行者使用的事物。可以把它理解為“給走路的人用的”，例如道路上供人過街的設施。","examples":[{"en":"The city built a pedestrian bridge over the highway.","zh":"這座城市在高速公路上方修建了一座人行天橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Drivers must stop at the pedestrian crossing.","zh":"司機必須在行人過街處停車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedestrian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9349af4f3cb8f65c","term":"pedestrian","forms":["pedestrian","more pedestrian","most pedestrian"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平庸乏味的","explanation":"從“平平走路、沒有特別動作”的形象引申而來，表示普通、缺乏新意或不夠精彩，常帶有輕微的貶義。","examples":[{"en":"The film had an interesting idea but a pedestrian ending.","zh":"這部電影的構想很有意思，但結尾平淡乏味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her presentation was clear, though somewhat pedestrian.","zh":"她的報告很清楚，不過有些平庸，缺乏新意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedestrian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8eee816b877b9b8","term":"pedestrian","forms":["pedestrian","pedestrians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"步行者；行人","explanation":"指正在走路、沒有使用車輛的人，尤其是在交通語境中與司機或車輛相對。它就是“用腳走路的人”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The driver slowed down to let a pedestrian cross.","zh":"司機減速讓一名行人過馬路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge has a separate path for pedestrians.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedestrian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ce8980ebe0167061739","word":"peek","forms":["peek"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-659f79e39c187999","term":"peek","forms":["peek","peeks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一瞥；偷看","explanation":"指快速、短暫地看一下，常帶有偷偷看或不想引人注意的感覺；它就是“從門縫後看一眼”這個畫面中的那一下檢視。","examples":[{"en":"Can I take a peek at your new camera?","zh":"我可以看一眼你的新相機嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had a quick peek inside the box.","zh":"她快速地往盒子裡看了一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f45aea24e1309481","term":"peek","forms":["peek","peeks","peeking","peeked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"窺看；偷看","explanation":"指偷偷地、快速地看，常像半眯著眼或從縫隙裡觀察；核心畫面就是躲在門縫後小心看一眼。","examples":[{"en":"He peeked through the door to see who was outside.","zh":"他從門縫裡偷偷看了一眼，想知道外面是誰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't peek at the answers before the test.","zh":"考試前不要偷看答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-099ae4672fc8922e18dc","word":"peel","forms":["peel"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aef91f2d8bcf0338","term":"peel","forms":["peel","peels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外皮","explanation":"peel 是水果、蔬菜等包在外面的皮，尤其常指可以剝下來的那一層。它和果肉相對，是“從表面剝開”這條核心概念的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The orange peel made the kitchen smell fresh.","zh":"橙子皮讓廚房裡充滿清新的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add the lemon peel to the cake mixture.","zh":"把檸檬皮加入蛋糕麵糊中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d89d0e3d97d15c4","term":"peel","forms":["peel","peels","peeling","peeled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剝去外皮","explanation":"peel 作及物動詞時，表示把水果、蔬菜等的外皮剝掉，就是把表面那一層從裡面分離出來。","examples":[{"en":"Please peel the potatoes before you boil them.","zh":"請先把土豆削皮再煮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He peeled an apple for his daughter.","zh":"他給女兒削了一個蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21a644c49ad8b3fd","term":"peel","forms":["peel","peels","peeling","peeled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剝去表層","explanation":"這個用法把“外皮”擴充套件為任何外部或頂部的一層，表示把那一層從物體上去掉。","examples":[{"en":"She peeled the sticker off the jar.","zh":"她把罐子上的貼紙撕了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers peeled away the old paint.","zh":"工人們剝掉了舊油漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bd90c53efda38d9","term":"peel","forms":["peel","peels","peeling","peeled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表層脫落","explanation":"peel 作不及物動詞時，表示表層自己脫開、成片或成條地掉落；皮膚曬傷後脫皮就是典型例子。","examples":[{"en":"The paint is peeling off the window frame.","zh":"窗框上的油漆正在脫落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My sunburned skin started to peel.","zh":"我曬傷的皮膚開始脫皮了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9ae0309808fc250ffbd","word":"peep","forms":["peep"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dca07bb945c2406b","term":"peep","forms":["peep","peeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啾啾聲；細小尖聲","explanation":"指小鳥等發出的輕短、尖細的聲音，也可泛指類似的微小聲音；這是“聲音”這條主線的中心義。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a tiny peep from the nest.","zh":"我們聽見巢裡傳來一聲細小的啾啾聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby bird gave a peep when its mother returned.","zh":"鳥媽媽回來時，小鳥發出了一聲啾啾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3059d2ba7d8ea8f1","term":"peep","forms":["peep","peeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偷看一眼","explanation":"指快速、通常不想被發現地看一眼，尤其是從小孔、縫隙或遮擋物後面看；這是“探頭看”這條主線的中心義。","examples":[{"en":"I took a quick peep through the curtain to see who was outside.","zh":"我從窗簾後面快速偷看了一眼，想知道外面是誰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can I have a peep inside the box?","zh":"我能偷偷看一眼盒子裡面嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad403a33c254d365","term":"peep","forms":["peep","peeps","peeping","peeped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"窺看；偷看","explanation":"指從小孔、縫隙或遮擋物後面快速看，往往是不想被注意到；它正是“探頭看一眼”這條核心影象的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"She peeped through the door before entering.","zh":"她進門前先從門縫裡偷看了一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child peeped at the presents under the bed.","zh":"孩子偷偷看了一眼床底下的禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ffc1d06387ef8bb7a34","word":"peer","forms":["peer"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb2b56f7dd7dbe16","term":"peer","forms":["peer","peers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同等者","explanation":"指在能力、地位、價值或水平上與另一個人或事物相當的物件。核心畫面是兩者並排站立，沒有明顯高下。","examples":[{"en":"She is widely regarded as a peer of the leading researchers in her field.","zh":"人們普遍認為她和本領域的頂尖研究人員水平相當。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new design has few peers in terms of reliability.","zh":"這種新設計在可靠性方面幾乎沒有同等的產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea0fd17c373c23e2","term":"peer","forms":["peer","peers","peering","peered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細窺看","explanation":"指眯著眼、伸頭或集中注意力去看，彷彿目光要從遮擋物或遠處搜出目標。它把“看”寫成一種費力探索的動作。","examples":[{"en":"She peered through the fog, trying to find the road.","zh":"她透過濃霧仔細張望，試圖找到那條路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He peered into the dark room before stepping inside.","zh":"他仔細往黑暗的房間裡看了看，才走進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e21a6b0cb193057e06ac","word":"pen","forms":["pen"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a82105c5232ff109","term":"pen","forms":["pen","pens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物圍欄","explanation":"pen 是用來把羊、牛等家畜圈在裡面的圍欄或圈養場所。核心畫面就是“用邊界把動物圈住”。","examples":[{"en":"The sheep are resting in the pen.","zh":"羊正在圍欄裡休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They built a new pen for the calves.","zh":"他們為小牛建了一個新的圍欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aaec4802e8b9c389","term":"pen","forms":["pen","pens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"筆","explanation":"pen 是用墨水書寫或做標記的工具，現代通常是細長的管狀書寫工具；它源自早期的羽毛筆。","examples":[{"en":"I always carry a pen in my bag.","zh":"我總是在包裡帶一支筆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She signed the form with a blue pen.","zh":"她用藍色的筆在表格上籤了名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-705081774d844130","term":"pen","forms":["pen","pens","penning","penned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"創作或寫下","explanation":"pen 作動詞時，表示寫作或創作一篇文章、一本書等，突出“拿起筆完成作品”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"She penned a moving article about her childhood.","zh":"她寫了一篇感人的文章，講述自己的童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor penned the lyrics for the film.","zh":"這位演員為這部電影創作了歌詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-debfc54303301ee216c1","word":"penalty","forms":["penalty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21b800a467dbd90a","term":"penalty","forms":["penalty","penalties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律刑罰","explanation":"指法律規定的刑罰，即犯罪者因犯罪而受到的正式懲處，可以是監禁、勞動等，不一定是交錢。","examples":[{"en":"The maximum penalty for the offense is five years in prison.","zh":"這項罪行的最高刑罰是五年監禁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He faced a severe penalty for violating the law.","zh":"他因違反法律而面臨嚴厲的刑罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penalty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b51e405718adb7f2","term":"penalty","forms":["penalty","penalties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育判罰","explanation":"在體育比賽中，指球員犯規後受到的判罰；在足球等專案中，常特指由犯規導致的點球機會。","examples":[{"en":"The referee awarded a penalty after the defender handled the ball.","zh":"後衛手球后，裁判判給對方一個點球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team conceded a penalty in the final minutes.","zh":"這支球隊在最後幾分鐘因犯規送給了對方一個點球機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penalty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad828533d6daa8c3","term":"penalty","forms":["penalty","penalties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行為帶來的不利後果","explanation":"指過去某個錯誤、決定或行為後來帶來的損失或不利結果；這裡不一定有人正式施加懲罰，而是事情本身讓人“付出代價”。","examples":[{"en":"The company paid the penalty for ignoring the safety warnings.","zh":"這家公司因忽視安全警告而付出了代價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team paid the penalty for its slow start.","zh":"這支球隊為開局緩慢付出了代價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penalty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13809668fb436386706f","word":"pencil","forms":["pencil"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b88b5580cfa5d5b","term":"pencil","forms":["pencil","pencils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鉛筆","explanation":"一種用石墨芯在紙上留下灰黑色線條的書寫工具，通常外面包著木頭，使用前要削尖。","examples":[{"en":"I sharpened my pencil before the test.","zh":"考試前我把鉛筆削尖了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote the address in pencil.","zh":"她用鉛筆寫下了地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pencil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62a2fed3d6e08c44835f","word":"pending","forms":["pending"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ca32aa4e76580bf","term":"pending","forms":["pending"],"pos":"adj","zh":"待定的；等待確認的","explanation":"事情已經提出或正在處理，但最後的決定、結果或確認還沒有出來，所以仍然懸而未決。","examples":[{"en":"Your application is still pending approval.","zh":"你的申請仍在等待批准。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The payment is pending confirmation from the bank.","zh":"這筆付款還在等待銀行確認。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pending","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25aaf1fda9445d62","term":"pending","forms":["pending"],"pos":"adj","zh":"尚未完成的","explanation":"事情已經開始或已經安排，但還沒有做完、處理完或正式結束，像一件暫時懸著的任務。","examples":[{"en":"Several orders are still pending.","zh":"還有幾筆訂單尚未處理完。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are still three pending applications to review.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pending","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-897f489f33f674ecd861","word":"penetrate","forms":["penetrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32284980166bc92b","term":"penetrate","forms":["penetrate","penetrates","penetrating","penetrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穿透並進入內部","explanation":"指光、聲音、物體或人穿過外層、障礙或表面，進入某個空間的內部。重點不是單純到達，而是“穿進去”，所以這個義項正是整詞“進入內部”這一核心形象的起點。","examples":[{"en":"A small amount of sunlight penetrated the thick curtains.","zh":"少量陽光穿透了厚厚的窗簾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The arrow penetrated the wooden shield.","zh":"箭穿透了木盾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penetrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3da648168ac276d5","term":"penetrate","forms":["penetrate","penetrates","penetrating","penetrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"深入理解","explanation":"指穿過晦澀、複雜或有意設定的障礙，終於理解某種思想、文字或問題的深層內容。它不是普通的“聽懂”或“知道”，而是像穿過表面進入意義內部。","examples":[{"en":"After several readings, she finally penetrated the author's argument.","zh":"讀了幾遍後，她終於理解了作者論證的深層意思。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Few readers penetrate the complexity of his argument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penetrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b543de760061e33","term":"penetrate","forms":["penetrate","penetrates","penetrating","penetrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"深深觸動","explanation":"指某種聲音、景象、話語或感情穿進人的內心，強烈地影響情緒。這裡穿透的不是身體，而是人的感受和內心，因此和“打動、觸動”相連。","examples":[{"en":"The singer's lonely voice penetrated my heart.","zh":"那位歌手孤獨的歌聲深深觸動了我的心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her account of the disaster penetrated his indifference.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penetrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a4346f806b28b3ce949","word":"penguin","forms":["penguin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b1e262577d4ec40","term":"penguin","forms":["penguin","penguins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"企鵝","explanation":"指企鵝科的海鳥：不會飛，擅長游泳，通常黑白相間，身體直立並用短腿行走。這是現代英語中 penguin 最常見、最應該先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a penguin dive into the water.","zh":"我們看著一隻企鵝潛入水中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Penguins huddle together to keep warm.","zh":"企鵝擠在一起取暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penguin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85af70cde80552a2dcb8","word":"peninsula","forms":["peninsula"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ee2789c7c2cb609","term":"peninsula","forms":["peninsula","peninsulas","peninsulae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"半島","explanation":"指從大陸或較大陸地向水中伸出去的一塊陸地，只有一側與主體陸地相連，因此看起來像一座沒有完全分離的島。記住“幾乎是島”這個畫面，就能抓住它的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The city sits on a narrow peninsula between the lake and the bay.","zh":"這座城市坐落在湖泊和海灣之間的一條狹窄半島上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We drove to the end of the peninsula to watch the sunset.","zh":"我們開車到半島盡頭看日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peninsula","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03d04f7fcebc3c449289","word":"penny","forms":["penny"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c625daa5e4db1bb","term":"penny","forms":["penny","pennies","pence","pens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英國的一便士","explanation":"在現代英國語境中，penny是一英鎊的百分之一，也可指面值為一便士的銅色硬幣；它是最基本的小額貨幣單位之一。","examples":[{"en":"I found a penny under the sofa.","zh":"我在沙發下面找到了一枚一便士硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sweets cost twenty pence.","zh":"這些糖果要二十便士。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56abb6b95b41b433","term":"penny","forms":["penny","pennies","pence","pens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美國一美分硬幣","explanation":"在美國以及過去的加拿大，penny通常是一美分硬幣，即美元的百分之一；日常說的“one cent”常常就是這枚硬幣。","examples":[{"en":"She put a penny in the jar.","zh":"她把一枚一美分硬幣放進罐子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This machine takes pennies and nickels.","zh":"這臺機器收一美分和五美分硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f94510ee44a9bbec84a7","word":"pension","forms":["pension"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c0b73cfb39c4ba9","term":"pension","forms":["pension","pensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"退休金；養老金","explanation":"這是人工作或服役多年後，按照相關安排定期領取的錢，用來維持退休後的生活。它不一定由政府發放，也可以來自私人養老金計劃。","examples":[{"en":"Many people rely on their pension to cover everyday expenses.","zh":"許多人依靠退休金支付日常開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She started receiving a pension after leaving the company.","zh":"她離開公司後開始領取退休金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecc2d095eb24be80","term":"pension","forms":["pension","pensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寄宿旅店；膳宿公寓","explanation":"這裡的 pension 不是退休金，而是讓旅客付費住宿、通常還提供部分餐食的小型旅店，常帶有家庭經營的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed at a quiet pension near the lake.","zh":"我們住在湖邊一家安靜的小旅店裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family-run pension serves breakfast on its sunny terrace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9022680f888674e2b22","word":"people","forms":["people"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fbbfb4150a0863bd","term":"people","forms":["people","peoples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人們；人群","explanation":"這是 person 的複數，指兩個或更多的人，常作為整體來談論。中文裡常對應“人們”“大家”或“人群”。","examples":[{"en":"There were so many people at the restaurant last night.","zh":"昨晚那家餐館裡人特別多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People often change their minds after hearing new information.","zh":"人們聽到新資訊後常常會改變想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/people","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1488c973e8cad781","term":"people","forms":["people","peoples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人類；一般人","explanation":"這裡把人作為一類生命或社會成員來泛指，意思接近“人類”或“人一般會……”。","examples":[{"en":"People need both rest and meaningful work.","zh":"人既需要休息，也需要有意義的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People do not like being treated as machines.","zh":"人們不喜歡被當成機器對待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/people","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8cbbcf29d9cef89675c5","word":"pepper","forms":["pepper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95e0a44cf25a1d18","term":"pepper","forms":["pepper","peppers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胡椒粉；胡椒","explanation":"pepper也指由胡椒的未成熟果實發酵、曬乾後製成的香料，通常是黑胡椒或白胡椒，既可以指顆粒，也可以指磨成的粉。","examples":[{"en":"Add a little salt and pepper to the soup.","zh":"給湯加一點鹽和胡椒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ground fresh pepper over the salad.","zh":"她把新鮮胡椒磨在沙拉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pepper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5626386491dae83","term":"pepper","forms":["pepper","peppers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辣椒；甜椒","explanation":"在許多英語地區，pepper還指辣椒科植物的果實，包括紅、綠、黃或白色的中空果實，既可以是不辣的甜椒，也可以是很辣的品種。","examples":[{"en":"Chop one red pepper and add it to the pan.","zh":"把一個紅辣椒切碎，放進鍋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These peppers are sweet rather than hot.","zh":"這些辣椒是甜的，不辣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pepper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b427c3dec9045990213c","word":"per","forms":["per"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e23a846a0c2c5859","term":"per","forms":["per"],"pos":"prep","zh":"每；每個","explanation":"把一個總量分攤到每個人或每個物件上，表示“每一個……得到多少”。這是“per”最重要、最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The museum charges ten dollars per visitor.","zh":"這家博物館每位遊客收費十美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Admission costs twelve dollars per adult.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/per","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28efc2762ca4188c","term":"per","forms":["per"],"pos":"prep","zh":"每單位；按比例","explanation":"表示兩個單位之間的換算或比例關係，例如一個英尺包含多少英寸，或一小時行駛多少英里。它仍然保留“把數量對應到每一個單位”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"This car can travel 60 miles per hour.","zh":"這輛車每小時可以行駛六十英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tickets cost twelve euros per person.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/per","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d27d1573bfd9ca915115","word":"perceive","forms":["perceive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea194bb3ff7e44b3","term":"perceive","forms":["perceive","perceives","perceiving","perceived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"察覺；感知到","explanation":"指透過眼睛、耳朵等感官，或透過心裡的理解，意識到某個事實、變化或情況。重點不是單純看到表面，而是把資訊“接住”並意識到它。","examples":[{"en":"She quickly perceived that something was wrong.","zh":"她很快察覺到出了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The animal can perceive tiny changes in temperature.","zh":"這種動物能夠感知到溫度的細微變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perceive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2ec15dcbb0db39d","term":"perceive","forms":["perceive","perceives","perceiving","perceived"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為；看作","explanation":"指人在心裡把某人或某事理解、評價成某種樣子，也就是對它形成特定印象。這裡的資訊已經不只是被感知，還被解釋成“是怎樣的”。","examples":[{"en":"The company is perceived as a leader in clean energy.","zh":"這家公司被認為是清潔能源領域的領先者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Residents perceive the project as a threat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perceive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd86717aca41c558c78c","word":"percent","forms":["percent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d74ca0e9ffadda84","term":"percent","forms":["percent","percents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"百分比；比例","explanation":"指一個整體中按每一百份計算的比例本身，而不是專門指某個數字後的形式。","examples":[{"en":"Only a small percent of applicants reached the final stage.","zh":"只有一小部分申請者進入了最後階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What percent of the budget goes to maintenance?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/percent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":5,"counts":{"111":4,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-8975c9b4ea061e5476c7","word":"percentage","forms":["percentage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d5f64911b548895","term":"percentage","forms":["percentage","percentages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"百分比；比例","explanation":"表示某個數量或人數佔總量的多少，通常按一百份來計算；也就是“整體中的一部分所佔的比例”。","examples":[{"en":"A small percentage of employees work from home on Fridays.","zh":"少數員工每週五在家辦公。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The percentage of people who recycle has increased.","zh":"進行回收的人所佔的比例提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/percentage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07dfb036f6e072c9","term":"percentage","forms":["percentage","percentages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提成；分成","explanation":"表示從銷售額、利潤或其他收入中按比例取得的一份錢，常見於銷售人員、代理人或合作方的報酬。","examples":[{"en":"The salesperson earns a percentage of every contract she signs.","zh":"這名銷售員每簽下一份合同，就能拿到一部分提成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agent receives a percentage of each sale.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/percentage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9327b46b590a1441bb4a","word":"perception","forms":["perception"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5cf9e9853a220c10","term":"perception","forms":["perception","perceptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感知與解釋感官資訊","explanation":"指人把視覺、聽覺等感官收到的資訊組織起來，並辨認、解釋成有意義的內容。重點不只是“收到刺激”，而是形成了對所感知事物的認識。","examples":[{"en":"Our perception of color changes in different lighting.","zh":"在不同的光線下，我們對顏色的感知會發生變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stress can affect your perception of the world around you.","zh":"壓力會影響你對周圍世界的感知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3de860de4d8f79da","term":"perception","forms":["perception","perceptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對事物的理解","explanation":"指意識中對某件事、某個情況或某段經歷形成的理解。它把感知到的資訊進一步整理成對事物的認識，因此常帶有“怎麼看、怎麼理解”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The article changed my perception of the problem.","zh":"這篇文章改變了我對這個問題的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Travel changed her perception of the neighboring country.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87fb00d259cbcd677063","word":"perch","forms":["perch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17f27335449c964e","term":"perch","forms":["perch","perches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鱸魚屬的淡水魚","explanation":"這裡的 perch 是鱸魚屬中的淡水魚，通常生活在湖泊、河流等水域。","examples":[{"en":"The children saw a yellow perch near the shore.","zh":"孩子們在岸邊看見了一條黃鱸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We caught several perch in the shallow lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf2295c51d43d7f8","term":"perch","forms":["perch","perches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鳥棲息的橫杆或樹枝","explanation":"perch 可以是鳥用來停歇的樹枝、橫杆、窗沿等高處，就像記憶畫面中的那根杆。","examples":[{"en":"The parrot sat quietly on its perch.","zh":"鸚鵡安靜地坐在自己的棲木上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bird watched us from a branch perch.","zh":"一隻鳥從樹枝棲木上看著我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f548789d6c4df82","term":"perch","forms":["perch","perches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顯眼而有利的位置","explanation":"從鳥站在高處的畫面引申，perch 也指一個穩固、突出、便於觀察或發揮優勢的位置。","examples":[{"en":"From her perch by the window, she could see the whole street.","zh":"她從窗邊那個高而有利的位置可以看清整條街。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"From her perch on the ladder, she directed the decorators.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcc5edbaf7c1f08a","term":"perch","forms":["perch","perches","perching","perched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鳥停棲","explanation":"鳥 perch，就是像落到橫杆上一樣停在樹枝、肩膀或其他高處。","examples":[{"en":"A small bird perched on the fence.","zh":"一隻小鳥停在籬笆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The owl perched above the doorway.","zh":"貓頭鷹停在門口上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fafe97f7def328bbd4f1","word":"perfect","forms":["perfect"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-663501367e77137c","term":"perfect","forms":["perfect","perfecter","more perfect","perfectest","most perfect"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完全符合定義","explanation":"指某物的形狀、性質或表現與規定的標準完全相符，像標準範例一樣準確。","examples":[{"en":"The artist drew a perfect circle without using a compass.","zh":"這位藝術家不用圓規就畫出了一個標準的圓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The timing was perfect for the surprise.","zh":"這個時間安排得恰到好處，正適合製造驚喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfa506aa44854216","term":"perfect","forms":["perfect","perfecter","more perfect","perfectest","most perfect"],"pos":"adj","zh":"各部分協調並適合用途","explanation":"強調事物的各個部分配合得當，或者某件東西雖然不一定毫無缺陷，卻特別適合某個具體目的。","examples":[{"en":"This small table is perfect for working beside the window.","zh":"這張小桌子非常適合放在窗邊工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team found the perfect solution for the problem.","zh":"團隊找到了這個問題的理想解決方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72bd23dc34da5158","term":"perfect","forms":["perfect","perfecter","more perfect","perfectest","most perfect"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沒有錯誤或瑕疵","explanation":"指表現、結果或質量達到極高水平，沒有明顯錯誤或缺陷；日常評價中常譯為“完美的”。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a perfect performance in the final round.","zh":"她在最後一輪中表現得無可挑剔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You made a perfect copy of the original.","zh":"你把原件複製得完全一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31567351a9441444","term":"perfect","forms":["perfect","perfects","perfecting","perfected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使完善；打磨","explanation":"指透過修改、練習或反覆打磨，使作品、技能或方法更加成熟、準確和無缺陷。","examples":[{"en":"He spent the weekend perfecting his presentation.","zh":"他整個週末都在打磨自己的演示稿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of practice perfected her technique.","zh":"多年的練習使她的技術達到了爐火純青的程度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b1d44d9f5fdb42391db","word":"perfection","forms":["perfection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce144cca6afe48ca","term":"perfection","forms":["perfection","perfections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完美；圓滿","explanation":"指某件事或某種狀態已經達到最高程度，幾乎沒有低於標準的部分；重點在整體質量和完整程度。","examples":[{"en":"Years of careful practice brought her performance close to perfection.","zh":"多年的認真練習使她的表演接近完美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No design achieves perfection on its first attempt.","zh":"沒有哪種設計第一次嘗試就能達到完美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8bc3b5488f12340","term":"perfection","forms":["perfection","perfections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完美之處；無瑕的優點","explanation":"指某個人或事物所具備的某種特別出色、近乎無瑕的品質或優點；它把“完美”落到一個具體的特質上。","examples":[{"en":"Her patience is one of the perfections that make her a remarkable teacher.","zh":"她的耐心是使她成為出色教師的諸多優點之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The biographer celebrates her many supposed perfections.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc6d1833bae465ef7440","word":"perform","forms":["perform"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c364920e750d433f","term":"perform","forms":["perform","performs","performing","performed","performest","performedst","performeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"執行；完成","explanation":"指按照要求把一項任務、動作或程式實際做出來，重點是執行而不是單純計劃。做實驗、進行檢查或完成操作時都可以用它。","examples":[{"en":"The technicians performed a safety check before opening the building.","zh":"技術人員在開放大樓前進行了一次安全檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scientists performed several experiments.","zh":"科學家進行了幾項實驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2756a12c3f6cb6e6","term":"perform","forms":["perform","performs","performing","performed","performest","performedst","performeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發揮；運轉","explanation":"指人、團隊、機器或系統按照應有的方式工作併產生相應效果。說某人表現好，強調實際工作結果和能力發揮。","examples":[{"en":"The new employee performs well under pressure.","zh":"這名新員工在壓力下表現很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engine performs well in freezing conditions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-208dfb3f2f2ece93","term":"perform","forms":["perform","performs","performing","performed","performest","performedst","performeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"登臺表演","explanation":"指演員、歌手或其他表演者在觀眾面前把戲劇、音樂等呈現出來，目的是展示或娛樂。這是“把東西做出來並讓人看見”最直觀的場景。","examples":[{"en":"The band will perform in the park this Saturday.","zh":"樂隊本週六將在公園演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She performed the song beautifully.","zh":"她把這首歌演繹得很動聽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a1898716ef67796fcc8","word":"performance","forms":["performance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5982c83ecf19cb8","term":"performance","forms":["performance","performances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"執行；表現","explanation":"指把任務、職責或計劃真正執行出來的過程，也可強調執行時呈現出的表現。它連線著“把事情做出來”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The performance of her duties requires great attention to detail.","zh":"履行她的職責需要非常注意細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager praised the team's performance during the project.","zh":"經理表揚了團隊在專案期間的表現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/performance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e72245815b07665b","term":"performance","forms":["performance","performances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現場演出","explanation":"指演員、樂隊或其他表演者在觀眾面前進行的一場現場演出。它仍然是“把某件事做出來”，只是場景變成了舞臺或現場。","examples":[{"en":"We bought tickets for the band's performance on Saturday.","zh":"我們買了週六那支樂隊演出的票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audience gave the dancers a standing ovation after the performance.","zh":"演出結束後，觀眾起立為舞者鼓掌喝彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/performance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f51be81307927c88b48","word":"performer","forms":["performer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e61d3a8e51395ef","term":"performer","forms":["performer","performers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表演者；演出者","explanation":"指在觀眾面前進行歌唱、舞蹈、戲劇、魔術等表演，以娛樂或展示給觀眾的人。這個詞強調“把表演呈現出來”，不只限於演員。","examples":[{"en":"The performer received a standing ovation after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，這位表演者贏得了全場起立鼓掌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a talented street performer.","zh":"她是一名很有天賦的街頭表演者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/performer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87115ffc0ff2450d","term":"performer","forms":["performer","performers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實施者；執行者","explanation":"泛指實際完成某個動作、行為或任務的人。這裡不一定有觀眾或舞臺，只強調這個人是行為的執行者。","examples":[{"en":"The performer of the action must be identified before the investigation can continue.","zh":"調查繼續進行前，必須先確定該行為的實施者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was the principal performer of these dangerous experiments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/performer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37ecf521c8f469c92ce4","word":"perfume","forms":["perfume"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0cae45de1bce2ac4","term":"perfume","forms":["perfume","perfumes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香味；芬芳","explanation":"指某種甜美、宜人的氣味，可能來自花、食物、空氣或其他散發香味的東西；這裡強調的是飄散出來、被聞到的那縷香氣。","examples":[{"en":"The perfume of the roses filled the garden.","zh":"玫瑰的芬芳充滿了花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A warm breeze carried the perfume of fresh bread.","zh":"一陣暖風送來了新鮮麵包的香味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c81a665502c6303","term":"perfume","forms":["perfume","perfumes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香水；香氛產品","explanation":"指為了製造宜人氣味而調製的物質，通常裝在瓶子裡供人塗抹或噴灑；它是產生那縷香味的東西。","examples":[{"en":"She wears a light perfume to work.","zh":"她上班時會噴一種淡淡的香水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He bought a bottle of perfume for his mother.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66ffb9a600ca5141","term":"perfume","forms":["perfume","perfumes","perfuming","perfumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……添香；使帶香味","explanation":"指把香水塗到某物上，或讓香味進入空氣、衣物等，使它們帶有宜人的香氣；這是把“香味”從氣息變成一種作用。","examples":[{"en":"She perfumed the room with a few drops of lavender oil.","zh":"她用幾滴薰衣草精油給房間增添了香味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Jasmine perfumed the warm evening air.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ba2ebb275e86668d38c","word":"perhaps","forms":["perhaps"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f04200a88457c90","term":"perhaps","forms":["perhaps"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也許；可能","explanation":"表示某件事有可能發生，但說話人不能確定，常用於提出推測或較委婉地表達意見。","examples":[{"en":"Perhaps John will come over for dinner.","zh":"約翰也許會過來吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Perhaps we should leave a little earlier.","zh":"我們也許應該早點出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perhaps","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3ec976bfe9099b5c8aec","word":"peril","forms":["peril"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02e03ac8d3c319b2","term":"peril","forms":["peril","perils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴重的迫近危險","explanation":"指某人或某物正面臨嚴重、可能很快造成傷害或損失的危險，重點是“處境很危險”，而不是一般的不方便。","examples":[{"en":"Several hikers were in peril after the bridge collapsed.","zh":"橋塌了以後，幾名徒步者陷入了危險之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement is in peril unless both sides compromise.","zh":"除非雙方都作出妥協，否則這項協議將面臨危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peril","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e6e01d1382cb394","term":"peril","forms":["peril","perils","periling","perilling","periled","perilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使處於危險中；危及","explanation":"表示主動把某人、某物或某項計劃推到危險邊緣，和名詞的核心畫面相連：名詞是站在懸崖邊的危險，動詞是把它推到懸崖邊。","examples":[{"en":"The careless decision could peril the future of the entire project.","zh":"這個草率的決定可能危及整個專案的未來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They refused to peril their children's safety for a shortcut.","zh":"他們不願為了走捷徑而危及孩子們的安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peril","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-514cb13f603464f97849","word":"period","forms":["period"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9294dc835aa62751","term":"period","forms":["period","periods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段時間","explanation":"指從一個時間點到另一個時間點之間、被當作整體看待的一段時間。它可以很短，也可以很長，關鍵是這段時間具有清楚的範圍或共同情況。","examples":[{"en":"There was a period of confusion after the announcement.","zh":"公告發布後有一段混亂時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a quiet period to finish this report.","zh":"我需要一段安靜的時間來完成這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/period","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29493c10cef0bc9f","term":"period","forms":["period","periods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歷史時期","explanation":"指歷史上具有相對統一特點的一段時期，通常比普通的一段時間更有時代範圍和歷史意義。","examples":[{"en":"Food rationing continued throughout the postwar period.","zh":"戰後時期一直實行食品配給。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibition covers the medieval period.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/period","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12452a0eb130ee9a","term":"period","forms":["period","periods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"句號","explanation":"指寫在句子末尾的“.”，表示一句話結束；在縮寫中也可以用來標記省略形式。","examples":[{"en":"Put a period at the end of the sentence.","zh":"在句子末尾加一個句號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The abbreviation ends with a period.","zh":"這個縮寫以句號結尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/period","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72d58a93377a82195599","word":"perish","forms":["perish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3b4915564bac44d","term":"perish","forms":["perish","perishes","perishing","perished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸消失","explanation":"事物在時間、忽視或不利條件下慢慢衰敗，最後不復存在；重點是從存在走向“沒有了”，不一定指突然毀壞。","examples":[{"en":"Many local traditions perish when younger generations stop learning them.","zh":"年輕一代不再學習時，許多地方傳統會逐漸消失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without care, the old garden slowly perished.","zh":"沒有照料，這座老花園漸漸衰敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8a9d22e7ff44b64","term":"perish","forms":["perish","perishes","perishing","perished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"死亡","explanation":"用於人或動物時，表示在事故、戰爭、災難等情況下死亡，把生命也看作走向徹底消亡；通常暗示悲慘或重大情境。","examples":[{"en":"Several passengers perished when the ferry caught fire.","zh":"渡輪起火時，幾名乘客不幸遇難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several sailors perished when the ship sank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0dd1b6d5c52eec73e28b","word":"permanent","forms":["permanent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b663deabaefa633","term":"permanent","forms":["permanent","more permanent","most permanent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"永久的；永恆的","explanation":"表示理論上沒有終點、不會消失或不會改變的狀態，常用於強調某事並非暫時存在。","examples":[{"en":"Nothing in this world is truly permanent.","zh":"這個世界上沒有什麼是真正永恆的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum wants to make the exhibit permanent.","zh":"博物館希望讓這項展覽永久保留下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permanent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-248c241f4a9ecdee","term":"permanent","forms":["permanent","more permanent","most permanent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"長期的；固定的","explanation":"表示會持續很長時間，或者在可預見的將來一直維持，重點是穩定而非短暫。","examples":[{"en":"She is looking for a permanent job near her home.","zh":"她正在找一份離家近的長期工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The countries are now locked in a permanent state of conflict.","zh":"這些國家如今陷入了長期衝突狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permanent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-55fefe05337374f40b7b","word":"permissible","forms":["permissible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3f8ad62aefba2ac","term":"permissible","forms":["permissible","more permissible","most permissible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獲准的；允許的","explanation":"指某種行為或做法得到規則、制度或有權決定者的許可，因此可以合法或合規地進行。記住那扇被門衛點頭放行的門：能透過，就是 permissible。","examples":[{"en":"Overtaking is permissible only when the road is clear.","zh":"只有道路暢通時才允許超車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rules state which types of payment are permissible.","zh":"規定說明了哪些付款方式是允許的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permissible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fdeb33892d1867626d6d","word":"permission","forms":["permission"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4daa383090b2158","term":"permission","forms":["permission","permissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"許可；准許","explanation":"指有權威或相關人士明確同意你做某事，重點是“得到通行的點頭”。它常用於正式請求或正式批准的場合。","examples":[{"en":"We need the owner's permission to use these photos.","zh":"我們需要得到所有者的許可才能使用這些照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She asked her parents for permission to stay out late.","zh":"她請求父母允許她晚點回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e3b6aa83ccac6f2","term":"permission","forms":["permission","permissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"准許這一行為","explanation":"強調“允許”這個決定或過程本身，而不只是某一項具體許可；可以把它看作有人為某件事開啟了門。","examples":[{"en":"The work began only after permission was granted.","zh":"獲得許可後，工作才開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Permission to enter must come from the landowner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85441a43c7cb9f242a5c","word":"permit","forms":["permit"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-287a7b426f705cb7","term":"permit","forms":["permit","permits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"許可證","explanation":"permit是官方檔案，證明某項活動已經獲准、合法，可以進行。它就是把“允許”具體寫在紙面或證件上的結果。","examples":[{"en":"You need a permit to park here overnight.","zh":"你需要許可證才能在這裡過夜停車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contractor displayed the building permit at the entrance.","zh":"承包商把建築許可證貼在入口處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0f6d1bcddbabeb0","term":"permit","forms":["permit","permits","permitting","permitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"允許某事發生","explanation":"permit表示放行某件事，讓它可以發生；重點在於不阻止、不禁止這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The rules do not permit outside food in the theater.","zh":"規定不允許把外帶食物帶進劇院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The quiet room permitted her to concentrate.","zh":"安靜的房間使她能夠集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a261fbdc48b3455","term":"permit","forms":["permit","permits","permitting","permitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"允許某人做某事","explanation":"permit也可以把“放行”物件明確為某個人，即准許某人做某事。","examples":[{"en":"The guard would not permit visitors to enter after dark.","zh":"警衛不允許訪客天黑後進入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her parents permitted her to travel alone.","zh":"她的父母允許她獨自旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46459f9bd8c39ba752f0","word":"persevere","forms":["persevere"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6862606ef64f72ce","term":"persevere","forms":["persevere","perseveres","persevering","persevered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堅持不懈","explanation":"即使任務困難、進展緩慢或受到挫折，也繼續努力完成目標；重點是“遇到阻力仍不放棄”。","examples":[{"en":"She persevered in her studies despite repeated failures.","zh":"儘管多次失敗，她還是堅持學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you persevere, you will eventually improve.","zh":"只要堅持下去，你最終會有所提高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persevere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c61425b1ba94748e725","word":"persist","forms":["persist"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-222441324d197f50","term":"persist","forms":["persist","persists","persisting","persisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堅持下去","explanation":"指面對困難、反對或失敗仍然繼續做某事，強調持續而且往往帶有堅定、不輕易放棄的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She persisted in asking questions until she understood the plan.","zh":"她堅持不斷提問，直到弄懂了這個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you persist despite the setbacks, you will eventually improve.","zh":"如果你儘管遇到挫折仍堅持下去，最終會有所進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68d1889e84bbcb02","term":"persist","forms":["persist","persists","persisting","persisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持續存在","explanation":"指某種狀態、問題、影響或現象沒有消失，仍然繼續存在；這裡堅持下去的不是人，而是事物本身。","examples":[{"en":"The smell persisted long after the windows were opened.","zh":"窗戶開啟很久以後，那股氣味仍然沒有消失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite repeated repairs, the electrical fault persisted for months.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d2a4d0e13a3e16b1027","word":"persistence","forms":["persistence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da23b3412be958d1","term":"persistence","forms":["persistence","persistences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅持不懈","explanation":"指一個人即使遇到拒絕、困難或失敗，仍繼續努力、不輕易放棄的品質。這裡的“持續”從行為延伸為堅定地堅持下去。","examples":[{"en":"Her persistence finally helped her get the job.","zh":"她堅持不懈，最終獲得了這份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I admire his persistence in learning the piano.","zh":"我很佩服他堅持學習鋼琴的毅力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persistence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-390d44ae8d56814d","term":"persistence","forms":["persistence","persistences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料持續儲存","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指資料在程式結束、裝置斷電或相關操作完成後仍然保留下來，而不是隨著程式停止而消失。","examples":[{"en":"The database provides persistence even after the application shuts down.","zh":"即使應用程式關閉，資料庫仍能儲存資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Database persistence keeps records intact after the program closes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persistence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75b07bb3ffb3b8ad63e7","word":"persistent","forms":["persistent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d401db8db58fa70","term":"persistent","forms":["persistent","more persistent","most persistent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅持不放棄","explanation":"形容人或其努力不肯停止，即使遇到困難或反覆失敗也繼續下去；這裡的“賴著不走”可以是堅韌，也可以是固執。","examples":[{"en":"Her persistent efforts finally opened the door to a new opportunity.","zh":"她堅持不懈的努力終於為自己開啟了新的機會之門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The persistent caller finally reached the department head.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persistent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0683a836479d3cd","term":"persistent","forms":["persistent","more persistent","most persistent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"反覆不斷","explanation":"形容聲音、動作或打擾一再出現，持續到讓人無法忽視，往往帶有令人厭煩的意味。","examples":[{"en":"A persistent buzzing kept us awake all night.","zh":"持續不斷的嗡嗡聲讓我們整夜無法入睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Persistent requests from readers persuaded the publisher to reprint the book.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persistent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38a81e87e79631e602bf","word":"person","forms":["person"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-83d0547ba1f64a47","term":"person","forms":["person","people","persons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人；個人","explanation":"指一個有獨立身份的個體，通常就是一個人。這個詞強調“一個具體的個人”，而不是泛泛的人類群體。","examples":[{"en":"Every person in the room received a name badge.","zh":"房間裡的每個人都領到了一張姓名牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a kind person who listens carefully.","zh":"她是一個善於認真傾聽的善良的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/person","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92b50d19244bfe1c","term":"person","forms":["person","people","persons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最重要的親密物件","explanation":"在現代非正式表達中，指和某人特別合拍、關係極深的人，常常是戀人、最好的朋友或人生伴侶。它把“一個具體的人”進一步突出為“對我來說最重要的那個人”。","examples":[{"en":"When I need advice, Maya is the person I call first—she's my person.","zh":"我需要建議時，第一個打電話的人總是瑪雅——她是我最重要的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whenever life gets difficult, she's my person.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/person","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a0a339b0c6d05538977","word":"personal","forms":["personal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1729b5f716ee0540","term":"personal","forms":["personal","more personal","most personal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"人的；關於人的","explanation":"表示與人本身有關，而不是與物品或動物有關。這是 personal“屬於人”的最基礎一層意思。","examples":[{"en":"The museum asks visitors not to leave personal belongings unattended.","zh":"博物館要求參觀者不要把個人物品放在無人看管的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study examines personal experiences of migration.","zh":"這項研究考察人們個人的遷移經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/personal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da6706bf4875ed8b","term":"personal","forms":["personal","more personal","most personal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"個人的；屬於某人的","explanation":"表示只屬於某個特定的人，或只與這個人的想法、選擇和生活有關，而不是代表所有人。","examples":[{"en":"Choosing a career is a deeply personal decision.","zh":"選擇職業是一個非常個人化的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She explained that the book reflected her personal values.","zh":"她解釋說，這本書反映了她個人的價值觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/personal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3489bee7b45e80ea","term":"personal","forms":["personal","more personal","most personal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"私人的；敏感的","explanation":"表示涉及個人隱私、親密關係或不願公開的話題，因此通常需要謹慎對待。","examples":[{"en":"He left the company for personal reasons.","zh":"他因為個人原因離開了公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I would rather not discuss such a personal matter at work.","zh":"我不想在工作場合討論這麼私人的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/personal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f046cfb2d0788f93898e","word":"personality","forms":["personality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33a158d5e95a4bdc","term":"personality","forms":["personality","personalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"性格；個性","explanation":"指構成一個人獨特身份的心理和社會特徵，例如一個人的脾氣、處事方式、興趣和待人方式。它強調“這個人整體上是什麼樣的人”，而不是某一個孤立行為。","examples":[{"en":"Her warm personality makes new students feel welcome.","zh":"她溫暖的性格讓新同學感到受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It took me time to understand his quiet personality.","zh":"我花了一些時間才瞭解他安靜的性格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/personality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd91546f9912fc37","term":"personality","forms":["personality","personalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鮮明特色；個性","explanation":"指文字、藝術作品、房間、品牌等非人的事物具有容易辨認、令人感興趣的獨特風格。它是把“人的獨特氣質”延伸到事物上。","examples":[{"en":"The small café has a lot of personality because of its colorful furniture.","zh":"這家小咖啡館因為傢俱色彩鮮豔而很有特色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old brick walls give the cafe personality.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/personality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45fa5047ae71ed93e17d","word":"personnel","forms":["personnel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13a9904b1df695db","term":"personnel","forms":["personnel","personnels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全體人員","explanation":"指某個機構、公司、部門或部隊中的工作人員整體，重點是“這一整隊人”，而不是其中的某一個人。","examples":[{"en":"All military personnel must attend the safety briefing.","zh":"所有軍方人員都必須參加安全簡報會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital is short of medical personnel this week.","zh":"這家醫院本週醫務人員不足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/personnel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82471fda285e5d14","term":"personnel","forms":["personnel","personnels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人事部門","explanation":"在公司或機構語境中，personnel 還可以指負責招聘、員工檔案和員工事務的人事部門，即“人事處”或“人力資源部門”。","examples":[{"en":"Please contact personnel if you need to change your address.","zh":"如果你需要更改地址，請聯絡人事部門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Contact personnel about your unused vacation days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/personnel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74425421116546fd8872","word":"perspective","forms":["perspective"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a09df566cf1e2cc","term":"perspective","forms":["perspective","perspectives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀點；角度","explanation":"指觀察、分析或評價某件事時所採用的角度，就像站在某個位置看一幅景色；換一個 perspective，結論可能也會不同。","examples":[{"en":"From a child's perspective, the journey seemed very long.","zh":"從孩子的角度看，這段旅程似乎很漫長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to consider the problem from a wider perspective.","zh":"我們需要從更寬廣的角度考慮這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perspective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fa941431fa1acd5","term":"perspective","forms":["perspective","perspectives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看問題的立場","explanation":"指選擇某一個角度來感受、分類、衡量或解釋經歷和資訊；它強調“用什麼框架來看”，比單個意見更有整體性。","examples":[{"en":"The book examines the war from a historical perspective.","zh":"這本書從歷史角度考察了這場戰爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her perspective on the issue changed after the meeting.","zh":"會議之後，她對這個問題的看法變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perspective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-e1721557ff52f415e5b5","word":"persuade","forms":["persuade"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b0b00936733d97c","term":"persuade","forms":["persuade","persuades","persuading","persuaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說服某人去做或接受某事","explanation":"透過理由、談話或影響使某人改變原來的打算，最後同意做某事、接受某物或採取某種行動。這是 persuade 在現代英語中的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"My friends persuaded me to stay for dinner.","zh":"我的朋友們說服我留下來吃晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She persuaded her brother into lending her his car.","zh":"她說服哥哥把車借給她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persuade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31438ab594c695ac18f3","word":"persuasion","forms":["persuasion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-277c293ee35dd256","term":"persuasion","forms":["persuasion","persuasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勸說；說服行為","explanation":"指試圖透過說理、請求或其他語言方式改變他人的想法，或讓對方採取某種行動；重點在“推動對方改變”的過程，不保證一定成功。","examples":[{"en":"The manager changed her mind after several weeks of persuasion.","zh":"經理經過幾周的勸說後改變了主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They settled the dispute by persuasion rather than force.","zh":"他們靠勸說而不是武力解決了爭端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persuasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab92c655801d6c95","term":"persuasion","forms":["persuasion","persuasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說服人的話；說服方法","explanation":"指用來影響某人觀點或決定的具體論點、說法或方法。它是“勸說”這個行動中拿出來使用的那套理由或表達。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm explanation was a powerful persuasion.","zh":"她冷靜的解釋是一種有力的說服手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No amount of persuasion could make him apologize.","zh":"無論怎樣勸說，都無法讓他道歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persuasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0067f3d5dd5d9bf9","term":"persuasion","forms":["persuasion","persuasions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說服力；影響力","explanation":"指一個人影響他人想法或感情的能力，即“說話能讓別人被打動、被改變”的力量。它是從“勸說行為”進一步抽象出的能力。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer won the case through the sheer power of persuasion.","zh":"那位律師憑藉純粹的說服力贏得了官司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His powers of persuasion finally secured their support.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persuasion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-610d1d8aaee3fc7dfc1c","word":"persuasive","forms":["persuasive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a32a400d0739e86","term":"persuasive","forms":["persuasive","more persuasive","most persuasive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有說服力的","explanation":"形容某人、觀點、理由或表達方式很能讓別人接受或改變想法。重點不是“聲音強硬”，而是它能有效地推動別人相信、同意或採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"She made a persuasive case for investing in public transport.","zh":"她為投資公共交通提出了很有說服力的理由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is persuasive enough to win over people who initially disagree.","zh":"他很有說服力，甚至能說服起初持反對意見的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/persuasive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39205ed78566d439026b","word":"pessimism","forms":["pessimism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0a662968da539a2","term":"pessimism","forms":["pessimism","pessimisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對壞結果的總體預期","explanation":"指一種總體的看法：認為事情往往會朝壞的方向發展，壞事很可能發生。它不只是某一次不開心，而是看待現實和未來時長期偏向消極的一種態度。","examples":[{"en":"Her pessimism made her expect the project to fail.","zh":"她的悲觀主義讓她預期這個專案會失敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the good news, he could not shake off his pessimism.","zh":"儘管有好訊息，他還是擺脫不了悲觀情緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pessimism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c9618dbf00ff0be","term":"pessimism","forms":["pessimism","pessimisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認為世界已壞到極點的哲學學說","explanation":"指一種系統的哲學觀點，認為現實世界已經是所有可能世界中最糟糕的一個。這裡的重點不是某個人暫時悲觀，而是把悲觀態度發展成一套關於世界本質的學說。","examples":[{"en":"The lecture compared philosophical pessimism with religious ideas about suffering.","zh":"這場講座比較了哲學悲觀主義與宗教關於苦難的觀念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The philosopher's pessimism treats existence as irredeemably painful.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pessimism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a53503b0a4c17d61a9cb","word":"pessimistic","forms":["pessimistic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8cbbbc3627867714","term":"pessimistic","forms":["pessimistic","more pessimistic","most pessimistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悲觀的","explanation":"形容一個人、觀點或判斷總是先想到不好的結果，對未來缺乏希望或信心。它的核心畫面是“先看見最壞的坑”，但不表示壞結果一定會發生。","examples":[{"en":"She is pessimistic about finding a new job.","zh":"她對找到新工作不太樂觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His pessimistic view made everyone worry about the project.","zh":"他的悲觀看法讓大家都開始擔心這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pessimistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f64e2d0a0c103cbe","term":"pessimistic","forms":["pessimistic","more pessimistic","most pessimistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"按最壞情況估計的","explanation":"用於計劃、預測或估算時，表示有意採用較保守、較不利的假設，把可能出現的最壞情況考慮進去。它仍然來自“先想到最壞結果”的核心意思，但不一定說明作出估計的人性格悲觀。","examples":[{"en":"Even the pessimistic estimate suggests that we have enough time.","zh":"即使按最悲觀的估計，我們的時間也夠用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even the pessimistic forecast predicts modest growth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pessimistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3975a18c2114c4d05cf0","word":"pest","forms":["pest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f867a63dbbf5e728","term":"pest","forms":["pest","pests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農業害蟲","explanation":"指會侵害農作物或牲畜、造成損失的昆蟲等小動物。核心形象就是“闖進農田並帶來損害的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers are looking for a safe way to control these pests.","zh":"農民正在尋找安全的方法來控制這些害蟲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A new pest has damaged the tomato plants.","zh":"一種新的害蟲損害了番茄植株。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8eb725bcf608dc6f","term":"pest","forms":["pest","pests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"討厭的人","explanation":"比喻一個不斷打擾別人、讓人覺得煩的人。它把“害蟲造成麻煩”的形象延伸到了人的行為上，通常帶有明顯的負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"My little brother can be a real pest when he wants attention.","zh":"我弟弟想引起別人注意時，真會變得特別煩人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please stop being a pest and let her finish her work.","zh":"別再煩人了，讓她把工作做完吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbba57318f71911354fd","word":"pet","forms":["pet"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-676df2369e82b12a","term":"pet","forms":["pet","pets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寵物","explanation":"指人為了陪伴而飼養的動物，例如狗、貓或魚；核心是“被人照料並陪伴的動物”。","examples":[{"en":"Our cat is the most playful pet in the house.","zh":"我們家的貓是屋裡最愛玩的寵物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you have any pets?","zh":"你養寵物嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f777828dc1f83c69","term":"pet","forms":["pet","pets","petting","petted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撫摸動物","explanation":"指用手輕柔地摸動物，通常是表達喜愛或安撫；這是從“寵物”這一物件自然發展出的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The children asked if they could pet the dog.","zh":"孩子們問能不能摸那條狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pet the cat gently.","zh":"請輕輕地摸這隻貓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe09b7f231ec19d6c8d3","word":"petition","forms":["petition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8288c0b938bd61a1","term":"petition","forms":["petition","petitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"請願書；請願","explanation":"指個人或團體向政府、君主等政治權力機構提交的正式書面請求，常希望獲得某項權利、保護或補救，也常附有許多人的簽名。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of residents signed a petition to protect the old forest.","zh":"數千名居民簽署了一份請願書，要求保護那片古老的森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The group submitted a petition for safer roads.","zh":"這個團體提交了一份要求改善道路安全的請願書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b92cb4dd1f184c7e3810","word":"petrol","forms":["petrol"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e74b40fba9b071a8","term":"petrol","forms":["petrol","petrols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽油","explanation":"一種從石油中提煉出來的液體燃料，通常裝進汽車油箱，為發動機提供動力。它就是從“地下的油”變成汽車能用的燃料。","examples":[{"en":"We need to stop at the next petrol station.","zh":"我們得在下一個加油站停一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This car runs on petrol.","zh":"這輛車用汽油驅動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petrol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78b276c9b6092746","term":"petrol","forms":["petrol","petrols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽油車","explanation":"非正式地，petrol 還可以指一輛使用汽油而不是柴油的汽車；這是從“使用這種燃料”轉指“使用這種燃料的車”。","examples":[{"en":"We compared a petrol with a diesel before buying the car.","zh":"買車前，我們比較了一輛汽油車和一輛柴油車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Older petrols often consume more fuel than newer models.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petrol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4212b193c22b64d7c6c","word":"petroleum","forms":["petroleum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a56dad6c192e666","term":"petroleum","forms":["petroleum","petroleums","petrolea"],"pos":"noun","zh":"石油；原油","explanation":"指自然埋藏在地下、由多種烴組成的可燃液體，通常就是我們說的石油或原油。它是“岩石中的油”這一核心畫面的直接體現，也可以作為燃料和許多工業產品的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"Many everyday products are made from petroleum.","zh":"許多日常用品都是用石油製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country imports most of its petroleum.","zh":"這個國家的大部分石油都依靠進口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petroleum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66f659ae21f1e819586c","word":"petty","forms":["petty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-918f5f131d7304a4","term":"petty","forms":["petty","pettier","more petty","pettiest","most petty"],"pos":"adj","zh":"瑣碎的；不重要的","explanation":"指某件事、某個錯誤或爭執很小，重要性低，不值得投入太多注意力。核心感覺是“只佔很小分量，卻被拿出來糾纏”。","examples":[{"en":"They spent the whole meeting arguing over a petty detail.","zh":"他們整個會議都在為一個無關緊要的細節爭論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dispute began with a petty misunderstanding.","zh":"這場爭執起初只是由一個小小的誤會引起的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4022f8634b0dd5cb","term":"petty","forms":["petty","pettier","more petty","pettiest","most petty"],"pos":"adj","zh":"心胸狹窄的；愛計較的","explanation":"形容人的興趣、眼界或行為侷限在狹小的個人得失上，缺少寬容和更大的視野。這裡的“小”從事情擴充套件到了人的心胸。","examples":[{"en":"It was petty of him to refuse to share the information.","zh":"他拒絕分享資訊，實在是心胸太狹窄了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is too petty to admit that someone else had a better idea.","zh":"她心胸太狹窄，不肯承認別人的想法更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e9926caf5a34b3625f9","word":"pharmacist","forms":["pharmacist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-424e96560675f3a0","term":"pharmacist","forms":["pharmacist","pharmacists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥劑師","explanation":"在藥房、醫院等場所負責配製、儲存和發放藥物，並向患者說明用法、用量和注意事項的專業人員。藥劑師的重點不只是把藥交給別人，還包括幫助人們安全、有效地使用藥物。","examples":[{"en":"If you have questions about this medicine, ask a pharmacist.","zh":"如果你對這種藥有疑問，可以諮詢藥劑師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pharmacist explained how often I should take the tablets.","zh":"藥劑師說明了我應該多久服一次這些藥片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pharmacist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20b04a4f018b89f369ce","word":"pharmacy","forms":["pharmacy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ef04ae2c9a2355e","term":"pharmacy","forms":["pharmacy","pharmacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥房；配藥處","explanation":"指出售或按處方配發藥物的地方，通常是人們買藥、取處方藥和諮詢用藥的場所。這個意義把“藥物”落實成一個可以前往的地點。","examples":[{"en":"I need to stop by the pharmacy after work.","zh":"我下班後得去一趟藥房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pharmacy filled my prescription this morning.","zh":"藥房今天早上配好了我的處方藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pharmacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60eefbbb8a897fae","term":"pharmacy","forms":["pharmacy","pharmacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥學","explanation":"指研究藥物及其製備、成分、作用和檢驗等內容的學科，是圍繞藥物展開的系統知識。這裡不再是一個地點，而是對藥物的專業研究。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to study pharmacy at university.","zh":"她決定在大學學習藥學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied pharmacy before opening her own dispensary.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pharmacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02195b8e989603e4dfb4","word":"phase","forms":["phase"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e1a73f986e28f05","term":"phase","forms":["phase","phases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"階段；一段過程","explanation":"指一個連續過程或迴圈中可以辨認的一段。一個專案、人生過程或變化過程都可以分成若干個 phase。","examples":[{"en":"The project has entered its final phase.","zh":"這個專案已經進入最後階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children often go through a phase of asking endless questions.","zh":"孩子常常會經歷一個不停提問的階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-384446340b1fc90a","term":"phase","forms":["phase","phases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外在表現；面貌","explanation":"指某個事物在特定時候顯現出來、可以被觀察到的一種面貌或狀態，尤其適用於同一事物有多種不同表現的情況。","examples":[{"en":"The artist captured the river in one of its quieter phases.","zh":"這位藝術家捕捉到了河流較為平靜的一種面貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibition explores different phases of urban life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fc677d1c2063b50","term":"phase","forms":["phase","phases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方面；層面","explanation":"指一個問題、經歷或事物可以從中觀察或理解的某個方面。這裡不一定有明確的時間順序，而是把複雜物件看成由多個方面組成。","examples":[{"en":"The problem has several phases that require different solutions.","zh":"這個問題有幾個方面，需要採用不同的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inquiry explored every phase of the dispute.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-faf587bfe020db38","term":"phase","forms":["phase","phases","phasing","phased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分階段引入或淘汰","explanation":"表示把某事物分步驟地引入或停止：phase in 是逐步採用，phase out 是逐步淘汰。這個義項直接來自“變化過程中的階段”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The company will phase in the new software over six months.","zh":"公司將在六個月內分階段引入這款新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city is phasing out diesel buses.","zh":"這座城市正在逐步淘汰柴油公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3754c68d4b05de4538e0","word":"phenomenon","forms":["phenomenon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-503c19a0756b82fd","term":"phenomenon","forms":["phenomenon","phenomena","phenomenons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可觀察的現象或事件","explanation":"指能夠透過感官觀察到，或作為事實發生的事物、事件和過程。它是最基本的用法，既可以說自然現象，也可以說社會現象或某個具體事件。","examples":[{"en":"The northern lights are a natural phenomenon.","zh":"北極光是一種自然現象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spread of remote work is a social phenomenon.","zh":"遠端工作的普及是一種社會現象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phenomenon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc24c53514b89601","term":"phenomenon","forms":["phenomenon","phenomena","phenomenons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可認識、可研究的現象","explanation":"強調某個現象或事件可以透過觀察、推理或科學研究來認識，不一定是肉眼直接看見的東西。電磁現象等抽象而可驗證的過程也屬於這一義。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying this unusual atmospheric phenomenon.","zh":"科學家正在研究這種不尋常的大氣現象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Memory is a complex psychological phenomenon.","zh":"記憶是一種複雜的心理現象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phenomenon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":4,"counts":{"112":3,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-542bce4a780c500a797c","word":"philosopher","forms":["philosopher"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a74083e1f6611e20","term":"philosopher","forms":["philosopher","philosophers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愛智慧的人","explanation":"這是這個詞最早的核心概念：把哲學家看成追求智慧、認真思考人生和世界的人。現代英語中，這個義項更多用於解釋詞源或強調哲學家的精神，而不是單獨作為最常用定義。","examples":[{"en":"A philosopher is traditionally described as a lover of wisdom.","zh":"傳統上，哲學家被描述為智慧的愛好者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At heart, the curious child was already a philosopher.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/philosopher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9e3747de78d8b5b","term":"philosopher","forms":["philosopher","philosophers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"哲學研究者或專家","explanation":"指從事哲學思考、研究或寫作，並對哲學問題有所貢獻的學者或專家。這是現代英語中最重要的專業義項。","examples":[{"en":"The philosopher wrote a book about freedom and responsibility.","zh":"這位哲學家寫了一本關於自由和責任的書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The philosopher devoted her career to ethics.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/philosopher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24335b433d1a5d01173e","word":"philosophical","forms":["philosophical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b82187cce492645","term":"philosophical","forms":["philosophical","more philosophical","most philosophical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"哲學的；與哲學有關的","explanation":"指屬於哲學領域，或涉及人生、知識、存在等根本問題的內容。它強調討論的主題和領域，而不只是說內容很有深度。","examples":[{"en":"The course raises philosophical questions about what makes a good life.","zh":"這門課程提出了關於什麼才是美好生活的哲學問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her book explores the philosophical meaning of freedom.","zh":"她的書探討了自由的哲學含義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/philosophical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3b5f792171a3fea","term":"philosophical","forms":["philosophical","more philosophical","most philosophical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"理性思考的；善於分析的","explanation":"形容人的頭腦、思維方式或處理問題的方法有條理，重視分析和反思，而不是隻憑衝動作判斷。","examples":[{"en":"She took a philosophical approach to the problem and considered every possibility.","zh":"她用理性的方式處理這個問題，把各種可能性都考慮了一遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a philosophical approach, examining each assumption carefully.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/philosophical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2331eb33ce2c3766148e","word":"philosophy","forms":["philosophy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a17681b306d3cd6f","term":"philosophy","forms":["philosophy","philosophies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"哲學學科","explanation":"研究存在、知識、推理、道德等根本問題的學科，主要透過概念分析和理性思考來追問答案。","examples":[{"en":"She studied philosophy at university.","zh":"她在大學學習哲學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Philosophy asks questions about knowledge, truth, and existence.","zh":"哲學探討知識、真理和存在等問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/philosophy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1769b0e72416763","term":"philosophy","forms":["philosophy","philosophies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某領域的理念","explanation":"指指導某個機構、活動或領域的一套基本看法：它說明這個領域應當依據什麼原則來運作。","examples":[{"en":"The school's philosophy of education emphasizes curiosity and independence.","zh":"這所學校的教育理念強調好奇心和獨立性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company's design philosophy favors repair over replacement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/philosophy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bd3142af446b3b98271","word":"photograph/photo","forms":["photograph","photo"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0382d57a35ddc5dc","term":"photograph","forms":["photograph","photographs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"照片","explanation":"指把現實中的人、物或場景用光影記錄下來的影象，可以印在膠片或紙上，也可以儲存在電子裝置中。","examples":[{"en":"I found an old photograph of my grandparents.","zh":"我找到了一張祖父母的老照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps a photograph of the beach on her desk.","zh":"她把一張海灘照片放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photograph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed530e79737c782f","term":"photograph","forms":["photograph","photographs","photographing","photographed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拍攝","explanation":"指用相機把人、物或場景的光影記錄下來，也就是給某人或某物拍照。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter photographed the damaged bridge.","zh":"記者拍攝了那座受損的橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stopped to photograph the sunset.","zh":"我們停下來拍攝日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photograph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9aa295f1a2913e91","term":"photo","forms":["photo","photos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"照片","explanation":"指用相機或其他裝置拍下並儲存下來的一張影象，可以是紙質照片，也可以是數字照片。","examples":[{"en":"I found an old photo of my grandparents.","zh":"我找到了一張祖父母的老照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you take a photo of us by the fountain?","zh":"你能給我們在噴泉旁拍張照片嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9dd511bd100843cc1cd","word":"photographer","forms":["photographer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ceb2a5723b2089c3","term":"photographer","forms":["photographer","photographers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攝影師；拍照片的人","explanation":"指用相機拍攝照片的人，最常見的是以攝影為工作的人，也可以泛指負責拍照的人。","examples":[{"en":"The photographer arrived early to take pictures of the wedding.","zh":"攝影師很早就到了，為婚禮拍照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to become a wildlife photographer.","zh":"她希望成為一名野生動物攝影師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photographer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bca1415d2372ddf753f","word":"photographic","forms":["photographic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-322d2dd28124f03e","term":"photographic","forms":["photographic","more photographic","most photographic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"攝影的；照片的","explanation":"表示與照片、攝影活動或攝影器材有關，重點是“用於攝影”或“屬於攝影領域”。","examples":[{"en":"The store sells photographic equipment and darkroom supplies.","zh":"這家商店出售攝影器材和暗房用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a course in photographic techniques.","zh":"她參加了一門攝影技術課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photographic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ec58d2c91915b8b","term":"photographic","forms":["photographic","more photographic","most photographic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其準確的；逼真的","explanation":"比喻某種記憶、描寫或記錄影照片一樣，細節清楚而且非常準確，未必真的涉及攝影。","examples":[{"en":"He has a photographic memory for faces and names.","zh":"他對人臉和姓名有著過目不忘般的記憶力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His photographic memory retained every number on the page.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photographic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25f3aeb51f1cc784d9d0","word":"photography","forms":["photography"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0093beb9802b9fb9","term":"photography","forms":["photography","photographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攝影藝術與技術","explanation":"指用相機等裝置記錄光線、製作影象的藝術和技術，包括傳統攝影和數碼攝影。這裡強調的是攝影這一領域、方法或活動本身，而不是某一張照片。","examples":[{"en":"She signed up for a weekend photography course.","zh":"她報名參加了一個週末攝影課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Digital photography has made taking pictures much easier.","zh":"數碼攝影讓拍照變得容易多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e89b2d50e8e17ca","term":"photography","forms":["photography","photographies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攝影職業","explanation":"指把攝影作為工作或職業，通常包含拍攝，有時也包括整理和沖印照片。它關注的是靠攝影謀生或從事攝影工作的這一職業方向。","examples":[{"en":"After college, he decided to make a career in photography.","zh":"大學畢業後，他決定以攝影為職業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Photography has been his livelihood for thirty years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/photography","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c00062f7ec9c80e2e77a","word":"phrase","forms":["phrase"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a9c172225ba64bc","term":"phrase","forms":["phrase","phrases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短語；簡短表達","explanation":"指一小段說出來或寫下來的表達，可以短到只有幾個詞，也可以是一句簡短的話。它強調的是一個相對獨立、可以被整體使用的表達單位。","examples":[{"en":"That phrase is easy to remember.","zh":"那句話很容易記住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote a short phrase on the card.","zh":"她在卡片上寫了一句簡短的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phrase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-067583fec7ad688f","term":"phrase","forms":["phrase","phrases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語法中的片語","explanation":"在語法中，phrase 是作為一個整體發揮作用的詞或片語，通常有一個核心詞，其他詞圍繞它補充說明。它可能出現在句子中，但本身不一定是完整句子。","examples":[{"en":"In this sentence, “the old house” is a noun phrase.","zh":"在這個句子中，“那座老房子”是一個名詞片語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The phrase “after lunch” tells us when it happened.","zh":"“午飯後”這個片語說明了事情發生的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phrase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44dcfec0f95d3dd9","term":"phrase","forms":["phrase","phrases","phrasing","phrased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"措辭表達","explanation":"指選擇並組織特定的詞語來表達一個想法、動作或情感。重點不是表達了什麼，而是用什麼方式說出來。","examples":[{"en":"Could you phrase that question more politely?","zh":"你能把那個問題說得更客氣一些嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He phrased his answer very carefully.","zh":"他非常謹慎地措辭回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phrase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b60d190e95e57693396","word":"physical","forms":["physical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-178fa574fafba76b","term":"physical","forms":["physical","more physical","most physical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"物質世界的；自然界的","explanation":"指由物質構成、能夠在現實世界中運動或被觀察到的事物，與思想、精神或抽象概念相對。","examples":[{"en":"The experiment tests how forces affect physical objects.","zh":"這個實驗檢驗力如何影響物質物體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The change exists only in the physical world, not in the computer model.","zh":"這種變化只存在於現實的物質世界中，不存在於計算機模型裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/physical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b24399c32706431a","term":"physical","forms":["physical","more physical","most physical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體的；肉體上的","explanation":"指與人的身體有關的感覺、狀態、影響或活動，而不是心理或情緒層面的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The medicine may cause some physical effects, such as dizziness.","zh":"這種藥可能會引起一些身體上的影響，例如頭暈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise improves both physical and mental health.","zh":"經常鍛鍊能改善身體和心理健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/physical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,115],"total":5,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1,"115":3}}},{"id":"ceec-da0e513b86418b1c956f","word":"physician","forms":["physician"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4acc96caa54e1c25","term":"physician","forms":["physician","physicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫生；醫師","explanation":"這是現代英語最重要的義項，指接受過人類醫學訓練、能夠診治病人的醫生；它可以泛指醫生，不限定具體專科。","examples":[{"en":"You should see a physician if the cough lasts more than two weeks.","zh":"如果咳嗽持續兩週以上，你應該去看醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The physician explained the test results in simple language.","zh":"醫生用簡單易懂的語言解釋了檢查結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/physician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-652f5e4fc04671bf","term":"physician","forms":["physician","physicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內科醫生","explanation":"這個義項把醫生的範圍縮窄到主要靠診斷、藥物和其他非手術方式治療的內科醫生，常用於和外科醫生作區別；它在較舊文字中尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"The physician adjusted his medication instead of recommending surgery.","zh":"這位內科醫生調整了他的藥物，而不是建議他做手術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her physician referred her to a heart specialist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/physician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5224be6f5ff96308d7af","word":"physicist","forms":["physicist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6cb8d0634e48d62","term":"physicist","forms":["physicist","physicists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物理學家","explanation":"專門研究物理學的人，研究物件可以包括力、物質、能量及其相互作用，通常指以此為職業或專業的人。","examples":[{"en":"The physicist explained how the new instrument measures tiny changes in temperature.","zh":"那位物理學家解釋了這種新儀器如何測量極其微小的溫度變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hopes to become a physicist and study the behavior of matter in extreme conditions.","zh":"她希望成為一名物理學家，研究極端條件下物質的行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/physicist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-742b27454919b5e1b2e8","word":"physics","forms":["physics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0a6f2d3c4165a04","term":"physics","forms":["physics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物理學","explanation":"研究空間、時間、物質和能量，以及它們如何相互作用的一門科學。它關注自然界中運動、力、熱、光等現象背後的普遍規律。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to study physics at university.","zh":"她決定在大學學習物理學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Modern physics helps us understand how tiny particles behave.","zh":"現代物理學幫助我們理解微小粒子如何運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/physics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f78485a82ce3a16","term":"physics","forms":["physics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物理機制","explanation":"指某種現象或系統中可以用物理學解釋的實際作用方式，強調事物為什麼會按照某種方式運動、碰撞或產生結果。","examples":[{"en":"The physics of the crash made it impossible for the driver to escape unharmed.","zh":"這場撞車事故中的物理作用使司機不可能毫髮無損地逃出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The game's physics makes falling objects bounce realistically.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/physics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-603cecc0fc313665196e","word":"pianist","forms":["pianist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a74979af269678b8","term":"pianist","forms":["pianist","pianists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋼琴演奏者","explanation":"指彈奏鋼琴的人，尤其是經過訓練、以演奏為職業，或因演奏水平較高而受到關注的人。這個詞不只表示“會彈鋼琴的人”，還常讓人聯想到正式演出或專業技能。","examples":[{"en":"The pianist played a beautiful piece at the concert.","zh":"那位鋼琴家在音樂會上演奏了一首優美的曲子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her daughter hopes to become a professional pianist.","zh":"她的女兒希望成為一名專業鋼琴家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pianist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d78e018e405ef26b7f7","word":"piano","forms":["piano"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de55874f792ec197","term":"piano","forms":["piano","pianos","pianoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋼琴","explanation":"一種用琴鍵控制琴槌敲擊琴絃的鍵盤樂器，既能彈奏旋律，也能同時演奏多個音。它的名稱還帶出了本詞“輕聲、弱力度”的音樂引申義。","examples":[{"en":"There is a piano in the corner of the living room.","zh":"客廳的角落裡有一架鋼琴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My daughter practices the piano every evening.","zh":"我女兒每天晚上練鋼琴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piano","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ce33c6c86e991f7b499","word":"pick","forms":["pick"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc1a747c142a0a00","term":"pick","forms":["pick","picks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鎬；鶴嘴鋤","explanation":"pick 是帶尖頭、用於挖土或鑿硬物的工具，和“用尖端把東西挑出來”這一記憶有關。","examples":[{"en":"He used a pick to break through the hard ground.","zh":"他用鎬鑿開堅硬的地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He loosened the hard soil with a pick.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0da02830bc1d80ec","term":"pick","forms":["pick","picks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇；選擇權","explanation":"pick 可指從多個選項中挑出一個的選擇，或進行這種選擇的權利；這正是“把一個挑出來”的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"You have the pick of the rooms on the second floor.","zh":"二樓的房間你可以任選。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take your pick from these three desserts.","zh":"這三種甜點你任選一種。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-faead1878e7181f1","term":"pick","forms":["pick","picks","picking","picked","pickest","pickedst","picketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用手指抓拉、摳取","explanation":"用手指或指甲把附著在某處的東西抓住並拉開、摳出來；記憶時可以想象把東西一點點“挑出來”。","examples":[{"en":"Don't pick at that scab.","zh":"別摳那塊痂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stop picking the loose threads from your sleeve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-840b5662b4770518","term":"pick","forms":["pick","picks","picking","picked","pickest","pickedst","picketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"選擇；挑選","explanation":"從多個可能的選項中把一個或一些“挑出來”，表示作出選擇。這是 pick 最常見的抽象用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"You can pick any seat you like.","zh":"你可以選任何你喜歡的座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She picked the blue dress for the party.","zh":"她為聚會選了那條藍色連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d08a4e630e4aa0d5cd8","word":"pickle","forms":["pickle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d502cf613bfeae92","term":"pickle","forms":["pickle","pickles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醃黃瓜；醃製食品","explanation":"指浸在鹽水或醋液中儲存的黃瓜，尤其是漢堡等食物旁常見的醃黃瓜；在部分英語地區也可泛指醃製食品。","examples":[{"en":"I added a pickle to my sandwich.","zh":"我在三明治里加了一根醃黃瓜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sandwich came with a crunchy dill pickle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd2ad5d05e82303d","term":"pickle","forms":["pickle","pickles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"困境；麻煩處境","explanation":"這是從“被醃泡、難以脫身”發展出的比喻義，表示某人陷入了棘手或危險的處境。","examples":[{"en":"We were in a pickle when the car broke down in the rain.","zh":"汽車在雨中拋錨時，我們陷入了麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Losing both keys left us in a pickle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afc82785f04e1196f515","word":"pickpocket","forms":["pickpocket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"pickpocket","forms":["pickpocket"],"pos":"n.","zh":"扒手","examples":[{"en":"A pickpocket took her wallet on the crowded train.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The police warned tourists to watch out for a pickpocket near the station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f64847ea58525bd846b","word":"pickup","forms":["pickup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b7a1fd2c2bea419","term":"pickup","forms":["pickup","pickups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拾音器","explanation":"指把聲音、振動等接收並轉成訊號的電子裝置，例如電吉他或唱片機上的拾音器；它正是把聲音“拾起來”。","examples":[{"en":"The guitarist replaced the pickup before the concert.","zh":"這名吉他手在音樂會前更換了拾音器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This record player has a very sensitive pickup.","zh":"這臺唱片機的拾音器非常靈敏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d58f4c115e80ef01","term":"pickup","forms":["pickup","pickups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮卡","explanation":"pickup truck 的省略說法，指帶開放式貨廂的小型卡車；它是用來把人或貨物接走、運走的車。","examples":[{"en":"They loaded the camping gear into the pickup.","zh":"他們把露營裝備裝進了皮卡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She drove her pickup to the farm.","zh":"她開著皮卡去了農場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e29a0dd25a7fc3f0","term":"pickup","forms":["pickup","pickups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接送或取走","explanation":"指把人或物收集起來並帶走，通常暗含用車接送或取貨；重點是把物件“接起來並帶走”。","examples":[{"en":"Your order will be ready for pickup at noon.","zh":"你的訂單中午可以取貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school arranged a pickup for the younger children.","zh":"學校為年幼的孩子安排了接送。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e878b5219508b0e1c9fe","word":"picnic","forms":["picnic"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b03d9c2ed2b6588","term":"picnic","forms":["picnic","picnics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"野餐活動","explanation":"指人們在公園、森林等戶外地方，帶上自己的食物和飲料，一邊吃一邊休閒的聚餐活動。","examples":[{"en":"We had a picnic by the lake on Sunday.","zh":"我們星期天在湖邊野餐了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let’s go on a picnic when the weather gets warmer.","zh":"天氣暖和些後我們去野餐吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/picnic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-276cf1efaa83b11b","term":"picnic","forms":["picnic","picnics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"野餐食物","explanation":"也可以指野餐時帶來並吃掉的那頓飯或那份食物，而不只是聚餐活動本身。","examples":[{"en":"I packed a picnic for the train journey.","zh":"我為火車旅程準備了一份便餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We packed a picnic of bread, cheese, and apples.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/picnic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2cea274d0bedc39ec4ab","word":"picture","forms":["picture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9e5cbaf60a1f1ef","term":"picture","forms":["picture","pictures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影象；圖畫","explanation":"指畫在紙、畫布等表面上的影象，也包括透過印刷、攝影等方式形成的視覺再現；它是“影象”這個核心意思的最寬泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"The child drew a picture of the family.","zh":"孩子畫了一幅全家人的畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a picture of a mountain on the wall.","zh":"牆上有一幅山的影象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/picture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ededa79f8c83e53","term":"picture","forms":["picture","pictures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"照片","explanation":"指用相機或手機拍下的照片。這是日常英語中picture非常常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Can you take a picture of us?","zh":"你能給我們拍張照片嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found an old picture of my grandparents.","zh":"我找到了一張祖父母的老照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/picture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef50c43427ea24c2","term":"picture","forms":["picture","pictures","picturing","pictured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想象；設想","explanation":"指在腦海中形成某個畫面，也就是把某種人、地方或未來情景想象出來。","examples":[{"en":"Picture yourself walking along a quiet beach.","zh":"想象一下自己走在安靜的海灘上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can picture him living in a small village.","zh":"我能想象出他住在一個小村莊裡的樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/picture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-558211ed72b2d6967037","word":"pie","forms":["pie"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b4665dc86851b93","term":"pie","forms":["pie","pies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"派","explanation":"一種有外皮、裡面包著餡的烘焙食物；餡可以是水果、肉、蔬菜等。它是pie最核心、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We baked an apple pie for the weekend.","zh":"我們為週末烤了一個蘋果派。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant serves hot meat pies.","zh":"這家餐館供應熱肉派。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c9b50cb2a20bd55","term":"pie","forms":["pie","pies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可分配的總量","explanation":"把資源或財富想成一整塊派，pie就可比喻一個需要由不同人或群體分配的總量。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone wants a larger share of the pie.","zh":"每個人都想分到更大的一份資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If the pie grows, more people can benefit.","zh":"如果總量擴大，更多人就能受益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34235a2c502e3919d3f0","word":"piece","forms":["piece"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0cad359404f59443","term":"piece","forms":["piece","pieces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一部分；一塊","explanation":"指從較大的整體中分離出來、仍能單獨辨認的一部分。這是 piece 最基本的“小片”概念。","examples":[{"en":"I found a piece of glass on the floor.","zh":"我在地板上發現了一塊玻璃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shared a piece of the story with us.","zh":"她把故事的一部分告訴了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piece","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d61eba219d82c8fc","term":"piece","forms":["piece","pieces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一件；一個單獨物品","explanation":"指同類物品中的一個單獨單位，重點不在它是整體的一部分，而在它本身是一件可計數的東西。","examples":[{"en":"This piece of equipment is very expensive.","zh":"這件裝置非常昂貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each piece of furniture bears the maker's mark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piece","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f65c8cbbec9fdcbe","term":"piece","forms":["piece","pieces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術作品","explanation":"指一件獨立完成的藝術創作，如繪畫、雕塑、文學作品或音樂作品；它是可以單獨欣賞的一“件”創作。","examples":[{"en":"The orchestra performed a beautiful piece by Mozart.","zh":"管弦樂團演奏了一首莫扎特的優美作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This piece of art explores the idea of memory.","zh":"這件藝術作品探討了記憶這一概念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piece","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26f956fcf1206cac","term":"piece","forms":["piece","pieces","piecing","pieced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拼合；拼湊","explanation":"把分散的線索、部件或資訊一塊塊接起來，形成一個完整的東西或結論；這是“小片重新組成整體”的直接動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The detective pieced together the clues.","zh":"偵探把這些線索拼湊了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are piecing together what happened.","zh":"我們正在逐步弄清發生了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piece","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d807432caec5f3e571c","word":"pier","forms":["pier"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb9a500140d4be09","term":"pier","forms":["pier","piers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水上碼頭平臺","explanation":"指從岸邊架到水面上、由樁支撐的平臺，船可以在那裡停靠，人也可以從那裡上下船或接近水面。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the sunset from the end of the pier.","zh":"我們在碼頭盡頭看日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fishing boat is waiting beside the pier.","zh":"那艘漁船正在碼頭旁等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbd3be06e9679eb2","term":"pier","forms":["pier","piers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橋墩","explanation":"指支撐橋樑兩段之間連線處的柱狀結構。這裡仍然保留了“支撐物”的核心概念，只是支撐物件從船和遊客變成了橋面。","examples":[{"en":"The old bridge rests on four stone piers.","zh":"這座老橋由四個石橋墩支撐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flood damaged one of the bridge piers.","zh":"洪水損壞了其中一個橋墩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0b8c9d84dd2b877e0b9","word":"pig","forms":["pig"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac7953f8070337d2","term":"pig","forms":["pig","pigs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豬","explanation":"指豬科的哺乳動物，尤其是人飼養的家豬；“豬”的核心畫面也由此產生了其他比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer keeps three pigs behind the barn.","zh":"農場主在穀倉後面養了三頭豬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A pig was sleeping in the shade.","zh":"一頭豬正在陰涼處睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-839df36b4df1d420","term":"pig","forms":["pig","pigs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豬肉","explanation":"指可食用的豬肉，也就是由“豬”這種動物產生的肉類。","examples":[{"en":"We bought some pig for the barbecue.","zh":"我們買了一些豬肉燒烤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soup is made with pig and vegetables.","zh":"這道湯是用豬肉和蔬菜做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a32028e0b413494","term":"pig","forms":["pig","pigs","pigging","pigged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"貪吃","explanation":"指像豬一樣毫無節制地吃東西，突出吃得很多、很貪。它直接來自“像豬一樣貪吃”的比喻畫面，通常帶有輕微到明顯的貶義。","examples":[{"en":"We pigged out on pizza after the game.","zh":"比賽結束後，我們大吃了一頓披薩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They were pigging on the free food at the party.","zh":"他們在聚會上對免費食物大吃特吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f79fd6cdc880e3914ac","word":"pigeon","forms":["pigeon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-794143b72970e090","term":"pigeon","forms":["pigeon","pigeons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鴿子","explanation":"pigeon是鴿科鳥類的統稱，日常最基本、最常見的意思就是“鴿子”。","examples":[{"en":"A pigeon landed on the balcony this morning.","zh":"今天早上一隻鴿子落在了陽臺上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were feeding pigeons in the square.","zh":"孩子們正在廣場上喂鴿子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pigeon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87553047fb0ea083","term":"pigeon","forms":["pigeon","pigeons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鴿肉","explanation":"在談論食物時，pigeon可以指這種鳥的肉，而不是活著的鳥。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves pigeon with roasted vegetables.","zh":"這家餐廳供應配烤蔬菜的鴿肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant serves roasted pigeon with wild mushrooms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pigeon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2eb8272d48d13634b6d7","word":"pile","forms":["pile"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3a642f913a21784","term":"pile","forms":["pile","piles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一堆","explanation":"pile 最核心的意思是許多東西堆在一起形成的一堆，正像記憶鉤子裡“堆起來的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"There was a pile of clothes on the chair.","zh":"椅子上有一堆衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We moved the pile of stones away from the gate.","zh":"我們把門口那堆石頭搬走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53528d77081f376a","term":"pile","forms":["pile","piles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"打入地下的樁","explanation":"pile 可以指打入土地或海床、用來支撐建築和橋樑的大木樁、鋼樁或混凝土樁；這正是記憶鉤子中“一根根豎著打入地下”的支撐物。","examples":[{"en":"The new pier rests on steel piles driven deep into the seabed.","zh":"新碼頭建在打入海床深處的鋼樁上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers drove a pile into the ground beside the road.","zh":"工人在路邊把一根樁打入了地下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73fa190bb259541f","term":"pile","forms":["pile","piles","piling","piled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堆放；積聚","explanation":"pile 作動詞時，表示把東西一件件堆起來，或使事物不斷積聚，正對應“堆起來的東西”這一記憶鉤子。","examples":[{"en":"They piled the boxes up beside the door.","zh":"他們把箱子堆在門旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unanswered emails began to pile up after the holiday.","zh":"假期過後，未回覆的郵件開始越積越多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1dd31cd072fdd30f9bbb","word":"pilgrim","forms":["pilgrim"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-768d55329cd4d2a2","term":"pilgrim","forms":["pilgrim","pilgrims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"朝聖者","explanation":"指為了拜訪具有宗教意義的地點而長途旅行的人；核心畫面就是揹著行囊向聖地走去。","examples":[{"en":"Every year, thousands of pilgrims travel to the shrine.","zh":"每年都有成千上萬名朝聖者前往這座聖地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pilgrims rested beside the road before dawn.","zh":"朝聖者們在黎明前到路邊休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilgrim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3127a4ce13edc51ba8d","word":"pill","forms":["pill"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-798436f036116468","term":"pill","forms":["pill","pills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥丸","explanation":"指通常做成小而圓或短柱狀、方便吞嚥的藥物。它把“可吞下的小團”這個基本形象具體化為藥丸。","examples":[{"en":"Take this pill with a full glass of water.","zh":"把這顆藥丸配一整杯水服下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I forgot to take my morning pills.","zh":"我忘了吃早上的藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca6e1f5f2a6603b9","term":"pill","forms":["pill","pills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口服避孕藥","explanation":"the pill 特指女性服用的口服避孕藥，是“藥丸”義在特定生活語境中的固定用法。","examples":[{"en":"She started taking the pill last year.","zh":"她去年開始服用口服避孕藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She discussed whether the pill would suit her needs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cc8e148c2a6760e","term":"pill","forms":["pill","pills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"難以接受的事","explanation":"把不愉快的事實想成必須吞下的苦藥，因此 pill 可指必須接受或忍受的冒犯、壞訊息或難題。","examples":[{"en":"Losing the contract was a bitter pill to swallow.","zh":"丟掉這份合同是個令人難以接受的打擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Accepting that his apprentice had surpassed him was a hard pill to swallow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14cc3e8d95ceb60a76c5","word":"pillar","forms":["pillar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a6407c1b7137cf6","term":"pillar","forms":["pillar","pillars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築柱子","explanation":"指建築物中粗大、豎直、用來承受或傳遞重量的柱子，是pillar最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The old hall has four stone pillars supporting the roof.","zh":"這座老大廳有四根支撐屋頂的石柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A marble pillar stands at the entrance to the temple.","zh":"寺廟入口處立著一根大理石柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pillar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6897a38209742887","term":"pillar","forms":["pillar","pillars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要支柱","explanation":"比喻某人或某事物像建築柱子一樣，為群體、機構或事業提供重要而穩定的支援。","examples":[{"en":"She has been a pillar of the local community for decades.","zh":"幾十年來，她一直是當地社群的重要支柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small businesses are a pillar of the national economy.","zh":"小企業是國民經濟的重要支柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pillar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f6000d4ef895fd961f13","word":"pillow","forms":["pillow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d693f76d8e0d5ffd","term":"pillow","forms":["pillow","pillows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"枕頭","explanation":"指睡覺時放在頭下、用來支撐頭部的柔軟墊子，是最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I always take my own pillow when I travel.","zh":"我旅行時總是帶上自己的枕頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rested her head on the pillow and fell asleep.","zh":"她把頭枕在枕頭上，很快睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pillow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07ae38b93d8054d84aac","word":"pilot","forms":["pilot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c613ca7aad9e1c15","term":"pilot","forms":["pilot","pilots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"試點；試行專案","explanation":"指在全面實施某個想法、產品或計劃前，先進行的小規模測試。它把“先替大家探路”的人變成了“先替正式方案探路”的專案。","examples":[{"en":"The company will run a pilot before introducing the service nationwide.","zh":"這家公司會先進行試點，然後再在全國推出這項服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school launched a pilot before expanding the program.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-450730eedaa9970e","term":"pilot","forms":["pilot","pilots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛行員","explanation":"指負責操控飛機的人，是現代英語中最常見的義項之一。這裡的“帶路”變成了直接控制飛機並把乘客帶到目的地。","examples":[{"en":"The pilot announced that we would land in ten minutes.","zh":"飛行員宣佈我們將在十分鐘後降落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pilot handled the rough landing calmly.","zh":"飛行員鎮定地處理了這次顛簸的降落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e050030ecf408c4","term":"pilot","forms":["pilot","pilots","piloting","piloted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"駕駛；操控","explanation":"指操控飛機或船隻，使其按預定方向前進。它把名詞“飛行員或舵手”的身份變成了實際執行“帶路和控制”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"She piloted the small plane through heavy clouds.","zh":"她駕駛小型飛機穿過了厚重的雲層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He piloted the small aircraft through the mountain pass.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73e3e4fa9af4a454","term":"pilot","forms":["pilot","pilots","piloting","piloted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"試行；試播","explanation":"指在正式推廣前先測試一個想法、產品、計劃或電視節目，以觀察效果並決定下一步。這是“先替大家探路”這一核心概念在抽象事物上的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital piloted a new appointment system last year.","zh":"這家醫院去年試行了一套新的預約系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The studio piloted the show with a younger audience.","zh":"製片公司先讓較年輕的觀眾試看了這部節目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pilot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bdce8283e0cc9ed037f","word":"pimple","forms":["pimple"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecb9632ba3c24b58","term":"pimple","forms":["pimple","pimples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痘痘；丘疹","explanation":"指皮膚表面出現的紅腫、隆起的小疙瘩，通常會疼，裡面可能有膿。它就像皮膚上突然冒出的一個小包，是這個詞最基本、最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I woke up with a pimple on my chin.","zh":"我醒來時發現下巴上長了一個痘痘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try not to touch that pimple.","zh":"儘量別碰那個痘痘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pimple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-64f46a7526a186d23465","word":"pin","forms":["pin"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30e4db3d15d58f84","term":"pin","forms":["pin","pins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"別針；針","explanation":"一種通常沒有針眼、一端尖銳而另一端有針頭的細金屬針，用來把布料、紙張等固定在一起；核心就是把東西固定在某處。","examples":[{"en":"She used a pin to hold the note to the board.","zh":"她用別針把便條固定在公告板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a pin in the sleeve of my jacket.","zh":"我夾克的袖子上彆著一枚別針。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce19eed0ac16aa66","term":"pin","forms":["pin","pins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"徽章","explanation":"一種通常較小、可別在衣服上的飾物，常為圓形並印有圖案、標誌或文字，可用於裝飾、表明身份或表達政治立場；也就是把某種標記固定在身上。","examples":[{"en":"He wore a campaign pin on his jacket.","zh":"他在夾克上戴了一枚競選徽章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each volunteer received a pin with the event logo.","zh":"每名志願者都拿到了一枚印有活動標誌的徽章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4cd392660f26a5a","term":"pin","forms":["pin","pins","pinning","pinned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用別針固定","explanation":"用別針、針或類似物把某件東西固定在某處，核心就是把東西“固定在這裡”。","examples":[{"en":"She pinned the notice to the wall.","zh":"她把通知用別針固定在牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I pinned the loose strap to the bag.","zh":"我把鬆開的帶子用別針固定在包上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f3e8d09c8995e28","term":"pin","forms":["pin","pins","pinning","pinned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按住使其不能動","explanation":"把人壓住或按倒，使對方暫時無法動彈；它仍然保留了“固定住”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The wrestler pinned his opponent to the mat.","zh":"那名摔跤手把對手按在墊子上，使他無法動彈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fallen beam pinned her legs until rescuers lifted it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46f9504a7a71e4b5b346","word":"pinch","forms":["pinch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e938dec4335fe11","term":"pinch","forms":["pinch","pinches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捏疼人的動作","explanation":"指用手指把人的皮肉捏在一起，使對方感到疼痛。","examples":[{"en":"The child gave his sister a playful pinch.","zh":"孩子淘氣地捏了妹妹一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sharp pinch on his arm made him yelp.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pinch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2506db826fc4f2d","term":"pinch","forms":["pinch","pinches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一小撮","explanation":"指拇指和食指尖之間能夾起的少量粉末或顆粒，尤其常用於烹飪。","examples":[{"en":"Add a pinch of pepper before serving.","zh":"上桌前加一小撮胡椒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add a pinch of cinnamon to the batter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pinch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c49aa6faa0a7ae5b","term":"pinch","forms":["pinch","pinches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"困境","explanation":"表示讓人難以脫身的尷尬或困難處境，常見的是經濟上的窘迫。就像身體被夾住一樣，人也被問題“夾”在其中。","examples":[{"en":"If you are in a pinch, I can lend you some money.","zh":"如果你手頭有困難，我可以借你一些錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In a pinch, we can use the spare bedroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pinch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-475a28d7b1a9d9ea","term":"pinch","forms":["pinch","pinches","pinching","pinched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"捏疼","explanation":"指用手指捏人的皮肉，使其疼痛。","examples":[{"en":"The children were pinching each other under the table.","zh":"孩子們在桌子底下互相捏對方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crab pinched my finger with its claw.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pinch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee3c1504b34cc1ad","term":"pinch","forms":["pinch","pinches","pinching","pinched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用手指夾住","explanation":"指用拇指和食指等手指把物體夾在中間，形成擠壓或拿取的動作。","examples":[{"en":"She pinched the corner of the paper between her fingers.","zh":"她用手指夾住紙的一角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pinch the fabric between your thumb and finger.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pinch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c0bda397784b2bc","term":"pinch","forms":["pinch","pinches","pinching","pinched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把兩邊擠到一起","explanation":"指兩個物體從兩側靠近，把中間的東西夾住或壓縮；這是“夾緊”概念從手指動作擴充套件到空間或結構。","examples":[{"en":"The cable was pinched between the door and the frame.","zh":"電纜被夾在門和門框之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pinch the pastry edges together to seal them.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pinch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2922372131239317837","word":"pine","forms":["pine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf1aa3eab0032cb0","term":"pine","forms":["pine","pines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"松樹","explanation":"指松屬的常綠針葉樹，也就是通常所說的松樹；這裡強調的是整棵樹。","examples":[{"en":"Several tall pines stood along the mountain road.","zh":"山路兩旁生長著幾棵高大的松樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The northern hillside is covered mainly in pine.","zh":"北面的山坡主要覆蓋著松林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-642b9932de8a01e0","term":"pine","forms":["pine","pines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"松木","explanation":"指松樹的木材，而不是樹本身；可以把它想成由松樹加工成的木料。","examples":[{"en":"The shelves are made of light-colored pine.","zh":"這些架子是用淺色松木製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shelves are made from inexpensive pine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0fef621727ff82a7d33","word":"pineapple","forms":["pineapple"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19e8ef338d32544e","term":"pineapple","forms":["pineapple","pineapples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"菠蘿植株","explanation":"指菠蘿這種熱帶植物：莖很粗，周圍長著一圈又長又尖、邊緣帶刺的葉子，果實從植株中長出。它是“菠蘿”這一名稱最基礎的植物義。","examples":[{"en":"Pineapple plants grow best in warm, sunny places.","zh":"菠蘿植株在溫暖、陽光充足的地方長得最好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pineapples need warmth and well-drained soil to grow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pineapple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d370c60146848c04","term":"pineapple","forms":["pineapple","pineapples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"菠蘿果實","explanation":"指這種植物結出的完整果實：外殼堅硬多刺，裡面有甜的白色或黃色果肉，中間有較硬的纖維芯。日常說“吃一個菠蘿”時，通常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a ripe pineapple at the market.","zh":"我們在市場買了一個熟透的菠蘿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut the pineapple into small pieces.","zh":"她把菠蘿切成了小塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pineapple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a67a41c8bc79d5da917b","word":"pink","forms":["pink"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37d8632d80aabf6b","term":"pink","forms":["pink","pinker","pinkest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粉紅色的","explanation":"表示顏色在紅色和白色之間，通常是較淺的紅色，是“粉紅色這一條主線”最基本的形容詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a pink dress to the party.","zh":"她穿了一條粉紅色的連衣裙去參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sky turned pink before sunset.","zh":"日落前天空變成了粉紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-248a4af8343afd4c","term":"pink","forms":["pink","pinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"粉紅色","explanation":"表示粉紅色這種顏色，是“粉紅色這一條主線”在名詞中的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"Pink is her favorite color.","zh":"粉紅色是她最喜歡的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The walls are painted a soft pink.","zh":"牆壁被刷成了柔和的粉紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84764246bdcc7a82","term":"pink","forms":["pink","pinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"石竹花","explanation":"指石竹屬中開粉紅色花的植物，有時也包括通常所說的康乃馨；這裡是由顏色聯想到花的具體名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"She planted pinks along the garden path.","zh":"她沿著花園小徑種了一排石竹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This pink has a delicate spicy scent.","zh":"這種石竹有一種淡淡的辛香味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b50c59260f8b95992b26","word":"pint","forms":["pint"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fd078760a6349fa","term":"pint","forms":["pint","pints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英國及英聯邦品脫","explanation":"在英國及許多采用英制傳統的地區，pint 是一種體積單位，約等於568毫升。它常用於牛奶、啤酒等液體，但不要把它和美國品脫混為一談。","examples":[{"en":"The recipe calls for a pint of milk.","zh":"這個食譜需要一品脫牛奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bottle holds two pints of water.","zh":"這個瓶子能裝兩品脫水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f715923c775d4559","term":"pint","forms":["pint","pints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美國品脫","explanation":"在美國，pint 通常指美國液量品脫，約等於473毫升，因此比英國品脫少一些。它同樣可以用來量牛奶、水或其他液體。","examples":[{"en":"Add one pint of water to the mixture.","zh":"往混合物中加入一品脫水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought a pint of ice cream.","zh":"我買了一品脫冰激凌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d3768aa924677985efce","word":"pioneer","forms":["pioneer"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3df999719166fd1","term":"pioneer","forms":["pioneer","pioneers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開路先行者","explanation":"指走在前面、在荒野或陌生環境中開闢道路，讓後來者能夠跟隨的人。這個具體形象是“先鋒、先驅”各種抽象用法的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The pioneers cleared a path through the forest.","zh":"先行者們清理出了一條穿過森林的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was a pioneer who opened the valley to new settlers.","zh":"她是一位為新定居者開闢這片山谷道路的先驅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pioneer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e110e22a97d1d603","term":"pioneer","forms":["pioneer","pioneers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領域先驅","explanation":"指在科學、藝術、商業或社會進步等領域最早探索、創新或取得突破的人，也可指這樣的機構或事物。重點不只是“很早”，而是為後來者樹立方向或創造條件。","examples":[{"en":"She became a pioneer in renewable-energy research.","zh":"她成了可再生能源研究領域的先驅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was a pioneer in underwater photography.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pioneer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76658fc041432115","term":"pioneer","forms":["pioneer","pioneers","pioneering","pioneered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"率先開創","explanation":"指第一個或最早的一批人去做成某事，併為後來者探索出道路；它把名詞“先驅”的開路形象變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"The team pioneered a safer way to store solar power.","zh":"這支團隊率先開創了一種更安全的太陽能儲存方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic pioneered new treatments for childhood diseases.","zh":"這家診所率先開創了治療兒童疾病的新方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pioneer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4008294739162e8f0119","word":"pipe","forms":["pipe"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ec1de14ae3b68fa","term":"pipe","forms":["pipe","pipes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管樂器","explanation":"pipe可以指靠空氣透過中空管體發聲的管樂器，記住“空氣透過中空通道，變成聲音”即可。它既可以泛指這類樂器，也可以指一組管樂器。","examples":[{"en":"She learned to play the pipes when she was a child.","zh":"她小時候學會了吹奏管樂器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sound of the pipes filled the valley.","zh":"管樂器的聲音充滿了山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b5f94e784ba137f","term":"pipe","forms":["pipe","pipes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管子；管道","explanation":"pipe是中空的管子或管道，液體、氣體或其他東西可以沿著它流動或輸送。這正是“中空的通道”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The workers replaced the old water pipe under the road.","zh":"工人更換了道路下面的舊水管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water flows through the pipe into the tank.","zh":"水透過管道流入水箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17f7c3408b0ff938","term":"pipe","forms":["pipe","pipes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"菸斗","explanation":"pipe也指用來抽菸的菸斗：菸草放在一端，煙霧透過中空的管狀部分進入口中。這仍然符合“中空的通道”這一記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"His grandfather smoked a pipe beside the fireplace.","zh":"他的祖父在壁爐旁抽菸鬥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave him a wooden pipe as a gift.","zh":"她送給他一隻木製菸斗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84316a9d070a63f8","term":"pipe","forms":["pipe","pipes","piping","piped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吹奏管樂器","explanation":"指吹奏長笛、風笛等管樂器，使空氣透過管體形成聲音；這個意義直接對應“讓聲音沿著中空通道出來”。","examples":[{"en":"She piped a lively tune on her flute.","zh":"她用長笛吹奏了一段歡快的曲子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The musician piped as the dancers entered the hall.","zh":"舞者走進大廳時，樂手吹奏了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23bf0d244a4cb62c85fc","word":"pipeline","forms":["pipeline"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b41d194fe85e31c","term":"pipeline","forms":["pipeline","pipelines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輸送物質的管道","explanation":"最基本的意思是由管子組成的輸送線路，讓水、天然氣或石油等從一個地方流到另一個地方。它就是“讓東西沿固定路線流動的管道”這一核心影象。","examples":[{"en":"The new gas pipeline will supply several towns.","zh":"這條新的天然氣管道將為幾個城鎮供氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The oil pipeline runs from the coast to the refinery.","zh":"這條輸油管道從海岸通到煉油廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pipeline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-021df2ab773b5755","term":"pipeline","forms":["pipeline","pipelines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資訊按順序傳遞的通道","explanation":"這裡的管道不一定是實體的，而是讓資訊依次經過各個環節的通道；前面的資訊先出來，後面的資訊隨後處理。計算機圖形處理和資料處理常用這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"The graphics pipeline converts the data into a final image.","zh":"圖形處理管線把資料轉換成最終影象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A problem in the pipeline slowed down the application.","zh":"處理管線中的一個問題拖慢了應用程式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pipeline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03bdd14ef87c5b28bc15","word":"pirate","forms":["pirate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c414f0a2c53e6d63","term":"pirate","forms":["pirate","pirates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海盜；海上劫掠者","explanation":"指在海上搶劫船隻、貨物，有時也襲擊港口城鎮的犯罪者。這是“未經允許奪走別人東西”這一核心畫面最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The pirates boarded the cargo ship at night.","zh":"海盜在夜裡登上了那艘貨船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pirates boarded the merchant ship before sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pirate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d793291fd84e7fcc","term":"pirate","forms":["pirate","pirates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盜版者；非法複製者","explanation":"指未經許可複製受保護的書籍、音樂、電影、軟體等內容的人。和海盜一樣，他們也是在未經允許的情況下奪取他人的成果，只是物件從貨物變成了作品或智慧財產權。","examples":[{"en":"The publisher sued a pirate who was selling unauthorized copies of the novel.","zh":"出版社起訴了一名出售這部小說盜版的盜版者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Software pirates distributed unauthorized copies of the program.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pirate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37ee4203dbbd319c","term":"pirate","forms":["pirate","pirates","pirating","pirated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"劫掠；劫持船隻","explanation":"指像海盜一樣搶劫船隻、貨物或其他海上目標。它把名詞“海盜”的核心行為直接變成動詞。","examples":[{"en":"The gang pirated the tanker and took its cargo.","zh":"那幫人劫持了油輪並搶走了船上的貨物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The raiders pirated merchant ships along the coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pirate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2d165dff04ba22532c7","word":"pit","forms":["pit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f07fcbb5d7ed2860","term":"pit","forms":["pit","pits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地上的坑","explanation":"指地面上挖出或自然形成的坑，是“凹進去的核心位置”最直接的畫面。大小可以從小坑到很深的坑。","examples":[{"en":"The children found an old pit behind the barn.","zh":"孩子們在穀倉後面發現了一箇舊坑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to step into that pit.","zh":"小心別踩進那個坑裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbc091e64a31fb98","term":"pit","forms":["pit","pits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賽車維修區","explanation":"指賽車場邊供賽車停下加油、換胎和維修的區域；車輛從賽道暫時進入這裡，就像回到一個用於處理問題的“凹進去的核心位置”。","examples":[{"en":"The driver went into the pit for new tires.","zh":"車手進維修區換了新輪胎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fast pit stop put our team back in the lead.","zh":"一次快速的進站讓我們車隊重新取得領先。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c685c039527d87f","term":"pit","forms":["pit","pits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水果硬核","explanation":"指桃、櫻桃、李子等水果果肉中堅硬的種核，是藏在果肉裡的“核心”。這正對應記憶鉤子裡水果內部凹進去的核心位置。","examples":[{"en":"Please remove the pit before slicing the peach.","zh":"請先把桃子的核去掉，再切片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I nearly broke a tooth on the cherry pit.","zh":"我差點被櫻桃核硌壞了牙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4502846f2b0708ba711f","word":"pitch","forms":["pitch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa880178c40be45e","term":"pitch","forms":["pitch","pitches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推銷說辭","explanation":"指為了讓別人購買、接受或支援某物而組織的一段說法；這是把想法“推向聽眾”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a clear pitch for the new recycling program.","zh":"她清楚地介紹並推銷了新的回收計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I listened to his pitch, but I still need time to decide.","zh":"我聽了他的推銷說辭，但還需要時間決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pitch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47f8b328bae2e9aa","term":"pitch","forms":["pitch","pitches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音高","explanation":"指人聽到的聲音高低，取決於聲音振動的頻率；可以把它記成把聲音定到某個高低位置。","examples":[{"en":"The singer raised the pitch of the final note.","zh":"歌手提高了最後一個音的音高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The whistle had such a high pitch that the dog ran over immediately.","zh":"口哨的音調非常高，狗馬上跑了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pitch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd759fc149a078aa","term":"pitch","forms":["pitch","pitches","pitching","pitched","pight"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投擲","explanation":"表示把某物用力投出去，是“把某物定到另一個位置”的最基本動作義。","examples":[{"en":"She pitched the ball across the yard.","zh":"她把球投過了院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pitched a stone into the river.","zh":"他把一塊石頭投進了河裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pitch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9eb325d0d132de4d548","word":"pitcher","forms":["pitcher"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ccf7cbfd16f38bf","term":"pitcher","forms":["pitcher","pitchers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棒球投手","explanation":"在棒球或壘球中，負責把球投給擊球員的球員。","examples":[{"en":"The pitcher threw a fastball past the batter.","zh":"投手投出一個快速球，騙過了擊球員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their pitcher struck out three players in a row.","zh":"他們的投手連續三振了三名球員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pitcher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfde59951b9bfdbf","term":"pitcher","forms":["pitcher","pitchers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水壺；大口壺","explanation":"一種有把手和壺嘴、用來盛水或其他液體的寬口深容器，常放在餐桌上供人倒水或飲料。","examples":[{"en":"Please put a pitcher of cold water on the table.","zh":"請在桌上放一壺涼水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She poured lemonade from the pitcher into our glasses.","zh":"她把壺裡的檸檬水倒進了我們的杯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pitcher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c0706c0a8dcb82cc8c7","word":"pity","forms":["pity"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-595a6276b4518ff2","term":"pity","forms":["pity","pities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同情","explanation":"指看到某人或某物遭受不幸、痛苦時產生的同情心，也就是心裡因對方受苦而變得柔軟。","examples":[{"en":"I felt pity for the injured dog and took it to a vet.","zh":"我同情那隻受傷的狗，就把它送去了獸醫那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had pity on the old man waiting in the rain.","zh":"她同情那個在雨中等待的老人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77c9d658d79eb822","term":"pity","forms":["pity","pities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人遺憾的事","explanation":"指一件讓人惋惜、覺得不應該這樣發生的事情；這裡不是同情某個人，而是對結果感到“真可惜”。","examples":[{"en":"It's a pity that you can't stay for dinner.","zh":"你不能留下來吃晚飯，真可惜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It's a pity you couldn't attend the wedding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4964d571ad839e8b","term":"pity","forms":["pity","pities","pitying","pitied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"同情","explanation":"指因為某人或某物遭遇不幸而同情它，彷彿把名詞 pity 所表示的柔軟感情直接施加到物件上。","examples":[{"en":"You have to pity him after everything he has lost.","zh":"他失去了一切，真讓人同情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't pity people who refuse every offer of help.","zh":"我不同情那些拒絕一切幫助的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ed1515819dec61fd361","word":"pizza","forms":["pizza"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-338cbb5bedb27557","term":"pizza","forms":["pizza","pizzas","pizze"],"pos":"noun","zh":"披薩這種食物","explanation":"泛指這種烤制的義大利麵餅，包括外層面餅以及鋪在上面的醬汁、乳酪和其他配料；重點是這一類食物，而不是某一張具體的成品。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered pizza for dinner.","zh":"我們點了披薩當晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ate pizza while watching the match.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pizza","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7876b48bc456263d","term":"pizza","forms":["pizza","pizzas","pizze"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一張披薩","explanation":"指烤好的一整張具體 pizza，可以把它看成一個完整的圓形成品來數；例如一張被吃完或切開分食的 pizza。","examples":[{"en":"He ate a whole pizza by himself.","zh":"他一個人吃掉了一整張披薩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ordered a pizza to share.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pizza","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81df63580cc9ff1550c9","word":"place","forms":["place"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-763daf6457bb24e0","term":"place","forms":["place","places"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地方；場所","explanation":"place 最基本的意思是某個區域中的地方或場所，可以是具體地點，也可以只是泛指某處。","examples":[{"en":"This is a quiet place to read.","zh":"這是一個適合閱讀的安靜地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to find a place to park.","zh":"我們得找個地方停車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/place","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fcd770ca15688244","term":"place","forms":["place","places"],"pos":"noun","zh":"位置","explanation":"place 可以表示物體、人或事件在空間中的具體位置；重點不是一片區域，而是“在哪裡”。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the keys back in the same place.","zh":"請把鑰匙放回原來的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I know the place where we first met.","zh":"我知道我們第一次見面的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/place","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94c9ad4c6270a543","term":"place","forms":["place","places","placing","placed","placest","placedst","placeth","-","yplaced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放置；安放","explanation":"place 作動詞就是把某人或某物放到指定位置，正是“給它找一個 place”。","examples":[{"en":"She placed the vase on the table.","zh":"她把花瓶放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Place the documents in this folder.","zh":"把這些檔案放進這個資料夾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/place","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1480fb125459cbca6cff","word":"placement","forms":["placement"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f7c421b9204d6ca","term":"placement","forms":["placement","placements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"放置；安排到位","explanation":"指把某人或某物放到合適位置的行為，或這種放置已經形成的狀態；重點是“落位、安排好”這一過程或結果。","examples":[{"en":"The careful placement of the lamp made the room feel much brighter.","zh":"把燈仔細放在合適的位置後，房間顯得明亮多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The placement of the chairs allowed everyone to see the stage.","zh":"椅子的擺放讓每個人都能看見舞臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/placement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88c99c519c35ee4a","term":"placement","forms":["placement","placements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"就業安置；工作安排","explanation":"指把求職者與合適的工作崗位匹配起來的安排，也可以指一次成功的錄用安置。","examples":[{"en":"The recruitment agency charges a fee for each successful placement.","zh":"這家招聘機構會為每次成功的就業安置收取費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency specializes in the placement of nursing staff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/placement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2af3dec4b269fc6ffb45","word":"plague","forms":["plague"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb670572622b423c","term":"plague","forms":["plague","plagues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴重傳染病","explanation":"通常指鼠疫，尤其是由鼠疫桿菌引起的嚴重傳染病；在歷史語境中也常指造成大規模死亡的那場疾病。","examples":[{"en":"The plague spread quickly through the crowded city.","zh":"鼠疫迅速在擁擠的城市中傳播開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people fled the town for fear of the plague.","zh":"許多人因為害怕鼠疫而逃離了這座城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plague","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58ab14a7971602bc","term":"plague","forms":["plague","plagues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大範圍災禍","explanation":"引申指席捲許多人或一個地區的嚴重災難、禍患或破壞性事物，重點是它造成的廣泛痛苦。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers saw the invading insects as a plague.","zh":"村民們把入侵的昆蟲看作一場災禍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plague of corruption damaged the country's institutions.","zh":"腐敗這一禍患破壞了這個國家的制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plague","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a116c9ed46d6207734a4","word":"plain","forms":["plain"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43e0d4456bfd7d46","term":"plain","forms":["plain","plainer","plainest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樸素的；無裝飾的","explanation":"由“沒有多餘裝飾”發展而來，表示簡單、不花哨，也可指未經加工或沒有特別變化的東西。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a plain black dress to the interview.","zh":"她穿了一條樸素的黑裙子去面試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I prefer plain yogurt without sugar.","zh":"我更喜歡不加糖的原味酸奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22ca7e554cade11d","term":"plain","forms":["plain","plainer","plainest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明顯的；顯而易見的","explanation":"因為沒有東西遮擋視線，所以很容易看清；plain 在這裡表示事實或答案十分明顯。","examples":[{"en":"It was plain that he had forgotten the appointment.","zh":"很明顯，他忘了這次約會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was plain that he had misunderstood the question.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-725c3df7891a0a8c","term":"plain","forms":["plain","plainer","plainest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直率的；坦白的","explanation":"說話不加遮掩、不繞彎，直接把真實想法說出來，因此表示坦率或直截了當。","examples":[{"en":"Let me be plain: we cannot afford another delay.","zh":"我直說吧：我們經不起再次拖延了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let me be plain: this behavior must stop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-861aed25be7e671b","term":"plain","forms":["plain","plains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平原","explanation":"指地勢相對低平、樹木較少的大片陸地，常給人開闊草地的畫面；這是名詞 plain 最重要的用法。","examples":[{"en":"A small village stood alone on the wide plain.","zh":"一座小村莊孤零零地坐落在遼闊的平原上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmers grow wheat across the plain.","zh":"農民們在這片平原上種植小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-64879f7d6b960a019097","word":"plan","forms":["plan"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c2d551891587772","term":"plan","forms":["plan","plans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"設計圖","explanation":"指用線條、符號和必要的技術細節表示建築、機器等如何設計的圖紙；它像一份把複雜物件簡化後呈現的藍圖。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer showed us the plans for the new bridge.","zh":"工程師給我們看了新橋的設計圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plans include details of the electrical system.","zh":"這套設計圖包含電氣系統的詳細資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5700bb6d33714285","term":"plan","forms":["plan","plans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動計劃","explanation":"指為達到某個目標而安排的一組相互關聯的行動；它把“想達到什麼”進一步變成“準備怎麼做”。","examples":[{"en":"We need a clear plan to finish the project on time.","zh":"我們需要一個明確的計劃，才能按時完成專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her plan worked better than we expected.","zh":"她的計劃執行得比我們預期的更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0fdda09739c302b","term":"plan","forms":["plan","plans","planning","planned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"制定計劃","explanation":"指為某項任務或目標安排步驟、時間和資源，形成一套可執行的計劃。","examples":[{"en":"They planned the event months in advance.","zh":"他們提前幾個月就為這次活動制定了計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are planning a short trip for the holidays.","zh":"我們正在計劃一次假期短途旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbea4ab04ac796e6","term":"plan","forms":["plan","plans","planning","planned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打算","explanation":"指已經有意向去做某事，但不一定已經把所有細節安排好；它把腦中的目標指向將來的行動。","examples":[{"en":"I plan to call her after work.","zh":"我打算下班後給她打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They planned to move next year, but changed their minds.","zh":"他們原打算明年搬家，但後來改變了主意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb5815fe5c3c9d7bf15d","word":"planet","forms":["planet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14ca7e923b4ddb70","term":"planet","forms":["planet","planets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行星","explanation":"現代科學中，planet 是足夠大的天體，能在自身引力作用下大致形成球狀，直接圍繞恆星執行，並在自己的軌道區域佔據主導地位。太陽系中的八大行星——包括地球——都屬於這一類；這就是最需要掌握的基本義。","examples":[{"en":"Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun.","zh":"火星是距離太陽第四近的行星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are searching for planets that might support life.","zh":"科學家正在尋找可能支援生命存在的行星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/planet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d64565c00f045312","term":"planet","forms":["planet","planets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地球","explanation":"在帶有 this、our 或 the 等限定詞的語境中，planet 可以不泛指某顆行星，而是把地球看作人類共同生活的這個世界。這一用法仍然保留“行星”本義，只是把所指物件限定成了地球。","examples":[{"en":"We all share this planet.","zh":"我們共同生活在這個星球上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We must reduce the waste we leave on the planet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/planet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96044d9734b6044127de","word":"plant","forms":["plant"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6de49c55310bef7b","term":"plant","forms":["plant","plants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物","explanation":"指不是動物的植物，通常是較小的草本植物，而不是樹。這個意義體現了“讓東西紮根並生長”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She put the new plant by the window.","zh":"她把新植物放在窗邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These plants need plenty of sunlight.","zh":"這些植物需要充足的陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0978d1987a62e32a","term":"plant","forms":["plant","plants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工廠；生產設施","explanation":"指固定的工廠或工業、機構設施，即能讓生產活動在那裡紮根並發揮作用的場所。","examples":[{"en":"The company opened a new production plant in Mexico.","zh":"這家公司在墨西哥開設了一座新的生產工廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plant employs more than five hundred people.","zh":"這家工廠僱用了五百多人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9af96ab0b21aef18","term":"plant","forms":["plant","plants","planting","planted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"種植","explanation":"把種子、幼苗或植物放進土壤等基質中，使它能夠生長；也就是把東西放下並讓它紮根。","examples":[{"en":"We planted tomatoes and herbs in the garden this spring.","zh":"今年春天我們在花園裡種了西紅柿和香草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children planted a small tree near the school.","zh":"孩子們在學校附近種了一棵小樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d7c58fbc2ab8a52","term":"plant","forms":["plant","plants","planting","planted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暗中安插；栽贓","explanation":"把人或物偷偷放到某處，通常是為了誤導別人、製造假象或讓某人看起來有罪；這仍然是“把東西放下讓它在那裡發揮作用”，但帶有欺騙目的。","examples":[{"en":"The police found a gun in the room, but the lawyer said someone had planted it there.","zh":"警方在房間裡發現了一把槍，但律師說那是有人栽在那裡陷害他的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporter suspected that the company had planted an employee in the meeting.","zh":"記者懷疑那家公司在會議中安插了一名員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4708b6a9e852767bb871","word":"plantation","forms":["plantation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f040291ee5cca85","term":"plantation","forms":["plantation","plantations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大型種植農場","explanation":"指面積很大的農業用地，通常集中種植某種作物，並可能包括所有者和工人的住房。它比一般的農場更突出規模以及成片、商業化經營的特點。","examples":[{"en":"The family runs a coffee plantation in the highlands.","zh":"這家人在高地經營一座咖啡種植園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Smoke from the burning plantations covered the nearby villages.","zh":"燃燒種植園產生的煙霧籠罩了附近的村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plantation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2877cb6c62ffa79","term":"plantation","forms":["plantation","plantations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成片種植的樹木","explanation":"指為了商業用途或美化莊園而成片栽種樹木的區域；重點是樹木被有計劃地種在一大片地方。","examples":[{"en":"A row of young trees marked the edge of the plantation.","zh":"一排小樹標出了這片成片林地的邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A pine plantation covered the hillside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plantation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72f7c894ad6c4ce2ef54","word":"plastic","forms":["plastic"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dd3ca2e03a2ee70","term":"plastic","forms":["plastic","more plastic","most plastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可塑的；易成形的","explanation":"指材料柔軟或可加工，能夠被彎曲、壓制或塑造成新的形狀；記住“可以被塑出來”這個基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The artist chose a plastic clay that was easy to shape.","zh":"這位藝術家選了一種容易塑形的可塑黏土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Warm clay remains plastic enough to shape by hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf0f8e94f2dec785","term":"plastic","forms":["plastic","more plastic","most plastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"塑膠制的","explanation":"指物品由塑膠這種可加工成形的合成材料製成，是“可塑材料”這個核心畫面最常見的具體結果。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the leftovers in a plastic container.","zh":"請把剩菜放進塑膠容器裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Store the screws in a plastic box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c924e8a81c8f6b6a","term":"plastic","forms":["plastic","more plastic","most plastic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"虛假做作的","explanation":"形容一個人、笑容或風格表面光滑漂亮，卻顯得不真誠、膚淺或刻意迎合；彷彿被塑造成了一個完美外殼。","examples":[{"en":"Her plastic smile disappeared as soon as the cameras turned away.","zh":"攝像機一轉開，她那做作的笑容立刻消失了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The host's plastic friendliness made the guests feel strangely unwelcome.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-366af63e47eb7ef1","term":"plastic","forms":["plastic","plastics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"塑膠","explanation":"指由合成聚合物製成的固體材料，可以加工成許多不同形狀；它就是“能被塑形的材料”這一核心畫面的具體化。","examples":[{"en":"This bottle is made of recycled plastic.","zh":"這個瓶子是用回收塑膠製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heat softened the plastic around the damaged socket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plastic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114,115],"total":9,"counts":{"112":6,"114":2,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-3b56c3520006aaeb038c","word":"plate","forms":["plate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a61c54d1a6db22a","term":"plate","forms":["plate","plates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盤子","explanation":"指略帶弧度、用來盛放或食用食物的盤子，是“扁平的板片”這一核心意象最常見的生活用法。","examples":[{"en":"She put the salad on a clean plate.","zh":"她把沙拉放在一個乾淨的盤子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pass me a plate.","zh":"請把一個盤子遞給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d885ad0462145260","term":"plate","forms":["plate","plates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"扁平板片","explanation":"指厚度均勻的扁平物體，可以是金屬、玻璃、矽等材料製成的板或片，直接體現“扁平的板片”這一核心意象。","examples":[{"en":"The technician replaced the cracked metal plate.","zh":"技術員更換了那塊有裂紋的金屬板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The solar panel contains a thin silicon plate.","zh":"這塊太陽能電池板裡有一片薄薄的矽片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4344c8affdd78f05","term":"plate","forms":["plate","plates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車輛號牌","explanation":"指車輛上的牌照或號牌，通常用複數表示整套車輛號牌；它也是“扁平板片”在車輛上的具體用途。","examples":[{"en":"The police recorded the car’s license plate.","zh":"警方記錄了那輛車的車牌號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She checked the plates before buying the used car.","zh":"她在買那輛二手車前核對了車牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d294fcce0cc885878430","word":"platform","forms":["platform"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-936bd727e0f8298e","term":"platform","forms":["platform","platforms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舞臺；講臺","explanation":"供人站在上面演講、表演或進行公開活動的架高平面；它保留了“站在高處讓別人看見”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The band walked onto the platform and began to play.","zh":"樂隊走上舞臺，開始演奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke from the platform about the need for change.","zh":"她在講臺上談到了改變的必要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42d4b98e4477f51d","term":"platform","forms":["platform","platforms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表達意見的機會","explanation":"引申為讓某個人、群體或觀點被公眾聽見的機會或渠道，就像站上舞臺發言一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper gave young writers a platform for their ideas.","zh":"這份報紙為年輕作者表達觀點提供了平臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Community radio provides a platform for voices rarely heard elsewhere.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d66b4e614fc5127","term":"platform","forms":["platform","platforms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車站站臺","explanation":"車站旁供乘客上下車的架高區域，是“架高平面”這一核心形象在交通中的直接應用。","examples":[{"en":"The train for Oxford leaves from platform 4.","zh":"開往牛津的火車從四號站臺出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train arrives at platform four.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9434ca67e8cefd79","term":"platform","forms":["platform","platforms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路平臺","explanation":"提供線上服務、連線使用者或促成交易的系統，就像一個讓各種活動站得住、進行得下去的數字場所。","examples":[{"en":"The company sells its products through an online platform.","zh":"這家公司透過一個網路平臺銷售產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The platform connects freelance designers with small businesses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aba4cc9b8af82df5d4ef","word":"play","forms":["play"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cfe752e2b80b2b0","term":"play","forms":["play","plays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玩耍；娛樂活動","explanation":"指為了娛樂而進行的活動，尤其常指兒童的玩耍；這裡強調讓活動自然地動起來，而不是為了完成實際任務。","examples":[{"en":"Children learn important social skills through play.","zh":"孩子們透過玩耍學習重要的社交技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher gave the children time for free play.","zh":"老師給孩子們留出了自由玩耍的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/play","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-afef3e8167131935","term":"play","forms":["play","plays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戲劇作品","explanation":"指供演員扮演角色、說出對白並在舞臺上演出的文學作品。","examples":[{"en":"The class read a short play by Shakespeare.","zh":"全班讀了一部莎士比亞的短劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This play is divided into three acts.","zh":"這部戲劇分為三幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/play","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9062dd8071a3b05d","term":"play","forms":["play","plays","playing","played"],"pos":"verb","zh":"玩耍；娛樂","explanation":"指為了娛樂而進行活動，讓活動動起來並從中獲得樂趣，常用於兒童或人們輕鬆消遣。","examples":[{"en":"The children played in the park until sunset.","zh":"孩子們在公園裡一直玩到日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I like to play with my dog after work.","zh":"我喜歡下班後和我的狗一起玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/play","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ea33f5847059a92","term":"play","forms":["play","plays","playing","played"],"pos":"verb","zh":"演奏；表演","explanation":"指人透過樂器、歌唱或表演來讓音樂或舞臺活動動起來。","examples":[{"en":"My sister plays the violin in the school orchestra.","zh":"我姐姐在學校管弦樂團裡演奏小提琴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He will play the lead role in the new production.","zh":"他將在新劇中飾演主角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/play","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cdb59355f3ba293977fc","word":"player","forms":["player"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-122c8cc6bcb4a29a","term":"player","forms":["player","players"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參加遊戲或活動的人","explanation":"player指實際參加遊戲、運動、演奏等活動的人，也就是“玩或進行某事的人”。這是最基本、最容易擴充套件的意思。","examples":[{"en":"He is an avid Minecraft player.","zh":"他是個非常熱衷於《我的世界》的玩家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every player must wear a numbered shirt.","zh":"每位參賽者都必須穿有號碼的上衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/player","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-233dad6ac05494a7","term":"player","forms":["player","players"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參與者；有影響力的一方","explanation":"在競爭、政治、商業或其他事務中，player可以泛指參與其中的人、團體或機構。這裡不一定真的有“玩遊戲”，而是把整個局面比作一場需要各方加入的活動。","examples":[{"en":"The company has become a major player in renewable energy.","zh":"這家公司已經成為可再生能源領域的重要參與者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small independent players are challenging the established airline giants.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/player","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e600bda8b7b82249ddf2","word":"playful","forms":["playful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75a0ff28a28d5524","term":"playful","forms":["playful","playfuller","more playful","playfullest","most playful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愛玩而活潑的","explanation":"形容人或動物喜歡玩耍、精力活潑，常讓人聯想到孩子或小貓一類輕快、好動的樣子。這個詞不一定批評對方調皮，重點是有玩心、富有活力。","examples":[{"en":"The playful puppy kept chasing its own tail.","zh":"那隻活潑的小狗不停地追著自己的尾巴跑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a playful side that comes out when she is with children.","zh":"她和孩子們在一起時，會表現出愛玩的一面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/playful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a718fcfc6541460","term":"playful","forms":["playful","playfuller","more playful","playfullest","most playful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"逗趣活潑的","explanation":"形容人的言行帶有幽默、打趣或輕快的意味，讓氣氛不那麼嚴肅。它也可以表示一個人性格活潑、喜歡開玩笑，而不只是喜歡身體上的玩耍。","examples":[{"en":"He gave me a playful smile and hid the keys behind his back.","zh":"他衝我頑皮地笑了笑，把鑰匙藏到了身後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her playful joke made everyone relax.","zh":"她那句逗趣的玩笑讓大家都放鬆了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/playful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f3cc87f78b21d53dcccd","word":"playground","forms":["playground"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9792ca7cf5d313da","term":"playground","forms":["playground","playgrounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兒童遊樂場","explanation":"指供兒童玩耍的較大戶外場地，通常設有秋千、滑梯等遊樂設施。它就是“可以玩耍的場地”這一核心形象的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children ran to the playground after lunch.","zh":"孩子們午飯後跑去了遊樂場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a new playground behind our apartment building.","zh":"我們公寓樓後面有一個新的遊樂場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/playground","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65dc834bc700b558","term":"playground","forms":["playground","playgrounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自由施展的領域","explanation":"比喻某個地方、行業或領域讓某人或某個組織擁有很大自由，可以按自己的意願行動和發揮。這裡保留了“在場地裡盡情玩耍”的畫面，但“玩”已經變成了自由施展本領。","examples":[{"en":"For ambitious designers, the city has become a playground for new ideas.","zh":"對有抱負的設計師來說，這座城市已經成了新創意自由施展的天地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laboratory became a playground for her scientific imagination.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/playground","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7827e8eb2cb3b95f4d0f","word":"playwright","forms":["playwright"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7d924ebaf793e08","term":"playwright","forms":["playwright","playwrights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劇作家","explanation":"專門創作供舞臺演出的戲劇文字、人物和情節的人；重點在於寫戲劇，而不是負責表演或導演。","examples":[{"en":"The playwright spent three years writing her new drama.","zh":"這位劇作家花了三年時間創作她的新戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The playwright of the award-winning play joined the discussion.","zh":"那部獲獎戲劇的劇作家參加了討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/playwright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27a95700beed98227393","word":"plea","forms":["plea"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aef2e502819f8d64","term":"plea","forms":["plea","pleas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懇求；呼籲","explanation":"指帶有迫切感的請求、呼籲或哀求，像是把自己的需要鄭重地擺到別人面前，希望對方回應或幫助。","examples":[{"en":"Her plea for help finally reached the right people.","zh":"她的求助呼籲終於傳到了能提供幫助的人那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He made a heartfelt plea to his neighbors to stay calm.","zh":"他真誠地懇求鄰居們保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-381177386fb92d73","term":"plea","forms":["plea","pleas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藉口；辯解理由","explanation":"指一個人用來解釋自己為什麼這樣做、為什麼沒有做到某事的理由；這個理由有時是真實的，有時也可能只是藉口。","examples":[{"en":"Lack of time is a poor plea for missing the deadline.","zh":"沒有時間並不是錯過截止日期的好藉口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He refused to help on the plea of ill health.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da4f52812732aafd1d01","word":"plead","forms":["plead"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5aee283cc311628b","term":"plead","forms":["plead","pleads","pleading","pleaded","pled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"答辯；提出抗辯","explanation":"在法庭或類似正式爭辯中，plead 表示提出自己的答辯、主張或法律立場，尤其常見於承認或否認有罪。它體現的是“站出來為自己說話”。","examples":[{"en":"The defendant pleaded not guilty to the charge.","zh":"被告對這項指控提出無罪答辯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pleaded her case before the judge.","zh":"她在法官面前為自己的案件進行辯護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a26af7b7346053e2","term":"plead","forms":["plead","pleads","pleading","pleaded","pled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懇求；苦苦哀求","explanation":"表示帶著強烈感情請求別人答應或不要做某事，往往暗示說話者很著急、害怕或無助。這是“為自己爭取回應”在日常人際關係中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She pleaded with him not to leave.","zh":"她苦苦哀求他不要離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I pleaded for one more chance.","zh":"我懇求再給我一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plead","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-54c0bcab0e7334379ea4","word":"pleasant","forms":["pleasant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0b4a6d65d2da693","term":"pleasant","forms":["pleasant","more pleasant","pleasanter","most pleasant","pleasantest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人愉快的；舒服的","explanation":"指某人、某事或某種經歷讓人感到輕鬆、舒服或開心。它可以描述天氣、環境、活動、談話，也可以描述一個待人友好、相處愉快的人。","examples":[{"en":"The café has a pleasant atmosphere and good coffee.","zh":"這家咖啡館氛圍舒適，咖啡也很好喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a pleasant walk along the river.","zh":"我們沿著河邊散了個愉快的步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pleasant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56ccc4dcfc96534b06fc","word":"please","forms":["please"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27c17319e7efbe9d","term":"please","forms":["please","pleases","pleasing","pleased","pleas'd","pleasest","pleasedst","pleaseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使滿意；使高興","explanation":"某件事、某種表現或某個結果讓某人感到合意、滿意或高興。這裡的畫面是“事情順了某人的心”，所以主語通常是帶來這種感受的人或事，而不是感受到它的人。","examples":[{"en":"The simple meal pleased everyone at the table.","zh":"這頓簡單的飯讓桌邊的每個人都很滿意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new arrangement pleased everyone in the office.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/please","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3680b9500db7e1de","term":"please","forms":["please","pleases","pleasing","pleased","pleas'd","pleasest","pleasedst","pleaseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隨自己的意願；想怎樣就怎樣","explanation":"表示按照自己的願望或判斷去做，不必服從別人的安排。它把“合自己的心意”推進了一步：不只是事情讓自己滿意，而是自己決定什麼才合心意。","examples":[{"en":"You may arrange the chairs as you please.","zh":"你可以按自己的意願擺放椅子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You may arrange the furniture however you please.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/please","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1a583b3f5beb4d29b97","word":"pleasure","forms":["pleasure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a617647c9e67317","term":"pleasure","forms":["pleasure","pleasures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"愉快；滿足；享受","explanation":"指人在某件事中感到的快樂、滿足或享受，是 pleasure 最基本的抽象意思。","examples":[{"en":"She takes great pleasure in cooking for her friends.","zh":"她很享受為朋友做飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He remembered his childhood with pleasure.","zh":"他愉快地回憶起自己的童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pleasure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c9dc17f78e382c1","term":"pleasure","forms":["pleasure","pleasures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樂事；令人愉快的人或事","explanation":"指讓人感到愉快的人、事情或經歷，例如一次愉快的會面或一項令人享受的活動。","examples":[{"en":"It was a pleasure to meet your family.","zh":"見到你的家人很愉快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Walking through the orchard was a simple pleasure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pleasure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9dd7dd2209298bf505aa","word":"pledge","forms":["pledge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28cdb14519e3cf6b","term":"pledge","forms":["pledge","pledges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鄭重承諾","explanation":"pledge 是鄭重、公開地承諾要做某事，通常比普通的答應更正式，也更強調責任。","examples":[{"en":"The company made a pledge to reduce its plastic waste.","zh":"這家公司鄭重承諾要減少塑膠垃圾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kept her pledge to support the local school.","zh":"她履行了支援當地學校的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e179e2a58629495","term":"pledge","forms":["pledge","pledges","pledging","pledged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鄭重承諾做某事","explanation":"pledge 作動詞時表示鄭重保證自己會做某事，常帶有公開表態或承擔責任的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor pledged to improve public transportation.","zh":"市長鄭重承諾要改善公共交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students pledged allegiance to the country.","zh":"學生們宣誓效忠這個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pledge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-289e6d75558b9003e9fe","word":"plentiful","forms":["plentiful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3712a264e69b1fc4","term":"plentiful","forms":["plentiful","plentifuller","plentifuler","more plentiful","plentifullest","plentifulest","most plentiful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量充足的","explanation":"表示某種東西數量很多，或供應量足夠，重點是“有得多、用不完或不容易缺”。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water is plentiful in this region.","zh":"這個地區淡水資源充足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There were plentiful opportunities for young artists.","zh":"年輕藝術家有很多機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plentiful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c686ba8f289f679","term":"plentiful","forms":["plentiful","plentifuller","plentifuler","more plentiful","plentifullest","plentifulest","most plentiful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"產出豐富的","explanation":"形容某個來源、植物或事物能持續提供大量某種東西；它不只是“自身很多”，還強調“能帶來很多”。","examples":[{"en":"The old tree is a plentiful source of apples every autumn.","zh":"這棵老樹每年秋天都能結出大量蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plentiful harvest filled every storage shed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plentiful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82b5f7770097973f2962","word":"plenty","forms":["plenty"],"officialPos":"pron./n./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b1b20ee8b988556","term":"plenty","forms":["plenty","plenties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"充足；富足","explanation":"指數量多到有餘的狀態，尤其可表示生活資料、資源或機會充足；核心畫面就是容器裝滿並且還有剩餘。","examples":[{"en":"There is plenty of food for everyone.","zh":"食物很充足，足夠每個人享用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the harvest, the village had plenty.","zh":"收穫之後，這個村莊物資很充足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plenty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-def12af6d26c760e","term":"plenty","forms":["plenty"],"pos":"pron","zh":"綽綽有餘；足夠多","explanation":"不帶後面的名詞時，plenty 表示“足夠多的東西或數量”，含有完全夠用、還有剩餘的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Don't worry—we have plenty for the whole week.","zh":"別擔心，我們的東西足夠整個星期用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You have plenty of time, so there is no need to hurry.","zh":"你有充足的時間，所以不用著急。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plenty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-0f3850ab36e9d43a8615","word":"plot","forms":["plot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fe025c10d32bafbb","term":"plot","forms":["plot","plots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事情節","explanation":"故事中的事件按照一定因果關係展開，整體形成一條情節線；它就像把許多事件畫在同一張圖上並連起來。","examples":[{"en":"The plot of the novel becomes more complicated after the discovery.","zh":"這部小說的情節在這個發現之後變得更加複雜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I enjoyed the film, but I found the plot hard to follow.","zh":"我喜歡這部電影，但覺得它的情節不太容易看懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61ba3d9fe806c9bf","term":"plot","forms":["plot","plots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地塊；小塊土地","explanation":"被劃定出來、用於建築或種植的一小片土地，就是一塊 plot；它保留了“圈出一塊範圍”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a small plot of land for a vegetable garden.","zh":"他們買了一小塊地來種菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They bought a small plot beside the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73b03ede23a915a1","term":"plot","forms":["plot","plots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰謀；密謀","explanation":"把一個秘密目標和一連序列動提前圈定出來，尤其是為了違法或可疑目的，就成了 plot，即陰謀或密謀。","examples":[{"en":"Police uncovered a plot to attack the airport.","zh":"警方發現了一個襲擊機場的陰謀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plot against the mayor was stopped in time.","zh":"針對市長的陰謀及時被制止了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bdd1afb025c9a185","term":"plot","forms":["plot","plots","plotting","plotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"密謀；策劃壞事","explanation":"plot 作動詞時，是在暗中把行動步驟和目標安排好，通常用於犯罪、傷害或其他可疑事情。","examples":[{"en":"The two men plotted to steal the painting.","zh":"那兩個人密謀偷走那幅畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was accused of plotting against her employer.","zh":"她被指控密謀對付自己的僱主。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b6f81c65c19a25c3b8a","word":"plow","forms":["plow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"plow","forms":["plow"],"pos":"n./v.","zh":"犁；犁田","examples":[{"en":"The farmer used a plow to prepare the field.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"They will plow this land before planting wheat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-0daf0c9ca37fec6e1d5a","word":"plug","forms":["plug"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b95026174fc075f7","term":"plug","forms":["plug","plugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電插頭","explanation":"插入插座、用來連線電路的帶插腳裝置，是 plug 最常見的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Make sure the plug is fully inserted into the socket.","zh":"確保插頭完全插入插座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charger plug is loose, so the phone keeps disconnecting.","zh":"充電器插頭鬆了，所以手機總是斷開連線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dfa924fad7b8b43d","term":"plug","forms":["plug","plugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"塞子；堵孔物","explanation":"用來堵住或填滿孔洞的木頭、金屬或其他物件；浴缸塞就是典型例子。","examples":[{"en":"Pull out the plug when the sink is full.","zh":"水槽裝滿水後，把塞子拔出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A rubber plug is blocking the hole in the tank.","zh":"一個橡膠塞堵住了水箱上的孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3c1c481471841c5","term":"plug","forms":["plug","plugs","plugging","plugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堵住；塞住","explanation":"把塞子或其他材料塞進孔、縫隙或漏洞，使其不再漏出或通行；這是從“塞子”名詞義直接發展來的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"They plugged the leak with a piece of rubber.","zh":"他們用一塊橡膠堵住了漏洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers plugged every crack before the tank was tested.","zh":"工人們在測試水箱前堵住了每一道裂縫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4a0d56df130a04c","term":"plug","forms":["plug","plugs","plugging","plugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"宣傳；推銷","explanation":"像把一個資訊不斷塞進談話中一樣，指反覆提到並推廣某個產品、服務、作品或想法。","examples":[{"en":"The presenter kept plugging her new podcast during the show.","zh":"主持人在節目中一直宣傳她的新播客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He plugged the local café in his travel video.","zh":"他在旅行影片中為那家本地咖啡館作了宣傳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0467255695084cc12ffe","word":"plum","forms":["plum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e10c3eb322e4eef9","term":"plum","forms":["plum","plums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"李子；李樹","explanation":"指結李子的果樹，也指這種樹結出的圓形核果；日常語境中通常首先理解為水果。","examples":[{"en":"We picked a basket of ripe plums from the tree.","zh":"我們從樹上摘了一籃熟李子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plum tree grows beside the kitchen window.","zh":"廚房窗邊長著一棵李樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9bcac1d88852c83d","term":"plum","forms":["plum","plums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"優厚職位；難得機會","explanation":"由李子的珍貴引申而來，指報酬高、工作輕鬆、待遇好或很令人羨慕的職位、任務和機會。","examples":[{"en":"The board gave her the plum of leading the new research team.","zh":"董事會把領導新研究團隊這一份令人羨慕的差事交給了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ambassador's post was the plum everyone wanted.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2cb46f8b213d3a1ec17","word":"plumber","forms":["plumber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f675652eba8d4e80","term":"plumber","forms":["plumber","plumbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水管工","explanation":"指安裝、接通和修理供水、燃氣或排水管道及相關裝置的工人，這是最常見、最應該先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We called a plumber to fix the leaking sink.","zh":"我們叫了水管工來修漏水的水槽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plumber replaced the old pipes in our bathroom.","zh":"水管工更換了我們浴室裡的舊管道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plumber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81dab76012c8817cb4a0","word":"plunge","forms":["plunge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0aa7a11c15009ed","term":"plunge","forms":["plunge","plunges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"浸入動作","explanation":"指把身體或物體猛然浸入水中或其他液體的動作，重點是“衝進去並沒入其中”這一過程。","examples":[{"en":"The plunge into the cold water woke me up.","zh":"浸入冷水的那一下讓我清醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took a refreshing plunge after the long, dusty walk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plunge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c7375bca5851c5a4","term":"plunge","forms":["plunge","plunges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛然跳入","explanation":"指一次跳水、躍入或猛衝進去的動作，畫面是人一下子進入水中或某個空間。","examples":[{"en":"She took a plunge into the lake before breakfast.","zh":"她早餐前跳進了湖裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One bold plunge carried him into the icy pool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plunge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fb93c37811e1781","term":"plunge","forms":["plunge","plunges","plunging","plunged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……浸入","explanation":"指把身體或物體用力壓入水、液體或其他可穿入的物質中，讓它沒入其中。","examples":[{"en":"He plunged his hands into the warm water.","zh":"他把雙手浸入溫水中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Plunge the vegetables into ice water after boiling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plunge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2ddb1b6ec353361","term":"plunge","forms":["plunge","plunges","plunging","plunged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跳入或衝入","explanation":"指人自己猛然跳入水或液體中，畫面是身體一下子衝進並部分或全部沒入其中。","examples":[{"en":"The children plunged into the pool as soon as it opened.","zh":"泳池一開放，孩子們就衝進了水裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog plunged into the lake after its ball.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plunge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9ec051ebf61a71a","term":"plunge","forms":["plunge","plunges","plunging","plunged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"陷入某種狀態","explanation":"表示人或事物突然、深度地陷入債務、困難、悲傷等狀態，是“衝進去”的比喻用法。","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected repairs plunged us into debt.","zh":"突如其來的維修費用讓我們陷入了債務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The announcement plunged the market into uncertainty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plunge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61d58cbe5bad3042630f","word":"plural","forms":["plural"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa3fed1acdf6eb38","term":"plural","forms":["plural","more plural","most plural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不止一個的","explanation":"表示某種事物不是單一的，而是包含兩個或更多個；重點在“有多個組成部分或例項”。","examples":[{"en":"The notion of culture is plural and changing.","zh":"文化這一概念不是單一固定的，而是多元且不斷變化的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee represents plural interests within the community.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca173b1402d42d30","term":"plural","forms":["plural","more plural","most plural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"複數的","explanation":"在語法中，表示一個詞或形式指向不止一個人或事物，而不是單數；有些語言還會另設表示兩個的“雙數”。","examples":[{"en":"English nouns usually have singular and plural forms.","zh":"英語名詞通常有單數形式和複數形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These two words have the same plural form.","zh":"這兩個詞的複數形式相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f51a32ec8ed0905","term":"plural","forms":["plural","plurals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"複數","explanation":"指表示不止一個的語法數量範疇；在英語中，它通常用於兩個或更多的人或事物。","examples":[{"en":"In this sentence, the verb is in the plural.","zh":"在這個句子中，動詞用了複數形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some languages have a dual as well as a plural.","zh":"有些語言除了複數，還有雙數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b91b65a0f3d7e18f","term":"plural","forms":["plural","plurals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"複數形式","explanation":"指一個詞在表示不止一個人或事物時所採用的具體形式，例如某些詞會改變詞尾，某些詞會完全改變形式。","examples":[{"en":"The plural of “child” is “children”.","zh":"child 的複數形式是 children。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plural of mouse is mice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-383ef36928344f56ffe8","word":"plus","forms":["plus"],"officialPos":"prep./n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f2f8cd0b8ac5f9b","term":"plus","forms":["plus"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正的；正數的","explanation":"在數學中，plus 表示數值大於零，或表示正號；它和 minus（負的、減號）相對。","examples":[{"en":"The answer is plus four.","zh":"答案是正四。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A plus sign is written before the number.","zh":"數字前寫一個正號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d22893afdc2c908f","term":"plus","forms":["plus"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有利的；加分的","explanation":"形容某人或某事能帶來額外好處，是整體評價中的優勢或加分項。","examples":[{"en":"Her experience is a big plus for the team.","zh":"她的經驗對團隊來說是很大的加分項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Previous teaching experience would be a plus factor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a910e72ace9e96f7","term":"plus","forms":["plus","pluses","plusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正數；正號所表示的量","explanation":"作為名詞，plus 可以指一個正的數量，或泛指“加號這一邊”的數值。","examples":[{"en":"The pluses outweigh the drawbacks.","zh":"有利之處多於不利之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two minuses multiplied together produce a plus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91776b1463e6a30e","term":"plus","forms":["plus","pluses","plusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"優點；有利條件","explanation":"指加入某個計劃、團隊或情況後帶來的實際好處，也就是一個“加分項”。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm manner is a real plus in this job.","zh":"她沉著的作風是做這份工作的一個真正優點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A short commute is a definite plus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e12f5a8969f0ce9c","term":"plus","forms":["plus"],"pos":"prep","zh":"加；加上","explanation":"連線兩個數或量，表示把前者和後者相加。","examples":[{"en":"Three plus five equals eight.","zh":"三加五等於八。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The total is ten dollars plus tax.","zh":"總價是十美元，另加稅費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3bc539e25eca2329d5f0","word":"pm/p.m.","forms":["p.m."],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba9df995e9cd5b5d","term":"p.m.","forms":["p.m."],"pos":"adv","zh":"下午；晚上","explanation":"在十二小時制中，表示從中午十二點到午夜之前的這半天。例如 3 p.m. 是下午三點，8 p.m. 是晚上八點。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting starts at 2 p.m.","zh":"會議下午兩點開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I usually get home around 6 p.m.","zh":"我通常下午六點左右到家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/p.m.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72a8df6694d5ca048cef","word":"pneumonia","forms":["pneumonia"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fbdd34e294d2bf2f","term":"pneumonia","forms":["pneumonia","pneumonias","pneumoniæ","pneumoniae"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肺炎","explanation":"肺炎是肺部發炎的疾病，通常由病毒、細菌或其他能引起感染的微生物造成；肺部像吸水的海綿一樣受到影響，患者可能出現咳嗽、發熱或呼吸困難。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor said that she had pneumonia and needed plenty of rest.","zh":"醫生說她得了肺炎，需要充分休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pneumonia can make it difficult to breathe.","zh":"肺炎可能使人呼吸困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pneumonia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62f5d588fd39c2bbb6b7","word":"pocket","forms":["pocket"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d81df57274d968d6","term":"pocket","forms":["pocket","pockets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣服口袋","explanation":"縫在衣服或其他物品上的小袋，用來裝鑰匙、零錢等小物品，是“裝東西的小袋或封閉空間”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I found my keys in the inside pocket of my coat.","zh":"我在外套的內口袋裡找到了鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She slipped the receipt into her pocket.","zh":"她把收據塞進了口袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pocket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a02363a1f5c0594","term":"pocket","forms":["pocket","pockets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人財力","explanation":"指一個人手頭能支配的錢，彷彿資源被裝在自己的口袋裡；因此“自己掏錢”就是從自己的口袋裡出錢。","examples":[{"en":"We paid for the repairs out of our own pockets.","zh":"修理費是我們自己掏的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The price increase will hurt families with shallow pockets most.","zh":"漲價對手頭不寬裕的家庭影響最大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pocket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc3a42ceadbadc1a","term":"pocket","forms":["pocket","pockets","pocketing","pocketed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放進口袋","explanation":"把某件東西放進衣服或其他物品上的口袋裡，也就是把它放進一個用來裝東西的小袋或封閉空間。","examples":[{"en":"She pocketed her phone before getting on the bus.","zh":"她上公交車前把手機放進了口袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She quietly pocketed the spare key so nobody would notice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pocket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6449cf6fe83d25e33848","word":"poem","forms":["poem"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63641c6f76f5e22d","term":"poem","forms":["poem","poems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一首詩","explanation":"指按照詩歌形式寫成的文學作品，通常有詩行、節奏、韻律或有意安排的語言結構；內容也可以是科學、社會或日常生活主題。","examples":[{"en":"She read a short poem about the changing seasons.","zh":"她朗讀了一首描寫四季變化的短詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students wrote poems about the stars.","zh":"學生們寫了關於星星的詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb31affc6c2f6fd4","term":"poem","forms":["poem","poems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詩歌作品；詩歌","explanation":"泛指屬於詩歌傳統的文字作品，重點不在某一首詩的具體形式，而在它作為詩歌創作或詩歌作品的性質。","examples":[{"en":"The collection includes poems by writers from several generations.","zh":"這部詩集收錄了幾代作家的詩作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She read a short poem at the ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ccc804f5546ab8ea960","word":"poet","forms":["poet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1389ffbdb94c0bf5","term":"poet","forms":["poet","poets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寫詩的人","explanation":"指創作詩歌的人，可以是以寫詩為職業的人，也可以只是創作詩歌的普通人。這個意義體現了“用語言創造世界”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The young poet published her first collection last year.","zh":"這位年輕詩人去年出版了她的第一部詩集。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became a poet after years of writing in secret.","zh":"他偷偷寫作多年後成為了一名詩人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ae14c7e56146cf9","term":"poet","forms":["poet","poets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"富有詩意的人","explanation":"指一個人不一定真的寫詩，卻有豐富的創造力或浪漫想象，能以新穎、詩意的方式看待事物。這是從“創造世界的詩人”擴充套件出來的比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"She is a poet at heart, finding beauty in ordinary streets.","zh":"她骨子裡是個詩人，總能在普通的街道中發現美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener was a poet with flowers, arranging colors like verses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b314f58f5f506fd28379","word":"poetic","forms":["poetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e68a3481b1ff1d64","term":"poetic","forms":["poetic","more poetic","most poetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"詩歌的；與詩歌有關的","explanation":"指直接屬於詩歌或用於詩歌的事物，例如詩歌的形式、語言、節奏和格律。這是“poetic”最直接、最字面的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The poem uses a simple poetic form.","zh":"這首詩採用了一種簡單的詩歌形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied the poetic traditions of medieval Persia.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-764db883f788349d","term":"poetic","forms":["poetic","more poetic","most poetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富有詩意的；浪漫而有想象力的","explanation":"形容人、語言、故事或想法像詩人創作的一樣浪漫、富有想象力，不一定真的屬於詩歌。它把“詩歌的”這個核心概念擴大到了生活和表達方式。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a poetic description of the old city.","zh":"她用富有詩意的語言描寫了那座古城。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His explanation was poetic but not very clear.","zh":"他的解釋很有詩意，但不太清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81c320ebd209ddddf590","word":"poetry","forms":["poetry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f71db37604b00e41","term":"poetry","forms":["poetry","poetries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詩歌文學","explanation":"指用詩行、節奏、聲音和富有表現力的語言創作的文學作品總體，不一定只強調押韻，也可以強調語言形式和情感表達。","examples":[{"en":"She began reading poetry in high school.","zh":"她從高中開始讀詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people write poetry to express feelings that are hard to say directly.","zh":"許多人寫詩，是為了表達那些難以直接說出口的感情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poetry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-50248f65c4a782d7","term":"poetry","forms":["poetry","poetries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詩意；藝術感染力","explanation":"指某種藝術形式或事物具有像詩一樣的節奏、畫面感和情感感染力；它不一定是文字作品，卻能讓人感到美和共鳴。","examples":[{"en":"Watching the skater move across the ice was poetry in motion.","zh":"看那名滑冰運動員在冰面上移動，簡直像一首流動的詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In her hands, the old recipe became poetry.","zh":"經過她的手，那道老食譜做出來竟有了詩意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poetry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-251fecd592e56e6c4a95","word":"point","forms":["point"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd4eb21d1697d79a","term":"point","forms":["point","points"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小點；標記","explanation":"point 可以是紙上、螢幕上或影象中的一個小點，也可以是用來標示位置的記號；“尖尖的一點”就是這個最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"There was a bright point of light in the distance.","zh":"遠處有一個明亮的光點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put a point on the map to show where we started.","zh":"在地圖上標出一個點，表示我們出發的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/point","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f1eb85b44263e3e","term":"point","forms":["point","points"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細節；要點","explanation":"point 可以是一個較大的話題中可單獨討論的細節、方面或論點；許多這樣的“尖尖的一點”合起來，就是事情的要點。","examples":[{"en":"She explained the main points of the agreement clearly.","zh":"她清楚地解釋了協議的要點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are several important points to discuss before we decide.","zh":"我們決定之前還有幾個重要問題要討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/point","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52694e6a15494d0a","term":"point","forms":["point","points"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖端；尖頭","explanation":"point 可以是刀、針、箭等物體最尖的末端；它正是“尖尖的一點”這一記憶形象最直接的實物用法。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful with the point of the needle.","zh":"小心針尖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pencil has a very sharp point.","zh":"這支鉛筆的筆尖非常尖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/point","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e69dfb63df7c70c6","term":"point","forms":["point","points","pointing","pointed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用手指指出","explanation":"把“尖尖的一點”伸向某人或某物，用來顯示它在哪裡或引起別人注意；通常就是“指著”。","examples":[{"en":"She pointed at the sign above the door.","zh":"她指著門上方的標牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't point at people while you are talking.","zh":"說話時不要用手指著別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/point","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5743abddddfa08c1e3a9","word":"poison","forms":["poison"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4432da9973f71523","term":"poison","forms":["poison","poisons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毒物；毒藥","explanation":"指被攝入後會使生物生病、受傷或死亡的物質。它可以是某一種具體毒物，也可以泛指毒性物質。","examples":[{"en":"The label warns that the liquid contains poison.","zh":"標籤警告說這種液體含有毒物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog was poisoned after eating the bait.","zh":"那條狗吃了誘餌後中毒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bee288c2e46d1717","term":"poison","forms":["poison","poisons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有害因素","explanation":"比喻指任何會損害人、事物或環境的因素，例如惡意流言、仇恨或汙染；它不一定是實際的化學毒物。","examples":[{"en":"Constant gossip can be poison to a friendship.","zh":"沒完沒了的流言會毒害友誼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Corruption proved a slow poison within the organization.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7be3e92f376500d0","term":"poison","forms":["poison","poisons","poisoning","poisoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……下毒","explanation":"指使用毒物使某人或某動物死亡、癱瘓或嚴重受傷，是名詞“毒物”轉成的直接動作。","examples":[{"en":"Someone poisoned the guard's food.","zh":"有人在守衛的食物裡下了毒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat was poisoned by a bowl of contaminated milk.","zh":"那隻貓因喝了一碗受汙染的牛奶而中毒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22ca9b144d68d7bb","term":"poison","forms":["poison","poisons","poisoning","poisoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使惡化；破壞","explanation":"比喻指像毒物擴散一樣，使關係、氣氛或局面變得明顯更糟。","examples":[{"en":"One careless remark poisoned the atmosphere in the room.","zh":"一句不經意的話破壞了房間裡的氣氛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Distrust poisoned the negotiations from the beginning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-847f5804f3fc1d3b2c11","word":"poisonous","forms":["poisonous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e075df7faf932cf9","term":"poisonous","forms":["poisonous","more poisonous","most poisonous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含毒的；有毒的","explanation":"指某種物質含有足以讓人或動物因接觸、吸入或吞食而受到危險傷害的毒物。核心畫面是“毒藏在東西里面”，因此重點在物質本身有毒，而不只是它會傳播傷害。","examples":[{"en":"This plant is poisonous if eaten.","zh":"這種植物吃下去會中毒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some mushrooms are poisonous to humans.","zh":"有些蘑菇對人類有毒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poisonous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57ab4d187bc52453","term":"poisonous","forms":["poisonous","more poisonous","most poisonous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"會釋放毒液的；有毒的動物","explanation":"描述蛇、蜘蛛等動物，或它們的咬傷、刺傷，表示能把毒液注入獵物或敵人體內。這裡的“毒”不是單純藏在身體裡，而是會透過咬、刺等方式主動傳出去。","examples":[{"en":"The guide warned us not to touch the poisonous snake.","zh":"導遊警告我們不要碰那條有毒的蛇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A poisonous spider bit him while he was sleeping.","zh":"他睡覺時被一隻會釋放毒液的蜘蛛咬了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poisonous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d138d529354619a22933","word":"poke","forms":["poke"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b911a10c60a8de4a","term":"poke","forms":["poke","pokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戳；捅一下","explanation":"“a poke”是用手指、棍子等戳或捅的一下，重點是短促地伸出去碰到某物。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a playful poke in the ribs.","zh":"她開玩笑地戳了一下我的肋部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt a sharp poke in my back.","zh":"我感到背部被猛地戳了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5961124abd240bc3","term":"poke","forms":["poke"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夏威夷生魚塊料理","explanation":"“poke”是一種夏威夷料理：把生魚或其他生海鮮切成小塊，再與芝麻油、海藻、海鹽、香草或香料等拌在一起食用。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered a bowl of tuna poke to share.","zh":"我們點了一碗金槍魚生魚塊料理一起吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This poke is mixed with sesame oil and seaweed.","zh":"這份生魚塊料理拌了芝麻油和海藻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cae73c81f76cfeb8","term":"poke","forms":["poke","pokes","poking","poked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"戳；捅","explanation":"“poke”表示用手指、棍子或其他物體短促地戳、捅某物，核心畫面是“伸出去碰一下”。","examples":[{"en":"The child poked the balloon with a pencil.","zh":"孩子用鉛筆戳了戳氣球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He poked me to get my attention.","zh":"他戳了我一下，想引起我的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f712d322b8f5a7e4431b","word":"polar","forms":["polar"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ac26dc3da0d49a0","term":"polar","forms":["polar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極地的；與極點有關的","explanation":"這個義項直接來自“兩極”的形象，指地球或其他天體的極點、極地區域，或與這些地方有關的事物，不等於單純的“寒冷”。","examples":[{"en":"They spent six months studying polar wildlife.","zh":"他們花了六個月研究極地野生動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A polar expedition can be dangerous without careful preparation.","zh":"沒有周密準備，極地考察可能很危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac76d75110647ec3","term":"polar","forms":["polar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"截然相反的；兩極的","explanation":"這裡把南北兩極的距離借來形容抽象事物，表示兩個觀點、立場或態度處在相反的極端，幾乎沒有共同點。","examples":[{"en":"The two candidates hold polar opposite views on the issue.","zh":"兩位候選人在這個問題上的看法截然相反。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The twins hold polar views on almost everything.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-b9425afde1f5e5eb96e8","word":"pole","forms":["pole"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-762690dff2cdccd9","term":"pole","forms":["pole","poles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長杆；柱","explanation":"pole 是細長而較堅硬的杆或柱，常用來支撐、固定、推動或承載東西。","examples":[{"en":"They used a long pole to lift the net.","zh":"他們用一根長杆把網提了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tent poles are made of light metal.","zh":"帳篷杆由輕質金屬製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1dc173695710c93e","term":"pole","forms":["pole","poles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地理極點；旋轉兩端","explanation":"pole 指物體旋轉軸兩端對應的點；在地球上，通常就是北極和南極。","examples":[{"en":"The expedition reached the North Pole in April.","zh":"探險隊在四月到達了北極。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Earth spins around an imaginary axis between its poles.","zh":"地球繞著連線兩極的假想軸旋轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07306ba043152432","term":"pole","forms":["pole","poles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兩個極端","explanation":"pole 可以把一條連續範圍想象成兩端，因此表示彼此相反或相距很遠的兩個極端。","examples":[{"en":"The two proposals lie at opposite poles of the debate.","zh":"這兩項提議處在這場爭論的兩個極端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village and the capital are at opposite poles of the country.","zh":"這個村莊和首都位於這個國家的兩端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1366fac71146793a85e9","word":"police","forms":["police"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c76172b315fff70e","term":"police","forms":["police"],"pos":"noun","zh":"警察機構","explanation":"指依法執行法律、維持公共秩序的公共機構，通常包括警察部門及其組織體系。","examples":[{"en":"The police are investigating the break-in.","zh":"警方正在調查這起入室盜竊案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Call the police if you see anything suspicious.","zh":"如果你看到可疑情況，就報警。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/police","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e14af837fa13c0bc","term":"police","forms":["police"],"pos":"noun","zh":"警察人員","explanation":"指一個警察機構中的警察人員整體，某些地區的非正式用法也可指一名警察。","examples":[{"en":"The police searched the building after the alarm went off.","zh":"警報響起後，警察搜查了這棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A police officer spoke to the witness.","zh":"一名警察和證人談了話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/police","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bad158b9695bfbe","term":"police","forms":["police","polices","policing","policed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"維持秩序","explanation":"指對人群、地區或活動進行警察式的監管，以執行法律並防止秩序被破壞。","examples":[{"en":"Extra officers were sent to police the crowd.","zh":"增派了警員來維持人群秩序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The border is difficult to police at night.","zh":"這條邊境在夜間很難監管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/police","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0de4923678a8631b8af8","word":"policeman/cop","forms":["policeman","cop"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3dc9d3c709c62872","term":"policeman","forms":["policeman","policemen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"男警察","explanation":"指在警察部門工作、負責維護治安和執行法律的男性。它突出“警察這一身份”以及“男性”這一資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The policeman stopped the car and asked for the driver's license.","zh":"那名男警察攔下汽車，要求司機出示駕駛證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A policeman helped the lost child find her parents.","zh":"一名男警察幫助走失的孩子找到了父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/policeman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18050b04ac4727cb","term":"policeman","forms":["policeman","policemen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冰球等運動中的執行者","explanation":"在冰球等運動中，指負責以強硬方式維持隊內或比賽秩序、執行懲罰性任務的隊員，也就是“執行者”。這是從“維持秩序的人”這一核心畫面引申出來的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The team relied on its policeman to protect the younger players.","zh":"這支隊伍依靠隊裡的執行者保護年輕隊員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team's policeman defended teammates against rough opponents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/policeman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc18a4ea6f7a5af1","term":"cop","forms":["cop","cops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"警察；監獄看守","explanation":"“cop”是非正式說法，指警察，也可以指監獄看守；它和“抓住、控制”這一核心畫面有關。","examples":[{"en":"A cop stopped me and asked to see my license.","zh":"一名警察攔住我，要求看我的駕照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cops arrived a few minutes later.","zh":"警察幾分鐘後趕到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-823412d1eacb67956220","word":"policy","forms":["policy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e27033e24fbba68","term":"policy","forms":["policy","policies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政策；方針","explanation":"指政府、公司、學校等正式採用的行動原則，說明它們打算怎樣處理某類事情。它像一張共同遵守的路線圖，決定行動的方向和邊界。","examples":[{"en":"The school has a strict policy on mobile phones.","zh":"這所學校對手機有嚴格的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company changed its policy on remote work.","zh":"公司改變了遠端辦公政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/policy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8d0fb808c3b4559","term":"policy","forms":["policy","policies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政策檔案；規定檔案","explanation":"指把政策內容正式寫下來的檔案。這裡強調的是承載規則的文字，而不只是背後的原則。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the privacy policy before creating an account.","zh":"建立賬戶前請閱讀隱私政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy is available on the company's website.","zh":"新政策檔案已釋出在公司網站上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/policy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10d74353e1b40223","term":"policy","forms":["policy","policies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險合同","explanation":"指投保人與保險公司約定保障範圍、期限、責任和費用的保險合同。它規定發生什麼情況時保險公司需要承擔責任。","examples":[{"en":"This policy covers damage caused by fire and theft.","zh":"這份保險涵蓋火災和盜竊造成的損失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check whether your policy covers accidental damage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/policy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8686d83b588472f","term":"policy","forms":["policy","policies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保單","explanation":"指載明或證明保險合同內容的檔案。日常使用中，人們常直接把這份檔案也稱為policy。","examples":[{"en":"Keep your policy in a safe place.","zh":"請把保單放在安全的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Read your policy carefully before filing an insurance claim.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/policy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a741eb9c8922e9e08fc","word":"polish","forms":["polish"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24c6afe7795629e4","term":"polish","forms":["polish"],"pos":"noun","zh":"波蘭語","explanation":"指波蘭使用的主要語言。它是語言名稱，首字母通常大寫。","examples":[{"en":"My neighbor speaks Polish at home.","zh":"我的鄰居在家說波蘭語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reads Polish as fluently as English.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b489d53cd094bbed","term":"polish","forms":["polish","polishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上光劑；拋光劑","explanation":"指用來擦亮或清潔某種表面的物質，例如擦銀器或鞋子的上光劑。它是“讓表面變亮”的具體工具。","examples":[{"en":"This furniture polish gives the table a soft shine.","zh":"這種傢俱上光劑能讓桌子呈現柔和的光澤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Apply a little polish with a soft cloth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3692edf967516da7","term":"polish","forms":["polish","polishes","polishing","polished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦亮；拋光","explanation":"透過擦、清潔或打磨，使表面變得平滑有光澤。這是從“把表面打磨得更好看”發展出的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"He polished the silver until it shone.","zh":"他把銀器擦得閃閃發亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please polish the table before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人到之前請把桌子擦亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e88309e401031d4","term":"polish","forms":["polish","polishes","polishing","polished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改進；打磨","explanation":"把作品、計劃、技能或表現反覆修改和練習，去掉不夠完善的地方，使其更成熟。這是從擦亮表面引申到提升質量。","examples":[{"en":"I need another evening to polish my speech.","zh":"我還需要一個晚上來打磨我的演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor helped polish the final draft.","zh":"編輯幫助潤色了最終稿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cad2a80df44e3abf27b7","word":"polite","forms":["polite"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8f4ff0afb85efa1","term":"polite","forms":["polite","politer","more polite","politest","most polite"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有禮貌的；得體的","explanation":"形容人的說話和行為尊重別人、符合社會禮儀，例如在公共場合注意自己的行為，或用客氣的方式提出請求。","examples":[{"en":"It's polite to silence your phone before the meeting.","zh":"開會前把手機調成靜音是有禮貌的做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Maya was polite to the waiter, even when her order was wrong.","zh":"即使服務員上錯了菜，瑪雅對他仍然很有禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec08467ce12be51213a6","word":"political","forms":["political"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43b8809ff5666e39","term":"political","forms":["political","more political","most political"],"pos":"adj","zh":"政治的；與治理有關的","explanation":"指直接涉及政治、政府治理或政治活動的事物，是這個詞最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The country is facing a serious political crisis.","zh":"這個國家正面臨嚴重的政治危機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote a book about political reform.","zh":"她寫了一本關於政治改革的書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/political","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0af4dc208fed948","term":"political","forms":["political","more political","most political"],"pos":"adj","zh":"政體或行政機構的","explanation":"強調某事物屬於一個政治共同體、政體或其行政組成部分，常用於談論政府部門、政治工作人員等。","examples":[{"en":"The minister reorganized the political office after the election.","zh":"選舉後，這位部長重組了政治事務辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The political system divides power among three branches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/political","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-c781f9e50e6d6ec24d8b","word":"politician","forms":["politician"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-026fab85ffdc8336","term":"politician","forms":["politician","politicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治人物；公職人員","explanation":"指參與政治、尤其是透過選舉產生或由任命擔任政府職務的人。這是 politician 最基本、最常用的意思，可以不帶褒貶色彩。","examples":[{"en":"Politicians should serve the public, not themselves.","zh":"政治人物應該為公眾服務，而不是為自己謀利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The politician promised to improve public transport.","zh":"這名政治人物承諾改善公共交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/politician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0aa48d703567da25","term":"politician","forms":["politician","politicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"以公職為職業的人","explanation":"特指把擔任民選政治職務當作長期職業的人，強調“從政是職業道路”，而不只是偶然擔任一次公職。","examples":[{"en":"She became a politician after working as a lawyer for ten years.","zh":"她當了十年律師後成為了一名職業政治人物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The politician spent two decades serving her constituency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/politician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a1d1484d3cbc7210704","word":"politics","forms":["politics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-79ce79bb294e77f4","term":"politics","forms":["politics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治活動；治理事務","explanation":"指管理政府、組織或社會運動時，圍繞決策、權力和規則展開的一整套活動與做法。它不只限於國家政府，也可以發生在學校、公司或社會運動中。","examples":[{"en":"The politics of the movement changed after the election.","zh":"選舉後，這場運動中的政治運作發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She entered politics after years of community organizing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/politics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbfadf8cc2445da7","term":"politics","forms":["politics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"從政；政治職業","explanation":"指把處理政治事務作為職業，或泛指政治這一職業領域。說某人進入這個領域時，重點是“從政”這條職業道路。","examples":[{"en":"She went into politics after working as a lawyer.","zh":"她做過律師後進入了政界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She entered politics after years of community organizing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/politics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-707165e9984b51dcdf1c","word":"poll","forms":["poll"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"poll","forms":["poll"],"pos":"n.","zh":"民意調查","examples":[{"en":"The latest poll shows strong support for the new park.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Our class conducted a poll about students' reading habits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"poll","forms":["poll"],"pos":"n.","zh":"投票；選舉","examples":[{"en":"The members chose a new chairperson in a poll.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A poll will be held next week to decide whether to approve the proposal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-3","term":"poll","forms":["poll"],"pos":"v.","zh":"對…進行民意調查","examples":[{"en":"The researchers will poll a thousand residents about the new policy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We plan to poll customers before changing the store's opening hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-4","term":"poll","forms":["poll"],"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得選票","examples":[{"en":"A new party may poll well in the next election.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She is expected to poll more votes than the other candidates.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-f16075a9eba806a610f8","word":"pollute","forms":["pollute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4eef446797f355a","term":"pollute","forms":["pollute","pollutes","polluting","polluted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"汙染；使有害","explanation":"指把有害物質或不需要的產物帶入某物，尤其使水、空氣、土地等受到危害。核心畫面是乾淨的環境被外來髒東西侵入。","examples":[{"en":"The factory polluted the river with chemical waste.","zh":"這家工廠用化學廢料汙染了河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Burning coal pollutes the air.","zh":"燃煤會汙染空氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pollute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45c214c137b5a630","term":"pollute","forms":["pollute","pollutes","polluting","polluted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"破壞純淨狀態；干擾","explanation":"指把不自然或不該出現的因素帶入某處或某種環境，使它不再適合原來的活動。比如燈光汙染夜空，使人無法清楚觀星。","examples":[{"en":"The bright signs polluted the night sky and hid the stars.","zh":"明亮的廣告牌干擾了夜空，遮住了星星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Too much noise can pollute the quiet of the countryside.","zh":"過多的噪聲會破壞鄉間的寧靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pollute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de2c2dcff9ee57e1065a","word":"pollution","forms":["pollution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d42ff85c719955b9","term":"pollution","forms":["pollution","pollutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"環境汙染","explanation":"指有害物質，或達到有害程度的噪聲、光線等，進入環境並破壞環境質量的現象。這是 pollution 最常見、最重要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Air pollution is especially serious during the winter months.","zh":"冬季月份的空氣汙染尤其嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city is trying to reduce noise pollution near schools.","zh":"這座城市正努力減少學校附近的噪聲汙染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pollution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-779bfdb7ba79dcbb","term":"pollution","forms":["pollution","pollutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汙染物","explanation":"指造成汙染的東西，即汙染源或汙染物本身。這個意思比“汙染”這一現象更具體，但在現代英語中通常不如 pollutant 常用。","examples":[{"en":"Plastic pollution has reached even the most remote beaches.","zh":"塑膠汙染甚至已經到達最偏遠的海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The filter removes pollution from the wastewater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pollution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e7914b0df8068b79cdc","word":"pond","forms":["pond"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f1330a280cf4dad","term":"pond","forms":["pond","ponds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"池塘；水塘","explanation":"pond 是比湖泊小的、基本靜止的內陸水體，可以是天然形成的，也可以是人工挖成的。腦中可以把它記成一塊被圈住、安靜存水的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The children were watching ducks swim across the pond.","zh":"孩子們正在看鴨子游過池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a small pond behind the house.","zh":"房子後面有一個小池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c65fba65e6af3813","term":"pond","forms":["pond","ponds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大西洋彼岸","explanation":"在 across the pond 中，pond 不再是真的池塘，而是把大西洋想成橫在兩邊之間的一片水；因此該短語常指大西洋另一邊，尤其是英國和美國相互指稱對方時。","examples":[{"en":"Her sister lives across the pond in Boston.","zh":"她姐姐住在大西洋彼岸的波士頓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their new album became a hit on both sides of the pond.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bcad0dd47c63afbebba","word":"ponder","forms":["ponder"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-287b7d8ca7ce7fe8","term":"ponder","forms":["ponder","ponders","pondering","pondered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"深入思考","explanation":"ponder 可以表示對某個問題反覆思考、試圖弄明白；重點是把想法放在心上仔細掂量。","examples":[{"en":"She pondered why he had left without saying goodbye.","zh":"她反覆思考他為什麼不辭而別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pondered the offer throughout the train journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ponder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2132fff1fbc5678d","term":"ponder","forms":["ponder","ponders","pondering","pondered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細考慮","explanation":"ponder 也可以表示在作決定前認真考慮某個方案、問題或後果，含有權衡利弊的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The committee is pondering several options before making a final decision.","zh":"委員會正在認真權衡幾個方案，然後再作出最終決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pondered whether moving abroad was the right choice.","zh":"他仔細考慮搬到國外是否是正確的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ponder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0363f1a98b0c507a2379","word":"pony","forms":["pony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7847a4bda2ab8219","term":"pony","forms":["pony","ponies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小馬","explanation":"pony 是一種體型較小的馬，通常特指肩部高度低於約一百四十四釐米的馬種；這是這個詞最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children took turns riding the pony.","zh":"孩子們輪流騎那匹小馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw three ponies in the field.","zh":"我們在田野裡看到了三匹小馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27cac5503836765cd107","word":"pool","forms":["pool"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-850809309cd97305","term":"pool","forms":["pool","pools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小水池","explanation":"指面積不大但通常較深、聚集起來的水，可能由泉水供給，也可能位於溪流或河流中。","examples":[{"en":"We found a quiet pool beneath the waterfall.","zh":"我們在瀑布下面發現了一處安靜的小水池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children cooled their feet in the shallow pool.","zh":"孩子們把腳泡在淺水池裡降溫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbf0107c5b58d53e","term":"pool","forms":["pool","pools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"游泳池","explanation":"是 swimming pool 的簡稱，指供人游泳的人工水池。","examples":[{"en":"I'll meet you at the pool after work.","zh":"下班後我在游泳池和你碰面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel has an outdoor pool.","zh":"這家酒店有一個室外游泳池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c03b40baf9128208","term":"pool","forms":["pool","pools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資源池","explanation":"指集中儲存、隨時可以呼叫的一批資源，例如資金、計算能力、人員或材料。","examples":[{"en":"The project has access to a large pool of funding.","zh":"這個專案可以使用一大筆集中資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital draws on a shared pool of specialist nurses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80e44f84ded6b0f6","term":"pool","forms":["pool","pools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共同資源","explanation":"指多人或多方集中起來、共同使用或共同承擔結果的一批資源。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone contributed to a common pool for the trip.","zh":"大家都為這次旅行共同湊了一筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The schools share a pool of specialist teaching staff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-742c9b727e11939a","term":"pool","forms":["pool","pools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檯球運動","explanation":"一種在檯球桌上進行的球類運動，通常要把自己一方的球全部擊入袋中，最後再擊入黑球。","examples":[{"en":"Do you want to play pool after dinner?","zh":"你晚飯後想打檯球嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He bought a pool table for the games room.","zh":"他為娛樂室買了一張檯球桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d58793812fff0c5f","term":"pool","forms":["pool","pools","pooling","pooled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"共同集中資源","explanation":"指各方把資源放到同一個共同池中，以便一起使用，並按約定分享收益或承擔損失。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams pooled their resources to finish the project.","zh":"兩個團隊集中各自的資源來完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We pooled our money and rented a larger house.","zh":"我們把錢湊在一起，租了一所更大的房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e3795d05d9d3ed261ea","word":"poor","forms":["poor"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55a141fd1bc8dd38","term":"poor","forms":["poor","poorer","poorest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貧窮的","explanation":"指一個人、家庭或群體擁有的錢財和物品很少，尤其是和周圍人相比處於貧困狀態。它強調經濟資源不足，不只是暫時手頭緊。","examples":[{"en":"Many families in the area are still poor.","zh":"這個地區的許多家庭仍然很貧困。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He grew up poor but worked hard at school.","zh":"他從小家境貧寒，但在學校學習很努力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcf643a9f91e482b","term":"poor","forms":["poor","poorer","poorest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"質量差的","explanation":"指表現、作品、服務或結果沒有達到通常的標準，重點在質量低，而不是價格低或數量少。","examples":[{"en":"The team gave a poor performance last night.","zh":"這支隊伍昨晚的表現很差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report was based on poor research.","zh":"這份報告建立在質量不高的研究之上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80cc24a8806a0cd1","term":"poor","forms":["poor","poorer","poorest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"缺乏某種成分的","explanation":"指某物所含的特定成分、資源或特徵很少，因此在這一方面不足；它不一定表示整體質量差。","examples":[{"en":"This soil is poor in nutrients.","zh":"這種土壤缺乏營養成分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At that altitude, the air is poor in oxygen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de70fa60cac227cbc132","word":"pop","forms":["pop"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abc803118e2c65d7","term":"pop","forms":["pop"],"pos":"adj","zh":"流行的","explanation":"指受到很多人喜歡、在一段時期內很流行的；這是從“流行”這一獨立詞源分支發展出的意義，不是“突然彈出”的核心意象。","examples":[{"en":"She listens to pop music on her way to work.","zh":"她上班路上聽流行音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She writes catchy pop songs for teenage listeners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-537da62f0e25cdcd","term":"pop","forms":["pop","pops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"砰的一聲","explanation":"指突然、短促而響亮的聲音，尤其像瓶塞因氣壓彈出時發出的聲音；這正是“突然、短促地彈出”這一核心意象的名詞化用法。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a pop as the cork came out of the bottle.","zh":"瓶塞從瓶口彈出時，我們聽到了一聲砰響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden pop came from the kitchen.","zh":"廚房裡突然傳來一聲砰響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acd5e96f196c8437","term":"pop","forms":["pop","pops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽水","explanation":"指有氣泡的飲料，通常是不含酒精的汽水；瓶塞“砰”地彈出、飲料帶有氣泡的聯絡幫助形成了這個詞義分支。","examples":[{"en":"We bought some pop for the picnic.","zh":"我們為野餐買了些汽水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He prefers orange pop to cola.","zh":"比起可樂，他更喜歡橙味汽水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a4ef253e3fef22cb9d3","word":"popcorn","forms":["popcorn"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82f7970c55093afd","term":"popcorn","forms":["popcorn","popcorns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爆米花這種食品","explanation":"指玉米粒經過乾熱後爆開的零食，通常作為看電影、聚會時吃的小吃；這是最基本、最常用的意義。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a large bag of popcorn before the movie started.","zh":"電影開始前，我們買了一大袋爆米花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She likes her popcorn with a little salt.","zh":"她喜歡在爆米花裡放一點鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/popcorn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c810fd03484ce327b84","word":"popular","forms":["popular"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cd6f3b0bfdb25ad","term":"popular","forms":["popular","more popular","most popular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大眾認可的","explanation":"指一個觀點、說法或事物得到普通大眾的普遍接受或認可，重點是“大家通常這樣認為”。","examples":[{"en":"Contrary to popular belief, bats are not blind.","zh":"與普遍看法相反，蝙蝠並不是瞎的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal failed to win popular support.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/popular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9e9dde8a8bf2294","term":"popular","forms":["popular","more popular","most popular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"受許多人喜愛的","explanation":"指許多人喜歡、欣賞或支援的事物或人，是 popular 最常見、最實用的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"This café is popular with local students.","zh":"這家咖啡館很受當地學生歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The show became popular around the world.","zh":"這檔節目在全世界都受到了歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/popular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b91d83b6c41a231217b7","word":"popularity","forms":["popularity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5b03c0076f5753b","term":"popularity","forms":["popularity","popularities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受歡迎程度","explanation":"指某人、某事物或某種活動受到大眾喜愛、支援或認可的程度。這裡的核心不是“有多少人知道”，而是“有多少人喜歡或擁護”。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant's popularity grew after a famous chef recommended it.","zh":"這家餐館在一位名廚推薦後越來越受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app has gained popularity among older users.","zh":"這款應用在年長使用者中越來越受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/popularity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113,115],"total":3,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-f1010f5da5aa80e25cff","word":"populate","forms":["populate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c0107b61679d2cf","term":"populate","forms":["populate","populates","populating","populated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給地方增加居民","explanation":"指把人遷入或安排到某個地方，使那裡有人居住，核心畫面是把原本空著的地方填滿居民。","examples":[{"en":"The new settlers populated the valley.","zh":"新移民使這片山谷有了居民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island was populated by families from the mainland.","zh":"這個島後來住進了來自大陸的家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/populate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36e1b1cb6177f6ed","term":"populate","forms":["populate","populates","populating","populated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"填充列表或集合","explanation":"在計算機等語境中，指把原本空的列表、表格、集合或其他專案填入資料，使它們顯示出內容；這是“把空處填滿”這一核心畫面的現代延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The app populates the menu with nearby restaurants.","zh":"這個應用會把附近的餐館填入選單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the search, the results table was populated with new entries.","zh":"搜尋後，結果表中填入了新的條目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/populate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f9edc4d3ed0a0e5741a","word":"population","forms":["population"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b3da7a6f1449172","term":"population","forms":["population","populations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某地的人口","explanation":"指生活在某個國家、城市、州或其他政治、地理範圍內的所有人，重點是“這一群人”本身。","examples":[{"en":"The population of the city has grown rapidly.","zh":"這座城市的人口增長很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government is building more homes for the growing population.","zh":"政府正在為不斷增長的人口建造更多住房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/population","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a50b5047db0dce6","term":"population","forms":["population","populations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人口數量","explanation":"指一個城鎮、國家或其他範圍內居民的總數，也就是對人口進行統計後得到的數字。","examples":[{"en":"The island has a population of about 20,000.","zh":"這座島大約有兩萬人口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town's population fell by ten percent last decade.","zh":"這個城鎮的人口在過去十年減少了百分之十。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/population","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa150d3005ceb681bba4","word":"porcelain","forms":["porcelain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3533397e73a8ac34","term":"porcelain","forms":["porcelain","porcelains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓷；瓷質材料","explanation":"一種通常潔白、堅硬並略帶透明感的陶瓷材料，傳統上由高嶺土等原料高溫燒製而成；它也常被用來象徵精緻卻易碎的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The bathroom tiles are made of porcelain.","zh":"浴室的瓷磚是用瓷製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The figurine has a delicate porcelain finish.","zh":"這件小雕像有精緻的瓷質表面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porcelain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca06eeb99ec31cc1","term":"porcelain","forms":["porcelain","porcelains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓷餐具；瓷器總稱","explanation":"在餐桌或家居語境中，porcelain 可以把瓷這種材料借指用它製成的盤子、杯子等一套餐具，即通常所說的瓷器。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves its desserts on fine porcelain.","zh":"這家餐廳用精美的瓷餐具盛放甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cabinet holds our grandmother's porcelain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porcelain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-698131fa10b8088ef574","word":"porch","forms":["porch"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5befdfe5a3d2c040","term":"porch","forms":["porch","porches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有頂門廊","explanation":"porch 是建築物入口處有頂的空間或平臺，常連線室內外，人們可以在那裡坐著、等人或進出房屋。","examples":[{"en":"We sat on the porch and watched the rain.","zh":"我們坐在門廊上看雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the package on the front porch.","zh":"請把包裹放在前門廊上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a96b538a4ed526e0","term":"porch","forms":["porch","porches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"柱廊；有頂走道","explanation":"在較正式的建築語境中，porch 也可以指由柱子或其他結構支撐的有頂入口空間，或供人通行的遮蓋走道。","examples":[{"en":"A long porch runs along the side of the old building.","zh":"一條長長的有頂走道沿著那座老建築的一側延伸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A covered porch connects the two wings of the building.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09aabcd859e4a72f9223","word":"pork","forms":["pork"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea925bc0d0e08610","term":"pork","forms":["pork","porks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豬肉","explanation":"指豬的肉，是日常飲食中最基本、最常見的意思。記住“豬”這條主線，就能把它和牛肉、雞肉等肉類名稱聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"We had pork with rice for dinner.","zh":"我們晚飯吃了豬肉配米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cafeteria serves pork on Tuesdays.","zh":"這家自助餐廳每週二供應豬肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pork","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b075169abc0386e5","term":"pork","forms":["pork","porks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治私利撥款","explanation":"在美國政治中，指國會議員為自己的選區或特殊利益集團爭取的政府資金，而不是面向全國整體利益的支出；因此常含批評意味。","examples":[{"en":"Critics called the bridge project political pork.","zh":"批評者稱這個橋樑專案是為政治私利服務的撥款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The senator secured pork for projects benefiting his own district.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pork","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f8d397a33fcb9725db96","word":"port","forms":["port"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-561b294d95a95931","term":"port","forms":["port","ports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"港口","explanation":"指船只可以避風、停靠並裝卸貨物或乘客的地方；可以把它記成讓船和貨物進出、被運送的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The ship entered the port before sunset.","zh":"船在日落前進入了港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The port handles thousands of containers every day.","zh":"這個港口每天處理數千個集裝箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/port","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3498127d28062a71","term":"port","forms":["port","ports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"左舷","explanation":"指船隻或飛機面向前方時的左側；它按交通工具本身的方向確定，不按乘客的左右確定。","examples":[{"en":"A warning light came on on the port side of the aircraft.","zh":"飛機左舷一側的警示燈亮了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain ordered a sharp turn to port.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/port","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4befa8ccb2a58aa2","term":"port","forms":["port","ports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝置介面","explanation":"指電子裝置上可以插入電纜接頭的介面；電纜插入這裡，電訊號或資料就能進出裝置。","examples":[{"en":"My phone has a separate port for charging and headphones.","zh":"我的手機有分別用於充電和連線耳機的介面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Make sure the cable is firmly plugged into the port.","zh":"確保電纜牢牢插在介面裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/port","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d16ac72437975a2d","term":"port","forms":["port","ports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"波特酒","explanation":"指主要產自葡萄牙的甜型加強葡萄酒，通常顏色較深；這個義項可透過“葡萄牙運出的酒”單獨記憶。","examples":[{"en":"We served port with the cheese after dinner.","zh":"晚餐後我們用波特酒搭配乳酪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered a small glass of port.","zh":"她點了一小杯波特酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/port","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01e782826ae5182220bd","word":"portable","forms":["portable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0cbb6ea1dc1722b6","term":"portable","forms":["portable","more portable","most portable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"便攜的；易搬動的","explanation":"表示東西可以輕鬆帶走或從一個地方搬到另一個地方，重點是攜帶和移動方便，而不只是重量輕。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a portable speaker for the picnic.","zh":"我們為野餐買了一個行動式音箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This portable table folds up in seconds.","zh":"這張便攜桌幾秒鐘就能摺疊起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f78b1bbdaafa735f1912","word":"porter","forms":["porter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-baf29024ab72c5f9","term":"porter","forms":["porter","porters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行李員","explanation":"porter是替旅客搬執行李等物品的人，常見於車站、酒店或機場等場所。核心畫面就是有人幫你把沉重的東西搬走。","examples":[{"en":"A porter carried our bags from the hotel to the taxi.","zh":"一名行李員把我們的包從酒店搬到了計程車旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We asked the porter to help with the largest suitcase.","zh":"我們請行李員幫忙搬最大的行李箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d8c2de321b75a0a","term":"porter","forms":["porter","porters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門衛","explanation":"porter可以是負責控制建築入口的人，例如替住戶開門、接待來訪者或看守入口的門衛。這個義項和“站在門邊的人”聯絡在一起記最容易。","examples":[{"en":"The porter opened the front door for the residents.","zh":"門衛為住戶開啟了前門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the parcel with the porter downstairs.","zh":"請把包裹交給樓下的門衛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e6a8e0b849ed9b064c5","word":"portfolio","forms":["portfolio"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9fae197548042d18","term":"portfolio","forms":["portfolio","portfolios"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作品集","explanation":"指一組集中展示的作品，尤其是藝術家、設計師、攝影師或求職者用來展示能力和經歷的作品集。它可以是紙質的，也可以是網站或電子檔案形式。","examples":[{"en":"The designer sent her portfolio to three studios.","zh":"那名設計師把自己的作品集寄給了三家工作室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His online portfolio includes photographs from five countries.","zh":"他的線上作品集收錄了來自五個國家的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portfolio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2f9b0f8b07ff709","term":"portfolio","forms":["portfolio","portfolios"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投資組合","explanation":"指投資者持有並一起管理的一組投資或其他資產，例如股票、債券和基金。把它理解成“放在同一個投資資料夾裡的資產”，重點是整體組合，而不是其中某一項。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps a diversified portfolio of stocks and bonds.","zh":"她持有一個由股票和債券組成的多元化投資組合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fund manager reviewed the portfolio before making a new investment.","zh":"基金經理在進行新投資前審查了這份投資組合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portfolio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83e01dda3eb5a450a0a4","word":"portion","forms":["portion"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-47bd0ae821fcda5d","term":"portion","forms":["portion","portions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分配的一份","explanation":"指按照需要、計劃或規定分給某人的數量或份額，可以是食物、錢、資源或工作量。","examples":[{"en":"Each family received a portion of the donated food.","zh":"每個家庭都分到了一份捐贈的食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A large portion of the budget goes to education.","zh":"預算中很大一部分用於教育。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a4279d24abab9cf","term":"portion","forms":["portion","portions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體中的一部分","explanation":"指從完整事物中分離出來的部分，重點在“整體被切分後得到的一塊”，不一定是預先分配給某人的份額。","examples":[{"en":"Only a portion of the wall was damaged.","zh":"只有牆的一部分受到了損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a small portion of the manuscript survives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-134d651e13c4b1d2","term":"portion","forms":["portion","portions","portioning","portioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分成份額並分配","explanation":"指為了不同目的或不同物件，把一個整體劃分成若干數量或份額；這個動作就是把整體變成一個個portion。","examples":[{"en":"The chef portioned the soup into six containers.","zh":"廚師把湯分裝進六個容器裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The supplies were portioned out among the teams.","zh":"物資被分配給了各個小組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51c5a8296a032ce7b301","word":"portrait","forms":["portrait"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60a32bb486fd9be5","term":"portrait","forms":["portrait","portraits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人物肖像","explanation":"指畫、照片、雕像等對一個人的肖像表現，尤其常指突出頭部和肩部的畫像。它的核心不是某一種媒介，而是把這個人作為畫面主體呈現出來。","examples":[{"en":"She found an old portrait of her grandmother in the attic.","zh":"她在閣樓裡找到了一幅祖母的舊肖像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist painted a portrait of the retiring mayor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portrait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89a432222af8f819b8fd","word":"portray","forms":["portray"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a613772ff6695ff2","term":"portray","forms":["portray","portrays","portraying","portrayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"畫出……的肖像","explanation":"指用畫筆或其他繪畫方式畫出某人的面貌或某物的形象，是“把物件畫出來”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The artist portrayed the child in a garden.","zh":"這位藝術家畫出了孩子在花園裡的形象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist portrayed her grandmother seated by a window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa0feebad0768476","term":"portray","forms":["portray","portrays","portraying","portrayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"以形象呈現","explanation":"不一定真的作畫，而是透過外表、影象或整體形象把某人的特點、狀態或某件事表現出來。它仍然保留著“讓人看見某種形象”的核心。","examples":[{"en":"The photograph portrays the village as peaceful and welcoming.","zh":"這張照片把這個村莊呈現得寧靜而友好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report portrays her as a careful and honest leader.","zh":"這份報告把她塑造成一位謹慎而誠實的領導者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60f7e0d37e178bbad3c0","word":"pose","forms":["pose"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba4c5b7a11686348","term":"pose","forms":["pose","poses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"姿勢；姿態","explanation":"指身體在某一時刻擺出的姿勢或位置，尤其常用於拍照、繪畫和表演；核心畫面就是把身體“擺”在那裡。","examples":[{"en":"She held the pose while the photographer adjusted the lights.","zh":"攝影師調燈時，她保持著這個姿勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The yoga teacher showed us a simple pose for beginners.","zh":"瑜伽老師給我們示範了一個適合初學者的簡單姿勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-040afa5b06813ad3","term":"pose","forms":["pose","poses","posing","posed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擺好姿勢","explanation":"指把某人或某物擺成適合拍照、繪畫或表演的固定姿勢，也就是把姿態“擺出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The photographer posed the family in front of the old house.","zh":"攝影師讓這家人在老房子前擺好姿勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family posed beside the old oak tree.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1174225bf2c775b","term":"pose","forms":["pose","poses","posing","posed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擺姿勢；擺出姿態","explanation":"指自己保持某種姿勢，或故意擺出某種態度給別人看；它與名詞“姿態”的核心畫面直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"The children posed for a photo in front of the fountain.","zh":"孩子們在噴泉前擺好姿勢拍照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He posed as a serious expert during the interview.","zh":"採訪時，他擺出一副嚴肅專家的樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a452459503be70d2ed2","word":"position","forms":["position"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d429426599dd2f6e","term":"position","forms":["position","positions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"位置；所在處","explanation":"指人或物所在的地方、方位或安排的位置，是 position 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please mark the position of the door on the plan.","zh":"請在平面圖上標出門的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chairs are now in position.","zh":"椅子現在已經就位了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/position","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a590501d1e75de7","term":"position","forms":["position","positions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職位；工作崗位","explanation":"指一個人可以申請、擔任或離開的工作崗位，也就是“職位”。","examples":[{"en":"She applied for a position in the sales department.","zh":"她申請了銷售部的一個職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A vacant teaching position attracted more than eighty applications.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/position","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-426af914d89543ea","term":"position","forms":["position","positions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立場；觀點","explanation":"指一個人對某個問題所站的那一邊，即明確的觀點或態度。","examples":[{"en":"The minister explained her position on the new law.","zh":"部長解釋了她對這項新法律的立場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to take a clear position on this issue.","zh":"我們需要明確表明對這個問題的立場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/position","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c539fae7250dab6b","term":"position","forms":["position","positions","positioning","positioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放置；使就位","explanation":"指有意識地把某人或某物放到指定、合適或有利的位置，就是把“位置”安排好。","examples":[{"en":"Position the lamp beside the sofa.","zh":"把燈放在沙發旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The photographer positioned the children in front of the wall.","zh":"攝影師把孩子們安排在牆前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/position","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afa6e9ab3ac6574d50e6","word":"positive","forms":["positive"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45f3a0009c476c1b","term":"positive","forms":["positive","more positive","most positive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大於零的","explanation":"在數學中，表示數值位於零的上方，也就是大於零，正是“朝向肯定和有利的一邊”。","examples":[{"en":"Every positive number is greater than zero.","zh":"每個正數都大於零。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The temperature became positive after sunrise.","zh":"日出後溫度升到了零度以上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/positive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e48c21db1d7a7a7","term":"positive","forms":["positive","more positive","most positive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樂觀的；積極的","explanation":"表示看待生活和未來時傾向於相信事情會向好的方向發展，體現了“朝向有利的一邊”。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps a positive attitude even when work is difficult.","zh":"即使工作很困難，她仍保持積極的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A positive outlook helped him recover from the setback.","zh":"樂觀的心態幫助他走出了那次挫折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/positive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8291378de2766cbb","term":"positive","forms":["positive","more positive","most positive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好的；令人愉快的","explanation":"表示某事物令人感到舒服、健康、愉快或值得肯定，是“朝向有利的一邊”的日常評價。","examples":[{"en":"Music fills the room with positive energy.","zh":"音樂讓房間充滿了愉快而積極的氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to focus on the positive things in your day.","zh":"試著把注意力放在一天中令人愉快的事情上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/positive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-992d3b44833316b5","term":"positive","forms":["positive","positives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陽性檢測結果","explanation":"指檢測結果確認存在目標物、感染、疾病或其他被檢測情況，也就是事實或檢測朝向“得到確認”的一邊。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic called to say that her test was positive.","zh":"診所打電話說她的檢測結果呈陽性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laboratory repeated the test to confirm the positive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/positive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4db4f7fc05070b09f946","word":"possess","forms":["possess"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75b04ddb9a747f72","term":"possess","forms":["possess","possesses","possessing","possessed","possessest","possessedst","possesseth","-","possest","possesst"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擁有；持有","explanation":"指把某物作為自己的財產或佔有物擁有，核心就是“手裡有並能控制它”。","examples":[{"en":"He possesses a rare collection of old maps.","zh":"他擁有一批珍貴的古地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She does not possess the patience required for this job.","zh":"她沒有做這份工作所需的耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-158099490cb95152","term":"possess","forms":["possess","possesses","possessing","possessed","possessest","possessedst","possesseth","-","possest","possesst"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支配思想；縈繞心頭","explanation":"指某個想法、念頭或情緒牢牢佔據人的心，使人不斷受到它的影響。","examples":[{"en":"The thought of failure possessed him throughout the night.","zh":"失敗的念頭整夜縈繞著他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strange desire possessed her to leave immediately.","zh":"一種奇怪的衝動支配著她，讓她立刻離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b616aa60af2d3584e4a","word":"possession","forms":["possession"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc1a075aa8958a17","term":"possession","forms":["possession","possessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擁有的物品","explanation":"possession 可以指某人擁有的一件物品，尤其常用於強調它很珍貴、很重要或很受珍愛。這裡關注的是“被擁有的東西”，而不是擁有這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"This old camera is my most treasured possession.","zh":"這臺舊相機是我最珍愛的物品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She packed her few possessions into one suitcase.","zh":"她把僅有的幾件物品裝進了一個手提箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32c8ad949bcded1e","term":"possession","forms":["possession","possessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擁有或控制的狀態","explanation":"這裡的 possession 指某物在某人手中、由某人佔有或控制的狀態。它比“擁有的物品”更強調關係或狀態：東西不一定是永久財產，也可以只是暫時由某人保管或掌握。","examples":[{"en":"The missing documents are now in the police’s possession.","zh":"那些失蹤的檔案現在已由警方掌握。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He came into possession of the house after his aunt died.","zh":"姑媽去世後，他獲得了這所房子的所有權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5a0aa306476543fef18","word":"possibility","forms":["possibility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8c7440c7e275681","term":"possibility","forms":["possibility","possibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可能性","explanation":"指某件事能夠發生、實現或成為現實的程度或狀態，重點在“這件事有沒有可能”。","examples":[{"en":"There is a real possibility of heavy rain tonight.","zh":"今晚確實有下大雨的可能性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We cannot ignore the possibility that the plan will fail.","zh":"我們不能忽視計劃可能失敗這一可能性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7db005ae0cb42a3","term":"possibility","forms":["possibility","possibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種可能的結果或事情","explanation":"指一件可能發生、出現或形成的具體事情，也就是那扇門後可能出現的某個結果。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are considering the possibility of life on other planets.","zh":"科學家正在考慮其他行星上存在生命的可能性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Canceling the trip remains a real possibility.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c4773daf2e6a2e27ea8e","word":"possible","forms":["possible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-219c4cb2d69dd8d3","term":"possible","forms":["possible","more possible","most possible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可能發生的","explanation":"表示某件事有機會發生，但並不確定；它只是沒有被排除在外，不能保證一定會發生。","examples":[{"en":"It is possible that the train will be late.","zh":"火車可能會晚點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A power cut is possible during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間可能會停電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-037bcee8a49c37c0","term":"possible","forms":["possible","more possible","most possible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能夠做到的；可實現的","explanation":"表示某件事在能力、條件或方法上做得到，因此是可行的，而不是註定無法完成。","examples":[{"en":"Is it possible to finish the work today?","zh":"今天能完成這項工作嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With enough practice, it is possible for anyone to improve.","zh":"只要練習足夠，任何人都有可能進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/possible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72231043bc1807e6f740","word":"post","forms":["post"],"officialPos":"n./v./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-62fdb152b75f511d","term":"post","forms":["post","posts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"郵政服務","explanation":"指負責投遞信件和包裹的郵政機構或整套郵政服務；也就是把郵件放進固定的郵遞系統，讓它到達收件地點。","examples":[{"en":"I sent the package by post yesterday.","zh":"我昨天透過郵政寄出了包裹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The letter should arrive by post tomorrow.","zh":"這封信應該明天透過郵政寄到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/post","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e3162f1211ff777","term":"post","forms":["post","posts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路帖子","explanation":"指釋出在論壇、部落格或其他網路平臺上的一條資訊；它把訊息“放到”網上，供別人閱讀或回應。","examples":[{"en":"Her post received hundreds of comments.","zh":"她的帖子收到了數百條評論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wrote a post about our trip.","zh":"我寫了一篇關於我們這次旅行的帖子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/post","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2530dcf8cfc8027","term":"post","forms":["post","posts","posting","posted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寄送郵件","explanation":"指透過郵政系統把信件、包裹等送出去，也就是把物品放進郵遞系統，讓它到達收件人那裡。","examples":[{"en":"She posted a handwritten thank-you letter to her former teacher.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"I need to post this parcel before the post office closes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/post","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eae6a1ffd71fee9e","term":"post","forms":["post","posts","posting","posted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"網上發帖","explanation":"指把文字、問題、圖片等釋出到論壇、部落格或其他網路平臺上，讓其他人看到；這正是把訊息放到網上成為帖子的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The bakery posts its daily specials on social media each morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"He posted a short video showing how to repair the broken hinge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/post","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-61a9ed08e99790ecba38","word":"postage","forms":["postage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdb47bf43af0a502","term":"postage","forms":["postage","postages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"郵資；寄送費用","explanation":"指把信件、包裹等寄出去時需要支付的錢。記住“先付錢才能讓郵件上路”這個畫面，就能把 postage 和郵寄聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"The postage for this package is more than I expected.","zh":"這個包裹的郵資比我預想的高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pay the postage when you send the documents.","zh":"寄這些檔案時請支付郵資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22f0b24b528b0902de75","word":"postcard","forms":["postcard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74c1ff67c6f0a3f8","term":"postcard","forms":["postcard","postcards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"明信片","explanation":"明信片是一張較厚的紙卡，可以在上面寫短訊息和地址，然後通常不裝信封就直接寄出。","examples":[{"en":"I sent my grandparents a postcard from Paris.","zh":"我從巴黎給祖父母寄了一張明信片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a postcard at the museum.","zh":"她在博物館買了一張明信片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postcard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-293b9207228b7854bc3c","word":"poster","forms":["poster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba9f33cd5e143330","term":"poster","forms":["poster","posters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海報；宣傳畫","explanation":"指貼在牆上等地方、用來展示人物、活動、電影或其他內容的大幅圖片或宣傳畫。","examples":[{"en":"There is a poster of my favorite singer above my desk.","zh":"我書桌上方貼著一張我最喜歡的歌手的海報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater put up posters for the new play.","zh":"劇院張貼了宣傳新劇的海報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fcecff165ce7fd07","term":"poster","forms":["poster","posters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宣傳海報","explanation":"指貼在電線杆、牆面、公交車等公共位置上，用來宣傳電影、活動、商品或服務的廣告海報。","examples":[{"en":"I saw a poster for a food festival on the bus.","zh":"我在公交車上看到了一張美食節的宣傳海報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A concert poster covered the café window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b0e87022fa7ec828a2f","word":"postpone(ment)","forms":["postpone","postponement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8879c03bb752c16","term":"postpone","forms":["postpone","postpones","postponing","postponed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推遲；延期","explanation":"把原定要發生的事情往後挪，使它不在原來的時間進行。物件可以是會議、約會、旅行、決定等。","examples":[{"en":"We had to postpone the meeting until Friday.","zh":"我們不得不把會議推遲到星期五。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She postponed making a decision until she had more information.","zh":"她把作決定的時間推遲到獲得更多資訊之後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postpone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0c9ee2087f9cfdf","term":"postponement","forms":["postponement","postponements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"延期；推遲","explanation":"指把原定的審判、會議、比賽或其他程式往後安排，而不是取消它。重點是時間被向後移動，新的時間通常仍會確定或等待確定。","examples":[{"en":"The court granted a postponement of the hearing.","zh":"法院批准了延期審理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy snow forced the postponement of the match.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postponement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-95e53cf467c737c772ed","word":"posture","forms":["posture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22c45f892e80046f","term":"posture","forms":["posture","postures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體姿勢","explanation":"指一個人身體保持或擺出的樣子，包括身體各部分的相對位置和整體姿態。它既可以是自然形成的姿勢，也可以是為了顯得優雅、舒服或引人注意而擺出的姿勢。","examples":[{"en":"Good posture can help you avoid back pain.","zh":"良好的姿勢有助於避免背痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She adjusted her posture before the photograph was taken.","zh":"拍照前她調整了一下姿勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/posture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60e3d36dcb417ef8","term":"posture","forms":["posture","postures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立場；態度","explanation":"指一個人、團體或政府面對某個問題或他人時所採取的態度和社會、政治立場。它可以是實際的立場，也常暗示一種公開表現出來的姿態。","examples":[{"en":"The government adopted a firm posture toward the trade dispute.","zh":"政府對這場貿易爭端採取了堅定的立場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her public posture was friendly, but her actions were less welcoming.","zh":"她公開表現出的態度很友好，但她的行動並沒有那麼歡迎對方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/posture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74a51c3ce9ff02552358","word":"pot","forms":["pot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2b9d17fa39b74a0","term":"pot","forms":["pot","pots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烹飪用鍋","explanation":"指有平底、通常帶敞口的容器，用來在爐子上煮、燉或加熱食物；它正是“裝東西的容器”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Put the soup in a large pot and bring it to a boil.","zh":"把湯倒進一個大鍋裡，煮至沸騰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beans have been cooking in the pot all morning.","zh":"豆子在鍋裡煮了一上午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60bb7ad603a0916c","term":"pot","forms":["pot","pots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賭池；總賭注","explanation":"在賭博或牌局中，指所有參與者押下、最後由贏家贏取的那筆總錢款；它延續了“容器裝東西”的形象，只是容器裡裝的是大家押下的錢，也可比喻為用來吸引人的一筆錢。","examples":[{"en":"The winner took the entire pot after the final round.","zh":"最後一輪結束後，贏家贏走了全部賭池。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They sweetened the pot by offering an extra prize.","zh":"他們增加了額外獎品，讓這項誘因更有吸引力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6f2dbf8f2462c0e","term":"pot","forms":["pot"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大麻","explanation":"指大麻這種毒品或娛樂性藥物；這是一個獨立形成的俚語義，不是“鍋”或“容器”的字面延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The film discusses how teenagers first encountered pot.","zh":"這部電影討論了青少年最初是如何接觸大麻的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was arrested for possessing pot.","zh":"他因持有大麻而被捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3013ddf13bab1a2","term":"pot","forms":["pot","pots","potting","potted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放進鍋裡","explanation":"把某種食物或物品放進鍋中烹煮，也可以指把植物等放進盆或容器裡；這正是“把東西放進容器”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"She potted the plant in a large clay pot.","zh":"她把這株植物栽進了一個大陶盆裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She potted the meat and covered it with stock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e91c254ad58860a02c78","word":"potato","forms":["potato"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af35444a220bd825","term":"potato","forms":["potato","potatoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"土豆；馬鈴薯","explanation":"最常見的意思是馬鈴薯這種植物的地下塊莖，也就是日常吃的土豆；既可以指一顆土豆，也可以指作為食材的土豆。","examples":[{"en":"I baked a potato and served it with butter.","zh":"我烤了一個土豆，配黃油一起吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add the potatoes to the soup and cook them until soft.","zh":"把土豆放進湯裡，煮到變軟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potato","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db3db599de8411637263","word":"potent","forms":["potent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05ae820316bca62c","term":"potent","forms":["potent","more potent","most potent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"強大的；很有效的","explanation":"形容某人、某物或某種力量作用很強，能夠產生明顯甚至強烈的結果。它既可以說實際力量強，也可以說藥物、論據或影響力很有作用。","examples":[{"en":"The new medicine is highly potent.","zh":"這種新藥的藥效非常強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She offered a potent argument against the plan.","zh":"她提出了一個極有力的反對該計劃的論據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7423f9e2d7a58a36","term":"potent","forms":["potent","more potent","most potent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有生殖能力的","explanation":"用於人或動物時，表示具有生育後代的能力，也就是生殖能力正常或很強。這是“有力量並能產生結果”這一核心概念在生殖方面的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor confirmed that he was still potent.","zh":"醫生確認他仍然具有生殖能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tests confirmed that the breeding stallion remained potent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81b6b2c874b787640efa","word":"potential","forms":["potential"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d83295ff5cee8b80","term":"potential","forms":["potential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"潛在的；可能的","explanation":"指某種能力、結果或狀態還沒有真正出現，但條件已經存在，未來可能實現。例如，一個有天賦的孩子可能成為優秀音樂家，所以可以說他是潛在的優秀音樂家。","examples":[{"en":"The new treatment has the potential to save thousands of lives.","zh":"這種新療法有可能挽救數千人的生命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should consider the potential risks before making a decision.","zh":"在作出決定前，我們應該考慮潛在的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ea3a4953e39f493","term":"potential","forms":["potential","potentials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"潛力；發展可能","explanation":"指某人或某事現在還沒有達到某種成就，但具備發展到那一步的能力或機會。它強調“還沒有實現的能力”，所以常用來評價人才、想法、技術或專案。","examples":[{"en":"The young player has the potential to become a national champion.","zh":"這名年輕選手有成為全國冠軍的潛力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This idea has great potential for improving public transport.","zh":"這個想法在改善公共交通方面有很大潛力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-0c2f83b433842710bcd0","word":"pottery","forms":["pottery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b9d72be3cd695db","term":"pottery","forms":["pottery","potteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陶器","explanation":"指用黏土製成並燒製的器物總稱，例如碗、罐、花瓶等。這裡強調一類陶製品，而不是某一件具體器物。","examples":[{"en":"The shelves were lined with pottery of all shapes and sizes.","zh":"架子上擺滿了各種形狀和大小的陶器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a beautiful piece of pottery at the market.","zh":"她在市場上買了一件漂亮的陶器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pottery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5c53b232bd62592","term":"pottery","forms":["pottery","potteries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"製陶藝術","explanation":"指把黏土塑形成器物並燒製出來的工藝或藝術；它和 pottery 的“陶器”意思相連，都是同一套製陶過程的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter has been studying pottery for two years.","zh":"我女兒學習製陶已經兩年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is skilled at pottery and teaches evening classes.","zh":"他很擅長製陶，並教授晚間課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pottery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4fac4f53ef59dba0b660","word":"poultry","forms":["poultry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9b9d1de1e394738","term":"poultry","forms":["poultry","poultries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"家禽","explanation":"指人們飼養來獲取肉、蛋或兩者的家禽總稱，例如雞、鴨、火雞和鵝。重點是“成群飼養、供人食用的禽鳥”，不是某一種鳥的專名。","examples":[{"en":"My uncle is a poultry farmer.","zh":"我叔叔是家禽養殖戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farm raises poultry for local restaurants.","zh":"這家農場為當地餐館飼養家禽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poultry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f073ef4b3c11e8cb","term":"poultry","forms":["poultry","poultries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禽肉","explanation":"在食品、選單或商店語境中，poultry 指雞、鴨、火雞等家禽的肉，即“禽肉”。這裡關注的不是活禽，而是作為食物出售或食用的肉。","examples":[{"en":"The supermarket has a large poultry counter.","zh":"這家超市有一個很大的禽肉櫃檯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cook poultry thoroughly before serving it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poultry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39d77c4bd9a79b5db22c","word":"pound","forms":["pound"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6cef06daa6103b2","term":"pound","forms":["pound","pounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"磅（重量單位）","explanation":"“pound”是多種計量體系中的重量單位，日常英語裡常指約等於四百五十四克的英制磅，具體數值要看使用的體系。它體現了記憶鉤子中的“計量”主線。","examples":[{"en":"The suitcase weighs nearly fifty pounds.","zh":"這個手提箱重將近五十磅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add two pounds of flour to the bowl.","zh":"向碗里加入兩磅麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b83dc1743428a441","term":"pound","forms":["pound","pounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英鎊等貨幣單位","explanation":"“pound”可表示一種貨幣單位，最常見的是英國的英鎊，也可指其他採用這一名稱的貨幣。它延續了記憶鉤子中的“計量”主線，只是計量的是金錢。","examples":[{"en":"The ticket costs twelve pounds.","zh":"這張票要十二英鎊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found a pound coin on the pavement.","zh":"她在人行道上撿到了一枚一英鎊硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55423331c1b5fda4","term":"pound","forms":["pound","pounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈的一擊","explanation":"“pound”可指一次沉重、有力的擊打，強調衝擊力很強。這個意思直接對應記憶鉤子中的“重重地打”。","examples":[{"en":"The boxer landed a powerful pound on his opponent's ribs.","zh":"那名拳擊手重重擊中了對手的肋部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden pound on the door woke everyone up.","zh":"門上突然傳來一記重重的敲擊，把大家都吵醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed29bcecc78d7ffb6724","word":"pour","forms":["pour"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73e1cfa13c463197","term":"pour","forms":["pour","pours","pouring","poured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"倒出；倒入","explanation":"讓液體從一個容器連續流出，或流進另一個容器；可以是人主動倒，也可以描述液體被倒動的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Pour the soup into a bowl and let it cool.","zh":"把湯倒進碗裡，晾涼一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She poured water from the bottle into my glass.","zh":"她把瓶裡的水倒進我的杯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5f08971321aea89","term":"pour","forms":["pour","pours","pouring","poured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"連續湧出；傾瀉","explanation":"主語自己像液體一樣成股流動、湧出或大量落下，不一定有人把它倒出來；雨水是最常見的例子，人群也可這樣移動。","examples":[{"en":"Rain poured down the windows all night.","zh":"雨水整夜沿著窗戶傾瀉而下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sunlight poured through the open door.","zh":"陽光從敞開的門裡傾瀉進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d488fb3b1d651218","term":"pour","forms":["pour","pours","pouring","poured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下大雨","explanation":"表示雨下得很大、很急，彷彿天空在不斷往下倒水；這是日常英語中非常常用的說法。","examples":[{"en":"Take an umbrella—it’s pouring outside.","zh":"帶把傘吧，外面正下著傾盆大雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It started pouring just as we left the station.","zh":"我們剛離開車站，天就開始下大雨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d84afde29cdd0153d2c1","word":"poverty","forms":["poverty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6981838041df409a","term":"poverty","forms":["poverty","poverties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貧窮；貧困","explanation":"指缺少錢和基本生活資源的狀態，也就是“手裡空空”的生活處境。","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people still live in poverty.","zh":"數百萬人仍然生活在貧困中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program aims to reduce poverty in rural areas.","zh":"這個專案旨在減少農村地區的貧困。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poverty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2ac1e24744ca5c5","term":"poverty","forms":["poverty","poverties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺乏；不足","explanation":"把“手裡空空”的概念擴大到其他事物，表示某種需要或想要的東西嚴重不足，例如土壤缺少養分。","examples":[{"en":"The plants grew poorly because of the poverty of the soil.","zh":"這些植物長得不好，因為土壤缺乏養分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report reveals a poverty of original ideas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poverty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e8eb8741d3daa5579df5","word":"powder","forms":["powder"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a41480de7d2b164","term":"powder","forms":["powder","powders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"粉末；塵粉","explanation":"指乾燥物質被搗碎、研磨或自然分解後形成的非常細小的顆粒，是 powder 最基本的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The old paint had turned to powder under the hot sun.","zh":"舊油漆在烈日下已經變成了粉末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add a little baking powder to the flour.","zh":"在麵粉里加入一點泡打粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f19abcd0318eb8fb","term":"powder","forms":["powder","powders","powdering","powdered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"研成粉末","explanation":"指透過搗、磨或摩擦把固體變成細粉，正是“粉末”這一核心概念的動作版本。","examples":[{"en":"Powder the dried herbs before adding them to the soup.","zh":"把幹香草研成粉後再加入湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Powder the dried spices with a pestle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63e03a5eebc4fc3d","term":"powder","forms":["powder","powders","powdering","powdered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撒粉；撲粉","explanation":"指把粉末撒在某物表面，或像撒粉一樣覆蓋在表面上。","examples":[{"en":"Powder the cake with sugar before serving.","zh":"上桌前在蛋糕上撒些糖粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baker powdered the cookies with cinnamon.","zh":"麵包師在餅乾上撒了肉桂粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07d715edb696fb5f628f","word":"power","forms":["power"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59400a44971f7627","term":"power","forms":["power","powers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"做某事的能力","explanation":"power 是使某人能夠做成某事，或使某物能夠發生某種作用的能力。它可以是身體、語言、思考、行動等方面的能力，例如失去說話的能力。","examples":[{"en":"After the accident, she lost the power to walk.","zh":"事故後，她失去了行走的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law gives citizens the power to appeal.","zh":"這項法律賦予公民上訴的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/power","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3683f0c3ae688dbc","term":"power","forms":["power","powers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支配或影響他人的權力","explanation":"這裡的 power 是讓一個人、組織或群體能夠命令、影響或控制別人和局勢的社會力量。它可以來自職位、資源、聲望或人數。","examples":[{"en":"The new leader quickly gained power.","zh":"新領導人很快掌握了權力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Money gives him power over the company.","zh":"金錢使他擁有了控制這家公司的權力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/power","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0b2eca781354d64","term":"power","forms":["power","powers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"力量；能量","explanation":"power 可以是身體、動作或物體產生效果時所表現出的強度。比如擊球需要很大的 power，就是需要很大的力量。","examples":[{"en":"He hit the ball with tremendous power.","zh":"他用巨大的力量擊中了球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine has enough power to lift the load.","zh":"這臺機器有足夠的力量提升這批貨物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/power","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6df84d5883d21989","term":"power","forms":["power","powers","powering","powered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給裝置供電；驅動","explanation":"power 作動詞時，可以把電力或其他能源提供給裝置，使裝置運轉。核心仍是“讓某物獲得使其工作的力量”。","examples":[{"en":"Solar panels power the lights in the garden.","zh":"太陽能電池板為花園裡的燈供電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The radio is powered by two batteries.","zh":"這臺收音機由兩節電池供電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/power","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f00799a7111484d5","term":"power","forms":["power","powers","powering","powered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推動；促成","explanation":"power 可以指某種資源、情感或原因為行動提供動力，使事情得以發展或擴大。這裡的“力量”不是直接打擊，而是從背後推動結果。","examples":[{"en":"The project was powered by donations from local residents.","zh":"這個專案是在當地居民捐款的推動下開展起來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New investment powered the region's rapid recovery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/power","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58c48602d373404d8acf","word":"powerful","forms":["powerful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-345e8deca5da243c","term":"powerful","forms":["powerful","more powerful","most powerful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"強大的；影響力大的","explanation":"表示某人或某物擁有很強的力量、能力或影響力，能夠明顯改變局面或影響他人。它既能形容實際力量，也能形容情感、藥物、演講等抽象作用。","examples":[{"en":"The new engine is powerful enough to pull the heavy trailer.","zh":"這臺新發動機動力很強，足以拉動那輛重拖車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a powerful speech about protecting the environment.","zh":"她發表了一場很有感染力的環保演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powerful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-339a55679c505255","term":"powerful","forms":["powerful","more powerful","most powerful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"論證力強的；能推出重要結論的","explanation":"形容思想、理論、方法或論證具有很強的解釋力和推導力，能夠支援許多重要結論。這裡的“力量”不是物理力量，而是邏輯或思想上的力量。","examples":[{"en":"This is a powerful argument for investing in public transportation.","zh":"這是一個支援投資公共交通的有力論據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theorem provides a powerful tool for proving convergence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powerful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e57a032cdd10dec9769","word":"practical","forms":["practical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e857896ffb5bad8b","term":"practical","forms":["practical","more practical","most practical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"實踐性的；非理論的","explanation":"指知識或能力建立在親自操作和現實經驗上，而不是隻停留在理論、假設或書本討論中。它強調“做過、用得上”的一面。","examples":[{"en":"She has practical experience repairing bicycles.","zh":"她有修理腳踏車的實踐經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course gives students practical training in first aid.","zh":"這門課為學生提供急救實踐訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/practical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0113625476b980b4","term":"practical","forms":["practical","more practical","most practical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"實用的；可行的","explanation":"指某個辦法、知識或建議能在真實情況下有效發揮作用，能夠解決問題或被真正採用。它從“親自實踐”進一步強調了現實中的效果和用途。","examples":[{"en":"We need a practical solution that works with our limited budget.","zh":"我們需要一個在預算有限的情況下也行得通的實用方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her practical advice helped me fix the problem quickly.","zh":"她實用的建議幫助我很快解決了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/practical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ada750e3f8464e9e1fd6","word":"practice","forms":["practice"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb944c8e3fc44706","term":"practice","forms":["practice","practices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"練習；訓練","explanation":"指為了提高某種技能而反覆進行的活動，重點是“透過不斷做而變得更熟練”。","examples":[{"en":"She needs more practice before she plays the song in public.","zh":"她還需要多練習，才能在公眾面前演奏這首歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular practice is the best way to improve your pronunciation.","zh":"經常練習是改善發音的最好方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/practice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0bb9c38b678d058","term":"practice","forms":["practice","practices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慣例；習慣做法","explanation":"指個人、群體或機構一貫採用的行為方式，也就是“通常都這樣做”的慣例。","examples":[{"en":"It is common practice to confirm the appointment by email.","zh":"透過電子郵件確認預約是常見做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company changed its practice of holding meetings on Friday afternoons.","zh":"公司改變了週五下午開會的慣例。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/practice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a7b65357391c991","term":"practice","forms":["practice","practices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實際應用；實踐","explanation":"指把理論、計劃或原則真正用於現實情況中的做法和效果，和抽象的理論相對。","examples":[{"en":"The plan sounds simple in theory, but it is difficult in practice.","zh":"這個計劃理論上聽起來很簡單，但實際執行起來很難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students learn how to apply the rules in practice.","zh":"學生學習如何在實際中運用這些規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/practice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8111196297d6c5de5c20","word":"practitioner","forms":["practitioner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c49ae38c621a246d","term":"practitioner","forms":["practitioner","practitioners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專業從業者","explanation":"指長期實踐某種職業或藝術的人，尤其指法律、醫學等專業領域的從業者。重點不只是擁有某種身份，而是實際從事並運用這門專業。","examples":[{"en":"She is a highly respected practitioner of family medicine.","zh":"她是一位備受尊敬的家庭醫學從業者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conference brought together legal practitioners from across the country.","zh":"這次會議彙集了來自全國各地的法律從業者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/practitioner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dbf236336f1c400","term":"practitioner","forms":["practitioner","practitioners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慣常參與者","explanation":"泛指經常從事某種活動、信仰或做法的人。這裡不一定是正式職業，只要這個人長期、習慣性地實踐某件事，就可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"The workshop was attended by practitioners of traditional meditation.","zh":"參加這次講習會的是一些長期實踐傳統冥想的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A seasoned practitioner of deception, he forged convincing references.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/practitioner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-154d763b6a255621fa9b","word":"praise","forms":["praise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6067e6680e3d08d6","term":"praise","forms":["praise","praises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"稱讚；讚揚","explanation":"指用肯定、讚揚的話評價某人或某物，強調把對方的優點說出來或傳播出去。它可以指讚揚這種行為，也可以指具體的讚美之詞。","examples":[{"en":"The new restaurant received widespread praise for its friendly service.","zh":"這家新餐館因服務熱情而廣受稱讚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her careful explanation earned praise from the whole team.","zh":"她解釋得很仔細，得到了整個團隊的讚揚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/praise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa6903e292d6509b","term":"praise","forms":["praise","praises","praising","praised","praisest","praisedst","praiseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"稱讚；讚美；頌揚","explanation":"指主動說出對某人、某物的肯定，或表達對神的讚美。它把名詞所表示的“讚揚”變成一個動作，可以根據語境譯為“表揚”“稱讚”或“頌揚”。","examples":[{"en":"The manager praised Maya for solving the problem so quickly.","zh":"經理稱讚瑪雅這麼快就解決了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people praise the film for its honest portrayal of family life.","zh":"許多人稱讚這部電影真實地呈現了家庭生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/praise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3cf48f3ba37d1157ddb7","word":"pray","forms":["pray"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9e9fba504ff7301","term":"pray","forms":["pray","prays","praying","prayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"祈禱；禱告","explanation":"指向神明或更高力量表達敬意、感謝，或請求幫助；核心畫面就是把願望鄭重地交託給神明。","examples":[{"en":"They pray for peace every evening.","zh":"他們每天晚上都為和平祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prayed to God for strength.","zh":"她向上帝祈求力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba9f71348659d4a1","term":"pray","forms":["pray","prays","praying","prayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懇求；求助","explanation":"把對神明的鄭重祈求轉向人時，pray 表示謙卑而認真地請求某人提供幫助、時間或行動。","examples":[{"en":"I pray you to give me one more chance.","zh":"我懇求你再給我一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He prayed for help when the boat began to sink.","zh":"船開始下沉時，他懇求有人幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25fe36108392295ccc16","word":"prayer","forms":["prayer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a265f951e57e8e24","term":"prayer","forms":["prayer","prayers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祈禱活動","explanation":"指人向自己的神或某種精神力量溝通、祈求或尋求指引這一整套活動，重點是“向更高力量開口”。","examples":[{"en":"Through prayer, I ask God for guidance.","zh":"我透過祈禱請求上帝指引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finds comfort in prayer during difficult times.","zh":"困難時期，祈禱給她帶來安慰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prayer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1eb7482b4f4b4631","term":"prayer","forms":["prayer","prayers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次祈禱","explanation":"指一次具體完成的祈禱行為，是“祈禱活動”這個整體中的一個單獨時刻或行動。","examples":[{"en":"We said a short prayer before the meal.","zh":"吃飯前我們做了一次簡短的祈禱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her prayer asked for the safe return of every fisherman.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prayer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b28020c52116a16","term":"prayer","forms":["prayer","prayers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"請求；祈求","explanation":"指向有權力的人或機構提出的正式請求，像是把原本向神的祈求轉向世俗的聽者。","examples":[{"en":"The defendant's prayer was that the court dismiss the charges.","zh":"被告請求法院撤銷指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prisoners' prayer for mercy went unanswered.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prayer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83e14e05271a0cfc859e","word":"preach","forms":["preach"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2dec23877d187826","term":"preach","forms":["preach","preaches","preaching","preached","praught"],"pos":"verb","zh":"講道","explanation":"指牧師或其他宗教人士發表佈道，向聽眾講解宗教信仰和道德教訓。這是 preach 最基本、最具體的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The minister preached at the village church on Sunday.","zh":"牧師星期天在村裡的教堂講道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has preached for more than twenty years.","zh":"她講道已經二十多年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b02ae5b0513f5eb1","term":"preach","forms":["preach","preaches","preaching","preached","praught"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鄭重勸告","explanation":"指反覆而認真地勸別人採取某種做法，彷彿在臺上講道理一樣；它比普通的“建議”更有強調和說服的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She is always preaching patience, but she loses her temper first.","zh":"她總是在勸別人要有耐心，可她自己卻最先發脾氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My parents preached the value of hard work.","zh":"我的父母反覆強調努力工作的價值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e42752764d383da1eab","word":"precaution","forms":["precaution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0b030924429181a","term":"precaution","forms":["precaution","precautions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預防措施","explanation":"指為提前擋住危險、損失或失敗而採取的具體行動，例如檢查裝置、戴防護用品或避開風險；這是最常見、最實用的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We took precautions against accidents before opening the site.","zh":"開放這個場地前，我們採取了防止事故的措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a precaution, she saved a copy of the document.","zh":"作為預防措施，她儲存了一份檔案副本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precaution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2434b1ebb24e6f72","term":"precaution","forms":["precaution","precautions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事先的謹慎防範","explanation":"指人在事情發生前已經保持警惕、採取小心做法，從而避免不幸或幫助事情順利進行；重點是“提前小心”。","examples":[{"en":"Her quick precaution saved the team from a serious mistake.","zh":"她及時採取的防範措施使團隊避免了一個嚴重錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a precaution, we unplugged every appliance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precaution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0dc0a1cc0af70cd7ac0c","word":"precede","forms":["precede"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ff9eae83e8740a1","term":"precede","forms":["precede","precedes","preceding","preceded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"先於；在前面","explanation":"表示某人或某事在時間、位置或順序上先出現，像走在隊伍前面一樣。它可以描述事件發生的先後，也可以描述空間位置上的前後。","examples":[{"en":"A loud warning preceded the earthquake.","zh":"地震發生前傳來了一聲響亮的警報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide preceded the group into the cave.","zh":"導遊走在隊伍前面進入了山洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precede","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aac6f77508eb3000f7cf","word":"precedent","forms":["precedent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bd4447266950a32","term":"precedent","forms":["precedent","precedents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先例；前例","explanation":"指過去發生過的一件事，它可以成為後來處理相似情況時的參考。這個意思不一定限於法律，組織決定、社會行為和日常做法也可以形成先例。","examples":[{"en":"The decision could set a dangerous precedent for future cases.","zh":"這個決定可能會為今後的案件開一個危險的先例。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is no precedent for closing the school during a heat wave.","zh":"在熱浪期間關閉學校沒有先例可循。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precedent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15302db16ea9bfd2","term":"precedent","forms":["precedent","precedents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律判例","explanation":"指法院已經作出的判決，後來處理相似案件時可以引用它來支援某種法律判斷。這是“先例”在法律領域中的具體形式。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyers cited a previous precedent to support their argument.","zh":"律師引用了一個先前的判例來支援他們的論點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge cited a precedent from an earlier appeal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precedent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-157fc55121ab2c59852c","word":"precious","forms":["precious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00a2574cf22e8461","term":"precious","forms":["precious","more precious","most precious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"珍貴的；價值很高的","explanation":"指價值、重要性或稀有程度很高，值得珍惜；價值不一定只體現在金錢上，也可以是時間、機會或生命。","examples":[{"en":"Water is our most precious resource.","zh":"水是我們最珍貴的資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kept the precious letter in a small wooden box.","zh":"她把那封珍貴的信放在一個小木盒裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82d346ee12fe280d","term":"precious","forms":["precious","more precious","most precious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"珍愛的；惹人憐愛的","explanation":"表示因為愛、親近或柔情而覺得某人或某物特別可愛、值得珍惜，重點是感情而不只是價值。","examples":[{"en":"Your little daughter is absolutely precious.","zh":"你的小女兒真是可愛極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This photo is precious to me because my grandmother took it.","zh":"這張照片對我來說很珍貴，因為它是我祖母拍的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-704a1142c7056b69b9b5","word":"precise","forms":["precise"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93cf31894812af47","term":"precise","forms":["precise","more precise","preciser","most precise","precisest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精確明確","explanation":"它表示說法、記憶、數字或範圍劃得很細，具體到不容易和其他可能情況混淆；這種細緻本身不保證內容一定正確。","examples":[{"en":"The witness gave a precise description of the car.","zh":"目擊者對那輛車作了非常具體的描述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please be precise about the date and location.","zh":"請把日期和地點說準確、說具體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa228c289732f1da","term":"precise","forms":["precise","more precise","preciser","most precise","precisest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"彼此集中一致","explanation":"在科學或工程語境中，它表示多次測量或多個結果彼此靠得很近、很一致；這些結果即使很集中，也可能整體偏離真實值。","examples":[{"en":"The new instrument gives more precise measurements.","zh":"這臺新儀器給出的測量結果彼此更一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archer's shots were precise, clustering around the center.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68c2f9ee314749c05c96","word":"precision","forms":["precision"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a401b1f27e7dad9f","term":"precision","forms":["precision","precisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精確；準確","explanation":"指把數值、位置或動作做到既準確又細緻的狀態，也就是那把尺子所代表的整體品質。","examples":[{"en":"The precision of the measurements improved after the machine was calibrated.","zh":"機器校準後，測量的精確度提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He cut the paper with remarkable precision.","zh":"他以驚人的精準度把紙剪開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/precision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9499e6aeffb2f5998ccd","word":"predator","forms":["predator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7282d4e2ea4698b1","term":"predator","forms":["predator","predators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捕食者","explanation":"指會追捕並殺死其他非植物生物、主要靠吃它們獲取食物的動物或其他生物。老虎捕鹿、青蛙捕昆蟲，都可以用這個詞來概括。","examples":[{"en":"The fox is a natural predator of rabbits.","zh":"狐狸是兔子的天敵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These birds help control insect predators in the garden.","zh":"這些鳥有助於控制花園裡的害蟲捕食者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/predator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4056eaec4b8d58ae","term":"predator","forms":["predator","predators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攻擊掠奪者","explanation":"比喻以攻擊、剝削或掠奪他人為獲利手段的人；這裡保留了“盯住目標並奪取利益”的捕獵形象。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation exposed a group of financial predators targeting elderly investors.","zh":"調查揭露了一群專門盯上老年投資者的金融掠奪者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Online predators may exploit trusting young users.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/predator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc2eed9acce3fcde24f3","word":"predecessor","forms":["predecessor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bef770ddb11127e","term":"predecessor","forms":["predecessor","predecessors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前任；前人","explanation":"指在同一個職位、角色或位置上先於某人、後來由某人接替的人。核心畫面是“前面那一棒已經交給後面的人”，所以它既可以指正式職位的前任，也可以泛指某人之前擔任該角色的人。","examples":[{"en":"The new director met with her predecessor to discuss the transition.","zh":"新任主管與她的前任見面，討論交接事宜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unlike his predecessor, he welcomes questions from the staff.","zh":"與他的前任不同，他歡迎員工提問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/predecessor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18debae9a528d7f9","term":"predecessor","forms":["predecessor","predecessors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"前身；舊型號","explanation":"指某種產品、機器或系統的較早版本，是後來版本的發展基礎。這裡不是說它只是“舊東西”，而是說後來的型號或設計是在它的基礎上發展出來的。","examples":[{"en":"This compact camera was the predecessor of the company's most popular model.","zh":"這款小型相機是該公司最暢銷型號的前身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new model consumes less power than its predecessor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/predecessor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e9afe9d1df3927e713c","word":"predict","forms":["predict"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03627c29609c5703","term":"predict","forms":["predict","predicts","predicting","predicted","predictest","predictedst","predicteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預測；預言","explanation":"根據已有知識、證據或推理判斷未來會發生什麼；也可以指憑神秘力量預言未來，但日常使用主要是前一種意思。","examples":[{"en":"Experts predict that house prices will rise next year.","zh":"專家預測明年房價會上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one could predict the outcome of the election.","zh":"沒人能預測這次選舉的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/predict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-071a9cdf1b7f16e2","term":"predict","forms":["predict","predicts","predicting","predicted","predictest","predictedst","predicteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預示；意味著","explanation":"主語不是人在做預測，而是理論、資料或某種模式提前顯示可能出現的結果，像是從規律中“說出”答案。","examples":[{"en":"The model predicts a sharp increase in demand.","zh":"這個模型預示需求會大幅增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These early sales figures predict a strong summer season.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/predict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70ad7b8f9a1c6c89a3cc","word":"prediction","forms":["prediction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b94b00ec086fe32e","term":"prediction","forms":["prediction","predictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對未來的預測","explanation":"指根據已有資訊、經驗或判斷，說出未來可能發生的事情。重點是“提前作出判斷”，不保證一定會實現。","examples":[{"en":"The scientist made a prediction about the next decade.","zh":"這位科學家對未來十年作出了預測。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her prediction that prices would rise came true.","zh":"她關於價格會上漲的預測實現了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prediction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa7e9fa6192b7fde","term":"prediction","forms":["prediction","predictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統計機率估計","explanation":"在數學、科學或資料分析中，指模型根據資料估算某個結果出現的可能性。這裡的 prediction 仍然是在“提前看未來”，只是依據從個人判斷變成了統計方法。","examples":[{"en":"The model's prediction of rainfall was based on years of data.","zh":"這個模型對降雨的預測以多年的資料為依據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The model's prediction assigns each outcome a probability.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prediction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-472dc7749c49f123491f","word":"prefer","forms":["prefer"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3fa6221b8c928d4","term":"prefer","forms":["prefer","prefers","preferring","preferred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"更喜歡；偏愛","explanation":"表示在兩個或多個選擇中把一個放在前面，覺得它更合意或更喜歡。它既可以說穩定的個人偏好，也可以說某一次選擇。","examples":[{"en":"I prefer tea to coffee.","zh":"比起咖啡，我更喜歡茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prefers to walk rather than take the bus.","zh":"她寧願步行，也不願坐公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prefer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b19ca937ead2957","term":"prefer","forms":["prefer","prefers","preferring","preferred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向權威提交；提出指控","explanation":"表示把請求、申訴或指控遞到有權處理的人或機構面前，讓對方正式受理。如今最常見於正式或法律表達“提出指控”。","examples":[{"en":"The police decided to prefer charges against the suspect.","zh":"警方決定對嫌疑人提出指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police preferred charges against the company director.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prefer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc5ece60fff82ba42305","word":"preference","forms":["preference"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c40333afa64267e2","term":"preference","forms":["preference","preferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偏好；選擇傾向","explanation":"指在幾個物件或做法中更傾向於選擇其中一個，重點是“更喜歡這一項”。它可以是個人口味，也可以是對某種做法的穩定選擇。","examples":[{"en":"She has a preference for quiet restaurants.","zh":"她偏愛安靜的餐廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you have a preference for tea or coffee?","zh":"你更喜歡茶還是咖啡？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4b2133600fa4157","term":"preference","forms":["preference","preferences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偏好設定；所選選項","explanation":"指已經選定、可以應用的具體選項，尤其常見於軟體、服務或表格中的個人設定。這裡的 preference 不只是“喜歡”，而是系統可以按照它來執行的選擇。","examples":[{"en":"You can change your notification preferences in the app.","zh":"你可以在應用中更改通知偏好設定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The website remembers my language preference.","zh":"這個網站會記住我的語言偏好設定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1d6a553546aa7a96824","word":"pregnancy","forms":["pregnancy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e05433aef0fb62a9","term":"pregnancy","forms":["pregnancy","pregnancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懷孕狀態；一次懷孕","explanation":"指女性體內正在孕育胎兒的狀態，也可以指一次具體的懷孕經歷。這裡關注的是“她現在懷孕了”這一狀態，而不是整個過程的時間長短。","examples":[{"en":"Her pregnancy was confirmed by a doctor.","zh":"醫生確認她懷孕了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They announced her pregnancy last week.","zh":"他們上週宣佈了她懷孕的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pregnancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-79e2e62e4e7773a4","term":"pregnancy","forms":["pregnancy","pregnancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"孕期；懷孕的一段時間","explanation":"指懷孕狀態持續的那段時間，也就是通常所說的孕期。重點從“懷孕這個狀態”轉到“這個狀態持續了多久或發生在什麼時候”。","examples":[{"en":"She avoided raw fish during her pregnancy.","zh":"她懷孕期間避免吃生魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She continued teaching throughout her pregnancy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pregnancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-376be72e38bba9182802","word":"pregnant","forms":["pregnant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6616238d2523ebd1","term":"pregnant","forms":["pregnant","more pregnant","most pregnant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"懷孕的","explanation":"指女性或雌性動物體內正在孕育發育中的孩子或幼崽，即處於懷孕狀態。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is pregnant with her first child.","zh":"我姐姐懷上了她的第一個孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is eight months pregnant and still working.","zh":"她已經懷孕八個月了，但仍在工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pregnant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14ce0780320fc041","term":"pregnant","forms":["pregnant","more pregnant","most pregnant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"意味深長的；蘊含可能性的","explanation":"把“孕育孩子”的形象轉用於話語、停頓、局勢等：表面上沒有立刻顯現，卻包含重要意義、暗示或發展可能。","examples":[{"en":"After the question, there was a pregnant pause.","zh":"這個問題之後出現了一陣意味深長的停頓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement was pregnant with possibilities for future cooperation.","zh":"這項協議蘊含著未來合作的多種可能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pregnant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac4532a6701899f44859","word":"prehistoric","forms":["prehistoric"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cfd56b10c989537","term":"prehistoric","forms":["prehistoric","more prehistoric","most prehistoric"],"pos":"adj","zh":"文字記錄以前的","explanation":"指有文字記錄以前的時期、文化或生物；它描繪的是文字歷史尚未開始的世界，是這個詞最基本、最嚴格的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists discovered prehistoric tools near the cave.","zh":"考古學家在洞穴附近發現了史前工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has an exhibition about prehistoric animals.","zh":"這家博物館舉辦了一個關於史前動物的展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prehistoric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-becf0f3ddb620adf","term":"prehistoric","forms":["prehistoric","more prehistoric","most prehistoric"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古老得離譜的；過時的","explanation":"借“像來自文字出現以前的世界”這個畫面，誇張地形容某物非常古老、落後或已經過時；不一定是在進行嚴格的歷史判斷。","examples":[{"en":"This computer is so prehistoric that it cannot even run the new software.","zh":"這臺電腦老舊得像史前的，連新軟體都執行不了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That prehistoric computer takes minutes to open a file.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prehistoric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14a62b33decfa1b79645","word":"prejudice","forms":["prejudice"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-772f7216e8509c67","term":"prejudice","forms":["prejudice","prejudices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先入之見","explanation":"指人在沒有充分了解事實前就形成的不利判斷或看法，因此容易對人或事作出不公平的評價。它是 prejudice 最基本的概念。","examples":[{"en":"Her decision was influenced by prejudice rather than by the evidence.","zh":"她的決定受先入之見影響，而不是受證據影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Prejudice can prevent people from judging others fairly.","zh":"偏見會妨礙人們公平地評價他人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prejudice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cee298305a405da","term":"prejudice","forms":["prejudice","prejudices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對群體的敵意偏見","explanation":"特指對某個種族、宗教、性別或其他群體的不合理恐懼、敵意或厭惡，是“有色眼鏡”最嚴重、最常見的社會意義。","examples":[{"en":"The organization works to combat racial prejudice in the workplace.","zh":"這個組織致力於消除職場中的種族偏見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign challenges prejudice against disabled people.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prejudice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d957d195b24fbaf6","term":"prejudice","forms":["prejudice","prejudices","prejudicing","prejudiced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"損害；使處於不利地位","explanation":"指某件事使某人的機會、立場或利益受到不利影響，就像有色眼鏡讓別人無法公平看待他一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The delay could prejudice her chances of getting the job.","zh":"這次延誤可能會損害她獲得這份工作的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report was released early and prejudiced the fairness of the trial.","zh":"報告過早公佈，損害了審判的公正性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prejudice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e7546ed18407142890e","word":"preliminary","forms":["preliminary"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da4c71344a3cc1f6","term":"preliminary","forms":["preliminary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"初步的；準備性的","explanation":"指正式結論、行動或主要內容出現以前的階段性內容；它像站在門檻前，先提供準備或初步資訊，而不是最終結果。","examples":[{"en":"The preliminary results look promising.","zh":"初步結果看起來很有希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We held a preliminary meeting before the conference.","zh":"我們在會議正式開始前舉行了一次準備會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preliminary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f506fe96d513862","term":"preliminary","forms":["preliminary","preliminaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"準備；開場","explanation":"指主要事情開始前必須做的準備、鋪墊或介紹，相當於先站在門檻前安排好進入正題所需的一切。","examples":[{"en":"After the preliminaries, the speaker finally addressed the main issue.","zh":"完成開場準備後，發言人終於談到了主要問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We finished the preliminaries and signed the agreement.","zh":"我們完成了準備工作，然後簽署了協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preliminary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bffcfe6a19a03f7206f","word":"premature","forms":["premature"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9b1e72741599093","term":"premature","forms":["premature","more premature","most premature"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未成熟就發生的","explanation":"事情在應有的成熟或準備階段到來之前就發生了，因此顯得太早、不夠成熟。例如，胎兒尚未足月就出生，就是 premature。","examples":[{"en":"The doctors were prepared for a premature birth.","zh":"醫生們已為早產做好準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The premature fruit drop worried the orchard owner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-336a62cf4b2fa806","term":"premature","forms":["premature","more premature","most premature"],"pos":"adj","zh":"時機過早的","explanation":"某事早於預期、準備妥當或人們希望的時間發生，因而現在做或說還不合適。比如證據不足時宣佈結論，就是 premature。","examples":[{"en":"It would be premature to celebrate before the results are confirmed.","zh":"結果確認之前就慶祝還為時過早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It would be premature to announce a winner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-672a81ef923ec75d16b0","word":"premier","forms":["premier"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cbed9d9d776a8ea3","term":"premier","forms":["premier"],"pos":"adj","zh":"首要的；頂尖的","explanation":"指在質量、地位或重要性上居首、最值得重視的事物，像站在“最前面”的位置一樣。","examples":[{"en":"She studied at one of the country's premier universities.","zh":"她就讀於該國最頂尖的大學之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city is home to a premier science museum.","zh":"這座城市擁有一座頂尖的科學博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-866735a560b65f96","term":"premier","forms":["premier","premiers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"議會制政府首腦","explanation":"指在議會制政府中領導內閣、主持政府工作的最高行政負責人；這裡的核心仍是“站在政府權力最前面的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The premier announced a new plan for public transport.","zh":"政府首腦宣佈了一項新的公共交通計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The premier met with opposition leaders after the vote.","zh":"投票結束後，政府首腦會見了反對黨領導人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7518cc15100be58c012","word":"premiere","forms":["premiere"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c20c0f83aceabe43","term":"premiere","forms":["premiere","premieres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"首映；首演","explanation":"指電影、戲劇等作品第一次向公眾放映或演出，通常是一個受到特別關注的正式活動。核心畫面就是作品第一次在觀眾面前亮相。","examples":[{"en":"The film's premiere attracted actors, critics, and fans.","zh":"這部電影的首映吸引了演員、評論家和影迷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We attended the premiere of her new play last night.","zh":"昨晚我們參加了她新戲的首演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premiere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-851e5febf379cdba","term":"premiere","forms":["premiere","premieres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"首播；首集","explanation":"指電視節目或某一季節目第一次播出的那一集，是這個節目在螢幕上的第一次亮相。它也可以指這次首播本身。","examples":[{"en":"The season premiere drew more viewers than expected.","zh":"這一季的首集吸引的觀眾比預期更多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The season premiere attracted a record audience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premiere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d68e3ec2d5ff0cb32153","word":"premise","forms":["premise"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3fdb72a816813b0","term":"premise","forms":["premise","premises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"論證前提；預先假定","explanation":"指在進一步推理之前先提出或接受的命題、條件或假設；後面的結論是否成立，往往取決於這個基礎是否可靠。","examples":[{"en":"The argument rests on the premise that everyone has equal access to education.","zh":"這個論證建立在人人都能平等接受教育這一前提上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If that premise is false, the whole argument falls apart.","zh":"如果那個前提是錯誤的，整個論證就站不住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9490a0ceaee8ae3a","term":"premise","forms":["premise","premises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事基本構想","explanation":"指電影、小說或電視節目的基本設定和驅動情節的核心想法，即創作者先提出的“如果……會怎樣”的故事基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The film's premise is simple: a child discovers that her new neighbor is a time traveler.","zh":"這部電影的基本設定很簡單：一個孩子發現新鄰居是時間旅行者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film's premise involves two strangers exchanging identities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-870dc23d21836b97b58a","word":"premium","forms":["premium"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a302f5a2f7f917f","term":"premium","forms":["premium","premiums","premia"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險費","explanation":"為保險保障定期或一次性支付的金額；這是“為了獲得額外保障而付出的費用”。","examples":[{"en":"My monthly insurance premium has gone up.","zh":"我的每月保險費上漲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We pay the annual premium by direct debit.","zh":"我們透過直接借記支付年度保費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d6f04754f9f8c5464cb","word":"preparation","forms":["preparation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27fc085566bab18b","term":"preparation","forms":["preparation","preparations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"準備；籌備","explanation":"指為即將發生的事情而進行的準備過程，例如整理資料、練習或安排所需物品。重點是“正在把事情準備好”這一行動。","examples":[{"en":"I reviewed my notes in preparation for the interview.","zh":"我複習了筆記，為面試做準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team spent weeks preparing for the exhibition.","zh":"團隊花了幾個星期為展覽做準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preparation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66568e17775502c2","term":"preparation","forms":["preparation","preparations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"準備就緒；有備狀態","explanation":"指經過準備後所處的狀態，也就是已經做好應對某事的條件，而不是準備本身的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Good preparation gave her confidence before the performance.","zh":"充分的準備讓她在演出前充滿信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Months of preparation left the team ready for anything.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preparation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45666d976bab316d970e","word":"prepare","forms":["prepare"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63564b8004edfe1a","term":"prepare","forms":["prepare","prepares","preparing","prepared","preparest","preparedst","prepareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"準備好某物","explanation":"表示提前處理、安排或裝備某樣東西，使它能用於特定的將來目的；物件可以是裝置、材料、場地或計劃。","examples":[{"en":"The team prepared the equipment for the long journey.","zh":"團隊為這次長途旅行準備好了裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please prepare the room for the meeting.","zh":"請為會議準備好房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prepare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01d58757d1e4c95f","term":"prepare","forms":["prepare","prepares","preparing","prepared","preparest","preparedst","prepareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為將來做好準備","explanation":"表示人或群體提前調整狀態、安排事務，以便應對將來的事件；焦點在“做好面對某事的準備”。","examples":[{"en":"We are preparing for a difficult exam.","zh":"我們正在為一場很難的考試做準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prepared herself to speak in front of the audience.","zh":"她讓自己做好了在觀眾面前發言的準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prepare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ce34a94e412486a6533","word":"prescribe","forms":["prescribe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed691597138e5868","term":"prescribe","forms":["prescribe","prescribes","prescribing","prescribed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開藥；開具治療用品","explanation":"指有資質的醫生等為特定病人正式開出藥物或醫療器械。可以把它想成醫生把“該用什麼”預先寫進處方中。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor prescribed a short course of antibiotics for Maya.","zh":"醫生給瑪雅開了一個療程的抗生素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor prescribed a different inhaler.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prescribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae21316b0b7006df","term":"prescribe","forms":["prescribe","prescribes","prescribing","prescribed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"規定；明確要求","explanation":"指以書面或權威方式規定某種程式、儀式、標準或行動準則，要求人們照此執行。這和醫生開藥共享同一個畫面：把應當做什麼預先寫定。","examples":[{"en":"The safety manual prescribes a check before every flight.","zh":"安全手冊規定每次飛行前都必須進行檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The regulations prescribe minimum standards for food storage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prescribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-758768c3ca261d8585e6","word":"prescription","forms":["prescription"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c1a1ce1aa7ddb88","term":"prescription","forms":["prescription","prescriptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫生處方","explanation":"醫生或其他有資格的醫療人員寫下的用藥、治療或配鏡指示，供藥房或相關機構據此提供治療。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor gave me a prescription for antibiotics.","zh":"醫生給我開了抗生素處方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need a prescription to buy this medicine.","zh":"買這種藥需要處方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prescription","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2eec75330b4031db","term":"prescription","forms":["prescription","prescriptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"處方藥或處方治療","explanation":"指按照處方獲得的藥物或治療本身，而不是寫下這些內容的那張單子。","examples":[{"en":"I picked up my prescriptions at the pharmacy after work.","zh":"我下班後在藥房取了我的處方藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My prescription is waiting at the pharmacy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prescription","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dff0669b4df441c26626","word":"presence","forms":["presence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-588dc0cdab4bdffb","term":"presence","forms":["presence","presences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"在場；存在","explanation":"指某人或某物確實在某處，或就在視線、聽覺能夠觸及的範圍內。這是 presence 最基本的意思：某種東西“就在這裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The presence of a guide made the visitors feel safer.","zh":"有導遊在場讓遊客感到更安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We noticed the presence of several birds in the garden.","zh":"我們注意到花園裡有幾隻鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62e26ac367d824ee","term":"presence","forms":["presence","presences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身邊；面前的範圍","explanation":"指一個人身邊、面前或能夠直接感知到的空間範圍。重點不只是“人在不在”，而是某件事發生在這個人在場的範圍內。","examples":[{"en":"Please do not discuss private matters in the presence of children.","zh":"請不要當著孩子的面討論私事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became unusually quiet in his presence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-4d4c7eee2e28d03cb2db","word":"present","forms":["present"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30a4b233a397bb84","term":"present","forms":["present","more present","most present"],"pos":"adj","zh":"現在的；當前的","explanation":"指時間上屬於現在或當前階段的事物，彷彿把這個時間放到了眼前。","examples":[{"en":"We must focus on the present situation.","zh":"我們必須關注當前的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rule remains in effect to the present day.","zh":"這項規定至今仍然有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/present","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-259b405c1e5e549d","term":"present","forms":["present","presents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現在；當前時期","explanation":"指眼下這一時刻或當前這段時期，也就是被放到眼前的時間。","examples":[{"en":"It is important to live in the present.","zh":"活在當下很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At present, the project has no clear deadline.","zh":"目前，這個專案還沒有明確的截止日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/present","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d19d570916fcf6dc","term":"present","forms":["present","presents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禮物","explanation":"指在生日、節日或其他特殊場合送給別人的東西，像是把某物放到對方眼前作為心意。","examples":[{"en":"She bought her brother a birthday present.","zh":"她給弟弟買了一份生日禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were excited to open their presents.","zh":"孩子們興奮地開啟他們的禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/present","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a05e4553030195fb","term":"present","forms":["present","presents","presenting","presented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"展示；提出","explanation":"指把實物、資訊或觀點放到別人眼前，使其能夠看見、瞭解或加以考慮；這正是“把某物放到眼前”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"She presented the results to the research team.","zh":"她向研究團隊展示了結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He presented a clear plan for reducing costs.","zh":"他提出了一項清晰的降本計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/present","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bfac314fefdc07451af1","word":"presentation","forms":["presentation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c023ac2f3948fe60","term":"presentation","forms":["presentation","presentations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"呈現；展示","explanation":"泛指把想法、資訊、作品或其他內容呈現給別人，也可以指呈現出來的內容或形式；演講和幻燈片都是這種“擺到別人面前”的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"The presentation of the new design was clear and convincing.","zh":"對新設計的展示清楚而有說服力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her presentation of the evidence changed the committee's view.","zh":"她對證據的呈現改變了委員會的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presentation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d73a79e21cae4b1","term":"presentation","forms":["presentation","presentations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演講；報告","explanation":"指在聽眾面前有準備地講解資訊、觀點或研究成果，是最常見的“把內容呈現給大家”的場景之一。","examples":[{"en":"I have to give a presentation on climate change tomorrow.","zh":"我明天必須做一個關於氣候變化的演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her presentation explains the findings without technical jargon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presentation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e8e8a8d6e788cc2","term":"presentation","forms":["presentation","presentations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簡報；幻燈片","explanation":"指用電腦製作、通常配合演講使用的一組幻燈片或簡報；它是把資訊呈現出來的具體工具。","examples":[{"en":"I sent the presentation to everyone before the meeting.","zh":"我在會議前把簡報發給了所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Email me the presentation before tomorrow's meeting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presentation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad3d7f7f6acda5454d41","word":"preservation","forms":["preservation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e13f4f36a88c45c","term":"preservation","forms":["preservation","preservations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護；儲存行為","explanation":"指採取保護措施，讓人、物或某種價值免於毀壞、衰敗或消失；重點在“撐起保護傘”的行動本身。","examples":[{"en":"The preservation of old forests benefits everyone.","zh":"保護古老的森林對每個人都有好處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum began a project for the preservation of the paintings.","zh":"博物館啟動了一個保護這些畫作的專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preservation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-064fb5a5721e36a6","term":"preservation","forms":["preservation","preservations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲存狀態；儲存得好","explanation":"指某物經過儲存後仍保持下來的狀況，尤其強調它沒有嚴重損壞、衰敗，或整體狀態很好；這是“保護傘”帶來的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The wooden boat is still in excellent preservation after two hundred years.","zh":"這艘木船經過兩百年後儲存狀況仍然極好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manuscript is in an excellent state of preservation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preservation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1daf82f62247f3a1d148","word":"preserve","forms":["preserve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c211b69912865d9b","term":"preserve","forms":["preserve","preserves","preserving","preserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；維護","explanation":"指採取行動使人、文化、環境或其他重要事物免受傷害或消失，重點是把它安全地守住。","examples":[{"en":"We must preserve the forest for future generations.","zh":"我們必須保護這片森林，為子孫後代保留下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum works to preserve the city's history.","zh":"這家博物館致力於保護這座城市的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8d71b57f35d0c0d","term":"preserve","forms":["preserve","preserves","preserving","preserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保持完整；維持","explanation":"指讓某種狀態、外觀、關係或事物繼續存在而不被破壞，例如保持沉默、維護體面或儲存原貌。","examples":[{"en":"She stayed quiet to preserve peace in the family.","zh":"她保持安靜，以維護家裡的和平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The renovation preserved the building's original character.","zh":"這次翻修保留了這座建築原有的特色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afa5349d7ce567160c0e","word":"preside","forms":["preside"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-077d243803cdd5dd","term":"preside","forms":["preside","presides","presiding","presided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"主持會議","explanation":"指擔任會議或正式活動的主持人，負責引導議程、維持秩序並讓討論繼續進行。它體現的是“坐在前面主持全場”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The vice president will preside over tomorrow's meeting.","zh":"副總裁將主持明天的會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A senior judge presided over the disciplinary hearing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-371291b930ac5699","term":"preside","forms":["preside","presides","presiding","presided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掌管；主管","explanation":"指對某個部門、機構或事務擁有領導和控制權，不一定親自處理每個細節，而是像坐在前面的人一樣總體負責。","examples":[{"en":"A senior engineer presides over the research department.","zh":"一名資深工程師主管研究部門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She presided over the department during its rapid expansion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e51b168bff14781f132","word":"presidency","forms":["presidency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78fffecb3c82d8ea","term":"presidency","forms":["presidency","presidencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總統職位","explanation":"指總統這個職位或擔任總統的身份，重點在那把象徵最高行政權力的“椅子”，而不是坐在椅子上的具體個人。","examples":[{"en":"She hopes to win the presidency next year.","zh":"她希望明年贏得總統職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He entered the presidency after a close election.","zh":"他在一場勢均力敵的選舉後就任總統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presidency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1c3ec67eb2e651d","term":"presidency","forms":["presidency","presidencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總統任期","explanation":"指某人坐在總統職位這把椅子上的一段時間，也就是一屆總統任期。","examples":[{"en":"A presidency lasts for four years in this country.","zh":"在這個國家，總統任期為四年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"During her presidency, unemployment fell sharply.","zh":"在她擔任總統期間，失業率大幅下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presidency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a47d46e30a5efe74919","word":"president","forms":["president"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e79de1f5886b38f","term":"president","forms":["president","presidents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共和國總統","explanation":"總統就是國家中處在最高領導位置、代表共和國行使國家職能的人，體現了“坐在前面主持國家事務”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The president addressed the nation on television.","zh":"總統透過電視向全國發表講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was elected president after a close election.","zh":"她在一場勢均力敵的選舉後當選總統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/president","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24e20e1ceaced720","term":"president","forms":["president","presidents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總統制國家的政府和國家元首","explanation":"在總統制共和國中，president 同時是國家元首和政府首腦，因此不僅代表國家，也直接領導政府運作。","examples":[{"en":"In that system, the president appoints the cabinet and leads the government.","zh":"在那個制度中，總統任命內閣並領導政府。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The president signed the bill after parliamentary approval.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/president","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b035184778e0627a153f","word":"presidential","forms":["presidential"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e770dfc695ae745","term":"presidential","forms":["presidential","more presidential","most presidential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"總統的；總統職位的","explanation":"表示與總統、總統職位或總統任期有關。它可以修飾選舉、政策、官邸等事物，重點是“屬於或涉及總統職位”，不一定表示由總統親自完成。","examples":[{"en":"The presidential election will be held in November.","zh":"總統選舉將於十一月舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee discussed the presidential report.","zh":"委員會討論了總統職位相關的報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presidential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3847a6a0e2bd0b5e","term":"presidential","forms":["presidential","more Presidential","most Presidential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"presidential 的大寫寫法","explanation":"這是 presidential 的另一種字母大小寫形式，含義仍是“與總統或總統職位有關”，並沒有新增的詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The Presidential Library opened a new exhibition.","zh":"總統圖書館開設了一個新展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Presidential Library houses documents from his administration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presidential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-842fcb5e60989a03d08e","word":"press","forms":["press"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a265aa086963647d","term":"press","forms":["press","presses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印刷機","explanation":"指透過施加壓力把文字或影象印到紙張等材料上的機器，也就是把“壓力產生結果”落實為印刷的裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The old press can still print beautiful posters.","zh":"這臺老式印刷機仍然能印出漂亮的海報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor shouted, “Stop the presses!”","zh":"編輯喊道：“暫停印刷！”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/press","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da974665fcdb5cc9","term":"press","forms":["press","presses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新聞媒體；新聞界","explanation":"指以印刷出版物為代表的新聞媒體及其從業者，後來也可泛指新聞界。它和印刷機的聯絡在於：印刷機把資訊傳播出去，於是press進一步表示傳播新聞的媒體。","examples":[{"en":"The press asked the minister several difficult questions.","zh":"新聞媒體向部長提出了幾個尖銳的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story received wide attention from the press.","zh":"這則報道受到新聞界的廣泛關注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/press","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3958c3d412f20020","term":"press","forms":["press","presses","pressing","pressed","prest","pressest","pressedst","presseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按壓；施加壓力","explanation":"把press理解為“施加壓力併產生結果”：可以用身體、手或其他力量壓在某物上，也可以表示對某人或某事施加壓力。","examples":[{"en":"Press the lid firmly until it clicks into place.","zh":"用力按下蓋子，直到它咔噠一聲到位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heavy box was pressing against the door.","zh":"那個重箱子正壓在門上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/press","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8116b4a86c6ab562","term":"press","forms":["press","presses","pressing","pressed","prest","pressest","pressedst","presseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按下按鈕或按鍵","explanation":"表示短暫地向下或向前施力來啟動按鈕、按鍵等，通常按下後馬上鬆開；這正是“施加壓力併產生結果”的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"Press the green button to start the machine.","zh":"按下綠色按鈕啟動機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Press any key to continue.","zh":"按任意鍵繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/press","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b667446e6eb2552fbe29","word":"pressure","forms":["pressure"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0263b7f1e1429f5a","term":"pressure","forms":["pressure","pressures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"按壓的力","explanation":"指實際施加在物體表面或身體某處的力，重點是“按住、壓住”的動作或效果。","examples":[{"en":"Apply firm pressure to the cut with a clean cloth.","zh":"用乾淨的布用力按住傷口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pressure from the heavy box damaged the lid.","zh":"沉重箱子施加的壓力把蓋子壓壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pressure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a0327318e5c310e","term":"pressure","forms":["pressure","pressures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外界施加的影響","explanation":"從實際的按壓引申而來，指貧困、稅收、社會環境或其他因素持續推動或限制某人、某事的發展。","examples":[{"en":"The company changed its policy under pressure from customers.","zh":"公司在顧客的壓力下改變了政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Public pressure forced the company to reconsider.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pressure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-865a03cddbcd9eac","term":"pressure","forms":["pressure","pressures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理壓力","explanation":"指人因為責任、期待或困難而感到的精神負擔，彷彿有一股力量一直壓在心上。","examples":[{"en":"He is under a lot of pressure at work this month.","zh":"他這個月工作壓力很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Examination pressure kept him awake at night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pressure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e686080306aa0a0","term":"pressure","forms":["pressure","pressures","pressuring","pressured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人施壓","explanation":"把“按壓”的形象轉到人際關係中，指不斷施加影響或要求，使某人被迫或勉強去做某事。","examples":[{"en":"They pressured me into signing the contract that night.","zh":"他們向我施壓，逼得我當晚簽了合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't pressure her to make a decision today.","zh":"別逼她今天就做決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pressure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bd2cdbe092fadb3fcef","word":"prestige","forms":["prestige"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7bc82b697368d28","term":"prestige","forms":["prestige","prestiges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聲望；威望","explanation":"指一個人、機構或事物因為被普遍看重、評價良好而擁有的社會地位和認可度。它比普通的“名氣”更強調受尊重和地位高低。","examples":[{"en":"The medical school has gained considerable prestige in recent years.","zh":"這所醫學院近年來獲得了相當高的聲望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Working for that organization carries a lot of prestige.","zh":"在那個機構工作很有聲望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prestige","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3aacd10c6e949520f741","word":"presumably","forms":["presumably"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f857ee99e8e6472","term":"presumably","forms":["presumably","more presumably","most presumably"],"pos":"adv","zh":"想來；估計；應該","explanation":"根據已經知道的情況，作出一個看起來合理的判斷：某事大概會發生，或某人應該會做某事。這個詞承認仍可能有例外，所以不是百分之百確定。","examples":[{"en":"Presumably, he will attend the opening.","zh":"想來他會參加開幕式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train is presumably delayed because of the storm.","zh":"估計火車是因為暴風雨晚點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presumably","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b241cdb8507323161f71","word":"presume","forms":["presume"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-566d6b4d53c4baeb","term":"presume","forms":["presume","presumes","presuming","presumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒昧地做","explanation":"指自認為可以做某事，實際上卻沒有足夠的許可權、資格或許可，因此帶有冒昧和越界意味。它把“先拿來用”的感覺放到了自己的行動上。","examples":[{"en":"I wouldn't presume to tell you how to raise your children.","zh":"我不敢冒昧教你該怎樣養育自己的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She presumed to speak for the entire committee without asking anyone.","zh":"她未經任何人同意就擅自代表整個委員會發言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d967a264d4f1477","term":"presume","forms":["presume","presumes","presuming","presumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推定；假定為真","explanation":"指根據跡象、常識或已有情況，暫時把某事當作真的，雖然還沒有完全證明。它不是斷言絕對正確，而是先接受一個合理判斷繼續思考。","examples":[{"en":"From the lights in the house, we presumed that someone was home.","zh":"我們根據屋裡的燈光推定有人在家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report presumes that the figures are accurate.","zh":"這份報告先假定這些數字是準確的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/presume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c6321751759867e97ea","word":"pretend","forms":["pretend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4881e3a6367a60ea","term":"pretend","forms":["pretend","pretends","pretending","pretended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"假裝；裝作","explanation":"指明知真實情況並非如此，卻用言語或行為擺出另一種樣子，讓別人以為那是真的。","examples":[{"en":"He pretended to be asleep when his sister came in.","zh":"姐姐進來時，他假裝睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I pretended that I had not heard the question.","zh":"我假裝沒有聽到那個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77049f6f8893dd97f1fc","word":"pretty","forms":["pretty"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23c65d279a12af96","term":"pretty","forms":["pretty","prettier","prettiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"漂亮的；好看的","explanation":"形容人，尤其是女性或兒童，外表使人覺得好看、討人喜歡。它也可以表示其他感官上的宜人，但最常見的是“漂亮”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a pretty dress to the wedding.","zh":"她穿了一條漂亮的裙子參加婚禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little girl has a pretty smile.","zh":"那個小女孩笑起來很可愛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43258c691606b9dd","term":"pretty","forms":["pretty","prettier","prettiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"好看的；討人喜歡的","explanation":"形容物品、作品、景色或聲音等外在上令人愉悅，核心仍是“看起來或感覺起來很討人喜歡”。它不一定表示有很高的價值或深度，只是說呈現效果不錯。","examples":[{"en":"They found a pretty little café near the station.","zh":"他們在車站附近找到了一家漂亮的小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The song has a pretty melody.","zh":"這首歌的旋律很好聽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b613a3f11d4f0d6d","term":"pretty","forms":["pretty"],"pos":"adv","zh":"相當；頗為；挺","explanation":"放在形容詞或副詞前，表示程度相當高，通常比“有一點”強，但未必表示“非常”。它來自“令人滿意”的核心感覺，表示某種程度已經足以引起注意。","examples":[{"en":"The instructions are pretty clear.","zh":"說明寫得相當清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We arrived pretty early.","zh":"我們到得挺早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e42f42ba2a2bd42276a","word":"prevail","forms":["prevail"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60860cb32dee2c86","term":"prevail","forms":["prevail","prevails","prevailing","prevailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"佔上風；壓倒其他事物","explanation":"指某人、某種力量或某種事物在強度、影響力、數量等方面勝過其他物件，因此取得優勢、佔據主導地位。重點不一定是最終比賽結束，而是“哪一方更強、更有影響”。","examples":[{"en":"In the final vote, caution prevailed over enthusiasm.","zh":"在最後的投票中，謹慎壓過了熱情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Blue prevails in the room's color scheme.","zh":"藍色在這個房間的配色中佔主導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prevail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-605e5fd4039eda6d","term":"prevail","forms":["prevail","prevails","prevailing","prevailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲勝；戰勝","explanation":"指經過沖突、競爭或困難後最終取得勝利。它把“佔上風”推進到結果層面：不只是有優勢，而是最後贏了。","examples":[{"en":"After a long struggle, the defenders prevailed.","zh":"經過長期鬥爭，守軍最終獲勝了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Justice prevailed in the end.","zh":"正義最終取得了勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prevail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4d5a180d618df82acd3","word":"prevent","forms":["prevent"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e83402523a26a24c","term":"prevent","forms":["prevent","prevents","preventing","prevented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"阻止；防止","explanation":"在事情發生之前採取行動，把某個壞結果擋住；也可以說阻止某人做某事。","examples":[{"en":"I brush my teeth regularly to prevent tooth decay.","zh":"我定期刷牙，以防止蛀牙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The locked gate prevented the children from entering the pool area.","zh":"上鎖的大門阻止孩子們進入游泳池區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prevent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114,115],"total":4,"counts":{"112":2,"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-93255449bc2d46d635fd","word":"prevention","forms":["prevention"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fde36d17494d9237","term":"prevention","forms":["prevention","preventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"阻止；防止","explanation":"指透過行動或阻礙，讓某件事無法發生、繼續或接近；可以是阻止火災，也可以是阻擋進入或妨礙行動。這是 prevention 最一般、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The town launched a fire prevention campaign before the dry season.","zh":"這個城鎮在旱季到來前發起了防火宣傳活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Better locks can help with the prevention of theft.","zh":"更好的鎖有助於防止盜竊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prevention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d3a9d3784a47653","term":"prevention","forms":["prevention","preventions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疾病預防；健康風險預防","explanation":"指為了減少疾病或其他健康風險而採取的措施，例如健康宣傳、接種疫苗和早期檢查。它仍然是“提前擋住問題”這個核心概念，只是應用範圍縮小到醫學和公共衛生。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise plays an important role in the prevention of heart disease.","zh":"經常鍛鍊在預防心臟病方面發揮重要作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Prevention is central to the clinic's public health work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prevention","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f941f4080eeed2c5d87","word":"preventive","forms":["preventive"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4f738f96f5b799b","term":"preventive","forms":["preventive","more preventive","most preventive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"預防性的；阻止性的","explanation":"指提前採取行動，阻止某件事發生，或像一道障礙一樣擋住某種結果；重點是“先防住”，而不是事後處理。","examples":[{"en":"Regular inspections are a preventive measure against accidents.","zh":"定期檢查是防止事故發生的一項預防措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new lock is a simple but effective preventive device.","zh":"這把新鎖是一種簡單但有效的防護裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preventive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c465ab3d14dc884a","term":"preventive","forms":["preventive","more preventive","most preventive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"預防疾病的","explanation":"指在疾病發生或惡化前，用來降低風險、減慢發展或保護健康的；它是醫療領域中的“提前豎起的防線”。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic offers preventive care for people with diabetes.","zh":"這家診所為糖尿病患者提供預防性護理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A preventive vaccine can reduce the risk of infection.","zh":"預防性疫苗可以降低感染風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preventive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5975cf1bba432391c946","word":"preview","forms":["preview"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1534b0fb22ed651","term":"preview","forms":["preview","previews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提前體驗","explanation":"指在某件事正式發生前，先獲得一部分體驗或瞭解；重點是“先看、先感受”，而不是完整經歷。","examples":[{"en":"The opening chapter gives readers a preview of the story to come.","zh":"開頭一章讓讀者提前感受到後面的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Subscribers get a preview of the new features.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preview","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-595385686a3a01b5","term":"preview","forms":["preview","previews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預告片","explanation":"指把電影、電視劇等中的片段剪在一起，用來提前吸引觀眾的短片，也就是通常所說的預告片。","examples":[{"en":"The preview made me want to see the movie immediately.","zh":"這部電影的預告片讓我馬上就想去看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The preview revealed almost nothing about the film's ending.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preview","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5507fd018647e2f7","term":"preview","forms":["preview","previews","previewing","previewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提前展示或觀看","explanation":"表示在某物尚未正式完成或公開前，先展示它的一部分，或先觀看這部分內容；核心仍是“先開啟小視窗看一眼”。","examples":[{"en":"The director previewed the new film for a small audience.","zh":"導演為一小群觀眾提前放映了新電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The website lets users preview the presentation before it is published.","zh":"這個網站讓使用者在簡報釋出前先預覽它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/preview","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6da0633528deaa0144e7","word":"previous","forms":["previous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ad24e32b7da3594","term":"previous","forms":["previous","more previous","most previous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"先前的；之前的","explanation":"指在時間或順序上發生在當前事情之前的人、事或階段。它把注意力放在時間線中“前面”的位置上，不一定表示兩者之間相隔很久。","examples":[{"en":"The previous manager left the company in June.","zh":"上一任經理在六月離開了公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the previous page before answering.","zh":"回答之前請先閱讀上一頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/previous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0afc24e1266de3b","term":"previous","forms":["previous","more previous","most previous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"過早的；操之過急的","explanation":"指某件事發生或某人採取行動時機太早，後來證明還沒有到合適的時候；它仍然是在“時間線前面”，只是前得不合適。","examples":[{"en":"I may have been previous in announcing the plan before all the details were ready.","zh":"所有細節還沒準備好，我就宣佈計劃，可能操之過急了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Asking about promotion on your first day seems a little previous.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/previous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb23298dffb8c7299bca","word":"prey","forms":["prey"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77de80b22b4b1557","term":"prey","forms":["prey","preys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被捕食的物件","explanation":"指會被動物抓住並吃掉的物件，重點在於它已經落入捕食者的攻擊範圍，是捕食鏈中的目標。","examples":[{"en":"The young seal became prey to a group of orcas.","zh":"這隻小海豹成了一群虎鯨的獵物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The owl carried its prey back to the nest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d9ca013ac75b5f2","term":"prey","forms":["prey","preys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受害者；被控制的物件","explanation":"從“落入捕食者爪下”引申而來，指被人、情緒、疾病或其他力量傷害、欺騙或控制的人或事物。","examples":[{"en":"Many inexperienced shoppers fall prey to online scams.","zh":"許多沒有經驗的購物者會落入網路騙局的圈套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village became prey to fear after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，這個村莊陷入了恐慌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4909444b95969c47","term":"prey","forms":["prey","preys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被另一種生物吃掉的動物","explanation":"特指作為食物被另一種生物吃掉的活物；它是捕食者的食物，而不是泛指任何受害者。","examples":[{"en":"At night, the owl searches for prey in the fields.","zh":"夜裡，貓頭鷹在田野裡尋找獵物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The owl carried its prey back to the nest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2ba517745f56244","term":"prey","forms":["prey","preys","preying","preyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"捕食；以……為食","explanation":"表示捕食者主動追捕並吃掉其他生物，正是名詞 prey 所指“獵物”關係的另一端。","examples":[{"en":"Foxes prey on rabbits and other small animals.","zh":"狐狸捕食兔子和其他小動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hawk preys on mice in the open fields.","zh":"這隻鷹以曠野裡的老鼠為食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-683b531f41ec88a2f345","word":"price","forms":["price"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-024466bb32484dd7","term":"price","forms":["price","prices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"價格；所需花費","explanation":"price是得到某物時必須付出的金額或成本，也就是通常所說的“價格”。它回答“要花多少錢才能擁有或使用這個東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The price of this jacket is too high for me.","zh":"這件夾克的價格對我來說太高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The price includes breakfast and local taxes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/price","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ee8acd384aa13c6","term":"price","forms":["price","prices","pricing","priced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……定價","explanation":"price作動詞時，是把物品放上“價值秤”，確定它應該賣多少錢。它可以表示估定價格，也可以表示把價格標在商品上。","examples":[{"en":"The store priced the table at two hundred dollars.","zh":"這家商店把這張桌子定價為兩百美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop priced the damaged lamp at half cost.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/price","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc668bb4b2cc41721e09","word":"priceless","forms":["priceless"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24e7df7001ca9666","term":"priceless","forms":["priceless","more priceless","most priceless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無價的；極其珍貴的","explanation":"指珍貴到即使願意付錢也買不到，價值無法用金錢衡量。它可以形容珍貴的物品，也可以形容信任、幫助、經驗等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"Her advice was priceless when I was starting my new job.","zh":"我剛開始新工作時，她的建議珍貴得無法估量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family photos are priceless to us.","zh":"這些家庭照片對我們來說無價之寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/priceless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91be00ac5552a831","term":"priceless","forms":["priceless","more priceless","most priceless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其珍貴的；備受珍視的","explanation":"強調某人、某物或某種關係受到高度珍視；它不一定能賣出高價，但在說話人心中非常重要。這是“無法用價格衡量”這一核心概念在人際和情感上的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Those quiet mornings with my grandfather are priceless memories.","zh":"那些和祖父一起度過的寧靜早晨，是無比珍貴的回憶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your friendship is priceless to me.","zh":"你的友誼對我來說無比珍貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/priceless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-470664bd59f587f32e6d","word":"pride","forms":["pride"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d281cbb560e029e","term":"pride","forms":["pride","prides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自豪；自尊","explanation":"指因為自己的成就、能力、身份或所屬群體而感到有價值和滿足的情緒，也可以指這種自尊狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She accepted the award with pride.","zh":"她自豪地接受了這個獎項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His parents watched the graduation ceremony with pride.","zh":"他的父母自豪地觀看了畢業典禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-611d653e49345f71","term":"pride","forms":["pride","prides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引以為傲的人或事","explanation":"指某人最自豪、最願意展示或稱讚的人、事物或成就，也就是“驕傲的物件”。","examples":[{"en":"The community garden is the pride of our neighborhood.","zh":"這個社群花園是我們社群的驕傲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restored garden is the pride of the village.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6dcbf260c13109cd","term":"pride","forms":["pride","prides","priding","prided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"以……為傲","explanation":"指把某件事、某種能力或某種品質看作自己的長處，並因此感到自豪。","examples":[{"en":"She prides herself on keeping her promises.","zh":"她以信守承諾為傲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our team prides itself on careful customer service.","zh":"我們團隊以提供細緻的客戶服務為傲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fc4816bb32221ae6b75","word":"priest","forms":["priest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19e24afb9f54dba8","term":"priest","forms":["priest","priests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神職人員；祭司","explanation":"priest 是在教堂、寺廟或其他宗教場所中主持儀式、進行祈禱或祭祀的神職人員。它強調的是宗教身份和儀式職責，而不只是一般的宗教信徒。","examples":[{"en":"The priest at the church spoke to the family after the service.","zh":"禮拜結束後，教堂裡的神父和那家人交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A priest performed the ceremony in the small village.","zh":"一位神父在這個小村莊主持了儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/priest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-986a1b7135f4986150aa","word":"primary","forms":["primary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e44310266f605af3","term":"primary","forms":["primary","more primary","most primary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最先的；首級的","explanation":"指在一組事物中排在最前面，或處於最早、最初的階段。它強調順序或層級上的“第一”，例如小學是基礎教育的第一階段。","examples":[{"en":"Children attend primary school before they move on to secondary school.","zh":"孩子們先上小學，然後再進入中學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Primary treatment removes solids before the next purification stage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/primary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fa62bf01a347e51","term":"primary","forms":["primary","more primary","most primary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"主要的；首要的","explanation":"指在多個因素、目標或權利中最重要、最應優先考慮的一個。它從“排在最前面”引申為“地位最高或作用最大”。","examples":[{"en":"Our primary goal is to keep everyone safe.","zh":"我們的首要目標是保證每個人的安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The primary reason for the delay was bad weather.","zh":"延誤的主要原因是天氣不好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/primary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dccc5d01dabcd1c0b9fa","word":"prime","forms":["prime"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e34a20bdb899c43","term":"prime","forms":["prime","primer","primest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"首要的；最重要的","explanation":"表示在重要性、程度或地位上排在最前面，因此是最需要優先考慮的。可以把它理解為“排在最前，所以最重要”。","examples":[{"en":"Our prime concern is the safety of the children.","zh":"我們最關心的是孩子們的安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Safety remains our prime concern during the renovation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86439a41153f95aa","term":"prime","forms":["prime","primer","primest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"質數的","explanation":"在數學中，prime 表示一個大於一的整數只能被一和它本身整除，不能再分成其他整數因子；這正像“不能再按整數分開的數”。","examples":[{"en":"Thirteen is a prime number.","zh":"十三是一個質數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A prime integer has exactly two positive divisors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bd3bf061a97c604","term":"prime","forms":["prime","primes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼎盛時期","explanation":"prime 指人、組織或事物最有活力、最成功、發展得最好的時期，也就是“排在最前、因此最出色”的階段。常說某人或某物“在鼎盛期”。","examples":[{"en":"She is still in the prime of her career.","zh":"她仍處於事業的鼎盛時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The athlete retired while he was still in his prime.","zh":"這名運動員在仍處於巔峰狀態時退役了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db1946d32afb3d7b4d9b","word":"primitive","forms":["primitive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae8f79d4621b7a9e","term":"primitive","forms":["primitive","more primitive","most primitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最早的；原始的","explanation":"指同類事物中最早出現、最接近起源的階段或形式，重點在“處於開端”。它不一定表示簡陋，例如早期宗教或最初形態都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displays tools from a primitive society.","zh":"這家博物館展出了原始社會使用的工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The primitive church had very different customs.","zh":"早期教會的習俗與後來很不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/primitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69e061587612ba77","term":"primitive","forms":["primitive","more primitive","most primitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"古老的；簡樸的","explanation":"指事物保留著過去時代的樣子，或結構、裝置和生活方式很簡單。這一義項把“早期”進一步延伸到“未現代化、未複雜化”。","examples":[{"en":"They lived in a primitive shelter made of branches.","zh":"他們住在一間用樹枝搭成的簡陋住所裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist is known for her primitive style.","zh":"這位藝術家以質樸而原始的風格聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/primitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9e79ffe5f04f844b411","word":"prince/princess","forms":["prince","princess"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-774050f948ba95f8","term":"prince","forms":["prince","princes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傑出人物","explanation":"指在某個領域特別出色、地位突出的人，好像這個領域中的“王子”。它可以形容一個人的才能、成就或受尊敬的地位。","examples":[{"en":"She is a prince among surgeons.","zh":"她是外科醫生中的佼佼者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His colleagues described him as a prince among editors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prince","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-154aa931803acebd","term":"prince","forms":["prince","princes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王室男性成員","explanation":"指王室中的男性成員，尤其是英國君主的兒子或孫子。現代新聞和日常閱讀中，這通常就是 prince 最常見的身份義。","examples":[{"en":"The prince greeted the crowd outside the palace.","zh":"王子在宮殿外向人群致意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The king's youngest brother was a prince.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prince","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd8847c76adb3241","term":"princess","forms":["princess","princesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王室公主","explanation":"指國王或其他君主的女兒、孫女等女性王室成員，通常譯為“公主”。","examples":[{"en":"The princess waved to the crowd from the balcony.","zh":"公主站在陽臺上向人群揮手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Princess Anne attended the ceremony.","zh":"安妮公主出席了典禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-207a13b35c3f4b61","term":"princess","forms":["princess","princesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某領域的“公主”","explanation":"用於比喻在某個領域特別成功、受歡迎或備受關注的女性，類似“歌壇公主”“網球公主”。","examples":[{"en":"She was called the princess of pop after her first album became a hit.","zh":"她的第一張專輯走紅後，被稱為流行樂壇公主。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The magazine hailed her as the princess of pop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69e03750027e6b1e9f95","word":"principal","forms":["principal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a8d27ac837a2c08","term":"principal","forms":["principal","more principal","most principal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"首要的；最重要的","explanation":"表示在多個物件中最重要、最主要的，或處在優先順序最高的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Safety is the principal concern during the construction.","zh":"施工期間最主要的考慮是安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The principal obstacle is the lack of funding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/principal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c87274aab3c80d2","term":"principal","forms":["principal","principals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本金","explanation":"指最初投入或借出的那筆錢，利息和回報通常以它為計算基礎；它不是利息本身。","examples":[{"en":"This month, more of my payment will go toward the principal.","zh":"這個月，我的還款中會有更多用於償還本金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monthly payment reduces both interest and principal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/principal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7a702cbb7760b9d","term":"principal","forms":["principal","principals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"校長","explanation":"在美國、加拿大、澳大利亞等英語地區，指負責管理學校的最高行政人員，也就是學校的校長。","examples":[{"en":"The principal spoke to the students after the fire drill.","zh":"消防演練後，校長對學生們講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The principal greeted new pupils at the school gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/principal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-763f2223af429e9217be","word":"principle","forms":["principle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31404c2738788adb","term":"principle","forms":["principle","principles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基本原則；指導思想","explanation":"指人們用來思考問題、判斷對錯或指導行動的基本想法，相當於一條可以據此推理和行動的底層準則。","examples":[{"en":"The team agreed on a few principles to guide its decisions.","zh":"團隊確定了幾條指導決策的基本原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tries to live by the principle that everyone deserves respect.","zh":"她努力按照“每個人都應受到尊重”這一原則生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/principle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d3add8a90e0818fd","term":"principle","forms":["principle","principles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇方案的基本規則","explanation":"指在多個解決辦法之間作選擇時所依據的規則或標準，例如先採用最少許可權、最少浪費等辦法。","examples":[{"en":"The design follows the principle of keeping the interface as simple as possible.","zh":"這個設計遵循讓介面儘可能簡單的原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fairness should be the guiding principle in selecting applicants.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/principle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3eca39ebe4f25e82","term":"principle","forms":["principle","principles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道德操守；原則","explanation":"指一個人堅持的道德標準和行為底線，尤其強調這個人是否願意在壓力下堅持自己的信念。","examples":[{"en":"He refused the offer because it went against his principles.","zh":"他拒絕了這個提議，因為它違背了他的原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refused the bribe as a matter of principle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/principle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce953a0eb08246617b7f","word":"print","forms":["print"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4396c9b000437d5b","term":"print","forms":["print","prints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印刷出版物；印刷媒介","explanation":"泛指透過印刷機制作的書籍、報紙等材料，也指把資訊以紙質印刷形式公開傳播的媒介。","examples":[{"en":"The article first appeared in print last year.","zh":"這篇文章去年首次以印刷形式發表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can find the full study in print at the library.","zh":"你可以在圖書館找到這項研究的完整印刷版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/print","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b157e18d1e23114","term":"print","forms":["print","prints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印刷體字；工整的分開書寫","explanation":"指字母一個個分開、像印刷品一樣清楚的書寫方式，區別於連寫的草書或手寫體。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your name in print so everyone can read it.","zh":"請用印刷體寫下你的名字，這樣大家都能看清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please write your address in clear print.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/print","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aef05e3f971608c","term":"print","forms":["print","prints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"字跡；印刷文字","explanation":"指檔案或頁面上實際呈現出來的文字，尤其強調字的大小、清晰度或可讀性。","examples":[{"en":"The print on this label is too small to read.","zh":"這個標籤上的字太小了，看不清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a magnifying glass for the fine print.","zh":"我需要放大鏡才能看清細小的文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/print","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dfbb2e61f9984ce","term":"print","forms":["print","prints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印痕；印記","explanation":"指物體接觸或按壓表面後留下的可見痕跡；它把“印刷”這個核心概念擴充套件到了自然或手工留下的印記。","examples":[{"en":"The wet shoe left a print on the clean floor.","zh":"溼鞋在乾淨的地板上留下了一個鞋印。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a print of the leaf with a crayon.","zh":"她用蠟筆印出了樹葉的圖案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/print","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77266d5868ebd6ce","term":"print","forms":["print","prints","printing","printed","printest","printedst","printeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"列印；印刷","explanation":"指用印表機或印刷裝置把文字、影象等複製到紙張或其他表面上。","examples":[{"en":"Please print two copies of the report.","zh":"請把這份報告列印兩份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I printed the tickets at home.","zh":"我在家把票列印出來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/print","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5724dc360300865","term":"print","forms":["print","prints","printing","printed","printest","printedst","printeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用印刷體書寫","explanation":"指清楚地寫出分開的字母或文字，不使用連寫草體。","examples":[{"en":"Print your full name at the top of the form.","zh":"請在表格頂部用印刷體寫下你的全名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He printed the address so I would not mistake it.","zh":"他把地址寫得很清楚，免得我弄錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/print","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba70e1dacc17e1a77072","word":"printer","forms":["printer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa8e50e17118608a","term":"printer","forms":["printer","printers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印表機","explanation":"指通常連線電腦、把文字或影象輸出到紙上的裝置，也可指能逐層製作立體物品的類似裝置。它把“印刷者”這一核心概念轉成了自動完成印刷工作的機器，是現代最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The printer is out of paper, so I can't print the report.","zh":"印表機沒紙了，所以我沒法列印報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They bought a 3D printer for the design studio.","zh":"他們為設計工作室買了一臺三維印表機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/printer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45717fb641775fc5","term":"printer","forms":["printer","printers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印刷工；印刷商","explanation":"指操作印刷機、負責印刷工作的人，也可以藉此指經營印刷業務的企業。這裡仍然是“負責把文字或影象印出來的一方”，只是重點從具體動作擴充套件到了職業或企業。","examples":[{"en":"She found a local printer to produce the invitations.","zh":"她找了一家當地印刷店來印請柬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The printer checked the ink before starting the press.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/printer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5bade0e979cb8cf6e53","word":"prior","forms":["prior"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c3a449361a0695b","term":"prior","forms":["prior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"先前的；之前的","explanation":"指在某件事或某個時間點之前已經發生、存在或擁有的事物，就是“排在前面的”。例如 prior experience 是做當前事情以前積累的經驗。","examples":[{"en":"Prior experience is helpful but not required for this job.","zh":"以前的經驗對這份工作有幫助，但不是必需條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tenant had no prior complaints against him.","zh":"這名租戶此前沒有受到過投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-694867e779d937a3","term":"prior","forms":["prior","more prior","most prior"],"pos":"adv","zh":"此前；事先","explanation":"表示某件事發生在另一個時間點或事件之前，和形容詞的“先前的”是同一條“排在前面”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor had seen the patient three months prior.","zh":"醫生此前三個月見過這位病人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please submit the form prior to departure.","zh":"請在出發前提交表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3092a5f0dba05ff3cadc","word":"priority","forms":["priority"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8023a046044e727a","term":"priority","forms":["priority","priorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要性；優先順序","explanation":"指一件事相對於其他事情有多重要，因此應當更早處理或得到更多注意。它強調的是事項在安排中的輕重次序，而不一定是某個人的具體目標。","examples":[{"en":"Finishing the safety checks is our top priority today.","zh":"完成安全檢查是我們今天最優先的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please give priority to messages marked urgent.","zh":"請優先處理標記為緊急的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/priority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-996eb66f767c77e1","term":"priority","forms":["priority","priorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重點目標；要優先做的事","explanation":"指一個人或組織當前最重視、最想先實現的目標。它把“重要性”進一步落到行動上：這個目標應當支配時間、精力和決定。","examples":[{"en":"Saving enough money for a home has become her main priority.","zh":"攢夠買房的錢已經成了她的主要目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repairing the leaking roof is our first priority.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/priority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-956a78f60f47452d","term":"priority","forms":["priority","priorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先後優先；優先處理的地位","explanation":"指因為時間上更早，或規則上應當先處理，而排在另一件事之前的地位。這裡的“排在前面”不一定表示更重要，也可能只是法律或制度規定它應先得到處理。","examples":[{"en":"The court gave priority to the older claim.","zh":"法院優先處理了較早提出的訴求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Emergency repairs take priority over cosmetic improvements.","zh":"緊急維修比外觀改進更應優先處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/priority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d591b76b7170de5ed66","word":"prison","forms":["prison"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-458aa691949ae147","term":"prison","forms":["prison","prisons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監獄；牢房機構","explanation":"指由政府或其他權力機構管理、用來限制犯人或其他被拘禁者自由的地方或機構，重點是“關人的那堵牆裡面”。","examples":[{"en":"The old prison now serves as a museum.","zh":"這座舊監獄現在被用作博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guards searched the prison after the alarm sounded.","zh":"警報響起後，獄警搜查了整座監獄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-154757d462027ac4","term":"prison","forms":["prison","prisons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監禁；坐牢","explanation":"指人被關在監獄裡的狀態或經歷，重點不是那座建築，而是自由被剝奪的處境。","examples":[{"en":"He spent five years in prison for theft.","zh":"他因盜竊罪坐了五年牢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was released from prison last month.","zh":"她上個月獲釋出獄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prison","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41c95f34ba8f0a674442","word":"prisoner","forms":["prisoner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da1405800e5a9465","term":"prisoner","forms":["prisoner","prisoners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監獄裡的囚犯","explanation":"指被關在監獄裡的人，可能正在等待審判，也可能正在服刑；重點是他失去了行動自由，而不單是“做了壞事的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The prisoner was taken to court early in the morning.","zh":"那名囚犯一大早就被帶到了法庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two prisoners shared the small cell.","zh":"兩名囚犯共用那間小牢房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prisoner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ed07df8139a5550","term":"prisoner","forms":["prisoner","prisoners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被強行扣留的人","explanation":"指被別人抓住、扣押或限制自由的人，即使他不在正式監獄中，也可以稱為 prisoner；例如戰爭中的俘虜或被綁架者。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers took three enemy fighters prisoner.","zh":"士兵俘虜了三名敵方戰士。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rebels held several aid workers prisoner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prisoner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4cc6bc01a927e2a78fd","word":"privacy","forms":["privacy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75ca73a768973dac","term":"privacy","forms":["privacy","privacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"私人空間不被看見或打擾","explanation":"指一個人能夠獨處，或讓自己的生活不被別人看到、聽到和了解的狀態；關上的房門、獨處的時間都可以體現這種 privacy。","examples":[{"en":"I need some privacy while I change clothes.","zh":"我換衣服時需要一點私人空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She closed the door to give her brother some privacy.","zh":"她關上門，讓弟弟有一點不受打擾的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/privacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-244d26de9b09ff78","term":"privacy","forms":["privacy","privacies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人資料和私人生活不被監控或公開","explanation":"指個人有權不被政府、公司或其他機構監控、公開曝光，或未經同意收集和披露個人資訊；網路賬號、位置和醫療資料都可能涉及這種 privacy。","examples":[{"en":"The app asks for too much personal information, raising privacy concerns.","zh":"這個應用要求提供過多個人資訊，引發了人們對隱私的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Users can change the settings to protect their privacy.","zh":"使用者可以修改設定來保護自己的隱私。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/privacy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-715dc8493c36579a5b11","word":"private","forms":["private"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edeaf7e0d8c89692","term":"private","forms":["private","more private","most private"],"pos":"adj","zh":"私人的；非公共機構的","explanation":"指屬於個人、私人團體或非政府機構，而不是國家或政府的。它強調所有權、經營者或所屬範圍在公共系統之外。","examples":[{"en":"Many families choose private healthcare when public hospitals are crowded.","zh":"公立醫院擁擠時，許多家庭會選擇私人醫療服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She runs a small private business from home.","zh":"她在家經營一家小型私人企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/private","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-883ceba741ecafaf","term":"private","forms":["private","more private","most private"],"pos":"adj","zh":"個人的；私下的","explanation":"指與某個人或小團體的私人身份、個人生活或非正式角色有關，而不是其公開職務或官方身份。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps a private journal beside her bed.","zh":"她把一本私人日記放在床邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister separated his private views from his official position.","zh":"這位部長把個人觀點與官方立場區分開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/private","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b632cc7b47a6d6d5","term":"private","forms":["private","more private","most private"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不公開的；機密的","explanation":"指資訊沒有向公眾透露，或只打算讓特定的人知道；用於訊息時，強調接收物件受到限制。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep this information private until the announcement is made.","zh":"在正式宣佈之前，請不要公開這條資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sent her a private message about the schedule.","zh":"我私信她詢問了日程安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/private","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42fbfc821dede64cbef0","word":"privatize","forms":["privatize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"privatize","forms":["privatize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使民營化","examples":[{"en":"The government plans to privatize the railway company.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Some residents oppose proposals to privatize the water supply.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-ffa2b8b37132b8d725d7","word":"privilege","forms":["privilege"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-947e48bf2f2560c2","term":"privilege","forms":["privilege","privileges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特殊權利或優待","explanation":"指只有某人或某些人享有的特別權利、便利或優待，重點是這種待遇並非人人都有；它可以是合理授予的，也可以暗示不公平的偏袒。","examples":[{"en":"Flexible working hours are a privilege not available to everyone.","zh":"靈活的工作時間是並非人人都能享有的特殊待遇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She regarded access to the private library as a privilege.","zh":"她把進入私人圖書館看作一種特殊待遇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/privilege","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae7d69a0e3d0b65c","term":"privilege","forms":["privilege","privileges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"難得的機會；榮幸","explanation":"指非常難得、令人感到幸運的機會，尤其是能與某人見面、共事或參與某件重要事情的機會；這裡不一定有權力或物質利益。","examples":[{"en":"It was a privilege to work with such a dedicated team.","zh":"能和這樣一支敬業的團隊一起工作，是我的榮幸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had the privilege of hearing her speak in person.","zh":"我們有幸親耳聆聽了她的演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/privilege","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e74a3f76b51d8c11","term":"privilege","forms":["privilege","privileges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特權地位；享有優勢的狀態","explanation":"指一個人或群體在社會、經濟等方面長期享有更多便利和優勢的狀態，常用於討論這些優勢如何與其他人的處境不同。它說的是一種整體地位，而不是某一項具體權利。","examples":[{"en":"The program aims to expose the hidden privileges enjoyed by wealthy families.","zh":"這個專案旨在揭示富裕家庭享有的隱性特權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She recognized the advantages that came with privilege.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/privilege","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72a7a4f82e487ef3a4dd","word":"prize","forms":["prize"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-15da804d28f88860","term":"prize","forms":["prize","prizes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎品；獎勵","explanation":"指在比賽、競賽或努力之後可以贏得的獎勵，是現代最常見的 prize 義項：原本值得爭取的東西最終被拿到手。","examples":[{"en":"Mina won first prize in the school art contest.","zh":"米娜在學校藝術比賽中贏得了一等獎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prize for the winner is a new bicycle.","zh":"獲勝者的獎品是一輛新腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f16836d90842e28","term":"prize","forms":["prize","prizes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"值得爭取或珍視的東西","explanation":"指任何值得付出努力去獲得、或已經擁有並珍惜的寶貴目標，不一定是正式比賽頒發的獎品。它把“最終拿到手的獎品”擴充套件成“人生中值得追求的收穫”。","examples":[{"en":"For her, a peaceful home was the greatest prize.","zh":"對她來說，一個安寧的家就是最大的珍寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For the rival collectors, the manuscript was the ultimate prize.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dbd0740d8548c48","term":"prize","forms":["prize","prizes","prizing","prized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"珍視；高度重視","explanation":"表示把某人或某物看得非常寶貴，像把辛苦爭取來的 prize 緊緊保留下來；它比普通的“喜歡”或“認為重要”更有珍惜意味。","examples":[{"en":"She prizes the letters her grandfather sent her.","zh":"她非常珍視祖父寄給她的那些信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He prizes honesty above personal convenience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b90f3c26a4734a89878f","word":"probable","forms":["probable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02955ec6b104d7c0","term":"probable","forms":["probable","more probable","most probable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很可能為真","explanation":"根據現有資訊判斷，某件事很可能是真的，但仍然留有不確定性；這正是“天平已經明顯傾斜、卻還沒有完全證明”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"It is probable that the train will be delayed.","zh":"火車很可能會晚點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The most probable explanation is a power failure.","zh":"最可能的解釋是停電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/probable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3c970d63e2a46c8","term":"probable","forms":["probable","more probable","most probable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很可能發生","explanation":"用於結果、事件或計劃時，表示它很有希望成為現實，重點是“發生的可能性很大”，而不是已經發生。","examples":[{"en":"A second meeting is probable if the talks fail.","zh":"如果會談失敗，很可能會舉行第二次會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rain is probable before the weekend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/probable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8ef01283d653e4638da","word":"probably","forms":["probably"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f614f258f5cf3244","term":"probably","forms":["probably","more probably","most probably"],"pos":"adv","zh":"很可能；大概","explanation":"表示說話人根據已有情況判斷，某事大概已經發生、正在發生或將會發生；可能性較高，但仍留有不確定性。","examples":[{"en":"She probably has arrived by now.","zh":"她現在大概已經到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The parcel will probably arrive before Friday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/probably","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba9c736f19e7f60b7f67","word":"probe","forms":["probe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb97cd1c9ffff694","term":"probe","forms":["probe","probes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醫學探針","explanation":"指醫生用來伸入傷口、器官等部位進行檢查或探查的器械，核心仍是“伸進去了解內部情況”。","examples":[{"en":"The surgeon used a probe to examine the wound.","zh":"外科醫生用探針檢查傷口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flexible probe allowed the physician to inspect the narrow passage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/probe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-871f1ef45e156c04","term":"probe","forms":["probe","probes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"探入或探查的東西","explanation":"泛指伸入另一物體內部進行探索，或用來獲取資訊的東西；既可以是真實裝置，也可以是比喻性的“探查手段”。","examples":[{"en":"The sensor probe reached deep into the ice to collect data.","zh":"感測器探頭伸入冰層深處收集資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dentist used a probe to inspect the gap.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/probe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4c52347f2f64768","term":"probe","forms":["probe","probes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調查","explanation":"指為查明原因、責任或事實而展開的調查，是“伸進去探查”在事件和資訊領域的引申。","examples":[{"en":"The authorities launched a probe into the factory fire.","zh":"有關部門對那場工廠火災展開了調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency opened a probe into the missing funds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/probe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47a49356720831b66f38","word":"problem","forms":["problem"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5df2a64ab15cc244","term":"problem","forms":["problem","problems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"需要解決的困難","explanation":"指擋在面前、需要想辦法解決或處理的困難、麻煩或不利情況。","examples":[{"en":"We need to find a solution to this problem.","zh":"我們需要找到解決這個問題的辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had a problem with her train ticket.","zh":"她的火車票出了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/problem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0487c249731a7d9064b8","word":"procedure","forms":["procedure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-027eac777c75d9ed","term":"procedure","forms":["procedure","procedures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"做事的方法","explanation":"指為完成某項任務而採用的一種具體方法，重點在“應該怎樣做”。它可以是工作方法，也可以是實驗、維修等活動中的操作方式。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse explained the procedure before the test.","zh":"護士在檢查前說明了操作方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a safer procedure for handling these chemicals.","zh":"我們需要一種更安全的化學品處理方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/procedure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d70497e75f8eb010","term":"procedure","forms":["procedure","procedures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一連串步驟","explanation":"指為達到目標而依次完成的一系列小步驟。這裡可以把它想成沿著一條路線逐步向前推進，而不是隻指其中某一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The procedure for applying takes about ten minutes.","zh":"申請的整個流程大約需要十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please follow the procedure step by step.","zh":"請一步一步地按照流程操作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/procedure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-119792136aa24c129810","word":"proceed","forms":["proceed"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-114f1558fd8edd6b","term":"proceed","forms":["proceed","proceeds","proceeding","proceeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續向前；前進","explanation":"表示人、隊伍或行動繼續向前走，也可以泛指從當前狀態繼續推進。核心畫面就是不停下來，向前移動。","examples":[{"en":"After a short rest, we proceeded on our journey.","zh":"短暫休息後，我們繼續上路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Proceed straight ahead until you reach the crossroads.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proceed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9293e20ea55b9ca2","term":"proceed","forms":["proceed","proceeds","proceeding","proceeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續進行；轉到下一步","explanation":"表示談話、故事、論證或活動從一個點繼續往下展開，或從一個階段轉入下一個階段。它仍然是“向前走”的比喻用法。","examples":[{"en":"Let us proceed with the next part of the discussion.","zh":"我們繼續討論的下一部分吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She proceeded to explain the new plan.","zh":"她接著解釋了新計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proceed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19ed40bf62c399b8492e","word":"process","forms":["process"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7cc3f83d227728d","term":"process","forms":["process","processes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過程；流程","explanation":"指一連串彼此相連的事件或步驟，這些步驟共同把事情從開始帶到某個結果。它可以用於學習、生產、決策等日常或正式場景。","examples":[{"en":"Learning a new language is a gradual process.","zh":"學習一門新語言是一個循序漸進的過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The process of choosing a university took her several months.","zh":"選擇大學的過程花了她幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/process","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-805e91a0ae015ee7","term":"process","forms":["process","processes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展過程；演變路徑","explanation":"指一個系統或事物依次經歷的一系列狀態，重點是它如何隨時間變化。它可以用於自然現象、社會變化，也可以用於超出人類日常感知尺度的科學過程。","examples":[{"en":"Climate change is a complex process that affects every region.","zh":"氣候變化是一個影響每個地區的複雜過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Learning to forgive can be a slow process.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/process","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef198c499ee42641","term":"process","forms":["process","processes","processing","processed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處理資料或訊號","explanation":"指用計算機技術提取、儲存、分類、修改或傳送資料、訊號等。它仍然是沿著規定的處理路線把輸入變成有用結果。","examples":[{"en":"The software processes the data in real time.","zh":"這款軟體實時處理這些資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The computer processes thousands of transactions each second.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/process","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-038ad4a23efc8d72","term":"process","forms":["process","processes","processing","processed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消化並理解資訊","explanation":"指人在心理上逐步理解、接受並整理一條資訊或一個想法，有時還會在此基礎上形成自己的看法。它把大腦看成一條處理資訊的路線。","examples":[{"en":"I need a little time to process what you just told me.","zh":"我需要一點時間消化你剛才告訴我的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is still processing the news.","zh":"她還在慢慢接受這個訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/process","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113,114],"total":6,"counts":{"111":2,"113":2,"114":2}}},{"id":"ceec-5785c2e5f5e92f140993","word":"procession","forms":["procession"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7dcff9491a9f4473","term":"procession","forms":["procession","processions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"莊重行進的隊伍","explanation":"指一群人或一列事物按照一定次序緩慢、莊重地向前移動，常讓人聯想到葬禮、宗教儀式或慶典中的隊伍。","examples":[{"en":"A long procession of mourners followed the coffin through the quiet streets.","zh":"一長隊哀悼者跟著棺材穿過寂靜的街道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wedding procession entered the hall to the sound of music.","zh":"婚禮隊伍伴著音樂走進大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/procession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1884d5d0650e0b7","term":"procession","forms":["procession","processions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續出現的一串事物","explanation":"指事件、人物或其他事物一個接一個地出現，彷彿排成隊向前移動；這裡不一定真的有人在行走。","examples":[{"en":"The manager faced a procession of difficult questions after the announcement.","zh":"公告發布後，經理接連面對一連串棘手的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A procession of minor faults delayed the launch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/procession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-126c3b743c630fcff8eb","word":"proclaim","forms":["proclaim"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23d7128c8bb5f851","term":"proclaim","forms":["proclaim","proclaims","proclaiming","proclaimed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"宣佈；顯露","explanation":"指公開、正式地宣佈某件事，也可指某人的外表、行為或某種跡象把他的特點明顯地表現出來。兩種用法都像是把原本的資訊“喊到外面”，讓別人清楚知道。","examples":[{"en":"The mayor proclaimed a new public holiday.","zh":"市長正式宣佈了一個新的公共假日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her confident smile proclaimed her confidence.","zh":"她自信的笑容明顯表現出她的自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proclaim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1198780b3af7203cac87","word":"produce","forms":["produce"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-db582c1d5b3f3f2d","term":"produce","forms":["produce"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生產出來的東西","explanation":"指被生產、製造或產生出來的東西，是動詞“產生、生產”的名詞對應義。它可以泛指某種生產成果，不一定只指食物。","examples":[{"en":"The factory sells its produce to shops across the country.","zh":"這家工廠把生產的產品賣給全國各地的商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The market sells the produce of nearby farms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff3a0c1429396394","term":"produce","forms":["produce"],"pos":"noun","zh":"農產品","explanation":"集體指農場或農田出產、準備出售的食物，尤其是水果和蔬菜，也可以包括雞蛋、奶製品和肉類。它是日常生活中最常見的名詞義之一。","examples":[{"en":"We buy fresh produce at the farmers' market every Saturday.","zh":"我們每週六都在農貿市場買新鮮農產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store gets its produce from nearby farms.","zh":"這家商店從附近的農場進農產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f7baae1a1293b75","term":"produce","forms":["produce","produces","producing","produced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"生產；產生","explanation":"指把產品、材料、結果或影響帶出來，可以是工廠製造，也可以是某種行為或事件產生效果。這是動詞produce最核心、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"This factory produces electric buses for cities around the world.","zh":"這家工廠為世界各地的城市生產電動公交車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new policy produced unexpected results.","zh":"這項新政策產生了意想不到的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1990f97a1f4fe7b8e86","word":"producer","forms":["producer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa154328ea4bd631","term":"producer","forms":["producer","producers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生產者；生產企業","explanation":"指生產商品或提供服務的個人、公司或其他組織，重點是把某種東西實際產出出來。","examples":[{"en":"The company is a leading producer of electric cars.","zh":"這家公司是電動汽車的主要生產商。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local producers sell fresh cheese at the market.","zh":"當地生產者在市場上銷售新鮮乳酪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/producer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a34ce9d5c56a6d85","term":"producer","forms":["producer","producers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"製作人","explanation":"指負責組織、統籌或推進電影、電視節目、專輯、戲劇、電子遊戲等藝術作品製作的人。這個人通常協調資金、人員和製作流程，不一定是導演、演員或主要創作者。","examples":[{"en":"The producer helped the band turn its ideas into a successful album.","zh":"製作人幫助樂隊把想法變成了一張成功的專輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked as a producer on a popular television series.","zh":"她擔任過一部熱門電視劇的製作人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/producer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8792157cb4f27fb949c","word":"product","forms":["product"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cbf622836df7bc5","term":"product","forms":["product","products"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成果；產物","explanation":"指某項工作、活動或過程最後產生的東西，不一定是實物，也可以是報告、決定或其他成果。它強調“做出來的結果”，正是從生產線末端出來的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy is the product of months of careful discussion.","zh":"這項新政策是數月認真討論的成果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This report is the product of a team effort.","zh":"這份報告是團隊共同努力的成果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/product","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd08a43abecb8804","term":"product","forms":["product","products"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商品；產品","explanation":"指公司或商店生產、提供並出售給顧客的東西，是“生產出來、擺出來供人使用或購買”的具體商品。","examples":[{"en":"The company plans to launch a new product next spring.","zh":"這家公司計劃明年春天推出一種新產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company manufactures cleaning products for hospitals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/product","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113,115],"total":5,"counts":{"112":1,"113":3,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-ab8e18ef4ebebeddc0b3","word":"production","forms":["production"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-992150277057d252","term":"production","forms":["production","productions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生產；製作過程","explanation":"指把原料、想法或其他材料做成某種東西的過程，核心就是“把東西做出來”。既可用於工廠製造，也可用於電影、音樂等創作。","examples":[{"en":"The factory has increased production of electric cars.","zh":"這家工廠增加了電動汽車的生產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine is being used for production.","zh":"這臺機器現在正用於生產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/production","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3db615fd66eb3490","term":"production","forms":["production","productions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"產量","explanation":"指生產線最終做出的總數量，是“把東西做出來”這一過程的結果和規模。","examples":[{"en":"The company plans to double production next year.","zh":"公司計劃明年把產量提高一倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Annual production reached two million bicycles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/production","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60c394d0e768748735a8","word":"productive","forms":["productive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c41f005b65845bbe","term":"productive","forms":["productive","more productive","most productive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多產的；豐產的","explanation":"指土地、農場等能夠產出大量農作物或其他東西，突出產量豐富。它把“能產出”這個核心意思直接用於自然資源或生產條件。","examples":[{"en":"The valley has some of the most productive farmland in the region.","zh":"這片山谷擁有本地區最豐產的一些農田。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These apple trees are exceptionally productive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/productive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52a045af4fcfa43e","term":"productive","forms":["productive","more productive","most productive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有成效的；富有成果的","explanation":"指行動、會議、討論或一段時間產生了有用而令人滿意的結果，而不是只是在忙碌。這裡是“能產出好結果”的引申用法。","examples":[{"en":"We had a productive discussion and agreed on the next steps.","zh":"我們進行了一次富有成效的討論，並商定了下一步計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a productive meeting and settled every issue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/productive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b625ef919d8f3ac","term":"productive","forms":["productive","more productive","most productive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生產性的；與商品或服務生產有關的","explanation":"指直接涉及商品或服務創造的活動、部門或資源，強調經濟上的生產和產出。它是把“產出東西”用於產業和經濟領域。","examples":[{"en":"The policy aims to move workers into more productive industries.","zh":"這項政策旨在讓勞動者轉入生產性更強的行業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Investment in productive capacity created hundreds of jobs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/productive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd1b16004d22b1a8de82","word":"productivity","forms":["productivity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4628b0276f753af","term":"productivity","forms":["productivity","productivities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生產效率；生產能力","explanation":"指個人、團隊、機器或系統把時間和資源轉化為有效成果的能力或狀態，重點是“做出成果有多有效率”。","examples":[{"en":"A quiet room can improve my productivity.","zh":"安靜的房間能提高我的工作效率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new system has increased productivity across the team.","zh":"新系統提高了整個團隊的工作效率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/productivity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db8d7b95c230ddbb","term":"productivity","forms":["productivity","productivities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勞動生產率","explanation":"指在一定時間或其他統一條件下，標準數量的工人能生產多少商品或提供多少服務，也就是用來衡量勞動效率的指標。","examples":[{"en":"The report compares productivity per worker in different countries.","zh":"這份報告比較了不同國家的勞動生產率。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Improved machinery increased output and worker productivity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/productivity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50e0d250228d28f81a60","word":"profession","forms":["profession"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8d5a6b2403eaad7","term":"profession","forms":["profession","professions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業","explanation":"指一個人從事的職業，尤其暗示這項工作需要專門知識、訓練或資格。它強調“一個人公開認定自己所做的職業”，所以可以自然地表示某人的職業身份。","examples":[{"en":"My father was a barrister by profession.","zh":"我父親的職業是出庭律師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose teaching as her profession.","zh":"她選擇了教師作為自己的職業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2a3fcfd587ebc0a","term":"profession","forms":["profession","professions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職業界；行業整體","explanation":"指從事同一種職業的人及其形成的整個行業或職業界，而不是某一個人的工作。比如法律行業、醫學界等，都可以作為一套共同規範和慣例來談。","examples":[{"en":"The legal profession has strict rules about confidentiality.","zh":"法律界對保密有嚴格的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medical profession criticized the proposed changes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd340d1a5c4151dea2fb","word":"professional","forms":["professional"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-200e3ccbc490d586","term":"professional","forms":["professional","more professional","most professional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"職業上的；符合專業標準的","explanation":"指與某種職業或專業領域有關，或者符合該領域通常認可的高標準。它強調做事像受過訓練的專業人士那樣規範、可靠。","examples":[{"en":"The company provides professional advice on home repairs.","zh":"這家公司為家庭維修提供專業建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep a professional attitude during the meeting.","zh":"請在會議期間保持職業、得體的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/professional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7caeae33e93c3b26","term":"professional","forms":["professional","more professional","most professional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"以此為生的；職業性的","explanation":"指某項活動不是業餘愛好，而是為了收入、把它當作謀生方式來做。重點在“靠此掙錢”，不一定表示水平特別高。","examples":[{"en":"She became a professional photographer after college.","zh":"她大學畢業後成了一名職業攝影師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a professional violinist after graduating.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/professional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":3,"counts":{"111":2,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-17c1532ca6cff8f6a3a8","word":"professor","forms":["professor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-391d2375d59ad7d0","term":"professor","forms":["professor","professors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學裡的正式教授","explanation":"指大學或類似高等教育機構中正式職級較高的學者和教師，通常意味著長期從事教學、研究並達到較高資歷。它最直接地體現了“有專門知識並公開傳授”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"Professor Lee is teaching a course on modern history.","zh":"李教授正在講授一門現代史課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a professor after years of research.","zh":"她經過多年的研究後成為了教授。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/professor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94a3e2580a9af43d","term":"professor","forms":["professor","Professors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教授這一職稱","explanation":"指某人所持有的“教授”這一正式頭銜，而不是泛指教授本人；它把核心形象集中在一種大學職稱上。","examples":[{"en":"The title of Professor was awarded to her in 2018.","zh":"她於2018年獲授教授這一職稱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was appointed professor of geology last year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/professor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-486956c50136fc45581b","word":"proficiency","forms":["proficiency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8b2f0bc5562e34d","term":"proficiency","forms":["proficiency","proficiencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熟練程度；能力","explanation":"指一個人在某項技能、知識或活動上的熟練水平；練習和經驗越充分，proficiency 通常就越高。它可以指語言能力，也可以指計算機、音樂、工作技能等方面的能力。","examples":[{"en":"The interview included a test of proficiency in English.","zh":"面試包括一項英語熟練程度測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular practice has greatly improved her proficiency in playing the piano.","zh":"定期練習大大提高了她彈鋼琴的熟練程度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proficiency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1900eab6c028483d7126","word":"profile","forms":["profile"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed0b14b9ff9ae838","term":"profile","forms":["profile","profiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外形輪廓","explanation":"指物體最外層的形狀、邊緣或從某個方向看到的外形。它是“用一條線勾出東西外觀”這一核心畫面最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The lamp's profile stood out against the wall.","zh":"這盞燈的輪廓映在牆上，十分醒目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sketched the profile of the old bridge.","zh":"她畫出了那座老橋的輪廓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e73bdf76f25af3e1","term":"profile","forms":["profile","profiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的側面輪廓","explanation":"特指人的頭部或臉從側面看出的形狀，也可以指展示這種側面形象的影象。它是從一般物體輪廓自然縮小到“人的側臉輪廓”。","examples":[{"en":"The artist captured her profile in a quick pencil drawing.","zh":"那位藝術家用鉛筆迅速畫出了她的側臉輪廓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sat in profile beside the window.","zh":"他側身坐在窗邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34568547e8b151d7","term":"profile","forms":["profile","profiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人物或事物概況","explanation":"指把有關某人、組織或事物的重要資訊集中整理出來的概況。這裡不再是畫出外形，而是用資料“勾勒”出物件的整體形象。","examples":[{"en":"The report includes a detailed profile of the local economy.","zh":"這份報告包含了當地經濟的詳細概況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The journalist wrote a profile of the new mayor.","zh":"那名記者寫了一篇關於新市長的人物特寫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0455144e02e8da3c","term":"profile","forms":["profile","profiles","profiling","profiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……建立概況","explanation":"指收集並整理關於某人、群體或事物的資訊，形成一份較完整的概況。它就是把物件的“輪廓”用資料勾勒出來。","examples":[{"en":"The magazine profiled three young scientists this month.","zh":"這本雜誌本月介紹並刻畫了三位年輕科學家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study profiled families living in the area.","zh":"這項研究整理了居住在該地區的家庭概況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d23be8d1141403ea5dd4","word":"profit","forms":["profit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c74c53de3ed7880","term":"profit","forms":["profit","profits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"利潤；收益","explanation":"profit 是賣出產品或服務後，扣除成本和其他支出所剩下的錢，也可泛指個人或非政府組織獲得的經濟收益。它強調“收入減去支出後得到的增量”。","examples":[{"en":"The company made a healthy profit last year.","zh":"這家公司去年獲得了可觀的利潤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Higher costs have reduced our profits.","zh":"成本上升降低了我們的利潤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de8e14fa0902825c","term":"profit","forms":["profit","profits","profiting","profited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲益；得到好處","explanation":"profit 作不及物動詞時，表示自己從某件事或某種機會中得到好處，與名詞“收益”相連，強調“從中有所增加”。","examples":[{"en":"You will profit from the experience if you reflect on it.","zh":"如果你認真反思，就會從這段經歷中受益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone can profit from constructive criticism.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94f2fe083e1bab131444","word":"profitable","forms":["profitable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e923141defd1edaf","term":"profitable","forms":["profitable","more profitable","most profitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有利可圖的；賺錢的","explanation":"指某項生意、投資或經營活動帶來的收入超過成本，因此能夠產生利潤。這裡的“收穫”主要是錢。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant became profitable after six months.","zh":"這家餐館六個月後開始盈利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are looking for a profitable investment.","zh":"他們正在尋找一項有利可圖的投資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-178fe93a6f751f19","term":"profitable","forms":["profitable","more profitable","most profitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有益的；有用的","explanation":"指某件事雖然不一定直接賺錢，卻能提供幫助、知識或實際價值，因此值得做或值得采用。這裡的“收穫”是幫助或效果。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting was profitable for everyone involved.","zh":"這次會議讓所有參與者都受益匪淺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The discussion proved profitable for everyone involved.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d750f652e8f2dd920abb","word":"profound","forms":["profound"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-67463221fbff5208","term":"profound","forms":["profound","more profound","most profound"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深沉的；非常嚴重的","explanation":"表示某件事的程度非常深、分量非常重，尤其可說問題、沉默、變化或後果。這是從空間上的“深”擴充套件到抽象程度上的“深”。","examples":[{"en":"The discovery had a profound effect on modern medicine.","zh":"這項發現對現代醫學產生了深遠的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the announcement, a profound silence filled the room.","zh":"訊息宣佈後，房間裡陷入了深沉的寂靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1f236481b4dc5a3","term":"profound","forms":["profound","more profound","most profound"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深刻的；深入徹底的","explanation":"形容思想、知識、理解或研究已經深入事物內部，試圖追到底層原因，而不是停留在表面。這是“向底部探入”轉化為智力上的深入。","examples":[{"en":"Her profound analysis revealed why the policy had failed.","zh":"她深入透徹的分析揭示了這項政策失敗的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a profound understanding of children's development.","zh":"他對兒童發展有著深刻的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/profound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1310ca2c8932dbd11866","word":"program","forms":["program"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-677e7642ddc938eb","term":"program","forms":["program","programs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計劃；活動安排","explanation":"指為實現某個目標而預先組織好的一系列活動或步驟，重點是“按計劃展開的一套安排”，不只是單獨的一項活動。","examples":[{"en":"The school started a reading program for younger students.","zh":"這所學校為低年級學生開設了一項閱讀計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined a fitness program after the holidays.","zh":"假期後她參加了一項健身計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/program","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f9cbd70f7124611","term":"program","forms":["program","programs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機程式；軟體","explanation":"指寫入計算機的一套指令，讓計算機按照預定步驟完成任務。它仍然是“預先寫好的安排”，只是執行者從人或活動變成了機器。","examples":[{"en":"This program lets you edit photos quickly.","zh":"這個程式可以讓你快速編輯照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program stopped responding during the update.","zh":"更新過程中，這個程式停止響應了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/program","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98fb13927ac74435","term":"program","forms":["program","programs","programming","programing","programmed","programed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給裝置寫入指令；設定","explanation":"指把一組指令或時間安排輸入計算機、錄影機等電子裝置，讓它自動完成某項任務；也就是把“安排表”寫進機器。","examples":[{"en":"I programmed the recorder to start at eight.","zh":"我把錄影機設定為八點開始錄製。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She programmed the lights to turn off automatically.","zh":"她把燈設定成自動關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/program","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-99e13475105dbba9","term":"program","forms":["program","programs","programming","programing","programmed","programed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編寫軟體","explanation":"指透過編寫程式程式碼來開發軟體或應用，讓計算機能夠完成設計好的任務。這是把“預先寫好的步驟”直接寫成機器能執行的程式碼。","examples":[{"en":"He learned to program in Python at university.","zh":"他在大學學會了用 Python 程式設計。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They programmed a simple game for the class.","zh":"他們為這門課編寫了一個簡單的遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/program","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5f90a96e680140d51e2","word":"progress","forms":["progress"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8b4fc2f221b1d6c","term":"progress","forms":["progress","progresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進展；進行情況","explanation":"progress 表示一件事情隨著時間向前展開的情況，重點是“進行到什麼程度”。專案、研究或工作可以 be in progress，也就是正在進行中。","examples":[{"en":"Testing for the new antidote is currently in progress.","zh":"新解毒劑的測試目前正在進行中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We made good progress on the report this morning.","zh":"我們今天上午在報告上取得了很好的進展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/progress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a1f6a46b41b1f6f","term":"progress","forms":["progress","progresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進步；發展","explanation":"這裡的 progress 不只是事情在進行，而是指它變得更好、更成熟或更發達，常用於科學、社會、個人能力等方面。","examples":[{"en":"Science has made extraordinary progress in the last fifty years.","zh":"過去五十年裡，科學取得了非凡的進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is making steady progress in her reading skills.","zh":"她的閱讀能力正在穩步提高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/progress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4648c34f152a358","term":"progress","forms":["progress","progresses","progressing","progressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"前進；繼續進行","explanation":"作動詞時，progress 表示人或事物沿著路線、階段或計劃繼續向前推進，和名詞“進展”的核心畫面相同。","examples":[{"en":"Visitors progress through the museum at their own pace.","zh":"參觀者按自己的節奏在博物館中前行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team progressed toward an agreement after several meetings.","zh":"經過幾次會議後，團隊逐步朝達成協議邁進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/progress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7c03e34b89e841ac47c","word":"progressive","forms":["progressive"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a2a5df47add5063","term":"progressive","forms":["progressive","more progressive","most progressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"進步的；先進的","explanation":"指支援社會、思想或制度向更好的方向發展，強調打破舊做法、接受新想法。","examples":[{"en":"The city has a progressive approach to public transport.","zh":"這座城市採用了促進公共交通發展的先進做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school adopted progressive methods of teaching.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/progressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f755d15c35fde51","term":"progressive","forms":["progressive","more progressive","most progressive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"逐漸增加的；逐步發展的","explanation":"指某種範圍、數量或程度沿著向前的方向一點點擴大或上升。","examples":[{"en":"The project requires a progressive increase in funding.","zh":"這個專案需要逐步增加資金投入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The illness caused progressive loss of muscle strength.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/progressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-756cf64933990b8f","term":"progressive","forms":["progressive","progressives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進步派人士","explanation":"指持自由派或改革立場、希望推動社會條件改善的人。","examples":[{"en":"The progressives called for stronger worker protections.","zh":"進步派人士要求加強對工人的保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Progressives supported the expansion of voting rights.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/progressive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8817071845b3943bf6d","word":"prohibit","forms":["prohibit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3a7c3df90718263","term":"prohibit","forms":["prohibit","prohibits","prohibiting","prohibited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式禁止","explanation":"指透過法律、規章或正式命令不準某事發生或進行；重點是“有明確規定，不被允許”，而不只是暫時把事情擋住。","examples":[{"en":"The library prohibits eating and drinking in the reading rooms.","zh":"圖書館規定閱覽室內禁止飲食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local law prohibits landlords from refusing tenants because of their pets.","zh":"當地法律禁止房東因租客養寵物而拒絕出租。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prohibit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0cb0d32615ca8f058c7e","word":"prohibition","forms":["prohibition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-204fa2bcc8a6ebb9","term":"prohibition","forms":["prohibition","prohibitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禁止；禁令","explanation":"指透過法律、規定或正式決定禁止某事的行為或結果，就像把某種行為擋在規則之外。","examples":[{"en":"The new law introduced a prohibition on smoking in public buildings.","zh":"新法律規定禁止在公共建築內吸菸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prohibition was intended to protect children.","zh":"這項禁令旨在保護兒童。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prohibition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a5858b789f5e150","term":"prohibition","forms":["prohibition","prohibitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禁酒法；禁酒政策","explanation":"指禁止製造或銷售酒精飲料的法律或政策，是“禁令”這一核心意思在酒類問題上的具體應用。","examples":[{"en":"The government debated whether prohibition would reduce alcohol-related crime.","zh":"政府討論了禁酒政策是否會減少與酒精有關的犯罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Prohibition drove alcohol sales into illegal underground markets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prohibition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-244210e48437b6556980","word":"project","forms":["project"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d34ff48e1eb40208","term":"project","forms":["project","projects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專案；計劃","explanation":"指為達到特定目標而設計、並分幾個步驟或階段完成的事情，可以是工作、研究、建設或個人計劃。","examples":[{"en":"Our team started a new project to improve the local park.","zh":"我們團隊啟動了一個改善當地公園的新專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project took six months and involved three different departments.","zh":"這個專案耗時六個月，涉及三個不同的部門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/project","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b250ea199bec73d392c","word":"projection","forms":["projection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a65acadcf62b364f","term":"projection","forms":["projection","projections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凸出物","explanation":"projection 可以指從表面向外凸出、伸出的部分，像巖壁上突出的平臺；這個意義保留了“向外伸出”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers rested on a narrow projection of rock.","zh":"徒步者在一塊狹窄的岩石凸出處休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Watch your head beneath that rocky projection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/projection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1729fdafe7f0249a","term":"projection","forms":["projection","projections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影象投影","explanation":"projection 可以指裝置把電影、影片或幻燈片影象投到螢幕上的呈現，也可以指這個呈現出來的影象；本質上仍是把影象向外“投”出去。","examples":[{"en":"The projection on the screen was too dark to see clearly.","zh":"螢幕上的投影太暗了，看不清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum uses projection to bring the old photographs to life.","zh":"博物館用投影讓老照片栩栩如生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/projection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2e54eb893d301bb","term":"projection","forms":["projection","projections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預測；推算","explanation":"projection 還表示根據目前的資料、趨勢或情況向未來推算出的結果，即把已有走勢向前“伸展”出去。","examples":[{"en":"The latest projections suggest that energy costs will rise next year.","zh":"最新預測顯示，能源成本明年會上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company revised its sales projections after the weak quarter.","zh":"經歷了業績疲軟的季度後，公司修訂了銷售預測。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/projection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2297db360d177d9b43c7","word":"prolong","forms":["prolong"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c6192ca410314921","term":"prolong","forms":["prolong","prolongs","prolonging","prolonged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"延長持續時間","explanation":"把某件事、某種狀態或某種感受維持得更久，是 prolong 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Arguing about the mistake will only prolong the problem.","zh":"繼續爭論這個錯誤只會讓問題拖得更久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment may prolong her life for several years.","zh":"這種治療可能會延長她幾年的生命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prolong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0cd61d0340f5b41194c","word":"prominent","forms":["prominent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94c2f4add76bc389","term":"prominent","forms":["prominent","more prominent","most prominent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯眼的；醒目的","explanation":"指某物因為位置、大小或設計而很容易吸引注意，像從背景中向前凸出來一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the warning sign in a prominent position.","zh":"請把警示牌放在顯眼的位置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her prominent red coat made her easy to spot in the crowd.","zh":"她那件醒目的紅外套讓她在人群中很容易被發現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prominent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa3c375ef8b33e24","term":"prominent","forms":["prominent","more prominent","most prominent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傑出的；重要的","explanation":"指某人在某個領域中地位突出、比一般人更受重視或更有影響力，是從“顯眼”引申出的社會地位義。","examples":[{"en":"Several prominent scientists attended the conference.","zh":"幾位傑出的科學家參加了這次會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several prominent campaigners signed the open letter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prominent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3513d9452af7c1768eeb","word":"promise","forms":["promise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a61cca769c110420","term":"promise","forms":["promise","promises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承諾；諾言","explanation":"promise 是把未來要做的事鄭重說出來，或向某人保證某個結果會發生；它既可以是日常口頭答應，也可以是較正式的誓言。","examples":[{"en":"I made a promise to call her every Sunday.","zh":"我答應每個星期天給她打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kept his promise even when it was difficult.","zh":"即使很困難，他也遵守了自己的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a671e8abc497cf7","term":"promise","forms":["promise","promises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"潛力；成功希望","explanation":"promise 也可以指某人或某事顯露出的未來潛力：現在還沒有完全成功，但已經讓人期待它會變得更好。","examples":[{"en":"The young player showed great promise in her first season.","zh":"這名年輕選手在第一個賽季就展現出了很大的潛力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her early sketches showed considerable promise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-866d5ceca8359c5c","term":"promise","forms":["promise","promises","promising","promised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承諾；答應","explanation":"promise 作動詞時，是把自己的行動或某個結果承諾給別人，表示“我會這樣做”或“事情會這樣發生”。它既可以是鄭重保證，也可以是日常答應。","examples":[{"en":"She promised to send me the address later.","zh":"她答應晚些時候把地址發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I promise you that I will be careful.","zh":"我向你保證，我會小心的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e1d290577f46141ea4b9","word":"promising","forms":["promising"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a47da9a240a17741","term":"promising","forms":["promising","more promising","most promising"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有希望的；有潛力的","explanation":"某人、某個想法、方法或事物已經顯出會向好的方向發展的跡象，因此被認為很有潛力。它就像在向人保證未來可能會有好結果。","examples":[{"en":"The young scientist has a promising career ahead of her.","zh":"這位年輕科學家的職業生涯前景很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Early tests show promising results.","zh":"初步測試顯示出令人鼓舞的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promising","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-358e3b49c954970e","term":"promising","forms":["promising","more promising","most promising"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人鼓舞的","explanation":"某個跡象、結果或進展讓人更有信心，覺得事情可能會成功。和“有潛力”相近，但更突出當下帶來的積極訊號。","examples":[{"en":"The first meeting was promising, and both sides agreed to talk again.","zh":"第一次會談很令人鼓舞，雙方都同意再次交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The first trial produced promising results.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promising","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-363256bd153813bc7b3e","word":"promote","forms":["promote"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97675abff300fa50","term":"promote","forms":["promote","promotes","promoting","promoted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"升職；晉升","explanation":"把某人提升到更重要、責任更大或薪酬更高的職位或級別，就像把他推到更高的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The company promoted Maya to regional manager.","zh":"公司把瑪雅提拔為區域經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After ten years as a constable, he was promoted to sergeant.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed9b2cf2650d8404","term":"promote","forms":["promote","promotes","promoting","promoted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"宣傳；推廣；倡導","explanation":"把產品、活動、觀點或某人推到公眾面前，使更多人注意、接受或購買；因此既可以是廣告推廣，也可以是公開倡導。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is promoting its summer exhibition online.","zh":"這家博物館正在網上推廣夏季展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She promotes equal access to education.","zh":"她倡導人人都能平等接受教育。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-adb8457527ddcdc802d8","word":"promotion","forms":["promotion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-263901d1d26bf424","term":"promotion","forms":["promotion","promotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"晉升；升職","explanation":"指人在工作或組織中的職位、級別得到提升，也就是被“向前推”到更高的位置。它既可以指晉升這件事，也可以指獲得的更高職位。","examples":[{"en":"After three years of hard work, Maya finally got a promotion.","zh":"努力工作了三年後，瑪雅終於升職了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His promotion to team leader came as a pleasant surprise.","zh":"他被提升為團隊負責人，這讓人又驚喜又高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfa83fec600c3cc7","term":"promotion","forms":["promotion","promotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宣傳；推廣","explanation":"指透過傳播資訊、觀點或理念，讓它被更多人知道、接受或支援；這裡是把一個想法“推”向更廣的人群。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign focuses on the promotion of healthy eating in schools.","zh":"這項活動重點是在學校推廣健康飲食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The publisher spent heavily on promotion of the novel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffbb6175599606ef","term":"promotion","forms":["promotion","promotions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"促銷；推廣活動","explanation":"指為了擴大商品或品牌的知名度和影響力而舉行的商業活動，例如特別宣傳、優惠安排或其他吸引顧客的活動；重點是把商品推到更多顧客面前。","examples":[{"en":"The supermarket is running a promotion for its new coffee brand.","zh":"這家超市正在為一種新咖啡品牌做促銷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A summer promotion offers two tickets for the price of one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promotion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf07194ee232eb531e15","word":"prompt","forms":["prompt"],"officialPos":"v./adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3506ca9c7deab62","term":"prompt","forms":["prompt","more prompt","most prompt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迅速的；及時的","explanation":"指行動或回應很快，沒有拖延。它強調事情在需要的時間內馬上得到處理，正是“提示一出現，就立刻行動”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The company was prompt in responding to my complaint.","zh":"這家公司及時回應了我的投訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.","zh":"感謝你及時處理這件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prompt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b3a12dccc81b982","term":"prompt","forms":["prompt","prompts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"給人工智慧的指令文字","explanation":"指輸入給語言模型或影象模型的文字要求，用來引導它生成想要的回答、文章或影象。它仍然是“用提示把結果引出來”的概念，只是接受提示的物件變成了人工智慧。","examples":[{"en":"I wrote a prompt asking the model to explain the idea simply.","zh":"我寫了一段提示文字，讓模型用簡單的方式解釋這個想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A clear prompt usually produces a more useful answer.","zh":"清楚的指令通常能得到更有用的回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prompt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd3cd637aa06a14e","term":"prompt","forms":["prompt","prompts","prompting","prompted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引起；促成","explanation":"指某件事引發了另一件事或一種想法。這裡不一定有人直接發出提示，而是某種情況把後續反應“推了出來”。","examples":[{"en":"Her question prompted a lively discussion.","zh":"她的問題引發了一場熱烈的討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accident prompted the city to improve the road.","zh":"這起事故促使這座城市改善了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prompt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c785119f1d81abf56e11","word":"prone","forms":["prone"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f94707ce4448a59","term":"prone","forms":["prone","proner","more prone","pronest","most prone"],"pos":"adj","zh":"俯臥的；臉朝下的","explanation":"指身體腹部朝下、臉朝向地面或床面的姿勢，是“向下倒”這一核心方向感最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The patient was lying prone on the examination table.","zh":"病人臉朝下俯臥在檢查臺上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lie prone and keep your arms beside your body.","zh":"俯臥，並把雙臂放在身體兩側。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e415f770bacc66d","term":"prone","forms":["prone","proner","more prone","pronest","most prone"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易……的；有……傾向的","explanation":"表示某人或某物很容易朝某種結果“倒過去”，因此容易出現某種問題或受到某種影響，如容易失敗、容易受傷。","examples":[{"en":"This old machine is prone to overheating in hot weather.","zh":"這臺舊機器在炎熱天氣裡容易過熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is prone to making careless mistakes when tired.","zh":"他累的時候容易犯粗心的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e718dfa13423e2e4f17a","word":"pronounce","forms":["pronounce"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4c5ece3cd4e026f","term":"pronounce","forms":["pronounce","pronounces","pronouncing","pronounced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式宣佈","explanation":"指在儀式、官方場合或鄭重語境中把某件事正式宣佈出來，彷彿說出口後就獲得了正式效力。","examples":[{"en":"The priest pronounced the marriage valid.","zh":"牧師正式宣佈這樁婚姻有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ceremony ended after the blessing was pronounced.","zh":"祝福正式宣佈後，儀式結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pronounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54464df837d97d83","term":"pronounce","forms":["pronounce","pronounces","pronouncing","pronounced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發音，讀出音","explanation":"指把一個詞或短語的聲音清楚地說出來，重點在於音怎麼讀，而不是它表達什麼意義。","examples":[{"en":"How do you pronounce this name?","zh":"這個名字怎麼發音？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She can pronounce every word clearly.","zh":"她能把每個詞都發得很清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pronounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7f2bd733f640540","term":"pronounce","forms":["pronounce","pronounces","pronouncing","pronounced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"被讀作","explanation":"這是“發音”義在被動結構中的用法，表示某個字母、詞或名稱實際被讀成某種音。","examples":[{"en":"The name is pronounced with a silent final letter.","zh":"這個名字的最後一個字母不發音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town is pronounced differently from the way it is spelled.","zh":"這個城鎮的名稱讀法與拼寫方式不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pronounce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce978dc7829d3b1d975a","word":"pronunciation","forms":["pronunciation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4c8ebd6a33d706b","term":"pronunciation","forms":["pronunciation","pronunciations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某個詞的讀法","explanation":"指一個具體詞、名字或音節說出來時應有的聲音形式，也就是別人問“這個詞怎麼讀”時所要了解的內容。","examples":[{"en":"I checked the pronunciation of the new name before the meeting.","zh":"開會前，我查了這個新名字的讀法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you tell me the correct pronunciation of this word?","zh":"你能告訴我這個詞的正確讀法嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pronunciation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf5414800c5b3bde","term":"pronunciation","forms":["pronunciation","pronunciations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人或語言的發音方式","explanation":"指一個人說話時整體呈現的發音特點，或一種語言中詞語通常被說出的聲音方式；它關注的不是一個孤立的詞，而是一整套發音表現。","examples":[{"en":"Her English pronunciation has become much clearer this year.","zh":"她今年的英語發音清楚多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His pronunciation reflects his childhood in northern England.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pronunciation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c1cda26362828b692665","word":"proof","forms":["proof"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a34a3e2337f7b32f","term":"proof","forms":["proof","proofs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檢驗或證明的過程","explanation":"指為了查明事實、測試效果或發現真相而進行的一次檢驗、嘗試或證明過程，是“把事情拿來考驗”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The trial was a proof of whether the new design would work.","zh":"這次試驗檢驗了新設計是否可行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The claim awaits proof through independent experiments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60e4be0661b49093","term":"proof","forms":["proof","proofs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"確鑿證據；證明","explanation":"指能使人相信某個事實或判斷的證據、論據或完整論證；它不一定是一張紙，也可以是一組事實。","examples":[{"en":"The photograph provided proof that he had been there.","zh":"這張照片證明他曾經在那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was no proof of wrongdoing.","zh":"沒有證據表明存在違法行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c82d3d4865e41e2a263f","word":"propaganda","forms":["propaganda"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56ddabb33d29e2d3","term":"propaganda","forms":["propaganda","propagandas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有目的的影響性宣傳","explanation":"指為了影響某個受眾、推動某種立場或議程而進行的公開傳播。它可以包含事實，也可以包含偏見或不完整的資訊，核心是“透過傳播來影響人們”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum created propaganda to encourage public support for the war effort.","zh":"這家博物館製作宣傳材料，以鼓勵公眾支援戰爭行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers examined the posters as propaganda aimed at changing public opinion.","zh":"研究人員把這些海報視為旨在改變公眾輿論的宣傳品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/propaganda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a07944508f60a9a6","term":"propaganda","forms":["propaganda","propagandas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶偏見或誤導性的煽動宣傳","explanation":"指宣傳機器中最常見的負面形態：傳播片面、誤導甚至不實的資訊，主要激發恐懼、憤怒等情緒，從而讓人接受某種立場或採取某種行動。","examples":[{"en":"The video was criticized as government propaganda designed to stir up fear.","zh":"這段影片被批評為旨在煽動恐懼的政府宣傳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newspaper exposed the propaganda behind the campaign's false claims.","zh":"這家報紙揭露了這場運動虛假說法背後的宣傳操弄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/propaganda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1431179c8c614f71332e","word":"propel","forms":["propel"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82a6c214e83eefcf","term":"propel","forms":["propel","propels","propelling","propelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推動向前","explanation":"指施加動力，使人、動物、交通工具或其他物體向前移動，重點是“給它一股向前的推力”。","examples":[{"en":"The powerful engine propels the boat through the water.","zh":"強勁的發動機推動船隻在水中前進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fins propel the fish forward.","zh":"魚鰭推動魚向前遊動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/propel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c355188f903faa0","term":"propel","forms":["propel","propels","propelling","propelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推動發展或結果","explanation":"把“向前推動”的畫面用於抽象事物，表示某種動力促使人、計劃、事業或變化走向某種情況或結果。","examples":[{"en":"Her curiosity propelled her into a career in science.","zh":"她的好奇心推動她投身科學事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her discovery propelled the research in a new direction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/propel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84ac874b232a019e0991","word":"proper","forms":["proper"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-894891a78e73a7f3","term":"proper","forms":["proper","more proper","most proper"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合適的；恰當的","explanation":"指符合當時需要、目的或規範，放在某個情境中正合適。比如 proper time 是“合適的時間”，重點不是絕對正確，而是時機恰當。","examples":[{"en":"We need to choose the proper time to start.","zh":"我們需要選擇合適的開始時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the proper tool for the job.","zh":"要用適合這項工作的工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7975a1de2228bb87","term":"proper","forms":["proper","more proper","most proper"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真正像樣的；完整規範的","explanation":"強調某物確實達到了應有的標準，或者以充分、正宗的方式出現。proper breakfast 不只是“合適的早餐”，還可指一頓像樣、實在的早餐。","examples":[{"en":"After the hike, we had a proper meal.","zh":"徒步之後，我們吃了一頓像樣的飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They finally replaced the shed with a proper workshop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc9184134ae567287841","word":"property","forms":["property"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0420b805cbf5a4c9","term":"property","forms":["property","properties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財產；所有物","explanation":"指某人擁有的東西，尤其是具有價值、需要受到保護或可以處置的物品；既可以是一件具體物品，也可以泛指個人財產。","examples":[{"en":"Please do not touch these documents; they are company property.","zh":"請不要碰這些檔案；它們是公司的財產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum returned the painting to its rightful property owner.","zh":"博物館把這幅畫歸還給了合法的所有者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/property","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92dbcd5795accccd","term":"property","forms":["property","properties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房地產；房產","explanation":"指一塊土地、房屋及其所屬的土地等不動產；也可以泛指某處房地產本身。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a small property near the lake.","zh":"他們在湖邊買了一處小房產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is an old barn on the property.","zh":"這處房產上有一座舊穀倉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/property","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-604d22127f312446","term":"property","forms":["property","properties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人特質；特性","explanation":"指某個人、物體或概念所具有的某種特徵或品質，尤其是可以用來描述它、評價它的特點。","examples":[{"en":"Patience is one of her most valuable properties.","zh":"耐心是她最可貴的品質之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adaptability was one of her most valuable personal properties.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/property","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b31cd845a11e279a","term":"property","forms":["property","properties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物質或概念的性質","explanation":"指一類物體、物質或概念共同具有、可以觀察或測量的特徵，例如顏色、質量或密度。","examples":[{"en":"The experiment measures the thermal properties of the material.","zh":"這個實驗測量這種材料的熱學性質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Conductivity is an important property of copper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/property","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57c4991869b96345e62c","word":"prophet","forms":["prophet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-050859a0d1f46b1d","term":"prophet","forms":["prophet","prophets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先知；神的傳話者","explanation":"prophet 指受到神或神聖力量啟示、並把神意傳達給人的人。重點不是普通的宗教領袖，而是“替神傳話”這一角色。","examples":[{"en":"Many believers regard Moses as a prophet.","zh":"許多信徒認為摩西是一位先知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prophet warned the people about the coming disaster.","zh":"先知警告人們即將發生災難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prophet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4a0275f9ab30615","term":"prophet","forms":["prophet","prophets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預言家；預言者","explanation":"在較寬泛或非嚴格宗教的用法中，prophet 可以指聲稱能夠預言未來的人。這個意思保留了“傳達尚未發生之事”的聯想，但不一定涉及真正的神啟。","examples":[{"en":"The self-proclaimed prophet predicted that the city would fall.","zh":"這位自稱預言家的人預言這座城市會陷落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prophet warned of an approaching famine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prophet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40b149bf4da1c2ad94b5","word":"proportion","forms":["proportion"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7be70b1c8293dc2","term":"proportion","forms":["proportion","proportions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體中的一部分","explanation":"指某物或某類人佔全部數量或總量的一部分，重點是這部分在整體中所佔的份額。","examples":[{"en":"A large proportion of the students walk to school.","zh":"很大一部分學生步行上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a small proportion of the budget goes to advertising.","zh":"預算中只有很小一部分用於廣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proportion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e64bfc8df85e5d06","term":"proportion","forms":["proportion","proportions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"各部分的協調比例","explanation":"指一個整體中各部分彼此配合、大小協調的關係；比例合適時，整體看起來或運作起來更平衡。","examples":[{"en":"The architect designed the windows in proportion to the size of the building.","zh":"建築師按照建築物的大小來設計窗戶，使各部分比例協調。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The statue's elegant proportions impressed the sculptor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proportion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6e74358f0306d3b","term":"proportion","forms":["proportion","proportions","proportioning","proportioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按比例分配","explanation":"把某物分成合適的份額，或根據承受量、需要等因素調整各份的大小；它把名詞“合適的份額”變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"The manager proportioned the funds to the needs of each department.","zh":"經理按照各部門的需要分配資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mixture must be proportioned carefully before it is used.","zh":"這種混合物使用前必須 carefully 按比例調配。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proportion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecd1378bc9dc130008f0","word":"proposal","forms":["proposal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65c95cf70162f38d","term":"proposal","forms":["proposal","proposals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提議；方案","explanation":"指把某個想法或計劃正式提出來，請別人考慮、討論或接受；它可以是口頭提議，也可以是一份書面方案。","examples":[{"en":"The committee approved a proposal for the construction of a new building.","zh":"委員會批准了建造一棟新樓的方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She submitted a proposal to improve public transportation.","zh":"她提交了一份改善公共交通的方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proposal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12df7f0ee89f9d7f17fb","word":"propose","forms":["propose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff2df16153719984","term":"propose","forms":["propose","proposes","proposing","proposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提出；提議","explanation":"把一個計劃、辦法或行動建議擺出來，請別人考慮或接受。例如，你可以提出一起看電影，也可以提出一項正式計劃。","examples":[{"en":"I propose taking a short break before we continue.","zh":"我提議我們繼續之前先休息一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee proposed a new plan for reducing waste.","zh":"委員會提出了一項減少浪費的新計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/propose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-568c8815154c7252","term":"propose","forms":["propose","proposes","proposing","proposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"求婚","explanation":"把結婚的打算鄭重地擺到某個人面前，也就是向對方求婚。","examples":[{"en":"He proposed to her during a quiet dinner.","zh":"他在一次安靜的晚餐中向她求婚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She said yes when he proposed.","zh":"他求婚時，她答應了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/propose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e8cc5a7ecc7cf5af31c","word":"prose","forms":["prose"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4d33a3a0e91987b","term":"prose","forms":["prose","proses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"散文；普通語言","explanation":"prose指不按詩歌的韻律、格律或分行方式組織的語言，尤其常指書面散文。它可以包括小說、隨筆、新聞和說明文字等，是相對於詩歌而言的一種表達方式。","examples":[{"en":"She is better known for her prose than for her poetry.","zh":"與詩歌相比，她因散文而更為人熟知。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story is written in clear, simple prose.","zh":"這個故事用清晰、簡潔的散文寫成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b00a44ac2671a3412ea8","word":"prosecute","forms":["prosecute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-487bc18cad5e279c","term":"prosecute","forms":["prosecute","prosecutes","prosecuting","prosecuted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起訴；檢控","explanation":"指國家或檢方正式對某人提起刑事訴訟，要求法院追究其犯罪責任。它體現了“依法追究到底”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The state decided to prosecute him for fraud.","zh":"州政府決定以欺詐罪起訴他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company was prosecuted for violating safety rules.","zh":"這家公司因違反安全規定而受到起訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosecute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c616d04ec415d55","term":"prosecute","forms":["prosecute","prosecutes","prosecuting","prosecuted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"控告並審判","explanation":"強調被告被正式控告並接受法院審理，是“起訴”進入司法審判程式的說法。","examples":[{"en":"He was prosecuted in federal court for tax evasion.","zh":"他因逃稅在聯邦法院受到審判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The authorities prosecuted the driver for dangerous driving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosecute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-886c67c66196d7478c9b","word":"prosecution","forms":["prosecution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5c8663e07b3aa9e","term":"prosecution","forms":["prosecution","prosecutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推進；實施","explanation":"指持續追著一個計劃、事業或行動向前做，把它推進到底；不一定涉及法律。","examples":[{"en":"The prosecution of the project continued despite the shortage of funds.","zh":"儘管資金不足，這個專案仍在繼續推進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prosecution of the war consumed the state's resources.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosecution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7af59cef51ac92b3","term":"prosecution","forms":["prosecution","prosecutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"起訴；訴訟程式","explanation":"在法律語境中，指國家或一方正式對某人提起刑事訴訟，或指這一法律程式本身。它體現的是“追究到底”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The prosecution of the suspect began after the police investigation.","zh":"警方調查後，對這名嫌疑人的起訴開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She could face prosecution for falsifying the records.","zh":"她可能因偽造記錄而面臨起訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosecution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40542f7e6b9ec1650870","word":"prospect","forms":["prospect"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7580c52f7881b653","term":"prospect","forms":["prospect","prospects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眼前的景色","explanation":"指從某個位置或視角一次看到的大片景象，重點是“視野中展開的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The view from the hill gave us a beautiful prospect of the valley.","zh":"從山上望去，我們看到了山谷的美麗景色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our room has a wide prospect over the lake.","zh":"我們的房間可以廣闊地俯瞰湖面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24d51ead2664367d","term":"prospect","forms":["prospect","prospects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對未來的展望","explanation":"由“向前看”的核心畫面引申而來，指對未來情況的預見、期待或判斷。","examples":[{"en":"The company has a positive prospect for the coming year.","zh":"這家公司來年的前景很樂觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prospect of retirement filled him with relief.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-912614a681bfc4d7","term":"prospect","forms":["prospect","prospects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可能發生的未來情況","explanation":"指未來可能出現的事情或局面，常暗示某種發展機會，也可以用於否定語境表示沒有希望。","examples":[{"en":"There is little prospect of an agreement this week.","zh":"本週達成協議的希望不大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prospect of another move worried the children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c556394e43f0b6b","term":"prospect","forms":["prospect","prospects","prospecting","prospected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"淘金或探礦","explanation":"指在土地或礦區中尋找金子等地下資源，核心仍是把目光向前、向未知處搜尋。","examples":[{"en":"They spent months prospecting for gold in the mountains.","zh":"他們花了幾個月在山裡尋找金礦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brothers prospected for gold in the northern hills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb224067545c37dea4b5","word":"prospective","forms":["prospective"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aaa6579040b84e6f","term":"prospective","forms":["prospective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"潛在的；預期會成為的","explanation":"指某人或某物目前還不是某種身份或結果，但很可能在之後成為那樣；常用於申請者、客戶、買家等潛在物件。","examples":[{"en":"The website offers useful advice for prospective homeowners.","zh":"這個網站為潛在的房主提供實用建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company invited prospective clients to a demonstration.","zh":"公司邀請潛在客戶參加演示。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e120377ee1b0555","term":"prospective","forms":["prospective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"預期將來的；計劃中的","explanation":"指預計在未來發生、出現或建成的事物，重點是它還沒有成為現實，但已經被期待或安排。","examples":[{"en":"The engineers inspected the prospective site of the new bridge.","zh":"工程師們考察了新橋預定的建設地點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They discussed the prospective changes to the law.","zh":"他們討論了法律可能出現的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f2a767d757fff528c8c","word":"prosper","forms":["prosper"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-646db04f64767bd0","term":"prosper","forms":["prosper","prospers","prospering","prospered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成功並興旺","explanation":"指人、事業、計劃等進展順利並取得好結果，帶有“越做越好、越來越興旺”的意味。它不只表示經濟上的獲利，也可用於更廣泛的成功。","examples":[{"en":"The small business prospered after it moved to a busier street.","zh":"這家小企業搬到更繁華的街道後興旺起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With careful planning, the project should prosper.","zh":"經過周密規劃，這個專案應該會順利發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-101025391a7db2c3","term":"prosper","forms":["prosper","prospers","prospering","prospered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"增長、發展","explanation":"強調數量、規模或狀態逐漸向上增長，是“不斷長得更旺”的畫面；不一定已經取得最終成功。","examples":[{"en":"The plants prosper in the warm, sunny climate.","zh":"這些植物在溫暖、陽光充足的氣候中長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little business prospered despite fierce competition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f54d93092faef94425c2","word":"prosperity","forms":["prosperity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fd6fe14a2a06bbc","term":"prosperity","forms":["prosperity","prosperities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繁榮；富足；興旺","explanation":"指生活、事業或社會整體順利而富足的狀態，重點是持續的興旺，而不只是某個人偶然賺到一筆錢。它既可以描述個人的好日子，也可以描述國家、城市或行業的發展。","examples":[{"en":"The prosperity of the town depends on its small businesses.","zh":"這座城鎮的繁榮依賴於當地的小企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Peace brought prosperity to the region.","zh":"和平給這個地區帶來了繁榮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosperity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c377ecb52bc52f5c7dc8","word":"prosperous","forms":["prosperous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a93087854a3e7cb8","term":"prosperous","forms":["prosperous","more prosperous","most prosperous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"成功的；繁榮的","explanation":"指事業、交易、計劃或發展取得了很好的結果，整體呈現出成功、興旺的狀態。它強調結果和發展勢頭，不只表示某一次事情順利。","examples":[{"en":"The company became prosperous after expanding overseas.","zh":"這家公司拓展海外市場後發展得很成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A prosperous business can create jobs for the local community.","zh":"繁榮的企業可以為當地社群創造就業機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosperous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-535c0b58262839bc","term":"prosperous","forms":["prosperous","more prosperous","most prosperous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富裕的；生活優裕的","explanation":"形容人、家庭、社群或地區經濟條件很好、生活富足。這裡的重點是擁有較多資源和良好生活條件，而不只是某件事取得成功。","examples":[{"en":"She grew up in a prosperous family near the city center.","zh":"她在市中心附近一個富裕的家庭中長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prosperous family funded several local scholarships.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prosperous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-680dce633db1189eb115","word":"protect","forms":["protect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8196a0f90187e296","term":"protect","forms":["protect","protects","protecting","protected","protectest","protectedst","protecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；防護","explanation":"設法讓人或事物保持安全，避免受到危險、傷害或損失；可以理解為站在前面替它擋住威脅。","examples":[{"en":"Parents try to protect their children from online scams.","zh":"父母努力保護孩子免受網路詐騙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This case protects the phone from scratches.","zh":"這個保護殼能防止手機被刮花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-433c3507c372d907a357","word":"protection","forms":["protection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60b4a4b366b11b71","term":"protection","forms":["protection","protections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護行為","explanation":"指主動採取措施，使某人或某物免受傷害、損壞或危險；重點是“進行保護”這一過程。","examples":[{"en":"Raincoats provide protection from heavy rain.","zh":"雨衣可以防止人被大雨淋溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trees offer protection against strong winds.","zh":"這些樹木可以抵擋強風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7bc8f38942b83430","term":"protection","forms":["protection","protections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安全狀態","explanation":"指已經受到保護、因此處於安全之中的狀態，而不強調具體採取了什麼保護措施。","examples":[{"en":"The endangered birds are now under legal protection.","zh":"這些瀕危鳥類現在受到法律保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The refugees sought protection in a neighboring country.","zh":"難民在鄰國尋求保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-520f8594072a44d4","term":"protection","forms":["protection","protections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護手段","explanation":"指用來保持安全、避免傷害的具體方法、裝置或安排，也就是“保護罩”本身。","examples":[{"en":"Wearing a helmet is an important form of protection.","zh":"戴頭盔是一種重要的防護措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers need better protection from falling objects.","zh":"工人需要更好的防護，以免被墜落物砸傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b373da8b1d3654724aa","word":"protective","forms":["protective"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26b943f8a2a9867d","term":"protective","forms":["protective","more protective","most protective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"保護性的；防護用的","explanation":"指某物的作用是擋住傷害、危險或損壞，重點在“用來保護別人或某物”。防護裝備、保護姿勢和安全措施都可以用這個詞描述。","examples":[{"en":"Wear protective gloves when handling the chemicals.","zh":"處理這些化學品時要戴防護手套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fighter dropped into a protective stance.","zh":"那名拳手擺出了防護姿勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ebccdac85a433702","term":"protective","forms":["protective","more protective","most protective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"護著別人的；防衛性的","explanation":"指某人本能地想保護某個物件，常帶有替對方擋住危險、維護對方的意味。它描述的是態度或行為傾向，而不只是實際採取了某項防護措施。","examples":[{"en":"Mother bears are famously protective of their cubs.","zh":"母熊出了名地護著自己的幼崽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt fiercely protective of her younger brother.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec871480d85b1756d8af","word":"protein","forms":["protein"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-873d85eebdc70fe1","term":"protein","forms":["protein","proteins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛋白質分子","explanation":"指由一條或多條氨基酸長鏈組成的複雜分子。它們像一串串能夠“做事”的功能鏈，在細胞中參與傳遞訊號、提供結構支援和加快化學反應等許多活動。","examples":[{"en":"Proteins help cells communicate with one another.","zh":"蛋白質幫助細胞彼此傳遞資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This protein supports the structure of the cell.","zh":"這種蛋白質支撐著細胞的結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protein","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df8eaa1b1b2a671c","term":"protein","forms":["protein","proteins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛋白質營養成分","explanation":"指飲食中的蛋白質這一類營養成分，而不是某一個具體分子。身體從食物中獲得它，用來提供氨基酸，因此它和碳水化合物、脂肪並列為主要營養成分。","examples":[{"en":"Protein helps keep you full between meals.","zh":"蛋白質有助於讓你在兩餐之間保持飽腹感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lentils are a good source of protein.","zh":"小扁豆是很好的蛋白質來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protein","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23e6783b47f8e8fedc54","word":"protest","forms":["protest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa3356a3d0010f64","term":"protest","forms":["protest","protests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式反對宣告","explanation":"指個人或團體以正式方式提出的反對意見，重點是把不滿明確地告訴有權處理的人或機構，不一定包含上街示威。","examples":[{"en":"The residents lodged a protest with the council about the new parking rules.","zh":"居民就新的停車規定向市議會提出了正式抗議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The embassy lodged a formal protest over the incident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65ebdd224b33c4be","term":"protest","forms":["protest","protests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公開抗議；示威","explanation":"指一群人透過集會、遊行等公開行動表達反對或不滿；這裡的重點從“提出意見”擴大到了“讓公眾看見這種反對”。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands joined a protest against the proposed factory.","zh":"數千人參加了反對擬建工廠的抗議活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thousands joined the protest outside parliament.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a26688a00478b4d","term":"protest","forms":["protest","protests","protesting","protested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強烈反對；提出抗議","explanation":"指明確而強烈地表示自己不同意某事，重點是把反對立場說出來，而不只是私下覺得不滿。","examples":[{"en":"Several parents protested against the sudden change in school hours.","zh":"幾位家長抗議學校突然改變上課時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The residents protested against the closure of their clinic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/protest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b34563e2ebeb771708ba","word":"prototype","forms":["prototype"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8787b99b70273c2","term":"prototype","forms":["prototype","prototypes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原型；基礎模型","explanation":"指最初的形式或物件，後來的一系列產品、形式或模型可以以它為基礎發展出來。它強調“作為起點的原樣”，不一定是可以直接銷售或使用的成品。","examples":[{"en":"This building became the prototype for modern public libraries.","zh":"這座建築成了現代公共圖書館的原型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer studied the prototype before developing the final product.","zh":"設計師研究了原型後，才開發最終產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d11afd905f20c585","term":"prototype","forms":["prototype","prototypes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"試製樣機；測試版","explanation":"指為了檢驗想法、功能或製作流程而先做出的早期樣品。它通常比較粗糙，重點是發現問題和驗證可行性，而不是立即作為最終產品使用。","examples":[{"en":"The team built a prototype to test the new safety feature.","zh":"團隊製作了一個樣機來測試新的安全功能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our first prototype was slow, but it showed that the idea could work.","zh":"我們的第一版樣機速度很慢，但證明了這個想法可行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d069c85283b98c2c0ca8","word":"proud","forms":["proud"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c79f434f19706fa7","term":"proud","forms":["proud","prouder","more proud","proudest","most proud"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到自豪","explanation":"因為自己的成就、努力，或與自己有關的人和事表現得好而感到滿足和自豪，就像昂首承認“這值得我驕傲”。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents are proud of the progress she has made.","zh":"她取得了這樣的進步，她的父母為她感到自豪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I am proud to be part of this team.","zh":"我很自豪能成為這個團隊的一員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f12d3dbae78bc13","term":"proud","forms":["proud","prouder","more proud","proudest","most proud"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自尊而不願低頭","explanation":"很看重自己的尊嚴或應得的地位，因此不願道歉、求助或接受自己認為有損身份的事；“昂首”在這裡變成了不肯低頭。","examples":[{"en":"He was too proud to admit that he needed help.","zh":"他太要面子，不肯承認自己需要幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is proud of her independence.","zh":"她以自己的獨立為傲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89448c7e938539a4","term":"proud","forms":["proud","prouder","more proud","proudest","most proud"],"pos":"adj","zh":"驕傲自負","explanation":"對自己的能力、地位或價值看得過高，因而顯得看不起別人或自命不凡；這是“昂首”走得太遠後的負面意義。","examples":[{"en":"He is too proud to ask anyone for advice.","zh":"他太自負了，不肯向任何人徵求意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proud manager refused to listen to the staff.","zh":"那個傲慢的經理拒絕聽取員工的意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proud","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52dabec3560592b39f94","word":"prove","forms":["prove"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d57f9e0e402b06a","term":"prove","forms":["prove","proves","proving","proved","proven","provest","provedst","proveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"證明為真","explanation":"透過事實、理由或證據說明某件事是真的、可行的或成立的。它把一個原本需要確認的說法放到證據面前，並讓它站得住腳。","examples":[{"en":"The evidence proved that she had told the truth.","zh":"證據證明她說的是實話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He proved himself capable of leading the team.","zh":"他證明了自己有能力帶領這個團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf6967a0fd0732ff","term":"prove","forms":["prove","proves","proving","proved","proven","provest","provedst","proveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結果證明","explanation":"表示事情發展到最後，顯示出某種結果或性質，相當於“後來事實表明……”。重點不在誰主動證明，而在現實給出了答案。","examples":[{"en":"The shortcut proved surprisingly useful.","zh":"這條近路後來證明出奇地有用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repair proved more difficult than expected.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c0d113aab13d18c","term":"prove","forms":["prove","proves","proving","proved","proven","provest","provedst","proveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"證明是……","explanation":"與上一義相近，但更明確地把主語說成後來被證實的某種身份、性質或情況，意思是“結果是……”。它仍然來自“讓現實檢驗並顯示答案”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The repair proved to be more expensive than expected.","zh":"這次維修結果比預想的更貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shortcut proved slower than the main road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44c768db2a1e20ba3201","word":"proverb","forms":["proverb"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9f8f55f5184d97d","term":"proverb","forms":["proverb","proverbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"諺語；格言","explanation":"指人們長期流傳、用簡短有力的話表達普遍經驗、智慧或勸告的句子，例如提醒人要謹慎、勤勞或接受現實的話。","examples":[{"en":"The proverb “Actions speak louder than words” reminds us to judge people by what they do.","zh":"“行動勝於言語”這句諺語提醒我們要根據一個人的所作所為來判斷他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My grandmother often quoted the proverb, “A stitch in time saves nine.”","zh":"我祖母常引用“及時縫一針，省得縫九針”這句諺語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/proverb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-405abc33f5f3b06b881c","word":"provide","forms":["provide"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8c3039752e5d5e3","term":"provide","forms":["provide","provides","providing","provided","providest","providedst","provideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"供養；掙錢維持生活","explanation":"provide for someone 表示靠工作或收入滿足某人的生活需要，通常指供養家人或受扶養者。它延續了“提前把生活所需準備好”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She works two jobs to provide for her children.","zh":"她做兩份工作來養活孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After his father died, he had to provide for the household.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c79467af78e6444f","term":"provide","forms":["provide","provides","providing","provided","providest","providedst","provideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提供所需之物","explanation":"provide something 表示把別人需要或想要的東西準備好並交給他們，尤其常指裝置、食物、資訊和服務等基本所需。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel provides free breakfast for all guests.","zh":"這家酒店為所有客人提供免費早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school will provide the necessary equipment.","zh":"學校會提供必要的裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed8af53ac33007d1","term":"provide","forms":["provide","provides","providing","provided","providest","providedst","provideth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人供應；為某處配備","explanation":"provide someone or something with something 表示把某項資源配給某人、某組織或某處，使其擁有所需之物。重點仍是“把資源準備到位”。","examples":[{"en":"The charity provides local families with fresh food.","zh":"這家慈善機構為當地家庭提供新鮮食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic provides patients with free advice.","zh":"這家診所為患者提供免費建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7788872de5b957dbd170","word":"province","forms":["province"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-020ebfc3ee1bc287","term":"province","forms":["province","provinces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大區域；地區","explanation":"province首先可以指地球或大陸上的一個較大區域，不一定是法律上正式設立的行政省；核心畫面就是地圖上被看作一塊的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The island forms a distinct province of the continent.","zh":"這座島構成了該大陸一個獨特的區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several plant species are found only in this province.","zh":"有幾種植物只在這個區域生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/province","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9377f1d1e97f5c28","term":"province","forms":["province","provinces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行政省","explanation":"province指某些國家正式設立的行政區，例如加拿大或中國的省；這裡的“分割槽”已經成為政府管理單位。","examples":[{"en":"She moved to a different province for university.","zh":"她為了上大學搬到了另一個省。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The province announced new rules for public schools.","zh":"該省宣佈了公立學校的新規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/province","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1abd7261ec4a48f3","term":"province","forms":["province","provinces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職責或知識範圍","explanation":"province還可以抽象地指某人的職責、活動範圍或知識領域，也就是“這塊事歸誰管、屬於誰熟悉的範圍”。","examples":[{"en":"Managing the budget is the province of the finance director.","zh":"管理預算是財務主管的職責範圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Advanced mathematics is outside my province.","zh":"高等數學不屬於我的知識範圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/province","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2144dd6d274368b80ed3","word":"provincial","forms":["provincial"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6d1074787c96b71","term":"provincial","forms":["provincial","more provincial","most provincial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"省的；地方政府的","explanation":"指屬於某個省、由省級層面管理，或與一個省有關的事物。這是最直接、最中性的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The provincial government announced new funding for rural hospitals.","zh":"省政府宣佈為農村醫院提供新的資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Provincial officials inspected the damaged flood defenses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provincial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42b4b7567605807e","term":"provincial","forms":["provincial","more provincial","most provincial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"土氣的；缺少世面的","explanation":"形容人或地方不夠現代、不夠講究，顯得土氣、閉塞或沒有大城市的見識。它從“有明顯地方特色”進一步發展成了帶批評意味的評價。","examples":[{"en":"He worried that his provincial clothes would look out of place in the capital.","zh":"他擔心自己土氣的衣服在首都會顯得格格不入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article mocks the town as provincial and unfashionable.","zh":"這篇文章嘲笑這個城鎮土氣又不時髦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provincial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-267d294ad2fe2618846a","word":"provision","forms":["provision"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ff4e00d87ed963b","term":"provision","forms":["provision","provisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預備物資","explanation":"指為了以後使用而提前取得並儲存的物品，尤其是食物或其他日用品；重點不在“正在供應”，而在“先準備好”。","examples":[{"en":"We packed enough provisions for a week in the mountains.","zh":"我們準備了足夠在山裡用一週的食物和用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sailors went ashore to buy fresh provisions.","zh":"水手們上岸去購買新鮮的食物和用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bc27d8c71ccc4f4","term":"provision","forms":["provision","provisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預先準備","explanation":"指為了應對將來可能發生的事情而提前作出的準備或安排，是“先想到，再準備”的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The plan makes provision for emergency medical care.","zh":"這項計劃為緊急醫療救助作了安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We made provisions for delays during the journey.","zh":"我們為旅途中可能出現的延誤作了準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d077068b1262657fbdcf","word":"provisional","forms":["provisional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58257f81b054a8d4","term":"provisional","forms":["provisional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"暫定的；臨時的","explanation":"它像正式版本出現前的“臨時橋”：當前可以使用，但以後可能被確認、替換或改成永久安排。重點不只是時間短，還包括“尚未最終定案”這一層意思。","examples":[{"en":"The coach announced a provisional squad for the tournament.","zh":"教練公佈了參加這項賽事的暫定名單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement is provisional until both sides sign it.","zh":"這份協議在雙方簽字前都只是暫定的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provisional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5b091bdd8553a9f15798","word":"provoke","forms":["provoke"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aefcfef37302f968","term":"provoke","forms":["provoke","provokes","provoking","provoked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"惹怒；激怒","explanation":"指透過故意刺激、冒犯或招惹，使某人或某動物變得惱怒，常常還可能促使對方採取行動。這個意義就是“碰了沉睡的狗，結果把它的怒氣激出來”。","examples":[{"en":"Don't provoke the dog; it may try to bite you.","zh":"別去招惹那條狗，它可能會咬你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His rude comment provoked her into leaving the meeting.","zh":"他無禮的評論激怒了她，導致她離開了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-99913d3f69005765","term":"provoke","forms":["provoke","provokes","provoking","provoked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引起；激發","explanation":"指某件事使人產生某種反應、情緒、想法或行動，不一定含有惡意。它仍然保留“把反應激發出來”的核心畫面，只是被激發出來的未必是憤怒。","examples":[{"en":"The film provoked a lively discussion among the students.","zh":"這部電影在學生中引發了熱烈的討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article provoked a lively public debate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/provoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3f0529b322c9d257c29","word":"psychiatry","forms":["psychiatry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bbdce95aec6473d","term":"psychiatry","forms":["psychiatry","psychiatries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精神醫學；精神病學","explanation":"psychiatry 是醫學的一個分支，專門關注精神健康和行為健康，透過醫學評估來診斷、治療或預防精神障礙及相關狀況。它的核心不是一般地討論思想，而是用醫學方法處理會影響生活和行為的精神健康問題。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to study psychiatry after volunteering at a mental health clinic.","zh":"她在一家心理健康診所做志願者後，決定學習精神醫學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Advances in psychiatry have improved treatment for many mental disorders.","zh":"精神醫學的進步改善了許多精神障礙的治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychiatry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-421556c6f6d720663b9b","word":"psychic","forms":["psychic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-347425174f784924","term":"psychic","forms":["psychic","more psychic","most psychic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"通靈的；有超感知能力的","explanation":"指據稱能夠預知未來、讀心或感知普通感官無法獲得的資訊；也可形容某人表現得像是有這種能力。","examples":[{"en":"She claims to have psychic powers.","zh":"她聲稱自己擁有通靈能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You must be psychic—I was just about to call you.","zh":"你一定會通靈吧——我正要給你打電話呢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-163d817fe8a87f7394f7","word":"psychological","forms":["psychological"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7c24bdd241c0158","term":"psychological","forms":["psychological"],"pos":"adj","zh":"心理學的；心理學方面的","explanation":"指直接屬於心理學這門學科，或採用心理學方法、理論進行研究和評估的內容。它強調學科或專業領域，而不只是某個人當下的心理感受。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers designed a psychological test for memory.","zh":"研究人員為記憶設計了一項心理學測試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report uses psychological theories to explain the decision.","zh":"這份報告用心理學理論解釋了這個決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychological","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e37acbc3bc148c83","term":"psychological","forms":["psychological"],"pos":"adj","zh":"心理的；與心理和行為有關的","explanation":"指一個人或群體的思維、情緒、心理狀態和行為特徵。它關注人的內在體驗及其對行為的影響，不一定涉及心理學這門專業學科。","examples":[{"en":"Moving to a new country can cause psychological stress.","zh":"搬到一個新的國家可能會造成心理壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study examines the psychological effects of isolation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychological","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc5945e7f9b7f87b97a7","word":"psychologist","forms":["psychologist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0861bf6ab8a204a","term":"psychologist","forms":["psychologist","psychologists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理學家；心理學專業人員","explanation":"指專門研究人的心理和行為的專家，也可以指運用心理學知識進行評估、諮詢或其他相關工作的專業人員。記住“解讀人的內心和行為地圖”這個畫面，就能把研究和實際幫助這兩類工作聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to see a psychologist after months of anxiety.","zh":"焦慮了幾個月後，她決定去找心理學專業人員諮詢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The psychologist studies how stress affects memory.","zh":"這位心理學家研究壓力如何影響記憶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychologist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f054cfcb3f1cdb5c350c","word":"psychology","forms":["psychology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1a4756657275721","term":"psychology","forms":["psychology","psychologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理學；對人的心理的研究","explanation":"指系統研究人的思想、感受和其他內在心理活動的學科。這裡的重點是看不見的心靈活動，以及它們如何影響人的反應和選擇。","examples":[{"en":"She studied psychology at university.","zh":"她在大學學習心理學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The psychology of decision-making is surprisingly complex.","zh":"決策心理學出人意料地複雜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3c852b5e62662c2","term":"psychology","forms":["psychology","psychologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對人類或動物行為的研究","explanation":"指透過觀察和分析行為來研究心理的學科範圍，研究物件可以是人，也可以是動物。它把內在心理和外在行動聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"Animal psychology can help us understand how species learn.","zh":"動物心理學有助於我們瞭解不同物種如何學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Psychology examines how people learn, remember, and behave.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab9bc9bf77d171dab9f8","word":"psychotherapy","forms":["psychotherapy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3ebbb07dd04836d","term":"psychotherapy","forms":["psychotherapy","psychotherapies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理治療","explanation":"透過談話以及其他心理學方法，幫助被診斷為有心理或情緒障礙的人認識和處理問題、改善狀態。它像為心理困擾疏通道路，重點在心理過程和專業方法，而不只是開藥。","examples":[{"en":"After several months of psychotherapy, she found it easier to manage her anxiety.","zh":"接受幾個月的心理治療後，她發現自己更容易控制焦慮了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Psychotherapy can help people understand the causes of their emotional difficulties.","zh":"心理治療可以幫助人們瞭解自己情緒困擾的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/psychotherapy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0017dea7770f7ecff7ab","word":"pub","forms":["pub"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b9199bcb80b50c3","term":"pub","forms":["pub","pubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒吧","explanation":"指向公眾開放的酒吧，裡面可以買酒和其他飲料，通常也能吃飯、聊天，有時還提供音樂或看電視等娛樂。它的核心不是單純“喝酒”，而是人們聚在一起的公共場所。","examples":[{"en":"We stopped at the pub for dinner after work.","zh":"我們下班後在酒吧吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pub was full of people watching the match.","zh":"酒吧裡擠滿了看比賽的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-efa1f375d76194fa51a3","word":"public","forms":["public"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80167f60a0a30111","term":"public","forms":["public","more public","most public"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公開的；當眾的","explanation":"指人人都能知道、看到或在場的，不加掩飾地發生在公開場合。它強調“向公眾敞開”，與 private“私人的、秘密的”相對。","examples":[{"en":"The couple made a public apology after the report was released.","zh":"報告發布後，這對夫婦公開道歉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He never discusses family problems in public.","zh":"他從不在公共場合談論家庭問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/public","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aa38cf0988fbb0a","term":"public","forms":["public","more public","most public"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公共的；向所有人開放的","explanation":"指社群成員通常都可以使用或參加的，尤其是由地方或國家機構提供、由稅收等公共資金支援的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The children spend every Saturday at the public library.","zh":"孩子們每週六都在公共圖書館度過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city is building a new public park.","zh":"這座城市正在修建一座新的公共公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/public","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7183866abe58414","term":"public","forms":["public","more public","most public"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公眾的；全社會的","explanation":"指關係到全體人民、整個社群或整個國家，而不是隻關係到某個小團體。它把注意力從私人圈子擴大到“大家共同面對的事情”。","examples":[{"en":"The decision raised serious questions about public safety.","zh":"這項決定引發了人們對公共安全的嚴重疑問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clean water is essential to public health.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/public","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9007a90e2efed808","term":"public","forms":["public","publics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公眾；民眾","explanation":"指社會中一般的人們，不特指某個組織、職業或私人圈子。它就是那扇敞開之門外的所有人。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is open to the public every day.","zh":"這家博物館每天都向公眾開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report was released to inform the public.","zh":"這份報告已經發布，旨在讓公眾瞭解情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/public","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f662004cb4676be8aa8","word":"publication","forms":["publication"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86ba32026ffbfa9f","term":"publication","forms":["publication","publications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出版；發表這一行為","explanation":"指把書、論文、報告等印刷或其他形式的內容正式推出、發表這一行為，重點在“推出”的過程，而不是推出後的那件東西。","examples":[{"en":"The publication of the study changed the way doctors treated the disease.","zh":"這項研究的發表改變了醫生治療這種疾病的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The publication of her first novel took nearly two years.","zh":"她的第一部小說從完成到出版花了將近兩年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c8abbe57bb333ee","term":"publication","forms":["publication","publications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出版物；刊物","explanation":"指已經出版、印刷或以其他形式推出，供人閱讀、銷售或分發的具體作品或刊物；這裡的焦點從“推出”轉到了“推出的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The university publishes a monthly publication for its students.","zh":"這所大學每月為學生出版一份刊物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found the article in a respected medical publication.","zh":"我在一份受尊敬的醫學刊物上找到了這篇文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publication","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb9d3dfade7c0127ed55","word":"publicity","forms":["publicity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb0f2188759c79c3","term":"publicity","forms":["publicity","publicities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宣傳活動","explanation":"指為了讓公眾知道並對某件事產生興趣而進行的宣傳活動，常見於電影、產品、活動或個人推廣。核心畫面是把事情主動推到公眾面前。","examples":[{"en":"The museum launched a publicity campaign for its new exhibition.","zh":"這家博物館為新展覽發起了一場宣傳活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The band hired an agency to handle publicity for the tour.","zh":"樂隊聘請了一家機構負責巡演的宣傳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publicity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-024f10913fc0daa0","term":"publicity","forms":["publicity","publicities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公眾關注","explanation":"指宣傳成功後吸引來的公眾興趣和注意力，也就是事情被更多人看見、談論的結果。它和前一個義項緊密相連：宣傳把事情推到人群面前，公眾關注隨之增加。","examples":[{"en":"The controversy brought the small company a great deal of publicity.","zh":"這場爭議給這家小公司帶來了大量公眾關注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The controversial advertisement generated enormous publicity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publicity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-503ea9e5a3981291628e","word":"publicize","forms":["publicize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"publicize","forms":["publicize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"宣傳；使公諸於世","examples":[{"en":"We need to publicize the charity concert before tickets go on sale.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The agency will publicize the results on its website.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5d47a4311d759db69e5","word":"publish","forms":["publish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-807bfcc6e9c9a0f9","term":"publish","forms":["publish","publishes","publishing","published","publishest","publishedst","publisheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出版併發行","explanation":"把書、文章、報道等正式製作出來並公開發行或銷售，就是 publish；重點是讓作品進入公眾可以獲得的渠道。","examples":[{"en":"The magazine published her first short story last month.","zh":"這本雜誌上個月刊登了她的第一篇短篇小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report was published online before the printed edition appeared.","zh":"這份報告在紙質版發行前就已經線上上釋出了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86b56a852b89524e","term":"publish","forms":["publish","publishes","publishing","published","publishest","publishedst","publisheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向公眾宣佈","explanation":"把決定、訊息、公告等正式告訴公眾，使原本未公開的資訊公開化；這裡不一定有一本書或一篇文章作為出版物。","examples":[{"en":"The city published a notice about the road closure.","zh":"市政府釋出了關於道路封閉的公告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government published notice of the proposed boundary change.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f03a060b7eb032972dc","word":"publisher","forms":["publisher"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42753acea915617f","term":"publisher","forms":["publisher","publishers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出版商；出版社","explanation":"指負責出版書籍、雜誌或其他內容的人或公司，把作者的作品組織、製作並推向讀者。它強調“讓內容正式出版併發行”的角色，不一定親自寫作或印刷。","examples":[{"en":"The publisher accepted her first novel.","zh":"出版社接受了她的第一部小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He works for a small educational publisher.","zh":"他在一家小型教育類出版社工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publisher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1d55a7cef49caae","term":"publisher","forms":["publisher","publishers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"釋出者元件","explanation":"在計算機或工程系統中，publisher是負責釋出事件、資料或通知的元件；其他稱為訂閱者的元件接收這些資訊。這裡保留了“把資訊送出去”的核心形象，但釋出的不是書，而是系統訊息。","examples":[{"en":"The publisher sends an event to all subscribed services.","zh":"釋出者會把事件傳送給所有已訂閱的服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If the publisher stops producing messages, its subscribers remain idle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/publisher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-910daa97a4052206954d","word":"pudding","forms":["pudding"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ca1b9569c842872","term":"pudding","forms":["pudding","puddings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蒸煮制食品","explanation":"指透過煮或蒸製成的食品，既可以是甜的，也可以是鹹的；重點是這種柔軟、凝固的製作形態，而不只是甜味。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves a savory pudding made with corn and cheese.","zh":"這家餐廳供應用玉米和乳酪做的鹹味蒸制食品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We made a bread pudding with the leftover rolls.","zh":"我們用剩下的小麵包做了麵包布丁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pudding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a10354124633386c","term":"pudding","forms":["pudding","puddings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蒸制蛋糕或甜點","explanation":"指通常透過煮或蒸製成的蛋糕狀甜點，吃起來厚實、柔軟，常在冬天或節日食用。","examples":[{"en":"My grandmother makes a rich steamed pudding every Christmas.","zh":"我祖母每年聖誕節都會做一種很濃郁的蒸制甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She served a steamed ginger pudding with custard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pudding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d551fc468a99a602","term":"pudding","forms":["pudding","puddings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛋奶凍般的甜點","explanation":"指質地像蛋奶凍或慕斯的甜點，通常靠澱粉等材料變稠；這是現代英語中最常見、最容易聯想到的食物義之一。","examples":[{"en":"The children ate chocolate pudding after dinner.","zh":"孩子們晚飯後吃了巧克力布丁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ate chocolate pudding from small glass bowls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pudding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5668e7edcd8a3ef87b00","word":"puff","forms":["puff"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9bf28a6d1e5b9fec","term":"puff","forms":["puff","puffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一口短促的氣","explanation":"指從嘴裡突然、短促地撥出的一小口氣，重點是“噗”的動作和聲音。","examples":[{"en":"He let out a puff of air to cool the soup.","zh":"他撥出一口氣給湯降溫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With one puff, she blew out the candle.","zh":"她吹了一口氣就把蠟燭吹滅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cad9a6902c0448f","term":"puff","forms":["puff","puffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喘氣能力","explanation":"指一個人持續運動時輕鬆呼吸、保持體力的能力；沒有這種能力就會很快喘起來。","examples":[{"en":"I was out of puff after climbing three flights of stairs.","zh":"我爬了三層樓梯後就喘得上氣不接下氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The steep stairs left him without any puff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91e8c66a2d1b9aba","term":"puff","forms":["puff","puffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一小團煙氣","explanation":"指漂浮在空氣中的一小團氣體、煙或蒸汽，仍然保留著“短促吹出的一團東西”這個核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A puff of smoke rose from the old chimney.","zh":"一縷煙從老煙囪裡升起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine released a puff of white steam.","zh":"機器噴出一小團白色蒸汽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d33e12e6e3f197b","term":"puff","forms":["puff","puffs","puffing","puffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"一陣陣噴出煙氣","explanation":"指煙、氣體等不是連續噴出，而是一小團一小團地冒出或噴出。","examples":[{"en":"The old train puffed smoke as it left the station.","zh":"那輛老火車離站時一陣陣地冒著煙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Steam puffed out of the kettle.","zh":"蒸汽一陣陣地從水壺裡冒出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9193cf91d7df5013","term":"puff","forms":["puff","puffs","puffing","puffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喘氣","explanation":"指因為跑步、爬樓或用力而呼吸急促、發出短促的氣聲。","examples":[{"en":"She puffed up the hill with a heavy backpack.","zh":"她揹著沉重的揹包喘著氣爬上山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He puffed as he climbed the final flight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aef8f76f548cc741","term":"puff","forms":["puff","puffs","puffing","puffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吹得自滿","explanation":"指透過成功、恭維或自我評價使某人變得驕傲自滿，常常達到“被吹得膨脹”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The praise puffed him up, and he stopped listening to advice.","zh":"那些讚美把他吹得飄飄然，使他不再聽取建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The applause puffed him up with pride.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5f5571c2c9c437485d5","word":"pull","forms":["pull"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66bfa0fa79c50154","term":"pull","forms":["pull","pulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拉動；一拉","explanation":"指一次把東西向自己或某個方向拉的動作，就像一股力把物體拉過來。","examples":[{"en":"Give the door a firm pull.","zh":"用力拉一下門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One sharp pull removed the loose thread.","zh":"猛地一拉，鬆掉的線就被扯掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b98ee27d1f89fc7","term":"pull","forms":["pull","pulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"把手；拉環","explanation":"指專門供人拉動的部件，例如拉鍊頭、抽屜拉手、開關拉柄或拉環，是承受那股拉力的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The zipper pull broke off my jacket.","zh":"我夾克上的拉鍊頭掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choose a metal pull for the kitchen drawers.","zh":"給廚房抽屜選一個金屬拉手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd4fabed383c0813","term":"pull","forms":["pull","pulls","pulling","pulled","pullest","pulledst","pulleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拉；拽","explanation":"施加一股把東西拉過來的力，使物體朝自己或指定方向移動。","examples":[{"en":"Please pull the rope slowly.","zh":"請慢慢拉繩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pulled the child away from the road.","zh":"她把孩子從路邊拉開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41c7545b805dad30","term":"pull","forms":["pull","pulls","pulling","pulled","pullest","pulledst","pulleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸引；招徠","explanation":"某人或某物像一股力量一樣把人吸引過來，或吸引來顧客、觀眾和資源。","examples":[{"en":"The new exhibit pulled thousands of visitors to the museum.","zh":"新展覽吸引了數千名遊客來到博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That restaurant pulls in customers all day.","zh":"那家餐館一整天都能吸引顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41b589ea15f2d94a20fb","word":"pulse","forms":["pulse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0bff32c93b391ec8","term":"pulse","forms":["pulse","pulses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脈搏","explanation":"指在手腕、頸部等處摸到的有規律跳動，是心臟泵血造成的。它是 pulse 最核心、最具體的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse checked my pulse before the examination.","zh":"護士在檢查前測了我的脈搏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I could feel a strong pulse in my wrist.","zh":"我能感覺到手腕處強勁的脈搏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pulse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d480a678820270c","term":"pulse","forms":["pulse","pulses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搏動；脈動","explanation":"指一次跳動，也可以指連續重複的跳動或振動；聲音、空氣和其他事物都可以有這種一下一下的變化。","examples":[{"en":"The machine sends out a pulse of sound every few seconds.","zh":"這臺機器每隔幾秒發出一陣聲脈衝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bright pulse of light crossed the screen.","zh":"一道明亮的光脈衝劃過螢幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pulse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-547d8c102984611a","term":"pulse","forms":["pulse","pulses","pulsing","pulsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搏動；跳動","explanation":"表示像動脈或心臟那樣反覆收縮、擴張和跳動，也可指血液、情緒或某種力量在體內有節奏地湧動。","examples":[{"en":"Her heart pulsed faster as she climbed the hill.","zh":"她爬坡時心臟跳得更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Warm blood pulsed through his arms.","zh":"溫熱的血液在他的手臂中一陣陣流動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pulse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b203c464bb32a27e862","word":"pump","forms":["pump"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ad7593b93841821","term":"pump","forms":["pump","pumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"泵；抽送裝置","explanation":"一種透過反覆推動來輸送或壓縮液體、氣體的裝置，例如水泵或空氣泵。","examples":[{"en":"This pump can move water from the tank to the garden.","zh":"這臺泵能把水從水箱輸送到花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The air pump is beside the bicycle.","zh":"氣泵在腳踏車旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f434111d9222cace","term":"pump","forms":["pump","pumps","pumping","pumped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用泵抽送","explanation":"使用泵把水或其他液體抽出來或輸送到別處，也可單獨指進行抽水動作。","examples":[{"en":"We pumped water from the cellar after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，我們把地下室裡的水抽了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kept pumping, but no water came out.","zh":"他一直抽水，但沒有水出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff48e511e1638fc379cb","word":"pumpkin","forms":["pumpkin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d55daaa1c962113c","term":"pumpkin","forms":["pumpkin","pumpkins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"南瓜植物","explanation":"指結出圓形果實的南瓜這種植物本身，而不是某一個果實。可以把它想成記憶主線的起點：先有南瓜植株，才有後面的南瓜果實和南瓜色。","examples":[{"en":"We grow pumpkin in the field behind the house.","zh":"我們在房子後面的田裡種南瓜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pumpkin plants need plenty of sunlight.","zh":"南瓜植株需要充足的陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pumpkin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c01cfd95db4c39a","term":"pumpkin","forms":["pumpkin","pumpkins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"南瓜果實","explanation":"指南瓜植株結出的圓形果實，通常想到成熟時呈黃色或橙色、可以食用的南瓜。這是日常生活中最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a large pumpkin for the autumn festival.","zh":"她為秋季節日買了一個大南瓜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We cut the pumpkin into pieces and roasted it.","zh":"我們把南瓜切成塊烤了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pumpkin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4d916fa9d2e6d4c0d99","word":"punch","forms":["punch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-485aea9d802a8a0e","term":"punch","forms":["punch","punches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拳頭的一擊","explanation":"指用拳頭頂向目標的一下，即一次出拳或拳擊。","examples":[{"en":"He took a punch to the jaw but stayed on his feet.","zh":"他下巴捱了一拳，但仍然站著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She threw a punch at the bag.","zh":"她朝沙袋打出了一拳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96419f061412d1a5","term":"punch","forms":["punch","punches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"打孔工具","explanation":"指細長而通常呈圓形的工具，用尖端頂穿薄材料、壓印標記，或把東西頂入已有的孔。核心畫面仍是“用力頂進去”。","examples":[{"en":"Use a hole punch to make two holes in the card.","zh":"用打孔器在卡片上打兩個孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He used a metal punch to drive the pin into place.","zh":"他用金屬衝頭把銷釘頂到位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7b1b7d41e188339","term":"punch","forms":["punch","punches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合飲料","explanation":"指把幾種飲料調在一起的混合飲品，通常含果汁，也可能含酒精；這是與“出拳、打孔”不同的一條詞源線。","examples":[{"en":"We served fruit punch at the children's party.","zh":"我們在孩子們的聚會上供應了水果混合飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a bowl of punch with orange juice and sparkling water.","zh":"她用橙汁和氣泡水調了一大碗混合飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3308f93b225ebe96","term":"punch","forms":["punch","punches","punching","punched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用拳頭打","explanation":"指把拳頭用力頂向某人或某物，即出拳擊打。","examples":[{"en":"The boxer punched his opponent in the ribs.","zh":"拳擊手一拳打在對手的肋部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't punch the wall; you'll hurt your hand.","zh":"別用拳頭打牆，你會弄傷手的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f036b21c8bbfb1149055","word":"punctual","forms":["punctual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9aba4b60778c14a6","term":"punctual","forms":["punctual","more punctual","most punctual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"準時的；守時的","explanation":"表示在約定的時間到達、開始或完成，不遲到也不拖延。它像是準確落在時間線上指定的那個點上，常用來稱讚一個人守時。","examples":[{"en":"She is always punctual for work.","zh":"她上班總是很準時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please be punctual for the meeting.","zh":"請準時參加會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punctual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cc0e52c0a8c194e","term":"punctual","forms":["punctual","more punctual","most punctual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"點狀的","explanation":"在數學和科學語境中，表示由一個點或一系列彼此分開的點構成，而不是連續鋪展開來的形態。","examples":[{"en":"The map shows a punctual distribution of the recorded events.","zh":"這張地圖顯示了所記錄事件的點狀分佈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The model treats the distant stars as punctual sources.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punctual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-17896b9659956c9dc05b","word":"punish(ment)","forms":["punish","punishment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a139f4a96f18f89","term":"punish","forms":["punish","punishes","punishing","punished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懲罰；處罰","explanation":"指有權威的人因為某人犯罪、違規或行為不當而讓其承擔痛苦或後果，例如父母懲罰孩子、老師處罰學生，或法律懲罰罪犯。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher punished the student for cheating on the test.","zh":"老師因這名學生考試作弊而處罰了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Drivers who break the law should be punished.","zh":"違反法律的司機應當受到懲罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06a6911a0808728b","term":"punish","forms":["punish","punishes","punishing","punished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"苛待；不公平地為難","explanation":"指某人或某種制度並非正式地處罰，而是以嚴厲、不公平的方式對待別人，讓對方因某種選擇或處境而不斷受阻。這裡保留了“讓人承受痛苦”的核心意思，但重點是苛刻和不公。","examples":[{"en":"The system seems to punish people for trying to improve their lives.","zh":"這個制度似乎在懲罰那些努力改善生活的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tax changes punish families with only one income.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35fe953317e1bcc8","term":"punishment","forms":["punishment","punishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懲罰行為","explanation":"指有權威的一方對犯錯者施加懲罰這一行為或過程，例如父母、老師或管理者對不當行為作出處置。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gave the students punishment for talking during the test.","zh":"老師因為學生在考試時講話而處罰了他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Punishment alone will not address the underlying problem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37ec9ac28c5d5f3c","term":"punishment","forms":["punishment","punishments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體處罰；刑罰","explanation":"指因違法或做錯事而受到的具體後果，例如罰款、禁賽或其他正式處罰；重點是已經施加或將要施加的那項處罰。","examples":[{"en":"The judge gave him a light punishment because it was his first offense.","zh":"因為這是他第一次犯罪，法官給了他較輕的處罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team faced punishment for breaking the league rules.","zh":"這支球隊因違反聯賽規定而面臨處罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punishment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-074f37062561f4fa72aa","word":"pupil","forms":["pupil"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6375cca11ceb605f","term":"pupil","forms":["pupil","pupils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瞳孔","explanation":"指虹膜中央的開口，光線透過這裡進入眼睛。它通常看起來像眼睛中央的黑色圓點，會根據光線強弱擴大或縮小。","examples":[{"en":"Her pupils grew smaller in the bright sunlight.","zh":"在明亮的陽光下，她的瞳孔變小了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor shone a light into his pupil.","zh":"醫生把燈光照進他的瞳孔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pupil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c23e695bd761e07","term":"pupil","forms":["pupil","pupils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學生","explanation":"指在學校中由教師負責指導和教育的學生，尤其常用於英國英語。它保留了“受到某人照看和指導的人”這條核心線索。","examples":[{"en":"Every pupil in the school must wear a uniform.","zh":"這所學校的每名學生都必須穿校服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pupils lined up quietly outside their classroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pupil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b02e0c6135a59245212","word":"puppet","forms":["puppet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d44d8bd2ac56382","term":"puppet","forms":["puppet","puppets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"木偶","explanation":"指能用線、杆或套在手上的方式操縱，使其做出動作的人形或動物形小模型。它的核心特點是自己不會主動行動，而是由操作者控制。","examples":[{"en":"The children watched a puppet show at the community center.","zh":"孩子們在社群中心觀看了一場木偶戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She moved the puppet with two thin rods.","zh":"她用兩根細杆操縱那個木偶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puppet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-643d5cee823aa5da","term":"puppet","forms":["puppet","puppets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傀儡","explanation":"比喻一個人、組織或國家表面上在行動，實際上卻聽命於另一個更有權力的物件；它就像舞臺上的木偶一樣沒有真正的自主權。","examples":[{"en":"The dictator installed a puppet government in the neighboring country.","zh":"那個獨裁者在鄰國扶植了一個傀儡政府。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruler was a puppet controlled by foreign interests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puppet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6588ef4db6a357d6d9ca","word":"puppy","forms":["puppy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ddca2c9bd5e88eb","term":"puppy","forms":["puppy","puppies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幼犬","explanation":"指尚未完全長大的狗，通常是出生後到性成熟前的階段；這是 puppy 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The puppy fell asleep beside her bowl.","zh":"那隻幼犬在自己的食盆旁睡著了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We adopted a puppy from the local shelter.","zh":"我們從當地的動物收容所領養了一隻幼犬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puppy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-066d950dbff99e07","term":"puppy","forms":["puppy","puppies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有幼態的狗；狗","explanation":"可指外表一直顯得幼小、活潑的狗，也可在某些語境中泛指一隻狗；這裡保留的是“像幼犬一樣”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Even at ten, our dog still looks like a puppy.","zh":"我們的狗十歲了，看起來仍像一隻幼犬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come here, puppy; let's get your leash on.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puppy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7048dc8aa7663e713097","word":"purchase","forms":["purchase"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7bf767d89a3535e5","term":"purchase","forms":["purchase","purchases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"購買；購買行為","explanation":"purchase 指付錢或付出等價代價來買東西這一行為，重點是“取得某物所進行的購買”。","examples":[{"en":"The store offers a free dessert with the purchase of a main course.","zh":"這家店購買主菜時贈送一份免費甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Proof of purchase is required for a refund.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purchase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d54263d15f5b409","term":"purchase","forms":["purchase","purchases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"買到的東西","explanation":"purchase 也指花錢買到的具體物品或商品，也就是一次購買的結果。","examples":[{"en":"I am very happy with my latest purchase.","zh":"我對最近買的東西很滿意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carried her purchases home in two paper bags.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purchase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77eb2972438ebfb2","term":"purchase","forms":["purchase","purchases","purchasing","purchased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"購買","explanation":"purchase 作動詞時表示用錢或等價代價買下某物，是最重要、最常見的動詞義項。","examples":[{"en":"They plan to purchase a larger apartment next year.","zh":"他們計劃明年買一套更大的公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She purchased the tickets through the theater's website.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purchase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8ba2ec7e90713c10437","word":"pure","forms":["pure"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6ba298a09d294ed","term":"pure","forms":["pure","purer","more pure","purest","most pure"],"pos":"adj","zh":"純淨無瑕","explanation":"表示沒有瑕疵、汙點或不良成分，既可以說物品，也可以說感情、友誼等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"Their friendship remained pure despite years of competition.","zh":"儘管競爭了多年，他們的友誼仍然真摯無瑕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was moved by the child's pure joy.","zh":"孩子那份純真的快樂打動了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aa4b878624e78ef","term":"pure","forms":["pure","purer","more pure","purest","most pure"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不含雜質","explanation":"表示某種物質中沒有混入其他材料、汙染物或合金，因此成分單一。","examples":[{"en":"The ring is made of pure gold.","zh":"這枚戒指是純金製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sample contains pure copper without other metals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50629139ea9a159925f0","word":"purify","forms":["purify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa71e585624b68a1","term":"purify","forms":["purify","purifies","purifying","purified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"淨化；除去雜質","explanation":"把水、空氣、金屬或其他東西中的雜質去掉，使它變得更純淨；也可指透過某種過程改善其潔淨程度。","examples":[{"en":"This filter purifies the water before it reaches the kitchen.","zh":"這臺過濾器會在水流到廚房前淨化水質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Plants help purify the air inside the building.","zh":"植物有助於淨化建築物內的空氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1d733b21b691190","term":"purify","forms":["purify","purifies","purifying","purified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洗清罪過；淨化心靈","explanation":"把人從罪過、內疚或道德汙點中解脫出來，使其在精神或道德上恢復純潔；這裡的“去除”是比喻性的。","examples":[{"en":"She believed that honest work could purify her heart.","zh":"她相信誠實的勞動能夠淨化自己的心靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ritual was intended to purify the worshippers' souls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6007b44327a48d4678d7","word":"purity","forms":["purity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-202365060e565b8a","term":"purity","forms":["purity","purities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"純淨；純潔；純度","explanation":"purity 指一個東西保持“沒有混入雜質”的狀態或程度：水可以很純淨，金屬可以有高純度，人的思想、動機或行為也可以被說成純潔。它把“沒有雜質”這一畫面從物質層面延伸到了道德和精神層面。","examples":[{"en":"The purity of the water was tested in a laboratory.","zh":"實驗室檢測了這水的純淨度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The purity of her intentions was clear to everyone.","zh":"大家都清楚她的動機是純潔的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e0a1b0ada42172886fd","word":"purple","forms":["purple"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33b2b699c0ecfcfc","term":"purple","forms":["purple","purpler","more purple","purplest","most purple"],"pos":"adj","zh":"紫色的","explanation":"指呈現紅色和藍色之間那種紫色的。它可以描述物體、衣服、天空等，是這個詞最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a purple scarf to the concert.","zh":"她戴著一條紫色圍巾去聽音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sky turned purple before sunset.","zh":"日落前天空變成了紫色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-79b745cfdc1e912d","term":"purple","forms":["purple","purples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紫色","explanation":"指紅色和藍色之間的顏色，通常也包括偏向紫羅蘭或洋紅的一段顏色範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Purple is her favorite color.","zh":"紫色是她最喜歡的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room was decorated in purple.","zh":"房間用紫色裝飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81b06df4303e6581efec","word":"purpose","forms":["purpose"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68d3ce53db2dd6e7","term":"purpose","forms":["purpose","purposes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目的；目標","explanation":"指做某事、製作某物或設立某種安排時想達到的目標，也就是“為什麼要做這件事以及希望得到什麼結果”。","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of this meeting is to agree on the next steps.","zh":"這次會議的目的是確定下一步行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What is the purpose of your visit?","zh":"你來訪的目的是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purpose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-052096752f82bc5b","term":"purpose","forms":["purpose","purposes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人生意義；生活目標感","explanation":"指讓人覺得生活或行動有價值、有方向的意義感。這裡的 purpose 不一定是一個具體目標，而是支撐長期投入和堅持的內在方向。","examples":[{"en":"Volunteering gave her a new sense of purpose.","zh":"做志願者讓她重新找到了生活的意義感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Teaching children gives his life purpose.","zh":"教孩子讓他覺得自己的人生有意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purpose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4566a3eca61559aff973","word":"purse","forms":["purse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f2fb51e6f200367","term":"purse","forms":["purse","purses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錢包；錢袋","explanation":"指用來裝錢的小袋，重點是“裝錢的袋子”，比普通的bag更具體。","examples":[{"en":"She found her keys at the bottom of her purse.","zh":"她在手提包底部找到了鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kept the coins in a small leather purse.","zh":"他把硬幣放在一個小皮錢包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f571e7c2d332077617c","word":"pursue","forms":["pursue"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e213db4e3d48f4a8","term":"pursue","forms":["pursue","pursues","pursuing","pursued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"追趕；追捕","explanation":"指緊緊跟隨某人或某物，通常帶有想趕上、抓住或阻止對方的意味。這是“追著不放”這一核心畫面的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The police pursued the car for several miles.","zh":"警方追趕那輛車追了好幾英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hounds pursued the fox across open fields.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pursue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0924cffbfe5cb1d","term":"pursue","forms":["pursue","pursues","pursuing","pursued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"沿著；採取","explanation":"把“追趕”擴充套件為沿著某條道路、路線或行動方向繼續走，表示選擇並堅持某種做法。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams pursued different strategies.","zh":"兩支隊伍採取了不同的策略。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee pursued a cautious course throughout negotiations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pursue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-328993e8c074844d","term":"pursue","forms":["pursue","pursues","pursuing","pursued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"追求；力爭實現","explanation":"表示持續努力去獲得某個目標、結果或理想，是英語中非常常見的抽象用法。夢想、和平、成功、機會等都可以成為被 pursue 的目標。","examples":[{"en":"She moved abroad to pursue her dream of becoming a designer.","zh":"她搬到國外去追求成為設計師的夢想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should pursue every opportunity to improve the service.","zh":"我們應該抓住每一個改進服務的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pursue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68fcfd9b4d77bfd0af3b","word":"pursuit","forms":["pursuit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-11899262d551e0de","term":"pursuit","forms":["pursuit","pursuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"追逐；追求","explanation":"指持續追趕某人、某物，或努力爭取某個目標，重點在“不斷朝著目標去”。目標可以是實際物件，也可以是財富、成功、知識等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"Her pursuit of excellence has inspired everyone on the team.","zh":"她對卓越的不懈追求鼓舞了團隊中的每個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police car followed in pursuit of the stolen vehicle.","zh":"警車跟在後面追趕那輛被盜車輛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pursuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d2f003c02e0cc91","term":"pursuit","forms":["pursuit","pursuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"興趣活動；業餘愛好","explanation":"指一個人經常投入時間去做的興趣或娛樂活動，通常帶有長期、規律進行的意味，而不只是偶爾做一次。","examples":[{"en":"Reading is a quiet pursuit that helps me relax after work.","zh":"閱讀是一項安靜的興趣活動，能幫助我下班後放松。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fishing and gardening are his favorite leisure pursuits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pursuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d107ea3629c326718876","word":"push","forms":["push"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77716804ee342bed","term":"push","forms":["push","pushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推；推力","explanation":"指一次明確而有方向的施力動作，通常是用手把物體推向前方或推離自己；也可指這種動作產生的推力。它對應記憶中的“向前施力”。","examples":[{"en":"Give the gate a gentle push; it should open.","zh":"輕輕推一下大門，它應該就會開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The box moved forward after one strong push.","zh":"用力推了一下後，箱子向前移動了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/push","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb1620e12881a89a","term":"push","forms":["push","pushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"努力；衝刺","explanation":"指為完成目標而集中投入的一番努力，尤其是在最後階段加把勁。這裡是“給自己施力”，把事情向前推動。","examples":[{"en":"We need one final push to finish the report tonight.","zh":"我們還需要最後衝刺一下，今晚才能完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her extra push helped the team meet the deadline.","zh":"她額外的努力幫助團隊趕上了截止日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/push","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e38cbb32111e0123","term":"push","forms":["push","pushes","pushing","pushed","pushest","pushedst","pusheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推開；推著移動","explanation":"用身體或其他力量使人或物向前、向外或離開施力者，就是實際的“向前施力”。既可以說推某個物體，也可以說人向前推。","examples":[{"en":"She pushed the heavy door open with both hands.","zh":"她用雙手把那扇沉重的門推開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pushed me aside and ran into the room.","zh":"他把我推到一邊，跑進了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/push","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22854f6066966d1f","term":"push","forms":["push","pushes","pushing","pushed","pushest","pushedst","pusheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"催促；勸說","explanation":"不斷給某人施加壓力，勸他採取某種行動，像是把對方往前推。這種施壓可以是催促回答，也可以是勸人接受建議。","examples":[{"en":"My parents keep pushing me to apply for the job.","zh":"我父母一直催我申請那份工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporter pushed the minister for a clear answer.","zh":"記者不斷催促部長給出明確答覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/push","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-373cb2c6d4fe2778441d","word":"put","forms":["put"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3cdbacced51f1ef","term":"put","forms":["put","puts","putting","putten","puttest","puttedst","putteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放置","explanation":"把某物或某人從一個位置放到另一個位置，核心畫面就是“把它放到那裡”。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the keys on the table.","zh":"請把鑰匙放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He put his coat over the back of the chair.","zh":"他把外套搭在椅背上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/put","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-129d53ef87a167d7","term":"put","forms":["put","puts","putting","putten","puttest","puttedst","putteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使處於某種抽象位置或關係","explanation":"把限制、責任、壓力等抽象事物“放到”某人或某事上，也就是施加、歸於或安排某種關係。","examples":[{"en":"The new rules put limits on what companies can advertise.","zh":"新規定限制了公司可以宣傳的內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They put the blame on the wrong person.","zh":"他們把責任歸咎於錯誤的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/put","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60ac38ba2667efc4","term":"put","forms":["put","puts","putting","putten","puttest","puttedst","putteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使進入某種狀態","explanation":"把人或事物“放進”某種狀態、條件或關係中，例如使某人陷入危險、使某物變成某種形式。","examples":[{"en":"The storm put the whole town in danger.","zh":"暴風雨使整個城鎮陷入危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She put the documents into a single file.","zh":"她把這些檔案整理到一個檔案中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/put","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-edeb7da6cbdaf5e4","term":"put","forms":["put","puts","putting","putten","puttest","puttedst","putteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用某種方式表達","explanation":"把想法“放進”某種說法中，表示用特定方式措辭、解釋或表達。","examples":[{"en":"I understand your point when you put it that way.","zh":"你這樣表達時，我就明白你的觀點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"How should I put this without upsetting her?","zh":"我該怎麼說才不會讓她不高興？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/put","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4fba09b856cc0aa0f2b","word":"puzzle","forms":["puzzle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8cefb3a6ee70efde","term":"puzzle","forms":["puzzle","puzzles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"難題；令人費解的事","explanation":"指事情的原因、答案或道理暫時無法理解，讓人不知道該怎樣解釋。","examples":[{"en":"Why the machine stopped is still a puzzle.","zh":"這臺機器為什麼停了，仍然是個謎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden change in his story was a puzzle to everyone.","zh":"他敘述中的突然變化讓所有人都感到費解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d868c5d27a4bd41","term":"puzzle","forms":["puzzle","puzzles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"益智遊戲；解謎題","explanation":"指需要一個人或多人動腦推理、尋找辦法，才能解決或完成的遊戲。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon doing a puzzle together.","zh":"我們一起做益智遊戲，度過了一個下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This puzzle is harder than it looks.","zh":"這個益智遊戲比看上去難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d61b1192ffced86","term":"puzzle","forms":["puzzle","puzzles","puzzling","puzzled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使困惑；使費解","explanation":"指某件事讓人找不到答案或解釋，就像碎片無法拼出完整圖案一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm reaction puzzled me.","zh":"她平靜的反應讓我感到困惑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strange message puzzled the police.","zh":"這條奇怪的資訊讓警方摸不著頭腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4684502d6bebd5fe","term":"puzzle","forms":["puzzle","puzzles","puzzling","puzzled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"苦思；困惑地思考","explanation":"指自己面對難題反覆思考，努力把零散線索拼成答案。","examples":[{"en":"I puzzled over the instructions for half an hour.","zh":"我對著說明琢磨了半個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They puzzled over how the door had opened.","zh":"他們苦苦思索門是怎麼開啟的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puzzle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22ba2d6f2848f4c040f5","word":"pyramid","forms":["pyramid"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a9b174be27d29808","term":"pyramid","forms":["pyramid","pyramids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"古代金字塔","explanation":"指底部通常是方形或長方形、四面向上收成尖頂的大型古代建築，最典型的是埃及用作陵墓的金字塔，也可指中美洲的類似建築。","examples":[{"en":"We visited the pyramids outside Cairo at sunrise.","zh":"我們在日出時參觀了開羅郊外的金字塔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ancient pyramid was built as a royal tomb.","zh":"這座古代金字塔是作為王室陵墓建造的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pyramid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b60b8a9fdcd26248","term":"pyramid","forms":["pyramid","pyramids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金字塔形建築","explanation":"泛指任何做成底部寬、頂部尖的金字塔形建築或大型構造，不一定是古代陵墓。","examples":[{"en":"A glass pyramid stands in the center of the courtyard.","zh":"庭院中央立著一座玻璃金字塔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a small pyramid on its roof.","zh":"那座博物館的屋頂上有一座小金字塔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pyramid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83142e46b908015c","term":"pyramid","forms":["pyramid","pyramids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金字塔式層級","explanation":"指底部人數或專案很多、越往上越少的組織、結構或圖表；核心仍是“底寬頂窄”的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The organization has a broad base and a narrow pyramid of leadership.","zh":"這個組織的基礎很廣，而領導層呈現出底寬頂窄的金字塔結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chart shows a pyramid of workers supporting a small executive team.","zh":"這張圖表顯示，大量員工支撐著一個人數很少的高管團隊，形成金字塔式結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pyramid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aae3ba6bd925f6fa90f7","word":"quake","forms":["quake"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab2f0afb61793918","term":"quake","forms":["quake","quakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"震動；顫抖","explanation":"指身體、物體或周圍環境發生的搖動或顫抖，重點是“動起來”這一感覺，不一定達到地震的強度。","examples":[{"en":"We felt a slight quake every time the train passed.","zh":"火車每次經過時，我們都會感到一陣輕微的震動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The windows quaked as the train passed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0348ed416fe9a66","term":"quake","forms":["quake","quakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地震","explanation":"指地面猛烈震動形成的地震，是“搖動”這一核心意思最常見的自然現象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The region has experienced several minor quakes this year.","zh":"這個地區今年發生了幾次小地震。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The quake damaged several bridges near the coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af8670b07ed2811b","term":"quake","forms":["quake","quakes","quaking","quaked","quoke","quook"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顫抖；震動","explanation":"表示人、物體或地面正在搖動或顫抖，直接描寫可觀察到的震動。","examples":[{"en":"The ground quaked beneath our feet.","zh":"地面在我們腳下震動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The floor quaked as the heavy machinery started.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1dbf39600b5761d58378","word":"qualification","forms":["qualification"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d02205780f53c5c0","term":"qualification","forms":["qualification","qualifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有助於獲得資格的能力或訓練","explanation":"指讓人更有機會透過門檻的能力、經驗、技能或專業訓練，尤其常指求職時具備的專業資歷。這裡強調“你具備什麼條件”，不一定強調已經拿到哪一張證書。","examples":[{"en":"Her qualifications for the position include five years of teaching experience.","zh":"她勝任這個職位的資歷包括五年的教學經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You have the qualifications to lead this project.","zh":"你具備領導這個專案的資歷和能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f6803bfc51aeab8","term":"qualification","forms":["qualification","qualifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"課程或考試合格後獲得的證書","explanation":"指完成課程、培訓或考試後正式獲得的證書、文憑或學位，是“透過門檻”留下來的憑據。這個用法在英國英語中尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"She gained a teaching qualification after completing the course.","zh":"她完成課程後取得了教師資格證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This qualification is recognized by employers across the country.","zh":"全國各地的僱主都認可這項資格證書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e48cfe4f6f37ec01bfb2","word":"qualify","forms":["qualify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5c186405e439a68","term":"qualify","forms":["qualify","qualifies","qualifying","qualified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"符合條件，算作","explanation":"某人或某事滿足規定條件，就 qualify for 某機會、身份或待遇，或 qualify as 某一類事物；也就是說，它跨過了“條件門檻”。","examples":[{"en":"If you meet the income requirement, you qualify for the housing program.","zh":"如果你達到收入要求，就有資格參加住房專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This small mistake does not qualify as a serious offense.","zh":"這個小錯誤不算嚴重違法行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dff10b1773ee98fe","term":"qualify","forms":["qualify","qualifies","qualifying","qualified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使具備資格","explanation":"qualify 也可以表示透過學習、訓練或經歷使某人達到任職或執行任務所需的能力和條件；反身用法則是“使自己具備資格”。","examples":[{"en":"Two years of training qualified her for the position.","zh":"兩年的培訓使她具備了擔任這個職位的資格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This certificate qualifies you to teach beginners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-600c6ef725352a7c","term":"qualify","forms":["qualify","qualifies","qualifying","qualified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"限定、修正說法","explanation":"qualify 一句話或一個判斷，就是給它加上條件、範圍或保留意見，使它不再無條件地適用於所有情況；這仍然是“加門檻、劃範圍”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She qualified her criticism by admitting that the plan had some strengths.","zh":"她承認這個計劃有一些優點，從而對自己的批評作了限定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report qualifies its conclusion with several important conditions.","zh":"這份報告用幾個重要條件限定了它的結論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qualify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acef2c15bcd349db900d","word":"quality","forms":["quality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa4fde2ab0bdc8a4","term":"quality","forms":["quality","qualities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"質量；品質","explanation":"表示某人或某物整體上好不好、水平高不高。它可以評價產品、服務、教育、工作以及人的表現。","examples":[{"en":"This school is well known for the high quality of its teachers.","zh":"這所學校以教師的高水平而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The quality of the food has improved.","zh":"食物的質量提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a7b308d8df661bad433","word":"quantity","forms":["quantity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8eb336fa1efa63c0","term":"quantity","forms":["quantity","quantities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數量；量","explanation":"quantity 是談“有多少”或“量有多大”的總稱，可以指物品的件數、物質的多少，也可以指一個數值所代表的量。它強調數量這一方面，常與 quality（質量）形成對比。","examples":[{"en":"The quantity of food we waste each week is shocking.","zh":"我們每週浪費的食物量大得驚人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company values quality over quantity.","zh":"這家公司重視質量勝過數量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quantity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c55f7b1605a6d6de","term":"quantity","forms":["quantity","quantities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一定量；多少","explanation":"這裡的 quantity 指還沒有精確說出的某一部分或某種程度的量，相當於“多少、一點量”。重點不是具體數字，而是指出確實取了或需要了某個量。","examples":[{"en":"Add a small quantity of salt to the soup.","zh":"在湯里加少量鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a large quantity of paper for the project.","zh":"這個專案需要大量紙張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quantity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dfc7e3b71bc98f59e014","word":"quarrel","forms":["quarrel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c68aaf5eb23ffeee","term":"quarrel","forms":["quarrel","quarrels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭吵；爭執","explanation":"指帶有火氣的口頭爭吵，通常是兩個人或幾個人因為某件事吵起來，而不只是平靜地表達不同意見。這是現代英語中最值得優先掌握的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We had a quarrel about who should pay the bill.","zh":"我們因為誰該付賬吵了一架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their small quarrel ended when both of them apologized.","zh":"他們的小爭吵在雙方道歉後結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarrel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2dbebf6e916c044","term":"quarrel","forms":["quarrel","quarrels","quarreling","quarrelling","quarreled","quarrelled","quarrelest","quarrellest","quarrelledst","quarreleth","quarrelleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"爭吵；鬧翻","explanation":"指激烈地爭論、吵架，甚至因此不再友好。它就是“帶著不滿吵起來”這條核心記憶線上動詞中的展開。","examples":[{"en":"The two brothers often quarrel over the television remote.","zh":"這兩兄弟經常為了電視遙控器吵架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She quarreled with her friend and left the party early.","zh":"她和朋友吵了一架，早早離開了聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarrel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16b60e9de6072d0e93d3","word":"quarter","forms":["quarter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-591e039c398f0356","term":"quarter","forms":["quarter","quarters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"四分之一","explanation":"指整體被分成四份後的一份，既可表示具體物體的一部分，也可表示數量或比例。","examples":[{"en":"A quarter of the pizza is still on the table.","zh":"披薩還有四分之一在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a quarter of the students arrived on time.","zh":"只有四分之一的學生準時到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9c3c1f7674502331a5a","word":"queen","forms":["queen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a54ca534474045f","term":"queen","forms":["queen","queens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國王的王后","explanation":"指國王的妻子、配偶或遺孀；核心形象是王室中擁有特殊地位的女性，但她本人不一定是統治者。","examples":[{"en":"The king and queen welcomed the guests together.","zh":"國王和王后一起迎接了賓客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the king died, the queen continued to live in the palace.","zh":"國王去世後，王后仍繼續住在宮殿裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7f8df3ef8cf486b","term":"queen","forms":["queen","queens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女性君主","explanation":"指以君主身份統治國家的女性；她的地位來自繼承或統治權，而不只是與國王的婚姻關係。","examples":[{"en":"The queen addressed the nation after the election.","zh":"選舉結束後，女王向全國發表了講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Queen Victoria ruled for more than sixty years.","zh":"維多利亞女王統治了六十多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e28bafe0cb1e3171","term":"queen","forms":["queen","queens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棋類等遊戲中的“後”","explanation":"在國際象棋等棋類遊戲中，指威力最強的棋子“後”；這個意義仍保留了“處於最高地位、力量最強”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"She moved her queen to protect the king.","zh":"她移動後去保護王。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The player sacrificed the queen to win the game.","zh":"這名棋手犧牲了後，以贏得比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d296bb84c0deefd6","term":"queen","forms":["queen","queens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜂群等昆蟲的繁殖雌蟲","explanation":"指螞蟻、蜜蜂、白蟻或黃蜂群體中負責繁殖的雌蟲，是整個群體的繁殖核心。","examples":[{"en":"The worker bees surrounded the queen in the hive.","zh":"工蜂在蜂巢裡圍在蜂王周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A healthy queen can keep the colony growing.","zh":"健康的蜂王能讓蜂群持續發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8171c4ecae07283cff5d","word":"queer","forms":["queer"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7ca2b82ee3c7386","term":"queer","forms":["queer","queerer","queerest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇怪的；不同尋常的","explanation":"表示某人或某物偏離通常狀態，因而顯得奇怪、古怪或與眾不同。這是理解該詞“偏離常規”核心意象的起點。","examples":[{"en":"There was something queer about the old house.","zh":"那所老房子有些古怪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a queer look when I mentioned his name.","zh":"我提到他的名字時，她用一種奇怪的眼神看著我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ac1a1c7143cb2199eb40","word":"quest","forms":["quest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-961aed1c4358ed77","term":"quest","forms":["quest","quests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"追尋；使命","explanation":"指為了一個重要或遠大的目標而踏上一段通常較長、較投入的旅程或行動，重點在“帶著目標去完成一項使命”。","examples":[{"en":"The young explorer began a quest to find the lost temple.","zh":"這位年輕的探險家開始了一段尋找失落神廟的旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her quest for justice lasted many years.","zh":"她追求正義的努力持續了許多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11082854d2bd2ecb","term":"quest","forms":["quest","quests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尋找；追求","explanation":"表示主動尋找、追求或設法獲得某物，既可以指實際尋找，也可以指對知識、真理等抽象目標的追求。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists are on a quest for a cleaner source of energy.","zh":"科學家們正在尋找更清潔的能源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent years in quest of the truth.","zh":"他花了多年時間追求真相。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f5087db919ced5c123c","word":"question","forms":["question"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2331e7d6c0333df9","term":"question","forms":["question","questions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問題；疑問句","explanation":"question是為了得到資訊、答覆或反應而說出或寫出的問句，也可以只是一兩個詢問性的詞。它對應記憶中的“把未知處敲出來”：說話人希望對方給出答案。","examples":[{"en":"I have a question about the bus schedule.","zh":"我想問一個關於公交車時刻表的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please write your questions on the card.","zh":"請把你們的問題寫在卡片上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/question","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d69727e2f9a927c1","term":"question","forms":["question","questions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疑問；質疑","explanation":"當question指對事實、準確性或有效性的懷疑時，它表示“這個說法經不起確認”。這仍然是把未知處敲出來，只是目的從求資訊變成檢查某事是否可信。","examples":[{"en":"Several experts have questioned the accuracy of the report.","zh":"幾位專家質疑了這份報告的準確性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His explanation has come under question.","zh":"他的解釋受到了質疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/question","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3529750fc0ce9211","term":"question","forms":["question","questions","questioning","questioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"詢問；盤問","explanation":"question某人就是把未知處直接向對方問出來，以獲取資訊；語氣可從普通詢問到正式盤問不等。它對應記憶中的主動動作：把問題投向一個人。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter questioned the mayor about the new plan.","zh":"記者就新計劃詢問市長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police questioned him for two hours.","zh":"警方盤問了他兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/question","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e57ac4e89ad5634d","term":"question","forms":["question","questions","questioning","questioned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"質疑；懷疑","explanation":"question某事表示不輕易接受它為真、正確或合理，而是要求重新檢查。這裡不是向某人索取資訊，而是把某個看似確定的說法敲開一個缺口。","examples":[{"en":"Many people questioned the decision to close the library.","zh":"許多人質疑關閉圖書館的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She began to question whether the story was true.","zh":"她開始懷疑這個故事是否屬實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/question","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba8850dcf4bd973fa65e","word":"questionnaire","forms":["questionnaire"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6eae78980f1898f8","term":"questionnaire","forms":["questionnaire","questionnaires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收集資訊的問題表","explanation":"問卷就是把許多問題集中在一張表格或一份電子表單中，讓人們回答，從而收集意見、資料或調查資料。","examples":[{"en":"Please complete the questionnaire before the interview.","zh":"請在面試前填寫這份問卷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our questionnaire asks visitors how they first heard about the museum.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/questionnaire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22c72aa82ce77c82e2ca","word":"quick","forms":["quick"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f2768a10b448055","term":"quick","forms":["quick","quicker","more quick","quickest","most quick"],"pos":"adj","zh":"速度快的","explanation":"表示移動、行動或完成任務的速度快，重點是比通常更迅速。","examples":[{"en":"We need a quick response before the meeting starts.","zh":"我們需要在會議開始前迅速作出回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is quick on his feet and reached the door first.","zh":"他動作很快，第一個到了門口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ce859254dd8af89","term":"quick","forms":["quick","quicker","more quick","quickest","most quick"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很快完成的","explanation":"表示某件事發生或完成所用的時間很短，例如快速吃飯、快速決定。","examples":[{"en":"I only have time for a quick lunch today.","zh":"我今天只有時間快速吃個午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a quick lunch before the meeting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c5bf5f9d2b7652f","term":"quick","forms":["quick","quicker","quickest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"迅速地","explanation":"表示以很快的速度做某事，或要求事情儘快完成。","examples":[{"en":"She finished the form quick and went back to work.","zh":"她很快填完表格，回去繼續工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come quick; the train is about to leave.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-008f0747f4e27c8462ba","word":"quiet","forms":["quiet"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2dd8ea8f02ba257d","term":"quiet","forms":["quiet","quieter","more quiet","quietest","most quiet"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聲音很小","explanation":"表示幾乎沒有聲音，或聲音小到不容易聽見，是 quiet 最直接、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The library is quiet in the early morning.","zh":"圖書館一大早很安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep quiet while the baby is sleeping.","zh":"寶寶睡覺時請保持安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21b85c225ed2cf3f","term":"quiet","forms":["quiet","quieter","more quiet","quietest","most quiet"],"pos":"adj","zh":"活動少而平靜","explanation":"把“沒有被打擾”的感覺從聲音擴充套件到動作和活動：海面、天氣或場面都可以 quiet，表示平靜、不喧鬧。","examples":[{"en":"The lake is quiet after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，湖面很平靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a quiet evening at home.","zh":"我們在家度過了一個安靜的夜晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ae41a1563ca746a","term":"quiet","forms":["quiet","quiets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無聲、安靜","explanation":"指周圍沒有聲音，或聲音突然消失後的安靜狀態，是形容詞 quiet 名詞化後的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"We enjoyed the quiet of the countryside.","zh":"我們享受鄉間的寧靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden quiet made the empty house feel strange.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65b8037675ab0cb6","term":"quiet","forms":["quiet","quiets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"靜止、平和","explanation":"指沒有明顯動作或變化的平靜狀態，例如風浪停歇、環境安穩；它承接了“沒有被打擾”的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"After the festival, the town settled into a welcome quiet.","zh":"節日過後，小鎮恢復了令人舒心的平靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She treasured the quiet of early Sunday mornings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-799f95b460f6a1e9","term":"quiet","forms":["quiet","quiets","quieting","quieted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……安靜","explanation":"表示主動消除聲音或騷動，讓人、動物或環境回到安靜狀態，是把那片“沒有被打擾的水面”帶回來的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher tried to quiet the class before the test.","zh":"考試前，老師試圖讓全班安靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse quieted the frightened child.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8b2eacffb5d4d4065e7","word":"quilt","forms":["quilt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66a86d223612603d","term":"quilt","forms":["quilt","quilts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"絎縫被子","explanation":"指把兩層布夾住填充物，再縫合固定而成的被子，通常也帶有圖案或裝飾性的針腳。記住“夾層並縫起來”這個畫面，就能和普通毯子區分開。","examples":[{"en":"My grandmother is sewing a quilt for the guest room.","zh":"我祖母正在為客房縫製一床被子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tucked the patchwork quilt around the sleeping child.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quilt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6d288e302a5b1b4","term":"quilt","forms":["quilt","quilts","quilting","quilted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縫製被子","explanation":"指用絎縫法制作一床 quilt，也就是把布層和填充物縫合固定。這個動詞義就是名詞“絎縫被子”中製作動作的展開。","examples":[{"en":"She quilted a baby blanket from soft cotton squares.","zh":"她用柔軟的棉布方塊縫製了一條嬰兒毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandmother quilts during the long winter evenings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quilt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8577da2ea54085708b3b","word":"quit","forms":["quit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5d711ae8fee4acc","term":"quit","forms":["quit","quits","quitting","quitted","quittest","quittedst","quitteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離開某地","explanation":"表示離開一個地點，強調從那裡退出，不只是暫時走開；這正是“從某個狀態或空間中出來”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The workers quit the building when the fire alarm rang.","zh":"火警響起時，工人們離開了大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They quit the city before the siege began.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f439e90dc8d4af3","term":"quit","forms":["quit","quits","quitting","quitted","quittest","quittedst","quitteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辭去工作或職位","explanation":"表示離開自己的工作、職位或任職崗位，也就是從職業身份中退出；這是日常英語中非常重要的用法。","examples":[{"en":"He quit his job to start a small business.","zh":"他辭去工作，開始經營一家小企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He quit his job to care for his mother.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e11824b2f5e7d8ce","term":"quit","forms":["quit","quits","quitting","quitted","quittest","quittedst","quitteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停止或戒掉","explanation":"表示不再繼續某項活動，尤其常指戒掉吸菸、飲酒等習慣；可以理解為從正在進行的行為中退出。","examples":[{"en":"My sister quit drinking last year.","zh":"我姐姐去年戒了酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He quit smoking after the birth of his daughter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a3058157de8b004fc5d","word":"quite","forms":["quite"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3379992d72cb1d33","term":"quite","forms":["quite"],"pos":"adv","zh":"完全；十分","explanation":"程度刻度推到頂端，表示某事徹底達到某種狀態，相當於“完全、十分”。","examples":[{"en":"The room was quite empty when we arrived.","zh":"我們到達時，房間裡完全空著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I quite understand your concern.","zh":"我完全理解你的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ef5f222ca226896","term":"quite","forms":["quite"],"pos":"adv","zh":"相當；有點","explanation":"程度刻度停在中間，表示達到了一定程度但沒有到頂，常譯為“相當、挺、比較”或“有點”。","examples":[{"en":"The basement is quite wet after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，地下室相當潮溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This book is quite easy to read.","zh":"這本書讀起來比較容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c59435a1e9474332701f","word":"quiver","forms":["quiver"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bae0cc5e00a3e4a","term":"quiver","forms":["quiver","quivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"箭袋","explanation":"指弓箭手用來裝箭的袋子或容器，也可裝弩箭、飛鏢等。記住“箭被集中收在袋中”這個畫面，就能理解它的基本義。","examples":[{"en":"The archer reached behind him and pulled an arrow from his quiver.","zh":"弓箭手伸手到身後，從箭袋裡抽出一支箭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carried a leather quiver filled with hunting arrows.","zh":"她帶著一個裝滿獵箭的皮箭袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7de065f4811436b","term":"quiver","forms":["quiver","quivers","quivering","quivered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕輕顫動","explanation":"指身體、聲音、樹葉等出現輕微而連續的抖動，像受到風吹的葉片一樣微微震顫。它可以由寒冷、緊張、激動或外力引起，但詞本身只說明動作，不限定原因。","examples":[{"en":"Her voice quivered as she told the audience the news.","zh":"她向觀眾宣佈訊息時，聲音微微顫抖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaves quivered in the evening breeze.","zh":"樹葉在晚風中輕輕顫動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d98ce221dd52eccf27c","word":"quiz","forms":["quiz"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5dcf1f1b6134491","term":"quiz","forms":["quiz","quizzes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問答比賽","explanation":"quiz可以是一場圍繞一連串問題展開的比賽，參加者靠回答問題得分，常見於酒吧、聚會、廣播或線上活動。","examples":[{"en":"Our team won the Friday night quiz at the local pub.","zh":"我們隊贏得了當地酒吧週五晚上的問答比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The host prepared a quiz about famous films.","zh":"主持人準備了一場關於著名電影的問答比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiz","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b878a6801d9a9e68b30e","word":"quota","forms":["quota"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29c3a1f32c934f62","term":"quota","forms":["quota","quotas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分配的份額","explanation":"指總量分配給某個人、團體或地區的那一部分，重點是“每方應得的一份”。這個意義是其他意義的基礎：當這份被分配的數量被正式規定下來，就可以進一步表示指標或限額。","examples":[{"en":"Each team received an equal quota of supplies.","zh":"每個團隊都分到了同等的物資份額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villages were given a quota of water for the dry season.","zh":"這些村莊獲分了一定的旱季用水份額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quota","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22849769d7b34997","term":"quota","forms":["quota","quotas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"規定的數量或指標","explanation":"指事先規定好的數量或百分比，可以是必須完成的目標、必須達到的最低數，也可以是不能超過的最高數。例如，銷售人員每月要完成的銷售量，就可以叫作 quota。","examples":[{"en":"The sales team reached its monthly quota ahead of schedule.","zh":"銷售團隊提前完成了月度指標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university has a quota of 200 new students for the program.","zh":"這所大學為該專案規定了招收兩百名新生的名額。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quota","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcd9bd43bf8c849a3d27","word":"quotation","forms":["quotation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d7b17799c4529e1","term":"quotation","forms":["quotation","quotations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引用語；引文","explanation":"指從某人的講話、文章或文學作品中原樣摘出、由別人再次說出或寫出的一段話。它強調的是被拿出來使用的具體語言片段，而不是引用這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"She began her speech with a quotation from a famous poem.","zh":"她用一首著名詩歌中的一段引文開始了演講。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wrote down that quotation because it perfectly described the situation.","zh":"我把那段引文記了下來，因為它恰好描述了當時的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quotation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b19e50f05558cbee","term":"quotation","forms":["quotation","quotations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報價；報價單","explanation":"指賣方為商品、服務或工程提出的價格，常常是供買方比較和決定的一份正式金額。它和“把原話報出來”共享同一個核心：把明確的資訊遞給別人。","examples":[{"en":"We asked three companies for a quotation for the kitchen renovation.","zh":"我們向三家公司詢問了廚房翻新的報價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We requested a quotation for replacing the windows.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quotation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6327245c3a45d3d9ea72","word":"quote","forms":["quote"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49e81df53b76e5d6","term":"quote","forms":["quote","quotes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引語；引用的話","explanation":"quote 是從某人說過或寫過的話中原樣取出的句子或一段話，重點是保留原來的措辭。","examples":[{"en":"She shared a quote from her favorite author.","zh":"她分享了自己最喜歡的作家說過的一句引語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Begin the essay with a short quote from the novel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e5074ce715800d3","term":"quote","forms":["quote","quotes","quoting","quoted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引用原話","explanation":"quote 作動詞時，表示把某人的準確措辭複述出來，讓聽者知道這些話確實出自那個人。","examples":[{"en":"The article quoted the minister's exact words.","zh":"這篇文章引用了部長的原話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She quoted a line from the poem.","zh":"她引用了這首詩中的一句話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-011999bba6b45ea7","term":"quote","forms":["quote","quotes","quoting","quoted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給出工作報價","explanation":"quote 作動詞時可以表示根據工作內容估算並報出費用，也就是告訴客戶這項服務大概要花多少錢。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic quoted me $300 for the repair.","zh":"修理工報給我三百美元的維修費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you quote us for painting the whole house?","zh":"你能給我們報一下整棟房子的刷漆費用嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d37d96b42ad43384915e","word":"rabbit","forms":["rabbit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d4a4df89b8172f9","term":"rabbit","forms":["rabbit","rabbits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兔子","explanation":"指一種長耳、後腿發達、尾巴短而蓬鬆的哺乳動物；既可指一隻兔，也可泛指這種動物。","examples":[{"en":"A rabbit appeared at the edge of the garden.","zh":"一隻兔子出現在花園邊上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rabbits can run surprisingly fast.","zh":"兔子跑得快得出奇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rabbit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a3a8ead184f2012","term":"rabbit","forms":["rabbit","rabbits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兔肉","explanation":"指作為食物的兔子肉，而不是活著的動物。","examples":[{"en":"They served rabbit with roasted vegetables.","zh":"他們端上了兔肉和烤蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stew contains rabbit, carrots, and fresh herbs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rabbit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-129ce50dd90bf2448587","word":"race","forms":["race"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b5c1c6a25b802b6","term":"race","forms":["race","races"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽；賽跑","explanation":"人、動物或車輛朝同一個目標衝去，並以誰先到達來競爭，這就是 race。它既可以指一次具體比賽，也可以泛指這類競賽。","examples":[{"en":"She won the race by less than a second.","zh":"她以不到一秒的優勢贏得了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children had a race to the gate.","zh":"孩子們比賽跑到大門口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/race","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f651b1c52f3b3b49","term":"race","forms":["race","races"],"pos":"noun","zh":"種族；族群","explanation":"指被認為具有共同祖先、歷史傳承或某些共同特徵的人群。這個詞涉及社會和歷史分類，不能簡單理解為每個人都能被清楚分開的自然類別。","examples":[{"en":"The city is home to people of many races and backgrounds.","zh":"這座城市居住著許多不同種族和背景的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Race has shaped the country's history in complex ways.","zh":"種族問題以複雜的方式塑造了這個國家的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/race","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f4385d34074a836","term":"race","forms":["race","races","racing","raced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加比賽","explanation":"表示參加以速度或到達先後決定勝負的比賽，也就是朝著目標衝去並與別人競爭。","examples":[{"en":"Several young athletes will race in the final tomorrow.","zh":"幾名年輕運動員明天將在決賽中參賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He races every weekend to stay fit.","zh":"他每個週末參加比賽，以保持健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/race","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80fc21686fe127cd","term":"race","forms":["race","races","racing","raced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"疾馳；趕快","explanation":"表示人、車輛等以很快的速度移動，或為了及時到達而匆忙趕去，延續了“朝著目標衝去”的記憶。","examples":[{"en":"She raced to the station when she heard the announcement.","zh":"聽到通知後，她趕緊衝向車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ambulance raced through the city.","zh":"救護車飛快地穿過城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/race","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-669c3696c4bfceb8daf0","word":"racial","forms":["racial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edeb681e71156748","term":"racial","forms":["racial","more racial","most racial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"種族的；與種族有關的","explanation":"凡是涉及不同種族、族群及其身份或關係的事物，都可以用 racial 來描述。它只是在給話題貼上“和種族有關”的標籤，具體是討論差異、平等還是衝突，要由後面的語境決定。","examples":[{"en":"The report examines racial inequality in the workplace.","zh":"這份報告研究了職場中的種族不平等問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school has students from many racial backgrounds.","zh":"這所學校的學生來自許多不同的種族背景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/racial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3d476abc838e2fec5780","word":"racism","forms":["racism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d9b3b2179bcb8ec","term":"racism","forms":["racism","racisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"種族優劣觀念","explanation":"指認為不同人類種族天生具有決定能力的差異，並進一步認為某些種族優於另一些種族的思想。這是“按種族給人分高低”的起點，後面的制度和行為都可能從這種觀念發展出來。","examples":[{"en":"Racism is based on the false belief that one race is naturally better than another.","zh":"種族主義建立在一種錯誤觀念之上，即一個種族天生比另一個種族優越。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Education can challenge the racist ideas that children learn at home.","zh":"教育可以挑戰孩子在家中學到的種族主義觀念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/racism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aecff978fab08cc0","term":"racism","forms":["racism","racisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"種族偏見或歧視","explanation":"指基於種族或族裔的偏見、排斥和不公平對待，也可以指一次具體的種族歧視行為。它是那把“按種族分高低的尺子”在現實人際交往中的直接表現。","examples":[{"en":"She reported the racist abuse because she did not want others to face the same racism.","zh":"她舉報了這種種族主義辱罵，因為她不希望別人遭遇同樣的種族歧視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The players refused to tolerate racism in the stadium.","zh":"球員們拒絕容忍體育場內的種族歧視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/racism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e9d1a8d5b1863f1e99e","word":"rack","forms":["rack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66da0b6c1cf68e89","term":"rack","forms":["rack","racks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"架子；置物架","explanation":"一種由一層或多層擱板組成的承託結構，用來放置或整理物品，正體現了把 rack 記成“承託的架子”。","examples":[{"en":"We put the books on a rack beside the window.","zh":"我們把書放在窗邊的書架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kitchen rack holds all our spices.","zh":"廚房置物架上放著我們所有的香料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-318e5973abc1d585","term":"rack","forms":["rack","racks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車輛或船上的行李架","explanation":"安裝在車輛或船上、用於承託和攜帶行李等物品的架子，是“承託的架子”這一核心形象的具體應用。","examples":[{"en":"We secured the bicycles to the roof rack.","zh":"我們把腳踏車固定在車頂行李架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please place your bag on the luggage rack.","zh":"請把你的包放到行李架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89e001f16c1bf64a","term":"rack","forms":["rack","racks","racking","racked","rackest","rackedst","racketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放上架子","explanation":"把物品放到架子上，或掛在架子上；這個動作正對應記憶鉤子裡“承託物品的架子”。","examples":[{"en":"She racked the clean plates after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，她把乾淨的盤子放上架子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rack the clean plates before they dry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f847222471c34240","term":"rack","forms":["rack","racks","racking","racked","rackest","rackedst","racketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使痛苦不堪","explanation":"使某人遭受強烈的身體或精神痛苦，好像被力量拉伸到極限，正與記憶鉤子中的“拉伸到極限”相連。","examples":[{"en":"The constant pain racked him for months.","zh":"持續的疼痛折磨了他好幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Guilt racked him after he betrayed their trust.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff2e963ff6d0c33aae94","word":"radar","forms":["radar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa36d4a3e2823d08","term":"radar","forms":["radar","radars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雷達探測技術","explanation":"指透過發出無線電波並分析反射訊號，發現遠方目標、判斷其位置或運動情況的一種探測方法。這裡的雷達重點是“探測過程或技術”，不一定指某一臺機器。","examples":[{"en":"The crew used radar to track the storm.","zh":"機組人員用雷達追蹤這場風暴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Radar detected a ship moving through the fog.","zh":"雷達探測到一艘船正在霧中航行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a44b4665df6a4247","term":"radar","forms":["radar","radars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雷達系統","explanation":"指按照某種平臺、頻率、功率或配置設計的一整套雷達系統。它強調“某一種型號或系統”，而不是雷達技術這個總稱。","examples":[{"en":"The airport installed a new radar to guide arriving planes.","zh":"機場安裝了一套新的雷達來引導進場飛機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Radar detected the vessel through the heavy fog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7252b3b66124954aa44","word":"radiant","forms":["radiant"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f536dd654895435d","term":"radiant","forms":["radiant","more radiant","most radiant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"發光發熱的","explanation":"指光或熱從某個物體向外放射，最常用於太陽、火焰或其他能量來源。核心畫面是光線從中心散出去。","examples":[{"en":"The radiant sun warmed the fields after the rain.","zh":"雨後，散發著光和熱的太陽溫暖了田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Radiant heat from the fire filled the small room.","zh":"火焰散發的熱量充滿了小房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81fd6ea7c394fee8","term":"radiant","forms":["radiant","more radiant","most radiant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容光煥發的","explanation":"形容人的臉、笑容或神態洋溢著快樂、活力和滿足感，好像內在的光芒向外散發。","examples":[{"en":"She looked radiant after hearing the good news.","zh":"聽到這個好訊息後，她看起來容光煥發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His radiant smile welcomed everyone into the room.","zh":"他燦爛的笑容讓房間裡的每個人都感到親切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b71f6d5e519b708c9f0","word":"radiate","forms":["radiate"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-282f34b2ab782876","term":"radiate","forms":["radiate","more radiate","most radiate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"放射狀的","explanation":"指各部分從同一個中心向外分開，像太陽光線或車輪輻條一樣排列。","examples":[{"en":"The mineral forms a radiate crystal.","zh":"這種礦物形成放射狀晶體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shell has a radiate pattern.","zh":"這個貝殼帶有放射狀圖案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4eae8b2a208266d4","term":"radiate","forms":["radiate","radiates","radiating","radiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從中心向外延伸","explanation":"指道路、線條、枝條等從同一個中心向四周展開，核心畫面仍是太陽光線向外伸展。","examples":[{"en":"Several narrow streets radiate from the old market.","zh":"幾條狹窄的街道從老市場向外延伸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Paths radiate from the garden's central fountain.","zh":"小路從花園中央的噴泉向四周伸展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db079b194b8635bf","term":"radiate","forms":["radiate","radiates","radiating","radiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出光、熱或波","explanation":"指某個物體主動向外釋放光、熱或其他能量，就像中心向四周射出看不見的光線。","examples":[{"en":"The metal roof radiates heat all afternoon.","zh":"金屬屋頂整個下午都在散發熱量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lamp radiates a soft, warm light.","zh":"這盞燈發出柔和而溫暖的光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a3de6c1ffc7676f","term":"radiate","forms":["radiate","radiates","radiating","radiated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從某處散發出來","explanation":"指光、熱或波從某個來源向外傳出，強調它們從哪裡出來，而不是來源主動把它們發出去。","examples":[{"en":"Warmth radiated from the stone wall.","zh":"溫暖從石牆上散發出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heat radiated from the newly lit stove.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23e6580eace0c3c4a169","word":"radiation","forms":["radiation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6563e179fd88291","term":"radiation","forms":["radiation","radiations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"波或粒子的輻射過程","explanation":"指波或粒子從某個來源向外發射、傳播的過程，例如電磁波或粒子從物體中輻射出來。","examples":[{"en":"Radiation from the sun reaches Earth in about eight minutes.","zh":"來自太陽的輻射大約八分鐘就能到達地球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The device detects radiation emitted by distant stars.","zh":"這臺裝置能探測到遙遠恆星發出的輻射。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b74c6b344bb42379","term":"radiation","forms":["radiation","radiations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"放射性輻射","explanation":"特指放射性物質或核反應釋放出的能量、波或粒子，可能對人體和環境造成傷害；這是日常新聞中最常見的“輻射”義之一。","examples":[{"en":"Workers were evacuated after radiation levels rose near the plant.","zh":"工廠附近的輻射水平升高後，工作人員被疏散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor warned that too much radiation can damage healthy tissue.","zh":"醫生警告說，過量輻射會損傷健康組織。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-909c272051bb6b905677","word":"radical","forms":["radical"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81485dff90755f92","term":"radical","forms":["radical","more radical","most radical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"主張根本改變的；激進的","explanation":"指主張從根本上改變制度、觀念或現狀，而不是隻作小幅修補；也可形容這種主張本身。","examples":[{"en":"Her radical ideas changed the way the team worked.","zh":"她的激進想法改變了團隊的工作方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government proposed radical reforms to the education system.","zh":"政府提出了對教育制度進行根本改革的方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca9780334af5dd71","term":"radical","forms":["radical","more radical","most radical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"根本的；本質的","explanation":"指某事物屬於最基本、最內在的性質，觸及它成立或存在的根基，而不只是表面特徵。","examples":[{"en":"The dispute reflects a radical difference in their values.","zh":"這場爭議反映出他們的價值觀存在根本差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal calls for a radical change in priorities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c18b2a35dd8e2990","term":"radical","forms":["radical","radicals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"根；數學中的根","explanation":"在數學中，指透過乘方關係得到的根，例如一個數的平方根；它保留了“從根部找出基礎量”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The student found the radical of 49 correctly.","zh":"這名學生正確求出了 49 的平方根。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Simplify the radical before combining the terms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa3a05d9d57c08d694cf","word":"radio","forms":["radio"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3262c87ff6a5044e","term":"radio","forms":["radio","radios"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無線電技術","explanation":"指利用電磁波調製並傳送聲音或其他訊號的技術，也就是記憶影象中的“電波通道”本身，而不是某一臺具體裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team sent a message by radio.","zh":"救援隊透過無線電傳送了一條訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Radio made communication with distant ships possible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5ccaf537b6b10e1","term":"radio","forms":["radio","radios"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收音機","explanation":"指接收無線電波並把其中的聲音播放出來的裝置，即日常最常見的“收音機”。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a lovely song on the radio.","zh":"我們在收音機裡聽到了一首很好聽的歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The radio sits on the kitchen windowsill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9f80516bd839426","term":"radio","forms":["radio","radios","radioes","radioing","radioed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用無線電傳送訊息","explanation":"指透過雙向無線電把訊息、座標或求救內容傳給另一臺裝置或另一名無線電操作員，就是把資訊送進記憶影象中的電波通道。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers radioed the park office for help.","zh":"徒步者用無線電向公園管理處求救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captain radioed their position to the coastguard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a301e035663a51f3aca","word":"radioactive","forms":["radioactive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64297b70e5809f61","term":"radioactive","forms":["radioactive","more radioactive","most radioactive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有放射性的","explanation":"指某種物質會發出輻射，因而具有放射性；這種性質可能需要檢測、隔離或防護。","examples":[{"en":"The soil near the old mine is radioactive.","zh":"那座舊礦附近的土壤具有放射性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers sealed the radioactive waste in special containers.","zh":"工人把放射性廢料封存在專用容器裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radioactive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b93751689d48324374b5","word":"radish","forms":["radish"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3b42d65a2388126","term":"radish","forms":["radish","radishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蘿蔔這種植物","explanation":"指蘿蔔屬中作為植物生長的蘿蔔，重點是整株植物，而不只是被吃的根。可以把它想成土裡長著根、地面上有葉子的那種菜。","examples":[{"en":"We grow radishes in the garden every spring.","zh":"我們每年春天都在菜園裡種蘿蔔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sow radishes between rows of slower-growing vegetables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57311c45651397d7","term":"radish","forms":["radish","radishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蘿蔔根，蘿蔔食材","explanation":"指從這種植物土裡取出的根，作為食物食用；它常生吃，也可以烹調，味道有時帶辛辣感。這是日常買菜、做沙拉和談飲食時最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She sliced a radish and put it in the salad.","zh":"她切了一個蘿蔔放進沙拉里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These radishes are crisp and slightly spicy.","zh":"這些蘿蔔很脆，帶一點辛辣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-981979a22bad8c7cdc44","word":"radius","forms":["radius"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd6220629d7c42bd","term":"radius","forms":["radius","radii","radiuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"從中心到圓周的線段","explanation":"在圓或球中，radius 是連線中心與圓周或球面的線段。核心畫面就是一根從中心伸向邊界的輻條。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a circle with a radius of three centimeters.","zh":"畫一個半徑為三釐米的圓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The radius of the planet is about 6,400 kilometers.","zh":"這顆行星的半徑約為六千四百公里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radius","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0144cf279b3c260","term":"radius","forms":["radius","radii","radiuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"半徑的長度","explanation":"radius 也可以不強調那條線段本身，而專門指從中心到邊界這一段的長度，也就是通常所說的“半徑”。","examples":[{"en":"The radius is five meters, so the diameter is ten meters.","zh":"半徑是五米，所以直徑是十米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The circle has a radius of six centimeters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radius","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3e690053061793bb12a","word":"rag","forms":["rag"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1532367ee3e2c19a","term":"rag","forms":["rag","rags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舊布片","explanation":"指一小塊舊布，尤其是用來擦拭、清潔、打補丁或包紮的布片；這是“rag”最基本的“破舊、粗糙的東西”這一形象。","examples":[{"en":"Use a damp rag to wipe the dust off the table.","zh":"用一塊溼抹布把桌上的灰塵擦掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She patched the hole with an old rag.","zh":"她用一塊舊布補上了那個洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a66a1104fb6e5881","term":"rag","forms":["rag","rags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低劣報刊","explanation":"非正式且帶貶義地指報紙或雜誌，暗示其新聞質量差；這是從“破舊、粗糙的東西”引申出的用法。","examples":[{"en":"That rag printed another ridiculous story about the mayor.","zh":"那家破報紙又刊登了一篇關於市長的可笑報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That sensationalist rag invents scandals to attract readers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b780b0f78f1d2f7f","term":"rag","forms":["rag","rags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拉格泰姆樂曲","explanation":"指拉格泰姆風格的歌曲、舞蹈或器樂曲，是“rag”在音樂領域的另一條詞義分支。","examples":[{"en":"The band played a lively rag at the end of the concert.","zh":"音樂會最後，樂隊演奏了一首歡快的拉格泰姆樂曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pianist opened with a lively rag.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e59389d9c81735276474","word":"rage","forms":["rage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4d3f682708721f1","term":"rage","forms":["rage","rages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴怒","explanation":"指強烈而難以控制的憤怒，像情緒突然衝破了理智。它既可以指這種情緒本身，也可以指一次暴怒發作。","examples":[{"en":"He stormed out of the room in a rage.","zh":"他暴怒地衝出了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sudden rage frightened everyone at the meeting.","zh":"她突然爆發的怒火嚇到了會議上的所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8d09b1cea02972e","term":"rage","forms":["rage","rages","raging","raged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"憤怒地發作","explanation":"指人在強烈憤怒中激烈地說話或行動，是名詞“暴怒”變成動作後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She raged against the unfair decision for hours.","zh":"她對這個不公平的決定憤怒地抗議了幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He raged at the reporter during the interview.","zh":"採訪時他對那名記者大發雷霆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65e50ce38fad2edf104c","word":"ragged","forms":["ragged"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd12b23a07226f80","term":"ragged","forms":["ragged","more ragged","most ragged"],"pos":"adj","zh":"破爛的；破碎的","explanation":"指東西破破爛爛，表面或整體像被撕裂、磨損過一樣，不再完整整齊。","examples":[{"en":"He was wearing a ragged coat in the cold wind.","zh":"他在寒風中穿著一件破舊的外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flag hung in ragged strips from the pole.","zh":"那面旗子撕成參差不齊的布條，掛在旗杆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ragged","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb2f2ab900e6deb4","term":"ragged","forms":["ragged","more ragged","most ragged"],"pos":"adj","zh":"參差不齊的；邊緣粗糙的","explanation":"指邊緣或形狀不平整，像被撕開或隨意弄斷一樣高低不齊。","examples":[{"en":"The path wound between ragged rocks and dry grass.","zh":"小路蜿蜒穿過參差不齊的岩石和枯草之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut the paper along a ragged edge.","zh":"她沿著參差不齊的邊緣把紙剪開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ragged","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-263dae9af8f889601ab6","word":"raid","forms":["raid"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-961265732b3cf8cb","term":"raid","forms":["raid","raids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突襲；襲擊","explanation":"指戰鬥中突然、快速地衝擊敵方或侵入某處的行動，重點是出其不意和行動迅速。它可以是小規模的襲擊，也可以是一次短促的入侵。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers launched a night raid on the enemy camp.","zh":"士兵們在夜間突襲了敵軍營地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village was destroyed during the raid.","zh":"村莊在那次突襲中被毀了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4aa6ac1e75a13c1","term":"raid","forms":["raid","raids"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突擊搜查；突襲抓捕","explanation":"指警方或其他執法人員突然進入某處抓捕人員、查封或奪取財物，常用於查處違法活動。這裡的“突襲”重點不在戰場，而在執法行動的突然性和集中性。","examples":[{"en":"Police raided the warehouse early this morning.","zh":"警方今天清晨突擊搜查了那座倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The raid led to three arrests and the seizure of illegal drugs.","zh":"這次突襲搜查導致三人被捕，警方還繳獲了非法毒品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd528ccc6aa6fe46","term":"raid","forms":["raid","raids","raiding","raided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突襲；突擊搜查","explanation":"表示對某個地方或目標發動突然而快速的襲擊，也可表示警方突然進入某處進行搜查。它把名詞所說的突襲行動變成了一個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The police raided the club after receiving several complaints.","zh":"警方接到幾次投訴後突擊搜查了那傢俱樂部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rebels raided the border town before dawn.","zh":"叛軍在黎明前突襲了邊境小鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8ff47839b16021d","term":"raid","forms":["raid","raids","raiding","raided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"順手拿取；搜刮","explanation":"表示為了滿足自己的需要而迅速從某處拿走東西，常帶有隨手翻找、一掃而空或未經正式許可的感覺。比如“突襲冰箱”就是把裡面能吃的東西拿出來。","examples":[{"en":"I raided the kitchen for something sweet after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我翻遍廚房，找了點甜食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children raided the snack cupboard while we were out.","zh":"我們外出時，孩子們把零食櫃翻了個遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fdf0d7533af5b16df5f1","word":"rail","forms":["rail"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f50343a185d47b59","term":"rail","forms":["rail","rails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"欄杆；橫杆","explanation":"橫向固定在支撐物之間、用來扶靠、阻擋或分隔的杆就是 rail，例如樓梯或船上的欄杆。","examples":[{"en":"She held on to the rail as the boat rocked.","zh":"船搖晃時，她抓住了欄杆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A metal rail keeps visitors away from the cliff edge.","zh":"一道金屬欄杆把遊客與懸崖邊隔開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e17473e4d0f2e124","term":"rail","forms":["rail","rails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵軌","explanation":"火車車輪在上面執行的金屬長條叫 rail；通常兩根並列的 rails 一起構成軌道。","examples":[{"en":"Workers replaced a damaged rail overnight.","zh":"工人連夜更換了一根損壞的鐵軌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train stayed on the rails despite the heavy rain.","zh":"儘管下著大雨，火車仍在鐵軌上行駛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-befe72f93ecde742","term":"rail","forms":["rail","rails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵路運輸","explanation":"rail 也可以把鐵路看作一種交通方式，表示乘火車或透過鐵路運輸。","examples":[{"en":"We sent the equipment by rail to the northern factory.","zh":"我們把裝置透過鐵路運到了北方的工廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They traveled by rail across the country.","zh":"他們乘火車穿越了全國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-691037e26fd9318e64fe","word":"railroad/railway","forms":["railroad","railway"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fa589e2189ccb77","term":"railroad","forms":["railroad","railroads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵軌；鐵路","explanation":"指鋪設固定金屬軌道、供列車或類似車輛行駛的線路。這裡關注的是列車行駛的實體軌道，而不一定包括車輛、人員和運營機構。","examples":[{"en":"The railroad runs through the mountain pass.","zh":"這條鐵路穿過山口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many railroads follow the routes of older roads.","zh":"許多鐵路沿用了舊道路的路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/railroad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a8482ec6324b3245","term":"railroad","forms":["railroad","railroads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵路運輸系統","explanation":"指由鐵路軌道、列車以及相關運輸設施組成的整體系統，重點不只是地面上的鐵軌，而是透過鐵路運送人和貨物的運輸方式。","examples":[{"en":"The railroad carries thousands of passengers every day.","zh":"鐵路運輸系統每天運送數千名乘客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The railroad links inland farms with coastal ports.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/railroad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03accd7375e1be4b","term":"railroad","forms":["railroad","railroads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強行倉促推進","explanation":"比喻把某項程式像列車沿固定鐵軌一樣硬推向終點，指不充分考慮意見、證據或正常步驟就迅速完成，通常暗含不公平或不妥當。","examples":[{"en":"The committee railroaded the proposal through without hearing objections.","zh":"委員會沒有聽取反對意見，就強行透過了這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trial felt like a railroad from the beginning.","zh":"這場審判從一開始就像是在走過場、強行定案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/railroad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6b9aea3df494e66","term":"railway","forms":["railway","railways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵路運輸系統","explanation":"指由鐵路線路、列車及相關運營組成的運輸體系，重點是“用鐵路運送乘客或貨物”這一整體，而不只是地面上的鐵軌。","examples":[{"en":"The railway connects the coastal towns with the capital.","zh":"這條鐵路把沿海城鎮和首都連線起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The national railway connects every major coastal city.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/railway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2232abef66e66f3f","term":"railway","forms":["railway","railways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵軌線路","explanation":"指鋪有兩條平行鐵軌、供火車等有輪車輛行駛的具體線路；它就是“鐵做的路”這一核心形象的直接體現。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers followed the old railway for several miles.","zh":"徒步者沿著那條舊鐵路走了好幾英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A railway runs along the valley floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/railway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-319b44c570a417ff3444","word":"rain","forms":["rain"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b37c8690665373f","term":"rain","forms":["rain","rains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雨；雨水","explanation":"指雲中凝結的水落到地面，即通常所說的雨。它通常不是一滴一滴單獨計數，而是把雨看作一種天氣現象或水。","examples":[{"en":"The rain kept falling all afternoon.","zh":"雨下了一整個下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had heavy rain last night.","zh":"昨晚下了大雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cacc19d743267a7f","term":"rain","forms":["rain","rains","raining","rained","rainest","rainedst","raineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下雨","explanation":"指雨從天空落下。這裡不是某個人主動做的動作，而是天氣現象，因此句子通常使用無實際指代物件的主語形式。","examples":[{"en":"It may rain before we get home.","zh":"我們到家前可能會下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It rained all morning.","zh":"整個上午都在下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fced00b6ce281456d69","word":"rainbow","forms":["rainbow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-effb865e2fd58562","term":"rainbow","forms":["rainbow","rainbows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"彩虹","explanation":"指雨滴把陽光折射成的、出現在天空中的多色弧形光帶。這是 rainbow 最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a bright rainbow after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，我們看見了一道明亮的彩虹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A rainbow appeared above the fields.","zh":"田野上方出現了一道彩虹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainbow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f4275b4242b69f0","term":"rainbow","forms":["rainbow","rainbows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"各種各樣的事物","explanation":"指種類、選擇或可能性非常豐富的一組事物，彷彿把許多不同顏色集中在一起。常用來表達“多種多樣”，不一定真的和顏色有關。","examples":[{"en":"The market offers a rainbow of fresh fruits.","zh":"這個市場提供各種各樣的新鮮水果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival brought a rainbow of musical styles together.","zh":"這個節日彙集了各種各樣的音樂風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainbow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6958aab121d91a7aeff","word":"raincoat","forms":["raincoat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"raincoat","forms":["raincoat"],"pos":"n.","zh":"雨衣","examples":[{"en":"Take a raincoat because a storm is coming.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Her yellow raincoat was easy to spot in the crowd.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-91bcb5a9bbf8b08a2821","word":"rainfall","forms":["rainfall"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-578a6d001228ea76","term":"rainfall","forms":["rainfall","rainfalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"降雨量","explanation":"指某次降雨或某一段時間內落下的雨水總量，通常可以透過雨量計測量。這裡的重點是“落下了多少雨”，而不是單純有沒有下雨。","examples":[{"en":"The rainfall this month is twice the yearly average.","zh":"本月的降雨量是年平均降雨量的兩倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rainfall caused flooding in several villages.","zh":"強降雨導致幾個村莊發生洪水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainfall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-613af24a6a792ef1","term":"rainfall","forms":["rainfall","rainfalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"降雨；下雨現象","explanation":"指雨水從天空落下這一自然現象，強調“下雨發生了”，不一定強調具體雨量。它和“降雨量”是同一幅畫面的兩個側面：一個看過程，一個看數量。","examples":[{"en":"The rainfall began shortly after noon.","zh":"降雨在中午過後不久開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rainfall continued throughout the night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainfall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b9e10dfed0288d691f7","word":"rainy","forms":["rainy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dfdcd82bf80d81c0","term":"rainy","forms":["rainy","rainier","rainiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"下雨的；多雨的","explanation":"指天空被雨籠罩的天氣，可能正在下雨，也可以泛指某一天、某段時間多雨或常下陣雨。它把“雨”看成天氣的整體特徵，而不是隻描述某一刻的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Because of the rainy weather, we stayed home and watched a movie.","zh":"因為天氣多雨，我們待在家裡看了一部電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was a rainy day, but the children still played outside.","zh":"那天下著雨，不過孩子們還是在外面玩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e49b5c7a9e738d485bc7","word":"raise","forms":["raise"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fec9626c4141ee51","term":"raise","forms":["raise","raises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"加薪","explanation":"指工資或薪水增加，通常是工作中得到的加薪。","examples":[{"en":"The boss gave me a raise.","zh":"老闆給我加薪了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She got a raise after taking on more responsibilities.","zh":"她承擔了更多責任後獲得了加薪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c37092b14e5ff34","term":"raise","forms":["raise","raises","raising","raised","raisest","raisedst","raiseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"舉起","explanation":"讓某物從較低位置向上移動，常用於手、手臂、旗幟或物體。","examples":[{"en":"Please raise your hand if you have a question.","zh":"如果你有問題，請舉手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He raised the box onto the shelf.","zh":"他把箱子舉到架子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b7dd07a04beb276","term":"raise","forms":["raise","raises","raising","raised","raisest","raisedst","raiseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提高；增加；培養","explanation":"把數量、水平、質量或某種狀態往上推，因此可表示提高價格、增加資金、培養孩子或發展某種能力。","examples":[{"en":"The company raised its prices last month.","zh":"那家公司上個月提高了價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are raising money for the new library.","zh":"他們正在為新圖書館籌款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9aa26756cc9def1c1f97","word":"raisin","forms":["raisin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5253672243d2bb9e","term":"raisin","forms":["raisin","raisins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葡萄乾","explanation":"葡萄失去水分後會縮小、變皺，形成raisin，也就是葡萄乾。","examples":[{"en":"I added a handful of raisins to my morning oatmeal.","zh":"我在早上的燕麥粥里加了一把葡萄乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child picked a raisin out of the cookie.","zh":"那個孩子從餅乾裡挑出了一顆葡萄乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raisin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afd5c5ae5738e2754912","word":"rally","forms":["rally"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dda636a8eb7e83a1","term":"rally","forms":["rally","rallies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"集會；造勢大會","explanation":"指許多人為了共同的事業、候選人或目標聚集在一起，以演講、鼓動等方式形成支援力量。它突出“把人聚攏起來鼓舞士氣”，不一定是在抗議。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of supporters attended the campaign rally in the city center.","zh":"數千名支持者參加了市中心的競選造勢大會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rally brought together people who wanted safer roads.","zh":"這次集會把希望道路更安全的人們聚集到了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-380ef634fca12a8d","term":"rally","forms":["rally","rallies","rallying","rallied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重新集合；整頓","explanation":"指把已經分散、混亂或受挫的人重新召集起來，使他們恢復秩序並繼續共同努力。它就是把散開的力量重新聚攏。","examples":[{"en":"The captain rallied the team after they fell behind.","zh":"球隊落後後，隊長重新鼓舞並團結了隊員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leader rallied supporters around the new plan.","zh":"這位領導者把支持者團結到新計劃周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ed15b24f6b905bc7","term":"rally","forms":["rally","rallies","rallying","rallied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重新聚攏；恢復隊形","explanation":"指原本分散或陷入混亂的一群人重新集合，恢復有組織的行動。與及物義相比，這裡重點是隊伍自己重新形成秩序。","examples":[{"en":"The players rallied together and turned the game around.","zh":"隊員們重新團結起來，扭轉了比賽局勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The retreating troops rallied behind the stone bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d480be68b0993805","term":"rally","forms":["rally","rallies","rallying","rallied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"恢復體力或精神","explanation":"指人在疲憊、沮喪、昏厥或生病後重新聚起身體或精神力量，恢復清醒和狀態。這裡是把自己的力量重新集中起來。","examples":[{"en":"She rallied her strength and finished the climb.","zh":"她重新振作起來，完成了攀登。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He slowly rallied after the operation.","zh":"手術後他的身體慢慢恢復了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rally","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1d648cffa6e2ba0f94c","word":"ranch","forms":["ranch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-797572f73f3d582e","term":"ranch","forms":["ranch","ranches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大型牧場","explanation":"指面積較大的土地，主要用來飼養牛、羊等牲畜；這是一片土地、生產場所和生活空間結合在一起的牧場。","examples":[{"en":"Her family owns a large ranch in Montana.","zh":"她家在蒙大拿州擁有一座大型牧場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The horses spend most of the day out on the ranch.","zh":"這些馬大部分時間都在牧場上活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ranch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1aba811cd8043e4","term":"ranch","forms":["ranch","ranches","ranching","ranched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經營牧場","explanation":"指負責管理和經營牧場，包括照料牲畜、安排土地使用等；也就是把 ranch 當作事業來經營。","examples":[{"en":"After college, she returned home to ranch with her parents.","zh":"大學畢業後，她回家和父母一起經營牧場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They ranch cattle on land that has been in the family for generations.","zh":"他們在家族傳了好幾代的土地上經營養牛業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ranch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a441b15fe9a3cf566611","word":"random","forms":["random"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09b94c4a287529ea","term":"random","forms":["random","more random","most random"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無規則、無明確原因的","explanation":"指事情發生得沒有明顯原因或安排，顯得雜亂而難以預料；重點是看不出背後的固定規律。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused random power cuts across the city.","zh":"暴風雨導致全城各處毫無規律地停電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He kept receiving random messages from unknown numbers.","zh":"他不斷收到陌生號碼發來的莫名其妙的資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/random","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96e9b4cfc83f94ba","term":"random","forms":["random","more random","most random"],"pos":"adj","zh":"機率上不可預測的","explanation":"在數學、統計學或科學語境中，指結果無法逐次預測，但可以用機率分佈來描述；理想情況下，各種結果的機會相等。","examples":[{"en":"The computer selects a random number between one and ten.","zh":"計算機在一到十之間隨機選擇一個數字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We used a random sample of five hundred households.","zh":"我們採用了五百戶家庭的隨機樣本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/random","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2269c0be009b610cfdbb","word":"range","forms":["range"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29a0f162c84ddbe8","term":"range","forms":["range","ranges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"山脈或一系列建築","explanation":"事物像被排開一樣連續延伸時，range可指一列山脈、建築物或其他成排的東西。這個意義體現了“排開並延展開來”的記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A long mountain range separates the two valleys.","zh":"一條綿延的山脈把兩個山谷分隔開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel stands among a range of old stone buildings.","zh":"這家旅館坐落在一排古老的石砌建築之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/range","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98a478888319d99c","term":"range","forms":["range","ranges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇範圍；一系列","explanation":"range可指排開的一系列可供選擇的事物，尤其常用於商品、服務、價格或型別。它強調選擇的寬窄和多樣程度。","examples":[{"en":"The store offers a wide range of affordable bicycles.","zh":"這家商店提供各種價格實惠的腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students can choose from a range of evening classes.","zh":"學生可以從一系列晚間課程中選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/range","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bac431c186f794e2","term":"range","forms":["range","ranges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"到目標的距離","explanation":"range可指人、感測器或觀察點到某個目標之間的距離，也就是目標延伸到觀察者這一端的遠近。它常用於說明某物在多遠處。","examples":[{"en":"We saw the lighthouse at a range of three miles.","zh":"我們看到了三英里外的燈塔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The device can detect movement within a range of ten meters.","zh":"這臺裝置能探測到十米範圍內的移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/range","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81495dda47279614","term":"range","forms":["range","ranges","ranging","ranged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漫遊；遍歷","explanation":"表示在一個地區或範圍內到處走動、漫遊，不一定有明確目的；可以把它想成人在排開並延展開來的空間裡來回走。","examples":[{"en":"Wolves range over a large area in search of food.","zh":"狼會在很大的區域內四處活動尋找食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent the summer ranging through the countryside.","zh":"她整個夏天都在鄉間各處漫遊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/range","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a8460f6b1bf96a87116","word":"rank","forms":["rank"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-714bd91a3ec205f8","term":"rank","forms":["rank","ranks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一排；一列","explanation":"指按一定次序橫向或縱向排成的一列人或物，核心畫面就是“排好的一行”。","examples":[{"en":"The children stood in two ranks for the photograph.","zh":"孩子們為拍照站成了兩排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The front rank moved forward first.","zh":"前排先向前移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e429256312878c9","term":"rank","forms":["rank","ranks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名次；排名","explanation":"指某人或某物按照成績、質量、受歡迎程度等標準排出的具體位置；它是“排成一列”在比較中的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The school ranks first in the region.","zh":"這所學校在該地區排名第一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a rank of 23 in the national list.","zh":"她在全國榜單中排名第二十三。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5fd7e0e85506aedd","term":"rank","forms":["rank","ranks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍銜；組織級別","explanation":"指軍隊或其他組織中的正式等級，決定一個人的職位層次；這仍是“佇列中的位置”變成制度化等級。","examples":[{"en":"She rose to the rank of captain.","zh":"她晉升到了上尉軍銜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every officer wears a badge showing their rank.","zh":"每名軍官都佩戴顯示其軍銜的徽章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fecbf77d6408c9f5","term":"rank","forms":["rank","ranks","ranking","ranked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排名","explanation":"表示某人或某物在比較中處於第幾名，是把物件排成次序後的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Our team ranked second in the tournament.","zh":"我們的隊伍在錦標賽中排名第二。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This book ranks among the year's best sellers.","zh":"這本書躋身年度暢銷書之列。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d0520a7f8b28e68","term":"rank","forms":["rank","ranks","ranking","ranked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排列；分類","explanation":"表示按照某個標準給物件安排合適的位置或類別，即把雜亂的物件排出秩序。","examples":[{"en":"The website ranks restaurants by customer reviews.","zh":"這個網站按顧客評價給餐館排名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Experts ranked the proposal as a high priority.","zh":"專家把這項提案列為高優先順序。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7c465019a477431771a","word":"rap","forms":["rap"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-235492f60cafe4e2","term":"rap","forms":["rap","raps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啪的一擊；敲擊聲","explanation":"指用硬物快速而有力地打一下，也可以指這種短促的敲擊聲。它是 rap 最基本的“啪地敲一下”這個畫面。","examples":[{"en":"There was a loud rap on the window.","zh":"窗戶上傳來一聲響亮的敲擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave the table a quick rap with his knuckles.","zh":"他用指關節在桌上快速敲了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fdc91dd6e32d08c","term":"rap","forms":["rap","raps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"責備；責任","explanation":"把“被敲打”引申為受到懲罰或責備，因此 rap 可以指某件事帶來的責任，尤其是一個人需要承擔的過錯。","examples":[{"en":"She made the mistake, but I took the rap for it.","zh":"錯誤是她犯的，但最後由我承擔了責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took the rap for his partner's mistake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64743673d08ca9e7","term":"rap","forms":["rap","raps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說唱音樂","explanation":"指以有節奏的語言表達為特點的音樂型別。它和“快速、帶節拍地說話”的感覺相連，是現代英語中最常見的 rap 義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"My brother listens to rap while he studies.","zh":"我弟弟學習時會聽說唱音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rap became popular with young listeners around the world.","zh":"說唱音樂在世界各地的年輕聽眾中流行起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ee6118994b5253368f0","word":"rapid","forms":["rapid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86b48c7fe1e1ddad","term":"rapid","forms":["rapid","more rapid","rapider","most rapid","rapidest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"快速的；迅速的","explanation":"指某種動作、變化或流動在很短時間內完成，速度明顯快。它是 rapid 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The rapid growth of the city has put pressure on its roads.","zh":"這座城市的快速發展給道路帶來了壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river becomes rapid after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨過後，這條河的水流變得很急。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rapid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50270c12c086cb3616ad","word":"rare","forms":["rare"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fe2ac0e4469cf74a","term":"rare","forms":["rare","rarer","rarest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"稀有的；少見的","explanation":"指某種東西數量很少，或很少遇到、很少發生，因此不常見。它既可以說具體物品，也可以說機會、現象等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"It is rare to see snow here in April.","zh":"這裡四月下雪很少見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a rare collection of old maps.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了一批稀有的舊地圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da3084a79a4bfd43","term":"rare","forms":["rare","rarer","more rare","rarest","most rare"],"pos":"adj","zh":"肉煎得很生","explanation":"指肉只經過很短時間的加熱，外部可能已經熟了，但內部仍然紅，含有較明顯的生肉狀態。這個義項可以和“稀有、少見”的核心義分開記作餐飲用語。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered my steak rare with a side salad.","zh":"我點了一份煎得很生的牛排，配一份沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prefers her beef rare and juicy.","zh":"她喜歡牛肉煎得很生、汁水充足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f6f064362e732b6e4c2","word":"rash","forms":["rash"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39c7e271252094a6","term":"rash","forms":["rash","rasher","rashest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"輕率的；魯莽的","explanation":"形容人在沒有認真考慮風險和後果時就做決定、說話或行動。核心不是單純“快”，而是因為過於衝動而顯得不謹慎。","examples":[{"en":"It was rash of him to quit his job without having another one lined up.","zh":"他還沒有找到下一份工作就辭職，實在太輕率了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She regretted making such a rash decision.","zh":"她後悔做出了這樣魯莽的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0499e7245a6abb38","term":"rash","forms":["rash","rashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮疹；紅疹","explanation":"皮膚受到過敏、刺激或其他因素影響後，出現一片發紅、發炎的斑點或小疙瘩，有時還會充滿液體或膿。這裡的 rash 是皮膚上突然冒出的一片異常痕跡。","examples":[{"en":"I got a red rash on my arms after using the new soap.","zh":"我用了這種新肥皂後，手臂上起了紅疹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor said the rash was probably caused by an allergy.","zh":"醫生說這種皮疹可能是過敏引起的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9950cec246ece55e46c9","word":"rat","forms":["rat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81debe7bca538592","term":"rat","forms":["rat","rats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"老鼠","explanation":"指鼠屬的一種中等大小齧齒動物，通常有尖嘴、短腿和長尾巴。","examples":[{"en":"A rat ran across the kitchen floor.","zh":"一隻老鼠跑過了廚房地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers tested the drug on rats.","zh":"研究人員在老鼠身上測試了這種藥物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c549779d79e5c8e9c9a6","word":"rate","forms":["rate"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb12409af49731ca","term":"rate","forms":["rate","rates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比例；比率","explanation":"表示一個數量相對於另一個數量的關係，例如單位時間內生產多少、人口如何變化。它是“用尺子衡量”的基礎義。","examples":[{"en":"The rate of online shopping has increased sharply this year.","zh":"今年網上購物的比例大幅上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine produces ten bottles at a rate of one minute.","zh":"這臺機器每分鐘生產十瓶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6f3c91d4f199746","term":"rate","forms":["rate","rates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"速度","explanation":"表示某人或某物移動得有多快，是把“衡量尺”用在運動上。","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist was traveling at a remarkable rate.","zh":"那名騎腳踏車的人騎得非常快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water escaped at a rate of two liters per minute.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5dddcd45e5af3fc2","term":"rate","forms":["rate","rates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變化或進展的速度","explanation":"表示生產、增長、進步等變化進行得快不快，重點不是移動，而是過程發展的速度。","examples":[{"en":"The rate of recovery varies from patient to patient.","zh":"每位病人的恢復速度各不相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The infection spread at an alarming rate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc7bd24ab3001246","term":"rate","forms":["rate","rates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統一收費標準","explanation":"指同類商品、服務或事務統一採用的一檔價格或收費標準，例如郵費、房費或運費。","examples":[{"en":"What is the standard rate for sending this package?","zh":"寄這個包裹的標準收費是多少？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel charges a flat rate for airport transfers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5fcf966766d7bd6a","term":"rate","forms":["rate","rates","rating","rated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"評定等級；排名","explanation":"按某個標準給人或物確定等級或名次，就像把它放到衡量尺上的某一格。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant is rated among the best in the city.","zh":"這家餐廳被評為全市最好的餐廳之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide rates hotels according to comfort and service.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-864861c5d46be35e","term":"rate","forms":["rate","rates","rating","rated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"評價價值或能力","explanation":"對某人或某物的價值、能力或質量作出估量，決定它在衡量尺上的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The coach rates her highly as a defender.","zh":"教練高度評價她作為防守球員的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Critics rate her among the country's finest poets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fea61bddd2bffcc","term":"rate","forms":["rate","rates","rating","rated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為；看作","explanation":"表示說話人認為某人或某物屬於某種水平或性質，是從“評價”進一步發展出的主觀判斷。","examples":[{"en":"I rate this as one of her strongest performances.","zh":"我認為這是她最出色的表現之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I rate her among the finest contemporary sculptors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1ffaf0265bbf7e10a65","word":"rather","forms":["rather"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a12a1ac2d4f5b9e2","term":"rather","forms":["rather"],"pos":"adv","zh":"寧願；更願意","explanation":"表示在兩個選擇中更偏向前者，常譯為“寧願、比較想要”。它把記憶中的“岔路口選擇”直接說出來：選擇一件事，而不選擇另一件事。","examples":[{"en":"I would rather stay home than go out tonight.","zh":"今晚我寧願待在家裡，也不想出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'd rather walk than wait for another bus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31583a85da601b95","term":"rather","forms":["rather"],"pos":"adv","zh":"相反；反而","explanation":"用於否定或糾正前面的說法，表示真正情況恰恰相反。它像是在岔路口把話題改道：不是前面說的方向，而是另一個方向。","examples":[{"en":"The plan was not meant to save money; rather, it was meant to save time.","zh":"這個計劃不是為了省錢；相反，它是為了節省時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs didn't save money; rather, they increased costs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c68d867664e9e3b2","term":"rather","forms":["rather"],"pos":"adv","zh":"相當；頗為","explanation":"放在形容詞或副詞前表示程度不低，常譯為“相當、頗為”。它可以帶出一點出乎預期的感覺，好像對程度重新作了衡量。","examples":[{"en":"The test was rather difficult, but everyone finished it.","zh":"這次考試相當難，但大家都做完了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The climb was rather steeper than we expected.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fdcdf8d87307f0d0b131","word":"ratify","forms":["ratify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02ffebc87fe93a4d","term":"ratify","forms":["ratify","ratifies","ratifying","ratified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"正式批准","explanation":"指有權機構對已經談妥或簽署的條約、協議等給予正式認可，使它從一份約定變成具有官方效力的檔案。","examples":[{"en":"The parliament ratified the agreement after a long debate.","zh":"議會經過長時間辯論後正式批准了這項協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treaty will take effect once all member states ratify it.","zh":"這項條約將在所有成員國正式批准後生效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ratify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f04a79ef13b95c1f6a2","word":"ratio","forms":["ratio"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26eddcc379e6d4a6","term":"ratio","forms":["ratio","ratios","rationes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兩個物件之間的比率","explanation":"ratio 表示把兩個明確指出的物件放在一起比較後得到的關係，例如比較男性和女性的人數，或比較兩種資源的數量。它關注的是“一個相對於另一個是多少”，不只是某個孤立的數字。","examples":[{"en":"The ratio of students to teachers is about twenty to one.","zh":"學生與教師的比例大約是二十比一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study found a nearly equal ratio of men to women.","zh":"這項研究發現，男性和女性的比例幾乎相等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ratio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9961f4cf15e90a98","term":"ratio","forms":["ratio","ratios","rationes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兩個數量的相對大小","explanation":"在算術中，ratio 指透過比較兩個數量而得到的相對大小，通常可以用商來表示。例如 2 比 3 的 ratio 是 2:3，也可以理解為一個數量相對於另一個數量的大小。","examples":[{"en":"Mix the paint and water in a ratio of two to one.","zh":"按二比一的比例混合顏料和水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mix the liquids in a ratio of three to one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ratio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fda503e47e82c440d7c5","word":"rational","forms":["rational"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8f576d89d6b98a5","term":"rational","forms":["rational","more rational","most rational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有理性的","explanation":"指能夠運用推理和判斷來思考，而不是隻憑衝動或本能。它常描述人，也可以描述人的思維能力。","examples":[{"en":"Humans are rational creatures capable of learning from experience.","zh":"人類是有理性的生物，能夠從經驗中學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to remain rational when the situation becomes stressful.","zh":"情況變得緊張時，儘量保持理性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0bb37d0c2cfa29e","term":"rational","forms":["rational","more rational","most rational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合乎邏輯的","explanation":"指一個說法、解釋或論證前後連貫，有依據，不自相矛盾，也不荒謬。重點在想法本身是否講得通。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a rational explanation for the unexpected delay.","zh":"她為這次意外的延誤給出了合乎邏輯的解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is no rational reason to reject the proposal.","zh":"沒有合乎邏輯的理由拒絕這項提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-309f3cbb242242718db4","word":"rattle","forms":["rattle"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8fbb756de523835","term":"rattle","forms":["rattle","rattles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"會噠噠響的物體","explanation":"指被搖動或碰撞時會發出噠噠聲的物體，例如嬰兒搖鈴或裝有小物件的玩具。這個意思抓住了“裡面或本身在晃動併發聲”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The baby shook the rattle and laughed.","zh":"嬰兒搖著撥浪鼓笑了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a small rattle in the gift box.","zh":"禮盒裡有一個小搖鈴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rattle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-152ce52baf86e618","term":"rattle","forms":["rattle","rattles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噠噠聲；格格聲","explanation":"指物體鬆動、碰撞或被搖動時發出的連續而不規則的噠噠聲。它既可以指聽見的一陣聲音，也可以指機器或車輛持續發出的異響。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a strange rattle under the car.","zh":"我聽見車底傳來一陣奇怪的噠噠聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rattle of loose windows kept us awake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rattle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb3fdb74720c774a","term":"rattle","forms":["rattle","rattles","rattling","rattled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搖響；使發出噠噠聲","explanation":"指搖動、敲擊或碰撞某物，使它發出連續的噠噠聲。重點不是單純移動，而是移動造成了這種聲音。","examples":[{"en":"The wind rattled the loose window.","zh":"風把鬆動的窗戶吹得哐啷作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He rattled the chain to get the dog's attention.","zh":"他搖響鏈子來吸引狗的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rattle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13a85e54af347836","term":"rattle","forms":["rattle","rattles","rattling","rattled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使慌亂；使心神不寧","explanation":"指突發的訊息、壓力或意外使人失去鎮定，彷彿內心被震得搖晃不穩。常見的過去分詞 rattled 表示“慌了、亂了陣腳”。","examples":[{"en":"The unexpected question rattled him.","zh":"這個出乎意料的問題讓他慌了神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't get rattled by one bad result.","zh":"不要因為一次糟糕的結果就亂了陣腳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rattle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa29aea9f4e19395","term":"rattle","forms":["rattle","rattles","rattling","rattled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出噠噠聲","explanation":"指物體自身因震動、鬆動或被碰撞而發出連續的噠噠聲。與及物義不同，這裡不強調誰讓它發聲。","examples":[{"en":"The old fan rattles whenever it starts.","zh":"那臺舊風扇每次啟動都會噠噠作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Something is rattling inside the wall.","zh":"牆裡面有什麼東西在噠噠作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rattle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7439bee24773bcbfa2d","word":"raw","forms":["raw"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cfef0c953bc952f0","term":"raw","forms":["raw","rawer","rawest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生的；未煮熟的","explanation":"食物還是生的，沒有經過烹調；這是 raw 最具體、最容易聯想到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She added raw onions to the salad.","zh":"她在沙拉里加了生洋蔥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chicken is still raw in the middle.","zh":"雞肉中間還是生的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5433c24f8f4509b8","term":"raw","forms":["raw","rawer","rawest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未經加工的；原始的","explanation":"材料、產品或其他東西還沒有經過加工、提純或整理，仍保持原始狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The factory buys raw materials from local suppliers.","zh":"這家工廠從當地供應商那裡購買原材料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to clean the raw data before analyzing it.","zh":"我們需要先清理原始資料，再進行分析。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-722cd79059482611","term":"raw","forms":["raw","rawer","rawest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"赤裸的；未經掩飾的","explanation":"情感、性格或反應沒有經過控制和修飾，直接而強烈地表現出來，像原料一樣沒有外層包裝。","examples":[{"en":"The film captures the raw grief of the family.","zh":"這部電影捕捉到了這個家庭赤裸而強烈的悲痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her raw anger was impossible to hide.","zh":"她無法掩飾自己的強烈憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c04bc270f965db4d7ab3","word":"ray","forms":["ray"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a4df279cefa3dde","term":"ray","forms":["ray","rays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光線；射線狀輻射","explanation":"ray 是從光源或其他輻射源向外傳播的一束光或類似能量，最常見的是“光線”。","examples":[{"en":"A ray of sunlight came through the window.","zh":"一縷陽光從窗戶照了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clouds opened and rays of light reached the valley.","zh":"雲層散開了，幾道光線照到了山谷裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b39d78add059ca90","term":"ray","forms":["ray","rays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數學射線","explanation":"在數學中，ray 是從一個確定的點出發、沿一個方向無限延伸的直線部分，正體現了“從中心向外伸展”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a ray from point A through point B.","zh":"畫一條從 A 點出發、經過 B 點的射線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two rays share the same endpoint.","zh":"這兩條射線有相同的端點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-079852400fbec099","term":"ray","forms":["ray","rays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鰩魚","explanation":"ray 是一種身體扁平、胸鰭寬大如翅、尾巴細長的海魚；它的外形像從身體中心向兩側展開，因此也能和“放射”這個核心形象聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a ray glide over the sandy seafloor.","zh":"我們看著一條鰩魚滑過沙質海底。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A ray buried itself under the sand.","zh":"一條鰩魚把自己埋進了沙子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b4f1d0e11dcc029c349","word":"razor","forms":["razor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cfd6656a4991938","term":"razor","forms":["razor","razors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剃刀","explanation":"指專門用來剃掉臉部或身體其他部位毛髮的鋒利刀具，核心形象就是貼近皮膚、把毛髮削掉。","examples":[{"en":"He used a razor to shave his beard.","zh":"他用剃刀刮鬍子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He replaced the dull blade in his razor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/razor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbbd13755a3f308c","term":"razor","forms":["razor","razors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排除解釋的原則","explanation":"指一種抽象的“剃刀”：透過刪去不太可能或不必要的解釋，幫助人們更簡潔地理解現象，例如Occam's razor。","examples":[{"en":"Occam's razor suggests choosing the simplest explanation that fits the facts.","zh":"奧卡姆剃刀原則提示我們選擇與事實相符的最簡單解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Occam's razor favors explanations requiring fewer unsupported assumptions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/razor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed4561f685f133532832","word":"reach","forms":["reach"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa4ae93bc020412d","term":"reach","forms":["reach","reaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"能力或影響力","explanation":"它指一個人、組織或行動向外伸展的能力、影響力或所能達到的範圍；影響伸到別人那裡，就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"The charity has a wide reach in rural communities.","zh":"這家慈善機構在農村社群擁有廣泛的影響力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No single manager has the reach to oversee every department.","zh":"沒有哪一位經理有能力管理所有部門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e37134305a445f5e","term":"reach","forms":["reach","reaches","reaching","reached","raught","rought","reachest","reachedst","reacheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"伸手去拿","explanation":"指把手臂或手中的東西向外伸，通常是為了拿到、碰到或抓住某物；記住“向外伸，直到碰到目標”即可。","examples":[{"en":"She reached for the phone beside her bed.","zh":"她伸手去拿床邊的電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Before I could reach the switch, the room went dark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7bb0552519ff722","term":"reach","forms":["reach","reaches","reaching","reached","raught","rought","reachest","reachedst","reacheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到達；達到","explanation":"指經過移動、努力或發展，最終到達某個地方、階段、職位或狀態；這仍然是“向外伸，直到碰到目標”。","examples":[{"en":"We reached the station just before the train left.","zh":"火車開走前，我們剛好趕到了車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After years of practice, she reached a high level of skill.","zh":"經過多年的練習，她達到了很高的技能水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93cc696c5ee112bd","term":"reach","forms":["reach","reaches","reaching","reached","raught","rought","reachest","reachedst","reacheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打動；使理解","explanation":"指話語、行動或感情伸到對方內心，使對方願意接受、回應或真正理解你的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher found a story that finally reached the quiet student.","zh":"老師找到一個故事，終於打動了那個沉默的學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The counselor finally reached the withdrawn teenager through music.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-275976081ce1abf67779","word":"react","forms":["react"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ab09f1e5e869c64","term":"react","forms":["react","reacts","reacting","reacted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"作出反應","explanation":"指人在得到訊息、遇到情況或受到刺激後作出回應，回應可以是情緒、言語或行動。這是 react 最重要、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"How did she react to the news?","zh":"她對這個訊息有什麼反應？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He reacted calmly when the plan changed.","zh":"計劃改變時，他鎮定地作出了反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/react","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f916714d774fb5f","term":"react","forms":["react","reacts","reacting","reacted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用表情回應帖子","explanation":"指在社交媒體上點選或釋出一個表情來表示自己對帖子或訊息的感受，是“作出反應”在網路交流中的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"You can react to the message with a heart.","zh":"你可以用愛心表情回應這條訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reacted to the announcement with a heart emoji.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/react","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-511639a4a9a23cceb83e","word":"reaction","forms":["reaction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1e0ce3d91bdab67","term":"reaction","forms":["reaction","reactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"回應；反應","explanation":"指人在受到某件事、某種刺激或某個訊息後表現出的情緒、言語或行為。它可以是個人的即時反應，也可以是公眾對重大事件的整體回應。","examples":[{"en":"Her reaction to the news was surprisingly calm.","zh":"她對這個訊息的反應出奇地平靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The decision caused an angry reaction from local residents.","zh":"這項決定引起了當地居民的憤怒反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67587ffbab2f6221","term":"reaction","forms":["reaction","reactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"化學反應","explanation":"指一種或多種物質發生變化，生成不同物質的過程。這裡的“反應”不是人的回應，而是物質之間發生了相互作用。","examples":[{"en":"The reaction between the acid and the metal produced gas.","zh":"酸和金屬之間的化學反應產生了氣體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reaction produces carbon dioxide and water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3316348dbadfb7b11c7c","word":"read","forms":["read"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf0fd54fda16d62e","term":"read","forms":["read","reads","reading","readen","redd","readest","readst","readeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閱讀文字","explanation":"表示透過看文字或其他書面資訊來理解內容，是“解讀資訊”這一核心概念最基本的用法。既可以不帶賓語表示閱讀，也可以直接接書、文章、說明等。","examples":[{"en":"Have you read this book?","zh":"你讀過這本書嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I read the instructions before using the machine.","zh":"我使用這臺機器前讀了說明書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/read","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbf643a8a4d4db76","term":"read","forms":["read","reads","reading","readen","redd","readest","readst","readeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"朗讀文字","explanation":"表示把書面文字用聲音說出來，也就是朗讀；重點從“看懂文字”轉向“把文字讀給別人聽”。","examples":[{"en":"She read the children a story before bed.","zh":"她睡前給孩子們讀了一個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He read us a passage from his new book.","zh":"他給我們朗讀了他新書中的一段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/read","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b24d6d33736ecd5604a4","word":"ready","forms":["ready"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-838a82246030f293","term":"ready","forms":["ready","readier","readiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"準備好了","explanation":"表示人、物或團隊已經具備立即行動或使用的條件，不一定表示事情已經開始。它可以說人準備好了，也可以說裝置、材料或計劃已經就緒。","examples":[{"en":"The children are ready for school.","zh":"孩子們已經準備好去上學了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is the presentation ready to begin?","zh":"演示準備好開始了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ready","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e13a5a4d2795975e","term":"ready","forms":["ready","readier","readiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易；傾向於","explanation":"表示某人容易做出某種反應，或某種事情很容易出現。這裡不是說已經發生，而是說這種可能性或傾向比較明顯。","examples":[{"en":"He is ready to believe any rumor he hears.","zh":"他聽到什麼傳言都容易相信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is always ready to believe the worst of him.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ready","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa33996d60e89311b4d1","word":"real","forms":["real"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-816d00d340d60499","term":"real","forms":["real","realer","more real","realest","most real"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真正的；名副其實的","explanation":"指某人或某物才是名副其實、真正重要或真正起作用的那個，而不是表面上的替代品。","examples":[{"en":"She is the real leader of the team.","zh":"她才是這個團隊真正的領導者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The real reason is that we ran out of time.","zh":"真正的原因是我們沒時間了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/real","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e02be6c091196c14","term":"real","forms":["real","realer","more real","realest","most real"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真的；非人造或非假冒的","explanation":"指材料、物品或身份確實是真的，不是仿製品、假貨或人工製造的替代物。","examples":[{"en":"This bag is made of real leather.","zh":"這個包是真皮做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are these real diamonds?","zh":"這些是真鑽石嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/real","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82fa2fa3690b13ad","term":"real","forms":["real","realer","more real","realest","most real"],"pos":"adj","zh":"現實的；非虛構的","explanation":"指確實發生、確實存在於現實中的人、事或生活，而不是故事、幻想或編造出來的內容。","examples":[{"en":"The film is based on real events.","zh":"這部電影取材於真實事件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In real life, he is much quieter.","zh":"在現實生活中，他安靜得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/real","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a609d2d7f515fd21e5ed","word":"realism","forms":["realism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed6523b62d9bc482","term":"realism","forms":["realism","realisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現實主義；務實態度","explanation":"指尊重事實和現實條件，不沉迷於不切實際的幻想或理想方案。這個意義把 realism 的核心牢牢放在“腳踩在地上”上。","examples":[{"en":"Her realism helped the team make a practical plan.","zh":"她的現實主義態度幫助團隊制訂了一個切實可行的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Realism is important when we set long-term goals.","zh":"制訂長期目標時，現實主義很重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9243b5c19e1ff828","term":"realism","forms":["realism","realisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寫實主義；寫實風格","explanation":"指藝術作品儘量按照現實中的樣子來表現人物、物體或生活，而不是把它們理想化或大幅變形。它仍然延續“如實看待現實”這條主線，只是從生活態度轉到了藝術表達。","examples":[{"en":"The novel is known for its realism and detailed description of village life.","zh":"這部小說以寫實主義和對鄉村生活的細緻描寫而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting's realism makes every wrinkle visible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d2f45fd706addb52c19","word":"realistic","forms":["realistic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c9d8f1ab1daab51","term":"realistic","forms":["realistic","more realistic","most realistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"現實可行的；切合實際的","explanation":"指對情況的判斷、目標或計劃建立在實際條件上，不憑空樂觀，也不要求不可能的結果。可以把它理解為“腳踩在地上來想事情”。","examples":[{"en":"We need a realistic plan before we start the project.","zh":"開始這個專案以前，我們需要一個切實可行的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to be realistic about how much you can finish today.","zh":"要現實一點，想想你今天到底能完成多少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c4eff46d8fba8dd","term":"realistic","forms":["realistic","more realistic","most realistic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寫實的；如實表現現實的","explanation":"指小說、電影、繪畫等作品對人物、行為或生活環境的表現接近現實，不刻意美化或理想化。這裡仍然是“按現實來呈現”，只是物件從計劃和判斷變成了藝術作品。","examples":[{"en":"The film gives a realistic picture of life in a small town.","zh":"這部電影真實地描繪了小城鎮的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist painted a realistic portrait of farm life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7ac1d220e6a2a27d87c","word":"reality","forms":["reality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8af7771ff56c0c0","term":"reality","forms":["reality","realities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"真實存在；真實性","explanation":"指某人、某事確實存在或確實發生的狀態，重點是“這不是假的，也不是想象出來的”。它常用來說明某種經歷、危險或情景的真實程度。","examples":[{"en":"Seeing the damage made the reality of the accident clear.","zh":"看到損壞的現場後，他才真正意識到這起事故的真實性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reality of working full-time was harder than she had expected.","zh":"全職工作的真實情況比她預想的更困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5095fedba67b0518","term":"reality","forms":["reality","realities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現實世界；實際情況","explanation":"指與幻想、願望、理論或表面印象相對的現實生活和實際情況，也就是人真正要面對的世界。","examples":[{"en":"He seems confident, but in reality he is very nervous.","zh":"他看起來很自信，但實際上非常緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dreams are important, but we still have to deal with reality.","zh":"夢想很重要，但我們仍然必須面對現實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8acb12bcffdf7fa15333","word":"realization","forms":["realization"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a88cbd8e345e501","term":"realization","forms":["realization","realizations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意識；領悟","explanation":"指一個人終於看清或意識到某個事實，常帶有“原先沒有完全明白，後來突然明白了”的感覺，就像腦中的燈亮起來一樣。","examples":[{"en":"She had the sudden realization that she had left her keys at home.","zh":"她突然意識到自己把鑰匙落在家裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The realization of how much he had changed made him pause.","zh":"意識到自己已經改變了這麼多，他停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f6eec7d586f63c4644e","word":"realize","forms":["realize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eed16b6d72db632f","term":"realize","forms":["realize","realizes","realizing","realized","realizest","realizedst","realizeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"意識到；明白","explanation":"指原來沒有注意到或沒有真正理解，後來突然明白某個事實或情況。它常帶有“這件事其實早已如此，只是現在才意識到”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"I suddenly realized that my keys were still in the office.","zh":"我突然意識到我的鑰匙還在辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She didn’t realize how late it was.","zh":"她沒有意識到時間已經這麼晚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-822a09f3bd1120e7","term":"realize","forms":["realize","realizes","realizing","realized","realizest","realizedst","realizeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"實現；使成為現實","explanation":"指把原本只是想法、目標或計劃的東西真正做出來，使它成為現實。這是“把抽象的東西變成真實結果”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"Years of hard work helped her realize her dream of opening a bakery.","zh":"多年的努力幫助她實現了開麵包店的夢想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project was finally realized after several delays.","zh":"這個專案幾經延誤後終於實現了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db8ffbe1cd19708b8ffb","word":"really","forms":["really"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ef6f573e5cdc775","term":"really","forms":["really","more really","most really"],"pos":"adv","zh":"確實；實際上","explanation":"用來確認或強調一個事實，相當於“確實如此、事實上”。它把“驗真燈”照向整件事，表示說話人認為這不是猜測或誇張。","examples":[{"en":"She really is a good friend.","zh":"她確實是個好朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I really saw him at the station.","zh":"我確實在車站看見他了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/really","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2cdd60816545287","term":"really","forms":["really","more really","most really"],"pos":"adv","zh":"非常；很","explanation":"放在形容詞前或動詞前，表示程度很高，相當於“非常、很”。這裡不一定是在證明某事真假，而是在把“驗真燈”變成更強的語氣燈。","examples":[{"en":"I really enjoyed the concert.","zh":"我非常喜歡那場音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soup is really hot.","zh":"這湯非常燙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/really","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d4e02d31a7eb0f8b579","word":"realm","forms":["realm"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c998826c9cf891b6","term":"realm","forms":["realm","realms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王國","explanation":"指由國王等最高統治者支配的領土或國家，常讓人聯想到故事、歷史敘述中的王國。它強調的不只是土地，也包括統治這片土地的權力結構。","examples":[{"en":"The young queen worked hard to protect her realm.","zh":"年輕的女王努力保護她的王國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trade brought new ideas into the coastal realm.","zh":"貿易把新的思想帶進了這個沿海王國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-200c93dd778ed29c","term":"realm","forms":["realm","realms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"領域；範圍","explanation":"指某種知識、活動、權力或影響所覆蓋的範圍，就像一種力量在自己的“王國”中發揮作用一樣。這是現代說明文和議論文中很重要的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"Her research has opened new possibilities in the realm of medicine.","zh":"她的研究在醫學領域開闢了新的可能性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Such fears belong to the realm of imagination, not fact.","zh":"這種恐懼屬於想象的範圍，而不是事實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/realm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3995ddb81dee48b29fa3","word":"reap","forms":["reap"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81fceb05861bb326","term":"reap","forms":["reap","reaps","reaping","reaped","reapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收割","explanation":"用鐮刀、鐮刀式機器等把成熟的穀物割下來，突出“把田裡的作物收走”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers reap the wheat in late summer.","zh":"農民在夏末收割小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmers reaped barley before the autumn rain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fa8ff227ca4a217","term":"reap","forms":["reap","reaps","reaping","reaped","reapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收割並收集","explanation":"不僅是把莊稼割斷，還包括把割下的莊稼作為收成收集起來；因此比單純“切割”更接近完整的收穫過程。","examples":[{"en":"By October, they had reaped the entire harvest.","zh":"到十月，他們已經收完了全部莊稼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers reaped the wheat before the autumn rain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-746e47e06d571c31","term":"reap","forms":["reap","reaps","reaping","reaped","reapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收穫結果或回報","explanation":"把先前的努力、行為或選擇看成播下的種子，後來“收割”由此產生的利益、獎勵，甚至壞結果；所以既可以是收穫好處，也可以是承擔後果。","examples":[{"en":"After years of hard work, she is finally reaping the benefits.","zh":"經過多年的努力，她終於開始收穫成果了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ignored the warnings and reaped the consequences.","zh":"他無視警告，最終承擔了後果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32b36ae43a5ea4895ec8","word":"rear","forms":["rear"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23a30ecb1e00b162","term":"rear","forms":["rear"],"pos":"adj","zh":"後面的；最後面的","explanation":"指處在後方或佇列最後面的，與前部相對。這是 rear 作形容詞時最常見、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please enter through the rear door.","zh":"請從後門進入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The luggage is in the rear compartment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8eac279d3c2b7b00","term":"rear","forms":["rear","rears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"後部；最後面","explanation":"指某個物體、隊伍或順序中的後方部分，也就是與前端相對的地方。這和形容詞“後面的”是同一個核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We found two empty seats at the rear of the bus.","zh":"我們在公共汽車後部找到了兩個空座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The emergency exit is at the rear.","zh":"緊急出口在後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fcfccf675b1f0bfd39d","word":"reason","forms":["reason"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4378224069bc0146","term":"reason","forms":["reason","reasons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"原因；理由","explanation":"導致某件事發生或使某種決定成立的依據，就是 reason。它既可以指客觀原因，也可以指人給出的解釋或理由。","examples":[{"en":"The reason this tree fell is that its roots had rotted.","zh":"這棵樹倒下的原因是它的根已經腐爛了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave no reason for leaving early.","zh":"她沒有說明提前離開的理由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reason","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5247ff4039a60652","term":"reason","forms":["reason","reasons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"理性；推理能力","explanation":"reason 也指人理解、判斷、推導和形成結論的理效能力，也就是“用道理思考”的能力。","examples":[{"en":"Good decisions require reason as well as experience.","zh":"好的決定既需要理性，也需要經驗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fear made it difficult for him to use reason.","zh":"恐懼使他難以保持理性思考。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reason","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86ffc49ebd5dd43f","term":"reason","forms":["reason","reasons","reasoning","reasoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推理得出結論","explanation":"reason 表示根據已有事實和資訊進行理性思考，逐步得出結論。它就是把“原因和證據”沿著思考的路連線到結論上。","examples":[{"en":"We reasoned from the evidence that the door had been opened earlier.","zh":"我們根據證據推斷門之前已經被開啟過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reasoned that taking the train would be faster.","zh":"她推斷坐火車會更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reason","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d7693a9e589f5c4","term":"reason","forms":["reason","reasons","reasoning","reasoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"論證；講道理","explanation":"reason 也表示透過演繹或歸納提出理由，支援自己的觀點，或用道理反駁別人。","examples":[{"en":"You cannot reason with someone who refuses to listen.","zh":"對一個拒絕傾聽的人，你沒法講道理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lawyer reasoned carefully from the available facts.","zh":"律師根據現有事實進行了嚴密論證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reason","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-53bc5c9386ea143b4beb","word":"reasonable","forms":["reasonable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc855cad628753a7","term":"reasonable","forms":["reasonable","more reasonable","most reasonable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合理的；公平的","explanation":"指要求、決定或做法符合常識和道理，相關的人通常有理由接受它。這裡的核心不是“聰明”，而是“公平、講得通”。","examples":[{"en":"Her request for more time was completely reasonable.","zh":"她要求多一點時間是完全合理的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to find a reasonable solution for everyone.","zh":"我們需要為大家找到一個公平合理的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reasonable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05f146143ccf36fa","term":"reasonable","forms":["reasonable","more reasonable","most reasonable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"適度的；不過分的","explanation":"指數量、要求、條件或行為沒有超過適當範圍，就像放在“講道理的尺度”上，既不是太多，也不是太少。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep the noise at a reasonable level.","zh":"請把噪音控制在適度的範圍內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager gave us a reasonable amount of time to finish.","zh":"經理給了我們適當的時間來完成任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reasonable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81c0d8e4cdce144127fb","word":"reassure","forms":["reassure"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-352832056e813a73","term":"reassure","forms":["reassure","reassures","reassuring","reassured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使安心；恢復信心","explanation":"指透過解釋、保證或安撫，讓害怕、擔心或缺乏信心的人重新感到放心。核心畫面是把一個人從不安的狀態拉回安全感中。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor reassured her that the pain was nothing serious.","zh":"醫生讓她放心，告訴她這種疼痛並不嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He reassured his children that he would be home before dark.","zh":"他讓孩子們放心，保證天黑前會回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reassure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52a39733bfab90ad7c9b","word":"rebel","forms":["rebel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1bfe280552f91445","term":"rebel","forms":["rebel","rebels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反抗者；叛亂者","explanation":"rebel 是拒絕服從既有權威、並試圖對抗它的人，常常還帶有武裝反抗的意味。它和核心畫面中的“轉身回頭反抗權威的人”相同。","examples":[{"en":"The rebels captured the town after several days of fighting.","zh":"經過幾天的戰鬥，反抗者佔領了這座城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was a rebel against the strict rules at school.","zh":"她反抗學校的嚴格規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rebel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b373aabe4700b11","term":"rebel","forms":["rebel","rebels","rebelling","rebelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反抗；不服從","explanation":"rebel 作動詞時表示轉身對抗原本應服從的權威、規則或制度，也就是把“反抗者”的行動說出來。","examples":[{"en":"Many young people rebel against their parents' expectations.","zh":"許多年輕人會反抗父母的期望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers rebelled against their commander.","zh":"士兵們反抗了他們的指揮官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rebel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1f718f462fbc4fc8c04","word":"rebellion","forms":["rebellion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c3e3b8c9ffe178c","term":"rebellion","forms":["rebellion","rebellions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"武裝叛亂","explanation":"指人們以武力反抗既有政府或統治者，通常涉及較大規模的政治衝突。這裡的重點不是單純不服從，而是公開、強力地挑戰統治。","examples":[{"en":"The government sent more troops to stop rebellion in the northern provinces.","zh":"政府增派了部隊，以制止北部各省的武裝叛亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The army crushed the rebellion within weeks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rebellion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1d208545b318edc","term":"rebellion","forms":["rebellion","rebellions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反抗權威","explanation":"指故意不接受他人的控制、規則或要求，是對權威的反抗。它不一定涉及武力，個人為了表達獨立或不滿而違抗父母、學校等，也可以叫 rebellion。","examples":[{"en":"Wearing bright clothes was her quiet rebellion against the school's strict rules.","zh":"穿鮮豔的衣服是她對學校嚴格規定的一種無聲反抗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His refusal to wear a tie was a small rebellion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rebellion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ed6b4c1ae9f8249477d","word":"recall","forms":["recall"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e69c9e37ea22f0a","term":"recall","forms":["recall","recalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"召回；撤回","explanation":"表示把人或物叫回來、收回來，或採取“召回”這一行動；產品出現問題時，廠家發起的召回也用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"The company announced a recall of 50,000 cars.","zh":"這家公司宣佈召回五萬輛汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recall affected every model sold last year.","zh":"這次召回影響了去年銷售的每一種車型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c32f871ad08c0242","term":"recall","forms":["recall","recalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"記憶；回憶","explanation":"表示記憶本身，或把過去的人、事重新帶回意識中的能力和行為；這裡可以把它理解為把過去“叫回”腦海。","examples":[{"en":"She has a clear recall of her first day at school.","zh":"她清楚地記得自己上學第一天的情景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old photograph brought back many happy memories to my recall.","zh":"那張老照片喚回了許多快樂的回憶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d54c7e260b9636ba","term":"recall","forms":["recall","recalls","recalling","recalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"召回；叫回","explanation":"表示把某人叫回某個地方、崗位或任務中；也可以把某物帶回原來的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The ambassador was recalled to the capital.","zh":"這名大使被召回首都。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach recalled the goalkeeper to the team.","zh":"教練把那名守門員召回了球隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fac08ae0913fffda","term":"recall","forms":["recall","recalls","recalling","recalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想起；回憶起","explanation":"表示把某人、某事或某段經歷重新帶回腦海，也就是想起或回憶起；這是“把過去叫回來”的直接引申。","examples":[{"en":"I can still recall the sound of the train.","zh":"我仍然能想起那列火車的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you recall meeting her at the conference?","zh":"你還記得在會議上見過她嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-6f32860910ca0fb2a20c","word":"receipt","forms":["receipt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4cdec8ce38aee19","term":"receipt","forms":["receipt","receipts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收入；進賬","explanation":"指收到的錢的數量，尤其是商店、演出或公司在一段時間內獲得的總收入；它仍然保留“收到錢”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The festival's ticket receipts exceeded expectations.","zh":"這個節日的門票收入超過了預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reduced opening hours caused a sharp fall in daily receipts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/receipt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87e2c3c6e90b6696","term":"receipt","forms":["receipt","receipts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"收據；收訖憑證","explanation":"指證明某件商品或某筆錢已經被收到的書面或電子憑證，例如商店付款後給你的紙條或郵件。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have a receipt for this purchase?","zh":"可以給我這筆購物開張收據嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep your receipt in case you need to return the item.","zh":"請保留收據，以防需要退貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/receipt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-95100519be0342216c9c","word":"receive","forms":["receive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1007bb8b8ca526d2","term":"receive","forms":["receive","receives","receiving","received","receivest","receivedst","receiveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收到；接到","explanation":"表示某物被送來、寄來或支付給某人，而這個人確實把它收到了。禮物、郵件、款項、訊息等都可以這樣說，是最常用的基本義。","examples":[{"en":"I received a package from my sister this morning.","zh":"我今天早上收到了姐姐寄來的包裹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school received hundreds of applications.","zh":"這所學校收到了數百份申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/receive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-713eb8157b64256a","term":"receive","forms":["receive","receives","receiving","received","receivest","receivedst","receiveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"接待；接納進入","explanation":"表示作為主人接待來客，或允許某人進入自己的住所、場合或社交圈。可以把它想成把人接到自己的空間裡。","examples":[{"en":"The ambassador received the visitors at his residence.","zh":"大使在官邸接待了來訪者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic receives patients by appointment only.","zh":"這家診所只接待預約的病人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/receive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdfb6ae9084033a6","term":"receive","forms":["receive","receives","receiving","received","receivest","receivedst","receiveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"接收訊號","explanation":"表示裝置從傳送端接到無線電、通訊或其他訊號，把資訊傳入系統。這裡仍然是“把外來的東西接進來”，只是接收者變成了裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The receiver can receive signals from several satellites.","zh":"這臺接收器可以接收來自多顆衛星的訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The station received the emergency transmission clearly.","zh":"這座電臺清楚地接收到了緊急傳輸訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/receive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81bae876b70513c9decc","word":"receiver","forms":["receiver"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f0725910c253456","term":"receiver","forms":["receiver","receivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接收者；收件人","explanation":"指實際收到信件、請求、款項或其他事物的人，也就是完成“接收”動作的那一方。","examples":[{"en":"The receiver of the package signed for it at the door.","zh":"包裹的接收人在門口簽收了它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was the receiver of several urgent messages.","zh":"她收到了幾條緊急訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/receiver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43ac6a6c5406f4e6","term":"receiver","forms":["receiver","receivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接收器；接收裝置","explanation":"指接收無線電、電視或其他訊號的裝置或部件。它不是主動傳送訊號的一方，而是把外來的訊號接進來的“終點”。","examples":[{"en":"The satellite receiver is not picking up any signal.","zh":"衛星接收器接收不到任何訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He bought a new radio receiver for the workshop.","zh":"他為工作室買了一臺新的無線電接收機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/receiver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-034a7e52c5c9534b709d","word":"recent","forms":["recent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-482f3c13d5e70a4e","term":"recent","forms":["recent","more recent","most recent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最近發生的","explanation":"指在離現在不久的時間內發生、出現或完成的事情，重點是它位於靠近現在的時間線上。","examples":[{"en":"A recent study found that the river is cleaner than before.","zh":"一項最近的研究發現，這條河比以前更乾淨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We discussed the recent changes at the meeting.","zh":"我們在會上討論了最近的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94c22edf5e5b1518","term":"recent","forms":["recent","more recent","most recent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"新近的；不過時的","explanation":"指事物年代較新、符合當前情況或觀念，不顯得陳舊；它強調“新近”帶來的時效性。","examples":[{"en":"Please use the most recent version of the report.","zh":"請使用這份報告的最新版本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use recent sources when researching current medical treatments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-066a4a70376da00eb9e5","word":"reception","forms":["reception"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-390577d8303e6261","term":"reception","forms":["reception","receptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接收；接待","explanation":"這個義項指把人、物或資訊接進來、接待到位的行為，是 reception 各種意思的核心。它可以泛指接收這一過程，也可以指一次正式的接待。","examples":[{"en":"The reception of the new equipment took several hours.","zh":"接收這批新裝置花了幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reception of visitors is handled by the security team.","zh":"訪客的接待由安保團隊負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f739307798a15e89","term":"reception","forms":["reception","receptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歡迎招待會","explanation":"指為正式歡迎某人或慶祝某事而舉行的社交活動，最常見的是婚禮後的宴會或招待會。這裡仍然是把來客“接進來並招待”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"They held a small reception for the visiting scientists.","zh":"他們為來訪的科學家舉行了一場小型招待會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wedding reception will begin at seven.","zh":"婚禮招待會將在七點開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reception","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c836905751e74c2eeb90","word":"recession","forms":["recession"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-494c8fcf4959b079","term":"recession","forms":["recession","recessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"退卻；撤回","explanation":"指人、事物或抽象狀態向後退、撤回，不再向前推進；這是其他意思中“退一步、往回走”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The recession of the floodwaters exposed several damaged roads.","zh":"洪水退去後，幾條受損的道路露了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recession of public support forced the mayor to reconsider the plan.","zh":"公眾支援度的退縮迫使市長重新考慮這項計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cb26fb3d24a561d","term":"recession","forms":["recession","recessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟衰退","explanation":"指經濟活動持續減弱，生產、消費、投資或就業等整體回落；經濟彷彿從較高水平向後退。它是現代英語中最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Many small businesses closed during the recession.","zh":"經濟衰退期間，許多小企業倒閉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government introduced tax cuts to help the country recover from the recession.","zh":"政府推出減稅措施，幫助國家走出經濟衰退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e1d8e552330911f9f779","word":"recipe","forms":["recipe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7afb956967dae8d2","term":"recipe","forms":["recipe","recipes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混合材料的製作配方","explanation":"指說明要用哪些材料、按什麼步驟混合或處理它們的一套配方，不限於食物，也可以用於藥物、化學品等。","examples":[{"en":"I found a simple recipe for homemade soap.","zh":"我找到了一份製作自制肥皂的簡單配方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe calls for two cups of flour and one egg.","zh":"這份配方需要兩杯麵粉和一個雞蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0db30109ff6c347f","term":"recipe","forms":["recipe","recipes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烹飪食譜","explanation":"這是日常生活中最常見的具體意義，指寫明食材、用量和烹調步驟的食譜；它正是“按說明做出結果”這一核心概念最直觀的例子。","examples":[{"en":"This recipe makes enough soup for four people.","zh":"按這份食譜做出的湯夠四個人喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shared her grandmother's recipe for apple pie.","zh":"她分享了祖母做蘋果派的食譜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-665d0698dbc8fb95afc2","word":"recipient","forms":["recipient"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7bc82ddc99b3f92d","term":"recipient","forms":["recipient","recipients"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接受者；接收者","explanation":"指收到錢、物品、獎項、資訊或幫助的人。記住它就是站在“接收端”的人，與提供或傳送的一方相對。","examples":[{"en":"Each recipient of the scholarship received a letter from the university.","zh":"每位獎學金獲得者都收到了大學寄來的信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity contacted the recipient before delivering the package.","zh":"慈善機構在遞送包裹前聯絡了收件人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recipient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36379614ecbe87c1","term":"recipient","forms":["recipient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"接收的；接受方的","explanation":"表示某人、機構或國家處在接收的一端，接受某種物品、資金、資訊或幫助。它和名詞義來自同一個核心：接收者的一方。","examples":[{"en":"The recipient country used the funds to build new schools.","zh":"受援國用這筆資金建造了新學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipient organization must account for every grant payment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recipient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16be882827ec3f5a5611","word":"recite","forms":["recite"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36e8db7e8cb1e737","term":"recite","forms":["recite","recites","reciting","recited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"背誦；朗誦","explanation":"把已經記住或眼前有的文字、詩歌、數字等大聲重複出來，通常是讓別人聽見。它的核心畫面是站在聽眾面前，按原內容完整說出一段話。","examples":[{"en":"The students took turns reciting the poem to the class.","zh":"學生們輪流向全班朗誦這首詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She can recite all the names of the planets.","zh":"她能背出所有行星的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e06088fe75ec89fc","term":"recite","forms":["recite","recites","reciting","recited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐項列舉","explanation":"把一組事項、理由或事實一個接一個說出來，就像把腦中的清單逐項念給別人聽。這裡不一定涉及背誦固定文字，但保留了“按順序說出”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"He recited the reasons why the plan would not work.","zh":"他把這個計劃行不通的理由一條條說了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The official recited a long list of violations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7c5630b7dd9c989d3b2","word":"reckless","forms":["reckless"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-731922024171a783","term":"reckless","forms":["reckless","recklesser","more reckless","recklessest","most reckless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粗心魯莽的","explanation":"指做事不夠小心，憑衝動行動，像是把應有的顧慮丟到一邊；這種魯莽可能讓人做出倉促而冒險的決定。","examples":[{"en":"It was reckless to drive so fast on such a narrow road.","zh":"在這麼窄的路上開得這麼快，實在太魯莽了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His reckless driving endangered everyone in the car.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-512ac0fbfc87f15d","term":"reckless","forms":["reckless","recklesser","more reckless","recklessest","most reckless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無視危險和後果的","explanation":"指明知有危險或可能帶來嚴重後果，卻仍然毫不在意地去做；這是“不計後果”這一核心概念最強的一層。","examples":[{"en":"His reckless decision put everyone on the boat in danger.","zh":"他那個不計後果的決定讓船上的所有人都陷入了危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reckless overtaking caused the collision.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18dc8a86709b6aa8c3a7","word":"reckon","forms":["reckon"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14ef26ecff91e105","term":"reckon","forms":["reckon","reckons","reckoning","reckoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"計算；數清","explanation":"指把數量一項項數出來，或透過計算得出結果。它體現了 reckon 最基本的“把事情算清楚”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She reckoned the cost of the materials before starting the project.","zh":"她在開始專案之前算了算材料的成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you reckon how many boxes we still need?","zh":"你能算出我們還需要多少個箱子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76c6e42c88bbd4b3","term":"reckon","forms":["reckon","reckons","reckoning","reckoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……算作；認為屬於","explanation":"指在評價或分類時把某人某事放進某一類，認為它具有某種地位、價值或性質。也就是把物件“算進”自己的判斷之中。","examples":[{"en":"She is reckoned as one of the best chefs in the city.","zh":"她被認為是城裡最優秀的廚師之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is reckoned among the country's finest translators.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80ae41f08b1d14d4","term":"reckon","forms":["reckon","reckons","reckoning","reckoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為；估計","explanation":"在口語中，reckon 常表示根據自己的判斷得出“認為”或“估計”。它像是先在心裡把情況掂量一番，再說出自己的結論。","examples":[{"en":"I reckon the train will arrive before noon.","zh":"我估計火車會在中午前到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you reckon we have enough food for everyone?","zh":"你覺得我們的食物夠大家吃嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reckon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c12bd84acfceacc8a75","word":"recognition","forms":["recognition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee6b755619d301ce","term":"recognition","forms":["recognition","recognitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認出；辨認","explanation":"指把眼前的人、物或情況和記憶中的物件對應起來，也就是“看出來這就是以前見過的那個”。重點是從陌生或不確定到認出。","examples":[{"en":"Recognition came when she heard his familiar laugh.","zh":"聽到他熟悉的笑聲時，她終於認出了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a moment of hesitation, he showed clear recognition.","zh":"猶豫片刻後，他明顯認出了對方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recognition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1f68156c8f5835c","term":"recognition","forms":["recognition","recognitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承認；認可","explanation":"指正式或公開地承認某件事真實、有效、合理，或承認某人的權利和地位。這裡不是“認出一個物件”，而是把它確認為什麼有效或應當被接受。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement included recognition of workers' rights.","zh":"這項協議承認了工人的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her contribution deserves recognition.","zh":"她的貢獻應當得到認可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recognition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-074d8d3c3a5c0d28","term":"recognition","forms":["recognition","recognitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"讚譽；受到關注","explanation":"指某人、團體或成就得到公眾注意和肯定，因此變得更受認可或更有知名度。它從“承認其價值”進一步發展為“給它應有的關注和讚譽”。","examples":[{"en":"The young artist is finally gaining recognition for her work.","zh":"這位年輕藝術家終於因自己的作品獲得了認可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prize brought recognition to her overlooked research.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recognition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b00de68c4c9617c7618","word":"recognize","forms":["recognize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1918d5bc2eb0013c","term":"recognize","forms":["recognize","recognizes","recognizing","recognized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認出；辨認出","explanation":"把眼前的人或事物同以前見過、聽過或接觸過的記憶對上，從而認出它是誰或是什麼。","examples":[{"en":"I recognized her voice before I saw her face.","zh":"我還沒看見她的臉，就先聽出了她的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He recognized the street from an old photograph.","zh":"他從一張老照片中認出了那條街。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recognize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d3f7d5d3dd75d56","term":"recognize","forms":["recognize","recognizes","recognizing","recognized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承認有效；承認其合法地位","explanation":"不只是看見某事存在，而是正式接受它的存在、合法性或有效性，常用於國家、政府、證件、規則和權利等。","examples":[{"en":"The court recognized the validity of the agreement.","zh":"法院承認這份協議有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several neighboring states recognized the new republic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recognize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da3b22241af3e472","term":"recognize","forms":["recognize","recognizes","recognizing","recognized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認定為；承認具有某種性質","explanation":"把某人或某事看作具有某種明確的性質或身份，常常是經過判斷後承認這一點。","examples":[{"en":"She is widely recognized as an expert in child development.","zh":"她被廣泛認為是兒童發展領域的專家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court recognized him as the legal guardian.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recognize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc00ae7e092d66fc","term":"recognize","forms":["recognize","recognizes","recognizing","recognized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"再次辨認","explanation":"強調重新把眼前物件同已有認識對應起來，現代英語中與前一組的“認出、辨認出”是同一個核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"I recognized the old house immediately.","zh":"我立刻認出了那棟老房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I recognized my former teacher despite his beard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recognize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0eb15ad185af2b351ef4","word":"recommend","forms":["recommend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-346a3a83dc645107","term":"recommend","forms":["recommend","recommends","recommending","recommended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推薦；稱許","explanation":"把某個人、物品或選擇介紹給別人，並明確表示它值得信任或選擇。重點不只是“提到”，而是帶有支援和認可。","examples":[{"en":"My colleague recommended this restaurant to me.","zh":"我的同事向我推薦了這家餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several teachers recommended her for the scholarship.","zh":"幾位老師推薦她獲得這項獎學金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recommend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c458ec901b509f17","term":"recommend","forms":["recommend","recommends","recommending","recommended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"建議；勸告","explanation":"把一個行動方案遞給別人，表示這是值得采納的做法。它通常是積極而有根據的建議，不等於強制命令。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor recommended getting more sleep.","zh":"醫生建議多睡一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I recommend that you book a table in advance.","zh":"我建議你提前訂位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recommend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dbfe937585b4147cb6f3","word":"recommendation","forms":["recommendation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7027439981b0a18","term":"recommendation","forms":["recommendation","recommendations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被推薦的內容","explanation":"指別人遞給你的具體推薦物件或推薦方案，例如一本書、一家餐館，或一組為解決問題而提出的措施。","examples":[{"en":"I followed her recommendation and booked the small hotel.","zh":"我聽從了她的推薦，訂了那家小旅館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report includes several recommendations for improving road safety.","zh":"這份報告包括幾項改善道路安全的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recommendation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efe03f48b666d78f","term":"recommendation","forms":["recommendation","recommendations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"認可或推薦信","explanation":"指對某人的能力、品格或工作表現的正式認可；在求職語境中，也可指由他人寫出的推薦信或推薦意見。","examples":[{"en":"The university asked for a recommendation from one of my professors.","zh":"這所大學要求我提供一位教授的推薦信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her tutor wrote a glowing recommendation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recommendation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1f5888248ab86be","term":"recommendation","forms":["recommendation","recommendations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動建議","explanation":"指關於接下來採取什麼做法更好的建議或提案，是把判斷遞給別人，幫助對方作出選擇或採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"She made a recommendation about which train we should take.","zh":"她建議我們應該乘哪趟火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor gave me a recommendation to rest for a few days.","zh":"醫生建議我休息幾天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recommendation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2c30d59264829011fe7","word":"reconcile","forms":["reconcile"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-083c73b078d852c1","term":"reconcile","forms":["reconcile","reconciles","reconciling","reconciled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使和好；恢復和諧","explanation":"把發生爭執、疏遠的人重新帶回友好關係中，就像把斷開的兩邊重新接起來。它既可以表示調解雙方，也可以表示雙方自己恢復和好。","examples":[{"en":"The mediator helped reconcile the two neighbors after their dispute.","zh":"調解員幫助兩位鄰居在爭執後重新和好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reconciled with her sister before the family celebration.","zh":"她在家庭慶祝活動前和姐姐和好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reconcile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de3c5dc629962049","term":"reconcile","forms":["reconcile","reconciles","reconciling","reconciled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使一致；調和差異","explanation":"把互相矛盾或不相容的說法、觀點和結果重新協調起來，使它們能夠同時成立或彼此吻合。這仍然是“把兩邊接回同一條線”的意思，只是物件從人變成了事物。","examples":[{"en":"The report tries to reconcile the two different estimates.","zh":"這份報告試圖協調兩個不同的估算結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The accountant reconciled the figures from both departments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reconcile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70ce871f8a3d3fb449bc","word":"record","forms":["record"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-895728e725f1c77b","term":"record","forms":["record","records"],"pos":"noun","zh":"記錄；記載的資訊","explanation":"指被寫下、錄入或儲存起來的一項資訊，方便以後查閱、核對或回想。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep a record of every payment you make.","zh":"請儲存好你每一筆付款的記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recording gave us a clear record of what happened.","zh":"這段錄音清楚地記錄了當時發生的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/record","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-703cfe6cc1c6b46a","term":"record","forms":["record","records"],"pos":"noun","zh":"記錄載體；檔案","explanation":"指用來儲存資訊、供以後查閱的檔案、表格、錄音或其他實體載體；重點從資訊本身轉向承載資訊的東西。","examples":[{"en":"There is no record of the payment in our files.","zh":"我們的檔案中沒有這筆付款的記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive holds detailed records of every voyage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/record","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b6c45eb91b6fb04","term":"record","forms":["record","records"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紀錄；最高成績","explanation":"指目前已知的最極端數值或比賽成績，因為它被儲存下來並作為後來比較的標準，所以可以說某人打破或創造了紀錄。","examples":[{"en":"She broke the school record for the 100-meter race.","zh":"她打破了學校一百米賽跑的紀錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lake reached a record low level this summer.","zh":"這座湖今年夏天的水位降到了創紀錄的低點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/record","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3bb881399852c9b2","term":"record","forms":["record","records","recording","recorded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"記錄；記下","explanation":"把發生的事實、細節或資料儲存下來，讓以後的人能夠查閱或核對。","examples":[{"en":"She recorded every detail in her notebook.","zh":"她把每個細節都記在了筆記本里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey recorded a sharp rise in housing costs.","zh":"調查記錄到住房成本大幅上升。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/record","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-332cb4e8c1d907dc","term":"record","forms":["record","records","recording","recorded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"錄製；錄音或錄影","explanation":"把聲音、影片或其他媒體內容儲存下來，使它以後可以播放或觀看。","examples":[{"en":"We recorded the interview for the evening news.","zh":"我們為晚間新聞錄製了這次採訪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We recorded the interview in a quiet room.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/record","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93384247058b5e037a16","word":"recorder","forms":["recorder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-991925750890fd6e","term":"recorder","forms":["recorder","recorders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"記錄裝置","explanation":"指把聲音、畫面或其他資訊記錄並儲存下來的裝置。它不只限於錄音，也可以是能記錄影像、資料等內容的裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter carried a small audio recorder to the interview.","zh":"記者帶著一臺小型錄音裝置去採訪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This camera has a built-in video recorder.","zh":"這臺相機內建了影片記錄器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recorder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-450342ea10880bae","term":"recorder","forms":["recorder","recorders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豎笛；木笛","explanation":"一種透過吹入氣流發聲的簡單木管樂器，常見於學校音樂課，也有從高音到低音的不同尺寸。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter is learning to play the recorder at school.","zh":"我女兒正在學校學習吹豎笛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He played a soft melody on the recorder.","zh":"他用豎笛吹奏了一段柔和的旋律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recorder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec3915f542e0f8cb6c18","word":"recover","forms":["recover"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0e5bb806ee1e2e9","term":"recover","forms":["recover","recovers","recovering","recovered","recoverest","recoveredst","recovereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"找回；重新獲得","explanation":"把已經失去、看不見或暫時無法取得的東西重新拿回來；在航海、天文等語境中，也可以指重新看到目標或訊號。","examples":[{"en":"The police recovered my stolen bicycle.","zh":"警方找回了我被偷的腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The telescope recovered the faint signal after the clouds cleared.","zh":"雲層散去後，望遠鏡重新捕捉到了微弱訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a9e4ed67e210b97","term":"recover","forms":["recover","recovers","recovering","recovered","recoverest","recoveredst","recovereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"恢復體力或狀態","explanation":"經過疲勞、打擊或疾病後，重新恢復原來的體力、精神狀態或良好狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She rested for a few days to recover her strength.","zh":"她休息了幾天來恢復體力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He needs a few days to recover from the journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcb51aaa13c50853","term":"recover","forms":["recover","recovers","recovering","recovered","recoverest","recoveredst","recovereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"康復；好轉","explanation":"人經歷疾病、受傷或困難後逐漸變好，重新恢復健康、力量或生活狀況；這是“狀態被帶回原處”這一主線的典型用法。","examples":[{"en":"He had a serious operation, but he is recovering well.","zh":"他做了一次大手術，但恢復得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She recovered slowly after the operation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-929b0a0c76a450ad","term":"recover","forms":["recover","recovers","recovering","recovered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重新覆蓋","explanation":"在已有覆蓋層上再蓋一層，使表面重新被材料覆蓋；可把它記成“再蓋一次”。","examples":[{"en":"They recovered the old shed with fresh metal panels.","zh":"他們給舊棚屋重新鋪上了新的金屬板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They recovered the sofa in durable green fabric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c585378513f5f7a2e14","word":"recovery","forms":["recovery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2bde3461b5cc14b3","term":"recovery","forms":["recovery","recoveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重新找回或收回","explanation":"指把原來丟失、被拿走或失去的東西重新得到；核心畫面就是“失去的東西回來”。","examples":[{"en":"The recovery of the stolen paintings took several years.","zh":"追回那些被盜畫作花了好幾年時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recovery of lost data was successful.","zh":"丟失資料的恢復很成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recovery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d530f3a27608c4a6","term":"recovery","forms":["recovery","recoveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"健康恢復；康復","explanation":"指人在生病、受傷或接受治療後，身體逐漸回到正常狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She made a quick recovery after the operation.","zh":"她手術後恢復得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His recovery from the injury took months.","zh":"他從那次受傷中恢復過來花了幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recovery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1c018a5175fd5b6","term":"recovery","forms":["recovery","recoveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟回升","explanation":"指經濟、市場或某個行業經歷低迷後重新增長，低谷中的活動逐步恢復。","examples":[{"en":"The latest figures suggest that the economic recovery is continuing.","zh":"最新資料表明，經濟復甦仍在繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lower borrowing costs helped support the economic recovery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recovery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3789e352cc1eacc0f1fd","word":"recreation","forms":["recreation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76cbb97d051b4554","term":"recreation","forms":["recreation","recreations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"消遣；娛樂活動","explanation":"指人在工作或日常事務之外，為了放鬆、獲得樂趣或恢復精神而進行的活動，例如遊戲、運動或其他休閒安排。","examples":[{"en":"Swimming is my favorite recreation after work.","zh":"下班後游泳是我最喜歡的消遣活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The park offers plenty of recreation for local families.","zh":"這座公園為當地家庭提供了豐富的休閒活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recreation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-768a39dc474d0a8e","term":"recreation","forms":["recreation","recreations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重新創造","explanation":"指按照原來的樣子、記憶或資料把某物再次創造出來；這裡的重點不是休閒，而是“重新做出”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum funded the recreation of the old theater.","zh":"這家博物館資助了那座舊劇院的重新建造。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their recreation of the ancient meal used ingredients found in excavations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recreation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-8575e43e52cfebdcf89f","word":"recreational","forms":["recreational"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92f8549061476d18","term":"recreational","forms":["recreational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"休閒娛樂的","explanation":"指為了放鬆、消遣或興趣而進行的，或與這類活動有關的；重點是它不以正式學習、工作或專業訓練為主要目的。","examples":[{"en":"I enjoy recreational reading on weekends.","zh":"我喜歡在週末進行休閒閱讀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The center offers recreational activities for children.","zh":"這個中心為兒童提供休閒活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recreational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fde2b189f66a29e29b49","word":"recruit","forms":["recruit"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06dd92ee92c64a8b","term":"recruit","forms":["recruit","recruits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新兵","explanation":"指剛被徵募或入伍、還屬於新手階段計程車兵，也就是剛加入軍隊的人。它保留了“把新人補進隊伍”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The recruits began their first week of training today.","zh":"這些新兵今天開始了第一週訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recruits began basic training before dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recruit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-411f7edebee2b0df","term":"recruit","forms":["recruit","recruits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新招募的員工或成員","explanation":"指剛被公司、組織、球隊等錄用或吸收的人。這裡不一定和軍隊有關，重點是這個人剛剛進入新的團隊。","examples":[{"en":"The new recruits joined the company after passing the interviews.","zh":"這些新員工透過面試後加入了公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new recruits spent their first week in training.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recruit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fc1f826e4fd7693","term":"recruit","forms":["recruit","recruits","recruiting","recruited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"招募；招聘","explanation":"指主動尋找並吸收新成員、員工、志願者、運動員或軍人，讓他們加入某個團隊或組織。這是 recruit 最重要、最常用的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital is recruiting more nurses this year.","zh":"這家醫院今年正在招聘更多護士。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They recruited several volunteers to help at the event.","zh":"他們招募了幾名志願者來協助這次活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recruit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32dfed947e8bca93c393","word":"rectangle","forms":["rectangle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e13689c24563ec54","term":"rectangle","forms":["rectangle","rectangles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"矩形；長方形","explanation":"指四個角都是直角、對邊平行的四邊形。按嚴格的幾何定義，正方形也是矩形；不過在許多日常語境裡，rectangle 更常讓人想到較長的長方形。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a rectangle with four equal sides.","zh":"畫一個四條邊相等的矩形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The window is a rectangle with rounded corners.","zh":"這扇窗是一個四角帶圓弧的長方形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rectangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5c8bb8c19301f92","term":"rectangle","forms":["rectangle","rectangles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長方形（非正方形）","explanation":"指長度大於寬度、不是正方形的矩形。這是日常使用中很常見的具體形狀概念，例如紙張、螢幕或桌面常被描述為這種形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The table is a long rectangle rather than a square.","zh":"這張桌子是長方形的，而不是正方形的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Draw a long rectangle twice as wide as it is tall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rectangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef5988103d7b93b73646","word":"recycle","forms":["recycle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3fed847a77934fc","term":"recycle","forms":["recycle","recycles","recycling","recycled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"回收並再利用材料","explanation":"指把紙、塑膠、金屬等材料收集並處理，使其中的成分成為新的可用材料。核心畫面是材料沒有被一次性丟棄，而是重新回到生產或使用迴圈中。","examples":[{"en":"Both paper and plastic can be recycled.","zh":"紙和塑膠都可以回收利用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company recycles old phones into new parts.","zh":"這家公司把舊手機回收處理成新的零部件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c57378debfbba557","term":"recycle","forms":["recycle","recycles","recycling","recycled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放入回收箱","explanation":"指把可回收物收集起來並放進指定的回收箱或回收流程，重點是讓它進入後續的回收處理，而不一定親自完成處理過程。","examples":[{"en":"Please rinse the bottles before you recycle them.","zh":"請先把瓶子沖洗乾淨，再放入回收箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please recycle those empty cardboard boxes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recycle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1f51a511f1da0cd348b","word":"red","forms":["red"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da18dd9331567493","term":"red","forms":["red","redder","reddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"紅色的","explanation":"指具有醒目紅色的事物，如血液、夕陽或草莓的顏色，是red最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The girl wore a red skirt.","zh":"那個女孩穿著一條紅裙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red balloon floated above the crowd.","zh":"一個紅氣球飄在了人群上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb8643c9c63188d4","term":"red","forms":["red","redder","reddest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"臉紅的","explanation":"指人的臉或其他身體部位因害羞、憤怒、日曬等原因比平時更紅，像顏色顯現在臉上一樣。","examples":[{"en":"He turned red when everyone started laughing.","zh":"大家開始笑時，他的臉紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After an hour in the sun, her face was red.","zh":"在太陽下待了一個小時後，她的臉紅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f7b59300cca8c68","term":"red","forms":["red","reds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紅色","explanation":"指紅色這種顏色，也就是血液、夕陽或草莓通常呈現的醒目顏色；它還可以泛指紅色這一視覺訊號。","examples":[{"en":"The walls are painted red to make the room feel warmer.","zh":"牆被漆成紅色，讓房間顯得更溫暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Red is often used to attract attention.","zh":"紅色常被用來吸引注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c7e98bfa0c750beb52c","word":"reduce","forms":["reduce"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e5a496084b84c9e","term":"reduce","forms":["reduce","reduces","reducing","reduced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"減少；降低","explanation":"把某物的數量、大小、程度、價值或強度壓低，使它比原來更少、更小、更弱或更便宜。這是 reduce 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The company reduced its prices to attract more customers.","zh":"這家公司降低了價格，以吸引更多顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Turning off the lights can reduce your electricity bill by ten percent.","zh":"關燈可以讓你的電費減少百分之十。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reduce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113,114],"total":4,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1,"114":2}}},{"id":"ceec-46401dc068e724efd350","word":"reduction","forms":["reduction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3136bdda8f16ab97","term":"reduction","forms":["reduction","reductions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"減少；降低","explanation":"指把數量、程度、速度、時間或規模變小的動作、過程，或這種變化本身。重點不在“少了多少”，而在“從多變少”這一整體變化。","examples":[{"en":"The new system led to a significant reduction in waiting times.","zh":"新系統使等待時間大幅減少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a reduction in household waste.","zh":"我們需要減少家庭垃圾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reduction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c8285708f67a873","term":"reduction","forms":["reduction","reductions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"減少的幅度；降幅","explanation":"指某項事物實際減少了多少，常用百分比、數字或比例來說明。它關注的是變化的大小，例如犯罪率下降了百分之五。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign achieved a 10% reduction in energy use.","zh":"這項活動使能源使用量減少了百分之十。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment produced a noticeable reduction in swelling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reduction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9be4c13b9175dcc6902","word":"redundancy","forms":["redundancy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea24184c0f1b5d94","term":"redundancy","forms":["redundancy","redundancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"多餘狀態","explanation":"指某物超出了實際需要，因此顯得多餘或沒有必要。它強調的是一種狀態，而不一定特指某個具體的多餘部分。","examples":[{"en":"The redundancy of these extra forms makes the application process unnecessarily long.","zh":"這些額外表格的多餘使申請流程變得不必要地冗長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report criticized the redundancy of several approval steps.","zh":"這份報告批評了幾個審批步驟的多餘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/redundancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d357982e161b80b","term":"redundancy","forms":["redundancy","redundancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"多餘部分；不必要的重複","explanation":"指具體多出來的內容，尤其是語言中重複表達同一意思的部分。它可以指一個多餘成分，也可以概括地指整段表達中過多的重複。","examples":[{"en":"The editor removed the redundancy from the final paragraph.","zh":"編輯刪去了最後一段中的多餘內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repeating the same point three times creates unnecessary redundancy.","zh":"把同一個觀點重複三遍會造成不必要的冗餘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/redundancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3297cb78604badb2f37a","word":"reef","forms":["reef"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4938976921f00ad3","term":"reef","forms":["reef","reefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"礁；礁石帶","explanation":"指伸到水面附近的一道礁石、沙洲或珊瑚礁，像水中的“脊”一樣可能影響船隻通行。","examples":[{"en":"The boat passed safely between the reef and the shore.","zh":"船安全地從礁石帶和海岸之間駛過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Divers explored a colorful coral reef near the island.","zh":"潛水員探索了島嶼附近色彩斑斕的珊瑚礁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reef","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4b64ad329a8b29e2008","word":"refer","forms":["refer"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a1b24c03e749e48","term":"refer","forms":["refer","refers","referring","referred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"指引某人去找","explanation":"把某人的注意力或行動引向一個地點、部門或能提供幫助的人，相當於告訴他下一步該去哪裡。","examples":[{"en":"The receptionist referred me to the customer service desk.","zh":"接待員把我指引到了客戶服務檯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The librarian referred me to a specialist archive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb6326464be1e68f","term":"refer","forms":["refer","refers","referring","referred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提到並引向","explanation":"說話或寫作時把聽者、讀者的注意力引向某個例子、事實或資料，也就是提到它並讓對方去看它。","examples":[{"en":"For the answer, refer to the example on the next page.","zh":"要找答案，請參看下一頁的例子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide refers readers to the appendix for further details.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9943104afba8f4ca","term":"refer","forms":["refer","refers","referring","referred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"涉及、指的是","explanation":"某句話、文章、物品或行為把內容指向某個物件，意思是“關於它”或“說的就是它”。","examples":[{"en":"The word “they” refers to the students in this sentence.","zh":"這個句子中的“they”指的是那些學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the original building, not the extension.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,113,114,115],"total":7,"counts":{"111":1,"112":2,"113":1,"114":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-81803dd4e410a92bc5d5","word":"referee","forms":["referee"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a8bbb4d372fb3e5","term":"referee","forms":["referee","referees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽裁判","explanation":"在比賽中，referee是站在比賽雙方之間、負責執行規則並作出判罰的裁判。","examples":[{"en":"The referee stopped the match after a player was injured.","zh":"一名球員受傷後，裁判中止了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The players argued with the referee about the penalty.","zh":"球員們就這次判罰與裁判爭論起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/referee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-513b0f0f1c9dc7a6","term":"referee","forms":["referee","referees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭端調解者","explanation":"在爭端中，referee是站在爭執雙方之間、幫助解決分歧並作出判斷的人，不一定出現在體育比賽中。","examples":[{"en":"The manager acted as a referee when the two teams disagreed.","zh":"兩隊發生分歧時，經理充當了調解人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They appointed a referee to resolve the contractual dispute.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/referee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d57365c50cd25b6","term":"referee","forms":["referee","referees","refereeing","refereed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擔任裁判","explanation":"作動詞時，referee表示在一場比賽中擔任裁判，監督規則並作出判罰。","examples":[{"en":"She referees local football matches on weekends.","zh":"她週末為當地的足球比賽擔任裁判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refereed the final despite a hostile crowd.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/referee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52367a6622b19f08825e","word":"reference","forms":["reference"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f2837b9b7b2a374","term":"reference","forms":["reference","references"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推薦資訊；證明人提供的評價","explanation":"指熟悉某人的人提供的評價或相關資訊，通常用於求職、申請學校或租房，以證明這個人的能力、品行或經歷。","examples":[{"en":"The employer asked me to provide two references.","zh":"僱主要求我提供兩位推薦人的資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her former employer supplied an excellent reference.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c20f1cd6eb1b26f4","term":"reference","forms":["reference","references"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文獻引用","explanation":"指在文章中用簡短形式標出某部已發表作品，以說明資訊或論點的來源。","examples":[{"en":"Every quotation in the article should have a reference.","zh":"文章中的每一處引文都應標註文獻出處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add a reference for the quotation in your essay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4e4441aecb2b511","term":"reference","forms":["reference","references"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參考文獻；資料來源","explanation":"指被文章、報告或作品引用的那部已出版作品本身，也就是資訊來源。","examples":[{"en":"The report lists all its references at the end.","zh":"這份報告在末尾列出了全部參考文獻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"List every reference at the end of the essay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reference","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-cf57d2d263f03f8f4271","word":"referendum","forms":["referendum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bbc5ff0fd70ddc01","term":"referendum","forms":["referendum","referenda","referendums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全民公投","explanation":"指讓全體選民直接投票，決定一項擬議的法律、憲法修正案或其他公共議題；重點是公眾直接對“要不要透過”作出判斷，而不是選出代表。","examples":[{"en":"The government announced a referendum on the proposed constitutional amendment.","zh":"政府宣佈就擬議中的憲法修正案舉行公投。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Voters rejected the proposal in yesterday's referendum.","zh":"選民在昨天的公投中否決了這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/referendum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b92d4c46e020a07","term":"referendum","forms":["referendum","referenda","referendums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作為評判","explanation":"指某人的行動、選擇或結果被看作在給另一件事下結論、作評判。例如，一個人的決定可能被誤解為在評價父母的教育表現。","examples":[{"en":"She treated my decision to move out as a referendum on her parenting.","zh":"她把我搬出去的決定看成是在評判她的教養方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The election became a referendum on the government's competence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/referendum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9e893154f468b8cb11d3","word":"refine(ment)","forms":["refine","refinement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5781a4d07e6785a","term":"refine","forms":["refine","refines","refining","refined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提純；除去雜質","explanation":"把含有雜質的原料加工成更純、更均勻的狀態，尤其常用於金屬、石油等材料。它保留了“去掉不需要的部分”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The company refines crude oil into fuel.","zh":"這家公司把原油提煉成燃料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The miners sent the gold to a factory to be refined.","zh":"礦工把黃金送到工廠提純。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9148ec2793094d99","term":"refine","forms":["refine","refines","refining","refined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使舉止或品味更文雅","explanation":"把人的行為、談吐、品味等方面的粗俗或不夠講究之處磨掉，使其顯得更有教養、更優雅；這是“去掉粗糙感”從物質轉到人的表現。","examples":[{"en":"Travel helped her refine her manners and broaden her taste.","zh":"旅行幫助她改善了舉止，也拓寬了品味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher encouraged him to refine his style of speaking.","zh":"老師鼓勵他改進自己的說話方式，使其更得體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ac58f4b2253be0e","term":"refine","forms":["refine","refines","refining","refined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改進；使更準確完善","explanation":"對計劃、方法、估計、論點或作品作進一步調整，去掉不準確或不成熟的部分，使它更可靠、更有效或更出色。","examples":[{"en":"We need to refine the plan before presenting it to the board.","zh":"我們需要先完善這份計劃，再向董事會提交。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineers refined the design after the first tests.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef7edc0b8251d683","term":"refinement","forms":["refinement","refinements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提純；改進","explanation":"指去除雜質、粗糙之處，使材料或事物變得更純、更精細的過程，也可以指由此得到的改良結果。這是 refinement 從“把東西打磨得更好”發展出來的基本含義。","examples":[{"en":"The refinement of the process reduced waste and improved the quality of the product.","zh":"對這一工藝的改進減少了浪費，也提高了產品質量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several refinements to the design made the machine easier to use.","zh":"對設計做了幾處改進後，這臺機器更容易使用了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refinement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efb50e22b3b6105c","term":"refinement","forms":["refinement","refinements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高雅；教養","explanation":"指一種顯得優雅、講究、有教養的風格或品質，通常用於人的舉止、談吐、藝術品味或生活方式。","examples":[{"en":"Her quiet confidence and refinement impressed everyone at the reception.","zh":"她沉靜的自信和優雅的舉止給招待會上的每個人都留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant combines traditional cooking with modern refinement.","zh":"這家餐廳把傳統烹飪與現代雅緻結合在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refinement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65c6c2c392557da5","term":"refinement","forms":["refinement","refinements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細微區別；細化","explanation":"指在原有想法、分類或說法上作出的更細緻區分，使表達或分析更加準確。它仍然保留了“把粗略內容打磨得更精細”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The new study offers a refinement of the theory rather than a complete rejection of it.","zh":"這項新研究是對該理論的細化，而不是完全否定它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This distinction is a useful refinement of the original classification.","zh":"這一區別是對原有分類的有益細化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refinement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-909ca0096d519dcf94ab","word":"reflect","forms":["reflect"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0ce5579abb7793f","term":"reflect","forms":["reflect","reflects","reflecting","reflected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反射光線","explanation":"指表面把光線等彈回去，使光改變方向；重點是“把某物反射出去”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"White walls reflect more sunlight than dark walls.","zh":"白牆比深色牆反射更多陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lake reflected the morning sun.","zh":"湖面反射著清晨的陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-223df77f85e42a7a","term":"reflect","forms":["reflect","reflects","reflecting","reflected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"映照出形象","explanation":"指光滑表面像鏡子一樣顯出某人或某物的影像；可以理解為把形象“轉回”到觀看者眼前。","examples":[{"en":"The calm pond reflected the trees along the shore.","zh":"平靜的池塘映照出岸邊的樹木。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The window reflected her face in the afternoon light.","zh":"窗戶在午後的光線中映照出她的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45c66d379e2935de","term":"reflect","forms":["reflect","reflects","reflecting","reflected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認真思考","explanation":"指把思緒轉回某個問題，安靜而認真地考慮它的意義、後果或自己的行為。","examples":[{"en":"Take some time to reflect on what you have learned.","zh":"花點時間認真想想你學到了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the argument, he reflected on his words.","zh":"爭吵過後，他認真反思了自己說的話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f30409c51a78ed6906df","word":"reflection","forms":["reflection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45da225640e116f4","term":"reflection","forms":["reflection","reflections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反射；反映的過程或狀態","explanation":"這是“折回來”這一核心概念本身：某種光、聲音或影響被返回，或處於被返回、被映出的狀態。它常作為較概括的說法，具體是物理反射還是思想、資訊的映照，要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"The reflection of light from the water made it difficult to see.","zh":"水面反射的光讓人很難看清東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glass gives a clear reflection of the street outside.","zh":"玻璃清楚地映出了外面的街道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62b23494868ef80d","term":"reflection","forms":["reflection","reflections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"波的反射","explanation":"在物理學中，reflection 指光、聲波等傳播到表面後被彈回的現象，仍然是“碰到表面又折回來”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The reflection of sunlight off the snow hurt my eyes.","zh":"陽光從雪地反射回來，刺得我眼睛疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The echo was caused by the reflection of sound waves from the cliff.","zh":"這聲迴音是聲波從懸崖反射回來造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44b08d1b1b21e1b8","term":"reflection","forms":["reflection","reflections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倒影；映像","explanation":"指被表面映出的具體影像，例如鏡子、玻璃或水面中的人和物。它是“光折回來”後呈現出來的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The child smiled at her reflection in the mirror.","zh":"孩子對著鏡中的自己笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could see the mountain’s reflection in the lake.","zh":"我們能看到山在湖中的倒影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a0d9562322f17bf7ce5","word":"reflective","forms":["reflective"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81db547edfc78304","term":"reflective","forms":["reflective","more reflective","most reflective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"反射的；反光的","explanation":"指表面或材料能把光、熱等向原來的方向或其他方向反射回去，像鏡子一樣把外來的東西“送回來”。","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist wore a reflective jacket at night.","zh":"騎腳踏車的人晚上穿了一件反光夾克。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lake was so still that its surface was reflective.","zh":"湖面非常平靜，像鏡子一樣能映出倒影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd91b06710217129","term":"reflective","forms":["reflective","more reflective","most reflective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沉思的；反思的","explanation":"形容人在回想過去、認真考慮經歷或人生問題，而不是立即行動或隨意閒聊；可以理解為思緒轉身照向過去。","examples":[{"en":"After visiting his old school, he became quiet and reflective.","zh":"參觀舊學校後，他變得安靜而沉思起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The holiday gave her a reflective moment to consider the past year.","zh":"這段假期讓她有機會靜下心來回顧過去一年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d164ad30cd61bbb2b32a","word":"reform","forms":["reform"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f2bbe43ba467ac4","term":"reform","forms":["reform","reforms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"改革；改良","explanation":"指把有缺陷、低效或不理想的制度、組織或做法重新塑造，使其得到糾正和改善；也可以指具體的一項改革措施。","examples":[{"en":"The government has promised major reforms to the education system.","zh":"政府承諾對教育制度進行重大改革。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The elections need serious reform.","zh":"選舉制度需要認真改革。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36bcdce1408dab44","term":"reform","forms":["reform","reforms","reforming","reformed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改革；改造；改進","explanation":"表示主動把有問題的人、制度、行為或事物重新塑造，使它從較差狀態變得更好。物件可以是具體的人，也可以是抽象的社會制度或道德行為。","examples":[{"en":"The new program aims to reform the prison system.","zh":"這項新計劃旨在改革監獄制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher believed that patience could reform troubled students.","zh":"這位老師相信耐心能夠幫助問題學生改過自新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c53cf9a0d9c36531005b","word":"refresh(ment)","forms":["refresh","refreshment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d8cd76a0c779f26","term":"refresh","forms":["refresh","refreshes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重新載入頁面","explanation":"在網頁或軟體中，refresh 指重新載入顯示內容，以便看到資料的最新版本，就像把舊畫面換成剛更新的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Refresh the page to see the latest results.","zh":"重新整理頁面就能看到最新結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A quick refresh fixed the display problem.","zh":"快速重新整理一下就解決了顯示問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refresh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83da635951e82747","term":"refresh","forms":["refresh","refreshes","refreshing","refreshed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使恢復活力","explanation":"refresh 某人或某物，就是讓它從疲憊、枯竭或缺乏活力的狀態重新恢復過來；睡眠、休息和涼爽的空氣都可能起到這種作用。","examples":[{"en":"A short walk refreshed my mind.","zh":"短暫散步讓我的頭腦恢復了活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cool water refreshed us after the hike.","zh":"徒步後，涼水讓我們恢復了精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refresh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-895a9e7f8693f68e","term":"refresh","forms":["refresh","refreshes","refreshing","refreshed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重新載入網頁","explanation":"在計算機語境中，refresh 指重新載入文件，尤其是網頁，以顯示發生的最新變化。","examples":[{"en":"She refreshed the page and saw that the price had changed.","zh":"她重新整理了頁面，看到價格已經變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If the message does not appear, refresh the browser.","zh":"如果訊息沒有出現，就重新整理瀏覽器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refresh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e3cfdb90c4ab19e","term":"refreshment","forms":["refreshment","refreshments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恢復精力的過程","explanation":"指透過休息、清涼空氣、安靜活動等使身體或精神重新有力、舒暢的過程。這裡的重點是“重新恢復狀態”，不專指吃喝。","examples":[{"en":"A quiet walk in the park provided welcome refreshment after the stressful meeting.","zh":"在公園裡安靜地散了會兒步，讓人在那場緊張的會議後恢復了精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A walk in the garden brought welcome refreshment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refreshment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66239cdbaa1b2834","term":"refreshment","forms":["refreshment","refreshments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"茶點和飲料","explanation":"指供人恢復體力或解渴的簡單食物和飲料，尤其是在會議、聚會或活動中提供的茶點。它可以指一類東西，通常用複數形式。","examples":[{"en":"Refreshments will be served in the lobby after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，大廳裡會提供茶點和飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Light refreshments will be served after the lecture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refreshment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e78b139c465a7facbf1","word":"refreshment(s)","forms":["refreshment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-52a64fa94fe11f77","term":"refreshment","forms":["refreshment","refreshments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恢復精力的過程","explanation":"指透過休息、清涼空氣、安靜活動等使身體或精神重新有力、舒暢的過程。這裡的重點是“重新恢復狀態”，不專指吃喝。","examples":[{"en":"A quiet walk in the park provided welcome refreshment after the stressful meeting.","zh":"在公園裡安靜地散了會兒步，讓人在那場緊張的會議後恢復了精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A walk beside the river offered much-needed refreshment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refreshment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47e0d3be50170aff","term":"refreshment","forms":["refreshment","refreshments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"茶點和飲料","explanation":"指供人恢復體力或解渴的簡單食物和飲料，尤其是在會議、聚會或活動中提供的茶點。它可以指一類東西，通常用複數形式。","examples":[{"en":"Refreshments will be served in the lobby after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，大廳裡會提供茶點和飲料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sandwiches and other refreshments were waiting in the committee room.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refreshment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b247a891b461d06f7478","word":"refrigerator/fridge","forms":["refrigerator","fridge"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-055468e2c903c1d9","term":"refrigerator","forms":["refrigerator","refrigerators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冰箱；冷藏裝置","explanation":"指利用製冷來保持食物新鮮的家用或商用裝置，也就是通常所說的冰箱。這是 refrigerator 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the milk in the refrigerator.","zh":"請把牛奶放進冰箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was almost nothing left in the refrigerator.","zh":"冰箱裡幾乎什麼都不剩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refrigerator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-755e254752e5173f","term":"refrigerator","forms":["refrigerator","refrigerators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專用冷藏裝置","explanation":"也可指為非食品物品提供低溫儲存條件的裝置，例如醫院或實驗室中用來冷藏血液、藥品和其他對溫度敏感物品的裝置。核心仍然是“用冷氣儲存東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The vaccines must be kept in a refrigerator.","zh":"這些疫苗必須放在冷藏裝置中儲存。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laboratory refrigerator holds temperature-sensitive biological samples.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refrigerator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a42b1c34c2c2a525","term":"fridge","forms":["fridge","fridges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冰箱","explanation":"指用來冷藏或儲存食物、飲料的家用電器，是 refrigerator 的常用非正式簡稱。","examples":[{"en":"There’s some juice in the fridge if you’re thirsty.","zh":"你要是渴了，冰箱裡有些果汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the leftovers in the fridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8cb7a8a0a8728edf5b08","word":"refuge","forms":["refuge"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5dddca100b4ca9d","term":"refuge","forms":["refuge","refuges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安全與庇護狀態","explanation":"指人在危險中得到保護、暫時安全的狀態，重點是“受到庇護”，不一定強調具體地點。","examples":[{"en":"Many families found refuge in neighboring countries.","zh":"許多家庭在鄰國找到了庇護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers sought refuge from the storm.","zh":"村民們尋求躲避暴風雨的地方和保護。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refuge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b1186b15279d819","term":"refuge","forms":["refuge","refuges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提供庇護的地方","explanation":"指一個能讓人躲避危險、獲得保護的具體地點，例如避難所、藏身處或安全地點。","examples":[{"en":"The old church became a refuge for people fleeing the fighting.","zh":"這座老教堂成了逃離戰火的人們的避難所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cave provided a refuge from the cold.","zh":"這個洞穴提供了躲避寒冷的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refuge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0c913ecf11318b1988a","word":"refugee","forms":["refugee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-606f100c4086d527","term":"refugee","forms":["refugee","refugees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"難民；避難者","explanation":"指因戰爭、政治或宗教迫害、自然災害等無法安全留在原居地，而逃到別處尋求保護的人，尤其常指逃往外國的人。重點不只是“離開”，而是被危險或迫害逼迫著逃離並需要安全保障。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of refugees fled the war and crossed the border.","zh":"數千名難民逃離戰爭，越過了邊境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was granted refugee status after proving that she faced persecution at home.","zh":"她證明自己在國內面臨迫害後，獲准取得難民身份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refugee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d630127108f1feaf1f7","word":"refund","forms":["refund"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0eab7a26ae42ae7e","term":"refund","forms":["refund","refunds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"退款；退還的錢","explanation":"指商家或其他收款方退回給付款人的錢，常見原因包括商品有問題、退貨、服務取消或付款過多。","examples":[{"en":"I asked for a refund because the headphones stopped working.","zh":"我申請了退款，因為這副耳機壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The airline gave us a full refund for the canceled flight.","zh":"航班取消後，航空公司給了我們全額退款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refund","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c73358b826c9981","term":"refund","forms":["refund","refunds","refunding","refunded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"退還錢款","explanation":"指商家、平臺或其他收款方把已經收取的錢退還給付款人，常用於退貨、服務取消或價格差額補償。","examples":[{"en":"The store refunded me the full price after I returned the damaged lamp.","zh":"我退回損壞的檯燈後，商店把全款退給了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They refunded the difference when I found the same jacket on sale.","zh":"我發現同一件夾克在打折後，他們把差價退給了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refund","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-424fb0794608103b88e8","word":"refusal","forms":["refusal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26ea4b3d6f409661","term":"refusal","forms":["refusal","refusals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拒絕；拒不接受","explanation":"指不答應要求、不接受提議，或不願意做某事的行為和結果；重點是把對方的要求擋在門外。","examples":[{"en":"Her refusal to answer the question made everyone suspicious.","zh":"她拒絕回答這個問題，讓大家都起了疑心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company sent a written refusal of our request.","zh":"公司書面拒絕了我們的請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refusal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5fde095c479bdfd93ade","word":"refuse","forms":["refuse"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-073fbf10be7b231e","term":"refuse","forms":["refuse","refuses","refusing","refused","refusest","refusedst","refuseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拒絕請求","explanation":"表示明確不接受某人的請求、要求或提議，把對方想要的事情推回去。","examples":[{"en":"She refused my request for more time.","zh":"她拒絕了我延長時間的請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bank refused his loan application.","zh":"銀行拒絕了他的貸款申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c454261c3348830","term":"refuse","forms":["refuse","refuses","refusing","refused","refusest","refusedst","refuseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拒不做某事","explanation":"表示主語不肯做某事，或不肯繼續接受某種要求；核心仍是把要求推回去。","examples":[{"en":"He refused to answer the question.","zh":"他拒絕回答這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refused to leave until the missing wages were paid.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refuse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bf0daf415a9141eeaa0","word":"refute","forms":["refute"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7efed7f79c077164","term":"refute","forms":["refute","refutes","refuting","refuted","refutest","refutedst","refuteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"證明錯誤；駁倒","explanation":"指透過事實、證據或嚴密推理，證明某個觀點、說法或論證是錯誤的或不能成立。重點在於“把對方的說法駁倒”，而不只是說自己不接受。","examples":[{"en":"The new evidence completely refuted the witness's account.","zh":"新的證據完全駁倒了那名證人的說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several studies have refuted the claim that the treatment is unsafe.","zh":"多項研究已經證明“這種治療不安全”的說法是錯誤的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/refute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe099a0620ce9759b542","word":"regard","forms":["regard"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f585868a449212a1","term":"regard","forms":["regard","regards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關切；尊重；關係","explanation":"當目光長期停留在某人身上時，就可以表示對對方的關心、重視或尊重；也可表示與某人或某事的關係、關聯。","examples":[{"en":"The committee has great regard for her judgment.","zh":"委員會非常看重她的判斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In regard to your question, we need more information.","zh":"關於你的問題，我們還需要更多資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2377072f532c53dd","term":"regard","forms":["regard","regards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方面；考慮","explanation":"指看待一件事時特別注意的某個方面，也就是“從哪一點來考慮”。它保留了“把目光放在某個方面上”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We have strict rules with regard to workplace safety.","zh":"關於工作場所安全，我們有嚴格的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In that regard, the smaller model performs better.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5b0599e3a2d0789","term":"regard","forms":["regard","regards","regarding","regarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看待；認為","explanation":"表示把某人或某事放在某種眼光下看，也就是“認為、視為”。這是 regard 在現代英語中最重要的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"Many people regard this book as a modern classic.","zh":"許多人把這本書看作現代經典。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I regard honesty as essential in a friendship.","zh":"我認為誠實在友誼中必不可少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed7f0287406dc11011f7","word":"regarding","forms":["regarding"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-889f8070769ff89a","term":"regarding","forms":["regarding"],"pos":"prep","zh":"關於；就……而言","explanation":"表示把注意力放到某個主題上，也就是“談到、涉及某事”。它常用於引出郵件、報告、討論或正式說明中的具體話題。","examples":[{"en":"I have a question regarding your application.","zh":"我有一個關於你的申請的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regarding tomorrow's meeting, we need to change the time.","zh":"關於明天的會議，我們需要調整時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regarding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-005cef244b8c15367552","word":"regardless","forms":["regardless"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29a400c54ca3ad87","term":"regardless","forms":["regardless","more regardless","most regardless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不理會；不顧","explanation":"表示對某人或某事不加註意，甚至有意把它放到一邊。它和“沒有把這件事放在心上”的畫面相連，常用於說明某人不顧某個情況仍然採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"She was regardless of the danger and walked into the dark room.","zh":"她完全不顧危險，走進了那間黑屋子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He remained regardless of my advice.","zh":"他根本不理會我的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regardless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83f884fc96c49229","term":"regardless","forms":["regardless","more regardless","most regardless"],"pos":"adv","zh":"無論如何；不管怎樣","explanation":"表示已經知道某個警告、問題或可能的壞結果，卻仍然做同一件事。它把“我知道，但我還是要做”的核心畫面單獨說出來。","examples":[{"en":"The road was icy, but we drove on regardless.","zh":"路面結了冰，但我們還是繼續開車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I know it may be difficult; I will try regardless.","zh":"我知道這可能很難，但無論如何我都會試試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regardless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ac98b1ff4e11fb492a7","word":"regime","forms":["regime"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04e86241ca82b6d8","term":"regime","forms":["regime","regimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管理制度","explanation":"指對人、機構或某個地方進行管理和控制時所採用的一整套規則與做法，重點在“怎樣管、怎樣執行”。","examples":[{"en":"The prison operates under a strict regime.","zh":"這所監獄實行嚴格的管理制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school introduced a new regime for handling complaints.","zh":"這所學校為處理投訴引入了新的管理制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ecef02ee9c9d4fb","term":"regime","forms":["regime","regimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政權","explanation":"指一個國家的政府或掌權集團，尤其常指以強制、專制或極權方式統治的政權。它仍然保留“統治的一整套安排”這個核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The regime censored newspapers and blocked several websites.","zh":"該政權審查報紙，並封鎖了幾個網站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thousands of people protested against the military regime.","zh":"數千人抗議這個軍人政權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e98f661ec01d01bf","term":"regime","forms":["regime","regimes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生活或訓練方案","explanation":"指為達到某種目標而嚴格遵守的一套生活、飲食、鍛鍊或治療安排；它和政治制度的共同點是都有持續、規則化的管理。","examples":[{"en":"She follows a daily fitness regime to prepare for the marathon.","zh":"她遵循每日健身計劃，為馬拉松做準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor put him on a strict diet regime.","zh":"醫生讓他嚴格遵守一套飲食方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c697d2981bf416569a16","word":"region","forms":["region"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ef25c4f68fd5c87","term":"region","forms":["region","regions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地區；區域","explanation":"指一片範圍較大、彼此相連但邊界不一定明確的陸地或海域，也可以泛指因地理、社會或文化特徵而被看作一個整體的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The coastal region is famous for its fresh seafood.","zh":"這個沿海地區以新鮮海鮮聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rain is expected in the northern regions.","zh":"北部地區預計會有大雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/region","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd3ff0274e2df243","term":"region","forms":["region","regions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行政區","explanation":"指城市、領土或國家中按行政管理劃分出來的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"The government plans to build a hospital in every region.","zh":"政府計劃在每個行政區都建一所醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each region elects representatives to the national assembly.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/region","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3a5741a84054b2e1c91","word":"regional","forms":["regional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf39f17004700463","term":"regional","forms":["regional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"地區的；區域性的","explanation":"指與某個特定地區或行政區域有關的事物，重點是它的範圍被限定在這塊“地區圈”內。","examples":[{"en":"The government is investing in regional hospitals.","zh":"政府正在投資建設區域醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conference brought together regional leaders.","zh":"這次會議聚集了各地區的領導人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a971931f4c5421c","term":"regional","forms":["regional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大區域的；區域範圍的","explanation":"指涉及一個較大的地理區域，而不是單個城市、村莊或其他小範圍地點；它仍然是在用“地區圈”界定範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying regional rainfall patterns.","zh":"科學家正在研究區域降雨模式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project promotes regional cooperation across national borders.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87780fa5de684e87cb92","word":"register","forms":["register"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e2d7e789a827307","term":"register","forms":["register","registers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"登記記錄","explanation":"register可以指把姓名、出勤情況、事件或交易等按規則記錄下來的登記記錄；它體現了“讓資訊清楚留下來”的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher checked the register before the lesson began.","zh":"老師在上課前核對了點名冊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please add your name to the visitor register.","zh":"請把你的名字登記在訪客登記冊上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/register","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95da49aa82443a11","term":"register","forms":["register","registers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語體","explanation":"register可以指語言在特定場合、對特定物件或為特定目的使用的風格；就像把語言放進不同的“語體”中，正式程度和措辭會隨場合改變。","examples":[{"en":"The report uses a formal register throughout.","zh":"這份報告始終使用正式語體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children often use a different register when speaking to teachers.","zh":"孩子和老師說話時往往會使用不同的語體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/register","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-205b4ce74244f8b5","term":"register","forms":["register","registers","registering","registered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"登記；註冊加入","explanation":"把姓名或相關資訊正式放進登記冊、名單或系統裡，也可以指登記加入某個組織或活動。記住“把資訊放進有規則的系統並留下來”，就是這個用法的核心。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic registered every new patient before the appointment.","zh":"診所在預約前為每位新病人登記了資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Register for the workshop before places fill up.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/register","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39883c2af5df0490","term":"register","forms":["register","registers","registering","registered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"記錄；記下","explanation":"把事實、結果或資訊清楚地記錄下來，尤其是寫進檔案、表格或正式記錄中；在比賽報道中，也可指留下某項成績或結果。","examples":[{"en":"The report registered a sharp rise in housing costs.","zh":"這份報告記錄了住房成本的大幅上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team failed to register a goal in the second half.","zh":"這支球隊在下半場沒能進球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/register","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29c9c30e0604515ced98","word":"registration","forms":["registration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f630024b0acc0a6","term":"registration","forms":["registration","registrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"登記；註冊；報名","explanation":"指把自己的姓名、資料或物件正式錄入某個系統、名單或活動中的行為，重點是完成獲得資格或正式身份所需的登記手續。","examples":[{"en":"Complete the registration process before Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前完成登記手續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Online registration opens next Monday.","zh":"網上報名下週一開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/registration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75b5a6898c911f7a","term":"registration","forms":["registration","registrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"登記證；註冊檔案","explanation":"指用來證明某人、車輛或其他物件已經登記，或使其登記正式生效的檔案、表格或證件。這裡說的是登記留下的具體憑證，而不是登記這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"Please keep your car registration in the glove compartment.","zh":"請把車輛登記證放在手套箱裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer asked to see my vehicle registration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/registration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5259acec0d80c4fe134","word":"regret","forms":["regret"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99fdd19f1da7b102","term":"regret","forms":["regret","regrets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"後悔；遺憾","explanation":"指回頭看過去做過或經歷過的事，覺得結果不理想，並希望當時有所不同的痛苦或不滿。它連線著“走錯路後回頭看”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She looked back on the decision with regret.","zh":"她回想起那個決定時感到後悔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has no regrets about leaving the city.","zh":"他不後悔離開那座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regret","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5508962cc314c72","term":"regret","forms":["regret","regrets","regretting","regretted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"後悔做過的事","explanation":"指因為某件已經發生或可能沒有發生的事而感到難過，並希望事情不是這樣。最典型的是回頭看自己的言語、行動或決定，覺得當初應該選擇另一條路。","examples":[{"en":"I regret telling her the secret.","zh":"我後悔把那個秘密告訴了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He deeply regrets his decision to leave.","zh":"他非常後悔自己決定離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regret","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-667937c3e7a68ea37471","word":"regular","forms":["regular"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-52f848a14e3c83d2","term":"regular","forms":["regular","more regular","most regular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"整齊有規律的","explanation":"形狀、排列或外觀呈現穩定而均勻的規律，符合“合乎規則、保持穩定”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The garden has regular rows of flowers.","zh":"花園裡的花排成整齊有規律的幾行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Arrange the stones in regular rows.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-450ff3aa00721a2f","term":"regular","forms":["regular","more regular","most regular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"定期發生的","explanation":"指事情以穩定的、通常較短的時間間隔反覆發生，正是“保持穩定”在時間上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"She makes regular visits to her grandparents.","zh":"她定期去看望祖父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise can improve your sleep.","zh":"定期鍛鍊可以改善睡眠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b67290f3d3f1937","term":"regular","forms":["regular","more regular","most regular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"規則變化的","explanation":"在語法中，指按照某種語言通常規則變化的詞，尤其常指按一般規則構成過去式或過去分詞的動詞。","examples":[{"en":"“Played” is the past tense of a regular verb.","zh":"“played”是規則動詞的過去式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Walk is a regular verb because its past form adds -ed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af662798cf5a1a37","term":"regular","forms":["regular","more regular","most regular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"普通正常的","explanation":"指具有通常預期的特徵，平常、標準而不特別；這是“符合通常標準”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll have a regular coffee, please.","zh":"請給我一杯普通咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store is closed on regular business days.","zh":"這家商店在正常營業日也關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77ede212aeb4c0999cbc","word":"regulate","forms":["regulate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1267a281bbfbe420","term":"regulate","forms":["regulate","regulates","regulating","regulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按規則控制","explanation":"指按照規則、原則或法律來控制某項活動、過程或關係，使其在規定範圍內進行。","examples":[{"en":"New laws regulate how companies handle customer data.","zh":"新法律規定了公司如何處理客戶資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency regulates the safety of public transportation.","zh":"該機構負責監管公共交通的安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab23edf8ea9c8997","term":"regulate","forms":["regulate","regulates","regulating","regulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"規定政策","explanation":"指由有權力的個人或機構決定並規定應遵循的政策或方針，是“用規則來管事”的起點。","examples":[{"en":"The government regulates national energy policy.","zh":"政府制定並規範國家能源政策。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency regulates how personal data may be stored.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-383b6630e8241d34d54b","word":"regulation","forms":["regulation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d86eb76b9a325c58","term":"regulation","forms":["regulation","regulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"調節；管控","explanation":"指把某種活動、過程或狀態控制在合適範圍內的行為，或這種受到控制的狀態。它強調“調節器”正在發揮作用，而不是某一條具體規則。","examples":[{"en":"The regulation of water supplies is essential during a drought.","zh":"在乾旱期間，對供水的調節十分重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Strict regulation of the industry has reduced pollution.","zh":"對這個行業的嚴格管控減少了汙染。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d41cb2f1a700ed70","term":"regulation","forms":["regulation","regulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"規章；規定","explanation":"指組織、學校、公司或其他機構制定的具體規則，用來規定成員應該怎樣做。它是“調節”這一核心概念落到紙面上的結果。","examples":[{"en":"All employees must follow the company's safety regulations.","zh":"所有員工都必須遵守公司的安全規章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new regulation limits the number of visitors each day.","zh":"這項新規定限制了每天的訪客人數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b9443bcd66ef05240ce","word":"rehabilitate","forms":["rehabilitate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e6a81e49215aa9d","term":"rehabilitate","forms":["rehabilitate","rehabilitates","rehabilitating","rehabilitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"恢復原有地位或狀態","explanation":"使某人或某物回到原來較好的狀態，包括恢復名譽、財產、身份或社會地位。這是最寬泛的用法，其他許多含義都可以看作“重新扶起來”。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign helped rehabilitate the mayor's image after the scandal.","zh":"這場宣傳活動幫助市長在醜聞後恢復了形象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new evidence rehabilitated the scientist in the eyes of the public.","zh":"新的證據使這位科學家重新贏得了公眾的認可。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rehabilitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c10cc2afa0bb9df2","term":"rehabilitate","forms":["rehabilitate","rehabilitates","rehabilitating","rehabilitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"恢復名譽；證明清白","explanation":"專門指讓一個人、一個觀點或一種做法重新獲得認可，尤其是在它曾被誤解、否定或認為不值得信任之後。","examples":[{"en":"The documentary rehabilitated the artist's reputation among younger viewers.","zh":"這部紀錄片使這位藝術家在年輕觀眾中的聲譽得到恢復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New evidence helped rehabilitate the wrongly accused officer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rehabilitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab9a5b26a10edd6a","term":"rehabilitate","forms":["rehabilitate","rehabilitates","rehabilitating","rehabilitated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使恢復健康","explanation":"透過治療、護理或戒除成癮等方式，使人在疾病、受傷或成癮後恢復良好身體或心理狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic rehabilitates patients after serious sports injuries.","zh":"這家診所幫助嚴重運動損傷患者進行康復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The center rehabilitates athletes recovering from serious injuries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rehabilitate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bcd3e14dca8fdb18ca3","word":"rehearsal","forms":["rehearsal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef5241d3e52f06ff","term":"rehearsal","forms":["rehearsal","rehearsals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排練；演練","explanation":"指表演、活動或一套流程正式進行前，參與者先把內容和配合完整走一遍，以發現問題、改進配合或調整裝置。它保留了“先走一遍再正式開始”的核心畫面，因此不只用於舞臺表演。","examples":[{"en":"The band is having a rehearsal before the concert tonight.","zh":"樂隊正在為今晚的音樂會排練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ran a full rehearsal of the emergency procedure.","zh":"我們對整套應急程式進行了一次完整演練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rehearsal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7668cf4452605ed5","term":"rehearsal","forms":["rehearsal","rehearsals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預演；前兆","explanation":"指某件已經發生的事只是另一件更大或更嚴重事情的提前示範。這裡不一定真的有人排練，而是借用“先走一遍”的畫面，表示未來情形的預演或警示。","examples":[{"en":"The power cuts were a rehearsal for the crisis that followed.","zh":"這些停電是後來那場危機的一次預演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The border clash proved a rehearsal for the wider war.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rehearsal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-017c3548afaae5f6b519","word":"rehearse","forms":["rehearse"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd970edf9b511b08","term":"rehearse","forms":["rehearse","rehearses","rehearsing","rehearsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重複說；重述","explanation":"指把已經說過的話再次說出來，常含有“又把同一個論點說一遍”的意味。它強調內容的重複，不一定表示正在為表演做準備。","examples":[{"en":"There is no need to rehearse the same old argument again.","zh":"沒必要再重複那套老論點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He rehearsed his grievances to anyone who would listen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rehearse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-146f2539fd138c8c","term":"rehearse","forms":["rehearse","rehearses","rehearsing","rehearsed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排練；反覆練習","explanation":"指在正式演出、展示或公開表達之前，反覆練習臺詞、動作或整段流程，以便發現問題並改進。這裡的“重複”從說話內容擴充套件到了表演動作和整體呈現。","examples":[{"en":"The actors rehearsed the final scene for two hours.","zh":"演員們排練了最後一幕兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are rehearsing for the school play this week.","zh":"我們這周正在為學校戲劇排練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rehearse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3291095b83319c890d97","word":"reign","forms":["reign"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8585947db4c143e4","term":"reign","forms":["reign","reigns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"君主統治","explanation":"指君主實際行使最高權力、管理國家的統治行為，重點是“掌權並治理”，而不是單純擁有王位。","examples":[{"en":"The country prospered under her reign.","zh":"這個國家在她的統治下繁榮起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The queen's reign lasted nearly five decades.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3496059d0adaa5ad","term":"reign","forms":["reign","reigns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統治時期","explanation":"指某位君主在位並統治國家的那段時間，重點是“從開始掌權到結束掌權的時期”。","examples":[{"en":"The reign of Victoria lasted for many years.","zh":"維多利亞女王的統治時期持續了許多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cathedral was completed during the queen's reign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5e6a5ec4c9455779","term":"reign","forms":["reign","reigns","reigning","reigned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"稱王統治","explanation":"指以君主身份掌握最高權力並統治國家，是名詞“君主統治”在動作上的對應表達。","examples":[{"en":"She reigned as queen for thirty years.","zh":"她當了三十年的女王。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The queen reigned for nearly sixty years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c17fb27fc5002b22e31","word":"reinforce","forms":["reinforce"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46160e99f11c0667","term":"reinforce","forms":["reinforce","reinforces","reinforcing","reinforced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加固；增強","explanation":"給物體增加材料、支撐或力量，使它更堅固、更能承受壓力。這個意義最接近“給牆再加一根支柱”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"They reinforced the bridge with extra steel beams.","zh":"他們用額外的鋼樑加固了這座橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The carpenter reinforced the shelf before we put the books on it.","zh":"木匠先加固了架子，然後我們才把書放上去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reinforce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cada7035c691603f","term":"reinforce","forms":["reinforce","reinforces","reinforcing","reinforced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鞏固；加強記憶或觀點","explanation":"透過複習、重複說明或補充證據，讓知識、觀點或印象變得更牢固。就像把學過的內容再支撐一次，使它不容易忘記或動搖。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher used a short quiz to reinforce the main points of the lesson.","zh":"老師用小測驗來鞏固這節課的重點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report reinforces the idea that regular exercise improves health.","zh":"這份報告進一步強化了定期鍛鍊有益健康這一觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reinforce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-084e990a49ba65e62292","word":"reject","forms":["reject"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-44fd146878c0092b","term":"reject","forms":["reject","rejects","rejecting","rejected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拒絕接受","explanation":"表示不接受某個提議、申請、想法、產品或條件，把它“扔回去”；這是reject最核心、最廣泛的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The committee rejected her application because it was incomplete.","zh":"委員會因為她的申請材料不完整而拒絕了她的申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I rejected their offer and asked them to reconsider the price.","zh":"我拒絕了他們的報價，並請他們重新考慮價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reject","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd793986cd6d45968d3c","word":"rejection","forms":["rejection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fbd5dd343e2fb061","term":"rejection","forms":["rejection","rejections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拒絕行為","explanation":"指主動不接受某個提議、申請、請求或某人，是“說不”這一行為本身。","examples":[{"en":"My offer was met with rejection.","zh":"我的提議遭到了拒絕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She handled the rejection calmly and tried again.","zh":"她平靜地面對這次拒絕，又試了一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81dadfcdfd4e250a","term":"rejection","forms":["rejection","rejections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被拒的狀態","explanation":"指某人或某事已經被拒絕、未被接受的處境或結果，重點不在拒絕動作，而在“被擋在外面”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The rejection of his application left him disappointed.","zh":"他的申請被拒，讓他感到失望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After several rejections, he changed his approach.","zh":"幾次被拒之後，他改變了方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecf811511d5d962c368b","word":"rejoice","forms":["rejoice"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-128972908104d1ce","term":"rejoice","forms":["rejoice","rejoices","rejoicing","rejoiced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"歡喜；欣喜","explanation":"指自己因為某件事而感到非常快樂、滿足或振奮，彷彿心裡一下子亮了起來。","examples":[{"en":"The whole town rejoiced at the news of the rescue.","zh":"全鎮的人都為獲救的訊息感到欣喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We rejoiced in the return of spring.","zh":"我們因春天的到來而歡欣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejoice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-158a60564f79bd15","term":"rejoice","forms":["rejoice","rejoices","rejoicing","rejoiced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使高興；使振奮","explanation":"指某件事把喜悅帶給別人，使對方的心情變得快樂或振奮；也就是讓別人的心“亮起來”。","examples":[{"en":"The children's success rejoiced their parents.","zh":"孩子們的成功讓父母感到欣慰和喜悅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It rejoiced her heart to see old friends together again.","zh":"看到老朋友再次聚在一起，她心裡十分高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejoice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e78618f499c47e470b9d","word":"relate","forms":["relate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc5ef8a7814ededb","term":"relate","forms":["relate","relates","relating","related"],"pos":"verb","zh":"講述；敘述","explanation":"把一件經歷、故事或事件按描述性的方式講給別人聽，就像把事情重新帶回來。重點不是簡單說出一個事實，而是較完整地敘述它。","examples":[{"en":"She related the whole story to us after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，她把整個故事講給我們聽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He related the strange events of the previous night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d90e56b9534c38a3","term":"relate","forms":["relate","relates","relating","related"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……聯絡起來","explanation":"把一個事物、事實或結果連到另一個事物上，說明它們之間的關係。這裡強調的是主動建立或指出聯絡，而不只是說兩者碰巧有關。","examples":[{"en":"The report relates the drop in sales to rising prices.","zh":"這份報告把銷售額下降與價格上漲聯絡起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher related the lesson to problems students face every day.","zh":"老師把這節課和學生每天遇到的問題聯絡起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd9a415847571e67","term":"relate","forms":["relate","relates","relating","related"],"pos":"verb","zh":"產生共鳴；理解認同","explanation":"表示把自己的感受或經歷和別人聯絡起來，因此能夠理解、認同對方。它常強調“我能不能在對方身上看到自己”，不只是理性地知道對方的處境。","examples":[{"en":"Many new parents can relate to her worries.","zh":"許多新手父母都能理解她的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can relate to her frustration with the delays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc8fbb48a3a16bfdd853","word":"relation","forms":["relation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7dfaccb783f24ff","term":"relation","forms":["relation","relations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯絡；關聯","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物彼此聯絡、相互關聯的方式，重點是說明它們之間有什麼聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The relation between diet and health is complex.","zh":"飲食和健康之間的聯絡很複雜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers are studying the relation of sleep to memory.","zh":"研究人員正在研究睡眠與記憶之間的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ac3bdf8ea98043b","term":"relation","forms":["relation","relations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關係；交往","explanation":"指人、團體或國家之間相處和互動的關係，也包括這種交往所呈現的狀態或方式。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries are working to improve their relations.","zh":"兩國正努力改善彼此的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dispute damaged relations between the neighboring countries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28d9e7bbbf81137ec80d","word":"relationship","forms":["relationship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26ed2131d347cd68","term":"relationship","forms":["relationship","relationships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯絡；關聯","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物、人物之間存在的聯絡或關聯，重點是它們彼此有關，而不一定說明這種聯絡具體是什麼。","examples":[{"en":"The study examines the relationship between sleep and memory.","zh":"這項研究考察睡眠與記憶之間的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a close relationship between language and culture.","zh":"語言和文化之間有著密切的聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relationship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0faa9c76ef25592","term":"relationship","forms":["relationship","relationships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相處關係","explanation":"指兩個人或多個群體實際相處、合作和彼此對待的方式，重點是關係的質量或狀態，例如融洽、緊張或專業。","examples":[{"en":"I have a good working relationship with my new manager.","zh":"我和新經理有很好的工作關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher worked hard to build a trusting relationship with her students.","zh":"這位老師努力與學生建立互信的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relationship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2d9e1f13413d3e07064","word":"relative","forms":["relative"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-061cb6e7f089370b","term":"relative","forms":["relative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相對的；比較而言的","explanation":"某種性質不是絕對固定的，而是要和其他事物比較後才能判斷。例如，一個結果可以說是“相對令人失望的”，意思是和原先的期待或其他結果相比顯得不理想。","examples":[{"en":"The team enjoyed relative success despite its limited budget.","zh":"儘管預算有限，這支隊伍還是取得了相對不錯的成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her quiet voice was a relative advantage in the noisy room.","zh":"在嘈雜的房間裡，她聲音小反而成了相對的優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea816ffc3a537897","term":"relative","forms":["relative","relatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親屬；家人","explanation":"作名詞時，relative 指和某人有血緣、婚姻或收養關係的人，也就是家庭關係中的“親屬”。這個意義和形容詞的“有關係的”相呼應，只是這裡關係具體指家庭關係。","examples":[{"en":"One of my relatives is coming to stay with us next week.","zh":"我的一位親戚下週要來和我們一起住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She invited all her close relatives to the wedding.","zh":"她邀請了所有近親參加婚禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51945df720a5a6e21693","word":"relax","forms":["relax"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c45866b5a9f785b","term":"relax","forms":["relax","relaxes","relaxing","relaxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使放鬆","explanation":"讓某人或某人的心情從緊張、壓力中緩解下來，使其能夠休息或平靜下來。","examples":[{"en":"A quiet walk helped relax her after the stressful meeting.","zh":"緊張的會議結束後，安靜地散步幫助她放鬆了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Soft music relaxes my mind.","zh":"輕柔的音樂能使我的心情放鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c4aabb16ed81db8","term":"relax","forms":["relax","relaxes","relaxing","relaxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放鬆休息","explanation":"自己從緊張或忙碌中緩解下來，休息並恢復輕鬆狀態；這是現代英語中最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I relax by listening to music before bed.","zh":"我睡前透過聽音樂來放鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We relaxed beside the pool after our long journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-394e3adb0572ad71bad9","word":"relaxation","forms":["relaxation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-781d61b53f374da7","term":"relaxation","forms":["relaxation","relaxations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"放鬆；鬆弛狀態","explanation":"指身體或心理從壓力、緊張中鬆開來的行為或狀態，也可泛指以減輕壓力為目的的休閒。它是 relaxation 最核心、最常用的意義。","examples":[{"en":"A little relaxation after work helps me sleep better.","zh":"下班後稍微放鬆一下有助於我睡得更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel offers a quiet space for relaxation.","zh":"這家酒店提供了一個安靜的放鬆空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relaxation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43535d919f9370b5","term":"relaxation","forms":["relaxation","relaxations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"休閒；放鬆活動","explanation":"指人在勞累或精神緊張之後用來恢復身心的休閒活動，也可以指由此得到的輕鬆狀態。它和 s1 相近，但更突出“用來休息的活動或消遣”。","examples":[{"en":"I go for a walk in the evening for relaxation.","zh":"我晚上散步來放鬆身心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reading is my favorite form of relaxation.","zh":"閱讀是我最喜歡的放鬆方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relaxation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-682fbae20f3428bcec4c","word":"relay","forms":["relay"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70720033879fbcbc","term":"relay","forms":["relay","relays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接力賽","explanation":"指由團隊成員輪流完成不同部分的比賽。每個人完成自己的階段後，把任務交給下一位隊員，這正是“接替”概念在體育中的典型用法。","examples":[{"en":"Our school won the four-by-four hundred-meter relay.","zh":"我們學校贏得了四乘一百米接力賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each runner passed the baton to the next member of the team.","zh":"每名跑步者都把接力棒交給了隊裡的下一名成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-955fe49b235de956","term":"relay","forms":["relay","relays","relaying","relayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳遞資訊或訊號","explanation":"指把資訊、影象或訊號從一個來源傳送到另一個人、地點或系統。它和接力的聯絡在於，資訊像接力棒一樣被交給下一個環節。","examples":[{"en":"The security cameras relay live images to the control room.","zh":"監控攝像頭把實時畫面傳送到控制室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please relay the manager's decision to the rest of the team.","zh":"請把經理的決定轉告給團隊其他成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4d451ec23463726f72c","word":"release","forms":["release"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce685af2ecc980c3","term":"release","forms":["release","releases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"釋放；放開","explanation":"指把原先被抓住、關著或卡住的人或東西放開，使其獲得自由或恢復活動。","examples":[{"en":"The release of the hostages was confirmed early this morning.","zh":"人質獲釋的訊息於今天一早得到確認。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The device has a safety release.","zh":"這個裝置有一個安全釋放裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/release","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-490e0e6de175fde6","term":"release","forms":["release","releases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"釋出；發行","explanation":"指把軟體、產品或其新版本正式提供給公眾或使用者使用。","examples":[{"en":"The company announced the release of a new version of the app.","zh":"公司宣佈將釋出這款應用的新版本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The software release fixed several security problems.","zh":"這次軟體釋出修復了幾個安全問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/release","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1eda60b8b7d7bb42","term":"release","forms":["release","releases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新推出的產品","explanation":"指最近被推出或提供購買、觀看、使用的東西，尤其是電影、音樂、書籍或產品。","examples":[{"en":"The store has all the latest movie releases.","zh":"這家店有所有最新發行的電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The publisher's latest release is a collection of essays.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/release","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88d6e1841cb8ec9a","term":"release","forms":["release","releases","releasing","released"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放開；鬆手","explanation":"指不再抓住、控制或容納某人或某物，讓它從手中或限制中出來。","examples":[{"en":"Release the handle slowly.","zh":"慢慢鬆開把手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She released her grip on the rope.","zh":"她鬆開了握住繩子的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/release","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-deb347f96f29c288","term":"release","forms":["release","releases","releasing","released"],"pos":"verb","zh":"釋出；發行","explanation":"指把新產品、軟體、電影或版本正式公開提供給使用者或公眾。","examples":[{"en":"The studio will release the film next month.","zh":"這家制片公司將於下個月發行這部電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They released an update for the app yesterday.","zh":"他們昨天釋出了這款應用的更新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/release","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b2fec8048697f16","term":"release","forms":["release","releases","releasing","released"],"pos":"verb","zh":"釋放；放出","explanation":"指解除對人的拘禁或限制，使其獲得自由，也可用於被關著的動物等。","examples":[{"en":"He was released from prison after two years.","zh":"他兩年後獲釋出獄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue team released the bird from the net.","zh":"救援隊把那隻鳥從網中解救出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/release","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7bf8d121771437b5e629","word":"relentless","forms":["relentless"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03964083c2d60a66","term":"relentless","forms":["relentless","more relentless","most relentless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴厲無情；毫不退讓","explanation":"形容態度、目光、壓力或行動等強硬得不肯緩和，讓人幾乎沒有喘息或退讓的餘地。這裡的重點是“不留情面地繼續施壓”，而不只是普通的堅持。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter faced relentless pressure to reveal her source.","zh":"那名記者面臨著毫不緩和的壓力，被逼著說出訊息來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was relentless in demanding an explanation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relentless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e067ea9d58dce336","term":"relentless","forms":["relentless","more relentless","most relentless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"持續不斷；堅持不懈","explanation":"形容某種努力、追求、行動或過程一直持續，幾乎不會停下來或放棄。它仍然保留“不會鬆手”的核心感覺，但這裡重點是持久和堅定，未必帶有負面意味。","examples":[{"en":"Her relentless pursuit of the truth eventually changed the investigation.","zh":"她對真相堅持不懈的追尋最終改變了這項調查的方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her relentless campaigning finally secured better safety standards.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relentless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4f3477880707e24b34a","word":"relevant","forms":["relevant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46d5282376ddda50","term":"relevant","forms":["relevant","more relevant","most relevant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相關的；切題的","explanation":"指資訊、事實、問題等能直接接上正在討論的主題，因此對理解或處理這個主題有幫助，而不是僅僅沾邊。","examples":[{"en":"The report includes only information relevant to the investigation.","zh":"這份報告只包含與調查有關的資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please focus on the points that are relevant to the question.","zh":"請集中討論與這個問題有關的要點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relevant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5aaf348fe9f9b0cd","term":"relevant","forms":["relevant","more relevant","most relevant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不過時的；仍有現實意義的","explanation":"把“接得上當前問題”的概念擴充套件到時間上：某個觀點、作品或資訊雖然不是新出現的，但今天仍然適用、值得考慮。","examples":[{"en":"Her advice is still relevant to the challenges we face today.","zh":"她的建議對我們今天面臨的挑戰仍然有現實意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The century-old play remains relevant to modern audiences.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relevant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20475dfea3a2deb72bb4","word":"reliable","forms":["reliable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8247df3a9ef2bff8","term":"reliable","forms":["reliable","more reliable","most reliable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得信賴的","explanation":"形容人或事物值得依靠，能夠按預期完成任務，或者提供可信的資訊。它可以形容朋友、證人、訊息來源、方法和裝置等。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is reliable, so I know she will finish the report on time.","zh":"瑪雅很可靠，所以我知道她會按時完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a reliable source before we publish the story.","zh":"我們在發表這篇報道前需要一個可靠的資訊來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reliable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c01a5a8cc8baac4","term":"reliable","forms":["reliable","more reliable","most reliable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傳輸可靠的","explanation":"在計算機、通訊和工程語境中，指系統能夠把資訊穩定地送到目的地；如果送不到，也會明確報告失敗，而不是讓結果含糊不清。","examples":[{"en":"The sensor needs a reliable connection to send data to the control room.","zh":"這個感測器需要可靠的連線，才能把資料傳送到控制室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The protocol provides reliable delivery through acknowledgments and retransmission.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reliable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bf923f90ab2c0c4ae8e","word":"reliance","forms":["reliance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eeb033abb566df87","term":"reliance","forms":["reliance","reliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信任；依靠","explanation":"指把判斷、希望或責任交給某人或某物，相信它能提供幫助或支援，重點在“依靠”這一行為或態度。","examples":[{"en":"Her reliance on her brother's advice made the decision easier.","zh":"她依靠哥哥的建議，因此更容易作出決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His reliance on online reviews makes choosing a restaurant difficult.","zh":"他太依賴網上的評價，反而很難選定一家餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e134a24a20cdf00f","term":"reliance","forms":["reliance","reliances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"依賴狀態","explanation":"指長期或結構性地需要某人、某物來維持運轉，強調“離不開”或“主要靠它”。它比單次的信任更突出持續的依賴關係。","examples":[{"en":"The company is reducing its reliance on imported materials.","zh":"這家公司正在減少對進口材料的依賴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reliance on imported fuel leaves the island vulnerable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reliance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92581b50c6036e0fb7a4","word":"reliant","forms":["reliant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19d58b11e28e76f5","term":"reliant","forms":["reliant","more reliant","most reliant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"依賴的；依靠的","explanation":"指某人、群體、機構或系統需要依靠某人或某事物才能維持生活、工作或正常運作，強調這種依靠關係，而不只是偶爾得到幫助。","examples":[{"en":"The village is heavily reliant on tourism for income.","zh":"這個村莊的收入嚴重依賴旅遊業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic remains reliant on donations to cover running costs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reliant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-942c59c72bf62ed73362","word":"relic","forms":["relic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecb14b2b18a3d134","term":"relic","forms":["relic","relics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"殘餘；遺留部分","explanation":"指某物消失、損失或衰變之後仍留下的部分。重點不在它是否有價值，而在它是過去事物留下的痕跡或殘片。","examples":[{"en":"The broken wall is a relic of the old city.","zh":"這面殘牆是那座舊城留下的遺蹟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a few relics of the ancient forest remain.","zh":"古森林只剩下少數遺留物了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49b3cd8eff75f29a","term":"relic","forms":["relic","relics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舊時代遺物","explanation":"指年代久遠、已經顯得過時，卻因為懷舊或紀念意義而儲存下來的物品。它通常讓人聯想到一個已經過去的時代。","examples":[{"en":"That fax machine is a relic of the pre-digital age.","zh":"那臺傳真機是數字化時代以前的舊時代遺物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The abandoned mill is a relic of industrial expansion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea6a344e27604dcb67a0","word":"relief","forms":["relief"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86c084c0e940455c","term":"relief","forms":["relief","reliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緩解；解脫","explanation":"指痛苦、壓力或擔憂被減輕，像有人把壓在身上的重擔抬走。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a wave of relief when the doctor called with good news.","zh":"醫生打來電話說是好訊息時，我頓時感到一陣如釋重負。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medicine brought relief from her back pain.","zh":"這種藥緩解了她的背痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10dec9f8a8031620","term":"relief","forms":["relief","reliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬慰的感覺","explanation":"指人在危險、擔憂或緊張消失後產生的輕鬆感，是“壓力被抬走”時的心理感受。","examples":[{"en":"A look of relief appeared on her face when her son came home.","zh":"兒子回家時，她臉上露出瞭如釋重負的神情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sighed with relief when the test came back clear.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bd2848a537638a9","term":"relief","forms":["relief","reliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"援助；救濟","explanation":"指在災難、貧困或緊急需要時提供的幫助，像把困難中的人托起來。","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers delivered relief supplies to the flooded villages.","zh":"志願者把救濟物資送到了被洪水淹沒的村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Emergency relief reached the flooded villages by boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1dd1d72b50993320","term":"relief","forms":["relief","reliefs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"浮雕技法","explanation":"指在平面背景上讓人物或圖案凸出來的雕塑方法，正是“從平面上抬起”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The figures are carved in relief on the stone wall.","zh":"這些人物形象以浮雕形式刻在石牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sculptor carved the figures in shallow relief.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be169a7e712b89de7b3d","word":"relieve","forms":["relieve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-858277d1372929d7","term":"relieve","forms":["relieve","relieves","relieving","relieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使焦慮減輕","explanation":"使某人不再那麼擔心、緊張或痛苦，好像把壓在心裡的重物抬開了。","examples":[{"en":"The good news relieved her anxiety.","zh":"這個好訊息減輕了她的焦慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was relieved to hear that everyone was safe.","zh":"聽說大家都安全，我鬆了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d08fb7967ffce6a1","term":"relieve","forms":["relieve","relieves","relieving","relieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緩解身體不適","explanation":"減輕人的身體疼痛或不適，像把身體上的負擔抬開。","examples":[{"en":"This cream should relieve the pain in your knee.","zh":"這種藥膏應該能緩解你膝蓋的疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A warm compress relieved the pain in his neck.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/relieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-139d14b61cae91c759a0","word":"religion","forms":["religion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1703b66504a62947","term":"religion","forms":["religion","religions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宗教信仰","explanation":"指相信神靈、超自然力量或其他精神性現實，並以相關觀念和實踐來理解世界、安排生活的總體信仰現象。","examples":[{"en":"Religion plays an important role in many people's lives.","zh":"宗教在許多人的生活中扮演著重要角色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course examines the relationship between religion and society.","zh":"這門課研究宗教與社會之間的關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/religion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5befa9285bdb989","term":"religion","forms":["religion","religions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體宗教","explanation":"指由一套信仰、教義、儀式和傳統組成的具體宗教體系，是“宗教”總體概念的一種實際形式。","examples":[{"en":"People from many different religions live in this city.","zh":"這座城市裡生活著信仰許多不同宗教的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a religion that matched her spiritual beliefs.","zh":"她選擇了一種與自己的精神信念相符的宗教。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/religion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f8b4464a99de3dc8c5c","word":"religious","forms":["religious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb249ba78ea87faa","term":"religious","forms":["religious","more religious","most religious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"宗教的；與宗教有關的","explanation":"指和宗教、信仰或宗教事務有關，而不一定說明某個人本人信教或虔誠。它可以修飾宗教問題、宗教儀式、宗教教育等事物。","examples":[{"en":"The school allows students to discuss religious questions in class.","zh":"這所學校允許學生在課堂上討論宗教問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a collection of religious art.","zh":"這家博物館收藏了一批宗教藝術品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/religious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16c2a66e956f04df","term":"religious","forms":["religious","more religious","most religious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"信教的；虔誠的","explanation":"形容一個人遵循宗教信仰或經常進行宗教實踐，重點在這個人的信仰和生活態度。它既可以表示一般的“信教”，也可以根據語境表示比較虔誠。","examples":[{"en":"She became more religious after a difficult period in her life.","zh":"經歷人生中的一段困難時期後，她變得更加虔誠了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My grandparents are religious and attend services every week.","zh":"我的祖父母信教，每週都參加禮拜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/religious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2de1346d707ccb43785","word":"reluctant","forms":["reluctant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e5497d145dfd282","term":"reluctant","forms":["reluctant","more reluctant","most reluctant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不情願的；不願意的","explanation":"指一個人心裡在抵抗某個行動，不太想做，但不一定完全拒絕。常常暗示對方經過勸說、考慮或必要時仍可能去做。","examples":[{"en":"She was reluctant to lend him the money.","zh":"她不太願意把錢借給他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was reluctant to admit that he had made a mistake.","zh":"他不太願意承認自己犯了錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reluctant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1f7124c563597b0c429","word":"rely","forms":["rely"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f61bc58cb03c082a","term":"rely","forms":["rely","relies","relying","relied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"依靠；信賴","explanation":"指把某件事交給某人或某物來支撐、幫助或完成，因此也含有相信對方可靠、可以託付的意思。它把“系在支點上”的畫面同時延伸到了實際依賴和信任。","examples":[{"en":"I rely on my calendar to remind me about appointments.","zh":"我靠日曆提醒自己不要忘記約會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can rely on Mia to keep a secret.","zh":"你可以信賴米婭，她一定會保守秘密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc2b6c264e75e681bcfe","word":"remain","forms":["remain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e119e86d6c3d6ab","term":"remain","forms":["remain","remains","remaining","remained","remainest","remainedst","remaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"留下； ಉಳ下","explanation":"指別人或其他部分離開、消失或被移除後，某人或某物還在原處；核心是“沒有隨之消失”。","examples":[{"en":"After everyone else left, Maya remained in the room.","zh":"其他人都離開後，瑪雅仍留在房間裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only three guests remained after midnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24893351e2cba2e5","term":"remain","forms":["remain","remains","remaining","remained","remainest","remainedst","remaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續保持；仍然是","explanation":"指位置、外形、數量或情況沒有改變，繼續處於原來的狀態；它把“留下”從地點擴充套件到了狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The museum remains open until six o’clock.","zh":"博物館一直開放到六點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the criticism, she remained calm.","zh":"儘管受到批評，她仍然保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fad7c57062b0877f515","word":"remainder","forms":["remainder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6bc96eadd6ce5ba3","term":"remainder","forms":["remainder","remainders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剩下的部分","explanation":"指整體中已經取走、使用或發生過一部分後留下的部分；可以是食物、錢、時間或其他事物。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the morning cleaning and used the remainder of the day to rest.","zh":"我們上午打掃衛生，把剩下的時間用來休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She packed the remainder of the food for tomorrow.","zh":"她把剩下的食物收起來，準備明天吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remainder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a443e507de6ddbc","term":"remainder","forms":["remainder","remainders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"除法餘數","explanation":"在整數除法中，除數儘可能多次減去被除數後仍留下的數。例如十七除以三得到五，還剩二，這個二就是 remainder。","examples":[{"en":"Twenty-three divided by five leaves a remainder of three.","zh":"二十三除以五，餘數是三。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write the remainder below the division sign.","zh":"把餘數寫在除號下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remainder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ffcd59e73280037cb72","word":"remark","forms":["remark"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3dee0382c3f63668","term":"remark","forms":["remark","remarks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說出的評論；提及","explanation":"指把自己注意到的事情用口頭或書面方式說出來，形成一條評論或提及。它可以只是中性的說明，並不一定帶有評價或批評。","examples":[{"en":"He made a remark about the weather before the meeting began.","zh":"會議開始前，他評論了一下天氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her remark that the room was too warm made everyone laugh.","zh":"她說房間太熱了，這句話讓大家都笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f05c803b65bc0fc","term":"remark","forms":["remark","remarks","remarking","remarked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說；指出","explanation":"指把自己的觀察用語言表達出來，尤其是明確說出某個事實或看法。它連線了“注意到”與“評論”兩個核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"He remarked that it was getting late.","zh":"他指出時間已經不早了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide remarked that the old bridge was still safe.","zh":"導遊說那座老橋仍然很安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fcd2e7dca02de24","term":"remark","forms":["remark","remarks","remarking","remarked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發表評論；評論","explanation":"指就某件事發表一兩句看法，也就是把注意到的內容說出來形成評論。它可以是中性的，也可以帶有輕微評價，但不必是正式評論文章。","examples":[{"en":"Several guests remarked on how quiet the hotel was.","zh":"幾位客人都評論說這家酒店很安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She remarked that the room seemed unusually cold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-113b67b03b8bd3ebb175","word":"remarkable","forms":["remarkable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef9390099cd58b07","term":"remarkable","forms":["remarkable","more remarkable","most remarkable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非凡的；值得注意的","explanation":"指某人的能力、成就或某件事突出到值得特別提起，通常含有讚賞和驚歎的意味。它把“值得評論”進一步發展成“很不一般、令人印象深刻”。","examples":[{"en":"She made remarkable progress in just three months.","zh":"她僅用了三個月就取得了驚人的進步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His remarkable ability to remember faces impressed everyone.","zh":"他非凡的面孔記憶能力給每個人都留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remarkable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08fbdf405acae1b7","term":"remarkable","forms":["remarkable","more remarkable","most remarkable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"罕見的；不尋常的","explanation":"指某事不同於通常情況，少見或異常，因此值得注意；這裡不一定是在稱讚，也可以只是客觀描述。","examples":[{"en":"The two paintings show a remarkable similarity.","zh":"這兩幅畫有著不尋常的相似之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden change in temperature was remarkable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remarkable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba605542cf569294fa14","word":"remedy","forms":["remedy"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d6aa89180b34672","term":"remedy","forms":["remedy","remedies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"補救辦法","explanation":"指能夠糾正問題、抵消不良影響或把事情拉回正常狀態的辦法。它可以是具體措施，也可以是較抽象的解決方案。","examples":[{"en":"Better communication may be the best remedy for this problem.","zh":"更好的溝通可能是解決這個問題的最佳辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is no easy remedy for years of neglect.","zh":"多年的疏忽沒有簡單的補救辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e2a4db243a96b5d","term":"remedy","forms":["remedy","remedies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥物；治療方法","explanation":"指用來緩解或治癒疾病、疼痛或其他身體不適的藥物、外用物或治療方法。這是“把身體治好”的具體補救手段。","examples":[{"en":"Ginger tea is a popular home remedy for a sore throat.","zh":"薑茶是緩解喉嚨痛的一種常見家庭療法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pharmacist recommended a remedy for the cough.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb8a1ff4ef6c0004","term":"remedy","forms":["remedy","remedies","remedying","remedied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"補救；糾正","explanation":"指採取行動消除缺陷、糾正錯誤或改善不良情況，也就是把出問題的地方重新處理好。","examples":[{"en":"The company acted quickly to remedy the safety problem.","zh":"公司迅速採取行動，補救這一安全問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New training could remedy the team's lack of experience.","zh":"新的培訓可以彌補團隊經驗不足的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35379d9c009e290d702b","word":"remember","forms":["remember"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7920b364c128781","term":"remember","forms":["remember","remembers","remembering","remembered","rememberest","rememberedst","remembereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想起；記得","explanation":"指從記憶中重新想起某人、某事或某個場景，腦海裡重新出現相關印象。","examples":[{"en":"I suddenly remembered where I had left my keys.","zh":"我突然想起把鑰匙落在哪裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you remember our first day at school?","zh":"你還記得我們上學的第一天嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remember","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89d4257a507f33c3","term":"remember","forms":["remember","remembers","remembering","remembered","rememberest","rememberedst","remembereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"牢記；放在心上","explanation":"指把某個事實、建議、約定或他人的話持續放在心裡，不要忽略它。","examples":[{"en":"Remember that everyone makes mistakes.","zh":"記住，每個人都會犯錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Remember what I told you about checking the address.","zh":"記住我告訴過你的，要核對地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remember","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7d25e754e9f1813","term":"remember","forms":["remember","remembers","remembering","remembered","rememberest","rememberedst","remembereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"記得去做","explanation":"指沒有忘記完成某個需要做的行動，通常用於提醒自己或別人按時行動。","examples":[{"en":"Please remember to lock the door when you leave.","zh":"你離開時請記得鎖門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Remember to bring your passport.","zh":"記得帶護照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remember","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-efafcd967c5eb1641bb2","word":"remind","forms":["remind"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77abe826c27ce3f8","term":"remind","forms":["remind","reminds","reminding","reminded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使想起；提醒","explanation":"把某人或某件事重新帶回另一個人的腦海中：可以是某個氣味使人想起過去，也可以是主動提醒對方注意某事或完成某個行動。","examples":[{"en":"The smell of rain reminds me of my childhood.","zh":"雨水的氣味讓我想起童年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please remind me to call the dentist tomorrow.","zh":"請提醒我明天給牙醫打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ce7011ab48f26c2e69f","word":"reminder","forms":["reminder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ef50bb0c2aa33a1","term":"reminder","forms":["reminder","reminders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提醒；提示","explanation":"指幫助人想起某件事，或提醒人去做某件事的人、物或資訊，例如便條、鬧鐘通知和訊息。它的核心不是“記憶”本身，而是把你拉回到應該記住或完成的事情上。","examples":[{"en":"I set a reminder to call my mother tomorrow.","zh":"我設定了一個提醒，明天給媽媽打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The photo on my desk is a reminder of our trip.","zh":"我桌上的照片讓人想起我們那次旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reminder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0f95c532ccf39c2","term":"reminder","forms":["reminder","reminders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"付款提醒；催款通知","explanation":"指提醒收件人支付尚未結清的賬單或款項的通知。它仍然是把人拉回某件待辦事項，只是這裡的待辦事項變成了付款。","examples":[{"en":"We sent a payment reminder because the invoice was overdue.","zh":"由於發票已經逾期，我們發了一份付款提醒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The utility company sent a payment reminder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reminder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-113e3bb5f968a3f1c582","word":"reminiscent","forms":["reminiscent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d989466fc7227927","term":"reminiscent","forms":["reminiscent","more reminiscent","most reminiscent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"帶有過去的影子","explanation":"形容眼前的事物在氣氛、形式或場景上使人聯想到較早的事件、時代或經歷，重點是它帶有過去的特徵。","examples":[{"en":"The town's narrow streets are reminiscent of an older era.","zh":"這座小鎮狹窄的街道帶有舊時代的氣息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The melody is reminiscent of old folk songs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reminiscent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1895c75f526d740c","term":"reminiscent","forms":["reminiscent","more reminiscent","most reminiscent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"使人想起","explanation":"形容某個景象、聲音、物品或作品會把某段記憶帶到腦海中，也就是讓人聯想到某人、某事或某種風格。","examples":[{"en":"The melody is reminiscent of the songs my grandmother used to sing.","zh":"這段旋律讓人想起祖母以前常唱的歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scent was reminiscent of her grandmother's garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reminiscent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b71199ebd070b36beab7","word":"remote","forms":["remote"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f04902a8ca6b84dc","term":"remote","forms":["remote","more remote","remoter","most remote","remotest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遙遠的；遠端的","explanation":"表示在空間上離得遠，或透過通訊裝置在遠處進行控制、操作；重點是人與物件不在同一地點。","examples":[{"en":"A remote operator can control the drone from a laptop.","zh":"遠端操作員可以用膝上型電腦控制無人機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They communicate with the remote weather station by satellite.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e57388d1cf4790d521cd","word":"removal","forms":["removal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ec8c3d63042542d","term":"removal","forms":["removal","removals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"移除；清除","explanation":"指把某物或某人從原來的位置、範圍或狀態中移開，也可以指這種行為或已經發生的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The removal of the old bridge will begin next week.","zh":"舊橋的拆除工作將於下週開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cream is effective for the removal of stains.","zh":"這種乳霜去除汙漬很有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/removal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33f6c77f96bdfe3e","term":"removal","forms":["removal","removals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搬遷；遷址","explanation":"指商店、公司等從原來的地點搬到另一個地點，重點是經營地點的改變，而不是單純把一件物品拿走。","examples":[{"en":"The removal of the business to a larger building created several new jobs.","zh":"這家企業搬到一棟更大的樓後，創造了幾個新工作崗位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An office removal requires careful labeling of every box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/removal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e5608ab610017afe6c1","word":"remove","forms":["remove"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-63520e9b0aaf49e3","term":"remove","forms":["remove","removes","removing","removed","removest","removedst","removeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刪除","explanation":"把文字、檔案、程式或其他內容從原來的位置或系統中刪去，使它不再保留。","examples":[{"en":"Please remove my name from the mailing list.","zh":"請把我的名字從郵件列表中刪掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can remove the app if you no longer use it.","zh":"如果你不再使用這個應用，可以把它解除安裝掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf7d41f80b384937","term":"remove","forms":["remove","removes","removing","removed","removest","removedst","removeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拿走；移開","explanation":"把人或物從一個地方移到別處，尤其強調從原處拿走；這是 remove 最基本的“移開”概念。","examples":[{"en":"Please remove the wet clothes from the floor.","zh":"請把溼衣服從地板上拿走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse carefully removed the bandage.","zh":"護士小心地取下了繃帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/remove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-887270d0cbc560af35f1","word":"render","forms":["render"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc7a8aab5142bdd8","term":"render","forms":["render","renders","rendering","rendered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變成某種狀態","explanation":"指使某人或某物變得處於某種狀態，強調結果被造成或呈現出來。可以把它看作“把物件變成某個樣子”。","examples":[{"en":"The loud noise rendered her unable to concentrate.","zh":"巨大的噪聲使她無法集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The damage rendered the vehicle unsafe to drive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/render","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb7e363af8bbfd1b","term":"render","forms":["render","renders","rendering","rendered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表達；演繹","explanation":"指用語言、音樂、繪畫或其他方式把某種意義、作品或感受呈現出來。它不只是機械地“做”，而是把內容轉成可理解的表現。","examples":[{"en":"The actor rendered the character with great warmth.","zh":"這位演員把這個角色演繹得十分溫暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rendered the old folk tune in a slow, mournful style.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/render","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe105ab57cc70b27","term":"render","forms":["render","renders","rendering","rendered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"渲染；生成影象","explanation":"指把模型、場景或資料處理成螢幕或其他媒介上可顯示的影象。它正是“把內部模型呈現出來”的技術化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The software renders the scene in real time.","zh":"這款軟體會實時渲染這個場景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The computer is rendering the final animation.","zh":"電腦正在渲染最終動畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/render","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a36a2ce1800626b7cf47","word":"renew","forms":["renew"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18b183ecf44e59e9","term":"renew","forms":["renew","renews","renewing","renewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使恢復如新","explanation":"把已經舊了、受損了或失去活力的東西恢復到較新的狀態，就像把舊物重新擦亮或修好。","examples":[{"en":"A short break renewed her energy.","zh":"短暫的休息使她恢復了精力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment helped renew the damaged soil.","zh":"這種處理有助於恢復受損土壤的活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8eb0b0a9da180500","term":"renew","forms":["renew","renews","renewing","renewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"補充；更換","explanation":"把已經用完、減少或失效的供應重新補上，也可以更換已經損壞的東西，讓原有供應繼續維持。","examples":[{"en":"The clinic renewed its supply of emergency medicine.","zh":"這家診所補充了急救藥品的供應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to renew the filters before winter.","zh":"我們需要在冬天前更換濾芯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-343842d7480519bf","term":"renew","forms":["renew","renews","renewing","renewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重新開始","explanation":"讓已經中斷、停止或暫緩的事情再次進行，因此可以理解為把舊的行動重新啟動。","examples":[{"en":"The police renewed their investigation after finding new evidence.","zh":"警方發現新證據後重新展開了調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two sides renewed negotiations in April.","zh":"雙方在四月重新開始了談判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2996395f154e8ae95e88","word":"renowned","forms":["renowned"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5908300959258675","term":"renowned","forms":["renowned","more renowned","most renowned"],"pos":"adj","zh":"著名且備受讚譽","explanation":"指某人、某地或某事物非常有名，而且因為出色的成就、品質或聲譽而受到廣泛尊敬和讚揚。","examples":[{"en":"The city is renowned for its beautiful gardens and historic buildings.","zh":"這座城市以美麗的花園和歷史悠久的建築而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied under a renowned scientist.","zh":"她曾師從一位著名科學家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renowned","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-0e9fd1596c4b1dfca8dd","word":"rent","forms":["rent"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6e67803a918bd69","term":"rent","forms":["rent","rents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"租金；房租","explanation":"指租客為了暫時使用房屋或其他場所，按周、按月等定期支付的錢。最常見的是房租，但也可以泛指租用房產所需的費用。","examples":[{"en":"We need to pay the rent by the first day of each month.","zh":"我們需要在每月第一天之前交房租。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rent for this small apartment is surprisingly high.","zh":"這套小公寓的房租高得出人意料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d0a41155459518d","term":"rent","forms":["rent","rents","renting","rented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"租用；租入","explanation":"指向別人付錢，暫時取得房屋、場所或其他物品的使用權。它和名詞“租金”屬於同一條核心詞義線。","examples":[{"en":"They rented a house from a local family for the summer.","zh":"他們向當地一家人租了一棟房子住整個夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can we rent bicycles near the beach?","zh":"我們可以在海灘附近租腳踏車嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0c146e3d9648bd10bf0","word":"rental","forms":["rental"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5d247b2a042a548","term":"rental","forms":["rental","rentals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"租來的東西","explanation":"指透過付費暫時使用的物品，例如租來的汽車、電影或裝置；它強調的是“這不是自己的，而是租來的”。","examples":[{"en":"We picked up the rental at the airport before driving to the coast.","zh":"我們在機場取了租來的車，然後開車去了海邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our rental has a small kitchen and two bedrooms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0e9b0369c4f5dce","term":"rental","forms":["rental","rentals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"租金；租賃費用","explanation":"指為了暫時使用某物而支付的錢，也就是租賃這項服務的費用。","examples":[{"en":"The museum paid a small rental for the audio equipment.","zh":"博物館為這些音訊裝置支付了一小筆租賃費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Weekly rental includes insurance and roadside assistance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1a14ff4aab4f1d3efbe","word":"repair","forms":["repair"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7aa4688c664dd111","term":"repair","forms":["repair","repairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"修理行為","explanation":"repair 可以指把損壞的東西修好的整個過程，而不是某個具體零件或工具。","examples":[{"en":"The old bridge is closed for repair.","zh":"這座舊橋因維修而關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I took my laptop in for repair yesterday.","zh":"我昨天把膝上型電腦送去維修了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f292dad3a2dc3ba","term":"repair","forms":["repair","repairs","repairing","repaired","repairest","repairedst","repaireth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修理；修復","explanation":"repair 作動詞時，就是把壞掉或受損的東西恢復到可以正常使用或較好狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic repaired the brakes before the trip.","zh":"修理工在出發前修好了剎車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to repair the roof before winter.","zh":"我們需要在冬天前修好屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66f49a3a27a7e385a95b","word":"repay","forms":["repay"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7b57c3924a85367","term":"repay","forms":["repay","repays","repaying","repaid"],"pos":"verb","zh":"償還；還清","explanation":"把借來的錢、欠下的債或應付的款項還回去。它可以強調一次還清，也可以表示持續償還的過程。","examples":[{"en":"She repaid the bank loan two years earlier than expected.","zh":"她比預期提前兩年還清了銀行貸款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I promised to repay him as soon as I received my salary.","zh":"我答應一領到工資就把錢還給他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-180fe2cde40ac4d4","term":"repay","forms":["repay","repays","repaying","repaid"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使努力得到回報","explanation":"某項努力、投資或行動最終產生了值得付出的成果，因此說它“回報了”先前的投入。這裡不一定涉及真正的金錢償還。","examples":[{"en":"The extra training repaid her effort when she won the final race.","zh":"額外的訓練在她贏得決賽時回報了她付出的努力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spectacular view repaid the difficult climb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25e2b6b106523880e277","word":"repeat","forms":["repeat"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2504da806dd44e6","term":"repeat","forms":["repeat","repeats","repeating","repeated","repeatest","repeatedst","repeateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重複做；重複說","explanation":"指把同一個動作、步驟、詞語或想法再做或再說一次，也可以連續重複多次。","examples":[{"en":"The scientists repeated the experiment to confirm the result.","zh":"科學家重複了這項實驗，以確認結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you repeat the last sentence, please?","zh":"請你把最後一句再說一遍，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repeat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f51e781bda5366e4","term":"repeat","forms":["repeat","repeats","repeating","repeated","repeatest","repeatedst","repeateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"再次發生","explanation":"指某件事重新發生，常帶有“同樣的情況又出現了”的意味；也常用反身形式表示某事自行重現。","examples":[{"en":"History may repeat itself if we ignore the warning signs.","zh":"如果我們忽視警告訊號，歷史可能會重演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The same mistake repeated itself several times.","zh":"同樣的錯誤重複出現了好幾次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repeat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aee9ef33b2f619607249","word":"repetition","forms":["repetition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7978073677135ace","term":"repetition","forms":["repetition","repetitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重複；反覆","explanation":"指同一件事、動作、聲音或情況再次發生或被再次做出，重點是“同樣的東西又來了一遍”。","examples":[{"en":"The repetition of the same mistake delayed the project.","zh":"同一個錯誤一再出現，拖慢了專案進度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The song becomes more powerful with each repetition.","zh":"這首歌每重複一遍，感染力就更強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repetition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-273938c0f9d18671","term":"repetition","forms":["repetition","repetitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"（鍛鍊中的）一次重複動作","explanation":"在力量訓練等鍛鍊中，指按照規定完成一次動作；連續若干次 repetition 組成一組訓練。","examples":[{"en":"Do three repetitions of each exercise before taking a break.","zh":"每項練習做三次後再休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Complete ten repetitions before changing to the other arm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/repetition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-149d442019627e8cebf0","word":"replace(ment)","forms":["replace","replacement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69df9ec69c72b2fd","term":"replace","forms":["replace","replaces","replacing","replaced","replacest","replacedst","replaceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放回原處","explanation":"指把用過或拿走的東西重新放回原來的位置、狀態或應在的地方，和“把東西歸位”的畫面相連。","examples":[{"en":"Please replace the books on the shelf when you are finished.","zh":"用完後請把書放回書架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She replaced the lid on the jar before putting it away.","zh":"她把蓋子重新蓋回罐子上，然後把罐子收好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/replace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7cbdc80fb1bdb7e","term":"replace","forms":["replace","replaces","replacing","replaced","replacest","replacedst","replaceth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"替換；換成","explanation":"指用新的或等價的東西換掉原來的東西，是“把舊東西的位置讓給新東西”。","examples":[{"en":"We replaced the broken printer with a faster model.","zh":"我們用一臺速度更快的型號替換了那臺壞掉的印表機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is time to replace these worn-out shoes.","zh":"該換掉這雙磨舊的鞋了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/replace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-877d126856a853f9","term":"replacement","forms":["replacement","replacements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"替代者；替代物","explanation":"指填補原來位置的人或物，也就是代替另一個人或物發揮作用的物件。它可以指臨時頂替的人，也可以指買來代替舊物的新物品。","examples":[{"en":"We need a replacement for the broken printer.","zh":"我們需要一臺替換那臺壞印表機的新印表機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her replacement will start work next Monday.","zh":"她的替代者下週一開始工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/replacement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61c70c22dc300dfe","term":"replacement","forms":["replacement","replacements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"替換；更換","explanation":"指把舊的、壞的或不再合適的東西拿走，再放入新的或合適的東西這一過程。重點不在替代者本身，而在“重新填上這個位置”的行動。","examples":[{"en":"The replacement of the roof will take two weeks.","zh":"更換屋頂需要兩週時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Replacement of the worn cable restored normal service.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/replacement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5782b18687e6cf8a482f","word":"reply","forms":["reply"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad144651ebea462d","term":"reply","forms":["reply","replies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"回應；答覆","explanation":"指對別人說的話、提出的問題或發來的資訊作出的口頭或書面回應。它就像把對方投來的話接住，再投回去。","examples":[{"en":"I’m still waiting for a reply to my message.","zh":"我還在等對方回覆我的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her reply was short but polite.","zh":"她的答覆很簡短，但很有禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fefa13fa0c3c6e31","term":"reply","forms":["reply","replies","replying","replied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"回答；回覆","explanation":"指對問題、請求、指責、批評或郵件作出口頭或書面回應。它就是把收到的資訊接住，再把自己的話投回去。","examples":[{"en":"Please reply to my letter by Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前回復我的信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She replied that she was too busy.","zh":"她回答說自己太忙了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-845e91831319e89c4d65","word":"report","forms":["report"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c78eb82b2ac17729","term":"report","forms":["report","reports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報告；報道","explanation":"指對某件事、某個情況或一段事件作出的說明，可以是正式檔案，也可以是新聞報道或口頭敘述。它的共同點是把已經瞭解的資訊整理後傳給別人。","examples":[{"en":"The company released a report on its plans for the next year.","zh":"這家公司釋出了一份關於明年計劃的報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The evening news included a report on the storm.","zh":"晚間新聞播出了一則關於這場暴風雨的報道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0609781f0592f588","term":"report","forms":["report","reports","reporting","reported","reportest","reportedst","reporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敘述；報道","explanation":"指把發生過的事情、觀察到的情況或事件細節講述或寫出來。它就像把訊息帶回來，再傳給聽眾、讀者或有關人員。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers reported that the treatment had improved patients' sleep.","zh":"研究人員報告說，這種治療改善了患者的睡眠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The journalist reported on the election from the capital.","zh":"這名記者從首都報道了這次選舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5acf25d493590770","term":"report","forms":["report","reports","reporting","reported","reportest","reportedst","reporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉述；傳達","explanation":"指把自己聽到的訊息、別人說的話或某項資訊再傳給第三方，重點在於把訊息繼續傳遞下去。","examples":[{"en":"Several passengers reported the problem to the station staff.","zh":"幾名乘客把這個問題告訴了車站工作人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness reported what she had heard upstairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d111712985f42317","term":"report","forms":["report","reports","reporting","reported","reportest","reportedst","reporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"報告；舉報","explanation":"指把事故、犯罪、損失、可疑行為等正式告知有關人員或機構，使其能夠處理。它仍然保留“把訊息傳回權威部門”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please report any suspicious activity to the security desk.","zh":"如發現任何可疑活動，請向保安臺報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He reported the stolen bicycle to the police.","zh":"他向警方報告了腳踏車被盜的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc504cc53b4c5279","term":"report","forms":["report","reports","reporting","reported","reportest","reportedst","reporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向……彙報；受……領導","explanation":"指在組織層級中向某人負責、接受其指示，並定期把工作進展傳達給對方。這裡的“傳回資訊”發展成了固定的上下級關係。","examples":[{"en":"I report directly to the head of the department.","zh":"我直接向部門主管彙報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineers report to the project manager.","zh":"這些工程師受專案經理領導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41d6d5322a9b546a16bd","word":"reporter","forms":["reporter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c19ea872b799a021","term":"reporter","forms":["reporter","reporters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報告資訊的人或裝置","explanation":"這是最寬的概念：凡是負責把某種情況、資料或事件報出來的人，甚至自動傳送資訊的程式或裝置，都可以這樣稱呼。新聞記者只是這個大概念中最常見的一類。","examples":[{"en":"The error reporter sends a message whenever the program stops working.","zh":"程式每次停止執行時，錯誤報告器都會傳送一條訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The alarm system records messages from each fault reporter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reporter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9611134ab2d8ad4d","term":"reporter","forms":["reporter","reporters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新聞記者","explanation":"指調查、編輯並向報紙、廣播或電視報道新聞的人，是日常英語中最常見的意思。這個人不只是轉述訊息，也可能負責採訪和核實事實。","examples":[{"en":"A reporter for the local newspaper interviewed the mayor after the meeting.","zh":"當地報紙的一名記者在會議結束後採訪了市長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The television reporter was covering the storm from the coast.","zh":"那名電視記者正在海岸報道這場暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reporter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8cfc12e7f78033dc69ab","word":"represent","forms":["represent"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42a78dcf0d57c928","term":"represent","forms":["represent","represents","representing","represented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"呈現；代替表示","explanation":"讓某個東西代替另一個東西出現在人們面前，或用它來呈現另一個東西的形象、性質或意義。這裡包含 represent 最基本的“站到另一個東西的位置上”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"This model represents the city as it looked a hundred years ago.","zh":"這個模型呈現了這座城市一百年前的樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm voice represented the confidence of the whole team.","zh":"她平靜的聲音體現了整個團隊的自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/represent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a0eece86abdb9f7","term":"represent","forms":["represent","represents","representing","represented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"描繪；畫出","explanation":"用圖畫、照片、模型或其他視覺形式把某個物件呈現出來，讓人能夠看見它的樣子。","examples":[{"en":"The painting represents a quiet village beside a river.","zh":"這幅畫描繪了河邊一個安靜的村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The map represents the hiking trail in great detail.","zh":"這張地圖非常詳細地描繪了徒步路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/represent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67fe14dc4d8f639e","term":"represent","forms":["represent","represents","representing","represented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"代表；代行","explanation":"站在某人的位置上參加活動、處理事務或行使對方的權利，替對方說話或行動。","examples":[{"en":"Her lawyer represented her at the hearing.","zh":"她的律師在聽證會上代表她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I cannot attend, so my colleague will represent me.","zh":"我無法出席，所以我的同事會代表我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/represent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8ad1f5f2bb3f4c78bf2","word":"representation","forms":["representation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-176f71099293a244","term":"representation","forms":["representation","representations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表物；呈現","explanation":"指代替另一個事物、把它呈現出來的東西或形象。它可以是雕像、圖畫、文字說明等，不一定是真實物件本身。","examples":[{"en":"The statue is a representation of the town's founder.","zh":"這座雕像是該鎮創始人的一種形象呈現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This map is a useful representation of the river system.","zh":"這張地圖很好地呈現了河流系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/representation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf483caf1caf2126","term":"representation","forms":["representation","representations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表或呈現的行為","explanation":"指代表某人、某組織或某事物並把它呈現給他人的行為；重點在“怎樣代表、怎樣呈現”這一過程。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is reviewing its representation of local history.","zh":"這家博物館正在審視自己呈現地方歷史的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company thanked her for her representation at the conference.","zh":"公司感謝她在會議上代表公司出席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/representation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-482a37dd98d937458a3d","word":"representative","forms":["representative"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64c0708ef7c432f1","term":"representative","forms":["representative","more representative","most representative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有代表性的；典型的","explanation":"指一個人、事物或樣本具有整體群體的典型特點，因此可以用來反映更大的範圍。它強調“這個個體能讓人看出整體大致是什麼樣”。","examples":[{"en":"This survey included a representative sample of local residents.","zh":"這項調查包含了一個能代表當地居民整體情況的樣本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting is representative of her early style.","zh":"這幅畫體現了她早期作品的典型風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/representative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ade391dcd96308b","term":"representative","forms":["representative","representatives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表；代理人","explanation":"指受一個團體、組織或其他人委託，站出來表達意見、參加會議或處理事務的人。他本人不是整個團體，但在特定場合代表團體行動。","examples":[{"en":"A representative of the workers spoke at the meeting.","zh":"一名工人代表在會上發了言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please contact our customer service representative.","zh":"請聯絡本公司的客戶服務代表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/representative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-469fb1948602cdc99fe5","word":"reproduce","forms":["reproduce"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b3b99a0a92b7ced","term":"reproduce","forms":["reproduce","reproduces","reproducing","reproduced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"複製影象或內容","explanation":"把已有的影象、檔案、文字或其他內容再製作一份，使其成為可用的副本，就是 reproduce。","examples":[{"en":"The museum reproduced the painting for its exhibition catalogue.","zh":"博物館為展覽圖錄複製了這幅畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This printer can reproduce fine details very accurately.","zh":"這臺印表機能非常準確地複製細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reproduce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14a09d6b1cf4de7b","term":"reproduce","forms":["reproduce","reproduces","reproducing","reproduced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繁殖後代","explanation":"使生物產生新的後代，或生物本身繁殖產生後代，都可以用 reproduce；這個過程可以是有性繁殖，也可以是無性繁殖。","examples":[{"en":"Some plants reproduce without producing seeds.","zh":"有些植物不產生種子也能繁殖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers bred the fish so they could reproduce in captivity.","zh":"研究人員培育這些魚，使它們能夠在圈養環境中繁殖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reproduce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a64551c19303783af0f","word":"reptile","forms":["reptile"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f227086f96adfb6","term":"reptile","forms":["reptile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"爬行的；匍匐的","explanation":"指身體貼近地面爬行，或靠短小的腿緩慢移動，和 reptile 作為“爬行動物”的核心形象直接相關。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a reptile creature from the ancient sea.","zh":"博物館展出了一種來自遠古海洋的爬行生物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reptile movement was slow but steady.","zh":"這種爬行式移動緩慢卻很穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reptile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9861b0b785a2214f","term":"reptile","forms":["reptile","reptiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爬行動物","explanation":"指通常體溫隨環境變化、皮膚有鱗片的脊椎動物，如蛇、蜥蜴、龜和鱷魚等；這是現代英語中最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A snake is a reptile, not an insect.","zh":"蛇是爬行動物，不是昆蟲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children saw several reptiles at the zoo.","zh":"孩子們在動物園看到了幾種爬行動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reptile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1cd94c4a9c0fa368dd2","word":"republic","forms":["republic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a22d47308952fdfc","term":"republic","forms":["republic","republics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共和國","explanation":"指沒有君主或皇帝、國家主權屬於人民或其代表的國家。核心畫面是國家屬於公眾，而不是某個王室的私人領地。","examples":[{"en":"The United States is a republic, while Norway is a constitutional monarchy.","zh":"美國是共和國，而挪威是君主立憲制國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new constitution established a republic.","zh":"新憲法建立了一個共和國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/republic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b24d904dc4043aec","term":"republic","forms":["republic","republics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"俄羅斯的共和國級行政區","explanation":"指俄羅斯聯邦的一個行政區型別，通常具有特定民族或地區身份；這裡是行政區名稱中的專門用法。","examples":[{"en":"The Republic of Udmurtia lies west of Perm Krai.","zh":"烏德穆爾特共和國位於彼爾姆邊疆區以西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Republic of Tatarstan lies within the Russian Federation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/republic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c4a1e6f3639a098e6806","word":"republican","forms":["republican"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84dcc97560d8d8ca","term":"republican","forms":["republican","more republican","most republican"],"pos":"adj","zh":"支援共和制的","explanation":"指主張以共和制作為政府形式，或擁護共和主義的。它強調國家不由世襲君主統治，而以共和國的政治理念為基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The movement called for a republican form of government.","zh":"這個運動要求建立共和制政府。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her republican views were shaped by the history of the revolution.","zh":"革命史塑造了她的共和主義觀點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/republican","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51e97fb5255fc8ea","term":"republican","forms":["republican","more Republican","most Republican"],"pos":"adj","zh":"共和黨的","explanation":"在美國語境中，通常指屬於或涉及美國共和黨的。這裡是政黨專名義，常與 Democratic 相對。","examples":[{"en":"The Republican candidate won the Senate election.","zh":"共和黨候選人贏得了參議院選舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Republican lawmakers opposed the proposal.","zh":"共和黨議員反對這項提案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/republican","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55edcfb7b308ddd7","term":"republican","forms":["republican","republicans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共和主義者","explanation":"指支援共和制、主張建立或維護共和國的人。這個名詞義與形容詞的制度和政治主張義直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"As a republican, she opposed the restoration of the monarchy.","zh":"作為一名共和主義者，她反對恢復君主制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The republicans organized a campaign for constitutional reform.","zh":"共和主義者組織了一場推動憲法改革的運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/republican","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7ec505a32193785","term":"republican","forms":["republican","Republicans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共和黨人","explanation":"在美國語境中，指美國共和黨的成員或支持者。它是美國兩大主要政黨之一的專名身份，不是泛指所有支援共和國的人。","examples":[{"en":"She has voted Republican in every national election.","zh":"她在每次全國選舉中都投票支援共和黨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several Republicans joined the debate.","zh":"幾名共和黨人參加了辯論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/republican","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-556ec7485db6ec259605","word":"reputation","forms":["reputation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88bf56ae14e148e3","term":"reputation","forms":["reputation","reputations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名聲；聲譽","explanation":"指一個人、團體或事物在別人心中通常被怎樣認識和評價；這種印象可能是正面的，也可能是負面的。它既可以來自真實表現，也可以來自長期流傳的看法。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant has a reputation for generous portions.","zh":"這家餐館以分量足而聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her reputation suffered after the mistake.","zh":"那次錯誤之後，她的聲譽受到了損害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reputation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f58b9145b24d108d7ac","word":"request","forms":["request"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1505d12bd2714bc0","term":"request","forms":["request","requests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"請求；要求","explanation":"指提出某種要求或請別人滿足某種需要的行為。它可以是禮貌請求，也可以是正式要求，重點在於“有人向別人提出要某物或要對方做某事”。","examples":[{"en":"The manager approved my request for a day off.","zh":"經理批准了我請一天假的請求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At her request, we kept the meeting short.","zh":"應她的要求，我們把會議開得很短。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/request","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2be3d06e39820fd0","term":"request","forms":["request","requests","requesting","requested","requestest","requestedst","requesteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"請求某物","explanation":"表示向某人或某機構提出要求，希望得到某物、服務或幫助。它就是“把請求遞出去”的動作，是 request 最核心的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The officer requested additional information from the witness.","zh":"那名官員向證人請求補充資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Passengers may request a refund within seven days.","zh":"乘客可以在七天內申請退款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/request","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ee2b72bd47709035b6d","word":"require(ment)","forms":["require","requirement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71e31cde8de8a618","term":"require","forms":["require","requires","requiring","required"],"pos":"verb","zh":"需要；以……為必要條件","explanation":"表示某件事要順利完成，天然需要某種資源、條件或處理方式；重點不在誰發出命令，而在這個條件本身不可缺少。","examples":[{"en":"This repair will require special tools.","zh":"這項維修需要專用工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment may require several weeks of rest.","zh":"這種治療可能需要休息幾周。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/require","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-753c84c9d7d4857b","term":"require","forms":["require","requires","requiring","required"],"pos":"verb","zh":"要求某人做某事","explanation":"表示把某項必須完成的行動交給某人，常用於法律、規定、工作職責等場合；核心仍是“設下一道必須滿足的門檻”。","examples":[{"en":"The law requires drivers to wear seat belts.","zh":"法律要求司機系安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New employees are required to complete this course.","zh":"新員工必須完成這門課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/require","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c051ad1b9d60176","term":"requirement","forms":["requirement","requirements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"必須滿足的條件","explanation":"它指為了進入、完成或獲准做某事而必須滿足的條件，也可以指某項工作、規則或任務所規定的必要條件；它的核心就是一道不能繞過的門檻。","examples":[{"en":"A driving test is a requirement for getting a license.","zh":"透過駕駛考試是取得駕照的必要條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check that you meet all the entry requirements.","zh":"請確認你符合所有入學條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/requirement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-347bebc9c235d14a","term":"requirement","forms":["requirement","requirements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提出的要求","explanation":"它也可以指某人明確提出、希望對方滿足的要求；此時重點不是抽象規則，而是提出要求的一方和他想要的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The customer's only requirement was a quiet room with a view.","zh":"這位顧客唯一的要求是要一間安靜且能看見景色的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The landlord added a requirement for written permission.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/requirement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-824ef7874151e9c8c4f7","word":"rescue","forms":["rescue"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c4332557323fef0","term":"rescue","forms":["rescue","rescues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"救援；營救","explanation":"指把人或動物從危險、災難或困境中救出來的行動，也可泛指救援本身。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue took several hours because the hikers were trapped by the storm.","zh":"這次救援花了幾個小時，因為徒步者被暴風雨困住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue of the child brought the whole neighborhood together.","zh":"孩子獲救這件事讓整個社群團結了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rescue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b15e770b4c545b91","term":"rescue","forms":["rescue","rescues","rescuing","rescued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"營救；救出","explanation":"指把人或動物從危險、暴力、災難或其他嚴重威脅中救出來，是 rescue 最核心的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Firefighters rescued two children from the burning house.","zh":"消防員把兩個孩子從著火的房子裡救了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lifeguard rescued the swimmer before he disappeared beneath the waves.","zh":"救生員在那名游泳者沉入海浪之前把他救了上來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rescue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66f62d1807d3821a3865","word":"research","forms":["research"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0b2979ad6e81795","term":"research","forms":["research","researches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"研究；調查","explanation":"指為了解事實、原理或實際應用而進行的持續、認真查詢和分析；重點不只是找資料，還包括核實和形成較可靠的結論。","examples":[{"en":"The team is conducting research into the effects of air pollution.","zh":"這個團隊正在研究空氣汙染的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"More research is needed before we can recommend the treatment.","zh":"在我們推薦這種治療方法之前，還需要進行更多研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/research","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-518c838e733a963c","term":"research","forms":["research","researches","researching","researched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"研究；仔細調查","explanation":"指持續而認真地查詢、核對並分析資訊，以便弄清某個問題；它比普通的“找”更強調系統性和深入程度。","examples":[{"en":"She researched the company carefully before accepting the job.","zh":"她接受這份工作前仔細調查了這家公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need to research the best options for my trip.","zh":"我需要查清楚旅行的最佳選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/research","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,113,114,115],"total":6,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1,"113":2,"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-3588bb7219b1faa3d01f","word":"researcher","forms":["researcher"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e174b89c83ee5d16","term":"researcher","forms":["researcher","researchers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"研究人員；研究者","explanation":"指以調查、實驗、觀察或分析為主要工作，透過研究問題來獲得或檢驗知識的人。這個詞的重點是“做研究的人”，不限定其所在的學科或機構。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers found that regular exercise can improve sleep quality.","zh":"研究人員發現，規律運動可以改善睡眠質量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a researcher in child development.","zh":"她是一名兒童發展研究人員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/researcher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb233c738048666fed9b","word":"resemblance","forms":["resemblance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-decb5c1d52b08c29","term":"resemblance","forms":["resemblance","resemblances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相似；相像之處","explanation":"指兩個人、事物或形象之間具有相似特徵這一事實，重點是“相似關係”本身，而不是某個具體的相似物。","examples":[{"en":"There is a strong resemblance between the two sisters.","zh":"這兩姐妹之間有很強的相似之處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The resemblance between the twins was easy to see.","zh":"這對雙胞胎之間的相似之處很容易看出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resemblance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9ff95b18b9468e4","term":"resemblance","forms":["resemblance","resemblances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相似物；畫像；摹本","explanation":"指一個看起來像另一個人或事物的具體形象、畫像或物件，即“相似關係”所呈現出來的那個相似物。","examples":[{"en":"The portrait is a close resemblance of its subject.","zh":"這幅肖像畫與本人十分相像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The statue bears a striking resemblance to the old king.","zh":"這座雕像與那位老國王非常相像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resemblance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5393b48316f7414dd29","word":"resemble","forms":["resemble"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdde6f0123d92202","term":"resemble","forms":["resemble","resembles","resembling","resembled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"像；與……相似","explanation":"指一個人或物在外貌、特徵、性質等方面看起來像另一個人或物，是現代英語中最主要的意思。相似不一定完全相同，只要讓人聯想到另一個物件，就可以使用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"The twins resemble each other.","zh":"這對雙胞胎彼此很像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This painting resembles a photograph.","zh":"這幅畫看起來像一張照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resemble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bd62e592162cadea99a","word":"resent(ment)","forms":["resent","resentment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bbcff7c0887752f9","term":"resent","forms":["resent","resents","resenting","resented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對……心懷怨氣","explanation":"因為覺得受到冒犯、不公平對待或被剝奪了應有的東西，而一直對某人或某事感到怨恨、不滿。這是 resent 在現代英語中的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"She resented being treated like a child.","zh":"她很怨恨別人把她當小孩子對待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He resents the fact that his ideas are ignored.","zh":"他對自己的想法被忽視這件事一直很不滿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e5122c2bbbd3d6f","term":"resent","forms":["resent","resents","resenting","resented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對……表示憤怒或不滿","explanation":"指明確表現出對某件事的憤怒、抗議或強烈不滿，而不只是把怨氣藏在心裡。這個義項在現代用法中不如核心義常見，常見於較正式的語境。","examples":[{"en":"The minister resented the accusation and demanded an apology.","zh":"部長對這一指控表示強烈不滿，並要求道歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She resented being excluded from the discussion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a18ca27bf8dfb4e2","term":"resentment","forms":["resentment","resentments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受了不公後的怨恨","explanation":"當一個人覺得自己或自己的群體被輕視、虧待、傷害或背叛，而這種不滿一直沒有消退時，就會產生 resentment；它強調積壓在心裡的怨氣，而不只是當下發火。","examples":[{"en":"Years of unfair treatment created deep resentment among the workers.","zh":"多年的不公平待遇在工人中積累了深深的怨恨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt resentment toward her brother after he took credit for her work.","zh":"弟弟把她的功勞據為己有後，她對弟弟產生了怨恨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resentment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9efa077f044e7a779c65","word":"reservation","forms":["reservation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2e1d9dc5555538f","term":"reservation","forms":["reservation","reservations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保留；留出","explanation":"指把資源、資金、權利等先留下來，不立即使用或交給別人，強調“暫時圈出、保住”。","examples":[{"en":"The committee approved the reservation of funds for emergencies.","zh":"委員會批准為緊急情況預留資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reservation of a front-row seat requires an additional fee.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reservation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c5174a6e84b1669","term":"reservation","forms":["reservation","reservations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疑慮；保留意見","explanation":"指對某人的動機、某個計劃或某個結論沒有完全把握，因此心裡留著疑問或擔心；彷彿沒有把自己的信任全部交出去。","examples":[{"en":"I have serious reservations about signing the contract.","zh":"我對簽署這份合同有嚴重的顧慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She agreed to the plan, but with some reservations.","zh":"她同意了這個計劃，但仍有一些保留意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reservation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e69744edc1ee98d","term":"reservation","forms":["reservation","reservations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"預訂；預約","explanation":"指提前把酒店房間、座位、交通工具等留給自己，確保到時候可以使用；這是“先圈出、暫時留著”的最常見日常用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"I made a reservation for two at the restaurant.","zh":"我在那家餐廳訂了兩個人的座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our hotel reservation is under the name of Chen.","zh":"我們的酒店預訂登記在陳先生名下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reservation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6df24c372c044a0fd8d0","word":"reserve","forms":["reserve"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31f7aae5d5b6168c","term":"reserve","forms":["reserve","reserves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保留；限制","explanation":"指某項權利、使用資格或內容被暫時保留下來，別人不能隨意動用；也可指這種保留本身。","examples":[{"en":"The book is on reserve at the library.","zh":"這本書在圖書館的保留書架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company reserves the right to change the schedule.","zh":"公司保留更改日程的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e52735213813ebc","term":"reserve","forms":["reserve","reserves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲備；留存物","explanation":"指為了將來或特殊用途而留下的資源、物品或數量，例如能源儲備；核心仍是“先留著不用”。","examples":[{"en":"The country has large reserves of natural gas.","zh":"這個國家有大量天然氣儲備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep a reserve of drinking water for emergencies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-669503db621d315a","term":"reserve","forms":["reserve","reserves","reserving","reserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保留；留住","explanation":"指不立即放棄、交出或使用某物，而是把它留在自己或某種安排中。保留權利、意見或改變空間，都來自“先留下”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"We reserve the right to make changes.","zh":"我們保留作出修改的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She reserved some money for emergencies.","zh":"她留了一些錢應急。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d63ba13f8d513e3","term":"reserve","forms":["reserve","reserves","reserving","reserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"留作以後或特殊用途","explanation":"指先把某物存放或留下，明確不供當前一般使用，而是留給將來或特定的人。","examples":[{"en":"This cake is reserved for the guests.","zh":"這塊蛋糕是留給客人的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reserve some flour for dusting the work surface.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0dda676792204118","term":"reserve","forms":["reserve","reserves","reserving","reserved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預訂","explanation":"指提前把座位、房間、票或服務留好，確保將來可以使用；這可以看作把一個位置先保留下來。","examples":[{"en":"I reserved a table for four at seven.","zh":"我預訂了晚上七點四人桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They reserved a room near the station.","zh":"他們預訂了車站附近的一間房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reserve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14f42b4e998bc5bc01ae","word":"reservoir","forms":["reservoir"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1043d4e89559c09","term":"reservoir","forms":["reservoir","reservoirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲藏處；儲備庫","explanation":"指集中儲存某種東西的地方或容器，不一定真的裝水；可以儲存物資、資訊、資金，也可以比喻集中擁有某種資源。","examples":[{"en":"The library is a reservoir of local history.","zh":"這座圖書館是當地歷史資料的寶庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company has a large reservoir of experienced workers.","zh":"這家公司擁有大量經驗豐富的員工儲備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reservoir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c62859a9ad2ec433","term":"reservoir","forms":["reservoir","reservoirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水庫","explanation":"指人工或天然形成、用來蓄水並供應用水的大型湖泊或水域。這是現代英語中最常見、最具體的含義之一。","examples":[{"en":"The city gets most of its drinking water from the reservoir.","zh":"這座城市的大部分飲用水都來自這座水庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reservoir was nearly full after weeks of rain.","zh":"連續下了幾周雨後，水庫幾乎滿了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reservoir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37dd149a2e88db1fdf64","word":"reside","forms":["reside"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7eaf8713fe9597fb","term":"reside","forms":["reside","resides","residing","resided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"居住；長期停留","explanation":"指人在某地有固定住所並住上一段較長時間，重點是“安定地住在那裡”，而不只是臨時經過或短暫停留。","examples":[{"en":"She resides in a small town near the coast.","zh":"她居住在海邊附近的一座小鎮上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist currently resides in Berlin.","zh":"這位藝術家目前居住在柏林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73d17fc200ad7818","term":"reside","forms":["reside","resides","residing","resided"],"pos":"verb","zh":"存在於；根源在於","explanation":"把某種性質、力量、原因或問題看成“固定在”某個事物或地方中，表示它的所在或根源在那裡。","examples":[{"en":"The real strength of the team resides in its unity.","zh":"這個團隊真正的力量在於團結一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The difficulty resides in the lack of reliable evidence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reside","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13d00b4f50b002bfb1c7","word":"residence","forms":["residence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c835d5e23d3aa159","term":"residence","forms":["residence","residences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"居住地；住所","explanation":"指某人實際居住或長期安頓的地方，重點是“住在哪裡”這一居住地點，也可以泛指自己的住處。","examples":[{"en":"After the wedding, they took up their residence in Bristol.","zh":"婚禮後，他們在布里斯托爾定居下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please send the documents to my residence.","zh":"請把檔案寄到我的住處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/residence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b6571bedec9a802","term":"residence","forms":["residence","residences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"住宅；住房","explanation":"指作為居所使用的具體建築物或其中的一套住房，重點從“住在哪裡”轉到了“那所房子本身”。","examples":[{"en":"The old residence has been converted into a small museum.","zh":"這座老住宅已經改成了一座小博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors may not enter the royal residence.","zh":"來訪者不得進入王室住宅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/residence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84816ff383c826e9c11e","word":"resident","forms":["resident"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac9fa061b1910a8f","term":"resident","forms":["resident","more resident","most resident"],"pos":"adj","zh":"居住的；常住的","explanation":"指人在某地長期居住，通常不是短暫停留；也可以說某人在自己的房產或固定住所中居住。","examples":[{"en":"She has been resident in the village for ten years.","zh":"她已經在這個村子裡住了十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only resident students may use this facility.","zh":"只有住校學生才能使用這個設施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a12f862ac1305dc0","term":"resident","forms":["resident","residents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"居民；居住者","explanation":"指生活在某個地點或區域的人，也可指長期生活在某地的動物或植物；核心仍是“住在這裡的物件”。","examples":[{"en":"Local residents asked the council to improve the roads.","zh":"當地居民要求市政委員會改善道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The park's residents include several rare species of bird.","zh":"這個公園的棲息者包括幾種珍稀鳥類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resident","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-53983477e4cf3e49dd95","word":"residential","forms":["residential"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3178a80fb67934b2","term":"residential","forms":["residential","more residential","most residential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"住宅的；居住區的","explanation":"指與人們居住的住宅或地點有關，重點是“這是用來住人的地方”。例如住宅區、居住街區都可以用這個詞來描述。","examples":[{"en":"They live in a quiet residential neighborhood.","zh":"他們住在一個安靜的住宅區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory stands well away from residential streets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/residential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e34682c3e265d8ca","term":"residential","forms":["residential","more residential","most residential"],"pos":"adj","zh":"供居住者使用的；居住用的","explanation":"指某物是給居民使用的，或某地、某設施具有居住用途；它仍然圍繞“住人”這個核心，只是重點從地點本身轉向使用者或用途。","examples":[{"en":"The building has separate entrances for residential and commercial tenants.","zh":"這棟樓為住宅租戶和商業租戶設定了不同的入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The upper floors are reserved for residential use.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/residential","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06028c9760f4dfd106aa","word":"resign","forms":["resign"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4e6f03017c96060","term":"resign","forms":["resign","resigns","resigning","resigned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辭去職位；辭職","explanation":"指主動離開自己的工作或職務，相當於把職位交還出去。這是現代英語中最常見、最需要優先掌握的意思，尤其用於正式職位或公開宣佈離職。","examples":[{"en":"The minister resigned after the scandal.","zh":"那名部長在醜聞發生後辭職了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I am resigning from my position at the end of the month.","zh":"我將在月底辭去目前的職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b82a9120e0e3548a","term":"resign","forms":["resign","resigns","resigning","resigned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"無奈接受；認輸","explanation":"指在無法改變的情況下被動地接受結果，或承認事情已經沒有希望。這裡仍然是“鬆開手”，但放棄的不是職位或物品，而是繼續抗爭或改變結果的希望。","examples":[{"en":"He resigned himself to waiting another year.","zh":"他只好接受還要再等一年的現實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After losing two players, the team resigned itself to defeat.","zh":"失去兩名隊員後，這支隊伍只能接受失敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d636fa71c59b22158606","word":"resignation","forms":["resignation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb5cb74e12228d1c","term":"resignation","forms":["resignation","resignations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辭職；辭去職務","explanation":"指主動結束自己所擔任的職位這一行為，重點是“把職位放下”。它既可以指辭職這個過程，也可以泛指辭職這件事。","examples":[{"en":"After ten years with the company, Maria announced her resignation.","zh":"在這家公司工作了十年後，瑪麗婭宣佈辭職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her resignation left the department without a leader.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resignation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6e382ac4d21f261","term":"resignation","forms":["resignation","resignations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"無奈接受","explanation":"指面對不好的、卻無法避免或改變的事情時，不再抱怨或抗爭而接受現實。這裡放下的不是職位，而是改變結果的希望。","examples":[{"en":"With resignation, she accepted that the damaged painting could not be restored.","zh":"她無奈地接受了那幅受損的畫無法修復這一事實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He accepted the disappointing result with quiet resignation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resignation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e3257a014cd30acfe77","word":"resist","forms":["resist"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cffea122890b78b9","term":"resist","forms":["resist","resists","resisting","resisted","resistest","resistedst","resisteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反抗；對抗","explanation":"指主動設法阻止某人的行動或某件事的影響，不接受對方強加的結果；重點在於“頂回去、不給它得逞”。","examples":[{"en":"The workers resisted the company's attempt to cut their pay.","zh":"工人們抵制公司削減他們工資的企圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She resisted pressure from her friends to leave school.","zh":"她頂住了朋友讓她退學的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27c3848e7030ff6b","term":"resist","forms":["resist","resists","resisting","resisted","resistest","resistedst","resisteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抵擋；經受住","explanation":"指某人或某物承受住外來的力量、影響或誘惑而沒有被改變或壓垮；這裡更強調“扛得住”，不一定有主動反擊。","examples":[{"en":"The bridge was built to resist strong winds and earthquakes.","zh":"這座橋建造時考慮了抵禦強風和地震。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I couldn't resist the temptation to check my phone.","zh":"我抵擋不住誘惑，還是檢視了手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":3,"counts":{"111":2,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-be970d090a9b0a231a60","word":"resistance","forms":["resistance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06b5f56bd1313b64","term":"resistance","forms":["resistance","resistances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抵抗；反抗","explanation":"指主動頂住某種力量、要求或控制的行為，也可以指抵抗的能力。它是最基本的義項，後面的“阻力”和“電阻”都可以看作某種形式的阻礙。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy met strong resistance from local residents.","zh":"這項新政策遭到了當地居民的強烈抵制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed little resistance to the suggestion.","zh":"她幾乎沒有反對這個建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resistance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bc710a84006133a","term":"resistance","forms":["resistance","resistances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"阻力","explanation":"在物理中，指妨礙物體運動的力。可以把它想成一隻看不見的手，運動越想向前，就越受到這隻手的拖拽。","examples":[{"en":"Air resistance slows the falling paper.","zh":"空氣阻力會減慢紙張下落的速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A streamlined shape reduces resistance as the submarine moves underwater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resistance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c39cfd639660e777f60d","word":"resistant","forms":["resistant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36024519c9122cd0","term":"resistant","forms":["resistant","more resistant","most resistant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"抵抗的；抗拒外力的","explanation":"指某人或某物會頂住、對抗來自外部的力量或影響，不輕易被改變或壓倒。","examples":[{"en":"This material is resistant to pressure.","zh":"這種材料能抵抗壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new coating makes the metal more resistant to damage.","zh":"這種新塗層使金屬更耐受損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resistant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f1b2a833cfdd10c","term":"resistant","forms":["resistant","more resistant","most resistant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"抗……的；不易受……影響的","explanation":"指疾病、細菌、材料或其他物件不會輕易被某種藥物、化學物質、溫度或環境因素消除、改變或破壞。","examples":[{"en":"The infection is resistant to antibiotics.","zh":"這種感染對抗生素具有耐藥性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These plants are resistant to extreme heat.","zh":"這些植物耐極端高溫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resistant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7fbd5853d11940e045a","word":"resolution","forms":["resolution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94c96a91adcedee0","term":"resolution","forms":["resolution","resolutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"決定；決議","explanation":"指已經明確作出的決定，既可以是個人的決定，也可以是機構或會議正式透過的決定；重點是“不再懸而未決”。","examples":[{"en":"The committee reached a resolution after a long discussion.","zh":"委員會經過長時間討論後作出了決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a resolution to exercise every morning.","zh":"她下定決心每天早晨鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9661ed42b7d9ba8c","term":"resolution","forms":["resolution","resolutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅定的決心","explanation":"指面對困難仍不改變目標的堅定意志，是把“想做”變成“堅持做下去”的力量。","examples":[{"en":"He faced the criticism with quiet resolution.","zh":"他以沉著堅定的態度面對批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her resolution never to give up impressed everyone.","zh":"她永不放棄的決心給每個人都留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fdf09cdfc26cccf610ed","word":"resolve","forms":["resolve"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b381e1f89df13f3","term":"resolve","forms":["resolve","resolves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅定意志","explanation":"指在困難、壓力或痛苦面前仍堅持做下去的意志力，也就是不輕易動搖的決心。","examples":[{"en":"It took all her resolve to keep working after the setback.","zh":"遭遇挫折後，她靠著全部的意志力才堅持繼續工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The setback only strengthened their resolve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-abf6428d1913fc2c","term":"resolve","forms":["resolve","resolves","resolving","resolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解決問題","explanation":"指找到辦法並處理好問題、困難或爭議，使原來的麻煩不再懸而未決。","examples":[{"en":"The support team resolved the billing problem within a day.","zh":"客服團隊在一天之內解決了賬單問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to resolve this issue before the meeting.","zh":"我們需要在會議前解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c60a4a55d0be26f","term":"resolve","forms":["resolve","resolves","resolving","resolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下定決心","explanation":"指堅定地決定採取某個行動或努力實現某個目標，把心意固定下來。","examples":[{"en":"I resolved to finish the report before leaving the office.","zh":"我下定決心在離開辦公室前完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She resolved never to repeat the mistake.","zh":"她下定決心再也不犯同樣的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acd33c597d26e632","term":"resolve","forms":["resolve","resolves","resolving","resolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"化解分歧","explanation":"指透過討論或處理，讓雙方的爭執、分歧或關係得到解決並恢復平和。","examples":[{"en":"The two departments met to resolve their differences.","zh":"兩個部門開會以化解彼此的分歧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mediator helped resolve their disagreement over costs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4bb6794bff884d75de01","word":"resort","forms":["resort"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-608b9dbac00e0e54","term":"resort","forms":["resort","resorts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"度假勝地","explanation":"指人們為了休閒、娛樂或度假而去的地方，通常有住宿、娛樂設施和放鬆的環境。它可以是一整片旅遊區，也可以指其中的度假設施。","examples":[{"en":"We spent a week at a quiet resort by the sea.","zh":"我們在海邊一個安靜的度假勝地住了一個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mountain resort is popular with families in winter.","zh":"這座山地度假勝地在冬天很受家庭遊客歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f47bd31a52a12dd2","term":"resort","forms":["resort","resorts","resorting","resorted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"訴諸；求助於","explanation":"指在困難、 frustration 或缺少更好辦法時，轉而採用某種手段或求助於某人。這正是“退回去尋找依靠”的動詞表達。","examples":[{"en":"If discussion fails, they may resort to legal action.","zh":"如果協商失敗，他們可能會訴諸法律行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She never resorts to insults during an argument.","zh":"她爭論時從不靠辱罵來解決問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5de95319f17467ed6dc5","word":"resource","forms":["resource"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8238207bd80654b3","term":"resource","forms":["resource","resources"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實現目標的可用資源","explanation":"resource 是為了完成某件事而可以呼叫的東西，包括物資、能源、人力和資金等。它們像儲備庫中的內容，關鍵在於能被利用來解決問題或推進目標。","examples":[{"en":"The project needs more resources to meet its deadline.","zh":"這個專案需要更多資源才能按時完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clean water is becoming a scarce resource in the region.","zh":"清潔水正在成為這個地區稀缺的資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resource","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b4b7a3072da4b38","term":"resource","forms":["resource","resources"],"pos":"noun","zh":"應對困難的能力或辦法","explanation":"這裡的 resource 不再是外部物資，而是一個人面對困難時能想出辦法、調動經驗和能力的內在儲備。說某人有 resource，就是說他機智、有應變能力。","examples":[{"en":"She is a woman of resource and always finds a way forward.","zh":"她很有辦法，總能找到繼續前進的辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With no tools available, he relied on his own resources.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resource","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-0c3e015009e5155c2c7c","word":"respect","forms":["respect"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b44886b6375d00a","term":"respect","forms":["respect","respects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尊重；敬意","explanation":"指認真看待某人、承認其價值並以應有的態度對待對方的感覺或態度，也可指對某人的敬意。","examples":[{"en":"I have great respect for her honesty.","zh":"我非常敬重她的誠實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children should show respect for their teachers.","zh":"孩子應該尊重老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b38c21701e8c53fc","term":"respect","forms":["respect","respects","respecting","respected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"尊重","explanation":"認真看待某人並承認其價值，因而以應有的態度對待對方。","examples":[{"en":"I respect her for speaking honestly.","zh":"我敬佩她敢於坦誠說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We respect our neighbors and their privacy.","zh":"我們尊重鄰居，也尊重他們的隱私。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68b9129160b628c3","term":"respect","forms":["respect","respects","respecting","respected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遵守；尊重","explanation":"認真對待某項權利、習俗、規則或做法，並按它的要求行事。","examples":[{"en":"Please respect the rules of the library.","zh":"請遵守圖書館的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They respect everyone’s right to disagree.","zh":"他們尊重每個人表達不同意見的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0e63ca0573f423eaf5d","word":"respectable","forms":["respectable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68a71ba948659ca0","term":"respectable","forms":["respectable","more respectable","most respectable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得尊敬的","explanation":"形容一個人的成就、品德或行為足以贏得別人的尊重；這是從“值得尊敬”這一核心概念直接發展出來的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She is a respectable person who always keeps her promises.","zh":"她是個值得尊敬的人，總是信守承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He built a respectable career through hard work.","zh":"他靠努力建立了一個值得認可的職業生涯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respectable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c129226198b98db5","term":"respectable","forms":["respectable","more respectable","most respectable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"體面的；還不錯的","explanation":"形容衣著、表現、成績或結果等達到“像樣、令人滿意”的程度。它不一定特別出色，但已經足夠體面，就像一個人整理好儀表後能自然地獲得認可。","examples":[{"en":"You should wear something respectable to the interview.","zh":"你應該穿得體面些去參加面試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team achieved a respectable result despite the difficult conditions.","zh":"儘管條件困難，這支隊伍還是取得了不錯的成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respectable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f280f2f378e8f50fc751","word":"respectful","forms":["respectful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d97deb5fb2e1398a","term":"respectful","forms":["respectful","more respectful","most respectful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"尊重的；恭敬的","explanation":"指一個人或他的言行表現出對他人、信仰、觀點等的尊重，通常也包含剋制、認真和禮貌的態度。這個詞強調“把尊重表現出來”，而不只是心裡覺得對方重要。","examples":[{"en":"Please be respectful to everyone in the meeting.","zh":"請對會議中的每個人都保持尊重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a respectful reply even though she disagreed.","zh":"儘管她並不同意，但她仍作出了尊重而禮貌的回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respectful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-969656cc5f0c62c224fb","word":"respective","forms":["respective"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e859e56968380f2","term":"respective","forms":["respective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"各自的；分別的","explanation":"指同一群體中的每個人或每件事都有自己的對應物件、位置或責任，就像各自站在屬於自己的格子裡。它常用於複數名詞前，說明這些物件分別屬於不同的人或事物。","examples":[{"en":"After the meeting, the team members returned to their respective offices.","zh":"會議結束後，團隊成員回到了各自的辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two companies announced their respective plans for the next year.","zh":"兩家公司公佈了各自來年的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-149d479f6a59e992d99e","word":"respond","forms":["respond"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d5970d093907975","term":"respond","forms":["respond","responds","responding","responded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"回答；回覆","explanation":"對問題、觀點或別人說的話作出口頭或書面的回答，把對方的話接回來。它既可以表示回答內容，也可以只表示作出答覆這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"She responded to my question with a clear explanation.","zh":"她清楚地回答了我的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He responded that he would arrive before noon.","zh":"他回答說自己會在中午前到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc9a674c118f2b5d","term":"respond","forms":["respond","responds","responding","responded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"作出反應","explanation":"受到行動、力量、環境變化或其他刺激後，作出相應的動作或變化；不一定涉及說話。這個意義仍像是把外來的“球”接住並作出回應。","examples":[{"en":"The plants responded well to the warmer weather.","zh":"這些植物對較暖的天氣反應良好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The alarm responds to movement in the room.","zh":"警報器會對房間裡的移動作出反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respond","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00e3874b77243522c34e","word":"respondent","forms":["respondent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-406d371d39df73b0","term":"respondent","forms":["respondent","respondents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"回應者；答覆者","explanation":"指對問題、請求或某人的話作出回應的人，也就是處在“有人發問，另一方回答”這條回應鏈上的人。","examples":[{"en":"Each respondent received a written reply.","zh":"每位回應者都收到了一份書面答覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The respondents were asked to explain their views.","zh":"研究人員要求這些回應者說明自己的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respondent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8e3530d5276d5f9","term":"respondent","forms":["respondent","respondents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問卷填寫者","explanation":"特指回答問卷或調查問題的人。這個意義是“一群人收到問題並作出回應”這一核心畫面的常見應用。","examples":[{"en":"Most respondents said they preferred online shopping.","zh":"大多數受訪者表示，他們更喜歡網上購物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each respondent completed the questionnaire anonymously.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/respondent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9f4b3d22a523fdada41","word":"response","forms":["response"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-538176a1d1f6aafd","term":"response","forms":["response","responses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"回答；回應","explanation":"指對問題、請求、評論或某種情況作出的回答或回應，可以是語言，也可以是行動。這個詞強調“對前面的東西回過去”的結果。","examples":[{"en":"We are still waiting for a response to our request.","zh":"我們仍在等待對請求的回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her smile was a warm response to his greeting.","zh":"她的微笑是對他問候的溫暖回應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/response","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e733d98e98f4923","term":"response","forms":["response","responses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反應；響應","explanation":"指身體、人的情緒或系統受到刺激、壓力或挑釁後產生的反應。它和“回答”共享同一條主線：某個外來訊號到來後，內部或外部作出回應。","examples":[{"en":"The patient had a strong response to the new treatment.","zh":"這名患者對新治療產生了強烈反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fear is a natural response to danger.","zh":"恐懼是人面對危險時的自然反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/response","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5f88e747d24a44c9d46","word":"responsibility","forms":["responsibility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d83ed2ffede2c02","term":"responsibility","forms":["responsibility","responsibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負責的狀態","explanation":"指一個人對某事負有責任、需要作出交代的狀態，重點是“這件事由誰負責”。它是一個總的概念，可以涵蓋履行職責，也可以涵蓋對結果負責。","examples":[{"en":"She took full responsibility for the mistake.","zh":"她對這個錯誤承擔了全部責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Responsibility for the project rests with the manager.","zh":"這個專案由經理負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84057947e3e9ab2b","term":"responsibility","forms":["responsibility","responsibilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體職責或義務","explanation":"指某人被分配或應當履行的一項任務、義務或職責，就像“手裡接住的一件事”。它不一定暗示已經出錯，而是說明某人本來就應該負責完成什麼。","examples":[{"en":"It is your responsibility to lock the door.","zh":"鎖門是你的責任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her responsibilities include scheduling and staff training.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsibility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9195f0946897bd7094a","word":"responsible","forms":["responsible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34d18a4661e1e8ce","term":"responsible","forms":["responsible","more responsible","most responsible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對……負責；承擔責任","explanation":"表示某人有義務照看、處理某事，並且要對自己的行為或由此產生的後果負責。它可以用於日常分工，也可以用於法律、政治等正式責任。","examples":[{"en":"Parents are responsible for teaching their children basic manners.","zh":"父母有責任教孩子基本的禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager is responsible for the safety of everyone in the building.","zh":"經理要對樓內所有人的安全負責。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57ab8aed6ea3d3f1","term":"responsible","forms":["responsible","more responsible","most responsible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"是……的原因；應為……負責","explanation":"表示某人、某個行為或某種因素直接造成了某種情況，因此可以受到責備，也可能因此得到肯定。這裡重點不是“負責照看”，而是“對結果起主要作用”。","examples":[{"en":"A blocked drain was responsible for the flooding in the basement.","zh":"地下室進水是排水管堵塞造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Who is responsible for this mistake?","zh":"這個錯誤是誰造成的？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3831b8ee33ff3bd","term":"responsible","forms":["responsible","more responsible","most responsible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可靠的；值得信賴的","explanation":"形容一個人做事可靠，會履行承諾，並能在需要時妥善處理事情。這個義項是“承擔責任”自然延伸出的性格評價：別人相信他拿得住那串責任鑰匙。","examples":[{"en":"He is responsible and always returns things he borrows.","zh":"他很可靠，總會歸還借來的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the keys with a responsible adult.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/responsible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e09d5210db8417757b0","word":"rest","forms":["rest"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e083f8138b37df9","term":"rest","forms":["rest","rests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"休息；睡眠","explanation":"指透過睡覺或停止活動來恢復精力的休息，記住“停下來並保持在那裡”，這裡是人暫時停下勞作。","examples":[{"en":"The exhausted rescue workers needed food and rest after the long search.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"A good night's rest restored his concentration.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0223081b13945f48","term":"rest","forms":["rest","rests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短暫休息","explanation":"指在活動或用力過程中停下來一會兒，以恢復體力或喘口氣；這是“停下來”的一次具體安排。","examples":[{"en":"After carrying the boxes upstairs, she sat down for a short rest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"We stopped for a rest beneath the trees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5cc4a0a42ccaf79a","term":"rest","forms":["rest"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剩餘部分","explanation":"指已經取走、使用或吃掉一部分後還留下來的部分，也就是“還留在那裡”的東西。","examples":[{"en":"We spent half the money on repairs and saved the rest for emergencies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"Take one biscuit and leave the rest for others.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3243bb348c60f3a","term":"rest","forms":["rest","rests","resting","rested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"休息；停止活動","explanation":"把它記成“停下來並保持在那裡”：人停止工作、活動或移動，就是休息。","examples":[{"en":"I need to rest for a few minutes after the walk.","zh":"散步後我需要休息幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rested at home instead of going out.","zh":"她待在家裡休息，沒有出門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee275d64dafcd283c25b","word":"restaurant","forms":["restaurant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3970cb7baedecb2","term":"restaurant","forms":["restaurant","restaurants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餐館；飯店","explanation":"指人們進去吃飯、由店家提供食物的場所，通常可以坐在桌邊用餐並由服務員提供服務，也可以指快餐櫃檯式的餐飲店。","examples":[{"en":"We found a small restaurant near the station.","zh":"我們在車站附近找到了一家小餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant serves traditional dishes made with local ingredients.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restaurant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7fd11ebf9937f9d1576","word":"restoration","forms":["restoration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8a58ac8c57f33500","term":"restoration","forms":["restoration","restorations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恢復；修復過程","explanation":"指把某物帶回原來的狀態，重點是恢復這一過程，而不只是最後得到的物品。它可以用於建築、藝術品、身體部位等具體物件。","examples":[{"en":"The restoration of the old theater took two years.","zh":"這座老劇院的修復花了兩年時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Experts are working on the restoration of the painting.","zh":"專家們正在修復這幅畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restoration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9a612daf2032885","term":"restoration","forms":["restoration","restorations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"修復成果；修復物","explanation":"指恢復過程完成後得到的成果，尤其可以指修復好的物品或牙科修復體。這裡關注的是“被恢復出來的東西”，而不是修復這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed several careful restorations of damaged paintings.","zh":"博物館展出了幾幅經過精心修復的受損畫作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restored clock is one of his finest restorations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restoration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f329e3a317eee6a8a1a7","word":"restore","forms":["restore"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aeea490f68ad6524","term":"restore","forms":["restore","restores","restoring","restored","restorest","restoredst","restoreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"恢復；重新建立","explanation":"指讓原本失去或中斷的關係、秩序、狀態重新出現，例如重新建立和諧或信任。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement helped restore peace between the two communities.","zh":"這項協議幫助兩個社群恢復了和平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new leader worked hard to restore public confidence.","zh":"新領導人努力恢復公眾的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-614ab812ca9e572e","term":"restore","forms":["restore","restores","restoring","restored","restorest","restoredst","restoreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修復；恢復良好狀態","explanation":"指把已經破損、衰敗或失去正常功能的人或物修復到較好的狀態，重點是恢復原有狀況。","examples":[{"en":"The team restored the old theater to its original condition.","zh":"團隊把這座老劇院修復到了原來的狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This treatment restored movement to her injured hand.","zh":"這種治療使她受傷的手恢復了活動能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf6e3c47f4a06ae7","term":"restore","forms":["restore","restores","restoring","restored","restorest","restoredst","restoreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從備份恢復","explanation":"指系統崩潰、檔案損壞或資料丟失後，從備份中把檔案、資料庫或系統恢復出來。","examples":[{"en":"We restored the deleted photos from a backup.","zh":"我們從備份中恢復了被刪除的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the crash, the technician restored the entire system.","zh":"系統崩潰後，技術員恢復了整個系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86c0c46bd552e693846a","word":"restrain","forms":["restrain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4846759fdff58bd3","term":"restrain","forms":["restrain","restrains","restraining","restrained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"控制；剋制","explanation":"指把情緒、衝動、行為或某種力量壓住，使它不繼續失控，就像用繩子拉住向前衝的東西。","examples":[{"en":"She struggled to restrain her anger during the meeting.","zh":"她努力控制住自己在會議上的怒氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He could barely restrain himself from laughing.","zh":"他幾乎忍不住要笑出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restrain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe86af4118e6f2aa","term":"restrain","forms":["restrain","restrains","restraining","restrained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剝奪自由；把人束縛住","explanation":"指用實際措施把人牢牢控制住，不讓其自由行動，像用繩子或其他束縛物把人固定住。","examples":[{"en":"The security guards restrained the man until the police arrived.","zh":"保安制服並控制住那名男子，直到警察趕到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guards restrained him with handcuffs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restrain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c36fc9be162d466d5dd","word":"restraint","forms":["restraint"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b01dd2622671eb4","term":"restraint","forms":["restraint","restraints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固定裝置；約束帶","explanation":"指用來把人或物固定、繫牢或限制其移動的具體裝置，可以把它想成一條把東西“按住”的帶子。","examples":[{"en":"The luggage restraints kept the boxes in place.","zh":"行李固定帶把箱子穩穩固定在原位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fasten the child restraint before starting the car.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restraint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82137861f010dcc7","term":"restraint","forms":["restraint","restraints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剋制；謹慎","explanation":"指主動把自己的情緒、言語或行為按住，不讓衝動完全表現出來；它是從“固定住東西”引申出的自我控制。","examples":[{"en":"He showed remarkable restraint and did not answer the insult.","zh":"他表現出非凡的剋制，沒有回應那句侮辱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed remarkable restraint despite the repeated insults.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restraint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd13d46bad4ba114699a","word":"restrict","forms":["restrict"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1bf20e969e87b099","term":"restrict","forms":["restrict","restricts","restricting","restricted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"限制；約束在一定範圍內","explanation":"把人、活動、選擇或資源收緊在規定的邊界內，使它們不能隨意超出這個範圍。它既可以表示限制行動，也可以表示規定只能使用某種選擇。","examples":[{"en":"After the storm, access to the bridge was restricted to emergency vehicles.","zh":"暴風雨過後，這座橋只允許應急車輛通行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor restricted her to a light diet for a week.","zh":"醫生規定她一週內只能吃清淡的食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restrict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea257421aa4a9af64bce","word":"restriction","forms":["restriction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6e48b39b77eb789","term":"restriction","forms":["restriction","restrictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制；受限狀態","explanation":"指限制某事的行為，或因此形成的受限狀態。重點不在某一條具體規定，而在“活動空間被關小了”這一整體概念。","examples":[{"en":"The new restrictions on travel made it harder to visit family.","zh":"新的出行限制讓探望家人變得更困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked under severe time restrictions.","zh":"她在嚴格的時間限制下工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restriction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4dba165da930f4f2","term":"restriction","forms":["restriction","restrictions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"限制規定；約束條件","explanation":"指具體寫明或實際執行的一條限制規則，例如規定誰可以進入、什麼時候可以做某事，或數量不能超過多少。它是“關小的門”在現實中的具體告示或制度。","examples":[{"en":"The park has restrictions on the use of drones.","zh":"這個公園對無人機的使用有明確限制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The permit includes restrictions on evening construction work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restriction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2ee8db7682b9f0ba180","word":"restroom","forms":["restroom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dee2f46a1ecb3df1","term":"restroom","forms":["restroom","restrooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公共廁所","explanation":"指商場、餐館、機場等公共場所供人如廁的房間；它通常是對“廁所”的委婉說法。","examples":[{"en":"Could you tell me where I can find the restroom?","zh":"請問廁所在哪裡？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restroom is at the end of the corridor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/restroom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f6a214f7a5fcda0c2cee","word":"result","forms":["result"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb7b466a042c036c","term":"result","forms":["result","results"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結果；後果","explanation":"result 是一件事、一個過程或一次計算最後產生的結論或後果，重點在“事情發展到最後落成了什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"The result of the investigation was unexpected.","zh":"調查的結果出人意料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add the two numbers and write down the result.","zh":"把這兩個數相加，然後寫下結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/result","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2489858cae95f2a2","term":"result","forms":["result","results"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成效；取得的成果","explanation":"當 result 強調努力最後帶來的實際收穫時，就是“成效”或“成果”，比單純的結果更容易帶有積極意味。","examples":[{"en":"After months of practice, she finally got results.","zh":"經過幾個月的練習，她終於取得了成效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new training program is already producing results.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/result","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce989f9843e57d64","term":"result","forms":["result","results","resulting","resulted","resultest","resultedst","resulteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"產生；由此得出","explanation":"某種結論、狀態或結果從事實、條件、思考或行動中自然產生時，可以說它 results from 那些因素，突出“結果從前面的情況中長出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The delay resulted from a mistake in the schedule.","zh":"延誤是由日程安排中的一個錯誤造成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Better decisions often result from careful planning.","zh":"更好的決定往往來自周密的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/result","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33afae505ba2e708","term":"result","forms":["result","results","resulting","resulted","resultest","resultedst","resulteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"導致；造成","explanation":"某項行動或條件最後帶來某種後果時，result in 表示“導致”，把前面的事情看作產生後果的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The heavy rain resulted in flooding across the town.","zh":"暴雨導致全鎮多處洪水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small changes can result in major improvements.","zh":"小小的改變可能帶來巨大的改善。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/result","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a83a31320d921b888a48","word":"resume","forms":["resume"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b55bd50fee6eed2","term":"resume","forms":["resume","resumes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"求職履歷；簡歷","explanation":"指介紹個人教育背景、工作經歷、技能和資格的檔案，通常用於申請工作，讓僱主快速瞭解求職者。","examples":[{"en":"I sent my resume to three companies this week.","zh":"我這周把簡歷發給了三家公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Attach your resume to the completed application form.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91c1707b4c28dc8e","term":"resume","forms":["resume","resumes","resuming","resumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續；恢復某事","explanation":"指某件事暫停後，從停下的位置繼續進行，而不是重新從頭開始；例如會議、談話、工作都可以這樣恢復。","examples":[{"en":"We will resume the meeting after lunch.","zh":"我們午飯後繼續開會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She resumed working once the power came back.","zh":"電力恢復後，她繼續工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1778c2d9b45bac0ae39a","word":"retail","forms":["retail"],"officialPos":"n./adj./adv./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76b8f0c943289939","term":"retail","forms":["retail"],"pos":"adj","zh":"零售的；面向消費者的","explanation":"描述商品或服務直接賣給最終個人消費者的業務、策略或市場，而不是賣給批發商或其他中間商。","examples":[{"en":"The company is expanding its retail business.","zh":"這家公司正在擴大零售業務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Retail customers can order the product online.","zh":"普通消費者可以線上訂購這款產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0638cf6678dc5c6d","term":"retail","forms":["retail"],"pos":"adv","zh":"以零售方式","explanation":"表示商品不是批次賣給經銷商，而是按零售數量或價格直接賣給最終消費者。","examples":[{"en":"We sell directly to customers, not retail through distributors.","zh":"我們直接向顧客銷售，不透過經銷商進行零售。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scarves sell retail for forty dollars each.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adc1899ddd033a70","term":"retail","forms":["retail"],"pos":"noun","zh":"零售業","explanation":"指把商品或服務直接賣給普通消費者的整個行業和銷售體系，包括商店、網站、廣告及相關運營機制。","examples":[{"en":"She has worked in retail for ten years.","zh":"她已經在零售業工作十年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked in retail before opening her own café.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ca9ee7388094d0c","term":"retail","forms":["retail","retails","retailing","retailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"零售；直接賣給顧客","explanation":"指把商品按零售數量直接賣給最終消費者，而不是整批賣給經銷商或其他商家。","examples":[{"en":"The farm retails fresh eggs to local families.","zh":"這家農場把新鮮雞蛋零售給當地家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop retails handmade toys and wooden puzzles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6b428ace0262db5de1ac","word":"retain","forms":["retain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e4a35a10f65fefb","term":"retain","forms":["retain","retains","retaining","retained","retainest","retainedst","retaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續擁有；保留","explanation":"繼續把某物留在自己手中、控制之下或原有狀態中，而不是失去、交出或放棄。這是 retain 最重要的基本義。","examples":[{"en":"She chose to retain ownership of the house after the divorce.","zh":"離婚後，她選擇繼續保留這棟房子的所有權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company retained most of its customers during the difficult year.","zh":"在困難的一年裡，這家公司留住了大部分客戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e225538e8db780b6","term":"retain","forms":["retain","retains","retaining","retained","retainest","retainedst","retaineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保留；不廢除","explanation":"決定繼續讓某個制度、特徵、做法或物品存在，而不是把它去掉、取消或替換。","examples":[{"en":"The redesigned building retains several features of the original.","zh":"重新設計後的建築保留了原建築的幾個特點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school decided to retain its traditional uniform.","zh":"這所學校決定保留傳統校服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f44ee0d67a411c29e50","word":"retire(ment)","forms":["retire","retirement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a8ed42bdaecadd7","term":"retire","forms":["retire","retires","retiring","retired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"退休","explanation":"指通常因年老或身體原因永久停止工作，就像從職業生活中退開。","examples":[{"en":"My father plans to retire next year.","zh":"我父親計劃明年退休。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She retired from teaching at sixty-five.","zh":"她六十五歲時從教師崗位上退休了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9d885d7453b7eb6","term":"retire","forms":["retire","retires","retiring","retired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"退到某處","explanation":"指離開原來的公開或活動場所，退回某處或進入私人空間；這是“向後拉開”這一核心意思的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"He retired to his room to read.","zh":"他回到自己的房間去讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guests retired to the garden after lunch.","zh":"午飯後，客人們退到花園去了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cb42e119e0b2231","term":"retirement","forms":["retirement","retirements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"退休後的生活；退休狀態","explanation":"指一個人已經永久離開職業、尤其是在達到退休年齡後所處的狀態，以及隨後的人生階段；這是現代最重要的含義之一。它把“從工作中退到後方”變成一種持續的生活狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She moved to the coast after retirement.","zh":"她退休後搬到了海邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is enjoying a quiet retirement with his family.","zh":"他正和家人享受安靜的退休生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retirement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2d0cb1be6720391","term":"retirement","forms":["retirement","retirements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"退休；離開職業","explanation":"指永久離開工作、職業或某項職業性活動這一行為，強調“退出”的決定或事件，而不是退休之後的生活狀態。體育和公共職務語境中也常用它表示某人結束職業生涯。","examples":[{"en":"The athlete announced his retirement from international football.","zh":"這名運動員宣佈退出國際足球賽場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her retirement from teaching came after forty years in the classroom.","zh":"她教了四十年書後退休了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retirement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc3f72308f2d2e30c208","word":"retort","forms":["retort"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f72b3fd20ce8c0b0","term":"retort","forms":["retort","retorts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機智反擊","explanation":"retort 是一句尖銳而機智的回話，尤其是把別人剛才的侮辱、指責或論點巧妙地反過來對付對方。它像把對方扔來的話接住，再原路彈回去。","examples":[{"en":"Her quick retort made everyone at the table laugh.","zh":"她機敏的回話讓桌邊的所有人都笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sharp retort left him without an answer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3f554334875d672","term":"retort","forms":["retort","retorts","retorting","retorted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"尖銳回話","explanation":"作動詞時，retort 表示針對某句話迅速作出尖銳或機智的回答，像把話鋒彈回去。","examples":[{"en":"“That is not my responsibility,” she retorted.","zh":"“那不是我的責任。”她尖銳地回道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He retorted that the mistake had been hers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-896f766e9dcec37b","term":"retort","forms":["retort","retorts","retorting","retorted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反推指責","explanation":"retort 還可以表示把對方的指責、批評或論點反過來施加給對方，也就是以其人之道反駁其人。","examples":[{"en":"When accused of being careless, he retorted that his colleague had ignored the instructions.","zh":"有人指責他粗心時，他反駁說是同事忽視了說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He retorted that her own report contained similar errors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a076332aa18967d7785","word":"retreat","forms":["retreat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b35b8b393a8f77aa","term":"retreat","forms":["retreat","retreats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"撤退；退回","explanation":"指為了躲避危險、不快或不利局面而向後退開，重點是從原來的位置或處境中退出。","examples":[{"en":"The army began its retreat before dawn.","zh":"軍隊在黎明前開始撤退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a long argument, she made a quiet retreat to her room.","zh":"長時間爭吵後，她悄悄退回了自己的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retreat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02d627f830ff7a58","term":"retreat","forms":["retreat","retreats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"隱居處；靜謐之所","explanation":"指讓人遠離喧鬧、獲得隱私或安全感的安靜地方；它可以是山間小屋、鄉間住所等。","examples":[{"en":"They bought a small cottage as a weekend retreat.","zh":"他們買了一座小屋，作為週末靜居之所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cottage became her peaceful retreat from city life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retreat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c604467081db8975","term":"retreat","forms":["retreat","retreats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"靜修期；退居獨處","explanation":"指暫時離開日常生活、獨處一段時間，常為了冥想、祈禱、學習或恢復精神；它把“退到安靜處”延伸成了一段時間。","examples":[{"en":"She went on a three-day retreat to recover from burnout.","zh":"她參加了為期三天的靜修，以從精疲力竭中恢復過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students spent the weekend on a writing retreat.","zh":"學生們在寫作靜修活動中度過了週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retreat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80953fad9eda4aac","term":"retreat","forms":["retreat","retreats","retreating","retreated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撤退；退回","explanation":"指人、軍隊或群體離開原來的位置，向後退到較安全的地方；這是 retreat 最核心的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers retreated from the cliff when the wind grew stronger.","zh":"風變大後，徒步者們從懸崖邊退了回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers retreated into the forest.","zh":"士兵們退入了森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retreat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50f2a151d15e0459729a","word":"retrieve","forms":["retrieve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-832c8792ab1b5571","term":"retrieve","forms":["retrieve","retrieves","retrieving","retrieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"找回；重新獲得","explanation":"指把丟失、被拿走或暫時失去的東西重新拿回來，也可指重新獲得名譽、獨立等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"She returned to the café to retrieve her phone.","zh":"她回到咖啡館取回了自己的手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is working to retrieve its good reputation.","zh":"這家公司正在努力挽回自己的良好聲譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retrieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-569cf9db524cd720","term":"retrieve","forms":["retrieve","retrieves","retrieving","retrieved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調取資料；檢索檔案","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指從資料庫、裝置或系統中找到並取出檔案、記錄或其他資料。","examples":[{"en":"The app can retrieve your account information from the server.","zh":"這個應用可以從伺服器調取你的賬戶資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please retrieve the report from the archive.","zh":"請從檔案庫中調出那份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retrieve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7187f0675eb382793974","word":"return","forms":["return"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5e73138b7bb93cd","term":"return","forms":["return","returns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"返回；回來","explanation":"指回到原來的地方或狀態這一行為，把 return 想成“回到原處”本身，而不是正在返回的動作。","examples":[{"en":"We will prepare the room before her return.","zh":"我們會在她回來前把房間準備好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His return to the village surprised everyone.","zh":"他回到村裡讓大家都很驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/return","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f9413c5a57960c2","term":"return","forms":["return","returns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"退回的物品；退貨","explanation":"指買回後被退回的商品，也可以指退回商品這一行為，通常因為商品有問題或不合適；它仍然體現了物品“回到原處”。","examples":[{"en":"The shop keeps a separate area for online returns.","zh":"這家商店為網上退貨設了專門區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The returns are stacked behind the customer-service desk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/return","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9da8e555114643b","term":"return","forms":["return","returns","returning","returned","returnest","returnedst","returneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"回來；返回","explanation":"指人、動物或其他移動中的事物回到原來的地方或某個人身邊，就像沿著路回到原處。","examples":[{"en":"After the holiday, she returned to her apartment in the city.","zh":"假期結束後，她回到了城裡的公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The birds return here every spring.","zh":"這些鳥每年春天都會回到這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/return","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b61a8498fda9c5c","term":"return","forms":["return","returns","returning","returned","returnest","returnedst","returneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"歸還","explanation":"指把借來的或暫時拿到的東西交還給原來的所有者或保管處，就像把物品送回它原來的主人那裡。","examples":[{"en":"Please return the keys to the front desk before you leave.","zh":"離開前請把鑰匙歸還給前臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I returned the book to the library yesterday.","zh":"我昨天把書還給了圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/return","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-608af3ec161f05bf4400","word":"reunion","forms":["reunion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6f842b7821b1fa79","term":"reunion","forms":["reunion","reunions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重新相聚","explanation":"指原本分開的人再次見面、聚在一起的過程或行為，重點在“重新回到一起”。","examples":[{"en":"Their reunion took years, but everyone was happy at last.","zh":"他們花了好幾年才重新相聚，但最後每個人都很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reunion with my old friends was deeply moving.","zh":"和老朋友重新相聚讓我非常感動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reunion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3a2aa12f7d8f387","term":"reunion","forms":["reunion","reunions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重聚會","explanation":"指提前安排的一次活動，曾經一起學習、工作或生活、後來分散的人在活動中再次見面。","examples":[{"en":"Are you going to the high-school reunion this year?","zh":"你今年要參加高中同學重聚會嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Former classmates organized a reunion at their old school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reunion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-419a636ccc2aa55c7347","word":"reveal","forms":["reveal"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64b66733a988f08c","term":"reveal","forms":["reveal","reveals","revealing","revealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭示；顯露","explanation":"reveal 表示把原本被遮住、隱藏或不明顯的東西展示出來，使別人能夠看見或瞭解；既可以是實物，也可以是事實、問題或情感。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation revealed several errors in the report.","zh":"調查揭示了報告中的幾處錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She revealed the plan to her closest friend.","zh":"她把這個計劃透露給了最親密的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reveal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4a3372c03e839b9b740","word":"revelation","forms":["revelation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd1de9049cc11d50","term":"revelation","forms":["revelation","revelations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揭露；揭示","explanation":"指把原本隱藏、不為人知的事實或身份公開出來這一動作，重點在“揭開”本身。","examples":[{"en":"The revelation of the secret shocked everyone in the office.","zh":"這個秘密被揭露出來，震驚了辦公室裡的所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report led to the revelation that the records had been altered.","zh":"這份報告揭示出那些記錄曾被篡改。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revelation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac33eda94f04084a","term":"revelation","forms":["revelation","revelations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被揭示的事實","explanation":"指已經被揭開的資訊、真相或秘密，也就是掀開幕布後看見的內容，而不是揭開的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Her revelation about the missing money changed the investigation.","zh":"她透露的那筆失蹤款項的真相改變了調查方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diary contained startling revelations about the expedition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revelation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16552853f9506d93252a","word":"revenge","forms":["revenge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d727887b4f8507a","term":"revenge","forms":["revenge","revenges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"報復；復仇","explanation":"指因為某人、機構或群體造成了被認為不公的傷害，而採取行動反擊或討回公道。報復不一定是直接傷害對方，也可以是讓對方失去原本想得到的東西。","examples":[{"en":"She took revenge on the company by exposing its unfair practices.","zh":"她揭露那家公司的不公平做法，以此報復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ignoring him completely was her quiet revenge.","zh":"完全不理他，就是她無聲的報復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revenge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ff6e75d92a9ec49","term":"revenge","forms":["revenge","revenges","revenging","revenged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……報仇；報復","explanation":"指主動採取行動，報復某個具體傷害，或替受到傷害的人討回公道。也可用於比賽中透過獲勝報先前失利之仇。","examples":[{"en":"The players revenged their earlier defeat by winning 3–0.","zh":"這些球員以三比零獲勝，為先前的失利報了仇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wanted to revenge the insult, but his sister stopped him.","zh":"他想為那次侮辱報復，但被姐姐阻止了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revenge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-371f7e4223809d8bce3d","word":"revenue","forms":["revenue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aaebee984d9d8110","term":"revenue","forms":["revenue","revenues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投資收益","explanation":"指投資帶回來的收入，強調資金投入後又產生了迴流；它不一定等於扣除全部成本後的利潤。","examples":[{"en":"The fund receives revenue from its investment in renewable energy.","zh":"該基金從對可再生能源的投資中獲得收入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rental revenue helped the company cover its operating costs.","zh":"租賃收入幫助這家公司支付了運營成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revenue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3883351551aa2f3a","term":"revenue","forms":["revenue","revenues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某來源帶來的總收入","explanation":"指來自某個明確來源的全部收入，重點在於說明這筆錢是從哪裡迴流來的。","examples":[{"en":"Advertising revenue from the website increased sharply this year.","zh":"這個網站今年的廣告收入大幅增加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Advertising revenue pays for most of the magazine's costs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revenue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bafae690da05651c","term":"revenue","forms":["revenue","revenues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銷售額；營業收入","explanation":"在商業和會計語境中，指企業透過銷售產品或服務獲得的收入總額，也就是常說的銷售額或營業收入。","examples":[{"en":"The company's revenue grew by 15 percent last year.","zh":"這家公司去年的營業收入增長了百分之十五。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Online sales now account for half of our total revenue.","zh":"網上銷售現在佔我們總收入的一半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revenue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2d7f24e833051d5fc29","word":"reverse","forms":["reverse"],"officialPos":"v./adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac2d8939e23b408b","term":"reverse","forms":["reverse"],"pos":"adj","zh":"反向的；相反的","explanation":"就像把方向轉回去一樣，表示方向、順序或性質與通常情況相反。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the instructions in reverse order.","zh":"請按相反的順序閱讀說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reverse side of the card is blank.","zh":"卡片的背面是空白的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5fb69fbfcc4472a8","term":"reverse","forms":["reverse","reverses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相反的一面；反面","explanation":"指某事物完全相反的情況，就像把方向轉回去一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Patience is the reverse of impulsiveness.","zh":"耐心與衝動正好相反。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reverse of the rule is also true.","zh":"這條規則的反面同樣成立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbe1510efd9fb316","term":"reverse","forms":["reverse","reverses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倒擋","explanation":"指汽車讓車輛向後移動的擋位，通常在換擋桿上標為 R，也就是車輛“轉回去”的擋位。","examples":[{"en":"Check behind you before putting the car in reverse.","zh":"把車掛入倒擋前，先檢查車後方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She backed out of the driveway in reverse.","zh":"她倒車駛出了車道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e60169c2aa3cc450","term":"reverse","forms":["reverse","reverses","reversing","reversed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"倒轉方向或順序","explanation":"把某物“轉回去”，使它朝相反方向，或使原來的先後順序完全倒過來。","examples":[{"en":"Please reverse the order of the names on the list.","zh":"請把名單上的名字順序倒過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car reversed direction and headed back toward town.","zh":"汽車調轉方向，朝城鎮駛回去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reverse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c97ace4c8fef2cee8fa0","word":"review","forms":["review"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bd03a37637418fbe","term":"review","forms":["review","reviews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"複習；重新研讀","explanation":"指把書、文章或其他材料重新讀一遍，以便獲得新的理解或發現先前忽略的內容。","examples":[{"en":"I did a careful review of the chapter before the seminar.","zh":"研討會前，我仔細複習了這一章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A brief review of yesterday's vocabulary began the lesson.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/review","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb054a0fe5dc4c6e","term":"review","forms":["review","reviews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"評論；評價文章","explanation":"指對書、電影、演出或其他作品進行分析和評價的文字，也可指這類評價本身。","examples":[{"en":"Her review of the film praised the acting but criticized the ending.","zh":"她對這部電影的評論稱讚了演技，但批評了結尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I read several restaurant reviews before booking a table.","zh":"預訂座位前，我看了幾篇餐館評論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/review","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3046264b432ba1d","term":"review","forms":["review","reviews","reviewing","reviewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"概覽；審閱","explanation":"指對某個問題、歷史或一組材料進行全面檢視，以瞭解其主要內容或處理方式。","examples":[{"en":"The opening section reviews the main theories behind the project.","zh":"開頭部分概述了這個專案所依據的主要理論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee conducted a review of local transport services.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/review","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a1a6c874b660773","term":"review","forms":["review","reviews","reviewing","reviewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重新檢查；修訂","explanation":"指回頭檢查已經寫好或安排好的內容，並根據發現的問題修改它。","examples":[{"en":"Please review the report and correct any errors before sending it.","zh":"傳送前請審閱這份報告並改正錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team reviewed its plan after the first test failed.","zh":"第一次測試失敗後，團隊重新審查了計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/review","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa53d35cdecfe4a2bc65","word":"revise","forms":["revise"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1bc203acf5b29fdb","term":"revise","forms":["revise","revises","revising","revised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修訂；修改","explanation":"重新檢查文字、檔案、計劃或規定，並改正問題、補充內容或使其更合適；重點是基於舊版本進行改進。","examples":[{"en":"The committee revised the safety guidelines after the accident.","zh":"事故發生後，委員會修訂了安全指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please revise your report before sending it to the client.","zh":"請在把報告發給客戶之前修改一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b214ddf3326016519af","word":"revision","forms":["revision"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a7ef9bf1569dd8c","term":"revision","forms":["revision","revisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"修改；修訂過程","explanation":"指重新檢查文字、計劃或作品並加以改進的過程，重點是“重新看過後變得更好”。","examples":[{"en":"The report needs one more revision before we send it to the client.","zh":"這份報告還需要再修改一次，才能發給客戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Careful revision made the proposal much clearer.","zh":"仔細修改後，這份提案清楚多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba5c141d36175781","term":"revision","forms":["revision","revisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考試複習","explanation":"在英國、澳大利亞和紐西蘭英語中，指為考試重新學習和鞏固知識，也就是“備考、複習”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to do some revision for tomorrow's mathematics exam.","zh":"我得為明天的數學考試複習一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent the weekend doing revision at the library.","zh":"她整個週末都在圖書館複習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30b90b0c8146d2841067","word":"revival","forms":["revival"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82b5be7e0af08914","term":"revival","forms":["revival","revivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"復甦；恢復","explanation":"指某人或某事物重新獲得生命力、活力或原有作用，也可以指這種恢復本身。這個意義是“重新醒來”這一核心畫面的最一般用法。","examples":[{"en":"The revival of the old theater brought new life to the neighborhood.","zh":"這座老劇院的復甦給附近街區帶來了新的活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient showed signs of revival after the treatment.","zh":"治療後，病人出現了恢復的跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f6002cb1d62d4c3","term":"revival","forms":["revival","revivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"恢復健康或精神","explanation":"特指人或群體從虛弱、低迷、沮喪或衰退中重新振作起來，重點是狀態變好、精神恢復。","examples":[{"en":"A few days in the countryside gave her spirits a welcome revival.","zh":"在鄉下待了幾天，她的精神得到了一次可喜的恢復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team enjoyed a revival after changing its coach.","zh":"換了教練後，這支隊伍重新振作起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77841c7aa2be1d8e","term":"revival","forms":["revival","revivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"復興；重新繁榮","explanation":"指文化、藝術、商業、農業等重新受到關注、重新發展，或重新進入興盛狀態。這裡的“醒來”從個人狀態擴充套件到了整個領域。","examples":[{"en":"The city is experiencing a revival of traditional crafts.","zh":"這座城市正在經歷傳統手工藝的復興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town experienced a revival after the railway reopened.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34f54b279dd0fa8b6fd6","word":"revive","forms":["revive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a522c0069856751","term":"revive","forms":["revive","revives","reviving","revived","revivest","revivedst","reviveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使甦醒","explanation":"指使昏厥的人或動物恢復意識，就像把暫時熄滅的生命之火重新點燃。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse revived him after he fainted.","zh":"他暈倒後，護士使他甦醒過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lifeguard revived the unconscious swimmer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ff987019a256f72","term":"revive","forms":["revive","revives","reviving","revived","revivest","revivedst","reviveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使重新興盛","explanation":"指使衰落、被忽視或幾乎消失的事物重新活躍起來，例如語言、傳統、行業或活動。","examples":[{"en":"The community is trying to revive the old festival.","zh":"這個社群正努力讓這個古老節日重新興盛起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign revived interest in local history.","zh":"這場活動重新激發了人們對地方歷史的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82a8d10283d9b2c5","term":"revive","forms":["revive","revives","reviving","revived","revivest","revivedst","reviveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"甦醒過來","explanation":"指昏厥的人或動物自己恢復意識，不是別人把它救醒。","examples":[{"en":"She fainted in the heat but soon revived.","zh":"她因炎熱暈倒了，但很快就甦醒過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unconscious swimmer revived after receiving emergency care.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2abd1a4d22630a2","term":"revive","forms":["revive","revives","reviving","revived","revivest","revivedst","reviveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重新興盛起來","explanation":"指衰落、被遺忘或不再活躍的事物自己重新興盛起來。與及物用法不同，這裡重點是事物發生了恢復。","examples":[{"en":"Interest in folk music has revived among young people.","zh":"年輕人對民間音樂的興趣重新興盛起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Traditional weaving revived as demand for handmade textiles grew.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b10198f778488767b4fd","word":"revolt","forms":["revolt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09615b00e9b184e3","term":"revolt","forms":["revolt","revolts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反抗行動；叛亂","explanation":"指人們不再服從權威或統治，集體採取反抗行動；重點是“轉身反對原來的掌權者”。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers put down a revolt against the governor.","zh":"士兵鎮壓了反對總督的叛亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The revolt began with a refusal to pay taxes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6bbc9b866070d4d2","term":"revolt","forms":["revolt","revolts","revolting","revolted","revoltest","revoltedst","revolteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反抗；反叛","explanation":"指拒絕服從權威並採取反抗行動，和名詞義相連：原本順從的人轉身站到了權威的對立面。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers revolted against the harsh new ruler.","zh":"村民們反抗那位嚴苛的新統治者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garrison revolted after three months without pay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70b6144fae4d4c163c6e","word":"revolution","forms":["revolution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ca66a8a57ed6271","term":"revolution","forms":["revolution","revolutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治劇變","explanation":"指政府或國家發生劇烈的政治變革，舊的統治結構被大幅改變，可能形成新的政治制度。","examples":[{"en":"The revolution transformed the monarchy into a republic.","zh":"這場革命把君主制徹底變成了共和制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country was shaken by a revolution.","zh":"這個國家因一場革命而受到劇烈衝擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c781e3b24c9c418","term":"revolution","forms":["revolution","revolutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繞軸轉一週","explanation":"指物體圍繞一條軸線轉動，也可以指這種轉動完成的一整圈。這裡保留了“轉一圈”的基本畫面，但不表示物體必須從一個地方移動到另一個地方。","examples":[{"en":"The wheel makes one complete revolution every second.","zh":"這個輪子每秒完整轉一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine records the speed of revolution of the disk.","zh":"這臺機器記錄圓盤的轉速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-009f1bcabc8de1fe","term":"revolution","forms":["revolution","revolutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巨大變革","explanation":"指某種情況、學科或人們思考和行事的方式突然發生範圍很大、影響很深的變化，不一定涉及政府或暴力。比如新技術徹底改變一個行業時，也可以稱為一場革命。","examples":[{"en":"The internet brought about a revolution in communication.","zh":"網際網路給通訊方式帶來了一場巨大變革。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence is causing a revolution in medicine.","zh":"人工智慧正在引發醫學領域的一場革命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,114],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-412f0bdbca4000c32af4","word":"revolutionary","forms":["revolutionary"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c0f16482960d6d7","term":"revolutionary","forms":["revolutionary","more revolutionary","most revolutionary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"革命的；推動革命的","explanation":"指與推翻舊政治秩序、建立新制度的革命有關，或支援、推動這種革命。它修飾戰爭、運動、組織等時，強調這些事物具有革命性質。","examples":[{"en":"The revolutionary army captured the capital after a long war.","zh":"革命軍隊經過長期戰爭後佔領了首都。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined a revolutionary movement in her youth.","zh":"她年輕時參加過一個革命運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolutionary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ae4d1fe94c29c7c","term":"revolutionary","forms":["revolutionary","more revolutionary","most revolutionary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"突破性的；顛覆性的","explanation":"指某種新技術、方法或思想帶來了巨大變化，把人們原有的認識或做法徹底轉變。這裡的“革命”是比喻用法，不一定與政治有關。","examples":[{"en":"The company has developed a revolutionary way to store solar energy.","zh":"這家公司開發出了一種儲存太陽能的突破性方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her revolutionary ideas changed the way we teach children.","zh":"她顛覆性的想法改變了我們教育孩子的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolutionary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68067ae139fb6ac91735","word":"revolve","forms":["revolve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1365df8a1a0d9c64","term":"revolve","forms":["revolve","revolves","revolving","revolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使繞中心旋轉","explanation":"表示讓某物圍繞一箇中心點或軸轉動，重點在於外力使它轉起來；這是“revolve”物理運動主線的及物用法。","examples":[{"en":"The motor revolves the wheel around a central axle.","zh":"電機使輪子繞中央軸轉動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She revolved the model slowly on its stand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43ca70b444c2791a","term":"revolve","forms":["revolve","revolves","revolving","revolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繞中心執行；公轉","explanation":"表示天體或其他物體沿軌道繞著某個中心執行，例如地球繞太陽執行；這裡的中心通常不是物體自身的軸。","examples":[{"en":"The Moon revolves around the Earth.","zh":"月球繞著地球執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The model shows three small moons revolving around the giant planet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b533000c34d8a058","term":"revolve","forms":["revolve","revolves","revolving","revolved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繞軸旋轉","explanation":"表示物體圍繞自身的一條軸持續轉動，重點是自轉或機械部件繞軸旋轉，而不是繞另一個天體執行。","examples":[{"en":"The Earth revolves on its axis once every twenty-four hours.","zh":"地球每二十四小時繞自身軸旋轉一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wheels revolved slowly as the cart moved forward.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revolve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7696fff84f26472a9737","word":"reward","forms":["reward"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9fdd87e63ae98c6","term":"reward","forms":["reward","rewards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎賞；回報","explanation":"指因為做了某件值得肯定的事而得到的有價值的東西，例如錢、禮物、獎品或其他好處。重點是“行為或努力換來回報”這一關係。","examples":[{"en":"She received a reward for returning the lost wallet.","zh":"她因歸還丟失的錢包而得到了一份獎勵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company offered a reward for useful suggestions.","zh":"公司為有用的建議提供了獎勵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbfa97a5b8ddabec","term":"reward","forms":["reward","rewards","rewarding","rewarded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獎勵；獎賞","explanation":"指因為某人的行為、努力或成績而給他回報，核心是“用回報肯定某人的表現”。回報可以是錢、禮物、機會或表揚等。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher rewarded the students for their hard work.","zh":"老師獎勵了努力學習的學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They rewarded her with a paid vacation.","zh":"他們獎勵她一次帶薪休假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3424482393d121796ddc","word":"rhetoric","forms":["rhetoric"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04fba3a595b91d14","term":"rhetoric","forms":["rhetoric","rhetorics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說服性的語言藝術","explanation":"指透過選擇和組織語言，尤其藉助公開演講來影響、打動或說服聽眾的藝術和表達方式；重點是語言如何成為說服工具。","examples":[{"en":"Her campaign rhetoric focused on hope and practical change.","zh":"她的競選演說主要強調希望和切實的改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister's rhetoric persuaded many undecided voters.","zh":"部長的說服性言辭讓許多尚未決定投票物件的選民改變了態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhetoric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a939732d1baca4b","term":"rhetoric","forms":["rhetoric","rhetorics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空洞的華麗說辭","explanation":"指聽起來誇張、有氣勢，實際上缺少具體內容或誠意的語言；這是“說服工具”只剩外表、沒有實質時產生的貶義用法。","examples":[{"en":"Voters are tired of empty rhetoric and want real solutions.","zh":"選民已經厭倦了空洞的說辭，想要真正的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Voters wanted practical answers rather than empty rhetoric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhetoric","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c79ce7ffd92648aa656","word":"rhyme","forms":["rhyme"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ba0cf58addbe184","term":"rhyme","forms":["rhyme","rhymes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"押韻詩；韻文","explanation":"指以押韻為重要形式寫成的詩歌或韻文，重點在於詩句之間的聲音相互對應，而不只是泛指任何詩。","examples":[{"en":"The children learned the story in rhyme.","zh":"孩子們透過押韻的故事學會了這個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She writes simple poems in rhyme for young readers.","zh":"她為年輕讀者寫簡單的押韻詩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhyme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30468a3716d4b942","term":"rhyme","forms":["rhyme","rhymes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"押韻；韻律對應","explanation":"指不同詞語從重讀母音到詞尾的字母或聲音相同或相近這一現象。它是“押韻詩”和“押韻詞”這兩個意思的共同基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The poem uses rhyme to make the final lines memorable.","zh":"這首詩用押韻讓結尾幾行更容易記住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The song has a simple rhyme that children can follow.","zh":"這首歌的押韻很簡單，孩子們跟得上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhyme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0f8a60ec09ee84b","term":"rhyme","forms":["rhyme","rhymes","rhyming","rhymed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使押韻","explanation":"指安排詞語的位置，使它們在重讀母音以後具有相同或相近的聲音，從而形成押韻。","examples":[{"en":"The poet rhymed “fire” with “desire.”","zh":"詩人讓“fire”和“desire”押韻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She changed the last line to rhyme it with the first.","zh":"她改了最後一行，使它和第一行押韻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhyme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80560cc3e643fd0f","term":"rhyme","forms":["rhyme","rhymes","rhyming","rhymed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與……押韻","explanation":"描述一個詞的發音與另一個詞從重讀母音到詞尾相同或相近，因此兩詞可以押韻。","examples":[{"en":"“Station” rhymes with “nation.”","zh":"“station”和“nation”押韻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The word “blue” rhymes with “true.”","zh":"“blue”和“true”押韻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhyme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00489c560ee8a257","term":"rhyme","forms":["rhyme","rhymes","rhyming","rhymed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"彼此押韻","explanation":"指兩個或多個詞互相具有相同或相近的押韻部分；這是 s3“某個詞與另一個詞押韻”的相互表達。","examples":[{"en":"“Moon” and “June” rhyme.","zh":"“moon”和“June”押韻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These two lines rhyme, but the third does not.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhyme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-add8bed82dd53765b774","word":"rhythm","forms":["rhythm"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05f7bc713c52d98f","term":"rhythm","forms":["rhythm","rhythms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聲音或音樂的節奏","explanation":"聲音中的強弱、長短或重音按照一定規律交替，聽起來形成可跟隨的拍子或節拍。它既可以指說話的節奏，也可以指音樂中的節奏。","examples":[{"en":"The dancers moved perfectly to the rhythm of the drums.","zh":"舞者完全跟著鼓聲的節奏起舞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancers clapped in rhythm with the drums.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhythm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5dc3bdc582d9ee7d","term":"rhythm","forms":["rhythm","rhythms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"做事或活動的規律步調","explanation":"某項活動不斷重複時形成的穩定流程或步調。掌握這種 rhythm 後，動作會變得自然，事情也往往更容易做。","examples":[{"en":"After a few days, I found a comfortable rhythm at my new job.","zh":"幾天後，我在新工作中找到了舒服的做事節奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Once you get into a rhythm, writing each morning becomes much easier.","zh":"一旦形成節奏，每天早上寫作就會容易得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhythm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b39e647572080f09c40b","word":"rib","forms":["rib"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73669deb26cfa906","term":"rib","forms":["rib","ribs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肋骨","explanation":"胸腔兩側成對排列的彎曲骨頭，從脊柱向前延伸，幫助保護心臟和肺。","examples":[{"en":"He broke a rib in the accident.","zh":"他在事故中摔斷了一根肋骨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take a deep breath if your ribs hurt.","zh":"如果肋骨疼，就深吸一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rib","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4740ef1f9e1f2daa","term":"rib","forms":["rib","ribs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肋狀支撐條","explanation":"任何形狀或作用像肋骨的細長彎曲部分，用來支撐、加固或確定某個物體的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"One rib of the umbrella snapped in the wind.","zh":"雨傘的一根傘骨被風吹斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ribs give the wing its shape.","zh":"這些翼肋使機翼保持形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rib","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4709446d901fac3b","term":"rib","forms":["rib","ribs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"打趣；調侃","explanation":"一個讓人發笑的善意玩笑，或針對某人的輕鬆取笑；它和“戳肋骨逗笑”的畫面相連。","examples":[{"en":"It was just a rib; nobody meant to offend you.","zh":"那只是句玩笑，沒人想冒犯你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team gave him a rib about his bright jacket.","zh":"隊友們拿他那件鮮豔的夾克打趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rib","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18a0cbec37f3f1e9","term":"rib","forms":["rib","ribs","ribbing","ribbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"善意取笑","explanation":"像輕輕戳人肋骨逗笑一樣，以輕鬆、通常無惡意的方式拿某人開玩笑。","examples":[{"en":"My friends ribbed me about being late again.","zh":"朋友們又拿我遲到這件事打趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gets ribbed for wearing that old hat.","zh":"他因為戴那頂舊帽子而被大家打趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rib","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-affc35bd6c6352aa5960","word":"ribbon","forms":["ribbon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ca6d5180e8b9a79","term":"ribbon","forms":["ribbon","ribbons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝飾帶；絲帶","explanation":"一種細長的帶狀材料，用來裝飾衣服、頭髮或禮物。這是 ribbon 最基本、最容易聯想到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She tied a blue ribbon around the gift.","zh":"她在禮物上繫了一條藍色絲帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little girl wore a ribbon in her hair.","zh":"小女孩在頭髮上戴了一條絲帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ribbon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-209f76418ece7c936b65","word":"rice","forms":["rice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f1891fa96b9fb9e","term":"rice","forms":["rice","rices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"稻；稻米這種作物","explanation":"rice 可以指結出米粒的稻這種禾本科作物，尤其是在農業、種植或植物學語境中；日常談吃飯時通常更常指米或米飯。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers grow rice in the flooded fields.","zh":"農民在灌水的田裡種稻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This region depends on rice as its main crop.","zh":"這個地區以稻米為主要農作物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e64ab7a127769233","term":"rice","forms":["rice","rices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"米飯；食用的米","explanation":"rice 最常見的日常意思是作為食物的米，既可以指生米，也可以根據上下文指煮熟的米飯。它通常是不可數名詞，表示一類食物，而不是一粒或一份。","examples":[{"en":"We had rice and vegetables for dinner.","zh":"我們晚飯吃了米飯和蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please add some rice to my bowl.","zh":"請在我的碗里加一些米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7baa68f2418ba82d2545","word":"rich","forms":["rich"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8902bcc97b83e731","term":"rich","forms":["rich","richer","more rich","richest","most rich"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富有的","explanation":"指擁有很多錢、財產或其他物質財富的人、家庭或社會階層。","examples":[{"en":"She grew up in a rich family but learned to live simply.","zh":"她在一個富裕家庭長大，但學會了過簡樸的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town became rich through trade.","zh":"這個城鎮靠貿易變得富裕起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rich","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-439d398e81716fc1","term":"rich","forms":["rich","richer","more rich","richest","most rich"],"pos":"adj","zh":"味道濃厚的","explanation":"指食物或飲料的油脂、糖分或整體味道很濃，吃起來厚重而有分量。","examples":[{"en":"The chocolate cake was delicious but too rich for me.","zh":"這塊巧克力蛋糕很好吃，但對我來說太甜膩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add a little lemon to balance the rich sauce.","zh":"加一點檸檬來調和濃厚的醬汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rich","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e926b73c7fd7d3a","term":"rich","forms":["rich","richer","more rich","richest","most rich"],"pos":"adj","zh":"豐富充足的","explanation":"指某處擁有大量資源、內容、活動或收穫，因而顯得充實而豐盛。","examples":[{"en":"The region has a rich cultural history.","zh":"這個地區擁有豐富的文化歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This book is a rich source of practical advice.","zh":"這本書是實用建議的豐富來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rich","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d5f24e66f8b9071ff13","word":"riches","forms":["riches"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c099f2cf7727cf24","term":"riches","forms":["riches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財富；財寶","explanation":"riches指金錢、貴重物品、土地等積累起來的財富，重點是“富足的一堆東西”，而不是某一件財物。","examples":[{"en":"He used his riches to support local schools.","zh":"他用自己的財富支援當地學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family lost its riches during the war.","zh":"這個家庭在戰爭期間失去了財富。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riches","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc9c54b39d8c0f3c","term":"riches","forms":["riches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豐富的收穫；寶藏","explanation":"這個意思把“財富”從金錢擴大到任何值得珍惜的豐富資源，例如知識、文化、經驗或大自然提供的收穫。","examples":[{"en":"Travel opened her eyes to the riches of other cultures.","zh":"旅行讓她看到了其他文化的豐富寶藏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive contains untold riches for local historians.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riches","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81466ee3cd6cf44d7a1c","word":"rid","forms":["rid"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-addc2968abc52e23","term":"rid","forms":["rid","rids","ridding","ridded","ridden","riddest","riddedst","riddeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擺脫；免除","explanation":"表示使自己、別人或某個地方不再受到麻煩、討厭的人或妨礙物的影響，重點是“從困擾中解脫出來”。","examples":[{"en":"I'm glad to be rid of that old computer.","zh":"我很高興終於擺脫了那臺舊電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was relieved to be rid of the constant noise.","zh":"擺脫了持續不斷的噪音後，她鬆了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4dbde25baffb808f","term":"rid","forms":["rid","rids","ridding","ridded","ridden","riddest","riddedst","riddeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"清除；處理掉","explanation":"表示主動把令人煩惱、礙事或不需要的人或東西移走，核心畫面是把它清出去。","examples":[{"en":"We need to get rid of these broken chairs.","zh":"我們得把這些壞椅子處理掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A short walk helped me get rid of the headache.","zh":"散了一會兒步幫助我擺脫了頭痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65b969ebf928fcf27536","word":"riddle","forms":["riddle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8fef4cb2aa11486","term":"riddle","forms":["riddle","riddles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"謎語；難題","explanation":"它把答案藏在表述裡，要求人透過思考猜出來；也可以泛指讓人困惑、難以解釋的問題。","examples":[{"en":"The children took turns telling each other riddles.","zh":"孩子們輪流給對方講謎語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children challenged each other with clever riddles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riddle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e049bd056f936d1b39b7","word":"ride","forms":["ride"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-385ea990d2f96613","term":"ride","forms":["ride","rides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"騎行或乘坐","explanation":"指騎在馬、腳踏車等承託物上移動，或乘坐車輛移動這件事，重點是“藉助承託物移動”的經歷本身。","examples":[{"en":"We went for a ride along the river after lunch.","zh":"午飯後我們沿著河邊騎行了一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children had a short ride on the train.","zh":"孩子們乘小火車走了一小段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d5a31f101a754cd","term":"ride","forms":["ride","rides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搭便車","explanation":"指別人用車輛送某人一程，也可指獲得或請求的這次乘車機會；車輛或他人提供了這種移動。","examples":[{"en":"Could you give me a ride to the station?","zh":"你能載我去車站嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her neighbor gave her a ride home after work.","zh":"下班後，她的鄰居開車送她回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08dc599e8654d3af","term":"ride","forms":["ride","rides","riding","rode","rade","rid","ridden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"騎行","explanation":"人坐在馬、腳踏車等承託物上並控制它前進，強調自己藉助承託物移動，而不是作為車輛乘客。","examples":[{"en":"I ride my bike to work whenever the weather is good.","zh":"天氣好的時候，我總是騎腳踏車上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned to ride a horse when she was eight.","zh":"她八歲時學會了騎馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2ac3f5b8083144e","term":"ride","forms":["ride","rides","riding","rode","rade","rid","ridden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"乘坐；搭乘","explanation":"人在車輛或其他交通工具中作為乘客移動，也就是由承託物或駕駛者帶著出行。","examples":[{"en":"We rode the train into the city this morning.","zh":"今天早上我們乘火車進城。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He rides to school with his older sister.","zh":"他和姐姐一起乘車去上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-409e364456fa93642cd2","word":"ridge","forms":["ridge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb7da637c1866dbf","term":"ridge","forms":["ridge","ridges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物背脊","explanation":"指動物背部中央或上方突出的脊部，尤其是四足動物背上的隆起部分。這是“狹長高起物”這一核心影象在身體上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"The saddle rested along the horse's ridge.","zh":"馬鞍沿著馬背的脊部放著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dark ridge of fur ran down the dog's back.","zh":"一條深色的毛脊沿著狗的背部延伸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4545c6132c4c3b96","term":"ridge","forms":["ridge","ridges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狹長隆起","explanation":"泛指任何延伸較長、呈線狀或帶狀的突出部分，例如犁溝之間隆起的土帶。它保留了“細長的凸起”這一最基本的概念。","examples":[{"en":"The plow left ridges of soil between the furrows.","zh":"犁在溝壟之間留下了一道道土脊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ridges of sand formed along the beach after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，海灘上形成了一道道沙脊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-574f6811b751a897","term":"ridge","forms":["ridge","ridges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斜坡交會的脊線","explanation":"指兩面向下分開的斜坡相交所形成的最高、狹長的線。山脊正是這種幾何形狀在自然地形中的典型例子。","examples":[{"en":"We followed the ridge until the trail descended into the valley.","zh":"我們沿著山脊走，直到小路下到山谷裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clouds gathered on the narrow ridge between the two slopes.","zh":"雲聚集在兩面斜坡之間狹窄的脊線上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4cca8463b6d6c5b70df","word":"ridiculous","forms":["ridiculous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a20cab43baddd38c","term":"ridiculous","forms":["ridiculous","more ridiculous","most ridiculous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"荒謬可笑的","explanation":"指某人、某物或某種做法荒唐得不合常理，容易引起嘲笑或不贊同；核心畫面就是“可笑到讓人發笑”。","examples":[{"en":"That hairstyle looks ridiculous.","zh":"那個髮型看起來很可笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It would be ridiculous to cancel the trip over a little rain.","zh":"因為下點小雨就取消旅行，實在太荒謬了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridiculous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b20ecdb8f5ea015b","term":"ridiculous","forms":["ridiculous","more ridiculous","most ridiculous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其誇張的","explanation":"在非正式語境中，ridiculous 可以把某種程度說得極端到難以置信；它仍然保留“誇張得讓人咋舌”的感覺，不一定是在批評。","examples":[{"en":"She ran a ridiculous distance before breakfast.","zh":"她在早餐前跑了遠得驚人的距離。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The goalkeeper made a ridiculous save from close range.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ridiculous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6dcdffaeac040a7037ac","word":"rifle","forms":["rifle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-771325c69138392c","term":"rifle","forms":["rifle","rifles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"步槍","explanation":"一種從肩部抵住發射的長槍，槍管內的螺旋膛線能讓子彈旋轉，從而提高射程和準確度。","examples":[{"en":"The hunter carried a rifle across the field.","zh":"獵人帶著一支步槍穿過田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers stored their rifles in a locked room.","zh":"士兵們把步槍存放在上鎖的房間裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rifle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2c88fc4f5257eda","term":"rifle","forms":["rifle","rifles","rifling","rifled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"快速翻找","explanation":"快速而凌亂地翻看一堆東西，通常是為了找到某件物品；畫面像手伸進抽屜或紙堆中不停撥動。","examples":[{"en":"I rifled through the drawer for my passport.","zh":"我快速翻遍抽屜尋找護照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rifled through the old photographs.","zh":"她快速翻看那些老照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rifle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27042f4e6eca7d0b2a7e","word":"right","forms":["right"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bab0de4f2ac74738","term":"right","forms":["right","further right","farther right","more right","righter","furthest right","farthest right","most right","rightmost","rightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"右邊的","explanation":"表示位於人體右側或某物的右側；把方向走直、放對，就是“右邊”。","examples":[{"en":"The sign on the right points to the station.","zh":"右邊的標牌指向車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Raise your right hand if you know the answer.","zh":"知道答案的話請舉起右手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/right","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f742b05bf78b718","term":"right","forms":["right","further right","farther right","more right","righter","furthest right","farthest right","most right","rightmost","rightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正確的；正當的","explanation":"表示符合事實、道理或正義；事情被“放正”了，就是正確、正當的。","examples":[{"en":"You were right about the meeting time.","zh":"你說的會議時間是對的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is not right to blame her for the mistake.","zh":"把這個錯誤怪到她頭上是不應該的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/right","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a08e60a08035cb88","term":"right","forms":["right"],"pos":"adv","zh":"正確地；妥當地","explanation":"表示以正確、合適的方式做某事；事情被“放正”並做對了。","examples":[{"en":"If you follow these steps, you should get it right.","zh":"如果你按這些步驟做，就應該能做對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please make sure you close the lid right.","zh":"請確保把蓋子正確地蓋好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/right","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1095e2bd7687897","term":"right","forms":["right","rights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"權利；正當權益","explanation":"指法律、道德或規則賦予某人的正當資格或權益，也就是一個人應當被放在正確位置上的東西。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone has the right to speak freely.","zh":"每個人都有自由發言的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You have no right to read my messages.","zh":"你沒有權利看我的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/right","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4bab36ce40d3a7f543a2","word":"rigid","forms":["rigid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f31862aeab21da68","term":"rigid","forms":["rigid","rigider","more rigid","rigidest","most rigid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅硬不易彎曲","explanation":"形容物體很硬，受到壓力也不容易彎曲或變形。這個最基本的“硬棍”畫面也構成了其他引申義的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The box is made of rigid plastic.","zh":"這個盒子是用硬質塑膠製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rigid frame kept the tent upright in the wind.","zh":"堅硬的框架讓帳篷在風中保持直立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rigid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e95fdd9ae6feea72","term":"rigid","forms":["rigid","rigider","more rigid","rigidest","most rigid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"思想僵化","explanation":"形容人的想法、觀點或信念像硬棍一樣不能彎轉，難以接受新情況或不同意見，因此常帶有“死板、僵化”的批評意味。","examples":[{"en":"She is too rigid about how the work must be done.","zh":"她對於工作必須怎樣完成這件事太死板了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A rigid way of thinking can prevent new ideas.","zh":"僵化的思維方式會阻礙新想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rigid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8e7867970436de6","term":"rigid","forms":["rigid","rigider","more rigid","rigidest","most rigid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"固定不動","explanation":"形容某物保持在一個位置或姿勢，不移動也不改變；它把“不能彎曲”進一步擴充套件成“不能動”。","examples":[{"en":"The dog stood rigid when it heard the noise.","zh":"那隻狗聽到聲音時僵直地站著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep your arm rigid while you lift the weight.","zh":"舉重時保持手臂不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rigid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cecef1fbdc4663a75682","word":"rigorous","forms":["rigorous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0cd9052ca39ea08","term":"rigorous","forms":["rigorous","more rigorous","most rigorous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴格周密的","explanation":"指按照很高的標準認真檢查或執行，細節不放過，因此結果通常可靠、準確。它可以形容人的做事方式，也可以形容研究、測試、規則或審查等過程。","examples":[{"en":"The study used rigorous testing methods.","zh":"這項研究採用了嚴格而周密的測試方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Applicants must undergo a rigorous selection process.","zh":"申請人必須經過嚴格的篩選過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rigorous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1569ec5b93084cc11380","word":"rim","forms":["rim"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19b1010475904a9f","term":"rim","forms":["rim","rims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊緣；外沿","explanation":"指圍繞某個物體的邊緣或外圈，特別常用於圓形物體，也可以指較大區域的邊界。","examples":[{"en":"We sat on the rim of the crater and watched the sunset.","zh":"我們坐在火山口邊緣看日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The moon was just visible above the rim of the forest.","zh":"月亮剛好露在森林邊緣的上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8912a2feb07aa9da","term":"rim","forms":["rim","rims","rimming","rimmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"沿輪廓圍繞","explanation":"指沿著某個地方或物體的外輪廓延伸，形成環繞或近似環繞的路線；畫面上像在邊緣圍出一圈。","examples":[{"en":"Tall trees rim the lake.","zh":"高大的樹木環繞著湖邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stone wall rims the garden.","zh":"一堵石牆圍著花園的邊緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91863c00afe75bb4","term":"rim","forms":["rim","rims","rimming","rimmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"沿邊緣滾動","explanation":"指球等圓形物體滾到一個圓形目標的邊緣，沿著邊緣轉動後可能落入，也可能彈出。","examples":[{"en":"The ball rimmed the cup and bounced away.","zh":"球沿著球洞邊緣滾了一下，又彈開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her putt rimmed the hole but did not drop.","zh":"她的推杆球擦著洞邊滾過，卻沒有進洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16b974583155fdcb11fb","word":"ring","forms":["ring"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84580fbfd96f137f","term":"ring","forms":["ring","rings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓環；環狀物","explanation":"指實心的圓形物體，常見於戒指、金屬環等；這是“圓環”這一中心畫面的直接含義。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a silver ring on her left hand.","zh":"她左手戴著一枚銀戒指。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The key was attached to a metal ring.","zh":"鑰匙系在一個金屬環上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5055ff6702dca397","term":"ring","forms":["ring","rings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鈴聲","explanation":"指鈴鐺、鍾或類似物發出的清亮迴響，是“鈴聲”這一中心畫面的直接含義。","examples":[{"en":"The ring of the school bell ended the lesson.","zh":"學校鈴聲結束了這堂課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard the ring of bicycle bells outside.","zh":"我們聽見了外面腳踏車鈴的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d2b6ce0f2e779e5","term":"ring","forms":["ring","rings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一通電話","explanation":"在口語中指一次電話聯絡，來源於電話鈴聲這一“鈴聲”畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll give you a ring after work.","zh":"我下班後給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave her brother a ring to check on him.","zh":"她給哥哥打了個電話，問問他的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff451221f1ec4687","term":"ring","forms":["ring","rings","ringing","rang","rung"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打電話給","explanation":"透過電話聯絡某人；這裡仍可聯絡到“鈴聲”這一畫面，即讓對方的電話響起來。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll ring you after work.","zh":"我下班後給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rang her mother to share the news.","zh":"她給母親打電話告訴了這個訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fccda8faefebb2ec1768","word":"riot","forms":["riot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7c32a782ce3270b","term":"riot","forms":["riot","riots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴動；騷亂","explanation":"指大群人衝破公共秩序、造成喧鬧，常伴隨暴力、破壞財物或與執法人員衝突。它體現了“人群失去控制地湧出”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The peaceful march turned into a riot after dark.","zh":"這場和平遊行天黑後變成了暴動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police were sent in to stop the riots.","zh":"警方被派去制止騷亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ee8b14f013ba748","term":"riot","forms":["riot","riots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紛繁豐富；五彩繽紛","explanation":"把“失控地湧出”引申為顏色、聲音或事物大量而不受限制地出現，強調豐富、強烈和充滿活力，而不一定含有負面意思。","examples":[{"en":"The hillside was a riot of wildflowers in spring.","zh":"春天，山坡上開滿了五彩繽紛的野花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The market is a riot of sounds and smells.","zh":"市場裡充滿了紛繁交織的聲音和氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b44d6dd3b1d600c1","term":"riot","forms":["riot","riots","rioting","rioted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加暴動；鬧事","explanation":"指人參加暴動，或以暴動的方式製造大規模騷亂；它把名詞中的“失控人群”變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of people rioted outside the courthouse.","zh":"數百人在法院外鬧事並引發了騷亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd rioted over the disputed election results.","zh":"人群因有爭議的選舉結果而發生暴動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec23f21a695f29e3a2f8","word":"rip","forms":["rip"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78bf23dd5e28879a","term":"rip","forms":["rip","rips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"撕裂處；裂口","explanation":"rip 是物體被猛力撕開後留下的裂口或破口，正對應“猛力撕開”這個畫面。","examples":[{"en":"There’s a rip in the pocket of my jacket.","zh":"我夾克的口袋上有一道裂口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She patched the rip with a piece of cloth.","zh":"她用一塊布補好了那道裂口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64554ba870805749","term":"rip","forms":["rip","rips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敲詐性高價","explanation":"俚語中，rip 指明顯不公平、貴得離譜的收費，也就是“宰客價”。它可以理解為價格把錢從人手裡“撕走”。","examples":[{"en":"Twenty dollars for a bottle of water is a rip.","zh":"一瓶水賣二十美元，簡直是在宰客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel was comfortable, but the parking fee was a total rip-off.","zh":"酒店很舒適，但停車費完全是在敲竹槓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c12fa485cf4a8d6c","term":"rip","forms":["rip","rips","ripping","ripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撕裂；撕開","explanation":"用力把紙、布等較薄或柔軟的東西撕開、撕破，或把某部分猛力撕下來；核心感覺就是“猛力撕開”。","examples":[{"en":"She ripped the envelope open with her finger.","zh":"她用手指把信封撕開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to rip the paper.","zh":"小心別把紙撕破。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0d0d4f2089f3b5a","term":"rip","forms":["rip","rips","ripping","ripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"飛奔；猛衝","explanation":"快速而猛烈地移動或行動，像猛力撕開阻礙一樣衝出去；重點是速度和衝勁。","examples":[{"en":"He ripped down the stairs when he heard the alarm.","zh":"聽到警報後，他飛快地衝下了樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The motorcycle ripped past us on the highway.","zh":"那輛摩托車在公路上從我們身邊疾馳而過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe41cc968e9814f57a3e","word":"ripe","forms":["ripe"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb7e8b92575cfa04","term":"ripe","forms":["ripe","riper","ripest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"成熟可採收","explanation":"指水果、蔬菜、穀物或種子已經達到成熟階段，可以採摘、收割或收集；這是“熟透的果實”這條記憶主線的起點。","examples":[{"en":"The peaches are ripe and ready to pick.","zh":"桃子熟了，可以摘了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wheat is ripe for harvesting.","zh":"小麥已經成熟，可以收割了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ripe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa95080843527aa4","term":"ripe","forms":["ripe","riper","ripest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熟成適用","explanation":"指食物經過足夠時間發展出適合食用的狀態，尤其常說乳酪等經過熟成、味道更充分。","examples":[{"en":"This ripe cheese has a rich, nutty flavor.","zh":"這塊熟成乳酪味道濃郁，還有堅果香。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cheese is ripe enough to serve now.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ripe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f18f806c9d23dd4a","term":"ripe","forms":["ripe","riper","ripest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"發展成熟完善","explanation":"把果實成熟的概念用於人、思想、作品或能力，表示已經充分發展，經驗豐富而且完善。","examples":[{"en":"Years of study gave her a ripe understanding of history.","zh":"多年的學習讓她對歷史有了成熟而深刻的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painter's ripe talent is evident in these later works.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ripe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-591b66b11758731f2d66","word":"ripple","forms":["ripple"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dccdeed4cabb98cf","term":"ripple","forms":["ripple","ripples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"波紋；漣漪","explanation":"指液體表面向外移動的一圈圈起伏，是 ripple 最具體、最核心的意思。它也可比喻一個小事件產生的影響逐步擴大。","examples":[{"en":"A ripple crossed the surface of the lake when the fish jumped.","zh":"魚躍出水面時，湖面上劃過一道波紋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The policy change sent ripples through the local economy.","zh":"這項政策變化給當地經濟帶來了逐步擴大的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ripple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2091173b2d515e27","term":"ripple","forms":["ripple","ripples","rippling","rippled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起伏；盪漾","explanation":"指某物像水面波紋一樣連續起伏，也可比喻影響從一個起點向外擴充套件。它把“波紋”的運動方式直接用於衣料、草地、市場或情緒等事物。","examples":[{"en":"The curtains rippled in the breeze.","zh":"窗簾在微風中輕輕起伏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Concern rippled through the community after the announcement.","zh":"訊息公佈後，擔憂情緒在社群中逐漸擴散。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ripple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dbfbe1cd2ee1f49a02ef","word":"rise","forms":["rise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f6cf173adbc7abe9","term":"rise","forms":["rise","rises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上升","explanation":"指向上移動或逐漸變高的過程，例如潮水、氣球或煙霧向上升起。","examples":[{"en":"The rise of the tide covered the lower part of the beach.","zh":"潮水上漲，淹沒了海灘較低的部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the slow rise of the smoke.","zh":"我們看著煙霧緩緩升起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab52bd221e29637a","term":"rise","forms":["rise","rises","rising","rose","risen","rised","risest","rosest","riseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上升","explanation":"指人或物相對於地面向上移動，例如氣球升空、太陽昇起或水位上升。","examples":[{"en":"The balloon rose slowly into the sky.","zh":"氣球緩緩升入天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sun rises earlier in summer.","zh":"夏天太陽昇起得更早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05997d158672c7ad","term":"rise","forms":["rise","rises","rising","rose","risen","rised","risest","rosest","riseth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上漲或提升","explanation":"指價格、數量、地位或聲望變得更高，是實際向上運動在抽象領域的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"House prices rose sharply last year.","zh":"去年房價大幅上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rose quickly in the company.","zh":"她在公司裡的地位很快提升了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2c6ef0f0d0e4cc6e9c15","word":"risk","forms":["risk"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a783b0ddc1f6ab14","term":"risk","forms":["risk","risks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不利結果的可能性","explanation":"risk 是某個決定或事件帶來壞結果的可能性，例如受傷、失敗或被捕的可能。它不表示壞結果一定會發生。","examples":[{"en":"There is a serious risk of flooding after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，發生洪水的風險很高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The risk of injury is greater on icy roads.","zh":"在結冰的道路上受傷的風險更大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f4f4e45e1c0048a","term":"risk","forms":["risk","risks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可能的損失程度","explanation":"risk 也可以強調壞結果一旦發生會造成多大損失；可能性不變時，損失越大，整體風險通常越高。","examples":[{"en":"The company accepted the risk of losing a large amount of money.","zh":"這家公司接受了可能損失一大筆錢的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Investing everything in one company carries considerable risk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87e0c9961430b73b","term":"risk","forms":["risk","risks","risking","risked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒著……的風險","explanation":"risk 表示明知某個壞結果可能發生，仍做某事，因此冒著受傷、失敗或其他不利後果的風險。","examples":[{"en":"You risk losing your job if you ignore the safety rules.","zh":"如果你無視安全規定，就有可能丟掉工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They risked their lives to rescue the climber.","zh":"他們冒著生命危險營救那名登山者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9f282d121b61bda","term":"risk","forms":["risk","risks","risking","risked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……面臨損害","explanation":"risk 也表示某個行動可能損害或危及某人、某物，重點是把原本擁有的安全、機會或未來置於危險之中。","examples":[{"en":"She refused to risk her children's safety for a shortcut.","zh":"她不願為了走近路而拿孩子們的安全冒險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You risk your reputation by making unverified accusations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":4,"counts":{"112":3,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-4dc53ebcd4e75d41371a","word":"risky","forms":["risky"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f11fa36935d0edac","term":"risky","forms":["risky","riskier","riskiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有風險的；不穩妥的","explanation":"指某件事可能失敗、造成損失或帶來危險，因此不太安全或不太穩妥。風險可以來自結果不確定，也可以來自行動本身可能造成傷害。","examples":[{"en":"Investing all your savings in one company is risky.","zh":"把全部積蓄投資在一家公司上是有風險的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Driving through the flooded valley would be risky.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/risky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7920fdeff9c52c2497a0","word":"ritual","forms":["ritual"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c583d5fb0242f397","term":"ritual","forms":["ritual","more ritual","most ritual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"儀式性的；與儀式有關的","explanation":"表示某件事屬於儀式的一部分，或帶有按固定步驟重複進行的特點。它可以修飾宗教儀式，也可以修飾較寬泛的典禮、習慣或固定行為。","examples":[{"en":"They performed the ritual lighting of the candles.","zh":"他們舉行了點燃蠟燭的儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ritual washing takes place before the ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ritual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f4f089685138811","term":"ritual","forms":["ritual","rituals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儀式；固定的重複做法","explanation":"指按照固定步驟完成的一套行動，最典型的是宗教或正式典禮中的儀式；在日常語境中，也可以指一個人反覆進行、幾乎形成固定模式的習慣。","examples":[{"en":"The priests carried out the religious ritual carefully.","zh":"牧師們認真地舉行了宗教儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Making tea became her comforting evening ritual.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ritual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":3,"counts":{"111":1,"112":2}}},{"id":"ceec-1db147fa22abae8a70c9","word":"rival","forms":["rival"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed3c26090810bbd5","term":"rival","forms":["rival"],"pos":"adj","zh":"競爭的；爭奪同一目標的","explanation":"指兩個或多個物件為了同一目標、地位或感情而相互競爭，重點是“彼此爭奪”，不是單純表示相似。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams are rival schools.","zh":"這兩支隊伍分別代表相互競爭的學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rival companies competed for the government contract.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75ad90f769471cd1","term":"rival","forms":["rival","rivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"競爭對手","explanation":"指和某人、團隊或公司有同一個目標，並努力取得同樣成果的競爭者；競爭對手可能是個人，也可能是集體或機構。","examples":[{"en":"Chris is my biggest rival in the 400-meter race.","zh":"在400米比賽中，克里斯是我最大的競爭對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two companies have been rivals for years.","zh":"這兩家公司多年來一直是競爭對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82e46c6eba862f0b","term":"rival","forms":["rival","rivals","rivaling","rivalling","rivaled","rivalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與……競爭","explanation":"表示主動對抗或爭奪，努力在愛情、比賽、職位等方面贏過另一個人或團隊；它把“競爭對手”的關係變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"Several students are rivaling her for the scholarship.","zh":"有幾名學生正在和她競爭這項獎學金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two singers rival each other on stage.","zh":"這兩位歌手在舞臺上彼此競爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7bd30a3563488aab","term":"rival","forms":["rival","rivals","rivaling","rivalling","rivaled","rivalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"匹敵；勝過","explanation":"表示某人或某物在品質、影響力、速度等方面達到或超過另一者的水平，也就是成為足以相提並論的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The new restaurant rivals the best places in town.","zh":"這家新餐館足以與城裡最好的餐館媲美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Few mountain views rival this one for grandeur.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-204507d4e9f561f8ac0d","word":"rivalry","forms":["rivalry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8bec479d2fa18316","term":"rivalry","forms":["rivalry","rivalries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對手之間的長期競爭","explanation":"指兩個或多個對手為了超過彼此、爭奪同一個目標而形成的持續競爭關係，重點在“雙方互相較量”這一關係，而不只是某一次比賽。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams have developed a fierce rivalry over the years.","zh":"這兩支球隊多年來逐漸形成了激烈的競爭關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a friendly rivalry between my brothers.","zh":"我兩個兄弟之間存在一種友好的競爭關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rivalry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08f597d9a73b3353","term":"rivalry","forms":["rivalry","rivalries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物或因素之間的競爭","explanation":"泛指兩個或多個事物、因素或力量之間爭奪優勢、影響力或結果的競爭，不一定涉及有意識的人類對手。它是把“爭奪同一個獎盃”的影象擴充套件到更廣泛的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The study examines the rivalry between the two visual signals.","zh":"這項研究考察了兩種視覺訊號之間的競爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rivalry between cost and quality shaped the design.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rivalry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f5a8ed8f139be6df7cf","word":"river","forms":["river"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90129b26e4f3482a","term":"river","forms":["river","rivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"河流","explanation":"river 是從較高處向較低處流動、通常最終匯入海洋或湖泊的大型天然水道。它強調的是一整條有持續水流的河，不只是岸邊的一小段水。","examples":[{"en":"We walked along the river until sunset.","zh":"我們沿著河走到日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river flows into the sea near the city.","zh":"這條河在城市附近流入大海。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c84692b390e89b29","term":"river","forms":["river","rivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量連續的液體","explanation":"這裡不是說真的有一條河，而是把大量液體連續流動的樣子比作河，突出數量多、流動不斷。","examples":[{"en":"A river of water rushed through the broken door.","zh":"大量水流從破裂的門口衝了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rivers of melted wax ran down the candle stand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-362a284952d3a7250e4b","word":"road","forms":["road"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb3390a7894b3c27","term":"road","forms":["road","roads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道路","explanation":"供人、馬或車輛從一個地方到另一個地方通行的路，是 road 最基本的意義；現代語境中通常指適合車輛行駛的道路。","examples":[{"en":"We turned off the main road and followed a narrow country road.","zh":"我們駛離主幹道，沿著一條狹窄的鄉間道路前進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fallen tree is blocking the road.","zh":"一棵倒下的樹擋住了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/road","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7060cc18a4288f69","term":"road","forms":["road","roads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人生或事業道路","explanation":"把人生、事業或某個目標想成一段要走的路，因此表示達到某種結果所選擇的方向或過程。","examples":[{"en":"Hard work put her on the road to success.","zh":"努力使她走上了通往成功的道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road to recovery may take several months.","zh":"康復之路可能需要幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/road","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01ff033d051e5a40b4e3","word":"roam","forms":["roam"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76a443e485782ed1","term":"roam","forms":["roam","roams","roaming","roamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"自由漫遊","explanation":"指沒有具體目的地地四處走，可以是人、動物，也可以帶有詩意地說人在世界各處漂泊。核心畫面就是“邊走邊看，暫時不決定要去哪兒”。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon roaming around the old town.","zh":"我們整個下午都在老城區隨意閒逛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After leaving home, she roamed from city to city.","zh":"離家後，她從一個城市漂泊到另一個城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eca7d3a932339c3b","term":"roam","forms":["roam","roams","roaming","roamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在某範圍內遊蕩","explanation":"表示在一個地區、空間或群體中到處走動、出沒，重點是“活動範圍覆蓋了那裡”，不一定強調旅行。","examples":[{"en":"Wild horses still roam the hills near the village.","zh":"野馬仍在村子附近的山丘間自由遊蕩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cattle roam freely across the moor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2b644a1f2f11fd832c0","word":"roar","forms":["roar"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0cb7e9569f132c3b","term":"roar","forms":["roar","roars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吼叫聲；怒喊聲","explanation":"指人因憤怒、痛苦或強烈情緒張大嘴發出的長而響亮、低沉的聲音；也可以指放聲大笑時爆發出的聲音。它是“聲音衝出去”這一核心畫面的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"A roar of anger came from the back of the hall.","zh":"大廳後面傳來一聲憤怒的吼叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The comedian's final joke brought a roar from the audience.","zh":"喜劇演員最後一個笑話引得觀眾鬨堂大笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d5639523ead4d66","term":"roar","forms":["roar","roars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轟鳴聲","explanation":"指發動機、車輛等沒有嘴的事物發出的巨大而持續的迴響聲；聲音像吼叫一樣衝出來，所以也用roar來描寫。","examples":[{"en":"The roar of the motorbike woke the baby.","zh":"摩托車的轟鳴聲把嬰兒吵醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roar of the engines drowned our conversation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60d7e78edb51ec3c","term":"roar","forms":["roar","roars","roaring","roared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吼叫；怒喊","explanation":"指人因痛苦、憤怒或強烈情緒發出深沉響亮的喊叫。重點不是“說了什麼”，而是聲音像爆發一樣衝出來。","examples":[{"en":"He roared with pain when the bandage was removed.","zh":"拆繃帶時，他痛得大聲吼叫起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She roared at the children to get out of the road.","zh":"她衝孩子們大聲吼道，讓他們離開馬路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e42dc0db036df723","term":"roar","forms":["roar","roars","roaring","roared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轟鳴；發出巨響","explanation":"指機器、車輛、風暴等沒有生命的事物發出持續而響亮的回聲。它把機器的聲音想象成動物在吼叫，仍然保留“聲音猛烈衝出”的核心。","examples":[{"en":"Trucks roared past our house all night.","zh":"卡車整夜轟鳴著駛過我們家門口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engines roared as the aircraft accelerated.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52b5cd277fbcd7882372","word":"roast","forms":["roast"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2247ec171b00253a","term":"roast","forms":["roast"],"pos":"adj","zh":"烤熟的","explanation":"指食物已經經過烘烤，通常表面變脆或帶有烤制的顏色和味道。","examples":[{"en":"We had roast chicken for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐吃了烤雞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She served roast chicken with potatoes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e94129af5f7e349","term":"roast","forms":["roast","roasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烤肉","explanation":"指適合烘烤的一大塊肉，或已經烤好的肉；重點是“作為烤制物件或成品的肉”。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a beef roast for Sunday dinner.","zh":"她買了一塊牛肉烤肉，準備週日吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roast needs another twenty minutes in the oven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-784f370facd1cdda","term":"roast","forms":["roast","roasts","roasting","roasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"烘烤","explanation":"指把食物放在烤箱、火上或其他高溫環境中，不加覆蓋地烤熟，使表面變脆，甚至略微焦黃。","examples":[{"en":"We roasted the vegetables with garlic and herbs.","zh":"我們用大蒜和香草烤了這些蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chicken is roasting in the oven.","zh":"雞肉正在烤箱裡烘烤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-84313ef39b0a979f0608","word":"rob","forms":["rob"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ee75795f82372d6","term":"rob","forms":["rob","robs","robbing","robbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搶劫；強行奪取","explanation":"指用武力、威脅或暴力從某人或某處奪走錢財等物品，是“把東西從別人手裡強行拿走”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"Two men robbed the bank just before closing time.","zh":"兩名男子就在銀行快關門前搶劫了那家銀行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The attacker robbed her of her purse.","zh":"襲擊者搶走了她的錢包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66de049d68bdf460","term":"rob","forms":["rob","robs","robbing","robbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使失去；剝奪","explanation":"這是“奪走”義的比喻用法，表示某件事消耗或奪走人的時間、精力、快樂等，使人失去原本擁有的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The long commute robs me of time with my family.","zh":"漫長的通勤讓我失去了和家人相處的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury robbed her of a promising athletic career.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eaf6ec1fa79b2d1a3285","word":"robber","forms":["robber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2716fbdf5720639d","term":"robber","forms":["robber","robbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搶劫者；劫匪","explanation":"指透過搶奪、威脅或其他強制手段奪取財物的人，重點是“實施搶劫的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The robber escaped before the police arrived.","zh":"劫匪在警察趕到前逃走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bank robber was caught on camera.","zh":"銀行劫匪被攝像頭拍到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a27bfbf467ec343fe73c","word":"robbery","forms":["robbery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55581a71b5663f38","term":"robbery","forms":["robbery","robberies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搶劫罪；搶劫案件","explanation":"指以暴力或暴力威脅奪取他人財物，或試圖這樣做的犯罪；也可指一宗具體的搶劫案，例如銀行搶劫案。","examples":[{"en":"The bank robbery was reported shortly after noon.","zh":"這起銀行搶劫案在中午過後不久被報告了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was arrested for attempting robbery.","zh":"他因企圖實施搶劫而被逮捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robbery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a919bb02757eff66","term":"robbery","forms":["robbery","robberies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搶劫行為","explanation":"指用暴力或暴力威脅奪取財物這一整類行為，重點在“搶劫”這個行為本身，不一定是在講某一宗具體案件。","examples":[{"en":"The police are working to prevent robbery in the area.","zh":"警方正在努力預防該地區的搶劫行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The robbery took place shortly before the bank closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robbery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d0f44502d8625d3a501","word":"robe","forms":["robe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e44607ee714ffd1","term":"robe","forms":["robe","robes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長袍；寬鬆外衣","explanation":"robe 是一種通常較長、較寬鬆的外衣，常讓人聯想到法官、學者、宗教人士或其他有正式身份的人所穿的長袍。","examples":[{"en":"The judge entered the courtroom wearing a black robe.","zh":"法官穿著黑色長袍走進法庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She put on a warm robe after her bath.","zh":"洗完澡後，她穿上了一件暖和的浴袍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18d63be10ad544a04a22","word":"robot","forms":["robot"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e51149819a16a507","term":"robot","forms":["robot","robots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"類人的機器人","explanation":"指被設計成像人或其他生物、能夠表現出智慧行為的機械體，通常強調它具有可觀察的行動能力和類似生物的外形。","examples":[{"en":"The robot walked across the stage and greeted the audience.","zh":"那個機器人走過舞臺，向觀眾打招呼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the film, robots look almost exactly like humans.","zh":"在這部電影裡，機器人長得幾乎和人一模一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c17b36c094d8748","term":"robot","forms":["robot","robots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"執行任務的機器","explanation":"指能夠透過身體移動來完成一項或一組複雜任務的機器，例如清掃、搬運或裝配裝置；它不必有人的外形。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a robot that cleans the kitchen floor every evening.","zh":"我們買了一臺每天晚上清掃廚房地板的機器人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory uses robots to move heavy parts.","zh":"這家工廠用機器人搬運沉重的零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f650dce81c641b4cf58","word":"robust","forms":["robust"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cb4813877525f68","term":"robust","forms":["robust","more robust","robuster","most robust","robustest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"經得起不利條件","explanation":"指某人或某物能夠承受惡劣環境、壓力或困難，不容易受損或失效。這是“粗壯的樹經得起風雨”這一核心形象的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"We need a robust plan that can survive unexpected delays.","zh":"我們需要一個能經受意外延誤的穩健計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The equipment is robust enough to operate in extreme weather.","zh":"這套裝置足夠堅固，即使在極端天氣下也能執行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48b86bae03e0c660","term":"robust","forms":["robust","more robust","robuster","most robust","robustest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"強健壯實","explanation":"形容人的身體強壯、健康，通常讓人聯想到體格結實而有力量，也可以形容動物或植物等生命體長得壯。","examples":[{"en":"The robust young farmer carried both bags without stopping.","zh":"那個強健的年輕農夫沒停下來就把兩個袋子都扛走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The seedlings are robust and growing quickly after the rain.","zh":"這些幼苗長得很健壯，雨後生長得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-350a770c0ec9f353e1a5","word":"rock","forms":["rock"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a0bd07be100ba03","term":"rock","forms":["rock","rocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"岩石","explanation":"指構成地面、山體或懸崖的堅硬天然礦物集合，是“rock”最基本的畫面。通常說一整類物質時不可數。","examples":[{"en":"The path was cut into solid rock.","zh":"這條小路是鑿進堅硬的岩石中的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cliff is made of pale gray rock.","zh":"這座懸崖由淺灰色岩石構成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2b5d79f6d415b9a","term":"rock","forms":["rock"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搖滾音樂","explanation":"指以鮮明節奏和樂隊演奏為特色的音樂型別；可以把它想成由身體來回搖擺發展出來的音樂。","examples":[{"en":"My parents introduced me to rock when I was a teenager.","zh":"我十幾歲時，父母讓我接觸了搖滾音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The club plays rock every Friday night.","zh":"這傢俱樂部每週五晚上都播放搖滾音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6def5e47eda1c11","term":"rock","forms":["rock","rocks","rocking","rocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕輕搖動","explanation":"指讓某人或某物輕柔地來回擺動，也可以指自己緩慢搖擺；最直接地對應“來回搖擺”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She rocked the baby gently to sleep.","zh":"她輕輕搖著嬰兒，把孩子哄睡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He rocked back and forth in his chair.","zh":"他在椅子上來回搖晃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1887d7e6ddd1684e","term":"rock","forms":["rock","rocks","rocking","rocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"演奏或欣賞搖滾","explanation":"指演奏、表演或欣賞搖滾音樂，通常帶有充滿能量、技藝嫻熟的感覺；它正是從“搖擺”發展出的音樂用法。","examples":[{"en":"The band rocked the crowd with three unforgettable songs.","zh":"這支樂隊用三首令人難忘的歌曲點燃了觀眾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We rocked out in the car on the way home.","zh":"回家的路上，我們在車裡盡情聽著搖滾音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c58dd0a3760008c90183","word":"rocket","forms":["rocket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33f168b564ee1aaf","term":"rocket","forms":["rocket","rockets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火箭；火箭彈","explanation":"一種靠發動機高速飛行、通常用於升空、探索太空或攻擊目標的飛行器，也可指火箭彈。它就是“猛衝向目標的東西”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The rocket lifted off just before sunrise.","zh":"火箭在日出前剛剛升空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several rockets were fired at the border town.","zh":"幾枚火箭彈向邊境小鎮發射過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6510126aae54bb1a39c3","word":"rocky","forms":["rocky"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-deb9e4ac6c789bdc","term":"rocky","forms":["rocky","rockier","more rocky","rockiest","most rocky"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多岩石的","explanation":"指某個地方有很多岩石，或地面、海岸等主要由岩石構成。這是 rocky 最直接、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We climbed a rocky mountain before sunrise.","zh":"我們在日出前爬上了一座多岩石的山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rocky shore was covered with seaweed.","zh":"多岩石的海岸上覆蓋著海藻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f832ffe67feab5e5","term":"rocky","forms":["rocky","rockier","more rocky","rockiest","most rocky"],"pos":"adj","zh":"搖晃不穩的","explanation":"指物體容易左右晃動、放置不穩，好像正在被來回搖動。桌子、椅子或其他物件出現這種狀態時可以用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"This chair is rocky, so don't lean back in it.","zh":"這把椅子不穩，所以別靠著椅背向後仰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A folded napkin steadied the rocky table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae4a6acd7198ca1c9843","word":"rod","forms":["rod"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73bda7b5e5548d0c","term":"rod","forms":["rod","rods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直杆；棒；棍","explanation":"指細長而筆直的圓形棒、杆、柄或手杖，可以由木頭、金屬等材料製成。這是其他許多義項共同的形象基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The worker bent the steel rod into a circle.","zh":"工人把鋼杆彎成了一個圓圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carried a walking rod on the steep trail.","zh":"她在陡峭的小路上帶著一根手杖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rod","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3be647f2a0fdb1c6","term":"rod","forms":["rod","rods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"釣魚竿","explanation":"指用於釣魚的細長杆，通常連線魚線和魚鉤；完整說法是 fishing rod。","examples":[{"en":"He left his fishing rod beside the lake.","zh":"他把魚竿放在湖邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I cast my rod toward the reeds.","zh":"我把魚竿朝蘆葦叢的方向甩了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rod","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b168d88dc872a7753c2","word":"role","forms":["role"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7eb52f14a6ad877","term":"role","forms":["role","roles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演員扮演的角色","explanation":"指演員在戲劇、電影等作品中所扮演的人物或承擔的表演部分，也可以指作品中的主要或次要角色。","examples":[{"en":"She played the lead role in the school musical.","zh":"她在學校音樂劇中扮演主角。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was offered a small role in the film.","zh":"有人請他在這部電影中出演一個小角色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/role","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c164365a2dad6064","term":"role","forms":["role","roles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物發揮的作用","explanation":"指某個人、團體、行動或事物在某件事情中所起的功能或影響，也就是它在整體過程中承擔的作用。","examples":[{"en":"Trees play a vital role in protecting the soil.","zh":"樹木在保護土壤方面發揮著至關重要的作用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Technology has changed its role in modern education.","zh":"技術在現代教育中的作用已經改變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/role","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acfe1fecda8bf79f258f","word":"roll","forms":["roll"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7217db35908483d","term":"roll","forms":["roll","rolls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滾動","explanation":"指物體滾動這一動作、結果，或處於被滾動的狀態，就像圓筒不斷向前轉動。","examples":[{"en":"The roll of the ball slowed on the grass.","zh":"球在草地上的滾動速度慢了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the roll of the waves from the pier.","zh":"我們從碼頭上看著海浪翻滾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4550de14dd5e4c68","term":"roll","forms":["roll","rolls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"官方名單","explanation":"指為正式用途儲存的人員或物件名單，例如獲准執業者名冊；它像把名字一條條卷錄儲存下來。","examples":[{"en":"Her name is on the roll of licensed nurses.","zh":"她的名字在持證護士名冊上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her name was missing from the electoral roll.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-892d494fff7aef57","term":"roll","forms":["roll","rolls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小圓麵包","explanation":"指一種較小的麵包，通常做成卷狀、對摺狀或略微隆起的形狀；它就是記憶中“卷狀的麵包卷”。","examples":[{"en":"She put butter on a warm bread roll.","zh":"她在一個熱麵包捲上抹了黃油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can I have a roll with my soup?","zh":"我可以要一個麵包卷配湯嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9b0dbe1e3cd72ed","term":"roll","forms":["roll","rolls","rolling","rolled","rollest","rolledst","rolleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滾動；使滾動","explanation":"表示物體自己轉動著向前移動，或讓物體這樣移動；這是把 roll 想成不斷轉動的圓筒的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"The ball rolled down the hill.","zh":"球滾下了山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rolled the suitcase to the door.","zh":"她把手提箱滾到門口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23f7c8c88742998e1171","word":"romance","forms":["romance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45f1b3481a51fd2f","term":"romance","forms":["romance","romances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戀愛關係","explanation":"指兩個人之間親密而帶有愛情的關係，通常強調一段戀情或戀愛經歷。","examples":[{"en":"She began a romance with a colleague from her office.","zh":"她和辦公室的一位同事開始了一段戀情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their summer romance ended when they returned home.","zh":"他們的夏日戀情在各自回家後結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-525cfa64347a5079c25c","word":"romantic","forms":["romantic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ab2b2ce26992187","term":"romantic","forms":["romantic","more romantic","most romantic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"理想化而不現實的","explanation":"形容想法、計劃或人過分相信美好可能實現，缺少現實可行性；這裡的 romantic 是“被美好想象吸引”，不一定和戀愛有關。","examples":[{"en":"Her romantic plan sounded wonderful, but it would cost far too much.","zh":"她那個理想化的計劃聽起來很美好，但花費會高得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His romantic view of farming ignored its hard physical labor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romantic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f80c9e33ef9357f","term":"romantic","forms":["romantic","more romantic","most romantic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"夢幻而富有感染力的","explanation":"形容景色、氛圍、生活想象等能強烈喚起美好情感和想象力，給人詩意、迷人的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The old town looks especially romantic at sunset.","zh":"這座老城在日落時分顯得格外夢幻迷人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruined castle gave the valley a romantic atmosphere.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romantic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06b8587722ca1d9d","term":"romantic","forms":["romantic","more romantic","most romantic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"浪漫的；適合戀愛的","explanation":"形容愛情、親密關係、舉動或場合帶有理想化、溫柔而深情的色彩，也可以表示正在發展愛情。","examples":[{"en":"They planned a romantic dinner by the river.","zh":"他們計劃在河邊享用一頓浪漫的晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The candlelit courtyard provided a romantic setting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romantic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1a0d6f4707493e53bc9","word":"roof","forms":["roof"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bcef56650cf48caf","term":"roof","forms":["roof","roofs","rooves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"屋頂","explanation":"指建築物最上方、用來覆蓋和保護內部空間的外部結構，是 roof 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The storm damaged the roof of our house.","zh":"暴風雨損壞了我們房子的屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could hear rain tapping on the roof.","zh":"我們能聽見雨點敲打屋頂的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-227fd831f4bba434","term":"roof","forms":["roof","roofs","rooves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頂層","explanation":"指建築物最上面的樓層或區域，重點不在覆蓋結構，而在“最上面那一層”。","examples":[{"en":"Let's have lunch on the roof.","zh":"我們去頂層吃午飯吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dark clouds formed a low roof over the valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81c1850156380b7e","term":"roof","forms":["roof","roofs","roofing","roofed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……加頂","explanation":"表示給建築、溝渠或其他空間裝上 roof，使它被頂蓋覆蓋；這是名詞“屋頂”直接轉成的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"They roofed the small extension before winter.","zh":"他們在冬天來臨前給那間小擴建房加上了屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers roofed over the shelter with metal sheets.","zh":"工人用金屬板給這個避難所蓋上了頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f1c5b2fad778434024f","word":"room","forms":["room"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31f690d42f50ce25","term":"room","forms":["room","rooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機會；餘地","explanation":"這裡的 room 不是實際房間，而是某件事能夠發生、某人能夠加入或某種變化能夠實現的餘地。它把“空出來的空間”引申成了行動或發展的空間。","examples":[{"en":"There is still room for improvement.","zh":"還有改進的餘地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan leaves room for changes later.","zh":"這個計劃為以後的調整留下了餘地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/room","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15c2f292b81f2455","term":"room","forms":["room","rooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空間；容納處","explanation":"指放置東西、容納人，或進行某項活動所需要的空間。它可以是桌面、車裡、房子裡等具體空處，不一定是一個獨立房間。","examples":[{"en":"Do we have enough room for one more chair?","zh":"我們還有地方再放一把椅子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There isn't much room to move around.","zh":"這裡沒有多少活動的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/room","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23de4de5ac912abe","term":"room","forms":["room","rooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"房間","explanation":"指建築物中由牆、地板和天花板圍成的獨立空間，是 room 最常見的具體意義之一。","examples":[{"en":"The children are playing in the living room.","zh":"孩子們正在客廳裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please close the door when you leave the room.","zh":"你離開房間時請關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/room","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab80177c2fa8dfa42997","word":"rooster","forms":["rooster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-793ad46b1e3885df","term":"rooster","forms":["rooster","roosters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公雞","explanation":"rooster最常見的意思是成年雄性家雞，也可泛指某些雉類鳥的雄鳥；核心畫面就是昂首、會打鳴的公雞。","examples":[{"en":"The rooster woke us before sunrise.","zh":"那隻公雞在日出前就把我們叫醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several roosters were crowing behind the farmhouse.","zh":"幾隻公雞在農舍後面打鳴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rooster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4813494d137e1631bba3","word":"root","forms":["root"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0df455d012c984da","term":"root","forms":["root","roots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物的根","explanation":"植物紮在地下、用來固定自身並吸收水分和養分的部分；它體現了“紮在地下的根”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The old oak has roots that reach deep into the soil.","zh":"這棵老橡樹的根深深扎入土壤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the roots moist while the plant is growing.","zh":"植物生長時要保持根部溼潤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/root","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3fd3eab49a403fe","term":"root","forms":["root","roots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"根源；基礎","explanation":"造成某種情況的最初原因，或使事物能夠穩固存在的基礎；事情“有了根”，就是有了根源和基礎。","examples":[{"en":"We need to find the root of the problem before fixing it.","zh":"我們得先找出問題的根源，再解決它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of trust was at the root of their disagreement.","zh":"缺乏信任是他們產生分歧的根本原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/root","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe4d55b9ffa53044e447","word":"rope","forms":["rope"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ae5c6fc41cf874c","term":"rope","forms":["rope","ropes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繩索材料","explanation":"指由多股纖維、金屬絲或其他線狀材料擰合而成的結實長線，強調“繩子”這種材料本身，而不是某一段具體長度。","examples":[{"en":"The climber checked the rope before starting up the wall.","zh":"登山者在開始攀登牆壁前檢查了繩索。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This rope is strong enough to hold the small boat.","zh":"這根繩索足夠結實，可以固定住那條小船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a1053111e963be9","term":"rope","forms":["rope","ropes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段繩子","explanation":"指一條具體、完整的繩子，重點是把繩索材料看成一個獨立物件或一段長度。","examples":[{"en":"We tied two ropes together to reach the other side.","zh":"我們把兩條繩子系在一起，以便到達對面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave a rope by the door in case we need it later.","zh":"在門邊放一條繩子，以防我們之後需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cff96568561b4b7f","term":"rope","forms":["rope","ropes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繩狀的一串或一股","explanation":"指許多東西連成一條長而連續的繩狀整體，例如一串珍珠；這裡保留了“像繩子一樣連在一起”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a long rope of pearls with her evening dress.","zh":"她穿晚禮服時戴了一長串珍珠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A rope of pearls lay inside the jewelry box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-618d663af0f1ec88a5a1","word":"rose","forms":["rose"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d146ea1193a2bf64","term":"rose","forms":["rose","roses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玫瑰植物","explanation":"指薔薇屬的一類灌木，通常開紅、粉、白或黃色的花；說一株植物時，rose就是整株玫瑰。","examples":[{"en":"There are three rose bushes beside the gate.","zh":"門旁有三叢玫瑰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My grandmother grows roses in her garden.","zh":"我祖母在花園裡種玫瑰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97ba91c23b2b6aa9","term":"rose","forms":["rose","roses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玫瑰花","explanation":"指玫瑰植物開出的花，常作為禮物、裝飾或愛情的象徵。","examples":[{"en":"He gave her a red rose.","zh":"他送給她一朵紅玫瑰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roses on the table smell wonderful.","zh":"桌上的玫瑰花聞起來很香。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ec879c8c860699e2314","word":"rot","forms":["rot"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-359ee90802db7826","term":"rot","forms":["rot","rots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腐爛；腐敗過程","explanation":"指有機物逐漸分解、變壞的過程，重點是“正在腐爛”這一變化，而不是已經腐爛的物體本身。","examples":[{"en":"The smell of rot came from the fallen tree.","zh":"腐爛的氣味從倒下的樹木那裡傳來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Paint can slow the rot in wooden doors.","zh":"油漆可以減緩木門的腐爛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c030bc14a50c90c3","term":"rot","forms":["rot","rots","rotting","rotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"腐爛；腐敗","explanation":"指有機物因細菌、真菌等生物作用而逐漸分解、變壞，是“rot”最基本的動詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"The apples will rot if you leave them in the damp shed.","zh":"如果把蘋果留在潮溼的棚子裡，它們會腐爛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fallen leaves began to rot after the rain.","zh":"落葉在下雨後開始腐爛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-299bcf54c044b1b5d49a","word":"rotate","forms":["rotate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f00986db37da2a78","term":"rotate","forms":["rotate","rotates","rotating","rotated","rotatest","rotatedst","rotateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"旋轉；轉身","explanation":"表示人或物體圍繞某個中心轉動，或轉過身體改變面對的方向。這是最基本的“輪子轉起來”這一義項。","examples":[{"en":"He rotated in his chair to face me.","zh":"他在椅子上轉過身來面對我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wheel rotated slowly in the wind.","zh":"輪子在風中緩慢地轉動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rotate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37107c6bc304db36","term":"rotate","forms":["rotate","rotates","rotating","rotated","rotatest","rotatedst","rotateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使旋轉；轉動","explanation":"表示讓某個物體轉動，例如轉旋鈕、轉盤或影象；這裡是把“輪子轉動”的動作施加到另一個東西上。","examples":[{"en":"Rotate the dial to the left until the light comes on.","zh":"向左轉動旋鈕，直到指示燈亮起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rotated the image ninety degrees.","zh":"她把影象旋轉了九十度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rotate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-224610f102890bc0e40c","word":"rotation","forms":["rotation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0864e76ac89f93ac","term":"rotation","forms":["rotation","rotations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圍繞中心或軸轉動","explanation":"指物體圍繞某個中心點或軸持續轉動，重點是“轉動”這一過程，而不是轉了多少圈。水流、煙霧、風暴等形成的旋轉都可以用這個詞表示。","examples":[{"en":"The rotation of the wheels keeps the machine moving.","zh":"輪子的轉動使機器不斷運轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists measured the rotation of the storm.","zh":"科學家測量了風暴的旋轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rotation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa595119a13c9bfb","term":"rotation","forms":["rotation","rotations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次完整旋轉","explanation":"指圍繞中心或軸完成一整圈的單次迴圈。這裡關注的是“轉完一圈”這個完整單位，而不是泛指持續轉動。","examples":[{"en":"The wheel makes one complete rotation every second.","zh":"這個輪子每秒完整轉一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The moon completes a rotation in about twenty-seven days.","zh":"月球大約二十七天自轉一週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rotation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eda565a9067e40495568","word":"rotten","forms":["rotten"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34ebfd3ea24086c0","term":"rotten","forms":["rotten","rottener","more rotten","rottenest","most rotten"],"pos":"adj","zh":"腐爛的；變質的","explanation":"指食物等容易變質的東西因細菌等作用而腐爛，已經不適合正常食用或使用。這個意思體現了“從內部開始壞掉”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The apples went rotten before we could eat them.","zh":"我們還沒來得及吃，這些蘋果就腐爛了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rotten pear collapsed when I picked it up.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rotten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bcac4568fd46627","term":"rotten","forms":["rotten","rottener","more rotten","rottenest","most rotten"],"pos":"adj","zh":"腐朽的；破敗的","explanation":"指木頭、建築材料等因長期損壞而腐朽、鬆散或不再牢固，重點不是表面髒，而是結構已經壞了。它把食物腐爛的“內部壞掉”形象擴充套件到了物體。","examples":[{"en":"We had to replace the rotten boards on the porch.","zh":"我們不得不更換門廊上已經腐朽的木板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rotten window frame crumbled beneath my fingers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rotten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f811eb5c56eeb90a48b9","word":"rough","forms":["rough"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d8f6a16027ff3b1","term":"rough","forms":["rough","rougher","roughest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粗糙的；不平的","explanation":"東西表面沒有打磨平整，摸起來不光滑，正是“表面不平、沒有打磨好”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The old wall felt rough under my fingers.","zh":"我用手指摸那面舊牆時，感覺表面很粗糙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has rough hands from working outdoors.","zh":"她常在戶外工作，雙手很粗糙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-389b45cd6a11bd05","term":"rough","forms":["rough","rougher","roughest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"粗略的；未完成的","explanation":"計劃、草稿或估計還沒有仔細打磨，只是先做出的粗略版本。","examples":[{"en":"I made a rough plan before starting the project.","zh":"開始這個專案前，我先做了一個粗略的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is only a rough draft, so please suggest changes.","zh":"這只是初稿，請提出修改意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f37c6179c715081","term":"rough","forms":["rough","rougher","roughest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"艱難的；難熬的","explanation":"生活、經歷或一段時期像沒有打磨好的粗糙表面一樣令人不舒服、難以應對。","examples":[{"en":"The first few months in the new city were rough.","zh":"剛到這座新城市的頭幾個月很難熬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has had a rough time since losing her job.","zh":"她失業後一直過得很艱難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf2b2ea7c52e94ab","term":"rough","forms":["rough","roughs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高爾夫球場的長草區","explanation":"高爾夫球場上沒有修剪得很短的粗草區域，球落進去後通常比在球道上更難擊打，正是“不平整的地方”這一畫面的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"Her ball landed in the rough beside the fairway.","zh":"她的球落在球道旁的長草區裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He used a stronger club to hit the ball out of the rough.","zh":"他用了杆面力量更大的球杆，把球從長草區打了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0debf3ab76f37f524711","word":"roughly","forms":["roughly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d72f109ace3c2e40","term":"roughly","forms":["roughly","roughlier","more roughly","roughliest","most roughly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不平整地；不均勻地","explanation":"表示表面、邊緣、排列或動作呈現出高低不平、參差不齊的狀態，像一條沒有被磨平的粗糙表面。","examples":[{"en":"The paint was applied roughly, so the wall looks uneven.","zh":"油漆刷得不均勻，所以牆面看起來凹凸不平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plaster had been roughly applied around the window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roughly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-341da72b946d20a3","term":"roughly","forms":["roughly","roughlier","more roughly","roughliest","most roughly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"大約；約略地","explanation":"表示數字、數量、時間或分類只是大致估計，並非精確數值；它保留了 rough 的“邊緣不平、細節未定”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Roughly fifty people attended the meeting.","zh":"大約有五十人參加了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The walk takes roughly forty minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roughly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-a97b0931730e83fbf928","word":"round","forms":["round"],"officialPos":"adj./n./adv./prep./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9fd25043cdb5a9c7","term":"round","forms":["round","rounder","more round","roundest","most round"],"pos":"adj","zh":"圓形的","explanation":"形狀像閉合的圓，沒有明顯的直角或尖角；可以把它想成一條回到起點的閉合路線。","examples":[{"en":"We sat around a round table during dinner.","zh":"晚餐時，我們圍坐在一張圓桌旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A round mirror hung above the basin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/round","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9048cc294e7f8284","term":"round","forms":["round","rounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圓形物","explanation":"指圓形或球形的物體，也可以指物體上呈圓形的部分；可以把它想成閉合路線圍成的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The children sat around a round table.","zh":"孩子們圍坐在一張圓桌旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut a round from the cardboard.","zh":"她從硬紙板上剪下了一個圓形片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/round","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a1bb62c748afea6","term":"round","forms":["round","rounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽的一回合","explanation":"指拳擊、摔跤等比賽中預先規定的一段比賽時間，回合結束後選手暫停；它就是比賽路線上的一個階段。","examples":[{"en":"The boxer knocked out his opponent in the third round.","zh":"這名拳擊手在第三回合擊倒了對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both players were exhausted after five rounds.","zh":"五個回合後，兩名選手都筋疲力盡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/round","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8c7e41744437af3","term":"round","forms":["round","rounds","rounding","rounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取整；約為","explanation":"把精確數字沿著數軸繞到最近的整數或其他整位數上，例如把帶小數的金額近似成整百數。","examples":[{"en":"The bill came to $101.65, so we rounded it to $100.","zh":"賬單金額是101.65美元，所以我們把它約成了100美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Round the answer to the nearest whole number.","zh":"把答案四捨五入到最接近的整數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/round","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a84e406c08ac9594f47","word":"route","forms":["route"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05f590551af7d4fe","term":"route","forms":["route","routes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行進路線","explanation":"指從一個地方到另一個地方時實際經過的方向或路徑，重點是“怎麼走”。","examples":[{"en":"We took a scenic route along the coast.","zh":"我們沿海岸走了一條風景優美的路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This route is shorter but much steeper.","zh":"這條路線更短，但陡得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/route","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b71878c569f1598c","term":"route","forms":["route","routes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固定線路","explanation":"指公交、送貨或其他定期服務反覆經過的一組站點和路徑。","examples":[{"en":"Our house is on the school bus route.","zh":"我們家在校車線路上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bus follows the same route every morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/route","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58da0a8b0de756af","term":"route","forms":["route","routes","routeing","routing","routed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按路線轉送","explanation":"指把人、車輛、郵件或其他東西安排到某條路線或某個中轉處，讓它沿指定方向前進。","examples":[{"en":"All customer requests are routed through the support team.","zh":"所有客戶請求都會先經過支援團隊處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The traffic was routed around the construction site.","zh":"車輛被引導繞過施工現場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/route","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,115],"total":7,"counts":{"111":1,"112":4,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-fde55b36ec36cbcd2832","word":"routine","forms":["routine"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd7198505db331f0","term":"routine","forms":["routine","more routine","most routine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"習慣性的；慣常的","explanation":"指某種行為或情況反覆出現，已經成了習慣，像沿著同一條固定路線行動。它可以是中性的，也可以暗示缺少變化。","examples":[{"en":"Her routine response was to check the figures twice.","zh":"她習慣性的做法是把數字核對兩遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"By Friday, the daily meeting had become routine for everyone.","zh":"到了星期五，每天的會議已經成了大家的慣例。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/routine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe91468cff6d2427","term":"routine","forms":["routine","routines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慣常做法；固定流程","explanation":"指需要定期遵循的一套行動步驟，例如每天起床後的安排或工作中的標準做法。它就是那條反覆走的固定路線。","examples":[{"en":"I follow the same routine before I start work.","zh":"我開始工作前總是遵循同樣的固定流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A short evening routine helps her sleep better.","zh":"簡短的晚間固定安排有助於她睡得更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/routine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-634768dae1474506e4bf","word":"row","forms":["row"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4088907e9f58fd9a","term":"row","forms":["row","rows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一排；一行","explanation":"row 是許多物體沿著一條線整齊排列形成的“一排”或“一行”，比如座位、樹木或蔬菜。","examples":[{"en":"We sat in the front row at the theater.","zh":"我們坐在劇院的第一排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She planted a row of tomatoes along the fence.","zh":"她沿著籬笆種了一排番茄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/row","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b42843abf60e212a","term":"row","forms":["row","rows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"划船；一次划船","explanation":"row 指用槳划船這一動作或一次這樣的活動，核心畫面是手臂向後拉槳，使船前進。","examples":[{"en":"We went for a row before breakfast.","zh":"我們早餐前去划了一會兒船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We went for a row across the quiet lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/row","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e829530d4c6a5b87","term":"row","forms":["row","rows","rowing","rowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"划船","explanation":"row 作動詞時表示用槳推動船在水上前進，核心仍是反覆向後拉槳。","examples":[{"en":"She rowed across the lake before sunrise.","zh":"她在日出前划船穿過了湖面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two volunteers rowed the injured sailor back to land.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/row","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa43038afb6314a3b24c","word":"royal","forms":["royal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-042229971430f166","term":"royal","forms":["royal","royaler","royaller","royalest","royallest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"王室的；君主的","explanation":"指屬於君主、王室或與他們有關的事物，就像蓋上“國王的印章”。它可以描述王室成員、制度、活動或場所。","examples":[{"en":"The royal family arrived at the ceremony together.","zh":"王室成員一起抵達了典禮現場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum is hosting an exhibition of royal portraits.","zh":"這家博物館正在舉辦王室肖像展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-79d950b29c6f25f2","term":"royal","forms":["royal","royaler","royaller","royalest","royallest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"君王般的；尊貴宏大的","explanation":"由“屬於國王”引申為像君王一樣有氣度、尊貴、慷慨，或規模和品質遠超一般水平。","examples":[{"en":"They gave us a royal welcome when we arrived.","zh":"我們到達時，他們以極其隆重的方式歡迎了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed royal patience throughout the crisis.","zh":"整個危機期間，她表現出了君王般的耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e232a78a47b90e37a15","word":"royalty","forms":["royalty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ac4e68245ed7f64","term":"royalty","forms":["royalty","royalties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王室地位與權威","explanation":"指君主所擁有的王位身份、等級、權力和權威，也就是“王冠”所代表的整體地位。它強調的是王室身份和統治資格，而不只是某一個王室成員。","examples":[{"en":"The ceremony celebrated the ancient royalty of the kingdom.","zh":"這場儀式讚頌了這個王國古老的王室地位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crown symbolizes royalty and its enduring authority.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royalty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4db21257c41e4ebc","term":"royalty","forms":["royalty","royalties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"智慧財產權使用費","explanation":"指作者、作曲家、發明者等因作品、音樂、發明或其他智慧財產權被銷售或使用而獲得的報酬。它仍然體現“擁有某種權利，因此別人使用時要付錢”的核心圖景。","examples":[{"en":"The songwriter earns royalties whenever the song is streamed.","zh":"這首歌每次被線上播放時，詞曲作者都會獲得版稅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The author receives royalties on every copy sold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royalty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-abaa209d9c23bcac2341","word":"rub","forms":["rub"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e381b6cf2c6c3423","term":"rub","forms":["rub","rubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擦動；摩擦","explanation":"指擦、摩擦這一動作本身，也就是物體在壓力下相互來回接觸。","examples":[{"en":"Give the table a quick rub with this cloth.","zh":"用這塊布快速擦一下桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Give the brass handle a good rub.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ffd018ed6244fa2","term":"rub","forms":["rub","rubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"難處；問題","explanation":"從“擦得不順、被卡住”引申為事情中的困難、棘手之處，尤其指妨礙事情順利進行的問題。","examples":[{"en":"The plan sounds simple, but there's the rub: nobody has enough time.","zh":"這個計劃聽起來很簡單，但難處在於沒人有足夠的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rub is that the cheapest option is also the slowest.","zh":"問題在於，最便宜的選擇也是最慢的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-488bcfc4276bb937","term":"rub","forms":["rub","rubs","rubbing","rubbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦；摩擦","explanation":"使一個物體在壓力下貼著另一個物體移動，從而產生摩擦。","examples":[{"en":"I rubbed the window with a dry towel.","zh":"我用乾毛巾擦了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rub the stain gently until it disappears.","zh":"輕輕擦汙漬，直到它消失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-058ce9bd95f5595d7894","word":"rubber","forms":["rubber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a814c2cd5e504e77","term":"rubber","forms":["rubber","rubbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橡膠材料","explanation":"一種有彈性、通常由橡膠樹乳汁製成的材料，可用於製造許多物品。","examples":[{"en":"These gloves are made of natural rubber.","zh":"這些手套是用天然橡膠製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rubber stretches when you pull it.","zh":"橡膠拉伸時會變長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rubber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fc82901a221543c","term":"rubber","forms":["rubber","rubbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橡皮","explanation":"在英國、澳大利亞等英語變體中，指用來擦掉鉛筆字跡的小塊橡膠，即通常所說的橡皮。","examples":[{"en":"Can I borrow your rubber to erase this word?","zh":"我可以借你的橡皮擦掉這個詞嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a rubber to remove the pencil marks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rubber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-71ca7d932e5a9bea82b1","word":"rubbish","forms":["rubbish"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a2cd8a6c099008e","term":"rubbish","forms":["rubbish","rubbishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"垃圾","explanation":"指被丟棄的廢物、雜物或不再需要的東西，是最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please take the rubbish outside.","zh":"請把垃圾拿到外面去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rubbish is collected on Mondays.","zh":"垃圾每週一收走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rubbish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66f9cf5fe0040b59","term":"rubbish","forms":["rubbish","rubbishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胡說八道","explanation":"指沒有道理、不真實或不值得相信的話，就像應該被清理掉的“語言垃圾”。","examples":[{"en":"That story about secret tunnels is rubbish.","zh":"關於秘密隧道的那個說法純屬胡說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His claim that the earth is flat is rubbish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rubbish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a88367105ff0f2e007a","word":"rude","forms":["rude"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cde0339e4c6fe181","term":"rude","forms":["rude","ruder","rudest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"沒禮貌的；粗魯的","explanation":"指說話或做事不尊重別人，缺少基本禮貌，就像把未經打磨的粗石直接撞向他人。","examples":[{"en":"It was rude of him to interrupt her while she was speaking.","zh":"他在她說話時打斷她，真是很沒禮貌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't be rude to the staff.","zh":"請不要對工作人員無禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9fdaa7ee3f13a29e53b1","word":"rug","forms":["rug"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e78ef62be4be28e","term":"rug","forms":["rug","rugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地毯；地墊","explanation":"指鋪在地板上的一塊地毯或地墊，通常可以單獨移動，不一定鋪滿整個房間；這正是“覆蓋物”這個核心形象的起點。","examples":[{"en":"We put a colorful rug in front of the sofa.","zh":"我們在沙發前鋪了一塊彩色地毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sat on the rug and played with blocks.","zh":"孩子們坐在地毯上玩積木。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f21a3401c1a6d48","term":"rug","forms":["rug","rugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毯子","explanation":"在英國和澳大利亞英語中，rug也可指蓋在床上或身上保暖的厚毯子；仍然是“用一層厚織物覆蓋”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"She wrapped the baby in a warm rug before going outside.","zh":"她出門前用一條暖和的毯子把嬰兒裹了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tucked a warm rug around her knees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3d200a5dd226550a74a","word":"rugged","forms":["rugged"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb54226ff7e8237d","term":"rugged","forms":["rugged","more rugged","most rugged"],"pos":"adj","zh":"崎嶇不平","explanation":"指表面有尖銳或不規則的起伏，走起來或摸起來都不平滑；這是 rugged 最直接的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers crossed a rugged trail before sunset.","zh":"徒步者們在日落前穿過了一條崎嶇的小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rugged coastline is difficult to reach by road.","zh":"這片崎嶇的海岸很難透過公路到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rugged","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-014a18be611493c4","term":"rugged","forms":["rugged","more rugged","most rugged"],"pos":"adj","zh":"強壯結實","explanation":"形容人的身體或體格強健、結實，給人能經受困難的印象；這是從崎嶇環境引申出的“堅韌”形象。","examples":[{"en":"The guide was rugged and fit enough for the long journey.","zh":"那名嚮導體格強健，足以應付這段漫長旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She admired his rugged good looks.","zh":"她很欣賞他那種粗獷英俊的外表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rugged","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a38d08340cba469053d","word":"ruin","forms":["ruin"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1622999ffead1222","term":"ruin","forms":["ruin","ruins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廢墟","explanation":"指建築物被毀壞或年久失修後留下的遺蹟，核心畫面就是倒塌城堡的殘垣斷壁。","examples":[{"en":"We explored the ruins of an ancient castle.","zh":"我們探索了一座古老城堡的廢墟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a few walls remain among the ruins.","zh":"廢墟中只剩下幾面牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb9a5dc9fad0571b","term":"ruin","forms":["ruin","ruins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衰敗狀態","explanation":"指某物已經毀壞、腐朽或失去原來的完整狀態，強調“處於廢墟般的狀態”，而不是具體的遺蹟。","examples":[{"en":"The old theater has fallen into ruin.","zh":"那座老劇院已經陷入衰敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Neglected canals and empty mills testified to the district's ruin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f46d50f759ab0f1","term":"ruin","forms":["ruin","ruins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禍根；毀滅性後果","explanation":"指會把人或事情推向嚴重麻煩、失敗甚至毀滅的事物；它就像導致城堡倒塌的那股力量。","examples":[{"en":"His addiction became the ruin of his family.","zh":"他的成癮問題成了他家庭毀滅的根源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gambling proved to be his ruin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca33aeaa9bffb4fc","term":"ruin","forms":["ruin","ruins","ruining","ruined","ruint"],"pos":"verb","zh":"毀壞；使不能使用","explanation":"指把物品毀壞到不能正常使用的程度，例如弄壞衣服、裝置或食物；核心仍是讓原本完整的東西變得不可用。","examples":[{"en":"I ruined my jacket when I spilled paint on it.","zh":"我把油漆灑到夾克上，把它弄壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Too much heat can ruin the equipment.","zh":"溫度過高可能會損壞裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a3a6d820480eed5","term":"ruin","forms":["ruin","ruins","ruining","ruined","ruint"],"pos":"verb","zh":"破壞計劃或進展","explanation":"指某件事對計劃、活動或進展造成災難性影響，使原本要順利進行的事情失敗或無法繼續。","examples":[{"en":"The storm ruined our plans for a picnic.","zh":"暴風雨打亂了我們去野餐的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One mistake ruined months of progress.","zh":"一個錯誤毀掉了幾個月的進展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7369949b47ef2c6ba26f","word":"rule","forms":["rule"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-450fa1a100b0192d","term":"rule","forms":["rule","rules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"規則；規定","explanation":"rule 是要求人們如何做事的規定，可以來自學校、組織、遊戲或法律；複數 rules 常指一整套規則。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone must follow the rules of the game.","zh":"每個人都必須遵守遊戲規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a strict rule against using phones in class.","zh":"課堂上嚴禁使用手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cd2d6fc616f8ec8","term":"rule","forms":["rule","rules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支配原則；規律","explanation":"這裡的 rule 不是一條具體命令，而是支配某種現象或行為的基本原則，表示事情通常按照什麼方式發展。","examples":[{"en":"As a general rule, plants need light to grow.","zh":"一般來說，植物需要光才能生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exception seems to challenge the general rule.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bd7ea563d0f48db","term":"rule","forms":["rule","rules","ruling","ruled","rulest","ruledst","ruleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"統治；管理","explanation":"rule 作動詞時表示掌權、管理一個國家或群體，並據此作決定；它就是名詞“規則、支配”主線的動作形式。","examples":[{"en":"The queen ruled the country for thirty years.","zh":"這位女王統治了這個國家三十年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dynasty ruled the region for three centuries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5972814068a183e232d6","word":"ruler","forms":["ruler"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e7974347a64d21a5","term":"ruler","forms":["ruler","rulers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"直尺","explanation":"一種通常堅硬、扁平而有刻度的長條工具，用來測量長度或畫直線。它的核心形象是“把線和長度定準”。","examples":[{"en":"Use a ruler to draw a straight line.","zh":"用直尺畫一條直線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruler shows that the box is 20 centimeters long.","zh":"直尺顯示這個盒子長二十釐米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruler","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c0c4cfb997422f4","term":"ruler","forms":["ruler","rulers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統治者；掌權者","explanation":"指統治國家、地區或某個群體的人，也可以比喻為在某個領域擁有壓倒性控制力的事物。這個意義延續了“制定規則、掌握界限”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The young ruler inherited the throne after his father's death.","zh":"這位年輕的統治者在父親去世後繼承了王位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ruler imposed heavy taxes on the farmers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruler","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16f6f50a7cc92ed1a49d","word":"rumor","forms":["rumor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8db4dbea603def96","term":"rumor","forms":["rumor","rumors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個傳聞","explanation":"指沒有可靠已知來源、真實性有疑問，卻在人們之間傳播的一條具體訊息。它可以是真的，也可以是錯誤的，但說話人強調的是它尚未得到可靠證實。","examples":[{"en":"There's a rumor going around that Maya is leaving the company.","zh":"有傳聞說瑪雅要離開公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I heard a rumor about a new café opening near the station.","zh":"我聽說有個傳聞，說車站附近要開一家新咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rumor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c0d1de75dad783a","term":"rumor","forms":["rumor","rumors","rumoring","rumored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"據傳；傳言說","explanation":"表示人們正在傳播某個未經證實的說法，常用於說明某人據說會得到某職位、某事據說即將發生等。它把“傳聞”這個名詞義變成了“傳出傳聞”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The director is rumored to be joining another studio.","zh":"據傳這位導演要加入另一家制片公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is rumored that the museum will close for renovations.","zh":"據傳這家博物館將因翻修而關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rumor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acba25512100f80b56fc","word":"run","forms":["run"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-657933817137331a","term":"run","forms":["run","runs","running","ran","runnest","ranst","rannest","runneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"奔跑","explanation":"指人或動物快速向前移動，就是通常所說的奔跑；可以把“run”想成身體持續向前移動。","examples":[{"en":"Run, or we’ll miss the bus!","zh":"快跑，不然我們要趕不上公共汽車了！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children ran across the playground.","zh":"孩子們跑過了操場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/run","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da6c5cc20b570761","term":"run","forms":["run","runs","running","ran","runnest","ranst","rannest","runneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"流動","explanation":"指水、液體或其他流體持續向前流動；河流沿著一定路線流過，也可以用“run”描述。","examples":[{"en":"A small stream runs through the village.","zh":"一條小溪流過這個村子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tears ran down her cheeks.","zh":"淚水順著她的臉頰流下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/run","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b49ea0006774c564","term":"run","forms":["run","runs","running","ran","runnest","ranst","rannest","runneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經營管理","explanation":"指負責經營、管理某項業務、組織或活動，讓它持續運轉下去；這正是“讓事情持續進行”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"She runs a small bakery near the station.","zh":"她在車站附近經營一家小麵包店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Who runs this community center?","zh":"誰負責管理這個社群中心？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/run","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-527aa9f431539da8e151","word":"runner","forms":["runner"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7db83f4b7ee27d94","term":"runner","forms":["runner","runners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跑步的人","explanation":"runner 最基本的意思是正在跑步的人，或參加跑步比賽的人。它不一定專指職業運動員。","examples":[{"en":"The first runner to cross the finish line wins the race.","zh":"第一個衝過終點線的跑步者贏得比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several runners were training in the park before sunrise.","zh":"天亮前，幾名跑步者正在公園裡訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/runner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3edfeb035af6312","term":"runner","forms":["runner","runners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跑鞋；軟底鞋","explanation":"在澳大利亞、加拿大、愛爾蘭和蘇格蘭等英語用法中，runner 可指原本供跑步者穿的軟底鞋，也就是一種運動鞋。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a new pair of runners for the school sports day.","zh":"她為學校運動會買了一雙新跑鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put on your runners before we leave for the gym.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/runner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc8c878e1eb1d9f5","term":"runner","forms":["runner","runners"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長條地毯","explanation":"runner 還可以指鋪在走廊、樓梯等狹長或人流量大的地方的長條地毯。這裡仍然有“沿著一條路線延伸”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"We put a washable runner in the front hall.","zh":"我們在前廳鋪了一條可清洗的長條地毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow runner protected the polished hallway floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/runner","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d359e52a5efb652d5cb6","word":"rural","forms":["rural"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64abf13ac60ee5de","term":"rural","forms":["rural","more rural","most rural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鄉村的；農村的","explanation":"指屬於鄉村、農村或農業環境的事物，重點是它與城市生活相對，和田野、村莊、農地等聯絡在一起。","examples":[{"en":"Many rural communities depend on farming and tourism.","zh":"許多農村社群依靠農業和旅遊業發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family moved from the city to a rural area.","zh":"這家人從城市搬到了一個鄉村地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d1fd0086934aca91293","word":"rush","forms":["rush"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a23304e048caf1b","term":"rush","forms":["rush","rushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛衝","explanation":"指突然而有力地向前衝，強調動作來得快、來得猛；就像記憶鉤子裡的“突然向前衝”。","examples":[{"en":"With a sudden rush, the dog ran through the open gate.","zh":"狗突然猛衝了一下，跑出了敞開的門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden rush of spectators overwhelmed the entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19dd9b3a5c960f0b","term":"rush","forms":["rush","rushes","rushing","rushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"趕快做；匆忙處理","explanation":"表示為了趕時間而迅速做某事或趕快離開，常帶有“衝得太快、可能做得不夠周全”的感覺，就像人急著向前衝。","examples":[{"en":"I had to rush to finish the report before lunch.","zh":"我不得不趕在午飯前匆匆完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't rush your answer; take a moment to think.","zh":"請不要急著回答，先花一點時間想想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b512d23ec05f12ba","term":"rush","forms":["rush","rushes","rushing","rushed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"快速奔流；迅速向前移動","explanation":"表示水流、人群、車輛或其他事物快速而有聲勢地向前移動，像一股力量突然衝出去。","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater rushed down the street after the storm.","zh":"暴雨過後，雨水沿街道急速流下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd rushed toward the exit when the doors opened.","zh":"門一開啟，人群就衝向出口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-521fe5c9ece1aa1f8b66","word":"rust","forms":["rust"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9de8d5d24398a8b2","term":"rust","forms":["rust","rusts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鏽；鏽蝕層","explanation":"rust是鐵或鋼受潮並氧化後形成的紅褐色物質，也可指這種鏽蝕狀態。它會使金屬表面變差，正是“舊化外殼”這個核心意象的來源。","examples":[{"en":"There was rust on the old bicycle chain.","zh":"那輛舊腳踏車的鏈條上有鏽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I scrubbed the rust off the garden gate.","zh":"我把花園門上的鏽刷掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c120b8e5ae45b472","term":"rust","forms":["rust","rusts","rusting","rusted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"生鏽","explanation":"rust作不及物動詞時，表示鐵、鋼等金屬逐漸形成鏽層，也就是“長出那層紅褐色外殼”。","examples":[{"en":"The tools will rust if you leave them outside.","zh":"這些工具如果放在外面，就會生鏽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hinges rusted after months in the rain.","zh":"鉸鏈在雨中放了幾個月後生鏽了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91c0b7c9c0fa9864fb4e","word":"rusty","forms":["rusty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98741db224d6b225","term":"rusty","forms":["rusty","rustier","rustiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生鏽的","explanation":"指金屬表面已經形成鐵鏽，通常暗示物品受潮、放置已久或缺少保養。","examples":[{"en":"The old gate was rusty and difficult to open.","zh":"那扇舊門鏽跡斑斑，很難開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found a rusty key under the floorboards.","zh":"她在地板下面找到了一把生鏽的鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rusty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e3d9cf148a4d698","term":"rusty","forms":["rusty","rustier","rustiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生疏的","explanation":"把久未練習的技能比作生了鏽，表示能力暫時不靈活、不熟練，但通常暗示練習後可以恢復。","examples":[{"en":"I'm a little rusty at playing the piano, but I can still read the music.","zh":"我彈鋼琴有些生疏了，但還是能看懂樂譜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After years away from the job, he felt rusty with the software.","zh":"離開這份工作多年後，他覺得自己對這款軟體的操作生疏了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rusty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bed2541acc96764b1d1","word":"ruthless","forms":["ruthless"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6390955424ccbcd3","term":"ruthless","forms":["ruthless","more ruthless","most ruthless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"殘酷無情的","explanation":"形容人或團體完全沒有憐憫心，為達到目的可以傷害、懲罰或犧牲別人。這個意義保留了“沒有憐憫”的原始畫面，語氣通常很負面。","examples":[{"en":"The ruthless dictator silenced anyone who opposed him.","zh":"那個殘酷無情的獨裁者壓制所有反對他的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gang was ruthless toward its rivals.","zh":"這個幫派對競爭對手毫不留情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruthless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b291774923a85817","term":"ruthless","forms":["ruthless","more ruthless","most ruthless"],"pos":"adj","zh":"毫不退讓的；不留餘地的","explanation":"形容行動、競爭或策略一旦開始就持續推進，不因阻力或他人的困難而放鬆。它是“對人不留情”的畫面向行動領域的延伸，常強調強硬、徹底和不妥協。","examples":[{"en":"The company launched a ruthless campaign to drive its competitor out of the market.","zh":"這家公司發起了一場毫不留情的行動，想把競爭對手趕出市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor was ruthless about cutting unnecessary words.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruthless","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ec327522ee89bcc4115","word":"sack","forms":["sack"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-638242fea086d218","term":"sack","forms":["sack","sacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"袋子；大袋","explanation":"通常指用結實粗布或類似材料製成、用來裝和搬運物品的大袋子，也可泛指購物袋等袋子。","examples":[{"en":"She carried a sack of potatoes home.","zh":"她提著一袋土豆回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the empty bottles in a sack.","zh":"把空瓶子放進袋子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9c6958aa1027e3c","term":"sack","forms":["sack","sacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洗劫","explanation":"指軍隊或攻擊者攻佔城鎮後掠奪財物，彷彿把財物裝進袋子帶走。","examples":[{"en":"The sack of the city lasted for three days.","zh":"這座城市遭到的洗劫持續了三天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city's sack destroyed many priceless manuscripts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8aa1a62cf736f542","term":"sack","forms":["sack","sacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解僱","explanation":"非正式地指被僱主辭退，或指辭退某人；可以把它記成“讓人收拾袋子離開”。","examples":[{"en":"The company sacked him after repeated warnings.","zh":"公司多次警告後解僱了他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He got the sack after repeatedly missing shifts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1894c24cf135e26d37ab","word":"sacred","forms":["sacred"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9a4089cf95d62f8e","term":"sacred","forms":["sacred","more sacred","most sacred"],"pos":"adj","zh":"神聖的；經祝聖的","explanation":"指經過宗教儀式而被認為屬於神聖領域的事物，尤其是神聖的地點、物品或儀式；重點是它被正式賦予了神聖性質。","examples":[{"en":"Visitors must remove their shoes before entering the sacred place.","zh":"遊客進入這處神聖場所前必須脫鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ceremony takes place beside a sacred river.","zh":"儀式在一條神聖的河流旁舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6396415da65417e","term":"sacred","forms":["sacred","more sacred","most sacred"],"pos":"adj","zh":"宗教的；非世俗的","explanation":"泛指與宗教、禮拜或宗教音樂等有關的事物，與世俗生活相對；它強調所屬領域是宗教，而不一定表示某個具體物件已經經過祝聖。","examples":[{"en":"The program includes both sacred and secular music.","zh":"這場演出既包括宗教音樂，也包括世俗音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studies sacred texts from several traditions.","zh":"她研究多個宗教傳統的經典文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b82c721f61a86957","term":"sacred","forms":["sacred","more sacred","most sacred"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不可侵犯的；必須尊重的","explanation":"比喻地指某事物被劃入不可觸犯的範圍，不能隨便洩露、破壞或違背；它可以用於秘密、承諾、家庭關係、原則和權利等。","examples":[{"en":"For her, the privacy of her family is sacred.","zh":"對她來說，家人的隱私是不可侵犯的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They regarded the promise as sacred.","zh":"他們把這個承諾看得神聖不可違。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d17bd922ea9dd14143a1","word":"sacrifice","forms":["sacrifice"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2623ab94f3ac31c1","term":"sacrifice","forms":["sacrifice","sacrifices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"為更大目標作出犧牲","explanation":"指為了更緊迫或更有價值的事情而毀掉、放棄某物，也可直接指被放棄的時間、機會或利益。這是現代日常語境中最重要的抽象意義。","examples":[{"en":"Success often requires the sacrifice of free time.","zh":"成功往往需要犧牲空閒時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made many sacrifices to support her family.","zh":"她為了養家作出了許多犧牲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb444c7350568d42","term":"sacrifice","forms":["sacrifice","sacrifices","sacrificing","sacrificed","sacrificest","sacrificedst","sacrificeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"犧牲或放棄","explanation":"指為了更重要、更緊迫的事情而放棄或毀掉某物，包括時間、金錢、機會、利益，甚至生命；這是動詞最常見的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"She sacrificed her career to care for her father.","zh":"她為了照顧父親放棄了自己的事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We cannot sacrifice safety for speed.","zh":"我們不能為了速度而犧牲安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sacrifice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-45c9a6614fccd4f9592d","word":"sad","forms":["sad"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2923891785eff4e","term":"sad","forms":["sad","sadder","more sad","saddest","most sad"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悲傷的；難過的","explanation":"指因為離別、壞訊息或其他原因而心情低落、難過。這是 sad 在現代英語中最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She gets sad when her friends move away.","zh":"朋友搬走時，她會感到難過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was sad to hear that the concert was canceled.","zh":"聽說音樂會取消了，我很難過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca1e62cc9f20263f","term":"sad","forms":["sad","sadder","more sad","saddest","most sad"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可悲的；沒品的","explanation":"在俚語中，sad 不一定表示真的難過，而是說某人或某事很可憐、沒品、在社交上不受歡迎。這是從“讓人感覺不好”發展出來的負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"He spends every weekend alone playing the same game—how sad.","zh":"他每個週末都一個人玩同一個遊戲，真可悲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mocking someone else's accent is pretty sad.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba08dad18ac84822bc25","word":"saddle","forms":["saddle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5da676d00e68018","term":"saddle","forms":["saddle","saddles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬鞍","explanation":"放在馬或其他動物背上供人騎坐的座具，通常前後隆起，並用帶子固定在動物身上。","examples":[{"en":"The rider adjusted the saddle before mounting the horse.","zh":"騎手上馬前調好了馬鞍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent the afternoon in the saddle.","zh":"她一下午都騎在馬背上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saddle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06b5df62e9878730","term":"saddle","forms":["saddle","saddles","saddling","saddled","saddlest","saddledst","saddleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給動物加鞍","explanation":"把鞍放到馬或其他動物背上並固定好，為騎乘做好準備。","examples":[{"en":"We saddled the horses before dawn.","zh":"我們天亮前給馬加好了鞍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He saddled his horse and rode toward the village.","zh":"他給馬加鞍後，騎馬向村子走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saddle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea24cd32c7b5cd14","term":"saddle","forms":["saddle","saddles","saddling","saddled","saddlest","saddledst","saddleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使承擔負擔","explanation":"把任務、問題、債務或責任像鞍一樣壓到某人身上，使其不得不承擔。","examples":[{"en":"The new manager was saddled with an impossible deadline.","zh":"新經理被迫承擔了一個根本不可能完成的期限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They were saddled with expensive repairs.","zh":"他們被迫承擔了昂貴的維修費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saddle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b3369944dd2a3fab39e","word":"safe","forms":["safe"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed821252837beaa8","term":"safe","forms":["safe","safer","more safe","safest","most safe"],"pos":"adj","zh":"安全的；沒有危險的","explanation":"指人或物沒有受到傷害的危險，處在保護之中。比如躲在結實的屋裡，就可以說人在暴風雨中是 safe 的。","examples":[{"en":"You’ll be safe from the storm here in the cabin.","zh":"你在這間小屋裡就不會受到暴風雨的傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Call me when you get home safe.","zh":"你安全到家後給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0636c0c408e99ca7","term":"safe","forms":["safe","safer","more safe","safest","most safe"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不會帶來危險的","explanation":"指某種食物、行為或選擇不會造成傷害，因此可以放心進行或使用。它關注的是“風險很低、不會傷人”，而不只是“身處安全地點”。","examples":[{"en":"It’s safe to eat this berry.","zh":"這種漿果可以放心吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is this water safe for children to drink?","zh":"這種水適合兒童飲用嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb16f58ce80ee9fd","term":"safe","forms":["safe","safer","more safe","safest","most safe"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能提供保護的","explanation":"強調地點、空間或庇護處本身能夠把人從危險中保護起來。它是“安全”這個核心概念向外延伸到“提供安全的地方或環境”。","examples":[{"en":"We need to find a safe place to wait.","zh":"我們得找個安全的地方等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bunker offered a safe refuge during the bombardment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4519b8976fb615a1","term":"safe","forms":["safe","safes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險箱","explanation":"指可以上鎖、用來存放現金、檔案和其他貴重物品的堅固箱子。它是“保護罩”最具體的實物形式。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps her passport and jewelry in a safe.","zh":"她把護照和珠寶放在保險箱裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager opened the safe before the store closed.","zh":"商店關門前，經理開啟了保險箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-856e8bd358ece398c72f","word":"safety","forms":["safety"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9b5020b00127523","term":"safety","forms":["safety","safeties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安全；平安","explanation":"指沒有受到傷害、危險或損失的狀態，也可以指人對這種狀態的安心感覺。它是 safety 最基本的意思：人在危險之外，或有措施把危險擋住。","examples":[{"en":"Please check the brakes for your own safety.","zh":"為了你自己的安全，請檢查剎車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide put our safety first.","zh":"導遊把我們的安全放在第一位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safety","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-019b0fb8a6ad1fe1","term":"safety","forms":["safety","safeties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保險裝置；保險栓","explanation":"指裝在槍械或其他危險裝置上的開關或鎖定機構，用來阻止裝置意外啟動或擊發。它是“安全屏障”這個核心概念在機器上的具體形式。","examples":[{"en":"Keep the safety on until you are ready to use the tool.","zh":"在準備使用工具之前，要一直開啟保險裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the safety engaged until you are ready.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safety","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d0350a6064de840458ae","word":"sail","forms":["sail"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f036fcf5de7c5178","term":"sail","forms":["sail","sails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帆","explanation":"裝在船上、張開後借風推動船前進的布或類似材料製成的部分。它是這個詞最具體、最核心的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The boat's white sail filled with wind.","zh":"小船的白帆鼓滿了風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They lowered the sail before the storm arrived.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，他們降下了帆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77c989f2b4a19a23","term":"sail","forms":["sail","sails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帆力；借帆航行","explanation":"指帆把風的力量轉成船的前進動力，也可以指利用這種力量航行的方式；這是從“帆”自然發展出的功能義。","examples":[{"en":"With no engine, the small boat moved under sail.","zh":"沒有發動機，這艘小船靠帆前進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vessel crossed the ocean under sail.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e33dbe952e69f0bf","term":"sail","forms":["sail","sails","sailing","sailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"航行；借風前進","explanation":"指船藉助帆、發動機等力量在水上前進；最初的畫面就是帆受風推動船航行。","examples":[{"en":"The old schooner sailed across the bay.","zh":"那艘老帆船駛過了海灣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ferry sailed through the fog before dawn.","zh":"渡船在黎明前穿過了霧氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aecc8d8a4cd508f7","term":"sail","forms":["sail","sails","sailing","sailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"乘船航行","explanation":"指人乘船，尤其是乘帆船出遊或航行；重點在參與這段水上旅程。","examples":[{"en":"We sailed around the island for two days.","zh":"我們乘船繞著這座島航行了兩天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sailed from the harbor just after sunrise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80974e50413f641d256a","word":"sailor","forms":["sailor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd368c7d567d90ca","term":"sailor","forms":["sailor","sailors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水手；航海者","explanation":"指駕駛、操縱或在船上工作的航海者，也可泛指經常在海上或其他水域航行的人。這是 sailor 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"He's a talented sailor and has spent many years at sea.","zh":"他是一名出色的水手，已經在海上度過了很多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young sailor checked the ropes before the boat left the harbor.","zh":"小水手在船離開港口前檢查了纜繩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sailor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de8da0f74191fd81","term":"sailor","forms":["sailor","sailors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水手帽","explanation":"指一種硬挺的草帽，帽簷平而圓，帽冠低而平，因外形或傳統上與水手相關而得名。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a straw sailor with a blue ribbon on the beach.","zh":"她在海灘上戴著一頂系藍色絲帶的水手草帽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her vintage sailor had a flat crown and a broad brim.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sailor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b49bda2606fd82b0206","word":"saint","forms":["saint"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1aa6c0281a9f2a65","term":"saint","forms":["saint","saints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式認可的聖人","explanation":"指已經去世，並被教會或其他宗教團體正式認可為特別聖潔、虔誠和有德行的人。","examples":[{"en":"The church proclaimed her a saint many years after her death.","zh":"這座教會在她去世多年後宣佈她為聖人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Saint Teresa devoted her life to helping the poor.","zh":"聖特蕾莎一生都致力於幫助窮人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f474e78ef971f84","term":"saint","forms":["saint","Saints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聖人稱號","explanation":"放在人名前，表示這個人被稱為聖人，是宗教稱號的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"Saint Patrick is remembered on March 17.","zh":"人們在3月17日紀念聖帕特里克。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The church was dedicated to Saint Andrew.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cef2e28b43f00b6c4201","word":"sake","forms":["sake"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dec696beec6be0d7","term":"sake","forms":["sake","sakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"為了某個討論目的或考慮","explanation":"表示為了某個討論、說明或實際考慮而暫時採取某種做法，重點是“為了這個目的”。例如在辯論中先假定某件事成立，只是為了繼續討論。","examples":[{"en":"For the sake of argument, let's assume that the plan will work.","zh":"為了便於討論，我們先假定這個計劃會成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For the sake of clarity, I have divided the report into three parts.","zh":"為了說得更清楚，我把報告分成了三部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b0af8d0ea364972","term":"sake","forms":["sake","sakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"為了某個目的或理由","explanation":"表示做某事是為了達到某個目的，或因為某種情感和理由；它把行動和背後的“為什麼”連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"For old times' sake, we visited the café where we first met.","zh":"為了懷念過去，我們去了第一次見面的那家咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She changed her schedule for the sake of a peaceful weekend.","zh":"為了度過一個平靜的週末，她調整了自己的日程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6c3fa689e291bba6f74","word":"salad","forms":["salad"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f0ab59d7c62e38c7","term":"salad","forms":["salad","salads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙拉；涼拌蔬菜","explanation":"指把生的或冷的食材，尤其是蔬菜，混合起來並配上調味汁的一道食物。它可以很簡單，只含幾種蔬菜，也可以加入肉、乳酪、蛋等其他冷食材。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a salad with grilled chicken and avocado.","zh":"我點了一份加烤雞肉和牛油果的沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We usually serve salad with the main course.","zh":"我們通常把沙拉和主菜一起上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8c3f342e9a906af","term":"salad","forms":["salad","salads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙拉用的生蔬菜","explanation":"在三明治、漢堡等語境中，salad可以不指整道沙拉，而是泛指夾在裡面的生菜葉或其他生蔬菜。這是從“沙拉的主要組成部分”延伸出來的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have some salad in my sandwich, please?","zh":"請在我的三明治里加一些生蔬菜，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Plant salad in shallow containers near the kitchen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6384e43c02b1fbdfb9b4","word":"salary","forms":["salary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a8c6cff003932f74","term":"salary","forms":["salary","salaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"固定工資；薪水","explanation":"salary指僱員按照固定週期領取的工作報酬，通常按月或按年計算，而不是每小時結算。它把“定期發下來的錢”這個核心意象具體化為較穩定的職業收入。","examples":[{"en":"The company offers a competitive salary and health insurance.","zh":"這家公司提供有競爭力的薪水和醫療保險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She earns a good salary as an engineer.","zh":"她當工程師，薪水很不錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f7101fe71011ba0872a","word":"sale","forms":["sale"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a87fdb2c71d6697","term":"sale","forms":["sale","sales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"出售；銷售","explanation":"指商品或服務從賣家交給買家，並換取金錢或信用，是 sale 最基本的意義。它強調完成或進行一次交易，而不一定表示降價。","examples":[{"en":"The sale of the house was completed last week.","zh":"這所房子的出售上週完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company made a large sale to a new customer.","zh":"這家公司向一位新客戶做成了一筆大交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a85ed3f5a60a2fc","term":"sale","forms":["sale","sales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"打折銷售；促銷活動","explanation":"指商店把商品以低於通常價格的方式集中出售，因此 sale 也常指“打折季”或“促銷活動”。這個意義是“出售”進一步縮小到低價出售。","examples":[{"en":"All winter coats are on sale this week.","zh":"本週所有冬季外套都在打折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store is having a summer sale.","zh":"這家商店正在進行夏季促銷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f20d1862825063df61f5","word":"salesperson/salesman/saleswoman","forms":["salesperson","salesman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1fd7c9162b9da7f0","term":"salesperson","forms":["salesperson","salespersons","salespeople"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銷售人員；售貨員","explanation":"指以賣東西為主要工作的人，尤其是在商店裡接待顧客、介紹商品並幫助顧客購買的人。這個詞把“銷售”與“人”直接連在一起，強調的是職業，而不是某一次臨時賣東西的行為。","examples":[{"en":"I asked a salesperson where I could find the winter coats.","zh":"我問了一位銷售人員冬季外套在哪裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The salesperson demonstrated how the folding mechanism worked.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salesperson","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6fadecfdf2c1417","term":"salesman","forms":["salesman","salesmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銷售員；推銷員","explanation":"指以賣東西為工作的人，可以在商店裡接待顧客，也可以在店外聯絡客戶、介紹和推銷商品。記住“把商品帶到顧客面前並促成購買”這條主線即可。","examples":[{"en":"The salesman showed us several cars before we chose one.","zh":"銷售員給我們看了幾輛車，我們才選定其中一輛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A salesman came to our office to introduce the company's new software.","zh":"一名推銷員來到我們辦公室，介紹這家公司開發的新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salesman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aeaa2cec33e27d65690e","word":"salmon","forms":["salmon"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c299706ad9f032d6","term":"salmon","forms":["salmon","salmons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鮭魚；三文魚","explanation":"指鮭魚類的魚，通常背部呈褐色、兩側銀亮，肉色偏粉橙；這種魚會向河流上游游去產卵。","examples":[{"en":"We had grilled salmon with rice for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐吃了烤鮭魚配米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The salmon are swimming upstream.","zh":"鮭魚正在向上遊游去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salmon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc9b33f77d3b1cd1","term":"salmon","forms":["salmon"],"pos":"adj","zh":"淡粉橙色的","explanation":"指接近熟鮭魚肉的淺粉色和橙色之間的顏色，常用於衣物、布料、牆面等。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a salmon dress to the party.","zh":"她穿了一條淡粉橙色的裙子去參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose salmon curtains for the guest bedroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salmon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a26b7dee6fc52c891e7","word":"salon","forms":["salon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f4ffa7dacb6edf0","term":"salon","forms":["salon","salons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"接待賓客的大廳","explanation":"它可以指一間較大的接待室或客廳，主人在這裡招待和陪伴客人；這是“讓人進來相聚”的最具體形象。","examples":[{"en":"The guests gathered in the salon after dinner.","zh":"晚餐後，客人們聚集在接待廳裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The house has a bright salon overlooking the garden.","zh":"這所房子有一間明亮的接待廳，可以俯瞰花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b08bc8ea0310e87","term":"salon","forms":["salon","salons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社交或思想交流會","explanation":"它也指一群人定期聚在一起交談、討論文學藝術或交換思想的活動；重點從“房間”轉到了“房間裡的人和交流”。","examples":[{"en":"She hosts a monthly salon for young writers.","zh":"她每月為年輕作家舉辦一次交流沙龍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The salon brought together musicians, poets, and painters.","zh":"這場沙龍彙集了音樂家、詩人和畫家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63479ad69a090b258277","word":"salt","forms":["salt"],"officialPos":"n./v./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-601945d8a4397c10","term":"salt","forms":["salt","more salt","most salt"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鹽醃的","explanation":"食物中加進鹽併發揮儲存作用，所以表示經過鹽醃或用鹽儲存的食物。","examples":[{"en":"Salt cod needs to be soaked before cooking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"Salt pork adds a rich flavor to this soup.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37fc80e73d821dee","term":"salt","forms":["salt","salts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"食鹽","explanation":"鹽被加入食物後帶來鹹味，還能幫助儲存食物；通常就是日常烹飪中的食鹽。","examples":[{"en":"Add a little salt to the soup before serving.","zh":"上湯前往湯里加一點鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Too much salt can make the dish unpleasantly salty.","zh":"鹽放得太多會讓這道菜鹹得難吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fafa300d3e83fc3","term":"salt","forms":["salt","salts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"味道；調味","explanation":"鹽被加進食物後產生味道，因此也可引申指食物的味道、調味效果或使生活有滋味的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The fresh herbs added salt to an otherwise plain meal.","zh":"新鮮香草給原本寡淡的飯菜增添了滋味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Travel brought salt and variety to her quiet life.","zh":"旅行給她平靜的生活增添了滋味和變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e647b599b5eff01b","term":"salt","forms":["salt","salts","salting","salted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加鹽；用鹽醃製","explanation":"把鹽加到食物或其他東西里，使其有鹹味，或利用鹽幫助儲存；也就是“鹽被加進去併產生作用”。","examples":[{"en":"Salt the vegetables lightly before serving.","zh":"上桌前給蔬菜略加一點鹽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They salt the fish to preserve it through the winter.","zh":"他們用鹽醃魚，以便儲存到冬天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0237742265ea9ac1dba0","word":"salty","forms":["salty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5447311c2ff9d635","term":"salty","forms":["salty","saltier","saltiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鹹的；有鹽味的","explanation":"指嚐起來能明顯嚐到鹽味，重點是味覺感受，而不是單純說明裡面含有多少鹽。","examples":[{"en":"The soup is too salty for me.","zh":"這湯對我來說太鹹了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These crackers taste salty but not spicy.","zh":"這些餅乾吃起來鹹，但不辣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-275a921d9a8fc504","term":"salty","forms":["salty","saltier","saltiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含鹽的","explanation":"指某種物質本身含有鹽分，例如水、土壤或礦石；不一定是在說人實際嚐到的味道。","examples":[{"en":"Only a few plants can grow in salty soil.","zh":"只有少數植物能在含鹽的土壤裡生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These salty crackers make me thirsty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94497f93095295ba7d21","word":"salute","forms":["salute"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce58bf9833146433","term":"salute","forms":["salute","salutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敬禮；致意動作","explanation":"指用手臂、手或其他正式動作向某人表示問候、尊敬或服從，最典型的就是軍人敬禮。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers gave the general a sharp salute.","zh":"士兵們向將軍乾脆利落地敬了個禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She raised her hand in salute as the flag passed.","zh":"旗幟經過時，她舉手敬禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1656414e516e11a6","term":"salute","forms":["salute","salutes","saluting","saluted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向……敬禮；致意","explanation":"指用敬禮等動作向人、旗幟或其他受尊敬的物件表達敬意，是動詞 salute 最核心、最具體的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The cadets saluted the flag during the ceremony.","zh":"典禮期間，學員們向旗幟敬禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He saluted the officer and left the room.","zh":"他向軍官敬禮後離開了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2394f3e1a4b135eb","term":"salute","forms":["salute","salutes","saluting","saluted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向……致敬；讚揚","explanation":"把“致意”從一個動作擴充套件成公開表達感謝、敬意或讚揚，常用於肯定某人的貢獻。","examples":[{"en":"We salute the volunteers for their tireless work.","zh":"我們向這些志願者不懈的工作致敬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We salute the volunteers who made this rescue possible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-224829cfb38f6b5e62c5","word":"salvage","forms":["salvage"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61621a5b3941c781","term":"salvage","forms":["salvage","salvages","salvaging","salvaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搶救；挽回","explanation":"指把處於危險中的人或物救出來，也可指把看似已經失去的局面挽回，例如避免失敗或爭取到平局。","examples":[{"en":"A late goal salvaged a draw for the home team.","zh":"主隊靠最後時刻的進球挽回了一場平局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Divers salvaged the boat before the storm arrived.","zh":"潛水員在暴風雨到來前搶救出了那艘船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salvage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0967115f2813a3541eae","word":"same","forms":["same"],"officialPos":"adj./pron./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e4a31851a8d757f","term":"same","forms":["same"],"pos":"adj","zh":"同一個；完全相同","explanation":"指兩個物件實際上是同一個，或在相關方面完全沒有區別，就像它們之間可以直接畫等號。","examples":[{"en":"We arrived at the same station.","zh":"我們到的是同一個車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is the same book I borrowed last week.","zh":"這就是我上週借的那本書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/same","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e95779f051baaade","term":"same","forms":["same"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相似；一樣","explanation":"指兩個人或事物在外表、性質或特點上相像，但不一定是同一個東西。","examples":[{"en":"Your new glasses are the same as mine.","zh":"你的新眼鏡和我的很像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two houses have the same shape.","zh":"這兩棟房子的形狀相同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/same","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f42aa25a0d91d48","term":"same","forms":["same"],"pos":"adv","zh":"同樣地；一樣程度地","explanation":"把同一種方式或程度延續到另一個動作、物件或情況上，就像把等號從一件事接到另一件事。","examples":[{"en":"I feel the same today as I did yesterday.","zh":"我今天的感覺和昨天一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please handle the second package the same.","zh":"請用同樣的方式處理第二個包裹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/same","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3751ef661ce7a96f","term":"same","forms":["same"],"pos":"pron","zh":"同一件事；同上","explanation":"把前面說過的同一個物件或事實再指一次，意思是“還是那個”“同樣的事”。","examples":[{"en":"The same can be said about the second plan.","zh":"同樣的話也適用於第二個計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'll have tea, and she wants the same.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/same","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89cc51c1249c14fc","term":"same","forms":["same"],"pos":"pron","zh":"同樣的東西；同類物品","explanation":"代替前面提到的同一種東西，表示“我也要那個”或“他們也是同一類人或事物”。","examples":[{"en":"You’re ordering soup? I’ll have the same.","zh":"你要點湯？那我也要一樣的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'll order the same as you.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/same","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af2bdbe1aa9b6ec1e2ad","word":"sample","forms":["sample"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c41f714b545624b","term":"sample","forms":["sample","samples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樣品；樣本","explanation":"從某種物質、產品或整體中取出一小部分，用來檢查、分析，或讓人據此瞭解整體。例如從血液中取出的部分就是血液樣本。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse took a blood sample for testing.","zh":"護士抽取了一份血液樣本進行檢測。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company sent us a sample of the new fabric.","zh":"公司給我們寄來了一塊新布料的樣品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sample","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ec02de3b35fb533","term":"sample","forms":["sample","samples","sampling","sampled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取樣；品嚐","explanation":"從某物中取一點來檢查、測試或判斷質量；對食物使用時，也可表示取一點品嚐。它把名詞 sample 的“取出一小部分”變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"Guests can sample the local cheese before buying it.","zh":"客人可以先品嚐當地乳酪，再決定是否購買。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lab sampled the river water every week.","zh":"實驗室每週都對河水取樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sample","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f79d7d24558304d8bce3","word":"sand","forms":["sand"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ec9c325b901789f3","term":"sand","forms":["sand","sands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙；沙子","explanation":"指由岩石磨碎形成的細小顆粒，常見於海灘、沙漠，也用於建築。它正是記憶影象中“一把沙”的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children built a castle in the wet sand.","zh":"孩子們在溼沙裡堆了一座城堡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sand covered the road after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，道路上覆蓋著沙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d82097af9d6e93c","term":"sand","forms":["sand","sands","sanding","sanded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用砂紙打磨","explanation":"指用沙、砂紙或類似磨料摩擦某物，使表面變得平滑或乾淨。這是從“沙粒摩擦表面”直接發展出的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I need to sand the table before painting it.","zh":"我得先把桌子打磨一下再刷漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sand the rough edges smooth.","zh":"把粗糙的邊緣打磨光滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c4d3352b8ac943f6e31","word":"sandal","forms":["sandal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-607103e43f79b52f","term":"sandal","forms":["sandal","sandals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"涼鞋","explanation":"指用帶子或條帶把鞋底固定在腳上的鞋，通常露出腳背或腳趾；可以把它想成“腳上由幾條帶子托住的鞋”。","examples":[{"en":"I wore sandals because it was hot.","zh":"天氣很熱，所以我穿了涼鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought a pair of leather sandals.","zh":"她買了一雙皮涼鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f5c570f55dd7921c986","word":"sandwich","forms":["sandwich"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd6ac1e826e3e28a","term":"sandwich","forms":["sandwich","sandwiches","sandwichs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"三明治；夾心麵包","explanation":"指把肉、乳酪、蔬菜等食物放在一片或通常兩片面包之間，作為一份便餐食用的食物。","examples":[{"en":"I made a chicken sandwich for lunch.","zh":"我做了一個雞肉三明治當午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered an open sandwich with smoked salmon.","zh":"她點了一份配煙燻三文魚的開放式三明治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandwich","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efa3d92338389f1e","term":"sandwich","forms":["sandwich","sandwiches","sandwiching","sandwiched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……夾在兩者之間","explanation":"把一個物體放在兩個通常較平或相對的物體之間，就像把餡料夾進麵包裡。","examples":[{"en":"Sandwich the cheese between two slices of bread.","zh":"把乳酪夾在兩片面包之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The document was sandwiched between two heavy books.","zh":"那份檔案被夾在兩本厚書之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandwich","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-71b483b44e0e789821b1","word":"sanitation","forms":["sanitation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bfdd462b01460854","term":"sanitation","forms":["sanitation","sanitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廢棄物衛生處理","explanation":"指把人的排洩物、汙水、垃圾等廢棄物安全處理或回收，避免它們汙染環境、傳播疾病；核心就是把“髒東西”妥善隔離和處理。","examples":[{"en":"The neighborhood needs better sanitation to keep waste out of the stream.","zh":"這個社群需要更好的衛生設施和廢棄物處理措施，才能防止垃圾進入溪流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Better sanitation reduced contamination in the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sanitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eead69638ee1e688","term":"sanitation","forms":["sanitation","sanitations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公共衛生措施體系","explanation":"指為保護人們健康而制定和實施的衛生政策、制度與實際措施；它比具體處理垃圾更寬，關注的是整體防病和衛生條件。","examples":[{"en":"The school improved its sanitation after several students became ill.","zh":"幾名學生生病後，學校改善了衛生措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Improved sanitation reduced disease in the crowded settlement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sanitation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc4b4e203f9dddce4687","word":"satellite","forms":["satellite"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2138f0672a7cc527","term":"satellite","forms":["satellite","satellites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繞行天體","explanation":"圍繞較大的天體執行的較小天體，例如月亮圍繞地球執行，因此月亮是地球的自然衛星。這裡的重點是“繞著更大的中心執行”。","examples":[{"en":"Mars has two small satellites.","zh":"火星有兩顆小型衛星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Jupiter has many satellites orbiting it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satellite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ae200db5592251d","term":"satellite","forms":["satellite","satellites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人造衛星","explanation":"人類製造並送入天體軌道的裝置，通常用來傳遞通訊訊號、收集資料或觀測地球等。它仍然保留了“圍繞中心執行”的核心形象，只是這個“附屬者”是人造的。","examples":[{"en":"The satellite sent fresh images of the storm to Earth.","zh":"這顆人造衛星把風暴的最新影象傳回了地球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The satellite transmits weather images every fifteen minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satellite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bce2966c0b0d85327956","word":"satisfaction","forms":["satisfaction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c90874bf7983bcce","term":"satisfaction","forms":["satisfaction","satisfactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"需要或願望的滿足","explanation":"指某種需要、願望或要求得到實現，好像原本的缺口被填上了。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy brought satisfaction to many local residents.","zh":"新政策滿足了許多當地居民的願望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She completed the project to her manager's satisfaction.","zh":"她完成了專案，達到了經理滿意的程度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satisfaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6d300164ed9142c","term":"satisfaction","forms":["satisfaction","satisfactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滿足感；愉悅","explanation":"指願望得到滿足後產生的愉快、安心或成就感，也就是“填上缺口”之後的內心感受。","examples":[{"en":"He gets great satisfaction from helping new employees.","zh":"幫助新員工讓他獲得了很大的滿足感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Finishing the difficult book gave her a quiet sense of satisfaction.","zh":"讀完這本難懂的書給她帶來了安靜而踏實的滿足感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satisfaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24b564a03f3b96392720","word":"satisfactory","forms":["satisfactory"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b53ea6ea87ea84e","term":"satisfactory","forms":["satisfactory","more satisfactory","most satisfactory"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人滿意的；合格的","explanation":"指某個結果、表現或條件達到要求，足以被接受，但不一定特別出色。它強調“滿意線已經達到”，而不是最高水平。","examples":[{"en":"The final report was satisfactory, although it needed a few small changes.","zh":"最終報告達到了要求，不過還需要做幾處小修改。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are looking for a satisfactory solution before the deadline.","zh":"我們希望在截止日期前找到一個可接受的解決方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satisfactory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ca0a730f2cae329","term":"satisfactory","forms":["satisfactory","more satisfactory","most satisfactory"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人滿足的；愜意的","explanation":"指某件事本身能帶來滿足、愉快或舒服的感覺，重點從“達到標準”轉向“讓人覺得滿意”。","examples":[{"en":"Finishing the repair gave her a deeply satisfactory sense of achievement.","zh":"修好東西讓她獲得了非常滿足的成就感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hearty meal brought the evening to a satisfactory close.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satisfactory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7688bd7c427206cbe6c6","word":"satisfy","forms":["satisfy"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46dd785ba4a6f36a","term":"satisfy","forms":["satisfy","satisfies","satisfying","satisfied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"足夠；令人滿意","explanation":"某件事本身達到所需程度，因此不再需要更多，也可以說它足以令人滿意。這裡重點是“東西夠不夠”，不一定明確說滿足了誰。","examples":[{"en":"A short answer will not satisfy in this case.","zh":"在這種情況下，簡短的回答不夠令人滿意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The evidence was finally strong enough to satisfy.","zh":"這些證據最終強到足以令人信服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satisfy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-138f4dc5f69dafad","term":"satisfy","forms":["satisfy","satisfies","satisfying","satisfied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使滿意；滿足需要或要求","explanation":"某人、某物或某個結果把對方的需要、期待或要求填補到“夠了”的程度，因此使對方滿意。","examples":[{"en":"The final rehearsal satisfied the director.","zh":"當天最後一次排練讓導演滿意了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This plan should satisfy everyone's needs.","zh":"這個計劃應該能滿足所有人的需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satisfy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-549ce58984289d8f0391","word":"sauce","forms":["sauce"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4378754525c548be","term":"sauce","forms":["sauce","sauces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醬汁；調味汁","explanation":"指澆在食物上、用來增加味道或陪伴食物的液體或較濃的調味品。這是 sauce 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Pour the sauce over the pasta before serving.","zh":"上桌前把醬汁澆在義大利麵上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sauce goes well with grilled fish.","zh":"這種醬汁很適合配烤魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sauce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1615b69d830f0ee25bdb","word":"saucer","forms":["saucer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-665dab43213314db","term":"saucer","forms":["saucer","saucers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"杯下小碟","explanation":"一種淺而小的圓碟，通常放在杯子下面，用來托住杯子並接住灑出的茶或咖啡。","examples":[{"en":"She placed the hot cup on the saucer.","zh":"她把熱杯子放在小碟上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A little coffee spilled onto the saucer.","zh":"一些咖啡灑到了小碟裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saucer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f9d64a3ad6c6f0c","term":"saucer","forms":["saucer","saucers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碟狀物","explanation":"指外形像小碟一樣扁平、圓而略微彎曲的物體；重點是形狀相似，不一定真的能盛東西。","examples":[{"en":"The strange saucer-shaped object hovered above the trees.","zh":"那個奇怪的碟狀物懸停在樹木上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flying saucer hovered over the village in the film.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saucer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30caae2fcb7c34ecadfd","word":"sausage","forms":["sausage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a992276b804ce1f9","term":"sausage","forms":["sausage","sausages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香腸","explanation":"用碎肉或肉類替代品加調味料製成，並裝進腸衣或類似圓筒形外皮中的食品；也可以指其中的一根。","examples":[{"en":"We had sausages and eggs for breakfast.","zh":"我們早餐吃了香腸和雞蛋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He grilled three sausages for the picnic.","zh":"他為野餐烤了三根香腸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sausage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28e12052a305cb82","term":"sausage","forms":["sausage","sausages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香腸形的東西","explanation":"指外形粗短、呈圓柱狀，整體看起來像香腸的東西。","examples":[{"en":"A sausage-shaped cloud drifted over the hills.","zh":"一朵香腸形的雲飄過山丘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Roll the dough into a long sausage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sausage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08234c948b5a00f9d33f","word":"savage","forms":["savage"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7769bbced9b0677","term":"savage","forms":["savage","more savage","most savage"],"pos":"adj","zh":"兇猛的；殘暴的","explanation":"指動物或人的攻擊性很強、力量猛烈，彷彿未經馴化的野獸突然撲來。","examples":[{"en":"A savage dog guarded the entrance to the farm.","zh":"一條兇猛的狗守在農場入口處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers fled after the savage beast charged at them.","zh":"那頭兇猛的野獸衝向徒步者後，他們趕緊逃走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/savage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fa36e091ab7a4b8","term":"savage","forms":["savage","savages","savaging","savaged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猛烈攻擊","explanation":"指像野獸一樣不加剋制地攻擊某人或某物，是“兇猛、殘酷”這一核心畫面直接變成動作。","examples":[{"en":"The bear savaged the hunter before the rangers arrived.","zh":"護林員趕到前，那頭熊猛烈攻擊了獵人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Critics savaged the director's latest film.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/savage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-157dca92e4250458339d","word":"save","forms":["save"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd2d6c1bc8ca0d01","term":"save","forms":["save","saves","saving","saved","savest","savedst","saveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"救下；避免傷害","explanation":"指把人或事物從危險、傷害或嚴重困難中救出來，是“把它拉回安全狀態”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"A passer-by saved the child from drowning.","zh":"一名路人把那個孩子從溺水危險中救了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your advice saved me from making a costly mistake.","zh":"你的建議幫我避免了一個代價高昂的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/save","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53083d6c68bb0eb3","term":"save","forms":["save","saves","saving","saved","savest","savedst","saveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"儲存檔案或進度","explanation":"在計算機或電子遊戲中，指把當前檔案、修改內容或遊戲進度記錄下來，防止之後丟失。","examples":[{"en":"Save your work before you close the program.","zh":"關閉程式前先儲存你的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I saved the document in a new folder.","zh":"我把檔案儲存到了一個新資料夾裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/save","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1cf6aa87da9a26f5e487","word":"saving(s)","forms":["saving"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8829176f7201be96","term":"saving","forms":["saving","savings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"節省；節約額","explanation":"表示因為少花錢、少用資源或採用更有效的方法而節省下來的金額或成本；重點是“原本要花的被省下來了”。","examples":[{"en":"The new supplier gave us a saving of ten percent.","zh":"換用新的供應商讓我們節省了百分之十的費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Buying in bulk can produce significant savings.","zh":"批次購買可以節省相當可觀的費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saving","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fbb5bfee9432379d","term":"saving","forms":["saving","savings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"存款；積蓄","explanation":"通常用複數 savings，指已經存下、留作將來使用的錢；它是“把錢保留下來”這一核心概念的名詞化。","examples":[{"en":"She used her savings to pay for the course.","zh":"她用自己的積蓄支付了課程費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her savings covered six months of living expenses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saving","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dfc1a1888f01d9476764","word":"saw","forms":["saw"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d73c7fb548c7210b","term":"saw","forms":["saw","saws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋸子","explanation":"saw 是有鋸齒刀刃的工具，用來來回切割木頭、金屬等堅硬材料。它是“鋸”這一動作所用的東西。","examples":[{"en":"He used a saw to cut the wooden board.","zh":"他用鋸子把木板鋸開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old saw is hanging in the shed.","zh":"那把舊鋸子掛在工具棚裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d2c333a16982798","term":"saw","forms":["saw","saws","sawing","sawed","sawn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用鋸切割","explanation":"動詞 saw 表示拿鋸子來回運動，把某物切開。它把“鋸子”這個工具義直接變成了動作義。","examples":[{"en":"They sawed the branch off the tree.","zh":"他們把樹枝從樹上鋸了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The carpenter sawed the plank in half.","zh":"木匠把木板鋸成了兩半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4108d7bc6e4abf06","term":"saw","forms":["saw"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看見的過去式","explanation":"saw 是 see 的一般過去時，表示過去某個時間看見、察覺或見到某人某物。這裡與“鋸子”或“用鋸鋸”沒有意義聯絡，只是同形詞。","examples":[{"en":"I saw Maya at the station yesterday.","zh":"我昨天在車站看見了瑪雅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw the lights go out.","zh":"我們看見燈熄滅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0b967fc60136d2ef96f","word":"say","forms":["say"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f88ac99d280b6da","term":"say","forms":["say","says","saying","said","sayest","saidst","sayeth","saith","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說出；念出","explanation":"把詞語或一段話清楚地從口中說出來，重點是實際發出這些話。","examples":[{"en":"Please say your name slowly and clearly.","zh":"請慢慢清楚地說出你的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please say your name clearly into the microphone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/say","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fba3f68d4dbace6","term":"say","forms":["say","says","saying","said","sayest","saidst","sayeth","saith","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"告訴；轉述","explanation":"把一個資訊或想法放出來，讓別人知道；既可以口頭說，也可以在文字中轉述。","examples":[{"en":"Mina said that she would call after work.","zh":"米娜說她下班後會打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She said that the train would be late.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/say","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1cf7f985ec941db","term":"say","forms":["say","says","saying","said","sayest","saidst","sayeth","saith","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寫著；顯示","explanation":"文字、標誌或標籤也能像人在說話一樣，把資訊明確寫出來或顯示出來。","examples":[{"en":"The sign says the museum closes at six.","zh":"牌子上寫著博物館六點關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her email says delivery will take another week.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/say","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa25d8a1c602dd868d62","word":"scale(s)","forms":["scale","scales"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c21a8032a1fad3e","term":"scale","forms":["scale","scales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刻度；尺度","explanation":"把 scale 想成“用刻度來量和調”：它可以是一套按順序排列的數值，用來測量、評分或表示程度。","examples":[{"en":"Please rate your experience on a scale from one to ten.","zh":"請按一到十分給你的體驗評分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey uses a five-point scale.","zh":"這項調查採用五級量表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5d9642c77f228e4","term":"scale","forms":["scale","scales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"規模；範圍","explanation":"指事情實際有多大、涉及多廣，強調活動、計劃、問題或影響的大小範圍。","examples":[{"en":"We underestimated the scale of the problem.","zh":"我們低估了這個問題的規模。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project has grown to an international scale.","zh":"這個專案已經發展到國際規模。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5ffbfcdea0c7225","term":"scale","forms":["scale","scales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秤；體重秤","explanation":"指測量物體重量或人的體重的裝置，是“用刻度來量”的最直觀畫面之一。","examples":[{"en":"I weighed the flour on the kitchen scale.","zh":"我用廚房秤稱了麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He stepped on the scale after the holiday.","zh":"假期後他站上體重秤稱了體重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-975029fe406f1e28","term":"scales","forms":["scales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秤；稱重器","explanation":"scales是用來測量物體重量的儀器，物品放上去後可以讀出重量。英語中這種家用或商用稱重器通常用複數形式表示。","examples":[{"en":"The butcher put the sausages on the scales.","zh":"肉販把香腸放到了秤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She checked her weight on the scales.","zh":"她用秤檢查自己的體重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scales","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59ad1b2fc74287ded1bb","word":"scan","forms":["scan"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-061204a1c4825f03","term":"scan","forms":["scan","scans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"仔細檢視","explanation":"指有目的地檢查或搜尋某個物件，可以是逐項細看，也可以是為了找到特定資訊而檢視。","examples":[{"en":"I gave the report a quick scan before the meeting.","zh":"開會前我快速瀏覽了一下報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A careful scan of the shelves revealed the missing file.","zh":"仔細檢視書架後，我們找到了那份丟失的檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65cf6d0f5a7d3923","term":"scan","forms":["scan","scans","scanning","scanned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細檢查或搜尋","explanation":"指有目的地逐項檢視某物，通常是為了找出特定資訊、問題或目標；可以快速完成，也可以認真細查。","examples":[{"en":"She scanned the page for the address.","zh":"她掃視頁面，尋找那個地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor scanned the article for errors.","zh":"編輯仔細檢查文章中的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aabf9db5d947f87a25fd","word":"scandal","forms":["scandal"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b6238c8d8385cc3","term":"scandal","forms":["scandal","scandals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醜聞；醜事","explanation":"指會使相關個人、團體或機構蒙羞並損害其名譽的事件，通常已經被公開報道或廣泛討論。","examples":[{"en":"The charity was caught in a financial scandal.","zh":"這家慈善機構捲入了一起財務醜聞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scandal forced the minister to resign.","zh":"這起醜聞迫使那名部長辭職。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scandal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c339fb18a1bc1439","term":"scandal","forms":["scandal","scandals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公憤；譁然","explanation":"指公眾因某種被認為不道德、不得體或不可接受的行為而產生強烈憤怒和震動。","examples":[{"en":"The judge's decision caused a public scandal.","zh":"法官的決定引起了公眾譁然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaked expenses caused widespread scandal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scandal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-715a6abcdb9f8a8eb157","word":"scar","forms":["scar"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-848acd59889ab679","term":"scar","forms":["scar","scars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮膚上的疤痕","explanation":"指傷口癒合後留在皮膚上的永久痕跡，例如手術、燒傷或割傷留下的印記。","examples":[{"en":"She has a small scar on her left knee.","zh":"她的左膝上有一道小疤痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The operation left him with a long scar across his chest.","zh":"那次手術在他胸前留下了一道長長的疤痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c870f926f66e4d6","term":"scar","forms":["scar","scars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心靈創傷","explanation":"指痛苦或創傷性經歷在人的心理上留下的長期負面影響，像身體上的疤痕一樣不容易消失。","examples":[{"en":"The bullying left emotional scars that took years to heal.","zh":"那段校園欺凌留下了多年的心理創傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The war left psychological scars long after the fighting stopped.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5461110a8658ad8","term":"scar","forms":["scar","scars","scarring","scarred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使留下皮膚疤痕","explanation":"指某件事使人的皮膚永久留下疤痕，重點是造成這個結果的一方。","examples":[{"en":"The broken glass scarred his face.","zh":"碎玻璃在他的臉上留下了疤痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The deep burn scarred his left forearm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ecf3a7b129e474a","term":"scar","forms":["scar","scars","scarring","scarred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"造成深重心理創傷","explanation":"指某段經歷深深影響一個人，使其在心理上留下長期難以消除的創傷。","examples":[{"en":"The accident scarred her for life.","zh":"那場事故給她留下了一生的心理創傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of bullying scarred his confidence deeply.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8ee5930e84539c717a6","word":"scarce","forms":["scarce"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f94da9265b9ddb0a","term":"scarce","forms":["scarce","scarcer","scarcest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"稀少；難找到","explanation":"某物數量很少，已經不容易找到；它把注意力放在“供應變少、尋找困難”上，而不一定表示這種東西本身珍貴。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water is scarce on the island.","zh":"這個島上淡水很少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Affordable apartments are scarce in the city center.","zh":"市中心價格能負擔得起的公寓很難找到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05fdc672eb5a6780","term":"scarce","forms":["scarce","scarcer","scarcest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"缺少；供應不足","explanation":"強調某個地方、系統或計劃沒有足夠的某種東西來滿足需要，重點是“供給不夠”。","examples":[{"en":"The region is scarce in medical supplies after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，這個地區醫療物資短缺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reliable transport is scarce in the mountain villages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c780d1d3701378b24ee","word":"scarcely","forms":["scarcely"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a3f667eabfa7029","term":"scarcely","forms":["scarcely","more scarcely","most scarcely"],"pos":"adv","zh":"幾乎不；大概不會","explanation":"表示某事發生的可能性或事實程度極低，接近於“幾乎不”。它把事情推到“只剩一條細縫”的程度，但不一定表示絕對不可能。","examples":[{"en":"We could scarcely hear the speaker over the noise.","zh":"噪聲太大了，我們幾乎聽不見演講者的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She scarcely remembers anything about that trip.","zh":"她幾乎不記得那次旅行的任何事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarcely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04724ca367c4a50c","term":"scarcely","forms":["scarcely","more scarcely","most scarcely"],"pos":"adv","zh":"剛剛；勉強才","explanation":"表示時間、數量或程度只勉強達到最低限度，像是“剛剛夠到”。在 scarcely had...when... 結構中，意思是“剛一……就……”，強調前一件事發生後幾乎立刻出現後一件事。","examples":[{"en":"Scarcely had the train left when it began to snow.","zh":"火車剛開走，天就開始下雪了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He had scarcely enough money to buy a meal.","zh":"他的錢勉強夠買一頓飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarcely","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad4c527da5938b221a65","word":"scare","forms":["scare"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df92d50e6150672e","term":"scare","forms":["scare","scares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一陣驚嚇","explanation":"scare 指某人突然受到的一次驚嚇，重點是害怕的經歷本身，而不是嚇人的動作。","examples":[{"en":"That loud noise gave me a scare.","zh":"那聲巨響把我嚇了一跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a real scare when the child disappeared.","zh":"孩子走丟時，我們著實嚇了一大跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07613ae9f9e6e250","term":"scare","forms":["scare","scares","scaring","scared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嚇到；使害怕","explanation":"scare 作及物動詞時表示某人或某事突然讓另一個人害怕，程度可以很輕，也可以比較強；它和名詞“一陣驚嚇”直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"You scared me when you came in so quietly.","zh":"你進來時一點聲音都沒有，把我嚇了一跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden change in the weather scared the hikers.","zh":"天氣突然變化，把那些徒步者嚇到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67f711e800796d61251f","word":"scared","forms":["scared"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01f210ebe1b6edc8","term":"scared","forms":["scared","more scared","scareder","most scared","scaredest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"害怕的；受到驚嚇的","explanation":"指人心裡產生恐懼，或剛剛被某個聲音、事件等嚇到；可以是短暫的驚嚇，也可以是持續的害怕。","examples":[{"en":"I got scared when I heard a noise downstairs.","zh":"我聽到樓下有聲音時嚇了一跳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is scared of dogs.","zh":"她害怕狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scared","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4a8d31d8a1108129ac5","word":"scarf","forms":["scarf"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6dceaae605fd7145","term":"scarf","forms":["scarf","scarves","scarfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圍巾","explanation":"一種長條形的布料或針織物，通常圍在脖子上，用來保暖或裝飾。","examples":[{"en":"She wrapped a warm scarf around her neck before leaving.","zh":"她出門前在脖子上圍了一條暖和的圍巾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red scarf was the only bright color in his winter outfit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51059046270b39e89912","word":"scary","forms":["scary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5ce72c785cb4c1b","term":"scary","forms":["scary","scarier","scariest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人害怕的","explanation":"某人或某事物會使人感到害怕、緊張或不安。它強調“讓別人害怕”，而不是“自己正在害怕”。","examples":[{"en":"That movie was too scary for my little brother.","zh":"那部電影對我弟弟來說太嚇人了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was scary walking home alone in the dark.","zh":"天黑後一個人走回家很嚇人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c380750635b6a1f3","term":"scary","forms":["scary","scarier","scariest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"驚人得不尋常的","explanation":"某種相似、變化或程度強烈得令人吃驚，甚至讓人覺得有些不安；不一定真的表示害怕。","examples":[{"en":"It’s scary how quickly children grow up.","zh":"孩子長大得這麼快，真讓人吃驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She can calculate those figures with scary speed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e1f92433f754e9f1213d","word":"scatter","forms":["scatter"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a50e60abb424c2e","term":"scatter","forms":["scatter","scatters","scattering","scattered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"散開；驅散","explanation":"表示人或物從聚集處向不同方向分開；可以說人群自己散開，也可以說某事物把人或物驅散。","examples":[{"en":"The children scattered when the rain began.","zh":"下雨時，孩子們四散開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The loud alarm scattered the birds from the roof.","zh":"刺耳的警報把鳥兒從屋頂上驚散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scatter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8822fa8994106466","term":"scatter","forms":["scatter","scatters","scattering","scattered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撒開；撒佈","explanation":"表示把少量東西松散地分佈到一片範圍內，例如撒種子、撒花瓣或撒灰燼；東西不是集中倒在一個地方，而是被分開撒出去。","examples":[{"en":"She scattered flower seeds across the sunny patch of soil.","zh":"她把花種子撒在那片向陽的土壤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind scattered dry leaves over the path.","zh":"風把幹樹葉吹得散落在小路上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scatter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee26f4137f88e2408f3f","word":"scenario","forms":["scenario"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1d430baebde9cd1","term":"scenario","forms":["scenario","scenarios","scenari"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事態發展設想","explanation":"指對一連串可能發生的事情及其發展順序的設想或概述，常用於分析某種局面會怎樣展開。","examples":[{"en":"We need a plan for the worst-case scenario.","zh":"我們需要為最壞的情況制訂計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In this scenario, the company would have to close two stores.","zh":"在這種情況下，公司將不得不關閉兩家店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scenario","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f48f7207cebf92638de","word":"scene","forms":["scene"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d5473aa122a6497","term":"scene","forms":["scene","scenes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事件現場","explanation":"scene可以指某件受人關注的事情發生的地點，尤其常用於事故、犯罪或緊急事件的現場。","examples":[{"en":"The police arrived at the scene within minutes.","zh":"警方幾分鐘內就趕到了現場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Investigators returned to the scene of the accident.","zh":"調查人員回到了事故現場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d5ece3a132bb000","term":"scene","forms":["scene","scenes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戲劇或電影中的一幕","explanation":"scene可以指戲劇、電影或故事中發生在同一地點或同一時間的一段；許多scene合起來構成一幕或更大的作品部分。","examples":[{"en":"The final scene takes place in a quiet hotel room.","zh":"最後一幕發生在一間安靜的旅館房間裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She replayed the opening scene several times.","zh":"她把開場那一幕重複播放了好幾遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e8a32c0ab98b46cb293","word":"scenery","forms":["scenery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a21b881afb73c0eb","term":"scenery","forms":["scenery","sceneries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自然風光；景色","explanation":"指一個地方展現出來的整體自然景觀，如山川、森林、海岸等，不是單獨的一件景物，而是眼前的一整片景色。","examples":[{"en":"We stopped the car to enjoy the beautiful mountain scenery.","zh":"我們停車欣賞美麗的山景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train journey offers spectacular coastal scenery.","zh":"這段火車旅程沿途能看到壯觀的海岸風光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scenery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-526e55cc1614cbec","term":"scenery","forms":["scenery","sceneries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舞臺佈景和道具","explanation":"指舞臺上用來讓觀眾感到故事發生在某個地點的背景、佈景和相關道具；它們共同構成戲劇中的“那一幕景”。","examples":[{"en":"The crew changed the scenery while the actors left the stage.","zh":"演員離開舞臺時，工作人員更換了佈景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scenery changed from a forest to a palace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scenery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-90037590f4bcacab45c1","word":"scenic","forms":["scenic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc7fdc791be15096","term":"scenic","forms":["scenic","more scenic","most scenic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"風景優美的","explanation":"指沿途或所在地點景色很美、值得觀賞。它把“景”這個核心概念進一步變成了“有觀賞價值的風景”，例如一條為了看景而走的路線。","examples":[{"en":"We have plenty of time, so let's take the scenic route.","zh":"我們時間很充裕，就走風景優美的路線吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scenic drive along the coast took nearly three hours.","zh":"沿海岸行駛的觀景路線花了將近三個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scenic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-376b0f4f7def1a2b","term":"scenic","forms":["scenic","more scenic","most scenic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與景色有關的","explanation":"指和自然景色、畫面或景觀有關，不一定強調景色特別美。這個義項仍然圍繞“可觀看的景”，但重點從“美”轉到了“景色本身”。","examples":[{"en":"The town is famous for its scenic views of the lake.","zh":"這座小鎮以湖泊的景觀聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report assesses the project's scenic impact on the valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scenic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebca3d187a58ba552304","word":"scent","forms":["scent"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69f436e784cbf148","term":"scent","forms":["scent","scents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨特氣味","explanation":"指能被聞到、並具有某種特徵的氣味，可以是香的，也可以是難聞的。它是“空氣裡留下的可辨認的線”的最基本形式。","examples":[{"en":"The scent of pine filled the cabin.","zh":"松樹的氣味充滿了小屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strange scent came from the kitchen.","zh":"廚房裡飄來一股奇怪的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32d399ef66273e94","term":"scent","forms":["scent","scents","scenting","scented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聞出、嗅到","explanation":"指透過嗅覺辨認出某物或某動物的氣味，相當於用鼻子找到那條氣味線。","examples":[{"en":"The hounds scented the fox in the woods.","zh":"獵犬在樹林裡聞出了狐狸的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog scented smoke before we saw the fire.","zh":"我們看到火之前，狗就聞到了煙味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8405c5b7f077e366","term":"scent","forms":["scent","scents","scenting","scented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"察覺、嗅出苗頭","explanation":"由聞出氣味引申為憑直覺或細微跡象察覺某種可能性，尤其是麻煩、危險或不誠實行為。","examples":[{"en":"I scented trouble when everyone suddenly went quiet.","zh":"大家突然安靜下來時，我察覺到事情不妙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager scented a chance to improve the project.","zh":"經理察覺到一個改進專案的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f72005e81c4ecbd5aa3","word":"schedule","forms":["schedule"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7da8c64d3352bbfa","term":"schedule","forms":["schedule","schedules"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日程表；安排","explanation":"指把一連串任務、活動和預計時間排在一起的計劃表，也可以泛指按這個計劃進行的安排。它的核心形象就是“把事情放進時間表裡”。","examples":[{"en":"We need to check the schedule before booking the tickets.","zh":"訂票前我們需要檢視日程安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project is running two weeks behind schedule.","zh":"這個專案比原計劃晚了兩週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/schedule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42d4d1193778f329","term":"schedule","forms":["schedule","schedules","scheduling","scheduled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"制定日程","explanation":"指建立一份時間安排，把任務或活動按先後和時間排好。它強調“做出那張安排表”，而不只是執行已經存在的計劃。","examples":[{"en":"The manager scheduled the team's work for the entire month.","zh":"經理安排了團隊整個月的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Schedule the inspection before the tenants move in.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/schedule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03ebd1db0e9de44a","term":"schedule","forms":["schedule","schedules","scheduling","scheduled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排定時間","explanation":"指為某項活動或事件確定具體的日期或時間，也就是把它放進日程表的某個位置。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting is scheduled for next Tuesday.","zh":"會議安排在下週二。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They scheduled the repair for early tomorrow morning.","zh":"他們把維修安排在明天一大早。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/schedule","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd892494455f6fa019e5","word":"scheme","forms":["scheme"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-996b242dd8da3f13","term":"scheme","forms":["scheme","schemes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計劃；方案","explanation":"scheme是一套把未來行動安排好的計劃，重點在於各步驟或部分已經被組織成一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The city introduced a scheme to help young families find affordable homes.","zh":"這座城市推出了一項幫助年輕家庭找到經濟適用住房的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Under the new scheme, employees can work from home twice a week.","zh":"根據新方案，員工每週可以在家辦公兩天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scheme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8ee9fa332e0bb44","term":"scheme","forms":["scheme","schemes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰謀；詭計","explanation":"當scheme指秘密而且通常不正當的計劃時，就是為了欺騙、操縱或獲利而設計的計謀；它仍然保留“把各步安排好”的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The police uncovered a scheme to steal money from elderly customers.","zh":"警方揭露了一個騙取老年客戶錢財的陰謀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was drawn into an elaborate scheme to defraud investors.","zh":"他被捲入了一場精心策劃的投資者詐騙陰謀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scheme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1643a70bec90a237","term":"scheme","forms":["scheme","schemes","scheming","schemed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暗中策劃","explanation":"不及物的scheme表示為了達到某個目的而暗中盤算、設計步驟，通常讓人感覺這個目的不太正當。","examples":[{"en":"They spent weeks scheming to get control of the company.","zh":"他們花了幾個星期暗中策劃，想要控制這家公司。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two officials were scheming together behind closed doors.","zh":"兩名官員在閉門秘密謀劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scheme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3f48726b892403e0552","word":"scholar","forms":["scholar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ed3111afc8d9b1f","term":"scholar","forms":["scholar","scholars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎學金學生；求學者","explanation":"指在學校或大學學習、通常因獲得獎學金而受到資助的學生。這個意義保留了“在學校裡認真學習的人”這一基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"She became a scholar at the university after winning a national scholarship.","zh":"她獲得國家獎學金後，成為這所大學的獎學金學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The college elected her a scholar and covered her tuition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scholar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69227ff1c9c18771","term":"scholar","forms":["scholar","scholars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某領域專家；學者","explanation":"指專門研究某一知識領域、並在該領域具有較深造詣的人。這是現代英語中很常見的意義，體現了從“學習者”發展為“研究者”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"She is a respected scholar of medieval history.","zh":"她是一位受人尊敬的中世紀歷史學者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scholar traced the manuscript to a medieval monastery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scholar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f552935eea2a6d769b05","word":"scholarship","forms":["scholarship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-885ff730eb4cbe73","term":"scholarship","forms":["scholarship","scholarships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎學金","explanation":"指學校、機構或個人為幫助學生學習而提供的錢或資助，通常用於支付學費、生活費或特定學習專案的費用。","examples":[{"en":"She received a scholarship to study engineering at university.","zh":"她獲得了一份在大學學習工程學的獎學金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scholarship covers tuition and accommodation for one year.","zh":"這份獎學金負擔一年的學費和住宿費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scholarship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44a0ce3607902825","term":"scholarship","forms":["scholarship","scholarships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學術研究；學術成果","explanation":"指學者進行研究、考證和論述的活動，也可指這些活動所體現出的專業水平和研究成果。","examples":[{"en":"Recent scholarship on climate history has changed our understanding of the region.","zh":"近來的氣候史研究改變了我們對這個地區的理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Recent scholarship has challenged that interpretation of the poem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scholarship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d64debd942d7dc26a851","word":"school","forms":["school"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-378fd7c3c5ed06db","term":"school","forms":["school","schools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學校；教育機構","explanation":"指專門進行教學和學習的機構，可以是公立或私立學校，也可以泛指一個教育場所或教育體系中的單位。","examples":[{"en":"Our children attend a public school in our neighborhood.","zh":"我們的孩子在附近的一所公立學校上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school has opened a new science building.","zh":"這所學校新建了一棟科學教學樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/school","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30d72c7adcdcbd93","term":"school","forms":["school","schools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中小學教育","explanation":"特指大學以前的基礎教育階段，既可以說這種教育本身，也可以說孩子在這一階段就讀的學校。","examples":[{"en":"Many children walk to school every morning.","zh":"許多孩子每天早上步行去上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The twins begin school next autumn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/school","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b44d1d9bffa41d8","term":"school","forms":["school","schools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上課時間；在校期間","explanation":"指學校開課、學生參加課程的時間段，也可以泛指一個人的學生時代或在校生活。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll see you after school.","zh":"放學後見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He learned to play chess at school.","zh":"他在學校期間學會了下棋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/school","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bb755cc914c118d","term":"school","forms":["school","schools","schooling","schooled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"教育；訓練","explanation":"指把知識、技能或行為方式教給某人，使其受到系統訓練；不一定真的發生在學校裡。","examples":[{"en":"Her coach schooled her in the basics of tennis.","zh":"她的教練訓練她掌握網球的基本功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was schooled at home by his parents.","zh":"他由父母在家裡教育長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/school","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-790fad4744a9da8d301e","word":"science","forms":["science"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cde213896c4d8b0c","term":"science","forms":["science","sciences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一門學科","explanation":"指一個有系統原則、能夠透過觀察或測量研究的知識領域，不只是憑直覺或手藝解決問題的技巧。經濟學、語言學等在特定語境下也可以被稱為一門science。","examples":[{"en":"Climate science helps us understand how the atmosphere is changing.","zh":"氣候科學幫助我們瞭解大氣正在如何變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He treats cooking as both an art and a science.","zh":"他把烹飪既看作藝術，也看作一門科學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/science","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e001951d0089f945","term":"science","forms":["science","sciences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自然科學","explanation":"特指研究自然界及其規律的學科總稱，例如物理、化學和生物學；在學校課程名稱中尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"Science was my favorite subject at school.","zh":"科學是我上學時最喜歡的科目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is studying science at university.","zh":"她在大學學習自然科學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/science","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42422a4f8e32e016","term":"science","forms":["science","sciences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"科學方法所得的知識","explanation":"指依靠科學學科、科學方法或其他系統研究得到的可靠知識，重點在“經過系統檢驗的認識成果”。","examples":[{"en":"Good science depends on careful measurements and honest reporting.","zh":"可靠的科學依賴於細緻的測量和誠實的報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Science has transformed our understanding of infectious disease.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/science","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8592edc04aed3012ef2f","word":"scientific","forms":["scientific"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8856596988ef5f86","term":"scientific","forms":["scientific","more scientific","most scientific"],"pos":"adj","zh":"科學的；與科學有關的","explanation":"指屬於科學領域，或直接和科學研究、科學知識有關。它可以修飾研究、發現、儀器等，核心畫面就是“把事情放進科學的框架裡理解”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displays scientific instruments from the nineteenth century.","zh":"這家博物館展出了十九世紀的科學儀器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is interested in scientific research on climate change.","zh":"她對氣候變化方面的科學研究感興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scientific","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fd33657d82d5ce8","term":"scientific","forms":["scientific","more scientific","most scientific"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有科學依據的；符合科學方法的","explanation":"指判斷或做法依靠觀察、實驗和證據，而不是隻憑感覺或猜測。它仍然圍繞“科學”，但重點從科學這個領域擴充套件到了做事和論證的方式。","examples":[{"en":"We need a scientific way to test whether the treatment works.","zh":"我們需要用科學的方法檢驗這種治療是否有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The claims lack a sound scientific basis.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scientific","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2da2700b851b132c6ca","word":"scientist","forms":["scientist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae3ab756c677213d","term":"scientist","forms":["scientist","scientists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"科學家","explanation":"指運用科學方法來回答關於可測量世界的問題的人。這個詞強調研究活動和方法，不限於某一個學科，因此物理學家、數學家或自然科學研究者都可能被稱為 scientist。","examples":[{"en":"The scientist tested the water to find out why the fish were dying.","zh":"這位科學家檢測了水質，以查明魚為什麼會死。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many scientists are studying how the climate is changing.","zh":"許多科學家正在研究氣候如何變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scientist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-493a15e7bda88b072720","word":"scissors","forms":["scissors"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3eaa3a32c9114b09","term":"scissors","forms":["scissors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剪薄材料的工具","explanation":"scissors是由兩片在中間交叉、圍繞轉軸開合的刀片組成的工具，用來剪紙、布、線等較薄的材料。這是這個詞最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please use the scissors to cut along the dotted line.","zh":"請用剪刀沿著虛線剪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a pair of scissors to open this package.","zh":"我需要一把剪刀來開啟這個包裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scissors","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b529a3349b914407","term":"scissors","forms":["scissors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剪刀手勢","explanation":"在“剪刀石頭布”中，scissors指食指和中指張開形成的剪刀形手勢；它能勝過布，卻輸給石頭，在特定版本中也能勝過蜥蜴、輸給斯波克。","examples":[{"en":"I chose scissors, but she chose rock.","zh":"我出了剪刀，但她出了石頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two outstretched fingers represented scissors in their deciding round.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scissors","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b781a9e933a765fe5197","word":"scold","forms":["scold"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c1d0969374ce170","term":"scold","forms":["scold","scolds","scolding","scolded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"生氣地責罵","explanation":"指因為不滿或認為對方做錯了事，而用生氣的語氣訓斥對方。這是 scold 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher scolded me for talking during the test.","zh":"老師因為我考試時說話而訓斥了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't want to scold you, but you need to be more careful.","zh":"我不想責罵你，但你需要更加小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-739123b666a7b12efb25","word":"scoop","forms":["scoop"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a499bdcce685f807","term":"scoop","forms":["scoop","scoops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舀取工具","explanation":"指帶柄的勺狀或碗狀工具，用來舀起、裝取和移動狗糧、咖啡、冰淇淋等鬆散或柔軟的物料。","examples":[{"en":"She used a scoop to fill the bird feeder.","zh":"她用一個舀勺給鳥食器裝滿了食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the scoop inside the bag of dog food.","zh":"把舀勺放在狗糧袋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scoop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-035d1b1a4f220a06","term":"scoop","forms":["scoop","scoops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一勺的分量","explanation":"指某個具體舀勺一次裝下的量，常用於咖啡、蛋白粉、冰淇淋等物料；重點不是工具，而是工具裝滿後得到的分量。","examples":[{"en":"Add one scoop of protein powder to the smoothie.","zh":"在奶昔里加入一勺蛋白粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ordered two scoops of chocolate ice cream.","zh":"他點了兩勺巧克力冰淇淋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scoop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e1f736b811c3c3e","term":"scoop","forms":["scoop","scoops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨家訊息","explanation":"指記者或媒體搶先得到並報道的重要訊息，也可指這條搶先獲得的訊息本身；就像把訊息從眾人面前先舀到自己手裡。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter got the scoop on the mayor's resignation.","zh":"那名記者搶先獲得了市長辭職的獨家訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Call me when you have the scoop on the new restaurant.","zh":"你拿到那家新餐館的獨家訊息後給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scoop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f4c9590b7be16b4","term":"scoop","forms":["scoop","scoops","scooping","scooped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"舀起或收集","explanation":"指用勺、手或類似動作把水、沙子、物品等舀起、移走或集中起來；即使沒有真正的勺子，也可以用來描寫相似的動作。","examples":[{"en":"He scooped water into his hands and splashed his face.","zh":"他把水舀到手裡，潑在自己臉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She scooped up the spilled rice with a spoon.","zh":"她用勺子把灑出的米飯舀了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scoop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5ad121307b9c486471d","word":"scooter","forms":["scooter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbcb4c85f1e2a44b","term":"scooter","forms":["scooter","scooters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑板車","explanation":"指有車把、踏板和輪子的滑板車，騎車人用腳蹬地推動它前進。這是理解其他交通工具義項的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The children rode their scooters to the park.","zh":"孩子們騎著滑板車去了公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pushed off with one foot and glided down the sidewalk.","zh":"她用一隻腳蹬地，沿著人行道滑了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scooter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9af49975cb54cc4","term":"scooter","forms":["scooter","scooters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電動滑板車","explanation":"指用電池和電動機驅動的滑板車，外形通常仍保留車把和供人站立的踏板。","examples":[{"en":"We rented electric scooters to explore the city.","zh":"我們租了電動滑板車來逛這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He commutes on an electric scooter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scooter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f161c9149882e0e1012","word":"scope","forms":["scope"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-278df15dbacab56c","term":"scope","forms":["scope","scopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"範圍；涵蓋面","explanation":"指一個主題、報告、任務或規則所涉及的廣度、深度和適用邊界，也就是“能管到、能談到哪裡”。","examples":[{"en":"Environmental impacts lie outside the scope of this report.","zh":"環境影響不在這份報告的範圍之內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tax policy falls outside the scope of this report.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5084b0bf15b77c8a","term":"scope","forms":["scope","scopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餘地；機會","explanation":"指採取行動、改變做法或發展自己的可能空間，也就是某件事還允許你做多少、發展多少。","examples":[{"en":"My job doesn't give me much scope for personal development.","zh":"我的工作沒有給我多少個人發展的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The empty room offers scope for creative redesign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a575b79868a2336db378","word":"score","forms":["score"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8426ffadf524e19","term":"score","forms":["score","scores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"得分；總成績","explanation":"比賽中一名選手或一支隊伍得到的總分，就是把每次得分一道道記下後的結果。","examples":[{"en":"Her final score was 92 points.","zh":"她的最終得分是九十二分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He set a new score for the game.","zh":"他創下了這項比賽的新成績。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/score","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcbf1b8e273eb75e","term":"score","forms":["score","scores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比分","explanation":"score 也可以指比賽雙方或多方當前各得多少分，常把這些數字連在一起表示比賽形勢。","examples":[{"en":"The score is 2–0 at halftime.","zh":"半場時比分是二比零。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final score was three goals to one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/score","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5daf5d751d1d2e6f","term":"score","forms":["score","scores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考試成績；分數","explanation":"考試或測驗中用數字、字母等表示的成績，也像把答題結果彙總成一筆分數。","examples":[{"en":"My math score improved after I practiced every day.","zh":"我每天練習後，數學成績提高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her score improved by twelve points.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/score","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b68535fddeb8e02","term":"score","forms":["score","scores","scoring","scored","scorest","scoredst","scoreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"得分；記分","explanation":"score 可以表示在比賽、比賽專案或考試中取得分數，或負責把分數記下來；這就是把刻痕式記賬變成實際得分。","examples":[{"en":"Maya scored twice in the second half.","zh":"瑪雅在下半場得了兩分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I scored 88 on the final exam.","zh":"我期末考試得了八十八分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/score","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2a9a0e7139cf7018059","word":"scorn","forms":["scorn"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-020df71bf54c2d45","term":"scorn","forms":["scorn","scorns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕蔑；鄙視","explanation":"指把某人或某事看得很低、認為不值得尊重的態度；重點不只是反感，而是帶有明顯的不屑和優越感。","examples":[{"en":"She spoke about the proposal with open scorn.","zh":"她帶著毫不掩飾的輕蔑談起那項提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He could not hide his scorn for their excuses.","zh":"他無法掩飾自己對他們那些藉口的鄙視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scorn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-593b2b1b4d199b3f","term":"scorn","forms":["scorn","scorns","scorning","scorned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鄙視；蔑視","explanation":"指以輕蔑的態度看待某人或某事，認為對方不值得尊重；也可以表示把這種輕蔑明確表現出來。","examples":[{"en":"The veteran scorned the new plan as foolish.","zh":"那位老兵鄙視這個新計劃，認為它很愚蠢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She scorns anyone who cheats to get ahead.","zh":"她鄙視任何靠作弊出人頭地的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scorn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3608e4bd0e693177369e","word":"scout","forms":["scout"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-131aa55b52e3a734","term":"scout","forms":["scout","scouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偵察員","explanation":"指被派到前方或陌生地區檢視情況、蒐集訊息並帶回報告的人，尤其指軍事偵察員。","examples":[{"en":"The scouts returned before sunset with news of the enemy.","zh":"偵察員在日落前帶著敵軍的訊息回來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scout returned with news of approaching troops.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15b40ccb3661f18b","term":"scout","forms":["scout","scouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"童軍成員","explanation":"指參加國際童軍運動及其各類組織的成員，男孩和女孩都可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter joined the Scouts when she was eight.","zh":"我女兒八歲時加入了童軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scouts learned to light fires without matches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdadbeeafd219322","term":"scout","forms":["scout","scouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球探；人才發掘者","explanation":"指負責觀察、評估併發掘有潛力的人，尤其是替體育隊尋找優秀運動員的人。","examples":[{"en":"A football scout watched the young player during the match.","zh":"一名足球球探在比賽中觀察那位年輕球員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A scout invited the young goalkeeper to a trial.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de5a39c3e4cd555f","term":"scout","forms":["scout","scouts","scouting","scouted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偵察；探查","explanation":"指在較大範圍內四處檢視、搜尋路線或目標，好像偵察員一樣摸清情況。","examples":[{"en":"We scouted the valley before choosing a place to camp.","zh":"我們先偵察了山谷，然後才選定露營地點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We scouted the valley for a suitable campsite.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d68b8f831ab9378","term":"scout","forms":["scout","scouts","scouting","scouted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"觀察；跟蹤偵察","explanation":"指像偵察員一樣觀察某人或某物，併為了持續瞭解情況而跟蹤檢視。","examples":[{"en":"The team scouted the rival before the final.","zh":"球隊在決賽前考察了對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They scouted the enemy camp from a nearby ridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2b7d61bec1eaa427952","word":"scramble","forms":["scramble"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0139cdf6d9a36d2","term":"scramble","forms":["scramble","scrambles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"匆忙忙亂","explanation":"指人為了趕到某處或完成某事而手腳並用、急急忙忙地行動，重點是匆忙和不夠從容。","examples":[{"en":"There was a last-minute scramble to finish the report.","zh":"大家在最後關頭一陣忙亂，終於把報告完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cancellation triggered a scramble to find replacement accommodation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scramble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9790033dcd1a696e","term":"scramble","forms":["scramble","scrambles","scrambling","scrambled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"匆忙移動","explanation":"指為了趕到某處而急忙移動，常常手腳並用，動作顯得不夠從容；人爬回場內或衝去救球都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"She scrambled back to her desk before the meeting started.","zh":"會議開始前，她匆匆趕回了自己的辦公桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child scrambled up the rocks after his father.","zh":"孩子跟在父親後面手腳並用地爬上岩石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scramble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db58e6a48556e7ea","term":"scramble","forms":["scramble","scrambles","scrambling","scrambled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把食材炒成雜亂的一團","explanation":"把雞蛋等食材攪散並一起烹調，使它們混合成鬆散的一團；這正是“打亂並混在一起”的廚房版本。","examples":[{"en":"I scrambled two eggs with spinach and cheese.","zh":"我把兩個雞蛋和菠菜、乳酪一起炒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He scrambled the eggs over low heat.","zh":"他用小火把雞蛋炒散。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scramble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0cfc539e460fe94c3fb","word":"scrap","forms":["scrap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c89edf6804bfb951","term":"scrap","forms":["scrap","scraps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碎片；小片","explanation":"指從完整物品上脫落或留下的一小塊、不完整的部分，例如布片、紙片或零星資料。","examples":[{"en":"She used a scrap of fabric to mend the torn pocket.","zh":"她用一小塊布料補好了撕破的口袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I found a scrap of paper with an address on it.","zh":"我找到一張寫著地址的紙片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8be6ae3f43186224","term":"scrap","forms":["scrap","scraps","scrapping","scrapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"丟棄；取消","explanation":"把原本考慮使用、實行或保留的東西當作無用殘餘處理掉；物件可以是物品，也可以是計劃或制度。","examples":[{"en":"The city scrapped its plan to build a new stadium.","zh":"這座城市取消了修建新體育場的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They scrapped the broken printer instead of repairing it.","zh":"他們把壞掉的印表機丟棄了，沒有修理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-174591972de079bef897","word":"scrape","forms":["scrape"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4483ac24c102179d","term":"scrape","forms":["scrape","scrapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擦傷","explanation":"指皮膚或其他表面被粗糙物擦過後留下的淺表傷口，通常不是深切口。","examples":[{"en":"He fell off his bike and got a scrape on his elbow.","zh":"他從腳踏車上摔下來，肘部擦傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fall left a small scrape on her elbow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32fde899261e0ffb","term":"scrape","forms":["scrape","scrapes","scraping","scraped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"沿表面刮擦","explanation":"指讓某個物體，尤其是尖銳或有稜角的物體，緊貼表面用力拖過。","examples":[{"en":"The chair legs scraped across the wooden floor.","zh":"椅子腿在木地板上刮出了刺耳的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scrape the old paint from the wooden frame.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7503ed7c3947b31","term":"scrape","forms":["scrape","scrapes","scraping","scraped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刮掉","explanation":"指用刮擦動作把附著在表面的東西去掉。","examples":[{"en":"Use a spoon to scrape the burnt rice off the bottom of the pot.","zh":"用勺子把鍋底燒焦的米飯刮下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scrape the burnt crumbs off the toast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6840b8857cc962c6","term":"scrape","forms":["scrape","scrapes","scraping","scraped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦傷；擦壞","explanation":"指因身體或物體在表面摩擦而使皮膚受傷或使表面受損。","examples":[{"en":"She scraped her knee on the rough pavement.","zh":"她的膝蓋在粗糙的人行道上擦傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The suitcase scraped the newly painted door as he carried it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a9cb6b54ea56d52a698","word":"scratch","forms":["scratch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-475a64bff84ca147","term":"scratch","forms":["scratch","scratches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劃痕；擦痕","explanation":"指尖銳物或粗糙物擦過表面後留下的細小破損或痕跡，正是“擦過表面”留下的第一道痕。","examples":[{"en":"There is a deep scratch on the table.","zh":"桌子上有一道很深的劃痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to scratch the car.","zh":"小心別把車刮出劃痕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scratch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c74b2aea462bd3ce","term":"scratch","forms":["scratch","scratches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抓撓","explanation":"指為了緩解瘙癢或刺激而用手抓皮膚的動作，就像用尖物擦過皮膚。","examples":[{"en":"The child had a quick scratch on his arm.","zh":"孩子很快抓了抓胳膊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A good scratch made the mosquito bite feel better.","zh":"好好抓撓一下後，蚊子叮的地方舒服多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scratch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2515fe53a48eb07","term":"scratch","forms":["scratch","scratches","scratching","scratched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓撓；撓癢","explanation":"用指甲、爪子或尖的東西擦過皮膚，以減輕發癢，也可表示這樣抓撓某人的身體部位。這個詞的基本畫面就是“擦過皮膚”。","examples":[{"en":"Could you scratch my back?","zh":"你能幫我撓撓背嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog scratched behind its ear with a hind leg.","zh":"那條狗用後腿撓了撓耳朵後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scratch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f501595d6f227955686","word":"scream","forms":["scream"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-155baca2959d5b2b","term":"scream","forms":["scream","screams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖叫聲","explanation":"指人在恐懼、疼痛、憤怒、興奮等強烈情緒下突然發出的尖銳而響亮的聲音，可以只是一個叫聲，也可以持續一段時間。","examples":[{"en":"A scream came from the room upstairs.","zh":"樓上的房間裡傳來一聲尖叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She let out a scream when the lights suddenly went out.","zh":"燈突然熄滅時，她發出了一聲驚叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83f9beaca1434f68","term":"scream","forms":["scream","screams","screaming","screamed","screamt","screamest","screamedst","screameth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"尖聲大叫","explanation":"指人或動物用尖銳、響亮的聲音突然叫喊，通常是因為害怕、疼痛或極度激動，也可以表示憤怒地大喊。","examples":[{"en":"The child screamed for help when he got lost.","zh":"孩子迷路後尖叫著求救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She screamed at me to get out of the car.","zh":"她衝我大喊，讓我下車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cd6c2914887dd4a68e4","word":"screen","forms":["screen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f81e15887630a566","term":"screen","forms":["screen","screens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"屏障；遮擋物","explanation":"指立起來擋住視線、風、火或其他危險的屏障，例如擋火屏或隔斷。核心畫面就是“把某個區域隔開並保護起來”。","examples":[{"en":"We put a folding screen between the beds.","zh":"我們在兩張床之間放了一扇摺疊屏風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A fire screen stood in front of the fireplace.","zh":"壁爐前放著一塊擋火屏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b7163269470b2f8","term":"screen","forms":["screen","screens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螢幕；銀幕","explanation":"指用來呈現影像、文字或投影畫面的表面，尤其是電影銀幕或投影屏。它可以看作把“隔開的表面”發展成了“承載影象的表面”。","examples":[{"en":"The title appeared on the screen before the film began.","zh":"電影開始前，片名出現在銀幕上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I could see her face clearly on the big screen.","zh":"我能在大銀幕上清楚地看到她的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df2b7e245fea79d47653","word":"screw","forms":["screw"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7fd17b2016a0646","term":"screw","forms":["screw","screws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螺釘；螺絲","explanation":"一種帶有螺旋結構、透過旋轉進入材料並起固定或連線作用的裝置，中文通常說“螺釘”或“螺絲”。","examples":[{"en":"This screw is too short to hold the shelf securely.","zh":"這顆螺絲太短，無法牢固地固定架子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a screwdriver and four screws to assemble the chair.","zh":"我需要一把螺絲刀和四顆螺絲來組裝椅子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd44829a41338479","term":"screw","forms":["screw","screws","screwing","screwed","screwn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用螺釘固定","explanation":"用螺釘旋入的方式把兩個或多個部件連線起來，核心畫面就是沿螺旋線把東西擰緊。","examples":[{"en":"Screw the bracket firmly to the wall.","zh":"把支架牢牢地擰到牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She screwed the lid onto the jar.","zh":"她把蓋子擰到罐子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f2d4a8891231d9024a9","word":"screwdriver","forms":["screwdriver"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eae6d2c37e15de1f","term":"screwdriver","forms":["screwdriver","screwdrivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螺絲刀","explanation":"一種手持或電動工具，前端卡住螺絲頭，透過轉動把螺絲擰進去、擰出來或擰緊、擰鬆。","examples":[{"en":"I need a screwdriver to tighten this loose screw.","zh":"我需要一把螺絲刀來擰緊這顆鬆動的螺絲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She used a screwdriver to open the battery compartment.","zh":"她用螺絲刀開啟了電池盒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screwdriver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5063a6ef33c86af","term":"screwdriver","forms":["screwdriver","screwdrivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"伏特加橙汁雞尾酒","explanation":"一種用伏特加和橙汁調成的雞尾酒；這裡的 screwdriver 不表示實際的工具。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered a screwdriver and two glasses of water.","zh":"我們點了一杯伏特加橙汁雞尾酒和兩杯水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ordered a screwdriver with extra orange juice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screwdriver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21a0270b7f66a1e4c259","word":"script","forms":["script"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f65939b842a6085","term":"script","forms":["script","scripts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戲劇或影視劇本","explanation":"指寫有對白、動作和場景安排的表演文字，演員、導演或製作人員可以照著它完成戲劇、電影等演出。","examples":[{"en":"The actors received the final script two days before filming.","zh":"演員們在開拍前兩天拿到了最終劇本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is writing a script for a short play.","zh":"她正在為一部短劇寫劇本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/script","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a26f3ee5e674d06c","term":"script","forms":["script","scripts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小型程式","explanation":"指為完成一個相對簡單的任務而寫的小程式；它就是給計算機寫好的“行動紙”，讓計算機按指定步驟工作。","examples":[{"en":"I wrote a script to rename all the photos.","zh":"我寫了一個指令碼來給所有照片重新命名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This script checks the files every morning.","zh":"這個指令碼每天早上檢查檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/script","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20373e409347d141","term":"script","forms":["script","scripts","scripting","scripted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"編寫指令碼","explanation":"指為表演、程式或其他活動寫出一份指令碼，把將要說的話、做的事或執行的步驟先安排好。","examples":[{"en":"He scripted the opening scene for the new film.","zh":"他為這部新電影寫了開場場景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She scripted the dialogue for the training video.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/script","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e16a9d4d1cf9ead81f53","word":"scroll","forms":["scroll"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2276a9147be05d38","term":"scroll","forms":["scroll","scrolls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"卷軸；捲起來的書寫材料","explanation":"指捲成一卷的紙、羊皮紙等，也可以指寫在這種卷軸上的文字。這個意義保留了 scroll 最直接的“把長條材料捲起來”的形象，常讓人聯想到古代文書或地圖。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a scroll with a map of the ancient city.","zh":"博物館展出了一卷繪有古城地圖的卷軸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ancient scroll was too fragile to unroll completely.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scroll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcb852fbf94b6ef9","term":"scroll","forms":["scroll","scrolls","scrolling","scrolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滾動螢幕或內容","explanation":"指透過滑鼠、觸控板或手指等，讓螢幕上的內容逐步移動，從而看到原來不在視野中的部分。也可以表示把某項內容滾出當前畫面；核心畫面仍是“一條長內容在眼前一段段展開”。","examples":[{"en":"Scroll down to see the rest of the article.","zh":"向下滾動就能看到文章的其餘部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She scrolled the photo out of view.","zh":"她把那張照片滾出了視野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scroll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e8927b61deaf6863a300","word":"scrub","forms":["scrub"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89e37ffaa1a804eb","term":"scrub","forms":["scrub","scrubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雜木叢；灌木叢","explanation":"指由低矮灌木或雜木組成的一片叢林，通常不是整齊栽培的樹林；它就像一大片粗硬的天然刷子。","examples":[{"en":"We walked through the oak scrub to reach the beach.","zh":"我們穿過橡樹林叢，走到了海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thick scrub concealed the ruined farmhouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9713241c143b82f","term":"scrub","forms":["scrub","scrubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"取消","explanation":"指原定活動、比賽或發射被取消，像把原計劃從日程上擦掉。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused a scrub of tonight's concert.","zh":"暴風雨導致今晚的音樂會被取消。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The launch scrub disappointed the waiting spectators.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-99b8f8296c55fb47","term":"scrub","forms":["scrub","scrubs","scrubbing","scrubbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用力擦洗","explanation":"用刷子、粗糙物或溼布反覆用力摩擦，把表面洗乾淨或擦亮；這是 scrub 最核心的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Please scrub the sink before the guests arrive.","zh":"請在客人到來前把水槽用力刷乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She scrubbed the mud off her boots.","zh":"她把靴子上的泥用力刷掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b442e521c36e1796","term":"scrub","forms":["scrub","scrubs","scrubbing","scrubbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取消","explanation":"把原定的活動、比賽、發射或計劃從安排中“刷掉”，即宣佈取消。","examples":[{"en":"Bad weather scrubbed the launch.","zh":"惡劣天氣導致發射取消了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The match was scrubbed because the field was flooded.","zh":"比賽因場地被水淹而取消。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-73043e4eaf1a8b05ab50","word":"scrutiny","forms":["scrutiny"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c78946a944daaad5","term":"scrutiny","forms":["scrutiny","scrutinies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細緻研究","explanation":"指把某個人或某件事拿來仔細觀察、分析，力求看清每個重要細節；核心畫面就是用放大鏡徹底檢視。","examples":[{"en":"The report deserves careful scrutiny before it is published.","zh":"這份報告發表前值得仔細審查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her research came under intense scrutiny from other scientists.","zh":"她的研究受到了其他科學家的嚴格審查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrutiny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cffe01c558da7c0b","term":"scrutiny","forms":["scrutiny","scrutinies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"徹底檢查","explanation":"指對一個情況、案件、決定或計劃進行全面而嚴格的檢查，以發現問題或確認事實；它是“拿放大鏡查清楚”的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The company’s safety practices came under scrutiny after the accident.","zh":"事故發生後，這家公司的安全做法受到了嚴格審查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal was subjected to intense scrutiny by the committee.","zh":"委員會對這項提案進行了嚴格審查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scrutiny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-038750191850488e4a95","word":"sculptor","forms":["sculptor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53458f8df38289ac","term":"sculptor","forms":["sculptor","sculptors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雕塑家","explanation":"指透過雕刻、塑形等方式創作雕塑作品的藝術家或專業創作者。記住“把材料雕出形狀的人”這個畫面，就能和表示動作或作品的詞區分開。","examples":[{"en":"The sculptor spent three months carving the marble figure.","zh":"這位雕塑家花了三個月雕刻那尊大理石雕像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her dream is to become a sculptor.","zh":"她的夢想是成為一名雕塑家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sculptor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8caa216763f1309e7f5e","word":"sculpture","forms":["sculpture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3f2e6701d26de5f","term":"sculpture","forms":["sculpture","sculptures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雕塑作品","explanation":"指透過雕刻石頭、木頭等材料，或塑形後使材料固定，製作出的三維藝術作品。重點是作品佔有真實的立體空間，而不只是畫在平面上的影象。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a sculpture of a sleeping lion.","zh":"這座博物館裡有一尊熟睡獅子的雕塑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made the sculpture from a block of wood.","zh":"她用一塊木頭製作了這件雕塑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sculpture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2db3b3ca4ff23a48","term":"sculpture","forms":["sculpture","sculptures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣義立體藝術作品","explanation":"在現代藝術語境中，sculpture 泛指任何材料或多種材料組合成的立體藝術作品，即使它不是傳統意義上“雕刻”出來的，也可以歸入這一類。","examples":[{"en":"The artist created a sculpture from recycled plastic and metal.","zh":"這位藝術家用回收塑膠和金屬創作了一件立體雕塑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sculpture combines discarded metal and colored glass.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sculpture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13bfe6cb4cd2755d","term":"sculpture","forms":["sculpture","sculptures","sculpturing","sculptured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"雕刻；塑形（較少見的動詞用法，通常用 sculpt）","explanation":"指透過切削、捏塑或其他手段，把材料做成立體形狀。這個動作義就是“製作 sculpture”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The students learned to sculpture simple figures from clay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"Artists once used these tools to sculpture stone ornaments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sculpture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a69f19c8c264850d0f0","word":"sea","forms":["sea"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08d4e7ee77bfa53e","term":"sea","forms":["sea","seas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大片鹹水海域","explanation":"sea 最基本的意思是大片鹹水組成的海域，通常比 ocean 小，但日常說法中也可泛指海洋。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon swimming in the sea.","zh":"我們整個下午都在海里游泳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat disappeared beyond the sea horizon.","zh":"那艘船消失在海平線之外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdc6bf9e0ac9163a","term":"sea","forms":["sea","seas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大型湖泊","explanation":"sea 也能指很大的湖，尤其是含鹽或半鹹水的湖；這是地名中常見的約定用法。","examples":[{"en":"The Caspian Sea is the largest enclosed body of water on Earth.","zh":"裡海是地球上最大的封閉水體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The Caspian Sea borders several countries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65cd9e48ef4dc4a01b90","word":"seafood","forms":["seafood"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-353249862ef4120c","term":"seafood","forms":["seafood","seafoods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海鮮；海產食物","explanation":"指來自海洋、可以食用的生物或食物，包括魚、蝦、蟹、貝類、海藻等。它是一個總稱，就像把海里的各種可食材料放進同一張選單裡。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered seafood for dinner.","zh":"我們點了海鮮當晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This restaurant is famous for fresh seafood.","zh":"這家餐廳以新鮮海鮮聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seafood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18bcfc7a9637793d7c39","word":"seagull/gull","forms":["seagull","gull"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0854ccb1bb1bb23","term":"seagull","forms":["seagull","seagulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海鷗","explanation":"海鷗是一種常見的海濱鳥類，通常有白色身體、較深色的翅背、尖長的翅膀和短腿。這個義項是seagull最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A seagull stole my sandwich while I was sitting by the pier.","zh":"我坐在碼頭邊時，一隻海鷗偷走了我的三明治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Seagulls were calling loudly above the fishing boats.","zh":"海鷗在漁船上方大聲鳴叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seagull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5514935ad53b8e71","term":"seagull","forms":["seagull","seagulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"布萊頓俱樂部支持者","explanation":"在英國足球語境中，Seagull可以指布萊頓足球俱樂部的球迷、球員或其他相關人士，因為海鷗是該俱樂部的暱稱來源。","examples":[{"en":"The Seagulls celebrated a dramatic win at home.","zh":"布萊頓隊在主場慶祝了一場戲劇性的勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lifelong Seagull, he never misses a Brighton match.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seagull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40d0cb4add20de2f","term":"gull","forms":["gull","gulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海鷗","explanation":"指常見的海邊鳥類，通常會在海面、海灘或港口上空盤旋、鳴叫，也常會尋找人類丟下的食物。","examples":[{"en":"A gull landed on the pier and waited for someone to drop a chip.","zh":"一隻海鷗落在碼頭上，等著有人掉下一根薯條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched gulls circle above the waves.","zh":"我們看著海鷗在海浪上方盤旋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0f668bf610e5cf9f11d","word":"seal","forms":["seal"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de8c510f095e1149","term":"seal","forms":["seal","seals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海豹","explanation":"seal可以指生活在海中的鰭足類動物，即海豹。它和“封印、密封”沒有意義上的直接聯絡，是需要單獨記憶的另一條詞義。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a seal swim past the rocks.","zh":"我們看著一隻海豹遊過岩石旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A seal surfaced beside the fishing boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da17dcc9e5d3f6a2","term":"seal","forms":["seal","seals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"印章","explanation":"seal可以是把圖案壓印到蠟或其他柔軟材料上的工具。它的核心作用是留下標誌，從而表明檔案或物品的來源、身份或正式性。","examples":[{"en":"The clerk pressed the seal into the warm wax.","zh":"辦事員把印章壓在溫熱的蠟上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The royal seal authenticated the letter delivered by the messenger.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33a3a9aa498d7ceb","term":"seal","forms":["seal","seals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"密封件；密封圈","explanation":"seal還可以指安裝在接縫處、用來阻止液體或氣體漏出的密封件。它仍然體現“把縫隙封住”的核心概念，但不一定留下印記。","examples":[{"en":"A worn seal is letting water into the machine.","zh":"磨損的密封圈正讓水進入機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The worn rubber seal allowed water to leak out.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc12f66250e5663a","term":"seal","forms":["seal","seals","sealing","sealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"封住並使其可見受損","explanation":"seal可以把容器封好，使別人不能在不留下明顯痕跡的情況下開啟它。這裡把“留下印記”的概念變成了“封住並留下被開啟的證據”。","examples":[{"en":"The medicine bottle was sealed to prevent tampering.","zh":"藥瓶已經封好，以防有人擅自開啟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Seal the sample bag so tampering will be obvious.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcdb826179d8311a","term":"seal","forms":["seal","seals","sealing","sealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"密封防漏","explanation":"seal可以把瓶子、管道或接縫封嚴，防止液體或氣體漏出。這是“封住”這一核心概念最直接的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Seal the bag tightly to keep the coffee fresh.","zh":"把袋子封嚴，保持咖啡新鮮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Seal the jar tightly to prevent leaks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1353898590b0f9ab","term":"seal","forms":["seal","seals","sealing","sealed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鎖定；保證成功","explanation":"seal可以引申為使結果確定下來，彷彿蓋上印章後就無法改變；因此“seal a victory”就是確保勝利。","examples":[{"en":"Her final goal sealed the team's victory.","zh":"她最後的進球鎖定了球隊的勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A late goal sealed their victory.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2419329067823cab5b4e","word":"search","forms":["search"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9d5fa7dff4aadfd","term":"search","forms":["search","searches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尋找；搜尋","explanation":"指為了找到某個具體的人或物而進行的一次尋找，重點在“尋找的行動”。例如找鑰匙、找失蹤人員或搜尋線索，都可以說 a search。","examples":[{"en":"The search for the missing child continued through the night.","zh":"尋找那名失蹤兒童的行動持續了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a long search, I finally found my passport.","zh":"找了很久以後，我終於找到了護照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/search","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98cbd7954c6cf956","term":"search","forms":["search","searches","searching","searched","searchest","searchedst","searcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搜查某處以尋找","explanation":"指在某個地方仔細翻找，目的是找到某物或某人；地點是被搜查的範圍，目標通常由 for 引出。","examples":[{"en":"We searched the whole house for the spare keys.","zh":"我們搜遍了整棟房子尋找備用鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue team searched the valley for survivors.","zh":"救援隊搜查了山谷，尋找倖存者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/search","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34467766aba5971a","term":"search","forms":["search","searches","searching","searched","searchest","searchedst","searcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細尋找；搜尋","explanation":"強調認真、徹底地尋找，常用於尋找證據、線索或某個失蹤的人；它本身可以不說明具體地點，但常與 for 連用。","examples":[{"en":"The police are searching for evidence in the apartment.","zh":"警方正在公寓裡尋找證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I searched everywhere for my glasses.","zh":"我到處尋找我的眼鏡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/search","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f8e24f65c57e9d506fe","word":"season","forms":["season"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4080f8879eba9ab2","term":"season","forms":["season","seasons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"季節","explanation":"一年按天氣和自然變化分成的四個主要時期：春、夏、秋、冬。","examples":[{"en":"The garden looks different in every season.","zh":"這個花園在每個季節看起來都不一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many birds migrate during the cold season.","zh":"許多鳥在寒冷的季節遷徙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/season","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-feafdda2c5c529ba","term":"season","forms":["season","seasons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某事發生的時期","explanation":"一年中某種自然現象、活動或行為特別容易發生的一段時間，例如繁殖期或收穫期。","examples":[{"en":"The rainy season begins in May.","zh":"雨季在五月開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Autumn is the season for harvesting apples.","zh":"秋天是收穫蘋果的季節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/season","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d2c13d6f9fa421125a9","word":"seat","forms":["seat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2df6c824fa68e47","term":"seat","forms":["seat","seats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"座位","explanation":"指供人坐下的位置，可以在椅子、車輛、劇院或教室中。重點是“坐的位置”，而不只是傢俱本身。","examples":[{"en":"There are two empty seats near the window.","zh":"窗邊有兩個空座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please take your seat before the film starts.","zh":"電影開始前請就座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7fcce1618845bc5f","term":"seat","forms":["seat","seats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構所在地","explanation":"由“某人坐的位置”擴充套件為“權力或機構所在的位置”，所以 seat of government 就是政府所在地。","examples":[{"en":"Washington, D.C. is the seat of the U.S. government.","zh":"華盛頓特區是美國政府所在地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city remains the seat of provincial government.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca9d46b09d0bc5fb","term":"seat","forms":["seat","seats","seating","seated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使物體就位","explanation":"把某個物件放到應在的位置，並使它穩穩貼合或固定；這是從“安置到座位上”發展出的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Make sure you seat the seal properly before closing the lid.","zh":"合上蓋子前，務必把密封圈正確裝到位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Seat the battery firmly in its compartment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e37a074a9d8dde9","term":"seat","forms":["seat","seats","seating","seated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為人安排座位","explanation":"給人提供可以坐下的位置，也就是把人安置到座位上。","examples":[{"en":"This hall can seat five hundred people.","zh":"這個大廳可以容納五百人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The host seated us near the entrance.","zh":"主人把我們安排在入口附近就座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16367aacb67a4a017c8d","word":"second","forms":["second"],"officialPos":"adj./n./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4fa451f958485c59","term":"second","forms":["second"],"pos":"adj","zh":"第二的；第二個的","explanation":"核心概念是“跟在第一之後”：在順序、編號或日期中排在第一之後的，就是第二個。","examples":[{"en":"She lives on Second Street, near the library.","zh":"她住在第二街，靠近圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is my second cup of coffee today.","zh":"這是我今天喝的第二杯咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60178bc57706647d","term":"second","forms":["second","seconds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"第二次機會；再試一次","explanation":"第一次沒有做好或沒有成功後，得到重新嘗試的機會；這個“第二次”常帶有這次有望成功的意味。","examples":[{"en":"I made a mistake, but the teacher gave me a second chance.","zh":"我犯了個錯誤，但老師又給了我一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She missed the first interview and did not get a second.","zh":"她錯過了第一次面試，沒有得到第二次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d8382a60d9122a8","term":"second","forms":["second","seconds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秒；時間單位","explanation":"“秒”是把一分鐘進一步分成六十份得到的時間單位，正好體現了記憶鉤子裡“進一步分割”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"The alarm rings every thirty seconds.","zh":"警報每三十秒響一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hold the button down for five seconds.","zh":"按住這個按鈕五秒鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/second","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0f69e19ba252767f183","word":"secondary","forms":["secondary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-083e298ac8f2182b","term":"secondary","forms":["secondary","more secondary","most secondary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"第二位的；次級的","explanation":"指在順序、來源、等級或地位上緊隨第一位或主要事物之後的。它強調“不是最初或最主要的一層”，但不一定表示沒有價值。","examples":[{"en":"The secondary effects of the treatment were carefully recorded.","zh":"這種治療的繼發影響被仔細記錄下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is a secondary source, not the original document.","zh":"這是二手資料，不是原始檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secondary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-401ec23b30b579ee","term":"secondary","forms":["secondary","more secondary","most secondary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"次要的","explanation":"表示重要性低於主要事項的。它不是說事情完全不重要，而是說在當前討論中不佔首要地位。","examples":[{"en":"Cost is secondary to safety in this project.","zh":"在這個專案中，安全比成本更重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The delay is a secondary issue compared with the technical failure.","zh":"與技術故障相比，延誤只是次要問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secondary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bb80d537b1da3e38bd3","word":"secret","forms":["secret"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e57d5d02c6bfaf3","term":"secret","forms":["secret","more secret","most secret"],"pos":"adj","zh":"秘密的；隱藏的","explanation":"指被藏起來、不公開，或有意不讓別人知道的事物。它可以修飾訊息、計劃、地點、通道等。","examples":[{"en":"They found a secret room behind the bookcase.","zh":"他們在書架後面發現了一個秘密房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team held a secret meeting before the announcement.","zh":"團隊在宣佈訊息前舉行了一次秘密會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secret","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-518e5a3e95dc5126","term":"secret","forms":["secret","secrets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秘密；機密","explanation":"指被隱藏、並且有意不讓別人知道的一條訊息、事實或情況。它通常是某個人或某些人知道、其他人不知道的內容。","examples":[{"en":"Can you keep a secret until Friday?","zh":"你能把這個秘密保守到星期五嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Maya told her brother the secret after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，瑪雅把這個秘密告訴了她弟弟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secret","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-300d7c649cc828e5","term":"secret","forms":["secret","secrets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"訣竅；關鍵","explanation":"指使某件事成功或變得容易理解的關鍵方法、原則或技巧，就像開啟隱藏之門的鑰匙。","examples":[{"en":"The secret to good bread is giving the dough enough time to rise.","zh":"做好麵包的訣竅是給麵糰足夠的發酵時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Patience is the secret to solving this puzzle.","zh":"耐心是解開這個謎題的關鍵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secret","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8148532caf684760a38","word":"secretary","forms":["secretary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24bfa25a98177929","term":"secretary","forms":["secretary","secretaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"秘書；行政助理","explanation":"指替個人或機構處理檔案、記錄、安排和一般辦公室事務的人。核心畫面是把重要資訊整理好、記下來並幫助別人順利辦事。","examples":[{"en":"I have a personal secretary to help me organize my clients.","zh":"我有一名私人秘書幫我整理客戶資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The secretary took notes during the meeting.","zh":"秘書在會議期間做了記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secretary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c77e170b1613870c","term":"secretary","forms":["secretary","secretaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政府部門負責人","explanation":"指政府中負責一個部門或領域的高階官員，級別通常遠高於普通辦公室秘書。這個義項仍保留“負責整理和管理一類事務”的核心概念，只是職責和地位擴大了。","examples":[{"en":"The Secretary of State met with the foreign minister.","zh":"國務卿會見了外交部長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The secretary of education announced the revised policy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secretary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fb45623cb3075a8af9a","word":"section","forms":["section"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ba52830932629ad","term":"section","forms":["section","sections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"切下來的部分","explanation":"指從整體上切下、分離出來的一塊或一部分，是“部分”這一系列意思的具體來源。","examples":[{"en":"The artist displayed a section cut from the old tree.","zh":"藝術家展示了一段從那棵老樹上切下來的木頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The geologist examined a thin section of volcanic rock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/section","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4aa473e562a709a1","term":"section","forms":["section","sections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體的一部分","explanation":"指某個整體、群體、領域或範圍中的一部分，不一定真的被切開；這是日常閱讀中最常見的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"A large section of the audience left before the end.","zh":"觀眾中有很大一部分人在結束前離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This section of the market is growing quickly.","zh":"市場的這一部分正在迅速增長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/section","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24cf5982f8acee02","term":"section","forms":["section","sections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檔案的一節或一部分","explanation":"指法律、報告、說明書等檔案中被劃分出來的一個部分，通常比普通段落更有結構性，也可指主要章節。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the section on safety before using the machine.","zh":"使用機器前請閱讀關於安全的那一節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rule is explained in Section 4 of the report.","zh":"這條規定在報告第四節中有說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/section","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d5d7fcf3aa35a4809f9","word":"sector","forms":["sector"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e728e8878c09ea9e","term":"sector","forms":["sector","sectors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"指定區域；分割槽","explanation":"指按行政、軍事、政治或其他管理需要劃定的區域。想象一張地圖被分成幾塊，每一塊都有明確的範圍和用途，這就是sector。","examples":[{"en":"The medical team was sent to the northern sector of the city.","zh":"醫療隊被派往這座城市的北部區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Soldiers were ordered to patrol their sector after dark.","zh":"士兵奉命在天黑後巡邏自己的分割槽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sector","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0d6a58f7249457d","term":"sector","forms":["sector","sectors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"扇形","explanation":"在幾何學中，指由圓心引出的兩條半徑和它們之間的圓弧圍成的部分。它就像從圓心切出的一塊扇面，是“整體圓形中的一個分割槽”的具體形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The diagram shows a sector of a circle with an angle of sixty degrees.","zh":"圖中顯示了一個圓心角為六十度的扇形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We calculated the area of the sector using the radius and the angle.","zh":"我們利用半徑和角度計算出了這個扇形的面積。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sector","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83a3634bf07d5b68","term":"sector","forms":["sector","sectors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟領域；行業","explanation":"指經濟活動中的一大類領域，例如金融、製造業或能源業。把整個經濟想成一個圓，sector就是其中按活動型別劃出的一個扇區。","examples":[{"en":"The technology sector created many new jobs this year.","zh":"科技行業今年創造了許多新的就業崗位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government is offering support to the agricultural sector.","zh":"政府正在為農業領域提供支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sector","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6a934b45144e3758911e","word":"secure","forms":["secure"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c23aaf1f5008bf6a","term":"secure","forms":["secure","securer","more secure","securest","most secure"],"pos":"adj","zh":"安全的；受保護的","explanation":"表示人、群體或地方不受攻擊和危險威脅，處在受到保護的狀態，是secure最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children felt secure in their new home.","zh":"孩子們在新家裡感到很安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village is secure from attack.","zh":"這個村莊不受攻擊威脅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1dd62a2fd521e815","term":"secure","forms":["secure","securer","more secure","securest","most secure"],"pos":"adj","zh":"穩固的；穩定的","explanation":"表示結構、地位、關係或安排牢靠，不容易倒塌、失敗或發生劇烈變化；這正是“保護層”帶來的穩固感。","examples":[{"en":"She finally has a secure job.","zh":"她終於有了一份穩定的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ladder is secure now.","zh":"梯子現在已經固定穩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68564f20fd9a4978","term":"secure","forms":["secure","securer","more secure","securest","most secure"],"pos":"adj","zh":"確信的；有把握的","explanation":"表示對某個判斷或結果沒有疑慮，認為它可靠而確定；這裡保護的不是人身，而是自己的判斷不受懷疑動搖。","examples":[{"en":"She felt secure of victory after the final debate.","zh":"最後一場辯論後，她確信自己會獲勝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt secure in the knowledge that help was near.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f1fcccb1459c8dd","term":"secure","forms":["secure","secures","securing","secured","securest","securedst","secureth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；使安全","explanation":"表示主動採取措施，使人或事物免受危險、攻擊或損害；也就是把物件放進安全的保護層。","examples":[{"en":"The guards secured the building before the event.","zh":"活動開始前，警衛保護好了那座大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The measures will secure the public against further attacks.","zh":"這些措施將保護公眾免受進一步的攻擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-71ab93531715c50c","term":"secure","forms":["secure","secures","securing","secured","securest","securedst","secureth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"確保；使免於損失","explanation":"表示透過安排、保證或擔保，使某個結果一定實現，或使某人不承擔某種損失；重點是把不確定的結果變得穩妥。","examples":[{"en":"The contract secured a regular income for the family.","zh":"這份合同確保了這個家庭有穩定的收入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Insurance can secure you against unexpected costs.","zh":"保險可以使你免受意外費用的損失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d2d3ceb7abe55234427","word":"security","forms":["security"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65fb4b903cdd7b44","term":"security","forms":["security","securities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安全；保障","explanation":"指不受身體、心理、情感或經濟方面威脅的狀態，也就是那扇門把危險擋在外面後的安心感。","examples":[{"en":"Regular savings give her a greater sense of financial security.","zh":"定期儲蓄讓她更有經濟安全感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children need to feel security and stability at home.","zh":"孩子需要在家裡感到安全和穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/security","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e7e4f28f91a769d","term":"security","forms":["security","securities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"證券","explanation":"在金融領域，指可以交易的金融資產，如股票或債券；它把投資者對資產或收益的權利變成可持有、可轉讓的“保障憑證”。","examples":[{"en":"The fund invests in government securities and company shares.","zh":"這隻基金投資於政府證券和公司股票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exchange suspended trading in the security.","zh":"交易所暫停了這項證券的交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/security","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ac21972b8c1d790c9ca","word":"seduce","forms":["seduce"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-048a913ee797a966","term":"seduce","forms":["seduce","seduces","seducing","seduced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引入歧途","explanation":"指用誘惑或花言巧語把某人從應守的職責、原則或正確行為上引開，使其走偏。","examples":[{"en":"The gang tried to seduce young people into joining them.","zh":"那個團伙試圖誘使年輕人加入他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was seduced into betraying his friends.","zh":"他被誘使背叛了朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seduce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75127c268025d692","term":"seduce","forms":["seduce","seduces","seducing","seduced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸引；迷住","explanation":"指某種外表、氣氛或魅力把人吸引過去，使人難以抗拒；這裡不一定涉及性，也不一定表示真的做錯事。","examples":[{"en":"She was seduced by the city's energy and endless possibilities.","zh":"這座城市的活力和無限可能吸引了她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The promise of quick success seduced him into taking the risky job.","zh":"迅速成功的誘惑使他接受了這份有風險的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seduce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa9e9b5c907d50feb410","word":"see","forms":["see"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-355bd5b34fe4eea5","term":"see","forms":["see","sees","seeing","saw","seen","seent","seed","seest","sawest","seeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看見；察覺","explanation":"用眼睛直接看到或察覺某人、某物，也可表示透過視覺發現它。","examples":[{"en":"I saw a fox near the garden this morning.","zh":"我今天早上在花園附近看見了一隻狐狸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Did you see the sign by the door?","zh":"你看見門旁邊的牌子了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/see","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-544612df79387500","term":"see","forms":["see","sees","seeing","saw","seen","seent","seed","seest","sawest","seeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"理解","explanation":"把對方的意思“看清楚”了，因此表示理解觀點、解釋或暗示。","examples":[{"en":"I see what you mean now.","zh":"我現在明白你的意思了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you see why this matters?","zh":"你明白這為什麼重要嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/see","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b469f5aaf7ae3d4b","term":"see","forms":["see","sees","seeing","saw","seen","seent","seed","seest","sawest","seeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"見面；拜訪","explanation":"把某人帶到眼前來相處，因此表示與人見面、拜訪或接受診治。","examples":[{"en":"I’m seeing my sister for lunch on Sunday.","zh":"我星期日要和姐姐見面吃午飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You should see a doctor about that cough.","zh":"你應該為那咳嗽去看醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/see","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-19b25856e1c150ca834c","word":"seed","forms":["seed"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0d4f14c54789e1b","term":"seed","forms":["seed","seeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物種子","explanation":"植物的種子，或任何可以播下並長成新植物的繁殖部分；這裡也包括有些類似種子的塊莖和鱗莖。","examples":[{"en":"She planted sunflower seeds along the fence.","zh":"她沿著籬笆種下了向日葵種子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These seeds should sprout within a week.","zh":"這些種子應該會在一週內發芽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-445f7e206a86389f","term":"seed","forms":["seed","seeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"萌芽因素；源頭","explanation":"指後來想法、變化或事件得以發展的最初因素，就像一粒種子孕育出一株植物一樣。","examples":[{"en":"That conversation planted the seed of a new idea.","zh":"那次談話為一個新想法埋下了種子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small acts of kindness can be the seed of lasting change.","zh":"微小的善舉可能成為持久改變的源頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67e2453803a642a2","term":"seed","forms":["seed","seeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"初始位置；種子排名","explanation":"在比賽中指根據實力或賽季成績安排的初始排名或位置；排名越靠前，通常越有利。","examples":[{"en":"She is the top seed in this year's tournament.","zh":"她是今年錦標賽的頭號種子選手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team earned a high seed after a strong season.","zh":"這支球隊憑藉出色的賽季表現獲得了較高的種子排名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cbd345d6a2815fa88d10","word":"seek","forms":["seek"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fda2edc89edc7f0b","term":"seek","forms":["seek","seeks","seeking","sought","seeked","seekest","soughtest","seeketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"尋找；搜尋","explanation":"主動去找某個人、東西、答案或知識，重點是帶著目的尋找。它可以表示實際搜尋，也可以表示尋找抽象的答案或智慧。","examples":[{"en":"She is seeking a better solution to the problem.","zh":"她正在尋找解決這個問題的更好辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people seek wisdom in difficult times.","zh":"許多人會在困難時期尋求智慧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00c39a5ee258fbed","term":"seek","forms":["seek","seeks","seeking","sought","seeked","seekest","soughtest","seeketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"請求；尋求","explanation":"把某種幫助、許可、意見或寬恕作為目標主動請求，像是“去尋求某物”。","examples":[{"en":"He sought advice from an experienced teacher.","zh":"他向一位有經驗的老師徵求意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company sought permission to use the image.","zh":"公司請求獲准使用這張圖片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efda5a5ed7a7a497","term":"seek","forms":["seek","seeks","seeking","sought","seeked","seekest","soughtest","seeketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"追求；爭取","explanation":"把某種財富、成功、機會或結果當作目標，主動努力去獲得它；這裡“找”的物件是想得到的目標。","examples":[{"en":"She moved to the city to seek new opportunities.","zh":"她搬到城裡去尋找新的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign seeks better conditions for temporary workers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d26b980930289c594463","word":"seem","forms":["seem"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08271ffefa222ede","term":"seem","forms":["seem","seems","seeming","seemed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看起來；似乎","explanation":"表示根據看到的外表、聽到的資訊或當前情況形成印象，相當於“看起來……、似乎……”。這種說法保留了一點不確定性，表示說話人是在作判斷，而不是斷言事實。","examples":[{"en":"You seem tired today.","zh":"你今天看起來很累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It seems to be raining outside.","zh":"外面似乎正在下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5d6350213caff46c28c","word":"seesaw","forms":["seesaw"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"seesaw","forms":["seesaw"],"pos":"n.","zh":"翹翹板","examples":[{"en":"The children took turns playing on the seesaw.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"One end of the seesaw rose as the other went down.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"seesaw","forms":["seesaw"],"pos":"v.","zh":"上下變動；交替變化","examples":[{"en":"Prices may seesaw as investors react to the news.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The two teams continued to seesaw between attack and defense.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-03e71c6d7dc6bd4e89ce","word":"segment","forms":["segment"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a902bc6bed19bb5e","term":"segment","forms":["segment","segments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段","explanation":"指某個連續物體中的一段，重點是它只是整體被擷取出來的一部分，不一定有特殊形狀。","examples":[{"en":"A segment of the rope was badly worn.","zh":"這根繩子有一段磨損得很厲害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers replaced a damaged segment of the pipe.","zh":"工人更換了管道中損壞的一段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/segment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44a376370fc662c8","term":"segment","forms":["segment","segments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體中的一部分","explanation":"指一個整體自然分開或被人為分割後形成的部分，例如水果的一瓣、葉子的一部分或複合結構中的一段。","examples":[{"en":"She peeled an orange and handed me a segment.","zh":"她剝開一個橙子，遞給我一瓣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This segment of the leaf has turned brown.","zh":"這片葉子的這一部分已經變黃褐了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/segment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c84b2805000227c","term":"segment","forms":["segment","segments","segmenting","segmented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分段","explanation":"指把文章、資料、圖表或其他整體劃分成若干部分，使每一段具有相對清楚的範圍或主題。","examples":[{"en":"Please segment the report by topic before the meeting.","zh":"請在會議前按主題把報告分成幾部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The study segments customers into three age groups.","zh":"這項研究把顧客分成三個年齡組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/segment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-313fac0832f7f9798797","word":"seize","forms":["seize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-795ce2cbe366f937","term":"seize","forms":["seize","seizes","seizing","seized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓住；攫取","explanation":"指有意而突然地伸手抓住、攫取或捕獲某人或某物，重點是動作迅速而有力。","examples":[{"en":"The child seized my hand and pulled me toward the door.","zh":"孩子一把抓住我的手，把我拉向門口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police seized the stolen car.","zh":"警方扣押了那輛被盜的汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3938fdf1133c9d73","term":"seize","forms":["seize","seizes","seizing","seized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抓住機會","explanation":"把機會或有利條件想象成可以抓住的東西，表示及時利用它，不讓它溜走。","examples":[{"en":"She seized the opportunity to study abroad.","zh":"她抓住了出國留學的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should seize this chance before it disappears.","zh":"我們應該在這個機會消失前抓住它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfe03a4d8631ff53","term":"seize","forms":["seize","seizes","seizing","seized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"奪取；依法沒收","explanation":"表示透過武力、法律或官方權力把某人或某物奪取並置於自己的控制之下。","examples":[{"en":"Customs officers seized the illegal drugs at the airport.","zh":"海關人員在機場查獲並沒收了那批非法毒品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government seized the company's assets.","zh":"政府沒收了這家公司的資產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-efe5d9ec82c31b1b2cd1","word":"seldom","forms":["seldom"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cacc09a4c47a3602","term":"seldom","forms":["seldom","more seldom","seldomer","most seldom","seldomest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"很少；不常","explanation":"表示某件事發生的次數很少，但不是一次也沒有；它正是“那扇門很少開啟”的副詞表達。","examples":[{"en":"They seldom come here now.","zh":"他們現在很少來這裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I seldom watch television during the week.","zh":"我平時工作日很少看電視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seldom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1a36d25d9633ed2ac04","word":"select","forms":["select"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4ebe28cef663198","term":"select","forms":["select","more select","most select"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精選的；少數受優待的","explanation":"指從一大群人或一批物件中挑出的少數，因而顯得特別受重視或有資格參加某事。它強調“被挑出來”，而不只是客觀上存在於一個選擇範圍內。","examples":[{"en":"Only a select few were invited to the private dinner.","zh":"只有少數受特別邀請的人參加了這場私人晚宴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a select group received invitations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/select","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a08819086c20d70c","term":"select","forms":["select","more select","most select"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精選的；上等的","explanation":"指某種東西是從同類中挑出來的優質部分，也就是“挑出來的好東西”。它和“少數受優待的人”共享同一個核心：先從整體中篩選，再突出被選物件的價值。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves select cuts of local beef.","zh":"這家餐館供應精選的本地牛肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel offers a select range of regional wines.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/select","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b3a68c698d4fcf4","term":"select","forms":["select","selects","selecting","selected","selectest","selectedst","selecteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"選擇；挑選","explanation":"指從多個可能物件中挑出一個或多個，重點是經過判斷後把目標單獨選出來。這個動作義是整詞的中心，也解釋了“精選的”和裝置上“選擇按鈕”等其他用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please select your preferred delivery date.","zh":"請選擇你希望的送貨日期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She selected the quietest table in the corner.","zh":"她挑選了角落裡最安靜的一張桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/select","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65045134064dd4d90566","word":"selection","forms":["selection"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7723f2dce815634b","term":"selection","forms":["selection","selections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選擇過程","explanation":"指從多個候選者或可能性中挑選一個或一些的過程，重點在“挑選”這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The selection of a new team leader took several weeks.","zh":"選擇新的團隊負責人花了好幾個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The large number of applicants made the selection difficult.","zh":"申請人數量很多，使這次選擇變得很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/selection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-99978d5e9cfa7bb2","term":"selection","forms":["selection","selections"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選中的東西","explanation":"指經過挑選後被選中的人、物或選項，重點在“挑出來的結果”。","examples":[{"en":"Our final selection was a small apartment near the station.","zh":"我們最後選定的是車站附近的一套小公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She showed us her selection for the school exhibition.","zh":"她向我們展示了她為學校展覽選出的作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/selection","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0f7c0be2df73e42f3ef","word":"selective","forms":["selective"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1cfeee8e1b7dff49","term":"selective","forms":["selective","more selective","most selective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"挑剔的；慎重挑選的","explanation":"形容一個人在選擇商品、朋友、食物等時標準較高，不會隨便接受。它是“篩選”這一核心意思在人身上的延伸：這個人像一張篩孔很細的網，只讓符合標準的東西透過。","examples":[{"en":"She is very selective about the clothes she buys.","zh":"她買衣服時非常挑剔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is selective about whom he invites to dinner.","zh":"他會慎重選擇邀請誰來吃飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/selective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5bff6fc3bfbc368","term":"selective","forms":["selective","more selective","most selective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與篩選過程有關的","explanation":"指按照某種標準從一批物件中篩掉一部分、留下另一部分，常用於演算法、資料處理或其他篩選過程。它突出的是“有選擇地處理”，而不是把所有物件一視同仁。","examples":[{"en":"The selective algorithm removes duplicate data before training.","zh":"這個篩選演算法會在訓練前刪除重複資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Selective breeding produced plants with larger fruit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/selective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06c604b332b386b6cce8","word":"self","forms":["self"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48e90fb0b622f26a","term":"self","forms":["self","selves","selfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自我；個性","explanation":"指一個人的獨特性格、氣質和處世方式，是這個人長期經歷中形成的“內在自己”。","examples":[{"en":"Travel helped her discover a more confident self.","zh":"旅行幫助她發現了一個更自信的自我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Travel helped her develop a stronger sense of self.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/self","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1be06d5449483d3d","term":"self","forms":["self","selves","selfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意識中的自我","explanation":"指正在感受、思考和體驗世界的那個“自己”，也就是各種感覺和思想所歸屬的主體。","examples":[{"en":"Meditation can change the way we experience the self.","zh":"冥想可以改變我們體驗自我的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diary reveals a growing awareness of self.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/self","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae6df10be39cd67b","term":"self","forms":["self","selves","selfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人；自我主體","explanation":"指作為獨立意識主體的一個人，強調“這個人本身”以及他對自身的認識。","examples":[{"en":"Each person develops a sense of self over time.","zh":"每個人都會逐漸形成自我意識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Meditation helped him develop a stronger sense of self.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/self","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18c76b5a4a409a0aff42","word":"selfish","forms":["selfish"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03f246fdd420a1f6","term":"selfish","forms":["selfish","more selfish","selfisher","most selfish","selfishest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"以自身利益為標準","explanation":"指一個人在作決定時主要拿自己的利益、需要或感受作標準，不一定已經達到完全不顧他人的程度。它強調“從自己的立場出發”，是“自私”這個更強烈意思的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"It is selfish to make every decision based only on what you want.","zh":"每個決定都只按自己的願望來作，是以自我利益為中心的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a selfish view of the problem and ignored the family's needs.","zh":"她從自身利益出發看待這個問題，忽略了家人的需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/selfish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-844a61e59c62f82f","term":"selfish","forms":["selfish","more selfish","selfisher","most selfish","selfishest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"只顧自己、不顧他人","explanation":"指一個人過分或專門關心自己的幸福、利益或享樂，對他人的需要幾乎不加考慮。這是日常英語中最常見、最明確的貶義用法。","examples":[{"en":"It was selfish of him to take the last seat without asking anyone else.","zh":"他不問別人就拿走最後一個座位，實在太自私了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be selfish; leave some cake for your sister.","zh":"別這麼自私，給你妹妹留一點蛋糕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/selfish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0f21d451463ec3e3254","word":"sell","forms":["sell"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16b0d81ba25cd496","term":"sell","forms":["sell","sells","selling","sold"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出售；賣","explanation":"把商品或服務交給別人，以換取錢或其他報酬。這是 sell 最基本、最需要先掌握的義項。","examples":[{"en":"She sold her old car to a neighbor.","zh":"她把自己的舊車賣給了鄰居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop sells fresh bread every morning.","zh":"這家店每天早上賣新鮮麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6fe883e48bf326d8","term":"sell","forms":["sell","sells","selling","sold"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推銷產品或服務","explanation":"不一定親自收錢，而是努力讓別人接受某個產品、服務或方案。它仍然來自“把東西賣出去”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The simple setup sells the service to busy parents.","zh":"這種簡單的安裝方式很能吸引忙碌的家長購買這項服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You do not need to sell the plan to me; I already like it.","zh":"你不用向我推銷這個計劃，我已經喜歡上它了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b4e58cd7cb1cbf25bcf0","word":"semester","forms":["semester"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49cf704c57701c17","term":"semester","forms":["semester","semesters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學期","explanation":"指學校或大學學年中的一個教學階段，通常一年分為秋季學期和春季學期等幾個部分；在美國語境中，一個學期常約為半年。","examples":[{"en":"I will graduate at the end of the spring semester.","zh":"我將在春季學期末畢業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This semester, I am taking three science classes.","zh":"這學期我選了三門理科課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/semester","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b246cf89fe828ae4e9e8","word":"seminar","forms":["seminar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-52356954d83eff11","term":"seminar","forms":["seminar","seminars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學術研討會","explanation":"指高等教育中圍繞某一研究主題定期討論的課程或會議，學生通常在教授指導下交流研究成果和觀點。它像一間播種思想的房間，重點不是單向聽講，而是深入討論。","examples":[{"en":"She is attending a seminar on modern political theory.","zh":"她正在參加一場關於現代政治理論的學術研討會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each student presented a paper at the seminar.","zh":"每名學生都在研討會上展示了一篇論文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seminar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97897cf425ea3249","term":"seminar","forms":["seminar","seminars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行業或培訓研討會","explanation":"指同一行業的人，或一群員工，為了交換實用資訊、接受培訓而舉行的會議。這裡播下的不是學術研究種子，而是工作方法和行業經驗。","examples":[{"en":"The company held a training seminar for new employees.","zh":"公司為新員工舉辦了一場培訓研討會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The seminar covers practical techniques for new managers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seminar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ac41e467f19c3ec0050","word":"senator","forms":["senator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25175a9c844b55fa","term":"senator","forms":["senator","senators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參議院議員","explanation":"指參議院這一立法機構的成員，通常由選舉產生，負責參與審議和制定法律；在美國、加拿大等國家的政治語境中尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"The senator from Ohio spoke against the bill.","zh":"來自俄亥俄州的那位參議員發言反對這項法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several senators called for an independent investigation.","zh":"幾名參議員要求進行獨立調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/senator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b94c92495192990e","term":"senator","forms":["senator","Senators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"參議員這一職銜","explanation":"指某人當選並擔任參議員這一職位時所使用的稱號，重點在正式身份或職銜本身。","examples":[{"en":"Senator Lee introduced the new education bill.","zh":"李參議員提出了新的教育法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Senator Evans will address the committee this afternoon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/senator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27ce1d1bf4270020e179","word":"send","forms":["send"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e2bf2445f65976a","term":"send","forms":["send","sends","sending","sent","sended","sendest","sentest","sendeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳送；派送","explanation":"send 的核心動詞義是讓人、物品或訊息離開這裡併到達另一處或另一個人那裡。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll send the documents to you this afternoon.","zh":"我今天下午把檔案發給你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sent her assistant out for coffee.","zh":"她派助理出去買咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/send","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2161403032b8314a5249","word":"senior","forms":["senior"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0858c0efcd29f416","term":"senior","forms":["senior","more senior","most senior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"年長的","explanation":"指年齡比另一個人或某一群體更大，常用於較正式地說“年長者”或“老年人”。這個意義保留了“走在前面、年紀更大”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The community center offers free classes for senior citizens.","zh":"社群中心為老年人提供免費課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The senior sibling usually picked up the younger children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/senior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45ba19c2a7e2fd44","term":"senior","forms":["senior","more senior","most senior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"資歷或級別更高的","explanation":"表示在職位、經驗、權威或組織等級上高於別人，因此可以理解為“走在隊伍前面的人”。它不一定表示年齡更大，也可能只是工作資歷更深。","examples":[{"en":"She is a senior member of the research team.","zh":"她是研究團隊中的資深成員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The director is senior to everyone on the committee.","zh":"這位主任的級別高於委員會中的所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/senior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e008c0408bcb1a2","term":"senior","forms":["senior","more senior","most senior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"高年級的；畢業班的","explanation":"在美國英語學校語境中，指高中或大學最後一年的學生或與這一年級有關的事物，也就是即將畢業的高年級身份。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is a senior at a university in California.","zh":"我姐姐是加利福尼亞一所大學的畢業班學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The senior class is preparing for graduation.","zh":"畢業班正在準備畢業典禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/senior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaad4ce65ed4a039","term":"senior","forms":["senior","seniors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比某人年長的人","explanation":"表示某人年齡比另一個人大，常用於明確的年齡比較。這裡的核心是“在年齡上走在對方前面”，不一定表示職位更高。","examples":[{"en":"He is five years her senior.","zh":"他比她大五歲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Although born in the same year, my cousin is my senior by eight months.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/senior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-595f053100ff29519921","word":"sensation","forms":["sensation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9df2f241a7fab38f","term":"sensation","forms":["sensation","sensations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體感覺","explanation":"指身體接觸、受到刺激或經歷某種狀態時產生的感覺或感知，例如疼痛、刺癢、溫暖，或一種難以說明的內心感受；它是“感覺被掀起的浪”最基本的一層。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a sharp sensation in my left foot.","zh":"我感到左腳有一陣尖銳的刺痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cool water gave me a pleasant sensation.","zh":"涼水給了我一種舒服的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcf335d34aa174c2","term":"sensation","forms":["sensation","sensations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引起轟動","explanation":"指某件事引起許多人強烈的興趣、興奮或議論，使個人的感覺擴散成公眾共同的“感覺浪”。它常可譯為“轟動、引起轟動的事”。","examples":[{"en":"The singer's surprise performance caused a sensation online.","zh":"這位歌手的驚喜演出在網上引起了轟動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her unusual invention made a sensation at the fair.","zh":"她那項不同尋常的發明在展會上引起了轟動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5146f25dc5079599b09b","word":"sense","forms":["sense"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5beb12357bcf16d0","term":"sense","forms":["sense","senses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感官","explanation":"指生物感知外界物理世界的能力，如視覺、聽覺、嗅覺、味覺和觸覺；也可以指其中的一種感官。","examples":[{"en":"Our sense of smell becomes weaker as we get older.","zh":"我們的嗅覺會隨著年齡增長而變弱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dark room made it harder to use our other senses.","zh":"黑暗的房間讓我們更難運用其他感官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1db5916d8f9bcc90","term":"sense","forms":["sense","senses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意識；感覺","explanation":"指心智對某種情況、狀態或危險的察覺，也可以表示由這種察覺形成的內在感覺，如安全感。","examples":[{"en":"She had a strong sense that something was wrong.","zh":"她強烈地感覺到有些不對勁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The warm lighting gives the room a sense of comfort.","zh":"溫暖的燈光讓房間給人一種舒適感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa9dc09fb366eeab","term":"sense","forms":["sense","senses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意義；道理","explanation":"指語言、行為或情況所表達的意義、理由或價值；如果某件事沒有 sense，就表示它讓人無法理解或不合道理。","examples":[{"en":"Your explanation makes sense now.","zh":"你的解釋現在講得通了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This rule makes no sense in practice.","zh":"這條規定在實際中毫無道理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9c11a88a50a72a7","term":"sense","forms":["sense","senses","sensing","sensed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感知","explanation":"指用視覺、聽覺、嗅覺、味覺或觸覺察覺到某個物件或變化。","examples":[{"en":"The dog sensed movement outside the house.","zh":"狗察覺到屋外有動靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sensed smoke before I saw the fire.","zh":"我還沒看到火，就先聞到了煙味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9210c20e2cf5cb0","term":"sense","forms":["sense","senses","sensing","sensed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"察覺；意識到","explanation":"指不一定經過明確推理，憑直覺或細微跡象意識到某種態度、情緒或情況。","examples":[{"en":"I sensed that he was disappointed.","zh":"我察覺到他很失望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sensed tension in the room.","zh":"她察覺到房間裡的氣氛很緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-166e1cc67cfbf03427b3","word":"sensible","forms":["sensible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2b89edfed1e0c14","term":"sensible","forms":["sensible","more sensible","most sensible","sensiblest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明智的；講道理的","explanation":"指一個人能根據事實和理性作出穩妥判斷，或某個想法、決定本身合理可行。它體現的是“能感覺並會判斷”的能力。","examples":[{"en":"It would be sensible to check the address before we leave.","zh":"我們出發前核對一下地址會比較明智。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mina gave me some sensible advice about saving money.","zh":"米娜給了我一些關於省錢的明智建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5811618cf5295b66","term":"sensible","forms":["sensible","more sensible","most sensible","sensiblest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"實用舒適的","explanation":"形容衣服、鞋子等重視舒適、耐用和方便，而不是隻追求漂亮、正式或時髦。這是“明智地選擇適合實際需要的東西”的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"Wear sensible shoes because we will be walking all day.","zh":"我們要走一整天，穿雙舒適實用的鞋子吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wear sensible shoes for walking on cobbled streets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d5e8600a4fba66e5c6a","word":"sensitive","forms":["sensitive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f71fd364849fd98c","term":"sensitive","forms":["sensitive","more sensitive","most sensitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易受傷或難過的","explanation":"指一個人像被輕輕碰到也會疼一樣，很容易因批評、壞訊息或別人的話而感到難過、生氣或受傷。","examples":[{"en":"She is sensitive about comments on her accent.","zh":"她很在意別人評論她的口音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is sensitive and takes criticism personally.","zh":"他比較敏感，總把批評當成針對自己。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30ce2394c090d8b2","term":"sensitive","forms":["sensitive","more sensitive","most sensitive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"體察他人感受的","explanation":"指能察覺別人的情緒和處境，並主動避免用話語或行為傷害對方；這是“感知很靈”在人際關係中的積極發展。","examples":[{"en":"She is sensitive to the needs of new employees.","zh":"她很體察新員工的需求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thank you for being sensitive to how I feel.","zh":"謝謝你體諒我的感受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensitive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c16250fd4bb6980cadb","word":"sensitivity","forms":["sensitivity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6767f74702babef4","term":"sensitivity","forms":["sensitivity","sensitivities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敏感性；敏感程度","explanation":"指人、群體、語言、問題或局勢容易受到影響、引起反應，因而需要小心處理的性質，也可以泛指“敏感”的狀態。它把“感應線”放在社會和人際關係中：一點變化就可能引起明顯反應。","examples":[{"en":"The editor handled the topic with great sensitivity.","zh":"編輯非常謹慎、體貼地處理了這個話題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The debate showed the sensitivity of the issue.","zh":"這場辯論顯示出這個問題的敏感性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensitivity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-583047ae03a3cf49","term":"sensitivity","forms":["sensitivity","sensitivities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對刺激作出反應的能力","explanation":"指生物、身體部位或感官察覺外界刺激並作出反應的能力或程度。這裡的“感應線”是生物系統：光、聲音、觸碰等刺激出現時，它能否及時感知並響應。","examples":[{"en":"Some people have high sensitivity to bright light.","zh":"有些人對強光非常敏感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise can improve sensitivity to insulin.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以提高身體對胰島素的敏感性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensitivity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca73f61034afc26d96c8","word":"sensor","forms":["sensor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-188d3714d8d931ca","term":"sensor","forms":["sensor","sensors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感測器；感知器官","explanation":"指能夠探測某種外界刺激，並把探測結果轉化為動作、訊號或其他反應的東西。最常見的是機器中的感測器，例如探測煙霧、光線、溫度或運動；在生物學語境中，也可以指負責感受刺激的器官或結構。","examples":[{"en":"The smoke sensor triggered the alarm.","zh":"煙霧感測器觸發了警報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sensor detects movement near the door.","zh":"這個感測器能探測門附近的活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-821119d79af8b9fcf86d","word":"sentence","forms":["sentence"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69e6e6981cb7cf10","term":"sentence","forms":["sentence","sentences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"判刑決定","explanation":"指法院針對已被定罪的人作出的處罰命令，也就是決定這個人應受到什麼刑罰。它強調法院作出的正式決定，而不只是刑罰本身。","examples":[{"en":"The judge imposed a five-year sentence on him.","zh":"法官判處他五年徒刑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She received a light sentence because it was her first offense.","zh":"因為這是她第一次犯罪，她受到的判刑較輕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sentence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-692c2da6cc34a4e8","term":"sentence","forms":["sentence","sentences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"句子","explanation":"指語法上完整表達一個想法的詞語組合，通常包含主語和謂語，書面上一般以大寫字母開頭並以句號、問號或感嘆號等結尾。","examples":[{"en":"Please write one sentence using the new word.","zh":"請用這個新詞寫一個句子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sentence has a clear subject and predicate.","zh":"這個句子有清楚的主語和謂語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sentence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2205d9d39fba658d","term":"sentence","forms":["sentence","sentences","sentencing","sentenced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"判處","explanation":"指法院在定罪後正式判處某人某種刑罰，核心是由司法機關作出懲罰決定。","examples":[{"en":"The court sentenced the thief to three years in prison.","zh":"法院判處這名小偷三年監禁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was sentenced for fraud.","zh":"他因欺詐罪被判刑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sentence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-df82d7244147796b6a64","word":"sentiment","forms":["sentiment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4e177d245f2f1e8","term":"sentiment","forms":["sentiment","sentiments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總體看法；態度","explanation":"指人們對某件事、某個決定或某類問題形成的總體想法和態度，往往不是一句明確的判斷，而是逐漸聚攏起來的共同傾向。","examples":[{"en":"The public sentiment was strongly against the proposal.","zh":"公眾對這項提議的總體態度強烈反對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A new sentiment emerged that the plan was too risky.","zh":"一種認為這項計劃風險太高的新看法逐漸形成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sentiment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b62bcb08b3f8c6a","term":"sentiment","forms":["sentiment","sentiments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"感傷情緒；柔情","explanation":"指偏柔軟、感傷或多愁善感的情緒，強調情感本身，而不是經過理性分析後的判斷；有時還暗含這種情緒顯得軟弱或不夠實際。","examples":[{"en":"The speech appealed to sentiment rather than reason.","zh":"這篇演講訴諸感情，而不是理性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farewell speech was full of sentiment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sentiment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69f32b0797ddb739ae1e","word":"sentimental","forms":["sentimental"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a45c64f61639d32","term":"sentimental","forms":["sentimental","more sentimental","most sentimental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多愁善感的；感情濃烈的","explanation":"形容一個人或一種表達很容易被情感觸動，尤其是面對回憶、離別等事情時顯得特別動情；有時也暗示這種情感過於濃重。","examples":[{"en":"I get sentimental whenever I look at these old family photos.","zh":"每當我看這些舊的家庭照片時，就會特別感傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The movie was warm and funny without becoming too sentimental.","zh":"這部電影溫馨又好笑，但沒有變得過分煽情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sentimental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06f3c992d791c619","term":"sentimental","forms":["sentimental","more sentimental","most sentimental"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感情用事的","explanation":"形容判斷、決定或觀點主要由個人情感推動，而不是由事實、證據或嚴密推理推動；重點在於情感壓過了理性。","examples":[{"en":"Keeping the broken car was a sentimental decision, not a practical one.","zh":"留下那輛壞車是出於感情，而不是出於實際考慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sentimental attachment prevented her from selling the house.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sentimental","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80ed840f94f7d1bdf549","word":"separate","forms":["separate"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e950f7c17b6aba83","term":"separate","forms":["separate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"單獨的；不相連的","explanation":"指某個東西是獨立的一件，不和其他部分連在一起。例如一把椅子可以拆成五個彼此獨立的部分。","examples":[{"en":"The machine has three separate sections.","zh":"這臺機器有三個彼此獨立的部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each guest has a separate bedroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/separate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d824ed5d0ad1739e","term":"separate","forms":["separate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"分開的；不在一起的","explanation":"指兩個人、兩件事或兩個領域沒有合在一起，各自保持獨立。比如個人生活和工作可以彼此分開。","examples":[{"en":"She keeps her study area separate from the bedroom.","zh":"她把學習區域和臥室分開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the chemicals in separate containers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/separate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff94a76160061277","term":"separate","forms":["separate","separates","separating","separated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拆分；分成幾部分","explanation":"指把一個整體拆成彼此獨立的部分，正是“把連在一起的東西分開”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Please separate the papers into three piles.","zh":"請把這些紙分成三堆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Separate the orange into segments for the children.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/separate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26fd88fadbb2ae96","term":"separate","forms":["separate","separates","separating","separated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使脫離；斷開","explanation":"指讓某人或某物離開原來的群體、連線或關係，不再和它們連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The fence separates the playground from the road.","zh":"圍欄把操場和道路隔開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Separate the damaged cable from the power supply.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/separate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aab50a27a230a31e","term":"separate","forms":["separate","separates","separating","separated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把人或物隔開","explanation":"指有意讓原本在一起的人或物分別待著，避免它們繼續靠在一起或互相影響。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher separated the two students after the argument.","zh":"爭吵後，老師把那兩個學生分開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A glass partition separates the office from the workshop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/separate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66af36d5b0569fdef4d9","word":"separation","forms":["separation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75106fd7b6ec1f80","term":"separation","forms":["separation","separations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分開；分離","explanation":"指把兩個或多個原本連線、靠近或放在一起的事物分開，也指分開這一過程或結果。這是 separation 最基礎、最能統領其他用法的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The separation of the two chemicals must be done carefully.","zh":"這兩種化學物質的分離必須小心進行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project requires a clear separation between work and personal time.","zh":"這個專案要求把工作時間和個人時間明確分開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/separation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0350f8c709057831","term":"separation","forms":["separation","separations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人與人之間的離別","explanation":"指人與人被分開、不能相處的過程或狀態，常帶有離別和感情上的距離感。它可以用於家人、朋友、團隊成員等，不一定涉及法律關係。","examples":[{"en":"The long separation from her family was difficult for her.","zh":"與家人長期分離對她來說很難熬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After years of separation, the friends finally met again.","zh":"多年分別後，這些朋友終於再次見面了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/separation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf37c7c208717d6de100","word":"sequence","forms":["sequence"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ff01fd84ed16f53","term":"sequence","forms":["sequence","sequences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有序的一串","explanation":"指彼此相鄰、並按照確定順序排列的一組事物，重點是“一個接一個排好”。","examples":[{"en":"The program runs through a sequence of checks before it starts.","zh":"這個程式啟動前會依次完成一連串檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher showed us a sequence of pictures.","zh":"老師給我們看了一組按順序排列的圖片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sequence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-618671b828ee8e99","term":"sequence","forms":["sequence","sequences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"先後順序","explanation":"指事物一個接一個發生時所遵循的先後次序，強調“依次進行”這一關係。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the instructions in sequence.","zh":"請按順序閱讀說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Arrange the photographs in chronological sequence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sequence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f0b03a32a189d90","term":"sequence","forms":["sequence","sequences","sequencing","sequenced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按順序排列","explanation":"指把原本分散的事物安排成一列，使它們具有明確的先後次序。","examples":[{"en":"We sequenced the tasks so that the hardest one came last.","zh":"我們安排了任務的順序，讓最難的任務最後完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sequence the photographs to show the repair process.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sequence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77bd5dd94c37c5b117eb","word":"serene","forms":["serene"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42547e6d01dc3dea","term":"serene","forms":["serene","more serene","serener","most serene","serenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"平靜安寧","explanation":"形容一個人、場面或氣氛安靜而從容，沒有慌亂和波動，就像沒有風的晴朗天空。","examples":[{"en":"She looked serene as she watched the children play.","zh":"她看著孩子們玩耍時顯得平靜而安詳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room felt serene after the music stopped.","zh":"音樂停止後，房間裡有一種寧靜安詳的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-101b1edb7a3df359","term":"serene","forms":["serene","more serene","serener","most serene","serenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"安然無憂","explanation":"表示事情沒有令人擔心的麻煩，或某人面對干擾仍然鎮定自若；核心仍是“不被風浪攪動”。","examples":[{"en":"Despite the delay, he remained serene and finished his work.","zh":"儘管有所耽擱，他仍然鎮定自若地完成了工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager assured us that everything was serene.","zh":"經理向我們保證一切都很平穩，沒有什麼可擔心的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57d8759063aff1e79491","word":"sergeant","forms":["sergeant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02d2c256bd48dd7d","term":"sergeant","forms":["sergeant","sergeants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中士","explanation":"指軍隊中的一種軍銜，通常高於下士而低於准尉等更高等級；在英國軍隊體系中通常譯為“中士”。","examples":[{"en":"The sergeant ordered the soldiers to move forward.","zh":"中士命令士兵向前推進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sergeant Lee checked everyone’s equipment.","zh":"李中士檢查了每個人的裝備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sergeant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c757bbf2d7463010","term":"sergeant","forms":["sergeant","sergeants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高階士官","explanation":"在一些非海軍軍隊和警察機構中，它可指最高一級或很高階的非軍官軍銜，重點仍是負責帶隊和執行管理的資深人員。","examples":[{"en":"A police sergeant arrived and spoke to the witnesses.","zh":"一名警長趕到後與目擊者交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sergeant inspected the recruits before breakfast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sergeant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0144b1defcf756108701","word":"serial","forms":["serial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65cb540789f8e235","term":"serial","forms":["serial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"系列的；連續排列的","explanation":"指許多同類事物按照一定順序一個接一個排列或出現，重點在於它們構成一個連續的序列。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed the coins in serial order.","zh":"博物館按連續編號的順序展示了這些硬幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine checks the serial numbers of each part.","zh":"這臺機器會檢查每個零件的序列號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-9cda38ea3a2bd78cbaec","word":"series","forms":["series"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27d406d960e168a1","term":"series","forms":["series","serieses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一連串；一系列","explanation":"指多個事物按先後順序接連出現，或彼此有聯絡地組成一組。重點不只是“很多”，而是這些事物像一串東西一樣連線在一起。","examples":[{"en":"A series of small mistakes delayed the project.","zh":"一連串小錯誤使專案延期了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report describes a series of changes in the local economy.","zh":"這份報告描述了當地經濟的一系列變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/series","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87d06c8c23c63672","term":"series","forms":["series","serieses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電視或廣播連續節目","explanation":"指由多集組成、按一定間隔播出的電視或廣播節目。每一集都是這串節目中的一個環節。","examples":[{"en":"We started watching a new comedy series last night.","zh":"我們昨晚開始看一部新的喜劇連續劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The series follows a family living on a remote island.","zh":"這部連續劇講述了一個住在偏遠島嶼上的家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/series","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-645dfcb4d1d2d7f1fa00","word":"serious","forms":["serious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29823bcda21b2488","term":"serious","forms":["serious","more serious","most serious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴肅的；不苟言笑的","explanation":"形容人的神態、語氣或氣氛沒有玩笑意味，顯得莊重、嚴肅；核心感覺是態度“有分量”，不是輕鬆打鬧。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher's serious expression made everyone stop talking.","zh":"老師嚴肅的表情讓大家都停止了說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was being serious when I said I would help.","zh":"我說我會幫忙時是認真的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cca095642572f41c","term":"serious","forms":["serious","more serious","most serious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴重的；重要的","explanation":"形容問題、疾病、損害或局勢等分量很大，不能忽視，往往需要及時處理；這裡不是說物件表情嚴肅，而是說事情本身嚴重或重要。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused serious damage to several villages.","zh":"暴風雨給幾個村莊造成了嚴重損害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge has suffered serious structural damage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fab2275d3de0342","term":"serious","forms":["serious","more serious","most serious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"認真的；當真的","explanation":"表示說話人不是開玩笑、欺騙或隨口一說，而是真心這樣想、確實打算這樣做；“有分量”的話會落實為真實意圖。","examples":[{"en":"Are you serious about moving to another city?","zh":"你是真的打算搬到另一個城市嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was serious when he offered to pay for the repairs.","zh":"他提出要支付修理費時是當真的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5cf0fe0efcc39f518a51","word":"sermon","forms":["sermon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ebe226a79158669","term":"sermon","forms":["sermon","sermons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"佈道；講道","explanation":"指牧師或其他宗教人士圍繞信仰、道德等主題發表的正式講話，也可以指這篇講話的文字。核心畫面就是在宗教場所對聽眾講道、勸人反省。","examples":[{"en":"The minister gave a sermon on forgiveness.","zh":"牧師作了一篇關於寬恕的佈道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stayed after the service to discuss the sermon.","zh":"禮拜結束後，我們留下來討論那篇佈道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sermon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47af10dfa7b84b7b","term":"sermon","forms":["sermon","sermons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冗長的訓話","explanation":"比喻一番像佈道那樣持續很久、不斷責備人的講話。重點不在宗教內容，而在說話者居高臨下地教育或訓斥別人。","examples":[{"en":"Dad gave me a sermon about leaving the door unlocked.","zh":"爸爸因為我沒鎖門而訓了我半天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I didn't ask for a sermon about tidiness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sermon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-295af2c55c713f23dc99","word":"servant","forms":["servant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-335c93cb6ae023fa","term":"servant","forms":["servant","servants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受僱服務的人","explanation":"指受僱定期做家務或其他工作並領取報酬的人，強調其身份是服務者而不是奴隸。","examples":[{"en":"The family employed a servant to cook and clean the house.","zh":"這家人僱了一名僕人做飯和打掃房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are three servants in the household.","zh":"這個家裡有三名傭人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/servant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8c1c75a955bfe1b","term":"servant","forms":["servant","servants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服務或幫助他人的人","explanation":"泛指願意為別人提供幫助、把服務他人當作職責或態度的人，不一定是受僱的家務人員。","examples":[{"en":"She has always been a faithful servant of her community.","zh":"她一直是社群忠誠的服務者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She described herself as a servant of the community.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/servant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24c458cfb46d9a456d31","word":"serve","forms":["serve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-217b103a9b7e1ca2","term":"serve","forms":["serve","serves","serving","served"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為某人提供服務或物品","explanation":"serve 的基本動作是把別人需要的幫助、服務、食物或飲料提供給他們；餐館、機構和個人都可以 serve 某人。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves fresh seafood every evening.","zh":"這家餐館每天晚上供應新鮮海鮮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She served the guests coffee.","zh":"她給客人端上了咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d10f37b94dbe68e","term":"serve","forms":["serve","serves","serving","served"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發球","explanation":"在網球、排球、乒乓球和羽毛球等運動中，serve 表示把球發出以開始或繼續比賽；這是名詞發球的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"She serves first in today's match.","zh":"她在今天的比賽中先發球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She served an ace to win the match.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3eacd33433b31b52523","word":"server","forms":["server"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6fc75023f339a261","term":"server","forms":["server","servers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"伺服器程式","explanation":"server可以是為其他程式或裝置提供資料、功能或計算服務的程式，就像一個持續回應請求的“服務端”。它可以執行在普通計算機上，不一定本身就是一臺獨立的機器。","examples":[{"en":"The app sends a request to the server and waits for a reply.","zh":"這個應用向伺服器傳送請求並等待回覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The server stores the user accounts and checks their passwords.","zh":"伺服器儲存使用者賬戶並核對密碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/server","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8f72397435a77e6","term":"server","forms":["server","servers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"伺服器計算機","explanation":"server也可以指專門執行這類服務程式的計算機。這裡強調的是承擔服務工作的整臺機器，而不是其中執行的單個程式。","examples":[{"en":"The company moved its website to a faster server.","zh":"公司把網站遷移到了速度更快的伺服器上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The server stores backups of all shared files.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/server","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9df6b026a8c6c26e3c3a","word":"service","forms":["service"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4e6f9d707a7ed28","term":"service","forms":["service","services"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幫助；服務","explanation":"指為某人做有益的事或提供幫助，核心概念是“為別人做事”。","examples":[{"en":"You did me a great service by warning me.","zh":"你提醒我，幫了我一個大忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel provides excellent service.","zh":"這家酒店提供很好的服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/service","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37048760f156287a","term":"service","forms":["service","services"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服務業；服務活動","explanation":"指把幫助、技能或工作作為經濟活動提供給客戶，而不是出售一件有形商品。","examples":[{"en":"The company offers online translation services.","zh":"這家公司提供線上翻譯服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The economy depends increasingly on services rather than manufacturing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/service","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4dc69fae4535aa426358","word":"serving","forms":["serving"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4de6a8391eb7731d","term":"serving","forms":["serving","servings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"服務這一行為","explanation":"指為別人提供幫助、食物或其他東西這一整個動作或過程，重點在“服務”本身，而不是某一次具體服務。","examples":[{"en":"The serving of meals begins at noon.","zh":"供餐從中午開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Serving customers politely requires patience and attention.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serving","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ca0a786a012853f","term":"serving","forms":["serving","servings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一人份；一次食用量","explanation":"指一次吃飯或喝飲料時，預定給一個人的量，也就是“一份”。它是“把食物遞給一個人”這一概念具體化後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"One serving of this soup contains 120 calories.","zh":"這份湯含有120卡路里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please add two servings of rice to the order.","zh":"請在訂單里加兩份米飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serving","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f3af1ecebbd1410ab41","word":"session","forms":["session"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a999ef750babdf76","term":"session","forms":["session","sessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段專門活動時間","explanation":"session可以指專門留出來做某件事的一段完整時間，例如諮詢、訓練、治療或拍攝。重點不只是“時間”，而是這段時間有明確的活動和開始、結束邊界。","examples":[{"en":"I have a counseling session at three o'clock.","zh":"我三點有一次諮詢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team had a short training session before the match.","zh":"比賽前，球隊進行了一次短暫訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/session","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce9927e9c1c99bfd","term":"session","forms":["session","sessions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式會議或會期","explanation":"在議會、法院或其他正式機構中，session指機構坐下來處理公務的一次會議，或連續一段會期。它保留了“集中坐下來辦事”的核心畫面，但比普通活動更正式。","examples":[{"en":"The court is now in session.","zh":"法庭現在開始開庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Parliament will return for a new session in September.","zh":"議會將在九月恢復新一屆會期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/session","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ee0eb490ff832101cf8","word":"set","forms":["set"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8976a768f8a8e0e","term":"set","forms":["set","sets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一組；一套","explanation":"指彼此相關、相互配套或外觀相同的一組東西，正如把東西安排在一起形成“一組”或“一套”。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a new set of dishes for the kitchen.","zh":"我們為廚房買了一套餐具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This set of keys opens every door in the building.","zh":"這串鑰匙能開啟這棟樓裡的每一扇門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/set","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f4441878330d200","term":"set","forms":["set","sets","setting","setten","settest","setteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放置","explanation":"把某物放到一個合適的位置，讓它在那裡放著，體現“放到位”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Set the books on the desk, please.","zh":"請把這些書放在桌子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Set the vase in the center of the table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/set","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7e852f390505da87","term":"set","forms":["set","sets","setting","setten","settest","setteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"整理並準備好","explanation":"表示把某物按需要整理、調整或準備到合適的狀態，使它可以使用；這正體現了把東西“放到合適的位置並固定下來”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please set the table before the guests arrive.","zh":"請在客人到來前把餐桌擺好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He set the camera for night photography.","zh":"他把相機調好了，以便進行夜間拍攝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/set","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bcc6937a5e116c5cdca4","word":"setback","forms":["setback"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43c0e23564fcccb7","term":"setback","forms":["setback","setbacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"挫折；阻礙；進度倒退","explanation":"指原本正在推進的計劃、事業或行動受到不利事件影響，因而變慢、受阻，甚至暫時倒退。重點不是普通的小麻煩，而是對目標進展造成了實際打擊。","examples":[{"en":"The team suffered a major setback when its main investor withdrew.","zh":"主要投資人退出後，這個團隊遭受了重大挫折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Despite the setback, the researchers continued their work.","zh":"儘管遇到了挫折，研究人員仍繼續開展工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/setback","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87364ae31c32d8b1","term":"setback","forms":["setback","setbacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不利事件；進展受阻","explanation":"這是對“挫折或阻礙”更寬泛的說法，可以涵蓋失敗、打擊、延誤等各種讓事情難以前進的不利情況。","examples":[{"en":"Several unexpected setbacks delayed the launch of the product.","zh":"幾次意外的挫折推遲了這款產品的釋出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The funding refusal was a serious setback.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/setback","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec72b9566a9c3501838a","word":"setting","forms":["setting"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a838e6dffe0ef1f5","term":"setting","forms":["setting","settings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事背景；環境","explanation":"指故事、電影或畫面被放置其中的時間、地點和整體環境，也就是它發生的背景。","examples":[{"en":"The setting of the novel is a small island in the 1920s.","zh":"這部小說的背景是二十世紀二十年代的一座小島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The quiet setting made the dinner feel special.","zh":"安靜的環境讓這頓晚餐顯得格外特別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/setting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a8a82de9d288499","term":"setting","forms":["setting","settings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檔位；設定值","explanation":"指旋鈕、開關或程式被調到的具體程度或模式，例如音量、溫度或亮度的檔位。","examples":[{"en":"Turn the volume setting down before the movie starts.","zh":"電影開始前把音量檔位調低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the lowest heat setting for delicate fabric.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/setting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9cab38670a28fbbbb941","word":"settle(ment)","forms":["settle","settlement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-487568e91c3aaa77","term":"settle","forms":["settle","settles","settling","settled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解決；定奪","explanation":"把爭議、問題或疑慮處理到有明確結果，像讓搖晃的東西終於落定。它常表示解決衝突，也可以表示使某人的擔憂平息。","examples":[{"en":"We need to settle this argument before the meeting.","zh":"我們得在會議前解決這場爭論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her kind words settled my fears.","zh":"她溫和的話讓我的擔憂平息了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ffe1575fb6cf9e7","term":"settle","forms":["settle","settles","settling","settled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"平靜下來","explanation":"指人、情緒、天氣或局面從動盪、激動變得安靜有序，也就是“落定”下來。","examples":[{"en":"The children settled down after a few minutes.","zh":"幾分鐘後孩子們安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The weather should settle by tomorrow.","zh":"天氣應該會在明天穩定下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fd428a6a45d715a","term":"settle","forms":["settle","settles","settling","settled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"定居","explanation":"把自己的住所固定在某個地方，從而在那裡長期生活；這是“人落定在一處”的核心引申義。","examples":[{"en":"My grandparents settled in this village after the war.","zh":"我的祖父母在戰後定居在這個村子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many artists have settled in the old harbor district.","zh":"許多藝術家已經在老港區定居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69bfbc8580a849c4","term":"settlement","forms":["settlement","settlements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"安頓；解決的過程","explanation":"指把人、事物或問題安頓到穩定狀態的行為或過程，是 settlement 各個具體意思的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The settlement of the debt took several months.","zh":"這筆債務的解決花了幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both sides are working toward a settlement.","zh":"雙方都在努力達成解決方案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settlement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4dcdfa8800e552d2","term":"settlement","forms":["settlement","settlements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"新建立的居住地","explanation":"指人們新遷入並建立起來的居住地，重點是“把人安頓在一個地方”；它可以是歷史上的殖民地或新開發的定居點。","examples":[{"en":"The first settlers built a small settlement near the river.","zh":"最早的定居者在河邊建起了一個小型定居點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island was home to an early European settlement.","zh":"這座島上曾有一個早期的歐洲殖民定居點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settlement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9a54380d1d95f75","term":"settlement","forms":["settlement","settlements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"庭外和解","explanation":"指爭議雙方透過協商達成協議，在不上法庭或不繼續訴訟的情況下讓案件落定；賠償金額和解協議就是常見例子。","examples":[{"en":"The parties reached an out-of-court settlement before the trial.","zh":"雙方在審判前達成了庭外和解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company paid a large settlement to the injured worker.","zh":"公司向受傷的工人支付了一大筆和解金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settlement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0794955d7269bbc4e43d","word":"settler","forms":["settler"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e401c33a14008ac6","term":"settler","forms":["settler","settlers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"定居者；殖民者","explanation":"指遷入一個新地方並在那裡居住、建立家園的人，尤其可指到原本無人居住或由外來者開發的地方定居的人。在歷史語境中，這個詞常譯為“殖民者”或“拓居者”。","examples":[{"en":"The first settlers built their homes beside the river.","zh":"最早的定居者在河邊建起了自己的家園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many settlers arrived in the region during the nineteenth century.","zh":"十九世紀，許多定居者來到這個地區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settler","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4bd699818bb1467","term":"settler","forms":["settler","settlers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爭端解決者","explanation":"指作出決定、調解雙方意見並使爭端得到解決的人或機構。這裡仍然保留“讓事情定下來”的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The committee acted as a settler of the dispute between the two companies.","zh":"委員會充當了兩家公司爭端的解決者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mediator proved an effective settler of neighborhood disputes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/settler","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2740e59ffb8c5eff0e0f","word":"several","forms":["several"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c382e10b3edd30b2","term":"several","forms":["several"],"pos":"det","zh":"幾個；數個","explanation":"表示數量不多但超過兩個的一些人或事物，數量沒有明確說出。它是 several 在現代英語中最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Several students stayed after class to ask questions.","zh":"幾名學生下課後留下來提問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have visited that city several times.","zh":"我去過那座城市幾次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/several","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec96dd32fecbac84","term":"several","forms":["several","more several","most several"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不同的；各種的","explanation":"指彼此不同的幾種人或事物，重點在“各有不同”，而不只是數量。","examples":[{"en":"The report compares several different approaches.","zh":"這份報告比較了幾種不同的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The partners returned to their several places of work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/several","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3bb61db1bc03ff467681","word":"severe","forms":["severe"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c8cb6305e1faf00","term":"severe","forms":["severe","severer","more severe","severest","most severe"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴重的；強烈的","explanation":"形容疾病、傷害、困難、天氣等達到很高的程度，已經十分嚴重或強烈。它對應“繃得很緊、幾乎沒有緩衝”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused severe damage to several villages.","zh":"這場暴風雨給幾個村莊造成了嚴重的損害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was taken to the hospital with severe chest pain.","zh":"她因嚴重的胸痛被送往醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/severe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fed1f247f7c1074f","term":"severe","forms":["severe","severer","more severe","severest","most severe"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴厲的；嚴格的","explanation":"形容對人、紀律或要求不留多少餘地，執行方式很嚴格，甚至顯得 harsh。這裡仍然是“繃得很緊”的形象，只是物件從事情變成了人的態度或規則。","examples":[{"en":"The coach was severe with players who ignored the rules.","zh":"教練對無視規則的隊員很嚴厲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company imposed severe penalties for data theft.","zh":"公司對竊取資料的行為處以嚴厲的懲罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/severe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-298e56c1cfbd9af4d097","word":"sew","forms":["sew"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8426b20b4548be0","term":"sew","forms":["sew","sews","sewing","sewed","sewn","sewen","sewest","sewedst","seweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縫製；縫合","explanation":"用針線穿過布料，把布片連線起來；既可以是製作衣物，也可以是把破處縫好。","examples":[{"en":"She sewed the two pieces of fabric together.","zh":"她把兩塊布縫在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My grandmother taught me to sew.","zh":"我祖母教會了我縫紉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-378fb8b6b2511fc6","term":"sew","forms":["sew","sews","sewing","sewed","sewn","sewen","sewest","sewedst","seweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縫紉","explanation":"不特別說明縫什麼時，表示使用針線進行縫紉這項活動。","examples":[{"en":"I learned to sew when I was at school.","zh":"我上學時學會了縫紉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She learned to sew by making simple bags.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98d44e13f455d916674d","word":"sex","forms":["sex"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-028f7a6475df89dd","term":"sex","forms":["sex","sexes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物學性別類別","explanation":"指按照生殖作用把有性生殖生物分成的類別，也可指某個個體所屬的性別。在研究、醫療和表格等語境中，常與年齡等個人或生物學因素並列。","examples":[{"en":"The study recorded each participant's age and sex.","zh":"這項研究記錄了每位參與者的年齡和性別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sex of the puppy was difficult to determine.","zh":"這隻小狗的性別很難確定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sex","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c8c5f212f2b2ca7a","term":"sex","forms":["sex","sexes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"性別區別與關係","explanation":"指不同性別之間的區別、關係以及由此形成的社會觀念。它與“性別類別”相連，但更強調這種區別本身和人們如何理解它。","examples":[{"en":"The book examines how sex and gender shape people's lives.","zh":"這本書探討性別和社會性別如何影響人們的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law should not treat people differently because of sex.","zh":"法律不應因為性別而區別對待人們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sex","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e683679358a5aea345d8","word":"sexual","forms":["sexual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28b73ce66da427f0","term":"sexual","forms":["sexual","more sexual","most sexual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與性別或男女關係有關","explanation":"表示與男性、女性、性別身份或男女之間的社會關係有關，不一定涉及性行為。","examples":[{"en":"Women face sexual discrimination in the workplace.","zh":"女性在職場中面臨性別歧視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The policy aims to prevent sexual harassment.","zh":"這項政策旨在防止性騷擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sexual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-499f0825fb5853d5","term":"sexual","forms":["sexual","more sexual","most sexual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與性行為或親密身體接觸有關","explanation":"表示與性交或其他親密的身體接觸有關，常用於說明行為、關係或身體接觸。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor asked whether the pain began after sexual intercourse.","zh":"醫生詢問疼痛是否始於性交之後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They discussed the risks of sexual contact.","zh":"他們討論了性接觸的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sexual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f5a9ba14cb89dc20e90","word":"sexy","forms":["sexy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc3d9e85df6dc713","term":"sexy","forms":["sexy","sexier","sexiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"性感迷人","explanation":"形容人的外表、氣質或舉止具有性吸引力，讓人覺得性感迷人。","examples":[{"en":"She looked sexy in that black dress.","zh":"她穿那條黑裙子看起來很性感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a confident, sexy smile.","zh":"他自信的笑容很有性感魅力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sexy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9fd9db1339dd494d","term":"sexy","forms":["sexy","sexier","sexiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"時髦誘人","explanation":"形容產品、設計、想法或計劃新潮、漂亮而有吸引力，能激起人們的興趣；這裡通常不是真的在說性。","examples":[{"en":"The company unveiled a sexy new smartphone.","zh":"這家公司推出了一款時髦又吸引人的新智慧手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Investors considered renewable energy a sexy new sector.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sexy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77ea8a2b3fee6beb665c","word":"shabby","forms":["shabby"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8e08166f62742a2","term":"shabby","forms":["shabby","shabbier","shabbiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"破舊邋遢的","explanation":"形容衣服、傢俱、房間等因為使用久了或沒人照料而破舊、磨損、顯得不整潔。核心畫面就是一件舊衣服：不一定完全壞掉，卻已經顯得寒酸、沒精神。","examples":[{"en":"They rented a shabby little house near the station.","zh":"他們在車站附近租了一間破舊的小房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sofa looked shabby, but it was still comfortable.","zh":"那張沙發看起來很破舊，但坐起來仍然很舒服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shabby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ed7811b6b82df08","term":"shabby","forms":["shabby","shabbier","shabbiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"衣著寒酸邋遢的","explanation":"形容人穿著破爛、磨損嚴重或不整潔的衣服，因此外表顯得寒酸。它主要描述人的衣著和外觀，不等於說這個人的品格不好。","examples":[{"en":"He arrived looking shabby after sleeping outdoors.","zh":"他在戶外睡了一晚後，衣著邋遢地到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shabby visitor wore a coat with torn cuffs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shabby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e02d7fca852ac60ed43f","word":"shade","forms":["shade"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e3527cd66e26dd5","term":"shade","forms":["shade","shades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰影；陰涼處","explanation":"shade 是光線被擋住後形成的較暗處，尤其常指陽光被樹木、建築物等擋住後的陰涼處。它強調的是沒有直射光的地方，而不一定是完全漆黑。","examples":[{"en":"We sat in the shade of a large tree.","zh":"我們坐在一棵大樹的陰涼處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The awning gives the patio plenty of shade.","zh":"遮陽篷給露臺提供了充足的陰涼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5464e62cbebce15b","term":"shade","forms":["shade","shades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遮光物","explanation":"shade 也指擋住窗戶等處光線的物件，例如窗簾、捲簾或遮陽簾；這裡關注的是“用來擋光的東西”，而不是它造成的陰影。","examples":[{"en":"Please lower the window shade; the sun is in my eyes.","zh":"請把窗簾放下來，陽光照得我睜不開眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought new shades for the bedroom.","zh":"我給臥室買了新的遮光簾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80b5a288536b1f77","term":"shade","forms":["shade","shades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"色調；色澤","explanation":"在顏色語境中，shade 指同一種顏色中較深或略有不同的一種色調，通常可以理解為在原色中加入黑色後形成的變化。","examples":[{"en":"This shade of blue looks good on you.","zh":"這種藍色色調很適合你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choose a lighter shade of blue for the ceiling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f41c714c53fb573","term":"shade","forms":["shade","shades","shading","shaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遮蔽；擋住光","explanation":"shade 作動詞表示用樹、建築物或其他東西擋住光線，使某人或某物處在陰影中。","examples":[{"en":"The trees shade the house in the afternoon.","zh":"下午樹木為房子遮擋陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A large umbrella shaded the children.","zh":"一把大傘為孩子們擋住了陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bb09d80600eec3eb9d7","word":"shadow","forms":["shadow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f30a89e6ed03ee43","term":"shadow","forms":["shadow","shadows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影子","explanation":"物體擋住光後投射到地面或其他表面的暗色形象。它通常會隨光源、物體和觀察角度改變。","examples":[{"en":"The tree cast a long shadow across the path.","zh":"那棵樹在小路上投下了一道長長的影子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My shadow grew longer as the sun went down.","zh":"太陽落下時，我的影子變得越來越長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d2ae83355c58d76","term":"shadow","forms":["shadow","shadows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰暗處","explanation":"指光線被遮擋後形成的相對黑暗，也可以泛指令人感到壓抑或晦暗的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"We sat in the shadow of the wall to escape the heat.","zh":"我們坐在牆的陰影裡躲避炎熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old building stood in shadow all afternoon.","zh":"那座老建築整個下午都處在陰暗中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-545a80767699e435","term":"shadow","forms":["shadow","shadows","shadowing","shadowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變暗","explanation":"使某個地方出現陰影、變暗或像被雲遮住一樣不明亮。","examples":[{"en":"The tall buildings shadowed the street in the afternoon.","zh":"高樓在下午遮得街道一片陰暗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist shadowed the corners of the room.","zh":"畫家把房間的角落畫得更暗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1a304847a689d9a","term":"shadow","forms":["shadow","shadows","shadowing","shadowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跟隨專家學習","explanation":"在工作或訓練中跟隨有經驗的人觀察一天或一段時間，以瞭解並學習這份職業。","examples":[{"en":"I shadowed a nurse to learn what the job was really like.","zh":"我跟著一名護士學習，以瞭解這份工作究竟是什麼樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new assistant will shadow the manager this morning.","zh":"新助理今天上午會跟著經理學習工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd77d2afa39ca78fa21f","word":"shady","forms":["shady"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8079507960a34f9b","term":"shady","forms":["shady","shadier","shadiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多陰影的","explanation":"指某個地方或環境有很多陰影，陽光不容易直接照到。它把“陰影”作為整體環境特徵來描述。","examples":[{"en":"We found a shady spot under the trees.","zh":"我們在樹下找到了一個陰涼的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a shady spot beneath the willow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6023521a01d8cea3","term":"shady","forms":["shady","shadier","shadiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能遮陰的","explanation":"指樹、建築物或其他物體能夠擋住陽光，為人或地方提供陰影。重點在於它具有“遮陰”的作用。","examples":[{"en":"The shady trees kept us cool during the walk.","zh":"這些能遮陰的樹讓我們散步時涼快了不少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A shady oak sheltered the picnic tables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1601992007735ba2","term":"shady","forms":["shady","shadier","shadiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陰涼避光的","explanation":"指被陰影覆蓋、能躲開強烈陽光或悶熱的地方。它強調人在這裡受到保護，不會直接暴露在刺眼的陽光下。","examples":[{"en":"Let's sit on the shady side of the building.","zh":"我們坐到建築物背陰的一邊吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The café has a shady terrace behind the building.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50d22da6c0d4799bb163","word":"shake","forms":["shake"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ced130421e4d83f5","term":"shake","forms":["shake","shakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搖動；顫抖","explanation":"shake表示來回晃動這一動作，或物體、身體正在發生的來回晃動；它既可以是主動搖動，也可以是被搖得晃動。","examples":[{"en":"The cat gave the toy a quick shake.","zh":"貓把玩具快速搖了幾下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a slight shake in her hands.","zh":"她的手有些輕微顫抖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dedb7be6a513fa60","term":"shake","forms":["shake","shakes","shaking","shook","shaked","shooketh","shaken","shooken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……來回晃動","explanation":"表示用力使某物快速地向相反方向來回移動；物體也可以在外力作用下發生這種晃動。記住“來回晃動”這個核心畫面即可。","examples":[{"en":"Shake the bottle well before you open it.","zh":"開啟瓶子前先把它充分搖勻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The explosion shook the windows.","zh":"爆炸震得窗戶都晃動起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec086d424f978c84","term":"shake","forms":["shake","shakes","shaking","shook","shaked","shooketh","shaken","shooken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搖頭表示拒絕","explanation":"表示左右搖動頭部，通常是在說“不”、表示不願意或不同意。這仍然是“來回晃動”的動作，只是晃動的物件變成了頭。","examples":[{"en":"She shook her head and refused to answer.","zh":"她搖了搖頭，拒絕回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shook his head when I asked if he needed help.","zh":"我問他是否需要幫助時，他搖了搖頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7ca2140cce85593","term":"shake","forms":["shake","shakes","shaking","shook","shaked","shooketh","shaken","shooken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使受到震動；使震驚","explanation":"表示某件事在情感上造成強烈衝擊，使人不安、震驚或難以平靜。這裡不是身體被搖動，而是人的內心彷彿被劇烈晃動了。","examples":[{"en":"The news of the accident shook everyone in the office.","zh":"事故的訊息讓辦公室裡的每個人都受到了震動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The experience shook her confidence.","zh":"這次經歷動搖了她的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56ee5b508706bf2de917","word":"shall","forms":["shall"],"officialPos":"aux.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6818b924834c23dc","term":"shall","forms":["shall","should"],"pos":"verb","zh":"第一人稱將來","explanation":"用於第一人稱時，shall 可以表示說話者預計或正式說明將來會發生的事，相當於一種較正式的“將……”。","examples":[{"en":"We shall meet again next week.","zh":"我們下週還會再見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I shall return before sunset.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bba864249cdbd4b2","term":"shall","forms":["shall","should"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徵求意見或提出建議","explanation":"在第一人稱疑問句中，shall 用來詢問下一步怎麼做，或提出一起做某事的建議，核心意思是“我該……嗎”或“我們要不要……”。","examples":[{"en":"Shall we take a break?","zh":"我們休息一下好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Shall we meet outside the station at six?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91d80a4942da5b036e4a","word":"shallow","forms":["shallow"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-493767b5facf7967","term":"shallow","forms":["shallow","shallower","more shallow","shallowest","most shallow"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深度小","explanation":"指一個空間、容器或地形的深度相對寬度很小，整體不深；這是從“向下空間很短”的基本畫面出發的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children played in a shallow pool.","zh":"孩子們在一個淺水池裡玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat ran aground in shallow water near the reeds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shallow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e85efd712e3b38fc","term":"shallow","forms":["shallow","shallower","more shallow","shallowest","most shallow"],"pos":"adj","zh":"思想感情流於表面","explanation":"把實際的“向下不深”轉用於人或生活：看起來有吸引力，卻缺少深層的感情、思考或內涵。","examples":[{"en":"Despite its luxury, the lifestyle felt shallow.","zh":"儘管生活很奢華，但這種生活方式讓人覺得很空洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His shallow analysis ignored the underlying causes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shallow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf197ff3615054b0560f","word":"shame","forms":["shame"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72c573408a6b668e","term":"shame","forms":["shame","shames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羞恥感","explanation":"指意識到自己做得不恰當、不光彩，或私密的事被暴露後產生的痛苦和難堪；這就是“難堪標籤”貼在自己身上的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"She felt a deep sense of shame after lying to her parents.","zh":"她對父母撒謊後感到深深的羞恥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt shame at having blamed an innocent colleague.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4820a88878a5009","term":"shame","forms":["shame","shames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遺憾；可惜","explanation":"指某件事沒有發生、沒有利用好機會，或結果令人失望，因此讓人覺得“真可惜”；這裡的標籤從“丟臉”轉成了“難以接受的遺憾”。","examples":[{"en":"It’s a shame that you had to leave before the concert began.","zh":"你不得不在音樂會開始前離開，真可惜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It's a shame the concert was canceled.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a8fa89ae0899515","term":"shame","forms":["shame","shames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羞恥心；自制","explanation":"指一個人因在意自己的品行和他人看法而不去做無恥之事的分寸感，也就是貼在心裡的“難堪標籤”所形成的約束。","examples":[{"en":"Have you no shame about treating your neighbors that way?","zh":"你那樣對待鄰居，難道一點羞恥心都沒有嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Have you no shame, lying to your closest friend?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a221d95db7cbf866","term":"shame","forms":["shame","shames","shaming","shamed","shamest","shamedst","shameth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使感到羞恥","explanation":"指讓某人產生羞恥或難堪的感覺，把“難堪標籤”貼到對方身上；不一定表示公開辱罵，也可以是某人的批評或失望造成的影響。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher’s harsh words shamed him into apologizing.","zh":"老師嚴厲的話使他羞愧得道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His generous example shamed them into helping.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86a8d1d3e1b8306095b1","word":"shameful","forms":["shameful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5fb91b3a9802fe1f","term":"shameful","forms":["shameful","more shameful","most shameful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可恥的；丟臉的","explanation":"指某件事或某種行為嚴重違背應有的體面或道德，足以讓相關的人蒙羞，或值得受到譴責。它就像把這件事釘在公開的恥辱柱上。","examples":[{"en":"It was shameful to leave the elderly man without help.","zh":"把那位老人丟在一邊不管，實在是可恥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The inquiry exposed shameful neglect of vulnerable residents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shameful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ed30e52d0effc3a","term":"shameful","forms":["shameful","more shameful","most shameful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人反感的；冒犯人的","explanation":"指言語或行為讓別人感到被冒犯、難以接受；這裡重點不一定是丟臉，而是它傷害了他人的感受或尊嚴。","examples":[{"en":"Those shameful jokes offended everyone at the table.","zh":"那些令人反感的玩笑冒犯了桌邊的每一個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their shameful treatment of the guests shocked everyone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shameful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-021624ecb7e008142371","word":"shampoo","forms":["shampoo"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9bc0d509456401f","term":"shampoo","forms":["shampoo","shampoos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洗髮水；清潔纖維的液體","explanation":"指用來洗頭的液體清潔產品，也可以指用於清潔地毯等纖維的類似產品。它是把“揉搓、清洗”固定在一種產品上的最常用名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"This shampoo leaves my hair soft and easy to comb.","zh":"這款洗髮水讓我的頭髮柔軟，好梳理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a special shampoo for the carpet.","zh":"我們需要一種專門清潔地毯的清潔劑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shampoo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-367023051bcc374f","term":"shampoo","forms":["shampoo","shampoos","shampooing","shampooed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洗自己的頭髮","explanation":"指用洗髮水洗自己的頭髮，重點是完成洗頭這一動作。它體現了從“揉搓、清潔”這個核心概念發展出的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I shampoo every other day because my hair gets oily quickly.","zh":"我隔天洗一次頭，因為我的頭髮很容易出油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shampoos every morning after swimming.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shampoo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f58940a313992e6838ac","word":"shape","forms":["shape"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6355136a084b6d9c","term":"shape","forms":["shape","shapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狀況；狀態","explanation":"指某件東西目前的狀況，尤其是是否完好、能否繼續使用。這個意義把“形狀”擴充套件成了事物呈現出來的整體樣子。","examples":[{"en":"The old bicycle is still in good shape.","zh":"那輛舊腳踏車狀況仍然很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sofa was in terrible shape after the move.","zh":"搬家後，那張沙發的狀況糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa6f71acc2f40a00","term":"shape","forms":["shape","shapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"健康和體能狀態","explanation":"專指人的身體健康、體力和肌肉狀態，尤其強調是否強健、是否適合運動。這裡仍然是“身體呈現出的狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"She swims every morning to stay in shape.","zh":"她每天早上游泳來保持體能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the illness, he is not yet back in shape.","zh":"生病後，他的體能還沒有恢復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b58c538112dbdcb9","term":"shape","forms":["shape","shapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"形狀；外輪廓","explanation":"指物體的外形、邊界或輪廓，例如圓形、星形或不規則形狀。這是最直接、最核心的“形狀”意義。","examples":[{"en":"We cut the sandwiches into the shape of stars.","zh":"我們把三明治切成星星的形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The table has an unusual oval shape.","zh":"這張桌子是很特別的橢圓形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3bc45ac352fe43ff8f0","word":"share","forms":["share"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b035852d20aa63da","term":"share","forms":["share","shares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一份；份額","explanation":"share 是從整體中分出來、由某人得到或承擔的一部分，可以是錢、食物、工作或責任。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone should get an equal share of the food.","zh":"每個人都應該分到同等的一份食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I did my share of the work before leaving.","zh":"我離開前完成了自己應做的那部分工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/share","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-699a957d88a34f94","term":"share","forms":["share","shares","sharing","shared","sharest","sharedst","shareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分享；分給","explanation":"把自己擁有的食物、物品、時間或機會拿出一部分給別人使用或享用，就是 share。","examples":[{"en":"Can you share your dessert with me?","zh":"你能和我一起吃你的甜點嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shared some useful advice with the new students.","zh":"他把一些有用的建議分享給了新學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/share","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e0601007d5a80cb","term":"share","forms":["share","shares","sharing","shared","sharest","sharedst","shareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"共同擁有或使用","explanation":"share 也可以表示兩個人或多人共同擁有、佔用或使用同一個東西，而不一定是把它分成幾份。","examples":[{"en":"The two students share a small room.","zh":"這兩個學生合住一個小房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The twins share a bedroom overlooking the garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/share","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51a9a6137b1d3d49e444","word":"shareholder","forms":["shareholder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2427262071d87be5","term":"shareholder","forms":["shareholder","shareholders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"股東","explanation":"持有公司股份的人，因此通常擁有部分所有權以及與股份相應的投票、分紅等權益；公司由管理層經營，並不等於每個 shareholder 都親自管理公司。","examples":[{"en":"Shareholders will vote on the proposal at the annual meeting.","zh":"股東將在年度會議上對這項提案進行投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a shareholder in the company after buying 500 shares.","zh":"她買入500股後成為了這家公司的股東。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shareholder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31fc15942b0c47f6c640","word":"shark","forms":["shark"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9786ce359f1118ef","term":"shark","forms":["shark","sharks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鯊魚","explanation":"一種大型捕食性魚類，骨骼主要由軟骨組成，頭部兩側有多條鰓裂，通常有多排鋒利的牙齒。","examples":[{"en":"A great white shark was spotted near the beach.","zh":"有人在海灘附近發現了一條大白鯊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sharks usually avoid people unless they feel threatened.","zh":"鯊魚通常會避開人類，除非它們感到受到威脅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a87cb8bb6de914f0","term":"shark","forms":["shark","sharks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剝削他人的無賴","explanation":"指利用欺騙、謊言、高利貸或勒索等手段佔別人便宜的人，形象上像不斷捕食的鯊魚。","examples":[{"en":"The loan shark threatened anyone who could not repay the money.","zh":"那個放高利貸的無賴威脅所有還不上錢的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone warned me that the broker was a shark.","zh":"所有人都警告我，那個經紀人是個吃人不吐骨頭的傢伙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-632e93023886160a2a54","word":"sharp","forms":["sharp"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0922b6c626c62198","term":"sharp","forms":["sharp","sharper","sharpest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"尖的；鋒利的","explanation":"像刀刃一樣有尖銳度，能輕易刺入或切開東西，而不是鈍的、圓的。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful—the edge of this knife is very sharp.","zh":"小心，這把刀的刃非常鋒利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sharpened the pencil to a sharp point.","zh":"她把鉛筆削成了尖尖的一頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sharp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-465eb4541bbaf9a8","term":"sharp","forms":["sharp","sharper","sharpest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聰明機敏的","explanation":"形容人頭腦反應快、理解力強，能很快看懂或處理事情；這裡的“刃”在頭腦上。","examples":[{"en":"Lena is sharp and notices small mistakes immediately.","zh":"莉娜很機敏，馬上就能發現小錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was a sharp question.","zh":"那個問題問得很有洞察力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sharp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0423c07b770db8d2","term":"sharp","forms":["sharp","sharper","sharpest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"突然而強烈的","explanation":"形容某種動作、變化、疼痛或感覺來得突然，而且強度很高，像帶著一道尖銳的“刃”。","examples":[{"en":"A sharp pain ran through her shoulder when she lifted the box.","zh":"她提起箱子時，肩膀突然傳來一陣劇痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car made a sharp turn at the corner.","zh":"汽車在拐角處來了個急轉彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sharp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ea5b198ef18ba4a11b8","word":"sharpen","forms":["sharpen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32888711837d4851","term":"sharpen","forms":["sharpen","sharpens","sharpening","sharpened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變鋒利；使更尖銳","explanation":"表示把刀、鉛筆等實際物體磨得更鋒利，也可以把“尖銳”延伸為使觀點更清楚、競爭更激烈或問題更突出。","examples":[{"en":"She sharpened the pencil before starting the drawing.","zh":"她在開始畫畫前把鉛筆削尖了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The debate sharpened his understanding of the issue.","zh":"這場辯論讓他對這個問題的理解更加清晰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sharpen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb92279d5cfb95c6","term":"sharpen","forms":["sharpen","sharpens","sharpening","sharpened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得鋒利；變得更尖銳","explanation":"表示某物或某種情況本身逐漸變得更尖銳。具體來說可以是刀刃變鋒利，抽象來說也可以是矛盾、競爭或暴力程度上升。","examples":[{"en":"As the election approaches, the differences between the two parties are sharpening.","zh":"隨著選舉臨近，兩黨之間的分歧越來越尖銳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The debate sharpened as the election approached.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sharpen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70929dc75e1fa981c1b6","word":"shatter","forms":["shatter"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c28bfe6541030312","term":"shatter","forms":["shatter","shatters","shattering","shattered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打碎成片","explanation":"指用很大的力量把完整的東西打成許多碎片，常用於玻璃、岩石、窗戶等堅硬物體。它比普通的“打破”更強調猛烈和徹底。","examples":[{"en":"The falling branch shattered the window.","zh":"掉下來的樹枝把窗戶砸得粉碎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vase shattered when it hit the floor.","zh":"花瓶撞到地板時碎成了許多片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shatter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-042f3fa2987c1269","term":"shatter","forms":["shatter","shatters","shattering","shattered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徹底摧毀","explanation":"從“打碎實體物品”引申為徹底破壞計劃、希望、秩序或某種體系，使它難以維持原狀。","examples":[{"en":"The unexpected defeat shattered the team's hopes of winning.","zh":"這場意外的失利徹底粉碎了這支隊伍獲勝的希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The verdict shattered their hopes of an early reunion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shatter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42088538eb00ab37","term":"shatter","forms":["shatter","shatters","shattering","shattered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擊垮精神","explanation":"指壞訊息、失敗或創傷在心理上徹底擊垮一個人，使其極度震驚、悲痛或失去精神力量；這是“完整狀態被擊碎”的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"The news of her brother's death shattered her.","zh":"她哥哥去世的訊息讓她悲痛欲絕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was shattered after hearing the verdict.","zh":"聽到判決後，他受到了沉重打擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shatter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14b42c3e81f60c0d0422","word":"shave","forms":["shave"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0218985446526d5","term":"shave","forms":["shave","shaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剃毛髮；一次剃毛","explanation":"指把毛髮剃短或剃掉的一次動作，或這種動作帶來的整潔狀態；重點是“把表面毛髮削去一層”。","examples":[{"en":"I instructed the barber to give me a shave.","zh":"我讓理髮師給我剃一次臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He needed a shave before the formal dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7ba3fb8b64beb0c","term":"shave","forms":["shave","shaves","shaving","shaved","shove","shaven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剃掉毛髮","explanation":"用剃刀、電推剪等把頭髮、體毛或其他毛髮貼近皮膚剪短或剃掉，是 shave 最基本、最常用的動作。","examples":[{"en":"She shaved her head before starting chemotherapy.","zh":"她在開始化療前剃光了頭髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shaved off his beard for the interview.","zh":"他為了面試把鬍子剃掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec51edc2963a7983","term":"shave","forms":["shave","shaves","shaving","shaved","shove","shaven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦著表面掠過","explanation":"表示某物沿著另一物的表面或邊緣飛過、經過，距離非常近，甚至輕輕碰到；這是“刀鋒貼面而過”的空間引申。","examples":[{"en":"The ball shaved the post and went wide.","zh":"球擦著門柱飛過，偏出了界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat shaved the rocks as it entered the bay.","zh":"船駛入海灣時擦著礁石邊掠過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30b46d1c9d316326","term":"shave","forms":["shave","shaves","shaving","shaved","shove","shaven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"略微減少","explanation":"表示把時間、重量、成本、長度等削掉一點，通常只是小幅減少，仍然對應“削去薄薄一層”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We need to shave ten minutes off the journey.","zh":"我們需要把這段行程縮短十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor shaved a few pages off the report.","zh":"編輯把報告刪短了幾頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e69fd91d4f4b65157eb9","word":"shaver","forms":["shaver"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02b3d5e39652749f","term":"shaver","forms":["shaver","shavers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剃鬚工具","explanation":"shaver可以指用來剃掉鬍鬚或體毛的工具，尤其是電動剃鬚刀。這是現代日常英語中最重要的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a new electric shaver before my trip.","zh":"我旅行前買了一把新的電動剃鬚刀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This shaver works well even on thick stubble.","zh":"這款剃鬚刀即使對付濃密的胡茬也很好用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shaver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d63f90d44face844","term":"shaver","forms":["shaver","shavers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小男孩；小傢伙","explanation":"口語中，shaver可以親暱或略帶調侃地指一個小男孩、小傢伙，突出他年紀小或有些調皮。這個義項和“剃鬚”沒有直接關係，是後來形成的獨立口語義。","examples":[{"en":"That little shaver hid my keys again.","zh":"那個小傢伙又把我的鑰匙藏起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little shaver followed his father around the workshop.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shaver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3510df1c82a80600e18","word":"she (her, hers, herself)","forms":["she"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d868a2c4a0b2785e","term":"she","forms":["she"],"pos":"pron","zh":"她；它（指雌性動物）","explanation":"she 指前文提到或語境中明確的女性，也常指雌性動物。它是主格形式，通常放在句子主語位置，核心概念就是“她在這裡做某事”。","examples":[{"en":"I asked Maria, and she answered right away.","zh":"我問了瑪麗亞，她馬上就回答了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat is hungry because she has not eaten all day.","zh":"這隻貓餓了，因為她一整天都沒吃東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/she","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2f3c3e5cf3c63b648b44","word":"shed","forms":["shed"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6cafba2470c7e0c1","term":"shed","forms":["shed","sheds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棚屋；簡易建築","explanation":"shed 是放工具、車輛或雜物的簡易小屋，通常沒有住宅那麼完整，有時前面敞開。","examples":[{"en":"We keep the bicycles in the shed.","zh":"我們把腳踏車放在棚屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He built a small shed behind the house.","zh":"他在房子後面搭了一間小棚屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4a44ce8e62bba52","term":"shed","forms":["shed","sheds","shedding","shedded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擺脫；脫去；脫落","explanation":"表示主動擺脫某種東西，或讓附著在身上的東西掉下來；東西從原來的狀態或位置被“分開、放走”。可用於衣物、皮膚、樹葉，也可用於恐懼、負擔等抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The trees shed their leaves in autumn.","zh":"樹木在秋天落葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finally shed her fear of flying.","zh":"她終於擺脫了對飛行的恐懼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1d3b413e59de0d0","term":"shed","forms":["shed","sheds","shedding","shedded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"散發；照亮；闡明","explanation":"表示光線從某處散發出來，或比喻某件事提供資訊、使問題更清楚；也就是把光“放出去”，照亮未知之處。","examples":[{"en":"The new evidence sheds light on what happened.","zh":"新的證據闡明瞭事情的經過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A lamp shed warm light across the room.","zh":"一盞燈把溫暖的光灑滿了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c599616ac500daae9e6","word":"sheep","forms":["sheep"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6ff0f333f0b9802","term":"sheep","forms":["sheep","sheeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羊；綿羊屬動物","explanation":"指有羊毛的反芻動物，尤其是人們通常所說的羊。這個意思是 sheep 最基本、最常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The sheep are grazing in the field.","zh":"羊群正在田裡吃草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw a sheep near the stone wall.","zh":"我們在石牆附近看見了一隻羊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46b5a3ad7ced5de7","term":"sheep","forms":["sheep","sheeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膽小而盲從的人","explanation":"把人比作跟著羊群走的羊，指性格膽小、缺乏主見、很容易受別人帶領或影響的人。這個比喻義從“羊群中的羊容易跟隨”發展而來，通常帶有批評意味。","examples":[{"en":"Don't be a sheep—think for yourself.","zh":"別做一個盲從的人，要有自己的判斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They followed the loudest voice like obedient sheep.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a505589b53821e87fd14","word":"sheer","forms":["sheer"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13b3b61748da83ff","term":"sheer","forms":["sheer","sheerer","more sheer","sheerest","most sheer"],"pos":"adj","zh":"純粹的；十足的","explanation":"表示某種性質完全由一個因素構成，或程度非常徹底，相當於“純粹的、十足的、徹頭徹尾的”。它常用來強調評價，而不一定表示說話人的讚許。","examples":[{"en":"Getting everyone to agree was sheer luck.","zh":"能讓所有人達成一致純粹是運氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The idea was sheer genius.","zh":"這個想法實在是天才之舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-678fb0f3b58d8e09","term":"sheer","forms":["sheer","sheerer","more sheer","sheerest","most sheer"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量或程度之大的","explanation":"放在表示數量、規模或程度的名詞前，強調其大到令人無法忽視，常譯為“龐大的、驚人的、單憑數量就足以造成影響的”。它仍然保留“純粹靠這一點就產生效果”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The sheer number of applications overwhelmed the small team.","zh":"申請數量之大讓這個小團隊應接不暇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sheer size of the building amazed us.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78af7bdb5626eb0a0467","word":"sheet","forms":["sheet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4967627e528edafa","term":"sheet","forms":["sheet","sheets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"床單","explanation":"sheet 是鋪在床墊上或蓋在睡覺者身上的一塊薄布，中文通常說“床單”或“床單被罩中的床單”。它體現了 sheet“薄而平地鋪開”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I changed the sheets before our guests arrived.","zh":"客人到來前，我換好了床單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby is sleeping under a clean sheet.","zh":"嬰兒正睡在一條幹淨的床單下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d395ff722c66682","term":"sheet","forms":["sheet","sheets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紙張","explanation":"sheet 也指一張完整、規則的紙，供書寫、繪畫、列印、包裝等使用。它比 scrap 更完整、更規整，重點仍是“一片平整的材料”。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your answer on a separate sheet of paper.","zh":"請把答案寫在另一張紙上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She folded the sheet in half and put it in the envelope.","zh":"她把那張紙對摺後放進了信封。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb1d0c8bed4218f2","term":"sheet","forms":["sheet","sheets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄片或薄層材料","explanation":"sheet 可泛指一塊薄而平的固體材料，如玻璃、金屬或塑膠片。與具體的紙張或床單相比，這個意義更寬，突出材料的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"They covered the roof with sheets of metal.","zh":"他們用金屬薄板覆蓋屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A thin sheet of ice coated the garden pond.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3eefa42d52064c480030","word":"shelf","forms":["shelf"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1c67629bfadf1b7","term":"shelf","forms":["shelf","shelves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擱板；架子","explanation":"指固定在牆上、櫃子裡或其他傢俱中的平直硬板，用來支撐、擺放或收納物品。它的核心形象就是一塊向外伸出的水平平臺。","examples":[{"en":"I put the books on the top shelf.","zh":"我把書放在最上層的擱板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kitchen shelf is full of jars.","zh":"廚房的擱板上擺滿了罐子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shelf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e406d8e0a3a7ea7","term":"shelf","forms":["shelf","shelves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一架所能容納的量","explanation":"這裡不是指擱板本身，而是指一塊擱板所能放下的一批東西，常用於概括某類物品的數量或容量。","examples":[{"en":"She has a shelf of old cookbooks.","zh":"她有一擱板的舊食譜書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She donated a shelf of books to the school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shelf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce635c4eabff5e4f56db","word":"shell","forms":["shell"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1e27f4a1d6d2ded","term":"shell","forms":["shell","shells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的硬外殼","explanation":"指動物身體外面堅硬的保護層，比如貝類、龜類或某些昆蟲的外殼；它像記憶鉤子裡的“殼”，包住裡面的身體。","examples":[{"en":"The turtle pulled its head inside its shell.","zh":"烏龜把頭縮排了殼裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found a small shell on the beach.","zh":"我們在海灘上發現了一個小貝殼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8962d533e2b1aa63","term":"shell","forms":["shell","shells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"命令介面","explanation":"在計算機中，指讓使用者輸入命令、啟動程式並控制系統互動的軟體介面；它就像包住系統內部功能的一層“軟體外殼”。","examples":[{"en":"I opened a shell to run the backup command.","zh":"我開啟了命令介面來執行備份命令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shell lets users control the system by typing commands.","zh":"使用者可以透過在命令介面中輸入命令來控制系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd96b5def4ed2b502ab6","word":"shelter","forms":["shelter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b20b2e0bfbee3129","term":"shelter","forms":["shelter","shelters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"避難處；遮蔽物","explanation":"指人可以躲進去或躲在後面、從而得到保護的具體地方，例如山洞、樹下或簡易棚屋。重點是“有一個可找到的遮蔽地點”，不一定是正式建築物。","examples":[{"en":"We found shelter under a rocky overhang before the storm arrived.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，我們在岩石突出的部分下面找到了避雨處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers built a simple shelter from branches.","zh":"徒步者用樹枝搭了一個簡易避難棚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shelter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-378738868b317946","term":"shelter","forms":["shelter","shelters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護性遮蔽物；庇護","explanation":"表示能夠擋住風雨、危險或傷害的保護物，也可以泛指滿足基本生存需要的住所和遮蔽。這裡關注的不是某一個地點，而是“提供遮擋的東西或條件”。","examples":[{"en":"Everyone deserves food, clean water, and shelter.","zh":"每個人都應當擁有食物、乾淨的水和住所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thick trees provided shelter from the wind.","zh":"茂密的樹木擋住了風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shelter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b959ba1307a6821","term":"shelter","forms":["shelter","shelters","sheltering","sheltered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；掩護","explanation":"指為人或物擋住天氣、危險、傷害或騷擾，就像給對方撐起一把傘。保護物件可以是人，也可以是植物、裝置等事物。","examples":[{"en":"The cave sheltered the travelers from the freezing wind.","zh":"山洞保護旅行者免受刺骨寒風侵襲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sheltered the plants from the afternoon sun.","zh":"她把植物遮起來，使它們免受午後陽光直曬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shelter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2aed127f29427f7c","term":"shelter","forms":["shelter","shelters","sheltering","sheltered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"躲避；避雨","explanation":"指自己躲到某個遮蔽物下或後面，以避開雨、風或危險。它把“尋找保護處”這個名詞概念變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"We sheltered under a bridge until the rain stopped.","zh":"我們躲在橋下，直到雨停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The animals sheltered from the heat in the shade.","zh":"動物們躲在陰涼處避暑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shelter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-def3735d7a0d2696775d","word":"shepherd","forms":["shepherd"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58b1cd1f68528d6c","term":"shepherd","forms":["shepherd","shepherds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牧羊人","explanation":"shepherd 是照看羊群、帶著羊在草地上放牧的人，這是它最具體、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The shepherd led his flock back to the village before dark.","zh":"牧羊人在天黑前把羊群趕回了村子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A young shepherd watched the sheep on the hillside.","zh":"一名年輕牧羊人在山坡上看守羊群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shepherd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8306d785aa6bdf3e","term":"shepherd","forms":["shepherd","shepherds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"照看和引導者","explanation":"由牧羊人看護並帶領羊群的形象引申而來，shepherd 可以指保護、照看或引導某人的人。","examples":[{"en":"She became a shepherd for young artists in the community.","zh":"她成了社群裡年輕藝術家的引路人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel portrays the leader as a shepherd protecting his people.","zh":"這部小說把那位領袖描寫成保護人民的牧者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shepherd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c05112240adc48cc0db","word":"sheriff","forms":["sheriff"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a21f8388d02f32d6","term":"sheriff","forms":["sheriff","sheriffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英國郡級司法官","explanation":"在英國（蘇格蘭除外），sheriff 或 High Sheriff 是郡級官員，負責執行法院命令、協助執法，並承擔其他郡級司法行政職責。","examples":[{"en":"The High Sheriff attended the county ceremony.","zh":"郡高階司法官出席了郡裡的儀式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The High Sheriff welcomed the visiting judges at the courthouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheriff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76db305f7c3bed34","term":"sheriff","forms":["sheriff","sheriffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美國郡警長","explanation":"在美國，sheriff 通常是負責一個郡執法工作的官員，往往還管理郡監獄、執行法院事務；許多地方的 sheriff 由選民選出。","examples":[{"en":"The sheriff was elected to a second term.","zh":"這名郡警長獲選連任第二屆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sheriff's office is investigating the incident.","zh":"郡警長辦公室正在調查這起事件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sheriff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-072a626ed2d6cc7d5da0","word":"shield","forms":["shield"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c64aa8b2a12bcf7","term":"shield","forms":["shield","shields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盾牌；防護物","explanation":"指用來擋住攻擊、傷害或危險的東西，可以是真正拿在手裡的盾牌，也可以是廣義上的防護物、屏障或庇護。","examples":[{"en":"The soldier raised his shield to block the blow.","zh":"士兵舉起盾牌擋住了這一擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trees can provide a shield against strong winds.","zh":"樹木可以抵擋強風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1c2db873aae83a6","term":"shield","forms":["shield","shields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護；庇護","explanation":"這是“盾牌”意義的抽象用法，指某人或某種力量像盾牌一樣保護人，使其免受危險、責難或不良影響。","examples":[{"en":"Her older brother was a shield for her during the difficult years.","zh":"那些艱難的歲月裡，她的哥哥一直保護著她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law acts as a shield against unfair dismissal.","zh":"這項法律保護人們不受不公平解僱的傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac763d800fafdc22","term":"shield","forms":["shield","shields","shielding","shielded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"保護；遮擋","explanation":"指像舉起盾牌一樣保護某人或某物，使其不受攻擊、傷害或有害事物影響。","examples":[{"en":"Wear a hat to shield your face from the sun.","zh":"戴上帽子，保護臉部免受陽光照射。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wall shields the garden from the wind.","zh":"這堵牆擋住了吹向花園的風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecd3fad7a4d35d7130c6","word":"shift","forms":["shift"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee103c5d6659c8fc","term":"shift","forms":["shift","shifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變化；轉變","explanation":"指某種情況、態度、重點或趨勢從原來的狀態挪向另一種狀態，通常是程度或方向上的改變。","examples":[{"en":"There has been a noticeable shift in public opinion.","zh":"公眾輿論出現了明顯變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is making a shift from print to digital services.","zh":"這家公司正在從紙質服務轉向數字服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-937a8d27f075bc76","term":"shift","forms":["shift","shifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輪班；一班工作時間","explanation":"指一組接替工作的人員，或他們連續工作的那段時間；也就是把工作時間挪到另一班來完成。","examples":[{"en":"I work the morning shift at the hospital.","zh":"我在醫院上早班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The night shift reported a problem with the machine.","zh":"夜班工作人員報告了機器出現的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-958ff0ba7fb0fe2d","term":"shift","forms":["shift","Shifts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"Shift鍵","explanation":"指鍵盤上的修改鍵，按住它並同時按另一個鍵，可以讓後者執行另一種功能，例如輸入大寫字母或其他符號。","examples":[{"en":"Hold down Shift while you select several files.","zh":"選擇多個檔案時，請按住Shift鍵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Press Shift and Enter to start a new line.","zh":"按Shift鍵加Enter鍵開始新行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4632d96aa6bf695","term":"shift","forms":["shift","shifts","shifting","shifted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改變方式或狀態","explanation":"改變原來的形式、性質、重點或做法，把事情挪到另一種狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The company shifted its focus from sales to customer service.","zh":"公司把重點從銷售轉向了客戶服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her mood shifted when she heard the news.","zh":"她聽到這個訊息後情緒變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d7cbfe8a1ceaf7d2c36","word":"shine","forms":["shine"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c55daa1db0f5aebe","term":"shine","forms":["shine","shines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光亮","explanation":"指光源發出的明亮光線，是“發光”這條核心概念的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"A soft shine came through the window.","zh":"一縷柔和的光從窗戶照進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Polishing restored the dull metal's shine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f801fb71a33eb61","term":"shine","forms":["shine","shines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反光；光澤","explanation":"指物體反射光後呈現的亮度或光澤，例如水面、金屬或拋光表面的亮光。","examples":[{"en":"The table has a beautiful shine after polishing.","zh":"這張桌子拋光後有漂亮的光澤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The polished brass had a brilliant shine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52d74d644db1a54e","term":"shine","forms":["shine","shines","shining","shone","shined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發光；閃耀","explanation":"指光源或發光物體發出光，形成“自己發光”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The stars shone brightly above us.","zh":"星星在我們頭頂閃耀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lighthouse shone through the drifting fog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19a694a2327aa1a7","term":"shine","forms":["shine","shines","shining","shone","shined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反射光線","explanation":"指物體接收到光後把光反射出來，看起來發亮；這是“光澤”概念的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The wet pavement shone under the streetlights.","zh":"溼漉漉的人行道在路燈下閃著光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her freshly polished shoes shone in the sunlight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1830dc9084f010c2","term":"shine","forms":["shine","shines","shining","shone","shined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表現出色","explanation":"把人的才華或表現比作發光，表示在某項活動中脫穎而出、做得特別好。","examples":[{"en":"She shines at explaining difficult ideas.","zh":"她很擅長把難懂的想法講清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shines whenever she's given a difficult problem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-619fd9c3e9b18b53cb8e","word":"shiny","forms":["shiny"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-67a1a8d8551a7499","term":"shiny","forms":["shiny","shinier","more shiny","shiniest","most shiny"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有光澤的；反光的","explanation":"指物體表面光滑或有光澤，能把光反射出來，看起來亮閃閃的。這是 shiny 最常見、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She polished her shiny black shoes before the interview.","zh":"她在面試前擦亮了自己的黑色皮鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were drawn to the shiny stickers.","zh":"孩子們被那些閃亮的貼紙吸引了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shiny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66c9b63928199074","term":"shiny","forms":["shiny","shinier","more shiny","shiniest","most shiny"],"pos":"adj","zh":"發光的","explanation":"指某物本身發出光，使周圍看起來明亮；重點不在反射別人的光，而在它自己有光亮。","examples":[{"en":"A shiny moon hung above the quiet lake.","zh":"一輪明亮的月亮掛在寧靜的湖面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shiny beetle glowed green in the sunlight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shiny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5d5b971139eefeb36d6","word":"ship","forms":["ship"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1077acabbef0d45b","term":"ship","forms":["ship","ships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船","explanation":"通常指比小船更大的水上船隻，用來載人或運貨。","examples":[{"en":"The ship carried hundreds of passengers across the sea.","zh":"這艘船載著數百名乘客渡過大海。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the ship leave the harbor.","zh":"我們看著那艘船駛離港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4f6685a70f29672b","term":"ship","forms":["ship","ships","shipping","shipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寄送；發貨","explanation":"把包裹、貨物或容器寄給收件人，不論具體使用卡車、飛機還是其他交通方式。","examples":[{"en":"We can ship your order to your home tomorrow.","zh":"我們明天可以把你的訂單寄到你家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The store shipped me a replacement charger.","zh":"商店給我寄來了一個替換充電器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaa79eb5ad657d3f","term":"ship","forms":["ship","ships","shipping","shipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"釋出；上市","explanation":"把產品、軟體或其他不一定是實體的東西正式推出給供應商或使用者；也可說產品本身“釋出了”。","examples":[{"en":"The new software will ship with several security improvements.","zh":"這款新軟體釋出時會包含幾項安全改進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our next model ships in September.","zh":"我們的下一款型號將在九月上市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a52514252adf86066966","word":"shirt","forms":["shirt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29557ec4f22cd5fb","term":"shirt","forms":["shirt","shirts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"襯衫；上衣","explanation":"穿在身體上半部的衣物，通常有短袖或長袖；在日常英語中也可以泛指某些上身衣物。","examples":[{"en":"I need a clean shirt for tomorrow's meeting.","zh":"我需要一件乾淨的襯衫參加明天的會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a blue shirt with jeans.","zh":"她穿了一件藍色上衣配牛仔褲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shirt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d24ffcc6f0388706a9a3","word":"shiver","forms":["shiver"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c37c5620ee3a8e0","term":"shiver","forms":["shiver","shivers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一陣發抖","explanation":"shiver 是身體突然輕微顫抖的一下或這種顫抖本身，常因寒冷、害怕或不適引起。","examples":[{"en":"A shiver went up my spine when I heard the noise.","zh":"聽到那個聲音時，我脊背一陣發涼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden shiver ran down his back.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shiver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b160cab018830f2e","term":"shiver","forms":["shiver","shivers","shivering","shivered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發抖；顫抖","explanation":"shiver 作動詞時表示因寒冷、害怕或緊張而不由自主地發抖，正是“身體細微顫動”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We shivered in the cold while waiting for the bus.","zh":"我們等公交車時冷得直髮抖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shivered with fear when the lights went out.","zh":"燈熄滅時，她嚇得發抖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shiver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74cac794aefecdbb2241","word":"shock","forms":["shock"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4bc8f56b33f58ec","term":"shock","forms":["shock","shocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈撞擊","explanation":"指物體突然受到的一次很重的撞擊或震動，是“衝擊波”這一核心意象最直接的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The bridge shook when the truck hit it with a heavy shock.","zh":"卡車猛烈撞上橋時，橋身震動了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shock of the collision threw him forward.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-970c869a6d6e9332","term":"shock","forms":["shock","shocks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理衝擊","explanation":"指突如其來的壞訊息或經歷給人造成的強烈震驚、痛苦或不安；它是“受到一記衝擊”從身體感覺向心理感覺的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden loss of her job was a terrible shock.","zh":"她突然失去工作是一個巨大的打擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Losing the family home came as a terrible shock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d252cadc228980a","term":"shock","forms":["shock","shocks","shocking","shocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使震驚","explanation":"指某件事讓人突然受到強烈的心理衝擊，感到震驚、難過或不安。這是“衝擊”核心概念最常見的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The news shocked everyone in the office.","zh":"這條訊息讓辦公室裡的每個人都震驚了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The news of his arrest shocked the entire village.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-944ae7654c01aad7256d","word":"shoe(s)","forms":["shoe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80cf6fa2c5be6668","term":"shoe","forms":["shoe","shoes","shoon","shoen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞋","explanation":"最基本的意思是穿在腳上的鞋，用來保護腳；通常指不超過腳踝的鞋，與靴子相對。","examples":[{"en":"Please put your shoes on before we leave.","zh":"我們出發前請把鞋穿上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These shoes are comfortable enough for walking all day.","zh":"這雙鞋很舒服，走一天也可以。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd9b8d8e9aa8e2aa24c0","word":"shoot","forms":["shoot"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ed4aaf65588ce2e","term":"shoot","forms":["shoot","shoots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物新芽","explanation":"指植物剛長出的嫩莖和初生葉片，是從植物主體向外伸出的新部分，正對應“猛地向外伸出”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"New shoots are appearing at the base of the rose bush.","zh":"玫瑰叢的根部正在長出新芽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener cut off the weak shoots.","zh":"園丁剪掉了瘦弱的新芽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93b4b5a736bb03b1","term":"shoot","forms":["shoot","shoots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攝影活動","explanation":"指集中安排的一次拍攝活動，通常包括為照片、廣告、電影或電視節目進行的一段連續工作；可以把它理解為把拍攝集中“推出去”的一次活動。","examples":[{"en":"The magazine arranged a photo shoot at the beach.","zh":"這家雜誌安排了一次在海灘進行的拍攝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actors arrived early for the morning shoot.","zh":"演員們很早就到了，參加上午的拍攝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f79bbe734a8b5ea","term":"shoot","forms":["shoot","shoots","shooting","shot","shotten","shooted","shootest","shootedst","shooteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發射；射擊","explanation":"把子彈、箭等從武器中猛地向外發射出去，重點是主動發射這個動作，不一定表示擊中目標。","examples":[{"en":"The police officer shot the gun into the air.","zh":"警察朝空中開了一槍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shot an arrow at the target.","zh":"他向靶子射了一箭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-294c7137aa2f7f9e","term":"shoot","forms":["shoot","shoots","shooting","shot","shotten","shooted","shootest","shootedst","shooteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猛增；迅速超過","explanation":"表示某人、某物或某個數值突然快速向前移動或上升，像猛地向外衝出去一樣。","examples":[{"en":"House prices shot up after the new station opened.","zh":"新車站開通後，房價猛漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runner shot past us near the finish line.","zh":"那名跑步者在終點線附近迅速超過了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d9001d32c6a703d9592","word":"shop","forms":["shop"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-faad2625b25a1ee1","term":"shop","forms":["shop","shops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商店；店鋪","explanation":"最基本的意思是向公眾出售商品或服務的地方；現在也可以是網上經營的店鋪。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small shop near our hotel.","zh":"我們酒店附近有一家小商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought the tickets from an online shop.","zh":"我從一家網上商店買了票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6281cc4838ddf17d","term":"shop","forms":["shop","shops","shopping","shopped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逛店購物","explanation":"指到商店裡瀏覽、挑選商品，通常帶有打算購買的意圖；重點是“去店裡看和選”。","examples":[{"en":"We’re shopping for gifts this Saturday.","zh":"我們這週六去買禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She likes to shop after work.","zh":"她喜歡下班後逛街購物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c279eb254ae9d10709bb","word":"shopkeeper","forms":["shopkeeper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1eeaa98b15d85f12","term":"shopkeeper","forms":["shopkeeper","shopkeepers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"店主；零售商","explanation":"指在商店裡經營、直接向顧客零售商品的人，通常就是守著店鋪做生意的店主。它強調面對顧客賣貨，與主要向商家供貨的批發商或挨家挨戶推銷的人不同。","examples":[{"en":"The shopkeeper greeted every customer who came in.","zh":"店主向每一位進店的顧客打招呼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A friendly shopkeeper recommended the right size.","zh":"一位熱情的店主推薦了合適的尺碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shopkeeper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa3ff1224ffaff030ba3","word":"shore","forms":["shore"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad20e57c0f207743","term":"shore","forms":["shore","shores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水邊的陸地","explanation":"shore 是海洋、湖泊、池塘、河口等水體旁的陸地。記住“水邊的一條岸”這個畫面，就能自然理解海岸、湖岸和巖岸等組合。","examples":[{"en":"We walked along the rocky shore at sunset.","zh":"日落時我們沿著岩石岸邊散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children built a small shelter near the lake shore.","zh":"孩子們在湖岸附近搭了一個小避難處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9b0078b5df596d2ea19","word":"short","forms":["short"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b3f0526c7294945","term":"short","forms":["short","shorter","shortest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"長度短","explanation":"表示從一端到另一端的距離不長，重點是沒有伸展開。既可形容橫向長度，也可形容縱向長度。","examples":[{"en":"The hallway is too short for the new shelves.","zh":"這條走廊太短，放不下新書架。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut the ribbon into short pieces.","zh":"她把絲帶剪成了短段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/short","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a48f6860817ba7f","term":"short","forms":["short","shorter","shortest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"時間短","explanation":"表示持續的時間不長，也就是事情很快結束，沒有持續到很久。","examples":[{"en":"We had a short break before the next class.","zh":"下一節課前我們休息了一小會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interview was surprisingly short.","zh":"這次面試短得出人意料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/short","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ece26ef93fdd59fa","term":"short","forms":["short","shorter","shortest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"簡短生硬的","explanation":"形容說話、回答或態度突然而簡短，常讓人感覺不夠客氣、帶有不耐煩或尖銳意味。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a short reply and returned to her work.","zh":"她簡短而生硬地回了我一句，就繼續工作了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was short with the waiter after a long delay.","zh":"等了很久之後，他對服務員的態度很生硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/short","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7b289bf46e2c61d","term":"short","forms":["short","shorter","shortest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"數量不足的","explanation":"表示數量不夠，尚未達到需要或預期的程度，也就是“短缺”。","examples":[{"en":"We are short of clean cups for the guests.","zh":"我們沒有足夠的乾淨杯子給客人用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop is running short of batteries.","zh":"這家店的電池快不夠用了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/short","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77d716e2532be480b4c8","word":"shortage","forms":["shortage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b14757225db3ab06","term":"shortage","forms":["shortage","shortages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短缺；不足","explanation":"指可獲得的人、物資、資源或其他供應少於實際需要，就像原本應該夠長的供應鏈被截短了一段。它既可指具體東西不夠，也可指這種不夠的局面。","examples":[{"en":"A shortage of clean water forced the village to limit daily use.","zh":"清潔水短缺，迫使這個村莊限制每天的用水量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital is facing a shortage of nurses this winter.","zh":"這家醫院今年冬天面臨護士短缺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shortage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ef946775e978754c68e","word":"shortcoming","forms":["shortcoming"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"shortcoming","forms":["shortcoming"],"pos":"n.","zh":"缺點；不足之處","examples":[{"en":"The main shortcoming of this plan is its high cost.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She recognized a shortcoming in her argument and revised it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-37942026d7437add4a97","word":"shorten","forms":["shorten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-730b87af0cc231eb","term":"shorten","forms":["shorten","shortens","shortening","shortened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變短；縮短","explanation":"把繩子、文章、路程等原本較長的東西弄得更短，重點是有人或某個動作使它發生變化。","examples":[{"en":"Could you shorten this report by two pages?","zh":"你能把這份報告縮短兩頁嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shortened the dress before the wedding.","zh":"她在婚禮前把裙子改短了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shorten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-415647efa81bbc4b","term":"shorten","forms":["shorten","shortens","shortening","shortened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變短","explanation":"某物自身的長度、持續時間或可用範圍變短了，不強調是誰使它變短。","examples":[{"en":"The days begin to shorten after midsummer.","zh":"仲夏過後，白晝開始變短。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The days shorten rapidly after the autumn equinox.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shorten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eed2d3e17776016d896f","word":"shortly","forms":["shortly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4381a8389bc0b31","term":"shortly","forms":["shortly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不久；很快","explanation":"表示某事發生在現在或另一個時間點之後不久，是 shortly 最常見、最值得優先掌握的時間用法。","examples":[{"en":"She left shortly after lunch.","zh":"她午飯後不久就離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Shortly before midnight, the lights went out.","zh":"午夜前不久，燈熄滅了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shortly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e45447cbb3fef572","term":"shortly","forms":["shortly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"簡短地；用很少的話","explanation":"表示用很少的話表達一個想法或說明一件事，重點是表達的長度短，而不是時間過得快。","examples":[{"en":"She shortly explained why the project had failed.","zh":"她簡要解釋了專案失敗的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She described the incident shortly, omitting unnecessary details.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shortly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-474a744f02d8b7ff5e1d","word":"shorts","forms":["shorts"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-873403fae3444e74","term":"shorts","forms":["shorts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短褲","explanation":"指褲腿短、通常不超過膝蓋的褲子，常在天氣暖和或進行運動時穿。這是 shorts 最常見、最應該優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I wore shorts because it was very hot outside.","zh":"因為外面很熱，我穿了短褲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These shorts are comfortable enough for running.","zh":"這條短褲舒服得很，適合跑步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shorts","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b44edb5c976ebd0e4b43","word":"shortsighted","forms":["shortsighted"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"shortsighted","forms":["shortsighted"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"近視的","examples":[{"en":"He is shortsighted and wears glasses when driving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The shortsighted student moved closer to the screen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"id":"manual-2","term":"shortsighted","forms":["shortsighted"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"目光短淺的；缺乏遠見的","examples":[{"en":"Cutting all training funds would be a shortsighted decision.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"It is shortsighted to ignore maintenance until a machine breaks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-8dccea5217902053b636","word":"shot","forms":["shot"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b4e8260daa977ecb","term":"shot","forms":["shot","shots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"射擊；射出的子彈","explanation":"指槍彈等被髮射出去的一次動作或結果，也可指射擊是否命中；這是“出手的一次”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The first shot missed the target.","zh":"第一槍沒有打中目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard a shot outside the house.","zh":"我們聽見屋外傳來一聲槍響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-953b92fcc8e67429","term":"shot","forms":["shot","shots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機會；嘗試","explanation":"指向目標挑戰或爭取成功的一次機會、一次嘗試；就像把一次“出手”投向想要的結果。","examples":[{"en":"Give it a shot—you might pass the test.","zh":"試一試吧——你可能會透過考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is my last shot at getting the job.","zh":"這是我爭取到這份工作的最後一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc87b6485a44d250","term":"shot","forms":["shot","shots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"照片；鏡頭","explanation":"指一次拍下的照片，或電影、電視中連續拍攝且未剪輯的一段畫面；都是快門或攝影機“出手的一次”。","examples":[{"en":"I got a great shot of the mountain at sunrise.","zh":"我拍到了一張日出時山景的好照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The director filmed the opening shot in one take.","zh":"導演一遍就拍完了開場鏡頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5b7c78d2f792dec","term":"shot","forms":["shot","shots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"注射；疫苗","explanation":"指把藥物或疫苗注入身體的一次治療或預防性注射，是針劑“打入身體的一次”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to get a flu shot before winter.","zh":"入冬前我需要打一針流感疫苗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse gave the child a shot in the arm.","zh":"護士給孩子的手臂打了一針。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89f45d4c8172f37edf9a","word":"shoulder","forms":["shoulder"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6623bf16384b8798","term":"shoulder","forms":["shoulder","shoulders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肩膀","explanation":"指脖子底部和手臂連線處之間的身體部位，也就是用來揹包、扛東西的肩膀。","examples":[{"en":"The parrot was sitting on Steve's shoulder.","zh":"那隻鸚鵡正停在史蒂夫的肩膀上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt a sharp pain in her right shoulder.","zh":"她的右肩感到一陣劇痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoulder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eedba2b6235678b5","term":"shoulder","forms":["shoulder","shoulders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"路肩","explanation":"指公路車道旁邊較平的帶狀區域，車輛可以在那裡臨時停靠；它像道路主體旁邊的一隻“肩膀”。","examples":[{"en":"He stopped the car on the shoulder to change the flat tire.","zh":"他把車停在路肩上更換漏氣的輪胎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Move onto the shoulder if your engine starts smoking.","zh":"如果發動機開始冒煙，就把車開到路肩上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoulder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6efa0bad673d029a3dd","word":"shout","forms":["shout"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43ad0b56746b7c30","term":"shout","forms":["shout","shouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喊聲；呼喊","explanation":"指突然爆發的響亮聲音，可能來自一個人，也可能來自一群人，常表達高興、憤怒、勝利或用力時的情緒。","examples":[{"en":"A loud shout came from the garden.","zh":"花園裡傳來一聲響亮的喊叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd let out a shout when the team scored.","zh":"球隊得分時，人群爆發出一陣歡呼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba508aa984ec78e5","term":"shout","forms":["shout","shouts","shouting","shouted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"大聲喊叫","explanation":"指突然、響亮地發出聲音，可能是因為興奮、憤怒、用力，或只是為了讓別人注意到自己。","examples":[{"en":"I shouted to my brother to wait for me.","zh":"我朝哥哥喊，讓他等我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don’t shout at the children.","zh":"請不要衝孩子們大喊大叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a321b0514504cdd","term":"shout","forms":["shout","shouts","shouting","shouted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"喊出；大聲說出","explanation":"指用喊叫的方式說出某個詞、名字或資訊，把內容強有力地傳到別人那裡。","examples":[{"en":"She shouted my name from across the street.","zh":"她在街對面大聲喊我的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone shouted a warning just before the roof collapsed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb91f54317e86c9a2330","word":"shove","forms":["shove"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9cfe2f949d7770c2","term":"shove","forms":["shove","shoves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用力一推","explanation":"指一次明顯帶力的推動，往往比輕輕一推更粗魯或更有衝擊感，也可以指推動某物使其動起來的動作。","examples":[{"en":"With one last shove, the stuck door opened.","zh":"又用力推了一下後，那扇卡住的門開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One shove sent the stalled cart rolling.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c41dfbc06f42b288","term":"shove","forms":["shove","shoves","shoving","shoved","shave","shoven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用力推","explanation":"指用手或身體把人、物往某個方向推，通常暗示力量較大，動作可能不夠溫和。","examples":[{"en":"He shoved the box under the bed.","zh":"他用力把箱子塞到床底下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shoved the stuck door with both hands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7371126a0f7f858cb707","word":"shovel","forms":["shovel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-165c36f84874cc43","term":"shovel","forms":["shovel","shovels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鏟子","explanation":"一種帶柄的手工具，用來把土、雪、煤或穀物等材料剷起並移到別處；有些形狀也適合挖土。","examples":[{"en":"She used a shovel to clear the snow from the path.","zh":"她用鏟子把小路上的雪鏟走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a shovel beside the pile of soil.","zh":"那堆土旁邊放著一把鏟子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shovel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f1e98460edcf388","term":"shovel","forms":["shovel","shovels","shoveling","shovelling","shoveled","shovelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用鏟子鏟運","explanation":"用鏟子把材料剷起來，再移到別處；重點是連續地搬運一堆東西。","examples":[{"en":"They shoveled gravel into the hole.","zh":"他們把碎石鏟進了坑裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent the morning shoveling snow off the driveway.","zh":"我們整個上午都在把車道上的雪鏟走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shovel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c6333509debf060200e","word":"show","forms":["show"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05aa8ae4a2731502","term":"show","forms":["show","shows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演出；娛樂節目","explanation":"把娛樂活動帶到觀眾眼前，就是一場演出或娛樂節目。","examples":[{"en":"There was a great show at the theater last night.","zh":"昨晚劇院裡有一場很精彩的演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We bought tickets for the evening comedy show.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/show","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a65b4384dc42d9ac","term":"show","forms":["show","shows","showing","showed","shew","shown","showest","showedst","showeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"展示；給人看","explanation":"把某物帶到別人的眼前，使對方看見或注意到它。重點是主動展示，也可以是某種痕跡自然顯露出來。","examples":[{"en":"She showed me the photos from her trip.","zh":"她給我看了旅行時拍的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The worn handle showed how often the door was used.","zh":"磨損的把手顯示出這扇門使用得多麼頻繁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/show","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9256490c4390636","term":"show","forms":["show","shows","showing","showed","shew","shown","showest","showedst","showeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表明；證明","explanation":"把證據或結果帶到眼前，讓人看出某個事實是真的，或證明某種說法成立。","examples":[{"en":"The results show that the new method saves time.","zh":"結果表明，這種新方法能夠節省時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm response showed everyone that she was prepared.","zh":"她鎮定的回應向大家表明她已經做好了準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/show","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4bce35a41d587902","term":"show","forms":["show","shows","showing","showed","shew","shown","showest","showedst","showeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顯現；看得見","explanation":"某物或某種特徵自己出現在眼前，變得能夠被看見；它不是主動展示，而是狀態或痕跡顯露出來。","examples":[{"en":"The first signs of spring are starting to show.","zh":"春天的最初跡象開始顯現了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stain still shows on the white shirt.","zh":"汙漬在白襯衫上仍然看得見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/show","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-528159b45697166be9a6","word":"shower","forms":["shower"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5de3ddd8af9bd729","term":"shower","forms":["shower","showers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陣雨；短時降水","explanation":"指短時間落下的一陣雨，也可指類似陣雨一樣突然落下的雪、雨夾雪或水流。它通常強調降水斷斷續續，而不是一直下個不停。","examples":[{"en":"There will be a few showers this afternoon.","zh":"今天下午會有幾陣陣雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We got caught in a sudden shower on the way home.","zh":"我們回家路上突然遇上了一陣雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76caa667624c7a66","term":"shower","forms":["shower","showers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"淋浴裝置","explanation":"指讓水從上方落到身體上的洗浴裝置，通常安裝在浴室裡。","examples":[{"en":"The shower is leaking again.","zh":"淋浴器又漏水了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shower needs a new hose and head.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00d16047e7054b42","term":"shower","forms":["shower","showers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"淋浴；洗澡","explanation":"指使用淋浴裝置洗澡這一行為，也就是讓水從上方沖洗身體。","examples":[{"en":"I’m going to have a shower before dinner.","zh":"我打算晚飯前洗個淋浴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had a quick shower after the run.","zh":"她跑完步後快速衝了個澡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c21c53767caa3763","term":"shower","forms":["shower","showers","showering","showered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洗淋浴","explanation":"指使用淋浴裝置洗澡，讓水從上方沖洗身體。","examples":[{"en":"I usually shower before I go to work.","zh":"我通常上班前洗淋浴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse showered the patient and changed the sheets.","zh":"護士給病人洗了淋浴並換了床單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2c8223fe0f7be43d4ef","word":"shred","forms":["shred"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f73f5e0acf86ee4","term":"shred","forms":["shred","shreds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碎片；一點兒","explanation":"可以指某物撕下或切下的一小片，也可以把抽象事物想成少得只剩一小片，表示“絲毫、一點兒”。","examples":[{"en":"There wasn't a shred of evidence against her.","zh":"沒有絲毫證據證明她有罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was left with only a few shreds of paper.","zh":"他只剩下幾片碎紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eeb44c7705ac9646","term":"shred","forms":["shred","shreds","shredding","shredded","shreddest","shreddedst","shreddeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撕碎；切成細條","explanation":"把某物切成或撕成長而窄的條，或切成很小的片，是這個詞最直接的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Shred the chicken and mix it with the sauce.","zh":"把雞肉撕成細條，再和醬汁拌在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog shredded the old pillow.","zh":"狗把那個舊枕頭撕得粉碎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8128b4994171254","term":"shred","forms":["shred","shreds","shredding","shredded","shreddest","shreddedst","shreddeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把檔案銷燬","explanation":"把檔案切成無法輕易讀出的細條或碎片，通常是為了銷燬其中的資訊；這是“撕碎”義在檔案上的具體應用。","examples":[{"en":"Please shred these old tax documents.","zh":"請把這些舊稅務檔案銷燬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shredded the letter after reading it.","zh":"她讀完信後把它撕碎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shred","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fe7dba0b29f8e79e981","word":"shriek","forms":["shriek"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-018b6b9d036f486b","term":"shriek","forms":["shriek","shrieks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖銳的尖叫聲","explanation":"指突然發出的尖銳、刺耳的叫聲，常常讓人聯想到驚恐、劇痛或極度激動；重點是聲音又高又刺耳。","examples":[{"en":"A shriek came from the room upstairs.","zh":"樓上的房間裡傳來一聲尖叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She let out a shriek when the spider landed on her hand.","zh":"蜘蛛落到她手上時，她尖叫了一聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shriek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64886463a437e90c","term":"shriek","forms":["shriek","shrieks","shrieking","shrieked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出尖叫","explanation":"指人、動物等突然發出尖銳刺耳的叫聲，通常是因為害怕、痛苦或受到強烈刺激；它就是名詞“尖叫聲”變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"The child shrieked with fear when the lights went out.","zh":"燈滅時，孩子嚇得尖叫起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bats shrieked in the dark.","zh":"蝙蝠在黑暗中發出尖銳的叫聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shriek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42a73cf9f258b8e49d85","word":"shrimp","forms":["shrimp"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d0b730ed37a8e74","term":"shrimp","forms":["shrimp","shrimps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蝦","explanation":"指生活在水中的小型甲殼動物，通常有細長的身體、長鬚和細腿，很多種類可以食用。","examples":[{"en":"We bought fresh shrimp for dinner.","zh":"我們買了新鮮蝦，準備晚飯吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tiny shrimp was hiding under the rock.","zh":"一隻小蝦藏在岩石下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrimp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6792706f67a60d81","term":"shrimp","forms":["shrimp","shrimps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"矮小、弱小的人","explanation":"把人的身材或存在感比作小蝦，指個子矮小、瘦弱或不重要的人，通常含有貶義或戲謔意味。","examples":[{"en":"The bully called him a shrimp, but he did not back down.","zh":"那個惡霸叫他小矮子，但他沒有退縮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At school, the bigger boys called him a shrimp.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrimp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66b490dd60054469bdfe","word":"shrink","forms":["shrink"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-79bf1e95391eeaa7","term":"shrink","forms":["shrink","shrinks","shrinking","shrank","shrunk","shrunken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變小；使縮水","explanation":"指透過洗滌、加熱或其他作用，讓某物的尺寸變小。這是“收縮”意象中主動施加作用的一面。","examples":[{"en":"The hot water shrank my cotton shirt.","zh":"熱水把我的棉襯衫洗縮水了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tailor shrank the fabric before cutting it.","zh":"裁縫在裁剪前先讓布料縮水了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f454d3ce78f4c4e7","term":"shrink","forms":["shrink","shrinks","shrinking","shrank","shrunk","shrunken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變小；收縮","explanation":"指某物自身尺寸、數量或體積減少，不強調是誰造成的；衣物洗後變小是最常見的例子。","examples":[{"en":"This wool sweater will shrink if you wash it in hot water.","zh":"這件羊毛衫如果用熱水洗就會縮水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puddle shrank in the afternoon sun.","zh":"水坑在午後的陽光下變小了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cd7bdea04a3032b","term":"shrink","forms":["shrink","shrinks","shrinking","shrank","shrunk","shrunken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"畏縮；瑟縮","explanation":"指人因為害怕、疼痛或受到威脅而身體縮起來，像物體收縮一樣表現出退縮。","examples":[{"en":"The child shrank from the barking dog.","zh":"孩子面對狂吠的狗瑟縮著往後退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shrank away when the doctor touched the wound.","zh":"醫生碰到傷口時，他瑟縮著躲開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b72e591cda2d41fa9da","word":"shrub","forms":["shrub"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6eed68306dc665c3","term":"shrub","forms":["shrub","shrubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"灌木","explanation":"一種木本植物，通常比樹矮，並且從靠近地面的地方長出幾根莖；花園裡的觀賞灌木和野外的低矮木本植物都可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"We planted a flowering shrub beside the front door.","zh":"我們在前門旁種了一株開花的灌木。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small shrubs covered the dry hillside.","zh":"低矮的灌木覆蓋著乾燥的山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40c2e21a3ff45d04","term":"shrub","forms":["shrub","shrubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酸甜果味飲品","explanation":"一種用果汁、糖和酸味成分調製的飲品，現代配方通常不含酒精；歷史上也可能加入白蘭地或朗姆酒。","examples":[{"en":"The café serves a refreshing lemon shrub over ice.","zh":"那家咖啡館供應一款加冰的清爽檸檬果味飲品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She mixed a berry shrub with sparkling water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b2c1b5052a53aaa7e82","word":"shrug","forms":["shrug"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-894880ed9b1ee835","term":"shrug","forms":["shrug","shrugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聳肩動作","explanation":"指抬起肩膀的一下動作，通常用來表示不知道、沒有把握、無所謂，或不想進一步解釋。","examples":[{"en":"He dismissed my comment with a shrug.","zh":"他聳了聳肩，表示不把我的話當回事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He answered with a shrug instead of an explanation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1f793f860b9dfc7","term":"shrug","forms":["shrug","shrugs","shrugging","shrugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聳肩表示態度","explanation":"指抬起肩膀，用動作表示自己不知道答案、沒有把握、不在乎，或不願認真回應某件事。","examples":[{"en":"I asked her why, but she just shrugged.","zh":"我問她為什麼，但她只是聳了聳肩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shrugged his shoulders and walked away.","zh":"他聳了聳肩，然後走開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f30a852b76d3f05119a","word":"shuffle","forms":["shuffle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80f229370e0b1a95","term":"shuffle","forms":["shuffle","shuffles","shuffling","shuffled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洗牌；打亂順序","explanation":"指把牌或其他專案混動，使它們進入隨機順序；最典型的場景是發牌前洗牌。","examples":[{"en":"Don't forget to shuffle the cards before the game.","zh":"別忘了在比賽前洗牌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Shuffle the cards before dealing another hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shuffle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7a14b9ace97326d","term":"shuffle","forms":["shuffle","shuffles","shuffling","shuffled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拖著腳走；拖步移動","explanation":"指走路或跳舞時把腳拖在地面上，動作顯得疲憊、懶散或不利落；也可以指發出摩擦地面的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The old dog shuffled slowly across the yard.","zh":"那隻老狗拖著腳慢慢走過院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He shuffled down the hallway in loose slippers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shuffle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a1db49adbe0e8281c06","word":"shut","forms":["shut"],"officialPos":"v./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13f9db60b7cf9b0e","term":"shut","forms":["shut"],"pos":"adj","zh":"關著的；閉合的","explanation":"指門、窗、蓋子等已經合上、沒有開啟的狀態，核心畫面就是那扇門完全合攏了。","examples":[{"en":"The front door was shut when I arrived.","zh":"我到達時，前門是關著的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the window shut during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間請讓窗戶保持關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d2e07ce383bb985","term":"shut","forms":["shut","shuts","shutting","shutten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"關上；關閉","explanation":"把門、窗、蓋子、裝置或其他開口合上，或使某物停止開放；這是 shut 最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Shut the door quietly, please.","zh":"請輕輕把門關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The café shuts at nine tonight.","zh":"這家咖啡館今晚九點關門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9db3a25b009c1e439aa6","word":"shutter","forms":["shutter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7281cd9aac611a34","term":"shutter","forms":["shutter","shutters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"窗戶擋板","explanation":"指安裝在窗戶外面或裡面的擋板，用來遮光、擋風或保護窗戶。它體現了“把開口關上”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She closed the wooden shutters before going to bed.","zh":"她睡覺前關上了木製窗戶擋板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shutters kept the bright morning sun out.","zh":"窗戶擋板擋住了清晨刺眼的陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shutter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42bb68efaf3eb350","term":"shutter","forms":["shutter","shutters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相機快門","explanation":"指相機中控制進光時間的部件。它平時關閉，拍照時短暫開啟，讓適量光線進入，因此也是“控制開口”的一種形式。","examples":[{"en":"A fast shutter speed froze the bird in midair.","zh":"較快的快門速度把飛在半空中的鳥定格了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shutter clicked just as the bird took flight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shutter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd4f66e1556f187a","term":"shutter","forms":["shutter","shutters","shuttering","shuttered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"關上擋板","explanation":"表示關上覆蓋窗戶或其他開口的擋板，是名詞“封閉裝置”對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Please shutter the windows before the storm arrives.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，請把窗戶擋板關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crew shuttered every opening on the boat.","zh":"工作人員把船上的每個開口都封閉起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shutter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48f42260a8448caa7a9c","word":"shuttle","forms":["shuttle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-adabdd61e291505f","term":"shuttle","forms":["shuttle","shuttles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"織布梭子","explanation":"織布時，梭子帶著緯線在經線之間來回穿過，把橫向的線織進布里。這是“在兩點之間來回移動並帶著東西”的最早形象。","examples":[{"en":"The shuttle carries the thread across the loom.","zh":"梭子帶著線穿過織布機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The weaver passed the shuttle between the threads.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shuttle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0ee99ea18e6aa29","term":"shuttle","forms":["shuttle","shuttles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"往返接送服務","explanation":"指在兩個或幾個固定地點之間反覆往返、接送乘客的交通服務，例如機場和車站之間的班車服務。這裡保留了梭子來回穿行的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel runs a free shuttle to the airport every thirty minutes.","zh":"這家酒店每三十分鐘有一班免費機場接送車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel operates a free airport shuttle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shuttle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b2df979cfe1e4ea","term":"shuttle","forms":["shuttle","shuttles","shuttling","shuttled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在兩地之間往返","explanation":"表示人、車輛或其他東西在兩個地點之間反覆來回，突出路線固定、動作重複的感覺。它把名詞中“梭子來回穿行”的畫面直接變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"During the conference, buses shuttled between the hotel and the venue.","zh":"會議期間，公交車往返於酒店和會場之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She shuttled between the two offices all morning.","zh":"她整個上午都在兩個辦公室之間來回奔波。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shuttle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9807eb6ec753a5173bda","word":"shy","forms":["shy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d43f384e0eaff2f0","term":"shy","forms":["shy","shier","shyer","more shy","shiest","shyest","most shy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易受驚；膽小","explanation":"形容人或動物容易受到驚嚇，不敢主動靠近；重點是遇到陌生或危險時會往後縮。","examples":[{"en":"The shy puppy hid behind its owner when visitors arrived.","zh":"客人來時，那隻怕生的小狗躲到了主人身後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shy horse startled at every sudden movement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-002c98774b86897c","term":"shy","forms":["shy","shier","shyer","more shy","shiest","shyest","most shy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"拘謹；不願與人親近","explanation":"形容人因為拘謹或缺乏自信，不願主動接近陌生人或進行熟悉的交往；不一定是真的害怕。","examples":[{"en":"He is shy with strangers but very talkative with his friends.","zh":"他在陌生人面前很拘謹，但和朋友在一起時非常健談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shy child hid behind her father.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d10de8554ed5ca40f9d","word":"sibling","forms":["sibling"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8147c5c2f031165","term":"sibling","forms":["sibling","siblings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兄弟姐妹","explanation":"指與某人至少有一個共同父母的兄弟或姐妹，包括同父異母、同母異父以及同父同母的兄弟姐妹。它是一個不區分性別和年齡的總稱。","examples":[{"en":"None of my siblings are married yet.","zh":"我的兄弟姐妹目前都還沒有結婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is my oldest sibling.","zh":"她是我最大的姐姐或哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sibling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c234b8df788657e3","term":"sibling","forms":["sibling","siblings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同一父節點下的節點","explanation":"在電腦科學中，指資料結構裡共享同一個父節點的節點。這裡把“父母”這個家庭概念抽象成了“父節點”，所以這些節點彼此就是 sibling。","examples":[{"en":"The two nodes are siblings because they have the same parent.","zh":"這兩個節點有同一個父節點，所以它們是同級節點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Deleting a node leaves its siblings intact within the tree.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sibling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b04837881bb07b621ae","word":"sick","forms":["sick"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23a0fc8041c346b6","term":"sick","forms":["sick","sicker","sickest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生病的","explanation":"表示身體處於患病或不健康的狀態，是 sick 最基本的意思。它既可以泛指生病，也可以和具體疾病、症狀連用。","examples":[{"en":"I stayed home because I was sick.","zh":"我因為生病待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been sick with the flu since Monday.","zh":"她從星期一開始就因流感生病了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db385227836f1383","term":"sick","forms":["sick","sicker","sickest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"噁心想吐的","explanation":"表示胃部不適、想要嘔吐的感覺；重點是“有嘔吐衝動”，不一定真的吐出來。","examples":[{"en":"I felt sick after the boat started rocking.","zh":"船開始搖晃後，我感到噁心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smell of the fish made him feel sick.","zh":"魚的氣味讓他感到噁心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1532f5792887f804","term":"sick","forms":["sick","sicker","sickest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"厭煩的","explanation":"在 be sick of something 中，表示因為反覆經歷某事而厭煩、受夠了；這是從身體不適引申出的“再也受不了了”。","examples":[{"en":"I'm sick of waiting for the bus.","zh":"我等公交車等得受夠了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are sick of hearing the same excuse.","zh":"他們聽夠了同一個藉口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea7bf4bb723041e7d63f","word":"side","forms":["side"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7879f4ce69f400f","term":"side","forms":["side","sides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一半；一側","explanation":"指某物或某人的左、右、前、後、上、下等其中一半或一側，正如盒子的某個側面。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the books on the right side of the desk.","zh":"請把書放在桌子的右側。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She slept on her left side.","zh":"她側著左身睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/side","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad9cf7cd92b4ebf3","term":"side","forms":["side","sides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某個位置；某一邊","explanation":"指相對於某個參照物的特定區域或方向位置。它把“側面”這個概念擴充套件成了某個地方的一邊。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small café on the other side of the street.","zh":"街對面有一家小咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Meet me on the north side of the station.","zh":"在車站北側和我碰面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/side","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d028668db39ca3f0","term":"side","forms":["side","sides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方面；一面","explanation":"指一個概念、人物或事情的某個方面，就像從盒子的某一側去觀察它。","examples":[{"en":"Every problem has a positive side if you look carefully.","zh":"只要仔細看，每個問題都有積極的一面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to see the bright side of the situation.","zh":"試著看到這種情況好的一面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/side","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6dce9d1302b80abcb3e","word":"sidewalk","forms":["sidewalk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29178e2e7c648348","term":"sidewalk","forms":["sidewalk","sidewalks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道路旁的人行道","explanation":"指鋪設在道路一側、供行人行走的人行道，是這個詞最典型的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Stay on the sidewalk.","zh":"待在人行道上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children walked along the sidewalk to school.","zh":"孩子們沿著人行道走去學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sidewalk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7cac0b4c407a01c","term":"sidewalk","forms":["sidewalk","sidewalks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋪設的人行步道","explanation":"在較寬的用法中，任何鋪設好的供人步行的步道都可以叫 sidewalk，即使它不在道路旁。","examples":[{"en":"A paved sidewalk leads from the parking lot to the entrance.","zh":"一條鋪設好的步道從停車場通向入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep bicycles off the sidewalk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sidewalk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d94ad715959767df33c4","word":"siege","forms":["siege"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9919f923047e5ff3","term":"siege","forms":["siege","sieges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"圍攻；圍城","explanation":"軍隊包圍城市、堡壘等，並透過進攻或封鎖迫使守方投降，這種軍事行動叫作 siege。重點是持續包圍和施壓，而不只是發生一次戰鬥。","examples":[{"en":"The army began a siege of the mountain fortress.","zh":"軍隊開始圍攻那座山地堡壘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city held out during the long siege.","zh":"這座城市在長期圍困中堅持了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/siege","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6da443cbd56cd2ab","term":"siege","forms":["siege","sieges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"持續的猛烈進攻；圍攻式壓力","explanation":"比喻某人或某方連續不斷地施加壓力，就像軍隊從四面圍住一座城一樣；體育報道中也可指一方長時間猛烈進攻另一方。","examples":[{"en":"The defense survived a late siege from the home team.","zh":"防守方頂住了主隊最後階段的猛烈圍攻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hospital came under siege from angry protesters.","zh":"這家醫院承受了憤怒抗議者持續不斷的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/siege","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7428b2c5284148533a13","word":"sigh","forms":["sigh"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-69f807aceee2ff32","term":"sigh","forms":["sigh","sighs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘆氣；嘆息","explanation":"sigh 是一次深而明顯的吸氣和呼氣，也就是把壓在胸口的氣撥出來；它常伴隨疲憊、煩惱、悲傷或放鬆。","examples":[{"en":"She let out a long sigh of relief when the test was over.","zh":"考試結束時，她長長地鬆了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He answered with a tired sigh.","zh":"他疲憊地嘆了口氣才回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sigh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e411fc2519252516","term":"sigh","forms":["sigh","sighs","sighing","sighed","sighest","sighedst","sigheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嘆氣","explanation":"sigh 表示吸入比平時更多的空氣，再明顯地撥出一口氣，用來釋放疲憊、煩惱、悲傷或如釋重負的情緒。","examples":[{"en":"When she saw the damage was minor, she sighed with relief.","zh":"她發現損壞不嚴重後，鬆了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sighed and closed the book.","zh":"他嘆了口氣，合上了書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sigh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b991a49b1b0aa2cc5850","word":"sight","forms":["sight"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4cc866ebff847709","term":"sight","forms":["sight","sights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"視力；視覺能力","explanation":"指用眼睛看東西的能力，也就是視力；這裡強調的是眼睛本身的視覺能力，而不是某一次看見。","examples":[{"en":"She began to lose her sight in her seventies.","zh":"她七十多歲時開始失去視力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gradually lost her sight after the accident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13a50751e29d0675","term":"sight","forms":["sight","sights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看見；視野","explanation":"指看見某物這一動作，或眼睛能夠看到的景象和範圍；它是從“視線碰到目標”發展出來的意義。","examples":[{"en":"We caught sight of the island just before sunset.","zh":"日落前我們看見了那座島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village soon disappeared from sight.","zh":"那個村莊很快從視野中消失了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1afd2bcc30249373","term":"sight","forms":["sight","sights","sighting","sighted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"看見；發現","explanation":"指在視覺上發現或看見某物，尤其用於遠處、突然出現或此前沒有注意到的目標；它是名詞“視線碰到目標”的動詞化。","examples":[{"en":"The sailors sighted land after three weeks at sea.","zh":"水手們在海上航行三週後看見了陸地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A deer was sighted near the road this morning.","zh":"今天早上有人在路邊發現了一隻鹿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ae0c105f08a7783d95f","word":"sightseeing","forms":["sightseeing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-14ce8b2db5e3ed97","term":"sightseeing","forms":["sightseeing","sightseeings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀光；遊覽","explanation":"指為了看名勝、景點或城市風貌而外出遊覽的活動，重點是“走出去看景物”，而不只是泛泛地旅行。","examples":[{"en":"We went sightseeing around the old town.","zh":"我們在老城區四處遊覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sightseeing is a popular activity for visitors to the city.","zh":"觀光是遊客來到這座城市後常參加的活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sightseeing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b6f395ca14ac202374d","word":"sign","forms":["sign"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54a4b1f7fd7ee07f","term":"sign","forms":["sign","signs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跡象；徵兆","explanation":"指一個看得見或能觀察到的事實，使人判斷某事已經存在、正在發生或可能發生。重點不在於它是人為製作的，而在於它提供了線索。","examples":[{"en":"Dark clouds are often a sign of rain.","zh":"烏雲常常是下雨的徵兆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her smile was a sign that she felt better.","zh":"她的微笑表明她感覺好些了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f3fb6ef507b1e954","term":"sign","forms":["sign","signs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"符號；標記","explanation":"指用來代表某個意思、聲音、數量或規則的圖形、記號或其他標記。它不是事情本身，而是讓人聯想到或讀出某種意義的東西。","examples":[{"en":"The plus sign means that you should add the numbers.","zh":"加號表示你應該把這些數字相加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red circle is a common sign of danger.","zh":"紅色圓圈是常見的危險標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5255b9e4dc184a49","term":"sign","forms":["sign","signs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"招牌；告示牌","explanation":"指通常放在顯眼位置、用文字或圖畫傳達簡簡訊息的平面物體，例如店鋪招牌、出租告示或交通牌。","examples":[{"en":"There was a sign on the door saying that the shop was closed.","zh":"門上有一塊牌子，寫著商店關門了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We put up a sign asking visitors not to feed the animals.","zh":"我們掛了一塊牌子，請遊客不要給動物餵食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc6c9087cae54338","term":"sign","forms":["sign","signs","signing","signed","signest","signedst","signeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"簽名；簽署","explanation":"指親自在檔案、表格或其他材料上寫下自己的名字，以表示確認、同意或承擔責任。這是“留下可識別標記”在現代生活中最常見的動作之一。","examples":[{"en":"Please sign this form at the bottom.","zh":"請在這張表格底部簽名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both sides signed the agreement yesterday.","zh":"雙方昨天簽署了協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d20420cf2096f697","term":"sign","forms":["sign","signs","signing","signed","signest","signedst","signeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打手勢示意","explanation":"指不用語言而用手勢、眼神或動作向某人傳達一個指令或意思，尤其是示意對方做某事。","examples":[{"en":"He signed to me to stay quiet.","zh":"他打手勢示意我保持安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide signed for us to follow her.","zh":"導遊打手勢示意我們跟著她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d041924c15885af6d065","word":"signal","forms":["signal"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c94a14847033813","term":"signal","forms":["signal","signals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"提示行動的訊號","explanation":"這是最典型的日常義項之一：某個手勢、聲音或動作告訴別人有事情發生、需要服從命令、注意危險，或可以開始共同的行動。","examples":[{"en":"When the referee gave the signal, the runners started.","zh":"裁判發出訊號後，跑步者們開始了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She raised her hand as a signal for everyone to stop.","zh":"她舉手示意大家停下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0cb937cbb2cbdbb","term":"signal","forms":["signal","signals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手機或無線電訊號","explanation":"在電話、電視和無線通訊中，signal 是承載聲音、影象或通訊內容的電磁訊號；日常說手機“有訊號”時也用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"I lost my phone signal in the underground tunnel.","zh":"我在地下隧道里沒有手機訊號了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The television signal is too weak to produce a clear picture.","zh":"電視訊號太弱，無法顯示清晰的畫面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d99a2d3f8318c2ee","term":"signal","forms":["signal","signals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跡象；預兆","explanation":"從“傳遞提示”的核心概念出發，signal 還可以是某件事即將發生或某種情況已經出現的跡象，例如烏雲是下雨的預兆。","examples":[{"en":"The early flowers were a signal of spring.","zh":"早開的花是春天到來的跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His repeated questions were a signal that he was worried.","zh":"他一再提問，說明他感到擔心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a08877af1d3cc0d","term":"signal","forms":["signal","signals","signaling","signalling","signaled","signalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發訊號表示；示意","explanation":"signal 作動詞時，表示用點頭、手勢、燈光或其他訊號主動傳達自己的意思，例如表示同意、停止或開始。","examples":[{"en":"He signaled that it was safe to cross the road.","zh":"他示意過馬路是安全的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She signaled to the waiter for the bill.","zh":"她向服務員示意要買單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,114],"total":8,"counts":{"111":1,"114":7}}},{"id":"ceec-1a2fc26dc7ea5a2a4748","word":"signature","forms":["signature"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edeac9b6fadf7218","term":"signature","forms":["signature","more signature","most signature"],"pos":"adj","zh":"標誌性的；最具代表性的","explanation":"指某事物非常能代表一個人、品牌、地方或風格，看到它就容易聯想到其來源，就像一個人的獨特簽名一樣。","examples":[{"en":"This restaurant is famous for its signature dish.","zh":"這家餐廳以它的招牌菜聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her signature dish combines roast duck and sour cherries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95676e67482f9451","term":"signature","forms":["signature","signatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簽名；署名","explanation":"指一個人親自寫下的名字，用來證明身份，或表示同意、認可某份檔案。它把“這個東西確實和我有關”明確標記出來。","examples":[{"en":"Please add your signature at the bottom of the form.","zh":"請在表格底部簽上你的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contract is not valid without her signature.","zh":"沒有她的簽名，這份合同就無效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59e0185b95958c13","term":"signature","forms":["signature","signatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標誌性特色；招牌產品","explanation":"指某人、品牌或作品最有辨識度的特點或產品，像一枚能讓人認出主人的簽名。它既可以指風格，也可以指具體商品或菜品。","examples":[{"en":"Her bold colors have become her signature.","zh":"大膽的色彩已經成為她的標誌性特色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chef's signature is a delicate lemon tart.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8698fb89e125b92abe7d","word":"significance","forms":["significance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc84785e4a05120f","term":"significance","forms":["significance","significances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要性；影響力","explanation":"表示某件事有多重要、會產生多大影響，或為什麼值得重視。也就是看這件事在整體中有多大的“分量”。","examples":[{"en":"The discovery was of great significance to medical research.","zh":"這項發現對醫學研究具有重大意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The decision has little significance for ordinary workers.","zh":"這個決定對普通工人來說沒什麼重要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/significance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3eeb68ec3f6f4df5","term":"significance","forms":["significance","significances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"含義；意義","explanation":"表示一個手勢、符號、事件或行為所傳達的內容，也就是它在表達什麼。這裡關注的不是事情有多重要，而是它背後代表什麼。","examples":[{"en":"She explained the significance of the symbol to the children.","zh":"她向孩子們解釋了這個符號的含義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I didn't understand the significance of her warning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/significance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e61db885bd6e7f403a7b","word":"significant","forms":["significant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-029bb2d2640ca9f5","term":"significant","forms":["significant","more significant","most significant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有意義的；傳達資訊的","explanation":"表示某個詞、聲音、動作或現象承載著可以理解的意義，不只是單純存在。它是“值得注意、因為帶有意義”的起點。","examples":[{"en":"The pause was significant because it changed the meaning of the sentence.","zh":"這次停頓很有意義，因為它改變了句子的意思。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They exchanged a significant glance when his name arose.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/significant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5c02b9b628f98a28","term":"significant","forms":["significant","more significant","most significant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"重要的；影響明顯的","explanation":"表示某件事帶來的影響足夠明顯，或在事情發展中佔有重要位置。它可以由“有意義”自然引申為“值得重視”。","examples":[{"en":"The new bridge was a significant step toward improving transport in the region.","zh":"這座新橋是改善該地區交通的重要一步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her advice had a significant effect on my decision.","zh":"她的建議對我的決定產生了明顯影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/significant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":3,"counts":{"112":1,"114":2}}},{"id":"ceec-e6c18fdbe59783dfefef","word":"silence","forms":["silence"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd0f1f49b5136ff2","term":"silence","forms":["silence","silences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寂靜；無聲","explanation":"指環境中完全或幾乎沒有聲音的狀態，就像所有聲音都被按下了靜音鍵。","examples":[{"en":"The silence of the empty house made me uneasy.","zh":"空屋裡的寂靜讓我感到不安。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Complete silence followed the last note of the song.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c776e80fe8fa9cc","term":"silence","forms":["silence","silences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沉默；不發言","explanation":"指人選擇不說話，或暫時不表達自己的想法；這裡被按下靜音鍵的是人的聲音。","examples":[{"en":"After the question, she chose silence.","zh":"面對這個問題，她選擇了沉默。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His silence during the debate disappointed his supporters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d0818815fa2ed62","term":"silence","forms":["silence","silences","silencing","silenced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使安靜；讓……不出聲","explanation":"指主動讓某人、某個群體或某種聲音停止發聲，就像替它按下靜音鍵。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher raised her hand to silence the class.","zh":"老師舉起手讓全班安靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher silenced the class with one gesture.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a9b9fc8e986cc2fc943","word":"silent","forms":["silent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18fad8eb69b461a3","term":"silent","forms":["silent","silenter","more silent","silentest","most silent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寂靜無聲","explanation":"周圍完全沒有聲音，安靜到幾乎聽不見任何動靜；這是 silent 最直接的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The village was silent after midnight.","zh":"午夜過後，村子一片寂靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For a moment, the entire room fell silent.","zh":"有那麼一會兒，整個房間都安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d832b74c7a2bc6d3","term":"silent","forms":["silent","silenter","more silent","silentest","most silent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不說話的","explanation":"形容人沒有開口說話，可能是暫時不願說、無話可說，或本來就少言寡語。","examples":[{"en":"She remained silent about what had happened.","zh":"她對發生的事情保持沉默。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room went silent when the teacher entered.","zh":"老師進來時，房間裡的人都安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b377d06e80ec2b2","term":"silent","forms":["silent","silenter","more silent","silentest","most silent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"靜音的","explanation":"裝置仍然開著或正在接收資訊，但聲音被關閉了；因此它處於“沒有發出聲音”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Please put your phone on silent during the meeting.","zh":"開會期間請把手機調成靜音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I missed the call because my phone was on silent.","zh":"我沒接到電話，因為我的手機開著靜音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2c819b6790de306847f","word":"silk","forms":["silk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cee62d6412d728d1","term":"silk","forms":["silk","silks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蠶絲等天然細纖維","explanation":"silk首先是蠶或其他節肢動物分泌出的細而結實的纖維，最常見的來源是蠶。它是還沒有織成布的“絲”。","examples":[{"en":"The spider used its silk to build a web.","zh":"蜘蛛用它的絲織了一張網。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The caterpillar spun a cocoon from fine silk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a7782d5c91e07dc","term":"silk","forms":["silk","silks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"絲綢布料","explanation":"silk也指用絲纖維織成的細軟布料，也就是通常所說的絲綢。這裡的重點從“原料”轉到了“用原料織成的布”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a light silk scarf on the train.","zh":"她在火車上戴著一條輕薄的絲綢圍巾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This silk feels cool against the skin.","zh":"這種絲綢貼在皮膚上感覺很涼爽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30b8795437a029dcf03c","word":"silly","forms":["silly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43b5f5dbd2f145a1","term":"silly","forms":["silly","sillier","silliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愚蠢而可笑的","explanation":"因為想法、外表或行為很蠢而顯得可笑，常常帶有輕微的嘲笑意味。","examples":[{"en":"They were laughing at a silly joke.","zh":"他們在笑一個傻氣的笑話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I felt silly when I realized I had been looking at the wrong map.","zh":"我發現自己一直看錯地圖時，覺得自己真傻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0860d892c87a2c19","term":"silly","forms":["silly","sillier","silliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愚蠢的、傻氣的","explanation":"指缺乏判斷力、做事不明智或犯了低階錯誤；這是現代最重要的義項之一。","examples":[{"en":"It was a silly mistake, but we fixed it quickly.","zh":"那是個低階錯誤，不過我們很快就改正了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be silly—of course you can come with us.","zh":"別傻了——你當然可以和我們一起去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78cde64c3e47f2cbfd9d","word":"silver","forms":["silver"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-efc2913633e365a7","term":"silver","forms":["silver","more silver","most silver"],"pos":"adj","zh":"銀製的","explanation":"指物品由銀製成，或通常被理解為銀製成的。核心畫面就是“閃亮的銀被做成了物件”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a silver necklace to the dinner.","zh":"她戴著一條銀項鍊參加晚宴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She polished the silver candlesticks before dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb8f4c4192deaf6b","term":"silver","forms":["silver","more silver","most silver"],"pos":"adj","zh":"銀白色的","explanation":"指顏色像銀，通常是有光澤的灰白色；這裡借用的是銀表面的閃亮外觀，而非金屬材料。","examples":[{"en":"The moonlight turned the lake silver.","zh":"月光把湖面映成了銀白色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has short silver hair.","zh":"他留著一頭銀白色的短髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8323981c94d40fb0","term":"silver","forms":["silver","silvers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銀","explanation":"指一種有光澤的白色金屬，是整組詞義的中心：其他許多用法都來自它的顏色、價值或製品。","examples":[{"en":"Silver is used in some jewelry and electronics.","zh":"銀被用於一些首飾和電子產品中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The necklace is made of pure silver.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00a9e08ce4c65c4c2471","word":"similar","forms":["similar"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-babf74f9316d47dd","term":"similar","forms":["similar","more similar","most similar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相似的；相近的","explanation":"指兩個事物在外形、性質、功能或其他特徵上有共同點，但不是完全一樣。它可以用於人、物、想法、經歷等各種比較。","examples":[{"en":"This design is very similar to the original.","zh":"這個設計與原來的非常相似。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two children have similar interests.","zh":"這兩個孩子有相似的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/similar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76001982ebfbec18","term":"similar","forms":["similar","more similar","most similar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相似的（幾何）","explanation":"在幾何中，兩個圖形雖然大小可能不同，但形狀對應：相應的角相等，相應的線段按同一比例變化。它仍然保留了“看起來是同一種形狀”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"These two triangles are similar but not congruent.","zh":"這兩個三角形相似，但不全等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These triangles are similar because their corresponding angles are equal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/similar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8cc0e56b16368984eb73","word":"similarity","forms":["similarity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68cd2f3da7f1cb91","term":"similarity","forms":["similarity","similarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外表或形式上的相似","explanation":"指一個事物在外表、形狀、聲音或整體樣式上像另一個事物，重點是容易觀察到的相像之處。","examples":[{"en":"The similarity between the two paintings is easy to see.","zh":"這兩幅畫之間的相似之處很容易看出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a strong similarity between the twins' voices.","zh":"這對雙胞胎的聲音非常相似。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/similarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f12bafb97c9cf41a","term":"similarity","forms":["similarity","similarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共同性質或相似關係","explanation":"指兩個或多個事物共享某些性質、特點或規律的關係；它不一定是外表相像，也可以是思想、事實、行為或結構上的共同點。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers found a surprising similarity in the two studies.","zh":"研究人員發現這兩項研究有一個令人驚訝的共同點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The similarity between their handwriting is remarkable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/similarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7a39b72f29718e653e7","word":"simple","forms":["simple"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-026af2722ed12b4d","term":"simple","forms":["simple","simpler","more simple","simplest","most simple"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不復雜的","explanation":"像只折一層的紙一樣，沒有許多附加部分或隱藏層次，事情本身容易看清。","examples":[{"en":"The machine has a simple design.","zh":"這臺機器的設計很簡單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There must be a simple explanation.","zh":"一定有一個簡單的解釋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf0c9c545d4b0044","term":"simple","forms":["simple","simpler","more simple","simplest","most simple"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易的","explanation":"因為步驟少、難度低而容易完成或理解，重點在“好做、好懂”。","examples":[{"en":"Here is a simple way to fix the problem.","zh":"這裡有一個解決這個問題的簡單方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The instructions are simple to follow.","zh":"這些說明很容易照著做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-602b3aed265722cf","term":"simple","forms":["simple","simpler","more simple","simplest","most simple"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樸素的","explanation":"沒有華麗裝飾或誇張設計，外表自然、剋制而不復雜。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a simple black dress.","zh":"她穿了一條樸素的黑裙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We chose simple decorations for the room.","zh":"我們為房間選了樸素的裝飾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ae0514924b1db04e8c4","word":"simplicity","forms":["simplicity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29aff539a66c6791","term":"simplicity","forms":["simplicity","simplicities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簡單；簡潔","explanation":"指某事物不復雜、沒有多餘步驟或裝飾的狀態，也可以指這種簡潔本身帶來的清楚和易懂。它既能描述結構簡單，也能描述風格樸素。","examples":[{"en":"The simplicity of the design makes it easy to use.","zh":"這個設計很簡潔，因此使用起來很方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I admire the simplicity of her explanation.","zh":"我很欣賞她解釋得簡明易懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simplicity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e55dea01f8db239db05a","word":"simplify","forms":["simplify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64eb2c8d19ba5a13","term":"simplify","forms":["simplify","simplifies","simplifying","simplified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"簡化；使更易理解","explanation":"指透過刪去不必要的部分、減少複雜步驟，或用更容易懂的方式表達，使某事物變得簡單。物件可以是說明、過程、設計、規則等。","examples":[{"en":"We simplified the instructions so that everyone could follow them.","zh":"我們簡化了說明，讓每個人都能照著做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This app simplifies the process of booking a ticket.","zh":"這個應用簡化了訂票流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simplify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d73952b7d98233f","term":"simplify","forms":["simplify","simplifies","simplifying","simplified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得簡單","explanation":"指某個過程、系統或事物隨著調整、發展或變化，本身逐漸減少複雜性，不強調誰主動把它改簡單。","examples":[{"en":"Over time, the process simplified and became easier for everyone to use.","zh":"隨著時間推移，這個流程變得更簡單，大家用起來也更容易了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The calculation simplifies when the terms cancel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simplify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ec8b3a4a10e5266e36a","word":"simply","forms":["simply"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a55f93059365abc2","term":"simply","forms":["simply","more simply","most simply"],"pos":"adv","zh":"簡單地；單獨地","explanation":"表示以簡單、直接、沒有額外步驟的方式做某事，也可以表示把物件單獨拿出來看，不加其他成分。","examples":[{"en":"You can simply click the button to continue.","zh":"你只要直接點選這個按鈕就可以繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Simply put, the plan will not work.","zh":"簡單地說，這個計劃行不通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f31fe0ff7c2c1d36","term":"simply","forms":["simply","more simply","most simply"],"pos":"adv","zh":"僅僅；只是","explanation":"表示範圍被限制在這一件事或這一點上，強調沒有更多含義、目的或物件。","examples":[{"en":"I was simply asking a question.","zh":"我只是問了一個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He simply wanted to help.","zh":"他只是想幫忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5fd35d093d8d45f5765e","word":"simultaneous","forms":["simultaneous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96c4a55ba86d1e63","term":"simultaneous","forms":["simultaneous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"同時發生的","explanation":"指兩個或多個事情在同一個時刻發生，就像幾盞燈同時亮起，而不是一個接著一個發生。","examples":[{"en":"The two alarms went off simultaneously.","zh":"兩個警報同時響了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The concert will be broadcast in several countries with simultaneous translation.","zh":"這場音樂會將在幾個國家播出，並提供同聲傳譯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/simultaneous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cccc68c7928e63feb966","word":"sin","forms":["sin"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1578d3b2a8012828","term":"sin","forms":["sin","sins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宗教上的罪","explanation":"指違背神意、宗教戒律或宗教法律的行為，是“罪”的正式宗教義。這個核心畫面就是人越過了神所規定的界線。","examples":[{"en":"Many believers see lying to protect a friend as a sin.","zh":"許多信徒認為，為了保護朋友而撒謊也是一種罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He confessed his sins to the priest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f04f42163ac71ae0","term":"sin","forms":["sin","sins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過錯；壞事","explanation":"泛指違背道德、規則或正常期望的錯事，是“罪”在日常語境中的較輕、更寬泛用法。它可以是嚴重的錯誤，也可以只是某個不妥之處。","examples":[{"en":"Leaving the children without dinner was a serious sin of carelessness.","zh":"讓孩子們沒飯吃是一個嚴重的粗心過錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wasting such good food would be a sin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c794d6a9ac225976","term":"sin","forms":["sin","sins","sinning","sinned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"犯罪；作惡","explanation":"表示做出違反神意、宗教戒律或重要道德規範的事，也可較寬泛地表示“犯錯、越界”。它是名詞“罪”的動詞形式，核心畫面仍是越過了應有的界線。","examples":[{"en":"He believed that he had sinned by betraying his closest friend.","zh":"他認為背叛最親密的朋友是自己犯下的罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sermon urged listeners to repent when they had sinned.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6b5a3ded016ab7826989","word":"since","forms":["since"],"officialPos":"conj./prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-affe40741c06beae","term":"since","forms":["since"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從那以後","explanation":"它把時間線上的起點接到前文提到的過去時刻，表示從那時以後一直如此，通常暗含延續到現在。","examples":[{"en":"She moved away in May and I haven't heard from her since.","zh":"她五月搬走了，從那以後我就沒收到過她的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We met last winter and haven't spoken since.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/since","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7daf4f8ed054dbd9","term":"since","forms":["since"],"pos":"prep","zh":"自……以來","explanation":"它直接指出時間線的起點：某種狀態或動作從這個過去時刻開始，一直延續到現在。","examples":[{"en":"I have worked here since 2021.","zh":"我從2021年起就在這裡工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have lived here since the bridge was built.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/since","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c9331652a12eb753f11d","word":"sincere","forms":["sincere"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5fcc59bc1fda69a7","term":"sincere","forms":["sincere","more sincere","sincerer","most sincere","sincerest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真誠的；發自內心的","explanation":"形容一個人說話、許諾或做事時確實抱著這樣的想法，不是在裝樣子或敷衍別人。它強調內心和外在表達是一致的，就像把真實的心意直接遞給別人。","examples":[{"en":"I believe he is sincere in his offer to help.","zh":"我相信他提出幫忙是真心的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sincere smile made everyone feel welcome.","zh":"她真誠的微笑讓每個人都感到受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sincere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5293dcceafe1b0fe","term":"sincere","forms":["sincere","more sincere","sincerer","most sincere","sincerest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真心實意的；誠懇的","explanation":"形容某個具體的努力、道歉、感謝或願望確實是認真投入、發自內心的，即使最後沒有成功，或者方法並不恰當，也仍然可以說是 sincere。","examples":[{"en":"She made a sincere if misguided effort to solve the problem.","zh":"她真心實意地努力解決這個問題，雖然方法並不恰當。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please accept my sincere thanks for your help.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sincere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4ed18aab7b22367c14e","word":"sincerity","forms":["sincerity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddf4f5338949a804","term":"sincerity","forms":["sincerity","sincerities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"真誠；真摯","explanation":"指一個人的感情、態度或意圖是發自內心的，沒有假裝或敷衍。它就像“心口一致”：外在的表達和內心的真實想法相符。","examples":[{"en":"She apologized with sincerity, and everyone could see that she regretted what she had done.","zh":"她真誠地道了歉，大家都看得出她確實為自己的所作所為感到後悔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His sincerity made it easier for the team to trust him.","zh":"他的真誠讓團隊更容易信任他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sincerity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6342d0648a74645722ea","word":"sing","forms":["sing"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-37d69cef51ab3421","term":"sing","forms":["sing","sings","singing","sang","sung","sungen","singest","sangest","sungest","singeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"唱歌","explanation":"指用嗓音發出有旋律的聲音，是“sing”最基本、最常用的意思；不要求唱得專業。","examples":[{"en":"I like to sing while I cook.","zh":"我喜歡一邊做飯一邊唱歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sings in the school choir.","zh":"她在學校合唱團唱歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84a0edb39b3c0dc5","term":"sing","forms":["sing","sings","singing","sang","sung","sungen","singest","sangest","sungest","singeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"演唱聲樂部分","explanation":"指在一首音樂作品中演唱自己的聲樂部分，強調參與演唱這件事，不強調唱得是否專業。","examples":[{"en":"Maya sings the main part in the school musical.","zh":"瑪雅在學校音樂劇中演唱主唱部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sang the soprano part in the final chorus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9cc8bd6e1c1bcc3b","term":"sing","forms":["sing","sings","singing","sang","sung","sungen","singest","sangest","sungest","singeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"唱出；用歌聲表達","explanation":"指把歌曲、歌詞或某種內容用有旋律的聲音唱出來，後面通常接歌曲或內容。","examples":[{"en":"He sang a lullaby to the baby.","zh":"他給嬰兒唱了一首搖籃曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sang the school song together.","zh":"孩子們一起唱了校歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92d74bb8bddbbb9c8b50","word":"singer","forms":["singer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7c3ad1b8d4cc75d","term":"singer","forms":["singer","singers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歌手","explanation":"指唱歌的人，尤其指以唱歌為職業或經常公開演唱的人。這個詞把注意力放在“發出歌聲的人”身上，而不是歌曲本身。","examples":[{"en":"The singer thanked the audience after the concert.","zh":"演唱會結束後，歌手向觀眾道謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My sister wants to become a singer.","zh":"我姐姐想成為一名歌手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/singer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f49436866af6cc21","term":"singer","forms":["singer","Singers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"Singer縫紉機","explanation":"指Singer品牌生產的縫紉機；這個名稱來自創始人Singer，而不是因為機器會唱歌。","examples":[{"en":"She learned to sew on her grandmother's old Singer.","zh":"她用祖母的舊Singer縫紉機學會了縫紉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandmother still sews on an old Singer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/singer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-947f187506f7629c81c8","word":"single","forms":["single"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-107909a4fbf9c868","term":"single","forms":["single"],"pos":"adj","zh":"單獨的；唯一的","explanation":"表示只有一個，或沒有其他東西陪同、配合；重點是數量上“一個”或狀態上“獨自”。","examples":[{"en":"She left without saying a single word.","zh":"她一言不發地離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a single reason to trust him.","zh":"我只需要一個相信他的理由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/single","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2239d674b5d68bca","term":"single","forms":["single"],"pos":"adj","zh":"單身的；沒有伴侶的","explanation":"表示沒有結婚，現代用法中通常也表示目前沒有戀愛伴侶；這是“獨自、不成對”在人際關係中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She is single and enjoys living on her own.","zh":"她是單身，喜歡獨自生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The form asks whether you are single or married.","zh":"這張表會詢問你是單身還是已婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/single","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8eba5de916690a66","term":"single","forms":["single","singles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"單身者","explanation":"指沒有結婚或沒有戀愛伴侶的人，是形容詞“single”名詞化後的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The community center hosts events for local singles.","zh":"社群中心為當地單身者舉辦活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many singles prefer meeting people through shared hobbies.","zh":"許多單身者更喜歡透過共同愛好認識別人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/single","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1900fbeafc62cc3","term":"single","forms":["single","singles","singling","singled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"單獨挑出","explanation":"single表示把某個人或某件事從一群物件中單獨挑出來，或把物件一個個分開處理。它正好體現“一個、分開、不成對”的主線。","examples":[{"en":"The coach singled out Maya for her calm leadership.","zh":"教練特別表揚了瑪雅沉著的領導能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One mistake was singled out as the main cause of the delay.","zh":"有一個錯誤被單獨指出是延誤的主要原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/single","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d0fe5ec8bf181535a0f","word":"singular","forms":["singular"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-259821f2de9ecbbe","term":"singular","forms":["singular","more singular","most singular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"單獨的；個別的","explanation":"指在較大的群體或數量中只取其中一個，強調它是一個獨立個體，而不是整體或多個物件。","examples":[{"en":"A singular case is not enough to prove the rule.","zh":"一個單獨的案例不足以證明這條規律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The collection contains several singular examples of the technique.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/singular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-484828a3c8fb3d21","term":"singular","forms":["singular","more singular","most singular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獨一無二的；獨特的","explanation":"指某人或某物在同類中只有一個，因而具有鮮明而不可替代的特點。它是“從一群中單獨站出來”的核心延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Her singular voice made the song unforgettable.","zh":"她獨特的嗓音讓這首歌令人難忘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He showed a singular ability to remain calm under pressure.","zh":"他表現出在壓力下保持冷靜的非凡能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/singular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-878773b806d359d2","term":"singular","forms":["singular","more singular","most singular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"單數的","explanation":"在語法中，指表示一個人、一個物或一個概念，而不是兩個或更多物件的形式。它把“只有一個”這條主線直接用於語言結構。","examples":[{"en":"The singular form of this noun takes a different article.","zh":"這個名詞的單數形式使用不同的冠詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a singular verb with this subject.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/singular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e5ecca974b14c3d","term":"singular","forms":["singular","singulars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"單數形式","explanation":"指一個詞表示一個人或一個事物時所採用的形式，例如與複數形式相對的名詞或動詞形式。它是“只有一個”這條主線在語法中的名詞化表達。","examples":[{"en":"The singular of “children” is “child”.","zh":"“children”的單數形式是“child”。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The singular of mice is mouse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/singular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1978baf2c153fd3bf363","word":"sink","forms":["sink"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3fbc16879bb1b01","term":"sink","forms":["sink","sinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水槽","explanation":"sink 是用來裝水、洗手或洗東西的水槽，通常固定在廚房或浴室的檯面上。它體現了“向下進入並被吸收”的核心概念：水先流進槽裡，再進入排水系統。","examples":[{"en":"I washed the vegetables in the kitchen sink.","zh":"我在廚房水槽裡洗了蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the dirty dishes in the sink.","zh":"請把髒盤子放在水槽裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a2c7400d29e30a5","term":"sink","forms":["sink","sinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排水口","explanation":"sink 也可以專指把廢水排走的排水口或排水裝置，水會從這裡向下流走並被排出。這個意思和“水槽”密切相關，但重點是排水功能。","examples":[{"en":"The sink is blocked, so the water is draining very slowly.","zh":"排水口堵住了，所以水排得很慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put a strainer over the sink to catch the food scraps.","zh":"在排水口上放一個濾網，擋住食物殘渣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3888d11832607ed","term":"sink","forms":["sink","sinks","sinking","sank","sunk","sunken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下沉；沉入","explanation":"表示人或物由於重力等原因向下進入水、泥土或其他空間，正對應“向下進入並被吸收”的核心畫面；也可表示太陽等看起來逐漸落下。","examples":[{"en":"The stone sank slowly into the mud.","zh":"石頭慢慢沉入了泥裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sun sank below the hills.","zh":"太陽落到了山丘下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dab0a5decbb22c37","term":"sink","forms":["sink","sinks","sinking","sank","sunk","sunken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"減弱；低落","explanation":"表示情緒、精神、活力或力量逐漸下降，好像向下沉入低處；它把“向下進入並被吸收”引申為狀態被削弱。","examples":[{"en":"Her spirits sank when she heard the bad news.","zh":"聽到這個壞訊息後，她的情緒低落了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team's confidence sank after the early goal.","zh":"球隊在開場失球后信心下降了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-6c126e81fa8dc29d6413","word":"sip","forms":["sip"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98360e684178b49e","term":"sip","forms":["sip","sips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一小口","explanation":"sip是輕輕喝下的一點飲料，重點在數量少、動作慢，而不是一口大量喝下。","examples":[{"en":"She took a sip of tea and smiled.","zh":"她喝了一小口茶，笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take small sips of water during the hike.","zh":"徒步時要一小口一小口地喝水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c532708943ba09e0","term":"sip","forms":["sip","sips","sipping","sipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"小口喝","explanation":"sip表示把飲料分成許多小口慢慢喝，而不是一下子喝完；可以想象嘴唇輕碰杯沿，一點點吸入。","examples":[{"en":"He sipped his coffee while reading the newspaper.","zh":"他一邊看報紙，一邊小口喝咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please sip the soup; it is still very hot.","zh":"請小口喝湯，湯還很燙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-30390115b066968fc062","word":"sir","forms":["sir"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33b1b4438f69594f","term":"sir","forms":["sir","sirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對成年男性的禮貌稱呼","explanation":"當不知道一位男性的姓名或正式稱號時，可以用sir禮貌地叫他，類似中文裡較正式的“先生”。它也常用於對年長男性表示尊重。","examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, sir, is this seat taken?","zh":"先生，不好意思，請問這個座位有人嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thank you for your help, sir.","zh":"先生，謝謝您的幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1afa3c39b2d2706","term":"sir","forms":["sir","sirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身份較高的男性","explanation":"這個意義把sir看作一種身份稱謂，指社會地位、職務或等級較高的男性；它和後面的直接稱呼意義相連，核心都是對男性表示尊敬。","examples":[{"en":"The young officer stood beside an important sir at the ceremony.","zh":"那名年輕軍官在儀式上站在一位重要男士身旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The servant bowed before his noble sir.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1980d3927f07fec9c8d7","word":"sister","forms":["sister"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2235069a7fb95e6c","term":"sister","forms":["sister","sisters","sistren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"姐妹","explanation":"指與某人有相同父母的女性兄弟姐妹，可以是姐姐，也可以是妹妹；具體年齡通常由上下文或其他詞說明。","examples":[{"en":"My sister is studying medicine at university.","zh":"我妹妹（或姐姐）正在大學學醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have two sisters, both older than me.","zh":"我有兩個姐姐，她們都比我大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sister","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bdc726690a8db2ca","term":"sister","forms":["sister","sisters","sistren"],"pos":"noun","zh":"姐妹般的女性；同一群體中的女性","explanation":"把沒有血緣關係但因性別、族群、職業、宗教、組織或共同信念而感到親近的女性稱為 sister，核心仍是“彼此站在同一邊”。","examples":[{"en":"After years of working together, she considered her colleague a sister.","zh":"一起工作多年後，她把那位同事當成了姐妹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She welcomed her fellow campaigners as sisters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sister","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-584178e5e3517ddcebc6","word":"sit","forms":["sit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0ed6df796f40e049","term":"sit","forms":["sit","sits","sitting","sat","sate","sitten","sattest","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"坐著","explanation":"表示身體保持上身直立、由臀部支撐的姿勢，即“處於坐姿”。","examples":[{"en":"She is sitting by the window.","zh":"她正坐在窗邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sat beside my brother on the bus.","zh":"我在公交車上坐在哥哥旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d761852cadec39df","term":"sit","forms":["sit","sits","sitting","sat","sate","sitten","sattest","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"坐下","explanation":"表示從站立或其他姿勢移動到坐姿，也就是“坐下來”。","examples":[{"en":"Please sit down and make yourself comfortable.","zh":"請坐，別拘束。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sit beside me while we check the map.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e43c342248ea41a9","term":"sit","forms":["sit","sits","sitting","sat","sate","sitten","sattest","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"處在某個位置","explanation":"把人或物看成“安放在某處”：人坐在那裡，物品也可以靜靜地放在那裡。","examples":[{"en":"Your keys are sitting on the kitchen table.","zh":"你的鑰匙放在廚房桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small lamp sits beside the bed.","zh":"床邊放著一盞小燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fbae041b02c41ed0fd8a","word":"site","forms":["site"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9488ed76572a3d1","term":"site","forms":["site","sites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物所在的地點","explanation":"指某座城市、房屋或其他事物實際所在的地方，重點是“它被固定或存在於哪裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The old site of the theater is now a public garden.","zh":"劇院原址現在是一座公共花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Archaeologists found tools at the site of the ancient settlement.","zh":"考古學家在這處古代聚居地遺址發現了工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/site","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c937f4dd7c69318","term":"site","forms":["site","sites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"選定的場地","explanation":"指為建造、經營或長期使用而專門選定或準備的地方；它不只是“所在地點”，還強調預定用途。","examples":[{"en":"The town has chosen a site for the new library.","zh":"鎮上已經為新圖書館選定了場地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are looking for a suitable site for a solar farm.","zh":"他們正在尋找適合建設太陽能農場的場地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/site","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e91bfe0264a82e70","term":"site","forms":["site","sites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網站","explanation":"指網際網路上提供資訊、服務或內容的一組頁面，可以把它理解成內容所在的“線上地點”。","examples":[{"en":"You can register for the course on the school's site.","zh":"你可以在學校的網站上報名這門課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The site lets visitors search the museum's collection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/site","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5df90148043e654b","term":"site","forms":["site","sites","siting","sited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為專案選址","explanation":"表示把建築物或建設專案安排、規劃在某個地點，使它在那裡建成或執行；這是名詞“場地”義的主動延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The new hospital will be sited near the railway station.","zh":"新醫院將選址在火車站附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council plans to site the recycling center outside the town.","zh":"市議會計劃把回收中心建在城外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/site","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113,115],"total":4,"counts":{"111":2,"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-fc097e65503cb3ad9eb8","word":"situation","forms":["situation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b689fc55d6ac7f43","term":"situation","forms":["situation","situations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"處境；局面","explanation":"指某一時刻由各種條件和事件共同形成的處境或局面。它可以是好是壞，也可以只是對當前狀態的客觀描述。","examples":[{"en":"We need to understand the situation before making a decision.","zh":"我們需要先了解情況，再作決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The situation at work has improved a lot.","zh":"工作上的情況已經大有改善。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/situation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9be8269789382fc5","term":"situation","forms":["situation","situations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麻煩局面；棘手問題","explanation":"指一組令人擔憂、難以處理或已經造成麻煩的情況。它是“局面”這個核心義的負面用法，常暗示說話人希望儘快處理。","examples":[{"en":"We have a situation here: the front door will not open.","zh":"這裡出了點狀況：前門打不開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police arrived quickly to deal with the situation.","zh":"警方很快趕到處理這個棘手局面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/situation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,114,115],"total":5,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1,"114":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-ccdcbe846f3da4eb044f","word":"size","forms":["size"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a151f54a27192699","term":"size","forms":["size","sizes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大小；規模","explanation":"size表示某個東西有多大，關注的是它的整體大小或規模，而不一定是某一條具體的長、寬或高。","examples":[{"en":"The size of the new library surprised everyone.","zh":"新圖書館的規模讓所有人都感到驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a box about this size.","zh":"我們需要一個大約這麼大的箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/size","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d9263d6cf97f4dc","term":"size","forms":["size","sizes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尺碼；規格","explanation":"size也可以指衣服、鞋子等商品按大小劃分出的具體規格，也就是適合某人的尺碼。","examples":[{"en":"Do you have this jacket in a smaller size?","zh":"這件夾克有小一號的嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These shoes are available in every size.","zh":"這種鞋每種尺碼都有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/size","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f054b3819d570a3f","term":"size","forms":["size","sizes","sizing","sized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"估量大小","explanation":"size可以表示憑觀察或經驗估計某物的大小，像是在心裡先用一把尺子量一量。","examples":[{"en":"She sized up the suitcase before deciding what to pack.","zh":"她先估量了一下行李箱的大小，再決定要裝什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Size the opening carefully before buying a new window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/size","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b22fca0ad0a2ff8b00f","word":"skate","forms":["skate"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce42f1b4fce5df13","term":"skate","forms":["skate","skates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑冰鞋","explanation":"指固定在腳底、用來在冰面上滑行的鞋，底部通常有金屬刀片。","examples":[{"en":"She rented a pair of skates at the rink.","zh":"她在溜冰場租了一雙滑冰鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One skate had a loose blade.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcf20d9332a7e542","term":"skate","forms":["skate","skates","skating","skated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滑行；滑冰","explanation":"指穿著滑冰鞋在冰面或地面上移動，核心畫面就是藉助鞋底或輪子輕快地滑過去。","examples":[{"en":"The children skated across the frozen pond.","zh":"孩子們滑過了結冰的池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I learned to skate when I was six.","zh":"我六歲時學會了滑冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ac11a92104c4d7d1403","word":"skeleton","forms":["skeleton"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-444aa5531aff7578","term":"skeleton","forms":["skeleton","skeletons","skeleta"],"pos":"noun","zh":"骨骼","explanation":"指生物體中支撐身體、由骨頭和軟骨組成的骨骼系統；在人類和許多脊椎動物體內，它位於身體內部。","examples":[{"en":"The skeleton supports the body and protects many vital organs.","zh":"骨骼支撐身體並保護許多重要器官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displayed a complete dinosaur skeleton.","zh":"博物館展出了一具完整的恐龍骨骼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skeleton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2667e805baa1f3d2","term":"skeleton","forms":["skeleton","skeletons","skeleta"],"pos":"noun","zh":"基本框架","explanation":"指一個組織、計劃、觀點或系統中支撐整體的核心結構；即使細節改變，這個骨架仍然保留。","examples":[{"en":"We have the skeleton of a plan, but many details still need to be added.","zh":"我們已經有了計劃的基本框架，但還需要補充許多細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new building keeps the skeleton of the old structure.","zh":"這座新建築保留了舊建築的基本結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skeleton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5cb6c6455ab737f29624","word":"skeptical","forms":["skeptical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a70f6ddbd5624954","term":"skeptical","forms":["skeptical","more skeptical","most skeptical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"持懷疑態度的","explanation":"形容一個人聽到某種說法後不會立刻相信，而是會追問、檢查證據或等待進一步證明。它強調“目前還不確定是否可信”，不等於已經斷定對方在說謊。","examples":[{"en":"The manager was skeptical about the sudden sales increase.","zh":"經理對銷售額突然增加這件事持懷疑態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was skeptical at first, but the evidence changed my mind.","zh":"我起初半信半疑，但證據改變了我的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skeptical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f416b363c6c5f07011f5","word":"sketch","forms":["sketch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f05e682ee1fa86f1","term":"sketch","forms":["sketch","sketches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"速寫；草圖","explanation":"用很短時間徒手畫出的粗略圖畫，重點是抓住形狀和大致關係，而不是完成細緻的成品。","examples":[{"en":"She made a quick sketch of the old bridge before the light disappeared.","zh":"天色暗下來之前，她快速畫了一張那座老橋的草圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer showed us a rough sketch of the new logo.","zh":"設計師給我們看了新標誌的草圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5428a5658dc1d7a","term":"sketch","forms":["sketch","sketches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"草案；粗略計劃","explanation":"把一個還沒有完成的作品、計劃或想法先用粗略形式寫出來，供以後修改和發展。","examples":[{"en":"I brought a rough sketch of my proposal to the meeting.","zh":"我帶著提案的初步草案來參加會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His sketch of the proposal fitted on one page.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75d1f11d26a55efe","term":"sketch","forms":["sketch","sketches","sketching","sketched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"畫速寫；畫草圖","explanation":"快速用幾筆畫出物件的大致形狀或結構，通常不追求細節和完成度。","examples":[{"en":"I like to sketch people on the train.","zh":"我喜歡在火車上給乘客畫速寫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sketched out the room layout on a napkin.","zh":"他在餐巾紙上畫出了房間佈局的草圖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11b5ece03305bd42","term":"sketch","forms":["sketch","sketches","sketching","sketched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"簡要描述；概述","explanation":"只抓住主要事實和輪廓來說明一個事件、人物或想法，不展開全部細節。","examples":[{"en":"The manager sketched out the plan at the start of the meeting.","zh":"經理在會議開始時簡要說明了計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sketched the project's history in a few sentences.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sketch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf659bd3fba074e3ae0e","word":"ski","forms":["ski"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb6e60505b9e69b5","term":"ski","forms":["ski","skis"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑雪板；滑具","explanation":"指一對用於在雪地或水面上滑行的長而扁的滑具，通常穿在腳上。這裡的核心畫面就是“腳下貼著地面滑行的長條板”。","examples":[{"en":"She left her skis by the door after a long day on the mountain.","zh":"她在山上滑了一整天后，把滑雪板放在門邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One ski came loose during the steep descent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ski","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f1f9117edaa2a7c","term":"ski","forms":["ski","skis","skies","skiing","skied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滑雪；用滑雪板滑行","explanation":"指人穿著滑雪板移動，核心就是“讓腳下的長條板帶著自己滑起來”。它通常不強調目的地，只說明正在進行滑行這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The children learned to ski during the winter holiday.","zh":"孩子們在寒假期間學會了滑雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They skied down the gentle slope together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ski","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c53c074d7ac6a2728b6","word":"skill","forms":["skill"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e425907d760ea62","term":"skill","forms":["skill","skills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"技能；技巧；能力","explanation":"指透過學習、訓練或經驗獲得的、把某件事做好或做得熟練的能力。它可以是具體技巧，也可以是較寬泛的工作或生活能力。","examples":[{"en":"She has excellent communication skills.","zh":"她有很強的溝通能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need patience and skill to repair a watch.","zh":"修理手錶需要耐心和技巧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38c8dec10f77441f6846","word":"skilled","forms":["skilled"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d1f5f60a6f2f810","term":"skilled","forms":["skilled","more skilled","most skilled"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熟練的；有技能的","explanation":"形容人掌握了某種技能，做這件事很熟練；這個“本領在手上”的畫面是 skilled 的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"She is skilled at repairing old machines.","zh":"她很擅長修理舊機器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum hired a skilled writer to tell the story clearly.","zh":"博物館聘請了一位寫作嫻熟的作家來清楚地講述這個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skilled","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b9981eadcb475278","term":"skilled","forms":["skilled","more skilled","most skilled"],"pos":"adj","zh":"需要專門技能的","explanation":"形容工作、職業或任務需要經過訓練的能力；重點從“人有本領”轉到“事情要求本領”。","examples":[{"en":"The factory is looking for skilled workers to operate the new equipment.","zh":"這家工廠正在尋找能夠操作新裝置的技術工人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repair requires skilled labor and specialized tools.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skilled","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6164dbb2e626033f79ad","word":"skillful","forms":["skillful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a071c8f02a64969","term":"skillful","forms":["skillful","more skillful","most skillful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有技巧的；熟練的","explanation":"形容人、動作或作品做得很有技巧，說明對某項活動掌握得好，能靈活而準確地完成。","examples":[{"en":"She is a skillful mechanic who can repair almost any engine.","zh":"她是一名技術熟練的機械師，幾乎什麼發動機都能修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The surgeon made a skillful movement and stopped the bleeding.","zh":"外科醫生做了一個嫻熟的動作，止住了出血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skillful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-769a27d2e089a703c66d","word":"skim","forms":["skim"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4dd256cffd525d1b","term":"skim","forms":["skim","skims","skimming","skimmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"貼面滑行","explanation":"指人或物沿著某個表面附近輕快、平穩地移動，像輕輕掠過而不是深入其中。","examples":[{"en":"A bird skimmed across the surface of the lake.","zh":"一隻鳥貼著湖面飛過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stone skimmed across the lake's surface.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-609f6e7c707fd03a","term":"skim","forms":["skim","skims","skimming","skimmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"快速略讀","explanation":"指快速閱讀或概括介紹，只取內容的大致輪廓，跳過許多細節；這是“視線掠過文字表面”的直接引申。","examples":[{"en":"Skim the article first, then read the important sections carefully.","zh":"先快速瀏覽這篇文章，再仔細閱讀重要部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She skimmed the report before the meeting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-676928331f2f2e7d","term":"skim","forms":["skim","skims","skimming","skimmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撇去液麵浮物","explanation":"指用勺子等工具貼著液麵，把浮沫、油脂或其他漂浮物撇走。","examples":[{"en":"Skim the foam from the top of the sauce.","zh":"把醬汁表面的泡沫撇掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She skimmed the fat that had risen overnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a0070d014bc41cb1fb0","word":"skin","forms":["skin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08a5474724dce610","term":"skin","forms":["skin","skins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皮膚","explanation":"指人或動物身體外面起保護作用的皮膚，是 skin 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The cold wind made my skin feel dry.","zh":"冷風吹得我的皮膚感覺很乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That scary story made my skin crawl.","zh":"那個恐怖故事讓我毛骨悚然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40c8115c8d91db20","term":"skin","forms":["skin","skins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"果皮","explanation":"指水果或植物外面的保護層，和人體皮膚一樣都是包在外面的“皮”。","examples":[{"en":"You can eat the apple skin, but wash it first.","zh":"蘋果皮可以吃，但要先洗乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The orange skin came off in one piece.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e7530f0815270ffacb3","word":"skinny","forms":["skinny"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a8c78d59bf1822a9","term":"skinny","forms":["skinny","skinnier","skinniest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"瘦得過頭","explanation":"形容人或身體非常瘦，常暗示缺少脂肪或肌肉，語氣通常不如“苗條”積極。","examples":[{"en":"He looked skinny after being sick for several weeks.","zh":"他生了幾周病後看起來瘦得厲害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That jacket makes me look skinny.","zh":"那件夾克讓我看起來很瘦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skinny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-42e93b9bb77d8a73e841","word":"skip","forms":["skip"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-67d2bd6949591b90","term":"skip","forms":["skip","skips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳躍動作","explanation":"指人或動物輕快地跳起、蹦跳的動作，正像把自己輕輕越過地面。","examples":[{"en":"She crossed the puddle with a little skip.","zh":"她輕輕一跳，越過了水窪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With a skip, she cleared the puddle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05fa5a0372a8f7ff","term":"skip","forms":["skip","skips","skipping","skipped","skippest","skippedst","skippeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"單腳交替跳著走","explanation":"人用兩隻腳交替輕快地跳著向前走，帶有活潑、輕鬆的感覺，就像把腳下的路一小段一小段地越過去。","examples":[{"en":"The children skipped along the path, singing loudly.","zh":"孩子們一邊大聲唱歌，一邊沿著小路蹦跳著向前走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She skipped from one end of the sidewalk to the other.","zh":"她從人行道這頭蹦跳著走到那頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d639358cc7f786f","term":"skip","forms":["skip","skips","skipping","skipped","skippest","skippedst","skippeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"略過；遺漏","explanation":"表示把連續內容中的某一部分、步驟或事件輕輕越過去，不處理、不閱讀或沒有經歷它；有時也表示某個正常動作短暫地漏掉，例如心跳漏了一下。","examples":[{"en":"I skipped the last chapter because I was running out of time.","zh":"因為時間快不夠了，我略過了最後一章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My heart skipped a beat when I heard the sudden noise.","zh":"聽到那聲突如其來的響動時，我的心跳漏了一拍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab161ea2b5578d6e","term":"skip","forms":["skip","skips","skipping","skipped","skippest","skippedst","skippeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不參加；缺席","explanation":"表示本來應該參加某堂課、會議或活動，卻決定不去，把這項安排越過去。","examples":[{"en":"I was tired, so I decided to skip the evening class.","zh":"我很累，所以決定不去上晚課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They skipped the meeting and sent their comments by email.","zh":"他們沒有參加會議，而是透過電子郵件發去了意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3abafce5bc548613ff47","word":"skirt","forms":["skirt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6848a15bd0d472fd","term":"skirt","forms":["skirt","skirts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裙子","explanation":"一種從腰部向下垂、覆蓋下半身的衣物，通常由女性或女孩穿著。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a blue skirt to the party.","zh":"她穿著一條藍裙子去參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This skirt is too long for me.","zh":"這條裙子對我來說太長了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skirt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-713db4d0156b6069","term":"skirt","forms":["skirt","skirts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邊緣；外圍","explanation":"指某個地方或事物的外緣、邊界，像裙子圍在身體外圍一樣。","examples":[{"en":"They built a cabin on the skirts of the forest.","zh":"他們在森林邊緣建了一間小屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small village lies on the skirts of the city.","zh":"一座小村莊坐落在城市邊緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skirt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8c1a64a5158bd82094f8","word":"skull","forms":["skull"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d51bc68b4aa8bd64","term":"skull","forms":["skull","skulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頭骨","explanation":"skull是構成頭部骨架的一組骨頭，包括包住腦部的顱骨、面部骨骼和下頜骨；日常說“頭骨”時通常把它看作一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed the skull of a young dinosaur.","zh":"博物館展出了一隻幼年恐龍的頭骨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The helmet protected his skull in the accident.","zh":"事故中，頭盔保護了他的頭骨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd942bdf24d7fdc6","term":"skull","forms":["skull","skulls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"死亡的象徵","explanation":"頭骨常與屍骨和死亡聯絡在一起，所以skull也可以不指一副真實的骨頭，而是代表死亡、危險或“死神之首”這一形象。","examples":[{"en":"A skull and crossbones warned visitors not to enter the room.","zh":"骷髏和交叉骨的圖案警告訪客不要進入房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The black flag carried a white skull as a sign of danger.","zh":"那面黑旗上有一個白色骷髏，表示危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skull","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05f514fae7ca5710f9e9","word":"sky","forms":["sky"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9699e66599911919","term":"sky","forms":["sky","skies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天空","explanation":"sky是我們從地面向上看到的廣闊空間，太陽、月亮、星星和雲都出現在其中。","examples":[{"en":"The stars filled the sky.","zh":"星星佈滿了天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bird flew across the sky.","zh":"一隻鳥飛過天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cbf4ba712fcb7ce0","term":"sky","forms":["sky","skies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某地或某時的天空","explanation":"加上顏色、地點或天氣等描述詞後，sky可以特指某個地方或某一時刻所看到的天空及其狀態。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the pink sky after sunset.","zh":"日落後，我們看著粉紅色的天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The desert sky blazed with stars that night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d41c3421332ffda7b796","word":"skyscraper","forms":["skyscraper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b34b08764cc33252","term":"skyscraper","forms":["skyscraper","skyscrapers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摩天大樓","explanation":"指樓層很多、遠高於周圍普通建築的大樓，通常是城市天際線中最醒目的高層建築。這個詞的核心畫面就是建築物彷彿一直向天空伸展。","examples":[{"en":"The new skyscraper dominates the city skyline.","zh":"這座新摩天大樓成為城市天際線中最醒目的建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took the elevator to the top of the skyscraper.","zh":"我們乘電梯到了這座摩天大樓的頂層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skyscraper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e6a0ab2937027144d3c","word":"slam","forms":["slam"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-00bbd5f1eedab710","term":"slam","forms":["slam","slams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈撞擊","explanation":"指突然發生的猛烈撞擊或重擊，重點在動作的力量和突然性，就像記憶鉤子裡帶著巨響的猛力動作。","examples":[{"en":"The heavy box hit the floor with a loud slam.","zh":"那個重箱子砰的一聲掉到了地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard a slam from the room upstairs.","zh":"我們聽見樓上房間傳來一聲猛烈的撞擊聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a7263c6faa3e432","term":"slam","forms":["slam","slams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賽季大滿貫","explanation":"指在一年或一個賽季中贏下全部，或幾乎全部指定的重要賽事，體現了記憶鉤子中“橫掃對手”的強力勝勢。","examples":[{"en":"The team completed a Grand Slam by winning every major event that season.","zh":"這支隊伍贏下了那個賽季的每項主要賽事，完成了大滿貫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is chasing a Grand Slam across the four biggest tournaments.","zh":"她正努力在四項最大型賽事中全部奪冠，以實現大滿貫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aacddcd183119a86","term":"slam","forms":["slam","slams","slamming","slammed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"砰地關上","explanation":"把門、蓋子等突然並用力地關上，發出撞擊聲；重點是“帶著巨響的猛力動作”。","examples":[{"en":"She slammed the door and walked away.","zh":"她砰地關上門，轉身走開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't slam the cabinet doors.","zh":"請不要把櫃門砰地關上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3240049d89d2d294","term":"slam","forms":["slam","slams","slamming","slammed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用力放下","explanation":"把某物猛地放到某處，通常伴隨很大的聲音；這種動作就像把東西帶著“猛”和“響”一起放下。","examples":[{"en":"He slammed the toolbox down on the floor.","zh":"他把工具箱砰地摔在地板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She slammed the book onto the desk.","zh":"她把書用力砸在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-007af6cfadfa92841983","word":"slang","forms":["slang"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e5c717e0eccec972","term":"slang","forms":["slang","slangs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"俚語；非正式說法","explanation":"指不屬於正式標準表達、常見於日常交談的詞語或說法，往往顯得輕鬆、幽默或隨意。它可以隨著年齡、地區和社群變化。","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers often use slang that older people do not understand.","zh":"青少年常用一些年長者聽不懂的俚語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article avoids slang and uses formal language instead.","zh":"這篇文章避免使用俚語，而改用正式語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-857ac77657edcfab","term":"slang","forms":["slang","slangs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行話；專業術語","explanation":"指某個職業、學科或活動圈子內部習慣使用的特殊詞彙。它不一定粗俗，重點是圈外人可能不容易理解。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor explained the medical slang in plain English.","zh":"醫生用通俗英語解釋了那些醫學行話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manual explains unfamiliar medical slang.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slang","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89405f34849adc70cd38","word":"slap","forms":["slap"],"officialPos":"n./v./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb37c55c88e20ec2","term":"slap","forms":["slap","slaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拍打；掌摑","explanation":"指用張開的手或寬平的東西用力打一下；輕鬆語境裡也可以是拍背等友好的動作，不一定帶有攻擊性。","examples":[{"en":"He gave me a friendly slap on the shoulder.","zh":"他友好地拍了拍我的肩膀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guard slapped the table to demand silence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d27994b3a6f8299","term":"slap","forms":["slap","slaps","slapping","slapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拍打；掌摑","explanation":"表示用手掌等重重打某人或某物一下，動作通常清楚而有衝擊力；物件可以是人，也可以是需要被拍擊的東西。","examples":[{"en":"She slapped his hand away from the hot pan.","zh":"她一巴掌把他的手從熱鍋旁拍開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He slapped the mosquito on his arm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-535fd5795c9c4705","term":"slap","forms":["slap","slaps","slapping","slapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"特別棒；很帶勁","explanation":"非正式俚語中表示音樂或歌曲非常好、很有衝擊力；這是從“拍擊有力”發展出的褒義。","examples":[{"en":"Their new track really slaps.","zh":"他們的新歌真的很帶勁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This song slaps; turn it up!","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-939d59d1285efa522f39","word":"slash","forms":["slash"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0808a0199acaa94","term":"slash","forms":["slash","slashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揮砍；劈砍動作","explanation":"指用刀、劍等快速劃過或砍下的一下動作，核心就是留下斜著劃開的力量感。","examples":[{"en":"A slash of the knife cut through the rope.","zh":"刀一揮就割斷了繩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guard blocked a slash from the attacker.","zh":"衛兵擋住了襲擊者的一記揮砍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-100b3eeeb36df710","term":"slash","forms":["slash","slashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大幅削減","explanation":"把金額、預算或數量像用刀砍掉一樣大幅減少，常用於抽象物件。","examples":[{"en":"The company announced a sharp slash in its advertising budget.","zh":"公司宣佈大幅削減廣告預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A slash in ticket prices brought more people to the theater.","zh":"票價大幅下調後，更多人來到劇院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cfa757447f59556","term":"slash","forms":["slash","slashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"切痕；砍傷","explanation":"指被刀、玻璃等劃出的長而窄的傷痕，像一道留在皮膚上的斜線。","examples":[{"en":"He had a deep slash across his cheek.","zh":"他的臉頰上有一道很深的劃傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The broken glass left a slash on her arm.","zh":"碎玻璃在她手臂上劃出了一道傷口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb286f82ad7cfc24","term":"slash","forms":["slash","slashes","slashing","slashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揮砍；砍切","explanation":"用刀、劍或類似物快速地砍、劃，動作像在空中或物體上畫出一道斜線。","examples":[{"en":"The attacker slashed at the door with a knife.","zh":"襲擊者拿刀猛砍那扇門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She slashed through the net and escaped.","zh":"她割破了網，逃了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2a5089b88863996","term":"slash","forms":["slash","slashes","slashing","slashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"大幅削減","explanation":"把價格、預算、數量等像用刀砍掉一樣大幅降低。","examples":[{"en":"The store slashed prices before the holiday.","zh":"商店在節日前大幅降價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency slashed its travel budget by a third.","zh":"該機構把差旅預算削減了三分之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-533f8cc06a1157bb0b9f","word":"slaughter","forms":["slaughter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2077ba8347bb6e70","term":"slaughter","forms":["slaughter","slaughters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"屠宰動物","explanation":"slaughter 指為了食物等目的集中殺死動物，重點是屠宰過程或這種行為本身。","examples":[{"en":"The animals were sent to the slaughterhouse before dawn.","zh":"這些動物在黎明前被送進了屠宰場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law aims to reduce the slaughter of wild animals.","zh":"這項法律旨在減少對野生動物的屠殺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slaughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10969f02ff1bb022","term":"slaughter","forms":["slaughter","slaughters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大規模屠殺","explanation":"slaughter 指大批殺死人，通常暗示戰爭、襲擊或其他極其慘烈的場面，常譯為“大屠殺”或“屠殺”。","examples":[{"en":"The attack led to the slaughter of hundreds of civilians.","zh":"這次襲擊導致數百名平民慘遭屠殺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Survivors described the scene as a terrible slaughter.","zh":"倖存者把現場描述成一場可怕的大屠殺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slaughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-098670c84093883b","term":"slaughter","forms":["slaughter","slaughters","slaughtering","slaughtered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"屠宰動物","explanation":"作動詞時，slaughter 指為了食物等目的屠宰動物，突出集中、成批或職業性的殺戮過程。","examples":[{"en":"The workers slaughtered the cattle and prepared the meat for market.","zh":"工人屠宰了牛，並把肉準備好拿到市場上出售。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Millions of chickens are slaughtered for food every year.","zh":"每年有數百萬只雞被屠宰供人食用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slaughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f873b1340e9e0e5","term":"slaughter","forms":["slaughter","slaughters","slaughtering","slaughtered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"大規模殺人","explanation":"slaughter 作動詞可表示大規模、殘酷地殺死人，常用於戰爭、襲擊或歷史敘述。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers slaughtered the villagers before retreating.","zh":"士兵們在撤退前屠殺了村民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thousands were slaughtered during the invasion.","zh":"入侵期間有數千人慘遭屠殺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slaughter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-183936b010c67d892541","word":"slave","forms":["slave"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6de4d9c7d0d94ee3","term":"slave","forms":["slave","slaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"奴隸","explanation":"指被另一個人當作財產佔有、被迫勞動，並且身體、生活和勞動都受對方控制的人。這是該詞最基本、最重要的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The museum explains how enslaved people were forced to work on the plantation.","zh":"這座博物館講解了被奴役的人如何被迫在種植園勞動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law was meant to protect slaves from being sold.","zh":"這項法律旨在保護奴隸不被販賣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-777f8e8307fe5818","term":"slave","forms":["slave","slaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受某物支配的人","explanation":"指一個人無法抵抗某種力量，完全受慾望、習慣或野心支配，好像成了它的奴隸。","examples":[{"en":"He became a slave to his ambition and neglected his family.","zh":"他成了野心的奴隸，忽視了自己的家人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a slave to routine and hates sudden changes.","zh":"她被日常規律牢牢束縛，討厭突然的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5778592072e93a9a160","word":"slavery","forms":["slavery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31b01e1eb4fcf9b4","term":"slavery","forms":["slavery","slaveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"奴隸制","explanation":"指把人當作財產來佔有，並以強迫勞動為主要目的的制度或社會實踐。這是 slavery 最核心、最常見的歷史和社會意義。","examples":[{"en":"Slavery was abolished in this country more than a century ago.","zh":"這個國家在一個多世紀前廢除了奴隸制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum tells the stories of people who fought against slavery.","zh":"這座博物館講述了那些反抗奴隸制的人們的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slavery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9fef1c1ada3250b","term":"slavery","forms":["slavery","slaveries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"被迫勞動","explanation":"泛指人在沒有真正自由選擇的情況下被迫工作，不一定特指某個正式的奴隸制社會。它把核心畫面從一種制度擴充套件到各種強迫勞動情形。","examples":[{"en":"The report found evidence of slavery on several farms.","zh":"這份報告發現了幾家農場存在強迫勞動的證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captives were sold into slavery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slavery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7837b0277c547e94ac94","word":"slay","forms":["slay"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e54582e7efc8729","term":"slay","forms":["slay","slays","slaying","slew","slayed","slain","yslain"],"pos":"verb","zh":"表現驚豔","explanation":"表示某人的表現、造型或作品好到令人震撼，彷彿用精彩表現把全場“擊倒”。這是現代網路和流行文化中最值得優先掌握的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"You slay in that jacket.","zh":"你穿那件夾克簡直太驚豔了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She slayed at the audition.","zh":"她在試鏡中表現得特別出色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0afa5bb5d5f1787945e5","word":"sleep","forms":["sleep"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc674e6b5313fbbc","term":"sleep","forms":["sleep","sleeps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"睡眠","explanation":"sleep 指人在清醒與活動之間進入的休息狀態，通常強調睡眠本身，而不是某一次具體的睡覺。","examples":[{"en":"I really need more sleep tonight.","zh":"今晚我真的需要多睡一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Lack of sleep makes it hard to concentrate.","zh":"睡眠不足會讓人難以集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sleep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf1d47ff655e60b1","term":"sleep","forms":["sleep","sleeps","sleeping","slept","sleepest","sleptst","sleptest","sleepeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"睡覺","explanation":"sleep 作動詞時表示處於睡眠狀態，是最基本的“睡覺”。它通常描述人或動物自己進入睡眠，不需要賓語。","examples":[{"en":"You should sleep eight hours a day.","zh":"你每天應該睡八個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby slept through the storm.","zh":"嬰兒安穩地睡過了暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sleep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e74ca13b4c0a61dcf774","word":"sleepy","forms":["sleepy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09498af5491bbb45","term":"sleepy","forms":["sleepy","sleepier","sleepiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"睏倦的；想睡的","explanation":"指人感到疲倦併產生睡意，最常見的意思是“困了、想睡覺”。它說的是當下的狀態，不表示這個人已經睡著。","examples":[{"en":"I always feel sleepy after a heavy lunch.","zh":"我吃完豐盛的午飯後總是覺得困。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby is sleepy but refuses to go to bed.","zh":"寶寶困了，卻不肯上床睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sleepy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-351ee0819ea79aba","term":"sleepy","forms":["sleepy","sleepier","sleepiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯出睏倦的","explanation":"指某人的話、表情或動作帶著睡意，讓人看出對方疲倦、反應不夠精神。","examples":[{"en":"He answered in a sleepy voice.","zh":"他用睏倦的聲音回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She answered with a sleepy smile and a yawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sleepy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-18159f6fa757e618ab6e","word":"sleeve","forms":["sleeve"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-80d98c7e40e71248","term":"sleeve","forms":["sleeve","sleeves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"袖子","explanation":"衣服上套住手臂的部分，就是袖子；這是sleeve最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The sleeves on my coat are too long.","zh":"我外套的袖子太長了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She rolled up her sleeves and started cooking.","zh":"她捲起袖子開始做飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sleeve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a376a58719fc7b4a","term":"sleeve","forms":["sleeve","sleeves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護套；襯套","explanation":"指套在機器零件或其他物體外面、用來保護或使其貼合的管狀套子，是“袖子”這一外部套筒形象的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"Put a protective sleeve over the cable before installing it.","zh":"安裝電纜前，先在外面套上保護套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This shaft needs a metal sleeve to fit the bearing.","zh":"這根軸需要一個金屬襯套才能與軸承貼合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sleeve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1557604f30f9988a36f","word":"slender","forms":["slender"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77917f2e791761b5","term":"slender","forms":["slender","slenderer","more slender","slenderest","most slender"],"pos":"adj","zh":"細長的；纖細的","explanation":"形容物體或人的外形細而長、線條纖細，重點是“細長”的整體形象，而不只是尺寸小。","examples":[{"en":"She has slender fingers and a graceful way of playing the piano.","zh":"她的手指纖細，彈鋼琴的姿勢很優雅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A slender branch reached across the window.","zh":"一根細長的樹枝伸到了窗前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e506f8725b38790","term":"slender","forms":["slender","slenderer","more slender","slenderest","most slender"],"pos":"adj","zh":"微薄的；不足的","explanation":"把“細”的形象引申到抽象事物上，表示錢、資源、機會或依據等少得不夠，帶有“薄弱、有限”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"With only a slender chance of success, they decided not to continue.","zh":"成功的希望十分渺茫，他們決定不再繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They survived on a slender income from odd jobs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-03fdb065d956f3fb9ccd","word":"slice","forms":["slice"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d68d4e10bb22a7d1","term":"slice","forms":["slice","slices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薄而寬的一片","explanation":"指形狀薄而寬的一片，重點是它像從較大物體上切下來的平面部分；它也可以只是某個物體呈現出的薄片狀部分。","examples":[{"en":"A slice of light showed through the opening in the roof.","zh":"一片光線從屋頂的開口處照了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut a thin slice of smoked salmon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e390bca3228be8f4","term":"slice","forms":["slice","slices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"切下的薄片","explanation":"指從麵包、乳酪、肉等食物或其他物體上切下來的薄而寬的一片，這是日常生活中最典型的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could you put two slices of cheese in the sandwich?","zh":"你能在三明治裡放兩片乳酪嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut the tomato into thin slices.","zh":"她把番茄切成了薄片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb0bccb36e4a4c75","term":"slice","forms":["slice","slices","slicing","sliced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"切成片","explanation":"指把食物或其他東西切成薄而寬的片，是名詞“薄片”義對應的最常見動作。","examples":[{"en":"Slice the cucumber thinly and add it to the salad.","zh":"把黃瓜切成薄片，加到沙拉里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sliced the loaf for the guests.","zh":"她把麵包切成片給客人吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-158f444739a0baed","term":"slice","forms":["slice","slices","slicing","sliced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用刃劃切","explanation":"指用刀刃等鋒利邊緣，以向後或向前拖拉的動作切過某物或某人的身體；重點是切割動作，不一定切成整齊的薄片。","examples":[{"en":"The sharp edge sliced through the rope.","zh":"鋒利的邊緣一下子割斷了繩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sliced his finger while opening the package.","zh":"他拆包裹時劃傷了手指。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8a7e24e95497806eafb","word":"slide","forms":["slide"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-445abc4d55d10cf5","term":"slide","forms":["slide","slides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑梯","explanation":"供孩子爬上去再滑下來的遊樂設施；可以把它想成沿著表面順滑地過去。","examples":[{"en":"The children raced to the slide as soon as the playground opened.","zh":"遊樂場一開放，孩子們就跑向了滑梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children queued for the playground slide.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a91663a1b8e738f0","term":"slide","forms":["slide","slides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簡報頁面","explanation":"指簡報中的一頁，內容可以包括文字、圖片、圖表或影片；它像頁面一樣一頁頁切換過去。","examples":[{"en":"I need to add one more slide to my presentation.","zh":"我還需要在簡報中再加一頁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final slide summarizes the team's findings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-545c80c56126a5fe","term":"slide","forms":["slide","slides","sliding","slid","slidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使沿表面滑動","explanation":"把某物貼著一個表面順滑地推、拉或帶過去，重點是物體在接觸表面的狀態下移動。","examples":[{"en":"She slid the box across the floor.","zh":"她把箱子沿著地板滑了過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He slid the note under the door.","zh":"他把紙條從門下滑了進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d5a672753533b3e","term":"slide","forms":["slide","slides","sliding","slid","slidden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在表面上滑行","explanation":"人、車輛或其他物體由於表面很光滑或摩擦力很小，沿著表面自行滑動或滑行。","examples":[{"en":"The car slid on the wet road.","zh":"汽車在溼滑的路面上打滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children slid across the frozen pond.","zh":"孩子們滑過了結冰的池塘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c7dad260e0b1d0f59ef","word":"slight","forms":["slight"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a95932bfa7b710a6","term":"slight","forms":["slight","slighter","slightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"輕微的；少量的","explanation":"表示數量、程度或影響很小，但仍然確實存在。它可以形容變化、疼痛、損傷、差異等，是現代英語中最常見的義項。","examples":[{"en":"There was a slight change in his voice.","zh":"他的聲音有一點變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt a slight pain in her shoulder.","zh":"她感到肩膀有輕微的疼痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a98f94394bf3bc4","term":"slight","forms":["slight","slights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冷落；怠慢","explanation":"a slight 是別人故意不重視你、忽略你或以無禮方式對待你的行為，因此常會讓人感到受冒犯。","examples":[{"en":"She took his failure to reply as a slight.","zh":"她把他沒有回覆看作一種怠慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He interpreted the missing invitation as a deliberate slight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-599569a169c732cc","term":"slight","forms":["slight","slights","slighting","slighted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕視；不把……當回事","explanation":"表示因為覺得某人某事不重要，就沒有給予應有的注意或重視；這裡的“輕”是把對方的分量看低。","examples":[{"en":"We should not slight the work of the volunteers.","zh":"我們不應輕視志願者所做的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt that his advice had been slighted.","zh":"他覺得自己的建議沒有受到重視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87fe9c02cf8e4bfe","term":"slight","forms":["slight","slights","slighting","slighted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"怠慢；冷落","explanation":"表示以無禮、帶偏見或冷淡的方式忽略某人，使對方感到沒有被公平對待；這是“把人看得沒有分量”更強烈的一步。","examples":[{"en":"She felt slighted when her invitation was ignored.","zh":"她的邀請被忽視後，覺得受到了冷落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The host slighted our team by introducing everyone except us.","zh":"主人介紹了所有人，唯獨沒有介紹我們隊，讓我們受到了怠慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebe4136fc8889cbf5560","word":"slim","forms":["slim"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d226b3aa91974889","term":"slim","forms":["slim","slimmer","slimmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"苗條的；纖細的","explanation":"形容人的身材或體態細而勻稱，通常含有健康、好看的正面意味。這是 slim 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She stays slim by walking to work every day.","zh":"她每天步行上班，所以一直保持著苗條的身材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor looked slim and elegant in the black suit.","zh":"那位演員穿黑色西裝時顯得苗條而優雅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e19b3f06106ef18","term":"slim","forms":["slim","slimmer","slimmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很小的；渺茫的","explanation":"表示數量、可能性或機會少得幾乎可以忽略，像一條變得很細的線。它尤其常用於表示某事成功的希望不大。","examples":[{"en":"There is only a slim chance that the train will arrive on time.","zh":"這列火車準時到達的可能性很小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our chances of finding the lost ring are slim.","zh":"我們找到丟失戒指的希望很渺茫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c1480e67eee52c17293","word":"slip","forms":["slip"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7fa6f3b1055c3dfe","term":"slip","forms":["slip","slips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滑倒；失足","explanation":"指滑動或失去平衡的一次動作，通常是腳下不穩而差點摔倒或真的摔倒；畫面就是身體從原位滑了出去。","examples":[{"en":"I had a slip on the wet floor and hurt my knee.","zh":"我在溼地板上滑了一跤，膝蓋受傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A slip on the wet steps left him bruised.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b19a0ad89ad49268","term":"slip","forms":["slip","slips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小錯誤；失誤","explanation":"指不小心犯下的一個小錯誤，像注意力從原來的位置悄悄滑開了一下，常常不是故意的。","examples":[{"en":"It was just a slip of the tongue; I did not mean to reveal the surprise.","zh":"那只是一次口誤，我不是故意要洩露這個驚喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One small slip in the address delayed the package.","zh":"地址上的一個小錯誤讓包裹延誤了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-260e2611c46464e3","term":"slip","forms":["slip","slips","slipping","slipped","slipt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打滑；滑倒","explanation":"指腳或車輛在溼滑、光滑的表面上失去抓地力而滑動，身體彷彿從原位悄悄滑了出去。","examples":[{"en":"I slipped on the wet floor but caught the table.","zh":"我在溼地板上滑了一下，但抓住了桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful on the icy steps; you could slip.","zh":"走結冰的臺階要小心，你可能會滑倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e009050e6ca4b27e","term":"slip","forms":["slip","slips","slipping","slipped","slipt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"無意洩密","explanation":"指說話時不小心把原本想保密的資訊說了出來，秘密彷彿從嘴邊滑了出去。","examples":[{"en":"She slipped and revealed where the surprise party would be held.","zh":"她一不小心說出了驚喜派對要在哪裡舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He let slip that the company was planning a merger.","zh":"他無意中透露了公司正在籌劃合併。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-637a997825390d339aac","word":"slipper(s)","forms":["slipper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c870648c679b3dab","term":"slipper","forms":["slipper","slippers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"易穿脫的軟鞋","explanation":"指低幫、柔軟、可以直接套上或脫下的鞋，是這個詞最基本的鞋類概念；室內拖鞋是其中最常見的一類。","examples":[{"en":"I left my slippers by the door.","zh":"我把拖鞋放在門邊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He slipped his cold feet into warm slippers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slipper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb3aaf3759bbed1f","term":"slipper","forms":["slipper","slippers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"室內拖鞋","explanation":"指在家裡或臥室穿的軟底鞋，通常起床後套上，或在室內走動時穿著。","examples":[{"en":"She put on her slippers before walking downstairs.","zh":"她穿上拖鞋後才下樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy hid my slipper beneath the sofa.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slipper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-971fa55cfccf2558e609","word":"slippery","forms":["slippery"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21d2ecc2065ee9b5","term":"slippery","forms":["slippery","slipperier","more slippery","slipperiest","most slippery"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易打滑的","explanation":"形容表面摩擦力小，手抓不牢，腳踩上去也容易滑倒；油、水等液體覆蓋在表面上時尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful—the kitchen floor is slippery.","zh":"小心，廚房地板很滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wet soap is slippery and hard to hold.","zh":"溼肥皂滑溜溜的，很難拿穩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slippery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1ec57018a0ce871","term":"slippery","forms":["slippery","slipperier","more slippery","slipperiest","most slippery"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難以捉摸的","explanation":"把“抓不住”的感覺用於人或說法，表示對方迴避明確回答、立場不固定，或總讓人難以確定其真實意圖。","examples":[{"en":"The witness was slippery when reporters asked about the missing money.","zh":"記者問到那筆失蹤的錢時，證人總是含糊其辭、避而不答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The slippery concept resisted a simple definition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slippery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c964454ae1e582ef74b6","word":"slogan","forms":["slogan"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49a3cbe5bedb8eaa","term":"slogan","forms":["slogan","slogans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口號；格言式標語","explanation":"指某個人、團體、政治運動或政黨的簡短固定話語，用來表達立場、原則或共同目標。它像一聲讓成員記住“我們相信什麼”的號召，因此往往簡潔、有力度、容易重複。","examples":[{"en":"“Protect our rivers” became the campaign's slogan.","zh":"“保護我們的河流”成了這場運動的口號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The party's slogan appealed to voters who wanted change.","zh":"這個政黨的口號打動了那些希望改變的選民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slogan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90d4ab1d90d8c9ec","term":"slogan","forms":["slogan","slogans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣告宣傳語","explanation":"指與某種商品、服務或品牌聯絡在一起的簡短廣告語。它把複雜的產品資訊壓縮成一句容易記住的話，讓消費者一聽就想到該品牌。","examples":[{"en":"The company created a catchy slogan for its new delivery service.","zh":"這家公司為新的配送服務創作了一句朗朗上口的宣傳語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The advertising slogan appeared on every bus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slogan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb1acd44962209a65826","word":"slope","forms":["slope"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d958de9a920e0ae7","term":"slope","forms":["slope","slopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斜坡","explanation":"指一塊均勻向上或向下延伸的地面，例如道路旁的小坡或通往某處的斜坡。","examples":[{"en":"We climbed a gentle slope to reach the cabin.","zh":"我們爬上一段平緩的斜坡，到達了小屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children rolled their balls down the slope.","zh":"孩子們把球滾下斜坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd4a999762f89ae1","term":"slope","forms":["slope","slopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傾斜度；坡度","explanation":"指表面向上或向下傾斜的程度；slope 越大，通常表示斜得越明顯或越陡。","examples":[{"en":"The road has a very steep slope near the bridge.","zh":"橋附近的道路坡度很陡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gentle slope lets rainwater run away slowly.","zh":"平緩的坡度讓雨水慢慢流走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c2cd97763a54eacfc6d","word":"sloppy","forms":["sloppy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2295eefee77cb27a","term":"sloppy","forms":["sloppy","sloppier","sloppiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"溼黏髒汙的","explanation":"指被稀泥、髒水等弄得溼黏、髒亂，或本身就是這種狀態；畫面就是東西拖著溼泥到處留下痕跡。","examples":[{"en":"The dog left sloppy footprints all over the clean floor.","zh":"那隻狗把溼黏的腳印踩得乾淨地板到處都是。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The path became a sloppy mess after the rain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sloppy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8b6b14d031e7c35","term":"sloppy","forms":["sloppy","sloppier","sloppiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"馬虎凌亂的","explanation":"形容做事、工作或成品沒有認真整理和處理，顯得粗糙、馬虎；這裡是把“溼泥般沒有收拾好”的感覺引申到做事方式上。","examples":[{"en":"The report was sloppy and contained several avoidable errors.","zh":"這份報告寫得很馬虎，裡面有幾處本來可以避免的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sloppy accounting made the missing money difficult to trace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sloppy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6558838331b742a6f1d5","word":"slot","forms":["slot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-958093a57882ee29","term":"slot","forms":["slot","slots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狹槽；插口","explanation":"指狹窄的凹槽、孔或開口，通常用來讓相應形狀的東西插入、滑入或固定進去。這是 slot 最具體、最基礎的形象。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the ticket into the slot beside the door.","zh":"請把票放進門旁邊的插槽裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The key fits neatly into the slot.","zh":"這把鑰匙正好插入這個槽口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0acdee455435d41","term":"slot","forms":["slot","slots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時間段；安排位置","explanation":"指日程表或一連串安排中的一段固定時間，也可以指順序中留給某人的位置。它是把“頁面或裝置上的槽位”借來表示“時間槽位”。","examples":[{"en":"Could we find a morning slot for the meeting?","zh":"我們能不能找一個上午的時間段開會？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The show has a regular evening slot on the channel.","zh":"這個節目在該頻道有固定的晚間時段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b3fd4a57f80e10fe","term":"slot","forms":["slot","slots","slotting","slotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"插入槽中","explanation":"指把硬幣或其他物體放進狹窄的槽口中，是名詞“槽、插口”對應的直接動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Slot the card into the reader and wait for the light.","zh":"把卡插入讀卡器，然後等待指示燈亮起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He slotted a coin into the machine.","zh":"他把一枚硬幣投入機器的投幣口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b9e1ca1249d9e33","term":"slot","forms":["slot","slots","slotting","slotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安排進時段或順序","explanation":"指把某人、某事安排進日程或順序中預留的空位，就像把物體插進一個合適的槽位。","examples":[{"en":"I can slot you in for a short call tomorrow afternoon.","zh":"我可以把你安排進明天下午的一個短時通話時段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor slotted the article into next week's issue.","zh":"編輯把這篇文章安排進了下週的那一期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e0cf7bd1dfa3831788b","word":"slow","forms":["slow"],"officialPos":"adj./v./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4c96682db313ccc","term":"slow","forms":["slow","slower","slowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"速度慢的","explanation":"指移動、執行或做某件事的速度低，需要較長時間才能完成。它是 slow 最基本的意思，像一輛低速行駛的車。","examples":[{"en":"The old train is slow, but it is comfortable.","zh":"這列舊火車速度很慢，但很舒適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My computer is too slow to open the file.","zh":"我的電腦太慢，打不開這個檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c420d7c28183eb4","term":"slow","forms":["slow","slower","slowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"進展緩慢的","explanation":"指變化、發展或事情發生得不快，過程被拉長到較長時間，而不是短時間內完成。","examples":[{"en":"The recovery has been slow but steady.","zh":"恢復過程一直很慢，但很穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town is experiencing slow growth.","zh":"這個城鎮正在經歷緩慢的增長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-430ee84a87807aec","term":"slow","forms":["slow","slower","slowest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"慢慢地","explanation":"表示動作以低速度進行，與“速度慢的”這一核心意思相同，只是此時修飾動作而不是名詞。","examples":[{"en":"Go slow on the icy road.","zh":"在結冰的路上慢點開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The elevator is running slow today.","zh":"電梯今天執行得很慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8755ea3f5459b8c4","term":"slow","forms":["slow","slows","slowing","slowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變慢","explanation":"指主動降低某物移動、執行或進行的速度，讓它不再那麼快。","examples":[{"en":"The driver slowed the car before the turn.","zh":"司機在轉彎前讓車減速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to slow the process down.","zh":"我們需要讓這個過程慢下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b162a31f44a0cc5","term":"slow","forms":["slow","slows","slowing","slowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變慢","explanation":"指人、車輛、機器或自然過程自身逐漸降低速度，不強調有人主動讓它變慢。","examples":[{"en":"The bus slowed as it approached the station.","zh":"公共汽車接近車站時慢了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind slowly slowed after sunset.","zh":"日落後，風漸漸減弱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9be3f7ab722e9029201","word":"slum","forms":["slum"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1f96b47631717e9d","term":"slum","forms":["slum","slums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貧民區；棚戶區","explanation":"指城市中房屋破敗、生活條件差、許多貧困人口居住的地區。這裡的核心畫面就是一片擁擠、破舊的居住區。","examples":[{"en":"Many families still live in the slums on the edge of the city.","zh":"許多家庭仍然住在城市邊緣的貧民區裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity is building clean water systems in a local slum.","zh":"這家慈善機構正在當地一個貧民區修建清潔供水系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65eb29297196602e","term":"slum","forms":["slum","slums","slumming","slummed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"到貧困地區遊逛","explanation":"指一個人到社會地位或生活條件低於自己的地區去看看、遊逛，和“走進那片破敗角落”的記憶畫面相連。這個詞有時暗示把貧困地區當成新奇體驗，因此不只是中性的“參觀”。","examples":[{"en":"They went slumming in the old district for an afternoon.","zh":"他們去老城區那個貧困地區遊逛了一個下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The writer was criticized for slumming in poor neighborhoods.","zh":"這位作家因到貧困社群獵奇而受到批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6b6a3f041cad044bebf","word":"slump","forms":["slump"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-519b0722d456cc6a","term":"slump","forms":["slump","slumps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"癱塌；低迷狀態","explanation":"指人沉重而無力地塌下去，或指這種姿勢；也可指一段持續不振、表現不佳的時期。它把“身體失去支撐而下沉”的畫面延伸到了工作、成績等狀態上。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, he sat in a slump by the door.","zh":"長途徒步後，他無力地塌坐在門邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team has been in a slump since the start of the season.","zh":"這個隊從賽季開始以來一直狀態低迷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e65a62413429deaf","term":"slump","forms":["slump","slumps","slumping","slumped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"無力地塌下","explanation":"指人因疲憊、震驚或無力而沉重地倒坐或塌下，動作通常顯得突然且缺乏控制。這個動作正是“失去支撐後向下沉”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She slumped down onto the bench after the exam.","zh":"考試後，她無力地塌坐到長椅上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He slumped in his chair and closed his eyes.","zh":"他鬆垮地陷在椅子裡，閉上了眼睛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c916f72837d7229a","term":"slump","forms":["slump","slumps","slumping","slumped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"活動或表現下滑","explanation":"指活動量、價格、銷售或表現明顯下降，進入低迷狀態。它把人的“往下塌”直接用於抽象事物，強調由較好狀態滑向較差狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Tourism slumped after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，旅遊業陷入低迷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sales slumped after the holiday season.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slump","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7be33532b3e9129dd1db","word":"sly","forms":["sly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0efbbdfa8356b074","term":"sly","forms":["sly","slier","slyer","sliest","slyest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"狡猾的；暗中使壞的","explanation":"形容一個人或動物很會暗中算計、耍小聰明，不輕易讓別人看出真實意圖，通常帶有不太信任或不太讚許的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The sly fox waited until the farmer turned away.","zh":"那隻狡猾的狐狸一直等到農夫轉過身去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a sly smile and hid the key behind her back.","zh":"她狡黠地朝我一笑，把鑰匙藏到了身後。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81db8ebbbbc69c6c6ad4","word":"small","forms":["small"],"officialPos":"adj./n./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39f8a110f80f1622","term":"small","forms":["small","smaller","smallest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"小的；少量的","explanation":"指尺寸不大、數量不多，或重要性、影響不大，是 small 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We live in a small apartment near the station.","zh":"我們住在車站附近的一套小公寓裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a small number of students missed the class.","zh":"只有少數學生沒來上課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/small","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09d872830d1854b2","term":"small","forms":["small","smalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小號規格","explanation":"指商品按大小劃分時的“小號”這一規格，而不是某一件具體商品。","examples":[{"en":"Do you have this jacket in small?","zh":"這件夾克有小號嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try a small; this medium is too loose.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/small","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-330331473a8f2982","term":"small","forms":["small","smalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小號商品","explanation":"指一件標為小號的商品，常見於點餐、購物或說明尺寸的場合。","examples":[{"en":"Two smalls and one large, please.","zh":"請來兩份小號的和一份大號的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medium is too loose; have you got a small?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/small","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-544e2d6145f6ea1d858b","word":"smart","forms":["smart"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4881a767d703c86","term":"smart","forms":["smart","smarter","smartest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聰明機靈","explanation":"形容人反應快、會處理事情，表現出實際的聰明和社交機靈。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is smart enough to solve the problem on her own.","zh":"瑪雅很聰明，足以自己解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was smart of you to leave early.","zh":"你早點離開是個明智的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e24938663336b251","term":"smart","forms":["smart","smarter","smartest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"造成刺痛的","explanation":"形容某種觸感或事物像針一樣刺人，能造成尖銳、短促的身體疼痛，也可用於比喻傷人的話。","examples":[{"en":"The salt made the cut smart.","zh":"鹽讓傷口感到刺痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her smart words stayed with him all day.","zh":"她那些刺人的話讓他難受了一整天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smart","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1606d14f9309c94a87b","word":"smash","forms":["smash"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a9faf38caf34d7fa","term":"smash","forms":["smash","smashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈撞擊聲；撞擊","explanation":"指猛烈撞擊時發出的聲音，或這種猛烈的碰撞本身；重點是“砰的一撞”。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a loud smash from the kitchen.","zh":"我聽見廚房裡傳來一聲巨響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smash of the falling glass woke everyone up.","zh":"玻璃掉落時的撞擊聲把所有人都吵醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-305988c9c88b3692","term":"smash","forms":["smash","smashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大獲成功的事物","explanation":"指音樂、節目、食品或時尚等非常成功、非常受歡迎的東西，彷彿它猛烈地“擊中”了大眾。","examples":[{"en":"Her first album was a smash with teenagers.","zh":"她的第一張專輯在青少年中大獲成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unexpected smash ran in theaters for months.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-faf1790a5622ba0d","term":"smash","forms":["smash","smashes","smashing","smashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猛力打碎","explanation":"用很大的力量把易碎物品打破或打成碎片，是 smash 最直接的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The ball smashed the window.","zh":"球把窗戶砸碎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He smashed the old vase to pieces.","zh":"他把那個舊花瓶砸得粉碎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcbfb246f3e5843d","term":"smash","forms":["smash","smashes","smashing","smashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猛烈擊打","explanation":"用極大的力量擊打某人或某物，不一定強調把它打碎；核心仍是猛烈的衝擊。","examples":[{"en":"He smashed the ball into the wall.","zh":"他把球狠狠地砸向牆壁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The waves smashed the boat against the rocks.","zh":"海浪把船猛地撞在礁石上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-012783dea27d3573","term":"smash","forms":["smash","smashes","smashing","smashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓倒性擊敗","explanation":"在比賽或競爭中大比分、以壓倒性的優勢擊敗對手，像把對方徹底撞倒一樣。","examples":[{"en":"Our team smashed the champions 5–0.","zh":"我們隊以五比零大勝衛冕冠軍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The home team smashed their rivals six-nil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8fca2d48e1ee96c1193a","word":"smell","forms":["smell"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee5f3f47502f5167","term":"smell","forms":["smell","smells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"氣味","explanation":"smell 可以指空氣中被鼻子察覺到的氣味，不論這種氣味好聞、難聞還是沒有明顯褒貶。","examples":[{"en":"I love the smell of fresh bread.","zh":"我喜歡新鮮麵包的香味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a strange smell in the kitchen.","zh":"廚房裡有一股奇怪的氣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4288e2fce5a46e35","term":"smell","forms":["smell","smells","smelling","smelled","smelt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聞到","explanation":"smell 表示用鼻子察覺到某種氣味，重點在“聞到了什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"I can smell fresh bread.","zh":"我聞得到新鮮麵包的香味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She smelled smoke and opened the window.","zh":"她聞到煙味，於是開啟了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-93d56c539721a12c","term":"smell","forms":["smell","smells","smelling","smelled","smelt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聞起來","explanation":"smell 可以說明某物散發出怎樣的氣味，重點是“它聞起來是什麼樣”。","examples":[{"en":"The roses smell lovely.","zh":"這些玫瑰聞起來很香。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The milk smells sour.","zh":"牛奶聞起來酸了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa1eadc4c69956674126","word":"smile","forms":["smile"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ce25add2af16483","term":"smile","forms":["smile","smiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"笑容；微笑","explanation":"指嘴角等面部肌肉形成的笑容，通常表達開心、愉快、友好，也可能只是禮貌或緊張時的表情。","examples":[{"en":"Her warm smile made everyone feel welcome.","zh":"她溫暖的笑容讓每個人都感到受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He answered the question with a nervous smile.","zh":"他帶著緊張的笑容回答了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa3a79666149f4dc","term":"smile","forms":["smile","smiles","smiling","smiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"微笑；臉上帶著笑容","explanation":"指臉上出現笑容這一動作或狀態，重點是“有笑容”，不一定強調這個笑容傳達了什麼具體意思。","examples":[{"en":"She smiled at me when I entered the room.","zh":"我走進房間時，她朝我微笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to smile for the photograph.","zh":"拍照時儘量微笑一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d30951eff3d933f","term":"smile","forms":["smile","smiles","smiling","smiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"以微笑表達情感","explanation":"指用微笑傳達開心、喜愛、親切或善意；相比 s1，它更強調微笑所傳遞的情感和人際態度。","examples":[{"en":"The child smiled with delight when she saw the puppy.","zh":"孩子看到小狗時高興地笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He smiled kindly to reassure his nervous friend.","zh":"他親切地微笑著，讓緊張的朋友安心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6247a5ccc27edc5161f4","word":"smog","forms":["smog"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-061f6dced3fb033b","term":"smog","forms":["smog","smogs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煙霧；霧霾","explanation":"指煙塵、汽車尾氣和其他氣體汙染物混在空氣中形成的有害煙霧，通常出現在城市或工業區。它不是普通天氣造成的霧，而是帶有明顯汙染性質的空氣。","examples":[{"en":"The city was covered in thick smog after several days without wind.","zh":"連續幾天沒有風后，這座城市被濃重的霧霾籠罩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many residents wear masks when the smog becomes severe.","zh":"霧霾嚴重時，許多居民會戴口罩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smog","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04d588cb41b8022d1233","word":"smoke","forms":["smoke"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-881cfe04b66fa1c5","term":"smoke","forms":["smoke","smokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燃燒產生的煙","explanation":"指東西燃燒或悶燒時散到空氣中的煙霧、氣體和細小顆粒；記住核心畫面裡的“煙”，就是這種會遮擋視線的煙。","examples":[{"en":"Smoke filled the kitchen after the toast caught fire.","zh":"吐司著火後，廚房裡充滿了煙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could see smoke rising from the hill.","zh":"我們看見煙從山上升起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d7e5bee4835d979","term":"smoke","forms":["smoke","smokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一支香菸","explanation":"口語中指一支香菸；這是把“煙”從煙霧轉而指產生煙霧的那件東西。","examples":[{"en":"He stepped outside to light a smoke.","zh":"他走到外面點了一支菸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could I bum a smoke off you?","zh":"我能向你討一支菸嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a47dd8632a7623de","term":"smoke","forms":["smoke","smokes","smoking","smoked","smoken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抽（煙）","explanation":"指吸入並撥出香菸、雪茄或菸斗等燃燒物產生的煙，也就是把“煙”吸進再撥出來。","examples":[{"en":"He smoked a cigarette outside the office.","zh":"他在辦公室外抽了一支菸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stopped smoking after her doctor warned her.","zh":"醫生警告她之後，她戒了煙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d645561d5033530","term":"smoke","forms":["smoke","smokes","smoking","smoked","smoken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒煙","explanation":"指物體，尤其是發動機、車輛或著火的東西，放出煙；這裡不是人在吸菸，而是東西自己產生了煙。","examples":[{"en":"The toaster started smoking, so I unplugged it.","zh":"烤麵包機開始冒煙，所以我把它拔掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old bus was smoking as it climbed the hill.","zh":"那輛舊公交車爬坡時一直冒煙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0f1779c16d26bac92c4","word":"smooth","forms":["smooth"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-508a243f3a9d36cf","term":"smooth","forms":["smooth","smoother","smoothest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表面光滑","explanation":"表示表面沒有粗糙感或明顯摩擦，摸起來平整順滑，是smooth最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The stone is smooth after years in the river.","zh":"這塊石頭經過多年的河水沖刷後變得很光滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This cream leaves your hands smooth.","zh":"這種護手霜能讓你的手變得光滑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smooth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5f589c228cb9289","term":"smooth","forms":["smooth","smoother","smoothest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"順利的","explanation":"表示事情進行得順暢，沒有明顯困難、意外或阻礙；這是從“表面沒有阻力”引申出來的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We had a smooth trip despite the bad weather.","zh":"儘管天氣不好，我們的旅程還是很順利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The handover to the new manager went smoothly.","zh":"向新經理交接的過程很順利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smooth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9cd797a970bbf811","term":"smooth","forms":["smooth","smoother","smoothest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"流暢、不生硬","explanation":"形容話語、聲音或動作連貫流暢，沒有停頓、阻塞或刺耳感。","examples":[{"en":"Her smooth presentation kept everyone interested.","zh":"她流暢的演講讓所有人都很投入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smooth dialogue made the film enjoyable to watch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smooth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27be0030aad7e26f","term":"smooth","forms":["smooth","smooths","smoothing","smoothed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使平整、撫平","explanation":"表示把皺褶、粗糙處或不平的表面弄平，讓它變得順滑。","examples":[{"en":"She smoothed the blanket before sitting down.","zh":"她坐下前把毯子撫平了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He smoothed the paper with his hand.","zh":"他用手把紙撫平了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smooth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-803173c990f53b7d","term":"smooth","forms":["smooth","smooths","smoothing","smoothed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使事情順利","explanation":"表示消除困難或阻礙，讓某人的經歷、安排或過程更容易進行。","examples":[{"en":"Her advice smoothed the way for the negotiations.","zh":"她的建議為談判順利進行鋪平了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A local interpreter helped smooth their dealings with the officials.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smooth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ab6217f21e927499076","word":"smuggle","forms":["smuggle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3aa61419b013cf7d","term":"smuggle","forms":["smuggle","smuggles","smuggling","smuggled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"走私","explanation":"指以非法或隱秘方式進出口物品或人員，以逃避合法的海關費用或關稅。","examples":[{"en":"The gang smuggled stolen paintings across the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Customs officers discovered diamonds smuggled inside a toy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smuggle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfa895bb4b286aaf","term":"smuggle","forms":["smuggle","smuggles","smuggling","smuggled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偷偷帶入","explanation":"指秘密地把某物或某人帶入某處，未必涉及違法行為。","examples":[{"en":"She smuggled sweets into the cinema beneath her coat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"He smuggled a rescue puppy into the strict hotel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smuggle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff488ab8733e4c47df71","word":"snack","forms":["snack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-015a712b5e1a4bcb","term":"snack","forms":["snack","snacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少量加餐","explanation":"snack是分量較小、用來墊一墊的飯或點心，通常吃在兩頓正餐之間。它強調的是輕便、少量，不一定特指某一種食物。","examples":[{"en":"I had a light snack before the meeting.","zh":"開會前我吃了點簡單的加餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pack a small snack for the afternoon walk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b55f7d06bc5ce40","term":"snack","forms":["snack","snacks","snacking","snacked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃點加餐","explanation":"snack作動詞時，表示吃一頓很輕的飯或少量食物；它把名詞所指的點心動作化了。","examples":[{"en":"She was snacking on fruit while she worked.","zh":"她工作時一邊吃水果一邊墊點東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We snacked on nuts during the long drive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62156a7b494a332c0b9b","word":"snail","forms":["snail"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1fe5e6a5cabfcbe","term":"snail","forms":["snail","snails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蝸牛","explanation":"一種身體柔軟、通常揹著螺旋形外殼、靠腹足緩慢爬行的小動物。這個最基本的形象也是其他相關義項的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"A snail was crawling across the wet stone.","zh":"一隻蝸牛正在潮溼的石頭上爬行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found several snails under the leaves.","zh":"我們在樹葉下面發現了幾隻蝸牛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2397913f9e5c2783","term":"snail","forms":["snail","snails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動遲緩的人","explanation":"把人比作爬得很慢的蝸牛，表示這個人做事或走路很慢，常帶有輕微的嫌棄、催促或打趣意味。","examples":[{"en":"Come on, you snail—we're going to miss the bus!","zh":"快點，你這個慢吞吞的傢伙——我們要趕不上公共汽車了！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come on, you snail; the bus is nearly here.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-538d7d9fe78e7baac47a","word":"snake","forms":["snake"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27f195640deba25a","term":"snake","forms":["snake","snakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛇","explanation":"snake 是一種沒有腿、身體細長、用蜿蜒方式移動並有分叉舌頭的爬行動物。","examples":[{"en":"A snake was hiding under the old bridge.","zh":"一條蛇正藏在那座舊橋下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saw several snakes near the rocks.","zh":"我們在岩石附近看到了幾條蛇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8413272617106fa","term":"snake","forms":["snake","snakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陰險背叛的人","explanation":"把人稱為 snake，是說這個人為了自己的利益欺騙或背叛別人，像蛇一樣危險而不可信。","examples":[{"en":"I trusted him, but he turned out to be a snake.","zh":"我信任過他，但後來發現他是個陰險的叛徒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That snake sold our confidential plans to a rival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e11f3c10ce5b82a","term":"snake","forms":["snake","snakes","snaking","snaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蜿蜒前進","explanation":"snake 作動詞時，表示沿著彎曲路線前進，或使路線像蛇一樣曲折延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The road snaked through the hills.","zh":"這條路蜿蜒穿過群山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A line of cars snaked around the block.","zh":"一列汽車繞著街區蜿蜒排開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c27324f013705cbf0c4","word":"snap","forms":["snap"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4082ac31e36153d3","term":"snap","forms":["snap","snaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啪的一聲；清脆斷裂聲","explanation":"指突然、迅速發出的清脆聲音，常像東西啪地斷開、撞擊或扣上時的聲音；也可以指發出這種聲音的動作。這個義項正對應記憶中的“啪”的一聲。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a loud snap behind us.","zh":"我們聽見身後傳來一聲巨響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The branch broke with a sharp snap.","zh":"樹枝啪的一聲斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-260a74fa6d1ef1c4","term":"snap","forms":["snap","snaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"快照；隨手拍的照片","explanation":"指一張照片，尤其是快速隨手拍下、沒有特別安排的照片。相機快門“啪”地一按，就形成了這層“快照”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I took a snap of the sunset from the train.","zh":"我在火車上拍了一張日落的快照。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sent me a few snaps from her trip.","zh":"她給我發來了幾張旅行時拍的照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-746b506d79dfc540","term":"snap","forms":["snap","snaps","snapping","snapped","snapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然斷裂","explanation":"東西啪地一下突然斷開或碎裂；也可以表示某人突然把某物折斷。這個意思最直接地體現了記憶鉤子裡“啪地斷開”。","examples":[{"en":"The dry branch snapped under my weight.","zh":"那根幹樹枝在我的重量下啪地斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He snapped the pencil in half.","zh":"他啪的一聲把鉛筆折成了兩半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca87097b10e313db","term":"snap","forms":["snap","snaps","snapping","snapped","snapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拍照","explanation":"迅速按下相機快門拍攝照片；這個意思來自快門按下時可能發出的“啪”聲。","examples":[{"en":"I snapped a picture of the sunset before it disappeared.","zh":"夕陽快要消失前，我拍了一張照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you snap a photo of us?","zh":"你能幫我們拍張照片嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cd512a819ae26ee1999","word":"snatch","forms":["snatch"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4cd2670ab5798be","term":"snatch","forms":["snatch","snatches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突然抓取","explanation":"指快速抓住或接住某物的動作，重點是出手突然、動作很快。","examples":[{"en":"The goalkeeper made a brilliant snatch to keep the ball out.","zh":"守門員漂亮地一把抓住了球，沒讓它進門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He snatched the letter before it reached the fire.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01d76d61890225a2","term":"snatch","forms":["snatch","snatches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短暫的一段時間","explanation":"指很短、往往不連續的一段時間，常用於休息、睡眠或做某事的零碎時間。","examples":[{"en":"I managed to sleep in snatches during the long flight.","zh":"長途飛行中，我只能斷斷續續地睡一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She slept only in short snatches that night.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-979a49cc743668f3","term":"snatch","forms":["snatch","snatches","snatching","snatched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迅速抓走","explanation":"指突然把某物抓住並迅速拿走，動作通常很快，有時帶有出其不意的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"She snatched up her keys and ran out the door.","zh":"她一把抓起鑰匙，跑出了門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child snatched the toy away from his brother.","zh":"孩子從哥哥手裡突然把玩具搶了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c8f3efe635ae914","term":"snatch","forms":["snatch","snatches","snatching","snatched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"倉促奪取","explanation":"指倉促、突然或不拘禮節地拿走某物，甚至未經允許取走；“搶一個吻”也屬於這種突然奪取的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"He snatched a quick kiss before the train doors closed.","zh":"火車門關上前，他匆匆親了對方一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boy snatched the letter from my hand.","zh":"男孩突然從我手裡奪走了那封信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snatch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94c75c39f25a90b76b36","word":"sneak","forms":["sneak"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6149c0dc0e3f0d92","term":"sneak","forms":["sneak","sneaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偷偷摸摸的人","explanation":"指總是暗中行動、偷偷獲取東西或資訊的人，通常暗示這個人不誠實或不值得信任。","examples":[{"en":"My brother is such a sneak that he reads my messages when I leave my phone unattended.","zh":"我弟弟太鬼鬼祟祟了，我手機沒人看著時他就會讀我的訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little sneak read my private messages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc5a38bd721ed273","term":"sneak","forms":["sneak","sneaks","sneaking","sneaked","snuck"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偷偷走進或離開","explanation":"指為了不被發現而悄悄移動或進入某處，核心是躲開別人的注意。","examples":[{"en":"I sneaked into the house after everyone had gone to bed.","zh":"大家都睡著後，我悄悄溜進了房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sneaked out before anyone noticed.","zh":"她趁沒人注意時悄悄離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a819d3e239417f83","term":"sneak","forms":["sneak","sneaks","sneaking","sneaked","snuck"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偷偷拿取","explanation":"指未經允許暗中拿走或取用某樣東西，動作重點是避開他人察覺；是否構成正式意義上的盜竊要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"The children sneaked some cookies from the kitchen.","zh":"孩子們從廚房偷偷拿了些餅乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I sneaked a look at the gift before my birthday.","zh":"生日之前我偷偷看了一眼禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21b1efff7a8c8db4","term":"sneak","forms":["sneak","sneaks","sneaking","sneaked","snuck"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偷偷帶給某人","explanation":"指暗中把某物帶給某人，通常因為不想讓別人發現或因為這樣做不被允許。","examples":[{"en":"Could you sneak me a sandwich when the manager leaves?","zh":"經理離開後，你能偷偷給我帶個三明治嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sneaked her brother an extra biscuit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-024cf4aa414bccbe1100","word":"sneaker(s)","forms":["sneaker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4b50fcc08bd461fe","term":"sneaker","forms":["sneaker","sneakers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運動鞋","explanation":"指鞋底通常較軟、適合運動或日常休閒穿著的鞋，也是 sneaker 在現代英語中最常見的意義。","examples":[{"en":"I wore my new sneakers for the long walk.","zh":"我穿著新運動鞋去走了很長一段路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These sneakers are comfortable enough for everyday use.","zh":"這雙運動鞋很舒服，適合日常穿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneaker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f00dbe22643b0203139f","word":"sneaky","forms":["sneaky"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53a1a7a8bd438b0e","term":"sneaky","forms":["sneaky","sneakier","sneakiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難以捉摸的；狡猾難抓的","explanation":"形容某人或某物總能躲開觀察、逃脫追捕，或不斷想辦法讓對手抓不到。重點是“藏得住、躲得掉”，不一定已經造成傷害。","examples":[{"en":"Those thieves are so sneaky that the police still can't catch them.","zh":"那些小偷太狡猾難捉了，警方到現在還抓不到他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sneaky fox repeatedly escaped the farmer's traps.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneaky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25f9326cab23fee8","term":"sneaky","forms":["sneaky","sneakier","sneakiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不誠實的；暗中耍手段的","explanation":"形容一個人不直接說清楚或公平行事，而是在暗地裡欺騙、設圈套或佔便宜，因此通常含有批評意味。","examples":[{"en":"That was a sneaky trick to make us pay for the damage.","zh":"讓我們為損壞的東西買單，這真是個暗中耍手段的伎倆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That sneaky trick left the other players furious.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneaky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69ade16b2a6a266605a3","word":"sneeze","forms":["sneeze"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5887128a7bc6b8b","term":"sneeze","forms":["sneeze","sneezes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噴嚏","explanation":"指一次鼻子受到刺激後突然排出空氣的動作或聲音，也就是“一個噴嚏”。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a sneeze from the next room.","zh":"我聽見隔壁房間傳來一個噴嚏聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden sneeze interrupted his explanation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17bd19a23b7f0877","term":"sneeze","forms":["sneeze","sneezes","sneezing","sneezed","snoze","snozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打噴嚏","explanation":"指鼻子受到灰塵、花粉、感冒等刺激後，身體反射性地把空氣猛地排出去。","examples":[{"en":"She started sneezing when the flowers opened.","zh":"花一開，她就開始打噴嚏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please sneeze into a tissue.","zh":"請對著紙巾打噴嚏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5f0077dc9e2ef7cb275","word":"sniff","forms":["sniff"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35e9f858b11827ae","term":"sniff","forms":["sniff","sniffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聞一下；吸鼻一下","explanation":"指一次短促的用鼻子吸氣，通常是為了聞某種氣味；重點是“一下”的動作，而不是持續呼吸。","examples":[{"en":"She gave the milk a quick sniff before drinking it.","zh":"她喝牛奶前先快速聞了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave the milk a cautious sniff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sniff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-efa4f60216ce828a","term":"sniff","forms":["sniff","sniffs","sniffing","sniffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸鼻；嗅聞","explanation":"指用鼻子短促而通常能聽見地吸氣，常為了聞氣味，也可以只是因為哭泣、感冒等。它是整組詞義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"The dog sniffed every corner of the room.","zh":"那隻狗聞遍了房間的每個角落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sniffed and wiped his nose with a tissue.","zh":"他吸了吸鼻子，用紙巾擦了擦鼻子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sniff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b070137ec98858e","term":"sniff","forms":["sniff","sniffs","sniffing","sniffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"模糊察覺","explanation":"表示憑直覺或微弱跡象察覺到某事，像鼻子捕捉到了一點還不清楚的氣味；常用於察覺麻煩、危險或機會。","examples":[{"en":"She could sniff trouble before anyone else noticed it.","zh":"別人還沒察覺時，她就已經聞出了麻煩的跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reporters sniffed a scandal behind the sudden resignation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sniff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a8d6bc40c357aa677f9","word":"snore","forms":["snore"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a8bb8a6ace0db87","term":"snore","forms":["snore","snores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼾聲；打鼾","explanation":"指人在睡眠中呼吸時，由口腔或咽部組織振動而發出的粗重聲音，也可以指打鼾這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"I woke up when I heard a loud snore from the next room.","zh":"我聽見隔壁房間傳來一聲很響的鼾聲，便醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His snore kept everyone awake during the trip.","zh":"旅途中他的鼾聲讓大家都沒睡著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-809731805c03fd57","term":"snore","forms":["snore","snores","snoring","snored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打鼾","explanation":"指人在睡著時呼吸，因口腔或咽部組織振動而發出粗重、帶鼻音的聲音。","examples":[{"en":"My brother snores loudly whenever he falls asleep on the sofa.","zh":"我哥哥每次在沙發上睡著都會打很響的鼾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I could hear my dog snoring in the basket.","zh":"我能聽見我的狗在窩裡打鼾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a746222f09d85605c52d","word":"snow","forms":["snow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7727b3e6f37209b","term":"snow","forms":["snow","snows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雪；降雪；積雪","explanation":"指水結成的白色晶體從天空落下，也指這些雪落在地面或物體上形成的白色覆蓋層。這是snow最基本、最常用的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The snow covered the roads overnight.","zh":"雪一夜之間覆蓋了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Snow is falling outside.","zh":"外面正在下雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cfc6c773566af7be","term":"snow","forms":["snow","snows","snowing","snowed","snew","snown","snowest","snowedst","snoweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下雪","explanation":"指雪從天空降落。英語通常用無實際所指的it作主語，所以不是“雪自己做動作”，而是用固定天氣句型表達正在或將要下雪。","examples":[{"en":"It started to snow just before dawn.","zh":"黎明前剛開始下雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It has been snowing all afternoon.","zh":"整個下午一直在下雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99f72d7e511685bae651","word":"snowy","forms":["snowy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-22e0d5235e6ab1e8","term":"snowy","forms":["snowy","snowier","snowiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"下雪的；多雪的","explanation":"指天氣、季節或某段時間有雪，畫面是雪正在落下或雪帶來的天氣狀態。","examples":[{"en":"We had a snowy day in the mountains.","zh":"我們在山裡度過了下雪的一天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roads may be dangerous after a snowy night.","zh":"下了一夜雪後，道路可能很危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f1ac04c0fdf8d8f","term":"snowy","forms":["snowy","snowier","snowiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"被雪覆蓋的","explanation":"指山坡、道路、樹木等表面蓋滿了雪，核心畫面是雪鋪在物體上。","examples":[{"en":"The children ran down the snowy hillside.","zh":"孩子們跑下了被雪覆蓋的山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We followed a snowy path through the forest.","zh":"我們沿著一條被雪覆蓋的小路穿過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1d9890884c1b4b960c2","word":"so","forms":["so"],"officialPos":"adv./conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-83520a2f01ebe776","term":"so","forms":["so"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到明確的程度","explanation":"表示達到前面明確說出的程度，常引出“如此……以至於……”的結果。","examples":[{"en":"It was so hot outside that all the plants died.","zh":"外面太熱了，所有植物都枯死了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke so quietly that nobody heard her.","zh":"她說話聲音太小，沒人聽見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/so","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ead3828f59ad72a","term":"so","forms":["so"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到暗示的程度","explanation":"表示某種程度沒有明說，但可以從語境、手勢或前文推斷出來，相當於“這麼、那麼”。","examples":[{"en":"Please cut the rope so long.","zh":"請把繩子剪成這麼長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I hadn't realized the bag was so heavy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/so","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-817ae0426ab6927c","term":"so","forms":["so"],"pos":"adv","zh":"同樣、也","explanation":"表示照前面那樣或達到同樣程度，也可以代替前面提到的整個想法。","examples":[{"en":"“I love this song.” “So do I.”","zh":"“我喜歡這首歌。”“我也是。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You have the right to speak, and so do I.","zh":"你有發言的權利，我也有。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/so","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c06f543b3ea6c597516e","word":"soak","forms":["soak"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7910c635e6f22e8","term":"soak","forms":["soak","soaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"浸泡；泡澡","explanation":"指把身體或物品浸在液體中的一段時間，重點是讓它充分泡在液體裡。它也常特指舒服地泡澡。","examples":[{"en":"After the hike, I had a long soak in the tub.","zh":"徒步之後，我在浴缸裡泡了很久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A long soak relieved her aching muscles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f77a3ebaf92a711f","term":"soak","forms":["soak","soaks","soaking","soaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"浸泡；泡透","explanation":"指某物浸在液體中，逐漸被液體充分浸透；也可指人在液體中泡著。這裡強調的是充分浸入，而不只是碰到水。","examples":[{"en":"I soaked in the hot bath until my muscles relaxed.","zh":"我在熱水澡裡泡到肌肉放鬆為止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The towel soaked in the spilled juice.","zh":"毛巾浸在灑出的果汁裡，很快泡透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7faa8604d02ecd67","term":"soak","forms":["soak","soaks","soaking","soaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"浸泡某物","explanation":"指把物品放進液體中一段時間，使液體充分進入內部。做飯時常把豆類、米或幹食材提前泡軟。","examples":[{"en":"Soak the dried mushrooms in warm water for twenty minutes.","zh":"把幹蘑菇放在溫水裡泡二十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Soak the dried beans overnight before cooking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa13ce40da67aa7f","term":"soak","forms":["soak","soaks","soaking","soaked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"滲入；浸透","explanation":"指液體逐漸進入材料、衣物或地面內部。畫面是水從外面一點點穿進去，而不是停留在表面。","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater soaked into my shoes during the walk.","zh":"走路時，雨水滲進了我的鞋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spilled oil soaked into the wooden floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-736bc2d4e0945110e88f","word":"soap","forms":["soap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df33caa6e772e767","term":"soap","forms":["soap","soaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肥皂","explanation":"一種主要由脂肪酸鹽製成的清潔用品，能幫助水帶走皮膚或物體表面的油汙。日常最常見的是洗手、洗澡或洗東西用的肥皂。","examples":[{"en":"Please wash your hands with soap before dinner.","zh":"請在飯前用肥皂洗手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I dropped the bar of soap in the shower.","zh":"我把那塊肥皂掉在淋浴間裡了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-177ff0502041088e","term":"soap","forms":["soap","soaps","soaping","soaped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用肥皂清洗","explanation":"表示把肥皂抹到身體、物體等表面並進行清洗，是名詞“肥皂”轉成的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"Soap your hands well, then rinse them under clean water.","zh":"把手好好抹上肥皂，然後用清水沖洗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She soaped the muddy boots before scrubbing them.","zh":"她先給沾泥的靴子抹上肥皂，再把它們刷乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3388452318b2e7225fe9","word":"soar","forms":["soar"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-006fee3d9b6157ed","term":"soar","forms":["soar","soars","soaring","soared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"高飛","explanation":"鳥張開翅膀，幾乎不費力地飛到高處，就是soar；這個畫面是全詞最核心的基礎。","examples":[{"en":"The hawk soared above the valley without flapping its wings.","zh":"鷹沒有拍動翅膀，在山谷上空翱翔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flock of gulls soared into the clear morning sky.","zh":"一群海鷗飛上了晴朗的晨空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e358a2d5dcf92f7","term":"soar","forms":["soar","soars","soaring","soared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"猛漲","explanation":"從鳥飛得越來越高的畫面引申出來，價格、數量或水平也可以soar，表示突然或異常地升到很高。","examples":[{"en":"Fuel prices soared after the refinery shut down.","zh":"煉油廠停產後，燃油價格猛漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cost of repairs soared to twice the original estimate.","zh":"維修費用猛增到原估價的兩倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-454bedc703c397ac8232","word":"sob","forms":["sob"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9d734ec1c3a3f88","term":"sob","forms":["sob","sobs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽泣聲；哽咽聲","explanation":"這是哭泣時因呼吸一陣陣抽動而發出的短促聲音，通常帶有悲傷、痛苦或強烈情緒。","examples":[{"en":"A quiet sob came from the next room.","zh":"隔壁房間傳來一聲輕輕的抽泣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She let out a sob when she saw the photograph.","zh":"她看到那張照片時忍不住抽泣了一聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-789c7dd1bb25c9a2","term":"sob","forms":["sob","sobs","sobbing","sobbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抽泣；啜泣","explanation":"指哭泣時呼吸一陣陣抽動，併發出斷續的聲音；比單純流淚更強調身體上的抽氣和聲音。","examples":[{"en":"The child sobbed quietly in the corner.","zh":"那個孩子在角落裡默默地抽泣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sobbed for several minutes after the call.","zh":"打完電話後，他抽泣了好幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-250f45a48d99d4b8","term":"sob","forms":["sob","sobs","sobbing","sobbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"抽泣著說","explanation":"表示人物一邊抽泣，一邊說出某句話；重點仍是說話時的抽泣狀態。","examples":[{"en":"“I can't go on,” she sobbed.","zh":"“我堅持不下去了。”她抽泣著說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Between gasps, he sobbed that his puppy was missing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sob","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d32f293e971b0859eed0","word":"sober","forms":["sober"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a3e4d1abd3bfda9","term":"sober","forms":["sober","soberer","soberest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清醒的；未醉的","explanation":"指人當下沒有喝醉，頭腦和行為沒有受到酒精的影響。這是 sober 最基本、最容易從“清醒”記住的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please make sure you are sober before you drive.","zh":"請務必在清醒後再開車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stayed sober at the party and drove everyone home.","zh":"她在聚會上沒有喝醉，最後開車送大家回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sober","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8aae29bf19b0f5b","term":"sober","forms":["sober","soberer","soberest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未受娛樂性藥物影響的","explanation":"指人沒有處於娛樂性藥物造成的影響之下。它把“清醒”從酒精擴充套件到其他使人失去正常判斷的藥物。","examples":[{"en":"He has been sober for a year and says he feels like himself again.","zh":"他已經一年沒有使用藥物了，並說自己又找回了原來的狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic helped her stay sober after treatment.","zh":"治療後，診所幫助她保持不使用藥物的狀態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sober","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1dc8011fdcad4c3","term":"sober","forms":["sober","soberer","soberest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冷靜剋制的；嚴肅現實的","explanation":"指一個人不衝動、不沉迷幻想，能夠冷靜、認真地面對現實。這是從“頭腦清醒”引申出的比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"After hearing the facts, we need to take a sober look at the problem.","zh":"聽到事實後，我們需要冷靜、現實地看待這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report gives a sober assessment of the country's future.","zh":"這份報告對這個國家的未來作出了冷靜務實的評估。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sober","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37e12267eb4e56b0","term":"sober","forms":["sober","sobers","sobering","sobered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使清醒；變得清醒","explanation":"表示讓自己或別人回到清醒狀態，是形容詞“清醒、不醉”對應的動作。它可以指從醉態中恢復，也可以泛指恢復正常判斷。","examples":[{"en":"He drank some water and walked outside to sober up.","zh":"他喝了些水，到外面走走讓自己清醒過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cold air sobered her up quickly.","zh":"冷空氣很快使她清醒了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sober","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f27f432fcbaa4b5180a","word":"soccer","forms":["soccer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d03a294ca97f9f7a","term":"soccer","forms":["soccer"],"pos":"noun","zh":"足球運動","explanation":"指以腳踢球、以進球得分為目標的足球運動，也可指這項運動中的比賽。這裡的重點是“用腳踢球”這一整體畫面。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter plays soccer every Saturday.","zh":"我女兒每週六都踢足球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a soccer match after dinner.","zh":"我們晚飯後看了一場足球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soccer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2817c11b7b27b32d3da8","word":"sociable","forms":["sociable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-acb99a2c1727c33c","term":"sociable","forms":["sociable","more sociable","most sociable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愛交際的；合群的","explanation":"形容一個人願意和別人來往、聊天，容易融入人群。它強調對社交的態度和習慣，不一定表示這個人非常外向或健談。","examples":[{"en":"Mia is sociable and quickly makes friends wherever she goes.","zh":"米婭很合群，無論走到哪裡都能很快交到朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He becomes more sociable after a cup of coffee.","zh":"他喝完一杯咖啡後就更願意和人交往了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sociable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3acf02313c3546c9","term":"sociable","forms":["sociable","more sociable","most sociable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"適合交談的","explanation":"形容聚會、環境或活動能讓人輕鬆聊天、彼此交流；重點不在場面熱鬧，而在於它給交談創造了條件。","examples":[{"en":"The small café is a sociable place where neighbors often chat.","zh":"這家小咖啡館很適合交談，鄰居們經常在那裡聊天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room's sociable layout encouraged guests to mingle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sociable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e860f41a5ea92c49803","word":"social","forms":["social"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09a272223b901fb1","term":"social","forms":["social","more social","most social"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愛交際的","explanation":"形容一個人喜歡和別人交往、認識很多人，性格外向或合群。這裡的 social 重點不是“屬於社會”，而是“願意進入人與人的關係中”。","examples":[{"en":"Mia is very social and makes friends wherever she goes.","zh":"米婭非常愛交際，走到哪裡都能交到朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was too shy to be social at the party.","zh":"我太害羞了，在聚會上沒能積極和別人交往。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/social","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b208c53b55c5c9b4","term":"social","forms":["social","more social","most social"],"pos":"adj","zh":"社會的；社會關係的","explanation":"表示與社會整體、社會成員之間的關係或社會問題有關。它把視線從個人擴大到由許多人組成的群體。","examples":[{"en":"The new law has caused serious social problems.","zh":"這項新法律造成了嚴重的社會問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project aims to reduce social inequality.","zh":"這個專案旨在減少社會不平等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/social","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4c0f5d754224dd43c69","word":"socialism","forms":["socialism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18ee7702f1e09d75","term":"socialism","forms":["socialism","socialisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會主義思想","explanation":"指一類主張由社會或政府共同擁有、管理生產資料，並共同安排商品生產和分配的經濟與政治理論。它的核心畫面是：重要的經濟資源不應完全由私人單獨控制，而應服務於整個社會。","examples":[{"en":"She began studying socialism after becoming interested in economic inequality.","zh":"她對經濟不平等產生興趣後，開始研究社會主義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The movement combines socialism with strong support for local democracy.","zh":"這個運動把社會主義與對地方民主的強烈支援結合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socialism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-094a922a486ce7f2","term":"socialism","forms":["socialism","socialisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬克思主義中的過渡階段","explanation":"在馬克思主義理論的特定框架中，socialism 指資本主義與共產主義之間的社會發展階段；這一階段通常強調國家控制生產資料。這裡不是泛指所有社會主義思想，而是理論體系中的專門用法。","examples":[{"en":"In Marxist theory, socialism is described as a stage between capitalism and communism.","zh":"在馬克思主義理論中，社會主義被描述為資本主義與共產主義之間的一個階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In Marxist theory, socialism precedes a fully communist society.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socialism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-102738617034c7655d06","word":"socialist","forms":["socialist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d2e93ee5781fd6cb","term":"socialist","forms":["socialist","socialists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會主義者","explanation":"指支援或主張社會主義的人；這個身份來自其政治思想或立場。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents were socialists who believed in public ownership.","zh":"她的父母是社會主義者，相信公有制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He describes himself as a democratic socialist.","zh":"他稱自己是民主社會主義者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socialist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eaba78c3f208f35f0157","word":"socialize","forms":["socialize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e545dc09fa23185f","term":"socialize","forms":["socialize","socializes","socializing","socialized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與人交往；社交","explanation":"指在正式工作或事務之外，和別人輕鬆地聊天、相處或參加社交活動，就是走進“社會圈子”與人建立聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"I usually socialize with my colleagues after work.","zh":"我通常下班後和同事們社交。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She went to the party to socialize and meet new people.","zh":"她去參加聚會是為了社交併認識新朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socialize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1f9b321e31b087d","term":"socialize","forms":["socialize","socializes","socializing","socialized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使習得社會規範","explanation":"指家庭、學校或社會透過教育、模仿和日常環境，讓一個人逐漸學會社會中的禮儀、偏好和行為方式；這裡不是簡單地“帶某人去社交”，而是塑造其社會行為。","examples":[{"en":"Children are socialized to respect rules through daily routines.","zh":"孩子們透過日常生活逐漸學會尊重規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Schools help socialize children into shared routines.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socialize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f5eae21697a35ca7a16","word":"society","forms":["society"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8eadbce203036a28","term":"society","forms":["society","societies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文化社會；社會群體","explanation":"指長期共同生活、共享語言、服飾、行為規範或藝術傳統的一群人，重點在於他們形成了相對穩定的文化和生活方式。","examples":[{"en":"This society has preserved its language and traditions for centuries.","zh":"這個社會群體幾個世紀以來一直保留著自己的語言和傳統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Different societies have different ideas about family life.","zh":"不同社會對家庭生活有不同的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/society","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59af0d613247d4c8","term":"society","forms":["society","societies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整個社會；社會大眾","explanation":"指一個國家、社群或全世界的人們作為整體，強調所有人共同組成的社會。這裡不是某個小群體，而是把視角拉遠後看到的整張“人際之網”。","examples":[{"en":"Technology is changing the way people live in society.","zh":"技術正在改變人們在社會中的生活方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Society as a whole must protect children.","zh":"整個社會都必須保護兒童。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/society","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f39199d63c4115b7c16","word":"sociology","forms":["sociology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90662c03c80aa5cc","term":"sociology","forms":["sociology","sociologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會學","explanation":"社會學是研究社會如何組織和運作的學科。它既看人與人之間的互動，也看群體、文化、制度和社會結構如何影響個人行為，因此研究範圍可以從日常交往延伸到整個社會。","examples":[{"en":"She studies sociology at a university in London.","zh":"她在倫敦的一所大學學習社會學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sociology helps us understand how social media changes relationships.","zh":"社會學幫助我們理解社交媒體如何改變人際關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sociology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a08ed46eaa714db7a93b","word":"sock(s)","forms":["sock"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f58fcd8bcd4d80e5","term":"sock","forms":["sock","socks","sox"],"pos":"noun","zh":"襪子","explanation":"穿在腳上、通常從腳踝向上包住腳部的衣物，是sock最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I put on a clean pair of socks before work.","zh":"我上班前換上了一雙乾淨的襪子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sock has a hole in it.","zh":"這隻襪子上有個洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-47dd56c2c7a7f7aac789","word":"socket","forms":["socket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b53432df57820a2a","term":"socket","forms":["socket","sockets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"插座；承介面","explanation":"指一個凹進去的部位或裝置，用來容納、套住或連線相匹配的另一部分。日常最常見的是牆上接電的插座，也可以泛指承接其他部件的介面或容槽。","examples":[{"en":"I plugged the lamp into the wall socket.","zh":"我把檯燈插進了牆上的插座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This cable does not fit the socket on the back of the monitor.","zh":"這根線纜與顯示器背面的介面不匹配。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1c2b82d1519bca5","term":"socket","forms":["socket","sockets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路通訊端點","explanation":"在計算機網路中，socket 是雙向通訊連線的一端，程式透過它傳送和接收資料。它保留了“接住另一端並建立連線”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The server opens a socket and waits for incoming connections.","zh":"伺服器開啟一個通訊端點，等待傳入的連線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Close the socket once the file has finished transferring.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4cf5e703ea05d936c9c","word":"soda","forms":["soda"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3f0c7230f020897","term":"soda","forms":["soda","sodas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碳酸水；蘇打水","explanation":"指溶有加壓二氧化碳、會冒泡的水，通常不強調甜味；這個義項連線了化學物質和飲料兩條意義。","examples":[{"en":"I ordered a glass of soda with my whiskey.","zh":"我點了一杯蘇打水配威士忌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you bring me some soda water, please?","zh":"請給我拿一些蘇打水，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2b36eafaf505ddd","term":"soda","forms":["soda","sodas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汽水；碳痠軟飲料","explanation":"泛指通常含糖、帶氣泡的軟飲料，如可樂等；在美國英語中，這是日常最常見的理解。","examples":[{"en":"The children had pizza and soda for lunch.","zh":"孩子們午餐吃了披薩，還喝了汽水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ordered a soda with his sandwich.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soda","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d32ce7bf0277fd2ca3b6","word":"sofa","forms":["sofa"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91845c460c9c00d0","term":"sofa","forms":["sofa","sofas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沙發","explanation":"指帶軟墊、靠背和一個或兩個扶手，長度足以讓兩人或更多人舒適坐下的傢俱。它是“sofa”最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a new sofa for the living room.","zh":"我們給客廳買了一張新沙發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sofa unfolds into a comfortable guest bed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sofa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5f445528f4a0134354c","word":"soft","forms":["soft"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f880abc1bd92c0d","term":"soft","forms":["soft","softer","softest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"柔軟的","explanation":"指物體受到壓力時容易讓步、變形，不會硬硬地頂住；可以把它想成沒有硬碰硬，按下去會陷進去。","examples":[{"en":"The baby slept on a soft pillow.","zh":"嬰兒睡在一個柔軟的枕頭上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soft cushion supported her aching back.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15af82f0f01883de","term":"soft","forms":["soft","softer","softest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"輕柔的；溫和的","explanation":"指風、觸碰或其他動作溫和輕柔，不會猛烈地衝擊人或物；這正是“沒有硬碰硬”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"A soft breeze came through the open window.","zh":"一陣輕柔的微風從開著的窗戶吹進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A soft voice came from behind the curtain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f4adac60e11ba1b","term":"soft","forms":["soft","softer","softest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易的；不費力的","explanation":"指工作、任務或機會所需的努力很少，做起來比較輕鬆；它是從“不硬、不費力”引申出來的。","examples":[{"en":"After weeks of training, the final test felt soft.","zh":"訓練了幾周後，最後的測試感覺很容易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wanted a soft job with few responsibilities.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-354d51ee5f356dcc56b6","word":"soften","forms":["soften"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c0fd271d6986236","term":"soften","forms":["soften","softens","softening","softened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變軟","explanation":"把原本堅硬的東西變得更軟，例如加熱黃油、浸泡材料或讓皮膚變柔軟。這是 soften 最直接的物理意義。","examples":[{"en":"Soften the butter before you mix in the flour.","zh":"把黃油軟化後再拌入麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cream will soften dry skin overnight.","zh":"這種乳霜一夜之間就能使乾燥的皮膚變柔軟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soften","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd0c5ea1b6c863c3","term":"soften","forms":["soften","softens","softening","softened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緩和嚴厲程度","explanation":"把批評、語氣、立場或規定說得不那麼尖銳、嚴厲或絕對，就像把堅硬的邊緣磨圓一樣。這是從物理“變軟”自然引申出的常用抽象意義。","examples":[{"en":"She softened her criticism after hearing the full story.","zh":"聽完整個故事後，她緩和了自己的批評。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The editor softened the wording of the announcement.","zh":"編輯把公告的措辭改得不那麼強硬了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soften","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35390f5453e810b62480","word":"software","forms":["software"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6c9c5a153c4f2a81","term":"software","forms":["software","softwares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機軟體","explanation":"指儲存在計算機等裝置中的程式和編碼指令，它們告訴硬體怎樣工作。它和硬體相對：硬體是裝置本身，software 是讓裝置完成任務的“柔性內容”。","examples":[{"en":"This software helps students organize their research notes.","zh":"這款軟體幫助學生整理研究筆記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You need to update the software before using the new device.","zh":"使用這臺新裝置前，你需要更新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/software","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e93d59a02163f846fecf","word":"soil","forms":["soil"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-634fb02d078277c1","term":"soil","forms":["soil","soils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物用土","explanation":"指由礦物顆粒和有機物組成、可以支援植物生長的土壤，園藝和日常種植中最常見。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a bag of soil for the houseplants.","zh":"我們買了一袋土來種室內植物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fill the pot with fresh soil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7f6cee68c7facdc","term":"soil","forms":["soil","soils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地表土層","explanation":"指地球表面供陸生植物紮根和生長的天然土層，範圍比園藝用土更廣。","examples":[{"en":"Healthy soil helps trees survive long periods without rain.","zh":"健康的土壤能幫助樹木熬過長時間沒有降雨的時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The topsoil is richer than the soil beneath it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bfbc118abcafe8c53ee","word":"solar","forms":["solar"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc15a30186000748","term":"solar","forms":["solar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"太陽的；與太陽有關的","explanation":"指屬於太陽、來自太陽，或直接與太陽有關的事物，是 solar 最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The room was filled with solar light through the glass roof.","zh":"陽光透過玻璃屋頂灑滿了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are studying how solar radiation affects the atmosphere.","zh":"科學家正在研究太陽輻射如何影響大氣層。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a12213167350b58","term":"solar","forms":["solar"],"pos":"adj","zh":"按太陽執行計算的","explanation":"指以太陽的週年執行作為時間計算依據的，如太陽年、太陽曆。","examples":[{"en":"A solar year is slightly longer than 365 days.","zh":"一個太陽年略長於365天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The calendar follows the solar year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0c08c2b1f538cd00a81","word":"soldier","forms":["soldier"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b0db33d6cfface7","term":"soldier","forms":["soldier","soldiers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"士兵；陸軍士兵","explanation":"指地面部隊中的軍人，軍銜可以很廣，但通常特別指入伍服役的普通士兵。它體現了記憶主線中“站在前線執行任務的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The soldier checked the road before the convoy moved on.","zh":"車隊繼續前進前，那名士兵檢查了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many soldiers were stationed near the border.","zh":"許多士兵駐紮在邊境附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soldier","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-979a3a5fbffb6dfb5821","word":"sole","forms":["sole"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fe73533da4f7e375","term":"sole","forms":["sole"],"pos":"adj","zh":"唯一的","explanation":"表示某類人或事物中只有這一個，沒有其他同類物件。","examples":[{"en":"She was the sole survivor of the accident.","zh":"她是這場事故中唯一的倖存者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is the sole reason I agreed.","zh":"這就是我同意的唯一原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e50411c27342796","term":"sole","forms":["sole","soles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腳底","explanation":"指腳接觸地面的最下面一面，也就是腳掌的底部。","examples":[{"en":"The cut on the sole of my foot made walking painful.","zh":"我腳底的傷口讓走路很疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sharp stone cut the sole of his foot.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ee18e05fe1fc2f4","term":"sole","forms":["sole","soles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞋底","explanation":"指鞋或靴子最下面、直接接觸地面的部分。","examples":[{"en":"The sole of my left boot is coming loose.","zh":"我左腳靴子的鞋底快脫開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mud lodged in the deep grooves of the shoe sole.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93278ec48f1c32814ca4","word":"solemn","forms":["solemn"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-42f85c97b8933cda","term":"solemn","forms":["solemn","solemner","more solemn","solemnest","most solemn"],"pos":"adj","zh":"莊重正式的","explanation":"指某個儀式、場合或行為按照正式而莊重的方式進行，往往讓人自然地放低聲音、收斂態度。它從“神聖儀式的莊嚴感”擴充套件到一般正式場合。","examples":[{"en":"The new president took the solemn oath of office.","zh":"新總統莊重地宣讀了就職誓詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A solemn ceremony was held to honor the victims.","zh":"人們舉行了莊重的儀式來悼念遇難者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solemn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16b713307a481b13","term":"solemn","forms":["solemn","solemner","more solemn","solemnest","most solemn"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴肅沉重的","explanation":"指人的態度、表情或談話內容非常認真、嚴肅，幾乎沒有輕鬆或玩笑的意味。它像莊嚴儀式中的神情一樣，讓人感到事情很重要。","examples":[{"en":"She gave us a solemn warning before we left.","zh":"我們離開前，她嚴肅地警告了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His face became solemn when he heard the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息後，他的表情變得嚴肅起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solemn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b3d4a0dd732f791ca89","word":"solid","forms":["solid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a644755c194d8bfc","term":"solid","forms":["solid","more solid","solider","most solid","solidest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"固體的","explanation":"指有固定形狀和質感、可以拿起或握住的物質狀態，與液體、氣體相對。這是“實心、不流動”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Almost all metals are solid at room temperature.","zh":"幾乎所有金屬在室溫下都是固體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water becomes solid ice below its freezing point.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0120c119ec6f747b","term":"solid","forms":["solid","more solid","solider","most solid","solidest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅固的；不易動搖的","explanation":"指基礎、物體或立場牢固有力，不容易倒塌、改變或被推翻。它把“實心”這個形象擴充套件到了抽象事物。","examples":[{"en":"The house needs a solid foundation.","zh":"這座房子需要堅固的地基。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a solid argument for changing the policy.","zh":"她提出了支援修改這項政策的有力論據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e25fb62e09615e9a42d","word":"solidarity","forms":["solidarity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e4dfc4f797a85ae","term":"solidarity","forms":["solidarity","solidarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"團結一致；共同支援","explanation":"指一群人因為共同目標、共同利益或共同面對的對手而站在一起，彼此支援。它尤其常用於工會、社會運動或群體行動的語境。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of workers marched in solidarity with the striking nurses.","zh":"數千名工人與罷工的護士並肩遊行，表示支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The students wore blue ribbons as a sign of solidarity with the victims.","zh":"學生們佩戴藍絲帶，以表示對受害者的支援和團結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solidarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d96325b67277e8f1","term":"solidarity","forms":["solidarity","solidarities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"在困境中給予支援","explanation":"指人們在某人遭遇困難、痛苦或失去親人時站在他身邊，給他情感或實際支援。這是“站在一起”這一核心概念在人際關係中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"Her friends' solidarity helped her get through the difficult months.","zh":"朋友們的支援幫助她熬過了那幾個月的困難時期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their neighbors stood beside them in solidarity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solidarity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fe62ade181eaca9b41b","word":"solitary","forms":["solitary"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f8633aba44142b8","term":"solitary","forms":["solitary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"孤獨的；獨自一人的","explanation":"指一個人獨自存在或生活，沒有同伴陪著；重點是“離開他人、處於獨處狀態”。","examples":[{"en":"He led a solitary life in the mountains.","zh":"他獨自一人在山裡生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A solitary figure stood by the window.","zh":"窗邊站著一個孤單的身影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solitary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7e4bcac618720f2","term":"solitary","forms":["solitary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"單獨進行的","explanation":"指某項旅程、活動或經歷由一個人獨自完成、度過或承受，不強調它一定令人傷感。","examples":[{"en":"She set out on a solitary journey across the desert.","zh":"她獨自踏上了穿越沙漠的旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent a solitary evening reading by the fire.","zh":"他獨自一人在爐火旁讀書，度過了一個晚上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solitary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00bddb36a62f5719e471","word":"solitude","forms":["solitude"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ed269f7b8b3912f","term":"solitude","forms":["solitude","solitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨處；獨居狀態","explanation":"指一個人沒有他人陪伴、與人群分開的狀態，重點是“獨自一人”，不一定意味著難過或被遺棄。它既可以是被動的孤單，也可以是為了安靜思考而主動選擇的獨處。","examples":[{"en":"She enjoys the solitude of her early-morning walks.","zh":"她喜歡清晨散步時獨處的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a busy week, I need some solitude.","zh":"忙了一週後，我需要一些獨處的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0a5b864891b8334","term":"solitude","forms":["solitude","solitudes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"荒涼之地；無人處","explanation":"指幾乎沒有人煙、顯得孤寂荒涼的地方。這個義項把“人與外界隔絕”的核心畫面從人的狀態擴充套件到了地點。","examples":[{"en":"Beyond the last village, the road leads into a vast solitude.","zh":"越過最後一個村莊，道路通向一片廣闊的荒涼之地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They crossed the desolate solitudes of the Arctic on skis.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solitude","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5364f2f2fc4f54e9d47a","word":"solo","forms":["solo"],"officialPos":"n./adv./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de6c7e1f603c9a9e","term":"solo","forms":["solo"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獨自的；單獨的","explanation":"表示沒有同伴或指導者，一個人完成某件事。它突出“身邊沒有一起做的人”，可以用於旅行、工作、訓練等情境。","examples":[{"en":"She took a solo trip across the country.","zh":"她獨自進行了一次橫跨全國的旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He launched a solo project after leaving the band.","zh":"離開樂隊後，他開始了一個個人專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-325b72aac9e5b045","term":"solo","forms":["solo"],"pos":"adv","zh":"獨自地；單獨地","explanation":"表示一個人完成某個動作，沒有同伴一起參加；它是“舞臺上只有一個人”這一核心意象在行動方式上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I decided to travel solo this summer.","zh":"我決定今年夏天獨自旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sailed solo across the Pacific.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c4793a1bfedc49f","term":"solo","forms":["solo","solos","soli"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獨奏曲；獨奏","explanation":"指專門為一名錶演者創作或由一名錶演者完成的音樂段落或作品，畫面就是一個人站在舞臺中央。","examples":[{"en":"The guitarist played a long solo during the final song.","zh":"吉他手在最後一首歌中演奏了一段很長的獨奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote a solo for flute and piano.","zh":"她為長笛和鋼琴創作了一段長笛獨奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8270f2824111e04d9278","word":"solution","forms":["solution"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5210f06252d86be","term":"solution","forms":["solution","solutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溶液","explanation":"在化學中，solution 是一種均勻的混合物：一種或多種物質溶解在另一種物質中，形成看起來均一的液體、氣體或固體體系。它可以理解為“把物質化開後得到的可處理混合物”。","examples":[{"en":"Add the powder to the water and stir until it forms a clear solution.","zh":"把粉末加入水中，攪拌到形成透明溶液。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The blue solution turned clear after the reagent was added.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1d80e6f24cbd184","term":"solution","forms":["solution","solutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解決辦法","explanation":"solution 可以是為解決問題而採取或提出的計劃、辦法或手段，重點在“用什麼方法處理難題”，不一定已經成功。","examples":[{"en":"We need a practical solution to the traffic problem.","zh":"我們需要一個解決交通問題的實際辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team proposed a simple solution.","zh":"團隊提出了一個簡單的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62b9aab7a748dade","term":"solution","forms":["solution","solutions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"答案","explanation":"solution 也可以是問題、謎題或數學題最後得到的答案，也就是“難題被解開後呈現出來的結果”。","examples":[{"en":"She finally found the solution to the puzzle.","zh":"她終於找到了這個謎題的答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The solution to the puzzle surprised everyone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solution","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c14cdb19563cb1644772","word":"solve","forms":["solve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5153efda2ad83c97","term":"solve","forms":["solve","solves","solving","solved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"解決；解答","explanation":"指透過思考、調查或嘗試找到問題的答案或可行辦法，就像把一個封閉的謎團開啟。物件可以是問題、難題、謎題或爭端。","examples":[{"en":"We need to solve this problem before the meeting.","zh":"我們需要在會議前解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She solved the puzzle in five minutes.","zh":"她五分鐘就解開了這個謎題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-471d42e5d3585ca9","term":"solve","forms":["solve","solves","solving","solved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偵破；查明","explanation":"指透過線索和調查查明犯罪的經過、動機或實施者，也就是把案件這個謎團解開。","examples":[{"en":"The detectives solved the case after finding a hidden camera.","zh":"偵探找到一個隱藏攝像頭後偵破了這起案件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The detective solved the murder using a single fingerprint.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6b46dd0d1ae5e86cbc8","word":"some","forms":["some"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cab53fbe4f3ab843","term":"some","forms":["some"],"pos":"det","zh":"一些；某些","explanation":"放在複數可數名詞前，表示一個不明確但至少包含不止一個物件的部分。說話人不想或不需要說明具體數量。","examples":[{"en":"Some students stayed after class to ask questions.","zh":"一些學生下課後留下來提問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some birds cannot fly.","zh":"有些鳥不會飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/some","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0bc043bcaa36936","term":"some","forms":["some"],"pos":"det","zh":"一些；若干","explanation":"放在複數可數名詞前，表示數量不確定的若干個物件；重點是“有一部分”，而不是準確數目。","examples":[{"en":"We bought some apples for the picnic.","zh":"我們為野餐買了一些蘋果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some children prefer drawing to team games.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/some","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6db91ccf7a35ba1","term":"some","forms":["some"],"pos":"det","zh":"一些；一點","explanation":"放在不可數名詞前，表示某種物質、抽象事物或其他不可數內容的一部分，數量不明確。","examples":[{"en":"Could you give me some advice?","zh":"你能給我一些建議嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is some milk in the fridge.","zh":"冰箱裡還有一些牛奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/some","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5c6ed528cb2e9ac","term":"some","forms":["some"],"pos":"pron","zh":"有些；有一些","explanation":"單獨使用時，some 表示某個群體或範圍中的一部分，數量至少不止一個，但具體是多少不說明。","examples":[{"en":"Some prefer tea, while others choose coffee.","zh":"有些人喜歡茶，而另一些人選擇咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some stayed for dinner, while others went home.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/some","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9bbf175eb1a7cf7","term":"some","forms":["some"],"pos":"pron","zh":"一些；一部分","explanation":"代替已經提到或容易確定的複數事物，表示其中數量不明確的一些，可以理解為“有一些這樣的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Some of the guests arrived early.","zh":"一些客人提前到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some stayed behind to help clear the tables.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/some","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37d290c980a1d001","term":"some","forms":["some"],"pos":"pron","zh":"一些；一部分","explanation":"代替不可數內容時，some 表示其中的一部分，具體量不明確；它可以指食物、材料、資訊等不能直接逐個數的東西。","examples":[{"en":"I saved some for you.","zh":"我給你留了一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some of the apples were too bruised to sell.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/some","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-233c0ee4290408f13428","word":"someday","forms":["someday"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5c1d0a0039cc8ce","term":"someday","forms":["someday"],"pos":"adv","zh":"總有一天；以後某天","explanation":"指未來某個沒有明確日期的時間，就像日曆上還沒有寫日期的某一天。它既可以表示計劃或承諾，也可以表示對未來的希望。","examples":[{"en":"I hope to visit Japan someday.","zh":"我希望將來有一天能去日本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someday, I’ll learn to play the piano.","zh":"總有一天，我會學會彈鋼琴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/someday","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd8736cdd6b052cfd09a","word":"somehow","forms":["somehow"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97495188c3ae2d1a","term":"somehow","forms":["somehow"],"pos":"adv","zh":"想辦法；以某種不明方式","explanation":"表示具體怎麼做還不知道、沒有說明，或者不管採用什麼方法都要把事情完成。核心感覺是“鑰匙是哪一把不清楚，但門總要開啟”。","examples":[{"en":"We have to finish this project somehow.","zh":"我們總得想辦法完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Somehow, she knew I needed help.","zh":"不知怎麼的，她知道我需要幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/somehow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf16c4ccd49172c72f0d","word":"someone/somebody","forms":["someone","somebody"],"officialPos":"pron./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd76e5777b975f9f","term":"someone","forms":["someone","someones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某個未點名的人","explanation":"它像一張沒有寫名字的人物卡，指某個具體但沒有說出姓名的人；在名詞用法中，常把這個人作為特別指出的物件。","examples":[{"en":"She is saving the letter for that special someone.","zh":"她要把這封信留給那個特別的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A certain someone has eaten the last cookie.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/someone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-093cadefbd304067","term":"someone","forms":["someone"],"pos":"pron","zh":"有人；某個人","explanation":"它指一個身份未說明的人，重點是“有這麼一個人”，而不是這個人的姓名、性別或其他具體資訊。它可以出現在請求中，也可以指已經做過某事但身份不明的人。","examples":[{"en":"Could someone close the window, please?","zh":"請有人把窗戶關上，好嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone left an umbrella by the door.","zh":"有人把一把傘落在門邊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/someone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7d89051e8c3caf9","term":"somebody","forms":["somebody"],"pos":"pron","zh":"有人；某個人","explanation":"它指某個身份沒有說明的人，相當於“有人”或“某個人”；說話人知道或只關心有這麼一個人，但不指出是誰。","examples":[{"en":"Somebody has to clean up this mess.","zh":"得有人把這個爛攤子收拾乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Somebody left a message for you.","zh":"有人給你留了言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/somebody","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3fc9b689459d738f8c88","word":"something","forms":["something"],"officialPos":"pron./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-932904af7cd1ecdb","term":"something","forms":["something"],"pos":"pron","zh":"某事；某物","explanation":"指一個未具體說明的人、事物、想法或內容，相當於“某個東西、某件事”。它是 something 最基礎、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I forgot to bring something important.","zh":"我忘了帶一件重要的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Would you like something to drink?","zh":"你想喝點什麼嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/something","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-669b763083cd7b813cdc","word":"sometime","forms":["sometime"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb2cab5d472023a8","term":"sometime","forms":["sometime"],"pos":"adv","zh":"某個時候","explanation":"表示事情會在過去或將來的某個不確定時刻發生；時間大致有範圍，但說話人不指出確切時刻。可以把它想成時間線上被故意留白的一個點。","examples":[{"en":"I'll call you sometime this evening.","zh":"我今晚某個時候給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let's meet sometime next week.","zh":"我們下週找個時候見面吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sometime","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28e5c066055aeb3de147","word":"sometimes","forms":["sometimes"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d17b559144920099","term":"sometimes","forms":["sometimes"],"pos":"adv","zh":"有時；偶爾","explanation":"表示某件事在一些時候或某些情況下會發生，但並不是每次都發生。它把“發生”和“不發生”交替放在同一條時間線上，是最常用、最重要的含義。","examples":[{"en":"I sometimes walk to work instead of taking the bus.","zh":"我有時步行去上班，而不是乘公共汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sometimes the simplest answer is the best one.","zh":"有時最簡單的答案才是最好的答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sometimes","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d8c872204eed624adb0","word":"somewhat","forms":["somewhat"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3be4b42a72338ea3","term":"somewhat","forms":["somewhat"],"pos":"adv","zh":"有點；在一定程度上","explanation":"表示某種性質或狀態達到了一定程度，但不是完全或特別強，常可理解為“有點”“稍微”“頗為”。它把程度刻度向前推了一小格，語氣通常比直接說“非常”弱。","examples":[{"en":"The new plan is somewhat more expensive than the old one.","zh":"新計劃比舊計劃貴一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was somewhat surprised by her answer.","zh":"她的回答讓我有點驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/somewhat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92b6359c721fcf6f815f","word":"somewhere","forms":["somewhere"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-179872cc34ead585","term":"somewhere","forms":["somewhere"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在某處","explanation":"表示某物或某人在一個未指明的地方，重點是“在那裡，但不知道或不說具體是哪兒”。","examples":[{"en":"I must have left my keys somewhere.","zh":"我一定是把鑰匙落在某處了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your phone is somewhere in this room.","zh":"你的手機就在這個房間的某個地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/somewhere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91b27214a6ea7ddd","term":"somewhere","forms":["somewhere"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到某處","explanation":"表示移動的目的地不明確，即要去一個沒有具體說明的地方；常帶有“找個地方去”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Let's go somewhere quiet for lunch.","zh":"我們找個安靜的地方吃午飯吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wants to travel somewhere warm this winter.","zh":"她想在今年冬天去一個暖和的地方旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/somewhere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98aa6675482552881925","word":"son","forms":["son"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48ef6f6be5ae78cf","term":"son","forms":["son","sons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兒子","explanation":"指某人的男性子女，是最基本、最常用的含義；畫面就是父母生下或養育的男孩、男子。","examples":[{"en":"Their son starts university this autumn.","zh":"他們的兒子今年秋天開始上大學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is proud of her youngest son.","zh":"她為自己的小兒子感到自豪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/son","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2c957202c1d1b25","term":"son","forms":["son","sons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"養子","explanation":"指男性養子，即透過收養關係成為某對父母的兒子；重點仍是“成為這個家庭的後代”。","examples":[{"en":"They welcomed their adopted son into the family.","zh":"他們歡迎養子成為家庭的一員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They adopted their son when he was six months old.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/son","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63f75c890b05405e6e1f","word":"song","forms":["song"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29c83df00295f3ec","term":"song","forms":["song","songs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歌曲","explanation":"指人用聲音演唱的一首歌曲，通常有旋律，也常有歌詞。","examples":[{"en":"I listened to my favorite song on the bus.","zh":"我在公交車上聽了自己最喜歡的歌曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you sing this song with me?","zh":"你能和我一起唱這首歌嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/song","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a32f25b89dfdf55a","term":"song","forms":["song","songs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂作品","explanation":"泛指音樂作品，不一定特別強調歌詞或演唱；在較寬泛的語境中，一段樂曲也可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"This song has no lyrics, but its melody is beautiful.","zh":"這首音樂作品沒有歌詞，但旋律很優美。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her latest song features a simple piano accompaniment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/song","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4a754148b88a68e18df1","word":"soon","forms":["soon"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58650252cfe9f1c8","term":"soon","forms":["soon","sooner","soonest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不久；很快","explanation":"表示事情會在不長的時間內發生，或一個事件緊跟在另一個事件之後；核心感覺仍是“時間距離不遠”。","examples":[{"en":"She will be back soon.","zh":"她很快就會回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We soon realized that the door was locked.","zh":"我們很快就意識到門鎖著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-020570fef6bd1b052312","word":"soothe","forms":["soothe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a18aed1e8261d35","term":"soothe","forms":["soothe","soothes","soothing","soothed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安撫；使平靜","explanation":"使緊張、激動或不安的人、動物和情緒恢復平靜，就像把躁動慢慢降下來。","examples":[{"en":"She sang softly to soothe the frightened child.","zh":"她輕聲唱歌來安撫受驚的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A warm bath helped soothe his nerves.","zh":"溫水澡幫助他緩解了緊張情緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soothe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab14083ad5eec5f8","term":"soothe","forms":["soothe","soothes","soothing","soothed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安撫某人或局面","explanation":"透過解釋、道歉或安慰讓生氣的人不再繼續激動，也可以讓失控的局面重新穩定。","examples":[{"en":"He tried to soothe the angry customer with a refund.","zh":"他試圖透過退款安撫那位憤怒的顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her calm explanation soothed the situation.","zh":"她冷靜的解釋緩和了局面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soothe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c24864ff79ca0fa","term":"soothe","forms":["soothe","soothes","soothing","soothed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緩解疼痛或痛苦","explanation":"減輕身體疼痛或精神上的痛苦，讓人感覺舒服一些；這是現代英語中很常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Honey can soothe a sore throat.","zh":"蜂蜜可以緩解喉嚨痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cream soothed the irritation on her skin.","zh":"這種乳霜緩解了她皮膚上的刺激感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soothe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e45c0ca14614471e9725","word":"sophisticated","forms":["sophisticated"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a57bb0070f96ae64","term":"sophisticated","forms":["sophisticated","more sophisticated","most sophisticated"],"pos":"adj","zh":"見多識廣的；老練世故的","explanation":"形容一個人經歷豐富、熟悉社會和不同生活方式，因此不容易天真地相信一切；有時也帶有“顯得不再單純”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She is sophisticated enough to recognize the difference between charm and honesty.","zh":"她見多識廣，足以看出魅力和誠實之間的區別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Living abroad made him more sophisticated about other cultures.","zh":"在國外生活讓他對其他文化有了更成熟、更廣的認識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticated","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-585279280c741a1b","term":"sophisticated","forms":["sophisticated","more sophisticated","most sophisticated"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精緻高雅的；有文化品位的","explanation":"形容藝術、設計、風格或品味經過細緻發展，能吸引有見識的人；重點不是昂貴，而是顯得雅緻、講究、有層次。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant has a sophisticated atmosphere without feeling formal.","zh":"這家餐廳的氛圍很雅緻，卻不會讓人覺得拘謹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sophisticated taste in music is easy to notice.","zh":"她在音樂方面的高雅品味很容易看出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticated","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2de992cac15364cfd4af","word":"sophomore","forms":["sophomore"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a63c3e68292decd9","term":"sophomore","forms":["sophomore","sophomores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"二年級學生","explanation":"指四年制大學或中學中的第二年學生，也就是已經完成第一年、但還沒有進入最後兩年的學生。","examples":[{"en":"My cousin is a sophomore at a university in California.","zh":"我表弟在加利福尼亞的一所大學讀大二。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a sophomore, he changed his major.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophomore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2eab005be0d086bc9815","word":"sore","forms":["sore"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df69380b396931c5","term":"sore","forms":["sore","sorer","sorest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"疼痛的；痠痛的","explanation":"指身體某處因受傷、勞累或刺激而疼痛、痠痛，或對觸碰特別敏感。核心畫面就是身體上有一塊“一碰就疼”的地方。","examples":[{"en":"My shoulders are sore from carrying the heavy boxes.","zh":"我扛那些重箱子後肩膀痠痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cut is still sore when I touch it.","zh":"那道傷口碰起來還是很疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ebd61cc0030f5f0","term":"sore","forms":["sore","sores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疼痛的傷口；潰瘍","explanation":"指皮膚上受傷、感染、發炎或患病而形成的一塊疼痛處，就是形容詞所說的那塊“一碰就疼”的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse cleaned the sore on his ankle and covered it with a bandage.","zh":"護士清理了他腳踝上的傷口，並給它包上了繃帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tight boots rubbed a sore on her heel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2cdbdd82910725464b02","word":"sorrow","forms":["sorrow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-097e499c1e996dc8","term":"sorrow","forms":["sorrow","sorrows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"悲傷；哀痛","explanation":"sorrow 是一種沉重、深切的悲傷或哀痛，強調心裡承受著失去、離別或不幸帶來的痛苦。","examples":[{"en":"She was filled with sorrow after her father's death.","zh":"父親去世後，她心中充滿了悲痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tried to hide his sorrow from the children.","zh":"他努力不讓孩子們看出自己的悲傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sorrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-617cccf2a5fb74cf06e7","word":"sorrowful","forms":["sorrowful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"sorrowful","forms":["sorrowful"],"pos":"adj.","zh":"悲傷的；悲痛的","examples":[{"en":"She gave us a sorrowful smile before leaving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The letter brought sorrowful news to the family.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-484aab2f2cd0f77b3c30","word":"sorry","forms":["sorry"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c13ecdaba60634f","term":"sorry","forms":["sorry","sorrier","sorriest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到抱歉","explanation":"因自己的行為造成麻煩或傷害而感到遺憾，並承認自己對此有歉意。","examples":[{"en":"I’m sorry I broke your mug.","zh":"對不起，我把你的杯子打破了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was sorry about the mistake.","zh":"她為這個錯誤感到抱歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sorry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e45c8b4c69c34a8c","term":"sorry","forms":["sorry","sorrier","sorriest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"為某人或某事難過","explanation":"看到別人遭遇不幸，或失去某人某物時感到悲傷和遺憾；重點是同情或惋惜，不一定是自己做錯了什麼。","examples":[{"en":"I feel sorry for Maya after she lost her job.","zh":"瑪雅失業後，我很為她難過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We were sorry to hear about his accident.","zh":"聽說他出了事故，我們很難過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sorry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-646964943fd2271187db","word":"sort","forms":["sort"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad8ff6128048d58e","term":"sort","forms":["sort","sorts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"種類；型別","explanation":"指具有共同特徵的一類人、事物或情況，相當於“型別、種類”。","examples":[{"en":"What sort of music do you usually listen to?","zh":"你通常聽什麼型別的音樂？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is a sort of bread made with whole grains.","zh":"這是一種用全穀物製作的麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2395314175fe3ed1","term":"sort","forms":["sort","sorts","sorting","sorted","sortest","sortedst","sorteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"分類","explanation":"按照類別或標準把混在一起的東西分開，放入不同的組中。","examples":[{"en":"Please sort the laundry into whites and colors.","zh":"請把要洗的衣物分成白色和彩色兩類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sorted the books by subject.","zh":"我們按主題給書分類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21fa99a891098fbe","term":"sort","forms":["sort","sorts","sorting","sorted","sortest","sortedst","sorteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"排序；排列","explanation":"按照數字、字母、時間等規則把專案排成一定順序。","examples":[{"en":"Can you sort these names alphabetically?","zh":"你能按字母順序排列這些名字嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app sorts messages by date.","zh":"這個應用按日期排列訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sort","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae0facccf0a3723adefb","word":"soul","forms":["soul"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f5c10847f7e1cc47","term":"soul","forms":["soul","souls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的靈魂","explanation":"指被認為存在於人的思想、性格和內在生命中的精神核心；在宗教或民間觀念中，它常被認為不會隨著身體死亡而消失。","examples":[{"en":"She believes that the soul lives on after death.","zh":"她相信靈魂在死後仍然存在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story touched my soul.","zh":"這個故事觸動了我的靈魂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0b22415d2fd3e733","term":"soul","forms":["soul","souls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物的精神或精髓","explanation":"把“靈魂”從人引申到事物，指一個地方、作品、活動或群體最有生命力、最能代表其本質的精神。","examples":[{"en":"The old market is the soul of the town.","zh":"這座老市場是這個城鎮的靈魂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She put her soul into the painting.","zh":"她把自己的全部精神都投入了這幅畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soul","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd29442deca69f52c500","word":"sound","forms":["sound"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fc7905b12cda8660","term":"sound","forms":["sound","sounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聲音","explanation":"指耳朵聽到的聲音，可能來自人、動物、物體或環境；這就是sound最基本的“耳朵聽到的”那條線。","examples":[{"en":"I heard the sound of rain on the roof.","zh":"我聽到了雨打在屋頂上的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep your voice down and don't make a sound.","zh":"請小聲一點，不要發出任何聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9014fac8184d7ba9e1dc","word":"soup","forms":["soup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1c502109e717e06","term":"soup","forms":["soup","soups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"湯；湯類食物","explanation":"由水或高湯和肉、蔬菜等食材組成的液體食物。它既可以指一份或一種具體的湯，也可以泛指湯這種食物，因此既有可數用法，也有不可數用法。","examples":[{"en":"We had hot soup for lunch.","zh":"我們午飯喝了熱湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soup is made with chicken and vegetables.","zh":"這道湯是用雞肉和蔬菜做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb3f4ce4fc4c89a4","term":"soup","forms":["soup","soups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一份或一種湯","explanation":"強調可以單獨數出的某一份湯，或選單上的某一種湯。這裡的重點不是“湯”這一類食物，而是一個具體的湯品。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant offers three soups every day.","zh":"這家餐館每天供應三種湯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'll have the tomato soup, please.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d4268591d78dcf6d5d9","word":"sour","forms":["sour"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a0194f5f1ee7518","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sourer","sourest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"酸的","explanation":"表示食物或飲料帶有明顯的酸味，例如檸檬的味道；這是 sour 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The lemonade is too sour for me.","zh":"這檸檬水對我來說太酸了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sour juice made her wrinkle her nose.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c09dfe5b649a56d","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sourer","sourest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"變質發酸的","explanation":"表示牛奶等食物因發酵或變質而變酸，重點是已經不新鮮、不能放心食用。","examples":[{"en":"The milk has turned sour, so pour it out.","zh":"牛奶已經變質發酸了，把它倒掉吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The milk smelled sour after a day in the sun.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2bf2631cb2cbbc6","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sourer","sourest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不友好的；陰沉的","explanation":"把“酸味帶來的皺眉感”轉用來形容人的表情、態度或反應，表示敵意、不高興或不友好。","examples":[{"en":"She gave him a sour look when he interrupted.","zh":"他打斷她時，她不友好地瞪了他一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave us a sour look and walked away.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f5b3bd29182b891","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酸味","explanation":"指酸這種味覺感受，或食物中讓人感到酸的味道。","examples":[{"en":"The sour of the lemon balanced the sweetness of the cake.","zh":"檸檬的酸味平衡了蛋糕的甜味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A dash of tamarind introduces a pleasant sour to the sauce.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c484c3b42f58ce7","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sours","souring","soured","sourest","souredst","soureth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變酸","explanation":"表示加入酸性成分或經過處理，使食物、飲料等產生酸味。","examples":[{"en":"A little vinegar will sour the sauce.","zh":"加一點醋就會使醬汁變酸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A little lemon juice soured the cream.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0bf7873443e09c98","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sours","souring","soured","sourest","souredst","soureth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變酸","explanation":"表示食物或飲料自己因發酵、變質等變酸，或液體的味道逐漸變壞。","examples":[{"en":"The cream soured in the heat.","zh":"奶油在高溫下變酸了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The milk soured during the long power cut.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0eb1b0b9ef695652","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sours","souring","soured","sourest","souredst","soureth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使掃興或破壞","explanation":"把食物變壞的意思用於事情，表示某事破壞了別人的快樂、期待或好心情。","examples":[{"en":"The unexpected bill soured our evening.","zh":"那張意外的賬單破壞了我們晚上的好心情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bitter argument soured the entire evening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7269abc4ff36c8a8","term":"sour","forms":["sour","sours","souring","soured","sourest","souredst","soureth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變壞；失去興趣","explanation":"表示關係、態度或心情逐漸惡化，從原本愉快或有希望變得冷淡、敵對或失望。","examples":[{"en":"Their friendship soured after the argument.","zh":"爭吵後，他們的友誼惡化了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Relations between the partners gradually soured over unpaid invoices.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41cf6794ba4200b839c5","word":"source","forms":["source"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-477ab78b657408a1","term":"source","forms":["source","sources"],"pos":"noun","zh":"來源；出處","explanation":"指某種資訊、物品或其他事物從中來、從中取得的人、地點或事物。它是最常見的用法，可以把不同事物追溯到各自的來處。","examples":[{"en":"The website is a useful source of information about local events.","zh":"這個網站是瞭解當地活動的有用資訊來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to check the source of these figures before publishing the report.","zh":"釋出報告前，我們需要核實這些資料的來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/source","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee89965db4283540","term":"source","forms":["source","sources"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水源；源頭","explanation":"指河流或其他水流開始的地方，通常是地面上或地下的一處泉水、蓄水處或水源。這裡保留了“源頭”這一核心概念，只是來源具體變成了水。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers followed the river upstream to find its source.","zh":"徒步旅行者沿河向上遊走，尋找它的源頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river's source lies high in the mountains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/source","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2daa8d4a05dfc643abb4","word":"south","forms":["south"],"officialPos":"n./adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54ad635818eaddee","term":"south","forms":["south"],"pos":"adj","zh":"朝南的；向南的","explanation":"表示方向朝向南方，或位於通向南方的方向上，是“南方”這個核心位置向外延伸出的方向意義。","examples":[{"en":"The village is south of the river.","zh":"這個村莊在河的南面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took the south road to avoid the traffic.","zh":"我們走了南邊的路來避開交通擁堵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/south","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d98d6255eae5e3c","term":"south","forms":["south"],"pos":"adj","zh":"南方的；南部的","explanation":"表示某事物屬於南方、位於南部，或與南部地區有關，是把“南方”當作一個區域來描述。","examples":[{"en":"They live on the south side of the city.","zh":"他們住在這座城市的南邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The south coast enjoys a milder climate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/south","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c6e48d072721376","term":"south","forms":["south"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向南","explanation":"表示移動或延伸的方向是南方，是“南方”作為目標方向的副詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The birds fly south every autumn.","zh":"這些鳥每年秋天向南飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river flows south toward the sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/south","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e79cc87354b60f4e","term":"south","forms":["south"],"pos":"adv","zh":"惡化；變糟","explanation":"在 go south 中，事情彷彿偏離了原本的正軌，朝不利方向發展，因此表示情況變糟或計劃失敗。","examples":[{"en":"Everything went south after the main supplier quit.","zh":"主要供應商退出後，一切都變糟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The negotiations went south after the final demand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/south","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec20d69417d396f8","term":"south","forms":["south","souths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"南方；南向","explanation":"指與東、西、北並列的基本方向，也可以指朝向南方的方向位置。","examples":[{"en":"Germany is south of Denmark.","zh":"德國在丹麥以南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sun was low in the south.","zh":"太陽低低地掛在南方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/south","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0344e73919703e9","term":"south","forms":["south","souths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"南部地區","explanation":"指一個國家、城市或區域的南部，也可指生活在該南部區域的人們；這裡的 south 從方向變成了一個地理區域。","examples":[{"en":"The south is warmer than the north in winter.","zh":"冬天南部比北部暖和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The south receives less snow than the mountains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/south","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1cac4d101ee696fd7a70","word":"southern","forms":["southern"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c9e013b247e94c7","term":"southern","forms":["southern","more southern","most southern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"南方的；向南的","explanation":"指位於南邊、面向南方，或從南方來的事物，是這個詞最基本的方位意義。","examples":[{"en":"The southern entrance is open all day.","zh":"南面的入口全天開放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The house's southern windows receive the most sunlight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/southern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fbe3877c495385c","term":"southern","forms":["southern","more southern","most southern"],"pos":"adj","zh":"南方地區的；南部特色的","explanation":"指屬於某個南方地區，尤其可指歐洲南部或美國南部的氣候、生活方式、文化和其他事物。","examples":[{"en":"The southern climate is mild in winter.","zh":"南方氣候在冬季比較溫和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The recipe reflects traditional Southern cooking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/southern","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15dacf6574831a179293","word":"souvenir","forms":["souvenir"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f17553093459fa9c","term":"souvenir","forms":["souvenir","souvenirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紀念品；紀念物","explanation":"指為了記住某個地方、事件或經歷而買來、收到或儲存的物件。它像是把一段記憶裝進一個可以看見、觸控的東西里。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a small souvenir from Kyoto for my sister.","zh":"我從京都買了一件小紀念品送給妹妹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kept the ticket as a souvenir of her first concert.","zh":"她把那張票留著，作為第一次參加音樂會的紀念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/souvenir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21aef37bf4ee4959fdbe","word":"sovereign","forms":["sovereign"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-44859fef1a4ef1de","term":"sovereign","forms":["sovereign","more sovereign","most sovereign"],"pos":"adj","zh":"主權的；行使統治權的","explanation":"指擁有或行使國家最高統治權的，尤其用於國家、政府或權力機構。它強調不受更高外部權力支配。","examples":[{"en":"Every sovereign nation has the right to protect its borders.","zh":"每個主權國家都有權保護自己的邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement recognizes the island as a sovereign state.","zh":"這項協議承認該島是一個主權國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sovereign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7df126dfc3891c3","term":"sovereign","forms":["sovereign","more sovereign","most sovereign"],"pos":"adj","zh":"擁有最高權力的","explanation":"指某人具有至高、最終的統治權，常用於君主或正式尊稱。","examples":[{"en":"The sovereign approved the new constitution.","zh":"君主批准了新憲法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constitution recognizes parliament as the sovereign authority.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sovereign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b33be415175230e","term":"sovereign","forms":["sovereign","sovereigns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"君主；國家統治者","explanation":"指統治一個國家的君主，是“擁有最高統治權的人”這一核心概念的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The sovereign opened the new session of Parliament.","zh":"君主主持了新一屆議會會議的開幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The people pledged loyalty to their sovereign.","zh":"人民向他們的君主宣誓效忠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sovereign","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7a8465f59c4743e8825","word":"sovereignty","forms":["sovereignty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b6dbfd23a4455f58","term":"sovereignty","forms":["sovereignty","sovereignties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主權；最高統治權","explanation":"指一個國家、人民或統治者作為最高權威、獨立作出最終決定的狀態或權力，重點是“誰擁有最終決定權”。","examples":[{"en":"The country defended its sovereignty against foreign interference.","zh":"這個國家捍衛自己的主權，反對外國干涉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sovereignty ultimately belongs to the people.","zh":"主權最終屬於人民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sovereignty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcd05523b82bce4d","term":"sovereignty","forms":["sovereignty","sovereignties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家或人民的自主決定權","explanation":"這是核心義的較寬泛說法，強調一個國家或人民有權自行決定政治制度、法律和公共事務，而不受外部權力支配。","examples":[{"en":"The agreement respects the sovereignty of each member state.","zh":"這項協議尊重每個成員國的主權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treaty affirmed the island's sovereignty.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sovereignty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-756e1aca491f16516fc8","word":"sow","forms":["sow"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16146cbb570a1f6a","term":"sow","forms":["sow","sows","sowing","sowed","sown"],"pos":"verb","zh":"播種","explanation":"sow 指把種子撒在土地裡，使它們在那裡生長。記住“把東西撒進田裡”這個動作，就能理解它後面的比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"They sowed the wheat in early spring.","zh":"他們在早春播下了小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer sows these seeds by hand.","zh":"農夫用手播種這些種子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aef2fb9dd3aabf7d7b1c","word":"soybean","forms":["soybean"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c46bbd2fb1a25853","term":"soybean","forms":["soybean","soybeans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大豆植株","explanation":"指大豆這種豆科作物本身，即地裡生長、結出豆莢的植物；這裡的畫面重點是“整株大豆”。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers plant soybean in the spring and harvest it in the fall.","zh":"農民在春天種植大豆，秋天收穫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soybeans flowered during the warmest part of summer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soybean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-147fa37218429ffe","term":"soybean","forms":["soybean","soybeans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大豆種子","explanation":"指從大豆植株上收下來的可食用種子，也就是通常所說的“大豆粒”；它可以作為食物或加工原料。","examples":[{"en":"Soybeans are used to make tofu, oil, and animal feed.","zh":"大豆可用來製作豆腐、豆油和動物飼料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The seeds in this sack are soybeans.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soybean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f49dbbfe051cb20cc03","word":"space","forms":["space"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0d3a99f8f08ec10","term":"space","forms":["space","spaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"空間；空隙","explanation":"space 是事物之間或周圍被拉開的範圍，可以是真實的物理空間，也可以泛指某種抽象的餘地。","examples":[{"en":"There isn't enough space between the two chairs.","zh":"兩把椅子之間沒有足夠的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave some space for the next car.","zh":"請給下一輛車留些空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ec0b630a4664d7b","term":"space","forms":["space","spaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體區域；場地","explanation":"當空處被限定了用途、邊界或位置時，space 就是一個具體的區域、空位或場地，例如展覽空間、公共空間。","examples":[{"en":"The library has created a quiet space for students.","zh":"圖書館為學生設立了一個安靜的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need more storage space in the kitchen.","zh":"我們需要在廚房增加一些儲物空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03f0d2e44978d926","term":"space","forms":["space","spaces","spacing","spaced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使保持間距","explanation":"space 作動詞時可以把物體拉開，按一定距離擺放，使它們之間留下空處。","examples":[{"en":"Space the plants about thirty centimeters apart.","zh":"把這些植物間隔約三十釐米種植。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chairs were evenly spaced around the table.","zh":"椅子均勻地分佈在桌子周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-babf4182ae1b482c","term":"space","forms":["space","spaces","spacing","spaced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加空格；留出文字間隔","explanation":"在書寫或排版中，space 表示在文字、詞語或行之間加入空格或空白，讓內容不擠在一起。","examples":[{"en":"Please space the words more clearly.","zh":"請把這些詞的間隔排得更清楚一些。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Space the letters evenly across the heading.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-296c65277b016fc41aad","word":"spacecraft/spaceship","forms":["spacecraft","spaceship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6fd227cad18d3cb0","term":"spacecraft","forms":["spacecraft","spacecrafts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"太空飛行器","explanation":"在地球大氣層以外飛行或執行的交通工具或裝置，既可以載人，也可以無人駕駛；探測器、飛船等都屬於這一概念。","examples":[{"en":"The spacecraft entered orbit around Mars.","zh":"這艘太空飛行器進入了繞火星執行的軌道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are preparing the spacecraft for launch.","zh":"科學家正在為發射準備這艘太空飛行器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spacecraft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-153411341810c0b5","term":"spaceship","forms":["spaceship","spaceships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"載人航天器","explanation":"指能夠載人並在太空中飛行的飛行器，是這個詞最主要、最容易遇到的意思；可以把它直接想成穿過太空的飛船。","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts entered the spaceship before sunrise.","zh":"宇航員在日出前進入了飛船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spaceship will carry three people to the space station.","zh":"這艘飛船將把三個人送到空間站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spaceship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d63f00430230ade7298f","word":"spacious","forms":["spacious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d9a1248342ef965","term":"spacious","forms":["spacious","more spacious","most spacious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬敞的；不擁擠的","explanation":"表示室內或其他實際空間很充足，活動和放置物品都有餘地，因此讓人感覺寬敞、不擁擠。","examples":[{"en":"The apartment has a spacious bedroom.","zh":"這套公寓有一間寬敞的臥室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We chose this car because the back seat is spacious.","zh":"我們選這輛車是因為後排座位很寬敞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spacious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3d373af663e089fb2a10","word":"spade","forms":["spade"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8df8b3544bd17b8","term":"spade","forms":["spade","spades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"翻土鏟","explanation":"spade是一種有長柄和平直刀刃的園藝工具，用來切入並翻鬆土地；它的核心畫面就是“扁平的刃插進土裡”。","examples":[{"en":"She used a spade to turn over the soil.","zh":"她用鏟子把土翻了一遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the spade by the garden gate.","zh":"把鏟子放在花園門旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c164fbd2cd6e0c23","term":"spade","forms":["spade","spades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黑桃","explanation":"在撲克牌中，spade指帶有♠符號的黑色花色，也可以指一張黑桃牌；這個符號的尖扁形狀讓它和“鏟刃”的畫面聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"I drew a spade from the deck.","zh":"我從牌堆裡抽到了一張黑桃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She played the ace of spades.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b4c539948ae24d8c7f3","word":"spaghetti","forms":["spaghetti"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0da3727e866926ed","term":"spaghetti","forms":["spaghetti","spaghettis"],"pos":"noun","zh":"義大利麵","explanation":"一種做成長條細線狀的義大利麵，是spaghetti最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We had spaghetti with tomato sauce for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐吃了番茄醬義大利麵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Drain the spaghetti and toss it with olive oil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spaghetti","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2100c349fb33b5c","term":"spaghetti","forms":["spaghetti","spaghettis"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細長條狀的義大利麵","explanation":"這是基本義的概括性用法，強調這種麵食的長而細的形狀，也可泛指不同種類或份量的這種面。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant offers three different spaghettis on its menu.","zh":"這家餐廳的選單上有三種不同的義大利麵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spaghetti needs another minute in boiling water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spaghetti","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37a0025aa1f2e29f9f88","word":"span","forms":["span"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b67ee968016fca38","term":"span","forms":["span","spans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手掌寬度","explanation":"span 最早的核心畫面是張開手後拇指尖到小指尖的距離，可作為一種非正式的長度單位。","examples":[{"en":"The gap between the two boards is about one span wide.","zh":"兩塊木板之間的縫隙大約有一掌寬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The kitten was barely a span in length.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/span","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e146734bd2b20a6","term":"span","forms":["span","spans","spanning","spanned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"橫跨","explanation":"動詞 span 把名詞“伸展開的範圍”變成動作，表示某物從一邊延伸到另一邊，橫跨一個空間。","examples":[{"en":"The suspension bridge spans the canyon.","zh":"這座懸索橋橫跨峽谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stone bridge spans the narrow gorge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/span","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fa202148e5bf880","term":"span","forms":["span","spans","spanning","spanned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"延續並覆蓋一段時間","explanation":"同樣的“從一端伸到另一端”也可以用於時間，表示某件事持續並覆蓋一段時期。","examples":[{"en":"Her career spanned more than three decades.","zh":"她的職業生涯持續了三十多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The correspondence spans the years between the two wars.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/span","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf2d9706736982fb2616","word":"spare","forms":["spare"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-971e1902b8bacc7e","term":"spare","forms":["spare","sparer","sparest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"額外的；備用的","explanation":"指沒有立即用掉、可以留待以後使用的東西，因此既可以是“多出來的”，也可以是“備用的”。","examples":[{"en":"Do you have a spare minute to look at this?","zh":"你有沒有空出一分鐘幫我看看這個？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep a spare key with a trusted friend.","zh":"把一把備用鑰匙放在信得過的朋友那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67bb1778f243d4bd","term":"spare","forms":["spare","sparer","sparest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不充裕的；簡樸的","explanation":"指數量少、安排不滿或裝飾不多，呈現出一種“只留下必要部分”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"They lived on a spare diet of soup and bread.","zh":"他們過著只吃湯和麵包的簡樸飲食生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monks lived on spare meals of bread and broth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65d17cd884ddb1a6","term":"spare","forms":["spare","spares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"未使用的東西；餘量","explanation":"指尚未被使用或花掉、因此還保留下來的東西，例如剩餘的錢、時間或物資。","examples":[{"en":"We have a spare, so you can use this one.","zh":"我們還有一個備用的，所以你可以用這個。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep a spare in case the first bulb breaks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7a1e897fa94ad13","term":"spare","forms":["spare","spares","sparing","spared","sparest","sparedst","spareth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"省下；保留","explanation":"指不使用、不消耗或不犧牲某物，把它留到以後；也可表示省下時間、金錢或精力。","examples":[{"en":"Can you spare five minutes for a quick call?","zh":"你能抽出五分鐘快速通個電話嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spared no expense on the wedding.","zh":"她為這場婚禮不惜花費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92f473809e5979a7da2b","word":"spark","forms":["spark"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7cb4c00ca907b17c","term":"spark","forms":["spark","sparks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火星；火花","explanation":"指燃燒、摩擦或高溫產生的一小粒發亮物質，可能點燃別的東西。","examples":[{"en":"A spark from the campfire landed on his jacket.","zh":"篝火裡飛出的一粒火星落在了他的夾克上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dry grass caught fire when a spark touched it.","zh":"乾草碰到火花後著火了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4200a4afdf4acb6","term":"spark","forms":["spark","sparks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"萌芽；誘因","explanation":"比喻一個很小的念頭、感情或跡象，後來可能像火花點燃火一樣發展成更大的變化。","examples":[{"en":"That first conversation was the spark of their friendship.","zh":"第一次談話成了他們友誼的起點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher's question gave the class a spark of curiosity.","zh":"老師的問題點燃了全班的一點好奇心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cd5c60ebab73c05","term":"spark","forms":["spark","sparks","sparking","sparked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引發；激起","explanation":"像火花點燃火一樣，使爭論、興趣、行動或其他變化突然開始。","examples":[{"en":"The article sparked a lively debate online.","zh":"這篇文章在網上引發了熱烈的討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her question sparked my interest in astronomy.","zh":"她的問題激起了我對天文學的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aefe4867ea407215f6c8","word":"sparkle","forms":["sparkle"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7350eee364859e79","term":"sparkle","forms":["sparkle","sparkles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小火星；閃光點","explanation":"指從火焰或其他發熱物中飛出的細小火星，也可指一次細小而明亮的閃光；這是“像火星一樣閃爍”這一核心形象的起點。","examples":[{"en":"A few sparkles flew up from the fire.","zh":"幾粒火星從火堆裡飛了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sparkle of light caught my eye.","zh":"一閃光亮吸引了我的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sparkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-861b679404634690","term":"sparkle","forms":["sparkle","sparkles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光彩；光澤","explanation":"指物體表面像飛出火星一樣明亮耀眼的光澤，尤其常用於寶石、眼睛或水面等。","examples":[{"en":"The sparkle of the necklace caught everyone's attention.","zh":"項鍊的閃耀光澤吸引了所有人的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cleaning restored the gemstones' sparkle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sparkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4841a473f28eabc6","term":"sparkle","forms":["sparkle","sparkles","sparkling","sparkled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迸出火星","explanation":"指燃燒的木頭等真正迸出細小火星，是名詞“火星”形象直接變成動作。","examples":[{"en":"The dry branches sparked and sparkled in the fire.","zh":"幹樹枝在火中噼啪作響，迸出點點火星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The grinder sparkled as its wheel met the steel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sparkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c84169e3f7e5123","term":"sparkle","forms":["sparkle","sparkles","sparkling","sparkled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閃閃發光","explanation":"指星星、寶石、水面等像不斷丟擲火星一樣發出明亮的閃光，也可譯為閃爍。","examples":[{"en":"Snow sparkled in the morning sun.","zh":"積雪在晨光中閃閃發亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stars sparkled above the quiet lake.","zh":"星星在寧靜的湖面上方閃爍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sparkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0454d527a7fa92d74a43","word":"sparrow","forms":["sparrow"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d554bbb767d4aaab","term":"sparrow","forms":["sparrow","sparrows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麻雀","explanation":"指家麻雀這種常見的小鳥，體形小，羽毛通常呈棕色、白色和灰色。看到城市、院子或屋邊的小麻雀時，通常就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"A sparrow landed on the garden fence.","zh":"一隻麻雀落在了花園的柵欄上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sparrows gathered under the tree.","zh":"麻雀們聚集在樹下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sparrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35040e037221ca69","term":"sparrow","forms":["sparrow","sparrows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雀科小型鳴禽","explanation":"在較寬的鳥類分類意義上，指雀科中的小型舊大陸鳴禽；這個意思比日常所說的某一隻麻雀更寬。","examples":[{"en":"This bird is a member of the sparrow family.","zh":"這種鳥屬於雀科。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sparrow nested beneath the station roof.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sparrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21e5205f73d9edbf72bc","word":"speak","forms":["speak"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c4eda410fd35733","term":"speak","forms":["speak","speaks","speaking","spoke","spake","speakest","spokest","speaketh","-","spoken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開口說話","explanation":"這是最基本的意思：用聲音把詞語說出來，讓別人聽見。它關注“說話”這一動作，不一定說明具體說了什麼。","examples":[{"en":"She was too nervous to speak in front of the class.","zh":"她太緊張了，不敢在全班同學面前說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please speak clearly so everyone can hear you.","zh":"請說清楚一點，這樣大家都能聽見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-85b9277ff26f4ebc","term":"speak","forms":["speak","speaks","speaking","spoke","spake","speakest","spokest","speaketh","-","spoken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交談","explanation":"這裡的 speak 是兩個人或幾個人互相說話、進行交流，重點從單方面發聲擴充套件到雙方談話。","examples":[{"en":"I haven't spoken with Maya since she moved away.","zh":"瑪雅搬走後，我就一直沒和她談過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could I speak to the manager, please?","zh":"請問我可以和經理談談嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d0663a2789ef579","term":"speak","forms":["speak","speaks","speaking","spoke","spake","speakest","spokest","speaketh","-","spoken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"會說某種語言","explanation":"這裡表示一個人有能力用某種語言交流；語言本身直接放在 speak 後面，熟練程度可以另行說明。","examples":[{"en":"My neighbor speaks three languages fluently.","zh":"我的鄰居能流利地說三種語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you speak Spanish?","zh":"你會說西班牙語嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-291ea5ef94dffda4f444","word":"speaker","forms":["speaker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ead8e6c741a105c0","term":"speaker","forms":["speaker","speakers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說話的人","explanation":"speaker首先就是“正在說話的人”或“能夠使用某種語言的人”。它強調發出語言的人，不一定是在正式演講；例如討論、採訪中開口的人都可以是speaker。","examples":[{"en":"There were three speakers at the meeting.","zh":"會議上有三位發言者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a native speaker of Spanish.","zh":"她以西班牙語為母語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speaker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d223e9920d426b9d","term":"speaker","forms":["speaker","speakers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揚聲器；音箱","explanation":"speaker也指把電訊號轉換成聲音並播放出來的揚聲器或音箱。這裡不是“會說話的人”，而是“把聲音發出來的裝置”，正好延續了“發出聲音”的記憶線索。","examples":[{"en":"The left speaker is not working.","zh":"左邊的音箱壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please turn down the speakers.","zh":"請把音箱的聲音調小一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speaker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f2cc936b1968c90ae37","word":"spear","forms":["spear"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de1bba2db0ab0b1f","term":"spear","forms":["spear","spears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長矛；矛刺動作","explanation":"一種細長而有尖端的武器，用來投擲或向前刺；也可泛指用長而尖的東西向前猛刺的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The hunter carried a spear through the forest.","zh":"獵人帶著一根長矛穿過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sharp spear of light pierced the darkness.","zh":"一道尖銳的光束刺破了黑暗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b774bb52743a364","term":"spear","forms":["spear","spears","spearing","speared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用矛刺","explanation":"用長矛刺穿或刺中某人、某動物或某物，直接延續了“尖端向前刺入”的核心意象。","examples":[{"en":"The warrior speared the fish before it could swim away.","zh":"那名戰士在魚遊走前用矛刺中了它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hunters were forbidden to spear the animals.","zh":"獵人們被禁止用矛刺殺那些動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d4c5c8894e016e772e9","word":"special","forms":["special"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95a0a7d5a9254e1a","term":"special","forms":["special","more special","specialer","most special","specialest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別的；獨特的","explanation":"指某人或某物有不同尋常的性質，因而被單獨注意或區別出來。","examples":[{"en":"The network aired a special episode for the show's anniversary.","zh":"電視臺為該節目週年紀念播出了一集特別節目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We made special arrangements for guests with young children.","zh":"我們為帶小孩的客人作了特殊安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/special","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9741bc0aaf294c2","term":"special","forms":["special","more special","specialer","most special","specialest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特殊的；珍愛的","explanation":"強調某人或某物對某個人有特別價值，常含親愛、珍視或重要的感情色彩。","examples":[{"en":"This old photograph is special to my family.","zh":"這張老照片對我們家來說很珍貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This little necklace has a special place in her heart.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/special","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ace72b3572c18de8b376","word":"specialist","forms":["specialist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-47c5b703948c36dd","term":"specialist","forms":["specialist","specialists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專家；專門人才","explanation":"指在某一特定學科、工作或研究領域擁有深入知識，或主要從事這一領域的人。核心畫面仍是把能力集中到一個窄領域。","examples":[{"en":"We asked a specialist in antique furniture to assess the desk.","zh":"我們請一位古董傢俱專家來評估這張書桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a specialist in child language development.","zh":"她是兒童語言發展方面的專家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specialist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ccd69193910d5fa9e155","word":"specialize","forms":["specialize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-464a51c6f6e68ce9","term":"specialize","forms":["specialize","specializes","specializing","specialized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使專門化","explanation":"把原本可以承擔多種功能的事物分化成專門承擔某一種功能；例如，一個器官經過分工後，就會專門負責某項任務。","examples":[{"en":"Over time, the cells specialize for different functions.","zh":"隨著時間推移，這些細胞會專門化，分別承擔不同的功能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The equipment is specialized for deep-sea research.","zh":"這套裝置是為深海研究而專門設計的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specialize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f480fe56bcde4860","term":"specialize","forms":["specialize","specializes","specializing","specialized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"專攻某領域","explanation":"指一個人或機構不再平均涉獵許多方面，而是把主要精力集中到某個專業領域。它是現代英語中最重要的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"She specializes in treating sports injuries.","zh":"她專門治療運動損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This firm specializes in renewable-energy projects.","zh":"這家公司專門從事可再生能源專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specialize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-435bee0ece4786884238","word":"specialty","forms":["specialty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8014e0f03d5b37d","term":"specialty","forms":["specialty","specialties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"專長；專門本領","explanation":"指一個人、機構或行業最擅長、最專門做的事情，也就是別人想到它時會聯想到的本領或領域。這是把“特別”貼在人身上的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Her specialty is designing small urban gardens.","zh":"她的專長是設計小型城市花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant's specialty is homemade pasta.","zh":"這家餐館的特色是自制義大利麵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specialty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf00e7c0866d8745","term":"specialty","forms":["specialty","specialties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地方特色產品","explanation":"指某個地方出產、製作，並且很能代表該地的產品或食品。它就像給產品貼上“這是這裡的特別招牌”的標籤。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh maple syrup is a specialty of the region.","zh":"新鮮楓糖漿是這個地區的特色產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Smoked cheese is a specialty of the mountain villages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specialty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1559d6aa3c36f76671d9","word":"species","forms":["species"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c325957dc5bec881","term":"species","forms":["species","specieses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物種；種類","explanation":"指具有共同特徵的一類生物、事物或人。","examples":[{"en":"The reserve protects several endangered bird species.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Scientists identified a new species of orchid in the valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/species","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-54b759dba2ded0937372","word":"specific","forms":["specific"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-799361dadfe878e7","term":"specific","forms":["specific","more specific","most specific"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明確具體的","explanation":"它把範圍或內容說得很清楚，讓人知道究竟指哪一項，而不是隻給出籠統說法。","examples":[{"en":"Could you give me a specific example?","zh":"你能給我一個具體的例子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The instructions are not specific enough.","zh":"這些說明還不夠具體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specific","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2930f36abb13d84e","term":"specific","forms":["specific","more specific","most specific"],"pos":"adj","zh":"針對特定物件的","explanation":"它表示某件事是為某個明確物件、用途或情況準備的，重點在“對準了誰或什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"We need a plan specific to this project.","zh":"我們需要一份針對這個專案的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The training is specific for new employees.","zh":"這項培訓是專門為新員工安排的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specific","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-a0aa99c86e2c4dd6e56c","word":"specify","forms":["specify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02d85728eedcd8bd","term":"specify","forms":["specify","specifies","specifying","specified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"明確說明；具體規定","explanation":"把原本籠統的內容、要求、條件或細節清楚地說出或寫出，讓別人知道準確範圍。這是 specify 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please specify the size and color you need.","zh":"請明確說明你需要的尺寸和顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The form does not specify where the documents should be sent.","zh":"表格沒有明確說明檔案應該寄到哪裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bde7c1c15bcd85e5","term":"specify","forms":["specify","specifies","specifying","specified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寫入規範；規定標準","explanation":"把某項要求或標準正式寫進規範、設計檔案或制度中，使它成為之後執行時的明確依據。這裡不只是“說出來”，而是把它納入一套正式的規定。","examples":[{"en":"The contract specifies the type of materials to be used.","zh":"合同規定了應使用的材料型別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contract specifies stainless steel for all external fittings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c6a8279d628d1606538","word":"specimen","forms":["specimen"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5dfcf61943c79d5","term":"specimen","forms":["specimen","specimens","specimina"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表一類的例項","explanation":"指某一類事物中的一個具體個體，可以用來代表或說明這一類；重點是“拿出一個來觀察，就能看出這一類的特點”。","examples":[{"en":"This painting is an early specimen of Picasso's art.","zh":"這幅畫是畢加索早期藝術作品的一個例項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a rare specimen of this pottery.","zh":"這家博物館收藏著這種陶器的一件稀有例項。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specimen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd97c30520a6d2e1","term":"specimen","forms":["specimen","specimens","specimina"],"pos":"noun","zh":"送檢樣本；標本","explanation":"指從人體、動物、植物或其他材料中取出的、用於檢查和分析的一小份樣本；它是“拿出來觀察”的核心概念在檢測場景中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse collected a specimen for testing.","zh":"護士採集了一份樣本送檢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The technician labeled each blood specimen carefully.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/specimen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52cfa9440177ced9b969","word":"spectacle","forms":["spectacle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9fb703b03f6fe97b","term":"spectacle","forms":["spectacle","spectacles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壯觀場面；精彩表演","explanation":"指吸引眾人觀看、令人興奮或驚歎的場面、表演或事件。它強調“值得一看、很有視覺衝擊力的一幕”，不一定只指正式演出。","examples":[{"en":"The fireworks created a spectacular spectacle over the harbor.","zh":"煙花在港口上空形成了壯觀的景象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The championship match was a spectacle that drew thousands of fans.","zh":"那場冠軍賽十分精彩，吸引了數千名球迷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectacle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1308cb047498194","term":"spectacle","forms":["spectacle","spectacles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"丟臉的場面；鬧劇","explanation":"指令人尷尬、難看或不體面的場面，常常是某人在眾人面前失控或出醜造成的。它仍然保留“被人圍觀看的一幕”這個核心，只是觀看者感到的不是驚歎，而是難堪。","examples":[{"en":"He made a spectacle of himself by shouting at the waiter.","zh":"他沖服務員大喊大叫，當眾出了醜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The argument turned into an ugly spectacle in front of the children.","zh":"這場爭吵在孩子們面前變成了一出難看的鬧劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectacle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52f7e22d230c8ec9162d","word":"spectacular","forms":["spectacular"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0124e22b7080455","term":"spectacular","forms":["spectacular","more spectacular","most spectacular"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精彩壯觀的","explanation":"形容場面、景色、表演或成就等非常精彩、引人注目，像被聚光燈照亮一樣讓人驚歎。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a spectacular sunset from the beach.","zh":"我們在海灘上看到了壯觀的日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her final performance was absolutely spectacular.","zh":"她的最後一場演出精彩極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectacular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45f5fcafed1449c2","term":"spectacular","forms":["spectacular","spectaculars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精彩展示；壯觀表演","explanation":"指一場本身就值得觀看、能吸引大量注意的精彩展示或表演，也就是“聚光燈下的那個大場面”。","examples":[{"en":"The festival ended with a spectacular of lights and music.","zh":"節日以一場燈光與音樂交織的精彩表演收尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival ended with a fireworks spectacular.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectacular","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-929f9a342442b12741c1","word":"spectator","forms":["spectator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55eb27aa520200b7","term":"spectator","forms":["spectator","spectators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀眾","explanation":"指在比賽、演出、煙火等活動現場觀看的人，通常不親自參加活動，而是在場邊看並可能加油。","examples":[{"en":"The spectators cheered when the runner crossed the finish line.","zh":"跑步者衝過終點線時，觀眾們歡呼起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thousands of spectators gathered to watch the fireworks.","zh":"數千名觀眾聚集起來觀看煙火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bffc718ca427d2b1","term":"spectator","forms":["spectator","spectators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旁觀者；觀察者","explanation":"泛指在旁邊觀看或觀察某件事的人，不一定身處正式活動現場；可以只是看著某種景象或事情發生。","examples":[{"en":"As a spectator, she could only watch the argument from a distance.","zh":"作為旁觀者，她只能遠遠地看著這場爭論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She remained a spectator rather than joining the argument.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1fd6202c9bb335c65040","word":"spectrum","forms":["spectrum"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-246259569d3f668f","term":"spectrum","forms":["spectrum","spectra","spectrums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續範圍","explanation":"spectrum可以是一條從一個極端延伸到另一個極端的連續範圍，重點不在幾個孤立專案，而在中間存在許多漸變可能。","examples":[{"en":"The policy has support across a broad political spectrum.","zh":"這項政策得到了政治光譜中各個立場的支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The disease can cause a spectrum of symptoms.","zh":"這種疾病可能引起一系列從輕到重的症狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectrum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b22f7ec4de5a794","term":"spectrum","forms":["spectrum","spectra","spectrums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"光譜","explanation":"在物理中，spectrum是光或其他電磁輻射按頻率展開後形成的連續範圍；可特指可見光的顏色帶，也可指整個電磁頻譜中的某一部分。","examples":[{"en":"A prism separates white light into the colors of the visible spectrum.","zh":"稜鏡把白光分解成可見光譜中的各種顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Radio waves occupy a low-frequency part of the electromagnetic spectrum.","zh":"無線電波位於電磁頻譜中低頻的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spectrum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-355ac7d4d96254b3dc63","word":"speculate","forms":["speculate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a0add75cc2f3ee6","term":"speculate","forms":["speculate","speculates","speculating","speculated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推測；猜想","explanation":"當證據不完整、無法確定事實時，speculate 表示根據現有線索提出一種可能解釋，而不是斷言事情一定如此。","examples":[{"en":"Experts speculate that the storm will weaken before reaching the coast.","zh":"專家推測，這場風暴到達海岸前會減弱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People are speculating about why the company delayed the launch.","zh":"人們正在猜測這家公司為什麼推遲了釋出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speculate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a92bae4caf82f124","term":"speculate","forms":["speculate","speculates","speculating","speculated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投機；冒險交易","explanation":"在金融或商業語境中，speculate 表示承擔較大風險進行買賣，希望價格變化帶來利潤；這裡的“猜測”從判斷走向了用錢下注。","examples":[{"en":"He made a fortune by speculating in property during the boom.","zh":"繁榮時期，他靠房地產投機賺了一大筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He speculated in commodities and lost heavily.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speculate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05fb617ad543807c0c3f","word":"speech","forms":["speech"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-75c388fb82729153","term":"speech","forms":["speech","speeches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說話能力","explanation":"指人用聲音說出詞語、進行交流的能力；這裡關注的是“能不能說、說話是否受影響”，而不是某一次具體講話。","examples":[{"en":"The injury affected her speech.","zh":"這次受傷影響了她的說話能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stroke affected his speech but spared his hearing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speech","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b3f59f40ce3a569","term":"speech","forms":["speech","speeches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說話；言語方式","explanation":"指實際說話這一行為，或一個人說話時的聲音、速度和表達方式；它仍然是從嘴裡出來的語言這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Her speech was so quiet that I could barely hear her.","zh":"她說話聲音太小了，我幾乎聽不見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor changed his speech for the role.","zh":"那名演員為了這個角色改變了說話方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speech","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01f7f47771d3602f","term":"speech","forms":["speech","speeches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"演講；講話","explanation":"指一個人在公眾面前連續說出的一段正式話語；普通的 speech 是“說話”，集中起來面對聽眾就是“一次演講”。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a short speech at the award ceremony.","zh":"她在頒獎典禮上發表了簡短講話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His speech focused on the need for better schools.","zh":"他的演講重點談到了改善學校的需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speech","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbccb9c002d5ed599478","word":"speed","forms":["speed"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4f441b39d63e7b0","term":"speed","forms":["speed","speeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"快速移動","explanation":"指快速移動的狀態或快速移動的能力，重點是“動得很快”。","examples":[{"en":"The horse ran at full speed toward the fence.","zh":"那匹馬全速朝柵欄跑去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was amazed by how quickly he moved at that speed.","zh":"他以那樣的速度移動，讓她感到驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01547a4899fcf16c","term":"speed","forms":["speed","speeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"速度數值","explanation":"指運動或行動的具體快慢，通常可以用距離和時間來衡量，例如車輛每小時行駛多少公里。","examples":[{"en":"The speed limit on this road is 50 miles per hour.","zh":"這條路的限速是每小時五十英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please reduce your speed near the school.","zh":"經過學校附近時請降低車速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77a97785870965e5","term":"speed","forms":["speed","speeds","speeding","sped","speeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"快速行駛","explanation":"表示人、車輛或其他事物快速移動，和名詞“速度”的核心概念直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"A motorcycle sped past us on the highway.","zh":"一輛摩托車在高速公路上從我們身邊飛馳而過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train sped through the countryside.","zh":"火車飛快地駛過鄉間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba17444f68827904","term":"speed","forms":["speed","speeds","speeding","sped","speeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"超速","explanation":"特指駕駛車輛超過規定的速度限制，是“快速移動”在交通語境中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"He was stopped for speeding on his way home.","zh":"他回家路上因超速被攔下了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don’t speed on this narrow, wet road.","zh":"這條路又窄又溼，別超速。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80168cb3e6619972","term":"speed","forms":["speed","speeds","speeding","sped","speeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使加快","explanation":"表示讓某個過程、動作或事物以更快的速度進行，即“加快某事”。","examples":[{"en":"The new system will speed up the checkout process.","zh":"新系統會加快結賬流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind sped the boat toward the shore.","zh":"風使船加速駛向岸邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f4a0aaa62c4ceef8857","word":"spell","forms":["spell"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-988203e010e329c3","term":"spell","forms":["spell","spells","spelling","spelled","spelt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拼寫","explanation":"spell 最常見的動詞義是按正確順序寫出或說出一個詞的字母；它就是把詞語的“組成字母”逐個說出來。","examples":[{"en":"Could you spell your last name for me?","zh":"你能把你的姓怎麼拼寫告訴我嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I always spell this word incorrectly.","zh":"我總是把這個詞拼錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1bc4dc7f94f0f8a","term":"spell","forms":["spell","spells","spelling","spelled","spelt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組成拼出","explanation":"當主語是字母時，spell 表示這些字母組合起來構成某個詞；也就是“這些字母拼成了什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"The letters C, A, T spell “cat.”","zh":"字母 C、A、T 拼成了“cat”。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The initials spell the name of the organization.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a6105b32383e5e20e540","word":"spelling","forms":["spelling"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6dc267beabd1460d","term":"spelling","forms":["spelling","spellings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拼寫活動或能力","explanation":"指用字母寫出詞語、讀出詞中字母，或學習和掌握這套規則的活動與能力。它強調“把詞裝進字母裡”這一整件事，而不是某一個詞的寫法。","examples":[{"en":"I need to improve my spelling before the exam.","zh":"考試前我需要提高拼寫能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She checked the spelling of every word in the report.","zh":"她檢查了報告中每個詞的拼寫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spelling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc9ac53a03436558","term":"spelling","forms":["spelling","spellings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拼法；拼寫形式","explanation":"指一個詞實際採用的字母寫法，尤其強調這種寫法是否正確，或不同地區、時代和文字之間採用的寫法是否不同。它是“拼寫活動”落在某個詞上的具體結果。","examples":[{"en":"Can you tell me the correct spelling of this word?","zh":"你能告訴我這個詞的正確拼法嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spelling of some names has changed over time.","zh":"有些名字的拼法隨著時間發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spelling","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f64a33ff88c38111769d","word":"spend","forms":["spend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6184ea9c69253e8d","term":"spend","forms":["spend","spends","spending","spent"],"pos":"verb","zh":"花費（金錢）","explanation":"指把錢支付出去，用於購買、活動或某個目的；這是 spend 最常見的動詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"She spends too much money on takeout.","zh":"她在外賣上花的錢太多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent nearly three hundred dollars repairing the car.","zh":"我們修車花了將近三百美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69695141880cbbca","term":"spend","forms":["spend","spends","spending","spent"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投入；用於","explanation":"指把時間、精力、判斷力等資源投入某件事，而不一定涉及金錢；本質上仍是把手裡的資源用出去。","examples":[{"en":"I spend most evenings reading or walking.","zh":"我大多數晚上都用來閱讀或散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team spent months developing the new software.","zh":"這個團隊花了幾個月開發新軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa946e0a39f3d90d","term":"spend","forms":["spend","spends","spending","spent"],"pos":"verb","zh":"度過（時間）；用掉","explanation":"指把一段時間用於某項活動，也就是讓時間像資源一樣被消耗掉。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon exploring the old town.","zh":"我們用整個下午遊覽了老城區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spends too much time checking his phone.","zh":"他花太多時間檢視手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f58b78bc54e0c3e5556","word":"sphere","forms":["sphere"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d692ff199d027894","term":"sphere","forms":["sphere","spheres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球面","explanation":"在三維空間裡，球面上的每一點到同一個中心的距離都相等；它指的是包住空間的外層表面，而不是表面裡面的全部內容。","examples":[{"en":"The points on a sphere are all the same distance from its center.","zh":"球面上的各點到其中心的距離都相等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"On a sphere, a triangle's angles can total more than 180 degrees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sphere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcad8d0cb927cba6","term":"sphere","forms":["sphere","spheres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"球狀物；球","explanation":"指外形近似球面的具體物體，重點是它整體呈圓球狀，而不強調數學上是否嚴格符合球面的定義。","examples":[{"en":"The sculpture is a smooth bronze sphere.","zh":"這件雕塑是一個光滑的青銅球體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A glass sphere hung above the shop entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sphere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87474ad1ef75c621","term":"sphere","forms":["sphere","spheres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"活動範圍；影響領域","explanation":"從“包圍在球面內的空間”引申而來，指個人、組織或國家實際活動或能夠施加影響的範圍。sphere of influence 就是“勢力範圍”，這裡的 sphere 是抽象的領域。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries are competing for influence in the region.","zh":"兩國正在爭奪該地區的勢力範圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Education lies outside this committee's sphere of responsibility.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sphere","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-58e989955f4b358feb6e","word":"spice","forms":["spice"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6145920ef910416","term":"spice","forms":["spice","spices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香料；調味植物材料","explanation":"指通常經過乾燥、帶有香氣或刺激性味道、用來給食物調味的植物材料。它可以指某一種香料，也可以泛指香料這類東西。","examples":[{"en":"Add a little spice to the soup before serving.","zh":"上桌前往湯里加一點香料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cinnamon is a common spice in desserts.","zh":"肉桂是甜點中常用的一種香料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e04b9456968ba8f","term":"spice","forms":["spice","spices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辛辣程度；刺激性味道","explanation":"指食物嚐起來有多辣或多有刺激性，也就是香料帶來的那種刺激感。","examples":[{"en":"You can choose the spice level when you order the curry.","zh":"點咖哩時可以選擇辣度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sauce has too much spice for me.","zh":"這個醬對我來說太辣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-942ab0a504f5ee95","term":"spice","forms":["spice","spices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"趣味；吸引力","explanation":"像香料讓食物更有味道一樣，某種新鮮、變化或特別之處也能給生活或活動增添趣味和吸引力。","examples":[{"en":"Travel adds spice to everyday life.","zh":"旅行為日常生活增添了趣味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A little surprise can add spice to the story.","zh":"一點意外能讓這個故事更有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49741bdbe48a4c98","term":"spice","forms":["spice","spices","spicing","spiced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"加香料調味","explanation":"指把香料加入食物，使食物更香或更有刺激性味道；這就是從“香料”這一核心概念直接發展出的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Spice the vegetables with garlic and pepper.","zh":"用大蒜和胡椒給蔬菜調味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chef spiced the rice with saffron.","zh":"廚師用藏紅花給米飯調味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2efa64f91736e51bfbca","word":"spicy","forms":["spicy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f845a434a77bd92","term":"spicy","forms":["spicy","spicier","spiciest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含香料的；香料味濃的","explanation":"指食物含有香料，或香料味道明顯，是 spicy 最基本、最穩妥的用法。","examples":[{"en":"He prepared a spicy casserole.","zh":"他做了一鍋香料味濃的焗菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I ordered a spicy noodle dish with extra herbs.","zh":"我點了一份香料味濃、還加了額外香草的面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spicy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-124b42f330a45fbc","term":"spicy","forms":["spicy","spicier","spiciest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"辛辣的；辣得刺激的","explanation":"指食物中的辣味會在口腔裡產生灼熱或刺痛感，尤其常用於含辣椒素的食物。","examples":[{"en":"This curry is too spicy for me.","zh":"這道咖哩對我來說太辣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you make the salsa less spicy?","zh":"你能把這份莎莎醬做得不那麼辣嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spicy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9bfa0b50a90e669907e7","word":"spider","forms":["spider"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3e736dcb4e25e9f","term":"spider","forms":["spider","spiders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜘蛛","explanation":"一種有八條腿的捕食性節肢動物，許多種類會織網捕捉獵物。這是 spider 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A small spider was crawling across the bathroom floor.","zh":"一隻小蜘蛛正在浴室地板上爬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are several spiders living under the old bridge.","zh":"那座舊橋下面住著好幾只蜘蛛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spider","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-234a838aaa5e6ae0a9a2","word":"spill","forms":["spill"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4e9a3a4b2758ebc","term":"spill","forms":["spill","spills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"灑出的東西；一攤灑落物","explanation":"指東西掉落或液體灑出後留在某處、造成凌亂的一攤，尤其常指灑出的液體。","examples":[{"en":"Please wipe up that spill before someone slips.","zh":"請把那攤灑出的東西擦乾淨，免得有人滑倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a small oil spill on the garage floor.","zh":"車庫地板上有一小攤灑出的油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4549d659648e8aa6","term":"spill","forms":["spill","spills","spilling","spilled","spilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把東西灑出","explanation":"指不小心把液體或其他東西弄掉，使它流開、散開並造成凌亂。","examples":[{"en":"I spilled tea on my shirt this morning.","zh":"我今天早上把茶灑到襯衫上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to spill the soup.","zh":"小心別把湯灑出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-809fa48412aa093c","term":"spill","forms":["spill","spills","spilling","spilled","spilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"自己灑出；散落出來","explanation":"指液體或物品自行從原處流出、掉出並散開，重點在結果而不是誰造成了它。","examples":[{"en":"The milk spilled onto the table when the cup tipped over.","zh":"杯子翻倒時，牛奶灑到了桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Coins spilled out of his pocket.","zh":"硬幣從他的口袋裡掉了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-784e1f0516d71647","term":"spill","forms":["spill","spills","spilling","spilled","spilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"湧出；湧到外面","explanation":"指人群、物體等從原本集中的地方大量湧出，越過原有邊界。","examples":[{"en":"Fans spilled out of the stadium after the match.","zh":"比賽結束後，球迷們從體育場裡湧了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crowd spilled onto the street.","zh":"人群湧到了街上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca1ac8dcbaa562ca","term":"spill","forms":["spill","spills","spilling","spilled","spilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洩露；全盤說出","explanation":"把原本藏在心裡或不該公開的資訊“倒”出來，尤其指洩露秘密、細節或個人感受。","examples":[{"en":"She spilled the secret to her best friend.","zh":"她把這個秘密告訴了最好的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come on, spill—what happened?","zh":"快說，到底發生了什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5a2729ffa0eeacc1532","word":"spin","forms":["spin"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a87a508722d0087","term":"spin","forms":["spin","spins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旋轉；打轉","explanation":"表示快速的圓周運動或物體不斷轉動的狀態；汽車、人在失去控制時也可以 go into a spin。這個意思直接延續了“旋轉”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The car went into a spin on the icy road.","zh":"汽車在結冰的路面上打起了轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dancer finished with a fast spin.","zh":"舞者最後快速旋轉了一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32ccfab55901edad","term":"spin","forms":["spin","spins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有利的解讀；輿論包裝","explanation":"指透過選擇特定說法或角度來呈現事實，使原本不利的事情看起來更容易被接受。這就是把事實“轉”到一個對自己有利的方向上。","examples":[{"en":"The company tried to put a positive spin on its falling sales.","zh":"這家公司試圖為銷量下滑作有利的包裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister's spokesperson gave the decision a reassuring spin.","zh":"部長的發言人用一種令人安心的說法來包裝這項決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f041ded2d85d40c7","term":"spin","forms":["spin","spins","spinning","spun","span","spinned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"旋轉；轉身","explanation":"表示人或物快速轉動，也可以指轉過身去面對另一個方向；記住“旋轉”這個核心畫面即可。","examples":[{"en":"The dancer spun around and faced the audience.","zh":"舞者轉過身來面對觀眾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coin spun on the table for several seconds.","zh":"硬幣在桌上轉了好幾秒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2571609ed0381388","term":"spin","forms":["spin","spins","spinning","spun","span","spinned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包裝；歪向性解讀","explanation":"表示用特定的說法或角度呈現事實，使它看起來更有利、更容易被接受；這就像把事實“轉”向某個有利方向。","examples":[{"en":"The company spun the delay as a necessary safety measure.","zh":"公司把這次延誤包裝成一項必要的安全措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The minister tried to put a positive spin on the poor results.","zh":"部長試圖用有利的說法來解讀糟糕的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a7feb4abff5cc24d4e8","word":"spinach","forms":["spinach"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d3c1e6e037ba428","term":"spinach","forms":["spinach","spinaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"菠菜；菠菜葉","explanation":"指菠菜這種可食用植物，或它的葉子；在日常英語中也常直接表示作為食材的菠菜。","examples":[{"en":"I added some spinach to the soup.","zh":"我往湯里加了一些菠菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wash the spinach before you cook it.","zh":"烹飪菠菜前先把它洗乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9c5ac37f591ec4d","term":"spinach","forms":["spinach","spinaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"類似菠菜的綠葉菜","explanation":"在較寬泛的用法中，spinach 也可以指其他被當作菠菜一樣食用，或外形、用途與菠菜相近的綠葉植物；核心仍是“可食用的綠葉”。","examples":[{"en":"This wild green is used as spinach in local cooking.","zh":"這種野生綠葉菜在當地烹飪中被當作菠菜使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New Zealand spinach grows well in hot weather.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0dd190c13c467edb0f2","word":"spine","forms":["spine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e1d9177bc175fdb","term":"spine","forms":["spine","spines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脊柱；脊椎","explanation":"指人從頸部延伸到骨盆、位於背部中央的一串骨骼；對動物來說，也可指從頭部延伸到尾部的類似結構。它像身體的主樑，既支撐身體，也保護脊髓。","examples":[{"en":"She injured her spine in a fall.","zh":"她摔倒時傷了脊柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The whale's spine runs almost the length of its body.","zh":"鯨的脊柱幾乎貫穿整個身體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d832e74ecb64745","term":"spine","forms":["spine","spines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"脊狀中央結構；主脊","explanation":"指形狀或作用像脊柱的長而突出的中央結構，例如山脈中的長脊，或某個整體中起支撐作用的中軸。","examples":[{"en":"A rocky spine runs along the center of the island.","zh":"一條岩石山脊貫穿島嶼中央。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road follows the mountain spine.","zh":"這條路沿著山脈主脊延伸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-afc01347cd6ba571","term":"spine","forms":["spine","spines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖刺；棘狀突起","explanation":"指動物、貝殼、蘑菇或植物上堅硬而尖的突出物；它和脊柱的共同點是都像一條堅硬、突出的“脊”。","examples":[{"en":"Wear gloves when handling this cactus because its spines are sharp.","zh":"拿這種仙人掌時要戴手套，因為它的刺很鋒利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cactus's spines pierced his glove.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f0e99f465a65c3cb8a7","word":"spiral","forms":["spiral"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-88032e408027360c","term":"spiral","forms":["spiral"],"pos":"adj","zh":"螺旋形的","explanation":"指像螺旋一樣圍繞中心盤繞、逐漸向外或向上展開的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The shell has a beautiful spiral shape.","zh":"這個貝殼有漂亮的螺旋形狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spiral staircase leads to the upper balcony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-677ecfa502e775de","term":"spiral","forms":["spiral","spirals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螺旋線","explanation":"指一個點繞著固定中心旋轉，同時與中心的距離不斷變化而形成的曲線；日常也可泛指平面上的螺旋圖形。","examples":[{"en":"She drew a spiral on the fogged-up window.","zh":"她在蒙上霧氣的窗戶上畫了一條螺旋線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shell's spiral widened toward its opening.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06820b8d3cad8050","term":"spiral","forms":["spiral","spirals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"不斷加劇的迴圈","explanation":"指某種過程一邊持續發展，一邊獲得越來越強的推動力，因此很難立刻停下來，常用於問題、情緒或局勢不斷惡化。","examples":[{"en":"Without help, his debts began a downward spiral.","zh":"沒有得到幫助，他的債務開始不斷惡化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rising prices triggered a spiral of wage demands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bfcbe6eb2fe5a4d","term":"spiral","forms":["spiral","spirals","spiraling","spiralling","spiraled","spiralled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"螺旋式移動","explanation":"指人、物體或氣流沿著螺旋或盤旋路線移動，通常同時改變高度或與中心的距離。","examples":[{"en":"The leaves spiraled down from the tree.","zh":"樹葉從樹上盤旋飄落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The helicopter spiraled upward until it cleared the ridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-887af9d22ca6de22","term":"spiral","forms":["spiral","spirals","spiraling","spiralling","spiraled","spiralled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"持續增加或惡化","explanation":"指數量、費用、債務或問題不斷上升，往往越升越快，最後變得難以控制；這裡保留了螺旋不斷擴大的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Food prices are spiraling out of control.","zh":"食品價格正在失控地不斷上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repair costs spiraled far beyond the original estimate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiral","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a68999add325ba9952dd","word":"spirit","forms":["spirit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2de601b2b5de8b7a","term":"spirit","forms":["spirit","spirits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"靈魂；精神","explanation":"指一個人或生物看不見的內在生命和自我；在較抽象的語境中，也可指人的精神力量。","examples":[{"en":"Her spirit stayed strong despite the illness.","zh":"儘管生病了，她的精神仍然很堅強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The poem speaks to the human spirit.","zh":"這首詩觸動了人類的精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-728773a2a1ff0c31","term":"spirit","forms":["spirit","spirits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熱情；團隊精神","explanation":"指使人積極投入、支援某項活動或群體的熱情和認同感，例如學校精神或團隊精神。","examples":[{"en":"The fans showed great team spirit during the match.","zh":"比賽期間，球迷表現出了很強的團隊精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their team spirit remained strong despite repeated defeats.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-563c1317711f8a00","term":"spirit","forms":["spirit","spirits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精神；風格","explanation":"指某種行為、作品或做法所體現的整體態度和風格，也就是它所傳達的精神氣質。","examples":[{"en":"In the spirit of cooperation, both sides shared their plans.","zh":"本著合作的精神，雙方分享了各自的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The renovation preserves the spirit of the original building.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-830d9c9fe9f74762","term":"spirit","forms":["spirit","spirits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本意；實質","explanation":"指規則、檔案或行動背後的真正意圖和實質，而不是表面上的字句或正式形式。","examples":[{"en":"They followed the spirit of the agreement, even if not every detail was covered.","zh":"他們遵守了協議的本意，雖然協議沒有涵蓋每個細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The decision respected the letter but violated the spirit of the law.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-908d6f7546387f24934e","word":"spiritual","forms":["spiritual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a759f4ac6244b246","term":"spiritual","forms":["spiritual","more spiritual","most spiritual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精神的；靈魂的","explanation":"表示與人的靈魂、內心信念或內在生命有關，而不是與身體或物質有關。它可以描述個人的內在追求，也可以描述某種重視靈魂層面的實踐。","examples":[{"en":"She began a spiritual journey after a difficult year.","zh":"經歷了艱難的一年後，她開始了一段內在的精神探索。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Meditation has helped him meet his spiritual needs.","zh":"冥想幫助他滿足了自己的精神需要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiritual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65c038a068df0b82","term":"spiritual","forms":["spiritual","more spiritual","most spiritual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"宗教的；神聖的","explanation":"表示與上帝、宗教信仰或禮拜場所有關，也可表示具有神聖性質。在基督教語境中，還可以特指受聖靈啟發的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The temple is an important spiritual place for local families.","zh":"這座寺廟是當地家庭重要的宗教場所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The retreat offered spiritual guidance to people from many backgrounds.","zh":"這次靜修為不同背景的人提供了精神和宗教方面的指導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spiritual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a7647a8e327e8e462cc","word":"spit","forms":["spit"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a6986ede6fbd5df","term":"spit","forms":["spit","spits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烤肉叉杆","explanation":"一種細長的金屬或木製尖杆，把肉穿在上面後放在火上轉動燒烤。它體現了“尖杆向前穿入”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The cook put the lamb on a spit over the fire.","zh":"廚師把羊肉穿在烤肉杆上，架在火上烤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They slowly turned the spit so the chicken would cook evenly.","zh":"他們慢慢轉動烤肉杆，讓雞肉均勻受熱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c18d68fcbd3aabcd","term":"spit","forms":["spit","spits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"唾液；吐出的唾沫","explanation":"指口腔裡的唾液，尤其是已經吐出來的唾沫；重點是液體從嘴裡向外排出。","examples":[{"en":"There was spit on the floor after the argument.","zh":"爭吵後，地板上有吐出的唾沫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wiped the spit from his chin.","zh":"他擦掉了下巴上的唾沫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3825b5d8ee807f8","term":"spit","forms":["spit","spits","spitting","spitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刺穿；穿在尖杆上","explanation":"用尖銳物體穿透某物，尤其是把肉穿到烤肉杆上；動作仍然是“尖杆向裡穿入”。","examples":[{"en":"The chef spitted the fish before placing it over the coals.","zh":"廚師把魚穿在烤肉杆上，然後放到炭火上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The branch spitted the soft fruit when it fell.","zh":"柔軟的果實掉下來時被樹枝刺穿了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d702102ba4d44c0e","term":"spit","forms":["spit","spits","spitting","spat"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吐出；吐唾沫","explanation":"把唾液、痰或嘴裡的其他東西從口中排出去；這是“向外噴出”的核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"He spat out the bitter candy at once.","zh":"他馬上把那顆苦糖吐了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child spat on the pavement.","zh":"那個孩子朝人行道上吐了口水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04726352b7def4cc77d1","word":"spite","forms":["spite"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f885236da2195a95","term":"spite","forms":["spite","spites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"惡意；故意使人難受的心態","explanation":"spite是針對某人的惡意，帶有想故意惹惱、傷害或阻撓對方的意思；重點不只是討厭，而是想讓對方不好受。","examples":[{"en":"He deleted the photos out of spite after their argument.","zh":"他們爭吵後，他出於惡意刪掉了那些照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was obvious spite in the way she answered him.","zh":"她回答他時，明顯帶著惡意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31d58043e5d08e036adf","word":"splash","forms":["splash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-951d6ce693a585b7","term":"splash","forms":["splash","splashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水花聲","explanation":"液體被物體擊中或物體落入液體時發出的“譁”聲，是“飛濺”這一核心畫面的聲音版本。","examples":[{"en":"I heard a splash when the stone fell into the pond.","zh":"石頭掉進池塘時，我聽到了一聲水花響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard a splash beneath the bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cd4ec8c990d05df","term":"splash","forms":["splash","splashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少量液體","explanation":"從一大團液體中飛出或灑出的少量液體，常常是幾滴或一小片水。","examples":[{"en":"A splash of rain hit my face as I opened the door.","zh":"我開門時，一小片雨水濺到了臉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add a splash of milk to the beaten eggs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91115eaba1bc87dd","term":"splash","forms":["splash","splashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一抹顏色","explanation":"像液體飛濺一樣出現的一小片顏色，用來給整體增添醒目或活潑的效果。","examples":[{"en":"The room needs a splash of yellow.","zh":"這個房間需要添上一抹黃色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red scarf added a splash of color.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4adb75fb71409f30","term":"splash","forms":["splash","splashes","splashing","splashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"玩水或使水花飛濺","explanation":"人在水中活動，使一部分水從主體水面飛濺出來，或在水裡撲騰玩耍。","examples":[{"en":"The children splashed in the shallow pool.","zh":"孩子們在淺水池裡嬉水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Otters rolled and splashed beside the riverbank.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e23fb5588eb1576","term":"splash","forms":["splash","splashes","splashing","splashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"液體突然四散","explanation":"液體受到碰撞或推動後突然向四周飛散，重點在液體自己濺開的結果。","examples":[{"en":"Water splashed onto the floor when the bucket fell.","zh":"水桶掉下時，水濺到了地板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water splashed over the edge of the basin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4126f15b9d44e26c","term":"splash","forms":["splash","splashes","splashing","splashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"潑灑液體","explanation":"主動讓液體飛濺出來，通常是把水等液體潑到某處或某物上。","examples":[{"en":"She splashed cold water onto her face.","zh":"她把冷水潑到臉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She splashed paint across the canvas in sweeping strokes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff2ce94823ad2511","term":"splash","forms":["splash","splashes","splashing","splashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把液體潑向某人","explanation":"主動把液體濺向某個人或目標，常帶有玩鬧或對抗意味。","examples":[{"en":"The children splashed each other with seawater.","zh":"孩子們互相潑海水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She splashed him with cold water from the bucket.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e08aef19080b45dade90","word":"splendid","forms":["splendid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90ee89d6903d6445","term":"splendid","forms":["splendid","splendider","more splendid","splendidest","most splendid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"燦爛耀眼的","explanation":"指光線很強、非常明亮，彷彿發出耀眼光芒，是“華美”和“出色”這兩個引申義的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We woke to a splendid sunrise over the hills.","zh":"我們醒來時，看到山丘上方燦爛的日出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The king appeared in splendid robes embroidered with gold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splendid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ee3d5d3ecd8b12e","term":"splendid","forms":["splendid","splendider","more splendid","splendidest","most splendid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極好的；出色的","explanation":"引申指某件事像閃閃發光一樣突出、令人滿意，表示“非常好、達到很高標準”。可評價表現、計劃、機會、訊息或結果，也可以作為感嘆表示贊同。","examples":[{"en":"You did a splendid job on the presentation.","zh":"你的演示做得非常出色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Splendid! I’ll meet you at the station.","zh":"太好了！我會在車站和你見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splendid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3c0edd8b6438dab2824","word":"splendor","forms":["splendor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5bfc0c5bff03e0e","term":"splendor","forms":["splendor","splendors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"耀眼的光輝","explanation":"指強烈而奪目的光線或光澤，是“光輝”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The splendor of the stars was breathtaking.","zh":"群星的光輝令人屏息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The splendor of the sunset lit the bay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splendor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc88bedd4607828d","term":"splendor","forms":["splendor","splendors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宏偉壯麗的氣派","explanation":"耀眼的光輝進一步變成整體的華美氣勢，指建築、儀式或場面顯得宏偉、豪華而令人讚歎。","examples":[{"en":"Visitors admired the splendor of the palace.","zh":"遊客讚歎宮殿的宏偉壯麗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The palace's splendor astonished the visiting delegation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splendor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad1a64057f9ab34fecfe","word":"split","forms":["split"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e6d86b5166269e2","term":"split","forms":["split","splits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"分裂；分歧","explanation":"指一個團體、關係或立場被分成兩邊，成員不再作為一個整體行動。這正是“一條線把整體分開”在抽象關係中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The dispute caused a split within the organization.","zh":"這場爭論導致組織內部發生了分裂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a clear split between younger and older voters.","zh":"年輕選民和年長選民之間存在明顯分歧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/split","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f02eb77673d95c3","term":"split","forms":["split","splits","splitting"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使裂開；分開","explanation":"把一個完整的東西沿著一條大致直的線分開，可能只是部分裂開，也可能完全分成兩塊；這正是“一條線把整體分開”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The ball split his lip when it hit him.","zh":"球撞到他時，把他的嘴唇撞裂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to split the envelope when you open it.","zh":"開啟信封時小心別把它撕裂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/split","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b838d9cc8f4a30e1","term":"split","forms":["split","splits","splitting"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離開","explanation":"從某個地方或和某些人分開並離開，就像從原來的整體中走出去；這是“分開”引申出的口語意思。","examples":[{"en":"It’s getting late, so I’m going to split.","zh":"時間不早了，我要走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We split after dinner and went home.","zh":"晚飯後我們分開，各自回家了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/split","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af1c686bc18b1227e171","word":"spoil","forms":["spoil"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-79821dd46c8a23c7","term":"spoil","forms":["spoil","spoils","spoiling","spoiled","spoilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"毀壞；破壞","explanation":"指把原本有用、漂亮或令人滿意的事物弄壞，使它失去原來的效果或價值。這是現代英語中非常重要的常用義，可以用於計劃、氣氛、機會、食物以外的許多事物。","examples":[{"en":"One careless comment spoiled the whole evening.","zh":"一句不經意的話毀掉了整個晚上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rain spoiled our plans for a picnic.","zh":"下雨打亂了我們野餐的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spoil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6dd2a0f78f3b644a","term":"spoil","forms":["spoil","spoils","spoiling","spoiled","spoilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變質；腐壞","explanation":"指食物等東西自行變壞，變酸、腐爛或不再適合食用。它是“失去原來狀態”的直接用法，主語通常是食物，而不是造成變化的人。","examples":[{"en":"Put the cheese in the fridge before it spoils.","zh":"在乳酪變質前把它放進冰箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heat spoiled all the fruit.","zh":"高溫使所有水果都壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spoil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-320cd09dfce439f5","term":"spoil","forms":["spoil","spoils","spoiling","spoiled","spoilt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"劇透；破壞驚喜","explanation":"指提前說出電影、書或比賽的重要情節，尤其是結局，從而破壞別人觀看或閱讀時的期待。它是“把驚喜弄壞”的現代常用引申義。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't spoil the ending for me.","zh":"請不要給我劇透結局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The review spoiled the biggest surprise in the film.","zh":"那篇評論劇透了電影中最大的驚喜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spoil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cebd02dacbba92e4728d","word":"spokesperson/spokesman/spokeswoman","forms":["spokesperson","spokesman","spokeswoman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5eea0998c7054195","term":"spokesperson","forms":["spokesperson","spokespersons","spokespeople"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發言人；代言人","explanation":"指代表另一個人、組織或一群人對外說明情況、表達立場的人。他的聲音不只是個人意見，而是被視為所代表一方的正式聲音。","examples":[{"en":"The company spokesperson said that the new policy would begin next month.","zh":"公司發言人表示，新政策將於下個月開始實施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spokesperson for the hospital answered reporters’ questions.","zh":"醫院的一名發言人回答了記者的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spokesperson","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b275d99e6376261","term":"spokesman","forms":["spokesman","spokesmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發言人","explanation":"指代表另一個人、團體或機構對外說話、釋出意見或回應問題的人；核心不是“說話”，而是替別人發聲。","examples":[{"en":"The company spokesman said that the factory would reopen on Monday.","zh":"公司發言人說，工廠將在星期一重新開工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spokesman for the hospital answered questions from reporters.","zh":"醫院的一名發言人回答了記者的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spokesman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68cf73040902812d","term":"spokeswoman","forms":["spokeswoman","spokeswomen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女性發言人","explanation":"指被一個團體、機構或專案授權、委託或安排來對外發聲的女性；她說的話通常被聽作該團體的公開立場，而不是單純的個人意見。","examples":[{"en":"The company spokeswoman announced the new safety measures.","zh":"公司的女發言人宣佈了新的安全措施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spokeswoman for the charity answered questions from reporters.","zh":"該慈善機構的一名女發言人回答了記者的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spokeswoman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46248ac6898288005021","word":"sponge","forms":["sponge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54e94611adfd9b08","term":"sponge","forms":["sponge","sponges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海綿動物","explanation":"指生活在海里的多孔無脊椎動物，其身體像天然海綿一樣有許多孔，可以讓水流透過。","examples":[{"en":"Some sponges live attached to rocks on the ocean floor.","zh":"有些海綿動物附著在海底的岩石上生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sponge attached itself to the submerged rock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-092dc5cd73a9c68b","term":"sponge","forms":["sponge","sponges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"清潔用海綿","explanation":"指用來洗滌、擦拭或吸收液體的多孔塊狀工具，過去常由天然海綿製成，現在多為人造材料。","examples":[{"en":"Use a clean sponge to wipe the soup off the table.","zh":"用一塊乾淨的海綿把桌上的湯汁擦掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She washed the dishes with a sponge and warm water.","zh":"她用海綿和溫水洗了碗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fecb21344f3b755","term":"sponge","forms":["sponge","sponges","sponging","sponged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"佔別人便宜","explanation":"像海綿吸水一樣，持續從別人的好意、資源或錢財中獲取好處，卻不作相應回報。","examples":[{"en":"He has been sponging off his parents for years.","zh":"多年來他一直靠佔父母的便宜過日子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent years sponging off his generous relatives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-322f8596f55b81e3","term":"sponge","forms":["sponge","sponges","sponging","sponged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用海綿擦或吸","explanation":"指用海綿清潔、擦拭、蘸取或吸走液體，把海綿作為實際工具使用。","examples":[{"en":"She sponged the spilled milk off the floor.","zh":"她用海綿把灑在地板上的牛奶吸乾淨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse sponged his forehead with cool water.","zh":"護士用涼水蘸溼海綿給他擦額頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a484241348622699","term":"sponge","forms":["sponge","sponges","sponging","sponged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸收；汲取","explanation":"比喻像海綿吸水一樣吸收液體、知識、經驗或其他東西。","examples":[{"en":"The new intern sponged up every bit of advice.","zh":"這名新實習生吸收了每一點建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dry soil sponged up the rain within minutes.","zh":"乾燥的土壤幾分鐘內就把雨水吸收了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13d853006f71ed7b6b09","word":"sponsor","forms":["sponsor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8743073457eb3509","term":"sponsor","forms":["sponsor","sponsors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"承擔責任或提供支援的人或機構","explanation":"指站在某人或某個組織背後、對其承擔一定責任或提供支援的人或機構，責任可能來自宗教、法律、加入組織等情境，也可以只是一般性的支援。","examples":[{"en":"She became my sponsor when I joined the club.","zh":"我加入俱樂部時，她成了我的擔保人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity found a local sponsor to support the project.","zh":"這家慈善機構找到了一個支援該專案的當地贊助方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponsor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04166f55f9f5bbe3","term":"sponsor","forms":["sponsor","sponsors","sponsoring","sponsored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"贊助或支援","explanation":"表示主動站在某人、組織或活動背後，提供資金、責任或其他支援；因此既可以是商業贊助，也可以是較一般的支援。","examples":[{"en":"The company sponsors a youth football team every year.","zh":"這家公司每年都會贊助一支青少年足球隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A local business sponsored the children's football team.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponsor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-600ccd5e0c3fee790399","word":"sponsorship","forms":["sponsorship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a05e5411ff870107","term":"sponsorship","forms":["sponsorship","sponsorships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"贊助關係或行為","explanation":"指成為贊助者、持續支援某人或某項事業這一狀態或行為，重點在“贊助”這層關係本身，而不是某一筆具體款項。","examples":[{"en":"Her sponsorship of the local shelter continued for many years.","zh":"她對當地收容所的贊助持續了許多年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The athlete thanked the company for its sponsorship.","zh":"這名運動員感謝公司對他的贊助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponsorship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-094918cf58d2f44b","term":"sponsorship","forms":["sponsorship","sponsorships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"贊助者提供的支援或資助","explanation":"指贊助者實際提供的資金、物資、資源或其他支援；可以理解為贊助關係落實後交到對方手裡的“幫助”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum received sponsorship from several local businesses.","zh":"這家博物館獲得了幾家當地企業的贊助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without sponsorship, the research project could not continue.","zh":"沒有贊助，這項研究專案就無法繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sponsorship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fd19d4493362e556af1","word":"spontaneous","forms":["spontaneous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-139ccf4446d0c091","term":"spontaneous","forms":["spontaneous","more spontaneous","most spontaneous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自發產生的","explanation":"指某事自己產生或發生，看不出明確的外部原因或推動者；重點是它像從內部自然冒出來，而不是被安排出來的。","examples":[{"en":"The crowd gave a spontaneous cheer when the singer returned.","zh":"歌手回來時，人群自發地歡呼起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spontaneous discussion began after the lecture.","zh":"講座結束後，自發的討論開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spontaneous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bdda72d106b959db","term":"spontaneous","forms":["spontaneous","more spontaneous","most spontaneous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自願且未計劃的","explanation":"指人憑自己的選擇去做某事，而且事先沒有安排；它把“自己願意”和“沒有提前計劃”結合在一起。","examples":[{"en":"We made a spontaneous offer to help the new neighbors.","zh":"我們自願且臨時決定幫助新鄰居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her spontaneous offer to help surprised everyone.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spontaneous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7be58b716eda890a","term":"spontaneous","forms":["spontaneous","more spontaneous","most spontaneous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"出於自然感情的","explanation":"指言行不是為了完成要求或遵守規則，而是自然流露出真實的感情或本能傾向。","examples":[{"en":"Her spontaneous kindness made the frightened child feel safe.","zh":"她自然流露出的善意讓受驚的孩子感到安心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her spontaneous smile reassured the nervous child.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spontaneous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9efb38dac23b98f4","term":"spontaneous","forms":["spontaneous","more spontaneous","most spontaneous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"一時衝動的","explanation":"指人在某個瞬間受到念頭或感覺推動，馬上做出決定或行動，沒有先作計劃。","examples":[{"en":"On a spontaneous impulse, she bought a ticket to the coast.","zh":"她一時興起，買了一張去海邊的票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We made a spontaneous decision to visit the coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spontaneous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7f480e744a79953eb916","word":"spoon","forms":["spoon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41c5c1b3001cdc29","term":"spoon","forms":["spoon","spoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勺子","explanation":"用於吃東西、盛東西或把食物送入口中的凹面餐具，通常帶有直長柄；它比湯勺更泛指各種勺子。","examples":[{"en":"She stirred her coffee with a small spoon.","zh":"她用小勺攪拌咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pass me the spoon.","zh":"請把那把勺子遞給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a9822e94e15357e","term":"spoon","forms":["spoon","spoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有限的日常精力","explanation":"在慢性病或殘障語境中，把每天有限的體力和腦力想象成一定數量的“勺子”；完成一項活動就會消耗一些，休息可以幫助恢復，但可用數量並不總是充足。","examples":[{"en":"I don't have enough spoons to go shopping today.","zh":"我今天沒有足夠的精力去購物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She saved her spoons for the doctor's appointment.","zh":"她把精力留給了預約看醫生這件事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec450786e26a51541735","word":"sport","forms":["sport"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff44a015c840e9d9","term":"sport","forms":["sport","sports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育運動；比賽專案","explanation":"sport 指按照規則、憑體力或技巧進行競爭的體育活動，可以是一個具體專案，也可以泛指體育運動。","examples":[{"en":"Swimming is her favorite sport.","zh":"游泳是她最喜歡的運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school offers several sports after class.","zh":"學校提供幾種課外體育專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-003a9f31a5265aec","term":"sport","forms":["sport","sports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輸得起、經得起打趣的人","explanation":"a good sport 特指一個被取笑、輸了比賽或遇到尷尬情況時仍能大方應對的人，也就是通常所說的“輸得起、開得起玩笑”。","examples":[{"en":"Thanks for being a good sport and trying the silly costume.","zh":"謝謝你這麼有風度，願意試穿這套傻傻的服裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be a good sport and congratulate the winners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-491a7064834c933b","term":"sport","forms":["sport","sports","sporting","sported"],"pos":"verb","zh":"玩樂；參加運動","explanation":"sport 作動詞時可以表示玩耍、消遣，也可以指進行體育活動，體現了從“運動”到“玩樂”的核心聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The children sported in the park all afternoon.","zh":"孩子們整個下午都在公園裡玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Otters sported in the shallow river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4233a88a84b9c06","term":"sport","forms":["sport","sports","sporting","sported"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穿戴或展示","explanation":"sport something 表示把某物顯眼地穿戴著、帶著或展示出來，好像把它當成值得別人注意的特色。","examples":[{"en":"He was sporting a bright red jacket.","zh":"他穿著一件鮮紅的夾克，十分顯眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is sporting a new haircut.","zh":"她換了一個新發型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c29ea9c56858224ccec9","word":"sportsman/sportswoman","forms":["sportsman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"sportsman","forms":["sportsman","sportswoman"],"pos":"n.","zh":"男性運動員；女性運動員","examples":[{"en":"The sportsman trained every morning before school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She became the first sportswoman from her town to win an international medal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-10ecfa5572a4a9a391bb","word":"sportsmanship","forms":["sportsmanship"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae0614f1fe685aa2","term":"sportsmanship","forms":["sportsmanship","sportsmanships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育精神","explanation":"指在比賽中公平競爭、尊重對手、遵守規則，並且無論獲勝還是失敗都保持風度的態度和行為。它最常用於讚揚一個人的比賽品格，而不只是比賽結果。","examples":[{"en":"She showed great sportsmanship by congratulating her opponent after the final.","zh":"決賽後，她向對手錶示祝賀，展現了很好的體育精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach praised the team for winning with skill and sportsmanship.","zh":"教練稱讚這支隊伍既憑實力取勝，又保持了體育精神。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sportsmanship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-573474b218f0586f","term":"sportsmanship","forms":["sportsmanship","sportsmanships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"比賽中的表現","explanation":"可較寬泛地指一個人在參加體育比賽時表現出來的行為和態度；這種表現可以是好的，也可以是不好的，但實際使用中常透過 good 或 poor 來說明性質。","examples":[{"en":"The referee stopped the match because the players were showing poor sportsmanship.","zh":"裁判暫停了比賽，因為球員們表現出了糟糕的比賽風度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runner's generous sportsmanship impressed his defeated rivals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sportsmanship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be2bdbb3100e41191874","word":"spot","forms":["spot"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24fa910b18e0fc30","term":"spot","forms":["spot","spots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斑點；色斑","explanation":"這是表面上被看見、被標出來的一個點，通常顏色或質地不同，可以是規則或不規則的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"The leopard has dark spots all over its coat.","zh":"這隻豹子的皮毛上到處都是深色斑點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There were bright spots on the wings of the butterfly.","zh":"蝴蝶的翅膀上有鮮豔的斑點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53a0f470fbe3c5d7","term":"spot","forms":["spot","spots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地點；地方","explanation":"把spot想成地圖上被標出來的點：它可以是適合某種活動的一個地方或位置，不一定是正式的地址。","examples":[{"en":"We found a shady spot for our picnic.","zh":"我們找到了一個適合野餐的陰涼地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is a great spot to watch the sunset.","zh":"這裡是觀看日落的好地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7090115b6e6a81ba","term":"spot","forms":["spot","spots","spotting","spotted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發現；認出","explanation":"把注意力落到一個“被標出來的點”上，從而看見、找出、辨認或認出某人某物。","examples":[{"en":"Can you spot the mistake in this sentence?","zh":"你能找出這個句子裡的錯誤嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I spotted Maya waiting outside the café.","zh":"我看見瑪雅正在咖啡館外面等著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-be46a22b1f8cddcc3562","word":"spotlight","forms":["spotlight"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4c519ba51633a782","term":"spotlight","forms":["spotlight","spotlights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聚光燈","explanation":"舞臺或其他場所中能把強光集中照向某個目標的燈，通常用來讓觀眾注意某位演員、物品或位置。","examples":[{"en":"The director placed a spotlight on the dancer.","zh":"導演用一盞聚光燈照亮了那位舞者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spotlight followed the dancer across the stage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spotlight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8aa41ba0723caf62","term":"spotlight","forms":["spotlight","spotlights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關注焦點","explanation":"借用聚光燈只照一個目標的畫面，指某人或某事成為公眾、媒體或一群人的主要關注物件。","examples":[{"en":"She is comfortable in the spotlight.","zh":"她很適應成為眾人關注的焦點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The investigation placed the contractor in the spotlight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spotlight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ebd930580c6008e1","term":"spotlight","forms":["spotlight","spotlights","spotlighting","spotlighted","spotlit"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用聚光燈照亮","explanation":"實際把聚光燈的光集中照向某人或某物，使其成為舞臺或現場的視覺焦點。","examples":[{"en":"The final scene spotlights the youngest actor.","zh":"最後一幕用聚光燈照亮了那位最年輕的演員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stage crew spotlighted the singer during her solo.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spotlight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-815fbec040e347c18722","word":"spouse","forms":["spouse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0479d04eba1d9f63","term":"spouse","forms":["spouse","spouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"配偶","explanation":"指與某人處於婚姻關係中的丈夫或妻子，不特別說明性別；重點是“已經結婚的伴侶”。","examples":[{"en":"People should treat their spouses with respect.","zh":"人們應該尊重自己的配偶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her spouse works at the same hospital.","zh":"她的配偶在同一家醫院工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e28b3a396b9c63a34eb3","word":"spray","forms":["spray"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9be65bd698e2e547","term":"spray","forms":["spray","sprays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噴霧；細小水花","explanation":"液體被打散成許多細小水珠後形成的霧狀水花，常見於海浪、噴水或噴灑。","examples":[{"en":"The spray from the waves covered the windows.","zh":"海浪濺起的水花打溼了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sea spray soaked our faces on the ferry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-106620d6cb858db8","term":"spray","forms":["spray","sprays","spraying","sprayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"噴灑；噴射","explanation":"把液體打散成細小水珠，朝某個物體或方向噴出去。這是動詞的核心意思，和名詞的“噴霧”直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"Please spray the leaves with water every morning.","zh":"請每天早上給葉子噴水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Spray the leaves lightly with clean water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25d8e243c1ac21b3","term":"spray","forms":["spray","sprays","spraying","sprayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"噴散；噴到某處","explanation":"表示液體以分散的方式噴出，既可以說人主動噴，也可以說液體自行噴散。它突出“向外散開”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Oil sprayed onto the hot pan.","zh":"油噴濺到了熱鍋上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The burst pipe sprayed water across the kitchen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-909802b269dee093387e","word":"spread","forms":["spread"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32afbccb919c3e4b","term":"spread","forms":["spread","spreads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豐盛的一桌食物","explanation":"指擺在桌上、種類豐富而分量充足的一餐，彷彿把食物鋪滿了整張桌子。","examples":[{"en":"The family prepared a generous spread for the holiday dinner.","zh":"這家人為節日晚餐準備了一桌豐盛的食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our hosts laid on a magnificent spread.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9471782a4ee3669","term":"spread","forms":["spread","spreads","spreading"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攤開以覆蓋更大面積","explanation":"把原本摺疊、捲起或集中在一起的東西攤開，使它更充分地鋪在某個表面或區域上，就像把毯子向四周展開。","examples":[{"en":"She spread the map across the kitchen table.","zh":"她把地圖攤在廚房桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spread a blanket on the grass.","zh":"他把一條毯子鋪在草地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-611251d5ea2d2139","term":"spread","forms":["spread","spreads","spreading"],"pos":"verb","zh":"散佈到一片區域","explanation":"把許多分散的小東西均勻地放到一個區域中，使它們從一點向四周鋪開。","examples":[{"en":"Spread the seeds evenly over the soil.","zh":"把種子均勻地撒在土壤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They spread the chairs around the hall.","zh":"他們把椅子分散擺在大廳各處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9635659ebff52f5e","term":"spread","forms":["spread","spreads","spreading"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使訊息或影響傳播開","explanation":"主動把訊息、思想、信仰或影響傳到更多地方或更多人那裡，使它變得廣為人知。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign spread awareness of water safety.","zh":"這項活動提高了人們對用水安全的認識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please spread the word about the schedule change.","zh":"請把日程變更的訊息告訴大家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-622a494d3ea8c7ba2fed","word":"spring","forms":["spring"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-87b90bfe404e8963","term":"spring","forms":["spring","springs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"跳躍","explanation":"spring 可以指身體突然向上或向前彈起的一次跳躍，像被力量猛地推出去一樣。","examples":[{"en":"With one spring, the cat jumped onto the wall.","zh":"貓一躍就跳到了牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The horse cleared the fence in a single spring.","zh":"那匹馬一躍越過了柵欄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9d771393411cdd0","term":"spring","forms":["spring","springs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"春天","explanation":"spring 指一年四季中的春季：天氣和日照逐漸增加，植物破土開花，冬眠的動物也開始活動，正對應“湧出、開始生長”的記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The garden is full of flowers in spring.","zh":"春天，花園裡開滿了花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We usually plant tomatoes in early spring.","zh":"我們通常在早春種西紅柿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d11df2ee3952dd4b","term":"spring","forms":["spring","springs","springing","sprang","sprung","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然衝出；迸發","explanation":"表示人、動物、物體或某種情況突然向外衝出、冒出或爆發，正像東西從裡面彈出來一樣。也常用於故障等突然出現。","examples":[{"en":"A rabbit sprang from the bushes and disappeared into the field.","zh":"一隻兔子從灌木叢中突然躥出，消失在田野裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old pipe sprang a leak during the night.","zh":"夜裡那根舊管道突然漏水了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6f0ebddbe0fe1b0ff9c","word":"sprinkle","forms":["sprinkle"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-131454e3175a27a8","term":"sprinkle","forms":["sprinkle","sprinkles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"少量撒上的一層","explanation":"指某種粉末、顆粒或碎屑被少量撒在表面後形成的薄薄一層，重點是零星分佈而不是厚厚堆積。","examples":[{"en":"Add a sprinkle of cheese over the soup.","zh":"在湯上撒一點乳酪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Finish the cake with a sprinkle of cocoa.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sprinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87586812a316b487","term":"sprinkle","forms":["sprinkle","sprinkles","sprinkling","sprinkled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撒下細滴或小顆粒","explanation":"指讓液體以細小水滴，或讓固體以小顆粒的形式零星落下；畫面是輕輕撒，而不是一口氣倒出。","examples":[{"en":"She sprinkled cinnamon over the oatmeal.","zh":"她在燕麥粥上撒了些肉桂粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sprinkle the seeds onto the soil.","zh":"把種子撒到土壤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sprinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63885fe05a1e6c589c6f","word":"spur","forms":["spur"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70905250e283acf0","term":"spur","forms":["spur","spurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬刺","explanation":"馬刺是固定在鞋跟上的硬質尖刺或尖頭器具，騎手用它輕刺馬身來催馬；它也常讓人聯想到牛仔或騎士。這個意思體現了“向前催”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The rider wore silver spurs on his boots.","zh":"騎手的靴子上戴著銀色馬刺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She removed her spurs before entering the house.","zh":"她進屋前摘下了馬刺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-328422e5c156f09f","term":"spur","forms":["spur","spurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刺激；動力","explanation":"它可比喻某件事像馬刺一樣從後面“頂”人，促使人開始行動、更加努力或做出勇敢的決定。這個刺激可以來自競爭、榮譽、壓力或某個具體目標。","examples":[{"en":"The competition was a spur to her hard work.","zh":"這場比賽促使她更加努力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His desire to help his family was a powerful spur to action.","zh":"幫助家人的願望是促使他採取行動的強大動力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01c4e3e42f6ffacd","term":"spur","forms":["spur","spurs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支線；突出部分","explanation":"spur可以指從較大的主體向外伸出的部分，例如從主幹道分出的短路，也可泛指從某物伸出的支脈、支段或突出結構。它正好對應記憶中的“向外頂”。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow road is a spur off the main highway.","zh":"一條狹窄的道路從公路幹線分支出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trail follows a spur that projects from the ridge.","zh":"這條小徑沿著從山脊伸出的支脈前行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b5656d6f1bbb1cf","term":"spur","forms":["spur","spurs","spurring","spurred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促使；激勵","explanation":"指某種願望、競爭、壓力或事件像馬刺一樣，促使人採取行動，或更加努力地追求目標。","examples":[{"en":"The deadline spurred the team to finish the project early.","zh":"截止日期促使團隊提前完成了專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her success spurred me on to practice every day.","zh":"她的成功激勵我每天練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spur","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57d4aa377250296d19d9","word":"spy","forms":["spy"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-225c786b95996892","term":"spy","forms":["spy","spies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"間諜","explanation":"指暗中監視個人、組織或國家並蒐集情報的人，通常是為了讓自己一方獲得優勢。","examples":[{"en":"The spy passed the documents to a foreign agent.","zh":"那名間諜把檔案交給了一名外國特工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They suspected that one of the guards was a spy.","zh":"他們懷疑其中一名警衛是間諜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ad41736a70fbefb","term":"spy","forms":["spy","spies","spying","spied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從事秘密偵察","explanation":"指像間諜一樣暗中觀察別人或組織，蒐集能夠幫助自己一方的資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries accused each other of spying on their officials.","zh":"兩國互相指責對方暗中監視本國官員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was arrested for spying for a foreign government.","zh":"她因替外國政府從事間諜活動而被捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bd3279565437b8fe82a","word":"squad","forms":["squad"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff07cefb53255886","term":"squad","forms":["squad","squads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"執行共同任務的小組","explanation":"squad最核心的意思是為同一個目標集合起來的一小隊人，通常人數不多，可以臨時組成，也可以有明確分工。","examples":[{"en":"She assembled a squad of volunteers to clean the park.","zh":"她組織了一隊志願者來清理公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small squad searched the building.","zh":"一支小隊搜查了那棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41708f75111f0911","term":"squad","forms":["squad","squads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"非正式的一小群人","explanation":"在較口語的用法中，squad仍保留“一群人一起行動”的核心概念，但不一定有正式任務，甚至可以只是一起做某件事的人。","examples":[{"en":"A squad of fans waited outside the theater.","zh":"一群粉絲在劇院外等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My squad meets at the skate park after school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squad","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ba3e8e3765f2970eb37","word":"square","forms":["square"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d709be483b0778a","term":"square","forms":["square","squarer","squarest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"正方形的","explanation":"形狀像正方形，四條邊等長、四個角都是直角，體現了“方正、對齊”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She placed the books in a square box.","zh":"她把書放進了一個方形盒子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden has a square shape.","zh":"這個花園呈正方形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/square","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08d771e24b2f9b61","term":"square","forms":["square","squarer","squarest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"誠實公正的","explanation":"表示待人坦誠、做事公平，不佔便宜，體現了“方正、公正”的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"We want a square deal for everyone involved.","zh":"我們希望所有相關人員都能得到公平的待遇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is a square and trustworthy person.","zh":"他是個正直可靠的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/square","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69d30af6fed07648","term":"square","forms":["square","squares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正方形","explanation":"四條邊長度相等、四個角都是直角的平面圖形；這個義項最直接體現了“方正、對齊”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a square with sides that are five centimetres long.","zh":"畫一個邊長為五釐米的正方形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The window is almost a perfect square.","zh":"這扇窗幾乎是一個標準的正方形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/square","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc1c489951489ee7","term":"square","forms":["square","squares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平方；平方數","explanation":"一個數或數量乘以自身所得的結果，例如 8 的平方是 64。可以把它理解為把同一個數量沿兩個方向“對齊”排列成一個正方形。","examples":[{"en":"The square of six is thirty-six.","zh":"六的平方是三十六。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"To find the area, square the length of the side.","zh":"要計算面積，就把邊長平方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/square","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-586abb54469a8ddcc161","word":"squash","forms":["squash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c861d63ebd5a942","term":"squash","forms":["squash","squashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壁球運動","explanation":"一種在四面有牆的場地裡用球拍擊打軟橡膠球的運動；名稱和“壓擠、撞擊”的核心畫面相呼應。","examples":[{"en":"I play squash twice a week.","zh":"我每週打兩次壁球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They play squash at the sports center.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1895c941bab47bad","term":"squash","forms":["squash","squashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"南瓜類果實或菜餚","explanation":"指這類植物的可食用或裝飾性果實，也可指用果實做成的菜；這就是選單和購物場景裡最常見的食物義。","examples":[{"en":"We roasted the squash with garlic and herbs.","zh":"我們把南瓜類蔬菜和大蒜、香草一起烤了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thick skin of this squash becomes tender during baking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-468ea4a35f0b4560","term":"squash","forms":["squash","squashes","squashing","squashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓碎；壓扁","explanation":"用力把柔軟或易碎的東西壓成扁平的一團，核心畫面就是把東西壓得失去原形。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful not to squash the tomatoes.","zh":"小心別把西紅柿壓壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't squash the tomatoes beneath the potatoes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0aade82e533530f","term":"squash","forms":["squash","squashes","squashing","squashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擠進；塞入","explanation":"把人或物壓縮、擠進很小的空間，或自己勉強擠進去；仍然是“壓縮成一團”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She squashed all her clothes into one small bag.","zh":"她把所有衣服都塞進了一個小包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We squashed all six suitcases into the trunk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e62e25e7cb79f72","term":"squash","forms":["squash","squashes","squashing","squashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓制；擊潰","explanation":"把反抗、計劃或對手強行壓下去，使其無法繼續，就像把東西壓扁一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The authorities quickly squashed the rumour.","zh":"當局很快就壓下了這則謠言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The champion squashed any resistance with a series of decisive attacks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-52edeccca7cd6511929e","word":"squat","forms":["squat"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fedd5c8340b45eb","term":"squat","forms":["squat","squatter","squattest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"低矮敦實的","explanation":"形容物體相對矮、寬或厚，整體看起來低低的、結實敦實，正像被壓扁後仍然保持寬厚的形狀。","examples":[{"en":"A squat stone house stood at the edge of the village.","zh":"村邊有一座低矮敦實的石屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A squat stone tower guarded the entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52f2ca866daaf942","term":"squat","forms":["squat","squats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蹲姿","explanation":"指身體深深屈膝、腳掌著地的姿勢，也就是“蹲著”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Stay in a squat and keep your back straight.","zh":"保持蹲姿，並讓背部挺直。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He lowered himself into a squat beside the fire.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81df2f6e6881a73d","term":"squat","forms":["squat","squats","squatting","squatted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蹲下","explanation":"指屈膝並讓身體下降，最後腳掌著地保持低姿勢，是整個詞最核心的動作畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She squatted down to tie her daughter's shoe.","zh":"她蹲下來給女兒繫鞋帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He squatted beside the stream to wash his hands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b11833a4396b84cb8262","word":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8142adbab6aa2b8","term":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze","squeezes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擠壓；一擠","explanation":"指用力擠壓的一下或一次動作，例如把檸檬擠一下、把球捏一下。它是整組詞義的最基本影象。","examples":[{"en":"Give the lemon a quick squeeze before you add it to the soup.","zh":"把檸檬快速擠一下，再加進湯裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby gave my finger a surprisingly strong squeeze.","zh":"嬰兒把我的手指捏得出奇地緊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c178ed37103e3d1","term":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze","squeezes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狹窄的容納空間","explanation":"指物體之間貼得很緊、幾乎沒有多餘空間的狀態；它來自“被擠在一起”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"There was a tight squeeze between the sofa and the wall.","zh":"沙發和牆之間的空隙非常狹窄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Six people in that tiny car was a tight squeeze.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfac6cc54afe69c5","term":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze","squeezes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"困境；緊張處境","explanation":"引申為多個壓力同時擠過來，使人沒有多少選擇或餘地的困難處境。","examples":[{"en":"With two bills due tomorrow, I'm in a tight squeeze.","zh":"兩筆賬單明天都要到期，我現在處境很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rent increase put them in a financial squeeze.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2426766b5636165a","term":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze","squeezes","squeezing","squeezed","squoze","squozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擠壓","explanation":"指從兩邊或多個方向施加壓力，把物體擠緊、壓扁或壓住，是 squeeze 最直接的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"She squeezed the sponge between her hands.","zh":"她用雙手擠壓海綿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Squeeze the tube gently to get out a little cream.","zh":"輕輕擠壓軟管，擠出一點乳霜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5fdb1e6c931855d","term":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze","squeezes","squeezing","squeezed","squoze","squozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勉強塞入","explanation":"指把人或物放進狹小空間，雖然擁擠但設法容納進去；也可以表示自己擠進某處。","examples":[{"en":"We squeezed three boxes into the small elevator.","zh":"我們把三個箱子勉強塞進了小電梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I squeezed into the last empty seat on the bus.","zh":"我擠進了公交車上最後一個空座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd0f065fe2baf295","term":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze","squeezes","squeezing","squeezed","squoze","squozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設法擠出；弄到","explanation":"指費力地從某處取出某物，或設法從某人那裡弄到錢、時間等；想象把東西從緊處擠出來即可。","examples":[{"en":"I squeezed a little more time out of my busy schedule.","zh":"我從忙碌的日程中又擠出了一點時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporter squeezed an apology out of the company.","zh":"記者設法讓公司道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c100c63b91129902","term":"squeeze","forms":["squeeze","squeezes","squeezing","squeezed","squoze","squozen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使陷入兩難","explanation":"指把人置於兩個或多個選擇之間，使其受到相互衝突的壓力，像被從兩邊擠住一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The new deadline squeezed us between speed and accuracy.","zh":"新的截止時間讓我們陷入了速度和準確性之間的兩難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt squeezed between her family and her job.","zh":"她感到夾在家庭和工作之間，左右為難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squeeze","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-960a38ace75a2fe9426a","word":"squirrel","forms":["squirrel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea5cb7e833e1243f","term":"squirrel","forms":["squirrel","squirrels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"松鼠","explanation":"指松鼠科的齧齒動物，通常讓人聯想到有大尾巴、會在樹上活動並收集食物的動物。","examples":[{"en":"A squirrel darted across the path and climbed the oak tree.","zh":"一隻松鼠竄過小路，爬上了橡樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A squirrel buried an acorn beneath the hedge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squirrel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b652ea885f7a74758cd5","word":"stab","forms":["stab"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a2cde720dabfe9e","term":"stab","forms":["stab","stabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刺擊","explanation":"指用刀、棍等尖物向前猛刺的一下，強調動作本身，而不是刺後留下的傷口。","examples":[{"en":"The attacker made a stab at the guard and ran away.","zh":"襲擊者向警衛刺了一下，然後逃走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The attacker stabbed him in the shoulder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8213ba1106bbeb67","term":"stab","forms":["stab","stabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刺傷；刀傷","explanation":"指被尖物刺入後留下的傷口，是“刺”造成的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor treated a deep stab wound in his shoulder.","zh":"醫生處理了他肩膀上的一道深刺傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two deep stabs required stitches and an overnight hospital stay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63b3c03208be919e","term":"stab","forms":["stab","stabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘗試","explanation":"表示對一件事試著做一次，常帶有“先試試看，未必成功”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"I have never repaired a bike, but I’ll give it a stab.","zh":"我從沒修過腳踏車，不過我會試試看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a stab at solving the puzzle.","zh":"她試著解這個謎題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b8a181800920bab","term":"stab","forms":["stab","stabs","stabbing","stabbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刺傷；刺入","explanation":"指用刀、匕首等尖銳工具刺入某人的身體並造成傷害，是最直接的“刺”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The criminal stabbed the victim with a kitchen knife.","zh":"罪犯用一把菜刀刺傷了受害者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was stabbed in the arm during the fight.","zh":"他在打鬥中手臂被刺傷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1e79532d5b97c775ed6","word":"stability","forms":["stability"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95dfa0257353102f","term":"stability","forms":["stability","stabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"穩固與平衡","explanation":"指事物處於穩固、平衡的狀態，不容易搖晃、倒下或發生變化。例如平臺站得穩，就是具有 stability。","examples":[{"en":"This platform offers good stability.","zh":"這個平臺很穩固。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new design improves the stability of the bridge.","zh":"新設計提高了這座橋的穩定性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1974fc47af2597f2","term":"stability","forms":["stability","stabilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受擾後恢復平衡","explanation":"指事物受到干擾、壓力或變化後，仍能保持平衡，或重新回到較穩定的狀態。人的情緒、機器和社會局勢都可以有這種 stability。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise has helped improve her emotional stability.","zh":"規律運動幫助她提高了情緒穩定性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country needs political stability to attract investment.","zh":"這個國家需要政治穩定來吸引投資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stability","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbf7cf0f2758f170a619","word":"stabilize","forms":["stabilize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ca432870e51fcb8","term":"stabilize","forms":["stabilize","stabilizes","stabilizing","stabilized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使穩定","explanation":"透過支撐、調整或採取措施，讓原本搖晃、不穩的物體、情況或系統變得穩定。這個意思就是“把它扶穩”。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse stabilized his condition before moving him to another room.","zh":"護士先穩定了他的病情，然後才把他轉到另一個房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stabilized the shelf by adding a metal bracket.","zh":"我們加了一個金屬託架，把架子固定穩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stabilize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0468992e8cc2da1","term":"stabilize","forms":["stabilize","stabilizes","stabilizing","stabilized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得穩定","explanation":"原本動盪、搖晃或變化很大的事物逐漸變穩，不一定有人直接使它穩定。這個意思就是“自己穩下來”。","examples":[{"en":"Prices began to stabilize after several months of rapid increases.","zh":"價格快速上漲了幾個月後，開始趨於穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her condition stabilized after the emergency treatment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stabilize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f379ccb92b9116442dc6","word":"stable","forms":["stable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee4d13bd2bc1cd7a","term":"stable","forms":["stable","stabler","more stable","stablest","most stable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"穩定的；牢固的","explanation":"表示某種狀態、關係或安排能夠持續，變化不大，也不容易被破壞或動搖。它強調相對穩定，不一定表示永遠不變。","examples":[{"en":"He was in a stable relationship.","zh":"他處於一段穩定的戀愛關係中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The patient's condition is stable now.","zh":"病人的狀況現在穩定了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ee08e6eb3bc6f45bc99","word":"stack","forms":["stack"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c88b749bb19f4e35","term":"stack","forms":["stack","stacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一堆；一疊","explanation":"指許多相同或相關的東西一層層堆在一起，核心畫面就是“往上堆成一堆”。","examples":[{"en":"There was a stack of books beside the sofa.","zh":"沙發旁邊有一疊書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the plates in a neat stack.","zh":"請把盤子整齊地疊成一摞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6534f73dd873f276","term":"stack","forms":["stack","stacks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棧；棧式資料結構","explanation":"在計算機中，stack 是一種把資料一層層放入、再按規定順序取出的結構，核心規則通常是後放入的先取出。","examples":[{"en":"The program stores the temporary values on the stack.","zh":"程式把臨時值存放在棧中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stack can return the last item that was added.","zh":"棧可以先返回最後加入的專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f123f77d149483c","term":"stack","forms":["stack","stacks","stacking","stacked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堆放；疊放","explanation":"指把物品一層層放好，或把新物品加到已有的堆上，是名詞“堆”的直接動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"They stacked the boxes against the wall.","zh":"他們把箱子靠牆堆放起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stack the towels on the shelf.","zh":"把毛巾疊放在架子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stack","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dafc4889ee011aab244b","word":"stadium","forms":["stadium"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf6d746028888352","term":"stadium","forms":["stadium","stadiums","stadia"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育場；運動場","explanation":"指舉行足球、板球、田徑等體育比賽的大型場地或場館，通常包括觀眾看臺。它保留了古代“跑道”的核心形象，但現代最常見的是觀看比賽的運動場。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of fans gathered at the stadium before the final.","zh":"決賽前，數千名球迷聚集在體育場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a cricket match at the stadium.","zh":"我們在體育場觀看了一場板球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stadium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd16f8cedf79e427","term":"stadium","forms":["stadium","stadiums","stadia"],"pos":"noun","zh":"古希臘賽跑場","explanation":"指古希臘用於賽跑的跑道或賽場，尤其指奧林匹亞等地舉行步行賽跑的場地。這是現代體育場一義的歷史來源。","examples":[{"en":"The ancient stadium at Olympia was used for foot races.","zh":"奧林匹亞的古代賽跑場曾用於舉行步行賽跑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ancient stadium hosted races during the festival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stadium","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1562206543da764123c2","word":"staff","forms":["staff"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4c47feddc7ac064","term":"staff","forms":["staff","staffs","staves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手杖；長杆","explanation":"指一根直而粗的長木杆，尤其是走路時用來支撐身體的手杖。這是staff最具體、最容易聯想到的基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"The old man walked slowly with a wooden staff.","zh":"老人拄著一根木手杖慢慢走著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The traveler leaned on his staff while resting.","zh":"旅行者休息時靠在手杖上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7060e255870b3413","term":"staff","forms":["staff","staffs","staves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"五線譜","explanation":"指音樂中用來寫音符的幾條水平線，也就是五線譜。這裡保留了“用一組線支撐和排列符號”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher wrote the melody on the staff.","zh":"老師把旋律寫在五線譜上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write the notes neatly on the staff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76eef97349ea976b","term":"staff","forms":["staff","staffs","staves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全體員工","explanation":"指在公司、學校、醫院或其他機構工作的一組員工，強調整個員工團隊，而不是某一個人。這個意思可以理解為“共同支撐機構運轉的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel staff were friendly and helpful.","zh":"這家酒店的員工既友好又樂於助人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a member of the school staff.","zh":"她是學校的一名員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c7ff6dcd94d7161eff5d","word":"stage","forms":["stage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d96a919be785b15c","term":"stage","forms":["stage","stages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"階段","explanation":"指一個過程中的某一段或某一發展時期，例如恢復過程中的一個階段。它是“程序被分成的一格”，也是 stage 最重要的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"She is in the final stage of recovery.","zh":"她正處於康復的最後階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project has reached a difficult stage.","zh":"這個專案已經進入了一個困難階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ab83caed89e28c2","term":"stage","forms":["stage","stages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舞臺；臺","explanation":"指演員、樂隊或其他表演者進行公開表演的檯面或場所。由“為活動安排的位置”這一核心概念，可以自然聯想到登上舞臺。","examples":[{"en":"The band came back on stage for one more song.","zh":"樂隊回到舞臺上又演唱了一首歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt nervous before going on stage.","zh":"她上臺前感到很緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ceb7c1c15aead975","term":"stage","forms":["stage","stages","staging","staged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上演；演出","explanation":"指把戲劇、音樂劇等搬上舞臺並進行演出。它是名詞“舞臺”發展出的動作義：把作品安排到舞臺上呈現。","examples":[{"en":"The school will stage a play next month.","zh":"學校下個月將上演一部戲劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater staged a new musical last winter.","zh":"那家劇院去年冬天上演了一部新音樂劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb7d05dc9f8ba837","term":"stage","forms":["stage","stages","staging","staged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"策劃並實施","explanation":"指有計劃地組織並執行一項行動或事件，例如罷工、抗議或活動。它仍然保留“把事情安排到位並公開呈現”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The workers staged a strike outside the factory.","zh":"工人在工廠外組織了一場罷工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thieves staged a distraction near the main entrance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0b469e88b4cb3583c4d","word":"stagger","forms":["stagger"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24683b513bf6bb63","term":"stagger","forms":["stagger","staggers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"踉蹌；搖晃","explanation":"指走路或站立時身體不穩、東搖西晃，彷彿馬上要摔倒，重點是動作本身像失去平衡的腳步。","examples":[{"en":"He crossed the finish line in a stagger, barely able to stand.","zh":"他踉踉蹌蹌地越過終點線，幾乎站不住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He staggered beneath the weight of the trunk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stagger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13cf6d83aca8bd6f","term":"stagger","forms":["stagger","staggers","staggering","staggered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"踉蹌；搖搖晃晃地走","explanation":"指人因醉酒、疲憊、受傷或失去平衡而走得東倒西歪，動作像隨時會摔倒。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, we staggered back to the cabin.","zh":"長途徒步後，我們踉踉蹌蹌地回到了小屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She staggered across the room and collapsed into a chair.","zh":"她搖搖晃晃地穿過房間，倒進了一把椅子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stagger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6303886bb6a3612","term":"stagger","forms":["stagger","staggers","staggering","staggered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"錯開；分批安排","explanation":"指把同類活動安排在不同但均勻分開的時間或地點開始，而不是讓所有人同時進行；這是把“踉蹌的腳步彼此錯開”抽象成日程安排。","examples":[{"en":"The school staggered lunch breaks so that the cafeteria would not be too crowded.","zh":"學校錯開了午餐休息時間，以免食堂過於擁擠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We staggered the interviews throughout the afternoon.","zh":"我們把面試分散安排在整個下午進行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stagger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b547adfe90823f5cb69","word":"stain","forms":["stain"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-366c13377c4e47d8","term":"stain","forms":["stain","stains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汙漬","explanation":"指液體或其他物質接觸表面後留下的有色汙點，例如衣服、地毯或桌面上的汙漬。","examples":[{"en":"There is a coffee stain on my shirt.","zh":"我的襯衫上有一塊咖啡漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This soap should remove the stain.","zh":"這種肥皂應該能去掉這塊汙漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cac11ffbd85d58dc","term":"stain","forms":["stain","stains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"名譽汙點","explanation":"指損害一個人、組織或記錄的行為或事實，彷彿在名譽上留下了洗不掉的汙點。","examples":[{"en":"The scandal left a stain on the company's reputation.","zh":"這起醜聞給公司的聲譽留下了汙點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The false accusation remained a stain on an otherwise honorable career.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0dfbb93e6082bc9","term":"stain","forms":["stain","stains","staining","stained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄髒；染上汙漬","explanation":"指液體或其他物質使某個表面留下顏色或汙點。","examples":[{"en":"The red wine stained the carpet.","zh":"紅酒把地毯染上了汙漬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful not to stain your hands with the ink.","zh":"小心別讓墨水把你的手染髒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a18da37fb228854","term":"stain","forms":["stain","stains","staining","stained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"玷汙名譽","explanation":"指某人的行為或某件事損害了一個人的名譽、聲譽或清白，像留下了無法輕易去掉的汙點。","examples":[{"en":"The false accusation stained his reputation.","zh":"這個誣告玷汙了他的名譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bribery scandal stained his political reputation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-243bd3749f282140","term":"stain","forms":["stain","stains","staining","stained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給表面染色","explanation":"指有意用染色劑給木材等表面上色，藉此改變顏色或突出紋理。","examples":[{"en":"They stained the cabinets a warm brown.","zh":"他們把櫥櫃染成了溫暖的棕色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stain the wooden shelves before applying varnish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8b40f3f8920b8aadf16","word":"stair","forms":["stair"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8ff7d56e40cb119","term":"stair","forms":["stair","stairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臺階","explanation":"指樓梯中的一個階面或一級高度，也就是人向上或向下邁的一步。","examples":[{"en":"I left my bag on the bottom stair.","zh":"我把包放在最下面一級臺階上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful on the last stair; it is uneven.","zh":"小心最後一級臺階，那一級不平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-46adca9e8ae6bc22","term":"stair","forms":["stair","stairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樓梯；一段臺階","explanation":"指許多臺階連續組成的通道，即供人上下樓層的一段樓梯；這個意思正是由“許多步連在一起”發展出來的。","examples":[{"en":"We climbed the narrow wooden stair to the attic.","zh":"我們沿著狹窄的木樓梯爬上了閣樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The narrow stair leads directly to the attic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4caf4ff95731a23e49c","word":"stake","forms":["stake"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8224b1b6c4f0b229","term":"stake","forms":["stake","stakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"木樁；尖樁","explanation":"指一端尖、可以打入地面的長木條或類似材料，常用來標記邊界或支撐東西。這是stake最基本的具體形象。","examples":[{"en":"They placed stakes along the edge of the garden.","zh":"他們沿著花園邊緣插了一排木樁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young trees need stakes for support.","zh":"這些小樹需要木樁支撐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6af790b849f19288","term":"stake","forms":["stake","stakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"利益份額；持有的股份","explanation":"指某人在企業、專案或某種局面中擁有的利益或份額。它來自“把自己的東西壓上去”的引申：投入越多，牽涉的利益通常越大。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a small stake in the company.","zh":"她買下了這家公司的一小部分股份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The investor bought a twenty-percent stake in the company.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a272998544991e9f","term":"stake","forms":["stake","stakes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賭注；押上的東西","explanation":"指為賭局、競爭或某個結果押上的錢、物品或承諾，也可以泛指面臨風險的利益。它和“股份”共享同一個核心：把某種東西壓在結果上。","examples":[{"en":"A lot of money was at stake in the final match.","zh":"決賽中有一大筆錢面臨得失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He put his reputation at stake by making that promise.","zh":"他作出那個承諾，把自己的聲譽置於風險之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-197d1f9a63457d7f","term":"stake","forms":["stake","stakes","staking","staked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用樁固定；標界","explanation":"指用木樁支撐植物、固定物體或標出邊界，就是把“木樁”這個名詞變成“用樁處理”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The gardener staked the tomato plants before the storm.","zh":"園丁在暴風雨來臨前給番茄植株插上支架固定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stake the young tree to keep it upright.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c303f27b051c32f1","term":"stake","forms":["stake","stakes","staking","staked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把某物押在結果上","explanation":"指把錢、名譽、機會等置於某個比賽結果或未來情況之上，結果好就可能獲益，結果不好就會受損。這正是“把東西壓上去”的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"They staked their future on the new product.","zh":"他們把自己的未來押在這款新產品上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I would stake my reputation on her honesty.","zh":"我願意用自己的聲譽擔保她是誠實的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a03f2386ae06b2110957","word":"stale","forms":["stale"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-af487c6f87819cc8","term":"stale","forms":["stale","staler","stalest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不新鮮的","explanation":"指食物等放久了，已經失去新鮮感，可能變幹、變味或開始變質；這正是“放久了，失去新鮮感”的基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"The bread has gone stale, so let's buy a fresh loaf.","zh":"麵包已經不新鮮了，我們買一條新鮮的吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crackers were stale and hard to chew.","zh":"這些餅乾不新鮮了，嚼起來很硬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6efeecbbb664601c","term":"stale","forms":["stale","staler","stalest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陳舊老套的","explanation":"指觀點、笑話、藉口等用得太多或流行太久，已經失去新意，令人覺得老套、乏味；就像笑話放久了一樣失去新鮮感。","examples":[{"en":"That stale joke is no longer funny.","zh":"那個老套的笑話已經不好笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team needs some fresh ideas instead of repeating stale arguments.","zh":"這個團隊需要一些新想法，而不是重複那些老套的論據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5b6a7364e8a1049a923","word":"stall","forms":["stall"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-99581962e40c20b2","term":"stall","forms":["stall","stalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攤位；小店面","explanation":"市場、食品區或類似場所裡向顧客開放的很小的售貨空間；商品和攤主都固定在這個位置上。","examples":[{"en":"We bought fresh fruit from a stall at the market.","zh":"我們在市場的一個攤位買了新鮮水果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a noodle stall near the station.","zh":"車站附近有一個麵攤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-654a4887389d7a7d","term":"stall","forms":["stall","stalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拖延；拖時間","explanation":"故意製造停頓或周旋，使事情暫時無法繼續推進；就像事情被卡在一個位置上。","examples":[{"en":"The repeated phone calls were just a stall until the manager arrived.","zh":"經理到來之前，那些一次次的電話只是用來拖時間的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His long explanation was a stall for time.","zh":"他的長篇解釋只是為了拖延時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c7d68019a1aca3e","term":"stall","forms":["stall","stalls","stalling","stalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"故意拖時間","explanation":"事情像被拖住一樣無法馬上繼續，某人故意放慢行動或東拉西扯，以便爭取時間。","examples":[{"en":"She kept asking pointless questions to stall for time.","zh":"她不停地問些無關緊要的問題，故意拖時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I knew he was stalling to wait for his friend.","zh":"我知道他是在拖時間等朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30a50ee8cf0f5d9c","term":"stall","forms":["stall","stalls","stalling","stalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使手動擋車輛熄火","explanation":"手動擋車輛的速度太低，卻仍使用不合適的高擋位，發動機像被卡住一樣停止運轉。","examples":[{"en":"I stalled the car twice while learning to drive.","zh":"我學開車時把車弄熄火了兩次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engine stalled as I released the clutch too quickly.","zh":"我松離合器太快，發動機熄火了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0afcdbf6ad4adf566c5","word":"stamp","forms":["stamp"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2469ffe3e11a9fa3","term":"stamp","forms":["stamp","stamps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壓出的印記；印痕","explanation":"指用力按壓或踩踏後留下的凹痕、圖案或標記；它是“壓下去並留下痕跡”這條主線的直接結果。","examples":[{"en":"There was a clear stamp of the seal on the document.","zh":"檔案上清楚地留下了印章的印記。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The passport is covered with entry stamps.","zh":"這本護照上蓋滿了入境印章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88f4482c906fb685","term":"stamp","forms":["stamp","stamps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"郵票；繳費票","explanation":"指貼在信件或其他物品上的小紙片，用來預付郵資，也可以表示預付稅費或許可證費用；它本質上是把“已付款”的標記貼上去。","examples":[{"en":"I need a stamp for this letter.","zh":"這封信需要貼一張郵票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put two stamps on the envelope.","zh":"請在信封上貼兩張郵票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1656cdbd23fda75a","term":"stamp","forms":["stamp","stamps","stamping","stamped","stampest","stampedst","stampeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跺腳","explanation":"指快速而用力地踩腳一次或多次，常表現出憤怒、急躁或強烈興奮；這是 stamp 最直接的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The child stamped because he wanted the toy.","zh":"孩子因為想要那個玩具而跺起腳來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stamped angrily out of the room.","zh":"她氣沖沖地跺著腳走出了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b14b550aa8948a9","term":"stamp","forms":["stamp","stamps","stamping","stamped","stampest","stampedst","stampeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓印；打上標記","explanation":"指快速而用力地按壓，在物體表面留下圖案、文字或形狀；這正是從“踩下並留下印記”發展來的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The machine stamps numbers onto each metal part.","zh":"這臺機器把編號壓印在每個金屬零件上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They stamped the bags with the company logo.","zh":"他們在袋子上蓋了公司的標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad195f5d3650f297","term":"stamp","forms":["stamp","stamps","stamping","stamped","stampest","stampedst","stampeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蓋章；加蓋官方標記","explanation":"指透過按壓或印刷給檔案、護照等加上官方認可的標記；它是“留下印記”在行政場景中的固定用法。","examples":[{"en":"The officer stamped my passport at the border.","zh":"工作人員在邊境給我的護照蓋了章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your form must be stamped before it is submitted.","zh":"你的表格必須蓋章後才能提交。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d651dabf895bfd67ce30","word":"stance","forms":["stance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7b0e2db0151b8a8","term":"stance","forms":["stance","stances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"站姿；姿勢","explanation":"指人站立時身體和雙腳的擺放方式，尤其是為了應對某種動作、比賽或危險而採取的姿勢。它就是“站穩的位置”這一核心概念在身體上的體現。","examples":[{"en":"The boxer widened his stance before throwing the punch.","zh":"拳擊手出拳前把雙腳站得更開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her relaxed stance made everyone feel welcome.","zh":"她放鬆自然的站姿讓每個人都感到自在。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b1fbb3e9bbd156d1","term":"stance","forms":["stance","stances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立場；觀點","explanation":"指一個人或組織對某個問題明確採取的態度或觀點，好像在爭論中選擇了一個要站的位置。它往往比普通的“意見”更正式，也更強調一貫性或公開性。","examples":[{"en":"The company has taken a clear stance on workplace safety.","zh":"這家公司已經明確表明了對工作場所安全的立場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I understand your stance, even though I do not agree with it.","zh":"我理解你的立場，儘管我並不同意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d37a24b801c6e2e33824","word":"stand","forms":["stand"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ec82cbbf57badfa","term":"stand","forms":["stand","stands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅定立場","explanation":"指面對反對或壓力時堅持不變的觀點、態度或行動；人是在觀點或原則上“穩穩站住”。","examples":[{"en":"The school took a firm stand against bullying.","zh":"這所學校堅定反對欺凌行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a stand for equal pay.","zh":"她站出來支援同工同酬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2db740362d7a8156","term":"stand","forms":["stand","stands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支架","explanation":"指用來把物品穩穩托住、支撐起來的架子或底座；物品需要藉助它“站住”。","examples":[{"en":"I put the vase on a small wooden stand.","zh":"我把花瓶放在一個小木架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave your umbrella in the stand by the door.","zh":"請把雨傘放在門邊的傘架裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c275ae7279c77eaa","term":"stand","forms":["stand","stands","standing","stood","standen","standest","stoodst","stoodest","standeth","-","stooden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"站著；處在某處","explanation":"指人或物以直立的狀態存在，或處在某個明確的位置；這就是“穩穩站住”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I stood by the window and watched the rain.","zh":"我站在窗邊看雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old tree still stands behind the house.","zh":"那棵老樹仍然立在房子後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0945e300b81cae46","term":"stand","forms":["stand","stands","standing","stood","standen","standest","stoodst","stoodest","standeth","-","stooden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"有望；很可能","explanation":"表示某人或某事處在一種很有可能獲得某種結果的位置上，也就是在機會面前“站得住、佔得上風”。","examples":[{"en":"If sales keep growing, the company stands to make a large profit.","zh":"如果銷量繼續增長，這家公司很可能會獲得豐厚利潤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You stand to lose more than you can afford.","zh":"你可能會損失超出承受能力的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe6d3468cf5c74d8ec2a","word":"standard","forms":["standard"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f4f2cc6a962366b","term":"standard","forms":["standard","most standard"],"pos":"adj","zh":"符合通常標準的","explanation":"表示大小、數量、能力或質量等落在社會或行業認可的正常範圍內。它強調“符合既定尺度”，不一定表示特別優秀。","examples":[{"en":"This model comes in a standard size.","zh":"這款型號有標準尺寸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room has standard ceiling height.","zh":"這個房間的層高符合通常標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/standard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-093f4f42c2c9312f","term":"standard","forms":["standard","most standard"],"pos":"adj","zh":"標配的","explanation":"表示某項裝置或功能通常隨產品一起提供，不需要另行選擇或購買；它是“預設配置”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Air conditioning comes standard on this model.","zh":"這款車型標配空調。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spare tire is standard equipment.","zh":"備胎是標準配置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/standard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01d8fb5958135ff6","term":"standard","forms":["standard","standards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標準；基準","explanation":"指用來比較、衡量或判斷的原則、樣板或水平，是“那把公認的尺子”。它可以是抽象的要求，也可以是一個具體範例。","examples":[{"en":"Safety is the most important standard for this project.","zh":"安全是這個專案最重要的標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new design sets a high standard.","zh":"這個新設計樹立了很高的標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/standard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8970a6e29537b655f643","word":"staple","forms":["staple"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65cfbad1252a4bb8","term":"staple","forms":["staple","staples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主食；基本供應","explanation":"指生活中經常需要、不可缺少的食物或用品，是日常生活的基本支柱。","examples":[{"en":"Beans are a staple in many family meals.","zh":"豆類是許多家庭餐桌上的主食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A flashlight is a camping staple for us.","zh":"手電筒是我們露營時必不可少的用品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ce7b7c4c5ac4014","term":"staple","forms":["staple","staples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"訂書釘","explanation":"指彎成形、用來把紙張或其他薄材料固定在一起的小金屬件。","examples":[{"en":"I found a staple stuck in the corner of the form.","zh":"我發現表格的一角卡著一枚訂書釘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please remove the old staples before scanning the papers.","zh":"掃描檔案前請先取下舊訂書釘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3077d7fb150f7925","term":"staple","forms":["staple","staples","stapling","stapled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用訂書釘固定","explanation":"指用訂書釘把紙張或其他材料固定在一起，正是辦公室裡訂書釘這一名詞義對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"She stapled the receipts together before filing them.","zh":"她把收據訂在一起後再歸檔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Staple the notice to the wall near the entrance.","zh":"把通知釘在入口附近的牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/staple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-525eca1d5089dbdcbb67","word":"star","forms":["star"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-882697f4095077d4","term":"star","forms":["star","stars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"夜空中的星星","explanation":"指夜空中看起來像小亮點的自然天體；在日常說法裡，人們有時也會把行星算作星星。它和記憶中的“夜空中醒目的亮點”直接對應。","examples":[{"en":"The children lay on the grass counting the stars.","zh":"孩子們躺在草地上數星星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stars are brighter than usual tonight.","zh":"今晚的星星比平時更亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/star","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a2d5c4c1be8b84f","term":"star","forms":["star","stars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"明星；名人","explanation":"指在電影、電視、音樂或其他公眾領域中非常出名、像夜空亮點一樣引人注目的人。它也可以泛指某個領域裡最受關注的人。","examples":[{"en":"The singer's new album topped the charts as soon as it was released.","zh":"這位歌星的新專輯一發行就登上了榜首。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many film stars attended the charity gala.","zh":"許多電影明星出席了慈善晚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/star","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-556aa651eedb93bd","term":"star","forms":["star","stars","starring","starred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擔任主演","explanation":"指演員在電影、電視劇、舞臺劇或其他節目中擔任最重要、最受關注的表演者。也就是成為作品中那顆最亮眼的“星星”。","examples":[{"en":"She starred in that historical drama.","zh":"她在那部歷史劇中擔任主演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor has starred in several successful films.","zh":"這名演員曾主演過多部暢銷電影。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/star","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0573feb0e8c35548","term":"star","forms":["star","stars","starring","starred"],"pos":"verb","zh":"由某人主演；讓某人擔任主演","explanation":"指一部電影、節目或演出以某位演員為主要表演者，或安排某人擔任主演。重點在作品把某位演員放在最醒目的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The comedy stars two up-and-coming actors.","zh":"這部喜劇由兩位新晉演員擔任主演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film stars a young actor from our town.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/star","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5884ec40704e38fb2eb1","word":"stare","forms":["stare"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d25fc67a064c740d","term":"stare","forms":["stare","stares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凝視；注視","explanation":"指目光固定在某人或某物上，持續看而不移開；它就是動詞“目不轉睛地看”所形成的名詞。","examples":[{"en":"The strange noise drew a stare from everyone in the room.","zh":"那奇怪的聲音引得房間裡每個人都盯著看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tried to ignore the stares of the passengers.","zh":"他努力不去理會乘客們投來的目光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce0bab818f017126","term":"stare","forms":["stare","stares","staring","stared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"凝視；目不轉睛地看","explanation":"指長時間、專注地看著某人或某物，彷彿眼睛被固定住了；這種目光常讓對方注意到自己。","examples":[{"en":"She stared at the message for several minutes.","zh":"她盯著那條訊息看了好幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't stare at people on the train.","zh":"請不要在火車上盯著別人看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cced28c6dc3f99c2396a","word":"start","forms":["start"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fa8d847746376c2","term":"start","forms":["start","starts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開始","explanation":"start 是一項活動從沒有進行到開始進行的那個階段或過程，也就是“開頭”。","examples":[{"en":"The movie was exciting from start to finish.","zh":"這部電影從頭到尾都很精彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to make a fresh start.","zh":"我們需要重新開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/start","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2a03a2d5ab8b738","term":"start","forms":["start","starts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"突然一驚","explanation":"這裡的 start 是身體或情緒因突然刺激而猛地一動、受到驚嚇的瞬間。","examples":[{"en":"She woke with a start when the door slammed.","zh":"門砰的一聲關上時，她猛然驚醒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A start of recognition crossed his face when he saw the photograph.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/start","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52de3ec2bd6e6da2","term":"start","forms":["start","starts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"起點","explanation":"在比賽、棋盤遊戲或路線中，start 是參與者開始動身的位置或時刻，也就是“起點”。","examples":[{"en":"Place your piece at the start of the board.","zh":"把你的棋子放在棋盤的起點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runners gathered at the start of the race.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/start","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f32b8a6d820ce816","term":"start","forms":["start","starts","starting","started"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開始；啟動","explanation":"start 的核心動詞義是讓活動、過程、計劃或事物從靜止狀態進入進行狀態，也就是“開始、啟動”。","examples":[{"en":"I started reading the book on the train.","zh":"我在火車上開始讀這本書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They started a small business together.","zh":"他們一起創辦了一家小企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/start","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eeecf3c8f5c10528","term":"start","forms":["start","starts","starting","started"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然一動","explanation":"start 也表示原本靜止的人突然動了一下，通常是因為驚嚇或意外刺激，相當於“猛然一驚、驚跳”。","examples":[{"en":"The baby started at the loud noise.","zh":"嬰兒被巨大的聲響嚇得一激靈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She woke with a start when the thunder cracked.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/start","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e34332514b63871ecb7b","word":"startle","forms":["startle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"startle","forms":["startle"],"pos":"v.","zh":"使吃驚；使嚇一跳","examples":[{"en":"Sudden loud noises startle the baby.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Please knock before entering so you do not startle me.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-bdcd69991500ee75d72a","word":"starvation","forms":["starvation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f44649d7091e59a","term":"starvation","forms":["starvation","starvations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飢餓；捱餓","explanation":"指因為沒有足夠食物而遭受嚴重痛苦，強調缺糧造成的危險或長期狀態，而不只是飯點前覺得餓。","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of people are at risk of starvation after the drought.","zh":"乾旱之後，成千上萬的人面臨飢餓的危險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The relief workers brought food to families suffering from starvation.","zh":"救援人員把食物送給遭受飢餓的家庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starvation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ad5233d1f0fe6ba","term":"starvation","forms":["starvation","starvations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資源嚴重短缺","explanation":"把“吃不到食物”的畫面擴充套件到燃料、資金或原材料等資源：某項活動因長期得不到足夠資源而無法正常進行。","examples":[{"en":"Fuel starvation forced the boat to return to port.","zh":"燃料不足迫使這艘船返回港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The service failed because of resource starvation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starvation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c357c470aa5b3c0b5dad","word":"starve","forms":["starve"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7fc74dbd788087b6","term":"starve","forms":["starve","starves","starving","starved","starven","starvest","starvedst","starveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"餓死","explanation":"因沒有食物或長期不進食而死亡，重點是飢餓最終導致了死亡。","examples":[{"en":"Many families starved to death during the famine.","zh":"饑荒期間，許多家庭餓死了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without emergency aid, thousands could starve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e522596ac1d0207","term":"starve","forms":["starve","starves","starving","starved","starven","starvest","starvedst","starveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"因缺糧而受苦","explanation":"因為缺少食物而遭受嚴重飢餓，但不一定已經死亡；它強調捱餓造成的痛苦和困境。","examples":[{"en":"Without help, the trapped hikers could starve for days.","zh":"沒有幫助的話，被困的徒步者可能會捱餓好幾天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Families were starving after months of crop failure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9faafcdf93c9facd","term":"starve","forms":["starve","starves","starving","starved","starven","starvest","starvedst","starveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"餓得厲害","explanation":"表示非常餓，常常是日常口語中的誇張說法，不一定真的會因缺食而受苦或死亡。","examples":[{"en":"I'm starving—let's get something to eat.","zh":"我餓死了，咱們找點東西吃吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were starving after the long hike.","zh":"長途徒步後，孩子們餓壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starve","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7bdf92040f944a6fb30","word":"state(ment)","forms":["state","statement"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed51f2ad8f10c7d4","term":"state","forms":["state","states"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狀態；狀況","explanation":"指某人、某物或某件事在某一時刻所處的情況或條件，也就是“站在什麼樣子裡”。","examples":[{"en":"The house was in a terrible state after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，這所房子的狀況糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Meditation helped her reach a calm state of mind.","zh":"冥想幫助她達到平靜的心境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/state","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-214286c4122682a0","term":"state","forms":["state","states"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家；政治共同體","explanation":"指由政府、法律和領土組織起來的政治共同體，即國家，也可以泛指一個有獨立政治結構的共同體。","examples":[{"en":"The state must protect the rights of its citizens.","zh":"國家必須保護公民的權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He refused to act against his conscience for the sake of the state.","zh":"他拒絕為了國家而違背自己的良心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/state","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5b4afabd6aac79fd","term":"state","forms":["state","states"],"pos":"noun","zh":"州；地方政治實體","explanation":"在聯邦制國家，尤其是美國，state 指組成聯邦的州；它有自己的政府和一定的立法權。","examples":[{"en":"Each state sets its own rules for public schools.","zh":"每個州都會為公立學校制定自己的規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each state has its own education department.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/state","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1eefda57e4b81221","term":"state","forms":["state","States"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家；州；政治實體","explanation":"指一個現實中正在運作的國家、州、城市國家或其他政治共同體，重點是它作為治理機構和公共權力實體的存在。","examples":[{"en":"A modern state needs clear laws and effective institutions.","zh":"現代國家需要明確的法律和有效的制度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each state sets its own school funding rules.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/state","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a98d82133e63a4c","term":"state","forms":["state","states","stating","stated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"陳述為事實","explanation":"指明確地說某件事是事實，常用於報告、宣告或正式表達中，帶有把資訊清楚擺出來的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The report states that the bridge is unsafe.","zh":"報告稱這座橋不安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She clearly stated her reasons for leaving.","zh":"她清楚地說明了自己離開的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/state","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cc42fbcb5d07356","term":"statement","forms":["statement","statements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宣告；說法","explanation":"指一個人或機構明確說出或寫下的一段話，重點是把資訊、態度或事實公開表達出來。","examples":[{"en":"The company made a statement about the safety issue.","zh":"公司就安全問題發表了一份宣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't want to make a statement until I know all the facts.","zh":"在瞭解全部事實之前，我不想發表任何說法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-118ef3653054e523","term":"statement","forms":["statement","statements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立場；觀點陳述","explanation":"指用語言明確表達自己的看法、態度或政治立場。它仍然是“把想法擺出來”，但重點不在報告事實，而在說明支援什麼、反對什麼或主張什麼。","examples":[{"en":"The group released a statement supporting the new policy.","zh":"該團體發表了一份支援新政策的立場宣告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manifesto includes a clear statement on housing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b481b5f2ea301d4c","term":"statement","forms":["statement","statements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"賬單；財務明細","explanation":"指把一段時間內的財務活動列出來的檔案，例如銀行賬戶的收入、支出、餘額和交易記錄。它是把賬目“擺出來給你看”，並不只是泛指任何財務報告。","examples":[{"en":"I checked my bank statement and found a charge I didn't recognize.","zh":"我檢視了銀行賬單，發現一筆無法確認的收費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check your bank statement for unfamiliar transactions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8c495a95067ddf162ff","word":"statesman","forms":["statesman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a8fb9846909d4df","term":"statesman","forms":["statesman","statesmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家或國際事務的男性領袖","explanation":"指在國家或國際事務中發揮領導作用的男性政治家，重點是他能從全域性出發處理重大問題，而不只是擔任某個政治職位。","examples":[{"en":"He became a respected statesman after decades in public life.","zh":"他從政數十年後成為一位受人尊敬的政治家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The summit brought together statesmen from several countries.","zh":"這次峰會聚集了來自幾個國家的政治領袖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statesman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d3046b11d15bba8","term":"statesman","forms":["statesman","statesmen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"以公共利益為重的男性政治家","explanation":"指不僅有政治領導力，而且被認為正直、有遠見、善於治理國家並促進公共利益的男性政治家；這裡的評價色彩比一般的“政治領袖”更強。","examples":[{"en":"Many people remember her opponent as a statesman who put peace before party politics.","zh":"許多人記得她的對手是一位把和平置於黨派政治之上的政治家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The respected statesman negotiated peace despite fierce domestic opposition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statesman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b4ef3e5b7b4d1759cb8","word":"station","forms":["station"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d969894dad232e6e","term":"station","forms":["station","stations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車站","explanation":"供火車、地鐵等交通工具停靠、讓乘客上下車的地點。這是 station 最常見、最容易先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The next station is Esperanza.","zh":"下一站是埃斯佩蘭薩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I left my umbrella at the station.","zh":"我把傘落在車站了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/station","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-90b4f65bedcd31b2","term":"station","forms":["station","stations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工作站點","explanation":"指警察、消防員、廣播員等工作人員固定值守或工作的地點，重點是“人在這裡執行職責”。","examples":[{"en":"The police station is opposite the fire station.","zh":"警察局在消防站對面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works at a small radio station.","zh":"她在一家小型廣播電臺工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/station","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8784022f140fb78c","term":"station","forms":["station","stations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身份地位","explanation":"把“固定位置”引申為一個人在社會中的身份、等級或應有的位置。通常暗含某種地位界限，例如認為某人的行為超出了自己的身份。","examples":[{"en":"She had ambitions beyond her station.","zh":"她有超出自己身份地位的抱負。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He married someone considered above his station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/station","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3f7fc136777eff3882e","word":"stationary","forms":["stationary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c074a3b324cf3c31","term":"stationary","forms":["stationary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"靜止的","explanation":"指人或物當時沒有移動，仍停在原處；重點是“站在那裡不動”這一狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The bus remained stationary while the driver checked the engine.","zh":"司機檢查發動機時，公共汽車一直停著不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the camera stationary during the exposure.","zh":"曝光期間要讓相機保持不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stationary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48dfd9cc07c8842f","term":"stationary","forms":["stationary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不能移動的","explanation":"強調某物本身無法被搬動或移動，而不只是眼下暫時停住；它像是被牢牢固定在原處。","examples":[{"en":"The large stone is stationary and cannot be lifted by one person.","zh":"這塊大石頭無法移動，一個人搬不起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stationary engine powered the mill machinery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stationary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2666691322310c79138","word":"stationery","forms":["stationery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e2b5013aba76e78e","term":"stationery","forms":["stationery","stationeries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文具；辦公用品","explanation":"stationery 指用來寫字、寄信或辦公的一整類材料，如紙張、信封、練習本和其他文具。它把許多具體用品看成一個不可數的整體，而不是某一件單獨的物品。","examples":[{"en":"I need to buy some stationery for the new school year.","zh":"我需要為新學年買些文具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps her stationery in the top drawer.","zh":"她把文具放在最上面的抽屜裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stationery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e6a5f6ccae60984b561","word":"statistic(s)","forms":["statistic","statistics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4701e53c0ba4e928","term":"statistic","forms":["statistic","statistics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統計數值","explanation":"指根據一組樣本資料計算出的、用來概括某個重要特徵的數值，例如平均數或標準差。它把一批資料壓縮成一個便於比較和分析的數字。","examples":[{"en":"The mean is a useful statistic for comparing the two groups.","zh":"平均數是比較這兩組資料的一個有用統計量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers reported several statistics from the sample.","zh":"研究人員報告了這個樣本的幾個統計量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statistic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-138c095308bb6d9a","term":"statistics","forms":["statistics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統計學","explanation":"統計學是一套從資料中尋找規律、作出分析和判斷的方法；它關注資料怎樣被收集、展示、分析和解釋。","examples":[{"en":"She studied statistics at university.","zh":"她在大學學習統計學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Statistics helps researchers understand large amounts of data.","zh":"統計學幫助研究人員理解大量資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statistics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-495aaf09fe2d033f","term":"statistics","forms":["statistics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統計資料","explanation":"統計資料是把人口、收入、年齡等觀察結果系統地記錄並彙總後得到的數字資料；它們是統計學處理現實資訊後的具體成果。","examples":[{"en":"The latest statistics show that more people are working from home.","zh":"最新統計資料顯示，越來越多的人在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The statistics show a steady decline in road deaths.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statistics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8f9c6d33384115eeb63","word":"statistical","forms":["statistical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17a4a3a590492634","term":"statistical","forms":["statistical","more statistical","most statistical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"統計的；與統計學有關的","explanation":"用於說明某件事涉及統計學，或依靠對資料的收集、整理和分析；例如統計分析是從大量資料中尋找規律的方法。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used statistical analysis to compare the two groups.","zh":"研究人員使用統計分析來比較這兩組人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report includes several statistical charts showing changes in population.","zh":"這份報告包含幾張展示人口變化的統計圖表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statistical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c12b7c138c5e2c139672","word":"statue","forms":["statue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3cfbc1d2c84d7b25","term":"statue","forms":["statue","statues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雕像；塑像","explanation":"指以人、動物等為物件，用雕刻、塑形或鑄造等方式製作的立體藝術作品；記住“把形象立起來並固定成形”即可掌握這個核心義。","examples":[{"en":"A statue of the town's founder stands in the square.","zh":"小鎮建立者的雕像立在廣場上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has a marble statue of a sleeping dog.","zh":"這家博物館裡有一尊大理石睡狗雕像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44d27fd7bb57ecd55792","word":"stature","forms":["stature"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e16bb867e0a074d4","term":"stature","forms":["stature","statures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身高；身材高度","explanation":"指人或動物直立時從腳到頭的自然高度，也就是站起來後量出的身高。這裡關注的是身體的垂直高度，不是體重或整體體格。","examples":[{"en":"Despite his small stature, the dog was surprisingly strong.","zh":"這隻狗雖然個頭不大，卻出奇地強壯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The athlete's stature made it easy to spot him in the crowd.","zh":"這名運動員的身高讓人很容易在人群中認出他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d67b4c00baf35ec6","term":"stature","forms":["stature","statures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地位；聲望；影響力","explanation":"把身體上的“高度”引申為一個人在社會、行業或團隊中的“分量”：一個人的成就越多，往往越受尊重，地位和影響力也越高。它強調透過能力、發展或成就逐漸獲得的聲望。","examples":[{"en":"Her research has greatly increased her stature in the scientific community.","zh":"她的研究成果大大提高了她在科學界的地位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The prize raised her international stature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-073c1634c496cdb649d1","word":"status","forms":["status"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d22181ddd4664389","term":"status","forms":["status","statuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"社會地位；身份條件","explanation":"指一個人在社會或群體中所處的位置，以及由此體現出的身份條件。它可以涉及財富、職業、背景等，但重點是“處在什麼位置”。","examples":[{"en":"Education can improve a person's social status.","zh":"教育可以提高一個人的社會地位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two groups have very different economic status.","zh":"這兩個群體的經濟地位非常不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/status","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64de49d75f975677","term":"status","forms":["status","statuses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"進展；當前情況","explanation":"把事情看成一張記錄進度的“位置卡”，表示某項工作、調查或計劃目前進行到什麼程度、處於什麼情況。","examples":[{"en":"Could you tell me the status of my application?","zh":"你能告訴我我的申請進展如何嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are waiting for an update on the status of the project.","zh":"我們正在等待專案進展的更新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/status","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-503acf004b50b4f97bea","word":"statute","forms":["statute"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3170acd4593dd50e","term":"statute","forms":["statute","statutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成文法；法令","explanation":"指由立法機關正式透過並寫成法律文字的規定，通常適用於整個社會或某一類人。","examples":[{"en":"The new statute limited working hours.","zh":"新法律限制了工作時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agency must act under the statute.","zh":"該機構必須依法行事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23c7caa14a7b00f5","term":"statute","forms":["statute","statutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機構規章","explanation":"指學校、公司、協會等組織正式制定的內部規則或章程性規定。","examples":[{"en":"The club's statutes require an annual election.","zh":"該俱樂部的規章要求每年舉行一次選舉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university's statutes determine how fellows are appointed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39be15289c7942a8e776","word":"stay","forms":["stay"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce6ce8b2d12d7b5c","term":"stay","forms":["stay","stays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"停留；住宿","explanation":"指人在某地留下並待了一段時間，時間長短可以不明確；核心仍是讓人保持在原處。","examples":[{"en":"Our stay by the sea was two days longer than planned.","zh":"我們在海邊的停留比原計劃多了兩天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had a three-night stay at the hotel.","zh":"她在這家旅館住了三晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29525146b76f66b7","term":"stay","forms":["stay","stays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支撐物","explanation":"指幫助物體保持位置、形狀或穩定性的支撐物，正如核心概念中“讓東西保持穩定”。","examples":[{"en":"This wooden post is an important stay for the roof.","zh":"這根木柱是屋頂的重要支撐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In difficult times, she was a constant stay for her family.","zh":"在困難時期，她一直是家人的精神支柱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0628373590ae599f","term":"stay","forms":["stay","stays","staying","stayed","staid","stayest","stayedst","stayeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停留；留下","explanation":"指人在某個地方保持不動或繼續在那裡一段時間，強調“留下來”，而不是馬上離開。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed in a small hotel near the station for three nights.","zh":"我們在車站附近的一家小旅館住了三個晚上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please stay here until I come back.","zh":"請留在這裡，直到我回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-594a08e65acb8687","term":"stay","forms":["stay","stays","staying","stayed","staid","stayest","stayedst","stayeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停止；延遲","explanation":"表示讓某件事保持不動、不繼續進行，因此可譯為“停止”或“延遲”。這是把“保持在原處”的概念用於行動或程序。","examples":[{"en":"The court stayed the order until the appeal was heard.","zh":"法院暫緩執行這項命令，直到審理上訴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy snow stayed the trains for several hours.","zh":"大雪使列車延誤了幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stay","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57e1f047b30bdadc4b84","word":"steady","forms":["steady"],"officialPos":"adj./v./adv./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae2b62c6d0022e14","term":"steady","forms":["steady","steadier","steadiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"穩固不搖","explanation":"形容物體站得穩、位置固定，不會搖晃或倒下。它對應記憶中的“穩穩放在桌上的杯子”。","examples":[{"en":"Please hold the camera steady.","zh":"請把相機拿穩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a steady hand for drawing.","zh":"她畫畫時手很穩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fe6db6cd94fd27e","term":"steady","forms":["steady","steadier","steadiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅定不變","explanation":"形容感情、目標或做事態度持續堅定，不輕易動搖或改變。物理上的“不搖”擴充套件成了思想和行動上的“站得住”。","examples":[{"en":"He remained steady in his decision.","zh":"他對自己的決定始終堅定不移。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has been a steady supporter of the project.","zh":"她一直堅定地支援這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6bec1f2de4f50f0","term":"steady","forms":["steady","steadies","steadying","steadied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使穩定","explanation":"把正在搖晃的物體、身體或情緒扶住、控制住，使它不再繼續搖擺；也可表示使自己的緊張情緒穩定下來。","examples":[{"en":"I took a deep breath to steady my nerves.","zh":"我深吸一口氣，讓自己鎮定下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He steadied the chair before the child climbed onto it.","zh":"孩子爬上去前，他先把椅子扶穩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steady","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aff0f313b5568afc194b","word":"steak","forms":["steak"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5054c0c0d869ed7d","term":"steak","forms":["steak","steaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牛排","explanation":"最常見的意思是切成適合煎、烤或炙烤的牛肉厚片，通常作為一份主菜。它是“從大塊肉上切下一片來烹調”這一核心形象的典型例子。","examples":[{"en":"We ordered two steaks and a salad for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐點了兩份牛排和一份沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cooked the steak until it was medium rare.","zh":"她把牛排煎到五分熟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c719451c5b64c5be","term":"steak","forms":["steak","steaks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"其他食材的厚片","explanation":"這個意思把“厚切的一片食材”這一形象擴充套件到牛肉以外的動物肉、魚類甚至蔬菜，所以可以說豬排、鹿排、三文魚排，也可以說花椰菜排或茄子排。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves grilled salmon steaks with lemon.","zh":"這家餐館供應配檸檬的烤三文魚排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She grilled a thick cauliflower steak for dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0fd408352bd19a22a88","word":"steal","forms":["steal"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddbf9b21a1a64b28","term":"steal","forms":["steal","steals","stealing","stole","stolen","stealest","stolest","stealeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偷走","explanation":"指未經物主允許拿走別人的東西，而且通常沒有打算歸還；這是 steal 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Someone stole my bicycle from outside the shop.","zh":"有人把我的腳踏車從商店外偷走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting was stolen from the museum.","zh":"那幅畫被人從博物館偷走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91b7f0fba71acb62","term":"steal","forms":["steal","steals","stealing","stole","stolen","stealest","stolest","stealeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偷偷取得","explanation":"指用不顯眼或巧妙的方式得到某物，未必是真正犯罪，例如偷偷看一眼或悄悄獲得一個機會。","examples":[{"en":"He stole a quick glance at the clock.","zh":"他偷偷瞥了一眼時鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stole a glance at the unopened letter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8b230dc11ff88c0","term":"steal","forms":["steal","steals","stealing","stole","stolen","stealest","stolest","stealeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"悄悄移動","explanation":"指安靜、秘密地移動，儘量不讓別人發現；這裡是把“偷偷拿走”擴充套件成“偷偷離開或靠近”。","examples":[{"en":"She stole out of the room before anyone noticed.","zh":"她趁沒人注意，悄悄走出了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child stole quietly out of the bedroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f1f29444c093e2890d2","word":"steam","forms":["steam"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43aee5828dee91dc","term":"steam","forms":["steam","steams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蒸汽","explanation":"水受熱後變成的熱氣，尤其是接近沸點時形成的氣體。這是 steam 最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Steam rose from the pot as the water began to boil.","zh":"水開始沸騰時，蒸汽從鍋裡升了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep your face away from the steam.","zh":"把臉離蒸汽遠一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f9ecfc4e86f982c","term":"steam","forms":["steam","steams","steaming","steamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蒸熟；用蒸汽烹調","explanation":"用蒸汽把食物煮熟，是 steam 作動詞最常用的意思之一。它把名詞“蒸汽”直接變成了烹調動作。","examples":[{"en":"Steam the fish for eight minutes.","zh":"把魚蒸八分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We steamed some dumplings for lunch.","zh":"我們午餐蒸了一些餃子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b86262f9bc892590bb31","word":"steel","forms":["steel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bf98cff04eb021f","term":"steel","forms":["steel","steels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋼","explanation":"指一種堅硬而有韌性的金屬，核心形象就是“鋼材”。","examples":[{"en":"The tools are made of steel.","zh":"這些工具是用鋼製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Steel is widely used in construction.","zh":"鋼廣泛用於建築業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04a6beca53b56eb6","term":"steel","forms":["steel","steels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鋼鐵般的堅韌","explanation":"比喻人的意志、性格或事物具有鋼一樣的硬度和抗打擊能力，即極其堅強、堅韌。","examples":[{"en":"She showed a remarkable steel under pressure.","zh":"她在壓力下表現出了非凡的堅韌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His nerves are steel.","zh":"他的神經堅如鋼鐵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aaa84acb9758cff125a1","word":"steep","forms":["steep"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7f15e8153520193","term":"steep","forms":["steep","steeper","steepest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陡峭的","explanation":"形容山坡、道路、屋頂等上升得很急，接近豎直方向。它強調角度大、走起來或爬起來費力。","examples":[{"en":"The path becomes very steep near the top.","zh":"這條小路接近山頂時變得非常陡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful on the steep steps.","zh":"走這些陡峭的臺階時要小心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57fce44d7c6df51ad852","word":"steer","forms":["steer"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-694d75c843cf9943","term":"steer","forms":["steer","steers","steering","steered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"駛向某處","explanation":"船、車或其他交通工具自己朝某個方向行進時，steer 表示沿著或轉向那條路線，就像交通工具被舵帶著走。","examples":[{"en":"The captain steered toward the quiet harbor.","zh":"船長把船駛向安靜的港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The canoe steered easily between the partly submerged trees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c6377e89bfc9f2c6","term":"steer","forms":["steer","steers","steering","steered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"操控交通工具","explanation":"steer 也表示用方向盤、船舵或類似裝置控制船、車等的方向。","examples":[{"en":"She learned to steer the small boat by herself.","zh":"她學會了自己操控那條小船的方向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She steered the boat away from the rocks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ead301037354f030","term":"steer","forms":["steer","steers","steering","steered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引導某人或某事走向某方向","explanation":"從控制交通工具的方向引申，steer 可以表示透過影響或安排，把人、團體或事情帶向某個地方、決定或結果。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher steered the discussion toward practical solutions.","zh":"老師把討論引向了切實可行的解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her friends steered her away from a risky investment.","zh":"她的朋友們勸她避開一項有風險的投資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-919a11f948095f31d922","word":"stem","forms":["stem"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e6b3c05616ef021","term":"stem","forms":["stem","stems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"植物的莖","explanation":"stem 是植物的主幹或莖，負責支撐枝葉、花或果實；在植物學中也可指形態相近的地下主軸。把它記成植物的“主幹”最容易掌握。","examples":[{"en":"The flower stem broke under the weight of the rain.","zh":"花莖在雨水的重壓下折斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"New leaves are growing from the stem.","zh":"新的葉子正從莖上長出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de6593cba7575851","term":"stem","forms":["stem","stems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詞幹","explanation":"在語言學中，stem 是一個詞去掉部分詞綴後、可以繼續加詞綴形成不同詞形的核心部分；它像詞語的“骨架”。它有時還包含詞根以外的成分，所以不一定等同於 root。","examples":[{"en":"The suffix is added to the verb stem to form the past tense.","zh":"在動詞詞幹後加上字尾可以構成過去時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Students should identify the stem before adding the ending.","zh":"學生應先找出詞幹，再新增詞尾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8a9df4471f75894","term":"stem","forms":["stem","stems","stemming","stemmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"源自","explanation":"stem from 表示某事由某個原因、背景或源頭產生，就像沿著“主幹”追溯回去。主語通常是問題、結果、情緒或事件。","examples":[{"en":"Most of the delays stem from a lack of staff.","zh":"大部分延誤都源於人手不足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her confidence stems from years of practice.","zh":"她的自信來自多年的練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-077f012746272fbb","term":"stem","forms":["stem","stems","stemming","stemmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"阻止；遏制","explanation":"像用主幹頂住來勢一樣，阻止河水、血液、潮流或某種不良趨勢繼續發展或擴散。","examples":[{"en":"The new barriers helped stem the flow of floodwater.","zh":"新的屏障幫助遏制了洪水的流動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign aims to stem the spread of false information.","zh":"這項活動旨在遏制虛假資訊的傳播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stem","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e64cc41cf8e07b43936","word":"step","forms":["step"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-061b815e863fbec2","term":"step","forms":["step","steps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腳步；一步","explanation":"指一隻腳向前落下所邁出的一步，正是“腳向前落下一步”這個核心畫面，也可以泛指邁步的動作或步伐。","examples":[{"en":"She took a step toward the door and stopped again.","zh":"她向門口邁了一步，又停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children walked step by step across the icy path.","zh":"孩子們一步一步地走過結冰的小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/step","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41f6875098e20aac","term":"step","forms":["step","steps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臺階；梯級","explanation":"指樓梯或梯子上供腳落下、支撐身體的一級，腳落下後就形成了一個可以上下的臺階。","examples":[{"en":"There are three high steps at the entrance.","zh":"入口處有三個很高的臺階。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please be careful on the last step.","zh":"請小心最後一級臺階。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/step","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-523aad767bd23a7b","term":"step","forms":["step","steps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"步驟；階段","explanation":"指一個過程中的獨立部分：腳步連續向前，就像事情也按一個個步驟向前推進，因而step可以表示階段或環節。","examples":[{"en":"Checking the information is the first step in applying for a loan.","zh":"核對資訊是申請貸款的第一步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We will solve this problem step by step.","zh":"我們會一步一步地解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/step","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a021948738abe71","term":"step","forms":["step","steps","stepping","stepped","stept","stope"],"pos":"verb","zh":"邁步；走動","explanation":"腳向前落下一步，就是邁步或走動；既可以表示向前，也可以表示向後退一步。","examples":[{"en":"Please step back so everyone can see the screen.","zh":"請往後退一步，讓大家都能看到螢幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stepped carefully onto the wet floor.","zh":"她小心地邁上了溼地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/step","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9cccd6bf8e102ba08e5","word":"stepchild","forms":["stepchild"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"stepchild","forms":["stepchild"],"pos":"n.","zh":"繼子；繼女","examples":[{"en":"She welcomed her stepchild into the family with patience and care.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"He has a close relationship with his teenage stepchild.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-fd2b9ca56af8ee2f1821","word":"stepfather","forms":["stepfather"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03e5c5676bdafdc4","term":"stepfather","forms":["stepfather","stepfathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繼父","explanation":"指母親在與孩子生父的婚姻或伴侶關係之後所嫁的丈夫，也就是後來進入家庭、承擔父親角色的男性。","examples":[{"en":"My stepfather taught me how to ride a bike.","zh":"我的繼父教我騎腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She moved to Chicago with her mother and stepfather.","zh":"她和母親及繼父搬到了芝加哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stepfather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa9528345ad79c6a","term":"stepfather","forms":["stepfather","stepfathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"非生父的父母一方的丈夫","explanation":"也可泛指與孩子父母中的一方結婚、因而成為孩子家庭中父親角色的男性，即使他並不是孩子母親在上一段關係之後再婚的丈夫。","examples":[{"en":"After the wedding, he became a stepfather to two young children.","zh":"婚禮後，他成了兩個年幼孩子的繼父。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her stepfather married her mother when she was ten.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stepfather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50ce7f637ab2bf4ecad7","word":"stepmother","forms":["stepmother"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-445704b6a0ed1d2f","term":"stepmother","forms":["stepmother","stepmothers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繼母","explanation":"指父親的妻子，但她不是自己的生母；重點是家庭關係中的“父親再婚後的母親角色”。","examples":[{"en":"My stepmother helped me choose a dress for the wedding.","zh":"我的繼母幫我挑選了婚禮上要穿的禮服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He still visits his stepmother every Sunday.","zh":"他每個星期天仍然去看望繼母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stepmother","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b526aece29170b6c0a5c","word":"stereo","forms":["stereo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-424fa73ad5ccd594","term":"stereo","forms":["stereo","stereos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"立體聲系統","explanation":"指用左右兩個聲道錄製、傳送或還原聲音的系統；核心想法仍是讓聲音聽起來像從不同位置傳來。","examples":[{"en":"This recording sounds much better in stereo.","zh":"這段錄音用立體聲播放好聽得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater recently upgraded its stereo system.","zh":"這家劇院最近升級了立體聲系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28fcc4572ac6fdf602bb","word":"stereotype","forms":["stereotype"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a6b07301028a3e7","term":"stereotype","forms":["stereotype","stereotypes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刻板印象","explanation":"指把某類人或群體都想成同一種樣子，並且往往忽略個體差異的固定看法。這種看法通常過於簡單，甚至帶有誇張或偏見。","examples":[{"en":"The film challenges the stereotype that older people dislike technology.","zh":"這部電影挑戰了“老年人不喜歡科技”的刻板印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Assuming that all artists are disorganized is a stereotype.","zh":"認為所有藝術家都不善於整理，是一種刻板印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-117beab7246ca05c","term":"stereotype","forms":["stereotype","stereotypes","stereotyping","stereotyped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使刻板化；用刻板印象看待","explanation":"指把某人、某群體或某種事物壓進固定模板，用一個簡單形象代替對真實差異的認識。","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement stereotypes women as shoppers who care only about appearance.","zh":"這則廣告把女性刻板地描繪成只在乎外表的購物者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children should not be stereotyped because of their accent.","zh":"不應該因為孩子的口音就對他們抱有刻板看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stereotype","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0727fc6654c3e54739f2","word":"stew","forms":["stew"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1aa924eb591a08e7","term":"stew","forms":["stew","stews"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燉菜","explanation":"指把肉、蔬菜等放在液體中，用小火慢慢煮成的菜。它保留了“食材在熱氣中慢慢翻滾”的核心畫面，通常味道濃厚、質地柔軟。","examples":[{"en":"We had a hearty beef stew for dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐吃了香濃的燉牛肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stew tastes even better the next day.","zh":"這道燉菜第二天吃味道更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c0275c3b8943efd","term":"stew","forms":["stew","stews","stewing","stewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用小火燉煮","explanation":"指讓食物在液體中保持低溫，慢慢煮熟，使食材逐漸變軟、味道融合。它就像讓食物在鍋裡安靜地“悶燒”。","examples":[{"en":"I'm going to stew some chicken with carrots.","zh":"我打算把雞肉和胡蘿蔔一起燉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Let the beans stew until they are tender.","zh":"把豆子燉到變軟為止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stew","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f53dd914ced58d84b4d","word":"stick","forms":["stick"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6a234a63057c2d4","term":"stick","forms":["stick","sticks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棍；棒","explanation":"指由木頭或類似材料製成的細長物，通常拿來支撐、敲打、引導或作其他用途；這正是“固定不動”的棍子形象。","examples":[{"en":"The children collected sticks to make a small shelter.","zh":"孩子們撿了些樹枝，搭了一個小避難所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He used a stick to support the young tree.","zh":"他用一根木棍支撐那棵小樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d9885fb9fbf11b0","term":"stick","forms":["stick","sticks","sticking","stuck","sticked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"粘住","explanation":"像棍子固定在表面上一樣，指某物附著在另一物上，不容易分開。","examples":[{"en":"This tape will stick to the wall.","zh":"這卷膠帶會粘在牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The label stuck to the glass.","zh":"標籤粘在玻璃上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4174c400c50b6d7","term":"stick","forms":["stick","sticks","sticking","stuck","sticked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"卡住","explanation":"像一根棍子被卡在那裡一樣，指某物停止移動，無法順利執行。","examples":[{"en":"The drawer sticks whenever I try to close it.","zh":"我每次想關抽屜時，它都會卡住。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The door got stuck in the cold weather.","zh":"天氣寒冷時，門卡住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-212bba9e65449775","term":"stick","forms":["stick","sticks","sticking","stuck","sticked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忍受；堅持","explanation":"指像固定住一樣繼續承受某種困難，或堅持做某事而不輕易放棄。","examples":[{"en":"I can’t stick this job much longer.","zh":"這份工作我再也忍受不了多久了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If you stick with the plan, you’ll see results.","zh":"如果你堅持這個計劃，就會看到成效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-964a9431ff491fd7e0d7","word":"sticky","forms":["sticky"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5295a60612f8f31","term":"sticky","forms":["sticky","stickier","stickiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有黏性的","explanation":"指表面或物質帶有黏性，能把別的東西粘住，通常是因為其中的液體或膠狀物正在變幹。","examples":[{"en":"The label is too sticky to remove easily.","zh":"這個標籤太黏了，不容易撕下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is this tape sticky enough to stay on the wall?","zh":"這膠帶夠黏嗎，能一直貼在牆上嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sticky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29c4fd22c670081f","term":"sticky","forms":["sticky","stickier","stickiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"棘手的","explanation":"把“黏住、難以擺脫”的感覺引申到事情上，表示局面複雜尷尬、難處理。","examples":[{"en":"We are in a sticky situation and need a careful plan.","zh":"我們正處在一個棘手的局面，需要仔細計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporter asked a sticky question.","zh":"那名記者問了一個很難回答的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sticky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-e7f93a628beebf7cd313","word":"stiff","forms":["stiff"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-23804c6c78d50ba5","term":"stiff","forms":["stiff","stiffer","stiffest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"堅硬的","explanation":"東西很硬，不容易彎曲或改變形狀；這是“硬”這個核心意思最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The cardboard is too stiff to fold neatly.","zh":"這張硬紙板太硬，沒法整齊地摺疊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The paintbrush became stiff after the varnish dried.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stiff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96625e43f123a848","term":"stiff","forms":["stiff","stiffer","stiffest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"拘謹的","explanation":"人的舉止像被“硬”住一樣，不放鬆、不自然，顯得正式而拘束。","examples":[{"en":"He seemed stiff at first, but soon joined the conversation.","zh":"他起初顯得很拘謹，但很快就加入了談話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their conversation remained stiff and formal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stiff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b7c18b52414ad79","term":"stiff","forms":["stiff","stiffer","stiffest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"僵痛的","explanation":"身體在不習慣或過量運動後變得又硬又痛，活動起來不靈活。","examples":[{"en":"My shoulders are still stiff after carrying those boxes.","zh":"搬完那些箱子後，我的肩膀現在還很僵痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My neck felt stiff after sleeping in the chair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stiff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-795423782e5af55d","term":"stiff","forms":["stiff","stiffer","stiffest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"強勁的；烈的","explanation":"風、酒、藥物或打擊的力量很“硬”，因此表示強勁、濃烈或效力大。","examples":[{"en":"A stiff wind pushed the boat away from the dock.","zh":"一陣強風把船從碼頭邊吹開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered a stiff drink after the stressful meeting.","zh":"那場令人緊張的會議結束後，她要了一杯烈酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stiff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94e8566ddfc123edf115","word":"still","forms":["still"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e528588c9ff9d43","term":"still","forms":["still","stiller","more still","stillest","most still"],"pos":"adj","zh":"靜止的","explanation":"表示人或物完全不動，像一池沒有波紋的水。","examples":[{"en":"Please hold still while I tie your shoelace.","zh":"我給你繫鞋帶時，請保持不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cat stayed still under the table.","zh":"那隻貓一動不動地待在桌子下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3e6ad3f60119ec9","term":"still","forms":["still"],"pos":"adv","zh":"仍然；還","explanation":"表示某種動作或狀態從之前延續到現在，就像水面一直沒有改變。","examples":[{"en":"Are you still working on that report?","zh":"你還在做那份報告嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is still raining outside.","zh":"外面還在下雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-519bb239b554c637","term":"still","forms":["still"],"pos":"adv","zh":"仍然；到那時還","explanation":"強調在某個過去或現在所指的時間點，情況依舊沒有改變。","examples":[{"en":"At midnight, the children were still awake.","zh":"到了午夜，孩子們還醒著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even after the apology, she still refused to speak.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-294050f9de4be10c","term":"still","forms":["still"],"pos":"adv","zh":"更加","explanation":"放在比較級前，表示在已經更高的程度上還要更高。","examples":[{"en":"The second route is still faster than the first.","zh":"第二條路線比第一條還要快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This version is better still.","zh":"這個版本還要更好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f765d7e0f70ec262","term":"still","forms":["still"],"pos":"adv","zh":"儘管如此；還是","explanation":"在前面情況不利或存在轉折時，表示後面的事仍然發生。","examples":[{"en":"I was tired, but I still went for a walk.","zh":"我雖然累了，但還是去散了步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was raining; still, we enjoyed the walk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab5e345f2c28facc30d7","word":"stimulate","forms":["stimulate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60154d40780d87c0","term":"stimulate","forms":["stimulate","stimulates","stimulating","stimulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"促進發展","explanation":"指採取措施或施加影響，使經濟、增長、需求等更快發展或更加活躍；這裡的核心畫面是把某件事向前推動。","examples":[{"en":"Lower interest rates are intended to stimulate economic growth.","zh":"降低利率旨在促進經濟增長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The grant stimulated investment in clean energy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stimulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5233274cfe7e075","term":"stimulate","forms":["stimulate","stimulates","stimulating","stimulated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"激發活動","explanation":"指使身體、器官、大腦或其他生物功能開始活動，或變得更加活躍；它仍然是“喚醒並推動運作”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Puzzles stimulate my mind and help me stay focused.","zh":"拼圖遊戲能激發我的思維，幫助我保持專注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The grant stimulated research into cheaper solar cells.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stimulate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-41a14ef0a30a812946b6","word":"stimulation","forms":["stimulation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9760c3192564505","term":"stimulation","forms":["stimulation","stimulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推動行動；激勵","explanation":"指用鼓勵、壓力或其他推動力，使某人開始行動或更積極地做事。核心畫面是按下啟動按鈕：原本沒有行動的人受到推動後動起來。","examples":[{"en":"The promise of a bonus provided stimulation to work harder.","zh":"獎金的承諾推動大家更加努力地工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children need stimulation to develop their skills.","zh":"孩子需要受到激發，才能發展各項技能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stimulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-158b74d39f6bf0c7","term":"stimulation","forms":["stimulation","stimulations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引起反應的刺激；感官輸入","explanation":"指任何讓身體、神經系統或其他物件產生反應的作用或條件，例如聲音、光線、觸碰或環境變化。這裡的“啟動按鈕”不是為了鼓勵行動，而是讓身體或感官接收到訊號並作出反應。","examples":[{"en":"Bright light can cause stimulation of the nerves in the eye.","zh":"強光會刺激眼睛裡的神經。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby responded to the gentle stimulation of her hands.","zh":"嬰兒對輕柔的手部觸碰作出了反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stimulation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8adb0ce65bdb70c8e4b2","word":"stimulus","forms":["stimulus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-070301fd0ce4fba5","term":"stimulus","forms":["stimulus","stimuluses","stimuli"],"pos":"noun","zh":"推動行動或變化的因素","explanation":"指外界提供的推動力，使個人、組織或經濟系統開始行動、改變做法或恢復活力。它可以是獎勵、壓力、政策或其他促成變化的因素，重點在於“推動人或系統動起來”。","examples":[{"en":"The tax cut was designed as a stimulus to small businesses.","zh":"這項減稅措施旨在推動小型企業發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A clear deadline can be a powerful stimulus to action.","zh":"明確的截止日期可以成為促使人採取行動的強大動力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stimulus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63f6337b7e305c70","term":"stimulus","forms":["stimulus","stimuluses","stimuli"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引起身體或心理反應的刺激","explanation":"指外界作用於身體、感官或心理、從而引起反應的東西或訊號，例如光、聲音、觸碰、氣味或疼痛相關因素。這裡不一定有“促使人行動”的意思，重點是它使神經、感官或心理產生反應。","examples":[{"en":"The patient's eyes responded normally to the bright stimulus.","zh":"患者的眼睛對強光刺激作出了正常反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden flash provided a strong visual stimulus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stimulus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04695fa805d662a7ca81","word":"sting","forms":["sting"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f940f7435425db10","term":"sting","forms":["sting","stings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"昆蟲或蛛形動物的叮刺","explanation":"指昆蟲或蛛形動物攻擊時刺入皮膚的傷口，通常還可能把毒液注入體內；也可以泛指這種叮咬事件。","examples":[{"en":"He had a painful wasp sting on his neck.","zh":"他的脖子被黃蜂狠狠叮了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was taken to hospital after a scorpion sting.","zh":"她被蠍子蜇傷後被送進了醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-055b4f0e90382fd8","term":"sting","forms":["sting","stings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刺痛","explanation":"指皮膚表面突然出現的尖銳、區域性疼痛，像被輕輕紮了一下；它可以來自植物、化學物質或小傷口。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a sharp sting when the soap got into my cut.","zh":"肥皂進入傷口時，我感到一陣刺痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a little sting in my eyes after I swam.","zh":"游泳後，我的眼睛有一點刺痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b993a2cb2cbc7e03","term":"sting","forms":["sting","stings","stinging","stung","stang"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刺痛或蜇傷","explanation":"指用尖端或毒液使某人或某物感到疼痛，強調“刺進去並造成痛苦”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The bee stung my finger.","zh":"蜜蜂蜇了我的手指。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful—the nettles sting.","zh":"小心，這些蕁麻會刺痛人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a25d6d832ae5dc5","term":"sting","forms":["sting","stings","stinging","stung","stang"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用刺刺入","explanation":"特指昆蟲或蛛形動物用自己的毒刺刺入某人的身體，重點是實際刺入的動作。","examples":[{"en":"A mosquito stung me on the ankle.","zh":"一隻蚊子叮了我的腳踝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wasp stung him on the wrist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sting","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d544f37f25e07333d1bb","word":"stingy","forms":["stingy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd0ebd526dcb2cab","term":"stingy","forms":["stingy","stingier","stingiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"吝嗇的；不肯給的","explanation":"形容一個人不願意花錢、給予或分享，像手被什麼東西扎住了一樣，總是捨不得放出東西，因此通常含有負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"My uncle is stingy with his money, even when the family needs help.","zh":"我叔叔很吝嗇，即使家裡需要幫助，他也不願意拿出錢來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be stingy—share the dessert with everyone.","zh":"別這麼吝嗇，和大家一起分甜點吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stingy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4759be0b840b885","term":"stingy","forms":["stingy","stingier","stingiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"少得可憐的；不足的","explanation":"形容數量、供應或分量少得不夠用，彷彿只勉強伸出一點點，重點不在人的性格，而在資源太少。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel served us a stingy portion of vegetables.","zh":"酒店給我們上的蔬菜分量少得可憐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stingy drizzle of dressing left the salad almost dry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stingy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86ed3bf1c2692900c271","word":"stink","forms":["stink"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-554a417bf0c4994c","term":"stink","forms":["stink","stinks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臭味","explanation":"stink 是一股強烈而難聞的氣味：它不是普通的氣味，而是讓人明顯感到不舒服的臭味。","examples":[{"en":"The stink from the garbage was impossible to ignore.","zh":"垃圾散發的臭味讓人無法忽視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A terrible stink filled the kitchen.","zh":"一股難聞的臭味充滿了廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2fea1e618498945","term":"stink","forms":["stink","stinks","stinking","stank","stunk"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發臭","explanation":"stink 的基本動詞義是散發強烈難聞的氣味：某物自身像一股臭味一樣向外冒出來。","examples":[{"en":"These wet towels stink.","zh":"這些溼毛巾發臭了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room stinks of smoke.","zh":"房間裡有一股煙臭味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-65ea5c55a9c3c88d87c7","word":"stir","forms":["stir"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-207e2cb071fbdf05","term":"stir","forms":["stir","stirs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攪拌","explanation":"指用勺子等把液體或其中的成分攪動起來，也可以指這個攪拌動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"Give the sauce a quick stir before you serve it.","zh":"上桌前把醬汁快速攪拌一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One vigorous stir blended the cocoa into the milk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe67c482f59e1479","term":"stir","forms":["stir","stirs","stirring","stirred","stirrest","stirredst","stirreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攪動液體","explanation":"用勺子、筷子等在液體中移動，使其中的成分改變位置並混合起來，這是 stir 最具體、最基礎的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Stir the coffee slowly with a clean spoon.","zh":"用乾淨的勺子慢慢攪拌咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stirred some honey into her tea.","zh":"她把一些蜂蜜攪進了茶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cdefe0dae72580d8","term":"stir","forms":["stir","stirs","stirring","stirred","stirrest","stirredst","stirreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"觸動感情","explanation":"指某件事讓人產生強烈感情或內心反應，好像把平靜的心攪動起來；常可譯為“觸動、感動、打動”。","examples":[{"en":"That old song stirred memories of my childhood.","zh":"那首老歌勾起了我童年的回憶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her story stirred something deep in me.","zh":"她的故事觸動了我內心深處的某種情感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stir","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-864a42c4bf81be054d34","word":"stitch","forms":["stitch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43132034bd38af85","term":"stitch","forms":["stitch","stitches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一針；針腳","explanation":"指縫紉時針穿過材料的一次動作，或這一次留下的線圈、針腳；它是整條“用針連線材料”主線中最基本的單位。","examples":[{"en":"She added one small stitch to repair the torn pocket.","zh":"她補了一小針，把撕破的口袋縫好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This stitch is too loose, so the seam may open.","zh":"這一針太鬆了，所以接縫可能會裂開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stitch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38b0a592a1f77044","term":"stitch","forms":["stitch","stitches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運動時的肋側痛","explanation":"指運動、跑步或大笑時肋骨下緣附近突然出現的強烈刺痛，感覺像被針扎一樣；這是“針刺感”從外部動作轉到身體感覺的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I got a stitch while running and had to slow down.","zh":"我跑步時肋側突然疼起來，只好放慢速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take a short break if you get a stitch in your side.","zh":"如果肋側疼起來，就稍微休息一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stitch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13603472ad361a6e","term":"stitch","forms":["stitch","stitches","stitching","stitched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縫製；縫出針腳","explanation":"指用針線縫製材料，尤其是讓表面顯出連續的一行針腳；這是把“一針”變成連續動作。","examples":[{"en":"She stitched a bright pattern onto the front of the bag.","zh":"她在包的正面縫上了一個鮮豔的圖案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tailor stitched the sleeves neatly by hand.","zh":"裁縫用手工把袖子縫得很整齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stitch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-08c4242b5f585628bb8c","word":"stock","forms":["stock"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-895485accf0cdb63","term":"stock","forms":["stock","stocks","stocken"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲備；供應","explanation":"指留存起來、隨時可以使用或出售的一批東西，正像樹的根基為後續生長提供儲備。既可指具體物品，也可泛指某種供應量。","examples":[{"en":"The shop keeps a large stock of batteries for emergencies.","zh":"這家店儲備了大量電池以備緊急使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medicine is currently out of stock.","zh":"這種藥目前缺貨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4190da0605c1fb8","term":"stock","forms":["stock","stocks","stocken"],"pos":"noun","zh":"股份；股票資本","explanation":"指公司透過發行股份籌集的資本，或某位股東持有的股份；它是公司經營的資本“根基”。","examples":[{"en":"She owns stock in several technology companies.","zh":"她持有幾家科技公司的股票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sold his stock before the price fell.","zh":"他在價格下跌前賣掉了自己的股票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa7c2f0ec1388e0f11e9","word":"stocking(s)","forms":["stocking","stockings"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d3aa29b08fc3a162","term":"stocking","forms":["stocking","stockings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長襪","explanation":"指通常由針織或織物製成、覆蓋腳和小腿下部並穿在鞋裡的襪子，核心畫面就是“套在腿上的柔軟覆蓋物”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a pair of black stockings with her dress.","zh":"她穿著一雙黑色長襪，配著她的連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These stockings are too thin for winter.","zh":"這雙長襪對冬天來說太薄了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stocking","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3985b083fa4bc8c9","term":"stocking","forms":["stocking","stockings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聖誕襪","explanation":"指聖誕節掛在壁爐架等地方、用來裝小禮物的大號襪形袋；它是“襪子”這個形狀被用作禮物袋的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The children hung their stockings by the fireplace before bed.","zh":"孩子們睡前把聖誕襪掛在壁爐旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An orange waited at the bottom of her Christmas stocking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stocking","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0678ea3e9152f55a","term":"stockings","forms":["stockings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長襪的複數","explanation":"這是 stocking 的複數形式，表示多隻長襪，或一雙長襪中的兩隻。它保留了“包住腿的襪子”這一基本形象。","examples":[{"en":"She bought two pairs of stockings for the winter.","zh":"她為冬天買了兩雙長襪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stockings were hanging by the fireplace.","zh":"那些長襪掛在壁爐旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stockings","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d5a0d90574d530f83da1","word":"stomach","forms":["stomach"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1146bd32b24c8b6","term":"stomach","forms":["stomach","stomachs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"胃","explanation":"指動物體內儲存食物並參與消化的器官，是 stomach 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The medicine may irritate your stomach.","zh":"這種藥可能會刺激你的胃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Food stays in the stomach for several hours.","zh":"食物會在胃裡停留幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stomach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c2a611eec197261","term":"stomach","forms":["stomach","stomachs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對某事的胃口或意願","explanation":"從“胃能不能裝下東西”引申而來，表示一個人是否願意面對或接受某種抽象事情；no stomach for something 就是“完全不想面對某事”。","examples":[{"en":"I have no stomach for another argument tonight.","zh":"我今晚一點也不想再爭吵了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has the stomach for difficult decisions.","zh":"她有魄力面對艱難的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stomach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1962693b66c092a2acc","word":"stomachache","forms":["stomachache"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"stomachache","forms":["stomachache"],"pos":"n.","zh":"胃痛；腹痛","examples":[{"en":"I had a stomachache after eating too much.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"A persistent stomachache should be checked by a doctor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc3d50da8dac041f660e","word":"stone","forms":["stone"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bb11250c02541629","term":"stone","forms":["stone","stones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"石材；石頭物質","explanation":"指堅硬的天然土質物質，尤其指作為建築材料使用的石材；這是“堅硬的石頭”這一核心畫面本身。","examples":[{"en":"The house was built from local stone.","zh":"這座房子用當地石材建成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mason chose stone rather than brick for the archway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d6734ec35df3c53","term":"stone","forms":["stone","stones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"石塊；石子","explanation":"指一塊具體的石頭、岩石或小石子，是核心畫面中可以拿在手裡的硬物。","examples":[{"en":"He picked up a smooth stone from the beach.","zh":"他從海灘上撿起一塊光滑的石頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The path was covered with small stones.","zh":"小路上鋪滿了小石子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ba507766c30bb1c","term":"stone","forms":["stone","stones","stoning","stoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給水果去核","explanation":"指從水果中取出堅硬的果核，就像從水果裡取走一塊小石頭；常用於李子、桃子、櫻桃等有硬核的水果。","examples":[{"en":"She stones the cherries before making the pie.","zh":"她做餡餅前先給櫻桃去核。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stone the peaches and cut them into wedges.","zh":"給桃子去核，然後把它們切成楔形塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b04cb09fabfe6b51ab9c","word":"stool","forms":["stool"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-70a08690ced8e742","term":"stool","forms":["stool","stools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"凳子","explanation":"指供一個人坐的座位，通常沒有靠背，常見於廚房、酒吧或櫃檯旁。它是這個詞最基本的“供身體停靠之物”這一形象。","examples":[{"en":"She pulled up a stool beside the counter.","zh":"她把一張凳子拉到櫃檯旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child stood on a stool to reach the shelf.","zh":"孩子站在凳子上去夠架子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c45cb72a36e63d522aa","word":"stop","forms":["stop"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08545be12bb00074","term":"stop","forms":["stop","stops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車輛停靠點","explanation":"車輛停下來讓乘客上下車的地點，通常比車站小，常見於公共汽車、電車或火車線路。它體現了 stop 讓運動暫時停下來的基本概念。","examples":[{"en":"Let's meet at the bus stop outside the library.","zh":"我們在圖書館外面的公交車站見面吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The next stop is only two minutes away.","zh":"下一站只有兩分鐘的路程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd5f2efa94e8ffcc","term":"stop","forms":["stop","stops","stopping","stopped","stoppest","stoppedst","stoppeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"停止移動；停下","explanation":"指人、車輛或其他正在移動的東西停下來，讓運動停住。","examples":[{"en":"The bus stopped outside the school.","zh":"公共汽車停在了學校外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I stopped when I heard my name.","zh":"聽到有人叫我的名字，我停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a4bcf5e763d714e","term":"stop","forms":["stop","stops","stopping","stopped","stoppest","stoppedst","stoppeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使停止；阻止前進","explanation":"指某人或某物使正在移動、發展的物件停下來，就像設定障礙讓運動停住。","examples":[{"en":"A fallen tree stopped the car.","zh":"一棵倒下的樹擋住了汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing could stop her from finishing the race.","zh":"沒有什麼能阻止她完成比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b6eade0a9ec82ba2","term":"stop","forms":["stop","stops","stopping","stopped","stoppest","stoppedst","stoppeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"堵住開口","explanation":"指用材料或物體封住開口、孔洞或傷口，阻止液體、空氣等透過；這是把運動擋住的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"She stopped the leak with a piece of rubber.","zh":"她用一塊橡膠堵住了漏處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Press the cloth firmly to stop the bleeding.","zh":"用力按住布來止血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49a25f9feefaffecad0f","word":"storage","forms":["storage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb39b85b79e3f4e0","term":"storage","forms":["storage","storages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲存；存放狀態","explanation":"指把東西儲存起來的行為，或東西處於被儲存狀態這一事實。它強調“放起來留著”，不一定指具體的房間或裝置。","examples":[{"en":"We need to find a dry place for storage.","zh":"我們需要找一個乾燥的地方來儲存這些東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The furniture has been in storage since last winter.","zh":"這些傢俱從去年冬天起就一直存放著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7604b6175249389","term":"storage","forms":["storage","storages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機儲存","explanation":"在計算機語境中，指長期儲存檔案和資料的空間或裝置，例如硬碟、固態硬碟或其他資料儲存介質。它仍然是“把資料放起來儲存”，但物件從實物變成了數字資訊。","examples":[{"en":"I moved the photos to cloud storage to free up my phone.","zh":"我把照片移到雲端儲存中，以騰出手機空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laptop does not have enough storage for the game.","zh":"這檯膝上型電腦沒有足夠的儲存空間安裝這個遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-824d80d71985f082a269","word":"store","forms":["store"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45348430774593a3","term":"store","forms":["store","stores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲藏處","explanation":"指專門用來存放物品的地方，重點是“把東西集中放在那裡”，不一定對外營業。","examples":[{"en":"The old barn is used as a store for farm tools.","zh":"那座舊穀倉被用作存放農具的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found several boxes in the store behind the kitchen.","zh":"我們在廚房後面的儲藏室裡發現了幾個箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/store","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ee71a0c988ab83a","term":"store","forms":["store","stores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲備；庫存","explanation":"指已經存下、留待以後使用的一批東西；這個意思把“存放的地方”轉成了“存放著的內容”。","examples":[{"en":"The village keeps a store of clean water for emergencies.","zh":"這個村子儲備了一些乾淨的水以備緊急情況使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a large store of practical knowledge.","zh":"她積累了大量實用知識。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/store","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab2899bf5e17faa6","term":"store","forms":["store","stores"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商店","explanation":"指人們購買商品的地方，尤其常見於北美英語；它和“儲藏處”的共同點是都與集中存放物品有關。","examples":[{"en":"I stopped at the store to buy some bread.","zh":"我去商店買了些麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a hardware store near the station.","zh":"車站附近有一家五金店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/store","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-098ad4a8bec872c7","term":"store","forms":["store","stores","storing","stored","storest","storedst","storeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"存放；儲存","explanation":"指把暫時不用的東西放到合適的地方，以便以後取用；這是動詞最核心的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please store the winter clothes in these boxes.","zh":"請把冬衣存放在這些箱子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We store extra food in the basement.","zh":"我們把多餘的食物存放在地下室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/store","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a105749cfcbac2e07d7","word":"storm","forms":["storm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c72d4aac451d76b","term":"storm","forms":["storm","storms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴風雨","explanation":"指伴有強風，常同時有雷電、雨雪或海上巨浪的惡劣天氣。它比一般的壞天氣更猛烈、更有破壞性。","examples":[{"en":"A powerful storm is moving toward the coast.","zh":"一場猛烈的暴風雨正向海岸逼近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm knocked out the electricity last night.","zh":"昨晚的暴風雨導致停電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f580e5c61391d94c","term":"storm","forms":["storm","storms","storming","stormed","stormest","stormedst","stormeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"下暴風雨","explanation":"指天氣出現強風，並常伴有雷電、雨、雪或冰雹。","examples":[{"en":"It stormed all night.","zh":"昨晚整夜都在下暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It stormed all night, shaking the cottage windows.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-864214ce42a276c9","term":"storm","forms":["storm","storms","storming","stormed","stormest","stormedst","stormeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"怒氣衝衝地衝走","explanation":"指像風暴一樣又快又吵地移動，通常因為生氣或現場一片混亂；最常見的是 storm out。","examples":[{"en":"She stormed out of the meeting.","zh":"她怒氣衝衝地離開了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stormed out before anyone could explain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07b8234d2e02edcf51d3","word":"stormy","forms":["stormy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77ee9d0a07d13c15","term":"stormy","forms":["stormy","stormier","stormiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"風雨猛烈的","explanation":"形容天氣或季節受到暴風雨影響，風很大、雨很急，整體顯得惡劣而不平靜。這是最直接、最容易聯想到暴風雨的用法。","examples":[{"en":"We stayed indoors because it was a stormy night.","zh":"因為那是一個風雨交加的夜晚，我們待在室內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stormy season made travel difficult.","zh":"風雨猛烈的季節讓出行變得困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stormy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53861d53ecfb40f7","term":"stormy","forms":["stormy","stormier","stormiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"激烈動盪的","explanation":"形容情緒、關係或局面像暴風雨一樣猛烈而不穩定，常帶有爭執、激情或劇烈變化的意味。","examples":[{"en":"They had a stormy relationship but never stopped caring about each other.","zh":"他們的關係充滿波折，但從未停止關心彼此。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her stormy passions shaped many of her paintings.","zh":"她強烈而翻湧的情感塑造了許多畫作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stormy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c478361e6869af259706","word":"story","forms":["story"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-926e55865c476483","term":"story","forms":["story","stories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事；敘述","explanation":"story 是把一連串真實或虛構的事件講出來的內容，可以是書、電影裡的情節，也可以是某人的經歷。","examples":[{"en":"The book tells the story of two roommates.","zh":"這本書講述了兩個室友的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She told us a funny story about her trip.","zh":"她給我們講了一個旅行中的趣事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/story","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89ba8c8914cbcdda","term":"story","forms":["story","stories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情況；事情經過","explanation":"story 也可以指一件事背後的來龍去脈，尤其是在詢問“到底是什麼情況”時；這裡不是在要求聽一個完整故事，而是在問事情的背景。","examples":[{"en":"What's the story with your new neighbor?","zh":"你那個新鄰居到底是什麼情況？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't know the whole story yet.","zh":"我還不知道事情的全部經過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/story","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5dc60efa39123ab6094f","word":"stove","forms":["stove"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48127b1d6aece4e2","term":"stove","forms":["stove","stoves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"取暖爐","explanation":"指燃燒燃料或使用熱源、專門給房間取暖的爐具。它是“把空間加熱起來的爐子”這一核心形象的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The old stove kept the cabin warm all night.","zh":"那臺舊爐子讓小屋整夜都很暖和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We brought in more wood for the stove.","zh":"我們又搬來一些木柴給爐子用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dbea06eab230b0e4","term":"stove","forms":["stove","stoves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"爐灶","explanation":"指用來加熱和烹飪食物的整臺裝置，相當於家裡的爐灶或炊具。這是現代生活中最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The soup is simmering on the stove.","zh":"湯正在爐子上慢慢燉著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old gas stove has four burners and a small oven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stove","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a424875a8475a99175f","word":"straight","forms":["straight"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9946666d23d8012f","term":"straight","forms":["straight","straighter","straightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直的；不彎的","explanation":"像記憶鉤子裡的那條不彎的直線一樣，表示形狀沒有彎曲、扭轉或捲曲。","examples":[{"en":"Draw a straight line across the page.","zh":"在頁面上畫一條直線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The path through the forest is straight and level.","zh":"穿過森林的小路又直又平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bcc171ef332c502","term":"straight","forms":["straight","straighter","straightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"坦率直接的","explanation":"把“不繞彎的直線”用於交流，表示說話直接、不迴避問題，也不故意含糊其辭。","examples":[{"en":"Please give me a straight answer: are you coming or not?","zh":"請直接回答我：你到底來不來？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was straight with us about the possible risks.","zh":"她坦率地告訴了我們可能存在的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c56d62bb94d5b9ad","term":"straight","forms":["straight","straighter","straightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"異性戀的","explanation":"把“直線”引申為沿傳統性別關係方向，表示一個人的性取向是異性戀。","examples":[{"en":"He identifies as straight and supports equal rights for everyone.","zh":"他認同自己是異性戀者，也支援所有人的平等權利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is straight, while his brother is gay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d0f172f7a7ee5a4a","term":"straight","forms":["straight","more straight","most straight"],"pos":"adv","zh":"直接地","explanation":"表示不暫停、不耽擱、也不繞路地做下一件事，體現了“一條不繞的直線”。","examples":[{"en":"After lunch, I went straight back to work.","zh":"午飯後，我直接回去工作了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Go straight to the front desk when you arrive.","zh":"你到了以後直接去前臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d942f0a84262979f6999","word":"straighten","forms":["straighten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ca1a1818706c168","term":"straighten","forms":["straighten","straightens","straightening","straightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變直","explanation":"把彎曲、歪斜或不平的東西弄直，正如把一條彎線拉回直線。","examples":[{"en":"She straightened the picture on the wall.","zh":"她把牆上的畫擺正了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He straightened his back and looked at me.","zh":"他挺直了背，看著我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5ef5fe929615d59b","term":"straighten","forms":["straighten","straightens","straightening","straightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變直","explanation":"原本彎曲或歪斜的東西自己恢復成直的狀態，是“使變直”的不及物對應形式。","examples":[{"en":"The bent wire slowly straightened.","zh":"彎曲的金屬絲慢慢變直了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His back straightened when the familiar tune began.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50f5f1b46dea63cc0506","word":"straightforward","forms":["straightforward"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3975acfe6aba93b5","term":"straightforward","forms":["straightforward","more straightforward","straighterforward","most straightforward","straightestforward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"簡單明瞭的","explanation":"指事情、任務或設計不復雜，步驟清楚，通常不需要特別費力就能理解或完成。它可以看作“沿著直路走”，沒有太多障礙和彎路。","examples":[{"en":"Installing the software is a straightforward process.","zh":"安裝這個軟體是個很簡單的過程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The instructions are straightforward enough for beginners.","zh":"這些說明足夠清楚，初學者也能看懂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straightforward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7137deedeeb5ba1","term":"straightforward","forms":["straightforward","more straightforward","straighterforward","most straightforward","straightestforward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直率坦誠的","explanation":"指說話或態度不繞圈子，坦率地表達真實想法，尤其是不迴避明確回答。這個義項把“筆直向前”從行動延伸到了交流。","examples":[{"en":"I appreciate your straightforward answer.","zh":"我很欣賞你坦率的回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was straightforward about the risks.","zh":"她坦率地說明了其中的風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straightforward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf0fa94d45324732cfdd","word":"strain","forms":["strain"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c9b95ed814123020","term":"strain","forms":["strain","strains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"壓力；負擔","explanation":"strain 是施加在某人、某物或某系統上的持續壓力和負擔；壓力像把繩子越拉越緊，最終會影響其承受能力。","examples":[{"en":"The long hours put a great strain on her health.","zh":"長時間工作給她的健康帶來了很大壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old bridge is under severe strain.","zh":"這座舊橋正承受著很大的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2946ee7db65c3680","term":"strain","forms":["strain","strains","straining","strained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拉緊；使受力","explanation":"strain 可以把繩子、材料或結構拉緊，使它承受拉力；這正是“越拉越緊”的核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"Do not strain the rope beyond its limit.","zh":"不要讓這根繩子承受超過極限的拉力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The heavy load strained the cable.","zh":"沉重的負載使纜繩承受了很大拉力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4afd7dddbbef1d22","term":"strain","forms":["strain","strains","straining","strained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"費力地做；竭力聽看","explanation":"strain to do something 表示把自己的體力、聽力、視力或注意力拉到不舒服的程度，竭力完成某事。","examples":[{"en":"I strained to hear the announcement over the noise.","zh":"噪聲太大，我竭力想聽清廣播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She strained her eyes to read the small print.","zh":"她費力睜大眼睛看那些小字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a4f798d8026dff67","term":"strain","forms":["strain","strains","straining","strained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"過濾；濾出","explanation":"strain 還可以把液體透過濾網或濾器，使固體留下、液體流過去；這也是把混合物“拉開”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Strain the soup through a fine sieve.","zh":"把湯用細篩過濾一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Strain the pasta and return it to the pot.","zh":"把意麵瀝出過濾好，再放回鍋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1c97db665f1495dc252b","word":"strait","forms":["strait"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ca43efea2f569cf","term":"strait","forms":["strait","straits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海峽","explanation":"指連線兩個較大水域的狹窄水道，是“狹窄通道”這一核心意象最典型的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The ship passed through the strait before sunrise.","zh":"船在日出前透過了海峽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Strong currents sweep through the narrow strait.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10d5502882c0fe35","term":"strait","forms":["strait","straits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"困境","explanation":"常用複數表示艱難處境：人彷彿被擠進沒有迴旋餘地的狹窄通道，因此陷入困境。","examples":[{"en":"The family is in dire straits after losing its main source of income.","zh":"失去主要收入來源後，這家人陷入了極其困難的境地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The failed harvest left the family in desperate straits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c71e2d9d4d0b64ae7d8a","word":"strand","forms":["strand"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a94d92c0f595b35","term":"strand","forms":["strand","strands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"海岸；海灘","explanation":"strand是海洋或大海旁的一片岸邊、沙灘或海濱；它強調的是沿水邊展開的一條岸帶。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon walking along the strand.","zh":"我們整個下午都沿著海灘散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A long strand of white sand stretches beyond the village.","zh":"村子外延伸著一大片白色沙灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea8aeb251cf898f2","term":"strand","forms":["strand","strands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繩或線中的一股","explanation":"strand指構成紗線、繩子或繩索的一股細線；許多strand擰在一起，才形成更粗的繩或線。","examples":[{"en":"One strand of the rope has come loose.","zh":"這根繩子有一股鬆開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cable is made from several twisted strands.","zh":"這根纜線由幾股擰在一起的線組成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28023829d3020a0b","term":"strand","forms":["strand","strands"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組成部分；線索","explanation":"strand可以表示複雜整體中的一條思想、事實、事件或論證線索，就像故事裡貫穿始終的一根線。","examples":[{"en":"The report follows one important strand of the investigation.","zh":"這份報告追蹤了調查中的一條重要線索。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a strong strand of humor throughout the novel.","zh":"這部小說始終貫穿著一種鮮明的幽默色彩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81a9107a9fb41879","term":"strand","forms":["strand","strands","stranding","stranded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使船擱淺","explanation":"strand作動詞時可以表示讓船衝上岸或擱淺，使它像被卡在岸邊一樣無法繼續航行。","examples":[{"en":"The storm stranded the fishing boat on a sandbank.","zh":"暴風雨使那艘漁船擱淺在沙洲上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hundreds of passengers were stranded at the airport.","zh":"數百名乘客被困在機場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a595cf04a8a877e2","term":"strand","forms":["strand","strands","stranding","stranded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使陷入困境；拋下","explanation":"引申後，strand表示把某人留在困難、孤立或無法解決的處境中，像被留在岸邊一樣無法前進。","examples":[{"en":"The cancelled train stranded us in a small town overnight.","zh":"火車取消，導致我們被困在一個小鎮過夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden closure left the workers stranded without pay.","zh":"突然關門讓工人陷入了沒有工資的困境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41b3ab146fd067194352","word":"strange","forms":["strange"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be2f64af36044467","term":"strange","forms":["strange","stranger","strangest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇怪的；不尋常的","explanation":"某人、某事或某種情況偏離平常，讓人感到意外、難以理解，常帶有輕微的負面感覺。","examples":[{"en":"It was strange that nobody answered the door.","zh":"沒人來開門，這很奇怪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a strange look and walked away.","zh":"她奇怪地看了我一眼，然後走開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-141e191584f225b6","term":"strange","forms":["strange","stranger","strangest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陌生的；不熟悉的","explanation":"對某人來說尚未接觸或尚未熟悉，因此感覺像來自熟悉範圍之外的人、地方或事物。","examples":[{"en":"The city felt strange to me at first.","zh":"起初，這座城市讓我感到很陌生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was nervous in the strange surroundings.","zh":"在陌生的環境裡，他很緊張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strange","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8aca4f36774f82a67c50","word":"stranger","forms":["stranger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b9dcadf35e487f29","term":"stranger","forms":["stranger","strangers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陌生人","explanation":"指你不認識、也不是朋友或熟人的人；重點是彼此沒有熟悉關係。","examples":[{"en":"A stranger offered to carry my bag.","zh":"一個陌生人主動提出幫我拿包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She never opens the door to strangers.","zh":"她從不給陌生人開門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stranger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-670212c9eae29bd6","term":"stranger","forms":["stranger","strangers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外來者；外國人","explanation":"指不屬於當地群體或共同體的人，強調他來自圈子之外，不一定只是“你個人不認識他”。","examples":[{"en":"As a stranger in the city, he found the local customs confusing.","zh":"作為這座城市的外來者，他覺得當地習俗令人費解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers welcomed the stranger from another country.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stranger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bedb0f81a005e35956b","word":"strangle","forms":["strangle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f37c4ce0396b2ee6","term":"strangle","forms":["strangle","strangles","strangling","strangled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勒死；掐住使窒息","explanation":"指用手、繩子或其他方式壓住喉嚨，使人或動物無法呼吸，嚴重時導致死亡。這個具體的“勒緊喉嚨”畫面是 strangle 最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The attacker tried to strangle the guard with a rope.","zh":"襲擊者試圖用繩子勒住那名保安的脖子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog was nearly strangled by its leash.","zh":"那條狗差點被自己的牽引繩勒死。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-996d583ad631b5cc","term":"strangle","forms":["strangle","strangles","strangling","strangled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓制；扼殺","explanation":"由“勒住喉嚨”引申為把聲音、情緒、想法或發展壓下去，使它無法自然表達或繼續發展。","examples":[{"en":"She strangled a scream when she saw the broken window.","zh":"她看到破碎的窗戶時強忍住了尖叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy taxes can strangle small businesses.","zh":"沉重的稅負可能會扼殺小企業的發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-833a63294a4cb1fc9c61","word":"strap","forms":["strap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-044ec3fa414128a1","term":"strap","forms":["strap","straps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶子；窄長條帶","explanation":"指皮革、布料等製成的長而窄、可以彎曲的帶子，是strap最基本的名詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"The strap on my bag broke on the way home.","zh":"我回家的路上，包上的帶子斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She adjusted the strap of her watch.","zh":"她調了調手錶的錶帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8643f6c7d6421604","term":"strap","forms":["strap","straps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帶狀裝置；帶子製品","explanation":"指用帶子本身、帶子的一部分，或幾條帶子組合製成的特定裝置；重點不在材料，而在它作為某種部件的用途。","examples":[{"en":"The helmet has a strap under the rider's chin.","zh":"這頂頭盔在騎手下巴下面有一條固定帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the straps to hold the box closed.","zh":"用這些帶子把箱子固定好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1e7f7d523c4ff4e","term":"strap","forms":["strap","straps","strapping","strapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用帶子固定；捆綁","explanation":"指用帶子把物品固定、捆在一起或固定到另一物上，是動詞strap最常用的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"We strapped the boxes to the roof of the car.","zh":"我們把箱子用帶子固定在汽車車頂上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please strap yourself in before the plane takes off.","zh":"飛機起飛前請繫好安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-850be92fa1e3f6a7013e","word":"strategic","forms":["strategic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dda998dd5d1aa9b6","term":"strategic","forms":["strategic","more strategic","most strategic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"戰略性的；著眼全域性和長遠的","explanation":"指與整體策略、長遠規劃或實現主要目標的方法有關，而不是隻處理眼前的一個小問題。它可以用於軍事，也可以用於商業、學習、談判等非軍事場景。","examples":[{"en":"We need a strategic plan for the next five years.","zh":"我們需要一份未來五年的戰略規劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a strategic approach to solving the problem.","zh":"她採用了著眼全域性的方法來解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strategic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dede115bdbf6680c","term":"strategic","forms":["strategic","more strategic","most strategic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"軍事上戰略層面的；非區域性戰術性的","explanation":"在軍事語境中，指影響整體戰局、涉及較大範圍或較長時間的行動、位置或武器，而不是隻針對眼前區域性目標的戰術行動。它仍然保留“從高處看全域性、著眼長遠”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The army moved to protect a strategic position.","zh":"軍隊轉移去保護一個具有戰略意義的陣地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fleet protected a route of strategic importance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strategic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-73dff70e25ad51ca765a","word":"strategy","forms":["strategy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01df0dd889e068b6","term":"strategy","forms":["strategy","strategies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實現目標的方案","explanation":"strategy指為了達到某個具體目標而設計的行動方案：它把目標、方向和主要行動聯絡起來，幫助人們按整體計劃推進。","examples":[{"en":"We need a clear strategy to attract more customers.","zh":"我們需要一個明確的方案來吸引更多顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her strategy for passing the exam was to review a little every day.","zh":"她透過考試的策略是每天覆習一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strategy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecda346246f90539","term":"strategy","forms":["strategy","strategies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軍事總體謀劃","explanation":"在軍事語境中，strategy指從全域性出發，對戰爭或軍事行動進行的總體指揮和規劃，重點是方向、部署以及如何爭取整體優勢，而不是單個動作。","examples":[{"en":"The army changed its strategy after several months of fighting.","zh":"經過幾個月的戰鬥後，軍隊改變了總體戰略。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their strategy aimed to cut the enemy's supply lines.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strategy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9fa0453869469e08db9","word":"straw","forms":["straw"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc10efb2070bdb63","term":"straw","forms":["straw","straws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一根幹穀物莖稈","explanation":"指穀物收割後留下並曬乾的莖稈，是記憶中那把幹稻草的基本含義。","examples":[{"en":"The children gathered a straw from the field.","zh":"孩子們從田裡撿起了一根幹穀物莖稈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A single straw floated on the puddle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8a827be93b97d36","term":"straw","forms":["straw","straws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸管","explanation":"指喝飲料用的細管，現代日常語境中很常見；它和稻草材料共用同一個詞。","examples":[{"en":"Could I have a straw for my iced tea?","zh":"可以給我一根冰茶吸管嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child sipped juice through a straw.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/straw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5e737f891db1175442a3","word":"strawberry","forms":["strawberry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c1fd92f0712b20b","term":"strawberry","forms":["strawberry","strawberries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"草莓","explanation":"指通常為紅色、甜味、可以食用的草莓果實；這是 strawberry 最核心的名詞意思。","examples":[{"en":"They went to pick strawberries today.","zh":"他們今天去採草莓了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I put some strawberry on top of the yogurt.","zh":"我在酸奶上放了一些草莓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e224ddc6b55af8b2a884","word":"stray","forms":["stray"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c572a3d84472aea0","term":"stray","forms":["stray"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遊蕩的；走失的","explanation":"指動物或人離開了原來的家、群體或應在的位置，在外面遊蕩或走失；最常見的是指無主、流浪的動物。","examples":[{"en":"A stray dog followed us home from the station.","zh":"一條流浪狗從車站一路跟著我們回了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They took a stray kitten to the animal shelter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0acb1b0c8b21648e","term":"stray","forms":["stray","strays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流浪動物；走失的動物","explanation":"指沒有主人陪伴、沒有被圈養，或已經走失而在外面遊蕩的家養動物。","examples":[{"en":"The shelter takes in strays and helps find them new homes.","zh":"這家收容所接收流浪動物，並幫助它們找到新家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They adopted a stray found outside the bakery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2fbe70c65a9d47c","term":"stray","forms":["stray","strays","straying","strayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偏離路線；走偏","explanation":"指行進時沒有繼續沿著直接或原定路線，而是向旁邊偏去；這是動詞最基本的空間意象。","examples":[{"en":"We strayed from the marked path and had to turn back.","zh":"我們偏離了標記的小路，只好折返回去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We strayed from the marked trail in the fog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65320483040fd605","term":"stray","forms":["stray","strays","straying","strayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"離群遊蕩；走失","explanation":"指離開同伴、規定範圍或原來的地方，在外面遊蕩或走失。","examples":[{"en":"The child strayed from her parents in the crowded market.","zh":"那個孩子在擁擠的市場裡和父母走散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One sheep strayed beyond the broken fence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dca83e717b1f64eb1410","word":"stream","forms":["stream"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-622cf7482edbdeec","term":"stream","forms":["stream","streams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小河；溪流","explanation":"指有河岸、持續流動的自然水道，通常比river小，但可以比普通的小溪更寬或更深。","examples":[{"en":"We followed the stream through the forest.","zh":"我們沿著溪流穿過森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children built a small bridge over the stream.","zh":"孩子們在小溪上搭了一座小橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f15be043889d943","term":"stream","forms":["stream","streams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續流；一連串","explanation":"從水流引申為任何持續不斷、接連透過的東西，例如聲音、話語、空氣、訊號或負面言論。","examples":[{"en":"A steady stream of visitors entered the museum.","zh":"參觀者絡繹不絕地進入博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stream of complaints followed the announcement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c667e25ac5fa823","term":"stream","forms":["stream","streams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"線上播放內容","explanation":"指音樂、影片等數字內容以連續方式傳到裝置上，使用者可以立即播放，而不必先完整下載。","examples":[{"en":"The movie is available as a stream on the service.","zh":"這部電影可以在該服務上線上播放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stream froze halfway through the live concert.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-219ebc08b70b6674","term":"stream","forms":["stream","streams","streaming","streamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"流動","explanation":"指液體或類似液體的東西持續、穩定地向前流動，是名詞“水流”意義的直接動詞化。","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater streamed down the window.","zh":"雨水順著窗戶流下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tears streamed down his face.","zh":"淚水不停地流過他的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5ae510134b94ab7","term":"stream","forms":["stream","streams","streaming","streamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"線上播放；串流傳送","explanation":"指伺服器把音樂、影片等連續資料傳到使用者裝置，讓內容在傳送過程中就能播放。","examples":[{"en":"We streamed the concert to our television.","zh":"我們把這場音樂會線上播放到電視上觀看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can stream the album without downloading it.","zh":"你可以線上播放這張專輯，不必把它下載下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stream","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6008c26f4452392acb19","word":"street","forms":["street"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa627c581a2a0c19","term":"street","forms":["street","streets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"街道","explanation":"street 是城鎮中鋪設好的道路，通常供車輛和行人通行，周圍有房屋、商店或其他建築。這是這個詞最核心、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Walk down the street and turn left at the library.","zh":"沿著這條街走，在圖書館處左轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bakery opened on our street last week.","zh":"上週我們這條街上開了一家麵包店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/street","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5e9114276f8bab7","term":"street","forms":["street","streets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"街道及其兩旁的城市環境","explanation":"有時 street 不只指路面，還連同街道兩旁的建築、店鋪和鄰近區域。說住在某條 street 上，通常是在說住在這條街及其沿線的社群環境裡。","examples":[{"en":"I live on a busy street near the train station.","zh":"我住在火車站附近一條繁忙的街道上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The street buzzed with cafes, markets, and evening shoppers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/street","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6b88623f7209b6c11fc","word":"strength","forms":["strength"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7762732e6ee09767","term":"strength","forms":["strength","strengths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"力量；體力","explanation":"表示一個人或事物強壯、有力的性質或程度，最常見的是身體力量，也可以泛指完成某件事所需要的力量。","examples":[{"en":"She did not have enough strength to carry the box upstairs.","zh":"她沒有足夠的力氣把箱子搬上樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a short rest, he regained his strength.","zh":"短暫休息後，他恢復了體力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strength","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f59011c760d0c044","term":"strength","forms":["strength","strengths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"力度；強度","explanation":"表示某種力、影響或作用有多強，重點不在誰擁有力量，而在力量本身達到什麼程度。","examples":[{"en":"This coffee is too strong for me, so I added some milk.","zh":"這咖啡對我來說太濃了，所以我加了些牛奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strength of the wind made it difficult to open the door.","zh":"風力太強，開門很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strength","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b9d0502424fb52f","term":"strength","forms":["strength","strengths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長處；優勢","explanation":"指一個人、團隊或事物具有的積極特點，尤其是比其他方面更出色、最值得發揮的能力。它把“強大”的核心概念轉到了能力和表現上。","examples":[{"en":"Clear communication is one of her greatest strengths.","zh":"清晰的溝通能力是她最大的優點之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Explaining difficult ideas is one of her strengths.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strength","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e617009b3fe47843132","word":"strengthen","forms":["strengthen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d41fbaf5f95ac99f","term":"strengthen","forms":["strengthen","strengthens","strengthening","strengthened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變強；加固","explanation":"把身體、結構或防禦力量提高，使它更強、更牢固。這個意義最直接地體現了“把力量加上去”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise can strengthen your back muscles.","zh":"經常鍛鍊可以增強你的背部肌肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The repairs should strengthen the old bridge.","zh":"這些修繕應該能加固這座舊橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strengthen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04322c9d7e758ebf","term":"strengthen","forms":["strengthen","strengthens","strengthening","strengthened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"增強勇氣；鼓舞","explanation":"把勇氣、信心或精神力量加給某人，使對方更有力量面對困難。這裡增強的不是身體，而是人的內在力量。","examples":[{"en":"Her kind words strengthened me before the difficult interview.","zh":"面試前，她的暖心話給了我力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her encouragement strengthened his resolve to continue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strengthen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-411df1b2a0fdcebc","term":"strengthen","forms":["strengthen","strengthens","strengthening","strengthened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"增強說服力；使更有根據","explanation":"給觀點、論據或立場補充力量，使它更可信、更能支援結論。可以把它想成給一座“理由之牆”加固。","examples":[{"en":"The statistics strengthen her argument about rising costs.","zh":"這些統計資料增強了她關於成本上升的論點的說服力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new evidence strengthened her case considerably.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strengthen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f43dc8790ed621568492","word":"stress","forms":["stress"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d0380ea4a237abd","term":"stress","forms":["stress","stresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理壓力","explanation":"這是日常最重要的意思之一：人或動物承受的緊張、負擔和焦慮感，就像有一股力壓在身上。","examples":[{"en":"She has been under a lot of stress at work.","zh":"她最近工作壓力很大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular exercise can help reduce stress.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於減輕壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-111067a8b2c3e13b","term":"stress","forms":["stress","stresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強調","explanation":"在說話或寫作中，把額外的注意力和力量放在某個觀點上，就是對它進行強調；這仍然是“把壓力壓到某處”的引申。","examples":[{"en":"The report places stress on the need for better training.","zh":"這份報告強調了加強培訓的必要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The speaker gave special stress to the final point.","zh":"演講者特別強調了最後一點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-931e5e22143b3fdf","term":"stress","forms":["stress","stresses","stressing","stressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使人承受心理壓力","explanation":"指給人或動物施加精神負擔，使其感到緊張、焦慮或難以應付。","examples":[{"en":"Too many deadlines are stressing me out.","zh":"太多截止日期讓我壓力大得受不了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constant uncertainty stressed the entire family.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d5866dbc0967eec","term":"stress","forms":["stress","stresses","stressing","stressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強調說出的詞","explanation":"說話時把更多力量或注意力放在某個詞上，使聽者特別注意它，就是對這個詞進行強調。","examples":[{"en":"She stressed the word “never” to make her meaning clear.","zh":"她重讀“絕不”這個詞，以便把意思說清楚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stress the second syllable when saying this word.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48be85364467c986","term":"stress","forms":["stress","stresses","stressing","stressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強調觀點","explanation":"在論證或討論中，stress 表示明確而有力地指出某個重點，讓別人不能忽略它。","examples":[{"en":"I must stress that safety comes first.","zh":"我必須強調，安全是第一位的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guide stressed the importance of staying together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1219929bd7c1c9f41265","word":"stretch","forms":["stretch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03bd64e1417d546d","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"伸展動作","explanation":"指把身體、四肢或某物拉開、伸長這一動作本身，而不是伸展後的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"I do a short stretch before I go running.","zh":"我跑步前會做一會兒伸展運動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try a gentle stretch before the run.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04f22d78cef55f9e","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段路程","explanation":"指旅程、道路或路線中連續的一段；這正是“向外延伸出一段長度”這一核心概念在空間上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The final stretch of the road is narrow and winding.","zh":"最後一段路又窄又彎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final stretch of road follows the coast.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be3f2c4731e78732","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段材料","explanation":"指連續的一段布料、土地或其他材料，強調它在空間上延伸出來的範圍。","examples":[{"en":"A wide stretch of grass lies beside the river.","zh":"河邊有一大片連續的草地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He cut a stretch of fabric for the curtain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a4c458f14b952ed","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches","stretching","stretched","straught","straight"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拉長","explanation":"用力把某物向兩邊拉，使它實際變長；這是最直接的“把橡皮筋拉開”這一核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"She stretched the elastic band until it nearly broke.","zh":"她把橡皮筋拉到幾乎要斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stretch the elastic until it reaches the marked line.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-648c2c1b3f506d5d","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches","stretching","stretched","straught","straight"],"pos":"verb","zh":"被拉長","explanation":"指某物在受到拉力時自行變長，重點是發生了伸長這一變化，而不是誰主動去拉它。","examples":[{"en":"The sweater stretched after I washed it.","zh":"這件毛衣洗過後變得松長了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The elastic stretches without losing its shape.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a24ddac118b5e93","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches","stretching","stretched","straught","straight"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把資源用得更久","explanation":"把有限的食物、錢或供應量分配得更節省，從而延長它能使用的時間；這是把資源的“使用長度”拉長。","examples":[{"en":"We need to stretch our savings until I find a new job.","zh":"我們得省著用存款，撐到我找到新工作為止。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Adding beans can stretch a small amount of meat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28d62345d1846631","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches","stretching","stretched","straught","straight"],"pos":"verb","zh":"延伸","explanation":"指道路、海灘、土地等從一個地點連續延伸到另一個地點，像一條被拉開的線。","examples":[{"en":"The beach stretches for miles along the coast.","zh":"這片海灘沿著海岸綿延數英里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fields stretch from the village to the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09fc26b5d3f4b03c","term":"stretch","forms":["stretch","stretches","stretching","stretched","straught","straight"],"pos":"verb","zh":"伸展身體","explanation":"伸開四肢或身體的一部分，以放鬆肌肉、活動身體或增加柔韌性；也可指動物自然伸懶腰。","examples":[{"en":"Take a moment to stretch your shoulders after working at the desk.","zh":"伏案工作後，花點時間伸展一下肩膀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stretched before beginning her morning run.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stretch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a3127f5ea0269b5c6cf","word":"strict","forms":["strict"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0f4d1ba5932c9bb","term":"strict","forms":["strict","stricter","more strict","strictest","most strict"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精確嚴謹的","explanation":"像把繩子拉到不能鬆動一樣，表示做事、記錄或判斷非常精確，幾乎不給誤差留下空間。","examples":[{"en":"We kept strict records of every payment.","zh":"我們準確記錄了每一筆付款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the strict sense, a square is also a rectangle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-524a1d1c0a309a35","term":"strict","forms":["strict","stricter","more strict","strictest","most strict"],"pos":"adj","zh":"嚴格遵守規則的；嚴厲的","explanation":"把規則的邊界拉得很緊，表示某人或某制度要求完全按規定辦，不輕易通融。","examples":[{"en":"Our school is strict about attendance.","zh":"我們學校對出勤要求很嚴格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laboratory has strict safety rules.","zh":"這所實驗室有嚴格的安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b08f5f538c62f096","term":"strict","forms":["strict","stricter","more strict","strictest","most strict"],"pos":"adj","zh":"管教嚴厲的","explanation":"形容人時，strict 表示他把行為標準拉得很緊，要求別人守規矩，違規時通常會受到懲罰。","examples":[{"en":"The coach is strict but fair.","zh":"教練很嚴厲，但也很公平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her parents were strict with her when she was young.","zh":"她小時候父母對她管教很嚴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6b59057098aeadb333a","word":"stride","forms":["stride"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a2be2405216d796","term":"stride","forms":["stride","strides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大步","explanation":"指走路時邁出的一大步，重點是步子比平常更長、更有力。它也可以引申為一個人前進時呈現出的步伐和節奏。","examples":[{"en":"She crossed the room in three quick strides.","zh":"她邁著三大步很快穿過了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The runner lengthened his stride near the finish line.","zh":"跑步者在接近終點時加大了步幅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8084b10791c55bbc","term":"stride","forms":["stride","strides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"步幅；一步的距離","explanation":"指一大步實際跨出的距離，也就是從一隻腳落地處到另一隻腳落地處的大致長度。這個意義仍然圍繞“邁開腿後能跨多遠”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The finish line was only a stride away.","zh":"終點線就在一步之遙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His long stride covered the gap in two steps.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74a85f4d256d4e91","term":"stride","forms":["stride","strides","striding","strode","stridden","strid"],"pos":"verb","zh":"邁大步走","explanation":"指邁開較大的步子向前走，動作通常顯得自信、從容或有力量。它就是“把 stride 這一步走出來”的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"He strode confidently into the meeting room.","zh":"他自信地邁著大步走進會議室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The woman strode along the beach at sunrise.","zh":"那位女士在日出時沿著海灘大步走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7cd58cdd64a3dcfcd4a5","word":"strike","forms":["strike"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ad0f16f39977a03","term":"strike","forms":["strike","strikes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"好球；三擊不中的一擊","explanation":"在棒球中，投手投出使擊球員揮空、未揮棒但進入好球區，或擊出未被接住的界外球，都可算作一次 strike；三次 strike 通常意味著擊球員出局。","examples":[{"en":"The batter watched the third strike go past him.","zh":"擊球員眼看著第三個好球從身邊飛過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The umpire called it a strike.","zh":"裁判判定這是一個好球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10fd1965fc8dd0dc","term":"strike","forms":["strike","strikes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"罷工；集體停工","explanation":"工人為了抗議或施加壓力而集體停止工作，就是 strike；這裡是把“工作”突然停下來，以造成強烈影響。","examples":[{"en":"The workers went on strike for better pay.","zh":"工人們舉行罷工，要求提高工資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teachers called a strike after negotiations failed.","zh":"談判失敗後，教師們宣佈舉行罷工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-942295c020e0cbd7","term":"strike","forms":["strike","strikes","striking","struck","striked","strook","stroke","strake","stricken","strucken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刪去；劃掉","explanation":"把文字或內容像用力擊中一樣從文字中去掉，通常是用線劃掉或刪除。","examples":[{"en":"Please strike the last sentence from the report.","zh":"請把報告的最後一句刪掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Strike that sentence from the minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76b4e33a79aa8f09","term":"strike","forms":["strike","strikes","striking","struck","striked","strook","stroke","strake","stricken","strucken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擊打；撞擊","explanation":"用突然而有力的動作擊中人、物或某個表面，也可指船等撞上障礙物。","examples":[{"en":"The ball struck the window and broke it.","zh":"球撞上窗戶，把窗戶打碎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car struck a tree on the icy road.","zh":"汽車在結冰的路上撞上了一棵樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f79769e7400e02ccb65","word":"striking","forms":["striking"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20a58d326b6fb617","term":"striking","forms":["striking","more striking","most striking"],"pos":"adj","zh":"醒目的；令人印象深刻的","explanation":"指外貌、景象、差異或效果特別顯眼，能像一次有力的擊打那樣立刻給人留下深刻印象。","examples":[{"en":"She has striking blue eyes.","zh":"她有一雙格外醒目的藍眼睛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contrast between the two buildings is striking.","zh":"這兩座建築之間的反差非常明顯，令人印象深刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/striking","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2601ba6b712de5ad","term":"striking","forms":["striking","more striking","most striking"],"pos":"adj","zh":"罷工中的；參加罷工的","explanation":"指工人或員工正在參加集體罷工，用停止勞動來表達訴求；這裡的強烈行動感來自集體“出手”抗議。","examples":[{"en":"The striking employees gathered outside the factory.","zh":"參加罷工的員工聚集在工廠外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A charity supplied meals to the families of striking miners.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/striking","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-473287f8298dba7163a8","word":"string","forms":["string"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2941325a9ef7ab97","term":"string","forms":["string","strings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"線；繩","explanation":"由多股纖維擰成的細長、柔韌的線或繩，是“用一條線連線起來”這一核心概念的實體基礎。","examples":[{"en":"She tied the package with a piece of string.","zh":"她用一根細繩把包裹捆了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The key was hanging from a string around his neck.","zh":"鑰匙掛在他脖子上的一根繩子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/string","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37298ecbf0455f13","term":"string","forms":["string","strings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"串；一串","explanation":"物品或部分被穿線上上，或像穿線上上一樣緊密、有序地排列成一串；這正體現了“用一條線連線起來”。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a string of wooden beads around her neck.","zh":"她脖子上戴著一串木珠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hung a string of lights across the balcony.","zh":"我們在陽臺上方掛了一串燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/string","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d791ecc6d355cb45","term":"string","forms":["string","strings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"字串","explanation":"在計算機中，指連續儲存、可以作為一個整體處理的一串文字字元；它是“把字元連線成一串”的抽象形式。","examples":[{"en":"The program stores the user's name as a string.","zh":"程式把使用者的姓名儲存為字串。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This function returns an empty string when no result is found.","zh":"找不到結果時，這個函式會返回一個空字串。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/string","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d60384034b77c13c2840","word":"strip","forms":["strip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd537349067e265b","term":"strip","forms":["strip","strips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狹長地帶","explanation":"指細長的一片土地或區域，就像把一大片地方拉成了一條狹長的帶子。","examples":[{"en":"The village lies on a narrow strip of land between the river and the hills.","zh":"這個村莊位於河流和山丘之間的一條狹長土地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A strip of forest separates the two farms.","zh":"一條狹長的森林把兩個農場隔開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fed5c2334230e38c","term":"strip","forms":["strip","strips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長條材料","explanation":"指任何細長的材料或材料條，可以是一條，也可以泛指許多這樣的長條。","examples":[{"en":"Cut the cardboard into thin strips.","zh":"把硬紙板剪成細長條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tied the package with a strip of cloth.","zh":"她用一條布帶把包裹紮好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22b5c13e5807e93f","term":"strip","forms":["strip","strips","stripping","stripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"剝去；除去","explanation":"表示把表面、外層或附著物除掉，常讓人聯想到把東西一條條剝下來。","examples":[{"en":"We stripped the old wallpaper before painting the room.","zh":"我們先把舊牆紙剝掉，再給房間刷漆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers stripped the bark from the logs.","zh":"工人們把原木上的樹皮剝了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ef29453488783085","term":"strip","forms":["strip","strips","stripping","stripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"脫掉衣服","explanation":"表示脫去身上的衣服，畫面上就是把覆蓋身體的那一層除掉；根據語境可指脫掉部分衣物，也可指脫光。","examples":[{"en":"He stripped off his wet clothes and wrapped himself in a towel.","zh":"他脫下溼衣服，用毛巾裹住了自己。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children stripped and jumped into the lake.","zh":"孩子們脫掉衣服，跳進了湖裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bed2032ed3d8300b771","word":"stripe","forms":["stripe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7fe0346c98a249b2","term":"stripe","forms":["stripe","stripes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"條紋圖案中的一道色帶","explanation":"指在重複圖案中，與相鄰區域顏色不同的一條長帶；許多這樣的帶子排列在一起，就形成衣物、動物皮毛或旗幟上的條紋圖案。","examples":[{"en":"The zebra has black and white stripes.","zh":"斑馬身上有黑白相間的條紋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a shirt with blue stripes.","zh":"她穿了一件帶藍色條紋的襯衫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stripe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9a1e68b20f15621","term":"stripe","forms":["stripe","stripes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一道細長的色帶或色痕","explanation":"指背景上單獨出現的一條較長、較直而且顏色不同的帶狀區域，不一定屬於重複圖案。","examples":[{"en":"A white stripe ran down the center of the road.","zh":"道路中央有一道白色標線延伸開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A blue stripe ran along the boat's hull.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stripe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc058f85f5680919cb2d","word":"strive","forms":["strive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-13ffa70d3c9cf8a7","term":"strive","forms":["strive","strives","striving","strove","strived","striven","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"努力爭取；奮力達到","explanation":"指為了實現某個結果而認真、持續地付出很大努力。這是 strive 最核心的意思，畫面就是迎著阻力向目標前進。","examples":[{"en":"We strive to provide the best service possible.","zh":"我們努力提供儘可能好的服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She strives for excellence in everything she does.","zh":"她做任何事都努力追求卓越。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c336dc41b12fe80","term":"strive","forms":["strive","strives","striving","strove","strived","striven","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"與……抗爭；奮力對抗","explanation":"指在阻力、困境或對立力量面前奮力抗爭。它仍然是“迎著阻力向前衝”的核心畫面，只是阻力被特別突出。","examples":[{"en":"They continued to strive against poverty.","zh":"他們繼續與貧困作鬥爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The community strove against discrimination for many years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ba7573640bbbb13a9e2","word":"stroke","forms":["stroke"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b173c84c02316e5","term":"stroke","forms":["stroke","strokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一擊；打擊","explanation":"指一次擊打或打在某處的一下，符合“一次有方向的移動或衝擊”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"He felt a sharp stroke on his shoulder.","zh":"他感到肩膀上被狠狠打了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One powerful stroke shattered the wooden panel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stroke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1b82a44db15ff06","term":"stroke","forms":["stroke","strokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"筆畫；一筆","explanation":"指筆、鉛筆、畫筆等工具一次移動留下的線條或痕跡；也就是筆移動後留下的一次“有方向的移動”。","examples":[{"en":"The character can be written in five strokes.","zh":"這個字可以用五筆寫成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She added a few dark strokes to the painting.","zh":"她給畫添了幾筆深色線條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stroke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29da8976fe9bd21d","term":"stroke","forms":["stroke","strokes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"中風","explanation":"指腦部血液供應突然中斷或出血，導致不同程度的腦損傷，可能危及生命；它像身體遭受了一次嚴重的衝擊。","examples":[{"en":"Her grandfather suffered a stroke last winter.","zh":"她的祖父去年冬天中風了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor explained that quick treatment after a stroke is essential.","zh":"醫生解釋說，中風後及時治療至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stroke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5525b916996d8ad7","term":"stroke","forms":["stroke","strokes","stroking","stroked","strokest","strokedst","stroketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕撫；撫摸","explanation":"指讓手或刷子沿表面朝一個方向輕輕移動，通常是為了撫摸、安撫或表達親近；這就是“一次有方向的移動”。","examples":[{"en":"She gently stroked the cat's back.","zh":"她輕輕撫摸著貓的背。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He stroked his daughter's hair to calm her down.","zh":"他撫摸女兒的頭髮，讓她平靜下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stroke","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-108821b3ae13d0bf1ca9","word":"stroll","forms":["stroll"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b53705f3e9f30e41","term":"stroll","forms":["stroll","strolls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"悠閒散步","explanation":"stroll 是不趕時間、帶著放鬆心情走一會兒，重點不在趕路，而在享受漫步的過程。","examples":[{"en":"We took a stroll along the beach after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們沿著海灘悠閒地散了會兒步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She went for a stroll through the old town.","zh":"她在老城區悠閒地逛了一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stroll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a34b889fe072ec2b","term":"stroll","forms":["stroll","strolls","strolling","strolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"悠閒漫步","explanation":"作動詞時，stroll 表示不趕時間地走動或閒逛，和名詞“悠閒散步”是同一個核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"They strolled around the park until sunset.","zh":"他們在公園裡悠閒地逛到日落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He strolled along the river, listening to music.","zh":"他一邊聽音樂，一邊沿河悠閒地走著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stroll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eda15ce4834ac303532b","word":"strong","forms":["strong"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da42d3b769bbfee9","term":"strong","forms":["strong","stronger","strongest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體強壯","explanation":"表示人或動物具有很大的體力、肌肉力量，能有力地完成動作。","examples":[{"en":"She is strong enough to carry the box upstairs.","zh":"她力氣很大，足以把箱子搬上樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young athlete has strong legs.","zh":"這名年輕運動員的腿很有力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e9bcd2ee7688bb5","term":"strong","forms":["strong","stronger","strongest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結實耐用","explanation":"表示東西能夠承受很大的外力，不容易斷裂、損壞或倒塌。","examples":[{"en":"This table is strong enough to hold all the books.","zh":"這張桌子很結實，放下這些書也沒問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tent needs strong ropes before the storm arrives.","zh":"暴風雨來臨前，這頂帳篷需要結實的繩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f358dfe216fb6f63","term":"strong","forms":["strong","stronger","strongest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"刺激性強","explanation":"表示光、聲音、顏色或其他感官刺激的強度很高，給人的感覺特別明顯。","examples":[{"en":"The strong sunlight made it hard to see.","zh":"強烈的陽光讓人很難看清東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has a strong feeling that something is wrong.","zh":"他強烈地感覺到有些不對勁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-adf0d3f5f1ada968fdea","word":"structural","forms":["structural"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb4c61f5c114f27e","term":"structural","forms":["structural","more structural","most structural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結構上的","explanation":"指與某個事物的內部結構、組織方式或基本構成有關，重點在“骨架”而不是外表。","examples":[{"en":"The building has serious structural problems.","zh":"這座建築存在嚴重的結構問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reforms brought about structural changes in the industry.","zh":"這些改革給這個行業帶來了結構性變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/structural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a20ecd7db54ef77f","term":"structural","forms":["structural","more structural","most structural"],"pos":"adj","zh":"涉及建造構造的","explanation":"指建造、支撐和連線建築物時所涉及的力學和工程構造；它關注建築骨架如何承重和保持穩定。","examples":[{"en":"A structural engineer checked the bridge before it opened.","zh":"大橋開放前，一名結構工程師檢查了它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey revealed serious structural defects in the roof.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/structural","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-520cdb563bf80b193aab","word":"structure","forms":["structure"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-625040fafd5621c7","term":"structure","forms":["structure","structures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"由部分搭成的整體","explanation":"指許多不同部分組合起來、彼此連線而形成的完整東西，可以是人建造的物體，也可以是動物搭出的東西。這個義項保留了“把部件搭在一起”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The children built a small structure from cardboard.","zh":"孩子們用硬紙板搭了一個小結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge is a remarkable steel structure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/structure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3da1bfc83cf17356","term":"structure","forms":["structure","structures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"整體的組織方式","explanation":"指文章、句子、活動或其他事物怎樣把各部分安排成一個有條理的整體。這裡不一定有實體材料，但仍然是“把部分組合好”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The structure of the report makes the main argument easy to follow.","zh":"這份報告的結構讓主要論點很容易理解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report examines the company's management structure.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/structure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-72b268f8262a02381219","word":"struggle","forms":["struggle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c80410942859afda","term":"struggle","forms":["struggle","struggles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體掙扎","explanation":"指人在被抓住、受困或執行困難動作時扭動身體、奮力擺脫的動作；這是“被阻力纏住而用力”的最具體畫面。","examples":[{"en":"After a short struggle, the child freed himself from the net.","zh":"掙扎了一會兒後，孩子從網中掙脫了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A violent struggle broke out beside the doorway.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/struggle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1916c1f53b90875b","term":"struggle","forms":["struggle","struggles","struggling","struggled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"艱難應對","explanation":"指面對問題、任務或處境時感到困難，因而苦苦應對；這裡不一定有實際的身體動作，但仍保留了“被阻力纏住、費力向前”的核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Many students struggle with time management.","zh":"許多學生在時間管理方面感到很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She struggled to understand the instructions.","zh":"她費了很大勁才理解這些說明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/struggle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34f9a187aeae47e4f367","word":"stubborn","forms":["stubborn"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-083404a154cfd6e3","term":"stubborn","forms":["stubborn","stubborner","stubbornest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"固執的；頑固的","explanation":"指一個人像被釘住一樣，不願改變自己的意見、決定或做法，即使別人已經提出了理由或建議。這個詞通常暗示這種堅持不夠理性或不聽勸。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is stubborn about doing everything herself.","zh":"瑪雅固執地什麼事都要自己做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was too stubborn to admit that he was wrong.","zh":"他太固執了，不肯承認自己錯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stubborn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2cc2c5926955ebeb","term":"stubborn","forms":["stubborn","stubborner","stubbornest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"僵硬難加工的","explanation":"形容材料不容易彎曲、熔化、移動或加工，彷彿也“不肯動”。這裡說的是材料本身的物理性質，不是說它有人的性格。","examples":[{"en":"This stubborn metal will not bend without special tools.","zh":"這種僵硬的金屬不用特殊工具就彎不過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stubborn clay resisted even his sharpest tools.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stubborn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-264c8c381bf16c982a4e","word":"student","forms":["student"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3393d6c868053872","term":"student","forms":["student","students"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某領域的學習者","explanation":"student 可以指專門學習或研究某個學科、領域或物件的人，不要求他一定在學校正式註冊；重點是持續投入學習和鑽研。","examples":[{"en":"She is a student of human behavior.","zh":"她是研究人類行為的學者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has always been a keen student of history.","zh":"他一直是歷史的熱心研究者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/student","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c2cd3d23cd78ea4","term":"student","forms":["student","students"],"pos":"noun","zh":"在校學生","explanation":"student 也指正式在學校、學院、大學或其他教育機構註冊學習的人；這是日常最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The students are preparing for their final exams.","zh":"學生們正在準備期末考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every student received a timetable on arrival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/student","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da0daaba4b156961c049","word":"studio","forms":["studio"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5e50db0dbe6f5c1f","term":"studio","forms":["studio","studios"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術家工作室","explanation":"指藝術家或攝影師工作的房間或作坊，是“創作空間”這一核心形象最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She spends most of the day in her studio painting.","zh":"她每天大部分時間都在自己的工作室裡畫畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The photographer invited us into his studio.","zh":"那位攝影師邀請我們進入他的工作室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/studio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5256d4bc924f685e","term":"studio","forms":["studio","studios"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錄音或影視製作場所","explanation":"指製作廣播、電視節目、唱片或電影的場所；核心仍是“作品在這裡被創作和製作出來”。","examples":[{"en":"The band is recording its new album in a studio.","zh":"這個樂隊正在錄音室錄製新專輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The show is broadcast live from the studio.","zh":"這個節目從演播室現場直播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/studio","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c87ed818fb90f3f88fa","word":"study","forms":["study"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a53410c87c31f741","term":"study","forms":["study","studies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學習；研習","explanation":"指為了獲得知識而進行的學習，也可以指某一門學習活動。這裡的核心是把注意力和精力持續投入到知識上。","examples":[{"en":"The study of languages is fascinating.","zh":"語言學習很有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her study of history began at school.","zh":"她從上學時就開始學習歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/study","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2557e30607a6a25","term":"study","forms":["study","studies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"研究；考察","explanation":"指有目的地仔細觀察、分析某人或某事的過程，重點不只是獲得知識，而是深入查明物件。","examples":[{"en":"The report is based on a careful study of local traffic.","zh":"這份報告基於對當地交通的仔細研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a study of the old building before restoring it.","zh":"修復那座老建築前，她對它進行了研究。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/study","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2a2a75e03d6828c","term":"study","forms":["study","studies","studying","studied","studiest","studieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"學習；複習","explanation":"指透過集中精力閱讀、練習和回顧來獲得或鞏固知識，常常是為了考試或避免遺忘。","examples":[{"en":"I need to study for my biology exam tonight.","zh":"今晚我得複習生物考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studies every evening after dinner.","zh":"她每天晚飯後學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/study","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02be0b03b8192084","term":"study","forms":["study","studies","studying","studied","studiest","studieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"研究","explanation":"指為了理解、說明或實際應用而系統地調查某個物件或問題；物件不一定是書本，也可以是生物、社會現象等。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists study how plants respond to light.","zh":"科學家研究植物如何對光線作出反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers study how whales communicate underwater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/study","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92a22b672be0fed1","term":"study","forms":["study","studies","studying","studied","studiest","studieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"仔細檢視","explanation":"指把目光集中在某物上，認真、細緻地檢視，以便弄清它的內容或細節。","examples":[{"en":"We studied the map before choosing a route.","zh":"我們仔細看了地圖後才選擇路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied his face for a moment.","zh":"她仔細端詳了他的臉片刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/study","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35bafb1ce99aef3ab068","word":"stuff","forms":["stuff"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d0ed426f0ed9c09","term":"stuff","forms":["stuff","stuffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"東西；個人物品","explanation":"指一堆沒有逐件說明的物品，尤其可指某人的隨身物品或個人 belongings。它強調“各種東西混在一起”，而不是某一種特定物件。","examples":[{"en":"What is all that stuff on your bedroom floor?","zh":"你臥室地板上的那些東西到底是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She packed all her stuff into two bags.","zh":"她把自己的所有東西都裝進了兩個袋子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stuff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b739f22908bbc49","term":"stuff","forms":["stuff","stuffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事情；各種事","explanation":"泛指沒有具體說明的事情、活動或要處理的內容，相當於“事情、雜事”。","examples":[{"en":"I have some stuff to finish before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前我還有些事情要做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We talked about work and other stuff.","zh":"我們聊了工作和其他一些事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stuff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c713476e3627782","term":"stuff","forms":["stuff","stuffs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"材料；物質","explanation":"指構成某個實物的有形材料或物質，重點是“做成它的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"What kind of stuff is this table made of?","zh":"這張桌子是用什麼材料做的？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What is that sticky stuff on the handle?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stuff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-debfeb7e8f5ab68a","term":"stuff","forms":["stuff","stuffs","stuffing","stuffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塞滿；填入","explanation":"把某物用力、密集地塞進另一個物體或空間，使其被填滿。","examples":[{"en":"I’m going to stuff this pillow with feathers.","zh":"我要用羽毛把這個枕頭填滿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He stuffed the clothes into the suitcase.","zh":"他把衣服一股腦兒塞進了手提箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stuff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06a0b2e5f36d3998","term":"stuff","forms":["stuff","stuffs","stuffing","stuffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擠入；塞進空間","explanation":"把東西壓縮後塞進一個空間，常常暗示空間不夠或動作很匆忙。","examples":[{"en":"She stuffed the papers into her desk drawer.","zh":"她把檔案塞進了書桌抽屜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stuffed the sleeping bag into its sack.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stuff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ca63f7be6e1758e","term":"stuff","forms":["stuff","stuffs","stuffing","stuffed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃得很飽","explanation":"表示吃了很多，已經飽到不想再吃；可以看作“把自己塞滿”的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"I’m stuffed after that huge dinner.","zh":"吃完那頓豐盛的晚餐，我撐得不行了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stuffed ourselves with dumplings at the festival.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stuff","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56648f5b0c21414fff59","word":"stumble","forms":["stumble"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-839a522859b95596","term":"stumble","forms":["stumble","stumbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"絆倒；失足","explanation":"指走路時被東西絆到、失去平衡，或因此跌倒的一下。這個名詞保留了“腳步突然被打亂”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"One stumble on the wet steps could send you down.","zh":"在溼臺階上絆一下，就可能一路摔下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stumbled over a root in the dark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2d03ad04995929d","term":"stumble","forms":["stumble","stumbles","stumbling","stumbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"絆倒；跌跌撞撞地走","explanation":"指腳被障礙物絆住而失去平衡，或因為不穩而跌跌撞撞地走。這是 stumble 最直接、最容易聯想到的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"He stumbled over a rock and dropped his backpack.","zh":"他被一塊石頭絆倒，揹包也掉了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stumbled through the dark hallway.","zh":"她在黑暗的走廊裡跌跌撞撞地走著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-796096df99028012","term":"stumble","forms":["stumble","stumbles","stumbling","stumbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"犯錯；遇到困難","explanation":"像走路絆了一下那樣，在說話、學習或做事時卡住、出錯或進展不順。它既可以表示偶爾犯錯，也可以表示處理某個問題時感到困難。","examples":[{"en":"I stumbled over her name during the introduction.","zh":"介紹時我把她的名字說得磕磕絆絆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project stumbled because the team lacked experience.","zh":"這個專案因為團隊缺乏經驗而進展不順。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcc94fafcf26fe73dd51","word":"stun","forms":["stun"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6e190be766aaf4c","term":"stun","forms":["stun","stuns","stunning","stunned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擊暈；使失去行動能力","explanation":"指透過擊打或其他強烈衝擊，使人或動物暫時失去清醒、方向感或行動能力。","examples":[{"en":"The keeper used a shield to stun the angry dog.","zh":"看守用盾牌把那隻發怒的狗擊懵了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The loud blast stunned everyone in the room.","zh":"巨大的爆炸聲把房間裡的所有人都震得一時反應不過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de65ddfe1dec58b5","term":"stun","forms":["stun","stuns","stunning","stunned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使震驚；使愣住","explanation":"指某個訊息、結果或事件強烈地衝擊某人，使其驚訝到一時難以作出反應。","examples":[{"en":"The final result stunned the entire audience.","zh":"最終結果讓全場觀眾都震驚不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was stunned by how quickly she solved the problem.","zh":"她解決這個問題的速度讓我震驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2d214a484e9d44d34c0","word":"stupid","forms":["stupid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a44d9ee0ee8a66aa","term":"stupid","forms":["stupid","stupider","more stupid","stupidest","most stupid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愚蠢的；不明智的","explanation":"表示缺乏理解力、判斷力或常識；既可以形容人，也可以形容決定、錯誤、問題等。形容事物時，重點通常不是它沒有智力，而是說它很不合理、很煩人或很糟糕。","examples":[{"en":"It was stupid to leave the door unlocked.","zh":"把門鎖著不管是很不明智的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I made a stupid mistake on the first question.","zh":"我在第一道題上犯了一個愚蠢的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stupid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f45e00229e1b1079","term":"stupid","forms":["stupid","stupider","more stupid","stupidest","most stupid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"該死的；惱人的","explanation":"有時並不是認真判斷某人智力低，而是把某個倒黴、荒唐或令人惱火的東西籠統地罵成 stupid。這是由“愚蠢”聯想到的情緒化用法，常帶有誇張或自嘲色彩。","examples":[{"en":"This stupid phone keeps turning off.","zh":"這破手機老是自動關機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't get this stupid printer to work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stupid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25a5c452fb9585d5c81a","word":"sturdy","forms":["sturdy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab6f9a008cbeb8ff","term":"sturdy","forms":["sturdy","sturdier","sturdiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結實的；強健的","explanation":"指人或物體有堅實、強健的外形或質地，不容易被弄壞；記住那棵經風的大樹即可。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a sturdy pair of boots for the long hike.","zh":"她買了一雙結實的靴子，準備走很長的路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sturdy young man carried the boxes upstairs.","zh":"那個健壯的年輕人把箱子搬上了樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sturdy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1e63c7717ca018c","term":"sturdy","forms":["sturdy","sturdier","sturdiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結構牢固的","explanation":"指建築、傢俱或其他物品整體結構紮實，能夠承受風吹、使用或壓力。","examples":[{"en":"We need a sturdy table that can hold the heavy machine.","zh":"我們需要一張能承受這臺重機器的結實桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sturdy shelves supported several heavy dictionaries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sturdy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36ee39884a2292eb5904","word":"stutter","forms":["stutter"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e85be72f2eec3a7b","term":"stutter","forms":["stutter","stutters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口吃；說話障礙","explanation":"指說話時聲音、音節或詞語反覆、拖住或突然停頓的說話障礙；重點是聲音像卡住一樣斷續，而不只是普通的思考猶豫。","examples":[{"en":"He has had a stutter since childhood.","zh":"他從小就有口吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her stutter becomes worse when she is nervous.","zh":"她緊張時口吃會更嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stutter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d56608f14124d35","term":"stutter","forms":["stutter","stutters","stuttering","stuttered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"結巴；口吃著說","explanation":"指說話時不由自主地重複聲音或音節，或在詞語之間卡住；它把“聲音卡頓”這個核心畫面變成了動作。","examples":[{"en":"He stuttered when he tried to introduce himself.","zh":"他試著介紹自己時結巴了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stuttered out a quiet apology.","zh":"她結結巴巴地小聲道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stutter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb86eb2d914d37df6857","word":"style","forms":["style"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ad830e3d01bc088","term":"style","forms":["style","styles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表達風格","explanation":"style 指一個人寫作、說話或表達思想時形成的獨特方式，尤其可以指被認為成熟、優秀或有特色的表達方式。","examples":[{"en":"Her writing style is clear and easy to recognize.","zh":"她的寫作風格清晰而且很容易辨認。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article is written in a formal style.","zh":"這篇文章採用了正式的寫作風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/style","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-172b86b29f54b1b4","term":"style","forms":["style","styles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"創作或呈現方式","explanation":"style 也指建築、繪畫、音樂、設計或其他創作所採用的整體方式，包括外觀、形式和給人的感覺；它就是把同一類事物“做成什麼樣”的方式。","examples":[{"en":"The house combines a traditional style with modern materials.","zh":"這座房子把傳統風格和現代材料結合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I like the simple style of this painting.","zh":"我喜歡這幅畫簡潔的風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/style","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88e4e87aeda09f63","term":"style","forms":["style","styles","styling","styled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"按某種風格設計","explanation":"style 作動詞時，可以表示按照某種形式、外觀或風格來設計、製作或安排某物，也就是把“風格”施加到作品或事物上。","examples":[{"en":"The designer styled the room in a clean, modern way.","zh":"設計師把房間設計成簡潔現代的風格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She styled her hair in loose waves for the event.","zh":"她為活動把頭髮做成了鬆散的波浪形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/style","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39d254bb15a2f6c35812","word":"stylish","forms":["stylish"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c2e23f4ad76d31a","term":"stylish","forms":["stylish","more stylish","most stylish"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有型的；時髦的","explanation":"形容人、衣服或物品看起來很有風格、很時髦，給人“有型”的印象。這是 stylish 最常見、最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a stylish jacket for the winter.","zh":"她買了一件很時髦的冬季外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small apartment is simple but stylish.","zh":"這套小公寓雖然簡潔，卻很有格調。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stylish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fe94cf88850a359","term":"stylish","forms":["stylish","more stylish","most stylish"],"pos":"adj","zh":"優雅而有品味的","explanation":"形容一個人的穿著、舉止或整體氣質不只是時髦，而且顯得優雅、得體、有審美。這是“有型”向“有品味”發展的意思。","examples":[{"en":"He is a stylish man who always dresses appropriately for the occasion.","zh":"他是個很有品味的人，總能根據場合穿著得體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her stylish apartment combines modern furniture with antique rugs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stylish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9491f4c1bf7b0cffbad","word":"subject","forms":["subject"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1257b0307194e95a","term":"subject","forms":["subject","subjects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主語","explanation":"在句子中，subject 是句子主要圍繞的成分；在主動句裡通常是執行動作的人或物，在被動句裡也可能是接受動作的物件。","examples":[{"en":"In “The dog chased the ball,” “the dog” is the subject.","zh":"在“狗追球”這句話中，“狗”是主語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The subject of the passive sentence is the person receiving the message.","zh":"這個被動句的主語是收到訊息的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subject","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5d7f3f64cd567bc","term":"subject","forms":["subject","subjects"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主題；談論物件","explanation":"指文章、談話、藝術作品或研究主要圍繞的內容，也就是被放在注意力中心的東西。","examples":[{"en":"Climate change was the main subject of the meeting.","zh":"氣候變化是這次會議的主要議題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting’s subject is a family gathered around a table.","zh":"這幅畫描繪的主題是一家人圍坐在桌旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subject","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31e54e952e25cdde3cd9","word":"subjective","forms":["subjective"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31c7849a76f7f7b6","term":"subjective","forms":["subjective","more subjective","most subjective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基於個人感受的","explanation":"指觀點、判斷或評價主要來自個人的感覺、直覺和立場，而不是完全依據可觀察的事實或嚴密的邏輯。它強調“從觀察者內部出發”，常與 objective“客觀的”相對。","examples":[{"en":"Whether the painting is beautiful is highly subjective.","zh":"這幅畫是否美，很大程度上取決於個人感受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reviewer gave a subjective assessment of the restaurant.","zh":"評論家根據個人感受評價了這家餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subjective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c27e30700fe8fce","term":"subjective","forms":["subjective","more subjective","most subjective"],"pos":"adj","zh":"源於個人心理狀態的","explanation":"指某種結果、判斷或測量受到人的心理狀態和個人經驗影響，來源在人的意識內部，不一定能直接從外部刺激中驗證。它和 s1 相近，但更強調心理過程或經驗本身。","examples":[{"en":"The survey relies on subjective measures of well-being.","zh":"這項調查依靠對幸福感的主觀測量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pain ratings rely on subjective experience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subjective","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3a48c2443b07faa22ab4","word":"submarine","forms":["submarine"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8daf6902c82cf7d6","term":"submarine","forms":["submarine"],"pos":"adj","zh":"水下的","explanation":"指位於水面下、在海底附近，或專門供水下使用的事物；這是“藏在海面下方”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The engineers built a submarine tunnel beneath the bay.","zh":"工程師們在海灣下方修建了一條水下隧道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The submarine equipment must work under extreme pressure.","zh":"水下裝置必須能在極高壓力下工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/submarine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69f0cc7eb8aae5c6","term":"submarine","forms":["submarine","submarines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"潛水艇","explanation":"一種可以潛入水下航行的船，正是“藏在海面下方”的核心名詞畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The submarine disappeared beneath the waves before dawn.","zh":"天亮前，那艘潛水艇潛入了海浪之下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a submarine surface near the harbor.","zh":"我們看見一艘潛水艇在港口附近浮出水面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/submarine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75490bd7b93e6fa7d18c","word":"submit","forms":["submit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2a1ae775de81f93","term":"submit","forms":["submit","submits","submitting","submitted","submittest","submittedst","submitteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"屈服；服從","explanation":"指不再抵抗，接受別人、權威或某種力量的要求或控制。重點是“把自己置於對方之下”，常常帶有被迫或不情願的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The rebels finally submitted to the king.","zh":"叛軍最終向國王屈服了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refused to submit to unfair pressure.","zh":"她拒絕屈服於不公平的壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/submit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7fdd974f68050a2a","term":"submit","forms":["submit","submits","submitting","submitted","submittest","submittedst","submitteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提交；呈交","explanation":"指把申請、計劃、文章等交給有權稽核、考慮、評分或批准的人或機構。這仍然保留“把東西放到對方手中處理”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Please submit your application by Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前提交申請。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The research team submitted its findings for review.","zh":"研究團隊提交了研究結果以供審閱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/submit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ee449b9b821e8fadc35","word":"subordinate","forms":["subordinate"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cff49c03227f577d","term":"subordinate","forms":["subordinate","more subordinate","most subordinate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"較低層級的","explanation":"指在等級、類別或組織位置上低於另一個物件的，核心意思是“處在下面一層”。它不一定表示能力差，只說明相對位置較低。","examples":[{"en":"The assistant plays a subordinate role in the department.","zh":"這名助理在部門中擔任較低層級的角色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Safety is not subordinate to speed.","zh":"安全並不次於速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subordinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3efb282768c14ad9","term":"subordinate","forms":["subordinate","more subordinate","most subordinate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"從屬的（語法）","explanation":"在語法中，指依附主句、用來補充或修飾主句的成分，尤其是不能像主句那樣獨立發揮完整作用的從句。","examples":[{"en":"“Because it was raining” is a subordinate clause.","zh":"“因為下雨了”是一個從句。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The subordinate clause begins with although.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subordinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb7613570b9a8182","term":"subordinate","forms":["subordinate","subordinates","subordinating","subordinated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使從屬於；使次要","explanation":"把某人或某事放到較低、依附的位置，使它服務於或服從另一個更主要的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The plan subordinates short-term profits to long-term stability.","zh":"這項計劃把短期利潤置於長期穩定之下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He subordinated personal ambition to the team's needs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subordinate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f40fd562f63078722310","word":"subscribe","forms":["subscribe"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ebb0a80390a4417","term":"subscribe","forms":["subscribe","subscribes","subscribing","subscribed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"訂閱出版物","explanation":"表示登記後在一段時間內定期收到報紙、雜誌等出版物。它保留了“把名字寫進持續名單”的核心畫面，重點是連續獲得，而不是隻買一次。","examples":[{"en":"I subscribed to a science magazine for two years.","zh":"我訂閱了一本科學雜誌兩年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She subscribed her son to the weekly newspaper.","zh":"她給兒子訂了這份週報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subscribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb1ec75ec79f3e8a","term":"subscribe","forms":["subscribe","subscribes","subscribing","subscribed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"訂購服務","explanation":"表示付費加入一項持續提供的服務，例如網路、手機套餐或流媒體服務。這裡仍然是“進入一個持續名單”，只是定期收到的東西從出版物變成了服務許可權。","examples":[{"en":"We subscribed to a music service last month.","zh":"我們上個月訂購了一項音樂服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many families subscribe to high-speed internet.","zh":"許多家庭都訂購高速網際網路服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subscribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c03b55b0e342649d","term":"subscribe","forms":["subscribe","subscribes","subscribing","subscribed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"贊同觀點","explanation":"表示接受或贊同某個理論、想法或原則。它把“加入名單”的畫面轉成了“把自己歸入某種觀點”，所以通常不是指訂閱一篇理論文章。","examples":[{"en":"I don't subscribe to the idea that success is only about money.","zh":"我不贊同成功只與金錢有關這種想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She subscribes to a very different view of education.","zh":"她贊同一種非常不同的教育觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subscribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a8fa7fd60893411a4990","word":"subscription","forms":["subscription"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7024c4fbacb7c23b","term":"subscription","forms":["subscription","subscriptions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"訂閱；訂閱資格","explanation":"指登記並通常付費後，在規定的一段時間內持續獲得某種資源或服務的資格，例如閱讀報紙、觀看影片或使用軟體。","examples":[{"en":"I renewed my music subscription for another year.","zh":"我把音樂服務的訂閱續了一年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her newspaper subscription includes delivery every morning.","zh":"她訂的報紙服務包括每天早晨送報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subscription","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb7cb8fb038e0b351510","word":"subsequent","forms":["subsequent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56bc348d8a3198dd","term":"subsequent","forms":["subsequent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"隨後發生的；後來的","explanation":"表示某件事在另一件事之後發生，重點是時間上的“跟在後面”。它常用於回顧前文已經提到的事件，並說明之後出現的年份、階段、結果或變化。","examples":[{"en":"The company expanded rapidly in the subsequent years.","zh":"這家公司在隨後的幾年裡迅速擴張。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A subsequent investigation revealed several errors.","zh":"後續調查發現了幾處錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subsequent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f25456f87cafd62","term":"subsequent","forms":["subsequent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"順序或位置上後面的","explanation":"表示在排列、地點或次序上跟在另一個物件後面，不一定強調時間先後。可以把它理解為“排在後面的那一個”。","examples":[{"en":"The subsequent chapters explain the method in greater detail.","zh":"後面的章節更詳細地解釋了這一方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rule applies to this page and all subsequent pages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subsequent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70b187f682fb59025286","word":"subsidize","forms":["subsidize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-161abc256f6cdb63","term":"subsidize","forms":["subsidize","subsidizes","subsidizing","subsidized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"補貼；資助","explanation":"指給某人、組織、行業或活動提供補貼，使其能夠繼續運作、降低成本或實現某專案標。補貼者通常是政府、機構或有資金的一方，受助者不一定需要償還這筆錢。","examples":[{"en":"The government subsidizes public transportation to keep fares low.","zh":"政府補貼公共交通，以維持較低的票價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity subsidized meals for low-income families.","zh":"這家慈善機構為低收入家庭的餐食提供補貼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subsidize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15fc7418ed949dd6e2d1","word":"subsidy","forms":["subsidy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0559145c6304b4ea","term":"subsidy","forms":["subsidy","subsidies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"補貼；資助","explanation":"指政府、機構或其他組織為支援某個行業、專案、產品或群體而提供的資金，相當於在背後“託一把”。","examples":[{"en":"The government offers subsidies to farmers who use less water.","zh":"政府向少用水的農民提供補貼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new subsidy helped make electric cars more affordable.","zh":"這項新補貼幫助降低了電動汽車的購買成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subsidy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-943ae60b331ded4aee35","word":"substance","forms":["substance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ef6de0e253040ec","term":"substance","forms":["substance","substances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"物質；材料","explanation":"指構成物體或存在於其中的實際物質，是讓東西真正存在的“材料”。","examples":[{"en":"The scientist found a strange substance in the bottle.","zh":"科學家在瓶子裡發現了一種奇怪的物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water is the main substance in the mixture.","zh":"水是這種混合物中的主要物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89ec940d8a45dc8f","term":"substance","forms":["substance","substances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實質；核心內容","explanation":"指一件事最重要、最有價值的部分，而不是表面形式或外在印象。","examples":[{"en":"The report has a clear structure, but it lacks substance.","zh":"這份報告結構清晰，但缺乏實質內容。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She focused on the substance of his proposal rather than its appearance.","zh":"她關注的是他的提議的實質，而不是它的表面形式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94a48d9e39baad15b24f","word":"substantial","forms":["substantial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cbd3e74b2f17201f","term":"substantial","forms":["substantial","more substantial","most substantial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真實的；確實的","explanation":"強調事情不是虛構、表面或空話，而是真實發生、確實有效的；它保留了“有實質、有分量”的核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy has brought substantial benefits to local families.","zh":"新政策確實給當地家庭帶來了很大的好處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need substantial evidence before making such a serious decision.","zh":"在作出如此重大的決定前，我們需要確鑿而充分的證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substantial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8e221f3bdd93e700","term":"substantial","forms":["substantial","more substantial","most substantial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"大量的；可觀的","explanation":"表示數量、金額、規模或程度很大，已經達到值得注意的分量；這是現代英語中非常常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The project requires a substantial amount of funding.","zh":"這個專案需要一大筆資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A substantial number of residents attended the meeting.","zh":"有相當多的居民參加了會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substantial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9992775f34927c0b","term":"substantial","forms":["substantial","more substantial","most substantial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"豐盛的；足以填飽的","explanation":"形容食物或一餐內容充足、營養和分量都夠，能讓人真正吃飽，而不只是簡單的小零食。","examples":[{"en":"After the hike, we stopped for a substantial meal.","zh":"徒步之後，我們停下來吃了一頓豐盛的飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prefers a substantial breakfast before a busy day.","zh":"她喜歡在忙碌的一天開始前吃一頓豐盛的早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substantial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75519932722f6e16485a","word":"substitute","forms":["substitute"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-95b77d8246de16a2","term":"substitute","forms":["substitute","substitutes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"替代物；替代者","explanation":"指可以代替另一個人或物、並完成相近功能的東西或人。重點不是完全相同，而是能夠在需要時頂上原來的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Yogurt is a good substitute for cream in this recipe.","zh":"在這個食譜裡，酸奶是奶油的不錯替代品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a substitute for the broken printer.","zh":"我們需要找一臺替代壞掉印表機的裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substitute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4cdb6fe954e802b9","term":"substitute","forms":["substitute","substitutes","substituting","substituted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用……代替……","explanation":"表示把一個東西放到另一個東西的位置上，使它承擔相同或相近的功能。","examples":[{"en":"I had no milk, so I substituted water for it.","zh":"我沒有牛奶，所以用水代替了牛奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can substitute beans for the meat in this dish.","zh":"你可以在這道菜裡用豆子代替肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substitute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2298c2ae6c6faae4e835","word":"subtle","forms":["subtle"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad8f6855b05430d5","term":"subtle","forms":["subtle","subtler","more subtle","subtlest","most subtle"],"pos":"adj","zh":"細微的；精巧而不明顯的","explanation":"指具體事物或感官效果很細、很輕、很精巧，因此不容易被直接察覺；它就像一根很細的線，存在卻不顯眼。","examples":[{"en":"The fabric has a subtle shine in the sunlight.","zh":"這塊布在陽光下泛著淡淡的光澤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a dress with a subtle pattern.","zh":"她選了一條帶有精細暗紋的連衣裙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subtle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68e3854564c94c54","term":"subtle","forms":["subtle","subtler","more subtle","subtlest","most subtle"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含蓄的；難以察覺的","explanation":"指意義、差別、影響或表達方式不直接顯露，需要仔細觀察或思考才能發現；細線從具體的“細微”變成了思想上的“隱約而有分寸”。","examples":[{"en":"There is a subtle difference between the two colors.","zh":"這兩種顏色之間有細微的差別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave me a subtle hint that it was time to leave.","zh":"他含蓄地暗示我該離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subtle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1cc624bbe4bb93f327c0","word":"subtract","forms":["subtract"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c48f98d5cb98da6","term":"subtract","forms":["subtract","subtracts","subtracting","subtracted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"減去；扣除","explanation":"從一個總數或數量中拿走一部分，求剩下多少；除了數學中的“減去”，也可以表示從總費用、收入或預算中扣除一筆數額。","examples":[{"en":"Subtract the delivery fee from the total to see how much the meal itself cost.","zh":"從總額中扣除配送費，就能看出這頓飯本身花了多少錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She subtracted $20 from her weekly budget for the bus pass.","zh":"她從每週預算中扣除了20美元，用來購買公交月票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subtract","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c47a58e12937ba7dd647","word":"suburb","forms":["suburb"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bd53c744727065c","term":"suburb","forms":["suburb","suburbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城市外圍的住宅區","explanation":"指城市或大城鎮外緣、以住宅為主的區域，通常配有學校、商店、餐館等日常設施；它仍是城市生活圈的一部分，而不是偏遠鄉村。","examples":[{"en":"They moved to a quiet suburb with good schools.","zh":"他們搬到了一個學校條件很好的安靜郊區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The suburb has several grocery stores and a small shopping center.","zh":"這個郊區有幾家雜貨店和一個小型購物中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suburb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94605ab07dc0610a","term":"suburb","forms":["suburb","suburbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城市群中的分割槽","explanation":"在澳大利亞、愛爾蘭、紐西蘭和英國等英語用法中，suburb 還可以指城市群裡的一個具體分割槽；它不一定位於整個城市群的最外圍，重點是“城市中的一個區域”。","examples":[{"en":"She lives in a suburb of Melbourne and takes the train downtown.","zh":"她住在墨爾本的一個城區，每天乘火車去市中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic serves several outer suburbs of Melbourne.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suburb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5c509152b44d4cf07880","word":"suburban","forms":["suburban"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e62aa408d724e0f","term":"suburban","forms":["suburban","more suburban","most suburban"],"pos":"adj","zh":"郊區的；城市外圍的","explanation":"指與城市郊區有關、位於城市邊緣，或帶有郊區生活特點的事物。核心畫面就是城市中心外面的那一圈居住區。","examples":[{"en":"They moved to a quiet suburban neighborhood last year.","zh":"他們去年搬到了一個安靜的郊區社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The suburban train is crowded every morning.","zh":"這趟郊區列車每天早上都很擁擠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suburban","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6016c3bca66aae178832","word":"subway/underground/metro","forms":["subway","metro"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb76e63dc684cff2","term":"subway","forms":["subway","subways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地鐵；地下鐵路","explanation":"指建在地下、為城市大量乘客提供運輸的鐵路系統。它強調的是整套交通設施，而不只是某一列車。","examples":[{"en":"We took the subway to the museum.","zh":"我們乘地鐵去了博物館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The subway is crowded during rush hour.","zh":"高峰時段地鐵很擁擠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-27a7b88c06dd4501","term":"subway","forms":["subway","subways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地鐵列車","explanation":"在具體上下車、到站或執行的語境中，subway也可以指在地下鐵路系統中行駛的那一列車。","examples":[{"en":"The subway arrived just as we reached the platform.","zh":"我們剛到站臺，地鐵列車就進站了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The subway arrived crowded with morning commuters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/subway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5e9ba99590127be","term":"metro","forms":["metro","metros"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地鐵；城市快速軌道交通","explanation":"指服務大城市的快速軌道交通系統，也可以泛指乘坐或等待的地鐵列車；核心畫面就是在城市中快速運送乘客的軌道網。","examples":[{"en":"He is going to the stadium by metro.","zh":"他要乘地鐵去體育場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took the metro downtown.","zh":"我們乘地鐵去了市中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metro","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6998ec8d781ca3a08ea2","word":"succeed","forms":["succeed"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e0c6e501252b337","term":"succeed","forms":["succeed","succeeds","succeeding","succeeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成功做到","explanation":"表示經過努力後達成原本想要的目標；前面的行動終於順利接上了預期結果。","examples":[{"en":"She succeeded in solving the problem before the deadline.","zh":"她成功地在截止日期前解決了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team succeeded in raising enough money for the project.","zh":"這個團隊成功籌集到了專案所需的資金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/succeed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f52bae071403289b","term":"succeed","forms":["succeed","succeeds","succeeding","succeeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取得成功","explanation":"泛指一個人或計劃發展順利、取得成功，未必特別指出某一個具體目標。","examples":[{"en":"With patience and practice, he hopes to succeed as a musician.","zh":"他希望憑藉耐心和練習成為一名成功的音樂家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She succeeded after several unsuccessful attempts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/succeed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aee408847d35e44e9943","word":"success","forms":["success"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2b34e44727ab970","term":"success","forms":["success","successes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"達到目標；成功","explanation":"指經過努力後達到原先設定的目標，例如考試透過、計劃完成或嘗試終於成功。這是 success 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Her first attempt to repair the bike was a success.","zh":"她第一次修腳踏車就成功了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project was a huge success.","zh":"這個專案取得了巨大的成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/success","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca84e363f5b72e59","term":"success","forms":["success","successes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟上的成功；盈利","explanation":"指事業或商業活動帶來的盈利和經濟上的成功，常用於商業語境。","examples":[{"en":"The small company achieved financial success within three years.","zh":"這家小公司在三年內取得了經濟上的成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The business finally achieved financial success.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/success","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2430e09ec2ec28450fe5","word":"successful","forms":["successful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-db21db86f14c76ab","term":"successful","forms":["successful","more successful","most successful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"成功的；有效的","explanation":"指人或事情順利達到原定目標，或者確實產生了想要的效果。目標可以是贏得比賽、完成計劃，也可以是讓實驗成功或讓治療發揮作用。","examples":[{"en":"The experiment was successful and produced the expected results.","zh":"這項實驗很成功，得出了預期結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is successful in building a small business.","zh":"她成功地建立起了一家小企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/successful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a130ddbc4e7fc2b9a7de","word":"succession","forms":["succession"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73237e898c5bfb29","term":"succession","forms":["succession","successions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續；接連出現","explanation":"指人或事物按照先後順序一個接一個地出現或發生，重點是這種連續的排列過程或一連串事件。","examples":[{"en":"The team won three games in succession.","zh":"這支隊連續贏了三場比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A succession of storms delayed the flight.","zh":"一場接一場的暴風雨導致航班延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/succession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-932fffd73ef21084","term":"succession","forms":["succession","successions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"繼承；接替","explanation":"指某人按照規定或傳統接替前任，取得王位、職位、財產等，尤其常用於歷史上的王位繼承。","examples":[{"en":"The king's death triggered a dispute over the succession.","zh":"國王去世引發了關於王位繼承的爭議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constitution sets clear rules for presidential succession.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/succession","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d64a6ee7e975d66ba75c","word":"successive","forms":["successive"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc96e7ebee09eeaa","term":"successive","forms":["successive"],"pos":"adj","zh":"連續的；接連的","explanation":"指同類事件或狀態一個接一個地發生，中間沒有被打斷，重點在連續的先後順序上。","examples":[{"en":"The team won three successive matches.","zh":"這支隊伍連續贏了三場比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rain fell on four successive days.","zh":"大雨連續下了四天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/successive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-548e56fceb6ba189d7cd","word":"successor","forms":["successor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7a8577b9f5e659c","term":"successor","forms":["successor","successors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職位或頭銜的繼任者","explanation":"指緊接前任之後接掌職位或頭銜的人，也可以指接替前一項職責或地位的事物。重點是“前任結束後，由誰或什麼接上來”。","examples":[{"en":"The board chose Maria as the successor to the retiring director.","zh":"董事會選瑪麗亞接替即將退休的主任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The retiring director introduced her successor to the staff.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/successor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b04ef031640cccab","term":"successor","forms":["successor","successors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"順位中的下一位繼承人","explanation":"指按照法律、傳統或家族順序排在下一位、將來有資格繼承某種權利或地位的人。這裡強調的是繼承順序，不一定表示已經正式接任。","examples":[{"en":"Under the old law, the eldest child was the successor in line to the throne.","zh":"按照舊法律，長子是王位的下一位繼承人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constitution identifies the successor to the throne.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/successor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5c935d142e9fa6eeb75","word":"such","forms":["such"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28d8f2a7e5cd3e63","term":"such","forms":["such"],"pos":"det","zh":"這樣的；這種的","explanation":"指前文或語境中已經暗示的某種型別、樣子或性質，相當於“像這樣、屬於這一類的”。","examples":[{"en":"I've never seen such clouds in the sky before.","zh":"我以前從未見過天空中有這樣的雲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Such kindness is rare these days.","zh":"如今這樣善良的行為很少見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/such","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89e4ac19f2a8fba2","term":"such","forms":["such"],"pos":"det","zh":"如此；這麼","explanation":"放在形容詞或名詞短語前，強調程度很高，表示“如此……、這麼……”，常帶有說話人的評價。","examples":[{"en":"It was such a beautiful evening that nobody wanted to leave.","zh":"那是一個如此美麗的夜晚，誰也不想離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had such fun at the party.","zh":"我們在聚會上玩得特別開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/such","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-954bafccc8afa13db7e1","word":"suck","forms":["suck"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-25e98963e4e46095","term":"suck","forms":["suck","sucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸吮；吸入的一口","explanation":"指用嘴吸入液體或空氣的一次動作，或吸吮本身；重點是“把東西吸進嘴裡”。","examples":[{"en":"She took a quick suck on the straw.","zh":"她用吸管快速吸了一口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby quieted after a few sucks.","zh":"嬰兒吸吮了幾下後安靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28ce1dcd587e8b8c","term":"suck","forms":["suck","sucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸入；抽吸","explanation":"指氣體或液體因吸力而被吸進去的過程或一次抽吸，仍然是“被吸向某處”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The suck of the pump pulled water from the tank.","zh":"泵的抽吸力把水從水箱裡抽了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One suck through the straw emptied the tiny carton.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c72dfbd1d941899c","term":"suck","forms":["suck","sucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸力","explanation":"指某個裝置或力量能夠把空氣、液體等吸過來的能力，也就是“吸得有多強”。","examples":[{"en":"This vacuum has enough suck to lift the dust from the carpet.","zh":"這臺吸塵器的吸力足以把地毯上的灰塵吸起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden suck of the current pulled him under.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ba450101a105b80","term":"suck","forms":["suck","sucks","sucking","sucked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸入；吮吸","explanation":"指用嘴唇和嘴把液體，尤其是奶，吸進嘴裡；這是全詞最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The baby sucked milk from the bottle.","zh":"嬰兒從奶瓶裡吸奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He sucked on a lemon wedge.","zh":"他吮吸著一瓣檸檬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c930efac16735077","term":"suck","forms":["suck","sucks","sucking","sucked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸取；抽走","explanation":"指把液體、氣體或其他東西從某處吸出來，動作上是“把東西吸走”。","examples":[{"en":"The machine sucked the water out of the basement.","zh":"機器把地下室裡的水抽了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mosquito sucked blood from my arm.","zh":"蚊子從我的胳膊上吸血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa82dfe978415153","term":"suck","forms":["suck","sucks","sucking","sucked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸向；吸走","explanation":"指某種力量把東西向一個方向拉過去，甚至不需要直接接觸；這是“吸力”從嘴巴擴充套件到物理作用。","examples":[{"en":"The wind sucked the smoke out through the window.","zh":"風把煙從窗戶吸了出去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat was sucked toward the rocks.","zh":"船被吸向了礁石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1afa3ca6fb1e88a26806","word":"sudden","forms":["sudden"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c6a2adc264ffcb2","term":"sudden","forms":["sudden","suddener","suddenest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"突然的；出乎意料的","explanation":"指事情在幾乎沒有預兆的情況下迅速發生，讓人感到意外或來不及準備。核心畫面就是門突然開啟，變化一下子來到眼前。","examples":[{"en":"A sudden storm forced us to cancel the picnic.","zh":"一場突如其來的暴雨迫使我們取消了野餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden change in his voice worried me.","zh":"他聲音的突然變化讓我很擔心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sudden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d015bafffbb48c3cb20","word":"sue","forms":["sue"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c519340b7a7b282","term":"sue","forms":["sue","sues","suing","sued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"起訴；提起民事訴訟","explanation":"sue someone表示把某人告到法院，通常指民事案件，例如因產品缺陷、損害或違約而要求賠償。它強調正式啟動法律行動，不只是私下抱怨。","examples":[{"en":"The customer sued the company for selling a dangerous product.","zh":"這名顧客起訴那家公司銷售危險產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sued the contractor over the unfinished work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cf14180a81b04a1f3cc","word":"suffer","forms":["suffer"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f5a5c3d934d5a28","term":"suffer","forms":["suffer","suffers","suffering","suffered","sufferest","sufferedst","suffereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經歷苦難","explanation":"指人在生活、工作或其他處境中承受困難和艱辛，重點是經歷一段不容易的過程，不一定專指身體疼痛。","examples":[{"en":"Many families suffered during the long drought.","zh":"許多家庭在長期乾旱期間受了苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She suffered for years after losing her home.","zh":"她失去家園後，多年來一直過得很艱難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suffer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5dfdb188c117960f","term":"suffer","forms":["suffer","suffers","suffering","suffered","sufferest","sufferedst","suffereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感到疼痛","explanation":"指身體或精神上承受痛苦，尤其強調痛苦本身，而不只是發生了受傷這件事。","examples":[{"en":"He suffered from severe back pain after the accident.","zh":"事故後，他飽受嚴重的背痛折磨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog was badly injured but did not suffer for long.","zh":"那隻狗傷得很重，但沒有痛苦太久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suffer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9abdfa5387bf94176ea","word":"sufficient","forms":["sufficient"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9f91fd8d314b49d1","term":"sufficient","forms":["sufficient","more sufficient","most sufficient"],"pos":"adj","zh":"足以滿足要求的","explanation":"指某個條件、數量或程度已經達到需要的標準，因此可以滿足要求；重點是“夠用、夠條件”，不一定很多。","examples":[{"en":"One example is not sufficient evidence.","zh":"一個例子不是充分的證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The explanation was sufficient to answer my question.","zh":"這個解釋足以回答我的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sufficient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11dd0f26b1e1b221","term":"sufficient","forms":["sufficient"],"pos":"det","zh":"足夠的","explanation":"放在名詞前，表示數量達到某項任務或需要所要求的程度，核心意思是“夠用的”。","examples":[{"en":"We have sufficient food for everyone.","zh":"我們有足夠的食物供大家食用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please bring sufficient copies for the whole team.","zh":"請帶夠全組需要的影印件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sufficient","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b15c961913da1c45d87b","word":"suffocate","forms":["suffocate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a89fbc2c6bebc0c7","term":"suffocate","forms":["suffocate","suffocates","suffocating","suffocated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"窒息；缺氧","explanation":"指身體因吸入的氧氣嚴重不足而難以呼吸，可能是暫時的窒息狀態，也可能繼續發展為死亡。這裡的核心畫面就是“空氣進不來，喘不過氣”。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers began to suffocate in the smoke.","zh":"徒步者開始在煙霧中窒息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trapped miners would suffocate without fresh air.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suffocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-452119940040a64d","term":"suffocate","forms":["suffocate","suffocates","suffocating","suffocated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使感到壓抑；被壓得喘不過氣","explanation":"比喻壓力、工作量、問題或某個人太強，使人感到像缺氧一樣無法承受。這裡沒有真的缺少氧氣，而是把“喘不過氣”的身體感覺用於心理或生活壓力。","examples":[{"en":"She felt suffocated by the constant demands of her job.","zh":"不斷的工作要求讓她感到壓抑得喘不過氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His constant attention began to suffocate her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suffocate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc767fb1c6efc232caf9","word":"sugar","forms":["sugar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4ceccc88f5c20c58","term":"sugar","forms":["sugar","sugars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"糖","explanation":"指從甘蔗或甜菜等製得、用於使食物和飲料變甜的糖，通常想到白砂糖等晶體。","examples":[{"en":"I don't take sugar in my tea.","zh":"我喝茶不加糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sauce has too much sugar in it.","zh":"這個醬汁含糖太多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sugar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d2894882ca3b4cc","term":"sugar","forms":["sugar","sugars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"親愛的","explanation":"作親暱稱呼時，表示對親近的人友好、溫柔地說話，類似“親愛的”。","examples":[{"en":"Take your time, sugar; there's no rush.","zh":"慢慢來，親愛的，不著急。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Come here, sugar, and give Grandma a hug.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sugar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc726d0a525fdaf759e4","word":"suggest","forms":["suggest"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8328f6301d15c9a","term":"suggest","forms":["suggest","suggests","suggesting","suggested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暗示；言下之意是","explanation":"說話人沒有把意思直接說出來，只是把這個想法遞給聽者，讓對方自己推斷出來；因此常譯為“暗示”或“言下之意是”。","examples":[{"en":"Are you suggesting that I lied?","zh":"你是在暗示我撒謊嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His silence suggested that he knew more than he said.","zh":"他的沉默暗示他知道的比說出來的更多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suggest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63c96024c50ba2a5","term":"suggest","forms":["suggest","suggests","suggesting","suggested"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提議；建議","explanation":"把一個可供選擇的辦法或行動遞出來，請別人考慮；這是日常英語中非常常見的“建議”義。","examples":[{"en":"I suggest taking a short break before we continue.","zh":"我建議我們繼續之前先休息一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She suggested a quieter restaurant for dinner.","zh":"她建議晚餐去一家安靜些的餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suggest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-650ffa82126b74c533df","word":"suggestion","forms":["suggestion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc7deeb1f57319f0","term":"suggestion","forms":["suggestion","suggestions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建議；提議","explanation":"指遞給別人考慮的一條具體想法，通常是為了幫助解決問題或決定怎麼做。這是 suggestion 最常見、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She made a suggestion for improving the website.","zh":"她提出了一個改進網站的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her suggestion solved the seating problem immediately.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suggestion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17ce61372782aff8","term":"suggestion","forms":["suggestion","suggestions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建議這一行為；暗示","explanation":"指把想法遞給別人、讓對方接受或考慮的過程，而不是某一條具體建議本身。這個意思強調“提出或暗示”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"Suggestion often works better than a direct order.","zh":"含蓄的建議往往比直接命令更有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"At his suggestion, we postponed the inspection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suggestion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5304378d007825ccb104","word":"suicide","forms":["suicide"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fcfcfaf0fd7f6b66","term":"suicide","forms":["suicide","suicides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自殺行為","explanation":"指一個人有意結束自己的生命，強調“毀滅轉向自己”這一核心概念。這裡說的是行為本身，通常不數具體次數。","examples":[{"en":"The campaign focuses on preventing suicide among young people.","zh":"這項活動重點是預防年輕人自殺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She died by suicide after years of severe depression.","zh":"她在多年嚴重抑鬱後自殺身亡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suicide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ef1d6341a5b1c50","term":"suicide","forms":["suicide","suicides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自取毀滅","explanation":"比喻某個行動雖然目的不一定是死亡，卻會把個人、事業或組織推向毀滅；核心仍是“毀滅的方向轉向自己”。","examples":[{"en":"Cutting the research budget now would be economic suicide.","zh":"現在削減研究預算無異於經濟上的自取毀滅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ignoring its biggest customers would be commercial suicide.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suicide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21839e0eb260dda7a564","word":"suit","forms":["suit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9c4d43ff73b7dc1","term":"suit","forms":["suit","suits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成套服裝；西裝","explanation":"指搭配成套穿著的衣服，尤其是配套的外套和褲子，通常譯為“西裝”；也可以泛指女式套裝。核心畫面是幾件衣服彼此配合、作為一套穿著。","examples":[{"en":"He wore a dark suit to the interview.","zh":"他穿了一套深色西裝去參加面試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This suit comes with a matching jacket and trousers.","zh":"這套衣服配有相配的外套和褲子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4d8cd9868b51731","term":"suit","forms":["suit","suits","suiting","suited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使相配；使適合","explanation":"指調整或安排某物，使它適合某人、某種用途或某個情境。它延續了“成套、彼此配合”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The designer suited the outfit to the dancer's movement.","zh":"設計師讓這套服裝適合舞者的動作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This training is suited to beginners.","zh":"這項訓練適合初學者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb0888a72d67320d","term":"suit","forms":["suit","suits","suiting","suited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"適合；與某人相稱","explanation":"指某個名字、特點、角色或行為與某人相稱，彷彿正好配得上這個人。它把“外表相配”擴充套件到了性格、事實或身份。","examples":[{"en":"The nickname suits him because he is always early.","zh":"這個綽號很適合他，因為他總是提前到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That shade of blue really suits you.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2d92fc5142e6a2c1e6c4","word":"suitable","forms":["suitable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c99cfab482ec6f38","term":"suitable","forms":["suitable","more suitable","most suitable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"合適的；適宜的","explanation":"某人或某物具備實現某個目的所需的條件，或者與某個場合相稱，因此可以被選用。它強調“匹配、用得上”，不一定表示這是所有選擇中最好的一個。","examples":[{"en":"This room is suitable for small meetings.","zh":"這個房間適合舉行小型會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are looking for a suitable candidate for the position.","zh":"我們正在尋找適合這個職位的人選。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suitable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9817a64167e5ea6c638f","word":"suitcase","forms":["suitcase"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3fe9999ab3d796ab","term":"suitcase","forms":["suitcase","suitcases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行李箱","explanation":"旅行時用來裝衣物和其他個人用品的大箱子，通常可以提著或拉著走。它強調的是旅行用的箱子，而不是一般的盒子或收納箱。","examples":[{"en":"I packed my suitcase the night before the flight.","zh":"我在航班起飛前一晚收拾好了行李箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her suitcase was too heavy to lift.","zh":"她的行李箱太重了，提不起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suitcase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f8ebd43dbef1f029bf49","word":"suite","forms":["suite"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9dd69c75f385e2e","term":"suite","forms":["suite","suites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成套的一組","explanation":"指彼此相關、連續出現，或被安排在一起使用的一組事物；重點不只是數量多，而是它們構成一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The company offers a suite of online training courses.","zh":"這家公司提供一套相互配套的線上培訓課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer created a suite of matching furniture.","zh":"這位設計師設計了一套相互配套的傢俱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83f085cb15b9b139","term":"suite","forms":["suite","suites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"套房","explanation":"指由幾個相連房間組成的一套房間，通常可以透過獨立入口進出；酒店裡的臥室、客廳等常合稱為一間 suite。","examples":[{"en":"We booked a suite with a separate living room.","zh":"我們訂了一間帶獨立客廳的套房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel upgraded us to a larger suite.","zh":"酒店把我們升級到了更大的套房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-09f5ffef28309853265c","word":"sum","forms":["sum"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-250415d0a39a1a65","term":"sum","forms":["sum","sums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總數；和","explanation":"把兩個或更多數相加後得到的結果就是 sum，例如幾個數合在一起所得的總數。","examples":[{"en":"The sum of 18 and 24 is 42.","zh":"18 加 24 的和是 42。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sum of seven and eight is fifteen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2982bed78d5e72c1","term":"sum","forms":["sum","sums"],"pos":"noun","zh":"概括；全部內容","explanation":"當許多事實、證據或想法被放在一起看時，它們的整體內容可以稱為 sum，即“總的概括”。","examples":[{"en":"The report is the sum of years of careful research.","zh":"這份報告是多年認真研究的總結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sum of his advice was to wait patiently.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4e3b62bf415f97d","term":"sum","forms":["sum","sums","summing","summed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相加","explanation":"sum 作動詞時表示把幾個數、金額或數量加在一起，得到一個合計結果。","examples":[{"en":"Sum the figures in the two columns and write down the total.","zh":"把兩列中的數字相加，然後寫下總數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sum the columns to calculate the overall cost.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-feadf054a2fa17d7","term":"sum","forms":["sum","sums","summing","summed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"概括","explanation":"sum 作動詞還可以把一段話、證據或經歷壓縮成幾個核心要點，也就是把複雜內容“收攏”起來。","examples":[{"en":"Could you sum up the main points at the end of the meeting?","zh":"你能在會議結束時概括一下要點嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She summed up the argument in one clear sentence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bae9264d6d972b80f4fe","word":"summarize","forms":["summarize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-757b8314a0d6bb2d","term":"summarize","forms":["summarize","summarizes","summarizing","summarized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"總結；概括成摘要","explanation":"指閱讀或處理一段較長的內容後，提取主要資訊並整理成簡明的摘要，重點在於“把內容壓縮整理出來”。","examples":[{"en":"Could you summarize the report in three sentences?","zh":"你能用三句話概括這份報告嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She summarized the article for her classmates.","zh":"她為同學們總結了這篇文章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summarize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-080376fc76dd789b","term":"summarize","forms":["summarize","summarizes","summarizing","summarized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"概述；回顧要點","explanation":"指把已經發生的討論、會議或事件中的關鍵事實、決定和結果重新簡要說一遍，重點在於“回顧主線和要點”。","examples":[{"en":"At the end of the meeting, the chair summarized the main decisions.","zh":"會議結束時，主席概述了主要決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Summarize the main findings in your final paragraph.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summarize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-761b7ad8ad439b2855fc","word":"summary","forms":["summary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91e1cb50199536f3","term":"summary","forms":["summary","summaries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摘要；總結","explanation":"指把文章、故事、報告或事件的主要內容壓縮後呈現出來的文字或說明。讀者藉此可以快速瞭解整體內容，而不必先讀完全部材料。","examples":[{"en":"I read a summary of the novel before choosing whether to buy it.","zh":"我先讀了這部小說的簡介，再決定要不要買。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The summary highlights the report's most important findings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-13984a4e7e0edce830a0","word":"summit","forms":["summit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a0f56bbd1e641d9","term":"summit","forms":["summit","summits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頂端；山頂","explanation":"指山、建築物或其他事物最高的那一點或那一面，最典型的畫面就是登上一座山的最高處。","examples":[{"en":"We reached the summit just before sunset.","zh":"我們在日落前剛好到達了山頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Snow covered the summit of the mountain.","zh":"積雪覆蓋了這座山的山頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bdc32dd6abf8adbf","term":"summit","forms":["summit","summits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成就的巔峰","explanation":"比喻一個人、事業或發展的最高成就和最輝煌階段，就像從山腳一路走到事業的頂峰。","examples":[{"en":"Winning the award marked the summit of her career.","zh":"贏得這個獎項標誌著她事業的巔峰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He reached the summit of his profession at a young age.","zh":"他很年輕時就達到了職業生涯的巔峰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2815cb02b95b6d15383b","word":"summon","forms":["summon"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f382ea044e3b5de7","term":"summon","forms":["summon","summons","summoning","summoned","summonest","summonedst","summoneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"叫某人到場","explanation":"正式要求某人來到指定地點，常帶有權威、命令或官方要求的意味；這是“把目標召到面前”的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"The manager summoned me to her office after lunch.","zh":"午飯後，經理叫我到她辦公室去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness was summoned to appear in court.","zh":"證人被傳召出庭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d794382d78508222","term":"summon","forms":["summon","summons","summoning","summoned","summonest","summonedst","summoneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用魔法召喚","explanation":"透過魔法或超自然力量把生物、元素或其他力量召到身邊，是“把某物召來”最直觀的幻想用法。","examples":[{"en":"The mage summoned a wall of ice to block the passage.","zh":"法師召出一道冰牆擋住了通道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spell summons a guardian whenever the village is threatened.","zh":"每當村莊受到威脅，這個法術就會召喚出一名守護者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27756f050e14a1cb1c1e","word":"sun","forms":["sun"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-253378ebf1dde4a4","term":"sun","forms":["sun","suns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"太陽；恆星","explanation":"指一顆像太陽一樣、位於某個行星系統中心併發光的恆星；日常語境中特別常指我們的太陽。","examples":[{"en":"The sun was already high when we left.","zh":"我們出發時太陽已經升得很高了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The distant planet circles a sun much smaller than ours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f42611ed1d690c0","term":"sun","forms":["sun","suns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陽光；日照","explanation":"指太陽照來的光和熱，也就是人們曬到、感受到的陽光。","examples":[{"en":"The children played in the sun all afternoon.","zh":"孩子們在陽光下玩了一下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the clothes out in the sun to dry.","zh":"把衣服放在陽光下曬乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91075b2b75b38f98","term":"sun","forms":["sun","suns","sunning","sunned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……拿去曬","explanation":"把身體、衣物或其他東西暴露在陽光下，讓它接受陽光的照射。","examples":[{"en":"She sunned her face on the balcony.","zh":"她在陽臺上曬臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sunned the blankets on the fence to remove their musty smell.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52864d6f00e66105","term":"sun","forms":["sun","suns","sunning","sunned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"曬太陽","explanation":"自己處在陽光下取暖或休息，也就是曬太陽。","examples":[{"en":"The cat was sunning itself by the window.","zh":"貓正在窗邊曬太陽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I like to sun on the porch in the morning.","zh":"我喜歡早上在門廊上曬太陽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2333a7e3a607935c67c","word":"sunny","forms":["sunny"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-420681cd5f5a0aa0","term":"sunny","forms":["sunny","sunnier","sunniest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"陽光明媚的","explanation":"指天氣中陽光很多、天空較晴朗的狀態，是 sunny 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"It was sunny when we left the house.","zh":"我們離開家時天氣陽光明媚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The forecast says it will be sunny tomorrow.","zh":"天氣預報說，明天會是晴天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-95858030ca952f44","term":"sunny","forms":["sunny","sunnier","sunniest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"開朗愉快的","explanation":"把陽光帶來的明亮、溫暖感用來形容人或性格，表示樂觀、親切、讓人感到愉快。","examples":[{"en":"Her sunny personality makes everyone feel welcome.","zh":"她開朗的性格讓每個人都感到受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sunny disposition brightened the gloomy office.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-73d1b1b1bc1dabfb97f2","word":"super","forms":["super"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a856429f8a5d83c8","term":"super","forms":["super"],"pos":"adj","zh":"特別優秀的","explanation":"指質量非常高、精緻出色，明顯超過普通水平；這是“super”表示“超過一般”的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"We had a super meal at that little restaurant.","zh":"我們在那家小餐館吃了一頓特別棒的飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You did a super job organizing the fair.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/super","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bf91ea09951bf22","term":"super","forms":["super"],"pos":"adv","zh":"非常","explanation":"放在形容詞或副詞前，把程度大幅提高，表示“非常、特別”。它仍然保留“超過平常程度”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The new café is super popular with students.","zh":"這家新咖啡館在學生中非常受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That puzzle was super difficult.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/super","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0178fa91fd0fe5bdd059","word":"superb","forms":["superb"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76fa81b5ae5480a9","term":"superb","forms":["superb","superber","superbest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極好的；一流的","explanation":"表示某物或某人的品質、表現等好得突出，遠超普通水平，常可譯為“極好的”“棒極了”或“一流的”。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves superb food.","zh":"這家餐館提供的食物棒極了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a superb performance.","zh":"她的表現非常出色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4795f26bd53836f","term":"superb","forms":["superb","superber","superbest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"宏偉壯麗的","explanation":"形容建築、景觀或場面規模宏大、外觀壯麗，給人莊嚴而震撼的感覺；它關注的不只是質量好，還包括氣勢和格局。","examples":[{"en":"We admired the superb palace from across the river.","zh":"我們從河對岸欣賞那座宏偉的宮殿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The palace offers superb views over the bay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-707ecbfbee9c35825861","word":"superficial","forms":["superficial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a07dcd76b526f348","term":"superficial","forms":["superficial","more superficial","most superficial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"貌似真實但經不起細看","explanation":"指某種印象、解釋或說法乍看似乎真實，進一步檢查後卻發現並不可靠；它像只看到了表面，裡面並沒有相應的根據。","examples":[{"en":"Their agreement was only superficial; they still disagreed on the main issue.","zh":"他們的共識只是表面上的，在主要問題上仍然意見不合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The resemblance was superficial and vanished on closer inspection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superficial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0bdcdfbdb79af2f","term":"superficial","forms":["superficial","more superficial","most superficial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"膚淺的；不深入的","explanation":"指研究、思考、知識或分析只停留在顯而易見的部分，沒有充分考察更深層的原因和細節。這是“目光只在表面滑過”最常見的抽象用法。","examples":[{"en":"A superficial reading of the report can lead to the wrong conclusion.","zh":"膚淺地讀這份報告可能會得出錯誤的結論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His knowledge of the subject is superficial.","zh":"他對這個 विषय的瞭解很膚淺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superficial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e5ab374362bce1357a7","word":"superintendent","forms":["superintendent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-194e9f2efc5def14","term":"superintendent","forms":["superintendent","superintendents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主管；監督人","explanation":"指獲授權監督、指揮或管理某項事務的人，也就是負責巡視全域性、讓工作正常運轉的主管。這是本詞最核心、最容易遷移到不同場景的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The superintendent oversees all the schools in the district.","zh":"這位主管負責監督該地區的所有學校。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was appointed superintendent of the factory.","zh":"她被任命為這家工廠的主管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superintendent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-690e7b4eb339cf9d","term":"superintendent","forms":["superintendent","superintendents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"警察總監級主管","explanation":"在英聯邦一些國家，這是警察系統中的一個職級，位於總督察之上、總警司之下。它仍然體現“監督一大片工作”的核心概念，但專指警察職位。","examples":[{"en":"The superintendent announced a new plan to reduce crime.","zh":"這位警察主管宣佈了一項減少犯罪的新計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The superintendent ordered a review of the investigation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superintendent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc4d6c9e874c1f120aa1","word":"superior","forms":["superior"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1406291a2bd5c4c4","term":"superior","forms":["superior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"更好；更高等","explanation":"指某人或某物在質量、能力或整體價值上高於另一個物件，也就是“優於……”。","examples":[{"en":"This material is superior to the cheaper alternative.","zh":"這種材料優於那種更便宜的替代品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She believed the new system was far superior to the old one.","zh":"她認為新系統比舊系統好得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-20267291201685bf","term":"superior","forms":["superior"],"pos":"adj","zh":"地位更高","explanation":"指人在職位、身份或等級上高於別人，核心仍是“站得更高”。","examples":[{"en":"He remained calm in front of his superior.","zh":"在上級面前，他仍然保持鎮定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a superior officer may authorize the search.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55eefe86d4bb7e98","term":"superior","forms":["superior","superiors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"上級；上司","explanation":"指在職位、等級或組織關係中高於某人的人，最常見於工作或正式上下級關係。","examples":[{"en":"She asked her superior for permission to leave early.","zh":"她向上級請示提前離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officer reported the problem to a superior.","zh":"這名官員向一位上級報告了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc26a9df87021d7d66e5","word":"superiority","forms":["superiority"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8fd1d31ff4ed7211","term":"superiority","forms":["superiority","superiorities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"優越性；優勢","explanation":"指某人、團體或事物在能力、表現、地位等方面高於別人或別的事物的狀態，也可以指這種高出所形成的優勢。它可以是實際表現上的領先，也可以是某種被認為更高的地位。","examples":[{"en":"The team gained superiority in the second half.","zh":"這支隊伍在下半場取得了優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She never claimed superiority over her colleagues.","zh":"她從未聲稱自己比同事高人一等。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superiority","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16d1c76df24f2f303ad1","word":"supermarket","forms":["supermarket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50392d8bc84512ce","term":"supermarket","forms":["supermarket","supermarkets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大型自助商店","explanation":"指一種大型商店，顧客通常自己拿取商品再到收銀處付款，裡面主要賣食品，也常賣藥品、家居用品、衣物等日常用品。這就是最常見的“超市”義。","examples":[{"en":"I went to the supermarket to buy some food.","zh":"我去超市買了些食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a supermarket near our apartment.","zh":"我們公寓附近有一家超市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supermarket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cea7179ca5c099cf","term":"supermarket","forms":["supermarket","supermarkets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"超市連鎖企業","explanation":"也可以不指某一家店，而指由許多家超市組成的連鎖企業或品牌；重點從“一個賣東西的地方”擴大到“經營這類店的整體企業”。","examples":[{"en":"The supermarket is opening three new stores this year.","zh":"這家連鎖超市今年要開三家新店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two supermarkets control most of the region's grocery market.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supermarket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b872323369bf4d0e641","word":"superstition","forms":["superstition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6fabab1db1bbdf4f","term":"superstition","forms":["superstition","superstitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"迷信；迷信觀念","explanation":"指沒有理性或科學依據，卻相信某種行為、徵兆或神秘力量能夠影響運氣和事件結果的觀念，也可以指具體的一種迷信說法。","examples":[{"en":"It is a common superstition that walking under a ladder brings bad luck.","zh":"人們普遍迷信，從梯子下面走過會帶來壞運氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He does not believe in superstition, but he still avoids the number thirteen.","zh":"他不相信迷信，但還是會避開十三這個數字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superstition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2b126945c422a4d223b","word":"superstitious","forms":["superstitious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7c6e4d77b37989c3","term":"superstitious","forms":["superstitious","more superstitious","most superstitious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"相信迷信的","explanation":"指容易相信沒有可靠依據的吉凶說法，或按照這類說法來判斷和行動的人。重點是這個人的態度：他把某些巧合、禁忌或儀式看成可能影響運氣的規則。","examples":[{"en":"My grandmother is superstitious about the number thirteen.","zh":"我祖母對數字十三很迷信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is too superstitious to walk under a ladder.","zh":"他太迷信了，不敢從梯子下面走過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superstitious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8f350c8d49a37067","term":"superstitious","forms":["superstitious","more superstitious","most superstitious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迷信的；帶有迷信色彩的","explanation":"指某種習俗、說法、儀式或做法本身建立在迷信觀念上，而不是說它只是神秘或難以解釋。它和核心義相連：人的迷信態度進一步形成了迷信的行為或傳統。","examples":[{"en":"Many people still follow superstitious customs at weddings.","zh":"許多人在婚禮上仍然遵循一些迷信習俗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He had a superstitious fear of broken mirrors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superstitious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afd63cca4f004105fe02","word":"supervise","forms":["supervise"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bed1c84078e5f897","term":"supervise","forms":["supervise","supervises","supervising","supervised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"監督並指導","explanation":"指負責觀察某項任務、團隊或組織的進展，並在需要時管理、指導和糾正方向；核心畫面就是站在較高位置看全域性，確保事情按計劃進行。","examples":[{"en":"The manager supervises a team of twelve designers.","zh":"經理負責監督一個由十二名設計師組成的團隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A nurse will supervise the students during their first shift.","zh":"一名護士會在學生第一次值班時負責指導和監督他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5ba526190b93c323cb1","word":"supervision","forms":["supervision"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7a3b4d1b3116364","term":"supervision","forms":["supervision","supervisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監督行為","explanation":"指有人在活動進行時持續看管、指導並確保事情按要求完成的行為，重點是“監督”這個過程本身。","examples":[{"en":"The children built the model under their teacher’s supervision.","zh":"孩子們在老師的監督下製作了模型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trainees work under close supervision.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82efb5a57a46bcbf","term":"supervision","forms":["supervision","supervisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"負責監管","explanation":"指對人員、工作或活動負有看管和把關責任的監管，強調“有人負責確保安全和正確進行”。","examples":[{"en":"The laboratory cannot be used without proper supervision.","zh":"沒有適當的監督，不得使用這個實驗室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children require adult supervision near the pool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0834c2d60725ac590225","word":"supervisor","forms":["supervisor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-83820503400caa05","term":"supervisor","forms":["supervisor","supervisors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"監督工作的人","explanation":"指被正式安排來檢視某個人或團隊工作進展、協調其活動並對工作負責的人。核心畫面是“站在一旁持續看著工作是否按要求進行”。","examples":[{"en":"Please speak to your supervisor if you have any questions about the schedule.","zh":"如果你對日程安排有疑問，請去問你的主管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The supervisor checked the team's work before the report was submitted.","zh":"報告提交前，主管檢查了團隊的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervisor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4faf7af148bdfd16","term":"supervisor","forms":["supervisor","supervisors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檢查是否合規的人","explanation":"指專門監視某人是否遵守規定、要求或操作標準的人。它仍然是“持續看著並確保事情符合要求”，只是重點從工作管理轉向規則檢查。","examples":[{"en":"A safety supervisor inspected the site to make sure everyone followed the rules.","zh":"安全監督員檢查了現場，以確保每個人都遵守規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The safety supervisor checked every fire exit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supervisor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-64199f675b8b8f25c442","word":"supper","forms":["supper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c905cdf3b8385da6","term":"supper","forms":["supper","suppers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"晚餐","explanation":"指晚上吃的一頓飯，也就是把一天主要的晚間飯食放在“晚上”這個時間段來理解；這是最值得先掌握的基本義。","examples":[{"en":"We usually have supper at seven.","zh":"我們通常七點吃晚餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had soup and bread for supper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03dd65bf2241cb43fca6","word":"supplement","forms":["supplement"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35ac14ce87eee58b","term":"supplement","forms":["supplement","supplements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"補充物；補足之物","explanation":"指加到原有事物上的東西，用來彌補缺少的部分或讓整體更加完整。它可以是物品、資料，也可以是某種額外幫助。","examples":[{"en":"This guide is a useful supplement to the main textbook.","zh":"這本指南是主教材的有用補充。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She takes extra classes as a supplement to her regular training.","zh":"她透過額外課程來補充日常訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supplement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd0408dc51a4f335","term":"supplement","forms":["supplement","supplements"],"pos":"noun","zh":"補充檔案；增刊","explanation":"指附在檔案、書籍或出版物後面的補充部分，用來增加新資訊、改正錯誤或更新原來的內容。它仍然依附於原文，不是完全獨立的新作品。","examples":[{"en":"The publisher released a supplement to the handbook with the latest rules.","zh":"出版社為這本手冊發行了補充版，收錄最新規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The newspaper included a supplement on local history.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supplement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5532257e69c868e0","term":"supplement","forms":["supplement","supplements","supplementing","supplemented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"補充；補足","explanation":"指給已有的東西增加所需內容或資源，使它更完整或彌補不足。這個動作可以針對資訊、食物、收入或訓練等。","examples":[{"en":"She supplements her income by teaching online in the evenings.","zh":"她晚上透過線上授課來增加收入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report supplements the survey results with interviews.","zh":"這份報告用訪談結果補充了調查資料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supplement","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f30dfe1cfb6de6d1c962","word":"supply","forms":["supply"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e14ed99d8da639dc","term":"supply","forms":["supply","supplies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"供應；供給","explanation":"指把所需東西補給到某處或某人那裡這一行為，重點是“補上並提供”的過程，而不是某一批具體物品。","examples":[{"en":"The town is working to improve the supply of clean water.","zh":"這個城鎮正在努力改善清潔水的供應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm interrupted the village's water supply.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d02217b03eecc284","term":"supply","forms":["supply","supplies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"供應量；供應物","explanation":"指已經提供或可以使用的一定數量，像裝在容器裡的存量；既可以是水、食物，也可以是電力等。","examples":[{"en":"We keep a small supply of bottled water at home.","zh":"我們在家裡存著少量瓶裝水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The battery has enough power to supply a steady supply of light.","zh":"這塊電池有足夠電力持續提供穩定的光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6840cff639689de4","term":"supply","forms":["supply","supplies","supplying","supplied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提供；供應","explanation":"把某物提供給需要的人、機構或地方，使它可以使用；這是“填補空缺”這一核心形象最直接的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"The farm supplies fresh vegetables to several local restaurants.","zh":"這家農場向幾家當地餐館供應新鮮蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company supplies schools with computer equipment.","zh":"這家公司為學校提供計算機裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supply","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a18603086e5bdf9df88c","word":"support","forms":["support"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1d99aeb8afb79b9","term":"support","forms":["support","supports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支撐物","explanation":"支撐某物、使它不倒或不塌的東西，例如承重梁、支架或柱子。","examples":[{"en":"Don't move that beam; it's a support for the platform.","zh":"別移動那根梁，它是平臺的支撐物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roof rests on four wooden supports.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/support","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-919c38b1253b7cda","term":"support","forms":["support","supports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"支援；援助","explanation":"給人、團體、事業或活動實際或精神上的幫助，使其能夠繼續發展或取得成功。","examples":[{"en":"The project could not continue without public support.","zh":"沒有公眾的支援，這個專案無法繼續。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project depends on continued community support.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/support","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-08e75d6d15b92dbf","term":"support","forms":["support","supports","supporting","supported","supportest","supportedst","supporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支撐","explanation":"從下面托住物體，防止它倒下、下落或塌陷。","examples":[{"en":"These pillars support the roof.","zh":"這些柱子支撐著屋頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two wooden beams support the sagging roof.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/support","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67966693d3ed693f","term":"support","forms":["support","supports","supporting","supported","supportest","supportedst","supporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支援；擁護","explanation":"在思想上贊成某人、政黨、事業或觀點，也可以透過行動來幫助它。","examples":[{"en":"Many residents support the plan to build a new library.","zh":"許多居民支援修建新圖書館的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local residents supported the campaign for cleaner water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/support","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b7257ae5c2563fe3","term":"support","forms":["support","supports","supporting","supported","supportest","supportedst","supporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……提供證據","explanation":"提供事實、資料或理由，使某個說法、理論或指控更可信。這裡仍是“托住”的比喻：證據托住了結論。","examples":[{"en":"The data support the researchers' conclusion.","zh":"這些資料支援研究人員的結論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The latest measurements support her original hypothesis.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/support","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-190ab894c1cba9552ecc","word":"suppose","forms":["suppose"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-491a1bf3e4af08bd","term":"suppose","forms":["suppose","supposes","supposing","supposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為；料想","explanation":"說話人沒有絕對把握，但根據已有情況把某事當作大概真實來判斷；中文常可譯為“我想、我猜、我認為”。","examples":[{"en":"I suppose the train will be late again.","zh":"我想這趟火車又要晚點了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was tired, I suppose, after the long meeting.","zh":"我想，開了那麼久的會以後，她累了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70760ec632914731","term":"suppose","forms":["suppose","supposes","supposing","supposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"假設；設定條件","explanation":"在推理、討論或解題時，先把一個尚未證實的情況當作前提，再觀察會推出什麼結果。","examples":[{"en":"Suppose the price rises by ten percent—how will that affect sales?","zh":"假設價格上漲百分之十，這會怎樣影響銷量？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Suppose we take the earlier bus; we could arrive before noon.","zh":"假設我們乘早一班公交車，就可能在中午前到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-286df35c0fa15c37","term":"suppose","forms":["suppose","supposes","supposing","supposed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"設想；想象成","explanation":"把某個事物或場景放進腦海中，當作一種可能的畫面或情況來想；重點在想象，而不一定是在進行嚴密推理。","examples":[{"en":"Suppose you wake up one morning and find that you can fly.","zh":"設想一下，你某天早晨醒來，發現自己會飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I supposed the dark shape was a tree.","zh":"我把那個黑影看成了一棵樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-371756e504cd1328d1ce","word":"supposedly","forms":["supposedly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1930a7e5712ed46a","term":"supposedly","forms":["supposedly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"據說；據稱","explanation":"表示某件事是根據別人所說、普遍看法或現有說法而成立的，但說話者不一定親自確認其真實性。它像是把一個傳來的說法放在句子裡，而不是把它當成絕對事實。","examples":[{"en":"The new restaurant is supposedly the best in town.","zh":"據說這家新餐館是城裡最好的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He supposedly left the office early, but no one saw him go.","zh":"據說他很早就離開辦公室了，但沒人看見他走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supposedly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dd2638abd6cd7127f0a8","word":"suppress","forms":["suppress"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a561368cf16b9a36","term":"suppress","forms":["suppress","suppresses","suppressing","suppressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"壓制；鎮壓；禁止","explanation":"指用強力或權力把反抗、活動等壓下去，使其不能繼續或不能公開進行。它是“向下壓住”的最典型用法，常見於政府、軍隊或有控制力的一方對異議和動亂的處理。","examples":[{"en":"The authorities suppressed the protest within hours.","zh":"當局在幾小時內就鎮壓了這場抗議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new law was designed to suppress political dissent.","zh":"這項新法律旨在壓制政治異議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5bb32305499ac2e9","term":"suppress","forms":["suppress","suppresses","suppressing","suppressed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忍住；抑制","explanation":"指把笑聲、表情、情緒或身體反應壓回去，不讓它自然表現出來。這裡壓住的不是外部群體，而是自己即將出現的反應。","examples":[{"en":"She tried to suppress a laugh during the meeting.","zh":"她開會時努力忍住笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He suppressed his anger and answered calmly.","zh":"他壓住怒火，平靜地作了回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f8f474a55befde8bbea5","word":"supreme","forms":["supreme"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2cb9e5bcc21b864b","term":"supreme","forms":["supreme","supremer","more supreme","supremest","most supreme"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最高權威的","explanation":"指擁有凌駕於其他人或機構之上的權力和地位。例如，最高法院之所以可以這樣稱呼，是因為它被視為該司法體系中的最高權威。","examples":[{"en":"The supreme court overturned the earlier decision.","zh":"最高法院推翻了先前的判決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The emperor claimed supreme authority over every provincial governor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supreme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d724745f5907f435","term":"supreme","forms":["supreme","supremer","more supreme","supremest","most supreme"],"pos":"adj","zh":"至高無上的；極度的","explanation":"表示某種品質、成就或感受達到最高、最強的程度，也就是“無可超越”或“極其強烈”。它可以形容優秀，也可以形容負面感受等極端狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She showed supreme confidence during the final.","zh":"她在決賽中表現出了極大的自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He reacted with supreme disgust to the spoiled food.","zh":"他對變質的食物表現出極度的厭惡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/supreme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0cafcf0e2d6a236aca7","word":"sure","forms":["sure"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f42827c6feda3230","term":"sure","forms":["sure","surer","surest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可靠的；穩妥的","explanation":"指某件事很可靠，結果有把握，不容易失效或出問題。重點不是人的主觀相信，而是事情本身值得依靠。","examples":[{"en":"This is a sure way to save time.","zh":"這是節省時間的穩妥辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her quick judgment is a sure guide in difficult situations.","zh":"遇到困難時，她的快速判斷是可靠的指引。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6dd484e25427cbe7","term":"sure","forms":["sure","surer","surest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"確信的；確定的","explanation":"指人對某個事實或判斷沒有疑問，心裡很有把握。這裡強調的是主觀上的確信，而不是事情本身必然可靠。","examples":[{"en":"I am sure that we have met before.","zh":"我確定我們以前見過面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you sure about this decision?","zh":"你確定要做這個決定嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0199311728be829918c1","word":"surf","forms":["surf"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-befe0fbcab40de42","term":"surf","forms":["surf","surfs","surfing","surfed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"乘浪板衝浪","explanation":"surf作動詞時最基本的動作義是站在衝浪板上順著海浪滑行，也可泛指參加衝浪運動。這正是從“海浪衝向海岸”這一核心畫面發展出的動作。","examples":[{"en":"He learned to surf when he was fifteen.","zh":"他十五歲時學會了衝浪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Experienced surfers can surf waves that look terrifying.","zh":"有經驗的衝浪者能駕馭看起來很嚇人的海浪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b4c50793e3e390d0","term":"surf","forms":["surf","surfs","surfing","surfed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上網瀏覽","explanation":"從順著海浪不斷移動的畫面出發，surf引申為在網際網路、電視節目等內容之間隨意切換和瀏覽，通常不強調完成明確的查詢任務。","examples":[{"en":"I spent an hour surfing the web after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我花了一個小時上網瀏覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He surfed through the channels without watching any program for long.","zh":"他不停地換臺，沒有長時間看任何一個節目。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-763cdc62a869262b6ff4","word":"surface","forms":["surface"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d2cee84c3d1af80","term":"surface","forms":["surface","surfaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表面；表層","explanation":"指平面物體的上面，或液體與空氣接觸的那一層。它是“最外面、最先接觸到的那一層”這一核心概念的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"A thin layer of dust covered the surface of the table.","zh":"桌面上覆蓋著一層薄薄的灰塵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaves floated on the surface of the pond.","zh":"樹葉漂浮在池塘水面上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surface","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-001346eec395f765","term":"surface","forms":["surface","surfaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外殼；外層","explanation":"指有形物體包在最外面的那一層，強調物體的外部邊界，而不只是一個平面。","examples":[{"en":"The metal surface became hot in the afternoon sun.","zh":"金屬外殼在午後的陽光下變熱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The probe measured temperatures at the planet's surface.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surface","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f9e4961fc1b07281","term":"surface","forms":["surface","surfaces","surfacing","surfaced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"浮出水面","explanation":"指人或物從水下上升到水面，進入能被看見的位置；它正好體現了“來到最外層”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The diver surfaced after two minutes underwater.","zh":"潛水員在水下兩分鐘後浮出了水面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The whale surfaced a few meters from our boat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surface","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b815a05f4e0c1716","term":"surface","forms":["surface","surfaces","surfacing","surfaced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"浮現；顯現","explanation":"指事實、問題、資訊或內容從隱藏狀態進入人們能看見、聽見或注意到的狀態。它把“來到表面”轉成了“變得明顯、被發現”。","examples":[{"en":"New details surfaced during the investigation.","zh":"調查過程中浮現出了新的細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mistake surfaced when we checked the final report.","zh":"我們檢查最終報告時發現了這個錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surface","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41ef29df4a53ab2d8b1d","word":"surge","forms":["surge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7c610ebd6e4ac91","term":"surge","forms":["surge","surges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驟增；突然湧動","explanation":"指數量、力量、人群或情緒在短時間內突然大幅上升，彷彿一股浪猛地湧了過來。","examples":[{"en":"The store saw a surge in online orders after the announcement.","zh":"公告發布後，這家商店的網上訂單突然激增。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A surge of anger swept through the crowd.","zh":"一陣憤怒席捲了人群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00255a600b75c5d6","term":"surge","forms":["surge","surges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電湧；電壓或電流驟升","explanation":"指電壓或電流在短時間內突然衝高，可能損壞裝置或造成停電；這裡的“湧”就是電力突然湧上來。","examples":[{"en":"A power surge damaged the office computers.","zh":"一次電湧損壞了辦公室裡的電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A surge protector saved our equipment during the electrical storm.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53354e79944c60bf","term":"surge","forms":["surge","surges","surging","surged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"突然猛增；湧起","explanation":"指數量、價格、需求或情緒突然大幅上升，像一股浪一下子湧了起來。","examples":[{"en":"Demand for cold drinks surged during the heatwave.","zh":"熱浪期間，冷飲需求猛增。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stock surged to a record high in the morning.","zh":"這隻股票早上飆升至歷史新高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48271388865ea6816866","word":"surgeon","forms":["surgeon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-648d35190a19ed0f","term":"surgeon","forms":["surgeon","surgeons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外科醫生","explanation":"指專門進行手術的醫生，可以為人或動物做手術；記住“用手和器械處理身體”的核心畫面即可。","examples":[{"en":"The surgeon operated on my knee yesterday.","zh":"外科醫生昨天給我的膝蓋做了手術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her brother wants to become a surgeon.","zh":"她哥哥想成為一名外科醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surgeon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36a6f56da2814250","term":"surgeon","forms":["surgeon","surgeons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刺尾魚","explanation":"指刺尾魚科的一類海魚；可以把它記成因尾部帶有鋒利突起而與“手術刀”畫面相連的魚名。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a blue surgeon near the coral reef.","zh":"我們在珊瑚礁附近看到了一條藍色的刺尾魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The surgeon fish defended its hiding place among the rocks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surgeon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fc00eb484b582cfb374e","word":"surgery","forms":["surgery"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0c14381c867a817","term":"surgery","forms":["surgery","surgeries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外科手術","explanation":"指透過較大的切口，對身體某一部分進行切除、修復或替換的醫療操作；這是 surgery 最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She will need surgery to repair the damaged valve.","zh":"她需要做手術來修復受損的瓣膜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is recovering well after surgery.","zh":"他手術後恢復得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surgery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b8810697da91579","term":"surgery","forms":["surgery","surgeries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"外科專業","explanation":"指專門進行外科手術的醫學領域，也就是醫院或醫學教育中的“外科”。","examples":[{"en":"After medical school, he chose surgery as his specialty.","zh":"醫學院畢業後，他選擇了外科作為自己的專業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He decided to specialize in surgery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surgery","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd8e8b81f9b51c859b11","word":"surgical","forms":["surgical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ab9bfa5d648fb03c","term":"surgical","forms":["surgical","more surgical","most surgical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"手術的；與手術有關的","explanation":"指屬於手術、用於手術，或由手術造成的事物；這是它最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The patient needs surgical treatment for the damaged tendon.","zh":"這名患者需要透過手術治療受損的肌腱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The surgical wound healed without infection.","zh":"手術傷口沒有感染，已經癒合。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surgical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de22e83b0838a63b","term":"surgical","forms":["surgical","more surgical","most surgical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精準的；極其準確的","explanation":"比喻像手術刀下刀一樣準確、利落，強調行動或處理能夠準確擊中目標，幾乎沒有多餘動作。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team made a surgical cut through the wreckage to reach the driver.","zh":"救援隊精準地切開殘骸，以接觸到司機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The striker placed the ball with surgical precision.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surgical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-655c32fb8455e927ccbd","word":"surname","forms":["surname"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d37af969fcbd31c","term":"surname","forms":["surname","surnames"],"pos":"noun","zh":"姓；姓氏","explanation":"指通常由家族成員共同使用、用來標示家族歸屬的名字部分，與個人的名相區別。可以把它理解為加在個人名字上的家族標籤。","examples":[{"en":"My first name is Anna, and my surname is Patel.","zh":"我的名是安娜，姓是帕特爾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone in the family has the same surname.","zh":"這個家族裡的每個人都姓同一個姓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surname","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3f729ce003728ec00f4","word":"surpass","forms":["surpass"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c946532214b258cc","term":"surpass","forms":["surpass","surpasses","surpassing","surpassed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"超過；勝過","explanation":"表示跨過某個水平或界線，在成績、能力、數量或成就上超過某人、某物或原先的期待。重點是“達到之後還更進一步”，因此既可以超過別人，也可以超過一個標準。","examples":[{"en":"Her final score surpassed everyone’s expectations.","zh":"她的最終成績超出了所有人的預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young athlete surpassed his previous record.","zh":"這名年輕運動員超過了自己原來的紀錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surpass","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bd305c929ba350e05b4","word":"surplus","forms":["surplus"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3899ad5100f54a1","term":"surplus","forms":["surplus"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多餘的；過剩的","explanation":"指某種東西或某批人超過實際需要或可合理使用的數量，因此成為多出來的部分。它和名詞用法中的“剩餘、盈餘”共享同一個核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The factory had to reduce its surplus staff.","zh":"這家工廠不得不裁減多餘的員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farm sold its surplus grain.","zh":"這家農場賣掉了多餘的糧食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surplus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e83aa82638c65823","term":"surplus","forms":["surplus","surpluses","surplusses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"剩餘；過剩；盈餘","explanation":"指先滿足使用或需要後留下的東西，或超過某個限額的部分，可以是實物，也可以是數量或金錢上的盈餘。它就是“分完必需部分後還剩下的一堆”。","examples":[{"en":"A surplus of tomatoes pushed prices down.","zh":"西紅柿供過於求，導致價格下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We donated the surplus food to a shelter.","zh":"我們把多餘的食物捐給了收容所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surplus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0832c0adf05418144b7b","word":"surprise","forms":["surprise"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8fbe8c75890e690c","term":"surprise","forms":["surprise","surprises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意外之事","explanation":"指沒有預料到、突然發生的事情。它可以是好事，也可以是壞事；關鍵不在於結果好壞，而在於事情沒有按預期出現。","examples":[{"en":"Finding a note from my old friend was a wonderful surprise.","zh":"發現老朋友留的一張字條真是個美好的意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden price increase came as a surprise to everyone.","zh":"價格突然上漲讓所有人都感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surprise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-135ab6bd117e43fb","term":"surprise","forms":["surprise","surprises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚訝的感覺","explanation":"指人發現事情出乎預料時產生的驚訝、詫異感。這裡重點不是外在事件，而是“被意外撞到”的心理反應。","examples":[{"en":"To my surprise, the quiet student knew the answer.","zh":"令我驚訝的是，那個安靜的學生知道答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stared at the empty box in surprise.","zh":"她驚訝地盯著空盒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surprise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-104489b323ccd99f","term":"surprise","forms":["surprise","surprises","surprising","surprised"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人感到意外","explanation":"指某件事使人沒有料到，從而感到驚訝、驚喜或驚嚇。它是“讓意外撞到某人”的基本動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"It surprised me that nobody complained.","zh":"讓我意外的是，竟然沒有人抱怨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gift surprised her, but it did not frighten her.","zh":"這份禮物讓她感到意外，但沒有嚇到她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surprise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f471c347284f2de40bd","word":"surprised","forms":["surprised"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be1a42d9e81c8fc1","term":"surprised","forms":["surprised","more surprised","most surprised"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到驚訝的","explanation":"指某人遇到沒有預料到的事情，因此感到驚訝、吃驚，或臉上表現出這種情緒。核心畫面是“意外突然出現在眼前，人被它撞得一愣”。","examples":[{"en":"I was surprised to find the door unlocked.","zh":"我驚訝地發現門沒有鎖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looked surprised when she saw the gift.","zh":"她看到禮物時看起來很驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surprised","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e75eb6e2d3fb49fbec43","word":"surrender","forms":["surrender"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c9d5b1012f86d32","term":"surrender","forms":["surrender","surrenders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投降；屈服","explanation":"指放棄抵抗，把自己置於他人的控制或支配之下；也可以泛指屈服、放棄抵抗的行為。","examples":[{"en":"The army's surrender ended the long battle.","zh":"軍隊的投降結束了這場持久的戰鬥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The general accepted the enemy's unconditional surrender.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surrender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a56c87a752663e2","term":"surrender","forms":["surrender","surrenders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交出；放棄佔有物","explanation":"指應要求把某件物品、房屋或其他佔有物交還給別人，因此重點是失去對該物的控制或佔有。","examples":[{"en":"The suspect's surrender of the weapon calmed the situation.","zh":"嫌疑人交出武器後，局勢平靜了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement required the surrender of all weapons.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surrender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0fb667e21ac8f823","term":"surrender","forms":["surrender","surrenders","surrendering","surrendered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交給他人控制","explanation":"指把某人或某物交到另一個人的權力、控制或佔有之下，是“交出去”這條核心意思最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She surrendered control of the company to her brother.","zh":"她把公司的控制權交給了哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He surrendered his passport to the authorities.","zh":"他把護照交給了當局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surrender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1797183c12f033e","term":"surrender","forms":["surrender","surrenders","surrendering","surrendered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向敵人交出城鎮或堡壘","explanation":"指軍隊、政府或守軍不再抵抗，把城鎮、堡壘等防守地點交給敵方控制；這是“交出控制權”在戰爭中的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"The defenders surrendered the fortress after three days.","zh":"守軍在三天後交出了堡壘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The general refused to surrender the city despite overwhelming losses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surrender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7e768208724804a","term":"surrender","forms":["surrender","surrenders","surrendering","surrendered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投降；自首","explanation":"不及物時指一個人停止抵抗、向對方投降，尤其是作為俘虜或向執法人員自首；這裡是把自己交出去。","examples":[{"en":"The police surrounded the building, and the suspect surrendered.","zh":"警察包圍了大樓，嫌疑人投降了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put down the weapon and surrender!","zh":"放下武器，投降吧！","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surrender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-151276b3a1066ac1","term":"surrender","forms":["surrender","surrenders","surrendering","surrendered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放棄權利或優勢","explanation":"指把自己擁有的權利、特權、優勢或利益交出去，不再堅持擁有它；它仍然保留“放棄控制或佔有”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"She refused to surrender her right to speak.","zh":"她拒絕放棄自己的發言權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team surrendered its early advantage.","zh":"這支隊伍丟掉了開局時的優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surrender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee48ee67db5d730efb11","word":"surround","forms":["surround"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-02747257f0e5eb0a","term":"surround","forms":["surround","surrounds","surrounding","surrounded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"圍繞；環繞","explanation":"表示某物從各個方向延伸到另一物周圍，形成一圈，但不一定帶有阻止對方行動的意思。樹木圍著房屋、建築被街道包圍，都可以用這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"Tall trees surround the old house.","zh":"高大的樹木環繞著那座老房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village is surrounded by green hills.","zh":"這個村莊四周都是青山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surround","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3319492f430937ef2414","word":"surroundings","forms":["surroundings"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4343004eee5a9f37","term":"surroundings","forms":["surroundings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"周圍環境；身邊景物和氛圍","explanation":"指圍繞著某人或某物的地方、物件、景色以及由此形成的整體氛圍。它強調“身處其中的那一圈環境”，不只是某一個相鄰物體。","examples":[{"en":"The quiet surroundings helped me concentrate.","zh":"安靜的周圍環境幫助我集中注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She quickly adapted to her new surroundings.","zh":"她很快適應了新環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surroundings","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0d24788cd8b5346f187","word":"surveillance","forms":["surveillance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f1ff5abc911a6de","term":"surveillance","forms":["surveillance","surveillances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對可疑物件的監視","explanation":"指持續盯住某個人或一群人，通常因為他們受到懷疑，觀察者想了解他們的行動或聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The suspect was kept under surveillance for several weeks.","zh":"這名嫌疑人被監視了好幾個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The detectives began surveillance of the gang's meeting place.","zh":"偵探開始監視這個團伙的聚會地點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surveillance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-566070a53dc1fbe4","term":"surveillance","forms":["surveillance","surveillances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"透過各種手段進行系統監視","explanation":"指利用攝像、錄音、電子裝置、照片或直接觀察等方式，有系統地監視地點和人員；範圍可以很廣，也可以由政府或機構實施。","examples":[{"en":"The city installed more cameras as part of its surveillance program.","zh":"這座城市安裝了更多攝像頭，作為其監視計劃的一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people are worried about government surveillance of private communications.","zh":"許多人擔心政府監視私人通訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/surveillance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-811f2a14b9850c9d9c75","word":"survey","forms":["survey"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d838109fd31fa56","term":"survey","forms":["survey","surveys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"檢查；調查","explanation":"指標對一組物品、建築或設施進行有目的的檢查，以瞭解它們的狀況、數量或質量；重點是把物件逐項看清。","examples":[{"en":"The engineer completed a survey of the old bridge.","zh":"工程師完成了對那座舊橋的檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The buyer ordered a survey of the house before making an offer.","zh":"買家在報價前要求對這棟房子進行檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2426721c6937e250","term":"survey","forms":["survey","surveys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"民意調查","explanation":"指透過向一群人提問來了解他們的意見、經歷或態度，結果通常用於分析或作決定。","examples":[{"en":"The council conducted a survey of local residents.","zh":"市政委員會對當地居民進行了一項調查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A recent survey found that many parents support the change.","zh":"最近的一項調查發現，許多家長支援這項改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be274fad5adf7ae3","term":"survey","forms":["survey","surveys","surveying","surveyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"檢視全貌；俯瞰","explanation":"指從較高處或有利位置仔細檢視一個地方的整體情況，重點是把周圍景象看遍。","examples":[{"en":"From the tower, we surveyed the valley below.","zh":"我們從塔上俯瞰下面的山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"From the balcony, she surveyed the busy harbor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c673ae26856cd2b4","term":"survey","forms":["survey","surveys","surveying","surveyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"檢查並評估","explanation":"指檢查建築、裝置或其他物件，以判斷其狀況、價值或風險；這裡的“看”服務於評估和作決定。","examples":[{"en":"A specialist will survey the roof for damage.","zh":"一名專家將檢查屋頂是否有損壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An engineer surveyed the building for structural damage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e736e142dad7c9fa","term":"survey","forms":["survey","surveys","surveying","surveyed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調查意見","explanation":"指透過向人們提問來了解他們的意見、經歷或態度，也就是開展一項民意調查。","examples":[{"en":"Researchers surveyed commuters about their daily travel.","zh":"研究人員調查了通勤者的日常出行情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers surveyed residents about the proposed changes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4032ee4038775060258f","word":"survival","forms":["survival"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b41ff1f95b38562","term":"survival","forms":["survival","survivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倖存；繼續存在","explanation":"指人在危險、困難或惡劣環境中活下來，也可指某種事物沒有消失、仍然存在。重點是“從可能消失或死亡的邊緣繼續留下來”。","examples":[{"en":"His survival in the wilderness depended on clean water and a warm shelter.","zh":"他能在荒野中活下來，靠的是乾淨的水和溫暖的庇護所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survival of the small bookstore surprised everyone.","zh":"那家小書店一直經營下來，讓所有人都感到意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-edf6b51ff5a1b240","term":"survival","forms":["survival","survivals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生存用的；有助於生存的","explanation":"表示與生存有關、能夠幫助人或事物撐下去的東西，常修飾另一個名詞；可以把它理解為“幫助抓住懸崖邊緣的”。","examples":[{"en":"The campers packed a survival kit with a flashlight, water, and a first-aid guide.","zh":"露營者帶上了一個生存裝備包，裡面有手電筒、水和急救指南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pack a survival kit before entering the wilderness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survival","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0fb542ca673346178bfd","word":"survive","forms":["survive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e338e797998d9a6f","term":"survive","forms":["survive","survives","surviving","survived","survivest","survivedst","surviveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"活下來；仍然活著","explanation":"指人在危險、疾病或事故之後仍然活著，重點是生命沒有終止。","examples":[{"en":"All the hikers survived.","zh":"所有徒步旅行者都活了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She survived despite her serious injuries.","zh":"儘管傷勢嚴重，她還是活了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8b5aa0c7f8743f0","term":"survive","forms":["survive","survives","surviving","survived","survivest","survivedst","surviveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繼續存在；留存下來","explanation":"主語不一定是人，也可以是建築、傳統、企業或想法，表示它經歷時間或變化後仍沒有消失。","examples":[{"en":"The old bridge survived the flood.","zh":"那座老橋經受住了洪水，保留了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only a few fragments of the original poem survive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60d090d2bfa957c3","term":"survive","forms":["survive","survives","surviving","survived","survivest","survivedst","surviveth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"熬過；在事件中活下來","explanation":"表示經歷一個可能致命或極其危險的事件後仍活著，強調“撐過了這件事”。","examples":[{"en":"He survived the plane crash.","zh":"他在那場飛機失事中活了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog survived the operation.","zh":"這隻狗熬過了手術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a01ac37408614bcf580","word":"survivor","forms":["survivor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b49faaa8b9e6a37","term":"survivor","forms":["survivor","survivors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倖存者","explanation":"指經歷事故、戰爭、疾病或其他創傷性事件後仍然活著的人，重點是從嚴重危險或打擊中留下來。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team found three survivors after the earthquake.","zh":"救援隊在地震後找到了三名倖存者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a survivor of a serious car accident.","zh":"她是一起嚴重車禍的倖存者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survivor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7aa972027eb0c55","term":"survivor","forms":["survivor","survivors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"堅強熬過困難的人","explanation":"用作比喻時，指一個人即使反覆遭遇困難、壓力或挫折，仍能堅持生活下去；這裡不一定有實際的災難。","examples":[{"en":"After losing her job and starting over, she calls herself a survivor.","zh":"失業並重新開始後，她稱自己是一個能熬過困難的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She's a survivor who rebuilt her life after bankruptcy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/survivor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-982776aa0b872d5a1b4d","word":"suspect","forms":["suspect"],"officialPos":"v./n./adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-57692f1c97723fc1","term":"suspect","forms":["suspect","more suspect","most suspect"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可疑的；不可靠的","explanation":"某人或某事看起來有問題，不能完全相信，因此受到懷疑。這個意思是“被懷疑的物件”，不是“正在懷疑別人的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The report looked suspect from the start.","zh":"這份報告從一開始就顯得可疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several details in the contract are suspect.","zh":"合同中的幾處細節都值得懷疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d8c706944ee9f42f","term":"suspect","forms":["suspect","suspects","suspecting","suspected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"推測；猜想","explanation":"沒有充分證據，卻認為某事可能是真的或某處可能存在某物；重點是未經證實的推測，不一定帶有強烈的不信任。","examples":[{"en":"Doctors suspect that the infection began in the kitchen.","zh":"醫生推測這起感染始於廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We suspect a problem with the heating system.","zh":"我們猜測供暖系統出了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2dee580b9c49d6f6","term":"suspect","forms":["suspect","suspects","suspecting","suspected"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懷疑；不信任","explanation":"覺得某人的話、某件事或某種解釋不可靠，因而不完全相信；懷疑的物件可以是人，也可以是說法、證據等。","examples":[{"en":"I suspect the explanation is incomplete.","zh":"我懷疑這個解釋並不完整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She began to suspect his promises after he missed several deadlines.","zh":"他幾次錯過期限後，她開始不再相信他的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspect","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f516e6c2649309364748","word":"suspend","forms":["suspend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d189dcebe535f55","term":"suspend","forms":["suspend","suspends","suspending","suspended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暫時暫停","explanation":"把正在進行的活動暫時“掛起”，之後通常還有可能繼續。例如會議、比賽、服務或談話都可以被 suspend。","examples":[{"en":"The meeting was suspended for lunch.","zh":"會議因午餐暫時暫停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The service was suspended during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間這項服務暫停了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-23301c0b0cbc20f7","term":"suspend","forms":["suspend","suspends","suspending","suspended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"暫緩決定","explanation":"把判斷或決定掛在那裡，暫時不作結論，等更多資訊或更合適的時機再決定。","examples":[{"en":"We should suspend judgment until we have all the facts.","zh":"在掌握全部事實前，我們應該暫不下判斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Suspend judgment until you've heard both witnesses.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a3ff9d244e5b19f","term":"suspend","forms":["suspend","suspends","suspending","suspended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"懸掛","explanation":"把物體掛在某個支撐物上，使它自由垂下或懸在空中。這是“掛起”這個核心畫面的字面意思。","examples":[{"en":"A small lamp was suspended from the ceiling.","zh":"一盞小燈懸掛在天花板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ball was suspended by a thin thread.","zh":"球由一根細線懸吊著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b71bcf017b2337de83b","word":"suspense","forms":["suspense"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-07b9e8e68b0cf80e","term":"suspense","forms":["suspense","suspenses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事懸念","explanation":"指讀者或觀眾在等待故事結局時產生的興奮期待，因為關鍵結果被暫時懸著，所以會想繼續讀下去或看下去。","examples":[{"en":"The film builds suspense until the final scene.","zh":"這部電影一直製造懸念，直到最後一幕才揭曉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The suspense kept me reading late into the night.","zh":"懸念讓我一直讀到深夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f06e8488f1a61914d012","word":"suspension","forms":["suspension"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74490bd922a68fd4","term":"suspension","forms":["suspension","suspensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懸掛；懸置狀態","explanation":"指某物被吊起、掛住，或處於暫時懸置、沒有落下的狀態，是“懸著”這一核心概念最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The suspension of the lamp from the ceiling keeps the table clear.","zh":"把燈懸掛在天花板上可以空出桌面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crystals remained in suspension for several minutes.","zh":"晶體顆粒在懸浮狀態中保持了幾分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26ee41133d1440af","term":"suspension","forms":["suspension","suspensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暫時中止；暫停","explanation":"指一項活動、服務、計劃或程式被暫時掛起，通常暗示以後可能恢復，而不是永久取消。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused the suspension of all ferry services.","zh":"暴風雨導致所有渡輪服務暫時停運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company announced a temporary suspension of production.","zh":"公司宣佈暫時停止生產。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5779368d6e888bc830fd","word":"suspicion","forms":["suspicion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0212799f52365482","term":"suspicion","forms":["suspicion","suspicions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懷疑有問題","explanation":"指因為覺得某人或某事可能不對、可能有不當行為而產生的懷疑。這是suspicion最核心的意思，重點是“開始不放心”，而不是事實已經查明。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden change in his story aroused my suspicion.","zh":"他突然改變說法，使我產生了懷疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She left the room without suspicion that anyone was watching her.","zh":"她離開房間時，完全沒有懷疑有人在監視她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspicion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d7881d95d3742b0","term":"suspicion","forms":["suspicion","suspicions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疑慮；不確定","explanation":"指心裡無法確定、因此對人或事抱有保留的疑慮。它可以沒有明確指向某項 wrongdoing，而只是覺得情況不夠可信或不夠明朗。","examples":[{"en":"The plan was accepted, but not without suspicion.","zh":"這個計劃被接受了，但人們並非沒有疑慮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He looked at the offer with suspicion.","zh":"他帶著疑慮看待這份提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspicion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80d8b1e97421d004d7e7","word":"suspicious","forms":["suspicious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-52f8932f5d2a5d3e","term":"suspicious","forms":["suspicious","more suspicious","most suspicious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可疑的；引起懷疑的","explanation":"指某件事、某種行為或某個情況讓人覺得不正常，因此產生懷疑。重點不在於已經證明它有問題，而在於它發出了“似乎不對勁”的訊號。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden change in his story sounded suspicious.","zh":"他突然改變說法，聽起來很可疑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guard noticed a suspicious package near the door.","zh":"警衛注意到門邊有一個可疑的包裹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspicious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c673cb3c8e397cf","term":"suspicious","forms":["suspicious","more suspicious","most suspicious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多疑的；不信任別人的","explanation":"指一個人習慣懷疑別人，不容易相信別人的話或動機。這裡不是說這個人本身一定可疑，而是說他心裡常亮著懷疑的紅燈。","examples":[{"en":"She is suspicious of anyone who asks too many personal questions.","zh":"她不信任任何問太多私人問題的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was suspicious of anyone offering easy money.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suspicious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07f5b83f6cec99c2cf51","word":"sustain","forms":["sustain"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0b5b2aaf2a662eb","term":"sustain","forms":["sustain","sustains","sustaining","sustained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"維持；使繼續存在","explanation":"表示把興趣、活動、關係或狀態維持下去，使它不至於中斷或消失；重點是持續提供支撐，而不只是“自己持續”。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher used stories to sustain the children's interest.","zh":"老師用故事維持孩子們的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project needs more funding to sustain its growth.","zh":"這個專案需要更多資金來維持增長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sustain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-429a3e334d722dfc","term":"sustain","forms":["sustain","sustains","sustaining","sustained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支撐；承託","explanation":"表示建築、地面、動物或其他承託物把重量托住，使其不掉落或不倒塌；這是“從下面托住”的最直接含義。","examples":[{"en":"The bridge was designed to sustain heavy loads.","zh":"這座橋的設計能夠承受過載。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roots help sustain the tree in strong winds.","zh":"樹根幫助支撐樹木，使它在強風中保持穩定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sustain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-711415eb4348502ead97","word":"sustainable","forms":["sustainable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2aa0308a33ec51b","term":"sustainable","forms":["sustainable","more sustainable","most sustainable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能長期維持的","explanation":"表示某件事、某種狀態或某個系統能夠繼續下去，不會很快失去支撐或無法維持。這裡的重點是“撐得住、延續得下去”，不一定專指環境問題。","examples":[{"en":"The current pace of spending is not sustainable.","zh":"目前這樣的支出速度無法長期維持。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a sustainable plan for the next five years.","zh":"我們需要一個未來五年能夠長期維持的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sustainable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c80b93524352de89","term":"sustainable","forms":["sustainable","more sustainable","most sustainable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"環保且可長期維持的","explanation":"表示生產、發展或使用資源的方式可以無限期延續，同時不會嚴重破壞環境或耗盡資源。因此它常譯為“可持續的”，尤其用於經濟、農業、能源和發展等話題。","examples":[{"en":"The city is investing in sustainable public transport.","zh":"這座城市正在投資建設可持續的公共交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sustainable farming can protect the soil for future generations.","zh":"可持續農業能夠為後代保護土壤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sustainable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7276e0a742cf9880d1cf","word":"swallow","forms":["swallow"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5f0a472048675e33","term":"swallow","forms":["swallow","swallows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"燕子","explanation":"swallow 是燕子，一種會遷徙、在空中捕食昆蟲的小鳥；這個義項與“吞下”同形但詞源不同。","examples":[{"en":"A swallow flew over the garden and caught an insect.","zh":"一隻燕子飛過花園，捉到了一隻昆蟲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A swallow built its nest beneath the eaves.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74d9ea72b4dae543","term":"swallow","forms":["swallow","swallows","swallowing","swallowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吞下","explanation":"指讓食物、飲料或藥物從嘴裡經過喉嚨進入胃裡，也就是把東西真正吞進去。","examples":[{"en":"He swallowed the pill with a glass of water.","zh":"他用一杯水把藥片吞了下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was too nervous to swallow my breakfast.","zh":"我緊張得連早餐都咽不下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swallow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d83a900c42d48e2ad9ba","word":"swamp","forms":["swamp"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40b0c6c8f3e47480","term":"swamp","forms":["swamp","swamps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沼澤；溼地","explanation":"指長期積水、土地鬆軟，常長著樹木和其他植物的溼地。由於地面像海綿一樣吸滿水，人和車輛通常不容易在其中通行或耕作。","examples":[{"en":"We saw several herons standing in the swamp.","zh":"我們看到幾隻蒼鷺站在沼澤裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road ends where the forest turns into a swamp.","zh":"森林變成沼澤的地方就是道路的盡頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4b1c51668d219355","term":"swamp","forms":["swamp","swamps","swamping","swamped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"淹沒；灌滿水","explanation":"指水進入船、車輛或其他容器，使其嚴重進水，甚至沉沒。這裡的核心畫面是沼澤般的水不斷湧來，把東西壓在水下。","examples":[{"en":"The fishing boat was swamped by a sudden wave.","zh":"那艘漁船被突然打來的海浪淹得進了大量水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy rain swamped the basement overnight.","zh":"一夜的大雨把地下室淹了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-087f944971232027","term":"swamp","forms":["swamp","swamps","swamping","swamped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使忙不過來；壓垮","explanation":"比喻任務、請求或問題像洪水一樣大量湧來，超過一個人或組織能夠處理的能力，使其應接不暇。","examples":[{"en":"I can't talk now—I’m swamped with emails.","zh":"我現在沒法聊天，郵件多得讓我應接不暇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small clinic was swamped with patients after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，這家小診所被大量患者忙得不可開交。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swamp","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6856daebb0115b3b8c74","word":"swan","forms":["swan"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d6270c338abdad8","term":"swan","forms":["swan","swans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天鵝","explanation":"swan是天鵝，一種脖子長、體形大的水鳥，許多種類的羽毛主要是白色。","examples":[{"en":"A pair of swans was floating on the lake.","zh":"一對天鵝正在湖面上漂浮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the swans from the bridge.","zh":"我們在橋上看天鵝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da47c2f450a4f9d538d8","word":"swap","forms":["swap"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46cec35b95bcdbdd","term":"swap","forms":["swap","swaps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交換；互換","explanation":"指雙方把兩個相當或相近的東西互相換過來，也可以指這次交換本身。它和動詞swap的核心“交換”相對應。","examples":[{"en":"We made a straight swap: my old camera for her tablet.","zh":"我們直接交換了：我用舊相機換了她的平板電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two teams agreed to a player swap.","zh":"兩支球隊同意交換球員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8fccb42038e59ca5","term":"swap","forms":["swap","swaps","swapping","swapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交換；互換","explanation":"指把某物交給別人，換回另一件物品、職位或安排；也可以表示兩個人彼此互換位置或任務。這是swap在現代英語中的核心用法。","examples":[{"en":"Can we swap seats so I can sit by the window?","zh":"我們能交換座位嗎？這樣我就能坐在窗邊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Mia swapped her Friday shift for my Monday shift.","zh":"米婭用她週五的班換了我週一的班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44eb92b46360c22af339","word":"swarm","forms":["swarm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-517f2f3528a431fe","term":"swarm","forms":["swarm","swarms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜂群；蟲群","explanation":"指大量昆蟲聚在一起並飛動、移動，尤其常指蜜蜂遷往新蜂巢時形成的蜂群。","examples":[{"en":"A swarm of bees settled near the garden gate.","zh":"一群蜜蜂落在花園門附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We ran inside when a swarm of wasps flew toward us.","zh":"一群黃蜂朝我們飛來時，我們跑進了屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7653528c050c32fb","term":"swarm","forms":["swarm","swarms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜂擁的人群；成群移動的事物","explanation":"指大量的人、動物或物體一起移動，場面像蜂群一樣密集、喧鬧或混亂。","examples":[{"en":"A swarm of tourists rushed toward the last bus.","zh":"一大群遊客朝最後一班公交車蜂擁而去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A swarm of tourists followed the guide upstairs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17a89d7c49fd1acb","term":"swarm","forms":["swarm","swarms","swarming","swarmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"成群移動","explanation":"指許多人、動物或物體像蜂群一樣一起移動，常帶有擁擠、忙亂的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Passengers swarmed through the station after the concert.","zh":"音樂會結束後，乘客們成群湧過車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fans swarmed around the singer outside the hotel.","zh":"歌迷們在酒店外蜂擁圍住了那位歌手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4ab64fc01e042ce","term":"swarm","forms":["swarm","swarms","swarming","swarmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擠滿；充斥著","explanation":"指某個地方到處都是昆蟲、人或其他東西，彷彿被蜂群佔滿。","examples":[{"en":"The beach was swarming with children during the holiday.","zh":"假日期間，海灘上擠滿了孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beach swarmed with visitors on the holiday weekend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swarm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-345c74edfb0ce0820409","word":"sway","forms":["sway"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-44ba697addd56577","term":"sway","forms":["sway","sways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搖擺動作","explanation":"sway 指左右或前後擺動的動作，也可以指武器揮動時形成的擺動或掃動；這是“在兩邊之間移動”這一核心意象的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The lantern moved in a slow sway above the porch.","zh":"門廊上方的燈籠緩慢地來回搖擺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sway of the carriage made her sleepy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b752eaaa3fd77477","term":"sway","forms":["sway","sways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搖晃；擺動","explanation":"sway 指有節奏或持續的搖晃、擺動，常見於樹木、建築物、人群或隨著音樂移動的身體。","examples":[{"en":"The music put the whole room into a gentle sway.","zh":"音樂讓整個房間裡的人都輕輕搖擺起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat's gentle sway made her sleepy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ef1f933bc1b2d2e","term":"sway","forms":["sway","sways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"影響力；分量","explanation":"sway 指使別人改變看法或讓事情向某一方發展的影響力；它就像把搖擺的物體推向一邊。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm advice still holds sway with the younger members.","zh":"她冷靜的建議對年輕成員仍然很有影響力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her opinion carries considerable sway within the committee.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4176bc4fefb9d05f","term":"sway","forms":["sway","sways","swaying","swayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"搖擺；搖動","explanation":"sway 作不及物動詞時表示從一邊向另一邊，或前後搖動、搖晃；人也可以隨著音樂搖擺。","examples":[{"en":"The branches swayed in the strong wind.","zh":"樹枝在強風中搖擺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They swayed to the music while waiting for the train.","zh":"他們等火車時隨著音樂搖擺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-821a1a53abc86ea5","term":"sway","forms":["sway","sways","swaying","swayed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"影響；左右","explanation":"sway 表示透過權力、說服力或道德力量影響別人，使其改變決定或行動方向。這裡的“搖擺”變成了把人的判斷推向一邊。","examples":[{"en":"Nothing could sway the committee's final decision.","zh":"沒有什麼能左右委員會的最終決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Advertisements can sway undecided voters.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3ef631dfff36845fe066","word":"swear","forms":["swear"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f948927b42cdcab","term":"swear","forms":["swear","swears","swearing","swore","sware","sworn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發誓；鄭重承諾","explanation":"swear 表示鄭重地承諾做或不做某事，語氣比普通的“答應”更強，常讓人想到宣誓或具有約束力的承諾。","examples":[{"en":"She swore to keep the secret.","zh":"她發誓要保守這個秘密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I swear I'll return before the gates close.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb08125d0075837d","term":"swear","forms":["swear","swears","swearing","swore","sware","sworn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發誓證明；宣誓說","explanation":"swear 表示以宣誓的方式保證某個說法真實，常用於證人、法庭或嚴肅陳述。它強調“我用誓言擔保這是真的”。","examples":[{"en":"The witness swore that she had seen the man before.","zh":"證人發誓說，她以前見過那名男子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He swore that he had never seen the weapon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02310878e11293aa","term":"swear","forms":["swear","swears","swearing","swore","sware","sworn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敢保證；強烈斷言","explanation":"在日常口語中，swear 常表示“我敢保證”或“我絕對說的是真的”，不一定真的舉行宣誓儀式。它把說話人的確信和強調放在前面。","examples":[{"en":"I swear I left my keys on the table.","zh":"我敢保證，我把鑰匙放在桌上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I swear I locked the door before leaving.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a581c1903903a8bd","term":"swear","forms":["swear","swears","swearing","swore","sware","sworn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說髒話；爆粗口","explanation":"swear 也表示使用粗俗、褻瀆或淫穢語言。這個義項正是從“鄭重發誓”進一步發展出來的：過去人們把隨意發誓、濫用神名視為不當語言。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't swear in front of the baby.","zh":"請不要在寶寶面前說髒話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He swore loudly when the hammer struck his thumb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cdaad7e096dd8f07d486","word":"sweat","forms":["sweat"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90b35104e4e56269","term":"sweat","forms":["sweat","sweats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"汗","explanation":"sweat是人在炎熱或運動等情況下從皮膚毛孔排出的液體，用來調節體溫。","examples":[{"en":"I wiped the sweat from my face after the run.","zh":"跑步後，我擦去了臉上的汗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sweat ran down his face during the climb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d013d89d79d49b1","term":"sweat","forms":["sweat","sweats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"辛苦勞動","explanation":"因為辛苦工作會讓人出汗，sweat可以引申為艱苦勞動或付出的辛勞。","examples":[{"en":"The team earned its success through sweat and discipline.","zh":"這支隊伍靠辛勤付出和自律贏得了成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She poured years of sweat into restoring the house.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c3e8f920777e30b","term":"sweat","forms":["sweat","sweats","sweating","sweated","sweaten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"出汗","explanation":"sweat作動詞時首先表示身體排出汗液，也就是“出汗”。","examples":[{"en":"I always sweat when I exercise in the heat.","zh":"我在高溫下運動時總會出汗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sweated through our shirts on the steep climb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-594f08b5328d2370","term":"sweat","forms":["sweat","sweats","sweating","sweated","sweaten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辛苦工作","explanation":"出汗象徵費力，因此sweat可表示長時間、辛苦地做某事。","examples":[{"en":"She has been sweating over the report all afternoon.","zh":"她整個下午都在埋頭苦寫那份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sweated all afternoon to finish the fence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-baad27842a513a95","term":"sweat","forms":["sweat","sweats","sweating","sweated","sweaten"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擔心某事","explanation":"在“不要擔心”的固定說法中，sweat表示把某件事放在心上、為它焦慮。","examples":[{"en":"Don't sweat it; I'll fix the mistake.","zh":"別擔心，我會把這個錯誤改好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't sweat the small mistakes in your draft.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3a89efbca9e4f45426b","word":"sweater","forms":["sweater"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff385aaace9fec81","term":"sweater","forms":["sweater","sweaters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運動前後穿的針織上衣","explanation":"指運動員在運動前或運動後穿的、通常較厚的針織上衣，幫助保暖。它是 sweater 最早且最具體的現代衣物義。","examples":[{"en":"The players put on thick sweaters before warming up.","zh":"隊員們熱身前穿上了厚毛衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He took off his sweater after the game.","zh":"比賽結束後，他脫下了毛衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a394004d8c0a7e91","term":"sweater","forms":["sweater","sweaters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保暖針織上衣","explanation":"泛指為了保暖而穿的針織上衣，可以是毛衣、羊毛衫或其他類似款式。這是日常閱讀和會話中最常見的意義。","examples":[{"en":"I packed a warm sweater because the evenings are cold.","zh":"我帶了一件暖和的毛衣，因為晚上很冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pulled a wool sweater over her shirt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dfd33796972c3baa5e1c","word":"sweep","forms":["sweep"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d71dadf47313ad53","term":"sweep","forms":["sweep","sweeps","sweeping","swept"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掃乾淨","explanation":"用掃帚、刷子等反覆掃動，把地面、街道或其他表面上的灰塵和雜物清理乾淨；這是“掃過去”最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"I sweep the kitchen floor every evening.","zh":"我每天晚上都掃廚房地板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They swept the street before the parade.","zh":"遊行前，他們把街道掃乾淨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba0dedf22aba8d6d","term":"sweep","forms":["sweep","sweeps","sweeping","swept"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掃過；掠過","explanation":"表示風、目光、火焰等沿著一條較長的弧線或橫向路徑掃過某個地方，重點是連續而開闊的移動。","examples":[{"en":"A cold wind swept across the fields.","zh":"一陣冷風掃過田野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Sunlight swept over the empty room.","zh":"陽光掠過空蕩蕩的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-877c54c0c1702939","term":"sweep","forms":["sweep","sweeps","sweeping","swept"],"pos":"verb","zh":"徹底搜查","explanation":"按照一定順序把一個地方全面搜查一遍，像把整個區域“掃過去”一樣，不遺漏可能藏有目標的角落。","examples":[{"en":"The officers swept the building for weapons.","zh":"警員徹底搜查了這棟樓，尋找武器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police swept through the park after the alarm.","zh":"警報響起後，警方徹底搜查了公園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9043c16af362f30807d","word":"sweet","forms":["sweet"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-717620c135d77fb0","term":"sweet","forms":["sweet","sweeter","sweetest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"甜的","explanation":"味道像糖一樣，能讓舌頭感到甜。這是 sweet 最基本、最容易擴充套件出的意思。","examples":[{"en":"This apple is wonderfully sweet.","zh":"這個蘋果甜得很可口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She added honey because the tea was not sweet enough.","zh":"她加了蜂蜜，因為茶還不夠甜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55920a002e4bc116","term":"sweet","forms":["sweet","sweeter","sweetest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可愛善良的","explanation":"形容人的性情溫和、可愛，讓別人相處時感到舒服；這是從“令人愉悅”擴充套件到人的典型用法。","examples":[{"en":"Their daughter is such a sweet child.","zh":"他們的女兒真是個可愛的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You are sweet to remember my birthday.","zh":"你還記得我的生日，真體貼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36603efb55eb1ebfda33","word":"swell","forms":["swell"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb85cb4104182c2b","term":"swell","forms":["swell","swells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膨脹；增大","explanation":"指變大這一過程，尤其是因液體、氣體或其他東西充入而鼓起；它對應動詞 swell 的“變大”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor noticed a slight swell in her ankle.","zh":"醫生注意到她的腳踝有一點腫脹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wooden door swelled in the damp weather.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5bc460a0530f245","term":"swell","forms":["swell","swells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鼓起處；隆起物","explanation":"指表面向外鼓出的部分，就像某個東西從平面上“鼓起來”形成的包或隆起。","examples":[{"en":"A small swell appeared beneath the paint on the door.","zh":"門上的油漆下面出現了一個小鼓包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The land rose in a gentle swell beside the road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18b22a61707b16eb","term":"swell","forms":["swell","swells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"湧浪","explanation":"指海面上綿長而有規律的浪，通常由風形成，即使風停後仍可能持續；海面彷彿一片片鼓起。","examples":[{"en":"The boat rose gently on the long ocean swells.","zh":"小船隨著綿長的海上湧浪輕輕起伏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A heavy swell rocked the boat at anchor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05128f8b21ea1ea2","term":"swell","forms":["swell","swells","swelling","swelled","swole","swoll","swollen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變大；腫脹","explanation":"主語自身逐漸變大，尤其是因為液體、氣體或血液等使其鼓起；這是 swell 最基本的動作畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Her fingers swelled up in the heat.","zh":"天氣炎熱時，她的手指腫了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bread dough will swell as it rises.","zh":"麵糰發酵時會逐漸膨脹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2fa0f69a55b043e","term":"swell","forms":["swell","swells","swelling","swelled","swole","swoll","swollen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變大；使膨脹","explanation":"表示某種力量使河流、物體或數量逐漸變大，是“讓東西鼓起來”的及物用法。","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rain swelled the stream within an hour.","zh":"大雨在一小時內就讓溪流漲大了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volunteers swelled the crowd outside the hall.","zh":"志願者們讓大廳外的人群擴大了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c19493d895ef0b7","term":"swell","forms":["swell","swells","swelling","swelled","swole","swoll","swollen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聲音逐漸增強","explanation":"不及物地表示音樂、聲音或情緒的力量慢慢變強，像聲音在空間裡鼓起來。","examples":[{"en":"The strings swelled as the dancers entered.","zh":"舞者入場時，絃樂聲逐漸增強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Applause swelled at the end of the speech.","zh":"演講結束時，掌聲越來越響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a33603bf79f74b056172","word":"swift","forms":["swift"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-081538b997bb38af","term":"swift","forms":["swift","swifter","swiftest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迅速的","explanation":"指事情發生、反應或行動來得很快，幾乎沒有耽擱，就像一道馬上掠過的快影。","examples":[{"en":"The company took swift action after the accident.","zh":"事故發生後，公司迅速採取了行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A swift response can prevent a small problem from growing.","zh":"迅速的反應可以防止小問題變大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swift","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d493f8869139bac710b9","word":"swim","forms":["swim"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-03ff6d6acb14f953","term":"swim","forms":["swim","swims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"游泳；一次游泳","explanation":"指游泳這項活動，或一次游泳的過程。它既可以指運動專案，也可以指“去遊一會兒泳”這樣的具體行動。","examples":[{"en":"Let's go for a swim before dinner.","zh":"我們晚飯前去遊會兒泳吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a swim every morning.","zh":"她每天早上都游泳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-baccc810fc66927c","term":"swim","forms":["swim","swims","swimming","swam","swum","swammest","-","swimmand"],"pos":"verb","zh":"游泳；在水中前進","explanation":"指不接觸水底，靠身體動作在水中前進。這是 swim 最基本、最需要先掌握的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The children swam across the lake.","zh":"孩子們遊過了湖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I swim for thirty minutes every evening.","zh":"我每天晚上游三十分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6c0822cf8ac0a05a7b7","word":"swimsuit","forms":["swimsuit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81eb6b5385b8d67e","term":"swimsuit","forms":["swimsuit","swimsuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"泳裝","explanation":"指游泳、戲水或參加水上活動時穿的衣服，是 swimsuit 最基本、最寬的意思，男女都可以穿。","examples":[{"en":"Put on your swimsuit before we go to the pool.","zh":"我們去游泳池之前先穿上你的泳裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need to buy a new swimsuit for the beach.","zh":"我需要為去海灘買一件新的泳裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swimsuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aaca072429a9268e","term":"swimsuit","forms":["swimsuit","swimsuits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連體泳衣","explanation":"指一種貼身的連體泳裝，傳統上尤其指女性或女孩穿的款式；它仍然屬於“為游泳準備的衣服”這一大類。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a blue one-piece swimsuit for her swimming lesson.","zh":"她為游泳課選了一件藍色連體泳衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her swimsuit has a bright floral pattern.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swimsuit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2da977e917bcbc5ef3b5","word":"swing","forms":["swing"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c34677282ccd6787","term":"swing","forms":["swing","swings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞦韆","explanation":"指懸掛在支架或天花板上、可以前後擺動的座椅；記憶鉤子裡的“懸掛著的座椅”就是這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"The children took turns on the swing.","zh":"孩子們輪流盪鞦韆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sat on the porch swing and watched the rain.","zh":"我們坐在門廊鞦韆上看雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bdce388bde564e62","term":"swing","forms":["swing","swings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變化幅度","explanation":"指某個數值、態度或局勢朝某方向改變的程度；就像擺動物體從一側移到另一側，重點是變化了多少。","examples":[{"en":"There was a sudden swing in public opinion.","zh":"公眾輿論突然發生了大幅轉變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The election saw a swing toward younger candidates.","zh":"這次選舉中，公眾的選擇大幅轉向了更年輕的候選人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad14abe88c830823","term":"swing","forms":["swing","swings","swinging","swung","swang","swungen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繞固定點擺動","explanation":"物體圍繞一個偏離中心但固定的點來回轉動，就像記憶鉤子裡的物體在風中擺動。","examples":[{"en":"The lamp swung gently in the breeze.","zh":"燈在微風中輕輕擺動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The door swung slowly on its rusty hinges.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4d14d1346d8edbd","term":"swing","forms":["swing","swings","swinging","swung","swang","swungen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揮動；來回移動","explanation":"指把物體向一邊又向另一邊移動，或用力揮動它；這正是記憶鉤子中“揮動”的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She swung the bag over her shoulder.","zh":"她把包甩到肩上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He swung the bat and missed the ball.","zh":"他揮棒擊球，但沒有打中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-78b49fb2cc2d2ed6c1bb","word":"switch","forms":["switch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f7a93086bd5d4a8","term":"switch","forms":["switch","switches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"開關","explanation":"一種透過撥動或按動來接通、切斷電流，或把電流引向不同線路的裝置，就像記憶鉤子裡把狀態撥到另一邊。","examples":[{"en":"Please turn off the switch before opening the cover.","zh":"開啟蓋子前請先關掉開關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small switch controls the fan.","zh":"一個小開關控制著風扇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/switch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1514effafdecefe","term":"switch","forms":["switch","switches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轉換；交換","explanation":"指從一種狀態、安排、身份或選擇變成另一種，也可以指兩個物件彼此交換；核心畫面是把方向或狀態撥到另一邊。","examples":[{"en":"The company made a switch from paper forms to an online system.","zh":"公司把紙質表格改成了線上系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We made a quick switch of seats before the show began.","zh":"演出開始前我們很快交換了座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/switch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3286966a893ab42f","term":"switch","forms":["switch","switches","switching","switched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交換","explanation":"指把兩個物件彼此調換，就像讓它們透過“開關”轉到對方的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Can we switch seats so I can sit by the window?","zh":"我們可以換一下座位嗎？我想坐在窗邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two players switched shirts after the match.","zh":"比賽結束後，兩名隊員交換了球衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/switch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c11fc91d91a8fc47","term":"switch","forms":["switch","switches","switching","switched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用開關改變狀態","explanation":"指撥動開關，使裝置或電路進入指定狀態，通常是開啟或關閉。","examples":[{"en":"Please switch the kitchen light on when you come in.","zh":"你進來時請開啟廚房的燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She switched off her phone during the meeting.","zh":"開會期間她關掉了手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/switch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a44c47b1ee24665db1a3","word":"sword","forms":["sword"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be32db9dd9d846f8","term":"sword","forms":["sword","swords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劍；長刃武器","explanation":"sword 是一種有劍柄、通常較長的刃器，可以用來刺、砍或劈。記住“手裡握著一把長劍”這個畫面，就能連到它的名詞意義和後面的動詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"The knight drew his sword and raised it above his head.","zh":"騎士拔出劍，把它舉過頭頂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum displays a sword from the medieval period.","zh":"這家博物館展出一把中世紀的劍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sword","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-479675e55c6d04c4","term":"sword","forms":["sword","swords"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劍牌組","explanation":"在某些西班牙或義大利牌組以及塔羅牌中，sword 指由劍圖案組成的一個牌組，而不是一把實際的武器。","examples":[{"en":"The card belongs to the suit of swords.","zh":"這張牌屬於劍牌組。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tarot reader turned over the Queen of Swords.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sword","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-db48f7ceb3b18e7adea5","word":"syllable","forms":["syllable"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2e959917e1315ce6","term":"syllable","forms":["syllable","syllables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音節","explanation":"一個詞在發音中按節拍分出的聲音單位，通常圍繞一個母音形成；說一個詞有幾個這樣的聲音拍子，就是說它有幾個音節。","examples":[{"en":"The word \"computer\" has three syllables.","zh":"“computer”這個詞有三個音節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please say the name slowly, syllable by syllable.","zh":"請把這個名字一個音節一個音節地慢慢說出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syllable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63749b9c94908c3c","term":"syllable","forms":["syllable","syllables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音節的書寫形式","explanation":"指把某個已發出的音節記錄在紙面上的文字部分，重點不在聲音本身，而在它的書面表示。","examples":[{"en":"The symbol represents the first syllable of the name.","zh":"這個符號代表這個名字的第一個音節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Underline the syllable written in bold type.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syllable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b76a7ca153c246716583","word":"symbol","forms":["symbol"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a40521a0e9b8ab39","term":"symbol","forms":["symbol","symbols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代表意義的符號或字元","explanation":"symbol 可以是字母、字元、圖案或其他記號，用來代表一個物件、概念或規定的意義；重點是“看到這個標記，就想到它所指的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The symbol for euros is often placed before the number.","zh":"歐元的符號通常放在數字前面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A red line is a symbol representing danger on the map.","zh":"地圖上的紅線是代表危險的符號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symbol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2b99222a79924de2","term":"symbol","forms":["symbol","symbols"],"pos":"noun","zh":"象徵某種觀念的事物","explanation":"symbol 也可以指一個具體的人、動物、物品或形象，因為它長期被看作某種品質或觀念的代表，於是成為該觀念的“象徵”。","examples":[{"en":"The dove has become a symbol of peace.","zh":"鴿子已經成為和平的象徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For many people, the old tree is a symbol of strength.","zh":"對許多人來說，那棵老樹是力量的象徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symbol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21e2db94d100d899bcf6","word":"symbolic","forms":["symbolic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90abec6d87116fd5","term":"symbolic","forms":["symbolic","more symbolic","most symbolic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與符號有關的","explanation":"表示某個事物本身屬於符號系統，或具有用來傳遞意義的符號性質。重點不在它是否實用，而在它是否承載或表達某種意義。","examples":[{"en":"The dove is a symbolic image of peace.","zh":"鴿子是和平的象徵性影象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The colors have symbolic meaning in the ceremony.","zh":"這些顏色在儀式中具有象徵意義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symbolic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a54bca114452269","term":"symbolic","forms":["symbolic","more symbolic","most symbolic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"象徵性的；代表另一層意義的","explanation":"表示一個動作、姿態、人物或物品表面上做的是一件事，實際上還在代表某種立場、情感或更大的事件。比如一個公開道歉可能不只是道歉，也象徵著承認錯誤。","examples":[{"en":"The visit was a symbolic gesture of support.","zh":"這次訪問是表示支援的象徵性姿態。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new law was symbolic, but it changed public attitudes.","zh":"這項新法律具有象徵意義，但它改變了公眾的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symbolic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a21765bd9737eea9b8b","word":"symbolize","forms":["symbolize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-334ca55651d94f31","term":"symbolize","forms":["symbolize","symbolizes","symbolizing","symbolized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"象徵；代表","explanation":"某個具體的人、物或形象承載著更抽象的意義，因此可以說它象徵或代表那種意義。重點是“它本身成為某種意義的標誌”，不一定是有人刻意設計的。","examples":[{"en":"The dove symbolizes peace.","zh":"鴿子象徵和平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For many people, the ring symbolizes love and commitment.","zh":"對許多人來說，這枚戒指象徵著愛情和承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symbolize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a817249c1d6f0c9d","term":"symbolize","forms":["symbolize","symbolizes","symbolizing","symbolized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用象徵手法表達","explanation":"指人透過符號、形象或象徵性事物來表達思想，而不是直接說明。這時重點從“某物代表什麼”轉為“主動用象徵來傳達什麼”。","examples":[{"en":"The artist uses a broken window to symbolize lost hope.","zh":"這位藝術家用一扇破窗來象徵失去的希望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novelist symbolizes isolation through the recurring locked gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symbolize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3781049acb7fd5d7de25","word":"symmetry","forms":["symmetry"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecade5d143504b2d","term":"symmetry","forms":["symmetry","symmetries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴格對稱","explanation":"指一條線、一個平面、一箇中心或一條軸兩側的部分彼此嚴格對應，像把圖形沿中線摺疊後能夠重合。這個意思常見於幾何、建築、圖案和自然形態。","examples":[{"en":"The butterfly's wings show perfect symmetry.","zh":"這隻蝴蝶的翅膀呈現出完美的對稱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The architect designed the building with symmetry around a central axis.","zh":"建築師按照圍繞中軸線對稱的方式設計了這座建築。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symmetry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ba3801ca83dc4539","term":"symmetry","forms":["symmetry","symmetries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"協調均衡","explanation":"指一個整體中各元素安排得均勻、協調，因而產生平衡和美感；它不一定意味著左右可以完全重合，而是強調整體看起來穩妥、和諧。","examples":[{"en":"The designer used symmetry to make the room feel calm and balanced.","zh":"設計師用均衡的佈局讓房間顯得平靜而協調。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The composition's symmetry gives the painting a restful balance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symmetry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f5362423349001832de3","word":"sympathetic","forms":["sympathetic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e2f8cda415d869a","term":"sympathetic","forms":["sympathetic","more sympathetic","most sympathetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表示同情的","explanation":"指理解並關心別人的痛苦、困難或感受，彷彿自己的心也和對方靠近了。它可以描述人的態度、表情、語氣或反應。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a sympathetic smile when I told her the news.","zh":"我告訴她這個訊息時，她給了我一個表示同情的微笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager was sympathetic to the workers' concerns.","zh":"經理理解並支援工人們的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sympathetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6546647157ea0b66","term":"sympathetic","forms":["sympathetic","more sympathetic","most sympathetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"討人喜歡的","explanation":"形容一個人親切、容易讓別人產生好感，因此大家願意接近他或她。這裡不是說這個人正在同情別人，而是說其性格或表現很有親和力。","examples":[{"en":"The novel's main character is intelligent and sympathetic.","zh":"這部小說的主人公聰明而且討人喜歡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor creates a sympathetic character despite his flaws.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sympathetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44933ef4d191bd13cdbb","word":"sympathize","forms":["sympathize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4728de1205cac6c","term":"sympathize","forms":["sympathize","sympathizes","sympathizing","sympathized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感同身受；表示同情","explanation":"知道別人正在經歷痛苦、困難或強烈情緒後，自己也產生相近的感受，並因此表示理解和同情。重點不只是“知道”，而是彷彿在情感上和對方連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"I really sympathize with you after everything that happened.","zh":"經歷了這一切之後，我真的很同情你，也能理解你的感受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many parents sympathize with her worries about the children.","zh":"許多家長都能體會她對孩子的擔憂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sympathize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c88f47dad448038","term":"sympathize","forms":["sympathize","sympathizes","sympathizing","sympathized"],"pos":"verb","zh":"支援；站在一邊","explanation":"由“和某人有共同感受”進一步發展為“站在某人或某個事業的一邊”，表示支援其立場、行動或目標。這裡未必是在表達悲傷或憐憫，而是表明自己的立場相同。","examples":[{"en":"She sympathizes with the workers’ demand for safer conditions.","zh":"她支援工人要求改善安全條件的訴求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many residents sympathized with the striking workers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sympathize","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcd8670ae2da2abab397","word":"sympathy","forms":["sympathy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a2a5bbedca0d3748","term":"sympathy","forms":["sympathy","sympathies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同情；憐憫","explanation":"指看到別人受苦、遇到困難或感到痛苦時，自己也產生關切和難過的感覺。它強調“和對方一起感受”，但不一定表示你贊成對方的做法。","examples":[{"en":"I have a lot of sympathy for people who lose their jobs unexpectedly.","zh":"我非常同情那些突然失去工作的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She offered her sympathy after hearing about his father's death.","zh":"聽說他父親去世後，她向他表示了慰問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sympathy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff5a21e588b0cec2","term":"sympathy","forms":["sympathy","sympathies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共鳴；志趣相投","explanation":"指兩個人或群體在想法、感情或態度上相近，彼此能夠理解和產生共鳴。這裡的“共同感受”不再只來自痛苦，也可以來自共同的興趣、價值觀或看法。","examples":[{"en":"I felt an immediate sympathy with her views on education.","zh":"我立刻就對她的教育觀點產生了共鳴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their shared sympathy for experimental music brought them together.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sympathy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c873ecbd3c57a0116ca","word":"symphony","forms":["symphony"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-803d7952ed810778","term":"symphony","forms":["symphony","symphonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交響樂；交響曲","explanation":"指為管絃樂隊創作的篇幅較長、結構較複雜的音樂作品。它不是泛指所有由許多樂器演奏的音樂，而是通常具有較完整的整體結構和藝術構思的作品。","examples":[{"en":"The orchestra performed a beautiful symphony by Beethoven.","zh":"這支管絃樂隊演奏了一部貝多芬的優美交響曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She listens to symphony every evening to relax.","zh":"她每天晚上聽交響樂來放鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symphony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a0c49170acbff85","term":"symphony","forms":["symphony","symphonies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"和諧交織的整體","explanation":"這是從“許多聲音協調成整體”引申出的比喻義，表示許多聲音、色彩、氣味或其他因素和諧地組合在一起。它突出的是整體效果，而不是某一個單獨的元素。","examples":[{"en":"At dawn, the garden became a symphony of birdsong and colour.","zh":"黎明時，花園變成了鳥鳴與色彩和諧交織的整體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The busy market was a symphony of voices, movement, and smells.","zh":"熱鬧的市場彷彿由各種聲音、動作和氣味共同組成的和諧交響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symphony","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b093720ae25363643156","word":"symptom","forms":["symptom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20dbc370e8f10207","term":"symptom","forms":["symptom","symptoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疾病症狀","explanation":"指人感覺到或身體表現出的異常變化，例如疼痛、發燒、咳嗽或皮疹；這些表現可能提示某種疾病或身體失調，但不等於疾病本身。","examples":[{"en":"Her symptoms include a sore throat and a mild fever.","zh":"她的症狀包括喉嚨痛和低燒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You should see a doctor if the symptoms get worse.","zh":"如果症狀加重，你應該去看醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symptom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-feb3683649513222","term":"symptom","forms":["symptom","symptoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問題的跡象","explanation":"指能夠顯示某種情況存在的訊號，尤其是顯示某個不良問題正在發生的外在表現；它就像事情發出的警報。","examples":[{"en":"Constant arguments can be a symptom of deeper problems in a relationship.","zh":"不斷爭吵可能是關係中存在更深層問題的跡象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The empty shops are a symptom of economic decline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/symptom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee1e5e7dd1c6d267a4f0","word":"syndrome","forms":["syndrome"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0578226bd02edc99","term":"syndrome","forms":["syndrome","syndromes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"症狀組合；綜合徵","explanation":"指一組經常共同出現、能夠識別某種疾病或醫學、心理狀態的症狀、體徵或行為。重點不在某一個表現，而在這些表現像一起跑來、聚成一個可辨認的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor recognized the syndrome from a combination of symptoms.","zh":"醫生根據一組症狀認出了這種綜合徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Down syndrome can affect learning and physical development.","zh":"唐氏綜合徵可能影響學習能力和身體發育。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syndrome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0e0a270e8f2644c","term":"syndrome","forms":["syndrome","syndromes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"典型問題的一套表現","explanation":"引申指某種人、處境或社會現象中成套出現的特徵，通常帶有負面或需要解決的意味。它仍然保留“許多表現聚在一起”的核心，只是物件不再一定是醫學狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The town is suffering from a serious not-in-my-backyard syndrome.","zh":"這個城鎮正受到嚴重的“別建在我家後院”綜合徵困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project suffered from the familiar too-many-managers syndrome.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syndrome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee6b5af5c21754a8217b","word":"synonym","forms":["synonym"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1cf0a291b8a1b633","term":"synonym","forms":["synonym","synonyms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"同義詞","explanation":"指與另一個詞或短語意義相同或相近的詞語。它們通常可以表達相近的核心概念，但不一定在每個句子裡都能完全替換。","examples":[{"en":"“Begin” is a synonym for “start.”","zh":"“Begin”是“start”的同義詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher asked us to find a synonym for “important.”","zh":"老師讓我們找出“important”的一個同義詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/synonym","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de21a8ea93e5d1dc","term":"synonym","forms":["synonym","synonyms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料庫中的替代名稱","explanation":"在資料庫中，指為某個物件定義的另一個名稱或別名，使用這個名稱也可以指向原來的物件。","examples":[{"en":"The administrator created a synonym for the shared table.","zh":"管理員為共享表建立了一個替代名稱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Create a synonym so users can access the renamed database table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/synonym","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3cc0475bb78a5026098","word":"synthetic","forms":["synthetic"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b121c9698fb25f64","term":"synthetic","forms":["synthetic","more synthetic","most synthetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與合成有關的","explanation":"指和把不同成分合在一起製成某種物質或結果有關，重點在“合成”這一過程或領域本身。","examples":[{"en":"The course introduces students to synthetic chemistry.","zh":"這門課向學生介紹合成化學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The laboratory uses a synthetic method to build the compound.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/synthetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66b4282006e3d27e","term":"synthetic","forms":["synthetic","more synthetic","most synthetic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"人造的；非天然的","explanation":"指不是天然形成或取得的，而是人為製造出來的；它可以強調材料或外觀是在模仿天然事物。","examples":[{"en":"The sofa is covered in synthetic leather.","zh":"這張沙發包著人造皮革。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jacket contains synthetic insulation rather than down.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/synthetic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1ac925abd78d567db94","word":"syrup","forms":["syrup"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5af61ee3ede273a","term":"syrup","forms":["syrup","syrups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"糖漿","explanation":"指含糖量高、質地濃稠的液體，通常加在食物裡或澆在食物表面來增加甜味，例如楓糖漿。","examples":[{"en":"She poured maple syrup over the pancakes.","zh":"她把楓糖漿澆在煎餅上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add a little syrup to the fruit salad.","zh":"給水果沙拉加一點糖漿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syrup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9452faf86d316310","term":"syrup","forms":["syrup","syrups"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黏稠液體","explanation":"泛指任何流動緩慢、質地黏稠的液體，不一定很甜，例如止咳糖漿。這個義項保留了“濃稠液體”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"Take two teaspoons of cough syrup before bed.","zh":"睡前服兩茶匙止咳糖漿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The medicine comes as a thick cherry syrup.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/syrup","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bbc5e661e106c6dcd8dc","word":"system","forms":["system"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48f14dd0f56bedcf","term":"system","forms":["system","systems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"由相關部分組成的整體","explanation":"指許多彼此有關的部分組合起來、共同發揮作用的整體，可以是機器、身體、組織、思想或自然現象。重點不只是“有很多東西”，而是這些部分互相配合，形成一個整體。","examples":[{"en":"The city has an efficient public transport system.","zh":"這座城市有一套高效的公共交通系統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our solar system includes the Sun and the planets that orbit it.","zh":"我們的太陽系包括太陽和圍繞它執行的行星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/system","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f82131e86747c14","term":"system","forms":["system","systems"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一套組織或計劃方法","explanation":"指為了完成任務、安排工作或實現目標而組織起來的一套方法和步驟。它與 s1 相連：這裡“站在一起”的不一定是物件，而是按一定邏輯配合的做法。","examples":[{"en":"She developed a system for keeping track of her expenses.","zh":"她制定了一套記錄開支的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teacher uses a simple system to organize the students' work.","zh":"這位老師用一套簡單的方法來安排學生的作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/system","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e452917780fb6603881c","word":"systematic","forms":["systematic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc376c44b359b1a3","term":"systematic","forms":["systematic","more systematic","most systematic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"按計劃和步驟進行的","explanation":"指做某件事時先有計劃，再按照明確的順序和程式一步步完成，而不是隨意處理。","examples":[{"en":"The team carried out a systematic review of the available evidence.","zh":"團隊對現有證據進行了系統的審查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A systematic plan helped us find the cause of the problem.","zh":"一套有步驟的計劃幫助我們找到了問題的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/systematic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61c88eaed0e68b52","term":"systematic","forms":["systematic","more systematic","most systematic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有條理而規律的","explanation":"強調行動、工作或處理方式穩定、有條理，往往讓人感覺每一步都安排得很清楚。","examples":[{"en":"She made a systematic effort to improve her writing.","zh":"她有條不紊地努力提高自己的寫作水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her systematic notes made the project easy to follow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/systematic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0d4fc4a78d3706edccaf","word":"table","forms":["table"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-308b06273370cc02","term":"table","forms":["table","tables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"桌子","explanation":"有平整桌面的傢俱，可以用來吃飯、工作、放東西或進行活動。這是 table 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please leave the keys on the table.","zh":"請把鑰匙放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sat around the table and had dinner.","zh":"我們圍坐在桌旁吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/table","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e3a02c5b454858a","term":"table","forms":["table","tables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"資料表格","explanation":"它把數字、文字或分類資訊按行和列鋪在一個平面上，方便檢視、比較和整理。這裡延續了“平整表面上整齊擺放東西”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The table shows the population of each city.","zh":"這張表顯示了每座城市的人口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please enter the results in the table below.","zh":"請把結果填入下面的表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/table","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5bed85bd69a5502a8f64","word":"tablet","forms":["tablet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8374a81b448e399a","term":"tablet","forms":["tablet","tablets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"刻字的石片、木片或泥板","explanation":"指用泥、石頭或木頭製成的扁平板塊，人們可以把文字刻寫在上面；它體現了“扁平片狀物承載內容”的核心影象。","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist found a clay tablet covered in writing.","zh":"考古學家發現了一塊刻滿文字的泥板。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tablet records a merchant's payment for grain in ancient Babylon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tablet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-10c66443409f3464","term":"tablet","forms":["tablet","tablets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藥片或固體片劑","explanation":"指壓制成小塊、便於吞服的固體藥物或其他物質；它把“扁平小片”的形狀用於盛裝或提供物質。","examples":[{"en":"Take one tablet with water after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後用水服一片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dissolve one tablet in a glass of water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tablet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b5281a710237c64","term":"tablet","forms":["tablet","tablets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"平板電腦","explanation":"指一種行動式電腦，通常有扁平觸控式螢幕；這是現代日常語境中最常見的義項之一，也是“扁平裝置”概念的發展。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter uses a tablet to read books on the train.","zh":"我女兒用平板電腦在火車上看書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tablet fits comfortably inside my shoulder bag.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tablet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ceab38a5bea502d0387d","word":"tackle","forms":["tackle"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a261f7e95b38c2e9","term":"tackle","forms":["tackle","tackles","tackling","tackled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把人摔倒","explanation":"指用自己的體重撲上去或撞上去，把對方強行弄倒；這是“抓住並控制住”的最直接動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The guard tackled the attacker before he reached the door.","zh":"襲擊者還沒到門口，保安就把他撲倒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The security guard tackled the intruder to the ground.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tackle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7590d43924b397f4","term":"tackle","forms":["tackle","tackles","tackling","tackled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"著手處理","explanation":"指正面面對問題、任務或困難，並努力解決或克服它；抽象物件也像被“抓住並控制”一樣成為處理目標。","examples":[{"en":"The city must tackle the problem of rising rents.","zh":"這座城市必須著手解決房租上漲的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We should tackle the drainage problem before winter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tackle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1b15728c37b0282acfe","word":"tactic(s)","forms":["tactic","tactics"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89ee6ecfa2e24813","term":"tactic","forms":["tactic","tactics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"達到目的的手段","explanation":"指為了達到某個目的而特意安排的一步行動或辦法，可以用於談判、工作、競賽等各種場合，不一定是軍事行動。","examples":[{"en":"Changing the meeting time was a tactic to catch the competitor off guard.","zh":"改變會議時間是為了讓競爭對手措手不及的一種手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team used a new tactic to attract more customers.","zh":"團隊採用了一種新辦法來吸引更多顧客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tactic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-273cb9e385d4d065","term":"tactic","forms":["tactic","tactics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對付敵手的戰術","explanation":"指專門用來對付敵人或競爭對手的行動，重點在利用局勢取得優勢；它可以是真正的軍事戰術，也可以用於政治或商業競爭。","examples":[{"en":"Pretending to retreat was a tactic used against the opposing army.","zh":"假裝撤退是用來對付敵軍的一種戰術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach changed tactics after losing the first set.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tactic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-264d6c2a63681388","term":"tactics","forms":["tactics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戰術學","explanation":"指研究如何在既定戰略目標下具體取勝、行動和部署的軍事學科。它關注“這一仗具體怎麼打”，而不是決定戰爭總方向的戰略。","examples":[{"en":"The course covers the tactics of modern warfare.","zh":"這門課程講授現代戰爭的戰術學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The officers studied tactics at the military academy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tactics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-455fccaca3384cad","term":"tactics","forms":["tactics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"力量部署","explanation":"指把人員、部隊或其他力量按一定位置、順序和配合方式安排起來，以便在具體行動中實現目標。這是“怎麼走這一步”的實際部署。","examples":[{"en":"The commander changed his tactics after the first attack.","zh":"第一次進攻後，指揮官改變了部署戰術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their defensive tactics kept the opposing team from scoring.","zh":"他們的防守戰術讓對方球隊無法得分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tactics","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a1073a6e67f0e5f09a5","word":"tag","forms":["tag"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-386d95d7e0d8e69a","term":"tag","forms":["tag","tags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實物標籤","explanation":"指掛在包、衣服或其他物品上的小牌、小片等附著物，用來提供資訊或作識別標記。","examples":[{"en":"There was a small tag on my suitcase.","zh":"我的行李箱上有一個小標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the tag before you wash the shirt.","zh":"洗這件襯衫前先看看標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8887fa96c2c8216c","term":"tag","forms":["tag","tags","tagging","tagged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……貼標籤","explanation":"給某人或某物加上標籤或分類標記，使其更容易被識別、整理或查詢。","examples":[{"en":"Please tag each box with its contents.","zh":"請給每個箱子貼上標明內容的標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I tagged the photos by location.","zh":"我按地點給這些照片加了標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-53806b59f69e37dd","term":"tag","forms":["tag","tags","tagging","tagged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在網上標記使用者","explanation":"在帖子、照片或訊息中標出某個使用者，使其與內容建立連結，並可能收到通知。","examples":[{"en":"I tagged Mia in the photo so she could find it.","zh":"我在照片中標記了米婭，這樣她就能找到這張照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't tag me in posts about work.","zh":"別在和工作有關的帖子裡標記我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c62f876ef1dea830de9","word":"tail","forms":["tail"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d0aa5bb4ac9d79b","term":"tail","forms":["tail","tails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的尾巴","explanation":"動物身體後端、靠近肛門並連線在軀幹上的尾部；這是把 tail 想成“拖在後面的尾巴”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The dog wagged its tail when I came home.","zh":"我回家時，那隻狗搖了搖尾巴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lizard lost its tail but soon grew another one.","zh":"那隻蜥蜴的尾巴掉了，但很快又長出了一條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18d8c9ef6a0f2ca3","term":"tail","forms":["tail","tails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"末端；後部","explanation":"指任何事物最後、後面或較低的一部分；這是從動物尾巴擴充套件出來的“拖在後面”的位置概念。","examples":[{"en":"We sat at the tail of the procession and could barely hear the music.","zh":"我們坐在隊伍的末尾，幾乎聽不見音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The small village lies at the tail of the valley.","zh":"這個小村莊位於山谷的後部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-758cb95fdc40c073054d","word":"tailor","forms":["tailor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-131f76cd775e48fb","term":"tailor","forms":["tailor","tailors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裁縫","explanation":"tailor 是專門製作、修補或修改衣服的人，尤其常指製作西裝等較正式服裝的專業人員。","examples":[{"en":"I took my suit to a tailor for a better fit.","zh":"我把西裝拿給裁縫改得更合身。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tailor measured my shoulders and shortened the sleeves.","zh":"裁縫量了我的肩寬，還把袖子改短了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tailor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1905cf90af29a5ac3f9","word":"take","forms":["take"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3240e79a01526c7a","term":"take","forms":["take","takes","taking","took","taken","tane","takest","tookst","tookest","taketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拿到手；奪取","explanation":"把某物拿到自己手裡、佔有或控制之中，既可以是正常取用，也可以帶有強行奪取的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please take the keys from the table.","zh":"請把桌上的鑰匙拿走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child took my hand and led me outside.","zh":"孩子拉住我的手，把我帶到了外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/take","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5c40dec22e53c3e","term":"take","forms":["take","takes","taking","took","taken","tane","takest","tookst","tookest","taketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"乘坐；搭乘","explanation":"把交通工具作為把自己帶到別處的方式，也就是乘坐公交車、火車、輪船等。","examples":[{"en":"We took the train to the coast.","zh":"我們乘火車去了海邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take the ferry across the river.","zh":"乘渡輪過河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/take","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-703b2ec0368151d6","term":"take","forms":["take","takes","taking","took","taken","tane","takest","tookst","tookest","taketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吃；喝","explanation":"攝取食物或飲料，把它們帶入自己的身體；在現代英語中主要用於固定搭配或較正式語境。","examples":[{"en":"We took dinner at a small restaurant by the harbor.","zh":"我們在港口附近的一家小餐館吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took a cup of tea before bed.","zh":"她睡前喝了一杯茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/take","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7a13d148eb05ea05702","word":"tale","forms":["tale"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3bbc31cd8b740be0","term":"tale","forms":["tale","tales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事；敘述","explanation":"把一連串發生的事情講出來，就是一個 tale；它可以是真實經歷，也可以是虛構故事，重點在於完整的敘述過程。","examples":[{"en":"She told us a funny tale about her first day at work.","zh":"她給我們講了一個關於自己第一天上班的有趣故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel tells the tale of a family separated by war.","zh":"這部小說講述了一個因戰爭而離散的家庭的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-721a659afbd1c867","term":"tale","forms":["tale","tales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳聞；閒話；謊話","explanation":"當 tale 講的是某件據稱發生的事、別人的私事或未經證實的訊息時，它可表示傳聞、閒話，甚至帶有惡意的誹謗；因此它不一定是真實報道。","examples":[{"en":"Please don't tell tales about your classmates.","zh":"請不要散佈你同學的閒話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't believe the tales they spread about him.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50cb3d000873ec971dad","word":"talent","forms":["talent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a0ebcc31c5ac0ce2","term":"talent","forms":["talent","talents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天賦才能","explanation":"指一個人特別突出的天生能力或才華，重點在於這種能力很有價值、值得發展；它不只表示後天練出來的普通技能。","examples":[{"en":"Her talent for music was obvious from an early age.","zh":"她從小就顯露出了音樂方面的天賦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program helps young artists develop their talent.","zh":"這個專案幫助年輕藝術家發展自己的才能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61e46de14bd9ab76","term":"talent","forms":["talent","talents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人才；有才華的人群","explanation":"可以把“才能”轉指擁有這些才能的人，尤其指某個行業、團隊或活動中的人才整體，而不只是一個人的能力。","examples":[{"en":"The studio is looking for fresh talent for its new series.","zh":"這家制片公司正在為新劇尋找新的人才。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival attracts musical talent from around the country.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,113],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-ce7611e7481e75f085f6","word":"talk","forms":["talk"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a28a3cbb7f88708b","term":"talk","forms":["talk","talks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"談話；討論","explanation":"指人們坐下來交換意見或談一件事情的談話，通常比隨意閒聊更有明確主題。","examples":[{"en":"We need to have a talk about your homework.","zh":"我們得談談你的作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I had a long talk with my sister last night.","zh":"昨晚我和姐姐談了很久。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7073a95dce7189f","term":"talk","forms":["talk","talks","talking","talked","talkest","talkedst","talketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說話；交談","explanation":"指透過語言與別人交流，重點是說話這一行為本身，而不一定強調具體內容。","examples":[{"en":"Let's sit down and talk.","zh":"我們坐下來談談吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can I talk to you for a minute?","zh":"我能和你談一分鐘嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c9b5d1712f3f2cc4","term":"talk","forms":["talk","talks","talking","talked","talkest","talkedst","talketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"談論；討論","explanation":"指圍繞某個主題交換意見或資訊，是“把話說到某件事上”。","examples":[{"en":"We sat down to talk about the problem.","zh":"我們坐下來討論這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They talked business over lunch.","zh":"他們午餐時談了生意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a5bc19e31c41c9e44f8","word":"talkative","forms":["talkative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-04f90f64c1b5afde","term":"talkative","forms":["talkative","more talkative","most talkative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"愛說話的；健談的","explanation":"指一個人很喜歡說話，往往比周圍人說得更多；重點是話多，不一定表示表達能力強，也不一定帶有褒貶。","examples":[{"en":"She is very talkative once she feels comfortable.","zh":"她一感到自在就特別愛說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My usually quiet brother became talkative during the trip.","zh":"我平時沉默寡言的弟弟在旅途中變得健談起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talkative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82e598abe64d0fe7","term":"talkative","forms":["talkative","more talkative","most talkative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多嘴而不顧隱私的","explanation":"指一個人說話過於敞開，不注意保守秘密、保護隱私或考慮後果；這是“話很多”進一步發展成“什麼都往外說”。","examples":[{"en":"He was too talkative about the company's private plans.","zh":"他把公司的私密計劃說得太多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her talkative neighbor spread every private detail around town.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talkative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-241daf2e753a6a2f37a1","word":"tall","forms":["tall"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-140369a7dd118303","term":"tall","forms":["tall","taller","tallest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"（人）高的","explanation":"形容人的身高明顯高於一般水平，核心畫面就是人向上長得很高。","examples":[{"en":"Being tall is an advantage in basketball.","zh":"個子高是打籃球的一項優勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tall woman reached the shelf without a stool.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77bed596adc5544e","term":"tall","forms":["tall","taller","tallest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"（物體）高的","explanation":"形容樹、建築物等從底部到頂部距離很大，強調向上的高度。","examples":[{"en":"A row of tall trees blocked the view of the mountains.","zh":"一排高大的樹擋住了山景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tall trees shaded the road throughout the afternoon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77cf9a363c0fb1f0b9cc","word":"tame","forms":["tame"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c674b4f7654d702","term":"tame","forms":["tame","tamer","tamest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"習慣與人接觸的","explanation":"指原本可能怕人或野生的動物已經習慣人的接觸，不再把人當作威脅。這是“被帶回家、逐漸熟悉人”的最基礎畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The young fox is tame enough to eat from my hand.","zh":"這隻小狐狸已經很親人，敢從我手裡吃東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tame robin ate seeds from her hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c056159deaf7fdc5","term":"tame","forms":["tame","tamer","tamest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"對人溫順的","explanation":"指動物面對人時溫和、順從，不容易攻擊或反抗。它比“習慣與人接觸”更進一步，突出相處時的性情平和。","examples":[{"en":"The lion was quite tame and let the keeper touch its head.","zh":"那頭獅子很溫順，任由飼養員觸控它的頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tame deer ate leaves from her hand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb1ab61f76fda0f8","term":"tame","forms":["tame","tames","taming","tamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"馴服；馴化","explanation":"指把野生或怕人的動物帶到習慣人、能夠受人管理的狀態。這正是核心畫面中“把野獸帶回家並讓它熟悉人”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"It took months to tame the rescued wolf.","zh":"馴服這隻獲救的狼花了好幾個月。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nobody had managed to tame the wild boar raised near the village.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tame","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e5123df1126f9d22824","word":"tan","forms":["tan"],"officialPos":"n./adj./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-07da35ad1fc5a785","term":"tan","forms":["tan","tanner","tannest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"棕黃色的","explanation":"指淺棕黃、黃褐色的顏色，常用於衣物、車輛、傢俱等物品。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a tan sofa for the living room.","zh":"她為客廳選了一張棕黃色的沙發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wore tan trousers and a white shirt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2e69455836de2fa1","term":"tan","forms":["tan","tans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棕褐色","explanation":"指淺棕黃或棕褐色本身，也可以指具有這種顏色的色調。","examples":[{"en":"The walls are painted a warm tan.","zh":"牆刷成了溫暖的棕褐色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose tan to match the leather seats.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-db328fd035fd1d2e","term":"tan","forms":["tan","tans","tanning","tanned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"曬黑；曬成棕褐色","explanation":"指皮膚因日曬或類似光照而變成棕褐色，也可指使皮膚產生這種顏色。它和名詞 tan 的“曬黑膚色”來自同一條“陽光染色”的概念。","examples":[{"en":"I tan easily, but my brother always burns.","zh":"我很容易曬黑，但我哥哥總是曬傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tans her legs in the garden.","zh":"她在花園裡曬黑自己的腿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb48108ea0d1b87a515d","word":"tangerine","forms":["tangerine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8f02d199a7e9fd8","term":"tangerine","forms":["tangerine","tangerines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橘子；柑橘","explanation":"指一種外皮較粗糙、通常容易剝開、味道酸甜的橙色柑橘類水果；這個具體的水果義是全詞最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I packed two tangerines for the hike.","zh":"我為徒步旅行裝了兩個橘子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She peeled a tangerine and shared the segments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangerine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-60cb125afa69dc041c49","word":"tangle","forms":["tangle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f728b15de64a0c0e","term":"tangle","forms":["tangle","tangles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"纏結的一團","explanation":"指線、頭髮、藤蔓等互相纏繞後形成的一團，重點是看得見、難以分開的纏結狀態。","examples":[{"en":"There was a tangle of wires behind the desk.","zh":"書桌後面有一團纏在一起的電線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She carefully pulled the tangle of hair apart.","zh":"她小心地把那團纏結的頭髮分開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84c2fda965821c7c","term":"tangle","forms":["tangle","tangles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混亂局面","explanation":"指各種問題、事實或關係互相糾纏，形成難以理清的複雜局面；它是“纏結的一團”從具體事物向抽象事情的引申。","examples":[{"en":"The project became a tangle of delays and unclear decisions.","zh":"這個專案變成了一個由延誤和不明確決定交織而成的混亂局面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I spent the morning trying to untangle this tangle of paperwork.","zh":"我花了一上午試圖理清這堆糾結的檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af8e91df04747d88","term":"tangle","forms":["tangle","tangles","tangling","tangled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"把……纏在一起","explanation":"指主動把線、頭髮、繩子等混合纏繞，使它們難以分開；這是整組詞最直接的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"The children tangled the ribbons together while making decorations.","zh":"孩子們做裝飾時把綵帶纏在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind tangled the fishing line around the branch.","zh":"風把魚線纏在了樹枝上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39d5817f89fdf0c2","term":"tangle","forms":["tangle","tangles","tangling","tangled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變得纏結","explanation":"指線、頭髮等自己纏繞在一起，或人的身體、衣物陷入纏結狀態；這是“纏結的一團”變成狀態變化。","examples":[{"en":"Her hair tangled in the strong wind.","zh":"她的頭髮被大風吹得纏在了一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My shoelaces got tangled under the chair.","zh":"我的鞋帶在椅子下面纏住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-281a37477f772e782178","word":"tank","forms":["tank"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-65f5e943b900b66f","term":"tank","forms":["tank","tanks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"儲存液體或氣體的密閉容器","explanation":"指用來儲存液體或氣體、通常相對封閉的容器，例如儲水罐、燃氣罐或工業儲罐；核心形象就是把東西穩穩裝住。","examples":[{"en":"The propane is stored in these tanks.","zh":"丙烷儲存在這些罐裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tank stores rainwater for the garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0992f739bef3eae","term":"tank","forms":["tank","tanks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車輛的油箱","explanation":"指汽車、卡車等車輛用來儲存燃油的容器，是“儲存容器”這個核心意義在車輛上的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The car's tank is nearly empty.","zh":"這輛車的油箱快沒油了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We filled the tank before leaving the last town.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-81dfe7765027fabb","term":"tank","forms":["tank","tanks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝甲戰車","explanation":"指有厚重灌甲、裝有火炮並靠履帶行駛的戰鬥車輛；它把“結實、能承受攻擊”的容器形象擴充套件成了戰車。","examples":[{"en":"The museum has a restored tank from the Second World War.","zh":"這家博物館裡有一輛修復過的二戰裝甲戰車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tank rolled slowly across the damaged bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-729cd87c6329408e2bbf","word":"tap","forms":["tap"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-77e79cea02bd22e6","term":"tap","forms":["tap","taps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水龍頭；閥門","explanation":"指控制水、飲料、煤氣等液體或氣體流出的裝置，也就是常說的水龍頭或閥門；它透過調節開口讓流體流出。","examples":[{"en":"There was no bottled water, so we filled our bottles from the tap.","zh":"沒有瓶裝水，所以我們從水龍頭接滿了水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Turn off the tap while brushing your teeth.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5fb9f49120547e24","term":"tap","forms":["tap","taps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輕敲；輕拍聲","explanation":"指輕輕敲打或拍打的一下，也指這種動作發出的清脆聲音；這正是“輕輕碰一下並讓某物發生變化”的基本意象。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a gentle tap on my shoulder and turned around.","zh":"我感到肩膀被輕輕拍了一下，便轉過身去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a tap at the window during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，窗戶上傳來輕輕的敲擊聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7f6c0a3cd382f1b","term":"tap","forms":["tap","taps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"螢幕輕觸","explanation":"指在手機等電子裝置的觸控式螢幕上輕觸按鈕、圖示或某個位置的一次操作；輕輕碰一下便會讓裝置執行功能。","examples":[{"en":"A single tap on the map showed the nearest station.","zh":"在地圖上輕觸一下，就顯示出了最近的車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can pay with a tap of your phone.","zh":"用手機輕觸一下就可以付款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-974a0df0695d9a8f","term":"tap","forms":["tap","taps","tapping","tapped","tappest","tappedst","tappeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕敲","explanation":"用手指、手或其他物體輕輕敲擊某人或某物，通常會發出清脆的聲音；這正是“輕輕碰一下並讓某物發生變化”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"She tapped me on the shoulder before the meeting began.","zh":"會議開始前，她輕輕拍了拍我的肩膀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tapped the glass with a spoon to get everyone's attention.","zh":"他用勺子敲了敲玻璃杯，吸引大家的注意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ba4ec7d634f794ec260","word":"tape","forms":["tape"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edeee6b7f71e322d","term":"tape","forms":["tape","tapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"膠帶","explanation":"指表面有黏性、可以把東西粘住或修補起來的帶狀材料，通常捲成一卷。","examples":[{"en":"Could you pass me some tape to repair this box?","zh":"你能遞給我一些膠帶來修這個盒子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The label keeps coming off, so I put tape over it.","zh":"標籤總是掉下來，所以我在上面貼了膠帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c95b138a091f38ee","term":"tape","forms":["tape","tapes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錄音或錄影帶","explanation":"指用於儲存聲音或影象的成卷記錄介質，傳統上主要指磁帶，也可指錄影帶。","examples":[{"en":"We found an old tape of my grandfather singing.","zh":"我們找到了一盤爺爺唱歌的舊錄音帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The interview was recorded on tape.","zh":"這次採訪被錄在磁帶上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tape","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34a04005bcaf206eec99","word":"target","forms":["target"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a33f95dd3b1a4dbc","term":"target","forms":["target","targets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"射擊靶子","explanation":"射擊、投擲或測試武器時用來瞄準和檢驗準確度的靶子；它是“目標”這一核心概念最具體的形式。","examples":[{"en":"The beginners took turns shooting at the target.","zh":"初學者輪流向靶子射擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She hit the target on her first try.","zh":"她第一次嘗試就擊中了靶子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/target","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7902b337676888b2","term":"target","forms":["target","targets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目標；指標","explanation":"希望實現或達到的結果，尤其是可以衡量的工作、銷售或增長指標。它把“靶心”從具體物體引申成努力要對準的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The team reached its sales target ahead of schedule.","zh":"團隊提前完成了銷售目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need a clear target for the next three months.","zh":"我們需要確定未來三個月的明確目標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/target","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8948e66e84f8c049","term":"target","forms":["target","targets","targeting","targetting","targeted","targetted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"瞄準；對準","explanation":"把武器或其他東西的方向對準某個目標，強調主動把注意力或力量集中到該物件上。","examples":[{"en":"The soldier targeted the vehicle from a safe distance.","zh":"士兵在安全距離外瞄準了那輛車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The camera is targeted at the entrance.","zh":"攝像機對準了入口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/target","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ebb429fa86d481c2630","word":"task","forms":["task"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-209d5dfaa84c8499","term":"task","forms":["task","tasks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職責中的一項工作","explanation":"指某人的職責、工作安排或崗位要求中的一項具體工作，重點是它屬於一套職責或計劃。","examples":[{"en":"Checking the daily reports is one of my regular tasks.","zh":"檢查每日報告是我的日常工作之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finished the task before lunch.","zh":"她午飯前完成了這項工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/task","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c104a01bc72b3ce8","term":"task","forms":["task","tasks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一項要做的工作","explanation":"泛指任何需要完成的工作，不必說明它是否屬於某人的正式職責；這是日常使用中最寬的一層意思。","examples":[{"en":"The software makes this task much easier.","zh":"這個軟體讓這項工作容易多了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please carry out this task by Friday.","zh":"請在星期五前完成這項工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/task","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-88aa7ca2b95cf84b","term":"task","forms":["task","tasks","tasking","tasked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交給某人一項工作","explanation":"指把一項具體工作分派給某人去完成，核心仍是把“待辦卡”交到對方手裡。","examples":[{"en":"The manager tasked Leo with updating the customer records.","zh":"經理把更新客戶記錄的工作交給了利奧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was tasked with organizing the meeting.","zh":"我被安排負責組織這次會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/task","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-814e6bcc41679ddd4302","word":"taste","forms":["taste"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39b3cfa4276c26e7","term":"taste","forms":["taste","tastes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"味道；味覺感受","explanation":"指舌頭接觸某些物質後產生的味道或口腔中的味覺感受，是“嘗一口”這條主線的起點。","examples":[{"en":"There was a bitter taste in my mouth.","zh":"我嘴裡有一股苦味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tea had a faint taste of mint.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07a63c3c5899a1e8","term":"taste","forms":["taste","tastes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"品味；審美判斷","explanation":"從辨別味道引申為辨別美醜、雅俗或是否合適的能力，尤其指審美、穿著和藝術方面的選擇。","examples":[{"en":"She has excellent taste in furniture.","zh":"她在傢俱選擇方面很有品味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her excellent taste shows in the apartment's furnishings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09c708afdd6a62ae","term":"taste","forms":["taste","tastes","tasting","tasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"品嚐","explanation":"用嘴嘗某種食物或飲料，以感受它的味道。","examples":[{"en":"Taste the sauce before you add more salt.","zh":"加更多鹽以前先嚐嘗醬汁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chef tasted each batch to check its seasoning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d16d5979a7c9d80f","term":"taste","forms":["taste","tastes","tasting","tasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嚐起來；呈現味道","explanation":"指某種食物、飲料或物質帶來某種味覺感受，相當於“嚐起來”。","examples":[{"en":"This tea tastes surprisingly fresh.","zh":"這茶喝起來清新得出人意料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This pear tastes sweeter than the others.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-26d9a1f3e4ec5bc151fc","word":"tasty","forms":["tasty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7838eda32ee58329","term":"tasty","forms":["tasty","tastier","tastiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"美味的；好吃的","explanation":"指食物或飲料味道好，吃起來令人滿意，是這個詞最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"You could make this tasty meal for breakfast.","zh":"你可以做這頓美味的飯當早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soup is simple but really tasty.","zh":"這湯很簡單，但真的很好喝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1828369332d92de","term":"tasty","forms":["tasty","tastier","tastiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"技藝高超的；很能幹的","explanation":"英國非正式用法中，指某人的做法、表現或能力很強，像是“做得漂亮、很有一手”。","examples":[{"en":"That was a tasty bit of work from the young defender.","zh":"這名年輕後衛剛才那一下處理得非常漂亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He's a tasty guitarist with years of experience.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tasty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1ffc0406b9891fcd265a","word":"tax","forms":["tax"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f44cbb7cdb432e7e","term":"tax","forms":["tax","taxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政府稅款","explanation":"政府為支付公共服務而向個人或企業徵收的錢，也可以是按收入、購買行為、財產或收成徵收的物品。它通常不是購買某件具體商品的價格，而是依法交給政府的款項。","examples":[{"en":"The new tax will raise the price of imported coffee.","zh":"新稅會提高進口咖啡的價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many workers pay tax directly from their monthly salaries.","zh":"許多工人的稅款會直接從月薪中扣除。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0052ef609d42de3","term":"tax","forms":["tax","taxes","taxing","taxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人徵稅","explanation":"指政府或有權機構要求某個人或企業繳納稅款，也就是把“收稅”這個動作直接施加到納稅人身上。","examples":[{"en":"The government plans to tax large companies more heavily.","zh":"政府計劃對大型企業徵收更重的稅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government taxes higher earners at a higher rate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20b5321050f8538b5b0d","word":"taxicab/taxi/cab","forms":["taxi","cab"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3923c4681c037ec7","term":"taxi","forms":["taxi","taxis","taxies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計程車","explanation":"一種可以臨時僱用、按行程收費的汽車，通常用計價器計算車費；它是 taxi 最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We took a taxi to the train station because it was raining.","zh":"因為下雨，我們乘計程車去了火車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A taxi stopped outside the hotel.","zh":"一輛計程車停在了酒店外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taxi","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67a506a6ab360866","term":"taxi","forms":["taxi","taxis","taxies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機滑行","explanation":"指飛機在機場跑道、滑行道或停機坪上靠自身動力移動的過程，也可指這一階段；它和“計程車在地面行駛”的畫面相聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The passengers stayed seated while the plane was taxiing.","zh":"飛機滑行時，乘客一直坐在座位上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The flight was delayed during taxi because another aircraft was crossing the runway.","zh":"飛機滑行時因為另一架飛機正在穿越跑道，航班延誤了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taxi","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58059d583303d4c3","term":"cab","forms":["cab","cabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"車輛駕駛室","explanation":"cab是卡車、火車等車輛前部供駕駛員坐著操控車輛的封閉空間。它像車輛上的一個小艙，重點是駕駛員所在的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The driver climbed into the cab and started the truck.","zh":"司機爬進駕駛室，發動了卡車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The driver climbed down from the truck's cab.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c090868a7989386c","term":"cab","forms":["cab","cabs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計程車","explanation":"cab是供乘客單次付費乘坐的計程車。它把“車輛上的小艙”變成了乘客付費使用的交通工具，是現代日常英語中最重要的義項。","examples":[{"en":"We took a cab to the airport because the buses had stopped running.","zh":"因為公交車已經停運，我們打車去了機場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took a cab to the airport.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cab","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9f74d1ec36ebdeb2da3","word":"tea","forms":["tea"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-beb3a4a5759ed51d","term":"tea","forms":["tea","teas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"茶葉","explanation":"tea 也指從茶樹上採下並曬乾的葉片或芽；不同品種的幹茶都可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"I bought some loose tea from the market.","zh":"我從市場買了一些散裝茶葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Store the tea in an airtight container.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f0234e845de663d","term":"tea","forms":["tea","teas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"茶飲","explanation":"tea 最常見的意思是把幹茶葉或茶芽泡在熱水中製成的飲料。","examples":[{"en":"Would you like some tea?","zh":"你想喝點茶嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She drinks tea every morning.","zh":"她每天早上喝茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eb0b4270edb36c1ea88c","word":"teach","forms":["teach"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a470f9986097165","term":"teach","forms":["teach","teaches","teaching","taught","teachest","taughtest","teacheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"教給某人知識或技能","explanation":"把知識、方法或技能指給別人看，並幫助對方掌握它；重點是傳授過程。","examples":[{"en":"My aunt taught me how to bake bread.","zh":"我姨媽教我怎麼烤麵包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He teaches English to children on weekends.","zh":"他週末教孩子們英語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-238af4ac5774586c","term":"teach","forms":["teach","teaches","teaching","taught","teachest","taughtest","teacheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"任教；從事教學","explanation":"不強調某一次具體傳授，而是說某人的職業或日常活動是教書。","examples":[{"en":"She teaches at a small college near the coast.","zh":"她在海邊附近的一所小學院任教。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She teaches at a village primary school.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1765111d4982b214","term":"teach","forms":["teach","teaches","teaching","taught","teachest","taughtest","teacheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某人學會或明白","explanation":"透過經歷、解釋或訓練，讓某人獲得理解；結果可以是學會一項技能，也可以是看懂一個道理。","examples":[{"en":"The experience taught him to be more patient.","zh":"這次經歷使他學會了更加耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mistake taught him to check every label.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teach","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1057a9604e04b274da5a","word":"teacher","forms":["teacher"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bea00b20e400914d","term":"teacher","forms":["teacher","teachers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教師；老師","explanation":"指教別人知識、技能或行為方式的人，尤其常指在學校任教的老師。這個人把自己掌握的東西傳給學習者，是“帶你學會東西的人”。","examples":[{"en":"Her teacher helped her understand the difficult problem.","zh":"她的老師幫助她弄懂了這道難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He works as a science teacher at a local school.","zh":"他在當地一所學校當科學教師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teacher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0149fec3b4cc562c","term":"teacher","forms":["teacher","teachers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啟示；教訓","explanation":"指某件事或某段經歷帶來的啟示、教訓，好像它在無形中教會了你什麼。這裡的teacher不是具體的人，而是能讓人增長認識的經驗或事件。","examples":[{"en":"The mistake was a valuable teacher, and I never repeated it.","zh":"這次錯誤給了我寶貴的教訓，我再也沒有重犯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The difficult journey became a teacher that changed how she saw the world.","zh":"這段艱難的旅程成了改變她看待世界方式的一課。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teacher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca8b22d0db83a22db163","word":"team","forms":["team"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-583c653e95068a22","term":"team","forms":["team","teams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"團隊；隊伍","explanation":"team是一群為同一項活動、比賽或工作共同努力的人，重點是成員之間有共同目標並一起行動。","examples":[{"en":"Our team finished the project ahead of schedule.","zh":"我們的團隊提前完成了專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She joined the school basketball team.","zh":"她加入了學校籃球隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d57b18482098c2b5","term":"team","forms":["team","teams","teaming","teamed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"組隊；合作","explanation":"作動詞時，team表示幾個人組成一隊，共同完成體育、工作或其他任務。","examples":[{"en":"The two designers teamed up to create the new app.","zh":"兩位設計師組隊開發了這款新應用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two designers teamed up to launch a clothing label.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/team","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33f38545e00a507fba8b","word":"teapot","forms":["teapot"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df99d452e82d585d","term":"teapot","forms":["teapot","teapots"],"pos":"noun","zh":"茶壺","explanation":"teapot 是用來泡茶並把茶倒出來的壺，通常有方便端拿的把手和方便倒茶的壺嘴；正因為外形醒目，它後來也能用來命名一片像茶壺的星群。","examples":[{"en":"She poured the freshly brewed tea from the teapot.","zh":"她從茶壺裡倒出剛泡好的茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We put the teapot in the middle of the table.","zh":"我們把茶壺放在桌子中央。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teapot","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f8ac0b8c10df0c4d952","word":"tear","forms":["tear"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f495ef6d119ca036","term":"tear","forms":["tear","tears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裂口；破損處","explanation":"指布、紙等材料被撕開後形成的破口或裂縫，重點是“被扯開留下的地方”。","examples":[{"en":"There is a small tear in my jacket.","zh":"我的夾克上有一個小破口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She repaired the tear with a needle and thread.","zh":"她用針線把破口縫好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2219b1aff362c77","term":"tear","forms":["tear","tears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眼淚","explanation":"指人因哭泣、疼痛或刺激而從眼睛流出的鹹味液體；它是從眼睛落下的一滴水。","examples":[{"en":"A tear rolled down his cheek.","zh":"一滴眼淚順著他的臉頰流下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tried to smile through her tears.","zh":"她強忍著淚水微笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05254326b526a741","term":"tear","forms":["tear","tears","tearing","tore","torn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撕裂；扯開","explanation":"指把一個物體固定或拉住兩處，再用力把它扯開；也可泛指使材料破裂或分離。","examples":[{"en":"I tore my shirt on a sharp branch.","zh":"我的襯衫被一根尖樹枝掛破了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please tear the paper in half.","zh":"請把這張紙撕成兩半。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7aadd7b670c0940d","term":"tear","forms":["tear","tears","tearing","tore","torn"],"pos":"verb","zh":"被撕破","explanation":"指衣物、紙張等自己變成破的狀態，通常是意外造成的；重點是物品承受了“被扯開”的結果。","examples":[{"en":"My backpack tore when I overloaded it.","zh":"我的揹包裝得太滿，結果被撐破了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This thin paper tears easily when wet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48b270119c4ed3df","term":"tear","forms":["tear","tears","tearing","teared"],"pos":"verb","zh":"流淚","explanation":"指眼睛產生並流出眼淚，可能是因為悲傷，也可能只是受到煙、風等刺激。","examples":[{"en":"My eyes tear whenever I cut onions.","zh":"我每次切洋蔥都會流眼淚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her eyes began to tear during the sad scene.","zh":"看到那段悲傷的場景時，她的眼睛開始流淚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-46a8f8f8697eb7b27eb7","word":"tease","forms":["tease"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5879601c876e8925","term":"tease","forms":["tease","teases","teasing","teased"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逗弄；取笑","explanation":"指以玩笑方式指出或利用某人的小缺點來逗對方，可能是親暱的，也可能變得刻薄傷人。","examples":[{"en":"The children teased Ben about his new haircut.","zh":"孩子們拿本的新發型逗他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was only teasing you.","zh":"我只是逗你玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tease","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83e3b78f14e08cc5e0bf","word":"technical","forms":["technical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c05ddd6b0df35fa","term":"technical","forms":["technical","more technical","most technical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"專業術語意義上的","explanation":"表示某個詞、概念或說法只在特定學科中按嚴格的專業定義使用，而不是日常的普通含義。","examples":[{"en":"In the technical sense, a whale is a mammal, not a fish.","zh":"嚴格按專業定義來說，鯨是哺乳動物，不是魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The word has a different meaning in a technical context.","zh":"這個詞在專業語境中有不同的含義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7b6807ae70913f8e","term":"technical","forms":["technical","more technical","most technical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與科技或技術發展有關的","explanation":"表示某事涉及機器、工程、科技裝置或技術進步，重點在實際的技術系統，而不只是專業說法。","examples":[{"en":"The company has made several technical improvements to the engine.","zh":"這家公司對發動機作了幾項技術改進。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please contact technical support if the device stops working.","zh":"如果裝置停止工作，請聯絡技術支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff2980a71bf08e3d","term":"technical","forms":["technical","more technical","most technical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與技巧或技術動作有關的","explanation":"表示某項活動需要精確的技巧、訓練或操作能力，常用於表演、運動和藝術評價。","examples":[{"en":"The pianist showed remarkable technical control.","zh":"這位鋼琴家展現了出色的技巧控制力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The routine is technically difficult but emotionally simple.","zh":"這套動作在技巧上很難，但情感表達很簡單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-29ba9d9cef5a66461116","word":"technician","forms":["technician"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f99aba61f227308","term":"technician","forms":["technician","technicians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"技術專業人員","explanation":"指學習、掌握並實際運用某項技術的人，尤其是負責安裝、維護、檢測或解決技術問題的專業人員。這個詞的核心畫面是：裝置或系統出了問題，技術人員用專業技能把它查明並修好。","examples":[{"en":"The technician checked the machine and replaced the broken part.","zh":"技術人員檢查了機器，並更換了損壞的零件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A technician came to fix the problem with our internet connection.","zh":"一名技術人員來解決我們的網路連線問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technician","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6cbdfcf83679e6943e42","word":"technique","forms":["technique"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40898d24df59b4bb","term":"technique","forms":["technique","techniques"],"pos":"noun","zh":"熟練技巧","explanation":"指一個人在某項活動中的實際操作能力，也就是把事情做得準確、熟練的“手上功夫”。它常和天賦、創造力或表現力區分開來。","examples":[{"en":"Her technique on the violin has improved greatly.","zh":"她的小提琴演奏技巧提高了很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has excellent technique but a very cautious style.","zh":"他的技巧非常出色，但風格比較謹慎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technique","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3bd23547b6d988a1","term":"technique","forms":["technique","techniques"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體方法","explanation":"指為了達到某個結果而採用的一套具體做法，尤其是需要一定知識或技能的方法。它可以看成把“手上功夫”整理成可重複使用的步驟。","examples":[{"en":"The coach taught us a technique for improving our balance.","zh":"教練教了我們一種改善平衡的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She demonstrated a simple technique for sharpening knives.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technique","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-665f15cc513c8cf6cf7e","word":"technological","forms":["technological"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7a12f8ffe67b15f","term":"technological","forms":["technological","more technological","most technological"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與技術有關的","explanation":"指與技術有關，尤其指現代科學技術及其應用、發展或影響。它可以修飾具體的技術裝置，也可以修飾技術進步、技術聯絡等較抽象的事物。","examples":[{"en":"Technological advances have changed the way people work.","zh":"技術進步改變了人們的工作方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two countries are building stronger technological ties.","zh":"兩國正在建立更緊密的技術聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technological","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e91fadf24f78c081972a","word":"technology","forms":["technology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35cbb5b785e6ab0f","term":"technology","forms":["technology","technologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"技術；科技","explanation":"指把科學知識和實用技巧結合起來，用於生產、設計、解決問題或改善生活的整體方法和成果。它強調的是“怎樣把知識做成有用的東西”，不只是一件具體裝置。","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology has made it easier for people to work from home.","zh":"現代科技讓人們更容易在家工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company invests heavily in clean-energy technology.","zh":"這家公司大力投資清潔能源技術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29a3afd1cfc6eaac","term":"technology","forms":["technology","technologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"技術裝置；技術產品","explanation":"指由技術設計和製造出來、可以直接看到或使用的機器、裝置或成套技術。這裡的重點從“技術方法”轉到了“技術做出的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The laboratory is equipped with the latest technology.","zh":"這間實驗室配備了最新的技術裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors could try several new technologies at the trade show.","zh":"參觀者可以在貿易展會上試用幾種新技術產品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/technology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d9b73003b497e43b0fc","word":"tedious","forms":["tedious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3b1e6bb2fcea0f40","term":"tedious","forms":["tedious","more tedious","most tedious"],"pos":"adj","zh":"冗長乏味的","explanation":"形容一件事持續很久、內容重複或缺少變化，讓人逐漸感到厭煩；它可以同時帶有“耗時、令人疲憊”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Sorting all these old documents is tedious.","zh":"整理這些舊檔案很枯燥乏味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lecture became tedious after the first hour.","zh":"講座進行到第一個小時後變得冗長乏味。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tedious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-705d0099fc64938376bd","word":"teenage","forms":["teenage"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cc2a4e7c36ec02d2","term":"teenage","forms":["teenage"],"pos":"adj","zh":"青少年的；十三至十九歲的","explanation":"指與十三至十九歲這一階段有關的人、事物或經歷，核心感覺就是“屬於青少年時期的”。它既可以修飾青少年本人，也可以修飾這段時期中的生活、問題和回憶。","examples":[{"en":"She moved to another city during her teenage years.","zh":"她在青少年時期搬到了另一座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many teenage students worry about fitting in.","zh":"許多青少年學生擔心自己能否融入集體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teenage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b77e03c668b898d943e1","word":"teenager","forms":["teenager"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd581bfb4cb1a26d","term":"teenager","forms":["teenager","teenagers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"13至19歲的青少年","explanation":"指年齡從13歲到19歲的人，核心就是“走在13至19這扇年齡門裡的人”。這個詞強調具體年齡範圍，不單是泛指年輕人。","examples":[{"en":"Every teenager needs some privacy.","zh":"每個青少年都需要一些私人空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My brother became a teenager last year.","zh":"我弟弟去年進入了13至19歲的年齡階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teenager","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a020aa82f17b6d1d929","word":"teens","forms":["teens"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1274468fb7a44dbd","term":"teens","forms":["teens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"十三至十九的數字","explanation":"teens 可以把十三到十九這些數字看成一個整體，意思接近“十幾”。例如統計人數、數量時，說數量處在 teens，表示大約有十三到十九個。","examples":[{"en":"The number of visitors was in the teens.","zh":"訪客人數在十三到十九之間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thermometer stayed in the teens all afternoon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teens","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c8dbff389f44874","term":"teens","forms":["teens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"十三至十九歲","explanation":"teens 也指從十三歲到十九歲這一整段人生時期，也就是“十幾歲”。說某人處於 teens，就是說這個人年齡在十三至十九歲之間。","examples":[{"en":"He started playing the guitar in his teens.","zh":"他在十幾歲時開始彈吉他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many people become more independent during their teens.","zh":"許多人在十幾歲時會變得更加獨立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teens","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-717a1cda828d2c9a2678","word":"telecommunications","forms":["telecommunications"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"telecommunications","forms":["telecommunications"],"pos":"n.","zh":"電信；遠距通訊","examples":[{"en":"Modern telecommunications allow people to work across continents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The storm damaged the region's telecommunications network.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-0684c60c14e870b7a16a","word":"telegraph","forms":["telegraph"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55ed32f0dddda32e","term":"telegraph","forms":["telegraph","telegraphs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電報機；電報系統","explanation":"telegraph 可以指用編碼訊號傳送電報的機器，也可以指包括架空線路和海底電纜在內的整套通訊系統；這是“把訊息送到遠方”這一核心畫面的具體裝置化。","examples":[{"en":"The railway station used the telegraph to report delays to the city.","zh":"火車站用電報向城裡報告晚點情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The telegraph connected the coastal town with the capital.","zh":"電報系統把這座沿海小鎮和首都連線了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/telegraph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca4fc304213d89a4","term":"telegraph","forms":["telegraph","telegraphs","telegraphing","telegraphed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提前洩露意圖","explanation":"telegraph 表示某人的皺眉、停頓、姿勢或態度變化讓別人提前看出他的情緒、意圖或下一步行動；這種資訊像電報一樣被“發”給了觀察者，而且不一定是有意的。","examples":[{"en":"His nervous laugh telegraphed that he was hiding something.","zh":"他緊張的笑聲暴露出他似乎在隱瞞什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She telegraphed her decision by refusing to make eye contact.","zh":"她拒絕與人對視，提前表明了自己的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/telegraph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a1481b323414eb55745c","word":"telephone/phone","forms":["telephone","phone"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-266072a5936bfb0b","term":"telephone","forms":["telephone","telephones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電話裝置","explanation":"指讓人能夠透過電訊號與遠處的人雙向通話的裝置，包括傳統電話和現代電子電話；日常說的phone常常就是它的簡稱。","examples":[{"en":"The telephone rang just as we sat down for dinner.","zh":"我們剛坐下吃晚飯，電話就響了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a telephone in the hallway for visitors.","zh":"走廊裡有一部供訪客使用的電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/telephone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f9395f52c39319e","term":"telephone","forms":["telephone","telephones","telephoning","telephoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打電話聯絡","explanation":"指嘗試透過電話聯絡某人或某處，核心畫面就是拿起電話把聲音傳到遠處。","examples":[{"en":"Please telephone me when you arrive at the station.","zh":"你到車站後請給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I telephoned the hotel to confirm our reservation.","zh":"我給酒店打了電話，確認我們的預訂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/telephone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-989e7d770543e4c3","term":"phone","forms":["phone","phones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電話；手機","explanation":"phone 是用來把聲音實時傳到遠方的電話裝置；在現代日常語境中，尤其常指手機，也可以指固定電話或打電話這一聯絡渠道。","examples":[{"en":"I left my phone at home, so I couldn't call anyone.","zh":"我把手機落在家裡了，所以沒法給任何人打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Maya is on the phone with her doctor.","zh":"瑪雅正在和醫生通電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-168add9c20114dab","term":"phone","forms":["phone","phones","phoning","phoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給某人打電話","explanation":"作動詞時，phone 就是拿電話把自己的聲音傳給某人，也就是“給某人打電話”。","examples":[{"en":"Phone me when you arrive at the station.","zh":"你到車站後給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'll phone the hotel to confirm our booking.","zh":"我會給酒店打電話確認預訂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/phone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-918d6b6a9b95943bf5e2","word":"telescope","forms":["telescope"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b083e030d1cdd33","term":"telescope","forms":["telescope","telescopes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"望遠鏡","explanation":"一種把遠處物體放大，使人能夠更清楚觀察的光學儀器，尤其常用於觀察天空中的目標。記住“把遠處看近”這個畫面，就能抓住它的核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"We looked at the moon through a telescope.","zh":"我們用望遠鏡觀察月亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps a small telescope by the window.","zh":"她在窗邊放著一架小望遠鏡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/telescope","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b16a1163cb6c4536bc2d","word":"television/TV","forms":["television","TV"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c870f19467fba132","term":"television","forms":["television","televisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電視媒介","explanation":"指利用電子訊號傳播實時影象，通常也傳播聲音的媒介或傳播方式，重點在“把遠處的畫面送來”，而不是某一臺機器。","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people watch television every evening.","zh":"每天晚上都有數百萬人看電視。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The story was first reported on television.","zh":"這則報道最先在電視上播出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/television","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e637aad3716f4253","term":"television","forms":["television","televisions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電視機","explanation":"指家中接收電視訊號、用螢幕和揚聲器播放影象與聲音的具體裝置，也就是通常所說的一臺電視機。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a new television for the living room.","zh":"我們給客廳買了一臺新電視機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The television is too loud.","zh":"電視機的聲音太大了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/television","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0176c9021eb364b6","term":"TV","forms":["TV","TVs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電視；電視機","explanation":"最常見的意思是電視這一媒介，或家裡用來看節目的電視機；同一個縮寫可以根據上下文表示“看電視”這一活動或具體裝置。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the final on TV last night.","zh":"我們昨晚在電視上看了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a new TV in the living room.","zh":"客廳裡有一臺新電視機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/TV","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-879915cfdc2cb4852ed0","word":"tell","forms":["tell"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9cd0632949c41192","term":"tell","forms":["tell","tells","telling","told","telled","tellest","toldest","telleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"講述故事","explanation":"tell 表示把一件事按語言講給別人聽，重點是傳達一段故事、經歷或經過；它把心裡的內容“說出來”，正是 tell 的主線。","examples":[{"en":"Grandpa told us a funny story after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，爺爺給我們講了一個有趣的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She told me what happened at school.","zh":"她告訴了我學校裡發生的事情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eedf71689008ca31","term":"tell","forms":["tell","tells","telling","told","telled","tellest","toldest","telleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說出或告訴","explanation":"tell 表示用語言把事實、意見、謊話等傳達出去，重點是讓別人聽到某個資訊；因此可以是告訴真相，也可以是說謊。","examples":[{"en":"Please tell me the truth.","zh":"請告訴我真相。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He told his parents that he was tired.","zh":"他告訴父母自己累了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-659d68a4abffcfff","term":"tell","forms":["tell","tells","telling","told","telled","tellest","toldest","telleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"辨認或判斷","explanation":"tell 也表示透過觀察或比較看出差別、辨認身份或判斷某種情況，相當於“看得出來”；這是從“把資訊說出來”擴充套件到“從跡象中讀出資訊”。","examples":[{"en":"Can you tell the difference between these two colors?","zh":"你能分辨出這兩種顏色的區別嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I couldn't tell whether he was joking.","zh":"我看不出他是不是在開玩笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4fd76659c9306a403dba","word":"teller","forms":["teller"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf59355d8ded5f60","term":"teller","forms":["teller","tellers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"講述者","explanation":"teller 可以指講故事、敘述經歷或傳達資訊的人，也就是把事情“講清楚”的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is a wonderful teller of stories.","zh":"她很會講故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old man was a gifted teller of tales.","zh":"那位老人很擅長講述故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teller","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17854e499b503b66","term":"teller","forms":["teller","tellers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銀行櫃員","explanation":"在銀行裡，teller 是為客戶收取或支付現金、辦理存款等櫃檯業務的工作人員；這個人把錢款清點並處理好。","examples":[{"en":"I asked the teller to deposit this check.","zh":"我請銀行櫃員把這張支票存入賬戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teller counted the cash twice.","zh":"銀行櫃員把現金數了兩遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teller","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca98e82217aeefd8bc2b","word":"temper","forms":["temper"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f175b8d7bab4236","term":"temper","forms":["temper","tempers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"性情；脾氣","explanation":"指一個人平時的情緒傾向和待人反應方式，可以是溫和、暴躁或容易激動的性情。","examples":[{"en":"She has a calm temper and rarely argues with anyone.","zh":"她性情平和，很少和別人爭吵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His quick temper makes teamwork difficult.","zh":"他急躁的脾氣讓團隊合作變得困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b831216fd88ecd99","term":"temper","forms":["temper","tempers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"易怒的傾向","explanation":"指一個人很容易生氣的習慣性傾向，是“脾氣”這個概念中特別突出的易怒一面。","examples":[{"en":"His hot temper often gets him into trouble.","zh":"他的暴脾氣常常給他惹麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His quick temper made colleagues reluctant to challenge him.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89cbd9a20f4aca5a","term":"temper","forms":["temper","tempers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"怒氣；發火","explanation":"指已經表現出來的一陣怒氣或發火行為，是“失去調節”後的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She lost her temper when the computer crashed again.","zh":"電腦再次宕機時，她發火了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He apologized for his outburst of temper.","zh":"他為自己發脾氣道了歉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38ad1e26f1cfa517","term":"temper","forms":["temper","tempers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鎮定；剋制","explanation":"指把怒氣和情緒控制住、保持冷靜的狀態，正好對應“調到合適狀態”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"Take a deep breath and keep your temper.","zh":"深呼吸，保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a short walk, he recovered his temper.","zh":"散了一會兒步後，他恢復了鎮定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b314ae60cb741e69f1cc","word":"temperature","forms":["temperature"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1c8c884c44a1587","term":"temperature","forms":["temperature","temperatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冷熱程度；溫度","explanation":"temperature是可以用溫度計測量的冷熱程度，適用於空氣、水、食物、房間等。它既可以表示一個範圍或狀態，也可以表示具體測得的數值。","examples":[{"en":"The temperature in the room is too low for the baby.","zh":"房間裡的溫度對嬰兒來說太低了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the soup at a low temperature while it cooks.","zh":"煮湯時要讓溫度保持在較低水平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temperature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-774f07bb455c851d","term":"temperature","forms":["temperature","temperatures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體溫升高；發燒","explanation":"在談論人的健康時，temperature可以表示異常升高的體溫，也就是發燒。這個意思通常由上下文判斷，尤其常見於看病或請假場景。","examples":[{"en":"Maya has a temperature, so she is staying home from school.","zh":"瑪雅發燒了，所以她今天不去上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse checked whether the child had a temperature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temperature","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-67425801bf1a60fe7ca3","word":"temple","forms":["temple"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31160b4b80183c79","term":"temple","forms":["temple","temples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寺廟；聖殿","explanation":"temple是供人禮拜神明或進行宗教活動的建築，範圍比某一種具體宗教建築更廣。它可以指古代神廟，也可以指現代宗教場所。","examples":[{"en":"We visited the temple of Zeus during our trip.","zh":"旅行期間，我們參觀了宙斯神廟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villagers gather at the temple every morning.","zh":"村民們每天早上在寺廟聚集。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-288e2d79cadbf40a","term":"temple","forms":["temple","temples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猶太會堂","explanation":"在猶太教語境中，temple有時指猶太人的禮拜場所，即猶太會堂。","examples":[{"en":"Her family goes to temple on major holidays.","zh":"她家人在重大節日去猶太會堂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The congregation built a new temple near the park.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d6546721a1d106cf8d2","word":"tempo","forms":["tempo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-df7c69b166b8ab68","term":"tempo","forms":["tempo","tempos","tempi"],"pos":"noun","zh":"速度；節奏","explanation":"tempo 指某項活動推進得快還是慢，也就是整體的速度或節奏；它可以描述工作、銷售、比賽等連續進行的事情。","examples":[{"en":"We need to increase the tempo if we want to finish the project this month.","zh":"如果想在本月完成專案，我們就得加快節奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the break, the team returned to the field at a much faster tempo.","zh":"休息後，球隊以快得多的節奏回到了場上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tempo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21b6b61e8dc1e88e","term":"tempo","forms":["tempo","tempos","tempi"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音樂速度；每分鐘拍數","explanation":"在音樂中，tempo 是樂曲演奏的快慢，通常用每分鐘的拍數表示，也可以用表示大致速度的術語來說明。","examples":[{"en":"The conductor asked the orchestra to return to the original tempo.","zh":"指揮要求樂團恢復原來的速度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This song sounds more relaxed when played at a slower tempo.","zh":"這首歌用較慢的速度演奏時聽起來更輕鬆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tempo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ea8b82a5c42a33f042e3","word":"temporary","forms":["temporary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afb8746c4aadef57","term":"temporary","forms":["temporary","more temporary","most temporary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"暫時的；臨時的","explanation":"指某個職位、安排、狀態或事物只在有限的一段時間記憶體在，之後通常會被正式或永久的安排取代。","examples":[{"en":"Sally took temporary charge of the department while the company looked for a permanent manager.","zh":"公司尋找正式經理期間，薩莉暫時負責這個部門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They found temporary accommodation near the hospital.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temporary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d5e0bd1776d1e78","term":"temporary","forms":["temporary","more temporary","most temporary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"短暫的；轉瞬即逝的","explanation":"強調某種狀態、現象或經歷持續時間很短，很快就會過去；它仍然屬於“只存在一陣”的核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused a temporary power cut in several neighborhoods.","zh":"暴風雨導致幾個街區暫時停電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their relief was temporary; another storm soon arrived.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temporary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf6a53ad2352bf509731","word":"tempt","forms":["tempt"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf6dbee35c86a73a","term":"tempt","forms":["tempt","tempts","tempting","tempted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引誘某人做某事","explanation":"指用獎勵、好處或其他誘人的東西，使某人想做尤其是不該做的事。重點是“把誘惑伸到對方面前，試探對方會不會動心”。","examples":[{"en":"The promise of easy money tempted him to break the rules.","zh":"輕鬆賺錢的承諾誘使他違反了規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't tempt me to skip work and go to the beach.","zh":"別誘惑我不去上班跑到海灘去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tempt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0384bebd6f979ef2","term":"tempt","forms":["tempt","tempts","tempting","tempted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吸引；誘人","explanation":"指某種東西本身很有吸引力，使人產生想要它或嘗試它的念頭，不一定真的有人在主動誘導。","examples":[{"en":"The smell of fresh bread tempted me to buy a loaf.","zh":"新鮮麵包的香味誘得我買了一條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smell of warm bread tempted us inside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tempt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20dd3be4a3b151d6c462","word":"temptation","forms":["temptation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e87bf4b267fc2eb","term":"temptation","forms":["temptation","temptations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受誘惑的狀態","explanation":"指一個人處在很想做某事、尤其是很想做不該做的事的心理狀態中。重點是“受到誘惑”這一處境，而不是造成這種感覺的具體事物。","examples":[{"en":"I felt the temptation to check my phone during the meeting.","zh":"開會時我很想拿出手機看一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He resisted temptation and left the cake untouched.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temptation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec4dc7bb523d4efb","term":"temptation","forms":["temptation","temptations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誘人的事物或機會","explanation":"指會讓人很想接受、購買或去做某事的具體事物、機會或提議，常常帶有“明知可能不合適，卻很難拒絕”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"She resisted the temptation to buy another pair of shoes.","zh":"她忍住了再買一雙鞋的誘惑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The free dessert was too much of a temptation.","zh":"免費的甜點實在太誘人了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temptation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e9da86d351cf9a7642d8","word":"tenant","forms":["tenant"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f5be45b03384cdc","term":"tenant","forms":["tenant","tenants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"租戶；房客","explanation":"tenant是按照租約使用房屋、房間或其他場所的人，重點在於他佔用這個地方而不是擁有它。","examples":[{"en":"The tenant paid the rent on time and kept the apartment clean.","zh":"這名租戶按時交了房租，並把公寓保持得很乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tenant reported a leak in the bathroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tenant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-676f289777563980","term":"tenant","forms":["tenant","tenants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"居住者；佔有某處的人","explanation":"這裡的範圍比“租戶”更寬：只要某人或某物佔據並處在一個地方，就可以被形容為那個地方的tenant，不一定真的簽了租約。","examples":[{"en":"The birds are the only tenants of the abandoned barn.","zh":"這些鳥是那座廢棄穀倉裡唯一的居住者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cave's former tenants had left scratches on the walls.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tenant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4f0a1f5aef53e953cc28","word":"tend","forms":["tend"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2764b766d8ae874e","term":"tend","forms":["tend","tends","tending","tended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"往往；傾向於","explanation":"表示某人或某事通常會朝某種行為或狀態發展，但不表示一定如此；這是 tend 最常見、最值得優先掌握的用法。","examples":[{"en":"People tend to remember bad news longer than good news.","zh":"人們往往比記住好訊息更久地記住壞訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Young children tend to get tired quickly.","zh":"年幼的孩子往往很快就會感到疲倦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc51ea2fd41e51bc","term":"tend","forms":["tend","tends","tending","tended"],"pos":"verb","zh":"照料；打理","explanation":"表示持續照顧病人、植物、動物或某件需要處理的事情，把注意力和行動放在它身上。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse stayed late to tend to the injured hikers.","zh":"護士留下來照料受傷的徒步者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tends the plants in the greenhouse every morning.","zh":"他每天早上照料溫室裡的植物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,114],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"114":1}}},{"id":"ceec-4c3200fefd8b69413376","word":"tendency","forms":["tendency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e0252e45380b4f7b","term":"tendency","forms":["tendency","tendencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傾向；趨勢","explanation":"指人或事物容易以某種方式行動，或經常朝某個方向發展。這種“被推向某處”的感覺可以用於個人習慣，也可以用於材料、社會現象等。","examples":[{"en":"Denim has a tendency to fade.","zh":"牛仔布容易褪色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a tendency to worry about small things.","zh":"她容易為小事擔心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tendency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e02b6d1abe2692f3","term":"tendency","forms":["tendency","tendencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治派別；組織內的傾向","explanation":"在政治或組織語境中，tendency 可以指大組織內部一群人共同堅持的思想方向，因此也可理解為組織中的一個派別。","examples":[{"en":"The new tendency within the party supports wider local control.","zh":"黨內的新派別支援擴大地方自治權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The party's radical tendency opposed the compromise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tendency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9eba7c405ea67a19929","word":"tender","forms":["tender"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01ec81f256a74fea","term":"tender","forms":["tender","tenderer","tenderest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"一碰就疼","explanation":"指身體某處觸碰時敏感或疼痛，好像柔軟而需要照料的部位經不起碰。","examples":[{"en":"The bruise is still tender, so please don't press it.","zh":"這塊淤青碰起來還疼，請不要按。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bruised area was tender to the touch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea2f639d271bf783","term":"tender","forms":["tender","tenderer","tenderest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"肉質軟嫩","explanation":"指肉等食物煮熟後柔軟，容易咀嚼，吃起來不柴；這是“柔軟而需要照料”在食物上的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Cook the beef slowly until it is tender.","zh":"把牛肉慢慢燉到軟嫩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chicken was tender and easy to cut.","zh":"雞肉很嫩，很容易切開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6c83dd66e385473","term":"tender","forms":["tender","tenderer","tenderest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"溫柔體貼","explanation":"指對人充滿愛意、關懷和耐心，表現得溫柔體貼；就像對柔軟而需要照料的東西小心呵護。","examples":[{"en":"She was tender with the frightened child.","zh":"她溫柔地照顧那個受驚的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His tender care helped his father recover.","zh":"他體貼的照料幫助父親康復。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tender","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f1996a7cda48bca0dc87","word":"tennis","forms":["tennis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fe68da28ed82df36","term":"tennis","forms":["tennis","tennises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網球運動","explanation":"指兩人單打或四人雙打時，隔著球網輪流用球拍擊球的運動；這是最主要、最常見的含義。","examples":[{"en":"She plays tennis every Saturday.","zh":"她每週六都打網球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tennis is popular at this club.","zh":"網球在這傢俱樂部很受歡迎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tennis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4fee8075f3c00b3f","term":"tennis","forms":["tennis","tennises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一場網球比賽","explanation":"指網球運動中的一場比賽或對局；這種用法能在舊式或特定語境中見到，但現代日常英語裡不如運動義自然。","examples":[{"en":"They watched tennis after lunch.","zh":"他們午飯後觀看了一場網球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their afternoon of tennis ended when the courts closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tennis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-deb8cc25f01429d62605","word":"tense","forms":["tense"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8cc7ae3d8e5dca6","term":"tense","forms":["tense","tenser","tensest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體或精神緊張的","explanation":"身體或精神像被拉緊一樣，不能自然放鬆；加班、壓力、擔心或期待都可能讓人處於這種狀態。","examples":[{"en":"You look tense—take a few deep breaths.","zh":"你看起來很緊張，做幾次深呼吸吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All the overtime has made her tense and irritable.","zh":"加班讓她變得緊張易怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tense","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ae1b844e0e937a4ab40","word":"tension","forms":["tension"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-08dbfcff55db42b6","term":"tension","forms":["tension","tensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對立造成的緊張關係","explanation":"指兩方或多方之間存在相互對抗、難以協調的力量，因此關係處於繃緊狀態。它可以指國家、團體或個人之間的矛盾，不一定已經發展成公開衝突。","examples":[{"en":"There is growing tension between the two teams.","zh":"兩支隊伍之間的緊張關係越來越嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting helped reduce tension between the neighbors.","zh":"這次會議幫助緩和了鄰居之間的緊張關係。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0d1b3431438ac6b","term":"tension","forms":["tension","tensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緊張的心理狀態","explanation":"指人因為壓力、擔心或即將發生的事情而身心繃緊的狀態。它像被拉緊的繩子一樣，強調壓力停留在身體或情緒中。","examples":[{"en":"She could feel the tension in her shoulders before the interview.","zh":"面試前，她能感覺到肩膀的緊繃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A short walk helped him release some tension.","zh":"散了會兒步幫助他釋放了一些壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-470f6ee06bb99c73","term":"tension","forms":["tension","tensions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事中的懸念和緊張氣氛","explanation":"指電影、小說或戲劇透過危險、未知結果或衝突製造的緊張感，讓觀眾或讀者想繼續看下去。這裡的“拉緊”不是人物一定在緊張，而是整個敘事氣氛被拉緊了。","examples":[{"en":"The director builds tension by keeping the killer off screen.","zh":"導演讓兇手始終不出現在畫面中，以此製造懸念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each unexplained disappearance adds to the novel's mounting tension.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tension","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a9810cb71316c9a03e5","word":"tent","forms":["tent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-46710c8fad445cf9","term":"tent","forms":["tent","tents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"帳篷","explanation":"用帆布等結實布料和杆子支起來的行動式住所，通常用於露營，也可以臨時遮風避雨。","examples":[{"en":"We put up our tent beside the lake before sunset.","zh":"我們在日落前把帳篷搭在了湖邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children spent the night in a small tent in the backyard.","zh":"孩子們在後院的一頂小帳篷裡過了一夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e5bd0feb6a233ac79e9","word":"tentative","forms":["tentative"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd16d71922056a5a","term":"tentative","forms":["tentative","more tentative","most tentative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"暫定的；不確定的","explanation":"表示目前只是一個暫時判斷或安排，之後仍可能改變。就像伸腳試路時還沒有完全確認方向，說話或計劃也因此留有餘地。","examples":[{"en":"Our tentative meeting date is Friday, but it may change.","zh":"我們暫定的會議日期是星期五，但可能會改變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave a tentative answer because she needed to check the figures.","zh":"她給出了一個不確定的回答，因為她需要核對數字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tentative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-569e44e68689b577","term":"tentative","forms":["tentative","more tentative","most tentative"],"pos":"adj","zh":"試驗性的；試探性的","explanation":"表示某事是為了試一試、觀察效果而進行的，還不是最終定型的做法。它和“嘗試”這一核心畫面相連：先做一個試驗，再根據結果決定下一步。","examples":[{"en":"The team agreed on a tentative approach and planned to review it after a month.","zh":"團隊同意先採用一種試驗性做法，並計劃一個月後再評估。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He gave the unfamiliar switch a tentative push.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tentative","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-599f7703547e9c8e980f","word":"term","forms":["term"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e828f4f04989d547","term":"term","forms":["term","terms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"期限；一段時間","explanation":"指被劃定出來的一段時間，或某項安排持續的期限，例如租約、服務或貸款的有效期。","examples":[{"en":"The lease has a term of two years.","zh":"這份租約的期限是兩年。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can cancel the service at the end of the term.","zh":"你可以在期限結束時取消這項服務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/term","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d7f50d269297d83","term":"term","forms":["term","terms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合同條款；條件","explanation":"指合同中規定雙方必須遵守的條件或承諾；這些條款劃出了雙方可以做什麼、必須做什麼的範圍。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the terms before you accept the offer.","zh":"接受這份提議前，請先閱讀條款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both sides agreed to the terms of the contract.","zh":"雙方同意了合同條款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/term","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-afbe5e755f18f6e1","term":"term","forms":["term","terms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"術語；名稱","explanation":"指用來命名某個概念的詞或短語，尤其是專業領域中的專門說法；它像是給概念劃界後貼上的名稱。","examples":[{"en":"“Cloud computing” is a common term in technology.","zh":"“雲端計算”是科技領域的常用術語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What is the term for this kind of agreement?","zh":"這種協議的名稱是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/term","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e686af7bdcc5ae005a2","word":"terminal","forms":["terminal"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2bebdb6d3ef819e5","term":"terminal","forms":["terminal","more terminal","most terminal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"致命的；不可治癒而將導致死亡的","explanation":"指疾病或病情已經發展到會導致死亡的階段，核心仍是“走到了生命的盡頭”。","examples":[{"en":"The doctors said that his cancer was terminal.","zh":"醫生說他的癌症已到了致命階段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is receiving care for a terminal illness.","zh":"她正在接受針對致命疾病的護理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terminal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-86da15578042d6ef","term":"terminal","forms":["terminal","terminals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機場航站樓","explanation":"機場中供旅客辦理登機、到達或轉乘，並通往飛機登機設施的建築物；它是地面旅程與飛行旅程相接的終點設施。","examples":[{"en":"Please meet me outside Terminal 3.","zh":"請在三號航站樓外面等我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We arrived at the terminal two hours before the flight.","zh":"我們在航班起飛前兩小時到達了航站樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terminal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b366de0a68dd69fd","term":"terminal","forms":["terminal","terminals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵路終點站","explanation":"鐵路線路開始或結束的車站，即“這條線走到盡頭的地方”。","examples":[{"en":"The train stopped at the terminal after midnight.","zh":"火車在午夜後停靠了終點站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train reached the terminal just before midnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terminal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5151c409d0477e1a","term":"terminal","forms":["terminal","terminals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機終端","explanation":"供人向計算機或通訊系統輸入資料、檢視資料的裝置，通常帶有鍵盤和文字顯示屏；它是人與系統相連的操作端點。","examples":[{"en":"The students used a terminal to access the library database.","zh":"學生們用計算機終端訪問圖書館資料庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please enter your password at the terminal.","zh":"請在終端上輸入密碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terminal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3ff758e26dd919e9e8d5","word":"terrace","forms":["terrace"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-81831470771e7848","term":"terrace","forms":["terrace","terraces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築頂層平臺","explanation":"指建築物或公寓最高一層的平坦開放區域，通常比普通房間更適合戶外活動。它是“建築物上伸出的平坦檯面”這一核心形象的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"We had breakfast on the terrace overlooking the sea.","zh":"我們在能俯瞰大海的露臺上吃了早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apartment has a sunny terrace on the top floor.","zh":"這套公寓頂層有一個陽光充足的露臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73d9b8efc8ba9c04","term":"terrace","forms":["terrace","terraces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築外的平臺","explanation":"指從建築物向外伸出的平坦平臺，可以連線房間，也可以供人站立、休息或活動。","examples":[{"en":"They moved the chairs onto the terrace for the party.","zh":"他們把椅子搬到外平臺上參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow terrace ran along the back of the house.","zh":"房子後面有一條狹長的平臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0fbdc5e6c0e5043","term":"terrace","forms":["terrace","terraces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"梯田或人工平臺地","explanation":"指在斜坡上修出的平坦土臺，常常一層接一層，用於耕種、休閒或種植；也可泛指河邊等處較高而平坦的土地。這裡仍然是“把坡地變成平坦檯面”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers grow tea on terraces cut into the hillside.","zh":"農民在山坡上修出的梯田裡種茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel garden is arranged in several terraces.","zh":"這家酒店的花園分成了幾層平臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fcfebb572f03efe3c548","word":"terrible","forms":["terrible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-db8c46be005533de","term":"terrible","forms":["terrible","terribler","more terrible","terriblest","most terrible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可怕的；令人恐懼的","explanation":"指某人或某事物會引起強烈的恐懼、驚慌或警惕，是“可怕到讓人想躲開”的基本含義。","examples":[{"en":"A terrible storm destroyed several houses.","zh":"一場可怕的暴風雨摧毀了幾棟房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had a terrible nightmare last night.","zh":"她昨晚做了一個可怕的噩夢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94cfae79e5a43fa6","term":"terrible","forms":["terrible","terribler","more terrible","terriblest","most terrible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人不快的；糟糕的","explanation":"在日常評價中，terrible 可從“令人害怕”弱化為“讓人非常不舒服或不滿意”，例如食物難吃、天氣惡劣或經歷令人討厭。","examples":[{"en":"The service at that restaurant was terrible.","zh":"那家餐館的服務糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had terrible weather during the trip.","zh":"旅行期間天氣糟糕透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-83e24fc2ae14e9bc","term":"terrible","forms":["terrible","terribler","more terrible","terriblest","most terrible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"很差的；差勁的","explanation":"指能力、表現或質量非常差，是日常口語裡很常見的“糟糕、差勁”用法；它可以把負面評價強調到很強。","examples":[{"en":"I'm a terrible cook, so we usually eat out.","zh":"我做飯很差，所以我們通常出去吃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel offered terrible service throughout our stay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9a21ba92fdb961082a53","word":"terrific","forms":["terrific"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8ff71e4ef5a0ef5","term":"terrific","forms":["terrific","more terrific","most terrific"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極好的；棒極了的","explanation":"這是現代最重要的用法，表示好得令人驚歎，可以稱讚人、表現、計劃或經歷；它正是從“令人震撼”發展出的褒義。","examples":[{"en":"She's a terrific tennis player.","zh":"她是一名非常出色的網球運動員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a terrific time at the concert.","zh":"我們在音樂會上玩得特別開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrific","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6d9ccfbe60a8132","term":"terrific","forms":["terrific","more terrific","most terrific"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極強的；驚人的","explanation":"這裡表示程度大得驚人，常用於速度、力量、聲勢等，不一定表達好壞評價；核心感覺仍是“強烈到令人震撼”。","examples":[{"en":"The car came around the bend at a terrific speed.","zh":"那輛車以驚人的速度拐過彎來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A terrific blast shattered windows across the square.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrific","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d70f695f0220d61c6da5","word":"terrify","forms":["terrify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f539001ab19c1b49","term":"terrify","forms":["terrify","terrifies","terrifying","terrified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使極度害怕","explanation":"指某人或某事讓另一個人產生非常強烈的恐懼，彷彿恐懼被直接壓到對方身上。這是 terrify 最核心、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden noise terrified the children.","zh":"突然的聲響把孩子們嚇壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was terrified of walking home alone at night.","zh":"她非常害怕晚上獨自走回家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fd84422fd8db5e4","term":"terrify","forms":["terrify","terrifies","terrifying","terrified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"威脅、震懾","explanation":"指透過威脅、武力、強大氣勢或令人畏懼的行為使別人不敢反抗。它仍然以“把恐懼壓給對方”為核心，但重點從恐懼感轉向震懾效果。","examples":[{"en":"The gang tried to terrify local businesses into paying them.","zh":"這個團伙試圖用恐嚇手段逼當地商家給他們錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The raiders terrified the villagers into surrendering their supplies.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b085a22402bf6ff4dcf9","word":"territory","forms":["territory"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-158e380a0fa9591d","term":"territory","forms":["territory","territories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大片土地；區域","explanation":"指一大片土地或較大的區域，可以是一個國家、地區或行政區，也可以只強調這片範圍本身。它是“某種地盤或範圍”這一核心概念最一般的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The expedition crossed a vast territory before reaching the coast.","zh":"這支探險隊穿過一大片土地後才到達海岸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Much of the territory is covered by forest.","zh":"這片區域的大部分被森林覆蓋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/territory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-62bf23ed8bad13ea","term":"territory","forms":["territory","territories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政治控制下的領土","explanation":"指某個國家、政府或地方機構實際控制的地理範圍，邊界主要由政治權力決定，而不只是由河流、山脊等自然地貌決定。這是“有人劃界並管理的地盤”這一核心概念的正式政治用法。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries are negotiating over disputed territory.","zh":"兩國正在就有爭議的領土進行談判。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The army withdrew from the territory at the end of the year.","zh":"軍隊在年底撤出了這片領土。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/territory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd778891dbe86ede8cdb","word":"terror","forms":["terror"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-076bb6c8ea3f8e23","term":"terror","forms":["terror","terrors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈的恐懼","explanation":"指強烈到令人發抖、失去鎮定的恐懼，是這個詞最核心的意思；它比普通的不安或擔心更猛烈。","examples":[{"en":"She woke up in terror when she heard the window break.","zh":"她聽到窗戶破裂的聲音後，驚恐地醒了過來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child has a terror of deep water.","zh":"這個孩子非常害怕深水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a2398352fb7e3d7","term":"terror","forms":["terror","terrors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"造成恐懼的特質或恐怖感","explanation":"指某個故事、場景或行為中使人感到恐懼的力量和氛圍，也就是“恐怖感”本身，而不一定是某個具體的怪物。","examples":[{"en":"The film creates terror through silence rather than violence.","zh":"這部電影不是靠暴力，而是靠寂靜營造恐怖感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The terror of the dark passage made her hesitate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terror","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36f4662ddaee362931df","word":"terrorism","forms":["terrorism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f30f406bc34e7751","term":"terrorism","forms":["terrorism","terrorisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"以政治目標為目的的恐怖暴力","explanation":"指個人或組織透過對人或財產施加非法暴力來製造恐懼，從而實現政治目標；“把恐懼變成武器”是這個現代核心義的關鍵。","examples":[{"en":"The government increased security measures to counter terrorism.","zh":"政府加強了安全措施，以打擊恐怖主義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Terrorism threatens civilians and public institutions.","zh":"恐怖主義威脅平民和公共機構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrorism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a4648096e98e5d5","term":"terrorism","forms":["terrorism","terrorisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廣義的系統性恐嚇","explanation":"在較寬的用法中，terrorism 不一定嚴格指達到政治目標的襲擊，也可以指持續、有組織地用暴力或威脅壓迫他人的做法；核心仍然是把恐懼當作控制手段。","examples":[{"en":"The workers described the constant threats as a kind of terrorism.","zh":"工人們把這些持續不斷的威脅稱為一種恐怖主義式的恐嚇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The regime maintained control through systematic terrorism.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrorism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a4c7815e0ca14c6d3d3e","word":"terrorist","forms":["terrorist"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45dbcf439ee4ba48","term":"terrorist","forms":["terrorist"],"pos":"adj","zh":"恐怖主義的；恐怖分子的","explanation":"指與恐怖主義、恐怖分子或他們實施的暴力行動有關的事物，例如襲擊、組織、威脅或同盟。它不是泛指“很可怕”，而是帶有政治暴力這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The government warned about a possible terrorist attack.","zh":"政府警告說可能會發生恐怖主義襲擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report examines links between several terrorist groups.","zh":"這份報告調查了幾個恐怖組織之間的聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrorist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9f86d081884c7d659a2f","word":"test","forms":["test"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e7550b6135391db","term":"test","forms":["test","tests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考驗；挑戰","explanation":"指需要經受並克服的困難或挑戰，重點是看一個人的能力、耐力或決心能否經得住考驗。","examples":[{"en":"Climbing that mountain was a real test of our stamina.","zh":"爬那座山真正考驗了我們的耐力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long journey will be a test of her patience.","zh":"這段漫長的旅程將考驗她的耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/test","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f060361e3b3070ad","term":"test","forms":["test","tests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"考試","explanation":"指用題目或任務檢查學生掌握知識和技能的正式考核。","examples":[{"en":"I have a math test on Friday.","zh":"我星期五有一場數學考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied all night for the test.","zh":"她為了這場考試學習了一整夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/test","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9bad785905bf48a0","term":"test","forms":["test","tests","testing","tested","testest","testedst","testeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"考驗；使承受壓力","explanation":"把人或事物置於困難、壓力或挑戰中，看它能否經受住，這正是“放上考驗臺”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The steep climb tested everyone's patience.","zh":"陡峭的攀登考驗了每個人的耐心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This job will test your ability to stay calm.","zh":"這份工作將考驗你保持冷靜的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/test","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b6dbf616476649a","term":"test","forms":["test","tests","testing","tested","testest","testedst","testeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"檢驗；驗證","explanation":"透過實驗、證據或某種標準檢查事物是否真實、可靠、有效或質量合格。","examples":[{"en":"The researchers tested whether the new material was safe.","zh":"研究人員檢驗了這種新材料是否安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to test the alarm before opening the building.","zh":"我們需要在開放大樓前測試警報器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/test","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9b29640175f1bcb15f3","word":"testify","forms":["testify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7e0e4b7398e3bea","term":"testify","forms":["testify","testifies","testifying","testified","testifiest","testifiedst","testifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在宣誓下作證","explanation":"指人在法庭或其他正式調查中宣誓後陳述自己知道的事實，並提供證據或證詞。這個意思帶有明確的法律或正式場合色彩，常常涉及支援或指控某一方。","examples":[{"en":"She agreed to testify against the man who had threatened her.","zh":"她同意出庭指證那個威脅過她的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness testified in court under oath.","zh":"證人在法庭上宣誓作證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/testify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ff0f9b3de39ca5b","term":"testify","forms":["testify","testifies","testifying","testified","testifiest","testifiedst","testifieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"根據所知或信念作陳述","explanation":"指人根據自己的親身經歷、觀察或信仰，鄭重地說出自己認為真實的事情；不一定發生在法庭上，但仍比普通的“說”更有見證或鄭重陳述的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Several residents testified that the road had been unsafe for years.","zh":"幾位居民都鄭重說明，這條路多年來一直不安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several former employees testified to his generosity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/testify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-982d9e3eb996f559e633","word":"text","forms":["text"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3c5a1d635e42360c","term":"text","forms":["text","texts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"文字；文字","explanation":"指寫下來、打出來或顯示出來的一組字母、符號、詞語或句子，是“把語言織成可讀形式”的基本文字材料。","examples":[{"en":"Please read the text carefully before answering.","zh":"回答前請仔細閱讀這段文字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The image is clear, but the text is too small to read.","zh":"影象很清楚，但文字太小，看不清。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/text","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa992a63fd4e063e","term":"text","forms":["text","texts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簡訊","explanation":"指手機或其他通訊裝置傳送的一條簡短文字訊息，是“織出一小段文字並傳給別人”的現代用法。","examples":[{"en":"I got a text from Maya this morning.","zh":"我今天早上收到瑪雅的一條簡訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Send me a text when you arrive.","zh":"你到了以後給我發條簡訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/text","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16a9b27cd7bdf707d7d1","word":"textbook","forms":["textbook"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2c72e894f4a7463a","term":"textbook","forms":["textbook","textbooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教科書；教材","explanation":"指圍繞某一學科系統編排的正式教學用書，通常供學校或大學課程使用。","examples":[{"en":"The professor wrote a new textbook on environmental science.","zh":"這位教授編寫了一本新的環境科學教材。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please bring your mathematics textbook to class tomorrow.","zh":"請明天把數學教科書帶到課堂上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/textbook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96663ba66fcd63665423","word":"textile","forms":["textile"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27a17cdb4b5f7a2e","term":"textile","forms":["textile","textiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紡織品；織物","explanation":"textile 指把纖維交錯織在一起形成的材料，範圍不只包括衣料，也包括地毯以及用於工程的土工織物等。","examples":[{"en":"The company makes textiles for clothing and carpets.","zh":"這家公司生產用於服裝和地毯的紡織品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These geotextiles help prevent soil erosion.","zh":"這些土工織物有助於防止水土流失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/textile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-38a3c50b7c1f9635ef15","word":"texture","forms":["texture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac8255db4df976af","term":"texture","forms":["texture","textures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"表面質感；觸感","explanation":"指物體或材料表面給人的感覺和外觀特徵，如光滑、粗糙、柔軟、顆粒感等。它既可以說實際摸到的觸感，也可以說肉眼看到的表面效果。","examples":[{"en":"The soup had a smooth, creamy texture.","zh":"這道湯口感順滑而濃稠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I like the rough texture of this handmade paper.","zh":"我喜歡這張手工紙粗糙的質感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/texture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5f249e8ff5973c9","term":"texture","forms":["texture","textures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藝術作品的層次感","explanation":"指繪畫、音樂等作品中，各個部分相互組合、交織後形成的豐富感和結構層次。這裡不一定是可以摸到的表面，而是把“交織成的質感”引申到藝術效果。","examples":[{"en":"The painting gains texture from the layers of thick paint.","zh":"厚重顏料一層層疊加，讓這幅畫有了豐富的層次感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The strings add texture to the song's simple melody.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/texture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7383711c1b05e72a1edd","word":"than","forms":["than"],"officialPos":"conj./prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a7428cf871db0f2","term":"than","forms":["than"],"pos":"prep","zh":"比；與……相比","explanation":"than把比較物件接到前面的比較表達上：前面說明某人或某物“更……、更少……”時，than引出拿來衡量的另一方。可以把它想成同一把尺子上的第二個刻度。","examples":[{"en":"This book is more useful than the old one.","zh":"這本書比那本舊的更有用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We received fewer complaints than last month.","zh":"我們收到的投訴比上個月少。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/than","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e67fd73a84918e64c84f","word":"thank","forms":["thank"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-55315ac641acd431","term":"thank","forms":["thank","thanks","thanking","thanked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感謝；向……表達謝意","explanation":"把對方給予的幫助、禮物或善意以語言表達出來，表示自己很感激。這是 thank 最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I thanked Maya for helping me move.","zh":"我感謝瑪雅幫我搬家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thank you for the thoughtful gift.","zh":"謝謝你送我這麼貼心的禮物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-855964c114e8f35a","term":"thank","forms":["thank","thanks","thanking","thanked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"請不要……；最好別……","explanation":"在特定將來時句式中，thank you 並不是真的表示感謝，而是用禮貌外表包裝命令、警告或不滿，意思接近“請你不要做某事”。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll thank you not to interrupt while I’m speaking.","zh":"我講話時請你不要打斷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I will thank you to keep your opinions about my appearance to yourself.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thank","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74a1e0449315b6f09c83","word":"thankful","forms":["thankful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bab567dbbb6772a8","term":"thankful","forms":["thankful","more thankful","most thankful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"感到感謝的","explanation":"指因為別人提供了幫助、自己得到了好處，或事情有了好的結果而心懷感謝。它強調一種內心狀態，常常是在說明“對什麼或對誰感到感謝”。","examples":[{"en":"We’re thankful for the support our neighbors gave us.","zh":"我們很感謝鄰居給我們的支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m thankful that everyone arrived safely.","zh":"我很慶幸大家都平安到達，也對此心懷感謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thankful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e7fc0236af43df93406","word":"that","forms":["that"],"officialPos":"conj./pron./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35f6baa1249fbb94","term":"that","forms":["that"],"pos":"adv","zh":"那麼；到那種程度","explanation":"這裡的 that 指向一個已經確定的程度，意思是“達到那樣的長度、大小或程度”，不是指某個具體物件。","examples":[{"en":"The shelf is that wide, so it will fit in the alcove.","zh":"架子就那麼寬，所以能放進壁龕裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I didn't realize the lake was that deep.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c9f4dea1d01c17f","term":"that","forms":["that","those"],"pos":"det","zh":"那個；那件","explanation":"that 放在名詞前，指向離說話者較遠、時間上較遠，或上下文中已經確定的物件，相當於“那個……”。","examples":[{"en":"That jacket by the window is mine.","zh":"窗邊的那件夾克是我的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please pass me that blue folder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f4177b10c6d5d0e4","term":"that","forms":["that","those"],"pos":"pron","zh":"那個；那件事","explanation":"that 單獨使用時，指向語境中已經明確、通常較遠或需要和 this 區分的事物、人或想法，相當於“那個、那件事”。","examples":[{"en":"That is the restaurant I told you about.","zh":"那就是我跟你提過的那家餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That is the house where I grew up.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-47901fa76f881db7","term":"that","forms":["that","those"],"pos":"pron","zh":"關係從句中的“……的那個”","explanation":"that 把後面的說明接回前面已經提到的名詞，表示“那個……的東西、那個人或那件事”。它可以指人，也可以指物。","examples":[{"en":"She found the keys that she had lost.","zh":"她找到了自己丟失的鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The neighbor that helped us has moved away.","zh":"幫助過我們的那位鄰居搬走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/that","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9776d7ddf459c9ad5b0","word":"the","forms":["the"],"officialPos":"art.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"the","forms":["the"],"pos":"art.","zh":"這個；那個；特定事物前的定冠詞","examples":[{"en":"Please close the door behind you.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The book on the table belongs to my sister.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-3121771b9c5973e0f089","word":"theater","forms":["theater"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-198755a6f2acde01","term":"theater","forms":["theater","theaters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劇院；演出場所","explanation":"指有舞臺和座位、供觀眾觀看戲劇、音樂演出或其他公開活動的建築或場所，是 theater 最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We arrived at the theater early to find our seats.","zh":"我們提前到了劇院，好找到自己的座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater was packed for the opening night.","zh":"首演之夜劇院裡座無虛席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00f7c98257f5d3d8","term":"theater","forms":["theater","theaters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"行動領域；戰區","explanation":"把劇院這個“行動展開的舞臺”引申為某項行動發生的地區，尤其常指戰爭中的戰區。","examples":[{"en":"The region became a major theater of conflict.","zh":"這個地區成了主要的衝突區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The regiment served in the Pacific theater.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theater","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2daf5a7240150afc0b22","word":"theft","forms":["theft"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89aed940cdeda1e2","term":"theft","forms":["theft","thefts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偷竊；盜竊案","explanation":"指未經物主允許拿走其財物的行為；在具體語境中，也可指發生的一宗偷竊案件。","examples":[{"en":"The theft of company data caused serious problems.","zh":"公司資料被盜造成了嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police are investigating a theft at the museum.","zh":"警方正在調查博物館裡的一宗盜竊案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theft","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3cb8201e7ff1e7777446","word":"theme","forms":["theme"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8a22062efbc9fbf","term":"theme","forms":["theme","themes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主題；話題","explanation":"theme 是談話、文章、電影、繪畫等所圍繞的中心內容或思想，也可以泛指正在討論的話題。它像一條把作品或討論各部分串起來的主線。","examples":[{"en":"The main theme of the film is forgiveness.","zh":"這部電影的主題是寬恕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Climate change was the central theme of her speech.","zh":"氣候變化是她演講的中心主題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60b5741f9dff8ad2","term":"theme","forms":["theme","themes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"反覆出現的思想或意象","explanation":"theme 也指作品中不斷回來的思想、形象或表達方式。它不是一次出現的細節，而是反覆加強作品主線的元素。","examples":[{"en":"Loneliness is a recurring theme in her novels.","zh":"孤獨是她小說中反覆出現的主題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Images of water develop the theme of renewal throughout the poem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theme","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21af6f1260f927f5b9b3","word":"then","forms":["then"],"officialPos":"adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-edfeb02d1529d667","term":"then","forms":["then"],"pos":"adj","zh":"當時的","explanation":"放在名詞前，表示這個人或事物在所說的那個時間點具有該身份、關係或狀態。","examples":[{"en":"My then manager later became a close friend.","zh":"我當時的經理後來成了我的密友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The then mayor opposed closing the market.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/then","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a15b373b53d47b83","term":"then","forms":["then"],"pos":"adv","zh":"那時","explanation":"指已經提到的某個過去時間，或指將來某個已經設定的時間點。","examples":[{"en":"I was living in London then.","zh":"那時我住在倫敦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report should be ready by then.","zh":"到那時報告應該準備好了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/then","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9634ae11fb25450c","term":"then","forms":["then"],"pos":"adv","zh":"然後","explanation":"表示一個動作或事件緊接著另一個動作或事件發生，沿著時間線向後推進。","examples":[{"en":"Turn off the oven, then let the cake cool.","zh":"關掉烤箱，然後讓蛋糕冷卻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She checked the address and then called a taxi.","zh":"她核對了地址，然後叫了一輛計程車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/then","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-03104a6b003133ce","term":"then","forms":["then"],"pos":"adv","zh":"那麼、就","explanation":"在條件或假設之後推出結果，相當於“如果前面的情況成立，那麼後面的結果就成立”。","examples":[{"en":"If you are tired, then take a short break.","zh":"如果你累了，那就休息一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"If the store is closed, then we will come back tomorrow.","zh":"如果商店關門了，那我們明天再來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/then","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a567db63a3f2b5d84983","word":"theology","forms":["theology"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19e3743f5b0a7d55","term":"theology","forms":["theology","theologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"神學；宗教思想研究","explanation":"指系統研究神、諸神、宗教信仰以及這些信仰是否真實、合理的學科。它把“信什麼”放到研究桌上，考察相關的思想、理由和解釋。","examples":[{"en":"She studied theology at university before becoming a minister.","zh":"她在成為牧師之前曾在大學學習神學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book examines the theology of forgiveness.","zh":"這本書探討寬恕的神學思想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ee7356ac6becfa9","term":"theology","forms":["theology","theologies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體的宗教信念","explanation":"指某一宗教或宗教傳統中關於某個問題的一條具體信念。它是研究桌上的一個明確結論，而不是整個宗教或完整的神學學科。","examples":[{"en":"They hold a theology that welcomes people from every background.","zh":"他們堅持一種歡迎各種背景人士的宗教信念。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her theology of suffering changed after the accident.","zh":"事故之後，她對苦難的宗教理解發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theology","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b49d04a79c55454d25c","word":"theoretical","forms":["theoretical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee9d201506ed5e03","term":"theoretical","forms":["theoretical","more theoretical","most theoretical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"理論上的；抽象的","explanation":"指與理論或抽象模型有關，主要靠概念和推理來說明問題，還不是直接從實踐或實驗結果中得出的結論。它的核心畫面是“先在紙上搭好模型”，模型可以很嚴謹，但與實際情況之間仍可能有距離。","examples":[{"en":"The idea is theoretically possible, but it would be difficult to put into practice.","zh":"這個想法在理論上是可行的，但實施起來會很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course combines theoretical knowledge with practical training.","zh":"這門課程把理論知識和實踐訓練結合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theoretical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4397b4805e00143d361","word":"theory","forms":["theory"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d187f76a99971149","term":"theory","forms":["theory","theories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"解釋並預測現象的科學理論","explanation":"指由觀察、實驗或推理支援的一套連貫觀點，能夠解釋已經發現的事實，還能對尚未觀察到的現象作出預測。這是學習科學、社會科學和其他知識領域時最重要的義項。","examples":[{"en":"The theory explains why the same treatment works differently for different patients.","zh":"這個理論解釋了為什麼同一種治療對不同患者的效果會不同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Researchers tested the theory against data from several countries.","zh":"研究人員用來自幾個國家的資料檢驗了這一理論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ee4367e6706e3ec","term":"theory","forms":["theory","theories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對事實或系統的概括說明","explanation":"指一套被認為能夠準確描述某個事件、系統或現象的觀點。它強調把許多事實整理成一個可理解的整體，是“理論”這一核心概念的較寬泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"The theory of language has changed over the past century.","zh":"過去一個世紀以來，語言理論發生了變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theory explains how continental plates move.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f78fe53a3f107b844ec9","word":"therapist","forms":["therapist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30271925c723df6b","term":"therapist","forms":["therapist","therapists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"治療師","explanation":"泛指提供治療或康復服務的專業人士，幫助人處理身體、心理或其他健康問題。具體是哪一類治療師，要由上下文決定。","examples":[{"en":"She decided to see a therapist after months of stress.","zh":"連續幾個月承受壓力後，她決定去找治療師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The therapist helped him build a plan for recovery.","zh":"這位治療師幫助他制定了康復計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/therapist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ca58a9d445c6872","term":"therapist","forms":["therapist","therapists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理治療師","explanation":"特指透過交談等心理治療方法，幫助來訪者處理情緒、壓力和心理問題的專業人士。這是日常英語中 therapist 很常見的具體含義。","examples":[{"en":"His therapist taught him ways to manage his anxiety.","zh":"他的心理治療師教他一些應對焦慮的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her therapist helped her manage recurring panic attacks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/therapist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4af009dcd561b8060a9e","word":"therapy","forms":["therapy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e623aee31a7d8931","term":"therapy","forms":["therapy","therapies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"治療；療法","explanation":"指在確定健康問題後，為改善、控制或治癒它而採用的治療方法或治療過程。它可以是藥物、訓練、護理或其他醫療手段，不限於某一種具體方法。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor recommended physical therapy for her injured knee.","zh":"醫生建議她為受傷的膝蓋接受物理治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He has been undergoing therapy for several months.","zh":"他已經接受治療好幾個月了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/therapy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fcb996ccdd61064f","term":"therapy","forms":["therapy","therapies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"療愈作用","explanation":"指某種活動、經歷或治療本身具有的安撫、修復和幫助恢復的力量。這裡強調的不是具體治療方案，而是它帶來的身心改善作用。","examples":[{"en":"For her, gardening is a kind of therapy after a stressful day.","zh":"對她來說，忙碌一天後園藝是一種療愈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Making pottery became his therapy during a difficult divorce.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/therapy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e244f187f696561d5fd7","word":"there","forms":["there"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-afae7710b5ced4ee","term":"there","forms":["there"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在那裡","explanation":"指離說話人有一定距離、已經提到或能從語境中確定的地點，意思是“在那裡”。","examples":[{"en":"I used to live there when I was a student.","zh":"我上學時曾經住在那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the keys there on the table.","zh":"請把鑰匙放在那裡，也就是桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/there","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-63b89d0e07c7a0ee","term":"there","forms":["there","theres"],"pos":"noun","zh":"那個地方","explanation":"把“那裡”當作一個地點來指代，通常是前文已經提到或雙方都知道的地方。","examples":[{"en":"The bus will take us from here to there in twenty minutes.","zh":"公交車二十分鐘就能把我們從這裡帶到那裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The distance from here to there is considerable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/there","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-818853f7cd4b4d46ad36","word":"thereafter","forms":["thereafter"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3162be0a53591ad","term":"thereafter","forms":["thereafter"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從那以後；此後","explanation":"先發生一個明確的事件，thereafter 指從那個事件之後開始，後面的情況一直按這個時間順序展開。","examples":[{"en":"She moved to London and thereafter worked as a teacher.","zh":"她搬到倫敦，從那以後一直當老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement was signed; thereafter, no further changes were allowed.","zh":"協議簽署後，此後不再允許作任何修改。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thereafter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e43c3a238333f1f65088","word":"thereby","forms":["thereby"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28cb96482a631d1f","term":"thereby","forms":["thereby"],"pos":"adv","zh":"由此；從而；藉此","explanation":"指透過前面提到的行動、辦法或事實，產生後面的結果；重點是“藉此而達到某種結果”，而不只是先後發生。","examples":[{"en":"I enrolled in Old English classes and thereby learned much about Germanic languages.","zh":"我報名學習古英語，從而對日耳曼語族有了更多瞭解。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She saved the document regularly, thereby avoiding the loss of her work.","zh":"她定期儲存檔案，從而避免了工作內容丟失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thereby","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bae0db182974fd465595","word":"therefore","forms":["therefore"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7a6473d0d941017","term":"therefore","forms":["therefore"],"pos":"adv","zh":"因此；所以","explanation":"表示“由前面所說的原因或事實，結果就是這樣”，把前文和後面的結果或結論連成一條因果箭頭。","examples":[{"en":"The road was closed; therefore, we took a different route.","zh":"這條路封閉了，所以我們改走了另一條路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had prepared carefully and therefore felt confident.","zh":"她準備得很充分，因此信心十足。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/therefore","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8744bbc75301096d7ff2","word":"thermometer","forms":["thermometer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-788943814d2ecaed","term":"thermometer","forms":["thermometer","thermometers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溫度計","explanation":"一種用來測量溫度並顯示讀數的儀器，可以測量空氣、人體或其他物體的冷熱程度。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse used a thermometer to check the child's temperature.","zh":"護士用溫度計測量孩子的體溫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thermometer outside says it is five degrees below zero.","zh":"外面的溫度計顯示氣溫是零下五度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thermometer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b808e156d18d1cecdcc1","word":"these","forms":["these"],"officialPos":"pron./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"these","forms":["these"],"pos":"pron./adj.","zh":"這些","examples":[{"en":"These are the keys you were looking for.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"These shoes are too small for me.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-2863229379aa76de9362","word":"thesis","forms":["thesis"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-088cdfd5f9f002e3","term":"thesis","forms":["thesis","theses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"論題；主張","explanation":"指一個明確擺出來、並且要用理由和證據加以支援的觀點或命題，常是文章、演講或討論的中心主張。","examples":[{"en":"The book's central thesis is that education should be available to everyone.","zh":"這本書的核心論點是教育應當面向所有人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She presented a clear thesis and supported it with strong evidence.","zh":"她提出了明確的論點，並用有力的證據加以支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thesis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7747f989ce69ca74","term":"thesis","forms":["thesis","theses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學位論文","explanation":"指學生為取得學位而完成並正式提交的較長學術研究論文，內容通常圍繞一個具體研究問題展開。","examples":[{"en":"He is writing his master's thesis on renewable energy.","zh":"他正在撰寫關於可再生能源的碩士論文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He defended his doctoral thesis before an international panel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thesis","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b60165c15a286434acf","word":"they (them, their, theirs, themselves)","forms":["they"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f05c745aea5a021","term":"they","forms":["they","themself"],"pos":"pron","zh":"他們；她們；它們","explanation":"they 最基本的用法是指前文已經提到的兩個人或更多人、動物或事物，相當於“他們、她們、它們”。它把這些物件作為“那一方”整體來指。","examples":[{"en":"Maya and Luis said they would meet us after lunch.","zh":"瑪雅和路易斯說他們午飯後會來見我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are waiting outside with their tickets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/they","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9f054e653b5111ce","term":"they","forms":["they","themself"],"pos":"pron","zh":"某人（性別未知或不強調）","explanation":"當只知道有一個人，卻不知道、不需要說明或不想說明其性別時，they 可以指這個單數的人。這種用法也常用於尊重不使用傳統性別代詞的人。","examples":[{"en":"A customer left their umbrella, so I hope they come back for it.","zh":"有位顧客落下了雨傘，我希望他或她能回來取。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone left their umbrella; perhaps they'll return soon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/they","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b1291e7ed8a6f3e8aa8","word":"thick","forms":["thick"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba55b2b95a34ab58","term":"thick","forms":["thick","thicker","thickest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"厚的","explanation":"指物體從一個表面到相對表面的距離較大，也就是在最小尺寸方向上很厚。這是 thick 最基礎的具體意義。","examples":[{"en":"This book has a thick cover.","zh":"這本書的封面很厚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore a thick wool coat in the snow.","zh":"她在下雪天穿了一件厚厚的羊毛外套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ab6b5ffe164213d","term":"thick","forms":["thick","thicker","thickest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"密集的","explanation":"指許多東西緊緊聚在一起，空隙很小，形成“擠得很滿”的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Thick bushes covered the sides of the path.","zh":"茂密的灌木覆蓋了小路兩旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The forest was thick with vines.","zh":"森林裡藤蔓密佈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8dd29add9992f7006f4d","word":"thief","forms":["thief"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de0e4f4f7179f57f","term":"thief","forms":["thief","thieves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"偷偷竊取他人財物的人","explanation":"這是最常見、最具體的畫面：一個人避開他人注意，不靠武力就把別人的財物拿走。它可以指偷錢包、商店商品等財物的人。","examples":[{"en":"The thief took her wallet while she was looking at the map.","zh":"她看地圖時，小偷拿走了她的錢包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A security camera caught the thief entering the shop at night.","zh":"監控攝像頭拍到了小偷夜裡進入商店的畫面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6621d552f9180d52","term":"thief","forms":["thief","thieves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"盜竊者；竊賊","explanation":"指實施盜竊的人，是對竊賊的泛稱；不論偷的是哪類財物，都可以用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"The thieves stole tools from several construction sites.","zh":"竊賊從幾個建築工地偷走了工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thief escaped with a bag of jewelry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thief","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8981a7d50d5581c0700a","word":"thigh","forms":["thigh"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aef0edf3a6fd9d7a","term":"thigh","forms":["thigh","thighs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的大腿","explanation":"指人體從髖部到膝蓋之間的腿部上段，是“上腿”這一整體部位。","examples":[{"en":"The child rested her head on her mother's thigh during the train journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"The cyclist strained a muscle in her thigh.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thigh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a01c755c5094eac9","term":"thigh","forms":["thigh","thighs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物對應的大腿部位；大腿肉","explanation":"也指動物腿上與人的大腿位置或作用相對應的部分，因此在買菜、做飯時可表示雞、火雞等動物的大腿肉。","examples":[{"en":"The butcher removed the bones from the turkey thighs before weighing them.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫修正"},{"en":"Roast the chicken thighs until the skin is crisp.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thigh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1a0dc227b5aa78f84008","word":"thin","forms":["thin"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-877f9c0155eeb27a","term":"thin","forms":["thin","thinner","thinnest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"薄的","explanation":"表示物體從一面到另一面的厚度很小，就像被拉開的薄膜。紙、金屬片、木板和覆蓋層都可以用這個詞形容。","examples":[{"en":"She wrote the note on a thin piece of paper.","zh":"她把便條寫在一張薄薄的紙上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The walls are too thin to block the noise.","zh":"牆太薄，擋不住噪音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43e7548dcd162a8f","term":"thin","forms":["thin","thinner","thinnest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"瘦的","explanation":"形容人的身體脂肪或肉少，表示身材瘦、苗條或消瘦，具體褒貶要由上下文決定。","examples":[{"en":"He was thin but strong from years of cycling.","zh":"他多年騎腳踏車，身材瘦但很強壯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child looks thin after being ill.","zh":"孩子生病後看起來瘦了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5de94d691ae3039a3f5d","word":"thing","forms":["thing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-97747919f9f26176","term":"thing","forms":["thing","things"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事物；事情","explanation":"指被看作獨立存在的任何物件、性質、想法或概念；這是 thing 最寬的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The most important thing is to stay calm.","zh":"最重要的事情是保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have a few things to discuss with you.","zh":"我有幾件事要和你討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ed079c650816176","term":"thing","forms":["thing","things"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個東西；一個個體","explanation":"指一個可以和其他物件分開的具體東西或獨立個體。","examples":[{"en":"There is one thing on the table that belongs to you.","zh":"桌上有一件東西是你的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put that heavy thing on the table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0fc714c72e63362","term":"thing","forms":["thing","things"],"pos":"noun","zh":"東西；用品","explanation":"複數 things 可指某人的隨身物品、裝備或雜物，尤其是說“拿上我的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to pack my things before we leave.","zh":"我們出發前我得收拾好我的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put your things in the cupboard by the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25ec8fd9d6c6ff78","term":"thing","forms":["thing","things"],"pos":"noun","zh":"關鍵點","explanation":"指一件事中最重要的中心、要點或癥結。","examples":[{"en":"That’s the thing: nobody knows the answer.","zh":"關鍵就在這裡：沒人知道答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thing is, we haven't enough money to continue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d580e8f6cccaccc","term":"thing","forms":["thing","things"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜歡的事；擅長的領域","explanation":"my thing 表示某人喜歡、認同或適合自己的活動、風格或領域。","examples":[{"en":"Cooking for a large group is not really my thing.","zh":"給一大群人做飯不太是我喜歡或擅長的事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Classical music has never been my thing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc2fc19d8fce376c4764","word":"think","forms":["think"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51f0f38da2b6bcae","term":"think","forms":["think","thinks","thinking","thought","thinkest","thoughtest","thinketh","-","thunk"],"pos":"verb","zh":"思考；琢磨","explanation":"指把問題或事情在腦中過一遍，努力理解它、分析它或決定下一步怎麼做，是 think 最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"I need some time to think about your offer.","zh":"我需要一些時間考慮你的提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She thought carefully about what to do next.","zh":"她認真思考了下一步該怎麼辦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/think","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cab13cc61a430f3","term":"think","forms":["think","thinks","thinking","thought","thinkest","thoughtest","thinketh","-","thunk"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想到；設想為","explanation":"表示把某人或某事放進腦中去想象、聯想到，或形成對它的概念；它把“腦中的念頭”指向一個物件。","examples":[{"en":"When I think of summer, I think of long days by the sea.","zh":"我一想到夏天，就會想到在海邊度過的漫長白天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They think of her as a careful and reliable manager.","zh":"他們把她看作一位謹慎可靠的經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/think","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fe26a85ae690ad2","term":"think","forms":["think","thinks","thinking","thought","thinkest","thoughtest","thinketh","-","thunk"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認為；看待","explanation":"表示從腦中的思考形成一個較明確的看法，把某事判斷為某種情況。","examples":[{"en":"I think this plan will save us a lot of time.","zh":"我認為這個計劃會為我們節省很多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What do you think of the new design?","zh":"你覺得這個新設計怎麼樣？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/think","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b1e99324505bd32da0e1","word":"third","forms":["third"],"officialPos":"adj./n./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1a2b4e5ab84605fb","term":"third","forms":["third"],"pos":"adj","zh":"第三的","explanation":"表示在順序上排在第二之後，也就是一組中的第三個或第三位。","examples":[{"en":"The third tree from the left is my favorite.","zh":"從左邊數第三棵樹是我最喜歡的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our third meeting will be next Monday.","zh":"我們的第三次會議將在下週一舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/third","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4a42b093b3d8c8a7","term":"third","forms":["third","thirds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"第三名；第三位","explanation":"指在比賽、佇列或某種排列中處於第三位置的人或物。","examples":[{"en":"Maya came in third in the race.","zh":"瑪雅在比賽中獲得了第三名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finished a close third in the race.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/third","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b01b1a8250ceae6d","term":"third","forms":["third","thirds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"三分之一","explanation":"指把一個整體平均分成三份後其中的一份，也可用於說明佔整體的比例。","examples":[{"en":"She drank a third of the bottle.","zh":"她喝掉了瓶子裡三分之一的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A third of the audience left before the interval.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/third","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70b18d5bdad8e3f7ead9","word":"thirst","forms":["thirst"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b714bff71e62d040","term":"thirst","forms":["thirst","thirsts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口渴","explanation":"喉嚨幹、身體需要喝液體時產生的口渴感覺；這裡的“渴”是身體上的實際感覺。","examples":[{"en":"After two hours of hiking, we felt a strong thirst.","zh":"徒步兩個小時後，我們感到非常口渴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A cold glass of water quickly relieved her thirst.","zh":"一杯涼水很快緩解了她的口渴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thirst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df76c4682bc25e0d","term":"thirst","forms":["thirst","thirsts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈渴望","explanation":"把身體想喝水的迫切感引申到心理上，表示對知識、訊息、成功等事物的強烈渴望。","examples":[{"en":"Her thirst for knowledge led her to study three languages.","zh":"她對知識的渴求促使她學習了三種語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nothing could satisfy the conqueror's thirst for power.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thirst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-03f3ef306333f494f7a9","word":"thirsty","forms":["thirsty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b212cb32cfde7ba","term":"thirsty","forms":["thirsty","thirstier","thirstiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"口渴的","explanation":"身體缺水、需要喝水或其他能補充水分的飲料時，就可以說 thirsty。這是最基本、最常見的含義。","examples":[{"en":"After the long hike, everyone was thirsty.","zh":"長途徒步後，大家都口渴了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'm thirsty—could I have a glass of water?","zh":"我口渴了，可以給我一杯水嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thirsty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7beda920265a8e4","term":"thirsty","forms":["thirsty","thirstier","thirstiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"渴望得到某物的","explanation":"把身體對水的急切需要延伸到無形目標：thirsty for knowledge 就是“對知識有強烈渴望”，也可以用於成功、權力或機會等。","examples":[{"en":"She is thirsty for knowledge and reads every evening.","zh":"她求知若渴，每天晚上都閱讀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young team is thirsty for success.","zh":"這支年輕的隊伍渴望成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thirsty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1eb79602411ef02cf6fe","word":"this","forms":["this"],"officialPos":"pron./adv./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f86a189e3a173d0","term":"this","forms":["this","these"],"pos":"det","zh":"這個；這件","explanation":"指說話人眼前或語境中明顯靠近自己的一個人、物或地方，相當於“這個”。這是 this 最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"This classroom is where I learned to read and write.","zh":"這個教室是我學會讀寫的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you pass me this book?","zh":"你能把這本書遞給我嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/this","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35895dc6958e5a1f","term":"this","forms":["this","these"],"pos":"det","zh":"這個（剛提到的）","explanation":"它把剛剛談到的人或事再次圈出來，表示“這個情況”或“這個東西”，不一定真的在眼前。","examples":[{"en":"The plan sounds simple, but this plan has one serious problem.","zh":"這個計劃聽起來很簡單，但這個計劃有一個嚴重的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She described a new method, and this method worked.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/this","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1e34e687f1ae772","term":"this","forms":["this","these"],"pos":"pron","zh":"這個；這件事","explanation":"它獨立指向一個已經被看見、指出或在語境中明確的物件，意思是“這個”或“這件事”。","examples":[{"en":"This isn't the item that I ordered.","zh":"這不是我訂購的那件東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put this on the table.","zh":"請把這個放在桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/this","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a06d7b2b0415505dbf70","word":"thorough","forms":["thorough"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-751381cf019a1284","term":"thorough","forms":["thorough","thorougher","more thorough","thoroughest","most thorough"],"pos":"adj","zh":"周密的；不遺漏細節的","explanation":"指做某項工作時從各方面認真檢查或處理，力求不漏掉任何重要細節。它就像把事情一路查到底，因此常用於調查、檢查、研究和準備等場合。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor gave me a thorough examination.","zh":"醫生給我做了一次全面的檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please be thorough when you check the figures.","zh":"請你核對這些數字時務必做到周密細緻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thorough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-18d8bc0e8af5e7d7","term":"thorough","forms":["thorough","thorougher","more thorough","thoroughest","most thorough"],"pos":"adj","zh":"徹底的；完全的","explanation":"表示某種狀態或程度已經達到徹底、毫無保留的地步。它可以從“把事情做到底”自然引申出來，未必涉及逐項檢查。","examples":[{"en":"The plan was a thorough failure.","zh":"這個計劃徹底失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the storm, the garden was in thorough disorder.","zh":"暴風雨過後，花園一片徹底的混亂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thorough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6120d7ff00ac60e0b8f9","word":"those","forms":["those"],"officialPos":"pron./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"those","forms":["those"],"pos":"pron./adj.","zh":"那些","examples":[{"en":"Those are the mountains we climbed last summer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Please put those boxes beside the door.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9bbc0222075becade10","word":"though","forms":["though"],"officialPos":"conj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a941e4dd77cfaf1e","term":"though","forms":["though"],"pos":"adv","zh":"不過；雖然如此","explanation":"它先承認前面的情況成立，再補出一個限制、例外或相反方面，核心感覺就是“即便如此，後面還要轉一下”。放在句末時尤其常譯為“不過、倒是”。","examples":[{"en":"The tickets were expensive. We had a great time, though.","zh":"票很貴，不過我們玩得很開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Though it was raining, we went for a walk.","zh":"雖然下著雨，我們還是去散步了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/though","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8192353a3982b4fe7ac","word":"thought","forms":["thought"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1e1ea9c8466208c8","term":"thought","forms":["thought","thoughts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"想法；念頭","explanation":"指頭腦中形成的一個具體想法、念頭或心理印象，就像腦海裡突然亮起的一盞小燈，可以選擇、改變或表達出來。","examples":[{"en":"A new thought came to me while I was walking home.","zh":"我走回家時突然有了一個新的想法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to replace that negative thought with a more hopeful one.","zh":"試著用一個更有希望的想法替代那個消極念頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thought","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28856948589fc151","term":"thought","forms":["thought","thoughts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"思考；思維活動","explanation":"指人在頭腦中形成、整理和運用想法的整個過程，而不是某一個單獨的念頭；它就是那盞燈持續運轉的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Quiet time gives her space for thought.","zh":"安靜的時間給了她思考的空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Education should encourage independent thought.","zh":"教育應當鼓勵獨立思考。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thought","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63c6ce2675dc8f8daa9a","word":"thoughtful","forms":["thoughtful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1d7db0cd6e8f305","term":"thoughtful","forms":["thoughtful","more thoughtful","most thoughtful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"深思熟慮的；認真考慮的","explanation":"指一個人或一種做法經過認真思考，而不是草率決定；重點是把事情想清楚、考慮周全。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a thoughtful answer to the difficult question.","zh":"她認真思考後回答了這個難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A thoughtful person checks the facts before making a decision.","zh":"考慮周全的人會在作出決定前核實事實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thoughtful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-473afb0e53f16abb","term":"thoughtful","forms":["thoughtful","more thoughtful","most thoughtful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"體貼的；周到的","explanation":"指一個人的言行考慮到了別人的感受、需要或處境，因此讓人感到體貼和周到；這是“把認真考慮用在別人身上”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Bringing her favorite tea was a thoughtful gesture.","zh":"帶來她最喜歡的茶是一個很體貼的舉動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was thoughtful of you to bring extra blankets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thoughtful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0af3a48cfad1fc07404","word":"thousand","forms":["thousand"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a4b9a2c17ff9967","term":"thousand","forms":["thousand","thousands"],"pos":"num","zh":"一千；千","explanation":"表示準確的數值1000，也就是十個一百；它像一個裝滿一千件東西的大捆，可用於人數、金額、距離等各種數量。","examples":[{"en":"The stadium can hold ten thousand people.","zh":"這座體育場能容納一萬人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She saved a thousand dollars for the trip.","zh":"她為這次旅行攢了一千美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thousand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39200d1e8a8dbbb6d7bc","word":"thread","forms":["thread"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d9832c505d62ad7","term":"thread","forms":["thread","threads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紡織線","explanation":"由紡織纖維紡成或擰成的細線，尤其用於縫紉。它是 thread 最基本、最具體的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She chose a blue thread to mend the tear in her shirt.","zh":"她選了一根藍線來縫補襯衫上的破口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use strong thread to sew the button back on.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-58eb64386fa8ac9c","term":"thread","forms":["thread","threads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"談話線索","explanation":"指談話、文章或故事中把各個部分連線起來的思路或主線。聽懂這條線，就能跟上對方在說什麼。","examples":[{"en":"I lost the thread of the lecture when the speaker changed topics.","zh":"演講者換了話題後，我就沒跟上講座的思路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The final chapter brings all the threads of the story together.","zh":"最後一章把故事中的所有線索都串聯了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe8665230d1d37f7","term":"thread","forms":["thread","threads"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網路討論串","explanation":"指圍繞同一主題排列的一串帖子或訊息，包括最初的發帖以及後續回覆；它就像一根線把相關內容串在一起。","examples":[{"en":"I found a helpful thread about choosing a laptop for college.","zh":"我找到了一串關於為上大學選擇膝上型電腦的有用討論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please read the whole thread before asking the same question.","zh":"請先讀完整個討論串，再提相同的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b691d2503f1da987","term":"thread","forms":["thread","threads","threading","threaded","thrid","thridden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穿針","explanation":"把線穿過針眼，使線進入針中，正是“線穿過一個狹小通道”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"Could you thread the needle for me? I can hardly see the eye.","zh":"你能幫我穿一下針嗎？我幾乎看不清針眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Threading needles became difficult as his eyesight weakened.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a166f1efa9472887","term":"thread","forms":["thread","threads","threading","threaded","thrid","thridden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穿行","explanation":"在狹窄空間或障礙物之間靈活透過，好像一根線彎曲著穿過縫隙。","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist threaded through the crowded market without stopping.","zh":"騎車人不停下來，穿過擁擠的市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She threaded her way between the parked cars.","zh":"她在停著的汽車之間穿行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a569b9b2250fe3236367","word":"threat","forms":["threat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c73566e967c643f","term":"threat","forms":["threat","threats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"威脅；恐嚇","explanation":"指明確表示要傷害或懲罰某人的話、動作或意圖，也就是用語言或行動給對方施壓。重點在於“要對某人做壞事”的訊號，而不一定真的已經造成傷害。","examples":[{"en":"The company received a threat after announcing the plan.","zh":"這家公司宣佈該計劃後收到了一條威脅資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She took his threat seriously and called the police.","zh":"她認真對待他的威脅，並報了警。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/threat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38654e0e34078836","term":"threat","forms":["threat","threats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"潛在危險；威脅","explanation":"指某種可能很快造成傷害、損失或問題的情況。這時 threat 不一定是某人說出來的話，而是正在逼近的危險因素。","examples":[{"en":"Rising sea levels pose a serious threat to coastal communities.","zh":"海平面上升給沿海社群帶來了嚴重威脅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unstable cliff poses a threat to walkers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/threat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75ed840ef93685506157","word":"threaten","forms":["threaten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd612a9898fc0608","term":"threaten","forms":["threaten","threatens","threatening","threatened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"威脅；恐嚇","explanation":"表示明確告訴某人將要傷害、懲罰或給他帶來不利後果，以迫使他服從或讓他害怕。","examples":[{"en":"He threatened to report the mistake to the manager.","zh":"他威脅說要把這個錯誤報告給經理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stranger threatened me with a knife.","zh":"那個陌生人拿刀威脅我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/threaten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d204bb02ecc66e15","term":"threaten","forms":["threaten","threatens","threatening","threatened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"預示；有……的徵兆","explanation":"表示某種跡象顯示不好的事情可能很快發生，像烏雲壓來，預示著暴雨即將到來。","examples":[{"en":"Dark clouds threatened rain during our hike.","zh":"我們徒步時，烏雲預示著要下雨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A sudden drop in temperature threatened to ruin the outdoor event.","zh":"氣溫突然下降，可能會毀掉這場戶外活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/threaten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-497e22fe854a24bcfb8a","word":"threshold","forms":["threshold"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d40e6afd97bf8ad8","term":"threshold","forms":["threshold","thresholds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"門檻","explanation":"指門口最下面、進出時需要跨過的橫木或地面部分。它是“跨入另一個空間”這一核心意象的字面來源。","examples":[{"en":"She paused on the threshold before entering the room.","zh":"她站在門檻上停了一會兒，才走進房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left his muddy shoes outside the threshold.","zh":"他把沾滿泥的鞋留在門檻外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/threshold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2768549e684cc004","term":"threshold","forms":["threshold","thresholds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"起點；開始階段","explanation":"指某件事剛要開始或某人即將進入一個新階段，好像已經站在門口、只差跨進去。它常用於人生、行動、冒險或重大事件的開端。","examples":[{"en":"The students stood on the threshold of their professional lives.","zh":"這些學生正站在人生職業階段的起點上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was on the threshold of making an important decision.","zh":"她正處在作出重要決定的關頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/threshold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc9d763e1a642e62d0ce","word":"thrill","forms":["thrill"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bc504a55cb10acfe","term":"thrill","forms":["thrill","thrills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"興奮感；戰慄","explanation":"指情緒突然變得很強烈時產生的興奮、快感或身體微微發顫的感覺。它既可以描述內心受到觸動，也可以描述這種感覺帶來的戰慄。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a thrill when the concert finally began.","zh":"音樂會終於開始時，我感到一陣興奮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There was a thrill in hearing the news firsthand.","zh":"親耳聽到這個訊息讓人感到一陣激動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c39e236ed6463253","term":"thrill","forms":["thrill","thrills","thrilling","thrilled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使興奮；使激動","explanation":"表示某件事讓某人突然產生強烈的興奮、快感或激動，也可以表示某人自己體驗到這種感覺。它和名詞義中的“興奮感”來自同一個“突然讓人戰慄”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The surprise visit thrilled my grandmother.","zh":"這次突然來訪讓我的祖母非常激動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was thrilled by the chance to perform on stage.","zh":"有機會登臺表演讓他興奮不已。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrill","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8191850cc246f7cfa3a7","word":"thriller","forms":["thriller"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-858105dbc92dcb5d","term":"thriller","forms":["thriller","thrillers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚心動魄的事件或比賽","explanation":"指過程緊張、結果難料、讓人持續興奮或屏息的事件，尤其常用來形容比分接近、反覆變化的比賽。核心畫面是某件事讓觀眾的心跳加速，而不只是“事情很有趣”。","examples":[{"en":"The final was a real thriller, with the winning goal coming in the last minute.","zh":"決賽非常驚心動魄，制勝球直到最後一分鐘才出現。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was a thriller from start to finish.","zh":"這場比賽從頭到尾都扣人心絃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thriller","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89e4bcc10fbd4c0c","term":"thriller","forms":["thriller","thrillers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"懸疑驚悚類作品","explanation":"指以懸念、危險和緊張推進情節的小說、電影、電視劇或戲劇型別。觀眾或讀者通常會不斷猜測接下來會發生什麼，因此它和“讓人心跳加速”的核心畫面直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"She stayed up late to finish the psychological thriller.","zh":"她熬夜讀完了那部心理驚悚小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new thriller keeps you guessing until the end.","zh":"這部新懸疑片一直讓你猜不透，直到結尾才揭曉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thriller","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8365f8634d0fc7e6f87b","word":"thrive","forms":["thrive"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38a842a00a2cff96","term":"thrive","forms":["thrive","thrives","thriving","throve","thrived","thriven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"茁壯成長","explanation":"指植物、動物或人在適合自己的環境中長得旺盛、狀態良好，不只是沒有死去或勉強維持。","examples":[{"en":"These plants thrive in bright, indirect light.","zh":"這些植物在明亮但不直射的光線下長得特別旺盛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some children thrive in a calm and predictable environment.","zh":"有些孩子在平靜而規律的環境中成長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f9465a725933c2b","term":"thrive","forms":["thrive","thrives","thriving","throve","thrived","thriven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"興旺成功","explanation":"指事業、公司、生意或個人發展得越來越好，取得成功，通常也含有收入或財富增加的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The family business has thrived since the new owner took over.","zh":"這家家族企業自從新老闆接手後一直髮展得很興旺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Independent bookshops thrive in this university town.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrive","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-48cf13f481ae6828d989","word":"throat","forms":["throat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98094cd802231a4e","term":"throat","forms":["throat","throats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喉嚨前部","explanation":"指脖子前面、外部可以感覺到的喉嚨部位，受擊、疼痛或檢查時常說到它。","examples":[{"en":"The ball hit me in the throat.","zh":"球打中了我的喉嚨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt a sharp pain in his throat.","zh":"他感到喉嚨一陣劇痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dd152bf7d235c60","term":"throat","forms":["throat","throats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"咽喉通道","explanation":"強調喉嚨裡面供食物、液體或空氣透過的部分，所以吞嚥、噎住或發聲時都可以用這個詞。","examples":[{"en":"I felt the tablet stuck in my throat.","zh":"我感覺藥片卡在了喉嚨裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cleared her throat before speaking.","zh":"她說話前清了清嗓子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab8b76517c436cdfab37","word":"throne","forms":["throne"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f35774dfcd206825","term":"throne","forms":["throne","thrones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王座","explanation":"指宮殿或王座室中供君主正式就座的華麗座椅，通常位於高臺上，並帶有莊嚴和權威的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The king rose from the throne to greet the visiting ambassador.","zh":"國王從王座上起身迎接來訪的大使。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children stared at the golden throne in the palace.","zh":"孩子們盯著宮殿裡的金色王座。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throne","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e71b844dde0fe29c","term":"throne","forms":["throne","thrones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"王位；統治權","explanation":"這裡不是指一把實際的椅子，而是指君主的職位、王位或統治權；“登上王座”因此也可以表示開始成為君主。","examples":[{"en":"After his father's death, the young prince inherited the throne.","zh":"父親去世後，年輕的王子繼承了王位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The princess eventually inherited the throne.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throne","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c6725dc269a48ce4b5b","word":"through","forms":["through"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a0dac4e944600f1","term":"through","forms":["through"],"pos":"adv","zh":"穿過去","explanation":"表示人或物從某處的一邊移動到另一邊，重點是完成穿越動作。","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist went straight through and disappeared around the corner.","zh":"騎車的人直穿過去，消失在拐角處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hole was wide enough to crawl through.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/through","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-791a11af60ff2abc","term":"through","forms":["through"],"pos":"prep","zh":"穿過；從一端到另一端","explanation":"表示從某個地點、物體或區域的一端進入併到達另一端，是 through 最基本的空間畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We walked through the forest before reaching the village.","zh":"我們穿過森林後才到達村子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Light came through the curtains.","zh":"光線從窗簾之間透了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/through","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d41d9e05fcfb0016518e","word":"throughout","forms":["throughout"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b962ce2440e3001a","term":"throughout","forms":["throughout"],"pos":"adv","zh":"遍及各處","explanation":"強調一個空間或整體範圍內沒有遺漏，裡面的每一處都呈現同樣的情況；可以把它想成一條路線上的每個位置都被覆蓋。","examples":[{"en":"Soft music played throughout the hotel.","zh":"整個酒店各處都播放著輕柔的音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The house was repainted throughout before the sale.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throughout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fc2b3dd75d2b235d","term":"throughout","forms":["throughout"],"pos":"adv","zh":"貫穿全程","explanation":"強調某種行動、狀態或情況在整個時間段內持續存在，從開始到結束都沒有離開這段過程。","examples":[{"en":"She remained calm throughout the interview.","zh":"整個面試過程中，她始終保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lecture lasted two hours, and she listened carefully throughout.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throughout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7b0456581bef4cb1f0e2","word":"throw","forms":["throw"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7d200080b3a11db1","term":"throw","forms":["throw","throws"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投擲動作","explanation":"指把某物從手中送離原位這一動作本身，而不是被扔出去的物體。","examples":[{"en":"With one quick throw, she knocked the can off the wall.","zh":"她迅速一扔，就把罐子從牆上打了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His final throw landed beyond the marked line.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-242fe43d67f66bbf","term":"throw","forms":["throw","throws","throwing","threw","throwed","thrown","throwest","threwst","throweth","-","thrun"],"pos":"verb","zh":"扔出；投擲","explanation":"把手裡的東西或器械中的物體用力送離原位，使它快速飛出去，這是“把某物送離原位”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"He threw the ball across the yard.","zh":"他把球扔過了院子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She threw her keys onto the table.","zh":"她把鑰匙扔到桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37a7fea8499e59a6","term":"throw","forms":["throw","throws","throwing","threw","throwed","thrown","throwest","threwst","throweth","-","thrun"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使移位；使轉到某狀態","explanation":"把人或物從原來的位置、狀態或安排中移到另一處，核心仍是“送離原位”；例如把開關撥到另一狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Throw the switch when the light turns green.","zh":"燈變綠時撥動開關。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden news threw her into a panic.","zh":"這個突然的訊息使她陷入恐慌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8dbce977059a510e","term":"throw","forms":["throw","throws","throwing","threw","throwed","thrown","throwest","threwst","throweth","-","thrun"],"pos":"verb","zh":"舉辦；組織活動","explanation":"把一場活動安排起來並讓它發生，尤其常指舉辦聚會；這是“把活動送到現實中”的引申用法。","examples":[{"en":"We’re throwing a party for her birthday.","zh":"我們要為她的生日舉辦一個聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They threw a small dinner for their new neighbors.","zh":"他們為新鄰居辦了一場小型晚宴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2081cc0de301a35dba48","word":"thrust","forms":["thrust"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-68baed8a67e35444","term":"thrust","forms":["thrust","thrusts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用力向前推或刺","explanation":"泛指一次有力的向前推動、猛刺或衝撞動作；擊劍中的突刺只是這種“力量向前頂出”的具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"He knocked the knife away before the next thrust.","zh":"他在下一次刺擊之前就把刀打落了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One quick thrust drove the blade into the timber.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07921528358a0fe8","term":"thrust","forms":["thrust","thrusts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主要著力點或重點","explanation":"把“向前推動”引申為推動一項工作前進的核心努力，因此表示文章、計劃或政策最主要的方向和重點。","examples":[{"en":"The main thrust of the proposal is to improve public transport.","zh":"這項提案的主要著力點是改善公共交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The main thrust of his argument concerns equal access.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d03db658f8e5f554","term":"thrust","forms":["thrust","thrusts","thrusting","thrusted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用力推開或頂動","explanation":"表示用手、腳或工具把某物用力推、頂或撞開，是“力量向前頂出”這一核心動作最直接的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"He thrust the door open and rushed inside.","zh":"他用力推開門，衝了進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He thrust the heavy door open with his shoulder.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05eeec2d70845694d3ba","word":"thumb","forms":["thumb"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d884bfba6e8d0998","term":"thumb","forms":["thumb","thumbs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拇指","explanation":"thumb 是手上短而粗、能與其他手指相對接觸的手指，即拇指。它因為活動範圍大，能幫助人抓握和操作物品。","examples":[{"en":"I cut my thumb while opening the package.","zh":"我拆包裝時割傷了拇指。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pressed the button with her thumb.","zh":"她用拇指按下了按鈕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thumb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0a9e7174baa9861","term":"thumb","forms":["thumb","thumbs","thumbing","thumbed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用拇指按住或覆蓋","explanation":"thumb 作動詞時，可以表示用拇指碰觸、按住或蓋住某處；動作的核心仍然是讓拇指直接接觸目標。","examples":[{"en":"He thumbed the small hole closed.","zh":"他用拇指把那個小孔按住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He thumbed the opening shut while carrying the bottle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thumb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49eff747f7b66f70133b","word":"thunder","forms":["thunder"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f249566d287ce834","term":"thunder","forms":["thunder","thunders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雷聲","explanation":"指閃電附近空氣急劇膨脹所產生的巨大轟鳴聲，也就是通常所說的雷聲。","examples":[{"en":"We heard thunder soon after the lightning.","zh":"閃電過後不久，我們聽到了雷聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Thunder rumbled beyond the darkening hills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thunder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-99b0f2b1bc8f6dc7","term":"thunder","forms":["thunder","thunders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轟鳴聲","explanation":"指深沉、連續而震耳的聲音，聲音本身不一定來自雷電，但聽起來像雷聲，例如馬群、火車或機器發出的轟鳴。","examples":[{"en":"The thunder of the approaching train shook the windows.","zh":"駛來的火車發出的轟鳴聲震得窗戶都在響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We heard the thunder of hooves approaching.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thunder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2b11bdf15b54548","term":"thunder","forms":["thunder","thunders","thundering","thundered","thunderest","thunderedst","thundereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打雷","explanation":"指天空發出雷聲，通常用來描述天氣中的打雷現象。","examples":[{"en":"It thundered all night, but hardly any rain fell.","zh":"整夜都在打雷，但幾乎沒下什麼雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It thundered for hours beyond the mountains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thunder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-feec52bd47756460","term":"thunder","forms":["thunder","thunders","thundering","thundered","thunderest","thunderedst","thundereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轟鳴","explanation":"指某物發出像雷一樣的巨大聲音，常用於火車、車輛、機器或人群等。","examples":[{"en":"The trucks thundered past us on the highway.","zh":"卡車在高速公路上轟鳴著從我們身邊駛過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trucks thundered across the metal bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thunder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c432b3dedcd6852f1ab5","word":"thus","forms":["thus"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a6d614f59f186b4a","term":"thus","forms":["thus"],"pos":"adv","zh":"如此；以這種方式","explanation":"表示按照眼前所示或前文說明的方式來做，即“這樣地、如此地”。它把“如此”看成一種具體的做法或動作方式。","examples":[{"en":"Hold the brush thus, with your fingers near the end.","zh":"像這樣拿著畫筆，手指靠近末端。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The machine is designed to fold the boxes thus.","zh":"這臺機器的設計就是要這樣摺疊箱子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d1eb5c6b228f2c9","term":"thus","forms":["thus"],"pos":"adv","zh":"因此；由此","explanation":"表示前面的事實或行動帶來了後面的結果，相當於“因此、由此、於是”。可以把它理解為“事情如此，所以結果也隨之出現”。","examples":[{"en":"The roads were closed; thus, we had to take a longer route.","zh":"道路封閉了，因此我們不得不走更遠的路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She saved a little every month and thus paid for the course herself.","zh":"她每個月存一點錢，於是靠自己付清了課程費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-55a4bc5be68ea5c30cbe","word":"tick","forms":["tick"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-27387d38636175a1","term":"tick","forms":["tick","ticks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"滴答聲","explanation":"指鐘錶或運轉中的機械發出的輕而規律的嗒嗒聲；這個聲音像一個個小節拍連續出現。","examples":[{"en":"The tick of the clock kept me awake.","zh":"鐘錶的滴答聲讓我一直睡不著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With each tick, the countdown moved closer to zero.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c08357345583199","term":"tick","forms":["tick","ticks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勾號","explanation":"指用來表示同意、正確或已確認的勾號“✓”；它仍保留了“輕輕做一個標記”的核心感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Please put a tick in the box if you agree.","zh":"如果你同意，請在方框裡打勾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put a tick beside each correct answer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-767c3b0e171c30fc","term":"tick","forms":["tick","ticks","ticking","ticked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"運轉；工作","explanation":"在非正式表達中，指機器或系統正常工作、運轉；也可引申為探究某人或某事運作的方式。它仍然帶有內部小部件持續“嗒嗒”執行的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"He opened the case to see how the machine ticked.","zh":"他開啟外殼，想看看這臺機器是怎樣運轉的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wonder what makes this old engine tick.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14069429150abcbf244c","word":"ticket","forms":["ticket"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-06637729a218424d","term":"ticket","forms":["ticket","tickets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"票；憑證","explanation":"指證明你有資格參加活動、乘坐交通工具或進入某處的小型憑證，可以是紙質的，也可以是電子的。它的共同點是“拿著它，某件事就被允許進行”。","examples":[{"en":"I bought two tickets for the concert next Friday.","zh":"我買了兩張下週五音樂會的票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please show your ticket at the entrance.","zh":"請在入口處出示你的票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ticket","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-20f759a1625250532102","word":"tickle","forms":["tickle"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-248b52aaea4cd285","term":"tickle","forms":["tickle","tickles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"撓癢","explanation":"指用輕柔反覆的觸碰讓人發癢、發笑的動作，也可以指這種動作本身。它就是“輕輕碰觸”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The child asked for one more tickle before bedtime.","zh":"孩子睡覺前要求再撓一次癢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tickled the baby's feet until he laughed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tickle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb2f908406494cd5","term":"tickle","forms":["tickle","tickles","tickling","tickled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撓癢；輕輕觸碰","explanation":"指反覆、輕柔地觸碰某人的身體，使對方發癢、發笑或不由自主地扭動。這個義項直接體現了“輕輕碰觸”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Dad tickled the baby's feet, and she burst out laughing.","zh":"爸爸撓了撓嬰兒的腳，嬰兒立刻大笑起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tickled the baby's toes gently.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tickle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ccc144f46479e7b","term":"tickle","forms":["tickle","tickles","tickling","tickled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引起興趣","explanation":"把“輕輕刺激身體”引申到想法或好奇心上，表示某事吸引了某人的興趣、口味或好奇心。","examples":[{"en":"The idea of a weekend cooking class tickled her fancy.","zh":"參加週末烹飪課的想法引起了她的興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unexpected proposal tickled her curiosity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tickle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8a28929ac7f9a17e97a4","word":"tide","forms":["tide"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9709fc5d6a5e107b","term":"tide","forms":["tide","tides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"潮汐","explanation":"海水受月亮和太陽引力影響，按規律升高和降低的現象。它是“潮流”這條記憶主線的起點。","examples":[{"en":"We should leave before the tide comes in.","zh":"我們應該在漲潮前離開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tide was unusually low this morning.","zh":"今天早上的潮水異常低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7236e7bc7b3484c","term":"tide","forms":["tide","tides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"潮水；潮流","explanation":"也可以指隨著潮汐進出、推動物體移動的水流；漂流物被潮水帶到岸邊，就是這個義項。","examples":[{"en":"The tide carried the small boat toward the shore.","zh":"潮水把小船帶向岸邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The outgoing tide exposed a wide stretch of sand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a61bf95b93665e27","term":"tide","forms":["tide","tides"],"pos":"noun","zh":"趨勢；潮流","explanation":"海水的方向會漲會退，因此 tide 可比喻輿論、支援、政治形勢等力量的發展方向；方向改變就是“潮頭轉了”。","examples":[{"en":"Public opinion is beginning to turn against the proposal.","zh":"公眾輿論開始轉而反對這項提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One late goal turned the tide of the match.","zh":"一個臨近終場的進球扭轉了比賽局勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-118a1de593252b71f178","word":"tidy","forms":["tidy"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-15cd9244aa1336cd","term":"tidy","forms":["tidy","tidier","tidiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"整齊有序","explanation":"表示東西擺放得很整齊、有條理，幾乎沒有物品亂放或錯位；這是 tidy 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Her desk is always tidy.","zh":"她的書桌總是很整齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I keep my notes tidy in separate folders.","zh":"我把筆記整齊地放在不同的資料夾裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tidy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecc56cc280149c3b","term":"tidy","forms":["tidy","tidies","tidying","tidied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"整理、收拾","explanation":"表示把散亂的物品收好、把空間收拾整齊，使原本雜亂的狀態變得有條理。它正是“整齊”這一核心概念的動作形式。","examples":[{"en":"The children tidied up their room before dinner.","zh":"孩子們晚飯前收拾好了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you tidy the books on the shelf?","zh":"你能把架子上的書整理一下嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tidy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6f595eba3f46ceaa9fd0","word":"tie","forms":["tie"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea9f11e297e7e805","term":"tie","forms":["tie","ties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結；繫緊處","explanation":"把繩子、線或類似材料繞住並固定後形成的結，就是 tie。它體現了“把東西系在一起”的基本意象。","examples":[{"en":"There is a tight tie in the end of the rope.","zh":"繩子末端有一個系得很緊的結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the tie securing the bundle of branches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-74b9f76dec9f78aa","term":"tie","forms":["tie","ties","tying","tied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打結；繞緊","explanation":"把繩子、線等繞到自身上並固定，使它不容易鬆開。這個動作是 tie 最基本的“繫住”意義。","examples":[{"en":"Please tie the rope tightly.","zh":"請把繩子繫緊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tie the ribbon tightly around the box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7be8fe6946a6cf64","term":"tie","forms":["tie","ties","tying","tied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打成平局","explanation":"比賽中雙方得到相同分數或處在相同名次，因而誰也沒有領先。它把雙方“系”在同一個結果上。","examples":[{"en":"The two teams tied 2–2.","zh":"兩隊以二比二打成平局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The teams tied after a tense final quarter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tie","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f15c16b99f82d8201767","word":"tiger","forms":["tiger"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1289e05422a10ed2","term":"tiger","forms":["tiger","tigers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"老虎","explanation":"一種生活在亞洲的大型貓科捕食動物，通常有明顯條紋，力量強、行動敏捷。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a tiger resting in the shade at the zoo.","zh":"我們在動物園看到一隻老虎在陰涼處休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tigers need large territories to hunt.","zh":"老虎需要很大的領地來捕獵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-860ca11dcc9e6415","term":"tiger","forms":["tiger","tigers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高速增長的經濟體","explanation":"“經濟虎”把國家或地區比作強勁有力的老虎，指規模可能不大但經濟增長很快的經濟體。","examples":[{"en":"The country became an economic tiger after decades of rapid growth.","zh":"這個國家經過數十年的快速增長後，成為了一個經濟虎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The country became one of Asia's economic tigers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-922b53ea837e15ffe640","word":"tight","forms":["tight"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33128c7cbbcec9c9","term":"tight","forms":["tight","tighter","tightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"緊固的；不松的","explanation":"指東西被牢牢繫住、壓緊或收攏，不容易鬆開，也沒有明顯的空隙。","examples":[{"en":"Tie the knot tight so it won't come undone.","zh":"把結繫緊，免得它鬆開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lid is too tight for me to open.","zh":"蓋子太緊了，我打不開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2ae0c930d9ea7041","term":"tight","forms":["tight","tighter","tightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"狹窄的","explanation":"指空間或通道收得很窄，東西或人很難透過。","examples":[{"en":"The gap was so tight that we had to turn sideways.","zh":"縫隙太窄了，我們只好側著身子過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This parking space is tight, but the car will fit.","zh":"這個停車位很窄，不過車還是停得進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ace02c18d5f27d94","term":"tight","forms":["tight","tighter","tightest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"緊張受限的","explanation":"表示可用的時間、空間或資源很少，安排被壓得很緊。","examples":[{"en":"We have a tight schedule, so please arrive on time.","zh":"我們的日程排得很緊，請準時到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project has a tight budget.","zh":"這個專案的預算很有限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91e53284a2d6829c","term":"tight","forms":["tight","tighter","tightest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"牢牢地","explanation":"表示抓、握或固定得很緊，不容易鬆手或脫落。","examples":[{"en":"Hold on tight while the boat turns.","zh":"船轉彎時要抓牢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hold tight while the boat crosses the waves.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05f053d780f957356b6d","word":"tighten","forms":["tighten"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74561cf3858720bb","term":"tighten","forms":["tighten","tightens","tightening","tightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變緊；擰緊","explanation":"把螺絲、繩子、蓋子等弄得更緊，使它們不容易鬆動。這裡強調有人主動改變物體的鬆緊程度。","examples":[{"en":"Please tighten that screw a quarter-turn.","zh":"請把那顆螺絲再擰緊四分之一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tightened the lid before putting the jar away.","zh":"她把蓋子擰緊後才把罐子收起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b57ad073180f15e","term":"tighten","forms":["tighten","tightens","tightening","tightened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變緊；越來越緊","explanation":"物體自身變得更緊，不一定有人直接去擰它；例如木頭乾燥後，接縫可能會逐漸收緊。這是“被弄緊”之外的另一條用法。","examples":[{"en":"That joint is tightening as the wood dries.","zh":"木頭變干時，那個接縫正在收緊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rope tightened when the load was lifted.","zh":"貨物被吊起時，繩子繃緊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tighten","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b668b8994aa84510739","word":"tile","forms":["tile"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6248bf302abc3b6","term":"tile","forms":["tile","tiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瓦片；瓷磚","explanation":"指固定在屋頂、牆面、地面等表面上，用來覆蓋或裝飾的規則片狀材料。它不一定是瓷做的，也可以是黏土、石材、玻璃或其他材料製成的瓦片或磚片。","examples":[{"en":"We chose blue tiles for the bathroom wall.","zh":"我們為浴室牆面選了藍色瓷磚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several roof tiles were damaged in the storm.","zh":"暴風雨損壞了幾片屋瓦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c19b052dbd678bdf","term":"tile","forms":["tile","tiles","tiling","tiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鋪瓦；鋪磚","explanation":"指在屋頂、牆面或地面上鋪設一塊塊瓦片或磚片，使表面被覆蓋。這個動詞把名詞 tile 的“片狀覆蓋物”變成了“用片狀物鋪滿表面”的動作。","examples":[{"en":"They tiled the kitchen floor last weekend.","zh":"他們上週末給廚房地面鋪了磚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We plan to tile the roof before winter.","zh":"我們打算在冬天前給屋頂鋪瓦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a64e98ff18a83009e15e","word":"till","forms":["till"],"officialPos":"conj./prep.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43240bb2854c65fe","term":"till","forms":["till"],"pos":"prep","zh":"直到……為止","explanation":"till 把一件事的持續時間拉到某個終點：動作一直進行，直到指定的時間或事件發生。","examples":[{"en":"We waited till the rain stopped.","zh":"我們一直等到雨停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop is open till nine tonight.","zh":"這家商店今晚營業到九點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/till","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b63bd1a162bbc8d18ce","word":"tilt","forms":["tilt"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eef7a45d34e6807e","term":"tilt","forms":["tilt","tilts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傾斜；斜度","explanation":"指物體或表面偏離水平或垂直位置的角度，也可以泛指這種向一邊偏的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The table has a slight tilt to the left.","zh":"這張桌子稍微向左傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Check the tilt of the screen before you tighten the stand.","zh":"擰緊支架前，檢查一下螢幕的傾斜角度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-40dd51194762c18c","term":"tilt","forms":["tilt","tilts","tilting","tilted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使傾斜；使偏斜","explanation":"把某物從平衡位置轉到斜的角度，常常是為了讓裡面的東西流出或改變方向。","examples":[{"en":"Tilt the bottle to pour the sauce into the bowl.","zh":"把瓶子傾斜，把醬汁倒進碗裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tilted the mirror toward the window.","zh":"她把鏡子朝窗戶方向傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb91a53479f92018","term":"tilt","forms":["tilt","tilts","tilting","tilted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傾斜；處於斜角","explanation":"指物體或身體自身偏離豎直或水平位置，重點是它所處的角度。","examples":[{"en":"The picture began to tilt to one side.","zh":"那幅畫開始向一邊傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat tilted sharply in the waves.","zh":"船在海浪中劇烈傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5dd46878bb0b580b3086","word":"timber","forms":["timber"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-192642f26a4a21db","term":"timber","forms":["timber","timbers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"木材資源","explanation":"指森林中的樹木，重點是把它們看作可以採伐和加工成木材的資源，而不是單獨的一棵樹。","examples":[{"en":"The company buys timber from managed forests.","zh":"這家公司從經過管理的森林中購買木材資源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The region's timber supplies supported a large shipbuilding industry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/timber","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-336074805fc853987abe","word":"time","forms":["time"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61124e5cd3ad1134","term":"time","forms":["time","times"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時間的流逝","explanation":"指從過去經過現在、繼續走向未來的整個過程，是時間線本身，而不是某一小段時間。","examples":[{"en":"Time passes quickly when we are having fun.","zh":"我們開心的時候，時間過得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Time seemed to pass more slowly in the hospital.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e757f0419de76906","term":"time","forms":["time","times"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段時間","explanation":"指持續了一段長度的時間，長短由語境決定；可以是完成事情所需的時間，也可以是可支配的時間。","examples":[{"en":"We need more time to finish the report.","zh":"我們需要更多時間完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We spent a pleasant time exploring the old harbor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76d86b2f5092c95d","term":"time","forms":["time","times"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段時光","explanation":"作為可數名詞時，指一段被當作整體來看的時間，例如很長的一段時間。","examples":[{"en":"I haven't seen her for a long time.","zh":"我已經很久沒見到她了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They enjoyed a peaceful time beside the lake.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26def43231c24693","term":"time","forms":["time","times"],"pos":"noun","zh":"現在幾點","explanation":"指一個具體的時間點，尤其是鐘錶顯示的時刻。","examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, do you have the time?","zh":"不好意思，請問現在幾點？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What time is it in Tokyo now?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4c5d9931e0e14384","term":"time","forms":["time","times"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時刻或時機","explanation":"指某件事應該發生的時刻，或做某事的合適時機；時間線上的一個具體點。","examples":[{"en":"It's time to leave for the airport.","zh":"該出發去機場了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are waiting for the right time to announce the news.","zh":"我們正在等待宣佈訊息的合適時機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c261c81fc772ad1d","term":"time","forms":["time","times","timing","timed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"計時","explanation":"用鐘錶、秒錶等測量某項活動持續了多久，或測量完成它所需的速度。","examples":[{"en":"I timed myself running five kilometers.","zh":"我給自己跑五公里計了時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Time how long the water takes to boil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f624ad5e19768554","term":"time","forms":["time","times","timing","timed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"安排時機","explanation":"選擇某事開始或發生的時間，讓它與某個機會、事件或節奏配合。","examples":[{"en":"She timed her arrival perfectly for the start of the meeting.","zh":"她把到達時間安排得恰到好處，正好趕上會議開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She timed her arrival to coincide with the break.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f09390ae1c6aed062a02","word":"timetable","forms":["timetable"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cdb6fa60f2ed1eb5","term":"timetable","forms":["timetable","timetables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"時刻表；日程表","explanation":"按時間列出一系列事件的表格，最常見的是列出火車、公共汽車等何時到達或出發的交通時刻表，也可以是課程或活動的日程表。","examples":[{"en":"The train timetable has changed several times this year.","zh":"今年火車時刻表已經改了好幾次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please check the timetable before you leave.","zh":"出發前請查一下時刻表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/timetable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-381854e7f5648d525b10","word":"timid","forms":["timid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-369a9d90bea3f071","term":"timid","forms":["timid","timider","more timid","timidest","most timid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"膽怯的；缺乏自信的","explanation":"指一個人因為害怕或沒有把握而不敢面對別人、表達自己或採取行動，像是想往前走卻縮了回來。","examples":[{"en":"She's too timid to ask for help.","zh":"她太膽怯了，不敢開口求助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was a timid child who rarely spoke in class.","zh":"他小時候很羞怯，在課堂上很少說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/timid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab547757da37eb600011","word":"tin","forms":["tin"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1d8c4e1f8d897308","term":"tin","forms":["tin","tins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錫","explanation":"一種柔軟、容易延展且不易腐蝕的金屬，是這個詞最基本的材料義。","examples":[{"en":"Tin is often used to protect other metals from corrosion.","zh":"錫常用於保護其他金屬免受腐蝕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old cup was made from tin.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e897eab998ed3495","term":"tin","forms":["tin","tins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金屬罐；罐頭","explanation":"指用錫或其他金屬製成、用來儲存食物或盛放液體等物品的密封容器；在英國等英語地區也直接指一罐食品。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a tin of soup for lunch.","zh":"我買了一罐湯當午餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The crushed tin still held a few spoonfuls of peaches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8950abfda7b727630760","word":"tiny","forms":["tiny"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-386edaf1d79e50aa","term":"tiny","forms":["tiny","tinier","tiniest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非常小的","explanation":"指尺寸非常小，常讓人想到小到不容易看清或處理的東西，例如微小的生物、細小的部件或很小的空間。","examples":[{"en":"A tiny insect landed on my glasses.","zh":"一隻微小的昆蟲落在了我的眼鏡上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The apartment has a tiny kitchen.","zh":"這套公寓有一個很小的廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiny","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-97380187a878903ffe72","word":"tip","forms":["tip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6bf778ad5d02beca","term":"tip","forms":["tip","tips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖端；末端","explanation":"tip指某物最外面的尖端或末端，尤其是細長、尖銳物體的最前端；記住“邊緣處的一點”，就能聯想到這個意思。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful not to touch the tip of the needle.","zh":"小心別碰到針尖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A drop of paint landed on the tip of her nose.","zh":"一滴油漆落在了她的鼻尖上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5490fa34b300313","term":"tip","forms":["tip","tips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小費","explanation":"tip指給服務人員的一小筆額外錢，用來表示感謝，例如給服務員、酒保或計程車司機；可以把它記成“遞給別人一點錢”的提示。","examples":[{"en":"We left a generous tip for the waiter.","zh":"我們給服務員留了一筆豐厚的小費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is the tip included in the bill?","zh":"賬單裡包含小費嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fadee079be93abaa","term":"tip","forms":["tip","tips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建議；訣竅","explanation":"tip也指幫助別人更好、更快完成某件事的一條建議或小訣竅；它和小費一樣，都可以理解為“遞給別人一點有用的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Here are three tips for keeping your phone battery healthy.","zh":"這裡有三個保持手機電池狀態良好的小建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave me a useful tip for remembering new words.","zh":"她給了我一個記新單詞的實用訣竅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-35343ebff257f0ba","term":"tip","forms":["tip","tips","tipping","tipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傾斜；使失去平衡","explanation":"表示物體處於一邊高、一邊低的傾斜狀態，或使它變得不平衡；可以把它想成在邊緣處被輕輕推了一下。","examples":[{"en":"The boat began to tip to one side in the rough water.","zh":"船在洶湧的水面上開始向一邊傾斜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tipped his chair back against the wall.","zh":"他把椅子向後傾斜，靠在牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e4d500afd4f5424bd11a","word":"tiptoe","forms":["tiptoe"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"tiptoe","forms":["tiptoe"],"pos":"v./adv./n.","zh":"踮腳走；踮著腳尖","examples":[{"en":"We had to tiptoe past the sleeping dog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"She stood on tiptoe to reach the top shelf.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-c91e5b2418a7d74124e3","word":"tire","forms":["tire"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b82b4712bbc528c7","term":"tire","forms":["tire","tires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輪胎","explanation":"車輪外面包著、直接接觸地面的橡膠部分，用來承受磨損並幫助車輛行駛。","examples":[{"en":"One of the car's tires is flat.","zh":"這輛車有一個輪胎沒氣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to replace the front tires before winter.","zh":"入冬前我們得更換前輪胎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8084babee3805bd9","term":"tire","forms":["tire","tires","tiring","tired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"感到疲倦","explanation":"人因為活動、工作或持續用力而精力下降，變得需要休息；這裡是人自己變累。","examples":[{"en":"I tire quickly when I run in the heat.","zh":"天氣炎熱時，我跑一會兒就會累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hikers tired after climbing for six hours.","zh":"這些徒步者爬了六個小時後累了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c3f0151b640bb23","term":"tire","forms":["tire","tires","tiring","tired"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使疲倦","explanation":"某項活動、工作或持續的壓力消耗了人的精力，使人感到疲倦；它是“讓別人累”的方向。","examples":[{"en":"The long meeting tired everyone in the room.","zh":"長時間的會議讓房間裡的每個人都累了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Walking through the airport tired me out.","zh":"在機場裡走來走去把我累壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c405760daf9bc32b76f4","word":"tired","forms":["tired"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cefbec22d5243a48","term":"tired","forms":["tired","more tired","tireder","most tired","tiredest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"疲倦的；需要休息的","explanation":"指身體或精神因為活動、工作等而疲倦，需要休息或睡眠。這是 tired 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I was tired after the long walk.","zh":"長途步行後我很累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looks tired and needs some sleep.","zh":"她看起來很疲倦，需要睡一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tired","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-57bbb6c9c5574350","term":"tired","forms":["tired","more tired","tireder","most tired","tiredest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"厭煩的；受夠了的","explanation":"表示對某人、某事或反覆出現的情況感到厭煩，彷彿耐心已經“用累了”。","examples":[{"en":"I'm tired of hearing the same excuse.","zh":"我聽夠了同一個藉口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are tired of waiting for an answer.","zh":"他們等答案已經等得不耐煩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tired","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41a9e04e8fe8c4a558b8","word":"tiresome","forms":["tiresome"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7c9498c50d37d53","term":"tiresome","forms":["tiresome","more tiresome","most tiresome"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人疲倦而厭煩的","explanation":"形容某人或某事持續、重複或乏味到讓人感到又累又煩。重點是它造成這種感受，而不是它自己或描述物件感到疲倦。","examples":[{"en":"His long stories eventually became tiresome.","zh":"他的長篇故事最後變得令人厭煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Repeating the same instructions is tiresome.","zh":"一遍遍重複同樣的指示很令人厭煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiresome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ea36b79cf7485758d9b","word":"tissue","forms":["tissue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a431220f615d088","term":"tissue","forms":["tissue","tissues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紙巾；薄吸水紙","explanation":"指一張可吸水的薄紙，通常用於擦手、擦鼻子或清潔；日常說 tissue 時，這往往是最先想到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could you pass me a tissue? I spilled coffee on my shirt.","zh":"請遞給我一張紙巾好嗎？我把咖啡灑到襯衫上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a box of tissues beside the bed.","zh":"床邊有一盒紙巾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tissue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f49383df7cf0ca30","term":"tissue","forms":["tissue","tissues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物組織","explanation":"指一群來源相近、一起完成某項功能的細胞及其周圍結構，例如肌肉組織或腦組織。這裡的核心仍是“許多小部分交織成一個有功能的整體”。","examples":[{"en":"The scan showed damage to the muscle tissue in his leg.","zh":"掃描顯示他腿部的肌肉組織受到了損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nervous tissue carries signals through the body.","zh":"神經組織在身體中傳遞訊號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tissue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aaf2320646108059a87a","word":"title","forms":["title"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e718053e24977325","term":"title","forms":["title","titles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"作品名稱","explanation":"指電影、音樂作品、繪畫等藝術作品的名稱，就像給作品貼上的身份標籤。","examples":[{"en":"What is the title of that film?","zh":"那部電影叫什麼名字？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The title of the song appears on the screen.","zh":"這首歌的歌名出現在螢幕上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/title","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-848c18fd918442b0","term":"title","forms":["title","titles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"書名或文章標題","explanation":"指書籍、文章等文字作品的名稱，通常能讓讀者知道作品的主題。","examples":[{"en":"The title of the book tells you what it is about.","zh":"這本書的書名讓你知道它講的是什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose a simple title for her essay.","zh":"她給自己的文章選了一個簡單的標題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/title","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05571934153133ba","term":"title","forms":["title","titles","titling","titled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……命名","explanation":"指給書、電影、文章等作品加上 title，也就是為它確定名稱。","examples":[{"en":"They titled the documentary \"A Changing City.\"","zh":"他們把這部紀錄片命名為《變化中的城市》。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The article is titled \"How to Save Water.\"","zh":"這篇文章名為《如何節約用水》。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/title","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-663ea1bfffe5038f3f0c","word":"to","forms":["to"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b857bc3ea545c81","term":"to","forms":["to"],"pos":"prep","zh":"朝向","explanation":"表示動作或視線朝著某個方向，但不一定已經到達那裡；箭頭只是指向目標。","examples":[{"en":"He turned to the window when he heard the noise.","zh":"聽到聲音後，他轉向了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog ran to the open gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/to","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-376e5530d3559be8","term":"to","forms":["to"],"pos":"prep","zh":"到達某地","explanation":"表示移動的目的地，即從當前位置沿著箭頭前往併到達某處。","examples":[{"en":"We walked to the station before sunrise.","zh":"我們在日出前走到了車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They are flying to Madrid tomorrow.","zh":"他們明天要飛往馬德里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/to","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-007722a881f32605","term":"to","forms":["to"],"pos":"prep","zh":"給某人","explanation":"表示動作所指向的接受者或物件，像把東西或資訊沿箭頭交給某人。","examples":[{"en":"Please send the address to me.","zh":"請把地址發給我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She explained the problem to her manager.","zh":"她向經理解釋了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/to","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a60ec1cf58f49cd2fab6","word":"toast","forms":["toast"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-07110e2a3af13d22","term":"toast","forms":["toast","toasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"烤麵包","explanation":"toast 最基本的意思是烤過的麵包，通常指早餐中切片食用的麵包。這裡強調的是食物本身，而不是烘烤這個動作。","examples":[{"en":"I had toast and coffee for breakfast.","zh":"我早餐吃了烤麵包，喝了咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you make me a piece of toast?","zh":"你能給我做一片烤麵包嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b14f1dca8fe9f258","term":"toast","forms":["toast","toasts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"祝酒；祝酒詞","explanation":"toast 也指飲酒時舉杯向某人或某事表示敬意的舉動，或這段祝酒詞。","examples":[{"en":"Her father gave a toast to the newlyweds.","zh":"她的父親為這對新婚夫婦致了祝酒詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please raise your glasses for a toast.","zh":"請舉杯祝酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9c1b8c011e935330","term":"toast","forms":["toast","toasts","toasting","toasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"烘烤至表面變褐","explanation":"指讓食物直接接觸火或熱源，表面受熱變成金褐色；它和名詞“烤麵包”來自同一個“受熱變香”的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We toasted marshmallows over the campfire.","zh":"我們在篝火上烤棉花糖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Toast the nuts for five minutes before adding them.","zh":"把堅果烤五分鐘再加進去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2e806d04c6da880","term":"toast","forms":["toast","toasts","toasting","toasted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"舉杯向某人或某事致敬","explanation":"指飲酒時舉起酒杯，為某人或某事表示祝福、敬意或慶賀。","examples":[{"en":"They toasted the couple's success with champagne.","zh":"他們用香檳為這對夫婦的成功舉杯慶祝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They toasted the newlyweds with sparkling wine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-da43f06caa04c6fd627b","word":"tobacco","forms":["tobacco"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35dbc8fbc627af97","term":"tobacco","forms":["tobacco","tobaccos","tobaccoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"菸草植物","explanation":"指 Nicotiana 屬的一類植物，也就是通常所說的菸草這種作物；重點在整株植物，而不只是收穫後的葉子。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers in this region grow tobacco alongside corn.","zh":"這個地區的農民把菸草和玉米一起種植。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farmers grow tobacco on the sandy hillside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tobacco","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b9831b7821303ec","term":"tobacco","forms":["tobacco","tobaccos","tobaccoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"菸草葉及其原料","explanation":"指從菸草植物上採收、加工，用來製作香菸、雪茄、鼻菸，或用於菸斗吸食、咀嚼的葉子。這個意思常常泛指菸草製品所用的原料。","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells loose tobacco for rolling cigarettes.","zh":"這家店出售用來卷香菸的散裝菸草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The smell of tobacco clung to his coat.","zh":"菸草的氣味久久留在他的外套上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tobacco","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e0f4f767ac88a9303e73","word":"today","forms":["today"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e5c718c46381bdd","term":"today","forms":["today"],"pos":"adv","zh":"今天；在今天","explanation":"指說話或所談日期的當天，也就是日曆上被圈出的“今天”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to finish this report today.","zh":"我今天得完成這份報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Today, the children are studying at home.","zh":"今天孩子們在家學習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/today","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f19b2ce34c9fa37","term":"today","forms":["today"],"pos":"adv","zh":"如今；當今","explanation":"這裡把“今天”從一天擴大到現在這個時代，和過去的情況作對比時尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"Today, most people use smartphones to stay in touch.","zh":"如今，大多數人用智慧手機保持聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Today, most applications are submitted electronically.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/today","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2639e77c9184a779","term":"today","forms":["today","todays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"今天","explanation":"指當前這一天本身，而不是這一天發生的某個具體事件。","examples":[{"en":"Today is the day we finally start the project.","zh":"今天就是我們終於開始這個專案的日子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Today's meeting starts at nine.","zh":"今天的會議九點開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/today","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d0ef3950c22cb1913d5","word":"toe","forms":["toe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-36a5af8f8f3def1d","term":"toe","forms":["toe","toes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腳趾","explanation":"toe 是腳最前端的一個趾，五個腳趾合在一起就是腳趾。這個核心義也構成了許多引申義的形象基礎。","examples":[{"en":"I stubbed my toe on the table.","zh":"我的腳趾撞到了桌子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She painted her toenails bright red.","zh":"她把腳趾甲塗成了鮮紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a500f537ff5cee3c","term":"toe","forms":["toe","toes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞋頭或襪頭","explanation":"toe 還指鞋或襪子包住腳趾的前端部分，也就是“腳趾所在的那一頭”。","examples":[{"en":"The toe of my shoe is scuffed.","zh":"我的鞋頭擦花了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There's a hole in the toe of my sock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-de2a639907c6e78b","term":"toe","forms":["toe","toes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"末端突出部","explanation":"因為腳趾伸在腳的末端，任何形狀或位置像腳趾一樣位於最外端的部分，也可以叫 toe，例如某些工具或器物的最前端。","examples":[{"en":"The toe of the club struck the ground first.","zh":"球杆的外側前端先碰到了地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glacier's toe reached nearly to the road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cc52e9ceb39eabd803ce","word":"tofu","forms":["tofu"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-89c316c3a96b342d","term":"tofu","forms":["tofu","tofus"],"pos":"noun","zh":"豆腐","explanation":"tofu是把豆漿凝固後製成的富含蛋白質的食物，通常呈白色方塊狀，可以直接烹調或加入其他菜餚。它的形狀也幫助記住這個詞在技術語境中的另一個方框義。","examples":[{"en":"We added tofu to the soup for extra protein.","zh":"我們在湯里加了豆腐，以增加蛋白質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cut the tofu into small cubes and fried them.","zh":"她把豆腐切成小方塊後煎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tofu","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c24734d7bf5954f08e5","word":"together","forms":["together"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-369ff6cfca7ba92e","term":"together","forms":["together"],"pos":"adv","zh":"一起；在同一處","explanation":"指兩個人或多個人共同做事，或共同出現在同一地點、同一場合。核心畫面是把彼此放在同一個圈裡。","examples":[{"en":"We went to the market together after breakfast.","zh":"我們吃過早飯後一起去了市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children sat together during the story.","zh":"講故事時，孩子們坐在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/together","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7c13354b82e31fd7","term":"together","forms":["together"],"pos":"adv","zh":"合在一起；拼到一起","explanation":"指把分散的部分、物品或資訊放到同一個整體中。它延續了“聚到同一個圈裡”的畫面，但重點從人共同活動變成了合併和組裝。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the documents together before the meeting.","zh":"請在會議前把這些檔案整理到一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These four pieces fit together perfectly.","zh":"這四個部件正好能拼在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/together","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78b76f4200d6d198","term":"together","forms":["together"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在一起；共同建立關係","explanation":"指兩個人或多個夥伴共同經營、合作，或維持戀愛等親密關係。這裡的“一起”不只是同處一地，而是持續把生活、工作或目標放在同一個圈裡。","examples":[{"en":"They have been together for three years.","zh":"他們在一起已經三年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They've been together since their university days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/together","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74f7fd1cf08b145c5859","word":"toilet","forms":["toilet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e21f27bd862d3229","term":"toilet","forms":["toilet","toilets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廁所；衛生間","explanation":"指供人小便或大便的房間、隔間或獨立小建築，重點是“可以進去使用的空間”，而不是裡面的器具。","examples":[{"en":"I'll be in the toilet for a minute.","zh":"我去一下廁所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toilet is at the end of the corridor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toilet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c09a2510ba2d39df","term":"toilet","forms":["toilet","toilets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬桶；坐便器","explanation":"指廁所裡的排洩器具，通常是帶環形座圈、用水沖走排洩物的馬桶；這裡說的是一個具體物件，而不是房間。","examples":[{"en":"The toilet is blocked, so please use the other bathroom.","zh":"馬桶堵了，請用另一個衛生間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please flush the toilet after you use it.","zh":"用完馬桶後請沖水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toilet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3c469e9d6c5875d37a43","word":"token","forms":["token"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01f05199d7990299","term":"token","forms":["token","tokens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"象徵物；信物","explanation":"指用來表達、代表另一種情感、關係、承諾或意義的東西，也就是把某種看不見的內容變成可見標記的“代表物”。","examples":[{"en":"The bracelet was a token of their friendship.","zh":"這條手鍊是他們友誼的象徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave him a flower as a token of thanks.","zh":"她送給他一朵花，以表達謝意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/token","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb5845531d6f398c","term":"token","forms":["token","tokens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代幣；兌換券","explanation":"指代表一定金額或一次服務的金屬片、塑膠片或紙券，可以用來付款或兌換商品、服務；它本身不是通常的錢，而是價值的替代標記。","examples":[{"en":"The old arcade still accepts tokens for the games.","zh":"那家老遊戲廳仍然接受用代幣玩遊戲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought three tokens for the airport shuttle.","zh":"我買了三枚機場接駁車代幣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/token","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-24cd57fa3b020b22","term":"token","forms":["token","tokens"],"pos":"noun","zh":"棋子；代表角色的物件","explanation":"指棋盤遊戲或類似活動中用來代表某個玩家、人物或角色的小物件；它不是角色本身，而是代表角色的標記。","examples":[{"en":"Choose a token and place it on the first square.","zh":"選一個棋子，把它放在第一個格子上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My blue token landed on the bonus space.","zh":"我的藍色棋子落在了獎勵格上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/token","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5d64216c1247c75dbb3","word":"tolerable","forms":["tolerable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8043a50180e351b2","term":"tolerable","forms":["tolerable","more tolerable","most tolerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可忍受的","explanation":"指某種痛苦、困難或不便雖然令人不舒服，但還沒有嚴重到無法承受的程度。","examples":[{"en":"The heat was barely tolerable without air conditioning.","zh":"沒有空調，這種高溫幾乎難以忍受。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The pain became tolerable after I took the medicine.","zh":"我吃藥後，疼痛變得可以忍受了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb67952e459d0665","term":"tolerable","forms":["tolerable","more tolerable","most tolerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"還過得去的","explanation":"指質量、表現或結果處在中等水平，不能算好，但勉強可以接受；常常相當於“尚可”或“馬馬虎虎”。","examples":[{"en":"The food was tolerable, but I would not recommend the restaurant.","zh":"這家餐館的食物還過得去，但我不會推薦它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The food was tolerable, though rather bland.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41e1e73d5586f1b64bf6","word":"tolerance","forms":["tolerance"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-598c21078cf5d3eb","term":"tolerance","forms":["tolerance","tolerances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬容；包容","explanation":"指接受或耐心對待他人與自己不同的信仰、意見和做法，不因差異而表現出偏見。這是 tolerance 在社會和日常討論中最重要的含義。","examples":[{"en":"Schools should teach tolerance toward people with different beliefs.","zh":"學校應該教導人們包容信仰不同的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her tolerance of criticism impressed everyone.","zh":"她對批評的包容讓所有人印象深刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02255125427a6b18","term":"tolerance","forms":["tolerance","tolerances"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公差；允許誤差","explanation":"指實際尺寸或數值可以偏離標準的範圍，仍然被認為合格。例如零件不必與標稱尺寸完全相同，只要偏差沒有超出 tolerance 即可。","examples":[{"en":"The part must be machined within a tolerance of two millimeters.","zh":"這個零件的加工誤差必須控制在兩毫米以內。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Even a tiny error exceeds the tolerance permitted for these engine components.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerance","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed80ec951eb5c9e17ad9","word":"tolerant","forms":["tolerant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5eb944e91e834536","term":"tolerant","forms":["tolerant","more tolerant","most tolerant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬容的；包容的","explanation":"指一個人或群體能夠接受與自己不同的觀點、行為或生活方式，不輕易排斥或責怪對方。它強調“容得下差異”，不等於認為對方一定正確。","examples":[{"en":"Our teacher is tolerant of different opinions in class.","zh":"我們的老師包容課堂上的不同意見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is tolerant of people whose lifestyles differ from hers.","zh":"她能包容生活方式與自己不同的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7e11a4f355765fb","term":"tolerant","forms":["tolerant","more tolerant","most tolerant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"耐受的；能經受的","explanation":"指植物、生物、材料或系統能夠在某種不利條件下繼續生存或正常運作。這裡把“容得下”從人的態度擴充套件到了對環境條件的承受能力。","examples":[{"en":"This grass is tolerant of heat and requires very little water.","zh":"這種草耐高溫，而且只需要很少的水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These plants are tolerant of salty coastal winds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3913e8d04d35e5ee8c9c","word":"tolerate","forms":["tolerate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-57148bc8ef45f560","term":"tolerate","forms":["tolerate","tolerates","tolerating","tolerated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"容忍；放任","explanation":"指明明認為某種行為不好，卻沒有明確制止，暫時讓它繼續存在。重點不是贊成，而是把不喜歡的東西留在身邊。","examples":[{"en":"The school will not tolerate bullying.","zh":"這所學校不會容忍欺凌行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tolerated his lies for too long.","zh":"她容忍他的謊言太久了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0f3bfaef928a937","term":"tolerate","forms":["tolerate","tolerates","tolerating","tolerated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"忍受；承受","explanation":"指身體或心理上能夠承受不舒服、困難或令人討厭的情況，哪怕並不喜歡。這裡不是讓別人繼續做某事，而是自己還能把這種情況撐下去。","examples":[{"en":"I can't tolerate the noise while I'm working.","zh":"我工作時無法忍受這種噪音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He can tolerate working under pressure.","zh":"他能夠忍受在壓力下工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tolerate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bcade5095df6aac49c93","word":"toll","forms":["toll"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8fcdf5f98c5ee4d9","term":"toll","forms":["toll","tolls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通行費","explanation":"toll 是為了獲得通行或使用某條道路、橋樑等權利而支付的錢，最常見的是高速公路或橋樑通行費。","examples":[{"en":"We had to pay a toll to cross the bridge.","zh":"我們過橋時必須支付通行費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This highway has no toll.","zh":"這條高速公路不收費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b5fd9d273882937","term":"toll","forms":["toll","tolls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"造成的損失","explanation":"在引申義中，toll 是災難、壓力或長期困難從人或社會身上“收走”的健康、力量或生命，指由此造成的損失。","examples":[{"en":"Years of stress have taken their toll on her health.","zh":"多年的壓力已經損害了她的健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The long journey began to take a toll on the team.","zh":"這段漫長的旅程開始讓團隊吃不消了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f645a2cdb60b60e9","term":"toll","forms":["toll","tolls","tolling","tolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收取使用費","explanation":"作動詞時，toll 表示因使用道路、橋樑等而向使用者收取費用，也就是讓對方支付通行費。","examples":[{"en":"The city plans to toll the new tunnel.","zh":"市政府計劃對這條新隧道收費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company tolls the bridge to fund maintenance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f9a6a6e94eac14a","term":"toll","forms":["toll","tolls","tolling","tolled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"緩慢敲鐘","explanation":"toll a bell 表示讓鍾緩慢而反覆地響，一聲一聲傳開。","examples":[{"en":"The bell tolled slowly as the ceremony began.","zh":"儀式開始時，鐘聲緩慢地一下一下響起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They tolled the bell for the victims.","zh":"他們為遇難者緩慢敲鐘致哀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toll","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ed728c2fa5d767bc6c1","word":"tomato","forms":["tomato"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de326b640d3c2d59","term":"tomato","forms":["tomato","tomatoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"番茄植物","explanation":"指結出番茄果實的植物本身；談種植、品種或園藝時，重點是整株植物。","examples":[{"en":"We planted three tomato plants in the garden.","zh":"我們在花園裡種了三株番茄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tomatoes need taller stakes to support their fruit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomato","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a4a51e11fcd77ae","term":"tomato","forms":["tomato","tomatoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"番茄果實","explanation":"指番茄植物結出的可食用果實，通常成熟時是紅色，做沙拉、醬汁等都很常見。","examples":[{"en":"I sliced a tomato for the salad.","zh":"我切了一個番茄放進沙拉里。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These tomatoes are very ripe.","zh":"這些番茄已經很熟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomato","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f2a6aa97adb2bf15c27a","word":"tomb","forms":["tomb"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b016bea2eb9e6e7a","term":"tomb","forms":["tomb","tombs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"墓、墓室","explanation":"指有牆和頂、用來安放死者遺體的墓室或陵墓，可以獨立建造，也可以位於教堂或地下墓室中。","examples":[{"en":"The family tomb stands behind the old church.","zh":"這座家族墓室坐落在老教堂後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Archaeologists opened the ancient tomb carefully.","zh":"考古學家小心地開啟了那座古墓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4364488159bde5b8","term":"tomb","forms":["tomb","tombs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"墓穴","explanation":"泛指埋葬人的坑穴或墓地；這裡不一定強調墓室的建築結構，是“墓”的較寬泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"The body was placed in a shallow tomb near the village.","zh":"遺體被安葬在村子附近的一處淺墓穴中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archaeologists uncovered a sealed stone tomb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bafd151a86f9a573b153","word":"tomorrow","forms":["tomorrow"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b901736c61d760d6","term":"tomorrow","forms":["tomorrow"],"pos":"adv","zh":"明天","explanation":"指緊接著今天的那一天，是 tomorrow 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll call you tomorrow.","zh":"我明天給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tomorrow will be sunny.","zh":"明天會是晴天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomorrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b8f0d11b0f19a4fd","term":"tomorrow","forms":["tomorrow"],"pos":"adv","zh":"以後；將來","explanation":"從“明天”擴充套件為眼下尚未到來的時間，常表示較寬泛的將來，而不強調具體是哪一天。","examples":[{"en":"If you ignore the problem today, you may regret it tomorrow.","zh":"如果你今天忽視這個問題，將來可能會後悔。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tomorrow's technology may solve problems we cannot address today.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomorrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b77046f2b0fe16e4","term":"tomorrow","forms":["tomorrow","tomorrows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"明天","explanation":"指今天之後的那一天，作名詞時可以充當句子的主語或其他名詞成分。","examples":[{"en":"Tomorrow is my day off.","zh":"明天是我的休息日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tomorrow is the last day to register.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tomorrow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d537bc9c04d322df1838","word":"ton","forms":["ton"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1bea0852299bbb3","term":"ton","forms":["ton","tons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噸；質量單位","explanation":"一種質量單位，通常譯作“噸”；不同地區使用的噸可能不是完全相同的標準。","examples":[{"en":"The truck can carry ten tons of sand.","zh":"這輛卡車能運十噸沙子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The delivery contained two tons of gravel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7cfb205661116c1","term":"ton","forms":["ton","tons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量；極多","explanation":"從“一個裝得滿滿的大桶”引申出來，表示某種東西多得像裝滿了很多桶，常用於誇張地說“很多、極多”。","examples":[{"en":"I’ve got a ton of work to do.","zh":"我有一大堆工作要做。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There were tons of people at the concert.","zh":"音樂會上人多得不得了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ton","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00cf4ce3935c8a60a1ac","word":"tone","forms":["tone"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-985915cb37085573","term":"tone","forms":["tone","tones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音高","explanation":"tone 可以指聲音本身處在什麼高低位置，也就是音高；它關注聲音高還是低，不主要關注聲音聽起來是否粗糙或圓潤。","examples":[{"en":"The singer reached a very high tone.","zh":"這位歌手唱到了很高的音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The instrument produces a clear, bright tone.","zh":"這種樂器發出的聲音清晰而明亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96ca4e5d62472d75","term":"tone","forms":["tone","tones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音質、音色","explanation":"tone 可以指聲音聽起來的質感，例如柔和、刺耳、溫暖或明亮；它和音高不同，更接近聲音的“顏色”。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm tone made everyone feel safe.","zh":"她平靜的聲音讓大家都感到安心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This guitar has a rich tone.","zh":"這把吉他的音色很渾厚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f0c0b42104ede061","term":"tone","forms":["tone","tones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說話或寫作的語氣","explanation":"tone 可以表示表達內容時流露出的態度和情緒，例如禮貌、諷刺、威脅、不滿或輕鬆；同一句話換一種 tone，給人的感覺就會不同。","examples":[{"en":"The tone of her email sounded impatient.","zh":"她那封郵件的語氣聽起來很不耐煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please keep a respectful tone in the discussion.","zh":"請在討論中保持尊重的語氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b2715212d939ec804d6d","word":"tongue","forms":["tongue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f087d56f009ff97","term":"tongue","forms":["tongue","tongues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舌頭","explanation":"指口腔中的柔軟肌肉器官，幫助移動食物、感受味道，也能改變氣流來發音。記住“舌頭”這個核心概念，就能理解它為什麼還表示語言和說話方式。","examples":[{"en":"She burned her tongue on the hot soup.","zh":"她喝熱湯時燙到了舌頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor asked him to stick out his tongue.","zh":"醫生讓他伸出舌頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tongue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a81c0cde8637a417","term":"tongue","forms":["tongue","tongues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"語言","explanation":"指一種語言；因為舌頭參與發音，所以“舌頭”引申出了“語言”這一意義。","examples":[{"en":"Spanish is her native tongue.","zh":"西班牙語是她的母語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several different tongues are spoken in the region.","zh":"這個地區使用幾種不同的語言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tongue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb263b082574d69d","term":"tongue","forms":["tongue","tongues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"說話方式","explanation":"指一個人慣常的說話方式，尤其是措辭給人的印象；舌頭會說話，因此可借“舌頭”來描述口才或言辭。","examples":[{"en":"Her sharp tongue often gets her into trouble.","zh":"她說話尖刻，常常因此惹上麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He held his tongue during the meeting.","zh":"開會時他忍住了沒有說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tongue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2769fc20451b51737baa","word":"tonight","forms":["tonight"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-400a935ce993c8d4","term":"tonight","forms":["tonight"],"pos":"adv","zh":"今晚；今夜","explanation":"表示事情發生在從今天傍晚到夜間的這段時間，也就是說話時所指的“今晚”。","examples":[{"en":"I want to stay home tonight.","zh":"我今晚想待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you free tonight?","zh":"你今晚有空嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tonight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69fb25fbe2285527","term":"tonight","forms":["tonight","tonights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"今晚；今夜這段時間","explanation":"把今晚當作一個時間段或一個特別的夜晚來談，而不是單純說明某個動作何時發生。","examples":[{"en":"Tonight is the night we finally celebrate.","zh":"今晚就是我們終於慶祝的日子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tonight promises clear skies and cooler temperatures.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tonight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94c05f1c45a1d1a913e0","word":"too","forms":["too"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-17ef028199c78a8e","term":"too","forms":["too"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也；同樣","explanation":"表示某人或某事與前面提到的情況相同，帶有把同樣的情況再添上的感覺；常用於突出“這個也一樣”。","examples":[{"en":"I want to come too.","zh":"我也想來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children were excited, and the teachers too.","zh":"孩子們很興奮，老師們也一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/too","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94f8d5d6e3722525","term":"too","forms":["too"],"pos":"adv","zh":"也；另外","explanation":"表示前一句說的情況同樣適用於另一件事或另一個人，相當於在已有資訊上再增加一項。","examples":[{"en":"The tickets are expensive, and the hotel is expensive too.","zh":"票很貴，酒店也很貴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her sister plays the violin, and she does too.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/too","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aeb9923b181e146c","term":"too","forms":["too"],"pos":"adv","zh":"太；過於","explanation":"表示某種程度超過了需要、合適範圍或說話人的接受限度，常帶有“不合適”的意味。","examples":[{"en":"This box is too heavy for me to carry.","zh":"這個箱子太重了，我搬不動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You are driving too fast.","zh":"你開得太快了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/too","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c9bbe5ec9b3fb774e8f","word":"tool","forms":["tool"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4545615c96bd16d","term":"tool","forms":["tool","tools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實體工具","explanation":"幫助人完成某項工作的具體器具，例如錘子、刀或石斧；核心概念是“用來做事的幫手”。","examples":[{"en":"A hammer is a simple tool for driving nails.","zh":"錘子是用來釘釘子的簡單工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archaeologists found several stone tools.","zh":"考古學家發現了幾件石制工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e3c8e3b6168e8cc4","term":"tool","forms":["tool","tools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抽象手段","explanation":"任何能幫助人完成操作、達到目的的方法、資源或手段，都可以比作 tool；它不必是有形物體。","examples":[{"en":"Language is a powerful tool for building trust.","zh":"語言是建立信任的有力工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The campaign used fear as a political tool.","zh":"這場運動把恐懼當作一種政治手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9722d4a4b59ce537542d","word":"tooth","forms":["tooth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-749516f65ac18e9a","term":"tooth","forms":["tooth","teeth"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牙齒","explanation":"指人或其他脊椎動物口中堅硬的結構，主要用來咬斷和咀嚼食物。這是 tooth 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I chipped a tooth while biting into an ice cube.","zh":"我咬冰塊時磕掉了一小塊牙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy has very sharp teeth.","zh":"這隻小狗的牙齒非常尖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tooth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7153a86186dd04c026f5","word":"toothache","forms":["toothache"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ba5d1340e7f40c5","term":"toothache","forms":["toothache","toothaches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牙痛","explanation":"指牙齒產生的疼痛或痠痛，是牙齒髮出的“疼痛警報”。既可以泛指牙痛這種症狀，也可以指一次具體的牙痛。","examples":[{"en":"I have had a toothache since yesterday.","zh":"我從昨天開始就牙痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She went to the dentist because of a terrible toothache.","zh":"她因為牙痛得厲害，所以去看牙醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toothache","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8d8d7dbe6559acfc6bb4","word":"toothbrush","forms":["toothbrush"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-50c873baa793151c","term":"toothbrush","forms":["toothbrush","toothbrushes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"牙刷","explanation":"用於配合牙膏清潔牙齒的刷子，就是牙刷；這個詞由“牙齒”和“刷子”直接組合而來。","examples":[{"en":"I need to buy a new toothbrush.","zh":"我需要買一把新牙刷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep your toothbrush dry between uses.","zh":"每次使用後都要讓牙刷保持乾燥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toothbrush","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28720365c5e7476a011e","word":"top","forms":["top"],"officialPos":"n./adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-828f514e521914aa","term":"top","forms":["top"],"pos":"adj","zh":"頂尖的；最優秀的","explanation":"表示質量、名望或等級達到最高水平，正如站在山頂一樣；可形容學校、機構、人才或事物。","examples":[{"en":"She was accepted by one of the top medical schools in the country.","zh":"她被這個國家最頂尖的醫學院之一錄取了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This restaurant is considered a top destination for seafood lovers.","zh":"這家餐廳被認為是海鮮愛好者的頂級去處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/top","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb726e72660108b5","term":"top","forms":["top","tops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"頂部；最上面","explanation":"指某個東西實際位於最上面的部分，就像山的山頂一樣；也可以指樹、建築物等的頂部。","examples":[{"en":"His kite got caught at the top of the tree.","zh":"他的風箏掛在了樹頂上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Dust covered the top of the wardrobe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/top","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6968797caf038360","term":"top","forms":["top","tops","topping","topped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"超過；勝過","explanation":"超過原來的最高點或對手，達到更高的位置；這裡正對應“登上山頂、超過別人”的記憶鉤子。","examples":[{"en":"The sequel topped the original at the box office.","zh":"這部續集的票房超過了前作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She topped her previous score in the final round.","zh":"她在最後一輪超過了自己之前的分數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/top","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d787197bb361922","term":"top","forms":["top","tops","topping","topped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"位居第一；登上榜首","explanation":"位於排行榜的最頂端，也就是登上第一位。","examples":[{"en":"The song topped the charts for three weeks.","zh":"這首歌連續三週位居排行榜榜首。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her novel topped the bestseller list.","zh":"她的小說登上了暢銷書榜首。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/top","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-23d611a6f6f8e3ef8775","word":"topic","forms":["topic"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a803a08d20240551","term":"topic","forms":["topic","topics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主題；話題","explanation":"指談話、文章、課程或活動所圍繞的內容或一般興趣範圍。可以把它想成大家圍著一起討論的中心牌子。","examples":[{"en":"Climate change was the main topic of our meeting.","zh":"氣候變化是我們會議的主要話題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose an interesting topic for her essay.","zh":"她為自己的文章選了一個有趣的主題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/topic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37bf51bfba4699a940ce","word":"torch","forms":["torch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f3b68b140717102","term":"torch","forms":["torch","torches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火炬；火把","explanation":"一種手持的照明工具，通常是一端著火的木棍或纖維束，用來照亮道路、場所或儀式現場。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers carried torches through the dark forest.","zh":"徒步旅行者們舉著火炬穿過漆黑的森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She lit a torch to look under the door.","zh":"她開啟手電筒，檢視門底下的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8785c5d1cae4fe6e","term":"torch","forms":["torch","torches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"需要傳承的事業或原則","explanation":"指一種需要被保護並交給下一代的事業、原則、傳統或責任，就像接力賽中一棒一棒傳遞火炬。","examples":[{"en":"The younger generation must carry the torch for equality.","zh":"年輕一代必須接過促進平等的火炬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The younger volunteers will carry the torch for reform.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5218c3a0b88f01a","term":"torch","forms":["torch","torches","torching","torched"],"pos":"verb","zh":"縱火焚燒","explanation":"故意放火燒燬某物，通常含有破壞、犯罪或惡意行為的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Someone torched an empty warehouse during the night.","zh":"有人在夜裡放火燒了一座空倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gang torched the car and fled.","zh":"那幫人燒掉汽車後逃走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2345b0d2fd69db3bfa9a","word":"torment","forms":["torment"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb1bb983d58680a1","term":"torment","forms":["torment","torments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酷刑；拷打","explanation":"torment可以指施加在身體上的嚴酷拷打，尤其讓人聯想到刑具造成的強烈痛苦；這是後來“精神折磨”等義項的具體來源。","examples":[{"en":"The prisoners endured weeks of torment before they were released.","zh":"囚犯們在獲釋前忍受了數週的酷刑折磨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captives suffered physical torment on the rack.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1aaf9758edab89c","term":"torment","forms":["torment","torments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"極度的身心痛苦","explanation":"torment也指強烈而持續的身體痛苦、精神 anguish或悲慘處境，不一定真的有刑具；失戀、內疚、疾病等都可能成為這種折磨的來源。","examples":[{"en":"She lived in torment after losing her closest friend.","zh":"失去最親密的朋友後，她一直生活在極度痛苦之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injury caused him constant torment.","zh":"這處傷讓他持續遭受劇烈痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-699744ea96c7cb5d","term":"torment","forms":["torment","torments","tormenting","tormented"],"pos":"verb","zh":"折磨；使痛苦","explanation":"作動詞時，torment就是把強烈、持續的痛苦施加給某人或某個生物，既可以是身體上的，也可以是精神上的；反覆騷擾、殘酷對待或讓人長期內疚，都可能構成這種折磨。","examples":[{"en":"The memory of the accident continued to torment him for years.","zh":"那場事故的記憶多年來一直折磨著他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The older children tormented the new student every day.","zh":"年齡較大的孩子每天都欺負、折磨那個新來的學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83716a35515f728928d7","word":"tornado","forms":["tornado"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-848d220343013ae3","term":"tornado","forms":["tornado","tornadoes","tornados"],"pos":"noun","zh":"龍捲風","explanation":"一種猛烈旋轉、呈漏斗狀並且接觸地面的風暴。它會沿著地面移動，因此核心畫面不是普通的大風，而是一根旋轉前進的風柱。","examples":[{"en":"A tornado touched down near the town last night.","zh":"昨晚一場龍捲風在城鎮附近接觸了地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tornado destroyed several houses in minutes.","zh":"這場龍捲風幾分鐘內就摧毀了幾棟房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tornado","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cad4058f8c157d4d9868","word":"torrent","forms":["torrent"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-968d0e4047d1cd4e","term":"torrent","forms":["torrent","torrents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈的急流","explanation":"指水、熔岩等突然增大並快速衝下來的強烈流動，重點是速度、力量和來勢兇猛。","examples":[{"en":"Rain fell in torrents throughout the night.","zh":"整夜大雨傾盆而下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A torrent of water rushed down the mountain.","zh":"一股急流衝下了山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torrent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b11601239f88115","term":"torrent","forms":["torrent","torrents"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量湧來的事物","explanation":"把具體急流的形象用於抽象事物，表示問題、批評、資訊或言語等接連不斷、大量地向某人或某處湧來。","examples":[{"en":"The actor faced a torrent of questions after the announcement.","zh":"公告發布後，這名演員面對著接連不斷的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The announcement unleashed a torrent of complaints.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torrent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-224ec67c8947961173b4","word":"tortoise","forms":["tortoise"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-38741444a44766e5","term":"tortoise","forms":["tortoise","tortoises"],"pos":"noun","zh":"陸地龜","explanation":"一種主要生活在陸地上的龜，身體外面有堅硬的甲殼，遇到危險時能把頭和四肢部分縮排殼裡。這個詞最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思就是這種動物。","examples":[{"en":"The tortoise pulled its head into its shell when it heard the dog.","zh":"聽到狗叫時，那隻陸地龜把頭縮排了殼裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a tortoise slowly crossing the garden.","zh":"我們看著一隻陸地龜慢慢穿過花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tortoise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9270c8c38be2579a7e73","word":"torture","forms":["torture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c3075776125200d6","term":"torture","forms":["torture","tortures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酷刑；折磨行為","explanation":"指故意讓人承受嚴重痛苦的行為，常用於審訊、逼供或懲罰；也可以指實施這種行為的手段或裝置。","examples":[{"en":"People confess to anything under torture.","zh":"人在酷刑下什麼都可能招供。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report condemned the use of torture in the prison.","zh":"這份報告譴責了監獄中使用酷刑的做法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c7e2e9bd790b3a6","term":"torture","forms":["torture","tortures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劇烈痛苦；極度煎熬","explanation":"指身體或精神上強烈到難以忍受的痛苦，重點是正在經歷的痛苦本身，而不一定強調是誰造成的。","examples":[{"en":"The long wait was torture for everyone.","zh":"漫長的等待對所有人來說都是一種煎熬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He was in torture after the accident.","zh":"事故後他承受著劇烈的痛苦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fba5fe70beddc387","term":"torture","forms":["torture","tortures","torturing","tortured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"折磨；施以酷刑","explanation":"指故意讓某人承受嚴重痛苦，通常是為了逼迫對方招供、提供資訊或接受懲罰；也可延伸為讓人長期精神受折磨。","examples":[{"en":"The guards tortured the prisoner to force a confession.","zh":"衛兵折磨那名囚犯，逼他認罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The constant noise tortured the residents all night.","zh":"持續不斷的噪聲讓居民整夜不堪其擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-35319a420294ee17f6cf","word":"toss","forms":["toss"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7a400ef2f9214aa2","term":"toss","forms":["toss","tosses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"向上拋擲","explanation":"指把球或其他東西向上丟擲，動作通常不像正式投擲那樣講究力度或準確性。","examples":[{"en":"With a quick toss, she sent the keys onto the table.","zh":"她迅速一拋，把鑰匙扔到了桌上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child gave the ball a toss and ran after it.","zh":"孩子把球向上一拋，便追了過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9482e06175d24e53","term":"toss","forms":["toss","tosses","tossing","tossed","tost"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向上拋","explanation":"指把某物向上丟擲，通常動作隨手而自然，不一定是為了把它扔得很遠。","examples":[{"en":"Toss the keys over here when you're done with them.","zh":"你用完鑰匙後把它拋到這邊來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tossed a coin into the fountain.","zh":"他把一枚硬幣拋進了噴泉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f62c0a2d1d97208","term":"toss","forms":["toss","tosses","tossing","tossed","tost"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擲硬幣決定","explanation":"指拋硬幣，用正反面來決定有爭議的選擇或誰先行動。","examples":[{"en":"We couldn't agree, so we tossed for the last seat.","zh":"我們無法達成一致，於是用擲硬幣決定誰坐最後一個座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They tossed a coin to decide who would drive.","zh":"他們擲硬幣決定由誰開車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-171c7abcabde7ff0","term":"toss","forms":["toss","tosses","tossing","tossed","tost"],"pos":"verb","zh":"攪拌沙拉","explanation":"指把沙拉里的食材向上翻動混合，使醬汁均勻裹在食材上。","examples":[{"en":"Toss the salad with the dressing just before serving.","zh":"上桌前把沙拉和調味汁拌勻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tossed the greens with lemon and olive oil.","zh":"她把綠葉菜和檸檬汁、橄欖油拌在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toss","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11239872d178729acc9e","word":"total","forms":["total"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-41dc0d0f87c77d53","term":"total","forms":["total","more total","most total"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全部的；整體的","explanation":"指涉及某個事物的全部，而不是其中一部分；也可強調從頭到尾的整體情況。","examples":[{"en":"The total cost of the trip was higher than we expected.","zh":"這次旅行的總費用比我們預想的高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The total number of visitors reached ten thousand.","zh":"訪客總數達到了一萬人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/total","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51ac208647505400","term":"total","forms":["total","more total","most total"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完全的；十足的","explanation":"表示某種性質或狀態達到徹底、毫無保留的程度，常帶有強烈強調色彩。","examples":[{"en":"The project was a total failure.","zh":"這個專案徹底失敗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His account was a total fabrication.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/total","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f099d7c2e62a7e0","term":"total","forms":["total","totals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"總數；總額","explanation":"指把幾個較小的數量加在一起後得到的最終數量或金額，是“零散部分匯成整體”這一核心畫面的名詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"The total came to thirty dollars.","zh":"總額是三十美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The total includes postage and insurance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/total","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02e54d3214eb2d2d","term":"total","forms":["total","totals","totaling","totalling","totaled","totalled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"合計；算出總和","explanation":"把若干收入、費用或其他數額加起來，求出最後的總數；這是“把零散部分收攏成整體”的動作形式。","examples":[{"en":"We totaled the receipts before closing the shop.","zh":"我們關店前把收據上的金額合計了一遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She totaled the scores from all three rounds.","zh":"她把三輪的分數都加起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/total","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0956726750ca787d943","word":"touch","forms":["touch"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4d9be874fd5c21ed","term":"touch","forms":["touch","touches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次觸碰","explanation":"指手、手指或其他身體部位接觸某物的一下，強調這個接觸動作本身。它就像“接觸”這個核心概念最直接的名詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a touch on my arm in the crowded station.","zh":"在擁擠的車站裡，我感覺到有人碰了一下我的胳膊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please don't move the picture without my touch.","zh":"沒有我的觸碰，請不要移動這幅畫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-315b8163e71694f8","term":"touch","forms":["touch","touches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一點點","explanation":"指很少的一點或很小的程度變化，好像某物只輕輕“碰到”了一點。常用於調整位置、味道、顏色或程度。","examples":[{"en":"Add just a touch of salt to the soup.","zh":"給湯里加一點點鹽就好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Move the chair a touch to the left.","zh":"把椅子向左挪一點點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-34f177c8d28ce88f","term":"touch","forms":["touch","touches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯絡","explanation":"指人與人之間保持溝通和了解的關係，也就是彼此持續“接觸”。","examples":[{"en":"Let's keep in touch after you move to another city.","zh":"你搬到另一個城市後，我們保持聯絡吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I lost touch with several classmates after graduation.","zh":"畢業後，我和幾位同學失去了聯絡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a234aaa5a5eb8c7","term":"touch","forms":["touch","touches","touching","touched","toucht","touchest","touchedst","toucheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"觸碰；摸到","explanation":"表示用手、身體或其他物體碰到某人或某物，重點是實際發生了接觸。這個意義最直接地體現了“接觸”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"I touched his face softly.","zh":"我輕輕地摸了摸他的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not touch the wet paint.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dede1e000407c85553e6","word":"tough","forms":["tough"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c65daa56d7d9e859","term":"tough","forms":["tough","tougher","toughest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"結實耐用","explanation":"指材料或物品堅韌結實，能夠承受反覆使用、拉扯或碰撞而不容易損壞。這是“經得住壓力”這條主線最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"These boots are tough enough for long hikes.","zh":"這雙靴子很結實，足以應付長途徒步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These tough boots should last for years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a9c4c260d2736f3","term":"tough","forms":["tough","tougher","toughest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"困難棘手","explanation":"形容任務、問題、決定或局面很難處理，需要付出很多努力；這是“難以對付”從物體和人延伸到事情。","examples":[{"en":"Making that decision was tough for everyone.","zh":"做出那個決定對所有人來說都很難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is a tough course, but you can pass it.","zh":"這門課很難，但你能透過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tough","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d7b44809a0359169b755","word":"tour","forms":["tour"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1ed63d9fd20d341","term":"tour","forms":["tour","tours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊覽；旅行","explanation":"指沿著安排好的路線遊覽某個地區、國家、建築或莊園，重點是按路線看一系列地方。","examples":[{"en":"We took a tour of the old villages along the coast.","zh":"我們遊覽了海岸邊的古老村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum offers a tour of the building every afternoon.","zh":"這家博物館每天下午都提供建築參觀活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d538a9ae8cc3f135","term":"tour","forms":["tour","tours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"導覽；參觀","explanation":"特指在導遊、工作人員或數字系統帶領下參觀某個地方，也可以是網上的虛擬參觀。","examples":[{"en":"The guide gave us a tour of the palace.","zh":"導遊帶我們參觀了宮殿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can take a virtual tour of the apartment online.","zh":"你可以在網上虛擬參觀這套公寓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6245a3ed8b7f0ac2","term":"tour","forms":["tour","tours"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巡演；巡迴訪問","explanation":"指表演者、樂隊或其他團隊按計劃走訪多個地方，通常在各地進行演出或活動。","examples":[{"en":"The band is going on tour in Europe this summer.","zh":"這支樂隊今年夏天要在歐洲巡演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her new tour includes shows in twelve cities.","zh":"她的新一輪巡演包括在十二座城市舉行演出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3918caaf3dab077","term":"tour","forms":["tour","tours","touring","toured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"巡遊；巡演","explanation":"指一個人、樂隊或團隊按計劃前往多個地方，進行旅行、表演或其他巡迴活動。","examples":[{"en":"The singer will tour across Asia next year.","zh":"這位歌手明年將在亞洲巡演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater company is touring in small towns.","zh":"這家劇團正在小城鎮巡演。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tour","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bd0f4bb7d222c5a808c","word":"tourism","forms":["tourism"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b13120ce30d26f93","term":"tourism","forms":["tourism","tourisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅行觀光活動","explanation":"指人們離開自己的居住地，到別處旅行、遊覽和觀光的總體活動，重點在這種活動本身，而不是某一個具體遊客或行程。","examples":[{"en":"Mass tourism damaged the beach.","zh":"大規模旅遊活動破壞了這片海灘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tourism is growing rapidly in the region.","zh":"這個地區的旅遊活動正在迅速增長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tourism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcbc615e794fb86c","term":"tourism","forms":["tourism","tourisms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅遊業","explanation":"指圍繞旅行和觀光形成的行業與經濟活動，包括吸引遊客、接待遊客以及由此產生的服務和收入。","examples":[{"en":"Tourism brings a lot of tax revenue to the area.","zh":"旅遊業為這個地區帶來了大量稅收。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tourism provides much of the island's income.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tourism","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b58951d8a9c710e08d39","word":"tourist","forms":["tourist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-544e3e63aa1708b1","term":"tourist","forms":["tourist","tourists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅遊者；遊客","explanation":"指為了休閒、觀光等娛樂目的而旅行的人，而不是主要為了工作出差的人。這是 tourist 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Tourists filled the old town before noon.","zh":"中午以前，遊客就擠滿了老城區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She traveled to Kyoto as a tourist, not for work.","zh":"她是以遊客身份去京都旅行的，不是去出差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tourist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8238480a99efeae39d7c","word":"tournament","forms":["tournament"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2518f733d38f8e71","term":"tournament","forms":["tournament","tournaments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錦標賽；系列賽","explanation":"tournament 是由多場相關比賽組成的競技賽事，參賽者或隊伍經過一輪輪較量，最後決出一個冠軍或贏家。它可以圍繞同一種遊戲展開，也可以是同一主題下的一系列比賽。","examples":[{"en":"Our team won the tournament after five close games.","zh":"我們隊經過五場勢均力敵的比賽後贏得了錦標賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is training hard for the tennis tournament next month.","zh":"她正在為下個月的網球錦標賽刻苦訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tournament","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f99c095d32405dac653b","word":"tow","forms":["tow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba5dd3de70616e13","term":"tow","forms":["tow","tows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拖車；牽引","explanation":"指用車輛或其他工具把不能自行移動的東西拖走，也指這種牽引行為或車輛被拖著的狀態。日常生活中常用於車輛拋錨後請求拖車。","examples":[{"en":"My car broke down, so I called for a tow.","zh":"我的車拋錨了，所以我叫了拖車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The van needs a tow to the repair shop.","zh":"這輛廂式貨車需要被拖到修理廠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4fa335bbaa9bb08","term":"tow","forms":["tow","tows","towing","towed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拖；牽引","explanation":"指用繩子、鏈條、車輛或其他連線方式把某物拖著移動。它可以用於拖車、船隻和裝置，核心畫面就是一個東西牽著另一個東西走。","examples":[{"en":"The truck towed the broken car off the road.","zh":"卡車把拋錨的汽車拖離了道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They towed the boat back to the marina.","zh":"他們把船拖回了碼頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-81d0c13ae59e5e0ac422","word":"toward/towards","forms":["toward"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f7c2ef03c219bd5","term":"toward","forms":["toward"],"pos":"prep","zh":"朝向","explanation":"表示移動或面對的方向，即朝某個地點或物體而去。它的核心畫面是“向著某處靠近”。","examples":[{"en":"The child ran toward the open gate.","zh":"孩子朝著敞開的門跑去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She turned toward the sound.","zh":"她轉身朝聲音傳來的方向看去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d66152ea145cc80","term":"toward","forms":["toward"],"pos":"prep","zh":"對於；對待","explanation":"表示一個人對另一個人或某件事的感情、態度或反應方向。這裡不是身體移動，而是把內心的態度“朝向”某個物件。","examples":[{"en":"His attitude toward the new staff was friendly.","zh":"他對新員工的態度很友好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His attitude toward the proposal changed after the meeting.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10ca50a8a7148afd6d2a","word":"towel","forms":["towel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-83d0e271838d24b4","term":"towel","forms":["towel","towels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毛巾；擦拭用布","explanation":"指用來吸乾或擦去水分的布，最常見的是洗澡後擦身體的毛巾，也可以是擦手、擦碗或擦地的布。","examples":[{"en":"I grabbed a clean towel after my shower.","zh":"洗完澡後，我拿了一條幹淨的毛巾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please use a towel to wipe up the water.","zh":"請用毛巾把水擦乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/towel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64f4c7c7ebc6a02c","term":"towel","forms":["towel","towels","toweling","towelling","toweled","towelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用毛巾擦乾","explanation":"表示用那塊吸水的布把自己或某件東西擦乾，是從名詞“毛巾”直接發展出來的核心動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"She toweled her hair dry before going outside.","zh":"她把頭髮擦乾後才出門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He got out of the pool and toweled off.","zh":"他從游泳池出來後把自己擦乾了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/towel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad2015263f339bff9681","word":"tower","forms":["tower"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4d38dc6c285947f","term":"tower","forms":["tower","towers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"通訊塔","explanation":"指很高的金屬框架結構，上面安裝微波、無線電、衛星等通訊天線；重點是“高高立起並承載裝置”。","examples":[{"en":"The radio tower stands on the hill.","zh":"那座無線電塔矗立在山上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers are repairing the antennas on the tower.","zh":"工人正在維修塔上的天線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-263e41dd4b087f7c","term":"tower","forms":["tower","towers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高大建築","explanation":"泛指很高的建築或結構，尤其可以指摩天大樓；這裡保留了“像塔一樣高聳”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The new office tower dominates the city skyline.","zh":"那座新的辦公大樓高聳在城市天際線上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could see the tower from the other side of the river.","zh":"我們從河對岸就能看見那座高樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-50ac81f970325a3e011f","word":"town","forms":["town"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ef3b951af2f516d","term":"town","forms":["town","towns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城鎮","explanation":"town 是有住宅、商店、公共服務和地方管理機構的聚居地，通常比村莊大、比大城市小。它的核心畫面就是一座有人生活、購物和辦事的城鎮。","examples":[{"en":"They moved to a quiet town near the coast.","zh":"他們搬到了海邊附近一個安靜的城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The town has three schools and a busy market.","zh":"這個城鎮有三所學校和一個熱鬧的市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/town","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ccb20c6082fe35e","term":"town","forms":["town","towns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"城裡；較城市化的地方","explanation":"相對於說話者所在的鄉村、郊區或較小地點，town 可以指更城市化的地方，常常就是大家去購物、工作或娛樂的“城裡”。","examples":[{"en":"I need to go into town to buy a new phone.","zh":"我得進城買部新手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She works in the village but shops in town.","zh":"她在村裡工作，但到城裡購物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/town","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04651cd5fa4e877d46f1","word":"toxic","forms":["toxic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eb49bf7b0620f94e","term":"toxic","forms":["toxic","more toxic","most toxic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有毒的","explanation":"指某種化學物質進入人體後會造成嚴重傷害，甚至導致死亡。這裡的“毒”可以透過吞食、吸入或其他方式進入身體，重點是它本身具有傷害身體的性質。","examples":[{"en":"Tobacco smoke contains many toxic substances.","zh":"菸草煙霧中含有許多有毒物質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chemical is toxic to fish even in small amounts.","zh":"這種化學物質即使含量很少，也會對魚類造成毒害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toxic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0d9516477bf49e2","term":"toxic","forms":["toxic","more toxic","most toxic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其有害的","explanation":"由身體受到毒害引申而來，形容環境、制度、文化或行為會持續造成嚴重負面影響。它不一定涉及真正的化學毒物，但表示人在其中會受到明顯的心理、社會或實際傷害。","examples":[{"en":"The company had a toxic work environment that drove good employees away.","zh":"這家公司有一種有害的工作環境，把優秀員工都逼走了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Constant criticism can create a toxic atmosphere at home.","zh":"不斷的批評會在家裡造成一種有害的氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toxic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f53133ce57ca8e8937b","word":"toy","forms":["toy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4046e7529dc336b5","term":"toy","forms":["toy","toys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"玩具","explanation":"供人玩耍的物品，尤其是給孩子玩的東西。它是“拿來玩的小東西”這一核心形象的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The child left her favorite toy on the bus.","zh":"那個孩子把自己最喜歡的玩具落在公交車上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toddler carried a wooden toy everywhere.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eafe895eb8119e6e5d06","word":"trace","forms":["trace"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-72324126b65d81c6","term":"trace","forms":["trace","traces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痕跡","explanation":"指人、動物或事物經過後留下的可見或可察覺的標記；腳印、劃痕等都可以是這種線索。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers left no trace in the snow.","zh":"徒步者沒有在雪地上留下任何痕跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Investigators found a trace of paint on the door.","zh":"調查人員在門上發現了一點油漆痕跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-560d53bdc5db5d2c","term":"trace","forms":["trace","traces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"微量殘留","explanation":"指某種物質剩下的一點點，像留下的殘跡一樣少，通常只夠被檢測到或隱約看見。","examples":[{"en":"There were traces of flour on the counter.","zh":"檯面上有少量麵粉殘留。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The glass contained traces of oil.","zh":"玻璃杯裡殘留著微量油。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bd4974f5595b50d7","term":"trace","forms":["trace","traces","tracing","traced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"追蹤線索","explanation":"沿著足跡、線索或證據尋找某人、某物或某個來源，就像順著地上的痕跡一路走回去。","examples":[{"en":"The detective traced the message to a hotel computer.","zh":"偵探追查出這條訊息來自一臺酒店電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We traced the footprints back to the river.","zh":"我們沿著腳印追查回河邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f10b958c82dd123d","term":"trace","forms":["trace","traces","tracing","traced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"追溯歷史","explanation":"沿著時間、發展或因果線索回頭查詢某事的來源和演變過程。","examples":[{"en":"The tradition can be traced back to the fifteenth century.","zh":"這個傳統可以追溯到十五世紀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We traced the custom back to medieval harvest festivals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5c8331addac0129","term":"trace","forms":["trace","traces","tracing","traced"],"pos":"verb","zh":"描出輪廓","explanation":"用筆沿著某物的邊緣或形狀仔細畫出輪廓，像把眼前的線條固定下來。","examples":[{"en":"She traced the outline of the leaf in her notebook.","zh":"她在筆記本上描出了葉子的輪廓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He traced the route on the map with his finger.","zh":"他用手指沿著地圖上的路線描了一遍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bb8bf7259c4ea0edaef","word":"track","forms":["track"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f148909cebe5fa1b","term":"track","forms":["track","tracks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"留下的痕跡","explanation":"track 可以指人、動物、船或車輛經過後留下的連續痕跡；順著這些痕跡，就能推測它走過的路線。","examples":[{"en":"We followed the track of the boat along the shore.","zh":"我們沿著船在岸邊留下的痕跡走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tracks in the mud led toward the river.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/track","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fee4a7f3c2780ed6","term":"track","forms":["track","tracks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鐵路軌道","explanation":"track 可以指火車車輪行駛的鐵軌及其所在的鐵路線路；它是“軌跡”在鐵路交通中的具體形式。","examples":[{"en":"Workers repaired the track after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，工人們修復了鐵軌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Never walk across the railway tracks.","zh":"千萬不要橫穿鐵路軌道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/track","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77b4fbf9b8fe863f","term":"track","forms":["track","tracks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一首歌曲或短音樂作品","explanation":"在專輯或唱片中，track 可以指被單獨錄製、播放並與其他作品分開的歌曲或較短音樂作品；每首歌都像聲音軌跡中的一個獨立部分。","examples":[{"en":"This is my favorite track on the new album.","zh":"這是我最喜歡的新專輯中的一首歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The last track is an instrumental piece.","zh":"最後一首是器樂曲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/track","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33dfc37e4f2a38ee","term":"track","forms":["track","tracks","tracking","tracked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"循跡查出位置","explanation":"沿著線索、痕跡或活動記錄，最終查明某個人或物在哪裡；這是“軌跡”從線索通向位置的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The police tracked the stolen phone to an apartment downtown.","zh":"警方根據線索查到被盜手機在市中心的一套公寓裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We tracked our missing dog to a park near the river.","zh":"我們順著線索找到了走失的狗，它在河邊的一座公園裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/track","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-276446ba01e3aa387c83","word":"trade","forms":["trade"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ed9282fbca956e3","term":"trade","forms":["trade","trades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貿易；買賣活動","explanation":"指在市場上買賣商品或服務的整個活動，是 trade 最基本的名詞意義之一。","examples":[{"en":"International trade has grown rapidly in recent years.","zh":"近年來國際貿易發展得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The two countries trade in coffee and machinery.","zh":"這兩個國家進行咖啡和機械貿易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2066535c28e9c28","term":"trade","forms":["trade","trades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交換；以物易物","explanation":"指雙方把自己的東西交給對方，換取另一件東西；重點是互換，而不一定涉及金錢。","examples":[{"en":"We made a trade: my old camera for his guitar.","zh":"我們做了筆交換：我用舊相機換了他的吉他。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children arranged a trade of stickers for marbles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-217069a012117e5c","term":"trade","forms":["trade","trades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手藝；專業技能","explanation":"指透過學習和實踐掌握的實際職業技能，也可以指這種技能所對應的手藝。","examples":[{"en":"She learned her trade from an experienced carpenter.","zh":"她跟一位經驗豐富的木匠學會了這門手藝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Plumbing is a trade that requires both training and practical judgment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c35c5232dada887","term":"trade","forms":["trade","trades","trading","traded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從事交易","explanation":"指買賣商品、服務或資產，強調參與貿易活動。","examples":[{"en":"The company trades in precious metals.","zh":"這家公司從事貴金屬交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small businesses trade with customers all over the region.","zh":"小企業與整個地區的顧客做生意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d861c8ff82eadebc","term":"trade","forms":["trade","trades","trading","traded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用某物換某物","explanation":"指把自己的東西交出去，換取另一件東西，核心是雙方交換。","examples":[{"en":"Would you trade your bicycle for my skateboard?","zh":"你願意用你的腳踏車換我的滑板嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He traded his old camera for a bicycle.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-40f41af6e6a817c86a9d","word":"trademark","forms":["trademark"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d46b67f38e11bd3d","term":"trademark","forms":["trademark","trademarks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商標","explanation":"公司用一個名稱、詞語、圖案或符號給自己的商品或服務留下專屬標記，消費者就能據此把它和其他公司的產品區分開。","examples":[{"en":"The company registered its new logo as a trademark.","zh":"這家公司把新標誌註冊成了商標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That name is a trademark of a famous sports brand.","zh":"那個名稱是一個知名運動品牌的商標。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trademark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ced21cb6acf34703","term":"trademark","forms":["trademark","trademarks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標誌；典型特徵","explanation":"如果某種特點總是和某人或某事聯絡在一起，它就像留下的專屬標記一樣，成了對方最為人熟知的特徵。","examples":[{"en":"Her calm response has become a trademark of her leadership.","zh":"她冷靜的應對已經成為她領導風格的標誌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His cheerful whistle became a familiar trademark.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trademark","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c40e36253c9be87e0101","word":"trader","forms":["trader"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-60c1039137f139cf","term":"trader","forms":["trader","traders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交易者；貿易商","explanation":"指把買進和賣出商品或證券當作工作、並靠這種交易謀生的人。核心畫面就是“用交易賺錢的人”，因此既可指市場上的交易員，也可指經營商品買賣的貿易商。","examples":[{"en":"The trader made a profit by buying the shares at a low price and selling them later.","zh":"這名交易員低價買入股票，後來賣出並獲利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local traders rely on the holiday season to sell more goods.","zh":"當地商人依靠節日購物季銷售更多商品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trader","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc4d895c3d00dd43be1d","word":"tradition","forms":["tradition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4b006a9b463f9a6","term":"tradition","forms":["tradition","traditions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代代相傳的傳統","explanation":"指一個家庭、群體或社會從前人那裡傳下來、後來繼續保留的做法或習俗；具體細節可能因家庭或地區而不同。","examples":[{"en":"It is a family tradition to eat dumplings together on New Year's Day.","zh":"全家在元旦一起吃餃子是我們家的傳統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village has a long tradition of making pottery by hand.","zh":"這個村莊有手工製陶的悠久傳統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tradition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aa581be2ae94cb19","term":"tradition","forms":["tradition","traditions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"共同認可的傳統體系","explanation":"指一個群體長期共同接受的一套思想、信仰或做法；重點不在某一次活動，而在背後持續存在的共同體系。","examples":[{"en":"The school belongs to a tradition of teaching that values careful observation.","zh":"這所學校屬於一種重視細緻觀察的教學傳統。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school belongs to a long tradition of public service.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tradition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-663666ccaaa4452e6cb9","word":"traditional","forms":["traditional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a437ad8c4dd0d8a1","term":"traditional","forms":["traditional","more traditional","most traditional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"傳統的；沿襲傳統的","explanation":"指與傳統有關，或由過去一代代傳下來的習俗、做法、形式等。這是最基本、最常見的意思，重點在於它和傳統傳承之間有聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"We ate traditional food during the festival.","zh":"節日期間我們吃了傳統食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This dance is a traditional custom in the area.","zh":"這種舞蹈是當地的傳統習俗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traditional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da23796dc6a2dc2d","term":"traditional","forms":["traditional","more traditional","most traditional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"遵循傳統的；守舊的","explanation":"指人、地方或生活方式堅持舊習俗和慣例，不太接受新式做法。它可以只是說明風格保守，也可以帶有“老派”的意味，具體態度要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents have very traditional views about marriage.","zh":"她的父母對婚姻持有非常傳統的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The restaurant serves food in a traditional setting.","zh":"這家餐廳在傳統的環境中提供食物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traditional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-075f4ab854e2a33c8ac1","word":"traffic","forms":["traffic"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ef5b7282fc5e954","term":"traffic","forms":["traffic","traffics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道路交通流量","explanation":"指道路上車輛或行人的持續流動，重點是整體的交通狀況，而不是某一輛車。交通擁堵、緩慢或繁忙，都是這條“流動通道”受到影響的表現。","examples":[{"en":"Traffic is unusually heavy on the highway this morning.","zh":"今天早上高速公路上的車流異常擁擠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We left early to avoid the traffic downtown.","zh":"我們很早就出發了，以避開市中心的擁堵車流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traffic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b47064d15242dcd8","term":"traffic","forms":["traffic","traffics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"商業往來或人員貨物流動","explanation":"指貨物、乘客或人群在運輸和交換中的流動，把“透過通道”從道路延伸到了商業活動。它可以是正常的貿易，也可以泛指某地或某路線上的運輸往來。","examples":[{"en":"The port handles a large amount of traffic between the two countries.","zh":"這個港口承擔著兩國之間大量的貨物和人員往來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The port handles heavy freight traffic throughout the year.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traffic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bf68c8f585383bc2918","word":"tragedy","forms":["tragedy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-78ce98b19f66289a","term":"tragedy","forms":["tragedy","tragedies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"悲劇作品","explanation":"指以人物遭遇毀滅、嚴重失敗或極端痛苦為結局的戲劇或類似文學作品；重點不是單純讓人難過，而是人物最終承受了災難性的後果。","examples":[{"en":"The play is a tragedy about a king who loses everything.","zh":"這部戲講的是一位失去一切的國王，是一部悲劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The theater staged a Greek tragedy last season.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tragedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-15c1ec85d1271182","term":"tragedy","forms":["tragedy","tragedies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慘劇；災難","explanation":"指現實中造成大量人員傷亡、嚴重傷害或巨大損失的災難性事件。它把“走向毀滅的結局”從舞臺上的故事延伸到了真實生活。","examples":[{"en":"The accident was a terrible tragedy for the whole community.","zh":"這場事故對整個社群來說都是一場可怕的慘劇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Losing both parents so young was a terrible tragedy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tragedy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2b6c372eb8584a6ac780","word":"tragic","forms":["tragic"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d121476cae75190","term":"tragic","forms":["tragic","more tragic","most tragic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悲慘的；造成巨大悲痛的","explanation":"形容某件事帶來極大的悲痛或苦難，往往是因為嚴重的不幸、損失或死亡。它比普通的“令人難過”語氣更重，正是“悲劇式的”核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"The family suffered a tragic loss.","zh":"這個家庭遭受了悲痛的損失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her father's early death was tragic.","zh":"她父親英年早逝，實在令人悲痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tragic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17eed05b397f3f6f","term":"tragic","forms":["tragic","more tragic","most tragic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"悲劇作品的；與悲劇有關的","explanation":"指文學、戲劇或其中的情節、人物屬於悲劇，而不是喜劇等其他戲劇型別。這個意思仍然圍繞“悲劇式的”核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The novel has a tragic ending.","zh":"這部小說有一個悲劇性的結局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The actor is famous for his tragic roles.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tragic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-897abbb178d59a98b5bb","word":"trail","forms":["trail"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2fe8433656f1955b","term":"trail","forms":["trail","trails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"痕跡；蹤跡","explanation":"指某人、某物經過後留下的可見線索，例如腳印、血跡，或飛機在天空中的尾跡。它強調“經過之後留下的一條線索”。","examples":[{"en":"The dog followed a trail of mud into the kitchen.","zh":"那隻狗沿著泥巴留下的痕跡走進了廚房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Investigators found a trail of broken branches in the forest.","zh":"調查人員在森林裡發現了一串折斷樹枝留下的蹤跡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37e4024420992393","term":"trail","forms":["trail","trails"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小路；步道","explanation":"指供人、馬等在陸地上行走的路線，通常比普通道路窄，也常常沒有鋪路。它可以是山間步道、森林小徑等。","examples":[{"en":"We took a narrow trail through the forest.","zh":"我們走了一條穿過森林的狹窄小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trail leads to a quiet lake.","zh":"這條小路通向一個安靜的湖泊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8b8ae2e9e9032e2f","term":"trail","forms":["trail","trails","trailing","trailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"跟隨；追蹤","explanation":"指沿著某人或某物留下的路線跟在後面，常含有追蹤目標的意思。它和名詞“痕跡”相連：跟著那條線走，就是 trail 某人或某物。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers trailed the guide through the valley.","zh":"徒步者們跟著嚮導穿過山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The police trailed the suspect for several hours.","zh":"警方跟蹤了嫌疑人幾個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94c5686647edfc67","term":"trail","forms":["trail","trails","trailing","trailed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拖著走","explanation":"指把某物放在身後，讓它在地面上被拖著移動。這個義項直接體現了“拖在後面”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Her scarf trailed along the wet pavement.","zh":"她的圍巾拖在溼漉漉的人行道上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He trailed the heavy net behind him.","zh":"他拖著那張沉重的網走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-116f54c41d0405dbb10e","word":"train","forms":["train"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c2c62505f382dd9","term":"train","forms":["train","trains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續排列的一隊","explanation":"指人或物被“拉成一條”後形成的連續佇列、隨從隊伍或一連串事物。它強調的是彼此相連、前後排列的整體。","examples":[{"en":"A train of visitors moved slowly through the narrow gallery.","zh":"一隊參觀者緩慢地穿過狹窄的展廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm brought a train of problems for the small town.","zh":"這場暴風雨給這個小鎮帶來了一連串問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/train","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-677b037a2ae05694","term":"train","forms":["train","trains","training","trained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"練習能力","explanation":"透過反覆練習把自己的某項能力拉到更好的狀態，通常為了比賽、工作或其他目標。","examples":[{"en":"She trained every morning for the marathon.","zh":"她每天早晨訓練，為馬拉松比賽做準備。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She trains her memory by reciting long poems.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/train","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d51388d77cd6c2d","term":"train","forms":["train","trains","training","trained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"訓練並培養","explanation":"透過練習、指導和教育把某人或某種動物培養到能夠完成特定事情的程度，就像把它拉向目標狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The coach trained the young players to work as a team.","zh":"教練訓練年輕隊員，讓他們學會團隊合作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She trained her assistant to recognize common errors.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/train","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-157e33b984b5723e","term":"train","forms":["train","trains","training","trained"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鍛鍊體能","explanation":"透過有計劃的運動和鍛鍊改善身體狀態，使體能逐漸被拉到更高水平。","examples":[{"en":"He trains with weights three times a week.","zh":"他每週進行三次力量訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The athletes train twice daily during the season.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/train","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-982055e51c25a06a7821","word":"trait","forms":["trait"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3d0b1e172c14644","term":"trait","forms":["trait","traits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"特徵；特點","explanation":"指能勾勒出一個人、動物或事物的穩定特點、習慣或傾向，例如外貌、性格或遺傳特點。它強調這是某個物件具有的可辨認一面，而不是一次偶然發生的事情。","examples":[{"en":"Patience is an important trait for a good teacher.","zh":"耐心是優秀教師的重要品質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppies inherited a distinctive coat trait from their mother.","zh":"這些小狗從母親那裡遺傳了一個獨特的毛色特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3d6951cd9237f968","term":"trait","forms":["trait","traits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可複用的功能集合","explanation":"在物件導向程式設計中，trait 是一組方法的集合；一個類可以借用這組方法，並透過自己的介面使用它們。它介於只規定行為的介面和直接混入實現程式碼的機制之間，重點是複用功能。","examples":[{"en":"This class uses a trait to share logging methods with several other classes.","zh":"這個類使用一種 trait，把日誌記錄方法與其他幾個類共享。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The class uses a trait that provides logging methods.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ace27c86f21a4517161","word":"traitor","forms":["traitor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f95a8bc023f2330","term":"traitor","forms":["traitor","traitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"叛徒；叛國者","explanation":"指背棄國家或所屬陣營、幫助敵人，或把受託防守的地方和軍隊交給敵人的人。這是 traitor 最核心、最典型的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The soldier was branded a traitor for helping the enemy.","zh":"這名士兵因幫助敵人而被罵作叛徒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They accused him of being a traitor to his country.","zh":"他們指控他是背叛祖國的叛徒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-338b1b502c4b2d34","term":"traitor","forms":["traitor","traitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"與本國交戰的叛徒","explanation":"特指拿起武器反對自己的國家，或幫助敵人征服本國的人；這是“叛國者”這一核心義的更具體表現。","examples":[{"en":"He was executed as a traitor after fighting alongside the invading army.","zh":"他與入侵軍隊並肩作戰後，以叛國者的罪名被處決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The traitor fought beside the army invading his homeland.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce922519a3c3ecaf9b09","word":"transaction","forms":["transaction"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d6548ea222728272","term":"transaction","forms":["transaction","transactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"事務的進行","explanation":"指開展或完成一項事務，例如商業活動、談判或計劃的執行；重點在“把事情辦起來、辦下去”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The transaction was completed after several weeks of negotiation.","zh":"經過幾周的談判，這項事務終於完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The office provides rooms for the transaction of business.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2391d4bec715ad4","term":"transaction","forms":["transaction","transactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交易；協議","explanation":"指雙方達成的商業交易或協議，也就是“交付與承諾已經談妥的那一單”。","examples":[{"en":"The company refused to approve the transaction.","zh":"公司拒絕批准這筆交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Both parties signed documents completing the property transaction.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92f6eab217db0d12","term":"transaction","forms":["transaction","transactions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交換；交易","explanation":"強調雙方交換錢、商品、想法等東西；它是“從一方交到另一方”這一核心影象的更廣泛用法。","examples":[{"en":"The two companies completed a transaction involving several patents.","zh":"兩家公司完成了一項涉及幾項專利的交易。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every transaction appears on your monthly statement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transaction","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-54e6289e14c7b0e7ad9a","word":"transcript","forms":["transcript"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dffe17407891261c","term":"transcript","forms":["transcript","transcripts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"抄錄本；文字副本","explanation":"指按照原文把內容寫下來的文字，儘量保留原來的措辭和順序，例如一份講話、檔案或錄音的完整文字稿。","examples":[{"en":"I read the transcript of the interview before writing my report.","zh":"寫報告前，我讀了那次採訪的文字稿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The transcript contains every word of the interview.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transcript","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-77b952a6b590744e","term":"transcript","forms":["transcript","transcripts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口述記錄；庭審文字記錄","explanation":"指把人說過的話逐字或基本完整地寫下來的記錄，例如採訪、會議、審判或演講的文字稿。","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer requested a transcript of the entire trial.","zh":"律師要求取得整場審判的文字記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The podcast transcript is available on the website.","zh":"這檔播客的文字稿可以在網站上找到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transcript","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f36948c908803d95","term":"transcript","forms":["transcript","transcripts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成績單","explanation":"指學校出具的正式記錄，列出學生修讀過的課程以及相應成績，有時還包括學分和學習期間等資訊。","examples":[{"en":"Please send your official transcript with your application.","zh":"請在申請材料中附上你的正式成績單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her transcript shows excellent grades in mathematics.","zh":"她的成績單顯示她的數學成績非常優秀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transcript","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-27f576cafbb263ed44be","word":"transfer","forms":["transfer"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5c8b9b655cb77a11","term":"transfer","forms":["transfer","transfers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轉移；轉交","explanation":"指把某人、某物、資訊或責任從一個地方、物件或狀態移到另一個地方、物件或狀態，重點是“從這裡到那裡”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The transfer of funds took two business days.","zh":"這筆資金轉移花了兩個工作日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The transfer of ownership took place in June.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transfer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b40e920dec867caa","term":"transfer","forms":["transfer","transfers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次轉移；轉交","explanation":"指一次具體的轉移或轉交，結果通常能被看作一個獨立事件，例如一筆轉賬、一次調動或一次物品交接。","examples":[{"en":"The bank confirmed the transfer this morning.","zh":"銀行今天上午確認了這筆轉賬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The transfer of ownership takes effect on Monday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transfer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5e9cd6002a826e5","term":"transfer","forms":["transfer","transfers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"換乘","explanation":"指為了繼續旅程而下車並改乘另一輛公共交通工具，通常是換到另一條線路或另一種交通方式。","examples":[{"en":"We need one transfer to get to the airport.","zh":"我們去機場需要換乘一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The journey requires a transfer at Central Station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transfer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c16ada805f2252d","term":"transfer","forms":["transfer","transfers","transferring","transferred","transferrest","transferredst","transferreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉移；轉交","explanation":"指把人、物、資訊、懷疑或責任從一個地方、物件或狀態轉到另一個地方、物件或狀態。它是 transfer 最基本的動詞用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please transfer the files to the new computer.","zh":"請把這些檔案轉移到新電腦上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Transfer the seedlings into larger pots.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transfer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6388e84c658f0296","term":"transfer","forms":["transfer","transfers","transferring","transferred","transferrest","transferredst","transferreth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"換乘","explanation":"指下車並改乘另一輛公共交通工具，以繼續前往目的地，通常是換到另一條線路或交通方式。","examples":[{"en":"Transfer to the green line at Central Station.","zh":"請在中央車站換乘綠線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Passengers must transfer at the junction for the coastal branch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transfer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa214ea38326805d9566","word":"transform","forms":["transform"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7623cd199d1c4aa","term":"transform","forms":["transform","transforms","transforming","transformed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使外形徹底改變","explanation":"指使某人或某物的外觀、形狀發生很大的改變，彷彿換了一副樣子。它強調變化明顯，而不只是做了小幅調整。","examples":[{"en":"A fresh coat of paint transformed the old room.","zh":"重新刷一層油漆讓那間舊房間煥然一新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The costume transformed her into a completely different character.","zh":"這套服裝把她變成了一個完全不同的角色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0148f1f5ac2987d2","term":"transform","forms":["transform","transforms","transforming","transformed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改變性質或功能","explanation":"指使事物的性質、狀態、功能，或人的性格和內心發生根本改變，也可以表示把一種事物轉化成另一種用途或狀態。這裡的變化不一定看得見，但通常比普通調整更深刻。","examples":[{"en":"The experience transformed her attitude toward failure.","zh":"這段經歷徹底改變了她對失敗的態度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new technology transformed the way people communicate.","zh":"這項新技術改變了人們交流的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b7e172afd07683e8e12","word":"transformation","forms":["transformation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b56355255c8822d3","term":"transformation","forms":["transformation","transformations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轉變；改變的過程或狀態","explanation":"指把某人或某物改變成另一種狀態的過程，或改變之後所處的狀態，重點在“從一種形式變成另一種形式”。","examples":[{"en":"The old factory underwent a complete transformation into a modern arts center.","zh":"這座舊工廠經歷了徹底轉變，變成了一座現代藝術中心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Digital technology has brought about a transformation in the way people work.","zh":"數字技術改變了人們工作的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transformation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2a0f52bbaf3f3a4","term":"transformation","forms":["transformation","transformations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"煥然一新的變化","explanation":"指外表、性格、行為或整體狀況發生顯著變化，通常暗示變化後的狀態更好、更有吸引力或更有效。","examples":[{"en":"After months of training, she made a remarkable transformation.","zh":"經過幾個月的訓練，她發生了顯著的變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The renovation resulted in a dramatic transformation of the neighborhood.","zh":"這次翻修讓這個街區煥然一新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transformation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-068b7e6c97f2284a48f4","word":"transit","forms":["transit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3a1f80ead08b7c94","term":"transit","forms":["transit","transits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經過；穿過","explanation":"指從某處、某一狀態或某個階段穿過去的過程，重點是“由這一邊到另一邊”。","examples":[{"en":"The country is in transit from a rural economy to an industrial one.","zh":"這個國家正在從農業經濟轉向工業經濟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The package was damaged while in transit.","zh":"包裹在運輸途中受損了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00c0d0b7c452bd9a","term":"transit","forms":["transit","transits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轉運；運輸","explanation":"指把人或貨物從一個地方運到另一個地方的過程，尤其強調經過公共運輸系統或途經某地。","examples":[{"en":"The transit of goods through the port has increased this year.","zh":"今年經由這個港口轉運的貨物增加了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fragile equipment was damaged in transit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4ad42dbac1897697","term":"transit","forms":["transit","transits","transiting","transited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穿過；經過","explanation":"指從某物、某地或某個階段穿過去，直接體現“越過並繼續前進”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The train transited through several border towns.","zh":"這列火車經過了幾個邊境城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cargo will transit the canal before dawn.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70dd37c11434d9c571dd","word":"transition","forms":["transition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ffad5dff18860f36","term":"transition","forms":["transition","transitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過渡；轉變","explanation":"指人、事物或情況從一種形式、狀態、風格或地點逐漸轉到另一種形式、狀態、風格或地點，重點是“從這邊到那邊”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"The transition from school to full-time work can be challenging.","zh":"從學校生活過渡到全職工作可能很有挑戰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is going through a major transition.","zh":"這家公司正在經歷一次重大轉型。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fd690e20d081646429b","word":"translate","forms":["translate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-93dc0223618d0632","term":"translate","forms":["translate","translates","translating","translated","translatest","translatedst","translateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"翻譯","explanation":"把文字、講話或其他資訊從一種語言轉換成另一種語言，使另一種語言的讀者或聽眾能夠理解。","examples":[{"en":"She translated the article into Chinese for our website.","zh":"她把這篇文章翻譯成中文，供我們的網站使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This guide has been translated from Japanese into English.","zh":"這本指南已從日語翻譯成英語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/translate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e9b7c2cad6300fce","term":"translate","forms":["translate","translates","translating","translated","translatest","translatedst","translateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"口譯","explanation":"在兩種語言之間即時傳達講話內容，通常發生在會議、旅行或交談中；重點是現場把一方的話說給另一方聽。","examples":[{"en":"Could you translate for us while we talk to the doctor?","zh":"我們和醫生談話時，你能幫我們做口譯嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She translated for the visiting delegation during dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/translate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-839cd11692e82b353998","word":"translation","forms":["translation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7a8470f288a9d71","term":"translation","forms":["translation","translations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"翻譯行為","explanation":"指把文字、語言或表達從一種語言轉換成另一種語言的過程，也就是“翻譯”這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"This contract needs translation into Chinese before we sign it.","zh":"這份合同在簽署前需要翻譯成中文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Automatic translation has improved, but it still makes mistakes.","zh":"自動翻譯已經有所改進，但仍然會出錯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/translation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d0551bbfb975832","term":"translation","forms":["translation","translations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"譯文；翻譯結果","explanation":"指翻譯完成後得到的具體文字、版本或其他表達成果，也就是從另一種語言搬運過來的成品。","examples":[{"en":"I bought a new translation of the novel.","zh":"我買了一本這部小說的新譯本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her translation preserves the humor of the original poem.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/translation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8935b10f056ecd093704","word":"translator","forms":["translator"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0abdb82942161d6a","term":"translator","forms":["translator","translators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"翻譯者","explanation":"指把一種語言的文字或話語轉換成另一種語言的人，是 translator 最常見的意思；有時也可泛指完成這種轉換的工具。","examples":[{"en":"The translator worked carefully on the final chapter of the novel.","zh":"這名譯者認真處理了這部小說的最後一章。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We hired a translator to turn the manual into Spanish.","zh":"我們聘請了一名譯者，把這份手冊翻譯成西班牙語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/translator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a8ad6980da13064","term":"translator","forms":["translator","translators"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口譯員（有時這樣使用）","explanation":"有時 translator 也被用來指把現場講話轉換成另一種語言的人，但這種用法在嚴格區分術語時不夠精確；正式場合通常把口譯員稱為 interpreter。","examples":[{"en":"The translator explained the speaker's answer to the visitors.","zh":"翻譯人員向來訪者解釋了發言人的回答。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The translator conveyed the minister's remarks to the waiting journalists.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/translator","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1d2cafdb2fbaa2b86fe4","word":"transmission","forms":["transmission"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c85fad258ba9cf0e","term":"transmission","forms":["transmission","transmissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳輸；傳送","explanation":"指把訊號、資料、電力等從一個地方或裝置傳到另一個地方的行為或過程。重點在“正在把某物送過去”這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The transmission of data slows down when too many users are online.","zh":"線上使用者太多時，資料傳輸會變慢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The system allows wireless transmission of electricity over short distances.","zh":"這個系統可以在短距離內無線傳輸電力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transmission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97ffb80c4290d95e","term":"transmission","forms":["transmission","transmissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳遞物；傳播","explanation":"可以指被傳送的具體東西，如訊息或圖片，也可以指把這些東西送出去；在公共衛生語境中，還能指病原體或疾病的傳播。","examples":[{"en":"Secure transmission of medical images is essential for patient privacy.","zh":"安全傳輸醫學影象對保護患者隱私至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The transmission of knowledge depends on clear communication.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transmission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9615308f9129db5d","term":"transmission","forms":["transmission","transmissions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變速器；傳動裝置","explanation":"汽車中的 transmission 是把發動機的動力傳到傳動軸和車輪的裝置，通常包含齒輪和離合器或液力變矩器，並能根據車速改變齒輪比。","examples":[{"en":"My car needs a new transmission after years of heavy use.","zh":"我的車使用多年後需要更換一個新的變速器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"An automatic transmission changes gears without a clutch pedal.","zh":"自動變速器不用離合器踏板就能換擋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transmission","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d4db189c0eaacca0fbf5","word":"transmit","forms":["transmit"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4238a5c46004c68f","term":"transmit","forms":["transmit","transmits","transmitting","transmitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳送；傳遞","explanation":"把人、物或其他內容從一個人、地點或事物送到另一個人、地點或事物，重點是完成了“從這裡到那裡”的傳遞。","examples":[{"en":"The device transmits data to the central computer.","zh":"這臺裝置把資料傳送到中央計算機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The message was transmitted from the ship to the shore.","zh":"這條訊息從船上傳到了岸上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transmit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-164a0f6938f28273","term":"transmit","forms":["transmit","transmits","transmitting","transmitted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傳播；傳染","explanation":"把疾病、訊號或其他影響從一個來源傳給另一個物件，使它擴散出去；這裡的“傳送”不一定是有形的移動。","examples":[{"en":"Mosquitoes can transmit this disease to humans.","zh":"蚊子能把這種疾病傳染給人類。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The antenna transmits a signal across the valley.","zh":"這根天線把訊號傳過山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transmit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10e9f5602d2492b386b4","word":"transparent","forms":["transparent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9718ba0a7b68236c","term":"transparent","forms":["transparent","more transparent","most transparent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"透明的；可看穿的","explanation":"指物體能讓光線大致不受阻礙地透過，因此人可以清楚地看見另一邊。它是“看得穿”這一核心形象的字面意義。","examples":[{"en":"The office has transparent glass walls.","zh":"這間辦公室有透明的玻璃牆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use a transparent folder so you can see the documents inside.","zh":"用透明資料夾，這樣你能看見裡面的檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transparent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d526acdf20b97de1","term":"transparent","forms":["transparent","more transparent","most transparent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"公開透明的","explanation":"把資訊、規則或辦事過程公開出來，讓人能夠看見並檢查，從而減少暗箱操作的空間。這是從“看得穿”引申出的抽象意義。","examples":[{"en":"The company needs to be more transparent about its hiring process.","zh":"這家公司需要更公開透明地說明招聘流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The committee promised a transparent selection process.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transparent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9d832614743ff5da","term":"transparent","forms":["transparent","more transparent","most transparent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯而易見的","explanation":"指某人的理由、意圖或事實很容易被看出或理解，幾乎沒有隱藏之處。它把“看得穿”進一步用於思想和動機。","examples":[{"en":"Her reasons for refusing the offer were transparent.","zh":"她拒絕這份提議的理由顯而易見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His transparent excuse fooled nobody.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transparent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6167cdc1bef986f0fed8","word":"transplant","forms":["transplant"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2000a0715bae2988","term":"transplant","forms":["transplant","transplants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"移植行為","explanation":"指把植物連根挖出並移栽到另一個地方這一行為，重點是從原來的土壤中移出，再在新地方紮根。","examples":[{"en":"The transplant of the young trees took place in early spring.","zh":"這些小樹在早春完成了移栽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The surgeon performed a successful kidney transplant.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transplant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-baf356a60995084f","term":"transplant","forms":["transplant","transplants","transplanting","transplanted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"移栽植物","explanation":"指把正在生長的植物從原來的土壤中挖出，再種到另一個地方；這是“換土紮根”這一核心畫面的最直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"We transplanted the tomato seedlings into larger pots.","zh":"我們把番茄幼苗移栽到了更大的花盆裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Transplant the roses while they are dormant.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transplant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e2386101050b7a96","term":"transplant","forms":["transplant","transplants","transplanting","transplanted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遷置或重新安置","explanation":"指把人、建築、傳統或其他事物從原來的環境移到另一處，並在那裡重新建立或安排；它是“移栽”概念向更廣物件的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The old farmhouse was transplanted to the museum grounds.","zh":"那座老農舍被遷到了博物館場地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family was transplanted from its village to a distant city.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transplant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6694ea8075001f6628da","word":"transport","forms":["transport"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-888cc20273c43b7d","term":"transport","forms":["transport","transports"],"pos":"noun","zh":"運輸；運送","explanation":"指把貨物、人或其他東西從一個地方運到另一個地方這一行為或過程，重點在“搬運過去”本身。","examples":[{"en":"The transport of the furniture will take two days.","zh":"這些傢俱的運輸需要兩天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Transport of the equipment required two large trucks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a356010a901add12","term":"transport","forms":["transport","transports","transporting","transported","transportest","transportedst","transporteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"運送；運輸","explanation":"指把人、貨物或其他東西從一個地方帶到另一個地方，是“跨過去搬運”這一核心動作。","examples":[{"en":"The company transports fresh food to restaurants every morning.","zh":"這家公司每天早上把新鮮食品運到餐館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injured hikers were transported to hospital.","zh":"受傷的徒步者被送往醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transport","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b349c79e44d2b99d730","word":"transportation","forms":["transportation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e07170ebe850dfd3","term":"transportation","forms":["transportation","transportations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交通運輸；運輸過程","explanation":"指把人或貨物從一個地方運到另一個地方的行為、過程，或由道路、車輛等組成的交通運輸方式。這裡強調的是“運送”這件事及其整體安排，而不只是某一輛車。","examples":[{"en":"Public transportation is the easiest way to get around the city.","zh":"公共交通是遊覽這座城市最方便的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need better transportation for people living outside the city.","zh":"我們需要為住在城外的人提供更好的交通條件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transportation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee97ac0064016dbb","term":"transportation","forms":["transportation","transportations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交通工具","explanation":"在美國英語的非正式用法中，指實際用來載人或移動的車輛，例如汽車；這是從“運輸方式”具體化來的用法。","examples":[{"en":"That is some nice transportation, but the brake lights are broken.","zh":"這車真不錯，不過剎車燈壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A bicycle was his only transportation for years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/transportation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11ba65852271cd24c56c","word":"trap","forms":["trap"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3f03794be292ef11","term":"trap","forms":["trap","traps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"捕捉動物的陷阱","explanation":"讓動物踩進去、被夾住或被困住的裝置，有時會使動物死亡。","examples":[{"en":"We set a trap under the sink to catch the mouse.","zh":"我們在水槽下面放了一個捕鼠器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The humane trap caught the mouse without injuring it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-11af1a75fc4f4678","term":"trap","forms":["trap","traps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"騙人的圈套","explanation":"一種設計好的騙局或安排，使人上當、受騙或陷入不利處境，就像被誘進陷阱。","examples":[{"en":"She fell into the trap of believing every promise he made.","zh":"她掉進了相信他每個承諾的圈套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The supposed prize offer was a trap.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1716449f1bd4270b","term":"trap","forms":["trap","traps","trapping","trapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"捕獲；困住","explanation":"把動物、人或其他目標用陷阱或類似陷阱的辦法抓住，使其無法逃脫；重點是目標真的被捕獲或困住。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue team trapped the injured fox safely.","zh":"救援隊安全地捕獲了那隻受傷的狐狸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The falling rocks trapped two hikers in the cave.","zh":"落石把兩名徒步者困在了洞裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72b00023808e3a1a","term":"trap","forms":["trap","traps","trapping","trapped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"誘入圈套；使陷入困境","explanation":"用計謀讓某人上當，或使人、手指等意外卡在一個無法輕易脫身的位置；這裡的“陷阱”可以是抽象的，也可以是具體的。","examples":[{"en":"The scam was designed to trap elderly customers into paying twice.","zh":"這個騙局是為了誘使老年顧客重複付款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I trapped my sleeve in the elevator door.","zh":"我的袖子被電梯門夾住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e06da30434b904a063a1","word":"trash","forms":["trash"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-074328a0075a24c8","term":"trash","forms":["trash","trashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"垃圾；廢棄物","explanation":"指沒有用、需要丟掉的實體東西，如廢紙、破物品或其他廢棄物。這是 trash 最基本的意思，也是其他多數義項的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the empty boxes in the trash.","zh":"請把空盒子扔進垃圾桶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beach was covered with trash after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨過後，海灘上滿是垃圾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7048caae484ace1b","term":"trash","forms":["trash","trashes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"劣質東西；差勁的事物","explanation":"把質量很差、沒有價值的事物比作應該被扔掉的垃圾，因此可以形容作品、產品、生活狀況等很糟糕。","examples":[{"en":"I watched the movie, and honestly, it was trash.","zh":"我看了那部電影，說實話，它糟透了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This cheap charger is complete trash.","zh":"這個便宜充電器完全是垃圾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e48e10a5c3f15cf6","term":"trash","forms":["trash","trashes","trashing","trashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"丟棄","explanation":"把某物當作垃圾處理掉，尤其常指刪除檔案或扔掉不再需要的東西。","examples":[{"en":"I trashed the draft because it was full of errors.","zh":"我把那份草稿刪掉了，因為裡面錯誤太多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to trash these broken chairs.","zh":"我們得把這些壞椅子扔掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65c0c75c3e0505c6","term":"trash","forms":["trash","trashes","trashing","trashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄得一團糟","explanation":"把房間、房屋或其他地方弄得像垃圾堆一樣亂，常暗示粗暴破壞或徹底弄亂。","examples":[{"en":"The children trashed the living room while we were away.","zh":"我們不在時，孩子們把客廳弄得一團糟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Someone trashed the hotel room after the party.","zh":"聚會後有人把酒店房間弄得一片狼藉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d9c1d6cbb545ffae","term":"trash","forms":["trash","trashes","trashing","trashed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在比賽中徹底擊敗","explanation":"在比賽或競爭中把對手打得很慘，像把對方當作毫無價值的東西一樣輕鬆擊敗。","examples":[{"en":"Our team trashed the rivals in yesterday’s final.","zh":"我們隊在昨天的決賽中徹底擊敗了對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They trashed their opponents six-nil in the final.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad12f62c45fc1344872a","word":"trauma","forms":["trauma"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-30ca7bdb0422236f","term":"trauma","forms":["trauma","traumas","traumata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體重傷","explanation":"指身體受到的嚴重損傷，通常由暴力、事故或其他強烈外力造成；這裡的重點是身體留下了實際的傷口或損害。","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist suffered serious trauma to his head in the crash.","zh":"那名騎腳踏車的人在事故中頭部受到嚴重創傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctors are checking her for internal trauma.","zh":"醫生正在檢查她是否有內傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trauma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-552e7be89cb5f9e5","term":"trauma","forms":["trauma","traumas","traumata"],"pos":"noun","zh":"心理創傷","explanation":"指令人極度痛苦的經歷在心理上留下的深刻傷口，可能持續很長時間，並影響一個人的情緒、記憶或生活。","examples":[{"en":"She is still dealing with the trauma of the accident.","zh":"她仍在應對那場事故造成的心理創傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The abuse left him with deep emotional trauma.","zh":"那段虐待經歷給他留下了深重的心理創傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trauma","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0209442e115ad7bc79fd","word":"travel","forms":["travel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-eee55850f27700ea","term":"travel","forms":["travel","travels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅行活動","explanation":"travel指從一個地方到另一個地方的旅行這一活動，重點是整體經歷，而不是某一次具體行程。","examples":[{"en":"I enjoy travel, even when the flights are long.","zh":"我喜歡旅行，即使航班時間很長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Travel broadens her understanding of other cultures.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/travel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bfa0c67f3c8851a1","term":"travel","forms":["travel","travels","traveling","travelling","traveled","travelled","travellest","travelest","travelledst","traveledst","travelleth","traveleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"旅行","explanation":"travel作動詞時，表示為了工作、休閒或其他目的，從一個地方到另一個地方旅行，通常帶有一段路程或行程。","examples":[{"en":"She travels to London every week for work.","zh":"她每週都因工作去倫敦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We travelled by train across the country.","zh":"我們乘火車穿越了這個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/travel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d6bc7c52cf46934","term":"travel","forms":["travel","travels","traveling","travelling","traveled","travelled","travellest","travelest","travelledst","traveledst","travelleth","traveleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遊歷某地","explanation":"travel作及物動詞時，可以直接接一個國家、地區或世界，表示在其中各處旅行、把它走遍，而不是隻去其中一個地點。","examples":[{"en":"After university, he travelled the world for two years.","zh":"大學畢業後，他花了兩年時間周遊世界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They traveled the country collecting traditional songs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/travel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd50fc998e7e535b8908","word":"traveler","forms":["traveler"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d50d89bbd949202","term":"traveler","forms":["traveler","travelers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅行者；旅客","explanation":"指正在旅行、途中或經常出行的人，可以是遊客，也可以是因工作、遷徙或其他目的而移動的人；traveler 是美國英語的標準拼寫。","examples":[{"en":"The traveler asked for directions to the nearest train station.","zh":"那名旅客詢問了去最近火車站的路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Experienced travelers know to keep their passports in a safe place.","zh":"有經驗的旅行者知道要把護照放在安全的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/traveler","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad9a0cab12eef9063923","word":"tray","forms":["tray"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc0c0483e5a27da9","term":"tray","forms":["tray","trays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"托盤；托架","explanation":"指一塊平而硬、通常有邊緣的承託物，用來放置、端送或搬運物品。","examples":[{"en":"She carried the glasses upstairs on a tray.","zh":"她用托盤把玻璃杯端上了樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please leave the mail on the tray by the door.","zh":"請把郵件放在門邊的托盤上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-589718f691b41a39","term":"tray","forms":["tray","trays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一托盤的東西","explanation":"可以從“承託物”進一步借指托盤上裝著的整批物品，尤其用於食物或商品。","examples":[{"en":"They ordered a tray of sandwiches for the meeting.","zh":"他們為會議訂了一整托盤三明治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We baked two trays of biscuits for the sale.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tray","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74ae323f9b9abcff9669","word":"treasure","forms":["treasure"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f9a30fa62b7b380e","term":"treasure","forms":["treasure","treasures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珍寶；財富","explanation":"指金錢、珠寶等有很高價值、被集中儲存的東西，也可泛指積累起來的財富；重點是“裝在寶箱裡的珍貴物品”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum protects treasures from ancient Egypt.","zh":"這座博物館保護著古埃及的珍寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children found a box of treasure in the attic.","zh":"孩子們在閣樓裡發現了一箱珍寶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-915906fb8ce540c1","term":"treasure","forms":["treasure","treasures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"珍貴的人或事物","explanation":"指任何被認為極其寶貴、值得珍惜的人、記憶、機會或事物；這裡的“寶”不一定有金錢價值，而是對說話人很重要。","examples":[{"en":"Her grandmother’s letters are a treasure to her.","zh":"她祖母的信對她來說是無比珍貴的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old caretaker is a treasure who knows every corner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cf7b4433670a8b79","term":"treasure","forms":["treasure","treasures","treasuring","treasured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"珍視；珍愛","explanation":"表示認為某人或某物非常珍貴，並在心裡長久重視它；這是把“珍寶”放在心上。","examples":[{"en":"I will always treasure the time we spent together.","zh":"我永遠都會珍惜我們共度的時光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She treasures the ring her mother gave her.","zh":"她很珍愛母親送給她的戒指。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-66fa9f9d3186b9c13a66","word":"treasury","forms":["treasury"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cbb3c0aaa9222cf5","term":"treasury","forms":["treasury","treasuries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財政部門","explanation":"treasury 也可省略指 Treasury Department，即負責國家財政事務的政府部門；這是“國家藏寶庫”發展出的現代機構義。","examples":[{"en":"The Treasury announced a new plan to reduce public spending.","zh":"財政部門宣佈了一項削減公共開支的新計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treasury published its annual spending report.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5aa9a89339a63da3","term":"treasury","forms":["treasury","Treasuries","Treasurys"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國債","explanation":"此義項專指財政部門發行的債券，尤其是美國財政部發行的國債；它是“國家藏寶庫”在金融市場上的憑證化形式。","examples":[{"en":"The fund increased its holdings of US Treasuries.","zh":"該基金增加了對美國國債的持有量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fund shifted its holdings from stocks into Treasuries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasury","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a13c320b24c689caa67","word":"treat(ment)","forms":["treat","treatment"],"officialPos":"v./(n.)","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8002ea090330c47f","term":"treat","forms":["treat","treats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"款待；享受","explanation":"指為了讓別人開心而提供的外出活動、食物、飲料或其他享受，重點是“有人特別安排給你享用”。","examples":[{"en":"I took the kids to the zoo for a treat.","zh":"我帶孩子們去動物園，讓他們好好玩一趟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A hot bath was a welcome treat after the climb.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe29ac1b83139ad8","term":"treat","forms":["treat","treats","treating","treated","tret","treatest","treatedst","treateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"對待；處理","explanation":"指以某種方式對待一個人，或以某種態度處理人與人的關係；核心是“把某人接過來，用某種方式對付或照顧”。","examples":[{"en":"You should treat everyone with respect.","zh":"你應該尊重地對待每一個人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They treated him like a member of the family.","zh":"他們把他當作家人一樣對待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1f9f3fd75fada574","term":"treat","forms":["treat","treats","treating","treated","tret","treatest","treatedst","treateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"請客；款待","explanation":"指由自己付錢或主動提供食物、飲料和活動，讓別人享受或慶祝；這是把“特別的享受”送給某人的動作。","examples":[{"en":"I treated my sister to dinner for her birthday.","zh":"我請妹妹吃晚飯慶祝她的生日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He treated us to coffee after the meeting.","zh":"會議結束後，他請我們喝了咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ecb26acf359b8dec","term":"treatment","forms":["treatment","treatments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對待方式；待遇","explanation":"指一個人或事物受到怎樣的對待、處理，尤其可表示他人給予的待遇是友好、惡劣或不公平的。","examples":[{"en":"The workers protested against their unfair treatment.","zh":"工人們抗議他們受到的不公平待遇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She received kind treatment from her neighbors.","zh":"她受到了鄰居們友善的對待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treatment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-351f1277bac04553","term":"treatment","forms":["treatment","treatments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"治療；療法","explanation":"指標對已經出現的疾病或傷害所採取的醫療照護、治療過程或具體療法，是“處理問題”的醫療延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor recommended a new treatment for her knee injury.","zh":"醫生為她的膝傷推薦了一種新的治療方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He is receiving treatment for asthma.","zh":"他正在接受哮喘治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treatment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-495ed3f6b5ebdce85ee8","word":"treaty","forms":["treaty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a6dc8f9682d6152","term":"treaty","forms":["treaty","treaties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式國際協議","explanation":"指國家或國際組織之間正式達成、對各方具有約束力的協議，通常涉及和平、邊界、貿易或其他國際事務。它就是談判桌上被寫下並需要共同遵守的正式承諾。","examples":[{"en":"The two countries signed a peace treaty after years of conflict.","zh":"兩國經過多年的衝突後簽署了和平條約。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treaty requires both governments to protect the river.","zh":"這項條約要求兩國政府都保護這條河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treaty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc9c5edb8b2d479e697b","word":"tree","forms":["tree"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c880055e083b546","term":"tree","forms":["tree","trees","treen"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樹","explanation":"tree 最基本的意思是有樹幹、枝條和葉子的多年生木本植物。它通常比灌木高大，樹幹會在離地一定高度處分出枝條。","examples":[{"en":"A tall tree shaded the garden in the afternoon.","zh":"一棵高樹在下午為花園遮陰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We planted three trees along the driveway.","zh":"我們沿著車道種了三棵樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1994d77b7cf4860a616b","word":"trek","forms":["trek"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f71f4c4f0120c6d1","term":"trek","forms":["trek","treks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"艱難的旅程","explanation":"trek是一段走得慢、路程長或過程很辛苦的旅程；重點不在交通方式，而在這段路很費力。","examples":[{"en":"We're planning a trek up Kilimanjaro next summer.","zh":"我們計劃明年夏天徒步攀登乞力馬扎羅山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trek through the desert took three days.","zh":"穿越沙漠的艱難旅程花了三天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f748bf8de622bc9c","term":"trek","forms":["trek","treks","trekking","trekked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"艱難地長途旅行","explanation":"trek作動詞時，表示緩慢、費力地走很長一段路或進行艱苦旅行，突出過程辛苦。","examples":[{"en":"The team trekked through the valley before sunrise.","zh":"隊伍在日出前艱難地穿過了山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They trekked to a remote village for supplies.","zh":"他們長途跋涉到一個偏遠村莊去取補給。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trek","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a0a2a7470c13ca4cc938","word":"tremble","forms":["tremble"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c7034d95a08414fa","term":"tremble","forms":["tremble","trembles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"顫抖；震動","explanation":"指身體、聲音或物體不由自主地輕微抖動，強調“抖動”這一現象本身，而不是產生抖動的原因。","examples":[{"en":"There was a slight tremble in her voice.","zh":"她的聲音裡帶著一絲顫抖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A slight tremble in his voice revealed his nervousness.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tremble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a37f43c8d125e5c3","term":"tremble","forms":["tremble","trembles","trembling","trembled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"顫抖；發抖","explanation":"指身體、嘴唇、聲音或物體不由自主地抖動，像細小而連續的震動。這個核心義可以直接描寫看得見或感覺得到的抖動。","examples":[{"en":"Her hands began to tremble as she opened the letter.","zh":"她開啟信時，雙手開始發抖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The windows trembled during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中，窗戶震顫起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tremble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-69d123863a9bd3ad","term":"tremble","forms":["tremble","trembles","trembling","trembled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"害怕；戰慄","explanation":"從實際發抖引申而來，表示因為恐懼或敬畏而戰慄；重點是害怕到身體出現顫抖的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The child trembled with fear when the lights went out.","zh":"燈熄滅時，那個孩子害怕得發抖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She trembled at the thought of losing her home.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tremble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85555b7bc5e611ce1cd2","word":"tremendous","forms":["tremendous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c170c709651b543b","term":"tremendous","forms":["tremendous","more tremendous","most tremendous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人震撼的；威勢驚人的","explanation":"指某人、某物或某個場面氣勢、力量或效果強烈到令人敬畏，重點不是單純的害怕，而是被其強大程度震住。","examples":[{"en":"The team showed tremendous courage under pressure.","zh":"這支隊伍在壓力下展現出了令人震撼的勇氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A tremendous explosion shook the valley.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tremendous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-409ef128296a684c","term":"tremendous","forms":["tremendous","more tremendous","most tremendous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"巨大的；極大的","explanation":"表示數量、程度、範圍或力量大得驚人，帶有“超過通常預期”的感覺；它既能形容積極事物，也能形容損失、壓力等令人難以承受的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The new program has received tremendous support from local residents.","zh":"這個新專案得到了當地居民的大力支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm caused tremendous damage along the coast.","zh":"這場暴風雨給沿海地區造成了巨大的損失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tremendous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2ab022d82080f5d941e0","word":"trend","forms":["trend"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3649e0b9a2fc7d24","term":"trend","forms":["trend","trends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"發展方向","explanation":"指某條線、某個過程或某種變化所朝的方向，重點是“往哪裡延伸或變化”。例如海岸線可以向西南延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The trend of the road is slightly downhill.","zh":"這條路的走向是略微下坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coastline trends north after the bay.","zh":"過了海灣後，海岸線向北延伸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c141435e0f6f31a","term":"trend","forms":["trend","trends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"趨勢；傾向","explanation":"指一段時間裡反覆出現、能夠看出方向的變化或行為傾向。它可以描述社會、經濟、技術，也可以描述人們逐漸形成的做法。","examples":[{"en":"There is a growing trend toward working from home.","zh":"在家辦公正日益成為一種趨勢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The latest figures confirm a downward trend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d7fe27db259a06dd","term":"trend","forms":["trend","trends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流行風潮","explanation":"指在一段時期內受到很多人追隨的樣式、做法或話題，也就是具體可見的流行趨勢。它可以很快消退，不一定長期存在。","examples":[{"en":"Reusable water bottles have become a popular trend among students.","zh":"可重複使用的水瓶已成為學生中流行的風潮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trend for oversized jackets has returned.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-79891e980747ffbd21e6","word":"trial","forms":["trial"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d7e037ace23f5da5","term":"trial","forms":["trial","trials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"試驗；測試","explanation":"指安排一次實際檢驗，看看某人或某物表現如何、是否適合某種用途；這正是“把東西放進現實中試一試”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The school ran a trial of the new reading program.","zh":"這所學校試行並測試了新的閱讀專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After a short trial, we decided to keep the software.","zh":"短期試用後，我們決定繼續使用這款軟體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ee1b85dd5ddd8af","term":"trial","forms":["trial","trials"],"pos":"noun","zh":"審判；庭審","explanation":"指法院中展示證據、聽取相關意見並決定法律問題的庭審，尤其是判斷被告是否有罪；它是“檢驗事實”的法律版本。","examples":[{"en":"The case will go to trial next month.","zh":"這起案件下個月將進入審判程式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was found not guilty at trial.","zh":"她在庭審中被判無罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a3f13c673af2389ecb9","word":"triangle","forms":["triangle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9e57898c0b415e10","term":"triangle","forms":["triangle","triangles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"三角形","explanation":"triangle是由三條邊圍成、具有三個角的平面圖形。它是這個詞最基本的形象，也是其他許多含義的來源。","examples":[{"en":"The children drew a triangle on the board.","zh":"孩子們在黑板上畫了一個三角形。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This triangle has two equal sides.","zh":"這個三角形有兩條相等的邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a21bb91de1ff7b4","term":"triangle","forms":["triangle","triangles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"三角戀","explanation":"triangle可以指三個人之間的愛情糾葛，也就是“三角戀”；這裡從三角形的三個角引申出三方關係。","examples":[{"en":"The film tells the story of a complicated love triangle.","zh":"這部電影講述了一個複雜的三角戀故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The novel centers on a love triangle between three friends.","zh":"這部小說圍繞三個朋友之間的三角戀展開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triangle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93196ca4a16ce11625d2","word":"tribal","forms":["tribal"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9aeb1fbf5d0e66c9","term":"tribal","forms":["tribal","more tribal","most tribal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"部落的；與部落有關的","explanation":"指屬於部落、來自部落，或與部落的生活、制度和關係有關。它把“部落”看作一個共同體，強調事物與這個共同體的聯絡。","examples":[{"en":"The village is governed by tribal law.","zh":"這個村莊由部落法律管理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is proud of her tribal heritage.","zh":"她為自己的部落傳統感到自豪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tribal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89c23cd94735af74","term":"tribal","forms":["tribal","more tribal","most tribal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"按部落組織的","explanation":"強調一個社會、群體或制度是以部落為基本單位來組織的，而不只是與某個部落有關係。","examples":[{"en":"The region once had a tribal society with many small clans.","zh":"這個地區過去曾有一個由許多小氏族組成的部落社會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The settlement retained its traditional tribal organization.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tribal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d22f4e0f2779f1044467","word":"tribe","forms":["tribe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7953e32eeab84377","term":"tribe","forms":["tribe","tribes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"部落；族群","explanation":"指規模通常大於小型幫派或氏族、但不一定達到國家規模的族群；成員往往以共同的血緣、文化、歷史或身份認同聯絡在一起。","examples":[{"en":"Several Germanic tribes settled in the region.","zh":"幾個日耳曼部落在這一地區定居下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum has an exhibit about the tribes of the Pacific Northwest.","zh":"這家博物館有一個介紹太平洋西北地區各族群的展覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89b012bfdb9c7667","term":"tribe","forms":["tribe","tribes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"志趣相投的一群人","explanation":"把現實社會中有共同興趣、價值觀或生活方式的人想象成同一“部落”，強調群體歸屬感和內部凝聚力。","examples":[{"en":"She finally found her tribe among the local artists.","zh":"她終於在當地藝術家中找到了志趣相投的一群人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every new employee wants to feel part of the tribe.","zh":"每個新員工都希望感到自己是這個群體的一員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tribe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-70edfd75bd0267f3653b","word":"tribute","forms":["tribute"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7e72c00d830d7aa4","term":"tribute","forms":["tribute","tributes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"致敬、感謝或讚美的表示","explanation":"指為了表達感謝、尊重或讚美而送出的禮物、言辭或行為；它仍然保留“向某人獻上一份東西”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The concert was a tribute to the singer's long career.","zh":"這場音樂會是對這位歌手長期演藝生涯的致敬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote a tribute to her former teacher.","zh":"她寫了一篇文章，表達對她以前老師的敬意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tribute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9dce6d513c881812","term":"tribute","forms":["tribute","tributes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"國家向另一國家繳納的貢金","explanation":"指一個國家在臣服或戰敗後，定期向另一個國家交付的錢物；這是“向更強者獻上東西”這一核心畫面的強制版本。","examples":[{"en":"The defeated kingdom had to pay tribute to the empire.","zh":"戰敗的王國不得不向這個帝國繳納貢金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The conquered kingdom paid tribute in gold.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tribute","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f39d5149a46edeaf4305","word":"trick","forms":["trick"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d20efb0ad680a1e","term":"trick","forms":["trick","tricks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詭計；騙局","explanation":"為了騙過、誤導或佔某人便宜而設計的做法；核心畫面是用一個小機關讓別人相信不真的事。","examples":[{"en":"The cheap price was just a trick to bring customers into the store.","zh":"那個低價只是把顧客吸引進店的一個騙局。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He played a trick on his brother by hiding the remote.","zh":"他把遙控器藏起來捉弄了弟弟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f93576fb04bfb0d2","term":"trick","forms":["trick","tricks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戲法；魔術","explanation":"表演者透過技巧和誤導製造驚奇效果的一個動作或節目，例如魔術師展示的花招。","examples":[{"en":"The magician performed a card trick for the children.","zh":"魔術師給孩子們表演了一個紙牌戲法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"For her next trick, she made a coin disappear.","zh":"她接下來要表演的戲法是讓一枚硬幣消失。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8f67b2e1916743c","term":"trick","forms":["trick","tricks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"技巧；特技動作","explanation":"需要練習才能完成的漂亮或困難動作，尤其用於滑板、運動和表演；它是把“戲法”變成身體技巧。","examples":[{"en":"She learned a new trick on her skateboard.","zh":"她學會了一個新的滑板技巧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can you land that trick without falling?","zh":"你能不摔倒地完成那個動作嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bcd1dd964e81bfe5","term":"trick","forms":["trick","tricks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"訣竅；巧辦法","explanation":"完成某件事的有效、聰明或快速方法；它把“巧妙機關”轉成解決問題的辦法。","examples":[{"en":"The trick to making good bread is to give the dough enough time.","zh":"做好麵包的訣竅是給麵糰足夠的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What's the trick to opening this jar?","zh":"開啟這個罐子的訣竅是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52119dfbf7ee557b","term":"trick","forms":["trick","tricks","tricking","tricked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"欺騙；騙使相信","explanation":"用詭計讓某人相信不真實的事，或在不知情的情況下做出某事；這是名詞“詭計”對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"They tricked me into signing the wrong contract.","zh":"他們騙我簽下了錯誤的合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tricked him out of his savings.","zh":"她騙走了他攢下的錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trick","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5a077f15ad0506be85c","word":"tricky","forms":["tricky"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8c02324215c7a9ab","term":"tricky","forms":["tricky","trickier","trickiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"棘手的；複雜的","explanation":"指事情表面上可能不難，但隱藏著容易出錯的地方，需要仔細判斷或靈活處理。它像一個藏著機關的局面，稍不注意就會陷入麻煩。","examples":[{"en":"Finding a fair solution to the dispute was tricky.","zh":"要為這場爭端找到一個公平的解決辦法很棘手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This is a tricky question, so think before you answer.","zh":"這是個容易出錯的問題，所以回答前先想一想。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tricky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0c44fd1fdbd7b15f","term":"tricky","forms":["tricky","trickier","trickiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"狡猾的；會耍花招的","explanation":"指某人善於利用欺騙、誤導或小花招來達到目的。這個意思把“藏著機關”的特點放到了人身上，通常帶有負面評價。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful with that tricky salesman; he may hide the extra costs.","zh":"小心那個狡猾的推銷員，他可能會把額外費用藏起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tricky salesman concealed the additional fees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tricky","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d69561c383e5872176d1","word":"trifle","forms":["trifle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e494c0ceebd00188","term":"trifle","forms":["trifle","trifles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瑣事；無關緊要的事物","explanation":"指價值、影響或重要性很小的事情或東西。它把某件事放在“只是小事”的位置上，因此常帶有輕視或不認真對待的意味。","examples":[{"en":"The argument started over a trifle and soon became serious.","zh":"這場爭吵起初只是因為一件小事，卻很快變得嚴重起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She refuses to let such trifles spoil her day.","zh":"她不願讓這種小事毀掉自己一天的心情。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trifle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-87eec868daf8c094","term":"trifle","forms":["trifle","trifles","trifling","trifled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輕率對待；玩弄","explanation":"指把重要的人、感情或事情當成無關緊要的東西來對待，因而顯得輕浮、不負責任。它尤其常表示玩弄別人的感情，而不是單純“覺得事情簡單”。","examples":[{"en":"You should never trifle with another person's trust.","zh":"你絕不應該輕率地辜負別人的信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He trifled with her feelings and then disappeared.","zh":"他玩弄了她的感情，隨後就消失了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trifle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-683259feabbf5eb39895","word":"trigger","forms":["trigger"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-54b16569f9925324","term":"trigger","forms":["trigger","triggers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"槍的扳機","explanation":"指用手指操作、用來發射槍械的扳機；它是“拉動後啟動反應”的最具體形象。","examples":[{"en":"The officer kept her finger away from the trigger.","zh":"那名警員的手指一直沒有碰到扳機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He pulled the trigger only after checking the target.","zh":"他確認目標後才扣動扳機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trigger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7f11758d17bf089b","term":"trigger","forms":["trigger","triggers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引發事件的誘因","explanation":"指啟動一連串事件、變化或行動的事情，相當於把某個結果“按下啟動鍵”的誘因。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden price increase was a trigger for public protests.","zh":"價格突然上漲是引發公眾抗議的一個誘因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting became the trigger for major changes in the company.","zh":"這次會議成了公司發生重大變化的導火索。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trigger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-67eb788b4d6b8038","term":"trigger","forms":["trigger","triggers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引起負面情緒的刺激","explanation":"指某個概念、畫面、話題或經歷，它像扳機一樣突然喚起某人的不安、痛苦或其他強烈負面情緒。","examples":[{"en":"For some people, loud arguments can be an emotional trigger.","zh":"對一些人來說，激烈的爭吵可能會引發強烈的負面情緒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film includes a warning about scenes that may be emotional triggers.","zh":"這部電影提醒觀眾，其中有些場景可能會引發強烈的情緒反應。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trigger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07ce99aece5cbb19","term":"trigger","forms":["trigger","triggers","triggering","triggered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引發、促成","explanation":"指某件事啟動或促成另一個事件、結果或變化，就像拉動扳機後事情開始發展。","examples":[{"en":"The announcement triggered a sharp fall in the company's share price.","zh":"這項宣告引發了公司股價的大幅下跌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A software update triggered several unexpected errors.","zh":"一次軟體更新引發了幾個意料之外的錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trigger","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112],"total":3,"counts":{"111":2,"112":1}}},{"id":"ceec-55b484fa51b492622efa","word":"trillion","forms":["trillion"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e82165afd9a81b87","term":"trillion","forms":["trillion","trillions"],"pos":"num","zh":"一萬億","explanation":"現代英語中，trillion 通常指一萬億，即10的12次方。它常用於描述極大的金額、人口、資料量或其他可計算的數量，是今天最應該優先掌握的數詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The company is worth more than a trillion dollars.","zh":"這家公司市值超過一萬億美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists estimate that there are trillions of stars in the universe.","zh":"科學家估計宇宙中有數萬億顆恆星。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trillion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2d683c0ce39e0a6","term":"trillion","forms":["trillion","trillions"],"pos":"num","zh":"多得不得了","explanation":"在口語或非正式表達中，trillion 可以不表示精確數字，只是誇張地說某種東西數量極多。它仍然保留“大數”的核心形象，只是重點從精確計算轉為強調數量驚人。","examples":[{"en":"I've told you a trillion times to check the door.","zh":"我都跟你說過無數次了，要檢查門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My inbox seems to contain a trillion unanswered messages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trillion","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-657c97bf2df3f6e23696","word":"trim","forms":["trim"],"officialPos":"v./n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4b3afa23f3dd88a","term":"trim","forms":["trim","trimmer","trimmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體健康勻稱","explanation":"形容人身體狀態好、體格健康，像是經過整理和保持後處於合適狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She swims twice a week to keep in trim.","zh":"她每週游泳兩次，以保持身體健康。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stays trim by cycling to work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a26d4817b51d89f2","term":"trim","forms":["trim","trimmer","trimmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身材苗條勻稱","explanation":"形容人的身材纖細、勻稱而不顯得臃腫，體現出整理得恰到好處的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The dancer has a trim figure and excellent posture.","zh":"這名舞者身材勻稱，姿態也非常好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular swimming keeps him remarkably trim.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea59102e757f8972","term":"trim","forms":["trim","trims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裝飾邊條","explanation":"指沿著物品邊緣或邊界新增的裝飾部分，核心感覺是把邊緣整理得更美觀。","examples":[{"en":"The white curtains have blue trim along the edges.","zh":"白色窗簾邊緣飾有藍色裝飾邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Gold trim decorated the edges of the costume.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd09d0bfe34e7d3f","term":"trim","forms":["trim","trims","trimming","trimmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"修剪；削減多餘部分","explanation":"透過剪掉、切去或略微減少多餘的部分，把東西整理到合適的狀態；修剪鬍鬚、頭髮、樹枝等都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"He trimmed his beard before the interview.","zh":"他在面試前修剪了鬍鬚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We trimmed the hedge to keep it neat.","zh":"我們修剪了樹籬，讓它保持整齊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34a389d790fc2bdd8458","word":"trip","forms":["trip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7019d7c3ed8903e4","term":"trip","forms":["trip","trips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旅行；行程","explanation":"指從一個地方到另一個地方的一次旅行或短途出行，可以強調過程，也可以指這次出行本身。把它記成腳步輕快地邁出去，走成一趟旅程。","examples":[{"en":"We took a trip to the beach last weekend.","zh":"我們上週末去海邊旅行了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is planning a business trip to Tokyo.","zh":"她正在計劃一次去東京的商務旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-72468e7bc0612860","term":"trip","forms":["trip","trips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"絆倒；失足","explanation":"指腳步被東西碰住或踩空而失去平衡，強調絆倒這一動作或結果。這正對應記憶鉤子裡“腳步碰到東西會絆倒”。","examples":[{"en":"I had a trip over the loose cable and nearly fell.","zh":"我被鬆動的電纜絆了一下，差點摔倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He hurt his ankle after a trip on the stairs.","zh":"他在樓梯上絆倒後扭傷了腳踝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7268d072ea32a8be","term":"trip","forms":["trip","trips","tripping","tripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"絆倒；被絆住","explanation":"腳步碰到東西后失去平衡而摔倒或差點摔倒，正是“腳步發生變化”中被東西絆住的情況。","examples":[{"en":"I tripped over a loose paving stone outside the station.","zh":"我在車站外被一塊鬆動的鋪路石絆了一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Watch your step, or you might trip on the cable.","zh":"走路小心點，不然可能會被電纜絆倒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7ddec13db1d60024","term":"trip","forms":["trip","trips","tripping","tripped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"旅行；出行","explanation":"表示去某地旅行或進行一次行程，是“腳步發生變化”中輕快地走出一趟路程。","examples":[{"en":"We tripped to the coast for a quiet weekend.","zh":"我們去海邊度過了一個安靜的週末。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They plan to trip across the country by train.","zh":"他們計劃坐火車橫穿全國旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aea96c13c0540a330ad5","word":"triple","forms":["triple"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6aee9664aabd1d2c","term":"triple","forms":["triple"],"pos":"adj","zh":"三重的；由三個部分組成","explanation":"指一個整體裡有三個相互關聯、常常相配的部分，重點是“三個組成部分”這一結構。","examples":[{"en":"The triple markings on this vase are quite unique.","zh":"這個花瓶上的三重紋飾很獨特。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The house has triple glazing to reduce noise.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dca1f188dcdda229","term":"triple","forms":["triple"],"pos":"adj","zh":"三倍的","explanation":"指數量、份量或大小是原來的三倍，也可以表示把通常的一份增加到三份。","examples":[{"en":"Give me a triple serving of mashed potatoes.","zh":"請給我三份量的土豆泥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They offered triple pay for working on the holiday.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5e7a623cddfff8f","term":"triple","forms":["triple","triples"],"pos":"noun","zh":"三倍的數量","explanation":"指某個數量、大小或份量的三倍，也就是把原來的量算三次。","examples":[{"en":"The recipe calls for a triple of the original amount.","zh":"這個食譜要求用原配方三倍的量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their new salary was triple what they earned before.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94f4e5a0d0c86482","term":"triple","forms":["triple","triples","tripling","tripled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使乘三；使變成三倍","explanation":"指主動把某個數量、收益或規模增加到原來的三倍。","examples":[{"en":"The company tripled its earnings per share over the last quarter.","zh":"這家公司上一季度的每股收益變成了原來的三倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory tripled production after installing new machinery.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1a6a1181c97be84c","term":"triple","forms":["triple","triples","tripling","tripled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變成三倍","explanation":"指數量、規模或數值自行增長到原來的三倍，不強調誰主動使它增長。","examples":[{"en":"Our earnings have tripled in the last year.","zh":"我們的收入在過去一年裡變成了原來的三倍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village's population tripled within twenty years.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triple","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9bb8c09c1ccb03a9e01d","word":"triumph","forms":["triumph"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d8e481856cba307","term":"triumph","forms":["triumph","triumphs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勝利；決定性成功","explanation":"指經過努力、衝突或困難後取得的決定性成功，重點是終於戰勝了阻礙或對手。","examples":[{"en":"The triumph of knowledge over fear changed the community.","zh":"知識戰勝恐懼的勝利改變了這個社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Winning the final was a personal triumph for her.","zh":"贏得決賽對她來說是一次個人的勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triumph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-076a9d2f615444d3","term":"triumph","forms":["triumph","triumphs","triumphing","triumphed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"戰勝；佔上風","explanation":"指克服對手、困難或挑戰並取得優勢，像凱旋者一樣勝出。","examples":[{"en":"The team triumphed over several stronger opponents.","zh":"這支隊伍戰勝了幾名更強的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Patience eventually triumphed over anger.","zh":"耐心最終戰勝了憤怒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/triumph","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6d4c9cf5e022a07ea801","word":"trivial","forms":["trivial"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d77a1e1733faf27b","term":"trivial","forms":["trivial","more trivial","most trivial"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無關緊要的；微不足道的","explanation":"指某件事太小、太簡單或價值太低，不值得花很多時間和注意力；這是 trivial 最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We should not waste time arguing over trivial details.","zh":"我們不該把時間浪費在爭論無關緊要的細節上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mistake seemed trivial, but it caused a serious delay.","zh":"這個錯誤看似微不足道，卻造成了嚴重的延誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trivial","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b3949bfd38344fd7943","word":"troop","forms":["troop"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6ac3bc9b3f74b8c9","term":"troop","forms":["troop","troops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一群；一隊","explanation":"troop 可以泛指聚在一起的一群人，重點是“成群、成隊”這一整體概念，不一定與軍隊有關。","examples":[{"en":"A troop of volunteers arrived before sunrise.","zh":"一隊志願者在日出前到達了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Troops of fans waited outside the stadium.","zh":"一群群球迷在體育場外等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/troop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-026c1a6d49e00ff3","term":"troop","forms":["troop","troops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"騎兵或裝甲部隊小隊","explanation":"在軍事組織中，troop 可以指由上尉指揮的一個小單位，規模大致相當於步兵中的排或連，具體編制隨軍種而變。","examples":[{"en":"The captain led his troop across the bridge.","zh":"上尉帶領他的小隊過了橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A troop of cavalry guarded the mountain road.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/troop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b39419ef79491b8efa0a","word":"trophy","forms":["trophy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fe2ca3980df4524b","term":"trophy","forms":["trophy","trophies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獎盃；獎品","explanation":"指因贏得比賽或取得特別成就而獲得、用來紀念成功的物品，常見形式包括獎盃、雕像或盾牌。","examples":[{"en":"Maya won a trophy for being the fastest runner in her school.","zh":"瑪雅因為是學校裡跑得最快的學生而贏得了一座獎盃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team proudly displayed its championship trophy in the school hall.","zh":"這支隊伍自豪地把冠軍獎盃展示在學校大廳裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trophy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9b247b350188a0d2","term":"trophy","forms":["trophy","trophies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戰利品；獵獲物","explanation":"指獵人、征服者或參戰者取得並展示的東西，用來證明一次成功的狩獵、征服或戰鬥。","examples":[{"en":"The hunter mounted the deer antlers as a trophy above the fireplace.","zh":"那名獵人把鹿角裝裱起來，作為戰利品掛在壁爐上方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The captured banner became a trophy of the campaign.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trophy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9d373cbd998b7ac3829","word":"tropic","forms":["tropic"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f55d8069a26648d7","term":"tropic","forms":["tropic","more tropic","most tropic"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱帶的","explanation":"表示與熱帶地區或熱帶環境有關，就像太陽在南北兩條熱帶線上轉向一樣。這是閱讀地理、氣候和自然描寫時最值得先掌握的形容詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Many species thrive in tropic climates.","zh":"許多物種在熱帶氣候中生長旺盛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The island is surrounded by warm tropic seas.","zh":"這座島嶼四周環繞著溫暖的熱帶海域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tropic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2812b8b318e3872e","term":"tropic","forms":["tropic","tropics"],"pos":"noun","zh":"迴歸線","explanation":"指赤道南北約二十三度半的兩條緯線：北迴歸線或南迴歸線。它們標誌著太陽能夠直射到的最北和最南位置，因此正好延續了“太陽轉向”的記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The Tropic of Cancer passes through several countries.","zh":"北迴歸線穿過幾個國家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monument stands just south of the tropic.","zh":"這座紀念碑就位於迴歸線以南。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tropic","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-16483ee69d8740609947","word":"tropical","forms":["tropical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5764a8b086bdc54","term":"tropical","forms":["tropical","more tropical","most tropical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"熱帶的","explanation":"指與熱帶地區有關的，即大致位於南北迴歸線之間、靠近赤道的地區或事物。它是這個詞最直接、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Many tropical fruits grow well in this region.","zh":"許多熱帶水果在這個地區生長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They spent their holiday on a tropical island.","zh":"他們在一個熱帶島嶼上度過了假期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tropical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1276cb8fbba2e906","term":"tropical","forms":["tropical","more tropical","most tropical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"炎熱潮溼的；有熱帶氣候特點的","explanation":"指天氣、環境或生活感受像熱帶一樣炎熱而潮溼，不一定真的位於熱帶地區。這個意思是從“熱帶地區的氣候”自然擴充套件出來的。","examples":[{"en":"We've had several tropical nights this summer.","zh":"今年夏天有好幾個夜晚又熱又悶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The greenhouse maintains tropical conditions for the orchids.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tropical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7130df43355ec25b38ba","word":"trouble","forms":["trouble"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c8e530a5b581ede6","term":"trouble","forms":["trouble","troubles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"困境；麻煩","explanation":"指令人擔憂、危險或難以脫身的處境，重點是人已經被捲入了麻煩之中。","examples":[{"en":"If we miss the last train, we'll be in trouble.","zh":"如果我們錯過末班車，就麻煩了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She called her brother when she was in trouble.","zh":"她遇到麻煩時給哥哥打了電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trouble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-04664e4835cd505e","term":"trouble","forms":["trouble","troubles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"問題；難題","explanation":"指造成麻煩的具體問題、狀況或行為；它可以是某件事本身出了問題，也可以是導致困境的原因。","examples":[{"en":"The trouble is that we don't have enough time.","zh":"問題在於我們沒有足夠的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The car's trouble started after the long trip.","zh":"這輛車的問題是在長途旅行後出現的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trouble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2eea0b569dcfceb","term":"trouble","forms":["trouble","troubles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"毛病；缺點","explanation":"指某人或某事中令人不滿意的部分，也就是會妨礙效果的缺點、弱點或短處。","examples":[{"en":"The trouble with this plan is that it costs too much.","zh":"這個計劃的問題是成本太高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is trouble with the new software.","zh":"這個新軟體有問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trouble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-209e047c55bd29d3","term":"trouble","forms":["trouble","troubles","troubling","troubled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使煩惱；使焦慮","explanation":"指讓某人心裡不安、困惑或憂慮，相當於把對方的內心攪亂；也可以表示某件事持續困擾某人。","examples":[{"en":"The uncertainty about his job is troubling him.","zh":"對工作的不確定讓他很煩惱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't let one mistake trouble you.","zh":"別讓一次錯誤困擾你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trouble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-376b607a5cd7f4b5","term":"trouble","forms":["trouble","troubles","troubling","troubled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打擾；麻煩","explanation":"指給別人造成不便，或讓別人額外幫忙；語氣通常比“使人焦慮”輕，重點是讓對方費事。","examples":[{"en":"Sorry to trouble you, but could you check this form?","zh":"抱歉打擾你，你能幫我檢查一下這張表嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I won't trouble you for an answer tonight.","zh":"我今晚不會麻煩你給出答覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trouble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2920981fe7657bc4a663","word":"troublesome","forms":["troublesome"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ad2aed36a606766f","term":"troublesome","forms":["troublesome","more troublesome","most troublesome"],"pos":"adj","zh":"麻煩的；令人煩惱的","explanation":"形容某人或某事不斷帶來困難，使人需要額外處理，甚至感到焦慮或煩惱。它抓住的核心就是“像一個不斷製造麻煩的小故障”。","examples":[{"en":"The computer has been very troublesome for me lately.","zh":"這臺電腦最近一直給我添麻煩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We finally solved the troublesome problem.","zh":"我們終於解決了這個棘手的問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/troublesome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2dbacce3e851bf99053","word":"trout","forms":["trout"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7f12bd28e7f3ad36","term":"trout","forms":["trout","trouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鱒魚","explanation":"鱒魚是一類與鮭魚近親的魚，常見於垂釣和食用語境。這個詞既能指一條鱒魚，也能泛指這種魚類或作為食物的鱒魚。","examples":[{"en":"We caught a trout in the mountain stream.","zh":"我們在山間溪流裡釣到了一條鱒魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She ordered grilled trout for dinner.","zh":"她晚餐點了烤鱒魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-24611dec0a0a3ae6f9f3","word":"truck","forms":["truck"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2faf3f7f012ee74","term":"truck","forms":["truck","trucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"卡車；貨車","explanation":"指體型較大、用於運貨或牽引貨運拖車的機動車，是“用輪子運東西”這一記憶鉤子中最典型的東西。","examples":[{"en":"We rented a truck to move the furniture.","zh":"我們租了一輛卡車來搬傢俱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The truck delivered the supplies before noon.","zh":"那輛卡車在中午前送來了物資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5bea41b6c623f7c09f1","word":"true","forms":["true"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f7de5c61ced50379","term":"true","forms":["true","truer","more true","truest","most true"],"pos":"adj","zh":"真實的；符合事實的","explanation":"事情確實如此，與現實或事實相符，而不是虛構或錯誤的。","examples":[{"en":"This is a true story.","zh":"這是一個真實的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is it true that the store is closing?","zh":"那家店要關門的訊息是真的嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/true","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bce47c30506c0a1b","term":"true","forms":["true","truer","more true","truest","most true"],"pos":"adj","zh":"準確的；符合標準的","explanation":"某物與規定的形狀、規則或範本完全吻合，沒有偏差。","examples":[{"en":"The museum displayed a true copy of the original map.","zh":"博物館展出了一份與原地圖完全相符的複製品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The measurement is true to the nearest millimeter.","zh":"這個測量結果精確到最接近的一毫米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/true","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6115684945f9ebae","term":"true","forms":["true","truer","more true","truest","most true"],"pos":"adj","zh":"忠實的；可靠的","explanation":"一個人始終可靠、守信，並且真誠地支援某人或某種原則；這正是“可靠而不偏離”的人際版本。","examples":[{"en":"She has been a true friend through every difficulty.","zh":"在每一次困難中，她都一直是個忠實可靠的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He stayed true to his promise.","zh":"他信守了自己的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/true","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b7dfa266adb6db500f72","word":"trumpet","forms":["trumpet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4bf9abe1e6c90cb","term":"trumpet","forms":["trumpet","trumpets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小號；號類銅管樂器","explanation":"一種透過嘴唇振動發聲的銅管樂器，通常有按鍵或活塞來改變音高；在日常英語中主要指小號。它保留了“把聲音送遠”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"My sister has been learning to play the trumpet.","zh":"我姐姐一直在學吹小號。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A trumpet sounded as the parade began.","zh":"遊行開始時，一支號吹響了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trumpet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e341d2d9c67be01819b","word":"trunk","forms":["trunk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-368d6ff20e875692","term":"trunk","forms":["trunk","trunks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軀幹","explanation":"指人體從頸部以下到腰部附近的主體部分，不包括四肢和頭部。它就是身體的“主幹”，與樹幹或血管主幹的形象相通。","examples":[{"en":"The exercise strengthens the muscles in your trunk.","zh":"這項運動能增強你軀幹的肌肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep your trunk upright while you climb.","zh":"攀爬時要保持軀幹直立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trunk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fe626baf5697313","term":"trunk","forms":["trunk","trunks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大行李箱","explanation":"指用來裝衣物和其他物品的大箱子，尤其是旅行時攜帶行李的箱子。它和“粗大的容器”這一核心形象相連。","examples":[{"en":"She packed her winter clothes in a large trunk.","zh":"她把冬衣裝進了一個大行李箱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old trunk was full of family photographs.","zh":"那個舊箱子裡裝滿了家庭照片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trunk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-739e023c4946f5fb","term":"trunk","forms":["trunk","trunks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"主幹","explanation":"指某個整體中最主要、最粗的部分，尤其是樹、血管、神經或其他有分支結構的主體。許多具體義項都可以看作這個“主幹”概念的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The tree trunk was too wide for one person to reach around.","zh":"這棵樹的樹幹太粗了，一個人無法環抱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artery divides into smaller branches from its main trunk.","zh":"這條動脈從主幹處分成更小的分支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trunk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f796e2f28ae5811737cc","word":"trust","forms":["trust"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6dea68419b5332b0","term":"trust","forms":["trust","trusts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"信任","explanation":"相信某人誠實、可靠，或相信某種品質值得依靠。信任一旦被破壞，就需要重新建立。","examples":[{"en":"She lost my trust after hiding the truth.","zh":"她隱瞞真相後失去了我的信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It takes time to build trust in a new team.","zh":"在一個新團隊中建立信任需要時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-97dd0ce9b8b5c942","term":"trust","forms":["trust","trusts","trusting","trusted","trustest","trustedst","trusteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"信任、相信可靠","explanation":"相信某人不會欺騙或傷害你，或者相信某事物可以依靠。這是 trust 最核心、最常用的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I trust her to keep the secret.","zh":"我相信她會保守這個秘密。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You can trust this old car.","zh":"這輛舊車是靠得住的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8908a675c218180c","term":"trust","forms":["trust","trusts","trusting","trusted","trustest","trustedst","trusteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"相信屬實","explanation":"接受某人的話、解釋或資訊，認為它可信或真實；重點在相信內容，而不只是信任說話的人。","examples":[{"en":"I don't trust what he says about the price.","zh":"我不相信他說的價格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I trust that your account is accurate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trust","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f1195f0903da53fc4e4","word":"trustee","forms":["trustee"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8da7a9afee867d3","term":"trustee","forms":["trustee","trustees"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財產受託人","explanation":"受託人是依法替別人持有和管理財產的人。財產名義上可能由他控制，但他不能為自己隨意使用，必須按照約定為受益人或公共目的服務。","examples":[{"en":"The trustee manages the fund for the children.","zh":"受託人為這些孩子管理這筆基金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trustee manages the inheritance until the child turns eighteen.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trustee","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c5c4bad89ee44b4da032","word":"truth","forms":["truth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ecc9d8e48a2e95ab","term":"truth","forms":["truth","truths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"真實情況；真相","explanation":"指事情實際上是什麼樣，或對現實的真實描述，重點是揭開隱瞞、誤解或謊言後的真實情況。","examples":[{"en":"The truth is that nobody knew how serious the problem was.","zh":"事實是，沒人知道這個問題有多嚴重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She finally told me the truth about the missing money.","zh":"她終於把那筆失蹤的錢的真相告訴了我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d58f442e135f131","term":"truth","forms":["truth","truths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"符合事實；正確性","explanation":"強調一個說法、判斷或描述與事實相符的程度；某句話不必完全正確，也可能“有一定真實性”。","examples":[{"en":"There is some truth in her criticism, even if her conclusion is too harsh.","zh":"她的批評有一定道理，儘管她的結論太嚴厲了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report questioned the truth of his explanation.","zh":"這份報告質疑了他的解釋是否屬實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a84249afd53c741caf0","word":"truthful","forms":["truthful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1452f8054c0dac5f","term":"truthful","forms":["truthful","more truthful","most truthful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"誠實說真話","explanation":"形容一個人誠實可靠，通常會如實說出自己知道的情況，不故意撒謊或歪曲事實。也可以形容這種人的性格或態度。","examples":[{"en":"Her truthful nature made everyone trust her.","zh":"她誠實的本性讓所有人都信任她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please be truthful about what happened.","zh":"請如實說說發生了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truthful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9cc34193c1a66ffe","term":"truthful","forms":["truthful","more truthful","most truthful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"如實表現現實","explanation":"形容畫像、描述、報道等準確地呈現真實情況，和現實相符，而不是美化、誇大或歪曲它。","examples":[{"en":"The film gives a truthful picture of life in the village.","zh":"這部電影如實呈現了村裡的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The film gives a truthful portrayal of working life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truthful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1e262cd7d110812f5726","word":"try","forms":["try"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6fb8db48ddeafa12","term":"try","forms":["try","tries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘗試；試一試","explanation":"try 可以指為了完成某事而進行的一次嘗試，不說明這次嘗試是否成功。它就是動詞“試著做”的名詞化結果。","examples":[{"en":"I gave unicycling a try, but I couldn't do it.","zh":"我試著騎獨輪車，但沒能做到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Give it another try before you give up.","zh":"放棄之前再試一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/try","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-89e1e2a80c88bb50","term":"try","forms":["try","tries","trying","tried","triest","triedst","trieth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"試著做；努力做","explanation":"try to do 表示採取行動並努力完成某事，但結果可能成功也可能失敗。這是 try 最核心、最常見的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"I tried to open the window, but it was stuck.","zh":"我試著開啟窗戶，但窗戶卡住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to arrive before dark.","zh":"儘量在天黑前到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/try","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d977e091ea89c4c46f07","word":"T-shirt","forms":["T-shirt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31ceb136963344de","term":"T-shirt","forms":["T-shirt","T-shirts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"T恤；短袖無領上衣","explanation":"一種輕便的上衣，通常沒有衣領和紐扣，袖子較短，多用棉布製作，胸前或背後常印有圖案、文字或標語。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a black T-shirt with a small logo on it.","zh":"她穿著一件印有小標誌的黑色T恤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought two T-shirts for the summer.","zh":"我買了兩件夏天穿的T恤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/T-shirt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-14cf0fbca484cf6cae8e","word":"tub","forms":["tub"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1a8298c412e7b6b","term":"tub","forms":["tub","tubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"矮寬的容器","explanation":"指一種底部平、通常矮而寬的容器，可用來存放、包裝東西，也可用來洗東西。這是理解其他多數義項的基礎形象。","examples":[{"en":"They kept the apples in a large wooden tub.","zh":"他們把蘋果放在一個大木桶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He washed the muddy boots in the tub.","zh":"他在大盆裡洗沾滿泥的靴子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65fd7d5aa6a6f7fb","term":"tub","forms":["tub","tubs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"浴缸","explanation":"指用來泡澡或洗澡的浴缸，是“裝水的大盆”這一核心形象在家庭中的常見用法。","examples":[{"en":"The children splashed happily in the tub.","zh":"孩子們在浴缸裡開心地潑水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I left the towel beside the tub.","zh":"我把毛巾放在浴缸旁邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tub","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05cc6c650fa6e8acf380","word":"tube","forms":["tube"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33bfb665e0bb1626","term":"tube","forms":["tube","tubes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"管子；中空圓筒","explanation":"tube 是內部空著、外形大致呈圓柱形的物體，重點在“像管子一樣中空”。它可以是很普通的管，也可以是裝置中的管狀部件。","examples":[{"en":"The plumber replaced the old metal tube.","zh":"水管工換掉了那根舊金屬管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Light passed through the glass tube.","zh":"光線穿過了玻璃管。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tube","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-860ed901913839a9","term":"tube","forms":["tube","tubes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倫敦地鐵","explanation":"在英國英語中，Tube 也指倫敦地鐵系統；這個意義可以理解為“在管狀隧道中執行的交通系統”擴充套件出來的名稱。","examples":[{"en":"She took the Tube to Waterloo.","zh":"她乘倫敦地鐵去了滑鐵盧車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took the Tube from Victoria to Oxford Circus.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tube","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf92efd25691b65fcb13","word":"tuck","forms":["tuck"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9ad4ba3ecd639ab","term":"tuck","forms":["tuck","tucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"褶襉；摺疊","explanation":"tuck 可以指把布料收攏後形成的褶襉，也可以泛指這種摺疊動作或結果。記住“向里拉並摺進去”的畫面，就能連線它的主要意義。","examples":[{"en":"The skirt has a neat tuck at the waist.","zh":"這條裙子腰部有一道整齊的褶襉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small tucks give the blouse shape at the waist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3323fa6d6f4fc45c","term":"tuck","forms":["tuck","tucks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜷曲姿勢","explanation":"tuck 也指身體收攏、彎曲成較緊的姿勢，像把膝蓋和四肢往身體旁邊收。它是“向裡折入”用於身體的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The child slept in a tight tuck on the sofa.","zh":"孩子蜷成一團睡在沙發上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The diver held a tight tuck during the somersault.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4da541af7ad679e9","term":"tuck","forms":["tuck","tucks","tucking","tucked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拉攏布料；收起","explanation":"tuck 作及物動詞時，可以把布料向里拉攏、折起或收好，形成褶襉或讓布料變得更緊湊。","examples":[{"en":"She tucked the loose fabric under the belt.","zh":"她把松垂的布料掖進腰帶下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tuck the loose blanket around the sleeping child.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d5cd060de01b6c57","term":"tuck","forms":["tuck","tucks","tucking","tucked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"塞入；掖好","explanation":"tuck 可以把東西推入一個貼身、安全、順手或不顯眼的位置，例如把衣服掖好、把被單塞住，或把錢放進衣袋。核心仍是“收攏後藏進合適的位置”。","examples":[{"en":"Tuck your shirt into your jeans before the photo.","zh":"拍照前把襯衫掖進牛仔褲裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tucked the letter into his coat pocket.","zh":"他把信塞進了外套口袋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e6bbc6867045359448c8","word":"tug","forms":["tug"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c88e4c8bf10564fb","term":"tug","forms":["tug","tugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用力一拉","explanation":"指突然而有力的一次拉動，重點在短促、明顯的拉力，而不只是輕輕牽引。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a sudden tug on the fishing line.","zh":"我感覺到魚線上突然傳來一股拉力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One hard tug opened the stuck drawer.","zh":"用力一拉，卡住的抽屜就開啟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-415c949179957652","term":"tug","forms":["tug","tugs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拖船","explanation":"指用來拖帶或推動其他船隻的船；它的名稱仍然來自“拉、拖”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"A tug guided the cargo ship into the narrow harbor.","zh":"一艘拖船引導貨船駛入狹窄的港口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The disabled freighter needed two tugs to reach the repair dock.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e2298f21f5722d5","term":"tug","forms":["tug","tugs","tugging","tugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用力拉出或拖動","explanation":"指費力地把人或物拉動、拖走，常常帶有物件不容易移動的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The rescuers tugged the man out of the overturned car.","zh":"救援人員費力地把那名男子從翻倒的汽車裡拉了出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She tugged the heavy suitcase up the stairs.","zh":"她費力地把沉重的行李箱拖上樓梯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4b2a8c9187ad7fc","term":"tug","forms":["tug","tugs","tugging","tugged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"反覆用力拉","explanation":"指一下一下地用力拉，通常是為了鬆開、開啟或移動某物；反覆拉動有時反而會使問題更嚴重。","examples":[{"en":"He kept tugging at the knot, but it only became tighter.","zh":"他不停地拽那個結，但結反而變得更緊了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child tugged repeatedly at his mother's sleeve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tug","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9c6d86c4393319c271d4","word":"tuition","forms":["tuition"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71981886d69040e1","term":"tuition","forms":["tuition","tuitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"教學；輔導","explanation":"指教師或導師實際提供的教學、訓練和指導，重點是“教的過程”，而不是為此支付的錢。這是英國、愛爾蘭等地區較常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She received private tuition in mathematics before the entrance exam.","zh":"她在入學考試前接受了私人數學輔導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school provides extra tuition for students who need help.","zh":"這所學校為需要幫助的學生提供額外輔導。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a0884d8134661e9","term":"tuition","forms":["tuition","tuitions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學費","explanation":"指為在學校、學院或大學接受教學而支付的一筆錢。這裡的tuition從“教學”轉而指獲得這種教學所需的費用，是美國、加拿大等地區很常見的用法。","examples":[{"en":"Her parents are saving money to pay her university tuition.","zh":"她的父母正在攢錢支付她的大學學費。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tuition at the private college has risen sharply this year.","zh":"這所私立學院今年的學費大幅上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuition","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fe8c45af02b4682d831e","word":"tumble","forms":["tumble"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a969bd4f847ae428","term":"tumble","forms":["tumble","tumbles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"翻滾；摔倒","explanation":"指身體翻滾著跌倒，尤其是連續翻轉或從高處滾落的一跤。","examples":[{"en":"I took a tumble on the icy pavement.","zh":"我在結冰的人行道上摔了一跤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cyclist took a nasty tumble near the finish line.","zh":"那名腳踏車手在終點線附近狠狠摔了一跤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-defb264d37757ee9","term":"tumble","forms":["tumble","tumbles","tumbling","tumbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"翻滾；滾落","explanation":"指人或物連續翻轉著跌落或向前滾動，是“失去控制地轉動”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The child tumbled down the grassy hill.","zh":"孩子沿著長滿草的小山坡翻滾下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A loose stone tumbled over the edge.","zh":"一塊鬆動的石頭翻滾著越過了邊緣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ce62a71c5140242","term":"tumble","forms":["tumble","tumbles","tumbling","tumbled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"迅速下跌","explanation":"指價格、數量或水平突然快速下降，彷彿一路翻滾下落。","examples":[{"en":"Oil prices tumbled after the announcement.","zh":"公告發布後，油價大幅下跌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Attendance tumbled when the weather turned cold.","zh":"天氣轉冷後，出席人數驟減。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumble","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee03fb050595ab93cf3b","word":"tumor","forms":["tumor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1ebcc13061a6c818","term":"tumor","forms":["tumor","tumors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"異常腫塊；腫瘤","explanation":"指身體組織異常長出或聚集形成的腫塊。它可能是良性的，也可能是惡性的，因此不能僅憑 tumor 判斷是否患癌。","examples":[{"en":"The scan showed a small tumor near her kidney.","zh":"掃描顯示她的腎臟附近有一個小腫塊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor said the tumor was benign.","zh":"醫生說這個腫瘤是良性的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tumor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32d6e4a20c1cd7a5aabd","word":"tuna","forms":["tuna"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ddd397aaed6e2488","term":"tuna","forms":["tuna","tunas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金槍魚","explanation":"指金槍魚這一類海魚；說捕魚、海洋生物或魚類時，通常指活魚或這種魚本身。","examples":[{"en":"A school of tuna passed beneath the boat.","zh":"一群金槍魚從船下游過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fishermen caught three tuna before sunset.","zh":"漁民們在日落前捕到了三條金槍魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuna","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9da6a2fff2e48792","term":"tuna","forms":["tuna","tunas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金槍魚肉","explanation":"指金槍魚可食用的肉，常見於餐館、食品包裝或談論做飯的語境。","examples":[{"en":"I made a tuna sandwich for lunch.","zh":"我午飯做了一個金槍魚三明治。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Add some tuna to the salad.","zh":"在沙拉里加一些金槍魚肉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuna","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28263836ea961ac7e409","word":"tune","forms":["tune"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ef510cae1c95a85","term":"tune","forms":["tune","tunes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"旋律","explanation":"tune 最基本的音樂義是可以被哼唱或演奏的旋律，重點在音符排列形成的曲調。","examples":[{"en":"She played a simple tune on the piano.","zh":"她用鋼琴彈奏了一段簡單的旋律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't get that tune out of my head.","zh":"我腦子裡一直揮不去那段旋律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9559cae0a39c3a86","term":"tune","forms":["tune","tunes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歌曲；短樂曲","explanation":"tune 也可以泛指一首歌曲或短小的音樂作品，尤其是強調其好聽、易記的音樂部分。","examples":[{"en":"The children sang a cheerful tune on the way home.","zh":"孩子們回家路上唱了一首歡快的歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fiddler played a lively tune for the dancers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1bbed742c4dac4b","term":"tune","forms":["tune","tunes","tuning","tuned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調準樂器","explanation":"tune 作動詞時首先表示調節樂器各音高，使它能正確發聲；這正是“把聲音調準”這一核心畫面的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"I need to tune my guitar before the concert.","zh":"音樂會前我需要把吉他調準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tuned the violin by ear.","zh":"他憑耳朵把小提琴調準了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0d69ef942035c63c","term":"tune","forms":["tune","tunes","tuning","tuned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調校裝置","explanation":"它還可以表示調整機器或電子裝置的引數，使其執行得更好；這裡是把“調準聲音”擴充套件成“調好整個系統”。","examples":[{"en":"The mechanic tuned the engine to improve its performance.","zh":"修理工調校了發動機，以提升它的效能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The software was tuned to use less power.","zh":"這款軟體經過調校，以減少耗電量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tune","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-94a35fdc30df7d129a44","word":"tunnel","forms":["tunnel"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90a2bcb6a3147f26","term":"tunnel","forms":["tunnel","tunnels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地下或水下通道","explanation":"指穿過地下、山體或水下的長通道，通常供人、車輛或鐵路透過。這是 tunnel 最核心、最常見的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The train disappeared into the tunnel.","zh":"火車駛入了隧道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A new tunnel will connect the two sides of the mountain.","zh":"一條新隧道將連線山的兩側。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tunnel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ec97962f1d8e5044","term":"tunnel","forms":["tunnel","tunnels","tunneling","tunnelling","tunneled","tunnelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"挖通或挖穿","explanation":"表示在某物下面或穿過某物挖出通道，重點是主動製造一條隧道。","examples":[{"en":"Workers tunneled beneath the river to build the subway line.","zh":"工人在河底下挖隧道，以修建地鐵線路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The engineers tunneled through the rock.","zh":"工程師們挖穿了岩石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tunnel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0279e85e721a66f7dfe8","word":"turmoil","forms":["turmoil"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2ccbe179ab116202","term":"turmoil","forms":["turmoil","turmoils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混亂；動盪","explanation":"指一個局面、組織或人的內心處於嚴重的無秩序和不確定狀態，事情像被風暴攪在一起，難以穩定下來。","examples":[{"en":"The company has been in turmoil since its chief executive resigned.","zh":"這家公司自執行長辭職後一直處於動盪之中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The announcement caused turmoil in the financial markets.","zh":"這項公告在金融市場引起了動盪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turmoil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b473845f684444f80a2","word":"turn","forms":["turn"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8240ec479d49eb1a","term":"turn","forms":["turn","turns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"轉向；轉動一下","explanation":"指方向、朝向或位置發生一次改變，也可以指把某物轉動一下；可以把它想成物體“轉過去”。","examples":[{"en":"Give the handle a turn, then pull it.","zh":"把手柄轉一下，然後拉它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We took a sharp turn into the narrow street.","zh":"我們急轉彎駛入了那條窄街。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-30926edd0ceb65c5","term":"turn","forms":["turn","turns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輪到使用；輪流","explanation":"表示共享某物或做某事時，機會按順序“轉到”某個人那裡；這就是“輪到你了”。","examples":[{"en":"The children took turns reading the story aloud.","zh":"孩子們輪流大聲朗讀這個故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Can I have a turn on the swing?","zh":"輪到我盪鞦韆了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-09b32add7af421a3","term":"turn","forms":["turn","turns","turning","turned","turnt","turnest","turnedst","turneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"轉動","explanation":"表示人或物體自身轉動、旋轉或改變朝向，正是“轉過去”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"The Earth turns as it travels around the Sun.","zh":"地球在繞太陽執行時不斷自轉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He turned slowly to face the door.","zh":"他慢慢轉過身來面對門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aba3af38298041fb","term":"turn","forms":["turn","turns","turning","turned","turnt","turnest","turnedst","turneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變成；變得","explanation":"表示人或事物的狀態、顏色、性情發生變化，也就是“轉過去”成為另一種樣子或態度。","examples":[{"en":"The sky turned pink at sunset.","zh":"日落時天空變成了粉紅色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He turned angry when I questioned his decision.","zh":"我質疑他的決定時，他變得生氣起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74dd730b5c36c1cb4fdb","word":"turtle","forms":["turtle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f195bff19bedff39","term":"turtle","forms":["turtle","turtles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"龜；有硬殼的龜類動物","explanation":"指身體被堅硬甲殼保護的龜類動物，包括陸龜和水龜等。這是 turtle 最基本、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"A turtle was resting on a log in the pond.","zh":"一隻龜正在池塘裡的木頭上休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children watched the turtle disappear into the water.","zh":"孩子們看著那隻龜消失在水中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turtle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-038740ef981ab56f4e05","word":"tutor","forms":["tutor"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9551d0b0b0790763","term":"tutor","forms":["tutor","tutors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輔導老師","explanation":"指專門幫助一個學生或少數學生學習的人，重點是針對性輔導，而不是面對整班進行普通授課。","examples":[{"en":"I meet my physics tutor twice a week.","zh":"我每週和物理輔導老師見兩次面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her tutor helped her prepare for the exam.","zh":"她的輔導老師幫助她準備考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tutor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-84b2dc36cf281462","term":"tutor","forms":["tutor","tutors","tutoring","tutored"],"pos":"verb","zh":"輔導、指導","explanation":"指標對個人或小組進行講解、練習和學習指導，就是把名詞tutor所做的工作變成動作。","examples":[{"en":"She tutors children in reading after school.","zh":"她放學後輔導孩子們閱讀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tutored me for the entrance exam.","zh":"他輔導我準備入學考試。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tutor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dc8ffdbf2736dbdf3950","word":"twice","forms":["twice"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e54c831e6151bfc","term":"twice","forms":["twice"],"pos":"adv","zh":"兩次；兩遍","explanation":"表示同一動作或事件發生兩回，重點是重複的次數，而不是數量變成兩倍。比如一天刷牙兩次，就是分別在兩個時間做這件事。","examples":[{"en":"You should brush your teeth twice a day.","zh":"你應該每天刷兩次牙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I have checked the address twice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00f05cbef999f155","term":"twice","forms":["twice"],"pos":"adv","zh":"兩倍；加倍","explanation":"表示數量、強度或程度變成原來的兩倍，把原來的一份看成兩份相同的份量。它不是說某事重複發生兩回，而是說結果或程度增加到兩倍。","examples":[{"en":"This box is twice as heavy as the old one.","zh":"這個箱子有舊箱子的兩倍重。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This suitcase weighs twice as much as that one.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b6b49e8e232ea080181","word":"twig","forms":["twig"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e8773b48dbf048a2","term":"twig","forms":["twig","twigs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"細枝","explanation":"指樹木或灌木上細而小的枝條，通常比 branch 更纖細；它可以被折下、收集或用來生火。","examples":[{"en":"They gathered dry twigs to start the fire.","zh":"他們收集了些幹樹枝來生火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A twig snapped under my shoe.","zh":"一根細樹枝在我的鞋底下折斷了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0edbdffac1b7169c3d9d","word":"twilight","forms":["twilight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8eaea8c52f90dbd8","term":"twilight","forms":["twilight","twilights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天空中的暮光","explanation":"指太陽將落或剛落後，天空中由大氣反射和散射形成的柔和微光。它不是太陽本身，而是白晝留下的、介於明亮和黑暗之間的光。","examples":[{"en":"The hills were still visible in the fading twilight.","zh":"群山在漸漸暗下去的暮光中仍然看得見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sat outside and watched the twilight spread across the sky.","zh":"我們坐在外面，看著暮光鋪展開來，籠罩天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twilight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dab257dc726157e3","term":"twilight","forms":["twilight","twilights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黃昏時分","explanation":"指暮光出現的那段時間，即白天將盡、黑夜尚未完全到來的過渡時段。重點不只是光線，而是一天中的這個時間段。","examples":[{"en":"It was already twilight when we reached the village.","zh":"我們到達村子時，天已經是黃昏了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We reached the cottage just before twilight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twilight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72b33a1cb0bfc9cdd3db","word":"twin","forms":["twin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e29f85d2f4874fae","term":"twin","forms":["twin","twins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雙胞胎中的一個","explanation":"指在同一次懷孕中出生、共享同一個子宮的兩個孩子中的一個，也可以較少用於動物。重點是“一對雙胞胎中的單獨一個”。","examples":[{"en":"One twin is quiet, but the other is very outgoing.","zh":"其中一個雙胞胎很安靜，另一個卻非常外向。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a twin brother who lives nearby.","zh":"她有一個住在附近的雙胞胎哥哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8641e464abd526e","term":"twin","forms":["twin","twins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"相似的一件；成對者","explanation":"指兩個相似、對應或關係密切的事物中的一個，不一定真的來自同一次出生。兩個建築、城市、物品或概念只要形成相似的一對，都可以這樣稱呼。","examples":[{"en":"The old bridge has a twin across the river.","zh":"那座老橋在河對岸有一座與它相似的橋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sculpture is the twin of the one in the museum.","zh":"這座雕塑與博物館裡的那座是一對相似品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2bf273baa98714c2434","word":"twinkle","forms":["twinkle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-28381b54b7fdface","term":"twinkle","forms":["twinkle","twinkles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"閃爍的微光","explanation":"指微弱、明暗交替或若隱若現的光，好像遠處的小星星在一閃一閃。","examples":[{"en":"A twinkle of light appeared between the trees.","zh":"樹叢之間出現了一點閃爍的微光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched the twinkles on the water after sunset.","zh":"日落後，我們看著水面上閃爍的微光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c57281759d96578e","term":"twinkle","forms":["twinkle","twinkles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眼中的喜悅神采","explanation":"指人的眼睛因開心、淘氣或興奮而顯得明亮有神，彷彿眼裡閃著光。","examples":[{"en":"There was a twinkle in her eye as she told the joke.","zh":"她講那個笑話時，眼中閃著頑皮而開心的神采。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His eyes had a warm twinkle when he talked about his grandchildren.","zh":"他談到孫輩時，眼中流露出溫暖的喜悅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7b08fd9003e705b","term":"twinkle","forms":["twinkle","twinkles","twinkling","twinkled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"閃爍發光","explanation":"指光線忽明忽暗、斷續地發亮，像遠處的小燈或星星在一閃一閃。","examples":[{"en":"The village lights twinkled far below us.","zh":"村莊的燈光在我們下方遠處閃爍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stars twinkled above the quiet lake.","zh":"星星在寧靜的湖面上方閃爍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91e36c30faef5ccf","term":"twinkle","forms":["twinkle","twinkles","twinkling","twinkled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"眼中閃現喜悅","explanation":"指人的眼睛因開心、機靈或淘氣而顯得明亮有神，像眼裡閃著一絲光。","examples":[{"en":"Her eyes twinkled with amusement.","zh":"她的眼中閃著愉快的神采。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His eyes twinkled when he heard the surprising news.","zh":"聽到這個令人意外的訊息時，他眼中閃出了喜悅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72554af938a392166526","word":"twist","forms":["twist"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09498414bf4868d7","term":"twist","forms":["twist","twists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"扭轉；纏繞；扭轉動作或結果","explanation":"指把東西擰轉、纏繞的動作，也可指這種動作留下的形狀或結果；就像把一根繩子擰緊，或擰了一下耳朵。","examples":[{"en":"Give the lid a twist and it should come off.","zh":"把蓋子擰一下，就應該能取下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She added a quick twist to the scarf before tying it.","zh":"她先把圍巾快速擰了一下，然後繫好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adb929a42b889b53","term":"twist","forms":["twist","twists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意外轉折","explanation":"指故事、事件或局勢突然出現的意外變化；故事像道路一樣拐出了新的方向。","examples":[{"en":"The film has an unexpected twist at the end.","zh":"這部電影結尾有一個意想不到的轉折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The investigation took a new twist after the witness came forward.","zh":"證人出面後，調查出現了新的轉折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fca95759b80278b2","term":"twist","forms":["twist","twists","twisting","twisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擰轉；扭轉","explanation":"把繩子、線或其他東西的兩端朝相反方向擰，使它扭轉成形；這正是把繩子擰轉的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"Twist the two wires together so they stay connected.","zh":"把這兩根電線擰在一起，讓它們保持連線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She twisted the cap hard, but it would not open.","zh":"她使勁擰瓶蓋，但還是打不開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4fd7a36bbb4546c","term":"twist","forms":["twist","twists","twisting","twisted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"歪曲話語或事實","explanation":"在轉述時故意或不準確地改變原話、證據或事實的含義，就像把話語擰向了另一個方向。","examples":[{"en":"You are twisting my words—I never said the plan was impossible.","zh":"你在歪曲我的話——我從沒說過這個計劃不可能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report twisted the facts to make the company look innocent.","zh":"這份報告歪曲了事實，想讓公司看起來無罪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1303c06b0b014d0ce7b9","word":"type","forms":["type"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c7a727a63eebae4","term":"type","forms":["type","types"],"pos":"noun","zh":"型別；類別","explanation":"具有共同特徵的一組事物就是一種 type。它可以是日常分類，也可以是比較明確的產品、動物或事物類別。","examples":[{"en":"This type of camera works well in low light.","zh":"這種型別的相機在光線不足時也拍得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There are several types of tea in the shop.","zh":"這家店裡有好幾種茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/type","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-947c9462d9540a77","term":"type","forms":["type","types"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喜歡的型別","explanation":"說某人是 my type，就是說這個人的性格、外表或其他特徵符合“我通常會喜歡的那一類人”。","examples":[{"en":"He is friendly and funny, but he is not really my type.","zh":"他友好又風趣，但不太是我喜歡的型別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is exactly his type.","zh":"她正是他喜歡的那種人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/type","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3a99fc8e48921dcb","term":"type","forms":["type","types","typing","typed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打字；用打字機輸入","explanation":"type 作動詞時，可以表示用鍵盤或打字機把文字輸入出來；核心畫面就是把文字一個個“打進去”。","examples":[{"en":"She typed a letter to her grandmother.","zh":"她給祖母打了一封信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I typed the address into the form.","zh":"我把地址輸入了表格。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/type","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-817211392559c50b","term":"type","forms":["type","types","typing","typed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"鍵盤輸入","explanation":"在電腦或手機上，type 表示用鍵盤輸入文字、命令或其他內容。","examples":[{"en":"Please type your password and press Enter.","zh":"請輸入密碼，然後按回車鍵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Type your name into the box at the top.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/type","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-331c96b8e9d67741d82c","word":"typhoon","forms":["typhoon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8605a151befc88ab","term":"typhoon","forms":["typhoon","typhoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"颱風；強烈熱帶氣旋","explanation":"typhoon 最常見的意思是颱風：一種猛烈旋轉、能帶來強風和暴雨的熱帶風暴。","examples":[{"en":"A powerful typhoon is approaching the coast.","zh":"一場強颱風正在逼近海岸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The typhoon forced the airport to close.","zh":"這場颱風迫使機場關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/typhoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c7f9e48e8afe569","term":"typhoon","forms":["typhoon","typhoons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"西北太平洋的颱風","explanation":"在較嚴格的氣象用法中，typhoon 特指西北太平洋地區達到一定強度的熱帶氣旋；換到其他海域，類似風暴可能使用別的名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The storm became a typhoon after forming over the western Pacific.","zh":"這場風暴在西太平洋上空形成後成為了颱風。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The typhoon struck the coast east of Taiwan.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/typhoon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9bfac98c5b6579fbb4b8","word":"typical","forms":["typical"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a7d58c41d6f3766f","term":"typical","forms":["typical","more typical","most typical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"典型的；有代表性的","explanation":"指某人、某物或某種形式很能代表一個類別、群體或觀念，像這個類別的“樣板照片”。","examples":[{"en":"She is a typical example of a careful and patient researcher.","zh":"她是細心而有耐心的研究人員的典型代表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The building has the typical features of a coastal village.","zh":"這座建築具有沿海村莊的典型特徵。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/typical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fad482c3627bc284","term":"typical","forms":["typical","more typical","most typical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"通常的；正常的","explanation":"指某種情況符合平常規律，是人們通常會看到或預料到的，不顯得特別反常。","examples":[{"en":"A typical workday for him begins at seven.","zh":"他通常的工作日從七點開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was a typical spring morning: cool and rainy.","zh":"那是一個很平常的春日早晨：天氣涼爽而多雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/typical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72de275ac0b40947de8b","word":"ugly","forms":["ugly"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-26f3aadd27100543","term":"ugly","forms":["ugly","uglier","ugliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難看的","explanation":"指外表不美觀、看起來讓人不舒服的；這是從“讓人想躲開”的核心感覺發展出的最常見意思。","examples":[{"en":"That old building is ugly but well made.","zh":"那座老建築很難看，但做工很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I bought an ugly sweater for the costume party.","zh":"我為化裝派對買了一件很難看的毛衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ugly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-188bbff056d61c62","term":"ugly","forms":["ugly","uglier","ugliest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"惡劣的；令人反感的","explanation":"把“看著就想躲開”的感覺轉到行為、做法或態度上，表示不道德、傷人或令人厭惡。","examples":[{"en":"It was an ugly trick to play on a friend.","zh":"對朋友耍這種卑劣的手段太過分了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The argument got ugly after midnight.","zh":"爭吵過了午夜後變得很難看。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ugly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f21adfd19983708d3855","word":"ultimate","forms":["ultimate"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cb9cf626f9387ea6","term":"ultimate","forms":["ultimate","more ultimate","most ultimate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最後的；末尾的","explanation":"指在一系列事物中排在最後的一個，重點是順序已經到達終點。","examples":[{"en":"The ultimate chapter explains what happened to the missing letter.","zh":"最後一章解釋了那封失蹤的信後來發生了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ultimate chapter brings the story back home.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ultimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55f5bdba7c2978f2","term":"ultimate","forms":["ultimate","more ultimate","most ultimate"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最大限度的；最極端的","explanation":"表示某種性質或程度達到可能的最高點，就像一路走到了極限；可以是最大的快樂、最嚴重的危險或最強的力量。","examples":[{"en":"For many climbers, reaching the summit is the ultimate challenge.","zh":"對許多登山者來說，登上山頂是最大的挑戰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She believes that helping others is the ultimate reward.","zh":"她認為幫助別人是最大的回報。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ultimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-726f3f20418754e2","term":"ultimate","forms":["ultimate","ultimates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最根本之物","explanation":"指一組事物中最基礎、最核心的那個部分，是追問到盡頭後留下的根本物件。","examples":[{"en":"The ultimate in comfort is a quiet room and a good book.","zh":"舒適的極致就是一間安靜的房間和一本好書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The researchers were searching for the ultimate behind the pattern.","zh":"研究人員正在尋找這一模式背後的根本原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ultimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2974744982f08b207751","word":"umbrella","forms":["umbrella"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb50f726076cff53","term":"umbrella","forms":["umbrella","umbrellas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雨傘；遮陽傘","explanation":"一種有布面和骨架的物品，開啟後可以擋雨或遮太陽。這是 umbrella 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Take an umbrella; it looks like rain.","zh":"帶把傘吧，看起來要下雨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She left her umbrella on the train.","zh":"她把傘落在火車上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/umbrella","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-59f483edba3c1a5a","term":"umbrella","forms":["umbrella","umbrellas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保護層；防護範圍","explanation":"指像傘一樣在上方或外圍提供保護的力量、裝置或範圍，不一定是真正的傘。例如防空力量可以保護一片區域。","examples":[{"en":"The aircraft operated under the umbrella of a powerful air-defense system.","zh":"這些飛機在強大防空系統的保護下行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The policy places dependents under the same insurance umbrella.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/umbrella","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-937c764e6f21c353dc07","word":"unanimous","forms":["unanimous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6114e63b1448cdf3","term":"unanimous","forms":["unanimous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全票透過的；一致同意的","explanation":"指一個決定、表決結果或行動得到相關人員全體同意，沒有人投反對票。重點在於“結果一致”，就像所有人的手都舉向同一個選項。","examples":[{"en":"The committee reached a unanimous decision to approve the plan.","zh":"委員會一致決定批准這項計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jury returned a unanimous verdict.","zh":"陪審團作出了一致裁決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unanimous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb45747e9d01fb87","term":"unanimous","forms":["unanimous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"意見一致的；立場相同的","explanation":"指群體中的人都持有相同觀點或判斷，彼此完全認同；這裡強調的是“大家心裡想的一樣”，不一定是在正式投票後形成的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The experts were unanimous in their support for the new safety rules.","zh":"專家們一致支援新的安全規定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The jury was unanimous in its verdict.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unanimous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3107ea0301a27894a212","word":"uncle","forms":["uncle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ffcc2f56129befc4","term":"uncle","forms":["uncle","uncles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"叔叔；舅舅","explanation":"指父母的兄弟，或父母的男性姻親，是 uncle 最基本的親屬義。中文需要根據具體親屬關係譯成“叔叔、伯伯、舅舅”等。","examples":[{"en":"My uncle lives near the coast.","zh":"我叔叔住在海邊附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her uncle taught her how to fish.","zh":"她舅舅教她怎麼釣魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uncle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49aac806eba9f99c35e7","word":"unconditional","forms":["unconditional"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ae017db6ba549071","term":"unconditional","forms":["unconditional","more unconditional","most unconditional"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無條件的；絕對的","explanation":"指某件事不以任何要求、限制或例外為前提，不管情況怎樣都成立或執行。它把“不附加條款”這個核心意思擴充套件為“徹底、沒有保留”。","examples":[{"en":"She gave her unconditional support to the new project.","zh":"她毫無保留地支援這個新專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement requires the unconditional release of all prisoners.","zh":"這項協議要求無條件釋放所有囚犯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unconditional","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1f7eba348f31fc9176de","word":"uncover","forms":["uncover"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b76af73afbf735d","term":"uncover","forms":["uncover","uncovers","uncovering","uncovered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭開覆蓋物","explanation":"把蓋在某物上面的東西移開，使它重新露出來。這是 uncover 最直接、最具體的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She uncovered the dish and let everyone see the meal.","zh":"她揭開盤子上的蓋子，讓大家看到裡面的飯菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers uncovered an old stone floor beneath the carpet.","zh":"工人們揭開地毯後，發現下面是一層古老的石地面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uncover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b041f1bf10a48539","term":"uncover","forms":["uncover","uncovers","uncovering","uncovered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭露身份","explanation":"查明並公開某人原本隱藏的身份，尤其常用於調查發現某人的真實身份。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation uncovered the identity of the anonymous donor.","zh":"調查查明瞭那位匿名捐贈者的身份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A security camera helped uncover the thief's identity.","zh":"一段監控錄影幫助查明瞭小偷的身份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uncover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2517978b3b5d847a","term":"uncover","forms":["uncover","uncovers","uncovering","uncovered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭露事實或秘密","explanation":"把隱藏的事實、問題、證據或秘密公開出來；它像是把遮住真相的“蓋子”掀開。","examples":[{"en":"The audit uncovered several mistakes in the company's accounts.","zh":"審計揭露了這家公司賬目中的幾處錯誤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audit uncovered years of unauthorized payments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uncover","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d767748a603799c85319","word":"under","forms":["under"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2f1ed03c00b04881","term":"under","forms":["under"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向下；在下方","explanation":"表示人或物處在較低處，或被帶到某物下面；這是“在下面”這一核心概念的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The strong currents pulled the swimmer under.","zh":"湍急的水流把游泳者拉到了水下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog crawled under and hid beneath the table.","zh":"狗鑽到下面，藏在桌子底下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/under","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3734fe6dcfcb6dbd","term":"under","forms":["under"],"pos":"adv","zh":"從下面穿過","explanation":"表示移動路線經過某物的下方，強調“穿到另一邊”或“從下面透過”。","examples":[{"en":"There's quite a gap, so you may be able to sneak under.","zh":"下面的縫隙很大，你也許能偷偷鑽過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dog squeezed under and escaped the fence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/under","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-60e608efacdc2b95","term":"under","forms":["under"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……下面","explanation":"表示某物位於另一物的下方，或處在其覆蓋、遮擋的範圍內；這是 under 最基本的空間意義。","examples":[{"en":"We found some shade under a tree.","zh":"我們在樹下找到了一片陰涼處。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The keys were hidden under a pile of papers.","zh":"鑰匙藏在一疊檔案下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/under","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-546057e0a00797bb","term":"under","forms":["under"],"pos":"prep","zh":"低於","explanation":"表示數量、年齡、價格、速度或其他數值沒有達到某個界限，落在這條標準線下面。","examples":[{"en":"Interest rates are now under 1%.","zh":"目前利率低於百分之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Children under twelve can enter for free.","zh":"十二歲以下的兒童可以免費入場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/under","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b38d369ea82dfef24bc","word":"underestimate","forms":["underestimate"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-523d194c69f87126","term":"underestimate","forms":["underestimate","underestimates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"過低的估計","explanation":"指估出來的數量、價值或程度比實際情況低。它把“刻度偏低”的畫面變成一個具體的估計結果。","examples":[{"en":"The original cost estimate was a serious underestimate.","zh":"最初的成本估計嚴重偏低。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey was an underestimate of the true demand.","zh":"這項調查低估了真實需求。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underestimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c3b3eb0ed054727e","term":"underestimate","forms":["underestimate","underestimates","underestimating","underestimated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"低估數量、價值或能力","explanation":"指認為某人或某物的數量、價值、能力等低於實際水平。就像用偏低的刻度去測量，得到的結果少了或輕了。","examples":[{"en":"We underestimated how many people would attend.","zh":"我們低估了會有多少人參加。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Never underestimate her ability to solve difficult problems.","zh":"永遠不要低估她解決難題的能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underestimate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2bf4fdc2bc8fe77d394","word":"undergo","forms":["undergo"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-686fe53c1e6cf463","term":"undergo","forms":["undergo","undergoes","undergoing","underwent","undergone"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經歷；經過","explanation":"表示親自經歷一個過程、階段或變化，就像一路走過它。重點是過程正在發生或已經發生，而不一定帶有痛苦意味。","examples":[{"en":"The building is undergoing major renovations.","zh":"這座建築正在進行大規模翻修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She underwent several medical tests last month.","zh":"她上個月接受了幾項醫學檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undergo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ddb7b64fec9c5713","term":"undergo","forms":["undergo","undergoes","undergoing","underwent","undergone"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經受；忍受","explanation":"表示走過艱難、痛苦或令人受損的經歷，強調承受和熬過，而不只是一般地遇到某件事。","examples":[{"en":"The patients underwent painful treatment.","zh":"這些病人接受了痛苦的治療。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survivors underwent years of hardship.","zh":"這些倖存者經歷了多年的艱難生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undergo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2bca9949a5516969043","word":"undergraduate","forms":["undergraduate"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-09afcc37857a306d","term":"undergraduate","forms":["undergraduate","undergraduates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"本科生","explanation":"指正在大學讀本科、尚未取得學位的學生。可以把他想成仍在通往大學學位的路上的人。","examples":[{"en":"She is an undergraduate in biology at a university in London.","zh":"她是倫敦一所大學的生物學本科生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library gives undergraduates free access to its research databases.","zh":"圖書館為本科生免費提供研究資料庫的使用許可權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undergraduate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-944969efb294d4641440","word":"underline","forms":["underline"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b08c13879cbe7e5e","term":"underline","forms":["underline","underlines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下劃線","explanation":"指畫在文字下方、用來突出文字或表示連結等功能的線。它就是“託在文字下面的線”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The title has an underline beneath it.","zh":"標題下面有一條下劃線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Click the underlined word to open the link.","zh":"點選帶下劃線的單詞即可開啟連結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38d45e080b93e21d","term":"underline","forms":["underline","underlines","underlining","underlined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"在……下畫線","explanation":"指在文字下面畫一條線，使它顯眼或提示讀者注意；這是 underline 最直接的“線上下面”用法。","examples":[{"en":"Please underline the words you do not understand.","zh":"請在你不理解的單詞下面畫線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She underlined the date in her calendar.","zh":"她在日曆上把日期畫了下劃線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9791eb1bdb535ccc","term":"underline","forms":["underline","underlines","underlining","underlined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強調；突出","explanation":"指在意義上把某件事“托出來”，讓它顯得特別重要，而不一定真的畫線。它可以強調事實、問題、重要性或某種態度。","examples":[{"en":"The mistake underlines the need for better training.","zh":"這個錯誤突顯了加強培訓的必要性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her reaction underlined how serious the problem was.","zh":"她的反應突顯了問題的嚴重性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underline","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-342c8c61e679d49001c5","word":"underlying","forms":["underlying"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6822e579b19e4873","term":"underlying","forms":["underlying"],"pos":"adj","zh":"位於下面的","explanation":"指實際處在表面、覆蓋物或其他東西下面的，強調空間位置。這是最具體的核心義，其他抽象義都可以看作“藏在下面、支撐上面”的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"We dug down to the underlying rock.","zh":"我們向下挖，挖到了下面的岩石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The underlying soil is very dry.","zh":"下面的土壤非常乾燥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underlying","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3407bbe64a2cdc2c","term":"underlying","forms":["underlying"],"pos":"adj","zh":"基礎的；根本的","explanation":"指位於問題或系統底層、支撐其成立的基本因素。它不一定真的在空間下面，而是像地下岩層一樣，為表面現象提供基礎。","examples":[{"en":"We need to understand the underlying cause of the problem.","zh":"我們需要了解這個問題背後的根本原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Trust is an underlying principle of the agreement.","zh":"信任是這份協議所依據的一項基本原則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underlying","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[113,115],"total":2,"counts":{"113":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-5d13e04fd93bd7d1a732","word":"undermine","forms":["undermine"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b47ad8bfaa1331c2","term":"undermine","forms":["undermine","undermines","undermining","undermined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"削弱；暗中阻礙","explanation":"指透過行動、言論或內部衝突削弱某人、某項計劃、某種權威或某段關係，使它更難成功或失去可信度。它就像從根基下面挖空，表面上未必直接攻擊，基礎卻在變弱。","examples":[{"en":"Constant criticism undermined her confidence.","zh":"不斷的批評削弱了她的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The argument undermined public trust in the project.","zh":"這場爭論削弱了公眾對該專案的信任。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undermine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-943cb31097f2d2d7","term":"undermine","forms":["undermine","undermines","undermining","undermined"],"pos":"verb","zh":"從下面挖掘","explanation":"指從某物下面挖出通道或空隙，尤其是為了使它倒塌、破壞它，或達到軍事目的。重點是從底部動手，讓上面的東西失去支撐。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers undermined the wall before the attack.","zh":"士兵們在進攻前從牆底挖掘，使牆失去支撐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The miners undermined the wall before setting their charges.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undermine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-49e7635616e042509b3c","word":"underneath","forms":["underneath"],"officialPos":"prep./adv./n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc133bc4bc25f289","term":"underneath","forms":["underneath"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在下面","explanation":"表示人或物位於另一物的下方，是 underneath 最核心、最容易擴充套件的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The cat is hiding underneath.","zh":"貓正躲在下面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wore a T-shirt underneath his jacket.","zh":"他在夾克裡面穿了一件短袖衫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underneath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4aa3fb343451de42","term":"underneath","forms":["underneath"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……下面","explanation":"表示某人或某物位於另一物的下方，直接體現“從下方承受或遮蔽”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Underneath the bridge, the water was completely still.","zh":"橋下面的水面完全沒有波動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found her keys underneath the newspaper.","zh":"她在報紙下面找到了鑰匙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underneath","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4584d4a67e5cba58145d","word":"underpass","forms":["underpass"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"underpass","forms":["underpass"],"pos":"n.","zh":"地下通道；下穿道路","examples":[{"en":"Use the underpass to cross the busy road safely.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The underpass was closed because of flooding.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9dc689e6d50ad6f35cc","word":"understand","forms":["understand"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-254d5f82841a7a63","term":"understand","forms":["understand","understands","understanding","understood","understandest","understoodest","understandeth","-","understanded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"聽懂；看懂","explanation":"把話語、文字、標誌或其他資訊的意義接通並正確解釋出來，就是“聽懂、看懂”。重點是理解了內容，而不只是聽見或看見。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't understand the last part of the instructions.","zh":"我沒看懂說明的最後一部分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you understand what she is asking?","zh":"你明白她在問什麼嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/understand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-767ed438ee0e26ee","term":"understand","forms":["understand","understands","understanding","understood","understandest","understoodest","understandeth","-","understanded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"掌握；熟悉做法","explanation":"對一項任務、工作或專業已經熟悉到能夠正確承擔或完成，不只是知道它的名稱。","examples":[{"en":"Before you begin, make sure you understand the task.","zh":"開始之前，務必確認自己已經明白這項任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He understands how to repair old mechanical clocks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/understand","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-884e4523ed453ba57253","word":"undertake","forms":["undertake"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9ba9117cfb8d92fe","term":"undertake","forms":["undertake","undertakes","undertaking","undertook","undertaken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承擔並開始做","explanation":"指主動接下某項任務、工作或計劃，並著手去完成；重點是把事情接到自己肩上，而不只是開始行動。","examples":[{"en":"The team undertook a detailed review of the safety procedures.","zh":"這個團隊著手對安全程式進行了詳細審查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She undertook the difficult task of restoring the old house.","zh":"她承擔了修復那座老房子的艱鉅任務。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e7a2369c5163a862","term":"undertake","forms":["undertake","undertakes","undertaking","undertook","undertaken"],"pos":"verb","zh":"承諾去做","explanation":"指鄭重地答應承擔某項義務或活動，承諾自己會去做；它仍然是“把責任接到手上”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The contractor undertook to finish the repairs by Friday.","zh":"承包商承諾在星期五前完成維修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The landlord undertook to install a handrail before our return.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8ba179f8de8b2b503acd","word":"underway","forms":["underway"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a891227f41a17b3a","term":"underway","forms":["underway","more underway","most underway"],"pos":"adv","zh":"正在進行；進展中","explanation":"事情已經啟動，正在向前推進，還沒有結束；也可以指人在旅途中或行動已經開始。這個意思可以理解為“事情已經在路上”。","examples":[{"en":"Construction on the new library is well underway.","zh":"新圖書館的建設已經進展得很順利了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The meeting was already underway when I arrived.","zh":"我到達時，會議已經開始了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underway","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-431e876d148bdfb0e477","word":"underwear","forms":["underwear"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-617ea690ecab9369","term":"underwear","forms":["underwear","underwears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"貼身內衣","explanation":"指穿在外衣裡面、直接貼著皮膚的衣物，是一個總稱，可以包括內褲、胸罩、背心等。","examples":[{"en":"Children should wear clean underwear every day.","zh":"孩子們應該每天穿乾淨的內衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She packed enough underwear for the whole trip.","zh":"她帶了足夠這次旅行用的內衣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underwear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5907c2fb3f247dab","term":"underwear","forms":["underwear","underwears"],"pos":"noun","zh":"內褲等貼身下裝","explanation":"在許多日常語境中，underwear 會縮小指內褲、平角褲、三角褲等貼身下裝，有時也把胸罩等一起包括在內；具體範圍要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"I need to buy some new underwear before the beach holiday.","zh":"海濱度假前，我得買些新內褲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pack several changes of underwear for the trip.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underwear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f015346ae3563d83d3a9","word":"undo","forms":["undo"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1670eea7ea77926","term":"undo","forms":["undo","undoes","undoing","undid","undone"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撤銷；反轉結果","explanation":"undo 表示把已經完成的動作或它造成的結果反過來，恢復到較早的狀態；電腦裡的“撤銷”就是這個核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"Can you undo the last change?","zh":"你能撤銷上一次更改嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The treatment helped undo some of the damage.","zh":"這種治療幫助挽回了一部分損傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c3665612bc8156de52ed","word":"undoubtedly","forms":["undoubtedly"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e14f10a21c81c49d","term":"undoubtedly","forms":["undoubtedly","more undoubtedly","most undoubtedly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"無疑；肯定地","explanation":"表示說話人認為某件事確定無疑，因而直接肯定地陳述它；它就是把結論放到“疑問”之外。","examples":[{"en":"She is undoubtedly the most experienced person on the team.","zh":"她無疑是團隊裡經驗最豐富的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This decision will undoubtedly affect the whole community.","zh":"這個決定肯定會影響整個社群。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undoubtedly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ab37c8e4a2ef4607964","word":"unemployment","forms":["unemployment"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ac7703537fbef5a","term":"unemployment","forms":["unemployment","unemployments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"沒有工作；失業狀態","explanation":"指一個人沒有工作、處於失業狀態，重點是個人暫時沒有就業，而不是專指某個統計數字。它是“工作崗位空著、人沒有工作”這一核心畫面最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"After losing his job, he struggled with unemployment for several months.","zh":"失去工作後，他經歷了幾個月的失業期，生活很困難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unemployment left him anxious about the rent.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unemployment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d1f7d1f976fb87f8","term":"unemployment","forms":["unemployment","unemployments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟中的失業現象","explanation":"指社會或經濟中許多人沒有工作的總體現象。這裡的畫面從一個沒有工作的人擴大到一批人同時找不到工作，因此常用於討論社會問題和經濟狀況。","examples":[{"en":"High unemployment can put pressure on families and local communities.","zh":"高失業率可能給家庭和當地社群帶來壓力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unemployment rose sharply after the factories closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unemployment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2549c03a28eeebc1","term":"unemployment","forms":["unemployment","unemployments"],"pos":"noun","zh":"失業率；失業水平","explanation":"指經濟體中沒有工作的勞動力所佔比例，常以百分比報告。它仍然來自“崗位空著”的核心畫面，但重點已經從現象轉為可以測量和比較的數字。","examples":[{"en":"Unemployment fell to 4.8% in the first quarter.","zh":"第一季度失業率降至4.8%。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unemployment rose sharply after the factory closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unemployment","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-37214dd6d7b6e2bd8caa","word":"unfold","forms":["unfold"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1afecb879c48dcb","term":"unfold","forms":["unfold","unfolds","unfolding","unfolded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開啟摺疊物","explanation":"指把地圖、布料、桌子等折起來的東西開啟，使它恢復展開的狀態；核心畫面就是把摺痕一層層開啟。","examples":[{"en":"Please unfold the map so we can find the trail.","zh":"請把地圖展開，好讓我們找到小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She unfolded the blanket and spread it on the grass.","zh":"她展開毯子，把它鋪在草地上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unfold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e290b0c740152188","term":"unfold","forms":["unfold","unfolds","unfolding","unfolded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐步發生","explanation":"指事件、故事或局勢像一張逐漸開啟的地圖一樣，按過程一步步發生並顯現出來。它通常強調發展的過程，而不只是最後的結果。","examples":[{"en":"We waited quietly to see how the story would unfold.","zh":"我們安靜地等著看故事會如何發展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan did not unfold as we had expected.","zh":"計劃的發展並不像我們預想的那樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unfold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2baaf8c0085ac22824b1","word":"unification","forms":["unification"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff8fbcf92b67d1a1","term":"unification","forms":["unification","unifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統一；合併過程","explanation":"指把原本分開的地區、制度、標準或其他部分合併為一個整體的行動或過程，重點在“正在統一”這件事。","examples":[{"en":"The unification of the two railway systems will simplify travel across the region.","zh":"兩套鐵路系統的統一將使整個地區的出行更加方便。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The government announced a plan for the unification of national safety standards.","zh":"政府宣佈了一項統一國家安全標準的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-61ace626794f30a4","term":"unification","forms":["unification","unifications"],"pos":"noun","zh":"統一狀態；合一","explanation":"指不同部分已經被合併後所形成的統一局面，重點在“已經成為一個整體”的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The unification of the country changed its political structure.","zh":"國家的統一改變了它的政治結構。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The agreement created political unification between the two regions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unification","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef379363dd0cb7be6663","word":"uniform","forms":["uniform"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7732761c191e78d1","term":"uniform","forms":["uniform","uniforms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"制服","explanation":"指學校、公司、軍隊、警察或其他群體成員穿的統一服裝，用來表明身份。","examples":[{"en":"All hotel staff must wear a uniform.","zh":"所有酒店員工都必須穿制服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She arrived at work in her new uniform.","zh":"她穿著新制服來上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uniform","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-91e776f8a587220fb5b6","word":"unify","forms":["unify"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3201cf7613ecb1b1","term":"unify","forms":["unify","unifies","unifying","unified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"統一；合併成一體","explanation":"把原本分開的部分、規則或組織合併起來，使它們成為一個統一的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The new system will unify the company's regional offices.","zh":"新系統將把公司的各地區辦事處整合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leader tried to unify the different groups around a common goal.","zh":"這位領導試圖讓不同團體圍繞共同目標團結成一個整體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb4b3527edfe3b3c","term":"unify","forms":["unify","unifies","unifying","unified"],"pos":"verb","zh":"合為一體；趨於一致","explanation":"多個原本分開的事物逐漸變得一致，最後像一個整體那樣存在；這裡不強調有人主動把它們合併。","examples":[{"en":"Over time, the separate traditions began to unify into a shared culture.","zh":"隨著時間推移，這些彼此分開的傳統開始融合成一種共同文化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The separate campaigning groups gradually unified.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unify","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ef3ff703d7565ab5215c","word":"union","forms":["union"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d438024e6b5b4e6","term":"union","forms":["union","unions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"聯合；合併","explanation":"指把兩個或多個分開的事物合併成一個整體的行為或過程，是“把東西拉到一起”這條主線的動作面。","examples":[{"en":"The union of the two companies created a stronger business.","zh":"兩家公司的合併造就了一家實力更強的企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their union brought peace to the region.","zh":"他們的聯合給這個地區帶來了和平。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/union","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9007ca4695d8b415","term":"union","forms":["union","unions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"團結狀態；和諧","explanation":"指事物已經聯合在一起的狀態，強調統一、協調或和諧，而不是合併這一動作。","examples":[{"en":"The ceremony celebrated the union of the two communities.","zh":"這場儀式慶祝了兩個社群的團結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team worked in perfect union.","zh":"這支隊伍配合得十分默契。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/union","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-41fd950bb3dcbcf3","term":"union","forms":["union","unions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工會","explanation":"指代表勞動者、維護其工資和工作條件等利益的組織，是日常英語中非常重要的具體義項。","examples":[{"en":"Most factory workers belong to a union.","zh":"大多數工廠工人都加入了工會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The union negotiated a better contract.","zh":"工會談判爭取到了一份更好的合同。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/union","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c2720445a45267813688","word":"unique","forms":["unique"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b7752a79b42caf6a","term":"unique","forms":["unique","uniquer","more unique","uniquest","most unique"],"pos":"adj","zh":"獨一無二的","explanation":"指某人、某物或某種經歷在同類中只有一個，沒有真正相同或可匹敵的物件；這是這個詞最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Every person has a unique life and a unique journey.","zh":"每個人都有獨一無二的人生和旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every snowflake has a unique pattern.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unique","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73e2fe27a648264e","term":"unique","forms":["unique","uniquer","more unique","uniquest","most unique"],"pos":"adj","zh":"僅某物件擁有的","explanation":"指某個特徵、能力或條件只屬於一個人或一件事，別人或其他事物沒有同樣的特徵；這裡的重點從“物件唯一”轉到“特徵只此一份”。","examples":[{"en":"This ability is unique to the human brain.","zh":"這種能力是人類大腦所獨有的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These markings are unique to this species.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unique","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,113,114,115],"total":11,"counts":{"111":2,"112":1,"113":1,"114":2,"115":5}}},{"id":"ceec-385cfdbc00ec32031699","word":"unit","forms":["unit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96ea7bbfb5d6915a","term":"unit","forms":["unit","units"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一；一個單位","explanation":"指作為整體組成部分的一個“單位”，也指數量上的一。它是理解其他用法的核心：整體可以由許多可分別計算或識別的unit組成。","examples":[{"en":"The machine measures the liquid in units of one milliliter.","zh":"這臺機器以一毫升為單位測量液體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Each unit in the set has a different color.","zh":"這套東西中的每個單元都有不同的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6cf7bb96c06354a9","term":"unit","forms":["unit","units"],"pos":"noun","zh":"標準計量單位","explanation":"指用來測量長度、重量、時間等量的標準。例如釐米可以是長度單位，小時可以是時間單位。","examples":[{"en":"The meter is a standard unit of length.","zh":"米是長度的標準單位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Choose the correct unit for measuring the package's weight.","zh":"選擇測量這個包裹重量的正確單位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-397c3c666ea4bf59","term":"unit","forms":["unit","units"],"pos":"noun","zh":"組織單位；小組","explanation":"指由人員、裝置或兩者組成、能夠作為一個整體執行任務的組織或小組。警察小隊、維修小組等都可以稱為unit。","examples":[{"en":"A special police unit searched the building.","zh":"一支特別警察小組搜查了這棟樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescue unit arrived before sunset.","zh":"救援小組在日落前趕到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5f6af583f79a4fd","term":"unit","forms":["unit","units"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可單獨出售的一件商品","explanation":"在商業和銷售中，unit指可以單獨計數和出售的一件商品或一個產品。賣出多少units，就是賣出多少件。","examples":[{"en":"The store sold 2,000 units of the new phone in its first week.","zh":"這家商店第一週賣出了2000部新手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop sold fifty units on its first day.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0ec19cbd2d3cc1d8f17a","word":"unite","forms":["unite"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-31e131d0eb46d0b3","term":"unite","forms":["unite","unites","uniting","united","unitest","unitedst","uniteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使聯合； объедин 成一體","explanation":"表示主動把原本分開的個人、團體或力量 объедин 成一個整體，重點在於“使它們合在一起”。","examples":[{"en":"The crisis united the whole community.","zh":"這場危機使整個社群團結了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leader hopes to unite the two parties.","zh":"這位領導人希望把兩個政黨聯合起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb0341ad09c8a3a3","term":"unite","forms":["unite","unites","uniting","united","unitest","unitedst","uniteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"團結起來","explanation":"表示原本分開的各方主動聚攏並形成共同立場或力量，重點在於“大家自己合到一起”。","examples":[{"en":"The workers united behind their common goal.","zh":"工人們團結在共同目標周圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The neighbors united to protect their shared garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5790b06f63b7c1646f0","word":"unity","forms":["unity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0150749adc2f084f","term":"unity","forms":["unity","unities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合一；一體","explanation":"指許多部分合在一起，成為一個不分裂的整體，重點是“作為一個整體存在”。","examples":[{"en":"The design has a strong sense of unity.","zh":"這個設計有很強的整體感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team stayed together in unity during the crisis.","zh":"危機期間，這個團隊團結一致。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6babee58db075f7","term":"unity","forms":["unity","unities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一致；和諧","explanation":"指人們的意見、目標或行動彼此協調，沒有明顯分裂；它是“一體”在人際合作中的表現。","examples":[{"en":"The leaders called for unity among the members.","zh":"領導人呼籲成員之間保持團結。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The choir sang with remarkable unity.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a9fd078562420a276b69","word":"universal","forms":["universal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c21b8b995622590","term":"universal","forms":["universal","more universal","most universal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全體共有的","explanation":"指某個群體或類別中的每一個成員都具有、適用或認可的性質。它把“覆蓋整個範圍”的概念用於一個明確的群體。","examples":[{"en":"There is no universal rule that works for every family.","zh":"沒有一條適用於每個家庭的普遍規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The desire for safety is nearly universal.","zh":"對安全的渴望幾乎是所有人共有的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/universal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-42575ab58f0398a2","term":"universal","forms":["universal","more universal","most universal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"全世界的；人人認可的","explanation":"指影響範圍擴充套件到全社會或全世界，幾乎所有人都知道、接受或經歷。它是“覆蓋整個群體”在現實社會中的常見延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The athlete received universal praise after the final.","zh":"那名運動員在決賽後獲得了全世界的讚譽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal won almost universal support.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/universal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-327a7380d2cc7cf09ed5","word":"universe","forms":["universe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ac307641fdd9adf","term":"universe","forms":["universe","universes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宇宙","explanation":"指所有存在的總和，是 universe 最基本、最廣的意義；它不只是星星和星系，還包括構成現實的時間與空間。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are still trying to understand how the universe began.","zh":"科學家仍在努力瞭解宇宙是如何開始的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The universe contains billions of galaxies.","zh":"宇宙包含數十億個星系。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/universe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dfa08f5dfe03fa1d","term":"universe","forms":["universe","universes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"全部相關事物","explanation":"把某個討論範圍裡的所有物件看成一個完整集合，不一定真的指天文學上的宇宙。","examples":[{"en":"A universe of possibilities opened up after the discovery.","zh":"這項發現帶來了無窮無盡的可能性。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survey covers the entire universe of registered applicants.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/universe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-adba6c0ec8a8d89efb03","word":"university","forms":["university"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33dc798d40dd9739","term":"university","forms":["university","universities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大學","explanation":"提供高等教育、開展深入學習和研究並授予學位的教育機構，通常招收高中畢業後的學生。","examples":[{"en":"She's studying mathematics at university.","zh":"她正在大學裡學習數學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The university offers courses in medicine and engineering.","zh":"這所大學開設醫學和工程學課程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/university","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c8a69f69754487458ba1","word":"unless","forms":["unless"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"unless","forms":["unless"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"除非；如果不","examples":[{"en":"We will have a picnic unless it rains.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Do not open the door unless you know who is outside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-787600ebe6d6c75b6bc0","word":"unlock","forms":["unlock"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-39d6f3a9de5852fd","term":"unlock","forms":["unlock","unlocks","unlocking","unlocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"開啟鎖住的東西","explanation":"指用鑰匙、密碼或其他方式解除鎖閉，使門、櫃子、裝置等能夠被開啟或使用。這是 unlock 最直接、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She unlocked the back door with her spare key.","zh":"她用備用鑰匙開啟了後門的鎖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unlock the cabinet before trying to lift the lid.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unlock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-031b4fb1e14dd010","term":"unlock","forms":["unlock","unlocks","unlocking","unlocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭示隱藏資訊或潛力","explanation":"指某個線索、發現或方法讓原本不明白的知識、謎團或潛在能力顯現出來。它保留了“開啟封閉之物”的核心畫面，只是被開啟的是抽象內容。","examples":[{"en":"The new evidence could unlock the mystery.","zh":"新的證據可能會揭開這個謎團。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular practice can unlock your musical potential.","zh":"經常練習能夠釋放你的音樂潛力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unlock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-077ef234b1df0008","term":"unlock","forms":["unlock","unlocks","unlocking","unlocked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使某物可用或開放","explanation":"指把原本無法使用、無法進入或受到限制的資源、計劃和機會開放出來。它是“開啟鎖”在抽象領域中的直接延伸。","examples":[{"en":"The partnership could unlock new opportunities for small businesses.","zh":"這項合作可能為小企業開放新的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Completing the tutorial unlocks the next chapter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unlock","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bae420d916bc899043e","word":"unprecedented","forms":["unprecedented"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61a1b0556f7d40dc","term":"unprecedented","forms":["unprecedented"],"pos":"adj","zh":"前所未有的","explanation":"指以前從未出現、發生或被經歷過的事，就像過去根本沒有一條可供參考的舊路，因此沒有先例可循。","examples":[{"en":"The city faced an unprecedented rise in housing costs.","zh":"這座城市面臨著前所未有的住房成本上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The team achieved unprecedented success this season.","zh":"這支球隊本賽季取得了前所未有的成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unprecedented","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2e3200de84b9cada8390","word":"until","forms":["until"],"officialPos":"conj./prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dc3d22fb218a42b5","term":"until","forms":["until"],"pos":"prep","zh":"直到……為止","explanation":"表示某個動作或狀態一直持續，到所說的時間或事件發生時才結束。它把時間看成一條路，until 後面的內容就是終點。","examples":[{"en":"If you can wait until after my meeting with her, we'll talk then.","zh":"如果你能等到我和她開完會，我們到時候再談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Stay here until the storm passes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/until","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-02ddbea2b67e54f6226a","word":"unveil","forms":["unveil"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6205de81641ecdc3","term":"unveil","forms":["unveil","unveils","unveiling","unveiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揭開；揭示隱藏之物","explanation":"把面紗、覆蓋物或其他遮擋物揭開，使原本看不見的東西顯露出來；也可引申為揭示隱藏的資訊或真相。","examples":[{"en":"The artist unveiled the finished painting at the gallery.","zh":"藝術家在畫廊揭開了完成作品的面紗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report unveiled serious problems in the system.","zh":"這份報告揭示了該系統中的嚴重問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unveil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c6e7c17b110dd92","term":"unveil","forms":["unveil","unveils","unveiling","unveiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"首次正式公開展示","explanation":"在公眾面前第一次正式展示新產品、計劃、設計或其他成果，就像在儀式上揭開它的面紗。","examples":[{"en":"The company will unveil its new electric car at the show.","zh":"這家公司將在展會上首次公開展示新款電動汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mayor unveiled a plan to improve public transport.","zh":"市長首次公佈了一項改善公共交通的計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/unveil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-75a288c0d6898c5f7b05","word":"up","forms":["up"],"officialPos":"adv./prep./adj./v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba89d337db73ded2","term":"up","forms":["up"],"pos":"adj","zh":"醒著且已起床","explanation":"表示人已經醒著，並且通常已經離開床鋪；這是“向上”從身體位置延伸到清醒狀態的常用含義。","examples":[{"en":"Are you still up, or have you gone to bed?","zh":"你還醒著嗎，還是已經睡了？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I was up early to catch the first train.","zh":"我很早就起床去趕第一班火車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/up","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f750da0a50596bb6","term":"up","forms":["up"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向上；在高處","explanation":"沿著“向上”這條主線，表示朝較高的位置移動，或位於較高的位置。","examples":[{"en":"I looked up and saw a plane overhead.","zh":"我抬頭一看，看到頭頂上方有一架飛機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The balloon drifted up toward the clouds.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/up","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e999c5cb7df637ac","term":"up","forms":["up"],"pos":"prep","zh":"向上方","explanation":"表示朝著較高的位置或物體頂部移動，正是“向上”這條主線的直接用法。","examples":[{"en":"The cat climbed up the tree.","zh":"那隻貓爬上了樹。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We walked up the hill before sunrise.","zh":"日出前我們走上了山坡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/up","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54cf4b1e4c6e7d33","term":"up","forms":["up","ups","upping","upped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"舉起；提升","explanation":"表示把物體實際舉高、抬起，或在固定短語中使某物離開原來的位置，體現“動作向上”。","examples":[{"en":"The crew upped anchor before dawn.","zh":"船員們在黎明前起錨了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He upped the flag from the ground and carried it inside.","zh":"他把旗子從地上撿起，帶進了屋裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/up","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2937013f2181810606b2","word":"update","forms":["update"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3569d53dbc9ce6dd","term":"update","forms":["update","updates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"最新訊息；進展通報","explanation":"指把目前已知情況補充到最新狀態的訊息，通常告訴別人事情最近有什麼進展。","examples":[{"en":"She gave us an update on the project after the meeting.","zh":"會議後，她向我們通報了專案的最新進展。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I'll send you an update when I hear more.","zh":"有更多訊息後我會把最新情況發給你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/update","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c61b750345a83165","term":"update","forms":["update","updates"],"pos":"noun","zh":"軟體或系統更新","explanation":"指把軟體、資料庫或其他系統改成較新的狀態；通常是小範圍的版本更新，不一定是全面升級。","examples":[{"en":"The app will install an update overnight.","zh":"這個應用會在夜間安裝更新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A security update is available for your phone.","zh":"你的手機有可用的安全更新。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/update","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-38c96576a4bcd743","term":"update","forms":["update","updates","updating","updated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"更新；使資料變新","explanation":"指把記錄、檔案、資料或系統改到包含最新資訊的狀態，也就是把舊內容換成現在有效的內容。","examples":[{"en":"Please update the customer records before Friday.","zh":"請在週五前更新客戶記錄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need to update the schedule with the new times.","zh":"我們需要把新的時間補充到日程表裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/update","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e1d452783be0344","term":"update","forms":["update","updates","updating","updated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"向某人通報最新進展","explanation":"指讓某人知道事情最近發生了什麼，把對方的瞭解補充到最新狀態。","examples":[{"en":"Can you update me on what happened while I was away?","zh":"我不在的時候發生了什麼，你能告訴我最新情況嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager updated the team about the change in plans.","zh":"經理向團隊通報了計劃變更的情況。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/update","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7fef9479c8bc5a3c8689","word":"upgrade","forms":["upgrade"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8bb8d4d92e66769d","term":"upgrade","forms":["upgrade","upgrades"],"pos":"noun","zh":"升級件；更好的替代品","explanation":"指把原來的裝置、軟體或部件換成更高一級、更好的版本，像沿坡道向上換到更高的位置。","examples":[{"en":"The new graphics card is a worthwhile upgrade for this computer.","zh":"這塊新顯示卡是這臺電腦很值得的一次升級。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We paid for an upgrade to a larger room.","zh":"我們付費把房間升級成了更大的房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upgrade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad21496bd5433560","term":"upgrade","forms":["upgrade","upgrades","upgrading","upgraded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"升級；改進","explanation":"指透過更換或改進，使裝置、系統、生活條件等達到更高水平；核心畫面就是向上走一個臺階。","examples":[{"en":"We need to upgrade the office computers before the new project starts.","zh":"新專案開始前，我們需要升級辦公室的電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel upgraded its rooms with faster internet and better lighting.","zh":"這家酒店升級了客房，配備了更快的網路和更好的照明。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upgrade","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ff4085ad157354dc8ea6","word":"upload","forms":["upload"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-96dc5b3259efe8f0","term":"upload","forms":["upload","uploads","uploading","uploaded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"上傳資料","explanation":"指把檔案、照片、影片等資料從自己的電腦或其他裝置傳到網路伺服器或網上。","examples":[{"en":"Please upload the completed form to the website before Friday.","zh":"請在星期五之前把填好的表格上傳到網站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I’m uploading the photos to our shared folder now.","zh":"我現在正把照片上傳到我們的共享資料夾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upload","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-261b09ff8d11731caa71","word":"upon","forms":["upon"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d4813e9f63ce783d","term":"upon","forms":["upon"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……上；加在……身上","explanation":"表示某物處在另一個表面或地點上，也可表示責任、影響、希望等落到某人或某事物身上。它把“放到某個支點上”的畫面說得比 on 更正式；在表示時間或事件時，還可引申為某事一發生，另一件事就隨即發生。","examples":[{"en":"A layer of dust lay upon the old books.","zh":"一層灰塵落在那些舊書上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The responsibility for the decision rests upon the director.","zh":"作出這個決定的責任落在主管身上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aee610558292023758a4","word":"upper","forms":["upper"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b1442b180047880","term":"upper","forms":["upper","uppermore","uppermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"等級或位置更高的","explanation":"表示在等級、地位、組織層級或空間位置上比另一個物件更高，核心就是“向上一級”。","examples":[{"en":"She moved to an upper position in the company.","zh":"她在公司裡升到了更高的職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The upper floors are reserved for offices.","zh":"較高樓層留作辦公室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6d9ba45963232b7e73c","word":"upright","forms":["upright"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf6a8b57c62b3b17","term":"upright","forms":["upright","more upright","most upright"],"pos":"adj","zh":"直立的；豎直的","explanation":"指物體或身體保持向上、筆直的狀態，而不是躺倒或彎曲；“向上站立”的畫面就是這個義項。","examples":[{"en":"The cat sat upright on the windowsill.","zh":"貓直立地坐在窗臺上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the bottle upright.","zh":"請讓瓶子保持直立。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce7c538ccb0a6d89","term":"upright","forms":["upright","more upright","most upright"],"pos":"adv","zh":"直立地","explanation":"表示“以站直、豎直的姿勢”，是把“向上站立”的畫面用作動作方式。","examples":[{"en":"He stood upright despite the strong wind.","zh":"儘管風很大，他仍然站得筆直。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep the bottle upright during transport.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upright","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0905c933e1344e47f320","word":"uprising","forms":["uprising"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2d1d35ad2ae98b31","term":"uprising","forms":["uprising","uprisings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"起義；民眾暴動","explanation":"指許多民眾一起“站起來”反抗政府、統治者或政府政策的行動，通常包含推翻或迫使當局改變現狀的意圖。","examples":[{"en":"The uprising against the military government lasted for several weeks.","zh":"反對軍政府的起義持續了數週。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The army moved into the city to suppress the uprising.","zh":"軍隊進入這座城市鎮壓起義。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uprising","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b2f406339328a5dd4c6","word":"upset","forms":["upset"],"officialPos":"adj./v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-765f1e18a36ab66d","term":"upset","forms":["upset","more upset","most upset"],"pos":"adj","zh":"難過、惱怒","explanation":"指人的情緒像被打亂一樣，感到難過、煩惱、生氣或失望，具體情緒要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"She was upset about missing the last train.","zh":"她因為錯過末班車而很難過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Don't be upset with him; he was only trying to help.","zh":"別生他的氣，他只是想幫忙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9993882c2737f09d","term":"upset","forms":["upset","more upset","most upset"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體不適","explanation":"指身體狀態被攪亂，尤其是胃部不舒服、噁心，或感覺快要嘔吐。","examples":[{"en":"I have an upset stomach, so I'll skip dinner.","zh":"我胃不舒服，所以不吃晚飯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boat ride made her feel upset.","zh":"坐船讓她感到噁心不適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d535663d5482444e","term":"upset","forms":["upset","upsets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擾亂、混亂","explanation":"指原本正常的安排、秩序或情緒被打亂而造成的混亂或困擾，是“upset”作為“打亂狀態”的名詞化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden cancellation caused a lot of upset among the passengers.","zh":"突然取消航班讓乘客們感到很困擾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The roadworks upset our usual delivery schedule.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2046f6353523772","term":"upset","forms":["upset","upsets","upsetting"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使難過或生氣","explanation":"指某件事把人的情緒打亂，使其難過、煩惱、生氣或失望。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't mean to upset you with that comment.","zh":"我不是故意要讓你因為那句話難過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unfair decision upset the whole team.","zh":"這個不公平的決定讓整個團隊都很難過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0be5b19d6ef8241f","term":"upset","forms":["upset","upsets","upsetting"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擾亂、破壞平衡","explanation":"指使計劃、秩序、系統或平衡脫離原來的狀態，造成混亂或不良變化。","examples":[{"en":"The extra expense upset our carefully planned budget.","zh":"這筆額外開支打亂了我們精心制定的預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small error can upset the entire process.","zh":"一個小錯誤就可能擾亂整個流程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2875af53a238f645","term":"upset","forms":["upset","upsets","upsetting"],"pos":"verb","zh":"爆冷擊敗","explanation":"指實力或聲望較弱的一方出人意料地擊敗熱門對手，結果像把原有的勝負預期掀翻。","examples":[{"en":"The underdog upset the tournament favorite in the final.","zh":"這支不被看好的隊伍在決賽中爆冷擊敗了奪冠熱門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The unseeded player upset the defending champion.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upset","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab5db4901670272a1c0d","word":"upstairs","forms":["upstairs"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f3187c8ca174e739","term":"upstairs","forms":["upstairs","further upstairs","farther upstairs","furthest upstairs","farthest upstairs"],"pos":"adj","zh":"樓上的；上層的","explanation":"指位於建築物較高樓層或較高位置的東西，核心畫面就是“在樓梯上方”。","examples":[{"en":"The upstairs bathroom needs a new light.","zh":"樓上的浴室需要換一盞新燈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They turned the upstairs room into a study.","zh":"他們把樓上的房間改成了書房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upstairs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d2c84ff9944ea970","term":"upstairs","forms":["upstairs","further upstairs","farther upstairs","furthest upstairs","farthest upstairs"],"pos":"adv","zh":"上樓；在樓上","explanation":"表示向較高樓層移動，或已經處在樓上；可以把它想成沿樓梯向“上面”走。","examples":[{"en":"I left my phone upstairs, so I have to go back for it.","zh":"我把手機落在樓上了，所以得回去拿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children are upstairs getting ready for bed.","zh":"孩子們在樓上準備睡覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upstairs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6e793afc12a445b","term":"upstairs","forms":["upstairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樓上；上層","explanation":"指房屋的上層或樓上的空間，是“在上面”這一核心畫面的名詞化用法。","examples":[{"en":"The upstairs of the house has three small bedrooms.","zh":"這棟房子的樓上有三個小臥室。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The upstairs contains three bedrooms and a bathroom.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upstairs","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-69b565816811be91c81d","word":"upward","forms":["upward"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c941cab0a623979","term":"upward","forms":["upward","more upward","most upward"],"pos":"adj","zh":"向上的","explanation":"表示方向朝向更高的位置，核心畫面就是從低處指向高處。","examples":[{"en":"She gave him an upward glance.","zh":"她向上瞥了他一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chart shows a steady upward trend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca920884325dd2edc3fa","word":"upward/upwards","forms":["upward","upwards"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c7427a30d0b445b","term":"upward","forms":["upward"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向上","explanation":"表示從較低處向較高處移動，也可以表示沿著通向源頭或起點的方向移動。","examples":[{"en":"The hikers climbed upward through the forest.","zh":"徒步者們穿過森林向上攀登。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Smoke drifted upward from the fire.","zh":"煙從火堆上方向上飄去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-932ca54cd31c35c2","term":"upwards","forms":["upwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向上；朝天空方向","explanation":"表示人或物從較低處向較高處移動，最直觀的畫面就是氣球、煙霧或人朝天空方向上升。","examples":[{"en":"The balloon drifted upwards into the sky.","zh":"氣球向上飄進了天空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She looked upwards and saw a bird above the trees.","zh":"她抬頭向上看，看到樹上方有一隻鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0960fcfdde2a16c2","term":"upwards","forms":["upwards"],"pos":"adv","zh":"數值上升；數量增加","explanation":"把數字或數量想成沿著刻度向上走，表示價格、費用、溫度等逐漸變高。這裡沒有真實的空間移動，而是“數值往上”。","examples":[{"en":"Food prices have been steadily moving upwards this year.","zh":"今年食品價格一直在穩步上漲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"House prices have moved steadily upwards.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upwards","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5909c3cc473fb34a1af","word":"urban","forms":["urban"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8df57d26916c57d","term":"urban","forms":["urban","more urban","most urban"],"pos":"adj","zh":"城市的；都市的","explanation":"表示屬於城市、發生在城市，或具有城市生活特點的事物，是 urban 最常見、最重要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Urban life can be exciting, but it is often expensive.","zh":"都市生活可能令人興奮，但往往消費很高。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The project aims to improve urban transport.","zh":"這個專案旨在改善城市交通。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urban","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-660db2169a28859c","term":"urban","forms":["urban","more urban","most urban"],"pos":"adj","zh":"居住在城市的","explanation":"強調某人或某群體生活在城市或城鎮中，是“城市居民的”這一層意思。","examples":[{"en":"Urban families often have less outdoor space than rural families.","zh":"城市家庭通常比農村家庭擁有更少的戶外空間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Urban residents often have better access to public transport.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urban","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7ecefc770b921cd7090","word":"urge","forms":["urge"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4886b512342a38bd","term":"urge","forms":["urge","urges"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈衝動","explanation":"指心裡突然出現的強烈願望，促使人想做某件事；重點是“忍不住想做”的感覺，而不一定真的採取行動。","examples":[{"en":"I had a sudden urge to call my old friend.","zh":"我突然很想給那位老朋友打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She resisted the urge to check her phone during the meeting.","zh":"她忍住了開會時檢視手機的衝動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94e06e180e861b5a","term":"urge","forms":["urge","urges","urging","urged","urgest","urgedst","urgeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"力勸；催促","explanation":"指反覆或強烈地勸某人做某事，試圖把對方推向一個決定或行動；這是動詞urge最重要的日常用法。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor urged him to get more exercise.","zh":"醫生敦促他多鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They urged us not to cancel the trip.","zh":"他們力勸我們不要取消這次旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b68aadd9eb8f334acbd4","word":"urgency","forms":["urgency"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0a71ee99ddc4b8f8","term":"urgency","forms":["urgency","urgencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"緊迫性；迫切性","explanation":"指某件事不能拖延、需要儘快處理的程度。它強調“現在就要重視和行動”的壓力，而不一定表示事情本身危險。","examples":[{"en":"The urgency of the problem became clear after the meeting.","zh":"會議結束後，這個問題的緊迫性變得十分明顯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke with urgency and asked everyone to act immediately.","zh":"她語氣迫切，請大家立即採取行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urgency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f0d85817cf77602","term":"urgency","forms":["urgency","urgencies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"強烈催促；迫切衝動","explanation":"指一種強烈得難以忽視的催促感或衝動，彷彿有什麼力量在推動你馬上做某事。它可以來自外界的壓力，也可以來自自己的突然需要。","examples":[{"en":"I felt a sudden urgency to call my parents.","zh":"我突然強烈地想給父母打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He felt an urgency to speak before she left.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urgency","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9d37c23fcc0f03c15a8","word":"urgent","forms":["urgent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a31b558369a95ba","term":"urgent","forms":["urgent","more urgent","most urgent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"迫切的；緊急的","explanation":"指某件事不能再拖，必須儘快得到關注、回應或處理。事情越像被時間壓緊，就越 urgent。","examples":[{"en":"The hospital sent an urgent appeal for blood donors.","zh":"醫院緊急呼籲獻血者前來獻血。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This problem is urgent and cannot wait until tomorrow.","zh":"這個問題很緊急，不能等到明天再處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urgent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0a4e4c29432ecb01b95f","word":"usage","forms":["usage"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7600be67cd6e2697","term":"usage","forms":["usage","usages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種慣例或習慣做法","explanation":"指某個地方、群體或場合反覆採用的一種做法，重點是“大家通常這樣做”，而不是某一次具體行動。這正是“東西被怎樣用”長期固定後形成的慣例。","examples":[{"en":"This usage is common in the northern part of the country.","zh":"這種慣例在這個國家北部很常見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Local usage allows visitors to enter the hall without shoes.","zh":"當地習俗允許訪客不穿鞋進入大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-19558286ad615822","term":"usage","forms":["usage","usages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使用情況；使用量","explanation":"指某種產品、設施或服務實際被使用的情況，常可進一步統計為次數、人數或總量。這裡仍然是“東西被怎樣用”的畫面，只是關注點從習慣方式轉向實際規模。","examples":[{"en":"Water usage fell sharply during the dry summer.","zh":"乾旱的夏季用水量大幅下降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The app tracks your monthly electricity usage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a3b142af6e97cfc3bb23","word":"use","forms":["use"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e46de30fd6acb945","term":"use","forms":["use","uses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使用這一行為","explanation":"指使用某人或某物這一行為本身，既可以談一般的使用，也可以談某一次或某一類使用。","examples":[{"en":"The use of cameras has changed the way people work.","zh":"攝像機的使用改變了人們的工作方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Unauthorized use of the equipment is prohibited.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/use","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af6af9feccb5bbe2","term":"use","forms":["use","uses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用處；價值","explanation":"指某人或某物能帶來的幫助或實際價值，也就是“有沒有用”。","examples":[{"en":"What's the use of a key if the lock is broken?","zh":"鎖壞了，鑰匙還有什麼用？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That broken machine is of little use now.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/use","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6e530d375fb99f71","term":"use","forms":["use","uses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"用途；功能","explanation":"指某物可以被用來做什麼，也可以指它具有的不同功能或用途。","examples":[{"en":"This small room has several uses.","zh":"這個小房間有好幾個用途。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One use of this small blade is opening sealed envelopes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/use","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cbc5ae883ae8652","term":"use","forms":["use","uses","using","used","usest","usedst","useth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使用；利用","explanation":"把某物拿來完成任務、達到目的或解決問題，就是use最基本的動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"Use this knife to slice the bread.","zh":"用這把刀切面包。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We use this app to track our expenses.","zh":"我們用這個應用記錄開支。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/use","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ff641d75ea095ad3","term":"use","forms":["use","uses","using","used","usest","usedst","useth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"過去常常","explanation":"在used to do something中，表示過去經常做某事或過去處於某種狀態，現在通常已不再如此。","examples":[{"en":"I used to walk to school every day.","zh":"我過去每天走路上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We used to swim in the river every summer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/use","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f839161355091fcd9e33","word":"used","forms":["used"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-901e5b0446feef47","term":"used","forms":["used","more used","most used"],"pos":"adj","zh":"用過的；已使用的","explanation":"指物品已經被人使用過，重點是它有使用經歷，而不一定表示已經損壞或不能再用。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the used towels in this basket.","zh":"請把用過的毛巾放進這個籃子裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The clinic safely disposed of the used needles.","zh":"診所安全地處理了用過的針頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/used","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a62ed7b95a2fe9e8759c","word":"useful","forms":["useful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32f33ed43f5b74e9","term":"useful","forms":["useful","more useful","usefuller","most useful","usefullest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有實際用途的；有幫助的","explanation":"指某物或某種方法在實際需要中能發揮作用，能幫助人完成事情或解決問題。它強調實際價值，而不一定表示外表好看、令人喜歡或作用非常重大。","examples":[{"en":"This app is useful for keeping track of your expenses.","zh":"這個應用程式對記錄日常開支很有用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her advice was useful when I started the new job.","zh":"我開始新工作時，她的建議很有幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/useful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-04f8996da763b7a969b1","word":"user","forms":["user"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c6f6ccb98c90eccd","term":"user","forms":["user","users"],"pos":"noun","zh":"使用者；使用者","explanation":"指使用、操作或享用某種東西的人，可以是商品或服務的消費者，也可以是獲准使用某物的人；在某些語境中甚至包括未經許可使用的人。","examples":[{"en":"The app has more than a million users.","zh":"這款應用的使用者超過一百萬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Heavy users of electricity should consider reducing their consumption.","zh":"用電量大的使用者應考慮減少用電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/user","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66d08080924d56d1","term":"user","forms":["user","users"],"pos":"noun","zh":"吸毒者","explanation":"指經常使用毒品，尤其是非法毒品的人；這裡的“使用”不是普通的使用物品，而是固定搭配中對毒品的反覆使用。","examples":[{"en":"The program offers support to drug users who want to stop.","zh":"這項計劃為想戒毒的吸毒者提供支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The outreach team provides counseling for drug users.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/user","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f7bb6eff92853145d359","word":"usher","forms":["usher"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4a688d7cf269d44a","term":"usher","forms":["usher","ushers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"引座員","explanation":"指在教堂、影院、劇院等場所接待觀眾並把他們帶到座位上的人。這個義項正是“站在門口把人領進去”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"An usher showed us to our seats before the concert began.","zh":"音樂會開始前，一名引座員把我們帶到了座位上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The church ushers welcomed the guests at the door.","zh":"教堂的引座員在門口迎接客人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6d1701b4166744e6","term":"usher","forms":["usher","ushers","ushering","ushered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"引人入座","explanation":"指把人帶到座位上，通常用於教堂、影院、劇院或其他有座位安排的場合。這是名詞“引座員”轉成的最直接動詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The attendant ushered the family to their seats.","zh":"工作人員把這一家人帶到了座位上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Guests were ushered into the hall in small groups.","zh":"客人們被分批帶進大廳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32280b6171bb74cd","term":"usher","forms":["usher","ushers","ushering","ushered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"為……揭幕","explanation":"指某件事在時間上先出現，為後來發生的重大變化、新時期或新局面開路。這個義項把“把人領進門”擴充套件成“把一個新時代領進來”。","examples":[{"en":"The invention ushered in a new era of communication.","zh":"這項發明開創了通訊的新紀元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The election ushered in major changes to the country's policies.","zh":"這場選舉為該國政策的重大變化拉開了序幕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-905301bf736f9b791431","word":"usual","forms":["usual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d50ed8d2429c986","term":"usual","forms":["usual","more usual","most usual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"通常的；常見的","explanation":"指某種情況經常出現，或者符合人們平時的習慣和一般模式；它強調“平常如此”，不一定表示正確或理想。","examples":[{"en":"It is usual for children to feel nervous on their first day at school.","zh":"孩子們上學第一天感到緊張是很常見的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The usual remedy is rest and plenty of fluids.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ceb1e2514a1f1b453097","word":"usually","forms":["usually"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6d07b10c0b8a9d8","term":"usually","forms":["usually","more usually","most usually"],"pos":"adv","zh":"通常；大多數時候","explanation":"表示一件事大多數時候會發生，但偶爾可能不發生，因此比“總是”弱一些。它把注意力放在一個反覆出現的習慣或常見結果上。","examples":[{"en":"I usually have tea after dinner.","zh":"我通常在晚飯後喝茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She usually takes the bus to school.","zh":"她通常乘公共汽車去上學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usually","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da8c1e99696cb2c2","term":"usually","forms":["usually","more usually","most usually"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在正常情況下","explanation":"表示按照平常的條件和規律，某事應當如此；這裡不一定是在統計發生次數，而是在說明沒有特殊情況時的正常結果。","examples":[{"en":"The shop is usually quiet in the morning.","zh":"這家商店早上通常很安靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The library usually opens at nine.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/usually","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b8268df1da5dc411ecdc","word":"utensil","forms":["utensil"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"utensil","forms":["utensil"],"pos":"n.","zh":"用具；器具","examples":[{"en":"A wooden spoon is a useful kitchen utensil.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"Wash each utensil carefully after preparing raw meat.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-57ffcc28d4b999760e3c","word":"utility","forms":["utility"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9cf2f26138b2eb86","term":"utility","forms":["utility","utilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有用性；效用","explanation":"指某件事或某種做法能夠派上用場、滿足實際需要的程度，也就是它的實用價值。","examples":[{"en":"The utility of this feature becomes clear when you work offline.","zh":"離線工作時，這項功能的實用價值就很明顯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We questioned the utility of building another parking garage.","zh":"我們對再建一座停車庫是否有用提出了疑問。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/utility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c27a37f99c442ac","term":"utility","forms":["utility","utilities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"公共事業服務","explanation":"指透過固定基礎設施持續提供的水、電、燃氣、汙水處理等服務，也可指這些服務本身。","examples":[{"en":"The rent includes water, but electricity is a separate utility.","zh":"房租包括水費，但電費是另外的公共事業服務費用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The storm damaged several utilities in the area.","zh":"暴風雨損壞了該地區的幾項公共事業設施。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/utility","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7bfc303b6d927d2830ea","word":"utilize","forms":["utilize"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"utilize","forms":["utilize"],"pos":"v.","zh":"利用；運用","examples":[{"en":"The school can utilize the empty room as a reading area.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We should utilize local materials whenever possible.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae19f6375b5500141978","word":"utter","forms":["utter"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fd4fe613a13c1a94","term":"utter","forms":["utter","uttermore","utmost","uttermost"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完全的；極端的","explanation":"表示某種狀態達到最徹底、最極端的程度，帶有“沒有任何保留或例外”的感覺。這是形容詞最值得優先掌握的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The plan ended in utter failure.","zh":"這個計劃以徹底失敗告終。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was filled with utter relief when the test was over.","zh":"考試結束時，她感到如釋重負。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/utter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48a11b18f8c46229","term":"utter","forms":["utter","utters","uttering","uttered","utterest","utteredst","uttereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"說出；講出","explanation":"表示把詞語、聲音或一句話從口中說出來，也就是把內容“推到外面”。常用於強調某人是否真的說出了某句話。","examples":[{"en":"He refused to utter a single word.","zh":"他拒絕說出一個字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please do not utter her name again.","zh":"請不要再提她的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/utter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51f362abd94840346d18","word":"vacancy","forms":["vacancy"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-077322d010ae577f","term":"vacancy","forms":["vacancy","vacancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"職位空缺","explanation":"指某個職位目前沒有人擔任，因而等待招聘或任命；它就是“空出來的職位格子”。","examples":[{"en":"The company has a vacancy for an experienced designer.","zh":"這家公司有一個經驗豐富的設計師職位空缺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She applied for the vacancy last week.","zh":"她上週申請了這個空缺職位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7098c2b2f5ad2409","term":"vacancy","forms":["vacancy","vacancies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酒店空房","explanation":"指旅館、酒店或民宿中尚未被客人訂住或入住的房間，也就是“空著的房間格子”。","examples":[{"en":"Do you have any vacancies for tonight?","zh":"你們今晚還有空房嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The hotel was full, so we looked for vacancies nearby.","zh":"這家酒店住滿了，所以我們去附近找空房。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacancy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c23c3188b938e5979ba","word":"vacant","forms":["vacant"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e729e6b7d2f2aa7c","term":"vacant","forms":["vacant","more vacant","most vacant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空著的；未佔用的","explanation":"指房間、座位、職位等目前沒有人或東西佔用，像一個空出來的位置。","examples":[{"en":"Is the room next to the kitchen vacant?","zh":"廚房旁邊的房間空著嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found a vacant seat near the window.","zh":"她在窗邊找到了一個空座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1aa9fd77f3142856","term":"vacant","forms":["vacant","more vacant","most vacant"],"pos":"adj","zh":"空白的","explanation":"指頁面、表格等上面還沒有寫入或印上內容，留下大片空白。","examples":[{"en":"He stared at the vacant page, unable to begin.","zh":"他盯著空白的頁面，不知如何下筆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Leave the vacant spaces for the examiner's comments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1b24e0c17e952e4c7cae","word":"vacation","forms":["vacation"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa90bb795ada21ea","term":"vacation","forms":["vacation","vacations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"休閒度假時間","explanation":"指離開工作或職責、專門用來休息和娛樂的一段時間；這是 vacation 最典型的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"We are taking a vacation by the sea next month.","zh":"我們下個月要去海邊度假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She needs a quiet vacation after a busy year.","zh":"忙了一年後，她需要一個安靜的假期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c2c364a9fe37df7b","term":"vacation","forms":["vacation","vacations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"離開工作或學校的較長假期","explanation":"指連續一段時間不上班或不上學，通常用於休息、娛樂或旅行；它比一般的短暫空閒更像完整的假期安排。","examples":[{"en":"The children are on vacation this week.","zh":"孩子們這周在放假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They took a month's vacation after finishing the project.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b09c40ca3c7c06a7","term":"vacation","forms":["vacation","vacations","vacationing","vacationed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"去度假","explanation":"指暫時離開工作或日常職責去休息、娛樂或旅行，是名詞“假期”所對應的動作。","examples":[{"en":"They are vacationing in Mexico this summer.","zh":"他們今年夏天要去墨西哥度假。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They vacation in the mountains every summer.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bcc3aa029a10fa3e5ede","word":"vaccine","forms":["vaccine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0504784feb5a36a3","term":"vaccine","forms":["vaccine","vaccines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"疫苗；一劑疫苗","explanation":"指送入人體或動物體內、讓免疫系統提前認識某種病原體，從而幫助預防疾病的物質，也可指使用的一劑。它像一面先讓身體演練過的安全護盾，並不以讓人患上該病為目的。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor recommended a vaccine against seasonal flu.","zh":"醫生建議接種一種預防季節性流感的疫苗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She received her second vaccine at the clinic.","zh":"她在診所接種了第二劑疫苗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vaccine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-657fdc2b228b14a6aba7","word":"vacuum","forms":["vacuum"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9b26414ef7192ccf","term":"vacuum","forms":["vacuum","vacuums","vacua"],"pos":"noun","zh":"真空空間","explanation":"指幾乎沒有任何物質、尤其沒有空氣的空間；重點是“裡面被抽空了”，而不是普通的空房間。","examples":[{"en":"Sound cannot travel through a vacuum.","zh":"聲音無法在真空中傳播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The equipment must be sealed in a vacuum.","zh":"這臺裝置必須密封在真空中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacuum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f73e5067fefdc8d7","term":"vacuum","forms":["vacuum","vacuums","vacua"],"pos":"noun","zh":"情感或生活空缺","explanation":"比喻親近的人或原本重要的工作、目標離開後，生活中留下的巨大空缺；這裡的“空”是情感和作用上的空。","examples":[{"en":"Her retirement left a vacuum in the organization.","zh":"她退休後，組織裡留下了一個空缺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her departure left a vacuum in his daily life.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacuum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c817639c6b7ceae","term":"vacuum","forms":["vacuum","vacuums","vacuuming","vacuumed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用吸塵器清理","explanation":"用吸塵器把某個表面或地方的灰塵吸乾淨，重點是清理的物件。","examples":[{"en":"I vacuum the carpet every Saturday.","zh":"我每週六都用吸塵器清理地毯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please vacuum the stairs before the guests arrive.","zh":"客人到之前請把樓梯吸乾淨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacuum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-71cac08484da8e73dac0","word":"vague","forms":["vague"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-424cc1766a394272","term":"vague","forms":["vague","vaguer","vaguest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"表達不明確","explanation":"指說出來或寫出來的話沒有給出清楚、具體的內容，讓人難以準確知道所指是什麼。重點不在於內容一定錯，而在於表達沒有把邊界說清楚。","examples":[{"en":"His answer was too vague to be useful.","zh":"他的回答太含糊了，根本派不上用場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The instructions are vague about where to meet.","zh":"說明沒有說清楚在哪裡見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vague","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aff0dc611c176703","term":"vague","forms":["vague","vaguer","vaguest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"含義不確定","explanation":"指一個詞、說法或標籤本身沒有固定而精確的含義，不同人可能會有不同理解。它強調的是詞語或概念的界限模糊，而不只是某次說話沒有解釋完整。","examples":[{"en":"“Soon” is a vague word when you are making plans.","zh":"安排計劃時，“很快”是個含義不明確的詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The law uses a vague definition of public danger.","zh":"這部法律對“公共危險”的定義很模糊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vague","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ccc669352fe82869","term":"vague","forms":["vague","vaguer","vaguest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"模糊的、不清楚的","explanation":"指某個想法、印象或認識只有大概輪廓，尚未形成清楚而具體的理解。它是最寬的一層常用義，可以涵蓋對事情“只知道個大概”的情況。","examples":[{"en":"I have a vague idea of how the machine works.","zh":"我大概知道這臺機器是怎麼工作的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She had only a vague notion of what she wanted.","zh":"她只是模模糊糊地知道自己想要什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vague","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9313dba0f7d6c6e1666d","word":"vain","forms":["vain"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20587f93dc3e530b","term":"vain","forms":["vain","vainer","more vain","vainest","most vain"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自負的；虛榮的","explanation":"形容一個人過分在意自己的外表、魅力或成就，並且對自己評價過高，常常超過了實際理由。這個人就像只看見外表的空殼，特別需要別人注意和讚美。","examples":[{"en":"He is vain about his appearance and checks the mirror before every meeting.","zh":"他很在意自己的外表，每次開會前都要照鏡子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was too vain to admit that she needed help.","zh":"她太自負了，不肯承認自己需要幫助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8413a6db4df0805","term":"vain","forms":["vain","vainer","more vain","vainest","most vain"],"pos":"adj","zh":"徒勞的；無效的","explanation":"形容某個努力、嘗試或行動沒有達到目的，付出了力氣卻沒有結果。它仍然體現“裡面沒有實際成果”的空洞感。","examples":[{"en":"We tried in vain to open the locked door.","zh":"我們徒勞地試圖開啟那扇鎖著的門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"All their efforts to repair the old machine were in vain.","zh":"他們修理那臺舊機器的一切努力都白費了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ec654fac9599f62e79e2","word":"valid","forms":["valid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51459c42b09d498c","term":"valid","forms":["valid","more valid","most valid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有充分根據的","explanation":"指觀點、答案或理由有事實、邏輯或合理依據，能夠經得起質疑，因此值得接受。這裡的“站得住”是記憶核心。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a valid reason for missing the meeting.","zh":"她為沒來開會給出了一個合理的理由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That is a valid answer to the question.","zh":"那是這個問題一個有充分根據的答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d741544d7e22af77","term":"valid","forms":["valid","more valid","most valid"],"pos":"adj","zh":"符合規定的；有效的","explanation":"指某個格式、證件、輸入或做法符合既定規則，因而能被系統或機構接受，就像透過檢查的通行證。","examples":[{"en":"Please enter a valid email address.","zh":"請輸入有效的電子郵件地址。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This ticket is valid for three days.","zh":"這張票三天內有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-627fd3d05a49a1839fad","word":"valley","forms":["valley"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e81a7f381a3ae865","term":"valley","forms":["valley","valleys","vallies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"山谷；谷地","explanation":"valley 是夾在山丘或山脈之間的狹長低地，裡面常有河流流過；它可以很窄，也可以很寬。","examples":[{"en":"A small river winds through the green valley.","zh":"一條小河蜿蜒流過這片綠色的山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The village lies in a quiet valley between two mountains.","zh":"這個村莊坐落在兩座山之間的一處寧靜谷地裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2206d68d78476afd","term":"valley","forms":["valley","valleys","vallies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"流域","explanation":"valley 還可以指一個向同一條河流排水的區域；這裡關注的不是單個低地，而是水流彙集的整個範圍。","examples":[{"en":"The entire valley drains into the same river.","zh":"整個流域的水都匯入同一條河。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Farming throughout the Nile valley depends on the river's water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8b6e13fa6c31087cfb3b","word":"valuable","forms":["valuable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33bcfd19bd021756","term":"valuable","forms":["valuable","more valuable","most valuable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"價值高的；貴重的","explanation":"指能賣得較高價格、經濟價值很大的東西，尤其常用於寶石、藝術品、資料等。核心畫面就是“帶著很高價值的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum protects several valuable gemstones.","zh":"這家博物館保護著幾顆貴重寶石。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She keeps the valuable painting in a locked room.","zh":"她把那幅貴重畫作放在上鎖的房間裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valuable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a10b010507801fe6","term":"valuable","forms":["valuable","more valuable","most valuable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有價值的；值得珍視的","explanation":"把“高價值”從金錢擴充套件到人的作用、資訊或關係：某人很可靠、某建議很有幫助，因而值得重視和珍惜。","examples":[{"en":"Your advice was valuable to me during the project.","zh":"在這個專案中，你的建議對我很有價值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is a valuable member of our team.","zh":"她是我們團隊中很重要的一員。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valuable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cd42404d52ad55ccfa9a","word":"value","forms":["value"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-daba6a2c73072747","term":"value","forms":["value","values"],"pos":"noun","zh":"價值；值得程度","explanation":"指某物本身有多值得擁有、使用或保留，既可以是實際價值，也可以是抽象價值。好的教育、可靠的建議或一件物品都可以有 value。","examples":[{"en":"There is great value in learning a second language.","zh":"學習第二語言很有價值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old map has considerable historical value.","zh":"這張舊地圖具有相當大的歷史價值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/value","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ac90026b8b9fd98","term":"value","forms":["value","values"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要性","explanation":"指某件事在人的判斷中有多重要；它不一定表示這件事值多少錢，而是表示它在生活或決策中的分量。","examples":[{"en":"She places great value on honesty.","zh":"她非常重視誠實。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She understands the value of a good night's sleep.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/value","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98414796cfc350d4","term":"value","forms":["value","values"],"pos":"noun","zh":"價格；等價金額","explanation":"指某物被認為公平對應的金錢、商品或服務數量，也就是市場或估價意義上的值多少。","examples":[{"en":"The painting is valued at nearly two million dollars.","zh":"這幅畫的估價接近兩百萬美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This phone offers excellent value for money.","zh":"這部手機物有所值。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/value","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dfef4884be9789cf","term":"value","forms":["value","values","valuing","valued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"估價；評估價值","explanation":"指判斷或估計某物值多少，尤其是由專業人士對物品、財產或收藏品作出估價。","examples":[{"en":"An expert valued the necklace at $8,000.","zh":"一位專家把這條項鍊估價為八千美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The house was valued before it was put on the market.","zh":"這棟房子在上市出售前接受了估價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/value","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ad451e3ee0ebf778","term":"value","forms":["value","values","valuing","valued"],"pos":"verb","zh":"重視","explanation":"指認為某人、某事很重要，因此給予它應有的關注或尊重；這是“價值”尺子用於人的判斷。","examples":[{"en":"We value your honest feedback.","zh":"我們重視你的誠實反饋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She values the freedom to choose her own working hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/value","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-970b1897af0abab6127d","word":"van","forms":["van"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5914b604944d771","term":"van","forms":["van","vans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廂式貨車；麵包車","explanation":"一種通常有封閉車廂的機動車，用來運送貨物或少量乘客，大小一般介於轎車和卡車之間。這是日常英語中最重要的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"The delivery van stopped outside our building.","zh":"送貨麵包車停在了我們樓外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We rented a van to move the furniture.","zh":"我們租了一輛廂式貨車來搬傢俱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/van","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5296c024e03e439ba3d7","word":"vanilla","forms":["vanilla"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4a88497bbab219b","term":"vanilla","forms":["vanilla","vanillas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香草植物","explanation":"指香草屬的熱帶攀援蘭花，尤其是結出香草豆莢、可用於調味和制香的那一種植物。","examples":[{"en":"Vanilla grows best in warm, humid climates.","zh":"香草最適合在溫暖、潮溼的氣候中生長。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The farmer grows vanilla beneath the shade trees.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanilla","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b4a19159ba37463","term":"vanilla","forms":["vanilla","vanillas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"香草提取物","explanation":"指從香草果實中製出的濃縮液，用來給食物、飲料或香水增加香味。","examples":[{"en":"Add a teaspoon of vanilla to the cake batter.","zh":"在蛋糕麵糊中加入一茶匙香草提取物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This ice cream is made with real vanilla.","zh":"這款冰激凌用的是真正的香草提取物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanilla","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-93ce248b8b9c8758eb55","word":"vanish","forms":["vanish"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aa0220f63164e847","term":"vanish","forms":["vanish","vanishes","vanishing","vanished"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消失；從視線中不見","explanation":"某人或某物 vanish，就是從視線中不見了，可能是移動到看不見的地方，也可能是不知不覺地離開。這個詞常帶有突然、神秘或沒有留下明顯線索的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The cat vanished under the sofa before I could catch it.","zh":"我還沒來得及抓住那隻貓，它就鑽到沙發下面不見了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My keys seem to have vanished from the kitchen table.","zh":"我的鑰匙好像從廚房桌上憑空不見了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae7fdaec0fbd9ce240f7","word":"vanity","forms":["vanity"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da259744cc4e6c1d","term":"vanity","forms":["vanity","vanities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"徒勞；空虛；無價值","explanation":"指某件事看似有意義，實際上沒有用處、沒有價值，或最終會歸於空無。這是從“空、虛、抓不住”的核心形象發展出來的抽象義。","examples":[{"en":"He finally saw the vanity of chasing wealth at any cost.","zh":"他終於看清了不惜一切代價追逐財富的徒勞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is vanity to argue about a result that cannot be changed.","zh":"為無法改變的結果爭論是徒勞的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91382571488c6d9e","term":"vanity","forms":["vanity","vanities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"虛榮；自負","explanation":"指過分欣賞或在意自己的外貌、能力、成就或財物，因而把自我形象看得太重要。它仍然帶有“只看表面、內容空虛”的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"Her vanity made her check her reflection before every meeting.","zh":"她的虛榮心使她每次開會前都要照一照鏡子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The advertisement appealed to his vanity by praising his style.","zh":"這則廣告誇讚他的風格，迎合了他的虛榮心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanity","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fb7ae694ba3fd90ae390","word":"vapor","forms":["vapor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-de6112280ad2d7d4","term":"vapor","forms":["vapor","vapors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"霧氣；蒸氣；煙霧","explanation":"指懸浮在空氣中的一團或一層朦朧氣體，例如霧、蒸汽或煙霧；重點是它飄散在空氣中，邊界通常不清楚。","examples":[{"en":"A cloud of vapor rose from the hot spring.","zh":"溫泉上方升起一團霧氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The windows were covered with vapor after the shower.","zh":"洗完澡後，窗戶上蒙了一層水汽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vapor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ee877d462504726","term":"vapor","forms":["vapor","vapors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"虛幻之物；空想；空話","explanation":"把現實中短暫、抓不住的氣霧比作不可靠的想法、空談或虛張聲勢，表示某事不實在、很快就會消失。","examples":[{"en":"His promises turned out to be nothing but vapor.","zh":"他的承諾最後證明不過是空話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dream vanished like vapor in the morning sun.","zh":"那個夢想像晨光中的霧氣一樣消散了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vapor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3b325109deb02ebf8150","word":"variable","forms":["variable"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c0429bb6e976ac97","term":"variable","forms":["variable","more variable","most variable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可變的；變化不定的","explanation":"指某個事物能夠改變，或者它的狀態、數量、強度不總是一樣。這個意義覆蓋天氣、風、季節、數量和裝置引數等常見情況。","examples":[{"en":"The region has variable weather throughout the year.","zh":"這個地區全年天氣多變。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brightness is variable and can be adjusted.","zh":"亮度是可調的，可以進行調整。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4273234432cc720f","term":"variable","forms":["variable","more variable","most variable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"易變的；不穩定的","explanation":"強調某人或某事很可能改變，尤其是態度、感情、承諾或結果不夠穩定。它是在“會變”的基礎上加入了不可預測的意味。","examples":[{"en":"Her variable mood made the meeting difficult to predict.","zh":"她情緒多變，讓會議很難預料。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Variable weather makes outdoor rehearsals difficult to schedule.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e9a32fc4300b83f","term":"variable","forms":["variable","variables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變數因素","explanation":"指一個可能影響結果、其具體情況需要觀察或判斷的因素。比如研究、計劃或決策中，天氣、價格和時間都可能是 variables。","examples":[{"en":"We need to consider several variables before making a decision.","zh":"作出決定前，我們需要考慮幾個可變因素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Rainfall is a crucial variable in predicting crop yields.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-819b60bb250f24cb8222","word":"variation","forms":["variation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5d95186e7d6ba3f0","term":"variation","forms":["variation","variations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變化；變動","explanation":"指事物的形式、位置、狀態或性質發生部分改變，也就是同一個基本事物出現了不同程度或不同樣子的變化。","examples":[{"en":"There is considerable variation in the quality of the products.","zh":"這些產品的質量有相當大的差異。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Natural variation helps plants adapt to different environments.","zh":"自然變異有助於植物適應不同的環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7acfc48851f90525","term":"variation","forms":["variation","variations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"變體；不同版本","explanation":"指與原來的事物有聯絡、但在某些方面不同的另一個版本；它仍然保留原型的基本特點，只是做了改動。","examples":[{"en":"This recipe is a variation on a traditional Italian dish.","zh":"這道菜是傳統義大利菜的一種變體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The designer created several variations of the original logo.","zh":"設計師製作了原始標誌的幾個不同版本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b530f329d65f246114bd","word":"variety","forms":["variety"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4b48a233d2ec728","term":"variety","forms":["variety","varieties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種具體型別","explanation":"指某類事物中的一個具體型別、版本或品種，是“多樣性”中可以單獨挑出來的一種。","examples":[{"en":"This variety of tomato grows well in cool weather.","zh":"這種番茄品種在涼爽的天氣里長得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop sells several varieties of tea.","zh":"這家店賣好幾種茶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variety","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-739ece36e2522c6c","term":"variety","forms":["variety","varieties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"各種不同的事物","explanation":"指許多不同事物組成的集合，突出“種類多、內容不一”。它把“一個具體型別”擴充套件成了“許多型別放在一起”。","examples":[{"en":"The market offers a variety of fresh vegetables.","zh":"這個市場提供各種新鮮蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stall sells a variety of handmade gifts.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variety","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-56c5c6d7c4dbb27d","term":"variety","forms":["variety","varieties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"多樣性","explanation":"指事物種類、形式或內容豐富而不單一的性質，是 variety 最核心的抽象意義之一。","examples":[{"en":"A little variety makes the class more interesting.","zh":"增加一點多樣性會讓這堂課更有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We need more variety in our meals.","zh":"我們的飲食需要更多樣化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/variety","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,113,114,115],"total":6,"counts":{"111":1,"112":1,"113":1,"114":1,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-1d35a94841cbfca17954","word":"various","forms":["various"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0c7a28b2856da40","term":"various","forms":["various"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多種多樣的","explanation":"像一張桌上擺著許多不同物品一樣，強調組成某事物的元素、原因或形式很多，而且彼此有區別。","examples":[{"en":"The project was delayed for various reasons.","zh":"這個專案因各種各樣的原因而延期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has worked in various fields of science.","zh":"她在科學的多個不同領域工作過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/various","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e984abc9184b4d57","term":"various","forms":["various"],"pos":"det","zh":"若干；多個","explanation":"從一組沒有明確列出的東西中指出不止一個，相當於“若干個、多個”；重點不是說出具體數量或具體物件。","examples":[{"en":"Various departments have been asked to review the plan.","zh":"已經要求多個部門審查這項計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Various residents offered to help with the cleanup.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/various","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,112,113,115],"total":8,"counts":{"111":2,"112":1,"113":3,"115":2}}},{"id":"ceec-8f289b828ab9b83eec66","word":"vary","forms":["vary"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ee451e967495220","term":"vary","forms":["vary","varies","varying","varied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"改變；變換","explanation":"主動把同一件事換成不同的形式、內容或做法，避免每次都完全一樣。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher varies the activities to keep the children interested.","zh":"老師變換活動形式，讓孩子們保持興趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try to vary your wording instead of repeating the same phrase.","zh":"儘量變換措辭，不要反覆使用同一個短語。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6063c31f0409512","term":"vary","forms":["vary","varies","varying","varied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"調整；改變做法","explanation":"主動把現有的安排、習慣或內容改成另一種樣子，突出“作出調整”。","examples":[{"en":"You should vary your exercise routine from week to week.","zh":"你應該每週調整一下鍛鍊計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We vary the menu according to the season.","zh":"我們根據季節調整選單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-902d6e389ce7102e","term":"vary","forms":["vary","varies","varying","varied"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隨情況變化","explanation":"某個數值、狀態或感受不會保持不變，而是隨著時間、地點或其他條件改變。","examples":[{"en":"Prices vary depending on the season.","zh":"價格會隨季節而變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her energy level varies throughout the day.","zh":"她的精力水平一整天都在變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[114,115],"total":2,"counts":{"114":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-30e436cb382491bb1f03","word":"vase","forms":["vase"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-43ec4e1232cb423e","term":"vase","forms":["vase","vases"],"pos":"noun","zh":"花瓶","explanation":"一種直立、有開口的容器，主要用來插花、展示鮮花，也可以放乾花或人造花。這是 vase 最常見、最值得優先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"She put the roses in a glass vase.","zh":"她把玫瑰插進了一個玻璃花瓶裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is a small vase of flowers on the table.","zh":"桌上有一個插著花的小花瓶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vase","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-375eca5944bc3c254740","word":"vast","forms":["vast"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ccaec3db62169c85","term":"vast","forms":["vast","vaster","more vast","vastest","most vast"],"pos":"adj","zh":"廣闊的；巨大的","explanation":"表示實際空間非常寬廣或物體非常大，也可以把這種“無邊無際”的感覺用於抽象事物。沙漠、海洋、天空等都可以用 vast 來形容。","examples":[{"en":"The Sahara is a vast desert.","zh":"撒哈拉是一片廣闊的沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We could see the vast ocean from the hill.","zh":"我們從山上可以看到一望無際的大海。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a22fc68451c6668c","term":"vast","forms":["vast","vaster","more vast","vastest","most vast"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極大的；程度很高的","explanation":"把“廣闊無邊”的核心感覺轉用於數量、範圍、差異、影響或強度，表示其規模或程度大得驚人。","examples":[{"en":"The project required a vast amount of money.","zh":"這個專案需要一大筆錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They showed vast enthusiasm for the ambitious proposal.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4715b734085d8d9c9981","word":"vegetable","forms":["vegetable"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90c1065a872d318d","term":"vegetable","forms":["vegetable","vegetables"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蔬菜","explanation":"指通常作為食物食用的植物，尤其是葉、根、莖、果實或花等部分；英語飲食分類通常不把被視為水果的植物算作 vegetable。","examples":[{"en":"Try to eat more vegetables with your dinner.","zh":"晚餐時儘量多吃些蔬菜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Is a tomato a fruit or a vegetable?","zh":"番茄是水果還是蔬菜？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vegetable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-28af4d7711a60323a070","word":"vegetarian","forms":["vegetarian"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b394c04b1721ead3","term":"vegetarian","forms":["vegetarian","vegetarians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"素食者","explanation":"指不吃動物肉的人；在某些人的定義中，還可能包括不使用部分或全部動物產品的人，但這個範圍因人而異。","examples":[{"en":"The hotel offers a special breakfast for vegetarians.","zh":"這家酒店為素食者提供特別早餐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He became a vegetarian last year.","zh":"他去年開始吃素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vegetarian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b404ed3c370c8c264e53","word":"vehicle","forms":["vehicle"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49d4eb0ba17daa9b","term":"vehicle","forms":["vehicle","vehicles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交通工具；運載工具","explanation":"指用來運送人、動物、物品或材料的工具，範圍比“汽車”更大，可以包括各種陸上、水上或空中的交通工具。","examples":[{"en":"The city is investing in cleaner public vehicles.","zh":"這座城市正在投資更清潔的公共交通工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small vehicle carried the supplies across the desert.","zh":"一輛小型運輸工具把物資運過了沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vehicle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-01979b66ee1794c473f5","word":"veil","forms":["veil"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-92e648eb66ea34bc","term":"veil","forms":["veil","veils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"面紗；遮臉或遮物的薄布","explanation":"指掛起或鋪開、用來遮住臉或物體的輕薄布料，通常讓形狀仍隱約可見；婚禮頭紗和宗教場合的面紗都屬於這一義。","examples":[{"en":"The bride lifted her veil before the ceremony.","zh":"新娘在儀式開始前掀起了面紗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A thin veil covered the statue.","zh":"一層薄薄的布遮住了雕像。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-459e83f4edb34e7a","term":"veil","forms":["veil","veils"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遮擋清晰視線的東西","explanation":"指任何讓人看不清、看不完整的遮擋物，既可以是煙霧、霧氣等實際東西，也可以是抽象的模糊因素。","examples":[{"en":"A veil of mist covered the valley at dawn.","zh":"黎明時，一層薄霧籠罩著山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A veil of smoke hid the distant hills.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-066034ea9c591500","term":"veil","forms":["veil","veils","veiling","veiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"遮住；掩飾","explanation":"指像蒙上一層面紗一樣遮住景物、聲音或真相，使人看不清或難以直接瞭解。","examples":[{"en":"Smoke veiled the mountains in the distance.","zh":"煙霧遮住了遠處的群山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report veiled the real reason for the delay.","zh":"這份報告掩飾了延誤的真正原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-099d67bf078028cc702e","word":"vein","forms":["vein"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8edc015a78e88cc6","term":"vein","forms":["vein","veins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"靜脈","explanation":"指把血液從毛細血管輸送回心臟的血管。它是身體裡那條“迴流”的脈絡，和把血液從心臟送出的動脈相對。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor inserted the needle into a vein in her arm.","zh":"醫生把針插入了她手臂上的一條靜脈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Some veins are easier to see when the skin is warm.","zh":"皮膚溫暖時，有些靜脈更容易看見。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vein","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be22c05e95a79653","term":"vein","forms":["vein","veins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"思路；話題脈絡","explanation":"指談話、寫作或思緒沿著某個方向展開的線索。就像一條脈絡把許多分散的內容連在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The second speaker continued in the same vein.","zh":"第二位發言者沿用了相同的思路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her essay follows a vein of thought that connects art and memory.","zh":"她的文章沿著一條把藝術和記憶聯絡起來的思路展開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vein","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6a2e9d042fdba67e","term":"vein","forms":["vein","veins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"風格；傾向","explanation":"指作品、表演或言論所呈現的總體風格或傾向。它可以看作思想脈絡進一步發展成作品的表達方向。","examples":[{"en":"The film is a warm comedy in the same vein as her earlier work.","zh":"這部電影是一部溫暖的喜劇，風格和她早期的作品相近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her next novel continued in a darker vein.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vein","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f4c44266a2dfad984793","word":"velvet","forms":["velvet"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9500368e92c5b6f","term":"velvet","forms":["velvet","more velvet","most velvet"],"pos":"adj","zh":"天鵝絨制的","explanation":"表示某物由天鵝絨製成，重點是材料，而不是僅僅具有柔軟觸感。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a velvet dress to the concert.","zh":"她穿了一條天鵝絨連衣裙去聽音樂會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A velvet curtain concealed the tiny stage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f533fa1c9d0de01d","term":"velvet","forms":["velvet","more velvet","most velvet"],"pos":"adj","zh":"柔軟細膩的","explanation":"形容觸感、聲音或動作像天鵝絨一樣柔和、細膩，不一定真的含有天鵝絨材料。","examples":[{"en":"The singer had a rich, velvet voice.","zh":"那位歌手的聲音醇厚而柔和。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cream left my hands feeling velvet-soft.","zh":"這種乳霜讓我的雙手摸起來像天鵝絨一樣柔軟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac9c10852245dd77","term":"velvet","forms":["velvet","velvets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天鵝絨織物","explanation":"一種表面有厚而短的絨毛、摸起來柔軟的織物，傳統上常用絲製作，現在也可用棉或合成纖維製作。","examples":[{"en":"The theater seats were covered in deep red velvet.","zh":"劇院的座椅鋪著深紅色天鵝絨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She chose velvet for the curtains because it blocks the light well.","zh":"她選天鵝絨做窗簾，因為它很能遮光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-630ba09448af522154f3","word":"vendor","forms":["vendor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-744d6ad2ea45fea4","term":"vendor","forms":["vendor","vendors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"銷售者；供應商","explanation":"vendor 是把商品、服務或產品提供給別人並收取費用的人或公司；重點在“賣出或供應”這一角色，而不在於對方在哪裡購買。","examples":[{"en":"The vendor offered us a discount on the camping equipment.","zh":"那家供應商給我們購買露營裝備打了折。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several local vendors sell food at the weekend market.","zh":"週末市場上有幾家當地攤販在賣食品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vendor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-352c00e4c6860a34dd5d","word":"venture","forms":["venture"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8919be0ba45989fa","term":"venture","forms":["venture","ventures"],"pos":"noun","zh":"冒險事業；冒險行動","explanation":"指需要勇氣、可能失敗或遇到危險的行動、旅程或事業。它就像把船駛向未知海域，重點是既有目標，又承擔不確定性。","examples":[{"en":"Starting a company is a risky venture.","zh":"創辦公司是一項有風險的冒險事業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They set out on a bold venture into the mountains.","zh":"他們踏上了大膽進山的冒險旅程。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a00df7c2c235010","term":"venture","forms":["venture","ventures","venturing","ventured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"冒險前往；冒險從事","explanation":"指明知前方未知或有危險，仍然前往某地或進入某個領域。它就是把船駛入未知海域的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Few travelers venture into the desert in summer.","zh":"很少有旅行者敢在夏天進入沙漠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is venturing into online education.","zh":"這家公司正冒險進入線上教育領域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab7c4d59bc673f5a","term":"venture","forms":["venture","ventures","venturing","ventured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拿去冒險；冒險投入","explanation":"指把錢、資源或機會押在一件結果不確定的事情上，願意承擔可能的損失。","examples":[{"en":"They ventured a large sum into the project.","zh":"他們冒險把一大筆錢投入了這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ventured his entire inheritance on the new business.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-22f7cd119207d751","term":"venture","forms":["venture","ventures","venturing","ventured"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敢於嘗試","explanation":"指在沒有成功把握的情況下仍敢去做某事，重點是鼓起勇氣嘗試，而不只是一般地試一試。","examples":[{"en":"I would not venture to guess the answer.","zh":"我不敢猜這個答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ventured to ask for a second chance.","zh":"他鼓起勇氣請求再給他一次機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venture","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e622da235a56977383e1","word":"venue","forms":["venue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d25764e0d0c57979","term":"venue","forms":["venue","venues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"活動場所","explanation":"指為演出、比賽或其他娛樂活動專門安排的場所，重點是人們聚集並觀看或參加活動的地點。","examples":[{"en":"The new venue can hold more than a thousand people.","zh":"這個新場館可以容納一千多人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We are looking for a small venue for the concert.","zh":"我們正在為這場音樂會尋找一個小型場地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3005170f6383b797","term":"venue","forms":["venue","venues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體育比賽場館","explanation":"指舉行體育比賽的體育場、體育館等建築，是“活動場所”這一核心意思在體育語境中的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"The final will take place at a larger venue next year.","zh":"明年的決賽將在一個更大的場館舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The stadium will be the venue for the final.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-713e270f9aebe83fe5c9","word":"verbal","forms":["verbal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74a49ea928c32040","term":"verbal","forms":["verbal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"與詞語有關的","explanation":"表示事情涉及詞語、言語表達或詞彙本身，而不是影象、動作等其他表達方式。這是 verbal 最基礎、最寬的概念。","examples":[{"en":"The exam tests verbal reasoning.","zh":"這場考試考查言語推理能力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has excellent verbal skills.","zh":"她的語言表達能力很強。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verbal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-07116800cb6116d6","term":"verbal","forms":["verbal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"口頭的","explanation":"表示透過說話而不是書面檔案來表達，尤其用於協議、同意、指示或承諾。這個義項是日常使用中非常重要的一支。","examples":[{"en":"We reached a verbal agreement yesterday.","zh":"我們昨天達成了口頭協議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager gave us verbal instructions.","zh":"經理向我們作了口頭指示。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verbal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7abaed964edc4bcd","term":"verbal","forms":["verbal","verbals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動詞形式","explanation":"語法上指由動詞構成、但不在句中直接充當謂語的形式，例如不定式、分詞和動名詞。可以把它記成“從動詞長出來、卻不獨立作謂語的詞形”。","examples":[{"en":"In this sentence, “running” is a verbal, not the main verb.","zh":"在這個句子中，running 是動詞形式，不是主要謂語動詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The infinitive is a verbal that can function as a noun.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verbal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-11e221bd1b7fc99544f3","word":"verdict","forms":["verdict"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0d1acf74ddfe2656","term":"verdict","forms":["verdict","verdicts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"法律裁決","explanation":"指陪審團、法官或調查機構根據案件事實作出的正式裁決，例如判定被告有罪、無罪，或確定某件事的責任。","examples":[{"en":"After two days of discussion, the jury returned a guilty verdict.","zh":"經過兩天的討論，陪審團作出了有罪裁決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge asked the jury to reach a verdict by Friday.","zh":"法官要求陪審團在星期五之前作出裁決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verdict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4deeff3ecffdab4b","term":"verdict","forms":["verdict","verdicts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"明確判斷；結論","explanation":"指對某個人、某件事或某種表現作出的明確評價或結論，核心仍是“權衡之後定下來的說法”，但不一定涉及法庭。","examples":[{"en":"The critics have given their verdict on the new film.","zh":"評論家已經對這部新電影作出了評價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The verdict on the new software is still out.","zh":"人們對這款新軟體的最終評價還沒有定論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verdict","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05681deae950628d00d7","word":"versatile","forms":["versatile"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e3a5e70be98fd32f","term":"versatile","forms":["versatile","more versatile","most versatile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"多才多藝的","explanation":"指一個人具備多種技能，能勝任不同型別的工作或活動，重點是適應面廣且有實際能力。","examples":[{"en":"She is a versatile musician who plays several instruments.","zh":"她是一位多才多藝的音樂家，會演奏好幾種樂器。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company needs versatile employees who can handle different tasks.","zh":"這家公司需要能處理不同任務的多面手員工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/versatile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dd271f86582f6270","term":"versatile","forms":["versatile","more versatile","most versatile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"用途多的；多功能的","explanation":"指物品、工具或方法可以用於多種目的，能夠靈活應對不同需要。","examples":[{"en":"A small knife is a versatile tool for camping.","zh":"小刀是露營時用途很廣的工具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This versatile tool cuts, drills, and sands.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/versatile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5abde01ff920313c1491","word":"verse","forms":["verse"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24eff86f74acec8f","term":"verse","forms":["verse","verses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"格律詩體","explanation":"指按照較固定的節拍、格律和押韻方式寫成的詩歌形式，重點在於它有明確的形式約束，而不只是泛指詩。","examples":[{"en":"The play is written in formal verse.","zh":"這部戲劇以格律詩體寫成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She prefers verse with a regular rhyme scheme.","zh":"她更喜歡押韻規則整齊的詩體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-633b82af079cc938","term":"verse","forms":["verse","verses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詩歌形式","explanation":"泛指詩歌或詩歌這種表達形式，不一定強調嚴格的格律和押韻；它是“把語言排成詩行”的大類概念。","examples":[{"en":"The story is told in verse rather than prose.","zh":"這個故事不是用散文，而是用詩歌形式講述的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He retold the legend in verse.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bf0aaec381d97b2","term":"verse","forms":["verse","verses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歌曲的一段","explanation":"指歌曲中由幾行歌片語成、通常會重複相似旋律的一個段落，常與副歌chorus相對；它仍然保留了“成排的詩句”這個核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The singer changed the melody in the final verse.","zh":"歌手在最後一段歌詞中改變了旋律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone joined in when the second verse began.","zh":"第二段歌詞開始時，大家都跟著唱了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/verse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ca4f3850ccc331aaf8a","word":"version","forms":["version"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dbc77b40a063692f","term":"version","forms":["version","versions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"具體版本；變體","explanation":"指同一事物在內容、形式或細節上有所不同的一個具體版本。電影、書籍、計劃或故事都可以有多個version。","examples":[{"en":"This is the original version of the song.","zh":"這是這首歌的原版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The director released a longer version of the film.","zh":"導演釋出了這部電影的加長版。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/version","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f01fee69b8fdde87","term":"version","forms":["version","versions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"譯本；翻譯版本","explanation":"指把同一文字用另一種語言表達出來的版本，例如某本書的中文譯本或某部宗教經典的特定譯本。重點是成品文字，而不只是翻譯這一行為。","examples":[{"en":"I read the Chinese version of the novel.","zh":"我讀了這部小說的中文譯本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Which version of the poem did you use?","zh":"你用的是這首詩的哪個譯本？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/version","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c86b9380b2eb5db","term":"version","forms":["version","versions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種說法；某個角度的敘述","explanation":"指某人從特定角度對一件事作出的描述或解釋。不同人可能針對同一事件給出不同的version，它們未必完全一致。","examples":[{"en":"She gave us her version of what happened.","zh":"她向我們講述了她所認為的事情經過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witnesses gave conflicting versions of the incident.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/version","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,113],"total":3,"counts":{"112":2,"113":1}}},{"id":"ceec-a5bfb753e5e8ac3ff91a","word":"versus","forms":["versus"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ff9961ad5b4b87d3","term":"versus","forms":["versus"],"pos":"prep","zh":"對抗；對陣","explanation":"表示兩方直接面對並爭奪勝負，常用於體育比賽、競賽或其他對抗場景。記住“面對面站在兩端”的畫面，就能理解它為什麼表示“甲對乙”。","examples":[{"en":"It will be Canada versus Mexico in the final.","zh":"決賽將由加拿大對墨西哥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Tonight's match is Tigers versus Eagles.","zh":"今晚的比賽是老虎隊對鷹隊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/versus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a6528503b634e4cf","term":"versus","forms":["versus"],"pos":"prep","zh":"與……相比；相對於","explanation":"表示把兩個數字、情況或觀點放在一起對照，不一定有敵對關係。它仍然保留“面對面擺出來”的核心畫面，只是雙方從競爭對手變成比較物件。","examples":[{"en":"The survey found 52% support versus 38% opposition.","zh":"調查顯示，支援率為百分之五十二，反對率為百分之三十八。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This year's sales are much higher versus last year's.","zh":"與去年相比，今年的銷量高得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/versus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-34da56029403e6f793b8","word":"vertical","forms":["vertical"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b4299933bc817a9","term":"vertical","forms":["vertical","more vertical","most vertical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"豎直的；垂直的","explanation":"表示像從地面向上立起那樣，沿上下方向延伸，或與水平面成直角。它是這個詞最基本、最常用的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The picture is hanging on a vertical wall.","zh":"這幅畫掛在一面豎直的牆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Draw a vertical line through the center of the page.","zh":"穿過頁面中心畫一條豎線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vertical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4be1a8d327e2b10","term":"vertical","forms":["vertical","more vertical","most vertical"],"pos":"adj","zh":"縱座標的；沿 y 軸的","explanation":"在二維座標系中，指與水平的 x 軸垂直、通常表示上下方向的 y 軸或相關方向。","examples":[{"en":"The vertical axis shows the number of visitors.","zh":"縱軸顯示訪客人數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vertical axis shows changes in temperature.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vertical","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4c6a4839f83d20d276e7","word":"very","forms":["very"],"officialPos":"adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-71c3c87b688a7056","term":"very","forms":["very"],"pos":"adv","zh":"非常；很","explanation":"放在形容詞或副詞前，表示程度很高，是現代英語中最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"The soup is very hot, so let it cool for a minute.","zh":"湯很燙，先讓它涼一分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spoke very quietly during the meeting.","zh":"她在會議期間說話非常輕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/very","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c27878e007eb0e8","term":"very","forms":["very"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最……的；正是最……的那個","explanation":"放在最高階前，強調某人或某物在相關範圍內確實達到最突出的位置，常可理解為“正是最……的那個”。","examples":[{"en":"This may be the very best solution we can find.","zh":"這可能正是我們能找到的最佳解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She arrived at the very last minute.","zh":"她在最後一刻才到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/very","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2df5712e1cf303a50fac","word":"vessel","forms":["vessel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a33a71b188f32593","term":"vessel","forms":["vessel","vessels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"船隻；交通工具","explanation":"vessel 可以指在水上運輸人員或貨物的船，也可較正式地指用於空中或太空運輸的交通工具。它仍然保留“承載東西並移動”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The rescue vessel reached the island before dawn.","zh":"救援船在黎明前抵達了那座島。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several vessels were waiting outside the harbor.","zh":"幾艘船正在港外等待。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vessel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-472295a564309b1b","term":"vessel","forms":["vessel","vessels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"容器","explanation":"vessel 可以指裝液體或其他物質的容器，如杯、碗、瓶、壺等。重點不在形狀，而在於它能夠把某種東西裝在裡面。","examples":[{"en":"Pour the oil into a clean glass vessel.","zh":"把油倒進一個乾淨的玻璃容器裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The potter shaped a wide-mouthed vessel for storing grain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vessel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-72dd029baa651351a853","word":"vest","forms":["vest"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dd7c7f6adbbc19b1","term":"vest","forms":["vest","vests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"馬甲；西裝背心","explanation":"在加拿大和美國，vest通常指前面扣合、穿在襯衫外面的無袖馬甲，常作為西裝的一部分。","examples":[{"en":"He wore a dark vest over a white shirt.","zh":"他在白襯衫外面穿了一件深色馬甲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The three-piece suit includes a jacket, trousers, and a vest.","zh":"這套三件式西裝包括外套、褲子和馬甲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d133a66dd576b4cfde78","word":"veteran","forms":["veteran"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9fbddd553ca593f3","term":"veteran","forms":["veteran","veterans"],"pos":"noun","zh":"老手；資深人士","explanation":"指在某項工作、活動或領域中做了很久、經驗很豐富的人。這個核心意思來自“走過很多次、已經熟悉各種情況”的形象。","examples":[{"en":"As a veteran of the software industry, he quickly spotted the problem.","zh":"作為軟體行業的資深人士，他很快就發現了問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new volunteers learned a lot from the campaign veterans.","zh":"新志願者從參加過多次活動的老手那裡學到了很多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veteran","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e20705dba1485a34b04f","word":"veterinarian/vet","forms":["veterinarian","vet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1642fd9063650c61","term":"veterinarian","forms":["veterinarian","veterinarians"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獸醫","explanation":"指給狗、貓、馬等非人類動物診斷疾病、進行治療或提供醫療建議的醫生。可以把它和 veterinary 一起記：veterinarian 是做動物醫療的人，veterinary 是動物醫療相關的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The veterinarian examined our cat and gave us some medicine.","zh":"獸醫給我們的貓做了檢查，並給了我們一些藥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The veterinarian examined the limping dog.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veterinarian","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6c867fe7186e1c8b","term":"vet","forms":["vet","vets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獸醫","explanation":"指專門檢查、診斷和治療動物的醫生。這個義項可以和“檢查動物是否健康”的核心畫面直接聯絡起來。","examples":[{"en":"We took our dog to the vet after it stopped eating.","zh":"我們的狗不吃東西后，我們把它帶去看獸醫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vet says the cat is recovering well.","zh":"獸醫說這隻貓恢復得很好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cb9bdb0732913b291235","word":"veto","forms":["veto"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a28be47f505c2ede","term":"veto","forms":["veto","vetoes","vetos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"否決權","explanation":"指某個個人、機構或職位擁有的、能夠阻止決定或法律透過的正式權力。它就像一枚能讓程式停下來的紅燈按鈕。","examples":[{"en":"The president has a veto over the proposed law.","zh":"總統對這項擬議法律擁有否決權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council gave the minority a veto on major decisions.","zh":"委員會賦予少數派對重大決定的否決權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91ba15c051bf7270","term":"veto","forms":["veto","vetoes","vetoing","vetoed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"否決","explanation":"指使用正式的否決權，阻止法律、決定或提案繼續透過。它對應名詞“否決權”真正被按下、發揮作用的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The governor vetoed the bill yesterday.","zh":"州長昨天否決了這項法案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal was vetoed by the committee.","zh":"這項提案被委員會否決了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veto","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d327af41f96c23c6b13","word":"via","forms":["via"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb85fd3caf279788","term":"via","forms":["via"],"pos":"prep","zh":"經由；途經","explanation":"via 表示沿某條路線經過一個地點，再到達目的地；核心畫面就是“透過一條中間通道”。","examples":[{"en":"We flew to Rome via Frankfurt.","zh":"我們經法蘭克福飛往羅馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train goes via the coast.","zh":"這趟火車經由海岸線行駛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/via","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5737a48ada11cb9b","term":"via","forms":["via"],"pos":"prep","zh":"透過；藉助","explanation":"via 也表示藉助某種工具、渠道或方法來完成事情，相當於“透過這個通道來做”。","examples":[{"en":"Please send the documents via email.","zh":"請透過電子郵件傳送這些檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sent the documents via a secure connection.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/via","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1977d46c03fe932cab46","word":"viable","forms":["viable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-803be96c2ff2ad87","term":"viable","forms":["viable","more viable","most viable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"可行的","explanation":"指某個想法、計劃或選擇有現實基礎，確實可以實施，而不是停留在紙面上的設想。","examples":[{"en":"We need to find a viable option before the deadline.","zh":"我們需要在截止日期前找到一個可行的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal is viable if we reduce the cost.","zh":"如果降低成本，這項提議就是可行的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6163a145a7fe5611","term":"viable","forms":["viable","more viable","most viable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"能成功運作的","explanation":"指一個系統、業務、專案或方法不僅能夠開始，而且能夠持續有效地執行並取得成功；這是從“能活下去”發展出的比喻義。","examples":[{"en":"The company is looking for a way to keep the project viable.","zh":"這家公司正在尋找讓這個專案持續運作下去的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new pricing model could make the business viable.","zh":"新的定價模式可能讓這項業務真正運轉起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3f3b4341e51c371706b7","word":"vibrate","forms":["vibrate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a07f1a5accc748d3","term":"vibrate","forms":["vibrate","vibrates","vibrating","vibrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"快速來回振動","explanation":"指物體以很小、很快的幅度來回移動，例如手機、琴絃或機器在執行時不斷顫動。","examples":[{"en":"The phone began to vibrate on the table.","zh":"手機開始在桌上振動起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The window vibrated when the truck passed.","zh":"卡車經過時，窗戶振動了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vibrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1ff4a0e805eea8a5","term":"vibrate","forms":["vibrate","vibrates","vibrating","vibrated"],"pos":"verb","zh":"產生共鳴","explanation":"由實際振動引申為聲音、思想或情緒在某處迴盪，或在某人心中引起強烈反應。","examples":[{"en":"The singer's voice vibrated through the small hall.","zh":"歌手的聲音在小禮堂裡迴盪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her words vibrated with quiet confidence.","zh":"她的話語中迴盪著一種沉靜的自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vibrate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d6740176da76c7e5ec36","word":"vibration","forms":["vibration"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4aa36df377aae48","term":"vibration","forms":["vibration","vibrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"振動；震動狀態","explanation":"指振動這一動作，或某物正處於被振動、不斷抖動的狀態；重點是“發生振動”這件事本身。","examples":[{"en":"I could feel a slight vibration under my feet.","zh":"我能感覺到腳下有輕微的震動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vibration of the engine made the windows rattle.","zh":"發動機的振動使窗戶哐哐作響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vibration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e4b6d84c81c3a62e","term":"vibration","forms":["vibration","vibrations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"週期性振動","explanation":"在物理學中，指物體圍繞平衡位置反覆來回運動的過程；它把普通的“抖動”說得更精確，強調規律性和往復性。","examples":[{"en":"The instrument measures the vibration of the bridge.","zh":"這臺儀器測量橋樑的振動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vibration became stronger as the machine sped up.","zh":"機器加速後，振動變得更強了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vibration","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0e1f6dec24570014bb36","word":"vice","forms":["vice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e1df5d687e3aacad","term":"vice","forms":["vice","vices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"惡習；道德缺點","explanation":"指反覆表現出來、被認為不道德或有害的行為習慣，例如驕傲、貪婪或酗酒；它是品德上的“缺口”。","examples":[{"en":"He admits that impatience is one of his worst vices.","zh":"他承認急躁是自己最嚴重的惡習之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Pride can become a vice when it hurts other people.","zh":"驕傲傷害他人時，就可能變成一種惡習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b7209539586cb6e","term":"vice","forms":["vice","vices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"臺鉗；夾具","explanation":"一種用螺旋裝置把物件夾牢的工具；它把物件固定在一個位置上，方便鋸、鑽或加工。","examples":[{"en":"Secure the metal rod in the vice before cutting it.","zh":"切割金屬桿前，先把它牢牢夾在臺鉗裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic tightened the vice around the pipe.","zh":"修理工用臺鉗夾緊了管子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f792bc226e4cd888f3cf","word":"vicious","forms":["vicious"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dda8310791562144","term":"vicious","forms":["vicious","more vicious","viciouser","most vicious","viciousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"兇暴殘忍的","explanation":"形容某人、某動物或某種行為兇暴、殘忍，而且可能造成嚴重傷害或破壞；重點在“會傷人、會毀壞”的危險性。","examples":[{"en":"The gang carried out a vicious attack on the shopkeeper.","zh":"這夥人殘忍地襲擊了店主。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A vicious dog was chained behind the house.","zh":"房子後面拴著一條兇猛的狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vicious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bde2a5ddaa664607","term":"vicious","forms":["vicious","more vicious","viciouser","most vicious","viciousest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"野蠻好攻擊的","explanation":"強調人或動物表現得像失控的猛獸，野蠻、好鬥並主動攻擊；也可形容某種疾病等來勢兇猛、令人難以應付。","examples":[{"en":"He developed a vicious cough that kept him awake all night.","zh":"他咳嗽得很厲害，整夜都睡不著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vicious dog lunged at anyone approaching the gate.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vicious","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bdd5b5b92e2d9f30a3b","word":"victim","forms":["victim"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-84fb3cf5544f0bc8","term":"victim","forms":["victim","victims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受害者","explanation":"指受到傷害、欺騙、壓迫或其他不利影響的人，重點是這個人承受了某種傷害或後果。","examples":[{"en":"The victim of the robbery gave a detailed statement.","zh":"這起搶劫案的受害者作了詳細陳述。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She became a victim of online fraud.","zh":"她成了網路詐騙的受害者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/victim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f7cd075fb6705c15","term":"victim","forms":["victim","victims"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴力或犯罪受害者","explanation":"常特指遭到襲擊、謀殺等暴力行為的人；它仍然強調被傷害的一方，而不是施害者。","examples":[{"en":"The victims of the attack were taken to hospital.","zh":"襲擊事件的受害者被送往醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The victim identified the attacker from photographs.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/victim","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-99bde068af2d49ed7fc8","word":"victor","forms":["victor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b1b8ac9fec564a5b","term":"victor","forms":["victor","victors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"獲勝者","explanation":"victor 是在比賽、戰鬥或競爭中勝出的一方，也就是“勝者”。它把“取得勝利的人或一方”這個核心畫面直接說出來。","examples":[{"en":"After a close final, our team emerged as the victor.","zh":"經過一場勢均力敵的決賽，我們隊成為了勝者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The victor of the debate thanked the audience.","zh":"辯論的獲勝者向觀眾表示了感謝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/victor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-21665ca201d4070f6fcc","word":"victory","forms":["victory"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-408a391c4bff87ae","term":"victory","forms":["victory","victories"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勝利；勝果","explanation":"指在戰鬥、比賽或某項努力中成功勝出這一結果；既可以說總體的勝利，也可以說某一次具體的勝仗或勝果。","examples":[{"en":"The team celebrated a victory over its strongest rival.","zh":"這支球隊慶祝戰勝了最強的對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their victory came after months of hard work.","zh":"他們的勝利是在幾個月的努力之後取得的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/victory","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0cab1c9617404faf2b24","word":"video","forms":["video"],"officialPos":"n./v./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1caa86683524950a","term":"video","forms":["video","videos","videmus","videoes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"短影片或短片","explanation":"指一段可以單獨播放的影像短片，可能有聲音，也可能沒有聲音；音樂影片和網路短影片都屬於這一類。","examples":[{"en":"She posted a video of her dog playing in the garden.","zh":"她上傳了一段狗在花園裡玩耍的影片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We made a video montage for his birthday.","zh":"我們為他的生日製作了一段影片剪輯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/video","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8de37b9c555c5a2e","term":"video","forms":["video","videoes","videoing","videoed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"錄下活動或影片","explanation":"泛指把活動、場景或動態影片錄製成影片，可以有聲音，也可以沒有聲音；它是動詞 video 最寬的一種“儲存影像”用法。","examples":[{"en":"They videoed the whole performance from the front row.","zh":"他們從第一排把整場演出都錄了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please video the experiment so we can review it later.","zh":"請把這個實驗錄下來，這樣我們之後可以複習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/video","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2bcb43cbc8f6b7ef6633","word":"view","forms":["view"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b0357f06e407e5bb","term":"view","forms":["view","views"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀看；觀看次數","explanation":"view 可以指一次觀看，也可以指某個內容被觀看的次數；這裡的核心仍是“看見”。在影片、文章等內容上，它常表示觀看量。","examples":[{"en":"The short video received over a million views.","zh":"這段短影片的觀看次數超過了一百萬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The video received a thousand views overnight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/view","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-327f4d105391f5d4","term":"view","forms":["view","views"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀點；看法","explanation":"從“你怎樣看見一件事”引申出來，view 可以表示對情況、問題或人的看法和判斷。","examples":[{"en":"In my view, the plan needs more time.","zh":"在我看來，這個計劃還需要更多時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People have different views on this issue.","zh":"人們對這個問題有不同的看法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/view","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70f1d5152c223bb1","term":"view","forms":["view","views","viewing","viewed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"觀看；檢視","explanation":"view 作動詞時表示有意識地看、觀看或檢視某個內容，和名詞中“觀看”這一核心直接相連。","examples":[{"en":"You can view the full report online.","zh":"你可以線上檢視完整報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exhibition was viewed by thousands of visitors.","zh":"這場展覽被數千名遊客參觀了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/view","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d35ca5051b82ffc326a3","word":"viewer","forms":["viewer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e8ac68a926477dc","term":"viewer","forms":["viewer","viewers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀看者；觀眾","explanation":"指觀看演出、藝術作品或其他景象的人，重點是“正在看的人”。","examples":[{"en":"The film invites viewers to question what they see.","zh":"這部電影引導觀看者思考自己所看到的東西。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The painting had a powerful effect on every viewer.","zh":"這幅畫給每一位觀看者都留下了強烈的影響。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viewer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2df73c8b54e9d0ac","term":"viewer","forms":["viewer","viewers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電視觀眾","explanation":"特指正在看電視節目的人，也可泛指某個電視節目的觀眾群體。","examples":[{"en":"Millions of viewers watched the final match on television.","zh":"數百萬電視觀眾觀看了這場決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The documentary attracted millions of viewers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viewer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2460c11d97e3239c55b","word":"viewpoint","forms":["viewpoint"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2b2bda699110473","term":"viewpoint","forms":["viewpoint","viewpoints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀察位置；觀景點","explanation":"指觀察某個地方或事物時所處的位置，重點是“站在哪裡看”。這個位置通常能帶來較好的視野，也可以指供人觀景的地點。","examples":[{"en":"The tower offers a wonderful viewpoint of the old city.","zh":"這座塔能欣賞老城區的絕佳景色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We stopped at a viewpoint to look over the valley.","zh":"我們在一個觀景點停下來俯瞰山谷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viewpoint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-517cad4db6621384","term":"viewpoint","forms":["viewpoint","viewpoints"],"pos":"noun","zh":"觀點；看法；立場","explanation":"指一個人看待問題的角度、立場或個人看法。這裡的“位置”不是實際地點，而是你在思想上站在哪一邊、用什麼角度判斷事情。","examples":[{"en":"From a parent’s viewpoint, safety must come first.","zh":"從家長的角度看，安全必須放在第一位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book presents the issue from several different viewpoints.","zh":"這本書從幾個不同的角度呈現了這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viewpoint","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-340bbcf62fb5b430085a","word":"vigor","forms":["vigor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"vigor","forms":["vigor"],"pos":"n.","zh":"精力；活力","examples":[{"en":"She returned to work with renewed vigor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The young trees grew with remarkable vigor after the rain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-ebefe6c88a3815194d66","word":"vigorous","forms":["vigorous"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ffbd660955b99e27","term":"vigorous","forms":["vigorous","more vigorous","most vigorous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"強健有力的","explanation":"形容人的身體很強壯、精力充沛，做事或運動時顯得很有力量。它強調身體裡有充足的活力，而不只是外表健壯。","examples":[{"en":"She remains vigorous despite her busy schedule.","zh":"儘管日程很忙，她仍然精力充沛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor encouraged him to take vigorous exercise.","zh":"醫生鼓勵他進行有活力的鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vigorous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0e2602a24135eac6","term":"vigorous","forms":["vigorous","more vigorous","most vigorous"],"pos":"adj","zh":"精神飽滿而有力的","explanation":"把“力量”從身體延伸到頭腦、態度或行動，表示思考積極有力、辯論強烈，或某項活動開展得很有勁。它強調精神上的活躍和推動力。","examples":[{"en":"The proposal received vigorous support from local residents.","zh":"這項提議得到了當地居民的大力支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The audience gave the orchestra vigorous applause.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vigorous","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2499e63cb269d5144487","word":"villa","forms":["villa"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac3d758e76eaface","term":"villa","forms":["villa","villas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鄉間或海邊住宅","explanation":"villa通常指遠離城市、位於鄉間或海邊的較大住宅，常被當作休憩或度假的住處；它比普通住宅更容易讓人聯想到寬敞和私密。","examples":[{"en":"They rented a small villa by the sea for the summer.","zh":"他們租了一棟海邊的小別墅過夏天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villa has a garden and a view of the hills.","zh":"這棟別墅有花園，還能看到山丘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/villa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-447643e3180bd795","term":"villa","forms":["villa","villas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"英國式郊區住宅","explanation":"在英國英語中，villa也可以指中產階級街區裡常見的家庭住宅，尤其是維多利亞或愛德華時代風格的住宅；它不一定在鄉間。","examples":[{"en":"She bought a red-brick villa in a quiet suburb.","zh":"她在一個安靜的郊區買了一棟紅磚住宅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their spacious villa stood behind the suburb's original railway station.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/villa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-05cfbe283381aab8902e","word":"village","forms":["village"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-221c388a369f671b","term":"village","forms":["village","villages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"村莊；鄉村聚居地","explanation":"指規模通常介於小村落和城鎮之間的鄉村聚居地，裡面可能有住宅、商店、學校或教堂等日常設施。這是 village 最常見、最應該先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"There are two churches and three shops in our village.","zh":"我們村裡有兩座教堂和三家商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She grew up in a small village near the coast.","zh":"她在海邊附近的一個小村莊長大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/village","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ad064baa78567c8b395b","word":"villain","forms":["villain"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fed6d1e025a755c2","term":"villain","forms":["villain","villains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"邪惡的壞人","explanation":"指品行惡劣、會傷害或欺騙他人的人，是 villain 最基本的現代意思。","examples":[{"en":"The villain robbed the old man and escaped into the night.","zh":"那個惡人搶了老人的東西，逃進了夜色中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Everyone knew that he was the villain behind the scheme.","zh":"大家都知道他是這場陰謀背後的惡人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/villain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3cc0f4f92653a9fb","term":"villain","forms":["villain","villains"],"pos":"noun","zh":"故事反派","explanation":"指小說、電影、戲劇等作品中負責作惡、阻礙主角或與英雄對抗的角色；這個人通常就是作品裡的主要反面人物。","examples":[{"en":"The villain in the movie wants to destroy the entire city.","zh":"這部電影裡的反派想摧毀整座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The villain escapes from prison halfway through the film.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/villain","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3958765b23d8a51d3445","word":"vine","forms":["vine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-12749194a0bb66b2","term":"vine","forms":["vine","vines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"攀援藤本植物","explanation":"vine首先指莖不能獨立挺立、需要藉助支架或其他植物向上攀爬的藤本植物。它常透過卷鬚纏住物體，或讓莖繞著支撐物生長。","examples":[{"en":"A vine climbed up the fence and covered the window.","zh":"一株藤蔓爬上籬笆，遮住了窗戶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gardener tied the young vines to a wooden frame.","zh":"園丁把幼藤綁在木架上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4842db44f413fd2","term":"vine","forms":["vine","vines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"藤莖；粗藤","explanation":"vine還可以把注意力從整株植物移到它的莖，尤其是粗而結實、像繩子一樣的藤莖；叢林中供人抓住或擺動的藤條就是這種用法。","examples":[{"en":"The child held onto a thick vine as he crossed the stream.","zh":"孩子抓住一根粗藤，跨過了小溪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A monkey swung from one vine to another.","zh":"一隻猴子從一根藤條盪到另一根藤條上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-005200467ae17fa9","term":"vine","forms":["vine","vines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葡萄藤","explanation":"在葡萄種植語境中，vine特指結葡萄的藤，葡萄是長在藤上的，而不是長在樹上。這是vine最常見、最容易直接遇到的專門用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"They picked ripe grapes from the vine in late summer.","zh":"他們在夏末從葡萄藤上摘下了成熟的葡萄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vines produced their first grapes in September.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1bc690684dc2af6fde78","word":"vinegar","forms":["vinegar"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4af56f67f938eb2","term":"vinegar","forms":["vinegar","vinegars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"醋","explanation":"由酒精發酵形成的酸味液體，常用來調味、醃製或儲存食物。這是 vinegar 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Add a little vinegar to the salad dressing.","zh":"在沙拉醬里加一點醋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vegetables are preserved in vinegar.","zh":"這些蔬菜是用醋醃製儲存的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vinegar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-938aa1abaef61568","term":"vinegar","forms":["vinegar","vinegars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某一種醋","explanation":"指醋的一個具體品種或變體，例如按原料、味道或加入的香草來區分的醋。","examples":[{"en":"The shop sells fruit vinegars and herb vinegars.","zh":"這家店出售水果醋和香草醋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop stocks several vinegars made from local fruit.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vinegar","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce349b41f2a5935cc5aa","word":"vineyard","forms":["vineyard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fb3178263c5fd05a","term":"vineyard","forms":["vineyard","vineyards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葡萄園","explanation":"指成片種植葡萄藤的園地，特別是為釀造葡萄酒而種植葡萄的地方。記住“葡萄藤排成園地”這個畫面，就能把它和“葡萄”或“酒莊”區分開。","examples":[{"en":"We spent the afternoon walking through the vineyard.","zh":"我們整個下午都在葡萄園裡散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vineyard produces grapes for several local wineries.","zh":"這座葡萄園為幾家當地酒莊提供葡萄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vineyard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-80c3675033fde5c6ad3d","word":"violate","forms":["violate"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f1b1d6b0928580c","term":"violate","forms":["violate","violates","violating","violated","violatest","violatedst","violateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"違反；違背","explanation":"指越過法律、規則、協議或社會約定所設的界限，故意或實際地不遵守它。這個意義把 violate 的核心形象從“撞過界線”用到了抽象規則上。","examples":[{"en":"Driving without a license violates the law.","zh":"無證駕駛違反法律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company violated the terms of the agreement.","zh":"這家公司違反了協議條款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b0699077c062ae92","term":"violate","forms":["violate","violates","violating","violated","violatest","violatedst","violateth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"強姦；嚴重侵犯身體","explanation":"指以強迫或暴力方式侵犯他人的身體和性自主權，通常特指強姦。這是“強行撞過他人身體界限”的極嚴重用法，不能把它當作普通的“冒犯”或“傷害”。","examples":[{"en":"The attacker was arrested for violating a woman.","zh":"那名襲擊者因強姦一名女子而被逮捕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The survivor testified that the soldiers had violated her.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f904a6b30a01bfb8964b","word":"violation","forms":["violation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-addd2cf2bc81444d","term":"violation","forms":["violation","violations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"違反或侵犯","explanation":"指越過規則、法律、協議、權利或原則所規定的界線，或指這種越界行為本身。重點不只是“做錯了”，而是某項應受尊重的條件被破壞了。","examples":[{"en":"Sharing her private messages without permission was a violation of her privacy.","zh":"未經允許分享她的私人訊息侵犯了她的隱私。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The referee called the tackle a violation of the rules.","zh":"裁判認定這次剷球違反了規則。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b99880c01d6f96e4","term":"violation","forms":["violation","violations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"對身體或性自主權的侵犯","explanation":"在委婉語境中，指對個人身體、性自主權或人身尊嚴的嚴重侵犯。這裡的詞義比一般的“違反規則”嚴重得多，常用於避免直接說出更具體的侵害行為。","examples":[{"en":"The report described the abuse as a serious violation of the victim’s dignity.","zh":"報告稱這起虐待嚴重侵犯了受害者的尊嚴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The assault was a profound violation of her bodily autonomy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2a6abca4e3345424c298","word":"violence","forms":["violence"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ac1ecc5f3627f515","term":"violence","forms":["violence","violences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"猛烈的力量","explanation":"這裡的 violence 指力量大到具有衝擊性和破壞性，不一定是人對人的暴力；風暴、爆炸等自然現象也可以有這種力量。","examples":[{"en":"The violence of the earthquake surprised even experienced engineers.","zh":"地震的猛烈程度讓有經驗的工程師也感到吃驚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The violence of the storm tore branches away.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-843332a80c627232","term":"violence","forms":["violence","violences"],"pos":"noun","zh":"暴力行為","explanation":"這是最常見的意思之一，指用身體力量或其他強制性行動造成破壞、傷害、疼痛或苦難。","examples":[{"en":"The school has a strict policy against violence.","zh":"這所學校嚴格禁止暴力行為。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They found a peaceful way to settle the dispute without violence.","zh":"他們找到了一種不使用暴力、和平解決爭端的方法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violence","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86fb8a2cd1f9cedcb3e2","word":"violent","forms":["violent"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e31baf7585e27b72","term":"violent","forms":["violent","violenter","more violent","violentest","most violent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"猛烈的；劇烈的","explanation":"指力量、運動或自然現象強得不尋常，彷彿一股猛力突然衝出去。常用於風暴、爆炸、撞擊等。","examples":[{"en":"A violent storm damaged several houses along the coast.","zh":"一場猛烈的暴風雨損壞了海岸邊的幾所房屋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden impact caused a violent shake of the bridge.","zh":"突然的撞擊使橋樑劇烈搖晃起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dcc50983c2760e97","term":"violent","forms":["violent","violenter","more violent","violentest","most violent"],"pos":"adj","zh":"暴力的；涉及武力衝突的","explanation":"指行為、衝突或手段中包含對人的身體傷害或強制性的力量。","examples":[{"en":"The peaceful march turned violent after dark.","zh":"這場和平遊行在天黑後演變成了暴力事件。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The group rejected violent methods and called for dialogue.","zh":"這個團體拒絕暴力手段，呼籲進行對話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-22d2084f01936c564e69","word":"violet","forms":["violet"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-98f5f80fc41e2661","term":"violet","forms":["violet","violeter","violetest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"紫色的","explanation":"指像紫羅蘭花瓣那樣的紫色，通常是藍紫色調。","examples":[{"en":"She wore a violet scarf to the party.","zh":"她戴著一條紫色圍巾參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room was filled with soft violet light.","zh":"房間裡充滿了柔和的紫色燈光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3efa06db0ca822c","term":"violet","forms":["violet","violets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紫羅蘭","explanation":"指紫羅蘭屬的植物或花，尤其是有香味的紫羅蘭；有時也泛指外形相近的花。","examples":[{"en":"A violet was growing beside the garden wall.","zh":"花園圍牆旁長著一株紫羅蘭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children picked a small bunch of violets.","zh":"孩子們摘了一小束紫羅蘭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94426a0306a3fca9","term":"violet","forms":["violet","violets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"紫羅蘭色","explanation":"指紫羅蘭通常呈現的顏色，也就是一種偏藍的紫色。","examples":[{"en":"The artist painted the sky in violet.","zh":"畫家把天空塗成了紫羅蘭色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Violet is her favorite color.","zh":"紫羅蘭色是她最喜歡的顏色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00e3e584e242f926ff6b","word":"violin","forms":["violin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e17502b703904086","term":"violin","forms":["violin","violins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小提琴","explanation":"一種通常夾在下巴旁、用弓拉奏的四絃樂器，音域和外形都比中提琴小。日常使用中，這就是該詞最主要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"My daughter has been learning the violin for three years.","zh":"我女兒學小提琴已經三年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He played a beautiful violin solo at the concert.","zh":"他在音樂會上演奏了一段優美的小提琴獨奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8037a7520777cf9d","term":"violin","forms":["violin","violins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小提琴聲部或演奏者","explanation":"在樂團或合奏語境中，複數形式可以借樂器名稱指小提琴聲部，或指該聲部的演奏者，而不是單純指幾把小提琴。","examples":[{"en":"The violins enter softly after the flute solo.","zh":"長笛獨奏後，小提琴聲部輕柔地進入。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The second violins enter after the clarinet solo.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa1d0cc936c71f4cc684","word":"violinist","forms":["violinist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b10f17b20e02f7a6","term":"violinist","forms":["violinist","violinists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小提琴演奏者","explanation":"指演奏小提琴的人，可以是專業音樂家，也可以是業餘演奏者。把它記成“拿著小提琴演奏的人”即可。","examples":[{"en":"The young violinist played a beautiful melody at the concert.","zh":"那位年輕的小提琴演奏者在音樂會上演奏了一段優美的旋律。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The violinist tuned her instrument before the recital.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violinist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4098e1a88ff7d1811c0b","word":"virgin","forms":["virgin"],"officialPos":"n./adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-51f141f0d74b7df8","term":"virgin","forms":["virgin","more virgin","most virgin"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未經觸碰的","explanation":"指物體仍保持原狀，沒有被人觸碰、改變或使用，核心畫面就是“還沒有被動過”。","examples":[{"en":"We woke to a field of virgin snow.","zh":"我們醒來時看到田野裡還是一片未經觸碰的白雪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archaeologists found a virgin layer of soil.","zh":"考古學家發現了一層未經擾動的土壤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virgin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-82221d67b6d67e99","term":"virgin","forms":["virgin","more virgin","most virgin"],"pos":"adj","zh":"未開發的；未探索的","explanation":"把“未經動過”延伸到土地、地區或資源，表示人類尚未耕種、探索或開發。","examples":[{"en":"The expedition crossed miles of virgin forest.","zh":"探險隊穿越了數英里的原始森林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company hopes to develop virgin land near the coast.","zh":"公司希望開發海岸附近尚未開發的土地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virgin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e2efdd7db924f31dc81b","word":"virtual","forms":["virtual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-271a1bcbb8d6a798","term":"virtual","forms":["virtual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"實際上等同於；模擬的","explanation":"某事物在事實或實體形式上並不完全真實，但產生的效果或表現幾乎等同於真實事物；也可指人為模擬出來的事物。","examples":[{"en":"The team’s late goal was a virtual victory after such a difficult match.","zh":"這支球隊在如此艱難的比賽中最後進球，實際上就等於取得了勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum offers a virtual tour of the ancient city.","zh":"這家博物館提供這座古城的虛擬導覽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5f2bbf766b655c76","term":"virtual","forms":["virtual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"線上的；非現場的","explanation":"透過計算機或網路進行，而不是讓人或事物以實體形式出現在現場，但仍能提供相應的服務或活動。","examples":[{"en":"I have a virtual meeting with my doctor tomorrow morning.","zh":"我明天上午要和醫生進行線上會診。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The virtual assistant helped me book a flight.","zh":"這個虛擬助手幫我訂了機票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3371305232c8dc10ce95","word":"virtue","forms":["virtue"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-477432768975c695","term":"virtue","forms":["virtue","virtues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"美德的總體概念","explanation":"指人身上各種值得稱讚的良好品質的總體概念，強調道德和人格上的優秀。","examples":[{"en":"The novel explores the virtue of patience.","zh":"這部小說探討了耐心這一美德。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was admired for her virtue and courage.","zh":"她因自己的美德和勇氣而受到讚賞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0cd1b39985f0bc73","term":"virtue","forms":["virtue","virtues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"道德操守","explanation":"指一個人的行為和思想符合道德原則，也就是有良好的道德操守。","examples":[{"en":"Without virtue, there is no freedom.","zh":"沒有道德操守，就沒有自由。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She believed public officials should demonstrate personal virtue.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0ebae9bfcd705950","term":"virtue","forms":["virtue","virtues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可讚的性格品質","explanation":"指使一個人更可能做出善行的性格品質，例如誠實、耐心或勇敢；這裡強調某一種可識別的人格優點。","examples":[{"en":"Honesty is one of his greatest virtues.","zh":"誠實是他最大的優點之一。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her patience is a real virtue.","zh":"她的耐心確實是一種可貴的品質。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-14eb99923c21abfa","term":"virtue","forms":["virtue","virtues"],"pos":"noun","zh":"優點；有利之處","explanation":"把“值得稱讚的力量”從人的品格擴充套件到事物，指某人或某物本身具有的優點、有利之處。","examples":[{"en":"The main virtue of this design is its simplicity.","zh":"這種設計的主要優點是簡單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Simplicity is the main virtue of this design.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virtue","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2898a07b2cf23dda8530","word":"virus","forms":["virus"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a1b32d7162ba663d","term":"virus","forms":["virus","viruses","virusses","vira","viri","virii"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生物病毒","explanation":"一種極其微小的感染性結構，通常由遺傳物質和蛋白質外殼組成，必須進入活細胞才能複製；有些病毒會使宿主患病。這是 virus 最基本、最正式的含義。","examples":[{"en":"The virus spreads quickly through crowded places.","zh":"這種病毒會在人群擁擠的地方迅速傳播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Scientists are studying how the virus enters human cells.","zh":"科學家正在研究這種病毒如何進入人體細胞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b2c38d6f306bc572","term":"virus","forms":["virus","viruses","virusses","vira","viri","virii"],"pos":"noun","zh":"病毒性疾病","explanation":"在非正式口語中，virus 還可以借指由病毒引起的疾病，比如說某人“得了病毒感染”。這裡說的是人的病情，而不是實驗室裡的病毒實體。","examples":[{"en":"I think I've got a virus, so I'm staying home today.","zh":"我覺得自己得了病毒感染，所以今天待在家裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A stomach virus kept him home for three days.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2c5178a148f956e2","term":"virus","forms":["virus","viruses","virusses","vira","viri","virii"],"pos":"noun","zh":"計算機病毒","explanation":"指能隱藏在電腦或檔案中，並透過網路、檔案或可移動儲存裝置傳播的惡意程式，常會破壞資料或系統。它沿用了生物病毒“進入宿主並複製傳播”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The attachment contained a computer virus.","zh":"這個附件裡含有計算機病毒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The virus spread from one computer to another through a USB drive.","zh":"這個病毒透過優盤從一臺電腦傳播到了另一臺電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/virus","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e759968ca9278b8dde9f","word":"visa","forms":["visa"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-32077e5d5447d4bc","term":"visa","forms":["visa","visas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"簽證","explanation":"由目的地國家的有關部門簽發、允許某人進入或離開該國的官方許可，通常會附在護照上或與護照關聯。","examples":[{"en":"I need a visa to visit Canada.","zh":"我去加拿大需要簽證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She applied for a six-month tourist visa.","zh":"她申請了六個月的旅遊簽證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2646358f98675f09","term":"visa","forms":["visa","Visas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"Visa信用卡","explanation":"指Visa公司發行或使用Visa支付網路的信用卡；重點是這張卡屬於Visa品牌。","examples":[{"en":"Can I pay with my Visa?","zh":"我可以用Visa卡付款嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He paid for the booking with his Visa.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d42ef1497900bc6e542c","word":"visible","forms":["visible"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-94bcff8dbde41e0f","term":"visible","forms":["visible","more visible","most visible"],"pos":"adj","zh":"看得見的","explanation":"表示某物能被眼睛看到；如果光線變強、遮擋移開或距離合適，原本不易察覺的東西也可能變得 visible。","examples":[{"en":"When the sun rises, the mountains become visible.","zh":"太陽昇起時，群山顯現出來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The label is clearly visible from across the room.","zh":"從房間的另一頭也能清楚地看見標籤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visible","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5944ae849448011ca08c","word":"vision","forms":["vision"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6336c779c731bbcb","term":"vision","forms":["vision","visions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"視覺；視力","explanation":"vision 可以指人用眼睛看東西的能力，也就是視覺或視力。這是“看見的能力”這一核心意義。","examples":[{"en":"Her vision has improved since she started wearing glasses.","zh":"她戴眼鏡後視力有所改善。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The surgery restored much of her vision.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7d1971dc4d889a05","term":"vision","forms":["vision","visions"],"pos":"noun","zh":"願景；理想目標","explanation":"把心裡的未來畫面變成想努力實現的方向，就是 vision 的“願景”或“理想目標”意義，常用於個人、組織和社會。","examples":[{"en":"The team shares a vision for cleaner and safer cities.","zh":"這個團隊有一個讓城市更清潔、更安全的共同願景。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She turned her vision into a successful business.","zh":"她把自己的願景變成了一家成功的企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vision","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0e68ac26df2184062ae","word":"visit","forms":["visit"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d9b0baea8de9cfa1","term":"visit","forms":["visit","visits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次拜訪或走訪","explanation":"指親自到某人那裡或某處去的一次行動，重點是“去那裡看望、相聚或走訪”這一件事。","examples":[{"en":"We had a lovely visit with our neighbors last night.","zh":"昨晚我們和鄰居愉快地聚了一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our visit to the museum lasted two hours.","zh":"我們參觀博物館用了兩個小時。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45412f08f123630d","term":"visit","forms":["visit","visits","visiting","visited","visitest","visitedst","visiteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拜訪某人","explanation":"指為了友好相聚、聊天或探望而去見某人，就是把“走到某人那裡”作為拜訪來做。","examples":[{"en":"I’m going to visit my grandparents this weekend.","zh":"這個週末我要去看望祖父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She visited her old friend after work.","zh":"她下班後去拜訪了老朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-00b56667ff7798bb","term":"visit","forms":["visit","visits","visiting","visited","visitest","visitedst","visiteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參觀或走訪某地","explanation":"指為了遊玩、辦事、檢視或瞭解情況而去某個地方；核心仍是“親自走到那裡去看”。","examples":[{"en":"We visited several small towns along the coast.","zh":"我們走訪了沿海的幾個小鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The manager visited the factory to check the new equipment.","zh":"經理到工廠檢視了新裝置。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5f14f9e6d80f802a6526","word":"visitor","forms":["visitor"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-861315bc51f3f1d7","term":"visitor","forms":["visitor","visitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拜訪某人的人；訪客","explanation":"指從外面來到某人身邊拜訪，或暫時作為客人待在某處的人。重點是“來訪”這一動作，不一定涉及旅遊或觀光。","examples":[{"en":"We have a visitor from the museum this afternoon.","zh":"今天下午博物館會來一位訪客。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our visitors stayed for dinner.","zh":"來訪的客人留下來吃了晚飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b37d5abc3a49e106","term":"visitor","forms":["visitor","visitors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"到某地或活動現場參觀的人","explanation":"指特意到某個地方、展覽或活動現場看一看的人，可以是遊客，也可以只是當地的參觀者。這裡的核心仍是“從外面來到這個地點”。","examples":[{"en":"The museum welcomes visitors throughout the year.","zh":"這座博物館全年歡迎參觀者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Visitors must sign in at the reception desk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visitor","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5961f3f5ac8a594d1c0","word":"visual","forms":["visual"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16ae9a8bbb2b095b","term":"visual","forms":["visual","more visual","most visual"],"pos":"adj","zh":"視覺的；與視覺有關的","explanation":"指和眼睛看到的東西、視覺感知或影象呈現有關。它可以描述視覺資訊、視覺背景，也可以說明某種效果主要靠看而不是靠聽來理解。","examples":[{"en":"The museum uses visual displays to explain the history of the city.","zh":"這家博物館用視覺展示來講解這座城市的歷史。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The animal relies on visual signals to find its group.","zh":"這種動物依靠視覺訊號尋找自己的群體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/visual","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-39ca0c269f8be5cbe8ac","word":"vital","forms":["vital"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-214d6cc086611b61","term":"vital","forms":["vital","more vital","most vital"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生命的；與生命有關的","explanation":"指直接屬於生命活動或人體生命機能的事物，是“生命這臺機器”本身的組成部分。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise helps maintain vital functions.","zh":"規律運動有助於維持生命機能。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The monitor records the patient's vital functions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3fe32cb1b1a78f2f","term":"vital","forms":["vital","more vital","most vital"],"pos":"adj","zh":"維持生命所必需的","explanation":"指某個器官、物質或條件是生命能夠繼續的關鍵，缺少它就可能無法正常生存。","examples":[{"en":"The heart is a vital organ.","zh":"心臟是維持生命的重要器官。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Oxygen is vital to the functioning of the brain.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4553ad8863eb2b07","term":"vital","forms":["vital","more vital","most vital"],"pos":"adj","zh":"生存或延續所必需的","explanation":"從“維持生命”擴大到維持社會、制度、計劃或其他事物繼續存在；它是整體能否延續的關鍵。","examples":[{"en":"Clean water is vital to the survival of the community.","zh":"清潔的水對這個社群的生存至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Regular maintenance is vital for keeping the lift safe.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2b4ee7fb57f0321","term":"vital","forms":["vital","more vital","most vital"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極其重要的","explanation":"表示某件事對結果、計劃或行動成敗非常關鍵，就像生命依賴它一樣；這是現代英語中很常用的引申義。","examples":[{"en":"It is vital that you save your work before closing the program.","zh":"關閉程式前儲存工作非常重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Clear communication is vital to the team's success.","zh":"清晰的溝通對團隊成功至關重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vital","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9609a9ac960097e3258c","word":"vitality","forms":["vitality"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-44771ac346d40b2f","term":"vitality","forms":["vitality","vitalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"生命力；生存和發展的能力","explanation":"指生命體維持自身、繼續生長和發展的能力，重點是“能活下去並不斷成長”的內在力量。這種生命力可以用於人、動物、植物，也可以比喻某個社會、傳統或事業。","examples":[{"en":"The vitality of the old forest depends on clean water and healthy soil.","zh":"這片老森林的生命力取決於潔淨的水和健康的土壤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The festival has given new vitality to the small town.","zh":"這個節日給這座小鎮注入了新的活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vitality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6b2ca23b9b70446","term":"vitality","forms":["vitality","vitalities"],"pos":"noun","zh":"活力；精力；朝氣","explanation":"指一個人或群體表現出來的旺盛精力、熱情和行動力，能讓人感到它充滿朝氣。這個意思比單純的體力更寬，常包含精神狀態和感染力。","examples":[{"en":"Despite her age, she spoke with remarkable vitality.","zh":"儘管年事已高，她說話時仍充滿驚人的活力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her vitality returned after several restful weeks.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vitality","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed31e03af5ae5ef07979","word":"vitamin","forms":["vitamin"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6592882cfe825bec","term":"vitamin","forms":["vitamin","vitamins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"維生素","explanation":"維生素是身體只需少量卻不可缺少的有機物，幫助維持生長、代謝和正常身體功能；不同維生素不足會造成不同問題。它就是“生命所需的一小點補給”。","examples":[{"en":"Carrots are rich in vitamins that support healthy vision.","zh":"胡蘿蔔富含有助於保持視力健康的維生素。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The doctor said I should get more vitamin D during the winter.","zh":"醫生說我冬天應該多攝取一些維生素D。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vitamin","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-685ee53b55aa432dc847","word":"vivid","forms":["vivid"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1fef96b38b075cf","term":"vivid","forms":["vivid","more vivid","vivider","most vivid","vividest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"清晰生動的","explanation":"形容畫面、記憶、想象或描述中的細節非常清楚具體，彷彿能直接看見或感受到。它體現的是那幅“活起來的畫面”的清晰度和感染力。","examples":[{"en":"She has a vivid memory of her first day at school.","zh":"她對自己上學第一天的經歷記憶非常清晰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book gives a vivid picture of life in the city.","zh":"這本書生動地描繪了城市裡的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vivid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7000330a1307b95","term":"vivid","forms":["vivid","more vivid","vivider","most vivid","vividest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"鮮豔強烈的","explanation":"形容顏色、光線或視覺效果明亮而強烈，非常醒目，就像畫面中的某個部分突然被突出顯示。","examples":[{"en":"The artist used vivid colors to paint the birds.","zh":"那位畫家用鮮豔的顏色描繪這些鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Vivid green parrots filled the branches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vivid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0c7e0de28a70f3c4f8d9","word":"vocabulary","forms":["vocabulary"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-56f84d1d61873af8","term":"vocabulary","forms":["vocabulary","vocabularies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詞表；詞彙表","explanation":"指把某個領域、主題或學習目的所需的詞集中整理並加以說明的一組詞，可以理解為一份專門的“詞彙庫”。","examples":[{"en":"The teacher gave us a vocabulary of words for describing weather.","zh":"老師給了我們一份描寫天氣的詞彙表。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The chapter ends with a vocabulary of nautical terms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocabulary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-caac249adfbb491d","term":"vocabulary","forms":["vocabulary","vocabularies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人詞彙量","explanation":"指某個人認識、理解並在說話或寫作中使用的詞彙總量；詞彙庫越大，通常能表達的內容就越豐富。","examples":[{"en":"Reading every day has greatly expanded her vocabulary.","zh":"每天閱讀大大豐富了她的詞彙量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My Russian vocabulary is very limited.","zh":"我的俄語詞彙量很有限。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocabulary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96a6b83f147c7d8b9c4f","word":"vocal","forms":["vocal"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5b44d59c492824b","term":"vocal","forms":["vocal","more vocal","most vocal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"聲音的；與人聲有關的","explanation":"表示和人的聲音、說話或發聲器官有關，核心畫面就是“從嘴裡發出的聲音”。例如，vocal problems 指發聲或嗓音方面的問題。","examples":[{"en":"The singer is taking a break because of vocal problems.","zh":"這位歌手因為嗓音問題正在休息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The singer rested to protect her vocal cords.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36cac3403ba7c332","term":"vocal","forms":["vocal","more vocal","most vocal"],"pos":"adj","zh":"用聲音表達的；聲樂的","explanation":"表示內容是透過說話、吟唱或其他發聲方式表達出來的，而不是只寫在紙上或只用樂器演奏；在音樂中尤其常指“聲樂的”。","examples":[{"en":"The song combines a soft vocal melody with electronic sounds.","zh":"這首歌把柔和的人聲旋律和電子音效結合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The singer practices vocal exercises every morning.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e541f9e0bb55c739","term":"vocal","forms":["vocal","vocals"],"pos":"noun","zh":"歌曲中的聲樂部分","explanation":"指一首音樂作品中由人唱出來的部分，也就是和器樂伴奏相對的人聲段落。它把 vocal 的“用聲音發出”直接延伸到了歌曲中。","examples":[{"en":"The vocals are clear even when the guitar gets louder.","zh":"即使吉他聲變大，人聲仍然很清晰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The producer recorded the vocals separately from the instruments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74e9efa7126bfe2e8009","word":"vocation","forms":["vocation"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cf5f5c269daa10f8","term":"vocation","forms":["vocation","vocations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"宗教或人生召喚","explanation":"指一種被上帝、信仰或內心認為召喚去承擔的人生道路，常用來解釋一個人為何選擇獨身、婚姻生活、神職等生活方式。這裡的重點不是普通興趣，而是把某種生活看成自己的使命。","examples":[{"en":"She felt that religious life was her vocation.","zh":"她覺得宗教生活是上帝召喚她走上的人生道路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He believed marriage was his vocation.","zh":"他相信婚姻生活是自己應當承擔的人生使命。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dad68f256f9ca94c","term":"vocation","forms":["vocation","vocations"],"pos":"noun","zh":"適合自己的職業","explanation":"指一個人憑藉能力、訓練或性格而適合從事的職業，尤其暗示這份工作不只是謀生手段，也是個人願意長期投入的方向。它正是從“被召喚去承擔某種人生道路”引申出來的。","examples":[{"en":"Teaching is a vocation that requires patience and dedication.","zh":"教學是一種需要耐心和奉獻精神的職業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She found her true vocation in nursing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocation","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cfc3eea2eae69d789db6","word":"vocational","forms":["vocational"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e42eb18c397d501","term":"vocational","forms":["vocational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"職業的；與職業有關的","explanation":"表示某事與一個人的職業、職業選擇或職業道路有關。它關注的是“以什麼職業為方向”，而不一定專指培訓或學校教育。","examples":[{"en":"The counselor helped students make informed vocational choices.","zh":"輔導員幫助學生作出明智的職業選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The college provides vocational training in electrical installation.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-507c0e8d599da6fa","term":"vocational","forms":["vocational"],"pos":"adj","zh":"職業技能培訓的；偏實用技能的","explanation":"特指為某種具體工作提供實用技能的教育或培訓。它與 academic 相對，重點不是抽象的學術知識，而是讓學習者能夠從事一項職業。","examples":[{"en":"She enrolled in a vocational program to train as an electrician.","zh":"她參加了一個職業培訓專案，學習成為電工。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Vocational training can help young people find work quickly.","zh":"職業培訓可以幫助年輕人更快找到工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vocational","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c57d7e92019708b614c9","word":"voice","forms":["voice"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b3efe87a8b6d321","term":"voice","forms":["voice","voices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人的聲音","explanation":"指人說話或唱歌時從口中發出的聲音，也可以強調這種聲音獨特的音色或特點。","examples":[{"en":"I recognized her voice immediately on the phone.","zh":"我在電話裡立刻聽出了她的聲音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His voice filled the small room.","zh":"他的聲音充滿了小房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bab2655366aac095","term":"voice","forms":["voice","voices"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意見、選擇或發言權","explanation":"指一個人表達意見、意願或選擇，也指這種意見受到重視的權利；所以“有 voice”就是有機會讓別人聽見並考慮自己的立場。","examples":[{"en":"Every student should have a voice in the decision.","zh":"每個學生都應該在這項決定中有發言權。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report gives a voice to people who are often ignored.","zh":"這份報告讓那些常被忽視的人有機會發聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voice","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-06612c2832341c9e69c8","word":"volcano","forms":["volcano"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16b8053216023f25","term":"volcano","forms":["volcano","volcanoes","volcanos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"火山","explanation":"指地表上的裂口或通道，通常呈山狀，並與地下的岩漿相連；它會週期性地把熔岩和火山氣體噴到地面上。","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are monitoring the volcano because it has started releasing more gas.","zh":"科學家正在監測這座火山，因為它開始釋放更多氣體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volcano sent ash high above the island.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volcano","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b086a22984221049","term":"volcano","forms":["volcano","volcanoes","volcanos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"噴火花煙火","explanation":"指一種會向上噴出一束火花的煙火，外形或效果像一座小型火山。","examples":[{"en":"We put a small volcano in the garden and lit it after sunset.","zh":"太陽落山後，我們在花園裡點燃了一個小型噴火花煙火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children watched the volcano scatter sparks across the patio.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volcano","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3580c9267518807d1480","word":"volleyball","forms":["volleyball"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3e6a1e62127f1bcc","term":"volleyball","forms":["volleyball","volleyballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排球運動","explanation":"一種隔著球網、由兩隊把球來回擊過球網的球類運動；這裡說的是比賽或運動本身，不是某一個球。","examples":[{"en":"My sister plays volleyball at school.","zh":"我妹妹在學校打排球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We watched a volleyball match last night.","zh":"我們昨晚看了一場排球比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volleyball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-580a1d1f0db386dd","term":"volleyball","forms":["volleyball","volleyballs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"排球","explanation":"指排球運動中被隊員擊打、在球網上方來回飛的那個球。","examples":[{"en":"The volleyball landed outside the court.","zh":"排球落在了場外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volleyball rolled beneath the bleachers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volleyball","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-62d7a6b1211d627650e2","word":"volume","forms":["volume"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-33c7b255c4e1ca7f","term":"volume","forms":["volume","volumes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"體積","explanation":"指一個物體或空間所佔的三維大小，也就是長度、寬度和高度共同形成的空間大小。","examples":[{"en":"The volume of the box is two cubic meters.","zh":"這個箱子的體積是兩立方米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We calculated the volume of water in the tank.","zh":"我們計算了水箱中水的體積。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-66b121848286bd53","term":"volume","forms":["volume","volumes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"音量","explanation":"指聲音聽起來有多大，尤其常用於收音機、電視、音樂播放器或電腦的聲音大小。","examples":[{"en":"Could you turn down the volume? I'm trying to read.","zh":"你能把音量調小一點嗎？我正想看書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The music was so loud that I lowered the volume.","zh":"音樂太大聲了，所以我把音量調低了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volume","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-347a5faf2ae6ce14e420","word":"voluntary","forms":["voluntary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19a4a94c47c60409","term":"voluntary","forms":["voluntary","more voluntary","most voluntary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自願的；出於本人意願的","explanation":"指行為、決定或給予是本人主動選擇的，不是被命令、脅迫或強制完成的。這是該詞最核心的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Attendance at the workshop is voluntary.","zh":"參加這個研討會完全自願。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She made a voluntary donation to the shelter.","zh":"她自願向那家收容所捐了款。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voluntary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ca3e1ebb899ce26f","term":"voluntary","forms":["voluntary","more voluntary","most voluntary"],"pos":"adj","zh":"故意的；有意的","explanation":"強調某個動作是有意識、按意圖做出的，而不是意外發生的。它仍然和“自己作出選擇”這個核心概念相連，但在法律或正式論述中尤其常見。","examples":[{"en":"The damage was the result of a voluntary act, not an accident.","zh":"這起損壞是有意造成的，並非意外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The court distinguished a voluntary act from an accidental movement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voluntary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dcbb0f3cafb30402d5ed","word":"volunteer","forms":["volunteer"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fbb01e100791797f","term":"volunteer","forms":["volunteer","volunteers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"志願者","explanation":"指不是被強迫、而是主動提供時間和精力來服務或幫忙的人，通常沒有報酬，但是否無償要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers at the animal shelter feed the cats every morning.","zh":"動物收容所的志願者每天早上給貓餵食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A volunteer showed us where to leave donations.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volunteer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-719291ecfd82bdbe","term":"volunteer","forms":["volunteer","volunteers","volunteering","volunteered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"主動提出做某事","explanation":"指沒有被要求，卻主動表示願意做某事；核心仍是那隻主動舉起的手。","examples":[{"en":"I volunteered to wash the dishes after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我主動提出洗碗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He volunteered to drive the visitors to their hotel.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volunteer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5ebdc7b074ec1caeffc7","word":"vomit","forms":["vomit"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2aa60c64f1d646da","term":"vomit","forms":["vomit","vomits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嘔吐物","explanation":"指從胃裡吐出來的東西，也就是嘔吐後留下的物質；它是“把胃裡的東西推出去”這一核心畫面留下的結果。","examples":[{"en":"Someone had left vomit on the bathroom floor.","zh":"有人把嘔吐物留在了浴室地板上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The nurse cleaned the vomit from the floor.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vomit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1b78e1c1336e245c","term":"vomit","forms":["vomit","vomits","vomiting","vomited"],"pos":"verb","zh":"嘔吐","explanation":"指把胃裡的東西透過嘴吐出來，是這個詞最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"She vomited after eating the spoiled seafood.","zh":"她吃了變質的海鮮後嘔吐了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child began to vomit during the journey.","zh":"孩子在旅途中開始嘔吐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vomit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ab274474a6aa82c100dd","word":"vote","forms":["vote"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-49bf1798e1011ee0","term":"vote","forms":["vote","votes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"正式表決；投票選擇","explanation":"指在選舉、議會、委員會或其他正式程式中，對某個方案、職位或爭議事項作出的選擇。這裡的重點是“透過投票作出決定”，而不是泛泛地表達個人看法。","examples":[{"en":"The committee will hold a vote on the new safety rules tomorrow.","zh":"委員會明天將就新的安全規則進行表決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The proposal passed by a narrow vote.","zh":"這項提案以微弱優勢透過了表決。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c24de43553569718","term":"vote","forms":["vote","votes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一票；投票行為","explanation":"指某人實際參與正式選擇的行為，或指這個行為本身的一票。它強調“參加表決並提交選擇”，也可以在上下文中表示一個人擁有的投票權或一票的分量。","examples":[{"en":"Every eligible citizen has a vote in the election.","zh":"每位符合資格的公民在這次選舉中都有一票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cast her vote before leaving for work.","zh":"她在上班前投下了自己的一票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f6f37722bf66db5e","term":"vote","forms":["vote","votes","voting","voted","votest","votedst","voteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投票；參加選舉","explanation":"指親自參加選舉或正式表決並作出選擇。它強調行動本身，而不是投下的那一票或最後的表決結果。","examples":[{"en":"Did you vote in the local election last month?","zh":"你上個月參加地方選舉投票了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most employees voted against the proposed schedule.","zh":"大多數員工投票反對擬議的日程安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-922c26595484b576","term":"vote","forms":["vote","votes","voting","voted","votest","votedst","voteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"投票選出；表決透過","explanation":"指透過投票或全體同意來選擇某人、授予某種職位，或批准某項安排。與只說“參加投票”不同，這個義項強調投票所產生的選擇結果。","examples":[{"en":"The board voted Maria chair of the committee.","zh":"董事會投票選瑪麗亞擔任委員會主席。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Members voted to approve the revised budget.","zh":"成員們投票批准了修訂後的預算。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vote","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-566e3a030b0f7c78286a","word":"voter","forms":["voter"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-74b17aa1aaa3bf41","term":"voter","forms":["voter","voters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"投票者；選民","explanation":"指實際參加投票、用選票表達選擇的人；在選舉語境中通常可譯為“選民”。","examples":[{"en":"Every voter should learn about the candidates before the election.","zh":"每位選民都應該在選舉前瞭解各位候選人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Many voters are concerned about the rising cost of living.","zh":"許多選民都在關注不斷上漲的生活成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8923fedfd16a77b1fe21","word":"voucher","forms":["voucher"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2681a674f9e2a606","term":"voucher","forms":["voucher","vouchers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"代金券；兌換券","explanation":"一張可以換取商品或服務、享受折扣，或代表某項權益的憑證；重點在於它能讓持有人兌現某種價值。","examples":[{"en":"They gave us a voucher for a free breakfast.","zh":"他們給了我們一張免費早餐兌換券。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I received a gift voucher for my birthday.","zh":"我生日時收到了一張禮品代金券。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voucher","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85da2ed4b4c3d9efad8d","word":"vow","forms":["vow"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bf74ff4e1bbb0cbe","term":"vow","forms":["vow","vows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"誓言；誓願","explanation":"指一個人鄭重承諾今後要做某事，或要按照某種方式生活，尤其常用於宗教誓願。","examples":[{"en":"The monk took a vow of silence.","zh":"那名僧人立下了沉默的誓言。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They made a vow to support each other through difficult times.","zh":"他們發誓要在困難時期互相支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c5d21f6739a3d9c1","term":"vow","forms":["vow","vows","vowing","vowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發誓；承諾","explanation":"指鄭重地作出誓言，承諾自己將做某事或遵守某種行為準則。","examples":[{"en":"She vowed to protect her younger brother.","zh":"她發誓要保護弟弟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new leader vowed to rebuild the city.","zh":"新任領導人承諾要重建這座城市。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-59981069c56a2c667397","word":"vowel","forms":["vowel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-76946ea5d16d25ac","term":"vowel","forms":["vowel","vowels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"母音（聲音）","explanation":"指發音時氣流在口腔中受到的阻礙較小、通常能成為音節核心的聲音。它是“聲音通道較開闊”的那一部分，而不是表示該聲音的書寫符號。","examples":[{"en":"The first sound in “apple” is a vowel.","zh":"“apple”的第一個音是母音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This language has five basic vowel sounds.","zh":"這種語言有五個基本母音。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vowel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1f130855438a411","term":"vowel","forms":["vowel","vowels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"母音字母","explanation":"指書面上代表母音聲音的字母或附加符號。英語學習中通常先把 a、e、i、o、u 作為母音字母來記，但具體語言的規則可能不同，某些字母在特定位置也能表示母音。","examples":[{"en":"The word “team” has two vowel letters.","zh":"單詞“team”裡有兩個母音字母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write each vowel in red and each consonant in black.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vowel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-763268b8dbdcf3275705","word":"voyage","forms":["voyage"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c52605253670f3e","term":"voyage","forms":["voyage","voyages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"長途旅行；航行","explanation":"指一次較長的旅程，尤其是乘船在海上或沿水路進行的旅行；重點是路程長、過程較完整，而不只是一次普通出門。","examples":[{"en":"They went on a voyage across the Atlantic.","zh":"他們進行了一次橫跨大西洋的航行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young sailor dreamed of a voyage to distant islands.","zh":"那個年輕水手夢想著航行到遙遠的島嶼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voyage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4886c340bfb06d56","term":"voyage","forms":["voyage","voyages","voyaging","voyaged","voyagest","voyagedst","voyageth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"進行長途旅行","explanation":"表示親自踏上並進行一次較長的旅程，尤其是乘船遠行；也可在文學中比喻思想或想象在陌生領域中探索。","examples":[{"en":"The explorers voyaged south in search of new islands.","zh":"探險家們向南航行，尋找新的島嶼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her imagination voyaged through worlds no one had seen.","zh":"她的想象力漫遊在無人見過的世界中。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voyage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[112,115],"total":2,"counts":{"112":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-f2b826b18b9de86628dd","word":"vulnerable","forms":["vulnerable"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64916e9a18fc8aa9","term":"vulnerable","forms":["vulnerable","more vulnerable","most vulnerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易受傷害的","explanation":"指一個人或群體容易受到身體、情感或其他方面的傷害，因此處在較不安全、較需要保護的位置。重點是“容易成為傷害的物件”，不等於已經受傷，也不一定表示這個人沒有力量。","examples":[{"en":"Children are especially vulnerable to online bullying.","zh":"兒童尤其容易受到網路欺凌的傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt vulnerable after sharing her private thoughts.","zh":"她分享了自己的私密想法後，感到自己很容易受到傷害。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vulnerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7a2ae04923710be7","term":"vulnerable","forms":["vulnerable","more vulnerable","most vulnerable"],"pos":"adj","zh":"容易遭受網路攻擊的","explanation":"用於電腦、網路或軟體時，指它存在容易被惡意程式、病毒或攻擊利用的薄弱點。這裡的“薄弱處”不一定是裝置已經出問題，而是說明它缺乏足夠的保護。","examples":[{"en":"The old server is vulnerable to cyberattacks.","zh":"這臺舊伺服器容易受到網路攻擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Weak passwords make otherwise secure accounts vulnerable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vulnerable","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6e75f2b67fc2de6283a3","word":"wag","forms":["wag"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8ba2b4b383a39609","term":"wag","forms":["wag","wags"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擺動","explanation":"指某個部位或物體左右、前後反覆擺動的動作，核心畫面就是尾巴不停地搖。","examples":[{"en":"The wag of her dog's tail showed that he was happy.","zh":"她的狗不停搖尾巴，表明它很高興。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"One wag of the dog's tail cleared the table.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-138362b2eb525ec7","term":"wag","forms":["wag","wags","wagging","wagged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"來回擺動","explanation":"指動物的尾巴、人的頭等部位左右來回擺動，常用動作表達態度或情緒；這就是整個詞最核心的“擺動”畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The puppy wagged its tail when I came home.","zh":"我回家時，小狗搖起了尾巴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wagged her head in disbelief.","zh":"她難以置信地搖了搖頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wag","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-86eb1a98dbc5e4a65034","word":"wage(s)","forms":["wage","wages"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0e48146c9c63ccac","term":"wage","forms":["wage","wages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工資；薪酬","explanation":"指勞動者完成一定工作後得到的錢，常按工作時間或工作量計算。它體現了“用勞動換取報酬”這一核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Many workers depend on their weekly wages to pay the bills.","zh":"許多工人靠每週的工資支付各種賬單。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The factory raised hourly wages after the negotiations.","zh":"談判後，這家工廠提高了小時工資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wage","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f989010bbdd0604","term":"wages","forms":["wages"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工資總額","explanation":"指某人在一段時間內掙得的全部工資，重點是把多次或一段時期的收入合在一起看，而不是某一次單獨的發薪。","examples":[{"en":"Her weekly wages are paid every Friday.","zh":"她每週的工資總額每週五發放。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company spends half its revenue on wages.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wages","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-baf6a0b70ab07cf16c76","word":"wagon","forms":["wagon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c4bc6cb0064e6eca","term":"wagon","forms":["wagon","wagons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"四輪貨車；馬車","explanation":"一種通常有四個輪子、用來載貨，有時也載人的較重車輛；傳統上常由馬拉動。","examples":[{"en":"The farmers loaded the wagon with sacks of grain.","zh":"農民們把一袋袋糧食裝上了貨車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A horse pulled the wagon slowly up the hill.","zh":"一匹馬拉著貨車慢慢上山。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wagon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e69becfc95e8cca8","term":"wagon","forms":["wagon","wagons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"兒童拖車","explanation":"指孩子坐在裡面、由人用前面的長柄拉動或控制的小車，是大車概念的縮小版。","examples":[{"en":"The children took turns riding in the little wagon.","zh":"孩子們輪流坐進那輛小拖車裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children pulled their toys in a little red wagon.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wagon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c2456b99b9b7ff36169","word":"waist","forms":["waist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-90e6cb51c3fbd6c3","term":"waist","forms":["waist","waists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人體的腰部","explanation":"指身體中部、胃部和骨盆之間的腰部，是人體把上身和下身連線起來的部分。","examples":[{"en":"She put her hands on her waist and took a deep breath.","zh":"她把雙手放在腰上，深深地吸了一口氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This exercise can strengthen your waist and back.","zh":"這項運動可以增強你的腰部和背部力量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d15a414d059d6e19","term":"waist","forms":["waist","waists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"衣服的腰部","explanation":"指裙子、褲子等衣物覆蓋或收束在腰部的那一段，也可指衣物的腰圍尺寸。","examples":[{"en":"The waist of these trousers is too loose for me.","zh":"這條褲子的腰對我來說太鬆了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dress is too tight at the waist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-716ecabb45ac6a88a049","word":"wait","forms":["wait"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5b0c7d2a6caee467","term":"wait","forms":["wait","waits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"等待；等候時間","explanation":"指從現在開始到某人或某事發生之間的一段等待時間，重點是“暫停後守著結果出現”。","examples":[{"en":"There was a long wait at the doctor's office.","zh":"在醫生診室等了很長時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We faced a forty-minute wait at the border.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91ec2c97438b9b62","term":"wait","forms":["wait","waits","waiting","waited","waitest","waitedst","waiteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"等待；等到","explanation":"暫時不行動，留在某處或保持準備，直到某個時間、事件或人到來。這是 wait 最核心的動詞意義。","examples":[{"en":"Please wait here until your name is called.","zh":"請在這裡等到有人叫你的名字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We waited for the bus in the rain.","zh":"我們在雨中等公共汽車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wait","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c92cb7721fc406beccb1","word":"waiter/waitress","forms":["waiter","waitress"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0cbd376abab680c6","term":"waiter","forms":["waiter","waiters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"餐館服務員","explanation":"在餐館、咖啡館等場所，waiter是在桌邊等候顧客、記錄點單並負責上菜等服務的人。這個詞的核心畫面就是一個隨時照應顧客需要的服務員。","examples":[{"en":"The waiter brought us the menu and a glass of water.","zh":"服務員給我們拿來了選單和一杯水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We asked the waiter for the bill.","zh":"我們請服務員拿賬單來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waiter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3dadfe135f400272","term":"waitress","forms":["waitress","waitresses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女服務員","explanation":"指在餐館、咖啡館或類似場所為顧客點單、上菜和提供服務的女性。","examples":[{"en":"The waitress brought us two menus and a glass of water.","zh":"女服務員給我們拿來了兩份選單和一杯水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The waitress brought our drinks to the terrace.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waitress","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-51391bf0ab33e8272bcf","word":"wake","forms":["wake"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a22817b80bb3ad68","term":"wake","forms":["wake","wakes","waking","woke","waked","woken","wakest","wokest","waketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"醒來","explanation":"wake 表示從睡眠中醒來，也就是自己停止睡覺。它描述主語的狀態變化，不需要另帶賓語。","examples":[{"en":"I usually wake up before my alarm.","zh":"我通常在鬧鐘響之前就醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She woke at dawn and opened the curtains.","zh":"她黎明時醒來，拉開了窗簾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c655b6c2b6822f82","term":"wake","forms":["wake","wakes","waking","woke","waked","woken","wakest","wokest","waketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"叫醒","explanation":"wake 也表示讓別人從睡眠中醒來，即把某人叫醒。","examples":[{"en":"Please wake me up at seven tomorrow.","zh":"請明天七點叫醒我。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The thunder woke the baby up.","zh":"雷聲把嬰兒吵醒了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wake","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-956f449b842b0f2cba37","word":"waken","forms":["waken"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"waken","forms":["waken"],"pos":"v.","zh":"喚醒；醒來","examples":[{"en":"Please do not waken the children before seven.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The smell of fresh bread can waken even the sleepiest guest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-7a6c4fac6c5cd7209ee2","word":"walk","forms":["walk"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1140d0989bd2b51","term":"walk","forms":["walk","walks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"散步；步行一趟","explanation":"walk 可以指一次以走路為主的外出或活動，也就是“散步、走一走”；記住腳步向前移動，就像把這段移動本身當作一次 walk。","examples":[{"en":"I take a walk every morning before work.","zh":"我每天早晨上班前散步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We went for a short walk after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們去短暫散了會兒步。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2601597d3b245ea4","term":"walk","forms":["walk","walks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"步道；人行道","explanation":"walk 還可以指專門供人行走的道路或小徑，是“腳步向前移動”所依靠的地方，例如花園中的步道或路旁的人行道。","examples":[{"en":"A narrow stone walk leads from the gate to the house.","zh":"一條狹窄的石頭小路從大門通向房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The garden walk was covered with fallen leaves.","zh":"花園小徑上鋪滿了落葉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1660946a6e48c641","term":"walk","forms":["walk","walks","walking","walked","walkest","walkedst","walketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"走路；步行","explanation":"指用腳一步一步向前移動，通常始終至少有一隻腳著地；這正是記憶鉤子中“腳步向前移動”的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"I walk to work every morning.","zh":"我每天早上步行去上班。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She walked slowly along the beach.","zh":"她沿著海灘慢慢走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-80088caec6cb16a5","term":"walk","forms":["walk","walks","walking","walked","walkest","walkedst","walketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"步行經過一段路","explanation":"指透過走路 traversing 一段距離或路線；也就是把“腳步向前移動”延伸到完整的一段路程。","examples":[{"en":"We walked three kilometers to the station.","zh":"我們步行了三公里到車站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He walks the same route every day.","zh":"他每天都走同一條路線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4d8aaa64f68587b18e27","word":"wall","forms":["wall"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-395afc5d89b0df31","term":"wall","forms":["wall","walls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築物的牆","explanation":"指建築物外部的牆，或把室內空間分隔開的牆；這是最基本的“擋住並分隔”的實體牆。","examples":[{"en":"We painted the living-room walls light blue.","zh":"我們把客廳的牆刷成了淺藍色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A thin wall separates my office from the kitchen.","zh":"一面薄牆把我的辦公室和廚房隔開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21caed29a5726cab","term":"wall","forms":["wall","walls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"阻礙行動的屏障","explanation":"指擋住人或事物自由移動的實體障礙，核心仍是“牆把路擋住了”，不一定真的是磚石牆。","examples":[{"en":"A wall of police blocked the protesters from entering the building.","zh":"一道人牆擋住了抗議者，不讓他們進入大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fallen trees formed a wall across the road.","zh":"倒下的樹木在路上形成了一道屏障。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-43e59c0566ac903f","term":"wall","forms":["wall","walls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"屏障","explanation":"泛指起阻擋作用的屏障，常見於複合詞中，如擋海水的海堤或隔離網路攻擊的防火牆。它把“牆”的擋住功能擴充套件到了不同材料和用途。","examples":[{"en":"The seawall protects the houses from high waves.","zh":"海堤保護房屋免受巨浪侵襲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Fear had built a wall between the two families.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e8d44050873dba865aa7","word":"wallet","forms":["wallet"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-35dc567497515514","term":"wallet","forms":["wallet","wallets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"錢包","explanation":"指通常較扁、用來裝現金、銀行卡和身份證等物品的小包，是這個詞最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I keep my driver's license in my wallet.","zh":"我把駕照放在錢包裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She left her wallet on the kitchen table.","zh":"她把錢包落在廚房桌上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wallet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28514cdc80f11f00","term":"wallet","forms":["wallet","wallets"],"pos":"noun","zh":"經濟能力；錢袋子","explanation":"把錢包看作一個人能拿出來的錢，因此可借指個人的財產或經濟狀況，尤其常表示某件事會不會讓人破財。","examples":[{"en":"The expensive repairs really hit me in the wallet.","zh":"昂貴的維修費確實讓我破了一筆財。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new tax will hit motorists' wallets.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wallet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3748fbd132cd645a3756","word":"walnut","forms":["walnut"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f1110f9426e70f22","term":"walnut","forms":["walnut","walnuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"核桃樹","explanation":"指結核桃的樹，強調的是植物本身，而不是樹上的果實。這個意義把 walnut 的其他意義串在一起：樹結出核桃，並提供核桃木。","examples":[{"en":"The old walnut in our garden gives us plenty of shade.","zh":"我們花園裡的那棵老核桃樹為我們提供了大片陰涼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The walnut shades almost the entire back garden.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5d414eed454a0d6a","term":"walnut","forms":["walnut","walnuts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"核桃","explanation":"指核桃樹結出的堅果，通常指帶殼或泛指這種果實。日常語境中這是最常見的理解。","examples":[{"en":"She cracked a walnut and added the pieces to the salad.","zh":"她敲開一個核桃，把核桃仁碎塊加進了沙拉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Crush the walnuts before folding them into the batter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walnut","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33430ae3a73f5974d083","word":"wander","forms":["wander"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-594182c64c97a29a","term":"wander","forms":["wander","wanders","wandering","wandered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"漫遊；閒逛","explanation":"指沒有明確目的地或固定路線地走動，常帶有隨意、慢慢探索的感覺；有時也指為了謀生而四處奔走。","examples":[{"en":"They wandered through the market until they found a quiet café.","zh":"他們在市場裡閒逛，直到找到一家安靜的咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spent the summer wandering around the country.","zh":"他整個夏天都在全國各地四處漫遊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wander","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7ccfaf043ea1ce8","term":"wander","forms":["wander","wanders","wandering","wandered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"偏離；走題","explanation":"指人、路線或話題離開原本正確、預定或正常的方向；用於寫作時，就是說話或文章從主題上岔開了。","examples":[{"en":"The speaker wandered from the main topic and lost the audience.","zh":"演講者偏離了主題，失去了聽眾的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The path wandered away from the river.","zh":"這條小路逐漸偏離了河流。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wander","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8656aa55d393b032b7f0","word":"want","forms":["want"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-15bf801430d3633d","term":"want","forms":["want","wants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"願望；想要的心情","explanation":"指心裡想得到或實現某人、某物或某件事的願望，也就是“想要”。","examples":[{"en":"Her want for adventure led her to travel alone.","zh":"她對冒險的渴望促使她獨自旅行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wrote down his wants before making a decision.","zh":"他在做決定前寫下了自己的願望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/want","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ffed0ffe2293cac3","term":"want","forms":["want","wants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"缺乏；不足","explanation":"指某種東西不夠或不存在，強調那個需要補上的空缺。","examples":[{"en":"The plan failed through a want of careful preparation.","zh":"這個計劃因缺乏周密準備而失敗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A want of sleep can affect your concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足會影響你的注意力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/want","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cd2f8a9f57573e9c","term":"want","forms":["want","wants","wanting","wanted","wantest","wantedst","wanteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想要某人或某物","explanation":"指對某人、某物或某種關係有願望，想把它得到或實現。","examples":[{"en":"I want you as a friend, not as a rival.","zh":"我想和你做朋友，而不是做對手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wants a quiet place to work.","zh":"她想要一個安靜的工作場所。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/want","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c84d38682391645d","term":"want","forms":["want","wants","wanting","wanted","wantest","wantedst","wanteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想要；要求得到","explanation":"指對某件事、某種結果或某種物品有明確要求，範圍很廣，可以只是普通的“想要”。","examples":[{"en":"They want more time to finish the project.","zh":"他們想要更多時間完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach wants the team to stay focused.","zh":"教練希望這支隊伍保持專注。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/want","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f223e8a843c34492","term":"want","forms":["want","wants","wanting","wanted","wantest","wantedst","wanteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想做；願意","explanation":"不帶賓語時，表示想做某事或願意做某事，具體動作通常由上下文補出。","examples":[{"en":"If you want, we can leave early.","zh":"如果你願意，我們可以早點走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I want to learn how to cook.","zh":"我想學做飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/want","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a2d8daa4281b886508f0","word":"war","forms":["war"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0340a93c8c9c8c7e","term":"war","forms":["war","wars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戰爭；武裝衝突","explanation":"指國家、民族或其他大型群體之間有組織、規模較大的武裝衝突，通常涉及軍隊。這裡強調的是戰爭這一總體狀態，而不是某一場具體戰爭。","examples":[{"en":"The country has been at war with its neighbor for two years.","zh":"這個國家已經與鄰國交戰兩年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The leaders are trying to prevent another war.","zh":"領導人正努力避免另一場戰爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/war","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28ce26c3c400fc86","term":"war","forms":["war","wars"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一場具體戰爭","explanation":"指一場有明確時間、地點或參與者的具體武裝衝突；它是總體概念war的一個例項。","examples":[{"en":"The war ended after a peace agreement was signed.","zh":"簽署和平協議後，這場戰爭結束了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She studied the wars that shaped modern Europe.","zh":"她研究了塑造現代歐洲的那些戰爭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/war","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-96b8f576c788b75e5918","word":"ward","forms":["ward"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-692d0241fb9f609c","term":"ward","forms":["ward","wards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受監護的人","explanation":"ward指由個人、法院或國家負責照顧和保護的人，通常因為年齡小或缺乏獨立處理事務的能力而受到監護。","examples":[{"en":"The court appointed her aunt as the child's legal guardian, and the boy became a ward of the state.","zh":"法院指定他的姨媽為法定監護人，這個男孩也因此成為國家的受監護人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guardian must protect the financial interests of her ward.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-079d8c8be0678b53","term":"ward","forms":["ward","wards","warding","warded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擋開；抵擋","explanation":"ward off表示把逼近的危險、疾病、攻擊或不良結果擋開，使它無法靠近或造成影響。","examples":[{"en":"Regular exercise can help ward off heart disease.","zh":"經常鍛鍊有助於預防心臟病。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She raised her arm to ward off the blow.","zh":"她抬起手臂擋開了那一擊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ward","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7d4b47cf84bb52b6cab5","word":"wardrobe","forms":["wardrobe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-58e63658e51c2777","term":"wardrobe","forms":["wardrobe","wardrobes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可移動衣櫃","explanation":"指專門存放衣物的可移動櫃子，通常是臥室裡較大的傢俱。它體現了“把衣物收進一個衣物庫”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a wooden wardrobe for the spare bedroom.","zh":"我們給客房買了一個木製衣櫃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her winter coats are hanging in the wardrobe.","zh":"她的冬衣掛在衣櫃裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wardrobe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3365f824f902a28b","term":"wardrobe","forms":["wardrobe","wardrobes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嵌入式衣櫃","explanation":"指臥室裡固定安裝的高櫃或壁櫥，裡面通常有掛衣杆，用來懸掛和存放衣物。它和可移動衣櫃一樣，都是“衣物庫”的具體形態。","examples":[{"en":"The bedroom has a built-in wardrobe beside the window.","zh":"臥室窗邊有一個嵌入式衣櫃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He put his shirts on the rail inside the wardrobe.","zh":"他把襯衫掛在衣櫃裡的掛衣杆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wardrobe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f8430c90e58f08c","term":"wardrobe","forms":["wardrobe","wardrobes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人全部衣物","explanation":"指一個人擁有的全部衣物，不是某一件衣服或某一個櫃子；這裡“衣物庫”從存放衣物的地方擴充套件成了其中的全部內容。","examples":[{"en":"She is updating her wardrobe for the new job.","zh":"她正在為新工作添置和調整自己的全部衣物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His wardrobe is mostly made up of simple, comfortable clothes.","zh":"他的衣物大多是簡單舒適的款式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wardrobe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ae1fd358c7612a02fdc6","word":"warehouse","forms":["warehouse"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0659f0178f2dfde9","term":"warehouse","forms":["warehouse","warehouses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"倉庫","explanation":"指集中存放大量產品或商品的建築或場所，貨物通常從生產商運到這裡，再發往零售商或顧客。","examples":[{"en":"The company built a new warehouse near the airport.","zh":"這家公司在機場附近建了一座新倉庫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Most of the furniture is still in the warehouse.","zh":"大部分傢俱還在倉庫裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warehouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ca55d04830796e4","term":"warehouse","forms":["warehouse","warehouses","warehousing","warehoused"],"pos":"verb","zh":"存入倉庫","explanation":"指把貨物放進倉庫儲存，強調貨物進入集中倉儲環節。","examples":[{"en":"The distributor warehoused the products until the stores were ready.","zh":"經銷商把這些產品存入倉庫，直到各家商店準備好接收。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The goods were warehoused until the customs documents arrived.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warehouse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f0aa408c1832abefd06","word":"warm","forms":["warm"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61bd2664ae5bdde6","term":"warm","forms":["warm","warmer","warmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"溫暖的；暖和的","explanation":"指溫度比涼或冷高，但通常仍然讓人感到舒服，不一定達到“很熱”的程度。","examples":[{"en":"The soup is warm enough to eat now.","zh":"湯現在溫度夠暖，可以吃了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sat outside in the warm evening air.","zh":"我們坐在外面，享受溫暖的晚間空氣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76cd655fd51cc19b","term":"warm","forms":["warm","warmer","warmest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"親切的；熱情友好的","explanation":"把人與人之間的感情想象成溫度：warm 的人或關係讓人感到友好、關心和有親近感。","examples":[{"en":"Her warm welcome made me feel at home.","zh":"她親切的歡迎讓我覺得像在自己家一樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They have a warm and lasting friendship.","zh":"他們有一段親切而長久的友誼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f5b3446c0ba35768","term":"warm","forms":["warm","warms","warming","warmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變暖；給……取暖","explanation":"把溫暖傳給某人或某物，使它不再冷；這是形容詞“溫暖的”最直接的動作形式。","examples":[{"en":"She warmed her hands over the fire.","zh":"她把手放在火上取暖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please warm the milk before giving it to the baby.","zh":"給寶寶喝之前，請把牛奶熱一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e0bbc64b4e1af3c8","term":"warm","forms":["warm","warms","warming","warmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變暖；熱起來","explanation":"某人或某物自己從冷變暖，強調溫度逐漸上升，而不是被別人直接加熱。","examples":[{"en":"The room began to warm up after we closed the windows.","zh":"關上窗戶後，房間開始暖起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"My feet are finally warming up.","zh":"我的腳終於暖起來了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be54ee02de8f545d","term":"warm","forms":["warm","warms","warming","warmed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸喜歡上","explanation":"把對某人或某事的態度想象成逐漸升溫：一開始冷淡，後來越來越有好感。","examples":[{"en":"I didn't like the plan at first, but I soon warmed to it.","zh":"我起初不喜歡這個計劃，但很快就逐漸接受並喜歡上了它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gradually warmed to the unfamiliar style of music.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ecc745a0d5a1f7577b5f","word":"warmth","forms":["warmth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-dcfea1094a2a53a9","term":"warmth","forms":["warmth","warmths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溫暖；暖意","explanation":"指適度的熱度，或身體感受到的暖意，例如陽光、火、房間或衣物帶來的溫暖。這是 warmth 最直接的意思，也是其他引申義的出發點。","examples":[{"en":"The warmth of the fire made the cold room comfortable.","zh":"爐火的暖意讓寒冷的房間變得舒適。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I stepped into the sunlight and felt its warmth on my face.","zh":"我走到陽光下，感到陽光的暖意照在臉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warmth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8b3f5b9b0201a00","term":"warmth","forms":["warmth","warmths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"友善；親切","explanation":"指一個人或群體表現出的友好、善意和親切，讓別人感到自己受到歡迎和善待。這裡的“溫暖”已經從身體感覺轉到了人與人之間的相處。","examples":[{"en":"The host welcomed us with warmth and made us feel at home.","zh":"主人親切地歡迎了我們，讓我們有賓至如歸的感覺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The warmth of their welcome immediately reassured us.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warmth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-aa63925edf225e26d79e","word":"warn","forms":["warn"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f8da555d4372197","term":"warn","forms":["warn","warns","warning","warned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"提醒某人注意即將發生的事","explanation":"透過言語、動作或標誌讓某人提前意識到危險、事故或其他即將發生的事情，重點是讓對方有所準備。","examples":[{"en":"The sign warns drivers about ice on the road.","zh":"這個標誌提醒司機路面有冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She warned me that the meeting might run late.","zh":"她提醒我會議可能會開得很晚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a8eedc8f5b7d651","term":"warn","forms":["warn","warns","warning","warned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"勸阻某人不要做某事","explanation":"在提醒危險的基礎上，進一步明確告訴某人某種行為不明智、不可接受或可能帶來後果。","examples":[{"en":"The doctor warned him against drinking too much coffee.","zh":"醫生勸他不要喝太多咖啡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She warned him not to cross the flooded bridge.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d9bceb39819ed7a46968","word":"warrant","forms":["warrant"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba460c2842f78d94","term":"warrant","forms":["warrant","warrants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保證；依據","explanation":"指能夠讓人相信某事真實、可靠或有希望成功的保證、證據或依據。它不一定是一份檔案，也可以是支援判斷的事實。","examples":[{"en":"Her careful testing provides a warrant for the product’s safety.","zh":"她的仔細測試為產品的安全性提供了依據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is no warrant for assuming that the plan will succeed.","zh":"沒有理由可以據此假定這個計劃會成功。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warrant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-aef2e67a764e6a55","term":"warrant","forms":["warrant","warrants"],"pos":"noun","zh":"搜查、逮捕等令狀","explanation":"指法院或司法機關簽發的正式命令，授權執法人員搜查、扣押、逮捕或執行判決。它是“憑正式憑證才能行動”這一核心影象最典型的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The judge signed a warrant for his arrest.","zh":"法官簽署了逮捕他的令狀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Police obtained a search warrant before entering the house.","zh":"警方在進入那所房子前取得了搜查令。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warrant","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ba5d957f2837308c846","word":"warranty","forms":["warranty"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2a6c786dea768867","term":"warranty","forms":["warranty","warranties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"保證；擔保","explanation":"指有人或某種制度正式保證某個結果會實現，或者某項義務會被履行。它是“出了問題，有一方應當負責”的一般概念，商品保修和合同保證都可以看作它的具體形式。","examples":[{"en":"The contract includes a warranty that the equipment will meet all safety standards.","zh":"合同保證這套裝置符合所有安全標準。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The seller gave us a warranty of good workmanship.","zh":"賣方保證產品做工良好。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warranty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3274ec28052b7653","term":"warranty","forms":["warranty","warranties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"合同中的質量保證","explanation":"指買賣雙方之間關於商品或房產狀態的法律保證：賣方明說或透過行為暗示，所售物品會符合承諾的狀態。它強調的是交易時對質量、效能或狀況的保證，不限於後來是否免費維修。","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement created an express warranty that the machine would last for ten years.","zh":"這則廣告構成了對機器可使用十年的明示保證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The contract includes a warranty covering defects in materials.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warranty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2bea8f822fb7b931","term":"warranty","forms":["warranty","warranties"],"pos":"noun","zh":"產品保修","explanation":"指賣方或製造商提供的書面保證，通常規定一個固定期限；如果產品損壞或出現製造缺陷，消費者可以免費維修或獲得更換部件。這是日常購物中最常見、最容易遇到的意思。","examples":[{"en":"My laptop is still under warranty, so the repair should be free.","zh":"我的膝上型電腦還在保修期內，所以維修應該是免費的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The washing machine comes with a three-year warranty.","zh":"這臺洗衣機附帶三年保修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warranty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ffb29103283b6b9997b8","word":"warrior","forms":["warrior"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-355c65da10e1ee54","term":"warrior","forms":["warrior","warriors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"戰士；勇士","explanation":"指正在參加戰鬥、衝突或戰爭的人，重點是親自作戰的身份；它可以指軍人，也可以指傳說或歷史中的勇士。","examples":[{"en":"The warrior raised his shield and moved toward the enemy.","zh":"那名戰士舉起盾牌，向敵人走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wounded warrior refused to abandon his companions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warrior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-70f98a0fe939ce71","term":"warrior","forms":["warrior","warriors"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拼搏者；鬥士","explanation":"比喻一個人在體育或其他活動中積極、勇敢、充滿幹勁地投入，彷彿在戰場上奮戰；這裡不一定真的有戰爭。","examples":[{"en":"Despite the injury, she returned to the court like a true warrior.","zh":"儘管受了傷，她還是像真正的鬥士一樣回到了球場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She's a tireless warrior for better public schools.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warrior","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9ecea3e810558da44ceb","word":"wary","forms":["wary"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3d0dde5fc62730ef","term":"wary","forms":["wary","warier","wariest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"警惕的；提防的","explanation":"因為察覺到可能有危險、欺騙或不可靠之處而保持警惕，隨時防備事情出問題。","examples":[{"en":"She is wary of strangers who ask for money.","zh":"她提防那些向她要錢的陌生人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be wary of offers that seem too good to be true.","zh":"對於好得令人難以置信的優惠要保持警惕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-16ab56168d87380a","term":"wary","forms":["wary","warier","wariest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"謹慎的；戒備的","explanation":"形容一個人或他的行為處處留神、有所保留，不輕易冒險或完全信任別人；這是“保持警惕”在日常行為中的表現。","examples":[{"en":"The child gave the new teacher a wary look.","zh":"那個孩子戒備地看了新老師一眼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be wary of anyone promising effortless profits.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-476994559e873a621c52","word":"wash","forms":["wash"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-48dc0475650c71ae","term":"wash","forms":["wash","washes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洗滌；洗澡","explanation":"指用水或其他液體清洗的過程，也可以指一次洗滌或洗澡；核心畫面就是水把身上的東西衝洗帶走。","examples":[{"en":"I had a quick wash before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前我快速洗了洗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These curtains need a wash.","zh":"這些窗簾需要洗一下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ecfc7b7b872902b","term":"wash","forms":["wash","washes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"洗液","explanation":"指用來清洗某物或某處的液體，是把“水流沖洗”裝進容器裡的洗滌用品。","examples":[{"en":"Use a mild wash for sensitive skin.","zh":"敏感皮膚要使用溫和的洗液。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This wash removes grease without damaging the paint.","zh":"這種洗液能去除油汙，又不會損壞漆面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e8c986d02ddd210","term":"wash","forms":["wash","washes","washing","washed","washen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用水清洗","explanation":"用水把物體表面的汙垢洗掉，就像讓水流沖走附著的東西。","examples":[{"en":"Please wash the dishes after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後請把碗洗了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She washed the mud off her shoes.","zh":"她把鞋上的泥洗掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-445d0dbf65ac191a","term":"wash","forms":["wash","washes","washing","washed","washen"],"pos":"verb","zh":"洗自己","explanation":"指人用水清潔自己的身體，就像讓水把身上的汗水和汙垢帶走。","examples":[{"en":"I wash before breakfast every morning.","zh":"我每天早飯前洗漱。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children washed their hands before lunch.","zh":"孩子們午飯前洗了手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wash","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0bb5e9329f190a4fa67f","word":"waste","forms":["waste"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73feb45786b89232","term":"waste","forms":["waste","wastes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"廢料；垃圾","explanation":"指已經沒有原來用途的材料、壞掉而不能出售的產品或一般垃圾；東西變空、失去價值後，就成了廢棄物。","examples":[{"en":"The factory must separate recyclable waste from other materials.","zh":"這家工廠必須把可回收廢料與其他材料分開。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please put the food waste in the green bin.","zh":"請把廚餘垃圾放進綠色垃圾桶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a24c9097fdafbf3","term":"waste","forms":["waste","wastes","wasting","wasted","wastest","wastedst","wasteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"浪費；揮霍","explanation":"把錢、時間、精力或資源白白用掉，沒有得到相稱的結果；它正好對應“東西變空、失去價值”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We wasted too much time arguing about a minor detail.","zh":"我們把太多時間浪費在爭論一個小細節上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please do not waste water while you are washing the dishes.","zh":"洗碗時請不要浪費水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0267f2a8b97dc41","term":"waste","forms":["waste","wastes","wasting","wasted","wastest","wastedst","wasteth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸消耗；損耗","explanation":"使物質、力量或儲備一點點減少，直到變少、變弱或用盡；例如燃料被用光、身體被疾病拖垮，都有逐漸變空的感覺。","examples":[{"en":"The long winter wasted the family's last supplies.","zh":"漫長的冬天一點點耗盡了這家人最後的補給。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of illness had wasted his strength.","zh":"多年的疾病逐漸耗盡了他的體力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-baed831623943be39ebf","word":"watch","forms":["watch"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f224c8a4c7fff4a9","term":"watch","forms":["watch","watches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"手錶","explanation":"手腕上用來顯示時間的行動式計時器；它像一雙一直盯著時間的眼睛。","examples":[{"en":"My watch stopped, so I was late for work.","zh":"我的手錶停了，所以我上班遲到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She checked her watch before leaving the meeting.","zh":"她離開會議前看了一下手錶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-752e4e1333169f46","term":"watch","forms":["watch","watches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"看守；守望","explanation":"持續盯著某人或某物，以便發現情況或保護它；這是“持續留意”作為名詞的直接體現。","examples":[{"en":"Two guards kept watch outside the building all night.","zh":"兩名守衛整夜在大樓外守望。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The parents took turns keeping watch over the sick child.","zh":"父母輪流守護生病的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9049f43358af5472","term":"watch","forms":["watch","watches","watching","watched","watchest","watchedst","watcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"觀看","explanation":"把視線和注意力持續放在某人、某物或某個活動上，而不是隻在一瞬間看見它。","examples":[{"en":"We watched the children play in the garden.","zh":"我們看著孩子們在花園裡玩耍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I watched a documentary on the train.","zh":"我在火車上看了一部紀錄片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3046e0266d850b9","term":"watch","forms":["watch","watches","watching","watched","watchest","watchedst","watcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"觀察；留意","explanation":"持續觀察某人或某事，以便注意到變化、結果或重要細節。","examples":[{"en":"Watch the soup carefully so it does not boil over.","zh":"仔細留意湯，別讓它煮沸溢位來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Watch the gauge and warn me if pressure rises.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-92299bc1029783de","term":"watch","forms":["watch","watches","watching","watched","watchest","watchedst","watcheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"照看；看守","explanation":"替別人持續留意某人或某物，確保它安全或沒有出問題；這是“盯著目標”變成承擔照看責任。","examples":[{"en":"Could you watch my bag while I buy a ticket?","zh":"我買票時你能幫我看一下包嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She watches her little brother after school.","zh":"她放學後照看弟弟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0f4168490e38b8447e11","word":"water","forms":["water"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d113ca0e87d0d404","term":"water","forms":["water","waters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"水","explanation":"指常溫下通常為透明液體的H₂O；結冰時是冰，變成氣體時是蒸汽。","examples":[{"en":"Please leave a bottle of water by my desk.","zh":"請在我桌邊放一瓶水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Water freezes at zero degrees Celsius.","zh":"水在零攝氏度時結冰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/water","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7dc7221717e13cfe","term":"water","forms":["water","waters","watering","watered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"澆水","explanation":"把水倒到植物周圍的土壤中，使植物得到水分。","examples":[{"en":"I water the herbs every morning.","zh":"我每天早上給香草澆水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Could you water my plants while I am away?","zh":"我不在時，你能幫我給植物澆水嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/water","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3cb562c897155ca6e376","word":"waterfall","forms":["waterfall"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ed0ec8bfc58728fd","term":"waterfall","forms":["waterfall","waterfalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瀑布","explanation":"水從懸崖、巖壁等高處連續流下形成的水流。記住“水從高處落下”這個畫面，就能抓住 waterfall 的核心。","examples":[{"en":"We followed the trail until we reached a waterfall.","zh":"我們沿著小路走，直到來到一處瀑布。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The waterfall was hidden behind a wall of trees.","zh":"瀑布藏在一片樹林後面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterfall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e50af774e4a9e040","term":"waterfall","forms":["waterfall","waterfalls"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瀑布般傾瀉的東西","explanation":"比喻霧、煙、液體等像瀑布一樣連續、大量地向下湧出，重點仍是“成股落下”的視覺形象。","examples":[{"en":"A waterfall of steam poured from the broken pipe.","zh":"蒸汽像瀑布一樣從破裂的管道中湧出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A waterfall of silver hair flowed down her back.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterfall","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31a2d5282683edb3a22c","word":"watermelon","forms":["watermelon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-20cdcf6f3980507e","term":"watermelon","forms":["watermelon","watermelons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"西瓜植物","explanation":"指結出西瓜的這種藤本植物本身，而不是某一個具體果實。看到它時，可以把它想成“長西瓜的整株植物”。","examples":[{"en":"Watermelon plants need plenty of sun and water.","zh":"西瓜植株需要充足的陽光和水分。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The watermelons spread rapidly across the sunny vegetable patch.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watermelon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3824b49d6c59a0ce","term":"watermelon","forms":["watermelon","watermelons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"西瓜果實","explanation":"指西瓜這種水果：外皮通常是綠色的，成熟后里面多為鮮紅色果肉，還帶有黑色種子。這是日常生活中最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We bought a large watermelon for the picnic.","zh":"我們為野餐買了一個大西瓜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The watermelon was sweet and full of black seeds.","zh":"這個西瓜很甜，裡面有很多黑色種子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/watermelon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-af3ba25ec6364577524b","word":"waterproof","forms":["waterproof"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82acf481611bc9d5","term":"waterproof","forms":["waterproof","more waterproof","most waterproof"],"pos":"adj","zh":"防水的；耐水的","explanation":"指某物能夠抵擋水，不容易因接觸水而受影響。重點是它具有防水能力，未必專指完全不讓水進入的材料。","examples":[{"en":"These shoes are waterproof, so you can wear them in the rain.","zh":"這雙鞋防水，所以你可以在雨天穿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I need a waterproof phone case for the beach.","zh":"我需要一個去海灘時用的防水手機套。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterproof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9e453a9a1dab35cd","term":"waterproof","forms":["waterproof","waterproofs","waterproofing","waterproofed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……防水","explanation":"指給某物加上防水層或採用防水處理，使水不容易進入或造成損壞。","examples":[{"en":"We waterproofed the roof before the rainy season.","zh":"我們在雨季到來前給屋頂做了防水處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company uses wax to waterproof the canvas.","zh":"這家公司用蠟給帆布做防水處理。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterproof","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b125ec99a74470517f9","word":"wave","forms":["wave"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e6148e37a00a44c4","term":"wave","forms":["wave","waves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"波浪；波動","explanation":"指液體表面上下起伏並向前移動的波，最典型的是海浪、湖面上的波或水波。","examples":[{"en":"A large wave knocked him off his surfboard.","zh":"一個大浪把他從衝浪板上掀了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Small waves were moving across the lake.","zh":"小波浪正在湖面上緩緩移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7dabc4eeecfe2356","term":"wave","forms":["wave","waves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"揮手；揮動","explanation":"指手向前後或左右來回擺動的動作，常用於打招呼、告別或吸引注意。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a quick wave from the bus.","zh":"她在公交車上向我快速揮了揮手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left with a friendly wave.","zh":"他友好地揮了揮手後離開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-383c0c5014324c4e","term":"wave","forms":["wave","waves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一陣；一股突然增加","explanation":"把人、情緒、事件或某種現象想成一陣陣湧來的波，因此表示數量或強度突然上升但通常不會持續太久。","examples":[{"en":"A wave of panic spread through the crowd.","zh":"一陣恐慌在人群中蔓延開來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop was hit by a wave of customers after lunch.","zh":"午飯後，一大批顧客突然湧進了這家商店。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0772669d74e047dc","term":"wave","forms":["wave","waves","waving","waved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擺動；飄動","explanation":"指物體在風中或其他作用下反覆、較鬆弛地來回移動，正如旗子在風中擺動。","examples":[{"en":"The flag waved gently in the breeze.","zh":"旗子在微風中輕輕飄動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Long grass waved in the afternoon breeze.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f60edd2b83248f92","term":"wave","forms":["wave","waves","waving","waved"],"pos":"verb","zh":"揮手","explanation":"指用手來回擺動來打招呼、告別或表示自己在場。","examples":[{"en":"I waved to my neighbor across the street.","zh":"我隔著街向鄰居揮了揮手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She waved goodbye as the train pulled away.","zh":"火車開走時，她揮手道別。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-57abfafa3540c266d66a","word":"wax","forms":["wax"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a5c21664231676ea","term":"wax","forms":["wax","waxes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蠟","explanation":"一種可以熔化、塑形並重新凝固的物質，最典型的是蜜蜂分泌的蜂蠟。它是 wax 最基礎、最值得先掌握的名詞義。","examples":[{"en":"She melted the wax to make a small candle.","zh":"她把蠟熔化後做成了一支小蠟燭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The artist mixed beeswax with colored pigment.","zh":"這位藝術家把蜂蠟和有色顏料混合在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ce357ed9eb56e418","term":"wax","forms":["wax","waxes","waxing","waxed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給……上蠟","explanation":"指把蠟塗到鞋、地板、汽車、蘋果等表面，通常是為了讓表面更光亮或受到保護。","examples":[{"en":"I wax my car twice a year.","zh":"我每年給汽車打兩次蠟。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shop waxes apples to make them look shiny.","zh":"這家店給蘋果上蠟，讓它們看起來更有光澤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wax","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44c5e7071f3a75a22457","word":"way","forms":["way"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b3a4442360e57aa","term":"way","forms":["way","ways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"路；方向","explanation":"指通往某地的道路、路線或方向，是way最具體、最容易延伸出的基本意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could you show me the way to the train station?","zh":"你能告訴我去火車站怎麼走嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The beach is only a short way from here.","zh":"海灘離這裡不遠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/way","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a4bf5ed4534ef2e","term":"way","forms":["way","ways"],"pos":"noun","zh":"方法；方式","explanation":"把“走一條路”引申為“用一種方式做事”，指解決問題、行動或表現某事的方法。","examples":[{"en":"There is a better way to solve this problem.","zh":"有更好的辦法可以解決這個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I like the way you explain things.","zh":"我喜歡你解釋事情的方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/way","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d99cb74cc24bf2304d05","word":"we (us, our, ours, ourselves)","forms":["we"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-62667b1e78d5a14f","term":"we","forms":["we","ourself"],"pos":"pron","zh":"我們","explanation":"指包括說話者或寫作者在內的兩人或多人，是 we 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We are meeting outside the station at six.","zh":"我們六點在車站外見面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We have finished the report.","zh":"我們已經完成報告了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/we","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a26f1e11fab4e26","term":"we","forms":["we"],"pos":"det","zh":"我們這些……人","explanation":"說話者把自己和同一類別的人放在一起稱呼，強調“我們這一類人”。","examples":[{"en":"We students need more time to finish the project.","zh":"我們這些學生需要更多時間完成這個專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We musicians depend on regular practice.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/we","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-481ba4019c9d2710c338","word":"weak","forms":["weak"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-24386cf7d90ce64c","term":"weak","forms":["weak","weaker","weakest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"力量不足；無力","explanation":"表示缺少體力、力量或完成某事的能力，核心形象就是“撐不起、動不了”。","examples":[{"en":"The child was too weak to move the boulder.","zh":"那個孩子太虛弱了，搬不動那塊大石頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After the long hike, my legs felt weak.","zh":"長途徒步後，我的雙腿感到很無力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ea3fcbea06c14ba2","term":"weak","forms":["weak","weaker","weakest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不牢固；承受力差","explanation":"表示繩子、木材、結構等承受不了重量、壓力或拉力，就像那根撐不住的細繩。","examples":[{"en":"The old rope is too weak to hold the load.","zh":"這根舊繩子太不結實，承受不了這批貨物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The bridge has a weak section near the entrance.","zh":"這座橋靠近入口處有一段不牢固。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1459163077b38f8a","term":"weak","forms":["weak","weaker","weakest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"意志薄弱；容易受影響","explanation":"表示一個人抵抗誘惑、勸說或壓力的能力弱，很容易被打動、說服或壓倒。","examples":[{"en":"He is weak in the face of peer pressure.","zh":"面對同伴壓力時，他很容易動搖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her weak resolve made her give up quickly.","zh":"她意志薄弱，很快就放棄了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weak","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3e66ba098b3789d68366","word":"weaken","forms":["weaken"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d5fce0f3271def79","term":"weaken","forms":["weaken","weakens","weakening","weakened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……變弱","explanation":"指透過某種原因或行動，讓力量、結構、關係、信心等不如以前強。它強調“有東西使物件的強度下降”，是“強度往下掉”這條記憶線中帶有施動者的一支。","examples":[{"en":"Repeated stress can weaken the bridge.","zh":"反覆的壓力可能使這座橋變得不牢固。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The argument weakened her confidence.","zh":"這個爭論削弱了她的信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weaken","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-783df5272ba14fce","term":"weaken","forms":["weaken","weakens","weakening","weakened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變弱","explanation":"指某人或某物自身逐漸失去力量、效果或強度，重點不是誰讓它變弱，而是它的狀態發生了下降。身體力量、興趣、風勢和影響力等都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"Her interest in the project gradually weakened.","zh":"她對這個專案的興趣逐漸減弱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind weakened after sunset.","zh":"日落後風力減弱了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weaken","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-739bf484f7f1c288c0e5","word":"wealth","forms":["wealth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b672cdf05580a6b","term":"wealth","forms":["wealth","wealths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"財富；資產","explanation":"指一個人、家庭、機構或社會擁有的大量金錢、財產和其他有價值的物品。它強調總體財富，不只指手頭的現金。","examples":[{"en":"Her family built its wealth through years of careful investment.","zh":"她的家族透過多年的謹慎投資積累了財富。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"True wealth is not measured only by the size of a bank account.","zh":"真正的財富不能只用銀行賬戶的金額來衡量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wealth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a0c09aa909487708","term":"wealth","forms":["wealth","wealths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大量；豐富的資源","explanation":"指某一方面擁有很多可利用或有價值的東西，例如知識、經驗、資訊或機會。這裡不一定和金錢有關，而是把某種東西看成“滿滿一倉庫”的資源。","examples":[{"en":"The new website offers a wealth of useful information for students.","zh":"這個新網站為學生提供了大量有用的資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The archive offers a wealth of material for researchers.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wealth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-093a169186a726bc6007","word":"wealthy","forms":["wealthy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8543d19cc01b9db8","term":"wealthy","forms":["wealthy","wealthier","more wealthy","wealthiest","most wealthy"],"pos":"adj","zh":"富有的；有錢的","explanation":"指個人、家庭或群體擁有很多錢財和資產，生活在經濟上較寬裕的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She grew up in a wealthy family but chose a simple life.","zh":"她在一個富裕家庭長大，卻選擇了簡樸的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The city is home to many wealthy investors.","zh":"這座城市有許多富有的投資者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wealthy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c68fef1abac63a835383","word":"weapon","forms":["weapon"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ea06ce296775fc7","term":"weapon","forms":["weapon","weapons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"武器","explanation":"用於戰鬥、狩獵或自衛的工具，例如槍、導彈、刀劍，也可以是棍棒等能用於攻擊或防禦的物品。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers laid down their weapons and left the building.","zh":"士兵們放下武器，離開了大樓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The club was once used as a weapon.","zh":"這根棍棒以前曾被當作武器使用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weapon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b216b8648af1a278","term":"weapon","forms":["weapon","weapons"],"pos":"noun","zh":"控制或傷害的手段","explanation":"比喻任何能傷害別人、迫使別人服從，或幫助自己取得優勢的力量或手段，例如金錢、資訊或宣傳。","examples":[{"en":"The company used personal data as a weapon against its critics.","zh":"這家公司把個人資料當作對付批評者的手段。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He used confidential information as a weapon against his rivals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weapon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c47fbc5d87a1298121dd","word":"wear","forms":["wear"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7b253f76300f4f7e","term":"wear","forms":["wear","wears","wearing","wore","ware","worn","worne"],"pos":"verb","zh":"穿著；佩戴","explanation":"表示把衣服、鞋、飾品或其他東西穿戴在身上，也可以表示臉上帶著某種表情或身上帶著某種外觀。它強調“處於穿戴狀態”，不只表示“把衣服穿上的瞬間”。","examples":[{"en":"She is wearing a blue jacket and white shoes.","zh":"她穿著一件藍色夾克和一雙白鞋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wear your seat belt on the bus.","zh":"請在公交車上繫好安全帶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-33e973829d0982e0","term":"wear","forms":["wear","wears","wearing","wore","ware","worn","worne"],"pos":"verb","zh":"磨損；磨壞","explanation":"表示使用、摩擦或時間使某物逐漸變薄、變舊或損壞。這裡的核心畫面仍是“長期貼著使用，最後留下損耗”。","examples":[{"en":"The rough ground wore a hole in his shoes.","zh":"粗糙的地面把他的鞋磨出了一個洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years of use have worn the handle smooth.","zh":"多年的使用把這個把手磨得光滑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wear","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1702a4bae332d66ff1a3","word":"weary","forms":["weary"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-21272f470af06657","term":"weary","forms":["weary","wearier","weariest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"疲憊的","explanation":"指經過勞動、行走或其他用力後，體力已經明顯消耗，人感到疲憊不堪。這個意思就是“體力的燈快熄滅了”。","examples":[{"en":"The weary hikers stopped beside the stream.","zh":"疲憊的徒步者在小溪旁停了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"After working all night, I was too weary to cook.","zh":"工作了一整夜後，我疲憊得連飯都不想做了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0a7495ae95eb69d6","term":"weary","forms":["weary","wearier","weariest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"厭倦的","explanation":"指耐心、興趣或滿足感被反覆經歷的事情耗盡，因此對某事感到厭煩或不想繼續。這裡耗盡的不是體力，而是“耐心的燈”。","examples":[{"en":"She grew weary of answering the same question.","zh":"她漸漸厭倦了一遍遍回答同一個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workers were weary of empty promises.","zh":"工人們已經厭倦了空洞的承諾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weary","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e5e72beb4e3c6926d3dc","word":"weather","forms":["weather"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b8fe25eac2b6fcea","term":"weather","forms":["weather","weathers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"天氣","explanation":"指某個時間和地點的大氣狀況，包括氣溫、溼度、雲、雨雪和風等，是最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The weather is warm and sunny today.","zh":"今天天氣溫暖晴朗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What will the weather be like tomorrow?","zh":"明天天氣會怎麼樣？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64b7969a3ef38d28","term":"weather","forms":["weather","weathers","weathering","weathered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"經受住；挺過","explanation":"把困難比作風暴，表示承受住壓力、危險或挫折併成功渡過。","examples":[{"en":"The small business weathered the economic crisis.","zh":"這家小企業挺過了經濟危機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She weathered months of criticism without giving up.","zh":"她頂住了數月的批評，沒有放棄。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weather","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-775e432bb7ff3e08df7a","word":"weave","forms":["weave"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-da47d01532d2540a","term":"weave","forms":["weave","weaves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"織法；織物組織","explanation":"weave 可以指線彼此交錯後形成的織法或織物組織，例如布料是織得很緊還是很鬆。","examples":[{"en":"This fabric has a loose weave, so light passes through it easily.","zh":"這種布的織法很鬆，所以光線很容易透過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The tight weave helps the fabric resist tearing.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8b062eb1a333a9c","term":"weave","forms":["weave","weaves","weaving","wove","weaved","woven"],"pos":"verb","zh":"交錯編織","explanation":"weave 表示讓線、紗或其他長條材料彼此穿過、上下交錯，從而製成布料、衣物等東西。","examples":[{"en":"The machine weaves cotton into soft blankets.","zh":"這臺機器把棉線織成柔軟的毯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her grandmother taught her to weave baskets from reeds.","zh":"她的祖母教她用蘆葦編籃子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weave","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4b5e57f6eb2f42b9039b","word":"web","forms":["web"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-829f35cc9c659ad6","term":"web","forms":["web","webs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蜘蛛網","explanation":"指蜘蛛用絲織成的網，是web最具體、最容易記住的本義。","examples":[{"en":"The sunlight glistened in the dew on the web.","zh":"陽光照在蜘蛛網上的露珠上，閃閃發亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A spider built a web between the two branches.","zh":"一隻蜘蛛在兩根樹枝之間結了一張網。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/web","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1160925f8e161836","term":"web","forms":["web","webs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"交織成的網路","explanation":"由人、地點、事物或關係彼此連線形成的複雜網路，就像蜘蛛網一樣互相牽連。","examples":[{"en":"The investigation uncovered a web of secret connections.","zh":"調查揭開了一張秘密關係交織成的網。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A complex web of alliances shaped the conflict.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/web","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-747a8f398395dde8e524","word":"website","forms":["website"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fdbc78b724d798ce","term":"website","forms":["website","websites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"網站","explanation":"網站就像網際網路上的一座站點，裡面包含許多彼此連結的網頁，通常透過同一個網址入口訪問。新聞、購物、學校或個人主頁都可以是網站。","examples":[{"en":"I found the information on the university's website.","zh":"我在這所大學的網站上找到了這條資訊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company is building a new website for its customers.","zh":"這家公司正在為客戶建設一個新網站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/website","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-318aadfe85eb7669ff9b","word":"wed","forms":["wed"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a612574c3f4ffddd","term":"wed","forms":["wed","weds","wedding","wedded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"娶或嫁給","explanation":"指把某人正式娶為配偶或嫁給某人，強調一個人作出婚姻承諾。","examples":[{"en":"She wed her longtime partner last spring.","zh":"她去年春天和相戀多年的伴侶結了婚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wed her childhood sweetheart in a small ceremony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-afd1a8fffb87f7a091c9","word":"wedding","forms":["wedding"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a463e871976a17e9","term":"wedding","forms":["wedding","weddings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"婚禮","explanation":"wedding是慶祝兩個人開始婚姻關係的正式儀式，重點在舉行的婚禮活動本身，而不是婚姻持續的狀態。","examples":[{"en":"We are invited to Maya's wedding next Saturday.","zh":"我們受邀參加瑪雅下週六的婚禮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wedding was held in a small garden.","zh":"婚禮在一個小花園裡舉行。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wedding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c95b29977134ce6a","term":"wedding","forms":["wedding","weddings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結合；合併","explanation":"這裡把不同的人、團體或事物想象成像新人一樣結合在一起，因此wedding可以比喻兩個或多個部分的合併。","examples":[{"en":"The wedding of the two companies created a much larger business.","zh":"這兩家公司的合併造就了一家規模大得多的企業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The design achieves a wedding of old stone and modern glass.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wedding","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d132e4bc948e1cc12383","word":"weed","forms":["weed"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c8b6ed5c4ff332a","term":"weed","forms":["weed","weeds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"雜草","explanation":"指在某個地方、某個時節生長，卻被認為不該生長的植物；同一種植物在合適的地方可能不是 weed。","examples":[{"en":"We pulled the weeds from the vegetable garden.","zh":"我們把菜園裡的雜草拔掉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These weeds are blocking the sunlight from the flowers.","zh":"這些雜草擋住了花朵的陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02ef4c627b45453b","term":"weed","forms":["weed","weeds","weeding","weeded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"除草","explanation":"把種植地裡不需要的植物拔掉或清除，正是從 weed“雜草”發展出的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"I need to weed the flower bed before the weekend.","zh":"我得在週末前給花壇除草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children helped their grandfather weed the fields.","zh":"孩子們幫祖父給田地除草。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weed","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6df37daaa46ce714fa41","word":"week","forms":["week"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ade4a5391e921769","term":"week","forms":["week","weeks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"連續七天","explanation":"指連續排列的七天，是最基本的時間單位；這七天不一定要按照日曆上的星期順序來劃分。","examples":[{"en":"I stayed in London for a week.","zh":"我在倫敦待了一個星期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They returned after a week of hiking.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/week","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bb1773137b6c3e08","term":"week","forms":["week","weeks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日曆周","explanation":"指按日曆劃分的一週，通常從星期日或星期一開始，到接下來的六天結束。","examples":[{"en":"The school term starts next week.","zh":"學期下週開始。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum closes every Monday at the start of the week.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/week","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-82d048d26ee2fdd4122f","word":"weekday","forms":["weekday"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a60048b63704099b","term":"weekday","forms":["weekday","weekdays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工作日；非週末日","explanation":"指一週中通常用於上班、上學的日子，也就是通常與週末相對的那些日子。它強調的是日曆中的時間類別，不表示某個特定職業或工作本身。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is open on weekdays but closed on Sundays.","zh":"這家博物館工作日開放，但星期天閉館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Weekday trains are usually more crowded than weekend trains.","zh":"工作日的列車通常比周末的列車更擁擠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weekday","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1197a20df1b4c87b10c8","word":"weekend","forms":["weekend"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-16af4465527ddcac","term":"weekend","forms":["weekend","weekends"],"pos":"noun","zh":"週末","explanation":"指一週工作或學習結束後的休息時段，通常是星期六和星期日。它是這個詞最基本的意思，其他用法都從“週末這個時間段”擴充套件而來。","examples":[{"en":"Are you free this weekend?","zh":"你這個週末有空嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We usually visit my parents at the weekend.","zh":"我們通常在週末去看望我的父母。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weekend","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8850eced986ec360f9b3","word":"weekly","forms":["weekly"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e4f4ed43efb10641","term":"weekly","forms":["weekly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"每週的；與一週有關的","explanation":"指與“一週”這個時間單位有關的事物，不一定強調每週發生一次，例如每週安排、週報等。","examples":[{"en":"I checked the weekly schedule before making plans.","zh":"我在制定計劃前檢視了每週安排。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The weekly timetable includes two swimming lessons.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weekly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2fa7195abdafea15","term":"weekly","forms":["weekly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"每週一次的","explanation":"指某件事每週固定或通常發生一次，就像日曆每完整轉過一週便重複一次。","examples":[{"en":"He has a weekly check-up at the hospital.","zh":"他每週在醫院做一次檢查。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The club holds weekly meetings in the library.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weekly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-501a68c5ba7cf4d5","term":"weekly","forms":["weekly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"每週一次地","explanation":"表示某個動作每隔一週發生一次，強調一次完整一週後的重複。","examples":[{"en":"She visits her mother weekly.","zh":"她每週去看望母親一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The volunteers meet weekly at the community center.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weekly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8f14105e19bbf0228bc5","word":"weep","forms":["weep"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a4c6123d9d825cfd","term":"weep","forms":["weep","weeps","weeping","wept","weeped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"哭泣；流淚","explanation":"指因悲傷、喜悅或其他強烈情緒而流淚，常常伴隨抽泣，甚至說不出話；這是 weep 的核心意思。","examples":[{"en":"They wept together in silence after hearing the news.","zh":"聽到這個訊息後，他們默默地一起哭了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wept with relief when his daughter came home safely.","zh":"女兒平安回家時，他如釋重負地哭了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weep","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-63b117d528b902edfd8c","word":"weigh","forms":["weigh"],"officialPos":"v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aedb312cb8a32fdb","term":"weigh","forms":["weigh","weighs","weighing","weighed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"稱出重量","explanation":"把物體放到秤上，測定它有多重；這是 weigh 最直接、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Please weigh the apples before you put them in the bag.","zh":"請先稱一下蘋果，再把它們裝進袋子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The package weighs two kilograms.","zh":"這個包裹重兩公斤。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weigh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f27cf91fe49fb241","term":"weigh","forms":["weigh","weighs","weighing","weighed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"衡量價值","explanation":"把某件事放到心裡的秤上，判斷它的價值、優點或缺點，而不是測量實際重量。","examples":[{"en":"We need to weigh the risks before making a decision.","zh":"我們作決定前需要權衡風險。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The judge weighed the evidence carefully.","zh":"法官仔細權衡了證據。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weigh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-823493964324feae","term":"weigh","forms":["weigh","weighs","weighing","weighed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"認真考慮","explanation":"把一個問題放到心裡的秤上仔細掂量，表示考慮某個主題、方案或因素。","examples":[{"en":"She is weighing whether to accept the offer.","zh":"她正在考慮是否接受這份提議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take some time to weigh your options.","zh":"花點時間權衡一下你的選擇。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weigh","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0844df8fee9eeadaa344","word":"weight","forms":["weight"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7073759cf569b992","term":"weight","forms":["weight","weights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重量；重力作用","explanation":"weight是物體受到重力向下拉時表現出的分量，也就是通常所說的重量。它可以指某件東西有多重，也可以泛指重量這一物理概念。","examples":[{"en":"The weight of the suitcase made it hard to carry.","zh":"這個手提箱的重量使它很難搬動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What is the weight of this package?","zh":"這個包裹有多重？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-081a7a383485cde3","term":"weight","forms":["weight","weights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"重要性；影響力","explanation":"抽象地說，weight就是某個觀點、證據、人物或決定所具有的“分量”，也就是它的重要性或影響力。分量越大，越能影響別人或左右結果。","examples":[{"en":"Her experience gives her opinion considerable weight.","zh":"她的經驗使她的意見很有分量。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The evidence carried little weight with the jury.","zh":"這些證據對陪審團來說分量不大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-629bdf2455505976","term":"weight","forms":["weight","weights"],"pos":"noun","zh":"舉重器材","explanation":"在鍛鍊中，weight指用來訓練力量的器材，例如槓鈴片、啞鈴或其他負重物。這裡的“分量”是訓練時主動加在身體或器械上的重量。","examples":[{"en":"I do strength exercises with weights twice a week.","zh":"我每週用器械做兩次力量訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He lifted the weights carefully to avoid injury.","zh":"他小心地舉起器械，以免受傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weight","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0728c355c79c3a080064","word":"weird","forms":["weird"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4e4d2c5e4ad94e05","term":"weird","forms":["weird","weirder","weirdest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"奇怪的；怪異的","explanation":"形容一個人的性格、舉止或整體給人不尋常、難以理解的感覺。它不一定表示這個人有害，只是說明對方不像通常所見的人。","examples":[{"en":"There are some weird people in my neighborhood.","zh":"我住的街區有一些舉止很怪的人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A weird humming sound came from the cellar.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weird","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ae8c5a83ed7c4d63","term":"weird","forms":["weird","weirder","weirdest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"反常的；不合常理的","explanation":"形容某件事偏離通常預期，讓人感到不對勁、離奇或難以解釋。它尤其常用於描述巧合、經歷、氣氛或情況。","examples":[{"en":"It was weird to see all three of them arrive at the same time.","zh":"看到他們三個同時到達，感覺很奇怪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That’s weird—I was sure I had locked the door.","zh":"這很奇怪——我明明確定自己鎖門了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weird","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-280d44ab1e9f79b5cce2","word":"welcome","forms":["welcome"],"officialPos":"v./adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6bd6b29aabddbb7d","term":"welcome","forms":["welcome","welcomer","welcomest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"受歡迎的","explanation":"指某人來到某處會讓人高興，並且會被願意接納；也可以說某人是在某個團體或場合中受歡迎的來客。","examples":[{"en":"A welcome visitor arrived just before dinner.","zh":"一位受歡迎的來客恰好在晚飯前到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Your advice would be welcome at this stage.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/welcome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4d5f1725226a882a","term":"welcome","forms":["welcome","welcomes","welcoming","welcomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"歡迎；迎接","explanation":"指主動迎接某人的到來，並讓對方感到自己受到歡迎；這就是門口主人向來客伸出手的動作。","examples":[{"en":"The guide welcomed us at the entrance.","zh":"導遊在入口處迎接了我們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our hosts welcomed us with hot tea and fresh bread.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/welcome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-acc42ad04ad2c6c0ccf0","word":"welfare","forms":["welfare"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a33def9575fc4751","term":"welfare","forms":["welfare","welfares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"福祉；安康","explanation":"指個人或群體整體上過得好，包括健康、安全、幸福、生活順利和繁榮等方面。它不是某一種具體好處，而是“生活狀態良好”這一總概念。","examples":[{"en":"The new policy was introduced for the welfare of local families.","zh":"這項新政策是為了當地家庭的福祉而推出的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The charity puts the welfare of children first.","zh":"這家慈善機構把兒童的福祉放在首位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/welfare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e78757cd0c5a661b","term":"welfare","forms":["welfare","welfares"],"pos":"noun","zh":"福利救助；福利金","explanation":"在美國英語非正式用法中，welfare 可以簡稱政府提供的社會福利、福利救助或福利金，通常指幫助低收入或失業者維持生活的援助。","examples":[{"en":"She went on welfare after losing her job.","zh":"她失業後開始領取福利救助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family relied on welfare during his unemployment.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/welfare","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a7722b765d15608d5d24","word":"well","forms":["well"],"officialPos":"adv./adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e9af42eb33f50564","term":"well","forms":["well","better","weller","best","wellest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"身體健康","explanation":"表示人的身體恢復到理想狀態，也就是健康、不再生病。","examples":[{"en":"I was ill last week, but I’m well again now.","zh":"我上週生病了，但現在又恢復健康了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She feels well enough to return to work.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/well","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-801587ce9d9a8d99","term":"well","forms":["well","better","best"],"pos":"adv","zh":"做得好","explanation":"表示動作完成得準確、熟練或令人滿意，也就是事情順利地達到理想狀態。","examples":[{"en":"She knows the software well and can solve problems quickly.","zh":"她很熟悉這款軟體，能迅速解決問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The plan worked well for everyone.","zh":"這個計劃對所有人都很奏效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/well","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-05a46ff1e96f3d1a","term":"well","forms":["well","wells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"井","explanation":"井是從地面向下挖出的深孔，人們可以從中取得地下水、石油、天然氣等液體。它正好對應“地下的水從某處湧出”的記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers share a well for drinking water.","zh":"村民們共用一口井取飲用水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They dug a well beside the house.","zh":"他們在房子旁邊挖了一口井。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/well","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-76a796208b71779c0331","word":"west","forms":["west"],"officialPos":"n./adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-61f8c9720d1df638","term":"west","forms":["west"],"pos":"adj","zh":"西邊的；向西的","explanation":"指位於西方或朝向西方的位置，是“太陽落下的那一邊”。","examples":[{"en":"Our room is on the west side of the building.","zh":"我們的房間在大樓的西側。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The west-facing windows get little morning sun.","zh":"朝西的窗戶早晨幾乎照不到陽光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/west","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2970b81244200b4b","term":"west","forms":["west"],"pos":"adv","zh":"向西；往西","explanation":"表示人、車輛或其他事物朝西方移動。","examples":[{"en":"After lunch, we drove west toward the mountains.","zh":"午飯後，我們向西開車，朝山的方向駛去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road turns west after the old mill.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/west","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eb0815e47ad2e05f","term":"west","forms":["west","wests"],"pos":"noun","zh":"西方；西邊","explanation":"指與地球自轉方向相反的基本方位，也就是太陽通常落下的方向。","examples":[{"en":"The sun was setting in the west.","zh":"太陽正在西邊落下。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wide river forms the border to the west.","zh":"一條寬闊的河流構成了西部邊界。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/west","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d461db619066bf79fdaa","word":"western","forms":["western"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-822e55185f19acaa","term":"western","forms":["western"],"pos":"adj","zh":"西部的；向西的","explanation":"指位於西邊、朝向西邊，或與某個地區的西部有關。記住地圖上的西邊即可理解這個最基本的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The western entrance is closed after sunset.","zh":"西側入口在日落後關閉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They traveled through the western part of the country.","zh":"他們穿過了這個國家的西部。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/western","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2d7aeb122c925fe","term":"western","forms":["western"],"pos":"adj","zh":"西方的","explanation":"指屬於西方世界、來自西方，或採用西方常見方式的事物。這是從“西邊”擴充套件出的文化和社會意義。","examples":[{"en":"The museum compares Eastern and Western art.","zh":"這家博物館比較東方藝術和西方藝術。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report explains how Western-style writing spread in the region.","zh":"這份報告解釋了西式書寫如何在該地區傳播。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/western","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9a6f079920ea05e2","term":"western","forms":["western","more Western","most Western"],"pos":"adj","zh":"西方世界的","explanation":"指西方國家、社會、文化或思想體系的，重點不在地圖上的西邊，而在“西方世界”這一文化概念。","examples":[{"en":"Western culture has influenced the city's food and music.","zh":"西方文化影響了這座城市的飲食和音樂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The course examines western approaches to individual rights.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/western","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-083033dc3c94cdd8","term":"western","forms":["western","westerns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"西部片","explanation":"這是把“西部”從地點擴充套件成作品型別：故事通常以美國歷史上的西部為背景，圍繞牛仔、執法者、罪犯、農場或鐵路等衝突展開。","examples":[{"en":"We watched a classic western about a sheriff and a gang.","zh":"我們看了一部講警長和幫派的經典西部片。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her new novel is a western set near a mining town.","zh":"她的新小說是一部以礦業小鎮附近為背景的西部題材作品。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/western","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-534c51e17770c9b7a5aa","word":"wet","forms":["wet"],"officialPos":"adj./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f4212550c7b95e57","term":"wet","forms":["wet","wetter","wettest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"被液體弄溼的","explanation":"指物體表面被水或其他液體覆蓋，或已經吸收了液體；這就是“被水或液體覆蓋”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"My shoes are wet from walking through the grass.","zh":"我的鞋因為走過草地而溼了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Hang the wet towels outside to dry.","zh":"把溼毛巾掛到外面晾乾。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1cd5b6839238d41a","term":"wet","forms":["wet","wets","wetting","wetted"],"pos":"verb","zh":"弄溼或變溼","explanation":"表示東西被水或其他液體沾上而變溼，或使東西沾上液體；這正是wet“被液體覆蓋”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"My shoes got wet in the rain.","zh":"我的鞋在雨中被淋溼了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wet the sponge before using it.","zh":"使用海綿前先把它弄溼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a5d2ae286d0d9e45c062","word":"whale","forms":["whale"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7497aceb5ca7c172","term":"whale","forms":["whale","whales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鯨","explanation":"指生活在海里的大型哺乳動物，通常說的鯨不包括海豚和鼠海豚。記住它的核心畫面就是體形龐大的海洋動物。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a whale surface near the boat.","zh":"我們看見一頭鯨在船附近浮出水面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several whales migrate through these waters every year.","zh":"每年都有幾種鯨經過這些海域遷徙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e6a46ebcbc93001","term":"whale","forms":["whale","whales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"龐然大物；規模特別大的人或事","explanation":"借鯨的巨大體形，whale 可指特別大的人、事物或任務，重點是規模驚人，不一定是重量大。","examples":[{"en":"That was a whale of a project, but we finished it on time.","zh":"那是個規模特別大的專案，但我們還是按時完成了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That's a whale of a dictionary to carry around.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3982ea295917ab203aa0","word":"wharf","forms":["wharf"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-01897e86eeb691ba","term":"wharf","forms":["wharf","wharves","wharfs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碼頭","explanation":"指修建在河邊或海邊、供船隻靠岸、上下貨物或人員的人工平臺，是wharf最核心、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The fishing boats returned to the wharf before sunset.","zh":"漁船在日落前回到了碼頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Workers loaded the crates onto the wharf.","zh":"工人們把木箱搬到了碼頭上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wharf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-749ab2c0d06c42ae3b84","word":"what","forms":["what"],"officialPos":"pron./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d14cb81e813ac450","term":"what","forms":["what"],"pos":"det","zh":"哪一種；什麼樣的","explanation":"what 放在名詞前，要求對方從開放的可能性中說明是哪一種或具有什麼性質，例如詢問顏色、職業或計劃。","examples":[{"en":"What colour would you like for the walls?","zh":"你想把牆刷成什麼顏色？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What kind of music does your sister enjoy?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/what","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-36904707d548fdc0","term":"what","forms":["what"],"pos":"pron","zh":"什麼；哪件事","explanation":"what 單獨作代詞時，直接指向說話人還不知道身份、數量、性質或用途的事物，是“伸手指向未知物件”的最基本用法。","examples":[{"en":"What are you looking for?","zh":"你在找什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"What should I bring to the picnic?","zh":"我該帶什麼去野餐？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/what","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7e710277619ca78","term":"what","forms":["what"],"pos":"pron","zh":"……的東西；……的內容","explanation":"what 引出的從句可以整體代替“某個東西或內容”，例如“我知道你想要的東西”，因此它既連線從句，又在從句中承擔賓語等成分。","examples":[{"en":"Take what you need from the cupboard.","zh":"把櫥櫃裡你需要的東西拿走。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I finally understand what she means.","zh":"我終於明白她是什麼意思了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/what","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-85738f8f9a7f1b04b532","word":"whatever","forms":["whatever"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ef9da5c346cc3529","term":"whatever","forms":["whatever"],"pos":"det","zh":"無論……","explanation":"表示無論後面的情況怎樣，主句結果都不改變；它把各種可能都包進“什麼情況都算”。","examples":[{"en":"Whatever route you take, leave before sunrise.","zh":"無論你走哪條路線，都要在日出前出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whatever the result, we will learn from it.","zh":"無論結果如何，我們都會從中吸取教訓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whatever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dab648cab62c9152","term":"whatever","forms":["whatever"],"pos":"det","zh":"任何……的；無論哪種……的","explanation":"限定一個名詞，表示符合後面條件的任何物件，不限制它屬於哪一種。","examples":[{"en":"Whatever advice you receive, check the source first.","zh":"無論你收到什麼建議，都先核實來源。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Take whatever tools you need from the cupboard.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whatever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3e64c28f9fd9ab75","term":"whatever","forms":["whatever"],"pos":"pron","zh":"無論什麼","explanation":"表示不論發生什麼事、採取什麼行動，後面的結果都成立；它把所有可能情況都包含進去。","examples":[{"en":"Whatever happens, stay calm.","zh":"無論發生什麼，都要保持冷靜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She will support you whatever you decide.","zh":"無論你決定什麼，她都會支援你。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whatever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-608e9e39d77f968f","term":"whatever","forms":["whatever"],"pos":"pron","zh":"凡是……的；任何……的東西","explanation":"指滿足某個動作或條件的任何事物，常可理解為“凡是能……的東西”。","examples":[{"en":"Take whatever you need.","zh":"你需要什麼就拿什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whatever survives the inspection will be donated to the shelter.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whatever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-006f92f1bdf8ced9c574","word":"whatsoever","forms":["whatsoever"],"officialPos":"adj./pron.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7ab7efc97435bb51","term":"whatsoever","forms":["whatsoever"],"pos":"det","zh":"任何的；無論什麼樣的","explanation":"放在名詞前時，它表示不論是哪一種目的、原因或其他情況，範圍都不受限制。這是副詞“徹底擴大範圍”這一核心意思在名詞前的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The funds may be used for whatsoever purpose the committee approves.","zh":"這筆資金可用於委員會批准的任何目的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He offered no explanation whatsoever for his absence.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whatsoever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-de6c334339ac3d3209cd","word":"wheat","forms":["wheat"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9d14fad305c0d8a7","term":"wheat","forms":["wheat","wheats"],"pos":"noun","zh":"小麥；麥粒","explanation":"指小麥這種穀物，尤其是可收穫、加工並磨成烘焙用麵粉的麥粒。它是記憶這個詞最重要的核心義：麥田裡的穀物可以進一步變成麵包、麵粉等食品。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers harvest the wheat in late summer.","zh":"農民在夏末收割小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This bread is made with whole wheat flour.","zh":"這種麵包是用全麥麵粉做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wheat","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba59926159d2aa256eb8","word":"wheel","forms":["wheel"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-19e96a336e435e1d","term":"wheel","forms":["wheel","wheels"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輪子","explanation":"能繞軸轉動、幫助車輛移動或讓機器工作的圓形裝置，是wheel最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"One of the car's wheels is flat.","zh":"這輛車有一個輪胎沒氣了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wheels of the cart turned slowly.","zh":"手推車的輪子慢慢轉動著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wheel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ce5793ab2acfeb622b6f","word":"wheelchair","forms":["wheelchair"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-648135085678f821","term":"wheelchair","forms":["wheelchair","wheelchairs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"輪椅","explanation":"一種裝有大輪子的椅子，行動不便的人可以坐在上面移動或被人推動。它是這個詞最常見、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"After the operation, she used a wheelchair for several weeks.","zh":"手術後，她有幾個星期都要使用輪椅。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The station has a ramp for people in wheelchairs.","zh":"這個車站有供坐輪椅的人使用的坡道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wheelchair","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-15eaa75240aed625be3e","word":"when","forms":["when"],"officialPos":"adv./conj./pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b5a0c951452c83e4","term":"when","forms":["when"],"pos":"adv","zh":"什麼時候；何時","explanation":"用於詢問某件事發生的時間，也可以引出間接疑問。它是“時間線索”最直接的用法。","examples":[{"en":"When will the meeting start?","zh":"會議什麼時候開始？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't know when she will be back.","zh":"我不知道她什麼時候回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/when","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c1a33a9eb7c059cc","term":"when","forms":["when"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在……的時候；那時","explanation":"用於連線一個表示時間的從句，說明主句事件發生在什麼時間。這裡的 when 就像把兩個時間點連起來。","examples":[{"en":"I still remember the day when we moved into this house.","zh":"我仍然記得我們搬進這所房子的那一天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That was the moment when everything changed.","zh":"那就是一切發生改變的時刻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/when","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3f79bb078863cb0c","term":"when","forms":["when"],"pos":"adv","zh":"……的時間；何時","explanation":"when 本身代替“那個時間”，不再直接修飾一個時間名詞，常用於回憶、說明或討論某件事發生的時間。","examples":[{"en":"Do you remember when this street was still quiet?","zh":"你還記得這條街還很安靜的時候嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"When will the repairs be finished?","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/when","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2e44a77c2ea0c2d6ca3","word":"whenever","forms":["whenever"],"officialPos":"conj./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e30d7ab5efc18abd","term":"whenever","forms":["whenever"],"pos":"adv","zh":"任何時候；隨時","explanation":"whenever 表示時間沒有限制，意思是“任何時候”或“隨時”；它把一個具體時間點擴大成整段可選擇的時間範圍。","examples":[{"en":"You can call me whenever.","zh":"你隨時都可以給我打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Call whenever you have a question.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whenever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ee7967d90974e71","term":"whenever","forms":["whenever"],"pos":"adv","zh":"究竟什麼時候","explanation":"在疑問句中，whenever 是 when 的強調形式，常帶有著急、困惑或不耐煩的語氣，相當於“究竟什麼時候”。","examples":[{"en":"Whenever will I find time to finish this puzzle?","zh":"我究竟什麼時候才能找到時間完成這個拼圖？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whenever was that rule introduced? Nobody told me.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whenever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b48111c10c65fc119368","word":"where","forms":["where"],"officialPos":"conj./adv./pron./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-64d1a53eddf51c77","term":"where","forms":["where"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在哪裡；到哪裡","explanation":"用於詢問某人或某物所在、來自或要去的地點，相當於“在哪兒、從哪兒或到哪兒”，具體方向由動詞決定。","examples":[{"en":"Where did you put my keys?","zh":"你把我的鑰匙放哪兒了？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Where are these buses going?","zh":"這些公共汽車要開到哪裡？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/where","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7529ddc711d86e80","term":"where","forms":["where"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在……的地方","explanation":"引導地點從句，表示某事發生在主句所說的那個地方，也可表示回到或留在某個位置。","examples":[{"en":"Stay where you are until I come back.","zh":"待在原地，直到我回來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found the café where you used to work.","zh":"我們找到了你以前工作過的那家咖啡館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/where","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-31f17acb2fa220cd19f2","word":"whereabouts","forms":["whereabouts"],"officialPos":"n./adv.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-167342683d691e35","term":"whereabouts","forms":["whereabouts"],"pos":"adv","zh":"在哪裡；在什麼地方","explanation":"用於詢問某人或某物大概位於什麼地方，重點是尋找“位置”這條資訊，而不一定要求精確地址。","examples":[{"en":"Whereabouts do you live?","zh":"你住在哪一帶？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you know whereabouts the station is?","zh":"你知道車站大概在哪裡嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whereabouts","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4beb25356a5862e2","term":"whereabouts","forms":["whereabouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"下落；所在位置","explanation":"指某人或某物實際位於哪裡，也可指尋找某人或某物時所要查明的下落；它把“在哪裡”這個問題變成了要尋找的位置資訊。","examples":[{"en":"The police are trying to discover the whereabouts of the missing hiker.","zh":"警方正設法查明那名失蹤徒步者的下落。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Nobody knew the whereabouts of the missing manuscript.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whereabouts","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-a97541517d61b2f6edb6","word":"whereas","forms":["whereas"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"whereas","forms":["whereas"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"然而；反之；鑑於（正式文件用語）","examples":[{"en":"My brother prefers tea, whereas I usually drink coffee.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"The coastal region is wet, whereas the inland area is dry.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-b3922e60250ba1a13b5b","word":"wherever","forms":["wherever"],"officialPos":"adv./conj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fa27feb4c7411cd6","term":"wherever","forms":["wherever"],"pos":"adv","zh":"隨便哪裡；任何地方","explanation":"表示地點可以由人自由選擇，不必限定在哪一個地方；核心感覺是“哪兒都可以”或“隨便哪兒”。","examples":[{"en":"You can sit wherever you like.","zh":"你想坐哪兒都可以。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put the box wherever there is room.","zh":"把箱子放在有空位的任何地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wherever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-adba3bb3c90beddf","term":"wherever","forms":["wherever"],"pos":"adv","zh":"無論在哪裡；無論是哪裡","explanation":"引出一個表示地點的從句，指“無論是哪個地方”或“從哪個地方”；具體地點不重要，重點是後面的整件事。","examples":[{"en":"Wherever she goes, people remember her.","zh":"無論她走到哪裡，人們都會記住她。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wherever she travels, she carries a sketchbook.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wherever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3509fd899235fb8b7604","word":"whether","forms":["whether"],"officialPos":"conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"manual-1","term":"whether","forms":["whether"],"pos":"conj.","zh":"是否；不論…與否","examples":[{"en":"I do not know whether the shop is open today.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"},{"en":"We must decide whether to take the train or drive.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}]},{"id":"ceec-77bc06c55d29ee3cfa29","word":"which","forms":["which"],"officialPos":"pron./adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b3bc4f47a5d6e147","term":"which","forms":["which"],"pos":"det","zh":"哪一個；哪一種","explanation":"在幾個已經提到、看得見或可以想象的物件中詢問具體是哪一個。它通常放在名詞前，幫助聽者在一個範圍內作選擇。","examples":[{"en":"Which bus goes to the city centre?","zh":"哪輛公共汽車去市中心？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Which jacket do you prefer?","zh":"你更喜歡哪件夾克？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/which","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-54a12bf2d8938651","term":"which","forms":["which"],"pos":"pron","zh":"哪一個；哪一些","explanation":"不重複名詞，直接詢問若干已知物件中的哪一個或哪些。它和限定詞用法的核心相同，只是名詞被省略了。","examples":[{"en":"Which of these is yours?","zh":"這些當中哪一個是你的？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Which did you choose?","zh":"你選了哪一個？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/which","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-07a8750738828ffd36a9","word":"while","forms":["while"],"officialPos":"conj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5a81b6ae7e7cf64a","term":"while","forms":["while","whiles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一段時間","explanation":"while 指長度不確定的一段時間，可以很短，也可以相當長；具體長短要看上下文。","examples":[{"en":"We talked for quite a while after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後我們聊了相當長一段時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I haven't seen her in a while.","zh":"我有一陣子沒見到她了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/while","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-98fc3d91028a0f7e","term":"while","forms":["while","whiles","whiling","whiled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"消磨時間","explanation":"while away 表示把一段時間慢慢打發過去，通常帶有悠閒等待、閱讀或閒逛的意味；它正好體現了“讓這段時間過去”的核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"I whiled away the afternoon reading by the window.","zh":"我在窗邊讀書，悠閒地消磨了整個下午。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We whiled away the wait with a game.","zh":"我們用一場遊戲打發了等待的時間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/while","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-543cedde2003419ecb13","word":"whine","forms":["whine"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e9414693d00a632","term":"whine","forms":["whine","whines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"尖細拖長的聲音","explanation":"指尖細、拖長、通常讓人覺得刺耳或煩人的叫聲、哼聲；人的聲音和機器的聲音都可以這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"A sharp whine came from the old refrigerator.","zh":"舊冰箱裡傳出一陣刺耳的尖鳴聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppy let out a soft whine at the door.","zh":"小狗在門邊發出一聲輕輕的嗚咽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e8d9a0ae051bbe94","term":"whine","forms":["whine","whines","whining","whined","whinest","whinedst","whineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發出尖叫或嗚咽聲","explanation":"指人或動物發出尖細、拖長的叫聲，核心畫面就是聲音像一條拉長的細線，聽起來刺耳或可憐。","examples":[{"en":"The frightened dog whined under the table.","zh":"受驚的狗躲在桌子下面嗚咽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby began to whine when the lights went out.","zh":"燈熄滅後，嬰兒開始哼哼唧唧地哭鬧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-667bd02db6db6949","term":"whine","forms":["whine","whines","whining","whined","whinest","whinedst","whineth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"發牢騷；抱怨","explanation":"指用尖細、拖長、令人厭煩的方式抱怨；即使沒有真的發出尖聲，只要語氣像這種聲音，也可以用 whine。","examples":[{"en":"Stop whining about the homework and get started.","zh":"別再抱怨作業了，開始做吧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She kept whining that nobody listened to her.","zh":"她一直抱怨沒有人聽她說話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-eaeeef0170ecaecb5ec9","word":"whip","forms":["whip"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-62771c477084b2bd","term":"whip","forms":["whip","whips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鞭子","explanation":"一種細長、柔韌的工具，揮動時會發出清脆的聲音，常用於驅趕或引導動物；它體現了“快速抽動並施加力量”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The rider carried a whip but never used it on the horse.","zh":"騎手帶著一根鞭子，但從未用它抽打馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trainer cracked the whip to make the horses move.","zh":"馴馬師甩響鞭子，讓馬匹動起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-64929a155c205f26","term":"whip","forms":["whip","whips"],"pos":"noun","zh":"政黨督導員","explanation":"在議會或政黨內部，負責督促本黨議員按照黨派立場投票、傳達投票安排並維持紀律的人；這也是把“施加力量、約束行動”的鞭子形象引申到政治中的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The party whip asked all members to attend the vote.","zh":"黨鞭要求所有成員參加投票。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She served as a whip for the governing party.","zh":"她曾擔任執政黨的黨鞭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96146e0632f4ff03","term":"whip","forms":["whip","whips","whipping","whipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"用鞭子抽打","explanation":"用鞭子抽打某人或某物，體現了記憶鉤子中“鞭子施加力量”的基本動作。","examples":[{"en":"The rider whipped the horse to make it move faster.","zh":"騎手用鞭子抽打馬，讓它跑得更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guard was accused of whipping the prisoner.","zh":"那名守衛被指控用鞭子抽打囚犯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6ffd7efe9bc79646","term":"whip","forms":["whip","whips","whipping","whipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"快速攪打","explanation":"快速攪打食物，使其混入空氣並變得蓬鬆，正如鞭子快速抽動、帶動混合物運動。","examples":[{"en":"Whip the cream until it forms soft peaks.","zh":"把奶油打發到形成柔軟的尖峰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She whipped the eggs before adding the flour.","zh":"她先把雞蛋快速攪打均勻，再加入麵粉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whip","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0b1cc88d42a1dfdc8f24","word":"whiskey/whisky","forms":["whiskey"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73e9c9155b3784d7","term":"whiskey","forms":["whiskey","whiskeys","whiskies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"威士忌這種烈酒","explanation":"whiskey 是用穀物發酵後再蒸餾製成的烈酒，常見原料包括黑麥、玉米或大麥。它指的是酒這一類東西，而不只是某一杯酒。","examples":[{"en":"He keeps a bottle of whiskey in the kitchen cabinet.","zh":"他在廚房櫥櫃裡放著一瓶威士忌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This whiskey is made from malted barley.","zh":"這種威士忌用麥芽大麥製成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whiskey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-25d87a71a055e058","term":"whiskey","forms":["whiskey","whiskeys","whiskies"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一杯威士忌","explanation":"在點酒或談論飲用時，whiskey 也可以指一杯具體的威士忌，也就是從“這種酒”延伸到“裝在杯中的一份酒”。","examples":[{"en":"I'll have a whiskey before dinner.","zh":"晚飯前我要來一杯威士忌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He ordered two whiskeys for himself and his guest.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whiskey","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba7955598f2007bc8cee","word":"whisper","forms":["whisper"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0c97fe9a341efd70","term":"whisper","forms":["whisper","whispers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"低聲說話","explanation":"指說話聲音很小，通常只讓近處的人聽見，有時還強調沒有正常說話時那樣明顯的聲帶振動。它是whisper最基本、最容易帶出其他義項的意思。","examples":[{"en":"I answered in a whisper so the baby would not wake up.","zh":"我用耳語聲回答，免得把嬰兒吵醒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her name came out as barely a whisper.","zh":"她的名字幾乎只是以一聲低語說出來的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-451d704f24e88766","term":"whisper","forms":["whisper","whispers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"傳聞","explanation":"指沒有被正式證實、在私下悄悄流傳的訊息，常常讓人感覺事情可能正在發生。複數whispers尤其常表示各種傳聞或風聲。","examples":[{"en":"There are whispers of a new restaurant opening near the station.","zh":"車站附近要開一家新餐館的訊息正在私下流傳。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whispers of a merger circulated through the office.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2186551c5232a4b8","term":"whisper","forms":["whisper","whispers","whispering","whispered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"低聲說話","explanation":"指把聲音壓得很低，只讓身邊的人聽見，或幾乎不發出正常說話時的聲音。這個動作義是whisper最核心的用法。","examples":[{"en":"They whispered to each other during the meeting.","zh":"他們在會議期間互相低聲交談。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"“Be careful,” she whispered.","zh":"她低聲說：“小心。”","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d38c03d676cbc5f","term":"whisper","forms":["whisper","whispers","whispering","whispered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"低聲說出","explanation":"指把某個詞、句子或訊息用耳語聲說出來，而不是用正常音量說出。它和不及物義的區別在於這裡明確包含說出的內容。","examples":[{"en":"He whispered the answer in my ear.","zh":"他在我耳邊低聲說出了答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She whispered that the door was unlocked.","zh":"她低聲說門沒有鎖。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-fa82948800a46459b9df","word":"whistle","forms":["whistle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6a9ee2c350069908","term":"whistle","forms":["whistle","whistles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"哨子；發出哨聲的裝置","explanation":"指透過吹氣、蒸汽或其他機械作用發出 whistle 聲音的工具，例如裁判、警察或火車使用的哨子。它是“尖銳聲音”這個核心概念的實體化。","examples":[{"en":"The referee blew the whistle to stop the game.","zh":"裁判吹響哨子，示意比賽暫停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep a whistle in your bag in case you need help.","zh":"在包裡放一個哨子，以防需要求助。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cb4300af066be9f0","term":"whistle","forms":["whistle","whistles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"口哨聲；尖銳的高音","explanation":"指人或工具實際發出的清脆、尖銳的聲音；它仍然直接來自“吹口哨”這個核心畫面。","examples":[{"en":"We heard a whistle from the platform and hurried to the train.","zh":"我們聽到站臺上傳來一聲口哨，趕緊向火車跑去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A long whistle came from the referee.","zh":"裁判吹出了一聲長長的哨聲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-91f5e52463cbf002","term":"whistle","forms":["whistle","whistles","whistling","whistled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"吹口哨","explanation":"指人透過嘴唇、舌頭和牙齒控制氣流，發出尖銳的 whistle 聲音。它是這個詞最直接、最值得先掌握的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"She whistled softly while she washed the dishes.","zh":"她洗碗時輕輕地吹著口哨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The boy can whistle three different songs.","zh":"這個男孩會吹三首不同的歌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whistle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-018fa96a44715c90bf93","word":"white","forms":["white"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a08f534c9ba66c41","term":"white","forms":["white","whiter","more white","whitest","most white"],"pos":"adj","zh":"白色的","explanation":"指明亮而沒有明顯色彩、通常能反射可見光的顏色；可以把它理解為“白”這種明亮、沒有顏色的底色。","examples":[{"en":"Write in black ink on white paper.","zh":"用黑墨水寫在白紙上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The walls are painted white.","zh":"牆刷成了白色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a7efb793717d418f","term":"white","forms":["white","whiter","more white","whitest","most white"],"pos":"adj","zh":"歐洲人或歐洲裔的","explanation":"大寫的“White”在社會身份語境中指歐洲人或歐洲裔人，不是單純描述膚色；這是“白”從顏色底色引申到人群分類的用法。","examples":[{"en":"The study included White and Black participants.","zh":"這項研究包括白人和黑人參與者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The census recorded both white and Indigenous residents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-acc5b365fd3d9634","term":"white","forms":["white","whites"],"pos":"noun","zh":"白色","explanation":"white可以指白色本身，像雪或牛奶那樣明亮、沒有明顯其他顏色的顏色；這個“白”也可以作為物體的外觀或背景色。","examples":[{"en":"The walls were painted white to make the room look brighter.","zh":"牆刷成了白色，使房間看起來更明亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wore white at the summer wedding.","zh":"她在夏季婚禮上穿了一身白色衣服。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6ed0337140bd32b4adc5","word":"who","forms":["who"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4aeffbfdfed1592b","term":"who","forms":["who"],"pos":"pron","zh":"誰；哪一個人","explanation":"“who”用來詢問一個人或幾個人的身份，核心問題就是“是哪一個人”。它既能單獨作疑問句成分，也能出現在間接疑問句中。","examples":[{"en":"Who left this note on the table?","zh":"是誰把這張便條放在桌上的？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do you know who she invited?","zh":"你知道她邀請了誰嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/who","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d4f8bda0e1598794","term":"who","forms":["who"],"pos":"pron","zh":"……的人（主語）","explanation":"“who”可以連線一個描述人的從句，指代前面提到的那個人，並在從句中充當主語。例如“the woman who called”就是“打來電話的那位女士”。","examples":[{"en":"The woman who runs the bakery lives next door.","zh":"經營那家麵包店的女士住在隔壁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I thanked the teacher who helped me.","zh":"我感謝了幫助過我的老師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/who","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bb5d54010a1c2cd39b11","word":"whoever","forms":["whoever"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a998d2cb506e9b97","term":"whoever","forms":["whoever"],"pos":"pron","zh":"究竟是誰；到底是誰","explanation":"這是 who 的強調形式，用來強烈地追問或驚訝地問“到底是誰”。它通常帶有說話人的不解、懷疑或責備語氣。","examples":[{"en":"Whoever thought this was a good idea?","zh":"到底是誰覺得這是個好主意？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whoever would do such a thing?","zh":"究竟誰會做出這種事？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whoever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b61bcd4ff00a23c3","term":"whoever","forms":["whoever"],"pos":"pron","zh":"任何……的人","explanation":"表示“任何符合後面條件的人”，相當於“任何……的人”。它把“誰”和“……的人”合在一個詞裡，常引出一個從句。","examples":[{"en":"Whoever breaks the law will be punished.","zh":"任何違法的人都會受到懲罰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whoever arrives first can choose a seat.","zh":"任何先到的人都可以選座位。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whoever","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5d5766cf2d7870161420","word":"whole","forms":["whole"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-441b09942d810272","term":"whole","forms":["whole","wholer","more whole","wholest","most whole"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完整的；全部的","explanation":"表示一個東西作為整體存在，沒有被切開、拆散或只取其中一部分；也可強調某件事的全部範圍。","examples":[{"en":"I ate the whole fish.","zh":"我把整條魚都吃了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She spent the whole morning reading.","zh":"她整個上午都在讀書。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-eaf9e8522005ef7c","term":"whole","forms":["whole","wholer","more whole","wholest","most whole"],"pos":"adj","zh":"完好無損的；健康的","explanation":"強調人、身體或精神沒有受到損傷，仍然完整、正常；這是“沒有破損的整體”這一核心概念在人身上的延伸。","examples":[{"en":"After the accident, she was lucky to come home whole.","zh":"事故之後，她能毫髮無損地回家真是幸運。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fragile vase arrived whole despite the rough journey.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-101a71f888c96866","term":"whole","forms":["whole","wholes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"完整的整體","explanation":"指由許多部分組成、但被當作一個完整單位來看的東西；重點是各部分合在一起形成一個沒有缺口的整體。","examples":[{"en":"The small details form a beautiful whole.","zh":"這些小細節組成了一個美麗的整體。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The fragments fit together to form a single whole.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whole","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-12ddcbf42dc486453aab","word":"wholesale","forms":["wholesale"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d78a657849887252","term":"wholesale","forms":["wholesale","more wholesale","most wholesale"],"pos":"adj","zh":"批發的；大宗銷售的","explanation":"指商品不是逐件賣給最終消費者，而是以較大數量賣給零售商或其他商家再轉售。它強調的是整批交易這一方式。","examples":[{"en":"The store buys wholesale clothing from local manufacturers.","zh":"這家商店從本地製造商那裡批發服裝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wholesale prices are usually lower than retail prices.","zh":"批發價通常低於零售價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wholesale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1e3a7fea77d19e20","term":"wholesale","forms":["wholesale","more wholesale","most wholesale"],"pos":"adv","zh":"整批地；大宗地","explanation":"表示購買、銷售或處理商品時按大批數量進行，而不是一件一件地處理。","examples":[{"en":"Small shops often buy wholesale to keep their costs down.","zh":"小商店常常批次進貨，以降低成本。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These farmers sell their produce wholesale.","zh":"這些農民把農產品整批賣出。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wholesale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-449965fd16938d8c","term":"wholesale","forms":["wholesale","wholesales"],"pos":"noun","zh":"批發；批發業務","explanation":"指商品以較大數量賣給零售商或其他商家，再由他們轉賣給消費者的銷售環節或業務。","examples":[{"en":"She has worked in wholesale for more than ten years.","zh":"她從事批發業務已經十多年了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The firm concentrates on wholesale rather than retail.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wholesale","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-428dfcd94ca02b8e902d","word":"wholesome","forms":["wholesome"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8aefa9905eb4b5a9","term":"wholesome","forms":["wholesome","more wholesome","wholesomer","most wholesome","wholesomest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有益健康的","explanation":"指食物、生活方式等能促進身體健康、讓人感覺更有活力。這裡的重點是整體上對身體有好處，而不只是某一種營養成分。","examples":[{"en":"Fresh vegetables and whole grains make a wholesome meal.","zh":"新鮮蔬菜和全穀物能組成一頓有益健康的飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The café serves fresh, wholesome meals.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wholesome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-196e5b1675b0976e","term":"wholesome","forms":["wholesome","more wholesome","wholesomer","most wholesome","wholesomest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有益身心的","explanation":"指某種經歷、建議或思想能讓人的心理狀態和精神面貌變得更健康、更成熟。它強調這種影響有建設性，而不是隻讓人短暫開心。","examples":[{"en":"Talking honestly with a trusted friend was a wholesome experience.","zh":"和一位信任的朋友坦誠交談是一次有益身心的經歷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The book offers wholesome advice for dealing with failure.","zh":"這本書提供了應對失敗的有益建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wholesome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8e5efdde68f006304185","word":"whom","forms":["whom"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1392621b5d94c51f","term":"whom","forms":["whom","of who"],"pos":"pron","zh":"誰；哪個人","explanation":"用於正式地詢問動作涉及的物件，相當於“你找了誰”中的“誰”。它通常指人，並且在句中不是動作的執行者，而是被詢問、被邀請或被聯絡的人。","examples":[{"en":"Whom should we invite to the meeting?","zh":"我們應該邀請誰參加會議？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With whom did you travel?","zh":"你和誰一起旅行的？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78b2eb6bc06dd22d","term":"whom","forms":["whom","of who"],"pos":"pron","zh":"那個人；所……的人","explanation":"用於指回前面已經提到的人，把這個人放進後面的關係從句中，表示“我談到的那個人”或“你見過的那個人”。它表達的仍是“動作落到誰身上”這一核心，只是疑問變成了說明。","examples":[{"en":"She is the doctor whom I recommended for the job.","zh":"她就是我推薦來做這份工作的那位醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The guest whom you invited has arrived.","zh":"你邀請的那位客人已經到了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-55efa0938f9f52fb6de3","word":"whose","forms":["whose"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6bc7c490e7c32a29","term":"whose","forms":["whose"],"pos":"det","zh":"誰的？","explanation":"用於直接詢問某件東西屬於誰，相當於“誰的”。它通常放在所修飾的名詞前，尋找這件東西的主人。","examples":[{"en":"Whose keys are these?","zh":"這些鑰匙是誰的？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Whose phone is ringing?","zh":"誰的手機在響？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fb9e7ed7ec003898","term":"whose","forms":["whose"],"pos":"det","zh":"其……的；某人的……","explanation":"用於關係從句，表示前面提到的人擁有或關聯後面的名詞，相當於“某人的……的”或“其……的”。它把“主人”和“所屬物”連線起來。","examples":[{"en":"I met a woman whose son works at the hospital.","zh":"我遇到一位女士，她的兒子在醫院工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They hired a designer whose ideas were very practical.","zh":"他們聘請了一位想法非常實用的設計師。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whose","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2be23c585f15e5fd3279","word":"why","forms":["why"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b364c04d19d34f6","term":"why","forms":["why"],"pos":"adv","zh":"為什麼；為何","explanation":"用來直接詢問某件事的原因、目的或理由，相當於在追問“這件事是出於什麼原因”。","examples":[{"en":"Why did Maya leave so early?","zh":"瑪雅為什麼這麼早就走了？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Why are you keeping the window open?","zh":"你為什麼一直開著窗戶？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/why","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9ea8e73e63b72cca","term":"why","forms":["why"],"pos":"adv","zh":"這就是為什麼","explanation":"用來把前面的原因和後面的結果連起來，說明“前面所說的情況導致了後面的事情”。","examples":[{"en":"The roads were icy, and that's why the school closed.","zh":"路面結冰了，這就是學校停課的原因。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He had already eaten, which is why he skipped dessert.","zh":"他已經吃過東西了，所以沒吃甜點。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/why","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-148bd3fdbb83f84886f4","word":"wicked","forms":["wicked"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-18a268f9f2de7f93","term":"wicked","forms":["wicked","wickeder","more wicked","wickedest","most wicked"],"pos":"adj","zh":"邪惡的；頑劣的","explanation":"指本性或行為很壞，違反道德，常用於形容人、勢力、計劃或行為。它是 wicked 最傳統、最基本的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The wicked ruler treated his people cruelly.","zh":"那個邪惡的統治者殘酷地對待自己的人民。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They uncovered a wicked plan to harm innocent people.","zh":"他們發現了一個要傷害無辜者的邪惡計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wicked","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ccb747ce938d89dd","term":"wicked","forms":["wicked","wickeder","more wicked","wickedest","most wicked"],"pos":"adj","zh":"極棒的；厲害的","explanation":"在非正式口語中，wicked 可以把“壞得很”反轉成“厲害得不得了”，表示某人或某事非常出色、令人佩服。","examples":[{"en":"She played a wicked guitar solo at the concert.","zh":"她在音樂會上彈了一段超棒的吉他獨奏。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That skateboard trick was wicked!","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wicked","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0abaa40b10436a8fbba4","word":"wide","forms":["wide"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6d6eac5532c165d4","term":"wide","forms":["wide","wider","more wide","widest","most wide"],"pos":"adj","zh":"寬的；橫向很大的","explanation":"指從一邊到另一邊的距離很大，強調橫向空間寬闊。","examples":[{"en":"We walked down a wide corridor.","zh":"我們沿著一條寬闊的走廊走去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The river is wide at this point.","zh":"這條河在這裡很寬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0f22e4501ace8d37","term":"wide","forms":["wide","wider","more wide","widest","most wide"],"pos":"adj","zh":"範圍廣的；涉及面大的","explanation":"把“向兩邊展開”的空間概念用於抽象內容，表示涉及許多方面、物件或領域。","examples":[{"en":"The course covers a wide range of topics.","zh":"這門課程涵蓋廣泛的主題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new rules give managers wide discretion over working hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f574989b16acda33","term":"wide","forms":["wide","wider","widest"],"pos":"adv","zh":"廣泛地；到處","explanation":"表示範圍向各處延伸，強調覆蓋得很廣、傳播得很遠。","examples":[{"en":"Her story soon spread far and wide.","zh":"她的故事很快傳遍了各地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They searched far and wide for the missing dog.","zh":"他們到處尋找那條失蹤的狗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f826b6e0c7965b86b0b9","word":"widen","forms":["widen"],"officialPos":"v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-abb9f66d8e807ccf","term":"widen","forms":["widen","widens","widening","widened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變寬；變得更寬","explanation":"指某物本身從窄變寬，重點在寬度發生了變化，不強調是誰造成的。人的眼睛、道路、裂縫或笑容等都可以這樣描述。","examples":[{"en":"The road widened after the bridge.","zh":"過了橋以後，道路變寬了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her eyes widened in surprise.","zh":"她驚訝得睜大了眼睛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/widen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7aaf59f5841abd27","term":"widen","forms":["widen","widens","widening","widened"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使變寬","explanation":"指人或某種力量把道路、空間、裂縫等撐得更寬，是“向兩邊擴充套件”的主動動作。","examples":[{"en":"The city plans to widen the main road.","zh":"市政府計劃把主幹道拓寬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They widened the doorway to make it easier for wheelchairs to pass.","zh":"他們把門口加寬了，方便輪椅透過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/widen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d811aa2ea4fed8eedb2f","word":"widespread","forms":["widespread"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b27c1b77e9cb8676","term":"widespread","forms":["widespread","more widespread","widerspread","most widespread","widestspread"],"pos":"adj","zh":"廣泛存在的；普遍的","explanation":"指某種事物、現象或影響遍佈很大的區域，在許多地方都能發現；重點是覆蓋範圍廣，而不只是數量多。","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused widespread damage across the region.","zh":"這場風暴給該地區造成了大範圍的破壞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"There is widespread support for the new policy.","zh":"這項新政策得到了廣泛支援。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/widespread","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f887da96758813f5daa3","word":"widow/widower","forms":["widow","widower"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-73e15ab4828ad7ca","term":"widow","forms":["widow","widows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喪偶女性；喪偶者","explanation":"指配偶已經去世、留下獨自生活的人，傳統上主要指女性；男性通常另稱鰥夫。","examples":[{"en":"After her husband died, she became a widow at the age of forty.","zh":"丈夫去世後，她四十歲就成了寡婦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The widow of the former mayor donated his papers to the library.","zh":"前市長的遺孀把他的檔案捐給了圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/widow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f9a1578f68e5410","term":"widow","forms":["widow","widows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"配偶缺席者","explanation":"較少見地，它可以寬泛地指配偶不在身邊的人；這種用法比表示喪偶者更不常見，常需結合上下文理解。","examples":[{"en":"For months, she lived like a widow while her husband worked overseas.","zh":"丈夫在海外工作期間，她有好幾個月都過著彷彿守寡般的生活。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She calls herself a golf widow every summer weekend.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/widow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cc32b6221ce20668","term":"widower","forms":["widower","widowers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"鰥夫；喪妻男子","explanation":"妻子去世後，且通常還沒有再婚的男性，就是 widower。這個詞強調的是他與已故妻子的關係，而不只是“一個獨身男人”。","examples":[{"en":"After his wife died, he became a widower with two young children.","zh":"妻子去世後，他成了一個帶著兩個年幼孩子的鰥夫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The widower visits her grave every Sunday.","zh":"這位鰥夫每個星期天都去她的墓前。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/widower","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dec0f004eaa07c2a283e","word":"width","forms":["width"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d42d1171d6c624df","term":"width","forms":["width","widths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寬闊狀態","explanation":"指某物呈現出寬的狀態，強調橫向展開的程度，而不一定是在報告一個精確數值。它仍然圍繞“從兩邊向外展開的空間”這一核心概念。","examples":[{"en":"The width of the valley makes the river look very small.","zh":"山谷的寬闊讓河流顯得非常小。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The room has enough width for a large dining table.","zh":"這個房間的寬度足以放下一張大餐桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/width","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-17848f22ecacc623","term":"width","forms":["width","widths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"橫向尺寸","explanation":"指用測量得到的、從物體一側到另一側的距離，例如門、桌子或道路的寬度。這是日常生活中最常見的具體用法。","examples":[{"en":"We measured the width of the doorway before buying the sofa.","zh":"買沙發前，我們量了門口的寬度。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The road has a width of six metres at this point.","zh":"這段路的寬度是六米。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/width","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9d52a3c8e4d6e27de4ad","word":"wife","forms":["wife"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e40962cc08bd60f3","term":"wife","forms":["wife","wives"],"pos":"noun","zh":"妻子","explanation":"指已經結婚的女性，重點是她與配偶之間的婚姻關係，而不只是“女性”這一性別。","examples":[{"en":"His wife works at the local library.","zh":"他的妻子在當地的圖書館工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She introduced me to her wife at the party.","zh":"她在聚會上把我介紹給了她的妻子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wife","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-2249476332138d1ed3ea","word":"wig","forms":["wig"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f9a4d7a3811fa48","term":"wig","forms":["wig","wigs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"假髮","explanation":"wig 是戴在頭上的一整頂真發或合成發製品，可以用來遮蓋禿髮、改變外貌、遵循文化或宗教習俗，也常用於時裝和表演。它強調的是“替代或偽裝頭髮的整件物品”，不是普通的頭髮。","examples":[{"en":"The actor put on a white wig for the role.","zh":"這名演員為了這個角色戴上了一頂白色假髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wears a wig when she goes out.","zh":"她出門時會戴假髮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wig","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e73b026cfd1b008c558","word":"wild","forms":["wild"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-53de26a7a88aa154","term":"wild","forms":["wild","wilder","wildest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"野生的；未馴服的","explanation":"指動物、植物或自然環境沒有被人馴養、培育或控制，保留著自然狀態。這是 wild 最基本、最容易連線到其他義項的意思。","examples":[{"en":"We saw several wild elephants near the river.","zh":"我們在河邊看到了幾頭野生大象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This bird is common in the wild but rarely kept as a pet.","zh":"這種鳥在野外很常見，但很少被當作寵物飼養。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-015ca4d1b8e02e38","term":"wild","forms":["wild","wilder","wildest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不受控制的；強烈奔放的","explanation":"從沒有圍欄的荒野引申而來，表示情緒、行為或力量衝破了通常的限制，顯得猛烈、奔放或無法自制。","examples":[{"en":"The crowd went wild when the home team scored.","zh":"主隊進球時，人群興奮得失去了控制。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was filled with wild anger after hearing the accusation.","zh":"聽到那項指責後，她滿腔怒火。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26bd833550318a4d","term":"wild","forms":["wild","wilds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"野外的自然狀態","explanation":"指動物沒有被馴養、生活在自然環境中的狀態，也就是“野外”這一與人類管理相對的空間或狀態。","examples":[{"en":"The rescued fox was healthy enough to return to the wild.","zh":"獲救的狐狸已經足夠健康，可以回到野外了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The rescued owl was returned to the wild.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7dab81ed42daebac0d1e","word":"wilderness","forms":["wilderness"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b617d83568a878d4","term":"wilderness","forms":["wilderness","wildernesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"自然荒野；未開發的荒地","explanation":"指沒有被耕種或定居、仍由野生動物和自然植物佔據的土地；也可指這樣的一片荒地。核心畫面就是沒有人工整理的自然空間。","examples":[{"en":"They spent three days hiking through the wilderness.","zh":"他們花了三天徒步穿越荒野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow trail led into the wilderness.","zh":"一條狹窄的小路通向荒野。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wilderness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55a145aea5afa7ee","term":"wilderness","forms":["wilderness","wildernesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"令人迷失的混亂處境","explanation":"指一個讓人摸不清方向、難以找到出路的地方或情境，可以是現實空間，也可以是思想、資訊或生活中的混亂。它就是“走進荒野而迷路”的比喻。","examples":[{"en":"Without a map, the city became a wilderness of unfamiliar streets.","zh":"沒有地圖，這座城市就變成了一片由陌生街道組成的迷宮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt lost in a wilderness of conflicting advice.","zh":"面對相互矛盾的建議，她感到無所適從。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wilderness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-33445260df1bc49114ee","word":"wildlife","forms":["wildlife"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8eec6b87ce132c7c","term":"wildlife","forms":["wildlife"],"pos":"noun","zh":"野生動物","explanation":"指生活在自然環境中、沒有被人類馴養的動物，最常見的是熊、鹿、兔子、鳥和魚等。這裡強調的是動物處於野外自然狀態，而不是家養狀態。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a lot of wildlife during our walk through the forest.","zh":"我們穿過森林時看到了許多野生動物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The park is famous for its wildlife tours.","zh":"這個公園以野生動物觀賞之旅聞名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wildlife","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a40810f94799a3af","term":"wildlife","forms":["wildlife"],"pos":"noun","zh":"野生生物","explanation":"泛指所有生活在自然環境中的未馴化生物，範圍比“野生動物”更大，也可以包括植物和其他生物。只有在上下文明確擴大範圍時，才需要這樣理解。","examples":[{"en":"The new road could harm wildlife in the area.","zh":"這條新公路可能會傷害當地的野生生物。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wetland supports a remarkable variety of wildlife.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wildlife","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bc16f5825a9dafc8c245","word":"will","forms":["will"],"officialPos":"aux./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4342fa5e87aa9c8c","term":"will","forms":["will","wills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意志；自主選擇能力","explanation":"will 是一個人按自己的選擇作決定、堅持行動的內在能力；它強調“自己能作主”，不只是短暫的想法。","examples":[{"en":"She found the will to start again.","zh":"她找到了重新開始的意志。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one can break his will.","zh":"沒有人能摧毀他的意志。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/will","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-9fcb565153c9387b","term":"will","forms":["will","wills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"意願；決定；命令","explanation":"當一個人的意志被別人接受並要求照辦時，will 可以指這個人的決定或命令；服從某人的 will，就是按其意願行事。","examples":[{"en":"The workers refused to obey the owner's will.","zh":"工人們拒絕服從老闆的意願。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council acted against the will of the residents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/will","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-06c780a740dfed61","term":"will","forms":["will","wills"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遺囑","explanation":"在法律語境中，will 是人預先寫下的正式檔案，用來說明去世後財產和其他事務應怎樣處理。","examples":[{"en":"Her house was named in the will.","zh":"遺囑中寫明瞭她的房子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He left his books to the library in his will.","zh":"他在遺囑中把自己的書留給了圖書館。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/will","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e5a872fdb558965d","term":"will","forms":["will","willing","would"],"pos":"verb","zh":"將要；會","explanation":"will 加動詞原形，表示說話時判斷某事將在將來發生；在第一人稱中有時還帶有“我決定要這樣做”的堅定意味。","examples":[{"en":"I will call you when I arrive.","zh":"我到了以後會給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The train will leave in ten minutes.","zh":"火車十分鐘後出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/will","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a570634ce8b2031d","term":"will","forms":["will","willing","would"],"pos":"verb","zh":"願意；肯","explanation":"在疑問句、否定句或請求中，will 表示一個人是否願意選擇做某事，核心仍是“作出意願和決定”。","examples":[{"en":"Will you help me carry this box?","zh":"你願意幫我搬這個箱子嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The baby won't sleep.","zh":"這個嬰兒就是不肯睡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/will","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca0f69b95d71fe5f9357","word":"willing","forms":["willing"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b87c2a34496f90bc","term":"willing","forms":["willing","more willing","most willing"],"pos":"adj","zh":"願意的；不反對的","explanation":"這個詞描寫一個人點頭並準備邁出一步：即使事情需要改變或付出努力，他也不拒絕去做。","examples":[{"en":"She is willing to listen and try again.","zh":"她願意聽取意見，再試一次。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Are you willing to change your plans?","zh":"你願意改變計劃嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/willing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-823a3180dad3c9c3c4de","word":"win","forms":["win"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-336fb8f9ca3f561c","term":"win","forms":["win","wins"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次勝利","explanation":"指在比賽、競爭或對抗中取得的一次勝利，也就是動詞 win 所產生的結果。","examples":[{"en":"The team celebrated its first win of the season.","zh":"這支隊伍慶祝了本賽季的首場勝利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow win secured her place in the championship final.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/win","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-030b0eab67271395","term":"win","forms":["win","wins","winning","won","wan","winnest","wonnest","winneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"贏得比賽","explanation":"指在比賽、戰爭或競爭中獲勝，把勝利拿到手。","examples":[{"en":"Our team won the final by two goals.","zh":"我們隊以兩球的優勢贏得了決賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She trained hard and won the race.","zh":"她刻苦訓練，贏得了這場比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/win","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c1059bbd6a79af1","term":"win","forms":["win","wins","winning","won","wan","winnest","wonnest","winneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"贏得獎品","explanation":"指透過比賽、抽獎或其他競爭成功獲得獎品、獎金等東西。","examples":[{"en":"He won a new bicycle in the school competition.","zh":"他在學校比賽中贏得了一輛新腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She won a silver medal in the relay.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/win","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-52d801f190e4d173","term":"win","forms":["win","wins","winning","won","wan","winnest","wonnest","winneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"獲勝","explanation":"不帶直接賓語時，表示自己或己方取得勝利，即“贏了”。","examples":[{"en":"Nobody expected us to win, but we did.","zh":"沒人料到我們會贏，但我們確實贏了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Who do you think will win?","zh":"你覺得誰會贏？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/win","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b58e68145a79ca0e199","word":"wind","forms":["wind"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c2fdce7849e65ae7","term":"wind","forms":["wind","winds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"風","explanation":"“wind”最基本的畫面是空氣在流動，也就是自然界中的風；它可以輕柔，也可以很強。","examples":[{"en":"A cold wind blew through the open window.","zh":"一陣冷風從敞開的窗戶吹了進來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wind grew stronger as the storm approached.","zh":"暴風雨臨近時，風變得更大了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-497c5f8cc55213c3","term":"wind","forms":["wind","winds","winding","wound","winded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"纏繞","explanation":"把線、繩等一圈圈繞到某物上，或繞成團；重點是東西在轉動中形成纏繞。","examples":[{"en":"She wound the thread around the spool.","zh":"她把線纏在了線軸上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He wound the loose cable into a neat coil.","zh":"他把鬆散的電纜纏成了整齊的一圈。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1fb7578d5a2e140e","term":"wind","forms":["wind","winds","winding","wound","winded"],"pos":"verb","zh":"給鐘錶上發條","explanation":"透過轉動發條，讓鐘錶或類似的機械裝置獲得執行所需的動力。","examples":[{"en":"I wound the old clock before going to bed.","zh":"我睡覺前給那隻舊鐘上了發條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The toy stopped because nobody had wound it up.","zh":"這個玩具停了，因為沒人給它上發條。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-44ff7b02c80d38b26dd6","word":"window","forms":["window"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce7f39d9ecb77ae9","term":"window","forms":["window","windows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"窗戶","explanation":"牆、屋頂或車輛上的開口，通常裝有玻璃，讓光線和空氣進入，也讓人能夠向外看。它是 window 最基本、最具體的意思。","examples":[{"en":"Could you open the window? The room is getting stuffy.","zh":"你能把窗戶開啟嗎？房間裡越來越悶了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She sat by the window and watched the rain.","zh":"她坐在窗邊看雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/window","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-541f086ffee4a541","term":"window","forms":["window","windows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"有限時段；機會視窗","explanation":"比喻一扇只在短時間內開啟的窗，指某件事可行、可獲得或可安排的有限時段和機會。","examples":[{"en":"We have a narrow window of time to finish the repairs.","zh":"我們只有很短的一段時間來完成維修。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The spacecraft will launch during a three-hour window.","zh":"航天器將在三個小時的發射時段內升空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/window","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-74d4f15c650db0982e84","word":"windshield","forms":["windshield"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-29e4ad851356224a","term":"windshield","forms":["windshield","windshields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擋風玻璃","explanation":"車輛前方供駕駛員和乘客前方使用的透明玻璃屏障，用來擋住行駛時的風、雨、冰雪等。它通常特指車前玻璃，不是車輛側面的普通車窗。","examples":[{"en":"The windshield was covered in frost, so I had to wait before driving.","zh":"擋風玻璃結滿了霜，所以我得等一會兒才能開車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small stone cracked the windshield on the highway.","zh":"在高速公路上，一塊小石子把擋風玻璃砸裂了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/windshield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2f8651280ea7970e","term":"windshield","forms":["windshield","windshields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"麥克風防風罩","explanation":"套在麥克風外面的罩子，用來減弱風聲和呼吸聲等氣流噪音，使錄音或擴音更清楚。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter put a windshield over the microphone before recording outside.","zh":"記者在戶外錄音前給麥克風套上了防風罩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wind noise ruined the interview because the recorder lacked a windshield.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/windshield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87480c5a4819536e47c0","word":"windy","forms":["windy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1b10581f6c910e10","term":"windy","forms":["windy","windier","windiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有風的；風大的","explanation":"指某處或某段時間風很明顯，風吹得到人或物。這是 windy 最基本、最常用的意思。","examples":[{"en":"It was too windy to sit outside.","zh":"風太大了，沒法坐在外面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We had a cold and windy morning.","zh":"那天早晨又冷，風又大。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/windy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-55acc25e0093b6a3","term":"windy","forms":["windy","windier","windiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"無遮蔽、迎風的","explanation":"指地方敞開、沒有遮擋，因此容易受到風吹。重點不只是天氣有風，而是這個地點本身暴露在風中。","examples":[{"en":"The hilltop is beautiful but very windy.","zh":"山頂很美，但風特別大，而且沒有什麼遮擋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The exposed plateau was too windy for a picnic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/windy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-32c4feed996880bc92a0","word":"wine","forms":["wine"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6b0be91bef9d7421","term":"wine","forms":["wine","wines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"葡萄酒","explanation":"wine 通常指由葡萄汁發酵製成的酒，是這個詞最核心、最常見的意思。它可以泛指這種飲料，也可以指餐桌上的葡萄酒。","examples":[{"en":"We had wine with dinner.","zh":"我們晚餐時喝了葡萄酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This wine goes well with fish.","zh":"這種葡萄酒很適合配魚。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a3b07164ab434e9","term":"wine","forms":["wine","wines"],"pos":"noun","zh":"其他材料釀成的類似酒","explanation":"wine 有時泛指酒精度和飲用方式類似葡萄酒的發酵飲料，即使原料不是葡萄，例如米、李子或蒲公英。","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant serves homemade plum wine.","zh":"這家餐館供應自制的梅酒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They make wine from elderberries grown nearby.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c047caef95b4d3e8d7f7","word":"wing","forms":["wing"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee5addfbad12d717","term":"wing","forms":["wing","wings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物的翅膀","explanation":"鳥、蝙蝠和某些昆蟲身體兩側用來飛行的部分；按照記憶中的畫面，它是從身體兩側伸展開、幫助動物移動的“翅膀”。","examples":[{"en":"The eagle spread its wings and rose above the valley.","zh":"那隻鷹展開翅膀，飛到了山谷上空。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young bird was flapping its wings but could not fly yet.","zh":"那隻幼鳥不停地扇動翅膀，但還不會飛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b49eec765c5afc8b","term":"wing","forms":["wing","wings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"飛機的機翼","explanation":"飛機兩側產生升力、幫助飛機升空和飛行的部分；它同樣是從主體兩側伸出的“翅膀”。","examples":[{"en":"We sat beside the wing and watched the flaps move during takeoff.","zh":"我們坐在機翼旁邊，看著襟翼在起飛時移動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Ice formed along the aircraft's wings.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8cdd77764a1f6033","term":"wing","forms":["wing","wings"],"pos":"noun","zh":"建築物或整體的側翼","explanation":"主體旁邊較小、與主體相連或相鄰的附加部分，例如醫院的西翼；它符合“從主體兩側伸展開”的記憶畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The children’s ward is in the west wing of the hospital.","zh":"兒童病房在醫院的西翼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The new wing contains laboratories and teaching rooms.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wing","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-43e26a97aa61e86dfc93","word":"wink","forms":["wink"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ebd75935f8c12b5d","term":"wink","forms":["wink","winks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"眨一隻眼；使眼色","explanation":"眨一隻眼的動作，常常是在不明說的情況下傳遞暗號、默契或調侃。","examples":[{"en":"She gave me a wink when the teacher turned around.","zh":"老師轉過身時，她朝我使了個眼色。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He answered with a wink and a smile.","zh":"他眨了眨眼，帶著笑回答了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a9005c2ef8126730","term":"wink","forms":["wink","winks","winking","winked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"眨一隻眼使眼色","explanation":"有意閉上一隻眼，把它當作暗號、默契、調侃或含蓄建議傳給別人。","examples":[{"en":"Tom winked at me to show that he was joking.","zh":"湯姆朝我眨了眨眼，表示他是在開玩笑。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She winked her left eye and pointed toward the door.","zh":"她眨了眨左眼，指了指門。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wink","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c6f51afdddd2551a91a3","word":"wipe","forms":["wipe"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05de71ae2bfdb8d8","term":"wipe","forms":["wipe","wipes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"溼巾；擦拭布","explanation":"指專門用來擦東西的柔軟布片或類似材料，常見的是溼巾，也可以泛指一小塊擦拭用材料。","examples":[{"en":"Keep a pack of wipes in the car for messy hands.","zh":"在車裡放一包溼巾，手弄髒時可以用。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She cleaned the phone with an alcohol wipe.","zh":"她用酒精溼巾清潔手機。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-648f4ee45bf6571c","term":"wipe","forms":["wipe","wipes","wiping","wiped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦拭","explanation":"讓某個物體沿著表面移動並保持接觸，目的是擦掉表面的灰塵、水或其他東西。這是 wipe 最基本的動作義。","examples":[{"en":"She wiped her glasses with a soft cloth.","zh":"她用軟布擦了擦眼鏡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Wipe the counter with a clean towel.","zh":"用乾淨的毛巾擦一下臺面。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab597fa71b38ddbf","term":"wipe","forms":["wipe","wipes","wiping","wiped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擦掉；抹去","explanation":"強調透過擦拭把液體、汙跡、眼淚等從表面去掉，重點是結果已經被清除。","examples":[{"en":"He wiped the tears from his face.","zh":"他擦去了臉上的淚水。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please wipe the mud off your shoes.","zh":"請把鞋上的泥擦掉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-44469a7ba4d1c100","term":"wipe","forms":["wipe","wipes","wiping","wiped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"刪除；抹掉資料","explanation":"把資訊從電腦、磁碟或其他系統中徹底刪除，概念上和把汙跡擦掉相同，只是被擦掉的是資料。","examples":[{"en":"Make a backup before you wipe the old laptop.","zh":"擦除舊膝上型電腦上的資料前，先做好備份。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The program securely wipes deleted files.","zh":"這個程式會安全地徹底擦除已刪除的檔案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9b2abfc29cc47494c871","word":"wire","forms":["wire"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ba741d1aff51b2e6","term":"wire","forms":["wire","wires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"金屬絲","explanation":"wire 最基本的畫面是一條均勻、細長的金屬線，通常由金屬拉制而成。它是許多電線、圍欄和其他金屬製品的基礎材料。","examples":[{"en":"The basket is made of thin wire.","zh":"這個籃子是用細金屬絲做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Be careful—the wire is sharp.","zh":"小心，這根金屬絲很鋒利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3b30f378b82758ea","term":"wire","forms":["wire","wires"],"pos":"noun","zh":"電線","explanation":"當這根金屬線用來傳輸電流時，wire 就是電線或導線；這是日常生活中最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"That wire powers the lamp.","zh":"那根電線給檯燈供電。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Do not touch the exposed wire.","zh":"不要碰裸露的電線。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wire","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7c68b70cea5555e5419f","word":"wisdom","forms":["wisdom"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3cf9c543baf7e72f","term":"wisdom","forms":["wisdom","wisdoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"明辨是非的智慧","explanation":"wisdom是一種人格品質，使人能分辨什麼做法明智、什麼做法不明智，並據此穩妥地生活和行動。","examples":[{"en":"She had the wisdom to wait until everyone had calmed down.","zh":"她很有智慧，知道要等大家都冷靜下來再行動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Age does not automatically bring wisdom.","zh":"年紀增長並不會自動帶來智慧。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wisdom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e23da8ea6e162dc9","term":"wisdom","forms":["wisdom","wisdoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"把知識靈活用於新處境","explanation":"這裡的智慧像一盞能換角度照路的燈：人不只是記住過去學到的東西，還能把它領會後遷移到不同的新情況中。","examples":[{"en":"He applied the wisdom he had learned in business to managing the community project.","zh":"他把在商業中學到的智慧運用到社群專案的管理上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Experience gave her the wisdom to adapt rather than panic.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wisdom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a31c931873b5924","term":"wisdom","forms":["wisdom","wisdoms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"結合知識與經驗作判斷","explanation":"這種智慧幫助人綜合知識、經驗和直覺，在不確定時作出穩妥而有根據的決定。","examples":[{"en":"With wisdom and patience, the nurse decided when to call the doctor.","zh":"護士憑藉智慧和耐心，判斷出了該在什麼時候叫醫生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her wisdom helped the family choose a safer course.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wisdom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c88af1b79306369631c6","word":"wise","forms":["wise"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e8e3a03b289df80","term":"wise","forms":["wise","wiser","more wise","wisest","most wise"],"pos":"adj","zh":"明智的；有判斷力的","explanation":"指一個人或決定能根據經驗和判斷作出正確、穩妥的選擇，不只是反應快或知識多。","examples":[{"en":"Saving some money for emergencies was a wise decision.","zh":"存一些錢應急是個明智的決定。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It would be wise to check the weather before we leave.","zh":"我們出發前先檢視天氣會比較明智。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8847eab462887e43","term":"wise","forms":["wise","wiser","more wise","wisest","most wise"],"pos":"adj","zh":"自作聰明的；無禮頂嘴的","explanation":"在帶有諷刺或惱怒的口語中，wise 表示一個人故意耍聰明、頂嘴或不尊重別人。","examples":[{"en":"Don't get wise with me, young man.","zh":"小夥子，別跟我耍聰明頂嘴。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He got wise with the teacher and was sent outside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wise","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-091e606752615c91da70","word":"wish","forms":["wish"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-86407533fb7ce843","term":"wish","forms":["wish","wishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"願望；希望","explanation":"指希望某件事發生，或希望得到某樣東西的心情。它強調心中朝向某個目標的願望，不一定表示這個目標很現實或很容易實現。","examples":[{"en":"Her greatest wish is to study medicine.","zh":"她最大的願望是學習醫學。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is my wish that the money be used to help children.","zh":"我希望這筆錢用於幫助兒童。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2a0ecb82648d30f9","term":"wish","forms":["wish","wishes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"許願；願望的表達","explanation":"指把願望說出來或在心裡提出，常帶有童話、魔法或儀式感。make a wish 就是“許願”，而不是單純地提出一個普通要求。","examples":[{"en":"Close your eyes and make a wish before you blow out the candles.","zh":"吹滅蠟燭前閉上眼睛許個願。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She closed her eyes and made a wish.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a1624c39dec1ffae","term":"wish","forms":["wish","wishes","wishing","wished","wishest","wishedst","wisheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想要；希望","explanation":"表示希望得到某物或希望某事發生，語氣通常比 want 更像“有某種願望”。它可以指現實可行的願望，也可以指未必能實現的願望。","examples":[{"en":"I wish for a quiet place where I can think.","zh":"我希望有一個能安靜思考的地方。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wish you all the best in your new job.","zh":"祝你在新工作中一切順利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3c4acb5b4d39751","term":"wish","forms":["wish","wishes","wishing","wished","wishest","wishedst","wisheth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"盼望（即使難以實現）","explanation":"表示強烈盼望某個結果，即使說話人知道它不太可能發生，甚至實際上無法發生。wish 常把現實和願望之間的距離表現出來。","examples":[{"en":"I wish I could stay longer, but my train leaves soon.","zh":"我真希望能多待一會兒，但我的火車很快就要開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wish the old cinema were still open.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wish","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-939df4a72606636c5f6a","word":"wit","forms":["wit"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-3ae0d2fb50356e4b","term":"wit","forms":["wit","wits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"思考和推理能力","explanation":"wit指理解問題、思考並作出判斷的腦力。它可以表示一個人的能力，也可以表示某件事超出了人的理解或解決能力。","examples":[{"en":"The puzzle was beyond the wit of everyone in the room.","zh":"房間裡沒有一個人能憑自己的思考能力解開這道謎題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No one could devise a solution within the wit of the committee.","zh":"委員會沒有能力想出解決辦法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-78466674a57ff4a6","term":"wit","forms":["wit","wits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機敏的反應；急智","explanation":"wit表示人在短時間內迅速想出辦法、說出恰當話語的機敏。它強調臨場反應快，而不只是平時聰明。","examples":[{"en":"Her quick wit saved the conversation from becoming awkward.","zh":"她的急智避免了談話變得尷尬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He answered the difficult question with remarkable wit.","zh":"他憑藉非凡的機敏回答了那個難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e610e83383b12a09","term":"wit","forms":["wit","wits"],"pos":"noun","zh":"機智幽默","explanation":"wit也指用聰明、迅速而巧妙的方式製造幽默，尤其是說出讓人會心一笑的話。它通常比普通的搞笑更強調語言或想法的巧妙。","examples":[{"en":"The host kept the audience entertained with her dry wit.","zh":"主持人用冷麵式的機智幽默讓觀眾始終興致盎然。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His wit made even a dull meeting enjoyable.","zh":"他的機智讓一場枯燥的會議也變得有趣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wit","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f18149f95e6b1719fb4f","word":"witch/wizard","forms":["witch","wizard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6e43412e0fcef1fa","term":"witch","forms":["witch","witches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"女巫；施巫術的人","explanation":"指被認為能施魔法、詛咒他人或預言事情的人，現代一般尤其指女性。這是witch最基本、最容易聯想到的意義。","examples":[{"en":"The villagers believed that the old woman was a witch.","zh":"村民們相信那個老婦人是女巫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witch cast a spell over the sleeping prince.","zh":"女巫對熟睡的王子施了魔法。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-658af59fb4c0d085","term":"witch","forms":["witch","witches"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巫術傳統的女性信徒","explanation":"指信奉Wicca或類似新異教傳統的女性。這裡的witch可以是宗教或精神身份，不一定表示邪惡的施法者。","examples":[{"en":"She identifies as a witch and celebrates the seasonal festivals.","zh":"她自稱是巫術傳統的信徒，並慶祝季節節日。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She identifies as a witch within a modern pagan tradition.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witch","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-912f81f4234a8f65","term":"wizard","forms":["wizard","wizards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"巫師；魔法師","explanation":"指會施展魔法、使用神秘物品或進行魔法實踐的人，是童話、奇幻作品和角色扮演語境中的基本義。","examples":[{"en":"The wizard raised his staff and called down a storm.","zh":"巫師舉起法杖，召來了一場暴風雨。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"In the story, a young wizard must save the village.","zh":"故事中，一個年輕巫師必須拯救村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wizard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-af14f921fce6f51c","term":"wizard","forms":["wizard","wizards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"高手；奇才","explanation":"比喻某人在特定領域擁有非凡的技巧或天賦，重點不是魔法，而是“像巫師一樣厲害”。","examples":[{"en":"Maya is a wizard at solving difficult puzzles.","zh":"瑪雅特別擅長解決難題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our accountant is a wizard with numbers.","zh":"我們的會計非常精通數字。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wizard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-0695b563acde461fc2f8","word":"with","forms":["with"],"officialPos":"prep.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-747eec0fdd0a3928","term":"with","forms":["with"],"pos":"prep","zh":"和……一起；與……相伴","explanation":"這是 with 最基本的用法，表示某人和另一個人或某物一起行動、處在相近的位置。它直接體現“與……連在一起”的核心影象。","examples":[{"en":"I went to the market with my sister.","zh":"我和姐姐一起去了市場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Please stay with me until the bus arrives.","zh":"請陪著我，直到公交車到站。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/with","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-51e3e224fb5d5ac0","term":"with","forms":["with"],"pos":"prep","zh":"用；藉助","explanation":"with 把動作和使用的工具連在一起，表示藉助某件具體物品完成動作。這是“與某物一起做事”向工具意義的自然延伸。","examples":[{"en":"He opened the box with a key.","zh":"他用鑰匙開啟了盒子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Cut the paper with these scissors.","zh":"用這把剪刀剪紙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/with","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c26f22db83dc51cea1eb","word":"withdraw","forms":["withdraw"],"officialPos":"v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-897575203118a95e","term":"withdraw","forms":["withdraw","withdraws","withdrawing","withdrew","withdrawn","withdrawest","withdrewst","withdraweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收回；撤銷","explanation":"把已經給出、允許或提供的東西重新拿回來，也就是把它從對方那裡“抽回”。可用於許可、提議、支援、服務等。","examples":[{"en":"The company withdrew its offer after the negotiations failed.","zh":"談判失敗後，公司撤回了報價。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum withdrew the painting from the exhibition.","zh":"博物館把那幅畫從展覽中撤了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/withdraw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-02dc7c7ca0a7c708","term":"withdraw","forms":["withdraw","withdraws","withdrawing","withdrew","withdrawn","withdrawest","withdrewst","withdraweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"收回言論","explanation":"把已經說出或寫下的評論、指控等收回來，表示不再堅持或承認不應這樣說。","examples":[{"en":"The reporter withdrew the accusation after checking the facts.","zh":"核實事實後，記者收回了這項指控。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I withdraw my earlier comment.","zh":"我收回先前的評論。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/withdraw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-31479a937afc4a3f","term":"withdraw","forms":["withdraw","withdraws","withdrawing","withdrew","withdrawn","withdrawest","withdrewst","withdraweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"取款；提取","explanation":"從銀行賬戶、存款或其他金融賬戶中把錢取出來，即把錢從賬戶裡“抽回”到手中。","examples":[{"en":"I withdrew some cash from the ATM.","zh":"我從自動取款機取了一些現金。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She withdrew $200 from her savings account.","zh":"她從儲蓄賬戶裡取出了200美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/withdraw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-2d87b38ec93c508a","term":"withdraw","forms":["withdraw","withdraws","withdrawing","withdrew","withdrawn","withdrawest","withdrewst","withdraweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撤離；離開","explanation":"人或部隊從某個地方、某人的身邊或某種局面中退開，回到別處；這裡是“自己抽身離開”。","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers withdrew from the village before sunset.","zh":"士兵們在日落前撤出了村莊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He withdrew from the room without saying goodbye.","zh":"他沒有道別就離開了房間。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/withdraw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-530a8bca4acbb743","term":"withdraw","forms":["withdraw","withdraws","withdrawing","withdrew","withdrawn","withdrawest","withdrewst","withdraweth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"退出；不再參與","explanation":"主動從活動、組織、公眾視野或他人的陪伴中退出來，不再繼續參與或出現。","examples":[{"en":"The athlete withdrew from the competition because of an injury.","zh":"這名運動員因傷退出了比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The injured runner withdrew from the championship.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/withdraw","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c87800095298a066aa19","word":"wither","forms":["wither"],"officialPos":"v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-378e04a9e08eb65c","term":"wither","forms":["wither","withers","withering","withered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"枯萎；幹縮","explanation":"植物因缺水、炎熱或失去生機而變得低垂、乾枯，就像那幅逐漸失去水分的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"The leaves began to wither in the afternoon heat.","zh":"葉子在午後的炎熱中開始枯萎。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Without water, the young plants quickly withered.","zh":"沒有水，幼苗很快就枯萎了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wither","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-608dd9356e940b7b","term":"wither","forms":["wither","withers","withering","withered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸衰退；失去活力","explanation":"把植物失去水分的畫面移到抽象事物上：熱情、希望、影響力或力量慢慢失去活力，最後衰退下去。","examples":[{"en":"Her enthusiasm began to wither after months of criticism.","zh":"經過幾個月的批評，她的熱情開始逐漸消退。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their hopes withered as each rescue attempt failed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wither","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d2454c4d8a166f48c3b6","word":"withhold","forms":["withhold"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-5ff50b597eb1b635","term":"withhold","forms":["withhold","withholds","withholding","withheld","withholden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"隱瞞資訊","explanation":"指明知某項資訊、意見或同意可以說出來，卻故意不透露；這是“把話握住不放”的常見引申義。","examples":[{"en":"The witness withheld an important detail from the investigators.","zh":"證人向調查人員隱瞞了一個重要細節。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The witness was accused of withholding crucial information.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/withhold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a98f1d23265c939e","term":"withhold","forms":["withhold","withholds","withholding","withheld","withholden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"扣留實物","explanation":"指已經拿到某件實物，卻暫時不把它交還給原主人；重點是把東西扣在自己手裡。","examples":[{"en":"The landlord withheld part of my deposit until the repairs were finished.","zh":"房東扣留了我的一部分押金，直到維修完成。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Customs officers withheld the parcel until the duty was paid.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/withhold","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f106376011688eda079c","word":"within","forms":["within"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b2734e502d0e8f13","term":"within","forms":["within"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在裡面；在內部","explanation":"它表示某人或某物位於一個空間邊界的裡面，正是“在邊界圈內”的基本畫面。","examples":[{"en":"Only staff members may work within the laboratory.","zh":"只有工作人員可以在實驗室內工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A small garden lies within the walls.","zh":"牆內有一個小花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/within","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-49de560fb147309d","term":"within","forms":["within"],"pos":"prep","zh":"在……結束以前","explanation":"這裡的邊界圈變成時間線：動作必須在指定期限的末端到來以前完成，因此表示“在……之內”。","examples":[{"en":"Please reply within two business days.","zh":"請在兩個工作日內回覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The package should arrive within a week.","zh":"包裹應該會在一週內送到。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/within","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-1216b2a88975f9d3c0ba","word":"without","forms":["without"],"officialPos":"prep./adv.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-931ed666051ff98c","term":"without","forms":["without"],"pos":"adv","zh":"沒有；缺少","explanation":"表示沒有某樣東西卻繼續生活、行動或應付情況，核心畫面就是把某物留在外面、不讓它進入自己的生活。","examples":[{"en":"She can manage without a car in the city.","zh":"她在城裡沒有汽車也能應付。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I can't live without coffee.","zh":"我沒有咖啡就過不下去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/without","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65c0a1d8be4efd6c","term":"without","forms":["without"],"pos":"prep","zh":"不帶；沒有","explanation":"表示某人做某事時沒有攜帶、擁有或處於某種東西或狀態；把該東西留在生活場景之外，就形成“沒有、不帶”的意思。","examples":[{"en":"He left the house without his phone.","zh":"他沒帶手機就離開了家。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We finished the project without extra help.","zh":"我們沒有額外幫助也完成了專案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/without","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ba1c566a4bad288c22a0","word":"witness","forms":["witness"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-91f02d391abe3bd9","term":"witness","forms":["witness","witnesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"證詞；作證","explanation":"指對事實或事件的證明、證詞，也就是見證者把自己知道的情況說出來。","examples":[{"en":"She can bear witness to what happened that night.","zh":"她可以為那天晚上發生的事作證。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His signed account bears witness to the events that followed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f9791ed20d9e493","term":"witness","forms":["witness","witnesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"目擊者；見證人","explanation":"指親眼看見某事，或憑親身經歷而瞭解情況的人。","examples":[{"en":"As a witness to the accident, I can describe exactly what happened.","zh":"作為這起事故的目擊者，我能準確描述發生了什麼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Several witnesses saw the car leave the scene.","zh":"幾名目擊者看到那輛車離開了現場。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e1a719aa03840237","term":"witness","forms":["witness","witnesses","witnessing","witnessed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"親眼見到；目睹","explanation":"指親自看到或透過經歷瞭解到某個事件，是名詞“目擊者”這一概念的動詞形式。","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of people witnessed the accident.","zh":"數百人目睹了這起事故。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We witnessed a remarkable change in the town.","zh":"我們親眼見證了這個城鎮的顯著變化。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witness","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6685bcd8109fc19f76b3","word":"witty","forms":["witty"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0f9d78780abe2bae","term":"witty","forms":["witty","wittier","wittiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"機智而風趣的","explanation":"形容人或言語既聰明又有趣，能用巧妙的說法讓人會心一笑；這是現代英語中最重要的用法。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a witty answer that made everyone laugh.","zh":"她給出了一個機智的回答，逗得大家都笑了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His witty comments kept the conversation lively.","zh":"他機智風趣的評論讓談話一直很活躍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-154718d855bbefe9","term":"witty","forms":["witty","wittier","wittiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"頭腦敏捷而有洞察力","explanation":"表示一個人反應快、理解力強、看問題透；這種聰明常常會進一步表現為 witty 的巧妙表達，但不一定真的逗笑別人。","examples":[{"en":"Even after many years, she remains witty and sharp.","zh":"多年過去了，她依然頭腦敏捷、思維犀利。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her witty observations exposed the plan's hidden contradictions.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witty","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bf65ad523768218f4577","word":"woe","forms":["woe"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-0b8a479a19190d5b","term":"woe","forms":["woe","woes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"深重的悲傷；苦難","explanation":"指非常強烈、沉重的悲傷或痛苦，也可以指造成這種痛苦的具體不幸。它把“苦啊”的哀嘆變成了一種持續或嚴重的苦難。","examples":[{"en":"The loss of her home brought her great woe.","zh":"失去家園給她帶來了深重的悲痛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He spoke quietly about the woe he had endured.","zh":"他平靜地談起自己所經受的苦難。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c595fb70773dee59","term":"woe","forms":["woe","woes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"災禍；麻煩","explanation":"指帶來悲傷和痛苦的災難、禍患或嚴重麻煩，是從“深重的苦難”進一步突出其外在原因或事件。","examples":[{"en":"Woe to anyone who breaks the king's law.","zh":"誰違反國王的法律，誰就要遭殃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company blamed its financial woes on falling demand.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woe","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f76b61b962db075bb76a","word":"wolf","forms":["wolf"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8c87e65884ed423","term":"wolf","forms":["wolf","wolves"],"pos":"noun","zh":"狼","explanation":"指犬科中體型最大的野生動物之一，形象通常與野性、捕獵和群體生活聯絡在一起。","examples":[{"en":"A wolf crossed the road just before dawn.","zh":"黎明前，一匹狼穿過了公路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The wolves stayed close to the edge of the forest.","zh":"狼群一直待在森林邊緣附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wolf","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cf2e5bff1ef03dcd20d1","word":"woman","forms":["woman"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d8e8ab0b68e50047","term":"woman","forms":["woman","women"],"pos":"noun","zh":"成年女性","explanation":"指一位已經成年的女性人類，這是woman最基本、最常用的意思。它描述的是性別和成年身份，不一定涉及婚姻、職業或性格。","examples":[{"en":"A woman helped me find the right platform.","zh":"一位女士幫我找到了正確的站臺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That woman is our new neighbor.","zh":"那位女士是我們的新鄰居。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woman","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-36296059cca8b7c7c7a5","word":"wonder","forms":["wonder"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4bc0f37743aa9757","term":"wonder","forms":["wonder","wonders"],"pos":"noun","zh":"驚奇；讚歎","explanation":"指面對新奇、出乎意料或難以解釋的事情時產生的驚奇、讚歎和好奇，重點是這種內心感受本身。","examples":[{"en":"The children watched the fireworks in wonder.","zh":"孩子們驚奇地看著煙花。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She felt a deep sense of wonder when she saw the ocean for the first time.","zh":"她第一次看到大海時，心中產生了深深的驚奇感。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f421ef74b3a62a65","term":"wonder","forms":["wonder","wonders","wondering","wondered","wonderest","wonderedst","wondereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"驚歎；感到驚奇","explanation":"指被某件事的壯觀、奇異或出乎意料所觸動，產生驚奇或讚歎。","examples":[{"en":"Visitors wonder at the beauty of the cave.","zh":"遊客們驚歎於這個洞穴的美麗。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"No wonder he was tired after working all night.","zh":"他工作了一整夜，難怪會累。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-020654a092c9b45c","term":"wonder","forms":["wonder","wonders","wondering","wondered","wonderest","wonderedst","wondereth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"想知道；納悶","explanation":"指在心裡琢磨某件事、對答案感到好奇或不確定，常常相當於“想知道、納悶”。","examples":[{"en":"I wonder whether they will arrive on time.","zh":"我想知道他們能不能準時到達。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wondered why the shop was closed.","zh":"她納悶這家店為什麼關門了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonder","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee04228c5c6d8b083f6c","word":"wonderful","forms":["wonderful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82e2da3f9862f582","term":"wonderful","forms":["wonderful","wonderfuller","wonderfuler","more wonderful","wonderfullest","wonderfulest","most wonderful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人驚奇的；非同尋常的","explanation":"指某事出乎意料、不同尋常，足以引起驚奇；這種驚奇可以是中性的，也可以帶有讚歎意味。","examples":[{"en":"It was wonderful how quickly the storm passed.","zh":"暴風雨這麼快就過去了，真讓人驚訝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The cave contains wonderful formations shaped over millennia.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonderful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-96ae6a382a9cdccf","term":"wonderful","forms":["wonderful","wonderfuller","wonderfuler","more wonderful","wonderfullest","wonderfulest","most wonderful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"非常棒的；令人讚歎的","explanation":"表示某人、某物或某種經歷好得超出預期，令人滿意、佩服或感到享受，是現代英語中最常見的用法之一。","examples":[{"en":"We had a wonderful time at the beach.","zh":"我們在海灘玩得非常開心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She gave us some wonderful advice.","zh":"她給了我們一些非常好的建議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonderful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-68939457dbd339f88f04","word":"wood(s)","forms":["wood","woods"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-cd0268067f1c9da5","term":"wood","forms":["wood","woods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"木材；木頭","explanation":"指樹幹和樹枝內部的木質材料，既可以作為建築和製作物品的材料，也可以作為燃料。這是最基礎、最常用的含義。","examples":[{"en":"This table is made of wood.","zh":"這張桌子是木頭做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The shelves are made from light wood.","zh":"這些架子是用輕質木材做的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-75f69cd47c96341e","term":"wood","forms":["wood","woods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樹林","explanation":"指覆蓋著許多樹的一片林地，規模通常比單獨說一棵樹大，但不一定是大片森林。","examples":[{"en":"We walked through the woods after lunch.","zh":"午飯後我們穿過了樹林。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A narrow path wound through the wood.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d6ce17060ada39d2","term":"woods","forms":["woods"],"pos":"noun","zh":"樹林","explanation":"woods指許多樹密集生長的一片地方，通常比forest小，但仍是可以走進去或穿過的自然區域。核心畫面就是樹木聚在一起形成一片林地。","examples":[{"en":"We found a quiet path through the woods.","zh":"我們在樹林裡找到了一條安靜的小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"These woods are part of the Campbell property.","zh":"這片樹林屬於坎貝爾家的土地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woods","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4e7d92dde35af0f2d66e","word":"wooden","forms":["wooden"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4f5fcf31383a0af3","term":"wooden","forms":["wooden","more wooden","most wooden"],"pos":"adj","zh":"木製的","explanation":"指物品由木頭製成；這是最直接的本義，就像把木頭固定成船、桌子或其他物品。","examples":[{"en":"The children built a small wooden boat.","zh":"孩子們造了一艘小木船。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We sat at a wooden table by the window.","zh":"我們坐在窗邊的一張木桌旁。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wooden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bf7f44b19f3f1c7b","term":"wooden","forms":["wooden","more wooden","most wooden"],"pos":"adj","zh":"僵硬呆板的","explanation":"比喻某人的動作、說話或表演像木頭一樣不靈活，缺少自然的感情和活力。","examples":[{"en":"The actor's delivery was wooden and unconvincing.","zh":"那名演員的臺詞表達很呆板，缺乏說服力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His wooden gestures made the performance feel rehearsed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wooden","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5a2bb24dc707f2a69361","word":"woodpecker","forms":["woodpecker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e67e7555aaede980","term":"woodpecker","forms":["woodpecker","woodpeckers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"啄木鳥","explanation":"一種喙堅硬尖長、善於啄擊樹幹並在木頭上鑿洞的鳥。記住它在樹上連續啄擊的畫面，就能把這個詞和普通的鳥名區分開。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a woodpecker tapping on the old oak tree.","zh":"我們看見一隻啄木鳥在那棵老橡樹上啄個不停。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The woodpecker made a small hole in the tree.","zh":"啄木鳥在樹上鑿出了一個小洞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woodpecker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-feb672a2e6ea299d8f1f","word":"wool","forms":["wool"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-658eef679d7eb48a","term":"wool","forms":["wool","wools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羊毛","explanation":"指羊身上剪下來的毛，也可泛指羊駝等部分反芻動物的類似毛纖維。這是wool最基本、最值得先掌握的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The farmer sells the wool from his sheep every spring.","zh":"這位農民每年春天出售自己羊群的羊毛。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This sweater is made from soft merino wool.","zh":"這件毛衣是用柔軟的美利奴羊毛製成的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-94c77bef3949cd0e","term":"wool","forms":["wool","wools"],"pos":"noun","zh":"羊毛料；羊毛線","explanation":"指用羊毛紡成的線，或用這種線織成的布料和衣物。這裡關注的不是動物身上的毛，而是已經加工成可穿、可織的材料。","examples":[{"en":"I packed a wool scarf because the evenings are cold.","zh":"我帶了一條羊毛圍巾，因為晚上很冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought blue wool to knit a blanket.","zh":"她買了藍色毛線來織毯子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wool","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-98c1eb4ee93476743763","word":"word","forms":["word"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-2b720ccf1af5fa48","term":"word","forms":["word","words"],"pos":"noun","zh":"詞；單詞","explanation":"word是語言中能夠獨立表達某種意義的基本單位，例如表示人、動作或事物的一個詞。它可以指口頭說出的詞，也可以指寫下來的詞。","examples":[{"en":"What is the English word for this object?","zh":"這個物品的英語單詞是什麼？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I don't know the right word to describe it.","zh":"我不知道用哪個恰當的詞來描述它。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/word","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-00e13ed7af55b27622f1","word":"work","forms":["work"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-963352fb2620fa6f","term":"work","forms":["work","works"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工作；職業","explanation":"指一個人通常從事的工作或職業，也可以指職業本身帶來的任務和安排；核心是投入時間和精力去做事。","examples":[{"en":"My work involves a lot of travel.","zh":"我的工作需要經常出差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She is looking for work after moving to the city.","zh":"她搬到這座城市後正在找工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/work","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-618b142b0735c7a7","term":"work","forms":["work","works"],"pos":"noun","zh":"努力；勞動","explanation":"指為完成任務或達到目標所投入的體力、時間和精力；也就是“投入力量併產生作用”的過程。","examples":[{"en":"Writing this report took a lot of work.","zh":"寫這份報告花了很多功夫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It is hard work to carry these boxes upstairs.","zh":"把這些箱子搬上樓很費力。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/work","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7465cc88eb7f4036","term":"work","forms":["work","works","working","worked","wrought","workest","workedst","worketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"做事；工作","explanation":"指投入時間、體力或腦力去完成一項具體任務，也可以泛指從事某種工作；正如記憶鉤子所說，這是“投入力量併產生作用”。","examples":[{"en":"I work on the garden every Saturday morning.","zh":"我每週六上午都在打理花園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She worked hard to finish the report before lunch.","zh":"她努力工作，爭取午飯前完成報告。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/work","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ee5e72d6d0cc8c53","term":"work","forms":["work","works","working","worked","wrought","workest","workedst","worketh","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"運轉正常；奏效","explanation":"指機器、裝置、方法或計劃能夠按預期執行並達到目的，也就是投入的力量確實產生了作用。","examples":[{"en":"The printer still works after all these years.","zh":"這臺印表機用了這麼多年仍然運轉正常。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That simple plan worked better than we expected.","zh":"那個簡單的計劃比我們預想的更有效。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/work","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-244f4e42fb0ee32cd423","word":"workbook","forms":["workbook"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e16041687d720298","term":"workbook","forms":["workbook","workbooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"學生練習冊","explanation":"指學生用來做題、填寫答案和寫出解題過程的書。它通常配有問題或練習，不只是用來閱讀。","examples":[{"en":"The students completed the workbook before the test.","zh":"學生們在考試前完成了這本練習冊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"This workbook gives children extra practice in reading.","zh":"這本練習冊讓孩子們在閱讀方面得到額外練習。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workbook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8bd2ead459b0d4cd","term":"workbook","forms":["workbook","workbooks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工作記錄簿","explanation":"指公司或工作團隊用來記錄要做的工作、工作進度或已經完成的工作的書面材料。核心仍是把實際工作集中記錄在一起。","examples":[{"en":"The technician recorded each repair in the workshop workbook.","zh":"技術員把每次維修都記錄在車間工作簿裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Record each day's measurements in your laboratory workbook.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workbook","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-87eba76e7f3164534045","word":"worker","forms":["worker"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-154f607a0a35c898","term":"worker","forms":["worker","workers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"勞動者；工作人員","explanation":"指透過工作來謀生或完成勞動任務的人，既可以是體力勞動者，也可以泛指某個單位、行業或專案中的工作人員。","examples":[{"en":"The factory employs more than five hundred workers.","zh":"這家工廠僱用了五百多名工人。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Every worker deserves a safe workplace.","zh":"每位勞動者都應當擁有安全的工作環境。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-37be12cc8a09a351","term":"worker","forms":["worker","workers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工蟻；工蜂等","explanation":"指螞蟻、蜜蜂、白蟻或黃蜂等社會性昆蟲中負責覓食、築巢和照料群體、通常不負責繁殖的個體；這裡延續的是“群體中的勞動者”這一核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The worker bees brought nectar back to the hive.","zh":"工蜂把花蜜帶回了蜂巢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ant workers carried food back to the colony.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worker","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b6f80f8db1ed2c2d73e1","word":"workforce","forms":["workforce"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8d3cfc8708e93350","term":"workforce","forms":["workforce","workforces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"某組織或行業的勞動力","explanation":"指受某個組織僱用、屬於某個行業，或參與某個專案的全部工作人員，重點是把他們看作一個整體。比如談年齡、規模或技能時，可以把這支“工作隊伍”作為一個群體來描述。","examples":[{"en":"The company is investing in training its future workforce.","zh":"這家公司正在投資培訓未來的員工隊伍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The construction industry's workforce is becoming more diverse.","zh":"建築業的勞動力隊伍正變得更加多元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workforce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d06fc04ba97e9d0","term":"workforce","forms":["workforce","workforces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一個地區的就業或可就業人口","explanation":"指一個國家或地區中已經就業、或具備就業條件並屬於勞動力市場的人口總數。這裡的“隊伍”不再屬於某一家機構，而是擴大到整個社會。","examples":[{"en":"About half of the country's workforce works in the service sector.","zh":"這個國家約有一半的勞動力從事服務業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The region's workforce is aging as younger workers move away.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workforce","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b10c94bd8ae38a2a3736","word":"workout","forms":["workout"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-34ccd75ff60bf966","term":"workout","forms":["workout","workouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一次鍛鍊","explanation":"指一段完整的身體鍛鍊時間，例如去健身房、游泳或進行其他運動的一次訓練。重點是這次實際進行的鍛鍊，而不只是抽象的健身目標。","examples":[{"en":"I usually do a short workout before breakfast.","zh":"我通常在早餐前做一會兒鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She planned three workouts for this week.","zh":"她安排了這周的三次鍛鍊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5a308ff1e6f641ce","term":"workout","forms":["workout","workouts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"訓練計劃或練習組合","explanation":"指按照特定目標設計的一套具體練習，例如為了增強力量、提高耐力或準備比賽而安排的動作組合。這裡強調的是訓練內容和安排，不只是正在鍛鍊的那段時間。","examples":[{"en":"The coach gave us a workout designed to improve our speed.","zh":"教練給我們安排了一套旨在提高速度的訓練。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The coach designed a workout for improving endurance.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workout","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-83366499299704fbf384","word":"workplace","forms":["workplace"],"officialPos":"n.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8f2b3219817112db","term":"workplace","forms":["workplace","workplaces"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工作場所","explanation":"指某人工作的地方，可以是辦公室、工廠、商店等整個場所。重點是“工作的地點”，而不只是其中的一張桌子或一個工作位置。","examples":[{"en":"The company wants to make the workplace safer.","zh":"這家公司想讓工作場所更安全。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She met her best friend at the workplace.","zh":"她在工作場所認識了自己最好的朋友。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workplace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ee510d1a07ac7e6491ea","word":"workshop","forms":["workshop"],"officialPos":"n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-6448ac8b8eb4fb52","term":"workshop","forms":["workshop","workshops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"工作間；作坊","explanation":"指用於製作、修理或進行輕型工業工作的房間或場所，通常不太大；可以把它看成原始的“邊工作邊做東西的房間”。","examples":[{"en":"My uncle spends most of the day in his workshop making wooden toys.","zh":"我叔叔每天大部分時間都在工作間裡製作木製玩具。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mechanic kept the old motorcycle in the workshop overnight.","zh":"修理工把那輛舊摩托車在工作間裡放了一夜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workshop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b588f29b80b7fc0c","term":"workshop","forms":["workshop","workshops"],"pos":"noun","zh":"實踐型研討課；工作坊","explanation":"指人數較少、時間較集中、強調互動和實際解決問題的學習或訓練活動。它就像把學習者帶進一個“共同動手修改的工作間”，而不只是聽講。","examples":[{"en":"I joined a weekend workshop on digital photography.","zh":"我參加了一個週末數碼攝影工作坊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The workshop gave students time to test their ideas and get feedback.","zh":"這次工作坊讓學生有時間檢驗自己的想法並獲得反饋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/workshop","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-486ea46224d1bb4fb680","word":"world","forms":["world"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4813c19c5dfab971","term":"world","forms":["world","worlds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"人類共同的世界","explanation":"指人類共同的生活經驗、社會存在和我們所處的現實整體；通常說 the world，強調“這個世界”。","examples":[{"en":"The world is changing faster than we expected.","zh":"這個世界變化得比我們預想的更快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wanted to see the world as it really was.","zh":"她想看看這個世界真實的樣子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/world","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3ec385907a87b58b","term":"world","forms":["world","worlds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"個人的生活天地","explanation":"指某個人自己的生活、感受和精神天地；因此 one’s world 可以理解為“某人的整個生活”。","examples":[{"en":"After the accident, her whole world changed.","zh":"事故之後，她的整個生活都變了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her children mean the world to her.","zh":"她的孩子對她來說無比重要。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/world","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f2898c8cd4374513","term":"world","forms":["world","worlds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"地球；全世界","explanation":"指作為一顆行星的地球，或地球上的各個國家和人類社會；all over the world 就是“遍佈全世界”。","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people around the world watched the match.","zh":"全世界有數百萬人觀看了這場比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"People all over the world are facing the same problem.","zh":"世界各地的人們都在面對同一個問題。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/world","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-01cfe6b21cec688d","term":"world","forms":["world","worlds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一種可能的世界","explanation":"指關於地球社會或現實狀態的一種設想，例如“像這樣的世界”或“一個沒有戰爭的世界”。","examples":[{"en":"Who would want to live in a world like this?","zh":"誰願意生活在這樣的世界裡？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She imagined a world where everyone had clean water.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/world","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b9af17af4fc5708e9ba6","word":"worm","forms":["worm"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-05dba45225dd617c","term":"worm","forms":["worm","worms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蟲；蚯蚓","explanation":"最基本的形象是柔軟、細長、靠蠕動前進的蟲，尤其可以指蚯蚓。","examples":[{"en":"The bird pulled a worm from the wet soil.","zh":"那隻鳥從溼土裡叼出了一條蟲。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We found an earthworm under the stone.","zh":"我們在石頭下面發現了一條蚯蚓。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-68a75b6d015269dc","term":"worm","forms":["worm","worms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蠕蟲程式","explanation":"計算機蠕蟲是一種能自行復制並透過網路傳播的程式；它延續了“小蟲悄悄鑽入並擴散”的核心形象。","examples":[{"en":"The security team stopped a worm from spreading across the network.","zh":"安全團隊阻止了一種蠕蟲程式在網路中擴散。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The worm spread automatically through the unpatched network.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da4963fc044691e3","term":"worm","forms":["worm","worms","worming","wormed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"蠕動著穿過","explanation":"worm作動詞時，首先是像蟲一樣貼近地面、曲折緩慢地前進。","examples":[{"en":"We wormed our way through the thick bushes.","zh":"我們蜿蜒鑽過了茂密的灌木叢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The child wormed his way under the fence.","zh":"孩子蠕動著從籬笆下面鑽了過去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6f9f2163f7e55daf","term":"worm","forms":["worm","worms","worming","wormed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"逐漸混入或滲入","explanation":"它還可表示慢慢把自己或某物弄進某處，延續了小蟲一點點鑽進去的畫面。","examples":[{"en":"A doubt wormed its way into her mind.","zh":"一個疑慮悄悄鑽進了她的心裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The reporter wormed his way into the private meeting.","zh":"那名記者設法悄悄混進了私人會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8bdec92cde5a4cf5","term":"worm","forms":["worm","worms","worming","wormed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"套出資訊","explanation":"像蟲子慢慢鑽出東西一樣，worm information out of someone表示透過反覆追問、勸說或巧妙周旋，套出對方本來不想說的資訊。","examples":[{"en":"She wormed the truth out of him after a long conversation.","zh":"她聊了很久，終於從他那裡套出了真相。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The lawyer wormed a confession out of the witness.","zh":"律師設法從證人那裡套出了供詞。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worm","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6de2f53e03e93dffb34a","word":"worry","forms":["worry"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-4aac9ca40916feae","term":"worry","forms":["worry","worries"],"pos":"noun","zh":"擔憂；焦慮","explanation":"指心裡被某種可能發生的壞事揪住，持續感到不安或焦慮。","examples":[{"en":"Constant worry kept her awake most of the night.","zh":"持續的擔憂讓她大半夜都睡不著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He tried to put his worries aside and focus on the meeting.","zh":"他努力把憂慮放到一邊，專心參加會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-377f8a018e81f9b6","term":"worry","forms":["worry","worries","worrying","worried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"擔心；感到憂慮","explanation":"指自己因為不確定或可能不好的結果而反覆不安，心思像被揪住一樣。","examples":[{"en":"I worry about my parents when they travel alone.","zh":"父母獨自出門時，我會擔心他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Try not to worry that every small mistake will ruin everything.","zh":"儘量別擔心每個小錯誤都會毀掉一切。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0808f167e8663fa3","term":"worry","forms":["worry","worries","worrying","worried"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使……擔心","explanation":"指某件事或某人的行為把另一個人的心緒揪緊，使其感到不安或苦惱。","examples":[{"en":"The sudden silence worried everyone in the office.","zh":"突然的沉默讓辦公室裡的每個人都擔心起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His failure to answer the phone worried his parents.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worry","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e760bdbe0be65db96a57","word":"worse","forms":["worse"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d78b80fb049de03e","term":"worse","forms":["worse"],"pos":"adj","zh":"更差；更糟","explanation":"表示某種情況、結果或品質比之前或另一個物件差，是 bad 的比較級。核心畫面就是在“壞”的下坡路上又往下走了一步。","examples":[{"en":"Your exam results are worse than before.","zh":"你的考試成績比以前更差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The weather is getting worse.","zh":"天氣越來越糟了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b5ac713a9400b22c","term":"worse","forms":["worse"],"pos":"adv","zh":"做得更差","explanation":"表示某個動作或表現比另一個時候或物件更差，是 badly 的比較級；仍然是同一條“壞事繼續下坡”的記憶線。","examples":[{"en":"The harder you try, the worse you do.","zh":"你越努力，做得反而越差。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He played worse after injuring his wrist.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worse","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bba00b1891afe83daa29","word":"worship","forms":["worship"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8b882bf6bdfe5177","term":"worship","forms":["worship","worships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"敬拜；崇敬","explanation":"指把神明或神聖物件當作至高物件來敬拜，強調虔敬和宗教性的尊崇。它通常不是普通的禮貌尊重，而是帶有信仰或神聖意味的敬意。","examples":[{"en":"The temple was built for the worship of the sun god.","zh":"這座神廟是為敬拜太陽神而建的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Their worship centers on gratitude and prayer.","zh":"他們的敬拜以感恩和祈禱為核心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-be4ae714b57e631c","term":"worship","forms":["worship","worships"],"pos":"noun","zh":"禮拜；宗教儀式","explanation":"指透過祈禱、歌唱等方式表達宗教敬意的活動或儀式，重點從“敬意”轉到了“表達敬意的禮拜”。","examples":[{"en":"We join in worship at the church every Sunday.","zh":"我們每週日都在教堂參加禮拜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The music helped create a quiet atmosphere for worship.","zh":"音樂營造了適合禮拜的寧靜氛圍。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8afcf8df51ffa465","term":"worship","forms":["worship","worships","worshiping","worshipping","worshiped","worshipped"],"pos":"verb","zh":"敬拜；崇敬","explanation":"指以最高程度的尊敬和敬畏對待神明或其他神聖物件，並以宗教方式表達這種敬意。","examples":[{"en":"Many people worship God through prayer and song.","zh":"許多人透過祈禱和歌唱敬拜上帝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The ancient people worshipped the river as a living spirit.","zh":"古人把這條河當作有生命的神靈來敬拜。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worship","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-41a1c14a0a3f4da2663e","word":"worst","forms":["worst"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-508169bf1bd5ef88","term":"worst","forms":["worst"],"pos":"adj","zh":"最壞的；最差的","explanation":"指在一組人或事物中壞、糟糕或不理想程度最高的那個；也可以泛指後果最嚴重的一種選擇。它把“壞”推到了最底端。","examples":[{"en":"That was the worst meal I've had all year.","zh":"那是我今年吃過的最糟糕的一頓飯。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The worst thing we can do is panic.","zh":"我們最不該做的事就是驚慌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6832c369836c6a66","term":"worst","forms":["worst"],"pos":"adv","zh":"最差地；最不順利地","explanation":"表示某個動作做得最差，或某種疼痛、問題等在某種情況下達到最嚴重的程度；核心仍是“落到最差的一格”。","examples":[{"en":"My knee hurts worst after I climb stairs.","zh":"我爬樓梯後膝蓋最疼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Of all my interviews, that one went worst.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worst","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c0a6eb55b12b7dfe01d9","word":"worth","forms":["worth"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-600bb91afbee0ce0","term":"worth","forms":["worth"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值……錢；價值相當於……","explanation":"用於說明某物在交易或估價中相當於某個金額，也可以表示它現在的價值和過去不同。核心畫面是把物品放在“價值秤”上，看它對應多少價值。","examples":[{"en":"The painting is worth more than I expected.","zh":"這幅畫比我預想的更值錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"How much is this old camera worth?","zh":"這臺舊相機值多少錢？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-29b694655fd5f52d","term":"worth","forms":["worth"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得……","explanation":"把一次行動放到“價值秤”上比較：如果得到的好處足以抵消時間、金錢或麻煩，就表示這件事值得做。它不一定表示價格，而是表示行動有意義或划算。","examples":[{"en":"The museum is small, but it is worth visiting.","zh":"這家博物館雖然不大，但值得參觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It took all day, but the result was worth it.","zh":"這花了一整天，但結果是值得的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1d1f916d9f3be0e2","term":"worth","forms":["worth","worths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"價值；值某金額的東西","explanation":"名詞worth就是“價值秤”上的結果：可以指某物本身值多少錢，也可以指按某金額購買的一批東西。","examples":[{"en":"I bought ten dollars' worth of fruit for the party.","zh":"我買了價值十美元的水果來參加聚會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The true worth of the invention became clear over time.","zh":"這項發明的真正價值隨著時間推移才顯現出來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ade5f219811f90312eea","word":"worthwhile","forms":["worthwhile"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-401425f3f7f9a571","term":"worthwhile","forms":["worthwhile","more worthwhile","most worthwhile"],"pos":"adj","zh":"值得投入；值得做","explanation":"如果一件事需要花時間、精力或金錢，但得到的價值足以抵消這些付出，就可以說它是 worthwhile。它關注的是“做這件事值不值”，可以用於學習、工作、旅行、志願服務等活動。","examples":[{"en":"Learning a new skill is worthwhile if you enjoy the process.","zh":"如果你享受學習的過程，學一項新技能就是值得的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was worthwhile to travel that far for the festival.","zh":"為了參加那個節日活動跑那麼遠是值得的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthwhile","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-200afd0641fa765e51d1","word":"worthy","forms":["worthy"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c1fa304feebd52e6","term":"worthy","forms":["worthy","worthier","worthiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"有價值；有才德","explanation":"指某人或某事本身有分量、有優點或有價值，因而值得被重視。它可以談實際價值，也可以談品質、能力或貢獻。","examples":[{"en":"She has done work worthy of recognition.","zh":"她完成了值得認可的工作。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The museum is worthy of a careful visit.","zh":"這座博物館值得認真參觀。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-0947684b6d4b74ed","term":"worthy","forms":["worthy","worthier","worthiest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"令人欽佩的；可敬的","explanation":"強調某人的品格、行為或成就令人讚賞、尊敬，重點不只是“有用”或“有價值”，而是值得給予較高評價。","examples":[{"en":"He is a worthy successor to the former director.","zh":"他是一位稱職而令人敬重的前任主任繼任者。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She proved a worthy leader during the emergency.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/worthy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-89364a0a769977b32c6e","word":"wound","forms":["wound"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d51a8a582a614f13","term":"wound","forms":["wound","wounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"身體傷口","explanation":"指皮膚或身體外部被割、刺、撕裂等造成的傷口，是 wound 最直接、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The nurse cleaned the wound on his arm.","zh":"護士清洗了他手臂上的傷口。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She was taken to hospital with a deep wound in her leg.","zh":"她腿上有一道很深的傷口，被送往醫院。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-32ca3f1a34305fd6","term":"wound","forms":["wound","wounds"],"pos":"noun","zh":"精神上的創傷","explanation":"比喻某件侮辱、拒絕或失敗在人的感情、自尊、名譽或前途上留下的傷害，就像在內心留下了一道傷口。","examples":[{"en":"The rejection left a deep wound to his confidence.","zh":"這次拒絕深深打擊了他的自信。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Years later, she was still trying to heal the wound of that betrayal.","zh":"多年以後，她仍在努力治癒那次背叛留下的創傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3057e9850e9f0ed2","term":"wound","forms":["wound","wounds","wounding","wounded","woundest","woundedst","woundeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使身體受傷","explanation":"指透過割、刺或撕裂皮膚使某人受傷，也就是把身體上的“裂口”造成出來。","examples":[{"en":"The broken glass wounded him in the hand.","zh":"碎玻璃割傷了他的手。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Two passengers were wounded in the accident.","zh":"兩名乘客在事故中受了傷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f51b91d3ec118cc4","term":"wound","forms":["wound","wounds","wounding","wounded","woundest","woundedst","woundeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"傷害感情或自尊","explanation":"比喻讓某人的感情、自尊或信心出現一道難以忽略的“裂口”，即使沒有身體傷口，也能造成深刻傷害。","examples":[{"en":"His careless remark wounded her pride.","zh":"他漫不經心的話傷害了她的自尊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The criticism wounded him more than he admitted.","zh":"這番批評對他的傷害比他承認的更深。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wound","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f0a289923ed634acec74","word":"wrap","forms":["wrap"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b054594d34919881","term":"wrap","forms":["wrap","wraps"],"pos":"noun","zh":"包裹材料","explanation":"指包在物品外面的紙、塑膠膜或其他薄材料，用來保護、裝東西或遮住裡面的內容。它既可以指一件包裹材料，也可以泛指這類材料。","examples":[{"en":"Please put the sandwiches in plastic wrap.","zh":"請把三明治用塑膠膜包起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The florist used colored paper wrap around the bouquet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a5ddf336431ecc87","term":"wrap","forms":["wrap","wraps","wrapping","wrapped","wrapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包住","explanation":"用紙、布或其他柔軟而薄的材料把物品整個包起來，使它被保護、裝好或遮住。","examples":[{"en":"I wrapped the book in brown paper.","zh":"我用棕色的紙把這本書包了起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The gift was wrapped in bright red paper.","zh":"禮物用鮮紅色的紙包著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-7128f71a9842e1ad","term":"wrap","forms":["wrap","wraps","wrapping","wrapped","wrapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"繞住","explanation":"把某物沿著另一個物體或生物的外部繞一圈或幾圈，使它抓住、纏住或包圍對方；核心仍是“繞到外面”。","examples":[{"en":"The child wrapped her arms around her father.","zh":"孩子伸出雙臂抱住了父親。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vine wrapped around the fence.","zh":"藤蔓纏繞在籬笆上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8d8dc3c2c79799f0","term":"wrap","forms":["wrap","wraps","wrapping","wrapped","wrapt"],"pos":"verb","zh":"包藏或隱藏","explanation":"把某個想法、事實或情感包在故事、言辭等外層裡面，使它不直接顯露；這是“包住”意義的比喻用法。","examples":[{"en":"The novel wraps a serious warning in a funny story.","zh":"這部小說把嚴肅的警告包在一個有趣的故事裡。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The negotiations remained wrapped in secrecy.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrap","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7e4353d9a9b2d35e73c4","word":"wreck","forms":["wreck"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a02a5c587c558ce1","term":"wreck","forms":["wreck","wrecks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"慘不忍睹的人或事物","explanation":"指某人或某物已經被嚴重打擊、損壞或折磨，呈現出幾乎無法收拾的狀態。說人時尤其常指精神上或身體上已經崩潰、憔悴不堪。","examples":[{"en":"After the long interview, I was a nervous wreck.","zh":"那場漫長的面試後，我緊張得幾乎崩潰。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The old garden was a wreck after years without care.","zh":"這座老花園多年無人照料，已經破敗不堪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8a95caa54133920d","term":"wreck","forms":["wreck","wrecks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嚴重損壞後的殘骸","explanation":"指某物遭到嚴重破壞後留下的殘餘部分，尤其是車輛、船隻或建築的殘骸。它強調的是毀壞之後留下來的東西，而不是毀壞的動作。","examples":[{"en":"Divers found the wreck of a small fishing boat.","zh":"潛水員發現了一艘小漁船的殘骸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Only the wreck of the cabin remained after the fire.","zh":"火災後只剩下那間小屋的殘骸。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dff8d689f0227033","term":"wreck","forms":["wreck","wrecks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碰撞造成的事故","explanation":"指車輛、船隻等發生碰撞並受到嚴重損壞的事故。這個詞也可以讓人聯想到事故後的殘骸，因此和“殘骸”這一核心概念相連。","examples":[{"en":"The highway was closed after a three-car wreck.","zh":"發生三車相撞事故後，這條高速公路被封閉了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A wreck near the tunnel stopped traffic for hours.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-12ce230426af8138","term":"wreck","forms":["wreck","wrecks","wrecking","wrecked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"撞壞；徹底毀掉","explanation":"指透過碰撞或其他猛烈方式，把某物損壞到無法正常使用的程度。它像把完整的交通工具撞成殘骸，因此也可引申為徹底破壞某件事。","examples":[{"en":"She wrecked her bicycle on the steep hill.","zh":"她在陡坡上把腳踏車撞壞了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The sudden storm wrecked our travel plans.","zh":"突如其來的暴風雨徹底打亂了我們的旅行計劃。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a3ea3416cc5400ed","term":"wreck","forms":["wreck","wrecks","wrecking","wrecked"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使破敗；毀掉","explanation":"指長期忽視、粗暴使用或其他原因使某物逐漸變得破敗不堪，也可指使事業、名聲或生活徹底毀掉。重點是結果像一堆殘骸一樣難以恢復。","examples":[{"en":"Years of neglect wrecked the once-beautiful house.","zh":"多年的疏於維護使這座曾經漂亮的房子破敗不堪。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Reckless spending wrecked their plans for retirement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreck","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4ff366d40ef0729acab0","word":"wrestle","forms":["wrestle"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c958da9e1a407af3","term":"wrestle","forms":["wrestle","wrestles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"摔跤；扭打","explanation":"指兩個人用身體互相抱住、推壓，試圖把對方摔倒，通常是體育比賽或徒手搏鬥。","examples":[{"en":"The two boys had a brief wrestle on the grass.","zh":"兩個男孩在草地上短暫地扭打了一會兒。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The puppies had a playful wrestle on the rug.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrestle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fe591751dc20ceea","term":"wrestle","forms":["wrestle","wrestles","wrestling","wrestled","wrestlest","wrestledst","wrestleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"參加摔跤；進行扭打","explanation":"指參加摔跤比賽或進行具體的徒手扭打，是身體上的“緊緊扭在一起、互相用力”。","examples":[{"en":"She wrestled in the final match and won by one point.","zh":"她參加了決賽，並以一分之差獲勝。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brothers wrestled on the grass until supper.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrestle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-cda2f382ba5f1ffa","term":"wrestle","forms":["wrestle","wrestles","wrestling","wrestled","wrestlest","wrestledst","wrestleth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"摔跤；扭打","explanation":"指與對手進行身體上的扭打，試圖把對方摔倒或壓制住，通常用於體育或徒手搏鬥。","examples":[{"en":"The two athletes wrestled for nearly five minutes.","zh":"兩名運動員摔跤摔了將近五分鐘。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The brothers wrestled on the grass until dinner.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrestle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d1aae4fb5babfe1c8bb9","word":"wrinkle","forms":["wrinkle"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ea21f0082155cfaa","term":"wrinkle","forms":["wrinkle","wrinkles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皺褶；褶痕","explanation":"指原本平整的表面上出現的小溝、凸起或摺痕，例如紙、衣服或布料上的皺褶。","examples":[{"en":"There is a wrinkle in the corner of the sheet.","zh":"床單的一角有一道皺褶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Iron the wrinkle out of the shirt sleeve.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-39e747e959e9c11c","term":"wrinkle","forms":["wrinkle","wrinkles"],"pos":"noun","zh":"皺紋","explanation":"指皮膚上形成的細小褶皺，常與年齡、疲勞或日曬有關。","examples":[{"en":"She has a few wrinkles around her eyes.","zh":"她眼睛周圍有幾道皺紋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Too much sun can cause wrinkles.","zh":"過度日曬會導致皺紋。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f19876b2f3f45af5","term":"wrinkle","forms":["wrinkle","wrinkles","wrinkling","wrinkled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"使起皺；弄皺","explanation":"指把原本平整的衣服、紙張等弄出皺褶，就是主動製造“皺紋”。","examples":[{"en":"Be careful not to wrinkle your shirt.","zh":"小心別把你的襯衫弄皺。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Packing the jacket too tightly will wrinkle it.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrinkle","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-e3c04dfa6e1192a9b21b","word":"wrist","forms":["wrist"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-e436a71af91e968b","term":"wrist","forms":["wrist","wrists"],"pos":"noun","zh":"腕關節","explanation":"wrist 是前臂和手連線處的腕關節。它既負責連線兩部分，也能靈活轉動，因此甩、揮或旋轉手時常會用到它。","examples":[{"en":"She twisted her wrist while opening the jar.","zh":"她開罐子時扭傷了手腕。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"With a flick of his wrist, he sent the ball across the room.","zh":"他手腕一甩，就把球扔到了房間另一頭。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrist","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-10fd874b68dad080ed70","word":"write","forms":["write"],"officialPos":"v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d66f69b69ed3c39b","term":"write","forms":["write","writes","writing","wrote","writ","written","ywriten","writest","wrotest","writeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寫字、寫下","explanation":"用筆、鍵盤等把字母、單詞或符號留在紙面或其他表面上，以便表達或儲存資訊。","examples":[{"en":"Please write your address on this form.","zh":"請把你的地址寫在這張表上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She wrote down the phone number before leaving.","zh":"她離開前把電話號碼記了下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/write","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-5155825777a0fe34","term":"write","forms":["write","writes","writing","wrote","writ","written","ywriten","writest","wrotest","writeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寫作","explanation":"創作書、文章、詩歌等較完整的文字作品；這裡不只是寫幾個字，而是承擔作者的角色。","examples":[{"en":"He writes short stories in his spare time.","zh":"他利用業餘時間寫短篇小說。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She writes poetry inspired by life beside the sea.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/write","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-a2d0b7c55b78d417","term":"write","forms":["write","writes","writing","wrote","writ","written","ywriten","writest","wrotest","writeth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"寫信給","explanation":"透過信件、電子郵件或其他文字資訊與某人聯絡，把訊息傳送給對方。","examples":[{"en":"Write to me when you arrive safely.","zh":"你平安到達後給我寫信或發訊息。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I wrote to the hotel to confirm our booking.","zh":"我給酒店寫信確認了我們的預訂。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/write","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b93006774cbdd4b29938","word":"writer","forms":["writer"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-fcea26c63c85b6a5","term":"writer","forms":["writer","writers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寫作者；作家","explanation":"writer 指寫東西的人，可以是寫信、文章、劇本或書的人，也可以泛指職業作家；重點是“進行寫作”這一動作，不限於文學創作。","examples":[{"en":"She is a talented writer who turns ordinary events into vivid stories.","zh":"她是一位很有才華的作家，能把平常的事情寫成生動的故事。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The writer of this letter wants to remain anonymous.","zh":"這封信的作者不想透露姓名。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/writer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fd9b19a5f838bad5","term":"writer","forms":["writer","writers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"寫入器；輸出裝置","explanation":"在計算機等技術語境中，writer 是把字元、檔案或其他資料寫入目標位置的程式或裝置；這裡不是真人在寫，而是“產生並寫出內容的裝置”。","examples":[{"en":"The file writer saves each record as soon as it is received.","zh":"檔案寫入器一收到每條記錄就會把它儲存下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The writer sends each completed record to disk.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/writer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8810ad581e59f2bc3928","word":"wrong","forms":["wrong"],"officialPos":"adj./adv./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f29be1ad390cd718","term":"wrong","forms":["wrong","more wrong","most wrong"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不正確的；不真實的","explanation":"表示答案、說法、判斷等與事實不符或不正確，是 wrong 最常見的意思之一。","examples":[{"en":"I chose the wrong answer on the last question.","zh":"我最後一道題選錯了答案。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"That date is wrong; the meeting is on Friday.","zh":"那個日期不對，會議是在星期五。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c0b4f475ce76e6d2","term":"wrong","forms":["wrong","more wrong","most wrong"],"pos":"adj","zh":"判斷或說法不對的","explanation":"用於直接指出某人的說法、判斷或理解不正確，重點是“你說錯了”，而不是單純說某件事本身錯誤。","examples":[{"en":"You are wrong about the train time; it leaves at six.","zh":"你把火車時間記錯了；火車六點出發。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I thought the shop was closed, but I was wrong.","zh":"我以為那家店關門了，但我錯了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc0db569766d4127","term":"wrong","forms":["wrong","more wrong","most wrong"],"pos":"adj","zh":"不正當的；不道德的","explanation":"表示某種行為違背道德或公平原則，例如撒謊、欺騙或傷害別人是不應該的。","examples":[{"en":"It is wrong to take money that does not belong to you.","zh":"拿不屬於自己的錢是不對的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"It was wrong of me to blame her without checking the facts.","zh":"我沒核實事實就責怪她，是我做得不對。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d89c6df323758528","term":"wrong","forms":["wrong","wrongs","wronging","wronged"],"pos":"verb","zh":"不公正地對待；傷害","explanation":"表示以不公平或不正當的方式對待某人，使對方受到損害或虧待。","examples":[{"en":"The company wronged its workers by withholding their pay.","zh":"那家公司扣下工人的工資，虧待了他們。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I know I wronged you, and I am sorry.","zh":"我知道我曾經傷害了你，對不起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wrong","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ed6a077c0b11da0d4eb6","word":"yacht","forms":["yacht"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f108e942d6c20754","term":"yacht","forms":["yacht","yachts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"遊艇；帆船","explanation":"指設計得輕快、漂亮，供私人休閒出海或參加水上比賽的船，通常有帆，但也可能主要靠發動機航行；有些還可長期作為水上住所。","examples":[{"en":"Would you like to go sailing on my uncle's yacht?","zh":"你願意乘我叔叔的遊艇出海嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"They spent the weekend racing their yacht along the coast.","zh":"他們週末駕駛自己的遊艇沿海岸參加比賽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yacht","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bc2a114ab0fed2f0","term":"yacht","forms":["yacht","yachts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"私人非商業船隻","explanation":"這裡不強調船的具體外形，而是把 yacht 泛指用於私人活動、而不是載客或運貨賺錢的船隻。","examples":[{"en":"The harbor has space for several private yachts.","zh":"這個港口有地方停放幾艘私人船隻。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The family spent the weekend aboard their yacht.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yacht","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d353fb7a5f5b83cb82eb","word":"yam","forms":["yam"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ce44efa3c24ef685","term":"yam","forms":["yam","yams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"薯蕷屬植物","explanation":"yam首先可以指薯蕷屬的一類攀緣植物，通常為了食用地下的塊根而栽培。","examples":[{"en":"Farmers grow yams along the fence because the vines need support.","zh":"農民沿著籬笆種薯蕷，因為藤蔓需要支撐。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The yam sends climbing stems up the wooden trellis.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-45f2eac4381dc707","term":"yam","forms":["yam","yams"],"pos":"noun","zh":"可食用的塊根","explanation":"yam也指這種植物地下長出的澱粉質塊根，是許多熱帶地區的重要主食。","examples":[{"en":"We boiled the yams and served them with beans.","zh":"我們把塊根煮熟，和豆子一起端上桌。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Yams are an important staple in many tropical regions.","zh":"在許多熱帶地區，薯蕷塊根是重要的主食。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yam","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-7ae4b7c7678e3e292739","word":"yard","forms":["yard"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-7aa63aadfa0839e4","term":"yard","forms":["yard","yards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"院子","explanation":"指房屋或其他建築旁、通常較小的戶外空間；可以有草地、花木，也可以只是空地。","examples":[{"en":"The children are playing in the yard.","zh":"孩子們正在院子裡玩。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She planted tomatoes in the backyard.","zh":"她在後院種了西紅柿。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6b54a907812ffd14","term":"yard","forms":["yard","yards"],"pos":"noun","zh":"碼","explanation":"英美傳統長度單位，等於 3 英尺，精確值為 0.9144 米；常用於布料、運動場和距離描述。","examples":[{"en":"The rope is six yards long.","zh":"這根繩子長六碼。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The finish line is only ten yards away.","zh":"終點線就在十碼之外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yard","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-25c4df8e80af42b65b48","word":"yawn","forms":["yawn"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-a3ab76e83757b102","term":"yawn","forms":["yawn","yawns"],"pos":"noun","zh":"哈欠","explanation":"yawn 是人張大嘴、吸入一口較深較長的氣時做出的動作，通常與疲倦或無聊有關，也可以指這個動作本身。","examples":[{"en":"She gave a huge yawn during the long lecture.","zh":"長時間的講座中，她打了一個大大的哈欠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I tried to hide my yawn.","zh":"我試著掩飾自己的哈欠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-26c92192c1c0e8ec","term":"yawn","forms":["yawn","yawns","yawning","yawned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"打哈欠","explanation":"作動詞時，yawn 就是張大嘴、深吸一口氣，通常因為疲倦或無聊而打哈欠。","examples":[{"en":"I always yawn when I am tired.","zh":"我累的時候總會打哈欠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children began yawning near the end of the film.","zh":"電影快結束時，孩子們開始打哈欠。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yawn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-4cb4ea25583c25647247","word":"year","forms":["year"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-b400959bd2343fff","term":"year","forms":["year","years"],"pos":"noun","zh":"一年；年","explanation":"指地球經歷一輪完整季節迴圈所需的時間，通常約為三百六十五天；日常也直接用來表示“年”這一時間單位。","examples":[{"en":"We moved to this town a year ago.","zh":"我們一年前搬到了這個城鎮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"I quit smoking exactly one year ago.","zh":"我整整一年前戒了煙。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/year","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-65a3f8bef21c4b50","term":"year","forms":["year","years"],"pos":"noun","zh":"日曆年度","explanation":"指由某種日曆規定的一個完整年度，例如公曆的一月一日至十二月三十一日；閏年比普通年多一天。","examples":[{"en":"A leap year has 366 days instead of 365.","zh":"閏年有366天，而不是365天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The company earned more money during the last calendar year.","zh":"這家公司在上一日曆年度賺了更多錢。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/year","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-bd3038078d1bb1725345","word":"yearly","forms":["yearly"],"officialPos":"adj./adv.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d0765a01a3bdec88","term":"yearly","forms":["yearly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"每年一次的","explanation":"指某件事每年發生一次，或每年定期出現，就像鍾每轉完一圈便重複一次。","examples":[{"en":"The town holds a yearly festival in July.","zh":"這個城鎮每年七月都會舉辦一次節慶活動。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Our yearly inspection falls in early September.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-3c0f6a06cfc7680b","term":"yearly","forms":["yearly"],"pos":"adj","zh":"按年計算的","explanation":"用於收入、費用、增長等數字時，表示把一年作為計算週期，例如把全年收入合在一起計算。","examples":[{"en":"Her yearly income is about $50,000.","zh":"她的年收入大約是五萬美元。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The report compares yearly expenditure across departments.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8c0d40a5163a412c","term":"yearly","forms":["yearly"],"pos":"adv","zh":"每年一次","explanation":"說明某個動作按一年一次的節奏進行，突出年度迴圈。","examples":[{"en":"The company reviews its salaries yearly.","zh":"公司每年審查一次薪資。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The orchard is inspected yearly for signs of disease.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearly","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56306cdfba0896f4c219","word":"yearn","forms":["yearn"],"officialPos":"v.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1526071e9e14e475","term":"yearn","forms":["yearn","yearns","yearning","yearned","yearnt","yearnest","yearnedst","yearneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"渴望；嚮往","explanation":"表示非常強烈、持續地想要某物，或非常想做某事；這種想望往往帶有距離感或感傷色彩。","examples":[{"en":"After years abroad, she yearned for the quiet streets of her hometown.","zh":"在國外生活多年後，她渴望回到家鄉安靜的街道。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He yearns to see his children again.","zh":"他渴望再次見到自己的孩子。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-960b564b8c56ce36","term":"yearn","forms":["yearn","yearns","yearning","yearned","yearnt","yearnest","yearnedst","yearneth","-"],"pos":"verb","zh":"渴望得到或做某事","explanation":"與 s1 基本相同，但常特別強調對某個機會、行動或目標的強烈嚮往；這種渴望也可能因為無法實現而令人遺憾。","examples":[{"en":"She yearned after the chance to travel freely again.","zh":"她渴望再次獲得自由旅行的機會。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He yearned to explore beyond the familiar coastline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yearn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-6c4c36ad42fd8a537787","word":"yell","forms":["yell"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f8dabf4dd2d4c5af","term":"yell","forms":["yell","yells"],"pos":"noun","zh":"喊叫聲","explanation":"yell 是人因疼痛、害怕、憤怒、興奮或想讓別人聽見而發出的高聲喊叫；重點是聲音很響、情緒或目的很強。","examples":[{"en":"A loud yell came from the garden.","zh":"花園裡傳來一聲很大的喊叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She let out a yell when the dog jumped up.","zh":"狗跳起來時，她發出了一聲喊叫。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-48ee6c53016fd097","term":"yell","forms":["yell","yells","yelling","yelled"],"pos":"verb","zh":"高聲喊叫","explanation":"yell 表示聲音突然變大地喊叫或吼叫，常由憤怒、興奮、害怕或需要讓別人聽見引起；不一定是在斥責別人。","examples":[{"en":"He yelled for help when he saw the smoke.","zh":"他看到煙時大聲呼救。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The children yelled with excitement.","zh":"孩子們興奮地大喊起來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yell","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-c685a2c9bab235ccdd2a","word":"yellow","forms":["yellow"],"officialPos":"adj./n./v.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aea8bc4b1d051069","term":"yellow","forms":["yellow","yellower","yellowest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"黃色的","explanation":"表示物體呈黃色，也就是接近檸檬或向日葵花瓣的顏色。","examples":[{"en":"He had a yellow laptop in his bag.","zh":"他的包裡有一臺黃色的膝上型電腦。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Yellow leaves covered the path beneath the birches.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-13f3d2e5332bb71d","term":"yellow","forms":["yellow","yellows"],"pos":"noun","zh":"黃色","explanation":"指黃色這種顏色本身，而不是某一個具體的黃色物體。","examples":[{"en":"The designer used yellow to brighten the room.","zh":"設計師用黃色讓房間顯得更明亮。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A touch of yellow warmed the otherwise gray design.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-dc2d0b25d5338537","term":"yellow","forms":["yellow","yellows","yellowing","yellowed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"變黃","explanation":"表示某物自己變成黃色，或顏色比原來更黃，常用於紙張、葉子、牆面和天空等。","examples":[{"en":"The pages yellowed with age.","zh":"這些書頁隨著時間推移變黃了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The curtains yellowed after years of direct sunlight.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-56ada3c6d2575830bd54","word":"yes/yeah","forms":["yes"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-ee0424022ab9bfec","term":"yes","forms":["yes","yeses","yesses"],"pos":"noun","zh":"肯定的回答","explanation":"名詞 yes 就是一個明確的“同意”或“答應”，把口頭說出的肯定看成一個可以討論、等待或改變的決定。","examples":[{"en":"I asked for permission, and I finally got a yes.","zh":"我請求了許可，最後終於得到了肯定答覆。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her answer was a clear yes.","zh":"她的回答明確表示同意。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yes","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-9523d9fbe79bcf3ee5f9","word":"yesterday","forms":["yesterday"],"officialPos":"adv./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-59bce0e7b04f5775","term":"yesterday","forms":["yesterday"],"pos":"adv","zh":"昨天","explanation":"指今天之前的那一天，也就是離現在約一天的過去時間。","examples":[{"en":"I called my sister yesterday.","zh":"我昨天給姐姐打了電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Yesterday was much colder than today.","zh":"昨天比今天冷得多。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yesterday","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-21c7e22c8de8a421","term":"yesterday","forms":["yesterday","yesterdays"],"pos":"noun","zh":"昨天；前一天","explanation":"指緊接在今天之前的那一天，強調它作為一個日期或時間段本身。","examples":[{"en":"Yesterday was the busiest day of the week.","zh":"昨天是這周最忙的一天。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Yesterday was a public holiday, so the banks were closed.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yesterday","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-cfd96dd92f7e0025b146","word":"yet","forms":["yet"],"officialPos":"adv./conj.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-bcb83169ba7bd8cd","term":"yet","forms":["yet"],"pos":"adv","zh":"到現在還","explanation":"表示截至說話時，事情仍沒有完成，或某種狀態一直持續到現在；最常見於否定句中，相當於“還沒有”。","examples":[{"en":"I haven't finished my homework yet.","zh":"我還沒有做完作業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Has the bus arrived yet?","zh":"公共汽車到了嗎？","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-76f299e1d8bc7004","term":"yet","forms":["yet"],"pos":"adv","zh":"以後還會","explanation":"表示事情雖然現在還沒有實現，但將來仍有可能實現，帶有“遲早會”的意味。它把時間線繼續向前延伸，強調當前結果並不是最終結果。","examples":[{"en":"You will understand it yet.","zh":"你以後總會明白的。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Keep practicing; you may win the tournament yet.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yet","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-8bbcba42d48dcffe6ea6","word":"yield","forms":["yield"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":5,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-678347e15321efb9","term":"yield","forms":["yield","yields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"產出；產品","explanation":"指生產出來的東西，重點在“交出來的產品或成果”本身，而不只是數量。","examples":[{"en":"The farm's main yield is wheat.","zh":"這座農場的主要產出是小麥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The vineyard sells most of its yield to local wineries.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-d14621997315b040","term":"yield","forms":["yield","yields"],"pos":"noun","zh":"產量；收益","explanation":"指某項活動、土地、投資或資源在一段時間內產生的數量或回報，核心是“交出了多少”。","examples":[{"en":"This year's rice yield was higher than expected.","zh":"今年的水稻產量高於預期。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The investment offers a steady yield.","zh":"這項投資能帶來穩定的收益。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f1595cdae3583bb8","term":"yield","forms":["yield","yields","yielding","yielded","yold","yolden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"產生；帶來","explanation":"指某種方法、行動或條件交出一個結果、產品或收益，即“產生、帶來”。","examples":[{"en":"The new method yielded better results.","zh":"這種新方法帶來了更好的結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The trees yield fruit in late summer.","zh":"這些樹在夏末結果。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-da92d4adac31027c","term":"yield","forms":["yield","yields","yielding","yielded","yold","yolden"],"pos":"verb","zh":"讓步；投降","explanation":"指人在爭執、衝突或壓力下交出立場或控制權，也就是讓步、屈服或投降。","examples":[{"en":"After hours of debate, she finally yielded to the committee's demands.","zh":"經過數小時的辯論，她最終向委員會的要求讓步了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The soldiers refused to yield to the enemy.","zh":"士兵們拒絕向敵人投降。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yield","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-ca3142d55e008e17dc28","word":"yoga","forms":["yoga"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-9c7093650e414b52","term":"yoga","forms":["yoga","yogas"],"pos":"noun","zh":"瑜伽練習或體系","explanation":"yoga是一套把身體訓練和意識訓練結合起來的練習或思想體系，目標不只是柔韌和力量，也包括更好的身心控制、精神洞見和寧靜。現代日常語境中，它常特指瑜伽動作、呼吸和冥想等練習。","examples":[{"en":"I do yoga in the morning to relax before work.","zh":"我早上練瑜伽，讓自己在工作前放鬆下來。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Yoga helps her combine breathing exercises with gentle movement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yoga","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-654e9dd6559377ce","term":"yoga","forms":["yoga"],"pos":"noun","zh":"大寫形式","explanation":"Yoga只是yoga的首字母大寫寫法，通常由句首、標題或專名書寫規則造成，本身不表示另一種瑜伽活動。","examples":[{"en":"Yoga can be a gentle way to begin the day.","zh":"瑜伽可以成為開始一天的一種溫和方式。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Yoga helps her unwind after a demanding shift.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yoga","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b0df7aca2b1494807e44","word":"yogurt","forms":["yogurt"],"officialPos":"n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c5dd15245d2051c9","term":"yogurt","forms":["yogurt","yogurts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"酸奶","explanation":"最常見的意思是用牛奶經過細菌發酵並凝固製成的食品，通常帶有酸味，也可能加入水果或其他調味料。","examples":[{"en":"I usually eat yogurt with fruit for breakfast.","zh":"我通常早餐吃加水果的酸奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She bought two yogurts after her workout.","zh":"鍛鍊後她買了兩盒酸奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yogurt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-df1fe156f98e3a30","term":"yogurt","forms":["yogurt","yogurts"],"pos":"noun","zh":"其他原料製成的類似酸奶","explanation":"這個意思把“發酵後凝固的乳狀食品”這一概念擴充套件到其他原料，例如豆漿，因此也可以指豆乳等製成的類似產品。","examples":[{"en":"This café offers soy yogurt for customers who avoid dairy.","zh":"這家咖啡館為不吃乳製品的顧客提供豆乳酸奶。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She stirred berries into her coconut yogurt.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yogurt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-77b29215862b3ae0fa98","word":"yolk","forms":["yolk"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-be9c3eed1502b580","term":"yolk","forms":["yolk","yolks"],"pos":"noun","zh":"蛋黃","explanation":"蛋裡面黃色的圓形部分，外面包著蛋清，能為正在發育的胚胎提供營養；在日常英語中，這是 yolk 最主要的意思。","examples":[{"en":"To make the sauce, whisk the egg yolks with the lemon juice.","zh":"製作這種醬汁時，把蛋黃和檸檬汁攪拌在一起。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She separated the yolk from the white before baking the cake.","zh":"烤蛋糕前，她把蛋黃和蛋清分開了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yolk","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-3aef5b6b3131a63c3aad","word":"you (your, yours, yourself, yourselves)","forms":["you"],"officialPos":"pron.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-1c0a57282d5c834d","term":"you","forms":["you","ye"],"pos":"det","zh":"你；你們","explanation":"指說話或寫信時正在面對的一個人或一群人；數量要由語境判斷。","examples":[{"en":"You students should hand in your papers by Friday.","zh":"你們學生應該在星期五前交論文。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You children need coats before going outside.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/you","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-73ac3313ce4fc8c9","term":"you","forms":["you","yourself","yourselves","ye"],"pos":"pron","zh":"你；你們（賓語）","explanation":"作動詞或介詞的物件，指被說話或寫信的一個人或一群人。","examples":[{"en":"I’ll call you after dinner.","zh":"我晚飯後給你打電話。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"We saved you a seat beside the window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/you","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-6053997b8ae8673c","term":"you","forms":["you","yourself","yourselves","ye"],"pos":"pron","zh":"你們（主語）","explanation":"作主語，指正在被說話的一群人。現代英語中同一形式也可指一個人。","examples":[{"en":"You are all invited to the meeting.","zh":"你們都受邀參加會議。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You must all bring your passports tomorrow.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/you","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1dfdb742fb831830","term":"you","forms":["you","yourself","yourselves","ye"],"pos":"pron","zh":"你（主語）","explanation":"作主語指正在被說話的一個人；歷史上曾帶有禮貌或尊敬色彩，現代英語中已是普通用法。","examples":[{"en":"You are right about the schedule.","zh":"你說得對，日程就是這樣。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"You have left your gloves beside the sink.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/you","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dbba921ce20510210ee7","word":"young","forms":["young"],"officialPos":"adj./n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-f2755fa4669e2a8d","term":"young","forms":["young","younger","youngest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"年幼的；年輕的","explanation":"指人或動物出生不久、年齡較小，處在生命的早期階段。這是 young 最基本、最常見的意思。","examples":[{"en":"The young boy was learning to ride a bicycle.","zh":"那個小男孩正在學騎腳踏車。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The mother bird fed her young in the nest.","zh":"鳥媽媽在巢裡餵養幼鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/young","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-189755c47b0a1cac","term":"young","forms":["young","younger","youngest"],"pos":"adj","zh":"新近開始的；尚處於早期的","explanation":"把“年齡小”的概念擴大到事物：某個行業、制度、技術或時期存在的時間還不長，仍在發展的早期。","examples":[{"en":"Space tourism is still a young industry.","zh":"太空旅遊仍是一個新興行業。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young company is growing quickly.","zh":"這家新成立的公司發展得很快。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/young","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c4d6bef80de906fb","term":"young","forms":["young","youngs"],"pos":"noun","zh":"幼崽；幼小動物","explanation":"名詞 young 指尚未成熟的動物後代，核心畫面就是“年幼的動物們”。它常根據上下文指幼獅、幼鳥、幼獸等，而不必重複動物名稱。","examples":[{"en":"The fox carried food back to its young.","zh":"那隻狐狸把食物帶回去喂幼崽。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The deer stayed near her young.","zh":"那隻母鹿守在幼崽附近。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/young","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-dbc9a3eeab8fb9d620c4","word":"youngster","forms":["youngster"],"officialPos":"n.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-45c53c40a76590d6","term":"youngster","forms":["youngster","youngsters"],"pos":"noun","zh":"年輕人；孩子","explanation":"指年輕的人，既可以是孩子，也可以是年紀較輕的成年人；重點在於年輕和充滿活力，而不在具體年齡。","examples":[{"en":"The youngsters played soccer in the park after school.","zh":"孩子們放學後在公園裡踢足球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"As a youngster, she spent every summer by the sea.","zh":"她年輕時每年夏天都在海邊度過。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youngster","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-b5bdafe95dec0c53112c","word":"youth","forms":["youth"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-501c22fe2acb4b15","term":"youth","forms":["youth","youths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"年輕狀態；青春","explanation":"指一個人年輕、有活力的狀態，重點在“年輕這一特徵”，而不是具體的年齡階段。","examples":[{"en":"Her youth and energy impressed everyone at the meeting.","zh":"她的年輕和活力給會議上的每個人都留下了深刻印象。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Her youth made the achievement even more remarkable.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-b517ad8caf6e7fdd","term":"youth","forms":["youth","youths"],"pos":"noun","zh":"年輕時期；青春期至成年前後","explanation":"指人生中從童年到成熟、年老以前的早期階段，也就是通常所說的青春歲月。","examples":[{"en":"She spent her youth traveling around the country.","zh":"她在年輕時走遍了全國。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Make the most of your youth while you have the chance.","zh":"趁年輕還有機會，好好珍惜你的青春時光。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youth","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-92801f858b6699026bff","word":"youthful","forms":["youthful"],"officialPos":"adj.","level":4,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-aff3eeac8dab139e","term":"youthful","forms":["youthful","more youthful","most youthful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"顯得年輕的","explanation":"指某人的外表、聲音或整體形象不像實際年齡那麼大，給人年輕的感覺。重點在“看起來年輕”，而不一定表示這個人確實年紀小。","examples":[{"en":"The youthful-looking teacher was often mistaken for a student.","zh":"那位看起來很年輕的老師常被誤認為是學生。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She has a youthful face despite being in her forties.","zh":"她雖然已經四十多歲了，但仍有一張年輕的臉。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youthful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-1c47072d39db7d60","term":"youthful","forms":["youthful","more youthful","most youthful"],"pos":"adj","zh":"充滿青春活力的","explanation":"指活潑、熱情、有朝氣等年輕人常有的特點；這裡不一定涉及外表，而是說精神狀態或行為帶有青春感。","examples":[{"en":"Her youthful enthusiasm made the whole team feel more confident.","zh":"她充滿青春活力的熱情讓整個團隊更有信心。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"His youthful curiosity kept him learning well into retirement.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/youthful","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-676cb75018edccf10fce","word":"zebra","forms":["zebra"],"officialPos":"n.","level":2,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-d1adcd8e464caaaf","term":"zebra","forms":["zebra","zebras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"斑馬","explanation":"指生活在非洲、身上有黑白條紋的馬科動物。這是 zebra 最基本、最常見的意思，也是其他許多引申義的形象來源。","examples":[{"en":"We saw a group of zebras near the river.","zh":"我們在河邊看見了一群斑馬。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The young zebra stayed close to its mother.","zh":"那匹小斑馬一直待在母斑馬身邊。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zebra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-fa365732153144d3","term":"zebra","forms":["zebra","zebras"],"pos":"noun","zh":"裁判","explanation":"體育俚語中，zebra 可指穿黑白條紋裁判服的裁判，意思來自斑馬的條紋。","examples":[{"en":"The zebra stopped the game and awarded a free kick.","zh":"裁判吹停了比賽，並判給一記任意球。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The zebra signaled a holding penalty from midfield.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"common","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zebra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-f9194e73f9e9459e3450","word":"zero","forms":["zero"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-40a0ba1e2ada0f6b","term":"zero","forms":["zero","zeros","zeroes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"零這個數字或符號","explanation":"zero 是表示“沒有數量”的數字，也可以指代表這個數字的符號。它是計數和計算的基礎，不只是“空白”。","examples":[{"en":"The final score was zero to three.","zh":"最終比分是零比三。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Put a zero before the number to make it six digits long.","zh":"在這個數字前加一個零，使它變成六位數。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zero","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-4746956130a57dcf","term":"zero","forms":["zero","zeros","zeroes"],"pos":"noun","zh":"數字 0","explanation":"zero 也專指寫在十進位制、二進位制等記數系統中的數字符號 0。它有時只佔一個位置，卻能改變整個數字的大小。","examples":[{"en":"There are three zeroes in one million.","zh":"一百萬裡有六個零。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Write a zero in the empty box.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zero","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ac035b55f3c671d0","term":"zero","forms":["zero"],"pos":"num","zh":"基數詞零","explanation":"作為數詞，zero 表示數量為零，即一個也沒有；它位於一之前，是完整數列中的一個數字。","examples":[{"en":"The passenger count was zero when the train left.","zh":"火車開走時，乘客人數為零。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The scoreboard still showed zero after ninety minutes.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zero","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-5827d8b677972a2621c1","word":"zipper","forms":["zipper"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-82cba60be0d4f541","term":"zipper","forms":["zipper","zippers"],"pos":"noun","zh":"拉鍊","explanation":"衣服、包或其他物品上用來把兩邊齒狀部分合攏或分開的閉合裝置。","examples":[{"en":"The zipper on my backpack is stuck.","zh":"我揹包上的拉鍊卡住了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"She pulled the zipper up on her coat.","zh":"她把外套的拉鍊拉上了。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zipper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-bbf64554f88acd9c","term":"zipper","forms":["zipper","zippers","zippering","zippered"],"pos":"verb","zh":"拉上拉鍊","explanation":"把衣服或其他物品上的拉鍊拉到閉合位置，使兩邊合攏。","examples":[{"en":"Zipper your jacket up before you go outside.","zh":"出門前把你的夾克拉鍊拉上。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"He zippered his sweater against the cold.","zh":"他把毛衣的拉鍊拉上以抵禦寒冷。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zipper","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-543e33c48b3c23d3b3ef","word":"zone","forms":["zone"],"officialPos":"n./v.","level":3,"categories":["ceec","gsat"],"senses":[{"id":"od-c05d92c9aa70cdad","term":"zone","forms":["zone","zones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"區域；地帶","explanation":"指世界上或某個地方的一片區域，重點只是把它看作一個有範圍的地帶，不一定帶有特殊限制。","examples":[{"en":"The coastal zone is home to many fishing villages.","zh":"沿海地區有許多漁村。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The dry zone receives very little annual rainfall.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-c529991ca5cac7ba","term":"zone","forms":["zone","zones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"按特徵劃出的區域","explanation":"指因為用途、規則、環境或某種特點而被明確劃出的區域，例如禁菸區、停車區或工業區。它是“區域”這個基本概念上增加了明確標準。","examples":[{"en":"Please wait in the loading zone while we bring out your boxes.","zh":"我們搬出箱子時，請在裝貨區等候。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The school has created a quiet zone for students who need to study.","zh":"學校為需要學習的學生設立了安靜區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f89429b18cee0da5","term":"zone","forms":["zone","zones"],"pos":"noun","zh":"受限區域；危險地帶","explanation":"可以是實際受到限制的地方，也可以是比喻意義上的某種狀態或處境，例如危險區、禁區。這裡的重點是“進入後會受到某種規則或風險影響”。","examples":[{"en":"That old bridge is still a danger zone after the storm.","zh":"那座舊橋在暴風雨後仍然是危險區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Talking to strangers used to be outside my comfort zone.","zh":"過去，和陌生人交談對我來說屬於舒適區之外。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-e6b6acaef181baf1","term":"zone","forms":["zone","zones","zoning","zoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"劃分成區域","explanation":"把一個地方分成幾個區域，或為不同人、活動和用途劃出各自的部分。它是名詞“區域”概念的直接動詞化。","examples":[{"en":"The organizers zoned off the hall for different activities.","zh":"組織者把大廳劃分成了不同的活動區域。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The planners zoned the site into three distinct areas.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-ab2d8f25e9650316","term":"zone","forms":["zone","zones","zoning","zoned"],"pos":"verb","zh":"規定土地用途","explanation":"按照規劃或法律規定某片土地可以作什麼用途，例如住宅、商業或工業用地。","examples":[{"en":"The land is zoned for residential use.","zh":"這塊土地被規劃為住宅用地。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The council zoned the waterfront for commercial development.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zone","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"exam":{"years":[111,115],"total":2,"counts":{"111":1,"115":1}}},{"id":"ceec-24fe93c9e17cb80452e5","word":"zoo","forms":["zoo"],"officialPos":"n.","level":1,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-66006316c65506fa","term":"zoo","forms":["zoo","zoos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"動物園","explanation":"展示活體動物、供人參觀的公園或場所。這裡的核心畫面就是把許多不同動物集中在一個地方。","examples":[{"en":"We took the children to the zoo on Sunday.","zh":"我們星期天帶孩子們去了動物園。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The zoo has a new enclosure for the elephants.","zh":"這家動物園為大象建了一個新的圍欄區。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zoo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-28106bf3c2191820","term":"zoo","forms":["zoo","zoos"],"pos":"noun","zh":"混亂擁擠的地方","explanation":"把人群和活動很多、嘈雜失控的地方比作擠滿動物的動物園，強調場面混亂而不是字面上的動物。","examples":[{"en":"The station was a zoo after the concert ended.","zh":"音樂會結束後，車站裡亂成了一鍋粥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The departure lounge became a zoo when three flights were canceled.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zoo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]},{"id":"ceec-d21bb537725d603ee2db","word":"zoom","forms":["zoom"],"officialPos":"v./n.","level":6,"categories":["ceec"],"senses":[{"id":"od-8e25aca11c01b146","term":"zoom","forms":["zoom","zooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"嗡嗡聲","explanation":"指快速移動的車輛、機器等發出的嗡嗡聲，和感嘆詞的聲音形象相同。","examples":[{"en":"The zoom of traffic kept us awake all night.","zh":"車輛持續的嗡嗡聲讓我們整夜睡不著。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"A distant zoom announced the approaching motorbike.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zoom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-783def9cc35e9426","term":"zoom","forms":["zoom","zooms"],"pos":"noun","zh":"放大功能","explanation":"指透過改變鏡頭焦距或調整數字畫面，把遠處或細小的內容拉近、放大的功能。","examples":[{"en":"This camera has a powerful zoom for photographing birds.","zh":"這臺相機的變焦功能很強，適合拍鳥。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Use the zoom to capture the detail on the distant tower.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zoom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-8ef85a5bf60ef93c","term":"zoom","forms":["zoom","zooms","zooming","zoomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"飛快移動併發出嗡聲","explanation":"指某人或某物高速移動，常讓人聯想到伴隨而來的嗡嗡聲。","examples":[{"en":"The motorcycle zoomed along the empty highway.","zh":"摩托車沿著空曠的高速公路飛馳而去。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"The little drone zoomed past the open window.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zoom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"id":"od-f8dcc94afb477c69","term":"zoom","forms":["zoom","zooms","zooming","zoomed"],"pos":"verb","zh":"放大或縮小顯示","explanation":"指調整螢幕、地圖或圖片的顯示比例，讓內容看得更大或容納更多內容。","examples":[{"en":"Zoom in on the map to find the walking trail.","zh":"把地圖放大，找出步行小路。","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0"},{"en":"Zoom out to see the whole coastline.","zh":"","source":"Wordgrove 補寫"}],"priority":"core","source":"Open Dictionary v2.0 / Wiktionary；部分例句由 Wordgrove 補寫","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zoom","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}]}]};
